Bible_Text_Genesis_1_1::
    .string "In the beginning God created the\n"
    .string "heaven and the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_2::
    .string "And the earth was without form, and\n"
    .string "void; and darkness was upon the face\l"
    .string "of the deep. And the Spirit of God\l"
    .string "moved upon the face of the waters.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_3::
    .string "And God said, Let there be light:\n"
    .string "and there was light.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_4::
    .string "And God saw the light, that it was\n"
    .string "good: and God divided the light from\l"
    .string "the darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_5::
    .string "And God called the light Day, and\n"
    .string "the darkness he called Night. And\l"
    .string "the evening and the morning were the\l"
    .string "first day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_6::
    .string "And God said, Let there be a\n"
    .string "firmament in the midst of the waters,\l"
    .string "and let it divide the waters from\l"
    .string "the waters.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_7::
    .string "And God made the firmament, and\n"
    .string "divided the waters which were under\l"
    .string "the firmament from the waters which\l"
    .string "were above the firmament: and it was\l"
    .string "so.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_8::
    .string "And God called the firmament Heaven\n"
    .string " And the evening and the morning\l"
    .string "were the second day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_9::
    .string "And God said, Let the waters under\n"
    .string "the heaven be gathered together unto\l"
    .string "one place, and let the dry land\l"
    .string "appear: and it was so.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_10::
    .string "And God called the dry land Earth;\n"
    .string "and the gathering together of the\l"
    .string "waters called he Seas: and God saw\l"
    .string "that it was good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_11::
    .string "And God said, Let the earth bring\n"
    .string "forth grass, the herb yielding seed,\l"
    .string "and the fruit tree yielding fruit\l"
    .string "after his kind, whose seed is in\l"
    .string "itself, upon the earth: and it was\l"
    .string "so.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_12::
    .string "And the earth brought forth grass,\n"
    .string "and herb yielding seed after his\l"
    .string "kind, and the tree yielding fruit,\l"
    .string "whose seed was in itself, after his\l"
    .string "kind: and God saw that it was good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_13::
    .string "And the evening and the morning were\n"
    .string "the third day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_14::
    .string "And God said, Let there be lights in\n"
    .string "the firmament of the heaven to divide\l"
    .string "the day from the night; and let them\l"
    .string "be for signs, and for seasons, and\l"
    .string "for days, and years:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_15::
    .string "And let them be for lights in the\n"
    .string "firmament of the heaven to give\l"
    .string "light upon the earth: and it was so$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_16::
    .string "And God made two great lights; the\n"
    .string "greater light to rule the day, and\l"
    .string "the lesser light to rule the night:\l"
    .string "he made the stars also.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_17::
    .string "And God set them in the firmament of\n"
    .string "the heaven to give light upon the\l"
    .string "earth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_18::
    .string "And to rule over the day and over\n"
    .string "the night, and to divide the light\l"
    .string "from the darkness: and God saw that\l"
    .string "it was good$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_19::
    .string "And the evening and the morning were\n"
    .string "the fourth day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_20::
    .string "And God said, Let the waters bring\n"
    .string "forth abundantly the moving\l"
    .string "creature that hath life, and fowl\l"
    .string "that may fly above the earth in the\l"
    .string "open firmament of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_21::
    .string "And God created great whales, and\n"
    .string "every living creature that moveth,\l"
    .string "which the waters brought forth\l"
    .string "abundantly, after their kind, and\l"
    .string "every winged fowl after his kind:\l"
    .string "and God saw that it was good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_22::
    .string "And God blessed them, saying, Be\n"
    .string "fruitful, and multiply, and fill\l"
    .string "the waters in the seas, and let fowl\l"
    .string "multiply in the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_23::
    .string "And the evening and the morning were\n"
    .string "the fifth day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_24::
    .string "And God said, Let the earth bring\n"
    .string "forth the living creature after his\l"
    .string "kind, cattle, and creeping thing,\l"
    .string "and beast of the earth after his\l"
    .string "kind: and it was so.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_25::
    .string "And God made the beast of the earth\n"
    .string "after his kind, and cattle after\l"
    .string "their kind, and every thing that\l"
    .string "creepeth upon the earth after his\l"
    .string "kind: and God saw that it was good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_26::
    .string "And God said, Let us make man in our\n"
    .string "image, after our likeness: and let\l"
    .string "them have dominion over the fish of\l"
    .string "the sea, and over the fowl of the\l"
    .string "air, and over the cattle, and over\l"
    .string "all the earth, and over every\l"
    .string "creeping thing that creepeth upon\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_27::
    .string "So God created man in his own image,\n"
    .string "in the image of God created he him;\l"
    .string "male and female created he them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_28::
    .string "And God blessed them, and God said\n"
    .string "unto them, Be fruitful, and\l"
    .string "multiply, and replenish the\l"
    .string "earth, and subdue it: and have\l"
    .string "dominion over the fish of the sea,\l"
    .string "and over the fowl of the air, and\l"
    .string "over every living thing that moveth\l"
    .string "upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_29::
    .string "And God said, Behold, I have given\n"
    .string "you every herb bearing seed, which is\l"
    .string "upon the face of all the earth, and\l"
    .string "every tree, in the which is the fruit\l"
    .string "of a tree yielding seed; to you it\l"
    .string "shall be for meat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_30::
    .string "And to every beast of the earth, and\n"
    .string "to every fowl of the air, and to\l"
    .string "every thing that creepeth upon the\l"
    .string "earth, wherein there is life, I have\l"
    .string "given every green herb for meat: and\l"
    .string "it was so.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_1_31::
    .string "And God saw every thing that he had\n"
    .string "made, and, behold, it was very good.\l"
    .string "And the evening and the morning were\l"
    .string "the sixth day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_1::
    .string "Thus the heavens and the earth were\n"
    .string "finished, and all the host of them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_2::
    .string "And on the seventh day God ended his\n"
    .string "work which he had made; and he rested\l"
    .string "on the seventh day from all his work\l"
    .string "which he had made.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_3::
    .string "And God blessed the seventh day,\n"
    .string "and sanctified it: because that in it\l"
    .string "he had rested from all his work\l"
    .string "which God created and made.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_4::
    .string "These are the generations of the\n"
    .string "heavens and of the earth when they\l"
    .string "were created, in the day that the\l"
    .string "LORD God made the earth and the\l"
    .string "heavens,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_5::
    .string "And every plant of the field\n"
    .string "before it was in the earth, and every\l"
    .string "herb of the field before it grew: for\l"
    .string "the LORD God had not caused it to\l"
    .string "rain upon the earth, and there was\l"
    .string "not a man to till the ground$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_6::
    .string "But there went up a mist from the\n"
    .string "earth, and watered the whole face of\l"
    .string "the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_7::
    .string "And the LORD God formed man of the\n"
    .string "dust of the ground, and breathed into\l"
    .string "his nostrils the breath of life; and\l"
    .string "man became a living soul.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_8::
    .string "And the LORD God planted a garden\n"
    .string "eastward in Eden; and there he put\l"
    .string "the man whom he had formed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_9::
    .string "And out of the ground made the LORD\n"
    .string "God to grow every tree that is\l"
    .string "pleasant to the sight, and good for\l"
    .string "food; the tree of life also in the\l"
    .string "midst of the garden, and the tree of\l"
    .string "knowledge of good and evil.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_10::
    .string "And a river went out of Eden to\n"
    .string "water the garden; and from thence it\l"
    .string "was parted, and became into four\l"
    .string "heads.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_11::
    .string "The name of the first is Pison: that\n"
    .string "is it which compasseth the whole\l"
    .string "land of Havilah, where there is\l"
    .string "gold;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_12::
    .string "And the gold of that land is good:\n"
    .string "there is bdellium and the onyx stone$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_13::
    .string "And the name of the second river is\n"
    .string "Gihon: the same is it that\l"
    .string "compasseth the whole land of\l"
    .string "Ethiopia.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_14::
    .string "And the name of the third river is\n"
    .string "Hiddekel: that is it which goeth\l"
    .string "toward the east of Assyria. And the\l"
    .string "fourth river is Euphrates.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_15::
    .string "And the LORD God took the man, and\n"
    .string "put him into the garden of Eden to\l"
    .string "dress it and to keep it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_16::
    .string "And the LORD God commanded the man,\n"
    .string "saying, Of every tree of the garden\l"
    .string "thou mayest freely eat:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_17::
    .string "But of the tree of the knowledge of\n"
    .string "good and evil, thou shalt not eat of\l"
    .string "it: for in the day that thou eatest\l"
    .string "thereof thou shalt surely die$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_18::
    .string "And the LORD God said, It is not good\n"
    .string "that the man should be alone; I\l"
    .string "will make him an help meet for him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_19::
    .string "And out of the ground the LORD God\n"
    .string "formed every beast of the field, and\l"
    .string "every fowl of the air; and brought\l"
    .string "them unto Adam to see what he would\l"
    .string "call them: and whatsoever Adam\l"
    .string "called every living creature, that\l"
    .string "was the name thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_20::
    .string "And Adam gave names to all cattle,\n"
    .string "and to the fowl of the air, and to\l"
    .string "every beast of the field; but for\l"
    .string "Adam there was not found an help\l"
    .string "meet for him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_21::
    .string "And the LORD God caused a deep\n"
    .string "sleep to fall upon Adam, and he\l"
    .string "slept: and he took one of his ribs,\l"
    .string "and closed up the flesh instead\l"
    .string "thereof;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_22::
    .string "And the rib, which the LORD God had\n"
    .string "taken from man, made he a woman, and\l"
    .string "brought her unto the man$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_23::
    .string "And Adam said, This is now bone of my\n"
    .string "bones, and flesh of my flesh: she\l"
    .string "shall be called Woman, because she\l"
    .string "was taken out of Man.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_24::
    .string "Therefore shall a man leave his\n"
    .string "father and his mother, and shall\l"
    .string "cleave unto his wife: and they\l"
    .string "shall be one flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_2_25::
    .string "And they were both naked, the man\n"
    .string "and his wife, and were not ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_1::
    .string "Now the serpent was more subtil\n"
    .string "than any beast of the field which\l"
    .string "the LORD God had made. And he said\l"
    .string "unto the woman, Yea, hath God said, Ye\l"
    .string "shall not eat of every tree of the\l"
    .string "garden?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_2::
    .string "And the woman said unto the\n"
    .string "serpent, We may eat of the fruit of\l"
    .string "the trees of the garden:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_3::
    .string "But of the fruit of the tree which\n"
    .string "is in the midst of the garden, God\l"
    .string "hath said, Ye shall not eat of it,\l"
    .string "neither shall ye touch it, lest ye\l"
    .string "die$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_4::
    .string "And the serpent said unto the\n"
    .string "woman, Ye shall not surely die:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_5::
    .string "For God doth know that in the day ye\n"
    .string "eat thereof, then your eyes shall be\l"
    .string "opened, and ye shall be as gods,\l"
    .string "knowing good and evil$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_6::
    .string "And when the woman saw that the tree\n"
    .string "was good for food, and that it was\l"
    .string "pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to\l"
    .string "be desired to make one wise, she took\l"
    .string "of the fruit thereof, and did eat,\l"
    .string "and gave also unto her husband with\l"
    .string "her; and he did eat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_7::
    .string "And the eyes of them both were\n"
    .string "opened, and they knew that they were\l"
    .string "naked; and they sewed fig leaves\l"
    .string "together, and made themselves\l"
    .string "aprons.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_8::
    .string "And they heard the voice of the LORD\n"
    .string "God walking in the garden in the\l"
    .string "cool of the day: and Adam and his\l"
    .string "wife hid themselves from the\l"
    .string "presence of the LORD God amongst the\l"
    .string "trees of the garden.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_9::
    .string "And the LORD God called unto Adam,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, Where art thou?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_10::
    .string "And he said, I heard thy voice in the\n"
    .string "garden, and I was afraid, because I\l"
    .string "was naked; and I hid myself$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_11::
    .string "And he said, Who told thee that thou\n"
    .string "wast naked? Hast thou eaten of the\l"
    .string "tree, whereof I commanded thee that\l"
    .string "thou shouldest not eat?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_12::
    .string "And the man said, The woman whom\n"
    .string "thou gavest to be with me, she gave me\l"
    .string "of the tree, and I did eat$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_13::
    .string "And the LORD God said unto the\n"
    .string "woman, What is this that thou hast\l"
    .string "done? And the woman said, The\l"
    .string "serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_14::
    .string "And the LORD God said unto the\n"
    .string "serpent, Because thou hast done\l"
    .string "this, thou art cursed above all\l"
    .string "cattle, and above every beast of the\l"
    .string "field; upon thy belly shalt thou\l"
    .string "go, and dust shalt thou eat all the\l"
    .string "days of thy life:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_15::
    .string "And I will put enmity between thee\n"
    .string "and the woman, and between thy seed\l"
    .string "and her seed; it shall bruise thy\l"
    .string "head, and thou shalt bruise his heel$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_16::
    .string "Unto the woman he said, I will\n"
    .string "greatly multiply thy sorrow and\l"
    .string "thy conception; in sorrow thou\l"
    .string "shalt bring forth children; and thy\l"
    .string "desire shall be to thy husband, and\l"
    .string "he shall rule over thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_17::
    .string "And unto Adam he said, Because thou\n"
    .string "hast hearkened unto the voice of thy\l"
    .string "wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of\l"
    .string "which I commanded thee, saying, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt not eat of it: cursed is the\l"
    .string "ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt\l"
    .string "thou eat of it all the days of thy\l"
    .string "life;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_18::
    .string "Thorns also and thistles shall it\n"
    .string "bring forth to thee; and thou shalt\l"
    .string "eat the herb of the field;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_19::
    .string "In the sweat of thy face shalt thou\n"
    .string "eat bread, till thou return unto the\l"
    .string "ground; for out of it wast thou\l"
    .string "taken: for dust thou art, and unto\l"
    .string "dust shalt thou return$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_20::
    .string "And Adam called his wife’s name\n"
    .string "Eve; because she was the mother of\l"
    .string "all living.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_21::
    .string "Unto Adam also and to his wife did\n"
    .string "the LORD God make coats of skins, and\l"
    .string "clothed them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_22::
    .string "And the LORD God said, Behold, the\n"
    .string "man is become as one of us, to know\l"
    .string "good and evil: and now, lest he put\l"
    .string "forth his hand, and take also of the\l"
    .string "tree of life, and eat, and live for\l"
    .string "ever:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_23::
    .string "Therefore the LORD God sent him\n"
    .string "forth from the garden of Eden, to\l"
    .string "till the ground from whence he was\l"
    .string "taken$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_3_24::
    .string "So he drove out the man; and he\n"
    .string "placed at the east of the garden of\l"
    .string "Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword\l"
    .string "which turned every way, to keep the\l"
    .string "way of the tree of life.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_1::
    .string "And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she\n"
    .string "conceived, and bare Cain, and said, I\l"
    .string "have gotten a man from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_2::
    .string "And she again bare his brother\n"
    .string "Abel. And Abel was a keeper of\l"
    .string "sheep, but Cain was a tiller of the\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_3::
    .string "And in process of time it came to\n"
    .string "pass, that Cain brought of the fruit\l"
    .string "of the ground an offering unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_4::
    .string "And Abel, he also brought of the\n"
    .string "firstlings of his flock and of the\l"
    .string "fat thereof. And the LORD had\l"
    .string "respect unto Abel and to his\l"
    .string "offering:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_5::
    .string "But unto Cain and to his offering he\n"
    .string "had not respect. And Cain was very\l"
    .string "wroth, and his countenance fell$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_6::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Cain, Why art\n"
    .string "thou wroth? and why is thy\l"
    .string "countenance fallen?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_7::
    .string "If thou doest well, shalt thou not\n"
    .string "be accepted? and if thou doest not\l"
    .string "well, sin lieth at the door. And\l"
    .string "unto thee shall be his desire, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt rule over him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_8::
    .string "And Cain talked with Abel his\n"
    .string "brother: and it came to pass, when\l"
    .string "they were in the field, that Cain\l"
    .string "rose up against Abel his brother,\l"
    .string "and slew him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Cain, Where\n"
    .string "is Abel thy brother? And he said, I\l"
    .string "know not: Am I my brother’s keeper?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_10::
    .string "And he said, What hast thou done?\n"
    .string "the voice of thy brother’s blood\l"
    .string "crieth unto me from the ground$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_11::
    .string "And now art thou cursed from the\n"
    .string "earth, which hath opened her mouth\l"
    .string "to receive thy brother’s blood from\l"
    .string "thy hand;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_12::
    .string "When thou tillest the ground, it\n"
    .string "shall not henceforth yield unto\l"
    .string "thee her strength; a fugitive and a\l"
    .string "vagabond shalt thou be in the earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_13::
    .string "And Cain said unto the LORD, My\n"
    .string "punishment is greater than I can bear.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_14::
    .string "Behold, thou hast driven me out\n"
    .string "this day from the face of the earth;\l"
    .string "and from thy face shall I be hid;\l"
    .string "and I shall be a fugitive and a\l"
    .string "vagabond in the earth; and it shall\l"
    .string "come to pass, that every one that\l"
    .string "findeth me shall slay me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_15::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him,\n"
    .string "Therefore whosoever slayeth Cain,\l"
    .string "vengeance shall be taken on him\l"
    .string "sevenfold. And the LORD set a mark\l"
    .string "upon Cain, lest any finding him\l"
    .string "should kill him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_16::
    .string "And Cain went out from the presence\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and dwelt in the land\l"
    .string "of Nod, on the east of Eden.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_17::
    .string "And Cain knew his wife; and she\n"
    .string "conceived, and bare Enoch: and he\l"
    .string "builded a city, and called the name\l"
    .string "of the city, after the name of his\l"
    .string "son, Enoch.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_18::
    .string "And unto Enoch was born Irad: and\n"
    .string "Irad begat Mehujael: and Mehujael\l"
    .string "begat Methusael: and Methusael\l"
    .string "begat Lamech.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_19::
    .string "And Lamech took unto him two wives:\n"
    .string "the name of the one was Adah, and the\l"
    .string "name of the other Zillah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_20::
    .string "And Adah bare Jabal: he was the\n"
    .string "father of such as dwell in tents,\l"
    .string "and of such as have cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_21::
    .string "And his brother’s name was Jubal:\n"
    .string "he was the father of all such as\l"
    .string "handle the harp and organ.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_22::
    .string "And Zillah, she also bare\n"
    .string "Tubalcain, an instructer of every\l"
    .string "artificer in brass and iron: and the\l"
    .string "sister of Tubalcain was Naamah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_23::
    .string "And Lamech said unto his wives, Adah\n"
    .string "and Zillah, Hear my voice; ye wives\l"
    .string "of Lamech, hearken unto my speech:\l"
    .string "for I have slain a man to my\l"
    .string "wounding, and a young man to my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_24::
    .string "If Cain shall be avenged\n"
    .string "sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and\l"
    .string "sevenfold.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_25::
    .string "And Adam knew his wife again; and\n"
    .string "she bare a son, and called his name\l"
    .string "Seth: For God, said she, hath\l"
    .string "appointed me another seed instead\l"
    .string "of Abel, whom Cain slew.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_4_26::
    .string "And to Seth, to him also there was\n"
    .string "born a son; and he called his name\l"
    .string "Enos: then began men to call upon\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_1::
    .string "This is the book of the generations\n"
    .string "of Adam. In the day that God created\l"
    .string "man, in the likeness of God made he\l"
    .string "him;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_2::
    .string "Male and female created he them;\n"
    .string "and blessed them, and called their\l"
    .string "name Adam, in the day when they were\l"
    .string "created$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_3::
    .string "And Adam lived an hundred and\n"
    .string "thirty years, and begat a son in his\l"
    .string "own likeness, and after his image;\l"
    .string "and called his name Seth:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_4::
    .string "And the days of Adam after he had\n"
    .string "begotten Seth were eight hundred\l"
    .string "years: and he begat sons and\l"
    .string "daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_5::
    .string "And all the days that Adam lived\n"
    .string "were nine hundred and thirty years:\l"
    .string "and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_6::
    .string "And Seth lived an hundred and five\n"
    .string "years, and begat Enos:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_7::
    .string "And Seth lived after he begat Enos\n"
    .string "eight hundred and seven years, and\l"
    .string "begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_8::
    .string "And all the days of Seth were nine\n"
    .string "hundred and twelve years: and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_9::
    .string "And Enos lived ninety years, and\n"
    .string "begat Cainan:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_10::
    .string "And Enos lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Cainan eight hundred and fifteen\l"
    .string "years, and begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_11::
    .string "And all the days of Enos were nine\n"
    .string "hundred and five years: and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_12::
    .string "And Cainan lived seventy years and\n"
    .string "begat Mahalaleel:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_13::
    .string "And Cainan lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Mahalaleel eight hundred and forty\l"
    .string "years, and begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_14::
    .string "And all the days of Cainan were\n"
    .string "nine hundred and ten years: and he\l"
    .string "died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_15::
    .string "And Mahalaleel lived sixty and\n"
    .string "five years, and begat Jared:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_16::
    .string "And Mahalaleel lived after he\n"
    .string "begat Jared eight hundred and thirty\l"
    .string "years, and begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_17::
    .string "And all the days of Mahalaleel\n"
    .string "were eight hundred ninety and five\l"
    .string "years: and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_18::
    .string "And Jared lived an hundred sixty\n"
    .string "and two years, and he begat Enoch:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_19::
    .string "And Jared lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Enoch eight hundred years, and begat\l"
    .string "sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_20::
    .string "And all the days of Jared were nine\n"
    .string "hundred sixty and two years: and he\l"
    .string "died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_21::
    .string "And Enoch lived sixty and five\n"
    .string "years, and begat Methuselah:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_22::
    .string "And Enoch walked with God after he\n"
    .string "begat Methuselah three hundred\l"
    .string "years, and begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_23::
    .string "And all the days of Enoch were\n"
    .string "three hundred sixty and five years:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_24::
    .string "And Enoch walked with God: and he\n"
    .string "was not; for God took him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_25::
    .string "And Methuselah lived an hundred\n"
    .string "eighty and seven years, and begat\l"
    .string "Lamech.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_26::
    .string "And Methuselah lived after he\n"
    .string "begat Lamech seven hundred eighty\l"
    .string "and two years, and begat sons and\l"
    .string "daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_27::
    .string "And all the days of Methuselah\n"
    .string "were nine hundred sixty and nine\l"
    .string "years: and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_28::
    .string "And Lamech lived an hundred eighty\n"
    .string "and two years, and begat a son:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_29::
    .string "And he called his name Noah,\n"
    .string "saying, This same shall comfort us\l"
    .string "concerning our work and toil of our\l"
    .string "hands, because of the ground which\l"
    .string "the LORD hath cursed$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_30::
    .string "And Lamech lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Noah five hundred ninety and five\l"
    .string "years, and begat sons and daughters:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_31::
    .string "And all the days of Lamech were\n"
    .string "seven hundred seventy and seven\l"
    .string "years: and he died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_5_32::
    .string "And Noah was five hundred years\n"
    .string "old: and Noah begat Shem, Ham, and\l"
    .string "Japheth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when men began\n"
    .string "to multiply on the face of the\l"
    .string "earth, and daughters were born unto\l"
    .string "them,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_2::
    .string "That the sons of God saw the\n"
    .string "daughters of men that they were fair;\l"
    .string "and they took them wives of all\l"
    .string "which they chose$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_3::
    .string "And the LORD said, My spirit shall\n"
    .string "not always strive with man, for that\l"
    .string "he also is flesh: yet his days\l"
    .string "shall be an hundred and twenty\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_4::
    .string "There were giants in the earth in\n"
    .string "those days; and also after that,\l"
    .string "when the sons of God came in unto the\l"
    .string "daughters of men, and they bare\l"
    .string "children to them, the same became\l"
    .string "mighty men which were of old, men of\l"
    .string "renown.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_5::
    .string "And God saw that the wickedness of\n"
    .string "man was great in the earth, and that\l"
    .string "every imagination of the thoughts of\l"
    .string "his heart was only evil\l"
    .string "continually.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_6::
    .string "And it repented the LORD that he\n"
    .string "had made man on the earth, and it\l"
    .string "grieved him at his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_7::
    .string "And the LORD said, I will destroy\n"
    .string "man whom I have created from the face\l"
    .string "of the earth; both man, and beast, and\l"
    .string "the creeping thing, and the fowls of\l"
    .string "the air; for it repenteth me that I\l"
    .string "have made them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_8::
    .string "But Noah found grace in the eyes of\n"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_9::
    .string "These are the generations of Noah:\n"
    .string "Noah was a just man and perfect in\l"
    .string "his generations, and Noah walked\l"
    .string "with God.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_10::
    .string "And Noah begat three sons, Shem,\n"
    .string "Ham, and Japheth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_11::
    .string "The earth also was corrupt before\n"
    .string "God, and the earth was filled with\l"
    .string "violence.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_12::
    .string "And God looked upon the earth, and,\n"
    .string "behold, it was corrupt; for all\l"
    .string "flesh had corrupted his way upon\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_13::
    .string "And God said unto Noah, The end of\n"
    .string "all flesh is come before me; for\l"
    .string "the earth is filled with violence\l"
    .string "through them; and, behold, I will\l"
    .string "destroy them with the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_14::
    .string "Make thee an ark of gopher wood;\n"
    .string "rooms shalt thou make in the ark, and\l"
    .string "shalt pitch it within and without\l"
    .string "with pitch.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_15::
    .string "And this is the fashion which thou\n"
    .string "shalt make it of: The length of the\l"
    .string "ark shall be three hundred cubits,\l"
    .string "the breadth of it fifty cubits, and\l"
    .string "the height of it thirty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_16::
    .string "A window shalt thou make to the ark,\n"
    .string "and in a cubit shalt thou finish it\l"
    .string "above; and the door of the ark shalt\l"
    .string "thou set in the side thereof; with\l"
    .string "lower, second, and third stories\l"
    .string "shalt thou make it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_17::
    .string "And, behold, I, even I, do bring a\n"
    .string "flood of waters upon the earth, to\l"
    .string "destroy all flesh, wherein is the\l"
    .string "breath of life, from under heaven;\l"
    .string "and every thing that is in the earth\l"
    .string "shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_18::
    .string "But with thee will I establish my\n"
    .string "covenant; and thou shalt come into\l"
    .string "the ark, thou, and thy sons, and thy\l"
    .string "wife, and thy sons’ wives with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_19::
    .string "And of every living thing of all\n"
    .string "flesh, two of every sort shalt thou\l"
    .string "bring into the ark, to keep them\l"
    .string "alive with thee; they shall be\l"
    .string "male and female.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_20::
    .string "Of fowls after their kind, and of\n"
    .string "cattle after their kind, of every\l"
    .string "creeping thing of the earth after\l"
    .string "his kind, two of every sort shall\l"
    .string "come unto thee, to keep them alive.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_21::
    .string "And take thou unto thee of all food\n"
    .string "that is eaten, and thou shalt gather\l"
    .string "it to thee; and it shall be for food\l"
    .string "for thee, and for them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_6_22::
    .string "Thus did Noah; according to all\n"
    .string "that God commanded him, so did he.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Noah, Come\n"
    .string "thou and all thy house into the ark;\l"
    .string "for thee have I seen righteous before\l"
    .string "me in this generation.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_2::
    .string "Of every clean beast thou shalt\n"
    .string "take to thee by sevens, the male and\l"
    .string "his female: and of beasts that are\l"
    .string "not clean by two, the male and his\l"
    .string "female.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_3::
    .string "Of fowls also of the air by sevens,\n"
    .string "the male and the female; to keep\l"
    .string "seed alive upon the face of all\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_4::
    .string "For yet seven days, and I will\n"
    .string "cause it to rain upon the earth\l"
    .string "forty days and forty nights; and\l"
    .string "every living substance that I have\l"
    .string "made will I destroy from off the\l"
    .string "face of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_5::
    .string "And Noah did according unto all\n"
    .string "that the LORD commanded him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_6::
    .string "And Noah was six hundred years old\n"
    .string "when the flood of waters was upon\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_7::
    .string "And Noah went in, and his sons, and\n"
    .string "his wife, and his sons’ wives with\l"
    .string "him, into the ark, because of the\l"
    .string "waters of the flood.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_8::
    .string "Of clean beasts, and of beasts that\n"
    .string "are not clean, and of fowls, and of\l"
    .string "every thing that creepeth upon the\l"
    .string "earth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_9::
    .string "There went in two and two unto Noah\n"
    .string "into the ark, the male and the\l"
    .string "female, as God had commanded Noah$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_10::
    .string "And it came to pass after seven\n"
    .string "days, that the waters of the flood\l"
    .string "were upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_11::
    .string "In the six hundredth year of Noah’s\n"
    .string "life, in the second month, the\l"
    .string "seventeenth day of the month, the\l"
    .string "same day were all the fountains of\l"
    .string "the great deep broken up, and the\l"
    .string "windows of heaven were opened.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_12::
    .string "And the rain was upon the earth\n"
    .string "forty days and forty nights.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_13::
    .string "In the selfsame day entered Noah,\n"
    .string "and Shem, and Ham, and Japheth, the\l"
    .string "sons of Noah, and Noah’s wife, and\l"
    .string "the three wives of his sons with\l"
    .string "them, into the ark;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_14::
    .string "They, and every beast after his\n"
    .string "kind, and all the cattle after\l"
    .string "their kind, and every creeping thing\l"
    .string "that creepeth upon the earth after\l"
    .string "his kind, and every fowl after his\l"
    .string "kind, every bird of every sort$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_15::
    .string "And they went in unto Noah into the\n"
    .string "ark, two and two of all flesh,\l"
    .string "wherein is the breath of life.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_16::
    .string "And they that went in, went in male\n"
    .string "and female of all flesh, as God had\l"
    .string "commanded him: and the LORD shut him\l"
    .string "in.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_17::
    .string "And the flood was forty days upon\n"
    .string "the earth; and the waters increased,\l"
    .string "and bare up the ark, and it was lift\l"
    .string "up above the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_18::
    .string "And the waters prevailed, and were\n"
    .string "increased greatly upon the earth;\l"
    .string "and the ark went upon the face of the\l"
    .string "waters.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_19::
    .string "And the waters prevailed\n"
    .string "exceedingly upon the earth; and\l"
    .string "all the high hills, that were\l"
    .string "under the whole heaven, were covered.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_20::
    .string "Fifteen cubits upward did the\n"
    .string "waters prevail; and the mountains\l"
    .string "were covered.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_21::
    .string "And all flesh died that moved\n"
    .string "upon the earth, both of fowl, and of\l"
    .string "cattle, and of beast, and of every\l"
    .string "creeping thing that creepeth upon\l"
    .string "the earth, and every man:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_22::
    .string "All in whose nostrils was the\n"
    .string "breath of life, of all that was in\l"
    .string "the dry land, died$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_23::
    .string "And every living substance was\n"
    .string "destroyed which was upon the face of\l"
    .string "the ground, both man, and cattle, and\l"
    .string "the creeping things, and the fowl of\l"
    .string "the heaven; and they were destroyed\l"
    .string "from the earth: and Noah only\l"
    .string "remained alive, and they that were\l"
    .string "with him in the ark.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_7_24::
    .string "And the waters prevailed upon the\n"
    .string "earth an hundred and fifty days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_1::
    .string "And God remembered Noah, and every\n"
    .string "living thing, and all the cattle\l"
    .string "that was with him in the ark: and God\l"
    .string "made a wind to pass over the earth,\l"
    .string "and the waters asswaged;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_2::
    .string "The fountains also of the deep and\n"
    .string "the windows of heaven were stopped,\l"
    .string "and the rain from heaven was\l"
    .string "restrained;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_3::
    .string "And the waters returned from off the\n"
    .string "earth continually: and after the\l"
    .string "end of the hundred and fifty days the\l"
    .string "waters were abated$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_4::
    .string "And the ark rested in the seventh\n"
    .string "month, on the seventeenth day of the\l"
    .string "month, upon the mountains of Ararat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_5::
    .string "And the waters decreased\n"
    .string "continually until the tenth month:\l"
    .string "in the tenth month, on the first day\l"
    .string "of the month, were the tops of the\l"
    .string "mountains seen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_6::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "forty days, that Noah opened the\l"
    .string "window of the ark which he had made:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_7::
    .string "And he sent forth a raven, which\n"
    .string "went forth to and fro, until the\l"
    .string "waters were dried up from off the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_8::
    .string "Also he sent forth a dove from him,\n"
    .string "to see if the waters were abated from\l"
    .string "off the face of the ground;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_9::
    .string "But the dove found no rest for the\n"
    .string "sole of her foot, and she returned\l"
    .string "unto him into the ark, for the waters\l"
    .string "were on the face of the whole earth:\l"
    .string "then he put forth his hand, and took\l"
    .string "her, and pulled her in unto him\l"
    .string "into the ark$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_10::
    .string "And he stayed yet other seven days;\n"
    .string "and again he sent forth the dove out\l"
    .string "of the ark;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_11::
    .string "And the dove came in to him in the\n"
    .string "evening; and, lo, in her mouth was an\l"
    .string "olive leaf pluckt off: so Noah\l"
    .string "knew that the waters were abated from\l"
    .string "off the earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_12::
    .string "And he stayed yet other seven days;\n"
    .string "and sent forth the dove; which\l"
    .string "returned not again unto him any more.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_13::
    .string "And it came to pass in the six\n"
    .string "hundredth and first year, in the\l"
    .string "first month, the first day of the\l"
    .string "month, the waters were dried up from\l"
    .string "off the earth: and Noah removed the\l"
    .string "covering of the ark, and looked, and,\l"
    .string "behold, the face of the ground was\l"
    .string "dry.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_14::
    .string "And in the second month, on the\n"
    .string "seven and twentieth day of the month,\l"
    .string "was the earth dried.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_15::
    .string "And God spake unto Noah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_16::
    .string "Go forth of the ark, thou, and thy\n"
    .string "wife, and thy sons, and thy sons’\l"
    .string "wives with thee$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_17::
    .string "Bring forth with thee every living\n"
    .string "thing that is with thee, of all\l"
    .string "flesh, both of fowl, and of cattle,\l"
    .string "and of every creeping thing that\l"
    .string "creepeth upon the earth; that they\l"
    .string "may breed abundantly in the earth,\l"
    .string "and be fruitful, and multiply\l"
    .string "upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_18::
    .string "And Noah went forth, and his sons,\n"
    .string "and his wife, and his sons’ wives\l"
    .string "with him:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_19::
    .string "Every beast, every creeping thing,\n"
    .string "and every fowl, and whatsoever\l"
    .string "creepeth upon the earth, after\l"
    .string "their kinds, went forth out of the ark$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_20::
    .string "And Noah builded an altar unto the\n"
    .string "LORD; and took of every clean beast,\l"
    .string "and of every clean fowl, and offered\l"
    .string "burnt offerings on the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_21::
    .string "And the LORD smelled a sweet\n"
    .string "savour; and the LORD said in his\l"
    .string "heart, I will not again curse the\l"
    .string "ground any more for man’s sake; for\l"
    .string "the imagination of man’s heart is\l"
    .string "evil from his youth; neither will I\l"
    .string "again smite any more every thing\l"
    .string "living, as I have done.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_8_22::
    .string "While the earth remaineth, seedtime\n"
    .string "and harvest, and cold and heat, and\l"
    .string "summer and winter, and day and night\l"
    .string "shall not cease.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_1::
    .string "And God blessed Noah and his sons,\n"
    .string "and said unto them, Be fruitful, and\l"
    .string "multiply, and replenish the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_2::
    .string "And the fear of you and the dread of\n"
    .string "you shall be upon every beast of\l"
    .string "the earth, and upon every fowl of\l"
    .string "the air, upon all that moveth upon\l"
    .string "the earth, and upon all the fishes\l"
    .string "of the sea; into your hand are they\l"
    .string "delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_3::
    .string "Every moving thing that liveth\n"
    .string "shall be meat for you; even as the\l"
    .string "green herb have I given you all\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_4::
    .string "But flesh with the life thereof,\n"
    .string "which is the blood thereof, shall\l"
    .string "ye not eat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_5::
    .string "And surely your blood of your\n"
    .string "lives will I require; at the hand of\l"
    .string "every beast will I require it, and\l"
    .string "at the hand of man; at the hand of\l"
    .string "every man’s brother will I require\l"
    .string "the life of man.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_6::
    .string "Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man\n"
    .string "shall his blood be shed: for in the\l"
    .string "image of God made he man.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_7::
    .string "And you, be ye fruitful, and\n"
    .string "multiply; bring forth abundantly\l"
    .string "in the earth, and multiply therein.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_8::
    .string "And God spake unto Noah, and to his\n"
    .string "sons with him, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_9::
    .string "And I, behold, I establish my\n"
    .string "covenant with you, and with your seed\l"
    .string "after you;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_10::
    .string "And with every living creature that\n"
    .string "is with you, of the fowl, of the\l"
    .string "cattle, and of every beast of the\l"
    .string "earth with you; from all that go out\l"
    .string "of the ark, to every beast of the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_11::
    .string "And I will establish my covenant\n"
    .string "with you, neither shall all flesh\l"
    .string "be cut off any more by the waters of a\l"
    .string "flood; neither shall there any more\l"
    .string "be a flood to destroy the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_12::
    .string "And God said, This is the token of\n"
    .string "the covenant which I make between me\l"
    .string "and you and every living creature\l"
    .string "that is with you, for perpetual\l"
    .string "generations:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_13::
    .string "I do set my bow in the cloud, and it\n"
    .string "shall be for a token of a covenant\l"
    .string "between me and the earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_14::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when I\n"
    .string "bring a cloud over the earth, that\l"
    .string "the bow shall be seen in the cloud:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_15::
    .string "And I will remember my covenant,\n"
    .string "which is between me and you and every\l"
    .string "living creature of all flesh; and\l"
    .string "the waters shall no more become a\l"
    .string "flood to destroy all flesh$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_16::
    .string "And the bow shall be in the cloud;\n"
    .string "and I will look upon it, that I may\l"
    .string "remember the everlasting covenant\l"
    .string "between God and every living\l"
    .string "creature of all flesh that is upon\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_17::
    .string "And God said unto Noah, This is the\n"
    .string "token of the covenant, which I have\l"
    .string "established between me and all\l"
    .string "flesh that is upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_18::
    .string "And the sons of Noah, that went\n"
    .string "forth of the ark, were Shem, and Ham,\l"
    .string "and Japheth: and Ham is the father of\l"
    .string "Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_19::
    .string "These are the three sons of Noah:\n"
    .string "and of them was the whole earth\l"
    .string "overspread.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_20::
    .string "And Noah began to be an husbandman,\n"
    .string "and he planted a vineyard:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_21::
    .string "And he drank of the wine, and was\n"
    .string "drunken; and he was uncovered within\l"
    .string "his tent$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_22::
    .string "And Ham, the father of Canaan, saw\n"
    .string "the nakedness of his father, and\l"
    .string "told his two brethren without.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_23::
    .string "And Shem and Japheth took a\n"
    .string "garment, and laid it upon both their\l"
    .string "shoulders, and went backward, and\l"
    .string "covered the nakedness of their\l"
    .string "father; and their faces were\l"
    .string "backward, and they saw not their\l"
    .string "father’s nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_24::
    .string "And Noah awoke from his wine, and\n"
    .string "knew what his younger son had done\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_25::
    .string "And he said, Cursed be Canaan; a\n"
    .string "servant of servants shall he be\l"
    .string "unto his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_26::
    .string "And he said, Blessed be the LORD God\n"
    .string "of Shem; and Canaan shall be his\l"
    .string "servant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_27::
    .string "God shall enlarge Japheth, and he\n"
    .string "shall dwell in the tents of Shem;\l"
    .string "and Canaan shall be his servant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_28::
    .string "And Noah lived after the flood\n"
    .string "three hundred and fifty years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_9_29::
    .string "And all the days of Noah were nine\n"
    .string "hundred and fifty years: and he died.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_1::
    .string "Now these are the generations of the\n"
    .string "sons of Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth:\l"
    .string "and unto them were sons born after\l"
    .string "the flood.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_2::
    .string "The sons of Japheth; Gomer, and\n"
    .string "Magog, and Madai, and Javan, and\l"
    .string "Tubal, and Meshech, and Tiras.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_3::
    .string "And the sons of Gomer; Ashkenaz, and\n"
    .string "Riphath, and Togarmah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_4::
    .string "And the sons of Javan; Elishah, and\n"
    .string "Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_5::
    .string "By these were the isles of the\n"
    .string "Gentiles divided in their lands;\l"
    .string "every one after his tongue, after\l"
    .string "their families, in their nations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_6::
    .string "And the sons of Ham; Cush, and\n"
    .string "Mizraim, and Phut, and Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_7::
    .string "And the sons of Cush; Seba, and\n"
    .string "Havilah, and Sabtah, and Raamah, and\l"
    .string "Sabtechah: and the sons of Raamah;\l"
    .string "Sheba, and Dedan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_8::
    .string "And Cush begat Nimrod: he began to\n"
    .string "be a mighty one in the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_9::
    .string "He was a mighty hunter before the\n"
    .string "LORD: wherefore it is said, Even as\l"
    .string "Nimrod the mighty hunter before the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_10::
    .string "And the beginning of his kingdom was\n"
    .string "Babel, and Erech, and Accad, and\l"
    .string "Calneh, in the land of Shinar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_11::
    .string "Out of that land went forth Asshur,\n"
    .string "and builded Nineveh, and the city\l"
    .string "Rehoboth, and Calah,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_12::
    .string "And Resen between Nineveh and\n"
    .string "Calah: the same is a great city$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_13::
    .string "And Mizraim begat Ludim, and Anamim,\n"
    .string "and Lehabim, and Naphtuhim,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_14::
    .string "And Pathrusim, and Casluhim, (out\n"
    .string "of whom came Philistim,) and\l"
    .string "Caphtorim$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_15::
    .string "And Canaan begat Sidon his first\n"
    .string "born, and Heth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_16::
    .string "And the Jebusite, and the Amorite,\n"
    .string "and the Girgasite,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_17::
    .string "And the Hivite, and the Arkite, and\n"
    .string "the Sinite,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_18::
    .string "And the Arvadite, and the Zemarite,\n"
    .string "and the Hamathite: and afterward were\l"
    .string "the families of the Canaanites\l"
    .string "spread abroad$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_19::
    .string "And the border of the Canaanites was\n"
    .string "from Sidon, as thou comest to Gerar,\l"
    .string "unto Gaza; as thou goest, unto Sodom,\l"
    .string "and Gomorrah, and Admah, and Zeboim,\l"
    .string "even unto Lasha.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_20::
    .string "These are the sons of Ham, after\n"
    .string "their families, after their tongues,\l"
    .string "in their countries, and in their\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_21::
    .string "Unto Shem also, the father of all\n"
    .string "the children of Eber, the brother of\l"
    .string "Japheth the elder, even to him were\l"
    .string "children born.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_22::
    .string "The children of Shem; Elam, and\n"
    .string "Asshur, and Arphaxad, and Lud, and\l"
    .string "Aram.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_23::
    .string "And the children of Aram; Uz, and\n"
    .string "Hul, and Gether, and Mash.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_24::
    .string "And Arphaxad begat Salah; and\n"
    .string "Salah begat Eber.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_25::
    .string "And unto Eber were born two sons:\n"
    .string "the name of one was Peleg; for in his\l"
    .string "days was the earth divided; and his\l"
    .string "brother’s name was Joktan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_26::
    .string "And Joktan begat Almodad, and\n"
    .string "Sheleph, and Hazarmaveth, and\l"
    .string "Jerah,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_27::
    .string "And Hadoram, and Uzal, and Diklah,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_28::
    .string "And Obal, and Abimael, and Sheba,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_29::
    .string "And Ophir, and Havilah, and Jobab:\n"
    .string "all these were the sons of Joktan$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_30::
    .string "And their dwelling was from Mesha,\n"
    .string "as thou goest unto Sephar a mount of\l"
    .string "the east.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_31::
    .string "These are the sons of Shem, after\n"
    .string "their families, after their tongues,\l"
    .string "in their lands, after their nations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_10_32::
    .string "These are the families of the sons\n"
    .string "of Noah, after their generations, in\l"
    .string "their nations: and by these were the\l"
    .string "nations divided in the earth after\l"
    .string "the flood.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_1::
    .string "And the whole earth was of one\n"
    .string "language, and of one speech.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they\n"
    .string "journeyed from the east, that they\l"
    .string "found a plain in the land of\l"
    .string "Shinar; and they dwelt there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_3::
    .string "And they said one to another, Go to,\n"
    .string "let us make brick, and burn them\l"
    .string "thoroughly. And they had brick for\l"
    .string "stone, and slime had they for morter.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_4::
    .string "And they said, Go to, let us build\n"
    .string "us a city and a tower, whose top may\l"
    .string "reach unto heaven; and let us make us\l"
    .string "a name, lest we be scattered abroad\l"
    .string "upon the face of the whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_5::
    .string "And the LORD came down to see the\n"
    .string "city and the tower, which the\l"
    .string "children of men builded.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_6::
    .string "And the LORD said, Behold, the\n"
    .string "people is one, and they have all\l"
    .string "one language; and this they begin to\l"
    .string "do: and now nothing will be\l"
    .string "restrained from them, which they have\l"
    .string "imagined to do.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_7::
    .string "Go to, let us go down, and there\n"
    .string "confound their language, that they\l"
    .string "may not understand one another’s\l"
    .string "speech.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_8::
    .string "So the LORD scattered them abroad\n"
    .string "from thence upon the face of all\l"
    .string "the earth: and they left off to\l"
    .string "build the city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_9::
    .string "Therefore is the name of it called\n"
    .string "Babel; because the LORD did there\l"
    .string "confound the language of all the\l"
    .string "earth: and from thence did the LORD\l"
    .string "scatter them abroad upon the face of\l"
    .string "all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_10::
    .string "These are the generations of Shem:\n"
    .string "Shem was an hundred years old, and\l"
    .string "begat Arphaxad two years after the\l"
    .string "flood:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_11::
    .string "And Shem lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Arphaxad five hundred years, and\l"
    .string "begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_12::
    .string "And Arphaxad lived five and thirty\n"
    .string "years, and begat Salah:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_13::
    .string "And Arphaxad lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Salah four hundred and three years,\l"
    .string "and begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_14::
    .string "And Salah lived thirty years, and\n"
    .string "begat Eber:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_15::
    .string "And Salah lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Eber four hundred and three years,\l"
    .string "and begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_16::
    .string "And Eber lived four and thirty\n"
    .string "years, and begat Peleg:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_17::
    .string "And Eber lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Peleg four hundred and thirty years,\l"
    .string "and begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_18::
    .string "And Peleg lived thirty years, and\n"
    .string "begat Reu:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_19::
    .string "And Peleg lived after he begat Reu\n"
    .string "two hundred and nine years, and begat\l"
    .string "sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_20::
    .string "And Reu lived two and thirty years,\n"
    .string "and begat Serug:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_21::
    .string "And Reu lived after he begat Serug\n"
    .string "two hundred and seven years, and\l"
    .string "begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_22::
    .string "And Serug lived thirty years, and\n"
    .string "begat Nahor:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_23::
    .string "And Serug lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Nahor two hundred years, and begat\l"
    .string "sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_24::
    .string "And Nahor lived nine and twenty\n"
    .string "years, and begat Terah:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_25::
    .string "And Nahor lived after he begat\n"
    .string "Terah an hundred and nineteen years,\l"
    .string "and begat sons and daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_26::
    .string "And Terah lived seventy years, and\n"
    .string "begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_27::
    .string "Now these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Terah: Terah begat Abram, Nahor, and\l"
    .string "Haran; and Haran begat Lot.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_28::
    .string "And Haran died before his father\n"
    .string "Terah in the land of his nativity, in\l"
    .string "Ur of the Chaldees.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_29::
    .string "And Abram and Nahor took them wives:\n"
    .string "the name of Abram’s wife was Sarai;\l"
    .string "and the name of Nahor’s wife,\l"
    .string "Milcah, the daughter of Haran, the\l"
    .string "father of Milcah, and the father of\l"
    .string "Iscah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_30::
    .string "But Sarai was barren; she had no\n"
    .string "child.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_31::
    .string "And Terah took Abram his son, and\n"
    .string "Lot the son of Haran his son’s son,\l"
    .string "and Sarai his daughter in law, his\l"
    .string "son Abram’s wife; and they went forth\l"
    .string "with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to\l"
    .string "go into the land of Canaan; and they\l"
    .string "came unto Haran, and dwelt there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_11_32::
    .string "And the days of Terah were two\n"
    .string "hundred and five years: and Terah\l"
    .string "died in Haran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_1::
    .string "Now the LORD had said unto Abram,\n"
    .string "Get thee out of thy country, and from\l"
    .string "thy kindred, and from thy father’s\l"
    .string "house, unto a land that I will shew\l"
    .string "thee:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_2::
    .string "And I will make of thee a great\n"
    .string "nation, and I will bless thee, and\l"
    .string "make thy name great; and thou shalt\l"
    .string "be a blessing:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_3::
    .string "And I will bless them that bless\n"
    .string "thee, and curse him that curseth\l"
    .string "thee: and in thee shall all\l"
    .string "families of the earth be blessed$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_4::
    .string "So Abram departed, as the LORD had\n"
    .string "spoken unto him; and Lot went with\l"
    .string "him: and Abram was seventy and five\l"
    .string "years old when he departed out of\l"
    .string "Haran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_5::
    .string "And Abram took Sarai his wife, and\n"
    .string "Lot his brother’s son, and all their\l"
    .string "substance that they had gathered, and\l"
    .string "the souls that they had gotten in\l"
    .string "Haran; and they went forth to go into\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan; and into the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan they came.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_6::
    .string "And Abram passed through the land\n"
    .string "unto the place of Sichem, unto the\l"
    .string "plain of Moreh. And the Canaanite\l"
    .string "was then in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_7::
    .string "And the LORD appeared unto Abram,\n"
    .string "and said, Unto thy seed will I give\l"
    .string "this land: and there builded he an\l"
    .string "altar unto the LORD, who appeared\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_8::
    .string "And he removed from thence unto a\n"
    .string "mountain on the east of Bethel, and\l"
    .string "pitched his tent, having Bethel on\l"
    .string "the west, and Hai on the east: and\l"
    .string "there he builded an altar unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, and called upon the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_9::
    .string "And Abram journeyed, going on\n"
    .string "still toward the south.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_10::
    .string "And there was a famine in the land:\n"
    .string "and Abram went down into Egypt to\l"
    .string "sojourn there; for the famine was\l"
    .string "grievous in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he was\n"
    .string "come near to enter into Egypt, that\l"
    .string "he said unto Sarai his wife, Behold\l"
    .string "now, I know that thou art a fair woman\l"
    .string "to look upon:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_12::
    .string "Therefore it shall come to pass,\n"
    .string "when the Egyptians shall see thee,\l"
    .string "that they shall say, This is his\l"
    .string "wife: and they will kill me, but\l"
    .string "they will save thee alive$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_13::
    .string "Say, I pray thee, thou art my\n"
    .string "sister: that it may be well with me\l"
    .string "for thy sake; and my soul shall\l"
    .string "live because of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_14::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when\n"
    .string "Abram was come into Egypt, the\l"
    .string "Egyptians beheld the woman that she\l"
    .string "was very fair.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_15::
    .string "The princes also of Pharaoh saw\n"
    .string "her, and commended her before\l"
    .string "Pharaoh: and the woman was taken into\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_16::
    .string "And he entreated Abram well for\n"
    .string "her sake: and he had sheep, and oxen,\l"
    .string "and he asses, and menservants, and\l"
    .string "maidservants, and she asses, and\l"
    .string "camels.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_17::
    .string "And the LORD plagued Pharaoh and\n"
    .string "his house with great plagues\l"
    .string "because of Sarai Abram’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_18::
    .string "And Pharaoh called Abram and said,\n"
    .string "What is this that thou hast done unto\l"
    .string "me? why didst thou not tell me that\l"
    .string "she was thy wife?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_19::
    .string "Why saidst thou, She is my sister?\n"
    .string "so I might have taken her to me to\l"
    .string "wife: now therefore behold thy wife,\l"
    .string "take her, and go thy way$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_12_20::
    .string "And Pharaoh commanded his men\n"
    .string "concerning him: and they sent him\l"
    .string "away, and his wife, and all that he\l"
    .string "had.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_1::
    .string "And Abram went up out of Egypt, he,\n"
    .string "and his wife, and all that he had,\l"
    .string "and Lot with him, into the south.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_2::
    .string "And Abram was very rich in cattle,\n"
    .string "in silver, and in gold.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_3::
    .string "And he went on his journeys from the\n"
    .string "south even to Bethel, unto the\l"
    .string "place where his tent had been at the\l"
    .string "beginning, between Bethel and Hai;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_4::
    .string "Unto the place of the altar, which\n"
    .string "he had made there at the first: and\l"
    .string "there Abram called on the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_5::
    .string "And Lot also, which went with\n"
    .string "Abram, had flocks, and herds, and\l"
    .string "tents.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_6::
    .string "And the land was not able to bear\n"
    .string "them, that they might dwell\l"
    .string "together: for their substance was\l"
    .string "great, so that they could not dwell\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_7::
    .string "And there was a strife between the\n"
    .string "herdmen of Abram’s cattle and the\l"
    .string "herdmen of Lot’s cattle: and the\l"
    .string "Canaanite and the Perizzite dwelled\l"
    .string "then in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_8::
    .string "And Abram said unto Lot, Let there\n"
    .string "be no strife, I pray thee, between me\l"
    .string "and thee, and between my herdmen and\l"
    .string "thy herdmen; for we be brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_9::
    .string "Is not the whole land before thee?\n"
    .string "separate thyself, I pray thee, from\l"
    .string "me: if thou wilt take the left hand,\l"
    .string "then I will go to the right; or if\l"
    .string "thou depart to the right hand, then I\l"
    .string "will go to the left.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_10::
    .string "And Lot lifted up his eyes, and\n"
    .string "beheld all the plain of Jordan,\l"
    .string "that it was well watered every\l"
    .string "where, before the LORD destroyed\l"
    .string "Sodom and Gomorrah, even as the\l"
    .string "garden of the LORD, like the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, as thou comest unto Zoar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_11::
    .string "Then Lot chose him all the plain\n"
    .string "of Jordan; and Lot journeyed east:\l"
    .string "and they separated themselves the\l"
    .string "one from the other.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_12::
    .string "Abram dwelled in the land of\n"
    .string "Canaan, and Lot dwelled in the\l"
    .string "cities of the plain, and pitched\l"
    .string "his tent toward Sodom.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_13::
    .string "But the men of Sodom were wicked and\n"
    .string "sinners before the LORD exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_14::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Abram, after\n"
    .string "that Lot was separated from him,\l"
    .string "Lift up now thine eyes, and look\l"
    .string "from the place where thou art\l"
    .string "northward, and southward, and\l"
    .string "eastward, and westward:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_15::
    .string "For all the land which thou seest,\n"
    .string "to thee will I give it, and to thy\l"
    .string "seed for ever$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_16::
    .string "And I will make thy seed as the\n"
    .string "dust of the earth: so that if a man\l"
    .string "can number the dust of the earth,\l"
    .string "then shall thy seed also be\l"
    .string "numbered.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_17::
    .string "Arise, walk through the land in the\n"
    .string "length of it and in the breadth of it;\l"
    .string "for I will give it unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_13_18::
    .string "Then Abram removed his tent, and\n"
    .string "came and dwelt in the plain of\l"
    .string "Mamre, which is in Hebron, and built\l"
    .string "there an altar unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the days of\n"
    .string "Amraphel king of Shinar, Arioch\l"
    .string "king of Ellasar, Chedorlaomer king\l"
    .string "of Elam, and Tidal king of nations;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_2::
    .string "That these made war with Bera king\n"
    .string "of Sodom, and with Birsha king of\l"
    .string "Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, and\l"
    .string "Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the\l"
    .string "king of Bela, which is Zoar$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_3::
    .string "All these were joined together in\n"
    .string "the vale of Siddim, which is the\l"
    .string "salt sea.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_4::
    .string "Twelve years they served\n"
    .string "Chedorlaomer, and in the thirteenth\l"
    .string "year they rebelled.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_5::
    .string "And in the fourteenth year came\n"
    .string "Chedorlaomer, and the kings that\l"
    .string "were with him, and smote the\l"
    .string "Rephaims in Ashteroth Karnaim, and\l"
    .string "the Zuzims in Ham, and the Emins in\l"
    .string "Shaveh Kiriathaim,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_6::
    .string "And the Horites in their mount Seir,\n"
    .string "unto Elparan, which is by the\l"
    .string "wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_7::
    .string "And they returned, and came to\n"
    .string "Enmishpat, which is Kadesh, and\l"
    .string "smote all the country of the\l"
    .string "Amalekites, and also the Amorites,\l"
    .string "that dwelt in Hazezontamar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_8::
    .string "And there went out the king of\n"
    .string "Sodom, and the king of Gomorrah, and\l"
    .string "the king of Admah, and the king of\l"
    .string "Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (the\l"
    .string "same is Zoar;) and they joined\l"
    .string "battle with them in the vale of\l"
    .string "Siddim;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_9::
    .string "With Chedorlaomer the king of\n"
    .string "Elam, and with Tidal king of\l"
    .string "nations, and Amraphel king of\l"
    .string "Shinar, and Arioch king of Ellasar;\l"
    .string "four kings with five$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_10::
    .string "And the vale of Siddim was full of\n"
    .string "slimepits; and the kings of Sodom\l"
    .string "and Gomorrah fled, and fell there;\l"
    .string "and they that remained fled to the\l"
    .string "mountain.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_11::
    .string "And they took all the goods of\n"
    .string "Sodom and Gomorrah, and all their\l"
    .string "victuals, and went their way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_12::
    .string "And they took Lot, Abram’s brother’s\n"
    .string "son, who dwelt in Sodom, and his\l"
    .string "goods, and departed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_13::
    .string "And there came one that had\n"
    .string "escaped, and told Abram the Hebrew;\l"
    .string "for he dwelt in the plain of Mamre\l"
    .string "the Amorite, brother of Eshcol, and\l"
    .string "brother of Aner: and these were\l"
    .string "confederate with Abram.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_14::
    .string "And when Abram heard that his\n"
    .string "brother was taken captive, he armed\l"
    .string "his trained servants, born in his own\l"
    .string "house, three hundred and eighteen,\l"
    .string "and pursued them unto Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_15::
    .string "And he divided himself against\n"
    .string "them, he and his servants, by night,\l"
    .string "and smote them, and pursued them\l"
    .string "unto Hobah, which is on the left hand\l"
    .string "of Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_16::
    .string "And he brought back all the goods,\n"
    .string "and also brought again his brother\l"
    .string "Lot, and his goods, and the women\l"
    .string "also, and the people.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_17::
    .string "And the king of Sodom went out to\n"
    .string "meet him after his return from the\l"
    .string "slaughter of Chedorlaomer, and of\l"
    .string "the kings that were with him, at the\l"
    .string "valley of Shaveh, which is the\l"
    .string "king’s dale.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_18::
    .string "And Melchizedek king of Salem\n"
    .string "brought forth bread and wine: and he\l"
    .string "was the priest of the most high God.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_19::
    .string "And he blessed him, and said,\n"
    .string "Blessed be Abram of the most high\l"
    .string "God, possessor of heaven and earth:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_20::
    .string "And blessed be the most high God,\n"
    .string "which hath delivered thine enemies\l"
    .string "into thy hand. And he gave him tithes\l"
    .string "of all$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_21::
    .string "And the king of Sodom said unto\n"
    .string "Abram, Give me the persons, and take\l"
    .string "the goods to thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_22::
    .string "And Abram said to the king of Sodom,\n"
    .string "I have lift up mine hand unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, the most high God, the\l"
    .string "possessor of heaven and earth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_23::
    .string "That I will not take from a thread\n"
    .string "even to a shoelatchet, and that I\l"
    .string "will not take any thing that is\l"
    .string "thine, lest thou shouldest say, I\l"
    .string "have made Abram rich:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_14_24::
    .string "Save only that which the young men\n"
    .string "have eaten, and the portion of the\l"
    .string "men which went with me, Aner, Eshcol,\l"
    .string "and Mamre; let them take their\l"
    .string "portion$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_1::
    .string "After these things the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD came unto Abram in a vision,\l"
    .string "saying, Fear not, Abram: I am thy\l"
    .string "shield, and thy exceeding great\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_2::
    .string "And Abram said, LORD God, what wilt\n"
    .string "thou give me, seeing I go childless,\l"
    .string "and the steward of my house is this\l"
    .string "Eliezer of Damascus?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_3::
    .string "And Abram said, Behold, to me thou\n"
    .string "hast given no seed: and, lo, one born\l"
    .string "in my house is mine heir$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_4::
    .string "And, behold, the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "came unto him, saying, This shall\l"
    .string "not be thine heir; but he that shall\l"
    .string "come forth out of thine own bowels\l"
    .string "shall be thine heir.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_5::
    .string "And he brought him forth abroad, and\n"
    .string "said, Look now toward heaven, and\l"
    .string "tell the stars, if thou be able to\l"
    .string "number them: and he said unto him, So\l"
    .string "shall thy seed be.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_6::
    .string "And he believed in the LORD; and he\n"
    .string "counted it to him for righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_7::
    .string "And he said unto him, I am the LORD\n"
    .string "that brought thee out of Ur of the\l"
    .string "Chaldees, to give thee this land to\l"
    .string "inherit it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_8::
    .string "And he said, LORD God, whereby\n"
    .string "shall I know that I shall inherit\l"
    .string "it?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_9::
    .string "And he said unto him, Take me an\n"
    .string "heifer of three years old, and a she\l"
    .string "goat of three years old, and a ram of\l"
    .string "three years old, and a turtledove,\l"
    .string "and a young pigeon$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_10::
    .string "And he took unto him all these, and\n"
    .string "divided them in the midst, and laid\l"
    .string "each piece one against another: but\l"
    .string "the birds divided he not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_11::
    .string "And when the fowls came down upon\n"
    .string "the carcases, Abram drove them away.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_12::
    .string "And when the sun was going down, a\n"
    .string "deep sleep fell upon Abram; and,\l"
    .string "lo, an horror of great darkness fell\l"
    .string "upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_13::
    .string "And he said unto Abram, Know of a\n"
    .string "surety that thy seed shall be a\l"
    .string "stranger in a land that is not\l"
    .string "theirs, and shall serve them; and\l"
    .string "they shall afflict them four\l"
    .string "hundred years;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_14::
    .string "And also that nation, whom they\n"
    .string "shall serve, will I judge: and\l"
    .string "afterward shall they come out with\l"
    .string "great substance$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_15::
    .string "And thou shalt go to thy fathers in\n"
    .string "peace; thou shalt be buried in a good\l"
    .string "old age.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_16::
    .string "But in the fourth generation they\n"
    .string "shall come hither again: for the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the Amorites is not yet\l"
    .string "full.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when the\n"
    .string "sun went down, and it was dark,\l"
    .string "behold a smoking furnace, and a\l"
    .string "burning lamp that passed between\l"
    .string "those pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_18::
    .string "In the same day the LORD made a\n"
    .string "covenant with Abram, saying, Unto thy\l"
    .string "seed have I given this land, from the\l"
    .string "river of Egypt unto the great river,\l"
    .string "the river Euphrates:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_19::
    .string "The Kenites, and the Kenizzites, and\n"
    .string "the Kadmonites,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_20::
    .string "And the Hittites, and the\n"
    .string "Perizzites, and the Rephaims,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_15_21::
    .string "And the Amorites, and the\n"
    .string "Canaanites, and the Girgashites, and\l"
    .string "the Jebusites$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_1::
    .string "Now Sarai Abram’s wife bare him no\n"
    .string "children: and she had an handmaid,\l"
    .string "an Egyptian, whose name was Hagar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_2::
    .string "And Sarai said unto Abram, Behold\n"
    .string "now, the LORD hath restrained me from\l"
    .string "bearing: I pray thee, go in unto my\l"
    .string "maid; it may be that I may obtain\l"
    .string "children by her. And Abram hearkened\l"
    .string "to the voice of Sarai.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_3::
    .string "And Sarai Abram’s wife took Hagar\n"
    .string "her maid the Egyptian, after Abram\l"
    .string "had dwelt ten years in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, and gave her to her husband\l"
    .string "Abram to be his wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_4::
    .string "And he went in unto Hagar, and she\n"
    .string "conceived: and when she saw that she\l"
    .string "had conceived, her mistress was\l"
    .string "despised in her eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_5::
    .string "And Sarai said unto Abram, My wrong\n"
    .string "be upon thee: I have given my maid\l"
    .string "into thy bosom; and when she saw that\l"
    .string "she had conceived, I was despised in\l"
    .string "her eyes: the LORD judge between me\l"
    .string "and thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_6::
    .string "But Abram said unto Sarai, Behold,\n"
    .string "thy maid is in thine hand; do to her\l"
    .string "as it pleaseth thee. And when Sarai\l"
    .string "dealt hardly with her, she fled\l"
    .string "from her face.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_7::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD found her\n"
    .string "by a fountain of water in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, by the fountain in the\l"
    .string "way to Shur.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_8::
    .string "And he said, Hagar, Sarai’s maid,\n"
    .string "whence camest thou? and whither wilt\l"
    .string "thou go? And she said, I flee from\l"
    .string "the face of my mistress Sarai.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_9::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "her, Return to thy mistress, and\l"
    .string "submit thyself under her hands.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_10::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "her, I will multiply thy seed\l"
    .string "exceedingly, that it shall not be\l"
    .string "numbered for multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_11::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "her, Behold, thou art with child and\l"
    .string "shalt bear a son, and shalt call\l"
    .string "his name Ishmael; because the LORD\l"
    .string "hath heard thy affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_12::
    .string "And he will be a wild man; his hand\n"
    .string "will be against every man, and every\l"
    .string "man’s hand against him; and he shall\l"
    .string "dwell in the presence of all his\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_13::
    .string "And she called the name of the LORD\n"
    .string "that spake unto her, Thou God seest\l"
    .string "me: for she said, Have I also here\l"
    .string "looked after him that seeth me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_14::
    .string "Wherefore the well was called\n"
    .string "Beerlahairoi; behold, it is between\l"
    .string "Kadesh and Bered$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_15::
    .string "And Hagar bare Abram a son: and\n"
    .string "Abram called his son’s name, which\l"
    .string "Hagar bare, Ishmael.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_16_16::
    .string "And Abram was fourscore and six\n"
    .string "years old, when Hagar bare Ishmael\l"
    .string "to Abram.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_1::
    .string "And when Abram was ninety years old\n"
    .string "and nine, the LORD appeared to\l"
    .string "Abram, and said unto him, I am the\l"
    .string "Almighty God; walk before me, and be\l"
    .string "thou perfect.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_2::
    .string "And I will make my covenant\n"
    .string "between me and thee, and will\l"
    .string "multiply thee exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_3::
    .string "And Abram fell on his face: and God\n"
    .string "talked with him, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_4::
    .string "As for me, behold, my covenant is\n"
    .string "with thee, and thou shalt be a father\l"
    .string "of many nations$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_5::
    .string "Neither shall thy name any more be\n"
    .string "called Abram, but thy name shall\l"
    .string "be Abraham; for a father of many\l"
    .string "nations have I made thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_6::
    .string "And I will make thee exceeding\n"
    .string "fruitful, and I will make nations\l"
    .string "of thee, and kings shall come out of\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_7::
    .string "And I will establish my covenant\n"
    .string "between me and thee and thy seed\l"
    .string "after thee in their generations for\l"
    .string "an everlasting covenant, to be a God\l"
    .string "unto thee, and to thy seed after thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_8::
    .string "And I will give unto thee, and to\n"
    .string "thy seed after thee, the land\l"
    .string "wherein thou art a stranger, all the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan, for an everlasting\l"
    .string "possession; and I will be their God.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_9::
    .string "And God said unto Abraham, Thou\n"
    .string "shalt keep my covenant therefore,\l"
    .string "thou, and thy seed after thee in\l"
    .string "their generations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_10::
    .string "This is my covenant, which ye shall\n"
    .string "keep, between me and you and thy seed\l"
    .string "after thee; Every man child among\l"
    .string "you shall be circumcised.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_11::
    .string "And ye shall circumcise the flesh\n"
    .string "of your foreskin; and it shall be a\l"
    .string "token of the covenant betwixt me and\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_12::
    .string "And he that is eight days old\n"
    .string "shall be circumcised among you,\l"
    .string "every man child in your generations,\l"
    .string "he that is born in the house, or\l"
    .string "bought with money of any stranger,\l"
    .string "which is not of thy seed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_13::
    .string "He that is born in thy house, and he\n"
    .string "that is bought with thy money, must\l"
    .string "needs be circumcised: and my covenant\l"
    .string "shall be in your flesh for an\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_14::
    .string "And the uncircumcised man child\n"
    .string "whose flesh of his foreskin is not\l"
    .string "circumcised, that soul shall be cut\l"
    .string "off from his people; he hath broken\l"
    .string "my covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_15::
    .string "And God said unto Abraham, As for\n"
    .string "Sarai thy wife, thou shalt not call\l"
    .string "her name Sarai, but Sarah shall her\l"
    .string "name be.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_16::
    .string "And I will bless her, and give\n"
    .string "thee a son also of her: yea, I will\l"
    .string "bless her, and she shall be a\l"
    .string "mother of nations; kings of people\l"
    .string "shall be of her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_17::
    .string "Then Abraham fell upon his face,\n"
    .string "and laughed, and said in his heart,\l"
    .string "Shall a child be born unto him that\l"
    .string "is an hundred years old? and shall\l"
    .string "Sarah, that is ninety years old,\l"
    .string "bear?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_18::
    .string "And Abraham said unto God, O that\n"
    .string "Ishmael might live before thee!"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_19::
    .string "And God said, Sarah thy wife shall\n"
    .string "bear thee a son indeed; and thou\l"
    .string "shalt call his name Isaac: and I\l"
    .string "will establish my covenant with\l"
    .string "him for an everlasting covenant, and\l"
    .string "with his seed after him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_20::
    .string "And as for Ishmael, I have heard\n"
    .string "thee: Behold, I have blessed him,\l"
    .string "and will make him fruitful, and\l"
    .string "will multiply him exceedingly;\l"
    .string "twelve princes shall he beget, and\l"
    .string "I will make him a great nation.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_21::
    .string "But my covenant will I establish\n"
    .string "with Isaac, which Sarah shall bear\l"
    .string "unto thee at this set time in the\l"
    .string "next year.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_22::
    .string "And he left off talking with him,\n"
    .string "and God went up from Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_23::
    .string "And Abraham took Ishmael his son,\n"
    .string "and all that were born in his house,\l"
    .string "and all that were bought with his\l"
    .string "money, every male among the men of\l"
    .string "Abraham’s house; and circumcised the\l"
    .string "flesh of their foreskin in the\l"
    .string "selfsame day, as God had said unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_24::
    .string "And Abraham was ninety years old\n"
    .string "and nine, when he was circumcised in\l"
    .string "the flesh of his foreskin.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_25::
    .string "And Ishmael his son was thirteen\n"
    .string "years old, when he was circumcised\l"
    .string "in the flesh of his foreskin.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_26::
    .string "In the selfsame day was Abraham\n"
    .string "circumcised, and Ishmael his son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_17_27::
    .string "And all the men of his house, born\n"
    .string "in the house, and bought with money\l"
    .string "of the stranger, were circumcised\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_1::
    .string "And the LORD appeared unto him in\n"
    .string "the plains of Mamre: and he sat in\l"
    .string "the tent door in the heat of the day;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_2::
    .string "And he lift up his eyes and\n"
    .string "looked, and, lo, three men stood by\l"
    .string "him: and when he saw them, he ran to\l"
    .string "meet them from the tent door, and\l"
    .string "bowed himself toward the ground,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_3::
    .string "And said, My LORD, if now I have\n"
    .string "found favour in thy sight, pass not\l"
    .string "away, I pray thee, from thy servant:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_4::
    .string "Let a little water, I pray you, be\n"
    .string "fetched, and wash your feet, and rest\l"
    .string "yourselves under the tree:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_5::
    .string "And I will fetch a morsel of\n"
    .string "bread, and comfort ye your hearts;\l"
    .string "after that ye shall pass on: for\l"
    .string "therefore are ye come to your\l"
    .string "servant. And they said, So do, as thou\l"
    .string "hast said$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_6::
    .string "And Abraham hastened into the tent\n"
    .string "unto Sarah, and said, Make ready\l"
    .string "quickly three measures of fine\l"
    .string "meal, knead it, and make cakes upon\l"
    .string "the hearth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_7::
    .string "And Abraham ran unto the herd, and\n"
    .string "fetcht a calf tender and good, and\l"
    .string "gave it unto a young man; and he\l"
    .string "hasted to dress it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_8::
    .string "And he took butter, and milk, and\n"
    .string "the calf which he had dressed, and\l"
    .string "set it before them; and he stood by\l"
    .string "them under the tree, and they did eat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_9::
    .string "And they said unto him, Where is\n"
    .string "Sarah thy wife? And he said, Behold,\l"
    .string "in the tent.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_10::
    .string "And he said, I will certainly\n"
    .string "return unto thee according to the\l"
    .string "time of life; and, lo, Sarah thy\l"
    .string "wife shall have a son. And Sarah\l"
    .string "heard it in the tent door, which was\l"
    .string "behind him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_11::
    .string "Now Abraham and Sarah were old and\n"
    .string "well stricken in age; and it ceased\l"
    .string "to be with Sarah after the manner of\l"
    .string "women.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_12::
    .string "Therefore Sarah laughed within\n"
    .string "herself, saying, After I am waxed\l"
    .string "old shall I have pleasure, my\l"
    .string "lord being old also?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_13::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Abraham,\n"
    .string "Wherefore did Sarah laugh, saying,\l"
    .string "Shall I of a surety bear a child,\l"
    .string "which am old?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_14::
    .string "Is any thing too hard for the LORD?\n"
    .string "At the time appointed I will\l"
    .string "return unto thee, according to the\l"
    .string "time of life, and Sarah shall have\l"
    .string "a son$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_15::
    .string "Then Sarah denied, saying, I\n"
    .string "laughed not; for she was afraid. And\l"
    .string "he said, Nay; but thou didst laugh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_16::
    .string "And the men rose up from thence, and\n"
    .string "looked toward Sodom: and Abraham went\l"
    .string "with them to bring them on the way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_17::
    .string "And the LORD said, Shall I hide\n"
    .string "from Abraham that thing which I do;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_18::
    .string "Seeing that Abraham shall surely\n"
    .string "become a great and mighty nation, and\l"
    .string "all the nations of the earth shall\l"
    .string "be blessed in him?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_19::
    .string "For I know him, that he will\n"
    .string "command his children and his\l"
    .string "household after him, and they shall\l"
    .string "keep the way of the LORD, to do\l"
    .string "justice and judgment; that the LORD\l"
    .string "may bring upon Abraham that which he\l"
    .string "hath spoken of him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_20::
    .string "And the LORD said, Because the cry\n"
    .string "of Sodom and Gomorrah is great, and\l"
    .string "because their sin is very grievous;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_21::
    .string "I will go down now, and see whether\n"
    .string "they have done altogether according\l"
    .string "to the cry of it, which is come unto\l"
    .string "me; and if not, I will know$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_22::
    .string "And the men turned their faces from\n"
    .string "thence, and went toward Sodom: but\l"
    .string "Abraham stood yet before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_23::
    .string "And Abraham drew near, and said,\n"
    .string "Wilt thou also destroy the\l"
    .string "righteous with the wicked?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_24::
    .string "Peradventure there be fifty\n"
    .string "righteous within the city: wilt thou\l"
    .string "also destroy and not spare the\l"
    .string "place for the fifty righteous that\l"
    .string "are therein?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_25::
    .string "That be far from thee to do after\n"
    .string "this manner, to slay the righteous\l"
    .string "with the wicked: and that the\l"
    .string "righteous should be as the wicked,\l"
    .string "that be far from thee: Shall not the\l"
    .string "Judge of all the earth do right?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_26::
    .string "And the LORD said, If I find in Sodom\n"
    .string "fifty righteous within the city, then\l"
    .string "I will spare all the place for\l"
    .string "their sakes$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_27::
    .string "And Abraham answered and said,\n"
    .string "Behold now, I have taken upon me to\l"
    .string "speak unto the LORD, which am but\l"
    .string "dust and ashes:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_28::
    .string "Peradventure there shall lack\n"
    .string "five of the fifty righteous: wilt\l"
    .string "thou destroy all the city for lack\l"
    .string "of five? And he said, If I find there\l"
    .string "forty and five, I will not destroy it$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_29::
    .string "And he spake unto him yet again, and\n"
    .string "said, Peradventure there shall be\l"
    .string "forty found there. And he said, I\l"
    .string "will not do it for forty’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_30::
    .string "And he said unto him, Oh let not the\n"
    .string "LORD be angry, and I will speak:\l"
    .string "Peradventure there shall thirty be\l"
    .string "found there. And he said, I will not\l"
    .string "do it, if I find thirty there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_31::
    .string "And he said, Behold now, I have\n"
    .string "taken upon me to speak unto the\l"
    .string "LORD: Peradventure there shall be\l"
    .string "twenty found there. And he said, I\l"
    .string "will not destroy it for twenty’s\l"
    .string "sake.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_32::
    .string "And he said, Oh let not the LORD be\n"
    .string "angry, and I will speak yet but\l"
    .string "this once: Peradventure ten shall\l"
    .string "be found there. And he said, I will\l"
    .string "not destroy it for ten’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_18_33::
    .string "And the LORD went his way, as soon as\n"
    .string "he had left communing with Abraham:\l"
    .string "and Abraham returned unto his place.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_1::
    .string "And there came two angels to Sodom\n"
    .string "at even; and Lot sat in the gate of\l"
    .string "Sodom: and Lot seeing them rose up to\l"
    .string "meet them; and he bowed himself with\l"
    .string "his face toward the ground;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_2::
    .string "And he said, Behold now, my lords,\n"
    .string "turn in, I pray you, into your\l"
    .string "servant’s house, and tarry all\l"
    .string "night, and wash your feet, and ye\l"
    .string "shall rise up early, and go on your\l"
    .string "ways. And they said, Nay; but we\l"
    .string "will abide in the street all night$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_3::
    .string "And he pressed upon them greatly;\n"
    .string "and they turned in unto him, and\l"
    .string "entered into his house; and he made\l"
    .string "them a feast, and did bake\l"
    .string "unleavened bread, and they did eat.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_4::
    .string "But before they lay down, the men of\n"
    .string "the city, even the men of Sodom,\l"
    .string "compassed the house round, both old\l"
    .string "and young, all the people from\l"
    .string "every quarter:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_5::
    .string "And they called unto Lot, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Where are the men which\l"
    .string "came in to thee this night? bring\l"
    .string "them out unto us, that we may know\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_6::
    .string "And Lot went out at the door unto\n"
    .string "them, and shut the door after him,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_7::
    .string "And said, I pray you, brethren, do\n"
    .string "not so wickedly$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_8::
    .string "Behold now, I have two daughters\n"
    .string "which have not known man; let me, I\l"
    .string "pray you, bring them out unto you,\l"
    .string "and do ye to them as is good in your\l"
    .string "eyes: only unto these men do\l"
    .string "nothing; for therefore came they\l"
    .string "under the shadow of my roof.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_9::
    .string "And they said, Stand back. And they\n"
    .string "said again, This one fellow came in\l"
    .string "to sojourn, and he will needs be a\l"
    .string "judge: now will we deal worse with\l"
    .string "thee, than with them. And they\l"
    .string "pressed sore upon the man, even Lot,\l"
    .string "and came near to break the door.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_10::
    .string "But the men put forth their hand,\n"
    .string "and pulled Lot into the house to\l"
    .string "them, and shut to the door.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_11::
    .string "And they smote the men that were at\n"
    .string "the door of the house with\l"
    .string "blindness, both small and great: so\l"
    .string "that they wearied themselves to find\l"
    .string "the door.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_12::
    .string "And the men said unto Lot, Hast thou\n"
    .string "here any besides? son in law, and thy\l"
    .string "sons, and thy daughters, and\l"
    .string "whatsoever thou hast in the city,\l"
    .string "bring them out of this place:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_13::
    .string "For we will destroy this place,\n"
    .string "because the cry of them is waxen\l"
    .string "great before the face of the LORD;\l"
    .string "and the LORD hath sent us to destroy\l"
    .string "it$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_14::
    .string "And Lot went out, and spake unto his\n"
    .string "sons in law, which married his\l"
    .string "daughters, and said, Up, get you out\l"
    .string "of this place; for the LORD will\l"
    .string "destroy this city. But he seemed as\l"
    .string "one that mocked unto his sons in law.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_15::
    .string "And when the morning arose, then the\n"
    .string "angels hastened Lot, saying, Arise,\l"
    .string "take thy wife, and thy two daughters,\l"
    .string "which are here; lest thou be\l"
    .string "consumed in the iniquity of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_16::
    .string "And while he lingered, the men\n"
    .string "laid hold upon his hand, and upon\l"
    .string "the hand of his wife, and upon the\l"
    .string "hand of his two daughters; the LORD\l"
    .string "being merciful unto him: and they\l"
    .string "brought him forth, and set him\l"
    .string "without the city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they had\n"
    .string "brought them forth abroad, that he\l"
    .string "said, Escape for thy life; look not\l"
    .string "behind thee, neither stay thou in\l"
    .string "all the plain; escape to the\l"
    .string "mountain, lest thou be consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_18::
    .string "And Lot said unto them, Oh, not so,\n"
    .string "my LORD:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_19::
    .string "Behold now, thy servant hath found\n"
    .string "grace in thy sight, and thou hast\l"
    .string "magnified thy mercy, which thou hast\l"
    .string "shewed unto me in saving my life; and\l"
    .string "I cannot escape to the mountain,\l"
    .string "lest some evil take me, and I die:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_20::
    .string "Behold now, this city is near to\n"
    .string "flee unto, and it is a little one:\l"
    .string "Oh, let me escape thither, (is it\l"
    .string "not a little one?) and my soul\l"
    .string "shall live$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_21::
    .string "And he said unto him, See, I have\n"
    .string "accepted thee concerning this thing\l"
    .string "also, that I will not overthrow\l"
    .string "this city, for the which thou hast\l"
    .string "spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_22::
    .string "Haste thee, escape thither; for I\n"
    .string "cannot do anything till thou be\l"
    .string "come thither. Therefore the name of\l"
    .string "the city was called Zoar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_23::
    .string "The sun was risen upon the earth\n"
    .string "when Lot entered into Zoar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_24::
    .string "Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and\n"
    .string "upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire\l"
    .string "from the LORD out of heaven;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_25::
    .string "And he overthrew those cities, and\n"
    .string "all the plain, and all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the cities, and that\l"
    .string "which grew upon the ground$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_26::
    .string "But his wife looked back from\n"
    .string "behind him, and she became a pillar\l"
    .string "of salt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_27::
    .string "And Abraham gat up early in the\n"
    .string "morning to the place where he stood\l"
    .string "before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_28::
    .string "And he looked toward Sodom and\n"
    .string "Gomorrah, and toward all the land\l"
    .string "of the plain, and beheld, and, lo,\l"
    .string "the smoke of the country went up as\l"
    .string "the smoke of a furnace$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, when God\n"
    .string "destroyed the cities of the plain,\l"
    .string "that God remembered Abraham, and sent\l"
    .string "Lot out of the midst of the\l"
    .string "overthrow, when he overthrew the\l"
    .string "cities in the which Lot dwelt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_30::
    .string "And Lot went up out of Zoar, and\n"
    .string "dwelt in the mountain, and his two\l"
    .string "daughters with him; for he feared to\l"
    .string "dwell in Zoar: and he dwelt in a\l"
    .string "cave, he and his two daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_31::
    .string "And the firstborn said unto the\n"
    .string "younger, Our father is old, and\l"
    .string "there is not a man in the earth to\l"
    .string "come in unto us after the manner of\l"
    .string "all the earth:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_32::
    .string "Come, let us make our father drink\n"
    .string "wine, and we will lie with him,\l"
    .string "that we may preserve seed of our\l"
    .string "father$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_33::
    .string "And they made their father drink\n"
    .string "wine that night: and the firstborn\l"
    .string "went in, and lay with her father; and\l"
    .string "he perceived not when she lay down,\l"
    .string "nor when she arose.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_34::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that the firstborn said unto the\l"
    .string "younger, Behold, I lay yesternight\l"
    .string "with my father: let us make him drink\l"
    .string "wine this night also; and go thou in,\l"
    .string "and lie with him, that we may\l"
    .string "preserve seed of our father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_35::
    .string "And they made their father drink\n"
    .string "wine that night also: and the\l"
    .string "younger arose, and lay with him; and\l"
    .string "he perceived not when she lay down,\l"
    .string "nor when she arose.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_36::
    .string "Thus were both the daughters of Lot\n"
    .string "with child by their father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_37::
    .string "And the first born bare a son, and\n"
    .string "called his name Moab: the same is\l"
    .string "the father of the Moabites unto this\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_19_38::
    .string "And the younger, she also bare a\n"
    .string "son, and called his name Benammi:\l"
    .string "the same is the father of the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_1::
    .string "And Abraham journeyed from thence\n"
    .string "toward the south country, and\l"
    .string "dwelled between Kadesh and Shur,\l"
    .string "and sojourned in Gerar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_2::
    .string "And Abraham said of Sarah his wife,\n"
    .string "She is my sister: and Abimelech king\l"
    .string "of Gerar sent, and took Sarah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_3::
    .string "But God came to Abimelech in a\n"
    .string "dream by night, and said to him,\l"
    .string "Behold, thou art but a dead man, for\l"
    .string "the woman which thou hast taken; for\l"
    .string "she is a man’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_4::
    .string "But Abimelech had not come near\n"
    .string "her: and he said, LORD, wilt thou\l"
    .string "slay also a righteous nation?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_5::
    .string "Said he not unto me, She is my\n"
    .string "sister? and she, even she herself\l"
    .string "said, He is my brother: in the\l"
    .string "integrity of my heart and innocency\l"
    .string "of my hands have I done this$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_6::
    .string "And God said unto him in a dream,\n"
    .string "Yea, I know that thou didst this in\l"
    .string "the integrity of thy heart; for I\l"
    .string "also withheld thee from sinning\l"
    .string "against me: therefore suffered I thee\l"
    .string "not to touch her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_7::
    .string "Now therefore restore the man his\n"
    .string "wife; for he is a prophet, and he\l"
    .string "shall pray for thee, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt live: and if thou restore her\l"
    .string "not, know thou that thou shalt\l"
    .string "surely die, thou, and all that are\l"
    .string "thine.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_8::
    .string "Therefore Abimelech rose early in\n"
    .string "the morning, and called all his\l"
    .string "servants, and told all these things\l"
    .string "in their ears: and the men were sore\l"
    .string "afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_9::
    .string "Then Abimelech called Abraham,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, What hast thou\l"
    .string "done unto us? and what have I\l"
    .string "offended thee, that thou hast brought\l"
    .string "on me and on my kingdom a great sin?\l"
    .string "thou hast done deeds unto me that\l"
    .string "ought not to be done.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_10::
    .string "And Abimelech said unto Abraham,\n"
    .string "What sawest thou, that thou hast done\l"
    .string "this thing?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_11::
    .string "And Abraham said, Because I thought,\n"
    .string "Surely the fear of God is not in this\l"
    .string "place; and they will slay me for my\l"
    .string "wife’s sake$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_12::
    .string "And yet indeed she is my sister; she\n"
    .string "is the daughter of my father, but not\l"
    .string "the daughter of my mother; and she\l"
    .string "became my wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, when God caused\n"
    .string "me to wander from my father’s house,\l"
    .string "that I said unto her, This is thy\l"
    .string "kindness which thou shalt shew unto\l"
    .string "me; at every place whither we\l"
    .string "shall come, say of me, He is my\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_14::
    .string "And Abimelech took sheep, and\n"
    .string "oxen, and menservants, and\l"
    .string "womenservants, and gave them unto\l"
    .string "Abraham, and restored him Sarah his\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_15::
    .string "And Abimelech said, Behold, my\n"
    .string "land is before thee: dwell where it\l"
    .string "pleaseth thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_16::
    .string "And unto Sarah he said, Behold, I\n"
    .string "have given thy brother a thousand\l"
    .string "pieces of silver: behold, he is to\l"
    .string "thee a covering of the eyes, unto\l"
    .string "all that are with thee, and with\l"
    .string "all other: thus she was reproved.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_17::
    .string "So Abraham prayed unto God: and God\n"
    .string "healed Abimelech, and his wife, and\l"
    .string "his maidservants; and they bare\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_20_18::
    .string "For the LORD had fast closed up\n"
    .string "all the wombs of the house of\l"
    .string "Abimelech, because of Sarah\l"
    .string "Abraham’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_1::
    .string "And the LORD visited Sarah as he had\n"
    .string "said, and the LORD did unto Sarah as\l"
    .string "he had spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_2::
    .string "For Sarah conceived, and bare\n"
    .string "Abraham a son in his old age, at the\l"
    .string "set time of which God had spoken to\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_3::
    .string "And Abraham called the name of his\n"
    .string "son that was born unto him, whom\l"
    .string "Sarah bare to him, Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_4::
    .string "And Abraham circumcised his son\n"
    .string "Isaac being eight days old, as God\l"
    .string "had commanded him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_5::
    .string "And Abraham was an hundred years\n"
    .string "old, when his son Isaac was born unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_6::
    .string "And Sarah said, God hath made me to\n"
    .string "laugh, so that all that hear will\l"
    .string "laugh with me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_7::
    .string "And she said, Who would have said\n"
    .string "unto Abraham, that Sarah should have\l"
    .string "given children suck? for I have born\l"
    .string "him a son in his old age.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_8::
    .string "And the child grew, and was weaned:\n"
    .string "and Abraham made a great feast the\l"
    .string "same day that Isaac was weaned.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_9::
    .string "And Sarah saw the son of Hagar the\n"
    .string "Egyptian, which she had born unto\l"
    .string "Abraham, mocking.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_10::
    .string "Wherefore she said unto Abraham,\n"
    .string "Cast out this bondwoman and her son:\l"
    .string "for the son of this bondwoman shall\l"
    .string "not be heir with my son, even with\l"
    .string "Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_11::
    .string "And the thing was very grievous in\n"
    .string "Abraham’s sight because of his son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_12::
    .string "And God said unto Abraham, Let it\n"
    .string "not be grievous in thy sight because\l"
    .string "of the lad, and because of thy\l"
    .string "bondwoman; in all that Sarah hath\l"
    .string "said unto thee, hearken unto her\l"
    .string "voice; for in Isaac shall thy seed\l"
    .string "be called.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_13::
    .string "And also of the son of the\n"
    .string "bondwoman will I make a nation,\l"
    .string "because he is thy seed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_14::
    .string "And Abraham rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and took bread, and a\l"
    .string "bottle of water, and gave it unto\l"
    .string "Hagar, putting it on her shoulder,\l"
    .string "and the child, and sent her away: and\l"
    .string "she departed, and wandered in the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_15::
    .string "And the water was spent in the\n"
    .string "bottle, and she cast the child under\l"
    .string "one of the shrubs.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_16::
    .string "And she went, and sat her down over\n"
    .string "against him a good way off, as it were\l"
    .string "a bow shot: for she said, Let me not\l"
    .string "see the death of the child. And she\l"
    .string "sat over against him, and lift up\l"
    .string "her voice, and wept.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_17::
    .string "And God heard the voice of the lad;\n"
    .string "and the angel of God called to\l"
    .string "Hagar out of heaven, and said unto\l"
    .string "her, What aileth thee, Hagar? fear\l"
    .string "not; for God hath heard the voice of\l"
    .string "the lad where he is.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_18::
    .string "Arise, lift up the lad, and hold\n"
    .string "him in thine hand; for I will make\l"
    .string "him a great nation.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_19::
    .string "And God opened her eyes, and she saw\n"
    .string "a well of water; and she went, and\l"
    .string "filled the bottle with water, and\l"
    .string "gave the lad drink.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_20::
    .string "And God was with the lad; and he\n"
    .string "grew, and dwelt in the wilderness,\l"
    .string "and became an archer.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_21::
    .string "And he dwelt in the wilderness of\n"
    .string "Paran: and his mother took him a wife\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_22::
    .string "And it came to pass at that time,\n"
    .string "that Abimelech and Phichol the\l"
    .string "chief captain of his host spake\l"
    .string "unto Abraham, saying, God is with\l"
    .string "thee in all that thou doest:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_23::
    .string "Now therefore swear unto me here by\n"
    .string "God that thou wilt not deal\l"
    .string "falsely with me, nor with my son,\l"
    .string "nor with my son’s son: but according\l"
    .string "to the kindness that I have done unto\l"
    .string "thee, thou shalt do unto me, and to\l"
    .string "the land wherein thou hast sojourned$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_24::
    .string "And Abraham said, I will swear.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_25::
    .string "And Abraham reproved Abimelech\n"
    .string "because of a well of water, which\l"
    .string "Abimelech’s servants had violently\l"
    .string "taken away.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_26::
    .string "And Abimelech said, I wot not who\n"
    .string "hath done this thing; neither didst\l"
    .string "thou tell me, neither yet heard I of\l"
    .string "it, but to day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_27::
    .string "And Abraham took sheep and oxen,\n"
    .string "and gave them unto Abimelech; and\l"
    .string "both of them made a covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_28::
    .string "And Abraham set seven ewe lambs of\n"
    .string "the flock by themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_29::
    .string "And Abimelech said unto Abraham,\n"
    .string "What mean these seven ewe lambs\l"
    .string "which thou hast set by themselves?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_30::
    .string "And he said, For these seven ewe\n"
    .string "lambs shalt thou take of my hand,\l"
    .string "that they may be a witness unto me,\l"
    .string "that I have digged this well$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_31::
    .string "Wherefore he called that place\n"
    .string "Beersheba; because there they sware\l"
    .string "both of them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_32::
    .string "Thus they made a covenant at\n"
    .string "Beersheba: then Abimelech rose up,\l"
    .string "and Phichol the chief captain of\l"
    .string "his host, and they returned into the\l"
    .string "land of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_33::
    .string "And Abraham planted a grove in\n"
    .string "Beersheba, and called there on the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD, the everlasting\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_21_34::
    .string "And Abraham sojourned in the\n"
    .string "Philistines’ land many days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that God did tempt Abraham,\l"
    .string "and said unto him, Abraham: and he\l"
    .string "said, Behold, here I am.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_2::
    .string "And he said, Take now thy son, thine\n"
    .string "only son Isaac, whom thou lovest,\l"
    .string "and get thee into the land of Moriah;\l"
    .string "and offer him there for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering upon one of the mountains\l"
    .string "which I will tell thee of.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_3::
    .string "And Abraham rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and saddled his ass, and\l"
    .string "took two of his young men with him,\l"
    .string "and Isaac his son, and clave the wood\l"
    .string "for the burnt offering, and rose up,\l"
    .string "and went unto the place of which God\l"
    .string "had told him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_4::
    .string "Then on the third day Abraham\n"
    .string "lifted up his eyes, and saw the\l"
    .string "place afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_5::
    .string "And Abraham said unto his young men,\n"
    .string "Abide ye here with the ass; and I and\l"
    .string "the lad will go yonder and\l"
    .string "worship, and come again to you.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_6::
    .string "And Abraham took the wood of the\n"
    .string "burnt offering, and laid it upon\l"
    .string "Isaac his son; and he took the fire in\l"
    .string "his hand, and a knife; and they went\l"
    .string "both of them together.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_7::
    .string "And Isaac spake unto Abraham his\n"
    .string "father, and said, My father: and he\l"
    .string "said, Here am I, my son. And he said,\l"
    .string "Behold the fire and the wood: but\l"
    .string "where is the lamb for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_8::
    .string "And Abraham said, My son, God will\n"
    .string "provide himself a lamb for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering: so they went both of them\l"
    .string "together$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_9::
    .string "And they came to the place which\n"
    .string "God had told him of; and Abraham\l"
    .string "built an altar there, and laid the\l"
    .string "wood in order, and bound Isaac his\l"
    .string "son, and laid him on the altar upon\l"
    .string "the wood.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_10::
    .string "And Abraham stretched forth his\n"
    .string "hand, and took the knife to slay his\l"
    .string "son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_11::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD called\n"
    .string "unto him out of heaven, and said,\l"
    .string "Abraham, Abraham: and he said, Here\l"
    .string "am I.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_12::
    .string "And he said, Lay not thine hand upon\n"
    .string "the lad, neither do thou any thing\l"
    .string "unto him: for now I know that thou\l"
    .string "fearest God, seeing thou hast not\l"
    .string "withheld thy son, thine only son\l"
    .string "from me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_13::
    .string "And Abraham lifted up his eyes, and\n"
    .string "looked, and behold behind him a ram\l"
    .string "caught in a thicket by his horns: and\l"
    .string "Abraham went and took the ram, and\l"
    .string "offered him up for a burnt offering\l"
    .string "in the stead of his son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_14::
    .string "And Abraham called the name of\n"
    .string "that place Jehovahjireh: as it is\l"
    .string "said to this day, In the mount of the\l"
    .string "LORD it shall be seen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_15::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD called\n"
    .string "unto Abraham out of heaven the second\l"
    .string "time,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_16::
    .string "And said, By myself have I sworn,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, for because thou hast\l"
    .string "done this thing, and hast not\l"
    .string "withheld thy son, thine only son:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_17::
    .string "That in blessing I will bless\n"
    .string "thee, and in multiplying I will\l"
    .string "multiply thy seed as the stars of\l"
    .string "the heaven, and as the sand which is\l"
    .string "upon the sea shore; and thy seed\l"
    .string "shall possess the gate of his\l"
    .string "enemies;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_18::
    .string "And in thy seed shall all the\n"
    .string "nations of the earth be blessed;\l"
    .string "because thou hast obeyed my voice$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_19::
    .string "So Abraham returned unto his young\n"
    .string "men, and they rose up and went\l"
    .string "together to Beersheba; and Abraham\l"
    .string "dwelt at Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_20::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that it was told Abraham,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold, Milcah, she hath\l"
    .string "also born children unto thy brother\l"
    .string "Nahor;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_21::
    .string "Huz his firstborn, and Buz his\n"
    .string "brother, and Kemuel the father of\l"
    .string "Aram,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_22::
    .string "And Chesed, and Hazo, and Pildash,\n"
    .string "and Jidlaph, and Bethuel$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_23::
    .string "And Bethuel begat Rebekah: these\n"
    .string "eight Milcah did bear to Nahor,\l"
    .string "Abraham’s brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_22_24::
    .string "And his concubine, whose name was\n"
    .string "Reumah, she bare also Tebah, and\l"
    .string "Gaham, and Thahash, and Maachah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_1::
    .string "And Sarah was an hundred and seven\n"
    .string "and twenty years old: these were the\l"
    .string "years of the life of Sarah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_2::
    .string "And Sarah died in Kirjatharba; the\n"
    .string "same is Hebron in the land of Canaan:\l"
    .string "and Abraham came to mourn for Sarah,\l"
    .string "and to weep for her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_3::
    .string "And Abraham stood up from before\n"
    .string "his dead, and spake unto the sons of\l"
    .string "Heth, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_4::
    .string "I am a stranger and a sojourner with\n"
    .string "you: give me a possession of a\l"
    .string "buryingplace with you, that I may\l"
    .string "bury my dead out of my sight$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_5::
    .string "And the children of Heth answered\n"
    .string "Abraham, saying unto him,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_6::
    .string "Hear us, my lord: thou art a mighty\n"
    .string "prince among us: in the choice of our\l"
    .string "sepulchres bury thy dead; none of us\l"
    .string "shall withhold from thee his\l"
    .string "sepulchre, but that thou mayest\l"
    .string "bury thy dead$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_7::
    .string "And Abraham stood up, and bowed\n"
    .string "himself to the people of the land,\l"
    .string "even to the children of Heth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_8::
    .string "And he communed with them, saying,\n"
    .string "If it be your mind that I should bury\l"
    .string "my dead out of my sight; hear me, and\l"
    .string "intreat for me to Ephron the son of\l"
    .string "Zohar,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_9::
    .string "That he may give me the cave of\n"
    .string "Machpelah, which he hath, which is\l"
    .string "in the end of his field; for as much\l"
    .string "money as it is worth he shall give\l"
    .string "it me for a possession of a\l"
    .string "buryingplace amongst you$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_10::
    .string "And Ephron dwelt among the\n"
    .string "children of Heth: and Ephron the\l"
    .string "Hittite answered Abraham in the\l"
    .string "audience of the children of Heth,\l"
    .string "even of all that went in at the gate\l"
    .string "of his city, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_11::
    .string "Nay, my lord, hear me: the field\n"
    .string "give I thee, and the cave that is\l"
    .string "therein, I give it thee; in the\l"
    .string "presence of the sons of my people\l"
    .string "give I it thee: bury thy dead$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_12::
    .string "And Abraham bowed down himself\n"
    .string "before the people of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_13::
    .string "And he spake unto Ephron in the\n"
    .string "audience of the people of the\l"
    .string "land, saying, But if thou wilt give\l"
    .string "it, I pray thee, hear me: I will\l"
    .string "give thee money for the field; take\l"
    .string "it of me, and I will bury my dead\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_14::
    .string "And Ephron answered Abraham, saying\n"
    .string "unto him,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_15::
    .string "My lord, hearken unto me: the land\n"
    .string "is worth four hundred shekels of\l"
    .string "silver; what is that betwixt me and\l"
    .string "thee? bury therefore thy dead$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_16::
    .string "And Abraham hearkened unto Ephron;\n"
    .string "and Abraham weighed to Ephron the\l"
    .string "silver, which he had named in the\l"
    .string "audience of the sons of Heth, four\l"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver, current\l"
    .string "money with the merchant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_17::
    .string "And the field of Ephron which was\n"
    .string "in Machpelah, which was before\l"
    .string "Mamre, the field, and the cave which\l"
    .string "was therein, and all the trees that\l"
    .string "were in the field, that were in all\l"
    .string "the borders round about, were made\l"
    .string "sure"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_18::
    .string "Unto Abraham for a possession in\n"
    .string "the presence of the children of\l"
    .string "Heth, before all that went in at the\l"
    .string "gate of his city$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_19::
    .string "And after this, Abraham buried Sarah\n"
    .string "his wife in the cave of the field of\l"
    .string "Machpelah before Mamre: the same is\l"
    .string "Hebron in the land of Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_23_20::
    .string "And the field, and the cave that is\n"
    .string "therein, were made sure unto Abraham\l"
    .string "for a possession of a buryingplace\l"
    .string "by the sons of Heth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_1::
    .string "And Abraham was old, and well\n"
    .string "stricken in age: and the LORD had\l"
    .string "blessed Abraham in all things.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_2::
    .string "And Abraham said unto his eldest\n"
    .string "servant of his house, that ruled\l"
    .string "over all that he had, Put, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, thy hand under my thigh:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_3::
    .string "And I will make thee swear by the\n"
    .string "LORD, the God of heaven, and the God\l"
    .string "of the earth, that thou shalt not\l"
    .string "take a wife unto my son of the\l"
    .string "daughters of the Canaanites, among\l"
    .string "whom I dwell:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_4::
    .string "But thou shalt go unto my country,\n"
    .string "and to my kindred, and take a wife\l"
    .string "unto my son Isaac$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_5::
    .string "And the servant said unto him,\n"
    .string "Peradventure the woman will not be\l"
    .string "willing to follow me unto this\l"
    .string "land: must I needs bring thy son\l"
    .string "again unto the land from whence thou\l"
    .string "camest?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_6::
    .string "And Abraham said unto him, Beware\n"
    .string "thou that thou bring not my son\l"
    .string "thither again$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_7::
    .string "The LORD God of heaven, which took\n"
    .string "me from my father’s house, and from\l"
    .string "the land of my kindred, and which\l"
    .string "spake unto me, and that sware unto\l"
    .string "me, saying, Unto thy seed will I\l"
    .string "give this land; he shall send his\l"
    .string "angel before thee, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "take a wife unto my son from thence.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_8::
    .string "And if the woman will not be\n"
    .string "willing to follow thee, then thou\l"
    .string "shalt be clear from this my oath:\l"
    .string "only bring not my son thither again.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_9::
    .string "And the servant put his hand under\n"
    .string "the thigh of Abraham his master, and\l"
    .string "sware to him concerning that matter.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_10::
    .string "And the servant took ten camels of\n"
    .string "the camels of his master, and\l"
    .string "departed; for all the goods of his\l"
    .string "master were in his hand: and he\l"
    .string "arose, and went to Mesopotamia, unto\l"
    .string "the city of Nahor.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_11::
    .string "And he made his camels to kneel\n"
    .string "down without the city by a well of\l"
    .string "water at the time of the evening,\l"
    .string "even the time that women go out to\l"
    .string "draw water.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_12::
    .string "And he said O LORD God of my master\n"
    .string "Abraham, I pray thee, send me good\l"
    .string "speed this day, and shew kindness\l"
    .string "unto my master Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_13::
    .string "Behold, I stand here by the well\n"
    .string "of water; and the daughters of the\l"
    .string "men of the city come out to draw\l"
    .string "water:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_14::
    .string "And let it come to pass, that the\n"
    .string "damsel to whom I shall say, Let\l"
    .string "down thy pitcher, I pray thee, that\l"
    .string "I may drink; and she shall say,\l"
    .string "Drink, and I will give thy camels\l"
    .string "drink also: let the same be she that\l"
    .string "thou hast appointed for thy servant\l"
    .string "Isaac; and thereby shall I know that\l"
    .string "thou hast shewed kindness unto my\l"
    .string "master$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, before he had\n"
    .string "done speaking, that, behold,\l"
    .string "Rebekah came out, who was born to\l"
    .string "Bethuel, son of Milcah, the wife of\l"
    .string "Nahor, Abraham’s brother, with her\l"
    .string "pitcher upon her shoulder.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_16::
    .string "And the damsel was very fair to\n"
    .string "look upon, a virgin, neither had any\l"
    .string "man known her: and she went down to\l"
    .string "the well, and filled her pitcher,\l"
    .string "and came up.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_17::
    .string "And the servant ran to meet her, and\n"
    .string "said, Let me, I pray thee, drink a\l"
    .string "little water of thy pitcher.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_18::
    .string "And she said, Drink, my lord: and\n"
    .string "she hasted, and let down her pitcher\l"
    .string "upon her hand, and gave him drink.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_19::
    .string "And when she had done giving him\n"
    .string "drink, she said, I will draw water\l"
    .string "for thy camels also, until they\l"
    .string "have done drinking.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_20::
    .string "And she hasted, and emptied her\n"
    .string "pitcher into the trough, and ran\l"
    .string "again unto the well to draw water,\l"
    .string "and drew for all his camels.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_21::
    .string "And the man wondering at her held\n"
    .string "his peace, to wit whether the LORD\l"
    .string "had made his journey prosperous or\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_22::
    .string "And it came to pass, as the camels\n"
    .string "had done drinking, that the man took\l"
    .string "a golden earring of half a shekel\l"
    .string "weight, and two bracelets for her\l"
    .string "hands of ten shekels weight of gold;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_23::
    .string "And said, Whose daughter art thou?\n"
    .string "tell me, I pray thee: is there room\l"
    .string "in thy father’s house for us to\l"
    .string "lodge in?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_24::
    .string "And she said unto him, I am the\n"
    .string "daughter of Bethuel the son of\l"
    .string "Milcah, which she bare unto Nahor$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_25::
    .string "She said moreover unto him, We have\n"
    .string "both straw and provender enough, and\l"
    .string "room to lodge in.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_26::
    .string "And the man bowed down his head, and\n"
    .string "worshipped the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_27::
    .string "And he said, Blessed be the LORD God\n"
    .string "of my master Abraham, who hath not\l"
    .string "left destitute my master of his mercy\l"
    .string "and his truth: I being in the way, the\l"
    .string "LORD led me to the house of my\l"
    .string "master’s brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_28::
    .string "And the damsel ran, and told them\n"
    .string "of her mother’s house these things.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_29::
    .string "And Rebekah had a brother, and his\n"
    .string "name was Laban: and Laban ran out\l"
    .string "unto the man, unto the well.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_30::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he saw the\n"
    .string "earring and bracelets upon his\l"
    .string "sister’s hands, and when he heard the\l"
    .string "words of Rebekah his sister, saying,\l"
    .string "Thus spake the man unto me; that he\l"
    .string "came unto the man; and, behold, he\l"
    .string "stood by the camels at the well.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_31::
    .string "And he said, Come in, thou blessed\n"
    .string "of the LORD; wherefore standest thou\l"
    .string "without? for I have prepared the\l"
    .string "house, and room for the camels.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_32::
    .string "And the man came into the house: and\n"
    .string "he ungirded his camels, and gave\l"
    .string "straw and provender for the camels,\l"
    .string "and water to wash his feet, and the\l"
    .string "men’s feet that were with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_33::
    .string "And there was set meat before him to\n"
    .string "eat: but he said, I will not eat,\l"
    .string "until I have told mine errand. And\l"
    .string "he said, Speak on.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_34::
    .string "And he said, I am Abraham’s servant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_35::
    .string "And the LORD hath blessed my master\n"
    .string "greatly; and he is become great: and\l"
    .string "he hath given him flocks, and herds,\l"
    .string "and silver, and gold, and\l"
    .string "menservants, and maidservants, and\l"
    .string "camels, and asses.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_36::
    .string "And Sarah my master’s wife bare a\n"
    .string "son to my master when she was old:\l"
    .string "and unto him hath he given all that\l"
    .string "he hath.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_37::
    .string "And my master made me swear, saying,\n"
    .string "Thou shalt not take a wife to my son\l"
    .string "of the daughters of the Canaanites,\l"
    .string "in whose land I dwell:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_38::
    .string "But thou shalt go unto my father’s\n"
    .string "house, and to my kindred, and take a\l"
    .string "wife unto my son$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_39::
    .string "And I said unto my master,\n"
    .string "Peradventure the woman will not\l"
    .string "follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_40::
    .string "And he said unto me, The LORD,\n"
    .string "before whom I walk, will send his\l"
    .string "angel with thee, and prosper thy\l"
    .string "way; and thou shalt take a wife for\l"
    .string "my son of my kindred, and of my\l"
    .string "father’s house:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_41::
    .string "Then shalt thou be clear from this\n"
    .string "my oath, when thou comest to my\l"
    .string "kindred; and if they give not thee\l"
    .string "one, thou shalt be clear from my oath$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_42::
    .string "And I came this day unto the well,\n"
    .string "and said, O LORD God of my master\l"
    .string "Abraham, if now thou do prosper my\l"
    .string "way which I go:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_43::
    .string "Behold, I stand by the well of\n"
    .string "water; and it shall come to pass,\l"
    .string "that when the virgin cometh forth to\l"
    .string "draw water, and I say to her, Give me,\l"
    .string "I pray thee, a little water of thy\l"
    .string "pitcher to drink;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_44::
    .string "And she say to me, Both drink thou,\n"
    .string "and I will also draw for thy\l"
    .string "camels: let the same be the woman\l"
    .string "whom the LORD hath appointed out\l"
    .string "for my master’s son$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_45::
    .string "And before I had done speaking in\n"
    .string "mine heart, behold, Rebekah came\l"
    .string "forth with her pitcher on her\l"
    .string "shoulder; and she went down unto the\l"
    .string "well, and drew water: and I said\l"
    .string "unto her, Let me drink, I pray thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_46::
    .string "And she made haste, and let down her\n"
    .string "pitcher from her shoulder, and said,\l"
    .string "Drink, and I will give thy camels\l"
    .string "drink also: so I drank, and she made\l"
    .string "the camels drink also.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_47::
    .string "And I asked her, and said, Whose\n"
    .string "daughter art thou? And she said, the\l"
    .string "daughter of Bethuel, Nahor’s son,\l"
    .string "whom Milcah bare unto him: and I put\l"
    .string "the earring upon her face, and the\l"
    .string "bracelets upon her hands.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_48::
    .string "And I bowed down my head, and\n"
    .string "worshipped the LORD, and blessed\l"
    .string "the LORD God of my master Abraham,\l"
    .string "which had led me in the right way to\l"
    .string "take my master’s brother’s daughter\l"
    .string "unto his son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_49::
    .string "And now if ye will deal kindly\n"
    .string "and truly with my master, tell me:\l"
    .string "and if not, tell me; that I may turn\l"
    .string "to the right hand, or to the left.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_50::
    .string "Then Laban and Bethuel answered and\n"
    .string "said, The thing proceedeth from the\l"
    .string "LORD: we cannot speak unto thee bad\l"
    .string "or good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_51::
    .string "Behold, Rebekah is before thee,\n"
    .string "take her, and go, and let her be thy\l"
    .string "master’s son’s wife, as the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_52::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when\n"
    .string "Abraham’s servant heard their words,\l"
    .string "he worshipped the LORD, bowing\l"
    .string "himself to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_53::
    .string "And the servant brought forth\n"
    .string "jewels of silver, and jewels of\l"
    .string "gold, and raiment, and gave them to\l"
    .string "Rebekah: he gave also to her brother\l"
    .string "and to her mother precious things.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_54::
    .string "And they did eat and drink, he and\n"
    .string "the men that were with him, and\l"
    .string "tarried all night; and they rose up\l"
    .string "in the morning, and he said, Send me\l"
    .string "away unto my master.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_55::
    .string "And her brother and her mother said,\n"
    .string "Let the damsel abide with us a few\l"
    .string "days, at the least ten; after that\l"
    .string "she shall go.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_56::
    .string "And he said unto them, Hinder me\n"
    .string "not, seeing the LORD hath prospered\l"
    .string "my way; send me away that I may go to\l"
    .string "my master.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_57::
    .string "And they said, We will call the\n"
    .string "damsel, and enquire at her mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_58::
    .string "And they called Rebekah, and said\n"
    .string "unto her, Wilt thou go with this man?\l"
    .string "And she said, I will go.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_59::
    .string "And they sent away Rebekah their\n"
    .string "sister, and her nurse, and Abraham’s\l"
    .string "servant, and his men.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_60::
    .string "And they blessed Rebekah, and said\n"
    .string "unto her, Thou art our sister, be\l"
    .string "thou the mother of thousands of\l"
    .string "millions, and let thy seed possess\l"
    .string "the gate of those which hate them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_61::
    .string "And Rebekah arose, and her damsels,\n"
    .string "and they rode upon the camels, and\l"
    .string "followed the man: and the servant\l"
    .string "took Rebekah, and went his way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_62::
    .string "And Isaac came from the way of the\n"
    .string "well Lahairoi; for he dwelt in the\l"
    .string "south country.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_63::
    .string "And Isaac went out to meditate in\n"
    .string "the field at the eventide: and he\l"
    .string "lifted up his eyes, and saw, and,\l"
    .string "behold, the camels were coming.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_64::
    .string "And Rebekah lifted up her eyes, and\n"
    .string "when she saw Isaac, she lighted off\l"
    .string "the camel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_65::
    .string "For she had said unto the servant,\n"
    .string "What man is this that walketh in the\l"
    .string "field to meet us? And the servant had\l"
    .string "said, It is my master: therefore she\l"
    .string "took a vail, and covered herself.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_66::
    .string "And the servant told Isaac all\n"
    .string "things that he had done.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_24_67::
    .string "And Isaac brought her into his\n"
    .string "mother Sarah’s tent, and took\l"
    .string "Rebekah, and she became his wife; and\l"
    .string "he loved her: and Isaac was\l"
    .string "comforted after his mother’s death.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_1::
    .string "Then again Abraham took a wife, and\n"
    .string "her name was Keturah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_2::
    .string "And she bare him Zimran, and\n"
    .string "Jokshan, and Medan, and Midian, and\l"
    .string "Ishbak, and Shuah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_3::
    .string "And Jokshan begat Sheba, and Dedan.\n"
    .string "And the sons of Dedan were Asshurim,\l"
    .string "and Letushim, and Leummim.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_4::
    .string "And the sons of Midian; Ephah, and\n"
    .string "Epher, and Hanoch, and Abidah, and\l"
    .string "Eldaah. All these were the\l"
    .string "children of Keturah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_5::
    .string "And Abraham gave all that he had\n"
    .string "unto Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_6::
    .string "But unto the sons of the concubines,\n"
    .string "which Abraham had, Abraham gave\l"
    .string "gifts, and sent them away from Isaac\l"
    .string "his son, while he yet lived,\l"
    .string "eastward, unto the east country.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_7::
    .string "And these are the days of the years\n"
    .string "of Abraham’s life which he lived, an\l"
    .string "hundred threescore and fifteen years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_8::
    .string "Then Abraham gave up the ghost, and\n"
    .string "died in a good old age, an old man,\l"
    .string "and full of years; and was gathered\l"
    .string "to his people.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_9::
    .string "And his sons Isaac and Ishmael\n"
    .string "buried him in the cave of Machpelah,\l"
    .string "in the field of Ephron the son of\l"
    .string "Zohar the Hittite, which is before\l"
    .string "Mamre;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_10::
    .string "The field which Abraham purchased\n"
    .string "of the sons of Heth: there was\l"
    .string "Abraham buried, and Sarah his wife$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_11::
    .string "And it came to pass after the death\n"
    .string "of Abraham, that God blessed his son\l"
    .string "Isaac; and Isaac dwelt by the well\l"
    .string "Lahairoi.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_12::
    .string "Now these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Ishmael, Abraham’s son, whom Hagar\l"
    .string "the Egyptian, Sarah’s handmaid, bare\l"
    .string "unto Abraham:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_13::
    .string "And these are the names of the sons\n"
    .string "of Ishmael, by their names,\l"
    .string "according to their generations: the\l"
    .string "firstborn of Ishmael, Nebajoth; and\l"
    .string "Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_14::
    .string "And Mishma, and Dumah, and Massa,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_15::
    .string "Hadar, and Tema, Jetur, Naphish,\n"
    .string "and Kedemah:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_16::
    .string "These are the sons of Ishmael, and\n"
    .string "these are their names, by their\l"
    .string "towns, and by their castles; twelve\l"
    .string "princes according to their nations$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_17::
    .string "And these are the years of the life\n"
    .string "of Ishmael, an hundred and thirty\l"
    .string "and seven years: and he gave up the\l"
    .string "ghost and died; and was gathered unto\l"
    .string "his people.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_18::
    .string "And they dwelt from Havilah unto\n"
    .string "Shur, that is before Egypt, as thou\l"
    .string "goest toward Assyria: and he died in\l"
    .string "the presence of all his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_19::
    .string "And these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Isaac, Abraham’s son: Abraham begat\l"
    .string "Isaac:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_20::
    .string "And Isaac was forty years old when\n"
    .string "he took Rebekah to wife, the daughter\l"
    .string "of Bethuel the Syrian of Padanaram,\l"
    .string "the sister to Laban the Syrian$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_21::
    .string "And Isaac intreated the LORD for his\n"
    .string "wife, because she was barren: and the\l"
    .string "LORD was intreated of him, and\l"
    .string "Rebekah his wife conceived.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_22::
    .string "And the children struggled\n"
    .string "together within her; and she said, If\l"
    .string "it be so, why am I thus? And she went\l"
    .string "to enquire of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_23::
    .string "And the LORD said unto her, Two\n"
    .string "nations are in thy womb, and two\l"
    .string "manner of people shall be\l"
    .string "separated from thy bowels; and the\l"
    .string "one people shall be stronger than\l"
    .string "the other people; and the elder\l"
    .string "shall serve the younger.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_24::
    .string "And when her days to be delivered\n"
    .string "were fulfilled, behold, there were\l"
    .string "twins in her womb.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_25::
    .string "And the first came out red, all\n"
    .string "over like an hairy garment; and they\l"
    .string "called his name Esau.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_26::
    .string "And after that came his brother out,\n"
    .string "and his hand took hold on Esau’s\l"
    .string "heel; and his name was called\l"
    .string "Jacob: and Isaac was threescore years\l"
    .string "old when she bare them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_27::
    .string "And the boys grew: and Esau was a\n"
    .string "cunning hunter, a man of the field;\l"
    .string "and Jacob was a plain man,\l"
    .string "dwelling in tents.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_28::
    .string "And Isaac loved Esau, because he\n"
    .string "did eat of his venison: but Rebekah\l"
    .string "loved Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_29::
    .string "And Jacob sod pottage: and Esau\n"
    .string "came from the field, and he was\l"
    .string "faint:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_30::
    .string "And Esau said to Jacob, Feed me, I\n"
    .string "pray thee, with that same red\l"
    .string "pottage; for I am faint: therefore\l"
    .string "was his name called Edom$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_31::
    .string "And Jacob said, Sell me this day\n"
    .string "thy birthright.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_32::
    .string "And Esau said, Behold, I am at the\n"
    .string "point to die: and what profit shall\l"
    .string "this birthright do to me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_33::
    .string "And Jacob said, Swear to me this\n"
    .string "day; and he sware unto him: and he\l"
    .string "sold his birthright unto Jacob$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_25_34::
    .string "Then Jacob gave Esau bread and\n"
    .string "pottage of lentiles; and he did eat\l"
    .string "and drink, and rose up, and went his\l"
    .string "way: thus Esau despised his\l"
    .string "birthright.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_1::
    .string "And there was a famine in the land,\n"
    .string "beside the first famine that was in\l"
    .string "the days of Abraham. And Isaac went\l"
    .string "unto Abimelech king of the\l"
    .string "Philistines unto Gerar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_2::
    .string "And the LORD appeared unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, Go not down into Egypt; dwell\l"
    .string "in the land which I shall tell\l"
    .string "thee of:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_3::
    .string "Sojourn in this land, and I will\n"
    .string "be with thee, and will bless thee;\l"
    .string "for unto thee, and unto thy seed, I\l"
    .string "will give all these countries, and\l"
    .string "I will perform the oath which I\l"
    .string "sware unto Abraham thy father;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_4::
    .string "And I will make thy seed to\n"
    .string "multiply as the stars of heaven,\l"
    .string "and will give unto thy seed all\l"
    .string "these countries; and in thy seed\l"
    .string "shall all the nations of the earth\l"
    .string "be blessed;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_5::
    .string "Because that Abraham obeyed my\n"
    .string "voice, and kept my charge, my\l"
    .string "commandments, my statutes, and my\l"
    .string "laws$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_6::
    .string "And Isaac dwelt in Gerar:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_7::
    .string "And the men of the place asked him\n"
    .string "of his wife; and he said, She is my\l"
    .string "sister: for he feared to say, She is\l"
    .string "my wife; lest, said he, the men of\l"
    .string "the place should kill me for\l"
    .string "Rebekah; because she was fair to\l"
    .string "look upon$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he had\n"
    .string "been there a long time, that\l"
    .string "Abimelech king of the Philistines\l"
    .string "looked out at a window, and saw, and,\l"
    .string "behold, Isaac was sporting with\l"
    .string "Rebekah his wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_9::
    .string "And Abimelech called Isaac, and\n"
    .string "said, Behold, of a surety she is thy\l"
    .string "wife; and how saidst thou, She is my\l"
    .string "sister? And Isaac said unto him,\l"
    .string "Because I said, Lest I die for her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_10::
    .string "And Abimelech said, What is this\n"
    .string "thou hast done unto us? one of the\l"
    .string "people might lightly have lien\l"
    .string "with thy wife, and thou shouldest\l"
    .string "have brought guiltiness upon us.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_11::
    .string "And Abimelech charged all his\n"
    .string "people, saying, He that toucheth\l"
    .string "this man or his wife shall surely\l"
    .string "be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_12::
    .string "Then Isaac sowed in that land, and\n"
    .string "received in the same year an\l"
    .string "hundredfold: and the LORD blessed\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_13::
    .string "And the man waxed great, and went\n"
    .string "forward, and grew until he became\l"
    .string "very great:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_14::
    .string "For he had possession of flocks,\n"
    .string "and possession of herds, and great\l"
    .string "store of servants: and the\l"
    .string "Philistines envied him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_15::
    .string "For all the wells which his\n"
    .string "father’s servants had digged in the\l"
    .string "days of Abraham his father, the\l"
    .string "Philistines had stopped them, and\l"
    .string "filled them with earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_16::
    .string "And Abimelech said unto Isaac, Go\n"
    .string "from us; for thou art much mightier\l"
    .string "than we.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_17::
    .string "And Isaac departed thence, and\n"
    .string "pitched his tent in the valley of\l"
    .string "Gerar, and dwelt there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_18::
    .string "And Isaac digged again the wells\n"
    .string "of water, which they had digged in\l"
    .string "the days of Abraham his father; for\l"
    .string "the Philistines had stopped them\l"
    .string "after the death of Abraham: and he\l"
    .string "called their names after the names\l"
    .string "by which his father had called them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_19::
    .string "And Isaac’s servants digged in the\n"
    .string "valley, and found there a well of\l"
    .string "springing water.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_20::
    .string "And the herdmen of Gerar did strive\n"
    .string "with Isaac’s herdmen, saying, The\l"
    .string "water is ours: and he called the\l"
    .string "name of the well Esek; because they\l"
    .string "strove with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_21::
    .string "And they digged another well, and\n"
    .string "strove for that also: and he called\l"
    .string "the name of it Sitnah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_22::
    .string "And he removed from thence, and\n"
    .string "digged another well; and for that\l"
    .string "they strove not: and he called the\l"
    .string "name of it Rehoboth; and he said, For\l"
    .string "now the LORD hath made room for us,\l"
    .string "and we shall be fruitful in the\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_23::
    .string "And he went up from thence to\n"
    .string "Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_24::
    .string "And the LORD appeared unto him the\n"
    .string "same night, and said, I am the God of\l"
    .string "Abraham thy father: fear not, for I\l"
    .string "am with thee, and will bless thee,\l"
    .string "and multiply thy seed for my\l"
    .string "servant Abraham’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_25::
    .string "And he builded an altar there, and\n"
    .string "called upon the name of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and pitched his tent there: and\l"
    .string "there Isaac’s servants digged a\l"
    .string "well.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_26::
    .string "Then Abimelech went to him from\n"
    .string "Gerar, and Ahuzzath one of his\l"
    .string "friends, and Phichol the chief\l"
    .string "captain of his army.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_27::
    .string "And Isaac said unto them, Wherefore\n"
    .string "come ye to me, seeing ye hate me, and\l"
    .string "have sent me away from you?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_28::
    .string "And they said, We saw certainly\n"
    .string "that the LORD was with thee: and we\l"
    .string "said, Let there be now an oath\l"
    .string "betwixt us, even betwixt us and thee,\l"
    .string "and let us make a covenant with thee;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_29::
    .string "That thou wilt do us no hurt, as we\n"
    .string "have not touched thee, and as we have\l"
    .string "done unto thee nothing but good, and\l"
    .string "have sent thee away in peace: thou\l"
    .string "art now the blessed of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_30::
    .string "And he made them a feast, and they\n"
    .string "did eat and drink.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_31::
    .string "And they rose up betimes in the\n"
    .string "morning, and sware one to another:\l"
    .string "and Isaac sent them away, and they\l"
    .string "departed from him in peace.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_32::
    .string "And it came to pass the same day,\n"
    .string "that Isaac’s servants came, and told\l"
    .string "him concerning the well which they\l"
    .string "had digged, and said unto him, We\l"
    .string "have found water.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_33::
    .string "And he called it Shebah: therefore\n"
    .string "the name of the city is Beersheba\l"
    .string "unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_34::
    .string "And Esau was forty years old when\n"
    .string "he took to wife Judith the daughter\l"
    .string "of Beeri the Hittite, and Bashemath\l"
    .string "the daughter of Elon the Hittite:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_26_35::
    .string "Which were a grief of mind unto\n"
    .string "Isaac and to Rebekah$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when Isaac\n"
    .string "was old, and his eyes were dim, so\l"
    .string "that he could not see, he called\l"
    .string "Esau his eldest son, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, My son: and he said unto him,\l"
    .string "Behold, here am I.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_2::
    .string "And he said, Behold now, I am old, I\n"
    .string "know not the day of my death:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_3::
    .string "Now therefore take, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "thy weapons, thy quiver and thy bow,\l"
    .string "and go out to the field, and take me\l"
    .string "some venison;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_4::
    .string "And make me savoury meat, such as I\n"
    .string "love, and bring it to me, that I may\l"
    .string "eat; that my soul may bless thee\l"
    .string "before I die$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_5::
    .string "And Rebekah heard when Isaac spake\n"
    .string "to Esau his son. And Esau went to the\l"
    .string "field to hunt for venison, and to\l"
    .string "bring it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_6::
    .string "And Rebekah spake unto Jacob her\n"
    .string "son, saying, Behold, I heard thy\l"
    .string "father speak unto Esau thy brother,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_7::
    .string "Bring me venison, and make me\n"
    .string "savoury meat, that I may eat, and\l"
    .string "bless thee before the LORD before my\l"
    .string "death$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_8::
    .string "Now therefore, my son, obey my voice\n"
    .string "according to that which I command\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_9::
    .string "Go now to the flock, and fetch me\n"
    .string "from thence two good kids of the\l"
    .string "goats; and I will make them savoury\l"
    .string "meat for thy father, such as he\l"
    .string "loveth:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_10::
    .string "And thou shalt bring it to thy\n"
    .string "father, that he may eat, and that he\l"
    .string "may bless thee before his death$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_11::
    .string "And Jacob said to Rebekah his\n"
    .string "mother, Behold, Esau my brother is a\l"
    .string "hairy man, and I am a smooth man:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_12::
    .string "My father peradventure will feel\n"
    .string "me, and I shall seem to him as a\l"
    .string "deceiver; and I shall bring a curse\l"
    .string "upon me, and not a blessing$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_13::
    .string "And his mother said unto him, Upon\n"
    .string "me be thy curse, my son: only obey my\l"
    .string "voice, and go fetch me them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_14::
    .string "And he went, and fetched, and\n"
    .string "brought them to his mother: and his\l"
    .string "mother made savoury meat, such as his\l"
    .string "father loved.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_15::
    .string "And Rebekah took goodly raiment of\n"
    .string "her eldest son Esau, which were with\l"
    .string "her in the house, and put them upon\l"
    .string "Jacob her younger son:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_16::
    .string "And she put the skins of the kids of\n"
    .string "the goats upon his hands, and upon\l"
    .string "the smooth of his neck:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_17::
    .string "And she gave the savoury meat and\n"
    .string "the bread, which she had prepared,\l"
    .string "into the hand of her son Jacob$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_18::
    .string "And he came unto his father, and\n"
    .string "said, My father: and he said, Here am\l"
    .string "I; who art thou, my son?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_19::
    .string "And Jacob said unto his father, I am\n"
    .string "Esau thy first born; I have done\l"
    .string "according as thou badest me: arise, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, sit and eat of my venison,\l"
    .string "that thy soul may bless me$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_20::
    .string "And Isaac said unto his son, How is\n"
    .string "it that thou hast found it so\l"
    .string "quickly, my son? And he said, Because\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God brought it to me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_21::
    .string "And Isaac said unto Jacob, Come\n"
    .string "near, I pray thee, that I may feel\l"
    .string "thee, my son, whether thou be my very\l"
    .string "son Esau or not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_22::
    .string "And Jacob went near unto Isaac his\n"
    .string "father; and he felt him, and said,\l"
    .string "The voice is Jacob’s voice, but the\l"
    .string "hands are the hands of Esau.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_23::
    .string "And he discerned him not, because\n"
    .string "his hands were hairy, as his brother\l"
    .string "Esau’s hands: so he blessed him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_24::
    .string "And he said, Art thou my very son\n"
    .string "Esau? And he said, I am.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_25::
    .string "And he said, Bring it near to me, and\n"
    .string "I will eat of my son’s venison, that\l"
    .string "my soul may bless thee. And he\l"
    .string "brought it near to him, and he did\l"
    .string "eat: and he brought him wine and he\l"
    .string "drank.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_26::
    .string "And his father Isaac said unto him,\n"
    .string "Come near now, and kiss me, my son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_27::
    .string "And he came near, and kissed him:\n"
    .string "and he smelled the smell of his\l"
    .string "raiment, and blessed him, and said,\l"
    .string "See, the smell of my son is as the\l"
    .string "smell of a field which the LORD\l"
    .string "hath blessed:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_28::
    .string "Therefore God give thee of the dew\n"
    .string "of heaven, and the fatness of the\l"
    .string "earth, and plenty of corn and wine:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_29::
    .string "Let people serve thee, and nations\n"
    .string "bow down to thee: be lord over thy\l"
    .string "brethren, and let thy mother’s sons\l"
    .string "bow down to thee: cursed be every one\l"
    .string "that curseth thee, and blessed be he\l"
    .string "that blesseth thee$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_30::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as\n"
    .string "Isaac had made an end of blessing\l"
    .string "Jacob, and Jacob was yet scarce gone\l"
    .string "out from the presence of Isaac his\l"
    .string "father, that Esau his brother came in\l"
    .string "from his hunting.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_31::
    .string "And he also had made savoury meat,\n"
    .string "and brought it unto his father, and\l"
    .string "said unto his father, Let my father\l"
    .string "arise, and eat of his son’s venison,\l"
    .string "that thy soul may bless me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_32::
    .string "And Isaac his father said unto him,\n"
    .string "Who art thou? And he said, I am thy\l"
    .string "son, thy firstborn Esau.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_33::
    .string "And Isaac trembled very\n"
    .string "exceedingly, and said, Who? where is\l"
    .string "he that hath taken venison, and\l"
    .string "brought it me, and I have eaten of\l"
    .string "all before thou camest, and have\l"
    .string "blessed him? yea, and he shall be\l"
    .string "blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_34::
    .string "And when Esau heard the words of his\n"
    .string "father, he cried with a great and\l"
    .string "exceeding bitter cry, and said unto\l"
    .string "his father, Bless me, even me also,\l"
    .string "O my father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_35::
    .string "And he said, Thy brother came with\n"
    .string "subtilty, and hath taken away thy\l"
    .string "blessing.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_36::
    .string "And he said, Is not he rightly named\n"
    .string "Jacob? for he hath supplanted me\l"
    .string "these two times: he took away my\l"
    .string "birthright; and, behold, now he hath\l"
    .string "taken away my blessing. And he said,\l"
    .string "Hast thou not reserved a blessing\l"
    .string "for me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_37::
    .string "And Isaac answered and said unto\n"
    .string "Esau, Behold, I have made him thy\l"
    .string "lord, and all his brethren have I\l"
    .string "given to him for servants; and with\l"
    .string "corn and wine have I sustained him:\l"
    .string "and what shall I do now unto thee,\l"
    .string "my son?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_38::
    .string "And Esau said unto his father, Hast\n"
    .string "thou but one blessing, my father?\l"
    .string "bless me, even me also, O my father.\l"
    .string "And Esau lifted up his voice, and\l"
    .string "wept$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_39::
    .string "And Isaac his father answered and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Behold, thy dwelling\l"
    .string "shall be the fatness of the earth,\l"
    .string "and of the dew of heaven from above;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_40::
    .string "And by thy sword shalt thou live,\n"
    .string "and shalt serve thy brother; and it\l"
    .string "shall come to pass when thou shalt\l"
    .string "have the dominion, that thou shalt\l"
    .string "break his yoke from off thy neck$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_41::
    .string "And Esau hated Jacob because of the\n"
    .string "blessing wherewith his father\l"
    .string "blessed him: and Esau said in his\l"
    .string "heart, The days of mourning for my\l"
    .string "father are at hand; then will I\l"
    .string "slay my brother Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_42::
    .string "And these words of Esau her elder\n"
    .string "son were told to Rebekah: and she\l"
    .string "sent and called Jacob her younger\l"
    .string "son, and said unto him, Behold, thy\l"
    .string "brother Esau, as touching thee, doth\l"
    .string "comfort himself, purposing to\l"
    .string "kill thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_43::
    .string "Now therefore, my son, obey my\n"
    .string "voice; arise, flee thou to Laban my\l"
    .string "brother to Haran;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_44::
    .string "And tarry with him a few days, until\n"
    .string "thy brother’s fury turn away;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_45::
    .string "Until thy brother’s anger turn away\n"
    .string "from thee, and he forget that which\l"
    .string "thou hast done to him: then I will\l"
    .string "send, and fetch thee from thence: why\l"
    .string "should I be deprived also of you\l"
    .string "both in one day?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_27_46::
    .string "And Rebekah said to Isaac, I am\n"
    .string "weary of my life because of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Heth: if Jacob take a\l"
    .string "wife of the daughters of Heth, such\l"
    .string "as these which are of the daughters\l"
    .string "of the land, what good shall my\l"
    .string "life do me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_1::
    .string "And Isaac called Jacob, and\n"
    .string "blessed him, and charged him, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Thou shalt not take a\l"
    .string "wife of the daughters of Canaan$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_2::
    .string "Arise, go to Padanaram, to the house\n"
    .string "of Bethuel thy mother’s father; and\l"
    .string "take thee a wife from thence of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Laban thy mother’s\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_3::
    .string "And God Almighty bless thee, and\n"
    .string "make thee fruitful, and multiply\l"
    .string "thee, that thou mayest be a\l"
    .string "multitude of people;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_4::
    .string "And give thee the blessing of\n"
    .string "Abraham, to thee, and to thy seed\l"
    .string "with thee; that thou mayest inherit\l"
    .string "the land wherein thou art a\l"
    .string "stranger, which God gave unto Abraham$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_5::
    .string "And Isaac sent away Jacob: and he\n"
    .string "went to Padanaram unto Laban, son of\l"
    .string "Bethuel the Syrian, the brother of\l"
    .string "Rebekah, Jacob’s and Esau’s mother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_6::
    .string "When Esau saw that Isaac had\n"
    .string "blessed Jacob, and sent him away to\l"
    .string "Padanaram, to take him a wife from\l"
    .string "thence; and that as he blessed him he\l"
    .string "gave him a charge, saying, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt not take a wife of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Canaan;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_7::
    .string "And that Jacob obeyed his father and\n"
    .string "his mother, and was gone to\l"
    .string "Padanaram;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_8::
    .string "And Esau seeing that the daughters\n"
    .string "of Canaan pleased not Isaac his\l"
    .string "father;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_9::
    .string "Then went Esau unto Ishmael, and\n"
    .string "took unto the wives which he had\l"
    .string "Mahalath the daughter of Ishmael\l"
    .string "Abraham’s son, the sister of\l"
    .string "Nebajoth, to be his wife$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_10::
    .string "And Jacob went out from Beersheba,\n"
    .string "and went toward Haran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_11::
    .string "And he lighted upon a certain\n"
    .string "place, and tarried there all night,\l"
    .string "because the sun was set; and he took\l"
    .string "of the stones of that place, and\l"
    .string "put them for his pillows, and lay\l"
    .string "down in that place to sleep.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_12::
    .string "And he dreamed, and behold a ladder\n"
    .string "set up on the earth, and the top of\l"
    .string "it reached to heaven: and behold the\l"
    .string "angels of God ascending and\l"
    .string "descending on it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_13::
    .string "And, behold, the LORD stood above\n"
    .string "it, and said, I am the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Abraham thy father, and the God of\l"
    .string "Isaac: the land whereon thou liest,\l"
    .string "to thee will I give it, and to thy\l"
    .string "seed;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_14::
    .string "And thy seed shall be as the dust\n"
    .string "of the earth, and thou shalt spread\l"
    .string "abroad to the west, and to the east,\l"
    .string "and to the north, and to the south:\l"
    .string "and in thee and in thy seed shall\l"
    .string "all the families of the earth be\l"
    .string "blessed$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_15::
    .string "And, behold, I am with thee, and\n"
    .string "will keep thee in all places\l"
    .string "whither thou goest, and will bring\l"
    .string "thee again into this land; for I\l"
    .string "will not leave thee, until I have\l"
    .string "done that which I have spoken to\l"
    .string "thee of.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_16::
    .string "And Jacob awaked out of his sleep,\n"
    .string "and he said, Surely the LORD is in\l"
    .string "this place; and I knew it not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_17::
    .string "And he was afraid, and said, How\n"
    .string "dreadful is this place! this is\l"
    .string "none other but the house of God, and\l"
    .string "this is the gate of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_18::
    .string "And Jacob rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and took the stone that he\l"
    .string "had put for his pillows, and set it\l"
    .string "up for a pillar, and poured oil\l"
    .string "upon the top of it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_19::
    .string "And he called the name of that\n"
    .string "place Bethel: but the name of that\l"
    .string "city was called Luz at the first.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_20::
    .string "And Jacob vowed a vow, saying, If\n"
    .string "God will be with me, and will keep\l"
    .string "me in this way that I go, and will\l"
    .string "give me bread to eat, and raiment to\l"
    .string "put on,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_21::
    .string "So that I come again to my father’s\n"
    .string "house in peace; then shall the LORD\l"
    .string "be my God:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_28_22::
    .string "And this stone, which I have set for\n"
    .string "a pillar, shall be God’s house:\l"
    .string "and of all that thou shalt give me\l"
    .string "I will surely give the tenth unto\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_1::
    .string "Then Jacob went on his journey, and\n"
    .string "came into the land of the people\l"
    .string "of the east.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_2::
    .string "And he looked, and behold a well\n"
    .string "in the field, and, lo, there were\l"
    .string "three flocks of sheep lying by it;\l"
    .string "for out of that well they watered\l"
    .string "the flocks: and a great stone was\l"
    .string "upon the well’s mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_3::
    .string "And thither were all the flocks\n"
    .string "gathered: and they rolled the stone\l"
    .string "from the well’s mouth, and watered\l"
    .string "the sheep, and put the stone again\l"
    .string "upon the well’s mouth in his\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_4::
    .string "And Jacob said unto them, My\n"
    .string "brethren, whence be ye? And they\l"
    .string "said, Of Haran are we.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, Know ye Laban\n"
    .string "the son of Nahor? And they said, We\l"
    .string "know him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_6::
    .string "And he said unto them, Is he well?\n"
    .string "And they said, He is well: and,\l"
    .string "behold, Rachel his daughter cometh\l"
    .string "with the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_7::
    .string "And he said, Lo, it is yet high day,\n"
    .string "neither is it time that the cattle\l"
    .string "should be gathered together: water\l"
    .string "ye the sheep, and go and feed them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_8::
    .string "And they said, We cannot, until\n"
    .string "all the flocks be gathered\l"
    .string "together, and till they roll the\l"
    .string "stone from the well’s mouth; then we\l"
    .string "water the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_9::
    .string "And while he yet spake with them,\n"
    .string "Rachel came with her father’s\l"
    .string "sheep; for she kept them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jacob saw\n"
    .string "Rachel the daughter of Laban his\l"
    .string "mother’s brother, and the sheep of\l"
    .string "Laban his mother’s brother, that\l"
    .string "Jacob went near, and rolled the\l"
    .string "stone from the well’s mouth, and\l"
    .string "watered the flock of Laban his\l"
    .string "mother’s brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_11::
    .string "And Jacob kissed Rachel, and\n"
    .string "lifted up his voice, and wept.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_12::
    .string "And Jacob told Rachel that he was\n"
    .string "her father’s brother, and that he was\l"
    .string "Rebekah’s son: and she ran and told\l"
    .string "her father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Laban\n"
    .string "heard the tidings of Jacob his\l"
    .string "sister’s son, that he ran to meet\l"
    .string "him, and embraced him, and kissed\l"
    .string "him, and brought him to his house.\l"
    .string "And he told Laban all these things.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_14::
    .string "And Laban said to him, Surely thou\n"
    .string "art my bone and my flesh. And he\l"
    .string "abode with him the space of a month.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_15::
    .string "And Laban said unto Jacob, Because\n"
    .string "thou art my brother, shouldest thou\l"
    .string "therefore serve me for nought? tell\l"
    .string "me, what shall thy wages be?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_16::
    .string "And Laban had two daughters: the\n"
    .string "name of the elder was Leah, and the\l"
    .string "name of the younger was Rachel$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_17::
    .string "Leah was tender eyed; but Rachel\n"
    .string "was beautiful and well favoured.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_18::
    .string "And Jacob loved Rachel; and said, I\n"
    .string "will serve thee seven years for\l"
    .string "Rachel thy younger daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_19::
    .string "And Laban said, It is better that I\n"
    .string "give her to thee, than that I should\l"
    .string "give her to another man: abide with\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_20::
    .string "And Jacob served seven years for\n"
    .string "Rachel; and they seemed unto him but\l"
    .string "a few days, for the love he had to\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_21::
    .string "And Jacob said unto Laban, Give me\n"
    .string "my wife, for my days are fulfilled,\l"
    .string "that I may go in unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_22::
    .string "And Laban gathered together all\n"
    .string "the men of the place, and made a\l"
    .string "feast.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_23::
    .string "And it came to pass in the evening,\n"
    .string "that he took Leah his daughter, and\l"
    .string "brought her to him; and he went in\l"
    .string "unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_24::
    .string "And Laban gave unto his daughter\n"
    .string "Leah Zilpah his maid for an\l"
    .string "handmaid.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_25::
    .string "And it came to pass, that in the\n"
    .string "morning, behold, it was Leah: and he\l"
    .string "said to Laban, What is this thou hast\l"
    .string "done unto me? did not I serve with\l"
    .string "thee for Rachel? wherefore then hast\l"
    .string "thou beguiled me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_26::
    .string "And Laban said, It must not be so\n"
    .string "done in our country, to give the\l"
    .string "younger before the firstborn$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_27::
    .string "Fulfil her week, and we will give\n"
    .string "thee this also for the service which\l"
    .string "thou shalt serve with me yet seven\l"
    .string "other years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_28::
    .string "And Jacob did so, and fulfilled\n"
    .string "her week: and he gave him Rachel his\l"
    .string "daughter to wife also.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_29::
    .string "And Laban gave to Rachel his\n"
    .string "daughter Bilhah his handmaid to be\l"
    .string "her maid.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_30::
    .string "And he went in also unto Rachel,\n"
    .string "and he loved also Rachel more than\l"
    .string "Leah, and served with him yet seven\l"
    .string "other years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_31::
    .string "And when the LORD saw that Leah was\n"
    .string "hated, he opened her womb: but\l"
    .string "Rachel was barren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_32::
    .string "And Leah conceived, and bare a son,\n"
    .string "and she called his name Reuben: for\l"
    .string "she said, Surely the LORD hath\l"
    .string "looked upon my affliction; now\l"
    .string "therefore my husband will love me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_33::
    .string "And she conceived again, and bare a\n"
    .string "son; and said, Because the LORD hath\l"
    .string "heard I was hated, he hath therefore\l"
    .string "given me this son also: and she\l"
    .string "called his name Simeon.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_34::
    .string "And she conceived again, and bare a\n"
    .string "son; and said, Now this time will my\l"
    .string "husband be joined unto me, because I\l"
    .string "have born him three sons: therefore\l"
    .string "was his name called Levi.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_29_35::
    .string "And she conceived again, and bare a\n"
    .string "son: and she said, Now will I\l"
    .string "praise the LORD: therefore she\l"
    .string "called his name Judah; and left\l"
    .string "bearing.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_1::
    .string "And when Rachel saw that she bare\n"
    .string "Jacob no children, Rachel envied\l"
    .string "her sister; and said unto Jacob, Give\l"
    .string "me children, or else I die.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_2::
    .string "And Jacob’s anger was kindled\n"
    .string "against Rachel: and he said, Am I in\l"
    .string "God’s stead, who hath withheld from\l"
    .string "thee the fruit of the womb?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_3::
    .string "And she said, Behold my maid\n"
    .string "Bilhah, go in unto her; and she\l"
    .string "shall bear upon my knees, that I\l"
    .string "may also have children by her$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_4::
    .string "And she gave him Bilhah her\n"
    .string "handmaid to wife: and Jacob went in\l"
    .string "unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_5::
    .string "And Bilhah conceived, and bare\n"
    .string "Jacob a son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_6::
    .string "And Rachel said, God hath judged\n"
    .string "me, and hath also heard my voice, and\l"
    .string "hath given me a son: therefore\l"
    .string "called she his name Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_7::
    .string "And Bilhah Rachel’s maid conceived\n"
    .string "again, and bare Jacob a second son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_8::
    .string "And Rachel said, With great\n"
    .string "wrestlings have I wrestled with my\l"
    .string "sister, and I have prevailed: and\l"
    .string "she called his name Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_9::
    .string "When Leah saw that she had left\n"
    .string "bearing, she took Zilpah her maid,\l"
    .string "and gave her Jacob to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_10::
    .string "And Zilpah Leah’s maid bare Jacob\n"
    .string "a son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_11::
    .string "And Leah said, A troop cometh: and\n"
    .string "she called his name Gad.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_12::
    .string "And Zilpah Leah’s maid bare Jacob\n"
    .string "a second son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_13::
    .string "And Leah said, Happy am I, for the\n"
    .string "daughters will call me blessed:\l"
    .string "and she called his name Asher.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_14::
    .string "And Reuben went in the days of wheat\n"
    .string "harvest, and found mandrakes in the\l"
    .string "field, and brought them unto his\l"
    .string "mother Leah. Then Rachel said to\l"
    .string "Leah, Give me, I pray thee, of thy\l"
    .string "son’s mandrakes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_15::
    .string "And she said unto her, Is it a\n"
    .string "small matter that thou hast taken\l"
    .string "my husband? and wouldest thou take\l"
    .string "away my son’s mandrakes also? And\l"
    .string "Rachel said, Therefore he shall\l"
    .string "lie with thee to night for thy son’s\l"
    .string "mandrakes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_16::
    .string "And Jacob came out of the field in\n"
    .string "the evening, and Leah went out to\l"
    .string "meet him, and said, Thou must come in\l"
    .string "unto me; for surely I have hired thee\l"
    .string "with my son’s mandrakes. And he lay\l"
    .string "with her that night.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_17::
    .string "And God hearkened unto Leah, and she\n"
    .string "conceived, and bare Jacob the fifth\l"
    .string "son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_18::
    .string "And Leah said, God hath given me my\n"
    .string "hire, because I have given my maiden\l"
    .string "to my husband: and she called his\l"
    .string "name Issachar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_19::
    .string "And Leah conceived again, and bare\n"
    .string "Jacob the sixth son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_20::
    .string "And Leah said, God hath endued me\n"
    .string "with a good dowry; now will my\l"
    .string "husband dwell with me, because I\l"
    .string "have born him six sons: and she\l"
    .string "called his name Zebulun.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_21::
    .string "And afterwards she bare a daughter,\n"
    .string "and called her name Dinah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_22::
    .string "And God remembered Rachel, and God\n"
    .string "hearkened to her, and opened her\l"
    .string "womb.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_23::
    .string "And she conceived, and bare a son;\n"
    .string "and said, God hath taken away my\l"
    .string "reproach:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_24::
    .string "And she called his name Joseph;\n"
    .string "and said, The LORD shall add to me\l"
    .string "another son$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_25::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Rachel\n"
    .string "had born Joseph, that Jacob said\l"
    .string "unto Laban, Send me away, that I may\l"
    .string "go unto mine own place, and to my\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_26::
    .string "Give me my wives and my children,\n"
    .string "for whom I have served thee, and let\l"
    .string "me go: for thou knowest my service\l"
    .string "which I have done thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_27::
    .string "And Laban said unto him, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, if I have found favour in thine\l"
    .string "eyes, tarry: for I have learned by\l"
    .string "experience that the LORD hath\l"
    .string "blessed me for thy sake.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_28::
    .string "And he said, Appoint me thy wages,\n"
    .string "and I will give it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_29::
    .string "And he said unto him, Thou knowest\n"
    .string "how I have served thee, and how thy\l"
    .string "cattle was with me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_30::
    .string "For it was little which thou hadst\n"
    .string "before I came, and it is now\l"
    .string "increased unto a multitude; and the\l"
    .string "LORD hath blessed thee since my\l"
    .string "coming: and now when shall I\l"
    .string "provide for mine own house also?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_31::
    .string "And he said, What shall I give\n"
    .string "thee? And Jacob said, Thou shalt not\l"
    .string "give me any thing: if thou wilt do\l"
    .string "this thing for me, I will again feed\l"
    .string "and keep thy flock$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_32::
    .string "I will pass through all thy\n"
    .string "flock to day, removing from thence\l"
    .string "all the speckled and spotted\l"
    .string "cattle, and all the brown cattle\l"
    .string "among the sheep, and the spotted and\l"
    .string "speckled among the goats: and of\l"
    .string "such shall be my hire.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_33::
    .string "So shall my righteousness answer\n"
    .string "for me in time to come, when it\l"
    .string "shall come for my hire before thy\l"
    .string "face: every one that is not speckled\l"
    .string "and spotted among the goats, and\l"
    .string "brown among the sheep, that shall\l"
    .string "be counted stolen with me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_34::
    .string "And Laban said, Behold, I would it\n"
    .string "might be according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_35::
    .string "And he removed that day the he goats\n"
    .string "that were ringstraked and spotted,\l"
    .string "and all the she goats that were\l"
    .string "speckled and spotted, and every one\l"
    .string "that had some white in it, and all\l"
    .string "the brown among the sheep, and gave\l"
    .string "them into the hand of his sons.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_36::
    .string "And he set three days’ journey\n"
    .string "betwixt himself and Jacob: and Jacob\l"
    .string "fed the rest of Laban’s flocks.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_37::
    .string "And Jacob took him rods of green\n"
    .string "poplar, and of the hazel and\l"
    .string "chestnut tree; and pilled white\l"
    .string "strakes in them, and made the white\l"
    .string "appear which was in the rods.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_38::
    .string "And he set the rods which he had\n"
    .string "pilled before the flocks in the\l"
    .string "gutters in the watering troughs when\l"
    .string "the flocks came to drink, that they\l"
    .string "should conceive when they came to\l"
    .string "drink.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_39::
    .string "And the flocks conceived before the\n"
    .string "rods, and brought forth cattle\l"
    .string "ringstraked, speckled, and spotted.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_40::
    .string "And Jacob did separate the lambs,\n"
    .string "and set the faces of the flocks\l"
    .string "toward the ringstraked, and all the\l"
    .string "brown in the flock of Laban; and he\l"
    .string "put his own flocks by themselves,\l"
    .string "and put them not unto Laban’s\l"
    .string "cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_41::
    .string "And it came to pass, whensoever the\n"
    .string "stronger cattle did conceive, that\l"
    .string "Jacob laid the rods before the eyes\l"
    .string "of the cattle in the gutters, that\l"
    .string "they might conceive among the rods.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_42::
    .string "But when the cattle were feeble, he\n"
    .string "put them not in: so the feebler were\l"
    .string "Laban’s, and the stronger Jacob’s.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_30_43::
    .string "And the man increased exceedingly,\n"
    .string "and had much cattle, and\l"
    .string "maidservants, and menservants, and\l"
    .string "camels, and asses.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_1::
    .string "And he heard the words of Laban’s\n"
    .string "sons, saying, Jacob hath taken away\l"
    .string "all that was our father’s; and of\l"
    .string "that which was our father’s hath he\l"
    .string "gotten all this glory.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_2::
    .string "And Jacob beheld the countenance of\n"
    .string "Laban, and, behold, it was not toward\l"
    .string "him as before.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_3::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Jacob, Return\n"
    .string "unto the land of thy fathers, and to\l"
    .string "thy kindred; and I will be with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_4::
    .string "And Jacob sent and called Rachel\n"
    .string "and Leah to the field unto his\l"
    .string "flock,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_5::
    .string "And said unto them, I see your\n"
    .string "father’s countenance, that it is not\l"
    .string "toward me as before; but the God of my\l"
    .string "father hath been with me$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_6::
    .string "And ye know that with all my power\n"
    .string "I have served your father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_7::
    .string "And your father hath deceived me,\n"
    .string "and changed my wages ten times; but\l"
    .string "God suffered him not to hurt me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_8::
    .string "If he said thus, The speckled\n"
    .string "shall be thy wages; then all the\l"
    .string "cattle bare speckled: and if he\l"
    .string "said thus, The ringstraked shall be\l"
    .string "thy hire; then bare all the cattle\l"
    .string "ringstraked.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_9::
    .string "Thus God hath taken away the cattle\n"
    .string "of your father, and given them to me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_10::
    .string "And it came to pass at the time that\n"
    .string "the cattle conceived, that I lifted\l"
    .string "up mine eyes, and saw in a dream,\l"
    .string "and, behold, the rams which leaped\l"
    .string "upon the cattle were ringstraked,\l"
    .string "speckled, and grisled.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_11::
    .string "And the angel of God spake unto me\n"
    .string "in a dream, saying, Jacob: And I said,\l"
    .string "Here am I.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_12::
    .string "And he said, Lift up now thine eyes,\n"
    .string "and see, all the rams which leap\l"
    .string "upon the cattle are ringstraked,\l"
    .string "speckled, and grisled: for I have\l"
    .string "seen all that Laban doeth unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_13::
    .string "I am the God of Bethel, where thou\n"
    .string "anointedst the pillar, and where\l"
    .string "thou vowedst a vow unto me: now\l"
    .string "arise, get thee out from this land,\l"
    .string "and return unto the land of thy\l"
    .string "kindred.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_14::
    .string "And Rachel and Leah answered and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Is there yet any\l"
    .string "portion or inheritance for us in our\l"
    .string "father’s house?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_15::
    .string "Are we not counted of him strangers?\n"
    .string "for he hath sold us, and hath quite\l"
    .string "devoured also our money$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_16::
    .string "For all the riches which God hath\n"
    .string "taken from our father, that is ours,\l"
    .string "and our children’s: now then,\l"
    .string "whatsoever God hath said unto thee,\l"
    .string "do.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_17::
    .string "Then Jacob rose up, and set his sons\n"
    .string "and his wives upon camels;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_18::
    .string "And he carried away all his\n"
    .string "cattle, and all his goods which he\l"
    .string "had gotten, the cattle of his\l"
    .string "getting, which he had gotten in\l"
    .string "Padanaram, for to go to Isaac his\l"
    .string "father in the land of Canaan$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_19::
    .string "And Laban went to shear his sheep:\n"
    .string "and Rachel had stolen the images\l"
    .string "that were her father’s.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_20::
    .string "And Jacob stole away unawares to\n"
    .string "Laban the Syrian, in that he told him\l"
    .string "not that he fled.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_21::
    .string "So he fled with all that he had;\n"
    .string "and he rose up, and passed over the\l"
    .string "river, and set his face toward the\l"
    .string "mount Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_22::
    .string "And it was told Laban on the third\n"
    .string "day that Jacob was fled.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_23::
    .string "And he took his brethren with him,\n"
    .string "and pursued after him seven days’\l"
    .string "journey; and they overtook him in the\l"
    .string "mount Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_24::
    .string "And God came to Laban the Syrian in\n"
    .string "a dream by night, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "Take heed that thou speak not to\l"
    .string "Jacob either good or bad.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_25::
    .string "Then Laban overtook Jacob. Now Jacob\n"
    .string "had pitched his tent in the mount:\l"
    .string "and Laban with his brethren pitched\l"
    .string "in the mount of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_26::
    .string "And Laban said to Jacob, What hast\n"
    .string "thou done, that thou hast stolen\l"
    .string "away unawares to me, and carried away\l"
    .string "my daughters, as captives taken with\l"
    .string "the sword?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_27::
    .string "Wherefore didst thou flee away\n"
    .string "secretly, and steal away from me;\l"
    .string "and didst not tell me, that I might\l"
    .string "have sent thee away with mirth, and\l"
    .string "with songs, with tabret, and with\l"
    .string "harp?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_28::
    .string "And hast not suffered me to kiss my\n"
    .string "sons and my daughters? thou hast now\l"
    .string "done foolishly in so doing$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_29::
    .string "It is in the power of my hand to do\n"
    .string "you hurt: but the God of your father\l"
    .string "spake unto me yesternight, saying,\l"
    .string "Take thou heed that thou speak not\l"
    .string "to Jacob either good or bad.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_30::
    .string "And now, though thou wouldest needs\n"
    .string "be gone, because thou sore longedst\l"
    .string "after thy father’s house, yet\l"
    .string "wherefore hast thou stolen my gods?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_31::
    .string "And Jacob answered and said to\n"
    .string "Laban, Because I was afraid: for I\l"
    .string "said, Peradventure thou wouldest\l"
    .string "take by force thy daughters from me$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_32::
    .string "With whomsoever thou findest thy\n"
    .string "gods, let him not live: before our\l"
    .string "brethren discern thou what is thine\l"
    .string "with me, and take it to thee. For\l"
    .string "Jacob knew not that Rachel had\l"
    .string "stolen them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_33::
    .string "And Laban went into Jacob’s tent,\n"
    .string "and into Leah’s tent, and into the\l"
    .string "two maidservants’ tents; but he found\l"
    .string "them not. Then went he out of Leah’s\l"
    .string "tent, and entered into Rachel’s tent.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_34::
    .string "Now Rachel had taken the images,\n"
    .string "and put them in the camel’s\l"
    .string "furniture, and sat upon them. And\l"
    .string "Laban searched all the tent, but\l"
    .string "found them not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_35::
    .string "And she said to her father, Let it\n"
    .string "not displease my lord that I cannot\l"
    .string "rise up before thee; for the custom\l"
    .string "of women is upon me. And he searched\l"
    .string "but found not the images.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_36::
    .string "And Jacob was wroth, and chode with\n"
    .string "Laban: and Jacob answered and said to\l"
    .string "Laban, What is my trespass? what is\l"
    .string "my sin, that thou hast so hotly\l"
    .string "pursued after me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_37::
    .string "Whereas thou hast searched all my\n"
    .string "stuff, what hast thou found of all\l"
    .string "thy household stuff? set it here\l"
    .string "before my brethren and thy brethren,\l"
    .string "that they may judge betwixt us both$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_38::
    .string "This twenty years have I been with\n"
    .string "thee; thy ewes and thy she goats have\l"
    .string "not cast their young, and the rams of\l"
    .string "thy flock have I not eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_39::
    .string "That which was torn of beasts I\n"
    .string "brought not unto thee; I bare the\l"
    .string "loss of it; of my hand didst thou\l"
    .string "require it, whether stolen by day,\l"
    .string "or stolen by night.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_40::
    .string "Thus I was; in the day the drought\n"
    .string "consumed me, and the frost by night;\l"
    .string "and my sleep departed from mine\l"
    .string "eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_41::
    .string "Thus have I been twenty years in thy\n"
    .string "house; I served thee fourteen years\l"
    .string "for thy two daughters, and six years\l"
    .string "for thy cattle: and thou hast\l"
    .string "changed my wages ten times.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_42::
    .string "Except the God of my father, the God\n"
    .string "of Abraham, and the fear of Isaac,\l"
    .string "had been with me, surely thou hadst\l"
    .string "sent me away now empty. God hath seen\l"
    .string "mine affliction and the labour of\l"
    .string "my hands, and rebuked thee\l"
    .string "yesternight.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_43::
    .string "And Laban answered and said unto\n"
    .string "Jacob, These daughters are my\l"
    .string "daughters, and these children are my\l"
    .string "children, and these cattle are my\l"
    .string "cattle, and all that thou seest is\l"
    .string "mine: and what can I do this day unto\l"
    .string "these my daughters, or unto their\l"
    .string "children which they have born?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_44::
    .string "Now therefore come thou, let us\n"
    .string "make a covenant, I and thou; and let\l"
    .string "it be for a witness between me and\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_45::
    .string "And Jacob took a stone, and set it\n"
    .string "up for a pillar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_46::
    .string "And Jacob said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "Gather stones; and they took stones,\l"
    .string "and made an heap: and they did eat\l"
    .string "there upon the heap.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_47::
    .string "And Laban called it\n"
    .string "Jegarsahadutha: but Jacob called it\l"
    .string "Galeed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_48::
    .string "And Laban said, This heap is a\n"
    .string "witness between me and thee this day.\l"
    .string "Therefore was the name of it called\l"
    .string "Galeed;$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_49::
    .string "And Mizpah; for he said, The LORD\n"
    .string "watch between me and thee, when we\l"
    .string "are absent one from another.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_50::
    .string "If thou shalt afflict my\n"
    .string "daughters, or if thou shalt take\l"
    .string "other wives beside my daughters, no\l"
    .string "man is with us; see, God is witness\l"
    .string "betwixt me and thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_51::
    .string "And Laban said to Jacob, Behold\n"
    .string "this heap, and behold this\l"
    .string "pillar, which I have cast betwixt me\l"
    .string "and thee:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_52::
    .string "This heap be witness, and this\n"
    .string "pillar be witness, that I will not\l"
    .string "pass over this heap to thee, and that\l"
    .string "thou shalt not pass over this heap\l"
    .string "and this pillar unto me, for harm$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_53::
    .string "The God of Abraham, and the God of\n"
    .string "Nahor, the God of their father, judge\l"
    .string "betwixt us. And Jacob sware by the\l"
    .string "fear of his father Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_54::
    .string "Then Jacob offered sacrifice upon\n"
    .string "the mount, and called his brethren\l"
    .string "to eat bread: and they did eat bread,\l"
    .string "and tarried all night in the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_31_55::
    .string "And early in the morning Laban rose\n"
    .string "up, and kissed his sons and his\l"
    .string "daughters, and blessed them: and\l"
    .string "Laban departed, and returned unto\l"
    .string "his place.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_1::
    .string "And Jacob went on his way, and the\n"
    .string "angels of God met him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_2::
    .string "And when Jacob saw them, he said,\n"
    .string "This is God’s host: and he called\l"
    .string "the name of that place Mahanaim.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_3::
    .string "And Jacob sent messengers before\n"
    .string "him to Esau his brother unto the\l"
    .string "land of Seir, the country of Edom.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_4::
    .string "And he commanded them, saying, Thus\n"
    .string "shall ye speak unto my lord Esau;\l"
    .string "Thy servant Jacob saith thus, I have\l"
    .string "sojourned with Laban, and stayed\l"
    .string "there until now:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_5::
    .string "And I have oxen, and asses, flocks,\n"
    .string "and menservants, and womenservants:\l"
    .string "and I have sent to tell my lord,\l"
    .string "that I may find grace in thy sight$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_6::
    .string "And the messengers returned to\n"
    .string "Jacob, saying, We came to thy brother\l"
    .string "Esau, and also he cometh to meet\l"
    .string "thee, and four hundred men with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_7::
    .string "Then Jacob was greatly afraid and\n"
    .string "distressed: and he divided the\l"
    .string "people that was with him, and the\l"
    .string "flocks, and herds, and the camels,\l"
    .string "into two bands;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_8::
    .string "And said, If Esau come to the one\n"
    .string "company, and smite it, then the\l"
    .string "other company which is left shall\l"
    .string "escape$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_9::
    .string "And Jacob said, O God of my father\n"
    .string "Abraham, and God of my father Isaac,\l"
    .string "the LORD which saidst unto me, Return\l"
    .string "unto thy country, and to thy kindred,\l"
    .string "and I will deal well with thee:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_10::
    .string "I am not worthy of the least of\n"
    .string "all the mercies, and of all the\l"
    .string "truth, which thou hast shewed unto\l"
    .string "thy servant; for with my staff I\l"
    .string "passed over this Jordan; and now I am\l"
    .string "become two bands$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_11::
    .string "Deliver me, I pray thee, from the\n"
    .string "hand of my brother, from the hand of\l"
    .string "Esau: for I fear him, lest he will\l"
    .string "come and smite me, and the mother\l"
    .string "with the children.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_12::
    .string "And thou saidst, I will surely do\n"
    .string "thee good, and make thy seed as the\l"
    .string "sand of the sea, which cannot be\l"
    .string "numbered for multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_13::
    .string "And he lodged there that same\n"
    .string "night; and took of that which came to\l"
    .string "his hand a present for Esau his\l"
    .string "brother;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_14::
    .string "Two hundred she goats, and twenty he\n"
    .string "goats, two hundred ewes, and twenty\l"
    .string "rams,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_15::
    .string "Thirty milch camels with their\n"
    .string "colts, forty kine, and ten bulls,\l"
    .string "twenty she asses, and ten foals$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_16::
    .string "And he delivered them into the hand\n"
    .string "of his servants, every drove by\l"
    .string "themselves; and said unto his\l"
    .string "servants, Pass over before me, and\l"
    .string "put a space betwixt drove and drove.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_17::
    .string "And he commanded the foremost,\n"
    .string "saying, When Esau my brother meeteth\l"
    .string "thee, and asketh thee, saying, Whose\l"
    .string "art thou? and whither goest thou? and\l"
    .string "whose are these before thee?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_18::
    .string "Then thou shalt say, They be thy\n"
    .string "servant Jacob’s; it is a present\l"
    .string "sent unto my lord Esau: and, behold,\l"
    .string "also he is behind us$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_19::
    .string "And so commanded he the second, and\n"
    .string "the third, and all that followed\l"
    .string "the droves, saying, On this manner\l"
    .string "shall ye speak unto Esau, when ye\l"
    .string "find him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_20::
    .string "And say ye moreover, Behold, thy\n"
    .string "servant Jacob is behind us. For he\l"
    .string "said, I will appease him with the\l"
    .string "present that goeth before me, and\l"
    .string "afterward I will see his face;\l"
    .string "peradventure he will accept of me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_21::
    .string "So went the present over before\n"
    .string "him: and himself lodged that night\l"
    .string "in the company.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_22::
    .string "And he rose up that night, and took\n"
    .string "his two wives, and his two\l"
    .string "womenservants, and his eleven sons,\l"
    .string "and passed over the ford Jabbok.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_23::
    .string "And he took them, and sent them over\n"
    .string "the brook, and sent over that he had.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_24::
    .string "And Jacob was left alone; and there\n"
    .string "wrestled a man with him until the\l"
    .string "breaking of the day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_25::
    .string "And when he saw that he prevailed\n"
    .string "not against him, he touched the\l"
    .string "hollow of his thigh; and the\l"
    .string "hollow of Jacob’s thigh was out of\l"
    .string "joint, as he wrestled with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_26::
    .string "And he said, Let me go, for the day\n"
    .string "breaketh. And he said, I will not\l"
    .string "let thee go, except thou bless me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_27::
    .string "And he said unto him, What is thy\n"
    .string "name? And he said, Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_28::
    .string "And he said, Thy name shall be\n"
    .string "called no more Jacob, but Israel:\l"
    .string "for as a prince hast thou power with\l"
    .string "God and with men, and hast\l"
    .string "prevailed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_29::
    .string "And Jacob asked him, and said, Tell\n"
    .string "me, I pray thee, thy name. And he\l"
    .string "said, Wherefore is it that thou dost\l"
    .string "ask after my name? And he blessed him\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_30::
    .string "And Jacob called the name of the\n"
    .string "place Peniel: for I have seen God\l"
    .string "face to face, and my life is\l"
    .string "preserved.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_31::
    .string "And as he passed over Penuel the\n"
    .string "sun rose upon him, and he halted\l"
    .string "upon his thigh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_32_32::
    .string "Therefore the children of Israel\n"
    .string "eat not of the sinew which shrank,\l"
    .string "which is upon the hollow of the\l"
    .string "thigh, unto this day: because he\l"
    .string "touched the hollow of Jacob’s thigh\l"
    .string "in the sinew that shrank.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_1::
    .string "And Jacob lifted up his eyes, and\n"
    .string "looked, and, behold, Esau came, and\l"
    .string "with him four hundred men. And he\l"
    .string "divided the children unto Leah, and\l"
    .string "unto Rachel, and unto the two\l"
    .string "handmaids.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_2::
    .string "And he put the handmaids and their\n"
    .string "children foremost, and Leah and her\l"
    .string "children after, and Rachel and\l"
    .string "Joseph hindermost.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_3::
    .string "And he passed over before them, and\n"
    .string "bowed himself to the ground seven\l"
    .string "times, until he came near to his\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_4::
    .string "And Esau ran to meet him, and\n"
    .string "embraced him, and fell on his neck,\l"
    .string "and kissed him: and they wept.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_5::
    .string "And he lifted up his eyes, and saw\n"
    .string "the women and the children; and\l"
    .string "said, Who are those with thee? And he\l"
    .string "said, The children which God hath\l"
    .string "graciously given thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_6::
    .string "Then the handmaidens came near, they\n"
    .string "and their children, and they bowed\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_7::
    .string "And Leah also with her children\n"
    .string "came near, and bowed themselves: and\l"
    .string "after came Joseph near and Rachel,\l"
    .string "and they bowed themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_8::
    .string "And he said, What meanest thou by\n"
    .string "all this drove which I met? And he\l"
    .string "said, These are to find grace in the\l"
    .string "sight of my lord.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_9::
    .string "And Esau said, I have enough, my\n"
    .string "brother; keep that thou hast unto\l"
    .string "thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_10::
    .string "And Jacob said, Nay, I pray thee, if\n"
    .string "now I have found grace in thy sight,\l"
    .string "then receive my present at my hand:\l"
    .string "for therefore I have seen thy face,\l"
    .string "as though I had seen the face of God,\l"
    .string "and thou wast pleased with me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_11::
    .string "Take, I pray thee, my blessing that\n"
    .string "is brought to thee; because God hath\l"
    .string "dealt graciously with me, and\l"
    .string "because I have enough. And he urged\l"
    .string "him, and he took it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_12::
    .string "And he said, Let us take our\n"
    .string "journey, and let us go, and I will\l"
    .string "go before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_13::
    .string "And he said unto him, My lord\n"
    .string "knoweth that the children are\l"
    .string "tender, and the flocks and herds\l"
    .string "with young are with me: and if men\l"
    .string "should overdrive them one day, all\l"
    .string "the flock will die.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_14::
    .string "Let my lord, I pray thee, pass\n"
    .string "over before his servant: and I will\l"
    .string "lead on softly, according as the\l"
    .string "cattle that goeth before me and the\l"
    .string "children be able to endure, until I\l"
    .string "come unto my lord unto Seir.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_15::
    .string "And Esau said, Let me now leave with\n"
    .string "thee some of the folk that are with\l"
    .string "me. And he said, What needeth it? let\l"
    .string "me find grace in the sight of my lord.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_16::
    .string "So Esau returned that day on his way\n"
    .string "unto Seir.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_17::
    .string "And Jacob journeyed to Succoth, and\n"
    .string "built him an house, and made booths\l"
    .string "for his cattle: therefore the name\l"
    .string "of the place is called Succoth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_18::
    .string "And Jacob came to Shalem, a city of\n"
    .string "Shechem, which is in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, when he came from Padanaram;\l"
    .string "and pitched his tent before the city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_19::
    .string "And he bought a parcel of a field,\n"
    .string "where he had spread his tent, at the\l"
    .string "hand of the children of Hamor,\l"
    .string "Shechem’s father, for an hundred\l"
    .string "pieces of money.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_33_20::
    .string "And he erected there an altar, and\n"
    .string "called it EleloheIsrael.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_1::
    .string "And Dinah the daughter of Leah,\n"
    .string "which she bare unto Jacob, went out\l"
    .string "to see the daughters of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_2::
    .string "And when Shechem the son of Hamor\n"
    .string "the Hivite, prince of the country,\l"
    .string "saw her, he took her, and lay with\l"
    .string "her, and defiled her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_3::
    .string "And his soul clave unto Dinah the\n"
    .string "daughter of Jacob, and he loved the\l"
    .string "damsel, and spake kindly unto the\l"
    .string "damsel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_4::
    .string "And Shechem spake unto his father\n"
    .string "Hamor, saying, Get me this damsel to\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_5::
    .string "And Jacob heard that he had defiled\n"
    .string "Dinah his daughter: now his sons were\l"
    .string "with his cattle in the field: and\l"
    .string "Jacob held his peace until they\l"
    .string "were come.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_6::
    .string "And Hamor the father of Shechem went\n"
    .string "out unto Jacob to commune with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_7::
    .string "And the sons of Jacob came out of\n"
    .string "the field when they heard it: and the\l"
    .string "men were grieved, and they were very\l"
    .string "wroth, because he had wrought folly\l"
    .string "in Israel in lying with Jacob’s\l"
    .string "daughter: which thing ought not to be\l"
    .string "done.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_8::
    .string "And Hamor communed with them,\n"
    .string "saying, The soul of my son Shechem\l"
    .string "longeth for your daughter: I pray\l"
    .string "you give her him to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_9::
    .string "And make ye marriages with us, and\n"
    .string "give your daughters unto us, and take\l"
    .string "our daughters unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_10::
    .string "And ye shall dwell with us: and\n"
    .string "the land shall be before you;\l"
    .string "dwell and trade ye therein, and get\l"
    .string "you possessions therein.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_11::
    .string "And Shechem said unto her father and\n"
    .string "unto her brethren, Let me find grace\l"
    .string "in your eyes, and what ye shall say\l"
    .string "unto me I will give.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_12::
    .string "Ask me never so much dowry and gift,\n"
    .string "and I will give according as ye\l"
    .string "shall say unto me: but give me the\l"
    .string "damsel to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_13::
    .string "And the sons of Jacob answered\n"
    .string "Shechem and Hamor his father\l"
    .string "deceitfully, and said, because he\l"
    .string "had defiled Dinah their sister:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_14::
    .string "And they said unto them, We cannot\n"
    .string "do this thing, to give our sister to\l"
    .string "one that is uncircumcised; for that\l"
    .string "were a reproach unto us:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_15::
    .string "But in this will we consent unto\n"
    .string "you: If ye will be as we be, that\l"
    .string "every male of you be circumcised;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_16::
    .string "Then will we give our daughters\n"
    .string "unto you, and we will take your\l"
    .string "daughters to us, and we will dwell\l"
    .string "with you, and we will become one\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_17::
    .string "But if ye will not hearken unto us,\n"
    .string "to be circumcised; then will we take\l"
    .string "our daughter, and we will be gone.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_18::
    .string "And their words pleased Hamor, and\n"
    .string "Shechem Hamor’s son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_19::
    .string "And the young man deferred not to do\n"
    .string "the thing, because he had delight in\l"
    .string "Jacob’s daughter: and he was more\l"
    .string "honourable than all the house of\l"
    .string "his father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_20::
    .string "And Hamor and Shechem his son came\n"
    .string "unto the gate of their city, and\l"
    .string "communed with the men of their city,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_21::
    .string "These men are peaceable with us;\n"
    .string "therefore let them dwell in the\l"
    .string "land, and trade therein; for the\l"
    .string "land, behold, it is large enough for\l"
    .string "them; let us take their daughters to\l"
    .string "us for wives, and let us give them\l"
    .string "our daughters$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_22::
    .string "Only herein will the men consent\n"
    .string "unto us for to dwell with us, to be\l"
    .string "one people, if every male among us\l"
    .string "be circumcised, as they are\l"
    .string "circumcised.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_23::
    .string "Shall not their cattle and their\n"
    .string "substance and every beast of theirs\l"
    .string "be ours? only let us consent unto\l"
    .string "them, and they will dwell with us.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_24::
    .string "And unto Hamor and unto Shechem his\n"
    .string "son hearkened all that went out of\l"
    .string "the gate of his city; and every male\l"
    .string "was circumcised, all that went out\l"
    .string "of the gate of his city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_25::
    .string "And it came to pass on the third\n"
    .string "day, when they were sore, that two of\l"
    .string "the sons of Jacob, Simeon and Levi,\l"
    .string "Dinah’s brethren, took each man his\l"
    .string "sword, and came upon the city\l"
    .string "boldly, and slew all the males.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_26::
    .string "And they slew Hamor and Shechem his\n"
    .string "son with the edge of the sword, and\l"
    .string "took Dinah out of Shechem’s house,\l"
    .string "and went out.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_27::
    .string "The sons of Jacob came upon the\n"
    .string "slain, and spoiled the city,\l"
    .string "because they had defiled their\l"
    .string "sister.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_28::
    .string "They took their sheep, and their\n"
    .string "oxen, and their asses, and that which\l"
    .string "was in the city, and that which was in\l"
    .string "the field,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_29::
    .string "And all their wealth, and all\n"
    .string "their little ones, and their wives\l"
    .string "took they captive, and spoiled even\l"
    .string "all that was in the house$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_30::
    .string "And Jacob said to Simeon and Levi,\n"
    .string "Ye have troubled me to make me to\l"
    .string "stink among the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "land, among the Canaanites and the\l"
    .string "Perizzites: and I being few in\l"
    .string "number, they shall gather\l"
    .string "themselves together against me, and\l"
    .string "slay me; and I shall be destroyed,\l"
    .string "I and my house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_34_31::
    .string "And they said, Should he deal with\n"
    .string "our sister as with an harlot?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_1::
    .string "And God said unto Jacob, Arise, go\n"
    .string "up to Bethel, and dwell there: and\l"
    .string "make there an altar unto God, that\l"
    .string "appeared unto thee when thou\l"
    .string "fleddest from the face of Esau thy\l"
    .string "brother$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_2::
    .string "Then Jacob said unto his household,\n"
    .string "and to all that were with him, Put\l"
    .string "away the strange gods that are among\l"
    .string "you, and be clean, and change your\l"
    .string "garments:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_3::
    .string "And let us arise, and go up to\n"
    .string "Bethel; and I will make there an\l"
    .string "altar unto God, who answered me in\l"
    .string "the day of my distress, and was with\l"
    .string "me in the way which I went$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_4::
    .string "And they gave unto Jacob all the\n"
    .string "strange gods which were in their\l"
    .string "hand, and all their earrings which\l"
    .string "were in their ears; and Jacob hid\l"
    .string "them under the oak which was by\l"
    .string "Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_5::
    .string "And they journeyed: and the terror\n"
    .string "of God was upon the cities that were\l"
    .string "round about them, and they did not\l"
    .string "pursue after the sons of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_6::
    .string "So Jacob came to Luz, which is in the\n"
    .string "land of Canaan, that is, Bethel, he\l"
    .string "and all the people that were with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_7::
    .string "And he built there an altar, and\n"
    .string "called the place Elbethel:\l"
    .string "because there God appeared unto\l"
    .string "him, when he fled from the face of\l"
    .string "his brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_8::
    .string "But Deborah Rebekah’s nurse died,\n"
    .string "and she was buried beneath Bethel\l"
    .string "under an oak: and the name of it was\l"
    .string "called Allonbachuth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_9::
    .string "And God appeared unto Jacob again,\n"
    .string "when he came out of Padanaram, and\l"
    .string "blessed him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_10::
    .string "And God said unto him, Thy name is\n"
    .string "Jacob: thy name shall not be\l"
    .string "called any more Jacob, but Israel\l"
    .string "shall be thy name: and he called\l"
    .string "his name Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_11::
    .string "And God said unto him, I am God\n"
    .string "Almighty: be fruitful and\l"
    .string "multiply; a nation and a company\l"
    .string "of nations shall be of thee, and\l"
    .string "kings shall come out of thy loins;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_12::
    .string "And the land which I gave Abraham\n"
    .string "and Isaac, to thee I will give it,\l"
    .string "and to thy seed after thee will I\l"
    .string "give the land$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_13::
    .string "And God went up from him in the\n"
    .string "place where he talked with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_14::
    .string "And Jacob set up a pillar in the\n"
    .string "place where he talked with him, even\l"
    .string "a pillar of stone: and he poured a\l"
    .string "drink offering thereon, and he\l"
    .string "poured oil thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_15::
    .string "And Jacob called the name of the\n"
    .string "place where God spake with him,\l"
    .string "Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_16::
    .string "And they journeyed from Bethel; and\n"
    .string "there was but a little way to come\l"
    .string "to Ephrath: and Rachel travailed,\l"
    .string "and she had hard labour.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, when she was in\n"
    .string "hard labour, that the midwife said\l"
    .string "unto her, Fear not; thou shalt have\l"
    .string "this son also.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, as her soul\n"
    .string "was in departing, (for she died)\l"
    .string "that she called his name Benoni: but\l"
    .string "his father called him Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_19::
    .string "And Rachel died, and was buried in\n"
    .string "the way to Ephrath, which is\l"
    .string "Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_20::
    .string "And Jacob set a pillar upon her\n"
    .string "grave: that is the pillar of\l"
    .string "Rachel’s grave unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_21::
    .string "And Israel journeyed, and spread\n"
    .string "his tent beyond the tower of Edar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_22::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Israel\n"
    .string "dwelt in that land, that Reuben went\l"
    .string "and lay with Bilhah his father’s\l"
    .string "concubine: and Israel heard it. Now\l"
    .string "the sons of Jacob were twelve:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_23::
    .string "The sons of Leah; Reuben, Jacob’s\n"
    .string "firstborn, and Simeon, and Levi, and\l"
    .string "Judah, and Issachar, and Zebulun:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_24::
    .string "The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and\n"
    .string "Benjamin:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_25::
    .string "And the sons of Bilhah, Rachel’s\n"
    .string "handmaid; Dan, and Naphtali:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_26::
    .string "And the sons of Zilpah, Leah’s\n"
    .string "handmaid: Gad, and Asher: these are\l"
    .string "the sons of Jacob, which were born to\l"
    .string "him in Padanaram$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_27::
    .string "And Jacob came unto Isaac his father\n"
    .string "unto Mamre, unto the city of Arbah,\l"
    .string "which is Hebron, where Abraham and\l"
    .string "Isaac sojourned.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_28::
    .string "And the days of Isaac were an\n"
    .string "hundred and fourscore years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_35_29::
    .string "And Isaac gave up the ghost, and\n"
    .string "died, and was gathered unto his\l"
    .string "people, being old and full of\l"
    .string "days: and his sons Esau and Jacob\l"
    .string "buried him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_1::
    .string "Now these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Esau, who is Edom.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_2::
    .string "Esau took his wives of the daughters\n"
    .string "of Canaan; Adah the daughter of Elon\l"
    .string "the Hittite, and Aholibamah the\l"
    .string "daughter of Anah the daughter of\l"
    .string "Zibeon the Hivite;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_3::
    .string "And Bashemath Ishmael’s daughter,\n"
    .string "sister of Nebajoth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_4::
    .string "And Adah bare to Esau Eliphaz; and\n"
    .string "Bashemath bare Reuel;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_5::
    .string "And Aholibamah bare Jeush, and\n"
    .string "Jaalam, and Korah: these are the\l"
    .string "sons of Esau, which were born unto\l"
    .string "him in the land of Canaan$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_6::
    .string "And Esau took his wives, and his\n"
    .string "sons, and his daughters, and all the\l"
    .string "persons of his house, and his\l"
    .string "cattle, and all his beasts, and\l"
    .string "all his substance, which he had got\l"
    .string "in the land of Canaan; and went into\l"
    .string "the country from the face of his\l"
    .string "brother Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_7::
    .string "For their riches were more than that\n"
    .string "they might dwell together; and the\l"
    .string "land wherein they were strangers\l"
    .string "could not bear them because of their\l"
    .string "cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_8::
    .string "Thus dwelt Esau in mount Seir: Esau\n"
    .string "is Edom.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_9::
    .string "And these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Esau the father of the Edomites in\l"
    .string "mount Seir:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_10::
    .string "These are the names of Esau’s sons;\n"
    .string "Eliphaz the son of Adah the wife of\l"
    .string "Esau, Reuel the son of Bashemath the\l"
    .string "wife of Esau$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_11::
    .string "And the sons of Eliphaz were Teman,\n"
    .string "Omar, Zepho, and Gatam, and Kenaz.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_12::
    .string "And Timna was concubine to Eliphaz\n"
    .string "Esau’s son; and she bare to Eliphaz\l"
    .string "Amalek: these were the sons of Adah\l"
    .string "Esau’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_13::
    .string "And these are the sons of Reuel;\n"
    .string "Nahath, and Zerah, Shammah, and\l"
    .string "Mizzah: these were the sons of\l"
    .string "Bashemath Esau’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_14::
    .string "And these were the sons of\n"
    .string "Aholibamah, the daughter of Anah the\l"
    .string "daughter of Zibeon, Esau’s wife: and\l"
    .string "she bare to Esau Jeush, and Jaalam,\l"
    .string "and Korah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_15::
    .string "These were dukes of the sons of\n"
    .string "Esau: the sons of Eliphaz the\l"
    .string "firstborn son of Esau; duke Teman,\l"
    .string "duke Omar, duke Zepho, duke Kenaz,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_16::
    .string "Duke Korah, duke Gatam, and duke\n"
    .string "Amalek: these are the dukes that\l"
    .string "came of Eliphaz in the land of\l"
    .string "Edom; these were the sons of Adah$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_17::
    .string "And these are the sons of Reuel\n"
    .string "Esau’s son; duke Nahath, duke Zerah,\l"
    .string "duke Shammah, duke Mizzah: these are\l"
    .string "the dukes that came of Reuel in the\l"
    .string "land of Edom; these are the sons of\l"
    .string "Bashemath Esau’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_18::
    .string "And these are the sons of\n"
    .string "Aholibamah Esau’s wife; duke Jeush,\l"
    .string "duke Jaalam, duke Korah: these were\l"
    .string "the dukes that came of Aholibamah\l"
    .string "the daughter of Anah, Esau’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_19::
    .string "These are the sons of Esau, who is\n"
    .string "Edom, and these are their dukes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_20::
    .string "These are the sons of Seir the\n"
    .string "Horite, who inhabited the land;\l"
    .string "Lotan, and Shobal, and Zibeon, and\l"
    .string "Anah,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_21::
    .string "And Dishon, and Ezer, and Dishan:\n"
    .string "these are the dukes of the Horites,\l"
    .string "the children of Seir in the land of\l"
    .string "Edom$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_22::
    .string "And the children of Lotan were Hori\n"
    .string "and Hemam; and Lotan’s sister was\l"
    .string "Timna.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_23::
    .string "And the children of Shobal were\n"
    .string "these; Alvan, and Manahath, and\l"
    .string "Ebal, Shepho, and Onam.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_24::
    .string "And these are the children of\n"
    .string "Zibeon; both Ajah, and Anah: this was\l"
    .string "that Anah that found the mules in\l"
    .string "the wilderness, as he fed the asses\l"
    .string "of Zibeon his father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_25::
    .string "And the children of Anah were\n"
    .string "these; Dishon, and Aholibamah the\l"
    .string "daughter of Anah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_26::
    .string "And these are the children of\n"
    .string "Dishon; Hemdan, and Eshban, and\l"
    .string "Ithran, and Cheran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_27::
    .string "The children of Ezer are these;\n"
    .string "Bilhan, and Zaavan, and Akan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_28::
    .string "The children of Dishan are these;\n"
    .string "Uz, and Aran.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_29::
    .string "These are the dukes that came of the\n"
    .string "Horites; duke Lotan, duke Shobal,\l"
    .string "duke Zibeon, duke Anah,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_30::
    .string "Duke Dishon, duke Ezer, duke Dishan:\n"
    .string "these are the dukes that came of\l"
    .string "Hori, among their dukes in the land\l"
    .string "of Seir$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_31::
    .string "And these are the kings that reigned\n"
    .string "in the land of Edom, before there\l"
    .string "reigned any king over the children\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_32::
    .string "And Bela the son of Beor reigned in\n"
    .string "Edom: and the name of his city was\l"
    .string "Dinhabah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_33::
    .string "And Bela died, and Jobab the son of\n"
    .string "Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_34::
    .string "And Jobab died, and Husham of the\n"
    .string "land of Temani reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_35::
    .string "And Husham died, and Hadad the son\n"
    .string "of Bedad, who smote Midian in the\l"
    .string "field of Moab, reigned in his stead:\l"
    .string "and the name of his city was Avith.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_36::
    .string "And Hadad died, and Samlah of\n"
    .string "Masrekah reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_37::
    .string "And Samlah died, and Saul of\n"
    .string "Rehoboth by the river reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_38::
    .string "And Saul died, and Baalhanan the\n"
    .string "son of Achbor reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_39::
    .string "And Baalhanan the son of Achbor\n"
    .string "died, and Hadar reigned in his stead:\l"
    .string "and the name of his city was Pau; and\l"
    .string "his wife’s name was Mehetabel, the\l"
    .string "daughter of Matred, the daughter of\l"
    .string "Mezahab.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_40::
    .string "And these are the names of the dukes\n"
    .string "that came of Esau, according to their\l"
    .string "families, after their places, by\l"
    .string "their names; duke Timnah, duke\l"
    .string "Alvah, duke Jetheth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_41::
    .string "Duke Aholibamah, duke Elah, duke\n"
    .string "Pinon,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_42::
    .string "Duke Kenaz, duke Teman, duke Mibzar,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_36_43::
    .string "Duke Magdiel, duke Iram: these be\n"
    .string "the dukes of Edom, according to their\l"
    .string "habitations in the land of their\l"
    .string "possession: he is Esau the father of\l"
    .string "the Edomites$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_1::
    .string "And Jacob dwelt in the land\n"
    .string "wherein his father was a stranger, in\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_2::
    .string "These are the generations of Jacob.\n"
    .string "Joseph, being seventeen years old,\l"
    .string "was feeding the flock with his\l"
    .string "brethren; and the lad was with the\l"
    .string "sons of Bilhah, and with the sons of\l"
    .string "Zilpah, his father’s wives: and\l"
    .string "Joseph brought unto his father their\l"
    .string "evil report.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_3::
    .string "Now Israel loved Joseph more than\n"
    .string "all his children, because he was\l"
    .string "the son of his old age: and he made\l"
    .string "him a coat of many colours.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_4::
    .string "And when his brethren saw that their\n"
    .string "father loved him more than all his\l"
    .string "brethren, they hated him, and could\l"
    .string "not speak peaceably unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_5::
    .string "And Joseph dreamed a dream, and he\n"
    .string "told it his brethren: and they hated\l"
    .string "him yet the more.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_6::
    .string "And he said unto them, Hear, I pray\n"
    .string "you, this dream which I have dreamed:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_7::
    .string "For, behold, we were binding\n"
    .string "sheaves in the field, and, lo, my\l"
    .string "sheaf arose, and also stood\l"
    .string "upright; and, behold, your sheaves\l"
    .string "stood round about, and made obeisance\l"
    .string "to my sheaf$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_8::
    .string "And his brethren said to him, Shalt\n"
    .string "thou indeed reign over us? or shalt\l"
    .string "thou indeed have dominion over us?\l"
    .string "And they hated him yet the more for\l"
    .string "his dreams, and for his words.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_9::
    .string "And he dreamed yet another dream,\n"
    .string "and told it his brethren, and said,\l"
    .string "Behold, I have dreamed a dream more;\l"
    .string "and, behold, the sun and the moon and\l"
    .string "the eleven stars made obeisance to\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_10::
    .string "And he told it to his father, and to\n"
    .string "his brethren: and his father rebuked\l"
    .string "him, and said unto him, What is this\l"
    .string "dream that thou hast dreamed? Shall\l"
    .string "I and thy mother and thy brethren\l"
    .string "indeed come to bow down ourselves to\l"
    .string "thee to the earth?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_11::
    .string "And his brethren envied him; but his\n"
    .string "father observed the saying$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_12::
    .string "And his brethren went to feed their\n"
    .string "father’s flock in Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_13::
    .string "And Israel said unto Joseph, Do not\n"
    .string "thy brethren feed the flock in\l"
    .string "Shechem? come, and I will send thee\l"
    .string "unto them. And he said to him, Here am\l"
    .string "I.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_14::
    .string "And he said to him, Go, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "see whether it be well with thy\l"
    .string "brethren, and well with the flocks;\l"
    .string "and bring me word again. So he sent\l"
    .string "him out of the vale of Hebron, and he\l"
    .string "came to Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_15::
    .string "And a certain man found him, and,\n"
    .string "behold, he was wandering in the\l"
    .string "field: and the man asked him, saying,\l"
    .string "What seekest thou?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_16::
    .string "And he said, I seek my brethren:\n"
    .string "tell me, I pray thee, where they\l"
    .string "feed their flocks$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_17::
    .string "And the man said, They are departed\n"
    .string "hence; for I heard them say, Let us go\l"
    .string "to Dothan. And Joseph went after his\l"
    .string "brethren, and found them in Dothan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_18::
    .string "And when they saw him afar off, even\n"
    .string "before he came near unto them, they\l"
    .string "conspired against him to slay him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_19::
    .string "And they said one to another,\n"
    .string "Behold, this dreamer cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_20::
    .string "Come now therefore, and let us slay\n"
    .string "him, and cast him into some pit, and\l"
    .string "we will say, Some evil beast hath\l"
    .string "devoured him: and we shall see what\l"
    .string "will become of his dreams.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_21::
    .string "And Reuben heard it, and he\n"
    .string "delivered him out of their hands;\l"
    .string "and said, Let us not kill him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_22::
    .string "And Reuben said unto them, Shed no\n"
    .string "blood, but cast him into this pit\l"
    .string "that is in the wilderness, and lay\l"
    .string "no hand upon him; that he might rid\l"
    .string "him out of their hands, to deliver\l"
    .string "him to his father again.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joseph\n"
    .string "was come unto his brethren, that they\l"
    .string "stript Joseph out of his coat, his\l"
    .string "coat of many colours that was on him;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_24::
    .string "And they took him, and cast him into\n"
    .string "a pit: and the pit was empty, there\l"
    .string "was no water in it$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_25::
    .string "And they sat down to eat bread: and\n"
    .string "they lifted up their eyes and\l"
    .string "looked, and, behold, a company of\l"
    .string "Ishmeelites came from Gilead with\l"
    .string "their camels bearing spicery and\l"
    .string "balm and myrrh, going to carry it\l"
    .string "down to Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_26::
    .string "And Judah said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "What profit is it if we slay our\l"
    .string "brother, and conceal his blood?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_27::
    .string "Come, and let us sell him to the\n"
    .string "Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be\l"
    .string "upon him; for he is our brother and\l"
    .string "our flesh. And his brethren were\l"
    .string "content$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_28::
    .string "Then there passed by Midianites\n"
    .string "merchantmen; and they drew and\l"
    .string "lifted up Joseph out of the pit,\l"
    .string "and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites\l"
    .string "for twenty pieces of silver: and\l"
    .string "they brought Joseph into Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_29::
    .string "And Reuben returned unto the pit;\n"
    .string "and, behold, Joseph was not in the\l"
    .string "pit; and he rent his clothes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_30::
    .string "And he returned unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "and said, The child is not; and I,\l"
    .string "whither shall I go?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_31::
    .string "And they took Joseph’s coat, and\n"
    .string "killed a kid of the goats, and\l"
    .string "dipped the coat in the blood;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_32::
    .string "And they sent the coat of many\n"
    .string "colours, and they brought it to\l"
    .string "their father; and said, This have we\l"
    .string "found: know now whether it be thy\l"
    .string "son’s coat or no$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_33::
    .string "And he knew it, and said, It is my\n"
    .string "son’s coat; an evil beast hath\l"
    .string "devoured him; Joseph is without\l"
    .string "doubt rent in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_34::
    .string "And Jacob rent his clothes, and put\n"
    .string "sackcloth upon his loins, and\l"
    .string "mourned for his son many days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_35::
    .string "And all his sons and all his\n"
    .string "daughters rose up to comfort him;\l"
    .string "but he refused to be comforted; and\l"
    .string "he said, For I will go down into the\l"
    .string "grave unto my son mourning. Thus his\l"
    .string "father wept for him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_37_36::
    .string "And the Midianites sold him into\n"
    .string "Egypt unto Potiphar, an officer of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s, and captain of the guard.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_1::
    .string "And it came to pass at that time,\n"
    .string "that Judah went down from his\l"
    .string "brethren, and turned in to a certain\l"
    .string "Adullamite, whose name was Hirah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_2::
    .string "And Judah saw there a daughter of a\n"
    .string "certain Canaanite, whose name was\l"
    .string "Shuah; and he took her, and went in\l"
    .string "unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_3::
    .string "And she conceived, and bare a son;\n"
    .string "and he called his name Er.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_4::
    .string "And she conceived again, and bare a\n"
    .string "son; and she called his name Onan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_5::
    .string "And she yet again conceived, and\n"
    .string "bare a son; and called his name\l"
    .string "Shelah: and he was at Chezib, when\l"
    .string "she bare him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_6::
    .string "And Judah took a wife for Er his\n"
    .string "firstborn, whose name was Tamar.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_7::
    .string "And Er, Judah’s firstborn, was\n"
    .string "wicked in the sight of the LORD; and\l"
    .string "the LORD slew him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_8::
    .string "And Judah said unto Onan, Go in unto\n"
    .string "thy brother’s wife, and marry her,\l"
    .string "and raise up seed to thy brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_9::
    .string "And Onan knew that the seed should\n"
    .string "not be his; and it came to pass, when\l"
    .string "he went in unto his brother’s wife,\l"
    .string "that he spilled it on the ground,\l"
    .string "lest that he should give seed to his\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_10::
    .string "And the thing which he did\n"
    .string "displeased the LORD: wherefore he\l"
    .string "slew him also.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_11::
    .string "Then said Judah to Tamar his\n"
    .string "daughter in law, Remain a widow at\l"
    .string "thy father’s house, till Shelah my\l"
    .string "son be grown: for he said, Lest\l"
    .string "peradventure he die also, as his\l"
    .string "brethren did. And Tamar went and\l"
    .string "dwelt in her father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_12::
    .string "And in process of time the daughter\n"
    .string "of Shuah Judah’s wife died; and Judah\l"
    .string "was comforted, and went up unto his\l"
    .string "sheepshearers to Timnath, he and his\l"
    .string "friend Hirah the Adullamite.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_13::
    .string "And it was told Tamar, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold thy father in law goeth up\l"
    .string "to Timnath to shear his sheep.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_14::
    .string "And she put her widow’s garments\n"
    .string "off from her, and covered her with a\l"
    .string "vail, and wrapped herself, and sat\l"
    .string "in an open place, which is by the\l"
    .string "way to Timnath; for she saw that\l"
    .string "Shelah was grown, and she was not\l"
    .string "given unto him to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_15::
    .string "When Judah saw her, he thought her\n"
    .string "to be an harlot; because she had\l"
    .string "covered her face.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_16::
    .string "And he turned unto her by the way,\n"
    .string "and said, Go to, I pray thee, let me\l"
    .string "come in unto thee; (for he knew not\l"
    .string "that she was his daughter in law.)\l"
    .string "And she said, What wilt thou give me,\l"
    .string "that thou mayest come in unto me?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_17::
    .string "And he said, I will send thee a kid\n"
    .string "from the flock. And she said, Wilt\l"
    .string "thou give me a pledge, till thou\l"
    .string "send it?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_18::
    .string "And he said, What pledge shall I\n"
    .string "give thee? And she said, Thy signet,\l"
    .string "and thy bracelets, and thy staff\l"
    .string "that is in thine hand. And he gave it\l"
    .string "her, and came in unto her, and she\l"
    .string "conceived by him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_19::
    .string "And she arose, and went away, and\n"
    .string "laid by her vail from her, and put\l"
    .string "on the garments of her widowhood.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_20::
    .string "And Judah sent the kid by the hand\n"
    .string "of his friend the Adullamite, to\l"
    .string "receive his pledge from the woman’s\l"
    .string "hand: but he found her not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_21::
    .string "Then he asked the men of that\n"
    .string "place, saying, Where is the harlot,\l"
    .string "that was openly by the way side? And\l"
    .string "they said, There was no harlot in\l"
    .string "this place.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_22::
    .string "And he returned to Judah, and said,\n"
    .string "I cannot find her; and also the men\l"
    .string "of the place said, that there was no\l"
    .string "harlot in this place.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_23::
    .string "And Judah said, Let her take it to\n"
    .string "her, lest we be shamed: behold, I\l"
    .string "sent this kid, and thou hast not\l"
    .string "found her.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_24::
    .string "And it came to pass about three\n"
    .string "months after, that it was told\l"
    .string "Judah, saying, Tamar thy daughter in\l"
    .string "law hath played the harlot; and\l"
    .string "also, behold, she is with child by\l"
    .string "whoredom. And Judah said, Bring her\l"
    .string "forth, and let her be burnt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_25::
    .string "When she was brought forth, she sent\n"
    .string "to her father in law, saying, By the\l"
    .string "man, whose these are, am I with\l"
    .string "child: and she said, Discern, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, whose are these, the signet,\l"
    .string "and bracelets, and staff.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_26::
    .string "And Judah acknowledged them, and\n"
    .string "said, She hath been more righteous\l"
    .string "than I; because that I gave her not to\l"
    .string "Shelah my son. And he knew her again\l"
    .string "no more.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_27::
    .string "And it came to pass in the time of\n"
    .string "her travail, that, behold, twins\l"
    .string "were in her womb.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_28::
    .string "And it came to pass, when she\n"
    .string "travailed, that the one put out his\l"
    .string "hand: and the midwife took and bound\l"
    .string "upon his hand a scarlet thread,\l"
    .string "saying, This came out first.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he drew back\n"
    .string "his hand, that, behold, his brother\l"
    .string "came out: and she said, How hast thou\l"
    .string "broken forth? this breach be upon\l"
    .string "thee: therefore his name was called\l"
    .string "Pharez.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_38_30::
    .string "And afterward came out his brother,\n"
    .string "that had the scarlet thread upon\l"
    .string "his hand: and his name was called\l"
    .string "Zarah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_1::
    .string "And Joseph was brought down to\n"
    .string "Egypt; and Potiphar, an officer of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, captain of the guard, an\l"
    .string "Egyptian, bought him of the hands of\l"
    .string "the Ishmeelites, which had brought\l"
    .string "him down thither.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_2::
    .string "And the LORD was with Joseph, and he\n"
    .string "was a prosperous man; and he was in\l"
    .string "the house of his master the Egyptian.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_3::
    .string "And his master saw that the LORD was\n"
    .string "with him, and that the LORD made all\l"
    .string "that he did to prosper in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_4::
    .string "And Joseph found grace in his\n"
    .string "sight, and he served him: and he made\l"
    .string "him overseer over his house, and all\l"
    .string "that he had he put into his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_5::
    .string "And it came to pass from the time\n"
    .string "that he had made him overseer in his\l"
    .string "house, and over all that he had,\l"
    .string "that the LORD blessed the\l"
    .string "Egyptian’s house for Joseph’s sake;\l"
    .string "and the blessing of the LORD was\l"
    .string "upon all that he had in the house,\l"
    .string "and in the field.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_6::
    .string "And he left all that he had in\n"
    .string "Joseph’s hand; and he knew not ought\l"
    .string "he had, save the bread which he did\l"
    .string "eat. And Joseph was a goodly\l"
    .string "person, and well favoured.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_7::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that his master’s wife cast\l"
    .string "her eyes upon Joseph; and she said,\l"
    .string "Lie with me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_8::
    .string "But he refused, and said unto his\n"
    .string "master’s wife, Behold, my master\l"
    .string "wotteth not what is with me in the\l"
    .string "house, and he hath committed all\l"
    .string "that he hath to my hand;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_9::
    .string "There is none greater in this house\n"
    .string "than I; neither hath he kept back any\l"
    .string "thing from me but thee, because thou\l"
    .string "art his wife: how then can I do this\l"
    .string "great wickedness, and sin against\l"
    .string "God?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, as she spake\n"
    .string "to Joseph day by day, that he\l"
    .string "hearkened not unto her, to lie by\l"
    .string "her, or to be with her$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_11::
    .string "And it came to pass about this time,\n"
    .string "that Joseph went into the house to\l"
    .string "do his business; and there was none\l"
    .string "of the men of the house there within.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_12::
    .string "And she caught him by his garment,\n"
    .string "saying, Lie with me: and he left his\l"
    .string "garment in her hand, and fled, and\l"
    .string "got him out.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, when she saw\n"
    .string "that he had left his garment in her\l"
    .string "hand, and was fled forth,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_14::
    .string "That she called unto the men of her\n"
    .string "house, and spake unto them, saying,\l"
    .string "See, he hath brought in an Hebrew\l"
    .string "unto us to mock us; he came in unto me\l"
    .string "to lie with me, and I cried with a\l"
    .string "loud voice:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he heard\n"
    .string "that I lifted up my voice and cried,\l"
    .string "that he left his garment with me, and\l"
    .string "fled, and got him out$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_16::
    .string "And she laid up his garment by her,\n"
    .string "until his lord came home.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_17::
    .string "And she spake unto him according to\n"
    .string "these words, saying, The Hebrew\l"
    .string "servant, which thou hast brought unto\l"
    .string "us, came in unto me to mock me:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, as I lifted up\n"
    .string "my voice and cried, that he left his\l"
    .string "garment with me, and fled out$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, when his master\n"
    .string "heard the words of his wife, which\l"
    .string "she spake unto him, saying, After\l"
    .string "this manner did thy servant to me;\l"
    .string "that his wrath was kindled.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_20::
    .string "And Joseph’s master took him, and\n"
    .string "put him into the prison, a place\l"
    .string "where the king’s prisoners were\l"
    .string "bound: and he was there in the\l"
    .string "prison.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_21::
    .string "But the LORD was with Joseph, and\n"
    .string "shewed him mercy, and gave him favour\l"
    .string "in the sight of the keeper of the\l"
    .string "prison.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_22::
    .string "And the keeper of the prison\n"
    .string "committed to Joseph’s hand all the\l"
    .string "prisoners that were in the prison;\l"
    .string "and whatsoever they did there, he was\l"
    .string "the doer of it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_39_23::
    .string "The keeper of the prison looked\n"
    .string "not to any thing that was under his\l"
    .string "hand; because the LORD was with him,\l"
    .string "and that which he did, the LORD made\l"
    .string "it to prosper.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that the butler of the king\l"
    .string "of Egypt and his baker had offended\l"
    .string "their lord the king of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_2::
    .string "And Pharaoh was wroth against two of\n"
    .string "his officers, against the chief of\l"
    .string "the butlers, and against the chief\l"
    .string "of the bakers.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_3::
    .string "And he put them in ward in the house\n"
    .string "of the captain of the guard, into the\l"
    .string "prison, the place where Joseph was\l"
    .string "bound.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_4::
    .string "And the captain of the guard\n"
    .string "charged Joseph with them, and he\l"
    .string "served them: and they continued a\l"
    .string "season in ward.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_5::
    .string "And they dreamed a dream both of\n"
    .string "them, each man his dream in one\l"
    .string "night, each man according to the\l"
    .string "interpretation of his dream, the\l"
    .string "butler and the baker of the king of\l"
    .string "Egypt, which were bound in the\l"
    .string "prison.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_6::
    .string "And Joseph came in unto them in the\n"
    .string "morning, and looked upon them, and,\l"
    .string "behold, they were sad.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_7::
    .string "And he asked Pharaoh’s officers\n"
    .string "that were with him in the ward of his\l"
    .string "lord’s house, saying, Wherefore look\l"
    .string "ye so sadly to day?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_8::
    .string "And they said unto him, We have\n"
    .string "dreamed a dream, and there is no\l"
    .string "interpreter of it. And Joseph said\l"
    .string "unto them, Do not interpretations\l"
    .string "belong to God? tell me them, I pray\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_9::
    .string "And the chief butler told his\n"
    .string "dream to Joseph, and said to him, In\l"
    .string "my dream, behold, a vine was before\l"
    .string "me;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_10::
    .string "And in the vine were three branches:\n"
    .string "and it was as though it budded, and\l"
    .string "her blossoms shot forth; and the\l"
    .string "clusters thereof brought forth ripe\l"
    .string "grapes:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_11::
    .string "And Pharaoh’s cup was in my hand:\n"
    .string "and I took the grapes, and pressed\l"
    .string "them into Pharaoh’s cup, and I gave\l"
    .string "the cup into Pharaoh’s hand$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_12::
    .string "And Joseph said unto him, This is\n"
    .string "the interpretation of it: The three\l"
    .string "branches are three days:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_13::
    .string "Yet within three days shall\n"
    .string "Pharaoh lift up thine head, and\l"
    .string "restore thee unto thy place: and\l"
    .string "thou shalt deliver Pharaoh’s cup\l"
    .string "into his hand, after the former\l"
    .string "manner when thou wast his butler$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_14::
    .string "But think on me when it shall be\n"
    .string "well with thee, and shew kindness, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, unto me, and make mention\l"
    .string "of me unto Pharaoh, and bring me out\l"
    .string "of this house:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_15::
    .string "For indeed I was stolen away out of\n"
    .string "the land of the Hebrews: and here\l"
    .string "also have I done nothing that they\l"
    .string "should put me into the dungeon$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_16::
    .string "When the chief baker saw that the\n"
    .string "interpretation was good, he said\l"
    .string "unto Joseph, I also was in my dream,\l"
    .string "and, behold, I had three white\l"
    .string "baskets on my head:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_17::
    .string "And in the uppermost basket there\n"
    .string "was of all manner of bakemeats for\l"
    .string "Pharaoh; and the birds did eat them\l"
    .string "out of the basket upon my head$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_18::
    .string "And Joseph answered and said, This\n"
    .string "is the interpretation thereof: The\l"
    .string "three baskets are three days:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_19::
    .string "Yet within three days shall\n"
    .string "Pharaoh lift up thy head from off\l"
    .string "thee, and shall hang thee on a tree;\l"
    .string "and the birds shall eat thy flesh\l"
    .string "from off thee$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_20::
    .string "And it came to pass the third day,\n"
    .string "which was Pharaoh’s birthday, that he\l"
    .string "made a feast unto all his servants:\l"
    .string "and he lifted up the head of the\l"
    .string "chief butler and of the chief baker\l"
    .string "among his servants.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_21::
    .string "And he restored the chief butler\n"
    .string "unto his butlership again; and he\l"
    .string "gave the cup into Pharaoh’s hand:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_22::
    .string "But he hanged the chief baker: as\n"
    .string "Joseph had interpreted to them$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_40_23::
    .string "Yet did not the chief butler\n"
    .string "remember Joseph, but forgat him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_1::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "two full years, that Pharaoh\l"
    .string "dreamed: and, behold, he stood by the\l"
    .string "river.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_2::
    .string "And, behold, there came up out of\n"
    .string "the river seven well favoured kine\l"
    .string "and fatfleshed; and they fed in a\l"
    .string "meadow.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_3::
    .string "And, behold, seven other kine came\n"
    .string "up after them out of the river, ill\l"
    .string "favoured and leanfleshed; and stood\l"
    .string "by the other kine upon the brink of\l"
    .string "the river.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_4::
    .string "And the ill favoured and\n"
    .string "leanfleshed kine did eat up the\l"
    .string "seven well favoured and fat kine. So\l"
    .string "Pharaoh awoke.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_5::
    .string "And he slept and dreamed the\n"
    .string "second time: and, behold, seven ears\l"
    .string "of corn came up upon one stalk,\l"
    .string "rank and good.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_6::
    .string "And, behold, seven thin ears and\n"
    .string "blasted with the east wind sprung\l"
    .string "up after them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_7::
    .string "And the seven thin ears devoured the\n"
    .string "seven rank and full ears. And\l"
    .string "Pharaoh awoke, and, behold, it was a\l"
    .string "dream.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_8::
    .string "And it came to pass in the morning\n"
    .string "that his spirit was troubled; and he\l"
    .string "sent and called for all the\l"
    .string "magicians of Egypt, and all the\l"
    .string "wise men thereof: and Pharaoh told\l"
    .string "them his dream; but there was none\l"
    .string "that could interpret them unto\l"
    .string "Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_9::
    .string "Then spake the chief butler unto\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, saying, I do remember my\l"
    .string "faults this day:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_10::
    .string "Pharaoh was wroth with his servants,\n"
    .string "and put me in ward in the captain of\l"
    .string "the guard’s house, both me and the\l"
    .string "chief baker:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_11::
    .string "And we dreamed a dream in one night,\n"
    .string "I and he; we dreamed each man\l"
    .string "according to the interpretation of\l"
    .string "his dream$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_12::
    .string "And there was there with us a young\n"
    .string "man, an Hebrew, servant to the\l"
    .string "captain of the guard; and we told\l"
    .string "him, and he interpreted to us our\l"
    .string "dreams; to each man according to his\l"
    .string "dream he did interpret.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he\n"
    .string "interpreted to us, so it was; me he\l"
    .string "restored unto mine office, and him he\l"
    .string "hanged.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_14::
    .string "Then Pharaoh sent and called\n"
    .string "Joseph, and they brought him\l"
    .string "hastily out of the dungeon: and he\l"
    .string "shaved himself, and changed his\l"
    .string "raiment, and came in unto Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_15::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, I\n"
    .string "have dreamed a dream, and there is\l"
    .string "none that can interpret it: and I\l"
    .string "have heard say of thee, that thou\l"
    .string "canst understand a dream to\l"
    .string "interpret it.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_16::
    .string "And Joseph answered Pharaoh,\n"
    .string "saying, It is not in me: God shall\l"
    .string "give Pharaoh an answer of peace.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_17::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, In my\n"
    .string "dream, behold, I stood upon the bank\l"
    .string "of the river:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_18::
    .string "And, behold, there came up out of\n"
    .string "the river seven kine, fatfleshed and\l"
    .string "well favoured; and they fed in a\l"
    .string "meadow:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_19::
    .string "And, behold, seven other kine came\n"
    .string "up after them, poor and very ill\l"
    .string "favoured and leanfleshed, such as I\l"
    .string "never saw in all the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "for badness:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_20::
    .string "And the lean and the ill favoured\n"
    .string "kine did eat up the first seven fat\l"
    .string "kine:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_21::
    .string "And when they had eaten them up, it\n"
    .string "could not be known that they had\l"
    .string "eaten them; but they were still\l"
    .string "ill favoured, as at the beginning.\l"
    .string "So I awoke$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_22::
    .string "And I saw in my dream, and, behold,\n"
    .string "seven ears came up in one stalk,\l"
    .string "full and good:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_23::
    .string "And, behold, seven ears, withered,\n"
    .string "thin, and blasted with the east\l"
    .string "wind, sprung up after them:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_24::
    .string "And the thin ears devoured the seven\n"
    .string "good ears: and I told this unto the\l"
    .string "magicians; but there was none that\l"
    .string "could declare it to me$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_25::
    .string "And Joseph said unto Pharaoh, The\n"
    .string "dream of Pharaoh is one: God hath\l"
    .string "shewed Pharaoh what he is about to do.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_26::
    .string "The seven good kine are seven years;\n"
    .string "and the seven good ears are seven\l"
    .string "years: the dream is one.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_27::
    .string "And the seven thin and ill\n"
    .string "favoured kine that came up after\l"
    .string "them are seven years; and the seven\l"
    .string "empty ears blasted with the east\l"
    .string "wind shall be seven years of famine.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_28::
    .string "This is the thing which I have\n"
    .string "spoken unto Pharaoh: What God is\l"
    .string "about to do he sheweth unto Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_29::
    .string "Behold, there come seven years of\n"
    .string "great plenty throughout all the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_30::
    .string "And there shall arise after them\n"
    .string "seven years of famine; and all the\l"
    .string "plenty shall be forgotten in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt; and the famine shall\l"
    .string "consume the land;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_31::
    .string "And the plenty shall not be known\n"
    .string "in the land by reason of that famine\l"
    .string "following; for it shall be very\l"
    .string "grievous$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_32::
    .string "And for that the dream was doubled\n"
    .string "unto Pharaoh twice; it is because the\l"
    .string "thing is established by God, and God\l"
    .string "will shortly bring it to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_33::
    .string "Now therefore let Pharaoh look out\n"
    .string "a man discreet and wise, and set him\l"
    .string "over the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_34::
    .string "Let Pharaoh do this, and let him\n"
    .string "appoint officers over the land, and\l"
    .string "take up the fifth part of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt in the seven plenteous\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_35::
    .string "And let them gather all the food\n"
    .string "of those good years that come, and\l"
    .string "lay up corn under the hand of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and let them keep food in\l"
    .string "the cities.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_36::
    .string "And that food shall be for store to\n"
    .string "the land against the seven years of\l"
    .string "famine, which shall be in the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt; that the land perish not\l"
    .string "through the famine.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_37::
    .string "And the thing was good in the eyes\n"
    .string "of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of all\l"
    .string "his servants.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_38::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto his servants,\n"
    .string "Can we find such a one as this is, a\l"
    .string "man in whom the Spirit of God is?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_39::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph,\n"
    .string "Forasmuch as God hath shewed thee\l"
    .string "all this, there is none so discreet\l"
    .string "and wise as thou art:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_40::
    .string "Thou shalt be over my house, and\n"
    .string "according unto thy word shall all\l"
    .string "my people be ruled: only in the\l"
    .string "throne will I be greater than thou$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_41::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, See,\n"
    .string "I have set thee over all the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_42::
    .string "And Pharaoh took off his ring from\n"
    .string "his hand, and put it upon Joseph’s\l"
    .string "hand, and arrayed him in vestures of\l"
    .string "fine linen, and put a gold chain\l"
    .string "about his neck;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_43::
    .string "And he made him to ride in the\n"
    .string "second chariot which he had; and they\l"
    .string "cried before him, Bow the knee: and\l"
    .string "he made him ruler over all the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_44::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, I am\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and without thee shall no\l"
    .string "man lift up his hand or foot in all\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_45::
    .string "And Pharaoh called Joseph’s name\n"
    .string "Zaphnathpaaneah; and he gave him to\l"
    .string "wife Asenath the daughter of\l"
    .string "Potipherah priest of On. And Joseph\l"
    .string "went out over all the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_46::
    .string "And Joseph was thirty years old\n"
    .string "when he stood before Pharaoh king of\l"
    .string "Egypt. And Joseph went out from the\l"
    .string "presence of Pharaoh, and went\l"
    .string "throughout all the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_47::
    .string "And in the seven plenteous years\n"
    .string "the earth brought forth by handfuls.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_48::
    .string "And he gathered up all the food of\n"
    .string "the seven years, which were in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, and laid up the food\l"
    .string "in the cities: the food of the field,\l"
    .string "which was round about every city,\l"
    .string "laid he up in the same.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_49::
    .string "And Joseph gathered corn as the\n"
    .string "sand of the sea, very much, until he\l"
    .string "left numbering; for it was without\l"
    .string "number.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_50::
    .string "And unto Joseph were born two sons\n"
    .string "before the years of famine came,\l"
    .string "which Asenath the daughter of\l"
    .string "Potipherah priest of On bare unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_51::
    .string "And Joseph called the name of the\n"
    .string "firstborn Manasseh: For God, said he,\l"
    .string "hath made me forget all my toil,\l"
    .string "and all my father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_52::
    .string "And the name of the second called\n"
    .string "he Ephraim: For God hath caused me to\l"
    .string "be fruitful in the land of my\l"
    .string "affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_53::
    .string "And the seven years of\n"
    .string "plenteousness, that was in the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, were ended.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_54::
    .string "And the seven years of dearth began\n"
    .string "to come, according as Joseph had\l"
    .string "said: and the dearth was in all\l"
    .string "lands; but in all the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "there was bread.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_55::
    .string "And when all the land of Egypt\n"
    .string "was famished, the people cried to\l"
    .string "Pharaoh for bread: and Pharaoh said\l"
    .string "unto all the Egyptians, Go unto\l"
    .string "Joseph; what he saith to you, do.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_56::
    .string "And the famine was over all the\n"
    .string "face of the earth: and Joseph opened\l"
    .string "all the storehouses, and sold unto\l"
    .string "the Egyptians; and the famine waxed\l"
    .string "sore in the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_41_57::
    .string "And all countries came into Egypt\n"
    .string "to Joseph for to buy corn; because\l"
    .string "that the famine was so sore in all\l"
    .string "lands.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_1::
    .string "Now when Jacob saw that there was\n"
    .string "corn in Egypt, Jacob said unto his\l"
    .string "sons, Why do ye look one upon\l"
    .string "another?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_2::
    .string "And he said, Behold, I have heard\n"
    .string "that there is corn in Egypt: get you\l"
    .string "down thither, and buy for us from\l"
    .string "thence; that we may live, and not die$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_3::
    .string "And Joseph’s ten brethren went down\n"
    .string "to buy corn in Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_4::
    .string "But Benjamin, Joseph’s brother,\n"
    .string "Jacob sent not with his brethren; for\l"
    .string "he said, Lest peradventure mischief\l"
    .string "befall him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_5::
    .string "And the sons of Israel came to buy\n"
    .string "corn among those that came: for the\l"
    .string "famine was in the land of Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_6::
    .string "And Joseph was the governor over\n"
    .string "the land, and he it was that sold to\l"
    .string "all the people of the land: and\l"
    .string "Joseph’s brethren came, and bowed\l"
    .string "down themselves before him with\l"
    .string "their faces to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_7::
    .string "And Joseph saw his brethren, and he\n"
    .string "knew them, but made himself strange\l"
    .string "unto them, and spake roughly unto\l"
    .string "them; and he said unto them, Whence\l"
    .string "come ye? And they said, From the land\l"
    .string "of Canaan to buy food.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_8::
    .string "And Joseph knew his brethren, but\n"
    .string "they knew not him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_9::
    .string "And Joseph remembered the dreams\n"
    .string "which he dreamed of them, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Ye are spies; to see the\l"
    .string "nakedness of the land ye are come.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_10::
    .string "And they said unto him, Nay, my\n"
    .string "lord, but to buy food are thy\l"
    .string "servants come.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_11::
    .string "We are all one man’s sons; we are\n"
    .string "true men, thy servants are no spies.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_12::
    .string "And he said unto them, Nay, but to\n"
    .string "see the nakedness of the land ye are\l"
    .string "come.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_13::
    .string "And they said, Thy servants are\n"
    .string "twelve brethren, the sons of one man\l"
    .string "in the land of Canaan; and, behold,\l"
    .string "the youngest is this day with our\l"
    .string "father, and one is not.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_14::
    .string "And Joseph said unto them, That is\n"
    .string "it that I spake unto you, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "are spies:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_15::
    .string "Hereby ye shall be proved: By the\n"
    .string "life of Pharaoh ye shall not go\l"
    .string "forth hence, except your youngest\l"
    .string "brother come hither$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_16::
    .string "Send one of you, and let him fetch\n"
    .string "your brother, and ye shall be kept\l"
    .string "in prison, that your words may be\l"
    .string "proved, whether there be any truth in\l"
    .string "you: or else by the life of Pharaoh\l"
    .string "surely ye are spies.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_17::
    .string "And he put them all together into\n"
    .string "ward three days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_18::
    .string "And Joseph said unto them the third\n"
    .string "day, This do, and live; for I fear\l"
    .string "God:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_19::
    .string "If ye be true men, let one of your\n"
    .string "brethren be bound in the house of\l"
    .string "your prison: go ye, carry corn for\l"
    .string "the famine of your houses:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_20::
    .string "But bring your youngest brother\n"
    .string "unto me; so shall your words be\l"
    .string "verified, and ye shall not die. And\l"
    .string "they did so$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_21::
    .string "And they said one to another, We are\n"
    .string "verily guilty concerning our\l"
    .string "brother, in that we saw the anguish\l"
    .string "of his soul, when he besought us, and\l"
    .string "we would not hear; therefore is this\l"
    .string "distress come upon us.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_22::
    .string "And Reuben answered them, saying,\n"
    .string "Spake I not unto you, saying, Do not\l"
    .string "sin against the child; and ye would\l"
    .string "not hear? therefore, behold, also\l"
    .string "his blood is required.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_23::
    .string "And they knew not that Joseph\n"
    .string "understood them; for he spake unto\l"
    .string "them by an interpreter.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_24::
    .string "And he turned himself about from\n"
    .string "them, and wept; and returned to them\l"
    .string "again, and communed with them, and\l"
    .string "took from them Simeon, and bound him\l"
    .string "before their eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_25::
    .string "Then Joseph commanded to fill\n"
    .string "their sacks with corn, and to restore\l"
    .string "every man’s money into his sack, and\l"
    .string "to give them provision for the way:\l"
    .string "and thus did he unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_26::
    .string "And they laded their asses with the\n"
    .string "corn, and departed thence.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_27::
    .string "And as one of them opened his sack\n"
    .string "to give his ass provender in the inn,\l"
    .string "he espied his money; for, behold, it\l"
    .string "was in his sack’s mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_28::
    .string "And he said unto his brethren, My\n"
    .string "money is restored; and, lo, it is\l"
    .string "even in my sack: and their heart\l"
    .string "failed them, and they were afraid,\l"
    .string "saying one to another, What is this\l"
    .string "that God hath done unto us?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_29::
    .string "And they came unto Jacob their\n"
    .string "father unto the land of Canaan, and\l"
    .string "told him all that befell unto\l"
    .string "them; saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_30::
    .string "The man, who is the lord of the\n"
    .string "land, spake roughly to us, and took\l"
    .string "us for spies of the country$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_31::
    .string "And we said unto him, We are true\n"
    .string "men; we are no spies:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_32::
    .string "We be twelve brethren, sons of our\n"
    .string "father; one is not, and the youngest\l"
    .string "is this day with our father in the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_33::
    .string "And the man, the lord of the\n"
    .string "country, said unto us, Hereby shall\l"
    .string "I know that ye are true men; leave\l"
    .string "one of your brethren here with me,\l"
    .string "and take food for the famine of your\l"
    .string "households, and be gone:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_34::
    .string "And bring your youngest brother\n"
    .string "unto me: then shall I know that ye\l"
    .string "are no spies, but that ye are true\l"
    .string "men: so will I deliver you your\l"
    .string "brother, and ye shall traffick in\l"
    .string "the land$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_35::
    .string "And it came to pass as they emptied\n"
    .string "their sacks, that, behold, every\l"
    .string "man’s bundle of money was in his\l"
    .string "sack: and when both they and their\l"
    .string "father saw the bundles of money,\l"
    .string "they were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_36::
    .string "And Jacob their father said unto\n"
    .string "them, Me have ye bereaved of my\l"
    .string "children: Joseph is not, and Simeon\l"
    .string "is not, and ye will take Benjamin\l"
    .string "away: all these things are against\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_37::
    .string "And Reuben spake unto his father,\n"
    .string "saying, Slay my two sons, if I bring\l"
    .string "him not to thee: deliver him into my\l"
    .string "hand, and I will bring him to thee\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_42_38::
    .string "And he said, My son shall not go\n"
    .string "down with you; for his brother is\l"
    .string "dead, and he is left alone: if\l"
    .string "mischief befall him by the way in\l"
    .string "the which ye go, then shall ye bring\l"
    .string "down my gray hairs with sorrow to the\l"
    .string "grave.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_1::
    .string "And the famine was sore in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they had\n"
    .string "eaten up the corn which they had\l"
    .string "brought out of Egypt, their father\l"
    .string "said unto them, Go again, buy us a\l"
    .string "little food.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_3::
    .string "And Judah spake unto him, saying,\n"
    .string "The man did solemnly protest unto\l"
    .string "us, saying, Ye shall not see my\l"
    .string "face, except your brother be with\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_4::
    .string "If thou wilt send our brother with\n"
    .string "us, we will go down and buy thee\l"
    .string "food:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_5::
    .string "But if thou wilt not send him, we\n"
    .string "will not go down: for the man said\l"
    .string "unto us, Ye shall not see my face,\l"
    .string "except your brother be with you$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_6::
    .string "And Israel said, Wherefore dealt\n"
    .string "ye so ill with me, as to tell the\l"
    .string "man whether ye had yet a brother?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_7::
    .string "And they said, The man asked us\n"
    .string "straitly of our state, and of our\l"
    .string "kindred, saying, Is your father yet\l"
    .string "alive? have ye another brother? and\l"
    .string "we told him according to the tenor\l"
    .string "of these words: could we certainly\l"
    .string "know that he would say, Bring your\l"
    .string "brother down?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_8::
    .string "And Judah said unto Israel his\n"
    .string "father, Send the lad with me, and we\l"
    .string "will arise and go; that we may\l"
    .string "live, and not die, both we, and thou,\l"
    .string "and also our little ones$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_9::
    .string "I will be surety for him; of my\n"
    .string "hand shalt thou require him: if I\l"
    .string "bring him not unto thee, and set him\l"
    .string "before thee, then let me bear the\l"
    .string "blame for ever:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_10::
    .string "For except we had lingered, surely\n"
    .string "now we had returned this second time$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_11::
    .string "And their father Israel said unto\n"
    .string "them, If it must be so now, do this;\l"
    .string "take of the best fruits in the land\l"
    .string "in your vessels, and carry down the\l"
    .string "man a present, a little balm, and a\l"
    .string "little honey, spices, and myrrh,\l"
    .string "nuts, and almonds:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_12::
    .string "And take double money in your hand;\n"
    .string "and the money that was brought again\l"
    .string "in the mouth of your sacks, carry it\l"
    .string "again in your hand; peradventure it\l"
    .string "was an oversight:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_13::
    .string "Take also your brother, and arise,\n"
    .string "go again unto the man:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_14::
    .string "And God Almighty give you mercy\n"
    .string "before the man, that he may send away\l"
    .string "your other brother, and Benjamin. If\l"
    .string "I be bereaved of my children, I am\l"
    .string "bereaved$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_15::
    .string "And the men took that present, and\n"
    .string "they took double money in their hand\l"
    .string "and Benjamin; and rose up, and went\l"
    .string "down to Egypt, and stood before\l"
    .string "Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_16::
    .string "And when Joseph saw Benjamin with\n"
    .string "them, he said to the ruler of his\l"
    .string "house, Bring these men home, and\l"
    .string "slay, and make ready; for these men\l"
    .string "shall dine with me at noon.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_17::
    .string "And the man did as Joseph bade; and\n"
    .string "the man brought the men into\l"
    .string "Joseph’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_18::
    .string "And the men were afraid, because\n"
    .string "they were brought into Joseph’s\l"
    .string "house; and they said, Because of the\l"
    .string "money that was returned in our sacks\l"
    .string "at the first time are we brought in;\l"
    .string "that he may seek occasion against us,\l"
    .string "and fall upon us, and take us for\l"
    .string "bondmen, and our asses.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_19::
    .string "And they came near to the steward of\n"
    .string "Joseph’s house, and they communed\l"
    .string "with him at the door of the house,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_20::
    .string "And said, O sir, we came indeed down\n"
    .string "at the first time to buy food:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_21::
    .string "And it came to pass, when we came to\n"
    .string "the inn, that we opened our sacks,\l"
    .string "and, behold, every man’s money was\l"
    .string "in the mouth of his sack, our money in\l"
    .string "full weight: and we have brought it\l"
    .string "again in our hand$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_22::
    .string "And other money have we brought down\n"
    .string "in our hands to buy food: we cannot\l"
    .string "tell who put our money in our sacks.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_23::
    .string "And he said, Peace be to you, fear\n"
    .string "not: your God, and the God of your\l"
    .string "father, hath given you treasure in\l"
    .string "your sacks: I had your money. And he\l"
    .string "brought Simeon out unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_24::
    .string "And the man brought the men into\n"
    .string "Joseph’s house, and gave them water,\l"
    .string "and they washed their feet; and he\l"
    .string "gave their asses provender.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_25::
    .string "And they made ready the present\n"
    .string "against Joseph came at noon: for\l"
    .string "they heard that they should eat\l"
    .string "bread there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_26::
    .string "And when Joseph came home, they\n"
    .string "brought him the present which was in\l"
    .string "their hand into the house, and bowed\l"
    .string "themselves to him to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_27::
    .string "And he asked them of their welfare,\n"
    .string "and said, Is your father well, the\l"
    .string "old man of whom ye spake? Is he yet\l"
    .string "alive?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_28::
    .string "And they answered, Thy servant our\n"
    .string "father is in good health, he is yet\l"
    .string "alive. And they bowed down their\l"
    .string "heads, and made obeisance$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_29::
    .string "And he lifted up his eyes, and saw\n"
    .string "his brother Benjamin, his mother’s\l"
    .string "son, and said, Is this your younger\l"
    .string "brother, of whom ye spake unto me?\l"
    .string "And he said, God be gracious unto\l"
    .string "thee, my son.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_30::
    .string "And Joseph made haste; for his\n"
    .string "bowels did yearn upon his brother:\l"
    .string "and he sought where to weep; and he\l"
    .string "entered into his chamber, and wept\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_31::
    .string "And he washed his face, and went\n"
    .string "out, and refrained himself, and\l"
    .string "said, Set on bread.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_32::
    .string "And they set on for him by himself,\n"
    .string "and for them by themselves, and for\l"
    .string "the Egyptians, which did eat with\l"
    .string "him, by themselves: because the\l"
    .string "Egyptians might not eat bread with\l"
    .string "the Hebrews; for that is an\l"
    .string "abomination unto the Egyptians.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_33::
    .string "And they sat before him, the\n"
    .string "firstborn according to his\l"
    .string "birthright, and the youngest\l"
    .string "according to his youth: and the men\l"
    .string "marvelled one at another.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_43_34::
    .string "And he took and sent messes unto\n"
    .string "them from before him: but Benjamin’s\l"
    .string "mess was five times so much as any of\l"
    .string "theirs. And they drank, and were\l"
    .string "merry with him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_1::
    .string "And he commanded the steward of his\n"
    .string "house, saying, Fill the men’s sacks\l"
    .string "with food, as much as they can carry,\l"
    .string "and put every man’s money in his\l"
    .string "sack’s mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_2::
    .string "And put my cup, the silver cup, in\n"
    .string "the sack’s mouth of the youngest, and\l"
    .string "his corn money. And he did according\l"
    .string "to the word that Joseph had spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_3::
    .string "As soon as the morning was light,\n"
    .string "the men were sent away, they and\l"
    .string "their asses.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_4::
    .string "And when they were gone out of the\n"
    .string "city, and not yet far off, Joseph\l"
    .string "said unto his steward, Up, follow\l"
    .string "after the men; and when thou dost\l"
    .string "overtake them, say unto them,\l"
    .string "Wherefore have ye rewarded evil for\l"
    .string "good?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_5::
    .string "Is not this it in which my lord\n"
    .string "drinketh, and whereby indeed he\l"
    .string "divineth? ye have done evil in so\l"
    .string "doing$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_6::
    .string "And he overtook them, and he spake\n"
    .string "unto them these same words.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_7::
    .string "And they said unto him, Wherefore\n"
    .string "saith my lord these words? God\l"
    .string "forbid that thy servants should do\l"
    .string "according to this thing:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_8::
    .string "Behold, the money, which we found\n"
    .string "in our sacks’ mouths, we brought\l"
    .string "again unto thee out of the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan: how then should we steal out\l"
    .string "of thy lord’s house silver or gold?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_9::
    .string "With whomsoever of thy servants it\n"
    .string "be found, both let him die, and we\l"
    .string "also will be my lord’s bondmen$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_10::
    .string "And he said, Now also let it be\n"
    .string "according unto your words: he with\l"
    .string "whom it is found shall be my\l"
    .string "servant; and ye shall be blameless.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_11::
    .string "Then they speedily took down every\n"
    .string "man his sack to the ground, and\l"
    .string "opened every man his sack.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_12::
    .string "And he searched, and began at the\n"
    .string "eldest, and left at the youngest:\l"
    .string "and the cup was found in Benjamin’s\l"
    .string "sack.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_13::
    .string "Then they rent their clothes, and\n"
    .string "laded every man his ass, and returned\l"
    .string "to the city.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_14::
    .string "And Judah and his brethren came to\n"
    .string "Joseph’s house; for he was yet\l"
    .string "there: and they fell before him on\l"
    .string "the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_15::
    .string "And Joseph said unto them, What\n"
    .string "deed is this that ye have done? wot ye\l"
    .string "not that such a man as I can\l"
    .string "certainly divine?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_16::
    .string "And Judah said, What shall we say\n"
    .string "unto my lord? what shall we speak?\l"
    .string "or how shall we clear ourselves?\l"
    .string "God hath found out the iniquity of\l"
    .string "thy servants: behold, we are my\l"
    .string "lord’s servants, both we, and he\l"
    .string "also with whom the cup is found$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_17::
    .string "And he said, God forbid that I\n"
    .string "should do so: but the man in whose\l"
    .string "hand the cup is found, he shall be\l"
    .string "my servant; and as for you, get you\l"
    .string "up in peace unto your father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_18::
    .string "Then Judah came near unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, Oh my lord, let thy servant, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, speak a word in my lord’s\l"
    .string "ears, and let not thine anger burn\l"
    .string "against thy servant: for thou art\l"
    .string "even as Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_19::
    .string "My lord asked his servants, saying,\n"
    .string "Have ye a father, or a brother?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_20::
    .string "And we said unto my lord, We have a\n"
    .string "father, an old man, and a child of\l"
    .string "his old age, a little one; and his\l"
    .string "brother is dead, and he alone is\l"
    .string "left of his mother, and his father\l"
    .string "loveth him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_21::
    .string "And thou saidst unto thy servants,\n"
    .string "Bring him down unto me, that I may set\l"
    .string "mine eyes upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_22::
    .string "And we said unto my lord, The lad\n"
    .string "cannot leave his father: for if he\l"
    .string "should leave his father, his father\l"
    .string "would die.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_23::
    .string "And thou saidst unto thy servants,\n"
    .string "Except your youngest brother come\l"
    .string "down with you, ye shall see my face\l"
    .string "no more.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_24::
    .string "And it came to pass when we came up\n"
    .string "unto thy servant my father, we told\l"
    .string "him the words of my lord.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_25::
    .string "And our father said, Go again, and\n"
    .string "buy us a little food.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_26::
    .string "And we said, We cannot go down: if\n"
    .string "our youngest brother be with us, then\l"
    .string "will we go down: for we may not see\l"
    .string "the man’s face, except our youngest\l"
    .string "brother be with us.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_27::
    .string "And thy servant my father said unto\n"
    .string "us, Ye know that my wife bare me two\l"
    .string "sons:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_28::
    .string "And the one went out from me, and I\n"
    .string "said, Surely he is torn in pieces;\l"
    .string "and I saw him not since:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_29::
    .string "And if ye take this also from me,\n"
    .string "and mischief befall him, ye shall\l"
    .string "bring down my gray hairs with sorrow\l"
    .string "to the grave$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_30::
    .string "Now therefore when I come to thy\n"
    .string "servant my father, and the lad be not\l"
    .string "with us; seeing that his life is\l"
    .string "bound up in the lad’s life;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_31::
    .string "It shall come to pass, when he\n"
    .string "seeth that the lad is not with us,\l"
    .string "that he will die: and thy servants\l"
    .string "shall bring down the gray hairs of\l"
    .string "thy servant our father with sorrow to\l"
    .string "the grave$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_32::
    .string "For thy servant became surety for\n"
    .string "the lad unto my father, saying, If I\l"
    .string "bring him not unto thee, then I\l"
    .string "shall bear the blame to my father\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_33::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, let thy\n"
    .string "servant abide instead of the lad a\l"
    .string "bondman to my lord; and let the lad\l"
    .string "go up with his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_44_34::
    .string "For how shall I go up to my father,\n"
    .string "and the lad be not with me? lest\l"
    .string "peradventure I see the evil that\l"
    .string "shall come on my father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_1::
    .string "Then Joseph could not refrain\n"
    .string "himself before all them that stood\l"
    .string "by him; and he cried, Cause every man\l"
    .string "to go out from me. And there stood no\l"
    .string "man with him, while Joseph made\l"
    .string "himself known unto his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_2::
    .string "And he wept aloud: and the\n"
    .string "Egyptians and the house of Pharaoh\l"
    .string "heard.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_3::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "I am Joseph; doth my father yet\l"
    .string "live? And his brethren could not\l"
    .string "answer him; for they were troubled\l"
    .string "at his presence.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_4::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "Come near to me, I pray you. And they\l"
    .string "came near. And he said, I am Joseph\l"
    .string "your brother, whom ye sold into\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_5::
    .string "Now therefore be not grieved, nor\n"
    .string "angry with yourselves, that ye sold\l"
    .string "me hither: for God did send me before\l"
    .string "you to preserve life.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_6::
    .string "For these two years hath the famine\n"
    .string "been in the land: and yet there are\l"
    .string "five years, in the which there shall\l"
    .string "neither be earing nor harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_7::
    .string "And God sent me before you to\n"
    .string "preserve you a posterity in the\l"
    .string "earth, and to save your lives by a\l"
    .string "great deliverance.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_8::
    .string "So now it was not you that sent me\n"
    .string "hither, but God: and he hath made me a\l"
    .string "father to Pharaoh, and lord of all\l"
    .string "his house, and a ruler throughout\l"
    .string "all the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_9::
    .string "Haste ye, and go up to my father,\n"
    .string "and say unto him, Thus saith thy son\l"
    .string "Joseph, God hath made me lord of\l"
    .string "all Egypt: come down unto me, tarry\l"
    .string "not:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_10::
    .string "And thou shalt dwell in the land\n"
    .string "of Goshen, and thou shalt be near\l"
    .string "unto me, thou, and thy children, and\l"
    .string "thy children’s children, and thy\l"
    .string "flocks, and thy herds, and all that\l"
    .string "thou hast:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_11::
    .string "And there will I nourish thee; for\n"
    .string "yet there are five years of famine;\l"
    .string "lest thou, and thy household, and\l"
    .string "all that thou hast, come to poverty$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_12::
    .string "And, behold, your eyes see, and the\n"
    .string "eyes of my brother Benjamin, that it\l"
    .string "is my mouth that speaketh unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_13::
    .string "And ye shall tell my father of\n"
    .string "all my glory in Egypt, and of all\l"
    .string "that ye have seen; and ye shall\l"
    .string "haste and bring down my father hither.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_14::
    .string "And he fell upon his brother\n"
    .string "Benjamin’s neck, and wept; and\l"
    .string "Benjamin wept upon his neck.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_15::
    .string "Moreover he kissed all his\n"
    .string "brethren, and wept upon them: and\l"
    .string "after that his brethren talked with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_16::
    .string "And the fame thereof was heard in\n"
    .string "Pharaoh’s house, saying, Joseph’s\l"
    .string "brethren are come: and it pleased\l"
    .string "Pharaoh well, and his servants.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_17::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, Say\n"
    .string "unto thy brethren, This do ye; lade\l"
    .string "your beasts, and go, get you unto the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_18::
    .string "And take your father and your\n"
    .string "households, and come unto me: and I\l"
    .string "will give you the good of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, and ye shall eat the fat\l"
    .string "of the land$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_19::
    .string "Now thou art commanded, this do ye;\n"
    .string "take you wagons out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt for your little ones, and for\l"
    .string "your wives, and bring your father,\l"
    .string "and come.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_20::
    .string "Also regard not your stuff; for the\n"
    .string "good of all the land of Egypt is\l"
    .string "yours.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_21::
    .string "And the children of Israel did so:\n"
    .string "and Joseph gave them wagons,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and gave them provision for\l"
    .string "the way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_22::
    .string "To all of them he gave each man\n"
    .string "changes of raiment; but to Benjamin\l"
    .string "he gave three hundred pieces of\l"
    .string "silver, and five changes of raiment.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_23::
    .string "And to his father he sent after this\n"
    .string "manner; ten asses laden with the\l"
    .string "good things of Egypt, and ten she\l"
    .string "asses laden with corn and bread and\l"
    .string "meat for his father by the way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_24::
    .string "So he sent his brethren away, and\n"
    .string "they departed: and he said unto\l"
    .string "them, See that ye fall not out by\l"
    .string "the way.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_25::
    .string "And they went up out of Egypt, and\n"
    .string "came into the land of Canaan unto\l"
    .string "Jacob their father,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_26::
    .string "And told him, saying, Joseph is yet\n"
    .string "alive, and he is governor over all\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt. And Jacob’s heart\l"
    .string "fainted, for he believed them not$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_27::
    .string "And they told him all the words of\n"
    .string "Joseph, which he had said unto them:\l"
    .string "and when he saw the wagons which\l"
    .string "Joseph had sent to carry him, the\l"
    .string "spirit of Jacob their father\l"
    .string "revived:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_45_28::
    .string "And Israel said, It is enough;\n"
    .string "Joseph my son is yet alive: I will\l"
    .string "go and see him before I die$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_1::
    .string "And Israel took his journey with\n"
    .string "all that he had, and came to\l"
    .string "Beersheba, and offered sacrifices\l"
    .string "unto the God of his father Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_2::
    .string "And God spake unto Israel in the\n"
    .string "visions of the night, and said,\l"
    .string "Jacob, Jacob. And he said, Here am I.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_3::
    .string "And he said, I am God, the God of thy\n"
    .string "father: fear not to go down into\l"
    .string "Egypt; for I will there make of\l"
    .string "thee a great nation:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_4::
    .string "I will go down with thee into\n"
    .string "Egypt; and I will also surely\l"
    .string "bring thee up again: and Joseph\l"
    .string "shall put his hand upon thine eyes$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_5::
    .string "And Jacob rose up from Beersheba:\n"
    .string "and the sons of Israel carried Jacob\l"
    .string "their father, and their little\l"
    .string "ones, and their wives, in the wagons\l"
    .string "which Pharaoh had sent to carry him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_6::
    .string "And they took their cattle, and\n"
    .string "their goods, which they had gotten in\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan, and came into\l"
    .string "Egypt, Jacob, and all his seed with\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_7::
    .string "His sons, and his sons’ sons with\n"
    .string "him, his daughters, and his sons’\l"
    .string "daughters, and all his seed brought\l"
    .string "he with him into Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_8::
    .string "And these are the names of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, which came into\l"
    .string "Egypt, Jacob and his sons: Reuben,\l"
    .string "Jacob’s firstborn.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_9::
    .string "And the sons of Reuben; Hanoch, and\n"
    .string "Phallu, and Hezron, and Carmi.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_10::
    .string "And the sons of Simeon; Jemuel, and\n"
    .string "Jamin, and Ohad, and Jachin, and\l"
    .string "Zohar, and Shaul the son of a\l"
    .string "Canaanitish woman.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_11::
    .string "And the sons of Levi; Gershon,\n"
    .string "Kohath, and Merari.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_12::
    .string "And the sons of Judah; Er, and Onan,\n"
    .string "and Shelah, and Pharez, and Zarah:\l"
    .string "but Er and Onan died in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan. And the sons of Pharez were\l"
    .string "Hezron and Hamul.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_13::
    .string "And the sons of Issachar; Tola, and\n"
    .string "Phuvah, and Job, and Shimron.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_14::
    .string "And the sons of Zebulun; Sered, and\n"
    .string "Elon, and Jahleel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_15::
    .string "These be the sons of Leah, which she\n"
    .string "bare unto Jacob in Padanaram, with\l"
    .string "his daughter Dinah: all the souls\l"
    .string "of his sons and his daughters were\l"
    .string "thirty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_16::
    .string "And the sons of Gad; Ziphion, and\n"
    .string "Haggi, Shuni, and Ezbon, Eri, and\l"
    .string "Arodi, and Areli.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_17::
    .string "And the sons of Asher; Jimnah, and\n"
    .string "Ishuah, and Isui, and Beriah, and\l"
    .string "Serah their sister: and the sons of\l"
    .string "Beriah; Heber, and Malchiel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_18::
    .string "These are the sons of Zilpah, whom\n"
    .string "Laban gave to Leah his daughter, and\l"
    .string "these she bare unto Jacob, even\l"
    .string "sixteen souls.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_19::
    .string "The sons of Rachel Jacob’s wife;\n"
    .string "Joseph, and Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_20::
    .string "And unto Joseph in the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt were born Manasseh and\l"
    .string "Ephraim, which Asenath the daughter\l"
    .string "of Potipherah priest of On bare\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_21::
    .string "And the sons of Benjamin were\n"
    .string "Belah, and Becher, and Ashbel, Gera,\l"
    .string "and Naaman, Ehi, and Rosh, Muppim,\l"
    .string "and Huppim, and Ard.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_22::
    .string "These are the sons of Rachel, which\n"
    .string "were born to Jacob: all the souls\l"
    .string "were fourteen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_23::
    .string "And the sons of Dan; Hushim.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_24::
    .string "And the sons of Naphtali; Jahzeel,\n"
    .string "and Guni, and Jezer, and Shillem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_25::
    .string "These are the sons of Bilhah, which\n"
    .string "Laban gave unto Rachel his daughter,\l"
    .string "and she bare these unto Jacob: all\l"
    .string "the souls were seven.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_26::
    .string "All the souls that came with Jacob\n"
    .string "into Egypt, which came out of his\l"
    .string "loins, besides Jacob’s sons’ wives,\l"
    .string "all the souls were threescore and\l"
    .string "six;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_27::
    .string "And the sons of Joseph, which were\n"
    .string "born him in Egypt, were two souls:\l"
    .string "all the souls of the house of\l"
    .string "Jacob, which came into Egypt, were\l"
    .string "threescore and ten$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_28::
    .string "And he sent Judah before him unto\n"
    .string "Joseph, to direct his face unto\l"
    .string "Goshen; and they came into the land\l"
    .string "of Goshen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_29::
    .string "And Joseph made ready his chariot,\n"
    .string "and went up to meet Israel his\l"
    .string "father, to Goshen, and presented\l"
    .string "himself unto him; and he fell on\l"
    .string "his neck, and wept on his neck a good\l"
    .string "while.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_30::
    .string "And Israel said unto Joseph, Now\n"
    .string "let me die, since I have seen thy\l"
    .string "face, because thou art yet alive.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_31::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "and unto his father’s house, I will\l"
    .string "go up, and shew Pharaoh, and say unto\l"
    .string "him, My brethren, and my father’s\l"
    .string "house, which were in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, are come unto me;"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_32::
    .string "And the men are shepherds, for\n"
    .string "their trade hath been to feed\l"
    .string "cattle; and they have brought their\l"
    .string "flocks, and their herds, and all\l"
    .string "that they have$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_33::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "Pharaoh shall call you, and shall\l"
    .string "say, What is your occupation?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_46_34::
    .string "That ye shall say, Thy servants’\n"
    .string "trade hath been about cattle from\l"
    .string "our youth even until now, both we,\l"
    .string "and also our fathers: that ye may\l"
    .string "dwell in the land of Goshen; for\l"
    .string "every shepherd is an abomination\l"
    .string "unto the Egyptians$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_1::
    .string "Then Joseph came and told Pharaoh,\n"
    .string "and said, My father and my brethren,\l"
    .string "and their flocks, and their herds,\l"
    .string "and all that they have, are come out\l"
    .string "of the land of Canaan; and, behold,\l"
    .string "they are in the land of Goshen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_2::
    .string "And he took some of his brethren,\n"
    .string "even five men, and presented them\l"
    .string "unto Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_3::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "What is your occupation? And they\l"
    .string "said unto Pharaoh, Thy servants are\l"
    .string "shepherds, both we, and also our\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_4::
    .string "They said morever unto Pharaoh, For\n"
    .string "to sojourn in the land are we come;\l"
    .string "for thy servants have no pasture for\l"
    .string "their flocks; for the famine is sore\l"
    .string "in the land of Canaan: now\l"
    .string "therefore, we pray thee, let thy\l"
    .string "servants dwell in the land of\l"
    .string "Goshen.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_5::
    .string "And Pharaoh spake unto Joseph,\n"
    .string "saying, Thy father and thy brethren\l"
    .string "are come unto thee:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_6::
    .string "The land of Egypt is before thee;\n"
    .string "in the best of the land make thy\l"
    .string "father and brethren to dwell; in the\l"
    .string "land of Goshen let them dwell: and\l"
    .string "if thou knowest any men of activity\l"
    .string "among them, then make them rulers\l"
    .string "over my cattle$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_7::
    .string "And Joseph brought in Jacob his\n"
    .string "father, and set him before Pharaoh:\l"
    .string "and Jacob blessed Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_8::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto Jacob, How\n"
    .string "old art thou?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_9::
    .string "And Jacob said unto Pharaoh, The\n"
    .string "days of the years of my pilgrimage\l"
    .string "are an hundred and thirty years: few\l"
    .string "and evil have the days of the years\l"
    .string "of my life been, and have not\l"
    .string "attained unto the days of the years\l"
    .string "of the life of my fathers in the days\l"
    .string "of their pilgrimage$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_10::
    .string "And Jacob blessed Pharaoh, and went\n"
    .string "out from before Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_11::
    .string "And Joseph placed his father and\n"
    .string "his brethren, and gave them a\l"
    .string "possession in the land of Egypt, in\l"
    .string "the best of the land, in the land of\l"
    .string "Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_12::
    .string "And Joseph nourished his father,\n"
    .string "and his brethren, and all his\l"
    .string "father’s household, with bread,\l"
    .string "according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_13::
    .string "And there was no bread in all the\n"
    .string "land; for the famine was very sore,\l"
    .string "so that the land of Egypt and all\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan fainted by reason\l"
    .string "of the famine.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_14::
    .string "And Joseph gathered up all the\n"
    .string "money that was found in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and in the land of Canaan,\l"
    .string "for the corn which they bought: and\l"
    .string "Joseph brought the money into\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_15::
    .string "And when money failed in the land\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan,\l"
    .string "all the Egyptians came unto\l"
    .string "Joseph, and said, Give us bread: for\l"
    .string "why should we die in thy presence?\l"
    .string "for the money faileth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_16::
    .string "And Joseph said, Give your cattle;\n"
    .string "and I will give you for your\l"
    .string "cattle, if money fail.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_17::
    .string "And they brought their cattle unto\n"
    .string "Joseph: and Joseph gave them bread\l"
    .string "in exchange for horses, and for the\l"
    .string "flocks, and for the cattle of the\l"
    .string "herds, and for the asses: and he fed\l"
    .string "them with bread for all their\l"
    .string "cattle for that year.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_18::
    .string "When that year was ended, they came\n"
    .string "unto him the second year, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, We will not hide it from\l"
    .string "my lord, how that our money is\l"
    .string "spent; my lord also hath our herds\l"
    .string "of cattle; there is not ought left\l"
    .string "in the sight of my lord, but our\l"
    .string "bodies, and our lands:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_19::
    .string "Wherefore shall we die before\n"
    .string "thine eyes, both we and our land? buy\l"
    .string "us and our land for bread, and we and\l"
    .string "our land will be servants unto\l"
    .string "Pharaoh: and give us seed, that we\l"
    .string "may live, and not die, that the land\l"
    .string "be not desolate$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_20::
    .string "And Joseph bought all the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt for Pharaoh; for the\l"
    .string "Egyptians sold every man his field,\l"
    .string "because the famine prevailed over\l"
    .string "them: so the land became Pharaoh’s.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_21::
    .string "And as for the people, he removed\n"
    .string "them to cities from one end of the\l"
    .string "borders of Egypt even to the other\l"
    .string "end thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_22::
    .string "Only the land of the priests\n"
    .string "bought he not; for the priests had a\l"
    .string "portion assigned them of Pharaoh, and\l"
    .string "did eat their portion which Pharaoh\l"
    .string "gave them: wherefore they sold not\l"
    .string "their lands.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_23::
    .string "Then Joseph said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Behold, I have bought you this day\l"
    .string "and your land for Pharaoh: lo, here\l"
    .string "is seed for you, and ye shall sow\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_24::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "increase, that ye shall give the\l"
    .string "fifth part unto Pharaoh, and four\l"
    .string "parts shall be your own, for seed of\l"
    .string "the field, and for your food, and for\l"
    .string "them of your households, and for\l"
    .string "food for your little ones.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_25::
    .string "And they said, Thou hast saved our\n"
    .string "lives: let us find grace in the sight\l"
    .string "of my lord, and we will be\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s servants.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_26::
    .string "And Joseph made it a law over the\n"
    .string "land of Egypt unto this day, that\l"
    .string "Pharaoh should have the fifth part,\l"
    .string "except the land of the priests\l"
    .string "only, which became not Pharaoh’s.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_27::
    .string "And Israel dwelt in the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt, in the country of Goshen; and\l"
    .string "they had possessions therein, and\l"
    .string "grew, and multiplied exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_28::
    .string "And Jacob lived in the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt seventeen years: so the whole\l"
    .string "age of Jacob was an hundred forty and\l"
    .string "seven years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_29::
    .string "And the time drew nigh that Israel\n"
    .string "must die: and he called his son\l"
    .string "Joseph, and said unto him, If now I\l"
    .string "have found grace in thy sight, put, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, thy hand under my thigh,\l"
    .string "and deal kindly and truly with me;\l"
    .string "bury me not, I pray thee, in Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_30::
    .string "But I will lie with my fathers,\n"
    .string "and thou shalt carry me out of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and bury me in their\l"
    .string "buryingplace. And he said, I will\l"
    .string "do as thou hast said$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_47_31::
    .string "And he said, Swear unto me. And he\n"
    .string "sware unto him. And Israel bowed\l"
    .string "himself upon the bed’s head.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that one told Joseph,\l"
    .string "Behold, thy father is sick: and he\l"
    .string "took with him his two sons, Manasseh\l"
    .string "and Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_2::
    .string "And one told Jacob, and said,\n"
    .string "Behold, thy son Joseph cometh unto\l"
    .string "thee: and Israel strengthened\l"
    .string "himself, and sat upon the bed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_3::
    .string "And Jacob said unto Joseph, God\n"
    .string "Almighty appeared unto me at Luz in\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan, and blessed me,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_4::
    .string "And said unto me, Behold, I will\n"
    .string "make thee fruitful, and multiply\l"
    .string "thee, and I will make of thee a\l"
    .string "multitude of people; and will\l"
    .string "give this land to thy seed after\l"
    .string "thee for an everlasting possession$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_5::
    .string "And now thy two sons, Ephraim and\n"
    .string "Manasseh, which were born unto thee\l"
    .string "in the land of Egypt before I came\l"
    .string "unto thee into Egypt, are mine; as\l"
    .string "Reuben and Simeon, they shall be\l"
    .string "mine.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_6::
    .string "And thy issue, which thou begettest\n"
    .string "after them, shall be thine, and\l"
    .string "shall be called after the name of\l"
    .string "their brethren in their inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_7::
    .string "And as for me, when I came from\n"
    .string "Padan, Rachel died by me in the land\l"
    .string "of Canaan in the way, when yet there\l"
    .string "was but a little way to come unto\l"
    .string "Ephrath: and I buried her there in\l"
    .string "the way of Ephrath; the same is\l"
    .string "Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_8::
    .string "And Israel beheld Joseph’s sons,\n"
    .string "and said, Who are these?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_9::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his father,\n"
    .string "They are my sons, whom God hath given\l"
    .string "me in this place. And he said, Bring\l"
    .string "them, I pray thee, unto me, and I\l"
    .string "will bless them$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_10::
    .string "Now the eyes of Israel were dim for\n"
    .string "age, so that he could not see. And he\l"
    .string "brought them near unto him; and he\l"
    .string "kissed them, and embraced them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_11::
    .string "And Israel said unto Joseph, I had\n"
    .string "not thought to see thy face: and, lo,\l"
    .string "God hath shewed me also thy seed.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_12::
    .string "And Joseph brought them out from\n"
    .string "between his knees, and he bowed\l"
    .string "himself with his face to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_13::
    .string "And Joseph took them both, Ephraim\n"
    .string "in his right hand toward Israel’s\l"
    .string "left hand, and Manasseh in his left\l"
    .string "hand toward Israel’s right hand, and\l"
    .string "brought them near unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_14::
    .string "And Israel stretched out his right\n"
    .string "hand, and laid it upon Ephraim’s\l"
    .string "head, who was the younger, and his\l"
    .string "left hand upon Manasseh’s head,\l"
    .string "guiding his hands wittingly; for\l"
    .string "Manasseh was the firstborn.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_15::
    .string "And he blessed Joseph, and said,\n"
    .string "God, before whom my fathers Abraham\l"
    .string "and Isaac did walk, the God which fed\l"
    .string "me all my life long unto this day,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_16::
    .string "The Angel which redeemed me from\n"
    .string "all evil, bless the lads; and let\l"
    .string "my name be named on them, and the name\l"
    .string "of my fathers Abraham and Isaac; and\l"
    .string "let them grow into a multitude in\l"
    .string "the midst of the earth$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_17::
    .string "And when Joseph saw that his father\n"
    .string "laid his right hand upon the head of\l"
    .string "Ephraim, it displeased him: and he\l"
    .string "held up his father’s hand, to remove\l"
    .string "it from Ephraim’s head unto\l"
    .string "Manasseh’s head.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_18::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his father,\n"
    .string "Not so, my father: for this is the\l"
    .string "firstborn; put thy right hand upon\l"
    .string "his head.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_19::
    .string "And his father refused, and said, I\n"
    .string "know it, my son, I know it: he also\l"
    .string "shall become a people, and he\l"
    .string "also shall be great: but truly his\l"
    .string "younger brother shall be greater\l"
    .string "than he, and his seed shall become a\l"
    .string "multitude of nations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_20::
    .string "And he blessed them that day,\n"
    .string "saying, In thee shall Israel\l"
    .string "bless, saying, God make thee as\l"
    .string "Ephraim and as Manasseh: and he set\l"
    .string "Ephraim before Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_21::
    .string "And Israel said unto Joseph,\n"
    .string "Behold, I die: but God shall be\l"
    .string "with you, and bring you again unto\l"
    .string "the land of your fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_48_22::
    .string "Moreover I have given to thee one\n"
    .string "portion above thy brethren, which I\l"
    .string "took out of the hand of the Amorite\l"
    .string "with my sword and with my bow.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_1::
    .string "And Jacob called unto his sons, and\n"
    .string "said, Gather yourselves together,\l"
    .string "that I may tell you that which\l"
    .string "shall befall you in the last days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_2::
    .string "Gather yourselves together, and\n"
    .string "hear, ye sons of Jacob; and hearken\l"
    .string "unto Israel your father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_3::
    .string "Reuben, thou art my firstborn, my\n"
    .string "might, and the beginning of my\l"
    .string "strength, the excellency of\l"
    .string "dignity, and the excellency of\l"
    .string "power:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_4::
    .string "Unstable as water, thou shalt not\n"
    .string "excel; because thou wentest up to\l"
    .string "thy father’s bed; then defiledst\l"
    .string "thou it: he went up to my couch$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_5::
    .string "Simeon and Levi are brethren;\n"
    .string "instruments of cruelty are in their\l"
    .string "habitations.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_6::
    .string "O my soul, come not thou into their\n"
    .string "secret; unto their assembly, mine\l"
    .string "honour, be not thou united: for in\l"
    .string "their anger they slew a man, and in\l"
    .string "their selfwill they digged down a\l"
    .string "wall.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_7::
    .string "Cursed be their anger, for it was\n"
    .string "fierce; and their wrath, for it was\l"
    .string "cruel: I will divide them in Jacob,\l"
    .string "and scatter them in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_8::
    .string "Judah, thou art he whom thy brethren\n"
    .string "shall praise: thy hand shall be in\l"
    .string "the neck of thine enemies; thy\l"
    .string "father’s children shall bow down\l"
    .string "before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_9::
    .string "Judah is a lion’s whelp: from the\n"
    .string "prey, my son, thou art gone up: he\l"
    .string "stooped down, he couched as a lion,\l"
    .string "and as an old lion; who shall rouse\l"
    .string "him up?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_10::
    .string "The sceptre shall not depart from\n"
    .string "Judah, nor a lawgiver from between\l"
    .string "his feet, until Shiloh come; and\l"
    .string "unto him shall the gathering of the\l"
    .string "people be$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_11::
    .string "Binding his foal unto the vine, and\n"
    .string "his ass’s colt unto the choice vine;\l"
    .string "he washed his garments in wine, and\l"
    .string "his clothes in the blood of grapes:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_12::
    .string "His eyes shall be red with wine,\n"
    .string "and his teeth white with milk$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_13::
    .string "Zebulun shall dwell at the haven\n"
    .string "of the sea; and he shall be for an\l"
    .string "haven of ships; and his border\l"
    .string "shall be unto Zidon.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_14::
    .string "Issachar is a strong ass couching\n"
    .string "down between two burdens:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_15::
    .string "And he saw that rest was good, and\n"
    .string "the land that it was pleasant; and\l"
    .string "bowed his shoulder to bear, and\l"
    .string "became a servant unto tribute$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_16::
    .string "Dan shall judge his people, as\n"
    .string "one of the tribes of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_17::
    .string "Dan shall be a serpent by the way,\n"
    .string "an adder in the path, that biteth the\l"
    .string "horse heels, so that his rider\l"
    .string "shall fall backward.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_18::
    .string "I have waited for thy salvation, O\n"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_19::
    .string "Gad, a troop shall overcome him:\n"
    .string "but he shall overcome at the last.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_20::
    .string "Out of Asher his bread shall be\n"
    .string "fat, and he shall yield royal\l"
    .string "dainties.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_21::
    .string "Naphtali is a hind let loose: he\n"
    .string "giveth goodly words.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_22::
    .string "Joseph is a fruitful bough, even a\n"
    .string "fruitful bough by a well; whose\l"
    .string "branches run over the wall:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_23::
    .string "The archers have sorely grieved\n"
    .string "him, and shot at him, and hated him:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_24::
    .string "But his bow abode in strength, and\n"
    .string "the arms of his hands were made\l"
    .string "strong by the hands of the mighty God\l"
    .string "of Jacob; (from thence is the\l"
    .string "shepherd, the stone of Israel:)"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_25::
    .string "Even by the God of thy father, who\n"
    .string "shall help thee; and by the\l"
    .string "Almighty, who shall bless thee\l"
    .string "with blessings of heaven above,\l"
    .string "blessings of the deep that lieth\l"
    .string "under, blessings of the breasts, and\l"
    .string "of the womb:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_26::
    .string "The blessings of thy father have\n"
    .string "prevailed above the blessings of my\l"
    .string "progenitors unto the utmost bound of\l"
    .string "the everlasting hills: they shall\l"
    .string "be on the head of Joseph, and on the\l"
    .string "crown of the head of him that was\l"
    .string "separate from his brethren$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_27::
    .string "Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in\n"
    .string "the morning he shall devour the\l"
    .string "prey, and at night he shall divide\l"
    .string "the spoil.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_28::
    .string "All these are the twelve tribes of\n"
    .string "Israel: and this is it that their\l"
    .string "father spake unto them, and blessed\l"
    .string "them; every one according to his\l"
    .string "blessing he blessed them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_29::
    .string "And he charged them, and said unto\n"
    .string "them, I am to be gathered unto my\l"
    .string "people: bury me with my fathers in\l"
    .string "the cave that is in the field of\l"
    .string "Ephron the Hittite,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_30::
    .string "In the cave that is in the field of\n"
    .string "Machpelah, which is before Mamre,\l"
    .string "in the land of Canaan, which Abraham\l"
    .string "bought with the field of Ephron the\l"
    .string "Hittite for a possession of a\l"
    .string "buryingplace$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_31::
    .string "There they buried Abraham and Sarah\n"
    .string "his wife; there they buried Isaac and\l"
    .string "Rebekah his wife; and there I buried\l"
    .string "Leah.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_32::
    .string "The purchase of the field and of\n"
    .string "the cave that is therein was from the\l"
    .string "children of Heth.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_49_33::
    .string "And when Jacob had made an end of\n"
    .string "commanding his sons, he gathered up\l"
    .string "his feet into the bed, and yielded\l"
    .string "up the ghost, and was gathered unto\l"
    .string "his people.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_1::
    .string "And Joseph fell upon his father’s\n"
    .string "face, and wept upon him, and kissed\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_2::
    .string "And Joseph commanded his servants\n"
    .string "the physicians to embalm his\l"
    .string "father: and the physicians embalmed\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_3::
    .string "And forty days were fulfilled for\n"
    .string "him; for so are fulfilled the days\l"
    .string "of those which are embalmed: and the\l"
    .string "Egyptians mourned for him\l"
    .string "threescore and ten days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_4::
    .string "And when the days of his mourning\n"
    .string "were past, Joseph spake unto the\l"
    .string "house of Pharaoh, saying, If now I\l"
    .string "have found grace in your eyes,\l"
    .string "speak, I pray you, in the ears of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_5::
    .string "My father made me swear, saying, Lo,\n"
    .string "I die: in my grave which I have digged\l"
    .string "for me in the land of Canaan, there\l"
    .string "shalt thou bury me. Now therefore\l"
    .string "let me go up, I pray thee, and bury\l"
    .string "my father, and I will come again$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_6::
    .string "And Pharaoh said, Go up, and bury\n"
    .string "thy father, according as he made thee\l"
    .string "swear.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_7::
    .string "And Joseph went up to bury his\n"
    .string "father: and with him went up all\l"
    .string "the servants of Pharaoh, the elders\l"
    .string "of his house, and all the elders of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_8::
    .string "And all the house of Joseph, and\n"
    .string "his brethren, and his father’s house:\l"
    .string "only their little ones, and their\l"
    .string "flocks, and their herds, they left\l"
    .string "in the land of Goshen$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_9::
    .string "And there went up with him both\n"
    .string "chariots and horsemen: and it was a\l"
    .string "very great company.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_10::
    .string "And they came to the threshingfloor\n"
    .string "of Atad, which is beyond Jordan, and\l"
    .string "there they mourned with a great and\l"
    .string "very sore lamentation: and he made a\l"
    .string "mourning for his father seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_11::
    .string "And when the inhabitants of the\n"
    .string "land, the Canaanites, saw the\l"
    .string "mourning in the floor of Atad, they\l"
    .string "said, This is a grievous mourning to\l"
    .string "the Egyptians: wherefore the name of\l"
    .string "it was called Abelmizraim, which is\l"
    .string "beyond Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_12::
    .string "And his sons did unto him according\n"
    .string "as he commanded them:"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_13::
    .string "For his sons carried him into the\n"
    .string "land of Canaan, and buried him in the\l"
    .string "cave of the field of Machpelah,\l"
    .string "which Abraham bought with the field\l"
    .string "for a possession of a buryingplace\l"
    .string "of Ephron the Hittite, before Mamre$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_14::
    .string "And Joseph returned into Egypt,\n"
    .string "he, and his brethren, and all that\l"
    .string "went up with him to bury his father,\l"
    .string "after he had buried his father.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_15::
    .string "And when Joseph’s brethren saw that\n"
    .string "their father was dead, they said,\l"
    .string "Joseph will peradventure hate us,\l"
    .string "and will certainly requite us all\l"
    .string "the evil which we did unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_16::
    .string "And they sent a messenger unto\n"
    .string "Joseph, saying, Thy father did\l"
    .string "command before he died, saying,"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_17::
    .string "So shall ye say unto Joseph,\n"
    .string "Forgive, I pray thee now, the\l"
    .string "trespass of thy brethren, and their\l"
    .string "sin; for they did unto thee evil: and\l"
    .string "now, we pray thee, forgive the\l"
    .string "trespass of the servants of the God\l"
    .string "of thy father. And Joseph wept when\l"
    .string "they spake unto him$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_18::
    .string "And his brethren also went and\n"
    .string "fell down before his face; and they\l"
    .string "said, Behold, we be thy servants.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_19::
    .string "And Joseph said unto them, Fear\n"
    .string "not: for am I in the place of God?"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_20::
    .string "But as for you, ye thought evil\n"
    .string "against me; but God meant it unto\l"
    .string "good, to bring to pass, as it is this\l"
    .string "day, to save much people alive$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_21::
    .string "Now therefore fear ye not: I will\n"
    .string "nourish you, and your little ones.\l"
    .string "And he comforted them, and spake\l"
    .string "kindly unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_22::
    .string "And Joseph dwelt in Egypt, he, and\n"
    .string "his father’s house: and Joseph\l"
    .string "lived an hundred and ten years.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_23::
    .string "And Joseph saw Ephraim’s children\n"
    .string "of the third generation: the\l"
    .string "children also of Machir the son of\l"
    .string "Manasseh were brought up upon\l"
    .string "Joseph’s knees.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_24::
    .string "And Joseph said unto his brethren,\n"
    .string "I die: and God will surely visit\l"
    .string "you, and bring you out of this land\l"
    .string "unto the land which he sware to\l"
    .string "Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_25::
    .string "And Joseph took an oath of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, saying, God\l"
    .string "will surely visit you, and ye\l"
    .string "shall carry up my bones from hence.$"
Bible_Text_Genesis_50_26::
    .string "So Joseph died, being an hundred\n"
    .string "and ten years old: and they embalmed\l"
    .string "him, and he was put in a coffin in\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_1::
    .string "Now these are the names of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, which came into\l"
    .string "Egypt; every man and his household\l"
    .string "came with Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_2::
    .string "Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_3::
    .string "Issachar, Zebulun, and Benjamin,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_4::
    .string "Dan, and Naphtali, Gad, and Asher$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_5::
    .string "And all the souls that came out of\n"
    .string "the loins of Jacob were seventy\l"
    .string "souls: for Joseph was in Egypt\l"
    .string "already.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_6::
    .string "And Joseph died, and all his\n"
    .string "brethren, and all that generation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_7::
    .string "And the children of Israel were\n"
    .string "fruitful, and increased abundantly,\l"
    .string "and multiplied, and waxed\l"
    .string "exceeding mighty; and the land was\l"
    .string "filled with them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_8::
    .string "Now there arose up a new king over\n"
    .string "Egypt, which knew not Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_9::
    .string "And he said unto his people,\n"
    .string "Behold, the people of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel are more and\l"
    .string "mightier than we:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_10::
    .string "Come on, let us deal wisely with\n"
    .string "them; lest they multiply, and it\l"
    .string "come to pass, that, when there\l"
    .string "falleth out any war, they join also\l"
    .string "unto our enemies, and fight against\l"
    .string "us, and so get them up out of the\l"
    .string "land$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_11::
    .string "Therefore they did set over them\n"
    .string "taskmasters to afflict them with\l"
    .string "their burdens. And they built for\l"
    .string "Pharaoh treasure cities, Pithom and\l"
    .string "Raamses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_12::
    .string "But the more they afflicted them,\n"
    .string "the more they multiplied and grew.\l"
    .string "And they were grieved because of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_13::
    .string "And the Egyptians made the\n"
    .string "children of Israel to serve with\l"
    .string "rigour:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_14::
    .string "And they made their lives bitter\n"
    .string "with hard bondage, in morter, and in\l"
    .string "brick, and in all manner of service\l"
    .string "in the field: all their service,\l"
    .string "wherein they made them serve, was\l"
    .string "with rigour$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_15::
    .string "And the king of Egypt spake to the\n"
    .string "Hebrew midwives, of which the name of\l"
    .string "the one was Shiphrah, and the name of\l"
    .string "the other Puah:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_16::
    .string "And he said, When ye do the office of\n"
    .string "a midwife to the Hebrew women, and\l"
    .string "see them upon the stools; if it be a\l"
    .string "son, then ye shall kill him: but if\l"
    .string "it be a daughter, then she shall\l"
    .string "live$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_17::
    .string "But the midwives feared God, and did\n"
    .string "not as the king of Egypt commanded\l"
    .string "them, but saved the men children\l"
    .string "alive.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_18::
    .string "And the king of Egypt called for\n"
    .string "the midwives, and said unto them, Why\l"
    .string "have ye done this thing, and have\l"
    .string "saved the men children alive?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_19::
    .string "And the midwives said unto Pharaoh,\n"
    .string "Because the Hebrew women are not as\l"
    .string "the Egyptian women; for they are\l"
    .string "lively, and are delivered ere the\l"
    .string "midwives come in unto them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_20::
    .string "Therefore God dealt well with the\n"
    .string "midwives: and the people\l"
    .string "multiplied, and waxed very mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_21::
    .string "And it came to pass, because the\n"
    .string "midwives feared God, that he made\l"
    .string "them houses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_1_22::
    .string "And Pharaoh charged all his\n"
    .string "people, saying, Every son that is\l"
    .string "born ye shall cast into the river,\l"
    .string "and every daughter ye shall save\l"
    .string "alive.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_1::
    .string "And there went a man of the house of\n"
    .string "Levi, and took to wife a daughter of\l"
    .string "Levi.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_2::
    .string "And the woman conceived, and bare a\n"
    .string "son: and when she saw him that he was\l"
    .string "a goodly child, she hid him three\l"
    .string "months.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_3::
    .string "And when she could not longer hide\n"
    .string "him, she took for him an ark of\l"
    .string "bulrushes, and daubed it with slime\l"
    .string "and with pitch, and put the child\l"
    .string "therein; and she laid it in the\l"
    .string "flags by the river’s brink.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_4::
    .string "And his sister stood afar off, to\n"
    .string "wit what would be done to him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_5::
    .string "And the daughter of Pharaoh came\n"
    .string "down to wash herself at the river;\l"
    .string "and her maidens walked along by the\l"
    .string "river’s side; and when she saw the\l"
    .string "ark among the flags, she sent her\l"
    .string "maid to fetch it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_6::
    .string "And when she had opened it, she saw\n"
    .string "the child: and, behold, the babe\l"
    .string "wept. And she had compassion on him,\l"
    .string "and said, This is one of the Hebrews’\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_7::
    .string "Then said his sister to Pharaoh’s\n"
    .string "daughter, Shall I go and call to\l"
    .string "thee a nurse of the Hebrew women,\l"
    .string "that she may nurse the child for\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_8::
    .string "And Pharaoh’s daughter said to her,\n"
    .string "Go. And the maid went and called the\l"
    .string "child’s mother$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_9::
    .string "And Pharaoh’s daughter said unto\n"
    .string "her, Take this child away, and nurse\l"
    .string "it for me, and I will give thee thy\l"
    .string "wages. And the woman took the child,\l"
    .string "and nursed it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_10::
    .string "And the child grew, and she brought\n"
    .string "him unto Pharaoh’s daughter, and he\l"
    .string "became her son. And she called his\l"
    .string "name Moses: and she said, Because I\l"
    .string "drew him out of the water.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_11::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "when Moses was grown, that he went\l"
    .string "out unto his brethren, and looked on\l"
    .string "their burdens: and he spied an\l"
    .string "Egyptian smiting an Hebrew, one of\l"
    .string "his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_12::
    .string "And he looked this way and that way,\n"
    .string "and when he saw that there was no man,\l"
    .string "he slew the Egyptian, and hid him in\l"
    .string "the sand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_13::
    .string "And when he went out the second day,\n"
    .string "behold, two men of the Hebrews\l"
    .string "strove together: and he said to him\l"
    .string "that did the wrong, Wherefore smitest\l"
    .string "thou thy fellow?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_14::
    .string "And he said, Who made thee a prince\n"
    .string "and a judge over us? intendest thou\l"
    .string "to kill me, as thou killedst the\l"
    .string "Egyptian? And Moses feared, and\l"
    .string "said, Surely this thing is known$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_15::
    .string "Now when Pharaoh heard this thing,\n"
    .string "he sought to slay Moses. But Moses\l"
    .string "fled from the face of Pharaoh, and\l"
    .string "dwelt in the land of Midian: and he\l"
    .string "sat down by a well.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_16::
    .string "Now the priest of Midian had seven\n"
    .string "daughters: and they came and drew\l"
    .string "water, and filled the troughs to\l"
    .string "water their father’s flock.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_17::
    .string "And the shepherds came and drove\n"
    .string "them away: but Moses stood up and\l"
    .string "helped them, and watered their\l"
    .string "flock.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_18::
    .string "And when they came to Reuel their\n"
    .string "father, he said, How is it that ye are\l"
    .string "come so soon to day?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_19::
    .string "And they said, An Egyptian\n"
    .string "delivered us out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "shepherds, and also drew water\l"
    .string "enough for us, and watered the flock$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_20::
    .string "And he said unto his daughters, And\n"
    .string "where is he? why is it that ye have\l"
    .string "left the man? call him, that he may\l"
    .string "eat bread.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_21::
    .string "And Moses was content to dwell\n"
    .string "with the man: and he gave Moses\l"
    .string "Zipporah his daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_22::
    .string "And she bare him a son, and he\n"
    .string "called his name Gershom: for he\l"
    .string "said, I have been a stranger in a\l"
    .string "strange land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_23::
    .string "And it came to pass in process of\n"
    .string "time, that the king of Egypt died:\l"
    .string "and the children of Israel sighed\l"
    .string "by reason of the bondage, and they\l"
    .string "cried, and their cry came up unto God\l"
    .string "by reason of the bondage.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_24::
    .string "And God heard their groaning, and\n"
    .string "God remembered his covenant with\l"
    .string "Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_2_25::
    .string "And God looked upon the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, and God had respect unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_1::
    .string "Now Moses kept the flock of Jethro\n"
    .string "his father in law, the priest of\l"
    .string "Midian: and he led the flock to the\l"
    .string "backside of the desert, and came to\l"
    .string "the mountain of God, even to Horeb.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_2::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD appeared\n"
    .string "unto him in a flame of fire out of\l"
    .string "the midst of a bush: and he looked,\l"
    .string "and, behold, the bush burned with\l"
    .string "fire, and the bush was not consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_3::
    .string "And Moses said, I will now turn\n"
    .string "aside, and see this great sight, why\l"
    .string "the bush is not burnt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_4::
    .string "And when the LORD saw that he turned\n"
    .string "aside to see, God called unto him\l"
    .string "out of the midst of the bush, and\l"
    .string "said, Moses, Moses. And he said, Here\l"
    .string "am I.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_5::
    .string "And he said, Draw not nigh hither:\n"
    .string "put off thy shoes from off thy feet,\l"
    .string "for the place whereon thou standest\l"
    .string "is holy ground.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_6::
    .string "Moreover he said, I am the God of thy\n"
    .string "father, the God of Abraham, the God\l"
    .string "of Isaac, and the God of Jacob. And\l"
    .string "Moses hid his face; for he was afraid\l"
    .string "to look upon God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_7::
    .string "And the LORD said, I have surely\n"
    .string "seen the affliction of my people\l"
    .string "which are in Egypt, and have heard\l"
    .string "their cry by reason of their\l"
    .string "taskmasters; for I know their\l"
    .string "sorrows;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_8::
    .string "And I am come down to deliver them\n"
    .string "out of the hand of the Egyptians, and\l"
    .string "to bring them up out of that land\l"
    .string "unto a good land and a large, unto a\l"
    .string "land flowing with milk and honey;\l"
    .string "unto the place of the Canaanites,\l"
    .string "and the Hittites, and the Amorites,\l"
    .string "and the Perizzites, and the Hivites,\l"
    .string "and the Jebusites$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_9::
    .string "Now therefore, behold, the cry of\n"
    .string "the children of Israel is come unto\l"
    .string "me: and I have also seen the\l"
    .string "oppression wherewith the Egyptians\l"
    .string "oppress them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_10::
    .string "Come now therefore, and I will send\n"
    .string "thee unto Pharaoh, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "bring forth my people the children\l"
    .string "of Israel out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_11::
    .string "And Moses said unto God, Who am I,\n"
    .string "that I should go unto Pharaoh, and\l"
    .string "that I should bring forth the\l"
    .string "children of Israel out of Egypt?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_12::
    .string "And he said, Certainly I will be\n"
    .string "with thee; and this shall be a token\l"
    .string "unto thee, that I have sent thee:\l"
    .string "When thou hast brought forth the\l"
    .string "people out of Egypt, ye shall\l"
    .string "serve God upon this mountain$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_13::
    .string "And Moses said unto God, Behold,\n"
    .string "when I come unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and shall say unto them,\l"
    .string "The God of your fathers hath sent me\l"
    .string "unto you; and they shall say to me,\l"
    .string "What is his name? what shall I say\l"
    .string "unto them?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_14::
    .string "And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I\n"
    .string "AM: and he said, Thus shalt thou say\l"
    .string "unto the children of Israel, I AM\l"
    .string "hath sent me unto you$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_15::
    .string "And God said moreover unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Thus shalt thou say unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, the LORD God of\l"
    .string "your fathers, the God of Abraham, the\l"
    .string "God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob,\l"
    .string "hath sent me unto you: this is my name\l"
    .string "for ever, and this is my memorial\l"
    .string "unto all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_16::
    .string "Go, and gather the elders of Israel\n"
    .string "together, and say unto them, The LORD\l"
    .string "God of your fathers, the God of\l"
    .string "Abraham, of Isaac, and of Jacob,\l"
    .string "appeared unto me, saying, I have\l"
    .string "surely visited you, and seen that\l"
    .string "which is done to you in Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_17::
    .string "And I have said, I will bring you\n"
    .string "up out of the affliction of Egypt\l"
    .string "unto the land of the Canaanites, and\l"
    .string "the Hittites, and the Amorites, and\l"
    .string "the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and\l"
    .string "the Jebusites, unto a land flowing\l"
    .string "with milk and honey$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_18::
    .string "And they shall hearken to thy\n"
    .string "voice: and thou shalt come, thou and\l"
    .string "the elders of Israel, unto the king\l"
    .string "of Egypt, and ye shall say unto\l"
    .string "him, The LORD God of the Hebrews hath\l"
    .string "met with us: and now let us go, we\l"
    .string "beseech thee, three days’ journey\l"
    .string "into the wilderness, that we may\l"
    .string "sacrifice to the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_19::
    .string "And I am sure that the king of Egypt\n"
    .string "will not let you go, no, not by a\l"
    .string "mighty hand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_20::
    .string "And I will stretch out my hand, and\n"
    .string "smite Egypt with all my wonders\l"
    .string "which I will do in the midst\l"
    .string "thereof: and after that he will let\l"
    .string "you go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_21::
    .string "And I will give this people\n"
    .string "favour in the sight of the\l"
    .string "Egyptians: and it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, that, when ye go, ye shall not\l"
    .string "go empty.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_3_22::
    .string "But every woman shall borrow of\n"
    .string "her neighbour, and of her that\l"
    .string "sojourneth in her house, jewels of\l"
    .string "silver, and jewels of gold, and\l"
    .string "raiment: and ye shall put them\l"
    .string "upon your sons, and upon your\l"
    .string "daughters; and ye shall spoil the\l"
    .string "Egyptians.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_1::
    .string "And Moses answered and said, But,\n"
    .string "behold, they will not believe me,\l"
    .string "nor hearken unto my voice: for they\l"
    .string "will say, The LORD hath not\l"
    .string "appeared unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, What is\n"
    .string "that in thine hand? And he said, A rod.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_3::
    .string "And he said, Cast it on the ground.\n"
    .string "And he cast it on the ground, and it\l"
    .string "became a serpent; and Moses fled\l"
    .string "from before it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_4::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Put\n"
    .string "forth thine hand, and take it by the\l"
    .string "tail. And he put forth his hand, and\l"
    .string "caught it, and it became a rod in his\l"
    .string "hand:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_5::
    .string "That they may believe that the LORD\n"
    .string "God of their fathers, the God of\l"
    .string "Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the\l"
    .string "God of Jacob, hath appeared unto\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_6::
    .string "And the LORD said furthermore unto\n"
    .string "him, Put now thine hand into thy bosom\l"
    .string " And he put his hand into his bosom:\l"
    .string "and when he took it out, behold, his\l"
    .string "hand was leprous as snow.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_7::
    .string "And he said, Put thine hand into thy\n"
    .string "bosom again. And he put his hand into\l"
    .string "his bosom again; and plucked it out\l"
    .string "of his bosom, and, behold, it was\l"
    .string "turned again as his other flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_8::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if they\n"
    .string "will not believe thee, neither\l"
    .string "hearken to the voice of the first\l"
    .string "sign, that they will believe the\l"
    .string "voice of the latter sign.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if they\n"
    .string "will not believe also these two\l"
    .string "signs, neither hearken unto thy\l"
    .string "voice, that thou shalt take of the\l"
    .string "water of the river, and pour it upon\l"
    .string "the dry land: and the water which\l"
    .string "thou takest out of the river shall\l"
    .string "become blood upon the dry land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_10::
    .string "And Moses said unto the LORD, O my\n"
    .string "LORD, I am not eloquent, neither\l"
    .string "heretofore, nor since thou hast\l"
    .string "spoken unto thy servant: but I am\l"
    .string "slow of speech, and of a slow\l"
    .string "tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_11::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Who hath\n"
    .string "made man’s mouth? or who maketh the\l"
    .string "dumb, or deaf, or the seeing, or the\l"
    .string "blind? have not I the LORD?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_12::
    .string "Now therefore go, and I will be\n"
    .string "with thy mouth, and teach thee what\l"
    .string "thou shalt say$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_13::
    .string "And he said, O my LORD, send, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, by the hand of him whom thou\l"
    .string "wilt send.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_14::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Moses, and he said,\l"
    .string "Is not Aaron the Levite thy brother?\l"
    .string "I know that he can speak well. And\l"
    .string "also, behold, he cometh forth to\l"
    .string "meet thee: and when he seeth thee, he\l"
    .string "will be glad in his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_15::
    .string "And thou shalt speak unto him, and\n"
    .string "put words in his mouth: and I will\l"
    .string "be with thy mouth, and with his\l"
    .string "mouth, and will teach you what ye\l"
    .string "shall do.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_16::
    .string "And he shall be thy spokesman unto\n"
    .string "the people: and he shall be, even\l"
    .string "he shall be to thee instead of a\l"
    .string "mouth, and thou shalt be to him\l"
    .string "instead of God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_17::
    .string "And thou shalt take this rod in\n"
    .string "thine hand, wherewith thou shalt do\l"
    .string "signs.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_18::
    .string "And Moses went and returned to\n"
    .string "Jethro his father in law, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Let me go, I pray thee, and\l"
    .string "return unto my brethren which are in\l"
    .string "Egypt, and see whether they be yet\l"
    .string "alive. And Jethro said to Moses, Go\l"
    .string "in peace.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_19::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses in\n"
    .string "Midian, Go, return into Egypt: for\l"
    .string "all the men are dead which sought\l"
    .string "thy life.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_20::
    .string "And Moses took his wife and his\n"
    .string "sons, and set them upon an ass, and\l"
    .string "he returned to the land of Egypt:\l"
    .string "and Moses took the rod of God in his\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_21::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, When\n"
    .string "thou goest to return into Egypt, see\l"
    .string "that thou do all those wonders\l"
    .string "before Pharaoh, which I have put in\l"
    .string "thine hand: but I will harden his\l"
    .string "heart, that he shall not let the\l"
    .string "people go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_22::
    .string "And thou shalt say unto Pharaoh,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Israel is my\l"
    .string "son, even my firstborn:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_23::
    .string "And I say unto thee, Let my son go,\n"
    .string "that he may serve me: and if thou\l"
    .string "refuse to let him go, behold, I\l"
    .string "will slay thy son, even thy\l"
    .string "firstborn$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_24::
    .string "And it came to pass by the way in\n"
    .string "the inn, that the LORD met him, and\l"
    .string "sought to kill him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_25::
    .string "Then Zipporah took a sharp stone,\n"
    .string "and cut off the foreskin of her son,\l"
    .string "and cast it at his feet, and said,\l"
    .string "Surely a bloody husband art thou to\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_26::
    .string "So he let him go: then she said, A\n"
    .string "bloody husband thou art, because of\l"
    .string "the circumcision.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_27::
    .string "And the LORD said to Aaron, Go into\n"
    .string "the wilderness to meet Moses. And he\l"
    .string "went, and met him in the mount of God,\l"
    .string "and kissed him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_28::
    .string "And Moses told Aaron all the words\n"
    .string "of the LORD who had sent him, and\l"
    .string "all the signs which he had\l"
    .string "commanded him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_29::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron went and\n"
    .string "gathered together all the elders\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_30::
    .string "And Aaron spake all the words\n"
    .string "which the LORD had spoken unto\l"
    .string "Moses, and did the signs in the sight\l"
    .string "of the people$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_4_31::
    .string "And the people believed: and when\n"
    .string "they heard that the LORD had visited\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, and that he\l"
    .string "had looked upon their affliction,\l"
    .string "then they bowed their heads and\l"
    .string "worshipped.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_1::
    .string "And afterward Moses and Aaron went\n"
    .string "in, and told Pharaoh, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, Let my people\l"
    .string "go, that they may hold a feast unto\l"
    .string "me in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_2::
    .string "And Pharaoh said, Who is the LORD,\n"
    .string "that I should obey his voice to let\l"
    .string "Israel go? I know not the LORD,\l"
    .string "neither will I let Israel go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_3::
    .string "And they said, The God of the\n"
    .string "Hebrews hath met with us: let us go,\l"
    .string "we pray thee, three days’ journey\l"
    .string "into the desert, and sacrifice unto\l"
    .string "the LORD our God; lest he fall upon\l"
    .string "us with pestilence, or with the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_4::
    .string "And the king of Egypt said unto\n"
    .string "them, Wherefore do ye, Moses and\l"
    .string "Aaron, let the people from their\l"
    .string "works? get you unto your burdens.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_5::
    .string "And Pharaoh said, Behold, the\n"
    .string "people of the land now are many,\l"
    .string "and ye make them rest from their\l"
    .string "burdens.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_6::
    .string "And Pharaoh commanded the same day\n"
    .string "the taskmasters of the people, and\l"
    .string "their officers, saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_7::
    .string "Ye shall no more give the people\n"
    .string "straw to make brick, as heretofore:\l"
    .string "let them go and gather straw for\l"
    .string "themselves$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_8::
    .string "And the tale of the bricks, which\n"
    .string "they did make heretofore, ye shall\l"
    .string "lay upon them; ye shall not\l"
    .string "diminish ought thereof: for they be\l"
    .string "idle; therefore they cry, saying,\l"
    .string "Let us go and sacrifice to our God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_9::
    .string "Let there more work be laid upon\n"
    .string "the men, that they may labour\l"
    .string "therein; and let them not regard\l"
    .string "vain words.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_10::
    .string "And the taskmasters of the people\n"
    .string "went out, and their officers, and\l"
    .string "they spake to the people, saying,\l"
    .string "Thus saith Pharaoh, I will not give\l"
    .string "you straw.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_11::
    .string "Go ye, get you straw where ye can\n"
    .string "find it: yet not ought of your work\l"
    .string "shall be diminished.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_12::
    .string "So the people were scattered\n"
    .string "abroad throughout all the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt to gather stubble instead of\l"
    .string "straw.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_13::
    .string "And the taskmasters hasted them,\n"
    .string "saying, Fulfil your works, your\l"
    .string "daily tasks, as when there was straw.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_14::
    .string "And the officers of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, which Pharaoh’s taskmasters\l"
    .string "had set over them, were beaten, and\l"
    .string "demanded, Wherefore have ye not\l"
    .string "fulfilled your task in making\l"
    .string "brick both yesterday and to day, as\l"
    .string "heretofore?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_15::
    .string "Then the officers of the children\n"
    .string "of Israel came and cried unto\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, saying, Wherefore dealest\l"
    .string "thou thus with thy servants?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_16::
    .string "There is no straw given unto thy\n"
    .string "servants, and they say to us, Make\l"
    .string "brick: and, behold, thy servants are\l"
    .string "beaten; but the fault is in thine own\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_17::
    .string "But he said, Ye are idle, ye are\n"
    .string "idle: therefore ye say, Let us go and\l"
    .string "do sacrifice to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_18::
    .string "Go therefore now, and work; for\n"
    .string "there shall no straw be given you,\l"
    .string "yet shall ye deliver the tale of\l"
    .string "bricks.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_19::
    .string "And the officers of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel did see that they were in\l"
    .string "evil case, after it was said, Ye\l"
    .string "shall not minish ought from your\l"
    .string "bricks of your daily task.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_20::
    .string "And they met Moses and Aaron, who\n"
    .string "stood in the way, as they came forth\l"
    .string "from Pharaoh:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_21::
    .string "And they said unto them, The LORD\n"
    .string "look upon you, and judge; because ye\l"
    .string "have made our savour to be abhorred\l"
    .string "in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the\l"
    .string "eyes of his servants, to put a sword\l"
    .string "in their hand to slay us$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_22::
    .string "And Moses returned unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and said, LORD, wherefore hast thou\l"
    .string "so evil entreated this people? why\l"
    .string "is it that thou hast sent me?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_5_23::
    .string "For since I came to Pharaoh to\n"
    .string "speak in thy name, he hath done evil\l"
    .string "to this people; neither hast thou\l"
    .string "delivered thy people at all$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_1::
    .string "Then the LORD said unto Moses, Now\n"
    .string "shalt thou see what I will do to\l"
    .string "Pharaoh: for with a strong hand\l"
    .string "shall he let them go, and with a\l"
    .string "strong hand shall he drive them out\l"
    .string "of his land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_2::
    .string "And God spake unto Moses, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, I am the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_3::
    .string "And I appeared unto Abraham, unto\n"
    .string "Isaac, and unto Jacob, by the name of\l"
    .string "God Almighty, but by my name JEHOVAH\l"
    .string "was I not known to them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_4::
    .string "And I have also established my\n"
    .string "covenant with them, to give them the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan, the land of their\l"
    .string "pilgrimage, wherein they were\l"
    .string "strangers.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_5::
    .string "And I have also heard the groaning\n"
    .string "of the children of Israel, whom the\l"
    .string "Egyptians keep in bondage; and I\l"
    .string "have remembered my covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_6::
    .string "Wherefore say unto the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, I am the LORD, and I will\l"
    .string "bring you out from under the burdens\l"
    .string "of the Egyptians, and I will rid\l"
    .string "you out of their bondage, and I will\l"
    .string "redeem you with a stretched out arm,\l"
    .string "and with great judgments:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_7::
    .string "And I will take you to me for a\n"
    .string "people, and I will be to you a God:\l"
    .string "and ye shall know that I am the LORD\l"
    .string "your God, which bringeth you out from\l"
    .string "under the burdens of the Egyptians$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_8::
    .string "And I will bring you in unto the\n"
    .string "land, concerning the which I did\l"
    .string "swear to give it to Abraham, to\l"
    .string "Isaac, and to Jacob; and I will give\l"
    .string "it you for an heritage: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_9::
    .string "And Moses spake so unto the\n"
    .string "children of Israel: but they\l"
    .string "hearkened not unto Moses for anguish\l"
    .string "of spirit, and for cruel bondage.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_10::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_11::
    .string "Go in, speak unto Pharaoh king of\n"
    .string "Egypt, that he let the children of\l"
    .string "Israel go out of his land$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_12::
    .string "And Moses spake before the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying, Behold, the children of\l"
    .string "Israel have not hearkened unto me;\l"
    .string "how then shall Pharaoh hear me, who\l"
    .string "am of uncircumcised lips?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_13::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, and gave them a charge\l"
    .string "unto the children of Israel, and\l"
    .string "unto Pharaoh king of Egypt, to bring\l"
    .string "the children of Israel out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_14::
    .string "These be the heads of their fathers’\n"
    .string "houses: The sons of Reuben the\l"
    .string "firstborn of Israel; Hanoch, and\l"
    .string "Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi: these be\l"
    .string "the families of Reuben.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_15::
    .string "And the sons of Simeon; Jemuel, and\n"
    .string "Jamin, and Ohad, and Jachin, and\l"
    .string "Zohar, and Shaul the son of a\l"
    .string "Canaanitish woman: these are the\l"
    .string "families of Simeon.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_16::
    .string "And these are the names of the sons\n"
    .string "of Levi according to their\l"
    .string "generations; Gershon, and Kohath, and\l"
    .string "Merari: and the years of the life of\l"
    .string "Levi were an hundred thirty and seven\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_17::
    .string "The sons of Gershon; Libni, and\n"
    .string "Shimi, according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_18::
    .string "And the sons of Kohath; Amram, and\n"
    .string "Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel: and\l"
    .string "the years of the life of Kohath were\l"
    .string "an hundred thirty and three years.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_19::
    .string "And the sons of Merari; Mahali and\n"
    .string "Mushi: these are the families of\l"
    .string "Levi according to their generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_20::
    .string "And Amram took him Jochebed his\n"
    .string "father’s sister to wife; and she bare\l"
    .string "him Aaron and Moses: and the years of\l"
    .string "the life of Amram were an hundred\l"
    .string "and thirty and seven years.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_21::
    .string "And the sons of Izhar; Korah, and\n"
    .string "Nepheg, and Zichri.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_22::
    .string "And the sons of Uzziel; Mishael,\n"
    .string "and Elzaphan, and Zithri.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_23::
    .string "And Aaron took him Elisheba,\n"
    .string "daughter of Amminadab, sister of\l"
    .string "Naashon, to wife; and she bare him\l"
    .string "Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar, and\l"
    .string "Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_24::
    .string "And the sons of Korah; Assir, and\n"
    .string "Elkanah, and Abiasaph: these are\l"
    .string "the families of the Korhites.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_25::
    .string "And Eleazar Aaron’s son took him\n"
    .string "one of the daughters of Putiel to\l"
    .string "wife; and she bare him Phinehas:\l"
    .string "these are the heads of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the Levites according to their\l"
    .string "families.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_26::
    .string "These are that Aaron and Moses, to\n"
    .string "whom the LORD said, Bring out the\l"
    .string "children of Israel from the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt according to their armies.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_27::
    .string "These are they which spake to\n"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, to bring out\l"
    .string "the children of Israel from Egypt:\l"
    .string "these are that Moses and Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_28::
    .string "And it came to pass on the day when\n"
    .string "the LORD spake unto Moses in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_29::
    .string "That the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying, I am the LORD: speak thou\l"
    .string "unto Pharaoh king of Egypt all that\l"
    .string "I say unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_6_30::
    .string "And Moses said before the LORD,\n"
    .string "Behold, I am of uncircumcised lips,\l"
    .string "and how shall Pharaoh hearken unto\l"
    .string "me?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, See, I\n"
    .string "have made thee a god to Pharaoh: and\l"
    .string "Aaron thy brother shall be thy\l"
    .string "prophet$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_2::
    .string "Thou shalt speak all that I\n"
    .string "command thee: and Aaron thy brother\l"
    .string "shall speak unto Pharaoh, that he\l"
    .string "send the children of Israel out of\l"
    .string "his land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_3::
    .string "And I will harden Pharaoh’s heart,\n"
    .string "and multiply my signs and my\l"
    .string "wonders in the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_4::
    .string "But Pharaoh shall not hearken unto\n"
    .string "you, that I may lay my hand upon\l"
    .string "Egypt, and bring forth mine armies,\l"
    .string "and my people the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, out of the land of Egypt by\l"
    .string "great judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_5::
    .string "And the Egyptians shall know that\n"
    .string "I am the LORD, when I stretch forth\l"
    .string "mine hand upon Egypt, and bring out\l"
    .string "the children of Israel from among\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_6::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron did as the LORD\n"
    .string "commanded them, so did they.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_7::
    .string "And Moses was fourscore years old,\n"
    .string "and Aaron fourscore and three years\l"
    .string "old, when they spake unto Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_8::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_9::
    .string "When Pharaoh shall speak unto you,\n"
    .string "saying, Shew a miracle for you: then\l"
    .string "thou shalt say unto Aaron, Take thy\l"
    .string "rod, and cast it before Pharaoh, and\l"
    .string "it shall become a serpent$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_10::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron went in unto\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and they did so as the LORD\l"
    .string "had commanded: and Aaron cast down\l"
    .string "his rod before Pharaoh, and before\l"
    .string "his servants, and it became a\l"
    .string "serpent.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_11::
    .string "Then Pharaoh also called the wise\n"
    .string "men and the sorcerers: now the\l"
    .string "magicians of Egypt, they also did in\l"
    .string "like manner with their enchantments.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_12::
    .string "For they cast down every man his\n"
    .string "rod, and they became serpents: but\l"
    .string "Aaron’s rod swallowed up their\l"
    .string "rods.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_13::
    .string "And he hardened Pharaoh’s heart,\n"
    .string "that he hearkened not unto them; as\l"
    .string "the LORD had said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_14::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Pharaoh’s heart is hardened, he\l"
    .string "refuseth to let the people go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_15::
    .string "Get thee unto Pharaoh in the\n"
    .string "morning; lo, he goeth out unto the\l"
    .string "water; and thou shalt stand by the\l"
    .string "river’s brink against he come; and\l"
    .string "the rod which was turned to a\l"
    .string "serpent shalt thou take in thine\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_16::
    .string "And thou shalt say unto him, The\n"
    .string "LORD God of the Hebrews hath sent me\l"
    .string "unto thee, saying, Let my people\l"
    .string "go, that they may serve me in the\l"
    .string "wilderness: and, behold, hitherto\l"
    .string "thou wouldest not hear.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_17::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, In this thou\n"
    .string "shalt know that I am the LORD:\l"
    .string "behold, I will smite with the rod\l"
    .string "that is in mine hand upon the waters\l"
    .string "which are in the river, and they\l"
    .string "shall be turned to blood.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_18::
    .string "And the fish that is in the river\n"
    .string "shall die, and the river shall\l"
    .string "stink; and the Egyptians shall\l"
    .string "lothe to drink of the water of the\l"
    .string "river.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_19::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses, Say\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, Take thy rod, and stretch\l"
    .string "out thine hand upon the waters of\l"
    .string "Egypt, upon their streams, upon\l"
    .string "their rivers, and upon their ponds,\l"
    .string "and upon all their pools of water,\l"
    .string "that they may become blood; and that\l"
    .string "there may be blood throughout all\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt, both in vessels\l"
    .string "of wood, and in vessels of stone.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_20::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron did so, as the\n"
    .string "LORD commanded; and he lifted up the\l"
    .string "rod, and smote the waters that were\l"
    .string "in the river, in the sight of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and in the sight of his\l"
    .string "servants; and all the waters that\l"
    .string "were in the river were turned to\l"
    .string "blood.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_21::
    .string "And the fish that was in the river\n"
    .string "died; and the river stank, and the\l"
    .string "Egyptians could not drink of the\l"
    .string "water of the river; and there was\l"
    .string "blood throughout all the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_22::
    .string "And the magicians of Egypt did so\n"
    .string "with their enchantments: and\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s heart was hardened,\l"
    .string "neither did he hearken unto them; as\l"
    .string "the LORD had said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_23::
    .string "And Pharaoh turned and went into his\n"
    .string "house, neither did he set his heart\l"
    .string "to this also.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_24::
    .string "And all the Egyptians digged\n"
    .string "round about the river for water to\l"
    .string "drink; for they could not drink of\l"
    .string "the water of the river.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_7_25::
    .string "And seven days were fulfilled,\n"
    .string "after that the LORD had smitten the\l"
    .string "river.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses, Go\n"
    .string "unto Pharaoh, and say unto him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Let my people go,\l"
    .string "that they may serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_2::
    .string "And if thou refuse to let them go,\n"
    .string "behold, I will smite all thy\l"
    .string "borders with frogs:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_3::
    .string "And the river shall bring forth\n"
    .string "frogs abundantly, which shall go\l"
    .string "up and come into thine house, and\l"
    .string "into thy bedchamber, and upon thy\l"
    .string "bed, and into the house of thy\l"
    .string "servants, and upon thy people, and\l"
    .string "into thine ovens, and into thy\l"
    .string "kneadingtroughs:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_4::
    .string "And the frogs shall come up both\n"
    .string "on thee, and upon thy people, and\l"
    .string "upon all thy servants$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_5::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses, Say\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, Stretch forth thine hand\l"
    .string "with thy rod over the streams, over\l"
    .string "the rivers, and over the ponds, and\l"
    .string "cause frogs to come up upon the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_6::
    .string "And Aaron stretched out his hand\n"
    .string "over the waters of Egypt; and the\l"
    .string "frogs came up, and covered the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_7::
    .string "And the magicians did so with their\n"
    .string "enchantments, and brought up frogs\l"
    .string "upon the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_8::
    .string "Then Pharaoh called for Moses and\n"
    .string "Aaron, and said, Intreat the LORD,\l"
    .string "that he may take away the frogs from\l"
    .string "me, and from my people; and I will\l"
    .string "let the people go, that they may do\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_9::
    .string "And Moses said unto Pharaoh, Glory\n"
    .string "over me: when shall I intreat for\l"
    .string "thee, and for thy servants, and for\l"
    .string "thy people, to destroy the frogs\l"
    .string "from thee and thy houses, that they\l"
    .string "may remain in the river only?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_10::
    .string "And he said, To morrow. And he said,\n"
    .string "Be it according to thy word: that\l"
    .string "thou mayest know that there is none\l"
    .string "like unto the LORD our God$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_11::
    .string "And the frogs shall depart from\n"
    .string "thee, and from thy houses, and from\l"
    .string "thy servants, and from thy people;\l"
    .string "they shall remain in the river only.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_12::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron went out from\n"
    .string "Pharaoh: and Moses cried unto the\l"
    .string "LORD because of the frogs which he\l"
    .string "had brought against Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_13::
    .string "And the LORD did according to the\n"
    .string "word of Moses; and the frogs died out\l"
    .string "of the houses, out of the villages,\l"
    .string "and out of the fields.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_14::
    .string "And they gathered them together\n"
    .string "upon heaps: and the land stank.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_15::
    .string "But when Pharaoh saw that there was\n"
    .string "respite, he hardened his heart, and\l"
    .string "hearkened not unto them; as the LORD\l"
    .string "had said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_16::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Say\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, Stretch out thy rod, and\l"
    .string "smite the dust of the land, that it\l"
    .string "may become lice throughout all the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_17::
    .string "And they did so; for Aaron stretched\n"
    .string "out his hand with his rod, and smote\l"
    .string "the dust of the earth, and it became\l"
    .string "lice in man, and in beast; all the\l"
    .string "dust of the land became lice\l"
    .string "throughout all the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_18::
    .string "And the magicians did so with their\n"
    .string "enchantments to bring forth lice,\l"
    .string "but they could not: so there were\l"
    .string "lice upon man, and upon beast.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_19::
    .string "Then the magicians said unto\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, This is the finger of God:\l"
    .string "and Pharaoh’s heart was hardened, and\l"
    .string "he hearkened not unto them; as the\l"
    .string "LORD had said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_20::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Rise\n"
    .string "up early in the morning, and stand\l"
    .string "before Pharaoh; lo, he cometh forth\l"
    .string "to the water; and say unto him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Let my people go,\l"
    .string "that they may serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_21::
    .string "Else, if thou wilt not let my\n"
    .string "people go, behold, I will send\l"
    .string "swarms of flies upon thee, and upon\l"
    .string "thy servants, and upon thy people,\l"
    .string "and into thy houses: and the houses\l"
    .string "of the Egyptians shall be full of\l"
    .string "swarms of flies, and also the ground\l"
    .string "whereon they are.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_22::
    .string "And I will sever in that day the\n"
    .string "land of Goshen, in which my people\l"
    .string "dwell, that no swarms of flies\l"
    .string "shall be there; to the end thou\l"
    .string "mayest know that I am the LORD in the\l"
    .string "midst of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_23::
    .string "And I will put a division between\n"
    .string "my people and thy people: to\l"
    .string "morrow shall this sign be.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_24::
    .string "And the LORD did so; and there came a\n"
    .string "grievous swarm of flies into the\l"
    .string "house of Pharaoh, and into his\l"
    .string "servants’ houses, and into all the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt: the land was\l"
    .string "corrupted by reason of the swarm of\l"
    .string "flies.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_25::
    .string "And Pharaoh called for Moses and\n"
    .string "for Aaron, and said, Go ye, sacrifice\l"
    .string "to your God in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_26::
    .string "And Moses said, It is not meet so to\n"
    .string "do; for we shall sacrifice the\l"
    .string "abomination of the Egyptians to the\l"
    .string "LORD our God: lo, shall we\l"
    .string "sacrifice the abomination of the\l"
    .string "Egyptians before their eyes, and\l"
    .string "will they not stone us?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_27::
    .string "We will go three days’ journey\n"
    .string "into the wilderness, and sacrifice\l"
    .string "to the LORD our God, as he shall\l"
    .string "command us$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_28::
    .string "And Pharaoh said, I will let you\n"
    .string "go, that ye may sacrifice to the LORD\l"
    .string "your God in the wilderness; only ye\l"
    .string "shall not go very far away: intreat\l"
    .string "for me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_29::
    .string "And Moses said, Behold, I go out\n"
    .string "from thee, and I will intreat the\l"
    .string "LORD that the swarms of flies may\l"
    .string "depart from Pharaoh, from his\l"
    .string "servants, and from his people, to\l"
    .string "morrow: but let not Pharaoh deal\l"
    .string "deceitfully any more in not\l"
    .string "letting the people go to sacrifice\l"
    .string "to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_30::
    .string "And Moses went out from Pharaoh, and\n"
    .string "intreated the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_31::
    .string "And the LORD did according to the\n"
    .string "word of Moses; and he removed the\l"
    .string "swarms of flies from Pharaoh, from\l"
    .string "his servants, and from his people;\l"
    .string "there remained not one.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_8_32::
    .string "And Pharaoh hardened his heart at\n"
    .string "this time also, neither would he\l"
    .string "let the people go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_1::
    .string "Then the LORD said unto Moses, Go in\n"
    .string "unto Pharaoh, and tell him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD God of the Hebrews,\l"
    .string "Let my people go, that they may\l"
    .string "serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_2::
    .string "For if thou refuse to let them go,\n"
    .string "and wilt hold them still,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_3::
    .string "Behold, the hand of the LORD is\n"
    .string "upon thy cattle which is in the\l"
    .string "field, upon the horses, upon the\l"
    .string "asses, upon the camels, upon the\l"
    .string "oxen, and upon the sheep: there\l"
    .string "shall be a very grievous murrain$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_4::
    .string "And the LORD shall sever between\n"
    .string "the cattle of Israel and the cattle\l"
    .string "of Egypt: and there shall nothing\l"
    .string "die of all that is the children’s\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_5::
    .string "And the LORD appointed a set time,\n"
    .string "saying, To morrow the LORD shall do\l"
    .string "this thing in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_6::
    .string "And the LORD did that thing on the\n"
    .string "morrow, and all the cattle of\l"
    .string "Egypt died: but of the cattle of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel died not one.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_7::
    .string "And Pharaoh sent, and, behold,\n"
    .string "there was not one of the cattle of\l"
    .string "the Israelites dead. And the heart\l"
    .string "of Pharaoh was hardened, and he did\l"
    .string "not let the people go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_8::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, Take to you handfuls of\l"
    .string "ashes of the furnace, and let Moses\l"
    .string "sprinkle it toward the heaven in\l"
    .string "the sight of Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_9::
    .string "And it shall become small dust in\n"
    .string "all the land of Egypt, and shall\l"
    .string "be a boil breaking forth with\l"
    .string "blains upon man, and upon beast,\l"
    .string "throughout all the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_10::
    .string "And they took ashes of the furnace,\n"
    .string "and stood before Pharaoh; and Moses\l"
    .string "sprinkled it up toward heaven; and\l"
    .string "it became a boil breaking forth with\l"
    .string "blains upon man, and upon beast.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_11::
    .string "And the magicians could not stand\n"
    .string "before Moses because of the boils;\l"
    .string "for the boil was upon the magicians,\l"
    .string "and upon all the Egyptians.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_12::
    .string "And the LORD hardened the heart of\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and he hearkened not unto\l"
    .string "them; as the LORD had spoken unto\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_13::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Rise\n"
    .string "up early in the morning, and stand\l"
    .string "before Pharaoh, and say unto him,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD God of the\l"
    .string "Hebrews, Let my people go, that\l"
    .string "they may serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_14::
    .string "For I will at this time send all\n"
    .string "my plagues upon thine heart, and\l"
    .string "upon thy servants, and upon thy\l"
    .string "people; that thou mayest know that\l"
    .string "there is none like me in all the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_15::
    .string "For now I will stretch out my hand,\n"
    .string "that I may smite thee and thy\l"
    .string "people with pestilence; and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be cut off from the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_16::
    .string "And in very deed for this cause have\n"
    .string "I raised thee up, for to shew in thee\l"
    .string "my power; and that my name may be\l"
    .string "declared throughout all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_17::
    .string "As yet exaltest thou thyself\n"
    .string "against my people, that thou wilt\l"
    .string "not let them go?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_18::
    .string "Behold, to morrow about this time I\n"
    .string "will cause it to rain a very\l"
    .string "grievous hail, such as hath not been\l"
    .string "in Egypt since the foundation\l"
    .string "thereof even until now$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_19::
    .string "Send therefore now, and gather thy\n"
    .string "cattle, and all that thou hast in\l"
    .string "the field; for upon every man and\l"
    .string "beast which shall be found in the\l"
    .string "field, and shall not be brought\l"
    .string "home, the hail shall come down\l"
    .string "upon them, and they shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_20::
    .string "He that feared the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "among the servants of Pharaoh made\l"
    .string "his servants and his cattle flee\l"
    .string "into the houses:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_21::
    .string "And he that regarded not the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD left his servants and his\l"
    .string "cattle in the field$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_22::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Stretch forth thine hand toward\l"
    .string "heaven, that there may be hail in\l"
    .string "all the land of Egypt, upon man,\l"
    .string "and upon beast, and upon every herb\l"
    .string "of the field, throughout the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_23::
    .string "And Moses stretched forth his rod\n"
    .string "toward heaven: and the LORD sent\l"
    .string "thunder and hail, and the fire ran\l"
    .string "along upon the ground; and the LORD\l"
    .string "rained hail upon the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_24::
    .string "So there was hail, and fire mingled\n"
    .string "with the hail, very grievous, such\l"
    .string "as there was none like it in all\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt since it became a\l"
    .string "nation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_25::
    .string "And the hail smote throughout all\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt all that was in\l"
    .string "the field, both man and beast; and\l"
    .string "the hail smote every herb of the\l"
    .string "field, and brake every tree of the\l"
    .string "field.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_26::
    .string "Only in the land of Goshen, where\n"
    .string "the children of Israel were, was\l"
    .string "there no hail.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_27::
    .string "And Pharaoh sent, and called for\n"
    .string "Moses and Aaron, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "I have sinned this time: the LORD is\l"
    .string "righteous, and I and my people are\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_28::
    .string "Intreat the LORD (for it is enough)\n"
    .string "that there be no more mighty\l"
    .string "thunderings and hail; and I will\l"
    .string "let you go, and ye shall stay no\l"
    .string "longer.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_29::
    .string "And Moses said unto him, As soon as I\n"
    .string "am gone out of the city, I will\l"
    .string "spread abroad my hands unto the\l"
    .string "LORD; and the thunder shall cease,\l"
    .string "neither shall there be any more\l"
    .string "hail; that thou mayest know how that\l"
    .string "the earth is the LORD’s.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_30::
    .string "But as for thee and thy servants, I\n"
    .string "know that ye will not yet fear the\l"
    .string "LORD God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_31::
    .string "And the flax and the barley was\n"
    .string "smitten: for the barley was in the\l"
    .string "ear, and the flax was bolled.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_32::
    .string "But the wheat and the rie were not\n"
    .string "smitten: for they were not grown up.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_33::
    .string "And Moses went out of the city from\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and spread abroad his hands\l"
    .string "unto the LORD: and the thunders and\l"
    .string "hail ceased, and the rain was not\l"
    .string "poured upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_34::
    .string "And when Pharaoh saw that the rain\n"
    .string "and the hail and the thunders were\l"
    .string "ceased, he sinned yet more, and\l"
    .string "hardened his heart, he and his\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_9_35::
    .string "And the heart of Pharaoh was\n"
    .string "hardened, neither would he let the\l"
    .string "children of Israel go; as the LORD\l"
    .string "had spoken by Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Go in\n"
    .string "unto Pharaoh: for I have hardened his\l"
    .string "heart, and the heart of his servants,\l"
    .string "that I might shew these my signs\l"
    .string "before him:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_2::
    .string "And that thou mayest tell in the\n"
    .string "ears of thy son, and of thy son’s son,\l"
    .string "what things I have wrought in Egypt,\l"
    .string "and my signs which I have done among\l"
    .string "them; that ye may know how that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_3::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron came in unto\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and said unto him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD God of the Hebrews,\l"
    .string "How long wilt thou refuse to humble\l"
    .string "thyself before me? let my people\l"
    .string "go, that they may serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_4::
    .string "Else, if thou refuse to let my\n"
    .string "people go, behold, to morrow will\l"
    .string "I bring the locusts into thy coast:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_5::
    .string "And they shall cover the face of\n"
    .string "the earth, that one cannot be able to\l"
    .string "see the earth: and they shall eat\l"
    .string "the residue of that which is\l"
    .string "escaped, which remaineth unto you\l"
    .string "from the hail, and shall eat every\l"
    .string "tree which groweth for you out of the\l"
    .string "field:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_6::
    .string "And they shall fill thy houses,\n"
    .string "and the houses of all thy servants,\l"
    .string "and the houses of all the\l"
    .string "Egyptians; which neither thy\l"
    .string "fathers, nor thy fathers’ fathers\l"
    .string "have seen, since the day that they\l"
    .string "were upon the earth unto this day.\l"
    .string "And he turned himself, and went out\l"
    .string "from Pharaoh$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_7::
    .string "And Pharaoh’s servants said unto\n"
    .string "him, How long shall this man be a\l"
    .string "snare unto us? let the men go, that\l"
    .string "they may serve the LORD their God:\l"
    .string "knowest thou not yet that Egypt is\l"
    .string "destroyed?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_8::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron were brought\n"
    .string "again unto Pharaoh: and he said unto\l"
    .string "them, Go, serve the LORD your God: but\l"
    .string "who are they that shall go?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_9::
    .string "And Moses said, We will go with our\n"
    .string "young and with our old, with our sons\l"
    .string "and with our daughters, with our\l"
    .string "flocks and with our herds will we\l"
    .string "go; for we must hold a feast unto the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_10::
    .string "And he said unto them, Let the LORD\n"
    .string "be so with you, as I will let you\l"
    .string "go, and your little ones: look to\l"
    .string "it; for evil is before you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_11::
    .string "Not so: go now ye that are men, and\n"
    .string "serve the LORD; for that ye did desire\l"
    .string " And they were driven out from\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s presence.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_12::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Stretch out thine hand over the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt for the locusts, that they\l"
    .string "may come up upon the land of Egypt,\l"
    .string "and eat every herb of the land, even\l"
    .string "all that the hail hath left.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_13::
    .string "And Moses stretched forth his rod\n"
    .string "over the land of Egypt, and the LORD\l"
    .string "brought an east wind upon the land\l"
    .string "all that day, and all that night;\l"
    .string "and when it was morning, the east\l"
    .string "wind brought the locusts.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_14::
    .string "And the locust went up over all\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt, and rested in\l"
    .string "all the coasts of Egypt: very\l"
    .string "grievous were they; before them there\l"
    .string "were no such locusts as they,\l"
    .string "neither after them shall be such.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_15::
    .string "For they covered the face of the\n"
    .string "whole earth, so that the land was\l"
    .string "darkened; and they did eat every herb\l"
    .string "of the land, and all the fruit of\l"
    .string "the trees which the hail had left:\l"
    .string "and there remained not any green\l"
    .string "thing in the trees, or in the herbs of\l"
    .string "the field, through all the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_16::
    .string "Then Pharaoh called for Moses and\n"
    .string "Aaron in haste; and he said, I have\l"
    .string "sinned against the LORD your God, and\l"
    .string "against you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_17::
    .string "Now therefore forgive, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "my sin only this once, and intreat\l"
    .string "the LORD your God, that he may take\l"
    .string "away from me this death only.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_18::
    .string "And he went out from Pharaoh, and\n"
    .string "intreated the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_19::
    .string "And the LORD turned a mighty strong\n"
    .string "west wind, which took away the\l"
    .string "locusts, and cast them into the Red\l"
    .string "sea; there remained not one locust\l"
    .string "in all the coasts of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_20::
    .string "But the LORD hardened Pharaoh’s\n"
    .string "heart, so that he would not let the\l"
    .string "children of Israel go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_21::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Stretch out thine hand toward heaven,\l"
    .string "that there may be darkness over the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, even darkness which\l"
    .string "may be felt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_22::
    .string "And Moses stretched forth his hand\n"
    .string "toward heaven; and there was a thick\l"
    .string "darkness in all the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "three days:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_23::
    .string "They saw not one another, neither\n"
    .string "rose any from his place for three\l"
    .string "days: but all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel had light in their\l"
    .string "dwellings$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_24::
    .string "And Pharaoh called unto Moses, and\n"
    .string "said, Go ye, serve the LORD; only\l"
    .string "let your flocks and your herds be\l"
    .string "stayed: let your little ones also\l"
    .string "go with you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_25::
    .string "And Moses said, Thou must give us\n"
    .string "also sacrifices and burnt offerings,\l"
    .string "that we may sacrifice unto the LORD\l"
    .string "our God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_26::
    .string "Our cattle also shall go with us;\n"
    .string "there shall not an hoof be left\l"
    .string "behind; for thereof must we take to\l"
    .string "serve the LORD our God; and we know\l"
    .string "not with what we must serve the LORD,\l"
    .string "until we come thither.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_27::
    .string "But the LORD hardened Pharaoh’s\n"
    .string "heart, and he would not let them go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_28::
    .string "And Pharaoh said unto him, Get thee\n"
    .string "from me, take heed to thyself, see my\l"
    .string "face no more; for in that day thou\l"
    .string "seest my face thou shalt die.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_10_29::
    .string "And Moses said, Thou hast spoken\n"
    .string "well, I will see thy face again no\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Yet\n"
    .string "will I bring one plague more upon\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and upon Egypt; afterwards\l"
    .string "he will let you go hence: when he\l"
    .string "shall let you go, he shall surely\l"
    .string "thrust you out hence altogether.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_2::
    .string "Speak now in the ears of the\n"
    .string "people, and let every man borrow of\l"
    .string "his neighbour, and every woman of her\l"
    .string "neighbour, jewels of silver and\l"
    .string "jewels of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_3::
    .string "And the LORD gave the people\n"
    .string "favour in the sight of the\l"
    .string "Egyptians. Moreover the man Moses\l"
    .string "was very great in the land of Egypt,\l"
    .string "in the sight of Pharaoh’s servants,\l"
    .string "and in the sight of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_4::
    .string "And Moses said, Thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "About midnight will I go out into\l"
    .string "the midst of Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_5::
    .string "And all the firstborn in the land\n"
    .string "of Egypt shall die, from the first\l"
    .string "born of Pharaoh that sitteth upon\l"
    .string "his throne, even unto the firstborn\l"
    .string "of the maidservant that is behind the\l"
    .string "mill; and all the firstborn of\l"
    .string "beasts$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_6::
    .string "And there shall be a great cry\n"
    .string "throughout all the land of Egypt,\l"
    .string "such as there was none like it, nor\l"
    .string "shall be like it any more.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_7::
    .string "But against any of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel shall not a dog move his\l"
    .string "tongue, against man or beast: that ye\l"
    .string "may know how that the LORD doth put a\l"
    .string "difference between the Egyptians\l"
    .string "and Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_8::
    .string "And all these thy servants shall\n"
    .string "come down unto me, and bow down\l"
    .string "themselves unto me, saying, Get thee\l"
    .string "out, and all the people that\l"
    .string "follow thee: and after that I will\l"
    .string "go out. And he went out from Pharaoh\l"
    .string "in a great anger.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Pharaoh shall not hearken unto you;\l"
    .string "that my wonders may be multiplied\l"
    .string "in the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_11_10::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron did all these\n"
    .string "wonders before Pharaoh: and the LORD\l"
    .string "hardened Pharaoh’s heart, so that he\l"
    .string "would not let the children of\l"
    .string "Israel go out of his land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "Aaron in the land of Egypt saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_2::
    .string "This month shall be unto you the\n"
    .string "beginning of months: it shall be the\l"
    .string "first month of the year to you$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_3::
    .string "Speak ye unto all the\n"
    .string "congregation of Israel, saying, In\l"
    .string "the tenth day of this month they\l"
    .string "shall take to them every man a\l"
    .string "lamb, according to the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, a lamb for an house:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_4::
    .string "And if the household be too little\n"
    .string "for the lamb, let him and his\l"
    .string "neighbour next unto his house take it\l"
    .string "according to the number of the\l"
    .string "souls; every man according to his\l"
    .string "eating shall make your count for\l"
    .string "the lamb$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_5::
    .string "Your lamb shall be without\n"
    .string "blemish, a male of the first year:\l"
    .string "ye shall take it out from the\l"
    .string "sheep, or from the goats:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_6::
    .string "And ye shall keep it up until the\n"
    .string "fourteenth day of the same month: and\l"
    .string "the whole assembly of the\l"
    .string "congregation of Israel shall kill\l"
    .string "it in the evening$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_7::
    .string "And they shall take of the blood,\n"
    .string "and strike it on the two side posts\l"
    .string "and on the upper door post of the\l"
    .string "houses, wherein they shall eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_8::
    .string "And they shall eat the flesh in\n"
    .string "that night, roast with fire, and\l"
    .string "unleavened bread; and with bitter\l"
    .string "herbs they shall eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_9::
    .string "Eat not of it raw, nor sodden at\n"
    .string "all with water, but roast with fire;\l"
    .string "his head with his legs, and with the\l"
    .string "purtenance thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_10::
    .string "And ye shall let nothing of it\n"
    .string "remain until the morning; and that\l"
    .string "which remaineth of it until the\l"
    .string "morning ye shall burn with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_11::
    .string "And thus shall ye eat it; with your\n"
    .string "loins girded, your shoes on your\l"
    .string "feet, and your staff in your hand;\l"
    .string "and ye shall eat it in haste: it is\l"
    .string "the LORD’s passover.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_12::
    .string "For I will pass through the land\n"
    .string "of Egypt this night, and will smite\l"
    .string "all the firstborn in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, both man and beast; and\l"
    .string "against all the gods of Egypt I\l"
    .string "will execute judgment: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_13::
    .string "And the blood shall be to you for\n"
    .string "a token upon the houses where ye are:\l"
    .string "and when I see the blood, I will\l"
    .string "pass over you, and the plague\l"
    .string "shall not be upon you to destroy\l"
    .string "you, when I smite the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_14::
    .string "And this day shall be unto you for\n"
    .string "a memorial; and ye shall keep it a\l"
    .string "feast to the LORD throughout your\l"
    .string "generations; ye shall keep it a\l"
    .string "feast by an ordinance for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_15::
    .string "Seven days shall ye eat\n"
    .string "unleavened bread; even the first day\l"
    .string "ye shall put away leaven out of\l"
    .string "your houses: for whosoever eateth\l"
    .string "leavened bread from the first day\l"
    .string "until the seventh day, that soul\l"
    .string "shall be cut off from Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_16::
    .string "And in the first day there shall be\n"
    .string "an holy convocation, and in the\l"
    .string "seventh day there shall be an holy\l"
    .string "convocation to you; no manner of work\l"
    .string "shall be done in them, save that\l"
    .string "which every man must eat, that only\l"
    .string "may be done of you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_17::
    .string "And ye shall observe the feast of\n"
    .string "unleavened bread; for in this\l"
    .string "selfsame day have I brought your\l"
    .string "armies out of the land of Egypt:\l"
    .string "therefore shall ye observe this day\l"
    .string "in your generations by an ordinance\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_18::
    .string "In the first month, on the\n"
    .string "fourteenth day of the month at even,\l"
    .string "ye shall eat unleavened bread,\l"
    .string "until the one and twentieth day of\l"
    .string "the month at even.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_19::
    .string "Seven days shall there be no\n"
    .string "leaven found in your houses: for\l"
    .string "whosoever eateth that which is\l"
    .string "leavened, even that soul shall be\l"
    .string "cut off from the congregation of\l"
    .string "Israel, whether he be a stranger, or\l"
    .string "born in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_20::
    .string "Ye shall eat nothing leavened; in\n"
    .string "all your habitations shall ye eat\l"
    .string "unleavened bread.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_21::
    .string "Then Moses called for all the\n"
    .string "elders of Israel, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Draw out and take you a lamb\l"
    .string "according to your families, and\l"
    .string "kill the passover.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_22::
    .string "And ye shall take a bunch of\n"
    .string "hyssop, and dip it in the blood\l"
    .string "that is in the bason, and strike the\l"
    .string "lintel and the two side posts with\l"
    .string "the blood that is in the bason; and\l"
    .string "none of you shall go out at the door\l"
    .string "of his house until the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_23::
    .string "For the LORD will pass through to\n"
    .string "smite the Egyptians; and when he\l"
    .string "seeth the blood upon the lintel,\l"
    .string "and on the two side posts, the LORD\l"
    .string "will pass over the door, and will\l"
    .string "not suffer the destroyer to come in\l"
    .string "unto your houses to smite you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_24::
    .string "And ye shall observe this thing\n"
    .string "for an ordinance to thee and to thy\l"
    .string "sons for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_25::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when ye\n"
    .string "be come to the land which the LORD\l"
    .string "will give you, according as he hath\l"
    .string "promised, that ye shall keep this\l"
    .string "service.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_26::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "your children shall say unto you,\l"
    .string "What mean ye by this service?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_27::
    .string "That ye shall say, It is the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of the LORD’s passover,\l"
    .string "who passed over the houses of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel in Egypt, when\l"
    .string "he smote the Egyptians, and\l"
    .string "delivered our houses. And the\l"
    .string "people bowed the head and\l"
    .string "worshipped$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_28::
    .string "And the children of Israel went\n"
    .string "away, and did as the LORD had\l"
    .string "commanded Moses and Aaron, so did\l"
    .string "they.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, that at\n"
    .string "midnight the LORD smote all the\l"
    .string "firstborn in the land of Egypt, from\l"
    .string "the firstborn of Pharaoh that sat on\l"
    .string "his throne unto the firstborn of the\l"
    .string "captive that was in the dungeon; and\l"
    .string "all the firstborn of cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_30::
    .string "And Pharaoh rose up in the night,\n"
    .string "he, and all his servants, and all\l"
    .string "the Egyptians; and there was a great\l"
    .string "cry in Egypt; for there was not a\l"
    .string "house where there was not one dead.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_31::
    .string "And he called for Moses and Aaron\n"
    .string "by night, and said, Rise up, and get\l"
    .string "you forth from among my people,\l"
    .string "both ye and the children of Israel;\l"
    .string "and go, serve the LORD, as ye have\l"
    .string "said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_32::
    .string "Also take your flocks and your\n"
    .string "herds, as ye have said, and be gone;\l"
    .string "and bless me also.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_33::
    .string "And the Egyptians were urgent upon\n"
    .string "the people, that they might send\l"
    .string "them out of the land in haste; for\l"
    .string "they said, We be all dead men.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_34::
    .string "And the people took their dough\n"
    .string "before it was leavened, their\l"
    .string "kneadingtroughs being bound up in\l"
    .string "their clothes upon their shoulders.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_35::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "according to the word of Moses; and\l"
    .string "they borrowed of the Egyptians\l"
    .string "jewels of silver, and jewels of\l"
    .string "gold, and raiment:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_36::
    .string "And the LORD gave the people\n"
    .string "favour in the sight of the\l"
    .string "Egyptians, so that they lent unto\l"
    .string "them such things as they required.\l"
    .string "And they spoiled the Egyptians$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_37::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "journeyed from Rameses to Succoth,\l"
    .string "about six hundred thousand on foot\l"
    .string "that were men, beside children.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_38::
    .string "And a mixed multitude went up also\n"
    .string "with them; and flocks, and herds,\l"
    .string "even very much cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_39::
    .string "And they baked unleavened cakes of\n"
    .string "the dough which they brought forth\l"
    .string "out of Egypt, for it was not\l"
    .string "leavened; because they were thrust\l"
    .string "out of Egypt, and could not tarry,\l"
    .string "neither had they prepared for\l"
    .string "themselves any victual.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_40::
    .string "Now the sojourning of the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, who dwelt in Egypt, was\l"
    .string "four hundred and thirty years.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_41::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "the four hundred and thirty years,\l"
    .string "even the selfsame day it came to\l"
    .string "pass, that all the hosts of the LORD\l"
    .string "went out from the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_42::
    .string "It is a night to be much observed\n"
    .string "unto the LORD for bringing them out\l"
    .string "from the land of Egypt: this is that\l"
    .string "night of the LORD to be observed of\l"
    .string "all the children of Israel in\l"
    .string "their generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_43::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses and\n"
    .string "Aaron, This is the ordinance of the\l"
    .string "passover: There shall no stranger\l"
    .string "eat thereof:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_44::
    .string "But every man’s servant that is\n"
    .string "bought for money, when thou hast\l"
    .string "circumcised him, then shall he eat\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_45::
    .string "A foreigner and an hired servant\n"
    .string "shall not eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_46::
    .string "In one house shall it be eaten;\n"
    .string "thou shalt not carry forth ought of\l"
    .string "the flesh abroad out of the house;\l"
    .string "neither shall ye break a bone\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_47::
    .string "All the congregation of Israel\n"
    .string "shall keep it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_48::
    .string "And when a stranger shall sojourn\n"
    .string "with thee, and will keep the\l"
    .string "passover to the LORD, let all his\l"
    .string "males be circumcised, and then let\l"
    .string "him come near and keep it; and he\l"
    .string "shall be as one that is born in the\l"
    .string "land: for no uncircumcised person\l"
    .string "shall eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_49::
    .string "One law shall be to him that is\n"
    .string "homeborn, and unto the stranger that\l"
    .string "sojourneth among you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_50::
    .string "Thus did all the children of\n"
    .string "Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses\l"
    .string "and Aaron, so did they.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_12_51::
    .string "And it came to pass the selfsame\n"
    .string "day, that the LORD did bring the\l"
    .string "children of Israel out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt by their armies.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_2::
    .string "Sanctify unto me all the\n"
    .string "firstborn, whatsoever openeth the\l"
    .string "womb among the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "both of man and of beast: it is mine$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_3::
    .string "And Moses said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Remember this day, in which ye came\l"
    .string "out from Egypt, out of the house of\l"
    .string "bondage; for by strength of hand the\l"
    .string "LORD brought you out from this\l"
    .string "place: there shall no leavened\l"
    .string "bread be eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_4::
    .string "This day came ye out in the month\n"
    .string "Abib.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_5::
    .string "And it shall be when the LORD\n"
    .string "shall bring thee into the land of\l"
    .string "the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and\l"
    .string "the Amorites, and the Hivites, and\l"
    .string "the Jebusites, which he sware unto\l"
    .string "thy fathers to give thee, a land\l"
    .string "flowing with milk and honey, that\l"
    .string "thou shalt keep this service in\l"
    .string "this month.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_6::
    .string "Seven days thou shalt eat\n"
    .string "unleavened bread, and in the seventh\l"
    .string "day shall be a feast to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_7::
    .string "Unleavened bread shall be eaten\n"
    .string "seven days; and there shall no\l"
    .string "leavened bread be seen with thee,\l"
    .string "neither shall there be leaven seen\l"
    .string "with thee in all thy quarters.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_8::
    .string "And thou shalt shew thy son in that\n"
    .string "day, saying, This is done because of\l"
    .string "that which the LORD did unto me when\l"
    .string "I came forth out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_9::
    .string "And it shall be for a sign unto\n"
    .string "thee upon thine hand, and for a\l"
    .string "memorial between thine eyes, that\l"
    .string "the LORD’s law may be in thy mouth:\l"
    .string "for with a strong hand hath the LORD\l"
    .string "brought thee out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_10::
    .string "Thou shalt therefore keep this\n"
    .string "ordinance in his season from year to\l"
    .string "year.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_11::
    .string "And it shall be when the LORD\n"
    .string "shall bring thee into the land of\l"
    .string "the Canaanites, as he sware unto thee\l"
    .string "and to thy fathers, and shall give\l"
    .string "it thee,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_12::
    .string "That thou shalt set apart unto the\n"
    .string "LORD all that openeth the matrix,\l"
    .string "and every firstling that cometh of a\l"
    .string "beast which thou hast; the males\l"
    .string "shall be the LORD’s$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_13::
    .string "And every firstling of an ass thou\n"
    .string "shalt redeem with a lamb; and if\l"
    .string "thou wilt not redeem it, then thou\l"
    .string "shalt break his neck: and all the\l"
    .string "firstborn of man among thy children\l"
    .string "shalt thou redeem.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_14::
    .string "And it shall be when thy son asketh\n"
    .string "thee in time to come, saying, What is\l"
    .string "this? that thou shalt say unto him,\l"
    .string "By strength of hand the LORD brought\l"
    .string "us out from Egypt, from the house of\l"
    .string "bondage:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Pharaoh\n"
    .string "would hardly let us go, that the\l"
    .string "LORD slew all the firstborn in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, both the firstborn of\l"
    .string "man, and the firstborn of beast:\l"
    .string "therefore I sacrifice to the LORD\l"
    .string "all that openeth the matrix, being\l"
    .string "males; but all the firstborn of my\l"
    .string "children I redeem$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_16::
    .string "And it shall be for a token upon\n"
    .string "thine hand, and for frontlets\l"
    .string "between thine eyes: for by strength\l"
    .string "of hand the LORD brought us forth out\l"
    .string "of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Pharaoh\n"
    .string "had let the people go, that God\l"
    .string "led them not through the way of the\l"
    .string "land of the Philistines, although\l"
    .string "that was near; for God said, Lest\l"
    .string "peradventure the people repent\l"
    .string "when they see war, and they return to\l"
    .string "Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_18::
    .string "But God led the people about,\n"
    .string "through the way of the wilderness of\l"
    .string "the Red sea: and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel went up harnessed out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_19::
    .string "And Moses took the bones of Joseph\n"
    .string "with him: for he had straitly sworn\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, saying, God\l"
    .string "will surely visit you; and ye\l"
    .string "shall carry up my bones away hence\l"
    .string "with you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_20::
    .string "And they took their journey from\n"
    .string "Succoth, and encamped in Etham, in\l"
    .string "the edge of the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_21::
    .string "And the LORD went before them by day\n"
    .string "in a pillar of a cloud, to lead\l"
    .string "them the way; and by night in a\l"
    .string "pillar of fire, to give them light;\l"
    .string "to go by day and night:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_13_22::
    .string "He took not away the pillar of the\n"
    .string "cloud by day, nor the pillar of\l"
    .string "fire by night, from before the\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "that they turn and encamp before\l"
    .string "Pihahiroth, between Migdol and the\l"
    .string "sea, over against Baalzephon:\l"
    .string "before it shall ye encamp by the sea$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_3::
    .string "For Pharaoh will say of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, They are\l"
    .string "entangled in the land, the\l"
    .string "wilderness hath shut them in.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_4::
    .string "And I will harden Pharaoh’s heart,\n"
    .string "that he shall follow after them;\l"
    .string "and I will be honoured upon\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and upon all his host;\l"
    .string "that the Egyptians may know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD. And they did so.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_5::
    .string "And it was told the king of Egypt\n"
    .string "that the people fled: and the\l"
    .string "heart of Pharaoh and of his servants\l"
    .string "was turned against the people, and\l"
    .string "they said, Why have we done this,\l"
    .string "that we have let Israel go from\l"
    .string "serving us?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_6::
    .string "And he made ready his chariot, and\n"
    .string "took his people with him:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_7::
    .string "And he took six hundred chosen\n"
    .string "chariots, and all the chariots of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and captains over every one\l"
    .string "of them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_8::
    .string "And the LORD hardened the heart of\n"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, and he\l"
    .string "pursued after the children of\l"
    .string "Israel: and the children of Israel\l"
    .string "went out with an high hand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_9::
    .string "But the Egyptians pursued after\n"
    .string "them, all the horses and chariots of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and his horsemen, and his\l"
    .string "army, and overtook them encamping by\l"
    .string "the sea, beside Pihahiroth, before\l"
    .string "Baalzephon.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_10::
    .string "And when Pharaoh drew nigh, the\n"
    .string "children of Israel lifted up their\l"
    .string "eyes, and, behold, the Egyptians\l"
    .string "marched after them; and they were\l"
    .string "sore afraid: and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel cried out unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_11::
    .string "And they said unto Moses, Because\n"
    .string "there were no graves in Egypt, hast\l"
    .string "thou taken us away to die in the\l"
    .string "wilderness? wherefore hast thou\l"
    .string "dealt thus with us, to carry us forth\l"
    .string "out of Egypt?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_12::
    .string "Is not this the word that we did\n"
    .string "tell thee in Egypt, saying, Let us\l"
    .string "alone, that we may serve the\l"
    .string "Egyptians? For it had been better\l"
    .string "for us to serve the Egyptians, than\l"
    .string "that we should die in the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_13::
    .string "And Moses said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Fear ye not, stand still, and see\l"
    .string "the salvation of the LORD, which he\l"
    .string "will shew to you to day: for the\l"
    .string "Egyptians whom ye have seen to day,\l"
    .string "ye shall see them again no more for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_14::
    .string "The LORD shall fight for you, and\n"
    .string "ye shall hold your peace.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_15::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Wherefore criest thou unto me? speak\l"
    .string "unto the children of Israel, that\l"
    .string "they go forward:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_16::
    .string "But lift thou up thy rod, and\n"
    .string "stretch out thine hand over the sea,\l"
    .string "and divide it: and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel shall go on dry ground\l"
    .string "through the midst of the sea$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_17::
    .string "And I, behold, I will harden the\n"
    .string "hearts of the Egyptians, and they\l"
    .string "shall follow them: and I will get\l"
    .string "me honour upon Pharaoh, and upon\l"
    .string "all his host, upon his chariots,\l"
    .string "and upon his horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_18::
    .string "And the Egyptians shall know that\n"
    .string "I am the LORD, when I have gotten me\l"
    .string "honour upon Pharaoh, upon his\l"
    .string "chariots, and upon his horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_19::
    .string "And the angel of God, which went\n"
    .string "before the camp of Israel, removed\l"
    .string "and went behind them; and the\l"
    .string "pillar of the cloud went from\l"
    .string "before their face, and stood behind\l"
    .string "them:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_20::
    .string "And it came between the camp of the\n"
    .string "Egyptians and the camp of Israel;\l"
    .string "and it was a cloud and darkness to\l"
    .string "them, but it gave light by night to\l"
    .string "these: so that the one came not near\l"
    .string "the other all the night$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_21::
    .string "And Moses stretched out his hand\n"
    .string "over the sea; and the LORD caused the\l"
    .string "sea to go back by a strong east wind\l"
    .string "all that night, and made the sea dry\l"
    .string "land, and the waters were divided.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_22::
    .string "And the children of Israel went\n"
    .string "into the midst of the sea upon the\l"
    .string "dry ground: and the waters were a\l"
    .string "wall unto them on their right hand,\l"
    .string "and on their left.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_23::
    .string "And the Egyptians pursued, and\n"
    .string "went in after them to the midst of\l"
    .string "the sea, even all Pharaoh’s horses,\l"
    .string "his chariots, and his horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_24::
    .string "And it came to pass, that in the\n"
    .string "morning watch the LORD looked unto\l"
    .string "the host of the Egyptians through\l"
    .string "the pillar of fire and of the\l"
    .string "cloud, and troubled the host of the\l"
    .string "Egyptians,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_25::
    .string "And took off their chariot wheels,\n"
    .string "that they drave them heavily: so\l"
    .string "that the Egyptians said, Let us flee\l"
    .string "from the face of Israel; for the LORD\l"
    .string "fighteth for them against the\l"
    .string "Egyptians$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_26::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Stretch out thine hand over the sea,\l"
    .string "that the waters may come again upon\l"
    .string "the Egyptians, upon their chariots,\l"
    .string "and upon their horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_27::
    .string "And Moses stretched forth his hand\n"
    .string "over the sea, and the sea returned to\l"
    .string "his strength when the morning\l"
    .string "appeared; and the Egyptians fled\l"
    .string "against it; and the LORD overthrew\l"
    .string "the Egyptians in the midst of the\l"
    .string "sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_28::
    .string "And the waters returned, and covered\n"
    .string "the chariots, and the horsemen, and\l"
    .string "all the host of Pharaoh that came\l"
    .string "into the sea after them; there\l"
    .string "remained not so much as one of them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_29::
    .string "But the children of Israel walked\n"
    .string "upon dry land in the midst of the\l"
    .string "sea; and the waters were a wall unto\l"
    .string "them on their right hand, and on\l"
    .string "their left.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_30::
    .string "Thus the LORD saved Israel that day\n"
    .string "out of the hand of the Egyptians; and\l"
    .string "Israel saw the Egyptians dead upon\l"
    .string "the sea shore.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_14_31::
    .string "And Israel saw that great work\n"
    .string "which the LORD did upon the\l"
    .string "Egyptians: and the people feared\l"
    .string "the LORD, and believed the LORD, and\l"
    .string "his servant Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_1::
    .string "Then sang Moses and the children of\n"
    .string "Israel this song unto the LORD, and\l"
    .string "spake, saying, I will sing unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, for he hath triumphed\l"
    .string "gloriously: the horse and his rider\l"
    .string "hath he thrown into the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_2::
    .string "The LORD is my strength and song,\n"
    .string "and he is become my salvation: he is\l"
    .string "my God, and I will prepare him an\l"
    .string "habitation; my father’s God, and I\l"
    .string "will exalt him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_3::
    .string "The LORD is a man of war: the LORD is\n"
    .string "his name.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_4::
    .string "Pharaoh’s chariots and his host\n"
    .string "hath he cast into the sea: his chosen\l"
    .string "captains also are drowned in the\l"
    .string "Red sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_5::
    .string "The depths have covered them: they\n"
    .string "sank into the bottom as a stone.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_6::
    .string "Thy right hand, O LORD, is become\n"
    .string "glorious in power: thy right hand, O\l"
    .string "LORD, hath dashed in pieces the\l"
    .string "enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_7::
    .string "And in the greatness of thine\n"
    .string "excellency thou hast overthrown\l"
    .string "them that rose up against thee: thou\l"
    .string "sentest forth thy wrath, which\l"
    .string "consumed them as stubble.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_8::
    .string "And with the blast of thy nostrils\n"
    .string "the waters were gathered together,\l"
    .string "the floods stood upright as an\l"
    .string "heap, and the depths were congealed\l"
    .string "in the heart of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_9::
    .string "The enemy said, I will pursue, I\n"
    .string "will overtake, I will divide the\l"
    .string "spoil; my lust shall be satisfied\l"
    .string "upon them; I will draw my sword, my\l"
    .string "hand shall destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_10::
    .string "Thou didst blow with thy wind, the\n"
    .string "sea covered them: they sank as lead\l"
    .string "in the mighty waters.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_11::
    .string "Who is like unto thee, O LORD, among\n"
    .string "the gods? who is like thee, glorious\l"
    .string "in holiness, fearful in praises,\l"
    .string "doing wonders?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_12::
    .string "Thou stretchedst out thy right hand,\n"
    .string "the earth swallowed them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_13::
    .string "Thou in thy mercy hast led forth\n"
    .string "the people which thou hast\l"
    .string "redeemed: thou hast guided them in\l"
    .string "thy strength unto thy holy\l"
    .string "habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_14::
    .string "The people shall hear, and be\n"
    .string "afraid: sorrow shall take hold on\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Palestina.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_15::
    .string "Then the dukes of Edom shall be\n"
    .string "amazed; the mighty men of Moab,\l"
    .string "trembling shall take hold upon\l"
    .string "them; all the inhabitants of Canaan\l"
    .string "shall melt away.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_16::
    .string "Fear and dread shall fall upon\n"
    .string "them; by the greatness of thine arm\l"
    .string "they shall be as still as a stone;\l"
    .string "till thy people pass over, O\l"
    .string "LORD, till the people pass over,\l"
    .string "which thou hast purchased.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_17::
    .string "Thou shalt bring them in, and\n"
    .string "plant them in the mountain of thine\l"
    .string "inheritance, in the place, O LORD,\l"
    .string "which thou hast made for thee to\l"
    .string "dwell in, in the Sanctuary, O LORD,\l"
    .string "which thy hands have established.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_18::
    .string "The LORD shall reign for ever and\n"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_19::
    .string "For the horse of Pharaoh went in\n"
    .string "with his chariots and with his\l"
    .string "horsemen into the sea, and the LORD\l"
    .string "brought again the waters of the sea\l"
    .string "upon them; but the children of\l"
    .string "Israel went on dry land in the midst\l"
    .string "of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_20::
    .string "And Miriam the prophetess, the\n"
    .string "sister of Aaron, took a timbrel in\l"
    .string "her hand; and all the women went out\l"
    .string "after her with timbrels and with\l"
    .string "dances.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_21::
    .string "And Miriam answered them, Sing ye to\n"
    .string "the LORD, for he hath triumphed\l"
    .string "gloriously; the horse and his rider\l"
    .string "hath he thrown into the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_22::
    .string "So Moses brought Israel from the\n"
    .string "Red sea, and they went out into the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Shur; and they went\l"
    .string "three days in the wilderness, and\l"
    .string "found no water.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_23::
    .string "And when they came to Marah, they\n"
    .string "could not drink of the waters of\l"
    .string "Marah, for they were bitter:\l"
    .string "therefore the name of it was called\l"
    .string "Marah.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_24::
    .string "And the people murmured against\n"
    .string "Moses, saying, What shall we drink?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_25::
    .string "And he cried unto the LORD; and the\n"
    .string "LORD shewed him a tree, which when he\l"
    .string "had cast into the waters, the waters\l"
    .string "were made sweet: there he made for\l"
    .string "them a statute and an ordinance, and\l"
    .string "there he proved them,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_26::
    .string "And said, If thou wilt diligently\n"
    .string "hearken to the voice of the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God, and wilt do that which is right\l"
    .string "in his sight, and wilt give ear to\l"
    .string "his commandments, and keep all his\l"
    .string "statutes, I will put none of these\l"
    .string "diseases upon thee, which I have\l"
    .string "brought upon the Egyptians: for I am\l"
    .string "the LORD that healeth thee$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_15_27::
    .string "And they came to Elim, where were\n"
    .string "twelve wells of water, and\l"
    .string "threescore and ten palm trees: and\l"
    .string "they encamped there by the waters.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_1::
    .string "And they took their journey from\n"
    .string "Elim, and all the congregation of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel came unto\l"
    .string "the wilderness of Sin, which is\l"
    .string "between Elim and Sinai, on the\l"
    .string "fifteenth day of the second month\l"
    .string "after their departing out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_2::
    .string "And the whole congregation of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel murmured against\l"
    .string "Moses and Aaron in the wilderness:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_3::
    .string "And the children of Israel said\n"
    .string "unto them, Would to God we had died\l"
    .string "by the hand of the LORD in the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, when we sat by the flesh\l"
    .string "pots, and when we did eat bread to the\l"
    .string "full; for ye have brought us forth\l"
    .string "into this wilderness, to kill this\l"
    .string "whole assembly with hunger$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_4::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Behold, I will rain bread from\l"
    .string "heaven for you; and the people\l"
    .string "shall go out and gather a certain\l"
    .string "rate every day, that I may prove\l"
    .string "them, whether they will walk in my\l"
    .string "law, or no.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_5::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that on\n"
    .string "the sixth day they shall prepare\l"
    .string "that which they bring in; and it\l"
    .string "shall be twice as much as they\l"
    .string "gather daily.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_6::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron said unto all\n"
    .string "the children of Israel, At even,\l"
    .string "then ye shall know that the LORD\l"
    .string "hath brought you out from the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_7::
    .string "And in the morning, then ye shall\n"
    .string "see the glory of the LORD; for that\l"
    .string "he heareth your murmurings against\l"
    .string "the LORD: and what are we, that ye\l"
    .string "murmur against us?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_8::
    .string "And Moses said, This shall be, when\n"
    .string "the LORD shall give you in the\l"
    .string "evening flesh to eat, and in the\l"
    .string "morning bread to the full; for that\l"
    .string "the LORD heareth your murmurings\l"
    .string "which ye murmur against him: and what\l"
    .string "are we? your murmurings are not\l"
    .string "against us, but against the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_9::
    .string "And Moses spake unto Aaron, Say\n"
    .string "unto all the congregation of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, Come near\l"
    .string "before the LORD: for he hath heard\l"
    .string "your murmurings.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, as Aaron spake\n"
    .string "unto the whole congregation of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, that they\l"
    .string "looked toward the wilderness, and,\l"
    .string "behold, the glory of the LORD\l"
    .string "appeared in the cloud.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_11::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_12::
    .string "I have heard the murmurings of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel: speak unto\l"
    .string "them, saying, At even ye shall eat\l"
    .string "flesh, and in the morning ye shall\l"
    .string "be filled with bread; and ye shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD your God$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, that at even\n"
    .string "the quails came up, and covered the\l"
    .string "camp: and in the morning the dew lay\l"
    .string "round about the host.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_14::
    .string "And when the dew that lay was gone\n"
    .string "up, behold, upon the face of the\l"
    .string "wilderness there lay a small round\l"
    .string "thing, as small as the hoar frost on\l"
    .string "the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_15::
    .string "And when the children of Israel\n"
    .string "saw it, they said one to another, It\l"
    .string "is manna: for they wist not what it\l"
    .string "was. And Moses said unto them, This\l"
    .string "is the bread which the LORD hath\l"
    .string "given you to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_16::
    .string "This is the thing which the LORD\n"
    .string "hath commanded, Gather of it every\l"
    .string "man according to his eating, an omer\l"
    .string "for every man, according to the\l"
    .string "number of your persons; take ye\l"
    .string "every man for them which are in his\l"
    .string "tents.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_17::
    .string "And the children of Israel did so,\n"
    .string "and gathered, some more, some less.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_18::
    .string "And when they did mete it with an\n"
    .string "omer, he that gathered much had\l"
    .string "nothing over, and he that gathered\l"
    .string "little had no lack; they gathered\l"
    .string "every man according to his eating.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_19::
    .string "And Moses said, Let no man leave of\n"
    .string "it till the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_20::
    .string "Notwithstanding they hearkened not\n"
    .string "unto Moses; but some of them left of\l"
    .string "it until the morning, and it bred\l"
    .string "worms, and stank: and Moses was wroth\l"
    .string "with them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_21::
    .string "And they gathered it every morning,\n"
    .string "every man according to his eating:\l"
    .string "and when the sun waxed hot, it\l"
    .string "melted.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_22::
    .string "And it came to pass, that on the\n"
    .string "sixth day they gathered twice as much\l"
    .string "bread, two omers for one man: and\l"
    .string "all the rulers of the congregation\l"
    .string "came and told Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_23::
    .string "And he said unto them, This is that\n"
    .string "which the LORD hath said, To morrow\l"
    .string "is the rest of the holy sabbath unto\l"
    .string "the LORD: bake that which ye will\l"
    .string "bake to day, and seethe that ye will\l"
    .string "seethe; and that which remaineth over\l"
    .string "lay up for you to be kept until the\l"
    .string "morning.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_24::
    .string "And they laid it up till the\n"
    .string "morning, as Moses bade: and it did\l"
    .string "not stink, neither was there any worm\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_25::
    .string "And Moses said, Eat that to day; for\n"
    .string "to day is a sabbath unto the LORD: to\l"
    .string "day ye shall not find it in the\l"
    .string "field.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_26::
    .string "Six days ye shall gather it; but on\n"
    .string "the seventh day, which is the\l"
    .string "sabbath, in it there shall be none.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_27::
    .string "And it came to pass, that there went\n"
    .string "out some of the people on the\l"
    .string "seventh day for to gather, and they\l"
    .string "found none.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_28::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, How\n"
    .string "long refuse ye to keep my\l"
    .string "commandments and my laws?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_29::
    .string "See, for that the LORD hath given\n"
    .string "you the sabbath, therefore he giveth\l"
    .string "you on the sixth day the bread of two\l"
    .string "days; abide ye every man in his\l"
    .string "place, let no man go out of his\l"
    .string "place on the seventh day$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_30::
    .string "So the people rested on the\n"
    .string "seventh day.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_31::
    .string "And the house of Israel called the\n"
    .string "name thereof Manna: and it was like\l"
    .string "coriander seed, white; and the taste\l"
    .string "of it was like wafers made with\l"
    .string "honey.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_32::
    .string "And Moses said, This is the thing\n"
    .string "which the LORD commandeth, Fill an\l"
    .string "omer of it to be kept for your\l"
    .string "generations; that they may see the\l"
    .string "bread wherewith I have fed you in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, when I brought you forth\l"
    .string "from the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_33::
    .string "And Moses said unto Aaron, Take a\n"
    .string "pot, and put an omer full of manna\l"
    .string "therein, and lay it up before the\l"
    .string "LORD, to be kept for your\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_34::
    .string "As the LORD commanded Moses, so\n"
    .string "Aaron laid it up before the\l"
    .string "Testimony, to be kept.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_35::
    .string "And the children of Israel did eat\n"
    .string "manna forty years, until they came\l"
    .string "to a land inhabited; they did eat\l"
    .string "manna, until they came unto the\l"
    .string "borders of the land of Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_16_36::
    .string "Now an omer is the tenth part of an\n"
    .string "ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_1::
    .string "And all the congregation of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel journeyed from\l"
    .string "the wilderness of Sin, after their\l"
    .string "journeys, according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD, and pitched\l"
    .string "in Rephidim: and there was no water\l"
    .string "for the people to drink.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_2::
    .string "Wherefore the people did chide\n"
    .string "with Moses, and said, Give us water\l"
    .string "that we may drink. And Moses said\l"
    .string "unto them, Why chide ye with me?\l"
    .string "wherefore do ye tempt the LORD?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_3::
    .string "And the people thirsted there for\n"
    .string "water; and the people murmured\l"
    .string "against Moses, and said, Wherefore is\l"
    .string "this that thou hast brought us up\l"
    .string "out of Egypt, to kill us and our\l"
    .string "children and our cattle with\l"
    .string "thirst?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_4::
    .string "And Moses cried unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying, What shall I do unto this\l"
    .string "people? they be almost ready to\l"
    .string "stone me$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_5::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Go on\n"
    .string "before the people, and take with\l"
    .string "thee of the elders of Israel; and\l"
    .string "thy rod, wherewith thou smotest the\l"
    .string "river, take in thine hand, and go.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_6::
    .string "Behold, I will stand before thee\n"
    .string "there upon the rock in Horeb; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt smite the rock, and there\l"
    .string "shall come water out of it, that the\l"
    .string "people may drink. And Moses did so\l"
    .string "in the sight of the elders of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_7::
    .string "And he called the name of the\n"
    .string "place Massah, and Meribah, because\l"
    .string "of the chiding of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and because they tempted\l"
    .string "the LORD, saying, Is the LORD among\l"
    .string "us, or not?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_8::
    .string "Then came Amalek, and fought with\n"
    .string "Israel in Rephidim$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_9::
    .string "And Moses said unto Joshua, Choose\n"
    .string "us out men, and go out, fight with\l"
    .string "Amalek: to morrow I will stand on\l"
    .string "the top of the hill with the rod of\l"
    .string "God in mine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_10::
    .string "So Joshua did as Moses had said to\n"
    .string "him, and fought with Amalek: and\l"
    .string "Moses, Aaron, and Hur went up to the\l"
    .string "top of the hill.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Moses\n"
    .string "held up his hand, that Israel\l"
    .string "prevailed: and when he let down his\l"
    .string "hand, Amalek prevailed.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_12::
    .string "But Moses’ hands were heavy; and\n"
    .string "they took a stone, and put it under\l"
    .string "him, and he sat thereon; and Aaron\l"
    .string "and Hur stayed up his hands, the one\l"
    .string "on the one side, and the other on the\l"
    .string "other side; and his hands were steady\l"
    .string "until the going down of the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_13::
    .string "And Joshua discomfited Amalek and\n"
    .string "his people with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_14::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Write\n"
    .string "this for a memorial in a book, and\l"
    .string "rehearse it in the ears of Joshua:\l"
    .string "for I will utterly put out the\l"
    .string "remembrance of Amalek from under\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_15::
    .string "And Moses built an altar, and\n"
    .string "called the name of it Jehovahnissi:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_17_16::
    .string "For he said, Because the LORD hath\n"
    .string "sworn that the LORD will have war\l"
    .string "with Amalek from generation to\l"
    .string "generation$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_1::
    .string "When Jethro, the priest of Midian,\n"
    .string "Moses’ father in law, heard of all\l"
    .string "that God had done for Moses, and for\l"
    .string "Israel his people, and that the\l"
    .string "LORD had brought Israel out of\l"
    .string "Egypt;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_2::
    .string "Then Jethro, Moses’ father in law,\n"
    .string "took Zipporah, Moses’ wife, after\l"
    .string "he had sent her back,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_3::
    .string "And her two sons; of which the name\n"
    .string "of the one was Gershom; for he said, I\l"
    .string "have been an alien in a strange\l"
    .string "land:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_4::
    .string "And the name of the other was\n"
    .string "Eliezer; for the God of my father,\l"
    .string "said he, was mine help, and\l"
    .string "delivered me from the sword of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_5::
    .string "And Jethro, Moses’ father in law,\n"
    .string "came with his sons and his wife unto\l"
    .string "Moses into the wilderness, where he\l"
    .string "encamped at the mount of God:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_6::
    .string "And he said unto Moses, I thy father\n"
    .string "in law Jethro am come unto thee, and\l"
    .string "thy wife, and her two sons with her$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_7::
    .string "And Moses went out to meet his\n"
    .string "father in law, and did obeisance,\l"
    .string "and kissed him; and they asked each\l"
    .string "other of their welfare; and they\l"
    .string "came into the tent.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_8::
    .string "And Moses told his father in law\n"
    .string "all that the LORD had done unto\l"
    .string "Pharaoh and to the Egyptians for\l"
    .string "Israel’s sake, and all the travail\l"
    .string "that had come upon them by the way,\l"
    .string "and how the LORD delivered them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_9::
    .string "And Jethro rejoiced for all the\n"
    .string "goodness which the LORD had done to\l"
    .string "Israel, whom he had delivered out of\l"
    .string "the hand of the Egyptians.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_10::
    .string "And Jethro said, Blessed be the\n"
    .string "LORD, who hath delivered you out of\l"
    .string "the hand of the Egyptians, and out of\l"
    .string "the hand of Pharaoh, who hath\l"
    .string "delivered the people from under\l"
    .string "the hand of the Egyptians.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_11::
    .string "Now I know that the LORD is greater\n"
    .string "than all gods: for in the thing\l"
    .string "wherein they dealt proudly he was\l"
    .string "above them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_12::
    .string "And Jethro, Moses’ father in law,\n"
    .string "took a burnt offering and sacrifices\l"
    .string "for God: and Aaron came, and all the\l"
    .string "elders of Israel, to eat bread with\l"
    .string "Moses’ father in law before God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_13::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that Moses sat to judge the people:\l"
    .string "and the people stood by Moses from\l"
    .string "the morning unto the evening.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_14::
    .string "And when Moses’ father in law saw\n"
    .string "all that he did to the people, he\l"
    .string "said, What is this thing that thou\l"
    .string "doest to the people? why sittest\l"
    .string "thou thyself alone, and all the\l"
    .string "people stand by thee from morning\l"
    .string "unto even?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_15::
    .string "And Moses said unto his father in\n"
    .string "law, Because the people come unto\l"
    .string "me to enquire of God:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_16::
    .string "When they have a matter, they come\n"
    .string "unto me; and I judge between one and\l"
    .string "another, and I do make them know the\l"
    .string "statutes of God, and his laws$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_17::
    .string "And Moses’ father in law said unto\n"
    .string "him, The thing that thou doest is not\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_18::
    .string "Thou wilt surely wear away, both\n"
    .string "thou, and this people that is with\l"
    .string "thee: for this thing is too heavy for\l"
    .string "thee; thou art not able to perform\l"
    .string "it thyself alone.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_19::
    .string "Hearken now unto my voice, I will\n"
    .string "give thee counsel, and God shall be\l"
    .string "with thee: Be thou for the people\l"
    .string "to God-ward, that thou mayest bring\l"
    .string "the causes unto God:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_20::
    .string "And thou shalt teach them\n"
    .string "ordinances and laws, and shalt shew\l"
    .string "them the way wherein they must walk,\l"
    .string "and the work that they must do$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_21::
    .string "Moreover thou shalt provide out of\n"
    .string "all the people able men, such as\l"
    .string "fear God, men of truth, hating\l"
    .string "covetousness; and place such over\l"
    .string "them, to be rulers of thousands, and\l"
    .string "rulers of hundreds, rulers of\l"
    .string "fifties, and rulers of tens:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_22::
    .string "And let them judge the people at\n"
    .string "all seasons: and it shall be, that\l"
    .string "every great matter they shall bring\l"
    .string "unto thee, but every small matter\l"
    .string "they shall judge: so shall it be\l"
    .string "easier for thyself, and they shall\l"
    .string "bear the burden with thee$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_23::
    .string "If thou shalt do this thing, and God\n"
    .string "command thee so, then thou shalt be\l"
    .string "able to endure, and all this\l"
    .string "people shall also go to their\l"
    .string "place in peace.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_24::
    .string "So Moses hearkened to the voice of\n"
    .string "his father in law, and did all that\l"
    .string "he had said.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_25::
    .string "And Moses chose able men out of\n"
    .string "all Israel, and made them heads\l"
    .string "over the people, rulers of\l"
    .string "thousands, rulers of hundreds,\l"
    .string "rulers of fifties, and rulers of\l"
    .string "tens.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_26::
    .string "And they judged the people at\n"
    .string "all seasons: the hard causes they\l"
    .string "brought unto Moses, but every small\l"
    .string "matter they judged themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_18_27::
    .string "And Moses let his father in law\n"
    .string "depart; and he went his way into his\l"
    .string "own land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_1::
    .string "In the third month, when the\n"
    .string "children of Israel were gone forth\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt, the same\l"
    .string "day came they into the wilderness of\l"
    .string "Sinai.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_2::
    .string "For they were departed from\n"
    .string "Rephidim, and were come to the\l"
    .string "desert of Sinai, and had pitched in\l"
    .string "the wilderness; and there Israel\l"
    .string "camped before the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_3::
    .string "And Moses went up unto God, and the\n"
    .string "LORD called unto him out of the\l"
    .string "mountain, saying, Thus shalt thou\l"
    .string "say to the house of Jacob, and tell\l"
    .string "the children of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_4::
    .string "Ye have seen what I did unto the\n"
    .string "Egyptians, and how I bare you on\l"
    .string "eagles’ wings, and brought you unto\l"
    .string "myself$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_5::
    .string "Now therefore, if ye will obey my\n"
    .string "voice indeed, and keep my covenant,\l"
    .string "then ye shall be a peculiar\l"
    .string "treasure unto me above all\l"
    .string "people: for all the earth is mine:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_6::
    .string "And ye shall be unto me a kingdom\n"
    .string "of priests, and an holy nation These\l"
    .string "are the words which thou shalt\l"
    .string "speak unto the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_7::
    .string "And Moses came and called for the\n"
    .string "elders of the people, and laid\l"
    .string "before their faces all these words\l"
    .string "which the LORD commanded him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_8::
    .string "And all the people answered\n"
    .string "together, and said, All that the\l"
    .string "LORD hath spoken we will do. And\l"
    .string "Moses returned the words of the\l"
    .string "people unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Lo, I\n"
    .string "come unto thee in a thick cloud, that\l"
    .string "the people may hear when I speak\l"
    .string "with thee, and believe thee for\l"
    .string "ever. And Moses told the words of the\l"
    .string "people unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_10::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Go\n"
    .string "unto the people, and sanctify them\l"
    .string "to day and to morrow, and let them\l"
    .string "wash their clothes,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_11::
    .string "And be ready against the third day:\n"
    .string "for the third day the LORD will come\l"
    .string "down in the sight of all the\l"
    .string "people upon mount Sinai$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_12::
    .string "And thou shalt set bounds unto the\n"
    .string "people round about, saying, Take\l"
    .string "heed to yourselves, that ye go not\l"
    .string "up into the mount, or touch the\l"
    .string "border of it: whosoever toucheth the\l"
    .string "mount shall be surely put to\l"
    .string "death:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_13::
    .string "There shall not an hand touch it,\n"
    .string "but he shall surely be stoned, or\l"
    .string "shot through; whether it be beast or\l"
    .string "man, it shall not live: when the\l"
    .string "trumpet soundeth long, they shall\l"
    .string "come up to the mount$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_14::
    .string "And Moses went down from the mount\n"
    .string "unto the people, and sanctified the\l"
    .string "people; and they washed their\l"
    .string "clothes.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_15::
    .string "And he said unto the people, Be\n"
    .string "ready against the third day: come not\l"
    .string "at your wives.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_16::
    .string "And it came to pass on the third day\n"
    .string "in the morning, that there were\l"
    .string "thunders and lightnings, and a thick\l"
    .string "cloud upon the mount, and the voice\l"
    .string "of the trumpet exceeding loud; so\l"
    .string "that all the people that was in\l"
    .string "the camp trembled.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_17::
    .string "And Moses brought forth the\n"
    .string "people out of the camp to meet with\l"
    .string "God; and they stood at the nether\l"
    .string "part of the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_18::
    .string "And mount Sinai was altogether on a\n"
    .string "smoke, because the LORD descended\l"
    .string "upon it in fire: and the smoke\l"
    .string "thereof ascended as the smoke of a\l"
    .string "furnace, and the whole mount quaked\l"
    .string "greatly.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_19::
    .string "And when the voice of the trumpet\n"
    .string "sounded long, and waxed louder and\l"
    .string "louder, Moses spake, and God\l"
    .string "answered him by a voice.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_20::
    .string "And the LORD came down upon mount\n"
    .string "Sinai, on the top of the mount: and\l"
    .string "the LORD called Moses up to the\l"
    .string "top of the mount; and Moses went up.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_21::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Go\n"
    .string "down, charge the people, lest they\l"
    .string "break through unto the LORD to gaze,\l"
    .string "and many of them perish.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_22::
    .string "And let the priests also, which\n"
    .string "come near to the LORD, sanctify\l"
    .string "themselves, lest the LORD break\l"
    .string "forth upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_23::
    .string "And Moses said unto the LORD, The\n"
    .string "people cannot come up to mount\l"
    .string "Sinai: for thou chargedst us, saying,\l"
    .string "Set bounds about the mount, and\l"
    .string "sanctify it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_24::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Away,\n"
    .string "get thee down, and thou shalt come\l"
    .string "up, thou, and Aaron with thee: but\l"
    .string "let not the priests and the people\l"
    .string "break through to come up unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, lest he break forth upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_19_25::
    .string "So Moses went down unto the\n"
    .string "people, and spake unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_1::
    .string "And God spake all these words,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_2::
    .string "I am the LORD thy God, which have\n"
    .string "brought thee out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, out of the house of bondage$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_3::
    .string "Thou shalt have no other gods\n"
    .string "before me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_4::
    .string "Thou shalt not make unto thee any\n"
    .string "graven image, or any likeness of any\l"
    .string "thing that is in heaven above, or\l"
    .string "that is in the earth beneath, or that\l"
    .string "is in the water under the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_5::
    .string "Thou shalt not bow down thyself to\n"
    .string "them, nor serve them: for I the LORD\l"
    .string "thy God am a jealous God, visiting\l"
    .string "the iniquity of the fathers upon the\l"
    .string "children unto the third and fourth\l"
    .string "generation of them that hate me;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_6::
    .string "And shewing mercy unto thousands of\n"
    .string "them that love me, and keep my\l"
    .string "commandments$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_7::
    .string "Thou shalt not take the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD thy God in vain; for the LORD\l"
    .string "will not hold him guiltless that\l"
    .string "taketh his name in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_8::
    .string "Remember the sabbath day, to keep\n"
    .string "it holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_9::
    .string "Six days shalt thou labour, and do\n"
    .string "all thy work:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_10::
    .string "But the seventh day is the sabbath\n"
    .string "of the LORD thy God: in it thou shalt\l"
    .string "not do any work, thou, nor thy son,\l"
    .string "nor thy daughter, thy manservant, nor\l"
    .string "thy maidservant, nor thy cattle, nor\l"
    .string "thy stranger that is within thy\l"
    .string "gates:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_11::
    .string "For in six days the LORD made heaven\n"
    .string "and earth, the sea, and all that in\l"
    .string "them is, and rested the seventh day:\l"
    .string "wherefore the LORD blessed the\l"
    .string "sabbath day, and hallowed it$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_12::
    .string "Honour thy father and thy mother:\n"
    .string "that thy days may be long upon the\l"
    .string "land which the LORD thy God giveth\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_13::
    .string "Thou shalt not kill.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_14::
    .string "Thou shalt not commit adultery.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_15::
    .string "Thou shalt not steal.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_16::
    .string "Thou shalt not bear false witness\n"
    .string "against thy neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_17::
    .string "Thou shalt not covet thy\n"
    .string "neighbour’s house, thou shalt not\l"
    .string "covet thy neighbour’s wife, nor his\l"
    .string "manservant, nor his maidservant, nor\l"
    .string "his ox, nor his ass, nor any thing\l"
    .string "that is thy neighbour’s.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_18::
    .string "And all the people saw the\n"
    .string "thunderings, and the lightnings, and\l"
    .string "the noise of the trumpet, and the\l"
    .string "mountain smoking: and when the\l"
    .string "people saw it, they removed, and\l"
    .string "stood afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_19::
    .string "And they said unto Moses, Speak\n"
    .string "thou with us, and we will hear: but\l"
    .string "let not God speak with us, lest we\l"
    .string "die.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_20::
    .string "And Moses said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Fear not: for God is come to prove\l"
    .string "you, and that his fear may be before\l"
    .string "your faces, that ye sin not.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_21::
    .string "And the people stood afar off, and\n"
    .string "Moses drew near unto the thick\l"
    .string "darkness where God was.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_22::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Thus\n"
    .string "thou shalt say unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, Ye have seen that I have\l"
    .string "talked with you from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_23::
    .string "Ye shall not make with me gods of\n"
    .string "silver, neither shall ye make unto\l"
    .string "you gods of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_24::
    .string "An altar of earth thou shalt make\n"
    .string "unto me, and shalt sacrifice thereon\l"
    .string "thy burnt offerings, and thy peace\l"
    .string "offerings, thy sheep, and thine\l"
    .string "oxen: in all places where I record\l"
    .string "my name I will come unto thee, and I\l"
    .string "will bless thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_25::
    .string "And if thou wilt make me an altar\n"
    .string "of stone, thou shalt not build it of\l"
    .string "hewn stone: for if thou lift up thy\l"
    .string "tool upon it, thou hast polluted\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_20_26::
    .string "Neither shalt thou go up by steps\n"
    .string "unto mine altar, that thy nakedness\l"
    .string "be not discovered thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_1::
    .string "Now these are the judgments which\n"
    .string "thou shalt set before them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_2::
    .string "If thou buy an Hebrew servant, six\n"
    .string "years he shall serve: and in the\l"
    .string "seventh he shall go out free for\l"
    .string "nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_3::
    .string "If he came in by himself, he shall\n"
    .string "go out by himself: if he were\l"
    .string "married, then his wife shall go out\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_4::
    .string "If his master have given him a wife,\n"
    .string "and she have born him sons or\l"
    .string "daughters; the wife and her children\l"
    .string "shall be her master’s, and he\l"
    .string "shall go out by himself.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_5::
    .string "And if the servant shall plainly\n"
    .string "say, I love my master, my wife, and\l"
    .string "my children; I will not go out\l"
    .string "free:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_6::
    .string "Then his master shall bring him\n"
    .string "unto the judges; he shall also\l"
    .string "bring him to the door, or unto the\l"
    .string "door post; and his master shall\l"
    .string "bore his ear through with an aul; and\l"
    .string "he shall serve him for ever$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_7::
    .string "And if a man sell his daughter to\n"
    .string "be a maidservant, she shall not go\l"
    .string "out as the menservants do.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_8::
    .string "If she please not her master, who\n"
    .string "hath betrothed her to himself, then\l"
    .string "shall he let her be redeemed: to\l"
    .string "sell her unto a strange nation he\l"
    .string "shall have no power, seeing he hath\l"
    .string "dealt deceitfully with her.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_9::
    .string "And if he have betrothed her unto\n"
    .string "his son, he shall deal with her\l"
    .string "after the manner of daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_10::
    .string "If he take him another wife; her\n"
    .string "food, her raiment, and her duty of\l"
    .string "marriage, shall he not diminish.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_11::
    .string "And if he do not these three unto\n"
    .string "her, then shall she go out free\l"
    .string "without money.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_12::
    .string "He that smiteth a man, so that he\n"
    .string "die, shall be surely put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_13::
    .string "And if a man lie not in wait, but\n"
    .string "God deliver him into his hand; then I\l"
    .string "will appoint thee a place\l"
    .string "whither he shall flee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_14::
    .string "But if a man come presumptuously\n"
    .string "upon his neighbour, to slay him with\l"
    .string "guile; thou shalt take him from mine\l"
    .string "altar, that he may die.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_15::
    .string "And he that smiteth his father, or\n"
    .string "his mother, shall be surely put to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_16::
    .string "And he that stealeth a man, and\n"
    .string "selleth him, or if he be found in\l"
    .string "his hand, he shall surely be put to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_17::
    .string "And he that curseth his father, or\n"
    .string "his mother, shall surely be put to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_18::
    .string "And if men strive together, and one\n"
    .string "smite another with a stone, or with\l"
    .string "his fist, and he die not, but keepeth\l"
    .string "his bed:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_19::
    .string "If he rise again, and walk abroad\n"
    .string "upon his staff, then shall he that\l"
    .string "smote him be quit: only he shall\l"
    .string "pay for the loss of his time, and\l"
    .string "shall cause him to be thoroughly\l"
    .string "healed$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_20::
    .string "And if a man smite his servant, or\n"
    .string "his maid, with a rod, and he die under\l"
    .string "his hand; he shall be surely\l"
    .string "punished.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_21::
    .string "Notwithstanding, if he continue a\n"
    .string "day or two, he shall not be\l"
    .string "punished: for he is his money.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_22::
    .string "If men strive, and hurt a woman with\n"
    .string "child, so that her fruit depart from\l"
    .string "her, and yet no mischief follow: he\l"
    .string "shall be surely punished,\l"
    .string "according as the woman’s husband\l"
    .string "will lay upon him; and he shall\l"
    .string "pay as the judges determine.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_23::
    .string "And if any mischief follow, then\n"
    .string "thou shalt give life for life,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_24::
    .string "Eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand\n"
    .string "for hand, foot for foot,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_25::
    .string "Burning for burning, wound for\n"
    .string "wound, stripe for stripe$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_26::
    .string "And if a man smite the eye of his\n"
    .string "servant, or the eye of his maid, that\l"
    .string "it perish; he shall let him go free\l"
    .string "for his eye’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_27::
    .string "And if he smite out his manservant’s\n"
    .string "tooth, or his maidservant’s tooth; he\l"
    .string "shall let him go free for his\l"
    .string "tooth’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_28::
    .string "If an ox gore a man or a woman, that\n"
    .string "they die: then the ox shall be\l"
    .string "surely stoned, and his flesh shall\l"
    .string "not be eaten; but the owner of the ox\l"
    .string "shall be quit.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_29::
    .string "But if the ox were wont to push with\n"
    .string "his horn in time past, and it hath\l"
    .string "been testified to his owner, and he\l"
    .string "hath not kept him in, but that he\l"
    .string "hath killed a man or a woman; the ox\l"
    .string "shall be stoned, and his owner also\l"
    .string "shall be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_30::
    .string "If there be laid on him a sum of\n"
    .string "money, then he shall give for the\l"
    .string "ransom of his life whatsoever is\l"
    .string "laid upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_31::
    .string "Whether he have gored a son, or have\n"
    .string "gored a daughter, according to this\l"
    .string "judgment shall it be done unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_32::
    .string "If the ox shall push a manservant\n"
    .string "or a maidservant; he shall give unto\l"
    .string "their master thirty shekels of\l"
    .string "silver, and the ox shall be stoned.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_33::
    .string "And if a man shall open a pit, or\n"
    .string "if a man shall dig a pit, and not\l"
    .string "cover it, and an ox or an ass fall\l"
    .string "therein;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_34::
    .string "The owner of the pit shall make it\n"
    .string "good, and give money unto the owner\l"
    .string "of them; and the dead beast shall be\l"
    .string "his$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_35::
    .string "And if one man’s ox hurt another’s,\n"
    .string "that he die; then they shall sell\l"
    .string "the live ox, and divide the money of\l"
    .string "it; and the dead ox also they shall\l"
    .string "divide.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_21_36::
    .string "Or if it be known that the ox hath\n"
    .string "used to push in time past, and his\l"
    .string "owner hath not kept him in; he\l"
    .string "shall surely pay ox for ox; and the\l"
    .string "dead shall be his own.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_1::
    .string "If a man shall steal an ox, or a\n"
    .string "sheep, and kill it, or sell it; he\l"
    .string "shall restore five oxen for an ox,\l"
    .string "and four sheep for a sheep.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_2::
    .string "If a thief be found breaking up, and\n"
    .string "be smitten that he die, there shall\l"
    .string "no blood be shed for him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_3::
    .string "If the sun be risen upon him, there\n"
    .string "shall be blood shed for him; for he\l"
    .string "should make full restitution; if he\l"
    .string "have nothing, then he shall be sold\l"
    .string "for his theft.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_4::
    .string "If the theft be certainly found in\n"
    .string "his hand alive, whether it be ox, or\l"
    .string "ass, or sheep; he shall restore\l"
    .string "double.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_5::
    .string "If a man shall cause a field or\n"
    .string "vineyard to be eaten, and shall put\l"
    .string "in his beast, and shall feed in\l"
    .string "another man’s field; of the best of\l"
    .string "his own field, and of the best of his\l"
    .string "own vineyard, shall he make\l"
    .string "restitution.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_6::
    .string "If fire break out, and catch in\n"
    .string "thorns, so that the stacks of corn,\l"
    .string "or the standing corn, or the field,\l"
    .string "be consumed therewith; he that\l"
    .string "kindled the fire shall surely make\l"
    .string "restitution.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_7::
    .string "If a man shall deliver unto his\n"
    .string "neighbour money or stuff to keep,\l"
    .string "and it be stolen out of the man’s\l"
    .string "house; if the thief be found, let him\l"
    .string "pay double.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_8::
    .string "If the thief be not found, then the\n"
    .string "master of the house shall be\l"
    .string "brought unto the judges, to see\l"
    .string "whether he have put his hand unto\l"
    .string "his neighbour’s goods.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_9::
    .string "For all manner of trespass,\n"
    .string "whether it be for ox, for ass, for\l"
    .string "sheep, for raiment, or for any\l"
    .string "manner of lost thing which another\l"
    .string "challengeth to be his, the cause of\l"
    .string "both parties shall come before the\l"
    .string "judges; and whom the judges shall\l"
    .string "condemn, he shall pay double unto\l"
    .string "his neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_10::
    .string "If a man deliver unto his neighbour\n"
    .string "an ass, or an ox, or a sheep, or any\l"
    .string "beast, to keep; and it die, or be\l"
    .string "hurt, or driven away, no man seeing\l"
    .string "it:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_11::
    .string "Then shall an oath of the LORD be\n"
    .string "between them both, that he hath not\l"
    .string "put his hand unto his neighbour’s\l"
    .string "goods; and the owner of it shall\l"
    .string "accept thereof, and he shall not\l"
    .string "make it good$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_12::
    .string "And if it be stolen from him, he\n"
    .string "shall make restitution unto the\l"
    .string "owner thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_13::
    .string "If it be torn in pieces, then let\n"
    .string "him bring it for witness, and he\l"
    .string "shall not make good that which was\l"
    .string "torn.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_14::
    .string "And if a man borrow ought of his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and it be hurt, or die, the\l"
    .string "owner thereof being not with it, he\l"
    .string "shall surely make it good.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_15::
    .string "But if the owner thereof be with it,\n"
    .string "he shall not make it good: if it be\l"
    .string "an hired thing, it came for his hire.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_16::
    .string "And if a man entice a maid that is\n"
    .string "not betrothed, and lie with her, he\l"
    .string "shall surely endow her to be his\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_17::
    .string "If her father utterly refuse to\n"
    .string "give her unto him, he shall pay\l"
    .string "money according to the dowry of\l"
    .string "virgins.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_18::
    .string "Thou shalt not suffer a witch to\n"
    .string "live.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_19::
    .string "Whosoever lieth with a beast\n"
    .string "shall surely be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_20::
    .string "He that sacrificeth unto any god,\n"
    .string "save unto the LORD only, he shall\l"
    .string "be utterly destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_21::
    .string "Thou shalt neither vex a stranger,\n"
    .string "nor oppress him: for ye were\l"
    .string "strangers in the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_22::
    .string "Ye shall not afflict any widow, or\n"
    .string "fatherless child.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_23::
    .string "If thou afflict them in any wise,\n"
    .string "and they cry at all unto me, I will\l"
    .string "surely hear their cry;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_24::
    .string "And my wrath shall wax hot, and I\n"
    .string "will kill you with the sword; and\l"
    .string "your wives shall be widows, and your\l"
    .string "children fatherless$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_25::
    .string "If thou lend money to any of my\n"
    .string "people that is poor by thee, thou\l"
    .string "shalt not be to him as an usurer,\l"
    .string "neither shalt thou lay upon him\l"
    .string "usury.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_26::
    .string "If thou at all take thy\n"
    .string "neighbour’s raiment to pledge, thou\l"
    .string "shalt deliver it unto him by that\l"
    .string "the sun goeth down:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_27::
    .string "For that is his covering only, it is\n"
    .string "his raiment for his skin: wherein\l"
    .string "shall he sleep? and it shall come\l"
    .string "to pass, when he crieth unto me, that\l"
    .string "I will hear; for I am gracious$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_28::
    .string "Thou shalt not revile the gods, nor\n"
    .string "curse the ruler of thy people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_29::
    .string "Thou shalt not delay to offer the\n"
    .string "first of thy ripe fruits, and of thy\l"
    .string "liquors: the firstborn of thy sons\l"
    .string "shalt thou give unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_30::
    .string "Likewise shalt thou do with thine\n"
    .string "oxen, and with thy sheep: seven days\l"
    .string "it shall be with his dam; on the\l"
    .string "eighth day thou shalt give it me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_22_31::
    .string "And ye shall be holy men unto me:\n"
    .string "neither shall ye eat any flesh that\l"
    .string "is torn of beasts in the field; ye\l"
    .string "shall cast it to the dogs.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_1::
    .string "Thou shalt not raise a false\n"
    .string "report: put not thine hand with the\l"
    .string "wicked to be an unrighteous witness.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_2::
    .string "Thou shalt not follow a multitude\n"
    .string "to do evil; neither shalt thou\l"
    .string "speak in a cause to decline after\l"
    .string "many to wrest judgment:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_3::
    .string "Neither shalt thou countenance a\n"
    .string "poor man in his cause$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_4::
    .string "If thou meet thine enemy’s ox or his\n"
    .string "ass going astray, thou shalt surely\l"
    .string "bring it back to him again.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_5::
    .string "If thou see the ass of him that\n"
    .string "hateth thee lying under his burden,\l"
    .string "and wouldest forbear to help him,\l"
    .string "thou shalt surely help with him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_6::
    .string "Thou shalt not wrest the judgment\n"
    .string "of thy poor in his cause.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_7::
    .string "Keep thee far from a false matter;\n"
    .string "and the innocent and righteous slay\l"
    .string "thou not: for I will not justify the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_8::
    .string "And thou shalt take no gift: for the\n"
    .string "gift blindeth the wise, and\l"
    .string "perverteth the words of the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_9::
    .string "Also thou shalt not oppress a\n"
    .string "stranger: for ye know the heart of a\l"
    .string "stranger, seeing ye were strangers in\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_10::
    .string "And six years thou shalt sow thy\n"
    .string "land, and shalt gather in the fruits\l"
    .string "thereof:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_11::
    .string "But the seventh year thou shalt\n"
    .string "let it rest and lie still; that the\l"
    .string "poor of thy people may eat: and\l"
    .string "what they leave the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field shall eat. In like manner\l"
    .string "thou shalt deal with thy vineyard,\l"
    .string "and with thy oliveyard$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_12::
    .string "Six days thou shalt do thy work, and\n"
    .string "on the seventh day thou shalt rest:\l"
    .string "that thine ox and thine ass may rest,\l"
    .string "and the son of thy handmaid, and the\l"
    .string "stranger, may be refreshed.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_13::
    .string "And in all things that I have said\n"
    .string "unto you be circumspect: and make no\l"
    .string "mention of the name of other gods,\l"
    .string "neither let it be heard out of thy\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_14::
    .string "Three times thou shalt keep a\n"
    .string "feast unto me in the year.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_15::
    .string "Thou shalt keep the feast of\n"
    .string "unleavened bread: (thou shalt eat\l"
    .string "unleavened bread seven days, as I\l"
    .string "commanded thee, in the time\l"
    .string "appointed of the month Abib; for in\l"
    .string "it thou camest out from Egypt: and\l"
    .string "none shall appear before me\l"
    .string "empty:)"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_16::
    .string "And the feast of harvest, the\n"
    .string "firstfruits of thy labours, which\l"
    .string "thou hast sown in the field: and the\l"
    .string "feast of ingathering, which is in the\l"
    .string "end of the year, when thou hast\l"
    .string "gathered in thy labours out of the\l"
    .string "field$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_17::
    .string "Three times in the year all thy\n"
    .string "males shall appear before the\l"
    .string "LORD God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_18::
    .string "Thou shalt not offer the blood of\n"
    .string "my sacrifice with leavened bread;\l"
    .string "neither shall the fat of my\l"
    .string "sacrifice remain until the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_19::
    .string "The first of the firstfruits of thy\n"
    .string "land thou shalt bring into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not\l"
    .string "seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_20::
    .string "Behold, I send an Angel before\n"
    .string "thee, to keep thee in the way, and to\l"
    .string "bring thee into the place which I\l"
    .string "have prepared.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_21::
    .string "Beware of him, and obey his voice,\n"
    .string "provoke him not; for he will not\l"
    .string "pardon your transgressions: for my\l"
    .string "name is in him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_22::
    .string "But if thou shalt indeed obey his\n"
    .string "voice, and do all that I speak;\l"
    .string "then I will be an enemy unto thine\l"
    .string "enemies, and an adversary unto thine\l"
    .string "adversaries.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_23::
    .string "For mine Angel shall go before\n"
    .string "thee, and bring thee in unto the\l"
    .string "Amorites, and the Hittites, and the\l"
    .string "Perizzites, and the Canaanites, the\l"
    .string "Hivites, and the Jebusites: and I\l"
    .string "will cut them off.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_24::
    .string "Thou shalt not bow down to their\n"
    .string "gods, nor serve them, nor do after\l"
    .string "their works: but thou shalt utterly\l"
    .string "overthrow them, and quite break down\l"
    .string "their images.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_25::
    .string "And ye shall serve the LORD your\n"
    .string "God, and he shall bless thy bread,\l"
    .string "and thy water; and I will take\l"
    .string "sickness away from the midst of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_26::
    .string "There shall nothing cast their\n"
    .string "young, nor be barren, in thy land:\l"
    .string "the number of thy days I will\l"
    .string "fulfil.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_27::
    .string "I will send my fear before thee,\n"
    .string "and will destroy all the people\l"
    .string "to whom thou shalt come, and I will\l"
    .string "make all thine enemies turn their\l"
    .string "backs unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_28::
    .string "And I will send hornets before\n"
    .string "thee, which shall drive out the\l"
    .string "Hivite, the Canaanite, and the\l"
    .string "Hittite, from before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_29::
    .string "I will not drive them out from\n"
    .string "before thee in one year; lest the\l"
    .string "land become desolate, and the beast\l"
    .string "of the field multiply against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_30::
    .string "By little and little I will\n"
    .string "drive them out from before thee,\l"
    .string "until thou be increased, and inherit\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_31::
    .string "And I will set thy bounds from the\n"
    .string "Red sea even unto the sea of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and from the desert\l"
    .string "unto the river: for I will deliver\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of the land into\l"
    .string "your hand; and thou shalt drive them\l"
    .string "out before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_32::
    .string "Thou shalt make no covenant with\n"
    .string "them, nor with their gods.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_23_33::
    .string "They shall not dwell in thy land,\n"
    .string "lest they make thee sin against me:\l"
    .string "for if thou serve their gods, it\l"
    .string "will surely be a snare unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_1::
    .string "And he said unto Moses, Come up unto\n"
    .string "the LORD, thou, and Aaron, Nadab, and\l"
    .string "Abihu, and seventy of the elders of\l"
    .string "Israel; and worship ye afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_2::
    .string "And Moses alone shall come near\n"
    .string "the LORD: but they shall not come\l"
    .string "nigh; neither shall the people go\l"
    .string "up with him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_3::
    .string "And Moses came and told the\n"
    .string "people all the words of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and all the judgments: and all the\l"
    .string "people answered with one voice, and\l"
    .string "said, All the words which the LORD\l"
    .string "hath said will we do.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_4::
    .string "And Moses wrote all the words of\n"
    .string "the LORD, and rose up early in the\l"
    .string "morning, and builded an altar under\l"
    .string "the hill, and twelve pillars,\l"
    .string "according to the twelve tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_5::
    .string "And he sent young men of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, which offered\l"
    .string "burnt offerings, and sacrificed\l"
    .string "peace offerings of oxen unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_6::
    .string "And Moses took half of the blood,\n"
    .string "and put it in basons; and half of\l"
    .string "the blood he sprinkled on the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_7::
    .string "And he took the book of the\n"
    .string "covenant, and read in the audience of\l"
    .string "the people: and they said, All\l"
    .string "that the LORD hath said will we do,\l"
    .string "and be obedient.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_8::
    .string "And Moses took the blood, and\n"
    .string "sprinkled it on the people, and\l"
    .string "said, Behold the blood of the\l"
    .string "covenant, which the LORD hath made\l"
    .string "with you concerning all these words.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_9::
    .string "Then went up Moses, and Aaron,\n"
    .string "Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the\l"
    .string "elders of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_10::
    .string "And they saw the God of Israel: and\n"
    .string "there was under his feet as it were a\l"
    .string "paved work of a sapphire stone, and\l"
    .string "as it were the body of heaven in his\l"
    .string "clearness$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_11::
    .string "And upon the nobles of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel he laid not his\l"
    .string "hand: also they saw God, and did eat\l"
    .string "and drink.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_12::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Come\n"
    .string "up to me into the mount, and be\l"
    .string "there: and I will give thee tables\l"
    .string "of stone, and a law, and\l"
    .string "commandments which I have written;\l"
    .string "that thou mayest teach them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_13::
    .string "And Moses rose up, and his minister\n"
    .string "Joshua: and Moses went up into the\l"
    .string "mount of God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_14::
    .string "And he said unto the elders, Tarry\n"
    .string "ye here for us, until we come again\l"
    .string "unto you: and, behold, Aaron and Hur\l"
    .string "are with you: if any man have any\l"
    .string "matters to do, let him come unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_15::
    .string "And Moses went up into the mount,\n"
    .string "and a cloud covered the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_16::
    .string "And the glory of the LORD abode\n"
    .string "upon mount Sinai, and the cloud\l"
    .string "covered it six days: and the seventh\l"
    .string "day he called unto Moses out of the\l"
    .string "midst of the cloud.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_17::
    .string "And the sight of the glory of the\n"
    .string "LORD was like devouring fire on the\l"
    .string "top of the mount in the eyes of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_24_18::
    .string "And Moses went into the midst of the\n"
    .string "cloud, and gat him up into the\l"
    .string "mount: and Moses was in the mount\l"
    .string "forty days and forty nights.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "that they bring me an offering: of\l"
    .string "every man that giveth it willingly\l"
    .string "with his heart ye shall take my\l"
    .string "offering$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_3::
    .string "And this is the offering which ye\n"
    .string "shall take of them; gold, and\l"
    .string "silver, and brass,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_4::
    .string "And blue, and purple, and\n"
    .string "scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’\l"
    .string "hair,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_5::
    .string "And rams’ skins dyed red, and\n"
    .string "badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_6::
    .string "Oil for the light, spices for\n"
    .string "anointing oil, and for sweet\l"
    .string "incense,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_7::
    .string "Onyx stones, and stones to be set in\n"
    .string "the ephod, and in the breastplate$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_8::
    .string "And let them make me a sanctuary;\n"
    .string "that I may dwell among them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_9::
    .string "According to all that I shew thee,\n"
    .string "after the pattern of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and the pattern of all\l"
    .string "the instruments thereof, even so\l"
    .string "shall ye make it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_10::
    .string "And they shall make an ark of\n"
    .string "shittim wood: two cubits and a half\l"
    .string "shall be the length thereof, and a\l"
    .string "cubit and a half the breadth\l"
    .string "thereof, and a cubit and a half the\l"
    .string "height thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_11::
    .string "And thou shalt overlay it with\n"
    .string "pure gold, within and without shalt\l"
    .string "thou overlay it, and shalt make\l"
    .string "upon it a crown of gold round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_12::
    .string "And thou shalt cast four rings of\n"
    .string "gold for it, and put them in the\l"
    .string "four corners thereof; and two rings\l"
    .string "shall be in the one side of it, and\l"
    .string "two rings in the other side of it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_13::
    .string "And thou shalt make staves of\n"
    .string "shittim wood, and overlay them with\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_14::
    .string "And thou shalt put the staves into\n"
    .string "the rings by the sides of the ark,\l"
    .string "that the ark may be borne with them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_15::
    .string "The staves shall be in the rings of\n"
    .string "the ark: they shall not be taken\l"
    .string "from it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_16::
    .string "And thou shalt put into the ark the\n"
    .string "testimony which I shall give thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_17::
    .string "And thou shalt make a mercy seat of\n"
    .string "pure gold: two cubits and a half\l"
    .string "shall be the length thereof, and a\l"
    .string "cubit and a half the breadth thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_18::
    .string "And thou shalt make two cherubims\n"
    .string "of gold, of beaten work shalt thou\l"
    .string "make them, in the two ends of the\l"
    .string "mercy seat.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_19::
    .string "And make one cherub on the one end,\n"
    .string "and the other cherub on the other\l"
    .string "end: even of the mercy seat shall ye\l"
    .string "make the cherubims on the two ends\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_20::
    .string "And the cherubims shall stretch\n"
    .string "forth their wings on high, covering\l"
    .string "the mercy seat with their wings, and\l"
    .string "their faces shall look one to\l"
    .string "another; toward the mercy seat\l"
    .string "shall the faces of the cherubims be.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_21::
    .string "And thou shalt put the mercy seat\n"
    .string "above upon the ark; and in the ark\l"
    .string "thou shalt put the testimony that I\l"
    .string "shall give thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_22::
    .string "And there I will meet with thee,\n"
    .string "and I will commune with thee from\l"
    .string "above the mercy seat, from between\l"
    .string "the two cherubims which are upon the\l"
    .string "ark of the testimony, of all things\l"
    .string "which I will give thee in\l"
    .string "commandment unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_23::
    .string "Thou shalt also make a table of\n"
    .string "shittim wood: two cubits shall be\l"
    .string "the length thereof, and a cubit the\l"
    .string "breadth thereof, and a cubit and a\l"
    .string "half the height thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_24::
    .string "And thou shalt overlay it with\n"
    .string "pure gold, and make thereto a crown\l"
    .string "of gold round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_25::
    .string "And thou shalt make unto it a\n"
    .string "border of an hand breadth round\l"
    .string "about, and thou shalt make a golden\l"
    .string "crown to the border thereof round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_26::
    .string "And thou shalt make for it four\n"
    .string "rings of gold, and put the rings in\l"
    .string "the four corners that are on the four\l"
    .string "feet thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_27::
    .string "Over against the border shall the\n"
    .string "rings be for places of the staves to\l"
    .string "bear the table.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_28::
    .string "And thou shalt make the staves of\n"
    .string "shittim wood, and overlay them with\l"
    .string "gold, that the table may be borne\l"
    .string "with them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_29::
    .string "And thou shalt make the dishes\n"
    .string "thereof, and spoons thereof, and\l"
    .string "covers thereof, and bowls thereof,\l"
    .string "to cover withal: of pure gold\l"
    .string "shalt thou make them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_30::
    .string "And thou shalt set upon the table\n"
    .string "shewbread before me alway.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_31::
    .string "And thou shalt make a candlestick\n"
    .string "of pure gold: of beaten work shall\l"
    .string "the candlestick be made: his shaft,\l"
    .string "and his branches, his bowls, his\l"
    .string "knops, and his flowers, shall be\l"
    .string "of the same.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_32::
    .string "And six branches shall come out of\n"
    .string "the sides of it; three branches of\l"
    .string "the candlestick out of the one side,\l"
    .string "and three branches of the\l"
    .string "candlestick out of the other side:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_33::
    .string "Three bowls made like unto\n"
    .string "almonds, with a knop and a flower\l"
    .string "in one branch; and three bowls made\l"
    .string "like almonds in the other branch,\l"
    .string "with a knop and a flower: so in the\l"
    .string "six branches that come out of the\l"
    .string "candlestick$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_34::
    .string "And in the candlesticks shall be\n"
    .string "four bowls made like unto almonds,\l"
    .string "with their knops and their flowers.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_35::
    .string "And there shall be a knop under\n"
    .string "two branches of the same, and a knop\l"
    .string "under two branches of the same, and a\l"
    .string "knop under two branches of the same,\l"
    .string "according to the six branches that\l"
    .string "proceed out of the candlestick.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_36::
    .string "Their knops and their branches\n"
    .string "shall be of the same: all it\l"
    .string "shall be one beaten work of pure\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_37::
    .string "And thou shalt make the seven\n"
    .string "lamps thereof: and they shall\l"
    .string "light the lamps thereof, that they\l"
    .string "may give light over against it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_38::
    .string "And the tongs thereof, and the\n"
    .string "snuffdishes thereof, shall be of\l"
    .string "pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_39::
    .string "Of a talent of pure gold shall he\n"
    .string "make it, with all these vessels.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_25_40::
    .string "And look that thou make them after\n"
    .string "their pattern, which was shewed thee\l"
    .string "in the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_1::
    .string "Moreover thou shalt make the\n"
    .string "tabernacle with ten curtains of fine\l"
    .string "twined linen, and blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet: with\l"
    .string "cherubims of cunning work shalt thou\l"
    .string "make them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_2::
    .string "The length of one curtain shall be\n"
    .string "eight and twenty cubits, and the\l"
    .string "breadth of one curtain four cubits:\l"
    .string "and every one of the curtains shall\l"
    .string "have one measure.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_3::
    .string "The five curtains shall be\n"
    .string "coupled together one to another;\l"
    .string "and other five curtains shall be\l"
    .string "coupled one to another.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_4::
    .string "And thou shalt make loops of blue\n"
    .string "upon the edge of the one curtain\l"
    .string "from the selvedge in the coupling;\l"
    .string "and likewise shalt thou make in the\l"
    .string "uttermost edge of another curtain, in\l"
    .string "the coupling of the second.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_5::
    .string "Fifty loops shalt thou make in the\n"
    .string "one curtain, and fifty loops shalt\l"
    .string "thou make in the edge of the curtain\l"
    .string "that is in the coupling of the\l"
    .string "second; that the loops may take\l"
    .string "hold one of another.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_6::
    .string "And thou shalt make fifty taches of\n"
    .string "gold, and couple the curtains\l"
    .string "together with the taches: and it\l"
    .string "shall be one tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_7::
    .string "And thou shalt make curtains of\n"
    .string "goats’ hair to be a covering upon\l"
    .string "the tabernacle: eleven curtains\l"
    .string "shalt thou make.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_8::
    .string "The length of one curtain shall be\n"
    .string "thirty cubits, and the breadth of one\l"
    .string "curtain four cubits: and the eleven\l"
    .string "curtains shall be all of one\l"
    .string "measure.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_9::
    .string "And thou shalt couple five\n"
    .string "curtains by themselves, and six\l"
    .string "curtains by themselves, and shalt\l"
    .string "double the sixth curtain in the\l"
    .string "forefront of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_10::
    .string "And thou shalt make fifty loops on\n"
    .string "the edge of the one curtain that is\l"
    .string "outmost in the coupling, and fifty\l"
    .string "loops in the edge of the curtain\l"
    .string "which coupleth the second.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_11::
    .string "And thou shalt make fifty taches of\n"
    .string "brass, and put the taches into the\l"
    .string "loops, and couple the tent\l"
    .string "together, that it may be one.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_12::
    .string "And the remnant that remaineth of\n"
    .string "the curtains of the tent, the half\l"
    .string "curtain that remaineth, shall hang\l"
    .string "over the backside of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_13::
    .string "And a cubit on the one side, and a\n"
    .string "cubit on the other side of that which\l"
    .string "remaineth in the length of the\l"
    .string "curtains of the tent, it shall hang\l"
    .string "over the sides of the tabernacle on\l"
    .string "this side and on that side, to cover\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_14::
    .string "And thou shalt make a covering for\n"
    .string "the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and\l"
    .string "a covering above of badgers’ skins.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_15::
    .string "And thou shalt make boards for the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of shittim wood standing\l"
    .string "up.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_16::
    .string "Ten cubits shall be the length of\n"
    .string "a board, and a cubit and a half\l"
    .string "shall be the breadth of one board.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_17::
    .string "Two tenons shall there be in one\n"
    .string "board, set in order one against\l"
    .string "another: thus shalt thou make for\l"
    .string "all the boards of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_18::
    .string "And thou shalt make the boards for\n"
    .string "the tabernacle, twenty boards on the\l"
    .string "south side southward.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_19::
    .string "And thou shalt make forty sockets\n"
    .string "of silver under the twenty boards;\l"
    .string "two sockets under one board for his\l"
    .string "two tenons, and two sockets under\l"
    .string "another board for his two tenons.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_20::
    .string "And for the second side of the\n"
    .string "tabernacle on the north side there\l"
    .string "shall be twenty boards:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_21::
    .string "And their forty sockets of silver;\n"
    .string "two sockets under one board, and two\l"
    .string "sockets under another board$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_22::
    .string "And for the sides of the tabernacle\n"
    .string "westward thou shalt make six boards.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_23::
    .string "And two boards shalt thou make for\n"
    .string "the corners of the tabernacle in the\l"
    .string "two sides.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_24::
    .string "And they shall be coupled\n"
    .string "together beneath, and they shall be\l"
    .string "coupled together above the head of\l"
    .string "it unto one ring: thus shall it be\l"
    .string "for them both; they shall be for the\l"
    .string "two corners.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_25::
    .string "And they shall be eight boards, and\n"
    .string "their sockets of silver, sixteen\l"
    .string "sockets; two sockets under one board,\l"
    .string "and two sockets under another board.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_26::
    .string "And thou shalt make bars of shittim\n"
    .string "wood; five for the boards of the one\l"
    .string "side of the tabernacle,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_27::
    .string "And five bars for the boards of the\n"
    .string "other side of the tabernacle, and\l"
    .string "five bars for the boards of the side\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle, for the two sides\l"
    .string "westward$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_28::
    .string "And the middle bar in the midst of\n"
    .string "the boards shall reach from end to\l"
    .string "end.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_29::
    .string "And thou shalt overlay the boards\n"
    .string "with gold, and make their rings of\l"
    .string "gold for places for the bars: and\l"
    .string "thou shalt overlay the bars with\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_30::
    .string "And thou shalt rear up the\n"
    .string "tabernacle according to the fashion\l"
    .string "thereof which was shewed thee in the\l"
    .string "mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_31::
    .string "And thou shalt make a vail of\n"
    .string "blue, and purple, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "fine twined linen of cunning work:\l"
    .string "with cherubims shall it be made:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_32::
    .string "And thou shalt hang it upon four\n"
    .string "pillars of shittim wood overlaid\l"
    .string "with gold: their hooks shall be of\l"
    .string "gold, upon the four sockets of\l"
    .string "silver$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_33::
    .string "And thou shalt hang up the vail\n"
    .string "under the taches, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "bring in thither within the vail the\l"
    .string "ark of the testimony: and the vail\l"
    .string "shall divide unto you between the\l"
    .string "holy place and the most holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_34::
    .string "And thou shalt put the mercy seat\n"
    .string "upon the ark of the testimony in the\l"
    .string "most holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_35::
    .string "And thou shalt set the table\n"
    .string "without the vail, and the\l"
    .string "candlestick over against the table\l"
    .string "on the side of the tabernacle toward\l"
    .string "the south: and thou shalt put the\l"
    .string "table on the north side.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_36::
    .string "And thou shalt make an hanging for\n"
    .string "the door of the tent, of blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "twined linen, wrought with\l"
    .string "needlework.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_26_37::
    .string "And thou shalt make for the hanging\n"
    .string "five pillars of shittim wood, and\l"
    .string "overlay them with gold, and their\l"
    .string "hooks shall be of gold: and thou\l"
    .string "shalt cast five sockets of brass for\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_1::
    .string "And thou shalt make an altar of\n"
    .string "shittim wood, five cubits long, and\l"
    .string "five cubits broad; the altar shall\l"
    .string "be foursquare: and the height thereof\l"
    .string "shall be three cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_2::
    .string "And thou shalt make the horns of it\n"
    .string "upon the four corners thereof: his\l"
    .string "horns shall be of the same: and thou\l"
    .string "shalt overlay it with brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_3::
    .string "And thou shalt make his pans to\n"
    .string "receive his ashes, and his shovels,\l"
    .string "and his basons, and his fleshhooks,\l"
    .string "and his firepans: all the vessels\l"
    .string "thereof thou shalt make of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_4::
    .string "And thou shalt make for it a grate\n"
    .string "of network of brass; and upon the net\l"
    .string "shalt thou make four brasen rings in\l"
    .string "the four corners thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_5::
    .string "And thou shalt put it under the\n"
    .string "compass of the altar beneath, that\l"
    .string "the net may be even to the midst of\l"
    .string "the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_6::
    .string "And thou shalt make staves for the\n"
    .string "altar, staves of shittim wood, and\l"
    .string "overlay them with brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_7::
    .string "And the staves shall be put into\n"
    .string "the rings, and the staves shall be\l"
    .string "upon the two sides of the altar, to\l"
    .string "bear it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_8::
    .string "Hollow with boards shalt thou\n"
    .string "make it: as it was shewed thee in the\l"
    .string "mount, so shall they make it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_9::
    .string "And thou shalt make the court of\n"
    .string "the tabernacle: for the south side\l"
    .string "southward there shall be hangings\l"
    .string "for the court of fine twined linen\l"
    .string "of an hundred cubits long for one\l"
    .string "side:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_10::
    .string "And the twenty pillars thereof\n"
    .string "and their twenty sockets shall be\l"
    .string "of brass; the hooks of the pillars\l"
    .string "and their fillets shall be of\l"
    .string "silver$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_11::
    .string "And likewise for the north side in\n"
    .string "length there shall be hangings of\l"
    .string "an hundred cubits long, and his\l"
    .string "twenty pillars and their twenty\l"
    .string "sockets of brass; the hooks of the\l"
    .string "pillars and their fillets of\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_12::
    .string "And for the breadth of the court on\n"
    .string "the west side shall be hangings of\l"
    .string "fifty cubits: their pillars ten,\l"
    .string "and their sockets ten.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_13::
    .string "And the breadth of the court on the\n"
    .string "east side eastward shall be fifty\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_14::
    .string "The hangings of one side of the gate\n"
    .string "shall be fifteen cubits: their\l"
    .string "pillars three, and their sockets\l"
    .string "three.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_15::
    .string "And on the other side shall be\n"
    .string "hangings fifteen cubits: their\l"
    .string "pillars three, and their sockets\l"
    .string "three.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_16::
    .string "And for the gate of the court shall\n"
    .string "be an hanging of twenty cubits, of\l"
    .string "blue, and purple, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "fine twined linen, wrought with\l"
    .string "needlework: and their pillars\l"
    .string "shall be four, and their sockets\l"
    .string "four.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_17::
    .string "All the pillars round about the\n"
    .string "court shall be filleted with\l"
    .string "silver; their hooks shall be of\l"
    .string "silver, and their sockets of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_18::
    .string "The length of the court shall be\n"
    .string "an hundred cubits, and the breadth\l"
    .string "fifty every where, and the height\l"
    .string "five cubits of fine twined linen,\l"
    .string "and their sockets of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_19::
    .string "All the vessels of the tabernacle\n"
    .string "in all the service thereof, and\l"
    .string "all the pins thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "pins of the court, shall be of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_20::
    .string "And thou shalt command the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, that they bring\l"
    .string "thee pure oil olive beaten for the\l"
    .string "light, to cause the lamp to burn\l"
    .string "always.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_27_21::
    .string "In the tabernacle of the\n"
    .string "congregation without the vail, which\l"
    .string "is before the testimony, Aaron and\l"
    .string "his sons shall order it from\l"
    .string "evening to morning before the LORD:\l"
    .string "it shall be a statute for ever unto\l"
    .string "their generations on the behalf of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_1::
    .string "And take thou unto thee Aaron thy\n"
    .string "brother, and his sons with him, from\l"
    .string "among the children of Israel, that\l"
    .string "he may minister unto me in the\l"
    .string "priest’s office, even Aaron, Nadab\l"
    .string "and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar,\l"
    .string "Aaron’s sons.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_2::
    .string "And thou shalt make holy garments\n"
    .string "for Aaron thy brother for glory and\l"
    .string "for beauty.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_3::
    .string "And thou shalt speak unto all\n"
    .string "that are wise hearted, whom I have\l"
    .string "filled with the spirit of wisdom,\l"
    .string "that they may make Aaron’s garments\l"
    .string "to consecrate him, that he may\l"
    .string "minister unto me in the priest’s\l"
    .string "office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_4::
    .string "And these are the garments which\n"
    .string "they shall make; a breastplate,\l"
    .string "and an ephod, and a robe, and a\l"
    .string "broidered coat, a mitre, and a\l"
    .string "girdle: and they shall make holy\l"
    .string "garments for Aaron thy brother, and\l"
    .string "his sons, that he may minister unto\l"
    .string "me in the priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_5::
    .string "And they shall take gold, and\n"
    .string "blue, and purple, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "fine linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_6::
    .string "And they shall make the ephod of\n"
    .string "gold, of blue, and of purple, of\l"
    .string "scarlet, and fine twined linen,\l"
    .string "with cunning work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_7::
    .string "It shall have the two\n"
    .string "shoulderpieces thereof joined at\l"
    .string "the two edges thereof; and so it\l"
    .string "shall be joined together.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_8::
    .string "And the curious girdle of the\n"
    .string "ephod, which is upon it, shall be\l"
    .string "of the same, according to the work\l"
    .string "thereof; even of gold, of blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "twined linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_9::
    .string "And thou shalt take two onyx\n"
    .string "stones, and grave on them the names\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_10::
    .string "Six of their names on one stone, and\n"
    .string "the other six names of the rest on\l"
    .string "the other stone, according to their\l"
    .string "birth$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_11::
    .string "With the work of an engraver in\n"
    .string "stone, like the engravings of a\l"
    .string "signet, shalt thou engrave the two\l"
    .string "stones with the names of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: thou shalt make\l"
    .string "them to be set in ouches of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_12::
    .string "And thou shalt put the two stones\n"
    .string "upon the shoulders of the ephod for\l"
    .string "stones of memorial unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: and Aaron\l"
    .string "shall bear their names before the\l"
    .string "LORD upon his two shoulders for a\l"
    .string "memorial.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_13::
    .string "And thou shalt make ouches of gold;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_14::
    .string "And two chains of pure gold at the\n"
    .string "ends; of wreathen work shalt thou\l"
    .string "make them, and fasten the wreathen\l"
    .string "chains to the ouches$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_15::
    .string "And thou shalt make the\n"
    .string "breastplate of judgment with\l"
    .string "cunning work; after the work of the\l"
    .string "ephod thou shalt make it; of gold,\l"
    .string "of blue, and of purple, and of\l"
    .string "scarlet, and of fine twined linen,\l"
    .string "shalt thou make it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_16::
    .string "Foursquare it shall be being\n"
    .string "doubled; a span shall be the\l"
    .string "length thereof, and a span shall be\l"
    .string "the breadth thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_17::
    .string "And thou shalt set in it settings\n"
    .string "of stones, even four rows of stones:\l"
    .string "the first row shall be a sardius, a\l"
    .string "topaz, and a carbuncle: this shall\l"
    .string "be the first row.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_18::
    .string "And the second row shall be an\n"
    .string "emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_19::
    .string "And the third row a ligure, an\n"
    .string "agate, and an amethyst.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_20::
    .string "And the fourth row a beryl, and an\n"
    .string "onyx, and a jasper: they shall be\l"
    .string "set in gold in their inclosings.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_21::
    .string "And the stones shall be with the\n"
    .string "names of the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "twelve, according to their names,\l"
    .string "like the engravings of a signet;\l"
    .string "every one with his name shall they\l"
    .string "be according to the twelve tribes.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_22::
    .string "And thou shalt make upon the\n"
    .string "breastplate chains at the ends of\l"
    .string "wreathen work of pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_23::
    .string "And thou shalt make upon the\n"
    .string "breastplate two rings of gold, and\l"
    .string "shalt put the two rings on the two\l"
    .string "ends of the breastplate.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_24::
    .string "And thou shalt put the two\n"
    .string "wreathen chains of gold in the two\l"
    .string "rings which are on the ends of the\l"
    .string "breastplate.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_25::
    .string "And the other two ends of the two\n"
    .string "wreathen chains thou shalt fasten in\l"
    .string "the two ouches, and put them on the\l"
    .string "shoulderpieces of the ephod before\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_26::
    .string "And thou shalt make two rings of\n"
    .string "gold, and thou shalt put them upon\l"
    .string "the two ends of the breastplate in\l"
    .string "the border thereof, which is in the\l"
    .string "side of the ephod inward.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_27::
    .string "And two other rings of gold thou\n"
    .string "shalt make, and shalt put them on\l"
    .string "the two sides of the ephod\l"
    .string "underneath, toward the forepart\l"
    .string "thereof, over against the other\l"
    .string "coupling thereof, above the curious\l"
    .string "girdle of the ephod.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_28::
    .string "And they shall bind the\n"
    .string "breastplate by the rings thereof\l"
    .string "unto the rings of the ephod with a\l"
    .string "lace of blue, that it may be above\l"
    .string "the curious girdle of the ephod, and\l"
    .string "that the breastplate be not loosed\l"
    .string "from the ephod.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_29::
    .string "And Aaron shall bear the names of\n"
    .string "the children of Israel in the\l"
    .string "breastplate of judgment upon his\l"
    .string "heart, when he goeth in unto the holy\l"
    .string "place, for a memorial before the\l"
    .string "LORD continually.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_30::
    .string "And thou shalt put in the\n"
    .string "breastplate of judgment the Urim\l"
    .string "and the Thummim; and they shall be\l"
    .string "upon Aaron’s heart, when he goeth in\l"
    .string "before the LORD: and Aaron shall\l"
    .string "bear the judgment of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel upon his heart before the\l"
    .string "LORD continually.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_31::
    .string "And thou shalt make the robe of the\n"
    .string "ephod all of blue.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_32::
    .string "And there shall be an hole in the\n"
    .string "top of it, in the midst thereof: it\l"
    .string "shall have a binding of woven work\l"
    .string "round about the hole of it, as it\l"
    .string "were the hole of an habergeon, that\l"
    .string "it be not rent.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_33::
    .string "And beneath upon the hem of it thou\n"
    .string "shalt make pomegranates of blue,\l"
    .string "and of purple, and of scarlet,\l"
    .string "round about the hem thereof; and\l"
    .string "bells of gold between them round\l"
    .string "about:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_34::
    .string "A golden bell and a pomegranate,\n"
    .string "a golden bell and a pomegranate,\l"
    .string "upon the hem of the robe round about$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_35::
    .string "And it shall be upon Aaron to\n"
    .string "minister: and his sound shall be\l"
    .string "heard when he goeth in unto the holy\l"
    .string "place before the LORD, and when he\l"
    .string "cometh out, that he die not.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_36::
    .string "And thou shalt make a plate of\n"
    .string "pure gold, and grave upon it, like\l"
    .string "the engravings of a signet, HOLINESS\l"
    .string "TO THE LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_37::
    .string "And thou shalt put it on a blue\n"
    .string "lace, that it may be upon the mitre;\l"
    .string "upon the forefront of the mitre it\l"
    .string "shall be.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_38::
    .string "And it shall be upon Aaron’s\n"
    .string "forehead, that Aaron may bear the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the holy things, which\l"
    .string "the children of Israel shall\l"
    .string "hallow in all their holy gifts;\l"
    .string "and it shall be always upon his\l"
    .string "forehead, that they may be accepted\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_39::
    .string "And thou shalt embroider the coat\n"
    .string "of fine linen, and thou shalt make\l"
    .string "the mitre of fine linen, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt make the girdle of\l"
    .string "needlework.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_40::
    .string "And for Aaron’s sons thou shalt\n"
    .string "make coats, and thou shalt make for\l"
    .string "them girdles, and bonnets shalt\l"
    .string "thou make for them, for glory and for\l"
    .string "beauty.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_41::
    .string "And thou shalt put them upon Aaron\n"
    .string "thy brother, and his sons with him;\l"
    .string "and shalt anoint them, and\l"
    .string "consecrate them, and sanctify them,\l"
    .string "that they may minister unto me in the\l"
    .string "priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_42::
    .string "And thou shalt make them linen\n"
    .string "breeches to cover their nakedness;\l"
    .string "from the loins even unto the thighs\l"
    .string "they shall reach:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_28_43::
    .string "And they shall be upon Aaron, and\n"
    .string "upon his sons, when they come in unto\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "or when they come near unto the\l"
    .string "altar to minister in the holy\l"
    .string "place; that they bear not iniquity,\l"
    .string "and die: it shall be a statute for\l"
    .string "ever unto him and his seed after him$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_1::
    .string "And this is the thing that thou\n"
    .string "shalt do unto them to hallow them,\l"
    .string "to minister unto me in the priest’s\l"
    .string "office: Take one young bullock, and\l"
    .string "two rams without blemish,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_2::
    .string "And unleavened bread, and cakes\n"
    .string "unleavened tempered with oil, and\l"
    .string "wafers unleavened anointed with\l"
    .string "oil: of wheaten flour shalt thou\l"
    .string "make them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_3::
    .string "And thou shalt put them into one\n"
    .string "basket, and bring them in the basket,\l"
    .string "with the bullock and the two rams.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_4::
    .string "And Aaron and his sons thou shalt\n"
    .string "bring unto the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "shalt wash them with water.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_5::
    .string "And thou shalt take the garments,\n"
    .string "and put upon Aaron the coat, and the\l"
    .string "robe of the ephod, and the ephod,\l"
    .string "and the breastplate, and gird him\l"
    .string "with the curious girdle of the\l"
    .string "ephod:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_6::
    .string "And thou shalt put the mitre upon\n"
    .string "his head, and put the holy crown\l"
    .string "upon the mitre$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_7::
    .string "Then shalt thou take the anointing\n"
    .string "oil, and pour it upon his head, and\l"
    .string "anoint him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_8::
    .string "And thou shalt bring his sons, and\n"
    .string "put coats upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_9::
    .string "And thou shalt gird them with\n"
    .string "girdles, Aaron and his sons, and put\l"
    .string "the bonnets on them: and the\l"
    .string "priest’s office shall be theirs for\l"
    .string "a perpetual statute: and thou\l"
    .string "shalt consecrate Aaron and his sons.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_10::
    .string "And thou shalt cause a bullock to\n"
    .string "be brought before the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation: and Aaron and his\l"
    .string "sons shall put their hands upon\l"
    .string "the head of the bullock.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_11::
    .string "And thou shalt kill the bullock\n"
    .string "before the LORD, by the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_12::
    .string "And thou shalt take of the blood of\n"
    .string "the bullock, and put it upon the\l"
    .string "horns of the altar with thy finger,\l"
    .string "and pour all the blood beside the\l"
    .string "bottom of the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_13::
    .string "And thou shalt take all the fat\n"
    .string "that covereth the inwards, and the\l"
    .string "caul that is above the liver, and\l"
    .string "the two kidneys, and the fat that is\l"
    .string "upon them, and burn them upon the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_14::
    .string "But the flesh of the bullock, and\n"
    .string "his skin, and his dung, shalt thou\l"
    .string "burn with fire without the camp: it\l"
    .string "is a sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_15::
    .string "Thou shalt also take one ram; and\n"
    .string "Aaron and his sons shall put their\l"
    .string "hands upon the head of the ram.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_16::
    .string "And thou shalt slay the ram, and\n"
    .string "thou shalt take his blood, and\l"
    .string "sprinkle it round about upon the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_17::
    .string "And thou shalt cut the ram in\n"
    .string "pieces, and wash the inwards of him,\l"
    .string "and his legs, and put them unto his\l"
    .string "pieces, and unto his head.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_18::
    .string "And thou shalt burn the whole ram\n"
    .string "upon the altar: it is a burnt\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD: it is a sweet\l"
    .string "savour, an offering made by fire unto\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_19::
    .string "And thou shalt take the other ram;\n"
    .string "and Aaron and his sons shall put\l"
    .string "their hands upon the head of the ram.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_20::
    .string "Then shalt thou kill the ram, and\n"
    .string "take of his blood, and put it upon\l"
    .string "the tip of the right ear of Aaron,\l"
    .string "and upon the tip of the right ear of\l"
    .string "his sons, and upon the thumb of their\l"
    .string "right hand, and upon the great toe of\l"
    .string "their right foot, and sprinkle the\l"
    .string "blood upon the altar round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_21::
    .string "And thou shalt take of the blood\n"
    .string "that is upon the altar, and of the\l"
    .string "anointing oil, and sprinkle it\l"
    .string "upon Aaron, and upon his garments,\l"
    .string "and upon his sons, and upon the\l"
    .string "garments of his sons with him: and he\l"
    .string "shall be hallowed, and his\l"
    .string "garments, and his sons, and his sons’\l"
    .string "garments with him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_22::
    .string "Also thou shalt take of the ram the\n"
    .string "fat and the rump, and the fat that\l"
    .string "covereth the inwards, and the caul\l"
    .string "above the liver, and the two\l"
    .string "kidneys, and the fat that is upon\l"
    .string "them, and the right shoulder; for it\l"
    .string "is a ram of consecration:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_23::
    .string "And one loaf of bread, and one cake\n"
    .string "of oiled bread, and one wafer out of\l"
    .string "the basket of the unleavened bread\l"
    .string "that is before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_24::
    .string "And thou shalt put all in the\n"
    .string "hands of Aaron, and in the hands of\l"
    .string "his sons; and shalt wave them for a\l"
    .string "wave offering before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_25::
    .string "And thou shalt receive them of\n"
    .string "their hands, and burn them upon the\l"
    .string "altar for a burnt offering, for a\l"
    .string "sweet savour before the LORD: it is\l"
    .string "an offering made by fire unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_26::
    .string "And thou shalt take the breast of\n"
    .string "the ram of Aaron’s consecration, and\l"
    .string "wave it for a wave offering before\l"
    .string "the LORD: and it shall be thy part.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_27::
    .string "And thou shalt sanctify the breast\n"
    .string "of the wave offering, and the\l"
    .string "shoulder of the heave offering,\l"
    .string "which is waved, and which is heaved\l"
    .string "up, of the ram of the consecration,\l"
    .string "even of that which is for Aaron, and\l"
    .string "of that which is for his sons:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_28::
    .string "And it shall be Aaron’s and his\n"
    .string "sons’ by a statute for ever from the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: for it is an\l"
    .string "heave offering: and it shall be an\l"
    .string "heave offering from the children of\l"
    .string "Israel of the sacrifice of their\l"
    .string "peace offerings, even their heave\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_29::
    .string "And the holy garments of Aaron\n"
    .string "shall be his sons’ after him, to be\l"
    .string "anointed therein, and to be\l"
    .string "consecrated in them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_30::
    .string "And that son that is priest in his\n"
    .string "stead shall put them on seven days,\l"
    .string "when he cometh into the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation to minister in\l"
    .string "the holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_31::
    .string "And thou shalt take the ram of the\n"
    .string "consecration, and seethe his flesh\l"
    .string "in the holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_32::
    .string "And Aaron and his sons shall eat\n"
    .string "the flesh of the ram, and the bread\l"
    .string "that is in the basket by the door of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_33::
    .string "And they shall eat those things\n"
    .string "wherewith the atonement was made, to\l"
    .string "consecrate and to sanctify them: but\l"
    .string "a stranger shall not eat thereof,\l"
    .string "because they are holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_34::
    .string "And if ought of the flesh of the\n"
    .string "consecrations, or of the bread,\l"
    .string "remain unto the morning, then thou\l"
    .string "shalt burn the remainder with fire:\l"
    .string "it shall not be eaten, because it is\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_35::
    .string "And thus shalt thou do unto Aaron,\n"
    .string "and to his sons, according to all\l"
    .string "things which I have commanded thee:\l"
    .string "seven days shalt thou consecrate\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_36::
    .string "And thou shalt offer every day a\n"
    .string "bullock for a sin offering for\l"
    .string "atonement: and thou shalt cleanse\l"
    .string "the altar, when thou hast made an\l"
    .string "atonement for it, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "anoint it, to sanctify it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_37::
    .string "Seven days thou shalt make an\n"
    .string "atonement for the altar, and\l"
    .string "sanctify it; and it shall be an\l"
    .string "altar most holy: whatsoever\l"
    .string "toucheth the altar shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_38::
    .string "Now this is that which thou shalt\n"
    .string "offer upon the altar; two lambs of\l"
    .string "the first year day by day\l"
    .string "continually.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_39::
    .string "The one lamb thou shalt offer in\n"
    .string "the morning; and the other lamb thou\l"
    .string "shalt offer at even:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_40::
    .string "And with the one lamb a tenth deal\n"
    .string "of flour mingled with the fourth\l"
    .string "part of an hin of beaten oil; and the\l"
    .string "fourth part of an hin of wine for a\l"
    .string "drink offering$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_41::
    .string "And the other lamb thou shalt\n"
    .string "offer at even, and shalt do thereto\l"
    .string "according to the meat offering of the\l"
    .string "morning, and according to the drink\l"
    .string "offering thereof, for a sweet savour,\l"
    .string "an offering made by fire unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_42::
    .string "This shall be a continual burnt\n"
    .string "offering throughout your generations\l"
    .string "at the door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation before the LORD: where I\l"
    .string "will meet you, to speak there unto\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_43::
    .string "And there I will meet with the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, and the\l"
    .string "tabernacle shall be sanctified by\l"
    .string "my glory.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_44::
    .string "And I will sanctify the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "the altar: I will sanctify also\l"
    .string "both Aaron and his sons, to minister\l"
    .string "to me in the priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_45::
    .string "And I will dwell among the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, and will be\l"
    .string "their God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_29_46::
    .string "And they shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD their God, that brought them\l"
    .string "forth out of the land of Egypt, that\l"
    .string "I may dwell among them: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_1::
    .string "And thou shalt make an altar to\n"
    .string "burn incense upon: of shittim wood\l"
    .string "shalt thou make it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_2::
    .string "A cubit shall be the length\n"
    .string "thereof, and a cubit the breadth\l"
    .string "thereof; foursquare shall it be:\l"
    .string "and two cubits shall be the height\l"
    .string "thereof: the horns thereof shall be\l"
    .string "of the same.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_3::
    .string "And thou shalt overlay it with\n"
    .string "pure gold, the top thereof, and the\l"
    .string "sides thereof round about, and the\l"
    .string "horns thereof; and thou shalt make\l"
    .string "unto it a crown of gold round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_4::
    .string "And two golden rings shalt thou\n"
    .string "make to it under the crown of it, by\l"
    .string "the two corners thereof, upon the\l"
    .string "two sides of it shalt thou make it;\l"
    .string "and they shall be for places for\l"
    .string "the staves to bear it withal.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_5::
    .string "And thou shalt make the staves of\n"
    .string "shittim wood, and overlay them with\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_6::
    .string "And thou shalt put it before the\n"
    .string "vail that is by the ark of the\l"
    .string "testimony, before the mercy seat that\l"
    .string "is over the testimony, where I will\l"
    .string "meet with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_7::
    .string "And Aaron shall burn thereon sweet\n"
    .string "incense every morning: when he\l"
    .string "dresseth the lamps, he shall burn\l"
    .string "incense upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_8::
    .string "And when Aaron lighteth the lamps\n"
    .string "at even, he shall burn incense upon\l"
    .string "it, a perpetual incense before the\l"
    .string "LORD throughout your generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_9::
    .string "Ye shall offer no strange incense\n"
    .string "thereon, nor burnt sacrifice, nor\l"
    .string "meat offering; neither shall ye\l"
    .string "pour drink offering thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_10::
    .string "And Aaron shall make an atonement\n"
    .string "upon the horns of it once in a year\l"
    .string "with the blood of the sin offering\l"
    .string "of atonements: once in the year\l"
    .string "shall he make atonement upon it\l"
    .string "throughout your generations: it is\l"
    .string "most holy unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_11::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_12::
    .string "When thou takest the sum of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel after their\l"
    .string "number, then shall they give every\l"
    .string "man a ransom for his soul unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, when thou numberest them; that\l"
    .string "there be no plague among them, when\l"
    .string "thou numberest them$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_13::
    .string "This they shall give, every one\n"
    .string "that passeth among them that are\l"
    .string "numbered, half a shekel after the\l"
    .string "shekel of the sanctuary: (a shekel\l"
    .string "is twenty gerahs:) an half shekel\l"
    .string "shall be the offering of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_14::
    .string "Every one that passeth among them\n"
    .string "that are numbered, from twenty years\l"
    .string "old and above, shall give an\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_15::
    .string "The rich shall not give more, and\n"
    .string "the poor shall not give less than\l"
    .string "half a shekel, when they give an\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD, to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for your souls.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_16::
    .string "And thou shalt take the atonement\n"
    .string "money of the children of Israel, and\l"
    .string "shalt appoint it for the service of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation;\l"
    .string "that it may be a memorial unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel before the LORD,\l"
    .string "to make an atonement for your souls.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_17::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_18::
    .string "Thou shalt also make a laver of\n"
    .string "brass, and his foot also of brass, to\l"
    .string "wash withal: and thou shalt put it\l"
    .string "between the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation and the altar, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt put water therein$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_19::
    .string "For Aaron and his sons shall wash\n"
    .string "their hands and their feet thereat:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_20::
    .string "When they go into the tabernacle of\n"
    .string "the congregation, they shall wash\l"
    .string "with water, that they die not; or\l"
    .string "when they come near to the altar to\l"
    .string "minister, to burn offering made by\l"
    .string "fire unto the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_21::
    .string "So they shall wash their hands and\n"
    .string "their feet, that they die not: and it\l"
    .string "shall be a statute for ever to them,\l"
    .string "even to him and to his seed\l"
    .string "throughout their generations$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_22::
    .string "Moreover the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_23::
    .string "Take thou also unto thee\n"
    .string "principal spices, of pure myrrh\l"
    .string "five hundred shekels, and of sweet\l"
    .string "cinnamon half so much, even two\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty shekels, and of\l"
    .string "sweet calamus two hundred and fifty\l"
    .string "shekels,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_24::
    .string "And of cassia five hundred shekels,\n"
    .string "after the shekel of the sanctuary,\l"
    .string "and of oil olive an hin:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_25::
    .string "And thou shalt make it an oil of\n"
    .string "holy ointment, an ointment compound\l"
    .string "after the art of the apothecary: it\l"
    .string "shall be an holy anointing oil$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_26::
    .string "And thou shalt anoint the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation\l"
    .string "therewith, and the ark of the\l"
    .string "testimony,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_27::
    .string "And the table and all his\n"
    .string "vessels, and the candlestick and\l"
    .string "his vessels, and the altar of\l"
    .string "incense,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_28::
    .string "And the altar of burnt offering\n"
    .string "with all his vessels, and the\l"
    .string "laver and his foot$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_29::
    .string "And thou shalt sanctify them, that\n"
    .string "they may be most holy: whatsoever\l"
    .string "toucheth them shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_30::
    .string "And thou shalt anoint Aaron and his\n"
    .string "sons, and consecrate them, that they\l"
    .string "may minister unto me in the priest’s\l"
    .string "office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_31::
    .string "And thou shalt speak unto the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, saying, This\l"
    .string "shall be an holy anointing oil\l"
    .string "unto me throughout your generations.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_32::
    .string "Upon man’s flesh shall it not be\n"
    .string "poured, neither shall ye make any\l"
    .string "other like it, after the\l"
    .string "composition of it: it is holy, and\l"
    .string "it shall be holy unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_33::
    .string "Whosoever compoundeth any like it,\n"
    .string "or whosoever putteth any of it upon\l"
    .string "a stranger, shall even be cut off\l"
    .string "from his people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_34::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Take\n"
    .string "unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and\l"
    .string "onycha, and galbanum; these sweet\l"
    .string "spices with pure frankincense: of\l"
    .string "each shall there be a like weight:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_35::
    .string "And thou shalt make it a perfume, a\n"
    .string "confection after the art of the\l"
    .string "apothecary, tempered together,\l"
    .string "pure and holy:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_36::
    .string "And thou shalt beat some of it very\n"
    .string "small, and put of it before the\l"
    .string "testimony in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, where I will meet\l"
    .string "with thee: it shall be unto you most\l"
    .string "holy$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_37::
    .string "And as for the perfume which thou\n"
    .string "shalt make, ye shall not make to\l"
    .string "yourselves according to the\l"
    .string "composition thereof: it shall be\l"
    .string "unto thee holy for the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_30_38::
    .string "Whosoever shall make like unto\n"
    .string "that, to smell thereto, shall even\l"
    .string "be cut off from his people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_2::
    .string "See, I have called by name\n"
    .string "Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of\l"
    .string "Hur, of the tribe of Judah:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_3::
    .string "And I have filled him with the\n"
    .string "spirit of God, in wisdom, and in\l"
    .string "understanding, and in knowledge, and\l"
    .string "in all manner of workmanship,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_4::
    .string "To devise cunning works, to work in\n"
    .string "gold, and in silver, and in brass,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_5::
    .string "And in cutting of stones, to set\n"
    .string "them, and in carving of timber, to\l"
    .string "work in all manner of workmanship$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_6::
    .string "And I, behold, I have given with him\n"
    .string "Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of\l"
    .string "the tribe of Dan: and in the hearts of\l"
    .string "all that are wise hearted I have\l"
    .string "put wisdom, that they may make all\l"
    .string "that I have commanded thee;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_7::
    .string "The tabernacle of the congregation,\n"
    .string "and the ark of the testimony, and the\l"
    .string "mercy seat that is thereupon, and\l"
    .string "all the furniture of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_8::
    .string "And the table and his furniture,\n"
    .string "and the pure candlestick with all\l"
    .string "his furniture, and the altar of\l"
    .string "incense,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_9::
    .string "And the altar of burnt offering\n"
    .string "with all his furniture, and the\l"
    .string "laver and his foot,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_10::
    .string "And the cloths of service, and the\n"
    .string "holy garments for Aaron the priest,\l"
    .string "and the garments of his sons, to\l"
    .string "minister in the priest’s office,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_11::
    .string "And the anointing oil, and sweet\n"
    .string "incense for the holy place:\l"
    .string "according to all that I have\l"
    .string "commanded thee shall they do$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_12::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_13::
    .string "Speak thou also unto the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, saying, Verily my\l"
    .string "sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a\l"
    .string "sign between me and you throughout\l"
    .string "your generations; that ye may know\l"
    .string "that I am the LORD that doth sanctify\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_14::
    .string "Ye shall keep the sabbath\n"
    .string "therefore; for it is holy unto you:\l"
    .string "every one that defileth it shall\l"
    .string "surely be put to death: for\l"
    .string "whosoever doeth any work therein,\l"
    .string "that soul shall be cut off from\l"
    .string "among his people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_15::
    .string "Six days may work be done; but in the\n"
    .string "seventh is the sabbath of rest, holy\l"
    .string "to the LORD: whosoever doeth any work\l"
    .string "in the sabbath day, he shall surely\l"
    .string "be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_16::
    .string "Wherefore the children of Israel\n"
    .string "shall keep the sabbath, to observe\l"
    .string "the sabbath throughout their\l"
    .string "generations, for a perpetual\l"
    .string "covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_17::
    .string "It is a sign between me and the\n"
    .string "children of Israel for ever: for in\l"
    .string "six days the LORD made heaven and\l"
    .string "earth, and on the seventh day he\l"
    .string "rested, and was refreshed.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_31_18::
    .string "And he gave unto Moses, when he had\n"
    .string "made an end of communing with him\l"
    .string "upon mount Sinai, two tables of\l"
    .string "testimony, tables of stone, written\l"
    .string "with the finger of God.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_1::
    .string "And when the people saw that Moses\n"
    .string "delayed to come down out of the\l"
    .string "mount, the people gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together unto Aaron, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Up, make us gods,\l"
    .string "which shall go before us; for as for\l"
    .string "this Moses, the man that brought us\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt, we wot\l"
    .string "not what is become of him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_2::
    .string "And Aaron said unto them, Break off\n"
    .string "the golden earrings, which are in\l"
    .string "the ears of your wives, of your sons,\l"
    .string "and of your daughters, and bring them\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_3::
    .string "And all the people brake off the\n"
    .string "golden earrings which were in their\l"
    .string "ears, and brought them unto Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_4::
    .string "And he received them at their hand,\n"
    .string "and fashioned it with a graving\l"
    .string "tool, after he had made it a molten\l"
    .string "calf: and they said, These be thy\l"
    .string "gods, O Israel, which brought thee\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_5::
    .string "And when Aaron saw it, he built an\n"
    .string "altar before it; and Aaron made\l"
    .string "proclamation, and said, To morrow is\l"
    .string "a feast to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_6::
    .string "And they rose up early on the\n"
    .string "morrow, and offered burnt offerings,\l"
    .string "and brought peace offerings; and the\l"
    .string "people sat down to eat and to drink,\l"
    .string "and rose up to play.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_7::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Go,\n"
    .string "get thee down; for thy people,\l"
    .string "which thou broughtest out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, have corrupted\l"
    .string "themselves:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_8::
    .string "They have turned aside quickly out\n"
    .string "of the way which I commanded them:\l"
    .string "they have made them a molten calf,\l"
    .string "and have worshipped it, and have\l"
    .string "sacrificed thereunto, and said,\l"
    .string "These be thy gods, O Israel, which\l"
    .string "have brought thee up out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, I have\n"
    .string "seen this people, and, behold, it\l"
    .string "is a stiffnecked people:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_10::
    .string "Now therefore let me alone, that my\n"
    .string "wrath may wax hot against them, and\l"
    .string "that I may consume them: and I will\l"
    .string "make of thee a great nation$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_11::
    .string "And Moses besought the LORD his God,\n"
    .string "and said, LORD, why doth thy wrath\l"
    .string "wax hot against thy people, which\l"
    .string "thou hast brought forth out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt with great power, and\l"
    .string "with a mighty hand?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_12::
    .string "Wherefore should the Egyptians\n"
    .string "speak, and say, For mischief did he\l"
    .string "bring them out, to slay them in the\l"
    .string "mountains, and to consume them from\l"
    .string "the face of the earth? Turn from thy\l"
    .string "fierce wrath, and repent of this\l"
    .string "evil against thy people$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_13::
    .string "Remember Abraham, Isaac, and\n"
    .string "Israel, thy servants, to whom thou\l"
    .string "swarest by thine own self, and\l"
    .string "saidst unto them, I will multiply\l"
    .string "your seed as the stars of heaven, and\l"
    .string "all this land that I have spoken\l"
    .string "of will I give unto your seed, and\l"
    .string "they shall inherit it for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_14::
    .string "And the LORD repented of the evil\n"
    .string "which he thought to do unto his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_15::
    .string "And Moses turned, and went down from\n"
    .string "the mount, and the two tables of the\l"
    .string "testimony were in his hand: the\l"
    .string "tables were written on both their\l"
    .string "sides; on the one side and on the\l"
    .string "other were they written.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_16::
    .string "And the tables were the work of God,\n"
    .string "and the writing was the writing of\l"
    .string "God, graven upon the tables.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_17::
    .string "And when Joshua heard the noise of\n"
    .string "the people as they shouted, he said\l"
    .string "unto Moses, There is a noise of war in\l"
    .string "the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_18::
    .string "And he said, It is not the voice of\n"
    .string "them that shout for mastery, neither\l"
    .string "is it the voice of them that cry for\l"
    .string "being overcome: but the noise of them\l"
    .string "that sing do I hear.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as he\n"
    .string "came nigh unto the camp, that he saw\l"
    .string "the calf, and the dancing: and\l"
    .string "Moses’ anger waxed hot, and he cast\l"
    .string "the tables out of his hands, and\l"
    .string "brake them beneath the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_20::
    .string "And he took the calf which they had\n"
    .string "made, and burnt it in the fire, and\l"
    .string "ground it to powder, and strawed it\l"
    .string "upon the water, and made the\l"
    .string "children of Israel drink of it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_21::
    .string "And Moses said unto Aaron, What did\n"
    .string "this people unto thee, that thou\l"
    .string "hast brought so great a sin upon\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_22::
    .string "And Aaron said, Let not the anger of\n"
    .string "my lord wax hot: thou knowest the\l"
    .string "people, that they are set on\l"
    .string "mischief$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_23::
    .string "For they said unto me, Make us gods,\n"
    .string "which shall go before us: for as for\l"
    .string "this Moses, the man that brought us\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt, we wot\l"
    .string "not what is become of him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_24::
    .string "And I said unto them, Whosoever hath\n"
    .string "any gold, let them break it off. So\l"
    .string "they gave it me: then I cast it into\l"
    .string "the fire, and there came out this\l"
    .string "calf.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_25::
    .string "And when Moses saw that the people\n"
    .string "were naked; (for Aaron had made them\l"
    .string "naked unto their shame among their\l"
    .string "enemies:)"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_26::
    .string "Then Moses stood in the gate of the\n"
    .string "camp, and said, Who is on the LORD’s\l"
    .string "side? let him come unto me. And all\l"
    .string "the sons of Levi gathered themselves\l"
    .string "together unto him$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_27::
    .string "And he said unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel, Put every man\l"
    .string "his sword by his side, and go in and\l"
    .string "out from gate to gate throughout the\l"
    .string "camp, and slay every man his\l"
    .string "brother, and every man his\l"
    .string "companion, and every man his\l"
    .string "neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_28::
    .string "And the children of Levi did\n"
    .string "according to the word of Moses: and\l"
    .string "there fell of the people that day\l"
    .string "about three thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_29::
    .string "For Moses had said, Consecrate\n"
    .string "yourselves today to the LORD, even\l"
    .string "every man upon his son, and upon his\l"
    .string "brother; that he may bestow upon you\l"
    .string "a blessing this day.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_30::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that Moses said unto the people, Ye\l"
    .string "have sinned a great sin: and now I\l"
    .string "will go up unto the LORD;\l"
    .string "peradventure I shall make an\l"
    .string "atonement for your sin.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_31::
    .string "And Moses returned unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and said, Oh, this people have\l"
    .string "sinned a great sin, and have made\l"
    .string "them gods of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_32::
    .string "Yet now, if thou wilt forgive their\n"
    .string "sin-; and if not, blot me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, out of thy book which thou hast\l"
    .string "written.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_33::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Whosoever hath sinned against me, him\l"
    .string "will I blot out of my book.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_34::
    .string "Therefore now go, lead the people\n"
    .string "unto the place of which I have\l"
    .string "spoken unto thee: behold, mine\l"
    .string "Angel shall go before thee:\l"
    .string "nevertheless in the day when I visit\l"
    .string "I will visit their sin upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_32_35::
    .string "And the LORD plagued the people,\n"
    .string "because they made the calf, which\l"
    .string "Aaron made.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Depart, and go up hence, thou and\l"
    .string "the people which thou hast brought\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt, unto\l"
    .string "the land which I sware unto Abraham,\l"
    .string "to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, Unto\l"
    .string "thy seed will I give it:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_2::
    .string "And I will send an angel before\n"
    .string "thee; and I will drive out the\l"
    .string "Canaanite, the Amorite, and the\l"
    .string "Hittite, and the Perizzite, the\l"
    .string "Hivite, and the Jebusite:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_3::
    .string "Unto a land flowing with milk and\n"
    .string "honey: for I will not go up in the\l"
    .string "midst of thee; for thou art a\l"
    .string "stiffnecked people: lest I consume\l"
    .string "thee in the way$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_4::
    .string "And when the people heard these\n"
    .string "evil tidings, they mourned: and no\l"
    .string "man did put on him his ornaments.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_5::
    .string "For the LORD had said unto Moses,\n"
    .string "Say unto the children of Israel, Ye\l"
    .string "are a stiffnecked people: I will\l"
    .string "come up into the midst of thee in a\l"
    .string "moment, and consume thee: therefore\l"
    .string "now put off thy ornaments from thee,\l"
    .string "that I may know what to do unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_6::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "stripped themselves of their\l"
    .string "ornaments by the mount Horeb.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_7::
    .string "And Moses took the tabernacle, and\n"
    .string "pitched it without the camp, afar\l"
    .string "off from the camp, and called it\l"
    .string "the Tabernacle of the congregation.\l"
    .string "And it came to pass, that every one\l"
    .string "which sought the LORD went out unto\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "which was without the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Moses went\n"
    .string "out unto the tabernacle, that all\l"
    .string "the people rose up, and stood\l"
    .string "every man at his tent door, and\l"
    .string "looked after Moses, until he was\l"
    .string "gone into the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_9::
    .string "And it came to pass, as Moses\n"
    .string "entered into the tabernacle, the\l"
    .string "cloudy pillar descended, and stood\l"
    .string "at the door of the tabernacle, and\l"
    .string "the Lord talked with Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_10::
    .string "And all the people saw the\n"
    .string "cloudy pillar stand at the\l"
    .string "tabernacle door: and all the\l"
    .string "people rose up and worshipped,\l"
    .string "every man in his tent door.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_11::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses face\n"
    .string "to face, as a man speaketh unto his\l"
    .string "friend. And he turned again into the\l"
    .string "camp: but his servant Joshua, the\l"
    .string "son of Nun, a young man, departed not\l"
    .string "out of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_12::
    .string "And Moses said unto the LORD, See,\n"
    .string "thou sayest unto me, Bring up this\l"
    .string "people: and thou hast not let me\l"
    .string "know whom thou wilt send with me. Yet\l"
    .string "thou hast said, I know thee by name,\l"
    .string "and thou hast also found grace in my\l"
    .string "sight.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_13::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, if I\n"
    .string "have found grace in thy sight, shew\l"
    .string "me now thy way, that I may know thee,\l"
    .string "that I may find grace in thy sight:\l"
    .string "and consider that this nation is thy\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_14::
    .string "And he said, My presence shall go\n"
    .string "with thee, and I will give thee rest.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_15::
    .string "And he said unto him, If thy\n"
    .string "presence go not with me, carry us not\l"
    .string "up hence.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_16::
    .string "For wherein shall it be known here\n"
    .string "that I and thy people have found\l"
    .string "grace in thy sight? is it not in that\l"
    .string "thou goest with us? so shall we be\l"
    .string "separated, I and thy people, from\l"
    .string "all the people that are upon the\l"
    .string "face of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_17::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, I\n"
    .string "will do this thing also that thou\l"
    .string "hast spoken: for thou hast found\l"
    .string "grace in my sight, and I know thee by\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_18::
    .string "And he said, I beseech thee, shew me\n"
    .string "thy glory.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_19::
    .string "And he said, I will make all my\n"
    .string "goodness pass before thee, and I\l"
    .string "will proclaim the name of the LORD\l"
    .string "before thee; and will be gracious to\l"
    .string "whom I will be gracious, and will\l"
    .string "shew mercy on whom I will shew mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_20::
    .string "And he said, Thou canst not see my\n"
    .string "face: for there shall no man see me,\l"
    .string "and live.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_21::
    .string "And the LORD said, Behold, there is\n"
    .string "a place by me, and thou shalt stand\l"
    .string "upon a rock:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_22::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, while\n"
    .string "my glory passeth by, that I will\l"
    .string "put thee in a clift of the rock, and\l"
    .string "will cover thee with my hand while\l"
    .string "I pass by:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_33_23::
    .string "And I will take away mine hand, and\n"
    .string "thou shalt see my back parts: but my\l"
    .string "face shall not be seen$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Hew\n"
    .string "thee two tables of stone like unto\l"
    .string "the first: and I will write upon\l"
    .string "these tables the words that were in\l"
    .string "the first tables, which thou brakest.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_2::
    .string "And be ready in the morning, and\n"
    .string "come up in the morning unto mount\l"
    .string "Sinai, and present thyself there to\l"
    .string "me in the top of the mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_3::
    .string "And no man shall come up with\n"
    .string "thee, neither let any man be seen\l"
    .string "throughout all the mount; neither\l"
    .string "let the flocks nor herds feed before\l"
    .string "that mount.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_4::
    .string "And he hewed two tables of stone\n"
    .string "like unto the first; and Moses rose\l"
    .string "up early in the morning, and went\l"
    .string "up unto mount Sinai, as the LORD had\l"
    .string "commanded him, and took in his hand\l"
    .string "the two tables of stone.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_5::
    .string "And the LORD descended in the\n"
    .string "cloud, and stood with him there, and\l"
    .string "proclaimed the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_6::
    .string "And the LORD passed by before him,\n"
    .string "and proclaimed, The LORD, The LORD\l"
    .string "God, merciful and gracious,\l"
    .string "longsuffering, and abundant in\l"
    .string "goodness and truth,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_7::
    .string "Keeping mercy for thousands,\n"
    .string "forgiving iniquity and transgression\l"
    .string "and sin, and that will by no means\l"
    .string "clear the guilty; visiting the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the fathers upon the\l"
    .string "children, and upon the children’s\l"
    .string "children, unto the third and to the\l"
    .string "fourth generation$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_8::
    .string "And Moses made haste, and bowed his\n"
    .string "head toward the earth, and\l"
    .string "worshipped.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_9::
    .string "And he said, If now I have found\n"
    .string "grace in thy sight, O LORD, let my\l"
    .string "LORD, I pray thee, go among us; for\l"
    .string "it is a stiffnecked people; and\l"
    .string "pardon our iniquity and our sin, and\l"
    .string "take us for thine inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_10::
    .string "And he said, Behold, I make a\n"
    .string "covenant: before all thy people I\l"
    .string "will do marvels, such as have not\l"
    .string "been done in all the earth, nor in\l"
    .string "any nation: and all the people\l"
    .string "among which thou art shall see the\l"
    .string "work of the LORD: for it is a\l"
    .string "terrible thing that I will do with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_11::
    .string "Observe thou that which I command\n"
    .string "thee this day: behold, I drive out\l"
    .string "before thee the Amorite, and the\l"
    .string "Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the\l"
    .string "Perizzite, and the Hivite, and the\l"
    .string "Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_12::
    .string "Take heed to thyself, lest thou\n"
    .string "make a covenant with the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of the land whither thou goest, lest\l"
    .string "it be for a snare in the midst of\l"
    .string "thee:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_13::
    .string "But ye shall destroy their altars,\n"
    .string "break their images, and cut down\l"
    .string "their groves:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_14::
    .string "For thou shalt worship no other\n"
    .string "god: for the LORD, whose name is\l"
    .string "Jealous, is a jealous God:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_15::
    .string "Lest thou make a covenant with the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of the land, and they go\l"
    .string "a whoring after their gods, and do\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto their gods, and one\l"
    .string "call thee, and thou eat of his\l"
    .string "sacrifice;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_16::
    .string "And thou take of their daughters\n"
    .string "unto thy sons, and their daughters go\l"
    .string "a whoring after their gods, and make\l"
    .string "thy sons go a whoring after their gods$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_17::
    .string "Thou shalt make thee no molten\n"
    .string "gods.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_18::
    .string "The feast of unleavened bread\n"
    .string "shalt thou keep. Seven days thou\l"
    .string "shalt eat unleavened bread, as I\l"
    .string "commanded thee, in the time of the\l"
    .string "month Abib: for in the month Abib\l"
    .string "thou camest out from Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_19::
    .string "All that openeth the matrix is\n"
    .string "mine; and every firstling among thy\l"
    .string "cattle, whether ox or sheep, that is\l"
    .string "male.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_20::
    .string "But the firstling of an ass thou\n"
    .string "shalt redeem with a lamb: and if\l"
    .string "thou redeem him not, then shalt thou\l"
    .string "break his neck. All the firstborn of\l"
    .string "thy sons thou shalt redeem. And none\l"
    .string "shall appear before me empty.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_21::
    .string "Six days thou shalt work, but on the\n"
    .string "seventh day thou shalt rest: in\l"
    .string "earing time and in harvest thou\l"
    .string "shalt rest.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_22::
    .string "And thou shalt observe the feast of\n"
    .string "weeks, of the firstfruits of wheat\l"
    .string "harvest, and the feast of ingathering\l"
    .string "at the year’s end.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_23::
    .string "Thrice in the year shall all your\n"
    .string "menchildren appear before the LORD\l"
    .string "God, the God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_24::
    .string "For I will cast out the nations\n"
    .string "before thee, and enlarge thy\l"
    .string "borders: neither shall any man\l"
    .string "desire thy land, when thou shalt go\l"
    .string "up to appear before the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God thrice in the year.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_25::
    .string "Thou shalt not offer the blood of\n"
    .string "my sacrifice with leaven; neither\l"
    .string "shall the sacrifice of the feast of\l"
    .string "the passover be left unto the\l"
    .string "morning.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_26::
    .string "The first of the firstfruits of thy\n"
    .string "land thou shalt bring unto the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not\l"
    .string "seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_27::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Write\n"
    .string "thou these words: for after the tenor\l"
    .string "of these words I have made a covenant\l"
    .string "with thee and with Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_28::
    .string "And he was there with the LORD forty\n"
    .string "days and forty nights; he did neither\l"
    .string "eat bread, nor drink water. And he\l"
    .string "wrote upon the tables the words of\l"
    .string "the covenant, the ten commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Moses came\n"
    .string "down from mount Sinai with the two\l"
    .string "tables of testimony in Moses’ hand,\l"
    .string "when he came down from the mount,\l"
    .string "that Moses wist not that the skin of\l"
    .string "his face shone while he talked with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_30::
    .string "And when Aaron and all the\n"
    .string "children of Israel saw Moses,\l"
    .string "behold, the skin of his face shone;\l"
    .string "and they were afraid to come nigh him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_31::
    .string "And Moses called unto them; and\n"
    .string "Aaron and all the rulers of the\l"
    .string "congregation returned unto him: and\l"
    .string "Moses talked with them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_32::
    .string "And afterward all the children of\n"
    .string "Israel came nigh: and he gave them in\l"
    .string "commandment all that the LORD had\l"
    .string "spoken with him in mount Sinai.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_33::
    .string "And till Moses had done speaking\n"
    .string "with them, he put a vail on his face.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_34::
    .string "But when Moses went in before the\n"
    .string "LORD to speak with him, he took the\l"
    .string "vail off, until he came out. And he\l"
    .string "came out, and spake unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel that which he\l"
    .string "was commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_34_35::
    .string "And the children of Israel saw the\n"
    .string "face of Moses, that the skin of\l"
    .string "Moses’ face shone: and Moses put the\l"
    .string "vail upon his face again, until he\l"
    .string "went in to speak with him.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_1::
    .string "And Moses gathered all the\n"
    .string "congregation of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel together, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "These are the words which the LORD\l"
    .string "hath commanded, that ye should do\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_2::
    .string "Six days shall work be done, but on\n"
    .string "the seventh day there shall be to\l"
    .string "you an holy day, a sabbath of rest to\l"
    .string "the LORD: whosoever doeth work\l"
    .string "therein shall be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_3::
    .string "Ye shall kindle no fire\n"
    .string "throughout your habitations upon\l"
    .string "the sabbath day.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_4::
    .string "And Moses spake unto all the\n"
    .string "congregation of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, saying, This is the thing\l"
    .string "which the LORD commanded, saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_5::
    .string "Take ye from among you an offering\n"
    .string "unto the LORD: whosoever is of a\l"
    .string "willing heart, let him bring it, an\l"
    .string "offering of the LORD; gold, and\l"
    .string "silver, and brass,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_6::
    .string "And blue, and purple, and\n"
    .string "scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’\l"
    .string "hair,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_7::
    .string "And rams’ skins dyed red, and\n"
    .string "badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_8::
    .string "And oil for the light, and spices\n"
    .string "for anointing oil, and for the sweet\l"
    .string "incense,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_9::
    .string "And onyx stones, and stones to be\n"
    .string "set for the ephod, and for the\l"
    .string "breastplate$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_10::
    .string "And every wise hearted among you\n"
    .string "shall come, and make all that the\l"
    .string "LORD hath commanded;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_11::
    .string "The tabernacle, his tent, and his\n"
    .string "covering, his taches, and his boards,\l"
    .string "his bars, his pillars, and his\l"
    .string "sockets,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_12::
    .string "The ark, and the staves thereof,\n"
    .string "with the mercy seat, and the vail of\l"
    .string "the covering,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_13::
    .string "The table, and his staves, and all\n"
    .string "his vessels, and the shewbread,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_14::
    .string "The candlestick also for the\n"
    .string "light, and his furniture, and his\l"
    .string "lamps, with the oil for the light,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_15::
    .string "And the incense altar, and his\n"
    .string "staves, and the anointing oil, and\l"
    .string "the sweet incense, and the hanging\l"
    .string "for the door at the entering in of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_16::
    .string "The altar of burnt offering, with\n"
    .string "his brasen grate, his staves, and\l"
    .string "all his vessels, the laver and his\l"
    .string "foot,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_17::
    .string "The hangings of the court, his\n"
    .string "pillars, and their sockets, and the\l"
    .string "hanging for the door of the court,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_18::
    .string "The pins of the tabernacle, and the\n"
    .string "pins of the court, and their cords,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_19::
    .string "The cloths of service, to do\n"
    .string "service in the holy place, the\l"
    .string "holy garments for Aaron the priest,\l"
    .string "and the garments of his sons, to\l"
    .string "minister in the priest’s office$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_20::
    .string "And all the congregation of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel departed from\l"
    .string "the presence of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_21::
    .string "And they came, every one whose heart\n"
    .string "stirred him up, and every one whom\l"
    .string "his spirit made willing, and they\l"
    .string "brought the LORD’s offering to the\l"
    .string "work of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and for all his\l"
    .string "service, and for the holy garments.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_22::
    .string "And they came, both men and women,\n"
    .string "as many as were willing hearted, and\l"
    .string "brought bracelets, and earrings, and\l"
    .string "rings, and tablets, all jewels of\l"
    .string "gold: and every man that offered\l"
    .string "offered an offering of gold unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_23::
    .string "And every man, with whom was found\n"
    .string "blue, and purple, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "fine linen, and goats’ hair, and red\l"
    .string "skins of rams, and badgers’ skins,\l"
    .string "brought them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_24::
    .string "Every one that did offer an offering\n"
    .string "of silver and brass brought the\l"
    .string "LORD’s offering: and every man, with\l"
    .string "whom was found shittim wood for any\l"
    .string "work of the service, brought it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_25::
    .string "And all the women that were wise\n"
    .string "hearted did spin with their hands,\l"
    .string "and brought that which they had\l"
    .string "spun, both of blue, and of purple,\l"
    .string "and of scarlet, and of fine linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_26::
    .string "And all the women whose heart\n"
    .string "stirred them up in wisdom spun\l"
    .string "goats’ hair.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_27::
    .string "And the rulers brought onyx stones,\n"
    .string "and stones to be set, for the ephod,\l"
    .string "and for the breastplate;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_28::
    .string "And spice, and oil for the light,\n"
    .string "and for the anointing oil, and for\l"
    .string "the sweet incense$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_29::
    .string "The children of Israel brought a\n"
    .string "willing offering unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "every man and woman, whose heart made\l"
    .string "them willing to bring for all\l"
    .string "manner of work, which the LORD had\l"
    .string "commanded to be made by the hand of\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_30::
    .string "And Moses said unto the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, See, the LORD hath called\l"
    .string "by name Bezaleel the son of Uri, the\l"
    .string "son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_31::
    .string "And he hath filled him with the\n"
    .string "spirit of God, in wisdom, in\l"
    .string "understanding, and in knowledge, and\l"
    .string "in all manner of workmanship;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_32::
    .string "And to devise curious works, to work\n"
    .string "in gold, and in silver, and in\l"
    .string "brass,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_33::
    .string "And in the cutting of stones, to set\n"
    .string "them, and in carving of wood, to make\l"
    .string "any manner of cunning work$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_34::
    .string "And he hath put in his heart that he\n"
    .string "may teach, both he, and Aholiab, the\l"
    .string "son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_35_35::
    .string "Them hath he filled with wisdom of\n"
    .string "heart, to work all manner of work,\l"
    .string "of the engraver, and of the cunning\l"
    .string "workman, and of the embroiderer, in\l"
    .string "blue, and in purple, in scarlet,\l"
    .string "and in fine linen, and of the weaver,\l"
    .string "even of them that do any work, and of\l"
    .string "those that devise cunning work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_1::
    .string "Then wrought Bezaleel and\n"
    .string "Aholiab, and every wise hearted man,\l"
    .string "in whom the LORD put wisdom and\l"
    .string "understanding to know how to work\l"
    .string "all manner of work for the service\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary, according to all\l"
    .string "that the LORD had commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_2::
    .string "And Moses called Bezaleel and\n"
    .string "Aholiab, and every wise hearted man,\l"
    .string "in whose heart the LORD had put\l"
    .string "wisdom, even every one whose heart\l"
    .string "stirred him up to come unto the work\l"
    .string "to do it:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_3::
    .string "And they received of Moses all the\n"
    .string "offering, which the children of\l"
    .string "Israel had brought for the work of\l"
    .string "the service of the sanctuary, to make\l"
    .string "it withal. And they brought yet unto\l"
    .string "him free offerings every morning$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_4::
    .string "And all the wise men, that wrought\n"
    .string "all the work of the sanctuary, came\l"
    .string "every man from his work which they\l"
    .string "made;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_5::
    .string "And they spake unto Moses, saying,\n"
    .string "The people bring much more than\l"
    .string "enough for the service of the work,\l"
    .string "which the LORD commanded to make$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_6::
    .string "And Moses gave commandment, and they\n"
    .string "caused it to be proclaimed\l"
    .string "throughout the camp, saying, Let\l"
    .string "neither man nor woman make any more\l"
    .string "work for the offering of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary. So the people were\l"
    .string "restrained from bringing.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_7::
    .string "For the stuff they had was\n"
    .string "sufficient for all the work to make\l"
    .string "it, and too much.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_8::
    .string "And every wise hearted man among\n"
    .string "them that wrought the work of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle made ten curtains of fine\l"
    .string "twined linen, and blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet: with\l"
    .string "cherubims of cunning work made he\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_9::
    .string "The length of one curtain was\n"
    .string "twenty and eight cubits, and the\l"
    .string "breadth of one curtain four cubits:\l"
    .string "the curtains were all of one size.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_10::
    .string "And he coupled the five curtains\n"
    .string "one unto another: and the other five\l"
    .string "curtains he coupled one unto\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_11::
    .string "And he made loops of blue on the\n"
    .string "edge of one curtain from the\l"
    .string "selvedge in the coupling: likewise\l"
    .string "he made in the uttermost side of\l"
    .string "another curtain, in the coupling of\l"
    .string "the second.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_12::
    .string "Fifty loops made he in one curtain,\n"
    .string "and fifty loops made he in the edge\l"
    .string "of the curtain which was in the\l"
    .string "coupling of the second: the loops\l"
    .string "held one curtain to another.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_13::
    .string "And he made fifty taches of gold,\n"
    .string "and coupled the curtains one unto\l"
    .string "another with the taches: so it became\l"
    .string "one tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_14::
    .string "And he made curtains of goats’ hair\n"
    .string "for the tent over the tabernacle:\l"
    .string "eleven curtains he made them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_15::
    .string "The length of one curtain was\n"
    .string "thirty cubits, and four cubits was\l"
    .string "the breadth of one curtain: the\l"
    .string "eleven curtains were of one size.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_16::
    .string "And he coupled five curtains by\n"
    .string "themselves, and six curtains by\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_17::
    .string "And he made fifty loops upon the\n"
    .string "uttermost edge of the curtain in the\l"
    .string "coupling, and fifty loops made he\l"
    .string "upon the edge of the curtain which\l"
    .string "coupleth the second.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_18::
    .string "And he made fifty taches of brass to\n"
    .string "couple the tent together, that it\l"
    .string "might be one.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_19::
    .string "And he made a covering for the tent\n"
    .string "of rams’ skins dyed red, and a\l"
    .string "covering of badgers’ skins above\l"
    .string "that.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_20::
    .string "And he made boards for the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of shittim wood, standing\l"
    .string "up.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_21::
    .string "The length of a board was ten\n"
    .string "cubits, and the breadth of a board\l"
    .string "one cubit and a half.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_22::
    .string "One board had two tenons, equally\n"
    .string "distant one from another: thus did he\l"
    .string "make for all the boards of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_23::
    .string "And he made boards for the\n"
    .string "tabernacle; twenty boards for the\l"
    .string "south side southward:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_24::
    .string "And forty sockets of silver he made\n"
    .string "under the twenty boards; two sockets\l"
    .string "under one board for his two tenons,\l"
    .string "and two sockets under another board\l"
    .string "for his two tenons$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_25::
    .string "And for the other side of the\n"
    .string "tabernacle, which is toward the\l"
    .string "north corner, he made twenty boards,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_26::
    .string "And their forty sockets of silver;\n"
    .string "two sockets under one board, and two\l"
    .string "sockets under another board$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_27::
    .string "And for the sides of the tabernacle\n"
    .string "westward he made six boards.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_28::
    .string "And two boards made he for the\n"
    .string "corners of the tabernacle in the two\l"
    .string "sides.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_29::
    .string "And they were coupled beneath, and\n"
    .string "coupled together at the head\l"
    .string "thereof, to one ring: thus he did to\l"
    .string "both of them in both the corners.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_30::
    .string "And there were eight boards; and\n"
    .string "their sockets were sixteen sockets\l"
    .string "of silver, under every board two\l"
    .string "sockets.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_31::
    .string "And he made bars of shittim wood;\n"
    .string "five for the boards of the one side\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_32::
    .string "And five bars for the boards of the\n"
    .string "other side of the tabernacle, and\l"
    .string "five bars for the boards of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle for the sides westward$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_33::
    .string "And he made the middle bar to shoot\n"
    .string "through the boards from the one end\l"
    .string "to the other.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_34::
    .string "And he overlaid the boards with\n"
    .string "gold, and made their rings of gold\l"
    .string "to be places for the bars, and\l"
    .string "overlaid the bars with gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_35::
    .string "And he made a vail of blue, and\n"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "twined linen: with cherubims made he\l"
    .string "it of cunning work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_36::
    .string "And he made thereunto four\n"
    .string "pillars of shittim wood, and\l"
    .string "overlaid them with gold: their\l"
    .string "hooks were of gold; and he cast for\l"
    .string "them four sockets of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_37::
    .string "And he made an hanging for the\n"
    .string "tabernacle door of blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "twined linen, of needlework;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_36_38::
    .string "And the five pillars of it with\n"
    .string "their hooks: and he overlaid their\l"
    .string "chapiters and their fillets with\l"
    .string "gold: but their five sockets were of\l"
    .string "brass$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_1::
    .string "And Bezaleel made the ark of\n"
    .string "shittim wood: two cubits and a half\l"
    .string "was the length of it, and a cubit and\l"
    .string "a half the breadth of it, and a cubit\l"
    .string "and a half the height of it:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_2::
    .string "And he overlaid it with pure gold\n"
    .string "within and without, and made a crown\l"
    .string "of gold to it round about$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_3::
    .string "And he cast for it four rings of\n"
    .string "gold, to be set by the four corners\l"
    .string "of it; even two rings upon the one\l"
    .string "side of it, and two rings upon the\l"
    .string "other side of it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_4::
    .string "And he made staves of shittim wood,\n"
    .string "and overlaid them with gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_5::
    .string "And he put the staves into the\n"
    .string "rings by the sides of the ark, to bear\l"
    .string "the ark.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_6::
    .string "And he made the mercy seat of pure\n"
    .string "gold: two cubits and a half was the\l"
    .string "length thereof, and one cubit and a\l"
    .string "half the breadth thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_7::
    .string "And he made two cherubims of gold,\n"
    .string "beaten out of one piece made he them,\l"
    .string "on the two ends of the mercy seat;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_8::
    .string "One cherub on the end on this side,\n"
    .string "and another cherub on the other end\l"
    .string "on that side: out of the mercy seat\l"
    .string "made he the cherubims on the two ends\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_9::
    .string "And the cherubims spread out their\n"
    .string "wings on high, and covered with their\l"
    .string "wings over the mercy seat, with their\l"
    .string "faces one to another; even to the\l"
    .string "mercy seatward were the faces of the\l"
    .string "cherubims.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_10::
    .string "And he made the table of shittim\n"
    .string "wood: two cubits was the length\l"
    .string "thereof, and a cubit the breadth\l"
    .string "thereof, and a cubit and a half the\l"
    .string "height thereof:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_11::
    .string "And he overlaid it with pure gold,\n"
    .string "and made thereunto a crown of gold\l"
    .string "round about$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_12::
    .string "Also he made thereunto a border of\n"
    .string "an handbreadth round about; and made\l"
    .string "a crown of gold for the border\l"
    .string "thereof round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_13::
    .string "And he cast for it four rings of\n"
    .string "gold, and put the rings upon the\l"
    .string "four corners that were in the four\l"
    .string "feet thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_14::
    .string "Over against the border were the\n"
    .string "rings, the places for the staves to\l"
    .string "bear the table.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_15::
    .string "And he made the staves of shittim\n"
    .string "wood, and overlaid them with gold,\l"
    .string "to bear the table.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_16::
    .string "And he made the vessels which were\n"
    .string "upon the table, his dishes, and his\l"
    .string "spoons, and his bowls, and his\l"
    .string "covers to cover withal, of pure\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_17::
    .string "And he made the candlestick of\n"
    .string "pure gold: of beaten work made he the\l"
    .string "candlestick; his shaft, and his\l"
    .string "branch, his bowls, his knops, and\l"
    .string "his flowers, were of the same:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_18::
    .string "And six branches going out of the\n"
    .string "sides thereof; three branches of the\l"
    .string "candlestick out of the one side\l"
    .string "thereof, and three branches of the\l"
    .string "candlestick out of the other side\l"
    .string "thereof:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_19::
    .string "Three bowls made after the fashion\n"
    .string "of almonds in one branch, a knop and\l"
    .string "a flower; and three bowls made like\l"
    .string "almonds in another branch, a knop\l"
    .string "and a flower: so throughout the six\l"
    .string "branches going out of the\l"
    .string "candlestick$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_20::
    .string "And in the candlestick were four\n"
    .string "bowls made like almonds, his\l"
    .string "knops, and his flowers:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_21::
    .string "And a knop under two branches of\n"
    .string "the same, and a knop under two\l"
    .string "branches of the same, and a knop\l"
    .string "under two branches of the same,\l"
    .string "according to the six branches going\l"
    .string "out of it$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_22::
    .string "Their knops and their branches were\n"
    .string "of the same: all of it was one\l"
    .string "beaten work of pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_23::
    .string "And he made his seven lamps, and\n"
    .string "his snuffers, and his snuffdishes, of\l"
    .string "pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_24::
    .string "Of a talent of pure gold made he\n"
    .string "it, and all the vessels thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_25::
    .string "And he made the incense altar of\n"
    .string "shittim wood: the length of it was a\l"
    .string "cubit, and the breadth of it a cubit;\l"
    .string "it was foursquare; and two cubits was\l"
    .string "the height of it; the horns thereof\l"
    .string "were of the same.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_26::
    .string "And he overlaid it with pure gold,\n"
    .string "both the top of it, and the sides\l"
    .string "thereof round about, and the horns of\l"
    .string "it: also he made unto it a crown of\l"
    .string "gold round about.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_27::
    .string "And he made two rings of gold for it\n"
    .string "under the crown thereof, by the two\l"
    .string "corners of it, upon the two sides\l"
    .string "thereof, to be places for the staves\l"
    .string "to bear it withal.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_28::
    .string "And he made the staves of shittim\n"
    .string "wood, and overlaid them with gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_37_29::
    .string "And he made the holy anointing oil,\n"
    .string "and the pure incense of sweet\l"
    .string "spices, according to the work of the\l"
    .string "apothecary.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_1::
    .string "And he made the altar of burnt\n"
    .string "offering of shittim wood: five cubits\l"
    .string "was the length thereof, and five\l"
    .string "cubits the breadth thereof; it was\l"
    .string "foursquare; and three cubits the\l"
    .string "height thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_2::
    .string "And he made the horns thereof on the\n"
    .string "four corners of it; the horns thereof\l"
    .string "were of the same: and he overlaid it\l"
    .string "with brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_3::
    .string "And he made all the vessels of the\n"
    .string "altar, the pots, and the shovels,\l"
    .string "and the basons, and the fleshhooks,\l"
    .string "and the firepans: all the vessels\l"
    .string "thereof made he of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_4::
    .string "And he made for the altar a brasen\n"
    .string "grate of network under the compass\l"
    .string "thereof beneath unto the midst of it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_5::
    .string "And he cast four rings for the four\n"
    .string "ends of the grate of brass, to be\l"
    .string "places for the staves.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_6::
    .string "And he made the staves of shittim\n"
    .string "wood, and overlaid them with brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_7::
    .string "And he put the staves into the\n"
    .string "rings on the sides of the altar, to\l"
    .string "bear it withal; he made the altar\l"
    .string "hollow with boards.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_8::
    .string "And he made the laver of brass, and\n"
    .string "the foot of it of brass, of the\l"
    .string "lookingglasses of the women\l"
    .string "assembling, which assembled at the\l"
    .string "door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_9::
    .string "And he made the court: on the south\n"
    .string "side southward the hangings of the\l"
    .string "court were of fine twined linen, an\l"
    .string "hundred cubits:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_10::
    .string "Their pillars were twenty, and\n"
    .string "their brasen sockets twenty; the\l"
    .string "hooks of the pillars and their\l"
    .string "fillets were of silver$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_11::
    .string "And for the north side the hangings\n"
    .string "were an hundred cubits, their\l"
    .string "pillars were twenty, and their\l"
    .string "sockets of brass twenty; the hooks of\l"
    .string "the pillars and their fillets of\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_12::
    .string "And for the west side were hangings\n"
    .string "of fifty cubits, their pillars ten,\l"
    .string "and their sockets ten; the hooks of\l"
    .string "the pillars and their fillets of\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_13::
    .string "And for the east side eastward fifty\n"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_14::
    .string "The hangings of the one side of the\n"
    .string "gate were fifteen cubits; their\l"
    .string "pillars three, and their sockets\l"
    .string "three.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_15::
    .string "And for the other side of the court\n"
    .string "gate, on this hand and that hand,\l"
    .string "were hangings of fifteen cubits;\l"
    .string "their pillars three, and their\l"
    .string "sockets three.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_16::
    .string "All the hangings of the court\n"
    .string "round about were of fine twined\l"
    .string "linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_17::
    .string "And the sockets for the pillars\n"
    .string "were of brass; the hooks of the\l"
    .string "pillars and their fillets of\l"
    .string "silver; and the overlaying of their\l"
    .string "chapiters of silver; and all the\l"
    .string "pillars of the court were filleted\l"
    .string "with silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_18::
    .string "And the hanging for the gate of the\n"
    .string "court was needlework, of blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "twined linen: and twenty cubits was\l"
    .string "the length, and the height in the\l"
    .string "breadth was five cubits, answerable\l"
    .string "to the hangings of the court.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_19::
    .string "And their pillars were four, and\n"
    .string "their sockets of brass four; their\l"
    .string "hooks of silver, and the overlaying\l"
    .string "of their chapiters and their\l"
    .string "fillets of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_20::
    .string "And all the pins of the\n"
    .string "tabernacle, and of the court round\l"
    .string "about, were of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_21::
    .string "This is the sum of the tabernacle,\n"
    .string "even of the tabernacle of testimony,\l"
    .string "as it was counted, according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of Moses, for the service\l"
    .string "of the Levites, by the hand of\l"
    .string "Ithamar, son to Aaron the priest.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_22::
    .string "And Bezaleel the son of Uri, the\n"
    .string "son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah,\l"
    .string "made all that the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_23::
    .string "And with him was Aholiab, son of\n"
    .string "Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan, an\l"
    .string "engraver, and a cunning workman, and\l"
    .string "an embroiderer in blue, and in\l"
    .string "purple, and in scarlet, and fine\l"
    .string "linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_24::
    .string "All the gold that was occupied\n"
    .string "for the work in all the work of the\l"
    .string "holy place, even the gold of the\l"
    .string "offering, was twenty and nine\l"
    .string "talents, and seven hundred and\l"
    .string "thirty shekels, after the shekel of\l"
    .string "the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_25::
    .string "And the silver of them that were\n"
    .string "numbered of the congregation was an\l"
    .string "hundred talents, and a thousand\l"
    .string "seven hundred and threescore and\l"
    .string "fifteen shekels, after the shekel\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_26::
    .string "A bekah for every man, that is, half\n"
    .string "a shekel, after the shekel of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, for every one that went to\l"
    .string "be numbered, from twenty years old\l"
    .string "and upward, for six hundred thousand\l"
    .string "and three thousand and five hundred\l"
    .string "and fifty men$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_27::
    .string "And of the hundred talents of\n"
    .string "silver were cast the sockets of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, and the sockets of the\l"
    .string "vail; an hundred sockets of the\l"
    .string "hundred talents, a talent for a\l"
    .string "socket.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_28::
    .string "And of the thousand seven hundred\n"
    .string "seventy and five shekels he made\l"
    .string "hooks for the pillars, and\l"
    .string "overlaid their chapiters, and\l"
    .string "filleted them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_29::
    .string "And the brass of the offering was\n"
    .string "seventy talents, and two thousand\l"
    .string "and four hundred shekels.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_30::
    .string "And therewith he made the sockets to\n"
    .string "the door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and the brasen altar,\l"
    .string "and the brasen grate for it, and all\l"
    .string "the vessels of the altar,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_38_31::
    .string "And the sockets of the court round\n"
    .string "about, and the sockets of the court\l"
    .string "gate, and all the pins of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and all the pins of\l"
    .string "the court round about$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_1::
    .string "And of the blue, and purple, and\n"
    .string "scarlet, they made cloths of\l"
    .string "service, to do service in the holy\l"
    .string "place, and made the holy garments\l"
    .string "for Aaron; as the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_2::
    .string "And he made the ephod of gold,\n"
    .string "blue, and purple, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "fine twined linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_3::
    .string "And they did beat the gold into\n"
    .string "thin plates, and cut it into wires,\l"
    .string "to work it in the blue, and in the\l"
    .string "purple, and in the scarlet, and in\l"
    .string "the fine linen, with cunning work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_4::
    .string "They made shoulderpieces for it,\n"
    .string "to couple it together: by the two\l"
    .string "edges was it coupled together.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_5::
    .string "And the curious girdle of his\n"
    .string "ephod, that was upon it, was of the\l"
    .string "same, according to the work thereof;\l"
    .string "of gold, blue, and purple, and\l"
    .string "scarlet, and fine twined linen; as\l"
    .string "the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_6::
    .string "And they wrought onyx stones\n"
    .string "inclosed in ouches of gold, graven,\l"
    .string "as signets are graven, with the names\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_7::
    .string "And he put them on the shoulders of\n"
    .string "the ephod, that they should be\l"
    .string "stones for a memorial to the\l"
    .string "children of Israel; as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_8::
    .string "And he made the breastplate of\n"
    .string "cunning work, like the work of the\l"
    .string "ephod; of gold, blue, and purple,\l"
    .string "and scarlet, and fine twined linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_9::
    .string "It was foursquare; they made the\n"
    .string "breastplate double: a span was the\l"
    .string "length thereof, and a span the\l"
    .string "breadth thereof, being doubled.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_10::
    .string "And they set in it four rows of\n"
    .string "stones: the first row was a sardius,\l"
    .string "a topaz, and a carbuncle: this was\l"
    .string "the first row.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_11::
    .string "And the second row, an emerald, a\n"
    .string "sapphire, and a diamond.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_12::
    .string "And the third row, a ligure, an\n"
    .string "agate, and an amethyst.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_13::
    .string "And the fourth row, a beryl, an\n"
    .string "onyx, and a jasper: they were\l"
    .string "inclosed in ouches of gold in their\l"
    .string "inclosings.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_14::
    .string "And the stones were according to the\n"
    .string "names of the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "twelve, according to their names,\l"
    .string "like the engravings of a signet,\l"
    .string "every one with his name, according to\l"
    .string "the twelve tribes.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_15::
    .string "And they made upon the\n"
    .string "breastplate chains at the ends, of\l"
    .string "wreathen work of pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_16::
    .string "And they made two ouches of gold,\n"
    .string "and two gold rings; and put the two\l"
    .string "rings in the two ends of the\l"
    .string "breastplate.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_17::
    .string "And they put the two wreathen\n"
    .string "chains of gold in the two rings on\l"
    .string "the ends of the breastplate.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_18::
    .string "And the two ends of the two wreathen\n"
    .string "chains they fastened in the two\l"
    .string "ouches, and put them on the\l"
    .string "shoulderpieces of the ephod,\l"
    .string "before it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_19::
    .string "And they made two rings of gold, and\n"
    .string "put them on the two ends of the\l"
    .string "breastplate, upon the border of it,\l"
    .string "which was on the side of the ephod\l"
    .string "inward.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_20::
    .string "And they made two other golden\n"
    .string "rings, and put them on the two sides\l"
    .string "of the ephod underneath, toward the\l"
    .string "forepart of it, over against the\l"
    .string "other coupling thereof, above the\l"
    .string "curious girdle of the ephod.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_21::
    .string "And they did bind the breastplate\n"
    .string "by his rings unto the rings of the\l"
    .string "ephod with a lace of blue, that it\l"
    .string "might be above the curious girdle of\l"
    .string "the ephod, and that the breastplate\l"
    .string "might not be loosed from the ephod;\l"
    .string "as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_22::
    .string "And he made the robe of the ephod of\n"
    .string "woven work, all of blue.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_23::
    .string "And there was an hole in the midst\n"
    .string "of the robe, as the hole of an\l"
    .string "habergeon, with a band round about\l"
    .string "the hole, that it should not rend.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_24::
    .string "And they made upon the hems of the\n"
    .string "robe pomegranates of blue, and\l"
    .string "purple, and scarlet, and twined\l"
    .string "linen.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_25::
    .string "And they made bells of pure gold,\n"
    .string "and put the bells between the\l"
    .string "pomegranates upon the hem of the\l"
    .string "robe, round about between the\l"
    .string "pomegranates;"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_26::
    .string "A bell and a pomegranate, a bell\n"
    .string "and a pomegranate, round about the\l"
    .string "hem of the robe to minister in; as the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_27::
    .string "And they made coats of fine linen\n"
    .string "of woven work for Aaron, and for his\l"
    .string "sons,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_28::
    .string "And a mitre of fine linen, and\n"
    .string "goodly bonnets of fine linen, and\l"
    .string "linen breeches of fine twined linen,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_29::
    .string "And a girdle of fine twined linen,\n"
    .string "and blue, and purple, and scarlet,\l"
    .string "of needlework; as the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_30::
    .string "And they made the plate of the\n"
    .string "holy crown of pure gold, and wrote\l"
    .string "upon it a writing, like to the\l"
    .string "engravings of a signet, HOLINESS TO\l"
    .string "THE LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_31::
    .string "And they tied unto it a lace of\n"
    .string "blue, to fasten it on high upon the\l"
    .string "mitre; as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_32::
    .string "Thus was all the work of the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the tent of the\l"
    .string "congregation finished: and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel did according to\l"
    .string "all that the LORD commanded Moses,\l"
    .string "so did they.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_33::
    .string "And they brought the tabernacle\n"
    .string "unto Moses, the tent, and all his\l"
    .string "furniture, his taches, his boards,\l"
    .string "his bars, and his pillars, and his\l"
    .string "sockets,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_34::
    .string "And the covering of rams’ skins dyed\n"
    .string "red, and the covering of badgers’\l"
    .string "skins, and the vail of the covering,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_35::
    .string "The ark of the testimony, and the\n"
    .string "staves thereof, and the mercy seat,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_36::
    .string "The table, and all the vessels\n"
    .string "thereof, and the shewbread,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_37::
    .string "The pure candlestick, with the\n"
    .string "lamps thereof, even with the lamps\l"
    .string "to be set in order, and all the\l"
    .string "vessels thereof, and the oil for\l"
    .string "light,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_38::
    .string "And the golden altar, and the\n"
    .string "anointing oil, and the sweet\l"
    .string "incense, and the hanging for the\l"
    .string "tabernacle door,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_39::
    .string "The brasen altar, and his grate of\n"
    .string "brass, his staves, and all his\l"
    .string "vessels, the laver and his foot,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_40::
    .string "The hangings of the court, his\n"
    .string "pillars, and his sockets, and the\l"
    .string "hanging for the court gate, his\l"
    .string "cords, and his pins, and all the\l"
    .string "vessels of the service of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, for the tent of the\l"
    .string "congregation,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_41::
    .string "The cloths of service to do service\n"
    .string "in the holy place, and the holy\l"
    .string "garments for Aaron the priest, and\l"
    .string "his sons’ garments, to minister in\l"
    .string "the priest’s office$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_42::
    .string "According to all that the LORD\n"
    .string "commanded Moses, so the children of\l"
    .string "Israel made all the work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_39_43::
    .string "And Moses did look upon all the\n"
    .string "work, and, behold, they had done it\l"
    .string "as the LORD had commanded, even so\l"
    .string "had they done it: and Moses blessed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_2::
    .string "On the first day of the first month\n"
    .string "shalt thou set up the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the tent of the congregation$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_3::
    .string "And thou shalt put therein the ark\n"
    .string "of the testimony, and cover the ark\l"
    .string "with the vail.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_4::
    .string "And thou shalt bring in the table,\n"
    .string "and set in order the things that are\l"
    .string "to be set in order upon it; and thou\l"
    .string "shalt bring in the candlestick, and\l"
    .string "light the lamps thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_5::
    .string "And thou shalt set the altar of\n"
    .string "gold for the incense before the ark\l"
    .string "of the testimony, and put the\l"
    .string "hanging of the door to the\l"
    .string "tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_6::
    .string "And thou shalt set the altar of the\n"
    .string "burnt offering before the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the tent of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_7::
    .string "And thou shalt set the laver\n"
    .string "between the tent of the congregation\l"
    .string "and the altar, and shalt put water\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_8::
    .string "And thou shalt set up the court\n"
    .string "round about, and hang up the hanging\l"
    .string "at the court gate.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_9::
    .string "And thou shalt take the anointing\n"
    .string "oil, and anoint the tabernacle, and\l"
    .string "all that is therein, and shalt\l"
    .string "hallow it, and all the vessels\l"
    .string "thereof: and it shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_10::
    .string "And thou shalt anoint the altar of\n"
    .string "the burnt offering, and all his\l"
    .string "vessels, and sanctify the altar:\l"
    .string "and it shall be an altar most holy.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_11::
    .string "And thou shalt anoint the laver\n"
    .string "and his foot, and sanctify it.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_12::
    .string "And thou shalt bring Aaron and his\n"
    .string "sons unto the door of the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation, and wash them\l"
    .string "with water.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_13::
    .string "And thou shalt put upon Aaron the\n"
    .string "holy garments, and anoint him, and\l"
    .string "sanctify him; that he may minister\l"
    .string "unto me in the priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_14::
    .string "And thou shalt bring his sons, and\n"
    .string "clothe them with coats:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_15::
    .string "And thou shalt anoint them, as thou\n"
    .string "didst anoint their father, that they\l"
    .string "may minister unto me in the priest’s\l"
    .string "office: for their anointing shall\l"
    .string "surely be an everlasting\l"
    .string "priesthood throughout their\l"
    .string "generations$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_16::
    .string "Thus did Moses: according to all\n"
    .string "that the LORD commanded him, so did\l"
    .string "he.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_17::
    .string "And it came to pass in the first\n"
    .string "month in the second year, on the\l"
    .string "first day of the month, that the\l"
    .string "tabernacle was reared up.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_18::
    .string "And Moses reared up the\n"
    .string "tabernacle, and fastened his\l"
    .string "sockets, and set up the boards\l"
    .string "thereof, and put in the bars\l"
    .string "thereof, and reared up his pillars.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_19::
    .string "And he spread abroad the tent over\n"
    .string "the tabernacle, and put the\l"
    .string "covering of the tent above upon it;\l"
    .string "as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_20::
    .string "And he took and put the testimony\n"
    .string "into the ark, and set the staves on\l"
    .string "the ark, and put the mercy seat above\l"
    .string "upon the ark:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_21::
    .string "And he brought the ark into the\n"
    .string "tabernacle, and set up the vail of\l"
    .string "the covering, and covered the ark of\l"
    .string "the testimony; as the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_22::
    .string "And he put the table in the tent of\n"
    .string "the congregation, upon the side of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle northward, without\l"
    .string "the vail.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_23::
    .string "And he set the bread in order upon\n"
    .string "it before the LORD; as the LORD had\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_24::
    .string "And he put the candlestick in the\n"
    .string "tent of the congregation, over\l"
    .string "against the table, on the side of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle southward.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_25::
    .string "And he lighted the lamps before\n"
    .string "the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_26::
    .string "And he put the golden altar in the\n"
    .string "tent of the congregation before the\l"
    .string "vail:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_27::
    .string "And he burnt sweet incense thereon;\n"
    .string "as the LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_28::
    .string "And he set up the hanging at the\n"
    .string "door of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_29::
    .string "And he put the altar of burnt\n"
    .string "offering by the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the tent of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and offered upon it\l"
    .string "the burnt offering and the meat\l"
    .string "offering; as the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_30::
    .string "And he set the laver between the\n"
    .string "tent of the congregation and the\l"
    .string "altar, and put water there, to wash\l"
    .string "withal.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_31::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron and his sons\n"
    .string "washed their hands and their feet\l"
    .string "thereat:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_32::
    .string "When they went into the tent of the\n"
    .string "congregation, and when they came near\l"
    .string "unto the altar, they washed; as the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_33::
    .string "And he reared up the court round\n"
    .string "about the tabernacle and the altar,\l"
    .string "and set up the hanging of the court\l"
    .string "gate. So Moses finished the work.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_34::
    .string "Then a cloud covered the tent of\n"
    .string "the congregation, and the glory of\l"
    .string "the LORD filled the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_35::
    .string "And Moses was not able to enter\n"
    .string "into the tent of the congregation,\l"
    .string "because the cloud abode thereon, and\l"
    .string "the glory of the LORD filled the\l"
    .string "tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_36::
    .string "And when the cloud was taken up\n"
    .string "from over the tabernacle, the\l"
    .string "children of Israel went onward in\l"
    .string "all their journeys:"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_37::
    .string "But if the cloud were not taken up,\n"
    .string "then they journeyed not till the\l"
    .string "day that it was taken up$"
Bible_Text_Exodus_40_38::
    .string "For the cloud of the LORD was upon\n"
    .string "the tabernacle by day, and fire was\l"
    .string "on it by night, in the sight of all\l"
    .string "the house of Israel, throughout all\l"
    .string "their journeys.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_1::
    .string "And the LORD called unto Moses, and\n"
    .string "spake unto him out of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, If any man of you\l"
    .string "bring an offering unto the LORD, ye\l"
    .string "shall bring your offering of the\l"
    .string "cattle, even of the herd, and of the\l"
    .string "flock$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_3::
    .string "If his offering be a burnt sacrifice\n"
    .string "of the herd, let him offer a male\l"
    .string "without blemish: he shall offer it\l"
    .string "of his own voluntary will at the\l"
    .string "door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_4::
    .string "And he shall put his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of the burnt offering; and\l"
    .string "it shall be accepted for him to\l"
    .string "make atonement for him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_5::
    .string "And he shall kill the bullock\n"
    .string "before the LORD: and the priests,\l"
    .string "Aaron’s sons, shall bring the\l"
    .string "blood, and sprinkle the blood\l"
    .string "round about upon the altar that is\l"
    .string "by the door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_6::
    .string "And he shall flay the burnt\n"
    .string "offering, and cut it into his pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_7::
    .string "And the sons of Aaron the priest\n"
    .string "shall put fire upon the altar, and\l"
    .string "lay the wood in order upon the fire:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_8::
    .string "And the priests, Aaron’s sons,\n"
    .string "shall lay the parts, the head, and\l"
    .string "the fat, in order upon the wood that\l"
    .string "is on the fire which is upon the\l"
    .string "altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_9::
    .string "But his inwards and his legs shall\n"
    .string "he wash in water: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall burn all on the altar, to be\l"
    .string "a burnt sacrifice, an offering made\l"
    .string "by fire, of a sweet savour unto the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_10::
    .string "And if his offering be of the\n"
    .string "flocks, namely, of the sheep, or of\l"
    .string "the goats, for a burnt sacrifice; he\l"
    .string "shall bring it a male without\l"
    .string "blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_11::
    .string "And he shall kill it on the side\n"
    .string "of the altar northward before the\l"
    .string "LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons,\l"
    .string "shall sprinkle his blood round\l"
    .string "about upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_12::
    .string "And he shall cut it into his\n"
    .string "pieces, with his head and his fat:\l"
    .string "and the priest shall lay them in\l"
    .string "order on the wood that is on the fire\l"
    .string "which is upon the altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_13::
    .string "But he shall wash the inwards and\n"
    .string "the legs with water: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall bring it all, and burn it\l"
    .string "upon the altar: it is a burnt\l"
    .string "sacrifice, an offering made by fire,\l"
    .string "of a sweet savour unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_14::
    .string "And if the burnt sacrifice for his\n"
    .string "offering to the LORD be of fowls,\l"
    .string "then he shall bring his offering of\l"
    .string "turtledoves, or of young pigeons.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_15::
    .string "And the priest shall bring it unto\n"
    .string "the altar, and wring off his head,\l"
    .string "and burn it on the altar; and the\l"
    .string "blood thereof shall be wrung out at\l"
    .string "the side of the altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_16::
    .string "And he shall pluck away his crop\n"
    .string "with his feathers, and cast it beside\l"
    .string "the altar on the east part, by the\l"
    .string "place of the ashes:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_1_17::
    .string "And he shall cleave it with the\n"
    .string "wings thereof, but shall not divide\l"
    .string "it asunder: and the priest shall\l"
    .string "burn it upon the altar, upon the\l"
    .string "wood that is upon the fire: it is a\l"
    .string "burnt sacrifice, an offering made by\l"
    .string "fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_1::
    .string "And when any will offer a meat\n"
    .string "offering unto the LORD, his offering\l"
    .string "shall be of fine flour; and he\l"
    .string "shall pour oil upon it, and put\l"
    .string "frankincense thereon:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_2::
    .string "And he shall bring it to Aaron’s\n"
    .string "sons the priests: and he shall take\l"
    .string "thereout his handful of the flour\l"
    .string "thereof, and of the oil thereof,\l"
    .string "with all the frankincense thereof;\l"
    .string "and the priest shall burn the\l"
    .string "memorial of it upon the altar, to\l"
    .string "be an offering made by fire, of a\l"
    .string "sweet savour unto the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_3::
    .string "And the remnant of the meat offering\n"
    .string "shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it\l"
    .string "is a thing most holy of the\l"
    .string "offerings of the LORD made by fire$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_4::
    .string "And if thou bring an oblation of a\n"
    .string "meat offering baken in the oven, it\l"
    .string "shall be unleavened cakes of fine\l"
    .string "flour mingled with oil, or\l"
    .string "unleavened wafers anointed with oil.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_5::
    .string "And if thy oblation be a meat\n"
    .string "offering baken in a pan, it shall\l"
    .string "be of fine flour unleavened,\l"
    .string "mingled with oil.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_6::
    .string "Thou shalt part it in pieces, and\n"
    .string "pour oil thereon: it is a meat\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_7::
    .string "And if thy oblation be a meat\n"
    .string "offering baken in the fryingpan, it\l"
    .string "shall be made of fine flour with\l"
    .string "oil.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_8::
    .string "And thou shalt bring the meat\n"
    .string "offering that is made of these things\l"
    .string "unto the LORD: and when it is\l"
    .string "presented unto the priest, he shall\l"
    .string "bring it unto the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_9::
    .string "And the priest shall take from the\n"
    .string "meat offering a memorial thereof,\l"
    .string "and shall burn it upon the altar:\l"
    .string "it is an offering made by fire, of a\l"
    .string "sweet savour unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_10::
    .string "And that which is left of the meat\n"
    .string "offering shall be Aaron’s and his\l"
    .string "sons’: it is a thing most holy of the\l"
    .string "offerings of the LORD made by fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_11::
    .string "No meat offering, which ye shall\n"
    .string "bring unto the LORD, shall be made\l"
    .string "with leaven: for ye shall burn no\l"
    .string "leaven, nor any honey, in any\l"
    .string "offering of the LORD made by fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_12::
    .string "As for the oblation of the\n"
    .string "firstfruits, ye shall offer them\l"
    .string "unto the LORD: but they shall not be\l"
    .string "burnt on the altar for a sweet\l"
    .string "savour.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_13::
    .string "And every oblation of thy meat\n"
    .string "offering shalt thou season with\l"
    .string "salt; neither shalt thou suffer the\l"
    .string "salt of the covenant of thy God to be\l"
    .string "lacking from thy meat offering: with\l"
    .string "all thine offerings thou shalt\l"
    .string "offer salt.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_14::
    .string "And if thou offer a meat offering of\n"
    .string "thy firstfruits unto the LORD, thou\l"
    .string "shalt offer for the meat offering of\l"
    .string "thy firstfruits green ears of corn\l"
    .string "dried by the fire, even corn beaten\l"
    .string "out of full ears.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_15::
    .string "And thou shalt put oil upon it,\n"
    .string "and lay frankincense thereon: it is\l"
    .string "a meat offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_2_16::
    .string "And the priest shall burn the\n"
    .string "memorial of it, part of the beaten\l"
    .string "corn thereof, and part of the oil\l"
    .string "thereof, with all the frankincense\l"
    .string "thereof: it is an offering made by\l"
    .string "fire unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_1::
    .string "And if his oblation be a sacrifice\n"
    .string "of peace offering, if he offer it of\l"
    .string "the herd; whether it be a male or\l"
    .string "female, he shall offer it without\l"
    .string "blemish before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_2::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of his offering, and kill\l"
    .string "it at the door of the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation: and Aaron’s sons\l"
    .string "the priests shall sprinkle the\l"
    .string "blood upon the altar round about.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_3::
    .string "And he shall offer of the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of the peace offering an\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD;\l"
    .string "the fat that covereth the inwards,\l"
    .string "and all the fat that is upon the\l"
    .string "inwards,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_4::
    .string "And the two kidneys, and the fat\n"
    .string "that is on them, which is by the\l"
    .string "flanks, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver, with the kidneys, it shall he\l"
    .string "take away$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_5::
    .string "And Aaron’s sons shall burn it on\n"
    .string "the altar upon the burnt sacrifice,\l"
    .string "which is upon the wood that is on the\l"
    .string "fire: it is an offering made by fire,\l"
    .string "of a sweet savour unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_6::
    .string "And if his offering for a sacrifice\n"
    .string "of peace offering unto the LORD be\l"
    .string "of the flock; male or female, he\l"
    .string "shall offer it without blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_7::
    .string "If he offer a lamb for his offering,\n"
    .string "then shall he offer it before the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_8::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of his offering, and kill\l"
    .string "it before the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation: and Aaron’s sons\l"
    .string "shall sprinkle the blood thereof\l"
    .string "round about upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_9::
    .string "And he shall offer of the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of the peace offering an\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD;\l"
    .string "the fat thereof, and the whole rump,\l"
    .string "it shall he take off hard by the\l"
    .string "backbone; and the fat that covereth\l"
    .string "the inwards, and all the fat that is\l"
    .string "upon the inwards,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_10::
    .string "And the two kidneys, and the fat\n"
    .string "that is upon them, which is by the\l"
    .string "flanks, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver, with the kidneys, it shall he\l"
    .string "take away$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_11::
    .string "And the priest shall burn it upon\n"
    .string "the altar: it is the food of the\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_12::
    .string "And if his offering be a goat, then\n"
    .string "he shall offer it before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_13::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of it, and kill it before\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation:\l"
    .string "and the sons of Aaron shall\l"
    .string "sprinkle the blood thereof upon\l"
    .string "the altar round about.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_14::
    .string "And he shall offer thereof his\n"
    .string "offering, even an offering made by\l"
    .string "fire unto the LORD; the fat that\l"
    .string "covereth the inwards, and all the\l"
    .string "fat that is upon the inwards,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_15::
    .string "And the two kidneys, and the fat\n"
    .string "that is upon them, which is by the\l"
    .string "flanks, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver, with the kidneys, it shall he\l"
    .string "take away$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_16::
    .string "And the priest shall burn them\n"
    .string "upon the altar: it is the food of\l"
    .string "the offering made by fire for a sweet\l"
    .string "savour: all the fat is the LORD’s.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_3_17::
    .string "It shall be a perpetual statute\n"
    .string "for your generations throughout all\l"
    .string "your dwellings, that ye eat neither\l"
    .string "fat nor blood.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, If a soul shall sin through\l"
    .string "ignorance against any of the\l"
    .string "commandments of the LORD concerning\l"
    .string "things which ought not to be done,\l"
    .string "and shall do against any of them:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_3::
    .string "If the priest that is anointed do\n"
    .string "sin according to the sin of the\l"
    .string "people; then let him bring for his\l"
    .string "sin, which he hath sinned, a young\l"
    .string "bullock without blemish unto the\l"
    .string "LORD for a sin offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_4::
    .string "And he shall bring the bullock\n"
    .string "unto the door of the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation before the LORD; and\l"
    .string "shall lay his hand upon the\l"
    .string "bullock’s head, and kill the\l"
    .string "bullock before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_5::
    .string "And the priest that is anointed\n"
    .string "shall take of the bullock’s\l"
    .string "blood, and bring it to the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_6::
    .string "And the priest shall dip his\n"
    .string "finger in the blood, and sprinkle\l"
    .string "of the blood seven times before the\l"
    .string "LORD, before the vail of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_7::
    .string "And the priest shall put some of\n"
    .string "the blood upon the horns of the\l"
    .string "altar of sweet incense before the\l"
    .string "LORD, which is in the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation; and shall pour\l"
    .string "all the blood of the bullock at\l"
    .string "the bottom of the altar of the burnt\l"
    .string "offering, which is at the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_8::
    .string "And he shall take off from it all\n"
    .string "the fat of the bullock for the sin\l"
    .string "offering; the fat that covereth the\l"
    .string "inwards, and all the fat that is\l"
    .string "upon the inwards,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_9::
    .string "And the two kidneys, and the fat\n"
    .string "that is upon them, which is by the\l"
    .string "flanks, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver, with the kidneys, it shall he\l"
    .string "take away,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_10::
    .string "As it was taken off from the\n"
    .string "bullock of the sacrifice of peace\l"
    .string "offerings: and the priest shall\l"
    .string "burn them upon the altar of the\l"
    .string "burnt offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_11::
    .string "And the skin of the bullock, and\n"
    .string "all his flesh, with his head, and\l"
    .string "with his legs, and his inwards, and\l"
    .string "his dung,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_12::
    .string "Even the whole bullock shall he\n"
    .string "carry forth without the camp unto a\l"
    .string "clean place, where the ashes are\l"
    .string "poured out, and burn him on the wood\l"
    .string "with fire: where the ashes are\l"
    .string "poured out shall he be burnt$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_13::
    .string "And if the whole congregation of\n"
    .string "Israel sin through ignorance, and\l"
    .string "the thing be hid from the eyes of the\l"
    .string "assembly, and they have done\l"
    .string "somewhat against any of the\l"
    .string "commandments of the LORD concerning\l"
    .string "things which should not be done, and\l"
    .string "are guilty;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_14::
    .string "When the sin, which they have sinned\n"
    .string "against it, is known, then the\l"
    .string "congregation shall offer a young\l"
    .string "bullock for the sin, and bring him\l"
    .string "before the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_15::
    .string "And the elders of the congregation\n"
    .string "shall lay their hands upon the\l"
    .string "head of the bullock before the LORD:\l"
    .string "and the bullock shall be killed\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_16::
    .string "And the priest that is anointed\n"
    .string "shall bring of the bullock’s\l"
    .string "blood to the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_17::
    .string "And the priest shall dip his\n"
    .string "finger in some of the blood, and\l"
    .string "sprinkle it seven times before the\l"
    .string "LORD, even before the vail$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_18::
    .string "And he shall put some of the\n"
    .string "blood upon the horns of the altar\l"
    .string "which is before the LORD, that is in\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "and shall pour out all the blood\l"
    .string "at the bottom of the altar of the\l"
    .string "burnt offering, which is at the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_19::
    .string "And he shall take all his fat\n"
    .string "from him, and burn it upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_20::
    .string "And he shall do with the bullock\n"
    .string "as he did with the bullock for a sin\l"
    .string "offering, so shall he do with this:\l"
    .string "and the priest shall make an\l"
    .string "atonement for them, and it shall be\l"
    .string "forgiven them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_21::
    .string "And he shall carry forth the\n"
    .string "bullock without the camp, and burn\l"
    .string "him as he burned the first bullock:\l"
    .string "it is a sin offering for the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_22::
    .string "When a ruler hath sinned, and done\n"
    .string "somewhat through ignorance against\l"
    .string "any of the commandments of the LORD\l"
    .string "his God concerning things which\l"
    .string "should not be done, and is guilty;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_23::
    .string "Or if his sin, wherein he hath\n"
    .string "sinned, come to his knowledge; he\l"
    .string "shall bring his offering, a kid of\l"
    .string "the goats, a male without blemish:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_24::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of the goat, and kill it in\l"
    .string "the place where they kill the\l"
    .string "burnt offering before the LORD: it is\l"
    .string "a sin offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_25::
    .string "And the priest shall take of the\n"
    .string "blood of the sin offering with his\l"
    .string "finger, and put it upon the horns of\l"
    .string "the altar of burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "shall pour out his blood at the\l"
    .string "bottom of the altar of burnt\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_26::
    .string "And he shall burn all his fat\n"
    .string "upon the altar, as the fat of the\l"
    .string "sacrifice of peace offerings: and\l"
    .string "the priest shall make an atonement\l"
    .string "for him as concerning his sin, and it\l"
    .string "shall be forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_27::
    .string "And if any one of the common\n"
    .string "people sin through ignorance,\l"
    .string "while he doeth somewhat against any\l"
    .string "of the commandments of the LORD\l"
    .string "concerning things which ought not to\l"
    .string "be done, and be guilty;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_28::
    .string "Or if his sin, which he hath sinned,\n"
    .string "come to his knowledge: then he\l"
    .string "shall bring his offering, a kid of\l"
    .string "the goats, a female without\l"
    .string "blemish, for his sin which he hath\l"
    .string "sinned$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_29::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of the sin offering, and\l"
    .string "slay the sin offering in the place\l"
    .string "of the burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_30::
    .string "And the priest shall take of the\n"
    .string "blood thereof with his finger, and\l"
    .string "put it upon the horns of the altar\l"
    .string "of burnt offering, and shall pour\l"
    .string "out all the blood thereof at the\l"
    .string "bottom of the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_31::
    .string "And he shall take away all the\n"
    .string "fat thereof, as the fat is taken away\l"
    .string "from off the sacrifice of peace\l"
    .string "offerings; and the priest shall\l"
    .string "burn it upon the altar for a sweet\l"
    .string "savour unto the LORD; and the priest\l"
    .string "shall make an atonement for him, and\l"
    .string "it shall be forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_32::
    .string "And if he bring a lamb for a sin\n"
    .string "offering, he shall bring it a\l"
    .string "female without blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_33::
    .string "And he shall lay his hand upon\n"
    .string "the head of the sin offering, and\l"
    .string "slay it for a sin offering in the\l"
    .string "place where they kill the burnt\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_34::
    .string "And the priest shall take of the\n"
    .string "blood of the sin offering with his\l"
    .string "finger, and put it upon the horns of\l"
    .string "the altar of burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "shall pour out all the blood\l"
    .string "thereof at the bottom of the altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_4_35::
    .string "And he shall take away all the\n"
    .string "fat thereof, as the fat of the lamb\l"
    .string "is taken away from the sacrifice of\l"
    .string "the peace offerings; and the priest\l"
    .string "shall burn them upon the altar,\l"
    .string "according to the offerings made by\l"
    .string "fire unto the LORD: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall make an atonement for his sin\l"
    .string "that he hath committed, and it shall\l"
    .string "be forgiven him$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_1::
    .string "And if a soul sin, and hear the\n"
    .string "voice of swearing, and is a witness,\l"
    .string "whether he hath seen or known of it;\l"
    .string "if he do not utter it, then he shall\l"
    .string "bear his iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_2::
    .string "Or if a soul touch any unclean\n"
    .string "thing, whether it be a carcase of an\l"
    .string "unclean beast, or a carcase of\l"
    .string "unclean cattle, or the carcase of\l"
    .string "unclean creeping things, and if it\l"
    .string "be hidden from him; he also shall\l"
    .string "be unclean, and guilty.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_3::
    .string "Or if he touch the uncleanness of\n"
    .string "man, whatsoever uncleanness it be\l"
    .string "that a man shall be defiled\l"
    .string "withal, and it be hid from him; when\l"
    .string "he knoweth of it, then he shall be\l"
    .string "guilty.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_4::
    .string "Or if a soul swear, pronouncing\n"
    .string "with his lips to do evil, or to do\l"
    .string "good, whatsoever it be that a man\l"
    .string "shall pronounce with an oath, and\l"
    .string "it be hid from him; when he knoweth of\l"
    .string "it, then he shall be guilty in one\l"
    .string "of these.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_5::
    .string "And it shall be, when he shall be\n"
    .string "guilty in one of these things, that\l"
    .string "he shall confess that he hath\l"
    .string "sinned in that thing:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_6::
    .string "And he shall bring his trespass\n"
    .string "offering unto the LORD for his sin\l"
    .string "which he hath sinned, a female from\l"
    .string "the flock, a lamb or a kid of the\l"
    .string "goats, for a sin offering; and the\l"
    .string "priest shall make an atonement for\l"
    .string "him concerning his sin$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_7::
    .string "And if he be not able to bring a\n"
    .string "lamb, then he shall bring for his\l"
    .string "trespass, which he hath committed,\l"
    .string "two turtledoves, or two young\l"
    .string "pigeons, unto the LORD; one for a sin\l"
    .string "offering, and the other for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_8::
    .string "And he shall bring them unto the\n"
    .string "priest, who shall offer that which\l"
    .string "is for the sin offering first, and\l"
    .string "wring off his head from his neck, but\l"
    .string "shall not divide it asunder:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_9::
    .string "And he shall sprinkle of the\n"
    .string "blood of the sin offering upon the\l"
    .string "side of the altar; and the rest of\l"
    .string "the blood shall be wrung out at the\l"
    .string "bottom of the altar: it is a sin\l"
    .string "offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_10::
    .string "And he shall offer the second for a\n"
    .string "burnt offering, according to the\l"
    .string "manner: and the priest shall make\l"
    .string "an atonement for him for his sin\l"
    .string "which he hath sinned, and it shall\l"
    .string "be forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_11::
    .string "But if he be not able to bring two\n"
    .string "turtledoves, or two young pigeons,\l"
    .string "then he that sinned shall bring for\l"
    .string "his offering the tenth part of an\l"
    .string "ephah of fine flour for a sin\l"
    .string "offering; he shall put no oil upon\l"
    .string "it, neither shall he put any\l"
    .string "frankincense thereon: for it is a sin\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_12::
    .string "Then shall he bring it to the\n"
    .string "priest, and the priest shall take\l"
    .string "his handful of it, even a memorial\l"
    .string "thereof, and burn it on the altar,\l"
    .string "according to the offerings made by\l"
    .string "fire unto the LORD: it is a sin\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_13::
    .string "And the priest shall make an\n"
    .string "atonement for him as touching his sin\l"
    .string "that he hath sinned in one of these,\l"
    .string "and it shall be forgiven him: and\l"
    .string "the remnant shall be the priest’s,\l"
    .string "as a meat offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_14::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_15::
    .string "If a soul commit a trespass, and\n"
    .string "sin through ignorance, in the holy\l"
    .string "things of the LORD; then he shall\l"
    .string "bring for his trespass unto the LORD\l"
    .string "a ram without blemish out of the\l"
    .string "flocks, with thy estimation by\l"
    .string "shekels of silver, after the shekel\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary, for a trespass\l"
    .string "offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_16::
    .string "And he shall make amends for the\n"
    .string "harm that he hath done in the holy\l"
    .string "thing, and shall add the fifth part\l"
    .string "thereto, and give it unto the\l"
    .string "priest: and the priest shall make\l"
    .string "an atonement for him with the ram of\l"
    .string "the trespass offering, and it shall\l"
    .string "be forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_17::
    .string "And if a soul sin, and commit any of\n"
    .string "these things which are forbidden to\l"
    .string "be done by the commandments of the\l"
    .string "LORD; though he wist it not, yet is he\l"
    .string "guilty, and shall bear his\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_18::
    .string "And he shall bring a ram without\n"
    .string "blemish out of the flock, with thy\l"
    .string "estimation, for a trespass offering,\l"
    .string "unto the priest: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall make an atonement for him\l"
    .string "concerning his ignorance wherein he\l"
    .string "erred and wist it not, and it shall\l"
    .string "be forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_5_19::
    .string "It is a trespass offering: he hath\n"
    .string "certainly trespassed against the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_2::
    .string "If a soul sin, and commit a\n"
    .string "trespass against the LORD, and lie\l"
    .string "unto his neighbour in that which was\l"
    .string "delivered him to keep, or in\l"
    .string "fellowship, or in a thing taken\l"
    .string "away by violence, or hath deceived\l"
    .string "his neighbour;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_3::
    .string "Or have found that which was lost,\n"
    .string "and lieth concerning it, and\l"
    .string "sweareth falsely; in any of all\l"
    .string "these that a man doeth, sinning\l"
    .string "therein:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_4::
    .string "Then it shall be, because he hath\n"
    .string "sinned, and is guilty, that he\l"
    .string "shall restore that which he took\l"
    .string "violently away, or the thing which\l"
    .string "he hath deceitfully gotten, or that\l"
    .string "which was delivered him to keep, or\l"
    .string "the lost thing which he found,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_5::
    .string "Or all that about which he hath\n"
    .string "sworn falsely; he shall even\l"
    .string "restore it in the principal, and\l"
    .string "shall add the fifth part more\l"
    .string "thereto, and give it unto him to whom\l"
    .string "it appertaineth, in the day of his\l"
    .string "trespass offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_6::
    .string "And he shall bring his trespass\n"
    .string "offering unto the LORD, a ram without\l"
    .string "blemish out of the flock, with thy\l"
    .string "estimation, for a trespass offering,\l"
    .string "unto the priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_7::
    .string "And the priest shall make an\n"
    .string "atonement for him before the LORD:\l"
    .string "and it shall be forgiven him for any\l"
    .string "thing of all that he hath done in\l"
    .string "trespassing therein$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_8::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_9::
    .string "Command Aaron and his sons, saying,\n"
    .string "This is the law of the burnt\l"
    .string "offering: It is the burnt offering,\l"
    .string "because of the burning upon the\l"
    .string "altar all night unto the morning,\l"
    .string "and the fire of the altar shall be\l"
    .string "burning in it$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_10::
    .string "And the priest shall put on his\n"
    .string "linen garment, and his linen\l"
    .string "breeches shall he put upon his\l"
    .string "flesh, and take up the ashes which\l"
    .string "the fire hath consumed with the burnt\l"
    .string "offering on the altar, and he shall\l"
    .string "put them beside the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_11::
    .string "And he shall put off his garments,\n"
    .string "and put on other garments, and carry\l"
    .string "forth the ashes without the camp\l"
    .string "unto a clean place.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_12::
    .string "And the fire upon the altar shall\n"
    .string "be burning in it; it shall not be\l"
    .string "put out: and the priest shall burn\l"
    .string "wood on it every morning, and lay the\l"
    .string "burnt offering in order upon it; and\l"
    .string "he shall burn thereon the fat of the\l"
    .string "peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_13::
    .string "The fire shall ever be burning\n"
    .string "upon the altar; it shall never go\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_14::
    .string "And this is the law of the meat\n"
    .string "offering: the sons of Aaron shall\l"
    .string "offer it before the LORD, before the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_15::
    .string "And he shall take of it his\n"
    .string "handful, of the flour of the meat\l"
    .string "offering, and of the oil thereof,\l"
    .string "and all the frankincense which is\l"
    .string "upon the meat offering, and shall\l"
    .string "burn it upon the altar for a sweet\l"
    .string "savour, even the memorial of it,\l"
    .string "unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_16::
    .string "And the remainder thereof shall\n"
    .string "Aaron and his sons eat: with\l"
    .string "unleavened bread shall it be eaten\l"
    .string "in the holy place; in the court of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation\l"
    .string "they shall eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_17::
    .string "It shall not be baken with leaven.\n"
    .string "I have given it unto them for their\l"
    .string "portion of my offerings made by fire;\l"
    .string "it is most holy, as is the sin\l"
    .string "offering, and as the trespass\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_18::
    .string "All the males among the children\n"
    .string "of Aaron shall eat of it. It shall\l"
    .string "be a statute for ever in your\l"
    .string "generations concerning the offerings\l"
    .string "of the LORD made by fire: every one\l"
    .string "that toucheth them shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_19::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_20::
    .string "This is the offering of Aaron and of\n"
    .string "his sons, which they shall offer\l"
    .string "unto the LORD in the day when he is\l"
    .string "anointed; the tenth part of an ephah\l"
    .string "of fine flour for a meat offering\l"
    .string "perpetual, half of it in the\l"
    .string "morning, and half thereof at night$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_21::
    .string "In a pan it shall be made with\n"
    .string "oil; and when it is baken, thou\l"
    .string "shalt bring it in: and the baken\l"
    .string "pieces of the meat offering shalt\l"
    .string "thou offer for a sweet savour unto\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_22::
    .string "And the priest of his sons that is\n"
    .string "anointed in his stead shall offer\l"
    .string "it: it is a statute for ever unto the\l"
    .string "LORD; it shall be wholly burnt.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_23::
    .string "For every meat offering for the\n"
    .string "priest shall be wholly burnt: it\l"
    .string "shall not be eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_24::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_25::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron and to his sons,\n"
    .string "saying, This is the law of the sin\l"
    .string "offering: In the place where the\l"
    .string "burnt offering is killed shall the\l"
    .string "sin offering be killed before the\l"
    .string "LORD: it is most holy$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_26::
    .string "The priest that offereth it for sin\n"
    .string "shall eat it: in the holy place\l"
    .string "shall it be eaten, in the court of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_27::
    .string "Whatsoever shall touch the flesh\n"
    .string "thereof shall be holy: and when\l"
    .string "there is sprinkled of the blood\l"
    .string "thereof upon any garment, thou\l"
    .string "shalt wash that whereon it was\l"
    .string "sprinkled in the holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_28::
    .string "But the earthen vessel wherein it\n"
    .string "is sodden shall be broken: and if it\l"
    .string "be sodden in a brasen pot, it shall\l"
    .string "be both scoured, and rinsed in water.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_29::
    .string "All the males among the priests\n"
    .string "shall eat thereof: it is most holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_6_30::
    .string "And no sin offering, whereof any of\n"
    .string "the blood is brought into the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation to\l"
    .string "reconcile withal in the holy\l"
    .string "place, shall be eaten: it shall be\l"
    .string "burnt in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_1::
    .string "Likewise this is the law of the\n"
    .string "trespass offering: it is most holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_2::
    .string "In the place where they kill the\n"
    .string "burnt offering shall they kill the\l"
    .string "trespass offering: and the blood\l"
    .string "thereof shall he sprinkle round\l"
    .string "about upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_3::
    .string "And he shall offer of it all the\n"
    .string "fat thereof; the rump, and the fat\l"
    .string "that covereth the inwards,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_4::
    .string "And the two kidneys, and the fat\n"
    .string "that is on them, which is by the\l"
    .string "flanks, and the caul that is above\l"
    .string "the liver, with the kidneys, it\l"
    .string "shall he take away:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_5::
    .string "And the priest shall burn them\n"
    .string "upon the altar for an offering made\l"
    .string "by fire unto the LORD: it is a\l"
    .string "trespass offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_6::
    .string "Every male among the priests\n"
    .string "shall eat thereof: it shall be\l"
    .string "eaten in the holy place: it is most\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_7::
    .string "As the sin offering is, so is the\n"
    .string "trespass offering: there is one law\l"
    .string "for them: the priest that maketh\l"
    .string "atonement therewith shall have it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_8::
    .string "And the priest that offereth any\n"
    .string "man’s burnt offering, even the\l"
    .string "priest shall have to himself the\l"
    .string "skin of the burnt offering which he\l"
    .string "hath offered.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_9::
    .string "And all the meat offering that is\n"
    .string "baken in the oven, and all that is\l"
    .string "dressed in the fryingpan, and in the\l"
    .string "pan, shall be the priest’s that\l"
    .string "offereth it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_10::
    .string "And every meat offering, mingled\n"
    .string "with oil, and dry, shall all the\l"
    .string "sons of Aaron have, one as much as\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_11::
    .string "And this is the law of the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of peace offerings, which\l"
    .string "he shall offer unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_12::
    .string "If he offer it for a thanksgiving,\n"
    .string "then he shall offer with the\l"
    .string "sacrifice of thanksgiving\l"
    .string "unleavened cakes mingled with oil,\l"
    .string "and unleavened wafers anointed with\l"
    .string "oil, and cakes mingled with oil, of\l"
    .string "fine flour, fried.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_13::
    .string "Besides the cakes, he shall offer\n"
    .string "for his offering leavened bread with\l"
    .string "the sacrifice of thanksgiving of his\l"
    .string "peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_14::
    .string "And of it he shall offer one out of\n"
    .string "the whole oblation for an heave\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD, and it shall\l"
    .string "be the priest’s that sprinkleth\l"
    .string "the blood of the peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_15::
    .string "And the flesh of the sacrifice of\n"
    .string "his peace offerings for\l"
    .string "thanksgiving shall be eaten the\l"
    .string "same day that it is offered; he\l"
    .string "shall not leave any of it until\l"
    .string "the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_16::
    .string "But if the sacrifice of his offering\n"
    .string "be a vow, or a voluntary offering, it\l"
    .string "shall be eaten the same day that he\l"
    .string "offereth his sacrifice: and on the\l"
    .string "morrow also the remainder of it\l"
    .string "shall be eaten:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_17::
    .string "But the remainder of the flesh of\n"
    .string "the sacrifice on the third day\l"
    .string "shall be burnt with fire$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_18::
    .string "And if any of the flesh of the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of his peace offerings be\l"
    .string "eaten at all on the third day, it\l"
    .string "shall not be accepted, neither\l"
    .string "shall it be imputed unto him that\l"
    .string "offereth it: it shall be an\l"
    .string "abomination, and the soul that\l"
    .string "eateth of it shall bear his\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_19::
    .string "And the flesh that toucheth any\n"
    .string "unclean thing shall not be eaten;\l"
    .string "it shall be burnt with fire: and as\l"
    .string "for the flesh, all that be clean\l"
    .string "shall eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_20::
    .string "But the soul that eateth of the\n"
    .string "flesh of the sacrifice of peace\l"
    .string "offerings, that pertain unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, having his uncleanness upon\l"
    .string "him, even that soul shall be cut\l"
    .string "off from his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_21::
    .string "Moreover the soul that shall\n"
    .string "touch any unclean thing, as the\l"
    .string "uncleanness of man, or any unclean\l"
    .string "beast, or any abominable unclean\l"
    .string "thing, and eat of the flesh of the\l"
    .string "sacrifice of peace offerings, which\l"
    .string "pertain unto the LORD, even that\l"
    .string "soul shall be cut off from his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_22::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_23::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, Ye shall eat no manner of\l"
    .string "fat, of ox, or of sheep, or of goat$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_24::
    .string "And the fat of the beast that dieth\n"
    .string "of itself, and the fat of that which\l"
    .string "is torn with beasts, may be used in\l"
    .string "any other use: but ye shall in no\l"
    .string "wise eat of it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_25::
    .string "For whosoever eateth the fat of the\n"
    .string "beast, of which men offer an offering\l"
    .string "made by fire unto the LORD, even the\l"
    .string "soul that eateth it shall be cut\l"
    .string "off from his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_26::
    .string "Moreover ye shall eat no manner of\n"
    .string "blood, whether it be of fowl or of\l"
    .string "beast, in any of your dwellings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_27::
    .string "Whatsoever soul it be that eateth\n"
    .string "any manner of blood, even that soul\l"
    .string "shall be cut off from his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_28::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_29::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, He that offereth the\l"
    .string "sacrifice of his peace offerings\l"
    .string "unto the LORD shall bring his\l"
    .string "oblation unto the LORD of the\l"
    .string "sacrifice of his peace offerings$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_30::
    .string "His own hands shall bring the\n"
    .string "offerings of the LORD made by fire,\l"
    .string "the fat with the breast, it shall he\l"
    .string "bring, that the breast may be waved\l"
    .string "for a wave offering before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_31::
    .string "And the priest shall burn the fat\n"
    .string "upon the altar: but the breast\l"
    .string "shall be Aaron’s and his sons’.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_32::
    .string "And the right shoulder shall ye\n"
    .string "give unto the priest for an heave\l"
    .string "offering of the sacrifices of your\l"
    .string "peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_33::
    .string "He among the sons of Aaron, that\n"
    .string "offereth the blood of the peace\l"
    .string "offerings, and the fat, shall have\l"
    .string "the right shoulder for his part.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_34::
    .string "For the wave breast and the heave\n"
    .string "shoulder have I taken of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel from off the\l"
    .string "sacrifices of their peace offerings,\l"
    .string "and have given them unto Aaron the\l"
    .string "priest and unto his sons by a statute\l"
    .string "for ever from among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_35::
    .string "This is the portion of the\n"
    .string "anointing of Aaron, and of the\l"
    .string "anointing of his sons, out of the\l"
    .string "offerings of the LORD made by fire,\l"
    .string "in the day when he presented them to\l"
    .string "minister unto the LORD in the\l"
    .string "priest’s office;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_36::
    .string "Which the LORD commanded to be given\n"
    .string "them of the children of Israel, in\l"
    .string "the day that he anointed them, by a\l"
    .string "statute for ever throughout their\l"
    .string "generations$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_37::
    .string "This is the law of the burnt\n"
    .string "offering, of the meat offering, and\l"
    .string "of the sin offering, and of the\l"
    .string "trespass offering, and of the\l"
    .string "consecrations, and of the sacrifice\l"
    .string "of the peace offerings;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_7_38::
    .string "Which the LORD commanded Moses in\n"
    .string "mount Sinai, in the day that he\l"
    .string "commanded the children of Israel to\l"
    .string "offer their oblations unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "in the wilderness of Sinai$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_2::
    .string "Take Aaron and his sons with him,\n"
    .string "and the garments, and the anointing\l"
    .string "oil, and a bullock for the sin\l"
    .string "offering, and two rams, and a basket\l"
    .string "of unleavened bread;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_3::
    .string "And gather thou all the\n"
    .string "congregation together unto the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_4::
    .string "And Moses did as the LORD commanded\n"
    .string "him; and the assembly was gathered\l"
    .string "together unto the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_5::
    .string "And Moses said unto the\n"
    .string "congregation, This is the thing which\l"
    .string "the LORD commanded to be done.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_6::
    .string "And Moses brought Aaron and his\n"
    .string "sons, and washed them with water.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_7::
    .string "And he put upon him the coat, and\n"
    .string "girded him with the girdle, and\l"
    .string "clothed him with the robe, and put\l"
    .string "the ephod upon him, and he girded\l"
    .string "him with the curious girdle of the\l"
    .string "ephod, and bound it unto him\l"
    .string "therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_8::
    .string "And he put the breastplate upon\n"
    .string "him: also he put in the\l"
    .string "breastplate the Urim and the\l"
    .string "Thummim.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_9::
    .string "And he put the mitre upon his head;\n"
    .string "also upon the mitre, even upon his\l"
    .string "forefront, did he put the golden\l"
    .string "plate, the holy crown; as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_10::
    .string "And Moses took the anointing oil,\n"
    .string "and anointed the tabernacle and\l"
    .string "all that was therein, and\l"
    .string "sanctified them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_11::
    .string "And he sprinkled thereof upon the\n"
    .string "altar seven times, and anointed the\l"
    .string "altar and all his vessels, both\l"
    .string "the laver and his foot, to sanctify\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_12::
    .string "And he poured of the anointing oil\n"
    .string "upon Aaron’s head, and anointed him,\l"
    .string "to sanctify him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_13::
    .string "And Moses brought Aaron’s sons, and\n"
    .string "put coats upon them, and girded them\l"
    .string "with girdles, and put bonnets upon\l"
    .string "them; as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_14::
    .string "And he brought the bullock for the\n"
    .string "sin offering: and Aaron and his sons\l"
    .string "laid their hands upon the head of\l"
    .string "the bullock for the sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_15::
    .string "And he slew it; and Moses took the\n"
    .string "blood, and put it upon the horns of\l"
    .string "the altar round about with his\l"
    .string "finger, and purified the altar, and\l"
    .string "poured the blood at the bottom of\l"
    .string "the altar, and sanctified it, to\l"
    .string "make reconciliation upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_16::
    .string "And he took all the fat that was\n"
    .string "upon the inwards, and the caul above\l"
    .string "the liver, and the two kidneys, and\l"
    .string "their fat, and Moses burned it upon\l"
    .string "the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_17::
    .string "But the bullock, and his hide, his\n"
    .string "flesh, and his dung, he burnt with\l"
    .string "fire without the camp; as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_18::
    .string "And he brought the ram for the burnt\n"
    .string "offering: and Aaron and his sons\l"
    .string "laid their hands upon the head of\l"
    .string "the ram.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_19::
    .string "And he killed it; and Moses\n"
    .string "sprinkled the blood upon the\l"
    .string "altar round about.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_20::
    .string "And he cut the ram into pieces; and\n"
    .string "Moses burnt the head, and the\l"
    .string "pieces, and the fat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_21::
    .string "And he washed the inwards and the\n"
    .string "legs in water; and Moses burnt the\l"
    .string "whole ram upon the altar: it was a\l"
    .string "burnt sacrifice for a sweet savour,\l"
    .string "and an offering made by fire unto the\l"
    .string "LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_22::
    .string "And he brought the other ram, the\n"
    .string "ram of consecration: and Aaron and\l"
    .string "his sons laid their hands upon the\l"
    .string "head of the ram.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_23::
    .string "And he slew it; and Moses took of\n"
    .string "the blood of it, and put it upon the\l"
    .string "tip of Aaron’s right ear, and upon\l"
    .string "the thumb of his right hand, and upon\l"
    .string "the great toe of his right foot.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_24::
    .string "And he brought Aaron’s sons, and\n"
    .string "Moses put of the blood upon the\l"
    .string "tip of their right ear, and upon the\l"
    .string "thumbs of their right hands, and\l"
    .string "upon the great toes of their right\l"
    .string "feet: and Moses sprinkled the blood\l"
    .string "upon the altar round about.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_25::
    .string "And he took the fat, and the rump,\n"
    .string "and all the fat that was upon the\l"
    .string "inwards, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver, and the two kidneys, and their\l"
    .string "fat, and the right shoulder:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_26::
    .string "And out of the basket of unleavened\n"
    .string "bread, that was before the LORD, he\l"
    .string "took one unleavened cake, and a cake\l"
    .string "of oiled bread, and one wafer, and\l"
    .string "put them on the fat, and upon the\l"
    .string "right shoulder:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_27::
    .string "And he put all upon Aaron’s\n"
    .string "hands, and upon his sons’ hands, and\l"
    .string "waved them for a wave offering before\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_28::
    .string "And Moses took them from off their\n"
    .string "hands, and burnt them on the altar\l"
    .string "upon the burnt offering: they were\l"
    .string "consecrations for a sweet savour: it\l"
    .string "is an offering made by fire unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_29::
    .string "And Moses took the breast, and waved\n"
    .string "it for a wave offering before the\l"
    .string "LORD: for of the ram of consecration\l"
    .string "it was Moses’ part; as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_30::
    .string "And Moses took of the anointing\n"
    .string "oil, and of the blood which was\l"
    .string "upon the altar, and sprinkled it\l"
    .string "upon Aaron, and upon his garments,\l"
    .string "and upon his sons, and upon his\l"
    .string "sons’ garments with him; and\l"
    .string "sanctified Aaron, and his garments,\l"
    .string "and his sons, and his sons’ garments\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_31::
    .string "And Moses said unto Aaron and to his\n"
    .string "sons, Boil the flesh at the door of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation:\l"
    .string "and there eat it with the bread that\l"
    .string "is in the basket of consecrations, as\l"
    .string "I commanded, saying, Aaron and his\l"
    .string "sons shall eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_32::
    .string "And that which remaineth of the\n"
    .string "flesh and of the bread shall ye\l"
    .string "burn with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_33::
    .string "And ye shall not go out of the door\n"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation in seven days, until\l"
    .string "the days of your consecration be at\l"
    .string "an end: for seven days shall he\l"
    .string "consecrate you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_34::
    .string "As he hath done this day, so the LORD\n"
    .string "hath commanded to do, to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_35::
    .string "Therefore shall ye abide at the\n"
    .string "door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation day and night seven\l"
    .string "days, and keep the charge of the\l"
    .string "LORD, that ye die not: for so I am\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_8_36::
    .string "So Aaron and his sons did all\n"
    .string "things which the LORD commanded by\l"
    .string "the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_1::
    .string "And it came to pass on the eighth\n"
    .string "day, that Moses called Aaron and his\l"
    .string "sons, and the elders of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_2::
    .string "And he said unto Aaron, Take thee a\n"
    .string "young calf for a sin offering, and a\l"
    .string "ram for a burnt offering, without\l"
    .string "blemish, and offer them before the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_3::
    .string "And unto the children of Israel\n"
    .string "thou shalt speak, saying, Take ye a\l"
    .string "kid of the goats for a sin offering;\l"
    .string "and a calf and a lamb, both of the\l"
    .string "first year, without blemish, for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_4::
    .string "Also a bullock and a ram for\n"
    .string "peace offerings, to sacrifice before\l"
    .string "the LORD; and a meat offering\l"
    .string "mingled with oil: for to day the\l"
    .string "LORD will appear unto you$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_5::
    .string "And they brought that which Moses\n"
    .string "commanded before the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation: and all the\l"
    .string "congregation drew near and stood\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_6::
    .string "And Moses said, This is the thing\n"
    .string "which the LORD commanded that ye\l"
    .string "should do: and the glory of the LORD\l"
    .string "shall appear unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_7::
    .string "And Moses said unto Aaron, Go unto\n"
    .string "the altar, and offer thy sin\l"
    .string "offering, and thy burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "make an atonement for thyself, and\l"
    .string "for the people: and offer the\l"
    .string "offering of the people, and make an\l"
    .string "atonement for them; as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_8::
    .string "Aaron therefore went unto the\n"
    .string "altar, and slew the calf of the sin\l"
    .string "offering, which was for himself.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_9::
    .string "And the sons of Aaron brought the\n"
    .string "blood unto him: and he dipped his\l"
    .string "finger in the blood, and put it\l"
    .string "upon the horns of the altar, and\l"
    .string "poured out the blood at the bottom\l"
    .string "of the altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_10::
    .string "But the fat, and the kidneys, and\n"
    .string "the caul above the liver of the sin\l"
    .string "offering, he burnt upon the altar;\l"
    .string "as the LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_11::
    .string "And the flesh and the hide he burnt\n"
    .string "with fire without the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_12::
    .string "And he slew the burnt offering; and\n"
    .string "Aaron’s sons presented unto him the\l"
    .string "blood, which he sprinkled round\l"
    .string "about upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_13::
    .string "And they presented the burnt\n"
    .string "offering unto him, with the pieces\l"
    .string "thereof, and the head: and he burnt\l"
    .string "them upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_14::
    .string "And he did wash the inwards and the\n"
    .string "legs, and burnt them upon the burnt\l"
    .string "offering on the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_15::
    .string "And he brought the people’s\n"
    .string "offering, and took the goat, which\l"
    .string "was the sin offering for the\l"
    .string "people, and slew it, and offered it\l"
    .string "for sin, as the first.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_16::
    .string "And he brought the burnt offering,\n"
    .string "and offered it according to the\l"
    .string "manner.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_17::
    .string "And he brought the meat offering,\n"
    .string "and took an handful thereof, and\l"
    .string "burnt it upon the altar, beside the\l"
    .string "burnt sacrifice of the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_18::
    .string "He slew also the bullock and the\n"
    .string "ram for a sacrifice of peace\l"
    .string "offerings, which was for the\l"
    .string "people: and Aaron’s sons presented\l"
    .string "unto him the blood, which he\l"
    .string "sprinkled upon the altar round\l"
    .string "about,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_19::
    .string "And the fat of the bullock and of\n"
    .string "the ram, the rump, and that which\l"
    .string "covereth the inwards, and the\l"
    .string "kidneys, and the caul above the\l"
    .string "liver:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_20::
    .string "And they put the fat upon the\n"
    .string "breasts, and he burnt the fat upon\l"
    .string "the altar:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_21::
    .string "And the breasts and the right\n"
    .string "shoulder Aaron waved for a wave\l"
    .string "offering before the LORD; as Moses\l"
    .string "commanded$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_22::
    .string "And Aaron lifted up his hand\n"
    .string "toward the people, and blessed\l"
    .string "them, and came down from offering of\l"
    .string "the sin offering, and the burnt\l"
    .string "offering, and peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_23::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron went into the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "came out, and blessed the people:\l"
    .string "and the glory of the LORD appeared\l"
    .string "unto all the people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_9_24::
    .string "And there came a fire out from\n"
    .string "before the LORD, and consumed upon\l"
    .string "the altar the burnt offering and the\l"
    .string "fat: which when all the people\l"
    .string "saw, they shouted, and fell on their\l"
    .string "faces.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_1::
    .string "And Nadab and Abihu, the sons of\n"
    .string "Aaron, took either of them his\l"
    .string "censer, and put fire therein, and\l"
    .string "put incense thereon, and offered\l"
    .string "strange fire before the LORD, which\l"
    .string "he commanded them not.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_2::
    .string "And there went out fire from the\n"
    .string "LORD, and devoured them, and they\l"
    .string "died before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_3::
    .string "Then Moses said unto Aaron, This is\n"
    .string "it that the LORD spake, saying, I\l"
    .string "will be sanctified in them that\l"
    .string "come nigh me, and before all the\l"
    .string "people I will be glorified. And\l"
    .string "Aaron held his peace.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_4::
    .string "And Moses called Mishael and\n"
    .string "Elzaphan, the sons of Uzziel the\l"
    .string "uncle of Aaron, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Come near, carry your brethren from\l"
    .string "before the sanctuary out of the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_5::
    .string "So they went near, and carried them\n"
    .string "in their coats out of the camp; as\l"
    .string "Moses had said.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_6::
    .string "And Moses said unto Aaron, and unto\n"
    .string "Eleazar and unto Ithamar, his sons,\l"
    .string "Uncover not your heads, neither rend\l"
    .string "your clothes; lest ye die, and lest\l"
    .string "wrath come upon all the people:\l"
    .string "but let your brethren, the whole\l"
    .string "house of Israel, bewail the burning\l"
    .string "which the LORD hath kindled.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_7::
    .string "And ye shall not go out from the\n"
    .string "door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, lest ye die: for the\l"
    .string "anointing oil of the LORD is upon\l"
    .string "you. And they did according to the\l"
    .string "word of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_8::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Aaron,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_9::
    .string "Do not drink wine nor strong drink,\n"
    .string "thou, nor thy sons with thee, when ye\l"
    .string "go into the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, lest ye die: it shall\l"
    .string "be a statute for ever throughout your\l"
    .string "generations:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_10::
    .string "And that ye may put difference\n"
    .string "between holy and unholy, and\l"
    .string "between unclean and clean;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_11::
    .string "And that ye may teach the children\n"
    .string "of Israel all the statutes which\l"
    .string "the LORD hath spoken unto them by\l"
    .string "the hand of Moses$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_12::
    .string "And Moses spake unto Aaron, and\n"
    .string "unto Eleazar and unto Ithamar, his\l"
    .string "sons that were left, Take the meat\l"
    .string "offering that remaineth of the\l"
    .string "offerings of the LORD made by fire,\l"
    .string "and eat it without leaven beside the\l"
    .string "altar: for it is most holy:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_13::
    .string "And ye shall eat it in the holy\n"
    .string "place, because it is thy due, and thy\l"
    .string "sons’ due, of the sacrifices of the\l"
    .string "LORD made by fire: for so I am\l"
    .string "commanded$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_14::
    .string "And the wave breast and heave\n"
    .string "shoulder shall ye eat in a clean\l"
    .string "place; thou, and thy sons, and thy\l"
    .string "daughters with thee: for they be thy\l"
    .string "due, and thy sons’ due, which are\l"
    .string "given out of the sacrifices of peace\l"
    .string "offerings of the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_15::
    .string "The heave shoulder and the wave\n"
    .string "breast shall they bring with the\l"
    .string "offerings made by fire of the fat, to\l"
    .string "wave it for a wave offering before\l"
    .string "the LORD; and it shall be thine, and\l"
    .string "thy sons’ with thee, by a statute for\l"
    .string "ever; as the LORD hath commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_16::
    .string "And Moses diligently sought the\n"
    .string "goat of the sin offering, and,\l"
    .string "behold, it was burnt: and he was\l"
    .string "angry with Eleazar and Ithamar, the\l"
    .string "sons of Aaron which were left alive,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_17::
    .string "Wherefore have ye not eaten the sin\n"
    .string "offering in the holy place, seeing\l"
    .string "it is most holy, and God hath given\l"
    .string "it you to bear the iniquity of the\l"
    .string "congregation, to make atonement for\l"
    .string "them before the LORD?"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_18::
    .string "Behold, the blood of it was not\n"
    .string "brought in within the holy place:\l"
    .string "ye should indeed have eaten it in\l"
    .string "the holy place, as I commanded$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_19::
    .string "And Aaron said unto Moses, Behold,\n"
    .string "this day have they offered their sin\l"
    .string "offering and their burnt offering\l"
    .string "before the LORD; and such things have\l"
    .string "befallen me: and if I had eaten the\l"
    .string "sin offering to day, should it have\l"
    .string "been accepted in the sight of the\l"
    .string "LORD?"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_10_20::
    .string "And when Moses heard that, he was\n"
    .string "content$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "to Aaron, saying unto them,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, These are the beasts which ye\l"
    .string "shall eat among all the beasts\l"
    .string "that are on the earth$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_3::
    .string "Whatsoever parteth the hoof, and is\n"
    .string "clovenfooted, and cheweth the cud,\l"
    .string "among the beasts, that shall ye eat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_4::
    .string "Nevertheless these shall ye not\n"
    .string "eat of them that chew the cud, or of\l"
    .string "them that divide the hoof: as the\l"
    .string "camel, because he cheweth the cud,\l"
    .string "but divideth not the hoof; he is\l"
    .string "unclean unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_5::
    .string "And the coney, because he cheweth\n"
    .string "the cud, but divideth not the hoof;\l"
    .string "he is unclean unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_6::
    .string "And the hare, because he cheweth the\n"
    .string "cud, but divideth not the hoof; he is\l"
    .string "unclean unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_7::
    .string "And the swine, though he divide the\n"
    .string "hoof, and be clovenfooted, yet he\l"
    .string "cheweth not the cud; he is unclean to\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_8::
    .string "Of their flesh shall ye not eat,\n"
    .string "and their carcase shall ye not\l"
    .string "touch; they are unclean to you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_9::
    .string "These shall ye eat of all that\n"
    .string "are in the waters: whatsoever hath\l"
    .string "fins and scales in the waters, in the\l"
    .string "seas, and in the rivers, them shall\l"
    .string "ye eat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_10::
    .string "And all that have not fins and\n"
    .string "scales in the seas, and in the\l"
    .string "rivers, of all that move in the\l"
    .string "waters, and of any living thing\l"
    .string "which is in the waters, they shall\l"
    .string "be an abomination unto you:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_11::
    .string "They shall be even an abomination\n"
    .string "unto you; ye shall not eat of their\l"
    .string "flesh, but ye shall have their\l"
    .string "carcases in abomination$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_12::
    .string "Whatsoever hath no fins nor scales\n"
    .string "in the waters, that shall be an\l"
    .string "abomination unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_13::
    .string "And these are they which ye shall\n"
    .string "have in abomination among the fowls;\l"
    .string "they shall not be eaten, they are an\l"
    .string "abomination: the eagle, and the\l"
    .string "ossifrage, and the ospray,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_14::
    .string "And the vulture, and the kite after\n"
    .string "his kind;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_15::
    .string "Every raven after his kind;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_16::
    .string "And the owl, and the night hawk, and\n"
    .string "the cuckow, and the hawk after his\l"
    .string "kind,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_17::
    .string "And the little owl, and the\n"
    .string "cormorant, and the great owl,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_18::
    .string "And the swan, and the pelican, and\n"
    .string "the gier eagle,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_19::
    .string "And the stork, the heron after her\n"
    .string "kind, and the lapwing, and the bat$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_20::
    .string "All fowls that creep, going upon\n"
    .string "all four, shall be an abomination\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_21::
    .string "Yet these may ye eat of every\n"
    .string "flying creeping thing that goeth\l"
    .string "upon all four, which have legs\l"
    .string "above their feet, to leap withal\l"
    .string "upon the earth;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_22::
    .string "Even these of them ye may eat; the\n"
    .string "locust after his kind, and the bald\l"
    .string "locust after his kind, and the\l"
    .string "beetle after his kind, and the\l"
    .string "grasshopper after his kind$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_23::
    .string "But all other flying creeping\n"
    .string "things, which have four feet, shall\l"
    .string "be an abomination unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_24::
    .string "And for these ye shall be unclean:\n"
    .string "whosoever toucheth the carcase of\l"
    .string "them shall be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_25::
    .string "And whosoever beareth ought of the\n"
    .string "carcase of them shall wash his\l"
    .string "clothes, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_26::
    .string "The carcases of every beast which\n"
    .string "divideth the hoof, and is not\l"
    .string "clovenfooted, nor cheweth the cud,\l"
    .string "are unclean unto you: every one that\l"
    .string "toucheth them shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_27::
    .string "And whatsoever goeth upon his\n"
    .string "paws, among all manner of beasts\l"
    .string "that go on all four, those are\l"
    .string "unclean unto you: whoso toucheth\l"
    .string "their carcase shall be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_28::
    .string "And he that beareth the carcase of\n"
    .string "them shall wash his clothes, and be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even: they are\l"
    .string "unclean unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_29::
    .string "These also shall be unclean unto\n"
    .string "you among the creeping things that\l"
    .string "creep upon the earth; the weasel,\l"
    .string "and the mouse, and the tortoise after\l"
    .string "his kind,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_30::
    .string "And the ferret, and the chameleon,\n"
    .string "and the lizard, and the snail, and\l"
    .string "the mole$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_31::
    .string "These are unclean to you among all\n"
    .string "that creep: whosoever doth touch\l"
    .string "them, when they be dead, shall be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_32::
    .string "And upon whatsoever any of them,\n"
    .string "when they are dead, doth fall, it\l"
    .string "shall be unclean; whether it be any\l"
    .string "vessel of wood, or raiment, or skin,\l"
    .string "or sack, whatsoever vessel it be,\l"
    .string "wherein any work is done, it must be\l"
    .string "put into water, and it shall be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even; so it\l"
    .string "shall be cleansed.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_33::
    .string "And every earthen vessel, whereinto\n"
    .string "any of them falleth, whatsoever is\l"
    .string "in it shall be unclean; and ye\l"
    .string "shall break it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_34::
    .string "Of all meat which may be eaten,\n"
    .string "that on which such water cometh\l"
    .string "shall be unclean: and all drink\l"
    .string "that may be drunk in every such\l"
    .string "vessel shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_35::
    .string "And every thing whereupon any part\n"
    .string "of their carcase falleth shall be\l"
    .string "unclean; whether it be oven, or\l"
    .string "ranges for pots, they shall be\l"
    .string "broken down: for they are unclean\l"
    .string "and shall be unclean unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_36::
    .string "Nevertheless a fountain or pit,\n"
    .string "wherein there is plenty of water,\l"
    .string "shall be clean: but that which\l"
    .string "toucheth their carcase shall be\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_37::
    .string "And if any part of their carcase\n"
    .string "fall upon any sowing seed which is\l"
    .string "to be sown, it shall be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_38::
    .string "But if any water be put upon the\n"
    .string "seed, and any part of their carcase\l"
    .string "fall thereon, it shall be unclean\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_39::
    .string "And if any beast, of which ye may\n"
    .string "eat, die; he that toucheth the\l"
    .string "carcase thereof shall be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_40::
    .string "And he that eateth of the carcase of\n"
    .string "it shall wash his clothes, and be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even: he also\l"
    .string "that beareth the carcase of it\l"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_41::
    .string "And every creeping thing that\n"
    .string "creepeth upon the earth shall be\l"
    .string "an abomination; it shall not be\l"
    .string "eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_42::
    .string "Whatsoever goeth upon the belly,\n"
    .string "and whatsoever goeth upon all four,\l"
    .string "or whatsoever hath more feet among\l"
    .string "all creeping things that creep\l"
    .string "upon the earth, them ye shall not\l"
    .string "eat; for they are an abomination.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_43::
    .string "Ye shall not make yourselves\n"
    .string "abominable with any creeping thing\l"
    .string "that creepeth, neither shall ye\l"
    .string "make yourselves unclean with them,\l"
    .string "that ye should be defiled thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_44::
    .string "For I am the LORD your God: ye\n"
    .string "shall therefore sanctify\l"
    .string "yourselves, and ye shall be holy;\l"
    .string "for I am holy: neither shall ye\l"
    .string "defile yourselves with any manner\l"
    .string "of creeping thing that creepeth\l"
    .string "upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_45::
    .string "For I am the LORD that bringeth you\n"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt, to be\l"
    .string "your God: ye shall therefore be\l"
    .string "holy, for I am holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_46::
    .string "This is the law of the beasts, and\n"
    .string "of the fowl, and of every living\l"
    .string "creature that moveth in the waters,\l"
    .string "and of every creature that creepeth\l"
    .string "upon the earth:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_11_47::
    .string "To make a difference between the\n"
    .string "unclean and the clean, and between\l"
    .string "the beast that may be eaten and the\l"
    .string "beast that may not be eaten$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, If a woman have conceived\l"
    .string "seed, and born a man child: then she\l"
    .string "shall be unclean seven days;\l"
    .string "according to the days of the\l"
    .string "separation for her infirmity shall\l"
    .string "she be unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_3::
    .string "And in the eighth day the flesh of\n"
    .string "his foreskin shall be circumcised.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_4::
    .string "And she shall then continue in the\n"
    .string "blood of her purifying three and\l"
    .string "thirty days; she shall touch no\l"
    .string "hallowed thing, nor come into the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, until the days of her\l"
    .string "purifying be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_5::
    .string "But if she bear a maid child, then\n"
    .string "she shall be unclean two weeks, as\l"
    .string "in her separation: and she shall\l"
    .string "continue in the blood of her\l"
    .string "purifying threescore and six days.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_6::
    .string "And when the days of her purifying\n"
    .string "are fulfilled, for a son, or for a\l"
    .string "daughter, she shall bring a lamb of\l"
    .string "the first year for a burnt offering,\l"
    .string "and a young pigeon, or a turtledove,\l"
    .string "for a sin offering, unto the door of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "unto the priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_7::
    .string "Who shall offer it before the LORD,\n"
    .string "and make an atonement for her; and\l"
    .string "she shall be cleansed from the\l"
    .string "issue of her blood. This is the law\l"
    .string "for her that hath born a male or a\l"
    .string "female$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_12_8::
    .string "And if she be not able to bring a\n"
    .string "lamb, then she shall bring two\l"
    .string "turtles, or two young pigeons; the\l"
    .string "one for the burnt offering, and the\l"
    .string "other for a sin offering: and the\l"
    .string "priest shall make an atonement for\l"
    .string "her, and she shall be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_2::
    .string "When a man shall have in the skin\n"
    .string "of his flesh a rising, a scab, or\l"
    .string "bright spot, and it be in the skin of\l"
    .string "his flesh like the plague of\l"
    .string "leprosy; then he shall be brought\l"
    .string "unto Aaron the priest, or unto one of\l"
    .string "his sons the priests:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_3::
    .string "And the priest shall look on the\n"
    .string "plague in the skin of the flesh: and\l"
    .string "when the hair in the plague is\l"
    .string "turned white, and the plague in\l"
    .string "sight be deeper than the skin of his\l"
    .string "flesh, it is a plague of leprosy:\l"
    .string "and the priest shall look on him,\l"
    .string "and pronounce him unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_4::
    .string "If the bright spot be white in the\n"
    .string "skin of his flesh, and in sight be\l"
    .string "not deeper than the skin, and the\l"
    .string "hair thereof be not turned white;\l"
    .string "then the priest shall shut up him\l"
    .string "that hath the plague seven days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_5::
    .string "And the priest shall look on him\n"
    .string "the seventh day: and, behold, if the\l"
    .string "plague in his sight be at a stay, and\l"
    .string "the plague spread not in the skin;\l"
    .string "then the priest shall shut him up\l"
    .string "seven days more:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_6::
    .string "And the priest shall look on him\n"
    .string "again the seventh day: and, behold,\l"
    .string "if the plague be somewhat dark, and\l"
    .string "the plague spread not in the skin,\l"
    .string "the priest shall pronounce him\l"
    .string "clean: it is but a scab: and he\l"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and be\l"
    .string "clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_7::
    .string "But if the scab spread much abroad\n"
    .string "in the skin, after that he hath been\l"
    .string "seen of the priest for his\l"
    .string "cleansing, he shall be seen of the\l"
    .string "priest again.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_8::
    .string "And if the priest see that, behold,\n"
    .string "the scab spreadeth in the skin, then\l"
    .string "the priest shall pronounce him\l"
    .string "unclean: it is a leprosy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_9::
    .string "When the plague of leprosy is in\n"
    .string "a man, then he shall be brought unto\l"
    .string "the priest;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_10::
    .string "And the priest shall see him: and,\n"
    .string "behold, if the rising be white in the\l"
    .string "skin, and it have turned the hair\l"
    .string "white, and there be quick raw flesh\l"
    .string "in the rising;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_11::
    .string "It is an old leprosy in the skin\n"
    .string "of his flesh, and the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him unclean, and shall\l"
    .string "not shut him up: for he is unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_12::
    .string "And if a leprosy break out abroad\n"
    .string "in the skin, and the leprosy cover\l"
    .string "all the skin of him that hath the\l"
    .string "plague from his head even to his\l"
    .string "foot, wheresoever the priest\l"
    .string "looketh;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_13::
    .string "Then the priest shall consider:\n"
    .string "and, behold, if the leprosy have\l"
    .string "covered all his flesh, he shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him clean that hath the\l"
    .string "plague: it is all turned white: he\l"
    .string "is clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_14::
    .string "But when raw flesh appeareth in\n"
    .string "him, he shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_15::
    .string "And the priest shall see the raw\n"
    .string "flesh, and pronounce him to be\l"
    .string "unclean: for the raw flesh is\l"
    .string "unclean: it is a leprosy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_16::
    .string "Or if the raw flesh turn again, and\n"
    .string "be changed unto white, he shall come\l"
    .string "unto the priest;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_17::
    .string "And the priest shall see him: and,\n"
    .string "behold, if the plague be turned\l"
    .string "into white; then the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him clean that hath the\l"
    .string "plague: he is clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_18::
    .string "The flesh also, in which, even in\n"
    .string "the skin thereof, was a boil, and is\l"
    .string "healed,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_19::
    .string "And in the place of the boil there\n"
    .string "be a white rising, or a bright spot,\l"
    .string "white, and somewhat reddish, and it\l"
    .string "be shewed to the priest;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_20::
    .string "And if, when the priest seeth it,\n"
    .string "behold, it be in sight lower than\l"
    .string "the skin, and the hair thereof be\l"
    .string "turned white; the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him unclean: it is a\l"
    .string "plague of leprosy broken out of the\l"
    .string "boil$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_21::
    .string "But if the priest look on it, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there be no white hairs\l"
    .string "therein, and if it be not lower than\l"
    .string "the skin, but be somewhat dark; then\l"
    .string "the priest shall shut him up seven\l"
    .string "days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_22::
    .string "And if it spread much abroad in the\n"
    .string "skin, then the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him unclean: it is a\l"
    .string "plague$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_23::
    .string "But if the bright spot stay in his\n"
    .string "place, and spread not, it is a\l"
    .string "burning boil; and the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_24::
    .string "Or if there be any flesh, in the\n"
    .string "skin whereof there is a hot burning,\l"
    .string "and the quick flesh that burneth\l"
    .string "have a white bright spot, somewhat\l"
    .string "reddish, or white;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_25::
    .string "Then the priest shall look upon\n"
    .string "it: and, behold, if the hair in the\l"
    .string "bright spot be turned white, and it\l"
    .string "be in sight deeper than the skin; it\l"
    .string "is a leprosy broken out of the\l"
    .string "burning: wherefore the priest\l"
    .string "shall pronounce him unclean: it is\l"
    .string "the plague of leprosy$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_26::
    .string "But if the priest look on it, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there be no white hair in the\l"
    .string "bright spot, and it be no lower than\l"
    .string "the other skin, but be somewhat dark;\l"
    .string "then the priest shall shut him up\l"
    .string "seven days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_27::
    .string "And the priest shall look upon\n"
    .string "him the seventh day: and if it be\l"
    .string "spread much abroad in the skin, then\l"
    .string "the priest shall pronounce him\l"
    .string "unclean: it is the plague of\l"
    .string "leprosy$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_28::
    .string "And if the bright spot stay in his\n"
    .string "place, and spread not in the skin,\l"
    .string "but it be somewhat dark; it is a\l"
    .string "rising of the burning, and the\l"
    .string "priest shall pronounce him clean:\l"
    .string "for it is an inflammation of the\l"
    .string "burning.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_29::
    .string "If a man or woman have a plague\n"
    .string "upon the head or the beard;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_30::
    .string "Then the priest shall see the\n"
    .string "plague: and, behold, if it be in\l"
    .string "sight deeper than the skin; and\l"
    .string "there be in it a yellow thin hair;\l"
    .string "then the priest shall pronounce\l"
    .string "him unclean: it is a dry scall,\l"
    .string "even a leprosy upon the head or\l"
    .string "beard$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_31::
    .string "And if the priest look on the\n"
    .string "plague of the scall, and, behold,\l"
    .string "it be not in sight deeper than the\l"
    .string "skin, and that there is no black hair\l"
    .string "in it; then the priest shall shut\l"
    .string "up him that hath the plague of the\l"
    .string "scall seven days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_32::
    .string "And in the seventh day the priest\n"
    .string "shall look on the plague: and,\l"
    .string "behold, if the scall spread not,\l"
    .string "and there be in it no yellow hair,\l"
    .string "and the scall be not in sight\l"
    .string "deeper than the skin;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_33::
    .string "He shall be shaven, but the scall\n"
    .string "shall he not shave; and the priest\l"
    .string "shall shut up him that hath the\l"
    .string "scall seven days more:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_34::
    .string "And in the seventh day the priest\n"
    .string "shall look on the scall: and,\l"
    .string "behold, if the scall be not spread\l"
    .string "in the skin, nor be in sight deeper\l"
    .string "than the skin; then the priest\l"
    .string "shall pronounce him clean: and he\l"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and be\l"
    .string "clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_35::
    .string "But if the scall spread much in\n"
    .string "the skin after his cleansing;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_36::
    .string "Then the priest shall look on\n"
    .string "him: and, behold, if the scall be\l"
    .string "spread in the skin, the priest\l"
    .string "shall not seek for yellow hair; he\l"
    .string "is unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_37::
    .string "But if the scall be in his sight at\n"
    .string "a stay, and that there is black hair\l"
    .string "grown up therein; the scall is\l"
    .string "healed, he is clean: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall pronounce him clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_38::
    .string "If a man also or a woman have in the\n"
    .string "skin of their flesh bright spots,\l"
    .string "even white bright spots;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_39::
    .string "Then the priest shall look: and,\n"
    .string "behold, if the bright spots in the\l"
    .string "skin of their flesh be darkish\l"
    .string "white; it is a freckled spot that\l"
    .string "groweth in the skin; he is clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_40::
    .string "And the man whose hair is fallen\n"
    .string "off his head, he is bald; yet is he\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_41::
    .string "And he that hath his hair fallen\n"
    .string "off from the part of his head toward\l"
    .string "his face, he is forehead bald: yet is\l"
    .string "he clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_42::
    .string "And if there be in the bald head, or\n"
    .string "bald forehead, a white reddish sore;\l"
    .string "it is a leprosy sprung up in his\l"
    .string "bald head, or his bald forehead.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_43::
    .string "Then the priest shall look upon\n"
    .string "it: and, behold, if the rising of the\l"
    .string "sore be white reddish in his bald\l"
    .string "head, or in his bald forehead, as the\l"
    .string "leprosy appeareth in the skin of\l"
    .string "the flesh;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_44::
    .string "He is a leprous man, he is\n"
    .string "unclean: the priest shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him utterly unclean; his\l"
    .string "plague is in his head$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_45::
    .string "And the leper in whom the plague\n"
    .string "is, his clothes shall be rent, and\l"
    .string "his head bare, and he shall put a\l"
    .string "covering upon his upper lip, and\l"
    .string "shall cry, Unclean, unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_46::
    .string "All the days wherein the plague\n"
    .string "shall be in him he shall be\l"
    .string "defiled; he is unclean: he shall\l"
    .string "dwell alone; without the camp\l"
    .string "shall his habitation be.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_47::
    .string "The garment also that the plague\n"
    .string "of leprosy is in, whether it be a\l"
    .string "woollen garment, or a linen\l"
    .string "garment;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_48::
    .string "Whether it be in the warp, or woof;\n"
    .string "of linen, or of woollen; whether in\l"
    .string "a skin, or in any thing made of skin;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_49::
    .string "And if the plague be greenish or\n"
    .string "reddish in the garment, or in the\l"
    .string "skin, either in the warp, or in the\l"
    .string "woof, or in any thing of skin; it is a\l"
    .string "plague of leprosy, and shall be\l"
    .string "shewed unto the priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_50::
    .string "And the priest shall look upon\n"
    .string "the plague, and shut up it that\l"
    .string "hath the plague seven days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_51::
    .string "And he shall look on the plague\n"
    .string "on the seventh day: if the plague be\l"
    .string "spread in the garment, either in the\l"
    .string "warp, or in the woof, or in a skin, or\l"
    .string "in any work that is made of skin; the\l"
    .string "plague is a fretting leprosy; it is\l"
    .string "unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_52::
    .string "He shall therefore burn that\n"
    .string "garment, whether warp or woof, in\l"
    .string "woollen or in linen, or any thing\l"
    .string "of skin, wherein the plague is: for\l"
    .string "it is a fretting leprosy; it shall\l"
    .string "be burnt in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_53::
    .string "And if the priest shall look,\n"
    .string "and, behold, the plague be not\l"
    .string "spread in the garment, either in the\l"
    .string "warp, or in the woof, or in any thing\l"
    .string "of skin;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_54::
    .string "Then the priest shall command\n"
    .string "that they wash the thing wherein the\l"
    .string "plague is, and he shall shut it up\l"
    .string "seven days more:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_55::
    .string "And the priest shall look on the\n"
    .string "plague, after that it is washed: and,\l"
    .string "behold, if the plague have not\l"
    .string "changed his colour, and the plague\l"
    .string "be not spread; it is unclean; thou\l"
    .string "shalt burn it in the fire; it is fret\l"
    .string "inward, whether it be bare within or\l"
    .string "without$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_56::
    .string "And if the priest look, and,\n"
    .string "behold, the plague be somewhat dark\l"
    .string "after the washing of it; then he\l"
    .string "shall rend it out of the garment, or\l"
    .string "out of the skin, or out of the warp,\l"
    .string "or out of the woof:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_57::
    .string "And if it appear still in the\n"
    .string "garment, either in the warp, or in\l"
    .string "the woof, or in any thing of skin; it\l"
    .string "is a spreading plague: thou shalt\l"
    .string "burn that wherein the plague is\l"
    .string "with fire$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_58::
    .string "And the garment, either warp, or\n"
    .string "woof, or whatsoever thing of skin it\l"
    .string "be, which thou shalt wash, if the\l"
    .string "plague be departed from them, then\l"
    .string "it shall be washed the second time,\l"
    .string "and shall be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_13_59::
    .string "This is the law of the plague of\n"
    .string "leprosy in a garment of woollen or\l"
    .string "linen, either in the warp, or woof,\l"
    .string "or any thing of skins, to pronounce\l"
    .string "it clean, or to pronounce it\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_2::
    .string "This shall be the law of the\n"
    .string "leper in the day of his cleansing:\l"
    .string "He shall be brought unto the\l"
    .string "priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_3::
    .string "And the priest shall go forth out\n"
    .string "of the camp; and the priest shall\l"
    .string "look, and, behold, if the plague of\l"
    .string "leprosy be healed in the leper;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_4::
    .string "Then shall the priest command to\n"
    .string "take for him that is to be cleansed\l"
    .string "two birds alive and clean, and cedar\l"
    .string "wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_5::
    .string "And the priest shall command that\n"
    .string "one of the birds be killed in an\l"
    .string "earthen vessel over running water:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_6::
    .string "As for the living bird, he shall\n"
    .string "take it, and the cedar wood, and the\l"
    .string "scarlet, and the hyssop, and shall\l"
    .string "dip them and the living bird in the\l"
    .string "blood of the bird that was killed\l"
    .string "over the running water:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_7::
    .string "And he shall sprinkle upon him\n"
    .string "that is to be cleansed from the\l"
    .string "leprosy seven times, and shall\l"
    .string "pronounce him clean, and shall let\l"
    .string "the living bird loose into the open\l"
    .string "field$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_8::
    .string "And he that is to be cleansed\n"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and shave\l"
    .string "off all his hair, and wash himself\l"
    .string "in water, that he may be clean: and\l"
    .string "after that he shall come into the\l"
    .string "camp, and shall tarry abroad out of\l"
    .string "his tent seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_9::
    .string "But it shall be on the seventh day,\n"
    .string "that he shall shave all his hair\l"
    .string "off his head and his beard and his\l"
    .string "eyebrows, even all his hair he\l"
    .string "shall shave off: and he shall wash\l"
    .string "his clothes, also he shall wash\l"
    .string "his flesh in water, and he shall be\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_10::
    .string "And on the eighth day he shall take\n"
    .string "two he lambs without blemish, and\l"
    .string "one ewe lamb of the first year\l"
    .string "without blemish, and three tenth\l"
    .string "deals of fine flour for a meat\l"
    .string "offering, mingled with oil, and one\l"
    .string "log of oil.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_11::
    .string "And the priest that maketh him\n"
    .string "clean shall present the man that\l"
    .string "is to be made clean, and those\l"
    .string "things, before the LORD, at the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_12::
    .string "And the priest shall take one he\n"
    .string "lamb, and offer him for a trespass\l"
    .string "offering, and the log of oil, and\l"
    .string "wave them for a wave offering before\l"
    .string "the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_13::
    .string "And he shall slay the lamb in the\n"
    .string "place where he shall kill the sin\l"
    .string "offering and the burnt offering, in\l"
    .string "the holy place: for as the sin\l"
    .string "offering is the priest’s, so is the\l"
    .string "trespass offering: it is most holy:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_14::
    .string "And the priest shall take some of\n"
    .string "the blood of the trespass offering,\l"
    .string "and the priest shall put it upon\l"
    .string "the tip of the right ear of him that\l"
    .string "is to be cleansed, and upon the\l"
    .string "thumb of his right hand, and upon the\l"
    .string "great toe of his right foot:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_15::
    .string "And the priest shall take some of\n"
    .string "the log of oil, and pour it into the\l"
    .string "palm of his own left hand:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_16::
    .string "And the priest shall dip his\n"
    .string "right finger in the oil that is in\l"
    .string "his left hand, and shall sprinkle\l"
    .string "of the oil with his finger seven\l"
    .string "times before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_17::
    .string "And of the rest of the oil that is\n"
    .string "in his hand shall the priest put\l"
    .string "upon the tip of the right ear of him\l"
    .string "that is to be cleansed, and upon the\l"
    .string "thumb of his right hand, and upon the\l"
    .string "great toe of his right foot, upon the\l"
    .string "blood of the trespass offering:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_18::
    .string "And the remnant of the oil that is\n"
    .string "in the priest’s hand he shall pour\l"
    .string "upon the head of him that is to be\l"
    .string "cleansed: and the priest shall\l"
    .string "make an atonement for him before the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_19::
    .string "And the priest shall offer the sin\n"
    .string "offering, and make an atonement for\l"
    .string "him that is to be cleansed from his\l"
    .string "uncleanness; and afterward he\l"
    .string "shall kill the burnt offering:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_20::
    .string "And the priest shall offer the\n"
    .string "burnt offering and the meat offering\l"
    .string "upon the altar: and the priest\l"
    .string "shall make an atonement for him, and\l"
    .string "he shall be clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_21::
    .string "And if he be poor, and cannot get so\n"
    .string "much; then he shall take one lamb\l"
    .string "for a trespass offering to be waved,\l"
    .string "to make an atonement for him, and one\l"
    .string "tenth deal of fine flour mingled\l"
    .string "with oil for a meat offering, and a\l"
    .string "log of oil;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_22::
    .string "And two turtledoves, or two young\n"
    .string "pigeons, such as he is able to get;\l"
    .string "and the one shall be a sin offering,\l"
    .string "and the other a burnt offering$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_23::
    .string "And he shall bring them on the\n"
    .string "eighth day for his cleansing unto\l"
    .string "the priest, unto the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_24::
    .string "And the priest shall take the\n"
    .string "lamb of the trespass offering, and\l"
    .string "the log of oil, and the priest\l"
    .string "shall wave them for a wave offering\l"
    .string "before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_25::
    .string "And he shall kill the lamb of the\n"
    .string "trespass offering, and the priest\l"
    .string "shall take some of the blood of the\l"
    .string "trespass offering, and put it upon\l"
    .string "the tip of the right ear of him that\l"
    .string "is to be cleansed, and upon the\l"
    .string "thumb of his right hand, and upon the\l"
    .string "great toe of his right foot:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_26::
    .string "And the priest shall pour of the\n"
    .string "oil into the palm of his own left\l"
    .string "hand:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_27::
    .string "And the priest shall sprinkle\n"
    .string "with his right finger some of the\l"
    .string "oil that is in his left hand seven\l"
    .string "times before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_28::
    .string "And the priest shall put of the\n"
    .string "oil that is in his hand upon the\l"
    .string "tip of the right ear of him that is\l"
    .string "to be cleansed, and upon the thumb\l"
    .string "of his right hand, and upon the great\l"
    .string "toe of his right foot, upon the\l"
    .string "place of the blood of the trespass\l"
    .string "offering:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_29::
    .string "And the rest of the oil that is in\n"
    .string "the priest’s hand he shall put\l"
    .string "upon the head of him that is to be\l"
    .string "cleansed, to make an atonement for\l"
    .string "him before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_30::
    .string "And he shall offer the one of the\n"
    .string "turtledoves, or of the young\l"
    .string "pigeons, such as he can get;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_31::
    .string "Even such as he is able to get, the\n"
    .string "one for a sin offering, and the other\l"
    .string "for a burnt offering, with the meat\l"
    .string "offering: and the priest shall make\l"
    .string "an atonement for him that is to be\l"
    .string "cleansed before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_32::
    .string "This is the law of him in whom is\n"
    .string "the plague of leprosy, whose hand\l"
    .string "is not able to get that which\l"
    .string "pertaineth to his cleansing.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_33::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_34::
    .string "When ye be come into the land of\n"
    .string "Canaan, which I give to you for a\l"
    .string "possession, and I put the plague of\l"
    .string "leprosy in a house of the land of\l"
    .string "your possession;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_35::
    .string "And he that owneth the house shall\n"
    .string "come and tell the priest, saying,\l"
    .string "It seemeth to me there is as it were a\l"
    .string "plague in the house:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_36::
    .string "Then the priest shall command\n"
    .string "that they empty the house, before\l"
    .string "the priest go into it to see the\l"
    .string "plague, that all that is in the\l"
    .string "house be not made unclean: and\l"
    .string "afterward the priest shall go in to\l"
    .string "see the house:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_37::
    .string "And he shall look on the plague,\n"
    .string "and, behold, if the plague be in\l"
    .string "the walls of the house with hollow\l"
    .string "strakes, greenish or reddish, which\l"
    .string "in sight are lower than the wall;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_38::
    .string "Then the priest shall go out of\n"
    .string "the house to the door of the house,\l"
    .string "and shut up the house seven days:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_39::
    .string "And the priest shall come again\n"
    .string "the seventh day, and shall look:\l"
    .string "and, behold, if the plague be\l"
    .string "spread in the walls of the house;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_40::
    .string "Then the priest shall command\n"
    .string "that they take away the stones in\l"
    .string "which the plague is, and they\l"
    .string "shall cast them into an unclean\l"
    .string "place without the city:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_41::
    .string "And he shall cause the house to be\n"
    .string "scraped within round about, and they\l"
    .string "shall pour out the dust that they\l"
    .string "scrape off without the city into an\l"
    .string "unclean place:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_42::
    .string "And they shall take other stones,\n"
    .string "and put them in the place of those\l"
    .string "stones; and he shall take other\l"
    .string "morter, and shall plaister the\l"
    .string "house$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_43::
    .string "And if the plague come again, and\n"
    .string "break out in the house, after that he\l"
    .string "hath taken away the stones, and after\l"
    .string "he hath scraped the house, and after\l"
    .string "it is plaistered;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_44::
    .string "Then the priest shall come and\n"
    .string "look, and, behold, if the plague be\l"
    .string "spread in the house, it is a fretting\l"
    .string "leprosy in the house; it is unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_45::
    .string "And he shall break down the house,\n"
    .string "the stones of it, and the timber\l"
    .string "thereof, and all the morter of the\l"
    .string "house; and he shall carry them forth\l"
    .string "out of the city into an unclean\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_46::
    .string "Moreover he that goeth into the\n"
    .string "house all the while that it is shut\l"
    .string "up shall be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_47::
    .string "And he that lieth in the house\n"
    .string "shall wash his clothes; and he that\l"
    .string "eateth in the house shall wash his\l"
    .string "clothes.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_48::
    .string "And if the priest shall come in,\n"
    .string "and look upon it, and, behold, the\l"
    .string "plague hath not spread in the house,\l"
    .string "after the house was plaistered:\l"
    .string "then the priest shall pronounce\l"
    .string "the house clean, because the plague\l"
    .string "is healed.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_49::
    .string "And he shall take to cleanse the\n"
    .string "house two birds, and cedar wood, and\l"
    .string "scarlet, and hyssop:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_50::
    .string "And he shall kill the one of the\n"
    .string "birds in an earthen vessel over\l"
    .string "running water:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_51::
    .string "And he shall take the cedar wood,\n"
    .string "and the hyssop, and the scarlet, and\l"
    .string "the living bird, and dip them in the\l"
    .string "blood of the slain bird, and in the\l"
    .string "running water, and sprinkle the\l"
    .string "house seven times:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_52::
    .string "And he shall cleanse the house\n"
    .string "with the blood of the bird, and with\l"
    .string "the running water, and with the\l"
    .string "living bird, and with the cedar wood,\l"
    .string "and with the hyssop, and with the\l"
    .string "scarlet:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_53::
    .string "But he shall let go the living\n"
    .string "bird out of the city into the open\l"
    .string "fields, and make an atonement for\l"
    .string "the house: and it shall be clean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_54::
    .string "This is the law for all manner of\n"
    .string "plague of leprosy, and scall,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_55::
    .string "And for the leprosy of a garment,\n"
    .string "and of a house,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_56::
    .string "And for a rising, and for a scab, and\n"
    .string "for a bright spot:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_14_57::
    .string "To teach when it is unclean, and\n"
    .string "when it is clean: this is the law of\l"
    .string "leprosy$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "to Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, When any man hath a\l"
    .string "running issue out of his flesh,\l"
    .string "because of his issue he is unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_3::
    .string "And this shall be his uncleanness\n"
    .string "in his issue: whether his flesh run\l"
    .string "with his issue, or his flesh be\l"
    .string "stopped from his issue, it is his\l"
    .string "uncleanness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_4::
    .string "Every bed, whereon he lieth that\n"
    .string "hath the issue, is unclean: and\l"
    .string "every thing, whereon he sitteth,\l"
    .string "shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_5::
    .string "And whosoever toucheth his bed\n"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and bathe\l"
    .string "himself in water, and be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_6::
    .string "And he that sitteth on any thing\n"
    .string "whereon he sat that hath the issue\l"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and bathe\l"
    .string "himself in water, and be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_7::
    .string "And he that toucheth the flesh of\n"
    .string "him that hath the issue shall wash\l"
    .string "his clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_8::
    .string "And if he that hath the issue spit\n"
    .string "upon him that is clean; then he\l"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and bathe\l"
    .string "himself in water, and be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_9::
    .string "And what saddle soever he rideth\n"
    .string "upon that hath the issue shall be\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_10::
    .string "And whosoever toucheth any thing\n"
    .string "that was under him shall be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even: and he that beareth\l"
    .string "any of those things shall wash his\l"
    .string "clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_11::
    .string "And whomsoever he toucheth that\n"
    .string "hath the issue, and hath not rinsed\l"
    .string "his hands in water, he shall wash\l"
    .string "his clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_12::
    .string "And the vessel of earth, that he\n"
    .string "toucheth which hath the issue,\l"
    .string "shall be broken: and every vessel\l"
    .string "of wood shall be rinsed in water.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_13::
    .string "And when he that hath an issue is\n"
    .string "cleansed of his issue; then he\l"
    .string "shall number to himself seven days\l"
    .string "for his cleansing, and wash his\l"
    .string "clothes, and bathe his flesh in\l"
    .string "running water, and shall be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_14::
    .string "And on the eighth day he shall take\n"
    .string "to him two turtledoves, or two young\l"
    .string "pigeons, and come before the LORD\l"
    .string "unto the door of the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation, and give them unto\l"
    .string "the priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_15::
    .string "And the priest shall offer them,\n"
    .string "the one for a sin offering, and the\l"
    .string "other for a burnt offering; and the\l"
    .string "priest shall make an atonement for\l"
    .string "him before the LORD for his issue$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_16::
    .string "And if any man’s seed of\n"
    .string "copulation go out from him, then he\l"
    .string "shall wash all his flesh in water,\l"
    .string "and be unclean until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_17::
    .string "And every garment, and every skin,\n"
    .string "whereon is the seed of copulation,\l"
    .string "shall be washed with water, and be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_18::
    .string "The woman also with whom man shall\n"
    .string "lie with seed of copulation, they\l"
    .string "shall both bathe themselves in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_19::
    .string "And if a woman have an issue, and her\n"
    .string "issue in her flesh be blood, she\l"
    .string "shall be put apart seven days: and\l"
    .string "whosoever toucheth her shall be\l"
    .string "unclean until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_20::
    .string "And every thing that she lieth\n"
    .string "upon in her separation shall be\l"
    .string "unclean: every thing also that she\l"
    .string "sitteth upon shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_21::
    .string "And whosoever toucheth her bed\n"
    .string "shall wash his clothes, and bathe\l"
    .string "himself in water, and be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_22::
    .string "And whosoever toucheth any thing\n"
    .string "that she sat upon shall wash his\l"
    .string "clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_23::
    .string "And if it be on her bed, or on any\n"
    .string "thing whereon she sitteth, when he\l"
    .string "toucheth it, he shall be unclean\l"
    .string "until the even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_24::
    .string "And if any man lie with her at all,\n"
    .string "and her flowers be upon him, he\l"
    .string "shall be unclean seven days; and\l"
    .string "all the bed whereon he lieth\l"
    .string "shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_25::
    .string "And if a woman have an issue of her\n"
    .string "blood many days out of the time of\l"
    .string "her separation, or if it run beyond\l"
    .string "the time of her separation; all the\l"
    .string "days of the issue of her uncleanness\l"
    .string "shall be as the days of her\l"
    .string "separation: she shall be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_26::
    .string "Every bed whereon she lieth all\n"
    .string "the days of her issue shall be unto\l"
    .string "her as the bed of her separation: and\l"
    .string "whatsoever she sitteth upon shall\l"
    .string "be unclean, as the uncleanness of\l"
    .string "her separation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_27::
    .string "And whosoever toucheth those things\n"
    .string "shall be unclean, and shall wash\l"
    .string "his clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_28::
    .string "But if she be cleansed of her issue,\n"
    .string "then she shall number to herself\l"
    .string "seven days, and after that she shall\l"
    .string "be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_29::
    .string "And on the eighth day she shall\n"
    .string "take unto her two turtles, or two\l"
    .string "young pigeons, and bring them unto\l"
    .string "the priest, to the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_30::
    .string "And the priest shall offer the one\n"
    .string "for a sin offering, and the other for\l"
    .string "a burnt offering; and the priest\l"
    .string "shall make an atonement for her\l"
    .string "before the LORD for the issue of her\l"
    .string "uncleanness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_31::
    .string "Thus shall ye separate the\n"
    .string "children of Israel from their\l"
    .string "uncleanness; that they die not in\l"
    .string "their uncleanness, when they defile\l"
    .string "my tabernacle that is among them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_32::
    .string "This is the law of him that hath an\n"
    .string "issue, and of him whose seed goeth\l"
    .string "from him, and is defiled therewith;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_15_33::
    .string "And of her that is sick of her\n"
    .string "flowers, and of him that hath an\l"
    .string "issue, of the man, and of the woman,\l"
    .string "and of him that lieth with her that\l"
    .string "is unclean$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses after\n"
    .string "the death of the two sons of Aaron,\l"
    .string "when they offered before the LORD,\l"
    .string "and died;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Speak\n"
    .string "unto Aaron thy brother, that he come\l"
    .string "not at all times into the holy\l"
    .string "place within the vail before the\l"
    .string "mercy seat, which is upon the ark;\l"
    .string "that he die not: for I will appear\l"
    .string "in the cloud upon the mercy seat$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_3::
    .string "Thus shall Aaron come into the\n"
    .string "holy place: with a young bullock\l"
    .string "for a sin offering, and a ram for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_4::
    .string "He shall put on the holy linen\n"
    .string "coat, and he shall have the linen\l"
    .string "breeches upon his flesh, and shall\l"
    .string "be girded with a linen girdle, and\l"
    .string "with the linen mitre shall he be\l"
    .string "attired: these are holy garments;\l"
    .string "therefore shall he wash his flesh\l"
    .string "in water, and so put them on.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_5::
    .string "And he shall take of the\n"
    .string "congregation of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel two kids of the goats for a\l"
    .string "sin offering, and one ram for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_6::
    .string "And Aaron shall offer his bullock\n"
    .string "of the sin offering, which is for\l"
    .string "himself, and make an atonement for\l"
    .string "himself, and for his house.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_7::
    .string "And he shall take the two goats,\n"
    .string "and present them before the LORD at\l"
    .string "the door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_8::
    .string "And Aaron shall cast lots upon\n"
    .string "the two goats; one lot for the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the other lot for the scapegoat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_9::
    .string "And Aaron shall bring the goat\n"
    .string "upon which the LORD’s lot fell,\l"
    .string "and offer him for a sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_10::
    .string "But the goat, on which the lot\n"
    .string "fell to be the scapegoat, shall be\l"
    .string "presented alive before the LORD, to\l"
    .string "make an atonement with him, and to\l"
    .string "let him go for a scapegoat into the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_11::
    .string "And Aaron shall bring the bullock\n"
    .string "of the sin offering, which is for\l"
    .string "himself, and shall make an\l"
    .string "atonement for himself, and for his\l"
    .string "house, and shall kill the bullock\l"
    .string "of the sin offering which is for\l"
    .string "himself:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_12::
    .string "And he shall take a censer full\n"
    .string "of burning coals of fire from off\l"
    .string "the altar before the LORD, and his\l"
    .string "hands full of sweet incense beaten\l"
    .string "small, and bring it within the\l"
    .string "vail:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_13::
    .string "And he shall put the incense upon\n"
    .string "the fire before the LORD, that the\l"
    .string "cloud of the incense may cover the\l"
    .string "mercy seat that is upon the\l"
    .string "testimony, that he die not:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_14::
    .string "And he shall take of the blood of\n"
    .string "the bullock, and sprinkle it with\l"
    .string "his finger upon the mercy seat\l"
    .string "eastward; and before the mercy seat\l"
    .string "shall he sprinkle of the blood\l"
    .string "with his finger seven times$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_15::
    .string "Then shall he kill the goat of\n"
    .string "the sin offering, that is for the\l"
    .string "people, and bring his blood within\l"
    .string "the vail, and do with that blood as\l"
    .string "he did with the blood of the\l"
    .string "bullock, and sprinkle it upon the\l"
    .string "mercy seat, and before the mercy\l"
    .string "seat:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_16::
    .string "And he shall make an atonement for\n"
    .string "the holy place, because of the\l"
    .string "uncleanness of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and because of their\l"
    .string "transgressions in all their sins:\l"
    .string "and so shall he do for the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, that\l"
    .string "remaineth among them in the midst of\l"
    .string "their uncleanness$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_17::
    .string "And there shall be no man in the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation when\l"
    .string "he goeth in to make an atonement in\l"
    .string "the holy place, until he come out,\l"
    .string "and have made an atonement for\l"
    .string "himself, and for his household, and\l"
    .string "for all the congregation of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_18::
    .string "And he shall go out unto the altar\n"
    .string "that is before the LORD, and make an\l"
    .string "atonement for it; and shall take of\l"
    .string "the blood of the bullock, and of\l"
    .string "the blood of the goat, and put it\l"
    .string "upon the horns of the altar round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_19::
    .string "And he shall sprinkle of the\n"
    .string "blood upon it with his finger seven\l"
    .string "times, and cleanse it, and hallow\l"
    .string "it from the uncleanness of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_20::
    .string "And when he hath made an end of\n"
    .string "reconciling the holy place, and\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "and the altar, he shall bring the\l"
    .string "live goat:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_21::
    .string "And Aaron shall lay both his hands\n"
    .string "upon the head of the live goat, and\l"
    .string "confess over him all the iniquities\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel, and all\l"
    .string "their transgressions in all their\l"
    .string "sins, putting them upon the head of\l"
    .string "the goat, and shall send him away by\l"
    .string "the hand of a fit man into the\l"
    .string "wilderness:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_22::
    .string "And the goat shall bear upon him\n"
    .string "all their iniquities unto a land\l"
    .string "not inhabited: and he shall let go\l"
    .string "the goat in the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_23::
    .string "And Aaron shall come into the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "shall put off the linen garments,\l"
    .string "which he put on when he went into the\l"
    .string "holy place, and shall leave them\l"
    .string "there:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_24::
    .string "And he shall wash his flesh with\n"
    .string "water in the holy place, and put on\l"
    .string "his garments, and come forth, and\l"
    .string "offer his burnt offering, and the\l"
    .string "burnt offering of the people, and\l"
    .string "make an atonement for himself, and\l"
    .string "for the people$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_25::
    .string "And the fat of the sin offering\n"
    .string "shall he burn upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_26::
    .string "And he that let go the goat for the\n"
    .string "scapegoat shall wash his clothes,\l"
    .string "and bathe his flesh in water, and\l"
    .string "afterward come into the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_27::
    .string "And the bullock for the sin\n"
    .string "offering, and the goat for the sin\l"
    .string "offering, whose blood was brought in\l"
    .string "to make atonement in the holy\l"
    .string "place, shall one carry forth\l"
    .string "without the camp; and they shall\l"
    .string "burn in the fire their skins, and\l"
    .string "their flesh, and their dung.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_28::
    .string "And he that burneth them shall\n"
    .string "wash his clothes, and bathe his\l"
    .string "flesh in water, and afterward he\l"
    .string "shall come into the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_29::
    .string "And this shall be a statute for\n"
    .string "ever unto you: that in the seventh\l"
    .string "month, on the tenth day of the month,\l"
    .string "ye shall afflict your souls, and\l"
    .string "do no work at all, whether it be one\l"
    .string "of your own country, or a stranger\l"
    .string "that sojourneth among you:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_30::
    .string "For on that day shall the priest\n"
    .string "make an atonement for you, to\l"
    .string "cleanse you, that ye may be clean\l"
    .string "from all your sins before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_31::
    .string "It shall be a sabbath of rest unto\n"
    .string "you, and ye shall afflict your\l"
    .string "souls, by a statute for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_32::
    .string "And the priest, whom he shall\n"
    .string "anoint, and whom he shall\l"
    .string "consecrate to minister in the\l"
    .string "priest’s office in his father’s\l"
    .string "stead, shall make the atonement,\l"
    .string "and shall put on the linen\l"
    .string "clothes, even the holy garments:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_33::
    .string "And he shall make an atonement for\n"
    .string "the holy sanctuary, and he shall\l"
    .string "make an atonement for the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation, and for the\l"
    .string "altar, and he shall make an\l"
    .string "atonement for the priests, and for\l"
    .string "all the people of the congregation$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_16_34::
    .string "And this shall be an everlasting\n"
    .string "statute unto you, to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for the children of\l"
    .string "Israel for all their sins once a\l"
    .string "year. And he did as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_2::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron, and unto his\n"
    .string "sons, and unto all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and say unto them; This is\l"
    .string "the thing which the LORD hath\l"
    .string "commanded, saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_3::
    .string "What man soever there be of the\n"
    .string "house of Israel, that killeth an\l"
    .string "ox, or lamb, or goat, in the camp, or\l"
    .string "that killeth it out of the camp,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_4::
    .string "And bringeth it not unto the door of\n"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "to offer an offering unto the LORD\l"
    .string "before the tabernacle of the LORD;\l"
    .string "blood shall be imputed unto that\l"
    .string "man; he hath shed blood; and that man\l"
    .string "shall be cut off from among his\l"
    .string "people:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_5::
    .string "To the end that the children of\n"
    .string "Israel may bring their sacrifices,\l"
    .string "which they offer in the open field,\l"
    .string "even that they may bring them unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, unto the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, unto\l"
    .string "the priest, and offer them for peace\l"
    .string "offerings unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_6::
    .string "And the priest shall sprinkle\n"
    .string "the blood upon the altar of the\l"
    .string "LORD at the door of the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation, and burn the fat\l"
    .string "for a sweet savour unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_7::
    .string "And they shall no more offer their\n"
    .string "sacrifices unto devils, after whom\l"
    .string "they have gone a whoring. This shall\l"
    .string "be a statute for ever unto them\l"
    .string "throughout their generations.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_8::
    .string "And thou shalt say unto them,\n"
    .string "Whatsoever man there be of the house\l"
    .string "of Israel, or of the strangers which\l"
    .string "sojourn among you, that offereth a\l"
    .string "burnt offering or sacrifice,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_9::
    .string "And bringeth it not unto the door of\n"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "to offer it unto the LORD; even that\l"
    .string "man shall be cut off from among his\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_10::
    .string "And whatsoever man there be of the\n"
    .string "house of Israel, or of the strangers\l"
    .string "that sojourn among you, that eateth\l"
    .string "any manner of blood; I will even\l"
    .string "set my face against that soul that\l"
    .string "eateth blood, and will cut him off\l"
    .string "from among his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_11::
    .string "For the life of the flesh is in the\n"
    .string "blood: and I have given it to you\l"
    .string "upon the altar to make an atonement\l"
    .string "for your souls: for it is the blood\l"
    .string "that maketh an atonement for the\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_12::
    .string "Therefore I said unto the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, No soul of you shall eat\l"
    .string "blood, neither shall any stranger\l"
    .string "that sojourneth among you eat blood.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_13::
    .string "And whatsoever man there be of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, or of the\l"
    .string "strangers that sojourn among you,\l"
    .string "which hunteth and catcheth any beast\l"
    .string "or fowl that may be eaten; he shall\l"
    .string "even pour out the blood thereof, and\l"
    .string "cover it with dust.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_14::
    .string "For it is the life of all flesh;\n"
    .string "the blood of it is for the life\l"
    .string "thereof: therefore I said unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, Ye shall eat\l"
    .string "the blood of no manner of flesh: for\l"
    .string "the life of all flesh is the blood\l"
    .string "thereof: whosoever eateth it shall\l"
    .string "be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_15::
    .string "And every soul that eateth that\n"
    .string "which died of itself, or that which\l"
    .string "was torn with beasts, whether it be\l"
    .string "one of your own country, or a\l"
    .string "stranger, he shall both wash his\l"
    .string "clothes, and bathe himself in\l"
    .string "water, and be unclean until the\l"
    .string "even: then shall he be clean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_17_16::
    .string "But if he wash them not, nor bathe\n"
    .string "his flesh; then he shall bear his\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, I am the LORD your\l"
    .string "God$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_3::
    .string "After the doings of the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt, wherein ye dwelt, shall ye\l"
    .string "not do: and after the doings of the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan, whither I bring you,\l"
    .string "shall ye not do: neither shall ye\l"
    .string "walk in their ordinances.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_4::
    .string "Ye shall do my judgments, and keep\n"
    .string "mine ordinances, to walk therein: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_5::
    .string "Ye shall therefore keep my\n"
    .string "statutes, and my judgments: which if\l"
    .string "a man do, he shall live in them: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_6::
    .string "None of you shall approach to any\n"
    .string "that is near of kin to him, to uncover\l"
    .string "their nakedness: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_7::
    .string "The nakedness of thy father, or the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy mother, shalt thou\l"
    .string "not uncover: she is thy mother; thou\l"
    .string "shalt not uncover her nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_8::
    .string "The nakedness of thy father’s wife\n"
    .string "shalt thou not uncover: it is thy\l"
    .string "father’s nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_9::
    .string "The nakedness of thy sister, the\n"
    .string "daughter of thy father, or daughter\l"
    .string "of thy mother, whether she be born at\l"
    .string "home, or born abroad, even their\l"
    .string "nakedness thou shalt not uncover.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_10::
    .string "The nakedness of thy son’s daughter,\n"
    .string "or of thy daughter’s daughter, even\l"
    .string "their nakedness thou shalt not\l"
    .string "uncover: for theirs is thine own\l"
    .string "nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_11::
    .string "The nakedness of thy father’s\n"
    .string "wife’s daughter, begotten of thy\l"
    .string "father, she is thy sister, thou\l"
    .string "shalt not uncover her nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_12::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy father’s sister: she\l"
    .string "is thy father’s near kinswoman.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_13::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy mother’s sister: for\l"
    .string "she is thy mother’s near kinswoman.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_14::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy father’s brother,\l"
    .string "thou shalt not approach to his\l"
    .string "wife: she is thine aunt.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_15::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy daughter in law:\l"
    .string "she is thy son’s wife; thou shalt not\l"
    .string "uncover her nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_16::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy brother’s wife: it\l"
    .string "is thy brother’s nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_17::
    .string "Thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of a woman and her\l"
    .string "daughter, neither shalt thou take\l"
    .string "her son’s daughter, or her daughter’s\l"
    .string "daughter, to uncover her nakedness;\l"
    .string "for they are her near kinswomen: it\l"
    .string "is wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_18::
    .string "Neither shalt thou take a wife to\n"
    .string "her sister, to vex her, to uncover\l"
    .string "her nakedness, beside the other in\l"
    .string "her life time.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_19::
    .string "Also thou shalt not approach unto\n"
    .string "a woman to uncover her nakedness, as\l"
    .string "long as she is put apart for her\l"
    .string "uncleanness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_20::
    .string "Moreover thou shalt not lie\n"
    .string "carnally with thy neighbour’s wife,\l"
    .string "to defile thyself with her.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_21::
    .string "And thou shalt not let any of thy\n"
    .string "seed pass through the fire to\l"
    .string "Molech, neither shalt thou profane\l"
    .string "the name of thy God: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_22::
    .string "Thou shalt not lie with mankind, as\n"
    .string "with womankind: it is abomination.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_23::
    .string "Neither shalt thou lie with any\n"
    .string "beast to defile thyself therewith:\l"
    .string "neither shall any woman stand\l"
    .string "before a beast to lie down thereto:\l"
    .string "it is confusion.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_24::
    .string "Defile not ye yourselves in any of\n"
    .string "these things: for in all these the\l"
    .string "nations are defiled which I cast out\l"
    .string "before you:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_25::
    .string "And the land is defiled: therefore\n"
    .string "I do visit the iniquity thereof upon\l"
    .string "it, and the land itself vomiteth out\l"
    .string "her inhabitants$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_26::
    .string "Ye shall therefore keep my\n"
    .string "statutes and my judgments, and\l"
    .string "shall not commit any of these\l"
    .string "abominations; neither any of your own\l"
    .string "nation, nor any stranger that\l"
    .string "sojourneth among you:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_27::
    .string "(For all these abominations have\n"
    .string "the men of the land done, which were\l"
    .string "before you, and the land is\l"
    .string "defiled;)"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_28::
    .string "That the land spue not you out\n"
    .string "also, when ye defile it, as it\l"
    .string "spued out the nations that were\l"
    .string "before you$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_29::
    .string "For whosoever shall commit any of\n"
    .string "these abominations, even the souls\l"
    .string "that commit them shall be cut off\l"
    .string "from among their people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_18_30::
    .string "Therefore shall ye keep mine\n"
    .string "ordinance, that ye commit not any one\l"
    .string "of these abominable customs, which\l"
    .string "were committed before you, and that\l"
    .string "ye defile not yourselves therein: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_2::
    .string "Speak unto all the congregation\n"
    .string "of the children of Israel, and say\l"
    .string "unto them, Ye shall be holy: for I\l"
    .string "the LORD your God am holy$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_3::
    .string "Ye shall fear every man his mother,\n"
    .string "and his father, and keep my\l"
    .string "sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_4::
    .string "Turn ye not unto idols, nor make to\n"
    .string "yourselves molten gods: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_5::
    .string "And if ye offer a sacrifice of\n"
    .string "peace offerings unto the LORD, ye\l"
    .string "shall offer it at your own will.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_6::
    .string "It shall be eaten the same day ye\n"
    .string "offer it, and on the morrow: and if\l"
    .string "ought remain until the third day, it\l"
    .string "shall be burnt in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_7::
    .string "And if it be eaten at all on the\n"
    .string "third day, it is abominable; it\l"
    .string "shall not be accepted.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_8::
    .string "Therefore every one that eateth it\n"
    .string "shall bear his iniquity, because he\l"
    .string "hath profaned the hallowed thing\l"
    .string "of the LORD: and that soul shall be\l"
    .string "cut off from among his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_9::
    .string "And when ye reap the harvest of\n"
    .string "your land, thou shalt not wholly\l"
    .string "reap the corners of thy field,\l"
    .string "neither shalt thou gather the\l"
    .string "gleanings of thy harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_10::
    .string "And thou shalt not glean thy\n"
    .string "vineyard, neither shalt thou gather\l"
    .string "every grape of thy vineyard; thou\l"
    .string "shalt leave them for the poor and\l"
    .string "stranger: I am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_11::
    .string "Ye shall not steal, neither deal\n"
    .string "falsely, neither lie one to\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_12::
    .string "And ye shall not swear by my name\n"
    .string "falsely, neither shalt thou\l"
    .string "profane the name of thy God: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_13::
    .string "Thou shalt not defraud thy\n"
    .string "neighbour, neither rob him: the wages\l"
    .string "of him that is hired shall not abide\l"
    .string "with thee all night until the\l"
    .string "morning.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_14::
    .string "Thou shalt not curse the deaf, nor\n"
    .string "put a stumblingblock before the\l"
    .string "blind, but shalt fear thy God: I am\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_15::
    .string "Ye shall do no unrighteousness in\n"
    .string "judgment: thou shalt not respect\l"
    .string "the person of the poor, nor honor\l"
    .string "the person of the mighty: but in\l"
    .string "righteousness shalt thou judge thy\l"
    .string "neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_16::
    .string "Thou shalt not go up and down as a\n"
    .string "talebearer among thy people:\l"
    .string "neither shalt thou stand against the\l"
    .string "blood of thy neighbour; I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_17::
    .string "Thou shalt not hate thy brother in\n"
    .string "thine heart: thou shalt in any wise\l"
    .string "rebuke thy neighbour, and not suffer\l"
    .string "sin upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_18::
    .string "Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any\n"
    .string "grudge against the children of thy\l"
    .string "people, but thou shalt love thy\l"
    .string "neighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_19::
    .string "Ye shall keep my statutes. Thou\n"
    .string "shalt not let thy cattle gender\l"
    .string "with a diverse kind: thou shalt not\l"
    .string "sow thy field with mingled seed:\l"
    .string "neither shall a garment mingled of\l"
    .string "linen and woollen come upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_20::
    .string "And whosoever lieth carnally with\n"
    .string "a woman, that is a bondmaid,\l"
    .string "betrothed to an husband, and not at\l"
    .string "all redeemed, nor freedom given\l"
    .string "her; she shall be scourged; they\l"
    .string "shall not be put to death, because\l"
    .string "she was not free.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_21::
    .string "And he shall bring his trespass\n"
    .string "offering unto the LORD, unto the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, even a ram for a\l"
    .string "trespass offering.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_22::
    .string "And the priest shall make an\n"
    .string "atonement for him with the ram of the\l"
    .string "trespass offering before the LORD\l"
    .string "for his sin which he hath done: and\l"
    .string "the sin which he hath done shall be\l"
    .string "forgiven him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_23::
    .string "And when ye shall come into the\n"
    .string "land, and shall have planted all\l"
    .string "manner of trees for food, then ye\l"
    .string "shall count the fruit thereof as\l"
    .string "uncircumcised: three years shall it\l"
    .string "be as uncircumcised unto you: it\l"
    .string "shall not be eaten of.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_24::
    .string "But in the fourth year all the\n"
    .string "fruit thereof shall be holy to\l"
    .string "praise the LORD withal.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_25::
    .string "And in the fifth year shall ye eat\n"
    .string "of the fruit thereof, that it may\l"
    .string "yield unto you the increase thereof:\l"
    .string "I am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_26::
    .string "Ye shall not eat any thing with the\n"
    .string "blood: neither shall ye use\l"
    .string "enchantment, nor observe times.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_27::
    .string "Ye shall not round the corners of\n"
    .string "your heads, neither shalt thou mar\l"
    .string "the corners of thy beard.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_28::
    .string "Ye shall not make any cuttings in\n"
    .string "your flesh for the dead, nor print\l"
    .string "any marks upon you: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_29::
    .string "Do not prostitute thy daughter, to\n"
    .string "cause her to be a whore; lest the\l"
    .string "land fall to whoredom, and the land\l"
    .string "become full of wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_30::
    .string "Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and\n"
    .string "reverence my sanctuary: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_31::
    .string "Regard not them that have familiar\n"
    .string "spirits, neither seek after wizards,\l"
    .string "to be defiled by them: I am the LORD\l"
    .string "your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_32::
    .string "Thou shalt rise up before the\n"
    .string "hoary head, and honour the face of\l"
    .string "the old man, and fear thy God: I am\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_33::
    .string "And if a stranger sojourn with thee\n"
    .string "in your land, ye shall not vex him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_34::
    .string "But the stranger that dwelleth\n"
    .string "with you shall be unto you as one\l"
    .string "born among you, and thou shalt love\l"
    .string "him as thyself; for ye were\l"
    .string "strangers in the land of Egypt: I am\l"
    .string "the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_35::
    .string "Ye shall do no unrighteousness in\n"
    .string "judgment, in meteyard, in weight, or\l"
    .string "in measure.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_36::
    .string "Just balances, just weights, a just\n"
    .string "ephah, and a just hin, shall ye\l"
    .string "have: I am the LORD your God, which\l"
    .string "brought you out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_19_37::
    .string "Therefore shall ye observe all my\n"
    .string "statutes, and all my judgments, and\l"
    .string "do them: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_2::
    .string "Again, thou shalt say to the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, Whosoever he be\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel, or of the\l"
    .string "strangers that sojourn in Israel,\l"
    .string "that giveth any of his seed unto\l"
    .string "Molech; he shall surely be put to\l"
    .string "death: the people of the land\l"
    .string "shall stone him with stones$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_3::
    .string "And I will set my face against that\n"
    .string "man, and will cut him off from among\l"
    .string "his people; because he hath given\l"
    .string "of his seed unto Molech, to defile\l"
    .string "my sanctuary, and to profane my holy\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_4::
    .string "And if the people of the land do\n"
    .string "any ways hide their eyes from the\l"
    .string "man, when he giveth of his seed unto\l"
    .string "Molech, and kill him not:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_5::
    .string "Then I will set my face against\n"
    .string "that man, and against his family,\l"
    .string "and will cut him off, and all that\l"
    .string "go a whoring after him, to commit\l"
    .string "whoredom with Molech, from among\l"
    .string "their people$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_6::
    .string "And the soul that turneth after\n"
    .string "such as have familiar spirits, and\l"
    .string "after wizards, to go a whoring after\l"
    .string "them, I will even set my face\l"
    .string "against that soul, and will cut him\l"
    .string "off from among his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_7::
    .string "Sanctify yourselves therefore, and\n"
    .string "be ye holy: for I am the LORD your\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_8::
    .string "And ye shall keep my statutes, and\n"
    .string "do them: I am the LORD which sanctify\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_9::
    .string "For every one that curseth his\n"
    .string "father or his mother shall be\l"
    .string "surely put to death: he hath cursed\l"
    .string "his father or his mother; his blood\l"
    .string "shall be upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_10::
    .string "And the man that committeth\n"
    .string "adultery with another man’s wife,\l"
    .string "even he that committeth adultery\l"
    .string "with his neighbour’s wife, the\l"
    .string "adulterer and the adulteress\l"
    .string "shall surely be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_11::
    .string "And the man that lieth with his\n"
    .string "father’s wife hath uncovered his\l"
    .string "father’s nakedness: both of them\l"
    .string "shall surely be put to death;\l"
    .string "their blood shall be upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_12::
    .string "And if a man lie with his daughter\n"
    .string "in law, both of them shall surely\l"
    .string "be put to death: they have wrought\l"
    .string "confusion; their blood shall be\l"
    .string "upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_13::
    .string "If a man also lie with mankind, as\n"
    .string "he lieth with a woman, both of them\l"
    .string "have committed an abomination: they\l"
    .string "shall surely be put to death;\l"
    .string "their blood shall be upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_14::
    .string "And if a man take a wife and her\n"
    .string "mother, it is wickedness: they\l"
    .string "shall be burnt with fire, both he\l"
    .string "and they; that there be no wickedness\l"
    .string "among you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_15::
    .string "And if a man lie with a beast, he\n"
    .string "shall surely be put to death: and\l"
    .string "ye shall slay the beast.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_16::
    .string "And if a woman approach unto any\n"
    .string "beast, and lie down thereto, thou\l"
    .string "shalt kill the woman, and the\l"
    .string "beast: they shall surely be put to\l"
    .string "death; their blood shall be upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_17::
    .string "And if a man shall take his sister,\n"
    .string "his father’s daughter, or his\l"
    .string "mother’s daughter, and see her\l"
    .string "nakedness, and she see his nakedness;\l"
    .string "it is a wicked thing; and they shall\l"
    .string "be cut off in the sight of their\l"
    .string "people: he hath uncovered his\l"
    .string "sister’s nakedness; he shall bear\l"
    .string "his iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_18::
    .string "And if a man shall lie with a\n"
    .string "woman having her sickness, and\l"
    .string "shall uncover her nakedness; he\l"
    .string "hath discovered her fountain, and she\l"
    .string "hath uncovered the fountain of her\l"
    .string "blood: and both of them shall be\l"
    .string "cut off from among their people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_19::
    .string "And thou shalt not uncover the\n"
    .string "nakedness of thy mother’s sister, nor\l"
    .string "of thy father’s sister: for he\l"
    .string "uncovereth his near kin: they shall\l"
    .string "bear their iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_20::
    .string "And if a man shall lie with his\n"
    .string "uncle’s wife, he hath uncovered his\l"
    .string "uncle’s nakedness: they shall bear\l"
    .string "their sin; they shall die\l"
    .string "childless.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_21::
    .string "And if a man shall take his\n"
    .string "brother’s wife, it is an unclean\l"
    .string "thing: he hath uncovered his\l"
    .string "brother’s nakedness; they shall be\l"
    .string "childless.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_22::
    .string "Ye shall therefore keep all my\n"
    .string "statutes, and all my judgments, and\l"
    .string "do them: that the land, whither I\l"
    .string "bring you to dwell therein, spue\l"
    .string "you not out.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_23::
    .string "And ye shall not walk in the\n"
    .string "manners of the nation, which I cast\l"
    .string "out before you: for they committed\l"
    .string "all these things, and therefore I\l"
    .string "abhorred them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_24::
    .string "But I have said unto you, Ye shall\n"
    .string "inherit their land, and I will give\l"
    .string "it unto you to possess it, a land\l"
    .string "that floweth with milk and honey: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD your God, which have\l"
    .string "separated you from other people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_25::
    .string "Ye shall therefore put difference\n"
    .string "between clean beasts and unclean,\l"
    .string "and between unclean fowls and\l"
    .string "clean: and ye shall not make your\l"
    .string "souls abominable by beast, or by\l"
    .string "fowl, or by any manner of living\l"
    .string "thing that creepeth on the ground,\l"
    .string "which I have separated from you as\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_26::
    .string "And ye shall be holy unto me: for I\n"
    .string "the LORD am holy, and have severed\l"
    .string "you from other people, that ye\l"
    .string "should be mine.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_20_27::
    .string "A man also or woman that hath a\n"
    .string "familiar spirit, or that is a\l"
    .string "wizard, shall surely be put to\l"
    .string "death: they shall stone them with\l"
    .string "stones: their blood shall be upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Speak\n"
    .string "unto the priests the sons of Aaron,\l"
    .string "and say unto them, There shall none\l"
    .string "be defiled for the dead among his\l"
    .string "people:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_2::
    .string "But for his kin, that is near unto\n"
    .string "him, that is, for his mother, and for\l"
    .string "his father, and for his son, and for\l"
    .string "his daughter, and for his brother$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_3::
    .string "And for his sister a virgin, that is\n"
    .string "nigh unto him, which hath had no\l"
    .string "husband; for her may he be defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_4::
    .string "But he shall not defile himself,\n"
    .string "being a chief man among his people,\l"
    .string "to profane himself.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_5::
    .string "They shall not make baldness upon\n"
    .string "their head, neither shall they\l"
    .string "shave off the corner of their beard,\l"
    .string "nor make any cuttings in their flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_6::
    .string "They shall be holy unto their God,\n"
    .string "and not profane the name of their\l"
    .string "God: for the offerings of the LORD\l"
    .string "made by fire, and the bread of their\l"
    .string "God, they do offer: therefore they\l"
    .string "shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_7::
    .string "They shall not take a wife that is\n"
    .string "a whore, or profane; neither shall\l"
    .string "they take a woman put away from her\l"
    .string "husband: for he is holy unto his God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_8::
    .string "Thou shalt sanctify him therefore;\n"
    .string "for he offereth the bread of thy God:\l"
    .string "he shall be holy unto thee: for I\l"
    .string "the LORD, which sanctify you, am\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_9::
    .string "And the daughter of any priest, if\n"
    .string "she profane herself by playing the\l"
    .string "whore, she profaneth her father: she\l"
    .string "shall be burnt with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_10::
    .string "And he that is the high priest\n"
    .string "among his brethren, upon whose head\l"
    .string "the anointing oil was poured, and\l"
    .string "that is consecrated to put on the\l"
    .string "garments, shall not uncover his\l"
    .string "head, nor rend his clothes;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_11::
    .string "Neither shall he go in to any dead\n"
    .string "body, nor defile himself for his\l"
    .string "father, or for his mother;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_12::
    .string "Neither shall he go out of the\n"
    .string "sanctuary, nor profane the sanctuary\l"
    .string "of his God; for the crown of the\l"
    .string "anointing oil of his God is upon\l"
    .string "him: I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_13::
    .string "And he shall take a wife in her\n"
    .string "virginity.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_14::
    .string "A widow, or a divorced woman, or\n"
    .string "profane, or an harlot, these shall\l"
    .string "he not take: but he shall take a\l"
    .string "virgin of his own people to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_15::
    .string "Neither shall he profane his seed\n"
    .string "among his people: for I the LORD do\l"
    .string "sanctify him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_16::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_17::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron, saying, Whosoever\n"
    .string "he be of thy seed in their\l"
    .string "generations that hath any blemish,\l"
    .string "let him not approach to offer the\l"
    .string "bread of his God$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_18::
    .string "For whatsoever man he be that hath a\n"
    .string "blemish, he shall not approach: a\l"
    .string "blind man, or a lame, or he that\l"
    .string "hath a flat nose, or any thing\l"
    .string "superfluous,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_19::
    .string "Or a man that is brokenfooted, or\n"
    .string "brokenhanded,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_20::
    .string "Or crookbackt, or a dwarf, or that\n"
    .string "hath a blemish in his eye, or be\l"
    .string "scurvy, or scabbed, or hath his\l"
    .string "stones broken;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_21::
    .string "No man that hath a blemish of the\n"
    .string "seed of Aaron the priest shall come\l"
    .string "nigh to offer the offerings of the\l"
    .string "LORD made by fire: he hath a blemish;\l"
    .string "he shall not come nigh to offer the\l"
    .string "bread of his God$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_22::
    .string "He shall eat the bread of his God,\n"
    .string "both of the most holy, and of the\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_23::
    .string "Only he shall not go in unto the\n"
    .string "vail, nor come nigh unto the altar,\l"
    .string "because he hath a blemish; that he\l"
    .string "profane not my sanctuaries: for I the\l"
    .string "LORD do sanctify them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_21_24::
    .string "And Moses told it unto Aaron, and to\n"
    .string "his sons, and unto all the children\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_2::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron and to his sons,\n"
    .string "that they separate themselves from\l"
    .string "the holy things of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and that they profane not my\l"
    .string "holy name in those things which they\l"
    .string "hallow unto me: I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_3::
    .string "Say unto them, Whosoever he be of\n"
    .string "all your seed among your\l"
    .string "generations, that goeth unto the\l"
    .string "holy things, which the children of\l"
    .string "Israel hallow unto the LORD, having\l"
    .string "his uncleanness upon him, that soul\l"
    .string "shall be cut off from my presence:\l"
    .string "I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_4::
    .string "What man soever of the seed of Aaron\n"
    .string "is a leper, or hath a running issue;\l"
    .string "he shall not eat of the holy\l"
    .string "things, until he be clean. And whoso\l"
    .string "toucheth any thing that is unclean\l"
    .string "by the dead, or a man whose seed goeth\l"
    .string "from him;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_5::
    .string "Or whosoever toucheth any creeping\n"
    .string "thing, whereby he may be made\l"
    .string "unclean, or a man of whom he may take\l"
    .string "uncleanness, whatsoever\l"
    .string "uncleanness he hath;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_6::
    .string "The soul which hath touched any\n"
    .string "such shall be unclean until even,\l"
    .string "and shall not eat of the holy\l"
    .string "things, unless he wash his flesh\l"
    .string "with water$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_7::
    .string "And when the sun is down, he shall\n"
    .string "be clean, and shall afterward eat\l"
    .string "of the holy things; because it is his\l"
    .string "food.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_8::
    .string "That which dieth of itself, or is\n"
    .string "torn with beasts, he shall not eat\l"
    .string "to defile himself therewith; I am\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_9::
    .string "They shall therefore keep mine\n"
    .string "ordinance, lest they bear sin for\l"
    .string "it, and die therefore, if they\l"
    .string "profane it: I the LORD do sanctify\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_10::
    .string "There shall no stranger eat of the\n"
    .string "holy thing: a sojourner of the\l"
    .string "priest, or an hired servant, shall\l"
    .string "not eat of the holy thing.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_11::
    .string "But if the priest buy any soul with\n"
    .string "his money, he shall eat of it, and\l"
    .string "he that is born in his house: they\l"
    .string "shall eat of his meat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_12::
    .string "If the priest’s daughter also be\n"
    .string "married unto a stranger, she may not\l"
    .string "eat of an offering of the holy\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_13::
    .string "But if the priest’s daughter be a\n"
    .string "widow, or divorced, and have no\l"
    .string "child, and is returned unto her\l"
    .string "father’s house, as in her youth, she\l"
    .string "shall eat of her father’s meat: but\l"
    .string "there shall be no stranger eat\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_14::
    .string "And if a man eat of the holy thing\n"
    .string "unwittingly, then he shall put the\l"
    .string "fifth part thereof unto it, and\l"
    .string "shall give it unto the priest with\l"
    .string "the holy thing.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_15::
    .string "And they shall not profane the\n"
    .string "holy things of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, which they offer unto the\l"
    .string "LORD;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_16::
    .string "Or suffer them to bear the iniquity\n"
    .string "of trespass, when they eat their\l"
    .string "holy things: for I the LORD do\l"
    .string "sanctify them$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_17::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_18::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron, and to his sons,\n"
    .string "and unto all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and say unto them,\l"
    .string "Whatsoever he be of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, or of the strangers in\l"
    .string "Israel, that will offer his\l"
    .string "oblation for all his vows, and for\l"
    .string "all his freewill offerings, which\l"
    .string "they will offer unto the LORD for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_19::
    .string "Ye shall offer at your own will a\n"
    .string "male without blemish, of the\l"
    .string "beeves, of the sheep, or of the goats$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_20::
    .string "But whatsoever hath a blemish, that\n"
    .string "shall ye not offer: for it shall\l"
    .string "not be acceptable for you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_21::
    .string "And whosoever offereth a sacrifice\n"
    .string "of peace offerings unto the LORD to\l"
    .string "accomplish his vow, or a freewill\l"
    .string "offering in beeves or sheep, it\l"
    .string "shall be perfect to be accepted;\l"
    .string "there shall be no blemish therein.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_22::
    .string "Blind, or broken, or maimed, or\n"
    .string "having a wen, or scurvy, or scabbed,\l"
    .string "ye shall not offer these unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, nor make an offering by fire of\l"
    .string "them upon the altar unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_23::
    .string "Either a bullock or a lamb that\n"
    .string "hath any thing superfluous or\l"
    .string "lacking in his parts, that mayest\l"
    .string "thou offer for a freewill offering;\l"
    .string "but for a vow it shall not be\l"
    .string "accepted.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_24::
    .string "Ye shall not offer unto the LORD\n"
    .string "that which is bruised, or crushed, or\l"
    .string "broken, or cut; neither shall ye\l"
    .string "make any offering thereof in your\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_25::
    .string "Neither from a stranger’s hand\n"
    .string "shall ye offer the bread of your God\l"
    .string "of any of these; because their\l"
    .string "corruption is in them, and\l"
    .string "blemishes be in them: they shall\l"
    .string "not be accepted for you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_26::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_27::
    .string "When a bullock, or a sheep, or a\n"
    .string "goat, is brought forth, then it\l"
    .string "shall be seven days under the dam;\l"
    .string "and from the eighth day and\l"
    .string "thenceforth it shall be accepted\l"
    .string "for an offering made by fire unto the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_28::
    .string "And whether it be cow, or ewe, ye\n"
    .string "shall not kill it and her young\l"
    .string "both in one day.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_29::
    .string "And when ye will offer a sacrifice\n"
    .string "of thanksgiving unto the LORD, offer\l"
    .string "it at your own will.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_30::
    .string "On the same day it shall be eaten\n"
    .string "up; ye shall leave none of it\l"
    .string "until the morrow: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_31::
    .string "Therefore shall ye keep my\n"
    .string "commandments, and do them: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_32::
    .string "Neither shall ye profane my holy\n"
    .string "name; but I will be hallowed among\l"
    .string "the children of Israel: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD which hallow you,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_22_33::
    .string "That brought you out of the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt, to be your God: I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, Concerning the\l"
    .string "feasts of the LORD, which ye shall\l"
    .string "proclaim to be holy convocations,\l"
    .string "even these are my feasts$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_3::
    .string "Six days shall work be done: but\n"
    .string "the seventh day is the sabbath of\l"
    .string "rest, an holy convocation; ye shall\l"
    .string "do no work therein: it is the sabbath\l"
    .string "of the LORD in all your dwellings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_4::
    .string "These are the feasts of the LORD,\n"
    .string "even holy convocations, which ye\l"
    .string "shall proclaim in their seasons.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_5::
    .string "In the fourteenth day of the first\n"
    .string "month at even is the LORD’s passover.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_6::
    .string "And on the fifteenth day of the same\n"
    .string "month is the feast of unleavened\l"
    .string "bread unto the LORD: seven days ye\l"
    .string "must eat unleavened bread.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_7::
    .string "In the first day ye shall have an\n"
    .string "holy convocation: ye shall do no\l"
    .string "servile work therein.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_8::
    .string "But ye shall offer an offering\n"
    .string "made by fire unto the LORD seven\l"
    .string "days: in the seventh day is an holy\l"
    .string "convocation: ye shall do no servile\l"
    .string "work therein.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_9::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_10::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, When ye be come\l"
    .string "into the land which I give unto you,\l"
    .string "and shall reap the harvest thereof,\l"
    .string "then ye shall bring a sheaf of the\l"
    .string "firstfruits of your harvest unto the\l"
    .string "priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_11::
    .string "And he shall wave the sheaf before\n"
    .string "the LORD, to be accepted for you: on\l"
    .string "the morrow after the sabbath the\l"
    .string "priest shall wave it$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_12::
    .string "And ye shall offer that day when ye\n"
    .string "wave the sheaf an he lamb without\l"
    .string "blemish of the first year for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_13::
    .string "And the meat offering thereof\n"
    .string "shall be two tenth deals of fine\l"
    .string "flour mingled with oil, an offering\l"
    .string "made by fire unto the LORD for a\l"
    .string "sweet savour: and the drink offering\l"
    .string "thereof shall be of wine, the fourth\l"
    .string "part of an hin.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_14::
    .string "And ye shall eat neither bread, nor\n"
    .string "parched corn, nor green ears, until\l"
    .string "the selfsame day that ye have\l"
    .string "brought an offering unto your God: it\l"
    .string "shall be a statute for ever\l"
    .string "throughout your generations in all\l"
    .string "your dwellings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_15::
    .string "And ye shall count unto you from\n"
    .string "the morrow after the sabbath, from\l"
    .string "the day that ye brought the sheaf of\l"
    .string "the wave offering; seven sabbaths\l"
    .string "shall be complete:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_16::
    .string "Even unto the morrow after the\n"
    .string "seventh sabbath shall ye number\l"
    .string "fifty days; and ye shall offer a new\l"
    .string "meat offering unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_17::
    .string "Ye shall bring out of your\n"
    .string "habitations two wave loaves of two\l"
    .string "tenth deals; they shall be of fine\l"
    .string "flour; they shall be baken with\l"
    .string "leaven; they are the firstfruits unto\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_18::
    .string "And ye shall offer with the bread\n"
    .string "seven lambs without blemish of the\l"
    .string "first year, and one young bullock,\l"
    .string "and two rams: they shall be for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering unto the LORD, with\l"
    .string "their meat offering, and their drink\l"
    .string "offerings, even an offering made by\l"
    .string "fire, of sweet savour unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_19::
    .string "Then ye shall sacrifice one kid of\n"
    .string "the goats for a sin offering, and two\l"
    .string "lambs of the first year for a\l"
    .string "sacrifice of peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_20::
    .string "And the priest shall wave them\n"
    .string "with the bread of the firstfruits for\l"
    .string "a wave offering before the LORD, with\l"
    .string "the two lambs: they shall be holy\l"
    .string "to the LORD for the priest.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_21::
    .string "And ye shall proclaim on the\n"
    .string "selfsame day, that it may be an holy\l"
    .string "convocation unto you: ye shall do no\l"
    .string "servile work therein: it shall be a\l"
    .string "statute for ever in all your\l"
    .string "dwellings throughout your\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_22::
    .string "And when ye reap the harvest of\n"
    .string "your land, thou shalt not make\l"
    .string "clean riddance of the corners of thy\l"
    .string "field when thou reapest, neither\l"
    .string "shalt thou gather any gleaning of\l"
    .string "thy harvest: thou shalt leave them\l"
    .string "unto the poor, and to the stranger: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_23::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_24::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, In the seventh month, in the\l"
    .string "first day of the month, shall ye\l"
    .string "have a sabbath, a memorial of\l"
    .string "blowing of trumpets, an holy\l"
    .string "convocation$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_25::
    .string "Ye shall do no servile work\n"
    .string "therein: but ye shall offer an\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_26::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_27::
    .string "Also on the tenth day of this\n"
    .string "seventh month there shall be a day\l"
    .string "of atonement: it shall be an holy\l"
    .string "convocation unto you; and ye shall\l"
    .string "afflict your souls, and offer an\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_28::
    .string "And ye shall do no work in that\n"
    .string "same day: for it is a day of\l"
    .string "atonement, to make an atonement for\l"
    .string "you before the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_29::
    .string "For whatsoever soul it be that\n"
    .string "shall not be afflicted in that same\l"
    .string "day, he shall be cut off from among\l"
    .string "his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_30::
    .string "And whatsoever soul it be that\n"
    .string "doeth any work in that same day, the\l"
    .string "same soul will I destroy from among\l"
    .string "his people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_31::
    .string "Ye shall do no manner of work: it\n"
    .string "shall be a statute for ever\l"
    .string "throughout your generations in all\l"
    .string "your dwellings.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_32::
    .string "It shall be unto you a sabbath of\n"
    .string "rest, and ye shall afflict your\l"
    .string "souls: in the ninth day of the month\l"
    .string "at even, from even unto even, shall\l"
    .string "ye celebrate your sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_33::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_34::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, The fifteenth day of this\l"
    .string "seventh month shall be the feast of\l"
    .string "tabernacles for seven days unto the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_35::
    .string "On the first day shall be an holy\n"
    .string "convocation: ye shall do no servile\l"
    .string "work therein.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_36::
    .string "Seven days ye shall offer an\n"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD:\l"
    .string "on the eighth day shall be an holy\l"
    .string "convocation unto you; and ye shall\l"
    .string "offer an offering made by fire unto\l"
    .string "the LORD: it is a solemn assembly;\l"
    .string "and ye shall do no servile work\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_37::
    .string "These are the feasts of the LORD,\n"
    .string "which ye shall proclaim to be\l"
    .string "holy convocations, to offer an\l"
    .string "offering made by fire unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "a burnt offering, and a meat\l"
    .string "offering, a sacrifice, and drink\l"
    .string "offerings, every thing upon his day:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_38::
    .string "Beside the sabbaths of the LORD, and\n"
    .string "beside your gifts, and beside all\l"
    .string "your vows, and beside all your\l"
    .string "freewill offerings, which ye give\l"
    .string "unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_39::
    .string "Also in the fifteenth day of the\n"
    .string "seventh month, when ye have gathered\l"
    .string "in the fruit of the land, ye shall\l"
    .string "keep a feast unto the LORD seven\l"
    .string "days: on the first day shall be a\l"
    .string "sabbath, and on the eighth day shall\l"
    .string "be a sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_40::
    .string "And ye shall take you on the first\n"
    .string "day the boughs of goodly trees,\l"
    .string "branches of palm trees, and the\l"
    .string "boughs of thick trees, and willows\l"
    .string "of the brook; and ye shall rejoice\l"
    .string "before the LORD your God seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_41::
    .string "And ye shall keep it a feast unto\n"
    .string "the LORD seven days in the year. It\l"
    .string "shall be a statute for ever in your\l"
    .string "generations: ye shall celebrate it\l"
    .string "in the seventh month.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_42::
    .string "Ye shall dwell in booths seven\n"
    .string "days; all that are Israelites born\l"
    .string "shall dwell in booths:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_43::
    .string "That your generations may know that\n"
    .string "I made the children of Israel to\l"
    .string "dwell in booths, when I brought them\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD your God$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_23_44::
    .string "And Moses declared unto the\n"
    .string "children of Israel the feasts of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_2::
    .string "Command the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "that they bring unto thee pure oil\l"
    .string "olive beaten for the light, to cause\l"
    .string "the lamps to burn continually$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_3::
    .string "Without the vail of the testimony,\n"
    .string "in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, shall Aaron order it\l"
    .string "from the evening unto the morning\l"
    .string "before the LORD continually: it\l"
    .string "shall be a statute for ever in your\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_4::
    .string "He shall order the lamps upon\n"
    .string "the pure candlestick before the\l"
    .string "LORD continually.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_5::
    .string "And thou shalt take fine flour, and\n"
    .string "bake twelve cakes thereof: two tenth\l"
    .string "deals shall be in one cake.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_6::
    .string "And thou shalt set them in two rows,\n"
    .string "six on a row, upon the pure table\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_7::
    .string "And thou shalt put pure\n"
    .string "frankincense upon each row, that it\l"
    .string "may be on the bread for a memorial,\l"
    .string "even an offering made by fire unto\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_8::
    .string "Every sabbath he shall set it in\n"
    .string "order before the LORD continually,\l"
    .string "being taken from the children of\l"
    .string "Israel by an everlasting covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_9::
    .string "And it shall be Aaron’s and his\n"
    .string "sons’; and they shall eat it in the\l"
    .string "holy place: for it is most holy\l"
    .string "unto him of the offerings of the LORD\l"
    .string "made by fire by a perpetual statute.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_10::
    .string "And the son of an Israelitish\n"
    .string "woman, whose father was an Egyptian,\l"
    .string "went out among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel: and this son of the\l"
    .string "Israelitish woman and a man of\l"
    .string "Israel strove together in the camp;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_11::
    .string "And the Israelitish woman’s son\n"
    .string "blasphemed the name of the Lord, and\l"
    .string "cursed. And they brought him unto\l"
    .string "Moses: (and his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of\l"
    .string "the tribe of Dan:)"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_12::
    .string "And they put him in ward, that the\n"
    .string "mind of the LORD might be shewed them$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_13::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_14::
    .string "Bring forth him that hath cursed\n"
    .string "without the camp; and let all that\l"
    .string "heard him lay their hands upon his\l"
    .string "head, and let all the congregation\l"
    .string "stone him$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_15::
    .string "And thou shalt speak unto the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, saying,\l"
    .string "Whosoever curseth his God shall\l"
    .string "bear his sin.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_16::
    .string "And he that blasphemeth the name\n"
    .string "of the LORD, he shall surely be put\l"
    .string "to death, and all the congregation\l"
    .string "shall certainly stone him: as\l"
    .string "well the stranger, as he that is\l"
    .string "born in the land, when he\l"
    .string "blasphemeth the name of the Lord,\l"
    .string "shall be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_17::
    .string "And he that killeth any man shall\n"
    .string "surely be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_18::
    .string "And he that killeth a beast shall\n"
    .string "make it good; beast for beast.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_19::
    .string "And if a man cause a blemish in his\n"
    .string "neighbour; as he hath done, so shall\l"
    .string "it be done to him;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_20::
    .string "Breach for breach, eye for eye,\n"
    .string "tooth for tooth: as he hath caused a\l"
    .string "blemish in a man, so shall it be\l"
    .string "done to him again$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_21::
    .string "And he that killeth a beast, he\n"
    .string "shall restore it: and he that\l"
    .string "killeth a man, he shall be put to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_22::
    .string "Ye shall have one manner of law,\n"
    .string "as well for the stranger, as for one\l"
    .string "of your own country: for I am the LORD\l"
    .string "your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_24_23::
    .string "And Moses spake to the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, that they should bring\l"
    .string "forth him that had cursed out of the\l"
    .string "camp, and stone him with stones. And\l"
    .string "the children of Israel did as the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses in\n"
    .string "mount Sinai, saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, When ye come into\l"
    .string "the land which I give you, then\l"
    .string "shall the land keep a sabbath unto\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_3::
    .string "Six years thou shalt sow thy field,\n"
    .string "and six years thou shalt prune thy\l"
    .string "vineyard, and gather in the fruit\l"
    .string "thereof;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_4::
    .string "But in the seventh year shall be a\n"
    .string "sabbath of rest unto the land, a\l"
    .string "sabbath for the LORD: thou shalt\l"
    .string "neither sow thy field, nor prune thy\l"
    .string "vineyard$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_5::
    .string "That which groweth of its own accord\n"
    .string "of thy harvest thou shalt not reap,\l"
    .string "neither gather the grapes of thy\l"
    .string "vine undressed: for it is a year of\l"
    .string "rest unto the land.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_6::
    .string "And the sabbath of the land shall\n"
    .string "be meat for you; for thee, and for thy\l"
    .string "servant, and for thy maid, and for\l"
    .string "thy hired servant, and for thy\l"
    .string "stranger that sojourneth with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_7::
    .string "And for thy cattle, and for the\n"
    .string "beast that are in thy land, shall\l"
    .string "all the increase thereof be meat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_8::
    .string "And thou shalt number seven\n"
    .string "sabbaths of years unto thee, seven\l"
    .string "times seven years; and the space of\l"
    .string "the seven sabbaths of years shall\l"
    .string "be unto thee forty and nine years.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_9::
    .string "Then shalt thou cause the trumpet\n"
    .string "of the jubile to sound on the tenth\l"
    .string "day of the seventh month, in the day\l"
    .string "of atonement shall ye make the\l"
    .string "trumpet sound throughout all your\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_10::
    .string "And ye shall hallow the fiftieth\n"
    .string "year, and proclaim liberty\l"
    .string "throughout all the land unto all\l"
    .string "the inhabitants thereof: it shall\l"
    .string "be a jubile unto you; and ye shall\l"
    .string "return every man unto his\l"
    .string "possession, and ye shall return\l"
    .string "every man unto his family.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_11::
    .string "A jubile shall that fiftieth year\n"
    .string "be unto you: ye shall not sow,\l"
    .string "neither reap that which groweth of\l"
    .string "itself in it, nor gather the grapes\l"
    .string "in it of thy vine undressed.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_12::
    .string "For it is the jubile; it shall be\n"
    .string "holy unto you: ye shall eat the\l"
    .string "increase thereof out of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_13::
    .string "In the year of this jubile ye\n"
    .string "shall return every man unto his\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_14::
    .string "And if thou sell ought unto thy\n"
    .string "neighbour, or buyest ought of thy\l"
    .string "neighbour’s hand, ye shall not\l"
    .string "oppress one another:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_15::
    .string "According to the number of years\n"
    .string "after the jubile thou shalt buy of\l"
    .string "thy neighbour, and according unto the\l"
    .string "number of years of the fruits he\l"
    .string "shall sell unto thee:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_16::
    .string "According to the multitude of years\n"
    .string "thou shalt increase the price\l"
    .string "thereof, and according to the fewness\l"
    .string "of years thou shalt diminish the\l"
    .string "price of it: for according to the\l"
    .string "number of the years of the fruits\l"
    .string "doth he sell unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_17::
    .string "Ye shall not therefore oppress\n"
    .string "one another; but thou shalt fear thy\l"
    .string "God: for I am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_18::
    .string "Wherefore ye shall do my statutes,\n"
    .string "and keep my judgments, and do them;\l"
    .string "and ye shall dwell in the land in\l"
    .string "safety.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_19::
    .string "And the land shall yield her\n"
    .string "fruit, and ye shall eat your fill,\l"
    .string "and dwell therein in safety.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_20::
    .string "And if ye shall say, What shall we\n"
    .string "eat the seventh year? behold, we\l"
    .string "shall not sow, nor gather in our\l"
    .string "increase:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_21::
    .string "Then I will command my blessing\n"
    .string "upon you in the sixth year, and it\l"
    .string "shall bring forth fruit for three\l"
    .string "years$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_22::
    .string "And ye shall sow the eighth year,\n"
    .string "and eat yet of old fruit until the\l"
    .string "ninth year; until her fruits come in\l"
    .string "ye shall eat of the old store.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_23::
    .string "The land shall not be sold for\n"
    .string "ever: for the land is mine, for ye\l"
    .string "are strangers and sojourners with me.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_24::
    .string "And in all the land of your\n"
    .string "possession ye shall grant a\l"
    .string "redemption for the land.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_25::
    .string "If thy brother be waxen poor, and\n"
    .string "hath sold away some of his\l"
    .string "possession, and if any of his kin\l"
    .string "come to redeem it, then shall he\l"
    .string "redeem that which his brother sold.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_26::
    .string "And if the man have none to redeem\n"
    .string "it, and himself be able to redeem\l"
    .string "it;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_27::
    .string "Then let him count the years of the\n"
    .string "sale thereof, and restore the\l"
    .string "overplus unto the man to whom he\l"
    .string "sold it; that he may return unto his\l"
    .string "possession$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_28::
    .string "But if he be not able to restore it\n"
    .string "to him, then that which is sold\l"
    .string "shall remain in the hand of him that\l"
    .string "hath bought it until the year of\l"
    .string "jubile: and in the jubile it shall\l"
    .string "go out, and he shall return unto his\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_29::
    .string "And if a man sell a dwelling\n"
    .string "house in a walled city, then he may\l"
    .string "redeem it within a whole year after\l"
    .string "it is sold; within a full year may\l"
    .string "he redeem it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_30::
    .string "And if it be not redeemed within the\n"
    .string "space of a full year, then the\l"
    .string "house that is in the walled city\l"
    .string "shall be established for ever to\l"
    .string "him that bought it throughout his\l"
    .string "generations: it shall not go out in\l"
    .string "the jubile.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_31::
    .string "But the houses of the villages\n"
    .string "which have no wall round about them\l"
    .string "shall be counted as the fields of\l"
    .string "the country: they may be redeemed,\l"
    .string "and they shall go out in the jubile.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_32::
    .string "Notwithstanding the cities of the\n"
    .string "Levites, and the houses of the cities\l"
    .string "of their possession, may the Levites\l"
    .string "redeem at any time.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_33::
    .string "And if a man purchase of the\n"
    .string "Levites, then the house that was\l"
    .string "sold, and the city of his\l"
    .string "possession, shall go out in the year\l"
    .string "of jubile: for the houses of the\l"
    .string "cities of the Levites are their\l"
    .string "possession among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_34::
    .string "But the field of the suburbs of\n"
    .string "their cities may not be sold; for it\l"
    .string "is their perpetual possession.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_35::
    .string "And if thy brother be waxen poor,\n"
    .string "and fallen in decay with thee; then\l"
    .string "thou shalt relieve him: yea, though\l"
    .string "he be a stranger, or a sojourner;\l"
    .string "that he may live with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_36::
    .string "Take thou no usury of him, or\n"
    .string "increase: but fear thy God; that thy\l"
    .string "brother may live with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_37::
    .string "Thou shalt not give him thy money\n"
    .string "upon usury, nor lend him thy\l"
    .string "victuals for increase.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_38::
    .string "I am the LORD your God, which\n"
    .string "brought you forth out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, to give you the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, and to be your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_39::
    .string "And if thy brother that dwelleth\n"
    .string "by thee be waxen poor, and be sold\l"
    .string "unto thee; thou shalt not compel\l"
    .string "him to serve as a bondservant:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_40::
    .string "But as an hired servant, and as a\n"
    .string "sojourner, he shall be with thee,\l"
    .string "and shall serve thee unto the year\l"
    .string "of jubile$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_41::
    .string "And then shall he depart from\n"
    .string "thee, both he and his children with\l"
    .string "him, and shall return unto his own\l"
    .string "family, and unto the possession of\l"
    .string "his fathers shall he return.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_42::
    .string "For they are my servants, which I\n"
    .string "brought forth out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt: they shall not be sold as\l"
    .string "bondmen.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_43::
    .string "Thou shalt not rule over him with\n"
    .string "rigour; but shalt fear thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_44::
    .string "Both thy bondmen, and thy bondmaids,\n"
    .string "which thou shalt have, shall be of\l"
    .string "the heathen that are round about you;\l"
    .string "of them shall ye buy bondmen and\l"
    .string "bondmaids.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_45::
    .string "Moreover of the children of the\n"
    .string "strangers that do sojourn among you,\l"
    .string "of them shall ye buy, and of their\l"
    .string "families that are with you, which\l"
    .string "they begat in your land: and they\l"
    .string "shall be your possession.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_46::
    .string "And ye shall take them as an\n"
    .string "inheritance for your children after\l"
    .string "you, to inherit them for a\l"
    .string "possession; they shall be your\l"
    .string "bondmen for ever: but over your\l"
    .string "brethren the children of Israel, ye\l"
    .string "shall not rule one over another\l"
    .string "with rigour.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_47::
    .string "And if a sojourner or stranger wax\n"
    .string "rich by thee, and thy brother that\l"
    .string "dwelleth by him wax poor, and sell\l"
    .string "himself unto the stranger or\l"
    .string "sojourner by thee, or to the stock of\l"
    .string "the stranger’s family:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_48::
    .string "After that he is sold he may be\n"
    .string "redeemed again; one of his brethren\l"
    .string "may redeem him:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_49::
    .string "Either his uncle, or his uncle’s\n"
    .string "son, may redeem him, or any that is\l"
    .string "nigh of kin unto him of his family\l"
    .string "may redeem him; or if he be able, he\l"
    .string "may redeem himself$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_50::
    .string "And he shall reckon with him that\n"
    .string "bought him from the year that he was\l"
    .string "sold to him unto the year of jubile:\l"
    .string "and the price of his sale shall be\l"
    .string "according unto the number of years,\l"
    .string "according to the time of an hired\l"
    .string "servant shall it be with him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_51::
    .string "If there be yet many years behind,\n"
    .string "according unto them he shall give\l"
    .string "again the price of his redemption\l"
    .string "out of the money that he was bought\l"
    .string "for.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_52::
    .string "And if there remain but few years\n"
    .string "unto the year of jubile, then he\l"
    .string "shall count with him, and according\l"
    .string "unto his years shall he give him\l"
    .string "again the price of his redemption.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_53::
    .string "And as a yearly hired servant\n"
    .string "shall he be with him: and the other\l"
    .string "shall not rule with rigour over him\l"
    .string "in thy sight.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_54::
    .string "And if he be not redeemed in these\n"
    .string "years, then he shall go out in the\l"
    .string "year of jubile, both he, and his\l"
    .string "children with him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_25_55::
    .string "For unto me the children of Israel\n"
    .string "are servants; they are my servants\l"
    .string "whom I brought forth out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt: I am the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_1::
    .string "Ye shall make you no idols nor\n"
    .string "graven image, neither rear you up a\l"
    .string "standing image, neither shall ye\l"
    .string "set up any image of stone in your\l"
    .string "land, to bow down unto it: for I am\l"
    .string "the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_2::
    .string "Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and\n"
    .string "reverence my sanctuary: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_3::
    .string "If ye walk in my statutes, and keep\n"
    .string "my commandments, and do them;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_4::
    .string "Then I will give you rain in due\n"
    .string "season, and the land shall yield\l"
    .string "her increase, and the trees of the\l"
    .string "field shall yield their fruit$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_5::
    .string "And your threshing shall reach\n"
    .string "unto the vintage, and the vintage\l"
    .string "shall reach unto the sowing time:\l"
    .string "and ye shall eat your bread to the\l"
    .string "full, and dwell in your land\l"
    .string "safely.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_6::
    .string "And I will give peace in the land,\n"
    .string "and ye shall lie down, and none\l"
    .string "shall make you afraid: and I will\l"
    .string "rid evil beasts out of the land,\l"
    .string "neither shall the sword go through\l"
    .string "your land.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_7::
    .string "And ye shall chase your enemies,\n"
    .string "and they shall fall before you by\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_8::
    .string "And five of you shall chase an\n"
    .string "hundred, and an hundred of you shall\l"
    .string "put ten thousand to flight: and your\l"
    .string "enemies shall fall before you by\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_9::
    .string "For I will have respect unto you,\n"
    .string "and make you fruitful, and\l"
    .string "multiply you, and establish my\l"
    .string "covenant with you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_10::
    .string "And ye shall eat old store, and\n"
    .string "bring forth the old because of the\l"
    .string "new.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_11::
    .string "And I set my tabernacle among you:\n"
    .string "and my soul shall not abhor you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_12::
    .string "And I will walk among you, and\n"
    .string "will be your God, and ye shall be\l"
    .string "my people.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_13::
    .string "I am the LORD your God, which\n"
    .string "brought you forth out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, that ye should not be their\l"
    .string "bondmen; and I have broken the bands\l"
    .string "of your yoke, and made you go\l"
    .string "upright.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_14::
    .string "But if ye will not hearken unto me,\n"
    .string "and will not do all these\l"
    .string "commandments;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_15::
    .string "And if ye shall despise my\n"
    .string "statutes, or if your soul abhor my\l"
    .string "judgments, so that ye will not do\l"
    .string "all my commandments, but that ye\l"
    .string "break my covenant:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_16::
    .string "I also will do this unto you; I\n"
    .string "will even appoint over you terror,\l"
    .string "consumption, and the burning ague,\l"
    .string "that shall consume the eyes, and\l"
    .string "cause sorrow of heart: and ye shall\l"
    .string "sow your seed in vain, for your\l"
    .string "enemies shall eat it$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_17::
    .string "And I will set my face against you,\n"
    .string "and ye shall be slain before your\l"
    .string "enemies: they that hate you shall\l"
    .string "reign over you; and ye shall flee\l"
    .string "when none pursueth you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_18::
    .string "And if ye will not yet for all\n"
    .string "this hearken unto me, then I will\l"
    .string "punish you seven times more for your\l"
    .string "sins.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_19::
    .string "And I will break the pride of your\n"
    .string "power; and I will make your heaven\l"
    .string "as iron, and your earth as brass:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_20::
    .string "And your strength shall be spent\n"
    .string "in vain: for your land shall not\l"
    .string "yield her increase, neither shall\l"
    .string "the trees of the land yield their\l"
    .string "fruits$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_21::
    .string "And if ye walk contrary unto me, and\n"
    .string "will not hearken unto me; I will\l"
    .string "bring seven times more plagues\l"
    .string "upon you according to your sins.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_22::
    .string "I will also send wild beasts\n"
    .string "among you, which shall rob you of\l"
    .string "your children, and destroy your\l"
    .string "cattle, and make you few in number;\l"
    .string "and your high ways shall be\l"
    .string "desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_23::
    .string "And if ye will not be reformed by\n"
    .string "me by these things, but will walk\l"
    .string "contrary unto me;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_24::
    .string "Then will I also walk contrary\n"
    .string "unto you, and will punish you yet\l"
    .string "seven times for your sins$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_25::
    .string "And I will bring a sword upon you,\n"
    .string "that shall avenge the quarrel of my\l"
    .string "covenant: and when ye are gathered\l"
    .string "together within your cities, I will\l"
    .string "send the pestilence among you; and\l"
    .string "ye shall be delivered into the hand\l"
    .string "of the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_26::
    .string "And when I have broken the staff of\n"
    .string "your bread, ten women shall bake\l"
    .string "your bread in one oven, and they\l"
    .string "shall deliver you your bread again\l"
    .string "by weight: and ye shall eat, and not\l"
    .string "be satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_27::
    .string "And if ye will not for all this\n"
    .string "hearken unto me, but walk contrary\l"
    .string "unto me;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_28::
    .string "Then I will walk contrary unto you\n"
    .string "also in fury; and I, even I, will\l"
    .string "chastise you seven times for your\l"
    .string "sins$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_29::
    .string "And ye shall eat the flesh of your\n"
    .string "sons, and the flesh of your\l"
    .string "daughters shall ye eat.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_30::
    .string "And I will destroy your high\n"
    .string "places, and cut down your images,\l"
    .string "and cast your carcases upon the\l"
    .string "carcases of your idols, and my soul\l"
    .string "shall abhor you.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_31::
    .string "And I will make your cities waste,\n"
    .string "and bring your sanctuaries unto\l"
    .string "desolation, and I will not smell\l"
    .string "the savour of your sweet odours.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_32::
    .string "And I will bring the land into\n"
    .string "desolation: and your enemies which\l"
    .string "dwell therein shall be astonished\l"
    .string "at it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_33::
    .string "And I will scatter you among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and will draw out a sword\l"
    .string "after you: and your land shall be\l"
    .string "desolate, and your cities waste.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_34::
    .string "Then shall the land enjoy her\n"
    .string "sabbaths, as long as it lieth\l"
    .string "desolate, and ye be in your enemies’\l"
    .string "land; even then shall the land\l"
    .string "rest, and enjoy her sabbaths.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_35::
    .string "As long as it lieth desolate it\n"
    .string "shall rest; because it did not rest\l"
    .string "in your sabbaths, when ye dwelt upon\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_36::
    .string "And upon them that are left alive\n"
    .string "of you I will send a faintness into\l"
    .string "their hearts in the lands of their\l"
    .string "enemies; and the sound of a shaken\l"
    .string "leaf shall chase them; and they\l"
    .string "shall flee, as fleeing from a\l"
    .string "sword; and they shall fall when\l"
    .string "none pursueth.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_37::
    .string "And they shall fall one upon\n"
    .string "another, as it were before a sword,\l"
    .string "when none pursueth: and ye shall\l"
    .string "have no power to stand before your\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_38::
    .string "And ye shall perish among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and the land of your\l"
    .string "enemies shall eat you up.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_39::
    .string "And they that are left of you\n"
    .string "shall pine away in their iniquity\l"
    .string "in your enemies’ lands; and also in\l"
    .string "the iniquities of their fathers\l"
    .string "shall they pine away with them.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_40::
    .string "If they shall confess their\n"
    .string "iniquity, and the iniquity of their\l"
    .string "fathers, with their trespass which\l"
    .string "they trespassed against me, and that\l"
    .string "also they have walked contrary unto\l"
    .string "me;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_41::
    .string "And that I also have walked\n"
    .string "contrary unto them, and have brought\l"
    .string "them into the land of their enemies;\l"
    .string "if then their uncircumcised hearts\l"
    .string "be humbled, and they then accept of\l"
    .string "the punishment of their iniquity:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_42::
    .string "Then will I remember my covenant\n"
    .string "with Jacob, and also my covenant\l"
    .string "with Isaac, and also my covenant\l"
    .string "with Abraham will I remember; and I\l"
    .string "will remember the land$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_43::
    .string "The land also shall be left of\n"
    .string "them, and shall enjoy her sabbaths,\l"
    .string "while she lieth desolate without\l"
    .string "them: and they shall accept of the\l"
    .string "punishment of their iniquity:\l"
    .string "because, even because they despised\l"
    .string "my judgments, and because their soul\l"
    .string "abhorred my statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_44::
    .string "And yet for all that, when they be\n"
    .string "in the land of their enemies, I\l"
    .string "will not cast them away, neither\l"
    .string "will I abhor them, to destroy them\l"
    .string "utterly, and to break my covenant\l"
    .string "with them: for I am the LORD their\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_45::
    .string "But I will for their sakes\n"
    .string "remember the covenant of their\l"
    .string "ancestors, whom I brought forth out\l"
    .string "of the land of Egypt in the sight of\l"
    .string "the heathen, that I might be their\l"
    .string "God: I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_26_46::
    .string "These are the statutes and\n"
    .string "judgments and laws, which the LORD\l"
    .string "made between him and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, When a man shall\l"
    .string "make a singular vow, the persons\l"
    .string "shall be for the LORD by thy\l"
    .string "estimation$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_3::
    .string "And thy estimation shall be of the\n"
    .string "male from twenty years old even\l"
    .string "unto sixty years old, even thy\l"
    .string "estimation shall be fifty shekels\l"
    .string "of silver, after the shekel of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_4::
    .string "And if it be a female, then thy\n"
    .string "estimation shall be thirty shekels.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_5::
    .string "And if it be from five years old\n"
    .string "even unto twenty years old, then thy\l"
    .string "estimation shall be of the male\l"
    .string "twenty shekels, and for the female\l"
    .string "ten shekels.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_6::
    .string "And if it be from a month old even\n"
    .string "unto five years old, then thy\l"
    .string "estimation shall be of the male\l"
    .string "five shekels of silver, and for the\l"
    .string "female thy estimation shall be\l"
    .string "three shekels of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_7::
    .string "And if it be from sixty years old\n"
    .string "and above; if it be a male, then thy\l"
    .string "estimation shall be fifteen\l"
    .string "shekels, and for the female ten\l"
    .string "shekels.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_8::
    .string "But if he be poorer than thy\n"
    .string "estimation, then he shall present\l"
    .string "himself before the priest, and the\l"
    .string "priest shall value him; according\l"
    .string "to his ability that vowed shall the\l"
    .string "priest value him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_9::
    .string "And if it be a beast, whereof men\n"
    .string "bring an offering unto the LORD, all\l"
    .string "that any man giveth of such unto the\l"
    .string "LORD shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_10::
    .string "He shall not alter it, nor change\n"
    .string "it, a good for a bad, or a bad for a\l"
    .string "good: and if he shall at all change\l"
    .string "beast for beast, then it and the\l"
    .string "exchange thereof shall be holy.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_11::
    .string "And if it be any unclean beast, of\n"
    .string "which they do not offer a sacrifice\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, then he shall\l"
    .string "present the beast before the priest:"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_12::
    .string "And the priest shall value it,\n"
    .string "whether it be good or bad: as thou\l"
    .string "valuest it, who art the priest, so\l"
    .string "shall it be$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_13::
    .string "But if he will at all redeem it,\n"
    .string "then he shall add a fifth part\l"
    .string "thereof unto thy estimation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_14::
    .string "And when a man shall sanctify his\n"
    .string "house to be holy unto the LORD, then\l"
    .string "the priest shall estimate it,\l"
    .string "whether it be good or bad: as the\l"
    .string "priest shall estimate it, so shall\l"
    .string "it stand.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_15::
    .string "And if he that sanctified it will\n"
    .string "redeem his house, then he shall add\l"
    .string "the fifth part of the money of thy\l"
    .string "estimation unto it, and it shall be\l"
    .string "his.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_16::
    .string "And if a man shall sanctify unto\n"
    .string "the LORD some part of a field of his\l"
    .string "possession, then thy estimation\l"
    .string "shall be according to the seed\l"
    .string "thereof: an homer of barley seed\l"
    .string "shall be valued at fifty shekels\l"
    .string "of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_17::
    .string "If he sanctify his field from the\n"
    .string "year of jubile, according to thy\l"
    .string "estimation it shall stand.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_18::
    .string "But if he sanctify his field after\n"
    .string "the jubile, then the priest shall\l"
    .string "reckon unto him the money according\l"
    .string "to the years that remain, even unto\l"
    .string "the year of the jubile, and it\l"
    .string "shall be abated from thy estimation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_19::
    .string "And if he that sanctified the field\n"
    .string "will in any wise redeem it, then he\l"
    .string "shall add the fifth part of the\l"
    .string "money of thy estimation unto it, and\l"
    .string "it shall be assured to him.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_20::
    .string "And if he will not redeem the\n"
    .string "field, or if he have sold the field\l"
    .string "to another man, it shall not be\l"
    .string "redeemed any more.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_21::
    .string "But the field, when it goeth out in\n"
    .string "the jubile, shall be holy unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, as a field devoted; the\l"
    .string "possession thereof shall be the\l"
    .string "priest’s.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_22::
    .string "And if a man sanctify unto the LORD\n"
    .string "a field which he hath bought, which\l"
    .string "is not of the fields of his\l"
    .string "possession;"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_23::
    .string "Then the priest shall reckon unto\n"
    .string "him the worth of thy estimation, even\l"
    .string "unto the year of the jubile: and he\l"
    .string "shall give thine estimation in that\l"
    .string "day, as a holy thing unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_24::
    .string "In the year of the jubile the field\n"
    .string "shall return unto him of whom it was\l"
    .string "bought, even to him to whom the\l"
    .string "possession of the land did belong.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_25::
    .string "And all thy estimations shall be\n"
    .string "according to the shekel of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary: twenty gerahs shall be\l"
    .string "the shekel.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_26::
    .string "Only the firstling of the beasts,\n"
    .string "which should be the LORD’s\l"
    .string "firstling, no man shall sanctify\l"
    .string "it; whether it be ox, or sheep: it is\l"
    .string "the LORD’s.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_27::
    .string "And if it be of an unclean beast,\n"
    .string "then he shall redeem it according\l"
    .string "to thine estimation, and shall add a\l"
    .string "fifth part of it thereto: or if it be\l"
    .string "not redeemed, then it shall be sold\l"
    .string "according to thy estimation.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_28::
    .string "Notwithstanding no devoted thing,\n"
    .string "that a man shall devote unto the\l"
    .string "LORD of all that he hath, both of\l"
    .string "man and beast, and of the field of\l"
    .string "his possession, shall be sold or\l"
    .string "redeemed: every devoted thing is most\l"
    .string "holy unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_29::
    .string "None devoted, which shall be\n"
    .string "devoted of men, shall be redeemed;\l"
    .string "but shall surely be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_30::
    .string "And all the tithe of the land,\n"
    .string "whether of the seed of the land, or\l"
    .string "of the fruit of the tree, is the\l"
    .string "LORD’s: it is holy unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_31::
    .string "And if a man will at all redeem\n"
    .string "ought of his tithes, he shall add\l"
    .string "thereto the fifth part thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_32::
    .string "And concerning the tithe of the\n"
    .string "herd, or of the flock, even of\l"
    .string "whatsoever passeth under the rod,\l"
    .string "the tenth shall be holy unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_33::
    .string "He shall not search whether it be\n"
    .string "good or bad, neither shall he change\l"
    .string "it: and if he change it at all, then\l"
    .string "both it and the change thereof\l"
    .string "shall be holy; it shall not be\l"
    .string "redeemed.$"
Bible_Text_Leviticus_27_34::
    .string "These are the commandments, which\n"
    .string "the LORD commanded Moses for the\l"
    .string "children of Israel in mount Sinai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses in\n"
    .string "the wilderness of Sinai, in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, on\l"
    .string "the first day of the second month, in\l"
    .string "the second year after they were come\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt, saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_2::
    .string "Take ye the sum of all the\n"
    .string "congregation of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, after their families, by\l"
    .string "the house of their fathers, with the\l"
    .string "number of their names, every male by\l"
    .string "their polls;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_3::
    .string "From twenty years old and upward,\n"
    .string "all that are able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war in Israel: thou and Aaron shall\l"
    .string "number them by their armies$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_4::
    .string "And with you there shall be a man\n"
    .string "of every tribe; every one head of the\l"
    .string "house of his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_5::
    .string "And these are the names of the men\n"
    .string "that shall stand with you: of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Reuben; Elizur the son of\l"
    .string "Shedeur.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_6::
    .string "Of Simeon; Shelumiel the son of\n"
    .string "Zurishaddai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_7::
    .string "Of Judah; Nahshon the son of\n"
    .string "Amminadab.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_8::
    .string "Of Issachar; Nethaneel the son of\n"
    .string "Zuar.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_9::
    .string "Of Zebulun; Eliab the son of Helon.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_10::
    .string "Of the children of Joseph: of\n"
    .string "Ephraim; Elishama the son of\l"
    .string "Ammihud: of Manasseh; Gamaliel the\l"
    .string "son of Pedahzur.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_11::
    .string "Of Benjamin; Abidan the son of\n"
    .string "Gideoni.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_12::
    .string "Of Dan; Ahiezer the son of\n"
    .string "Ammishaddai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_13::
    .string "Of Asher; Pagiel the son of Ocran.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_14::
    .string "Of Gad; Eliasaph the son of Deuel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_15::
    .string "Of Naphtali; Ahira the son of Enan.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_16::
    .string "These were the renowned of the\n"
    .string "congregation, princes of the tribes\l"
    .string "of their fathers, heads of thousands\l"
    .string "in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_17::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron took these men\n"
    .string "which are expressed by their names:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_18::
    .string "And they assembled all the\n"
    .string "congregation together on the first\l"
    .string "day of the second month, and they\l"
    .string "declared their pedigrees after\l"
    .string "their families, by the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers, according to the\l"
    .string "number of the names, from twenty\l"
    .string "years old and upward, by their\l"
    .string "polls$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_19::
    .string "As the LORD commanded Moses, so he\n"
    .string "numbered them in the wilderness of\l"
    .string "Sinai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_20::
    .string "And the children of Reuben,\n"
    .string "Israel’s eldest son, by their\l"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "by their polls, every male from\l"
    .string "twenty years old and upward, all\l"
    .string "that were able to go forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_21::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Reuben, were\l"
    .string "forty and six thousand and five\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_22::
    .string "Of the children of Simeon, by their\n"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers, those\l"
    .string "that were numbered of them, according\l"
    .string "to the number of the names, by their\l"
    .string "polls, every male from twenty years\l"
    .string "old and upward, all that were able\l"
    .string "to go forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_23::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Simeon, were\l"
    .string "fifty and nine thousand and three\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_24::
    .string "Of the children of Gad, by their\n"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and upward,\l"
    .string "all that were able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_25::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Gad, were forty\l"
    .string "and five thousand six hundred and\l"
    .string "fifty$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_26::
    .string "Of the children of Judah, by their\n"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and upward,\l"
    .string "all that were able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_27::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Judah, were\l"
    .string "threescore and fourteen thousand and\l"
    .string "six hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_28::
    .string "Of the children of Issachar, by\n"
    .string "their generations, after their\l"
    .string "families, by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, according to the number of\l"
    .string "the names, from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "upward, all that were able to go\l"
    .string "forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_29::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Issachar, were\l"
    .string "fifty and four thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_30::
    .string "Of the children of Zebulun, by\n"
    .string "their generations, after their\l"
    .string "families, by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, according to the number of\l"
    .string "the names, from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "upward, all that were able to go\l"
    .string "forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_31::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Zebulun, were\l"
    .string "fifty and seven thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_32::
    .string "Of the children of Joseph, namely,\n"
    .string "of the children of Ephraim, by their\l"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and upward,\l"
    .string "all that were able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_33::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Ephraim, were\l"
    .string "forty thousand and five hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_34::
    .string "Of the children of Manasseh, by\n"
    .string "their generations, after their\l"
    .string "families, by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, according to the number of\l"
    .string "the names, from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "upward, all that were able to go\l"
    .string "forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_35::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Manasseh, were\l"
    .string "thirty and two thousand and two\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_36::
    .string "Of the children of Benjamin, by\n"
    .string "their generations, after their\l"
    .string "families, by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, according to the number of\l"
    .string "the names, from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "upward, all that were able to go\l"
    .string "forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_37::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Benjamin, were\l"
    .string "thirty and five thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_38::
    .string "Of the children of Dan, by their\n"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and upward,\l"
    .string "all that were able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_39::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Dan, were\l"
    .string "threescore and two thousand and\l"
    .string "seven hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_40::
    .string "Of the children of Asher, by their\n"
    .string "generations, after their families,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "according to the number of the names,\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and upward,\l"
    .string "all that were able to go forth to\l"
    .string "war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_41::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Asher, were\l"
    .string "forty and one thousand and five\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_42::
    .string "Of the children of Naphtali,\n"
    .string "throughout their generations, after\l"
    .string "their families, by the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers, according to the\l"
    .string "number of the names, from twenty\l"
    .string "years old and upward, all that\l"
    .string "were able to go forth to war;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_43::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "even of the tribe of Naphtali, were\l"
    .string "fifty and three thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_44::
    .string "These are those that were numbered,\n"
    .string "which Moses and Aaron numbered, and\l"
    .string "the princes of Israel, being twelve\l"
    .string "men: each one was for the house of his\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_45::
    .string "So were all those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "by the house of their fathers, from\l"
    .string "twenty years old and upward, all\l"
    .string "that were able to go forth to war in\l"
    .string "Israel;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_46::
    .string "Even all they that were numbered\n"
    .string "were six hundred thousand and three\l"
    .string "thousand and five hundred and fifty$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_47::
    .string "But the Levites after the tribe of\n"
    .string "their fathers were not numbered\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_48::
    .string "For the LORD had spoken unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_49::
    .string "Only thou shalt not number the\n"
    .string "tribe of Levi, neither take the sum\l"
    .string "of them among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_50::
    .string "But thou shalt appoint the\n"
    .string "Levites over the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "testimony, and over all the vessels\l"
    .string "thereof, and over all things that\l"
    .string "belong to it: they shall bear the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and all the vessels\l"
    .string "thereof; and they shall minister\l"
    .string "unto it, and shall encamp round\l"
    .string "about the tabernacle$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_51::
    .string "And when the tabernacle setteth\n"
    .string "forward, the Levites shall take it\l"
    .string "down: and when the tabernacle is to\l"
    .string "be pitched, the Levites shall set\l"
    .string "it up: and the stranger that cometh\l"
    .string "nigh shall be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_52::
    .string "And the children of Israel shall\n"
    .string "pitch their tents, every man by his\l"
    .string "own camp, and every man by his own\l"
    .string "standard, throughout their hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_53::
    .string "But the Levites shall pitch round\n"
    .string "about the tabernacle of testimony,\l"
    .string "that there be no wrath upon the\l"
    .string "congregation of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel: and the Levites shall keep\l"
    .string "the charge of the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "testimony.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_1_54::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "according to all that the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses, so did they.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_2::
    .string "Every man of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel shall pitch by his own\l"
    .string "standard, with the ensign of their\l"
    .string "father’s house: far off about the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation\l"
    .string "shall they pitch$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_3::
    .string "And on the east side toward the\n"
    .string "rising of the sun shall they of the\l"
    .string "standard of the camp of Judah pitch\l"
    .string "throughout their armies: and Nahshon\l"
    .string "the son of Amminadab shall be\l"
    .string "captain of the children of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_4::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were threescore and\l"
    .string "fourteen thousand and six hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_5::
    .string "And those that do pitch next unto\n"
    .string "him shall be the tribe of Issachar:\l"
    .string "and Nethaneel the son of Zuar shall\l"
    .string "be captain of the children of\l"
    .string "Issachar.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_6::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered thereof, were fifty and four\l"
    .string "thousand and four hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_7::
    .string "Then the tribe of Zebulun: and\n"
    .string "Eliab the son of Helon shall be\l"
    .string "captain of the children of Zebulun.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_8::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered thereof, were fifty and\l"
    .string "seven thousand and four hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_9::
    .string "All that were numbered in the camp\n"
    .string "of Judah were an hundred thousand and\l"
    .string "fourscore thousand and six thousand\l"
    .string "and four hundred, throughout their\l"
    .string "armies. These shall first set forth.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_10::
    .string "On the south side shall be the\n"
    .string "standard of the camp of Reuben\l"
    .string "according to their armies: and the\l"
    .string "captain of the children of Reuben\l"
    .string "shall be Elizur the son of Shedeur.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_11::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered thereof, were forty and six\l"
    .string "thousand and five hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_12::
    .string "And those which pitch by him shall\n"
    .string "be the tribe of Simeon: and the\l"
    .string "captain of the children of Simeon\l"
    .string "shall be Shelumiel the son of\l"
    .string "Zurishaddai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_13::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were fifty and nine\l"
    .string "thousand and three hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_14::
    .string "Then the tribe of Gad: and the\n"
    .string "captain of the sons of Gad shall be\l"
    .string "Eliasaph the son of Reuel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_15::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were forty and five\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred and fifty.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_16::
    .string "All that were numbered in the camp\n"
    .string "of Reuben were an hundred thousand\l"
    .string "and fifty and one thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty, throughout their\l"
    .string "armies. And they shall set forth in\l"
    .string "the second rank.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_17::
    .string "Then the tabernacle of the\n"
    .string "congregation shall set forward with\l"
    .string "the camp of the Levites in the midst\l"
    .string "of the camp: as they encamp, so\l"
    .string "shall they set forward, every man in\l"
    .string "his place by their standards.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_18::
    .string "On the west side shall be the\n"
    .string "standard of the camp of Ephraim\l"
    .string "according to their armies: and the\l"
    .string "captain of the sons of Ephraim\l"
    .string "shall be Elishama the son of\l"
    .string "Ammihud.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_19::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were forty thousand\l"
    .string "and five hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_20::
    .string "And by him shall be the tribe of\n"
    .string "Manasseh: and the captain of the\l"
    .string "children of Manasseh shall be\l"
    .string "Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_21::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were thirty and two\l"
    .string "thousand and two hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_22::
    .string "Then the tribe of Benjamin: and the\n"
    .string "captain of the sons of Benjamin\l"
    .string "shall be Abidan the son of Gideoni.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_23::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were thirty and\l"
    .string "five thousand and four hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_24::
    .string "All that were numbered of the camp\n"
    .string "of Ephraim were an hundred thousand\l"
    .string "and eight thousand and an hundred,\l"
    .string "throughout their armies. And they\l"
    .string "shall go forward in the third rank.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_25::
    .string "The standard of the camp of Dan\n"
    .string "shall be on the north side by their\l"
    .string "armies: and the captain of the\l"
    .string "children of Dan shall be Ahiezer\l"
    .string "the son of Ammishaddai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_26::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were threescore and\l"
    .string "two thousand and seven hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_27::
    .string "And those that encamp by him shall\n"
    .string "be the tribe of Asher: and the\l"
    .string "captain of the children of Asher\l"
    .string "shall be Pagiel the son of Ocran.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_28::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were forty and one\l"
    .string "thousand and five hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_29::
    .string "Then the tribe of Naphtali: and the\n"
    .string "captain of the children of\l"
    .string "Naphtali shall be Ahira the son of\l"
    .string "Enan.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_30::
    .string "And his host, and those that were\n"
    .string "numbered of them, were fifty and\l"
    .string "three thousand and four hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_31::
    .string "All they that were numbered in the\n"
    .string "camp of Dan were an hundred thousand\l"
    .string "and fifty and seven thousand and six\l"
    .string "hundred. They shall go hindmost\l"
    .string "with their standards.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_32::
    .string "These are those which were numbered\n"
    .string "of the children of Israel by the\l"
    .string "house of their fathers: all those\l"
    .string "that were numbered of the camps\l"
    .string "throughout their hosts were six\l"
    .string "hundred thousand and three thousand\l"
    .string "and five hundred and fifty.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_33::
    .string "But the Levites were not numbered\n"
    .string "among the children of Israel; as the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_2_34::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "according to all that the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses: so they pitched by\l"
    .string "their standards, and so they set\l"
    .string "forward, every one after their\l"
    .string "families, according to the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_1::
    .string "These also are the generations of\n"
    .string "Aaron and Moses in the day that the\l"
    .string "LORD spake with Moses in mount Sinai.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_2::
    .string "And these are the names of the sons\n"
    .string "of Aaron; Nadab the firstborn, and\l"
    .string "Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_3::
    .string "These are the names of the sons of\n"
    .string "Aaron, the priests which were\l"
    .string "anointed, whom he consecrated to\l"
    .string "minister in the priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_4::
    .string "And Nadab and Abihu died before the\n"
    .string "LORD, when they offered strange fire\l"
    .string "before the LORD, in the wilderness\l"
    .string "of Sinai, and they had no children:\l"
    .string "and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered\l"
    .string "in the priest’s office in the sight\l"
    .string "of Aaron their father.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_5::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_6::
    .string "Bring the tribe of Levi near, and\n"
    .string "present them before Aaron the\l"
    .string "priest, that they may minister unto\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_7::
    .string "And they shall keep his charge,\n"
    .string "and the charge of the whole\l"
    .string "congregation before the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation, to do the\l"
    .string "service of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_8::
    .string "And they shall keep all the\n"
    .string "instruments of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and the charge of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, to do the\l"
    .string "service of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_9::
    .string "And thou shalt give the Levites\n"
    .string "unto Aaron and to his sons: they are\l"
    .string "wholly given unto him out of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_10::
    .string "And thou shalt appoint Aaron and\n"
    .string "his sons, and they shall wait on\l"
    .string "their priest’s office: and the\l"
    .string "stranger that cometh nigh shall be\l"
    .string "put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_11::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_12::
    .string "And I, behold, I have taken the\n"
    .string "Levites from among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel instead of all the\l"
    .string "firstborn that openeth the matrix\l"
    .string "among the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "therefore the Levites shall be\l"
    .string "mine;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_13::
    .string "Because all the firstborn are\n"
    .string "mine; for on the day that I smote\l"
    .string "all the firstborn in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt I hallowed unto me all the\l"
    .string "firstborn in Israel, both man and\l"
    .string "beast: mine shall they be: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_14::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses in\n"
    .string "the wilderness of Sinai, saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_15::
    .string "Number the children of Levi after\n"
    .string "the house of their fathers, by their\l"
    .string "families: every male from a month\l"
    .string "old and upward shalt thou number\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_16::
    .string "And Moses numbered them according\n"
    .string "to the word of the LORD, as he was\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_17::
    .string "And these were the sons of Levi by\n"
    .string "their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and\l"
    .string "Merari.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_18::
    .string "And these are the names of the sons\n"
    .string "of Gershon by their families; Libni,\l"
    .string "and Shimei.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_19::
    .string "And the sons of Kohath by their\n"
    .string "families; Amram, and Izehar, Hebron,\l"
    .string "and Uzziel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_20::
    .string "And the sons of Merari by their\n"
    .string "families; Mahli, and Mushi. These\l"
    .string "are the families of the Levites\l"
    .string "according to the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_21::
    .string "Of Gershon was the family of the\n"
    .string "Libnites, and the family of the\l"
    .string "Shimites: these are the families of\l"
    .string "the Gershonites.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_22::
    .string "Those that were numbered of them,\n"
    .string "according to the number of all the\l"
    .string "males, from a month old and upward,\l"
    .string "even those that were numbered of them\l"
    .string "were seven thousand and five hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_23::
    .string "The families of the Gershonites\n"
    .string "shall pitch behind the tabernacle\l"
    .string "westward.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_24::
    .string "And the chief of the house of the\n"
    .string "father of the Gershonites shall be\l"
    .string "Eliasaph the son of Lael.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_25::
    .string "And the charge of the sons of\n"
    .string "Gershon in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation shall be the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and the tent, the\l"
    .string "covering thereof, and the hanging for\l"
    .string "the door of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_26::
    .string "And the hangings of the court, and\n"
    .string "the curtain for the door of the\l"
    .string "court, which is by the tabernacle,\l"
    .string "and by the altar round about, and the\l"
    .string "cords of it for all the service\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_27::
    .string "And of Kohath was the family of the\n"
    .string "Amramites, and the family of the\l"
    .string "Izeharites, and the family of the\l"
    .string "Hebronites, and the family of the\l"
    .string "Uzzielites: these are the families\l"
    .string "of the Kohathites.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_28::
    .string "In the number of all the males,\n"
    .string "from a month old and upward, were\l"
    .string "eight thousand and six hundred,\l"
    .string "keeping the charge of the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_29::
    .string "The families of the sons of Kohath\n"
    .string "shall pitch on the side of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle southward.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_30::
    .string "And the chief of the house of the\n"
    .string "father of the families of the\l"
    .string "Kohathites shall be Elizaphan the\l"
    .string "son of Uzziel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_31::
    .string "And their charge shall be the ark,\n"
    .string "and the table, and the candlestick,\l"
    .string "and the altars, and the vessels of\l"
    .string "the sanctuary wherewith they\l"
    .string "minister, and the hanging, and all\l"
    .string "the service thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_32::
    .string "And Eleazar the son of Aaron the\n"
    .string "priest shall be chief over the\l"
    .string "chief of the Levites, and have the\l"
    .string "oversight of them that keep the\l"
    .string "charge of the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_33::
    .string "Of Merari was the family of the\n"
    .string "Mahlites, and the family of the\l"
    .string "Mushites: these are the families of\l"
    .string "Merari.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_34::
    .string "And those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "them, according to the number of all\l"
    .string "the males, from a month old and\l"
    .string "upward, were six thousand and two\l"
    .string "hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_35::
    .string "And the chief of the house of the\n"
    .string "father of the families of Merari was\l"
    .string "Zuriel the son of Abihail: these\l"
    .string "shall pitch on the side of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle northward.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_36::
    .string "And under the custody and charge of\n"
    .string "the sons of Merari shall be the\l"
    .string "boards of the tabernacle, and the\l"
    .string "bars thereof, and the pillars\l"
    .string "thereof, and the sockets thereof, and\l"
    .string "all the vessels thereof, and all\l"
    .string "that serveth thereto,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_37::
    .string "And the pillars of the court round\n"
    .string "about, and their sockets, and their\l"
    .string "pins, and their cords$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_38::
    .string "But those that encamp before the\n"
    .string "tabernacle toward the east, even\l"
    .string "before the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation eastward, shall be\l"
    .string "Moses, and Aaron and his sons,\l"
    .string "keeping the charge of the sanctuary\l"
    .string "for the charge of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel; and the stranger that cometh\l"
    .string "nigh shall be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_39::
    .string "All that were numbered of the\n"
    .string "Levites, which Moses and Aaron\l"
    .string "numbered at the commandment of the\l"
    .string "LORD, throughout their families,\l"
    .string "all the males from a month old and\l"
    .string "upward, were twenty and two thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_40::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Moses, Number\n"
    .string "all the firstborn of the males of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel from a month\l"
    .string "old and upward, and take the number\l"
    .string "of their names.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_41::
    .string "And thou shalt take the Levites for\n"
    .string "me (I am the LORD) instead of all\l"
    .string "the firstborn among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel; and the cattle of the\l"
    .string "Levites instead of all the\l"
    .string "firstlings among the cattle of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_42::
    .string "And Moses numbered, as the LORD\n"
    .string "commanded him, all the firstborn\l"
    .string "among the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_43::
    .string "And all the firstborn males by the\n"
    .string "number of names, from a month old and\l"
    .string "upward, of those that were numbered\l"
    .string "of them, were twenty and two thousand\l"
    .string "two hundred and threescore and\l"
    .string "thirteen.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_44::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_45::
    .string "Take the Levites instead of all\n"
    .string "the firstborn among the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and the cattle of the\l"
    .string "Levites instead of their cattle; and\l"
    .string "the Levites shall be mine: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_46::
    .string "And for those that are to be\n"
    .string "redeemed of the two hundred and\l"
    .string "threescore and thirteen of the\l"
    .string "firstborn of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, which are more than the\l"
    .string "Levites;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_47::
    .string "Thou shalt even take five shekels\n"
    .string "apiece by the poll, after the\l"
    .string "shekel of the sanctuary shalt thou\l"
    .string "take them: (the shekel is twenty\l"
    .string "gerahs:)"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_48::
    .string "And thou shalt give the money,\n"
    .string "wherewith the odd number of them is\l"
    .string "to be redeemed, unto Aaron and to his\l"
    .string "sons$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_49::
    .string "And Moses took the redemption money\n"
    .string "of them that were over and above them\l"
    .string "that were redeemed by the Levites:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_50::
    .string "Of the firstborn of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel took he the money; a thousand\l"
    .string "three hundred and threescore and\l"
    .string "five shekels, after the shekel of\l"
    .string "the sanctuary:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_3_51::
    .string "And Moses gave the money of them\n"
    .string "that were redeemed unto Aaron and to\l"
    .string "his sons, according to the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron, saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_2::
    .string "Take the sum of the sons of Kohath\n"
    .string "from among the sons of Levi, after\l"
    .string "their families, by the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_3::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even until fifty years old, all\l"
    .string "that enter into the host, to do the\l"
    .string "work in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_4::
    .string "This shall be the service of the\n"
    .string "sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation, about the most\l"
    .string "holy things:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_5::
    .string "And when the camp setteth forward,\n"
    .string "Aaron shall come, and his sons, and\l"
    .string "they shall take down the covering\l"
    .string "vail, and cover the ark of testimony\l"
    .string "with it:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_6::
    .string "And shall put thereon the\n"
    .string "covering of badgers’ skins, and\l"
    .string "shall spread over it a cloth\l"
    .string "wholly of blue, and shall put in\l"
    .string "the staves thereof$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_7::
    .string "And upon the table of shewbread\n"
    .string "they shall spread a cloth of blue,\l"
    .string "and put thereon the dishes, and the\l"
    .string "spoons, and the bowls, and covers to\l"
    .string "cover withal: and the continual\l"
    .string "bread shall be thereon:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_8::
    .string "And they shall spread upon them a\n"
    .string "cloth of scarlet, and cover the same\l"
    .string "with a covering of badgers’ skins,\l"
    .string "and shall put in the staves thereof$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_9::
    .string "And they shall take a cloth of\n"
    .string "blue, and cover the candlestick of\l"
    .string "the light, and his lamps, and his\l"
    .string "tongs, and his snuffdishes, and all\l"
    .string "the oil vessels thereof, wherewith\l"
    .string "they minister unto it:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_10::
    .string "And they shall put it and all the\n"
    .string "vessels thereof within a covering of\l"
    .string "badgers’ skins, and shall put it\l"
    .string "upon a bar$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_11::
    .string "And upon the golden altar they\n"
    .string "shall spread a cloth of blue, and\l"
    .string "cover it with a covering of badgers’\l"
    .string "skins, and shall put to the staves\l"
    .string "thereof:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_12::
    .string "And they shall take all the\n"
    .string "instruments of ministry, wherewith\l"
    .string "they minister in the sanctuary, and\l"
    .string "put them in a cloth of blue, and\l"
    .string "cover them with a covering of\l"
    .string "badgers’ skins, and shall put them\l"
    .string "on a bar:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_13::
    .string "And they shall take away the ashes\n"
    .string "from the altar, and spread a\l"
    .string "purple cloth thereon:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_14::
    .string "And they shall put upon it all\n"
    .string "the vessels thereof, wherewith they\l"
    .string "minister about it, even the censers,\l"
    .string "the fleshhooks, and the shovels,\l"
    .string "and the basons, all the vessels of\l"
    .string "the altar; and they shall spread\l"
    .string "upon it a covering of badgers’\l"
    .string "skins, and put to the staves of it$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_15::
    .string "And when Aaron and his sons have\n"
    .string "made an end of covering the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, and all the vessels of\l"
    .string "the sanctuary, as the camp is to set\l"
    .string "forward; after that, the sons of\l"
    .string "Kohath shall come to bear it: but\l"
    .string "they shall not touch any holy\l"
    .string "thing, lest they die. These things\l"
    .string "are the burden of the sons of Kohath\l"
    .string "in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_16::
    .string "And to the office of Eleazar the\n"
    .string "son of Aaron the priest pertaineth\l"
    .string "the oil for the light, and the sweet\l"
    .string "incense, and the daily meat\l"
    .string "offering, and the anointing oil, and\l"
    .string "the oversight of all the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and of all that therein\l"
    .string "is, in the sanctuary, and in the\l"
    .string "vessels thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_17::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses and\n"
    .string "unto Aaron saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_18::
    .string "Cut ye not off the tribe of the\n"
    .string "families of the Kohathites from\l"
    .string "among the Levites:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_19::
    .string "But thus do unto them, that they may\n"
    .string "live, and not die, when they\l"
    .string "approach unto the most holy things:\l"
    .string "Aaron and his sons shall go in, and\l"
    .string "appoint them every one to his\l"
    .string "service and to his burden:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_20::
    .string "But they shall not go in to see\n"
    .string "when the holy things are covered,\l"
    .string "lest they die$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_21::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_22::
    .string "Take also the sum of the sons of\n"
    .string "Gershon, throughout the houses of\l"
    .string "their fathers, by their families;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_23::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "until fifty years old shalt thou\l"
    .string "number them; all that enter in to\l"
    .string "perform the service, to do the work\l"
    .string "in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_24::
    .string "This is the service of the families\n"
    .string "of the Gershonites, to serve, and for\l"
    .string "burdens:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_25::
    .string "And they shall bear the curtains\n"
    .string "of the tabernacle, and the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, his\l"
    .string "covering, and the covering of the\l"
    .string "badgers’ skins that is above upon\l"
    .string "it, and the hanging for the door of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_26::
    .string "And the hangings of the court, and\n"
    .string "the hanging for the door of the gate\l"
    .string "of the court, which is by the\l"
    .string "tabernacle and by the altar round\l"
    .string "about, and their cords, and all the\l"
    .string "instruments of their service, and\l"
    .string "all that is made for them: so shall\l"
    .string "they serve$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_27::
    .string "At the appointment of Aaron and\n"
    .string "his sons shall be all the service\l"
    .string "of the sons of the Gershonites, in\l"
    .string "all their burdens, and in all\l"
    .string "their service: and ye shall\l"
    .string "appoint unto them in charge all\l"
    .string "their burdens.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_28::
    .string "This is the service of the families\n"
    .string "of the sons of Gershon in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation: and\l"
    .string "their charge shall be under the\l"
    .string "hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the\l"
    .string "priest.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_29::
    .string "As for the sons of Merari, thou\n"
    .string "shalt number them after their\l"
    .string "families, by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_30::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even unto fifty years old shalt\l"
    .string "thou number them, every one that\l"
    .string "entereth into the service, to do the\l"
    .string "work of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_31::
    .string "And this is the charge of their\n"
    .string "burden, according to all their\l"
    .string "service in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation; the boards of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and the bars thereof,\l"
    .string "and the pillars thereof, and\l"
    .string "sockets thereof,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_32::
    .string "And the pillars of the court round\n"
    .string "about, and their sockets, and their\l"
    .string "pins, and their cords, with all\l"
    .string "their instruments, and with all\l"
    .string "their service: and by name ye shall\l"
    .string "reckon the instruments of the charge\l"
    .string "of their burden$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_33::
    .string "This is the service of the families\n"
    .string "of the sons of Merari, according to\l"
    .string "all their service, in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "under the hand of Ithamar the son of\l"
    .string "Aaron the priest.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_34::
    .string "And Moses and Aaron and the chief of\n"
    .string "the congregation numbered the sons\l"
    .string "of the Kohathites after their\l"
    .string "families, and after the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_35::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even unto fifty years old, every one\l"
    .string "that entereth into the service, for\l"
    .string "the work in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_36::
    .string "And those that were numbered of them\n"
    .string "by their families were two thousand\l"
    .string "seven hundred and fifty$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_37::
    .string "These were they that were numbered\n"
    .string "of the families of the Kohathites,\l"
    .string "all that might do service in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation,\l"
    .string "which Moses and Aaron did number\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of the\l"
    .string "LORD by the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_38::
    .string "And those that were numbered of the\n"
    .string "sons of Gershon, throughout their\l"
    .string "families, and by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_39::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even unto fifty years old, every one\l"
    .string "that entereth into the service, for\l"
    .string "the work in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_40::
    .string "Even those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "them, throughout their families, by\l"
    .string "the house of their fathers, were two\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred and thirty$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_41::
    .string "These are they that were numbered of\n"
    .string "the families of the sons of Gershon,\l"
    .string "of all that might do service in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, whom\l"
    .string "Moses and Aaron did number according\l"
    .string "to the commandment of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_42::
    .string "And those that were numbered of the\n"
    .string "families of the sons of Merari,\l"
    .string "throughout their families, by the\l"
    .string "house of their fathers,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_43::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even unto fifty years old, every one\l"
    .string "that entereth into the service, for\l"
    .string "the work in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_44::
    .string "Even those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "them after their families, were\l"
    .string "three thousand and two hundred$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_45::
    .string "These be those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "the families of the sons of Merari,\l"
    .string "whom Moses and Aaron numbered\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD by\l"
    .string "the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_46::
    .string "All those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "the Levites, whom Moses and Aaron and\l"
    .string "the chief of Israel numbered, after\l"
    .string "their families, and after the house\l"
    .string "of their fathers,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_47::
    .string "From thirty years old and upward\n"
    .string "even unto fifty years old, every one\l"
    .string "that came to do the service of the\l"
    .string "ministry, and the service of the\l"
    .string "burden in the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_48::
    .string "Even those that were numbered of\n"
    .string "them, were eight thousand and five\l"
    .string "hundred and fourscore,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_4_49::
    .string "According to the commandment of the\n"
    .string "LORD they were numbered by the hand\l"
    .string "of Moses, every one according to his\l"
    .string "service, and according to his burden:\l"
    .string "thus were they numbered of him, as\l"
    .string "the LORD commanded Moses$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_2::
    .string "Command the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "that they put out of the camp every\l"
    .string "leper, and every one that hath an\l"
    .string "issue, and whosoever is defiled by\l"
    .string "the dead:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_3::
    .string "Both male and female shall ye\n"
    .string "put out, without the camp shall ye\l"
    .string "put them; that they defile not their\l"
    .string "camps, in the midst whereof I dwell$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_4::
    .string "And the children of Israel did so,\n"
    .string "and put them out without the camp:\l"
    .string "as the LORD spake unto Moses, so did\l"
    .string "the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_5::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_6::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "When a man or woman shall commit any\l"
    .string "sin that men commit, to do a trespass\l"
    .string "against the LORD, and that person be\l"
    .string "guilty;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_7::
    .string "Then they shall confess their sin\n"
    .string "which they have done: and he shall\l"
    .string "recompense his trespass with the\l"
    .string "principal thereof, and add unto it\l"
    .string "the fifth part thereof, and give it\l"
    .string "unto him against whom he hath\l"
    .string "trespassed$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_8::
    .string "But if the man have no kinsman to\n"
    .string "recompense the trespass unto, let\l"
    .string "the trespass be recompensed unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, even to the priest; beside\l"
    .string "the ram of the atonement, whereby an\l"
    .string "atonement shall be made for him.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_9::
    .string "And every offering of all the holy\n"
    .string "things of the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "which they bring unto the priest,\l"
    .string "shall be his.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_10::
    .string "And every man’s hallowed things\n"
    .string "shall be his: whatsoever any man\l"
    .string "giveth the priest, it shall be his.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_11::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_12::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, If any man’s wife\l"
    .string "go aside, and commit a trespass\l"
    .string "against him,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_13::
    .string "And a man lie with her carnally,\n"
    .string "and it be hid from the eyes of her\l"
    .string "husband, and be kept close, and she\l"
    .string "be defiled, and there be no witness\l"
    .string "against her, neither she be taken\l"
    .string "with the manner;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_14::
    .string "And the spirit of jealousy come\n"
    .string "upon him, and he be jealous of his\l"
    .string "wife, and she be defiled: or if the\l"
    .string "spirit of jealousy come upon him,\l"
    .string "and he be jealous of his wife, and\l"
    .string "she be not defiled:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_15::
    .string "Then shall the man bring his wife\n"
    .string "unto the priest, and he shall bring\l"
    .string "her offering for her, the tenth part\l"
    .string "of an ephah of barley meal; he\l"
    .string "shall pour no oil upon it, nor\l"
    .string "put frankincense thereon; for it is\l"
    .string "an offering of jealousy, an offering\l"
    .string "of memorial, bringing iniquity to\l"
    .string "remembrance$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_16::
    .string "And the priest shall bring her\n"
    .string "near, and set her before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_17::
    .string "And the priest shall take holy\n"
    .string "water in an earthen vessel; and of\l"
    .string "the dust that is in the floor of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle the priest shall take,\l"
    .string "and put it into the water:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_18::
    .string "And the priest shall set the woman\n"
    .string "before the LORD, and uncover the\l"
    .string "woman’s head, and put the offering\l"
    .string "of memorial in her hands, which is\l"
    .string "the jealousy offering: and the\l"
    .string "priest shall have in his hand the\l"
    .string "bitter water that causeth the curse:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_19::
    .string "And the priest shall charge her by\n"
    .string "an oath, and say unto the woman, If no\l"
    .string "man have lain with thee, and if thou\l"
    .string "hast not gone aside to uncleanness\l"
    .string "with another instead of thy husband,\l"
    .string "be thou free from this bitter water\l"
    .string "that causeth the curse:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_20::
    .string "But if thou hast gone aside to\n"
    .string "another instead of thy husband, and\l"
    .string "if thou be defiled, and some man have\l"
    .string "lain with thee beside thine husband:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_21::
    .string "Then the priest shall charge the\n"
    .string "woman with an oath of cursing, and\l"
    .string "the priest shall say unto the\l"
    .string "woman, The LORD make thee a curse and\l"
    .string "an oath among thy people, when the\l"
    .string "LORD doth make thy thigh to rot, and\l"
    .string "thy belly to swell;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_22::
    .string "And this water that causeth the\n"
    .string "curse shall go into thy bowels, to\l"
    .string "make thy belly to swell, and thy\l"
    .string "thigh to rot: And the woman shall\l"
    .string "say, Amen, amen$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_23::
    .string "And the priest shall write these\n"
    .string "curses in a book, and he shall blot\l"
    .string "them out with the bitter water:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_24::
    .string "And he shall cause the woman to\n"
    .string "drink the bitter water that causeth\l"
    .string "the curse: and the water that causeth\l"
    .string "the curse shall enter into her, and\l"
    .string "become bitter$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_25::
    .string "Then the priest shall take the\n"
    .string "jealousy offering out of the woman’s\l"
    .string "hand, and shall wave the offering\l"
    .string "before the LORD, and offer it upon\l"
    .string "the altar:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_26::
    .string "And the priest shall take an\n"
    .string "handful of the offering, even the\l"
    .string "memorial thereof, and burn it upon\l"
    .string "the altar, and afterward shall\l"
    .string "cause the woman to drink the water$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_27::
    .string "And when he hath made her to drink\n"
    .string "the water, then it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, that, if she be defiled, and\l"
    .string "have done trespass against her\l"
    .string "husband, that the water that causeth\l"
    .string "the curse shall enter into her, and\l"
    .string "become bitter, and her belly shall\l"
    .string "swell, and her thigh shall rot:\l"
    .string "and the woman shall be a curse among\l"
    .string "her people.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_28::
    .string "And if the woman be not defiled, but\n"
    .string "be clean; then she shall be free,\l"
    .string "and shall conceive seed.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_29::
    .string "This is the law of jealousies, when\n"
    .string "a wife goeth aside to another instead\l"
    .string "of her husband, and is defiled;"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_30::
    .string "Or when the spirit of jealousy\n"
    .string "cometh upon him, and he be jealous\l"
    .string "over his wife, and shall set the\l"
    .string "woman before the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "priest shall execute upon her all\l"
    .string "this law$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_5_31::
    .string "Then shall the man be guiltless\n"
    .string "from iniquity, and this woman shall\l"
    .string "bear her iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_1::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_2::
    .string "Speak unto the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, When either man or\l"
    .string "woman shall separate themselves\l"
    .string "to vow a vow of a Nazarite, to\l"
    .string "separate themselves unto the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_3::
    .string "He shall separate himself from\n"
    .string "wine and strong drink, and shall\l"
    .string "drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar\l"
    .string "of strong drink, neither shall he\l"
    .string "drink any liquor of grapes, nor eat\l"
    .string "moist grapes, or dried$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_4::
    .string "All the days of his separation\n"
    .string "shall he eat nothing that is made of\l"
    .string "the vine tree, from the kernels even\l"
    .string "to the husk.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_5::
    .string "All the days of the vow of his\n"
    .string "separation there shall no razor\l"
    .string "come upon his head: until the days\l"
    .string "be fulfilled, in the which he\l"
    .string "separateth himself unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "he shall be holy, and shall let\l"
    .string "the locks of the hair of his head\l"
    .string "grow.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_6::
    .string "All the days that he separateth\n"
    .string "himself unto the LORD he shall come\l"
    .string "at no dead body.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_7::
    .string "He shall not make himself unclean\n"
    .string "for his father, or for his mother,\l"
    .string "for his brother, or for his sister,\l"
    .string "when they die: because the\l"
    .string "consecration of his God is upon his\l"
    .string "head.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_8::
    .string "All the days of his separation he\n"
    .string "is holy unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_9::
    .string "And if any man die very suddenly by\n"
    .string "him, and he hath defiled the head of\l"
    .string "his consecration; then he shall\l"
    .string "shave his head in the day of his\l"
    .string "cleansing, on the seventh day shall\l"
    .string "he shave it.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_10::
    .string "And on the eighth day he shall\n"
    .string "bring two turtles, or two young\l"
    .string "pigeons, to the priest, to the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_11::
    .string "And the priest shall offer the one\n"
    .string "for a sin offering, and the other for\l"
    .string "a burnt offering, and make an\l"
    .string "atonement for him, for that he sinned\l"
    .string "by the dead, and shall hallow his\l"
    .string "head that same day$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_12::
    .string "And he shall consecrate unto the\n"
    .string "LORD the days of his separation, and\l"
    .string "shall bring a lamb of the first\l"
    .string "year for a trespass offering: but\l"
    .string "the days that were before shall be\l"
    .string "lost, because his separation was\l"
    .string "defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_13::
    .string "And this is the law of the Nazarite,\n"
    .string "when the days of his separation are\l"
    .string "fulfilled: he shall be brought\l"
    .string "unto the door of the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the congregation:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_14::
    .string "And he shall offer his offering\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, one he lamb of the\l"
    .string "first year without blemish for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering, and one ewe lamb of\l"
    .string "the first year without blemish for a\l"
    .string "sin offering, and one ram without\l"
    .string "blemish for peace offerings,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_15::
    .string "And a basket of unleavened bread,\n"
    .string "cakes of fine flour mingled with\l"
    .string "oil, and wafers of unleavened bread\l"
    .string "anointed with oil, and their meat\l"
    .string "offering, and their drink offerings$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_16::
    .string "And the priest shall bring them\n"
    .string "before the LORD, and shall offer his\l"
    .string "sin offering, and his burnt offering:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_17::
    .string "And he shall offer the ram for a\n"
    .string "sacrifice of peace offerings unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, with the basket of\l"
    .string "unleavened bread: the priest shall\l"
    .string "offer also his meat offering, and\l"
    .string "his drink offering$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_18::
    .string "And the Nazarite shall shave the\n"
    .string "head of his separation at the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and shall take the\l"
    .string "hair of the head of his separation,\l"
    .string "and put it in the fire which is under\l"
    .string "the sacrifice of the peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_19::
    .string "And the priest shall take the\n"
    .string "sodden shoulder of the ram, and one\l"
    .string "unleavened cake out of the basket,\l"
    .string "and one unleavened wafer, and shall\l"
    .string "put them upon the hands of the\l"
    .string "Nazarite, after the hair of his\l"
    .string "separation is shaven:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_20::
    .string "And the priest shall wave them for\n"
    .string "a wave offering before the LORD: this\l"
    .string "is holy for the priest, with the\l"
    .string "wave breast and heave shoulder: and\l"
    .string "after that the Nazarite may drink\l"
    .string "wine$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_21::
    .string "This is the law of the Nazarite who\n"
    .string "hath vowed, and of his offering unto\l"
    .string "the LORD for his separation, beside\l"
    .string "that that his hand shall get:\l"
    .string "according to the vow which he vowed,\l"
    .string "so he must do after the law of his\l"
    .string "separation.$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_22::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Moses,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_23::
    .string "Speak unto Aaron and unto his sons,\n"
    .string "saying, On this wise ye shall bless\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, saying unto\l"
    .string "them,"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_24::
    .string "The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_25::
    .string "The LORD make his face shine upon\n"
    .string "thee, and be gracious unto thee:"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_26::
    .string "The LORD lift up his countenance\n"
    .string "upon thee, and give thee peace$"
Bible_Text_Numbers_6_27::
    .string "And they shall put my name upon\n"
    .string "the children of Israel, and I will\l"
    .string "bless them.$"
