Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_18_21::
    .string "And if thou say in thine heart, How\n"
    .string "shall we know the word which the\l"
    .string "LORD hath not spoken?"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_18_22::
    .string "When a prophet speaketh in the\n"
    .string "name of the LORD, if the thing\l"
    .string "follow not, nor come to pass, that\l"
    .string "is the thing which the LORD hath not\l"
    .string "spoken, but the prophet hath\l"
    .string "spoken it presumptuously: thou\l"
    .string "shalt not be afraid of him$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_1::
    .string "When the LORD thy God hath cut off\n"
    .string "the nations, whose land the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God giveth thee, and thou succeedest\l"
    .string "them, and dwellest in their cities,\l"
    .string "and in their houses;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_2::
    .string "Thou shalt separate three cities\n"
    .string "for thee in the midst of thy land,\l"
    .string "which the LORD thy God giveth thee to\l"
    .string "possess it$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_3::
    .string "Thou shalt prepare thee a way, and\n"
    .string "divide the coasts of thy land, which\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God giveth thee to\l"
    .string "inherit, into three parts, that\l"
    .string "every slayer may flee thither.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_4::
    .string "And this is the case of the slayer,\n"
    .string "which shall flee thither, that he\l"
    .string "may live: Whoso killeth his\l"
    .string "neighbour ignorantly, whom he hated\l"
    .string "not in time past;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_5::
    .string "As when a man goeth into the wood\n"
    .string "with his neighbour to hew wood, and\l"
    .string "his hand fetcheth a stroke with the\l"
    .string "axe to cut down the tree, and the head\l"
    .string "slippeth from the helve, and\l"
    .string "lighteth upon his neighbour, that he\l"
    .string "die; he shall flee unto one of\l"
    .string "those cities, and live:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_6::
    .string "Lest the avenger of the blood\n"
    .string "pursue the slayer, while his heart\l"
    .string "is hot, and overtake him, because the\l"
    .string "way is long, and slay him; whereas\l"
    .string "he was not worthy of death, inasmuch\l"
    .string "as he hated him not in time past$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_7::
    .string "Wherefore I command thee, saying,\n"
    .string "Thou shalt separate three cities\l"
    .string "for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_8::
    .string "And if the LORD thy God enlarge thy\n"
    .string "coast, as he hath sworn unto thy\l"
    .string "fathers, and give thee all the land\l"
    .string "which he promised to give unto thy\l"
    .string "fathers;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_9::
    .string "If thou shalt keep all these\n"
    .string "commandments to do them, which I\l"
    .string "command thee this day, to love the\l"
    .string "LORD thy God, and to walk ever in his\l"
    .string "ways; then shalt thou add three\l"
    .string "cities more for thee, beside these\l"
    .string "three:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_10::
    .string "That innocent blood be not shed in\n"
    .string "thy land, which the LORD thy God\l"
    .string "giveth thee for an inheritance, and\l"
    .string "so blood be upon thee$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_11::
    .string "But if any man hate his neighbour,\n"
    .string "and lie in wait for him, and rise up\l"
    .string "against him, and smite him mortally\l"
    .string "that he die, and fleeth into one of\l"
    .string "these cities:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_12::
    .string "Then the elders of his city shall\n"
    .string "send and fetch him thence, and\l"
    .string "deliver him into the hand of the\l"
    .string "avenger of blood, that he may die$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_13::
    .string "Thine eye shall not pity him, but\n"
    .string "thou shalt put away the guilt of\l"
    .string "innocent blood from Israel, that it\l"
    .string "may go well with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_14::
    .string "Thou shalt not remove thy\n"
    .string "neighbour’s landmark, which they of\l"
    .string "old time have set in thine\l"
    .string "inheritance, which thou shalt\l"
    .string "inherit in the land that the LORD\l"
    .string "thy God giveth thee to possess it.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_15::
    .string "One witness shall not rise up\n"
    .string "against a man for any iniquity, or\l"
    .string "for any sin, in any sin that he\l"
    .string "sinneth: at the mouth of two\l"
    .string "witnesses, or at the mouth of three\l"
    .string "witnesses, shall the matter be\l"
    .string "established.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_16::
    .string "If a false witness rise up against\n"
    .string "any man to testify against him that\l"
    .string "which is wrong;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_17::
    .string "Then both the men, between whom the\n"
    .string "controversy is, shall stand before\l"
    .string "the LORD, before the priests and the\l"
    .string "judges, which shall be in those\l"
    .string "days;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_18::
    .string "And the judges shall make\n"
    .string "diligent inquisition: and, behold,\l"
    .string "if the witness be a false witness,\l"
    .string "and hath testified falsely against\l"
    .string "his brother;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_19::
    .string "Then shall ye do unto him, as he\n"
    .string "had thought to have done unto his\l"
    .string "brother: so shalt thou put the evil\l"
    .string "away from among you$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_20::
    .string "And those which remain shall hear,\n"
    .string "and fear, and shall henceforth\l"
    .string "commit no more any such evil among\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_19_21::
    .string "And thine eye shall not pity; but\n"
    .string "life shall go for life, eye for\l"
    .string "eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand,\l"
    .string "foot for foot.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_1::
    .string "When thou goest out to battle\n"
    .string "against thine enemies, and seest\l"
    .string "horses, and chariots, and a people\l"
    .string "more than thou, be not afraid of\l"
    .string "them: for the LORD thy God is with\l"
    .string "thee, which brought thee up out of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_2::
    .string "And it shall be, when ye are come\n"
    .string "nigh unto the battle, that the\l"
    .string "priest shall approach and speak\l"
    .string "unto the people,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_3::
    .string "And shall say unto them, Hear, O\n"
    .string "Israel, ye approach this day unto\l"
    .string "battle against your enemies: let\l"
    .string "not your hearts faint, fear not, and\l"
    .string "do not tremble, neither be ye\l"
    .string "terrified because of them;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_4::
    .string "For the LORD your God is he that\n"
    .string "goeth with you, to fight for you\l"
    .string "against your enemies, to save you$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_5::
    .string "And the officers shall speak unto\n"
    .string "the people, saying, What man is\l"
    .string "there that hath built a new house,\l"
    .string "and hath not dedicated it? let him go\l"
    .string "and return to his house, lest he die\l"
    .string "in the battle, and another man\l"
    .string "dedicate it.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_6::
    .string "And what man is he that hath\n"
    .string "planted a vineyard, and hath not yet\l"
    .string "eaten of it? let him also go and\l"
    .string "return unto his house, lest he die in\l"
    .string "the battle, and another man eat of\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_7::
    .string "And what man is there that hath\n"
    .string "betrothed a wife, and hath not taken\l"
    .string "her? let him go and return unto his\l"
    .string "house, lest he die in the battle,\l"
    .string "and another man take her.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_8::
    .string "And the officers shall speak\n"
    .string "further unto the people, and they\l"
    .string "shall say, What man is there that is\l"
    .string "fearful and fainthearted? let him\l"
    .string "go and return unto his house, lest\l"
    .string "his brethren’s heart faint as well\l"
    .string "as his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_9::
    .string "And it shall be, when the officers\n"
    .string "have made an end of speaking unto\l"
    .string "the people that they shall make\l"
    .string "captains of the armies to lead the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_10::
    .string "When thou comest nigh unto a city to\n"
    .string "fight against it, then proclaim\l"
    .string "peace unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_11::
    .string "And it shall be, if it make thee\n"
    .string "answer of peace, and open unto thee,\l"
    .string "then it shall be, that all the\l"
    .string "people that is found therein shall\l"
    .string "be tributaries unto thee, and they\l"
    .string "shall serve thee.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_12::
    .string "And if it will make no peace with\n"
    .string "thee, but will make war against\l"
    .string "thee, then thou shalt besiege it:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_13::
    .string "And when the LORD thy God hath\n"
    .string "delivered it into thine hands, thou\l"
    .string "shalt smite every male thereof with\l"
    .string "the edge of the sword:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_14::
    .string "But the women, and the little ones,\n"
