    .string "man’s life) to employ them in the\l"
    .string "siege:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_20_20::
    .string "Only the trees which thou knowest\n"
    .string "that they be not trees for meat, thou\l"
    .string "shalt destroy and cut them down; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt build bulwarks against\l"
    .string "the city that maketh war with thee,\l"
    .string "until it be subdued$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_1::
    .string "If one be found slain in the land\n"
    .string "which the LORD thy God giveth thee to\l"
    .string "possess it, lying in the field, and\l"
    .string "it be not known who hath slain him:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_2::
    .string "Then thy elders and thy judges\n"
    .string "shall come forth, and they shall\l"
    .string "measure unto the cities which are\l"
    .string "round about him that is slain:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_3::
    .string "And it shall be, that the city\n"
    .string "which is next unto the slain man,\l"
    .string "even the elders of that city shall\l"
    .string "take an heifer, which hath not been\l"
    .string "wrought with, and which hath not\l"
    .string "drawn in the yoke;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_4::
    .string "And the elders of that city shall\n"
    .string "bring down the heifer unto a rough\l"
    .string "valley, which is neither eared nor\l"
    .string "sown, and shall strike off the\l"
    .string "heifer’s neck there in the valley:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_5::
    .string "And the priests the sons of Levi\n"
    .string "shall come near; for them the LORD\l"
    .string "thy God hath chosen to minister unto\l"
    .string "him, and to bless in the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD; and by their word shall every\l"
    .string "controversy and every stroke be\l"
    .string "tried:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_6::
    .string "And all the elders of that city,\n"
    .string "that are next unto the slain man,\l"
    .string "shall wash their hands over the\l"
    .string "heifer that is beheaded in the\l"
    .string "valley:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_7::
    .string "And they shall answer and say, Our\n"
    .string "hands have not shed this blood,\l"
    .string "neither have our eyes seen it$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_8::
    .string "Be merciful, O LORD, unto thy\n"
    .string "people Israel, whom thou hast\l"
    .string "redeemed, and lay not innocent\l"
    .string "blood unto thy people of Israel’s\l"
    .string "charge. And the blood shall be\l"
