Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_9::
    .string "So shalt thou put away the guilt\n"
    .string "of innocent blood from among you,\l"
    .string "when thou shalt do that which is\l"
    .string "right in the sight of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_10::
    .string "When thou goest forth to war against\n"
    .string "thine enemies, and the LORD thy God\l"
    .string "hath delivered them into thine\l"
    .string "hands, and thou hast taken them\l"
    .string "captive,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_11::
    .string "And seest among the captives a\n"
    .string "beautiful woman, and hast a desire\l"
    .string "unto her, that thou wouldest have\l"
    .string "her to thy wife;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_12::
    .string "Then thou shalt bring her home to\n"
    .string "thine house, and she shall shave her\l"
    .string "head, and pare her nails;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_13::
    .string "And she shall put the raiment of\n"
    .string "her captivity from off her, and\l"
    .string "shall remain in thine house, and\l"
    .string "bewail her father and her mother a\l"
    .string "full month: and after that thou\l"
    .string "shalt go in unto her, and be her\l"
    .string "husband, and she shall be thy wife$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_14::
    .string "And it shall be, if thou have no\n"
    .string "delight in her, then thou shalt let\l"
    .string "her go whither she will; but thou\l"
    .string "shalt not sell her at all for\l"
    .string "money, thou shalt not make\l"
    .string "merchandise of her, because thou hast\l"
    .string "humbled her.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_21_15::
    .string "If a man have two wives, one\n"
