    .string "case bring them again unto thy\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_2::
    .string "And if thy brother be not nigh unto\n"
    .string "thee, or if thou know him not, then\l"
    .string "thou shalt bring it unto thine own\l"
    .string "house, and it shall be with thee\l"
    .string "until thy brother seek after it, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt restore it to him again.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_3::
    .string "In like manner shalt thou do with\n"
    .string "his ass; and so shalt thou do with\l"
    .string "his raiment; and with all lost\l"
    .string "thing of thy brother’s, which he hath\l"
    .string "lost, and thou hast found, shalt\l"
    .string "thou do likewise: thou mayest not\l"
    .string "hide thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_4::
    .string "Thou shalt not see thy brother’s\n"
    .string "ass or his ox fall down by the way,\l"
    .string "and hide thyself from them: thou\l"
    .string "shalt surely help him to lift\l"
    .string "them up again.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_5::
    .string "The woman shall not wear that\n"
    .string "which pertaineth unto a man, neither\l"
    .string "shall a man put on a woman’s\l"
    .string "garment: for all that do so are\l"
    .string "abomination unto the LORD thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_6::
    .string "If a bird’s nest chance to be before\n"
    .string "thee in the way in any tree, or on the\l"
    .string "ground, whether they be young ones,\l"
    .string "or eggs, and the dam sitting upon the\l"
    .string "young, or upon the eggs, thou shalt\l"
    .string "not take the dam with the young:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_7::
    .string "But thou shalt in any wise let the\n"
    .string "dam go, and take the young to thee;\l"
    .string "that it may be well with thee, and\l"
    .string "that thou mayest prolong thy days$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_8::
    .string "When thou buildest a new house,\n"
    .string "then thou shalt make a battlement\l"
    .string "for thy roof, that thou bring not\l"
    .string "blood upon thine house, if any man\l"
    .string "fall from thence.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_9::
    .string "Thou shalt not sow thy vineyard\n"
    .string "with divers seeds: lest the fruit of\l"
    .string "thy seed which thou hast sown, and\l"
    .string "the fruit of thy vineyard, be\l"
    .string "defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_10::
    .string "Thou shalt not plow with an ox and\n"
    .string "an ass together.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_11::
    .string "Thou shalt not wear a garment of\n"
    .string "divers sorts, as of woollen and\l"
    .string "linen together.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_12::
    .string "Thou shalt make thee fringes upon\n"
    .string "the four quarters of thy vesture,\l"
    .string "wherewith thou coverest thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_13::
    .string "If any man take a wife, and go in\n"
    .string "unto her, and hate her,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_14::
    .string "And give occasions of speech\n"
    .string "against her, and bring up an evil\l"
    .string "name upon her, and say, I took this\l"
    .string "woman, and when I came to her, I found\l"
    .string "her not a maid:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_15::
    .string "Then shall the father of the\n"
    .string "damsel, and her mother, take and\l"
    .string "bring forth the tokens of the\l"
    .string "damsel’s virginity unto the elders\l"
    .string "of the city in the gate:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_16::
    .string "And the damsel’s father shall say\n"
    .string "unto the elders, I gave my daughter\l"
    .string "unto this man to wife, and he hateth\l"
    .string "her;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_17::
    .string "And, lo, he hath given occasions of\n"
    .string "speech against her, saying, I found\l"
    .string "not thy daughter a maid; and yet\l"
    .string "these are the tokens of my daughter’s\l"
    .string "virginity. And they shall spread\l"
    .string "the cloth before the elders of the\l"
    .string "city$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_18::
    .string "And the elders of that city shall\n"
    .string "take that man and chastise him;"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_19::
    .string "And they shall amerce him in an\n"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver, and give\l"
    .string "them unto the father of the damsel,\l"
    .string "because he hath brought up an evil\l"
    .string "name upon a virgin of Israel: and\l"
    .string "she shall be his wife; he may not\l"
    .string "put her away all his days$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_20::
    .string "But if this thing be true, and the\n"
    .string "tokens of virginity be not found for\l"
    .string "the damsel:"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_21::
    .string "Then they shall bring out the\n"
    .string "damsel to the door of her father’s\l"
    .string "house, and the men of her city shall\l"
    .string "stone her with stones that she die:\l"
    .string "because she hath wrought folly in\l"
    .string "Israel, to play the whore in her\l"
    .string "father’s house: so shalt thou put\l"
    .string "evil away from among you$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_22_22::
    .string "If a man be found lying with a woman\n"
    .string "married to an husband, then they\l"
