    .string "down dew.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_33_29::
    .string "Happy art thou, O Israel: who is\n"
    .string "like unto thee, O people saved by\l"
    .string "the LORD, the shield of thy help,\l"
    .string "and who is the sword of thy\l"
    .string "excellency! and thine enemies\l"
    .string "shall be found liars unto thee; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt tread upon their high\l"
    .string "places.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_1::
    .string "And Moses went up from the plains\n"
    .string "of Moab unto the mountain of Nebo, to\l"
    .string "the top of Pisgah, that is over\l"
    .string "against Jericho. And the LORD shewed\l"
    .string "him all the land of Gilead, unto\l"
    .string "Dan,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_2::
    .string "And all Naphtali, and the land of\n"
    .string "Ephraim, and Manasseh, and all the\l"
    .string "land of Judah, unto the utmost sea,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_3::
    .string "And the south, and the plain of the\n"
    .string "valley of Jericho, the city of\l"
    .string "palm trees, unto Zoar$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_4::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, This is\n"
    .string "the land which I sware unto Abraham,\l"
    .string "unto Isaac, and unto Jacob, saying, I\l"
    .string "will give it unto thy seed: I have\l"
    .string "caused thee to see it with thine\l"
    .string "eyes, but thou shalt not go over\l"
    .string "thither.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_5::
    .string "So Moses the servant of the LORD\n"
    .string "died there in the land of Moab,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_6::
    .string "And he buried him in a valley in\n"
    .string "the land of Moab, over against\l"
    .string "Bethpeor: but no man knoweth of his\l"
    .string "sepulchre unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_7::
    .string "And Moses was an hundred and twenty\n"
    .string "years old when he died: his eye was\l"
    .string "not dim, nor his natural force\l"
    .string "abated.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_8::
    .string "And the children of Israel wept\n"
    .string "for Moses in the plains of Moab\l"
    .string "thirty days: so the days of weeping\l"
    .string "and mourning for Moses were ended.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_9::
    .string "And Joshua the son of Nun was full\n"
    .string "of the spirit of wisdom; for Moses\l"
    .string "had laid his hands upon him: and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel hearkened unto\l"
    .string "him, and did as the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_10::
    .string "And there arose not a prophet\n"
    .string "since in Israel like unto Moses,\l"
    .string "whom the LORD knew face to face,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_11::
    .string "In all the signs and the wonders,\n"
    .string "which the LORD sent him to do in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt to Pharaoh, and to\l"
    .string "all his servants, and to all his\l"
    .string "land,"
Bible_Text_Deuteronomy_34_12::
    .string "And in all that mighty hand, and in\n"
    .string "all the great terror which Moses\l"
    .string "shewed in the sight of all Israel$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_1::
    .string "Now after the death of Moses the\n"
    .string "servant of the LORD it came to pass,\l"
    .string "that the LORD spake unto Joshua the\l"
    .string "son of Nun, Moses’ minister, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_2::
    .string "Moses my servant is dead; now\n"
    .string "therefore arise, go over this Jordan,\l"
    .string "thou, and all this people, unto\l"
    .string "the land which I do give to them,\l"
    .string "even to the children of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_3::
    .string "Every place that the sole of your\n"
    .string "foot shall tread upon, that have I\l"
    .string "given unto you, as I said unto Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_4::
    .string "From the wilderness and this\n"
    .string "Lebanon even unto the great river,\l"
    .string "the river Euphrates, all the land\l"
    .string "of the Hittites, and unto the great\l"
    .string "sea toward the going down of the sun,\l"
    .string "shall be your coast.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_5::
    .string "There shall not any man be able to\n"
    .string "stand before thee all the days of\l"
    .string "thy life: as I was with Moses, so I\l"
    .string "will be with thee: I will not fail\l"
    .string "thee, nor forsake thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_6::
    .string "Be strong and of a good courage: for\n"
    .string "unto this people shalt thou divide\l"
    .string "for an inheritance the land, which I\l"
    .string "sware unto their fathers to give them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_7::
    .string "Only be thou strong and very\n"
    .string "courageous, that thou mayest observe\l"
    .string "to do according to all the law,\l"
    .string "which Moses my servant commanded\l"
    .string "thee: turn not from it to the right\l"
    .string "hand or to the left, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "prosper whithersoever thou goest.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_8::
    .string "This book of the law shall not\n"
    .string "depart out of thy mouth; but thou\l"
    .string "shalt meditate therein day and\l"
    .string "night, that thou mayest observe to do\l"
    .string "according to all that is written\l"
    .string "therein: for then thou shalt make\l"
    .string "thy way prosperous, and then thou\l"
    .string "shalt have good success.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_9::
    .string "Have not I commanded thee? Be strong\n"
    .string "and of a good courage; be not afraid,\l"
    .string "neither be thou dismayed: for the\l"
    .string "LORD thy God is with thee\l"
    .string "whithersoever thou goest.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_10::
    .string "Then Joshua commanded the officers\n"
    .string "of the people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_11::
    .string "Pass through the host, and command\n"
    .string "the people, saying, Prepare you\l"
    .string "victuals; for within three days ye\l"
    .string "shall pass over this Jordan, to go\l"
    .string "in to possess the land, which the\l"
    .string "LORD your God giveth you to possess\l"
    .string "it$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_12::
    .string "And to the Reubenites, and to the\n"
    .string "Gadites, and to half the tribe of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, spake Joshua, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_13::
    .string "Remember the word which Moses the\n"
    .string "servant of the LORD commanded you,\l"
    .string "saying, The LORD your God hath given\l"
    .string "you rest, and hath given you this\l"
    .string "land$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_14::
    .string "Your wives, your little ones, and\n"
    .string "your cattle, shall remain in the\l"
    .string "land which Moses gave you on this\l"
    .string "side Jordan; but ye shall pass\l"
    .string "before your brethren armed, all the\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, and help\l"
    .string "them;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_15::
    .string "Until the LORD have given your\n"
    .string "brethren rest, as he hath given you,\l"
    .string "and they also have possessed the\l"
    .string "land which the LORD your God giveth\l"
    .string "them: then ye shall return unto the\l"
    .string "land of your possession, and enjoy\l"
    .string "it, which Moses the LORD’s servant\l"
    .string "gave you on this side Jordan toward\l"
    .string "the sunrising$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_16::
    .string "And they answered Joshua, saying,\n"
    .string "All that thou commandest us we\l"
    .string "will do, and whithersoever thou\l"
    .string "sendest us, we will go.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_17::
    .string "According as we hearkened unto\n"
    .string "Moses in all things, so will we\l"
    .string "hearken unto thee: only the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God be with thee, as he was with\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_1_18::
    .string "Whosoever he be that doth rebel\n"
    .string "against thy commandment, and will\l"
    .string "not hearken unto thy words in all\l"
    .string "that thou commandest him, he shall\l"
    .string "be put to death: only be strong and\l"
    .string "of a good courage.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_1::
    .string "And Joshua the son of Nun sent out\n"
    .string "of Shittim two men to spy secretly,\l"
    .string "saying, Go view the land, even\l"
    .string "Jericho. And they went, and came into\l"
    .string "an harlot’s house, named Rahab, and\l"
    .string "lodged there.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_2::
    .string "And it was told the king of Jericho,\n"
    .string "saying, Behold, there came men in\l"
    .string "hither to night of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel to search out the country.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_3::
    .string "And the king of Jericho sent unto\n"
    .string "Rahab, saying, Bring forth the men\l"
    .string "that are come to thee, which are\l"
    .string "entered into thine house: for they be\l"
    .string "come to search out all the country.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_4::
    .string "And the woman took the two men, and\n"
    .string "hid them, and said thus, There came\l"
    .string "men unto me, but I wist not whence\l"
    .string "they were:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_5::
    .string "And it came to pass about the time\n"
    .string "of shutting of the gate, when it was\l"
    .string "dark, that the men went out: whither\l"
    .string "the men went I wot not: pursue after\l"
    .string "them quickly; for ye shall overtake\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_6::
    .string "But she had brought them up to the\n"
    .string "roof of the house, and hid them with\l"
    .string "the stalks of flax, which she had\l"
    .string "laid in order upon the roof.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_7::
    .string "And the men pursued after them the\n"
    .string "way to Jordan unto the fords: and as\l"
    .string "soon as they which pursued after\l"
    .string "them were gone out, they shut the\l"
    .string "gate.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_8::
    .string "And before they were laid down, she\n"
    .string "came up unto them upon the roof;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_9::
    .string "And she said unto the men, I know\n"
    .string "that the LORD hath given you the\l"
    .string "land, and that your terror is fallen\l"
    .string "upon us, and that all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land faint\l"
    .string "because of you$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_10::
    .string "For we have heard how the LORD dried\n"
    .string "up the water of the Red sea for you,\l"
    .string "when ye came out of Egypt; and what\l"
    .string "ye did unto the two kings of the\l"
    .string "Amorites, that were on the other side\l"
    .string "Jordan, Sihon and Og, whom ye\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_11::
    .string "And as soon as we had heard these\n"
    .string "things, our hearts did melt, neither\l"
    .string "did there remain any more courage in\l"
    .string "any man, because of you: for the LORD\l"
    .string "your God, he is God in heaven above,\l"
    .string "and in earth beneath.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_12::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray you, swear\n"
    .string "unto me by the LORD, since I have\l"
    .string "shewed you kindness, that ye will\l"
    .string "also shew kindness unto my father’s\l"
    .string "house, and give me a true token:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_13::
    .string "And that ye will save alive my\n"
    .string "father, and my mother, and my\l"
    .string "brethren, and my sisters, and all\l"
    .string "that they have, and deliver our\l"
    .string "lives from death$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_14::
    .string "And the men answered her, Our life\n"
    .string "for yours, if ye utter not this our\l"
    .string "business. And it shall be, when the\l"
    .string "LORD hath given us the land, that we\l"
    .string "will deal kindly and truly with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_15::
    .string "Then she let them down by a cord\n"
    .string "through the window: for her house was\l"
    .string "upon the town wall, and she dwelt\l"
    .string "upon the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_16::
    .string "And she said unto them, Get you to\n"
    .string "the mountain, lest the pursuers\l"
    .string "meet you; and hide yourselves there\l"
    .string "three days, until the pursuers be\l"
    .string "returned: and afterward may ye go\l"
    .string "your way.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_17::
    .string "And the men said unto her, We will\n"
    .string "be blameless of this thine oath\l"
    .string "which thou hast made us swear.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_18::
    .string "Behold, when we come into the land,\n"
    .string "thou shalt bind this line of\l"
    .string "scarlet thread in the window which\l"
    .string "thou didst let us down by: and thou\l"
    .string "shalt bring thy father, and thy\l"
    .string "mother, and thy brethren, and all\l"
    .string "thy father’s household, home unto\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_19::
    .string "And it shall be, that whosoever\n"
    .string "shall go out of the doors of thy\l"
    .string "house into the street, his blood\l"
    .string "shall be upon his head, and we\l"
    .string "will be guiltless: and whosoever\l"
    .string "shall be with thee in the house, his\l"
    .string "blood shall be on our head, if any\l"
    .string "hand be upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_20::
    .string "And if thou utter this our business,\n"
    .string "then we will be quit of thine oath\l"
    .string "which thou hast made us to swear.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_21::
    .string "And she said, According unto your\n"
    .string "words, so be it. And she sent them\l"
    .string "away, and they departed: and she\l"
    .string "bound the scarlet line in the\l"
    .string "window.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_22::
    .string "And they went, and came unto the\n"
    .string "mountain, and abode there three days,\l"
    .string "until the pursuers were returned:\l"
    .string "and the pursuers sought them\l"
    .string "throughout all the way, but found\l"
    .string "them not.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_23::
    .string "So the two men returned, and\n"
    .string "descended from the mountain, and\l"
    .string "passed over, and came to Joshua the\l"
    .string "son of Nun, and told him all things\l"
    .string "that befell them:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_2_24::
    .string "And they said unto Joshua, Truly\n"
    .string "the LORD hath delivered into our\l"
    .string "hands all the land; for even all\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of the country do\l"
    .string "faint because of us$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_1::
    .string "And Joshua rose early in the\n"
    .string "morning; and they removed from\l"
    .string "Shittim, and came to Jordan, he and\l"
    .string "all the children of Israel, and\l"
    .string "lodged there before they passed over.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_2::
    .string "And it came to pass after three\n"
    .string "days, that the officers went through\l"
    .string "the host;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_3::
    .string "And they commanded the people,\n"
    .string "saying, When ye see the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD your God, and\l"
    .string "the priests the Levites bearing it,\l"
    .string "then ye shall remove from your\l"
    .string "place, and go after it$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_4::
    .string "Yet there shall be a space between\n"
    .string "you and it, about two thousand cubits\l"
    .string "by measure: come not near unto it,\l"
    .string "that ye may know the way by which ye\l"
    .string "must go: for ye have not passed this\l"
    .string "way heretofore.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_5::
    .string "And Joshua said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Sanctify yourselves: for to morrow\l"
    .string "the LORD will do wonders among you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_6::
    .string "And Joshua spake unto the priests,\n"
    .string "saying, Take up the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant, and pass over before the\l"
    .string "people. And they took up the ark of\l"
    .string "the covenant, and went before the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_7::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, This\n"
    .string "day will I begin to magnify thee in\l"
    .string "the sight of all Israel, that they\l"
    .string "may know that, as I was with Moses, so\l"
    .string "I will be with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_8::
    .string "And thou shalt command the priests\n"
    .string "that bear the ark of the covenant,\l"
    .string "saying, When ye are come to the brink\l"
    .string "of the water of Jordan, ye shall\l"
    .string "stand still in Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_9::
    .string "And Joshua said unto the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, Come hither, and hear the\l"
    .string "words of the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_10::
    .string "And Joshua said, Hereby ye shall\n"
    .string "know that the living God is among\l"
    .string "you, and that he will without fail\l"
    .string "drive out from before you the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the\l"
    .string "Hivites, and the Perizzites, and the\l"
    .string "Girgashites, and the Amorites, and\l"
    .string "the Jebusites.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_11::
    .string "Behold, the ark of the covenant of\n"
    .string "the LORD of all the earth passeth\l"
    .string "over before you into Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_12::
    .string "Now therefore take you twelve men\n"
    .string "out of the tribes of Israel, out of\l"
    .string "every tribe a man.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_13::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, as soon\n"
    .string "as the soles of the feet of the\l"
    .string "priests that bear the ark of the\l"
    .string "LORD, the LORD of all the earth,\l"
    .string "shall rest in the waters of Jordan,\l"
    .string "that the waters of Jordan shall be\l"
    .string "cut off from the waters that come\l"
    .string "down from above; and they shall\l"
    .string "stand upon an heap.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_14::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "people removed from their tents, to\l"
    .string "pass over Jordan, and the priests\l"
    .string "bearing the ark of the covenant\l"
    .string "before the people;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_15::
    .string "And as they that bare the ark were\n"
    .string "come unto Jordan, and the feet of the\l"
    .string "priests that bare the ark were\l"
    .string "dipped in the brim of the water,\l"
    .string "(for Jordan overfloweth all his\l"
    .string "banks all the time of harvest,)"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_16::
    .string "That the waters which came down from\n"
    .string "above stood and rose up upon an\l"
    .string "heap very far from the city Adam,\l"
    .string "that is beside Zaretan: and those\l"
    .string "that came down toward the sea of the\l"
    .string "plain, even the salt sea, failed,\l"
    .string "and were cut off: and the people\l"
    .string "passed over right against Jericho$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_3_17::
    .string "And the priests that bare the ark\n"
    .string "of the covenant of the LORD stood\l"
    .string "firm on dry ground in the midst of\l"
    .string "Jordan, and all the Israelites\l"
    .string "passed over on dry ground, until\l"
    .string "all the people were passed clean\l"
    .string "over Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all the\n"
    .string "people were clean passed over\l"
    .string "Jordan, that the LORD spake unto\l"
    .string "Joshua, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_2::
    .string "Take you twelve men out of the\n"
    .string "people, out of every tribe a man,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_3::
    .string "And command ye them, saying, Take\n"
    .string "you hence out of the midst of Jordan,\l"
    .string "out of the place where the priests’\l"
    .string "feet stood firm, twelve stones, and\l"
    .string "ye shall carry them over with you,\l"
    .string "and leave them in the lodging\l"
    .string "place, where ye shall lodge this\l"
    .string "night$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_4::
    .string "Then Joshua called the twelve men,\n"
    .string "whom he had prepared of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, out of every\l"
    .string "tribe a man:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_5::
    .string "And Joshua said unto them, Pass over\n"
    .string "before the ark of the LORD your God\l"
    .string "into the midst of Jordan, and take\l"
    .string "you up every man of you a stone upon\l"
    .string "his shoulder, according unto the\l"
    .string "number of the tribes of the children\l"
    .string "of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_6::
    .string "That this may be a sign among you,\n"
    .string "that when your children ask their\l"
    .string "fathers in time to come, saying, What\l"
    .string "mean ye by these stones?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_7::
    .string "Then ye shall answer them, That the\n"
    .string "waters of Jordan were cut off before\l"
    .string "the ark of the covenant of the LORD;\l"
    .string "when it passed over Jordan, the\l"
    .string "waters of Jordan were cut off: and\l"
    .string "these stones shall be for a\l"
    .string "memorial unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel for ever$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_8::
    .string "And the children of Israel did so\n"
    .string "as Joshua commanded, and took up\l"
    .string "twelve stones out of the midst of\l"
    .string "Jordan, as the LORD spake unto\l"
    .string "Joshua, according to the number of\l"
    .string "the tribes of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and carried them over with\l"
    .string "them unto the place where they\l"
    .string "lodged, and laid them down there.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_9::
    .string "And Joshua set up twelve stones in\n"
    .string "the midst of Jordan, in the place\l"
    .string "where the feet of the priests which\l"
    .string "bare the ark of the covenant stood:\l"
    .string "and they are there unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_10::
    .string "For the priests which bare the ark\n"
    .string "stood in the midst of Jordan, until\l"
    .string "everything was finished that the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Joshua to speak unto\l"
    .string "the people, according to all that\l"
    .string "Moses commanded Joshua: and the\l"
    .string "people hasted and passed over.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all the\n"
    .string "people were clean passed over,\l"
    .string "that the ark of the LORD passed over,\l"
    .string "and the priests, in the presence of\l"
    .string "the people.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_12::
    .string "And the children of Reuben, and the\n"
    .string "children of Gad, and half the tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh, passed over armed\l"
    .string "before the children of Israel, as\l"
    .string "Moses spake unto them:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_13::
    .string "About forty thousand prepared for\n"
    .string "war passed over before the LORD unto\l"
    .string "battle, to the plains of Jericho$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_14::
    .string "On that day the LORD magnified\n"
    .string "Joshua in the sight of all Israel;\l"
    .string "and they feared him, as they feared\l"
    .string "Moses, all the days of his life.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_15::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Joshua,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_16::
    .string "Command the priests that bear the\n"
    .string "ark of the testimony, that they come\l"
    .string "up out of Jordan$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_17::
    .string "Joshua therefore commanded the\n"
    .string "priests, saying, Come ye up out of\l"
    .string "Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "priests that bare the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD were come up\l"
    .string "out of the midst of Jordan, and the\l"
    .string "soles of the priests’ feet were\l"
    .string "lifted up unto the dry land, that\l"
    .string "the waters of Jordan returned unto\l"
    .string "their place, and flowed over all\l"
    .string "his banks, as they did before.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_19::
    .string "And the people came up out of\n"
    .string "Jordan on the tenth day of the first\l"
    .string "month, and encamped in Gilgal, in\l"
    .string "the east border of Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_20::
    .string "And those twelve stones, which they\n"
    .string "took out of Jordan, did Joshua pitch\l"
    .string "in Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_21::
    .string "And he spake unto the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, saying, When your children\l"
    .string "shall ask their fathers in time to\l"
    .string "come, saying, What mean these stones?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_22::
    .string "Then ye shall let your children\n"
    .string "know, saying, Israel came over this\l"
    .string "Jordan on dry land$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_23::
    .string "For the LORD your God dried up the\n"
    .string "waters of Jordan from before you,\l"
    .string "until ye were passed over, as the\l"
    .string "LORD your God did to the Red sea,\l"
    .string "which he dried up from before us,\l"
    .string "until we were gone over:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_4_24::
    .string "That all the people of the earth\n"
    .string "might know the hand of the LORD, that\l"
    .string "it is mighty: that ye might fear the\l"
    .string "LORD your God for ever$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all the\n"
    .string "kings of the Amorites, which were on\l"
    .string "the side of Jordan westward, and all\l"
    .string "the kings of the Canaanites, which\l"
    .string "were by the sea, heard that the LORD\l"
    .string "had dried up the waters of Jordan\l"
    .string "from before the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "until we were passed over, that\l"
    .string "their heart melted, neither was\l"
    .string "there spirit in them any more,\l"
    .string "because of the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_2::
    .string "At that time the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "Joshua, Make thee sharp knives, and\l"
    .string "circumcise again the children of\l"
    .string "Israel the second time.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_3::
    .string "And Joshua made him sharp knives,\n"
    .string "and circumcised the children of\l"
    .string "Israel at the hill of the foreskins.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_4::
    .string "And this is the cause why Joshua did\n"
    .string "circumcise: All the people that\l"
    .string "came out of Egypt, that were males,\l"
    .string "even all the men of war, died in the\l"
    .string "wilderness by the way, after they\l"
    .string "came out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_5::
    .string "Now all the people that came out\n"
    .string "were circumcised: but all the\l"
    .string "people that were born in the\l"
    .string "wilderness by the way as they came\l"
    .string "forth out of Egypt, them they had not\l"
    .string "circumcised.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_6::
    .string "For the children of Israel walked\n"
    .string "forty years in the wilderness, till\l"
    .string "all the people that were men of\l"
    .string "war, which came out of Egypt, were\l"
    .string "consumed, because they obeyed not the\l"
    .string "voice of the LORD: unto whom the LORD\l"
    .string "sware that he would not shew them\l"
    .string "the land, which the LORD sware unto\l"
    .string "their fathers that he would give us,\l"
    .string "a land that floweth with milk and\l"
    .string "honey.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_7::
    .string "And their children, whom he raised\n"
    .string "up in their stead, them Joshua\l"
    .string "circumcised: for they were\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, because they had not\l"
    .string "circumcised them by the way.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they had\n"
    .string "done circumcising all the people,\l"
    .string "that they abode in their places in\l"
    .string "the camp, till they were whole.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, This\n"
    .string "day have I rolled away the reproach\l"
    .string "of Egypt from off you. Wherefore the\l"
    .string "name of the place is called\l"
    .string "Gilgal unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_10::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "encamped in Gilgal, and kept the\l"
    .string "passover on the fourteenth day of the\l"
    .string "month at even in the plains of\l"
    .string "Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_11::
    .string "And they did eat of the old corn of\n"
    .string "the land on the morrow after the\l"
    .string "passover, unleavened cakes, and\l"
    .string "parched corn in the selfsame day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_12::
    .string "And the manna ceased on the morrow\n"
    .string "after they had eaten of the old corn\l"
    .string "of the land; neither had the\l"
    .string "children of Israel manna any more;\l"
    .string "but they did eat of the fruit of the\l"
    .string "land of Canaan that year.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joshua was\n"
    .string "by Jericho, that he lifted up his\l"
    .string "eyes and looked, and, behold, there\l"
    .string "stood a man over against him with his\l"
    .string "sword drawn in his hand: and Joshua\l"
    .string "went unto him, and said unto him, Art\l"
    .string "thou for us, or for our adversaries?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_14::
    .string "And he said, Nay; but as captain of\n"
    .string "the host of the LORD am I now come.\l"
    .string "And Joshua fell on his face to the\l"
    .string "earth, and did worship, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, What saith my Lord unto his\l"
    .string "servant?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_5_15::
    .string "And the captain of the LORD’s host\n"
    .string "said unto Joshua, Loose thy shoe from\l"
    .string "off thy foot; for the place whereon\l"
    .string "thou standest is holy. And Joshua\l"
    .string "did so$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_1::
    .string "Now Jericho was straitly shut up\n"
    .string "because of the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "none went out, and none came in.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, See,\n"
    .string "I have given into thine hand Jericho,\l"
    .string "and the king thereof, and the mighty\l"
    .string "men of valour.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_3::
    .string "And ye shall compass the city,\n"
    .string "all ye men of war, and go round\l"
    .string "about the city once. Thus shalt thou\l"
    .string "do six days.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_4::
    .string "And seven priests shall bear\n"
    .string "before the ark seven trumpets of\l"
    .string "rams’ horns: and the seventh day ye\l"
    .string "shall compass the city seven times,\l"
    .string "and the priests shall blow with\l"
    .string "the trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_5::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "when they make a long blast with the\l"
    .string "ram’s horn, and when ye hear the\l"
    .string "sound of the trumpet, all the\l"
    .string "people shall shout with a great\l"
    .string "shout; and the wall of the city\l"
    .string "shall fall down flat, and the\l"
    .string "people shall ascend up every man\l"
    .string "straight before him.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_6::
    .string "And Joshua the son of Nun called\n"
    .string "the priests, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Take up the ark of the covenant, and\l"
    .string "let seven priests bear seven\l"
    .string "trumpets of rams’ horns before the\l"
    .string "ark of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_7::
    .string "And he said unto the people, Pass\n"
    .string "on, and compass the city, and let\l"
    .string "him that is armed pass on before the\l"
    .string "ark of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joshua had\n"
    .string "spoken unto the people, that the\l"
    .string "seven priests bearing the seven\l"
    .string "trumpets of rams’ horns passed on\l"
    .string "before the LORD, and blew with the\l"
    .string "trumpets: and the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD followed them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_9::
    .string "And the armed men went before the\n"
    .string "priests that blew with the\l"
    .string "trumpets, and the rereward came\l"
    .string "after the ark, the priests going on,\l"
    .string "and blowing with the trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_10::
    .string "And Joshua had commanded the\n"
    .string "people, saying, Ye shall not\l"
    .string "shout, nor make any noise with your\l"
    .string "voice, neither shall any word\l"
    .string "proceed out of your mouth, until the\l"
    .string "day I bid you shout; then shall ye\l"
    .string "shout.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_11::
    .string "So the ark of the LORD compassed\n"
    .string "the city, going about it once: and\l"
    .string "they came into the camp, and lodged\l"
    .string "in the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_12::
    .string "And Joshua rose early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and the priests took up the\l"
    .string "ark of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_13::
    .string "And seven priests bearing seven\n"
    .string "trumpets of rams’ horns before the\l"
    .string "ark of the LORD went on continually,\l"
    .string "and blew with the trumpets: and the\l"
    .string "armed men went before them; but the\l"
    .string "rereward came after the ark of the\l"
    .string "LORD, the priests going on, and\l"
    .string "blowing with the trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_14::
    .string "And the second day they compassed\n"
    .string "the city once, and returned into the\l"
    .string "camp: so they did six days.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_15::
    .string "And it came to pass on the seventh\n"
    .string "day, that they rose early about the\l"
    .string "dawning of the day, and compassed\l"
    .string "the city after the same manner seven\l"
    .string "times: only on that day they\l"
    .string "compassed the city seven times.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_16::
    .string "And it came to pass at the seventh\n"
    .string "time, when the priests blew with the\l"
    .string "trumpets, Joshua said unto the\l"
    .string "people, Shout; for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "given you the city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_17::
    .string "And the city shall be accursed,\n"
    .string "even it, and all that are therein,\l"
    .string "to the LORD: only Rahab the harlot\l"
    .string "shall live, she and all that are\l"
    .string "with her in the house, because she\l"
    .string "hid the messengers that we sent.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_18::
    .string "And ye, in any wise keep yourselves\n"
    .string "from the accursed thing, lest ye\l"
    .string "make yourselves accursed, when ye\l"
    .string "take of the accursed thing, and make\l"
    .string "the camp of Israel a curse, and\l"
    .string "trouble it.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_19::
    .string "But all the silver, and gold, and\n"
    .string "vessels of brass and iron, are\l"
    .string "consecrated unto the LORD: they\l"
    .string "shall come into the treasury of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_20::
    .string "So the people shouted when the\n"
    .string "priests blew with the trumpets: and\l"
    .string "it came to pass, when the people\l"
    .string "heard the sound of the trumpet, and\l"
    .string "the people shouted with a great\l"
    .string "shout, that the wall fell down\l"
    .string "flat, so that the people went up\l"
    .string "into the city, every man straight\l"
    .string "before him, and they took the city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_21::
    .string "And they utterly destroyed all\n"
    .string "that was in the city, both man and\l"
    .string "woman, young and old, and ox, and\l"
    .string "sheep, and ass, with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_22::
    .string "But Joshua had said unto the two men\n"
    .string "that had spied out the country, Go\l"
    .string "into the harlot’s house, and bring\l"
    .string "out thence the woman, and all that\l"
    .string "she hath, as ye sware unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_23::
    .string "And the young men that were spies\n"
    .string "went in, and brought out Rahab, and\l"
    .string "her father, and her mother, and her\l"
    .string "brethren, and all that she had; and\l"
    .string "they brought out all her kindred,\l"
    .string "and left them without the camp of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_24::
    .string "And they burnt the city with fire,\n"
    .string "and all that was therein: only the\l"
    .string "silver, and the gold, and the\l"
    .string "vessels of brass and of iron, they\l"
    .string "put into the treasury of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_25::
    .string "And Joshua saved Rahab the harlot\n"
    .string "alive, and her father’s household,\l"
    .string "and all that she had; and she\l"
    .string "dwelleth in Israel even unto this\l"
    .string "day; because she hid the messengers,\l"
    .string "which Joshua sent to spy out Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_26::
    .string "And Joshua adjured them at that\n"
    .string "time, saying, Cursed be the man\l"
    .string "before the LORD, that riseth up and\l"
    .string "buildeth this city Jericho: he\l"
    .string "shall lay the foundation thereof\l"
    .string "in his firstborn, and in his youngest\l"
    .string "son shall he set up the gates of it.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_6_27::
    .string "So the LORD was with Joshua; and his\n"
    .string "fame was noised throughout all the\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_1::
    .string "But the children of Israel\n"
    .string "committed a trespass in the accursed\l"
    .string "thing: for Achan, the son of Carmi,\l"
    .string "the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of\l"
    .string "the tribe of Judah, took of the\l"
    .string "accursed thing: and the anger of the\l"
    .string "LORD was kindled against the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_2::
    .string "And Joshua sent men from Jericho to\n"
    .string "Ai, which is beside Bethaven, on the\l"
    .string "east of Bethel, and spake unto them,\l"
    .string "saying, Go up and view the country.\l"
    .string "And the men went up and viewed Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_3::
    .string "And they returned to Joshua, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Let not all the\l"
    .string "people go up; but let about two or\l"
    .string "three thousand men go up and smite\l"
    .string "Ai; and make not all the people to\l"
    .string "labour thither; for they are but few.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_4::
    .string "So there went up thither of the\n"
    .string "people about three thousand men:\l"
    .string "and they fled before the men of Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_5::
    .string "And the men of Ai smote of them\n"
    .string "about thirty and six men: for they\l"
    .string "chased them from before the gate even\l"
    .string "unto Shebarim, and smote them in the\l"
    .string "going down: wherefore the hearts of\l"
    .string "the people melted, and became as\l"
    .string "water.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_6::
    .string "And Joshua rent his clothes, and\n"
    .string "fell to the earth upon his face\l"
    .string "before the ark of the LORD until the\l"
    .string "eventide, he and the elders of\l"
    .string "Israel, and put dust upon their\l"
    .string "heads.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_7::
    .string "And Joshua said, Alas, O LORD God,\n"
    .string "wherefore hast thou at all brought\l"
    .string "this people over Jordan, to\l"
    .string "deliver us into the hand of the\l"
    .string "Amorites, to destroy us? would to\l"
    .string "God we had been content, and dwelt on\l"
    .string "the other side Jordan!"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_8::
    .string "O LORD, what shall I say, when\n"
    .string "Israel turneth their backs before\l"
    .string "their enemies!"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_9::
    .string "For the Canaanites and all the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of the land shall hear\l"
    .string "of it, and shall environ us round,\l"
    .string "and cut off our name from the earth:\l"
    .string "and what wilt thou do unto thy great\l"
    .string "name?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_10::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, Get\n"
    .string "thee up; wherefore liest thou thus\l"
    .string "upon thy face?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_11::
    .string "Israel hath sinned, and they have\n"
    .string "also transgressed my covenant which\l"
    .string "I commanded them: for they have even\l"
    .string "taken of the accursed thing, and have\l"
    .string "also stolen, and dissembled also,\l"
    .string "and they have put it even among\l"
    .string "their own stuff$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_12::
    .string "Therefore the children of Israel\n"
    .string "could not stand before their\l"
    .string "enemies, but turned their backs\l"
    .string "before their enemies, because they\l"
    .string "were accursed: neither will I be\l"
    .string "with you any more, except ye destroy\l"
    .string "the accursed from among you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_13::
    .string "Up, sanctify the people, and say,\n"
    .string "Sanctify yourselves against to\l"
    .string "morrow: for thus saith the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel, There is an accursed\l"
    .string "thing in the midst of thee, O Israel:\l"
    .string "thou canst not stand before thine\l"
    .string "enemies, until ye take away the\l"
    .string "accursed thing from among you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_14::
    .string "In the morning therefore ye shall\n"
    .string "be brought according to your tribes:\l"
    .string "and it shall be, that the tribe\l"
    .string "which the LORD taketh shall come\l"
    .string "according to the families thereof;\l"
    .string "and the family which the LORD shall\l"
    .string "take shall come by households; and\l"
    .string "the household which the LORD shall\l"
    .string "take shall come man by man.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_15::
    .string "And it shall be, that he that is\n"
    .string "taken with the accursed thing shall\l"
    .string "be burnt with fire, he and all that\l"
    .string "he hath: because he hath transgressed\l"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD, and because\l"
    .string "he hath wrought folly in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_16::
    .string "So Joshua rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and brought Israel by their\l"
    .string "tribes; and the tribe of Judah was\l"
    .string "taken:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_17::
    .string "And he brought the family of Judah;\n"
    .string "and he took the family of the\l"
    .string "Zarhites: and he brought the family\l"
    .string "of the Zarhites man by man; and Zabdi\l"
    .string "was taken:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_18::
    .string "And he brought his household man by\n"
    .string "man; and Achan, the son of Carmi, the\l"
    .string "son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Judah, was taken$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_19::
    .string "And Joshua said unto Achan, My son,\n"
    .string "give, I pray thee, glory to the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, and make confession\l"
    .string "unto him; and tell me now what thou\l"
    .string "hast done; hide it not from me.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_20::
    .string "And Achan answered Joshua, and said,\n"
    .string "Indeed I have sinned against the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, and thus and thus have\l"
    .string "I done:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_21::
    .string "When I saw among the spoils a\n"
    .string "goodly Babylonish garment, and two\l"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver, and a\l"
    .string "wedge of gold of fifty shekels\l"
    .string "weight, then I coveted them, and took\l"
    .string "them; and, behold, they are hid in\l"
    .string "the earth in the midst of my tent, and\l"
    .string "the silver under it$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_22::
    .string "So Joshua sent messengers, and they\n"
    .string "ran unto the tent; and, behold, it\l"
    .string "was hid in his tent, and the silver\l"
    .string "under it.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_23::
    .string "And they took them out of the midst\n"
    .string "of the tent, and brought them unto\l"
    .string "Joshua, and unto all the children\l"
    .string "of Israel, and laid them out before\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_24::
    .string "And Joshua, and all Israel with\n"
    .string "him, took Achan the son of Zerah, and\l"
    .string "the silver, and the garment, and the\l"
    .string "wedge of gold, and his sons, and his\l"
    .string "daughters, and his oxen, and his\l"
    .string "asses, and his sheep, and his tent,\l"
    .string "and all that he had: and they\l"
    .string "brought them unto the valley of\l"
    .string "Achor.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_25::
    .string "And Joshua said, Why hast thou\n"
    .string "troubled us? the LORD shall\l"
    .string "trouble thee this day. And all\l"
    .string "Israel stoned him with stones, and\l"
    .string "burned them with fire, after they had\l"
    .string "stoned them with stones.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_7_26::
    .string "And they raised over him a great\n"
    .string "heap of stones unto this day. So the\l"
    .string "LORD turned from the fierceness of\l"
    .string "his anger. Wherefore the name of that\l"
    .string "place was called, The valley of\l"
    .string "Achor, unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, Fear\n"
    .string "not, neither be thou dismayed: take\l"
    .string "all the people of war with thee,\l"
    .string "and arise, go up to Ai: see, I have\l"
    .string "given into thy hand the king of Ai,\l"
    .string "and his people, and his city, and\l"
    .string "his land:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_2::
    .string "And thou shalt do to Ai and her king\n"
    .string "as thou didst unto Jericho and her\l"
    .string "king: only the spoil thereof, and\l"
    .string "the cattle thereof, shall ye take\l"
    .string "for a prey unto yourselves: lay\l"
    .string "thee an ambush for the city behind it$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_3::
    .string "So Joshua arose, and all the\n"
    .string "people of war, to go up against Ai:\l"
    .string "and Joshua chose out thirty thousand\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, and sent them\l"
    .string "away by night.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_4::
    .string "And he commanded them, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold, ye shall lie in wait\l"
    .string "against the city, even behind the\l"
    .string "city: go not very far from the city,\l"
    .string "but be ye all ready:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_5::
    .string "And I, and all the people that\n"
    .string "are with me, will approach unto\l"
    .string "the city: and it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, when they come out against us,\l"
    .string "as at the first, that we will flee\l"
    .string "before them,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_6::
    .string "(For they will come out after us)\n"
    .string "till we have drawn them from the\l"
    .string "city; for they will say, They flee\l"
    .string "before us, as at the first: therefore\l"
    .string "we will flee before them$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_7::
    .string "Then ye shall rise up from the\n"
    .string "ambush, and seize upon the city: for\l"
    .string "the LORD your God will deliver it\l"
    .string "into your hand.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_8::
    .string "And it shall be, when ye have taken\n"
    .string "the city, that ye shall set the city\l"
    .string "on fire: according to the commandment\l"
    .string "of the LORD shall ye do. See, I have\l"
    .string "commanded you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_9::
    .string "Joshua therefore sent them forth:\n"
    .string "and they went to lie in ambush, and\l"
    .string "abode between Bethel and Ai, on the\l"
    .string "west side of Ai: but Joshua lodged\l"
    .string "that night among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_10::
    .string "And Joshua rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and numbered the people,\l"
    .string "and went up, he and the elders of\l"
    .string "Israel, before the people to Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_11::
    .string "And all the people, even the\n"
    .string "people of war that were with him,\l"
    .string "went up, and drew nigh, and came\l"
    .string "before the city, and pitched on the\l"
    .string "north side of Ai: now there was a\l"
    .string "valley between them and Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_12::
    .string "And he took about five thousand men,\n"
    .string "and set them to lie in ambush\l"
    .string "between Bethel and Ai, on the west\l"
    .string "side of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_13::
    .string "And when they had set the people,\n"
    .string "even all the host that was on the\l"
    .string "north of the city, and their liers in\l"
    .string "wait on the west of the city, Joshua\l"
    .string "went that night into the midst of the\l"
    .string "valley.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_14::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "of Ai saw it, that they hasted and\l"
    .string "rose up early, and the men of the\l"
    .string "city went out against Israel to\l"
    .string "battle, he and all his people, at\l"
    .string "a time appointed, before the\l"
    .string "plain; but he wist not that there\l"
    .string "were liers in ambush against him\l"
    .string "behind the city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_15::
    .string "And Joshua and all Israel made as\n"
    .string "if they were beaten before them, and\l"
    .string "fled by the way of the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_16::
    .string "And all the people that were in\n"
    .string "Ai were called together to pursue\l"
    .string "after them: and they pursued after\l"
    .string "Joshua, and were drawn away from the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_17::
    .string "And there was not a man left in Ai\n"
    .string "or Bethel, that went not out after\l"
    .string "Israel: and they left the city\l"
    .string "open, and pursued after Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_18::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua,\n"
    .string "Stretch out the spear that is in thy\l"
    .string "hand toward Ai; for I will give it\l"
    .string "into thine hand. And Joshua stretched\l"
    .string "out the spear that he had in his hand\l"
    .string "toward the city.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_19::
    .string "And the ambush arose quickly out of\n"
    .string "their place, and they ran as soon as\l"
    .string "he had stretched out his hand: and\l"
    .string "they entered into the city, and took\l"
    .string "it, and hasted and set the city on\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_20::
    .string "And when the men of Ai looked\n"
    .string "behind them, they saw, and, behold,\l"
    .string "the smoke of the city ascended up to\l"
    .string "heaven, and they had no power to\l"
    .string "flee this way or that way: and the\l"
    .string "people that fled to the wilderness\l"
    .string "turned back upon the pursuers.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_21::
    .string "And when Joshua and all Israel saw\n"
    .string "that the ambush had taken the city,\l"
    .string "and that the smoke of the city\l"
    .string "ascended, then they turned again, and\l"
    .string "slew the men of Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_22::
    .string "And the other issued out of the city\n"
    .string "against them; so they were in the\l"
    .string "midst of Israel, some on this side,\l"
    .string "and some on that side: and they smote\l"
    .string "them, so that they let none of them\l"
    .string "remain or escape.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_23::
    .string "And the king of Ai they took alive,\n"
    .string "and brought him to Joshua.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_24::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Israel\n"
    .string "had made an end of slaying all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Ai in the field, in\l"
    .string "the wilderness wherein they chased\l"
    .string "them, and when they were all\l"
    .string "fallen on the edge of the sword,\l"
    .string "until they were consumed, that all\l"
    .string "the Israelites returned unto Ai, and\l"
    .string "smote it with the edge of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_25::
    .string "And so it was, that all that fell\n"
    .string "that day, both of men and women, were\l"
    .string "twelve thousand, even all the men\l"
    .string "of Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_26::
    .string "For Joshua drew not his hand back,\n"
    .string "wherewith he stretched out the\l"
    .string "spear, until he had utterly\l"
    .string "destroyed all the inhabitants of Ai.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_27::
    .string "Only the cattle and the spoil of\n"
    .string "that city Israel took for a prey\l"
    .string "unto themselves, according unto the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD which he commanded\l"
    .string "Joshua.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_28::
    .string "And Joshua burnt Ai, and made it an\n"
    .string "heap for ever, even a desolation\l"
    .string "unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_29::
    .string "And the king of Ai he hanged on a\n"
    .string "tree until eventide: and as soon as\l"
    .string "the sun was down, Joshua commanded\l"
    .string "that they should take his carcase\l"
    .string "down from the tree, and cast it at the\l"
    .string "entering of the gate of the city, and\l"
    .string "raise thereon a great heap of\l"
    .string "stones, that remaineth unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_30::
    .string "Then Joshua built an altar unto\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel in mount\l"
    .string "Ebal,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_31::
    .string "As Moses the servant of the LORD\n"
    .string "commanded the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "as it is written in the book of the\l"
    .string "law of Moses, an altar of whole\l"
    .string "stones, over which no man hath lift\l"
    .string "up any iron: and they offered\l"
    .string "thereon burnt offerings unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, and sacrificed peace offerings$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_32::
    .string "And he wrote there upon the stones\n"
    .string "a copy of the law of Moses, which he\l"
    .string "wrote in the presence of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_33::
    .string "And all Israel, and their elders,\n"
    .string "and officers, and their judges, stood\l"
    .string "on this side the ark and on that side\l"
    .string "before the priests the Levites,\l"
    .string "which bare the ark of the covenant of\l"
    .string "the LORD, as well the stranger, as\l"
    .string "he that was born among them; half of\l"
    .string "them over against mount Gerizim, and\l"
    .string "half of them over against mount\l"
    .string "Ebal; as Moses the servant of the\l"
    .string "LORD had commanded before, that they\l"
    .string "should bless the people of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_34::
    .string "And afterward he read all the\n"
    .string "words of the law, the blessings and\l"
    .string "cursings, according to all that is\l"
    .string "written in the book of the law.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_8_35::
    .string "There was not a word of all that\n"
    .string "Moses commanded, which Joshua read\l"
    .string "not before all the congregation of\l"
    .string "Israel, with the women, and the\l"
    .string "little ones, and the strangers that\l"
    .string "were conversant among them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all the\n"
    .string "kings which were on this side Jordan,\l"
    .string "in the hills, and in the valleys,\l"
    .string "and in all the coasts of the great\l"
    .string "sea over against Lebanon, the\l"
    .string "Hittite, and the Amorite, the\l"
    .string "Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite,\l"
    .string "and the Jebusite, heard thereof;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_2::
    .string "That they gathered themselves\n"
    .string "together, to fight with Joshua and\l"
    .string "with Israel, with one accord$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_3::
    .string "And when the inhabitants of Gibeon\n"
    .string "heard what Joshua had done unto\l"
    .string "Jericho and to Ai,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_4::
    .string "They did work wilily, and went and\n"
    .string "made as if they had been ambassadors,\l"
    .string "and took old sacks upon their asses,\l"
    .string "and wine bottles, old, and rent, and\l"
    .string "bound up;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_5::
    .string "And old shoes and clouted upon\n"
    .string "their feet, and old garments upon\l"
    .string "them; and all the bread of their\l"
    .string "provision was dry and mouldy$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_6::
    .string "And they went to Joshua unto the\n"
    .string "camp at Gilgal, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "and to the men of Israel, We be come\l"
    .string "from a far country: now therefore\l"
    .string "make ye a league with us.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_7::
    .string "And the men of Israel said unto the\n"
    .string "Hivites, Peradventure ye dwell\l"
    .string "among us; and how shall we make a\l"
    .string "league with you?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_8::
    .string "And they said unto Joshua, We are\n"
    .string "thy servants. And Joshua said unto\l"
    .string "them, Who are ye? and from whence\l"
    .string "come ye?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_9::
    .string "And they said unto him, From a very\n"
    .string "far country thy servants are come\l"
    .string "because of the name of the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God: for we have heard the fame of\l"
    .string "him, and all that he did in Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_10::
    .string "And all that he did to the two\n"
    .string "kings of the Amorites, that were\l"
    .string "beyond Jordan, to Sihon king of\l"
    .string "Heshbon, and to Og king of Bashan,\l"
    .string "which was at Ashtaroth$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_11::
    .string "Wherefore our elders and all the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of our country spake to\l"
    .string "us, saying, Take victuals with you\l"
    .string "for the journey, and go to meet them,\l"
    .string "and say unto them, We are your\l"
    .string "servants: therefore now make ye a\l"
    .string "league with us.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_12::
    .string "This our bread we took hot for our\n"
    .string "provision out of our houses on the\l"
    .string "day we came forth to go unto you; but\l"
    .string "now, behold, it is dry, and it is\l"
    .string "mouldy:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_13::
    .string "And these bottles of wine, which we\n"
    .string "filled, were new; and, behold, they\l"
    .string "be rent: and these our garments and\l"
    .string "our shoes are become old by reason\l"
    .string "of the very long journey$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_14::
    .string "And the men took of their victuals,\n"
    .string "and asked not counsel at the mouth\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_15::
    .string "And Joshua made peace with them,\n"
    .string "and made a league with them, to let\l"
    .string "them live: and the princes of the\l"
    .string "congregation sware unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_16::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "three days after they had made a\l"
    .string "league with them, that they heard\l"
    .string "that they were their neighbours, and\l"
    .string "that they dwelt among them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_17::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "journeyed, and came unto their cities\l"
    .string "on the third day. Now their cities\l"
    .string "were Gibeon, and Chephirah, and\l"
    .string "Beeroth, and Kirjathjearim.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_18::
    .string "And the children of Israel smote\n"
    .string "them not, because the princes of the\l"
    .string "congregation had sworn unto them by\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel. And all the\l"
    .string "congregation murmured against the\l"
    .string "princes.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_19::
    .string "But all the princes said unto\n"
    .string "all the congregation, We have sworn\l"
    .string "unto them by the LORD God of Israel:\l"
    .string "now therefore we may not touch them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_20::
    .string "This we will do to them; we will\n"
    .string "even let them live, lest wrath be\l"
    .string "upon us, because of the oath which we\l"
    .string "sware unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_21::
    .string "And the princes said unto them, Let\n"
    .string "them live; but let them be hewers of\l"
    .string "wood and drawers of water unto all\l"
    .string "the congregation; as the princes had\l"
    .string "promised them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_22::
    .string "And Joshua called for them, and he\n"
    .string "spake unto them, saying, Wherefore\l"
    .string "have ye beguiled us, saying, We are\l"
    .string "very far from you; when ye dwell\l"
    .string "among us?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_23::
    .string "Now therefore ye are cursed, and\n"
    .string "there shall none of you be freed\l"
    .string "from being bondmen, and hewers of\l"
    .string "wood and drawers of water for the\l"
    .string "house of my God$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_24::
    .string "And they answered Joshua, and said,\n"
    .string "Because it was certainly told thy\l"
    .string "servants, how that the LORD thy God\l"
    .string "commanded his servant Moses to give\l"
    .string "you all the land, and to destroy\l"
    .string "all the inhabitants of the land\l"
    .string "from before you, therefore we were\l"
    .string "sore afraid of our lives because of\l"
    .string "you, and have done this thing.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_25::
    .string "And now, behold, we are in thine\n"
    .string "hand: as it seemeth good and right\l"
    .string "unto thee to do unto us, do.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_26::
    .string "And so did he unto them, and\n"
    .string "delivered them out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, that they\l"
    .string "slew them not.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_9_27::
    .string "And Joshua made them that day hewers\n"
    .string "of wood and drawers of water for the\l"
    .string "congregation, and for the altar of\l"
    .string "the LORD, even unto this day, in the\l"
    .string "place which he should choose.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when\n"
    .string "Adonizedec king of Jerusalem had\l"
    .string "heard how Joshua had taken Ai, and\l"
    .string "had utterly destroyed it; as he had\l"
    .string "done to Jericho and her king, so he\l"
    .string "had done to Ai and her king; and how\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Gibeon had made\l"
    .string "peace with Israel, and were among\l"
    .string "them;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_2::
    .string "That they feared greatly, because\n"
    .string "Gibeon was a great city, as one of the\l"
    .string "royal cities, and because it was\l"
    .string "greater than Ai, and all the men\l"
    .string "thereof were mighty$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_3::
    .string "Wherefore Adonizedec king of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, sent unto Hoham king of\l"
    .string "Hebron, and unto Piram king of\l"
    .string "Jarmuth, and unto Japhia king of\l"
    .string "Lachish, and unto Debir king of\l"
    .string "Eglon, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_4::
    .string "Come up unto me, and help me, that\n"
    .string "we may smite Gibeon: for it hath made\l"
    .string "peace with Joshua and with the\l"
    .string "children of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_5::
    .string "Therefore the five kings of the\n"
    .string "Amorites, the king of Jerusalem, the\l"
    .string "king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth,\l"
    .string "the king of Lachish, the king of\l"
    .string "Eglon, gathered themselves\l"
    .string "together, and went up, they and all\l"
    .string "their hosts, and encamped before\l"
    .string "Gibeon, and made war against it.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_6::
    .string "And the men of Gibeon sent unto\n"
    .string "Joshua to the camp to Gilgal,\l"
    .string "saying, Slack not thy hand from thy\l"
    .string "servants; come up to us quickly, and\l"
    .string "save us, and help us: for all the\l"
    .string "kings of the Amorites that dwell in\l"
    .string "the mountains are gathered together\l"
    .string "against us.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_7::
    .string "So Joshua ascended from Gilgal,\n"
    .string "he, and all the people of war with\l"
    .string "him, and all the mighty men of\l"
    .string "valour.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_8::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, Fear\n"
    .string "them not: for I have delivered them\l"
    .string "into thine hand; there shall not a\l"
    .string "man of them stand before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_9::
    .string "Joshua therefore came unto them\n"
    .string "suddenly, and went up from Gilgal\l"
    .string "all night.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_10::
    .string "And the LORD discomfited them\n"
    .string "before Israel, and slew them with a\l"
    .string "great slaughter at Gibeon, and\l"
    .string "chased them along the way that goeth\l"
    .string "up to Bethhoron, and smote them to\l"
    .string "Azekah, and unto Makkedah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they fled\n"
    .string "from before Israel, and were in the\l"
    .string "going down to Bethhoron, that the\l"
    .string "LORD cast down great stones from\l"
    .string "heaven upon them unto Azekah, and\l"
    .string "they died: they were more which died\l"
    .string "with hailstones than they whom the\l"
    .string "children of Israel slew with the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_12::
    .string "Then spake Joshua to the LORD in\n"
    .string "the day when the LORD delivered up\l"
    .string "the Amorites before the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, and he said in the sight of\l"
    .string "Israel, Sun, stand thou still upon\l"
    .string "Gibeon; and thou, Moon, in the\l"
    .string "valley of Ajalon.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_13::
    .string "And the sun stood still, and the\n"
    .string "moon stayed, until the people had\l"
    .string "avenged themselves upon their\l"
    .string "enemies. Is not this written in the\l"
    .string "book of Jasher? So the sun stood\l"
    .string "still in the midst of heaven, and\l"
    .string "hasted not to go down about a whole\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_14::
    .string "And there was no day like that\n"
    .string "before it or after it, that the LORD\l"
    .string "hearkened unto the voice of a man:\l"
    .string "for the LORD fought for Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_15::
    .string "And Joshua returned, and all\n"
    .string "Israel with him, unto the camp to\l"
    .string "Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_16::
    .string "But these five kings fled, and hid\n"
    .string "themselves in a cave at Makkedah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_17::
    .string "And it was told Joshua, saying, The\n"
    .string "five kings are found hid in a cave at\l"
    .string "Makkedah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_18::
    .string "And Joshua said, Roll great stones\n"
    .string "upon the mouth of the cave, and set\l"
    .string "men by it for to keep them:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_19::
    .string "And stay ye not, but pursue after\n"
    .string "your enemies, and smite the hindmost\l"
    .string "of them; suffer them not to enter\l"
    .string "into their cities: for the LORD your\l"
    .string "God hath delivered them into your\l"
    .string "hand$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_20::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joshua and\n"
    .string "the children of Israel had made an\l"
    .string "end of slaying them with a very\l"
    .string "great slaughter, till they were\l"
    .string "consumed, that the rest which\l"
    .string "remained of them entered into fenced\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_21::
    .string "And all the people returned to\n"
    .string "the camp to Joshua at Makkedah in\l"
    .string "peace: none moved his tongue against\l"
    .string "any of the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_22::
    .string "Then said Joshua, Open the mouth of\n"
    .string "the cave, and bring out those five\l"
    .string "kings unto me out of the cave.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_23::
    .string "And they did so, and brought forth\n"
    .string "those five kings unto him out of the\l"
    .string "cave, the king of Jerusalem, the\l"
    .string "king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth,\l"
    .string "the king of Lachish, and the king of\l"
    .string "Eglon.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_24::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they\n"
    .string "brought out those kings unto Joshua,\l"
    .string "that Joshua called for all the men\l"
    .string "of Israel, and said unto the\l"
    .string "captains of the men of war which\l"
    .string "went with him, Come near, put your\l"
    .string "feet upon the necks of these kings.\l"
    .string "And they came near, and put their\l"
    .string "feet upon the necks of them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_25::
    .string "And Joshua said unto them, Fear not,\n"
    .string "nor be dismayed, be strong and of\l"
    .string "good courage: for thus shall the\l"
    .string "LORD do to all your enemies against\l"
    .string "whom ye fight.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_26::
    .string "And afterward Joshua smote them, and\n"
    .string "slew them, and hanged them on five\l"
    .string "trees: and they were hanging upon\l"
    .string "the trees until the evening.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_27::
    .string "And it came to pass at the time of\n"
    .string "the going down of the sun, that\l"
    .string "Joshua commanded, and they took them\l"
    .string "down off the trees, and cast them\l"
    .string "into the cave wherein they had been\l"
    .string "hid, and laid great stones in the\l"
    .string "cave’s mouth, which remain until\l"
    .string "this very day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_28::
    .string "And that day Joshua took Makkedah,\n"
    .string "and smote it with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword, and the king thereof he\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed, them, and all\l"
    .string "the souls that were therein; he let\l"
    .string "none remain: and he did to the king of\l"
    .string "Makkedah as he did unto the king of\l"
    .string "Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_29::
    .string "Then Joshua passed from Makkedah,\n"
    .string "and all Israel with him, unto\l"
    .string "Libnah, and fought against Libnah:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_30::
    .string "And the LORD delivered it also, and\n"
    .string "the king thereof, into the hand of\l"
    .string "Israel; and he smote it with the edge\l"
    .string "of the sword, and all the souls\l"
    .string "that were therein; he let none\l"
    .string "remain in it; but did unto the king\l"
    .string "thereof as he did unto the king of\l"
    .string "Jericho$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_31::
    .string "And Joshua passed from Libnah, and\n"
    .string "all Israel with him, unto Lachish,\l"
    .string "and encamped against it, and fought\l"
    .string "against it:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_32::
    .string "And the LORD delivered Lachish into\n"
    .string "the hand of Israel, which took it on\l"
    .string "the second day, and smote it with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword, and all the\l"
    .string "souls that were therein, according\l"
    .string "to all that he had done to Libnah$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_33::
    .string "Then Horam king of Gezer came up to\n"
    .string "help Lachish; and Joshua smote him\l"
    .string "and his people, until he had left\l"
    .string "him none remaining.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_34::
    .string "And from Lachish Joshua passed unto\n"
    .string "Eglon, and all Israel with him;\l"
    .string "and they encamped against it, and\l"
    .string "fought against it:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_35::
    .string "And they took it on that day, and\n"
    .string "smote it with the edge of the sword,\l"
    .string "and all the souls that were therein\l"
    .string "he utterly destroyed that day,\l"
    .string "according to all that he had done to\l"
    .string "Lachish$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_36::
    .string "And Joshua went up from Eglon, and\n"
    .string "all Israel with him, unto Hebron;\l"
    .string "and they fought against it:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_37::
    .string "And they took it, and smote it with\n"
    .string "the edge of the sword, and the king\l"
    .string "thereof, and all the cities\l"
    .string "thereof, and all the souls that\l"
    .string "were therein; he left none\l"
    .string "remaining, according to all that he\l"
    .string "had done to Eglon; but destroyed it\l"
    .string "utterly, and all the souls that\l"
    .string "were therein$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_38::
    .string "And Joshua returned, and all\n"
    .string "Israel with him, to Debir; and\l"
    .string "fought against it:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_39::
    .string "And he took it, and the king\n"
    .string "thereof, and all the cities\l"
    .string "thereof; and they smote them with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword, and utterly\l"
    .string "destroyed all the souls that were\l"
    .string "therein; he left none remaining: as\l"
    .string "he had done to Hebron, so he did to\l"
    .string "Debir, and to the king thereof; as he\l"
    .string "had done also to Libnah, and to her\l"
    .string "king$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_40::
    .string "So Joshua smote all the country of\n"
    .string "the hills, and of the south, and of\l"
    .string "the vale, and of the springs, and\l"
    .string "all their kings: he left none\l"
    .string "remaining, but utterly destroyed\l"
    .string "all that breathed, as the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_41::
    .string "And Joshua smote them from\n"
    .string "Kadeshbarnea even unto Gaza, and\l"
    .string "all the country of Goshen, even unto\l"
    .string "Gibeon.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_42::
    .string "And all these kings and their land\n"
    .string "did Joshua take at one time, because\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel fought for\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_10_43::
    .string "And Joshua returned, and all\n"
    .string "Israel with him, unto the camp to\l"
    .string "Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jabin king\n"
    .string "of Hazor had heard those things, that\l"
    .string "he sent to Jobab king of Madon, and to\l"
    .string "the king of Shimron, and to the king\l"
    .string "of Achshaph,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_2::
    .string "And to the kings that were on the\n"
    .string "north of the mountains, and of the\l"
    .string "plains south of Chinneroth, and in\l"
    .string "the valley, and in the borders of\l"
    .string "Dor on the west,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_3::
    .string "And to the Canaanite on the east and\n"
    .string "on the west, and to the Amorite, and\l"
    .string "the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and\l"
    .string "the Jebusite in the mountains, and to\l"
    .string "the Hivite under Hermon in the land\l"
    .string "of Mizpeh$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_4::
    .string "And they went out, they and all\n"
    .string "their hosts with them, much people,\l"
    .string "even as the sand that is upon the sea\l"
    .string "shore in multitude, with horses and\l"
    .string "chariots very many.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_5::
    .string "And when all these kings were met\n"
    .string "together, they came and pitched\l"
    .string "together at the waters of Merom, to\l"
    .string "fight against Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_6::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Joshua, Be\n"
    .string "not afraid because of them: for to\l"
    .string "morrow about this time will I\l"
    .string "deliver them up all slain before\l"
    .string "Israel: thou shalt hough their\l"
    .string "horses, and burn their chariots with\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_7::
    .string "So Joshua came, and all the\n"
    .string "people of war with him, against them\l"
    .string "by the waters of Merom suddenly; and\l"
    .string "they fell upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_8::
    .string "And the LORD delivered them into\n"
    .string "the hand of Israel, who smote them,\l"
    .string "and chased them unto great Zidon, and\l"
    .string "unto Misrephothmaim, and unto the\l"
    .string "valley of Mizpeh eastward; and they\l"
    .string "smote them, until they left them\l"
    .string "none remaining.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_9::
    .string "And Joshua did unto them as the LORD\n"
    .string "bade him: he houghed their horses,\l"
    .string "and burnt their chariots with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_10::
    .string "And Joshua at that time turned back,\n"
    .string "and took Hazor, and smote the king\l"
    .string "thereof with the sword: for Hazor\l"
    .string "beforetime was the head of all\l"
    .string "those kingdoms.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_11::
    .string "And they smote all the souls that\n"
    .string "were therein with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword, utterly destroying them:\l"
    .string "there was not any left to breathe:\l"
    .string "and he burnt Hazor with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_12::
    .string "And all the cities of those kings,\n"
    .string "and all the kings of them, did\l"
    .string "Joshua take, and smote them with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword, and he utterly\l"
    .string "destroyed them, as Moses the servant\l"
    .string "of the LORD commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_13::
    .string "But as for the cities that stood\n"
    .string "still in their strength, Israel\l"
    .string "burned none of them, save Hazor\l"
    .string "only; that did Joshua burn.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_14::
    .string "And all the spoil of these\n"
    .string "cities, and the cattle, the\l"
    .string "children of Israel took for a prey\l"
    .string "unto themselves; but every man they\l"
    .string "smote with the edge of the sword,\l"
    .string "until they had destroyed them,\l"
    .string "neither left they any to breathe.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_15::
    .string "As the LORD commanded Moses his\n"
    .string "servant, so did Moses command Joshua,\l"
    .string "and so did Joshua; he left nothing\l"
    .string "undone of all that the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_16::
    .string "So Joshua took all that land, the\n"
    .string "hills, and all the south country,\l"
    .string "and all the land of Goshen, and the\l"
    .string "valley, and the plain, and the\l"
    .string "mountain of Israel, and the valley\l"
    .string "of the same;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_17::
    .string "Even from the mount Halak, that\n"
    .string "goeth up to Seir, even unto Baalgad\l"
    .string "in the valley of Lebanon under\l"
    .string "mount Hermon: and all their kings he\l"
    .string "took, and smote them, and slew them$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_18::
    .string "Joshua made war a long time with\n"
    .string "all those kings.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_19::
    .string "There was not a city that made\n"
    .string "peace with the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "save the Hivites the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Gibeon: all other they took in\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_20::
    .string "For it was of the LORD to harden\n"
    .string "their hearts, that they should come\l"
    .string "against Israel in battle, that he\l"
    .string "might destroy them utterly, and that\l"
    .string "they might have no favour, but that\l"
    .string "he might destroy them, as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_21::
    .string "And at that time came Joshua, and\n"
    .string "cut off the Anakims from the\l"
    .string "mountains, from Hebron, from Debir,\l"
    .string "from Anab, and from all the\l"
    .string "mountains of Judah, and from all the\l"
    .string "mountains of Israel: Joshua\l"
    .string "destroyed them utterly with their\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_22::
    .string "There was none of the Anakims left\n"
    .string "in the land of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel: only in Gaza, in Gath, and\l"
    .string "in Ashdod, there remained.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_11_23::
    .string "So Joshua took the whole land,\n"
    .string "according to all that the LORD said\l"
    .string "unto Moses; and Joshua gave it for an\l"
    .string "inheritance unto Israel according\l"
    .string "to their divisions by their tribes.\l"
    .string "And the land rested from war.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_1::
    .string "Now these are the kings of the land,\n"
    .string "which the children of Israel smote,\l"
    .string "and possessed their land on the\l"
    .string "other side Jordan toward the rising\l"
    .string "of the sun, from the river Arnon unto\l"
    .string "mount Hermon, and all the plain on\l"
    .string "the east:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_2::
    .string "Sihon king of the Amorites, who\n"
    .string "dwelt in Heshbon, and ruled from\l"
    .string "Aroer, which is upon the bank of the\l"
    .string "river Arnon, and from the middle of\l"
    .string "the river, and from half Gilead,\l"
    .string "even unto the river Jabbok, which is\l"
    .string "the border of the children of Ammon;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_3::
    .string "And from the plain to the sea of\n"
    .string "Chinneroth on the east, and unto the\l"
    .string "sea of the plain, even the salt sea\l"
    .string "on the east, the way to\l"
    .string "Bethjeshimoth; and from the south,\l"
    .string "under Ashdothpisgah:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_4::
    .string "And the coast of Og king of Bashan,\n"
    .string "which was of the remnant of the\l"
    .string "giants, that dwelt at Ashtaroth and\l"
    .string "at Edrei,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_5::
    .string "And reigned in mount Hermon, and in\n"
    .string "Salcah, and in all Bashan, unto the\l"
    .string "border of the Geshurites and the\l"
    .string "Maachathites, and half Gilead, the\l"
    .string "border of Sihon king of Heshbon$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_6::
    .string "Them did Moses the servant of the\n"
    .string "LORD and the children of Israel\l"
    .string "smite: and Moses the servant of the\l"
    .string "LORD gave it for a possession unto\l"
    .string "the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and\l"
    .string "the half tribe of Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_7::
    .string "And these are the kings of the\n"
    .string "country which Joshua and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel smote on this\l"
    .string "side Jordan on the west, from\l"
    .string "Baalgad in the valley of Lebanon\l"
    .string "even unto the mount Halak, that\l"
    .string "goeth up to Seir; which Joshua gave\l"
    .string "unto the tribes of Israel for a\l"
    .string "possession according to their\l"
    .string "divisions;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_8::
    .string "In the mountains, and in the\n"
    .string "valleys, and in the plains, and in\l"
    .string "the springs, and in the wilderness,\l"
    .string "and in the south country; the\l"
    .string "Hittites, the Amorites, and the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, the Perizzites, the\l"
    .string "Hivites, and the Jebusites:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_9::
    .string "The king of Jericho, one; the king\n"
    .string "of Ai, which is beside Bethel, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_10::
    .string "The king of Jerusalem, one; the\n"
    .string "king of Hebron, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_11::
    .string "The king of Jarmuth, one; the king\n"
    .string "of Lachish, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_12::
    .string "The king of Eglon, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Gezer, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_13::
    .string "The king of Debir, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Geder, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_14::
    .string "The king of Hormah, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Arad, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_15::
    .string "The king of Libnah, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Adullam, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_16::
    .string "The king of Makkedah, one; the king\n"
    .string "of Bethel, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_17::
    .string "The king of Tappuah, one; the king\n"
    .string "of Hepher, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_18::
    .string "The king of Aphek, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Lasharon, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_19::
    .string "The king of Madon, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Hazor, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_20::
    .string "The king of Shimronmeron, one; the\n"
    .string "king of Achshaph, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_21::
    .string "The king of Taanach, one; the king\n"
    .string "of Megiddo, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_22::
    .string "The king of Kedesh, one; the king of\n"
    .string "Jokneam of Carmel, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_23::
    .string "The king of Dor in the coast of Dor,\n"
    .string "one; the king of the nations of\l"
    .string "Gilgal, one;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_12_24::
    .string "The king of Tirzah, one: all the\n"
    .string "kings thirty and one$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_1::
    .string "Now Joshua was old and stricken in\n"
    .string "years; and the LORD said unto him,\l"
    .string "Thou art old and stricken in years,\l"
    .string "and there remaineth yet very much\l"
    .string "land to be possessed.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_2::
    .string "This is the land that yet\n"
    .string "remaineth: all the borders of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and all Geshuri,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_3::
    .string "From Sihor, which is before Egypt,\n"
    .string "even unto the borders of Ekron\l"
    .string "northward, which is counted to the\l"
    .string "Canaanite: five lords of the\l"
    .string "Philistines; the Gazathites, and the\l"
    .string "Ashdothites, the Eshkalonites, the\l"
    .string "Gittites, and the Ekronites; also\l"
    .string "the Avites:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_4::
    .string "From the south, all the land of\n"
    .string "the Canaanites, and Mearah that is\l"
    .string "beside the Sidonians unto Aphek, to\l"
    .string "the borders of the Amorites:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_5::
    .string "And the land of the Giblites, and\n"
    .string "all Lebanon, toward the sunrising,\l"
    .string "from Baalgad under mount Hermon unto\l"
    .string "the entering into Hamath$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_6::
    .string "All the inhabitants of the hill\n"
    .string "country from Lebanon unto\l"
    .string "Misrephothmaim, and all the\l"
    .string "Sidonians, them will I drive out\l"
    .string "from before the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "only divide thou it by lot unto the\l"
    .string "Israelites for an inheritance, as I\l"
    .string "have commanded thee.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_7::
    .string "Now therefore divide this land for\n"
    .string "an inheritance unto the nine tribes,\l"
    .string "and the half tribe of Manasseh,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_8::
    .string "With whom the Reubenites and the\n"
    .string "Gadites have received their\l"
    .string "inheritance, which Moses gave them,\l"
    .string "beyond Jordan eastward, even as Moses\l"
    .string "the servant of the LORD gave them;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_9::
    .string "From Aroer, that is upon the bank of\n"
    .string "the river Arnon, and the city that is\l"
    .string "in the midst of the river, and all\l"
    .string "the plain of Medeba unto Dibon;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_10::
    .string "And all the cities of Sihon king of\n"
    .string "the Amorites, which reigned in\l"
    .string "Heshbon, unto the border of the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_11::
    .string "And Gilead, and the border of the\n"
    .string "Geshurites and Maachathites, and\l"
    .string "all mount Hermon, and all Bashan\l"
    .string "unto Salcah;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_12::
    .string "All the kingdom of Og in Bashan,\n"
    .string "which reigned in Ashtaroth and in\l"
    .string "Edrei, who remained of the remnant of\l"
    .string "the giants: for these did Moses\l"
    .string "smite, and cast them out$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_13::
    .string "Nevertheless the children of\n"
    .string "Israel expelled not the\l"
    .string "Geshurites, nor the Maachathites:\l"
    .string "but the Geshurites and the\l"
    .string "Maachathites dwell among the\l"
    .string "Israelites until this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_14::
    .string "Only unto the tribes of Levi he\n"
    .string "gave none inheritance; the\l"
    .string "sacrifices of the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "made by fire are their inheritance,\l"
    .string "as he said unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_15::
    .string "And Moses gave unto the tribe of the\n"
    .string "children of Reuben inheritance\l"
    .string "according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_16::
    .string "And their coast was from Aroer, that\n"
    .string "is on the bank of the river Arnon, and\l"
    .string "the city that is in the midst of the\l"
    .string "river, and all the plain by\l"
    .string "Medeba;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_17::
    .string "Heshbon, and all her cities that\n"
    .string "are in the plain; Dibon, and\l"
    .string "Bamothbaal, and Bethbaalmeon,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_18::
    .string "And Jahaza, and Kedemoth, and\n"
    .string "Mephaath,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_19::
    .string "And Kirjathaim, and Sibmah, and\n"
    .string "Zarethshahar in the mount of the\l"
    .string "valley,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_20::
    .string "And Bethpeor, and Ashdothpisgah,\n"
    .string "and Bethjeshimoth,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_21::
    .string "And all the cities of the plain,\n"
    .string "and all the kingdom of Sihon king of\l"
    .string "the Amorites, which reigned in\l"
    .string "Heshbon, whom Moses smote with the\l"
    .string "princes of Midian, Evi, and Rekem,\l"
    .string "and Zur, and Hur, and Reba, which were\l"
    .string "dukes of Sihon, dwelling in the\l"
    .string "country$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_22::
    .string "Balaam also the son of Beor, the\n"
    .string "soothsayer, did the children of\l"
    .string "Israel slay with the sword among\l"
    .string "them that were slain by them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_23::
    .string "And the border of the children of\n"
    .string "Reuben was Jordan, and the border\l"
    .string "thereof. This was the inheritance of\l"
    .string "the children of Reuben after their\l"
    .string "families, the cities and the\l"
    .string "villages thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_24::
    .string "And Moses gave inheritance unto the\n"
    .string "tribe of Gad, even unto the children\l"
    .string "of Gad according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_25::
    .string "And their coast was Jazer, and all\n"
    .string "the cities of Gilead, and half the\l"
    .string "land of the children of Ammon, unto\l"
    .string "Aroer that is before Rabbah;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_26::
    .string "And from Heshbon unto Ramathmizpeh,\n"
    .string "and Betonim; and from Mahanaim unto\l"
    .string "the border of Debir;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_27::
    .string "And in the valley, Betharam, and\n"
    .string "Bethnimrah, and Succoth, and Zaphon,\l"
    .string "the rest of the kingdom of Sihon king\l"
    .string "of Heshbon, Jordan and his border,\l"
    .string "even unto the edge of the sea of\l"
    .string "Chinnereth on the other side Jordan\l"
    .string "eastward$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_28::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the\n"
    .string "children of Gad after their\l"
    .string "families, the cities, and their\l"
    .string "villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_29::
    .string "And Moses gave inheritance unto the\n"
    .string "half tribe of Manasseh: and this was\l"
    .string "the possession of the half tribe of\l"
    .string "the children of Manasseh by their\l"
    .string "families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_30::
    .string "And their coast was from Mahanaim,\n"
    .string "all Bashan, all the kingdom of Og\l"
    .string "king of Bashan, and all the towns of\l"
    .string "Jair, which are in Bashan, threescore\l"
    .string "cities:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_31::
    .string "And half Gilead, and Ashtaroth,\n"
    .string "and Edrei, cities of the kingdom of\l"
    .string "Og in Bashan, were pertaining unto\l"
    .string "the children of Machir the son of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, even to the one half of the\l"
    .string "children of Machir by their families$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_32::
    .string "These are the countries which Moses\n"
    .string "did distribute for inheritance in\l"
    .string "the plains of Moab, on the other\l"
    .string "side Jordan, by Jericho, eastward.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_13_33::
    .string "But unto the tribe of Levi Moses\n"
    .string "gave not any inheritance: the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel was their inheritance,\l"
    .string "as he said unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_1::
    .string "And these are the countries which\n"
    .string "the children of Israel inherited in\l"
    .string "the land of Canaan, which Eleazar\l"
    .string "the priest, and Joshua the son of\l"
    .string "Nun, and the heads of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the tribes of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, distributed for inheritance\l"
    .string "to them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_2::
    .string "By lot was their inheritance, as\n"
    .string "the LORD commanded by the hand of\l"
    .string "Moses, for the nine tribes, and for\l"
    .string "the half tribe.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_3::
    .string "For Moses had given the inheritance\n"
    .string "of two tribes and an half tribe on\l"
    .string "the other side Jordan: but unto the\l"
    .string "Levites he gave none inheritance\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_4::
    .string "For the children of Joseph were\n"
    .string "two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim:\l"
    .string "therefore they gave no part unto the\l"
    .string "Levites in the land, save cities to\l"
    .string "dwell in, with their suburbs for\l"
    .string "their cattle and for their substance.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_5::
    .string "As the LORD commanded Moses, so the\n"
    .string "children of Israel did, and they\l"
    .string "divided the land.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_6::
    .string "Then the children of Judah came\n"
    .string "unto Joshua in Gilgal: and Caleb\l"
    .string "the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite\l"
    .string "said unto him, Thou knowest the thing\l"
    .string "that the LORD said unto Moses the man\l"
    .string "of God concerning me and thee in\l"
    .string "Kadeshbarnea.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_7::
    .string "Forty years old was I when Moses\n"
    .string "the servant of the LORD sent me from\l"
    .string "Kadeshbarnea to espy out the land;\l"
    .string "and I brought him word again as it\l"
    .string "was in mine heart.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_8::
    .string "Nevertheless my brethren that went\n"
    .string "up with me made the heart of the\l"
    .string "people melt: but I wholly\l"
    .string "followed the LORD my God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_9::
    .string "And Moses sware on that day, saying,\n"
    .string "Surely the land whereon thy feet\l"
    .string "have trodden shall be thine\l"
    .string "inheritance, and thy children’s for\l"
    .string "ever, because thou hast wholly\l"
    .string "followed the LORD my God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_10::
    .string "And now, behold, the LORD hath kept\n"
    .string "me alive, as he said, these forty and\l"
    .string "five years, even since the LORD\l"
    .string "spake this word unto Moses, while\l"
    .string "the children of Israel wandered in\l"
    .string "the wilderness: and now, lo, I am\l"
    .string "this day fourscore and five years\l"
    .string "old.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_11::
    .string "As yet I am as strong this day as I\n"
    .string "was in the day that Moses sent me: as\l"
    .string "my strength was then, even so is my\l"
    .string "strength now, for war, both to go out,\l"
    .string "and to come in.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_12::
    .string "Now therefore give me this mountain,\n"
    .string "whereof the LORD spake in that day;\l"
    .string "for thou heardest in that day how the\l"
    .string "Anakims were there, and that the\l"
    .string "cities were great and fenced: if so\l"
    .string "be the LORD will be with me, then I\l"
    .string "shall be able to drive them out, as\l"
    .string "the LORD said.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_13::
    .string "And Joshua blessed him, and gave\n"
    .string "unto Caleb the son of Jephunneh\l"
    .string "Hebron for an inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_14::
    .string "Hebron therefore became the\n"
    .string "inheritance of Caleb the son of\l"
    .string "Jephunneh the Kenezite unto this\l"
    .string "day, because that he wholly\l"
    .string "followed the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_14_15::
    .string "And the name of Hebron before was\n"
    .string "Kirjatharba; which Arba was a great\l"
    .string "man among the Anakims. And the land\l"
    .string "had rest from war.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_1::
    .string "This then was the lot of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Judah by their\l"
    .string "families; even to the border of Edom\l"
    .string "the wilderness of Zin southward was\l"
    .string "the uttermost part of the south\l"
    .string "coast.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_2::
    .string "And their south border was from the\n"
    .string "shore of the salt sea, from the bay\l"
    .string "that looketh southward:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_3::
    .string "And it went out to the south side to\n"
    .string "Maalehacrabbim, and passed along\l"
    .string "to Zin, and ascended up on the south\l"
    .string "side unto Kadeshbarnea, and passed\l"
    .string "along to Hezron, and went up to\l"
    .string "Adar, and fetched a compass to\l"
    .string "Karkaa:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_4::
    .string "From thence it passed toward Azmon,\n"
    .string "and went out unto the river of Egypt;\l"
    .string "and the goings out of that coast were\l"
    .string "at the sea: this shall be your south\l"
    .string "coast$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_5::
    .string "And the east border was the salt\n"
    .string "sea, even unto the end of Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_6::
    .string "And the border went up to\n"
    .string "Bethhogla, and passed along by the\l"
    .string "north of Betharabah; and the border\l"
    .string "went up to the stone of Bohan the son\l"
    .string "of Reuben:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_7::
    .string "And the border went up toward Debir\n"
    .string "from the valley of Achor, and so\l"
    .string "northward, looking toward Gilgal,\l"
    .string "that is before the going up to\l"
    .string "Adummim, which is on the south side\l"
    .string "of the river: and the border passed\l"
    .string "toward the waters of Enshemesh, and\l"
    .string "the goings out thereof were at\l"
    .string "Enrogel:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_8::
    .string "And the border went up by the\n"
    .string "valley of the son of Hinnom unto the\l"
    .string "south side of the Jebusite; the same\l"
    .string "is Jerusalem: and the border went up\l"
    .string "to the top of the mountain that\l"
    .string "lieth before the valley of Hinnom\l"
    .string "westward, which is at the end of the\l"
    .string "valley of the giants northward:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_9::
    .string "And the border was drawn from the\n"
    .string "top of the hill unto the fountain\l"
    .string "of the water of Nephtoah, and went\l"
    .string "out to the cities of mount Ephron;\l"
    .string "and the border was drawn to Baalah,\l"
    .string "which is Kirjathjearim:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_10::
    .string "And the border compassed from\n"
    .string "Baalah westward unto mount Seir, and\l"
    .string "passed along unto the side of mount\l"
    .string "Jearim, which is Chesalon, on the\l"
    .string "north side, and went down to\l"
    .string "Bethshemesh, and passed on to\l"
    .string "Timnah:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_11::
    .string "And the border went out unto the\n"
    .string "side of Ekron northward: and the\l"
    .string "border was drawn to Shicron, and\l"
    .string "passed along to mount Baalah, and\l"
    .string "went out unto Jabneel; and the\l"
    .string "goings out of the border were at the\l"
    .string "sea$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_12::
    .string "And the west border was to the great\n"
    .string "sea, and the coast thereof. This is\l"
    .string "the coast of the children of Judah\l"
    .string "round about according to their\l"
    .string "families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_13::
    .string "And unto Caleb the son of\n"
    .string "Jephunneh he gave a part among the\l"
    .string "children of Judah, according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD to Joshua,\l"
    .string "even the city of Arba the father of\l"
    .string "Anak, which city is Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_14::
    .string "And Caleb drove thence the three\n"
    .string "sons of Anak, Sheshai, and Ahiman,\l"
    .string "and Talmai, the children of Anak.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_15::
    .string "And he went up thence to the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Debir: and the name of\l"
    .string "Debir before was Kirjathsepher.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_16::
    .string "And Caleb said, He that smiteth\n"
    .string "Kirjathsepher, and taketh it, to him\l"
    .string "will I give Achsah my daughter to\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_17::
    .string "And Othniel the son of Kenaz, the\n"
    .string "brother of Caleb, took it: and he\l"
    .string "gave him Achsah his daughter to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, as she came\n"
    .string "unto him, that she moved him to ask of\l"
    .string "her father a field: and she lighted\l"
    .string "off her ass; and Caleb said unto her,\l"
    .string "What wouldest thou?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_19::
    .string "Who answered, Give me a blessing;\n"
    .string "for thou hast given me a south land;\l"
    .string "give me also springs of water. And\l"
    .string "he gave her the upper springs, and\l"
    .string "the nether springs$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_20::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Judah according\l"
    .string "to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_21::
    .string "And the uttermost cities of the\n"
    .string "tribe of the children of Judah\l"
    .string "toward the coast of Edom southward\l"
    .string "were Kabzeel, and Eder, and Jagur,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_22::
    .string "And Kinah, and Dimonah, and Adadah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_23::
    .string "And Kedesh, and Hazor, and Ithnan,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_24::
    .string "Ziph, and Telem, and Bealoth,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_25::
    .string "And Hazor, Hadattah, and Kerioth,\n"
    .string "and Hezron, which is Hazor,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_26::
    .string "Amam, and Shema, and Moladah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_27::
    .string "And Hazargaddah, and Heshmon, and\n"
    .string "Bethpalet,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_28::
    .string "And Hazarshual, and Beersheba, and\n"
    .string "Bizjothjah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_29::
    .string "Baalah, and Iim, and Azem,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_30::
    .string "And Eltolad, and Chesil, and\n"
    .string "Hormah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_31::
    .string "And Ziklag, and Madmannah, and\n"
    .string "Sansannah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_32::
    .string "And Lebaoth, and Shilhim, and Ain,\n"
    .string "and Rimmon: all the cities are\l"
    .string "twenty and nine, with their\l"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_33::
    .string "And in the valley, Eshtaol, and\n"
    .string "Zoreah, and Ashnah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_34::
    .string "And Zanoah, and Engannim, Tappuah,\n"
    .string "and Enam,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_35::
    .string "Jarmuth, and Adullam, Socoh, and\n"
    .string "Azekah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_36::
    .string "And Sharaim, and Adithaim, and\n"
    .string "Gederah, and Gederothaim; fourteen\l"
    .string "cities with their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_37::
    .string "Zenan, and Hadashah, and Migdalgad,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_38::
    .string "And Dilean, and Mizpeh, and\n"
    .string "Joktheel,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_39::
    .string "Lachish, and Bozkath, and Eglon,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_40::
    .string "And Cabbon, and Lahmam, and\n"
    .string "Kithlish,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_41::
    .string "And Gederoth, Bethdagon, and Naamah,\n"
    .string "and Makkedah; sixteen cities with\l"
    .string "their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_42::
    .string "Libnah, and Ether, and Ashan,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_43::
    .string "And Jiphtah, and Ashnah, and Nezib,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_44::
    .string "And Keilah, and Achzib, and\n"
    .string "Mareshah; nine cities with their\l"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_45::
    .string "Ekron, with her towns and her\n"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_46::
    .string "From Ekron even unto the sea, all\n"
    .string "that lay near Ashdod, with their\l"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_47::
    .string "Ashdod with her towns and her\n"
    .string "villages, Gaza with her towns and\l"
    .string "her villages, unto the river of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and the great sea, and the\l"
    .string "border thereof:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_48::
    .string "And in the mountains, Shamir, and\n"
    .string "Jattir, and Socoh,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_49::
    .string "And Dannah, and Kirjathsannah,\n"
    .string "which is Debir,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_50::
    .string "And Anab, and Eshtemoh, and Anim,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_51::
    .string "And Goshen, and Holon, and Giloh;\n"
    .string "eleven cities with their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_52::
    .string "Arab, and Dumah, and Eshean,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_53::
    .string "And Janum, and Bethtappuah, and\n"
    .string "Aphekah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_54::
    .string "And Humtah, and Kirjatharba, which\n"
    .string "is Hebron, and Zior; nine cities with\l"
    .string "their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_55::
    .string "Maon, Carmel, and Ziph, and Juttah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_56::
    .string "And Jezreel, and Jokdeam, and\n"
    .string "Zanoah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_57::
    .string "Cain, Gibeah, and Timnah; ten cities\n"
    .string "with their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_58::
    .string "Halhul, Bethzur, and Gedor,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_59::
    .string "And Maarath, and Bethanoth, and\n"
    .string "Eltekon; six cities with their\l"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_60::
    .string "Kirjathbaal, which is\n"
    .string "Kirjathjearim, and Rabbah; two\l"
    .string "cities with their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_61::
    .string "In the wilderness, Betharabah,\n"
    .string "Middin, and Secacah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_62::
    .string "And Nibshan, and the city of Salt,\n"
    .string "and Engedi; six cities with their\l"
    .string "villages$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_15_63::
    .string "As for the Jebusites the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, the\l"
    .string "children of Judah could not drive\l"
    .string "them out; but the Jebusites dwell\l"
    .string "with the children of Judah at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_1::
    .string "And the lot of the children of\n"
    .string "Joseph fell from Jordan by Jericho,\l"
    .string "unto the water of Jericho on the\l"
    .string "east, to the wilderness that goeth\l"
    .string "up from Jericho throughout mount\l"
    .string "Bethel,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_2::
    .string "And goeth out from Bethel to Luz,\n"
    .string "and passeth along unto the borders\l"
    .string "of Archi to Ataroth,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_3::
    .string "And goeth down westward to the coast\n"
    .string "of Japhleti, unto the coast of\l"
    .string "Bethhoron the nether, and to Gezer;\l"
    .string "and the goings out thereof are at the\l"
    .string "sea$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_4::
    .string "So the children of Joseph,\n"
    .string "Manasseh and Ephraim, took their\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_5::
    .string "And the border of the children of\n"
    .string "Ephraim according to their families\l"
    .string "was thus: even the border of their\l"
    .string "inheritance on the east side was\l"
    .string "Atarothaddar, unto Bethhoron the\l"
    .string "upper;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_6::
    .string "And the border went out toward the\n"
    .string "sea to Michmethah on the north side;\l"
    .string "and the border went about eastward\l"
    .string "unto Taanathshiloh, and passed by\l"
    .string "it on the east to Janohah;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_7::
    .string "And it went down from Janohah to\n"
    .string "Ataroth, and to Naarath, and came to\l"
    .string "Jericho, and went out at Jordan$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_8::
    .string "The border went out from Tappuah\n"
    .string "westward unto the river Kanah; and\l"
    .string "the goings out thereof were at the sea\l"
    .string " This is the inheritance of the\l"
    .string "tribe of the children of Ephraim by\l"
    .string "their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_9::
    .string "And the separate cities for the\n"
    .string "children of Ephraim were among the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the children of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, all the cities with their\l"
    .string "villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_16_10::
    .string "And they drave not out the\n"
    .string "Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer: but\l"
    .string "the Canaanites dwell among the\l"
    .string "Ephraimites unto this day, and serve\l"
    .string "under tribute.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_1::
    .string "There was also a lot for the tribe\n"
    .string "of Manasseh; for he was the firstborn\l"
    .string "of Joseph; to wit, for Machir the\l"
    .string "firstborn of Manasseh, the father of\l"
    .string "Gilead: because he was a man of war,\l"
    .string "therefore he had Gilead and Bashan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_2::
    .string "There was also a lot for the rest\n"
    .string "of the children of Manasseh by their\l"
    .string "families; for the children of\l"
    .string "Abiezer, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Helek, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Asriel, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Shechem, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Hepher, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Shemida: these were the male\l"
    .string "children of Manasseh the son of\l"
    .string "Joseph by their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_3::
    .string "But Zelophehad, the son of Hepher,\n"
    .string "the son of Gilead, the son of Machir,\l"
    .string "the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but\l"
    .string "daughters: and these are the names of\l"
    .string "his daughters, Mahlah, and Noah,\l"
    .string "Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_4::
    .string "And they came near before Eleazar\n"
    .string "the priest, and before Joshua the\l"
    .string "son of Nun, and before the princes,\l"
    .string "saying, The LORD commanded Moses to\l"
    .string "give us an inheritance among our\l"
    .string "brethren. Therefore according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD he gave them\l"
    .string "an inheritance among the brethren of\l"
    .string "their father.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_5::
    .string "And there fell ten portions to\n"
    .string "Manasseh, beside the land of Gilead\l"
    .string "and Bashan, which were on the other\l"
    .string "side Jordan;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_6::
    .string "Because the daughters of Manasseh\n"
    .string "had an inheritance among his sons:\l"
    .string "and the rest of Manasseh’s sons had\l"
    .string "the land of Gilead$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_7::
    .string "And the coast of Manasseh was from\n"
    .string "Asher to Michmethah, that lieth\l"
    .string "before Shechem; and the border went\l"
    .string "along on the right hand unto the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Entappuah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_8::
    .string "Now Manasseh had the land of\n"
    .string "Tappuah: but Tappuah on the border\l"
    .string "of Manasseh belonged to the\l"
    .string "children of Ephraim;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_9::
    .string "And the coast descended unto the\n"
    .string "river Kanah, southward of the river:\l"
    .string "these cities of Ephraim are among\l"
    .string "the cities of Manasseh: the coast of\l"
    .string "Manasseh also was on the north side\l"
    .string "of the river, and the outgoings of it\l"
    .string "were at the sea:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_10::
    .string "Southward it was Ephraim’s, and\n"
    .string "northward it was Manasseh’s, and the\l"
    .string "sea is his border; and they met\l"
    .string "together in Asher on the north, and\l"
    .string "in Issachar on the east$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_11::
    .string "And Manasseh had in Issachar and in\n"
    .string "Asher Bethshean and her towns, and\l"
    .string "Ibleam and her towns, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Dor and her towns, and\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Endor and her\l"
    .string "towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach\l"
    .string "and her towns, and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Megiddo and her towns, even three\l"
    .string "countries.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_12::
    .string "Yet the children of Manasseh could\n"
    .string "not drive out the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "those cities; but the Canaanites\l"
    .string "would dwell in that land.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_13::
    .string "Yet it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "children of Israel were waxen\l"
    .string "strong, that they put the Canaanites\l"
    .string "to tribute, but did not utterly\l"
    .string "drive them out.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_14::
    .string "And the children of Joseph spake\n"
    .string "unto Joshua, saying, Why hast thou\l"
    .string "given me but one lot and one portion\l"
    .string "to inherit, seeing I am a great\l"
    .string "people, forasmuch as the LORD hath\l"
    .string "blessed me hitherto?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_15::
    .string "And Joshua answered them, If thou be\n"
    .string "a great people, then get thee up to\l"
    .string "the wood country, and cut down for\l"
    .string "thyself there in the land of the\l"
    .string "Perizzites and of the giants, if\l"
    .string "mount Ephraim be too narrow for thee$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_16::
    .string "And the children of Joseph said,\n"
    .string "The hill is not enough for us: and\l"
    .string "all the Canaanites that dwell in\l"
    .string "the land of the valley have\l"
    .string "chariots of iron, both they who are\l"
    .string "of Bethshean and her towns, and they\l"
    .string "who are of the valley of Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_17::
    .string "And Joshua spake unto the house of\n"
    .string "Joseph, even to Ephraim and to\l"
    .string "Manasseh, saying, Thou art a great\l"
    .string "people, and hast great power: thou\l"
    .string "shalt not have one lot only:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_17_18::
    .string "But the mountain shall be thine;\n"
    .string "for it is a wood, and thou shalt cut\l"
    .string "it down: and the outgoings of it\l"
    .string "shall be thine: for thou shalt\l"
    .string "drive out the Canaanites, though they\l"
    .string "have iron chariots, and though they\l"
    .string "be strong$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_1::
    .string "And the whole congregation of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel assembled\l"
    .string "together at Shiloh, and set up the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation there\l"
    .string " And the land was subdued before\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_2::
    .string "And there remained among the\n"
    .string "children of Israel seven tribes,\l"
    .string "which had not yet received their\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_3::
    .string "And Joshua said unto the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, How long are ye slack to\l"
    .string "go to possess the land, which the\l"
    .string "LORD God of your fathers hath given\l"
    .string "you?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_4::
    .string "Give out from among you three men\n"
    .string "for each tribe: and I will send\l"
    .string "them, and they shall rise, and go\l"
    .string "through the land, and describe it\l"
    .string "according to the inheritance of them;\l"
    .string "and they shall come again to me$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_5::
    .string "And they shall divide it into\n"
    .string "seven parts: Judah shall abide in\l"
    .string "their coast on the south, and the\l"
    .string "house of Joseph shall abide in\l"
    .string "their coasts on the north.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_6::
    .string "Ye shall therefore describe the\n"
    .string "land into seven parts, and bring the\l"
    .string "description hither to me, that I may\l"
    .string "cast lots for you here before the\l"
    .string "LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_7::
    .string "But the Levites have no part among\n"
    .string "you; for the priesthood of the LORD\l"
    .string "is their inheritance: and Gad, and\l"
    .string "Reuben, and half the tribe of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, have received their\l"
    .string "inheritance beyond Jordan on the\l"
    .string "east, which Moses the servant of the\l"
    .string "LORD gave them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_8::
    .string "And the men arose, and went away:\n"
    .string "and Joshua charged them that went to\l"
    .string "describe the land, saying, Go and\l"
    .string "walk through the land, and describe\l"
    .string "it, and come again to me, that I may\l"
    .string "here cast lots for you before the\l"
    .string "LORD in Shiloh.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_9::
    .string "And the men went and passed through\n"
    .string "the land, and described it by cities\l"
    .string "into seven parts in a book, and came\l"
    .string "again to Joshua to the host at\l"
    .string "Shiloh.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_10::
    .string "And Joshua cast lots for them in\n"
    .string "Shiloh before the LORD: and there\l"
    .string "Joshua divided the land unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel according to\l"
    .string "their divisions.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_11::
    .string "And the lot of the tribe of the\n"
    .string "children of Benjamin came up\l"
    .string "according to their families: and the\l"
    .string "coast of their lot came forth\l"
    .string "between the children of Judah and\l"
    .string "the children of Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_12::
    .string "And their border on the north side\n"
    .string "was from Jordan; and the border went\l"
    .string "up to the side of Jericho on the\l"
    .string "north side, and went up through the\l"
    .string "mountains westward; and the goings\l"
    .string "out thereof were at the wilderness\l"
    .string "of Bethaven.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_13::
    .string "And the border went over from thence\n"
    .string "toward Luz, to the side of Luz, which\l"
    .string "is Bethel, southward; and the border\l"
    .string "descended to Atarothadar, near the\l"
    .string "hill that lieth on the south side\l"
    .string "of the nether Bethhoron.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_14::
    .string "And the border was drawn thence, and\n"
    .string "compassed the corner of the sea\l"
    .string "southward, from the hill that lieth\l"
    .string "before Bethhoron southward; and the\l"
    .string "goings out thereof were at\l"
    .string "Kirjathbaal, which is\l"
    .string "Kirjathjearim, a city of the\l"
    .string "children of Judah: this was the west\l"
    .string "quarter.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_15::
    .string "And the south quarter was from the\n"
    .string "end of Kirjathjearim, and the border\l"
    .string "went out on the west, and went out to\l"
    .string "the well of waters of Nephtoah:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_16::
    .string "And the border came down to the end\n"
    .string "of the mountain that lieth before\l"
    .string "the valley of the son of Hinnom, and\l"
    .string "which is in the valley of the giants\l"
    .string "on the north, and descended to the\l"
    .string "valley of Hinnom, to the side of\l"
    .string "Jebusi on the south, and descended to\l"
    .string "Enrogel,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_17::
    .string "And was drawn from the north, and\n"
    .string "went forth to Enshemesh, and went\l"
    .string "forth toward Geliloth, which is\l"
    .string "over against the going up of\l"
    .string "Adummim, and descended to the stone\l"
    .string "of Bohan the son of Reuben,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_18::
    .string "And passed along toward the side\n"
    .string "over against Arabah northward, and\l"
    .string "went down unto Arabah:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_19::
    .string "And the border passed along to the\n"
    .string "side of Bethhoglah northward: and\l"
    .string "the outgoings of the border were at\l"
    .string "the north bay of the salt sea at the\l"
    .string "south end of Jordan: this was the\l"
    .string "south coast$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_20::
    .string "And Jordan was the border of it on\n"
    .string "the east side. This was the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, by the coasts thereof round\l"
    .string "about, according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_21::
    .string "Now the cities of the tribe of the\n"
    .string "children of Benjamin according to\l"
    .string "their families were Jericho, and\l"
    .string "Bethhoglah, and the valley of\l"
    .string "Keziz,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_22::
    .string "And Betharabah, and Zemaraim, and\n"
    .string "Bethel,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_23::
    .string "And Avim, and Pharah, and Ophrah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_24::
    .string "And Chepharhaammonai, and Ophni,\n"
    .string "and Gaba; twelve cities with their\l"
    .string "villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_25::
    .string "Gibeon, and Ramah, and Beeroth,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_26::
    .string "And Mizpeh, and Chephirah, and\n"
    .string "Mozah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_27::
    .string "And Rekem, and Irpeel, and\n"
    .string "Taralah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_18_28::
    .string "And Zelah, Eleph, and Jebusi,\n"
    .string "which is Jerusalem, Gibeath, and\l"
    .string "Kirjath; fourteen cities with their\l"
    .string "villages. This is the inheritance\l"
    .string "of the children of Benjamin\l"
    .string "according to their families$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_1::
    .string "And the second lot came forth to\n"
    .string "Simeon, even for the tribe of the\l"
    .string "children of Simeon according to\l"
    .string "their families: and their\l"
    .string "inheritance was within the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the children of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_2::
    .string "And they had in their inheritance\n"
    .string "Beersheba, and Sheba, and Moladah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_3::
    .string "And Hazarshual, and Balah, and\n"
    .string "Azem,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_4::
    .string "And Eltolad, and Bethul, and\n"
    .string "Hormah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_5::
    .string "And Ziklag, and Bethmarcaboth, and\n"
    .string "Hazarsusah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_6::
    .string "And Bethlebaoth, and Sharuhen;\n"
    .string "thirteen cities and their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_7::
    .string "Ain, Remmon, and Ether, and Ashan;\n"
    .string "four cities and their villages:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_8::
    .string "And all the villages that were\n"
    .string "round about these cities to\l"
    .string "Baalathbeer, Ramath of the south.\l"
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\l"
    .string "of the children of Simeon according\l"
    .string "to their families$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_9::
    .string "Out of the portion of the children\n"
    .string "of Judah was the inheritance of the\l"
    .string "children of Simeon: for the part of\l"
    .string "the children of Judah was too much\l"
    .string "for them: therefore the children of\l"
    .string "Simeon had their inheritance within\l"
    .string "the inheritance of them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_10::
    .string "And the third lot came up for the\n"
    .string "children of Zebulun according to\l"
    .string "their families: and the border of\l"
    .string "their inheritance was unto Sarid:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_11::
    .string "And their border went up toward the\n"
    .string "sea, and Maralah, and reached to\l"
    .string "Dabbasheth, and reached to the river\l"
    .string "that is before Jokneam;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_12::
    .string "And turned from Sarid eastward\n"
    .string "toward the sunrising unto the border\l"
    .string "of Chislothtabor, and then goeth out\l"
    .string "to Daberath, and goeth up to Japhia,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_13::
    .string "And from thence passeth on along\n"
    .string "on the east to Gittahhepher, to\l"
    .string "Ittahkazin, and goeth out to\l"
    .string "Remmonmethoar to Neah;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_14::
    .string "And the border compasseth it on the\n"
    .string "north side to Hannathon: and the\l"
    .string "outgoings thereof are in the valley\l"
    .string "of Jiphthahel:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_15::
    .string "And Kattath, and Nahallal, and\n"
    .string "Shimron, and Idalah, and Bethlehem:\l"
    .string "twelve cities with their villages$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_16::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the\n"
    .string "children of Zebulun according to\l"
    .string "their families, these cities with\l"
    .string "their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_17::
    .string "And the fourth lot came out to\n"
    .string "Issachar, for the children of\l"
    .string "Issachar according to their\l"
    .string "families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_18::
    .string "And their border was toward\n"
    .string "Jezreel, and Chesulloth, and\l"
    .string "Shunem,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_19::
    .string "And Haphraim, and Shihon, and\n"
    .string "Anaharath,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_20::
    .string "And Rabbith, and Kishion, and Abez,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_21::
    .string "And Remeth, and Engannim, and\n"
    .string "Enhaddah, and Bethpazzez;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_22::
    .string "And the coast reacheth to Tabor, and\n"
    .string "Shahazimah, and Bethshemesh; and the\l"
    .string "outgoings of their border were at\l"
    .string "Jordan: sixteen cities with their\l"
    .string "villages$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_23::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Issachar\l"
    .string "according to their families, the\l"
    .string "cities and their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_24::
    .string "And the fifth lot came out for the\n"
    .string "tribe of the children of Asher\l"
    .string "according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_25::
    .string "And their border was Helkath, and\n"
    .string "Hali, and Beten, and Achshaph,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_26::
    .string "And Alammelech, and Amad, and\n"
    .string "Misheal; and reacheth to Carmel\l"
    .string "westward, and to Shihorlibnath;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_27::
    .string "And turneth toward the sunrising to\n"
    .string "Bethdagon, and reacheth to Zebulun,\l"
    .string "and to the valley of Jiphthahel\l"
    .string "toward the north side of Bethemek,\l"
    .string "and Neiel, and goeth out to Cabul on\l"
    .string "the left hand,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_28::
    .string "And Hebron, and Rehob, and Hammon,\n"
    .string "and Kanah, even unto great Zidon;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_29::
    .string "And then the coast turneth to Ramah,\n"
    .string "and to the strong city Tyre; and the\l"
    .string "coast turneth to Hosah; and the\l"
    .string "outgoings thereof are at the sea from\l"
    .string "the coast to Achzib:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_30::
    .string "Ummah also, and Aphek, and Rehob:\n"
    .string "twenty and two cities with their\l"
    .string "villages$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_31::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Asher according\l"
    .string "to their families, these cities with\l"
    .string "their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_32::
    .string "The sixth lot came out to the\n"
    .string "children of Naphtali, even for the\l"
    .string "children of Naphtali according to\l"
    .string "their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_33::
    .string "And their coast was from Heleph,\n"
    .string "from Allon to Zaanannim, and Adami,\l"
    .string "Nekeb, and Jabneel, unto Lakum; and\l"
    .string "the outgoings thereof were at Jordan:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_34::
    .string "And then the coast turneth westward\n"
    .string "to Aznothtabor, and goeth out from\l"
    .string "thence to Hukkok, and reacheth to\l"
    .string "Zebulun on the south side, and\l"
    .string "reacheth to Asher on the west side,\l"
    .string "and to Judah upon Jordan toward the\l"
    .string "sunrising$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_35::
    .string "And the fenced cities are Ziddim,\n"
    .string "Zer, and Hammath, Rakkath, and\l"
    .string "Chinnereth,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_36::
    .string "And Adamah, and Ramah, and Hazor,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_37::
    .string "And Kedesh, and Edrei, and Enhazor,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_38::
    .string "And Iron, and Migdalel, Horem, and\n"
    .string "Bethanath, and Bethshemesh; nineteen\l"
    .string "cities with their villages$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_39::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Naphtali\l"
    .string "according to their families, the\l"
    .string "cities and their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_40::
    .string "And the seventh lot came out for\n"
    .string "the tribe of the children of Dan\l"
    .string "according to their families.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_41::
    .string "And the coast of their inheritance\n"
    .string "was Zorah, and Eshtaol, and\l"
    .string "Irshemesh,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_42::
    .string "And Shaalabbin, and Ajalon, and\n"
    .string "Jethlah,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_43::
    .string "And Elon, and Thimnathah, and\n"
    .string "Ekron,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_44::
    .string "And Eltekeh, and Gibbethon, and\n"
    .string "Baalath,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_45::
    .string "And Jehud, and Beneberak, and\n"
    .string "Gathrimmon,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_46::
    .string "And Mejarkon, and Rakkon, with the\n"
    .string "border before Japho$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_47::
    .string "And the coast of the children of\n"
    .string "Dan went out too little for them:\l"
    .string "therefore the children of Dan went\l"
    .string "up to fight against Leshem, and took\l"
    .string "it, and smote it with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword, and possessed it, and dwelt\l"
    .string "therein, and called Leshem, Dan,\l"
    .string "after the name of Dan their father.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_48::
    .string "This is the inheritance of the tribe\n"
    .string "of the children of Dan according to\l"
    .string "their families, these cities with\l"
    .string "their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_49::
    .string "When they had made an end of\n"
    .string "dividing the land for inheritance by\l"
    .string "their coasts, the children of\l"
    .string "Israel gave an inheritance to Joshua\l"
    .string "the son of Nun among them:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_50::
    .string "According to the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "they gave him the city which he\l"
    .string "asked, even Timnathserah in mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim: and he built the city, and\l"
    .string "dwelt therein$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_19_51::
    .string "These are the inheritances, which\n"
    .string "Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the\l"
    .string "son of Nun, and the heads of the\l"
    .string "fathers of the tribes of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, divided for an\l"
    .string "inheritance by lot in Shiloh before\l"
    .string "the LORD, at the door of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation. So\l"
    .string "they made an end of dividing the\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_1::
    .string "The LORD also spake unto Joshua,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_2::
    .string "Speak to the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "saying, Appoint out for you cities\l"
    .string "of refuge, whereof I spake unto you\l"
    .string "by the hand of Moses:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_3::
    .string "That the slayer that killeth any\n"
    .string "person unawares and unwittingly may\l"
    .string "flee thither: and they shall be\l"
    .string "your refuge from the avenger of blood$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_4::
    .string "And when he that doth flee unto one\n"
    .string "of those cities shall stand at the\l"
    .string "entering of the gate of the city, and\l"
    .string "shall declare his cause in the ears\l"
    .string "of the elders of that city, they\l"
    .string "shall take him into the city unto\l"
    .string "them, and give him a place, that he\l"
    .string "may dwell among them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_5::
    .string "And if the avenger of blood pursue\n"
    .string "after him, then they shall not\l"
    .string "deliver the slayer up into his\l"
    .string "hand; because he smote his neighbour\l"
    .string "unwittingly, and hated him not\l"
    .string "beforetime.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_6::
    .string "And he shall dwell in that city,\n"
    .string "until he stand before the\l"
    .string "congregation for judgment, and until\l"
    .string "the death of the high priest that\l"
    .string "shall be in those days: then shall\l"
    .string "the slayer return, and come unto his\l"
    .string "own city, and unto his own house,\l"
    .string "unto the city from whence he fled.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_7::
    .string "And they appointed Kedesh in\n"
    .string "Galilee in mount Naphtali, and\l"
    .string "Shechem in mount Ephraim, and\l"
    .string "Kirjatharba, which is Hebron, in the\l"
    .string "mountain of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_8::
    .string "And on the other side Jordan by\n"
    .string "Jericho eastward, they assigned\l"
    .string "Bezer in the wilderness upon the\l"
    .string "plain out of the tribe of Reuben, and\l"
    .string "Ramoth in Gilead out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Gad, and Golan in Bashan out of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_20_9::
    .string "These were the cities appointed\n"
    .string "for all the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "and for the stranger that sojourneth\l"
    .string "among them, that whosoever killeth\l"
    .string "any person at unawares might flee\l"
    .string "thither, and not die by the hand of\l"
    .string "the avenger of blood, until he stood\l"
    .string "before the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_1::
    .string "Then came near the heads of the\n"
    .string "fathers of the Levites unto Eleazar\l"
    .string "the priest, and unto Joshua the son\l"
    .string "of Nun, and unto the heads of the\l"
    .string "fathers of the tribes of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_2::
    .string "And they spake unto them at Shiloh\n"
    .string "in the land of Canaan, saying, The\l"
    .string "LORD commanded by the hand of Moses\l"
    .string "to give us cities to dwell in, with\l"
    .string "the suburbs thereof for our cattle$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_3::
    .string "And the children of Israel gave\n"
    .string "unto the Levites out of their\l"
    .string "inheritance, at the commandment of\l"
    .string "the LORD, these cities and their\l"
    .string "suburbs.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_4::
    .string "And the lot came out for the\n"
    .string "families of the Kohathites: and the\l"
    .string "children of Aaron the priest, which\l"
    .string "were of the Levites, had by lot out\l"
    .string "of the tribe of Judah, and out of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Simeon, and out of the tribe\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, thirteen cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_5::
    .string "And the rest of the children of\n"
    .string "Kohath had by lot out of the\l"
    .string "families of the tribe of Ephraim,\l"
    .string "and out of the tribe of Dan, and out\l"
    .string "of the half tribe of Manasseh, ten\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_6::
    .string "And the children of Gershon had by\n"
    .string "lot out of the families of the tribe\l"
    .string "of Issachar, and out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Asher, and out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Naphtali, and out of the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh in Bashan, thirteen\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_7::
    .string "The children of Merari by their\n"
    .string "families had out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Reuben, and out of the tribe of Gad,\l"
    .string "and out of the tribe of Zebulun,\l"
    .string "twelve cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_8::
    .string "And the children of Israel gave by\n"
    .string "lot unto the Levites these cities\l"
    .string "with their suburbs, as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded by the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_9::
    .string "And they gave out of the tribe of\n"
    .string "the children of Judah, and out of the\l"
    .string "tribe of the children of Simeon,\l"
    .string "these cities which are here\l"
    .string "mentioned by name.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_10::
    .string "Which the children of Aaron, being\n"
    .string "of the families of the Kohathites,\l"
    .string "who were of the children of Levi,\l"
    .string "had: for theirs was the first lot.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_11::
    .string "And they gave them the city of Arba\n"
    .string "the father of Anak, which city is\l"
    .string "Hebron, in the hill country of\l"
    .string "Judah, with the suburbs thereof round\l"
    .string "about it.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_12::
    .string "But the fields of the city, and the\n"
    .string "villages thereof, gave they to\l"
    .string "Caleb the son of Jephunneh for his\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_13::
    .string "Thus they gave to the children of\n"
    .string "Aaron the priest Hebron with her\l"
    .string "suburbs, to be a city of refuge for\l"
    .string "the slayer; and Libnah with her\l"
    .string "suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_14::
    .string "And Jattir with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Eshtemoa with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_15::
    .string "And Holon with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Debir with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_16::
    .string "And Ain with her suburbs, and Juttah\n"
    .string "with her suburbs, and Bethshemesh\l"
    .string "with her suburbs; nine cities out of\l"
    .string "those two tribes$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_17::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Benjamin,\n"
    .string "Gibeon with her suburbs, Geba with\l"
    .string "her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_18::
    .string "Anathoth with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Almon with her suburbs; four cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_19::
    .string "All the cities of the children of\n"
    .string "Aaron, the priests, were thirteen\l"
    .string "cities with their suburbs.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_20::
    .string "And the families of the children\n"
    .string "of Kohath, the Levites which remained\l"
    .string "of the children of Kohath, even they\l"
    .string "had the cities of their lot out of\l"
    .string "the tribe of Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_21::
    .string "For they gave them Shechem with her\n"
    .string "suburbs in mount Ephraim, to be a\l"
    .string "city of refuge for the slayer; and\l"
    .string "Gezer with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_22::
    .string "And Kibzaim with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Bethhoron with her suburbs; four\l"
    .string "cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_23::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Dan, Eltekeh\n"
    .string "with her suburbs, Gibbethon with her\l"
    .string "suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_24::
    .string "Aijalon with her suburbs,\n"
    .string "Gathrimmon with her suburbs; four\l"
    .string "cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_25::
    .string "And out of the half tribe of\n"
    .string "Manasseh, Tanach with her suburbs,\l"
    .string "and Gathrimmon with her suburbs; two\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_26::
    .string "All the cities were ten with their\n"
    .string "suburbs for the families of the\l"
    .string "children of Kohath that remained.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_27::
    .string "And unto the children of Gershon,\n"
    .string "of the families of the Levites, out\l"
    .string "of the other half tribe of Manasseh\l"
    .string "they gave Golan in Bashan with her\l"
    .string "suburbs, to be a city of refuge for\l"
    .string "the slayer; and Beeshterah with her\l"
    .string "suburbs; two cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_28::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Issachar,\n"
    .string "Kishon with her suburbs, Dabareh with\l"
    .string "her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_29::
    .string "Jarmuth with her suburbs, Engannim\n"
    .string "with her suburbs; four cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_30::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Asher,\n"
    .string "Mishal with her suburbs, Abdon with\l"
    .string "her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_31::
    .string "Helkath with her suburbs, and Rehob\n"
    .string "with her suburbs; four cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_32::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Naphtali,\n"
    .string "Kedesh in Galilee with her suburbs,\l"
    .string "to be a city of refuge for the\l"
    .string "slayer; and Hammothdor with her\l"
    .string "suburbs, and Kartan with her suburbs;\l"
    .string "three cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_33::
    .string "All the cities of the Gershonites\n"
    .string "according to their families were\l"
    .string "thirteen cities with their suburbs.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_34::
    .string "And unto the families of the\n"
    .string "children of Merari, the rest of the\l"
    .string "Levites, out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Zebulun, Jokneam with her suburbs,\l"
    .string "and Kartah with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_35::
    .string "Dimnah with her suburbs, Nahalal\n"
    .string "with her suburbs; four cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_36::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Reuben,\n"
    .string "Bezer with her suburbs, and Jahazah\l"
    .string "with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_37::
    .string "Kedemoth with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Mephaath with her suburbs; four\l"
    .string "cities$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_38::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Gad, Ramoth\n"
    .string "in Gilead with her suburbs, to be a\l"
    .string "city of refuge for the slayer; and\l"
    .string "Mahanaim with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_39::
    .string "Heshbon with her suburbs, Jazer with\n"
    .string "her suburbs; four cities in all$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_40::
    .string "So all the cities for the children\n"
    .string "of Merari by their families, which\l"
    .string "were remaining of the families of\l"
    .string "the Levites, were by their lot\l"
    .string "twelve cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_41::
    .string "All the cities of the Levites\n"
    .string "within the possession of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel were forty and\l"
    .string "eight cities with their suburbs.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_42::
    .string "These cities were every one with\n"
    .string "their suburbs round about them: thus\l"
    .string "were all these cities.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_43::
    .string "And the LORD gave unto Israel all\n"
    .string "the land which he sware to give unto\l"
    .string "their fathers; and they possessed\l"
    .string "it, and dwelt therein.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_44::
    .string "And the LORD gave them rest round\n"
    .string "about, according to all that he\l"
    .string "sware unto their fathers: and there\l"
    .string "stood not a man of all their enemies\l"
    .string "before them; the LORD delivered all\l"
    .string "their enemies into their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_21_45::
    .string "There failed not ought of any good\n"
    .string "thing which the LORD had spoken unto\l"
    .string "the house of Israel; all came to\l"
    .string "pass.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_1::
    .string "Then Joshua called the Reubenites,\n"
    .string "and the Gadites, and the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_2::
    .string "And said unto them, Ye have kept\n"
    .string "all that Moses the servant of the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded you, and have obeyed\l"
    .string "my voice in all that I commanded\l"
    .string "you:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_3::
    .string "Ye have not left your brethren\n"
    .string "these many days unto this day, but\l"
    .string "have kept the charge of the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD your God$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_4::
    .string "And now the LORD your God hath given\n"
    .string "rest unto your brethren, as he\l"
    .string "promised them: therefore now return\l"
    .string "ye, and get you unto your tents, and\l"
    .string "unto the land of your possession,\l"
    .string "which Moses the servant of the LORD\l"
    .string "gave you on the other side Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_5::
    .string "But take diligent heed to do the\n"
    .string "commandment and the law, which Moses\l"
    .string "the servant of the LORD charged you,\l"
    .string "to love the LORD your God, and to\l"
    .string "walk in all his ways, and to keep\l"
    .string "his commandments, and to cleave unto\l"
    .string "him, and to serve him with all your\l"
    .string "heart and with all your soul.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_6::
    .string "So Joshua blessed them, and sent\n"
    .string "them away: and they went unto their\l"
    .string "tents.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_7::
    .string "Now to the one half of the tribe of\n"
    .string "Manasseh Moses had given possession\l"
    .string "in Bashan: but unto the other half\l"
    .string "thereof gave Joshua among their\l"
    .string "brethren on this side Jordan westward\l"
    .string " And when Joshua sent them away\l"
    .string "also unto their tents, then he\l"
    .string "blessed them,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_8::
    .string "And he spake unto them, saying,\n"
    .string "Return with much riches unto your\l"
    .string "tents, and with very much cattle,\l"
    .string "with silver, and with gold, and with\l"
    .string "brass, and with iron, and with very\l"
    .string "much raiment: divide the spoil of\l"
    .string "your enemies with your brethren$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_9::
    .string "And the children of Reuben and the\n"
    .string "children of Gad and the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh returned, and departed\l"
    .string "from the children of Israel out of\l"
    .string "Shiloh, which is in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, to go unto the country of\l"
    .string "Gilead, to the land of their\l"
    .string "possession, whereof they were\l"
    .string "possessed, according to the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD by the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_10::
    .string "And when they came unto the borders\n"
    .string "of Jordan, that are in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, the children of Reuben and\l"
    .string "the children of Gad and the half\l"
    .string "tribe of Manasseh built there an\l"
    .string "altar by Jordan, a great altar to\l"
    .string "see to.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_11::
    .string "And the children of Israel heard\n"
    .string "say, Behold, the children of Reuben\l"
    .string "and the children of Gad and the half\l"
    .string "tribe of Manasseh have built an\l"
    .string "altar over against the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, in the borders of Jordan, at\l"
    .string "the passage of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_12::
    .string "And when the children of Israel\n"
    .string "heard of it, the whole congregation\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together at Shiloh, to\l"
    .string "go up to war against them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_13::
    .string "And the children of Israel sent\n"
    .string "unto the children of Reuben, and to\l"
    .string "the children of Gad, and to the half\l"
    .string "tribe of Manasseh, into the land of\l"
    .string "Gilead, Phinehas the son of Eleazar\l"
    .string "the priest,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_14::
    .string "And with him ten princes, of each\n"
    .string "chief house a prince throughout\l"
    .string "all the tribes of Israel; and each\l"
    .string "one was an head of the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers among the thousands of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_15::
    .string "And they came unto the children of\n"
    .string "Reuben, and to the children of Gad,\l"
    .string "and to the half tribe of Manasseh,\l"
    .string "unto the land of Gilead, and they\l"
    .string "spake with them, saying,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_16::
    .string "Thus saith the whole congregation\n"
    .string "of the LORD, What trespass is this\l"
    .string "that ye have committed against the\l"
    .string "God of Israel, to turn away this day\l"
    .string "from following the LORD, in that ye\l"
    .string "have builded you an altar, that ye\l"
    .string "might rebel this day against the\l"
    .string "LORD?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_17::
    .string "Is the iniquity of Peor too little\n"
    .string "for us, from which we are not\l"
    .string "cleansed until this day, although\l"
    .string "there was a plague in the\l"
    .string "congregation of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_18::
    .string "But that ye must turn away this day\n"
    .string "from following the LORD? and it\l"
    .string "will be, seeing ye rebel to day\l"
    .string "against the LORD, that to morrow he\l"
    .string "will be wroth with the whole\l"
    .string "congregation of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_19::
    .string "Notwithstanding, if the land of\n"
    .string "your possession be unclean, then\l"
    .string "pass ye over unto the land of the\l"
    .string "possession of the LORD, wherein the\l"
    .string "LORD’s tabernacle dwelleth, and\l"
    .string "take possession among us: but rebel\l"
    .string "not against the LORD, nor rebel\l"
    .string "against us, in building you an altar\l"
    .string "beside the altar of the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_20::
    .string "Did not Achan the son of Zerah\n"
    .string "commit a trespass in the accursed\l"
    .string "thing, and wrath fell on all the\l"
    .string "congregation of Israel? and that man\l"
    .string "perished not alone in his iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_21::
    .string "Then the children of Reuben and the\n"
    .string "children of Gad and the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh answered, and said unto\l"
    .string "the heads of the thousands of\l"
    .string "Israel,"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_22::
    .string "The LORD God of gods, the LORD God of\n"
    .string "gods, he knoweth, and Israel he\l"
    .string "shall know; if it be in rebellion,\l"
    .string "or if in transgression against the\l"
    .string "LORD, (save us not this day,)"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_23::
    .string "That we have built us an altar to\n"
    .string "turn from following the LORD, or if\l"
    .string "to offer thereon burnt offering or\l"
    .string "meat offering, or if to offer peace\l"
    .string "offerings thereon, let the LORD\l"
    .string "himself require it;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_24::
    .string "And if we have not rather done it\n"
    .string "for fear of this thing, saying, In\l"
    .string "time to come your children might\l"
    .string "speak unto our children, saying,\l"
    .string "What have ye to do with the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel?"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_25::
    .string "For the LORD hath made Jordan a\n"
    .string "border between us and you, ye\l"
    .string "children of Reuben and children of\l"
    .string "Gad; ye have no part in the LORD: so\l"
    .string "shall your children make our\l"
    .string "children cease from fearing the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_26::
    .string "Therefore we said, Let us now\n"
    .string "prepare to build us an altar, not\l"
    .string "for burnt offering, nor for\l"
    .string "sacrifice:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_27::
    .string "But that it may be a witness between\n"
    .string "us, and you, and our generations\l"
    .string "after us, that we might do the\l"
    .string "service of the LORD before him with\l"
    .string "our burnt offerings, and with our\l"
    .string "sacrifices, and with our peace\l"
    .string "offerings; that your children may\l"
    .string "not say to our children in time to\l"
    .string "come, Ye have no part in the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_28::
    .string "Therefore said we, that it shall\n"
    .string "be, when they should so say to us or\l"
    .string "to our generations in time to come,\l"
    .string "that we may say again, Behold the\l"
    .string "pattern of the altar of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which our fathers made, not for burnt\l"
    .string "offerings, nor for sacrifices; but it\l"
    .string "is a witness between us and you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_29::
    .string "God forbid that we should rebel\n"
    .string "against the LORD, and turn this day\l"
    .string "from following the LORD, to build\l"
    .string "an altar for burnt offerings, for\l"
    .string "meat offerings, or for sacrifices,\l"
    .string "beside the altar of the LORD our God\l"
    .string "that is before his tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_30::
    .string "And when Phinehas the priest, and\n"
    .string "the princes of the congregation and\l"
    .string "heads of the thousands of Israel\l"
    .string "which were with him, heard the words\l"
    .string "that the children of Reuben and the\l"
    .string "children of Gad and the children of\l"
    .string "Manasseh spake, it pleased them.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_31::
    .string "And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the\n"
    .string "priest said unto the children of\l"
    .string "Reuben, and to the children of Gad,\l"
    .string "and to the children of Manasseh,\l"
    .string "This day we perceive that the LORD\l"
    .string "is among us, because ye have not\l"
    .string "committed this trespass against the\l"
    .string "LORD: now ye have delivered the\l"
    .string "children of Israel out of the hand\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_32::
    .string "And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the\n"
    .string "priest, and the princes, returned\l"
    .string "from the children of Reuben, and\l"
    .string "from the children of Gad, out of the\l"
    .string "land of Gilead, unto the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, to the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "and brought them word again.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_33::
    .string "And the thing pleased the\n"
    .string "children of Israel; and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel blessed God, and\l"
    .string "did not intend to go up against them\l"
    .string "in battle, to destroy the land\l"
    .string "wherein the children of Reuben and\l"
    .string "Gad dwelt.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_22_34::
    .string "And the children of Reuben and the\n"
    .string "children of Gad called the altar\l"
    .string "Ed: for it shall be a witness\l"
    .string "between us that the LORD is God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_1::
    .string "And it came to pass a long time\n"
    .string "after that the LORD had given rest\l"
    .string "unto Israel from all their enemies\l"
    .string "round about, that Joshua waxed old\l"
    .string "and stricken in age.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_2::
    .string "And Joshua called for all\n"
    .string "Israel, and for their elders, and\l"
    .string "for their heads, and for their\l"
    .string "judges, and for their officers, and\l"
    .string "said unto them, I am old and stricken\l"
    .string "in age:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_3::
    .string "And ye have seen all that the LORD\n"
    .string "your God hath done unto all these\l"
    .string "nations because of you; for the LORD\l"
    .string "your God is he that hath fought for\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_4::
    .string "Behold, I have divided unto you by\n"
    .string "lot these nations that remain, to be\l"
    .string "an inheritance for your tribes, from\l"
    .string "Jordan, with all the nations that I\l"
    .string "have cut off, even unto the great sea\l"
    .string "westward.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_5::
    .string "And the LORD your God, he shall\n"
    .string "expel them from before you, and\l"
    .string "drive them from out of your sight;\l"
    .string "and ye shall possess their land,\l"
    .string "as the LORD your God hath promised\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_6::
    .string "Be ye therefore very courageous to\n"
    .string "keep and to do all that is written\l"
    .string "in the book of the law of Moses, that\l"
    .string "ye turn not aside therefrom to the\l"
    .string "right hand or to the left;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_7::
    .string "That ye come not among these\n"
    .string "nations, these that remain among you;\l"
    .string "neither make mention of the name of\l"
    .string "their gods, nor cause to swear by\l"
    .string "them, neither serve them, nor bow\l"
    .string "yourselves unto them:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_8::
    .string "But cleave unto the LORD your God,\n"
    .string "as ye have done unto this day$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_9::
    .string "For the LORD hath driven out from\n"
    .string "before you great nations and strong:\l"
    .string "but as for you, no man hath been able\l"
    .string "to stand before you unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_10::
    .string "One man of you shall chase a\n"
    .string "thousand: for the LORD your God, he\l"
    .string "it is that fighteth for you, as he\l"
    .string "hath promised you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_11::
    .string "Take good heed therefore unto\n"
    .string "yourselves, that ye love the LORD\l"
    .string "your God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_12::
    .string "Else if ye do in any wise go back,\n"
    .string "and cleave unto the remnant of these\l"
    .string "nations, even these that remain among\l"
    .string "you, and shall make marriages with\l"
    .string "them, and go in unto them, and they to\l"
    .string "you:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_13::
    .string "Know for a certainty that the LORD\n"
    .string "your God will no more drive out any\l"
    .string "of these nations from before you; but\l"
    .string "they shall be snares and traps unto\l"
    .string "you, and scourges in your sides, and\l"
    .string "thorns in your eyes, until ye perish\l"
    .string "from off this good land which the\l"
    .string "LORD your God hath given you$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_14::
    .string "And, behold, this day I am going the\n"
    .string "way of all the earth: and ye know in\l"
    .string "all your hearts and in all your\l"
    .string "souls, that not one thing hath\l"
    .string "failed of all the good things which\l"
    .string "the LORD your God spake concerning\l"
    .string "you; all are come to pass unto you,\l"
    .string "and not one thing hath failed\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_15::
    .string "Therefore it shall come to pass,\n"
    .string "that as all good things are come\l"
    .string "upon you, which the LORD your God\l"
    .string "promised you; so shall the LORD\l"
    .string "bring upon you all evil things,\l"
    .string "until he have destroyed you from off\l"
    .string "this good land which the LORD your\l"
    .string "God hath given you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_23_16::
    .string "When ye have transgressed the\n"
    .string "covenant of the LORD your God, which\l"
    .string "he commanded you, and have gone and\l"
    .string "served other gods, and bowed\l"
    .string "yourselves to them; then shall the\l"
    .string "anger of the LORD be kindled against\l"
    .string "you, and ye shall perish quickly\l"
    .string "from off the good land which he hath\l"
    .string "given unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_1::
    .string "And Joshua gathered all the tribes\n"
    .string "of Israel to Shechem, and called\l"
    .string "for the elders of Israel, and for\l"
    .string "their heads, and for their judges,\l"
    .string "and for their officers; and they\l"
    .string "presented themselves before God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_2::
    .string "And Joshua said unto all the\n"
    .string "people, Thus saith the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel, Your fathers dwelt on the\l"
    .string "other side of the flood in old time,\l"
    .string "even Terah, the father of Abraham,\l"
    .string "and the father of Nachor: and they\l"
    .string "served other gods.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_3::
    .string "And I took your father Abraham from\n"
    .string "the other side of the flood, and led\l"
    .string "him throughout all the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan, and multiplied his seed,\l"
    .string "and gave him Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_4::
    .string "And I gave unto Isaac Jacob and\n"
    .string "Esau: and I gave unto Esau mount\l"
    .string "Seir, to possess it; but Jacob and\l"
    .string "his children went down into Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_5::
    .string "I sent Moses also and Aaron, and I\n"
    .string "plagued Egypt, according to that\l"
    .string "which I did among them: and afterward\l"
    .string "I brought you out.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_6::
    .string "And I brought your fathers out of\n"
    .string "Egypt: and ye came unto the sea; and\l"
    .string "the Egyptians pursued after your\l"
    .string "fathers with chariots and horsemen\l"
    .string "unto the Red sea.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_7::
    .string "And when they cried unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "he put darkness between you and the\l"
    .string "Egyptians, and brought the sea upon\l"
    .string "them, and covered them; and your eyes\l"
    .string "have seen what I have done in Egypt:\l"
    .string "and ye dwelt in the wilderness a\l"
    .string "long season.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_8::
    .string "And I brought you into the land of\n"
    .string "the Amorites, which dwelt on the\l"
    .string "other side Jordan; and they fought\l"
    .string "with you: and I gave them into your\l"
    .string "hand, that ye might possess their\l"
    .string "land; and I destroyed them from\l"
    .string "before you.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_9::
    .string "Then Balak the son of Zippor, king\n"
    .string "of Moab, arose and warred against\l"
    .string "Israel, and sent and called Balaam\l"
    .string "the son of Beor to curse you:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_10::
    .string "But I would not hearken unto\n"
    .string "Balaam; therefore he blessed you\l"
    .string "still: so I delivered you out of\l"
    .string "his hand$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_11::
    .string "And you went over Jordan, and came\n"
    .string "unto Jericho: and the men of Jericho\l"
    .string "fought against you, the Amorites, and\l"
    .string "the Perizzites, and the Canaanites,\l"
    .string "and the Hittites, and the\l"
    .string "Girgashites, the Hivites, and the\l"
    .string "Jebusites; and I delivered them into\l"
    .string "your hand.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_12::
    .string "And I sent the hornet before you,\n"
    .string "which drave them out from before you,\l"
    .string "even the two kings of the Amorites;\l"
    .string "but not with thy sword, nor with thy\l"
    .string "bow.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_13::
    .string "And I have given you a land for\n"
    .string "which ye did not labour, and cities\l"
    .string "which ye built not, and ye dwell in\l"
    .string "them; of the vineyards and\l"
    .string "oliveyards which ye planted not do\l"
    .string "ye eat.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_14::
    .string "Now therefore fear the LORD, and\n"
    .string "serve him in sincerity and in truth:\l"
    .string "and put away the gods which your\l"
    .string "fathers served on the other side of\l"
    .string "the flood, and in Egypt; and serve\l"
    .string "ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_15::
    .string "And if it seem evil unto you to\n"
    .string "serve the LORD, choose you this day\l"
    .string "whom ye will serve; whether the gods\l"
    .string "which your fathers served that were\l"
    .string "on the other side of the flood, or\l"
    .string "the gods of the Amorites, in whose\l"
    .string "land ye dwell: but as for me and my\l"
    .string "house, we will serve the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_16::
    .string "And the people answered and said,\n"
    .string "God forbid that we should forsake\l"
    .string "the LORD, to serve other gods;"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_17::
    .string "For the LORD our God, he it is that\n"
    .string "brought us up and our fathers out of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt, from the house of\l"
    .string "bondage, and which did those great\l"
    .string "signs in our sight, and preserved us\l"
    .string "in all the way wherein we went, and\l"
    .string "among all the people through whom\l"
    .string "we passed:"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_18::
    .string "And the LORD drave out from before\n"
    .string "us all the people, even the\l"
    .string "Amorites which dwelt in the land:\l"
    .string "therefore will we also serve the\l"
    .string "LORD; for he is our God$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_19::
    .string "And Joshua said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Ye cannot serve the LORD: for he is an\l"
    .string "holy God; he is a jealous God; he\l"
    .string "will not forgive your\l"
    .string "transgressions nor your sins.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_20::
    .string "If ye forsake the LORD, and serve\n"
    .string "strange gods, then he will turn and\l"
    .string "do you hurt, and consume you, after\l"
    .string "that he hath done you good.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_21::
    .string "And the people said unto Joshua,\n"
    .string "Nay; but we will serve the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_22::
    .string "And Joshua said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Ye are witnesses against yourselves\l"
    .string "that ye have chosen you the LORD, to\l"
    .string "serve him. And they said, We are\l"
    .string "witnesses.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_23::
    .string "Now therefore put away, said he,\n"
    .string "the strange gods which are among you,\l"
    .string "and incline your heart unto the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_24::
    .string "And the people said unto Joshua,\n"
    .string "The LORD our God will we serve, and\l"
    .string "his voice will we obey.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_25::
    .string "So Joshua made a covenant with the\n"
    .string "people that day, and set them a\l"
    .string "statute and an ordinance in Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_26::
    .string "And Joshua wrote these words in the\n"
    .string "book of the law of God, and took a\l"
    .string "great stone, and set it up there\l"
    .string "under an oak, that was by the\l"
    .string "sanctuary of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_27::
    .string "And Joshua said unto all the\n"
    .string "people, Behold, this stone shall\l"
    .string "be a witness unto us; for it hath\l"
    .string "heard all the words of the LORD\l"
    .string "which he spake unto us: it shall be\l"
    .string "therefore a witness unto you, lest\l"
    .string "ye deny your God.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_28::
    .string "So Joshua let the people depart,\n"
    .string "every man unto his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_29::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that Joshua the son of Nun,\l"
    .string "the servant of the LORD, died, being\l"
    .string "an hundred and ten years old.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_30::
    .string "And they buried him in the border of\n"
    .string "his inheritance in Timnathserah,\l"
    .string "which is in mount Ephraim, on the\l"
    .string "north side of the hill of Gaash.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_31::
    .string "And Israel served the LORD all the\n"
    .string "days of Joshua, and all the days of\l"
    .string "the elders that overlived Joshua,\l"
    .string "and which had known all the works of\l"
    .string "the LORD, that he had done for\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_32::
    .string "And the bones of Joseph, which the\n"
    .string "children of Israel brought up out\l"
    .string "of Egypt, buried they in Shechem, in\l"
    .string "a parcel of ground which Jacob\l"
    .string "bought of the sons of Hamor the\l"
    .string "father of Shechem for an hundred\l"
    .string "pieces of silver: and it became the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the children of\l"
    .string "Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Joshua_24_33::
    .string "And Eleazar the son of Aaron died;\n"
    .string "and they buried him in a hill that\l"
    .string "pertained to Phinehas his son, which\l"
    .string "was given him in mount Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_1::
    .string "Now after the death of Joshua it\n"
    .string "came to pass, that the children of\l"
    .string "Israel asked the LORD, saying, Who\l"
    .string "shall go up for us against the\l"
    .string "Canaanites first, to fight against\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_2::
    .string "And the LORD said, Judah shall go\n"
    .string "up: behold, I have delivered the\l"
    .string "land into his hand$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_3::
    .string "And Judah said unto Simeon his\n"
    .string "brother, Come up with me into my\l"
    .string "lot, that we may fight against the\l"
    .string "Canaanites; and I likewise will go\l"
    .string "with thee into thy lot. So Simeon\l"
    .string "went with him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_4::
    .string "And Judah went up; and the LORD\n"
    .string "delivered the Canaanites and the\l"
    .string "Perizzites into their hand: and they\l"
    .string "slew of them in Bezek ten thousand\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_5::
    .string "And they found Adonibezek in Bezek:\n"
    .string "and they fought against him, and they\l"
    .string "slew the Canaanites and the\l"
    .string "Perizzites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_6::
    .string "But Adonibezek fled; and they\n"
    .string "pursued after him, and caught him,\l"
    .string "and cut off his thumbs and his great\l"
    .string "toes.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_7::
    .string "And Adonibezek said, Threescore and\n"
    .string "ten kings, having their thumbs and\l"
    .string "their great toes cut off, gathered\l"
    .string "their meat under my table: as I have\l"
    .string "done, so God hath requited me. And\l"
    .string "they brought him to Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "there he died.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_8::
    .string "Now the children of Judah had\n"
    .string "fought against Jerusalem, and had\l"
    .string "taken it, and smitten it with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword, and set the city on\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_9::
    .string "And afterward the children of Judah\n"
    .string "went down to fight against the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, that dwelt in the\l"
    .string "mountain, and in the south, and in\l"
    .string "the valley.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_10::
    .string "And Judah went against the\n"
    .string "Canaanites that dwelt in Hebron:\l"
    .string "(now the name of Hebron before was\l"
    .string "Kirjatharba:) and they slew Sheshai,\l"
    .string "and Ahiman, and Talmai.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_11::
    .string "And from thence he went against the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Debir: and the name of\l"
    .string "Debir before was Kirjathsepher:"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_12::
    .string "And Caleb said, He that smiteth\n"
    .string "Kirjathsepher, and taketh it, to him\l"
    .string "will I give Achsah my daughter to\l"
    .string "wife$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_13::
    .string "And Othniel the son of Kenaz,\n"
    .string "Caleb’s younger brother, took it:\l"
    .string "and he gave him Achsah his daughter\l"
    .string "to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_14::
    .string "And it came to pass, when she came\n"
    .string "to him, that she moved him to ask of\l"
    .string "her father a field: and she lighted\l"
    .string "from off her ass; and Caleb said unto\l"
    .string "her, What wilt thou?"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_15::
    .string "And she said unto him, Give me a\n"
    .string "blessing: for thou hast given me a\l"
    .string "south land; give me also springs of\l"
    .string "water. And Caleb gave her the upper\l"
    .string "springs and the nether springs$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_16::
    .string "And the children of the Kenite,\n"
    .string "Moses’ father in law, went up out of\l"
    .string "the city of palm trees with the\l"
    .string "children of Judah into the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Judah, which lieth in\l"
    .string "the south of Arad; and they went and\l"
    .string "dwelt among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_17::
    .string "And Judah went with Simeon his\n"
    .string "brother, and they slew the\l"
    .string "Canaanites that inhabited Zephath,\l"
    .string "and utterly destroyed it. And the\l"
    .string "name of the city was called Hormah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_18::
    .string "Also Judah took Gaza with the coast\n"
    .string "thereof, and Askelon with the coast\l"
    .string "thereof, and Ekron with the coast\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_19::
    .string "And the LORD was with Judah; and he\n"
    .string "drave out the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "mountain; but could not drive out\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of the valley,\l"
    .string "because they had chariots of iron.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_20::
    .string "And they gave Hebron unto Caleb, as\n"
    .string "Moses said: and he expelled thence\l"
    .string "the three sons of Anak.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_21::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin did\n"
    .string "not drive out the Jebusites that\l"
    .string "inhabited Jerusalem; but the\l"
    .string "Jebusites dwell with the children\l"
    .string "of Benjamin in Jerusalem unto this\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_22::
    .string "And the house of Joseph, they also\n"
    .string "went up against Bethel: and the LORD\l"
    .string "was with them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_23::
    .string "And the house of Joseph sent to\n"
    .string "descry Bethel. (Now the name of the\l"
    .string "city before was Luz.)"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_24::
    .string "And the spies saw a man come forth\n"
    .string "out of the city, and they said unto\l"
    .string "him, Shew us, we pray thee, the\l"
    .string "entrance into the city, and we will\l"
    .string "shew thee mercy$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_25::
    .string "And when he shewed them the entrance\n"
    .string "into the city, they smote the city\l"
    .string "with the edge of the sword; but they\l"
    .string "let go the man and all his family.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_26::
    .string "And the man went into the land of\n"
    .string "the Hittites, and built a city, and\l"
    .string "called the name thereof Luz: which\l"
    .string "is the name thereof unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_27::
    .string "Neither did Manasseh drive out the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Bethshean and her\l"
    .string "towns, nor Taanach and her towns, nor\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Dor and her towns,\l"
    .string "nor the inhabitants of Ibleam and\l"
    .string "her towns, nor the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Megiddo and her towns: but the\l"
    .string "Canaanites would dwell in that\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_28::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Israel\n"
    .string "was strong, that they put the\l"
    .string "Canaanites to tribute, and did not\l"
    .string "utterly drive them out.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_29::
    .string "Neither did Ephraim drive out the\n"
    .string "Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer; but\l"
    .string "the Canaanites dwelt in Gezer among\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_30::
    .string "Neither did Zebulun drive out the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Kitron, nor the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Nahalol; but the\l"
    .string "Canaanites dwelt among them, and\l"
    .string "became tributaries.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_31::
    .string "Neither did Asher drive out the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Accho, nor the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Zidon, nor of Ahlab,\l"
    .string "nor of Achzib, nor of Helbah, nor of\l"
    .string "Aphik, nor of Rehob:"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_32::
    .string "But the Asherites dwelt among the\n"
    .string "Canaanites, the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "land: for they did not drive them out$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_33::
    .string "Neither did Naphtali drive out the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Bethshemesh, nor the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Bethanath; but he\l"
    .string "dwelt among the Canaanites, the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land:\l"
    .string "nevertheless the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Bethshemesh and of Bethanath became\l"
    .string "tributaries unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_34::
    .string "And the Amorites forced the\n"
    .string "children of Dan into the mountain:\l"
    .string "for they would not suffer them to\l"
    .string "come down to the valley:"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_35::
    .string "But the Amorites would dwell in\n"
    .string "mount Heres in Aijalon, and in\l"
    .string "Shaalbim: yet the hand of the house\l"
    .string "of Joseph prevailed, so that they\l"
    .string "became tributaries$"
Bible_Text_Judges_1_36::
    .string "And the coast of the Amorites was\n"
    .string "from the going up to Akrabbim, from\l"
    .string "the rock, and upward.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_1::
    .string "And an angel of the LORD came up\n"
    .string "from Gilgal to Bochim, and said, I\l"
    .string "made you to go up out of Egypt, and\l"
    .string "have brought you unto the land which\l"
    .string "I sware unto your fathers; and I\l"
    .string "said, I will never break my covenant\l"
    .string "with you.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_2::
    .string "And ye shall make no league with\n"
    .string "the inhabitants of this land; ye\l"
    .string "shall throw down their altars: but\l"
    .string "ye have not obeyed my voice: why have\l"
    .string "ye done this?"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_3::
    .string "Wherefore I also said, I will not\n"
    .string "drive them out from before you; but\l"
    .string "they shall be as thorns in your\l"
    .string "sides, and their gods shall be a\l"
    .string "snare unto you$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the angel\n"
    .string "of the LORD spake these words unto\l"
    .string "all the children of Israel, that\l"
    .string "the people lifted up their voice,\l"
    .string "and wept.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_5::
    .string "And they called the name of that\n"
    .string "place Bochim: and they sacrificed\l"
    .string "there unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_6::
    .string "And when Joshua had let the\n"
    .string "people go, the children of Israel\l"
    .string "went every man unto his inheritance\l"
    .string "to possess the land.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_7::
    .string "And the people served the LORD\n"
    .string "all the days of Joshua, and all the\l"
    .string "days of the elders that outlived\l"
    .string "Joshua, who had seen all the great\l"
    .string "works of the LORD, that he did for\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_8::
    .string "And Joshua the son of Nun, the\n"
    .string "servant of the LORD, died, being an\l"
    .string "hundred and ten years old.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_9::
    .string "And they buried him in the border of\n"
    .string "his inheritance in Timnathheres, in\l"
    .string "the mount of Ephraim, on the north\l"
    .string "side of the hill Gaash.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_10::
    .string "And also all that generation were\n"
    .string "gathered unto their fathers: and\l"
    .string "there arose another generation after\l"
    .string "them, which knew not the LORD, nor\l"
    .string "yet the works which he had done for\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_11::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil in the sight of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "served Baalim:"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_12::
    .string "And they forsook the LORD God of\n"
    .string "their fathers, which brought them out\l"
    .string "of the land of Egypt, and followed\l"
    .string "other gods, of the gods of the\l"
    .string "people that were round about them,\l"
    .string "and bowed themselves unto them, and\l"
    .string "provoked the LORD to anger$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_13::
    .string "And they forsook the LORD, and\n"
    .string "served Baal and Ashtaroth.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_14::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was hot\n"
    .string "against Israel, and he delivered\l"
    .string "them into the hands of spoilers\l"
    .string "that spoiled them, and he sold them\l"
    .string "into the hands of their enemies round\l"
    .string "about, so that they could not any\l"
    .string "longer stand before their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_15::
    .string "Whithersoever they went out, the\n"
    .string "hand of the LORD was against them for\l"
    .string "evil, as the LORD had said, and as\l"
    .string "the LORD had sworn unto them: and\l"
    .string "they were greatly distressed.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_16::
    .string "Nevertheless the LORD raised up\n"
    .string "judges, which delivered them out of\l"
    .string "the hand of those that spoiled them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_17::
    .string "And yet they would not hearken unto\n"
    .string "their judges, but they went a whoring\l"
    .string "after other gods, and bowed\l"
    .string "themselves unto them: they turned\l"
    .string "quickly out of the way which their\l"
    .string "fathers walked in, obeying the\l"
    .string "commandments of the LORD; but they\l"
    .string "did not so.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_18::
    .string "And when the LORD raised them up\n"
    .string "judges, then the LORD was with the\l"
    .string "judge, and delivered them out of the\l"
    .string "hand of their enemies all the days\l"
    .string "of the judge: for it repented the\l"
    .string "LORD because of their groanings by\l"
    .string "reason of them that oppressed them\l"
    .string "and vexed them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the judge\n"
    .string "was dead, that they returned, and\l"
    .string "corrupted themselves more than\l"
    .string "their fathers, in following other\l"
    .string "gods to serve them, and to bow down\l"
    .string "unto them; they ceased not from their\l"
    .string "own doings, nor from their stubborn\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_20::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was hot\n"
    .string "against Israel; and he said, Because\l"
    .string "that this people hath transgressed\l"
    .string "my covenant which I commanded their\l"
    .string "fathers, and have not hearkened unto\l"
    .string "my voice;"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_21::
    .string "I also will not henceforth drive\n"
    .string "out any from before them of the\l"
    .string "nations which Joshua left when he\l"
    .string "died:"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_22::
    .string "That through them I may prove\n"
    .string "Israel, whether they will keep the\l"
    .string "way of the LORD to walk therein, as\l"
    .string "their fathers did keep it, or not$"
Bible_Text_Judges_2_23::
    .string "Therefore the LORD left those\n"
    .string "nations, without driving them out\l"
    .string "hastily; neither delivered he them\l"
    .string "into the hand of Joshua.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_1::
    .string "Now these are the nations which the\n"
    .string "LORD left, to prove Israel by them,\l"
    .string "even as many of Israel as had not\l"
    .string "known all the wars of Canaan;"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_2::
    .string "Only that the generations of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel might know, to\l"
    .string "teach them war, at the least such as\l"
    .string "before knew nothing thereof;"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_3::
    .string "Namely, five lords of the\n"
    .string "Philistines, and all the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, and the Sidonians, and\l"
    .string "the Hivites that dwelt in mount\l"
    .string "Lebanon, from mount Baalhermon unto\l"
    .string "the entering in of Hamath$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_4::
    .string "And they were to prove Israel by\n"
    .string "them, to know whether they would\l"
    .string "hearken unto the commandments of the\l"
    .string "LORD, which he commanded their\l"
    .string "fathers by the hand of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_5::
    .string "And the children of Israel dwelt\n"
    .string "among the Canaanites, Hittites, and\l"
    .string "Amorites, and Perizzites, and\l"
    .string "Hivites, and Jebusites:"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_6::
    .string "And they took their daughters to be\n"
    .string "their wives, and gave their daughters\l"
    .string "to their sons, and served their gods$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_7::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil in the sight of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "forgat the LORD their God, and served\l"
    .string "Baalim and the groves.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_8::
    .string "Therefore the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "hot against Israel, and he sold them\l"
    .string "into the hand of Chushanrishathaim\l"
    .string "king of Mesopotamia: and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel served\l"
    .string "Chushanrishathaim eight years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_9::
    .string "And when the children of Israel\n"
    .string "cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised\l"
    .string "up a deliverer to the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, who delivered them, even\l"
    .string "Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb’s\l"
    .string "younger brother.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_10::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD came\n"
    .string "upon him, and he judged Israel, and\l"
    .string "went out to war: and the LORD\l"
    .string "delivered Chushanrishathaim king of\l"
    .string "Mesopotamia into his hand; and his\l"
    .string "hand prevailed against\l"
    .string "Chushanrishathaim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_11::
    .string "And the land had rest forty years.\n"
    .string "And Othniel the son of Kenaz died.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_12::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil again in the sight of the LORD:\l"
    .string "and the LORD strengthened Eglon the\l"
    .string "king of Moab against Israel, because\l"
    .string "they had done evil in the sight of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_13::
    .string "And he gathered unto him the\n"
    .string "children of Ammon and Amalek, and\l"
    .string "went and smote Israel, and\l"
    .string "possessed the city of palm trees.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_14::
    .string "So the children of Israel served\n"
    .string "Eglon the king of Moab eighteen\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_15::
    .string "But when the children of Israel\n"
    .string "cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised\l"
    .string "them up a deliverer, Ehud the son of\l"
    .string "Gera, a Benjamite, a man lefthanded:\l"
    .string "and by him the children of Israel\l"
    .string "sent a present unto Eglon the king\l"
    .string "of Moab.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_16::
    .string "But Ehud made him a dagger which had\n"
    .string "two edges, of a cubit length; and he\l"
    .string "did gird it under his raiment upon\l"
    .string "his right thigh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_17::
    .string "And he brought the present unto\n"
    .string "Eglon king of Moab: and Eglon was a\l"
    .string "very fat man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_18::
    .string "And when he had made an end to offer\n"
    .string "the present, he sent away the\l"
    .string "people that bare the present.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_19::
    .string "But he himself turned again from\n"
    .string "the quarries that were by Gilgal,\l"
    .string "and said, I have a secret errand unto\l"
    .string "thee, O king: who said, Keep\l"
    .string "silence. And all that stood by him\l"
    .string "went out from him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_20::
    .string "And Ehud came unto him; and he was\n"
    .string "sitting in a summer parlour, which\l"
    .string "he had for himself alone. And Ehud\l"
    .string "said, I have a message from God unto\l"
    .string "thee. And he arose out of his seat.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_21::
    .string "And Ehud put forth his left hand,\n"
    .string "and took the dagger from his right\l"
    .string "thigh, and thrust it into his belly:"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_22::
    .string "And the haft also went in after the\n"
    .string "blade; and the fat closed upon the\l"
    .string "blade, so that he could not draw the\l"
    .string "dagger out of his belly; and the\l"
    .string "dirt came out$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_23::
    .string "Then Ehud went forth through the\n"
    .string "porch, and shut the doors of the\l"
    .string "parlour upon him, and locked them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_24::
    .string "When he was gone out, his servants\n"
    .string "came; and when they saw that, behold,\l"
    .string "the doors of the parlour were\l"
    .string "locked, they said, Surely he\l"
    .string "covereth his feet in his summer\l"
    .string "chamber.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_25::
    .string "And they tarried till they were\n"
    .string "ashamed: and, behold, he opened not\l"
    .string "the doors of the parlour; therefore\l"
    .string "they took a key, and opened them:\l"
    .string "and, behold, their lord was fallen\l"
    .string "down dead on the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_26::
    .string "And Ehud escaped while they\n"
    .string "tarried, and passed beyond the\l"
    .string "quarries, and escaped unto Seirath.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_27::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he was\n"
    .string "come, that he blew a trumpet in the\l"
    .string "mountain of Ephraim, and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel went down with\l"
    .string "him from the mount, and he before\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_28::
    .string "And he said unto them, Follow after\n"
    .string "me: for the LORD hath delivered your\l"
    .string "enemies the Moabites into your hand.\l"
    .string "And they went down after him, and\l"
    .string "took the fords of Jordan toward Moab,\l"
    .string "and suffered not a man to pass over.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_29::
    .string "And they slew of Moab at that time\n"
    .string "about ten thousand men, all lusty,\l"
    .string "and all men of valour; and there\l"
    .string "escaped not a man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_30::
    .string "So Moab was subdued that day under\n"
    .string "the hand of Israel. And the land had\l"
    .string "rest fourscore years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_3_31::
    .string "And after him was Shamgar the son of\n"
    .string "Anath, which slew of the\l"
    .string "Philistines six hundred men with an\l"
    .string "ox goad: and he also delivered\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_1::
    .string "And the children of Israel again\n"
    .string "did evil in the sight of the LORD,\l"
    .string "when Ehud was dead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_2::
    .string "And the LORD sold them into the\n"
    .string "hand of Jabin king of Canaan, that\l"
    .string "reigned in Hazor; the captain of\l"
    .string "whose host was Sisera, which dwelt\l"
    .string "in Harosheth of the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_3::
    .string "And the children of Israel cried\n"
    .string "unto the LORD: for he had nine\l"
    .string "hundred chariots of iron; and twenty\l"
    .string "years he mightily oppressed the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_4::
    .string "And Deborah, a prophetess, the\n"
    .string "wife of Lapidoth, she judged Israel\l"
    .string "at that time.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_5::
    .string "And she dwelt under the palm tree\n"
    .string "of Deborah between Ramah and Bethel\l"
    .string "in mount Ephraim: and the children\l"
    .string "of Israel came up to her for\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_6::
    .string "And she sent and called Barak the\n"
    .string "son of Abinoam out of\l"
    .string "Kedeshnaphtali, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "Hath not the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "commanded, saying, Go and draw toward\l"
    .string "mount Tabor, and take with thee ten\l"
    .string "thousand men of the children of\l"
    .string "Naphtali and of the children of\l"
    .string "Zebulun?"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_7::
    .string "And I will draw unto thee to the\n"
    .string "river Kishon Sisera, the captain of\l"
    .string "Jabin’s army, with his chariots and\l"
    .string "his multitude; and I will deliver\l"
    .string "him into thine hand$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_8::
    .string "And Barak said unto her, If thou\n"
    .string "wilt go with me, then I will go: but\l"
    .string "if thou wilt not go with me, then I\l"
    .string "will not go.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_9::
    .string "And she said, I will surely go\n"
    .string "with thee: notwithstanding the\l"
    .string "journey that thou takest shall not\l"
    .string "be for thine honour; for the LORD\l"
    .string "shall sell Sisera into the hand of\l"
    .string "a woman. And Deborah arose, and went\l"
    .string "with Barak to Kedesh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_10::
    .string "And Barak called Zebulun and\n"
    .string "Naphtali to Kedesh; and he went up\l"
    .string "with ten thousand men at his feet:\l"
    .string "and Deborah went up with him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_11::
    .string "Now Heber the Kenite, which was of\n"
    .string "the children of Hobab the father in\l"
    .string "law of Moses, had severed himself\l"
    .string "from the Kenites, and pitched his\l"
    .string "tent unto the plain of Zaanaim,\l"
    .string "which is by Kedesh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_12::
    .string "And they shewed Sisera that Barak\n"
    .string "the son of Abinoam was gone up to\l"
    .string "mount Tabor.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_13::
    .string "And Sisera gathered together all\n"
    .string "his chariots, even nine hundred\l"
    .string "chariots of iron, and all the\l"
    .string "people that were with him, from\l"
    .string "Harosheth of the Gentiles unto the\l"
    .string "river of Kishon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_14::
    .string "And Deborah said unto Barak, Up;\n"
    .string "for this is the day in which the LORD\l"
    .string "hath delivered Sisera into thine\l"
    .string "hand: is not the LORD gone out before\l"
    .string "thee? So Barak went down from mount\l"
    .string "Tabor, and ten thousand men after him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_15::
    .string "And the LORD discomfited Sisera, and\n"
    .string "all his chariots, and all his\l"
    .string "host, with the edge of the sword\l"
    .string "before Barak; so that Sisera lighted\l"
    .string "down off his chariot, and fled away\l"
    .string "on his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_16::
    .string "But Barak pursued after the\n"
    .string "chariots, and after the host, unto\l"
    .string "Harosheth of the Gentiles: and all\l"
    .string "the host of Sisera fell upon the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword; and there was not a\l"
    .string "man left.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_17::
    .string "Howbeit Sisera fled away on his\n"
    .string "feet to the tent of Jael the wife of\l"
    .string "Heber the Kenite: for there was\l"
    .string "peace between Jabin the king of Hazor\l"
    .string "and the house of Heber the Kenite.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_18::
    .string "And Jael went out to meet Sisera,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, Turn in, my lord,\l"
    .string "turn in to me; fear not. And when he\l"
    .string "had turned in unto her into the tent,\l"
    .string "she covered him with a mantle.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_19::
    .string "And he said unto her, Give me, I\n"
    .string "pray thee, a little water to drink;\l"
    .string "for I am thirsty. And she opened a\l"
    .string "bottle of milk, and gave him drink,\l"
    .string "and covered him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_20::
    .string "Again he said unto her, Stand in the\n"
    .string "door of the tent, and it shall be,\l"
    .string "when any man doth come and enquire of\l"
    .string "thee, and say, Is there any man here?\l"
    .string "that thou shalt say, No.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_21::
    .string "Then Jael Heber’s wife took a nail\n"
    .string "of the tent, and took an hammer in her\l"
    .string "hand, and went softly unto him, and\l"
    .string "smote the nail into his temples,\l"
    .string "and fastened it into the ground: for\l"
    .string "he was fast asleep and weary. So he\l"
    .string "died.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_22::
    .string "And, behold, as Barak pursued\n"
    .string "Sisera, Jael came out to meet him,\l"
    .string "and said unto him, Come, and I will\l"
    .string "shew thee the man whom thou seekest.\l"
    .string "And when he came into her tent,\l"
    .string "behold, Sisera lay dead, and the\l"
    .string "nail was in his temples.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_23::
    .string "So God subdued on that day Jabin the\n"
    .string "king of Canaan before the children\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_4_24::
    .string "And the hand of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel prospered, and prevailed\l"
    .string "against Jabin the king of Canaan,\l"
    .string "until they had destroyed Jabin king\l"
    .string "of Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_1::
    .string "Then sang Deborah and Barak the son\n"
    .string "of Abinoam on that day, saying,"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_2::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD for the avenging\n"
    .string "of Israel, when the people\l"
    .string "willingly offered themselves$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_3::
    .string "Hear, O ye kings; give ear, O ye\n"
    .string "princes; I, even I, will sing unto\l"
    .string "the LORD; I will sing praise to the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_4::
    .string "LORD, when thou wentest out of Seir,\n"
    .string "when thou marchedst out of the field\l"
    .string "of Edom, the earth trembled, and the\l"
    .string "heavens dropped, the clouds also\l"
    .string "dropped water.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_5::
    .string "The mountains melted from before\n"
    .string "the LORD, even that Sinai from before\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_6::
    .string "In the days of Shamgar the son of\n"
    .string "Anath, in the days of Jael, the\l"
    .string "highways were unoccupied, and the\l"
    .string "travellers walked through byways.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_7::
    .string "The inhabitants of the villages\n"
    .string "ceased, they ceased in Israel,\l"
    .string "until that I Deborah arose, that I\l"
    .string "arose a mother in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_8::
    .string "They chose new gods; then was war in\n"
    .string "the gates: was there a shield or\l"
    .string "spear seen among forty thousand in\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_9::
    .string "My heart is toward the governors of\n"
    .string "Israel, that offered themselves\l"
    .string "willingly among the people.\l"
    .string "Bless ye the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_10::
    .string "Speak, ye that ride on white asses,\n"
    .string "ye that sit in judgment, and walk by\l"
    .string "the way.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_11::
    .string "They that are delivered from the\n"
    .string "noise of archers in the places of\l"
    .string "drawing water, there shall they\l"
    .string "rehearse the righteous acts of the\l"
    .string "LORD, even the righteous acts toward\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of his villages in\l"
    .string "Israel: then shall the people of\l"
    .string "the LORD go down to the gates.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_12::
    .string "Awake, awake, Deborah: awake, awake,\n"
    .string "utter a song: arise, Barak, and lead\l"
    .string "thy captivity captive, thou son of\l"
    .string "Abinoam.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_13::
    .string "Then he made him that remaineth have\n"
    .string "dominion over the nobles among the\l"
    .string "people: the LORD made me have\l"
    .string "dominion over the mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_14::
    .string "Out of Ephraim was there a root of\n"
    .string "them against Amalek; after thee,\l"
    .string "Benjamin, among thy people; out of\l"
    .string "Machir came down governors, and out\l"
    .string "of Zebulun they that handle the pen\l"
    .string "of the writer.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_15::
    .string "And the princes of Issachar were\n"
    .string "with Deborah; even Issachar, and\l"
    .string "also Barak: he was sent on foot into\l"
    .string "the valley. For the divisions of\l"
    .string "Reuben there were great thoughts of\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_16::
    .string "Why abodest thou among the\n"
    .string "sheepfolds, to hear the bleatings\l"
    .string "of the flocks? For the divisions of\l"
    .string "Reuben there were great searchings\l"
    .string "of heart.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_17::
    .string "Gilead abode beyond Jordan: and why\n"
    .string "did Dan remain in ships? Asher\l"
    .string "continued on the sea shore, and abode\l"
    .string "in his breaches.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_18::
    .string "Zebulun and Naphtali were a\n"
    .string "people that jeoparded their lives\l"
    .string "unto the death in the high places of\l"
    .string "the field.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_19::
    .string "The kings came and fought, then\n"
    .string "fought the kings of Canaan in Taanach\l"
    .string "by the waters of Megiddo; they took\l"
    .string "no gain of money.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_20::
    .string "They fought from heaven; the stars\n"
    .string "in their courses fought against\l"
    .string "Sisera.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_21::
    .string "The river of Kishon swept them\n"
    .string "away, that ancient river, the river\l"
    .string "Kishon. O my soul, thou hast trodden\l"
    .string "down strength.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_22::
    .string "Then were the horsehoofs broken by\n"
    .string "the means of the pransings, the\l"
    .string "pransings of their mighty ones.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_23::
    .string "Curse ye Meroz, said the angel of\n"
    .string "the LORD, curse ye bitterly the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof; because they\l"
    .string "came not to the help of the LORD, to\l"
    .string "the help of the LORD against the\l"
    .string "mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_24::
    .string "Blessed above women shall Jael\n"
    .string "the wife of Heber the Kenite be,\l"
    .string "blessed shall she be above women in\l"
    .string "the tent.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_25::
    .string "He asked water, and she gave him\n"
    .string "milk; she brought forth butter in a\l"
    .string "lordly dish.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_26::
    .string "She put her hand to the nail, and\n"
    .string "her right hand to the workmen’s\l"
    .string "hammer; and with the hammer she smote\l"
    .string "Sisera, she smote off his head, when\l"
    .string "she had pierced and stricken through\l"
    .string "his temples.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_27::
    .string "At her feet he bowed, he fell, he\n"
    .string "lay down: at her feet he bowed, he\l"
    .string "fell: where he bowed, there he\l"
    .string "fell down dead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_28::
    .string "The mother of Sisera looked out at\n"
    .string "a window, and cried through the\l"
    .string "lattice, Why is his chariot so long\l"
    .string "in coming? why tarry the wheels of\l"
    .string "his chariots?"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_29::
    .string "Her wise ladies answered her, yea,\n"
    .string "she returned answer to herself,"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_30::
    .string "Have they not sped? have they not\n"
    .string "divided the prey; to every man a\l"
    .string "damsel or two; to Sisera a prey of\l"
    .string "divers colours, a prey of divers\l"
    .string "colours of needlework, of divers\l"
    .string "colours of needlework on both\l"
    .string "sides, meet for the necks of them\l"
    .string "that take the spoil?"
Bible_Text_Judges_5_31::
    .string "So let all thine enemies perish,\n"
    .string "O LORD: but let them that love him\l"
    .string "be as the sun when he goeth forth in\l"
    .string "his might. And the land had rest\l"
    .string "forty years$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_1::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil in the sight of the LORD: and\l"
    .string "the LORD delivered them into the\l"
    .string "hand of Midian seven years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_2::
    .string "And the hand of Midian prevailed\n"
    .string "against Israel: and because of the\l"
    .string "Midianites the children of Israel\l"
    .string "made them the dens which are in the\l"
    .string "mountains, and caves, and strong\l"
    .string "holds.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_3::
    .string "And so it was, when Israel had sown,\n"
    .string "that the Midianites came up, and the\l"
    .string "Amalekites, and the children of the\l"
    .string "east, even they came up against\l"
    .string "them;"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_4::
    .string "And they encamped against them, and\n"
    .string "destroyed the increase of the earth,\l"
    .string "till thou come unto Gaza, and left\l"
    .string "no sustenance for Israel, neither\l"
    .string "sheep, nor ox, nor ass$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_5::
    .string "For they came up with their cattle\n"
    .string "and their tents, and they came as\l"
    .string "grasshoppers for multitude; for\l"
    .string "both they and their camels were\l"
    .string "without number: and they entered into\l"
    .string "the land to destroy it.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_6::
    .string "And Israel was greatly\n"
    .string "impoverished because of the\l"
    .string "Midianites; and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel cried unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_7::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "children of Israel cried unto the\l"
    .string "LORD because of the Midianites,"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_8::
    .string "That the LORD sent a prophet unto\n"
    .string "the children of Israel, which said\l"
    .string "unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel, I brought you up from\l"
    .string "Egypt, and brought you forth out of\l"
    .string "the house of bondage;"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_9::
    .string "And I delivered you out of the hand\n"
    .string "of the Egyptians, and out of the hand\l"
    .string "of all that oppressed you, and\l"
    .string "drave them out from before you, and\l"
    .string "gave you their land;"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_10::
    .string "And I said unto you, I am the LORD\n"
    .string "your God; fear not the gods of the\l"
    .string "Amorites, in whose land ye dwell:\l"
    .string "but ye have not obeyed my voice$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_11::
    .string "And there came an angel of the LORD,\n"
    .string "and sat under an oak which was in\l"
    .string "Ophrah, that pertained unto Joash\l"
    .string "the Abiezrite: and his son Gideon\l"
    .string "threshed wheat by the winepress, to\l"
    .string "hide it from the Midianites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_12::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD appeared\n"
    .string "unto him, and said unto him, The LORD\l"
    .string "is with thee, thou mighty man of\l"
    .string "valour.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_13::
    .string "And Gideon said unto him, Oh my\n"
    .string "Lord, if the LORD be with us, why then\l"
    .string "is all this befallen us? and where\l"
    .string "be all his miracles which our\l"
    .string "fathers told us of, saying, Did not\l"
    .string "the LORD bring us up from Egypt? but\l"
    .string "now the LORD hath forsaken us, and\l"
    .string "delivered us into the hands of the\l"
    .string "Midianites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_14::
    .string "And the LORD looked upon him, and\n"
    .string "said, Go in this thy might, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt save Israel from the hand of\l"
    .string "the Midianites: have not I sent thee?"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_15::
    .string "And he said unto him, Oh my Lord,\n"
    .string "wherewith shall I save Israel?\l"
    .string "behold, my family is poor in\l"
    .string "Manasseh, and I am the least in my\l"
    .string "father’s house$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_16::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Surely I\n"
    .string "will be with thee, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "smite the Midianites as one man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_17::
    .string "And he said unto him, If now I have\n"
    .string "found grace in thy sight, then shew\l"
    .string "me a sign that thou talkest with me.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_18::
    .string "Depart not hence, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "until I come unto thee, and bring\l"
    .string "forth my present, and set it before\l"
    .string "thee. And he said, I will tarry\l"
    .string "until thou come again.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_19::
    .string "And Gideon went in, and made ready a\n"
    .string "kid, and unleavened cakes of an\l"
    .string "ephah of flour: the flesh he put in\l"
    .string "a basket, and he put the broth in a\l"
    .string "pot, and brought it out unto him\l"
    .string "under the oak, and presented it.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_20::
    .string "And the angel of God said unto him,\n"
    .string "Take the flesh and the unleavened\l"
    .string "cakes, and lay them upon this rock,\l"
    .string "and pour out the broth. And he did so.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_21::
    .string "Then the angel of the LORD put\n"
    .string "forth the end of the staff that was\l"
    .string "in his hand, and touched the flesh\l"
    .string "and the unleavened cakes; and there\l"
    .string "rose up fire out of the rock, and\l"
    .string "consumed the flesh and the\l"
    .string "unleavened cakes. Then the angel of\l"
    .string "the LORD departed out of his sight.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_22::
    .string "And when Gideon perceived that he\n"
    .string "was an angel of the LORD, Gideon\l"
    .string "said, Alas, O LORD God! for because I\l"
    .string "have seen an angel of the LORD face\l"
    .string "to face.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_23::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Peace be\n"
    .string "unto thee; fear not: thou shalt not\l"
    .string "die.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_24::
    .string "Then Gideon built an altar there\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, and called it\l"
    .string "Jehovahshalom: unto this day it is\l"
    .string "yet in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_25::
    .string "And it came to pass the same night,\n"
    .string "that the LORD said unto him, Take thy\l"
    .string "father’s young bullock, even the\l"
    .string "second bullock of seven years old,\l"
    .string "and throw down the altar of Baal\l"
    .string "that thy father hath, and cut down\l"
    .string "the grove that is by it:"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_26::
    .string "And build an altar unto the LORD\n"
    .string "thy God upon the top of this rock,\l"
    .string "in the ordered place, and take the\l"
    .string "second bullock, and offer a burnt\l"
    .string "sacrifice with the wood of the grove\l"
    .string "which thou shalt cut down$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_27::
    .string "Then Gideon took ten men of his\n"
    .string "servants, and did as the LORD had\l"
    .string "said unto him: and so it was, because\l"
    .string "he feared his father’s household,\l"
    .string "and the men of the city, that he\l"
    .string "could not do it by day, that he did\l"
    .string "it by night.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_28::
    .string "And when the men of the city arose\n"
    .string "early in the morning, behold, the\l"
    .string "altar of Baal was cast down, and the\l"
    .string "grove was cut down that was by it, and\l"
    .string "the second bullock was offered\l"
    .string "upon the altar that was built.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_29::
    .string "And they said one to another, Who\n"
    .string "hath done this thing? And when they\l"
    .string "enquired and asked, they said, Gideon\l"
    .string "the son of Joash hath done this thing.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_30::
    .string "Then the men of the city said unto\n"
    .string "Joash, Bring out thy son, that he may\l"
    .string "die: because he hath cast down the\l"
    .string "altar of Baal, and because he hath\l"
    .string "cut down the grove that was by it.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_31::
    .string "And Joash said unto all that stood\n"
    .string "against him, Will ye plead for\l"
    .string "Baal? will ye save him? he that\l"
    .string "will plead for him, let him be\l"
    .string "put to death whilst it is yet\l"
    .string "morning: if he be a god, let him\l"
    .string "plead for himself, because one hath\l"
    .string "cast down his altar.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_32::
    .string "Therefore on that day he called\n"
    .string "him Jerubbaal, saying, Let Baal\l"
    .string "plead against him, because he hath\l"
    .string "thrown down his altar.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_33::
    .string "Then all the Midianites and the\n"
    .string "Amalekites and the children of the\l"
    .string "east were gathered together, and went\l"
    .string "over, and pitched in the valley of\l"
    .string "Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_34::
    .string "But the Spirit of the LORD came\n"
    .string "upon Gideon, and he blew a trumpet;\l"
    .string "and Abiezer was gathered after him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_35::
    .string "And he sent messengers throughout\n"
    .string "all Manasseh; who also was gathered\l"
    .string "after him: and he sent messengers\l"
    .string "unto Asher, and unto Zebulun, and\l"
    .string "unto Naphtali; and they came up to\l"
    .string "meet them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_36::
    .string "And Gideon said unto God, If thou\n"
    .string "wilt save Israel by mine hand, as\l"
    .string "thou hast said,"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_37::
    .string "Behold, I will put a fleece of\n"
    .string "wool in the floor; and if the dew be\l"
    .string "on the fleece only, and it be dry\l"
    .string "upon all the earth beside, then\l"
    .string "shall I know that thou wilt save\l"
    .string "Israel by mine hand, as thou hast\l"
    .string "said$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_38::
    .string "And it was so: for he rose up early\n"
    .string "on the morrow, and thrust the fleece\l"
    .string "together, and wringed the dew out of\l"
    .string "the fleece, a bowl full of water.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_39::
    .string "And Gideon said unto God, Let not\n"
    .string "thine anger be hot against me, and I\l"
    .string "will speak but this once: let me\l"
    .string "prove, I pray thee, but this once\l"
    .string "with the fleece; let it now be dry\l"
    .string "only upon the fleece, and upon\l"
    .string "all the ground let there be dew.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_6_40::
    .string "And God did so that night: for it was\n"
    .string "dry upon the fleece only, and there\l"
    .string "was dew on all the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_1::
    .string "Then Jerubbaal, who is Gideon, and\n"
    .string "all the people that were with him,\l"
    .string "rose up early, and pitched beside\l"
    .string "the well of Harod: so that the host\l"
    .string "of the Midianites were on the north\l"
    .string "side of them, by the hill of Moreh,\l"
    .string "in the valley.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Gideon, The\n"
    .string "people that are with thee are too\l"
    .string "many for me to give the Midianites\l"
    .string "into their hands, lest Israel vaunt\l"
    .string "themselves against me, saying, Mine\l"
    .string "own hand hath saved me.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_3::
    .string "Now therefore go to, proclaim in\n"
    .string "the ears of the people, saying,\l"
    .string "Whosoever is fearful and afraid,\l"
    .string "let him return and depart early\l"
    .string "from mount Gilead. And there\l"
    .string "returned of the people twenty and\l"
    .string "two thousand; and there remained ten\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_4::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Gideon, The\n"
    .string "people are yet too many; bring them\l"
    .string "down unto the water, and I will try\l"
    .string "them for thee there: and it shall\l"
    .string "be, that of whom I say unto thee, This\l"
    .string "shall go with thee, the same shall\l"
    .string "go with thee; and of whomsoever I say\l"
    .string "unto thee, This shall not go with\l"
    .string "thee, the same shall not go.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_5::
    .string "So he brought down the people unto\n"
    .string "the water: and the LORD said unto\l"
    .string "Gideon, Every one that lappeth of\l"
    .string "the water with his tongue, as a dog\l"
    .string "lappeth, him shalt thou set by\l"
    .string "himself; likewise every one that\l"
    .string "boweth down upon his knees to drink.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_6::
    .string "And the number of them that\n"
    .string "lapped, putting their hand to their\l"
    .string "mouth, were three hundred men: but\l"
    .string "all the rest of the people bowed\l"
    .string "down upon their knees to drink water.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_7::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Gideon, By\n"
    .string "the three hundred men that lapped\l"
    .string "will I save you, and deliver the\l"
    .string "Midianites into thine hand: and let\l"
    .string "all the other people go every man\l"
    .string "unto his place.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_8::
    .string "So the people took victuals in\n"
    .string "their hand, and their trumpets: and\l"
    .string "he sent all the rest of Israel\l"
    .string "every man unto his tent, and retained\l"
    .string "those three hundred men: and the host\l"
    .string "of Midian was beneath him in the\l"
    .string "valley.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_9::
    .string "And it came to pass the same night,\n"
    .string "that the LORD said unto him, Arise,\l"
    .string "get thee down unto the host; for I\l"
    .string "have delivered it into thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_10::
    .string "But if thou fear to go down, go thou\n"
    .string "with Phurah thy servant down to the\l"
    .string "host:"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_11::
    .string "And thou shalt hear what they say;\n"
    .string "and afterward shall thine hands be\l"
    .string "strengthened to go down unto the\l"
    .string "host. Then went he down with Phurah\l"
    .string "his servant unto the outside of the\l"
    .string "armed men that were in the host$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_12::
    .string "And the Midianites and the\n"
    .string "Amalekites and all the children of\l"
    .string "the east lay along in the valley\l"
    .string "like grasshoppers for multitude;\l"
    .string "and their camels were without\l"
    .string "number, as the sand by the sea side\l"
    .string "for multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_13::
    .string "And when Gideon was come, behold,\n"
    .string "there was a man that told a dream\l"
    .string "unto his fellow, and said, Behold,\l"
    .string "I dreamed a dream, and, lo, a cake of\l"
    .string "barley bread tumbled into the host\l"
    .string "of Midian, and came unto a tent, and\l"
    .string "smote it that it fell, and\l"
    .string "overturned it, that the tent lay\l"
    .string "along.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_14::
    .string "And his fellow answered and said,\n"
    .string "This is nothing else save the sword\l"
    .string "of Gideon the son of Joash, a man of\l"
    .string "Israel: for into his hand hath God\l"
    .string "delivered Midian, and all the host.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_15::
    .string "And it was so, when Gideon heard the\n"
    .string "telling of the dream, and the\l"
    .string "interpretation thereof, that he\l"
    .string "worshipped, and returned into the\l"
    .string "host of Israel, and said, Arise; for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath delivered into your\l"
    .string "hand the host of Midian.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_16::
    .string "And he divided the three hundred men\n"
    .string "into three companies, and he put a\l"
    .string "trumpet in every man’s hand, with\l"
    .string "empty pitchers, and lamps within\l"
    .string "the pitchers.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_17::
    .string "And he said unto them, Look on me,\n"
    .string "and do likewise: and, behold, when I\l"
    .string "come to the outside of the camp, it\l"
    .string "shall be that, as I do, so shall ye\l"
    .string "do.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_18::
    .string "When I blow with a trumpet, I and\n"
    .string "all that are with me, then blow ye\l"
    .string "the trumpets also on every side of\l"
    .string "all the camp, and say, The sword of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and of Gideon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_19::
    .string "So Gideon, and the hundred men that\n"
    .string "were with him, came unto the outside\l"
    .string "of the camp in the beginning of the\l"
    .string "middle watch; and they had but newly\l"
    .string "set the watch: and they blew the\l"
    .string "trumpets, and brake the pitchers\l"
    .string "that were in their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_20::
    .string "And the three companies blew the\n"
    .string "trumpets, and brake the pitchers,\l"
    .string "and held the lamps in their left\l"
    .string "hands, and the trumpets in their\l"
    .string "right hands to blow withal: and they\l"
    .string "cried, The sword of the LORD, and of\l"
    .string "Gideon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_21::
    .string "And they stood every man in his\n"
    .string "place round about the camp; and\l"
    .string "all the host ran, and cried, and\l"
    .string "fled.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_22::
    .string "And the three hundred blew the\n"
    .string "trumpets, and the LORD set every\l"
    .string "man’s sword against his fellow,\l"
    .string "even throughout all the host: and\l"
    .string "the host fled to Bethshittah in\l"
    .string "Zererath, and to the border of\l"
    .string "Abelmeholah, unto Tabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_23::
    .string "And the men of Israel gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together out of\l"
    .string "Naphtali, and out of Asher, and out\l"
    .string "of all Manasseh, and pursued after\l"
    .string "the Midianites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_24::
    .string "And Gideon sent messengers\n"
    .string "throughout all mount Ephraim,\l"
    .string "saying, come down against the\l"
    .string "Midianites, and take before them the\l"
    .string "waters unto Bethbarah and Jordan.\l"
    .string "Then all the men of Ephraim\l"
    .string "gathered themselves together, and\l"
    .string "took the waters unto Bethbarah and\l"
    .string "Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_7_25::
    .string "And they took two princes of the\n"
    .string "Midianites, Oreb and Zeeb; and they\l"
    .string "slew Oreb upon the rock Oreb, and\l"
    .string "Zeeb they slew at the winepress of\l"
    .string "Zeeb, and pursued Midian, and\l"
    .string "brought the heads of Oreb and Zeeb to\l"
    .string "Gideon on the other side Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_1::
    .string "And the men of Ephraim said unto\n"
    .string "him, Why hast thou served us thus,\l"
    .string "that thou calledst us not, when thou\l"
    .string "wentest to fight with the Midianites?\l"
    .string "And they did chide with him sharply.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_2::
    .string "And he said unto them, What have I\n"
    .string "done now in comparison of you? Is not\l"
    .string "the gleaning of the grapes of\l"
    .string "Ephraim better than the vintage of\l"
    .string "Abiezer?"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_3::
    .string "God hath delivered into your hands\n"
    .string "the princes of Midian, Oreb and\l"
    .string "Zeeb: and what was I able to do in\l"
    .string "comparison of you? Then their anger\l"
    .string "was abated toward him, when he had\l"
    .string "said that$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_4::
    .string "And Gideon came to Jordan, and\n"
    .string "passed over, he, and the three\l"
    .string "hundred men that were with him,\l"
    .string "faint, yet pursuing them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_5::
    .string "And he said unto the men of Succoth,\n"
    .string "Give, I pray you, loaves of bread\l"
    .string "unto the people that follow me;\l"
    .string "for they be faint, and I am pursuing\l"
    .string "after Zebah and Zalmunna, kings of\l"
    .string "Midian.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_6::
    .string "And the princes of Succoth said,\n"
    .string "Are the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna\l"
    .string "now in thine hand, that we should\l"
    .string "give bread unto thine army?"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_7::
    .string "And Gideon said, Therefore when the\n"
    .string "LORD hath delivered Zebah and\l"
    .string "Zalmunna into mine hand, then I\l"
    .string "will tear your flesh with the\l"
    .string "thorns of the wilderness and with\l"
    .string "briers$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_8::
    .string "And he went up thence to Penuel,\n"
    .string "and spake unto them likewise: and\l"
    .string "the men of Penuel answered him as\l"
    .string "the men of Succoth had answered him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_9::
    .string "And he spake also unto the men of\n"
    .string "Penuel, saying, When I come again in\l"
    .string "peace, I will break down this tower.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_10::
    .string "Now Zebah and Zalmunna were in\n"
    .string "Karkor, and their hosts with them,\l"
    .string "about fifteen thousand men, all\l"
    .string "that were left of all the hosts of\l"
    .string "the children of the east: for there\l"
    .string "fell an hundred and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "men that drew sword.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_11::
    .string "And Gideon went up by the way of\n"
    .string "them that dwelt in tents on the east\l"
    .string "of Nobah and Jogbehah, and smote the\l"
    .string "host; for the host was secure.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_12::
    .string "And when Zebah and Zalmunna fled,\n"
    .string "he pursued after them, and took the\l"
    .string "two kings of Midian, Zebah and\l"
    .string "Zalmunna, and discomfited all the\l"
    .string "host.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_13::
    .string "And Gideon the son of Joash returned\n"
    .string "from battle before the sun was up,"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_14::
    .string "And caught a young man of the men of\n"
    .string "Succoth, and enquired of him: and he\l"
    .string "described unto him the princes of\l"
    .string "Succoth, and the elders thereof,\l"
    .string "even threescore and seventeen men$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_15::
    .string "And he came unto the men of Succoth,\n"
    .string "and said, Behold Zebah and\l"
    .string "Zalmunna, with whom ye did upbraid\l"
    .string "me, saying, Are the hands of Zebah\l"
    .string "and Zalmunna now in thine hand, that\l"
    .string "we should give bread unto thy men\l"
    .string "that are weary?"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_16::
    .string "And he took the elders of the city,\n"
    .string "and thorns of the wilderness and\l"
    .string "briers, and with them he taught the\l"
    .string "men of Succoth$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_17::
    .string "And he beat down the tower of\n"
    .string "Penuel, and slew the men of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_18::
    .string "Then said he unto Zebah and\n"
    .string "Zalmunna, What manner of men were\l"
    .string "they whom ye slew at Tabor? And they\l"
    .string "answered, As thou art, so were they;\l"
    .string "each one resembled the children of\l"
    .string "a king.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_19::
    .string "And he said, They were my brethren,\n"
    .string "even the sons of my mother: as the\l"
    .string "LORD liveth, if ye had saved them\l"
    .string "alive, I would not slay you.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_20::
    .string "And he said unto Jether his\n"
    .string "firstborn, Up, and slay them. But\l"
    .string "the youth drew not his sword: for he\l"
    .string "feared, because he was yet a youth.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_21::
    .string "Then Zebah and Zalmunna said, Rise\n"
    .string "thou, and fall upon us: for as the\l"
    .string "man is, so is his strength. And\l"
    .string "Gideon arose, and slew Zebah and\l"
    .string "Zalmunna, and took away the\l"
    .string "ornaments that were on their camels’\l"
    .string "necks.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_22::
    .string "Then the men of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Gideon, Rule thou over us, both thou,\l"
    .string "and thy son, and thy son’s son also:\l"
    .string "for thou hast delivered us from the\l"
    .string "hand of Midian.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_23::
    .string "And Gideon said unto them, I will\n"
    .string "not rule over you, neither shall my\l"
    .string "son rule over you: the LORD shall\l"
    .string "rule over you.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_24::
    .string "And Gideon said unto them, I would\n"
    .string "desire a request of you, that ye\l"
    .string "would give me every man the earrings\l"
    .string "of his prey. (For they had golden\l"
    .string "earrings, because they were\l"
    .string "Ishmaelites.)"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_25::
    .string "And they answered, We will\n"
    .string "willingly give them. And they\l"
    .string "spread a garment, and did cast\l"
    .string "therein every man the earrings of his\l"
    .string "prey$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_26::
    .string "And the weight of the golden\n"
    .string "earrings that he requested was a\l"
    .string "thousand and seven hundred shekels\l"
    .string "of gold; beside ornaments, and\l"
    .string "collars, and purple raiment that\l"
    .string "was on the kings of Midian, and\l"
    .string "beside the chains that were about\l"
    .string "their camels’ necks.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_27::
    .string "And Gideon made an ephod thereof,\n"
    .string "and put it in his city, even in\l"
    .string "Ophrah: and all Israel went\l"
    .string "thither a whoring after it: which\l"
    .string "thing became a snare unto Gideon, and\l"
    .string "to his house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_28::
    .string "Thus was Midian subdued before the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, so that they\l"
    .string "lifted up their heads no more. And\l"
    .string "the country was in quietness forty\l"
    .string "years in the days of Gideon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_29::
    .string "And Jerubbaal the son of Joash went\n"
    .string "and dwelt in his own house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_30::
    .string "And Gideon had threescore and ten\n"
    .string "sons of his body begotten: for he had\l"
    .string "many wives.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_31::
    .string "And his concubine that was in\n"
    .string "Shechem, she also bare him a son,\l"
    .string "whose name he called Abimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_32::
    .string "And Gideon the son of Joash died in\n"
    .string "a good old age, and was buried in the\l"
    .string "sepulchre of Joash his father, in\l"
    .string "Ophrah of the Abiezrites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_33::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as\n"
    .string "Gideon was dead, that the children\l"
    .string "of Israel turned again, and went a\l"
    .string "whoring after Baalim, and made\l"
    .string "Baalberith their god.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_34::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "remembered not the LORD their God,\l"
    .string "who had delivered them out of the\l"
    .string "hands of all their enemies on every\l"
    .string "side:"
Bible_Text_Judges_8_35::
    .string "Neither shewed they kindness to the\n"
    .string "house of Jerubbaal, namely, Gideon,\l"
    .string "according to all the goodness which\l"
    .string "he had shewed unto Israel$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_1::
    .string "And Abimelech the son of Jerubbaal\n"
    .string "went to Shechem unto his mother’s\l"
    .string "brethren, and communed with them, and\l"
    .string "with all the family of the house of\l"
    .string "his mother’s father, saying,"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_2::
    .string "Speak, I pray you, in the ears of\n"
    .string "all the men of Shechem, Whether is\l"
    .string "better for you, either that all the\l"
    .string "sons of Jerubbaal, which are\l"
    .string "threescore and ten persons, reign\l"
    .string "over you, or that one reign over you?\l"
    .string "remember also that I am your bone\l"
    .string "and your flesh$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_3::
    .string "And his mother’s brethren spake of\n"
    .string "him in the ears of all the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem all these words: and their\l"
    .string "hearts inclined to follow\l"
    .string "Abimelech; for they said, He is our\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_4::
    .string "And they gave him threescore and ten\n"
    .string "pieces of silver out of the house of\l"
    .string "Baalberith, wherewith Abimelech\l"
    .string "hired vain and light persons, which\l"
    .string "followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_5::
    .string "And he went unto his father’s house\n"
    .string "at Ophrah, and slew his brethren the\l"
    .string "sons of Jerubbaal, being threescore\l"
    .string "and ten persons, upon one stone:\l"
    .string "notwithstanding yet Jotham the\l"
    .string "youngest son of Jerubbaal was left;\l"
    .string "for he hid himself.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_6::
    .string "And all the men of Shechem\n"
    .string "gathered together, and all the\l"
    .string "house of Millo, and went, and made\l"
    .string "Abimelech king, by the plain of the\l"
    .string "pillar that was in Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_7::
    .string "And when they told it to Jotham, he\n"
    .string "went and stood in the top of mount\l"
    .string "Gerizim, and lifted up his voice,\l"
    .string "and cried, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Hearken unto me, ye men of Shechem,\l"
    .string "that God may hearken unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_8::
    .string "The trees went forth on a time to\n"
    .string "anoint a king over them; and they\l"
    .string "said unto the olive tree, Reign thou\l"
    .string "over us.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_9::
    .string "But the olive tree said unto them,\n"
    .string "Should I leave my fatness,\l"
    .string "wherewith by me they honour God and\l"
    .string "man, and go to be promoted over the\l"
    .string "trees?"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_10::
    .string "And the trees said to the fig tree,\n"
    .string "Come thou, and reign over us$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_11::
    .string "But the fig tree said unto them,\n"
    .string "Should I forsake my sweetness, and\l"
    .string "my good fruit, and go to be promoted\l"
    .string "over the trees?"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_12::
    .string "Then said the trees unto the vine,\n"
    .string "Come thou, and reign over us$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_13::
    .string "And the vine said unto them, Should\n"
    .string "I leave my wine, which cheereth God\l"
    .string "and man, and go to be promoted over\l"
    .string "the trees?"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_14::
    .string "Then said all the trees unto the\n"
    .string "bramble, Come thou, and reign over us$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_15::
    .string "And the bramble said unto the\n"
    .string "trees, If in truth ye anoint me king\l"
    .string "over you, then come and put your\l"
    .string "trust in my shadow: and if not, let\l"
    .string "fire come out of the bramble, and\l"
    .string "devour the cedars of Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_16::
    .string "Now therefore, if ye have done\n"
    .string "truly and sincerely, in that ye have\l"
    .string "made Abimelech king, and if ye have\l"
    .string "dealt well with Jerubbaal and his\l"
    .string "house, and have done unto him\l"
    .string "according to the deserving of his\l"
    .string "hands;"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_17::
    .string "(For my father fought for you, and\n"
    .string "adventured his life far, and\l"
    .string "delivered you out of the hand of\l"
    .string "Midian:"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_18::
    .string "And ye are risen up against my\n"
    .string "father’s house this day, and have\l"
    .string "slain his sons, threescore and ten\l"
    .string "persons, upon one stone, and have\l"
    .string "made Abimelech, the son of his\l"
    .string "maidservant, king over the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem, because he is your brother;)"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_19::
    .string "If ye then have dealt truly and\n"
    .string "sincerely with Jerubbaal and with\l"
    .string "his house this day, then rejoice ye\l"
    .string "in Abimelech, and let him also\l"
    .string "rejoice in you:"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_20::
    .string "But if not, let fire come out from\n"
    .string "Abimelech, and devour the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem, and the house of Millo; and\l"
    .string "let fire come out from the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem, and from the house of\l"
    .string "Millo, and devour Abimelech$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_21::
    .string "And Jotham ran away, and fled, and\n"
    .string "went to Beer, and dwelt there, for\l"
    .string "fear of Abimelech his brother.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_22::
    .string "When Abimelech had reigned three\n"
    .string "years over Israel,"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_23::
    .string "Then God sent an evil spirit\n"
    .string "between Abimelech and the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem; and the men of Shechem\l"
    .string "dealt treacherously with\l"
    .string "Abimelech:"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_24::
    .string "That the cruelty done to the\n"
    .string "threescore and ten sons of Jerubbaal\l"
    .string "might come, and their blood be laid\l"
    .string "upon Abimelech their brother, which\l"
    .string "slew them; and upon the men of\l"
    .string "Shechem, which aided him in the\l"
    .string "killing of his brethren$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_25::
    .string "And the men of Shechem set liers in\n"
    .string "wait for him in the top of the\l"
    .string "mountains, and they robbed all that\l"
    .string "came along that way by them: and it\l"
    .string "was told Abimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_26::
    .string "And Gaal the son of Ebed came with\n"
    .string "his brethren, and went over to\l"
    .string "Shechem: and the men of Shechem put\l"
    .string "their confidence in him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_27::
    .string "And they went out into the fields,\n"
    .string "and gathered their vineyards, and\l"
    .string "trode the grapes, and made merry,\l"
    .string "and went into the house of their god,\l"
    .string "and did eat and drink, and cursed\l"
    .string "Abimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_28::
    .string "And Gaal the son of Ebed said, Who\n"
    .string "is Abimelech, and who is Shechem,\l"
    .string "that we should serve him? is not he\l"
    .string "the son of Jerubbaal? and Zebul his\l"
    .string "officer? serve the men of Hamor the\l"
    .string "father of Shechem: for why should we\l"
    .string "serve him?"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_29::
    .string "And would to God this people were\n"
    .string "under my hand! then would I remove\l"
    .string "Abimelech. And he said to\l"
    .string "Abimelech, Increase thine army, and\l"
    .string "come out$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_30::
    .string "And when Zebul the ruler of the\n"
    .string "city heard the words of Gaal the son\l"
    .string "of Ebed, his anger was kindled.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_31::
    .string "And he sent messengers unto\n"
    .string "Abimelech privily, saying, Behold,\l"
    .string "Gaal the son of Ebed and his\l"
    .string "brethren be come to Shechem; and,\l"
    .string "behold, they fortify the city\l"
    .string "against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_32::
    .string "Now therefore up by night, thou and\n"
    .string "the people that is with thee, and\l"
    .string "lie in wait in the field:"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_33::
    .string "And it shall be, that in the\n"
    .string "morning, as soon as the sun is up,\l"
    .string "thou shalt rise early, and set upon\l"
    .string "the city: and, behold, when he and\l"
    .string "the people that is with him come\l"
    .string "out against thee, then mayest thou do\l"
    .string "to them as thou shalt find occasion$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_34::
    .string "And Abimelech rose up, and all\n"
    .string "the people that were with him, by\l"
    .string "night, and they laid wait against\l"
    .string "Shechem in four companies.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_35::
    .string "And Gaal the son of Ebed went out,\n"
    .string "and stood in the entering of the gate\l"
    .string "of the city: and Abimelech rose up,\l"
    .string "and the people that were with him,\l"
    .string "from lying in wait.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_36::
    .string "And when Gaal saw the people, he\n"
    .string "said to Zebul, Behold, there come\l"
    .string "people down from the top of the\l"
    .string "mountains. And Zebul said unto him,\l"
    .string "Thou seest the shadow of the\l"
    .string "mountains as if they were men.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_37::
    .string "And Gaal spake again, and said, See\n"
    .string "there come people down by the\l"
    .string "middle of the land, and another\l"
    .string "company come along by the plain of\l"
    .string "Meonenim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_38::
    .string "Then said Zebul unto him, Where is\n"
    .string "now thy mouth, wherewith thou saidst,\l"
    .string "Who is Abimelech, that we should\l"
    .string "serve him? is not this the people\l"
    .string "that thou hast despised? go out, I\l"
    .string "pray now, and fight with them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_39::
    .string "And Gaal went out before the men of\n"
    .string "Shechem, and fought with Abimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_40::
    .string "And Abimelech chased him, and he\n"
    .string "fled before him, and many were\l"
    .string "overthrown and wounded, even unto the\l"
    .string "entering of the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_41::
    .string "And Abimelech dwelt at Arumah: and\n"
    .string "Zebul thrust out Gaal and his\l"
    .string "brethren, that they should not\l"
    .string "dwell in Shechem.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_42::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that the people went out into the\l"
    .string "field; and they told Abimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_43::
    .string "And he took the people, and\n"
    .string "divided them into three companies,\l"
    .string "and laid wait in the field, and\l"
    .string "looked, and, behold, the people\l"
    .string "were come forth out of the city; and\l"
    .string "he rose up against them, and smote\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_44::
    .string "And Abimelech, and the company\n"
    .string "that was with him, rushed forward,\l"
    .string "and stood in the entering of the gate\l"
    .string "of the city: and the two other\l"
    .string "companies ran upon all the\l"
    .string "people that were in the fields, and\l"
    .string "slew them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_45::
    .string "And Abimelech fought against the\n"
    .string "city all that day; and he took the\l"
    .string "city, and slew the people that was\l"
    .string "therein, and beat down the city, and\l"
    .string "sowed it with salt.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_46::
    .string "And when all the men of the tower\n"
    .string "of Shechem heard that, they entered\l"
    .string "into an hold of the house of the god\l"
    .string "Berith.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_47::
    .string "And it was told Abimelech, that\n"
    .string "all the men of the tower of Shechem\l"
    .string "were gathered together.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_48::
    .string "And Abimelech gat him up to mount\n"
    .string "Zalmon, he and all the people\l"
    .string "that were with him; and Abimelech\l"
    .string "took an axe in his hand, and cut down\l"
    .string "a bough from the trees, and took it,\l"
    .string "and laid it on his shoulder, and\l"
    .string "said unto the people that were with\l"
    .string "him, What ye have seen me do, make\l"
    .string "haste, and do as I have done.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_49::
    .string "And all the people likewise cut\n"
    .string "down every man his bough, and\l"
    .string "followed Abimelech, and put them\l"
    .string "to the hold, and set the hold on\l"
    .string "fire upon them; so that all the men\l"
    .string "of the tower of Shechem died also,\l"
    .string "about a thousand men and women.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_50::
    .string "Then went Abimelech to Thebez, and\n"
    .string "encamped against Thebez, and took it.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_51::
    .string "But there was a strong tower within\n"
    .string "the city, and thither fled all the\l"
    .string "men and women, and all they of the\l"
    .string "city, and shut it to them, and gat\l"
    .string "them up to the top of the tower.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_52::
    .string "And Abimelech came unto the tower,\n"
    .string "and fought against it, and went hard\l"
    .string "unto the door of the tower to burn it\l"
    .string "with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_53::
    .string "And a certain woman cast a piece of\n"
    .string "a millstone upon Abimelech’s head,\l"
    .string "and all to brake his skull.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_54::
    .string "Then he called hastily unto the\n"
    .string "young man his armourbearer, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Draw thy sword, and slay\l"
    .string "me, that men say not of me, A women\l"
    .string "slew him. And his young man thrust\l"
    .string "him through, and he died.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_55::
    .string "And when the men of Israel saw that\n"
    .string "Abimelech was dead, they departed\l"
    .string "every man unto his place.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_56::
    .string "Thus God rendered the wickedness of\n"
    .string "Abimelech, which he did unto his\l"
    .string "father, in slaying his seventy\l"
    .string "brethren:"
Bible_Text_Judges_9_57::
    .string "And all the evil of the men of\n"
    .string "Shechem did God render upon their\l"
    .string "heads: and upon them came the curse\l"
    .string "of Jotham the son of Jerubbaal$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_1::
    .string "And after Abimelech there arose to\n"
    .string "defend Israel Tola the son of Puah,\l"
    .string "the son of Dodo, a man of Issachar;\l"
    .string "and he dwelt in Shamir in mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_2::
    .string "And he judged Israel twenty and\n"
    .string "three years, and died, and was buried\l"
    .string "in Shamir.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_3::
    .string "And after him arose Jair, a\n"
    .string "Gileadite, and judged Israel twenty\l"
    .string "and two years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_4::
    .string "And he had thirty sons that rode on\n"
    .string "thirty ass colts, and they had\l"
    .string "thirty cities, which are called\l"
    .string "Havothjair unto this day, which are\l"
    .string "in the land of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_5::
    .string "And Jair died, and was buried in\n"
    .string "Camon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_6::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil again in the sight of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and served Baalim, and Ashtaroth,\l"
    .string "and the gods of Syria, and the gods of\l"
    .string "Zidon, and the gods of Moab, and the\l"
    .string "gods of the children of Ammon, and\l"
    .string "the gods of the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "forsook the LORD, and served not him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_7::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was hot\n"
    .string "against Israel, and he sold them\l"
    .string "into the hands of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "and into the hands of the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_8::
    .string "And that year they vexed and\n"
    .string "oppressed the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "eighteen years, all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel that were on the other side\l"
    .string "Jordan in the land of the Amorites,\l"
    .string "which is in Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_9::
    .string "Moreover the children of Ammon\n"
    .string "passed over Jordan to fight also\l"
    .string "against Judah, and against Benjamin,\l"
    .string "and against the house of Ephraim; so\l"
    .string "that Israel was sore distressed.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_10::
    .string "And the children of Israel cried\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, saying, We have sinned\l"
    .string "against thee, both because we have\l"
    .string "forsaken our God, and also served\l"
    .string "Baalim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_11::
    .string "And the LORD said unto the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, Did not I deliver you\l"
    .string "from the Egyptians, and from the\l"
    .string "Amorites, from the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, and from the Philistines?"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_12::
    .string "The Zidonians also, and the\n"
    .string "Amalekites, and the Maonites, did\l"
    .string "oppress you; and ye cried to me, and\l"
    .string "I delivered you out of their hand$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_13::
    .string "Yet ye have forsaken me, and served\n"
    .string "other gods: wherefore I will\l"
    .string "deliver you no more.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_14::
    .string "Go and cry unto the gods which ye\n"
    .string "have chosen; let them deliver you in\l"
    .string "the time of your tribulation.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_15::
    .string "And the children of Israel said\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, We have sinned: do\l"
    .string "thou unto us whatsoever seemeth good\l"
    .string "unto thee; deliver us only, we pray\l"
    .string "thee, this day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_16::
    .string "And they put away the strange gods\n"
    .string "from among them, and served the LORD:\l"
    .string "and his soul was grieved for the\l"
    .string "misery of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_17::
    .string "Then the children of Ammon were\n"
    .string "gathered together, and encamped in\l"
    .string "Gilead. And the children of Israel\l"
    .string "assembled themselves together, and\l"
    .string "encamped in Mizpeh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_10_18::
    .string "And the people and princes of\n"
    .string "Gilead said one to another, What man\l"
    .string "is he that will begin to fight\l"
    .string "against the children of Ammon? he\l"
    .string "shall be head over all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_1::
    .string "Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a\n"
    .string "mighty man of valour, and he was the\l"
    .string "son of an harlot: and Gilead begat\l"
    .string "Jephthah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_2::
    .string "And Gilead’s wife bare him sons;\n"
    .string "and his wife’s sons grew up, and they\l"
    .string "thrust out Jephthah, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Thou shalt not inherit in our\l"
    .string "father’s house; for thou art the son\l"
    .string "of a strange woman.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_3::
    .string "Then Jephthah fled from his\n"
    .string "brethren, and dwelt in the land of\l"
    .string "Tob: and there were gathered vain men\l"
    .string "to Jephthah, and went out with him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_4::
    .string "And it came to pass in process of\n"
    .string "time, that the children of Ammon\l"
    .string "made war against Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_5::
    .string "And it was so, that when the\n"
    .string "children of Ammon made war against\l"
    .string "Israel, the elders of Gilead went\l"
    .string "to fetch Jephthah out of the land of\l"
    .string "Tob:"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_6::
    .string "And they said unto Jephthah, Come,\n"
    .string "and be our captain, that we may fight\l"
    .string "with the children of Ammon$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_7::
    .string "And Jephthah said unto the elders\n"
    .string "of Gilead, Did not ye hate me, and\l"
    .string "expel me out of my father’s house?\l"
    .string "and why are ye come unto me now when\l"
    .string "ye are in distress?"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_8::
    .string "And the elders of Gilead said unto\n"
    .string "Jephthah, Therefore we turn again to\l"
    .string "thee now, that thou mayest go with\l"
    .string "us, and fight against the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon, and be our head over all\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Gilead$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_9::
    .string "And Jephthah said unto the elders\n"
    .string "of Gilead, If ye bring me home again\l"
    .string "to fight against the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, and the LORD deliver them\l"
    .string "before me, shall I be your head?"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_10::
    .string "And the elders of Gilead said unto\n"
    .string "Jephthah, The LORD be witness\l"
    .string "between us, if we do not so according\l"
    .string "to thy words$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_11::
    .string "Then Jephthah went with the elders\n"
    .string "of Gilead, and the people made him\l"
    .string "head and captain over them: and\l"
    .string "Jephthah uttered all his words\l"
    .string "before the LORD in Mizpeh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_12::
    .string "And Jephthah sent messengers unto\n"
    .string "the king of the children of Ammon,\l"
    .string "saying, What hast thou to do with me,\l"
    .string "that thou art come against me to\l"
    .string "fight in my land?"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_13::
    .string "And the king of the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon answered unto the messengers\l"
    .string "of Jephthah, Because Israel took\l"
    .string "away my land, when they came up out\l"
    .string "of Egypt, from Arnon even unto\l"
    .string "Jabbok, and unto Jordan: now\l"
    .string "therefore restore those lands again\l"
    .string "peaceably$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_14::
    .string "And Jephthah sent messengers again\n"
    .string "unto the king of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon:"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_15::
    .string "And said unto him, Thus saith\n"
    .string "Jephthah, Israel took not away the\l"
    .string "land of Moab, nor the land of the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon:"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_16::
    .string "But when Israel came up from\n"
    .string "Egypt, and walked through the\l"
    .string "wilderness unto the Red sea, and\l"
    .string "came to Kadesh;"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_17::
    .string "Then Israel sent messengers unto\n"
    .string "the king of Edom, saying, Let me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, pass through thy land:\l"
    .string "but the king of Edom would not\l"
    .string "hearken thereto. And in like manner\l"
    .string "they sent unto the king of Moab: but\l"
    .string "he would not consent: and Israel\l"
    .string "abode in Kadesh$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_18::
    .string "Then they went along through the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and compassed the land\l"
    .string "of Edom, and the land of Moab, and\l"
    .string "came by the east side of the land of\l"
    .string "Moab, and pitched on the other side\l"
    .string "of Arnon, but came not within the\l"
    .string "border of Moab: for Arnon was the\l"
    .string "border of Moab.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_19::
    .string "And Israel sent messengers unto\n"
    .string "Sihon king of the Amorites, the king\l"
    .string "of Heshbon; and Israel said unto\l"
    .string "him, Let us pass, we pray thee,\l"
    .string "through thy land into my place.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_20::
    .string "But Sihon trusted not Israel to\n"
    .string "pass through his coast: but Sihon\l"
    .string "gathered all his people together,\l"
    .string "and pitched in Jahaz, and fought\l"
    .string "against Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_21::
    .string "And the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "delivered Sihon and all his\l"
    .string "people into the hand of Israel, and\l"
    .string "they smote them: so Israel\l"
    .string "possessed all the land of the\l"
    .string "Amorites, the inhabitants of that\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_22::
    .string "And they possessed all the coasts\n"
    .string "of the Amorites, from Arnon even unto\l"
    .string "Jabbok, and from the wilderness even\l"
    .string "unto Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_23::
    .string "So now the LORD God of Israel hath\n"
    .string "dispossessed the Amorites from\l"
    .string "before his people Israel, and\l"
    .string "shouldest thou possess it?"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_24::
    .string "Wilt not thou possess that which\n"
    .string "Chemosh thy god giveth thee to\l"
    .string "possess? So whomsoever the LORD our\l"
    .string "God shall drive out from before us,\l"
    .string "them will we possess$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_25::
    .string "And now art thou any thing better\n"
    .string "than Balak the son of Zippor, king\l"
    .string "of Moab? did he ever strive against\l"
    .string "Israel, or did he ever fight against\l"
    .string "them,"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_26::
    .string "While Israel dwelt in Heshbon and\n"
    .string "her towns, and in Aroer and her\l"
    .string "towns, and in all the cities that be\l"
    .string "along by the coasts of Arnon, three\l"
    .string "hundred years? why therefore did ye\l"
    .string "not recover them within that time?"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_27::
    .string "Wherefore I have not sinned against\n"
    .string "thee, but thou doest me wrong to war\l"
    .string "against me: the LORD the Judge be\l"
    .string "judge this day between the children\l"
    .string "of Israel and the children of Ammon$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_28::
    .string "Howbeit the king of the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon hearkened not unto the words of\l"
    .string "Jephthah which he sent him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_29::
    .string "Then the Spirit of the LORD came\n"
    .string "upon Jephthah, and he passed over\l"
    .string "Gilead, and Manasseh, and passed\l"
    .string "over Mizpeh of Gilead, and from\l"
    .string "Mizpeh of Gilead he passed over\l"
    .string "unto the children of Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_30::
    .string "And Jephthah vowed a vow unto the\n"
    .string "LORD, and said, If thou shalt\l"
    .string "without fail deliver the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon into mine hands,"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_31::
    .string "Then it shall be, that whatsoever\n"
    .string "cometh forth of the doors of my house\l"
    .string "to meet me, when I return in peace\l"
    .string "from the children of Ammon, shall\l"
    .string "surely be the LORD’s, and I will\l"
    .string "offer it up for a burnt offering$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_32::
    .string "So Jephthah passed over unto the\n"
    .string "children of Ammon to fight against\l"
    .string "them; and the LORD delivered them\l"
    .string "into his hands.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_33::
    .string "And he smote them from Aroer, even\n"
    .string "till thou come to Minnith, even\l"
    .string "twenty cities, and unto the plain of\l"
    .string "the vineyards, with a very great\l"
    .string "slaughter. Thus the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon were subdued before the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_34::
    .string "And Jephthah came to Mizpeh unto\n"
    .string "his house, and, behold, his daughter\l"
    .string "came out to meet him with timbrels\l"
    .string "and with dances: and she was his only\l"
    .string "child; beside her he had neither son\l"
    .string "nor daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_35::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he saw\n"
    .string "her, that he rent his clothes, and\l"
    .string "said, Alas, my daughter! thou hast\l"
    .string "brought me very low, and thou art one\l"
    .string "of them that trouble me: for I have\l"
    .string "opened my mouth unto the LORD, and I\l"
    .string "cannot go back.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_36::
    .string "And she said unto him, My father, if\n"
    .string "thou hast opened thy mouth unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, do to me according to that\l"
    .string "which hath proceeded out of thy\l"
    .string "mouth; forasmuch as the LORD hath\l"
    .string "taken vengeance for thee of thine\l"
    .string "enemies, even of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_37::
    .string "And she said unto her father, Let\n"
    .string "this thing be done for me: let me\l"
    .string "alone two months, that I may go up\l"
    .string "and down upon the mountains, and\l"
    .string "bewail my virginity, I and my\l"
    .string "fellows.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_38::
    .string "And he said, Go. And he sent her away\n"
    .string "for two months: and she went with her\l"
    .string "companions, and bewailed her\l"
    .string "virginity upon the mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_39::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "two months, that she returned unto\l"
    .string "her father, who did with her\l"
    .string "according to his vow which he had\l"
    .string "vowed: and she knew no man. And it was\l"
    .string "a custom in Israel,"
Bible_Text_Judges_11_40::
    .string "That the daughters of Israel went\n"
    .string "yearly to lament the daughter of\l"
    .string "Jephthah the Gileadite four days in\l"
    .string "a year$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_1::
    .string "And the men of Ephraim gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together, and went\l"
    .string "northward, and said unto Jephthah,\l"
    .string "Wherefore passedst thou over to\l"
    .string "fight against the children of Ammon,\l"
    .string "and didst not call us to go with\l"
    .string "thee? we will burn thine house upon\l"
    .string "thee with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_2::
    .string "And Jephthah said unto them, I and\n"
    .string "my people were at great strife with\l"
    .string "the children of Ammon; and when I\l"
    .string "called you, ye delivered me not out\l"
    .string "of their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_3::
    .string "And when I saw that ye delivered me\n"
    .string "not, I put my life in my hands, and\l"
    .string "passed over against the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, and the LORD delivered them\l"
    .string "into my hand: wherefore then are ye\l"
    .string "come up unto me this day, to fight\l"
    .string "against me?"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_4::
    .string "Then Jephthah gathered together\n"
    .string "all the men of Gilead, and fought\l"
    .string "with Ephraim: and the men of Gilead\l"
    .string "smote Ephraim, because they said, Ye\l"
    .string "Gileadites are fugitives of Ephraim\l"
    .string "among the Ephraimites, and among the\l"
    .string "Manassites$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_5::
    .string "And the Gileadites took the\n"
    .string "passages of Jordan before the\l"
    .string "Ephraimites: and it was so, that\l"
    .string "when those Ephraimites which were\l"
    .string "escaped said, Let me go over; that\l"
    .string "the men of Gilead said unto him, Art\l"
    .string "thou an Ephraimite? If he said, Nay;"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_6::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Say now\n"
    .string "Shibboleth: and he said Sibboleth:\l"
    .string "for he could not frame to pronounce\l"
    .string "it right. Then they took him, and\l"
    .string "slew him at the passages of Jordan:\l"
    .string "and there fell at that time of the\l"
    .string "Ephraimites forty and two thousand$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_7::
    .string "And Jephthah judged Israel six\n"
    .string "years. Then died Jephthah the\l"
    .string "Gileadite, and was buried in one of\l"
    .string "the cities of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_8::
    .string "And after him Ibzan of Bethlehem\n"
    .string "judged Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_9::
    .string "And he had thirty sons, and thirty\n"
    .string "daughters, whom he sent abroad, and\l"
    .string "took in thirty daughters from abroad\l"
    .string "for his sons. And he judged Israel\l"
    .string "seven years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_10::
    .string "Then died Ibzan, and was buried at\n"
    .string "Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_11::
    .string "And after him Elon, a Zebulonite,\n"
    .string "judged Israel; and he judged Israel\l"
    .string "ten years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_12::
    .string "And Elon the Zebulonite died, and\n"
    .string "was buried in Aijalon in the country\l"
    .string "of Zebulun.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_13::
    .string "And after him Abdon the son of\n"
    .string "Hillel, a Pirathonite, judged\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_14::
    .string "And he had forty sons and thirty\n"
    .string "nephews, that rode on threescore and\l"
    .string "ten ass colts: and he judged Israel\l"
    .string "eight years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_12_15::
    .string "And Abdon the son of Hillel the\n"
    .string "Pirathonite died, and was buried in\l"
    .string "Pirathon in the land of Ephraim, in\l"
    .string "the mount of the Amalekites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_1::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "evil again in the sight of the LORD;\l"
    .string "and the LORD delivered them into the\l"
    .string "hand of the Philistines forty years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_2::
    .string "And there was a certain man of\n"
    .string "Zorah, of the family of the Danites,\l"
    .string "whose name was Manoah; and his wife\l"
    .string "was barren, and bare not.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_3::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD appeared\n"
    .string "unto the woman, and said unto her,\l"
    .string "Behold now, thou art barren, and\l"
    .string "bearest not: but thou shalt\l"
    .string "conceive, and bear a son.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_4::
    .string "Now therefore beware, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "and drink not wine nor strong drink,\l"
    .string "and eat not any unclean thing:"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_5::
    .string "For, lo, thou shalt conceive, and\n"
    .string "bear a son; and no razor shall come\l"
    .string "on his head: for the child shall be\l"
    .string "a Nazarite unto God from the womb:\l"
    .string "and he shall begin to deliver\l"
    .string "Israel out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_6::
    .string "Then the woman came and told her\n"
    .string "husband, saying, A man of God came\l"
    .string "unto me, and his countenance was\l"
    .string "like the countenance of an angel of\l"
    .string "God, very terrible: but I asked him\l"
    .string "not whence he was, neither told he me\l"
    .string "his name:"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_7::
    .string "But he said unto me, Behold, thou\n"
    .string "shalt conceive, and bear a son; and\l"
    .string "now drink no wine nor strong drink,\l"
    .string "neither eat any unclean thing: for\l"
    .string "the child shall be a Nazarite to\l"
    .string "God from the womb to the day of his\l"
    .string "death$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_8::
    .string "Then Manoah intreated the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, O my Lord, let the man of God\l"
    .string "which thou didst send come again unto\l"
    .string "us, and teach us what we shall do\l"
    .string "unto the child that shall be born.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_9::
    .string "And God hearkened to the voice of\n"
    .string "Manoah; and the angel of God came\l"
    .string "again unto the woman as she sat in\l"
    .string "the field: but Manoah her husband\l"
    .string "was not with her.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_10::
    .string "And the woman made haste, and ran,\n"
    .string "and shewed her husband, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Behold, the man hath appeared\l"
    .string "unto me, that came unto me the other\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_11::
    .string "And Manoah arose, and went after his\n"
    .string "wife, and came to the man, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Art thou the man that\l"
    .string "spakest unto the woman? And he said,\l"
    .string "I am.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_12::
    .string "And Manoah said, Now let thy words\n"
    .string "come to pass. How shall we order\l"
    .string "the child, and how shall we do unto\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_13::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "Manoah, Of all that I said unto the\l"
    .string "woman let her beware$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_14::
    .string "She may not eat of any thing that\n"
    .string "cometh of the vine, neither let her\l"
    .string "drink wine or strong drink, nor eat\l"
    .string "any unclean thing: all that I\l"
    .string "commanded her let her observe.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_15::
    .string "And Manoah said unto the angel of\n"
    .string "the LORD, I pray thee, let us detain\l"
    .string "thee, until we shall have made\l"
    .string "ready a kid for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_16::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "Manoah, Though thou detain me, I\l"
    .string "will not eat of thy bread: and if\l"
    .string "thou wilt offer a burnt offering,\l"
    .string "thou must offer it unto the LORD. For\l"
    .string "Manoah knew not that he was an angel\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_17::
    .string "And Manoah said unto the angel of\n"
    .string "the LORD, What is thy name, that when\l"
    .string "thy sayings come to pass we may do\l"
    .string "thee honour?"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_18::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "him, Why askest thou thus after my\l"
    .string "name, seeing it is secret?"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_19::
    .string "So Manoah took a kid with a meat\n"
    .string "offering, and offered it upon a rock\l"
    .string "unto the LORD: and the angel did\l"
    .string "wonderously; and Manoah and his wife\l"
    .string "looked on$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_20::
    .string "For it came to pass, when the flame\n"
    .string "went up toward heaven from off the\l"
    .string "altar, that the angel of the LORD\l"
    .string "ascended in the flame of the altar.\l"
    .string "And Manoah and his wife looked on it,\l"
    .string "and fell on their faces to the\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_21::
    .string "But the angel of the LORD did no\n"
    .string "more appear to Manoah and to his\l"
    .string "wife. Then Manoah knew that he was an\l"
    .string "angel of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_22::
    .string "And Manoah said unto his wife, We\n"
    .string "shall surely die, because we have\l"
    .string "seen God.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_23::
    .string "But his wife said unto him, If the\n"
    .string "LORD were pleased to kill us, he\l"
    .string "would not have received a burnt\l"
    .string "offering and a meat offering at our\l"
    .string "hands, neither would he have shewed\l"
    .string "us all these things, nor would as\l"
    .string "at this time have told us such\l"
    .string "things as these.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_24::
    .string "And the woman bare a son, and\n"
    .string "called his name Samson: and the\l"
    .string "child grew, and the LORD blessed\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_13_25::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD began to\n"
    .string "move him at times in the camp of Dan\l"
    .string "between Zorah and Eshtaol.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_1::
    .string "And Samson went down to Timnath, and\n"
    .string "saw a woman in Timnath of the\l"
    .string "daughters of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_2::
    .string "And he came up, and told his father\n"
    .string "and his mother, and said, I have seen\l"
    .string "a woman in Timnath of the daughters\l"
    .string "of the Philistines: now therefore\l"
    .string "get her for me to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_3::
    .string "Then his father and his mother said\n"
    .string "unto him, Is there never a woman\l"
    .string "among the daughters of thy brethren,\l"
    .string "or among all my people, that thou\l"
    .string "goest to take a wife of the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised Philistines? And\l"
    .string "Samson said unto his father, Get her\l"
    .string "for me; for she pleaseth me well.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_4::
    .string "But his father and his mother knew\n"
    .string "not that it was of the LORD, that he\l"
    .string "sought an occasion against the\l"
    .string "Philistines: for at that time the\l"
    .string "Philistines had dominion over\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_5::
    .string "Then went Samson down, and his\n"
    .string "father and his mother, to Timnath,\l"
    .string "and came to the vineyards of Timnath:\l"
    .string "and, behold, a young lion roared\l"
    .string "against him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_6::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD came\n"
    .string "mightily upon him, and he rent him\l"
    .string "as he would have rent a kid, and he\l"
    .string "had nothing in his hand: but he told\l"
    .string "not his father or his mother what he\l"
    .string "had done.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_7::
    .string "And he went down, and talked with\n"
    .string "the woman; and she pleased Samson\l"
    .string "well.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_8::
    .string "And after a time he returned to take\n"
    .string "her, and he turned aside to see the\l"
    .string "carcase of the lion: and, behold,\l"
    .string "there was a swarm of bees and honey\l"
    .string "in the carcase of the lion.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_9::
    .string "And he took thereof in his hands,\n"
    .string "and went on eating, and came to his\l"
    .string "father and mother, and he gave them,\l"
    .string "and they did eat: but he told not\l"
    .string "them that he had taken the honey out\l"
    .string "of the carcase of the lion.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_10::
    .string "So his father went down unto the\n"
    .string "woman: and Samson made there a feast;\l"
    .string "for so used the young men to do.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they saw\n"
    .string "him, that they brought thirty\l"
    .string "companions to be with him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_12::
    .string "And Samson said unto them, I will\n"
    .string "now put forth a riddle unto you: if\l"
    .string "ye can certainly declare it me\l"
    .string "within the seven days of the feast,\l"
    .string "and find it out, then I will give\l"
    .string "you thirty sheets and thirty change\l"
    .string "of garments:"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_13::
    .string "But if ye cannot declare it me, then\n"
    .string "shall ye give me thirty sheets and\l"
    .string "thirty change of garments. And they\l"
    .string "said unto him, Put forth thy riddle,\l"
    .string "that we may hear it$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_14::
    .string "And he said unto them, Out of the\n"
    .string "eater came forth meat, and out of the\l"
    .string "strong came forth sweetness. And they\l"
    .string "could not in three days expound the\l"
    .string "riddle.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_15::
    .string "And it came to pass on the seventh\n"
    .string "day, that they said unto Samson’s\l"
    .string "wife, Entice thy husband, that he may\l"
    .string "declare unto us the riddle, lest we\l"
    .string "burn thee and thy father’s house with\l"
    .string "fire: have ye called us to take that\l"
    .string "we have? is it not so?"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_16::
    .string "And Samson’s wife wept before him,\n"
    .string "and said, Thou dost but hate me, and\l"
    .string "lovest me not: thou hast put forth a\l"
    .string "riddle unto the children of my\l"
    .string "people, and hast not told it me.\l"
    .string "And he said unto her, Behold, I have\l"
    .string "not told it my father nor my mother,\l"
    .string "and shall I tell it thee?"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_17::
    .string "And she wept before him the seven\n"
    .string "days, while their feast lasted: and\l"
    .string "it came to pass on the seventh day,\l"
    .string "that he told her, because she lay\l"
    .string "sore upon him: and she told the\l"
    .string "riddle to the children of her\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_18::
    .string "And the men of the city said unto\n"
    .string "him on the seventh day before the sun\l"
    .string "went down, What is sweeter than\l"
    .string "honey? And what is stronger than a\l"
    .string "lion? and he said unto them, If ye had\l"
    .string "not plowed with my heifer, ye had\l"
    .string "not found out my riddle.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_19::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD came\n"
    .string "upon him, and he went down to\l"
    .string "Ashkelon, and slew thirty men of\l"
    .string "them, and took their spoil, and gave\l"
    .string "change of garments unto them which\l"
    .string "expounded the riddle. And his anger\l"
    .string "was kindled, and he went up to his\l"
    .string "father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_14_20::
    .string "But Samson’s wife was given to his\n"
    .string "companion, whom he had used as his\l"
    .string "friend.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_1::
    .string "But it came to pass within a while\n"
    .string "after, in the time of wheat harvest,\l"
    .string "that Samson visited his wife with a\l"
    .string "kid; and he said, I will go in to my\l"
    .string "wife into the chamber. But her father\l"
    .string "would not suffer him to go in.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_2::
    .string "And her father said, I verily\n"
    .string "thought that thou hadst utterly\l"
    .string "hated her; therefore I gave her to\l"
    .string "thy companion: is not her younger\l"
    .string "sister fairer than she? take her, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, instead of her.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_3::
    .string "And Samson said concerning them, Now\n"
    .string "shall I be more blameless than the\l"
    .string "Philistines, though I do them a\l"
    .string "displeasure.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_4::
    .string "And Samson went and caught three\n"
    .string "hundred foxes, and took firebrands,\l"
    .string "and turned tail to tail, and put a\l"
    .string "firebrand in the midst between two\l"
    .string "tails.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_5::
    .string "And when he had set the brands on\n"
    .string "fire, he let them go into the\l"
    .string "standing corn of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "and burnt up both the shocks, and\l"
    .string "also the standing corn, with the\l"
    .string "vineyards and olives.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_6::
    .string "Then the Philistines said, Who hath\n"
    .string "done this? And they answered, Samson,\l"
    .string "the son in law of the Timnite,\l"
    .string "because he had taken his wife, and\l"
    .string "given her to his companion. And the\l"
    .string "Philistines came up, and burnt her\l"
    .string "and her father with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_7::
    .string "And Samson said unto them, Though ye\n"
    .string "have done this, yet will I be\l"
    .string "avenged of you, and after that I\l"
    .string "will cease.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_8::
    .string "And he smote them hip and thigh\n"
    .string "with a great slaughter: and he went\l"
    .string "down and dwelt in the top of the\l"
    .string "rock Etam.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_9::
    .string "Then the Philistines went up, and\n"
    .string "pitched in Judah, and spread\l"
    .string "themselves in Lehi.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_10::
    .string "And the men of Judah said, Why are ye\n"
    .string "come up against us? And they\l"
    .string "answered, To bind Samson are we come\l"
    .string "up, to do to him as he hath done to\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_11::
    .string "Then three thousand men of Judah\n"
    .string "went to the top of the rock Etam, and\l"
    .string "said to Samson, Knowest thou not that\l"
    .string "the Philistines are rulers over us?\l"
    .string "what is this that thou hast done unto\l"
    .string "us? And he said unto them, As they did\l"
    .string "unto me, so have I done unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_12::
    .string "And they said unto him, We are come\n"
    .string "down to bind thee, that we may\l"
    .string "deliver thee into the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines. And Samson said unto\l"
    .string "them, Swear unto me, that ye will\l"
    .string "not fall upon me yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_13::
    .string "And they spake unto him, saying, No;\n"
    .string "but we will bind thee fast, and\l"
    .string "deliver thee into their hand: but\l"
    .string "surely we will not kill thee. And\l"
    .string "they bound him with two new cords,\l"
    .string "and brought him up from the rock.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_14::
    .string "And when he came unto Lehi, the\n"
    .string "Philistines shouted against him: and\l"
    .string "the Spirit of the LORD came\l"
    .string "mightily upon him, and the cords\l"
    .string "that were upon his arms became as\l"
    .string "flax that was burnt with fire, and\l"
    .string "his bands loosed from off his hands.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_15::
    .string "And he found a new jawbone of an ass,\n"
    .string "and put forth his hand, and took it,\l"
    .string "and slew a thousand men therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_16::
    .string "And Samson said, With the jawbone of\n"
    .string "an ass, heaps upon heaps, with the\l"
    .string "jaw of an ass have I slain a thousand\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he had\n"
    .string "made an end of speaking, that he cast\l"
    .string "away the jawbone out of his hand, and\l"
    .string "called that place Ramathlehi.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_18::
    .string "And he was sore athirst, and called\n"
    .string "on the LORD, and said, Thou hast\l"
    .string "given this great deliverance into\l"
    .string "the hand of thy servant: and now\l"
    .string "shall I die for thirst, and fall\l"
    .string "into the hand of the uncircumcised?"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_19::
    .string "But God clave an hollow place\n"
    .string "that was in the jaw, and there came\l"
    .string "water thereout; and when he had\l"
    .string "drunk, his spirit came again, and he\l"
    .string "revived: wherefore he called the\l"
    .string "name thereof Enhakkore, which is in\l"
    .string "Lehi unto this day$"
Bible_Text_Judges_15_20::
    .string "And he judged Israel in the days of\n"
    .string "the Philistines twenty years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_1::
    .string "Then went Samson to Gaza, and saw\n"
    .string "there an harlot, and went in unto\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_2::
    .string "And it was told the Gazites,\n"
    .string "saying, Samson is come hither. And\l"
    .string "they compassed him in, and laid wait\l"
    .string "for him all night in the gate of the\l"
    .string "city, and were quiet all the night,\l"
    .string "saying, In the morning, when it is\l"
    .string "day, we shall kill him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_3::
    .string "And Samson lay till midnight, and\n"
    .string "arose at midnight, and took the doors\l"
    .string "of the gate of the city, and the two\l"
    .string "posts, and went away with them, bar\l"
    .string "and all, and put them upon his\l"
    .string "shoulders, and carried them up to\l"
    .string "the top of an hill that is before\l"
    .string "Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_4::
    .string "And it came to pass afterward, that\n"
    .string "he loved a woman in the valley of\l"
    .string "Sorek, whose name was Delilah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_5::
    .string "And the lords of the Philistines\n"
    .string "came up unto her, and said unto her,\l"
    .string "Entice him, and see wherein his great\l"
    .string "strength lieth, and by what means we\l"
    .string "may prevail against him, that we may\l"
    .string "bind him to afflict him; and we\l"
    .string "will give thee every one of us\l"
    .string "eleven hundred pieces of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_6::
    .string "And Delilah said to Samson, Tell\n"
    .string "me, I pray thee, wherein thy great\l"
    .string "strength lieth, and wherewith thou\l"
    .string "mightest be bound to afflict thee.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_7::
    .string "And Samson said unto her, If they\n"
    .string "bind me with seven green withs that\l"
    .string "were never dried, then shall I be\l"
    .string "weak, and be as another man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_8::
    .string "Then the lords of the Philistines\n"
    .string "brought up to her seven green withs\l"
    .string "which had not been dried, and she\l"
    .string "bound him with them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_9::
    .string "Now there were men lying in wait,\n"
    .string "abiding with her in the chamber. And\l"
    .string "she said unto him, The Philistines\l"
    .string "be upon thee, Samson. And he brake\l"
    .string "the withs, as a thread of tow is\l"
    .string "broken when it toucheth the fire. So\l"
    .string "his strength was not known.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_10::
    .string "And Delilah said unto Samson,\n"
    .string "Behold, thou hast mocked me, and\l"
    .string "told me lies: now tell me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, wherewith thou mightest be\l"
    .string "bound.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_11::
    .string "And he said unto her, If they bind me\n"
    .string "fast with new ropes that never were\l"
    .string "occupied, then shall I be weak, and\l"
    .string "be as another man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_12::
    .string "Delilah therefore took new ropes,\n"
    .string "and bound him therewith, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, The Philistines be upon\l"
    .string "thee, Samson. And there were liers\l"
    .string "in wait abiding in the chamber. And\l"
    .string "he brake them from off his arms like\l"
    .string "a thread.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_13::
    .string "And Delilah said unto Samson,\n"
    .string "Hitherto thou hast mocked me, and\l"
    .string "told me lies: tell me wherewith\l"
    .string "thou mightest be bound. And he said\l"
    .string "unto her, If thou weavest the seven\l"
    .string "locks of my head with the web.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_14::
    .string "And she fastened it with the pin,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, The Philistines\l"
    .string "be upon thee, Samson. And he awaked\l"
    .string "out of his sleep, and went away with\l"
    .string "the pin of the beam, and with the web.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_15::
    .string "And she said unto him, How canst\n"
    .string "thou say, I love thee, when thine\l"
    .string "heart is not with me? thou hast\l"
    .string "mocked me these three times, and hast\l"
    .string "not told me wherein thy great\l"
    .string "strength lieth.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, when she\n"
    .string "pressed him daily with her words,\l"
    .string "and urged him, so that his soul was\l"
    .string "vexed unto death;"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_17::
    .string "That he told her all his heart,\n"
    .string "and said unto her, There hath not\l"
    .string "come a razor upon mine head; for I\l"
    .string "have been a Nazarite unto God from my\l"
    .string "mother’s womb: if I be shaven, then\l"
    .string "my strength will go from me, and I\l"
    .string "shall become weak, and be like any\l"
    .string "other man$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_18::
    .string "And when Delilah saw that he had\n"
    .string "told her all his heart, she sent\l"
    .string "and called for the lords of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, saying, Come up this\l"
    .string "once, for he hath shewed me all his\l"
    .string "heart. Then the lords of the\l"
    .string "Philistines came up unto her, and\l"
    .string "brought money in their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_19::
    .string "And she made him sleep upon her\n"
    .string "knees; and she called for a man, and\l"
    .string "she caused him to shave off the seven\l"
    .string "locks of his head; and she began to\l"
    .string "afflict him, and his strength went\l"
    .string "from him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_20::
    .string "And she said, The Philistines be\n"
    .string "upon thee, Samson. And he awoke out\l"
    .string "of his sleep, and said, I will go\l"
    .string "out as at other times before, and\l"
    .string "shake myself. And he wist not that\l"
    .string "the LORD was departed from him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_21::
    .string "But the Philistines took him, and\n"
    .string "put out his eyes, and brought him\l"
    .string "down to Gaza, and bound him with\l"
    .string "fetters of brass; and he did grind in\l"
    .string "the prison house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_22::
    .string "Howbeit the hair of his head began\n"
    .string "to grow again after he was shaven.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_23::
    .string "Then the lords of the Philistines\n"
    .string "gathered them together for to offer a\l"
    .string "great sacrifice unto Dagon their god,\l"
    .string "and to rejoice: for they said, Our\l"
    .string "god hath delivered Samson our enemy\l"
    .string "into our hand.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_24::
    .string "And when the people saw him, they\n"
    .string "praised their god: for they said, Our\l"
    .string "god hath delivered into our hands\l"
    .string "our enemy, and the destroyer of our\l"
    .string "country, which slew many of us.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_25::
    .string "And it came to pass, when their\n"
    .string "hearts were merry, that they said,\l"
    .string "Call for Samson, that he may make us\l"
    .string "sport. And they called for Samson\l"
    .string "out of the prison house; and he made\l"
    .string "them sport: and they set him between\l"
    .string "the pillars.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_26::
    .string "And Samson said unto the lad that\n"
    .string "held him by the hand, Suffer me that\l"
    .string "I may feel the pillars whereupon\l"
    .string "the house standeth, that I may lean\l"
    .string "upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_27::
    .string "Now the house was full of men and\n"
    .string "women; and all the lords of the\l"
    .string "Philistines were there; and there\l"
    .string "were upon the roof about three\l"
    .string "thousand men and women, that beheld\l"
    .string "while Samson made sport.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_28::
    .string "And Samson called unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and said, O Lord God, remember me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, and strengthen me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, only this once, O God, that I\l"
    .string "may be at once avenged of the\l"
    .string "Philistines for my two eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_29::
    .string "And Samson took hold of the two\n"
    .string "middle pillars upon which the\l"
    .string "house stood, and on which it was\l"
    .string "borne up, of the one with his right\l"
    .string "hand, and of the other with his left.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_30::
    .string "And Samson said, Let me die with the\n"
    .string "Philistines. And he bowed himself\l"
    .string "with all his might; and the house\l"
    .string "fell upon the lords, and upon\l"
    .string "all the people that were therein.\l"
    .string "So the dead which he slew at his\l"
    .string "death were more than they which he\l"
    .string "slew in his life.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_16_31::
    .string "Then his brethren and all the\n"
    .string "house of his father came down, and\l"
    .string "took him, and brought him up, and\l"
    .string "buried him between Zorah and Eshtaol\l"
    .string "in the buryingplace of Manoah his\l"
    .string "father. And he judged Israel twenty\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_1::
    .string "And there was a man of mount\n"
    .string "Ephraim, whose name was Micah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_2::
    .string "And he said unto his mother, The\n"
    .string "eleven hundred shekels of silver\l"
    .string "that were taken from thee, about\l"
    .string "which thou cursedst, and spakest of\l"
    .string "also in mine ears, behold, the\l"
    .string "silver is with me; I took it. And his\l"
    .string "mother said, Blessed be thou of the\l"
    .string "LORD, my son.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_3::
    .string "And when he had restored the eleven\n"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver to his\l"
    .string "mother, his mother said, I had\l"
    .string "wholly dedicated the silver unto\l"
    .string "the LORD from my hand for my son, to\l"
    .string "make a graven image and a molten\l"
    .string "image: now therefore I will restore\l"
    .string "it unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_4::
    .string "Yet he restored the money unto his\n"
    .string "mother; and his mother took two\l"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver, and gave\l"
    .string "them to the founder, who made thereof\l"
    .string "a graven image and a molten image:\l"
    .string "and they were in the house of Micah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_5::
    .string "And the man Micah had an house of\n"
    .string "gods, and made an ephod, and\l"
    .string "teraphim, and consecrated one of his\l"
    .string "sons, who became his priest.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_6::
    .string "In those days there was no king in\n"
    .string "Israel, but every man did that which\l"
    .string "was right in his own eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_7::
    .string "And there was a young man out of\n"
    .string "Bethlehemjudah of the family of\l"
    .string "Judah, who was a Levite, and he\l"
    .string "sojourned there.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_8::
    .string "And the man departed out of the\n"
    .string "city from Bethlehemjudah to sojourn\l"
    .string "where he could find a place: and he\l"
    .string "came to mount Ephraim to the house\l"
    .string "of Micah, as he journeyed.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_9::
    .string "And Micah said unto him, Whence\n"
    .string "comest thou? And he said unto him, I\l"
    .string "am a Levite of Bethlehemjudah, and I\l"
    .string "go to sojourn where I may find a\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_10::
    .string "And Micah said unto him, Dwell with\n"
    .string "me, and be unto me a father and a\l"
    .string "priest, and I will give thee ten\l"
    .string "shekels of silver by the year, and a\l"
    .string "suit of apparel, and thy victuals.\l"
    .string "So the Levite went in.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_11::
    .string "And the Levite was content to\n"
    .string "dwell with the man; and the young\l"
    .string "man was unto him as one of his sons.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_12::
    .string "And Micah consecrated the Levite;\n"
    .string "and the young man became his priest,\l"
    .string "and was in the house of Micah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_17_13::
    .string "Then said Micah, Now know I that the\n"
    .string "LORD will do me good, seeing I have\l"
    .string "a Levite to my priest.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_1::
    .string "In those days there was no king in\n"
    .string "Israel: and in those days the tribe\l"
    .string "of the Danites sought them an\l"
    .string "inheritance to dwell in; for unto\l"
    .string "that day all their inheritance had\l"
    .string "not fallen unto them among the\l"
    .string "tribes of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_2::
    .string "And the children of Dan sent of\n"
    .string "their family five men from their\l"
    .string "coasts, men of valour, from Zorah,\l"
    .string "and from Eshtaol, to spy out the\l"
    .string "land, and to search it; and they said\l"
    .string "unto them, Go, search the land: who\l"
    .string "when they came to mount Ephraim, to\l"
    .string "the house of Micah, they lodged\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_3::
    .string "When they were by the house of\n"
    .string "Micah, they knew the voice of the\l"
    .string "young man the Levite: and they turned\l"
    .string "in thither, and said unto him, Who\l"
    .string "brought thee hither? and what makest\l"
    .string "thou in this place? and what hast\l"
    .string "thou here?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_4::
    .string "And he said unto them, Thus and thus\n"
    .string "dealeth Micah with me, and hath\l"
    .string "hired me, and I am his priest$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_5::
    .string "And they said unto him, Ask\n"
    .string "counsel, we pray thee, of God, that\l"
    .string "we may know whether our way which we\l"
    .string "go shall be prosperous.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_6::
    .string "And the priest said unto them, Go in\n"
    .string "peace: before the LORD is your way\l"
    .string "wherein ye go.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_7::
    .string "Then the five men departed, and\n"
    .string "came to Laish, and saw the people\l"
    .string "that were therein, how they dwelt\l"
    .string "careless, after the manner of the\l"
    .string "Zidonians, quiet and secure; and\l"
    .string "there was no magistrate in the land,\l"
    .string "that might put them to shame in any\l"
    .string "thing; and they were far from the\l"
    .string "Zidonians, and had no business with\l"
    .string "any man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_8::
    .string "And they came unto their brethren to\n"
    .string "Zorah and Eshtaol: and their\l"
    .string "brethren said unto them, What say ye?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_9::
    .string "And they said, Arise, that we may go\n"
    .string "up against them: for we have seen the\l"
    .string "land, and, behold, it is very good:\l"
    .string "and are ye still? be not slothful\l"
    .string "to go, and to enter to possess the\l"
    .string "land$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_10::
    .string "When ye go, ye shall come unto a\n"
    .string "people secure, and to a large\l"
    .string "land: for God hath given it into your\l"
    .string "hands; a place where there is no\l"
    .string "want of any thing that is in the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_11::
    .string "And there went from thence of the\n"
    .string "family of the Danites, out of Zorah\l"
    .string "and out of Eshtaol, six hundred men\l"
    .string "appointed with weapons of war.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_12::
    .string "And they went up, and pitched in\n"
    .string "Kirjathjearim, in Judah: wherefore\l"
    .string "they called that place Mahanehdan\l"
    .string "unto this day: behold, it is behind\l"
    .string "Kirjathjearim.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_13::
    .string "And they passed thence unto mount\n"
    .string "Ephraim, and came unto the house of\l"
    .string "Micah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_14::
    .string "Then answered the five men that went\n"
    .string "to spy out the country of Laish, and\l"
    .string "said unto their brethren, Do ye know\l"
    .string "that there is in these houses an\l"
    .string "ephod, and teraphim, and a graven\l"
    .string "image, and a molten image? now\l"
    .string "therefore consider what ye have to do.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_15::
    .string "And they turned thitherward, and\n"
    .string "came to the house of the young man\l"
    .string "the Levite, even unto the house of\l"
    .string "Micah, and saluted him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_16::
    .string "And the six hundred men appointed\n"
    .string "with their weapons of war, which\l"
    .string "were of the children of Dan, stood by\l"
    .string "the entering of the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_17::
    .string "And the five men that went to spy\n"
    .string "out the land went up, and came in\l"
    .string "thither, and took the graven image,\l"
    .string "and the ephod, and the teraphim, and\l"
    .string "the molten image: and the priest\l"
    .string "stood in the entering of the gate\l"
    .string "with the six hundred men that were\l"
    .string "appointed with weapons of war.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_18::
    .string "And these went into Micah’s house,\n"
    .string "and fetched the carved image, the\l"
    .string "ephod, and the teraphim, and the\l"
    .string "molten image. Then said the priest\l"
    .string "unto them, What do ye?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_19::
    .string "And they said unto him, Hold thy\n"
    .string "peace, lay thine hand upon thy\l"
    .string "mouth, and go with us, and be to us a\l"
    .string "father and a priest: is it better for\l"
    .string "thee to be a priest unto the house of\l"
    .string "one man, or that thou be a priest\l"
    .string "unto a tribe and a family in Israel?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_20::
    .string "And the priest’s heart was glad,\n"
    .string "and he took the ephod, and the\l"
    .string "teraphim, and the graven image, and\l"
    .string "went in the midst of the people$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_21::
    .string "So they turned and departed, and\n"
    .string "put the little ones and the cattle\l"
    .string "and the carriage before them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_22::
    .string "And when they were a good way from\n"
    .string "the house of Micah, the men that were\l"
    .string "in the houses near to Micah’s house\l"
    .string "were gathered together, and overtook\l"
    .string "the children of Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_23::
    .string "And they cried unto the children of\n"
    .string "Dan. And they turned their faces, and\l"
    .string "said unto Micah, What aileth thee,\l"
    .string "that thou comest with such a\l"
    .string "company?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_24::
    .string "And he said, Ye have taken away my\n"
    .string "gods which I made, and the priest,\l"
    .string "and ye are gone away: and what have I\l"
    .string "more? and what is this that ye say\l"
    .string "unto me, What aileth thee?"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_25::
    .string "And the children of Dan said unto\n"
    .string "him, Let not thy voice be heard among\l"
    .string "us, lest angry fellows run upon\l"
    .string "thee, and thou lose thy life, with\l"
    .string "the lives of thy household$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_26::
    .string "And the children of Dan went their\n"
    .string "way: and when Micah saw that they\l"
    .string "were too strong for him, he turned\l"
    .string "and went back unto his house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_27::
    .string "And they took the things which Micah\n"
    .string "had made, and the priest which he\l"
    .string "had, and came unto Laish, unto a\l"
    .string "people that were at quiet and\l"
    .string "secure: and they smote them with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword, and burnt the city\l"
    .string "with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_28::
    .string "And there was no deliverer, because\n"
    .string "it was far from Zidon, and they had no\l"
    .string "business with any man; and it was in\l"
    .string "the valley that lieth by Bethrehob.\l"
    .string "And they built a city, and dwelt\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_29::
    .string "And they called the name of the\n"
    .string "city Dan, after the name of Dan their\l"
    .string "father, who was born unto Israel:\l"
    .string "howbeit the name of the city was\l"
    .string "Laish at the first.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_30::
    .string "And the children of Dan set up the\n"
    .string "graven image: and Jonathan, the son\l"
    .string "of Gershom, the son of Manasseh, he\l"
    .string "and his sons were priests to the\l"
    .string "tribe of Dan until the day of the\l"
    .string "captivity of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_18_31::
    .string "And they set them up Micah’s graven\n"
    .string "image, which he made, all the time\l"
    .string "that the house of God was in Shiloh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "when there was no king in Israel,\l"
    .string "that there was a certain Levite\l"
    .string "sojourning on the side of mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim, who took to him a concubine\l"
    .string "out of Bethlehemjudah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_2::
    .string "And his concubine played the whore\n"
    .string "against him, and went away from him\l"
    .string "unto her father’s house to\l"
    .string "Bethlehemjudah, and was there four\l"
    .string "whole months.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_3::
    .string "And her husband arose, and went\n"
    .string "after her, to speak friendly unto\l"
    .string "her, and to bring her again, having\l"
    .string "his servant with him, and a couple\l"
    .string "of asses: and she brought him into\l"
    .string "her father’s house: and when the\l"
    .string "father of the damsel saw him, he\l"
    .string "rejoiced to meet him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_4::
    .string "And his father in law, the damsel’s\n"
    .string "father, retained him; and he abode\l"
    .string "with him three days: so they did eat\l"
    .string "and drink, and lodged there.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_5::
    .string "And it came to pass on the fourth\n"
    .string "day, when they arose early in the\l"
    .string "morning, that he rose up to depart:\l"
    .string "and the damsel’s father said unto\l"
    .string "his son in law, Comfort thine heart\l"
    .string "with a morsel of bread, and\l"
    .string "afterward go your way.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_6::
    .string "And they sat down, and did eat and\n"
    .string "drink both of them together: for the\l"
    .string "damsel’s father had said unto the\l"
    .string "man, Be content, I pray thee, and\l"
    .string "tarry all night, and let thine\l"
    .string "heart be merry.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_7::
    .string "And when the man rose up to depart,\n"
    .string "his father in law urged him:\l"
    .string "therefore he lodged there again.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_8::
    .string "And he arose early in the morning\n"
    .string "on the fifth day to depart; and the\l"
    .string "damsel’s father said, Comfort thine\l"
    .string "heart, I pray thee. And they tarried\l"
    .string "until afternoon, and they did eat\l"
    .string "both of them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_9::
    .string "And when the man rose up to depart,\n"
    .string "he, and his concubine, and his\l"
    .string "servant, his father in law, the\l"
    .string "damsel’s father, said unto him,\l"
    .string "Behold, now the day draweth toward\l"
    .string "evening, I pray you tarry all\l"
    .string "night: behold, the day groweth to an\l"
    .string "end, lodge here, that thine heart\l"
    .string "may be merry; and to morrow get you\l"
    .string "early on your way, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "go home.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_10::
    .string "But the man would not tarry that\n"
    .string "night, but he rose up and departed,\l"
    .string "and came over against Jebus, which is\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and there were with him\l"
    .string "two asses saddled, his concubine\l"
    .string "also was with him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_11::
    .string "And when they were by Jebus, the day\n"
    .string "was far spent; and the servant said\l"
    .string "unto his master, Come, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "and let us turn in into this city of\l"
    .string "the Jebusites, and lodge in it.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_12::
    .string "And his master said unto him, We\n"
    .string "will not turn aside hither into the\l"
    .string "city of a stranger, that is not of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel; we will pass\l"
    .string "over to Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_13::
    .string "And he said unto his servant, Come,\n"
    .string "and let us draw near to one of these\l"
    .string "places to lodge all night, in\l"
    .string "Gibeah, or in Ramah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_14::
    .string "And they passed on and went their\n"
    .string "way; and the sun went down upon them\l"
    .string "when they were by Gibeah, which\l"
    .string "belongeth to Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_15::
    .string "And they turned aside thither, to go\n"
    .string "in and to lodge in Gibeah: and when\l"
    .string "he went in, he sat him down in a\l"
    .string "street of the city: for there was no\l"
    .string "man that took them into his house to\l"
    .string "lodging.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_16::
    .string "And, behold, there came an old man\n"
    .string "from his work out of the field at\l"
    .string "even, which was also of mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim; and he sojourned in Gibeah:\l"
    .string "but the men of the place were\l"
    .string "Benjamites.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_17::
    .string "And when he had lifted up his eyes,\n"
    .string "he saw a wayfaring man in the street\l"
    .string "of the city: and the old man said,\l"
    .string "Whither goest thou? and whence comest\l"
    .string "thou?"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_18::
    .string "And he said unto him, We are passing\n"
    .string "from Bethlehemjudah toward the side\l"
    .string "of mount Ephraim; from thence am I:\l"
    .string "and I went to Bethlehemjudah, but I\l"
    .string "am now going to the house of the LORD;\l"
    .string "and there is no man that receiveth me\l"
    .string "to house$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_19::
    .string "Yet there is both straw and\n"
    .string "provender for our asses; and there is\l"
    .string "bread and wine also for me, and for\l"
    .string "thy handmaid, and for the young man\l"
    .string "which is with thy servants: there is\l"
    .string "no want of any thing.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_20::
    .string "And the old man said, Peace be with\n"
    .string "thee; howsoever let all thy wants\l"
    .string "lie upon me; only lodge not in the\l"
    .string "street.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_21::
    .string "So he brought him into his house,\n"
    .string "and gave provender unto the asses:\l"
    .string "and they washed their feet, and did\l"
    .string "eat and drink.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_22::
    .string "Now as they were making their hearts\n"
    .string "merry, behold, the men of the city,\l"
    .string "certain sons of Belial, beset the\l"
    .string "house round about, and beat at the\l"
    .string "door, and spake to the master of the\l"
    .string "house, the old man, saying, Bring\l"
    .string "forth the man that came into thine\l"
    .string "house, that we may know him.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_23::
    .string "And the man, the master of the\n"
    .string "house, went out unto them, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Nay, my brethren, nay, I\l"
    .string "pray you, do not so wickedly; seeing\l"
    .string "that this man is come into mine\l"
    .string "house, do not this folly.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_24::
    .string "Behold, here is my daughter a\n"
    .string "maiden, and his concubine; them I\l"
    .string "will bring out now, and humble ye\l"
    .string "them, and do with them what seemeth\l"
    .string "good unto you: but unto this man do\l"
    .string "not so vile a thing.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_25::
    .string "But the men would not hearken to\n"
    .string "him: so the man took his concubine,\l"
    .string "and brought her forth unto them; and\l"
    .string "they knew her, and abused her all\l"
    .string "the night until the morning: and\l"
    .string "when the day began to spring, they\l"
    .string "let her go.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_26::
    .string "Then came the woman in the dawning\n"
    .string "of the day, and fell down at the\l"
    .string "door of the man’s house where her\l"
    .string "lord was, till it was light.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_27::
    .string "And her lord rose up in the\n"
    .string "morning, and opened the doors of the\l"
    .string "house, and went out to go his way:\l"
    .string "and, behold, the woman his concubine\l"
    .string "was fallen down at the door of the\l"
    .string "house, and her hands were upon the\l"
    .string "threshold.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_28::
    .string "And he said unto her, Up, and let\n"
    .string "us be going. But none answered. Then\l"
    .string "the man took her up upon an ass, and\l"
    .string "the man rose up, and gat him unto his\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_29::
    .string "And when he was come into his house,\n"
    .string "he took a knife, and laid hold on\l"
    .string "his concubine, and divided her,\l"
    .string "together with her bones, into twelve\l"
    .string "pieces, and sent her into all the\l"
    .string "coasts of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_19_30::
    .string "And it was so, that all that saw it\n"
    .string "said, There was no such deed done nor\l"
    .string "seen from the day that the children\l"
    .string "of Israel came up out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt unto this day: consider of\l"
    .string "it, take advice, and speak your\l"
    .string "minds.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_1::
    .string "Then all the children of Israel\n"
    .string "went out, and the congregation was\l"
    .string "gathered together as one man, from\l"
    .string "Dan even to Beersheba, with the land\l"
    .string "of Gilead, unto the LORD in Mizpeh.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_2::
    .string "And the chief of all the people,\n"
    .string "even of all the tribes of Israel,\l"
    .string "presented themselves in the\l"
    .string "assembly of the people of God,\l"
    .string "four hundred thousand footmen that\l"
    .string "drew sword.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_3::
    .string "(Now the children of Benjamin heard\n"
    .string "that the children of Israel were\l"
    .string "gone up to Mizpeh.) Then said the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, Tell us, how\l"
    .string "was this wickedness?"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_4::
    .string "And the Levite, the husband of the\n"
    .string "woman that was slain, answered and\l"
    .string "said, I came into Gibeah that\l"
    .string "belongeth to Benjamin, I and my\l"
    .string "concubine, to lodge$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_5::
    .string "And the men of Gibeah rose against\n"
    .string "me, and beset the house round about\l"
    .string "upon me by night, and thought to have\l"
    .string "slain me: and my concubine have they\l"
    .string "forced, that she is dead.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_6::
    .string "And I took my concubine, and cut her\n"
    .string "in pieces, and sent her throughout\l"
    .string "all the country of the inheritance\l"
    .string "of Israel: for they have committed\l"
    .string "lewdness and folly in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_7::
    .string "Behold, ye are all children of\n"
    .string "Israel; give here your advice and\l"
    .string "counsel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_8::
    .string "And all the people arose as one\n"
    .string "man, saying, We will not any of us\l"
    .string "go to his tent, neither will we any\l"
    .string "of us turn into his house.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_9::
    .string "But now this shall be the thing\n"
    .string "which we will do to Gibeah; we will\l"
    .string "go up by lot against it;"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_10::
    .string "And we will take ten men of an\n"
    .string "hundred throughout all the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel, and an hundred of a\l"
    .string "thousand, and a thousand out of ten\l"
    .string "thousand, to fetch victual for the\l"
    .string "people, that they may do, when they\l"
    .string "come to Gibeah of Benjamin, according\l"
    .string "to all the folly that they have\l"
    .string "wrought in Israel$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_11::
    .string "So all the men of Israel were\n"
    .string "gathered against the city, knit\l"
    .string "together as one man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_12::
    .string "And the tribes of Israel sent men\n"
    .string "through all the tribe of Benjamin,\l"
    .string "saying, What wickedness is this that\l"
    .string "is done among you?"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_13::
    .string "Now therefore deliver us the men,\n"
    .string "the children of Belial, which are\l"
    .string "in Gibeah, that we may put them to\l"
    .string "death, and put away evil from Israel\l"
    .string " But the children of Benjamin\l"
    .string "would not hearken to the voice of\l"
    .string "their brethren the children of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_14::
    .string "But the children of Benjamin\n"
    .string "gathered themselves together out of\l"
    .string "the cities unto Gibeah, to go out to\l"
    .string "battle against the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_15::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin were\n"
    .string "numbered at that time out of the\l"
    .string "cities twenty and six thousand men\l"
    .string "that drew sword, beside the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Gibeah, which were\l"
    .string "numbered seven hundred chosen men.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_16::
    .string "Among all this people there were\n"
    .string "seven hundred chosen men lefthanded;\l"
    .string "every one could sling stones at an\l"
    .string "hair breadth, and not miss.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_17::
    .string "And the men of Israel, beside\n"
    .string "Benjamin, were numbered four hundred\l"
    .string "thousand men that drew sword: all\l"
    .string "these were men of war.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_18::
    .string "And the children of Israel arose,\n"
    .string "and went up to the house of God, and\l"
    .string "asked counsel of God, and said,\l"
    .string "Which of us shall go up first to\l"
    .string "the battle against the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin? And the LORD said, Judah\l"
    .string "shall go up first.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_19::
    .string "And the children of Israel rose up\n"
    .string "in the morning, and encamped against\l"
    .string "Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_20::
    .string "And the men of Israel went out to\n"
    .string "battle against Benjamin; and the men\l"
    .string "of Israel put themselves in array\l"
    .string "to fight against them at Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_21::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin came\n"
    .string "forth out of Gibeah, and destroyed\l"
    .string "down to the ground of the Israelites\l"
    .string "that day twenty and two thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_22::
    .string "And the people the men of Israel\n"
    .string "encouraged themselves, and set their\l"
    .string "battle again in array in the place\l"
    .string "where they put themselves in array\l"
    .string "the first day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_23::
    .string "(And the children of Israel went\n"
    .string "up and wept before the LORD until\l"
    .string "even, and asked counsel of the LORD,\l"
    .string "saying, Shall I go up again to\l"
    .string "battle against the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin my brother? And the LORD\l"
    .string "said, Go up against him.)"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_24::
    .string "And the children of Israel came\n"
    .string "near against the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin the second day$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_25::
    .string "And Benjamin went forth against\n"
    .string "them out of Gibeah the second day,\l"
    .string "and destroyed down to the ground of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel again\l"
    .string "eighteen thousand men; all these\l"
    .string "drew the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_26::
    .string "Then all the children of Israel,\n"
    .string "and all the people, went up, and\l"
    .string "came unto the house of God, and wept,\l"
    .string "and sat there before the LORD, and\l"
    .string "fasted that day until even, and\l"
    .string "offered burnt offerings and peace\l"
    .string "offerings before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_27::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "enquired of the LORD, (for the ark of\l"
    .string "the covenant of God was there in\l"
    .string "those days,"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_28::
    .string "And Phinehas, the son of Eleazar,\n"
    .string "the son of Aaron, stood before it in\l"
    .string "those days,) saying, Shall I yet\l"
    .string "again go out to battle against the\l"
    .string "children of Benjamin my brother, or\l"
    .string "shall I cease? And the LORD said, Go\l"
    .string "up; for to morrow I will deliver\l"
    .string "them into thine hand$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_29::
    .string "And Israel set liers in wait round\n"
    .string "about Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_30::
    .string "And the children of Israel went up\n"
    .string "against the children of Benjamin on\l"
    .string "the third day, and put themselves in\l"
    .string "array against Gibeah, as at other\l"
    .string "times.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_31::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin went\n"
    .string "out against the people, and were\l"
    .string "drawn away from the city; and they\l"
    .string "began to smite of the people, and\l"
    .string "kill, as at other times, in the\l"
    .string "highways, of which one goeth up to\l"
    .string "the house of God, and the other to\l"
    .string "Gibeah in the field, about thirty\l"
    .string "men of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_32::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin said,\n"
    .string "They are smitten down before us, as\l"
    .string "at the first. But the children of\l"
    .string "Israel said, Let us flee, and draw\l"
    .string "them from the city unto the highways.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_33::
    .string "And all the men of Israel rose up\n"
    .string "out of their place, and put\l"
    .string "themselves in array at Baaltamar:\l"
    .string "and the liers in wait of Israel came\l"
    .string "forth out of their places, even out\l"
    .string "of the meadows of Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_34::
    .string "And there came against Gibeah ten\n"
    .string "thousand chosen men out of all\l"
    .string "Israel, and the battle was sore: but\l"
    .string "they knew not that evil was near\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_35::
    .string "And the LORD smote Benjamin before\n"
    .string "Israel: and the children of Israel\l"
    .string "destroyed of the Benjamites that day\l"
    .string "twenty and five thousand and an\l"
    .string "hundred men: all these drew the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_36::
    .string "So the children of Benjamin saw\n"
    .string "that they were smitten: for the men\l"
    .string "of Israel gave place to the\l"
    .string "Benjamites, because they trusted\l"
    .string "unto the liers in wait which they\l"
    .string "had set beside Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_37::
    .string "And the liers in wait hasted, and\n"
    .string "rushed upon Gibeah; and the liers in\l"
    .string "wait drew themselves along, and\l"
    .string "smote all the city with the edge of\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_38::
    .string "Now there was an appointed sign\n"
    .string "between the men of Israel and the\l"
    .string "liers in wait, that they should make\l"
    .string "a great flame with smoke rise up out\l"
    .string "of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_39::
    .string "And when the men of Israel retired\n"
    .string "in the battle, Benjamin began to\l"
    .string "smite and kill of the men of Israel\l"
    .string "about thirty persons: for they said,\l"
    .string "Surely they are smitten down before\l"
    .string "us, as in the first battle.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_40::
    .string "But when the flame began to arise\n"
    .string "up out of the city with a pillar of\l"
    .string "smoke, the Benjamites looked behind\l"
    .string "them, and, behold, the flame of the\l"
    .string "city ascended up to heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_41::
    .string "And when the men of Israel turned\n"
    .string "again, the men of Benjamin were\l"
    .string "amazed: for they saw that evil was\l"
    .string "come upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_42::
    .string "Therefore they turned their backs\n"
    .string "before the men of Israel unto the\l"
    .string "way of the wilderness; but the\l"
    .string "battle overtook them; and them which\l"
    .string "came out of the cities they destroyed\l"
    .string "in the midst of them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_43::
    .string "Thus they inclosed the Benjamites\n"
    .string "round about, and chased them, and\l"
    .string "trode them down with ease over\l"
    .string "against Gibeah toward the sunrising.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_44::
    .string "And there fell of Benjamin\n"
    .string "eighteen thousand men; all these\l"
    .string "were men of valour.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_45::
    .string "And they turned and fled toward the\n"
    .string "wilderness unto the rock of Rimmon:\l"
    .string "and they gleaned of them in the\l"
    .string "highways five thousand men; and\l"
    .string "pursued hard after them unto Gidom,\l"
    .string "and slew two thousand men of them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_46::
    .string "So that all which fell that day\n"
    .string "of Benjamin were twenty and five\l"
    .string "thousand men that drew the sword;\l"
    .string "all these were men of valour.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_47::
    .string "But six hundred men turned and fled\n"
    .string "to the wilderness unto the rock\l"
    .string "Rimmon, and abode in the rock Rimmon\l"
    .string "four months.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_20_48::
    .string "And the men of Israel turned again\n"
    .string "upon the children of Benjamin, and\l"
    .string "smote them with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword, as well the men of every\l"
    .string "city, as the beast, and all that\l"
    .string "came to hand: also they set on fire\l"
    .string "all the cities that they came to.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_1::
    .string "Now the men of Israel had sworn in\n"
    .string "Mizpeh, saying, There shall not any\l"
    .string "of us give his daughter unto Benjamin\l"
    .string "to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_2::
    .string "And the people came to the house\n"
    .string "of God, and abode there till even\l"
    .string "before God, and lifted up their\l"
    .string "voices, and wept sore;"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_3::
    .string "And said, O LORD God of Israel, why\n"
    .string "is this come to pass in Israel, that\l"
    .string "there should be to day one tribe\l"
    .string "lacking in Israel?"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_4::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that the people rose early, and\l"
    .string "built there an altar, and offered\l"
    .string "burnt offerings and peace offerings$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_5::
    .string "And the children of Israel said,\n"
    .string "Who is there among all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel that came not up with the\l"
    .string "congregation unto the LORD? For they\l"
    .string "had made a great oath concerning him\l"
    .string "that came not up to the LORD to\l"
    .string "Mizpeh, saying, He shall surely be\l"
    .string "put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_6::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "repented them for Benjamin their\l"
    .string "brother, and said, There is one tribe\l"
    .string "cut off from Israel this day.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_7::
    .string "How shall we do for wives for them\n"
    .string "that remain, seeing we have sworn by\l"
    .string "the LORD that we will not give them\l"
    .string "of our daughters to wives?"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_8::
    .string "And they said, What one is there of\n"
    .string "the tribes of Israel that came not\l"
    .string "up to Mizpeh to the LORD? And,\l"
    .string "behold, there came none to the camp\l"
    .string "from Jabeshgilead to the assembly$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_9::
    .string "For the people were numbered, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there were none of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jabeshgilead there.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_10::
    .string "And the congregation sent thither\n"
    .string "twelve thousand men of the\l"
    .string "valiantest, and commanded them,\l"
    .string "saying, Go and smite the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of Jabeshgilead with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword, with the women and the\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_11::
    .string "And this is the thing that ye shall\n"
    .string "do, Ye shall utterly destroy every\l"
    .string "male, and every woman that hath lain\l"
    .string "by man.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_12::
    .string "And they found among the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Jabeshgilead four\l"
    .string "hundred young virgins, that had known\l"
    .string "no man by lying with any male: and\l"
    .string "they brought them unto the camp to\l"
    .string "Shiloh, which is in the land of\l"
    .string "Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_13::
    .string "And the whole congregation sent\n"
    .string "some to speak to the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin that were in the rock\l"
    .string "Rimmon, and to call peaceably unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_14::
    .string "And Benjamin came again at that\n"
    .string "time; and they gave them wives which\l"
    .string "they had saved alive of the women of\l"
    .string "Jabeshgilead: and yet so they\l"
    .string "sufficed them not.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_15::
    .string "And the people repented them for\n"
    .string "Benjamin, because that the LORD had\l"
    .string "made a breach in the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_16::
    .string "Then the elders of the congregation\n"
    .string "said, How shall we do for wives for\l"
    .string "them that remain, seeing the women\l"
    .string "are destroyed out of Benjamin?"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_17::
    .string "And they said, There must be an\n"
    .string "inheritance for them that be escaped\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, that a tribe be not\l"
    .string "destroyed out of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_18::
    .string "Howbeit we may not give them wives\n"
    .string "of our daughters: for the children\l"
    .string "of Israel have sworn, saying, Cursed\l"
    .string "be he that giveth a wife to Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_19::
    .string "Then they said, Behold, there is a\n"
    .string "feast of the LORD in Shiloh yearly\l"
    .string "in a place which is on the north\l"
    .string "side of Bethel, on the east side of\l"
    .string "the highway that goeth up from\l"
    .string "Bethel to Shechem, and on the south\l"
    .string "of Lebonah.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_20::
    .string "Therefore they commanded the\n"
    .string "children of Benjamin, saying, Go and\l"
    .string "lie in wait in the vineyards;"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_21::
    .string "And see, and, behold, if the\n"
    .string "daughters of Shiloh come out to\l"
    .string "dance in dances, then come ye out of\l"
    .string "the vineyards, and catch you every\l"
    .string "man his wife of the daughters of\l"
    .string "Shiloh, and go to the land of\l"
    .string "Benjamin$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_22::
    .string "And it shall be, when their fathers\n"
    .string "or their brethren come unto us to\l"
    .string "complain, that we will say unto\l"
    .string "them, Be favourable unto them for\l"
    .string "our sakes: because we reserved not to\l"
    .string "each man his wife in the war: for ye\l"
    .string "did not give unto them at this time,\l"
    .string "that ye should be guilty.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_23::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin did\n"
    .string "so, and took them wives, according to\l"
    .string "their number, of them that danced,\l"
    .string "whom they caught: and they went and\l"
    .string "returned unto their inheritance, and\l"
    .string "repaired the cities, and dwelt in\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_24::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "departed thence at that time, every\l"
    .string "man to his tribe and to his family,\l"
    .string "and they went out from thence every\l"
    .string "man to his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Judges_21_25::
    .string "In those days there was no king in\n"
    .string "Israel: every man did that which was\l"
    .string "right in his own eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the days when\n"
    .string "the judges ruled, that there was a\l"
    .string "famine in the land. And a certain man\l"
    .string "of Bethlehemjudah went to sojourn in\l"
    .string "the country of Moab, he, and his wife,\l"
    .string "and his two sons.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_2::
    .string "And the name of the man was\n"
    .string "Elimelech, and the name of his wife\l"
    .string "Naomi, and the name of his two sons\l"
    .string "Mahlon and Chilion, Ephrathites of\l"
    .string "Bethlehemjudah. And they came into\l"
    .string "the country of Moab, and continued\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_3::
    .string "And Elimelech Naomi’s husband\n"
    .string "died; and she was left, and her two\l"
    .string "sons.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_4::
    .string "And they took them wives of the\n"
    .string "women of Moab; the name of the one was\l"
    .string "Orpah, and the name of the other\l"
    .string "Ruth: and they dwelled there about\l"
    .string "ten years.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_5::
    .string "And Mahlon and Chilion died also\n"
    .string "both of them; and the woman was left\l"
    .string "of her two sons and her husband.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_6::
    .string "Then she arose with her daughters in\n"
    .string "law, that she might return from the\l"
    .string "country of Moab: for she had heard in\l"
    .string "the country of Moab how that the LORD\l"
    .string "had visited his people in giving\l"
    .string "them bread.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_7::
    .string "Wherefore she went forth out of the\n"
    .string "place where she was, and her two\l"
    .string "daughters in law with her; and they\l"
    .string "went on the way to return unto the\l"
    .string "land of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_8::
    .string "And Naomi said unto her two\n"
    .string "daughters in law, Go, return each to\l"
    .string "her mother’s house: the LORD deal\l"
    .string "kindly with you, as ye have dealt\l"
    .string "with the dead, and with me.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_9::
    .string "The LORD grant you that ye may find\n"
    .string "rest, each of you in the house of her\l"
    .string "husband. Then she kissed them; and\l"
    .string "they lifted up their voice, and\l"
    .string "wept.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_10::
    .string "And they said unto her, Surely we\n"
    .string "will return with thee unto thy\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_11::
    .string "And Naomi said, Turn again, my\n"
    .string "daughters: why will ye go with me?\l"
    .string "are there yet any more sons in my\l"
    .string "womb, that they may be your husbands?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_12::
    .string "Turn again, my daughters, go your\n"
    .string "way; for I am too old to have an\l"
    .string "husband. If I should say, I have\l"
    .string "hope, if I should have an husband\l"
    .string "also to night, and should also bear\l"
    .string "sons;"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_13::
    .string "Would ye tarry for them till they\n"
    .string "were grown? would ye stay for them\l"
    .string "from having husbands? nay, my\l"
    .string "daughters; for it grieveth me much\l"
    .string "for your sakes that the hand of the\l"
    .string "LORD is gone out against me$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_14::
    .string "And they lifted up their voice, and\n"
    .string "wept again: and Orpah kissed her\l"
    .string "mother in law; but Ruth clave unto\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_15::
    .string "And she said, Behold, thy sister in\n"
    .string "law is gone back unto her people,\l"
    .string "and unto her gods: return thou after\l"
    .string "thy sister in law.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_16::
    .string "And Ruth said, Intreat me not to\n"
    .string "leave thee, or to return from\l"
    .string "following after thee: for whither\l"
    .string "thou goest, I will go; and where\l"
    .string "thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy\l"
    .string "people shall be my people, and\l"
    .string "thy God my God:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_17::
    .string "Where thou diest, will I die, and\n"
    .string "there will I be buried: the LORD do\l"
    .string "so to me, and more also, if ought but\l"
    .string "death part thee and me$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_18::
    .string "When she saw that she was\n"
    .string "stedfastly minded to go with her,\l"
    .string "then she left speaking unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_19::
    .string "So they two went until they came to\n"
    .string "Bethlehem. And it came to pass, when\l"
    .string "they were come to Bethlehem, that\l"
    .string "all the city was moved about them,\l"
    .string "and they said, Is this Naomi?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_20::
    .string "And she said unto them, Call me not\n"
    .string "Naomi, call me Mara: for the\l"
    .string "Almighty hath dealt very bitterly\l"
    .string "with me$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_21::
    .string "I went out full and the LORD hath\n"
    .string "brought me home again empty: why\l"
    .string "then call ye me Naomi, seeing the\l"
    .string "LORD hath testified against me, and\l"
    .string "the Almighty hath afflicted me?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_1_22::
    .string "So Naomi returned, and Ruth the\n"
    .string "Moabitess, her daughter in law, with\l"
    .string "her, which returned out of the\l"
    .string "country of Moab: and they came to\l"
    .string "Bethlehem in the beginning of\l"
    .string "barley harvest$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_1::
    .string "And Naomi had a kinsman of her\n"
    .string "husband’s, a mighty man of wealth,\l"
    .string "of the family of Elimelech; and his\l"
    .string "name was Boaz.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_2::
    .string "And Ruth the Moabitess said unto\n"
    .string "Naomi, Let me now go to the field,\l"
    .string "and glean ears of corn after him in\l"
    .string "whose sight I shall find grace. And\l"
    .string "she said unto her, Go, my daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_3::
    .string "And she went, and came, and gleaned\n"
    .string "in the field after the reapers: and\l"
    .string "her hap was to light on a part of\l"
    .string "the field belonging unto Boaz, who\l"
    .string "was of the kindred of Elimelech.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_4::
    .string "And, behold, Boaz came from\n"
    .string "Bethlehem, and said unto the\l"
    .string "reapers, The LORD be with you. And\l"
    .string "they answered him, The LORD bless\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_5::
    .string "Then said Boaz unto his servant that\n"
    .string "was set over the reapers, Whose\l"
    .string "damsel is this?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_6::
    .string "And the servant that was set over\n"
    .string "the reapers answered and said, It is\l"
    .string "the Moabitish damsel that came back\l"
    .string "with Naomi out of the country of\l"
    .string "Moab:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_7::
    .string "And she said, I pray you, let me\n"
    .string "glean and gather after the reapers\l"
    .string "among the sheaves: so she came, and\l"
    .string "hath continued even from the morning\l"
    .string "until now, that she tarried a\l"
    .string "little in the house$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_8::
    .string "Then said Boaz unto Ruth, Hearest\n"
    .string "thou not, my daughter? Go not to\l"
    .string "glean in another field, neither go\l"
    .string "from hence, but abide here fast by my\l"
    .string "maidens:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_9::
    .string "Let thine eyes be on the field that\n"
    .string "they do reap, and go thou after them:\l"
    .string "have I not charged the young men that\l"
    .string "they shall not touch thee? and when\l"
    .string "thou art athirst, go unto the\l"
    .string "vessels, and drink of that which the\l"
    .string "young men have drawn$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_10::
    .string "Then she fell on her face, and\n"
    .string "bowed herself to the ground, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Why have I found grace\l"
    .string "in thine eyes, that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "take knowledge of me, seeing I am a\l"
    .string "stranger?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_11::
    .string "And Boaz answered and said unto her,\n"
    .string "It hath fully been shewed me, all\l"
    .string "that thou hast done unto thy mother\l"
    .string "in law since the death of thine\l"
    .string "husband: and how thou hast left thy\l"
    .string "father and thy mother, and the land\l"
    .string "of thy nativity, and art come unto a\l"
    .string "people which thou knewest not\l"
    .string "heretofore$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_12::
    .string "The LORD recompense thy work, and a\n"
    .string "full reward be given thee of the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, under whose\l"
    .string "wings thou art come to trust.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_13::
    .string "Then she said, Let me find favour in\n"
    .string "thy sight, my lord; for that thou\l"
    .string "hast comforted me, and for that thou\l"
    .string "hast spoken friendly unto thine\l"
    .string "handmaid, though I be not like unto\l"
    .string "one of thine handmaidens.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_14::
    .string "And Boaz said unto her, At mealtime\n"
    .string "come thou hither, and eat of the\l"
    .string "bread, and dip thy morsel in the\l"
    .string "vinegar. And she sat beside the\l"
    .string "reapers: and he reached her parched\l"
    .string "corn, and she did eat, and was\l"
    .string "sufficed, and left.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_15::
    .string "And when she was risen up to glean,\n"
    .string "Boaz commanded his young men, saying,\l"
    .string "Let her glean even among the\l"
    .string "sheaves, and reproach her not:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_16::
    .string "And let fall also some of the\n"
    .string "handfuls of purpose for her, and\l"
    .string "leave them, that she may glean them,\l"
    .string "and rebuke her not$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_17::
    .string "So she gleaned in the field until\n"
    .string "even, and beat out that she had\l"
    .string "gleaned: and it was about an ephah\l"
    .string "of barley.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_18::
    .string "And she took it up, and went into\n"
    .string "the city: and her mother in law saw\l"
    .string "what she had gleaned: and she\l"
    .string "brought forth, and gave to her that\l"
    .string "she had reserved after she was\l"
    .string "sufficed.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_19::
    .string "And her mother in law said unto her,\n"
    .string "Where hast thou gleaned to day? and\l"
    .string "where wroughtest thou? blessed be he\l"
    .string "that did take knowledge of thee. And\l"
    .string "she shewed her mother in law with\l"
    .string "whom she had wrought, and said, The\l"
    .string "man’s name with whom I wrought to day\l"
    .string "is Boaz.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_20::
    .string "And Naomi said unto her daughter in\n"
    .string "law, Blessed be he of the LORD, who\l"
    .string "hath not left off his kindness to\l"
    .string "the living and to the dead. And Naomi\l"
    .string "said unto her, The man is near of kin\l"
    .string "unto us, one of our next kinsmen.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_21::
    .string "And Ruth the Moabitess said, He said\n"
    .string "unto me also, Thou shalt keep fast\l"
    .string "by my young men, until they have\l"
    .string "ended all my harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_22::
    .string "And Naomi said unto Ruth her\n"
    .string "daughter in law, It is good, my\l"
    .string "daughter, that thou go out with his\l"
    .string "maidens, that they meet thee not in\l"
    .string "any other field.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_2_23::
    .string "So she kept fast by the maidens of\n"
    .string "Boaz to glean unto the end of barley\l"
    .string "harvest and of wheat harvest; and\l"
    .string "dwelt with her mother in law.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_1::
    .string "Then Naomi her mother in law said\n"
    .string "unto her, My daughter, shall I not\l"
    .string "seek rest for thee, that it may be\l"
    .string "well with thee?"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_2::
    .string "And now is not Boaz of our kindred,\n"
    .string "with whose maidens thou wast?\l"
    .string "Behold, he winnoweth barley to\l"
    .string "night in the threshingfloor$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_3::
    .string "Wash thyself therefore, and anoint\n"
    .string "thee, and put thy raiment upon thee,\l"
    .string "and get thee down to the floor: but\l"
    .string "make not thyself known unto the man,\l"
    .string "until he shall have done eating and\l"
    .string "drinking.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_4::
    .string "And it shall be, when he lieth\n"
    .string "down, that thou shalt mark the\l"
    .string "place where he shall lie, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt go in, and uncover his feet,\l"
    .string "and lay thee down; and he will\l"
    .string "tell thee what thou shalt do.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_5::
    .string "And she said unto her, All that\n"
    .string "thou sayest unto me I will do.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_6::
    .string "And she went down unto the floor,\n"
    .string "and did according to all that her\l"
    .string "mother in law bade her.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_7::
    .string "And when Boaz had eaten and drunk,\n"
    .string "and his heart was merry, he went to\l"
    .string "lie down at the end of the heap of\l"
    .string "corn: and she came softly, and\l"
    .string "uncovered his feet, and laid her\l"
    .string "down.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_8::
    .string "And it came to pass at midnight,\n"
    .string "that the man was afraid, and turned\l"
    .string "himself: and, behold, a woman lay\l"
    .string "at his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_9::
    .string "And he said, Who art thou? And she\n"
    .string "answered, I am Ruth thine handmaid:\l"
    .string "spread therefore thy skirt over\l"
    .string "thine handmaid; for thou art a near\l"
    .string "kinsman.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_10::
    .string "And he said, Blessed be thou of the\n"
    .string "LORD, my daughter: for thou hast\l"
    .string "shewed more kindness in the latter\l"
    .string "end than at the beginning, inasmuch\l"
    .string "as thou followedst not young men,\l"
    .string "whether poor or rich.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_11::
    .string "And now, my daughter, fear not; I\n"
    .string "will do to thee all that thou\l"
    .string "requirest: for all the city of my\l"
    .string "people doth know that thou art a\l"
    .string "virtuous woman.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_12::
    .string "And now it is true that I am thy near\n"
    .string "kinsman: howbeit there is a kinsman\l"
    .string "nearer than I.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_13::
    .string "Tarry this night, and it shall be\n"
    .string "in the morning, that if he will\l"
    .string "perform unto thee the part of a\l"
    .string "kinsman, well; let him do the\l"
    .string "kinsman’s part: but if he will not\l"
    .string "do the part of a kinsman to thee,\l"
    .string "then will I do the part of a\l"
    .string "kinsman to thee, as the LORD liveth:\l"
    .string "lie down until the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_14::
    .string "And she lay at his feet until the\n"
    .string "morning: and she rose up before one\l"
    .string "could know another. And he said, Let\l"
    .string "it not be known that a woman came\l"
    .string "into the floor.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_15::
    .string "Also he said, Bring the vail that\n"
    .string "thou hast upon thee, and hold it.\l"
    .string "And when she held it, he measured six\l"
    .string "measures of barley, and laid it on\l"
    .string "her: and she went into the city.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_16::
    .string "And when she came to her mother in\n"
    .string "law, she said, Who art thou, my\l"
    .string "daughter? And she told her all that\l"
    .string "the man had done to her.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_17::
    .string "And she said, These six measures of\n"
    .string "barley gave he me; for he said to me,\l"
    .string "Go not empty unto thy mother in law.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_3_18::
    .string "Then said she, Sit still, my\n"
    .string "daughter, until thou know how the\l"
    .string "matter will fall: for the man\l"
    .string "will not be in rest, until he have\l"
    .string "finished the thing this day.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_1::
    .string "Then went Boaz up to the gate, and\n"
    .string "sat him down there: and, behold, the\l"
    .string "kinsman of whom Boaz spake came by;\l"
    .string "unto whom he said, Ho, such a one!\l"
    .string "turn aside, sit down here. And he\l"
    .string "turned aside, and sat down.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_2::
    .string "And he took ten men of the elders of\n"
    .string "the city, and said, Sit ye down here.\l"
    .string "And they sat down.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_3::
    .string "And he said unto the kinsman, Naomi,\n"
    .string "that is come again out of the country\l"
    .string "of Moab, selleth a parcel of land,\l"
    .string "which was our brother Elimelech’s:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_4::
    .string "And I thought to advertise thee,\n"
    .string "saying, Buy it before the\l"
    .string "inhabitants, and before the elders\l"
    .string "of my people. If thou wilt redeem\l"
    .string "it, redeem it: but if thou wilt not\l"
    .string "redeem it, then tell me, that I may\l"
    .string "know: for there is none to redeem it\l"
    .string "beside thee; and I am after thee. And\l"
    .string "he said, I will redeem it$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_5::
    .string "Then said Boaz, What day thou buyest\n"
    .string "the field of the hand of Naomi, thou\l"
    .string "must buy it also of Ruth the\l"
    .string "Moabitess, the wife of the dead, to\l"
    .string "raise up the name of the dead upon\l"
    .string "his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_6::
    .string "And the kinsman said, I cannot\n"
    .string "redeem it for myself, lest I mar\l"
    .string "mine own inheritance: redeem thou my\l"
    .string "right to thyself; for I cannot\l"
    .string "redeem it.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_7::
    .string "Now this was the manner in former\n"
    .string "time in Israel concerning redeeming\l"
    .string "and concerning changing, for to\l"
    .string "confirm all things; a man plucked\l"
    .string "off his shoe, and gave it to his\l"
    .string "neighbour: and this was a testimony\l"
    .string "in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_8::
    .string "Therefore the kinsman said unto\n"
    .string "Boaz, Buy it for thee. So he drew off\l"
    .string "his shoe.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_9::
    .string "And Boaz said unto the elders, and\n"
    .string "unto all the people, Ye are\l"
    .string "witnesses this day, that I have\l"
    .string "bought all that was Elimelech’s,\l"
    .string "and all that was Chilion’s and\l"
    .string "Mahlon’s, of the hand of Naomi.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_10::
    .string "Moreover Ruth the Moabitess, the\n"
    .string "wife of Mahlon, have I purchased to\l"
    .string "be my wife, to raise up the name of\l"
    .string "the dead upon his inheritance, that\l"
    .string "the name of the dead be not cut off\l"
    .string "from among his brethren, and from the\l"
    .string "gate of his place: ye are witnesses\l"
    .string "this day.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_11::
    .string "And all the people that were in\n"
    .string "the gate, and the elders, said, We\l"
    .string "are witnesses. The LORD make the\l"
    .string "woman that is come into thine house\l"
    .string "like Rachel and like Leah, which two\l"
    .string "did build the house of Israel: and\l"
    .string "do thou worthily in Ephratah, and be\l"
    .string "famous in Bethlehem:"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_12::
    .string "And let thy house be like the house\n"
    .string "of Pharez, whom Tamar bare unto\l"
    .string "Judah, of the seed which the LORD\l"
    .string "shall give thee of this young woman$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_13::
    .string "So Boaz took Ruth, and she was his\n"
    .string "wife: and when he went in unto her,\l"
    .string "the LORD gave her conception, and\l"
    .string "she bare a son.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_14::
    .string "And the women said unto Naomi,\n"
    .string "Blessed be the LORD, which hath not\l"
    .string "left thee this day without a kinsman,\l"
    .string "that his name may be famous in\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_15::
    .string "And he shall be unto thee a\n"
    .string "restorer of thy life, and a\l"
    .string "nourisher of thine old age: for thy\l"
    .string "daughter in law, which loveth thee,\l"
    .string "which is better to thee than seven\l"
    .string "sons, hath born him.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_16::
    .string "And Naomi took the child, and laid\n"
    .string "it in her bosom, and became nurse\l"
    .string "unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_17::
    .string "And the women her neighbours gave it\n"
    .string "a name, saying, There is a son born to\l"
    .string "Naomi; and they called his name\l"
    .string "Obed: he is the father of Jesse, the\l"
    .string "father of David.$"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_18::
    .string "Now these are the generations of\n"
    .string "Pharez: Pharez begat Hezron,"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_19::
    .string "And Hezron begat Ram, and Ram begat\n"
    .string "Amminadab,"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_20::
    .string "And Amminadab begat Nahshon, and\n"
    .string "Nahshon begat Salmon,"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_21::
    .string "And Salmon begat Boaz, and Boaz\n"
    .string "begat Obed,"
Bible_Text_Ruth_4_22::
    .string "And Obed begat Jesse, and Jesse\n"
    .string "begat David$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_1::
    .string "Now there was a certain man of\n"
    .string "Ramathaimzophim, of mount Ephraim,\l"
    .string "and his name was Elkanah, the son of\l"
    .string "Jeroham, the son of Elihu, the son of\l"
    .string "Tohu, the son of Zuph, an\l"
    .string "Ephrathite:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_2::
    .string "And he had two wives; the name of the\n"
    .string "one was Hannah, and the name of the\l"
    .string "other Peninnah: and Peninnah had\l"
    .string "children, but Hannah had no children$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_3::
    .string "And this man went up out of his city\n"
    .string "yearly to worship and to sacrifice\l"
    .string "unto the LORD of hosts in Shiloh. And\l"
    .string "the two sons of Eli, Hophni and\l"
    .string "Phinehas, the priests of the LORD,\l"
    .string "were there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_4::
    .string "And when the time was that Elkanah\n"
    .string "offered, he gave to Peninnah his\l"
    .string "wife, and to all her sons and her\l"
    .string "daughters, portions:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_5::
    .string "But unto Hannah he gave a worthy\n"
    .string "portion; for he loved Hannah: but\l"
    .string "the LORD had shut up her womb$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_6::
    .string "And her adversary also provoked\n"
    .string "her sore, for to make her fret,\l"
    .string "because the LORD had shut up her\l"
    .string "womb.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_7::
    .string "And as he did so year by year, when\n"
    .string "she went up to the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "so she provoked her; therefore she\l"
    .string "wept, and did not eat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_8::
    .string "Then said Elkanah her husband to\n"
    .string "her, Hannah, why weepest thou? and\l"
    .string "why eatest thou not? and why is thy\l"
    .string "heart grieved? am not I better to\l"
    .string "thee than ten sons?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_9::
    .string "So Hannah rose up after they had\n"
    .string "eaten in Shiloh, and after they had\l"
    .string "drunk. Now Eli the priest sat upon\l"
    .string "a seat by a post of the temple of\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_10::
    .string "And she was in bitterness of soul,\n"
    .string "and prayed unto the LORD, and wept\l"
    .string "sore.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_11::
    .string "And she vowed a vow, and said, O LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts, if thou wilt indeed look\l"
    .string "on the affliction of thine handmaid,\l"
    .string "and remember me, and not forget thine\l"
    .string "handmaid, but wilt give unto thine\l"
    .string "handmaid a man child, then I will\l"
    .string "give him unto the LORD all the days\l"
    .string "of his life, and there shall no\l"
    .string "razor come upon his head.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_12::
    .string "And it came to pass, as she\n"
    .string "continued praying before the LORD,\l"
    .string "that Eli marked her mouth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_13::
    .string "Now Hannah, she spake in her heart;\n"
    .string "only her lips moved, but her voice\l"
    .string "was not heard: therefore Eli thought\l"
    .string "she had been drunken.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_14::
    .string "And Eli said unto her, How long\n"
    .string "wilt thou be drunken? put away thy\l"
    .string "wine from thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_15::
    .string "And Hannah answered and said, No, my\n"
    .string "lord, I am a woman of a sorrowful\l"
    .string "spirit: I have drunk neither wine\l"
    .string "nor strong drink, but have poured\l"
    .string "out my soul before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_16::
    .string "Count not thine handmaid for a\n"
    .string "daughter of Belial: for out of the\l"
    .string "abundance of my complaint and grief\l"
    .string "have I spoken hitherto.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_17::
    .string "Then Eli answered and said, Go in\n"
    .string "peace: and the God of Israel grant\l"
    .string "thee thy petition that thou hast\l"
    .string "asked of him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_18::
    .string "And she said, Let thine handmaid\n"
    .string "find grace in thy sight. So the woman\l"
    .string "went her way, and did eat, and her\l"
    .string "countenance was no more sad.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_19::
    .string "And they rose up in the morning\n"
    .string "early, and worshipped before the\l"
    .string "LORD, and returned, and came to their\l"
    .string "house to Ramah: and Elkanah knew\l"
    .string "Hannah his wife; and the LORD\l"
    .string "remembered her.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_20::
    .string "Wherefore it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "time was come about after Hannah had\l"
    .string "conceived, that she bare a son, and\l"
    .string "called his name Samuel, saying,\l"
    .string "Because I have asked him of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_21::
    .string "And the man Elkanah, and all his\n"
    .string "house, went up to offer unto the LORD\l"
    .string "the yearly sacrifice, and his vow.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_22::
    .string "But Hannah went not up; for she said\n"
    .string "unto her husband, I will not go up\l"
    .string "until the child be weaned, and then\l"
    .string "I will bring him, that he may\l"
    .string "appear before the LORD, and there\l"
    .string "abide for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_23::
    .string "And Elkanah her husband said unto\n"
    .string "her, Do what seemeth thee good; tarry\l"
    .string "until thou have weaned him; only the\l"
    .string "LORD establish his word. So the\l"
    .string "woman abode, and gave her son suck\l"
    .string "until she weaned him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_24::
    .string "And when she had weaned him, she\n"
    .string "took him up with her, with three\l"
    .string "bullocks, and one ephah of flour,\l"
    .string "and a bottle of wine, and brought him\l"
    .string "unto the house of the LORD in Shiloh:\l"
    .string "and the child was young.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_25::
    .string "And they slew a bullock, and\n"
    .string "brought the child to Eli.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_26::
    .string "And she said, Oh my lord, as thy\n"
    .string "soul liveth, my lord, I am the\l"
    .string "woman that stood by thee here,\l"
    .string "praying unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_27::
    .string "For this child I prayed; and the\n"
    .string "LORD hath given me my petition which\l"
    .string "I asked of him:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_1_28::
    .string "Therefore also I have lent him to\n"
    .string "the LORD; as long as he liveth he\l"
    .string "shall be lent to the LORD. And he\l"
    .string "worshipped the LORD there$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_1::
    .string "And Hannah prayed, and said, My\n"
    .string "heart rejoiceth in the LORD, mine\l"
    .string "horn is exalted in the LORD: my mouth\l"
    .string "is enlarged over mine enemies;\l"
    .string "because I rejoice in thy salvation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_2::
    .string "There is none holy as the LORD: for\n"
    .string "there is none beside thee: neither is\l"
    .string "there any rock like our God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_3::
    .string "Talk no more so exceeding proudly;\n"
    .string "let not arrogancy come out of your\l"
    .string "mouth: for the LORD is a God of\l"
    .string "knowledge, and by him actions are\l"
    .string "weighed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_4::
    .string "The bows of the mighty men are\n"
    .string "broken, and they that stumbled are\l"
    .string "girded with strength.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_5::
    .string "They that were full have hired out\n"
    .string "themselves for bread; and they that\l"
    .string "were hungry ceased: so that the\l"
    .string "barren hath born seven; and she that\l"
    .string "hath many children is waxed feeble.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_6::
    .string "The LORD killeth, and maketh\n"
    .string "alive: he bringeth down to the\l"
    .string "grave, and bringeth up.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_7::
    .string "The LORD maketh poor, and maketh\n"
    .string "rich: he bringeth low, and lifteth\l"
    .string "up.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_8::
    .string "He raiseth up the poor out of the\n"
    .string "dust, and lifteth up the beggar from\l"
    .string "the dunghill, to set them among\l"
    .string "princes, and to make them inherit the\l"
    .string "throne of glory: for the pillars\l"
    .string "of the earth are the LORD’s, and he\l"
    .string "hath set the world upon them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_9::
    .string "He will keep the feet of his\n"
    .string "saints, and the wicked shall be\l"
    .string "silent in darkness; for by strength\l"
    .string "shall no man prevail.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_10::
    .string "The adversaries of the LORD shall\n"
    .string "be broken to pieces; out of heaven\l"
    .string "shall he thunder upon them: the\l"
    .string "LORD shall judge the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth; and he shall give strength\l"
    .string "unto his king, and exalt the horn of\l"
    .string "his anointed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_11::
    .string "And Elkanah went to Ramah to his\n"
    .string "house. And the child did minister\l"
    .string "unto the LORD before Eli the priest.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_12::
    .string "Now the sons of Eli were sons of\n"
    .string "Belial; they knew not the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_13::
    .string "And the priest’s custom with the\n"
    .string "people was, that, when any man\l"
    .string "offered sacrifice, the priest’s\l"
    .string "servant came, while the flesh was in\l"
    .string "seething, with a fleshhook of three\l"
    .string "teeth in his hand;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_14::
    .string "And he struck it into the pan, or\n"
    .string "kettle, or caldron, or pot; all\l"
    .string "that the fleshhook brought up the\l"
    .string "priest took for himself. So they did\l"
    .string "in Shiloh unto all the Israelites\l"
    .string "that came thither$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_15::
    .string "Also before they burnt the fat, the\n"
    .string "priest’s servant came, and said to\l"
    .string "the man that sacrificed, Give flesh\l"
    .string "to roast for the priest; for he\l"
    .string "will not have sodden flesh of thee,\l"
    .string "but raw.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_16::
    .string "And if any man said unto him, Let\n"
    .string "them not fail to burn the fat\l"
    .string "presently, and then take as much as\l"
    .string "thy soul desireth; then he would\l"
    .string "answer him, Nay; but thou shalt give\l"
    .string "it me now: and if not, I will take it\l"
    .string "by force.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_17::
    .string "Wherefore the sin of the young men\n"
    .string "was very great before the LORD: for\l"
    .string "men abhorred the offering of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_18::
    .string "But Samuel ministered before the\n"
    .string "LORD, being a child, girded with a\l"
    .string "linen ephod.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_19::
    .string "Moreover his mother made him a\n"
    .string "little coat, and brought it to him\l"
    .string "from year to year, when she came up\l"
    .string "with her husband to offer the yearly\l"
    .string "sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_20::
    .string "And Eli blessed Elkanah and his\n"
    .string "wife, and said, The LORD give thee\l"
    .string "seed of this woman for the loan\l"
    .string "which is lent to the LORD. And they\l"
    .string "went unto their own home.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_21::
    .string "And the LORD visited Hannah, so that\n"
    .string "she conceived, and bare three sons\l"
    .string "and two daughters. And the child\l"
    .string "Samuel grew before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_22::
    .string "Now Eli was very old, and heard\n"
    .string "all that his sons did unto all\l"
    .string "Israel; and how they lay with the\l"
    .string "women that assembled at the door of\l"
    .string "the tabernacle of the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_23::
    .string "And he said unto them, Why do ye such\n"
    .string "things? for I hear of your evil\l"
    .string "dealings by all this people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_24::
    .string "Nay, my sons; for it is no good\n"
    .string "report that I hear: ye make the\l"
    .string "LORD’s people to transgress.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_25::
    .string "If one man sin against another, the\n"
    .string "judge shall judge him: but if a man\l"
    .string "sin against the LORD, who shall\l"
    .string "intreat for him? Notwithstanding\l"
    .string "they hearkened not unto the voice of\l"
    .string "their father, because the LORD would\l"
    .string "slay them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_26::
    .string "And the child Samuel grew on, and\n"
    .string "was in favour both with the LORD, and\l"
    .string "also with men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_27::
    .string "And there came a man of God unto\n"
    .string "Eli, and said unto him, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD, Did I plainly appear\l"
    .string "unto the house of thy father, when\l"
    .string "they were in Egypt in Pharaoh’s\l"
    .string "house?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_28::
    .string "And did I choose him out of all the\n"
    .string "tribes of Israel to be my priest, to\l"
    .string "offer upon mine altar, to burn\l"
    .string "incense, to wear an ephod before me?\l"
    .string "and did I give unto the house of thy\l"
    .string "father all the offerings made by\l"
    .string "fire of the children of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_29::
    .string "Wherefore kick ye at my sacrifice\n"
    .string "and at mine offering, which I have\l"
    .string "commanded in my habitation; and\l"
    .string "honourest thy sons above me, to make\l"
    .string "yourselves fat with the chiefest of\l"
    .string "all the offerings of Israel my\l"
    .string "people?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_30::
    .string "Wherefore the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "saith, I said indeed that thy house,\l"
    .string "and the house of thy father, should\l"
    .string "walk before me for ever: but now the\l"
    .string "LORD saith, Be it far from me; for\l"
    .string "them that honour me I will honour,\l"
    .string "and they that despise me shall be\l"
    .string "lightly esteemed$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_31::
    .string "Behold, the days come, that I will\n"
    .string "cut off thine arm, and the arm of thy\l"
    .string "father’s house, that there shall\l"
    .string "not be an old man in thine house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_32::
    .string "And thou shalt see an enemy in my\n"
    .string "habitation, in all the wealth which\l"
    .string "God shall give Israel: and there\l"
    .string "shall not be an old man in thine\l"
    .string "house for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_33::
    .string "And the man of thine, whom I shall\n"
    .string "not cut off from mine altar, shall\l"
    .string "be to consume thine eyes, and to\l"
    .string "grieve thine heart: and all the\l"
    .string "increase of thine house shall die\l"
    .string "in the flower of their age.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_34::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto thee,\n"
    .string "that shall come upon thy two sons,\l"
    .string "on Hophni and Phinehas; in one day\l"
    .string "they shall die both of them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_35::
    .string "And I will raise me up a faithful\n"
    .string "priest, that shall do according to\l"
    .string "that which is in mine heart and in my\l"
    .string "mind: and I will build him a sure\l"
    .string "house; and he shall walk before\l"
    .string "mine anointed for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_2_36::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "every one that is left in thine\l"
    .string "house shall come and crouch to him\l"
    .string "for a piece of silver and a morsel\l"
    .string "of bread, and shall say, Put me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, into one of the priests’\l"
    .string "offices, that I may eat a piece of\l"
    .string "bread.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_1::
    .string "And the child Samuel ministered\n"
    .string "unto the LORD before Eli. And the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD was precious in\l"
    .string "those days; there was no open vision.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_2::
    .string "And it came to pass at that time,\n"
    .string "when Eli was laid down in his\l"
    .string "place, and his eyes began to wax dim,\l"
    .string "that he could not see;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_3::
    .string "And ere the lamp of God went out in\n"
    .string "the temple of the LORD, where the\l"
    .string "ark of God was, and Samuel was laid\l"
    .string "down to sleep;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_4::
    .string "That the LORD called Samuel: and\n"
    .string "he answered, Here am I$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_5::
    .string "And he ran unto Eli, and said, Here\n"
    .string "am I; for thou calledst me. And he\l"
    .string "said, I called not; lie down again.\l"
    .string "And he went and lay down.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_6::
    .string "And the LORD called yet again,\n"
    .string "Samuel. And Samuel arose and went to\l"
    .string "Eli, and said, Here am I; for thou\l"
    .string "didst call me. And he answered, I\l"
    .string "called not, my son; lie down again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_7::
    .string "Now Samuel did not yet know the\n"
    .string "LORD, neither was the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD yet revealed unto him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_8::
    .string "And the LORD called Samuel again\n"
    .string "the third time. And he arose and went\l"
    .string "to Eli, and said, Here am I; for thou\l"
    .string "didst call me. And Eli perceived\l"
    .string "that the LORD had called the child.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_9::
    .string "Therefore Eli said unto Samuel,\n"
    .string "Go, lie down: and it shall be, if he\l"
    .string "call thee, that thou shalt say,\l"
    .string "Speak, LORD; for thy servant\l"
    .string "heareth. So Samuel went and lay down\l"
    .string "in his place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_10::
    .string "And the LORD came, and stood, and\n"
    .string "called as at other times, Samuel,\l"
    .string "Samuel. Then Samuel answered,\l"
    .string "Speak; for thy servant heareth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_11::
    .string "And the LORD said to Samuel,\n"
    .string "Behold, I will do a thing in\l"
    .string "Israel, at which both the ears of\l"
    .string "every one that heareth it shall\l"
    .string "tingle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_12::
    .string "In that day I will perform against\n"
    .string "Eli all things which I have spoken\l"
    .string "concerning his house: when I begin, I\l"
    .string "will also make an end.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_13::
    .string "For I have told him that I will\n"
    .string "judge his house for ever for the\l"
    .string "iniquity which he knoweth; because\l"
    .string "his sons made themselves vile, and\l"
    .string "he restrained them not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_14::
    .string "And therefore I have sworn unto the\n"
    .string "house of Eli, that the iniquity of\l"
    .string "Eli’s house shall not be purged\l"
    .string "with sacrifice nor offering for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_15::
    .string "And Samuel lay until the morning,\n"
    .string "and opened the doors of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD. And Samuel feared to shew\l"
    .string "Eli the vision.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_16::
    .string "Then Eli called Samuel, and said,\n"
    .string "Samuel, my son. And he answered, Here\l"
    .string "am I.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_17::
    .string "And he said, What is the thing that\n"
    .string "the LORD hath said unto thee? I pray\l"
    .string "thee hide it not from me: God do so to\l"
    .string "thee, and more also, if thou hide any\l"
    .string "thing from me of all the things that\l"
    .string "he said unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_18::
    .string "And Samuel told him every whit, and\n"
    .string "hid nothing from him. And he said, It\l"
    .string "is the LORD: let him do what seemeth\l"
    .string "him good.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_19::
    .string "And Samuel grew, and the LORD was\n"
    .string "with him, and did let none of his\l"
    .string "words fall to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_20::
    .string "And all Israel from Dan even to\n"
    .string "Beersheba knew that Samuel was\l"
    .string "established to be a prophet of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_3_21::
    .string "And the LORD appeared again in\n"
    .string "Shiloh: for the LORD revealed\l"
    .string "himself to Samuel in Shiloh by the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_1::
    .string "And the word of Samuel came to all\n"
    .string "Israel. Now Israel went out against\l"
    .string "the Philistines to battle, and\l"
    .string "pitched beside Ebenezer: and the\l"
    .string "Philistines pitched in Aphek.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_2::
    .string "And the Philistines put\n"
    .string "themselves in array against Israel:\l"
    .string "and when they joined battle, Israel\l"
    .string "was smitten before the Philistines:\l"
    .string "and they slew of the army in the\l"
    .string "field about four thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_3::
    .string "And when the people were come into\n"
    .string "the camp, the elders of Israel\l"
    .string "said, Wherefore hath the LORD smitten\l"
    .string "us to day before the Philistines?\l"
    .string "Let us fetch the ark of the covenant\l"
    .string "of the LORD out of Shiloh unto us,\l"
    .string "that, when it cometh among us, it may\l"
    .string "save us out of the hand of our\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_4::
    .string "So the people sent to Shiloh,\n"
    .string "that they might bring from thence the\l"
    .string "ark of the covenant of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, which dwelleth between the\l"
    .string "cherubims: and the two sons of Eli,\l"
    .string "Hophni and Phinehas, were there with\l"
    .string "the ark of the covenant of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_5::
    .string "And when the ark of the covenant of\n"
    .string "the LORD came into the camp, all\l"
    .string "Israel shouted with a great shout,\l"
    .string "so that the earth rang again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_6::
    .string "And when the Philistines heard the\n"
    .string "noise of the shout, they said, What\l"
    .string "meaneth the noise of this great shout\l"
    .string "in the camp of the Hebrews? And they\l"
    .string "understood that the ark of the LORD\l"
    .string "was come into the camp.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_7::
    .string "And the Philistines were afraid,\n"
    .string "for they said, God is come into the\l"
    .string "camp. And they said, Woe unto us! for\l"
    .string "there hath not been such a thing\l"
    .string "heretofore.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_8::
    .string "Woe unto us! who shall deliver us\n"
    .string "out of the hand of these mighty Gods?\l"
    .string "these are the Gods that smote the\l"
    .string "Egyptians with all the plagues in\l"
    .string "the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_9::
    .string "Be strong and quit yourselves like\n"
    .string "men, O ye Philistines, that ye be not\l"
    .string "servants unto the Hebrews, as they\l"
    .string "have been to you: quit yourselves\l"
    .string "like men, and fight.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_10::
    .string "And the Philistines fought, and\n"
    .string "Israel was smitten, and they fled\l"
    .string "every man into his tent: and there\l"
    .string "was a very great slaughter; for\l"
    .string "there fell of Israel thirty\l"
    .string "thousand footmen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_11::
    .string "And the ark of God was taken; and the\n"
    .string "two sons of Eli, Hophni and\l"
    .string "Phinehas, were slain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_12::
    .string "And there ran a man of Benjamin out\n"
    .string "of the army, and came to Shiloh the\l"
    .string "same day with his clothes rent, and\l"
    .string "with earth upon his head.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_13::
    .string "And when he came, lo, Eli sat upon\n"
    .string "a seat by the wayside watching: for\l"
    .string "his heart trembled for the ark of God\l"
    .string " And when the man came into the city,\l"
    .string "and told it, all the city cried out.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_14::
    .string "And when Eli heard the noise of the\n"
    .string "crying, he said, What meaneth the\l"
    .string "noise of this tumult? And the man\l"
    .string "came in hastily, and told Eli.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_15::
    .string "Now Eli was ninety and eight years\n"
    .string "old; and his eyes were dim, that he\l"
    .string "could not see.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_16::
    .string "And the man said unto Eli, I am he\n"
    .string "that came out of the army, and I fled\l"
    .string "to day out of the army. And he said,\l"
    .string "What is there done, my son?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_17::
    .string "And the messenger answered and said,\n"
    .string "Israel is fled before the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and there hath been\l"
    .string "also a great slaughter among the\l"
    .string "people, and thy two sons also,\l"
    .string "Hophni and Phinehas, are dead, and\l"
    .string "the ark of God is taken$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he made\n"
    .string "mention of the ark of God, that he\l"
    .string "fell from off the seat backward by\l"
    .string "the side of the gate, and his neck\l"
    .string "brake, and he died: for he was an old\l"
    .string "man, and heavy. And he had judged\l"
    .string "Israel forty years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_19::
    .string "And his daughter in law, Phinehas’\n"
    .string "wife, was with child, near to be\l"
    .string "delivered: and when she heard the\l"
    .string "tidings that the ark of God was\l"
    .string "taken, and that her father in law and\l"
    .string "her husband were dead, she bowed\l"
    .string "herself and travailed; for her\l"
    .string "pains came upon her.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_20::
    .string "And about the time of her death the\n"
    .string "women that stood by her said unto\l"
    .string "her, Fear not; for thou hast born a\l"
    .string "son. But she answered not, neither\l"
    .string "did she regard it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_21::
    .string "And she named the child Ichabod,\n"
    .string "saying, The glory is departed from\l"
    .string "Israel: because the ark of God was\l"
    .string "taken, and because of her father in\l"
    .string "law and her husband.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_4_22::
    .string "And she said, The glory is departed\n"
    .string "from Israel: for the ark of God is\l"
    .string "taken.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_1::
    .string "And the Philistines took the ark of\n"
    .string "God, and brought it from Ebenezer\l"
    .string "unto Ashdod.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_2::
    .string "When the Philistines took the ark\n"
    .string "of God, they brought it into the\l"
    .string "house of Dagon, and set it by Dagon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_3::
    .string "And when they of Ashdod arose early\n"
    .string "on the morrow, behold, Dagon was\l"
    .string "fallen upon his face to the earth\l"
    .string "before the ark of the LORD. And they\l"
    .string "took Dagon, and set him in his place\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_4::
    .string "And when they arose early on the\n"
    .string "morrow morning, behold, Dagon was\l"
    .string "fallen upon his face to the ground\l"
    .string "before the ark of the LORD; and the\l"
    .string "head of Dagon and both the palms of\l"
    .string "his hands were cut off upon the\l"
    .string "threshold; only the stump of Dagon\l"
    .string "was left to him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_5::
    .string "Therefore neither the priests of\n"
    .string "Dagon, nor any that come into Dagon’s\l"
    .string "house, tread on the threshold of\l"
    .string "Dagon in Ashdod unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_6::
    .string "But the hand of the LORD was heavy\n"
    .string "upon them of Ashdod, and he\l"
    .string "destroyed them, and smote them with\l"
    .string "emerods, even Ashdod and the coasts\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_7::
    .string "And when the men of Ashdod saw that\n"
    .string "it was so, they said, The ark of the\l"
    .string "God of Israel shall not abide with\l"
    .string "us: for his hand is sore upon us, and\l"
    .string "upon Dagon our god.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_8::
    .string "They sent therefore and gathered\n"
    .string "all the lords of the Philistines\l"
    .string "unto them, and said, What shall we\l"
    .string "do with the ark of the God of Israel?\l"
    .string "And they answered, Let the ark of the\l"
    .string "God of Israel be carried about unto\l"
    .string "Gath. And they carried the ark of the\l"
    .string "God of Israel about thither.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_9::
    .string "And it was so, that, after they had\n"
    .string "carried it about, the hand of the\l"
    .string "LORD was against the city with a very\l"
    .string "great destruction: and he smote the\l"
    .string "men of the city, both small and\l"
    .string "great, and they had emerods in their\l"
    .string "secret parts.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_10::
    .string "Therefore they sent the ark of God\n"
    .string "to Ekron. And it came to pass, as the\l"
    .string "ark of God came to Ekron, that the\l"
    .string "Ekronites cried out, saying, They\l"
    .string "have brought about the ark of the God\l"
    .string "of Israel to us, to slay us and our\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_11::
    .string "So they sent and gathered together\n"
    .string "all the lords of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "and said, Send away the ark of the God\l"
    .string "of Israel, and let it go again to\l"
    .string "his own place, that it slay us not,\l"
    .string "and our people: for there was a\l"
    .string "deadly destruction throughout all\l"
    .string "the city; the hand of God was very\l"
    .string "heavy there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_5_12::
    .string "And the men that died not were\n"
    .string "smitten with the emerods: and the cry\l"
    .string "of the city went up to heaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_1::
    .string "And the ark of the LORD was in the\n"
    .string "country of the Philistines seven\l"
    .string "months.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_2::
    .string "And the Philistines called for\n"
    .string "the priests and the diviners,\l"
    .string "saying, What shall we do to the ark\l"
    .string "of the LORD? tell us wherewith we\l"
    .string "shall send it to his place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_3::
    .string "And they said, If ye send away the\n"
    .string "ark of the God of Israel, send it not\l"
    .string "empty; but in any wise return him a\l"
    .string "trespass offering: then ye shall be\l"
    .string "healed, and it shall be known to\l"
    .string "you why his hand is not removed from\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_4::
    .string "Then said they, What shall be the\n"
    .string "trespass offering which we shall\l"
    .string "return to him? They answered, Five\l"
    .string "golden emerods, and five golden\l"
    .string "mice, according to the number of the\l"
    .string "lords of the Philistines: for one\l"
    .string "plague was on you all, and on your\l"
    .string "lords.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_5::
    .string "Wherefore ye shall make images of\n"
    .string "your emerods, and images of your mice\l"
    .string "that mar the land; and ye shall\l"
    .string "give glory unto the God of Israel:\l"
    .string "peradventure he will lighten his\l"
    .string "hand from off you, and from off your\l"
    .string "gods, and from off your land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_6::
    .string "Wherefore then do ye harden your\n"
    .string "hearts, as the Egyptians and Pharaoh\l"
    .string "hardened their hearts? when he had\l"
    .string "wrought wonderfully among them, did\l"
    .string "they not let the people go, and\l"
    .string "they departed?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_7::
    .string "Now therefore make a new cart, and\n"
    .string "take two milch kine, on which there\l"
    .string "hath come no yoke, and tie the kine to\l"
    .string "the cart, and bring their calves\l"
    .string "home from them:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_8::
    .string "And take the ark of the LORD, and\n"
    .string "lay it upon the cart; and put the\l"
    .string "jewels of gold, which ye return him\l"
    .string "for a trespass offering, in a coffer\l"
    .string "by the side thereof; and send it\l"
    .string "away, that it may go$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_9::
    .string "And see, if it goeth up by the way\n"
    .string "of his own coast to Bethshemesh, then\l"
    .string "he hath done us this great evil: but\l"
    .string "if not, then we shall know that it\l"
    .string "is not his hand that smote us: it was\l"
    .string "a chance that happened to us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_10::
    .string "And the men did so; and took two\n"
    .string "milch kine, and tied them to the\l"
    .string "cart, and shut up their calves at\l"
    .string "home:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_11::
    .string "And they laid the ark of the LORD\n"
    .string "upon the cart, and the coffer with\l"
    .string "the mice of gold and the images of\l"
    .string "their emerods$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_12::
    .string "And the kine took the straight way\n"
    .string "to the way of Bethshemesh, and went\l"
    .string "along the highway, lowing as they\l"
    .string "went, and turned not aside to the\l"
    .string "right hand or to the left; and the\l"
    .string "lords of the Philistines went after\l"
    .string "them unto the border of Bethshemesh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_13::
    .string "And they of Bethshemesh were\n"
    .string "reaping their wheat harvest in the\l"
    .string "valley: and they lifted up their\l"
    .string "eyes, and saw the ark, and rejoiced\l"
    .string "to see it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_14::
    .string "And the cart came into the field of\n"
    .string "Joshua, a Bethshemite, and stood\l"
    .string "there, where there was a great stone:\l"
    .string "and they clave the wood of the cart,\l"
    .string "and offered the kine a burnt offering\l"
    .string "unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_15::
    .string "And the Levites took down the ark of\n"
    .string "the LORD, and the coffer that was\l"
    .string "with it, wherein the jewels of gold\l"
    .string "were, and put them on the great\l"
    .string "stone: and the men of Bethshemesh\l"
    .string "offered burnt offerings and\l"
    .string "sacrificed sacrifices the same day\l"
    .string "unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_16::
    .string "And when the five lords of the\n"
    .string "Philistines had seen it, they\l"
    .string "returned to Ekron the same day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_17::
    .string "And these are the golden emerods\n"
    .string "which the Philistines returned for a\l"
    .string "trespass offering unto the LORD; for\l"
    .string "Ashdod one, for Gaza one, for\l"
    .string "Askelon one, for Gath one, for Ekron\l"
    .string "one;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_18::
    .string "And the golden mice, according to\n"
    .string "the number of all the cities of the\l"
    .string "Philistines belonging to the five\l"
    .string "lords, both of fenced cities, and of\l"
    .string "country villages, even unto the\l"
    .string "great stone of Abel, whereon they\l"
    .string "set down the ark of the LORD: which\l"
    .string "stone remaineth unto this day in the\l"
    .string "field of Joshua, the Bethshemite$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_19::
    .string "And he smote the men of Bethshemesh,\n"
    .string "because they had looked into the ark\l"
    .string "of the LORD, even he smote of the\l"
    .string "people fifty thousand and\l"
    .string "threescore and ten men: and the\l"
    .string "people lamented, because the LORD\l"
    .string "had smitten many of the people with\l"
    .string "a great slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_20::
    .string "And the men of Bethshemesh said, Who\n"
    .string "is able to stand before this holy\l"
    .string "LORD God? and to whom shall he go up\l"
    .string "from us?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_6_21::
    .string "And they sent messengers to the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Kirjathjearim,\l"
    .string "saying, The Philistines have brought\l"
    .string "again the ark of the LORD; come ye\l"
    .string "down, and fetch it up to you$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_1::
    .string "And the men of Kirjathjearim came,\n"
    .string "and fetched up the ark of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and brought it into the house of\l"
    .string "Abinadab in the hill, and\l"
    .string "sanctified Eleazar his son to keep\l"
    .string "the ark of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, while the ark\n"
    .string "abode in Kirjathjearim, that the time\l"
    .string "was long; for it was twenty years:\l"
    .string "and all the house of Israel\l"
    .string "lamented after the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_3::
    .string "And Samuel spake unto all the\n"
    .string "house of Israel, saying, If ye do\l"
    .string "return unto the LORD with all your\l"
    .string "hearts, then put away the strange\l"
    .string "gods and Ashtaroth from among you,\l"
    .string "and prepare your hearts unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, and serve him only: and he\l"
    .string "will deliver you out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_4::
    .string "Then the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "put away Baalim and Ashtaroth, and\l"
    .string "served the LORD only.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_5::
    .string "And Samuel said, Gather all\n"
    .string "Israel to Mizpeh, and I will pray\l"
    .string "for you unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_6::
    .string "And they gathered together to\n"
    .string "Mizpeh, and drew water, and poured\l"
    .string "it out before the LORD, and fasted on\l"
    .string "that day, and said there, We have\l"
    .string "sinned against the LORD. And Samuel\l"
    .string "judged the children of Israel in\l"
    .string "Mizpeh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_7::
    .string "And when the Philistines heard that\n"
    .string "the children of Israel were\l"
    .string "gathered together to Mizpeh, the\l"
    .string "lords of the Philistines went up\l"
    .string "against Israel. And when the\l"
    .string "children of Israel heard it, they\l"
    .string "were afraid of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_8::
    .string "And the children of Israel said to\n"
    .string "Samuel, Cease not to cry unto the\l"
    .string "LORD our God for us, that he will\l"
    .string "save us out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_9::
    .string "And Samuel took a sucking lamb, and\n"
    .string "offered it for a burnt offering\l"
    .string "wholly unto the LORD: and Samuel\l"
    .string "cried unto the LORD for Israel; and\l"
    .string "the LORD heard him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_10::
    .string "And as Samuel was offering up the\n"
    .string "burnt offering, the Philistines drew\l"
    .string "near to battle against Israel: but\l"
    .string "the LORD thundered with a great\l"
    .string "thunder on that day upon the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and discomfited them;\l"
    .string "and they were smitten before Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_11::
    .string "And the men of Israel went out of\n"
    .string "Mizpeh, and pursued the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and smote them, until\l"
    .string "they came under Bethcar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_12::
    .string "Then Samuel took a stone, and set it\n"
    .string "between Mizpeh and Shen, and called\l"
    .string "the name of it Ebenezer, saying,\l"
    .string "Hitherto hath the LORD helped us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_13::
    .string "So the Philistines were subdued,\n"
    .string "and they came no more into the coast\l"
    .string "of Israel: and the hand of the LORD\l"
    .string "was against the Philistines all\l"
    .string "the days of Samuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_14::
    .string "And the cities which the\n"
    .string "Philistines had taken from Israel\l"
    .string "were restored to Israel, from Ekron\l"
    .string "even unto Gath; and the coasts\l"
    .string "thereof did Israel deliver out of\l"
    .string "the hands of the Philistines. And\l"
    .string "there was peace between Israel and\l"
    .string "the Amorites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_15::
    .string "And Samuel judged Israel all the\n"
    .string "days of his life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_16::
    .string "And he went from year to year in\n"
    .string "circuit to Bethel, and Gilgal, and\l"
    .string "Mizpeh, and judged Israel in all\l"
    .string "those places.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_7_17::
    .string "And his return was to Ramah; for\n"
    .string "there was his house; and there he\l"
    .string "judged Israel; and there he built an\l"
    .string "altar unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Samuel\n"
    .string "was old, that he made his sons judges\l"
    .string "over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_2::
    .string "Now the name of his firstborn was\n"
    .string "Joel; and the name of his second,\l"
    .string "Abiah: they were judges in Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_3::
    .string "And his sons walked not in his ways,\n"
    .string "but turned aside after lucre, and\l"
    .string "took bribes, and perverted judgment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_4::
    .string "Then all the elders of Israel\n"
    .string "gathered themselves together, and\l"
    .string "came to Samuel unto Ramah,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_5::
    .string "And said unto him, Behold, thou art\n"
    .string "old, and thy sons walk not in thy\l"
    .string "ways: now make us a king to judge us\l"
    .string "like all the nations$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_6::
    .string "But the thing displeased Samuel,\n"
    .string "when they said, Give us a king to\l"
    .string "judge us. And Samuel prayed unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_7::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Samuel,\n"
    .string "Hearken unto the voice of the\l"
    .string "people in all that they say unto\l"
    .string "thee: for they have not rejected\l"
    .string "thee, but they have rejected me, that\l"
    .string "I should not reign over them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_8::
    .string "According to all the works which\n"
    .string "they have done since the day that I\l"
    .string "brought them up out of Egypt even\l"
    .string "unto this day, wherewith they have\l"
    .string "forsaken me, and served other gods,\l"
    .string "so do they also unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_9::
    .string "Now therefore hearken unto their\n"
    .string "voice: howbeit yet protest\l"
    .string "solemnly unto them, and shew them\l"
    .string "the manner of the king that shall\l"
    .string "reign over them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_10::
    .string "And Samuel told all the words of\n"
    .string "the LORD unto the people that asked\l"
    .string "of him a king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_11::
    .string "And he said, This will be the\n"
    .string "manner of the king that shall reign\l"
    .string "over you: He will take your sons,\l"
    .string "and appoint them for himself, for\l"
    .string "his chariots, and to be his horsemen;\l"
    .string "and some shall run before his\l"
    .string "chariots.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_12::
    .string "And he will appoint him captains\n"
    .string "over thousands, and captains over\l"
    .string "fifties; and will set them to ear\l"
    .string "his ground, and to reap his harvest,\l"
    .string "and to make his instruments of war,\l"
    .string "and instruments of his chariots.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_13::
    .string "And he will take your daughters to\n"
    .string "be confectionaries, and to be cooks,\l"
    .string "and to be bakers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_14::
    .string "And he will take your fields, and\n"
    .string "your vineyards, and your oliveyards,\l"
    .string "even the best of them, and give them\l"
    .string "to his servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_15::
    .string "And he will take the tenth of your\n"
    .string "seed, and of your vineyards, and give\l"
    .string "to his officers, and to his servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_16::
    .string "And he will take your menservants,\n"
    .string "and your maidservants, and your\l"
    .string "goodliest young men, and your asses,\l"
    .string "and put them to his work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_17::
    .string "He will take the tenth of your\n"
    .string "sheep: and ye shall be his servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_18::
    .string "And ye shall cry out in that day\n"
    .string "because of your king which ye shall\l"
    .string "have chosen you; and the LORD will\l"
    .string "not hear you in that day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_19::
    .string "Nevertheless the people refused\n"
    .string "to obey the voice of Samuel; and they\l"
    .string "said, Nay; but we will have a king\l"
    .string "over us;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_20::
    .string "That we also may be like all the\n"
    .string "nations; and that our king may judge\l"
    .string "us, and go out before us, and fight\l"
    .string "our battles$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_21::
    .string "And Samuel heard all the words of\n"
    .string "the people, and he rehearsed them\l"
    .string "in the ears of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_8_22::
    .string "And the LORD said to Samuel,\n"
    .string "Hearken unto their voice, and make\l"
    .string "them a king. And Samuel said unto the\l"
    .string "men of Israel, Go ye every man unto\l"
    .string "his city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_1::
    .string "Now there was a man of Benjamin,\n"
    .string "whose name was Kish, the son of\l"
    .string "Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of\l"
    .string "Bechorath, the son of Aphiah, a\l"
    .string "Benjamite, a mighty man of power.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_2::
    .string "And he had a son, whose name was\n"
    .string "Saul, a choice young man, and a\l"
    .string "goodly: and there was not among the\l"
    .string "children of Israel a goodlier\l"
    .string "person than he: from his shoulders\l"
    .string "and upward he was higher than any of\l"
    .string "the people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_3::
    .string "And the asses of Kish Saul’s father\n"
    .string "were lost. And Kish said to Saul his\l"
    .string "son, Take now one of the servants\l"
    .string "with thee, and arise, go seek the\l"
    .string "asses.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_4::
    .string "And he passed through mount\n"
    .string "Ephraim, and passed through the\l"
    .string "land of Shalisha, but they found\l"
    .string "them not: then they passed through\l"
    .string "the land of Shalim, and there they\l"
    .string "were not: and he passed through the\l"
    .string "land of the Benjamites, but they\l"
    .string "found them not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_5::
    .string "And when they were come to the land\n"
    .string "of Zuph, Saul said to his servant\l"
    .string "that was with him, Come, and let us\l"
    .string "return; lest my father leave caring\l"
    .string "for the asses, and take thought for\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_6::
    .string "And he said unto him, Behold now,\n"
    .string "there is in this city a man of God,\l"
    .string "and he is an honourable man; all\l"
    .string "that he saith cometh surely to pass:\l"
    .string "now let us go thither; peradventure\l"
    .string "he can shew us our way that we should\l"
    .string "go.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_7::
    .string "Then said Saul to his servant, But,\n"
    .string "behold, if we go, what shall we\l"
    .string "bring the man? for the bread is spent\l"
    .string "in our vessels, and there is not a\l"
    .string "present to bring to the man of God:\l"
    .string "what have we?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_8::
    .string "And the servant answered Saul\n"
    .string "again, and said, Behold, I have here\l"
    .string "at hand the fourth part of a shekel\l"
    .string "of silver: that will I give to the\l"
    .string "man of God, to tell us our way$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_9::
    .string "(Beforetime in Israel, when a man\n"
    .string "went to enquire of God, thus he\l"
    .string "spake, Come, and let us go to the\l"
    .string "seer: for he that is now called a\l"
    .string "Prophet was beforetime called a\l"
    .string "Seer.)"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_10::
    .string "Then said Saul to his servant,\n"
    .string "Well said; come, let us go. So they\l"
    .string "went unto the city where the man of\l"
    .string "God was$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_11::
    .string "And as they went up the hill to\n"
    .string "the city, they found young maidens\l"
    .string "going out to draw water, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Is the seer here?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_12::
    .string "And they answered them, and said, He\n"
    .string "is; behold, he is before you: make\l"
    .string "haste now, for he came to day to the\l"
    .string "city; for there is a sacrifice of the\l"
    .string "people to day in the high place:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_13::
    .string "As soon as ye be come into the city,\n"
    .string "ye shall straightway find him,\l"
    .string "before he go up to the high place\l"
    .string "to eat: for the people will not\l"
    .string "eat until he come, because he doth\l"
    .string "bless the sacrifice; and afterwards\l"
    .string "they eat that be bidden. Now\l"
    .string "therefore get you up; for about this\l"
    .string "time ye shall find him$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_14::
    .string "And they went up into the city: and\n"
    .string "when they were come into the city,\l"
    .string "behold, Samuel came out against\l"
    .string "them, for to go up to the high\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_15::
    .string "Now the LORD had told Samuel in his\n"
    .string "ear a day before Saul came, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_16::
    .string "To morrow about this time I will\n"
    .string "send thee a man out of the land of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, and thou shalt anoint him\l"
    .string "to be captain over my people\l"
    .string "Israel, that he may save my people\l"
    .string "out of the hand of the Philistines:\l"
    .string "for I have looked upon my people,\l"
    .string "because their cry is come unto me$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_17::
    .string "And when Samuel saw Saul, the LORD\n"
    .string "said unto him, Behold the man whom I\l"
    .string "spake to thee of! this same shall\l"
    .string "reign over my people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_18::
    .string "Then Saul drew near to Samuel in\n"
    .string "the gate, and said, Tell me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, where the seer’s house is.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_19::
    .string "And Samuel answered Saul, and\n"
    .string "said, I am the seer: go up before me\l"
    .string "unto the high place; for ye shall\l"
    .string "eat with me to day, and to morrow I\l"
    .string "will let thee go, and will tell\l"
    .string "thee all that is in thine heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_20::
    .string "And as for thine asses that were\n"
    .string "lost three days ago, set not thy mind\l"
    .string "on them; for they are found. And on\l"
    .string "whom is all the desire of Israel?\l"
    .string "Is it not on thee, and on all thy\l"
    .string "father’s house?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_21::
    .string "And Saul answered and said, Am not I\n"
    .string "a Benjamite, of the smallest of the\l"
    .string "tribes of Israel? and my family the\l"
    .string "least of all the families of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Benjamin? wherefore then\l"
    .string "speakest thou so to me?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_22::
    .string "And Samuel took Saul and his\n"
    .string "servant, and brought them into the\l"
    .string "parlour, and made them sit in the\l"
    .string "chiefest place among them that were\l"
    .string "bidden, which were about thirty\l"
    .string "persons$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_23::
    .string "And Samuel said unto the cook,\n"
    .string "Bring the portion which I gave thee,\l"
    .string "of which I said unto thee, Set it by\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_24::
    .string "And the cook took up the shoulder,\n"
    .string "and that which was upon it, and set\l"
    .string "it before Saul. And Samuel said,\l"
    .string "Behold that which is left! set it\l"
    .string "before thee, and eat: for unto this\l"
    .string "time hath it been kept for thee\l"
    .string "since I said, I have invited the\l"
    .string "people. So Saul did eat with\l"
    .string "Samuel that day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_25::
    .string "And when they were come down from\n"
    .string "the high place into the city,\l"
    .string "Samuel communed with Saul upon the\l"
    .string "top of the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_26::
    .string "And they arose early: and it came to\n"
    .string "pass about the spring of the day,\l"
    .string "that Samuel called Saul to the\l"
    .string "top of the house, saying, Up, that I\l"
    .string "may send thee away. And Saul arose,\l"
    .string "and they went out both of them, he and\l"
    .string "Samuel, abroad.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_9_27::
    .string "And as they were going down to the\n"
    .string "end of the city, Samuel said to\l"
    .string "Saul, Bid the servant pass on before\l"
    .string "us, (and he passed on), but stand\l"
    .string "thou still a while, that I may shew\l"
    .string "thee the word of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_1::
    .string "Then Samuel took a vial of oil,\n"
    .string "and poured it upon his head, and\l"
    .string "kissed him, and said, Is it not\l"
    .string "because the LORD hath anointed thee\l"
    .string "to be captain over his inheritance?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_2::
    .string "When thou art departed from me to\n"
    .string "day, then thou shalt find two men by\l"
    .string "Rachel’s sepulchre in the border\l"
    .string "of Benjamin at Zelzah; and they\l"
    .string "will say unto thee, The asses which\l"
    .string "thou wentest to seek are found: and,\l"
    .string "lo, thy father hath left the care of\l"
    .string "the asses, and sorroweth for you,\l"
    .string "saying, What shall I do for my son?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_3::
    .string "Then shalt thou go on forward from\n"
    .string "thence, and thou shalt come to the\l"
    .string "plain of Tabor, and there shall\l"
    .string "meet thee three men going up to God\l"
    .string "to Bethel, one carrying three kids,\l"
    .string "and another carrying three loaves of\l"
    .string "bread, and another carrying a bottle\l"
    .string "of wine:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_4::
    .string "And they will salute thee, and\n"
    .string "give thee two loaves of bread; which\l"
    .string "thou shalt receive of their hands$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_5::
    .string "After that thou shalt come to the\n"
    .string "hill of God, where is the garrison\l"
    .string "of the Philistines: and it shall\l"
    .string "come to pass, when thou art come\l"
    .string "thither to the city, that thou shalt\l"
    .string "meet a company of prophets coming\l"
    .string "down from the high place with a\l"
    .string "psaltery, and a tabret, and a pipe,\l"
    .string "and a harp, before them; and they\l"
    .string "shall prophesy:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_6::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD will\n"
    .string "come upon thee, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "prophesy with them, and shalt be\l"
    .string "turned into another man$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_7::
    .string "And let it be, when these signs are\n"
    .string "come unto thee, that thou do as\l"
    .string "occasion serve thee; for God is with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_8::
    .string "And thou shalt go down before me to\n"
    .string "Gilgal; and, behold, I will come\l"
    .string "down unto thee, to offer burnt\l"
    .string "offerings, and to sacrifice\l"
    .string "sacrifices of peace offerings: seven\l"
    .string "days shalt thou tarry, till I come\l"
    .string "to thee, and shew thee what thou\l"
    .string "shalt do.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_9::
    .string "And it was so, that when he had\n"
    .string "turned his back to go from Samuel,\l"
    .string "God gave him another heart: and all\l"
    .string "those signs came to pass that day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_10::
    .string "And when they came thither to the\n"
    .string "hill, behold, a company of\l"
    .string "prophets met him; and the Spirit of\l"
    .string "God came upon him, and he\l"
    .string "prophesied among them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all that\n"
    .string "knew him beforetime saw that,\l"
    .string "behold, he prophesied among the\l"
    .string "prophets, then the people said one\l"
    .string "to another, What is this that is come\l"
    .string "unto the son of Kish? Is Saul also\l"
    .string "among the prophets?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_12::
    .string "And one of the same place answered\n"
    .string "and said, But who is their father?\l"
    .string "Therefore it became a proverb, Is\l"
    .string "Saul also among the prophets?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_13::
    .string "And when he had made an end of\n"
    .string "prophesying, he came to the high\l"
    .string "place$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_14::
    .string "And Saul’s uncle said unto him and\n"
    .string "to his servant, Whither went ye? And\l"
    .string "he said, To seek the asses: and when\l"
    .string "we saw that they were no where, we\l"
    .string "came to Samuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_15::
    .string "And Saul’s uncle said, Tell me, I\n"
    .string "pray thee, what Samuel said unto you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_16::
    .string "And Saul said unto his uncle, He\n"
    .string "told us plainly that the asses\l"
    .string "were found. But of the matter of the\l"
    .string "kingdom, whereof Samuel spake, he\l"
    .string "told him not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_17::
    .string "And Samuel called the people\n"
    .string "together unto the LORD to Mizpeh;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_18::
    .string "And said unto the children of\n"
    .string "Israel, Thus saith the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel, I brought up Israel out of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and delivered you out of the\l"
    .string "hand of the Egyptians, and out of the\l"
    .string "hand of all kingdoms, and of them\l"
    .string "that oppressed you:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_19::
    .string "And ye have this day rejected your\n"
    .string "God, who himself saved you out of\l"
    .string "all your adversities and your\l"
    .string "tribulations; and ye have said unto\l"
    .string "him, Nay, but set a king over us. Now\l"
    .string "therefore present yourselves\l"
    .string "before the LORD by your tribes, and\l"
    .string "by your thousands$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_20::
    .string "And when Samuel had caused all the\n"
    .string "tribes of Israel to come near, the\l"
    .string "tribe of Benjamin was taken.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_21::
    .string "When he had caused the tribe of\n"
    .string "Benjamin to come near by their\l"
    .string "families, the family of Matri was\l"
    .string "taken, and Saul the son of Kish was\l"
    .string "taken: and when they sought him, he\l"
    .string "could not be found.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_22::
    .string "Therefore they enquired of the LORD\n"
    .string "further, if the man should yet come\l"
    .string "thither. And the LORD answered,\l"
    .string "Behold he hath hid himself among\l"
    .string "the stuff.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_23::
    .string "And they ran and fetched him thence:\n"
    .string "and when he stood among the people,\l"
    .string "he was higher than any of the\l"
    .string "people from his shoulders and\l"
    .string "upward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_24::
    .string "And Samuel said to all the\n"
    .string "people, See ye him whom the LORD\l"
    .string "hath chosen, that there is none like\l"
    .string "him among all the people? And\l"
    .string "all the people shouted, and said,\l"
    .string "God save the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_25::
    .string "Then Samuel told the people the\n"
    .string "manner of the kingdom, and wrote it\l"
    .string "in a book, and laid it up before the\l"
    .string "LORD. And Samuel sent all the\l"
    .string "people away, every man to his house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_26::
    .string "And Saul also went home to Gibeah;\n"
    .string "and there went with him a band of men,\l"
    .string "whose hearts God had touched.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_10_27::
    .string "But the children of Belial said,\n"
    .string "How shall this man save us? And they\l"
    .string "despised him, and brought no\l"
    .string "presents. But he held his peace.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_1::
    .string "Then Nahash the Ammonite came up,\n"
    .string "and encamped against Jabeshgilead:\l"
    .string "and all the men of Jabesh said unto\l"
    .string "Nahash, Make a covenant with us, and\l"
    .string "we will serve thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_2::
    .string "And Nahash the Ammonite answered\n"
    .string "them, On this condition will I make\l"
    .string "a covenant with you, that I may\l"
    .string "thrust out all your right eyes, and\l"
    .string "lay it for a reproach upon all\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_3::
    .string "And the elders of Jabesh said unto\n"
    .string "him, Give us seven days’ respite,\l"
    .string "that we may send messengers unto\l"
    .string "all the coasts of Israel: and then,\l"
    .string "if there be no man to save us, we\l"
    .string "will come out to thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_4::
    .string "Then came the messengers to Gibeah\n"
    .string "of Saul, and told the tidings in the\l"
    .string "ears of the people: and all the\l"
    .string "people lifted up their voices, and\l"
    .string "wept.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_5::
    .string "And, behold, Saul came after the\n"
    .string "herd out of the field; and Saul\l"
    .string "said, What aileth the people that\l"
    .string "they weep? And they told him the\l"
    .string "tidings of the men of Jabesh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_6::
    .string "And the Spirit of God came upon\n"
    .string "Saul when he heard those tidings,\l"
    .string "and his anger was kindled greatly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_7::
    .string "And he took a yoke of oxen, and hewed\n"
    .string "them in pieces, and sent them\l"
    .string "throughout all the coasts of\l"
    .string "Israel by the hands of messengers,\l"
    .string "saying, Whosoever cometh not forth\l"
    .string "after Saul and after Samuel, so\l"
    .string "shall it be done unto his oxen. And\l"
    .string "the fear of the LORD fell on the\l"
    .string "people, and they came out with one\l"
    .string "consent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_8::
    .string "And when he numbered them in Bezek,\n"
    .string "the children of Israel were three\l"
    .string "hundred thousand, and the men of\l"
    .string "Judah thirty thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_9::
    .string "And they said unto the messengers\n"
    .string "that came, Thus shall ye say unto\l"
    .string "the men of Jabeshgilead, To morrow,\l"
    .string "by that time the sun be hot, ye\l"
    .string "shall have help. And the\l"
    .string "messengers came and shewed it to the\l"
    .string "men of Jabesh; and they were glad.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_10::
    .string "Therefore the men of Jabesh said, To\n"
    .string "morrow we will come out unto you,\l"
    .string "and ye shall do with us all that\l"
    .string "seemeth good unto you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_11::
    .string "And it was so on the morrow, that\n"
    .string "Saul put the people in three\l"
    .string "companies; and they came into the\l"
    .string "midst of the host in the morning\l"
    .string "watch, and slew the Ammonites until\l"
    .string "the heat of the day: and it came to\l"
    .string "pass, that they which remained were\l"
    .string "scattered, so that two of them were\l"
    .string "not left together.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_12::
    .string "And the people said unto Samuel,\n"
    .string "Who is he that said, Shall Saul\l"
    .string "reign over us? bring the men, that we\l"
    .string "may put them to death.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_13::
    .string "And Saul said, There shall not a\n"
    .string "man be put to death this day: for to\l"
    .string "day the LORD hath wrought salvation\l"
    .string "in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_14::
    .string "Then said Samuel to the people,\n"
    .string "Come, and let us go to Gilgal, and\l"
    .string "renew the kingdom there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_11_15::
    .string "And all the people went to\n"
    .string "Gilgal; and there they made Saul\l"
    .string "king before the LORD in Gilgal; and\l"
    .string "there they sacrificed sacrifices of\l"
    .string "peace offerings before the LORD; and\l"
    .string "there Saul and all the men of\l"
    .string "Israel rejoiced greatly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_1::
    .string "And Samuel said unto all Israel,\n"
    .string "Behold, I have hearkened unto your\l"
    .string "voice in all that ye said unto me,\l"
    .string "and have made a king over you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_2::
    .string "And now, behold, the king walketh\n"
    .string "before you: and I am old and\l"
    .string "grayheaded; and, behold, my sons are\l"
    .string "with you: and I have walked before\l"
    .string "you from my childhood unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_3::
    .string "Behold, here I am: witness against\n"
    .string "me before the LORD, and before his\l"
    .string "anointed: whose ox have I taken? or\l"
    .string "whose ass have I taken? or whom have I\l"
    .string "defrauded? whom have I oppressed?\l"
    .string "or of whose hand have I received any\l"
    .string "bribe to blind mine eyes therewith?\l"
    .string "and I will restore it you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_4::
    .string "And they said, Thou hast not\n"
    .string "defrauded us, nor oppressed us,\l"
    .string "neither hast thou taken ought of any\l"
    .string "man’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, The LORD is\n"
    .string "witness against you, and his anointed\l"
    .string "is witness this day, that ye have not\l"
    .string "found ought in my hand. And they\l"
    .string "answered, He is witness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_6::
    .string "And Samuel said unto the people,\n"
    .string "It is the LORD that advanced Moses\l"
    .string "and Aaron, and that brought your\l"
    .string "fathers up out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_7::
    .string "Now therefore stand still, that I\n"
    .string "may reason with you before the LORD\l"
    .string "of all the righteous acts of the\l"
    .string "LORD, which he did to you and to your\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_8::
    .string "When Jacob was come into Egypt, and\n"
    .string "your fathers cried unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "then the LORD sent Moses and Aaron,\l"
    .string "which brought forth your fathers out\l"
    .string "of Egypt, and made them dwell in\l"
    .string "this place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_9::
    .string "And when they forgat the LORD their\n"
    .string "God, he sold them into the hand of\l"
    .string "Sisera, captain of the host of\l"
    .string "Hazor, and into the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and into the hand of\l"
    .string "the king of Moab, and they fought\l"
    .string "against them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_10::
    .string "And they cried unto the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, We have sinned, because we have\l"
    .string "forsaken the LORD, and have served\l"
    .string "Baalim and Ashtaroth: but now\l"
    .string "deliver us out of the hand of our\l"
    .string "enemies, and we will serve thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_11::
    .string "And the LORD sent Jerubbaal, and\n"
    .string "Bedan, and Jephthah, and Samuel, and\l"
    .string "delivered you out of the hand of\l"
    .string "your enemies on every side, and ye\l"
    .string "dwelled safe.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_12::
    .string "And when ye saw that Nahash the king\n"
    .string "of the children of Ammon came\l"
    .string "against you, ye said unto me, Nay; but\l"
    .string "a king shall reign over us: when the\l"
    .string "LORD your God was your king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_13::
    .string "Now therefore behold the king whom\n"
    .string "ye have chosen, and whom ye have\l"
    .string "desired! and, behold, the LORD hath\l"
    .string "set a king over you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_14::
    .string "If ye will fear the LORD, and serve\n"
    .string "him, and obey his voice, and not\l"
    .string "rebel against the commandment of the\l"
    .string "LORD, then shall both ye and also\l"
    .string "the king that reigneth over you\l"
    .string "continue following the LORD your\l"
    .string "God:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_15::
    .string "But if ye will not obey the voice\n"
    .string "of the LORD, but rebel against the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD, then shall\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD be against you,\l"
    .string "as it was against your fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_16::
    .string "Now therefore stand and see this\n"
    .string "great thing, which the LORD will do\l"
    .string "before your eyes.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_17::
    .string "Is it not wheat harvest to day? I\n"
    .string "will call unto the LORD, and he\l"
    .string "shall send thunder and rain; that ye\l"
    .string "may perceive and see that your\l"
    .string "wickedness is great, which ye have\l"
    .string "done in the sight of the LORD, in\l"
    .string "asking you a king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_18::
    .string "So Samuel called unto the LORD;\n"
    .string "and the LORD sent thunder and rain\l"
    .string "that day: and all the people\l"
    .string "greatly feared the LORD and Samuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_19::
    .string "And all the people said unto\n"
    .string "Samuel, Pray for thy servants unto\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God, that we die not: for\l"
    .string "we have added unto all our sins this\l"
    .string "evil, to ask us a king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_20::
    .string "And Samuel said unto the people,\n"
    .string "Fear not: ye have done all this\l"
    .string "wickedness: yet turn not aside from\l"
    .string "following the LORD, but serve the\l"
    .string "LORD with all your heart;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_21::
    .string "And turn ye not aside: for then\n"
    .string "should ye go after vain things,\l"
    .string "which cannot profit nor deliver;\l"
    .string "for they are vain$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_22::
    .string "For the LORD will not forsake his\n"
    .string "people for his great name’s sake:\l"
    .string "because it hath pleased the LORD to\l"
    .string "make you his people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_23::
    .string "Moreover as for me, God forbid that\n"
    .string "I should sin against the LORD in\l"
    .string "ceasing to pray for you: but I will\l"
    .string "teach you the good and the right way:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_24::
    .string "Only fear the LORD, and serve him in\n"
    .string "truth with all your heart: for\l"
    .string "consider how great things he hath\l"
    .string "done for you$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_12_25::
    .string "But if ye shall still do\n"
    .string "wickedly, ye shall be consumed,\l"
    .string "both ye and your king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_1::
    .string "Saul reigned one year; and when he\n"
    .string "had reigned two years over Israel,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_2::
    .string "Saul chose him three thousand men\n"
    .string "of Israel; whereof two thousand were\l"
    .string "with Saul in Michmash and in mount\l"
    .string "Bethel, and a thousand were with\l"
    .string "Jonathan in Gibeah of Benjamin: and\l"
    .string "the rest of the people he sent\l"
    .string "every man to his tent$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_3::
    .string "And Jonathan smote the garrison of\n"
    .string "the Philistines that was in Geba,\l"
    .string "and the Philistines heard of it. And\l"
    .string "Saul blew the trumpet throughout\l"
    .string "all the land, saying, Let the\l"
    .string "Hebrews hear.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_4::
    .string "And all Israel heard say that\n"
    .string "Saul had smitten a garrison of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and that Israel also\l"
    .string "was had in abomination with the\l"
    .string "Philistines. And the people were\l"
    .string "called together after Saul to\l"
    .string "Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_5::
    .string "And the Philistines gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together to fight with\l"
    .string "Israel, thirty thousand chariots,\l"
    .string "and six thousand horsemen, and\l"
    .string "people as the sand which is on the\l"
    .string "sea shore in multitude: and they\l"
    .string "came up, and pitched in Michmash,\l"
    .string "eastward from Bethaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_6::
    .string "When the men of Israel saw that\n"
    .string "they were in a strait, (for the\l"
    .string "people were distressed,) then the\l"
    .string "people did hide themselves in\l"
    .string "caves, and in thickets, and in rocks,\l"
    .string "and in high places, and in pits.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_7::
    .string "And some of the Hebrews went over\n"
    .string "Jordan to the land of Gad and\l"
    .string "Gilead. As for Saul, he was yet in\l"
    .string "Gilgal, and all the people\l"
    .string "followed him trembling.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_8::
    .string "And he tarried seven days, according\n"
    .string "to the set time that Samuel had\l"
    .string "appointed: but Samuel came not to\l"
    .string "Gilgal; and the people were\l"
    .string "scattered from him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_9::
    .string "And Saul said, Bring hither a burnt\n"
    .string "offering to me, and peace offerings.\l"
    .string "And he offered the burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, that as soon as\n"
    .string "he had made an end of offering the\l"
    .string "burnt offering, behold, Samuel\l"
    .string "came; and Saul went out to meet him,\l"
    .string "that he might salute him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_11::
    .string "And Samuel said, What hast thou\n"
    .string "done? And Saul said, Because I saw\l"
    .string "that the people were scattered\l"
    .string "from me, and that thou camest not\l"
    .string "within the days appointed, and that\l"
    .string "the Philistines gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together at Michmash;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_12::
    .string "Therefore said I, The Philistines\n"
    .string "will come down now upon me to\l"
    .string "Gilgal, and I have not made\l"
    .string "supplication unto the LORD: I\l"
    .string "forced myself therefore, and offered\l"
    .string "a burnt offering$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_13::
    .string "And Samuel said to Saul, Thou hast\n"
    .string "done foolishly: thou hast not kept\l"
    .string "the commandment of the LORD thy God,\l"
    .string "which he commanded thee: for now\l"
    .string "would the LORD have established thy\l"
    .string "kingdom upon Israel for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_14::
    .string "But now thy kingdom shall not\n"
    .string "continue: the LORD hath sought him a\l"
    .string "man after his own heart, and the LORD\l"
    .string "hath commanded him to be captain\l"
    .string "over his people, because thou hast\l"
    .string "not kept that which the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_15::
    .string "And Samuel arose, and gat him up\n"
    .string "from Gilgal unto Gibeah of\l"
    .string "Benjamin. And Saul numbered the\l"
    .string "people that were present with him,\l"
    .string "about six hundred men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_16::
    .string "And Saul, and Jonathan his son, and\n"
    .string "the people that were present with\l"
    .string "them, abode in Gibeah of Benjamin:\l"
    .string "but the Philistines encamped in\l"
    .string "Michmash.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_17::
    .string "And the spoilers came out of the\n"
    .string "camp of the Philistines in three\l"
    .string "companies: one company turned unto\l"
    .string "the way that leadeth to Ophrah, unto\l"
    .string "the land of Shual:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_18::
    .string "And another company turned the way\n"
    .string "to Bethhoron: and another company\l"
    .string "turned to the way of the border that\l"
    .string "looketh to the valley of Zeboim\l"
    .string "toward the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_19::
    .string "Now there was no smith found\n"
    .string "throughout all the land of Israel:\l"
    .string "for the Philistines said, Lest the\l"
    .string "Hebrews make them swords or spears:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_20::
    .string "But all the Israelites went down\n"
    .string "to the Philistines, to sharpen\l"
    .string "every man his share, and his\l"
    .string "coulter, and his axe, and his mattock$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_21::
    .string "Yet they had a file for the\n"
    .string "mattocks, and for the coulters, and\l"
    .string "for the forks, and for the axes, and\l"
    .string "to sharpen the goads.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_22::
    .string "So it came to pass in the day of\n"
    .string "battle, that there was neither sword\l"
    .string "nor spear found in the hand of any of\l"
    .string "the people that were with Saul and\l"
    .string "Jonathan: but with Saul and with\l"
    .string "Jonathan his son was there found.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_13_23::
    .string "And the garrison of the Philistines\n"
    .string "went out to the passage of Michmash.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass upon a day,\n"
    .string "that Jonathan the son of Saul said\l"
    .string "unto the young man that bare his\l"
    .string "armour, Come, and let us go over to\l"
    .string "the Philistines’ garrison, that is\l"
    .string "on the other side. But he told not\l"
    .string "his father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_2::
    .string "And Saul tarried in the uttermost\n"
    .string "part of Gibeah under a pomegranate\l"
    .string "tree which is in Migron: and the\l"
    .string "people that were with him were\l"
    .string "about six hundred men;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_3::
    .string "And Ahiah, the son of Ahitub,\n"
    .string "Ichabod’s brother, the son of\l"
    .string "Phinehas, the son of Eli, the LORD’s\l"
    .string "priest in Shiloh, wearing an ephod.\l"
    .string "And the people knew not that\l"
    .string "Jonathan was gone$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_4::
    .string "And between the passages, by which\n"
    .string "Jonathan sought to go over unto the\l"
    .string "Philistines’ garrison, there was a\l"
    .string "sharp rock on the one side, and a\l"
    .string "sharp rock on the other side: and the\l"
    .string "name of the one was Bozez, and the\l"
    .string "name of the other Seneh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_5::
    .string "The forefront of the one was situate\n"
    .string "northward over against Michmash, and\l"
    .string "the other southward over against\l"
    .string "Gibeah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_6::
    .string "And Jonathan said to the young man\n"
    .string "that bare his armour, Come, and let\l"
    .string "us go over unto the garrison of these\l"
    .string "uncircumcised: it may be that the\l"
    .string "LORD will work for us: for there is\l"
    .string "no restraint to the LORD to save by\l"
    .string "many or by few.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_7::
    .string "And his armourbearer said unto him,\n"
    .string "Do all that is in thine heart: turn\l"
    .string "thee; behold, I am with thee\l"
    .string "according to thy heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_8::
    .string "Then said Jonathan, Behold, we\n"
    .string "will pass over unto these men, and\l"
    .string "we will discover ourselves unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_9::
    .string "If they say thus unto us, Tarry\n"
    .string "until we come to you; then we will\l"
    .string "stand still in our place, and\l"
    .string "will not go up unto them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_10::
    .string "But if they say thus, Come up unto\n"
    .string "us; then we will go up: for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath delivered them into our hand:\l"
    .string "and this shall be a sign unto us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_11::
    .string "And both of them discovered\n"
    .string "themselves unto the garrison of the\l"
    .string "Philistines: and the Philistines\l"
    .string "said, Behold, the Hebrews come forth\l"
    .string "out of the holes where they had hid\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_12::
    .string "And the men of the garrison answered\n"
    .string "Jonathan and his armourbearer, and\l"
    .string "said, Come up to us, and we will\l"
    .string "shew you a thing. And Jonathan said\l"
    .string "unto his armourbearer, Come up after\l"
    .string "me: for the LORD hath delivered them\l"
    .string "into the hand of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_13::
    .string "And Jonathan climbed up upon his\n"
    .string "hands and upon his feet, and his\l"
    .string "armourbearer after him: and they\l"
    .string "fell before Jonathan; and his\l"
    .string "armourbearer slew after him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_14::
    .string "And that first slaughter, which\n"
    .string "Jonathan and his armourbearer made,\l"
    .string "was about twenty men, within as it\l"
    .string "were an half acre of land, which a\l"
    .string "yoke of oxen might plow.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_15::
    .string "And there was trembling in the\n"
    .string "host, in the field, and among all\l"
    .string "the people: the garrison, and the\l"
    .string "spoilers, they also trembled, and\l"
    .string "the earth quaked: so it was a very\l"
    .string "great trembling.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_16::
    .string "And the watchmen of Saul in Gibeah\n"
    .string "of Benjamin looked; and, behold, the\l"
    .string "multitude melted away, and they\l"
    .string "went on beating down one another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_17::
    .string "Then said Saul unto the people\n"
    .string "that were with him, Number now, and\l"
    .string "see who is gone from us. And when they\l"
    .string "had numbered, behold, Jonathan and\l"
    .string "his armourbearer were not there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_18::
    .string "And Saul said unto Ahiah, Bring\n"
    .string "hither the ark of God. For the ark of\l"
    .string "God was at that time with the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, while Saul\n"
    .string "talked unto the priest, that the\l"
    .string "noise that was in the host of the\l"
    .string "Philistines went on and increased:\l"
    .string "and Saul said unto the priest,\l"
    .string "Withdraw thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_20::
    .string "And Saul and all the people that\n"
    .string "were with him assembled themselves,\l"
    .string "and they came to the battle: and,\l"
    .string "behold, every man’s sword was\l"
    .string "against his fellow, and there was a\l"
    .string "very great discomfiture.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_21::
    .string "Moreover the Hebrews that were with\n"
    .string "the Philistines before that time,\l"
    .string "which went up with them into the\l"
    .string "camp from the country round about,\l"
    .string "even they also turned to be with the\l"
    .string "Israelites that were with Saul and\l"
    .string "Jonathan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_22::
    .string "Likewise all the men of Israel\n"
    .string "which had hid themselves in mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim, when they heard that the\l"
    .string "Philistines fled, even they also\l"
    .string "followed hard after them in the\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_23::
    .string "So the LORD saved Israel that day:\n"
    .string "and the battle passed over unto\l"
    .string "Bethaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_24::
    .string "And the men of Israel were\n"
    .string "distressed that day: for Saul had\l"
    .string "adjured the people, saying, Cursed\l"
    .string "be the man that eateth any food\l"
    .string "until evening, that I may be avenged\l"
    .string "on mine enemies. So none of the\l"
    .string "people tasted any food.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_25::
    .string "And all they of the land came to a\n"
    .string "wood; and there was honey upon the\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_26::
    .string "And when the people were come into\n"
    .string "the wood, behold, the honey\l"
    .string "dropped; but no man put his hand to\l"
    .string "his mouth: for the people feared\l"
    .string "the oath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_27::
    .string "But Jonathan heard not when his\n"
    .string "father charged the people with the\l"
    .string "oath: wherefore he put forth the end\l"
    .string "of the rod that was in his hand, and\l"
    .string "dipped it in an honeycomb, and put\l"
    .string "his hand to his mouth; and his eyes\l"
    .string "were enlightened.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_28::
    .string "Then answered one of the people,\n"
    .string "and said, Thy father straitly\l"
    .string "charged the people with an oath,\l"
    .string "saying, Cursed be the man that eateth\l"
    .string "any food this day. And the people\l"
    .string "were faint.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_29::
    .string "Then said Jonathan, My father hath\n"
    .string "troubled the land: see, I pray you,\l"
    .string "how mine eyes have been enlightened,\l"
    .string "because I tasted a little of this\l"
    .string "honey.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_30::
    .string "How much more, if haply the\n"
    .string "people had eaten freely to day of\l"
    .string "the spoil of their enemies which\l"
    .string "they found? for had there not been\l"
    .string "now a much greater slaughter among\l"
    .string "the Philistines?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_31::
    .string "And they smote the Philistines that\n"
    .string "day from Michmash to Aijalon: and\l"
    .string "the people were very faint$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_32::
    .string "And the people flew upon the\n"
    .string "spoil, and took sheep, and oxen,\l"
    .string "and calves, and slew them on the\l"
    .string "ground: and the people did eat them\l"
    .string "with the blood.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_33::
    .string "Then they told Saul, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold, the people sin against the\l"
    .string "LORD, in that they eat with the blood\l"
    .string " And he said, Ye have transgressed:\l"
    .string "roll a great stone unto me this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_34::
    .string "And Saul said, Disperse\n"
    .string "yourselves among the people, and\l"
    .string "say unto them, Bring me hither every\l"
    .string "man his ox, and every man his sheep,\l"
    .string "and slay them here, and eat; and sin\l"
    .string "not against the LORD in eating with\l"
    .string "the blood. And all the people\l"
    .string "brought every man his ox with him\l"
    .string "that night, and slew them there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_35::
    .string "And Saul built an altar unto the\n"
    .string "LORD: the same was the first altar\l"
    .string "that he built unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_36::
    .string "And Saul said, Let us go down after\n"
    .string "the Philistines by night, and spoil\l"
    .string "them until the morning light, and\l"
    .string "let us not leave a man of them. And\l"
    .string "they said, Do whatsoever seemeth good\l"
    .string "unto thee. Then said the priest, Let\l"
    .string "us draw near hither unto God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_37::
    .string "And Saul asked counsel of God,\n"
    .string "Shall I go down after the\l"
    .string "Philistines? wilt thou deliver\l"
    .string "them into the hand of Israel? But he\l"
    .string "answered him not that day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_38::
    .string "And Saul said, Draw ye near hither,\n"
    .string "all the chief of the people: and\l"
    .string "know and see wherein this sin hath\l"
    .string "been this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_39::
    .string "For, as the LORD liveth, which\n"
    .string "saveth Israel, though it be in\l"
    .string "Jonathan my son, he shall surely die\l"
    .string " But there was not a man among all\l"
    .string "the people that answered him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_40::
    .string "Then said he unto all Israel, Be\n"
    .string "ye on one side, and I and Jonathan my\l"
    .string "son will be on the other side. And\l"
    .string "the people said unto Saul, Do what\l"
    .string "seemeth good unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_41::
    .string "Therefore Saul said unto the LORD\n"
    .string "God of Israel, Give a perfect lot.\l"
    .string "And Saul and Jonathan were taken:\l"
    .string "but the people escaped.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_42::
    .string "And Saul said, Cast lots between me\n"
    .string "and Jonathan my son. And Jonathan was\l"
    .string "taken.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_43::
    .string "Then Saul said to Jonathan, Tell\n"
    .string "me what thou hast done. And Jonathan\l"
    .string "told him, and said, I did but taste a\l"
    .string "little honey with the end of the rod\l"
    .string "that was in mine hand, and, lo, I\l"
    .string "must die.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_44::
    .string "And Saul answered, God do so and\n"
    .string "more also: for thou shalt surely\l"
    .string "die, Jonathan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_45::
    .string "And the people said unto Saul,\n"
    .string "Shall Jonathan die, who hath\l"
    .string "wrought this great salvation in\l"
    .string "Israel? God forbid: as the LORD\l"
    .string "liveth, there shall not one hair of\l"
    .string "his head fall to the ground; for he\l"
    .string "hath wrought with God this day. So\l"
    .string "the people rescued Jonathan, that\l"
    .string "he died not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_46::
    .string "Then Saul went up from following\n"
    .string "the Philistines: and the\l"
    .string "Philistines went to their own\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_47::
    .string "So Saul took the kingdom over\n"
    .string "Israel, and fought against all his\l"
    .string "enemies on every side, against Moab,\l"
    .string "and against the children of Ammon,\l"
    .string "and against Edom, and against the\l"
    .string "kings of Zobah, and against the\l"
    .string "Philistines: and whithersoever he\l"
    .string "turned himself, he vexed them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_48::
    .string "And he gathered an host, and smote\n"
    .string "the Amalekites, and delivered\l"
    .string "Israel out of the hands of them that\l"
    .string "spoiled them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_49::
    .string "Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan,\n"
    .string "and Ishui, and Melchishua: and the\l"
    .string "names of his two daughters were\l"
    .string "these; the name of the firstborn\l"
    .string "Merab, and the name of the younger\l"
    .string "Michal:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_50::
    .string "And the name of Saul’s wife was\n"
    .string "Ahinoam, the daughter of Ahimaaz: and\l"
    .string "the name of the captain of his host\l"
    .string "was Abner, the son of Ner, Saul’s\l"
    .string "uncle$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_51::
    .string "And Kish was the father of Saul; and\n"
    .string "Ner the father of Abner was the son\l"
    .string "of Abiel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_14_52::
    .string "And there was sore war against the\n"
    .string "Philistines all the days of Saul:\l"
    .string "and when Saul saw any strong man, or\l"
    .string "any valiant man, he took him unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_1::
    .string "Samuel also said unto Saul, The\n"
    .string "LORD sent me to anoint thee to be\l"
    .string "king over his people, over Israel:\l"
    .string "now therefore hearken thou unto the\l"
    .string "voice of the words of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I\n"
    .string "remember that which Amalek did to\l"
    .string "Israel, how he laid wait for him in\l"
    .string "the way, when he came up from Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_3::
    .string "Now go and smite Amalek, and\n"
    .string "utterly destroy all that they have,\l"
    .string "and spare them not; but slay both\l"
    .string "man and woman, infant and suckling,\l"
    .string "ox and sheep, camel and ass.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_4::
    .string "And Saul gathered the people\n"
    .string "together, and numbered them in\l"
    .string "Telaim, two hundred thousand\l"
    .string "footmen, and ten thousand men of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_5::
    .string "And Saul came to a city of Amalek,\n"
    .string "and laid wait in the valley.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_6::
    .string "And Saul said unto the Kenites, Go,\n"
    .string "depart, get you down from among the\l"
    .string "Amalekites, lest I destroy you with\l"
    .string "them: for ye shewed kindness to all\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, when they\l"
    .string "came up out of Egypt. So the Kenites\l"
    .string "departed from among the Amalekites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_7::
    .string "And Saul smote the Amalekites from\n"
    .string "Havilah until thou comest to Shur,\l"
    .string "that is over against Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_8::
    .string "And he took Agag the king of the\n"
    .string "Amalekites alive, and utterly\l"
    .string "destroyed all the people with the\l"
    .string "edge of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_9::
    .string "But Saul and the people spared\n"
    .string "Agag, and the best of the sheep, and\l"
    .string "of the oxen, and of the fatlings, and\l"
    .string "the lambs, and all that was good,\l"
    .string "and would not utterly destroy them:\l"
    .string "but every thing that was vile and\l"
    .string "refuse, that they destroyed utterly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_10::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "Samuel, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_11::
    .string "It repenteth me that I have set up\n"
    .string "Saul to be king: for he is turned\l"
    .string "back from following me, and hath not\l"
    .string "performed my commandments. And it\l"
    .string "grieved Samuel; and he cried unto\l"
    .string "the LORD all night$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_12::
    .string "And when Samuel rose early to meet\n"
    .string "Saul in the morning, it was told\l"
    .string "Samuel, saying, Saul came to\l"
    .string "Carmel, and, behold, he set him up a\l"
    .string "place, and is gone about, and passed\l"
    .string "on, and gone down to Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_13::
    .string "And Samuel came to Saul: and Saul\n"
    .string "said unto him, Blessed be thou of the\l"
    .string "LORD: I have performed the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_14::
    .string "And Samuel said, What meaneth then\n"
    .string "this bleating of the sheep in mine\l"
    .string "ears, and the lowing of the oxen\l"
    .string "which I hear?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_15::
    .string "And Saul said, They have brought\n"
    .string "them from the Amalekites: for the\l"
    .string "people spared the best of the\l"
    .string "sheep and of the oxen, to sacrifice\l"
    .string "unto the LORD thy God; and the rest we\l"
    .string "have utterly destroyed$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_16::
    .string "Then Samuel said unto Saul, Stay,\n"
    .string "and I will tell thee what the LORD\l"
    .string "hath said to me this night. And he\l"
    .string "said unto him, Say on.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_17::
    .string "And Samuel said, When thou wast\n"
    .string "little in thine own sight, wast thou\l"
    .string "not made the head of the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel, and the LORD anointed thee\l"
    .string "king over Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_18::
    .string "And the LORD sent thee on a journey,\n"
    .string "and said, Go and utterly destroy the\l"
    .string "sinners the Amalekites, and fight\l"
    .string "against them until they be consumed$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_19::
    .string "Wherefore then didst thou not obey\n"
    .string "the voice of the LORD, but didst fly\l"
    .string "upon the spoil, and didst evil in\l"
    .string "the sight of the LORD?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_20::
    .string "And Saul said unto Samuel, Yea, I\n"
    .string "have obeyed the voice of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and have gone the way which the LORD\l"
    .string "sent me, and have brought Agag the\l"
    .string "king of Amalek, and have utterly\l"
    .string "destroyed the Amalekites$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_21::
    .string "But the people took of the spoil,\n"
    .string "sheep and oxen, the chief of the\l"
    .string "things which should have been\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed, to sacrifice unto\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God in Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_22::
    .string "And Samuel said, Hath the LORD as\n"
    .string "great delight in burnt offerings and\l"
    .string "sacrifices, as in obeying the voice\l"
    .string "of the LORD? Behold, to obey is\l"
    .string "better than sacrifice, and to hearken\l"
    .string "than the fat of rams.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_23::
    .string "For rebellion is as the sin of\n"
    .string "witchcraft, and stubbornness is as\l"
    .string "iniquity and idolatry. Because thou\l"
    .string "hast rejected the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "he hath also rejected thee from\l"
    .string "being king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_24::
    .string "And Saul said unto Samuel, I have\n"
    .string "sinned: for I have transgressed the\l"
    .string "commandment of the LORD, and thy\l"
    .string "words: because I feared the people,\l"
    .string "and obeyed their voice.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_25::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, pardon\n"
    .string "my sin, and turn again with me, that I\l"
    .string "may worship the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_26::
    .string "And Samuel said unto Saul, I will\n"
    .string "not return with thee: for thou hast\l"
    .string "rejected the word of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "the LORD hath rejected thee from\l"
    .string "being king over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_27::
    .string "And as Samuel turned about to go\n"
    .string "away, he laid hold upon the skirt\l"
    .string "of his mantle, and it rent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_28::
    .string "And Samuel said unto him, The LORD\n"
    .string "hath rent the kingdom of Israel from\l"
    .string "thee this day, and hath given it to a\l"
    .string "neighbour of thine, that is better\l"
    .string "than thou.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_29::
    .string "And also the Strength of Israel\n"
    .string "will not lie nor repent: for he is\l"
    .string "not a man, that he should repent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_30::
    .string "Then he said, I have sinned: yet\n"
    .string "honour me now, I pray thee, before\l"
    .string "the elders of my people, and\l"
    .string "before Israel, and turn again with\l"
    .string "me, that I may worship the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_31::
    .string "So Samuel turned again after Saul;\n"
    .string "and Saul worshipped the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_32::
    .string "Then said Samuel, Bring ye hither\n"
    .string "to me Agag the king of the Amalekites\l"
    .string " And Agag came unto him delicately.\l"
    .string "And Agag said, Surely the bitterness\l"
    .string "of death is past.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_33::
    .string "And Samuel said, As the sword hath\n"
    .string "made women childless, so shall thy\l"
    .string "mother be childless among women.\l"
    .string "And Samuel hewed Agag in pieces\l"
    .string "before the LORD in Gilgal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_34::
    .string "Then Samuel went to Ramah; and Saul\n"
    .string "went up to his house to Gibeah of\l"
    .string "Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_15_35::
    .string "And Samuel came no more to see Saul\n"
    .string "until the day of his death:\l"
    .string "nevertheless Samuel mourned for\l"
    .string "Saul: and the LORD repented that he\l"
    .string "had made Saul king over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_1::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Samuel, How\n"
    .string "long wilt thou mourn for Saul,\l"
    .string "seeing I have rejected him from\l"
    .string "reigning over Israel? fill thine\l"
    .string "horn with oil, and go, I will send\l"
    .string "thee to Jesse the Bethlehemite: for\l"
    .string "I have provided me a king among his\l"
    .string "sons.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_2::
    .string "And Samuel said, How can I go? if\n"
    .string "Saul hear it, he will kill me. And\l"
    .string "the LORD said, Take an heifer with\l"
    .string "thee, and say, I am come to sacrifice\l"
    .string "to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_3::
    .string "And call Jesse to the sacrifice,\n"
    .string "and I will shew thee what thou\l"
    .string "shalt do: and thou shalt anoint unto\l"
    .string "me him whom I name unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_4::
    .string "And Samuel did that which the LORD\n"
    .string "spake, and came to Bethlehem. And\l"
    .string "the elders of the town trembled at\l"
    .string "his coming, and said, Comest thou\l"
    .string "peaceably?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_5::
    .string "And he said, Peaceably: I am come to\n"
    .string "sacrifice unto the LORD: sanctify\l"
    .string "yourselves, and come with me to the\l"
    .string "sacrifice. And he sanctified Jesse\l"
    .string "and his sons, and called them to the\l"
    .string "sacrifice$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they were\n"
    .string "come, that he looked on Eliab, and\l"
    .string "said, Surely the LORD’s anointed is\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_7::
    .string "But the LORD said unto Samuel, Look\n"
    .string "not on his countenance, or on the\l"
    .string "height of his stature; because I have\l"
    .string "refused him: for the LORD seeth not\l"
    .string "as man seeth; for man looketh on the\l"
    .string "outward appearance, but the LORD\l"
    .string "looketh on the heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_8::
    .string "Then Jesse called Abinadab, and\n"
    .string "made him pass before Samuel. And he\l"
    .string "said, Neither hath the LORD chosen\l"
    .string "this.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_9::
    .string "Then Jesse made Shammah to pass by.\n"
    .string "And he said, Neither hath the LORD\l"
    .string "chosen this.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_10::
    .string "Again, Jesse made seven of his sons\n"
    .string "to pass before Samuel. And Samuel\l"
    .string "said unto Jesse, The LORD hath not\l"
    .string "chosen these.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_11::
    .string "And Samuel said unto Jesse, Are\n"
    .string "here all thy children? And he said,\l"
    .string "There remaineth yet the youngest,\l"
    .string "and, behold, he keepeth the sheep.\l"
    .string "And Samuel said unto Jesse, Send and\l"
    .string "fetch him: for we will not sit down\l"
    .string "till he come hither.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_12::
    .string "And he sent, and brought him in. Now\n"
    .string "he was ruddy, and withal of a\l"
    .string "beautiful countenance, and goodly\l"
    .string "to look to. And the LORD said, Arise,\l"
    .string "anoint him: for this is he.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_13::
    .string "Then Samuel took the horn of oil,\n"
    .string "and anointed him in the midst of his\l"
    .string "brethren: and the Spirit of the LORD\l"
    .string "came upon David from that day forward\l"
    .string " So Samuel rose up, and went to\l"
    .string "Ramah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_14::
    .string "But the Spirit of the LORD\n"
    .string "departed from Saul, and an evil\l"
    .string "spirit from the LORD troubled him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_15::
    .string "And Saul’s servants said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold now, an evil spirit from God\l"
    .string "troubleth thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_16::
    .string "Let our lord now command thy\n"
    .string "servants, which are before thee, to\l"
    .string "seek out a man, who is a cunning\l"
    .string "player on an harp: and it shall\l"
    .string "come to pass, when the evil spirit\l"
    .string "from God is upon thee, that he\l"
    .string "shall play with his hand, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be well.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_17::
    .string "And Saul said unto his servants,\n"
    .string "Provide me now a man that can play\l"
    .string "well, and bring him to me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_18::
    .string "Then answered one of the servants,\n"
    .string "and said, Behold, I have seen a son\l"
    .string "of Jesse the Bethlehemite, that is\l"
    .string "cunning in playing, and a mighty\l"
    .string "valiant man, and a man of war, and\l"
    .string "prudent in matters, and a comely\l"
    .string "person, and the LORD is with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_19::
    .string "Wherefore Saul sent messengers\n"
    .string "unto Jesse, and said, Send me David\l"
    .string "thy son, which is with the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_20::
    .string "And Jesse took an ass laden with\n"
    .string "bread, and a bottle of wine, and a\l"
    .string "kid, and sent them by David his son\l"
    .string "unto Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_21::
    .string "And David came to Saul, and stood\n"
    .string "before him: and he loved him\l"
    .string "greatly; and he became his\l"
    .string "armourbearer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_22::
    .string "And Saul sent to Jesse, saying, Let\n"
    .string "David, I pray thee, stand before me;\l"
    .string "for he hath found favour in my sight.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_16_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the evil\n"
    .string "spirit from God was upon Saul, that\l"
    .string "David took an harp, and played with\l"
    .string "his hand: so Saul was refreshed, and\l"
    .string "was well, and the evil spirit\l"
    .string "departed from him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_1::
    .string "Now the Philistines gathered\n"
    .string "together their armies to battle, and\l"
    .string "were gathered together at Shochoh,\l"
    .string "which belongeth to Judah, and\l"
    .string "pitched between Shochoh and Azekah,\l"
    .string "in Ephesdammim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_2::
    .string "And Saul and the men of Israel were\n"
    .string "gathered together, and pitched by\l"
    .string "the valley of Elah, and set the\l"
    .string "battle in array against the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_3::
    .string "And the Philistines stood on a\n"
    .string "mountain on the one side, and Israel\l"
    .string "stood on a mountain on the other\l"
    .string "side: and there was a valley between\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_4::
    .string "And there went out a champion out\n"
    .string "of the camp of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "named Goliath, of Gath, whose height\l"
    .string "was six cubits and a span.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_5::
    .string "And he had an helmet of brass upon\n"
    .string "his head, and he was armed with a coat\l"
    .string "of mail; and the weight of the coat\l"
    .string "was five thousand shekels of brass.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_6::
    .string "And he had greaves of brass upon\n"
    .string "his legs, and a target of brass\l"
    .string "between his shoulders.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_7::
    .string "And the staff of his spear was like\n"
    .string "a weaver’s beam; and his spear’s\l"
    .string "head weighed six hundred shekels of\l"
    .string "iron: and one bearing a shield went\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_8::
    .string "And he stood and cried unto the\n"
    .string "armies of Israel, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Why are ye come out to set your\l"
    .string "battle in array? am not I a\l"
    .string "Philistine, and ye servants to\l"
    .string "Saul? choose you a man for you, and\l"
    .string "let him come down to me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_9::
    .string "If he be able to fight with me, and\n"
    .string "to kill me, then will we be your\l"
    .string "servants: but if I prevail against\l"
    .string "him, and kill him, then shall ye be\l"
    .string "our servants, and serve us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_10::
    .string "And the Philistine said, I defy the\n"
    .string "armies of Israel this day; give me a\l"
    .string "man, that we may fight together.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_11::
    .string "When Saul and all Israel heard\n"
    .string "those words of the Philistine, they\l"
    .string "were dismayed, and greatly afraid.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_12::
    .string "Now David was the son of that\n"
    .string "Ephrathite of Bethlehemjudah, whose\l"
    .string "name was Jesse; and he had eight\l"
    .string "sons: and the man went among men for\l"
    .string "an old man in the days of Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_13::
    .string "And the three eldest sons of Jesse\n"
    .string "went and followed Saul to the\l"
    .string "battle: and the names of his three\l"
    .string "sons that went to the battle were\l"
    .string "Eliab the firstborn, and next unto\l"
    .string "him Abinadab, and the third Shammah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_14::
    .string "And David was the youngest: and the\n"
    .string "three eldest followed Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_15::
    .string "But David went and returned from\n"
    .string "Saul to feed his father’s sheep at\l"
    .string "Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_16::
    .string "And the Philistine drew near\n"
    .string "morning and evening, and presented\l"
    .string "himself forty days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_17::
    .string "And Jesse said unto David his son,\n"
    .string "Take now for thy brethren an ephah\l"
    .string "of this parched corn, and these ten\l"
    .string "loaves, and run to the camp of thy\l"
    .string "brethren;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_18::
    .string "And carry these ten cheeses unto the\n"
    .string "captain of their thousand, and look\l"
    .string "how thy brethren fare, and take their\l"
    .string "pledge$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_19::
    .string "Now Saul, and they, and all the\n"
    .string "men of Israel, were in the valley\l"
    .string "of Elah, fighting with the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_20::
    .string "And David rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and left the sheep with a\l"
    .string "keeper, and took, and went, as Jesse\l"
    .string "had commanded him; and he came to the\l"
    .string "trench, as the host was going forth\l"
    .string "to the fight, and shouted for the\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_21::
    .string "For Israel and the Philistines had\n"
    .string "put the battle in array, army\l"
    .string "against army.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_22::
    .string "And David left his carriage in the\n"
    .string "hand of the keeper of the carriage,\l"
    .string "and ran into the army, and came and\l"
    .string "saluted his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_23::
    .string "And as he talked with them, behold,\n"
    .string "there came up the champion, the\l"
    .string "Philistine of Gath, Goliath by\l"
    .string "name, out of the armies of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and spake according to\l"
    .string "the same words: and David heard them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_24::
    .string "And all the men of Israel, when\n"
    .string "they saw the man, fled from him, and\l"
    .string "were sore afraid.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_25::
    .string "And the men of Israel said, Have ye\n"
    .string "seen this man that is come up?\l"
    .string "surely to defy Israel is he come\l"
    .string "up: and it shall be, that the man\l"
    .string "who killeth him, the king will\l"
    .string "enrich him with great riches, and\l"
    .string "will give him his daughter, and make\l"
    .string "his father’s house free in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_26::
    .string "And David spake to the men that\n"
    .string "stood by him, saying, What shall be\l"
    .string "done to the man that killeth this\l"
    .string "Philistine, and taketh away the\l"
    .string "reproach from Israel? for who is\l"
    .string "this uncircumcised Philistine, that\l"
    .string "he should defy the armies of the\l"
    .string "living God?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_27::
    .string "And the people answered him after\n"
    .string "this manner, saying, So shall it be\l"
    .string "done to the man that killeth him$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_28::
    .string "And Eliab his eldest brother heard\n"
    .string "when he spake unto the men; and\l"
    .string "Eliab’s anger was kindled against\l"
    .string "David, and he said, Why camest thou\l"
    .string "down hither? and with whom hast thou\l"
    .string "left those few sheep in the\l"
    .string "wilderness? I know thy pride, and\l"
    .string "the naughtiness of thine heart; for\l"
    .string "thou art come down that thou mightest\l"
    .string "see the battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_29::
    .string "And David said, What have I now\n"
    .string "done? Is there not a cause?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_30::
    .string "And he turned from him toward\n"
    .string "another, and spake after the same\l"
    .string "manner: and the people answered him\l"
    .string "again after the former manner$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_31::
    .string "And when the words were heard which\n"
    .string "David spake, they rehearsed them\l"
    .string "before Saul: and he sent for him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_32::
    .string "And David said to Saul, Let no man’s\n"
    .string "heart fail because of him; thy\l"
    .string "servant will go and fight with this\l"
    .string "Philistine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_33::
    .string "And Saul said to David, Thou art not\n"
    .string "able to go against this Philistine\l"
    .string "to fight with him: for thou art but a\l"
    .string "youth, and he a man of war from his\l"
    .string "youth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_34::
    .string "And David said unto Saul, Thy\n"
    .string "servant kept his father’s sheep,\l"
    .string "and there came a lion, and a bear,\l"
    .string "and took a lamb out of the flock:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_35::
    .string "And I went out after him, and smote\n"
    .string "him, and delivered it out of his\l"
    .string "mouth: and when he arose against me,\l"
    .string "I caught him by his beard, and smote\l"
    .string "him, and slew him$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_36::
    .string "Thy servant slew both the lion and\n"
    .string "the bear: and this uncircumcised\l"
    .string "Philistine shall be as one of them,\l"
    .string "seeing he hath defied the armies of\l"
    .string "the living God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_37::
    .string "David said moreover, The LORD that\n"
    .string "delivered me out of the paw of the\l"
    .string "lion, and out of the paw of the bear,\l"
    .string "he will deliver me out of the hand\l"
    .string "of this Philistine. And Saul said\l"
    .string "unto David, Go, and the LORD be with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_38::
    .string "And Saul armed David with his\n"
    .string "armour, and he put an helmet of\l"
    .string "brass upon his head; also he armed\l"
    .string "him with a coat of mail.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_39::
    .string "And David girded his sword upon his\n"
    .string "armour, and he assayed to go; for he\l"
    .string "had not proved it. And David said\l"
    .string "unto Saul, I cannot go with these;\l"
    .string "for I have not proved them. And David\l"
    .string "put them off him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_40::
    .string "And he took his staff in his hand,\n"
    .string "and chose him five smooth stones out\l"
    .string "of the brook, and put them in a\l"
    .string "shepherd’s bag which he had, even in\l"
    .string "a scrip; and his sling was in his\l"
    .string "hand: and he drew near to the\l"
    .string "Philistine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_41::
    .string "And the Philistine came on and drew\n"
    .string "near unto David; and the man that\l"
    .string "bare the shield went before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_42::
    .string "And when the Philistine looked\n"
    .string "about, and saw David, he disdained\l"
    .string "him: for he was but a youth, and\l"
    .string "ruddy, and of a fair countenance.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_43::
    .string "And the Philistine said unto David,\n"
    .string "Am I a dog, that thou comest to me\l"
    .string "with staves? And the Philistine\l"
    .string "cursed David by his gods.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_44::
    .string "And the Philistine said to David,\n"
    .string "Come to me, and I will give thy\l"
    .string "flesh unto the fowls of the air, and\l"
    .string "to the beasts of the field.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_45::
    .string "Then said David to the Philistine,\n"
    .string "Thou comest to me with a sword, and\l"
    .string "with a spear, and with a shield: but\l"
    .string "I come to thee in the name of the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts, the God of the armies of\l"
    .string "Israel, whom thou hast defied.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_46::
    .string "This day will the LORD deliver\n"
    .string "thee into mine hand; and I will\l"
    .string "smite thee, and take thine head from\l"
    .string "thee; and I will give the carcases\l"
    .string "of the host of the Philistines this\l"
    .string "day unto the fowls of the air, and to\l"
    .string "the wild beasts of the earth; that\l"
    .string "all the earth may know that there is\l"
    .string "a God in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_47::
    .string "And all this assembly shall know\n"
    .string "that the LORD saveth not with sword\l"
    .string "and spear: for the battle is the\l"
    .string "LORD’s, and he will give you into\l"
    .string "our hands.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_48::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "Philistine arose, and came, and drew\l"
    .string "nigh to meet David, that David\l"
    .string "hastened, and ran toward the army to\l"
    .string "meet the Philistine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_49::
    .string "And David put his hand in his bag,\n"
    .string "and took thence a stone, and slang\l"
    .string "it, and smote the Philistine in his\l"
    .string "forehead, that the stone sunk into\l"
    .string "his forehead; and he fell upon his\l"
    .string "face to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_50::
    .string "So David prevailed over the\n"
    .string "Philistine with a sling and with a\l"
    .string "stone, and smote the Philistine, and\l"
    .string "slew him; but there was no sword in\l"
    .string "the hand of David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_51::
    .string "Therefore David ran, and stood upon\n"
    .string "the Philistine, and took his sword,\l"
    .string "and drew it out of the sheath\l"
    .string "thereof, and slew him, and cut off\l"
    .string "his head therewith. And when the\l"
    .string "Philistines saw their champion was\l"
    .string "dead, they fled.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_52::
    .string "And the men of Israel and of Judah\n"
    .string "arose, and shouted, and pursued the\l"
    .string "Philistines, until thou come to the\l"
    .string "valley, and to the gates of Ekron.\l"
    .string "And the wounded of the Philistines\l"
    .string "fell down by the way to Shaaraim,\l"
    .string "even unto Gath, and unto Ekron.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_53::
    .string "And the children of Israel\n"
    .string "returned from chasing after the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and they spoiled\l"
    .string "their tents.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_54::
    .string "And David took the head of the\n"
    .string "Philistine, and brought it to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; but he put his armour in\l"
    .string "his tent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_55::
    .string "And when Saul saw David go forth\n"
    .string "against the Philistine, he said unto\l"
    .string "Abner, the captain of the host,\l"
    .string "Abner, whose son is this youth? And\l"
    .string "Abner said, As thy soul liveth, O\l"
    .string "king, I cannot tell.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_56::
    .string "And the king said, Enquire thou\n"
    .string "whose son the stripling is.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_57::
    .string "And as David returned from the\n"
    .string "slaughter of the Philistine, Abner\l"
    .string "took him, and brought him before\l"
    .string "Saul with the head of the\l"
    .string "Philistine in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_17_58::
    .string "And Saul said to him, Whose son art\n"
    .string "thou, thou young man? And David\l"
    .string "answered, I am the son of thy servant\l"
    .string "Jesse the Bethlehemite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he had\n"
    .string "made an end of speaking unto Saul,\l"
    .string "that the soul of Jonathan was knit\l"
    .string "with the soul of David, and Jonathan\l"
    .string "loved him as his own soul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_2::
    .string "And Saul took him that day, and\n"
    .string "would let him go no more home to his\l"
    .string "father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_3::
    .string "Then Jonathan and David made a\n"
    .string "covenant, because he loved him as\l"
    .string "his own soul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_4::
    .string "And Jonathan stripped himself of\n"
    .string "the robe that was upon him, and gave\l"
    .string "it to David, and his garments, even\l"
    .string "to his sword, and to his bow, and to\l"
    .string "his girdle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_5::
    .string "And David went out whithersoever\n"
    .string "Saul sent him, and behaved himself\l"
    .string "wisely: and Saul set him over the\l"
    .string "men of war, and he was accepted in\l"
    .string "the sight of all the people, and\l"
    .string "also in the sight of Saul’s\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_6::
    .string "And it came to pass as they came,\n"
    .string "when David was returned from the\l"
    .string "slaughter of the Philistine, that\l"
    .string "the women came out of all cities of\l"
    .string "Israel, singing and dancing, to meet\l"
    .string "king Saul, with tabrets, with joy,\l"
    .string "and with instruments of musick.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_7::
    .string "And the women answered one another\n"
    .string "as they played, and said, Saul hath\l"
    .string "slain his thousands, and David his\l"
    .string "ten thousands.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_8::
    .string "And Saul was very wroth, and the\n"
    .string "saying displeased him; and he said,\l"
    .string "They have ascribed unto David ten\l"
    .string "thousands, and to me they have\l"
    .string "ascribed but thousands: and what can\l"
    .string "he have more but the kingdom?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_9::
    .string "And Saul eyed David from that day\n"
    .string "and forward$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_10::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that the evil spirit from God came\l"
    .string "upon Saul, and he prophesied in\l"
    .string "the midst of the house: and David\l"
    .string "played with his hand, as at other\l"
    .string "times: and there was a javelin in\l"
    .string "Saul’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_11::
    .string "And Saul cast the javelin; for he\n"
    .string "said, I will smite David even to the\l"
    .string "wall with it. And David avoided out\l"
    .string "of his presence twice.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_12::
    .string "And Saul was afraid of David,\n"
    .string "because the LORD was with him, and\l"
    .string "was departed from Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_13::
    .string "Therefore Saul removed him from\n"
    .string "him, and made him his captain over a\l"
    .string "thousand; and he went out and came in\l"
    .string "before the people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_14::
    .string "And David behaved himself wisely\n"
    .string "in all his ways; and the LORD was\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_15::
    .string "Wherefore when Saul saw that he\n"
    .string "behaved himself very wisely, he was\l"
    .string "afraid of him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_16::
    .string "But all Israel and Judah loved\n"
    .string "David, because he went out and came\l"
    .string "in before them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_17::
    .string "And Saul said to David, Behold my\n"
    .string "elder daughter Merab, her will I\l"
    .string "give thee to wife: only be thou\l"
    .string "valiant for me, and fight the LORD’s\l"
    .string "battles. For Saul said, Let not mine\l"
    .string "hand be upon him, but let the hand\l"
    .string "of the Philistines be upon him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_18::
    .string "And David said unto Saul, Who am I?\n"
    .string "and what is my life, or my father’s\l"
    .string "family in Israel, that I should be\l"
    .string "son in law to the king?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_19::
    .string "But it came to pass at the time when\n"
    .string "Merab Saul’s daughter should have\l"
    .string "been given to David, that she was\l"
    .string "given unto Adriel the Meholathite\l"
    .string "to wife$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_20::
    .string "And Michal Saul’s daughter loved\n"
    .string "David: and they told Saul, and the\l"
    .string "thing pleased him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_21::
    .string "And Saul said, I will give him\n"
    .string "her, that she may be a snare to him,\l"
    .string "and that the hand of the Philistines\l"
    .string "may be against him. Wherefore Saul\l"
    .string "said to David, Thou shalt this day be\l"
    .string "my son in law in the one of the twain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_22::
    .string "And Saul commanded his servants,\n"
    .string "saying, Commune with David secretly,\l"
    .string "and say, Behold, the king hath\l"
    .string "delight in thee, and all his\l"
    .string "servants love thee: now therefore be\l"
    .string "the king’s son in law.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_23::
    .string "And Saul’s servants spake those\n"
    .string "words in the ears of David. And David\l"
    .string "said, Seemeth it to you a light thing\l"
    .string "to be a king’s son in law, seeing\l"
    .string "that I am a poor man, and lightly\l"
    .string "esteemed?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_24::
    .string "And the servants of Saul told him,\n"
    .string "saying, On this manner spake David$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_25::
    .string "And Saul said, Thus shall ye say\n"
    .string "to David, The king desireth not any\l"
    .string "dowry, but an hundred foreskins of\l"
    .string "the Philistines, to be avenged of\l"
    .string "the king’s enemies. But Saul thought\l"
    .string "to make David fall by the hand of\l"
    .string "the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_26::
    .string "And when his servants told David\n"
    .string "these words, it pleased David well\l"
    .string "to be the king’s son in law: and the\l"
    .string "days were not expired.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_27::
    .string "Wherefore David arose and went, he\n"
    .string "and his men, and slew of the\l"
    .string "Philistines two hundred men; and\l"
    .string "David brought their foreskins, and\l"
    .string "they gave them in full tale to the\l"
    .string "king, that he might be the king’s son\l"
    .string "in law. And Saul gave him Michal\l"
    .string "his daughter to wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_28::
    .string "And Saul saw and knew that the LORD\n"
    .string "was with David, and that Michal\l"
    .string "Saul’s daughter loved him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_29::
    .string "And Saul was yet the more afraid of\n"
    .string "David; and Saul became David’s enemy\l"
    .string "continually.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_18_30::
    .string "Then the princes of the\n"
    .string "Philistines went forth: and it came\l"
    .string "to pass, after they went forth, that\l"
    .string "David behaved himself more wisely\l"
    .string "than all the servants of Saul; so\l"
    .string "that his name was much set by.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_1::
    .string "And Saul spake to Jonathan his son,\n"
    .string "and to all his servants, that they\l"
    .string "should kill David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_2::
    .string "But Jonathan Saul’s son delighted\n"
    .string "much in David: and Jonathan told\l"
    .string "David, saying, Saul my father\l"
    .string "seeketh to kill thee: now\l"
    .string "therefore, I pray thee, take heed to\l"
    .string "thyself until the morning, and\l"
    .string "abide in a secret place, and hide\l"
    .string "thyself:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_3::
    .string "And I will go out and stand beside\n"
    .string "my father in the field where thou\l"
    .string "art, and I will commune with my\l"
    .string "father of thee; and what I see, that I\l"
    .string "will tell thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_4::
    .string "And Jonathan spake good of David\n"
    .string "unto Saul his father, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Let not the king sin against his\l"
    .string "servant, against David; because he\l"
    .string "hath not sinned against thee, and\l"
    .string "because his works have been to\l"
    .string "thee-ward very good:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_5::
    .string "For he did put his life in his\n"
    .string "hand, and slew the Philistine, and\l"
    .string "the LORD wrought a great salvation\l"
    .string "for all Israel: thou sawest it, and\l"
    .string "didst rejoice: wherefore then wilt\l"
    .string "thou sin against innocent blood, to\l"
    .string "slay David without a cause?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_6::
    .string "And Saul hearkened unto the voice\n"
    .string "of Jonathan: and Saul sware, As the\l"
    .string "LORD liveth, he shall not be slain$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_7::
    .string "And Jonathan called David, and\n"
    .string "Jonathan shewed him all those things\l"
    .string " And Jonathan brought David to\l"
    .string "Saul, and he was in his presence, as\l"
    .string "in times past.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_8::
    .string "And there was war again: and David\n"
    .string "went out, and fought with the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and slew them with a\l"
    .string "great slaughter; and they fled from\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_9::
    .string "And the evil spirit from the LORD\n"
    .string "was upon Saul, as he sat in his\l"
    .string "house with his javelin in his hand:\l"
    .string "and David played with his hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_10::
    .string "And Saul sought to smite David even\n"
    .string "to the wall with the javelin: but\l"
    .string "he slipped away out of Saul’s\l"
    .string "presence, and he smote the javelin\l"
    .string "into the wall: and David fled, and\l"
    .string "escaped that night.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_11::
    .string "Saul also sent messengers unto\n"
    .string "David’s house, to watch him, and to\l"
    .string "slay him in the morning: and Michal\l"
    .string "David’s wife told him, saying, If\l"
    .string "thou save not thy life to night, to\l"
    .string "morrow thou shalt be slain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_12::
    .string "So Michal let David down through a\n"
    .string "window: and he went, and fled, and\l"
    .string "escaped.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_13::
    .string "And Michal took an image, and laid\n"
    .string "it in the bed, and put a pillow of\l"
    .string "goats’ hair for his bolster, and\l"
    .string "covered it with a cloth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_14::
    .string "And when Saul sent messengers to\n"
    .string "take David, she said, He is sick.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_15::
    .string "And Saul sent the messengers again\n"
    .string "to see David, saying, Bring him up to\l"
    .string "me in the bed, that I may slay him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_16::
    .string "And when the messengers were come\n"
    .string "in, behold, there was an image in the\l"
    .string "bed, with a pillow of goats’ hair\l"
    .string "for his bolster.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_17::
    .string "And Saul said unto Michal, Why hast\n"
    .string "thou deceived me so, and sent away\l"
    .string "mine enemy, that he is escaped? And\l"
    .string "Michal answered Saul, He said unto\l"
    .string "me, Let me go; why should I kill\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_18::
    .string "So David fled, and escaped, and\n"
    .string "came to Samuel to Ramah, and told\l"
    .string "him all that Saul had done to him.\l"
    .string "And he and Samuel went and dwelt in\l"
    .string "Naioth$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_19::
    .string "And it was told Saul, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold, David is at Naioth in Ramah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_20::
    .string "And Saul sent messengers to take\n"
    .string "David: and when they saw the company\l"
    .string "of the prophets prophesying, and\l"
    .string "Samuel standing as appointed over\l"
    .string "them, the Spirit of God was upon the\l"
    .string "messengers of Saul, and they also\l"
    .string "prophesied.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_21::
    .string "And when it was told Saul, he sent\n"
    .string "other messengers, and they\l"
    .string "prophesied likewise. And Saul sent\l"
    .string "messengers again the third time, and\l"
    .string "they prophesied also.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_22::
    .string "Then went he also to Ramah, and came\n"
    .string "to a great well that is in Sechu:\l"
    .string "and he asked and said, Where are\l"
    .string "Samuel and David? And one said,\l"
    .string "Behold, they be at Naioth in Ramah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_23::
    .string "And he went thither to Naioth in\n"
    .string "Ramah: and the Spirit of God was\l"
    .string "upon him also, and he went on, and\l"
    .string "prophesied, until he came to Naioth\l"
    .string "in Ramah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_19_24::
    .string "And he stripped off his clothes\n"
    .string "also, and prophesied before Samuel\l"
    .string "in like manner, and lay down naked\l"
    .string "all that day and all that night.\l"
    .string "Wherefore they say, Is Saul also\l"
    .string "among the prophets?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_1::
    .string "And David fled from Naioth in\n"
    .string "Ramah, and came and said before\l"
    .string "Jonathan, What have I done? what is\l"
    .string "mine iniquity? and what is my sin\l"
    .string "before thy father, that he seeketh my\l"
    .string "life?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_2::
    .string "And he said unto him, God forbid;\n"
    .string "thou shalt not die: behold, my\l"
    .string "father will do nothing either great\l"
    .string "or small, but that he will shew it\l"
    .string "me: and why should my father hide\l"
    .string "this thing from me? it is not so$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_3::
    .string "And David sware moreover, and said,\n"
    .string "Thy father certainly knoweth that I\l"
    .string "have found grace in thine eyes; and\l"
    .string "he saith, Let not Jonathan know this,\l"
    .string "lest he be grieved: but truly as the\l"
    .string "LORD liveth, and as thy soul\l"
    .string "liveth, there is but a step between\l"
    .string "me and death.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_4::
    .string "Then said Jonathan unto David,\n"
    .string "Whatsoever thy soul desireth, I\l"
    .string "will even do it for thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_5::
    .string "And David said unto Jonathan,\n"
    .string "Behold, to morrow is the new moon,\l"
    .string "and I should not fail to sit with\l"
    .string "the king at meat: but let me go, that\l"
    .string "I may hide myself in the field unto\l"
    .string "the third day at even.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_6::
    .string "If thy father at all miss me, then\n"
    .string "say, David earnestly asked leave of\l"
    .string "me that he might run to Bethlehem\l"
    .string "his city: for there is a yearly\l"
    .string "sacrifice there for all the family.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_7::
    .string "If he say thus, It is well; thy\n"
    .string "servant shall have peace: but if he\l"
    .string "be very wroth, then be sure that evil\l"
    .string "is determined by him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_8::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt deal kindly\n"
    .string "with thy servant; for thou hast\l"
    .string "brought thy servant into a covenant\l"
    .string "of the LORD with thee:\l"
    .string "notwithstanding, if there be in me\l"
    .string "iniquity, slay me thyself; for why\l"
    .string "shouldest thou bring me to thy\l"
    .string "father?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_9::
    .string "And Jonathan said, Far be it from\n"
    .string "thee: for if I knew certainly that\l"
    .string "evil were determined by my father to\l"
    .string "come upon thee, then would not I\l"
    .string "tell it thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_10::
    .string "Then said David to Jonathan, Who\n"
    .string "shall tell me? or what if thy\l"
    .string "father answer thee roughly?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_11::
    .string "And Jonathan said unto David, Come,\n"
    .string "and let us go out into the field.\l"
    .string "And they went out both of them into\l"
    .string "the field$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_12::
    .string "And Jonathan said unto David, O LORD\n"
    .string "God of Israel, when I have sounded my\l"
    .string "father about to morrow any time, or\l"
    .string "the third day, and, behold, if there\l"
    .string "be good toward David, and I then send\l"
    .string "not unto thee, and shew it thee;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_13::
    .string "The LORD do so and much more to\n"
    .string "Jonathan: but if it please my father\l"
    .string "to do thee evil, then I will shew it\l"
    .string "thee, and send thee away, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest go in peace: and the LORD be\l"
    .string "with thee, as he hath been with my\l"
    .string "father$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_14::
    .string "And thou shalt not only while yet\n"
    .string "I live shew me the kindness of the\l"
    .string "LORD, that I die not:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_15::
    .string "But also thou shalt not cut off thy\n"
    .string "kindness from my house for ever: no,\l"
    .string "not when the LORD hath cut off the\l"
    .string "enemies of David every one from the\l"
    .string "face of the earth$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_16::
    .string "So Jonathan made a covenant with the\n"
    .string "house of David, saying, Let the LORD\l"
    .string "even require it at the hand of\l"
    .string "David’s enemies.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_17::
    .string "And Jonathan caused David to swear\n"
    .string "again, because he loved him: for he\l"
    .string "loved him as he loved his own soul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_18::
    .string "Then Jonathan said to David, To\n"
    .string "morrow is the new moon: and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be missed, because thy seat\l"
    .string "will be empty.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_19::
    .string "And when thou hast stayed three\n"
    .string "days, then thou shalt go down\l"
    .string "quickly, and come to the place\l"
    .string "where thou didst hide thyself when\l"
    .string "the business was in hand, and shalt\l"
    .string "remain by the stone Ezel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_20::
    .string "And I will shoot three arrows on\n"
    .string "the side thereof, as though I shot at\l"
    .string "a mark.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_21::
    .string "And, behold, I will send a lad,\n"
    .string "saying, Go, find out the arrows. If I\l"
    .string "expressly say unto the lad,\l"
    .string "Behold, the arrows are on this side\l"
    .string "of thee, take them; then come thou:\l"
    .string "for there is peace to thee, and no\l"
    .string "hurt; as the LORD liveth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_22::
    .string "But if I say thus unto the young man,\n"
    .string "Behold, the arrows are beyond thee;\l"
    .string "go thy way: for the LORD hath sent\l"
    .string "thee away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_23::
    .string "And as touching the matter which\n"
    .string "thou and I have spoken of, behold,\l"
    .string "the LORD be between thee and me for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_24::
    .string "So David hid himself in the field:\n"
    .string "and when the new moon was come, the\l"
    .string "king sat him down to eat meat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_25::
    .string "And the king sat upon his seat, as\n"
    .string "at other times, even upon a seat by\l"
    .string "the wall: and Jonathan arose, and\l"
    .string "Abner sat by Saul’s side, and\l"
    .string "David’s place was empty.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_26::
    .string "Nevertheless Saul spake not any\n"
    .string "thing that day: for he thought,\l"
    .string "Something hath befallen him, he is\l"
    .string "not clean; surely he is not clean.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_27::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "which was the second day of the\l"
    .string "month, that David’s place was\l"
    .string "empty: and Saul said unto Jonathan\l"
    .string "his son, Wherefore cometh not the son\l"
    .string "of Jesse to meat, neither yesterday,\l"
    .string "nor to day?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_28::
    .string "And Jonathan answered Saul, David\n"
    .string "earnestly asked leave of me to go to\l"
    .string "Bethlehem:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_29::
    .string "And he said, Let me go, I pray thee;\n"
    .string "for our family hath a sacrifice in\l"
    .string "the city; and my brother, he hath\l"
    .string "commanded me to be there: and now, if\l"
    .string "I have found favour in thine eyes,\l"
    .string "let me get away, I pray thee, and see\l"
    .string "my brethren. Therefore he cometh not\l"
    .string "unto the king’s table$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_30::
    .string "Then Saul’s anger was kindled\n"
    .string "against Jonathan, and he said unto\l"
    .string "him, Thou son of the perverse\l"
    .string "rebellious woman, do not I know that\l"
    .string "thou hast chosen the son of Jesse to\l"
    .string "thine own confusion, and unto the\l"
    .string "confusion of thy mother’s nakedness?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_31::
    .string "For as long as the son of Jesse\n"
    .string "liveth upon the ground, thou shalt\l"
    .string "not be established, nor thy kingdom.\l"
    .string "Wherefore now send and fetch him unto\l"
    .string "me, for he shall surely die$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_32::
    .string "And Jonathan answered Saul his\n"
    .string "father, and said unto him, Wherefore\l"
    .string "shall he be slain? what hath he\l"
    .string "done?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_33::
    .string "And Saul cast a javelin at him to\n"
    .string "smite him: whereby Jonathan knew that\l"
    .string "it was determined of his father to\l"
    .string "slay David$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_34::
    .string "So Jonathan arose from the table in\n"
    .string "fierce anger, and did eat no meat the\l"
    .string "second day of the month: for he was\l"
    .string "grieved for David, because his father\l"
    .string "had done him shame.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_35::
    .string "And it came to pass in the morning,\n"
    .string "that Jonathan went out into the\l"
    .string "field at the time appointed with\l"
    .string "David, and a little lad with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_36::
    .string "And he said unto his lad, Run, find\n"
    .string "out now the arrows which I shoot. And\l"
    .string "as the lad ran, he shot an arrow\l"
    .string "beyond him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_37::
    .string "And when the lad was come to the\n"
    .string "place of the arrow which Jonathan\l"
    .string "had shot, Jonathan cried after the\l"
    .string "lad, and said, Is not the arrow\l"
    .string "beyond thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_38::
    .string "And Jonathan cried after the lad,\n"
    .string "Make speed, haste, stay not. And\l"
    .string "Jonathan’s lad gathered up the\l"
    .string "arrows, and came to his master$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_39::
    .string "But the lad knew not any thing:\n"
    .string "only Jonathan and David knew the\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_40::
    .string "And Jonathan gave his artillery\n"
    .string "unto his lad, and said unto him, Go,\l"
    .string "carry them to the city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_41::
    .string "And as soon as the lad was gone,\n"
    .string "David arose out of a place toward\l"
    .string "the south, and fell on his face to\l"
    .string "the ground, and bowed himself three\l"
    .string "times: and they kissed one another,\l"
    .string "and wept one with another, until\l"
    .string "David exceeded.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_20_42::
    .string "And Jonathan said to David, Go in\n"
    .string "peace, forasmuch as we have sworn\l"
    .string "both of us in the name of the LORD,\l"
    .string "saying, The LORD be between me and\l"
    .string "thee, and between my seed and thy\l"
    .string "seed for ever. And he arose and\l"
    .string "departed: and Jonathan went into the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_1::
    .string "Then came David to Nob to Ahimelech\n"
    .string "the priest: and Ahimelech was\l"
    .string "afraid at the meeting of David, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Why art thou alone,\l"
    .string "and no man with thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_2::
    .string "And David said unto Ahimelech the\n"
    .string "priest, The king hath commanded me a\l"
    .string "business, and hath said unto me, Let\l"
    .string "no man know any thing of the business\l"
    .string "whereabout I send thee, and what I\l"
    .string "have commanded thee: and I have\l"
    .string "appointed my servants to such and\l"
    .string "such a place$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_3::
    .string "Now therefore what is under thine\n"
    .string "hand? give me five loaves of bread in\l"
    .string "mine hand, or what there is present.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_4::
    .string "And the priest answered David, and\n"
    .string "said, There is no common bread under\l"
    .string "mine hand, but there is hallowed\l"
    .string "bread; if the young men have kept\l"
    .string "themselves at least from women.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_5::
    .string "And David answered the priest, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Of a truth women have\l"
    .string "been kept from us about these three\l"
    .string "days, since I came out, and the\l"
    .string "vessels of the young men are holy,\l"
    .string "and the bread is in a manner common,\l"
    .string "yea, though it were sanctified this\l"
    .string "day in the vessel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_6::
    .string "So the priest gave him hallowed\n"
    .string "bread: for there was no bread there\l"
    .string "but the shewbread, that was taken\l"
    .string "from before the LORD, to put hot\l"
    .string "bread in the day when it was taken\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_7::
    .string "Now a certain man of the servants of\n"
    .string "Saul was there that day, detained\l"
    .string "before the LORD; and his name was\l"
    .string "Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the\l"
    .string "herdmen that belonged to Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_8::
    .string "And David said unto Ahimelech, And\n"
    .string "is there not here under thine hand\l"
    .string "spear or sword? for I have neither\l"
    .string "brought my sword nor my weapons with\l"
    .string "me, because the king’s business\l"
    .string "required haste.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_9::
    .string "And the priest said, The sword of\n"
    .string "Goliath the Philistine, whom thou\l"
    .string "slewest in the valley of Elah,\l"
    .string "behold, it is here wrapped in a\l"
    .string "cloth behind the ephod: if thou\l"
    .string "wilt take that, take it: for there is\l"
    .string "no other save that here. And David\l"
    .string "said, There is none like that; give\l"
    .string "it me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_10::
    .string "And David arose and fled that day\n"
    .string "for fear of Saul, and went to Achish\l"
    .string "the king of Gath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_11::
    .string "And the servants of Achish said unto\n"
    .string "him, Is not this David the king of the\l"
    .string "land? did they not sing one to\l"
    .string "another of him in dances, saying,\l"
    .string "Saul hath slain his thousands, and\l"
    .string "David his ten thousands?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_12::
    .string "And David laid up these words in\n"
    .string "his heart, and was sore afraid of\l"
    .string "Achish the king of Gath$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_13::
    .string "And he changed his behaviour before\n"
    .string "them, and feigned himself mad in\l"
    .string "their hands, and scrabbled on the\l"
    .string "doors of the gate, and let his\l"
    .string "spittle fall down upon his beard.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_14::
    .string "Then said Achish unto his servants,\n"
    .string "Lo, ye see the man is mad: wherefore\l"
    .string "then have ye brought him to me?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_21_15::
    .string "Have I need of mad men, that ye have\n"
    .string "brought this fellow to play the\l"
    .string "mad man in my presence? shall this\l"
    .string "fellow come into my house?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_1::
    .string "David therefore departed thence,\n"
    .string "and escaped to the cave Adullam:\l"
    .string "and when his brethren and all his\l"
    .string "father’s house heard it, they went\l"
    .string "down thither to him$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_2::
    .string "And every one that was in distress,\n"
    .string "and every one that was in debt, and\l"
    .string "every one that was discontented,\l"
    .string "gathered themselves unto him; and he\l"
    .string "became a captain over them: and\l"
    .string "there were with him about four\l"
    .string "hundred men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_3::
    .string "And David went thence to Mizpeh of\n"
    .string "Moab: and he said unto the king of\l"
    .string "Moab, Let my father and my mother, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, come forth, and be with\l"
    .string "you, till I know what God will do\l"
    .string "for me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_4::
    .string "And he brought them before the king\n"
    .string "of Moab: and they dwelt with him\l"
    .string "all the while that David was in the\l"
    .string "hold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_5::
    .string "And the prophet Gad said unto\n"
    .string "David, Abide not in the hold;\l"
    .string "depart, and get thee into the land\l"
    .string "of Judah. Then David departed, and\l"
    .string "came into the forest of Hareth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_6::
    .string "When Saul heard that David was\n"
    .string "discovered, and the men that were\l"
    .string "with him, (now Saul abode in Gibeah\l"
    .string "under a tree in Ramah, having his\l"
    .string "spear in his hand, and all his\l"
    .string "servants were standing about him;)"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_7::
    .string "Then Saul said unto his servants\n"
    .string "that stood about him, Hear now, ye\l"
    .string "Benjamites; will the son of Jesse\l"
    .string "give every one of you fields and\l"
    .string "vineyards, and make you all\l"
    .string "captains of thousands, and captains\l"
    .string "of hundreds;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_8::
    .string "That all of you have conspired\n"
    .string "against me, and there is none that\l"
    .string "sheweth me that my son hath made a\l"
    .string "league with the son of Jesse, and\l"
    .string "there is none of you that is sorry\l"
    .string "for me, or sheweth unto me that my son\l"
    .string "hath stirred up my servant against\l"
    .string "me, to lie in wait, as at this day?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_9::
    .string "Then answered Doeg the Edomite,\n"
    .string "which was set over the servants of\l"
    .string "Saul, and said, I saw the son of\l"
    .string "Jesse coming to Nob, to Ahimelech\l"
    .string "the son of Ahitub$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_10::
    .string "And he enquired of the LORD for him,\n"
    .string "and gave him victuals, and gave him\l"
    .string "the sword of Goliath the Philistine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_11::
    .string "Then the king sent to call\n"
    .string "Ahimelech the priest, the son of\l"
    .string "Ahitub, and all his father’s house,\l"
    .string "the priests that were in Nob: and\l"
    .string "they came all of them to the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_12::
    .string "And Saul said, Hear now, thou son of\n"
    .string "Ahitub. And he answered, Here I am, my\l"
    .string "lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_13::
    .string "And Saul said unto him, Why have ye\n"
    .string "conspired against me, thou and the\l"
    .string "son of Jesse, in that thou hast given\l"
    .string "him bread, and a sword, and hast\l"
    .string "enquired of God for him, that he\l"
    .string "should rise against me, to lie in\l"
    .string "wait, as at this day?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_14::
    .string "Then Ahimelech answered the king,\n"
    .string "and said, And who is so faithful\l"
    .string "among all thy servants as David,\l"
    .string "which is the king’s son in law, and\l"
    .string "goeth at thy bidding, and is\l"
    .string "honourable in thine house?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_15::
    .string "Did I then begin to enquire of God\n"
    .string "for him? be it far from me: let not\l"
    .string "the king impute any thing unto his\l"
    .string "servant, nor to all the house of my\l"
    .string "father: for thy servant knew nothing\l"
    .string "of all this, less or more$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_16::
    .string "And the king said, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "surely die, Ahimelech, thou, and\l"
    .string "all thy father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_17::
    .string "And the king said unto the footmen\n"
    .string "that stood about him, Turn, and slay\l"
    .string "the priests of the LORD: because\l"
    .string "their hand also is with David, and\l"
    .string "because they knew when he fled, and\l"
    .string "did not shew it to me. But the\l"
    .string "servants of the king would not put\l"
    .string "forth their hand to fall upon the\l"
    .string "priests of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_18::
    .string "And the king said to Doeg, Turn\n"
    .string "thou, and fall upon the priests.\l"
    .string "And Doeg the Edomite turned, and he\l"
    .string "fell upon the priests, and slew on\l"
    .string "that day fourscore and five persons\l"
    .string "that did wear a linen ephod.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_19::
    .string "And Nob, the city of the priests,\n"
    .string "smote he with the edge of the sword,\l"
    .string "both men and women, children and\l"
    .string "sucklings, and oxen, and asses, and\l"
    .string "sheep, with the edge of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_20::
    .string "And one of the sons of Ahimelech\n"
    .string "the son of Ahitub, named Abiathar,\l"
    .string "escaped, and fled after David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_21::
    .string "And Abiathar shewed David that Saul\n"
    .string "had slain the LORD’s priests.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_22::
    .string "And David said unto Abiathar, I knew\n"
    .string "it that day, when Doeg the Edomite\l"
    .string "was there, that he would surely\l"
    .string "tell Saul: I have occasioned the\l"
    .string "death of all the persons of thy\l"
    .string "father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_22_23::
    .string "Abide thou with me, fear not: for he\n"
    .string "that seeketh my life seeketh thy\l"
    .string "life: but with me thou shalt be in\l"
    .string "safeguard.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_1::
    .string "Then they told David, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold, the Philistines fight\l"
    .string "against Keilah, and they rob the\l"
    .string "threshingfloors.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_2::
    .string "Therefore David enquired of the\n"
    .string "LORD, saying, Shall I go and smite\l"
    .string "these Philistines? And the LORD said\l"
    .string "unto David, Go, and smite the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and save Keilah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_3::
    .string "And David’s men said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold, we be afraid here in Judah:\l"
    .string "how much more then if we come to\l"
    .string "Keilah against the armies of the\l"
    .string "Philistines?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_4::
    .string "Then David enquired of the LORD yet\n"
    .string "again. And the LORD answered him and\l"
    .string "said, Arise, go down to Keilah; for I\l"
    .string "will deliver the Philistines into\l"
    .string "thine hand$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_5::
    .string "So David and his men went to Keilah,\n"
    .string "and fought with the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "brought away their cattle, and smote\l"
    .string "them with a great slaughter. So\l"
    .string "David saved the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Keilah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Abiathar\n"
    .string "the son of Ahimelech fled to David\l"
    .string "to Keilah, that he came down with an\l"
    .string "ephod in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_7::
    .string "And it was told Saul that David was\n"
    .string "come to Keilah. And Saul said, God\l"
    .string "hath delivered him into mine hand;\l"
    .string "for he is shut in, by entering into a\l"
    .string "town that hath gates and bars.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_8::
    .string "And Saul called all the people\n"
    .string "together to war, to go down to\l"
    .string "Keilah, to besiege David and his men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_9::
    .string "And David knew that Saul secretly\n"
    .string "practised mischief against him; and\l"
    .string "he said to Abiathar the priest,\l"
    .string "Bring hither the ephod.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_10::
    .string "Then said David, O LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel, thy servant hath certainly\l"
    .string "heard that Saul seeketh to come to\l"
    .string "Keilah, to destroy the city for my\l"
    .string "sake.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_11::
    .string "Will the men of Keilah deliver me\n"
    .string "up into his hand? will Saul come\l"
    .string "down, as thy servant hath heard? O\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, I beseech thee,\l"
    .string "tell thy servant. And the LORD said,\l"
    .string "He will come down.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_12::
    .string "Then said David, Will the men of\n"
    .string "Keilah deliver me and my men into\l"
    .string "the hand of Saul? And the LORD said,\l"
    .string "They will deliver thee up.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_13::
    .string "Then David and his men, which were\n"
    .string "about six hundred, arose and\l"
    .string "departed out of Keilah, and went\l"
    .string "whithersoever they could go. And it\l"
    .string "was told Saul that David was\l"
    .string "escaped from Keilah; and he forbare\l"
    .string "to go forth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_14::
    .string "And David abode in the wilderness\n"
    .string "in strong holds, and remained in a\l"
    .string "mountain in the wilderness of Ziph.\l"
    .string "And Saul sought him every day, but\l"
    .string "God delivered him not into his hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_15::
    .string "And David saw that Saul was come\n"
    .string "out to seek his life: and David was\l"
    .string "in the wilderness of Ziph in a wood.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_16::
    .string "And Jonathan Saul’s son arose, and\n"
    .string "went to David into the wood, and\l"
    .string "strengthened his hand in God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_17::
    .string "And he said unto him, Fear not: for\n"
    .string "the hand of Saul my father shall\l"
    .string "not find thee; and thou shalt be king\l"
    .string "over Israel, and I shall be next\l"
    .string "unto thee; and that also Saul my\l"
    .string "father knoweth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_18::
    .string "And they two made a covenant before\n"
    .string "the LORD: and David abode in the\l"
    .string "wood, and Jonathan went to his house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_19::
    .string "Then came up the Ziphites to Saul\n"
    .string "to Gibeah, saying, Doth not David\l"
    .string "hide himself with us in strong\l"
    .string "holds in the wood, in the hill of\l"
    .string "Hachilah, which is on the south of\l"
    .string "Jeshimon?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_20::
    .string "Now therefore, O king, come down\n"
    .string "according to all the desire of thy\l"
    .string "soul to come down; and our part\l"
    .string "shall be to deliver him into the\l"
    .string "king’s hand$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_21::
    .string "And Saul said, Blessed be ye of the\n"
    .string "LORD; for ye have compassion on me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_22::
    .string "Go, I pray you, prepare yet, and\n"
    .string "know and see his place where his\l"
    .string "haunt is, and who hath seen him\l"
    .string "there: for it is told me that he\l"
    .string "dealeth very subtilly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_23::
    .string "See therefore, and take knowledge\n"
    .string "of all the lurking places where\l"
    .string "he hideth himself, and come ye again\l"
    .string "to me with the certainty, and I will\l"
    .string "go with you: and it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, if he be in the land, that I\l"
    .string "will search him out throughout all\l"
    .string "the thousands of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_24::
    .string "And they arose, and went to Ziph\n"
    .string "before Saul: but David and his men\l"
    .string "were in the wilderness of Maon, in\l"
    .string "the plain on the south of Jeshimon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_25::
    .string "Saul also and his men went to seek\n"
    .string "him. And they told David; wherefore\l"
    .string "he came down into a rock, and abode in\l"
    .string "the wilderness of Maon. And when\l"
    .string "Saul heard that, he pursued after\l"
    .string "David in the wilderness of Maon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_26::
    .string "And Saul went on this side of the\n"
    .string "mountain, and David and his men on\l"
    .string "that side of the mountain: and David\l"
    .string "made haste to get away for fear of\l"
    .string "Saul; for Saul and his men\l"
    .string "compassed David and his men round\l"
    .string "about to take them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_27::
    .string "But there came a messenger unto\n"
    .string "Saul, saying, Haste thee, and come;\l"
    .string "for the Philistines have invaded the\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_28::
    .string "Wherefore Saul returned from\n"
    .string "pursuing after David, and went\l"
    .string "against the Philistines: therefore\l"
    .string "they called that place\l"
    .string "Selahammahlekoth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_23_29::
    .string "And David went up from thence, and\n"
    .string "dwelt in strong holds at Engedi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Saul was\n"
    .string "returned from following the\l"
    .string "Philistines, that it was told him,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold, David is in the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Engedi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_2::
    .string "Then Saul took three thousand\n"
    .string "chosen men out of all Israel, and\l"
    .string "went to seek David and his men upon\l"
    .string "the rocks of the wild goats.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_3::
    .string "And he came to the sheepcotes by\n"
    .string "the way, where was a cave; and Saul\l"
    .string "went in to cover his feet: and David\l"
    .string "and his men remained in the sides of\l"
    .string "the cave.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_4::
    .string "And the men of David said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold the day of which the LORD\l"
    .string "said unto thee, Behold, I will\l"
    .string "deliver thine enemy into thine hand,\l"
    .string "that thou mayest do to him as it\l"
    .string "shall seem good unto thee. Then\l"
    .string "David arose, and cut off the skirt of\l"
    .string "Saul’s robe privily.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_5::
    .string "And it came to pass afterward, that\n"
    .string "David’s heart smote him, because he\l"
    .string "had cut off Saul’s skirt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_6::
    .string "And he said unto his men, The LORD\n"
    .string "forbid that I should do this thing\l"
    .string "unto my master, the LORD’s anointed,\l"
    .string "to stretch forth mine hand against\l"
    .string "him, seeing he is the anointed of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_7::
    .string "So David stayed his servants with\n"
    .string "these words, and suffered them not to\l"
    .string "rise against Saul. But Saul rose up\l"
    .string "out of the cave, and went on his way.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_8::
    .string "David also arose afterward, and\n"
    .string "went out of the cave, and cried after\l"
    .string "Saul, saying, My lord the king. And\l"
    .string "when Saul looked behind him, David\l"
    .string "stooped with his face to the earth,\l"
    .string "and bowed himself.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_9::
    .string "And David said to Saul, Wherefore\n"
    .string "hearest thou men’s words, saying,\l"
    .string "Behold, David seeketh thy hurt?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_10::
    .string "Behold, this day thine eyes have\n"
    .string "seen how that the LORD had delivered\l"
    .string "thee to day into mine hand in the\l"
    .string "cave: and some bade me kill thee:\l"
    .string "but mine eye spared thee; and I said,\l"
    .string "I will not put forth mine hand\l"
    .string "against my lord; for he is the LORD’s\l"
    .string "anointed$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_11::
    .string "Moreover, my father, see, yea, see\n"
    .string "the skirt of thy robe in my hand: for\l"
    .string "in that I cut off the skirt of thy\l"
    .string "robe, and killed thee not, know thou\l"
    .string "and see that there is neither evil\l"
    .string "nor transgression in mine hand, and I\l"
    .string "have not sinned against thee; yet\l"
    .string "thou huntest my soul to take it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_12::
    .string "The LORD judge between me and thee,\n"
    .string "and the LORD avenge me of thee: but\l"
    .string "mine hand shall not be upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_13::
    .string "As saith the proverb of the\n"
    .string "ancients, Wickedness proceedeth\l"
    .string "from the wicked: but mine hand shall\l"
    .string "not be upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_14::
    .string "After whom is the king of Israel\n"
    .string "come out? after whom dost thou\l"
    .string "pursue? after a dead dog, after a\l"
    .string "flea.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_15::
    .string "The LORD therefore be judge, and\n"
    .string "judge between me and thee, and see,\l"
    .string "and plead my cause, and deliver me\l"
    .string "out of thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, when David had\n"
    .string "made an end of speaking these words\l"
    .string "unto Saul, that Saul said, Is this\l"
    .string "thy voice, my son David? And Saul\l"
    .string "lifted up his voice, and wept.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_17::
    .string "And he said to David, Thou art more\n"
    .string "righteous than I: for thou hast\l"
    .string "rewarded me good, whereas I have\l"
    .string "rewarded thee evil.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_18::
    .string "And thou hast shewed this day how\n"
    .string "that thou hast dealt well with me:\l"
    .string "forasmuch as when the LORD had\l"
    .string "delivered me into thine hand, thou\l"
    .string "killedst me not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_19::
    .string "For if a man find his enemy, will\n"
    .string "he let him go well away? wherefore\l"
    .string "the LORD reward thee good for that\l"
    .string "thou hast done unto me this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_20::
    .string "And now, behold, I know well that\n"
    .string "thou shalt surely be king, and that\l"
    .string "the kingdom of Israel shall be\l"
    .string "established in thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_21::
    .string "Swear now therefore unto me by the\n"
    .string "LORD, that thou wilt not cut off my\l"
    .string "seed after me, and that thou wilt not\l"
    .string "destroy my name out of my father’s\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_24_22::
    .string "And David sware unto Saul. And Saul\n"
    .string "went home; but David and his men gat\l"
    .string "them up unto the hold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_1::
    .string "And Samuel died; and all the\n"
    .string "Israelites were gathered together,\l"
    .string "and lamented him, and buried him in\l"
    .string "his house at Ramah. And David arose,\l"
    .string "and went down to the wilderness of\l"
    .string "Paran.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_2::
    .string "And there was a man in Maon, whose\n"
    .string "possessions were in Carmel; and the\l"
    .string "man was very great, and he had three\l"
    .string "thousand sheep, and a thousand\l"
    .string "goats: and he was shearing his sheep\l"
    .string "in Carmel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_3::
    .string "Now the name of the man was Nabal;\n"
    .string "and the name of his wife Abigail: and\l"
    .string "she was a woman of good\l"
    .string "understanding, and of a beautiful\l"
    .string "countenance: but the man was\l"
    .string "churlish and evil in his doings; and\l"
    .string "he was of the house of Caleb.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_4::
    .string "And David heard in the wilderness\n"
    .string "that Nabal did shear his sheep.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_5::
    .string "And David sent out ten young men,\n"
    .string "and David said unto the young men,\l"
    .string "Get you up to Carmel, and go to\l"
    .string "Nabal, and greet him in my name:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_6::
    .string "And thus shall ye say to him that\n"
    .string "liveth in prosperity, Peace be both\l"
    .string "to thee, and peace be to thine house,\l"
    .string "and peace be unto all that thou hast$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_7::
    .string "And now I have heard that thou hast\n"
    .string "shearers: now thy shepherds which\l"
    .string "were with us, we hurt them not,\l"
    .string "neither was there ought missing unto\l"
    .string "them, all the while they were in\l"
    .string "Carmel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_8::
    .string "Ask thy young men, and they will\n"
    .string "shew thee. Wherefore let the young\l"
    .string "men find favour in thine eyes: for we\l"
    .string "come in a good day: give, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, whatsoever cometh to thine hand\l"
    .string "unto thy servants, and to thy son\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_9::
    .string "And when David’s young men came,\n"
    .string "they spake to Nabal according to\l"
    .string "all those words in the name of\l"
    .string "David, and ceased.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_10::
    .string "And Nabal answered David’s\n"
    .string "servants, and said, Who is David? and\l"
    .string "who is the son of Jesse? there be many\l"
    .string "servants now a days that break away\l"
    .string "every man from his master.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_11::
    .string "Shall I then take my bread, and my\n"
    .string "water, and my flesh that I have\l"
    .string "killed for my shearers, and give it\l"
    .string "unto men, whom I know not whence they\l"
    .string "be?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_12::
    .string "So David’s young men turned their\n"
    .string "way, and went again, and came and\l"
    .string "told him all those sayings$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_13::
    .string "And David said unto his men, Gird ye\n"
    .string "on every man his sword. And they\l"
    .string "girded on every man his sword; and\l"
    .string "David also girded on his sword: and\l"
    .string "there went up after David about four\l"
    .string "hundred men; and two hundred abode by\l"
    .string "the stuff.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_14::
    .string "But one of the young men told\n"
    .string "Abigail, Nabal’s wife, saying,\l"
    .string "Behold, David sent messengers out of\l"
    .string "the wilderness to salute our\l"
    .string "master; and he railed on them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_15::
    .string "But the men were very good unto us,\n"
    .string "and we were not hurt, neither missed\l"
    .string "we any thing, as long as we were\l"
    .string "conversant with them, when we were in\l"
    .string "the fields:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_16::
    .string "They were a wall unto us both by\n"
    .string "night and day, all the while we\l"
    .string "were with them keeping the sheep$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_17::
    .string "Now therefore know and consider\n"
    .string "what thou wilt do; for evil is\l"
    .string "determined against our master, and\l"
    .string "against all his household: for he\l"
    .string "is such a son of Belial, that a man\l"
    .string "cannot speak to him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_18::
    .string "Then Abigail made haste, and took\n"
    .string "two hundred loaves, and two bottles\l"
    .string "of wine, and five sheep ready\l"
    .string "dressed, and five measures of\l"
    .string "parched corn, and an hundred\l"
    .string "clusters of raisins, and two hundred\l"
    .string "cakes of figs, and laid them on\l"
    .string "asses.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_19::
    .string "And she said unto her servants, Go\n"
    .string "on before me; behold, I come after\l"
    .string "you. But she told not her husband\l"
    .string "Nabal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_20::
    .string "And it was so, as she rode on the\n"
    .string "ass, that she came down by the covert\l"
    .string "on the hill, and, behold, David and\l"
    .string "his men came down against her; and\l"
    .string "she met them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_21::
    .string "Now David had said, Surely in vain\n"
    .string "have I kept all that this fellow\l"
    .string "hath in the wilderness, so that\l"
    .string "nothing was missed of all that\l"
    .string "pertained unto him: and he hath\l"
    .string "requited me evil for good.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_22::
    .string "So and more also do God unto the\n"
    .string "enemies of David, if I leave of all\l"
    .string "that pertain to him by the morning\l"
    .string "light any that pisseth against the\l"
    .string "wall.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_23::
    .string "And when Abigail saw David, she\n"
    .string "hasted, and lighted off the ass, and\l"
    .string "fell before David on her face, and\l"
    .string "bowed herself to the ground,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_24::
    .string "And fell at his feet, and said,\n"
    .string "Upon me, my lord, upon me let this\l"
    .string "iniquity be: and let thine handmaid,\l"
    .string "I pray thee, speak in thine\l"
    .string "audience, and hear the words of thine\l"
    .string "handmaid$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_25::
    .string "Let not my lord, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "regard this man of Belial, even\l"
    .string "Nabal: for as his name is, so is he;\l"
    .string "Nabal is his name, and folly is\l"
    .string "with him: but I thine handmaid saw\l"
    .string "not the young men of my lord, whom\l"
    .string "thou didst send.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_26::
    .string "Now therefore, my lord, as the LORD\n"
    .string "liveth, and as thy soul liveth,\l"
    .string "seeing the LORD hath withholden thee\l"
    .string "from coming to shed blood, and from\l"
    .string "avenging thyself with thine own\l"
    .string "hand, now let thine enemies, and\l"
    .string "they that seek evil to my lord, be\l"
    .string "as Nabal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_27::
    .string "And now this blessing which thine\n"
    .string "handmaid hath brought unto my lord,\l"
    .string "let it even be given unto the young\l"
    .string "men that follow my lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_28::
    .string "I pray thee, forgive the trespass\n"
    .string "of thine handmaid: for the LORD will\l"
    .string "certainly make my lord a sure house;\l"
    .string "because my lord fighteth the\l"
    .string "battles of the LORD, and evil hath\l"
    .string "not been found in thee all thy days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_29::
    .string "Yet a man is risen to pursue thee,\n"
    .string "and to seek thy soul: but the soul\l"
    .string "of my lord shall be bound in the\l"
    .string "bundle of life with the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God; and the souls of thine enemies,\l"
    .string "them shall he sling out, as out of\l"
    .string "the middle of a sling.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_30::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "the LORD shall have done to my lord\l"
    .string "according to all the good that he\l"
    .string "hath spoken concerning thee, and\l"
    .string "shall have appointed thee ruler\l"
    .string "over Israel;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_31::
    .string "That this shall be no grief unto\n"
    .string "thee, nor offence of heart unto my\l"
    .string "lord, either that thou hast shed\l"
    .string "blood causeless, or that my lord\l"
    .string "hath avenged himself: but when the\l"
    .string "LORD shall have dealt well with\l"
    .string "my lord, then remember thine handmaid$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_32::
    .string "And David said to Abigail, Blessed\n"
    .string "be the LORD God of Israel, which sent\l"
    .string "thee this day to meet me:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_33::
    .string "And blessed be thy advice, and\n"
    .string "blessed be thou, which hast kept me\l"
    .string "this day from coming to shed blood,\l"
    .string "and from avenging myself with mine\l"
    .string "own hand$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_34::
    .string "For in very deed, as the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel liveth, which hath kept me\l"
    .string "back from hurting thee, except thou\l"
    .string "hadst hasted and come to meet me,\l"
    .string "surely there had not been left unto\l"
    .string "Nabal by the morning light any that\l"
    .string "pisseth against the wall.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_35::
    .string "So David received of her hand that\n"
    .string "which she had brought him, and said\l"
    .string "unto her, Go up in peace to thine\l"
    .string "house; see, I have hearkened to thy\l"
    .string "voice, and have accepted thy person.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_36::
    .string "And Abigail came to Nabal; and,\n"
    .string "behold, he held a feast in his\l"
    .string "house, like the feast of a king; and\l"
    .string "Nabal’s heart was merry within him,\l"
    .string "for he was very drunken: wherefore\l"
    .string "she told him nothing, less or more,\l"
    .string "until the morning light.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_37::
    .string "But it came to pass in the morning,\n"
    .string "when the wine was gone out of Nabal,\l"
    .string "and his wife had told him these\l"
    .string "things, that his heart died within\l"
    .string "him, and he became as a stone.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_38::
    .string "And it came to pass about ten days\n"
    .string "after, that the LORD smote Nabal,\l"
    .string "that he died.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_39::
    .string "And when David heard that Nabal was\n"
    .string "dead, he said, Blessed be the LORD,\l"
    .string "that hath pleaded the cause of my\l"
    .string "reproach from the hand of Nabal, and\l"
    .string "hath kept his servant from evil: for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath returned the\l"
    .string "wickedness of Nabal upon his own\l"
    .string "head. And David sent and communed\l"
    .string "with Abigail, to take her to him to\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_40::
    .string "And when the servants of David were\n"
    .string "come to Abigail to Carmel, they\l"
    .string "spake unto her, saying, David sent\l"
    .string "us unto thee, to take thee to him to\l"
    .string "wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_41::
    .string "And she arose, and bowed herself on\n"
    .string "her face to the earth, and said,\l"
    .string "Behold, let thine handmaid be a\l"
    .string "servant to wash the feet of the\l"
    .string "servants of my lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_42::
    .string "And Abigail hasted, and arose and\n"
    .string "rode upon an ass, with five damsels\l"
    .string "of hers that went after her; and she\l"
    .string "went after the messengers of David,\l"
    .string "and became his wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_43::
    .string "David also took Ahinoam of\n"
    .string "Jezreel; and they were also both of\l"
    .string "them his wives.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_25_44::
    .string "But Saul had given Michal his\n"
    .string "daughter, David’s wife, to Phalti\l"
    .string "the son of Laish, which was of\l"
    .string "Gallim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_1::
    .string "And the Ziphites came unto Saul to\n"
    .string "Gibeah, saying, Doth not David hide\l"
    .string "himself in the hill of Hachilah,\l"
    .string "which is before Jeshimon?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_2::
    .string "Then Saul arose, and went down to\n"
    .string "the wilderness of Ziph, having\l"
    .string "three thousand chosen men of Israel\l"
    .string "with him, to seek David in the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Ziph$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_3::
    .string "And Saul pitched in the hill of\n"
    .string "Hachilah, which is before Jeshimon,\l"
    .string "by the way. But David abode in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, and he saw that Saul\l"
    .string "came after him into the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_4::
    .string "David therefore sent out spies, and\n"
    .string "understood that Saul was come in\l"
    .string "very deed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_5::
    .string "And David arose, and came to the\n"
    .string "place where Saul had pitched: and\l"
    .string "David beheld the place where Saul\l"
    .string "lay, and Abner the son of Ner, the\l"
    .string "captain of his host: and Saul lay\l"
    .string "in the trench, and the people\l"
    .string "pitched round about him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_6::
    .string "Then answered David and said to\n"
    .string "Ahimelech the Hittite, and to\l"
    .string "Abishai the son of Zeruiah, brother\l"
    .string "to Joab, saying, Who will go down\l"
    .string "with me to Saul to the camp? And\l"
    .string "Abishai said, I will go down with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_7::
    .string "So David and Abishai came to the\n"
    .string "people by night: and, behold, Saul\l"
    .string "lay sleeping within the trench, and\l"
    .string "his spear stuck in the ground at his\l"
    .string "bolster: but Abner and the people\l"
    .string "lay round about him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_8::
    .string "Then said Abishai to David, God hath\n"
    .string "delivered thine enemy into thine\l"
    .string "hand this day: now therefore let me\l"
    .string "smite him, I pray thee, with the\l"
    .string "spear even to the earth at once, and\l"
    .string "I will not smite him the second time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_9::
    .string "And David said to Abishai, Destroy\n"
    .string "him not: for who can stretch forth\l"
    .string "his hand against the LORD’s anointed,\l"
    .string "and be guiltless?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_10::
    .string "David said furthermore, As the LORD\n"
    .string "liveth, the LORD shall smite him; or\l"
    .string "his day shall come to die; or he\l"
    .string "shall descend into battle, and\l"
    .string "perish$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_11::
    .string "The LORD forbid that I should\n"
    .string "stretch forth mine hand against the\l"
    .string "LORD’s anointed: but, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "take thou now the spear that is at\l"
    .string "his bolster, and the cruse of water,\l"
    .string "and let us go.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_12::
    .string "So David took the spear and the\n"
    .string "cruse of water from Saul’s bolster;\l"
    .string "and they gat them away, and no man saw\l"
    .string "it, nor knew it, neither awaked: for\l"
    .string "they were all asleep; because a\l"
    .string "deep sleep from the LORD was\l"
    .string "fallen upon them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_13::
    .string "Then David went over to the other\n"
    .string "side, and stood on the top of an\l"
    .string "hill afar off; a great space being\l"
    .string "between them:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_14::
    .string "And David cried to the people, and\n"
    .string "to Abner the son of Ner, saying,\l"
    .string "Answerest thou not, Abner? Then Abner\l"
    .string "answered and said, Who art thou that\l"
    .string "criest to the king?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_15::
    .string "And David said to Abner, Art not\n"
    .string "thou a valiant man? and who is like\l"
    .string "to thee in Israel? wherefore then\l"
    .string "hast thou not kept thy lord the\l"
    .string "king? for there came one of the\l"
    .string "people in to destroy the king thy\l"
    .string "lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_16::
    .string "This thing is not good that thou\n"
    .string "hast done. As the LORD liveth, ye are\l"
    .string "worthy to die, because ye have not\l"
    .string "kept your master, the LORD’s anointed\l"
    .string " And now see where the king’s spear\l"
    .string "is, and the cruse of water that was at\l"
    .string "his bolster.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_17::
    .string "And Saul knew David’s voice, and\n"
    .string "said, Is this thy voice, my son David?\l"
    .string "And David said, It is my voice, my\l"
    .string "lord, O king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_18::
    .string "And he said, Wherefore doth my lord\n"
    .string "thus pursue after his servant? for\l"
    .string "what have I done? or what evil is in\l"
    .string "mine hand?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_19::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, let my\n"
    .string "lord the king hear the words of his\l"
    .string "servant. If the LORD have stirred\l"
    .string "thee up against me, let him accept\l"
    .string "an offering: but if they be the\l"
    .string "children of men, cursed be they\l"
    .string "before the LORD; for they have driven\l"
    .string "me out this day from abiding in the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the LORD, saying, Go,\l"
    .string "serve other gods$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_20::
    .string "Now therefore, let not my blood\n"
    .string "fall to the earth before the face of\l"
    .string "the LORD: for the king of Israel is\l"
    .string "come out to seek a flea, as when one\l"
    .string "doth hunt a partridge in the\l"
    .string "mountains.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_21::
    .string "Then said Saul, I have sinned:\n"
    .string "return, my son David: for I will no\l"
    .string "more do thee harm, because my soul\l"
    .string "was precious in thine eyes this day:\l"
    .string "behold, I have played the fool,\l"
    .string "and have erred exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_22::
    .string "And David answered and said, Behold\n"
    .string "the king’s spear! and let one of the\l"
    .string "young men come over and fetch it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_23::
    .string "The LORD render to every man his\n"
    .string "righteousness and his faithfulness;\l"
    .string "for the LORD delivered thee into my\l"
    .string "hand to day, but I would not stretch\l"
    .string "forth mine hand against the LORD’s\l"
    .string "anointed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_24::
    .string "And, behold, as thy life was much\n"
    .string "set by this day in mine eyes, so let\l"
    .string "my life be much set by in the eyes of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and let him deliver me out\l"
    .string "of all tribulation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_26_25::
    .string "Then Saul said to David, Blessed be\n"
    .string "thou, my son David: thou shalt both\l"
    .string "do great things, and also shalt\l"
    .string "still prevail. So David went on\l"
    .string "his way, and Saul returned to his\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_1::
    .string "And David said in his heart, I\n"
    .string "shall now perish one day by the\l"
    .string "hand of Saul: there is nothing\l"
    .string "better for me than that I should\l"
    .string "speedily escape into the land of\l"
    .string "the Philistines; and Saul shall\l"
    .string "despair of me, to seek me any more in\l"
    .string "any coast of Israel: so shall I\l"
    .string "escape out of his hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_2::
    .string "And David arose, and he passed over\n"
    .string "with the six hundred men that were\l"
    .string "with him unto Achish, the son of\l"
    .string "Maoch, king of Gath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_3::
    .string "And David dwelt with Achish at\n"
    .string "Gath, he and his men, every man with\l"
    .string "his household, even David with his\l"
    .string "two wives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess,\l"
    .string "and Abigail the Carmelitess,\l"
    .string "Nabal’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_4::
    .string "And it was told Saul that David was\n"
    .string "fled to Gath: and he sought no more\l"
    .string "again for him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_5::
    .string "And David said unto Achish, If I\n"
    .string "have now found grace in thine eyes,\l"
    .string "let them give me a place in some\l"
    .string "town in the country, that I may\l"
    .string "dwell there: for why should thy\l"
    .string "servant dwell in the royal city\l"
    .string "with thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_6::
    .string "Then Achish gave him Ziklag that\n"
    .string "day: wherefore Ziklag pertaineth\l"
    .string "unto the kings of Judah unto this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_7::
    .string "And the time that David dwelt in\n"
    .string "the country of the Philistines was a\l"
    .string "full year and four months.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_8::
    .string "And David and his men went up, and\n"
    .string "invaded the Geshurites, and the\l"
    .string "Gezrites, and the Amalekites: for\l"
    .string "those nations were of old the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land, as thou\l"
    .string "goest to Shur, even unto the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_9::
    .string "And David smote the land, and left\n"
    .string "neither man nor woman alive, and\l"
    .string "took away the sheep, and the oxen,\l"
    .string "and the asses, and the camels, and\l"
    .string "the apparel, and returned, and came\l"
    .string "to Achish.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_10::
    .string "And Achish said, Whither have ye\n"
    .string "made a road to day? And David said,\l"
    .string "Against the south of Judah, and\l"
    .string "against the south of the\l"
    .string "Jerahmeelites, and against the south\l"
    .string "of the Kenites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_11::
    .string "And David saved neither man nor\n"
    .string "woman alive, to bring tidings to\l"
    .string "Gath, saying, Lest they should tell\l"
    .string "on us, saying, So did David, and so\l"
    .string "will be his manner all the while\l"
    .string "he dwelleth in the country of the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_27_12::
    .string "And Achish believed David, saying,\n"
    .string "He hath made his people Israel\l"
    .string "utterly to abhor him; therefore he\l"
    .string "shall be my servant for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "that the Philistines gathered their\l"
    .string "armies together for warfare, to fight\l"
    .string "with Israel. And Achish said unto\l"
    .string "David, Know thou assuredly, that\l"
    .string "thou shalt go out with me to battle,\l"
    .string "thou and thy men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_2::
    .string "And David said to Achish, Surely\n"
    .string "thou shalt know what thy servant can\l"
    .string "do. And Achish said to David,\l"
    .string "Therefore will I make thee keeper\l"
    .string "of mine head for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_3::
    .string "Now Samuel was dead, and all\n"
    .string "Israel had lamented him, and buried\l"
    .string "him in Ramah, even in his own city.\l"
    .string "And Saul had put away those that had\l"
    .string "familiar spirits, and the wizards,\l"
    .string "out of the land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_4::
    .string "And the Philistines gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together, and came and\l"
    .string "pitched in Shunem: and Saul gathered\l"
    .string "all Israel together, and they\l"
    .string "pitched in Gilboa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_5::
    .string "And when Saul saw the host of the\n"
    .string "Philistines, he was afraid, and his\l"
    .string "heart greatly trembled.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_6::
    .string "And when Saul enquired of the LORD,\n"
    .string "the LORD answered him not, neither by\l"
    .string "dreams, nor by Urim, nor by prophets.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_7::
    .string "Then said Saul unto his servants,\n"
    .string "Seek me a woman that hath a familiar\l"
    .string "spirit, that I may go to her, and\l"
    .string "enquire of her. And his servants said\l"
    .string "to him, Behold, there is a woman that\l"
    .string "hath a familiar spirit at Endor.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_8::
    .string "And Saul disguised himself, and\n"
    .string "put on other raiment, and he went,\l"
    .string "and two men with him, and they came to\l"
    .string "the woman by night: and he said, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, divine unto me by the\l"
    .string "familiar spirit, and bring me him\l"
    .string "up, whom I shall name unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_9::
    .string "And the woman said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold, thou knowest what Saul hath\l"
    .string "done, how he hath cut off those that\l"
    .string "have familiar spirits, and the\l"
    .string "wizards, out of the land: wherefore\l"
    .string "then layest thou a snare for my\l"
    .string "life, to cause me to die?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_10::
    .string "And Saul sware to her by the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying, As the LORD liveth, there\l"
    .string "shall no punishment happen to\l"
    .string "thee for this thing$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_11::
    .string "Then said the woman, Whom shall I\n"
    .string "bring up unto thee? And he said,\l"
    .string "Bring me up Samuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_12::
    .string "And when the woman saw Samuel, she\n"
    .string "cried with a loud voice: and the\l"
    .string "woman spake to Saul, saying, Why\l"
    .string "hast thou deceived me? for thou art\l"
    .string "Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_13::
    .string "And the king said unto her, Be not\n"
    .string "afraid: for what sawest thou? And the\l"
    .string "woman said unto Saul, I saw gods\l"
    .string "ascending out of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_14::
    .string "And he said unto her, What form is he\n"
    .string "of? And she said, An old man cometh\l"
    .string "up; and he is covered with a mantle.\l"
    .string "And Saul perceived that it was\l"
    .string "Samuel, and he stooped with his face\l"
    .string "to the ground, and bowed himself.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_15::
    .string "And Samuel said to Saul, Why hast\n"
    .string "thou disquieted me, to bring me up?\l"
    .string "And Saul answered, I am sore\l"
    .string "distressed; for the Philistines make\l"
    .string "war against me, and God is departed\l"
    .string "from me, and answereth me no more,\l"
    .string "neither by prophets, nor by dreams:\l"
    .string "therefore I have called thee, that\l"
    .string "thou mayest make known unto me what I\l"
    .string "shall do.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_16::
    .string "Then said Samuel, Wherefore then\n"
    .string "dost thou ask of me, seeing the LORD\l"
    .string "is departed from thee, and is become\l"
    .string "thine enemy?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_17::
    .string "And the LORD hath done to him, as he\n"
    .string "spake by me: for the LORD hath rent\l"
    .string "the kingdom out of thine hand, and\l"
    .string "given it to thy neighbour, even to\l"
    .string "David:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_18::
    .string "Because thou obeyedst not the voice\n"
    .string "of the LORD, nor executedst his\l"
    .string "fierce wrath upon Amalek, therefore\l"
    .string "hath the LORD done this thing unto\l"
    .string "thee this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_19::
    .string "Moreover the LORD will also\n"
    .string "deliver Israel with thee into the\l"
    .string "hand of the Philistines: and to\l"
    .string "morrow shalt thou and thy sons be\l"
    .string "with me: the LORD also shall\l"
    .string "deliver the host of Israel into the\l"
    .string "hand of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_20::
    .string "Then Saul fell straightway all\n"
    .string "along on the earth, and was sore\l"
    .string "afraid, because of the words of\l"
    .string "Samuel: and there was no strength in\l"
    .string "him; for he had eaten no bread all\l"
    .string "the day, nor all the night.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_21::
    .string "And the woman came unto Saul, and\n"
    .string "saw that he was sore troubled, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Behold, thine\l"
    .string "handmaid hath obeyed thy voice, and I\l"
    .string "have put my life in my hand, and\l"
    .string "have hearkened unto thy words which\l"
    .string "thou spakest unto me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_22::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, hearken\n"
    .string "thou also unto the voice of thine\l"
    .string "handmaid, and let me set a morsel of\l"
    .string "bread before thee; and eat, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest have strength, when thou goest\l"
    .string "on thy way.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_23::
    .string "But he refused, and said, I will\n"
    .string "not eat. But his servants, together\l"
    .string "with the woman, compelled him; and\l"
    .string "he hearkened unto their voice. So he\l"
    .string "arose from the earth, and sat upon\l"
    .string "the bed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_24::
    .string "And the woman had a fat calf in the\n"
    .string "house; and she hasted, and killed\l"
    .string "it, and took flour, and kneaded it,\l"
    .string "and did bake unleavened bread\l"
    .string "thereof:"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_28_25::
    .string "And she brought it before Saul, and\n"
    .string "before his servants; and they did\l"
    .string "eat. Then they rose up, and went away\l"
    .string "that night$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_1::
    .string "Now the Philistines gathered\n"
    .string "together all their armies to Aphek:\l"
    .string "and the Israelites pitched by a\l"
    .string "fountain which is in Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_2::
    .string "And the lords of the Philistines\n"
    .string "passed on by hundreds, and by\l"
    .string "thousands: but David and his men\l"
    .string "passed on in the rereward with Achish.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_3::
    .string "Then said the princes of the\n"
    .string "Philistines, What do these Hebrews\l"
    .string "here? And Achish said unto the\l"
    .string "princes of the Philistines, Is not\l"
    .string "this David, the servant of Saul the\l"
    .string "king of Israel, which hath been with\l"
    .string "me these days, or these years, and I\l"
    .string "have found no fault in him since he\l"
    .string "fell unto me unto this day?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_4::
    .string "And the princes of the Philistines\n"
    .string "were wroth with him; and the princes\l"
    .string "of the Philistines said unto him,\l"
    .string "Make this fellow return, that he may\l"
    .string "go again to his place which thou\l"
    .string "hast appointed him, and let him not\l"
    .string "go down with us to battle, lest in\l"
    .string "the battle he be an adversary to us:\l"
    .string "for wherewith should he reconcile\l"
    .string "himself unto his master? should it\l"
    .string "not be with the heads of these men?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_5::
    .string "Is not this David, of whom they sang\n"
    .string "one to another in dances, saying,\l"
    .string "Saul slew his thousands, and David\l"
    .string "his ten thousands?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_6::
    .string "Then Achish called David, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Surely, as the LORD\l"
    .string "liveth, thou hast been upright, and\l"
    .string "thy going out and thy coming in with\l"
    .string "me in the host is good in my sight:\l"
    .string "for I have not found evil in thee\l"
    .string "since the day of thy coming unto me\l"
    .string "unto this day: nevertheless the\l"
    .string "lords favour thee not$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_7::
    .string "Wherefore now return, and go in\n"
    .string "peace, that thou displease not the\l"
    .string "lords of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_8::
    .string "And David said unto Achish, But what\n"
    .string "have I done? and what hast thou found\l"
    .string "in thy servant so long as I have been\l"
    .string "with thee unto this day, that I may\l"
    .string "not go fight against the enemies of\l"
    .string "my lord the king?"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_9::
    .string "And Achish answered and said to\n"
    .string "David, I know that thou art good in my\l"
    .string "sight, as an angel of God:\l"
    .string "notwithstanding the princes of the\l"
    .string "Philistines have said, He shall not\l"
    .string "go up with us to the battle$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_10::
    .string "Wherefore now rise up early in the\n"
    .string "morning with thy master’s servants\l"
    .string "that are come with thee: and as soon\l"
    .string "as ye be up early in the morning,\l"
    .string "and have light, depart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_29_11::
    .string "So David and his men rose up early\n"
    .string "to depart in the morning, to return\l"
    .string "into the land of the Philistines.\l"
    .string "And the Philistines went up to\l"
    .string "Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when David and\n"
    .string "his men were come to Ziklag on the\l"
    .string "third day, that the Amalekites had\l"
    .string "invaded the south, and Ziklag, and\l"
    .string "smitten Ziklag, and burned it with\l"
    .string "fire;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_2::
    .string "And had taken the women captives,\n"
    .string "that were therein: they slew not\l"
    .string "any, either great or small, but\l"
    .string "carried them away, and went on their\l"
    .string "way$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_3::
    .string "So David and his men came to the\n"
    .string "city, and, behold, it was burned with\l"
    .string "fire; and their wives, and their\l"
    .string "sons, and their daughters, were taken\l"
    .string "captives.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_4::
    .string "Then David and the people that\n"
    .string "were with him lifted up their voice\l"
    .string "and wept, until they had no more\l"
    .string "power to weep.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_5::
    .string "And David’s two wives were taken\n"
    .string "captives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess,\l"
    .string "and Abigail the wife of Nabal the\l"
    .string "Carmelite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_6::
    .string "And David was greatly distressed;\n"
    .string "for the people spake of stoning\l"
    .string "him, because the soul of all the\l"
    .string "people was grieved, every man for\l"
    .string "his sons and for his daughters: but\l"
    .string "David encouraged himself in the LORD\l"
    .string "his God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_7::
    .string "And David said to Abiathar the\n"
    .string "priest, Ahimelech’s son, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, bring me hither the ephod. And\l"
    .string "Abiathar brought thither the ephod\l"
    .string "to David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_8::
    .string "And David enquired at the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying, Shall I pursue after this\l"
    .string "troop? shall I overtake them? And\l"
    .string "he answered him, Pursue: for thou\l"
    .string "shalt surely overtake them, and\l"
    .string "without fail recover all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_9::
    .string "So David went, he and the six\n"
    .string "hundred men that were with him, and\l"
    .string "came to the brook Besor, where those\l"
    .string "that were left behind stayed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_10::
    .string "But David pursued, he and four\n"
    .string "hundred men: for two hundred abode\l"
    .string "behind, which were so faint that they\l"
    .string "could not go over the brook Besor.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_11::
    .string "And they found an Egyptian in the\n"
    .string "field, and brought him to David, and\l"
    .string "gave him bread, and he did eat; and\l"
    .string "they made him drink water;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_12::
    .string "And they gave him a piece of a cake\n"
    .string "of figs, and two clusters of\l"
    .string "raisins: and when he had eaten, his\l"
    .string "spirit came again to him: for he had\l"
    .string "eaten no bread, nor drunk any water,\l"
    .string "three days and three nights$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_13::
    .string "And David said unto him, To whom\n"
    .string "belongest thou? and whence art thou?\l"
    .string "And he said, I am a young man of\l"
    .string "Egypt, servant to an Amalekite; and\l"
    .string "my master left me, because three\l"
    .string "days agone I fell sick.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_14::
    .string "We made an invasion upon the south\n"
    .string "of the Cherethites, and upon the\l"
    .string "coast which belongeth to Judah, and\l"
    .string "upon the south of Caleb; and we\l"
    .string "burned Ziklag with fire.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_15::
    .string "And David said to him, Canst thou\n"
    .string "bring me down to this company? And he\l"
    .string "said, Swear unto me by God, that thou\l"
    .string "wilt neither kill me, nor deliver\l"
    .string "me into the hands of my master, and I\l"
    .string "will bring thee down to this\l"
    .string "company.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_16::
    .string "And when he had brought him down,\n"
    .string "behold, they were spread abroad\l"
    .string "upon all the earth, eating and\l"
    .string "drinking, and dancing, because of\l"
    .string "all the great spoil that they had\l"
    .string "taken out of the land of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and out of the land of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_17::
    .string "And David smote them from the\n"
    .string "twilight even unto the evening of\l"
    .string "the next day: and there escaped not a\l"
    .string "man of them, save four hundred young\l"
    .string "men, which rode upon camels, and\l"
    .string "fled.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_18::
    .string "And David recovered all that the\n"
    .string "Amalekites had carried away: and\l"
    .string "David rescued his two wives.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_19::
    .string "And there was nothing lacking to\n"
    .string "them, neither small nor great,\l"
    .string "neither sons nor daughters, neither\l"
    .string "spoil, nor any thing that they had\l"
    .string "taken to them: David recovered all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_20::
    .string "And David took all the flocks and\n"
    .string "the herds, which they drave before\l"
    .string "those other cattle, and said, This\l"
    .string "is David’s spoil.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_21::
    .string "And David came to the two hundred\n"
    .string "men, which were so faint that they\l"
    .string "could not follow David, whom they\l"
    .string "had made also to abide at the brook\l"
    .string "Besor: and they went forth to meet\l"
    .string "David, and to meet the people that\l"
    .string "were with him: and when David came\l"
    .string "near to the people, he saluted\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_22::
    .string "Then answered all the wicked men\n"
    .string "and men of Belial, of those that\l"
    .string "went with David, and said, Because\l"
    .string "they went not with us, we will not\l"
    .string "give them ought of the spoil that we\l"
    .string "have recovered, save to every man his\l"
    .string "wife and his children, that they may\l"
    .string "lead them away, and depart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_23::
    .string "Then said David, Ye shall not do\n"
    .string "so, my brethren, with that which the\l"
    .string "LORD hath given us, who hath\l"
    .string "preserved us, and delivered the\l"
    .string "company that came against us into\l"
    .string "our hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_24::
    .string "For who will hearken unto you in\n"
    .string "this matter? but as his part is that\l"
    .string "goeth down to the battle, so shall\l"
    .string "his part be that tarrieth by the\l"
    .string "stuff: they shall part alike.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_25::
    .string "And it was so from that day forward,\n"
    .string "that he made it a statute and an\l"
    .string "ordinance for Israel unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_26::
    .string "And when David came to Ziklag, he\n"
    .string "sent of the spoil unto the elders\l"
    .string "of Judah, even to his friends,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold a present for you of\l"
    .string "the spoil of the enemies of the\l"
    .string "LORD;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_27::
    .string "To them which were in Bethel, and to\n"
    .string "them which were in south Ramoth, and\l"
    .string "to them which were in Jattir,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_28::
    .string "And to them which were in Aroer, and\n"
    .string "to them which were in Siphmoth, and\l"
    .string "to them which were in Eshtemoa,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_29::
    .string "And to them which were in Rachal,\n"
    .string "and to them which were in the cities\l"
    .string "of the Jerahmeelites, and to them\l"
    .string "which were in the cities of the\l"
    .string "Kenites,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_30::
    .string "And to them which were in Hormah,\n"
    .string "and to them which were in Chorashan,\l"
    .string "and to them which were in Athach,"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_30_31::
    .string "And to them which were in Hebron,\n"
    .string "and to all the places where David\l"
    .string "himself and his men were wont to\l"
    .string "haunt$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_1::
    .string "Now the Philistines fought against\n"
    .string "Israel: and the men of Israel fled\l"
    .string "from before the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "fell down slain in mount Gilboa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_2::
    .string "And the Philistines followed hard\n"
    .string "upon Saul and upon his sons; and\l"
    .string "the Philistines slew Jonathan, and\l"
    .string "Abinadab, and Melchishua, Saul’s\l"
    .string "sons.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_3::
    .string "And the battle went sore against\n"
    .string "Saul, and the archers hit him; and he\l"
    .string "was sore wounded of the archers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_4::
    .string "Then said Saul unto his\n"
    .string "armourbearer, Draw thy sword, and\l"
    .string "thrust me through therewith; lest\l"
    .string "these uncircumcised come and thrust\l"
    .string "me through, and abuse me. But his\l"
    .string "armourbearer would not; for he was\l"
    .string "sore afraid. Therefore Saul took a\l"
    .string "sword, and fell upon it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_5::
    .string "And when his armourbearer saw that\n"
    .string "Saul was dead, he fell likewise\l"
    .string "upon his sword, and died with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_6::
    .string "So Saul died, and his three sons,\n"
    .string "and his armourbearer, and all his\l"
    .string "men, that same day together.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_7::
    .string "And when the men of Israel that\n"
    .string "were on the other side of the\l"
    .string "valley, and they that were on the\l"
    .string "other side Jordan, saw that the men\l"
    .string "of Israel fled, and that Saul and\l"
    .string "his sons were dead, they forsook the\l"
    .string "cities, and fled; and the\l"
    .string "Philistines came and dwelt in them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_8::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "when the Philistines came to strip\l"
    .string "the slain, that they found Saul and\l"
    .string "his three sons fallen in mount\l"
    .string "Gilboa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_9::
    .string "And they cut off his head, and\n"
    .string "stripped off his armour, and sent\l"
    .string "into the land of the Philistines\l"
    .string "round about, to publish it in the\l"
    .string "house of their idols, and among the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_10::
    .string "And they put his armour in the\n"
    .string "house of Ashtaroth: and they fastened\l"
    .string "his body to the wall of Bethshan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_11::
    .string "And when the inhabitants of\n"
    .string "Jabeshgilead heard of that which the\l"
    .string "Philistines had done to Saul;"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_12::
    .string "All the valiant men arose, and\n"
    .string "went all night, and took the body of\l"
    .string "Saul and the bodies of his sons from\l"
    .string "the wall of Bethshan, and came to\l"
    .string "Jabesh, and burnt them there$"
Bible_Text_1_Samuel_31_13::
    .string "And they took their bones, and\n"
    .string "buried them under a tree at Jabesh,\l"
    .string "and fasted seven days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass after the death\n"
    .string "of Saul, when David was returned\l"
    .string "from the slaughter of the\l"
    .string "Amalekites, and David had abode two\l"
    .string "days in Ziklag;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_2::
    .string "It came even to pass on the third\n"
    .string "day, that, behold, a man came out of\l"
    .string "the camp from Saul with his clothes\l"
    .string "rent, and earth upon his head: and so\l"
    .string "it was, when he came to David, that he\l"
    .string "fell to the earth, and did obeisance$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_3::
    .string "And David said unto him, From whence\n"
    .string "comest thou? And he said unto him,\l"
    .string "Out of the camp of Israel am I\l"
    .string "escaped.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_4::
    .string "And David said unto him, How went\n"
    .string "the matter? I pray thee, tell me.\l"
    .string "And he answered, That the people\l"
    .string "are fled from the battle, and many\l"
    .string "of the people also are fallen and\l"
    .string "dead; and Saul and Jonathan his son\l"
    .string "are dead also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_5::
    .string "And David said unto the young man\n"
    .string "that told him, How knowest thou that\l"
    .string "Saul and Jonathan his son be dead?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_6::
    .string "And the young man that told him\n"
    .string "said, As I happened by chance upon\l"
    .string "mount Gilboa, behold, Saul leaned\l"
    .string "upon his spear; and, lo, the\l"
    .string "chariots and horsemen followed hard\l"
    .string "after him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_7::
    .string "And when he looked behind him, he\n"
    .string "saw me, and called unto me. And I\l"
    .string "answered, Here am I.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_8::
    .string "And he said unto me, Who art thou?\n"
    .string "And I answered him, I am an\l"
    .string "Amalekite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_9::
    .string "He said unto me again, Stand, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, upon me, and slay me: for\l"
    .string "anguish is come upon me, because my\l"
    .string "life is yet whole in me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_10::
    .string "So I stood upon him, and slew him,\n"
    .string "because I was sure that he could not\l"
    .string "live after that he was fallen: and I\l"
    .string "took the crown that was upon his\l"
    .string "head, and the bracelet that was on\l"
    .string "his arm, and have brought them hither\l"
    .string "unto my lord.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_11::
    .string "Then David took hold on his\n"
    .string "clothes, and rent them; and\l"
    .string "likewise all the men that were with\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_12::
    .string "And they mourned, and wept, and\n"
    .string "fasted until even, for Saul, and for\l"
    .string "Jonathan his son, and for the\l"
    .string "people of the LORD, and for the\l"
    .string "house of Israel; because they were\l"
    .string "fallen by the sword$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_13::
    .string "And David said unto the young man\n"
    .string "that told him, Whence art thou? And\l"
    .string "he answered, I am the son of a\l"
    .string "stranger, an Amalekite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_14::
    .string "And David said unto him, How wast\n"
    .string "thou not afraid to stretch forth\l"
    .string "thine hand to destroy the LORD’s\l"
    .string "anointed?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_15::
    .string "And David called one of the young\n"
    .string "men, and said, Go near, and fall\l"
    .string "upon him. And he smote him that he\l"
    .string "died$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_16::
    .string "And David said unto him, Thy blood\n"
    .string "be upon thy head; for thy mouth hath\l"
    .string "testified against thee, saying, I\l"
    .string "have slain the LORD’s anointed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_17::
    .string "And David lamented with this\n"
    .string "lamentation over Saul and over\l"
    .string "Jonathan his son:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_18::
    .string "(Also he bade them teach the\n"
    .string "children of Judah the use of the bow:\l"
    .string "behold, it is written in the book of\l"
    .string "Jasher.)"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_19::
    .string "The beauty of Israel is slain upon\n"
    .string "thy high places: how are the mighty\l"
    .string "fallen!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_20::
    .string "Tell it not in Gath, publish it\n"
    .string "not in the streets of Askelon; lest\l"
    .string "the daughters of the Philistines\l"
    .string "rejoice, lest the daughters of the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised triumph$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_21::
    .string "Ye mountains of Gilboa, let there\n"
    .string "be no dew, neither let there be rain,\l"
    .string "upon you, nor fields of offerings:\l"
    .string "for there the shield of the mighty\l"
    .string "is vilely cast away, the shield of\l"
    .string "Saul, as though he had not been\l"
    .string "anointed with oil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_22::
    .string "From the blood of the slain, from\n"
    .string "the fat of the mighty, the bow of\l"
    .string "Jonathan turned not back, and the\l"
    .string "sword of Saul returned not empty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_23::
    .string "Saul and Jonathan were lovely and\n"
    .string "pleasant in their lives, and in\l"
    .string "their death they were not divided:\l"
    .string "they were swifter than eagles, they\l"
    .string "were stronger than lions.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_24::
    .string "Ye daughters of Israel, weep over\n"
    .string "Saul, who clothed you in scarlet,\l"
    .string "with other delights, who put on\l"
    .string "ornaments of gold upon your\l"
    .string "apparel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_25::
    .string "How are the mighty fallen in the\n"
    .string "midst of the battle! O Jonathan,\l"
    .string "thou wast slain in thine high\l"
    .string "places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_26::
    .string "I am distressed for thee, my brother\n"
    .string "Jonathan: very pleasant hast thou\l"
    .string "been unto me: thy love to me was\l"
    .string "wonderful, passing the love of\l"
    .string "women.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_1_27::
    .string "How are the mighty fallen, and the\n"
    .string "weapons of war perished!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "David enquired of the LORD, saying,\l"
    .string "Shall I go up into any of the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah? And the LORD said\l"
    .string "unto him, Go up. And David said,\l"
    .string "Whither shall I go up? And he said,\l"
    .string "Unto Hebron$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_2::
    .string "So David went up thither, and his\n"
    .string "two wives also, Ahinoam the\l"
    .string "Jezreelitess, and Abigail Nabal’s\l"
    .string "wife the Carmelite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_3::
    .string "And his men that were with him did\n"
    .string "David bring up, every man with his\l"
    .string "household: and they dwelt in the\l"
    .string "cities of Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_4::
    .string "And the men of Judah came, and there\n"
    .string "they anointed David king over the\l"
    .string "house of Judah. And they told David,\l"
    .string "saying, That the men of Jabeshgilead\l"
    .string "were they that buried Saul.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_5::
    .string "And David sent messengers unto the\n"
    .string "men of Jabeshgilead, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Blessed be ye of the LORD, that\l"
    .string "ye have shewed this kindness unto\l"
    .string "your lord, even unto Saul, and have\l"
    .string "buried him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_6::
    .string "And now the LORD shew kindness and\n"
    .string "truth unto you: and I also will\l"
    .string "requite you this kindness, because ye\l"
    .string "have done this thing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_7::
    .string "Therefore now let your hands be\n"
    .string "strengthened, and be ye valiant: for\l"
    .string "your master Saul is dead, and also\l"
    .string "the house of Judah have anointed me\l"
    .string "king over them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_8::
    .string "But Abner the son of Ner, captain of\n"
    .string "Saul’s host, took Ishbosheth the son\l"
    .string "of Saul, and brought him over to\l"
    .string "Mahanaim;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_9::
    .string "And made him king over Gilead, and\n"
    .string "over the Ashurites, and over\l"
    .string "Jezreel, and over Ephraim, and over\l"
    .string "Benjamin, and over all Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_10::
    .string "Ishbosheth Saul’s son was forty\n"
    .string "years old when he began to reign\l"
    .string "over Israel, and reigned two years.\l"
    .string "But the house of Judah followed\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_11::
    .string "And the time that David was king in\n"
    .string "Hebron over the house of Judah was\l"
    .string "seven years and six months.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_12::
    .string "And Abner the son of Ner, and the\n"
    .string "servants of Ishbosheth the son of\l"
    .string "Saul, went out from Mahanaim to\l"
    .string "Gibeon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_13::
    .string "And Joab the son of Zeruiah, and the\n"
    .string "servants of David, went out, and met\l"
    .string "together by the pool of Gibeon: and\l"
    .string "they sat down, the one on the one side\l"
    .string "of the pool, and the other on the\l"
    .string "other side of the pool.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_14::
    .string "And Abner said to Joab, Let the\n"
    .string "young men now arise, and play before\l"
    .string "us. And Joab said, Let them arise.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_15::
    .string "Then there arose and went over by\n"
    .string "number twelve of Benjamin, which\l"
    .string "pertained to Ishbosheth the son of\l"
    .string "Saul, and twelve of the servants of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_16::
    .string "And they caught every one his\n"
    .string "fellow by the head, and thrust his\l"
    .string "sword in his fellow’s side; so they\l"
    .string "fell down together: wherefore that\l"
    .string "place was called Helkathhazzurim,\l"
    .string "which is in Gibeon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_17::
    .string "And there was a very sore battle\n"
    .string "that day; and Abner was beaten, and\l"
    .string "the men of Israel, before the\l"
    .string "servants of David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_18::
    .string "And there were three sons of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "there, Joab, and Abishai, and\l"
    .string "Asahel: and Asahel was as light of\l"
    .string "foot as a wild roe.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_19::
    .string "And Asahel pursued after Abner;\n"
    .string "and in going he turned not to the\l"
    .string "right hand nor to the left from\l"
    .string "following Abner.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_20::
    .string "Then Abner looked behind him, and\n"
    .string "said, Art thou Asahel? And he\l"
    .string "answered, I am.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_21::
    .string "And Abner said to him, Turn thee\n"
    .string "aside to thy right hand or to thy\l"
    .string "left, and lay thee hold on one of\l"
    .string "the young men, and take thee his\l"
    .string "armour. But Asahel would not turn\l"
    .string "aside from following of him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_22::
    .string "And Abner said again to Asahel,\n"
    .string "Turn thee aside from following me:\l"
    .string "wherefore should I smite thee to the\l"
    .string "ground? how then should I hold up\l"
    .string "my face to Joab thy brother?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_23::
    .string "Howbeit he refused to turn aside:\n"
    .string "wherefore Abner with the hinder end\l"
    .string "of the spear smote him under the\l"
    .string "fifth rib, that the spear came out\l"
    .string "behind him; and he fell down there,\l"
    .string "and died in the same place: and it\l"
    .string "came to pass, that as many as came to\l"
    .string "the place where Asahel fell down\l"
    .string "and died stood still$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_24::
    .string "Joab also and Abishai pursued\n"
    .string "after Abner: and the sun went down\l"
    .string "when they were come to the hill of\l"
    .string "Ammah, that lieth before Giah by the\l"
    .string "way of the wilderness of Gibeon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_25::
    .string "And the children of Benjamin\n"
    .string "gathered themselves together after\l"
    .string "Abner, and became one troop, and\l"
    .string "stood on the top of an hill.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_26::
    .string "Then Abner called to Joab, and\n"
    .string "said, Shall the sword devour for\l"
    .string "ever? knowest thou not that it will\l"
    .string "be bitterness in the latter end? how\l"
    .string "long shall it be then, ere thou bid\l"
    .string "the people return from following\l"
    .string "their brethren?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_27::
    .string "And Joab said, As God liveth,\n"
    .string "unless thou hadst spoken, surely\l"
    .string "then in the morning the people had\l"
    .string "gone up every one from following\l"
    .string "his brother$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_28::
    .string "So Joab blew a trumpet, and all\n"
    .string "the people stood still, and\l"
    .string "pursued after Israel no more,\l"
    .string "neither fought they any more.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_29::
    .string "And Abner and his men walked all\n"
    .string "that night through the plain, and\l"
    .string "passed over Jordan, and went through\l"
    .string "all Bithron, and they came to\l"
    .string "Mahanaim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_30::
    .string "And Joab returned from following\n"
    .string "Abner: and when he had gathered all\l"
    .string "the people together, there lacked\l"
    .string "of David’s servants nineteen men and\l"
    .string "Asahel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_31::
    .string "But the servants of David had\n"
    .string "smitten of Benjamin, and of Abner’s\l"
    .string "men, so that three hundred and\l"
    .string "threescore men died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_2_32::
    .string "And they took up Asahel, and buried\n"
    .string "him in the sepulchre of his father,\l"
    .string "which was in Bethlehem. And Joab and\l"
    .string "his men went all night, and they\l"
    .string "came to Hebron at break of day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_1::
    .string "Now there was long war between the\n"
    .string "house of Saul and the house of David:\l"
    .string "but David waxed stronger and\l"
    .string "stronger, and the house of Saul\l"
    .string "waxed weaker and weaker.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_2::
    .string "And unto David were sons born in\n"
    .string "Hebron: and his firstborn was Amnon,\l"
    .string "of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_3::
    .string "And his second, Chileab, of\n"
    .string "Abigail the wife of Nabal the\l"
    .string "Carmelite; and the third, Absalom\l"
    .string "the son of Maacah the daughter of\l"
    .string "Talmai king of Geshur;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_4::
    .string "And the fourth, Adonijah the son of\n"
    .string "Haggith; and the fifth, Shephatiah\l"
    .string "the son of Abital;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_5::
    .string "And the sixth, Ithream, by Eglah\n"
    .string "David’s wife. These were born to\l"
    .string "David in Hebron$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, while there\n"
    .string "was war between the house of Saul\l"
    .string "and the house of David, that Abner\l"
    .string "made himself strong for the house of\l"
    .string "Saul.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_7::
    .string "And Saul had a concubine, whose\n"
    .string "name was Rizpah, the daughter of\l"
    .string "Aiah: and Ishbosheth said to Abner,\l"
    .string "Wherefore hast thou gone in unto my\l"
    .string "father’s concubine?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_8::
    .string "Then was Abner very wroth for the\n"
    .string "words of Ishbosheth, and said, Am I a\l"
    .string "dog’s head, which against Judah do\l"
    .string "shew kindness this day unto the house\l"
    .string "of Saul thy father, to his brethren,\l"
    .string "and to his friends, and have not\l"
    .string "delivered thee into the hand of\l"
    .string "David, that thou chargest me to day\l"
    .string "with a fault concerning this woman?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_9::
    .string "So do God to Abner, and more also,\n"
    .string "except, as the LORD hath sworn to\l"
    .string "David, even so I do to him;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_10::
    .string "To translate the kingdom from the\n"
    .string "house of Saul, and to set up the\l"
    .string "throne of David over Israel and over\l"
    .string "Judah, from Dan even to Beersheba$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_11::
    .string "And he could not answer Abner a\n"
    .string "word again, because he feared him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_12::
    .string "And Abner sent messengers to David\n"
    .string "on his behalf, saying, Whose is the\l"
    .string "land? saying also, Make thy league\l"
    .string "with me, and, behold, my hand shall\l"
    .string "be with thee, to bring about all\l"
    .string "Israel unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_13::
    .string "And he said, Well; I will make a\n"
    .string "league with thee: but one thing I\l"
    .string "require of thee, that is, Thou shalt\l"
    .string "not see my face, except thou first\l"
    .string "bring Michal Saul’s daughter, when\l"
    .string "thou comest to see my face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_14::
    .string "And David sent messengers to\n"
    .string "Ishbosheth Saul’s son, saying,\l"
    .string "Deliver me my wife Michal, which I\l"
    .string "espoused to me for an hundred\l"
    .string "foreskins of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_15::
    .string "And Ishbosheth sent, and took her\n"
    .string "from her husband, even from\l"
    .string "Phaltiel the son of Laish.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_16::
    .string "And her husband went with her along\n"
    .string "weeping behind her to Bahurim. Then\l"
    .string "said Abner unto him, Go, return. And\l"
    .string "he returned.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_17::
    .string "And Abner had communication with\n"
    .string "the elders of Israel, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "sought for David in times past to be\l"
    .string "king over you:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_18::
    .string "Now then do it: for the LORD hath\n"
    .string "spoken of David, saying, By the hand\l"
    .string "of my servant David I will save my\l"
    .string "people Israel out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the Philistines, and out of the hand\l"
    .string "of all their enemies$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_19::
    .string "And Abner also spake in the ears of\n"
    .string "Benjamin: and Abner went also to\l"
    .string "speak in the ears of David in Hebron\l"
    .string "all that seemed good to Israel, and\l"
    .string "that seemed good to the whole house\l"
    .string "of Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_20::
    .string "So Abner came to David to Hebron,\n"
    .string "and twenty men with him. And David\l"
    .string "made Abner and the men that were with\l"
    .string "him a feast.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_21::
    .string "And Abner said unto David, I will\n"
    .string "arise and go, and will gather all\l"
    .string "Israel unto my lord the king, that\l"
    .string "they may make a league with thee, and\l"
    .string "that thou mayest reign over all\l"
    .string "that thine heart desireth. And David\l"
    .string "sent Abner away; and he went in\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_22::
    .string "And, behold, the servants of David\n"
    .string "and Joab came from pursuing a troop,\l"
    .string "and brought in a great spoil with\l"
    .string "them: but Abner was not with David in\l"
    .string "Hebron; for he had sent him away, and\l"
    .string "he was gone in peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_23::
    .string "When Joab and all the host that was\n"
    .string "with him were come, they told Joab,\l"
    .string "saying, Abner the son of Ner came to\l"
    .string "the king, and he hath sent him away,\l"
    .string "and he is gone in peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_24::
    .string "Then Joab came to the king, and\n"
    .string "said, What hast thou done? behold,\l"
    .string "Abner came unto thee; why is it that\l"
    .string "thou hast sent him away, and he is\l"
    .string "quite gone?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_25::
    .string "Thou knowest Abner the son of Ner,\n"
    .string "that he came to deceive thee, and to\l"
    .string "know thy going out and thy coming in,\l"
    .string "and to know all that thou doest$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_26::
    .string "And when Joab was come out from\n"
    .string "David, he sent messengers after\l"
    .string "Abner, which brought him again from\l"
    .string "the well of Sirah: but David knew it\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_27::
    .string "And when Abner was returned to\n"
    .string "Hebron, Joab took him aside in the\l"
    .string "gate to speak with him quietly, and\l"
    .string "smote him there under the fifth rib,\l"
    .string "that he died, for the blood of\l"
    .string "Asahel his brother.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_28::
    .string "And afterward when David heard it,\n"
    .string "he said, I and my kingdom are\l"
    .string "guiltless before the LORD for ever\l"
    .string "from the blood of Abner the son of\l"
    .string "Ner:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_29::
    .string "Let it rest on the head of Joab, and\n"
    .string "on all his father’s house; and let\l"
    .string "there not fail from the house of\l"
    .string "Joab one that hath an issue, or that\l"
    .string "is a leper, or that leaneth on a\l"
    .string "staff, or that falleth on the sword,\l"
    .string "or that lacketh bread$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_30::
    .string "So Joab, and Abishai his brother\n"
    .string "slew Abner, because he had slain\l"
    .string "their brother Asahel at Gibeon in\l"
    .string "the battle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_31::
    .string "And David said to Joab, and to all\n"
    .string "the people that were with him, Rend\l"
    .string "your clothes, and gird you with\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and mourn before Abner.\l"
    .string "And king David himself followed\l"
    .string "the bier.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_32::
    .string "And they buried Abner in Hebron: and\n"
    .string "the king lifted up his voice, and\l"
    .string "wept at the grave of Abner; and all\l"
    .string "the people wept.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_33::
    .string "And the king lamented over Abner,\n"
    .string "and said, Died Abner as a fool dieth?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_34::
    .string "Thy hands were not bound, nor thy\n"
    .string "feet put into fetters: as a man\l"
    .string "falleth before wicked men, so\l"
    .string "fellest thou. And all the people\l"
    .string "wept again over him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_35::
    .string "And when all the people came to\n"
    .string "cause David to eat meat while it was\l"
    .string "yet day, David sware, saying, So do\l"
    .string "God to me, and more also, if I taste\l"
    .string "bread, or ought else, till the sun\l"
    .string "be down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_36::
    .string "And all the people took notice\n"
    .string "of it, and it pleased them: as\l"
    .string "whatsoever the king did pleased\l"
    .string "all the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_37::
    .string "For all the people and all\n"
    .string "Israel understood that day that it\l"
    .string "was not of the king to slay Abner the\l"
    .string "son of Ner.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_38::
    .string "And the king said unto his servants,\n"
    .string "Know ye not that there is a prince\l"
    .string "and a great man fallen this day in\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_3_39::
    .string "And I am this day weak, though\n"
    .string "anointed king; and these men the sons\l"
    .string "of Zeruiah be too hard for me: the\l"
    .string "LORD shall reward the doer of evil\l"
    .string "according to his wickedness$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_1::
    .string "And when Saul’s son heard that\n"
    .string "Abner was dead in Hebron, his hands\l"
    .string "were feeble, and all the\l"
    .string "Israelites were troubled.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_2::
    .string "And Saul’s son had two men that\n"
    .string "were captains of bands: the name of\l"
    .string "the one was Baanah, and the name of\l"
    .string "the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon\l"
    .string "a Beerothite, of the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin: (for Beeroth also was\l"
    .string "reckoned to Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_3::
    .string "And the Beerothites fled to\n"
    .string "Gittaim, and were sojourners there\l"
    .string "until this day.)"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_4::
    .string "And Jonathan, Saul’s son, had a son\n"
    .string "that was lame of his feet. He was\l"
    .string "five years old when the tidings came\l"
    .string "of Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel,\l"
    .string "and his nurse took him up, and fled:\l"
    .string "and it came to pass, as she made\l"
    .string "haste to flee, that he fell, and\l"
    .string "became lame. And his name was\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_5::
    .string "And the sons of Rimmon the\n"
    .string "Beerothite, Rechab and Baanah, went,\l"
    .string "and came about the heat of the day to\l"
    .string "the house of Ishbosheth, who lay on a\l"
    .string "bed at noon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_6::
    .string "And they came thither into the midst\n"
    .string "of the house, as though they would\l"
    .string "have fetched wheat; and they smote\l"
    .string "him under the fifth rib: and Rechab\l"
    .string "and Baanah his brother escaped.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_7::
    .string "For when they came into the house,\n"
    .string "he lay on his bed in his bedchamber,\l"
    .string "and they smote him, and slew him, and\l"
    .string "beheaded him, and took his head, and\l"
    .string "gat them away through the plain\l"
    .string "all night.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_8::
    .string "And they brought the head of\n"
    .string "Ishbosheth unto David to Hebron, and\l"
    .string "said to the king, Behold the head of\l"
    .string "Ishbosheth the son of Saul thine\l"
    .string "enemy, which sought thy life; and\l"
    .string "the LORD hath avenged my lord the\l"
    .string "king this day of Saul, and of his\l"
    .string "seed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_9::
    .string "And David answered Rechab and\n"
    .string "Baanah his brother, the sons of\l"
    .string "Rimmon the Beerothite, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, As the LORD liveth, who hath\l"
    .string "redeemed my soul out of all\l"
    .string "adversity,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_10::
    .string "When one told me, saying, Behold,\n"
    .string "Saul is dead, thinking to have\l"
    .string "brought good tidings, I took hold of\l"
    .string "him, and slew him in Ziklag, who\l"
    .string "thought that I would have given him\l"
    .string "a reward for his tidings:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_11::
    .string "How much more, when wicked men have\n"
    .string "slain a righteous person in his own\l"
    .string "house upon his bed? shall I not\l"
    .string "therefore now require his blood of\l"
    .string "your hand, and take you away from the\l"
    .string "earth?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_4_12::
    .string "And David commanded his young men,\n"
    .string "and they slew them, and cut off their\l"
    .string "hands and their feet, and hanged them\l"
    .string "up over the pool in Hebron. But\l"
    .string "they took the head of Ishbosheth, and\l"
    .string "buried it in the sepulchre of Abner\l"
    .string "in Hebron$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_1::
    .string "Then came all the tribes of Israel\n"
    .string "to David unto Hebron, and spake,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold, we are thy bone and\l"
    .string "thy flesh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_2::
    .string "Also in time past, when Saul was\n"
    .string "king over us, thou wast he that\l"
    .string "leddest out and broughtest in\l"
    .string "Israel: and the LORD said to thee,\l"
    .string "Thou shalt feed my people Israel,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt be a captain over\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_3::
    .string "So all the elders of Israel came\n"
    .string "to the king to Hebron; and king David\l"
    .string "made a league with them in Hebron\l"
    .string "before the LORD: and they anointed\l"
    .string "David king over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_4::
    .string "David was thirty years old when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned forty\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_5::
    .string "In Hebron he reigned over Judah\n"
    .string "seven years and six months: and in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem he reigned thirty and\l"
    .string "three years over all Israel and\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_6::
    .string "And the king and his men went to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem unto the Jebusites, the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land: which\l"
    .string "spake unto David, saying, Except\l"
    .string "thou take away the blind and the\l"
    .string "lame, thou shalt not come in hither:\l"
    .string "thinking, David cannot come in\l"
    .string "hither.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_7::
    .string "Nevertheless David took the strong\n"
    .string "hold of Zion: the same is the city of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_8::
    .string "And David said on that day,\n"
    .string "Whosoever getteth up to the gutter,\l"
    .string "and smiteth the Jebusites, and the\l"
    .string "lame and the blind that are hated of\l"
    .string "David’s soul, he shall be chief and\l"
    .string "captain. Wherefore they said, The\l"
    .string "blind and the lame shall not come\l"
    .string "into the house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_9::
    .string "So David dwelt in the fort, and\n"
    .string "called it the city of David. And\l"
    .string "David built round about from Millo\l"
    .string "and inward.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_10::
    .string "And David went on, and grew great,\n"
    .string "and the LORD God of hosts was with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_11::
    .string "And Hiram king of Tyre sent\n"
    .string "messengers to David, and cedar trees,\l"
    .string "and carpenters, and masons: and they\l"
    .string "built David an house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_12::
    .string "And David perceived that the LORD\n"
    .string "had established him king over\l"
    .string "Israel, and that he had exalted his\l"
    .string "kingdom for his people Israel’s\l"
    .string "sake.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_13::
    .string "And David took him more concubines\n"
    .string "and wives out of Jerusalem, after he\l"
    .string "was come from Hebron: and there were\l"
    .string "yet sons and daughters born to David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_14::
    .string "And these be the names of those that\n"
    .string "were born unto him in Jerusalem;\l"
    .string "Shammuah, and Shobab, and Nathan, and\l"
    .string "Solomon,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_15::
    .string "Ibhar also, and Elishua, and\n"
    .string "Nepheg, and Japhia,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_16::
    .string "And Elishama, and Eliada, and\n"
    .string "Eliphalet$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_17::
    .string "But when the Philistines heard that\n"
    .string "they had anointed David king over\l"
    .string "Israel, all the Philistines came\l"
    .string "up to seek David; and David heard of\l"
    .string "it, and went down to the hold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_18::
    .string "The Philistines also came and\n"
    .string "spread themselves in the valley of\l"
    .string "Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_19::
    .string "And David enquired of the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying, Shall I go up to the\l"
    .string "Philistines? wilt thou deliver\l"
    .string "them into mine hand? And the LORD\l"
    .string "said unto David, Go up: for I will\l"
    .string "doubtless deliver the Philistines\l"
    .string "into thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_20::
    .string "And David came to Baalperazim, and\n"
    .string "David smote them there, and said, The\l"
    .string "LORD hath broken forth upon mine\l"
    .string "enemies before me, as the breach of\l"
    .string "waters. Therefore he called the\l"
    .string "name of that place Baalperazim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_21::
    .string "And there they left their images,\n"
    .string "and David and his men burned them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_22::
    .string "And the Philistines came up yet\n"
    .string "again, and spread themselves in the\l"
    .string "valley of Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_23::
    .string "And when David enquired of the LORD,\n"
    .string "he said, Thou shalt not go up; but\l"
    .string "fetch a compass behind them, and\l"
    .string "come upon them over against the\l"
    .string "mulberry trees.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_24::
    .string "And let it be, when thou hearest the\n"
    .string "sound of a going in the tops of the\l"
    .string "mulberry trees, that then thou\l"
    .string "shalt bestir thyself: for then\l"
    .string "shall the LORD go out before thee,\l"
    .string "to smite the host of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_5_25::
    .string "And David did so, as the LORD had\n"
    .string "commanded him; and smote the\l"
    .string "Philistines from Geba until thou\l"
    .string "come to Gazer.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_1::
    .string "Again, David gathered together all\n"
    .string "the chosen men of Israel, thirty\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_2::
    .string "And David arose, and went with all\n"
    .string "the people that were with him from\l"
    .string "Baale of Judah, to bring up from\l"
    .string "thence the ark of God, whose name is\l"
    .string "called by the name of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts that dwelleth between the\l"
    .string "cherubims.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_3::
    .string "And they set the ark of God upon a\n"
    .string "new cart, and brought it out of the\l"
    .string "house of Abinadab that was in Gibeah:\l"
    .string "and Uzzah and Ahio, the sons of\l"
    .string "Abinadab, drave the new cart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_4::
    .string "And they brought it out of the house\n"
    .string "of Abinadab which was at Gibeah,\l"
    .string "accompanying the ark of God: and\l"
    .string "Ahio went before the ark.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_5::
    .string "And David and all the house of\n"
    .string "Israel played before the LORD on\l"
    .string "all manner of instruments made of\l"
    .string "fir wood, even on harps, and on\l"
    .string "psalteries, and on timbrels, and on\l"
    .string "cornets, and on cymbals.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_6::
    .string "And when they came to Nachon’s\n"
    .string "threshingfloor, Uzzah put forth his\l"
    .string "hand to the ark of God, and took hold\l"
    .string "of it; for the oxen shook it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_7::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Uzzah; and God smote\l"
    .string "him there for his error; and there he\l"
    .string "died by the ark of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_8::
    .string "And David was displeased, because\n"
    .string "the LORD had made a breach upon\l"
    .string "Uzzah: and he called the name of the\l"
    .string "place Perezuzzah to this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_9::
    .string "And David was afraid of the LORD\n"
    .string "that day, and said, How shall the\l"
    .string "ark of the LORD come to me?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_10::
    .string "So David would not remove the ark\n"
    .string "of the LORD unto him into the city of\l"
    .string "David: but David carried it aside\l"
    .string "into the house of Obededom the\l"
    .string "Gittite$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_11::
    .string "And the ark of the LORD continued in\n"
    .string "the house of Obededom the Gittite\l"
    .string "three months: and the LORD blessed\l"
    .string "Obededom, and all his household.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_12::
    .string "And it was told king David, saying,\n"
    .string "The LORD hath blessed the house of\l"
    .string "Obededom, and all that pertaineth\l"
    .string "unto him, because of the ark of God.\l"
    .string "So David went and brought up the ark\l"
    .string "of God from the house of Obededom\l"
    .string "into the city of David with gladness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_13::
    .string "And it was so, that when they that\n"
    .string "bare the ark of the LORD had gone six\l"
    .string "paces, he sacrificed oxen and\l"
    .string "fatlings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_14::
    .string "And David danced before the LORD\n"
    .string "with all his might; and David was\l"
    .string "girded with a linen ephod.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_15::
    .string "So David and all the house of\n"
    .string "Israel brought up the ark of the\l"
    .string "LORD with shouting, and with the\l"
    .string "sound of the trumpet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_16::
    .string "And as the ark of the LORD came into\n"
    .string "the city of David, Michal Saul’s\l"
    .string "daughter looked through a window,\l"
    .string "and saw king David leaping and\l"
    .string "dancing before the LORD; and she\l"
    .string "despised him in her heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_17::
    .string "And they brought in the ark of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and set it in his place, in\l"
    .string "the midst of the tabernacle that\l"
    .string "David had pitched for it: and David\l"
    .string "offered burnt offerings and peace\l"
    .string "offerings before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_18::
    .string "And as soon as David had made an end\n"
    .string "of offering burnt offerings and\l"
    .string "peace offerings, he blessed the\l"
    .string "people in the name of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_19::
    .string "And he dealt among all the\n"
    .string "people, even among the whole\l"
    .string "multitude of Israel, as well to\l"
    .string "the women as men, to every one a cake\l"
    .string "of bread, and a good piece of flesh,\l"
    .string "and a flagon of wine. So all the\l"
    .string "people departed every one to his\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_20::
    .string "Then David returned to bless his\n"
    .string "household. And Michal the daughter\l"
    .string "of Saul came out to meet David, and\l"
    .string "said, How glorious was the king of\l"
    .string "Israel to day, who uncovered\l"
    .string "himself to day in the eyes of the\l"
    .string "handmaids of his servants, as one of\l"
    .string "the vain fellows shamelessly\l"
    .string "uncovereth himself!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_21::
    .string "And David said unto Michal, It was\n"
    .string "before the LORD, which chose me\l"
    .string "before thy father, and before all\l"
    .string "his house, to appoint me ruler over\l"
    .string "the people of the LORD, over\l"
    .string "Israel: therefore will I play\l"
    .string "before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_22::
    .string "And I will yet be more vile than\n"
    .string "thus, and will be base in mine own\l"
    .string "sight: and of the maidservants which\l"
    .string "thou hast spoken of, of them shall\l"
    .string "I be had in honour.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_6_23::
    .string "Therefore Michal the daughter of\n"
    .string "Saul had no child unto the day of\l"
    .string "her death.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "sat in his house, and the LORD had\l"
    .string "given him rest round about from all\l"
    .string "his enemies;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_2::
    .string "That the king said unto Nathan the\n"
    .string "prophet, See now, I dwell in an\l"
    .string "house of cedar, but the ark of God\l"
    .string "dwelleth within curtains$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_3::
    .string "And Nathan said to the king, Go, do\n"
    .string "all that is in thine heart; for the\l"
    .string "LORD is with thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_4::
    .string "And it came to pass that night, that\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD came unto\l"
    .string "Nathan, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_5::
    .string "Go and tell my servant David, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, Shalt thou build me\l"
    .string "an house for me to dwell in?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_6::
    .string "Whereas I have not dwelt in any\n"
    .string "house since the time that I brought\l"
    .string "up the children of Israel out of\l"
    .string "Egypt, even to this day, but have\l"
    .string "walked in a tent and in a tabernacle$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_7::
    .string "In all the places wherein I have\n"
    .string "walked with all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel spake I a word with any of\l"
    .string "the tribes of Israel, whom I\l"
    .string "commanded to feed my people\l"
    .string "Israel, saying, Why build ye not me\l"
    .string "an house of cedar?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_8::
    .string "Now therefore so shalt thou say\n"
    .string "unto my servant David, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, I took thee from the\l"
    .string "sheepcote, from following the\l"
    .string "sheep, to be ruler over my people,\l"
    .string "over Israel:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_9::
    .string "And I was with thee whithersoever\n"
    .string "thou wentest, and have cut off all\l"
    .string "thine enemies out of thy sight, and\l"
    .string "have made thee a great name, like\l"
    .string "unto the name of the great men that\l"
    .string "are in the earth$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_10::
    .string "Moreover I will appoint a place\n"
    .string "for my people Israel, and will\l"
    .string "plant them, that they may dwell in\l"
    .string "a place of their own, and move no\l"
    .string "more; neither shall the children of\l"
    .string "wickedness afflict them any more, as\l"
    .string "beforetime,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_11::
    .string "And as since the time that I\n"
    .string "commanded judges to be over my\l"
    .string "people Israel, and have caused thee\l"
    .string "to rest from all thine enemies.\l"
    .string "Also the LORD telleth thee that he\l"
    .string "will make thee an house$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_12::
    .string "And when thy days be fulfilled,\n"
    .string "and thou shalt sleep with thy\l"
    .string "fathers, I will set up thy seed\l"
    .string "after thee, which shall proceed out\l"
    .string "of thy bowels, and I will\l"
    .string "establish his kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_13::
    .string "He shall build an house for my\n"
    .string "name, and I will stablish the\l"
    .string "throne of his kingdom for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_14::
    .string "I will be his father, and he shall\n"
    .string "be my son. If he commit iniquity, I\l"
    .string "will chasten him with the rod of\l"
    .string "men, and with the stripes of the\l"
    .string "children of men:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_15::
    .string "But my mercy shall not depart away\n"
    .string "from him, as I took it from Saul,\l"
    .string "whom I put away before thee$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_16::
    .string "And thine house and thy kingdom\n"
    .string "shall be established for ever\l"
    .string "before thee: thy throne shall be\l"
    .string "established for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_17::
    .string "According to all these words, and\n"
    .string "according to all this vision, so did\l"
    .string "Nathan speak unto David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_18::
    .string "Then went king David in, and sat\n"
    .string "before the LORD, and he said, Who am\l"
    .string "I, O Lord GOD? and what is my house,\l"
    .string "that thou hast brought me hitherto?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_19::
    .string "And this was yet a small thing in\n"
    .string "thy sight, O Lord GOD; but thou hast\l"
    .string "spoken also of thy servant’s house\l"
    .string "for a great while to come. And is\l"
    .string "this the manner of man, O Lord GOD?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_20::
    .string "And what can David say more unto\n"
    .string "thee? for thou, Lord GOD, knowest thy\l"
    .string "servant$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_21::
    .string "For thy word’s sake, and according\n"
    .string "to thine own heart, hast thou done\l"
    .string "all these great things, to make thy\l"
    .string "servant know them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_22::
    .string "Wherefore thou art great, O LORD\n"
    .string "God: for there is none like thee,\l"
    .string "neither is there any God beside thee,\l"
    .string "according to all that we have heard\l"
    .string "with our ears.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_23::
    .string "And what one nation in the earth is\n"
    .string "like thy people, even like\l"
    .string "Israel, whom God went to redeem for a\l"
    .string "people to himself, and to make him\l"
    .string "a name, and to do for you great things\l"
    .string "and terrible, for thy land, before\l"
    .string "thy people, which thou redeemedst\l"
    .string "to thee from Egypt, from the nations\l"
    .string "and their gods?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_24::
    .string "For thou hast confirmed to thyself\n"
    .string "thy people Israel to be a people\l"
    .string "unto thee for ever: and thou, LORD,\l"
    .string "art become their God$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_25::
    .string "And now, O LORD God, the word that\n"
    .string "thou hast spoken concerning thy\l"
    .string "servant, and concerning his house,\l"
    .string "establish it for ever, and do as thou\l"
    .string "hast said.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_26::
    .string "And let thy name be magnified for\n"
    .string "ever, saying, The LORD of hosts is\l"
    .string "the God over Israel: and let the\l"
    .string "house of thy servant David be\l"
    .string "established before thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_27::
    .string "For thou, O LORD of hosts, God of\n"
    .string "Israel, hast revealed to thy\l"
    .string "servant, saying, I will build thee\l"
    .string "an house: therefore hath thy servant\l"
    .string "found in his heart to pray this\l"
    .string "prayer unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_28::
    .string "And now, O Lord GOD, thou art that\n"
    .string "God, and thy words be true, and thou\l"
    .string "hast promised this goodness unto thy\l"
    .string "servant:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_7_29::
    .string "Therefore now let it please thee\n"
    .string "to bless the house of thy servant,\l"
    .string "that it may continue for ever before\l"
    .string "thee: for thou, O Lord GOD, hast\l"
    .string "spoken it: and with thy blessing\l"
    .string "let the house of thy servant be\l"
    .string "blessed for ever$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_1::
    .string "And after this it came to pass that\n"
    .string "David smote the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "subdued them: and David took\l"
    .string "Methegammah out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_2::
    .string "And he smote Moab, and measured them\n"
    .string "with a line, casting them down to the\l"
    .string "ground; even with two lines measured\l"
    .string "he to put to death, and with one\l"
    .string "full line to keep alive. And so\l"
    .string "the Moabites became David’s\l"
    .string "servants, and brought gifts.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_3::
    .string "David smote also Hadadezer, the son\n"
    .string "of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to\l"
    .string "recover his border at the river\l"
    .string "Euphrates.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_4::
    .string "And David took from him a thousand\n"
    .string "chariots, and seven hundred\l"
    .string "horsemen, and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "footmen: and David houghed all the\l"
    .string "chariot horses, but reserved of them\l"
    .string "for an hundred chariots.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_5::
    .string "And when the Syrians of Damascus\n"
    .string "came to succour Hadadezer king of\l"
    .string "Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two\l"
    .string "and twenty thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_6::
    .string "Then David put garrisons in Syria\n"
    .string "of Damascus: and the Syrians became\l"
    .string "servants to David, and brought gifts.\l"
    .string "And the LORD preserved David\l"
    .string "whithersoever he went.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_7::
    .string "And David took the shields of gold\n"
    .string "that were on the servants of\l"
    .string "Hadadezer, and brought them to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_8::
    .string "And from Betah, and from Berothai,\n"
    .string "cities of Hadadezer, king David took\l"
    .string "exceeding much brass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_9::
    .string "When Toi king of Hamath heard that\n"
    .string "David had smitten all the host of\l"
    .string "Hadadezer,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_10::
    .string "Then Toi sent Joram his son unto\n"
    .string "king David, to salute him, and to\l"
    .string "bless him, because he had fought\l"
    .string "against Hadadezer, and smitten him:\l"
    .string "for Hadadezer had wars with Toi. And\l"
    .string "Joram brought with him vessels of\l"
    .string "silver, and vessels of gold, and\l"
    .string "vessels of brass:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_11::
    .string "Which also king David did dedicate\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, with the silver and\l"
    .string "gold that he had dedicated of all\l"
    .string "nations which he subdued;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_12::
    .string "Of Syria, and of Moab, and of the\n"
    .string "children of Ammon, and of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and of Amalek, and of\l"
    .string "the spoil of Hadadezer, son of\l"
    .string "Rehob, king of Zobah$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_13::
    .string "And David gat him a name when he\n"
    .string "returned from smiting of the Syrians\l"
    .string "in the valley of salt, being\l"
    .string "eighteen thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_14::
    .string "And he put garrisons in Edom;\n"
    .string "throughout all Edom put he\l"
    .string "garrisons, and all they of Edom\l"
    .string "became David’s servants. And the LORD\l"
    .string "preserved David whithersoever he\l"
    .string "went.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_15::
    .string "And David reigned over all Israel;\n"
    .string "and David executed judgment and\l"
    .string "justice unto all his people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_16::
    .string "And Joab the son of Zeruiah was over\n"
    .string "the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of\l"
    .string "Ahilud was recorder;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_17::
    .string "And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and\n"
    .string "Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, were\l"
    .string "the priests; and Seraiah was the\l"
    .string "scribe;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_8_18::
    .string "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was\n"
    .string "over both the Cherethites and the\l"
    .string "Pelethites; and David’s sons were\l"
    .string "chief rulers$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_1::
    .string "And David said, Is there yet any\n"
    .string "that is left of the house of Saul,\l"
    .string "that I may shew him kindness for\l"
    .string "Jonathan’s sake?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_2::
    .string "And there was of the house of Saul a\n"
    .string "servant whose name was Ziba. And when\l"
    .string "they had called him unto David, the\l"
    .string "king said unto him, Art thou Ziba?\l"
    .string "And he said, Thy servant is he$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_3::
    .string "And the king said, Is there not yet\n"
    .string "any of the house of Saul, that I may\l"
    .string "shew the kindness of God unto him?\l"
    .string "And Ziba said unto the king, Jonathan\l"
    .string "hath yet a son, which is lame on his\l"
    .string "feet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_4::
    .string "And the king said unto him, Where is\n"
    .string "he? And Ziba said unto the king,\l"
    .string "Behold, he is in the house of Machir,\l"
    .string "the son of Ammiel, in Lodebar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_5::
    .string "Then king David sent, and fetched\n"
    .string "him out of the house of Machir, the\l"
    .string "son of Ammiel, from Lodebar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_6::
    .string "Now when Mephibosheth, the son of\n"
    .string "Jonathan, the son of Saul, was come\l"
    .string "unto David, he fell on his face, and\l"
    .string "did reverence. And David said,\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth. And he answered,\l"
    .string "Behold thy servant!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_7::
    .string "And David said unto him, Fear not:\n"
    .string "for I will surely shew thee\l"
    .string "kindness for Jonathan thy father’s\l"
    .string "sake, and will restore thee all\l"
    .string "the land of Saul thy father; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt eat bread at my table\l"
    .string "continually$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_8::
    .string "And he bowed himself, and said,\n"
    .string "What is thy servant, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest look upon such a dead dog\l"
    .string "as I am?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_9::
    .string "Then the king called to Ziba,\n"
    .string "Saul’s servant, and said unto him, I\l"
    .string "have given unto thy master’s son\l"
    .string "all that pertained to Saul and to\l"
    .string "all his house$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_10::
    .string "Thou therefore, and thy sons, and\n"
    .string "thy servants, shall till the land\l"
    .string "for him, and thou shalt bring in the\l"
    .string "fruits, that thy master’s son may\l"
    .string "have food to eat: but Mephibosheth\l"
    .string "thy master’s son shall eat bread\l"
    .string "alway at my table. Now Ziba had\l"
    .string "fifteen sons and twenty servants.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_11::
    .string "Then said Ziba unto the king,\n"
    .string "According to all that my lord the\l"
    .string "king hath commanded his servant, so\l"
    .string "shall thy servant do. As for\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth, said the king, he\l"
    .string "shall eat at my table, as one of the\l"
    .string "king’s sons.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_12::
    .string "And Mephibosheth had a young son,\n"
    .string "whose name was Micha. And all that\l"
    .string "dwelt in the house of Ziba were\l"
    .string "servants unto Mephibosheth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_9_13::
    .string "So Mephibosheth dwelt in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: for he did eat\l"
    .string "continually at the king’s table;\l"
    .string "and was lame on both his feet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "the king of the children of Ammon\l"
    .string "died, and Hanun his son reigned in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_2::
    .string "Then said David, I will shew\n"
    .string "kindness unto Hanun the son of\l"
    .string "Nahash, as his father shewed kindness\l"
    .string "unto me. And David sent to comfort\l"
    .string "him by the hand of his servants for\l"
    .string "his father. And David’s servants came\l"
    .string "into the land of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_3::
    .string "And the princes of the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon said unto Hanun their lord,\l"
    .string "Thinkest thou that David doth honour\l"
    .string "thy father, that he hath sent\l"
    .string "comforters unto thee? hath not David\l"
    .string "rather sent his servants unto thee,\l"
    .string "to search the city, and to spy it\l"
    .string "out, and to overthrow it?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_4::
    .string "Wherefore Hanun took David’s\n"
    .string "servants, and shaved off the one\l"
    .string "half of their beards, and cut off\l"
    .string "their garments in the middle, even\l"
    .string "to their buttocks, and sent them away$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_5::
    .string "When they told it unto David, he\n"
    .string "sent to meet them, because the men\l"
    .string "were greatly ashamed: and the king\l"
    .string "said, Tarry at Jericho until your\l"
    .string "beards be grown, and then return.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_6::
    .string "And when the children of Ammon saw\n"
    .string "that they stank before David, the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon sent and hired the\l"
    .string "Syrians of Bethrehob and the Syrians\l"
    .string "of Zoba, twenty thousand footmen, and\l"
    .string "of king Maacah a thousand men, and of\l"
    .string "Ishtob twelve thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_7::
    .string "And when David heard of it, he sent\n"
    .string "Joab, and all the host of the mighty\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_8::
    .string "And the children of Ammon came out,\n"
    .string "and put the battle in array at the\l"
    .string "entering in of the gate: and the\l"
    .string "Syrians of Zoba, and of Rehob, and\l"
    .string "Ishtob, and Maacah, were by\l"
    .string "themselves in the field.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_9::
    .string "When Joab saw that the front of the\n"
    .string "battle was against him before and\l"
    .string "behind, he chose of all the choice\l"
    .string "men of Israel, and put them in array\l"
    .string "against the Syrians:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_10::
    .string "And the rest of the people he\n"
    .string "delivered into the hand of Abishai\l"
    .string "his brother, that he might put them\l"
    .string "in array against the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_11::
    .string "And he said, If the Syrians be too\n"
    .string "strong for me, then thou shalt help\l"
    .string "me: but if the children of Ammon be\l"
    .string "too strong for thee, then I will\l"
    .string "come and help thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_12::
    .string "Be of good courage, and let us\n"
    .string "play the men for our people, and\l"
    .string "for the cities of our God: and the\l"
    .string "LORD do that which seemeth him good.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_13::
    .string "And Joab drew nigh, and the people\n"
    .string "that were with him, unto the battle\l"
    .string "against the Syrians: and they fled\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_14::
    .string "And when the children of Ammon saw\n"
    .string "that the Syrians were fled, then\l"
    .string "fled they also before Abishai, and\l"
    .string "entered into the city. So Joab\l"
    .string "returned from the children of Ammon,\l"
    .string "and came to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_15::
    .string "And when the Syrians saw that they\n"
    .string "were smitten before Israel, they\l"
    .string "gathered themselves together.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_16::
    .string "And Hadarezer sent, and brought out\n"
    .string "the Syrians that were beyond the\l"
    .string "river: and they came to Helam; and\l"
    .string "Shobach the captain of the host of\l"
    .string "Hadarezer went before them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_17::
    .string "And when it was told David, he\n"
    .string "gathered all Israel together, and\l"
    .string "passed over Jordan, and came to Helam\l"
    .string " And the Syrians set themselves in\l"
    .string "array against David, and fought with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_18::
    .string "And the Syrians fled before\n"
    .string "Israel; and David slew the men of\l"
    .string "seven hundred chariots of the\l"
    .string "Syrians, and forty thousand\l"
    .string "horsemen, and smote Shobach the\l"
    .string "captain of their host, who died\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_10_19::
    .string "And when all the kings that were\n"
    .string "servants to Hadarezer saw that they\l"
    .string "were smitten before Israel, they\l"
    .string "made peace with Israel, and served\l"
    .string "them. So the Syrians feared to help\l"
    .string "the children of Ammon any more.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, after the year\n"
    .string "was expired, at the time when kings\l"
    .string "go forth to battle, that David sent\l"
    .string "Joab, and his servants with him, and\l"
    .string "all Israel; and they destroyed the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon, and besieged\l"
    .string "Rabbah. But David tarried still at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_2::
    .string "And it came to pass in an\n"
    .string "eveningtide, that David arose from\l"
    .string "off his bed, and walked upon the\l"
    .string "roof of the king’s house: and from\l"
    .string "the roof he saw a woman washing\l"
    .string "herself; and the woman was very\l"
    .string "beautiful to look upon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_3::
    .string "And David sent and enquired after\n"
    .string "the woman. And one said, Is not this\l"
    .string "Bathsheba, the daughter of Eliam,\l"
    .string "the wife of Uriah the Hittite?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_4::
    .string "And David sent messengers, and took\n"
    .string "her; and she came in unto him, and he\l"
    .string "lay with her; for she was purified\l"
    .string "from her uncleanness: and she\l"
    .string "returned unto her house$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_5::
    .string "And the woman conceived, and sent\n"
    .string "and told David, and said, I am with\l"
    .string "child.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_6::
    .string "And David sent to Joab, saying, Send\n"
    .string "me Uriah the Hittite. And Joab sent\l"
    .string "Uriah to David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_7::
    .string "And when Uriah was come unto him,\n"
    .string "David demanded of him how Joab did,\l"
    .string "and how the people did, and how the\l"
    .string "war prospered.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_8::
    .string "And David said to Uriah, Go down to\n"
    .string "thy house, and wash thy feet. And\l"
    .string "Uriah departed out of the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and there followed him a mess\l"
    .string "of meat from the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_9::
    .string "But Uriah slept at the door of the\n"
    .string "king’s house with all the servants\l"
    .string "of his lord, and went not down to his\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_10::
    .string "And when they had told David,\n"
    .string "saying, Uriah went not down unto his\l"
    .string "house, David said unto Uriah, Camest\l"
    .string "thou not from thy journey? why then\l"
    .string "didst thou not go down unto thine\l"
    .string "house?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_11::
    .string "And Uriah said unto David, The ark,\n"
    .string "and Israel, and Judah, abide in\l"
    .string "tents; and my lord Joab, and the\l"
    .string "servants of my lord, are encamped in\l"
    .string "the open fields; shall I then go\l"
    .string "into mine house, to eat and to drink,\l"
    .string "and to lie with my wife? as thou\l"
    .string "livest, and as thy soul liveth, I\l"
    .string "will not do this thing$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_12::
    .string "And David said to Uriah, Tarry here\n"
    .string "to day also, and to morrow I will\l"
    .string "let thee depart. So Uriah abode in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem that day, and the morrow.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_13::
    .string "And when David had called him, he\n"
    .string "did eat and drink before him; and he\l"
    .string "made him drunk: and at even he went\l"
    .string "out to lie on his bed with the\l"
    .string "servants of his lord, but went not\l"
    .string "down to his house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_14::
    .string "And it came to pass in the morning,\n"
    .string "that David wrote a letter to Joab,\l"
    .string "and sent it by the hand of Uriah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_15::
    .string "And he wrote in the letter, saying,\n"
    .string "Set ye Uriah in the forefront of the\l"
    .string "hottest battle, and retire ye from\l"
    .string "him, that he may be smitten, and die.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joab\n"
    .string "observed the city, that he assigned\l"
    .string "Uriah unto a place where he knew\l"
    .string "that valiant men were.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_17::
    .string "And the men of the city went out, and\n"
    .string "fought with Joab: and there fell\l"
    .string "some of the people of the servants\l"
    .string "of David; and Uriah the Hittite died\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_18::
    .string "Then Joab sent and told David all\n"
    .string "the things concerning the war;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_19::
    .string "And charged the messenger, saying,\n"
    .string "When thou hast made an end of\l"
    .string "telling the matters of the war unto\l"
    .string "the king,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_20::
    .string "And if so be that the king’s wrath\n"
    .string "arise, and he say unto thee,\l"
    .string "Wherefore approached ye so nigh\l"
    .string "unto the city when ye did fight? knew\l"
    .string "ye not that they would shoot from\l"
    .string "the wall?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_21::
    .string "Who smote Abimelech the son of\n"
    .string "Jerubbesheth? did not a woman cast a\l"
    .string "piece of a millstone upon him from\l"
    .string "the wall, that he died in Thebez?\l"
    .string "why went ye nigh the wall? then say\l"
    .string "thou, Thy servant Uriah the Hittite\l"
    .string "is dead also$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_22::
    .string "So the messenger went, and came and\n"
    .string "shewed David all that Joab had sent\l"
    .string "him for.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_23::
    .string "And the messenger said unto David,\n"
    .string "Surely the men prevailed against\l"
    .string "us, and came out unto us into the\l"
    .string "field, and we were upon them even\l"
    .string "unto the entering of the gate.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_24::
    .string "And the shooters shot from off the\n"
    .string "wall upon thy servants; and some of\l"
    .string "the king’s servants be dead, and thy\l"
    .string "servant Uriah the Hittite is dead\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_25::
    .string "Then David said unto the messenger,\n"
    .string "Thus shalt thou say unto Joab, Let\l"
    .string "not this thing displease thee, for\l"
    .string "the sword devoureth one as well as\l"
    .string "another: make thy battle more strong\l"
    .string "against the city, and overthrow it:\l"
    .string "and encourage thou him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_26::
    .string "And when the wife of Uriah heard\n"
    .string "that Uriah her husband was dead, she\l"
    .string "mourned for her husband.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_11_27::
    .string "And when the mourning was past,\n"
    .string "David sent and fetched her to his\l"
    .string "house, and she became his wife, and\l"
    .string "bare him a son. But the thing that\l"
    .string "David had done displeased the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_1::
    .string "And the LORD sent Nathan unto David.\n"
    .string "And he came unto him, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, There were two men in one city;\l"
    .string "the one rich, and the other poor.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_2::
    .string "The rich man had exceeding many\n"
    .string "flocks and herds:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_3::
    .string "But the poor man had nothing, save\n"
    .string "one little ewe lamb, which he had\l"
    .string "bought and nourished up: and it grew\l"
    .string "up together with him, and with his\l"
    .string "children; it did eat of his own meat,\l"
    .string "and drank of his own cup, and lay in\l"
    .string "his bosom, and was unto him as a\l"
    .string "daughter$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_4::
    .string "And there came a traveller unto\n"
    .string "the rich man, and he spared to take\l"
    .string "of his own flock and of his own herd,\l"
    .string "to dress for the wayfaring man that\l"
    .string "was come unto him; but took the poor\l"
    .string "man’s lamb, and dressed it for the\l"
    .string "man that was come to him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_5::
    .string "And David’s anger was greatly\n"
    .string "kindled against the man; and he said\l"
    .string "to Nathan, As the LORD liveth, the\l"
    .string "man that hath done this thing shall\l"
    .string "surely die:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_6::
    .string "And he shall restore the lamb\n"
    .string "fourfold, because he did this thing,\l"
    .string "and because he had no pity$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_7::
    .string "And Nathan said to David, Thou art\n"
    .string "the man. Thus saith the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel, I anointed thee king over\l"
    .string "Israel, and I delivered thee out of\l"
    .string "the hand of Saul;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_8::
    .string "And I gave thee thy master’s house,\n"
    .string "and thy master’s wives into thy\l"
    .string "bosom, and gave thee the house of\l"
    .string "Israel and of Judah; and if that had\l"
    .string "been too little, I would moreover\l"
    .string "have given unto thee such and such\l"
    .string "things$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_9::
    .string "Wherefore hast thou despised the\n"
    .string "commandment of the LORD, to do evil\l"
    .string "in his sight? thou hast killed Uriah\l"
    .string "the Hittite with the sword, and hast\l"
    .string "taken his wife to be thy wife, and\l"
    .string "hast slain him with the sword of the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_10::
    .string "Now therefore the sword shall\n"
    .string "never depart from thine house;\l"
    .string "because thou hast despised me, and\l"
    .string "hast taken the wife of Uriah the\l"
    .string "Hittite to be thy wife.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_11::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will raise up evil against thee\l"
    .string "out of thine own house, and I will\l"
    .string "take thy wives before thine eyes, and\l"
    .string "give them unto thy neighbour, and he\l"
    .string "shall lie with thy wives in the\l"
    .string "sight of this sun.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_12::
    .string "For thou didst it secretly: but I\n"
    .string "will do this thing before all\l"
    .string "Israel, and before the sun.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_13::
    .string "And David said unto Nathan, I have\n"
    .string "sinned against the LORD. And Nathan\l"
    .string "said unto David, The LORD also hath\l"
    .string "put away thy sin; thou shalt not die.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_14::
    .string "Howbeit, because by this deed thou\n"
    .string "hast given great occasion to the\l"
    .string "enemies of the LORD to blaspheme,\l"
    .string "the child also that is born unto\l"
    .string "thee shall surely die.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_15::
    .string "And Nathan departed unto his house.\n"
    .string "And the LORD struck the child that\l"
    .string "Uriah’s wife bare unto David, and it\l"
    .string "was very sick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_16::
    .string "David therefore besought God for\n"
    .string "the child; and David fasted, and\l"
    .string "went in, and lay all night upon the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_17::
    .string "And the elders of his house arose,\n"
    .string "and went to him, to raise him up from\l"
    .string "the earth: but he would not, neither\l"
    .string "did he eat bread with them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_18::
    .string "And it came to pass on the seventh\n"
    .string "day, that the child died. And the\l"
    .string "servants of David feared to tell\l"
    .string "him that the child was dead: for they\l"
    .string "said, Behold, while the child was\l"
    .string "yet alive, we spake unto him, and he\l"
    .string "would not hearken unto our voice:\l"
    .string "how will he then vex himself, if we\l"
    .string "tell him that the child is dead?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_19::
    .string "But when David saw that his servants\n"
    .string "whispered, David perceived that the\l"
    .string "child was dead: therefore David said\l"
    .string "unto his servants, Is the child\l"
    .string "dead? And they said, He is dead$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_20::
    .string "Then David arose from the earth, and\n"
    .string "washed, and anointed himself, and\l"
    .string "changed his apparel, and came into\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "worshipped: then he came to his own\l"
    .string "house; and when he required, they set\l"
    .string "bread before him, and he did eat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_21::
    .string "Then said his servants unto him,\n"
    .string "What thing is this that thou hast\l"
    .string "done? thou didst fast and weep for\l"
    .string "the child, while it was alive; but\l"
    .string "when the child was dead, thou didst\l"
    .string "rise and eat bread.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_22::
    .string "And he said, While the child was\n"
    .string "yet alive, I fasted and wept: for I\l"
    .string "said, Who can tell whether GOD\l"
    .string "will be gracious to me, that the\l"
    .string "child may live?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_23::
    .string "But now he is dead, wherefore\n"
    .string "should I fast? can I bring him back\l"
    .string "again? I shall go to him, but he\l"
    .string "shall not return to me$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_24::
    .string "And David comforted Bathsheba his\n"
    .string "wife, and went in unto her, and lay\l"
    .string "with her: and she bare a son, and he\l"
    .string "called his name Solomon: and the\l"
    .string "LORD loved him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_25::
    .string "And he sent by the hand of Nathan\n"
    .string "the prophet; and he called his\l"
    .string "name Jedidiah, because of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_26::
    .string "And Joab fought against Rabbah of\n"
    .string "the children of Ammon, and took the\l"
    .string "royal city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_27::
    .string "And Joab sent messengers to David,\n"
    .string "and said, I have fought against\l"
    .string "Rabbah, and have taken the city of\l"
    .string "waters.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_28::
    .string "Now therefore gather the rest of the\n"
    .string "people together, and encamp\l"
    .string "against the city, and take it: lest I\l"
    .string "take the city, and it be called\l"
    .string "after my name.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_29::
    .string "And David gathered all the\n"
    .string "people together, and went to\l"
    .string "Rabbah, and fought against it, and\l"
    .string "took it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_30::
    .string "And he took their king’s crown from\n"
    .string "off his head, the weight whereof was\l"
    .string "a talent of gold with the precious\l"
    .string "stones: and it was set on David’s head\l"
    .string " And he brought forth the spoil of\l"
    .string "the city in great abundance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_12_31::
    .string "And he brought forth the people\n"
    .string "that were therein, and put them\l"
    .string "under saws, and under harrows of\l"
    .string "iron, and under axes of iron, and\l"
    .string "made them pass through the\l"
    .string "brick-kiln: and thus did he unto\l"
    .string "all the cities of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon. So David and all the people\l"
    .string "returned unto Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "Absalom the son of David had a fair\l"
    .string "sister, whose name was Tamar; and\l"
    .string "Amnon the son of David loved her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_2::
    .string "And Amnon was so vexed, that he\n"
    .string "fell sick for his sister Tamar; for\l"
    .string "she was a virgin; and Amnon thought\l"
    .string "it hard for him to do anything to her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_3::
    .string "But Amnon had a friend, whose name\n"
    .string "was Jonadab, the son of Shimeah\l"
    .string "David’s brother: and Jonadab was a\l"
    .string "very subtil man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_4::
    .string "And he said unto him, Why art thou,\n"
    .string "being the king’s son, lean from day\l"
    .string "to day? wilt thou not tell me? And\l"
    .string "Amnon said unto him, I love Tamar, my\l"
    .string "brother Absalom’s sister.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_5::
    .string "And Jonadab said unto him, Lay thee\n"
    .string "down on thy bed, and make thyself\l"
    .string "sick: and when thy father cometh to\l"
    .string "see thee, say unto him, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "let my sister Tamar come, and give me\l"
    .string "meat, and dress the meat in my sight,\l"
    .string "that I may see it, and eat it at her\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_6::
    .string "So Amnon lay down, and made himself\n"
    .string "sick: and when the king was come to\l"
    .string "see him, Amnon said unto the king, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, let Tamar my sister come,\l"
    .string "and make me a couple of cakes in my\l"
    .string "sight, that I may eat at her hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_7::
    .string "Then David sent home to Tamar,\n"
    .string "saying, Go now to thy brother Amnon’s\l"
    .string "house, and dress him meat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_8::
    .string "So Tamar went to her brother Amnon’s\n"
    .string "house; and he was laid down. And she\l"
    .string "took flour, and kneaded it, and made\l"
    .string "cakes in his sight, and did bake the\l"
    .string "cakes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_9::
    .string "And she took a pan, and poured them\n"
    .string "out before him; but he refused to\l"
    .string "eat. And Amnon said, Have out all\l"
    .string "men from me. And they went out every\l"
    .string "man from him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_10::
    .string "And Amnon said unto Tamar, Bring the\n"
    .string "meat into the chamber, that I may eat\l"
    .string "of thine hand. And Tamar took the\l"
    .string "cakes which she had made, and brought\l"
    .string "them into the chamber to Amnon her\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_11::
    .string "And when she had brought them unto\n"
    .string "him to eat, he took hold of her, and\l"
    .string "said unto her, Come lie with me, my\l"
    .string "sister.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_12::
    .string "And she answered him, Nay, my\n"
    .string "brother, do not force me; for no such\l"
    .string "thing ought to be done in Israel: do\l"
    .string "not thou this folly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_13::
    .string "And I, whither shall I cause my\n"
    .string "shame to go? and as for thee, thou\l"
    .string "shalt be as one of the fools in\l"
    .string "Israel. Now therefore, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "speak unto the king; for he will\l"
    .string "not withhold me from thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_14::
    .string "Howbeit he would not hearken unto\n"
    .string "her voice: but, being stronger than\l"
    .string "she, forced her, and lay with her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_15::
    .string "Then Amnon hated her exceedingly;\n"
    .string "so that the hatred wherewith he hated\l"
    .string "her was greater than the love\l"
    .string "wherewith he had loved her. And\l"
    .string "Amnon said unto her, Arise, be gone.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_16::
    .string "And she said unto him, There is no\n"
    .string "cause: this evil in sending me away\l"
    .string "is greater than the other that thou\l"
    .string "didst unto me. But he would not\l"
    .string "hearken unto her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_17::
    .string "Then he called his servant that\n"
    .string "ministered unto him, and said, Put\l"
    .string "now this woman out from me, and bolt\l"
    .string "the door after her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_18::
    .string "And she had a garment of divers\n"
    .string "colours upon her: for with such\l"
    .string "robes were the king’s daughters that\l"
    .string "were virgins apparelled. Then his\l"
    .string "servant brought her out, and bolted\l"
    .string "the door after her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_19::
    .string "And Tamar put ashes on her head, and\n"
    .string "rent her garment of divers colours\l"
    .string "that was on her, and laid her hand on\l"
    .string "her head, and went on crying.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_20::
    .string "And Absalom her brother said unto\n"
    .string "her, Hath Amnon thy brother been with\l"
    .string "thee? but hold now thy peace, my\l"
    .string "sister: he is thy brother; regard not\l"
    .string "this thing. So Tamar remained\l"
    .string "desolate in her brother Absalom’s\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_21::
    .string "But when king David heard of all\n"
    .string "these things, he was very wroth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_22::
    .string "And Absalom spake unto his brother\n"
    .string "Amnon neither good nor bad: for\l"
    .string "Absalom hated Amnon, because he had\l"
    .string "forced his sister Tamar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_23::
    .string "And it came to pass after two full\n"
    .string "years, that Absalom had\l"
    .string "sheepshearers in Baalhazor, which\l"
    .string "is beside Ephraim: and Absalom\l"
    .string "invited all the king’s sons.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_24::
    .string "And Absalom came to the king, and\n"
    .string "said, Behold now, thy servant hath\l"
    .string "sheepshearers; let the king, I\l"
    .string "beseech thee, and his servants go\l"
    .string "with thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_25::
    .string "And the king said to Absalom, Nay,\n"
    .string "my son, let us not all now go, lest\l"
    .string "we be chargeable unto thee. And he\l"
    .string "pressed him: howbeit he would not\l"
    .string "go, but blessed him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_26::
    .string "Then said Absalom, If not, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, let my brother Amnon go with us\l"
    .string " And the king said unto him, Why\l"
    .string "should he go with thee?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_27::
    .string "But Absalom pressed him, that he\n"
    .string "let Amnon and all the king’s sons go\l"
    .string "with him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_28::
    .string "Now Absalom had commanded his\n"
    .string "servants, saying, Mark ye now when\l"
    .string "Amnon’s heart is merry with wine, and\l"
    .string "when I say unto you, Smite Amnon;\l"
    .string "then kill him, fear not: have not I\l"
    .string "commanded you? be courageous, and be\l"
    .string "valiant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_29::
    .string "And the servants of Absalom did\n"
    .string "unto Amnon as Absalom had commanded.\l"
    .string "Then all the king’s sons arose, and\l"
    .string "every man gat him up upon his mule,\l"
    .string "and fled.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_30::
    .string "And it came to pass, while they\n"
    .string "were in the way, that tidings came to\l"
    .string "David, saying, Absalom hath slain\l"
    .string "all the king’s sons, and there is\l"
    .string "not one of them left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_31::
    .string "Then the king arose, and tare his\n"
    .string "garments, and lay on the earth; and\l"
    .string "all his servants stood by with\l"
    .string "their clothes rent.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_32::
    .string "And Jonadab, the son of Shimeah\n"
    .string "David’s brother, answered and said,\l"
    .string "Let not my lord suppose that they\l"
    .string "have slain all the young men the\l"
    .string "king’s sons; for Amnon only is dead:\l"
    .string "for by the appointment of Absalom\l"
    .string "this hath been determined from the\l"
    .string "day that he forced his sister Tamar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_33::
    .string "Now therefore let not my lord the\n"
    .string "king take the thing to his heart, to\l"
    .string "think that all the king’s sons are\l"
    .string "dead: for Amnon only is dead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_34::
    .string "But Absalom fled. And the young man\n"
    .string "that kept the watch lifted up his\l"
    .string "eyes, and looked, and, behold, there\l"
    .string "came much people by the way of the\l"
    .string "hill side behind him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_35::
    .string "And Jonadab said unto the king,\n"
    .string "Behold, the king’s sons come: as thy\l"
    .string "servant said, so it is.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_36::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as he\n"
    .string "had made an end of speaking, that,\l"
    .string "behold, the king’s sons came, and\l"
    .string "lifted up their voice and wept: and\l"
    .string "the king also and all his servants\l"
    .string "wept very sore.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_37::
    .string "But Absalom fled, and went to\n"
    .string "Talmai, the son of Ammihud, king of\l"
    .string "Geshur. And David mourned for his son\l"
    .string "every day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_38::
    .string "So Absalom fled, and went to\n"
    .string "Geshur, and was there three years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_13_39::
    .string "And the soul of king David longed\n"
    .string "to go forth unto Absalom: for he was\l"
    .string "comforted concerning Amnon, seeing\l"
    .string "he was dead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_1::
    .string "Now Joab the son of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "perceived that the king’s heart was\l"
    .string "toward Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_2::
    .string "And Joab sent to Tekoah, and fetched\n"
    .string "thence a wise woman, and said unto\l"
    .string "her, I pray thee, feign thyself to\l"
    .string "be a mourner, and put on now mourning\l"
    .string "apparel, and anoint not thyself\l"
    .string "with oil, but be as a woman that had\l"
    .string "a long time mourned for the dead:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_3::
    .string "And come to the king, and speak on\n"
    .string "this manner unto him. So Joab put the\l"
    .string "words in her mouth$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_4::
    .string "And when the woman of Tekoah spake\n"
    .string "to the king, she fell on her face to\l"
    .string "the ground, and did obeisance, and\l"
    .string "said, Help, O king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_5::
    .string "And the king said unto her, What\n"
    .string "aileth thee? And she answered, I am\l"
    .string "indeed a widow woman, and mine\l"
    .string "husband is dead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_6::
    .string "And thy handmaid had two sons, and\n"
    .string "they two strove together in the\l"
    .string "field, and there was none to part\l"
    .string "them, but the one smote the other,\l"
    .string "and slew him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_7::
    .string "And, behold, the whole family is\n"
    .string "risen against thine handmaid, and\l"
    .string "they said, Deliver him that smote\l"
    .string "his brother, that we may kill him,\l"
    .string "for the life of his brother whom he\l"
    .string "slew; and we will destroy the heir\l"
    .string "also: and so they shall quench my\l"
    .string "coal which is left, and shall not\l"
    .string "leave to my husband neither name nor\l"
    .string "remainder upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_8::
    .string "And the king said unto the woman, Go\n"
    .string "to thine house, and I will give\l"
    .string "charge concerning thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_9::
    .string "And the woman of Tekoah said unto\n"
    .string "the king, My lord, O king, the\l"
    .string "iniquity be on me, and on my father’s\l"
    .string "house: and the king and his throne be\l"
    .string "guiltless.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_10::
    .string "And the king said, Whoever saith\n"
    .string "ought unto thee, bring him to me, and\l"
    .string "he shall not touch thee any more.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_11::
    .string "Then said she, I pray thee, let the\n"
    .string "king remember the LORD thy God, that\l"
    .string "thou wouldest not suffer the\l"
    .string "revengers of blood to destroy any\l"
    .string "more, lest they destroy my son. And\l"
    .string "he said, As the LORD liveth, there\l"
    .string "shall not one hair of thy son fall\l"
    .string "to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_12::
    .string "Then the woman said, Let thine\n"
    .string "handmaid, I pray thee, speak one\l"
    .string "word unto my lord the king. And he\l"
    .string "said, Say on.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_13::
    .string "And the woman said, Wherefore then\n"
    .string "hast thou thought such a thing\l"
    .string "against the people of God? for the\l"
    .string "king doth speak this thing as one\l"
    .string "which is faulty, in that the king\l"
    .string "doth not fetch home again his\l"
    .string "banished.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_14::
    .string "For we must needs die, and are as\n"
    .string "water spilt on the ground, which\l"
    .string "cannot be gathered up again; neither\l"
    .string "doth God respect any person: yet\l"
    .string "doth he devise means, that his\l"
    .string "banished be not expelled from him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_15::
    .string "Now therefore that I am come to\n"
    .string "speak of this thing unto my lord the\l"
    .string "king, it is because the people have\l"
    .string "made me afraid: and thy handmaid\l"
    .string "said, I will now speak unto the\l"
    .string "king; it may be that the king will\l"
    .string "perform the request of his handmaid.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_16::
    .string "For the king will hear, to deliver\n"
    .string "his handmaid out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "man that would destroy me and my son\l"
    .string "together out of the inheritance of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_17::
    .string "Then thine handmaid said, The word\n"
    .string "of my lord the king shall now be\l"
    .string "comfortable: for as an angel of God,\l"
    .string "so is my lord the king to discern\l"
    .string "good and bad: therefore the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God will be with thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_18::
    .string "Then the king answered and said unto\n"
    .string "the woman, Hide not from me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, the thing that I shall ask thee\l"
    .string " And the woman said, Let my lord the\l"
    .string "king now speak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_19::
    .string "And the king said, Is not the hand of\n"
    .string "Joab with thee in all this? And the\l"
    .string "woman answered and said, As thy soul\l"
    .string "liveth, my lord the king, none can\l"
    .string "turn to the right hand or to the left\l"
    .string "from ought that my lord the king\l"
    .string "hath spoken: for thy servant Joab,\l"
    .string "he bade me, and he put all these\l"
    .string "words in the mouth of thine handmaid:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_20::
    .string "To fetch about this form of speech\n"
    .string "hath thy servant Joab done this\l"
    .string "thing: and my lord is wise,\l"
    .string "according to the wisdom of an angel\l"
    .string "of God, to know all things that are\l"
    .string "in the earth$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_21::
    .string "And the king said unto Joab, Behold\n"
    .string "now, I have done this thing: go\l"
    .string "therefore, bring the young man\l"
    .string "Absalom again.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_22::
    .string "And Joab fell to the ground on his\n"
    .string "face, and bowed himself, and thanked\l"
    .string "the king: and Joab said, To day thy\l"
    .string "servant knoweth that I have found\l"
    .string "grace in thy sight, my lord, O king,\l"
    .string "in that the king hath fulfilled the\l"
    .string "request of his servant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_23::
    .string "So Joab arose and went to Geshur,\n"
    .string "and brought Absalom to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_24::
    .string "And the king said, Let him turn to\n"
    .string "his own house, and let him not see my\l"
    .string "face. So Absalom returned to his own\l"
    .string "house, and saw not the king’s face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_25::
    .string "But in all Israel there was none\n"
    .string "to be so much praised as Absalom for\l"
    .string "his beauty: from the sole of his foot\l"
    .string "even to the crown of his head there\l"
    .string "was no blemish in him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_26::
    .string "And when he polled his head, (for\n"
    .string "it was at every year’s end that he\l"
    .string "polled it: because the hair was\l"
    .string "heavy on him, therefore he polled\l"
    .string "it:) he weighed the hair of his head\l"
    .string "at two hundred shekels after the\l"
    .string "king’s weight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_27::
    .string "And unto Absalom there were born\n"
    .string "three sons, and one daughter, whose\l"
    .string "name was Tamar: she was a woman of a\l"
    .string "fair countenance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_28::
    .string "So Absalom dwelt two full years\n"
    .string "in Jerusalem, and saw not the king’s\l"
    .string "face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_29::
    .string "Therefore Absalom sent for Joab, to\n"
    .string "have sent him to the king; but he\l"
    .string "would not come to him: and when he\l"
    .string "sent again the second time, he would\l"
    .string "not come.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_30::
    .string "Therefore he said unto his servants,\n"
    .string "See, Joab’s field is near mine, and\l"
    .string "he hath barley there; go and set it\l"
    .string "on fire. And Absalom’s servants set\l"
    .string "the field on fire.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_31::
    .string "Then Joab arose, and came to\n"
    .string "Absalom unto his house, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Wherefore have thy servants\l"
    .string "set my field on fire?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_32::
    .string "And Absalom answered Joab, Behold,\n"
    .string "I sent unto thee, saying, Come\l"
    .string "hither, that I may send thee to the\l"
    .string "king, to say, Wherefore am I come\l"
    .string "from Geshur? it had been good for me\l"
    .string "to have been there still: now\l"
    .string "therefore let me see the king’s\l"
    .string "face; and if there be any iniquity in\l"
    .string "me, let him kill me$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_14_33::
    .string "So Joab came to the king, and told\n"
    .string "him: and when he had called for\l"
    .string "Absalom, he came to the king, and\l"
    .string "bowed himself on his face to the\l"
    .string "ground before the king: and the king\l"
    .string "kissed Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "Absalom prepared him chariots and\l"
    .string "horses, and fifty men to run before\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_2::
    .string "And Absalom rose up early, and\n"
    .string "stood beside the way of the gate: and\l"
    .string "it was so, that when any man that had\l"
    .string "a controversy came to the king for\l"
    .string "judgment, then Absalom called unto\l"
    .string "him, and said, Of what city art thou?\l"
    .string "And he said, Thy servant is of one of\l"
    .string "the tribes of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_3::
    .string "And Absalom said unto him, See, thy\n"
    .string "matters are good and right; but there\l"
    .string "is no man deputed of the king to hear\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_4::
    .string "Absalom said moreover, Oh that I\n"
    .string "were made judge in the land, that\l"
    .string "every man which hath any suit or\l"
    .string "cause might come unto me, and I would\l"
    .string "do him justice!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_5::
    .string "And it was so, that when any man came\n"
    .string "nigh to him to do him obeisance, he\l"
    .string "put forth his hand, and took him, and\l"
    .string "kissed him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_6::
    .string "And on this manner did Absalom to\n"
    .string "all Israel that came to the king\l"
    .string "for judgment: so Absalom stole the\l"
    .string "hearts of the men of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_7::
    .string "And it came to pass after forty\n"
    .string "years, that Absalom said unto the\l"
    .string "king, I pray thee, let me go and pay\l"
    .string "my vow, which I have vowed unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, in Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_8::
    .string "For thy servant vowed a vow while I\n"
    .string "abode at Geshur in Syria, saying, If\l"
    .string "the LORD shall bring me again\l"
    .string "indeed to Jerusalem, then I will\l"
    .string "serve the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_9::
    .string "And the king said unto him, Go in\n"
    .string "peace. So he arose, and went to\l"
    .string "Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_10::
    .string "But Absalom sent spies throughout\n"
    .string "all the tribes of Israel, saying,\l"
    .string "As soon as ye hear the sound of the\l"
    .string "trumpet, then ye shall say,\l"
    .string "Absalom reigneth in Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_11::
    .string "And with Absalom went two hundred\n"
    .string "men out of Jerusalem, that were\l"
    .string "called; and they went in their\l"
    .string "simplicity, and they knew not any\l"
    .string "thing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_12::
    .string "And Absalom sent for Ahithophel\n"
    .string "the Gilonite, David’s counsellor,\l"
    .string "from his city, even from Giloh,\l"
    .string "while he offered sacrifices. And the\l"
    .string "conspiracy was strong; for the\l"
    .string "people increased continually with\l"
    .string "Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_13::
    .string "And there came a messenger to David,\n"
    .string "saying, The hearts of the men of\l"
    .string "Israel are after Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_14::
    .string "And David said unto all his\n"
    .string "servants that were with him at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, Arise, and let us flee;\l"
    .string "for we shall not else escape from\l"
    .string "Absalom: make speed to depart,\l"
    .string "lest he overtake us suddenly, and\l"
    .string "bring evil upon us, and smite the\l"
    .string "city with the edge of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_15::
    .string "And the king’s servants said unto\n"
    .string "the king, Behold, thy servants are\l"
    .string "ready to do whatsoever my lord the\l"
    .string "king shall appoint.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_16::
    .string "And the king went forth, and all\n"
    .string "his household after him. And the\l"
    .string "king left ten women, which were\l"
    .string "concubines, to keep the house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_17::
    .string "And the king went forth, and all\n"
    .string "the people after him, and tarried\l"
    .string "in a place that was far off.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_18::
    .string "And all his servants passed on\n"
    .string "beside him; and all the\l"
    .string "Cherethites, and all the\l"
    .string "Pelethites, and all the Gittites,\l"
    .string "six hundred men which came after him\l"
    .string "from Gath, passed on before the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_19::
    .string "Then said the king to Ittai the\n"
    .string "Gittite, Wherefore goest thou also\l"
    .string "with us? return to thy place, and\l"
    .string "abide with the king: for thou art a\l"
    .string "stranger, and also an exile.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_20::
    .string "Whereas thou camest but yesterday,\n"
    .string "should I this day make thee go up\l"
    .string "and down with us? seeing I go whither\l"
    .string "I may, return thou, and take back thy\l"
    .string "brethren: mercy and truth be with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_21::
    .string "And Ittai answered the king, and\n"
    .string "said, As the LORD liveth, and as my\l"
    .string "lord the king liveth, surely in what\l"
    .string "place my lord the king shall be,\l"
    .string "whether in death or life, even there\l"
    .string "also will thy servant be.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_22::
    .string "And David said to Ittai, Go and pass\n"
    .string "over. And Ittai the Gittite passed\l"
    .string "over, and all his men, and all the\l"
    .string "little ones that were with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_23::
    .string "And all the country wept with a\n"
    .string "loud voice, and all the people\l"
    .string "passed over: the king also himself\l"
    .string "passed over the brook Kidron, and\l"
    .string "all the people passed over,\l"
    .string "toward the way of the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_24::
    .string "And lo Zadok also, and all the\n"
    .string "Levites were with him, bearing the\l"
    .string "ark of the covenant of God: and they\l"
    .string "set down the ark of God; and Abiathar\l"
    .string "went up, until all the people\l"
    .string "had done passing out of the city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_25::
    .string "And the king said unto Zadok, Carry\n"
    .string "back the ark of God into the city: if\l"
    .string "I shall find favour in the eyes of\l"
    .string "the LORD, he will bring me again,\l"
    .string "and shew me both it, and his\l"
    .string "habitation:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_26::
    .string "But if he thus say, I have no\n"
    .string "delight in thee; behold, here am I,\l"
    .string "let him do to me as seemeth good unto\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_27::
    .string "The king said also unto Zadok the\n"
    .string "priest, Art not thou a seer? return\l"
    .string "into the city in peace, and your two\l"
    .string "sons with you, Ahimaaz thy son, and\l"
    .string "Jonathan the son of Abiathar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_28::
    .string "See, I will tarry in the plain of\n"
    .string "the wilderness, until there come\l"
    .string "word from you to certify me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_29::
    .string "Zadok therefore and Abiathar\n"
    .string "carried the ark of God again to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: and they tarried there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_30::
    .string "And David went up by the ascent of\n"
    .string "mount Olivet, and wept as he went\l"
    .string "up, and had his head covered, and he\l"
    .string "went barefoot: and all the people\l"
    .string "that was with him covered every man\l"
    .string "his head, and they went up, weeping\l"
    .string "as they went up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_31::
    .string "And one told David, saying,\n"
    .string "Ahithophel is among the\l"
    .string "conspirators with Absalom. And\l"
    .string "David said, O LORD, I pray thee, turn\l"
    .string "the counsel of Ahithophel into\l"
    .string "foolishness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_32::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when David\n"
    .string "was come to the top of the mount,\l"
    .string "where he worshipped God, behold,\l"
    .string "Hushai the Archite came to meet him\l"
    .string "with his coat rent, and earth upon\l"
    .string "his head:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_33::
    .string "Unto whom David said, If thou\n"
    .string "passest on with me, then thou shalt\l"
    .string "be a burden unto me:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_34::
    .string "But if thou return to the city, and\n"
    .string "say unto Absalom, I will be thy\l"
    .string "servant, O king; as I have been thy\l"
    .string "father’s servant hitherto, so will\l"
    .string "I now also be thy servant: then\l"
    .string "mayest thou for me defeat the\l"
    .string "counsel of Ahithophel$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_35::
    .string "And hast thou not there with thee\n"
    .string "Zadok and Abiathar the priests?\l"
    .string "therefore it shall be, that what\l"
    .string "thing soever thou shalt hear out of\l"
    .string "the king’s house, thou shalt tell\l"
    .string "it to Zadok and Abiathar the priests.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_36::
    .string "Behold, they have there with them\n"
    .string "their two sons, Ahimaaz Zadok’s son,\l"
    .string "and Jonathan Abiathar’s son; and by\l"
    .string "them ye shall send unto me every\l"
    .string "thing that ye can hear.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_15_37::
    .string "So Hushai David’s friend came into\n"
    .string "the city, and Absalom came into\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_1::
    .string "And when David was a little past\n"
    .string "the top of the hill, behold, Ziba\l"
    .string "the servant of Mephibosheth met him,\l"
    .string "with a couple of asses saddled, and\l"
    .string "upon them two hundred loaves of\l"
    .string "bread, and an hundred bunches of\l"
    .string "raisins, and an hundred of summer\l"
    .string "fruits, and a bottle of wine.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_2::
    .string "And the king said unto Ziba, What\n"
    .string "meanest thou by these? And Ziba said,\l"
    .string "The asses be for the king’s\l"
    .string "household to ride on; and the bread\l"
    .string "and summer fruit for the young men to\l"
    .string "eat; and the wine, that such as be\l"
    .string "faint in the wilderness may drink.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_3::
    .string "And the king said, And where is thy\n"
    .string "master’s son? And Ziba said unto the\l"
    .string "king, Behold, he abideth at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: for he said, To day\l"
    .string "shall the house of Israel restore\l"
    .string "me the kingdom of my father.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_4::
    .string "Then said the king to Ziba, Behold,\n"
    .string "thine are all that pertained unto\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth. And Ziba said, I\l"
    .string "humbly beseech thee that I may find\l"
    .string "grace in thy sight, my lord, O king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_5::
    .string "And when king David came to Bahurim,\n"
    .string "behold, thence came out a man of the\l"
    .string "family of the house of Saul, whose\l"
    .string "name was Shimei, the son of Gera: he\l"
    .string "came forth, and cursed still as he\l"
    .string "came.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_6::
    .string "And he cast stones at David, and at\n"
    .string "all the servants of king David: and\l"
    .string "all the people and all the\l"
    .string "mighty men were on his right hand and\l"
    .string "on his left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_7::
    .string "And thus said Shimei when he cursed,\n"
    .string "Come out, come out, thou bloody man,\l"
    .string "and thou man of Belial:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_8::
    .string "The LORD hath returned upon thee\n"
    .string "all the blood of the house of Saul,\l"
    .string "in whose stead thou hast reigned; and\l"
    .string "the LORD hath delivered the kingdom\l"
    .string "into the hand of Absalom thy son:\l"
    .string "and, behold, thou art taken in thy\l"
    .string "mischief, because thou art a bloody\l"
    .string "man$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_9::
    .string "Then said Abishai the son of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "unto the king, Why should this dead\l"
    .string "dog curse my lord the king? let me\l"
    .string "go over, I pray thee, and take off\l"
    .string "his head.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_10::
    .string "And the king said, What have I to do\n"
    .string "with you, ye sons of Zeruiah? so let\l"
    .string "him curse, because the LORD hath said\l"
    .string "unto him, Curse David. Who shall\l"
    .string "then say, Wherefore hast thou done\l"
    .string "so?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_11::
    .string "And David said to Abishai, and to\n"
    .string "all his servants, Behold, my son,\l"
    .string "which came forth of my bowels,\l"
    .string "seeketh my life: how much more now\l"
    .string "may this Benjamite do it? let him\l"
    .string "alone, and let him curse; for the\l"
    .string "LORD hath bidden him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_12::
    .string "It may be that the LORD will look\n"
    .string "on mine affliction, and that the\l"
    .string "LORD will requite me good for his\l"
    .string "cursing this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_13::
    .string "And as David and his men went by the\n"
    .string "way, Shimei went along on the\l"
    .string "hill’s side over against him, and\l"
    .string "cursed as he went, and threw stones\l"
    .string "at him, and cast dust.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_14::
    .string "And the king, and all the people\n"
    .string "that were with him, came weary, and\l"
    .string "refreshed themselves there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_15::
    .string "And Absalom, and all the people\n"
    .string "the men of Israel, came to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and Ahithophel with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Hushai the\n"
    .string "Archite, David’s friend, was come\l"
    .string "unto Absalom, that Hushai said unto\l"
    .string "Absalom, God save the king, God save\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_17::
    .string "And Absalom said to Hushai, Is this\n"
    .string "thy kindness to thy friend? why\l"
    .string "wentest thou not with thy friend?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_18::
    .string "And Hushai said unto Absalom, Nay;\n"
    .string "but whom the LORD, and this people,\l"
    .string "and all the men of Israel, choose,\l"
    .string "his will I be, and with him will I\l"
    .string "abide$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_19::
    .string "And again, whom should I serve?\n"
    .string "should I not serve in the presence\l"
    .string "of his son? as I have served in thy\l"
    .string "father’s presence, so will I be in\l"
    .string "thy presence.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_20::
    .string "Then said Absalom to Ahithophel,\n"
    .string "Give counsel among you what we\l"
    .string "shall do.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_21::
    .string "And Ahithophel said unto Absalom,\n"
    .string "Go in unto thy father’s concubines,\l"
    .string "which he hath left to keep the\l"
    .string "house; and all Israel shall hear\l"
    .string "that thou art abhorred of thy father:\l"
    .string "then shall the hands of all that\l"
    .string "are with thee be strong.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_22::
    .string "So they spread Absalom a tent upon\n"
    .string "the top of the house; and Absalom\l"
    .string "went in unto his father’s concubines\l"
    .string "in the sight of all Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_16_23::
    .string "And the counsel of Ahithophel,\n"
    .string "which he counselled in those days,\l"
    .string "was as if a man had enquired at the\l"
    .string "oracle of God: so was all the\l"
    .string "counsel of Ahithophel both with\l"
    .string "David and with Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_1::
    .string "Moreover Ahithophel said unto\n"
    .string "Absalom, Let me now choose out\l"
    .string "twelve thousand men, and I will\l"
    .string "arise and pursue after David this\l"
    .string "night:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_2::
    .string "And I will come upon him while he\n"
    .string "is weary and weak handed, and will\l"
    .string "make him afraid: and all the\l"
    .string "people that are with him shall\l"
    .string "flee; and I will smite the king\l"
    .string "only:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_3::
    .string "And I will bring back all the\n"
    .string "people unto thee: the man whom thou\l"
    .string "seekest is as if all returned: so\l"
    .string "all the people shall be in peace$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_4::
    .string "And the saying pleased Absalom\n"
    .string "well, and all the elders of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_5::
    .string "Then said Absalom, Call now Hushai\n"
    .string "the Archite also, and let us hear\l"
    .string "likewise what he saith.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_6::
    .string "And when Hushai was come to\n"
    .string "Absalom, Absalom spake unto him,\l"
    .string "saying, Ahithophel hath spoken\l"
    .string "after this manner: shall we do after\l"
    .string "his saying? if not; speak thou.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_7::
    .string "And Hushai said unto Absalom, The\n"
    .string "counsel that Ahithophel hath given\l"
    .string "is not good at this time.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_8::
    .string "For, said Hushai, thou knowest thy\n"
    .string "father and his men, that they be\l"
    .string "mighty men, and they be chafed in\l"
    .string "their minds, as a bear robbed of her\l"
    .string "whelps in the field: and thy father\l"
    .string "is a man of war, and will not lodge\l"
    .string "with the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_9::
    .string "Behold, he is hid now in some pit,\n"
    .string "or in some other place: and it will\l"
    .string "come to pass, when some of them be\l"
    .string "overthrown at the first, that\l"
    .string "whosoever heareth it will say,\l"
    .string "There is a slaughter among the\l"
    .string "people that follow Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_10::
    .string "And he also that is valiant, whose\n"
    .string "heart is as the heart of a lion,\l"
    .string "shall utterly melt: for all\l"
    .string "Israel knoweth that thy father is a\l"
    .string "mighty man, and they which be with\l"
    .string "him are valiant men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_11::
    .string "Therefore I counsel that all\n"
    .string "Israel be generally gathered unto\l"
    .string "thee, from Dan even to Beersheba, as\l"
    .string "the sand that is by the sea for\l"
    .string "multitude; and that thou go to\l"
    .string "battle in thine own person.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_12::
    .string "So shall we come upon him in some\n"
    .string "place where he shall be found, and\l"
    .string "we will light upon him as the dew\l"
    .string "falleth on the ground: and of him\l"
    .string "and of all the men that are with him\l"
    .string "there shall not be left so much as\l"
    .string "one.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_13::
    .string "Moreover, if he be gotten into a\n"
    .string "city, then shall all Israel bring\l"
    .string "ropes to that city, and we will\l"
    .string "draw it into the river, until there\l"
    .string "be not one small stone found there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_14::
    .string "And Absalom and all the men of\n"
    .string "Israel said, The counsel of Hushai\l"
    .string "the Archite is better than the\l"
    .string "counsel of Ahithophel. For the LORD\l"
    .string "had appointed to defeat the good\l"
    .string "counsel of Ahithophel, to the\l"
    .string "intent that the LORD might bring\l"
    .string "evil upon Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_15::
    .string "Then said Hushai unto Zadok and to\n"
    .string "Abiathar the priests, Thus and thus\l"
    .string "did Ahithophel counsel Absalom\l"
    .string "and the elders of Israel; and thus\l"
    .string "and thus have I counselled.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_16::
    .string "Now therefore send quickly, and\n"
    .string "tell David, saying, Lodge not this\l"
    .string "night in the plains of the\l"
    .string "wilderness, but speedily pass\l"
    .string "over; lest the king be swallowed\l"
    .string "up, and all the people that are\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_17::
    .string "Now Jonathan and Ahimaaz stayed by\n"
    .string "Enrogel; for they might not be seen\l"
    .string "to come into the city: and a wench\l"
    .string "went and told them; and they went and\l"
    .string "told king David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_18::
    .string "Nevertheless a lad saw them, and\n"
    .string "told Absalom: but they went both of\l"
    .string "them away quickly, and came to a\l"
    .string "man’s house in Bahurim, which had a\l"
    .string "well in his court; whither they went\l"
    .string "down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_19::
    .string "And the woman took and spread a\n"
    .string "covering over the well’s mouth, and\l"
    .string "spread ground corn thereon; and the\l"
    .string "thing was not known.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_20::
    .string "And when Absalom’s servants came to\n"
    .string "the woman to the house, they said,\l"
    .string "Where is Ahimaaz and Jonathan? And\l"
    .string "the woman said unto them, They be\l"
    .string "gone over the brook of water. And\l"
    .string "when they had sought and could not\l"
    .string "find them, they returned to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_21::
    .string "And it came to pass, after they were\n"
    .string "departed, that they came up out of\l"
    .string "the well, and went and told king\l"
    .string "David, and said unto David, Arise,\l"
    .string "and pass quickly over the water: for\l"
    .string "thus hath Ahithophel counselled\l"
    .string "against you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_22::
    .string "Then David arose, and all the\n"
    .string "people that were with him, and they\l"
    .string "passed over Jordan: by the morning\l"
    .string "light there lacked not one of them\l"
    .string "that was not gone over Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_23::
    .string "And when Ahithophel saw that his\n"
    .string "counsel was not followed, he\l"
    .string "saddled his ass, and arose, and gat\l"
    .string "him home to his house, to his city,\l"
    .string "and put his household in order, and\l"
    .string "hanged himself, and died, and was\l"
    .string "buried in the sepulchre of his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_24::
    .string "Then David came to Mahanaim. And\n"
    .string "Absalom passed over Jordan, he and\l"
    .string "all the men of Israel with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_25::
    .string "And Absalom made Amasa captain of\n"
    .string "the host instead of Joab: which Amasa\l"
    .string "was a man’s son, whose name was Ithra\l"
    .string "an Israelite, that went in to\l"
    .string "Abigail the daughter of Nahash,\l"
    .string "sister to Zeruiah Joab’s mother.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_26::
    .string "So Israel and Absalom pitched in\n"
    .string "the land of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_27::
    .string "And it came to pass, when David was\n"
    .string "come to Mahanaim, that Shobi the son\l"
    .string "of Nahash of Rabbah of the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon, and Machir the son of\l"
    .string "Ammiel of Lodebar, and Barzillai\l"
    .string "the Gileadite of Rogelim,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_28::
    .string "Brought beds, and basons, and\n"
    .string "earthen vessels, and wheat, and\l"
    .string "barley, and flour, and parched\l"
    .string "corn, and beans, and lentiles, and\l"
    .string "parched pulse,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_17_29::
    .string "And honey, and butter, and sheep,\n"
    .string "and cheese of kine, for David, and\l"
    .string "for the people that were with him,\l"
    .string "to eat: for they said, The people\l"
    .string "is hungry, and weary, and thirsty, in\l"
    .string "the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_1::
    .string "And David numbered the people\n"
    .string "that were with him, and set captains\l"
    .string "of thousands, and captains of\l"
    .string "hundreds over them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_2::
    .string "And David sent forth a third part\n"
    .string "of the people under the hand of\l"
    .string "Joab, and a third part under the hand\l"
    .string "of Abishai the son of Zeruiah, Joab’s\l"
    .string "brother, and a third part under the\l"
    .string "hand of Ittai the Gittite. And the\l"
    .string "king said unto the people, I will\l"
    .string "surely go forth with you myself\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_3::
    .string "But the people answered, Thou\n"
    .string "shalt not go forth: for if we flee\l"
    .string "away, they will not care for us;\l"
    .string "neither if half of us die, will\l"
    .string "they care for us: but now thou art\l"
    .string "worth ten thousand of us: therefore\l"
    .string "now it is better that thou succour us\l"
    .string "out of the city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_4::
    .string "And the king said unto them, What\n"
    .string "seemeth you best I will do. And the\l"
    .string "king stood by the gate side, and all\l"
    .string "the people came out by hundreds and\l"
    .string "by thousands.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_5::
    .string "And the king commanded Joab and\n"
    .string "Abishai and Ittai, saying, Deal\l"
    .string "gently for my sake with the young\l"
    .string "man, even with Absalom. And all the\l"
    .string "people heard when the king gave\l"
    .string "all the captains charge concerning\l"
    .string "Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_6::
    .string "So the people went out into the\n"
    .string "field against Israel: and the\l"
    .string "battle was in the wood of Ephraim;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_7::
    .string "Where the people of Israel were\n"
    .string "slain before the servants of David,\l"
    .string "and there was there a great\l"
    .string "slaughter that day of twenty\l"
    .string "thousand men$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_8::
    .string "For the battle was there scattered\n"
    .string "over the face of all the country:\l"
    .string "and the wood devoured more people\l"
    .string "that day than the sword devoured.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_9::
    .string "And Absalom met the servants of\n"
    .string "David. And Absalom rode upon a\l"
    .string "mule, and the mule went under the\l"
    .string "thick boughs of a great oak, and his\l"
    .string "head caught hold of the oak, and he\l"
    .string "was taken up between the heaven and\l"
    .string "the earth; and the mule that was\l"
    .string "under him went away.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_10::
    .string "And a certain man saw it, and told\n"
    .string "Joab, and said, Behold, I saw\l"
    .string "Absalom hanged in an oak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_11::
    .string "And Joab said unto the man that\n"
    .string "told him, And, behold, thou sawest\l"
    .string "him, and why didst thou not smite him\l"
    .string "there to the ground? and I would have\l"
    .string "given thee ten shekels of silver,\l"
    .string "and a girdle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_12::
    .string "And the man said unto Joab, Though I\n"
    .string "should receive a thousand shekels\l"
    .string "of silver in mine hand, yet would I\l"
    .string "not put forth mine hand against the\l"
    .string "king’s son: for in our hearing the\l"
    .string "king charged thee and Abishai and\l"
    .string "Ittai, saying, Beware that none touch\l"
    .string "the young man Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_13::
    .string "Otherwise I should have wrought\n"
    .string "falsehood against mine own life:\l"
    .string "for there is no matter hid from the\l"
    .string "king, and thou thyself wouldest\l"
    .string "have set thyself against me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_14::
    .string "Then said Joab, I may not tarry thus\n"
    .string "with thee. And he took three darts in\l"
    .string "his hand, and thrust them through the\l"
    .string "heart of Absalom, while he was yet\l"
    .string "alive in the midst of the oak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_15::
    .string "And ten young men that bare Joab’s\n"
    .string "armour compassed about and smote\l"
    .string "Absalom, and slew him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_16::
    .string "And Joab blew the trumpet, and the\n"
    .string "people returned from pursuing\l"
    .string "after Israel: for Joab held back the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_17::
    .string "And they took Absalom, and cast him\n"
    .string "into a great pit in the wood, and\l"
    .string "laid a very great heap of stones\l"
    .string "upon him: and all Israel fled\l"
    .string "every one to his tent.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_18::
    .string "Now Absalom in his lifetime had\n"
    .string "taken and reared up for himself a\l"
    .string "pillar, which is in the king’s\l"
    .string "dale: for he said, I have no son to\l"
    .string "keep my name in remembrance: and he\l"
    .string "called the pillar after his own\l"
    .string "name: and it is called unto this\l"
    .string "day, Absalom’s place.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_19::
    .string "Then said Ahimaaz the son of Zadok,\n"
    .string "Let me now run, and bear the king\l"
    .string "tidings, how that the LORD hath\l"
    .string "avenged him of his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_20::
    .string "And Joab said unto him, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "not bear tidings this day, but thou\l"
    .string "shalt bear tidings another day: but\l"
    .string "this day thou shalt bear no tidings,\l"
    .string "because the king’s son is dead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_21::
    .string "Then said Joab to Cushi, Go tell\n"
    .string "the king what thou hast seen. And\l"
    .string "Cushi bowed himself unto Joab, and\l"
    .string "ran.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_22::
    .string "Then said Ahimaaz the son of Zadok\n"
    .string "yet again to Joab, But howsoever,\l"
    .string "let me, I pray thee, also run after\l"
    .string "Cushi. And Joab said, Wherefore wilt\l"
    .string "thou run, my son, seeing that thou\l"
    .string "hast no tidings ready?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_23::
    .string "But howsoever, said he, let me run.\n"
    .string "And he said unto him, Run. Then\l"
    .string "Ahimaaz ran by the way of the plain,\l"
    .string "and overran Cushi$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_24::
    .string "And David sat between the two gates:\n"
    .string "and the watchman went up to the roof\l"
    .string "over the gate unto the wall, and\l"
    .string "lifted up his eyes, and looked, and\l"
    .string "behold a man running alone.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_25::
    .string "And the watchman cried, and told\n"
    .string "the king. And the king said, If he be\l"
    .string "alone, there is tidings in his\l"
    .string "mouth. And he came apace, and drew\l"
    .string "near.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_26::
    .string "And the watchman saw another man\n"
    .string "running: and the watchman called\l"
    .string "unto the porter, and said, Behold\l"
    .string "another man running alone. And the\l"
    .string "king said, He also bringeth tidings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_27::
    .string "And the watchman said, Me thinketh\n"
    .string "the running of the foremost is like\l"
    .string "the running of Ahimaaz the son of\l"
    .string "Zadok. And the king said, He is a good\l"
    .string "man, and cometh with good tidings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_28::
    .string "And Ahimaaz called, and said unto\n"
    .string "the king, All is well. And he\l"
    .string "fell down to the earth upon his\l"
    .string "face before the king, and said,\l"
    .string "Blessed be the LORD thy God, which\l"
    .string "hath delivered up the men that\l"
    .string "lifted up their hand against my\l"
    .string "lord the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_29::
    .string "And the king said, Is the young man\n"
    .string "Absalom safe? And Ahimaaz answered,\l"
    .string "When Joab sent the king’s servant,\l"
    .string "and me thy servant, I saw a great\l"
    .string "tumult, but I knew not what it was.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_30::
    .string "And the king said unto him, Turn\n"
    .string "aside, and stand here. And he turned\l"
    .string "aside, and stood still.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_31::
    .string "And, behold, Cushi came; and Cushi\n"
    .string "said, Tidings, my lord the king: for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath avenged thee this day\l"
    .string "of all them that rose up against\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_32::
    .string "And the king said unto Cushi, Is the\n"
    .string "young man Absalom safe? And Cushi\l"
    .string "answered, The enemies of my lord the\l"
    .string "king, and all that rise against thee\l"
    .string "to do thee hurt, be as that young man\l"
    .string "is.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_18_33::
    .string "And the king was much moved, and\n"
    .string "went up to the chamber over the gate,\l"
    .string "and wept: and as he went, thus he\l"
    .string "said, O my son Absalom, my son, my\l"
    .string "son Absalom! would God I had died\l"
    .string "for thee, O Absalom, my son, my son!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_1::
    .string "And it was told Joab, Behold, the\n"
    .string "king weepeth and mourneth for\l"
    .string "Absalom$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_2::
    .string "And the victory that day was turned\n"
    .string "into mourning unto all the\l"
    .string "people: for the people heard say\l"
    .string "that day how the king was grieved for\l"
    .string "his son.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_3::
    .string "And the people gat them by\n"
    .string "stealth that day into the city, as\l"
    .string "people being ashamed steal away\l"
    .string "when they flee in battle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_4::
    .string "But the king covered his face, and\n"
    .string "the king cried with a loud voice, O\l"
    .string "my son Absalom, O Absalom, my son,\l"
    .string "my son!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_5::
    .string "And Joab came into the house to the\n"
    .string "king, and said, Thou hast shamed this\l"
    .string "day the faces of all thy servants,\l"
    .string "which this day have saved thy life,\l"
    .string "and the lives of thy sons and of thy\l"
    .string "daughters, and the lives of thy\l"
    .string "wives, and the lives of thy\l"
    .string "concubines;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_6::
    .string "In that thou lovest thine enemies,\n"
    .string "and hatest thy friends. For thou hast\l"
    .string "declared this day, that thou\l"
    .string "regardest neither princes nor\l"
    .string "servants: for this day I perceive,\l"
    .string "that if Absalom had lived, and all\l"
    .string "we had died this day, then it had\l"
    .string "pleased thee well$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_7::
    .string "Now therefore arise, go forth, and\n"
    .string "speak comfortably unto thy\l"
    .string "servants: for I swear by the LORD, if\l"
    .string "thou go not forth, there will not\l"
    .string "tarry one with thee this night: and\l"
    .string "that will be worse unto thee than\l"
    .string "all the evil that befell thee\l"
    .string "from thy youth until now.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_8::
    .string "Then the king arose, and sat in the\n"
    .string "gate. And they told unto all the\l"
    .string "people, saying, Behold, the king\l"
    .string "doth sit in the gate. And all the\l"
    .string "people came before the king: for\l"
    .string "Israel had fled every man to his\l"
    .string "tent.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_9::
    .string "And all the people were at\n"
    .string "strife throughout all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel, saying, The king saved us\l"
    .string "out of the hand of our enemies, and he\l"
    .string "delivered us out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines; and now he is fled out\l"
    .string "of the land for Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_10::
    .string "And Absalom, whom we anointed over\n"
    .string "us, is dead in battle. Now therefore\l"
    .string "why speak ye not a word of bringing\l"
    .string "the king back?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_11::
    .string "And king David sent to Zadok and to\n"
    .string "Abiathar the priests, saying, Speak\l"
    .string "unto the elders of Judah, saying,\l"
    .string "Why are ye the last to bring the king\l"
    .string "back to his house? seeing the speech\l"
    .string "of all Israel is come to the king,\l"
    .string "even to his house$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_12::
    .string "Ye are my brethren, ye are my bones\n"
    .string "and my flesh: wherefore then are ye\l"
    .string "the last to bring back the king?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_13::
    .string "And say ye to Amasa, Art thou not of\n"
    .string "my bone, and of my flesh? God do so\l"
    .string "to me, and more also, if thou be not\l"
    .string "captain of the host before me\l"
    .string "continually in the room of Joab$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_14::
    .string "And he bowed the heart of all the\n"
    .string "men of Judah, even as the heart of one\l"
    .string "man; so that they sent this word unto\l"
    .string "the king, Return thou, and all thy\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_15::
    .string "So the king returned, and came to\n"
    .string "Jordan. And Judah came to Gilgal, to\l"
    .string "go to meet the king, to conduct the\l"
    .string "king over Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_16::
    .string "And Shimei the son of Gera, a\n"
    .string "Benjamite, which was of Bahurim,\l"
    .string "hasted and came down with the men of\l"
    .string "Judah to meet king David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_17::
    .string "And there were a thousand men of\n"
    .string "Benjamin with him, and Ziba the\l"
    .string "servant of the house of Saul, and his\l"
    .string "fifteen sons and his twenty servants\l"
    .string "with him; and they went over Jordan\l"
    .string "before the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_18::
    .string "And there went over a ferry boat to\n"
    .string "carry over the king’s household, and\l"
    .string "to do what he thought good. And\l"
    .string "Shimei the son of Gera fell down\l"
    .string "before the king, as he was come over\l"
    .string "Jordan;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_19::
    .string "And said unto the king, Let not my\n"
    .string "lord impute iniquity unto me,\l"
    .string "neither do thou remember that which\l"
    .string "thy servant did perversely the day\l"
    .string "that my lord the king went out of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, that the king should\l"
    .string "take it to his heart$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_20::
    .string "For thy servant doth know that I\n"
    .string "have sinned: therefore, behold, I am\l"
    .string "come the first this day of all the\l"
    .string "house of Joseph to go down to meet my\l"
    .string "lord the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_21::
    .string "But Abishai the son of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "answered and said, Shall not Shimei\l"
    .string "be put to death for this, because he\l"
    .string "cursed the LORD’s anointed?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_22::
    .string "And David said, What have I to do\n"
    .string "with you, ye sons of Zeruiah, that ye\l"
    .string "should this day be adversaries unto\l"
    .string "me? shall there any man be put to\l"
    .string "death this day in Israel? for do not\l"
    .string "I know that I am this day king over\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_23::
    .string "Therefore the king said unto Shimei,\n"
    .string "Thou shalt not die. And the king\l"
    .string "sware unto him$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_24::
    .string "And Mephibosheth the son of Saul\n"
    .string "came down to meet the king, and had\l"
    .string "neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed\l"
    .string "his beard, nor washed his clothes,\l"
    .string "from the day the king departed\l"
    .string "until the day he came again in peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_25::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he was\n"
    .string "come to Jerusalem to meet the king,\l"
    .string "that the king said unto him,\l"
    .string "Wherefore wentest not thou with me,\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_26::
    .string "And he answered, My lord, O king, my\n"
    .string "servant deceived me: for thy servant\l"
    .string "said, I will saddle me an ass, that\l"
    .string "I may ride thereon, and go to the\l"
    .string "king; because thy servant is lame$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_27::
    .string "And he hath slandered thy servant\n"
    .string "unto my lord the king; but my lord\l"
    .string "the king is as an angel of God: do\l"
    .string "therefore what is good in thine eyes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_28::
    .string "For all of my father’s house were\n"
    .string "but dead men before my lord the king:\l"
    .string "yet didst thou set thy servant among\l"
    .string "them that did eat at thine own table.\l"
    .string "What right therefore have I yet to\l"
    .string "cry any more unto the king?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_29::
    .string "And the king said unto him, Why\n"
    .string "speakest thou any more of thy\l"
    .string "matters? I have said, Thou and Ziba\l"
    .string "divide the land$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_30::
    .string "And Mephibosheth said unto the\n"
    .string "king, Yea, let him take all,\l"
    .string "forasmuch as my lord the king is\l"
    .string "come again in peace unto his own\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_31::
    .string "And Barzillai the Gileadite came\n"
    .string "down from Rogelim, and went over\l"
    .string "Jordan with the king, to conduct him\l"
    .string "over Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_32::
    .string "Now Barzillai was a very aged man,\n"
    .string "even fourscore years old: and he had\l"
    .string "provided the king of sustenance\l"
    .string "while he lay at Mahanaim; for he was\l"
    .string "a very great man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_33::
    .string "And the king said unto Barzillai,\n"
    .string "Come thou over with me, and I will\l"
    .string "feed thee with me in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_34::
    .string "And Barzillai said unto the king,\n"
    .string "How long have I to live, that I\l"
    .string "should go up with the king unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_35::
    .string "I am this day fourscore years old:\n"
    .string "and can I discern between good and\l"
    .string "evil? can thy servant taste what I\l"
    .string "eat or what I drink? can I hear any\l"
    .string "more the voice of singing men and\l"
    .string "singing women? wherefore then should\l"
    .string "thy servant be yet a burden unto my\l"
    .string "lord the king?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_36::
    .string "Thy servant will go a little way\n"
    .string "over Jordan with the king: and why\l"
    .string "should the king recompense it me\l"
    .string "with such a reward?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_37::
    .string "Let thy servant, I pray thee, turn\n"
    .string "back again, that I may die in mine own\l"
    .string "city, and be buried by the grave of my\l"
    .string "father and of my mother. But behold\l"
    .string "thy servant Chimham; let him go over\l"
    .string "with my lord the king; and do to him\l"
    .string "what shall seem good unto thee$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_38::
    .string "And the king answered, Chimham\n"
    .string "shall go over with me, and I will\l"
    .string "do to him that which shall seem good\l"
    .string "unto thee: and whatsoever thou shalt\l"
    .string "require of me, that will I do for\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_39::
    .string "And all the people went over\n"
    .string "Jordan. And when the king was come\l"
    .string "over, the king kissed Barzillai,\l"
    .string "and blessed him; and he returned\l"
    .string "unto his own place.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_40::
    .string "Then the king went on to Gilgal,\n"
    .string "and Chimham went on with him: and\l"
    .string "all the people of Judah conducted\l"
    .string "the king, and also half the people\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_41::
    .string "And, behold, all the men of\n"
    .string "Israel came to the king, and said\l"
    .string "unto the king, Why have our brethren\l"
    .string "the men of Judah stolen thee away,\l"
    .string "and have brought the king, and his\l"
    .string "household, and all David’s men with\l"
    .string "him, over Jordan?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_42::
    .string "And all the men of Judah answered\n"
    .string "the men of Israel, Because the king\l"
    .string "is near of kin to us: wherefore then\l"
    .string "be ye angry for this matter? have we\l"
    .string "eaten at all of the king’s cost? or\l"
    .string "hath he given us any gift?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_19_43::
    .string "And the men of Israel answered the\n"
    .string "men of Judah, and said, We have ten\l"
    .string "parts in the king, and we have also\l"
    .string "more right in David than ye: why then\l"
    .string "did ye despise us, that our advice\l"
    .string "should not be first had in bringing\l"
    .string "back our king? And the words of the\l"
    .string "men of Judah were fiercer than the\l"
    .string "words of the men of Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_1::
    .string "And there happened to be there a\n"
    .string "man of Belial, whose name was Sheba,\l"
    .string "the son of Bichri, a Benjamite: and\l"
    .string "he blew a trumpet, and said, We have\l"
    .string "no part in David, neither have we\l"
    .string "inheritance in the son of Jesse:\l"
    .string "every man to his tents, O Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_2::
    .string "So every man of Israel went up from\n"
    .string "after David, and followed Sheba the\l"
    .string "son of Bichri: but the men of Judah\l"
    .string "clave unto their king, from Jordan\l"
    .string "even to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_3::
    .string "And David came to his house at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem; and the king took the ten\l"
    .string "women his concubines, whom he had\l"
    .string "left to keep the house, and put them\l"
    .string "in ward, and fed them, but went not in\l"
    .string "unto them. So they were shut up unto\l"
    .string "the day of their death, living in\l"
    .string "widowhood.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_4::
    .string "Then said the king to Amasa,\n"
    .string "Assemble me the men of Judah within\l"
    .string "three days, and be thou here present.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_5::
    .string "So Amasa went to assemble the men\n"
    .string "of Judah: but he tarried longer than\l"
    .string "the set time which he had appointed\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_6::
    .string "And David said to Abishai, Now\n"
    .string "shall Sheba the son of Bichri do us\l"
    .string "more harm than did Absalom: take\l"
    .string "thou thy lord’s servants, and\l"
    .string "pursue after him, lest he get him\l"
    .string "fenced cities, and escape us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_7::
    .string "And there went out after him Joab’s\n"
    .string "men, and the Cherethites, and the\l"
    .string "Pelethites, and all the mighty men:\l"
    .string "and they went out of Jerusalem, to\l"
    .string "pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_8::
    .string "When they were at the great stone\n"
    .string "which is in Gibeon, Amasa went before\l"
    .string "them. And Joab’s garment that he had\l"
    .string "put on was girded unto him, and upon\l"
    .string "it a girdle with a sword fastened\l"
    .string "upon his loins in the sheath\l"
    .string "thereof; and as he went forth it\l"
    .string "fell out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_9::
    .string "And Joab said to Amasa, Art thou in\n"
    .string "health, my brother? And Joab took\l"
    .string "Amasa by the beard with the right\l"
    .string "hand to kiss him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_10::
    .string "But Amasa took no heed to the sword\n"
    .string "that was in Joab’s hand: so he smote\l"
    .string "him therewith in the fifth rib, and\l"
    .string "shed out his bowels to the ground,\l"
    .string "and struck him not again; and he\l"
    .string "died. So Joab and Abishai his brother\l"
    .string "pursued after Sheba the son of Bichri.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_11::
    .string "And one of Joab’s men stood by him,\n"
    .string "and said, He that favoureth Joab, and\l"
    .string "he that is for David, let him go\l"
    .string "after Joab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_12::
    .string "And Amasa wallowed in blood in the\n"
    .string "midst of the highway. And when the\l"
    .string "man saw that all the people stood\l"
    .string "still, he removed Amasa out of the\l"
    .string "highway into the field, and cast a\l"
    .string "cloth upon him, when he saw that\l"
    .string "every one that came by him stood\l"
    .string "still.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_13::
    .string "When he was removed out of the\n"
    .string "highway, all the people went on\l"
    .string "after Joab, to pursue after Sheba\l"
    .string "the son of Bichri.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_14::
    .string "And he went through all the tribes\n"
    .string "of Israel unto Abel, and to\l"
    .string "Bethmaachah, and all the Berites:\l"
    .string "and they were gathered together, and\l"
    .string "went also after him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_15::
    .string "And they came and besieged him in\n"
    .string "Abel of Bethmaachah, and they cast\l"
    .string "up a bank against the city, and it\l"
    .string "stood in the trench: and all the\l"
    .string "people that were with Joab battered\l"
    .string "the wall, to throw it down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_16::
    .string "Then cried a wise woman out of the\n"
    .string "city, Hear, hear; say, I pray you,\l"
    .string "unto Joab, Come near hither, that I\l"
    .string "may speak with thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_17::
    .string "And when he was come near unto her,\n"
    .string "the woman said, Art thou Joab? And he\l"
    .string "answered, I am he. Then she said unto\l"
    .string "him, Hear the words of thine\l"
    .string "handmaid. And he answered, I do hear.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_18::
    .string "Then she spake, saying, They were\n"
    .string "wont to speak in old time, saying,\l"
    .string "They shall surely ask counsel at\l"
    .string "Abel: and so they ended the matter.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_19::
    .string "I am one of them that are peaceable\n"
    .string "and faithful in Israel: thou\l"
    .string "seekest to destroy a city and a\l"
    .string "mother in Israel: why wilt thou\l"
    .string "swallow up the inheritance of the\l"
    .string "LORD?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_20::
    .string "And Joab answered and said, Far be\n"
    .string "it, far be it from me, that I should\l"
    .string "swallow up or destroy$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_21::
    .string "The matter is not so: but a man of\n"
    .string "mount Ephraim, Sheba the son of\l"
    .string "Bichri by name, hath lifted up his\l"
    .string "hand against the king, even against\l"
    .string "David: deliver him only, and I\l"
    .string "will depart from the city. And the\l"
    .string "woman said unto Joab, Behold, his\l"
    .string "head shall be thrown to thee over\l"
    .string "the wall.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_22::
    .string "Then the woman went unto all the\n"
    .string "people in her wisdom. And they cut\l"
    .string "off the head of Sheba the son of\l"
    .string "Bichri, and cast it out to Joab. And\l"
    .string "he blew a trumpet, and they retired\l"
    .string "from the city, every man to his tent.\l"
    .string "And Joab returned to Jerusalem unto\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_23::
    .string "Now Joab was over all the host of\n"
    .string "Israel: and Benaiah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoiada was over the Cherethites\l"
    .string "and over the Pelethites:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_24::
    .string "And Adoram was over the tribute: and\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was\l"
    .string "recorder:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_25::
    .string "And Sheva was scribe: and Zadok and\n"
    .string "Abiathar were the priests:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_20_26::
    .string "And Ira also the Jairite was a\n"
    .string "chief ruler about David$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_1::
    .string "Then there was a famine in the days\n"
    .string "of David three years, year after\l"
    .string "year; and David enquired of the LORD.\l"
    .string "And the LORD answered, It is for\l"
    .string "Saul, and for his bloody house,\l"
    .string "because he slew the Gibeonites.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_2::
    .string "And the king called the\n"
    .string "Gibeonites, and said unto them; (now\l"
    .string "the Gibeonites were not of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, but of the\l"
    .string "remnant of the Amorites; and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel had sworn unto\l"
    .string "them: and Saul sought to slay them\l"
    .string "in his zeal to the children of\l"
    .string "Israel and Judah.)"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_3::
    .string "Wherefore David said unto the\n"
    .string "Gibeonites, What shall I do for you?\l"
    .string "and wherewith shall I make the\l"
    .string "atonement, that ye may bless the\l"
    .string "inheritance of the LORD?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_4::
    .string "And the Gibeonites said unto him, We\n"
    .string "will have no silver nor gold of\l"
    .string "Saul, nor of his house; neither for\l"
    .string "us shalt thou kill any man in\l"
    .string "Israel. And he said, What ye shall\l"
    .string "say, that will I do for you$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_5::
    .string "And they answered the king, The man\n"
    .string "that consumed us, and that devised\l"
    .string "against us that we should be\l"
    .string "destroyed from remaining in any of\l"
    .string "the coasts of Israel,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_6::
    .string "Let seven men of his sons be\n"
    .string "delivered unto us, and we will hang\l"
    .string "them up unto the LORD in Gibeah of\l"
    .string "Saul, whom the LORD did choose. And\l"
    .string "the king said, I will give them$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_7::
    .string "But the king spared Mephibosheth,\n"
    .string "the son of Jonathan the son of Saul,\l"
    .string "because of the LORD’s oath that was\l"
    .string "between them, between David and\l"
    .string "Jonathan the son of Saul.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_8::
    .string "But the king took the two sons of\n"
    .string "Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom\l"
    .string "she bare unto Saul, Armoni and\l"
    .string "Mephibosheth; and the five sons of\l"
    .string "Michal the daughter of Saul, whom\l"
    .string "she brought up for Adriel the son of\l"
    .string "Barzillai the Meholathite:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_9::
    .string "And he delivered them into the\n"
    .string "hands of the Gibeonites, and they\l"
    .string "hanged them in the hill before the\l"
    .string "LORD: and they fell all seven\l"
    .string "together, and were put to death in\l"
    .string "the days of harvest, in the first\l"
    .string "days, in the beginning of barley\l"
    .string "harvest$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_10::
    .string "And Rizpah the daughter of Aiah\n"
    .string "took sackcloth, and spread it for\l"
    .string "her upon the rock, from the\l"
    .string "beginning of harvest until water\l"
    .string "dropped upon them out of heaven,\l"
    .string "and suffered neither the birds of the\l"
    .string "air to rest on them by day, nor the\l"
    .string "beasts of the field by night.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_11::
    .string "And it was told David what Rizpah\n"
    .string "the daughter of Aiah, the concubine\l"
    .string "of Saul, had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_12::
    .string "And David went and took the bones of\n"
    .string "Saul and the bones of Jonathan his\l"
    .string "son from the men of Jabeshgilead,\l"
    .string "which had stolen them from the\l"
    .string "street of Bethshan, where the\l"
    .string "Philistines had hanged them, when\l"
    .string "the Philistines had slain Saul in\l"
    .string "Gilboa:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_13::
    .string "And he brought up from thence the\n"
    .string "bones of Saul and the bones of\l"
    .string "Jonathan his son; and they gathered\l"
    .string "the bones of them that were hanged$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_14::
    .string "And the bones of Saul and Jonathan\n"
    .string "his son buried they in the country of\l"
    .string "Benjamin in Zelah, in the sepulchre\l"
    .string "of Kish his father: and they\l"
    .string "performed all that the king\l"
    .string "commanded. And after that God was\l"
    .string "intreated for the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_15::
    .string "Moreover the Philistines had yet\n"
    .string "war again with Israel; and David\l"
    .string "went down, and his servants with him,\l"
    .string "and fought against the Philistines:\l"
    .string "and David waxed faint.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_16::
    .string "And Ishbibenob, which was of the\n"
    .string "sons of the giant, the weight of\l"
    .string "whose spear weighed three hundred\l"
    .string "shekels of brass in weight, he being\l"
    .string "girded with a new sword, thought to\l"
    .string "have slain David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_17::
    .string "But Abishai the son of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "succoured him, and smote the\l"
    .string "Philistine, and killed him. Then\l"
    .string "the men of David sware unto him,\l"
    .string "saying, Thou shalt go no more out\l"
    .string "with us to battle, that thou quench\l"
    .string "not the light of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_18::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "there was again a battle with the\l"
    .string "Philistines at Gob: then Sibbechai\l"
    .string "the Hushathite slew Saph, which was\l"
    .string "of the sons of the giant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_19::
    .string "And there was again a battle in Gob\n"
    .string "with the Philistines, where Elhanan\l"
    .string "the son of Jaareoregim, a\l"
    .string "Bethlehemite, slew the brother of\l"
    .string "Goliath the Gittite, the staff of\l"
    .string "whose spear was like a weaver’s\l"
    .string "beam.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_20::
    .string "And there was yet a battle in Gath,\n"
    .string "where was a man of great stature,\l"
    .string "that had on every hand six fingers,\l"
    .string "and on every foot six toes, four and\l"
    .string "twenty in number; and he also was\l"
    .string "born to the giant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_21::
    .string "And when he defied Israel, Jonathan\n"
    .string "the son of Shimeah the brother of\l"
    .string "David slew him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_21_22::
    .string "These four were born to the giant in\n"
    .string "Gath, and fell by the hand of David,\l"
    .string "and by the hand of his servants.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_1::
    .string "And David spake unto the LORD the\n"
    .string "words of this song in the day that\l"
    .string "the LORD had delivered him out of\l"
    .string "the hand of all his enemies, and out\l"
    .string "of the hand of Saul:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_2::
    .string "And he said, The LORD is my rock, and\n"
    .string "my fortress, and my deliverer;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_3::
    .string "The God of my rock; in him will I\n"
    .string "trust: he is my shield, and the horn\l"
    .string "of my salvation, my high tower, and\l"
    .string "my refuge, my saviour; thou savest me\l"
    .string "from violence$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_4::
    .string "I will call on the LORD, who is\n"
    .string "worthy to be praised: so shall I be\l"
    .string "saved from mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_5::
    .string "When the waves of death compassed\n"
    .string "me, the floods of ungodly men made\l"
    .string "me afraid;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_6::
    .string "The sorrows of hell compassed me\n"
    .string "about; the snares of death prevented\l"
    .string "me;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_7::
    .string "In my distress I called upon the\n"
    .string "LORD, and cried to my God: and he did\l"
    .string "hear my voice out of his temple, and\l"
    .string "my cry did enter into his ears$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_8::
    .string "Then the earth shook and trembled;\n"
    .string "the foundations of heaven moved and\l"
    .string "shook, because he was wroth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_9::
    .string "There went up a smoke out of his\n"
    .string "nostrils, and fire out of his mouth\l"
    .string "devoured: coals were kindled by it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_10::
    .string "He bowed the heavens also, and came\n"
    .string "down; and darkness was under his feet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_11::
    .string "And he rode upon a cherub, and did\n"
    .string "fly: and he was seen upon the wings\l"
    .string "of the wind.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_12::
    .string "And he made darkness pavilions\n"
    .string "round about him, dark waters, and\l"
    .string "thick clouds of the skies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_13::
    .string "Through the brightness before him\n"
    .string "were coals of fire kindled.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_14::
    .string "The LORD thundered from heaven, and\n"
    .string "the most High uttered his voice.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_15::
    .string "And he sent out arrows, and\n"
    .string "scattered them; lightning, and\l"
    .string "discomfited them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_16::
    .string "And the channels of the sea\n"
    .string "appeared, the foundations of the\l"
    .string "world were discovered, at the\l"
    .string "rebuking of the LORD, at the blast of\l"
    .string "the breath of his nostrils.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_17::
    .string "He sent from above, he took me; he\n"
    .string "drew me out of many waters;"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_18::
    .string "He delivered me from my strong\n"
    .string "enemy, and from them that hated me:\l"
    .string "for they were too strong for me$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_19::
    .string "They prevented me in the day of my\n"
    .string "calamity: but the LORD was my stay.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_20::
    .string "He brought me forth also into a\n"
    .string "large place: he delivered me,\l"
    .string "because he delighted in me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_21::
    .string "The LORD rewarded me according to my\n"
    .string "righteousness: according to the\l"
    .string "cleanness of my hands hath he\l"
    .string "recompensed me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_22::
    .string "For I have kept the ways of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and have not wickedly\l"
    .string "departed from my God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_23::
    .string "For all his judgments were before\n"
    .string "me: and as for his statutes, I did not\l"
    .string "depart from them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_24::
    .string "I was also upright before him, and\n"
    .string "have kept myself from mine iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_25::
    .string "Therefore the LORD hath\n"
    .string "recompensed me according to my\l"
    .string "righteousness; according to my\l"
    .string "cleanness in his eye sight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_26::
    .string "With the merciful thou wilt shew\n"
    .string "thyself merciful, and with the\l"
    .string "upright man thou wilt shew thyself\l"
    .string "upright.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_27::
    .string "With the pure thou wilt shew\n"
    .string "thyself pure; and with the froward\l"
    .string "thou wilt shew thyself unsavoury.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_28::
    .string "And the afflicted people thou\n"
    .string "wilt save: but thine eyes are upon\l"
    .string "the haughty, that thou mayest bring\l"
    .string "them down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_29::
    .string "For thou art my lamp, O LORD: and\n"
    .string "the LORD will lighten my darkness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_30::
    .string "For by thee I have run through a\n"
    .string "troop: by my God have I leaped over\l"
    .string "a wall.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_31::
    .string "As for God, his way is perfect; the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD is tried: he is a\l"
    .string "buckler to all them that trust in\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_32::
    .string "For who is God, save the LORD? and\n"
    .string "who is a rock, save our God?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_33::
    .string "God is my strength and power: and he\n"
    .string "maketh my way perfect$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_34::
    .string "He maketh my feet like hinds’ feet:\n"
    .string "and setteth me upon my high places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_35::
    .string "He teacheth my hands to war; so that\n"
    .string "a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_36::
    .string "Thou hast also given me the shield\n"
    .string "of thy salvation: and thy\l"
    .string "gentleness hath made me great.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_37::
    .string "Thou hast enlarged my steps under\n"
    .string "me; so that my feet did not slip.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_38::
    .string "I have pursued mine enemies, and\n"
    .string "destroyed them; and turned not again\l"
    .string "until I had consumed them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_39::
    .string "And I have consumed them, and\n"
    .string "wounded them, that they could not\l"
    .string "arise: yea, they are fallen under my\l"
    .string "feet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_40::
    .string "For thou hast girded me with\n"
    .string "strength to battle: them that rose\l"
    .string "up against me hast thou subdued\l"
    .string "under me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_41::
    .string "Thou hast also given me the necks\n"
    .string "of mine enemies, that I might destroy\l"
    .string "them that hate me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_42::
    .string "They looked, but there was none to\n"
    .string "save; even unto the LORD, but he\l"
    .string "answered them not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_43::
    .string "Then did I beat them as small as\n"
    .string "the dust of the earth, I did stamp\l"
    .string "them as the mire of the street, and\l"
    .string "did spread them abroad.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_44::
    .string "Thou also hast delivered me from\n"
    .string "the strivings of my people, thou\l"
    .string "hast kept me to be head of the\l"
    .string "heathen: a people which I knew not\l"
    .string "shall serve me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_45::
    .string "Strangers shall submit themselves\n"
    .string "unto me: as soon as they hear, they\l"
    .string "shall be obedient unto me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_46::
    .string "Strangers shall fade away, and\n"
    .string "they shall be afraid out of their\l"
    .string "close places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_47::
    .string "The LORD liveth; and blessed be my\n"
    .string "rock; and exalted be the God of the\l"
    .string "rock of my salvation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_48::
    .string "It is God that avengeth me, and that\n"
    .string "bringeth down the people under me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_49::
    .string "And that bringeth me forth from mine\n"
    .string "enemies: thou also hast lifted me\l"
    .string "up on high above them that rose up\l"
    .string "against me: thou hast delivered me\l"
    .string "from the violent man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_50::
    .string "Therefore I will give thanks unto\n"
    .string "thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and I\l"
    .string "will sing praises unto thy name.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_22_51::
    .string "He is the tower of salvation for\n"
    .string "his king: and sheweth mercy to his\l"
    .string "anointed, unto David, and to his seed\l"
    .string "for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_1::
    .string "Now these be the last words of David\n"
    .string " David the son of Jesse said, and the\l"
    .string "man who was raised up on high, the\l"
    .string "anointed of the God of Jacob, and the\l"
    .string "sweet psalmist of Israel, said,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_2::
    .string "The Spirit of the LORD spake by me,\n"
    .string "and his word was in my tongue$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_3::
    .string "The God of Israel said, the Rock of\n"
    .string "Israel spake to me, He that ruleth\l"
    .string "over men must be just, ruling in the\l"
    .string "fear of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_4::
    .string "And he shall be as the light of\n"
    .string "the morning, when the sun riseth,\l"
    .string "even a morning without clouds; as\l"
    .string "the tender grass springing out of\l"
    .string "the earth by clear shining after\l"
    .string "rain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_5::
    .string "Although my house be not so with\n"
    .string "God; yet he hath made with me an\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant, ordered in\l"
    .string "all things, and sure: for this is\l"
    .string "all my salvation, and all my\l"
    .string "desire, although he make it not to\l"
    .string "grow.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_6::
    .string "But the sons of Belial shall be\n"
    .string "all of them as thorns thrust away,\l"
    .string "because they cannot be taken with\l"
    .string "hands:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_7::
    .string "But the man that shall touch them\n"
    .string "must be fenced with iron and the\l"
    .string "staff of a spear; and they shall be\l"
    .string "utterly burned with fire in the same\l"
    .string "place$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_8::
    .string "These be the names of the mighty men\n"
    .string "whom David had: The Tachmonite that\l"
    .string "sat in the seat, chief among the\l"
    .string "captains; the same was Adino the\l"
    .string "Eznite: he lift up his spear\l"
    .string "against eight hundred, whom he slew\l"
    .string "at one time.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_9::
    .string "And after him was Eleazar the son\n"
    .string "of Dodo the Ahohite, one of the three\l"
    .string "mighty men with David, when they\l"
    .string "defied the Philistines that were\l"
    .string "there gathered together to battle,\l"
    .string "and the men of Israel were gone away:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_10::
    .string "He arose, and smote the Philistines\n"
    .string "until his hand was weary, and his\l"
    .string "hand clave unto the sword: and the\l"
    .string "LORD wrought a great victory that\l"
    .string "day; and the people returned after\l"
    .string "him only to spoil$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_11::
    .string "And after him was Shammah the son of\n"
    .string "Agee the Hararite. And the\l"
    .string "Philistines were gathered together\l"
    .string "into a troop, where was a piece of\l"
    .string "ground full of lentiles: and the\l"
    .string "people fled from the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_12::
    .string "But he stood in the midst of the\n"
    .string "ground, and defended it, and slew\l"
    .string "the Philistines: and the LORD\l"
    .string "wrought a great victory.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_13::
    .string "And three of the thirty chief went\n"
    .string "down, and came to David in the\l"
    .string "harvest time unto the cave of\l"
    .string "Adullam: and the troop of the\l"
    .string "Philistines pitched in the valley\l"
    .string "of Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_14::
    .string "And David was then in an hold, and\n"
    .string "the garrison of the Philistines was\l"
    .string "then in Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_15::
    .string "And David longed, and said, Oh that\n"
    .string "one would give me drink of the water\l"
    .string "of the well of Bethlehem, which is\l"
    .string "by the gate!"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_16::
    .string "And the three mighty men brake\n"
    .string "through the host of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "and drew water out of the well of\l"
    .string "Bethlehem, that was by the gate, and\l"
    .string "took it, and brought it to David:\l"
    .string "nevertheless he would not drink\l"
    .string "thereof, but poured it out unto the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_17::
    .string "And he said, Be it far from me, O\n"
    .string "LORD, that I should do this: is not\l"
    .string "this the blood of the men that went\l"
    .string "in jeopardy of their lives?\l"
    .string "therefore he would not drink it.\l"
    .string "These things did these three mighty\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_18::
    .string "And Abishai, the brother of Joab,\n"
    .string "the son of Zeruiah, was chief among\l"
    .string "three. And he lifted up his spear\l"
    .string "against three hundred, and slew\l"
    .string "them, and had the name among three.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_19::
    .string "Was he not most honourable of\n"
    .string "three? therefore he was their\l"
    .string "captain: howbeit he attained not\l"
    .string "unto the first three.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_20::
    .string "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the\n"
    .string "son of a valiant man, of Kabzeel,\l"
    .string "who had done many acts, he slew two\l"
    .string "lionlike men of Moab: he went down\l"
    .string "also and slew a lion in the midst\l"
    .string "of a pit in time of snow:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_21::
    .string "And he slew an Egyptian, a goodly\n"
    .string "man: and the Egyptian had a spear in\l"
    .string "his hand; but he went down to him with\l"
    .string "a staff, and plucked the spear out\l"
    .string "of the Egyptian’s hand, and slew him\l"
    .string "with his own spear$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_22::
    .string "These things did Benaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Jehoiada, and had the name among\l"
    .string "three mighty men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_23::
    .string "He was more honourable than the\n"
    .string "thirty, but he attained not to the\l"
    .string "first three. And David set him over\l"
    .string "his guard.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_24::
    .string "Asahel the brother of Joab was one\n"
    .string "of the thirty; Elhanan the son of\l"
    .string "Dodo of Bethlehem,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_25::
    .string "Shammah the Harodite, Elika the\n"
    .string "Harodite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_26::
    .string "Helez the Paltite, Ira the son of\n"
    .string "Ikkesh the Tekoite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_27::
    .string "Abiezer the Anethothite, Mebunnai\n"
    .string "the Hushathite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_28::
    .string "Zalmon the Ahohite, Maharai the\n"
    .string "Netophathite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_29::
    .string "Heleb the son of Baanah, a\n"
    .string "Netophathite, Ittai the son of Ribai\l"
    .string "out of Gibeah of the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_30::
    .string "Benaiah the Pirathonite, Hiddai of\n"
    .string "the brooks of Gaash,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_31::
    .string "Abialbon the Arbathite, Azmaveth\n"
    .string "the Barhumite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_32::
    .string "Eliahba the Shaalbonite, of the\n"
    .string "sons of Jashen, Jonathan,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_33::
    .string "Shammah the Hararite, Ahiam the son\n"
    .string "of Sharar the Hararite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_34::
    .string "Eliphelet the son of Ahasbai, the\n"
    .string "son of the Maachathite, Eliam the\l"
    .string "son of Ahithophel the Gilonite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_35::
    .string "Hezrai the Carmelite, Paarai the\n"
    .string "Arbite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_36::
    .string "Igal the son of Nathan of Zobah,\n"
    .string "Bani the Gadite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_37::
    .string "Zelek the Ammonite, Nahari the\n"
    .string "Beerothite, armourbearer to Joab the\l"
    .string "son of Zeruiah,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_38::
    .string "Ira an Ithrite, Gareb an Ithrite,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_23_39::
    .string "Uriah the Hittite: thirty and seven\n"
    .string "in all$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_1::
    .string "And again the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Israel, and he\l"
    .string "moved David against them to say, Go,\l"
    .string "number Israel and Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_2::
    .string "For the king said to Joab the\n"
    .string "captain of the host, which was with\l"
    .string "him, Go now through all the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel, from Dan even to\l"
    .string "Beersheba, and number ye the\l"
    .string "people, that I may know the number\l"
    .string "of the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_3::
    .string "And Joab said unto the king, Now the\n"
    .string "LORD thy God add unto the people,\l"
    .string "how many soever they be, an\l"
    .string "hundredfold, and that the eyes of my\l"
    .string "lord the king may see it: but why doth\l"
    .string "my lord the king delight in this\l"
    .string "thing?"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_4::
    .string "Notwithstanding the king’s word\n"
    .string "prevailed against Joab, and against\l"
    .string "the captains of the host. And Joab\l"
    .string "and the captains of the host went\l"
    .string "out from the presence of the king, to\l"
    .string "number the people of Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_5::
    .string "And they passed over Jordan, and\n"
    .string "pitched in Aroer, on the right side\l"
    .string "of the city that lieth in the midst\l"
    .string "of the river of Gad, and toward\l"
    .string "Jazer:"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_6::
    .string "Then they came to Gilead, and to the\n"
    .string "land of Tahtimhodshi; and they came\l"
    .string "to Danjaan, and about to Zidon,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_7::
    .string "And came to the strong hold of Tyre,\n"
    .string "and to all the cities of the\l"
    .string "Hivites, and of the Canaanites: and\l"
    .string "they went out to the south of Judah,\l"
    .string "even to Beersheba$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_8::
    .string "So when they had gone through all\n"
    .string "the land, they came to Jerusalem at\l"
    .string "the end of nine months and twenty\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_9::
    .string "And Joab gave up the sum of the\n"
    .string "number of the people unto the king:\l"
    .string "and there were in Israel eight\l"
    .string "hundred thousand valiant men that\l"
    .string "drew the sword; and the men of Judah\l"
    .string "were five hundred thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_10::
    .string "And David’s heart smote him after\n"
    .string "that he had numbered the people.\l"
    .string "And David said unto the LORD, I have\l"
    .string "sinned greatly in that I have done:\l"
    .string "and now, I beseech thee, O LORD, take\l"
    .string "away the iniquity of thy servant; for\l"
    .string "I have done very foolishly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_11::
    .string "For when David was up in the\n"
    .string "morning, the word of the LORD came\l"
    .string "unto the prophet Gad, David’s seer,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_12::
    .string "Go and say unto David, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, I offer thee three things;\l"
    .string "choose thee one of them, that I may do\l"
    .string "it unto thee$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_13::
    .string "So Gad came to David, and told him,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, Shall seven years\l"
    .string "of famine come unto thee in thy land?\l"
    .string "or wilt thou flee three months\l"
    .string "before thine enemies, while they\l"
    .string "pursue thee? or that there be three\l"
    .string "days’ pestilence in thy land? now\l"
    .string "advise, and see what answer I shall\l"
    .string "return to him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_14::
    .string "And David said unto Gad, I am in a\n"
    .string "great strait: let us fall now into\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD; for his mercies\l"
    .string "are great: and let me not fall into\l"
    .string "the hand of man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_15::
    .string "So the LORD sent a pestilence upon\n"
    .string "Israel from the morning even to the\l"
    .string "time appointed: and there died of\l"
    .string "the people from Dan even to\l"
    .string "Beersheba seventy thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_16::
    .string "And when the angel stretched out\n"
    .string "his hand upon Jerusalem to destroy\l"
    .string "it, the LORD repented him of the\l"
    .string "evil, and said to the angel that\l"
    .string "destroyed the people, It is enough:\l"
    .string "stay now thine hand. And the angel of\l"
    .string "the LORD was by the threshingplace\l"
    .string "of Araunah the Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_17::
    .string "And David spake unto the LORD when\n"
    .string "he saw the angel that smote the\l"
    .string "people, and said, Lo, I have sinned,\l"
    .string "and I have done wickedly: but these\l"
    .string "sheep, what have they done? let\l"
    .string "thine hand, I pray thee, be against\l"
    .string "me, and against my father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_18::
    .string "And Gad came that day to David, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Go up, rear an altar\l"
    .string "unto the LORD in the threshingfloor\l"
    .string "of Araunah the Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_19::
    .string "And David, according to the saying\n"
    .string "of Gad, went up as the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_20::
    .string "And Araunah looked, and saw the\n"
    .string "king and his servants coming on\l"
    .string "toward him: and Araunah went out, and\l"
    .string "bowed himself before the king on his\l"
    .string "face upon the ground.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_21::
    .string "And Araunah said, Wherefore is my\n"
    .string "lord the king come to his servant?\l"
    .string "And David said, To buy the\l"
    .string "threshingfloor of thee, to build an\l"
    .string "altar unto the LORD, that the\l"
    .string "plague may be stayed from the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_22::
    .string "And Araunah said unto David, Let my\n"
    .string "lord the king take and offer up what\l"
    .string "seemeth good unto him: behold, here\l"
    .string "be oxen for burnt sacrifice, and\l"
    .string "threshing instruments and other\l"
    .string "instruments of the oxen for wood.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_23::
    .string "All these things did Araunah, as a\n"
    .string "king, give unto the king. And Araunah\l"
    .string "said unto the king, The LORD thy God\l"
    .string "accept thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_24::
    .string "And the king said unto Araunah, Nay;\n"
    .string "but I will surely buy it of thee at\l"
    .string "a price: neither will I offer burnt\l"
    .string "offerings unto the LORD my God of\l"
    .string "that which doth cost me nothing. So\l"
    .string "David bought the threshingfloor and\l"
    .string "the oxen for fifty shekels of\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_2_Samuel_24_25::
    .string "And David built there an altar\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, and offered burnt\l"
    .string "offerings and peace offerings. So\l"
    .string "the LORD was intreated for the land,\l"
    .string "and the plague was stayed from\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_1::
    .string "Now king David was old and stricken\n"
    .string "in years; and they covered him with\l"
    .string "clothes, but he gat no heat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_2::
    .string "Wherefore his servants said unto\n"
    .string "him, Let there be sought for my lord\l"
    .string "the king a young virgin: and let her\l"
    .string "stand before the king, and let her\l"
    .string "cherish him, and let her lie in thy\l"
    .string "bosom, that my lord the king may get\l"
    .string "heat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_3::
    .string "So they sought for a fair damsel\n"
    .string "throughout all the coasts of\l"
    .string "Israel, and found Abishag a\l"
    .string "Shunammite, and brought her to the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_4::
    .string "And the damsel was very fair, and\n"
    .string "cherished the king, and ministered to\l"
    .string "him: but the king knew her not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_5::
    .string "Then Adonijah the son of Haggith\n"
    .string "exalted himself, saying, I will be\l"
    .string "king: and he prepared him chariots\l"
    .string "and horsemen, and fifty men to run\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_6::
    .string "And his father had not displeased\n"
    .string "him at any time in saying, Why hast\l"
    .string "thou done so? and he also was a very\l"
    .string "goodly man; and his mother bare him\l"
    .string "after Absalom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_7::
    .string "And he conferred with Joab the son\n"
    .string "of Zeruiah, and with Abiathar the\l"
    .string "priest: and they following Adonijah\l"
    .string "helped him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_8::
    .string "But Zadok the priest, and Benaiah\n"
    .string "the son of Jehoiada, and Nathan the\l"
    .string "prophet, and Shimei, and Rei, and the\l"
    .string "mighty men which belonged to David,\l"
    .string "were not with Adonijah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_9::
    .string "And Adonijah slew sheep and oxen\n"
    .string "and fat cattle by the stone of\l"
    .string "Zoheleth, which is by Enrogel, and\l"
    .string "called all his brethren the king’s\l"
    .string "sons, and all the men of Judah the\l"
    .string "king’s servants:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_10::
    .string "But Nathan the prophet, and\n"
    .string "Benaiah, and the mighty men, and\l"
    .string "Solomon his brother, he called not$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_11::
    .string "Wherefore Nathan spake unto\n"
    .string "Bathsheba the mother of Solomon,\l"
    .string "saying, Hast thou not heard that\l"
    .string "Adonijah the son of Haggith doth\l"
    .string "reign, and David our lord knoweth it\l"
    .string "not?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_12::
    .string "Now therefore come, let me, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, give thee counsel, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest save thine own life, and the\l"
    .string "life of thy son Solomon$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_13::
    .string "Go and get thee in unto king David,\n"
    .string "and say unto him, Didst not thou, my\l"
    .string "lord, O king, swear unto thine\l"
    .string "handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon\l"
    .string "thy son shall reign after me, and he\l"
    .string "shall sit upon my throne? why then\l"
    .string "doth Adonijah reign?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_14::
    .string "Behold, while thou yet talkest\n"
    .string "there with the king, I also will\l"
    .string "come in after thee, and confirm thy\l"
    .string "words$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_15::
    .string "And Bathsheba went in unto the king\n"
    .string "into the chamber: and the king was\l"
    .string "very old; and Abishag the Shunammite\l"
    .string "ministered unto the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_16::
    .string "And Bathsheba bowed, and did\n"
    .string "obeisance unto the king. And the king\l"
    .string "said, What wouldest thou?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_17::
    .string "And she said unto him, My lord, thou\n"
    .string "swarest by the LORD thy God unto\l"
    .string "thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly\l"
    .string "Solomon thy son shall reign after\l"
    .string "me, and he shall sit upon my throne$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_18::
    .string "And now, behold, Adonijah reigneth;\n"
    .string "and now, my lord the king, thou\l"
    .string "knowest it not:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_19::
    .string "And he hath slain oxen and fat\n"
    .string "cattle and sheep in abundance, and\l"
    .string "hath called all the sons of the\l"
    .string "king, and Abiathar the priest, and\l"
    .string "Joab the captain of the host: but\l"
    .string "Solomon thy servant hath he not\l"
    .string "called$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_20::
    .string "And thou, my lord, O king, the eyes\n"
    .string "of all Israel are upon thee, that\l"
    .string "thou shouldest tell them who\l"
    .string "shall sit on the throne of my lord\l"
    .string "the king after him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_21::
    .string "Otherwise it shall come to pass,\n"
    .string "when my lord the king shall sleep\l"
    .string "with his fathers, that I and my son\l"
    .string "Solomon shall be counted offenders.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_22::
    .string "And, lo, while she yet talked with\n"
    .string "the king, Nathan the prophet also\l"
    .string "came in.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_23::
    .string "And they told the king, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold Nathan the prophet. And when\l"
    .string "he was come in before the king, he\l"
    .string "bowed himself before the king with\l"
    .string "his face to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_24::
    .string "And Nathan said, My lord, O king,\n"
    .string "hast thou said, Adonijah shall\l"
    .string "reign after me, and he shall sit\l"
    .string "upon my throne?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_25::
    .string "For he is gone down this day, and\n"
    .string "hath slain oxen and fat cattle and\l"
    .string "sheep in abundance, and hath called\l"
    .string "all the king’s sons, and the\l"
    .string "captains of the host, and Abiathar\l"
    .string "the priest; and, behold, they eat\l"
    .string "and drink before him, and say, God\l"
    .string "save king Adonijah$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_26::
    .string "But me, even me thy servant, and\n"
    .string "Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the\l"
    .string "son of Jehoiada, and thy servant\l"
    .string "Solomon, hath he not called.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_27::
    .string "Is this thing done by my lord the\n"
    .string "king, and thou hast not shewed it\l"
    .string "unto thy servant, who should sit on\l"
    .string "the throne of my lord the king after\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_28::
    .string "Then king David answered and said,\n"
    .string "Call me Bathsheba. And she came into\l"
    .string "the king’s presence, and stood\l"
    .string "before the king$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_29::
    .string "And the king sware, and said, As the\n"
    .string "LORD liveth, that hath redeemed my\l"
    .string "soul out of all distress,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_30::
    .string "Even as I sware unto thee by the\n"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, saying,\l"
    .string "Assuredly Solomon thy son shall\l"
    .string "reign after me, and he shall sit\l"
    .string "upon my throne in my stead; even so\l"
    .string "will I certainly do this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_31::
    .string "Then Bathsheba bowed with her face\n"
    .string "to the earth, and did reverence to\l"
    .string "the king, and said, Let my lord king\l"
    .string "David live for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_32::
    .string "And king David said, Call me Zadok\n"
    .string "the priest, and Nathan the prophet,\l"
    .string "and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And\l"
    .string "they came before the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_33::
    .string "The king also said unto them, Take\n"
    .string "with you the servants of your lord,\l"
    .string "and cause Solomon my son to ride\l"
    .string "upon mine own mule, and bring him\l"
    .string "down to Gihon:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_34::
    .string "And let Zadok the priest and\n"
    .string "Nathan the prophet anoint him there\l"
    .string "king over Israel: and blow ye with\l"
    .string "the trumpet, and say, God save king\l"
    .string "Solomon$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_35::
    .string "Then ye shall come up after him,\n"
    .string "that he may come and sit upon my\l"
    .string "throne; for he shall be king in my\l"
    .string "stead: and I have appointed him to\l"
    .string "be ruler over Israel and over Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_36::
    .string "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada\n"
    .string "answered the king, and said, Amen:\l"
    .string "the LORD God of my lord the king say\l"
    .string "so too.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_37::
    .string "As the LORD hath been with my lord\n"
    .string "the king, even so be he with Solomon,\l"
    .string "and make his throne greater than the\l"
    .string "throne of my lord king David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_38::
    .string "So Zadok the priest, and Nathan the\n"
    .string "prophet, and Benaiah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and\l"
    .string "the Pelethites, went down, and\l"
    .string "caused Solomon to ride upon king\l"
    .string "David’s mule, and brought him to\l"
    .string "Gihon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_39::
    .string "And Zadok the priest took an horn\n"
    .string "of oil out of the tabernacle, and\l"
    .string "anointed Solomon. And they blew the\l"
    .string "trumpet; and all the people said,\l"
    .string "God save king Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_40::
    .string "And all the people came up after\n"
    .string "him, and the people piped with\l"
    .string "pipes, and rejoiced with great joy,\l"
    .string "so that the earth rent with the sound\l"
    .string "of them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_41::
    .string "And Adonijah and all the guests\n"
    .string "that were with him heard it as they\l"
    .string "had made an end of eating. And when\l"
    .string "Joab heard the sound of the trumpet,\l"
    .string "he said, Wherefore is this noise of\l"
    .string "the city being in an uproar?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_42::
    .string "And while he yet spake, behold,\n"
    .string "Jonathan the son of Abiathar the\l"
    .string "priest came; and Adonijah said unto\l"
    .string "him, Come in; for thou art a valiant\l"
    .string "man, and bringest good tidings$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_43::
    .string "And Jonathan answered and said to\n"
    .string "Adonijah, Verily our lord king\l"
    .string "David hath made Solomon king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_44::
    .string "And the king hath sent with him\n"
    .string "Zadok the priest, and Nathan the\l"
    .string "prophet, and Benaiah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and\l"
    .string "the Pelethites, and they have caused\l"
    .string "him to ride upon the king’s mule:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_45::
    .string "And Zadok the priest and Nathan the\n"
    .string "prophet have anointed him king in\l"
    .string "Gihon: and they are come up from\l"
    .string "thence rejoicing, so that the city\l"
    .string "rang again. This is the noise that ye\l"
    .string "have heard$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_46::
    .string "And also Solomon sitteth on the\n"
    .string "throne of the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_47::
    .string "And moreover the king’s servants\n"
    .string "came to bless our lord king David,\l"
    .string "saying, God make the name of Solomon\l"
    .string "better than thy name, and make his\l"
    .string "throne greater than thy throne. And\l"
    .string "the king bowed himself upon the bed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_48::
    .string "And also thus said the king,\n"
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God of Israel,\l"
    .string "which hath given one to sit on my\l"
    .string "throne this day, mine eyes even\l"
    .string "seeing it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_49::
    .string "And all the guests that were with\n"
    .string "Adonijah were afraid, and rose up,\l"
    .string "and went every man his way.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_50::
    .string "And Adonijah feared because of\n"
    .string "Solomon, and arose, and went, and\l"
    .string "caught hold on the horns of the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_51::
    .string "And it was told Solomon, saying,\n"
    .string "Behold, Adonijah feareth king\l"
    .string "Solomon: for, lo, he hath caught\l"
    .string "hold on the horns of the altar,\l"
    .string "saying, Let king Solomon swear unto\l"
    .string "me today that he will not slay his\l"
    .string "servant with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_52::
    .string "And Solomon said, If he will shew\n"
    .string "himself a worthy man, there shall\l"
    .string "not an hair of him fall to the\l"
    .string "earth: but if wickedness shall be\l"
    .string "found in him, he shall die.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_1_53::
    .string "So king Solomon sent, and they\n"
    .string "brought him down from the altar. And\l"
    .string "he came and bowed himself to king\l"
    .string "Solomon: and Solomon said unto him,\l"
    .string "Go to thine house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_1::
    .string "Now the days of David drew nigh that\n"
    .string "he should die; and he charged\l"
    .string "Solomon his son, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_2::
    .string "I go the way of all the earth: be\n"
    .string "thou strong therefore, and shew\l"
    .string "thyself a man;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_3::
    .string "And keep the charge of the LORD thy\n"
    .string "God, to walk in his ways, to keep\l"
    .string "his statutes, and his commandments,\l"
    .string "and his judgments, and his\l"
    .string "testimonies, as it is written in the\l"
    .string "law of Moses, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "prosper in all that thou doest, and\l"
    .string "whithersoever thou turnest thyself:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_4::
    .string "That the LORD may continue his word\n"
    .string "which he spake concerning me,\l"
    .string "saying, If thy children take heed to\l"
    .string "their way, to walk before me in truth\l"
    .string "with all their heart and with all\l"
    .string "their soul, there shall not fail\l"
    .string "thee (said he) a man on the throne of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_5::
    .string "Moreover thou knowest also what\n"
    .string "Joab the son of Zeruiah did to me, and\l"
    .string "what he did to the two captains of\l"
    .string "the hosts of Israel, unto Abner the\l"
    .string "son of Ner, and unto Amasa the son of\l"
    .string "Jether, whom he slew, and shed the\l"
    .string "blood of war in peace, and put the\l"
    .string "blood of war upon his girdle that\l"
    .string "was about his loins, and in his shoes\l"
    .string "that were on his feet.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_6::
    .string "Do therefore according to thy\n"
    .string "wisdom, and let not his hoar head go\l"
    .string "down to the grave in peace.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_7::
    .string "But shew kindness unto the sons of\n"
    .string "Barzillai the Gileadite, and let\l"
    .string "them be of those that eat at thy\l"
    .string "table: for so they came to me when I\l"
    .string "fled because of Absalom thy brother.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_8::
    .string "And, behold, thou hast with thee\n"
    .string "Shimei the son of Gera, a Benjamite\l"
    .string "of Bahurim, which cursed me with a\l"
    .string "grievous curse in the day when I went\l"
    .string "to Mahanaim: but he came down to meet\l"
    .string "me at Jordan, and I sware to him by\l"
    .string "the LORD, saying, I will not put\l"
    .string "thee to death with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_9::
    .string "Now therefore hold him not\n"
    .string "guiltless: for thou art a wise man,\l"
    .string "and knowest what thou oughtest to do\l"
    .string "unto him; but his hoar head bring\l"
    .string "thou down to the grave with blood.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_10::
    .string "So David slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and was buried in the city of David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_11::
    .string "And the days that David reigned over\n"
    .string "Israel were forty years: seven years\l"
    .string "reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and\l"
    .string "three years reigned he in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_12::
    .string "Then sat Solomon upon the throne\n"
    .string "of David his father; and his kingdom\l"
    .string "was established greatly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_13::
    .string "And Adonijah the son of Haggith came\n"
    .string "to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon.\l"
    .string "And she said, Comest thou\l"
    .string "peaceably? And he said, Peaceably.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_14::
    .string "He said moreover, I have somewhat to\n"
    .string "say unto thee. And she said, Say on.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_15::
    .string "And he said, Thou knowest that the\n"
    .string "kingdom was mine, and that all\l"
    .string "Israel set their faces on me, that I\l"
    .string "should reign: howbeit the kingdom is\l"
    .string "turned about, and is become my\l"
    .string "brother’s: for it was his from the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_16::
    .string "And now I ask one petition of thee,\n"
    .string "deny me not. And she said unto him,\l"
    .string "Say on.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_17::
    .string "And he said, Speak, I pray thee,\n"
    .string "unto Solomon the king, (for he will\l"
    .string "not say thee nay,) that he give me\l"
    .string "Abishag the Shunammite to wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_18::
    .string "And Bathsheba said, Well; I will\n"
    .string "speak for thee unto the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_19::
    .string "Bathsheba therefore went unto king\n"
    .string "Solomon, to speak unto him for\l"
    .string "Adonijah. And the king rose up to\l"
    .string "meet her, and bowed himself unto\l"
    .string "her, and sat down on his throne, and\l"
    .string "caused a seat to be set for the\l"
    .string "king’s mother; and she sat on his\l"
    .string "right hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_20::
    .string "Then she said, I desire one small\n"
    .string "petition of thee; I pray thee, say me\l"
    .string "not nay. And the king said unto her,\l"
    .string "Ask on, my mother: for I will not\l"
    .string "say thee nay.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_21::
    .string "And she said, Let Abishag the\n"
    .string "Shunammite be given to Adonijah thy\l"
    .string "brother to wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_22::
    .string "And king Solomon answered and said\n"
    .string "unto his mother, And why dost thou\l"
    .string "ask Abishag the Shunammite for\l"
    .string "Adonijah? ask for him the kingdom\l"
    .string "also; for he is mine elder brother;\l"
    .string "even for him, and for Abiathar the\l"
    .string "priest, and for Joab the son of\l"
    .string "Zeruiah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_23::
    .string "Then king Solomon sware by the\n"
    .string "LORD, saying, God do so to me, and\l"
    .string "more also, if Adonijah have not\l"
    .string "spoken this word against his own\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_24::
    .string "Now therefore, as the LORD liveth,\n"
    .string "which hath established me, and set\l"
    .string "me on the throne of David my father,\l"
    .string "and who hath made me an house, as he\l"
    .string "promised, Adonijah shall be put to\l"
    .string "death this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_25::
    .string "And king Solomon sent by the hand\n"
    .string "of Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and\l"
    .string "he fell upon him that he died.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_26::
    .string "And unto Abiathar the priest said\n"
    .string "the king, Get thee to Anathoth, unto\l"
    .string "thine own fields; for thou art\l"
    .string "worthy of death: but I will not at\l"
    .string "this time put thee to death, because\l"
    .string "thou barest the ark of the LORD God\l"
    .string "before David my father, and because\l"
    .string "thou hast been afflicted in all\l"
    .string "wherein my father was afflicted.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_27::
    .string "So Solomon thrust out Abiathar from\n"
    .string "being priest unto the LORD; that he\l"
    .string "might fulfil the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake concerning the house\l"
    .string "of Eli in Shiloh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_28::
    .string "Then tidings came to Joab: for Joab\n"
    .string "had turned after Adonijah, though he\l"
    .string "turned not after Absalom. And Joab\l"
    .string "fled unto the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and caught hold on the horns of\l"
    .string "the altar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_29::
    .string "And it was told king Solomon that\n"
    .string "Joab was fled unto the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the LORD; and, behold, he is by\l"
    .string "the altar. Then Solomon sent\l"
    .string "Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, saying,\l"
    .string "Go, fall upon him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_30::
    .string "And Benaiah came to the tabernacle\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and said unto him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the king, Come forth. And he\l"
    .string "said, Nay; but I will die here. And\l"
    .string "Benaiah brought the king word again,\l"
    .string "saying, Thus said Joab, and thus he\l"
    .string "answered me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_31::
    .string "And the king said unto him, Do as he\n"
    .string "hath said, and fall upon him, and\l"
    .string "bury him; that thou mayest take away\l"
    .string "the innocent blood, which Joab shed,\l"
    .string "from me, and from the house of my\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_32::
    .string "And the LORD shall return his\n"
    .string "blood upon his own head, who fell\l"
    .string "upon two men more righteous and\l"
    .string "better than he, and slew them with\l"
    .string "the sword, my father David not\l"
    .string "knowing thereof, to wit, Abner the\l"
    .string "son of Ner, captain of the host of\l"
    .string "Israel, and Amasa the son of Jether,\l"
    .string "captain of the host of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_33::
    .string "Their blood shall therefore\n"
    .string "return upon the head of Joab, and\l"
    .string "upon the head of his seed for ever:\l"
    .string "but upon David, and upon his seed,\l"
    .string "and upon his house, and upon his\l"
    .string "throne, shall there be peace for\l"
    .string "ever from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_34::
    .string "So Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went\n"
    .string "up, and fell upon him, and slew\l"
    .string "him: and he was buried in his own\l"
    .string "house in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_35::
    .string "And the king put Benaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Jehoiada in his room over the host:\l"
    .string "and Zadok the priest did the king\l"
    .string "put in the room of Abiathar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_36::
    .string "And the king sent and called for\n"
    .string "Shimei, and said unto him, Build\l"
    .string "thee an house in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "dwell there, and go not forth thence\l"
    .string "any whither.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_37::
    .string "For it shall be, that on the day\n"
    .string "thou goest out, and passest over the\l"
    .string "brook Kidron, thou shalt know for\l"
    .string "certain that thou shalt surely die:\l"
    .string "thy blood shall be upon thine own\l"
    .string "head.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_38::
    .string "And Shimei said unto the king, The\n"
    .string "saying is good: as my lord the king\l"
    .string "hath said, so will thy servant do.\l"
    .string "And Shimei dwelt in Jerusalem many\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_39::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "three years, that two of the servants\l"
    .string "of Shimei ran away unto Achish son of\l"
    .string "Maachah king of Gath. And they told\l"
    .string "Shimei, saying, Behold, thy servants\l"
    .string "be in Gath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_40::
    .string "And Shimei arose, and saddled his\n"
    .string "ass, and went to Gath to Achish to\l"
    .string "seek his servants: and Shimei went,\l"
    .string "and brought his servants from Gath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_41::
    .string "And it was told Solomon that\n"
    .string "Shimei had gone from Jerusalem to\l"
    .string "Gath, and was come again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_42::
    .string "And the king sent and called for\n"
    .string "Shimei, and said unto him, Did I not\l"
    .string "make thee to swear by the LORD, and\l"
    .string "protested unto thee, saying, Know for\l"
    .string "a certain, on the day thou goest out,\l"
    .string "and walkest abroad any whither, that\l"
    .string "thou shalt surely die? and thou\l"
    .string "saidst unto me, The word that I have\l"
    .string "heard is good.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_43::
    .string "Why then hast thou not kept the\n"
    .string "oath of the LORD, and the commandment\l"
    .string "that I have charged thee with?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_44::
    .string "The king said moreover to Shimei,\n"
    .string "Thou knowest all the wickedness\l"
    .string "which thine heart is privy to, that\l"
    .string "thou didst to David my father:\l"
    .string "therefore the LORD shall return thy\l"
    .string "wickedness upon thine own head;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_45::
    .string "And king Solomon shall be\n"
    .string "blessed, and the throne of David\l"
    .string "shall be established before the\l"
    .string "LORD for ever$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_2_46::
    .string "So the king commanded Benaiah the\n"
    .string "son of Jehoiada; which went out, and\l"
    .string "fell upon him, that he died. And\l"
    .string "the kingdom was established in the\l"
    .string "hand of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_1::
    .string "And Solomon made affinity with\n"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, and took\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s daughter, and brought her\l"
    .string "into the city of David, until he had\l"
    .string "made an end of building his own\l"
    .string "house, and the house of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "the wall of Jerusalem round about.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_2::
    .string "Only the people sacrificed in\n"
    .string "high places, because there was no\l"
    .string "house built unto the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD, until those days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_3::
    .string "And Solomon loved the LORD,\n"
    .string "walking in the statutes of David his\l"
    .string "father: only he sacrificed and burnt\l"
    .string "incense in high places.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_4::
    .string "And the king went to Gibeon to\n"
    .string "sacrifice there; for that was the\l"
    .string "great high place: a thousand burnt\l"
    .string "offerings did Solomon offer upon\l"
    .string "that altar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_5::
    .string "In Gibeon the LORD appeared to\n"
    .string "Solomon in a dream by night: and God\l"
    .string "said, Ask what I shall give thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_6::
    .string "And Solomon said, Thou hast shewed\n"
    .string "unto thy servant David my father\l"
    .string "great mercy, according as he walked\l"
    .string "before thee in truth, and in\l"
    .string "righteousness, and in uprightness of\l"
    .string "heart with thee; and thou hast kept\l"
    .string "for him this great kindness, that\l"
    .string "thou hast given him a son to sit on\l"
    .string "his throne, as it is this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_7::
    .string "And now, O LORD my God, thou hast\n"
    .string "made thy servant king instead of\l"
    .string "David my father: and I am but a\l"
    .string "little child: I know not how to go\l"
    .string "out or come in.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_8::
    .string "And thy servant is in the midst of\n"
    .string "thy people which thou hast chosen,\l"
    .string "a great people, that cannot be\l"
    .string "numbered nor counted for multitude.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_9::
    .string "Give therefore thy servant an\n"
    .string "understanding heart to judge thy\l"
    .string "people, that I may discern between\l"
    .string "good and bad: for who is able to\l"
    .string "judge this thy so great a people?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_10::
    .string "And the speech pleased the LORD,\n"
    .string "that Solomon had asked this thing$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_11::
    .string "And God said unto him, Because thou\n"
    .string "hast asked this thing, and hast not\l"
    .string "asked for thyself long life;\l"
    .string "neither hast asked riches for\l"
    .string "thyself, nor hast asked the life of\l"
    .string "thine enemies; but hast asked for\l"
    .string "thyself understanding to discern\l"
    .string "judgment;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_12::
    .string "Behold, I have done according to\n"
    .string "thy words: lo, I have given thee a\l"
    .string "wise and an understanding heart; so\l"
    .string "that there was none like thee before\l"
    .string "thee, neither after thee shall any\l"
    .string "arise like unto thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_13::
    .string "And I have also given thee that\n"
    .string "which thou hast not asked, both\l"
    .string "riches, and honour: so that there\l"
    .string "shall not be any among the kings\l"
    .string "like unto thee all thy days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_14::
    .string "And if thou wilt walk in my ways,\n"
    .string "to keep my statutes and my\l"
    .string "commandments, as thy father David did\l"
    .string "walk, then I will lengthen thy\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_15::
    .string "And Solomon awoke; and, behold, it\n"
    .string "was a dream. And he came to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and stood before the ark\l"
    .string "of the covenant of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "offered up burnt offerings, and\l"
    .string "offered peace offerings, and made a\l"
    .string "feast to all his servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_16::
    .string "Then came there two women, that were\n"
    .string "harlots, unto the king, and stood\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_17::
    .string "And the one woman said, O my lord, I\n"
    .string "and this woman dwell in one house;\l"
    .string "and I was delivered of a child with\l"
    .string "her in the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_18::
    .string "And it came to pass the third day\n"
    .string "after that I was delivered, that\l"
    .string "this woman was delivered also: and\l"
    .string "we were together; there was no\l"
    .string "stranger with us in the house, save\l"
    .string "we two in the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_19::
    .string "And this woman’s child died in the\n"
    .string "night; because she overlaid it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_20::
    .string "And she arose at midnight, and took\n"
    .string "my son from beside me, while thine\l"
    .string "handmaid slept, and laid it in her\l"
    .string "bosom, and laid her dead child in my\l"
    .string "bosom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_21::
    .string "And when I rose in the morning to\n"
    .string "give my child suck, behold, it was\l"
    .string "dead: but when I had considered it in\l"
    .string "the morning, behold, it was not my\l"
    .string "son, which I did bear.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_22::
    .string "And the other woman said, Nay; but\n"
    .string "the living is my son, and the dead is\l"
    .string "thy son. And this said, No; but the\l"
    .string "dead is thy son, and the living is my\l"
    .string "son. Thus they spake before the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_23::
    .string "Then said the king, The one saith,\n"
    .string "This is my son that liveth, and thy\l"
    .string "son is the dead: and the other saith,\l"
    .string "Nay; but thy son is the dead, and my\l"
    .string "son is the living.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_24::
    .string "And the king said, Bring me a sword.\n"
    .string "And they brought a sword before the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_25::
    .string "And the king said, Divide the\n"
    .string "living child in two, and give half\l"
    .string "to the one, and half to the other.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_26::
    .string "Then spake the woman whose the\n"
    .string "living child was unto the king, for\l"
    .string "her bowels yearned upon her son, and\l"
    .string "she said, O my lord, give her the\l"
    .string "living child, and in no wise slay\l"
    .string "it. But the other said, Let it be\l"
    .string "neither mine nor thine, but divide it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_27::
    .string "Then the king answered and said,\n"
    .string "Give her the living child, and in no\l"
    .string "wise slay it: she is the mother\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_3_28::
    .string "And all Israel heard of the\n"
    .string "judgment which the king had judged;\l"
    .string "and they feared the king: for they\l"
    .string "saw that the wisdom of God was in him,\l"
    .string "to do judgment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_1::
    .string "So king Solomon was king over all\n"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_2::
    .string "And these were the princes which he\n"
    .string "had; Azariah the son of Zadok the\l"
    .string "priest,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_3::
    .string "Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of\n"
    .string "Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son\l"
    .string "of Ahilud, the recorder$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_4::
    .string "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was\n"
    .string "over the host: and Zadok and Abiathar\l"
    .string "were the priests:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_5::
    .string "And Azariah the son of Nathan was\n"
    .string "over the officers: and Zabud the son\l"
    .string "of Nathan was principal officer,\l"
    .string "and the king’s friend:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_6::
    .string "And Ahishar was over the household:\n"
    .string "and Adoniram the son of Abda was over\l"
    .string "the tribute$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_7::
    .string "And Solomon had twelve officers\n"
    .string "over all Israel, which provided\l"
    .string "victuals for the king and his\l"
    .string "household: each man his month in a\l"
    .string "year made provision.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_8::
    .string "And these are their names: The son\n"
    .string "of Hur, in mount Ephraim:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_9::
    .string "The son of Dekar, in Makaz, and in\n"
    .string "Shaalbim, and Bethshemesh, and\l"
    .string "Elonbethhanan:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_10::
    .string "The son of Hesed, in Aruboth; to him\n"
    .string "pertained Sochoh, and all the land\l"
    .string "of Hepher:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_11::
    .string "The son of Abinadab, in all the\n"
    .string "region of Dor; which had Taphath the\l"
    .string "daughter of Solomon to wife:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_12::
    .string "Baana the son of Ahilud; to him\n"
    .string "pertained Taanach and Megiddo, and\l"
    .string "all Bethshean, which is by Zartanah\l"
    .string "beneath Jezreel, from Bethshean to\l"
    .string "Abelmeholah, even unto the place\l"
    .string "that is beyond Jokneam:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_13::
    .string "The son of Geber, in Ramothgilead;\n"
    .string "to him pertained the towns of Jair\l"
    .string "the son of Manasseh, which are in\l"
    .string "Gilead; to him also pertained the\l"
    .string "region of Argob, which is in Bashan,\l"
    .string "threescore great cities with walls\l"
    .string "and brasen bars:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_14::
    .string "Ahinadab the son of Iddo had\n"
    .string "Mahanaim:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_15::
    .string "Ahimaaz was in Naphtali; he also\n"
    .string "took Basmath the daughter of Solomon\l"
    .string "to wife:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_16::
    .string "Baanah the son of Hushai was in\n"
    .string "Asher and in Aloth:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_17::
    .string "Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in\n"
    .string "Issachar:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_18::
    .string "Shimei the son of Elah, in\n"
    .string "Benjamin:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_19::
    .string "Geber the son of Uri was in the\n"
    .string "country of Gilead, in the country of\l"
    .string "Sihon king of the Amorites, and of Og\l"
    .string "king of Bashan; and he was the only\l"
    .string "officer which was in the land$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_20::
    .string "Judah and Israel were many, as the\n"
    .string "sand which is by the sea in\l"
    .string "multitude, eating and drinking, and\l"
    .string "making merry.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_21::
    .string "And Solomon reigned over all\n"
    .string "kingdoms from the river unto the\l"
    .string "land of the Philistines, and unto\l"
    .string "the border of Egypt: they brought\l"
    .string "presents, and served Solomon all\l"
    .string "the days of his life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_22::
    .string "And Solomon’s provision for one\n"
    .string "day was thirty measures of fine\l"
    .string "flour, and threescore measures of\l"
    .string "meal,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_23::
    .string "Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of\n"
    .string "the pastures, and an hundred sheep,\l"
    .string "beside harts, and roebucks, and\l"
    .string "fallowdeer, and fatted fowl$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_24::
    .string "For he had dominion over all the\n"
    .string "region on this side the river, from\l"
    .string "Tiphsah even to Azzah, over all the\l"
    .string "kings on this side the river: and he\l"
    .string "had peace on all sides round about\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_25::
    .string "And Judah and Israel dwelt safely,\n"
    .string "every man under his vine and under\l"
    .string "his fig tree, from Dan even to\l"
    .string "Beersheba, all the days of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_26::
    .string "And Solomon had forty thousand\n"
    .string "stalls of horses for his chariots,\l"
    .string "and twelve thousand horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_27::
    .string "And those officers provided\n"
    .string "victual for king Solomon, and for\l"
    .string "all that came unto king Solomon’s\l"
    .string "table, every man in his month: they\l"
    .string "lacked nothing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_28::
    .string "Barley also and straw for the\n"
    .string "horses and dromedaries brought they\l"
    .string "unto the place where the officers\l"
    .string "were, every man according to his\l"
    .string "charge.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_29::
    .string "And God gave Solomon wisdom and\n"
    .string "understanding exceeding much, and\l"
    .string "largeness of heart, even as the sand\l"
    .string "that is on the sea shore.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_30::
    .string "And Solomon’s wisdom excelled the\n"
    .string "wisdom of all the children of the\l"
    .string "east country, and all the wisdom of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_31::
    .string "For he was wiser than all men; than\n"
    .string "Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and\l"
    .string "Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of\l"
    .string "Mahol: and his fame was in all\l"
    .string "nations round about.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_32::
    .string "And he spake three thousand\n"
    .string "proverbs: and his songs were a\l"
    .string "thousand and five.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_33::
    .string "And he spake of trees, from the\n"
    .string "cedar tree that is in Lebanon even\l"
    .string "unto the hyssop that springeth out\l"
    .string "of the wall: he spake also of\l"
    .string "beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping\l"
    .string "things, and of fishes.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_4_34::
    .string "And there came of all people to\n"
    .string "hear the wisdom of Solomon, from\l"
    .string "all kings of the earth, which had\l"
    .string "heard of his wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_1::
    .string "And Hiram king of Tyre sent his\n"
    .string "servants unto Solomon; for he had\l"
    .string "heard that they had anointed him king\l"
    .string "in the room of his father: for Hiram\l"
    .string "was ever a lover of David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_2::
    .string "And Solomon sent to Hiram, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_3::
    .string "Thou knowest how that David my\n"
    .string "father could not build an house\l"
    .string "unto the name of the LORD his God for\l"
    .string "the wars which were about him on\l"
    .string "every side, until the LORD put them\l"
    .string "under the soles of his feet$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_4::
    .string "But now the LORD my God hath given\n"
    .string "me rest on every side, so that there\l"
    .string "is neither adversary nor evil\l"
    .string "occurrent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_5::
    .string "And, behold, I purpose to build\n"
    .string "an house unto the name of the LORD my\l"
    .string "God, as the LORD spake unto David my\l"
    .string "father, saying, Thy son, whom I will\l"
    .string "set upon thy throne in thy room, he\l"
    .string "shall build an house unto my name.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_6::
    .string "Now therefore command thou that\n"
    .string "they hew me cedar trees out of\l"
    .string "Lebanon; and my servants shall be\l"
    .string "with thy servants: and unto thee\l"
    .string "will I give hire for thy servants\l"
    .string "according to all that thou shalt\l"
    .string "appoint: for thou knowest that\l"
    .string "there is not among us any that can\l"
    .string "skill to hew timber like unto the\l"
    .string "Sidonians.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_7::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Hiram\n"
    .string "heard the words of Solomon, that he\l"
    .string "rejoiced greatly, and said, Blessed\l"
    .string "be the LORD this day, which hath\l"
    .string "given unto David a wise son over this\l"
    .string "great people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_8::
    .string "And Hiram sent to Solomon, saying,\n"
    .string "I have considered the things which\l"
    .string "thou sentest to me for: and I will\l"
    .string "do all thy desire concerning timber\l"
    .string "of cedar, and concerning timber of\l"
    .string "fir.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_9::
    .string "My servants shall bring them down\n"
    .string "from Lebanon unto the sea: and I\l"
    .string "will convey them by sea in floats\l"
    .string "unto the place that thou shalt\l"
    .string "appoint me, and will cause them to\l"
    .string "be discharged there, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "receive them: and thou shalt\l"
    .string "accomplish my desire, in giving\l"
    .string "food for my household.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_10::
    .string "So Hiram gave Solomon cedar trees\n"
    .string "and fir trees according to all his\l"
    .string "desire.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_11::
    .string "And Solomon gave Hiram twenty\n"
    .string "thousand measures of wheat for food\l"
    .string "to his household, and twenty\l"
    .string "measures of pure oil: thus gave\l"
    .string "Solomon to Hiram year by year.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_12::
    .string "And the LORD gave Solomon wisdom,\n"
    .string "as he promised him: and there was\l"
    .string "peace between Hiram and Solomon; and\l"
    .string "they two made a league together.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_13::
    .string "And king Solomon raised a levy out\n"
    .string "of all Israel; and the levy was\l"
    .string "thirty thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_14::
    .string "And he sent them to Lebanon, ten\n"
    .string "thousand a month by courses: a month\l"
    .string "they were in Lebanon, and two months\l"
    .string "at home: and Adoniram was over the\l"
    .string "levy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_15::
    .string "And Solomon had threescore and ten\n"
    .string "thousand that bare burdens, and\l"
    .string "fourscore thousand hewers in the\l"
    .string "mountains;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_16::
    .string "Beside the chief of Solomon’s\n"
    .string "officers which were over the work,\l"
    .string "three thousand and three hundred,\l"
    .string "which ruled over the people that\l"
    .string "wrought in the work$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_17::
    .string "And the king commanded, and they\n"
    .string "brought great stones, costly stones,\l"
    .string "and hewed stones, to lay the\l"
    .string "foundation of the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_5_18::
    .string "And Solomon’s builders and Hiram’s\n"
    .string "builders did hew them, and the\l"
    .string "stonesquarers: so they prepared\l"
    .string "timber and stones to build the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the four\n"
    .string "hundred and eightieth year after the\l"
    .string "children of Israel were come out of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt, in the fourth\l"
    .string "year of Solomon’s reign over\l"
    .string "Israel, in the month Zif, which is\l"
    .string "the second month, that he began to\l"
    .string "build the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_2::
    .string "And the house which king Solomon\n"
    .string "built for the LORD, the length\l"
    .string "thereof was threescore cubits, and\l"
    .string "the breadth thereof twenty cubits,\l"
    .string "and the height thereof thirty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_3::
    .string "And the porch before the temple of\n"
    .string "the house, twenty cubits was the\l"
    .string "length thereof, according to the\l"
    .string "breadth of the house; and ten cubits\l"
    .string "was the breadth thereof before the\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_4::
    .string "And for the house he made windows of\n"
    .string "narrow lights.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_5::
    .string "And against the wall of the house\n"
    .string "he built chambers round about,\l"
    .string "against the walls of the house\l"
    .string "round about, both of the temple and\l"
    .string "of the oracle: and he made chambers\l"
    .string "round about:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_6::
    .string "The nethermost chamber was five\n"
    .string "cubits broad, and the middle was six\l"
    .string "cubits broad, and the third was seven\l"
    .string "cubits broad: for without in the\l"
    .string "wall of the house he made narrowed\l"
    .string "rests round about, that the beams\l"
    .string "should not be fastened in the walls\l"
    .string "of the house$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_7::
    .string "And the house, when it was in\n"
    .string "building, was built of stone made\l"
    .string "ready before it was brought thither:\l"
    .string "so that there was neither hammer nor\l"
    .string "axe nor any tool of iron heard in the\l"
    .string "house, while it was in building.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_8::
    .string "The door for the middle chamber was\n"
    .string "in the right side of the house: and\l"
    .string "they went up with winding stairs\l"
    .string "into the middle chamber, and out of\l"
    .string "the middle into the third.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_9::
    .string "So he built the house, and finished\n"
    .string "it; and covered the house with beams\l"
    .string "and boards of cedar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_10::
    .string "And then he built chambers against\n"
    .string "all the house, five cubits high: and\l"
    .string "they rested on the house with timber\l"
    .string "of cedar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_11::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Solomon, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_12::
    .string "Concerning this house which thou\n"
    .string "art in building, if thou wilt walk\l"
    .string "in my statutes, and execute my\l"
    .string "judgments, and keep all my\l"
    .string "commandments to walk in them; then\l"
    .string "will I perform my word with thee,\l"
    .string "which I spake unto David thy father:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_13::
    .string "And I will dwell among the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, and will not\l"
    .string "forsake my people Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_14::
    .string "So Solomon built the house, and\n"
    .string "finished it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_15::
    .string "And he built the walls of the\n"
    .string "house within with boards of cedar,\l"
    .string "both the floor of the house, and the\l"
    .string "walls of the ceiling: and he\l"
    .string "covered them on the inside with wood,\l"
    .string "and covered the floor of the house\l"
    .string "with planks of fir.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_16::
    .string "And he built twenty cubits on the\n"
    .string "sides of the house, both the floor\l"
    .string "and the walls with boards of cedar:\l"
    .string "he even built them for it within,\l"
    .string "even for the oracle, even for the\l"
    .string "most holy place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_17::
    .string "And the house, that is, the temple\n"
    .string "before it, was forty cubits long.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_18::
    .string "And the cedar of the house within\n"
    .string "was carved with knops and open\l"
    .string "flowers: all was cedar; there was\l"
    .string "no stone seen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_19::
    .string "And the oracle he prepared in the\n"
    .string "house within, to set there the ark of\l"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_20::
    .string "And the oracle in the forepart was\n"
    .string "twenty cubits in length, and twenty\l"
    .string "cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits\l"
    .string "in the height thereof: and he\l"
    .string "overlaid it with pure gold; and so\l"
    .string "covered the altar which was of cedar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_21::
    .string "So Solomon overlaid the house\n"
    .string "within with pure gold: and he made a\l"
    .string "partition by the chains of gold\l"
    .string "before the oracle; and he overlaid\l"
    .string "it with gold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_22::
    .string "And the whole house he overlaid\n"
    .string "with gold, until he had finished\l"
    .string "all the house: also the whole\l"
    .string "altar that was by the oracle he\l"
    .string "overlaid with gold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_23::
    .string "And within the oracle he made two\n"
    .string "cherubims of olive tree, each ten\l"
    .string "cubits high.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_24::
    .string "And five cubits was the one wing of\n"
    .string "the cherub, and five cubits the other\l"
    .string "wing of the cherub: from the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of the one wing unto\l"
    .string "the uttermost part of the other were\l"
    .string "ten cubits.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_25::
    .string "And the other cherub was ten cubits:\n"
    .string "both the cherubims were of one\l"
    .string "measure and one size.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_26::
    .string "The height of the one cherub was ten\n"
    .string "cubits, and so was it of the other\l"
    .string "cherub.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_27::
    .string "And he set the cherubims within the\n"
    .string "inner house: and they stretched forth\l"
    .string "the wings of the cherubims, so that\l"
    .string "the wing of the one touched the one\l"
    .string "wall, and the wing of the other\l"
    .string "cherub touched the other wall; and\l"
    .string "their wings touched one another in\l"
    .string "the midst of the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_28::
    .string "And he overlaid the cherubims with\n"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_29::
    .string "And he carved all the walls of\n"
    .string "the house round about with carved\l"
    .string "figures of cherubims and palm trees\l"
    .string "and open flowers, within and\l"
    .string "without.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_30::
    .string "And the floors of the house he\n"
    .string "overlaid with gold, within and\l"
    .string "without.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_31::
    .string "And for the entering of the oracle\n"
    .string "he made doors of olive tree: the\l"
    .string "lintel and side posts were a fifth\l"
    .string "part of the wall.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_32::
    .string "The two doors also were of olive\n"
    .string "tree; and he carved upon them\l"
    .string "carvings of cherubims and palm\l"
    .string "trees and open flowers, and\l"
    .string "overlaid them with gold, and spread\l"
    .string "gold upon the cherubims, and upon\l"
    .string "the palm trees.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_33::
    .string "So also made he for the door of the\n"
    .string "temple posts of olive tree, a\l"
    .string "fourth part of the wall.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_34::
    .string "And the two doors were of fir tree:\n"
    .string "the two leaves of the one door were\l"
    .string "folding, and the two leaves of the\l"
    .string "other door were folding.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_35::
    .string "And he carved thereon cherubims and\n"
    .string "palm trees and open flowers: and\l"
    .string "covered them with gold fitted upon\l"
    .string "the carved work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_36::
    .string "And he built the inner court with\n"
    .string "three rows of hewed stone, and a row\l"
    .string "of cedar beams.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_37::
    .string "In the fourth year was the\n"
    .string "foundation of the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "laid, in the month Zif:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_6_38::
    .string "And in the eleventh year, in the\n"
    .string "month Bul, which is the eighth\l"
    .string "month, was the house finished\l"
    .string "throughout all the parts thereof,\l"
    .string "and according to all the fashion of\l"
    .string "it. So was he seven years in building\l"
    .string "it$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_1::
    .string "But Solomon was building his own\n"
    .string "house thirteen years, and he finished\l"
    .string "all his house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_2::
    .string "He built also the house of the\n"
    .string "forest of Lebanon; the length\l"
    .string "thereof was an hundred cubits, and\l"
    .string "the breadth thereof fifty cubits, and\l"
    .string "the height thereof thirty cubits,\l"
    .string "upon four rows of cedar pillars,\l"
    .string "with cedar beams upon the pillars.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_3::
    .string "And it was covered with cedar above\n"
    .string "upon the beams, that lay on forty\l"
    .string "five pillars, fifteen in a row.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_4::
    .string "And there were windows in three\n"
    .string "rows, and light was against light in\l"
    .string "three ranks.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_5::
    .string "And all the doors and posts were\n"
    .string "square, with the windows: and light\l"
    .string "was against light in three ranks.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_6::
    .string "And he made a porch of pillars;\n"
    .string "the length thereof was fifty cubits,\l"
    .string "and the breadth thereof thirty\l"
    .string "cubits: and the porch was before\l"
    .string "them: and the other pillars and the\l"
    .string "thick beam were before them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_7::
    .string "Then he made a porch for the throne\n"
    .string "where he might judge, even the porch\l"
    .string "of judgment: and it was covered with\l"
    .string "cedar from one side of the floor to\l"
    .string "the other.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_8::
    .string "And his house where he dwelt had\n"
    .string "another court within the porch,\l"
    .string "which was of the like work. Solomon\l"
    .string "made also an house for Pharaoh’s\l"
    .string "daughter, whom he had taken to wife,\l"
    .string "like unto this porch.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_9::
    .string "All these were of costly stones,\n"
    .string "according to the measures of hewed\l"
    .string "stones, sawed with saws, within and\l"
    .string "without, even from the foundation\l"
    .string "unto the coping, and so on the\l"
    .string "outside toward the great court.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_10::
    .string "And the foundation was of costly\n"
    .string "stones, even great stones, stones of\l"
    .string "ten cubits, and stones of eight\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_11::
    .string "And above were costly stones, after\n"
    .string "the measures of hewed stones, and\l"
    .string "cedars.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_12::
    .string "And the great court round about was\n"
    .string "with three rows of hewed stones, and\l"
    .string "a row of cedar beams, both for the\l"
    .string "inner court of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and for the porch of the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_13::
    .string "And king Solomon sent and fetched\n"
    .string "Hiram out of Tyre.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_14::
    .string "He was a widow’s son of the tribe of\n"
    .string "Naphtali, and his father was a man\l"
    .string "of Tyre, a worker in brass: and he was\l"
    .string "filled with wisdom, and\l"
    .string "understanding, and cunning to work\l"
    .string "all works in brass. And he came to\l"
    .string "king Solomon, and wrought all his\l"
    .string "work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_15::
    .string "For he cast two pillars of brass,\n"
    .string "of eighteen cubits high apiece: and\l"
    .string "a line of twelve cubits did compass\l"
    .string "either of them about.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_16::
    .string "And he made two chapiters of\n"
    .string "molten brass, to set upon the tops\l"
    .string "of the pillars: the height of the\l"
    .string "one chapiter was five cubits, and\l"
    .string "the height of the other chapiter was\l"
    .string "five cubits:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_17::
    .string "And nets of checker work, and\n"
    .string "wreaths of chain work, for the\l"
    .string "chapiters which were upon the top\l"
    .string "of the pillars; seven for the one\l"
    .string "chapiter, and seven for the other\l"
    .string "chapiter$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_18::
    .string "And he made the pillars, and two\n"
    .string "rows round about upon the one\l"
    .string "network, to cover the chapiters that\l"
    .string "were upon the top, with\l"
    .string "pomegranates: and so did he for the\l"
    .string "other chapiter.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_19::
    .string "And the chapiters that were upon\n"
    .string "the top of the pillars were of\l"
    .string "lily work in the porch, four cubits.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_20::
    .string "And the chapiters upon the two\n"
    .string "pillars had pomegranates also\l"
    .string "above, over against the belly which\l"
    .string "was by the network: and the\l"
    .string "pomegranates were two hundred in\l"
    .string "rows round about upon the other\l"
    .string "chapiter.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_21::
    .string "And he set up the pillars in the\n"
    .string "porch of the temple: and he set up\l"
    .string "the right pillar, and called the\l"
    .string "name thereof Jachin: and he set up\l"
    .string "the left pillar, and called the\l"
    .string "name thereof Boaz.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_22::
    .string "And upon the top of the pillars\n"
    .string "was lily work: so was the work of\l"
    .string "the pillars finished.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_23::
    .string "And he made a molten sea, ten cubits\n"
    .string "from the one brim to the other: it was\l"
    .string "round all about, and his height was\l"
    .string "five cubits: and a line of thirty\l"
    .string "cubits did compass it round about.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_24::
    .string "And under the brim of it round about\n"
    .string "there were knops compassing it, ten\l"
    .string "in a cubit, compassing the sea round\l"
    .string "about: the knops were cast in two\l"
    .string "rows, when it was cast.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_25::
    .string "It stood upon twelve oxen, three\n"
    .string "looking toward the north, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the west, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the south, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the east: and the sea\l"
    .string "was set above upon them, and all\l"
    .string "their hinder parts were inward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_26::
    .string "And it was an hand breadth thick,\n"
    .string "and the brim thereof was wrought\l"
    .string "like the brim of a cup, with flowers\l"
    .string "of lilies: it contained two\l"
    .string "thousand baths.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_27::
    .string "And he made ten bases of brass; four\n"
    .string "cubits was the length of one base,\l"
    .string "and four cubits the breadth thereof,\l"
    .string "and three cubits the height of it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_28::
    .string "And the work of the bases was on\n"
    .string "this manner: they had borders, and\l"
    .string "the borders were between the ledges:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_29::
    .string "And on the borders that were between\n"
    .string "the ledges were lions, oxen, and\l"
    .string "cherubims: and upon the ledges\l"
    .string "there was a base above: and beneath\l"
    .string "the lions and oxen were certain\l"
    .string "additions made of thin work$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_30::
    .string "And every base had four brasen\n"
    .string "wheels, and plates of brass: and\l"
    .string "the four corners thereof had\l"
    .string "undersetters: under the laver were\l"
    .string "undersetters molten, at the side of\l"
    .string "every addition.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_31::
    .string "And the mouth of it within the\n"
    .string "chapiter and above was a cubit: but\l"
    .string "the mouth thereof was round after the\l"
    .string "work of the base, a cubit and an\l"
    .string "half: and also upon the mouth of it\l"
    .string "were gravings with their borders,\l"
    .string "foursquare, not round.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_32::
    .string "And under the borders were four\n"
    .string "wheels; and the axletrees of the\l"
    .string "wheels were joined to the base: and\l"
    .string "the height of a wheel was a cubit and\l"
    .string "half a cubit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_33::
    .string "And the work of the wheels was like\n"
    .string "the work of a chariot wheel: their\l"
    .string "axletrees, and their naves, and\l"
    .string "their felloes, and their spokes,\l"
    .string "were all molten.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_34::
    .string "And there were four undersetters to\n"
    .string "the four corners of one base: and the\l"
    .string "undersetters were of the very base\l"
    .string "itself.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_35::
    .string "And in the top of the base was there\n"
    .string "a round compass of half a cubit\l"
    .string "high: and on the top of the base the\l"
    .string "ledges thereof and the borders\l"
    .string "thereof were of the same.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_36::
    .string "For on the plates of the ledges\n"
    .string "thereof, and on the borders thereof,\l"
    .string "he graved cherubims, lions, and\l"
    .string "palm trees, according to the\l"
    .string "proportion of every one, and\l"
    .string "additions round about.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_37::
    .string "After this manner he made the ten\n"
    .string "bases: all of them had one casting,\l"
    .string "one measure, and one size.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_38::
    .string "Then made he ten lavers of brass:\n"
    .string "one laver contained forty baths: and\l"
    .string "every laver was four cubits: and\l"
    .string "upon every one of the ten bases one\l"
    .string "laver.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_39::
    .string "And he put five bases on the right\n"
    .string "side of the house, and five on the\l"
    .string "left side of the house: and he set the\l"
    .string "sea on the right side of the house\l"
    .string "eastward over against the south.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_40::
    .string "And Hiram made the lavers, and the\n"
    .string "shovels, and the basons. So Hiram\l"
    .string "made an end of doing all the work\l"
    .string "that he made king Solomon for the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_41::
    .string "The two pillars, and the two\n"
    .string "bowls of the chapiters that were on\l"
    .string "the top of the two pillars; and the\l"
    .string "two networks, to cover the two bowls\l"
    .string "of the chapiters which were upon\l"
    .string "the top of the pillars;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_42::
    .string "And four hundred pomegranates for\n"
    .string "the two networks, even two rows of\l"
    .string "pomegranates for one network, to\l"
    .string "cover the two bowls of the\l"
    .string "chapiters that were upon the\l"
    .string "pillars;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_43::
    .string "And the ten bases, and ten lavers on\n"
    .string "the bases;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_44::
    .string "And one sea, and twelve oxen under\n"
    .string "the sea;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_45::
    .string "And the pots, and the shovels, and\n"
    .string "the basons: and all these vessels,\l"
    .string "which Hiram made to king Solomon for\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, were of bright\l"
    .string "brass$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_46::
    .string "In the plain of Jordan did the king\n"
    .string "cast them, in the clay ground\l"
    .string "between Succoth and Zarthan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_47::
    .string "And Solomon left all the vessels\n"
    .string "unweighed, because they were\l"
    .string "exceeding many: neither was the\l"
    .string "weight of the brass found out.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_48::
    .string "And Solomon made all the vessels\n"
    .string "that pertained unto the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD: the altar of gold, and the\l"
    .string "table of gold, whereupon the\l"
    .string "shewbread was,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_49::
    .string "And the candlesticks of pure gold,\n"
    .string "five on the right side, and five on\l"
    .string "the left, before the oracle, with\l"
    .string "the flowers, and the lamps, and the\l"
    .string "tongs of gold,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_50::
    .string "And the bowls, and the snuffers,\n"
    .string "and the basons, and the spoons, and\l"
    .string "the censers of pure gold; and the\l"
    .string "hinges of gold, both for the doors of\l"
    .string "the inner house, the most holy\l"
    .string "place, and for the doors of the\l"
    .string "house, to wit, of the temple$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_7_51::
    .string "So was ended all the work that king\n"
    .string "Solomon made for the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD. And Solomon brought in the\l"
    .string "things which David his father had\l"
    .string "dedicated; even the silver, and the\l"
    .string "gold, and the vessels, did he put\l"
    .string "among the treasures of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_1::
    .string "Then Solomon assembled the elders\n"
    .string "of Israel, and all the heads of the\l"
    .string "tribes, the chief of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, unto king\l"
    .string "Solomon in Jerusalem, that they\l"
    .string "might bring up the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD out of the city\l"
    .string "of David, which is Zion.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_2::
    .string "And all the men of Israel\n"
    .string "assembled themselves unto king\l"
    .string "Solomon at the feast in the month\l"
    .string "Ethanim, which is the seventh month.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_3::
    .string "And all the elders of Israel\n"
    .string "came, and the priests took up the\l"
    .string "ark.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_4::
    .string "And they brought up the ark of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and all the holy\l"
    .string "vessels that were in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, even those did the\l"
    .string "priests and the Levites bring up.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_5::
    .string "And king Solomon, and all the\n"
    .string "congregation of Israel, that were\l"
    .string "assembled unto him, were with him\l"
    .string "before the ark, sacrificing sheep\l"
    .string "and oxen, that could not be told nor\l"
    .string "numbered for multitude.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_6::
    .string "And the priests brought in the ark\n"
    .string "of the covenant of the LORD unto his\l"
    .string "place, into the oracle of the house,\l"
    .string "to the most holy place, even under\l"
    .string "the wings of the cherubims.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_7::
    .string "For the cherubims spread forth\n"
    .string "their two wings over the place of\l"
    .string "the ark, and the cherubims covered\l"
    .string "the ark and the staves thereof above.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_8::
    .string "And they drew out the staves, that\n"
    .string "the ends of the staves were seen out\l"
    .string "in the holy place before the\l"
    .string "oracle, and they were not seen\l"
    .string "without: and there they are unto this\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_9::
    .string "There was nothing in the ark save\n"
    .string "the two tables of stone, which Moses\l"
    .string "put there at Horeb, when the LORD\l"
    .string "made a covenant with the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, when they came out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "priests were come out of the holy\l"
    .string "place, that the cloud filled the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_11::
    .string "So that the priests could not\n"
    .string "stand to minister because of the\l"
    .string "cloud: for the glory of the LORD had\l"
    .string "filled the house of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_12::
    .string "Then spake Solomon, The LORD said\n"
    .string "that he would dwell in the thick\l"
    .string "darkness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_13::
    .string "I have surely built thee an house\n"
    .string "to dwell in, a settled place for\l"
    .string "thee to abide in for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_14::
    .string "And the king turned his face about,\n"
    .string "and blessed all the congregation\l"
    .string "of Israel: (and all the\l"
    .string "congregation of Israel stood;)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_15::
    .string "And he said, Blessed be the LORD God\n"
    .string "of Israel, which spake with his\l"
    .string "mouth unto David my father, and hath\l"
    .string "with his hand fulfilled it, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_16::
    .string "Since the day that I brought forth\n"
    .string "my people Israel out of Egypt, I\l"
    .string "chose no city out of all the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel to build an house, that my\l"
    .string "name might be therein; but I chose\l"
    .string "David to be over my people Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_17::
    .string "And it was in the heart of David my\n"
    .string "father to build an house for the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_18::
    .string "And the LORD said unto David my\n"
    .string "father, Whereas it was in thine heart\l"
    .string "to build an house unto my name, thou\l"
    .string "didst well that it was in thine\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_19::
    .string "Nevertheless thou shalt not build\n"
    .string "the house; but thy son that shall\l"
    .string "come forth out of thy loins, he\l"
    .string "shall build the house unto my name.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_20::
    .string "And the LORD hath performed his\n"
    .string "word that he spake, and I am risen\l"
    .string "up in the room of David my father,\l"
    .string "and sit on the throne of Israel, as\l"
    .string "the LORD promised, and have built an\l"
    .string "house for the name of the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_21::
    .string "And I have set there a place for\n"
    .string "the ark, wherein is the covenant of\l"
    .string "the LORD, which he made with our\l"
    .string "fathers, when he brought them out of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_22::
    .string "And Solomon stood before the altar\n"
    .string "of the LORD in the presence of all\l"
    .string "the congregation of Israel, and\l"
    .string "spread forth his hands toward\l"
    .string "heaven:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_23::
    .string "And he said, LORD God of Israel,\n"
    .string "there is no God like thee, in heaven\l"
    .string "above, or on earth beneath, who\l"
    .string "keepest covenant and mercy with thy\l"
    .string "servants that walk before thee with\l"
    .string "all their heart:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_24::
    .string "Who hast kept with thy servant\n"
    .string "David my father that thou promisedst\l"
    .string "him: thou spakest also with thy\l"
    .string "mouth, and hast fulfilled it with\l"
    .string "thine hand, as it is this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_25::
    .string "Therefore now, LORD God of Israel,\n"
    .string "keep with thy servant David my\l"
    .string "father that thou promisedst him,\l"
    .string "saying, There shall not fail thee a\l"
    .string "man in my sight to sit on the throne\l"
    .string "of Israel; so that thy children take\l"
    .string "heed to their way, that they walk\l"
    .string "before me as thou hast walked before\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_26::
    .string "And now, O God of Israel, let thy\n"
    .string "word, I pray thee, be verified, which\l"
    .string "thou spakest unto thy servant David\l"
    .string "my father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_27::
    .string "But will God indeed dwell on the\n"
    .string "earth? behold, the heaven and heaven\l"
    .string "of heavens cannot contain thee; how\l"
    .string "much less this house that I have\l"
    .string "builded?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_28::
    .string "Yet have thou respect unto the\n"
    .string "prayer of thy servant, and to his\l"
    .string "supplication, O LORD my God, to\l"
    .string "hearken unto the cry and to the\l"
    .string "prayer, which thy servant prayeth\l"
    .string "before thee to day:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_29::
    .string "That thine eyes may be open toward\n"
    .string "this house night and day, even toward\l"
    .string "the place of which thou hast said,\l"
    .string "My name shall be there: that thou\l"
    .string "mayest hearken unto the prayer which\l"
    .string "thy servant shall make toward this\l"
    .string "place$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_30::
    .string "And hearken thou to the\n"
    .string "supplication of thy servant, and of\l"
    .string "thy people Israel, when they\l"
    .string "shall pray toward this place: and\l"
    .string "hear thou in heaven thy dwelling\l"
    .string "place: and when thou hearest,\l"
    .string "forgive.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_31::
    .string "If any man trespass against his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and an oath be laid upon\l"
    .string "him to cause him to swear, and the\l"
    .string "oath come before thine altar in this\l"
    .string "house:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_32::
    .string "Then hear thou in heaven, and do,\n"
    .string "and judge thy servants, condemning\l"
    .string "the wicked, to bring his way upon his\l"
    .string "head; and justifying the righteous,\l"
    .string "to give him according to his\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_33::
    .string "When thy people Israel be smitten\n"
    .string "down before the enemy, because they\l"
    .string "have sinned against thee, and shall\l"
    .string "turn again to thee, and confess thy\l"
    .string "name, and pray, and make\l"
    .string "supplication unto thee in this\l"
    .string "house:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_34::
    .string "Then hear thou in heaven, and\n"
    .string "forgive the sin of thy people\l"
    .string "Israel, and bring them again unto\l"
    .string "the land which thou gavest unto\l"
    .string "their fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_35::
    .string "When heaven is shut up, and there is\n"
    .string "no rain, because they have sinned\l"
    .string "against thee; if they pray toward\l"
    .string "this place, and confess thy name,\l"
    .string "and turn from their sin, when thou\l"
    .string "afflictest them:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_36::
    .string "Then hear thou in heaven, and\n"
    .string "forgive the sin of thy servants, and\l"
    .string "of thy people Israel, that thou\l"
    .string "teach them the good way wherein they\l"
    .string "should walk, and give rain upon thy\l"
    .string "land, which thou hast given to thy\l"
    .string "people for an inheritance$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_37::
    .string "If there be in the land famine, if\n"
    .string "there be pestilence, blasting,\l"
    .string "mildew, locust, or if there be\l"
    .string "caterpiller; if their enemy\l"
    .string "besiege them in the land of their\l"
    .string "cities; whatsoever plague,\l"
    .string "whatsoever sickness there be;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_38::
    .string "What prayer and supplication\n"
    .string "soever be made by any man, or by all\l"
    .string "thy people Israel, which shall\l"
    .string "know every man the plague of his own\l"
    .string "heart, and spread forth his hands\l"
    .string "toward this house:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_39::
    .string "Then hear thou in heaven thy\n"
    .string "dwelling place, and forgive, and\l"
    .string "do, and give to every man according\l"
    .string "to his ways, whose heart thou\l"
    .string "knowest; (for thou, even thou only,\l"
    .string "knowest the hearts of all the\l"
    .string "children of men;)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_40::
    .string "That they may fear thee all the\n"
    .string "days that they live in the land\l"
    .string "which thou gavest unto our fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_41::
    .string "Moreover concerning a stranger,\n"
    .string "that is not of thy people Israel,\l"
    .string "but cometh out of a far country for\l"
    .string "thy name’s sake;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_42::
    .string "(For they shall hear of thy great\n"
    .string "name, and of thy strong hand, and of\l"
    .string "thy stretched out arm;) when he\l"
    .string "shall come and pray toward this\l"
    .string "house;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_43::
    .string "Hear thou in heaven thy dwelling\n"
    .string "place, and do according to all that\l"
    .string "the stranger calleth to thee for:\l"
    .string "that all people of the earth may\l"
    .string "know thy name, to fear thee, as do thy\l"
    .string "people Israel; and that they may\l"
    .string "know that this house, which I have\l"
    .string "builded, is called by thy name$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_44::
    .string "If thy people go out to battle\n"
    .string "against their enemy, whithersoever\l"
    .string "thou shalt send them, and shall\l"
    .string "pray unto the LORD toward the city\l"
    .string "which thou hast chosen, and toward\l"
    .string "the house that I have built for thy\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_45::
    .string "Then hear thou in heaven their\n"
    .string "prayer and their supplication, and\l"
    .string "maintain their cause$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_46::
    .string "If they sin against thee, (for there\n"
    .string "is no man that sinneth not,) and thou\l"
    .string "be angry with them, and deliver them\l"
    .string "to the enemy, so that they carry them\l"
    .string "away captives unto the land of the\l"
    .string "enemy, far or near;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_47::
    .string "Yet if they shall bethink\n"
    .string "themselves in the land whither they\l"
    .string "were carried captives, and repent,\l"
    .string "and make supplication unto thee in\l"
    .string "the land of them that carried them\l"
    .string "captives, saying, We have sinned,\l"
    .string "and have done perversely, we have\l"
    .string "committed wickedness;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_48::
    .string "And so return unto thee with all\n"
    .string "their heart, and with all their\l"
    .string "soul, in the land of their enemies,\l"
    .string "which led them away captive, and\l"
    .string "pray unto thee toward their land,\l"
    .string "which thou gavest unto their fathers,\l"
    .string "the city which thou hast chosen, and\l"
    .string "the house which I have built for thy\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_49::
    .string "Then hear thou their prayer and\n"
    .string "their supplication in heaven thy\l"
    .string "dwelling place, and maintain their\l"
    .string "cause,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_50::
    .string "And forgive thy people that have\n"
    .string "sinned against thee, and all their\l"
    .string "transgressions wherein they have\l"
    .string "transgressed against thee, and give\l"
    .string "them compassion before them who\l"
    .string "carried them captive, that they may\l"
    .string "have compassion on them:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_51::
    .string "For they be thy people, and thine\n"
    .string "inheritance, which thou broughtest\l"
    .string "forth out of Egypt, from the midst of\l"
    .string "the furnace of iron:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_52::
    .string "That thine eyes may be open unto\n"
    .string "the supplication of thy servant,\l"
    .string "and unto the supplication of thy\l"
    .string "people Israel, to hearken unto them\l"
    .string "in all that they call for unto thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_53::
    .string "For thou didst separate them from\n"
    .string "among all the people of the earth,\l"
    .string "to be thine inheritance, as thou\l"
    .string "spakest by the hand of Moses thy\l"
    .string "servant, when thou broughtest our\l"
    .string "fathers out of Egypt, O LORD God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_54::
    .string "And it was so, that when Solomon had\n"
    .string "made an end of praying all this\l"
    .string "prayer and supplication unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, he arose from before the altar\l"
    .string "of the LORD, from kneeling on his\l"
    .string "knees with his hands spread up to\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_55::
    .string "And he stood, and blessed all the\n"
    .string "congregation of Israel with a loud\l"
    .string "voice, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_56::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD, that hath\n"
    .string "given rest unto his people Israel,\l"
    .string "according to all that he promised:\l"
    .string "there hath not failed one word of\l"
    .string "all his good promise, which he\l"
    .string "promised by the hand of Moses his\l"
    .string "servant$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_57::
    .string "The LORD our God be with us, as he\n"
    .string "was with our fathers: let him not\l"
    .string "leave us, nor forsake us:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_58::
    .string "That he may incline our hearts unto\n"
    .string "him, to walk in all his ways, and to\l"
    .string "keep his commandments, and his\l"
    .string "statutes, and his judgments, which he\l"
    .string "commanded our fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_59::
    .string "And let these my words, wherewith I\n"
    .string "have made supplication before the\l"
    .string "LORD, be nigh unto the LORD our God\l"
    .string "day and night, that he maintain the\l"
    .string "cause of his servant, and the cause\l"
    .string "of his people Israel at all\l"
    .string "times, as the matter shall require:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_60::
    .string "That all the people of the earth\n"
    .string "may know that the LORD is God, and\l"
    .string "that there is none else$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_61::
    .string "Let your heart therefore be perfect\n"
    .string "with the LORD our God, to walk in his\l"
    .string "statutes, and to keep his\l"
    .string "commandments, as at this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_62::
    .string "And the king, and all Israel with\n"
    .string "him, offered sacrifice before the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_63::
    .string "And Solomon offered a sacrifice of\n"
    .string "peace offerings, which he offered\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, two and twenty\l"
    .string "thousand oxen, and an hundred and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand sheep. So the king\l"
    .string "and all the children of Israel\l"
    .string "dedicated the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_64::
    .string "The same day did the king hallow\n"
    .string "the middle of the court that was\l"
    .string "before the house of the LORD: for\l"
    .string "there he offered burnt offerings, and\l"
    .string "meat offerings, and the fat of the\l"
    .string "peace offerings: because the brasen\l"
    .string "altar that was before the LORD was\l"
    .string "too little to receive the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings, and meat offerings, and\l"
    .string "the fat of the peace offerings.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_65::
    .string "And at that time Solomon held a\n"
    .string "feast, and all Israel with him, a\l"
    .string "great congregation, from the\l"
    .string "entering in of Hamath unto the river\l"
    .string "of Egypt, before the LORD our God,\l"
    .string "seven days and seven days, even\l"
    .string "fourteen days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_8_66::
    .string "On the eighth day he sent the\n"
    .string "people away: and they blessed the\l"
    .string "king, and went unto their tents\l"
    .string "joyful and glad of heart for all\l"
    .string "the goodness that the LORD had done\l"
    .string "for David his servant, and for\l"
    .string "Israel his people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Solomon\n"
    .string "had finished the building of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and all Solomon’s desire\l"
    .string "which he was pleased to do,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_2::
    .string "That the LORD appeared to Solomon\n"
    .string "the second time, as he had appeared\l"
    .string "unto him at Gibeon$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_3::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, I have\n"
    .string "heard thy prayer and thy\l"
    .string "supplication, that thou hast made\l"
    .string "before me: I have hallowed this\l"
    .string "house, which thou hast built, to put\l"
    .string "my name there for ever; and mine eyes\l"
    .string "and mine heart shall be there\l"
    .string "perpetually.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_4::
    .string "And if thou wilt walk before me, as\n"
    .string "David thy father walked, in\l"
    .string "integrity of heart, and in\l"
    .string "uprightness, to do according to all\l"
    .string "that I have commanded thee, and wilt\l"
    .string "keep my statutes and my judgments:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_5::
    .string "Then I will establish the throne\n"
    .string "of thy kingdom upon Israel for ever,\l"
    .string "as I promised to David thy father,\l"
    .string "saying, There shall not fail thee a\l"
    .string "man upon the throne of Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_6::
    .string "But if ye shall at all turn from\n"
    .string "following me, ye or your children,\l"
    .string "and will not keep my commandments\l"
    .string "and my statutes which I have set\l"
    .string "before you, but go and serve other\l"
    .string "gods, and worship them:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_7::
    .string "Then will I cut off Israel out of\n"
    .string "the land which I have given them; and\l"
    .string "this house, which I have hallowed\l"
    .string "for my name, will I cast out of my\l"
    .string "sight; and Israel shall be a\l"
    .string "proverb and a byword among all\l"
    .string "people:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_8::
    .string "And at this house, which is high,\n"
    .string "every one that passeth by it shall\l"
    .string "be astonished, and shall hiss; and\l"
    .string "they shall say, Why hath the LORD\l"
    .string "done thus unto this land, and to this\l"
    .string "house?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_9::
    .string "And they shall answer, Because\n"
    .string "they forsook the LORD their God, who\l"
    .string "brought forth their fathers out of\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt, and have taken\l"
    .string "hold upon other gods, and have\l"
    .string "worshipped them, and served them:\l"
    .string "therefore hath the LORD brought upon\l"
    .string "them all this evil$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_10::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "twenty years, when Solomon had\l"
    .string "built the two houses, the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and the king’s house,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_11::
    .string "(Now Hiram the king of Tyre had\n"
    .string "furnished Solomon with cedar trees\l"
    .string "and fir trees, and with gold,\l"
    .string "according to all his desire,) that\l"
    .string "then king Solomon gave Hiram twenty\l"
    .string "cities in the land of Galilee$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_12::
    .string "And Hiram came out from Tyre to see\n"
    .string "the cities which Solomon had given\l"
    .string "him; and they pleased him not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_13::
    .string "And he said, What cities are these\n"
    .string "which thou hast given me, my brother?\l"
    .string "And he called them the land of\l"
    .string "Cabul unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_14::
    .string "And Hiram sent to the king sixscore\n"
    .string "talents of gold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_15::
    .string "And this is the reason of the levy\n"
    .string "which king Solomon raised; for to\l"
    .string "build the house of the LORD, and his\l"
    .string "own house, and Millo, and the wall\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, and Hazor, and\l"
    .string "Megiddo, and Gezer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_16::
    .string "For Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone\n"
    .string "up, and taken Gezer, and burnt it\l"
    .string "with fire, and slain the Canaanites\l"
    .string "that dwelt in the city, and given it\l"
    .string "for a present unto his daughter,\l"
    .string "Solomon’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_17::
    .string "And Solomon built Gezer, and\n"
    .string "Bethhoron the nether,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_18::
    .string "And Baalath, and Tadmor in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, in the land,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_19::
    .string "And all the cities of store that\n"
    .string "Solomon had, and cities for his\l"
    .string "chariots, and cities for his\l"
    .string "horsemen, and that which Solomon\l"
    .string "desired to build in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "in Lebanon, and in all the land of\l"
    .string "his dominion$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_20::
    .string "And all the people that were\n"
    .string "left of the Amorites, Hittites,\l"
    .string "Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites,\l"
    .string "which were not of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_21::
    .string "Their children that were left\n"
    .string "after them in the land, whom the\l"
    .string "children of Israel also were not\l"
    .string "able utterly to destroy, upon those\l"
    .string "did Solomon levy a tribute of\l"
    .string "bondservice unto this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_22::
    .string "But of the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "Solomon make no bondmen: but they\l"
    .string "were men of war, and his servants,\l"
    .string "and his princes, and his captains,\l"
    .string "and rulers of his chariots, and his\l"
    .string "horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_23::
    .string "These were the chief of the officers\n"
    .string "that were over Solomon’s work, five\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty, which bare rule\l"
    .string "over the people that wrought in the\l"
    .string "work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_24::
    .string "But Pharaoh’s daughter came up out\n"
    .string "of the city of David unto her house\l"
    .string "which Solomon had built for her:\l"
    .string "then did he build Millo.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_25::
    .string "And three times in a year did\n"
    .string "Solomon offer burnt offerings and\l"
    .string "peace offerings upon the altar\l"
    .string "which he built unto the LORD, and he\l"
    .string "burnt incense upon the altar that\l"
    .string "was before the LORD. So he finished\l"
    .string "the house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_26::
    .string "And king Solomon made a navy of\n"
    .string "ships in Eziongeber, which is beside\l"
    .string "Eloth, on the shore of the Red sea,\l"
    .string "in the land of Edom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_27::
    .string "And Hiram sent in the navy his\n"
    .string "servants, shipmen that had\l"
    .string "knowledge of the sea, with the\l"
    .string "servants of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_9_28::
    .string "And they came to Ophir, and fetched\n"
    .string "from thence gold, four hundred and\l"
    .string "twenty talents, and brought it to\l"
    .string "king Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_1::
    .string "And when the queen of Sheba heard of\n"
    .string "the fame of Solomon concerning the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD, she came to prove\l"
    .string "him with hard questions.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_2::
    .string "And she came to Jerusalem with a\n"
    .string "very great train, with camels that\l"
    .string "bare spices, and very much gold, and\l"
    .string "precious stones: and when she was\l"
    .string "come to Solomon, she communed with\l"
    .string "him of all that was in her heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_3::
    .string "And Solomon told her all her\n"
    .string "questions: there was not any thing\l"
    .string "hid from the king, which he told her\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_4::
    .string "And when the queen of Sheba had seen\n"
    .string "all Solomon’s wisdom, and the house\l"
    .string "that he had built,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_5::
    .string "And the meat of his table, and the\n"
    .string "sitting of his servants, and the\l"
    .string "attendance of his ministers, and\l"
    .string "their apparel, and his cupbearers,\l"
    .string "and his ascent by which he went up\l"
    .string "unto the house of the LORD; there was\l"
    .string "no more spirit in her$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_6::
    .string "And she said to the king, It was a\n"
    .string "true report that I heard in mine own\l"
    .string "land of thy acts and of thy wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_7::
    .string "Howbeit I believed not the words,\n"
    .string "until I came, and mine eyes had seen\l"
    .string "it: and, behold, the half was not\l"
    .string "told me: thy wisdom and prosperity\l"
    .string "exceedeth the fame which I heard.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_8::
    .string "Happy are thy men, happy are\n"
    .string "these thy servants, which stand\l"
    .string "continually before thee, and that\l"
    .string "hear thy wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_9::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD thy God, which\n"
    .string "delighted in thee, to set thee on the\l"
    .string "throne of Israel: because the LORD\l"
    .string "loved Israel for ever, therefore\l"
    .string "made he thee king, to do judgment and\l"
    .string "justice.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_10::
    .string "And she gave the king an hundred and\n"
    .string "twenty talents of gold, and of\l"
    .string "spices very great store, and\l"
    .string "precious stones: there came no more\l"
    .string "such abundance of spices as these\l"
    .string "which the queen of Sheba gave to king\l"
    .string "Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_11::
    .string "And the navy also of Hiram, that\n"
    .string "brought gold from Ophir, brought in\l"
    .string "from Ophir great plenty of almug\l"
    .string "trees, and precious stones.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_12::
    .string "And the king made of the almug\n"
    .string "trees pillars for the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and for the king’s house,\l"
    .string "harps also and psalteries for\l"
    .string "singers: there came no such almug\l"
    .string "trees, nor were seen unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_13::
    .string "And king Solomon gave unto the\n"
    .string "queen of Sheba all her desire,\l"
    .string "whatsoever she asked, beside that\l"
    .string "which Solomon gave her of his royal\l"
    .string "bounty. So she turned and went to her\l"
    .string "own country, she and her servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_14::
    .string "Now the weight of gold that came to\n"
    .string "Solomon in one year was six hundred\l"
    .string "threescore and six talents of gold,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_15::
    .string "Beside that he had of the\n"
    .string "merchantmen, and of the traffick of\l"
    .string "the spice merchants, and of all the\l"
    .string "kings of Arabia, and of the governors\l"
    .string "of the country$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_16::
    .string "And king Solomon made two hundred\n"
    .string "targets of beaten gold: six hundred\l"
    .string "shekels of gold went to one target.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_17::
    .string "And he made three hundred shields\n"
    .string "of beaten gold; three pound of gold\l"
    .string "went to one shield: and the king put\l"
    .string "them in the house of the forest of\l"
    .string "Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_18::
    .string "Moreover the king made a great\n"
    .string "throne of ivory, and overlaid it\l"
    .string "with the best gold.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_19::
    .string "The throne had six steps, and the\n"
    .string "top of the throne was round behind:\l"
    .string "and there were stays on either side\l"
    .string "on the place of the seat, and two\l"
    .string "lions stood beside the stays.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_20::
    .string "And twelve lions stood there on\n"
    .string "the one side and on the other upon\l"
    .string "the six steps: there was not the\l"
    .string "like made in any kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_21::
    .string "And all king Solomon’s drinking\n"
    .string "vessels were of gold, and all the\l"
    .string "vessels of the house of the forest\l"
    .string "of Lebanon were of pure gold; none\l"
    .string "were of silver: it was nothing\l"
    .string "accounted of in the days of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_22::
    .string "For the king had at sea a navy of\n"
    .string "Tharshish with the navy of Hiram:\l"
    .string "once in three years came the navy of\l"
    .string "Tharshish, bringing gold, and\l"
    .string "silver, ivory, and apes, and\l"
    .string "peacocks.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_23::
    .string "So king Solomon exceeded all the\n"
    .string "kings of the earth for riches and for\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_24::
    .string "And all the earth sought to\n"
    .string "Solomon, to hear his wisdom, which\l"
    .string "God had put in his heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_25::
    .string "And they brought every man his\n"
    .string "present, vessels of silver, and\l"
    .string "vessels of gold, and garments, and\l"
    .string "armour, and spices, horses, and\l"
    .string "mules, a rate year by year.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_26::
    .string "And Solomon gathered together\n"
    .string "chariots and horsemen: and he had a\l"
    .string "thousand and four hundred chariots,\l"
    .string "and twelve thousand horsemen, whom\l"
    .string "he bestowed in the cities for\l"
    .string "chariots, and with the king at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_27::
    .string "And the king made silver to be in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem as stones, and cedars made\l"
    .string "he to be as the sycomore trees that\l"
    .string "are in the vale, for abundance.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_28::
    .string "And Solomon had horses brought out\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king’s\l"
    .string "merchants received the linen yarn at\l"
    .string "a price.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_10_29::
    .string "And a chariot came up and went out\n"
    .string "of Egypt for six hundred shekels of\l"
    .string "silver, and an horse for an hundred\l"
    .string "and fifty: and so for all the kings\l"
    .string "of the Hittites, and for the kings of\l"
    .string "Syria, did they bring them out by\l"
    .string "their means.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_1::
    .string "But king Solomon loved many\n"
    .string "strange women, together with the\l"
    .string "daughter of Pharaoh, women of the\l"
    .string "Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites,\l"
    .string "Zidonians, and Hittites:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_2::
    .string "Of the nations concerning which the\n"
    .string "LORD said unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, Ye shall not go in to them,\l"
    .string "neither shall they come in unto you:\l"
    .string "for surely they will turn away your\l"
    .string "heart after their gods: Solomon\l"
    .string "clave unto these in love$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_3::
    .string "And he had seven hundred wives,\n"
    .string "princesses, and three hundred\l"
    .string "concubines: and his wives turned away\l"
    .string "his heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_4::
    .string "For it came to pass, when Solomon\n"
    .string "was old, that his wives turned away\l"
    .string "his heart after other gods: and his\l"
    .string "heart was not perfect with the LORD\l"
    .string "his God, as was the heart of David his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_5::
    .string "For Solomon went after Ashtoreth\n"
    .string "the goddess of the Zidonians, and\l"
    .string "after Milcom the abomination of the\l"
    .string "Ammonites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_6::
    .string "And Solomon did evil in the sight\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and went not fully\l"
    .string "after the LORD, as did David his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_7::
    .string "Then did Solomon build an high\n"
    .string "place for Chemosh, the abomination\l"
    .string "of Moab, in the hill that is before\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and for Molech, the\l"
    .string "abomination of the children of Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_8::
    .string "And likewise did he for all his\n"
    .string "strange wives, which burnt incense\l"
    .string "and sacrificed unto their gods.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_9::
    .string "And the LORD was angry with\n"
    .string "Solomon, because his heart was\l"
    .string "turned from the LORD God of Israel,\l"
    .string "which had appeared unto him twice,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_10::
    .string "And had commanded him concerning\n"
    .string "this thing, that he should not go\l"
    .string "after other gods: but he kept not\l"
    .string "that which the LORD commanded$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_11::
    .string "Wherefore the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "Solomon, Forasmuch as this is done\l"
    .string "of thee, and thou hast not kept my\l"
    .string "covenant and my statutes, which I\l"
    .string "have commanded thee, I will surely\l"
    .string "rend the kingdom from thee, and will\l"
    .string "give it to thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_12::
    .string "Notwithstanding in thy days I will\n"
    .string "not do it for David thy father’s\l"
    .string "sake: but I will rend it out of the\l"
    .string "hand of thy son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_13::
    .string "Howbeit I will not rend away all\n"
    .string "the kingdom; but will give one tribe\l"
    .string "to thy son for David my servant’s\l"
    .string "sake, and for Jerusalem’s sake which\l"
    .string "I have chosen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_14::
    .string "And the LORD stirred up an\n"
    .string "adversary unto Solomon, Hadad the\l"
    .string "Edomite: he was of the king’s seed in\l"
    .string "Edom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_15::
    .string "For it came to pass, when David was\n"
    .string "in Edom, and Joab the captain of the\l"
    .string "host was gone up to bury the slain,\l"
    .string "after he had smitten every male in\l"
    .string "Edom;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_16::
    .string "(For six months did Joab remain\n"
    .string "there with all Israel, until he\l"
    .string "had cut off every male in Edom:)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_17::
    .string "That Hadad fled, he and certain\n"
    .string "Edomites of his father’s servants\l"
    .string "with him, to go into Egypt; Hadad\l"
    .string "being yet a little child$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_18::
    .string "And they arose out of Midian, and\n"
    .string "came to Paran: and they took men with\l"
    .string "them out of Paran, and they came to\l"
    .string "Egypt, unto Pharaoh king of Egypt;\l"
    .string "which gave him an house, and\l"
    .string "appointed him victuals, and gave\l"
    .string "him land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_19::
    .string "And Hadad found great favour in the\n"
    .string "sight of Pharaoh, so that he gave him\l"
    .string "to wife the sister of his own wife,\l"
    .string "the sister of Tahpenes the queen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_20::
    .string "And the sister of Tahpenes bare him\n"
    .string "Genubath his son, whom Tahpenes\l"
    .string "weaned in Pharaoh’s house: and\l"
    .string "Genubath was in Pharaoh’s household\l"
    .string "among the sons of Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_21::
    .string "And when Hadad heard in Egypt that\n"
    .string "David slept with his fathers, and\l"
    .string "that Joab the captain of the host\l"
    .string "was dead, Hadad said to Pharaoh, Let\l"
    .string "me depart, that I may go to mine own\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_22::
    .string "Then Pharaoh said unto him, But what\n"
    .string "hast thou lacked with me, that,\l"
    .string "behold, thou seekest to go to thine\l"
    .string "own country? And he answered,\l"
    .string "Nothing: howbeit let me go in any\l"
    .string "wise.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_23::
    .string "And God stirred him up another\n"
    .string "adversary, Rezon the son of Eliadah,\l"
    .string "which fled from his lord Hadadezer\l"
    .string "king of Zobah:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_24::
    .string "And he gathered men unto him, and\n"
    .string "became captain over a band, when\l"
    .string "David slew them of Zobah: and they\l"
    .string "went to Damascus, and dwelt therein,\l"
    .string "and reigned in Damascus$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_25::
    .string "And he was an adversary to Israel\n"
    .string "all the days of Solomon, beside the\l"
    .string "mischief that Hadad did: and he\l"
    .string "abhorred Israel, and reigned over\l"
    .string "Syria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_26::
    .string "And Jeroboam the son of Nebat, an\n"
    .string "Ephrathite of Zereda, Solomon’s\l"
    .string "servant, whose mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Zeruah, a widow woman, even he\l"
    .string "lifted up his hand against the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_27::
    .string "And this was the cause that he\n"
    .string "lifted up his hand against the king:\l"
    .string "Solomon built Millo, and repaired\l"
    .string "the breaches of the city of David his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_28::
    .string "And the man Jeroboam was a mighty\n"
    .string "man of valour: and Solomon seeing\l"
    .string "the young man that he was\l"
    .string "industrious, he made him ruler over\l"
    .string "all the charge of the house of\l"
    .string "Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_29::
    .string "And it came to pass at that time\n"
    .string "when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "that the prophet Ahijah the\l"
    .string "Shilonite found him in the way; and\l"
    .string "he had clad himself with a new\l"
    .string "garment; and they two were alone in\l"
    .string "the field:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_30::
    .string "And Ahijah caught the new garment\n"
    .string "that was on him, and rent it in\l"
    .string "twelve pieces:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_31::
    .string "And he said to Jeroboam, Take thee\n"
    .string "ten pieces: for thus saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "the God of Israel, Behold, I will\l"
    .string "rend the kingdom out of the hand of\l"
    .string "Solomon, and will give ten tribes\l"
    .string "to thee:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_32::
    .string "(But he shall have one tribe for my\n"
    .string "servant David’s sake, and for\l"
    .string "Jerusalem’s sake, the city which I\l"
    .string "have chosen out of all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel:)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_33::
    .string "Because that they have forsaken me,\n"
    .string "and have worshipped Ashtoreth the\l"
    .string "goddess of the Zidonians, Chemosh the\l"
    .string "god of the Moabites, and Milcom the\l"
    .string "god of the children of Ammon, and\l"
    .string "have not walked in my ways, to do\l"
    .string "that which is right in mine eyes, and\l"
    .string "to keep my statutes and my\l"
    .string "judgments, as did David his father$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_34::
    .string "Howbeit I will not take the whole\n"
    .string "kingdom out of his hand: but I will\l"
    .string "make him prince all the days of his\l"
    .string "life for David my servant’s sake,\l"
    .string "whom I chose, because he kept my\l"
    .string "commandments and my statutes:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_35::
    .string "But I will take the kingdom out of\n"
    .string "his son’s hand, and will give it\l"
    .string "unto thee, even ten tribes$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_36::
    .string "And unto his son will I give one\n"
    .string "tribe, that David my servant may have\l"
    .string "a light alway before me in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, the city which I have\l"
    .string "chosen me to put my name there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_37::
    .string "And I will take thee, and thou\n"
    .string "shalt reign according to all that\l"
    .string "thy soul desireth, and shalt be king\l"
    .string "over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_38::
    .string "And it shall be, if thou wilt\n"
    .string "hearken unto all that I command\l"
    .string "thee, and wilt walk in my ways, and\l"
    .string "do that is right in my sight, to keep\l"
    .string "my statutes and my commandments, as\l"
    .string "David my servant did; that I will be\l"
    .string "with thee, and build thee a sure\l"
    .string "house, as I built for David, and\l"
    .string "will give Israel unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_39::
    .string "And I will for this afflict the\n"
    .string "seed of David, but not for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_40::
    .string "Solomon sought therefore to kill\n"
    .string "Jeroboam. And Jeroboam arose, and\l"
    .string "fled into Egypt, unto Shishak king\l"
    .string "of Egypt, and was in Egypt until\l"
    .string "the death of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_41::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Solomon,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, and his wisdom,\l"
    .string "are they not written in the book of\l"
    .string "the acts of Solomon?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_42::
    .string "And the time that Solomon reigned\n"
    .string "in Jerusalem over all Israel was\l"
    .string "forty years$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_11_43::
    .string "And Solomon slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried in the city\l"
    .string "of David his father: and Rehoboam his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_1::
    .string "And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for\n"
    .string "all Israel were come to Shechem to\l"
    .string "make him king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jeroboam\n"
    .string "the son of Nebat, who was yet in\l"
    .string "Egypt, heard of it, (for he was fled\l"
    .string "from the presence of king Solomon,\l"
    .string "and Jeroboam dwelt in Egypt;)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_3::
    .string "That they sent and called him. And\n"
    .string "Jeroboam and all the congregation\l"
    .string "of Israel came, and spake unto\l"
    .string "Rehoboam, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_4::
    .string "Thy father made our yoke grievous:\n"
    .string "now therefore make thou the grievous\l"
    .string "service of thy father, and his heavy\l"
    .string "yoke which he put upon us, lighter,\l"
    .string "and we will serve thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, Depart yet\n"
    .string "for three days, then come again to\l"
    .string "me. And the people departed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_6::
    .string "And king Rehoboam consulted with\n"
    .string "the old men, that stood before\l"
    .string "Solomon his father while he yet\l"
    .string "lived, and said, How do ye advise\l"
    .string "that I may answer this people?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_7::
    .string "And they spake unto him, saying, If\n"
    .string "thou wilt be a servant unto this\l"
    .string "people this day, and wilt serve\l"
    .string "them, and answer them, and speak\l"
    .string "good words to them, then they will\l"
    .string "be thy servants for ever$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_8::
    .string "But he forsook the counsel of the\n"
    .string "old men, which they had given him,\l"
    .string "and consulted with the young men\l"
    .string "that were grown up with him, and\l"
    .string "which stood before him:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_9::
    .string "And he said unto them, What counsel\n"
    .string "give ye that we may answer this\l"
    .string "people, who have spoken to me,\l"
    .string "saying, Make the yoke which thy\l"
    .string "father did put upon us lighter?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_10::
    .string "And the young men that were grown\n"
    .string "up with him spake unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Thus shalt thou speak unto this\l"
    .string "people that spake unto thee,\l"
    .string "saying, Thy father made our yoke\l"
    .string "heavy, but make thou it lighter unto\l"
    .string "us; thus shalt thou say unto them, My\l"
    .string "little finger shall be thicker\l"
    .string "than my father’s loins$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_11::
    .string "And now whereas my father did lade\n"
    .string "you with a heavy yoke, I will add to\l"
    .string "your yoke: my father hath chastised\l"
    .string "you with whips, but I will chastise\l"
    .string "you with scorpions.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_12::
    .string "So Jeroboam and all the people\n"
    .string "came to Rehoboam the third day, as\l"
    .string "the king had appointed, saying,\l"
    .string "Come to me again the third day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_13::
    .string "And the king answered the people\n"
    .string "roughly, and forsook the old men’s\l"
    .string "counsel that they gave him;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_14::
    .string "And spake to them after the\n"
    .string "counsel of the young men, saying, My\l"
    .string "father made your yoke heavy, and I\l"
    .string "will add to your yoke: my father\l"
    .string "also chastised you with whips, but I\l"
    .string "will chastise you with scorpions$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_15::
    .string "Wherefore the king hearkened not\n"
    .string "unto the people; for the cause was\l"
    .string "from the LORD, that he might perform\l"
    .string "his saying, which the LORD spake by\l"
    .string "Ahijah the Shilonite unto Jeroboam\l"
    .string "the son of Nebat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_16::
    .string "So when all Israel saw that the\n"
    .string "king hearkened not unto them, the\l"
    .string "people answered the king, saying,\l"
    .string "What portion have we in David?\l"
    .string "neither have we inheritance in the\l"
    .string "son of Jesse: to your tents, O\l"
    .string "Israel: now see to thine own house,\l"
    .string "David. So Israel departed unto\l"
    .string "their tents.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_17::
    .string "But as for the children of Israel\n"
    .string "which dwelt in the cities of Judah,\l"
    .string "Rehoboam reigned over them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_18::
    .string "Then king Rehoboam sent Adoram, who\n"
    .string "was over the tribute; and all\l"
    .string "Israel stoned him with stones, that\l"
    .string "he died. Therefore king Rehoboam made\l"
    .string "speed to get him up to his chariot,\l"
    .string "to flee to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_19::
    .string "So Israel rebelled against the\n"
    .string "house of David unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_20::
    .string "And it came to pass, when all\n"
    .string "Israel heard that Jeroboam was come\l"
    .string "again, that they sent and called him\l"
    .string "unto the congregation, and made him\l"
    .string "king over all Israel: there was\l"
    .string "none that followed the house of\l"
    .string "David, but the tribe of Judah only.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_21::
    .string "And when Rehoboam was come to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, he assembled all the\l"
    .string "house of Judah, with the tribe of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, an hundred and fourscore\l"
    .string "thousand chosen men, which were\l"
    .string "warriors, to fight against the house\l"
    .string "of Israel, to bring the kingdom\l"
    .string "again to Rehoboam the son of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_22::
    .string "But the word of God came unto\n"
    .string "Shemaiah the man of God, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_23::
    .string "Speak unto Rehoboam, the son of\n"
    .string "Solomon, king of Judah, and unto\l"
    .string "all the house of Judah and Benjamin,\l"
    .string "and to the remnant of the people,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_24::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not\n"
    .string "go up, nor fight against your\l"
    .string "brethren the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "return every man to his house; for\l"
    .string "this thing is from me. They hearkened\l"
    .string "therefore to the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and returned to depart, according to\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_25::
    .string "Then Jeroboam built Shechem in\n"
    .string "mount Ephraim, and dwelt therein;\l"
    .string "and went out from thence, and built\l"
    .string "Penuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_26::
    .string "And Jeroboam said in his heart, Now\n"
    .string "shall the kingdom return to the\l"
    .string "house of David:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_27::
    .string "If this people go up to do\n"
    .string "sacrifice in the house of the LORD at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, then shall the heart of\l"
    .string "this people turn again unto their\l"
    .string "lord, even unto Rehoboam king of\l"
    .string "Judah, and they shall kill me, and\l"
    .string "go again to Rehoboam king of Judah$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_28::
    .string "Whereupon the king took counsel,\n"
    .string "and made two calves of gold, and\l"
    .string "said unto them, It is too much for you\l"
    .string "to go up to Jerusalem: behold thy\l"
    .string "gods, O Israel, which brought thee\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_29::
    .string "And he set the one in Bethel, and\n"
    .string "the other put he in Dan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_30::
    .string "And this thing became a sin: for the\n"
    .string "people went to worship before the\l"
    .string "one, even unto Dan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_31::
    .string "And he made an house of high\n"
    .string "places, and made priests of the\l"
    .string "lowest of the people, which were\l"
    .string "not of the sons of Levi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_32::
    .string "And Jeroboam ordained a feast in the\n"
    .string "eighth month, on the fifteenth day of\l"
    .string "the month, like unto the feast that\l"
    .string "is in Judah, and he offered upon the\l"
    .string "altar. So did he in Bethel,\l"
    .string "sacrificing unto the calves that he\l"
    .string "had made: and he placed in Bethel\l"
    .string "the priests of the high places\l"
    .string "which he had made.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_12_33::
    .string "So he offered upon the altar which\n"
    .string "he had made in Bethel the fifteenth\l"
    .string "day of the eighth month, even in the\l"
    .string "month which he had devised of his own\l"
    .string "heart; and ordained a feast unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: and he offered\l"
    .string "upon the altar, and burnt incense.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_1::
    .string "And, behold, there came a man of God\n"
    .string "out of Judah by the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "unto Bethel: and Jeroboam stood by\l"
    .string "the altar to burn incense.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_2::
    .string "And he cried against the altar in\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD, and said, O\l"
    .string "altar, altar, thus saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "Behold, a child shall be born unto\l"
    .string "the house of David, Josiah by name;\l"
    .string "and upon thee shall he offer the\l"
    .string "priests of the high places that\l"
    .string "burn incense upon thee, and men’s\l"
    .string "bones shall be burnt upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_3::
    .string "And he gave a sign the same day,\n"
    .string "saying, This is the sign which the\l"
    .string "LORD hath spoken; Behold, the altar\l"
    .string "shall be rent, and the ashes that\l"
    .string "are upon it shall be poured out.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, when king\n"
    .string "Jeroboam heard the saying of the man\l"
    .string "of God, which had cried against the\l"
    .string "altar in Bethel, that he put forth\l"
    .string "his hand from the altar, saying, Lay\l"
    .string "hold on him. And his hand, which he\l"
    .string "put forth against him, dried up, so\l"
    .string "that he could not pull it in again\l"
    .string "to him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_5::
    .string "The altar also was rent, and the\n"
    .string "ashes poured out from the altar,\l"
    .string "according to the sign which the man\l"
    .string "of God had given by the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_6::
    .string "And the king answered and said unto\n"
    .string "the man of God, Intreat now the face\l"
    .string "of the LORD thy God, and pray for me,\l"
    .string "that my hand may be restored me\l"
    .string "again. And the man of God besought\l"
    .string "the LORD, and the king’s hand was\l"
    .string "restored him again, and became as it\l"
    .string "was before.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_7::
    .string "And the king said unto the man of\n"
    .string "God, Come home with me, and refresh\l"
    .string "thyself, and I will give thee a\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_8::
    .string "And the man of God said unto the\n"
    .string "king, If thou wilt give me half\l"
    .string "thine house, I will not go in with\l"
    .string "thee, neither will I eat bread nor\l"
    .string "drink water in this place:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_9::
    .string "For so was it charged me by the word\n"
    .string "of the LORD, saying, Eat no bread, nor\l"
    .string "drink water, nor turn again by the\l"
    .string "same way that thou camest$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_10::
    .string "So he went another way, and returned\n"
    .string "not by the way that he came to Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_11::
    .string "Now there dwelt an old prophet in\n"
    .string "Bethel; and his sons came and told\l"
    .string "him all the works that the man of\l"
    .string "God had done that day in Bethel: the\l"
    .string "words which he had spoken unto the\l"
    .string "king, them they told also to their\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_12::
    .string "And their father said unto them,\n"
    .string "What way went he? For his sons had\l"
    .string "seen what way the man of God went,\l"
    .string "which came from Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_13::
    .string "And he said unto his sons, Saddle me\n"
    .string "the ass. So they saddled him the ass:\l"
    .string "and he rode thereon,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_14::
    .string "And went after the man of God, and\n"
    .string "found him sitting under an oak: and\l"
    .string "he said unto him, Art thou the man of\l"
    .string "God that camest from Judah? And he\l"
    .string "said, I am$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_15::
    .string "Then he said unto him, Come home\n"
    .string "with me, and eat bread.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_16::
    .string "And he said, I may not return with\n"
    .string "thee, nor go in with thee: neither\l"
    .string "will I eat bread nor drink water\l"
    .string "with thee in this place:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_17::
    .string "For it was said to me by the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD, Thou shalt eat no bread nor\l"
    .string "drink water there, nor turn again to\l"
    .string "go by the way that thou camest$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_18::
    .string "He said unto him, I am a prophet\n"
    .string "also as thou art; and an angel\l"
    .string "spake unto me by the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD, saying, Bring him back with\l"
    .string "thee into thine house, that he may\l"
    .string "eat bread and drink water. But he\l"
    .string "lied unto him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_19::
    .string "So he went back with him, and did eat\n"
    .string "bread in his house, and drank water.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_20::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they sat at\n"
    .string "the table, that the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "came unto the prophet that brought\l"
    .string "him back:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_21::
    .string "And he cried unto the man of God\n"
    .string "that came from Judah, saying, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou\l"
    .string "hast disobeyed the mouth of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and hast not kept the commandment\l"
    .string "which the LORD thy God commanded\l"
    .string "thee,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_22::
    .string "But camest back, and hast eaten\n"
    .string "bread and drunk water in the place,\l"
    .string "of the which the Lord did say to thee,\l"
    .string "Eat no bread, and drink no water; thy\l"
    .string "carcase shall not come unto the\l"
    .string "sepulchre of thy fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, after he had\n"
    .string "eaten bread, and after he had drunk,\l"
    .string "that he saddled for him the ass, to\l"
    .string "wit, for the prophet whom he had\l"
    .string "brought back.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_24::
    .string "And when he was gone, a lion met him\n"
    .string "by the way, and slew him: and his\l"
    .string "carcase was cast in the way, and the\l"
    .string "ass stood by it, the lion also stood\l"
    .string "by the carcase.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_25::
    .string "And, behold, men passed by, and saw\n"
    .string "the carcase cast in the way, and the\l"
    .string "lion standing by the carcase: and\l"
    .string "they came and told it in the city\l"
    .string "where the old prophet dwelt.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_26::
    .string "And when the prophet that brought\n"
    .string "him back from the way heard thereof,\l"
    .string "he said, It is the man of God, who was\l"
    .string "disobedient unto the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD: therefore the LORD hath\l"
    .string "delivered him unto the lion, which\l"
    .string "hath torn him, and slain him,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake unto him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_27::
    .string "And he spake to his sons, saying,\n"
    .string "Saddle me the ass. And they saddled\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_28::
    .string "And he went and found his carcase\n"
    .string "cast in the way, and the ass and the\l"
    .string "lion standing by the carcase: the\l"
    .string "lion had not eaten the carcase, nor\l"
    .string "torn the ass.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_29::
    .string "And the prophet took up the\n"
    .string "carcase of the man of God, and laid\l"
    .string "it upon the ass, and brought it back:\l"
    .string "and the old prophet came to the\l"
    .string "city, to mourn and to bury him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_30::
    .string "And he laid his carcase in his own\n"
    .string "grave; and they mourned over him,\l"
    .string "saying, Alas, my brother!"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_31::
    .string "And it came to pass, after he had\n"
    .string "buried him, that he spake to his\l"
    .string "sons, saying, When I am dead, then\l"
    .string "bury me in the sepulchre wherein\l"
    .string "the man of God is buried; lay my\l"
    .string "bones beside his bones:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_32::
    .string "For the saying which he cried by the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD against the altar\l"
    .string "in Bethel, and against all the\l"
    .string "houses of the high places which are\l"
    .string "in the cities of Samaria, shall\l"
    .string "surely come to pass$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_33::
    .string "After this thing Jeroboam returned\n"
    .string "not from his evil way, but made again\l"
    .string "of the lowest of the people\l"
    .string "priests of the high places:\l"
    .string "whosoever would, he consecrated him,\l"
    .string "and he became one of the priests of\l"
    .string "the high places.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_13_34::
    .string "And this thing became sin unto the\n"
    .string "house of Jeroboam, even to cut it\l"
    .string "off, and to destroy it from off the\l"
    .string "face of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_1::
    .string "At that time Abijah the son of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam fell sick.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_2::
    .string "And Jeroboam said to his wife,\n"
    .string "Arise, I pray thee, and disguise\l"
    .string "thyself, that thou be not known to be\l"
    .string "the wife of Jeroboam; and get thee to\l"
    .string "Shiloh: behold, there is Ahijah the\l"
    .string "prophet, which told me that I\l"
    .string "should be king over this people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_3::
    .string "And take with thee ten loaves, and\n"
    .string "cracknels, and a cruse of honey, and\l"
    .string "go to him: he shall tell thee what\l"
    .string "shall become of the child.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_4::
    .string "And Jeroboam’s wife did so, and\n"
    .string "arose, and went to Shiloh, and came\l"
    .string "to the house of Ahijah. But Ahijah\l"
    .string "could not see; for his eyes were set\l"
    .string "by reason of his age.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_5::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Ahijah,\n"
    .string "Behold, the wife of Jeroboam cometh\l"
    .string "to ask a thing of thee for her son;\l"
    .string "for he is sick: thus and thus shalt\l"
    .string "thou say unto her: for it shall be,\l"
    .string "when she cometh in, that she shall\l"
    .string "feign herself to be another woman.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_6::
    .string "And it was so, when Ahijah heard the\n"
    .string "sound of her feet, as she came in at\l"
    .string "the door, that he said, Come in, thou\l"
    .string "wife of Jeroboam; why feignest thou\l"
    .string "thyself to be another? for I am sent\l"
    .string "to thee with heavy tidings.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_7::
    .string "Go, tell Jeroboam, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, Forasmuch as I\l"
    .string "exalted thee from among the\l"
    .string "people, and made thee prince over\l"
    .string "my people Israel,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_8::
    .string "And rent the kingdom away from the\n"
    .string "house of David, and gave it thee: and\l"
    .string "yet thou hast not been as my servant\l"
    .string "David, who kept my commandments, and\l"
    .string "who followed me with all his\l"
    .string "heart, to do that only which was\l"
    .string "right in mine eyes;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_9::
    .string "But hast done evil above all that\n"
    .string "were before thee: for thou hast gone\l"
    .string "and made thee other gods, and molten\l"
    .string "images, to provoke me to anger, and\l"
    .string "hast cast me behind thy back:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_10::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will bring\n"
    .string "evil upon the house of Jeroboam, and\l"
    .string "will cut off from Jeroboam him that\l"
    .string "pisseth against the wall, and him\l"
    .string "that is shut up and left in Israel,\l"
    .string "and will take away the remnant of\l"
    .string "the house of Jeroboam, as a man\l"
    .string "taketh away dung, till it be all\l"
    .string "gone$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_11::
    .string "Him that dieth of Jeroboam in the\n"
    .string "city shall the dogs eat; and him\l"
    .string "that dieth in the field shall the\l"
    .string "fowls of the air eat: for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_12::
    .string "Arise thou therefore, get thee to\n"
    .string "thine own house: and when thy feet\l"
    .string "enter into the city, the child\l"
    .string "shall die.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_13::
    .string "And all Israel shall mourn for\n"
    .string "him, and bury him: for he only of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam shall come to the grave,\l"
    .string "because in him there is found some\l"
    .string "good thing toward the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel in the house of Jeroboam.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_14::
    .string "Moreover the LORD shall raise him\n"
    .string "up a king over Israel, who shall\l"
    .string "cut off the house of Jeroboam that\l"
    .string "day: but what? even now.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_15::
    .string "For the LORD shall smite Israel,\n"
    .string "as a reed is shaken in the water, and\l"
    .string "he shall root up Israel out of\l"
    .string "this good land, which he gave to\l"
    .string "their fathers, and shall scatter\l"
    .string "them beyond the river, because they\l"
    .string "have made their groves, provoking\l"
    .string "the LORD to anger.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_16::
    .string "And he shall give Israel up\n"
    .string "because of the sins of Jeroboam, who\l"
    .string "did sin, and who made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_17::
    .string "And Jeroboam’s wife arose, and\n"
    .string "departed, and came to Tirzah: and\l"
    .string "when she came to the threshold of\l"
    .string "the door, the child died;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_18::
    .string "And they buried him; and all\n"
    .string "Israel mourned for him, according to\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD, which he spake\l"
    .string "by the hand of his servant Ahijah the\l"
    .string "prophet$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_19::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam, how he warred, and how he\l"
    .string "reigned, behold, they are written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_20::
    .string "And the days which Jeroboam reigned\n"
    .string "were two and twenty years: and he\l"
    .string "slept with his fathers, and Nadab\l"
    .string "his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_21::
    .string "And Rehoboam the son of Solomon\n"
    .string "reigned in Judah. Rehoboam was forty\l"
    .string "and one years old when he began to\l"
    .string "reign, and he reigned seventeen years\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem, the city which the\l"
    .string "LORD did choose out of all the\l"
    .string "tribes of Israel, to put his name\l"
    .string "there. And his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Naamah an Ammonitess.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_22::
    .string "And Judah did evil in the sight of\n"
    .string "the LORD, and they provoked him to\l"
    .string "jealousy with their sins which they\l"
    .string "had committed, above all that their\l"
    .string "fathers had done.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_23::
    .string "For they also built them high\n"
    .string "places, and images, and groves, on\l"
    .string "every high hill, and under every\l"
    .string "green tree.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_24::
    .string "And there were also sodomites in\n"
    .string "the land: and they did according to\l"
    .string "all the abominations of the nations\l"
    .string "which the LORD cast out before the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_25::
    .string "And it came to pass in the fifth\n"
    .string "year of king Rehoboam, that Shishak\l"
    .string "king of Egypt came up against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_26::
    .string "And he took away the treasures of\n"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "treasures of the king’s house; he\l"
    .string "even took away all: and he took away\l"
    .string "all the shields of gold which\l"
    .string "Solomon had made$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_27::
    .string "And king Rehoboam made in their\n"
    .string "stead brasen shields, and committed\l"
    .string "them unto the hands of the chief of\l"
    .string "the guard, which kept the door of the\l"
    .string "king’s house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_28::
    .string "And it was so, when the king went\n"
    .string "into the house of the LORD, that the\l"
    .string "guard bare them, and brought them\l"
    .string "back into the guard chamber.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_29::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Rehoboam, and all that he did, are\l"
    .string "they not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_30::
    .string "And there was war between Rehoboam\n"
    .string "and Jeroboam all their days$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_14_31::
    .string "And Rehoboam slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried with his\l"
    .string "fathers in the city of David. And his\l"
    .string "mother’s name was Naamah an\l"
    .string "Ammonitess. And Abijam his son\l"
    .string "reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_1::
    .string "Now in the eighteenth year of king\n"
    .string "Jeroboam the son of Nebat reigned\l"
    .string "Abijam over Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_2::
    .string "Three years reigned he in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem. and his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Maachah, the daughter of Abishalom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_3::
    .string "And he walked in all the sins of\n"
    .string "his father, which he had done before\l"
    .string "him: and his heart was not perfect\l"
    .string "with the LORD his God, as the heart of\l"
    .string "David his father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_4::
    .string "Nevertheless for David’s sake did\n"
    .string "the LORD his God give him a lamp in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, to set up his son after\l"
    .string "him, and to establish Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_5::
    .string "Because David did that which was\n"
    .string "right in the eyes of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "turned not aside from any thing that\l"
    .string "he commanded him all the days of his\l"
    .string "life, save only in the matter of\l"
    .string "Uriah the Hittite$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_6::
    .string "And there was war between Rehoboam\n"
    .string "and Jeroboam all the days of his\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_7::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Abijam,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?\l"
    .string "And there was war between Abijam and\l"
    .string "Jeroboam.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_8::
    .string "And Abijam slept with his fathers;\n"
    .string "and they buried him in the city of\l"
    .string "David: and Asa his son reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_9::
    .string "And in the twentieth year of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam king of Israel reigned Asa\l"
    .string "over Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_10::
    .string "And forty and one years reigned he\n"
    .string "in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name\l"
    .string "was Maachah, the daughter of\l"
    .string "Abishalom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_11::
    .string "And Asa did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the eyes of the LORD, as did David his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_12::
    .string "And he took away the sodomites out\n"
    .string "of the land, and removed all the\l"
    .string "idols that his fathers had made.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_13::
    .string "And also Maachah his mother, even\n"
    .string "her he removed from being queen,\l"
    .string "because she had made an idol in a\l"
    .string "grove; and Asa destroyed her idol,\l"
    .string "and burnt it by the brook Kidron.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_14::
    .string "But the high places were not\n"
    .string "removed: nevertheless Asa’s heart\l"
    .string "was perfect with the LORD all his\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_15::
    .string "And he brought in the things which\n"
    .string "his father had dedicated, and the\l"
    .string "things which himself had dedicated,\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD, silver,\l"
    .string "and gold, and vessels.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_16::
    .string "And there was war between Asa and\n"
    .string "Baasha king of Israel all their\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_17::
    .string "And Baasha king of Israel went up\n"
    .string "against Judah, and built Ramah, that\l"
    .string "he might not suffer any to go out or\l"
    .string "come in to Asa king of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_18::
    .string "Then Asa took all the silver and\n"
    .string "the gold that were left in the\l"
    .string "treasures of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the treasures of the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and delivered them into the\l"
    .string "hand of his servants: and king Asa\l"
    .string "sent them to Benhadad, the son of\l"
    .string "Tabrimon, the son of Hezion, king of\l"
    .string "Syria, that dwelt at Damascus,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_19::
    .string "There is a league between me and\n"
    .string "thee, and between my father and thy\l"
    .string "father: behold, I have sent unto\l"
    .string "thee a present of silver and gold;\l"
    .string "come and break thy league with\l"
    .string "Baasha king of Israel, that he may\l"
    .string "depart from me$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_20::
    .string "So Benhadad hearkened unto king Asa,\n"
    .string "and sent the captains of the hosts\l"
    .string "which he had against the cities of\l"
    .string "Israel, and smote Ijon, and Dan, and\l"
    .string "Abelbethmaachah, and all\l"
    .string "Cinneroth, with all the land of\l"
    .string "Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_21::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Baasha\n"
    .string "heard thereof, that he left off\l"
    .string "building of Ramah, and dwelt in\l"
    .string "Tirzah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_22::
    .string "Then king Asa made a proclamation\n"
    .string "throughout all Judah; none was\l"
    .string "exempted: and they took away the\l"
    .string "stones of Ramah, and the timber\l"
    .string "thereof, wherewith Baasha had\l"
    .string "builded; and king Asa built with\l"
    .string "them Geba of Benjamin, and Mizpah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_23::
    .string "The rest of all the acts of Asa,\n"
    .string "and all his might, and all that he\l"
    .string "did, and the cities which he built,\l"
    .string "are they not written in the book of\l"
    .string "the chronicles of the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah? Nevertheless in the time of\l"
    .string "his old age he was diseased in his\l"
    .string "feet.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_24::
    .string "And Asa slept with his fathers, and\n"
    .string "was buried with his fathers in the\l"
    .string "city of David his father: and\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_25::
    .string "And Nadab the son of Jeroboam began\n"
    .string "to reign over Israel in the second\l"
    .string "year of Asa king of Judah, and\l"
    .string "reigned over Israel two years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_26::
    .string "And he did evil in the sight of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and walked in the way of his\l"
    .string "father, and in his sin wherewith he\l"
    .string "made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_27::
    .string "And Baasha the son of Ahijah, of the\n"
    .string "house of Issachar, conspired against\l"
    .string "him; and Baasha smote him at\l"
    .string "Gibbethon, which belonged to the\l"
    .string "Philistines; for Nadab and all\l"
    .string "Israel laid siege to Gibbethon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_28::
    .string "Even in the third year of Asa king\n"
    .string "of Judah did Baasha slay him, and\l"
    .string "reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he\n"
    .string "reigned, that he smote all the house\l"
    .string "of Jeroboam; he left not to Jeroboam\l"
    .string "any that breathed, until he had\l"
    .string "destroyed him, according unto the\l"
    .string "saying of the LORD, which he spake by\l"
    .string "his servant Ahijah the Shilonite:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_30::
    .string "Because of the sins of Jeroboam\n"
    .string "which he sinned, and which he made\l"
    .string "Israel sin, by his provocation\l"
    .string "wherewith he provoked the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel to anger$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_31::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Nadab,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_32::
    .string "And there was war between Asa and\n"
    .string "Baasha king of Israel all their\l"
    .string "days$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_33::
    .string "In the third year of Asa king of\n"
    .string "Judah began Baasha the son of Ahijah\l"
    .string "to reign over all Israel in Tirzah,\l"
    .string "twenty and four years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_15_34::
    .string "And he did evil in the sight of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and walked in the way of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam, and in his sin wherewith he\l"
    .string "made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_1::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Jehu the son of Hanani against\l"
    .string "Baasha, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_2::
    .string "Forasmuch as I exalted thee out of\n"
    .string "the dust, and made thee prince over\l"
    .string "my people Israel; and thou hast\l"
    .string "walked in the way of Jeroboam, and\l"
    .string "hast made my people Israel to sin,\l"
    .string "to provoke me to anger with their\l"
    .string "sins;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_3::
    .string "Behold, I will take away the\n"
    .string "posterity of Baasha, and the\l"
    .string "posterity of his house; and will\l"
    .string "make thy house like the house of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam the son of Nebat$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_4::
    .string "Him that dieth of Baasha in the city\n"
    .string "shall the dogs eat; and him that\l"
    .string "dieth of his in the fields shall\l"
    .string "the fowls of the air eat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_5::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Baasha,\n"
    .string "and what he did, and his might, are\l"
    .string "they not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_6::
    .string "So Baasha slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah\l"
    .string "his son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_7::
    .string "And also by the hand of the\n"
    .string "prophet Jehu the son of Hanani came\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD against Baasha,\l"
    .string "and against his house, even for all\l"
    .string "the evil that he did in the sight of\l"
    .string "the LORD, in provoking him to anger\l"
    .string "with the work of his hands, in being\l"
    .string "like the house of Jeroboam; and\l"
    .string "because he killed him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_8::
    .string "In the twenty and sixth year of Asa\n"
    .string "king of Judah began Elah the son of\l"
    .string "Baasha to reign over Israel in\l"
    .string "Tirzah, two years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_9::
    .string "And his servant Zimri, captain of\n"
    .string "half his chariots, conspired\l"
    .string "against him, as he was in Tirzah,\l"
    .string "drinking himself drunk in the house\l"
    .string "of Arza steward of his house in\l"
    .string "Tirzah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_10::
    .string "And Zimri went in and smote him, and\n"
    .string "killed him, in the twenty and\l"
    .string "seventh year of Asa king of Judah,\l"
    .string "and reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he began\n"
    .string "to reign, as soon as he sat on his\l"
    .string "throne, that he slew all the house\l"
    .string "of Baasha: he left him not one that\l"
    .string "pisseth against a wall, neither of\l"
    .string "his kinsfolks, nor of his friends.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_12::
    .string "Thus did Zimri destroy all the\n"
    .string "house of Baasha, according to the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD, which he spake\l"
    .string "against Baasha by Jehu the prophet.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_13::
    .string "For all the sins of Baasha, and the\n"
    .string "sins of Elah his son, by which they\l"
    .string "sinned, and by which they made\l"
    .string "Israel to sin, in provoking the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel to anger with their\l"
    .string "vanities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_14::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Elah,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_15::
    .string "In the twenty and seventh year of\n"
    .string "Asa king of Judah did Zimri reign\l"
    .string "seven days in Tirzah. And the\l"
    .string "people were encamped against\l"
    .string "Gibbethon, which belonged to the\l"
    .string "Philistines$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_16::
    .string "And the people that were encamped\n"
    .string "heard say, Zimri hath conspired, and\l"
    .string "hath also slain the king: wherefore\l"
    .string "all Israel made Omri, the captain\l"
    .string "of the host, king over Israel that\l"
    .string "day in the camp.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_17::
    .string "And Omri went up from Gibbethon,\n"
    .string "and all Israel with him, and they\l"
    .string "besieged Tirzah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Zimri saw\n"
    .string "that the city was taken, that he went\l"
    .string "into the palace of the king’s house,\l"
    .string "and burnt the king’s house over him\l"
    .string "with fire, and died.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_19::
    .string "For his sins which he sinned in\n"
    .string "doing evil in the sight of the LORD,\l"
    .string "in walking in the way of Jeroboam,\l"
    .string "and in his sin which he did, to make\l"
    .string "Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_20::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Zimri,\n"
    .string "and his treason that he wrought, are\l"
    .string "they not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_21::
    .string "Then were the people of Israel\n"
    .string "divided into two parts: half of the\l"
    .string "people followed Tibni the son of\l"
    .string "Ginath, to make him king; and half\l"
    .string "followed Omri$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_22::
    .string "But the people that followed\n"
    .string "Omri prevailed against the people\l"
    .string "that followed Tibni the son of\l"
    .string "Ginath: so Tibni died, and Omri\l"
    .string "reigned.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_23::
    .string "In the thirty and first year of Asa\n"
    .string "king of Judah began Omri to reign\l"
    .string "over Israel, twelve years: six\l"
    .string "years reigned he in Tirzah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_24::
    .string "And he bought the hill Samaria of\n"
    .string "Shemer for two talents of silver,\l"
    .string "and built on the hill, and called\l"
    .string "the name of the city which he built,\l"
    .string "after the name of Shemer, owner of\l"
    .string "the hill, Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_25::
    .string "But Omri wrought evil in the eyes\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and did worse than all\l"
    .string "that were before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_26::
    .string "For he walked in all the way of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and in his\l"
    .string "sin wherewith he made Israel to sin,\l"
    .string "to provoke the LORD God of Israel to\l"
    .string "anger with their vanities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_27::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Omri\n"
    .string "which he did, and his might that he\l"
    .string "shewed, are they not written in the\l"
    .string "book of the chronicles of the kings\l"
    .string "of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_28::
    .string "So Omri slept with his fathers, and\n"
    .string "was buried in Samaria: and Ahab his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_29::
    .string "And in the thirty and eighth year of\n"
    .string "Asa king of Judah began Ahab the son\l"
    .string "of Omri to reign over Israel: and\l"
    .string "Ahab the son of Omri reigned over\l"
    .string "Israel in Samaria twenty and two\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_30::
    .string "And Ahab the son of Omri did evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD above all that\l"
    .string "were before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_31::
    .string "And it came to pass, as if it had\n"
    .string "been a light thing for him to walk\l"
    .string "in the sins of Jeroboam the son of\l"
    .string "Nebat, that he took to wife Jezebel\l"
    .string "the daughter of Ethbaal king of the\l"
    .string "Zidonians, and went and served Baal,\l"
    .string "and worshipped him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_32::
    .string "And he reared up an altar for Baal\n"
    .string "in the house of Baal, which he had\l"
    .string "built in Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_33::
    .string "And Ahab made a grove; and Ahab did\n"
    .string "more to provoke the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel to anger than all the kings\l"
    .string "of Israel that were before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_16_34::
    .string "In his days did Hiel the Bethelite\n"
    .string "build Jericho: he laid the\l"
    .string "foundation thereof in Abiram his\l"
    .string "firstborn, and set up the gates\l"
    .string "thereof in his youngest son Segub,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake by Joshua the son of\l"
    .string "Nun.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_1::
    .string "And Elijah the Tishbite, who was of\n"
    .string "the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto\l"
    .string "Ahab, As the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "liveth, before whom I stand, there\l"
    .string "shall not be dew nor rain these\l"
    .string "years, but according to my word.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_2::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "him, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_3::
    .string "Get thee hence, and turn thee\n"
    .string "eastward, and hide thyself by the\l"
    .string "brook Cherith, that is before Jordan$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_4::
    .string "And it shall be, that thou shalt\n"
    .string "drink of the brook; and I have\l"
    .string "commanded the ravens to feed thee\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_5::
    .string "So he went and did according unto\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD: for he went and\l"
    .string "dwelt by the brook Cherith, that is\l"
    .string "before Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_6::
    .string "And the ravens brought him bread and\n"
    .string "flesh in the morning, and bread and\l"
    .string "flesh in the evening; and he drank of\l"
    .string "the brook.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_7::
    .string "And it came to pass after a while,\n"
    .string "that the brook dried up, because\l"
    .string "there had been no rain in the land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_8::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "him, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_9::
    .string "Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which\n"
    .string "belongeth to Zidon, and dwell\l"
    .string "there: behold, I have commanded a\l"
    .string "widow woman there to sustain thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_10::
    .string "So he arose and went to Zarephath.\n"
    .string "And when he came to the gate of the\l"
    .string "city, behold, the widow woman was\l"
    .string "there gathering of sticks: and he\l"
    .string "called to her, and said, Fetch me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, a little water in a\l"
    .string "vessel, that I may drink.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_11::
    .string "And as she was going to fetch it, he\n"
    .string "called to her, and said, Bring me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, a morsel of bread in thine\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_12::
    .string "And she said, As the LORD thy God\n"
    .string "liveth, I have not a cake, but an\l"
    .string "handful of meal in a barrel, and a\l"
    .string "little oil in a cruse: and, behold,\l"
    .string "I am gathering two sticks, that I may\l"
    .string "go in and dress it for me and my son,\l"
    .string "that we may eat it, and die.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_13::
    .string "And Elijah said unto her, Fear not;\n"
    .string "go and do as thou hast said: but make\l"
    .string "me thereof a little cake first, and\l"
    .string "bring it unto me, and after make for\l"
    .string "thee and for thy son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_14::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel, The barrel of meal shall\l"
    .string "not waste, neither shall the cruse\l"
    .string "of oil fail, until the day that the\l"
    .string "LORD sendeth rain upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_15::
    .string "And she went and did according to\n"
    .string "the saying of Elijah: and she, and\l"
    .string "he, and her house, did eat many days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_16::
    .string "And the barrel of meal wasted not,\n"
    .string "neither did the cruse of oil fail,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake by Elijah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_17::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that the son of the woman,\l"
    .string "the mistress of the house, fell\l"
    .string "sick; and his sickness was so sore,\l"
    .string "that there was no breath left in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_18::
    .string "And she said unto Elijah, What have\n"
    .string "I to do with thee, O thou man of God?\l"
    .string "art thou come unto me to call my sin\l"
    .string "to remembrance, and to slay my son?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_19::
    .string "And he said unto her, Give me thy son\n"
    .string " And he took him out of her bosom,\l"
    .string "and carried him up into a loft,\l"
    .string "where he abode, and laid him upon\l"
    .string "his own bed$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_20::
    .string "And he cried unto the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, O LORD my God, hast thou also\l"
    .string "brought evil upon the widow with\l"
    .string "whom I sojourn, by slaying her son?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_21::
    .string "And he stretched himself upon the\n"
    .string "child three times, and cried unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, let this child’s soul\l"
    .string "come into him again$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_22::
    .string "And the LORD heard the voice of\n"
    .string "Elijah; and the soul of the child\l"
    .string "came into him again, and he revived.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_23::
    .string "And Elijah took the child, and\n"
    .string "brought him down out of the chamber\l"
    .string "into the house, and delivered him\l"
    .string "unto his mother: and Elijah said,\l"
    .string "See, thy son liveth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_17_24::
    .string "And the woman said to Elijah, Now by\n"
    .string "this I know that thou art a man of\l"
    .string "God, and that the word of the LORD in\l"
    .string "thy mouth is truth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after many days,\n"
    .string "that the word of the LORD came to\l"
    .string "Elijah in the third year, saying, Go,\l"
    .string "shew thyself unto Ahab; and I will\l"
    .string "send rain upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_2::
    .string "And Elijah went to shew himself\n"
    .string "unto Ahab. And there was a sore\l"
    .string "famine in Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_3::
    .string "And Ahab called Obadiah, which was\n"
    .string "the governor of his house. (Now\l"
    .string "Obadiah feared the LORD greatly:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_4::
    .string "For it was so, when Jezebel cut off\n"
    .string "the prophets of the LORD, that\l"
    .string "Obadiah took an hundred prophets,\l"
    .string "and hid them by fifty in a cave, and\l"
    .string "fed them with bread and water.)"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_5::
    .string "And Ahab said unto Obadiah, Go into\n"
    .string "the land, unto all fountains of\l"
    .string "water, and unto all brooks:\l"
    .string "peradventure we may find grass to\l"
    .string "save the horses and mules alive,\l"
    .string "that we lose not all the beasts$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_6::
    .string "So they divided the land between\n"
    .string "them to pass throughout it: Ahab\l"
    .string "went one way by himself, and Obadiah\l"
    .string "went another way by himself.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_7::
    .string "And as Obadiah was in the way,\n"
    .string "behold, Elijah met him: and he knew\l"
    .string "him, and fell on his face, and said,\l"
    .string "Art thou that my lord Elijah?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_8::
    .string "And he answered him, I am: go, tell\n"
    .string "thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_9::
    .string "And he said, What have I sinned,\n"
    .string "that thou wouldest deliver thy\l"
    .string "servant into the hand of Ahab, to\l"
    .string "slay me?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_10::
    .string "As the LORD thy God liveth, there is\n"
    .string "no nation or kingdom, whither my\l"
    .string "lord hath not sent to seek thee: and\l"
    .string "when they said, He is not there; he\l"
    .string "took an oath of the kingdom and\l"
    .string "nation, that they found thee not$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_11::
    .string "And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy\n"
    .string "lord, Behold, Elijah is here.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_12::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, as soon\n"
    .string "as I am gone from thee, that the\l"
    .string "Spirit of the LORD shall carry thee\l"
    .string "whither I know not; and so when I come\l"
    .string "and tell Ahab, and he cannot find\l"
    .string "thee, he shall slay me: but I thy\l"
    .string "servant fear the LORD from my youth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_13::
    .string "Was it not told my lord what I did\n"
    .string "when Jezebel slew the prophets of\l"
    .string "the LORD, how I hid an hundred men of\l"
    .string "the LORD’s prophets by fifty in a\l"
    .string "cave, and fed them with bread and\l"
    .string "water?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_14::
    .string "And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy\n"
    .string "lord, Behold, Elijah is here: and he\l"
    .string "shall slay me$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_15::
    .string "And Elijah said, As the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts liveth, before whom I stand, I\l"
    .string "will surely shew myself unto him\l"
    .string "to day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_16::
    .string "So Obadiah went to meet Ahab, and\n"
    .string "told him: and Ahab went to meet\l"
    .string "Elijah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Ahab saw\n"
    .string "Elijah, that Ahab said unto him, Art\l"
    .string "thou he that troubleth Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_18::
    .string "And he answered, I have not\n"
    .string "troubled Israel; but thou, and thy\l"
    .string "father’s house, in that ye have\l"
    .string "forsaken the commandments of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and thou hast followed Baalim$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_19::
    .string "Now therefore send, and gather to me\n"
    .string "all Israel unto mount Carmel, and\l"
    .string "the prophets of Baal four hundred\l"
    .string "and fifty, and the prophets of the\l"
    .string "groves four hundred, which eat at\l"
    .string "Jezebel’s table.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_20::
    .string "So Ahab sent unto all the children\n"
    .string "of Israel, and gathered the\l"
    .string "prophets together unto mount Carmel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_21::
    .string "And Elijah came unto all the\n"
    .string "people, and said, How long halt ye\l"
    .string "between two opinions? if the LORD be\l"
    .string "God, follow him: but if Baal, then\l"
    .string "follow him. And the people\l"
    .string "answered him not a word.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_22::
    .string "Then said Elijah unto the people,\n"
    .string "I, even I only, remain a prophet of\l"
    .string "the LORD; but Baal’s prophets are\l"
    .string "four hundred and fifty men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_23::
    .string "Let them therefore give us two\n"
    .string "bullocks; and let them choose one\l"
    .string "bullock for themselves, and cut it\l"
    .string "in pieces, and lay it on wood, and\l"
    .string "put no fire under: and I will dress\l"
    .string "the other bullock, and lay it on\l"
    .string "wood, and put no fire under:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_24::
    .string "And call ye on the name of your\n"
    .string "gods, and I will call on the name\l"
    .string "of the LORD: and the God that\l"
    .string "answereth by fire, let him be God.\l"
    .string "And all the people answered and\l"
    .string "said, It is well spoken$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_25::
    .string "And Elijah said unto the prophets\n"
    .string "of Baal, Choose you one bullock for\l"
    .string "yourselves, and dress it first; for\l"
    .string "ye are many; and call on the name of\l"
    .string "your gods, but put no fire under.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_26::
    .string "And they took the bullock which\n"
    .string "was given them, and they dressed it,\l"
    .string "and called on the name of Baal from\l"
    .string "morning even until noon, saying, O\l"
    .string "Baal, hear us. But there was no\l"
    .string "voice, nor any that answered. And\l"
    .string "they leaped upon the altar which\l"
    .string "was made.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_27::
    .string "And it came to pass at noon, that\n"
    .string "Elijah mocked them, and said, Cry\l"
    .string "aloud: for he is a god; either he is\l"
    .string "talking, or he is pursuing, or he is\l"
    .string "in a journey, or peradventure he\l"
    .string "sleepeth, and must be awaked.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_28::
    .string "And they cried aloud, and cut\n"
    .string "themselves after their manner with\l"
    .string "knives and lancets, till the blood\l"
    .string "gushed out upon them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, when midday was\n"
    .string "past, and they prophesied until the\l"
    .string "time of the offering of the evening\l"
    .string "sacrifice, that there was neither\l"
    .string "voice, nor any to answer, nor any\l"
    .string "that regarded.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_30::
    .string "And Elijah said unto all the\n"
    .string "people, Come near unto me. And all\l"
    .string "the people came near unto him. And\l"
    .string "he repaired the altar of the LORD\l"
    .string "that was broken down.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_31::
    .string "And Elijah took twelve stones,\n"
    .string "according to the number of the tribes\l"
    .string "of the sons of Jacob, unto whom the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD came, saying,\l"
    .string "Israel shall be thy name:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_32::
    .string "And with the stones he built an\n"
    .string "altar in the name of the LORD: and he\l"
    .string "made a trench about the altar, as\l"
    .string "great as would contain two measures\l"
    .string "of seed$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_33::
    .string "And he put the wood in order, and\n"
    .string "cut the bullock in pieces, and\l"
    .string "laid him on the wood, and said, Fill\l"
    .string "four barrels with water, and pour it\l"
    .string "on the burnt sacrifice, and on the\l"
    .string "wood.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_34::
    .string "And he said, Do it the second time.\n"
    .string "And they did it the second time. And\l"
    .string "he said, Do it the third time. And\l"
    .string "they did it the third time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_35::
    .string "And the water ran round about the\n"
    .string "altar; and he filled the trench\l"
    .string "also with water.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_36::
    .string "And it came to pass at the time of\n"
    .string "the offering of the evening\l"
    .string "sacrifice, that Elijah the prophet\l"
    .string "came near, and said, LORD God of\l"
    .string "Abraham, Isaac, and of Israel, let\l"
    .string "it be known this day that thou art\l"
    .string "God in Israel, and that I am thy\l"
    .string "servant, and that I have done all\l"
    .string "these things at thy word.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_37::
    .string "Hear me, O LORD, hear me, that this\n"
    .string "people may know that thou art the\l"
    .string "LORD God, and that thou hast turned\l"
    .string "their heart back again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_38::
    .string "Then the fire of the LORD fell, and\n"
    .string "consumed the burnt sacrifice, and the\l"
    .string "wood, and the stones, and the dust,\l"
    .string "and licked up the water that was in\l"
    .string "the trench.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_39::
    .string "And when all the people saw it,\n"
    .string "they fell on their faces: and they\l"
    .string "said, The LORD, he is the God; the\l"
    .string "LORD, he is the God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_40::
    .string "And Elijah said unto them, Take the\n"
    .string "prophets of Baal; let not one of\l"
    .string "them escape. And they took them: and\l"
    .string "Elijah brought them down to the\l"
    .string "brook Kishon, and slew them there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_41::
    .string "And Elijah said unto Ahab, Get thee\n"
    .string "up, eat and drink; for there is a\l"
    .string "sound of abundance of rain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_42::
    .string "So Ahab went up to eat and to drink.\n"
    .string "And Elijah went up to the top of\l"
    .string "Carmel; and he cast himself down\l"
    .string "upon the earth, and put his face\l"
    .string "between his knees,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_43::
    .string "And said to his servant, Go up now,\n"
    .string "look toward the sea. And he went up,\l"
    .string "and looked, and said, There is\l"
    .string "nothing. And he said, Go again seven\l"
    .string "times$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_44::
    .string "And it came to pass at the seventh\n"
    .string "time, that he said, Behold, there\l"
    .string "ariseth a little cloud out of the\l"
    .string "sea, like a man’s hand. And he said,\l"
    .string "Go up, say unto Ahab, Prepare thy\l"
    .string "chariot, and get thee down that the\l"
    .string "rain stop thee not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_45::
    .string "And it came to pass in the mean\n"
    .string "while, that the heaven was black\l"
    .string "with clouds and wind, and there was a\l"
    .string "great rain. And Ahab rode, and went\l"
    .string "to Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_18_46::
    .string "And the hand of the LORD was on\n"
    .string "Elijah; and he girded up his loins,\l"
    .string "and ran before Ahab to the entrance\l"
    .string "of Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_1::
    .string "And Ahab told Jezebel all that\n"
    .string "Elijah had done, and withal how he\l"
    .string "had slain all the prophets with\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_2::
    .string "Then Jezebel sent a messenger unto\n"
    .string "Elijah, saying, So let the gods do\l"
    .string "to me, and more also, if I make not\l"
    .string "thy life as the life of one of them\l"
    .string "by to morrow about this time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_3::
    .string "And when he saw that, he arose, and\n"
    .string "went for his life, and came to\l"
    .string "Beersheba, which belongeth to Judah,\l"
    .string "and left his servant there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_4::
    .string "But he himself went a day’s journey\n"
    .string "into the wilderness, and came and\l"
    .string "sat down under a juniper tree: and he\l"
    .string "requested for himself that he might\l"
    .string "die; and said, It is enough; now, O\l"
    .string "LORD, take away my life; for I am not\l"
    .string "better than my fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_5::
    .string "And as he lay and slept under a\n"
    .string "juniper tree, behold, then an angel\l"
    .string "touched him, and said unto him, Arise\l"
    .string "and eat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_6::
    .string "And he looked, and, behold, there\n"
    .string "was a cake baken on the coals, and a\l"
    .string "cruse of water at his head. And he did\l"
    .string "eat and drink, and laid him down\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_7::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD came\n"
    .string "again the second time, and touched\l"
    .string "him, and said, Arise and eat; because\l"
    .string "the journey is too great for thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_8::
    .string "And he arose, and did eat and drink,\n"
    .string "and went in the strength of that meat\l"
    .string "forty days and forty nights unto\l"
    .string "Horeb the mount of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_9::
    .string "And he came thither unto a cave, and\n"
    .string "lodged there; and, behold, the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD came to him, and he said\l"
    .string "unto him, What doest thou here,\l"
    .string "Elijah?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_10::
    .string "And he said, I have been very\n"
    .string "jealous for the LORD God of hosts:\l"
    .string "for the children of Israel have\l"
    .string "forsaken thy covenant, thrown down\l"
    .string "thine altars, and slain thy\l"
    .string "prophets with the sword; and I, even\l"
    .string "I only, am left; and they seek my\l"
    .string "life, to take it away$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_11::
    .string "And he said, Go forth, and stand\n"
    .string "upon the mount before the LORD. And,\l"
    .string "behold, the LORD passed by, and a\l"
    .string "great and strong wind rent the\l"
    .string "mountains, and brake in pieces the\l"
    .string "rocks before the LORD; but the LORD\l"
    .string "was not in the wind: and after the\l"
    .string "wind an earthquake; but the LORD was\l"
    .string "not in the earthquake:$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_12::
    .string "And after the earthquake a fire; but\n"
    .string "the LORD was not in the fire: and\l"
    .string "after the fire a still small voice.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_13::
    .string "And it was so, when Elijah heard it,\n"
    .string "that he wrapped his face in his\l"
    .string "mantle, and went out, and stood in\l"
    .string "the entering in of the cave. And,\l"
    .string "behold, there came a voice unto him,\l"
    .string "and said, What doest thou here,\l"
    .string "Elijah?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_14::
    .string "And he said, I have been very\n"
    .string "jealous for the LORD God of hosts:\l"
    .string "because the children of Israel have\l"
    .string "forsaken thy covenant, thrown down\l"
    .string "thine altars, and slain thy\l"
    .string "prophets with the sword; and I, even\l"
    .string "I only, am left; and they seek my\l"
    .string "life, to take it away$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_15::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Go,\n"
    .string "return on thy way to the wilderness\l"
    .string "of Damascus: and when thou comest,\l"
    .string "anoint Hazael to be king over Syria:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_16::
    .string "And Jehu the son of Nimshi shalt\n"
    .string "thou anoint to be king over Israel:\l"
    .string "and Elisha the son of Shaphat of\l"
    .string "Abelmeholah shalt thou anoint to\l"
    .string "be prophet in thy room$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_17::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "him that escapeth the sword of\l"
    .string "Hazael shall Jehu slay: and him\l"
    .string "that escapeth from the sword of Jehu\l"
    .string "shall Elisha slay.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_18::
    .string "Yet I have left me seven thousand\n"
    .string "in Israel, all the knees which have\l"
    .string "not bowed unto Baal, and every mouth\l"
    .string "which hath not kissed him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_19::
    .string "So he departed thence, and found\n"
    .string "Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was\l"
    .string "plowing with twelve yoke of oxen\l"
    .string "before him, and he with the twelfth:\l"
    .string "and Elijah passed by him, and cast\l"
    .string "his mantle upon him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_20::
    .string "And he left the oxen, and ran after\n"
    .string "Elijah, and said, Let me, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, kiss my father and my mother,\l"
    .string "and then I will follow thee. And he\l"
    .string "said unto him, Go back again: for\l"
    .string "what have I done to thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_19_21::
    .string "And he returned back from him, and\n"
    .string "took a yoke of oxen, and slew them,\l"
    .string "and boiled their flesh with the\l"
    .string "instruments of the oxen, and gave\l"
    .string "unto the people, and they did eat.\l"
    .string "Then he arose, and went after\l"
    .string "Elijah, and ministered unto him$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_1::
    .string "And Benhadad the king of Syria\n"
    .string "gathered all his host together: and\l"
    .string "there were thirty and two kings with\l"
    .string "him, and horses, and chariots; and he\l"
    .string "went up and besieged Samaria, and\l"
    .string "warred against it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_2::
    .string "And he sent messengers to Ahab king\n"
    .string "of Israel into the city, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Thus saith Benhadad,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_3::
    .string "Thy silver and thy gold is mine;\n"
    .string "thy wives also and thy children,\l"
    .string "even the goodliest, are mine$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_4::
    .string "And the king of Israel answered and\n"
    .string "said, My lord, O king, according to\l"
    .string "thy saying, I am thine, and all that\l"
    .string "I have.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_5::
    .string "And the messengers came again, and\n"
    .string "said, Thus speaketh Benhadad,\l"
    .string "saying, Although I have sent unto\l"
    .string "thee, saying, Thou shalt deliver me\l"
    .string "thy silver, and thy gold, and thy\l"
    .string "wives, and thy children;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_6::
    .string "Yet I will send my servants unto\n"
    .string "thee to morrow about this time, and\l"
    .string "they shall search thine house, and\l"
    .string "the houses of thy servants; and it\l"
    .string "shall be, that whatsoever is\l"
    .string "pleasant in thine eyes, they shall\l"
    .string "put it in their hand, and take it away$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_7::
    .string "Then the king of Israel called\n"
    .string "all the elders of the land, and\l"
    .string "said, Mark, I pray you, and see how\l"
    .string "this man seeketh mischief: for he\l"
    .string "sent unto me for my wives, and for my\l"
    .string "children, and for my silver, and for\l"
    .string "my gold; and I denied him not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_8::
    .string "And all the elders and all the\n"
    .string "people said unto him, Hearken not\l"
    .string "unto him, nor consent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_9::
    .string "Wherefore he said unto the\n"
    .string "messengers of Benhadad, Tell my\l"
    .string "lord the king, All that thou didst\l"
    .string "send for to thy servant at the first\l"
    .string "I will do: but this thing I may not\l"
    .string "do. And the messengers departed, and\l"
    .string "brought him word again.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_10::
    .string "And Benhadad sent unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, The gods do so unto me, and more\l"
    .string "also, if the dust of Samaria shall\l"
    .string "suffice for handfuls for all the\l"
    .string "people that follow me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_11::
    .string "And the king of Israel answered and\n"
    .string "said, Tell him, Let not him that\l"
    .string "girdeth on his harness boast himself\l"
    .string "as he that putteth it off.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_12::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Benhadad\n"
    .string "heard this message, as he was\l"
    .string "drinking, he and the kings in the\l"
    .string "pavilions, that he said unto his\l"
    .string "servants, Set yourselves in array.\l"
    .string "And they set themselves in array\l"
    .string "against the city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_13::
    .string "And, behold, there came a prophet\n"
    .string "unto Ahab king of Israel, saying,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Hast thou seen\l"
    .string "all this great multitude? behold,\l"
    .string "I will deliver it into thine hand\l"
    .string "this day; and thou shalt know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_14::
    .string "And Ahab said, By whom? And he said,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Even by the\l"
    .string "young men of the princes of the\l"
    .string "provinces. Then he said, Who shall\l"
    .string "order the battle? And he answered,\l"
    .string "Thou.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_15::
    .string "Then he numbered the young men of\n"
    .string "the princes of the provinces, and\l"
    .string "they were two hundred and thirty two:\l"
    .string "and after them he numbered all the\l"
    .string "people, even all the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, being seven thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_16::
    .string "And they went out at noon. But\n"
    .string "Benhadad was drinking himself drunk\l"
    .string "in the pavilions, he and the kings,\l"
    .string "the thirty and two kings that\l"
    .string "helped him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_17::
    .string "And the young men of the princes of\n"
    .string "the provinces went out first; and\l"
    .string "Benhadad sent out, and they told\l"
    .string "him, saying, There are men come out\l"
    .string "of Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_18::
    .string "And he said, Whether they be come\n"
    .string "out for peace, take them alive; or\l"
    .string "whether they be come out for war,\l"
    .string "take them alive.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_19::
    .string "So these young men of the princes\n"
    .string "of the provinces came out of the\l"
    .string "city, and the army which followed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_20::
    .string "And they slew every one his man: and\n"
    .string "the Syrians fled; and Israel\l"
    .string "pursued them: and Benhadad the king\l"
    .string "of Syria escaped on an horse with\l"
    .string "the horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_21::
    .string "And the king of Israel went out, and\n"
    .string "smote the horses and chariots, and\l"
    .string "slew the Syrians with a great\l"
    .string "slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_22::
    .string "And the prophet came to the king of\n"
    .string "Israel, and said unto him, Go,\l"
    .string "strengthen thyself, and mark, and\l"
    .string "see what thou doest: for at the\l"
    .string "return of the year the king of Syria\l"
    .string "will come up against thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_23::
    .string "And the servants of the king of\n"
    .string "Syria said unto him, Their gods are\l"
    .string "gods of the hills; therefore they\l"
    .string "were stronger than we; but let us\l"
    .string "fight against them in the plain, and\l"
    .string "surely we shall be stronger than\l"
    .string "they.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_24::
    .string "And do this thing, Take the kings\n"
    .string "away, every man out of his place,\l"
    .string "and put captains in their rooms:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_25::
    .string "And number thee an army, like the\n"
    .string "army that thou hast lost, horse for\l"
    .string "horse, and chariot for chariot: and\l"
    .string "we will fight against them in the\l"
    .string "plain, and surely we shall be\l"
    .string "stronger than they. And he hearkened\l"
    .string "unto their voice, and did so$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_26::
    .string "And it came to pass at the return of\n"
    .string "the year, that Benhadad numbered the\l"
    .string "Syrians, and went up to Aphek, to\l"
    .string "fight against Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_27::
    .string "And the children of Israel were\n"
    .string "numbered, and were all present, and\l"
    .string "went against them: and the children\l"
    .string "of Israel pitched before them like\l"
    .string "two little flocks of kids; but the\l"
    .string "Syrians filled the country.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_28::
    .string "And there came a man of God, and\n"
    .string "spake unto the king of Israel, and\l"
    .string "said, Thus saith the LORD, Because\l"
    .string "the Syrians have said, The LORD is\l"
    .string "God of the hills, but he is not God\l"
    .string "of the valleys, therefore will I\l"
    .string "deliver all this great multitude\l"
    .string "into thine hand, and ye shall know\l"
    .string "that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_29::
    .string "And they pitched one over against\n"
    .string "the other seven days. And so it was,\l"
    .string "that in the seventh day the battle\l"
    .string "was joined: and the children of\l"
    .string "Israel slew of the Syrians an\l"
    .string "hundred thousand footmen in one day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_30::
    .string "But the rest fled to Aphek, into\n"
    .string "the city; and there a wall fell\l"
    .string "upon twenty and seven thousand of\l"
    .string "the men that were left. And Benhadad\l"
    .string "fled, and came into the city, into an\l"
    .string "inner chamber.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_31::
    .string "And his servants said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold now, we have heard that the\l"
    .string "kings of the house of Israel are\l"
    .string "merciful kings: let us, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, put sackcloth on our loins,\l"
    .string "and ropes upon our heads, and go out\l"
    .string "to the king of Israel: peradventure\l"
    .string "he will save thy life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_32::
    .string "So they girded sackcloth on their\n"
    .string "loins, and put ropes on their heads,\l"
    .string "and came to the king of Israel, and\l"
    .string "said, Thy servant Benhadad saith, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, let me live. And he said,\l"
    .string "Is he yet alive? he is my brother.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_33::
    .string "Now the men did diligently observe\n"
    .string "whether any thing would come from\l"
    .string "him, and did hastily catch it: and\l"
    .string "they said, Thy brother Benhadad. Then\l"
    .string "he said, Go ye, bring him. Then\l"
    .string "Benhadad came forth to him; and he\l"
    .string "caused him to come up into the\l"
    .string "chariot.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_34::
    .string "And Benhadad said unto him, The\n"
    .string "cities, which my father took from thy\l"
    .string "father, I will restore; and thou\l"
    .string "shalt make streets for thee in\l"
    .string "Damascus, as my father made in Samaria\l"
    .string " Then said Ahab, I will send thee\l"
    .string "away with this covenant. So he made a\l"
    .string "covenant with him, and sent him away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_35::
    .string "And a certain man of the sons of the\n"
    .string "prophets said unto his neighbour in\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD, Smite me, I\l"
    .string "pray thee. And the man refused to\l"
    .string "smite him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_36::
    .string "Then said he unto him, Because thou\n"
    .string "hast not obeyed the voice of the\l"
    .string "LORD, behold, as soon as thou art\l"
    .string "departed from me, a lion shall\l"
    .string "slay thee. And as soon as he was\l"
    .string "departed from him, a lion found him,\l"
    .string "and slew him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_37::
    .string "Then he found another man, and said,\n"
    .string "Smite me, I pray thee. And the man\l"
    .string "smote him, so that in smiting he\l"
    .string "wounded him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_38::
    .string "So the prophet departed, and\n"
    .string "waited for the king by the way, and\l"
    .string "disguised himself with ashes upon\l"
    .string "his face.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_39::
    .string "And as the king passed by, he cried\n"
    .string "unto the king: and he said, Thy\l"
    .string "servant went out into the midst of\l"
    .string "the battle; and, behold, a man\l"
    .string "turned aside, and brought a man unto\l"
    .string "me, and said, Keep this man: if by\l"
    .string "any means he be missing, then shall\l"
    .string "thy life be for his life, or else\l"
    .string "thou shalt pay a talent of silver.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_40::
    .string "And as thy servant was busy here and\n"
    .string "there, he was gone. And the king of\l"
    .string "Israel said unto him, So shall thy\l"
    .string "judgment be; thyself hast decided it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_41::
    .string "And he hasted, and took the ashes\n"
    .string "away from his face; and the king of\l"
    .string "Israel discerned him that he was of\l"
    .string "the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_42::
    .string "And he said unto him, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, Because thou hast let go out of\l"
    .string "thy hand a man whom I appointed to\l"
    .string "utter destruction, therefore thy\l"
    .string "life shall go for his life, and thy\l"
    .string "people for his people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_20_43::
    .string "And the king of Israel went to his\n"
    .string "house heavy and displeased, and\l"
    .string "came to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_1::
    .string "And it came to pass after these\n"
    .string "things, that Naboth the Jezreelite\l"
    .string "had a vineyard, which was in\l"
    .string "Jezreel, hard by the palace of Ahab\l"
    .string "king of Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_2::
    .string "And Ahab spake unto Naboth, saying,\n"
    .string "Give me thy vineyard, that I may have\l"
    .string "it for a garden of herbs, because it\l"
    .string "is near unto my house: and I will\l"
    .string "give thee for it a better vineyard\l"
    .string "than it; or, if it seem good to thee,\l"
    .string "I will give thee the worth of it in\l"
    .string "money.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_3::
    .string "And Naboth said to Ahab, The LORD\n"
    .string "forbid it me, that I should give the\l"
    .string "inheritance of my fathers unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_4::
    .string "And Ahab came into his house heavy\n"
    .string "and displeased because of the word\l"
    .string "which Naboth the Jezreelite had\l"
    .string "spoken to him: for he had said, I\l"
    .string "will not give thee the inheritance\l"
    .string "of my fathers. And he laid him down\l"
    .string "upon his bed, and turned away his\l"
    .string "face, and would eat no bread.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_5::
    .string "But Jezebel his wife came to him,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, Why is thy spirit\l"
    .string "so sad, that thou eatest no bread?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_6::
    .string "And he said unto her, Because I\n"
    .string "spake unto Naboth the Jezreelite,\l"
    .string "and said unto him, Give me thy\l"
    .string "vineyard for money; or else, if it\l"
    .string "please thee, I will give thee\l"
    .string "another vineyard for it: and he\l"
    .string "answered, I will not give thee my\l"
    .string "vineyard$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_7::
    .string "And Jezebel his wife said unto him,\n"
    .string "Dost thou now govern the kingdom of\l"
    .string "Israel? arise, and eat bread, and\l"
    .string "let thine heart be merry: I will\l"
    .string "give thee the vineyard of Naboth the\l"
    .string "Jezreelite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_8::
    .string "So she wrote letters in Ahab’s\n"
    .string "name, and sealed them with his seal,\l"
    .string "and sent the letters unto the\l"
    .string "elders and to the nobles that were\l"
    .string "in his city, dwelling with Naboth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_9::
    .string "And she wrote in the letters,\n"
    .string "saying, Proclaim a fast, and set\l"
    .string "Naboth on high among the people:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_10::
    .string "And set two men, sons of Belial,\n"
    .string "before him, to bear witness against\l"
    .string "him, saying, Thou didst blaspheme\l"
    .string "God and the king. And then carry him\l"
    .string "out, and stone him, that he may die$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_11::
    .string "And the men of his city, even the\n"
    .string "elders and the nobles who were the\l"
    .string "inhabitants in his city, did as\l"
    .string "Jezebel had sent unto them, and as it\l"
    .string "was written in the letters which she\l"
    .string "had sent unto them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_12::
    .string "They proclaimed a fast, and set\n"
    .string "Naboth on high among the people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_13::
    .string "And there came in two men, children\n"
    .string "of Belial, and sat before him: and\l"
    .string "the men of Belial witnessed against\l"
    .string "him, even against Naboth, in the\l"
    .string "presence of the people, saying,\l"
    .string "Naboth did blaspheme God and the\l"
    .string "king. Then they carried him forth out\l"
    .string "of the city, and stoned him with\l"
    .string "stones, that he died.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_14::
    .string "Then they sent to Jezebel, saying,\n"
    .string "Naboth is stoned, and is dead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jezebel\n"
    .string "heard that Naboth was stoned, and was\l"
    .string "dead, that Jezebel said to Ahab,\l"
    .string "Arise, take possession of the\l"
    .string "vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite,\l"
    .string "which he refused to give thee for\l"
    .string "money: for Naboth is not alive, but\l"
    .string "dead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Ahab heard\n"
    .string "that Naboth was dead, that Ahab rose\l"
    .string "up to go down to the vineyard of\l"
    .string "Naboth the Jezreelite, to take\l"
    .string "possession of it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_17::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Elijah the Tishbite, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_18::
    .string "Arise, go down to meet Ahab king of\n"
    .string "Israel, which is in Samaria: behold,\l"
    .string "he is in the vineyard of Naboth,\l"
    .string "whither he is gone down to possess it$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_19::
    .string "And thou shalt speak unto him,\n"
    .string "saying, Thus saith the LORD, Hast\l"
    .string "thou killed, and also taken\l"
    .string "possession? And thou shalt speak\l"
    .string "unto him, saying, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, In the place where dogs\l"
    .string "licked the blood of Naboth shall\l"
    .string "dogs lick thy blood, even thine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_20::
    .string "And Ahab said to Elijah, Hast thou\n"
    .string "found me, O mine enemy? And he\l"
    .string "answered, I have found thee: because\l"
    .string "thou hast sold thyself to work evil\l"
    .string "in the sight of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_21::
    .string "Behold, I will bring evil upon\n"
    .string "thee, and will take away thy\l"
    .string "posterity, and will cut off from\l"
    .string "Ahab him that pisseth against the\l"
    .string "wall, and him that is shut up and\l"
    .string "left in Israel,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_22::
    .string "And will make thine house like the\n"
    .string "house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat,\l"
    .string "and like the house of Baasha the son\l"
    .string "of Ahijah, for the provocation\l"
    .string "wherewith thou hast provoked me to\l"
    .string "anger, and made Israel to sin$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_23::
    .string "And of Jezebel also spake the\n"
    .string "LORD, saying, The dogs shall eat\l"
    .string "Jezebel by the wall of Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_24::
    .string "Him that dieth of Ahab in the city\n"
    .string "the dogs shall eat; and him that\l"
    .string "dieth in the field shall the fowls\l"
    .string "of the air eat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_25::
    .string "But there was none like unto Ahab,\n"
    .string "which did sell himself to work\l"
    .string "wickedness in the sight of the LORD,\l"
    .string "whom Jezebel his wife stirred up.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_26::
    .string "And he did very abominably in\n"
    .string "following idols, according to all\l"
    .string "things as did the Amorites, whom the\l"
    .string "LORD cast out before the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_27::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Ahab heard\n"
    .string "those words, that he rent his\l"
    .string "clothes, and put sackcloth upon\l"
    .string "his flesh, and fasted, and lay in\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and went softly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_28::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Elijah the Tishbite, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_21_29::
    .string "Seest thou how Ahab humbleth\n"
    .string "himself before me? because he\l"
    .string "humbleth himself before me, I will\l"
    .string "not bring the evil in his days: but\l"
    .string "in his son’s days will I bring the\l"
    .string "evil upon his house$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_1::
    .string "And they continued three years\n"
    .string "without war between Syria and Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_2::
    .string "And it came to pass in the third\n"
    .string "year, that Jehoshaphat the king of\l"
    .string "Judah came down to the king of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_3::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "his servants, Know ye that Ramoth in\l"
    .string "Gilead is ours, and we be still,\l"
    .string "and take it not out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "king of Syria?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_4::
    .string "And he said unto Jehoshaphat, Wilt\n"
    .string "thou go with me to battle to\l"
    .string "Ramothgilead? And Jehoshaphat said\l"
    .string "to the king of Israel, I am as thou\l"
    .string "art, my people as thy people, my\l"
    .string "horses as thy horses$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_5::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat said unto the king\n"
    .string "of Israel, Enquire, I pray thee, at\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD to day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_6::
    .string "Then the king of Israel gathered\n"
    .string "the prophets together, about four\l"
    .string "hundred men, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Shall I go against Ramothgilead to\l"
    .string "battle, or shall I forbear? And\l"
    .string "they said, Go up; for the LORD\l"
    .string "shall deliver it into the hand of\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_7::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat said, Is there not\n"
    .string "here a prophet of the LORD besides,\l"
    .string "that we might enquire of him?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_8::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man,\l"
    .string "Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we\l"
    .string "may enquire of the LORD: but I hate\l"
    .string "him; for he doth not prophesy good\l"
    .string "concerning me, but evil. And\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king\l"
    .string "say so$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_9::
    .string "Then the king of Israel called an\n"
    .string "officer, and said, Hasten hither\l"
    .string "Micaiah the son of Imlah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_10::
    .string "And the king of Israel and\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat the king of Judah sat\l"
    .string "each on his throne, having put on\l"
    .string "their robes, in a void place in the\l"
    .string "entrance of the gate of Samaria; and\l"
    .string "all the prophets prophesied\l"
    .string "before them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_11::
    .string "And Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah\n"
    .string "made him horns of iron: and he said,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, With these\l"
    .string "shalt thou push the Syrians, until\l"
    .string "thou have consumed them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_12::
    .string "And all the prophets prophesied\n"
    .string "so, saying, Go up to Ramothgilead,\l"
    .string "and prosper: for the LORD shall\l"
    .string "deliver it into the king’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_13::
    .string "And the messenger that was gone to\n"
    .string "call Micaiah spake unto him,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold now, the words of the\l"
    .string "prophets declare good unto the king\l"
    .string "with one mouth: let thy word, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, be like the word of one of\l"
    .string "them, and speak that which is good.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_14::
    .string "And Micaiah said, As the LORD\n"
    .string "liveth, what the LORD saith unto me,\l"
    .string "that will I speak.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_15::
    .string "So he came to the king. And the king\n"
    .string "said unto him, Micaiah, shall we go\l"
    .string "against Ramothgilead to battle, or\l"
    .string "shall we forbear? And he answered\l"
    .string "him, Go, and prosper: for the LORD\l"
    .string "shall deliver it into the hand of\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_16::
    .string "And the king said unto him, How many\n"
    .string "times shall I adjure thee that thou\l"
    .string "tell me nothing but that which is\l"
    .string "true in the name of the LORD?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_17::
    .string "And he said, I saw all Israel\n"
    .string "scattered upon the hills, as sheep\l"
    .string "that have not a shepherd: and the\l"
    .string "LORD said, These have no master: let\l"
    .string "them return every man to his house in\l"
    .string "peace$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_18::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, Did I not tell thee\l"
    .string "that he would prophesy no good\l"
    .string "concerning me, but evil?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_19::
    .string "And he said, Hear thou therefore the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD: I saw the LORD\l"
    .string "sitting on his throne, and all the\l"
    .string "host of heaven standing by him on his\l"
    .string "right hand and on his left$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_20::
    .string "And the LORD said, Who shall\n"
    .string "persuade Ahab, that he may go up and\l"
    .string "fall at Ramothgilead? And one said\l"
    .string "on this manner, and another said on\l"
    .string "that manner.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_21::
    .string "And there came forth a spirit, and\n"
    .string "stood before the LORD, and said, I\l"
    .string "will persuade him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_22::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him,\n"
    .string "Wherewith? And he said, I will go\l"
    .string "forth, and I will be a lying spirit\l"
    .string "in the mouth of all his prophets.\l"
    .string "And he said, Thou shalt persuade\l"
    .string "him, and prevail also: go forth,\l"
    .string "and do so.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_23::
    .string "Now therefore, behold, the LORD\n"
    .string "hath put a lying spirit in the\l"
    .string "mouth of all these thy prophets,\l"
    .string "and the LORD hath spoken evil\l"
    .string "concerning thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_24::
    .string "But Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah\n"
    .string "went near, and smote Micaiah on the\l"
    .string "cheek, and said, Which way went the\l"
    .string "Spirit of the LORD from me to speak\l"
    .string "unto thee?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_25::
    .string "And Micaiah said, Behold, thou\n"
    .string "shalt see in that day, when thou\l"
    .string "shalt go into an inner chamber to\l"
    .string "hide thyself$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_26::
    .string "And the king of Israel said, Take\n"
    .string "Micaiah, and carry him back unto Amon\l"
    .string "the governor of the city, and to\l"
    .string "Joash the king’s son;"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_27::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the king, Put\n"
    .string "this fellow in the prison, and feed\l"
    .string "him with bread of affliction and\l"
    .string "with water of affliction, until I\l"
    .string "come in peace$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_28::
    .string "And Micaiah said, If thou return at\n"
    .string "all in peace, the LORD hath not\l"
    .string "spoken by me. And he said, Hearken, O\l"
    .string "people, every one of you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_29::
    .string "So the king of Israel and\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went\l"
    .string "up to Ramothgilead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_30::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, I will disguise\l"
    .string "myself, and enter into the battle;\l"
    .string "but put thou on thy robes. And the\l"
    .string "king of Israel disguised himself,\l"
    .string "and went into the battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_31::
    .string "But the king of Syria commanded his\n"
    .string "thirty and two captains that had\l"
    .string "rule over his chariots, saying,\l"
    .string "Fight neither with small nor great,\l"
    .string "save only with the king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_32::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "captains of the chariots saw\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, that they said, Surely\l"
    .string "it is the king of Israel. And they\l"
    .string "turned aside to fight against him:\l"
    .string "and Jehoshaphat cried out.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_33::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "captains of the chariots perceived\l"
    .string "that it was not the king of Israel,\l"
    .string "that they turned back from pursuing\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_34::
    .string "And a certain man drew a bow at a\n"
    .string "venture, and smote the king of\l"
    .string "Israel between the joints of the\l"
    .string "harness: wherefore he said unto the\l"
    .string "driver of his chariot, Turn thine\l"
    .string "hand, and carry me out of the host;\l"
    .string "for I am wounded.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_35::
    .string "And the battle increased that day:\n"
    .string "and the king was stayed up in his\l"
    .string "chariot against the Syrians, and died\l"
    .string "at even: and the blood ran out of the\l"
    .string "wound into the midst of the chariot.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_36::
    .string "And there went a proclamation\n"
    .string "throughout the host about the going\l"
    .string "down of the sun, saying, Every man to\l"
    .string "his city, and every man to his own\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_37::
    .string "So the king died, and was brought to\n"
    .string "Samaria; and they buried the king in\l"
    .string "Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_38::
    .string "And one washed the chariot in the\n"
    .string "pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked\l"
    .string "up his blood; and they washed his\l"
    .string "armour; according unto the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD which he spake.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_39::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Ahab, and\n"
    .string "all that he did, and the ivory house\l"
    .string "which he made, and all the cities\l"
    .string "that he built, are they not written\l"
    .string "in the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_40::
    .string "So Ahab slept with his fathers; and\n"
    .string "Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_41::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat the son of Asa\n"
    .string "began to reign over Judah in the\l"
    .string "fourth year of Ahab king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_42::
    .string "Jehoshaphat was thirty and five\n"
    .string "years old when he began to reign; and\l"
    .string "he reigned twenty and five years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_43::
    .string "And he walked in all the ways of\n"
    .string "Asa his father; he turned not aside\l"
    .string "from it, doing that which was right\l"
    .string "in the eyes of the LORD:\l"
    .string "nevertheless the high places were\l"
    .string "not taken away; for the people\l"
    .string "offered and burnt incense yet in the\l"
    .string "high places.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_44::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat made peace with\n"
    .string "the king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_45::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, and his might that he\l"
    .string "shewed, and how he warred, are they\l"
    .string "not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_46::
    .string "And the remnant of the sodomites,\n"
    .string "which remained in the days of his\l"
    .string "father Asa, he took out of the land$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_47::
    .string "There was then no king in Edom: a\n"
    .string "deputy was king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_48::
    .string "Jehoshaphat made ships of\n"
    .string "Tharshish to go to Ophir for gold:\l"
    .string "but they went not; for the ships were\l"
    .string "broken at Eziongeber.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_49::
    .string "Then said Ahaziah the son of Ahab\n"
    .string "unto Jehoshaphat, Let my servants go\l"
    .string "with thy servants in the ships. But\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat would not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_50::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried with his\l"
    .string "fathers in the city of David his\l"
    .string "father: and Jehoram his son reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_51::
    .string "Ahaziah the son of Ahab began to\n"
    .string "reign over Israel in Samaria the\l"
    .string "seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat\l"
    .string "king of Judah, and reigned two years\l"
    .string "over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_52::
    .string "And he did evil in the sight of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and walked in the way of his\l"
    .string "father, and in the way of his mother,\l"
    .string "and in the way of Jeroboam the son of\l"
    .string "Nebat, who made Israel to sin:"
Bible_Text_1_Kings_22_53::
    .string "For he served Baal, and worshipped\n"
    .string "him, and provoked to anger the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, according to all\l"
    .string "that his father had done$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_1::
    .string "Then Moab rebelled against Israel\n"
    .string "after the death of Ahab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_2::
    .string "And Ahaziah fell down through a\n"
    .string "lattice in his upper chamber that\l"
    .string "was in Samaria, and was sick: and he\l"
    .string "sent messengers, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Go, enquire of Baalzebub the god of\l"
    .string "Ekron whether I shall recover of\l"
    .string "this disease.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_3::
    .string "But the angel of the LORD said to\n"
    .string "Elijah the Tishbite, Arise, go up to\l"
    .string "meet the messengers of the king of\l"
    .string "Samaria, and say unto them, Is it not\l"
    .string "because there is not a God in Israel,\l"
    .string "that ye go to enquire of Baalzebub\l"
    .string "the god of Ekron?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_4::
    .string "Now therefore thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "Thou shalt not come down from that\l"
    .string "bed on which thou art gone up, but\l"
    .string "shalt surely die. And Elijah\l"
    .string "departed$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_5::
    .string "And when the messengers turned back\n"
    .string "unto him, he said unto them, Why are\l"
    .string "ye now turned back?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_6::
    .string "And they said unto him, There came a\n"
    .string "man up to meet us, and said unto us,\l"
    .string "Go, turn again unto the king that\l"
    .string "sent you, and say unto him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Is it not because\l"
    .string "there is not a God in Israel, that\l"
    .string "thou sendest to enquire of Baalzebub\l"
    .string "the god of Ekron? therefore thou\l"
    .string "shalt not come down from that bed on\l"
    .string "which thou art gone up, but shalt\l"
    .string "surely die$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_7::
    .string "And he said unto them, What manner\n"
    .string "of man was he which came up to meet\l"
    .string "you, and told you these words?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_8::
    .string "And they answered him, He was an\n"
    .string "hairy man, and girt with a girdle of\l"
    .string "leather about his loins. And he\l"
    .string "said, It is Elijah the Tishbite$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_9::
    .string "Then the king sent unto him a\n"
    .string "captain of fifty with his fifty. And\l"
    .string "he went up to him: and, behold, he\l"
    .string "sat on the top of an hill. And he\l"
    .string "spake unto him, Thou man of God, the\l"
    .string "king hath said, Come down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_10::
    .string "And Elijah answered and said to the\n"
    .string "captain of fifty, If I be a man of\l"
    .string "God, then let fire come down from\l"
    .string "heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty\l"
    .string " And there came down fire from\l"
    .string "heaven, and consumed him and his\l"
    .string "fifty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_11::
    .string "Again also he sent unto him another\n"
    .string "captain of fifty with his fifty. And\l"
    .string "he answered and said unto him, O man\l"
    .string "of God, thus hath the king said, Come\l"
    .string "down quickly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_12::
    .string "And Elijah answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, If I be a man of God, let fire\l"
    .string "come down from heaven, and consume\l"
    .string "thee and thy fifty. And the fire of\l"
    .string "God came down from heaven, and\l"
    .string "consumed him and his fifty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_13::
    .string "And he sent again a captain of the\n"
    .string "third fifty with his fifty. And the\l"
    .string "third captain of fifty went up, and\l"
    .string "came and fell on his knees before\l"
    .string "Elijah, and besought him, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, O man of God, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "let my life, and the life of these\l"
    .string "fifty thy servants, be precious in\l"
    .string "thy sight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_14::
    .string "Behold, there came fire down from\n"
    .string "heaven, and burnt up the two\l"
    .string "captains of the former fifties with\l"
    .string "their fifties: therefore let my\l"
    .string "life now be precious in thy sight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_15::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD said unto\n"
    .string "Elijah, Go down with him: be not\l"
    .string "afraid of him. And he arose, and went\l"
    .string "down with him unto the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_16::
    .string "And he said unto him, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast sent\l"
    .string "messengers to enquire of Baalzebub\l"
    .string "the god of Ekron, is it not because\l"
    .string "there is no God in Israel to enquire\l"
    .string "of his word? therefore thou shalt\l"
    .string "not come down off that bed on which\l"
    .string "thou art gone up, but shalt surely\l"
    .string "die.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_17::
    .string "So he died according to the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD which Elijah had spoken.\l"
    .string "And Jehoram reigned in his stead in\l"
    .string "the second year of Jehoram the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because\l"
    .string "he had no son.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_1_18::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah\n"
    .string "which he did, are they not written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the LORD\n"
    .string "would take up Elijah into heaven by\l"
    .string "a whirlwind, that Elijah went with\l"
    .string "Elisha from Gilgal$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_2::
    .string "And Elijah said unto Elisha, Tarry\n"
    .string "here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "sent me to Bethel. And Elisha said\l"
    .string "unto him, As the LORD liveth, and as\l"
    .string "thy soul liveth, I will not leave\l"
    .string "thee. So they went down to Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_3::
    .string "And the sons of the prophets that\n"
    .string "were at Bethel came forth to Elisha,\l"
    .string "and said unto him, Knowest thou that\l"
    .string "the LORD will take away thy master\l"
    .string "from thy head to day? And he said,\l"
    .string "Yea, I know it; hold ye your peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_4::
    .string "And Elijah said unto him, Elisha,\n"
    .string "tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath sent me to Jericho. And he said,\l"
    .string "As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul\l"
    .string "liveth, I will not leave thee. So\l"
    .string "they came to Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_5::
    .string "And the sons of the prophets that\n"
    .string "were at Jericho came to Elisha, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Knowest thou that the\l"
    .string "LORD will take away thy master from\l"
    .string "thy head to day? And he answered, Yea,\l"
    .string "I know it; hold ye your peace.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_6::
    .string "And Elijah said unto him, Tarry, I\n"
    .string "pray thee, here; for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "sent me to Jordan. And he said, As the\l"
    .string "LORD liveth, and as thy soul\l"
    .string "liveth, I will not leave thee. And\l"
    .string "they two went on.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_7::
    .string "And fifty men of the sons of the\n"
    .string "prophets went, and stood to view\l"
    .string "afar off: and they two stood by\l"
    .string "Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_8::
    .string "And Elijah took his mantle, and\n"
    .string "wrapped it together, and smote the\l"
    .string "waters, and they were divided hither\l"
    .string "and thither, so that they two went\l"
    .string "over on dry ground.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_9::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they were\n"
    .string "gone over, that Elijah said unto\l"
    .string "Elisha, Ask what I shall do for\l"
    .string "thee, before I be taken away from thee\l"
    .string " And Elisha said, I pray thee, let\l"
    .string "a double portion of thy spirit be\l"
    .string "upon me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_10::
    .string "And he said, Thou hast asked a hard\n"
    .string "thing: nevertheless, if thou see me\l"
    .string "when I am taken from thee, it shall\l"
    .string "be so unto thee; but if not, it\l"
    .string "shall not be so.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they still\n"
    .string "went on, and talked, that, behold,\l"
    .string "there appeared a chariot of fire,\l"
    .string "and horses of fire, and parted them\l"
    .string "both asunder; and Elijah went up by\l"
    .string "a whirlwind into heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_12::
    .string "And Elisha saw it, and he cried, My\n"
    .string "father, my father, the chariot of\l"
    .string "Israel, and the horsemen thereof.\l"
    .string "And he saw him no more: and he took\l"
    .string "hold of his own clothes, and rent\l"
    .string "them in two pieces.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_13::
    .string "He took up also the mantle of\n"
    .string "Elijah that fell from him, and went\l"
    .string "back, and stood by the bank of\l"
    .string "Jordan;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_14::
    .string "And he took the mantle of Elijah\n"
    .string "that fell from him, and smote the\l"
    .string "waters, and said, Where is the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Elijah? and when he also had\l"
    .string "smitten the waters, they parted\l"
    .string "hither and thither: and Elisha went\l"
    .string "over$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_15::
    .string "And when the sons of the prophets\n"
    .string "which were to view at Jericho saw\l"
    .string "him, they said, The spirit of Elijah\l"
    .string "doth rest on Elisha. And they came to\l"
    .string "meet him, and bowed themselves to\l"
    .string "the ground before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_16::
    .string "And they said unto him, Behold now,\n"
    .string "there be with thy servants fifty\l"
    .string "strong men; let them go, we pray\l"
    .string "thee, and seek thy master: lest\l"
    .string "peradventure the Spirit of the LORD\l"
    .string "hath taken him up, and cast him upon\l"
    .string "some mountain, or into some valley.\l"
    .string "And he said, Ye shall not send.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_17::
    .string "And when they urged him till he was\n"
    .string "ashamed, he said, Send. They sent\l"
    .string "therefore fifty men; and they sought\l"
    .string "three days, but found him not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_18::
    .string "And when they came again to him,\n"
    .string "(for he tarried at Jericho,) he said\l"
    .string "unto them, Did I not say unto you, Go\l"
    .string "not?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_19::
    .string "And the men of the city said unto\n"
    .string "Elisha, Behold, I pray thee, the\l"
    .string "situation of this city is pleasant,\l"
    .string "as my lord seeth: but the water is\l"
    .string "naught, and the ground barren$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_20::
    .string "And he said, Bring me a new cruse,\n"
    .string "and put salt therein. And they\l"
    .string "brought it to him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_21::
    .string "And he went forth unto the spring\n"
    .string "of the waters, and cast the salt in\l"
    .string "there, and said, Thus saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "I have healed these waters; there\l"
    .string "shall not be from thence any more\l"
    .string "death or barren land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_22::
    .string "So the waters were healed unto this\n"
    .string "day, according to the saying of\l"
    .string "Elisha which he spake.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_23::
    .string "And he went up from thence unto\n"
    .string "Bethel: and as he was going up by\l"
    .string "the way, there came forth little\l"
    .string "children out of the city, and mocked\l"
    .string "him, and said unto him, Go up, thou\l"
    .string "bald head; go up, thou bald head.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_24::
    .string "And he turned back, and looked on\n"
    .string "them, and cursed them in the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD. And there came forth two\l"
    .string "she bears out of the wood, and tare\l"
    .string "forty and two children of them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_2_25::
    .string "And he went from thence to mount\n"
    .string "Carmel, and from thence he returned\l"
    .string "to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_1::
    .string "Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to\n"
    .string "reign over Israel in Samaria the\l"
    .string "eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king\l"
    .string "of Judah, and reigned twelve years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_2::
    .string "And he wrought evil in the sight of\n"
    .string "the LORD; but not like his father,\l"
    .string "and like his mother: for he put away\l"
    .string "the image of Baal that his father\l"
    .string "had made.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_3::
    .string "Nevertheless he cleaved unto the\n"
    .string "sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat,\l"
    .string "which made Israel to sin; he\l"
    .string "departed not therefrom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_4::
    .string "And Mesha king of Moab was a\n"
    .string "sheepmaster, and rendered unto the\l"
    .string "king of Israel an hundred thousand\l"
    .string "lambs, and an hundred thousand rams,\l"
    .string "with the wool.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_5::
    .string "But it came to pass, when Ahab was\n"
    .string "dead, that the king of Moab rebelled\l"
    .string "against the king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_6::
    .string "And king Jehoram went out of Samaria\n"
    .string "the same time, and numbered all\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_7::
    .string "And he went and sent to Jehoshaphat\n"
    .string "the king of Judah, saying, The king\l"
    .string "of Moab hath rebelled against me:\l"
    .string "wilt thou go with me against Moab to\l"
    .string "battle? And he said, I will go up:\l"
    .string "I am as thou art, my people as thy\l"
    .string "people, and my horses as thy horses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_8::
    .string "And he said, Which way shall we go\n"
    .string "up? And he answered, The way through\l"
    .string "the wilderness of Edom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_9::
    .string "So the king of Israel went, and the\n"
    .string "king of Judah, and the king of Edom:\l"
    .string "and they fetched a compass of seven\l"
    .string "days’ journey: and there was no water\l"
    .string "for the host, and for the cattle that\l"
    .string "followed them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_10::
    .string "And the king of Israel said, Alas!\n"
    .string "that the LORD hath called these\l"
    .string "three kings together, to deliver\l"
    .string "them into the hand of Moab!"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_11::
    .string "But Jehoshaphat said, Is there not\n"
    .string "here a prophet of the LORD, that we\l"
    .string "may enquire of the LORD by him? And\l"
    .string "one of the king of Israel’s servants\l"
    .string "answered and said, Here is Elisha\l"
    .string "the son of Shaphat, which poured\l"
    .string "water on the hands of Elijah$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_12::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat said, The word of\n"
    .string "the LORD is with him. So the king of\l"
    .string "Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king\l"
    .string "of Edom went down to him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_13::
    .string "And Elisha said unto the king of\n"
    .string "Israel, What have I to do with thee?\l"
    .string "get thee to the prophets of thy\l"
    .string "father, and to the prophets of thy\l"
    .string "mother. And the king of Israel said\l"
    .string "unto him, Nay: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "called these three kings together,\l"
    .string "to deliver them into the hand of\l"
    .string "Moab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_14::
    .string "And Elisha said, As the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts liveth, before whom I stand,\l"
    .string "surely, were it not that I regard the\l"
    .string "presence of Jehoshaphat the king of\l"
    .string "Judah, I would not look toward thee,\l"
    .string "nor see thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_15::
    .string "But now bring me a minstrel. And it\n"
    .string "came to pass, when the minstrel\l"
    .string "played, that the hand of the LORD\l"
    .string "came upon him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_16::
    .string "And he said, Thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "Make this valley full of ditches.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_17::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Ye shall\n"
    .string "not see wind, neither shall ye see\l"
    .string "rain; yet that valley shall be\l"
    .string "filled with water, that ye may\l"
    .string "drink, both ye, and your cattle, and\l"
    .string "your beasts.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_18::
    .string "And this is but a light thing in the\n"
    .string "sight of the LORD: he will deliver\l"
    .string "the Moabites also into your hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_19::
    .string "And ye shall smite every fenced\n"
    .string "city, and every choice city, and\l"
    .string "shall fell every good tree, and\l"
    .string "stop all wells of water, and mar\l"
    .string "every good piece of land with\l"
    .string "stones.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_20::
    .string "And it came to pass in the morning,\n"
    .string "when the meat offering was offered,\l"
    .string "that, behold, there came water by\l"
    .string "the way of Edom, and the country was\l"
    .string "filled with water.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_21::
    .string "And when all the Moabites heard\n"
    .string "that the kings were come up to fight\l"
    .string "against them, they gathered all\l"
    .string "that were able to put on armour, and\l"
    .string "upward, and stood in the border.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_22::
    .string "And they rose up early in the\n"
    .string "morning, and the sun shone upon the\l"
    .string "water, and the Moabites saw the water\l"
    .string "on the other side as red as blood:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_23::
    .string "And they said, This is blood: the\n"
    .string "kings are surely slain, and they\l"
    .string "have smitten one another: now\l"
    .string "therefore, Moab, to the spoil$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_24::
    .string "And when they came to the camp of\n"
    .string "Israel, the Israelites rose up and\l"
    .string "smote the Moabites, so that they\l"
    .string "fled before them: but they went\l"
    .string "forward smiting the Moabites, even in\l"
    .string "their country.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_25::
    .string "And they beat down the cities, and\n"
    .string "on every good piece of land cast\l"
    .string "every man his stone, and filled it;\l"
    .string "and they stopped all the wells of\l"
    .string "water, and felled all the good\l"
    .string "trees: only in Kirharaseth left\l"
    .string "they the stones thereof; howbeit the\l"
    .string "slingers went about it, and smote it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_26::
    .string "And when the king of Moab saw that\n"
    .string "the battle was too sore for him, he\l"
    .string "took with him seven hundred men that\l"
    .string "drew swords, to break through even\l"
    .string "unto the king of Edom: but they could\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_3_27::
    .string "Then he took his eldest son that\n"
    .string "should have reigned in his stead,\l"
    .string "and offered him for a burnt offering\l"
    .string "upon the wall. And there was great\l"
    .string "indignation against Israel: and they\l"
    .string "departed from him, and returned to\l"
    .string "their own land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_1::
    .string "Now there cried a certain woman of\n"
    .string "the wives of the sons of the\l"
    .string "prophets unto Elisha, saying, Thy\l"
    .string "servant my husband is dead; and thou\l"
    .string "knowest that thy servant did fear the\l"
    .string "LORD: and the creditor is come to\l"
    .string "take unto him my two sons to be\l"
    .string "bondmen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_2::
    .string "And Elisha said unto her, What\n"
    .string "shall I do for thee? tell me, what\l"
    .string "hast thou in the house? And she said,\l"
    .string "Thine handmaid hath not any thing in\l"
    .string "the house, save a pot of oil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_3::
    .string "Then he said, Go, borrow thee\n"
    .string "vessels abroad of all thy\l"
    .string "neighbours, even empty vessels;\l"
    .string "borrow not a few.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_4::
    .string "And when thou art come in, thou\n"
    .string "shalt shut the door upon thee and\l"
    .string "upon thy sons, and shalt pour out\l"
    .string "into all those vessels, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt set aside that which is full.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_5::
    .string "So she went from him, and shut the\n"
    .string "door upon her and upon her sons, who\l"
    .string "brought the vessels to her; and she\l"
    .string "poured out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "vessels were full, that she said\l"
    .string "unto her son, Bring me yet a vessel.\l"
    .string "And he said unto her, There is not a\l"
    .string "vessel more. And the oil stayed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_7::
    .string "Then she came and told the man of\n"
    .string "God. And he said, Go, sell the oil,\l"
    .string "and pay thy debt, and live thou and\l"
    .string "thy children of the rest.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_8::
    .string "And it fell on a day, that Elisha\n"
    .string "passed to Shunem, where was a great\l"
    .string "woman; and she constrained him to eat\l"
    .string "bread. And so it was, that as oft as\l"
    .string "he passed by, he turned in thither to\l"
    .string "eat bread.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_9::
    .string "And she said unto her husband,\n"
    .string "Behold now, I perceive that this is\l"
    .string "an holy man of God, which passeth by\l"
    .string "us continually.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_10::
    .string "Let us make a little chamber, I\n"
    .string "pray thee, on the wall; and let us\l"
    .string "set for him there a bed, and a table,\l"
    .string "and a stool, and a candlestick: and\l"
    .string "it shall be, when he cometh to us,\l"
    .string "that he shall turn in thither.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_11::
    .string "And it fell on a day, that he came\n"
    .string "thither, and he turned into the\l"
    .string "chamber, and lay there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_12::
    .string "And he said to Gehazi his servant,\n"
    .string "Call this Shunammite. And when he\l"
    .string "had called her, she stood before\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_13::
    .string "And he said unto him, Say now unto\n"
    .string "her, Behold, thou hast been careful\l"
    .string "for us with all this care; what is\l"
    .string "to be done for thee? wouldest thou be\l"
    .string "spoken for to the king, or to the\l"
    .string "captain of the host? And she\l"
    .string "answered, I dwell among mine own\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_14::
    .string "And he said, What then is to be done\n"
    .string "for her? And Gehazi answered, Verily\l"
    .string "she hath no child, and her husband is\l"
    .string "old.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_15::
    .string "And he said, Call her. And when he\n"
    .string "had called her, she stood in the\l"
    .string "door.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_16::
    .string "And he said, About this season,\n"
    .string "according to the time of life, thou\l"
    .string "shalt embrace a son. And she said,\l"
    .string "Nay, my lord, thou man of God, do not\l"
    .string "lie unto thine handmaid.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_17::
    .string "And the woman conceived, and bare a\n"
    .string "son at that season that Elisha had\l"
    .string "said unto her, according to the time\l"
    .string "of life.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_18::
    .string "And when the child was grown, it\n"
    .string "fell on a day, that he went out to\l"
    .string "his father to the reapers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_19::
    .string "And he said unto his father, My\n"
    .string "head, my head. And he said to a lad,\l"
    .string "Carry him to his mother.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_20::
    .string "And when he had taken him, and\n"
    .string "brought him to his mother, he sat on\l"
    .string "her knees till noon, and then died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_21::
    .string "And she went up, and laid him on\n"
    .string "the bed of the man of God, and shut\l"
    .string "the door upon him, and went out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_22::
    .string "And she called unto her husband,\n"
    .string "and said, Send me, I pray thee, one\l"
    .string "of the young men, and one of the\l"
    .string "asses, that I may run to the man of\l"
    .string "God, and come again.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_23::
    .string "And he said, Wherefore wilt thou go\n"
    .string "to him to day? it is neither new moon,\l"
    .string "nor sabbath. And she said, It shall\l"
    .string "be well.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_24::
    .string "Then she saddled an ass, and said to\n"
    .string "her servant, Drive, and go forward;\l"
    .string "slack not thy riding for me, except\l"
    .string "I bid thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_25::
    .string "So she went and came unto the man of\n"
    .string "God to mount Carmel. And it came to\l"
    .string "pass, when the man of God saw her afar\l"
    .string "off, that he said to Gehazi his\l"
    .string "servant, Behold, yonder is that\l"
    .string "Shunammite:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_26::
    .string "Run now, I pray thee, to meet her,\n"
    .string "and say unto her, Is it well with\l"
    .string "thee? is it well with thy husband?\l"
    .string "is it well with the child? And she\l"
    .string "answered, It is well:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_27::
    .string "And when she came to the man of God\n"
    .string "to the hill, she caught him by the\l"
    .string "feet: but Gehazi came near to thrust\l"
    .string "her away. And the man of God said, Let\l"
    .string "her alone; for her soul is vexed\l"
    .string "within her: and the LORD hath hid it\l"
    .string "from me, and hath not told me$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_28::
    .string "Then she said, Did I desire a son of\n"
    .string "my lord? did I not say, Do not\l"
    .string "deceive me?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_29::
    .string "Then he said to Gehazi, Gird up thy\n"
    .string "loins, and take my staff in thine\l"
    .string "hand, and go thy way: if thou meet any\l"
    .string "man, salute him not; and if any\l"
    .string "salute thee, answer him not again:\l"
    .string "and lay my staff upon the face of\l"
    .string "the child$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_30::
    .string "And the mother of the child said, As\n"
    .string "the LORD liveth, and as thy soul\l"
    .string "liveth, I will not leave thee. And\l"
    .string "he arose, and followed her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_31::
    .string "And Gehazi passed on before them,\n"
    .string "and laid the staff upon the face of\l"
    .string "the child; but there was neither\l"
    .string "voice, nor hearing. Wherefore he went\l"
    .string "again to meet him, and told him,\l"
    .string "saying, The child is not awaked.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_32::
    .string "And when Elisha was come into the\n"
    .string "house, behold, the child was dead,\l"
    .string "and laid upon his bed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_33::
    .string "He went in therefore, and shut the\n"
    .string "door upon them twain, and prayed\l"
    .string "unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_34::
    .string "And he went up, and lay upon the\n"
    .string "child, and put his mouth upon his\l"
    .string "mouth, and his eyes upon his eyes,\l"
    .string "and his hands upon his hands: and\l"
    .string "stretched himself upon the child;\l"
    .string "and the flesh of the child waxed\l"
    .string "warm.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_35::
    .string "Then he returned, and walked in the\n"
    .string "house to and fro; and went up, and\l"
    .string "stretched himself upon him: and the\l"
    .string "child sneezed seven times, and the\l"
    .string "child opened his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_36::
    .string "And he called Gehazi, and said,\n"
    .string "Call this Shunammite. So he called\l"
    .string "her. And when she was come in unto\l"
    .string "him, he said, Take up thy son.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_37::
    .string "Then she went in, and fell at his\n"
    .string "feet, and bowed herself to the\l"
    .string "ground, and took up her son, and went\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_38::
    .string "And Elisha came again to Gilgal:\n"
    .string "and there was a dearth in the land;\l"
    .string "and the sons of the prophets were\l"
    .string "sitting before him: and he said unto\l"
    .string "his servant, Set on the great pot,\l"
    .string "and seethe pottage for the sons of\l"
    .string "the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_39::
    .string "And one went out into the field to\n"
    .string "gather herbs, and found a wild vine,\l"
    .string "and gathered thereof wild gourds his\l"
    .string "lap full, and came and shred them\l"
    .string "into the pot of pottage: for they\l"
    .string "knew them not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_40::
    .string "So they poured out for the men to\n"
    .string "eat. And it came to pass, as they\l"
    .string "were eating of the pottage, that\l"
    .string "they cried out, and said, O thou man\l"
    .string "of God, there is death in the pot.\l"
    .string "And they could not eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_41::
    .string "But he said, Then bring meal. And he\n"
    .string "cast it into the pot; and he said,\l"
    .string "Pour out for the people, that they\l"
    .string "may eat. And there was no harm in the\l"
    .string "pot.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_42::
    .string "And there came a man from\n"
    .string "Baalshalisha, and brought the man\l"
    .string "of God bread of the firstfruits,\l"
    .string "twenty loaves of barley, and full\l"
    .string "ears of corn in the husk thereof. And\l"
    .string "he said, Give unto the people, that\l"
    .string "they may eat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_43::
    .string "And his servitor said, What, should\n"
    .string "I set this before an hundred men? He\l"
    .string "said again, Give the people, that\l"
    .string "they may eat: for thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, They shall eat, and shall\l"
    .string "leave thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_4_44::
    .string "So he set it before them, and they\n"
    .string "did eat, and left thereof, according\l"
    .string "to the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_1::
    .string "Now Naaman, captain of the host of\n"
    .string "the king of Syria, was a great man\l"
    .string "with his master, and honourable,\l"
    .string "because by him the LORD had given\l"
    .string "deliverance unto Syria: he was also\l"
    .string "a mighty man in valour, but he was a\l"
    .string "leper.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_2::
    .string "And the Syrians had gone out by\n"
    .string "companies, and had brought away\l"
    .string "captive out of the land of Israel a\l"
    .string "little maid; and she waited on\l"
    .string "Naaman’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_3::
    .string "And she said unto her mistress,\n"
    .string "Would God my lord were with the\l"
    .string "prophet that is in Samaria! for he\l"
    .string "would recover him of his leprosy.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_4::
    .string "And one went in, and told his lord,\n"
    .string "saying, Thus and thus said the maid\l"
    .string "that is of the land of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_5::
    .string "And the king of Syria said, Go to,\n"
    .string "go, and I will send a letter unto\l"
    .string "the king of Israel. And he departed,\l"
    .string "and took with him ten talents of\l"
    .string "silver, and six thousand pieces of\l"
    .string "gold, and ten changes of raiment.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_6::
    .string "And he brought the letter to the\n"
    .string "king of Israel, saying, Now when\l"
    .string "this letter is come unto thee,\l"
    .string "behold, I have therewith sent Naaman\l"
    .string "my servant to thee, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "recover him of his leprosy.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_7::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "of Israel had read the letter, that\l"
    .string "he rent his clothes, and said, Am I\l"
    .string "God, to kill and to make alive,\l"
    .string "that this man doth send unto me to\l"
    .string "recover a man of his leprosy?\l"
    .string "wherefore consider, I pray you, and\l"
    .string "see how he seeketh a quarrel against\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_8::
    .string "And it was so, when Elisha the man\n"
    .string "of God had heard that the king of\l"
    .string "Israel had rent his clothes, that he\l"
    .string "sent to the king, saying, Wherefore\l"
    .string "hast thou rent thy clothes? let him\l"
    .string "come now to me, and he shall know\l"
    .string "that there is a prophet in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_9::
    .string "So Naaman came with his horses and\n"
    .string "with his chariot, and stood at the\l"
    .string "door of the house of Elisha.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_10::
    .string "And Elisha sent a messenger unto\n"
    .string "him, saying, Go and wash in Jordan\l"
    .string "seven times, and thy flesh shall\l"
    .string "come again to thee, and thou shalt be\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_11::
    .string "But Naaman was wroth, and went away,\n"
    .string "and said, Behold, I thought, He\l"
    .string "will surely come out to me, and\l"
    .string "stand, and call on the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD his God, and strike his hand\l"
    .string "over the place, and recover the\l"
    .string "leper.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_12::
    .string "Are not Abana and Pharpar, rivers\n"
    .string "of Damascus, better than all the\l"
    .string "waters of Israel? may I not wash in\l"
    .string "them, and be clean? So he turned and\l"
    .string "went away in a rage.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_13::
    .string "And his servants came near, and\n"
    .string "spake unto him, and said, My father,\l"
    .string "if the prophet had bid thee do some\l"
    .string "great thing, wouldest thou not have\l"
    .string "done it? how much rather then, when\l"
    .string "he saith to thee, Wash, and be clean?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_14::
    .string "Then went he down, and dipped\n"
    .string "himself seven times in Jordan,\l"
    .string "according to the saying of the man of\l"
    .string "God: and his flesh came again like\l"
    .string "unto the flesh of a little child,\l"
    .string "and he was clean$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_15::
    .string "And he returned to the man of God, he\n"
    .string "and all his company, and came, and\l"
    .string "stood before him: and he said,\l"
    .string "Behold, now I know that there is no\l"
    .string "God in all the earth, but in\l"
    .string "Israel: now therefore, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "take a blessing of thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_16::
    .string "But he said, As the LORD liveth,\n"
    .string "before whom I stand, I will receive\l"
    .string "none. And he urged him to take it; but\l"
    .string "he refused.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_17::
    .string "And Naaman said, Shall there not\n"
    .string "then, I pray thee, be given to thy\l"
    .string "servant two mules’ burden of earth?\l"
    .string "for thy servant will henceforth\l"
    .string "offer neither burnt offering nor\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto other gods, but unto\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_18::
    .string "In this thing the LORD pardon thy\n"
    .string "servant, that when my master goeth\l"
    .string "into the house of Rimmon to worship\l"
    .string "there, and he leaneth on my hand, and\l"
    .string "I bow myself in the house of Rimmon:\l"
    .string "when I bow down myself in the house\l"
    .string "of Rimmon, the LORD pardon thy\l"
    .string "servant in this thing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_19::
    .string "And he said unto him, Go in peace.\n"
    .string "So he departed from him a little\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_20::
    .string "But Gehazi, the servant of Elisha\n"
    .string "the man of God, said, Behold, my\l"
    .string "master hath spared Naaman this\l"
    .string "Syrian, in not receiving at his hands\l"
    .string "that which he brought: but, as the\l"
    .string "LORD liveth, I will run after him,\l"
    .string "and take somewhat of him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_21::
    .string "So Gehazi followed after Naaman.\n"
    .string "And when Naaman saw him running after\l"
    .string "him, he lighted down from the\l"
    .string "chariot to meet him, and said, Is\l"
    .string "all well?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_22::
    .string "And he said, All is well. My\n"
    .string "master hath sent me, saying, Behold,\l"
    .string "even now there be come to me from\l"
    .string "mount Ephraim two young men of the\l"
    .string "sons of the prophets: give them, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, a talent of silver, and\l"
    .string "two changes of garments$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_23::
    .string "And Naaman said, Be content, take\n"
    .string "two talents. And he urged him, and\l"
    .string "bound two talents of silver in two\l"
    .string "bags, with two changes of garments,\l"
    .string "and laid them upon two of his\l"
    .string "servants; and they bare them before\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_24::
    .string "And when he came to the tower, he\n"
    .string "took them from their hand, and\l"
    .string "bestowed them in the house: and he\l"
    .string "let the men go, and they departed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_25::
    .string "But he went in, and stood before his\n"
    .string "master. And Elisha said unto him,\l"
    .string "Whence comest thou, Gehazi? And he\l"
    .string "said, Thy servant went no whither.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_26::
    .string "And he said unto him, Went not mine\n"
    .string "heart with thee, when the man turned\l"
    .string "again from his chariot to meet thee?\l"
    .string "Is it a time to receive money, and to\l"
    .string "receive garments, and oliveyards,\l"
    .string "and vineyards, and sheep, and oxen,\l"
    .string "and menservants, and maidservants?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_5_27::
    .string "The leprosy therefore of Naaman\n"
    .string "shall cleave unto thee, and unto\l"
    .string "thy seed for ever. And he went out\l"
    .string "from his presence a leper as white\l"
    .string "as snow$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_1::
    .string "And the sons of the prophets said\n"
    .string "unto Elisha, Behold now, the place\l"
    .string "where we dwell with thee is too\l"
    .string "strait for us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_2::
    .string "Let us go, we pray thee, unto\n"
    .string "Jordan, and take thence every man a\l"
    .string "beam, and let us make us a place\l"
    .string "there, where we may dwell. And he\l"
    .string "answered, Go ye.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_3::
    .string "And one said, Be content, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, and go with thy servants. And\l"
    .string "he answered, I will go.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_4::
    .string "So he went with them. And when they\n"
    .string "came to Jordan, they cut down wood.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_5::
    .string "But as one was felling a beam, the\n"
    .string "axe head fell into the water: and he\l"
    .string "cried, and said, Alas, master! for it\l"
    .string "was borrowed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_6::
    .string "And the man of God said, Where fell\n"
    .string "it? And he shewed him the place. And\l"
    .string "he cut down a stick, and cast it in\l"
    .string "thither; and the iron did swim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_7::
    .string "Therefore said he, Take it up to\n"
    .string "thee. And he put out his hand, and\l"
    .string "took it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_8::
    .string "Then the king of Syria warred\n"
    .string "against Israel, and took counsel\l"
    .string "with his servants, saying, In such\l"
    .string "and such a place shall be my camp.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_9::
    .string "And the man of God sent unto the\n"
    .string "king of Israel, saying, Beware that\l"
    .string "thou pass not such a place; for\l"
    .string "thither the Syrians are come down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_10::
    .string "And the king of Israel sent to the\n"
    .string "place which the man of God told him\l"
    .string "and warned him of, and saved himself\l"
    .string "there, not once nor twice.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_11::
    .string "Therefore the heart of the king of\n"
    .string "Syria was sore troubled for this\l"
    .string "thing; and he called his servants,\l"
    .string "and said unto them, Will ye not shew\l"
    .string "me which of us is for the king of\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_12::
    .string "And one of his servants said, None,\n"
    .string "my lord, O king: but Elisha, the\l"
    .string "prophet that is in Israel, telleth\l"
    .string "the king of Israel the words that\l"
    .string "thou speakest in thy bedchamber$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_13::
    .string "And he said, Go and spy where he is,\n"
    .string "that I may send and fetch him. And it\l"
    .string "was told him, saying, Behold, he is\l"
    .string "in Dothan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_14::
    .string "Therefore sent he thither horses,\n"
    .string "and chariots, and a great host: and\l"
    .string "they came by night, and compassed\l"
    .string "the city about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_15::
    .string "And when the servant of the man of\n"
    .string "God was risen early, and gone forth,\l"
    .string "behold, an host compassed the city\l"
    .string "both with horses and chariots. And\l"
    .string "his servant said unto him, Alas, my\l"
    .string "master! how shall we do?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_16::
    .string "And he answered, Fear not: for they\n"
    .string "that be with us are more than they\l"
    .string "that be with them$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_17::
    .string "And Elisha prayed, and said, LORD,\n"
    .string "I pray thee, open his eyes, that he\l"
    .string "may see. And the LORD opened the eyes\l"
    .string "of the young man; and he saw: and,\l"
    .string "behold, the mountain was full of\l"
    .string "horses and chariots of fire round\l"
    .string "about Elisha.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_18::
    .string "And when they came down to him,\n"
    .string "Elisha prayed unto the LORD, and\l"
    .string "said, Smite this people, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, with blindness. And he smote\l"
    .string "them with blindness according to the\l"
    .string "word of Elisha.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_19::
    .string "And Elisha said unto them, This is\n"
    .string "not the way, neither is this the\l"
    .string "city: follow me, and I will bring\l"
    .string "you to the man whom ye seek. But he\l"
    .string "led them to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_20::
    .string "And it came to pass, when they were\n"
    .string "come into Samaria, that Elisha said,\l"
    .string "LORD, open the eyes of these men,\l"
    .string "that they may see. And the LORD\l"
    .string "opened their eyes, and they saw; and,\l"
    .string "behold, they were in the midst of\l"
    .string "Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_21::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Elisha, when he saw them, My father,\l"
    .string "shall I smite them? shall I smite\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_22::
    .string "And he answered, Thou shalt not\n"
    .string "smite them: wouldest thou smite\l"
    .string "those whom thou hast taken captive\l"
    .string "with thy sword and with thy bow? set\l"
    .string "bread and water before them, that\l"
    .string "they may eat and drink, and go to\l"
    .string "their master$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_23::
    .string "And he prepared great provision\n"
    .string "for them: and when they had eaten and\l"
    .string "drunk, he sent them away, and they\l"
    .string "went to their master. So the bands of\l"
    .string "Syria came no more into the land of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_24::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "Benhadad king of Syria gathered all\l"
    .string "his host, and went up, and besieged\l"
    .string "Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_25::
    .string "And there was a great famine in\n"
    .string "Samaria: and, behold, they besieged\l"
    .string "it, until an ass’s head was sold for\l"
    .string "fourscore pieces of silver, and the\l"
    .string "fourth part of a cab of dove’s dung\l"
    .string "for five pieces of silver.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_26::
    .string "And as the king of Israel was\n"
    .string "passing by upon the wall, there\l"
    .string "cried a woman unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Help, my lord, O king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_27::
    .string "And he said, If the LORD do not\n"
    .string "help thee, whence shall I help\l"
    .string "thee? out of the barnfloor, or out of\l"
    .string "the winepress?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_28::
    .string "And the king said unto her, What\n"
    .string "aileth thee? And she answered, This\l"
    .string "woman said unto me, Give thy son,\l"
    .string "that we may eat him to day, and we\l"
    .string "will eat my son to morrow$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_29::
    .string "So we boiled my son, and did eat\n"
    .string "him: and I said unto her on the next\l"
    .string "day, Give thy son, that we may eat\l"
    .string "him: and she hath hid her son.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_30::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "heard the words of the woman, that he\l"
    .string "rent his clothes; and he passed by\l"
    .string "upon the wall, and the people\l"
    .string "looked, and, behold, he had\l"
    .string "sackcloth within upon his flesh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_31::
    .string "Then he said, God do so and more\n"
    .string "also to me, if the head of Elisha\l"
    .string "the son of Shaphat shall stand on\l"
    .string "him this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_32::
    .string "But Elisha sat in his house, and the\n"
    .string "elders sat with him; and the king\l"
    .string "sent a man from before him: but ere\l"
    .string "the messenger came to him, he said to\l"
    .string "the elders, See ye how this son of a\l"
    .string "murderer hath sent to take away mine\l"
    .string "head? look, when the messenger\l"
    .string "cometh, shut the door, and hold him\l"
    .string "fast at the door: is not the sound of\l"
    .string "his master’s feet behind him?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_6_33::
    .string "And while he yet talked with them,\n"
    .string "behold, the messenger came down unto\l"
    .string "him: and he said, Behold, this evil\l"
    .string "is of the LORD; what should I wait\l"
    .string "for the LORD any longer?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_1::
    .string "Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word\n"
    .string "of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To\l"
    .string "morrow about this time shall a\l"
    .string "measure of fine flour be sold for a\l"
    .string "shekel, and two measures of barley\l"
    .string "for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_2::
    .string "Then a lord on whose hand the king\n"
    .string "leaned answered the man of God, and\l"
    .string "said, Behold, if the LORD would make\l"
    .string "windows in heaven, might this thing\l"
    .string "be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt\l"
    .string "see it with thine eyes, but shalt not\l"
    .string "eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_3::
    .string "And there were four leprous men at\n"
    .string "the entering in of the gate: and they\l"
    .string "said one to another, Why sit we here\l"
    .string "until we die?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_4::
    .string "If we say, We will enter into the\n"
    .string "city, then the famine is in the city,\l"
    .string "and we shall die there: and if we\l"
    .string "sit still here, we die also. Now\l"
    .string "therefore come, and let us fall\l"
    .string "unto the host of the Syrians: if they\l"
    .string "save us alive, we shall live; and\l"
    .string "if they kill us, we shall but die$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_5::
    .string "And they rose up in the twilight,\n"
    .string "to go unto the camp of the Syrians:\l"
    .string "and when they were come to the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of the camp of Syria,\l"
    .string "behold, there was no man there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_6::
    .string "For the LORD had made the host of\n"
    .string "the Syrians to hear a noise of\l"
    .string "chariots, and a noise of horses, even\l"
    .string "the noise of a great host: and they\l"
    .string "said one to another, Lo, the king of\l"
    .string "Israel hath hired against us the\l"
    .string "kings of the Hittites, and the kings\l"
    .string "of the Egyptians, to come upon us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_7::
    .string "Wherefore they arose and fled in\n"
    .string "the twilight, and left their tents,\l"
    .string "and their horses, and their asses,\l"
    .string "even the camp as it was, and fled\l"
    .string "for their life.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_8::
    .string "And when these lepers came to the\n"
    .string "uttermost part of the camp, they\l"
    .string "went into one tent, and did eat and\l"
    .string "drink, and carried thence silver,\l"
    .string "and gold, and raiment, and went and\l"
    .string "hid it; and came again, and entered\l"
    .string "into another tent, and carried thence\l"
    .string "also, and went and hid it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_9::
    .string "Then they said one to another, We do\n"
    .string "not well: this day is a day of good\l"
    .string "tidings, and we hold our peace: if\l"
    .string "we tarry till the morning light,\l"
    .string "some mischief will come upon us:\l"
    .string "now therefore come, that we may go\l"
    .string "and tell the king’s household.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_10::
    .string "So they came and called unto the\n"
    .string "porter of the city: and they told\l"
    .string "them, saying, We came to the camp of\l"
    .string "the Syrians, and, behold, there was\l"
    .string "no man there, neither voice of man,\l"
    .string "but horses tied, and asses tied, and\l"
    .string "the tents as they were.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_11::
    .string "And he called the porters; and\n"
    .string "they told it to the king’s house\l"
    .string "within.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_12::
    .string "And the king arose in the night, and\n"
    .string "said unto his servants, I will now\l"
    .string "shew you what the Syrians have done\l"
    .string "to us. They know that we be hungry;\l"
    .string "therefore are they gone out of the\l"
    .string "camp to hide themselves in the\l"
    .string "field, saying, When they come out of\l"
    .string "the city, we shall catch them\l"
    .string "alive, and get into the city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_13::
    .string "And one of his servants answered and\n"
    .string "said, Let some take, I pray thee,\l"
    .string "five of the horses that remain, which\l"
    .string "are left in the city, (behold, they\l"
    .string "are as all the multitude of Israel\l"
    .string "that are left in it: behold, I say,\l"
    .string "they are even as all the multitude\l"
    .string "of the Israelites that are\l"
    .string "consumed:) and let us send and see.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_14::
    .string "They took therefore two chariot\n"
    .string "horses; and the king sent after the\l"
    .string "host of the Syrians, saying, Go and\l"
    .string "see.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_15::
    .string "And they went after them unto\n"
    .string "Jordan: and, lo, all the way was\l"
    .string "full of garments and vessels, which\l"
    .string "the Syrians had cast away in their\l"
    .string "haste. And the messengers returned,\l"
    .string "and told the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_16::
    .string "And the people went out, and\n"
    .string "spoiled the tents of the Syrians. So\l"
    .string "a measure of fine flour was sold for\l"
    .string "a shekel, and two measures of barley\l"
    .string "for a shekel, according to the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_17::
    .string "And the king appointed the lord on\n"
    .string "whose hand he leaned to have the\l"
    .string "charge of the gate: and the people\l"
    .string "trode upon him in the gate, and he\l"
    .string "died, as the man of God had said, who\l"
    .string "spake when the king came down to him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_18::
    .string "And it came to pass as the man of\n"
    .string "God had spoken to the king, saying,\l"
    .string "Two measures of barley for a shekel,\l"
    .string "and a measure of fine flour for a\l"
    .string "shekel, shall be to morrow about\l"
    .string "this time in the gate of Samaria:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_19::
    .string "And that lord answered the man of\n"
    .string "God, and said, Now, behold, if the\l"
    .string "LORD should make windows in heaven,\l"
    .string "might such a thing be? And he said,\l"
    .string "Behold, thou shalt see it with thine\l"
    .string "eyes, but shalt not eat thereof$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_7_20::
    .string "And so it fell out unto him: for\n"
    .string "the people trode upon him in the\l"
    .string "gate, and he died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_1::
    .string "Then spake Elisha unto the woman,\n"
    .string "whose son he had restored to life,\l"
    .string "saying, Arise, and go thou and thine\l"
    .string "household, and sojourn wheresoever\l"
    .string "thou canst sojourn: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "called for a famine; and it shall\l"
    .string "also come upon the land seven years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_2::
    .string "And the woman arose, and did after\n"
    .string "the saying of the man of God: and she\l"
    .string "went with her household, and\l"
    .string "sojourned in the land of the\l"
    .string "Philistines seven years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_3::
    .string "And it came to pass at the seven\n"
    .string "years’ end, that the woman returned\l"
    .string "out of the land of the Philistines:\l"
    .string "and she went forth to cry unto the\l"
    .string "king for her house and for her land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_4::
    .string "And the king talked with Gehazi the\n"
    .string "servant of the man of God, saying,\l"
    .string "Tell me, I pray thee, all the\l"
    .string "great things that Elisha hath done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_5::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he was\n"
    .string "telling the king how he had\l"
    .string "restored a dead body to life, that,\l"
    .string "behold, the woman, whose son he had\l"
    .string "restored to life, cried to the king\l"
    .string "for her house and for her land. And\l"
    .string "Gehazi said, My lord, O king, this is\l"
    .string "the woman, and this is her son, whom\l"
    .string "Elisha restored to life.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_6::
    .string "And when the king asked the woman,\n"
    .string "she told him. So the king appointed\l"
    .string "unto her a certain officer, saying,\l"
    .string "Restore all that was hers, and all\l"
    .string "the fruits of the field since the\l"
    .string "day that she left the land, even\l"
    .string "until now.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_7::
    .string "And Elisha came to Damascus; and\n"
    .string "Benhadad the king of Syria was sick;\l"
    .string "and it was told him, saying, The man\l"
    .string "of God is come hither.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_8::
    .string "And the king said unto Hazael, Take\n"
    .string "a present in thine hand, and go, meet\l"
    .string "the man of God, and enquire of the\l"
    .string "LORD by him, saying, Shall I recover\l"
    .string "of this disease?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_9::
    .string "So Hazael went to meet him, and took\n"
    .string "a present with him, even of every\l"
    .string "good thing of Damascus, forty\l"
    .string "camels’ burden, and came and stood\l"
    .string "before him, and said, Thy son\l"
    .string "Benhadad king of Syria hath sent me\l"
    .string "to thee, saying, Shall I recover of\l"
    .string "this disease?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_10::
    .string "And Elisha said unto him, Go, say\n"
    .string "unto him, Thou mayest certainly\l"
    .string "recover: howbeit the LORD hath shewed\l"
    .string "me that he shall surely die$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_11::
    .string "And he settled his countenance\n"
    .string "stedfastly, until he was ashamed:\l"
    .string "and the man of God wept.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_12::
    .string "And Hazael said, Why weepeth my\n"
    .string "lord? And he answered, Because I know\l"
    .string "the evil that thou wilt do unto the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: their strong\l"
    .string "holds wilt thou set on fire, and\l"
    .string "their young men wilt thou slay with\l"
    .string "the sword, and wilt dash their\l"
    .string "children, and rip up their women\l"
    .string "with child.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_13::
    .string "And Hazael said, But what, is thy\n"
    .string "servant a dog, that he should do this\l"
    .string "great thing? And Elisha answered,\l"
    .string "The LORD hath shewed me that thou\l"
    .string "shalt be king over Syria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_14::
    .string "So he departed from Elisha, and\n"
    .string "came to his master; who said to him,\l"
    .string "What said Elisha to thee? And he\l"
    .string "answered, He told me that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest surely recover.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_15::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that he took a thick cloth, and\l"
    .string "dipped it in water, and spread it\l"
    .string "on his face, so that he died: and\l"
    .string "Hazael reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_16::
    .string "And in the fifth year of Joram the\n"
    .string "son of Ahab king of Israel,\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat being then king of\l"
    .string "Judah, Jehoram the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat king of Judah began to\l"
    .string "reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_17::
    .string "Thirty and two years old was he\n"
    .string "when he began to reign; and he\l"
    .string "reigned eight years in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_18::
    .string "And he walked in the way of the\n"
    .string "kings of Israel, as did the house of\l"
    .string "Ahab: for the daughter of Ahab was\l"
    .string "his wife: and he did evil in the\l"
    .string "sight of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_19::
    .string "Yet the LORD would not destroy\n"
    .string "Judah for David his servant’s sake,\l"
    .string "as he promised him to give him alway\l"
    .string "a light, and to his children.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_20::
    .string "In his days Edom revolted from\n"
    .string "under the hand of Judah, and made a\l"
    .string "king over themselves.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_21::
    .string "So Joram went over to Zair, and all\n"
    .string "the chariots with him: and he rose by\l"
    .string "night, and smote the Edomites which\l"
    .string "compassed him about, and the\l"
    .string "captains of the chariots: and the\l"
    .string "people fled into their tents.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_22::
    .string "Yet Edom revolted from under the\n"
    .string "hand of Judah unto this day. Then\l"
    .string "Libnah revolted at the same time.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_23::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Joram,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_24::
    .string "And Joram slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and was buried with his fathers in\l"
    .string "the city of David: and Ahaziah his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_25::
    .string "In the twelfth year of Joram the\n"
    .string "son of Ahab king of Israel did\l"
    .string "Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of\l"
    .string "Judah begin to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_26::
    .string "Two and twenty years old was\n"
    .string "Ahaziah when he began to reign; and\l"
    .string "he reigned one year in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Athaliah,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Omri king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_27::
    .string "And he walked in the way of the\n"
    .string "house of Ahab, and did evil in the\l"
    .string "sight of the LORD, as did the house of\l"
    .string "Ahab: for he was the son in law of\l"
    .string "the house of Ahab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_28::
    .string "And he went with Joram the son of\n"
    .string "Ahab to the war against Hazael king\l"
    .string "of Syria in Ramothgilead; and the\l"
    .string "Syrians wounded Joram.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_8_29::
    .string "And king Joram went back to be\n"
    .string "healed in Jezreel of the wounds\l"
    .string "which the Syrians had given him at\l"
    .string "Ramah, when he fought against Hazael\l"
    .string "king of Syria. And Ahaziah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoram king of Judah went down to\l"
    .string "see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel,\l"
    .string "because he was sick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_1::
    .string "And Elisha the prophet called\n"
    .string "one of the children of the\l"
    .string "prophets, and said unto him, Gird up\l"
    .string "thy loins, and take this box of oil\l"
    .string "in thine hand, and go to\l"
    .string "Ramothgilead:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_2::
    .string "And when thou comest thither, look\n"
    .string "out there Jehu the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and\l"
    .string "go in, and make him arise up from\l"
    .string "among his brethren, and carry him to\l"
    .string "an inner chamber;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_3::
    .string "Then take the box of oil, and pour\n"
    .string "it on his head, and say, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD, I have anointed thee king\l"
    .string "over Israel. Then open the door, and\l"
    .string "flee, and tarry not$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_4::
    .string "So the young man, even the young man\n"
    .string "the prophet, went to Ramothgilead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_5::
    .string "And when he came, behold, the\n"
    .string "captains of the host were sitting;\l"
    .string "and he said, I have an errand to thee,\l"
    .string "O captain. And Jehu said, Unto which\l"
    .string "of all us? And he said, To thee, O\l"
    .string "captain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_6::
    .string "And he arose, and went into the\n"
    .string "house; and he poured the oil on his\l"
    .string "head, and said unto him, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel, I have\l"
    .string "anointed thee king over the people\l"
    .string "of the LORD, even over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_7::
    .string "And thou shalt smite the house of\n"
    .string "Ahab thy master, that I may avenge\l"
    .string "the blood of my servants the\l"
    .string "prophets, and the blood of all the\l"
    .string "servants of the LORD, at the hand of\l"
    .string "Jezebel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_8::
    .string "For the whole house of Ahab shall\n"
    .string "perish: and I will cut off from Ahab\l"
    .string "him that pisseth against the wall,\l"
    .string "and him that is shut up and left in\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_9::
    .string "And I will make the house of Ahab\n"
    .string "like the house of Jeroboam the son of\l"
    .string "Nebat, and like the house of Baasha\l"
    .string "the son of Ahijah:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_10::
    .string "And the dogs shall eat Jezebel in\n"
    .string "the portion of Jezreel, and there\l"
    .string "shall be none to bury her. And he\l"
    .string "opened the door, and fled$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_11::
    .string "Then Jehu came forth to the servants\n"
    .string "of his lord: and one said unto him,\l"
    .string "Is all well? wherefore came this\l"
    .string "mad fellow to thee? And he said unto\l"
    .string "them, Ye know the man, and his\l"
    .string "communication.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_12::
    .string "And they said, It is false; tell\n"
    .string "us now. And he said, Thus and thus\l"
    .string "spake he to me, saying, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD, I have anointed thee king\l"
    .string "over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_13::
    .string "Then they hasted, and took every man\n"
    .string "his garment, and put it under him on\l"
    .string "the top of the stairs, and blew with\l"
    .string "trumpets, saying, Jehu is king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_14::
    .string "So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the\n"
    .string "son of Nimshi conspired against\l"
    .string "Joram. (Now Joram had kept\l"
    .string "Ramothgilead, he and all Israel,\l"
    .string "because of Hazael king of Syria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_15::
    .string "But king Joram was returned to be\n"
    .string "healed in Jezreel of the wounds\l"
    .string "which the Syrians had given him, when\l"
    .string "he fought with Hazael king of\l"
    .string "Syria.) And Jehu said, If it be your\l"
    .string "minds, then let none go forth nor\l"
    .string "escape out of the city to go to\l"
    .string "tell it in Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_16::
    .string "So Jehu rode in a chariot, and went\n"
    .string "to Jezreel; for Joram lay there. And\l"
    .string "Ahaziah king of Judah was come down\l"
    .string "to see Joram.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_17::
    .string "And there stood a watchman on the\n"
    .string "tower in Jezreel, and he spied the\l"
    .string "company of Jehu as he came, and said,\l"
    .string "I see a company. And Joram said, Take\l"
    .string "an horseman, and send to meet them,\l"
    .string "and let him say, Is it peace?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_18::
    .string "So there went one on horseback to\n"
    .string "meet him, and said, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "king, Is it peace? And Jehu said,\l"
    .string "What hast thou to do with peace? turn\l"
    .string "thee behind me. And the watchman\l"
    .string "told, saying, The messenger came to\l"
    .string "them, but he cometh not again$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_19::
    .string "Then he sent out a second on\n"
    .string "horseback, which came to them, and\l"
    .string "said, Thus saith the king, Is it\l"
    .string "peace? And Jehu answered, What hast\l"
    .string "thou to do with peace? turn thee\l"
    .string "behind me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_20::
    .string "And the watchman told, saying, He\n"
    .string "came even unto them, and cometh not\l"
    .string "again: and the driving is like the\l"
    .string "driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi;\l"
    .string "for he driveth furiously.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_21::
    .string "And Joram said, Make ready. And his\n"
    .string "chariot was made ready. And Joram\l"
    .string "king of Israel and Ahaziah king of\l"
    .string "Judah went out, each in his chariot,\l"
    .string "and they went out against Jehu, and\l"
    .string "met him in the portion of Naboth the\l"
    .string "Jezreelite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_22::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Joram saw\n"
    .string "Jehu, that he said, Is it peace,\l"
    .string "Jehu? And he answered, What peace, so\l"
    .string "long as the whoredoms of thy mother\l"
    .string "Jezebel and her witchcrafts are so\l"
    .string "many?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_23::
    .string "And Joram turned his hands, and\n"
    .string "fled, and said to Ahaziah, There is\l"
    .string "treachery, O Ahaziah$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_24::
    .string "And Jehu drew a bow with his full\n"
    .string "strength, and smote Jehoram between\l"
    .string "his arms, and the arrow went out at\l"
    .string "his heart, and he sunk down in his\l"
    .string "chariot.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_25::
    .string "Then said Jehu to Bidkar his\n"
    .string "captain, Take up, and cast him in\l"
    .string "the portion of the field of Naboth\l"
    .string "the Jezreelite: for remember how\l"
    .string "that, when I and thou rode together\l"
    .string "after Ahab his father, the LORD laid\l"
    .string "this burden upon him;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_26::
    .string "Surely I have seen yesterday the\n"
    .string "blood of Naboth, and the blood of\l"
    .string "his sons, saith the LORD; and I will\l"
    .string "requite thee in this plat, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD. Now therefore take and cast him\l"
    .string "into the plat of ground, according\l"
    .string "to the word of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_27::
    .string "But when Ahaziah the king of Judah\n"
    .string "saw this, he fled by the way of the\l"
    .string "garden house. And Jehu followed\l"
    .string "after him, and said, Smite him also\l"
    .string "in the chariot. And they did so at the\l"
    .string "going up to Gur, which is by Ibleam.\l"
    .string "And he fled to Megiddo, and died\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_28::
    .string "And his servants carried him in a\n"
    .string "chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him\l"
    .string "in his sepulchre with his fathers\l"
    .string "in the city of David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_29::
    .string "And in the eleventh year of Joram\n"
    .string "the son of Ahab began Ahaziah to\l"
    .string "reign over Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_30::
    .string "And when Jehu was come to Jezreel,\n"
    .string "Jezebel heard of it; and she painted\l"
    .string "her face, and tired her head, and\l"
    .string "looked out at a window.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_31::
    .string "And as Jehu entered in at the gate,\n"
    .string "she said, Had Zimri peace, who slew\l"
    .string "his master?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_32::
    .string "And he lifted up his face to the\n"
    .string "window, and said, Who is on my side?\l"
    .string "who? And there looked out to him two\l"
    .string "or three eunuchs$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_33::
    .string "And he said, Throw her down. So they\n"
    .string "threw her down: and some of her blood\l"
    .string "was sprinkled on the wall, and on\l"
    .string "the horses: and he trode her under\l"
    .string "foot.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_34::
    .string "And when he was come in, he did eat\n"
    .string "and drink, and said, Go, see now this\l"
    .string "cursed woman, and bury her: for she\l"
    .string "is a king’s daughter.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_35::
    .string "And they went to bury her: but they\n"
    .string "found no more of her than the skull,\l"
    .string "and the feet, and the palms of her\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_36::
    .string "Wherefore they came again, and told\n"
    .string "him. And he said, This is the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD, which he spake by his\l"
    .string "servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying,\l"
    .string "In the portion of Jezreel shall\l"
    .string "dogs eat the flesh of Jezebel:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_9_37::
    .string "And the carcase of Jezebel shall\n"
    .string "be as dung upon the face of the\l"
    .string "field in the portion of Jezreel; so\l"
    .string "that they shall not say, This is\l"
    .string "Jezebel$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_1::
    .string "And Ahab had seventy sons in\n"
    .string "Samaria. And Jehu wrote letters, and\l"
    .string "sent to Samaria, unto the rulers of\l"
    .string "Jezreel, to the elders, and to them\l"
    .string "that brought up Ahab’s children,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_2::
    .string "Now as soon as this letter cometh\n"
    .string "to you, seeing your master’s sons are\l"
    .string "with you, and there are with you\l"
    .string "chariots and horses, a fenced city\l"
    .string "also, and armour;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_3::
    .string "Look even out the best and meetest\n"
    .string "of your master’s sons, and set him on\l"
    .string "his father’s throne, and fight for\l"
    .string "your master’s house$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_4::
    .string "But they were exceedingly afraid,\n"
    .string "and said, Behold, two kings stood\l"
    .string "not before him: how then shall we\l"
    .string "stand?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_5::
    .string "And he that was over the house, and\n"
    .string "he that was over the city, the elders\l"
    .string "also, and the bringers up of the\l"
    .string "children, sent to Jehu, saying, We\l"
    .string "are thy servants, and will do all\l"
    .string "that thou shalt bid us; we will not\l"
    .string "make any king: do thou that which is\l"
    .string "good in thine eyes$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_6::
    .string "Then he wrote a letter the second\n"
    .string "time to them, saying, If ye be mine,\l"
    .string "and if ye will hearken unto my\l"
    .string "voice, take ye the heads of the men\l"
    .string "your master’s sons, and come to me to\l"
    .string "Jezreel by to morrow this time. Now\l"
    .string "the king’s sons, being seventy\l"
    .string "persons, were with the great men of\l"
    .string "the city, which brought them up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_7::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "letter came to them, that they took\l"
    .string "the king’s sons, and slew seventy\l"
    .string "persons, and put their heads in\l"
    .string "baskets, and sent him them to\l"
    .string "Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_8::
    .string "And there came a messenger, and\n"
    .string "told him, saying, They have brought\l"
    .string "the heads of the king’s sons. And he\l"
    .string "said, Lay ye them in two heaps at the\l"
    .string "entering in of the gate until the\l"
    .string "morning.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_9::
    .string "And it came to pass in the morning,\n"
    .string "that he went out, and stood, and said\l"
    .string "to all the people, Ye be\l"
    .string "righteous: behold, I conspired\l"
    .string "against my master, and slew him: but\l"
    .string "who slew all these?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_10::
    .string "Know now that there shall fall\n"
    .string "unto the earth nothing of the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD, which the LORD spake\l"
    .string "concerning the house of Ahab: for the\l"
    .string "LORD hath done that which he spake\l"
    .string "by his servant Elijah$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_11::
    .string "So Jehu slew all that remained of\n"
    .string "the house of Ahab in Jezreel, and\l"
    .string "all his great men, and his\l"
    .string "kinsfolks, and his priests, until\l"
    .string "he left him none remaining.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_12::
    .string "And he arose and departed, and came\n"
    .string "to Samaria. And as he was at the\l"
    .string "shearing house in the way,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_13::
    .string "Jehu met with the brethren of\n"
    .string "Ahaziah king of Judah, and said, Who\l"
    .string "are ye? And they answered, We are the\l"
    .string "brethren of Ahaziah; and we go down\l"
    .string "to salute the children of the king\l"
    .string "and the children of the queen$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_14::
    .string "And he said, Take them alive. And\n"
    .string "they took them alive, and slew them\l"
    .string "at the pit of the shearing house,\l"
    .string "even two and forty men; neither left\l"
    .string "he any of them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_15::
    .string "And when he was departed thence, he\n"
    .string "lighted on Jehonadab the son of\l"
    .string "Rechab coming to meet him: and he\l"
    .string "saluted him, and said to him, Is\l"
    .string "thine heart right, as my heart is\l"
    .string "with thy heart? And Jehonadab\l"
    .string "answered, It is. If it be, give me\l"
    .string "thine hand. And he gave him his hand;\l"
    .string "and he took him up to him into the\l"
    .string "chariot.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_16::
    .string "And he said, Come with me, and see my\n"
    .string "zeal for the LORD. So they made him\l"
    .string "ride in his chariot.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_17::
    .string "And when he came to Samaria, he slew\n"
    .string "all that remained unto Ahab in\l"
    .string "Samaria, till he had destroyed him,\l"
    .string "according to the saying of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake to Elijah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_18::
    .string "And Jehu gathered all the people\n"
    .string "together, and said unto them, Ahab\l"
    .string "served Baal a little; but Jehu\l"
    .string "shall serve him much.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_19::
    .string "Now therefore call unto me all\n"
    .string "the prophets of Baal, all his\l"
    .string "servants, and all his priests; let\l"
    .string "none be wanting: for I have a great\l"
    .string "sacrifice to do to Baal; whosoever\l"
    .string "shall be wanting, he shall not\l"
    .string "live. But Jehu did it in subtilty, to\l"
    .string "the intent that he might destroy the\l"
    .string "worshippers of Baal.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_20::
    .string "And Jehu said, Proclaim a solemn\n"
    .string "assembly for Baal. And they\l"
    .string "proclaimed it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_21::
    .string "And Jehu sent through all Israel:\n"
    .string "and all the worshippers of Baal\l"
    .string "came, so that there was not a man\l"
    .string "left that came not. And they came\l"
    .string "into the house of Baal; and the house\l"
    .string "of Baal was full from one end to\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_22::
    .string "And he said unto him that was over\n"
    .string "the vestry, Bring forth vestments for\l"
    .string "all the worshippers of Baal. And\l"
    .string "he brought them forth vestments.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_23::
    .string "And Jehu went, and Jehonadab the son\n"
    .string "of Rechab, into the house of Baal,\l"
    .string "and said unto the worshippers of\l"
    .string "Baal, Search, and look that there be\l"
    .string "here with you none of the servants of\l"
    .string "the LORD, but the worshippers of\l"
    .string "Baal only.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_24::
    .string "And when they went in to offer\n"
    .string "sacrifices and burnt offerings, Jehu\l"
    .string "appointed fourscore men without,\l"
    .string "and said, If any of the men whom I\l"
    .string "have brought into your hands escape,\l"
    .string "he that letteth him go, his life\l"
    .string "shall be for the life of him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_25::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as he\n"
    .string "had made an end of offering the burnt\l"
    .string "offering, that Jehu said to the guard\l"
    .string "and to the captains, Go in, and slay\l"
    .string "them; let none come forth. And they\l"
    .string "smote them with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword; and the guard and the\l"
    .string "captains cast them out, and went to\l"
    .string "the city of the house of Baal.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_26::
    .string "And they brought forth the images\n"
    .string "out of the house of Baal, and burned\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_27::
    .string "And they brake down the image of\n"
    .string "Baal, and brake down the house of\l"
    .string "Baal, and made it a draught house\l"
    .string "unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_28::
    .string "Thus Jehu destroyed Baal out of\n"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_29::
    .string "Howbeit from the sins of Jeroboam\n"
    .string "the son of Nebat, who made Israel to\l"
    .string "sin, Jehu departed not from after\l"
    .string "them, to wit, the golden calves that\l"
    .string "were in Bethel, and that were in Dan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_30::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Jehu, Because\n"
    .string "thou hast done well in executing\l"
    .string "that which is right in mine eyes, and\l"
    .string "hast done unto the house of Ahab\l"
    .string "according to all that was in mine\l"
    .string "heart, thy children of the fourth\l"
    .string "generation shall sit on the throne\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_31::
    .string "But Jehu took no heed to walk in the\n"
    .string "law of the LORD God of Israel with\l"
    .string "all his heart: for he departed not\l"
    .string "from the sins of Jeroboam, which made\l"
    .string "Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_32::
    .string "In those days the LORD began to cut\n"
    .string "Israel short: and Hazael smote them\l"
    .string "in all the coasts of Israel;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_33::
    .string "From Jordan eastward, all the land\n"
    .string "of Gilead, the Gadites, and the\l"
    .string "Reubenites, and the Manassites, from\l"
    .string "Aroer, which is by the river Arnon,\l"
    .string "even Gilead and Bashan$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_34::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Jehu, and\n"
    .string "all that he did, and all his might,\l"
    .string "are they not written in the book of\l"
    .string "the chronicles of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_35::
    .string "And Jehu slept with his fathers:\n"
    .string "and they buried him in Samaria. And\l"
    .string "Jehoahaz his son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_10_36::
    .string "And the time that Jehu reigned over\n"
    .string "Israel in Samaria was twenty and\l"
    .string "eight years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_1::
    .string "And when Athaliah the mother of\n"
    .string "Ahaziah saw that her son was dead,\l"
    .string "she arose and destroyed all the\l"
    .string "seed royal.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_2::
    .string "But Jehosheba, the daughter of king\n"
    .string "Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash\l"
    .string "the son of Ahaziah, and stole him\l"
    .string "from among the king’s sons which were\l"
    .string "slain; and they hid him, even him and\l"
    .string "his nurse, in the bedchamber from\l"
    .string "Athaliah, so that he was not slain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_3::
    .string "And he was with her hid in the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD six years. And Athaliah\l"
    .string "did reign over the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_4::
    .string "And the seventh year Jehoiada sent\n"
    .string "and fetched the rulers over\l"
    .string "hundreds, with the captains and the\l"
    .string "guard, and brought them to him into\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and made a\l"
    .string "covenant with them, and took an oath\l"
    .string "of them in the house of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "shewed them the king’s son.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_5::
    .string "And he commanded them, saying, This\n"
    .string "is the thing that ye shall do; A\l"
    .string "third part of you that enter in on\l"
    .string "the sabbath shall even be keepers\l"
    .string "of the watch of the king’s house;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_6::
    .string "And a third part shall be at the\n"
    .string "gate of Sur; and a third part at the\l"
    .string "gate behind the guard: so shall ye\l"
    .string "keep the watch of the house, that it\l"
    .string "be not broken down$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_7::
    .string "And two parts of all you that go\n"
    .string "forth on the sabbath, even they\l"
    .string "shall keep the watch of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD about the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_8::
    .string "And ye shall compass the king\n"
    .string "round about, every man with his\l"
    .string "weapons in his hand: and he that\l"
    .string "cometh within the ranges, let him be\l"
    .string "slain: and be ye with the king as he\l"
    .string "goeth out and as he cometh in.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_9::
    .string "And the captains over the hundreds\n"
    .string "did according to all things that\l"
    .string "Jehoiada the priest commanded: and\l"
    .string "they took every man his men that were\l"
    .string "to come in on the sabbath, with them\l"
    .string "that should go out on the sabbath,\l"
    .string "and came to Jehoiada the priest.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_10::
    .string "And to the captains over hundreds\n"
    .string "did the priest give king David’s\l"
    .string "spears and shields, that were in the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_11::
    .string "And the guard stood, every man with\n"
    .string "his weapons in his hand, round about\l"
    .string "the king, from the right corner of\l"
    .string "the temple to the left corner of\l"
    .string "the temple, along by the altar and\l"
    .string "the temple.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_12::
    .string "And he brought forth the king’s son,\n"
    .string "and put the crown upon him, and gave\l"
    .string "him the testimony; and they made him\l"
    .string "king, and anointed him; and they\l"
    .string "clapped their hands, and said, God\l"
    .string "save the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_13::
    .string "And when Athaliah heard the noise\n"
    .string "of the guard and of the people, she\l"
    .string "came to the people into the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_14::
    .string "And when she looked, behold, the\n"
    .string "king stood by a pillar, as the\l"
    .string "manner was, and the princes and the\l"
    .string "trumpeters by the king, and all the\l"
    .string "people of the land rejoiced, and\l"
    .string "blew with trumpets: and Athaliah\l"
    .string "rent her clothes, and cried,\l"
    .string "Treason, Treason.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_15::
    .string "But Jehoiada the priest commanded\n"
    .string "the captains of the hundreds, the\l"
    .string "officers of the host, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Have her forth without the\l"
    .string "ranges: and him that followeth her\l"
    .string "kill with the sword. For the priest\l"
    .string "had said, Let her not be slain in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_16::
    .string "And they laid hands on her; and she\n"
    .string "went by the way by the which the\l"
    .string "horses came into the king’s house:\l"
    .string "and there was she slain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_17::
    .string "And Jehoiada made a covenant\n"
    .string "between the LORD and the king and the\l"
    .string "people, that they should be the\l"
    .string "LORD’s people; between the king\l"
    .string "also and the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_18::
    .string "And all the people of the land\n"
    .string "went into the house of Baal, and\l"
    .string "brake it down; his altars and his\l"
    .string "images brake they in pieces\l"
    .string "thoroughly, and slew Mattan the\l"
    .string "priest of Baal before the altars.\l"
    .string "And the priest appointed officers\l"
    .string "over the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_19::
    .string "And he took the rulers over\n"
    .string "hundreds, and the captains, and the\l"
    .string "guard, and all the people of the\l"
    .string "land; and they brought down the king\l"
    .string "from the house of the LORD, and came\l"
    .string "by the way of the gate of the guard to\l"
    .string "the king’s house. And he sat on the\l"
    .string "throne of the kings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_20::
    .string "And all the people of the land\n"
    .string "rejoiced, and the city was in quiet:\l"
    .string "and they slew Athaliah with the\l"
    .string "sword beside the king’s house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_11_21::
    .string "Seven years old was Jehoash when he\n"
    .string "began to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_1::
    .string "In the seventh year of Jehu Jehoash\n"
    .string "began to reign; and forty years\l"
    .string "reigned he in Jerusalem. And his\l"
    .string "mother’s name was Zibiah of\l"
    .string "Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_2::
    .string "And Jehoash did that which was right\n"
    .string "in the sight of the LORD all his\l"
    .string "days wherein Jehoiada the priest\l"
    .string "instructed him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_3::
    .string "But the high places were not taken\n"
    .string "away: the people still sacrificed\l"
    .string "and burnt incense in the high\l"
    .string "places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_4::
    .string "And Jehoash said to the priests,\n"
    .string "All the money of the dedicated\l"
    .string "things that is brought into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, even the money of every\l"
    .string "one that passeth the account, the\l"
    .string "money that every man is set at, and\l"
    .string "all the money that cometh into any\l"
    .string "man’s heart to bring into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_5::
    .string "Let the priests take it to them,\n"
    .string "every man of his acquaintance: and\l"
    .string "let them repair the breaches of the\l"
    .string "house, wheresoever any breach shall\l"
    .string "be found$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_6::
    .string "But it was so, that in the three and\n"
    .string "twentieth year of king Jehoash the\l"
    .string "priests had not repaired the\l"
    .string "breaches of the house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_7::
    .string "Then king Jehoash called for\n"
    .string "Jehoiada the priest, and the other\l"
    .string "priests, and said unto them, Why\l"
    .string "repair ye not the breaches of the\l"
    .string "house? now therefore receive no more\l"
    .string "money of your acquaintance, but\l"
    .string "deliver it for the breaches of the\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_8::
    .string "And the priests consented to\n"
    .string "receive no more money of the\l"
    .string "people, neither to repair the\l"
    .string "breaches of the house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_9::
    .string "But Jehoiada the priest took a\n"
    .string "chest, and bored a hole in the lid\l"
    .string "of it, and set it beside the altar,\l"
    .string "on the right side as one cometh into\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD: and the\l"
    .string "priests that kept the door put\l"
    .string "therein all the money that was\l"
    .string "brought into the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_10::
    .string "And it was so, when they saw that\n"
    .string "there was much money in the chest,\l"
    .string "that the king’s scribe and the high\l"
    .string "priest came up, and they put up in\l"
    .string "bags, and told the money that was\l"
    .string "found in the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_11::
    .string "And they gave the money, being\n"
    .string "told, into the hands of them that did\l"
    .string "the work, that had the oversight of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD: and they laid\l"
    .string "it out to the carpenters and\l"
    .string "builders, that wrought upon the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_12::
    .string "And to masons, and hewers of stone,\n"
    .string "and to buy timber and hewed stone to\l"
    .string "repair the breaches of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and for all that was laid\l"
    .string "out for the house to repair it$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_13::
    .string "Howbeit there were not made for the\n"
    .string "house of the LORD bowls of silver,\l"
    .string "snuffers, basons, trumpets, any\l"
    .string "vessels of gold, or vessels of\l"
    .string "silver, of the money that was\l"
    .string "brought into the house of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_14::
    .string "But they gave that to the workmen,\n"
    .string "and repaired therewith the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_15::
    .string "Moreover they reckoned not with the\n"
    .string "men, into whose hand they delivered\l"
    .string "the money to be bestowed on workmen:\l"
    .string "for they dealt faithfully.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_16::
    .string "The trespass money and sin money\n"
    .string "was not brought into the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD: it was the priests’.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_17::
    .string "Then Hazael king of Syria went up,\n"
    .string "and fought against Gath, and took it:\l"
    .string "and Hazael set his face to go up to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_18::
    .string "And Jehoash king of Judah took all\n"
    .string "the hallowed things that\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, and Jehoram, and\l"
    .string "Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah,\l"
    .string "had dedicated, and his own hallowed\l"
    .string "things, and all the gold that was\l"
    .string "found in the treasures of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and in the king’s house,\l"
    .string "and sent it to Hazael king of Syria:\l"
    .string "and he went away from Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_19::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Joash,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_20::
    .string "And his servants arose, and made a\n"
    .string "conspiracy, and slew Joash in the\l"
    .string "house of Millo, which goeth down to\l"
    .string "Silla$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_12_21::
    .string "For Jozachar the son of Shimeath,\n"
    .string "and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his\l"
    .string "servants, smote him, and he died; and\l"
    .string "they buried him with his fathers in\l"
    .string "the city of David: and Amaziah his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_1::
    .string "In the three and twentieth year of\n"
    .string "Joash the son of Ahaziah king of\l"
    .string "Judah Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began\l"
    .string "to reign over Israel in Samaria, and\l"
    .string "reigned seventeen years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_2::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, and followed\l"
    .string "the sins of Jeroboam the son of\l"
    .string "Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he\l"
    .string "departed not therefrom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_3::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Israel, and he\l"
    .string "delivered them into the hand of\l"
    .string "Hazael king of Syria, and into the\l"
    .string "hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael,\l"
    .string "all their days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_4::
    .string "And Jehoahaz besought the LORD, and\n"
    .string "the LORD hearkened unto him: for he\l"
    .string "saw the oppression of Israel,\l"
    .string "because the king of Syria oppressed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_5::
    .string "(And the LORD gave Israel a\n"
    .string "saviour, so that they went out from\l"
    .string "under the hand of the Syrians: and\l"
    .string "the children of Israel dwelt in\l"
    .string "their tents, as beforetime.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_6::
    .string "Nevertheless they departed not\n"
    .string "from the sins of the house of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam, who made Israel sin, but\l"
    .string "walked therein: and there remained\l"
    .string "the grove also in Samaria.)"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_7::
    .string "Neither did he leave of the\n"
    .string "people to Jehoahaz but fifty\l"
    .string "horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten\l"
    .string "thousand footmen; for the king of\l"
    .string "Syria had destroyed them, and had\l"
    .string "made them like the dust by threshing$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_8::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jehoahaz, and all that he did, and\l"
    .string "his might, are they not written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_9::
    .string "And Jehoahaz slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers; and they buried him in\l"
    .string "Samaria: and Joash his son reigned in\l"
    .string "his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_10::
    .string "In the thirty and seventh year of\n"
    .string "Joash king of Judah began Jehoash the\l"
    .string "son of Jehoahaz to reign over Israel\l"
    .string "in Samaria, and reigned sixteen\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_11::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD; he departed\l"
    .string "not from all the sins of Jeroboam\l"
    .string "the son of Nebat, who made Israel\l"
    .string "sin: but he walked therein.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_12::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Joash,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, and his might\l"
    .string "wherewith he fought against Amaziah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, are they not written\l"
    .string "in the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_13::
    .string "And Joash slept with his fathers;\n"
    .string "and Jeroboam sat upon his throne:\l"
    .string "and Joash was buried in Samaria with\l"
    .string "the kings of Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_14::
    .string "Now Elisha was fallen sick of his\n"
    .string "sickness whereof he died. And Joash\l"
    .string "the king of Israel came down unto\l"
    .string "him, and wept over his face, and\l"
    .string "said, O my father, my father, the\l"
    .string "chariot of Israel, and the horsemen\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_15::
    .string "And Elisha said unto him, Take bow\n"
    .string "and arrows. And he took unto him bow\l"
    .string "and arrows.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_16::
    .string "And he said to the king of Israel,\n"
    .string "Put thine hand upon the bow. And he\l"
    .string "put his hand upon it: and Elisha\l"
    .string "put his hands upon the king’s hands.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_17::
    .string "And he said, Open the window\n"
    .string "eastward. And he opened it. Then\l"
    .string "Elisha said, Shoot. And he shot. And\l"
    .string "he said, The arrow of the LORD’s\l"
    .string "deliverance, and the arrow of\l"
    .string "deliverance from Syria: for thou\l"
    .string "shalt smite the Syrians in Aphek,\l"
    .string "till thou have consumed them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_18::
    .string "And he said, Take the arrows. And he\n"
    .string "took them. And he said unto the king\l"
    .string "of Israel, Smite upon the ground.\l"
    .string "And he smote thrice, and stayed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_19::
    .string "And the man of God was wroth with\n"
    .string "him, and said, Thou shouldest have\l"
    .string "smitten five or six times; then hadst\l"
    .string "thou smitten Syria till thou hadst\l"
    .string "consumed it: whereas now thou shalt\l"
    .string "smite Syria but thrice.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_20::
    .string "And Elisha died, and they buried him\n"
    .string " And the bands of the Moabites\l"
    .string "invaded the land at the coming in of\l"
    .string "the year.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_21::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they were\n"
    .string "burying a man, that, behold, they\l"
    .string "spied a band of men; and they cast\l"
    .string "the man into the sepulchre of\l"
    .string "Elisha: and when the man was let\l"
    .string "down, and touched the bones of\l"
    .string "Elisha, he revived, and stood up on\l"
    .string "his feet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_22::
    .string "But Hazael king of Syria\n"
    .string "oppressed Israel all the days of\l"
    .string "Jehoahaz.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_23::
    .string "And the LORD was gracious unto them,\n"
    .string "and had compassion on them, and had\l"
    .string "respect unto them, because of his\l"
    .string "covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and\l"
    .string "Jacob, and would not destroy them,\l"
    .string "neither cast he them from his\l"
    .string "presence as yet.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_24::
    .string "So Hazael king of Syria died; and\n"
    .string "Benhadad his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_13_25::
    .string "And Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz took\n"
    .string "again out of the hand of Benhadad the\l"
    .string "son of Hazael the cities, which he\l"
    .string "had taken out of the hand of Jehoahaz\l"
    .string "his father by war. Three times did\l"
    .string "Joash beat him, and recovered the\l"
    .string "cities of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_1::
    .string "In the second year of Joash son of\n"
    .string "Jehoahaz king of Israel reigned\l"
    .string "Amaziah the son of Joash king of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_2::
    .string "He was twenty and five years old\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and reigned\l"
    .string "twenty and nine years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_3::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, yet not like\l"
    .string "David his father: he did according to\l"
    .string "all things as Joash his father did.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_4::
    .string "Howbeit the high places were not\n"
    .string "taken away: as yet the people did\l"
    .string "sacrifice and burnt incense on the\l"
    .string "high places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_5::
    .string "And it came to pass, as soon as the\n"
    .string "kingdom was confirmed in his hand,\l"
    .string "that he slew his servants which had\l"
    .string "slain the king his father.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_6::
    .string "But the children of the murderers\n"
    .string "he slew not: according unto that\l"
    .string "which is written in the book of the\l"
    .string "law of Moses, wherein the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded, saying, The fathers\l"
    .string "shall not be put to death for the\l"
    .string "children, nor the children be put\l"
    .string "to death for the fathers; but every\l"
    .string "man shall be put to death for his\l"
    .string "own sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_7::
    .string "He slew of Edom in the valley of\n"
    .string "salt ten thousand, and took Selah by\l"
    .string "war, and called the name of it\l"
    .string "Joktheel unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_8::
    .string "Then Amaziah sent messengers to\n"
    .string "Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of\l"
    .string "Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come,\l"
    .string "let us look one another in the face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_9::
    .string "And Jehoash the king of Israel sent\n"
    .string "to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The\l"
    .string "thistle that was in Lebanon sent to\l"
    .string "the cedar that was in Lebanon,\l"
    .string "saying, Give thy daughter to my son\l"
    .string "to wife: and there passed by a wild\l"
    .string "beast that was in Lebanon, and trode\l"
    .string "down the thistle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_10::
    .string "Thou hast indeed smitten Edom, and\n"
    .string "thine heart hath lifted thee up:\l"
    .string "glory of this, and tarry at home: for\l"
    .string "why shouldest thou meddle to thy\l"
    .string "hurt, that thou shouldest fall,\l"
    .string "even thou, and Judah with thee?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_11::
    .string "But Amaziah would not hear.\n"
    .string "Therefore Jehoash king of Israel\l"
    .string "went up; and he and Amaziah king of\l"
    .string "Judah looked one another in the face\l"
    .string "at Bethshemesh, which belongeth to\l"
    .string "Judah$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_12::
    .string "And Judah was put to the worse\n"
    .string "before Israel; and they fled every\l"
    .string "man to their tents.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_13::
    .string "And Jehoash king of Israel took\n"
    .string "Amaziah king of Judah, the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at\l"
    .string "Bethshemesh, and came to Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and brake down the wall of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim\l"
    .string "unto the corner gate, four hundred\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_14::
    .string "And he took all the gold and\n"
    .string "silver, and all the vessels that\l"
    .string "were found in the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and in the treasures of the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and hostages, and returned to\l"
    .string "Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_15::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash\n"
    .string "which he did, and his might, and how\l"
    .string "he fought with Amaziah king of Judah,\l"
    .string "are they not written in the book of\l"
    .string "the chronicles of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_16::
    .string "And Jehoash slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried in Samaria\l"
    .string "with the kings of Israel; and\l"
    .string "Jeroboam his son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_17::
    .string "And Amaziah the son of Joash king of\n"
    .string "Judah lived after the death of\l"
    .string "Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of\l"
    .string "Israel fifteen years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_18::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Amaziah,\n"
    .string "are they not written in the book of\l"
    .string "the chronicles of the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_19::
    .string "Now they made a conspiracy against\n"
    .string "him in Jerusalem: and he fled to\l"
    .string "Lachish; but they sent after him to\l"
    .string "Lachish, and slew him there$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_20::
    .string "And they brought him on horses: and\n"
    .string "he was buried at Jerusalem with his\l"
    .string "fathers in the city of David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_21::
    .string "And all the people of Judah took\n"
    .string "Azariah, which was sixteen years\l"
    .string "old, and made him king instead of his\l"
    .string "father Amaziah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_22::
    .string "He built Elath, and restored it to\n"
    .string "Judah, after that the king slept\l"
    .string "with his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_23::
    .string "In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the\n"
    .string "son of Joash king of Judah Jeroboam\l"
    .string "the son of Joash king of Israel\l"
    .string "began to reign in Samaria, and\l"
    .string "reigned forty and one years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_24::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD: he departed\l"
    .string "not from all the sins of Jeroboam\l"
    .string "the son of Nebat, who made Israel to\l"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_25::
    .string "He restored the coast of Israel\n"
    .string "from the entering of Hamath unto the\l"
    .string "sea of the plain, according to the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD God of Israel, which\l"
    .string "he spake by the hand of his servant\l"
    .string "Jonah, the son of Amittai, the\l"
    .string "prophet, which was of Gathhepher.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_26::
    .string "For the LORD saw the affliction of\n"
    .string "Israel, that it was very bitter: for\l"
    .string "there was not any shut up, nor any\l"
    .string "left, nor any helper for Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_27::
    .string "And the LORD said not that he would\n"
    .string "blot out the name of Israel from\l"
    .string "under heaven: but he saved them by\l"
    .string "the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_28::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam, and all that he did, and\l"
    .string "his might, how he warred, and how he\l"
    .string "recovered Damascus, and Hamath,\l"
    .string "which belonged to Judah, for\l"
    .string "Israel, are they not written in the\l"
    .string "book of the chronicles of the kings\l"
    .string "of Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_14_29::
    .string "And Jeroboam slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, even with the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel; and Zachariah his son\l"
    .string "reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_1::
    .string "In the twenty and seventh year of\n"
    .string "Jeroboam king of Israel began\l"
    .string "Azariah son of Amaziah king of Judah\l"
    .string "to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_2::
    .string "Sixteen years old was he when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned two\l"
    .string "and fifty years in Jerusalem. And\l"
    .string "his mother’s name was Jecholiah of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_3::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his father Amaziah had\l"
    .string "done;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_4::
    .string "Save that the high places were not\n"
    .string "removed: the people sacrificed and\l"
    .string "burnt incense still on the high\l"
    .string "places$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_5::
    .string "And the LORD smote the king, so that\n"
    .string "he was a leper unto the day of his\l"
    .string "death, and dwelt in a several house.\l"
    .string "And Jotham the king’s son was over\l"
    .string "the house, judging the people of\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_6::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Azariah,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_7::
    .string "So Azariah slept with his fathers;\n"
    .string "and they buried him with his fathers\l"
    .string "in the city of David: and Jotham his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_8::
    .string "In the thirty and eighth year of\n"
    .string "Azariah king of Judah did Zachariah\l"
    .string "the son of Jeroboam reign over\l"
    .string "Israel in Samaria six months.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_9::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, as his fathers\l"
    .string "had done: he departed not from the\l"
    .string "sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat,\l"
    .string "who made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_10::
    .string "And Shallum the son of Jabesh\n"
    .string "conspired against him, and smote him\l"
    .string "before the people, and slew him,\l"
    .string "and reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_11::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Zachariah, behold, they are written\l"
    .string "in the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_12::
    .string "This was the word of the LORD which\n"
    .string "he spake unto Jehu, saying, Thy sons\l"
    .string "shall sit on the throne of Israel\l"
    .string "unto the fourth generation. And so it\l"
    .string "came to pass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_13::
    .string "Shallum the son of Jabesh began to\n"
    .string "reign in the nine and thirtieth year\l"
    .string "of Uzziah king of Judah; and he\l"
    .string "reigned a full month in Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_14::
    .string "For Menahem the son of Gadi went up\n"
    .string "from Tirzah, and came to Samaria, and\l"
    .string "smote Shallum the son of Jabesh in\l"
    .string "Samaria, and slew him, and reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_15::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Shallum, and his conspiracy which\l"
    .string "he made, behold, they are written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_16::
    .string "Then Menahem smote Tiphsah, and\n"
    .string "all that were therein, and the\l"
    .string "coasts thereof from Tirzah: because\l"
    .string "they opened not to him, therefore he\l"
    .string "smote it; and all the women therein\l"
    .string "that were with child he ripped up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_17::
    .string "In the nine and thirtieth year of\n"
    .string "Azariah king of Judah began Menahem\l"
    .string "the son of Gadi to reign over Israel,\l"
    .string "and reigned ten years in Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_18::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD: he departed\l"
    .string "not all his days from the sins of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made\l"
    .string "Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_19::
    .string "And Pul the king of Assyria came\n"
    .string "against the land: and Menahem gave\l"
    .string "Pul a thousand talents of silver,\l"
    .string "that his hand might be with him to\l"
    .string "confirm the kingdom in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_20::
    .string "And Menahem exacted the money of\n"
    .string "Israel, even of all the mighty men\l"
    .string "of wealth, of each man fifty shekels\l"
    .string "of silver, to give to the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria. So the king of Assyria\l"
    .string "turned back, and stayed not there in\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_21::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Menahem,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_22::
    .string "And Menahem slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers; and Pekahiah his son reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_23::
    .string "In the fiftieth year of Azariah king\n"
    .string "of Judah Pekahiah the son of Menahem\l"
    .string "began to reign over Israel in\l"
    .string "Samaria, and reigned two years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_24::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD: he departed\l"
    .string "not from the sins of Jeroboam the son\l"
    .string "of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_25::
    .string "But Pekah the son of Remaliah, a\n"
    .string "captain of his, conspired against\l"
    .string "him, and smote him in Samaria, in the\l"
    .string "palace of the king’s house, with\l"
    .string "Argob and Arieh, and with him fifty\l"
    .string "men of the Gileadites: and he\l"
    .string "killed him, and reigned in his room.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_26::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Pekahiah, and all that he did,\l"
    .string "behold, they are written in the book\l"
    .string "of the chronicles of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_27::
    .string "In the two and fiftieth year of\n"
    .string "Azariah king of Judah Pekah the son\l"
    .string "of Remaliah began to reign over\l"
    .string "Israel in Samaria, and reigned\l"
    .string "twenty years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_28::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD: he departed\l"
    .string "not from the sins of Jeroboam the son\l"
    .string "of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_29::
    .string "In the days of Pekah king of Israel\n"
    .string "came Tiglathpileser king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and took Ijon, and\l"
    .string "Abelbethmaachah, and Janoah, and\l"
    .string "Kedesh, and Hazor, and Gilead, and\l"
    .string "Galilee, all the land of\l"
    .string "Naphtali, and carried them captive\l"
    .string "to Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_30::
    .string "And Hoshea the son of Elah made a\n"
    .string "conspiracy against Pekah the son of\l"
    .string "Remaliah, and smote him, and slew\l"
    .string "him, and reigned in his stead, in the\l"
    .string "twentieth year of Jotham the son of\l"
    .string "Uzziah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_31::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Pekah,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, behold, they\l"
    .string "are written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_32::
    .string "In the second year of Pekah the son\n"
    .string "of Remaliah king of Israel began\l"
    .string "Jotham the son of Uzziah king of\l"
    .string "Judah to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_33::
    .string "Five and twenty years old was he\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Jerusha,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Zadok.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_34::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD: he did\l"
    .string "according to all that his father\l"
    .string "Uzziah had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_35::
    .string "Howbeit the high places were not\n"
    .string "removed: the people sacrificed and\l"
    .string "burned incense still in the high\l"
    .string "places. He built the higher gate of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_36::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Jotham,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_37::
    .string "In those days the LORD began to send\n"
    .string "against Judah Rezin the king of\l"
    .string "Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_15_38::
    .string "And Jotham slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and was buried with his fathers in\l"
    .string "the city of David his father: and\l"
    .string "Ahaz his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_1::
    .string "In the seventeenth year of Pekah the\n"
    .string "son of Remaliah Ahaz the son of\l"
    .string "Jotham king of Judah began to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_2::
    .string "Twenty years old was Ahaz when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and reigned sixteen\l"
    .string "years in Jerusalem, and did not that\l"
    .string "which was right in the sight of the\l"
    .string "LORD his God, like David his father.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_3::
    .string "But he walked in the way of the\n"
    .string "kings of Israel, yea, and made his\l"
    .string "son to pass through the fire,\l"
    .string "according to the abominations of the\l"
    .string "heathen, whom the LORD cast out from\l"
    .string "before the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_4::
    .string "And he sacrificed and burnt incense\n"
    .string "in the high places, and on the\l"
    .string "hills, and under every green tree.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_5::
    .string "Then Rezin king of Syria and Pekah\n"
    .string "son of Remaliah king of Israel came\l"
    .string "up to Jerusalem to war: and they\l"
    .string "besieged Ahaz, but could not\l"
    .string "overcome him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_6::
    .string "At that time Rezin king of Syria\n"
    .string "recovered Elath to Syria, and drave\l"
    .string "the Jews from Elath: and the Syrians\l"
    .string "came to Elath, and dwelt there unto\l"
    .string "this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_7::
    .string "So Ahaz sent messengers to\n"
    .string "Tiglathpileser king of Assyria,\l"
    .string "saying, I am thy servant and thy son:\l"
    .string "come up, and save me out of the hand\l"
    .string "of the king of Syria, and out of the\l"
    .string "hand of the king of Israel, which\l"
    .string "rise up against me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_8::
    .string "And Ahaz took the silver and gold\n"
    .string "that was found in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and in the treasures of the\l"
    .string "king’s house, and sent it for a\l"
    .string "present to the king of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_9::
    .string "And the king of Assyria hearkened\n"
    .string "unto him: for the king of Assyria\l"
    .string "went up against Damascus, and took\l"
    .string "it, and carried the people of it\l"
    .string "captive to Kir, and slew Rezin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_10::
    .string "And king Ahaz went to Damascus to\n"
    .string "meet Tiglathpileser king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and saw an altar that was at\l"
    .string "Damascus: and king Ahaz sent to\l"
    .string "Urijah the priest the fashion of the\l"
    .string "altar, and the pattern of it,\l"
    .string "according to all the workmanship\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_11::
    .string "And Urijah the priest built an\n"
    .string "altar according to all that king\l"
    .string "Ahaz had sent from Damascus: so\l"
    .string "Urijah the priest made it against\l"
    .string "king Ahaz came from Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_12::
    .string "And when the king was come from\n"
    .string "Damascus, the king saw the altar:\l"
    .string "and the king approached to the\l"
    .string "altar, and offered thereon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_13::
    .string "And he burnt his burnt offering and\n"
    .string "his meat offering, and poured his\l"
    .string "drink offering, and sprinkled the\l"
    .string "blood of his peace offerings, upon\l"
    .string "the altar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_14::
    .string "And he brought also the brasen\n"
    .string "altar, which was before the LORD,\l"
    .string "from the forefront of the house, from\l"
    .string "between the altar and the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and put it on the north\l"
    .string "side of the altar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_15::
    .string "And king Ahaz commanded Urijah the\n"
    .string "priest, saying, Upon the great\l"
    .string "altar burn the morning burnt\l"
    .string "offering, and the evening meat\l"
    .string "offering, and the king’s burnt\l"
    .string "sacrifice, and his meat offering,\l"
    .string "with the burnt offering of all the\l"
    .string "people of the land, and their meat\l"
    .string "offering, and their drink offerings;\l"
    .string "and sprinkle upon it all the\l"
    .string "blood of the burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "all the blood of the sacrifice: and\l"
    .string "the brasen altar shall be for me to\l"
    .string "enquire by.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_16::
    .string "Thus did Urijah the priest,\n"
    .string "according to all that king Ahaz\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_17::
    .string "And king Ahaz cut off the borders of\n"
    .string "the bases, and removed the laver\l"
    .string "from off them; and took down the sea\l"
    .string "from off the brasen oxen that were\l"
    .string "under it, and put it upon the\l"
    .string "pavement of stones.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_18::
    .string "And the covert for the sabbath that\n"
    .string "they had built in the house, and the\l"
    .string "king’s entry without, turned he from\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD for the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_19::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Ahaz\n"
    .string "which he did, are they not written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_16_20::
    .string "And Ahaz slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and was buried with his fathers in\l"
    .string "the city of David: and Hezekiah his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_1::
    .string "In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of\n"
    .string "Judah began Hoshea the son of Elah\l"
    .string "to reign in Samaria over Israel nine\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_2::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, but not as the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel that were before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_3::
    .string "Against him came up Shalmaneser\n"
    .string "king of Assyria; and Hoshea became\l"
    .string "his servant, and gave him presents.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_4::
    .string "And the king of Assyria found\n"
    .string "conspiracy in Hoshea: for he had\l"
    .string "sent messengers to So king of Egypt,\l"
    .string "and brought no present to the king\l"
    .string "of Assyria, as he had done year by\l"
    .string "year: therefore the king of Assyria\l"
    .string "shut him up, and bound him in prison.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_5::
    .string "Then the king of Assyria came up\n"
    .string "throughout all the land, and went\l"
    .string "up to Samaria, and besieged it three\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_6::
    .string "In the ninth year of Hoshea the king\n"
    .string "of Assyria took Samaria, and carried\l"
    .string "Israel away into Assyria, and\l"
    .string "placed them in Halah and in Habor by\l"
    .string "the river of Gozan, and in the cities\l"
    .string "of the Medes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_7::
    .string "For so it was, that the children of\n"
    .string "Israel had sinned against the LORD\l"
    .string "their God, which had brought them up\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt, from under\l"
    .string "the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt,\l"
    .string "and had feared other gods,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_8::
    .string "And walked in the statutes of the\n"
    .string "heathen, whom the LORD cast out from\l"
    .string "before the children of Israel, and\l"
    .string "of the kings of Israel, which they\l"
    .string "had made$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_9::
    .string "And the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "secretly those things that were not\l"
    .string "right against the LORD their God, and\l"
    .string "they built them high places in\l"
    .string "all their cities, from the tower of\l"
    .string "the watchmen to the fenced city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_10::
    .string "And they set them up images and\n"
    .string "groves in every high hill, and under\l"
    .string "every green tree:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_11::
    .string "And there they burnt incense in\n"
    .string "all the high places, as did the\l"
    .string "heathen whom the LORD carried away\l"
    .string "before them; and wrought wicked\l"
    .string "things to provoke the LORD to anger:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_12::
    .string "For they served idols, whereof the\n"
    .string "LORD had said unto them, Ye shall\l"
    .string "not do this thing$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_13::
    .string "Yet the LORD testified against\n"
    .string "Israel, and against Judah, by all\l"
    .string "the prophets, and by all the\l"
    .string "seers, saying, Turn ye from your\l"
    .string "evil ways, and keep my commandments\l"
    .string "and my statutes, according to all\l"
    .string "the law which I commanded your\l"
    .string "fathers, and which I sent to you by my\l"
    .string "servants the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_14::
    .string "Notwithstanding they would not\n"
    .string "hear, but hardened their necks, like\l"
    .string "to the neck of their fathers, that\l"
    .string "did not believe in the LORD their\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_15::
    .string "And they rejected his statutes, and\n"
    .string "his covenant that he made with their\l"
    .string "fathers, and his testimonies which he\l"
    .string "testified against them; and they\l"
    .string "followed vanity, and became vain,\l"
    .string "and went after the heathen that were\l"
    .string "round about them, concerning whom the\l"
    .string "LORD had charged them, that they\l"
    .string "should not do like them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_16::
    .string "And they left all the\n"
    .string "commandments of the LORD their God,\l"
    .string "and made them molten images, even\l"
    .string "two calves, and made a grove, and\l"
    .string "worshipped all the host of heaven,\l"
    .string "and served Baal.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_17::
    .string "And they caused their sons and their\n"
    .string "daughters to pass through the fire,\l"
    .string "and used divination and\l"
    .string "enchantments, and sold themselves\l"
    .string "to do evil in the sight of the LORD,\l"
    .string "to provoke him to anger.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_18::
    .string "Therefore the LORD was very angry\n"
    .string "with Israel, and removed them out of\l"
    .string "his sight: there was none left but\l"
    .string "the tribe of Judah only.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_19::
    .string "Also Judah kept not the\n"
    .string "commandments of the LORD their God,\l"
    .string "but walked in the statutes of\l"
    .string "Israel which they made.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_20::
    .string "And the LORD rejected all the seed\n"
    .string "of Israel, and afflicted them, and\l"
    .string "delivered them into the hand of\l"
    .string "spoilers, until he had cast them\l"
    .string "out of his sight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_21::
    .string "For he rent Israel from the house\n"
    .string "of David; and they made Jeroboam the\l"
    .string "son of Nebat king: and Jeroboam drave\l"
    .string "Israel from following the LORD, and\l"
    .string "made them sin a great sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_22::
    .string "For the children of Israel walked\n"
    .string "in all the sins of Jeroboam which he\l"
    .string "did; they departed not from them;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_23::
    .string "Until the LORD removed Israel out\n"
    .string "of his sight, as he had said by all\l"
    .string "his servants the prophets. So was\l"
    .string "Israel carried away out of their own\l"
    .string "land to Assyria unto this day$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_24::
    .string "And the king of Assyria brought men\n"
    .string "from Babylon, and from Cuthah, and\l"
    .string "from Ava, and from Hamath, and from\l"
    .string "Sepharvaim, and placed them in the\l"
    .string "cities of Samaria instead of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel: and they\l"
    .string "possessed Samaria, and dwelt in the\l"
    .string "cities thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_25::
    .string "And so it was at the beginning of\n"
    .string "their dwelling there, that they\l"
    .string "feared not the LORD: therefore the\l"
    .string "LORD sent lions among them, which\l"
    .string "slew some of them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_26::
    .string "Wherefore they spake to the king of\n"
    .string "Assyria, saying, The nations which\l"
    .string "thou hast removed, and placed in the\l"
    .string "cities of Samaria, know not the\l"
    .string "manner of the God of the land:\l"
    .string "therefore he hath sent lions among\l"
    .string "them, and, behold, they slay them,\l"
    .string "because they know not the manner of\l"
    .string "the God of the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_27::
    .string "Then the king of Assyria commanded,\n"
    .string "saying, Carry thither one of the\l"
    .string "priests whom ye brought from thence;\l"
    .string "and let them go and dwell there,\l"
    .string "and let him teach them the manner of\l"
    .string "the God of the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_28::
    .string "Then one of the priests whom they\n"
    .string "had carried away from Samaria came\l"
    .string "and dwelt in Bethel, and taught them\l"
    .string "how they should fear the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_29::
    .string "Howbeit every nation made gods of\n"
    .string "their own, and put them in the houses\l"
    .string "of the high places which the\l"
    .string "Samaritans had made, every nation in\l"
    .string "their cities wherein they dwelt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_30::
    .string "And the men of Babylon made\n"
    .string "Succothbenoth, and the men of Cuth\l"
    .string "made Nergal, and the men of Hamath\l"
    .string "made Ashima,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_31::
    .string "And the Avites made Nibhaz and\n"
    .string "Tartak, and the Sepharvites burnt\l"
    .string "their children in fire to\l"
    .string "Adrammelech and Anammelech, the\l"
    .string "gods of Sepharvaim$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_32::
    .string "So they feared the LORD, and made\n"
    .string "unto themselves of the lowest of\l"
    .string "them priests of the high places,\l"
    .string "which sacrificed for them in the\l"
    .string "houses of the high places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_33::
    .string "They feared the LORD, and served\n"
    .string "their own gods, after the manner of\l"
    .string "the nations whom they carried away\l"
    .string "from thence.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_34::
    .string "Unto this day they do after the\n"
    .string "former manners: they fear not the\l"
    .string "LORD, neither do they after their\l"
    .string "statutes, or after their ordinances,\l"
    .string "or after the law and commandment\l"
    .string "which the LORD commanded the\l"
    .string "children of Jacob, whom he named\l"
    .string "Israel;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_35::
    .string "With whom the LORD had made a\n"
    .string "covenant, and charged them, saying,\l"
    .string "Ye shall not fear other gods, nor\l"
    .string "bow yourselves to them, nor serve\l"
    .string "them, nor sacrifice to them:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_36::
    .string "But the LORD, who brought you up out\n"
    .string "of the land of Egypt with great\l"
    .string "power and a stretched out arm, him\l"
    .string "shall ye fear, and him shall ye\l"
    .string "worship, and to him shall ye do\l"
    .string "sacrifice$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_37::
    .string "And the statutes, and the\n"
    .string "ordinances, and the law, and the\l"
    .string "commandment, which he wrote for you,\l"
    .string "ye shall observe to do for evermore;\l"
    .string "and ye shall not fear other gods.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_38::
    .string "And the covenant that I have made\n"
    .string "with you ye shall not forget;\l"
    .string "neither shall ye fear other gods.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_39::
    .string "But the LORD your God ye shall\n"
    .string "fear; and he shall deliver you out\l"
    .string "of the hand of all your enemies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_40::
    .string "Howbeit they did not hearken, but\n"
    .string "they did after their former manner.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_17_41::
    .string "So these nations feared the LORD,\n"
    .string "and served their graven images, both\l"
    .string "their children, and their\l"
    .string "children’s children: as did their\l"
    .string "fathers, so do they unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the third\n"
    .string "year of Hoshea son of Elah king of\l"
    .string "Israel, that Hezekiah the son of\l"
    .string "Ahaz king of Judah began to reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_2::
    .string "Twenty and five years old was he\n"
    .string "when he began to reign; and he\l"
    .string "reigned twenty and nine years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. His mother’s name also\l"
    .string "was Abi, the daughter of Zachariah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_3::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that David his father did.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_4::
    .string "He removed the high places, and\n"
    .string "brake the images, and cut down the\l"
    .string "groves, and brake in pieces the\l"
    .string "brasen serpent that Moses had made:\l"
    .string "for unto those days the children of\l"
    .string "Israel did burn incense to it: and he\l"
    .string "called it Nehushtan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_5::
    .string "He trusted in the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel; so that after him was none\l"
    .string "like him among all the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah, nor any that were before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_6::
    .string "For he clave to the LORD, and\n"
    .string "departed not from following him,\l"
    .string "but kept his commandments, which the\l"
    .string "LORD commanded Moses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_7::
    .string "And the LORD was with him; and he\n"
    .string "prospered whithersoever he went\l"
    .string "forth: and he rebelled against the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria, and served him not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_8::
    .string "He smote the Philistines, even unto\n"
    .string "Gaza, and the borders thereof, from\l"
    .string "the tower of the watchmen to the\l"
    .string "fenced city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_9::
    .string "And it came to pass in the fourth\n"
    .string "year of king Hezekiah, which was the\l"
    .string "seventh year of Hoshea son of Elah\l"
    .string "king of Israel, that Shalmaneser\l"
    .string "king of Assyria came up against\l"
    .string "Samaria, and besieged it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_10::
    .string "And at the end of three years they\n"
    .string "took it: even in the sixth year of\l"
    .string "Hezekiah, that is in the ninth year\l"
    .string "of Hoshea king of Israel, Samaria\l"
    .string "was taken.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_11::
    .string "And the king of Assyria did carry\n"
    .string "away Israel unto Assyria, and put\l"
    .string "them in Halah and in Habor by the\l"
    .string "river of Gozan, and in the cities of\l"
    .string "the Medes:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_12::
    .string "Because they obeyed not the voice of\n"
    .string "the LORD their God, but transgressed\l"
    .string "his covenant, and all that Moses the\l"
    .string "servant of the LORD commanded, and\l"
    .string "would not hear them, nor do them$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_13::
    .string "Now in the fourteenth year of king\n"
    .string "Hezekiah did Sennacherib king of\l"
    .string "Assyria come up against all the\l"
    .string "fenced cities of Judah, and took them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_14::
    .string "And Hezekiah king of Judah sent to\n"
    .string "the king of Assyria to Lachish,\l"
    .string "saying, I have offended; return from\l"
    .string "me: that which thou puttest on me\l"
    .string "will I bear. And the king of Assyria\l"
    .string "appointed unto Hezekiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah three hundred talents of\l"
    .string "silver and thirty talents of gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_15::
    .string "And Hezekiah gave him all the\n"
    .string "silver that was found in the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and in the treasures of\l"
    .string "the king’s house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_16::
    .string "At that time did Hezekiah cut off\n"
    .string "the gold from the doors of the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD, and from the\l"
    .string "pillars which Hezekiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah had overlaid, and gave it to\l"
    .string "the king of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_17::
    .string "And the king of Assyria sent Tartan\n"
    .string "and Rabsaris and Rabshakeh from\l"
    .string "Lachish to king Hezekiah with a great\l"
    .string "host against Jerusalem. And they\l"
    .string "went up and came to Jerusalem. And\l"
    .string "when they were come up, they came and\l"
    .string "stood by the conduit of the upper\l"
    .string "pool, which is in the highway of the\l"
    .string "fuller’s field.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_18::
    .string "And when they had called to the\n"
    .string "king, there came out to them Eliakim\l"
    .string "the son of Hilkiah, which was over\l"
    .string "the household, and Shebna the\l"
    .string "scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the\l"
    .string "recorder.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_19::
    .string "And Rabshakeh said unto them, Speak\n"
    .string "ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "great king, the king of Assyria, What\l"
    .string "confidence is this wherein thou\l"
    .string "trustest?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_20::
    .string "Thou sayest, (but they are but vain\n"
    .string "words,) I have counsel and strength\l"
    .string "for the war. Now on whom dost thou\l"
    .string "trust, that thou rebellest against\l"
    .string "me?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_21::
    .string "Now, behold, thou trustest upon\n"
    .string "the staff of this bruised reed, even\l"
    .string "upon Egypt, on which if a man lean,\l"
    .string "it will go into his hand, and\l"
    .string "pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of\l"
    .string "Egypt unto all that trust on him$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_22::
    .string "But if ye say unto me, We trust in\n"
    .string "the LORD our God: is not that he,\l"
    .string "whose high places and whose altars\l"
    .string "Hezekiah hath taken away, and hath\l"
    .string "said to Judah and Jerusalem, Ye\l"
    .string "shall worship before this altar in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_23::
    .string "Now therefore, I pray thee, give\n"
    .string "pledges to my lord the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and I will deliver thee\l"
    .string "two thousand horses, if thou be able\l"
    .string "on thy part to set riders upon them$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_24::
    .string "How then wilt thou turn away the\n"
    .string "face of one captain of the least of\l"
    .string "my master’s servants, and put thy\l"
    .string "trust on Egypt for chariots and for\l"
    .string "horsemen?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_25::
    .string "Am I now come up without the LORD\n"
    .string "against this place to destroy it?\l"
    .string "The LORD said to me, Go up against\l"
    .string "this land, and destroy it$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_26::
    .string "Then said Eliakim the son of\n"
    .string "Hilkiah, and Shebna, and Joah, unto\l"
    .string "Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, to\l"
    .string "thy servants in the Syrian language;\l"
    .string "for we understand it: and talk not\l"
    .string "with us in the Jews’ language in the\l"
    .string "ears of the people that are on the\l"
    .string "wall.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_27::
    .string "But Rabshakeh said unto them, Hath\n"
    .string "my master sent me to thy master, and\l"
    .string "to thee, to speak these words? hath\l"
    .string "he not sent me to the men which sit on\l"
    .string "the wall, that they may eat their\l"
    .string "own dung, and drink their own piss\l"
    .string "with you?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_28::
    .string "Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with\n"
    .string "a loud voice in the Jews’ language,\l"
    .string "and spake, saying, Hear the word of\l"
    .string "the great king, the king of Assyria:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_29::
    .string "Thus saith the king, Let not\n"
    .string "Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall\l"
    .string "not be able to deliver you out of\l"
    .string "his hand:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_30::
    .string "Neither let Hezekiah make you trust\n"
    .string "in the LORD, saying, The LORD will\l"
    .string "surely deliver us, and this city\l"
    .string "shall not be delivered into the\l"
    .string "hand of the king of Assyria$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_31::
    .string "Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus\n"
    .string "saith the king of Assyria, Make an\l"
    .string "agreement with me by a present, and\l"
    .string "come out to me, and then eat ye every\l"
    .string "man of his own vine, and every one of\l"
    .string "his fig tree, and drink ye every one\l"
    .string "the waters of his cistern:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_32::
    .string "Until I come and take you away to a\n"
    .string "land like your own land, a land of\l"
    .string "corn and wine, a land of bread and\l"
    .string "vineyards, a land of oil olive and\l"
    .string "of honey, that ye may live, and not\l"
    .string "die: and hearken not unto Hezekiah,\l"
    .string "when he persuadeth you, saying, The\l"
    .string "LORD will deliver us$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_33::
    .string "Hath any of the gods of the nations\n"
    .string "delivered at all his land out of\l"
    .string "the hand of the king of Assyria?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_34::
    .string "Where are the gods of Hamath, and of\n"
    .string "Arpad? where are the gods of\l"
    .string "Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah? have\l"
    .string "they delivered Samaria out of mine\l"
    .string "hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_35::
    .string "Who are they among all the gods of\n"
    .string "the countries, that have delivered\l"
    .string "their country out of mine hand, that\l"
    .string "the LORD should deliver Jerusalem\l"
    .string "out of mine hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_36::
    .string "But the people held their peace,\n"
    .string "and answered him not a word: for the\l"
    .string "king’s commandment was, saying,\l"
    .string "Answer him not$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_18_37::
    .string "Then came Eliakim the son of\n"
    .string "Hilkiah, which was over the\l"
    .string "household, and Shebna the scribe,\l"
    .string "and Joah the son of Asaph the\l"
    .string "recorder, to Hezekiah with their\l"
    .string "clothes rent, and told him the words\l"
    .string "of Rabshakeh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when king\n"
    .string "Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his\l"
    .string "clothes, and covered himself with\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and went into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_2::
    .string "And he sent Eliakim, which was over\n"
    .string "the household, and Shebna the\l"
    .string "scribe, and the elders of the\l"
    .string "priests, covered with sackcloth, to\l"
    .string "Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_3::
    .string "And they said unto him, Thus saith\n"
    .string "Hezekiah, This day is a day of\l"
    .string "trouble, and of rebuke, and\l"
    .string "blasphemy; for the children are\l"
    .string "come to the birth, and there is not\l"
    .string "strength to bring forth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_4::
    .string "It may be the LORD thy God will\n"
    .string "hear all the words of Rabshakeh,\l"
    .string "whom the king of Assyria his master\l"
    .string "hath sent to reproach the living\l"
    .string "God; and will reprove the words\l"
    .string "which the LORD thy God hath heard:\l"
    .string "wherefore lift up thy prayer for\l"
    .string "the remnant that are left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_5::
    .string "So the servants of king Hezekiah\n"
    .string "came to Isaiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_6::
    .string "And Isaiah said unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "shall ye say to your master, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the\l"
    .string "words which thou hast heard, with\l"
    .string "which the servants of the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria have blasphemed me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_7::
    .string "Behold, I will send a blast upon\n"
    .string "him, and he shall hear a rumour, and\l"
    .string "shall return to his own land; and I\l"
    .string "will cause him to fall by the\l"
    .string "sword in his own land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_8::
    .string "So Rabshakeh returned, and found the\n"
    .string "king of Assyria warring against\l"
    .string "Libnah: for he had heard that he was\l"
    .string "departed from Lachish.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_9::
    .string "And when he heard say of Tirhakah\n"
    .string "king of Ethiopia, Behold, he is come\l"
    .string "out to fight against thee: he sent\l"
    .string "messengers again unto Hezekiah,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_10::
    .string "Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah\n"
    .string "king of Judah, saying, Let not thy\l"
    .string "God in whom thou trustest deceive\l"
    .string "thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not\l"
    .string "be delivered into the hand of the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_11::
    .string "Behold, thou hast heard what the\n"
    .string "kings of Assyria have done to all\l"
    .string "lands, by destroying them utterly:\l"
    .string "and shalt thou be delivered?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_12::
    .string "Have the gods of the nations\n"
    .string "delivered them which my fathers have\l"
    .string "destroyed; as Gozan, and Haran, and\l"
    .string "Rezeph, and the children of Eden\l"
    .string "which were in Thelasar?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_13::
    .string "Where is the king of Hamath, and the\n"
    .string "king of Arpad, and the king of the\l"
    .string "city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and\l"
    .string "Ivah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_14::
    .string "And Hezekiah received the letter of\n"
    .string "the hand of the messengers, and read\l"
    .string "it: and Hezekiah went up into the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and spread it\l"
    .string "before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_15::
    .string "And Hezekiah prayed before the\n"
    .string "LORD, and said, O LORD God of Israel,\l"
    .string "which dwellest between the\l"
    .string "cherubims, thou art the God, even\l"
    .string "thou alone, of all the kingdoms of\l"
    .string "the earth; thou hast made heaven and\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_16::
    .string "LORD, bow down thine ear, and hear:\n"
    .string "open, LORD, thine eyes, and see: and\l"
    .string "hear the words of Sennacherib, which\l"
    .string "hath sent him to reproach the\l"
    .string "living God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_17::
    .string "Of a truth, LORD, the kings of\n"
    .string "Assyria have destroyed the nations\l"
    .string "and their lands,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_18::
    .string "And have cast their gods into the\n"
    .string "fire: for they were no gods, but the\l"
    .string "work of men’s hands, wood and stone:\l"
    .string "therefore they have destroyed them$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_19::
    .string "Now therefore, O LORD our God, I\n"
    .string "beseech thee, save thou us out of his\l"
    .string "hand, that all the kingdoms of the\l"
    .string "earth may know that thou art the LORD\l"
    .string "God, even thou only.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_20::
    .string "Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to\n"
    .string "Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, That which thou hast\l"
    .string "prayed to me against Sennacherib\l"
    .string "king of Assyria I have heard.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_21::
    .string "This is the word that the LORD hath\n"
    .string "spoken concerning him; The virgin\l"
    .string "the daughter of Zion hath despised\l"
    .string "thee, and laughed thee to scorn; the\l"
    .string "daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken\l"
    .string "her head at thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_22::
    .string "Whom hast thou reproached and\n"
    .string "blasphemed? and against whom hast\l"
    .string "thou exalted thy voice, and lifted\l"
    .string "up thine eyes on high? even against\l"
    .string "the Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_23::
    .string "By thy messengers thou hast\n"
    .string "reproached the LORD, and hast said,\l"
    .string "With the multitude of my chariots I\l"
    .string "am come up to the height of the\l"
    .string "mountains, to the sides of Lebanon,\l"
    .string "and will cut down the tall cedar\l"
    .string "trees thereof, and the choice fir\l"
    .string "trees thereof: and I will enter into\l"
    .string "the lodgings of his borders, and\l"
    .string "into the forest of his Carmel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_24::
    .string "I have digged and drunk strange\n"
    .string "waters, and with the sole of my feet\l"
    .string "have I dried up all the rivers of\l"
    .string "besieged places.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_25::
    .string "Hast thou not heard long ago how I\n"
    .string "have done it, and of ancient times\l"
    .string "that I have formed it? now have I\l"
    .string "brought it to pass, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest be to lay waste fenced\l"
    .string "cities into ruinous heaps.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_26::
    .string "Therefore their inhabitants were of\n"
    .string "small power, they were dismayed and\l"
    .string "confounded; they were as the grass of\l"
    .string "the field, and as the green herb, as\l"
    .string "the grass on the house tops, and as\l"
    .string "corn blasted before it be grown up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_27::
    .string "But I know thy abode, and thy going\n"
    .string "out, and thy coming in, and thy rage\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_28::
    .string "Because thy rage against me and thy\n"
    .string "tumult is come up into mine ears,\l"
    .string "therefore I will put my hook in thy\l"
    .string "nose, and my bridle in thy lips,\l"
    .string "and I will turn thee back by the way\l"
    .string "by which thou camest.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_29::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto thee,\n"
    .string "Ye shall eat this year such things\l"
    .string "as grow of themselves, and in the\l"
    .string "second year that which springeth of\l"
    .string "the same; and in the third year sow\l"
    .string "ye, and reap, and plant vineyards,\l"
    .string "and eat the fruits thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_30::
    .string "And the remnant that is escaped of\n"
    .string "the house of Judah shall yet again\l"
    .string "take root downward, and bear fruit\l"
    .string "upward.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_31::
    .string "For out of Jerusalem shall go\n"
    .string "forth a remnant, and they that\l"
    .string "escape out of mount Zion: the zeal\l"
    .string "of the LORD of hosts shall do this.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_32::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "concerning the king of Assyria, He\l"
    .string "shall not come into this city, nor\l"
    .string "shoot an arrow there, nor come before\l"
    .string "it with shield, nor cast a bank\l"
    .string "against it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_33::
    .string "By the way that he came, by the same\n"
    .string "shall he return, and shall not\l"
    .string "come into this city, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_34::
    .string "For I will defend this city, to\n"
    .string "save it, for mine own sake, and for my\l"
    .string "servant David’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_35::
    .string "And it came to pass that night, that\n"
    .string "the angel of the LORD went out, and\l"
    .string "smote in the camp of the Assyrians\l"
    .string "an hundred fourscore and five\l"
    .string "thousand: and when they arose early\l"
    .string "in the morning, behold, they were\l"
    .string "all dead corpses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_36::
    .string "So Sennacherib king of Assyria\n"
    .string "departed, and went and returned, and\l"
    .string "dwelt at Nineveh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_19_37::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he was\n"
    .string "worshipping in the house of Nisroch\l"
    .string "his god, that Adrammelech and\l"
    .string "Sharezer his sons smote him with the\l"
    .string "sword: and they escaped into the\l"
    .string "land of Armenia. And Esarhaddon his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_1::
    .string "In those days was Hezekiah sick unto\n"
    .string "death. And the prophet Isaiah the\l"
    .string "son of Amoz came to him, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine\l"
    .string "house in order; for thou shalt die,\l"
    .string "and not live.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_2::
    .string "Then he turned his face to the\n"
    .string "wall, and prayed unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_3::
    .string "I beseech thee, O LORD, remember now\n"
    .string "how I have walked before thee in\l"
    .string "truth and with a perfect heart, and\l"
    .string "have done that which is good in thy\l"
    .string "sight. And Hezekiah wept sore$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, afore Isaiah\n"
    .string "was gone out into the middle court,\l"
    .string "that the word of the LORD came to him,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_5::
    .string "Turn again, and tell Hezekiah the\n"
    .string "captain of my people, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD, the God of David thy\l"
    .string "father, I have heard thy prayer, I\l"
    .string "have seen thy tears: behold, I will\l"
    .string "heal thee: on the third day thou\l"
    .string "shalt go up unto the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_6::
    .string "And I will add unto thy days\n"
    .string "fifteen years; and I will deliver\l"
    .string "thee and this city out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the king of Assyria; and I will\l"
    .string "defend this city for mine own sake,\l"
    .string "and for my servant David’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_7::
    .string "And Isaiah said, Take a lump of figs\n"
    .string " And they took and laid it on the\l"
    .string "boil, and he recovered.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_8::
    .string "And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah, What\n"
    .string "shall be the sign that the LORD\l"
    .string "will heal me, and that I shall go\l"
    .string "up into the house of the LORD the\l"
    .string "third day?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_9::
    .string "And Isaiah said, This sign shalt\n"
    .string "thou have of the LORD, that the LORD\l"
    .string "will do the thing that he hath\l"
    .string "spoken: shall the shadow go forward\l"
    .string "ten degrees, or go back ten degrees?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_10::
    .string "And Hezekiah answered, It is a\n"
    .string "light thing for the shadow to go down\l"
    .string "ten degrees: nay, but let the shadow\l"
    .string "return backward ten degrees$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_11::
    .string "And Isaiah the prophet cried unto\n"
    .string "the LORD: and he brought the shadow\l"
    .string "ten degrees backward, by which it had\l"
    .string "gone down in the dial of Ahaz.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_12::
    .string "At that time Berodachbaladan, the\n"
    .string "son of Baladan, king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "sent letters and a present unto\l"
    .string "Hezekiah: for he had heard that\l"
    .string "Hezekiah had been sick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_13::
    .string "And Hezekiah hearkened unto them,\n"
    .string "and shewed them all the house of his\l"
    .string "precious things, the silver, and the\l"
    .string "gold, and the spices, and the\l"
    .string "precious ointment, and all the\l"
    .string "house of his armour, and all that\l"
    .string "was found in his treasures: there was\l"
    .string "nothing in his house, nor in all his\l"
    .string "dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_14::
    .string "Then came Isaiah the prophet unto\n"
    .string "king Hezekiah, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "What said these men? and from whence\l"
    .string "came they unto thee? And Hezekiah\l"
    .string "said, They are come from a far\l"
    .string "country, even from Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_15::
    .string "And he said, What have they seen in\n"
    .string "thine house? And Hezekiah answered,\l"
    .string "All the things that are in mine\l"
    .string "house have they seen: there is\l"
    .string "nothing among my treasures that I\l"
    .string "have not shewed them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_16::
    .string "And Isaiah said unto Hezekiah, Hear\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_17::
    .string "Behold, the days come, that all\n"
    .string "that is in thine house, and that\l"
    .string "which thy fathers have laid up in\l"
    .string "store unto this day, shall be\l"
    .string "carried into Babylon: nothing\l"
    .string "shall be left, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_18::
    .string "And of thy sons that shall issue\n"
    .string "from thee, which thou shalt beget,\l"
    .string "shall they take away; and they\l"
    .string "shall be eunuchs in the palace of\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_19::
    .string "Then said Hezekiah unto Isaiah, Good\n"
    .string "is the word of the LORD which thou\l"
    .string "hast spoken. And he said, Is it not\l"
    .string "good, if peace and truth be in my\l"
    .string "days?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_20::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Hezekiah, and all his might, and how\l"
    .string "he made a pool, and a conduit, and\l"
    .string "brought water into the city, are they\l"
    .string "not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_20_21::
    .string "And Hezekiah slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers: and Manasseh his son reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_1::
    .string "Manasseh was twelve years old when\n"
    .string "he began to reign, and reigned fifty\l"
    .string "and five years in Jerusalem. And his\l"
    .string "mother’s name was Hephzibah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_2::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, after the\l"
    .string "abominations of the heathen, whom the\l"
    .string "LORD cast out before the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_3::
    .string "For he built up again the high\n"
    .string "places which Hezekiah his father had\l"
    .string "destroyed; and he reared up altars\l"
    .string "for Baal, and made a grove, as did\l"
    .string "Ahab king of Israel; and worshipped\l"
    .string "all the host of heaven, and served\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_4::
    .string "And he built altars in the house of\n"
    .string "the LORD, of which the LORD said, In\l"
    .string "Jerusalem will I put my name.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_5::
    .string "And he built altars for all the\n"
    .string "host of heaven in the two courts of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_6::
    .string "And he made his son pass through\n"
    .string "the fire, and observed times, and\l"
    .string "used enchantments, and dealt with\l"
    .string "familiar spirits and wizards: he\l"
    .string "wrought much wickedness in the sight\l"
    .string "of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_7::
    .string "And he set a graven image of the\n"
    .string "grove that he had made in the house,\l"
    .string "of which the LORD said to David, and\l"
    .string "to Solomon his son, In this house,\l"
    .string "and in Jerusalem, which I have\l"
    .string "chosen out of all tribes of Israel,\l"
    .string "will I put my name for ever:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_8::
    .string "Neither will I make the feet of\n"
    .string "Israel move any more out of the land\l"
    .string "which I gave their fathers; only if\l"
    .string "they will observe to do according\l"
    .string "to all that I have commanded them,\l"
    .string "and according to all the law that\l"
    .string "my servant Moses commanded them$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_9::
    .string "But they hearkened not: and Manasseh\n"
    .string "seduced them to do more evil than\l"
    .string "did the nations whom the LORD\l"
    .string "destroyed before the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_10::
    .string "And the LORD spake by his servants\n"
    .string "the prophets, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_11::
    .string "Because Manasseh king of Judah hath\n"
    .string "done these abominations, and hath\l"
    .string "done wickedly above all that the\l"
    .string "Amorites did, which were before him,\l"
    .string "and hath made Judah also to sin with\l"
    .string "his idols:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_12::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel, Behold, I am bringing such\l"
    .string "evil upon Jerusalem and Judah, that\l"
    .string "whosoever heareth of it, both his\l"
    .string "ears shall tingle$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_13::
    .string "And I will stretch over Jerusalem\n"
    .string "the line of Samaria, and the\l"
    .string "plummet of the house of Ahab: and I\l"
    .string "will wipe Jerusalem as a man\l"
    .string "wipeth a dish, wiping it, and\l"
    .string "turning it upside down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_14::
    .string "And I will forsake the remnant of\n"
    .string "mine inheritance, and deliver them\l"
    .string "into the hand of their enemies; and\l"
    .string "they shall become a prey and a\l"
    .string "spoil to all their enemies;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_15::
    .string "Because they have done that which\n"
    .string "was evil in my sight, and have\l"
    .string "provoked me to anger, since the day\l"
    .string "their fathers came forth out of\l"
    .string "Egypt, even unto this day$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_16::
    .string "Moreover Manasseh shed innocent\n"
    .string "blood very much, till he had\l"
    .string "filled Jerusalem from one end to\l"
    .string "another; beside his sin wherewith he\l"
    .string "made Judah to sin, in doing that\l"
    .string "which was evil in the sight of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_17::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Manasseh, and all that he did, and\l"
    .string "his sin that he sinned, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_18::
    .string "And Manasseh slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried in the garden\l"
    .string "of his own house, in the garden of\l"
    .string "Uzza: and Amon his son reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_19::
    .string "Amon was twenty and two years old\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned two years in Jerusalem. And\l"
    .string "his mother’s name was Meshullemeth,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_20::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, as his father\l"
    .string "Manasseh did.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_21::
    .string "And he walked in all the way that\n"
    .string "his father walked in, and served the\l"
    .string "idols that his father served, and\l"
    .string "worshipped them:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_22::
    .string "And he forsook the LORD God of his\n"
    .string "fathers, and walked not in the way of\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_23::
    .string "And the servants of Amon conspired\n"
    .string "against him, and slew the king in his\l"
    .string "own house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_24::
    .string "And the people of the land slew\n"
    .string "all them that had conspired\l"
    .string "against king Amon; and the people\l"
    .string "of the land made Josiah his son king\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_25::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Amon\n"
    .string "which he did, are they not written in\l"
    .string "the book of the chronicles of the\l"
    .string "kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_21_26::
    .string "And he was buried in his sepulchre\n"
    .string "in the garden of Uzza: and Josiah his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_1::
    .string "Josiah was eight years old when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned thirty\l"
    .string "and one years in Jerusalem. And his\l"
    .string "mother’s name was Jedidah, the\l"
    .string "daughter of Adaiah of Boscath.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_2::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, and walked in\l"
    .string "all the way of David his father, and\l"
    .string "turned not aside to the right hand or\l"
    .string "to the left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_3::
    .string "And it came to pass in the\n"
    .string "eighteenth year of king Josiah, that\l"
    .string "the king sent Shaphan the son of\l"
    .string "Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, the\l"
    .string "scribe, to the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_4::
    .string "Go up to Hilkiah the high priest,\n"
    .string "that he may sum the silver which is\l"
    .string "brought into the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which the keepers of the door have\l"
    .string "gathered of the people:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_5::
    .string "And let them deliver it into the\n"
    .string "hand of the doers of the work, that\l"
    .string "have the oversight of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD: and let them give it to the\l"
    .string "doers of the work which is in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, to repair the\l"
    .string "breaches of the house,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_6::
    .string "Unto carpenters, and builders, and\n"
    .string "masons, and to buy timber and hewn\l"
    .string "stone to repair the house$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_7::
    .string "Howbeit there was no reckoning made\n"
    .string "with them of the money that was\l"
    .string "delivered into their hand, because\l"
    .string "they dealt faithfully.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_8::
    .string "And Hilkiah the high priest said\n"
    .string "unto Shaphan the scribe, I have\l"
    .string "found the book of the law in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD. And Hilkiah gave\l"
    .string "the book to Shaphan, and he read it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_9::
    .string "And Shaphan the scribe came to the\n"
    .string "king, and brought the king word\l"
    .string "again, and said, Thy servants have\l"
    .string "gathered the money that was found in\l"
    .string "the house, and have delivered it\l"
    .string "into the hand of them that do the\l"
    .string "work, that have the oversight of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_10::
    .string "And Shaphan the scribe shewed the\n"
    .string "king, saying, Hilkiah the priest\l"
    .string "hath delivered me a book. And\l"
    .string "Shaphan read it before the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "had heard the words of the book of\l"
    .string "the law, that he rent his clothes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_12::
    .string "And the king commanded Hilkiah the\n"
    .string "priest, and Ahikam the son of\l"
    .string "Shaphan, and Achbor the son of\l"
    .string "Michaiah, and Shaphan the scribe,\l"
    .string "and Asahiah a servant of the king’s,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_13::
    .string "Go ye, enquire of the LORD for me,\n"
    .string "and for the people, and for all\l"
    .string "Judah, concerning the words of this\l"
    .string "book that is found: for great is the\l"
    .string "wrath of the LORD that is kindled\l"
    .string "against us, because our fathers have\l"
    .string "not hearkened unto the words of this\l"
    .string "book, to do according unto all that\l"
    .string "which is written concerning us$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_14::
    .string "So Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam,\n"
    .string "and Achbor, and Shaphan, and\l"
    .string "Asahiah, went unto Huldah the\l"
    .string "prophetess, the wife of Shallum the\l"
    .string "son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas,\l"
    .string "keeper of the wardrobe; (now she\l"
    .string "dwelt in Jerusalem in the\l"
    .string "college;) and they communed with\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_15::
    .string "And she said unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel, Tell the\l"
    .string "man that sent you to me,"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_16::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will bring evil upon this place,\l"
    .string "and upon the inhabitants thereof,\l"
    .string "even all the words of the book which\l"
    .string "the king of Judah hath read:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_17::
    .string "Because they have forsaken me, and\n"
    .string "have burned incense unto other gods,\l"
    .string "that they might provoke me to anger\l"
    .string "with all the works of their hands;\l"
    .string "therefore my wrath shall be\l"
    .string "kindled against this place, and\l"
    .string "shall not be quenched$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_18::
    .string "But to the king of Judah which sent\n"
    .string "you to enquire of the LORD, thus\l"
    .string "shall ye say to him, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, As touching the\l"
    .string "words which thou hast heard;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_19::
    .string "Because thine heart was tender, and\n"
    .string "thou hast humbled thyself before\l"
    .string "the LORD, when thou heardest what I\l"
    .string "spake against this place, and\l"
    .string "against the inhabitants thereof,\l"
    .string "that they should become a\l"
    .string "desolation and a curse, and hast\l"
    .string "rent thy clothes, and wept before\l"
    .string "me; I also have heard thee, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_22_20::
    .string "Behold therefore, I will gather\n"
    .string "thee unto thy fathers, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be gathered into thy grave in\l"
    .string "peace; and thine eyes shall not see\l"
    .string "all the evil which I will bring\l"
    .string "upon this place. And they brought\l"
    .string "the king word again.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_1::
    .string "And the king sent, and they gathered\n"
    .string "unto him all the elders of Judah\l"
    .string "and of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_2::
    .string "And the king went up into the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and all the men of\l"
    .string "Judah and all the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem with him, and the\l"
    .string "priests, and the prophets, and all\l"
    .string "the people, both small and great:\l"
    .string "and he read in their ears all the\l"
    .string "words of the book of the covenant\l"
    .string "which was found in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_3::
    .string "And the king stood by a pillar,\n"
    .string "and made a covenant before the LORD,\l"
    .string "to walk after the LORD, and to keep\l"
    .string "his commandments and his testimonies\l"
    .string "and his statutes with all their\l"
    .string "heart and all their soul, to\l"
    .string "perform the words of this covenant\l"
    .string "that were written in this book. And\l"
    .string "all the people stood to the\l"
    .string "covenant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_4::
    .string "And the king commanded Hilkiah the\n"
    .string "high priest, and the priests of the\l"
    .string "second order, and the keepers of the\l"
    .string "door, to bring forth out of the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD all the\l"
    .string "vessels that were made for Baal, and\l"
    .string "for the grove, and for all the host\l"
    .string "of heaven: and he burned them without\l"
    .string "Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron,\l"
    .string "and carried the ashes of them unto\l"
    .string "Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_5::
    .string "And he put down the idolatrous\n"
    .string "priests, whom the kings of Judah had\l"
    .string "ordained to burn incense in the high\l"
    .string "places in the cities of Judah, and in\l"
    .string "the places round about Jerusalem;\l"
    .string "them also that burned incense unto\l"
    .string "Baal, to the sun, and to the moon,\l"
    .string "and to the planets, and to all the\l"
    .string "host of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_6::
    .string "And he brought out the grove from\n"
    .string "the house of the LORD, without\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, unto the brook Kidron,\l"
    .string "and burned it at the brook Kidron,\l"
    .string "and stamped it small to powder,\l"
    .string "and cast the powder thereof upon\l"
    .string "the graves of the children of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_7::
    .string "And he brake down the houses of the\n"
    .string "sodomites, that were by the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, where the women wove\l"
    .string "hangings for the grove.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_8::
    .string "And he brought all the priests out\n"
    .string "of the cities of Judah, and defiled\l"
    .string "the high places where the priests\l"
    .string "had burned incense, from Geba to\l"
    .string "Beersheba, and brake down the high\l"
    .string "places of the gates that were in the\l"
    .string "entering in of the gate of Joshua the\l"
    .string "governor of the city, which were on a\l"
    .string "man’s left hand at the gate of the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_9::
    .string "Nevertheless the priests of the\n"
    .string "high places came not up to the\l"
    .string "altar of the LORD in Jerusalem, but\l"
    .string "they did eat of the unleavened bread\l"
    .string "among their brethren.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_10::
    .string "And he defiled Topheth, which is in\n"
    .string "the valley of the children of\l"
    .string "Hinnom, that no man might make his\l"
    .string "son or his daughter to pass through\l"
    .string "the fire to Molech.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_11::
    .string "And he took away the horses that the\n"
    .string "kings of Judah had given to the sun,\l"
    .string "at the entering in of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, by the chamber of\l"
    .string "Nathanmelech the chamberlain, which\l"
    .string "was in the suburbs, and burned the\l"
    .string "chariots of the sun with fire.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_12::
    .string "And the altars that were on the top\n"
    .string "of the upper chamber of Ahaz, which\l"
    .string "the kings of Judah had made, and the\l"
    .string "altars which Manasseh had made in\l"
    .string "the two courts of the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, did the king beat down, and\l"
    .string "brake them down from thence, and cast\l"
    .string "the dust of them into the brook\l"
    .string "Kidron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_13::
    .string "And the high places that were\n"
    .string "before Jerusalem, which were on the\l"
    .string "right hand of the mount of\l"
    .string "corruption, which Solomon the king\l"
    .string "of Israel had builded for Ashtoreth\l"
    .string "the abomination of the Zidonians, and\l"
    .string "for Chemosh the abomination of the\l"
    .string "Moabites, and for Milcom the\l"
    .string "abomination of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, did the king defile.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_14::
    .string "And he brake in pieces the images,\n"
    .string "and cut down the groves, and filled\l"
    .string "their places with the bones of men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_15::
    .string "Moreover the altar that was at\n"
    .string "Bethel, and the high place which\l"
    .string "Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made\l"
    .string "Israel to sin, had made, both that\l"
    .string "altar and the high place he brake\l"
    .string "down, and burned the high place, and\l"
    .string "stamped it small to powder, and\l"
    .string "burned the grove.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_16::
    .string "And as Josiah turned himself, he\n"
    .string "spied the sepulchres that were\l"
    .string "there in the mount, and sent, and\l"
    .string "took the bones out of the\l"
    .string "sepulchres, and burned them upon\l"
    .string "the altar, and polluted it,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "which the man of God proclaimed, who\l"
    .string "proclaimed these words.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_17::
    .string "Then he said, What title is that\n"
    .string "that I see? And the men of the city\l"
    .string "told him, It is the sepulchre of\l"
    .string "the man of God, which came from\l"
    .string "Judah, and proclaimed these things\l"
    .string "that thou hast done against the\l"
    .string "altar of Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_18::
    .string "And he said, Let him alone; let no\n"
    .string "man move his bones. So they let his\l"
    .string "bones alone, with the bones of the\l"
    .string "prophet that came out of Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_19::
    .string "And all the houses also of the\n"
    .string "high places that were in the cities\l"
    .string "of Samaria, which the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel had made to provoke the Lord\l"
    .string "to anger, Josiah took away, and did\l"
    .string "to them according to all the acts\l"
    .string "that he had done in Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_20::
    .string "And he slew all the priests of\n"
    .string "the high places that were there\l"
    .string "upon the altars, and burned men’s\l"
    .string "bones upon them, and returned to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_21::
    .string "And the king commanded all the\n"
    .string "people, saying, Keep the passover\l"
    .string "unto the LORD your God, as it is\l"
    .string "written in the book of this covenant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_22::
    .string "Surely there was not holden such a\n"
    .string "passover from the days of the judges\l"
    .string "that judged Israel, nor in all the\l"
    .string "days of the kings of Israel, nor of\l"
    .string "the kings of Judah;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_23::
    .string "But in the eighteenth year of king\n"
    .string "Josiah, wherein this passover was\l"
    .string "holden to the LORD in Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_24::
    .string "Moreover the workers with familiar\n"
    .string "spirits, and the wizards, and the\l"
    .string "images, and the idols, and all the\l"
    .string "abominations that were spied in the\l"
    .string "land of Judah and in Jerusalem, did\l"
    .string "Josiah put away, that he might\l"
    .string "perform the words of the law which\l"
    .string "were written in the book that\l"
    .string "Hilkiah the priest found in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_25::
    .string "And like unto him was there no king\n"
    .string "before him, that turned to the LORD\l"
    .string "with all his heart, and with all\l"
    .string "his soul, and with all his might,\l"
    .string "according to all the law of Moses;\l"
    .string "neither after him arose there any\l"
    .string "like him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_26::
    .string "Notwithstanding the LORD turned not\n"
    .string "from the fierceness of his great\l"
    .string "wrath, wherewith his anger was\l"
    .string "kindled against Judah, because of\l"
    .string "all the provocations that Manasseh\l"
    .string "had provoked him withal.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_27::
    .string "And the LORD said, I will remove\n"
    .string "Judah also out of my sight, as I have\l"
    .string "removed Israel, and will cast off\l"
    .string "this city Jerusalem which I have\l"
    .string "chosen, and the house of which I\l"
    .string "said, My name shall be there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_28::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Josiah,\n"
    .string "and all that he did, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_29::
    .string "In his days Pharaohnechoh king of\n"
    .string "Egypt went up against the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria to the river Euphrates: and\l"
    .string "king Josiah went against him; and he\l"
    .string "slew him at Megiddo, when he had seen\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_30::
    .string "And his servants carried him in a\n"
    .string "chariot dead from Megiddo, and\l"
    .string "brought him to Jerusalem, and buried\l"
    .string "him in his own sepulchre. And the\l"
    .string "people of the land took Jehoahaz\l"
    .string "the son of Josiah, and anointed him,\l"
    .string "and made him king in his father’s\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_31::
    .string "Jehoahaz was twenty and three years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign; and he\l"
    .string "reigned three months in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Hamutal,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_32::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his fathers had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_33::
    .string "And Pharaohnechoh put him in bands\n"
    .string "at Riblah in the land of Hamath,\l"
    .string "that he might not reign in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and put the land to a\l"
    .string "tribute of an hundred talents of\l"
    .string "silver, and a talent of gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_34::
    .string "And Pharaohnechoh made Eliakim the\n"
    .string "son of Josiah king in the room of\l"
    .string "Josiah his father, and turned his\l"
    .string "name to Jehoiakim, and took Jehoahaz\l"
    .string "away: and he came to Egypt, and died\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_35::
    .string "And Jehoiakim gave the silver and\n"
    .string "the gold to Pharaoh; but he taxed the\l"
    .string "land to give the money according to\l"
    .string "the commandment of Pharaoh: he\l"
    .string "exacted the silver and the gold of\l"
    .string "the people of the land, of every\l"
    .string "one according to his taxation, to\l"
    .string "give it unto Pharaohnechoh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_36::
    .string "Jehoiakim was twenty and five years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign; and he\l"
    .string "reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Zebudah,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Pedaiah of Rumah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_23_37::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his fathers had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_1::
    .string "In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of\n"
    .string "Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim\l"
    .string "became his servant three years: then\l"
    .string "he turned and rebelled against him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_2::
    .string "And the LORD sent against him bands\n"
    .string "of the Chaldees, and bands of the\l"
    .string "Syrians, and bands of the Moabites,\l"
    .string "and bands of the children of Ammon,\l"
    .string "and sent them against Judah to\l"
    .string "destroy it, according to the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD, which he spake by his\l"
    .string "servants the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_3::
    .string "Surely at the commandment of the\n"
    .string "LORD came this upon Judah, to remove\l"
    .string "them out of his sight, for the sins of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, according to all that he\l"
    .string "did;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_4::
    .string "And also for the innocent blood\n"
    .string "that he shed: for he filled\l"
    .string "Jerusalem with innocent blood;\l"
    .string "which the LORD would not pardon$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_5::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim, and all that he did, are\l"
    .string "they not written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_6::
    .string "So Jehoiakim slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers: and Jehoiachin his son\l"
    .string "reigned in his stead$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_7::
    .string "And the king of Egypt came not\n"
    .string "again any more out of his land: for\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon had taken from\l"
    .string "the river of Egypt unto the river\l"
    .string "Euphrates all that pertained to\l"
    .string "the king of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_8::
    .string "Jehoiachin was eighteen years old\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned in Jerusalem three months.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Nehushta,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Elnathan of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_9::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his father had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_10::
    .string "At that time the servants of\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came\l"
    .string "up against Jerusalem, and the city\l"
    .string "was besieged.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_11::
    .string "And Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon\n"
    .string "came against the city, and his\l"
    .string "servants did besiege it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_12::
    .string "And Jehoiachin the king of Judah\n"
    .string "went out to the king of Babylon, he,\l"
    .string "and his mother, and his servants, and\l"
    .string "his princes, and his officers: and\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon took him in the\l"
    .string "eighth year of his reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_13::
    .string "And he carried out thence all the\n"
    .string "treasures of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the treasures of the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and cut in pieces all the\l"
    .string "vessels of gold which Solomon king\l"
    .string "of Israel had made in the temple of\l"
    .string "the LORD, as the LORD had said.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_14::
    .string "And he carried away all Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and all the princes, and all the\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, even ten\l"
    .string "thousand captives, and all the\l"
    .string "craftsmen and smiths: none remained,\l"
    .string "save the poorest sort of the\l"
    .string "people of the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_15::
    .string "And he carried away Jehoiachin to\n"
    .string "Babylon, and the king’s mother, and\l"
    .string "the king’s wives, and his officers,\l"
    .string "and the mighty of the land, those\l"
    .string "carried he into captivity from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_16::
    .string "And all the men of might, even\n"
    .string "seven thousand, and craftsmen and\l"
    .string "smiths a thousand, all that were\l"
    .string "strong and apt for war, even them the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon brought captive to\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_17::
    .string "And the king of Babylon made\n"
    .string "Mattaniah his father’s brother king\l"
    .string "in his stead, and changed his name to\l"
    .string "Zedekiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_18::
    .string "Zedekiah was twenty and one years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Hamutal,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_19::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that Jehoiakim had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_24_20::
    .string "For through the anger of the LORD it\n"
    .string "came to pass in Jerusalem and Judah,\l"
    .string "until he had cast them out from his\l"
    .string "presence, that Zedekiah rebelled\l"
    .string "against the king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the ninth\n"
    .string "year of his reign, in the tenth\l"
    .string "month, in the tenth day of the month,\l"
    .string "that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon\l"
    .string "came, he, and all his host, against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and pitched against it;\l"
    .string "and they built forts against it\l"
    .string "round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_2::
    .string "And the city was besieged unto the\n"
    .string "eleventh year of king Zedekiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_3::
    .string "And on the ninth day of the fourth\n"
    .string "month the famine prevailed in the\l"
    .string "city, and there was no bread for the\l"
    .string "people of the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_4::
    .string "And the city was broken up, and\n"
    .string "all the men of war fled by night by\l"
    .string "the way of the gate between two\l"
    .string "walls, which is by the king’s\l"
    .string "garden: (now the Chaldees were\l"
    .string "against the city round about:) and\l"
    .string "the king went the way toward the\l"
    .string "plain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_5::
    .string "And the army of the Chaldees\n"
    .string "pursued after the king, and overtook\l"
    .string "him in the plains of Jericho: and\l"
    .string "all his army were scattered from\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_6::
    .string "So they took the king, and brought\n"
    .string "him up to the king of Babylon to\l"
    .string "Riblah; and they gave judgment upon\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_7::
    .string "And they slew the sons of Zedekiah\n"
    .string "before his eyes, and put out the eyes\l"
    .string "of Zedekiah, and bound him with\l"
    .string "fetters of brass, and carried him to\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_8::
    .string "And in the fifth month, on the\n"
    .string "seventh day of the month, which is\l"
    .string "the nineteenth year of king\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, came\l"
    .string "Nebuzaradan, captain of the guard, a\l"
    .string "servant of the king of Babylon, unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_9::
    .string "And he burnt the house of the LORD,\n"
    .string "and the king’s house, and all the\l"
    .string "houses of Jerusalem, and every great\l"
    .string "man’s house burnt he with fire$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_10::
    .string "And all the army of the Chaldees,\n"
    .string "that were with the captain of the\l"
    .string "guard, brake down the walls of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_11::
    .string "Now the rest of the people that\n"
    .string "were left in the city, and the\l"
    .string "fugitives that fell away to the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon, with the remnant of\l"
    .string "the multitude, did Nebuzaradan the\l"
    .string "captain of the guard carry away.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_12::
    .string "But the captain of the guard left\n"
    .string "of the poor of the land to be\l"
    .string "vinedressers and husbandmen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_13::
    .string "And the pillars of brass that were\n"
    .string "in the house of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "bases, and the brasen sea that was in\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, did the\l"
    .string "Chaldees break in pieces, and\l"
    .string "carried the brass of them to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_14::
    .string "And the pots, and the shovels, and\n"
    .string "the snuffers, and the spoons, and\l"
    .string "all the vessels of brass wherewith\l"
    .string "they ministered, took they away.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_15::
    .string "And the firepans, and the bowls,\n"
    .string "and such things as were of gold, in\l"
    .string "gold, and of silver, in silver, the\l"
    .string "captain of the guard took away.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_16::
    .string "The two pillars, one sea, and the\n"
    .string "bases which Solomon had made for the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD; the brass of all\l"
    .string "these vessels was without weight.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_17::
    .string "The height of the one pillar was\n"
    .string "eighteen cubits, and the chapiter\l"
    .string "upon it was brass: and the height of\l"
    .string "the chapiter three cubits; and the\l"
    .string "wreathen work, and pomegranates\l"
    .string "upon the chapiter round about, all\l"
    .string "of brass: and like unto these had the\l"
    .string "second pillar with wreathen work.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_18::
    .string "And the captain of the guard took\n"
    .string "Seraiah the chief priest, and\l"
    .string "Zephaniah the second priest, and\l"
    .string "the three keepers of the door:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_19::
    .string "And out of the city he took an\n"
    .string "officer that was set over the men of\l"
    .string "war, and five men of them that were in\l"
    .string "the king’s presence, which were\l"
    .string "found in the city, and the\l"
    .string "principal scribe of the host, which\l"
    .string "mustered the people of the land,\l"
    .string "and threescore men of the people of\l"
    .string "the land that were found in the city:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_20::
    .string "And Nebuzaradan captain of the\n"
    .string "guard took these, and brought them to\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon to Riblah:"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_21::
    .string "And the king of Babylon smote them,\n"
    .string "and slew them at Riblah in the land\l"
    .string "of Hamath. So Judah was carried away\l"
    .string "out of their land$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_22::
    .string "And as for the people that\n"
    .string "remained in the land of Judah, whom\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had\l"
    .string "left, even over them he made\l"
    .string "Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son\l"
    .string "of Shaphan, ruler.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_23::
    .string "And when all the captains of the\n"
    .string "armies, they and their men, heard\l"
    .string "that the king of Babylon had made\l"
    .string "Gedaliah governor, there came to\l"
    .string "Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael\l"
    .string "the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan the\l"
    .string "son of Careah, and Seraiah the son of\l"
    .string "Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and\l"
    .string "Jaazaniah the son of a Maachathite,\l"
    .string "they and their men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_24::
    .string "And Gedaliah sware to them, and to\n"
    .string "their men, and said unto them, Fear\l"
    .string "not to be the servants of the\l"
    .string "Chaldees: dwell in the land, and\l"
    .string "serve the king of Babylon; and it\l"
    .string "shall be well with you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_25::
    .string "But it came to pass in the seventh\n"
    .string "month, that Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of\l"
    .string "the seed royal, came, and ten men\l"
    .string "with him, and smote Gedaliah, that\l"
    .string "he died, and the Jews and the\l"
    .string "Chaldees that were with him at\l"
    .string "Mizpah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_26::
    .string "And all the people, both small\n"
    .string "and great, and the captains of the\l"
    .string "armies, arose, and came to Egypt: for\l"
    .string "they were afraid of the Chaldees.$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_27::
    .string "And it came to pass in the seven and\n"
    .string "thirtieth year of the captivity of\l"
    .string "Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the\l"
    .string "twelfth month, on the seven and\l"
    .string "twentieth day of the month, that\l"
    .string "Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the\l"
    .string "year that he began to reign did lift\l"
    .string "up the head of Jehoiachin king of\l"
    .string "Judah out of prison;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_28::
    .string "And he spake kindly to him, and set\n"
    .string "his throne above the throne of the\l"
    .string "kings that were with him in Babylon;"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_29::
    .string "And changed his prison garments:\n"
    .string "and he did eat bread continually\l"
    .string "before him all the days of his life$"
Bible_Text_2_Kings_25_30::
    .string "And his allowance was a continual\n"
    .string "allowance given him of the king, a\l"
    .string "daily rate for every day, all the\l"
    .string "days of his life.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_1::
    .string "Adam, Sheth, Enosh,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_2::
    .string "Kenan, Mahalaleel, Jered,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_3::
    .string "Henoch, Methuselah, Lamech,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_4::
    .string "Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_5::
    .string "The sons of Japheth; Gomer, and\n"
    .string "Magog, and Madai, and Javan, and\l"
    .string "Tubal, and Meshech, and Tiras.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_6::
    .string "And the sons of Gomer; Ashchenaz,\n"
    .string "and Riphath, and Togarmah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_7::
    .string "And the sons of Javan; Elishah, and\n"
    .string "Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_8::
    .string "The sons of Ham; Cush, and Mizraim,\n"
    .string "Put, and Canaan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_9::
    .string "And the sons of Cush; Seba, and\n"
    .string "Havilah, and Sabta, and Raamah, and\l"
    .string "Sabtecha. And the sons of Raamah;\l"
    .string "Sheba, and Dedan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_10::
    .string "And Cush begat Nimrod: he began to\n"
    .string "be mighty upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_11::
    .string "And Mizraim begat Ludim, and Anamim,\n"
    .string "and Lehabim, and Naphtuhim,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_12::
    .string "And Pathrusim, and Casluhim, (of\n"
    .string "whom came the Philistines,) and\l"
    .string "Caphthorim$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_13::
    .string "And Canaan begat Zidon his\n"
    .string "firstborn, and Heth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_14::
    .string "The Jebusite also, and the Amorite,\n"
    .string "and the Girgashite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_15::
    .string "And the Hivite, and the Arkite, and\n"
    .string "the Sinite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_16::
    .string "And the Arvadite, and the Zemarite,\n"
    .string "and the Hamathite$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_17::
    .string "The sons of Shem; Elam, and Asshur,\n"
    .string "and Arphaxad, and Lud, and Aram, and\l"
    .string "Uz, and Hul, and Gether, and Meshech.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_18::
    .string "And Arphaxad begat Shelah, and\n"
    .string "Shelah begat Eber.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_19::
    .string "And unto Eber were born two sons:\n"
    .string "the name of the one was Peleg;\l"
    .string "because in his days the earth was\l"
    .string "divided: and his brother’s name was\l"
    .string "Joktan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_20::
    .string "And Joktan begat Almodad, and\n"
    .string "Sheleph, and Hazarmaveth, and\l"
    .string "Jerah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_21::
    .string "Hadoram also, and Uzal, and\n"
    .string "Diklah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_22::
    .string "And Ebal, and Abimael, and Sheba,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_23::
    .string "And Ophir, and Havilah, and Jobab.\n"
    .string "All these were the sons of Joktan$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_24::
    .string "Shem, Arphaxad, Shelah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_25::
    .string "Eber, Peleg, Reu,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_26::
    .string "Serug, Nahor, Terah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_27::
    .string "Abram; the same is Abraham$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_28::
    .string "The sons of Abraham; Isaac, and\n"
    .string "Ishmael.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_29::
    .string "These are their generations: The\n"
    .string "firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth; then\l"
    .string "Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_30::
    .string "Mishma, and Dumah, Massa, Hadad, and\n"
    .string "Tema,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_31::
    .string "Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These\n"
    .string "are the sons of Ishmael$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_32::
    .string "Now the sons of Keturah, Abraham’s\n"
    .string "concubine: she bare Zimran, and\l"
    .string "Jokshan, and Medan, and Midian, and\l"
    .string "Ishbak, and Shuah. And the sons of\l"
    .string "Jokshan; Sheba, and Dedan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_33::
    .string "And the sons of Midian; Ephah, and\n"
    .string "Epher, and Henoch, and Abida, and\l"
    .string "Eldaah. All these are the sons of\l"
    .string "Keturah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_34::
    .string "And Abraham begat Isaac. The sons of\n"
    .string "Isaac; Esau and Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_35::
    .string "The sons of Esau; Eliphaz, Reuel,\n"
    .string "and Jeush, and Jaalam, and Korah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_36::
    .string "The sons of Eliphaz; Teman, and\n"
    .string "Omar, Zephi, and Gatam, Kenaz, and\l"
    .string "Timna, and Amalek.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_37::
    .string "The sons of Reuel; Nahath, Zerah,\n"
    .string "Shammah, and Mizzah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_38::
    .string "And the sons of Seir; Lotan, and\n"
    .string "Shobal, and Zibeon, and Anah, and\l"
    .string "Dishon, and Ezar, and Dishan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_39::
    .string "And the sons of Lotan; Hori, and\n"
    .string "Homam: and Timna was Lotan’s sister.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_40::
    .string "The sons of Shobal; Alian, and\n"
    .string "Manahath, and Ebal, Shephi, and Onam\l"
    .string " and the sons of Zibeon; Aiah, and\l"
    .string "Anah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_41::
    .string "The sons of Anah; Dishon. And the\n"
    .string "sons of Dishon; Amram, and Eshban,\l"
    .string "and Ithran, and Cheran.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_42::
    .string "The sons of Ezer; Bilhan, and Zavan,\n"
    .string "and Jakan. The sons of Dishan; Uz, and\l"
    .string "Aran.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_43::
    .string "Now these are the kings that reigned\n"
    .string "in the land of Edom before any king\l"
    .string "reigned over the children of\l"
    .string "Israel; Bela the son of Beor: and\l"
    .string "the name of his city was Dinhabah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_44::
    .string "And when Bela was dead, Jobab the\n"
    .string "son of Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_45::
    .string "And when Jobab was dead, Husham of\n"
    .string "the land of the Temanites reigned in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_46::
    .string "And when Husham was dead, Hadad the\n"
    .string "son of Bedad, which smote Midian in\l"
    .string "the field of Moab, reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead: and the name of his city was\l"
    .string "Avith.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_47::
    .string "And when Hadad was dead, Samlah of\n"
    .string "Masrekah reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_48::
    .string "And when Samlah was dead, Shaul of\n"
    .string "Rehoboth by the river reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_49::
    .string "And when Shaul was dead, Baalhanan\n"
    .string "the son of Achbor reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_50::
    .string "And when Baalhanan was dead, Hadad\n"
    .string "reigned in his stead: and the name of\l"
    .string "his city was Pai; and his wife’s name\l"
    .string "was Mehetabel, the daughter of\l"
    .string "Matred, the daughter of Mezahab.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_51::
    .string "Hadad died also. And the dukes of\n"
    .string "Edom were; duke Timnah, duke Aliah,\l"
    .string "duke Jetheth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_52::
    .string "Duke Aholibamah, duke Elah, duke\n"
    .string "Pinon,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_53::
    .string "Duke Kenaz, duke Teman, duke Mibzar,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_1_54::
    .string "Duke Magdiel, duke Iram. These are\n"
    .string "the dukes of Edom$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_1::
    .string "These are the sons of Israel;\n"
    .string "Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah,\l"
    .string "Issachar, and Zebulun,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_2::
    .string "Dan, Joseph, and Benjamin,\n"
    .string "Naphtali, Gad, and Asher$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_3::
    .string "The sons of Judah; Er, and Onan, and\n"
    .string "Shelah: which three were born unto\l"
    .string "him of the daughter of Shua the\l"
    .string "Canaanitess. And Er, the firstborn of\l"
    .string "Judah, was evil in the sight of the\l"
    .string "LORD; and he slew him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_4::
    .string "And Tamar his daughter in law bore\n"
    .string "him Pharez and Zerah. All the sons\l"
    .string "of Judah were five.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_5::
    .string "The sons of Pharez; Hezron, and\n"
    .string "Hamul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_6::
    .string "And the sons of Zerah; Zimri, and\n"
    .string "Ethan, and Heman, and Calcol, and\l"
    .string "Dara: five of them in all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_7::
    .string "And the sons of Carmi; Achar, the\n"
    .string "troubler of Israel, who\l"
    .string "transgressed in the thing accursed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_8::
    .string "And the sons of Ethan; Azariah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_9::
    .string "The sons also of Hezron, that were\n"
    .string "born unto him; Jerahmeel, and Ram,\l"
    .string "and Chelubai.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_10::
    .string "And Ram begat Amminadab; and\n"
    .string "Amminadab begat Nahshon, prince of\l"
    .string "the children of Judah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_11::
    .string "And Nahshon begat Salma, and Salma\n"
    .string "begat Boaz,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_12::
    .string "And Boaz begat Obed, and Obed begat\n"
    .string "Jesse,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_13::
    .string "And Jesse begat his firstborn\n"
    .string "Eliab, and Abinadab the second, and\l"
    .string "Shimma the third,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_14::
    .string "Nethaneel the fourth, Raddai the\n"
    .string "fifth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_15::
    .string "Ozem the sixth, David the seventh:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_16::
    .string "Whose sisters were Zeruiah, and\n"
    .string "Abigail. And the sons of Zeruiah;\l"
    .string "Abishai, and Joab, and Asahel, three$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_17::
    .string "And Abigail bare Amasa: and the\n"
    .string "father of Amasa was Jether the\l"
    .string "Ishmeelite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_18::
    .string "And Caleb the son of Hezron begat\n"
    .string "children of Azubah his wife, and of\l"
    .string "Jerioth: her sons are these; Jesher,\l"
    .string "and Shobab, and Ardon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_19::
    .string "And when Azubah was dead, Caleb\n"
    .string "took unto him Ephrath, which bare\l"
    .string "him Hur.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_20::
    .string "And Hur begat Uri, and Uri begat\n"
    .string "Bezaleel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_21::
    .string "And afterward Hezron went in to the\n"
    .string "daughter of Machir the father of\l"
    .string "Gilead, whom he married when he was\l"
    .string "threescore years old; and she bare\l"
    .string "him Segub.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_22::
    .string "And Segub begat Jair, who had three\n"
    .string "and twenty cities in the land of\l"
    .string "Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_23::
    .string "And he took Geshur, and Aram, with\n"
    .string "the towns of Jair, from them, with\l"
    .string "Kenath, and the towns thereof, even\l"
    .string "threescore cities. All these\l"
    .string "belonged to the sons of Machir the\l"
    .string "father of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_24::
    .string "And after that Hezron was dead in\n"
    .string "Calebephratah, then Abiah Hezron’s\l"
    .string "wife bare him Ashur the father of\l"
    .string "Tekoa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_25::
    .string "And the sons of Jerahmeel the\n"
    .string "firstborn of Hezron were, Ram the\l"
    .string "firstborn, and Bunah, and Oren, and\l"
    .string "Ozem, and Ahijah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_26::
    .string "Jerahmeel had also another wife,\n"
    .string "whose name was Atarah; she was the\l"
    .string "mother of Onam.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_27::
    .string "And the sons of Ram the firstborn of\n"
    .string "Jerahmeel were, Maaz, and Jamin, and\l"
    .string "Eker.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_28::
    .string "And the sons of Onam were, Shammai,\n"
    .string "and Jada. And the sons of Shammai;\l"
    .string "Nadab and Abishur.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_29::
    .string "And the name of the wife of Abishur\n"
    .string "was Abihail, and she bare him Ahban,\l"
    .string "and Molid.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_30::
    .string "And the sons of Nadab; Seled, and\n"
    .string "Appaim: but Seled died without\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_31::
    .string "And the sons of Appaim; Ishi. And\n"
    .string "the sons of Ishi; Sheshan. And the\l"
    .string "children of Sheshan; Ahlai.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_32::
    .string "And the sons of Jada the brother of\n"
    .string "Shammai; Jether, and Jonathan: and\l"
    .string "Jether died without children.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_33::
    .string "And the sons of Jonathan; Peleth,\n"
    .string "and Zaza. These were the sons of\l"
    .string "Jerahmeel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_34::
    .string "Now Sheshan had no sons, but\n"
    .string "daughters. And Sheshan had a servant,\l"
    .string "an Egyptian, whose name was Jarha.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_35::
    .string "And Sheshan gave his daughter to\n"
    .string "Jarha his servant to wife; and she\l"
    .string "bare him Attai.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_36::
    .string "And Attai begat Nathan, and Nathan\n"
    .string "begat Zabad,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_37::
    .string "And Zabad begat Ephlal, and\n"
    .string "Ephlal begat Obed,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_38::
    .string "And Obed begat Jehu, and Jehu begat\n"
    .string "Azariah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_39::
    .string "And Azariah begat Helez, and Helez\n"
    .string "begat Eleasah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_40::
    .string "And Eleasah begat Sisamai, and\n"
    .string "Sisamai begat Shallum,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_41::
    .string "And Shallum begat Jekamiah, and\n"
    .string "Jekamiah begat Elishama$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_42::
    .string "Now the sons of Caleb the brother\n"
    .string "of Jerahmeel were, Mesha his\l"
    .string "firstborn, which was the father of\l"
    .string "Ziph; and the sons of Mareshah the\l"
    .string "father of Hebron.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_43::
    .string "And the sons of Hebron; Korah, and\n"
    .string "Tappuah, and Rekem, and Shema.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_44::
    .string "And Shema begat Raham, the father of\n"
    .string "Jorkoam: and Rekem begat Shammai.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_45::
    .string "And the son of Shammai was Maon: and\n"
    .string "Maon was the father of Bethzur.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_46::
    .string "And Ephah, Caleb’s concubine, bare\n"
    .string "Haran, and Moza, and Gazez: and Haran\l"
    .string "begat Gazez.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_47::
    .string "And the sons of Jahdai; Regem, and\n"
    .string "Jotham, and Gesham, and Pelet, and\l"
    .string "Ephah, and Shaaph.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_48::
    .string "Maachah, Caleb’s concubine, bare\n"
    .string "Sheber, and Tirhanah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_49::
    .string "She bare also Shaaph the father of\n"
    .string "Madmannah, Sheva the father of\l"
    .string "Machbenah, and the father of Gibea:\l"
    .string "and the daughter of Caleb was Achsa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_50::
    .string "These were the sons of Caleb the\n"
    .string "son of Hur, the firstborn of\l"
    .string "Ephratah; Shobal the father of\l"
    .string "Kirjathjearim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_51::
    .string "Salma the father of Bethlehem,\n"
    .string "Hareph the father of Bethgader.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_52::
    .string "And Shobal the father of\n"
    .string "Kirjathjearim had sons; Haroeh, and\l"
    .string "half of the Manahethites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_53::
    .string "And the families of Kirjathjearim;\n"
    .string "the Ithrites, and the Puhites, and\l"
    .string "the Shumathites, and the Mishraites;\l"
    .string "of them came the Zareathites, and the\l"
    .string "Eshtaulites,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_54::
    .string "The sons of Salma; Bethlehem, and\n"
    .string "the Netophathites, Ataroth, the\l"
    .string "house of Joab, and half of the\l"
    .string "Manahethites, the Zorites$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_2_55::
    .string "And the families of the scribes\n"
    .string "which dwelt at Jabez; the\l"
    .string "Tirathites, the Shimeathites, and\l"
    .string "Suchathites. These are the Kenites\l"
    .string "that came of Hemath, the father of\l"
    .string "the house of Rechab.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_1::
    .string "Now these were the sons of David,\n"
    .string "which were born unto him in Hebron;\l"
    .string "the firstborn Amnon, of Ahinoam the\l"
    .string "Jezreelitess; the second Daniel, of\l"
    .string "Abigail the Carmelitess:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_2::
    .string "The third, Absalom the son of\n"
    .string "Maachah the daughter of Talmai king\l"
    .string "of Geshur: the fourth, Adonijah the\l"
    .string "son of Haggith:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_3::
    .string "The fifth, Shephatiah of Abital:\n"
    .string "the sixth, Ithream by Eglah his wife$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_4::
    .string "These six were born unto him in\n"
    .string "Hebron; and there he reigned seven\l"
    .string "years and six months: and in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem he reigned thirty and\l"
    .string "three years.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_5::
    .string "And these were born unto him in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem; Shimea, and Shobab, and\l"
    .string "Nathan, and Solomon, four, of\l"
    .string "Bathshua the daughter of Ammiel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_6::
    .string "Ibhar also, and Elishama, and\n"
    .string "Eliphelet,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_7::
    .string "And Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_8::
    .string "And Elishama, and Eliada, and\n"
    .string "Eliphelet, nine$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_9::
    .string "These were all the sons of David,\n"
    .string "beside the sons of the concubines,\l"
    .string "and Tamar their sister.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_10::
    .string "And Solomon’s son was Rehoboam,\n"
    .string "Abia his son, Asa his son,\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_11::
    .string "Joram his son, Ahaziah his son,\n"
    .string "Joash his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_12::
    .string "Amaziah his son, Azariah his son,\n"
    .string "Jotham his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_13::
    .string "Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son,\n"
    .string "Manasseh his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_14::
    .string "Amon his son, Josiah his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_15::
    .string "And the sons of Josiah were, the\n"
    .string "firstborn Johanan, the second\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim, the third Zedekiah, the\l"
    .string "fourth Shallum.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_16::
    .string "And the sons of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah\n"
    .string "his son, Zedekiah his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_17::
    .string "And the sons of Jeconiah; Assir,\n"
    .string "Salathiel his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_18::
    .string "Malchiram also, and Pedaiah, and\n"
    .string "Shenazar, Jecamiah, Hoshama, and\l"
    .string "Nedabiah$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_19::
    .string "And the sons of Pedaiah were,\n"
    .string "Zerubbabel, and Shimei: and the sons\l"
    .string "of Zerubbabel; Meshullam, and\l"
    .string "Hananiah, and Shelomith their\l"
    .string "sister:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_20::
    .string "And Hashubah, and Ohel, and\n"
    .string "Berechiah, and Hasadiah,\l"
    .string "Jushabhesed, five$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_21::
    .string "And the sons of Hananiah; Pelatiah,\n"
    .string "and Jesaiah: the sons of Rephaiah,\l"
    .string "the sons of Arnan, the sons of\l"
    .string "Obadiah, the sons of Shechaniah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_22::
    .string "And the sons of Shechaniah;\n"
    .string "Shemaiah: and the sons of Shemaiah;\l"
    .string "Hattush, and Igeal, and Bariah, and\l"
    .string "Neariah, and Shaphat, six.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_23::
    .string "And the sons of Neariah; Elioenai,\n"
    .string "and Hezekiah, and Azrikam, three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_3_24::
    .string "And the sons of Elioenai were,\n"
    .string "Hodaiah, and Eliashib, and Pelaiah,\l"
    .string "and Akkub, and Johanan, and Dalaiah,\l"
    .string "and Anani, seven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_1::
    .string "The sons of Judah; Pharez, Hezron,\n"
    .string "and Carmi, and Hur, and Shobal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_2::
    .string "And Reaiah the son of Shobal begat\n"
    .string "Jahath; and Jahath begat Ahumai, and\l"
    .string "Lahad. These are the families of the\l"
    .string "Zorathites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_3::
    .string "And these were of the father of\n"
    .string "Etam; Jezreel, and Ishma, and\l"
    .string "Idbash: and the name of their sister\l"
    .string "was Hazelelponi:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_4::
    .string "And Penuel the father of Gedor, and\n"
    .string "Ezer the father of Hushah. These are\l"
    .string "the sons of Hur, the firstborn of\l"
    .string "Ephratah, the father of Bethlehem$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_5::
    .string "And Ashur the father of Tekoa had\n"
    .string "two wives, Helah and Naarah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_6::
    .string "And Naarah bare him Ahuzam, and\n"
    .string "Hepher, and Temeni, and Haahashtari.\l"
    .string "These were the sons of Naarah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_7::
    .string "And the sons of Helah were, Zereth,\n"
    .string "and Jezoar, and Ethnan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_8::
    .string "And Coz begat Anub, and Zobebah, and\n"
    .string "the families of Aharhel the son of\l"
    .string "Harum.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_9::
    .string "And Jabez was more honourable than\n"
    .string "his brethren: and his mother called\l"
    .string "his name Jabez, saying, Because I\l"
    .string "bare him with sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_10::
    .string "And Jabez called on the God of\n"
    .string "Israel, saying, Oh that thou\l"
    .string "wouldest bless me indeed, and\l"
    .string "enlarge my coast, and that thine\l"
    .string "hand might be with me, and that thou\l"
    .string "wouldest keep me from evil, that it\l"
    .string "may not grieve me! And God granted\l"
    .string "him that which he requested.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_11::
    .string "And Chelub the brother of Shuah\n"
    .string "begat Mehir, which was the father of\l"
    .string "Eshton.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_12::
    .string "And Eshton begat Bethrapha, and\n"
    .string "Paseah, and Tehinnah the father of\l"
    .string "Irnahash. These are the men of Rechah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_13::
    .string "And the sons of Kenaz; Othniel, and\n"
    .string "Seraiah: and the sons of Othniel;\l"
    .string "Hathath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_14::
    .string "And Meonothai begat Ophrah: and\n"
    .string "Seraiah begat Joab, the father of the\l"
    .string "valley of Charashim; for they were\l"
    .string "craftsmen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_15::
    .string "And the sons of Caleb the son of\n"
    .string "Jephunneh; Iru, Elah, and Naam: and\l"
    .string "the sons of Elah, even Kenaz.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_16::
    .string "And the sons of Jehaleleel; Ziph,\n"
    .string "and Ziphah, Tiria, and Asareel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_17::
    .string "And the sons of Ezra were, Jether,\n"
    .string "and Mered, and Epher, and Jalon: and\l"
    .string "she bare Miriam, and Shammai, and\l"
    .string "Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_18::
    .string "And his wife Jehudijah bare Jered\n"
    .string "the father of Gedor, and Heber the\l"
    .string "father of Socho, and Jekuthiel the\l"
    .string "father of Zanoah. And these are the\l"
    .string "sons of Bithiah the daughter of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, which Mered took.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_19::
    .string "And the sons of his wife Hodiah the\n"
    .string "sister of Naham, the father of\l"
    .string "Keilah the Garmite, and Eshtemoa the\l"
    .string "Maachathite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_20::
    .string "And the sons of Shimon were, Amnon,\n"
    .string "and Rinnah, Benhanan, and Tilon. And\l"
    .string "the sons of Ishi were, Zoheth, and\l"
    .string "Benzoheth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_21::
    .string "The sons of Shelah the son of Judah\n"
    .string "were, Er the father of Lecah, and\l"
    .string "Laadah the father of Mareshah, and\l"
    .string "the families of the house of them\l"
    .string "that wrought fine linen, of the\l"
    .string "house of Ashbea,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_22::
    .string "And Jokim, and the men of Chozeba,\n"
    .string "and Joash, and Saraph, who had the\l"
    .string "dominion in Moab, and Jashubilehem.\l"
    .string "And these are ancient things$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_23::
    .string "These were the potters, and those\n"
    .string "that dwelt among plants and hedges:\l"
    .string "there they dwelt with the king for\l"
    .string "his work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_24::
    .string "The sons of Simeon were, Nemuel,\n"
    .string "and Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_25::
    .string "Shallum his son, Mibsam his son,\n"
    .string "Mishma his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_26::
    .string "And the sons of Mishma; Hamuel his\n"
    .string "son, Zacchur his son, Shimei his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_27::
    .string "And Shimei had sixteen sons and six\n"
    .string "daughters: but his brethren had not\l"
    .string "many children, neither did all\l"
    .string "their family multiply, like to\l"
    .string "the children of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_28::
    .string "And they dwelt at Beersheba, and\n"
    .string "Moladah, and Hazarshual,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_29::
    .string "And at Bilhah, and at Ezem, and at\n"
    .string "Tolad,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_30::
    .string "And at Bethuel, and at Hormah, and\n"
    .string "at Ziklag,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_31::
    .string "And at Bethmarcaboth, and\n"
    .string "Hazarsusim, and at Bethbirei, and at\l"
    .string "Shaaraim. These were their cities\l"
    .string "unto the reign of David$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_32::
    .string "And their villages were, Etam, and\n"
    .string "Ain, Rimmon, and Tochen, and Ashan,\l"
    .string "five cities:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_33::
    .string "And all their villages that were\n"
    .string "round about the same cities, unto\l"
    .string "Baal. These were their habitations,\l"
    .string "and their genealogy$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_34::
    .string "And Meshobab, and Jamlech, and\n"
    .string "Joshah, the son of Amaziah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_35::
    .string "And Joel, and Jehu the son of\n"
    .string "Josibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son\l"
    .string "of Asiel,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_36::
    .string "And Elioenai, and Jaakobah, and\n"
    .string "Jeshohaiah, and Asaiah, and Adiel,\l"
    .string "and Jesimiel, and Benaiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_37::
    .string "And Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son\n"
    .string "of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the\l"
    .string "son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_38::
    .string "These mentioned by their names were\n"
    .string "princes in their families: and the\l"
    .string "house of their fathers increased\l"
    .string "greatly$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_39::
    .string "And they went to the entrance of\n"
    .string "Gedor, even unto the east side of the\l"
    .string "valley, to seek pasture for their\l"
    .string "flocks.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_40::
    .string "And they found fat pasture and\n"
    .string "good, and the land was wide, and\l"
    .string "quiet, and peaceable; for they of\l"
    .string "Ham had dwelt there of old.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_41::
    .string "And these written by name came in\n"
    .string "the days of Hezekiah king of Judah,\l"
    .string "and smote their tents, and the\l"
    .string "habitations that were found there,\l"
    .string "and destroyed them utterly unto this\l"
    .string "day, and dwelt in their rooms:\l"
    .string "because there was pasture there for\l"
    .string "their flocks.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_42::
    .string "And some of them, even of the sons of\n"
    .string "Simeon, five hundred men, went to\l"
    .string "mount Seir, having for their\l"
    .string "captains Pelatiah, and Neariah, and\l"
    .string "Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of\l"
    .string "Ishi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_4_43::
    .string "And they smote the rest of the\n"
    .string "Amalekites that were escaped, and\l"
    .string "dwelt there unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_1::
    .string "Now the sons of Reuben the firstborn\n"
    .string "of Israel, (for he was the\l"
    .string "firstborn; but forasmuch as he\l"
    .string "defiled his father’s bed, his\l"
    .string "birthright was given unto the sons of\l"
    .string "Joseph the son of Israel: and the\l"
    .string "genealogy is not to be reckoned\l"
    .string "after the birthright.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_2::
    .string "For Judah prevailed above his\n"
    .string "brethren, and of him came the chief\l"
    .string "ruler; but the birthright was\l"
    .string "Joseph’s:)"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_3::
    .string "The sons, I say, of Reuben the\n"
    .string "firstborn of Israel were, Hanoch,\l"
    .string "and Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_4::
    .string "The sons of Joel; Shemaiah his son,\n"
    .string "Gog his son, Shimei his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_5::
    .string "Micah his son, Reaia his son, Baal\n"
    .string "his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_6::
    .string "Beerah his son, whom\n"
    .string "Tilgathpilneser king of Assyria\l"
    .string "carried away captive: he was prince\l"
    .string "of the Reubenites$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_7::
    .string "And his brethren by their families,\n"
    .string "when the genealogy of their\l"
    .string "generations was reckoned, were the\l"
    .string "chief, Jeiel, and Zechariah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_8::
    .string "And Bela the son of Azaz, the son of\n"
    .string "Shema, the son of Joel, who dwelt in\l"
    .string "Aroer, even unto Nebo and Baalmeon:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_9::
    .string "And eastward he inhabited unto the\n"
    .string "entering in of the wilderness from\l"
    .string "the river Euphrates: because their\l"
    .string "cattle were multiplied in the\l"
    .string "land of Gilead$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_10::
    .string "And in the days of Saul they made\n"
    .string "war with the Hagarites, who fell by\l"
    .string "their hand: and they dwelt in their\l"
    .string "tents throughout all the east land\l"
    .string "of Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_11::
    .string "And the children of Gad dwelt over\n"
    .string "against them, in the land of Bashan\l"
    .string "unto Salcah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_12::
    .string "Joel the chief, and Shapham the\n"
    .string "next, and Jaanai, and Shaphat in\l"
    .string "Bashan$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_13::
    .string "And their brethren of the house of\n"
    .string "their fathers were, Michael, and\l"
    .string "Meshullam, and Sheba, and Jorai, and\l"
    .string "Jachan, and Zia, and Heber, seven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_14::
    .string "These are the children of Abihail\n"
    .string "the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah,\l"
    .string "the son of Gilead, the son of\l"
    .string "Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the\l"
    .string "son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_15::
    .string "Ahi the son of Abdiel, the son of\n"
    .string "Guni, chief of the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_16::
    .string "And they dwelt in Gilead in Bashan,\n"
    .string "and in her towns, and in all the\l"
    .string "suburbs of Sharon, upon their\l"
    .string "borders.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_17::
    .string "All these were reckoned by\n"
    .string "genealogies in the days of Jotham\l"
    .string "king of Judah, and in the days of\l"
    .string "Jeroboam king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_18::
    .string "The sons of Reuben, and the Gadites,\n"
    .string "and half the tribe of Manasseh, of\l"
    .string "valiant men, men able to bear\l"
    .string "buckler and sword, and to shoot with\l"
    .string "bow, and skilful in war, were four\l"
    .string "and forty thousand seven hundred and\l"
    .string "threescore, that went out to the war.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_19::
    .string "And they made war with the\n"
    .string "Hagarites, with Jetur, and Nephish,\l"
    .string "and Nodab.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_20::
    .string "And they were helped against them,\n"
    .string "and the Hagarites were delivered\l"
    .string "into their hand, and all that were\l"
    .string "with them: for they cried to God in\l"
    .string "the battle, and he was intreated of\l"
    .string "them; because they put their trust\l"
    .string "in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_21::
    .string "And they took away their cattle; of\n"
    .string "their camels fifty thousand, and of\l"
    .string "sheep two hundred and fifty\l"
    .string "thousand, and of asses two thousand,\l"
    .string "and of men an hundred thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_22::
    .string "For there fell down many slain,\n"
    .string "because the war was of God. And they\l"
    .string "dwelt in their steads until the\l"
    .string "captivity.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_23::
    .string "And the children of the half tribe\n"
    .string "of Manasseh dwelt in the land: they\l"
    .string "increased from Bashan unto\l"
    .string "Baalhermon and Senir, and unto mount\l"
    .string "Hermon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_24::
    .string "And these were the heads of the\n"
    .string "house of their fathers, even Epher,\l"
    .string "and Ishi, and Eliel, and Azriel,\l"
    .string "and Jeremiah, and Hodaviah, and\l"
    .string "Jahdiel, mighty men of valour,\l"
    .string "famous men, and heads of the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_25::
    .string "And they transgressed against the\n"
    .string "God of their fathers, and went a\l"
    .string "whoring after the gods of the\l"
    .string "people of the land, whom God\l"
    .string "destroyed before them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_5_26::
    .string "And the God of Israel stirred up\n"
    .string "the spirit of Pul king of Assyria,\l"
    .string "and the spirit of Tilgathpilneser\l"
    .string "king of Assyria, and he carried them\l"
    .string "away, even the Reubenites, and the\l"
    .string "Gadites, and the half tribe of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, and brought them unto\l"
    .string "Halah, and Habor, and Hara, and to\l"
    .string "the river Gozan, unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_1::
    .string "The sons of Levi; Gershon, Kohath,\n"
    .string "and Merari.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_2::
    .string "And the sons of Kohath; Amram,\n"
    .string "Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_3::
    .string "And the children of Amram; Aaron,\n"
    .string "and Moses, and Miriam. The sons also\l"
    .string "of Aaron; Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar,\l"
    .string "and Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_4::
    .string "Eleazar begat Phinehas, Phinehas\n"
    .string "begat Abishua,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_5::
    .string "And Abishua begat Bukki, and Bukki\n"
    .string "begat Uzzi,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_6::
    .string "And Uzzi begat Zerahiah, and\n"
    .string "Zerahiah begat Meraioth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_7::
    .string "Meraioth begat Amariah, and Amariah\n"
    .string "begat Ahitub,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_8::
    .string "And Ahitub begat Zadok, and Zadok\n"
    .string "begat Ahimaaz,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_9::
    .string "And Ahimaaz begat Azariah, and\n"
    .string "Azariah begat Johanan,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_10::
    .string "And Johanan begat Azariah, (he it is\n"
    .string "that executed the priest’s office in\l"
    .string "the temple that Solomon built in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:)"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_11::
    .string "And Azariah begat Amariah, and\n"
    .string "Amariah begat Ahitub,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_12::
    .string "And Ahitub begat Zadok, and Zadok\n"
    .string "begat Shallum,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_13::
    .string "And Shallum begat Hilkiah, and\n"
    .string "Hilkiah begat Azariah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_14::
    .string "And Azariah begat Seraiah, and\n"
    .string "Seraiah begat Jehozadak,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_15::
    .string "And Jehozadak went into captivity,\n"
    .string "when the LORD carried away Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem by the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_16::
    .string "The sons of Levi; Gershom, Kohath,\n"
    .string "and Merari.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_17::
    .string "And these be the names of the sons\n"
    .string "of Gershom; Libni, and Shimei.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_18::
    .string "And the sons of Kohath were, Amram,\n"
    .string "and Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_19::
    .string "The sons of Merari; Mahli, and Mushi\n"
    .string " And these are the families of the\l"
    .string "Levites according to their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_20::
    .string "Of Gershom; Libni his son, Jahath\n"
    .string "his son, Zimmah his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_21::
    .string "Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah\n"
    .string "his son, Jeaterai his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_22::
    .string "The sons of Kohath; Amminadab his\n"
    .string "son, Korah his son, Assir his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_23::
    .string "Elkanah his son, and Ebiasaph his\n"
    .string "son, and Assir his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_24::
    .string "Tahath his son, Uriel his son,\n"
    .string "Uzziah his son, and Shaul his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_25::
    .string "And the sons of Elkanah; Amasai,\n"
    .string "and Ahimoth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_26::
    .string "As for Elkanah: the sons of\n"
    .string "Elkanah; Zophai his son, and Nahath\l"
    .string "his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_27::
    .string "Eliab his son, Jeroham his son,\n"
    .string "Elkanah his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_28::
    .string "And the sons of Samuel; the\n"
    .string "firstborn Vashni, and Abiah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_29::
    .string "The sons of Merari; Mahli, Libni\n"
    .string "his son, Shimei his son, Uzza his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_30::
    .string "Shimea his son, Haggiah his son,\n"
    .string "Asaiah his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_31::
    .string "And these are they whom David set\n"
    .string "over the service of song in the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, after that the ark had\l"
    .string "rest.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_32::
    .string "And they ministered before the\n"
    .string "dwelling place of the tabernacle\l"
    .string "of the congregation with singing,\l"
    .string "until Solomon had built the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD in Jerusalem: and then\l"
    .string "they waited on their office\l"
    .string "according to their order.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_33::
    .string "And these are they that waited with\n"
    .string "their children. Of the sons of the\l"
    .string "Kohathites: Heman a singer, the son\l"
    .string "of Joel, the son of Shemuel,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_34::
    .string "The son of Elkanah, the son of\n"
    .string "Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son\l"
    .string "of Toah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_35::
    .string "The son of Zuph, the son of\n"
    .string "Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son\l"
    .string "of Amasai,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_36::
    .string "The son of Elkanah, the son of\n"
    .string "Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of\l"
    .string "Zephaniah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_37::
    .string "The son of Tahath, the son of Assir,\n"
    .string "the son of Ebiasaph, the son of\l"
    .string "Korah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_38::
    .string "The son of Izhar, the son of Kohath,\n"
    .string "the son of Levi, the son of Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_39::
    .string "And his brother Asaph, who stood on\n"
    .string "his right hand, even Asaph the son of\l"
    .string "Berachiah, the son of Shimea,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_40::
    .string "The son of Michael, the son of\n"
    .string "Baaseiah, the son of Malchiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_41::
    .string "The son of Ethni, the son of Zerah,\n"
    .string "the son of Adaiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_42::
    .string "The son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah,\n"
    .string "the son of Shimei,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_43::
    .string "The son of Jahath, the son of\n"
    .string "Gershom, the son of Levi$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_44::
    .string "And their brethren the sons of\n"
    .string "Merari stood on the left hand: Ethan\l"
    .string "the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the\l"
    .string "son of Malluch,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_45::
    .string "The son of Hashabiah, the son of\n"
    .string "Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_46::
    .string "The son of Amzi, the son of Bani, the\n"
    .string "son of Shamer,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_47::
    .string "The son of Mahli, the son of Mushi,\n"
    .string "the son of Merari, the son of Levi$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_48::
    .string "Their brethren also the Levites\n"
    .string "were appointed unto all manner of\l"
    .string "service of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "house of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_49::
    .string "But Aaron and his sons offered upon\n"
    .string "the altar of the burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "on the altar of incense, and were\l"
    .string "appointed for all the work of the\l"
    .string "place most holy, and to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for Israel, according to\l"
    .string "all that Moses the servant of God\l"
    .string "had commanded.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_50::
    .string "And these are the sons of Aaron;\n"
    .string "Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son,\l"
    .string "Abishua his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_51::
    .string "Bukki his son, Uzzi his son,\n"
    .string "Zerahiah his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_52::
    .string "Meraioth his son, Amariah his son,\n"
    .string "Ahitub his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_53::
    .string "Zadok his son, Ahimaaz his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_54::
    .string "Now these are their dwelling\n"
    .string "places throughout their castles in\l"
    .string "their coasts, of the sons of Aaron,\l"
    .string "of the families of the Kohathites:\l"
    .string "for theirs was the lot.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_55::
    .string "And they gave them Hebron in the\n"
    .string "land of Judah, and the suburbs\l"
    .string "thereof round about it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_56::
    .string "But the fields of the city, and the\n"
    .string "villages thereof, they gave to\l"
    .string "Caleb the son of Jephunneh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_57::
    .string "And to the sons of Aaron they gave\n"
    .string "the cities of Judah, namely, Hebron,\l"
    .string "the city of refuge, and Libnah with\l"
    .string "her suburbs, and Jattir, and\l"
    .string "Eshtemoa, with their suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_58::
    .string "And Hilen with her suburbs, Debir\n"
    .string "with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_59::
    .string "And Ashan with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Bethshemesh with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_60::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Benjamin;\n"
    .string "Geba with her suburbs, and Alemeth\l"
    .string "with her suburbs, and Anathoth with\l"
    .string "her suburbs. All their cities\l"
    .string "throughout their families were\l"
    .string "thirteen cities$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_61::
    .string "And unto the sons of Kohath, which\n"
    .string "were left of the family of that\l"
    .string "tribe, were cities given out of the\l"
    .string "half tribe, namely, out of the half\l"
    .string "tribe of Manasseh, by lot, ten\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_62::
    .string "And to the sons of Gershom\n"
    .string "throughout their families out of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Issachar, and out of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Asher, and out of the tribe\l"
    .string "of Naphtali, and out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Manasseh in Bashan, thirteen cities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_63::
    .string "Unto the sons of Merari were given\n"
    .string "by lot, throughout their families,\l"
    .string "out of the tribe of Reuben, and out of\l"
    .string "the tribe of Gad, and out of the tribe\l"
    .string "of Zebulun, twelve cities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_64::
    .string "And the children of Israel gave to\n"
    .string "the Levites these cities with their\l"
    .string "suburbs.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_65::
    .string "And they gave by lot out of the\n"
    .string "tribe of the children of Judah, and\l"
    .string "out of the tribe of the children of\l"
    .string "Simeon, and out of the tribe of the\l"
    .string "children of Benjamin, these cities,\l"
    .string "which are called by their names.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_66::
    .string "And the residue of the families of\n"
    .string "the sons of Kohath had cities of\l"
    .string "their coasts out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_67::
    .string "And they gave unto them, of the\n"
    .string "cities of refuge, Shechem in mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim with her suburbs; they gave\l"
    .string "also Gezer with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_68::
    .string "And Jokmeam with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Bethhoron with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_69::
    .string "And Aijalon with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Gathrimmon with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_70::
    .string "And out of the half tribe of\n"
    .string "Manasseh; Aner with her suburbs, and\l"
    .string "Bileam with her suburbs, for the\l"
    .string "family of the remnant of the sons of\l"
    .string "Kohath$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_71::
    .string "Unto the sons of Gershom were given\n"
    .string "out of the family of the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh, Golan in Bashan with\l"
    .string "her suburbs, and Ashtaroth with her\l"
    .string "suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_72::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Issachar;\n"
    .string "Kedesh with her suburbs, Daberath\l"
    .string "with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_73::
    .string "And Ramoth with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Anem with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_74::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Asher;\n"
    .string "Mashal with her suburbs, and Abdon\l"
    .string "with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_75::
    .string "And Hukok with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Rehob with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_76::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Naphtali;\n"
    .string "Kedesh in Galilee with her suburbs,\l"
    .string "and Hammon with her suburbs, and\l"
    .string "Kirjathaim with her suburbs$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_77::
    .string "Unto the rest of the children of\n"
    .string "Merari were given out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Zebulun, Rimmon with her suburbs,\l"
    .string "Tabor with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_78::
    .string "And on the other side Jordan by\n"
    .string "Jericho, on the east side of Jordan,\l"
    .string "were given them out of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Reuben, Bezer in the wilderness with\l"
    .string "her suburbs, and Jahzah with her\l"
    .string "suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_79::
    .string "Kedemoth also with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Mephaath with her suburbs:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_80::
    .string "And out of the tribe of Gad; Ramoth\n"
    .string "in Gilead with her suburbs, and\l"
    .string "Mahanaim with her suburbs,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_6_81::
    .string "And Heshbon with her suburbs, and\n"
    .string "Jazer with her suburbs$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_1::
    .string "Now the sons of Issachar were,\n"
    .string "Tola, and Puah, Jashub, and Shimrom,\l"
    .string "four.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_2::
    .string "And the sons of Tola; Uzzi, and\n"
    .string "Rephaiah, and Jeriel, and Jahmai,\l"
    .string "and Jibsam, and Shemuel, heads of\l"
    .string "their father’s house, to wit, of\l"
    .string "Tola: they were valiant men of might\l"
    .string "in their generations; whose number\l"
    .string "was in the days of David two and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand and six hundred.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_3::
    .string "And the sons of Uzzi; Izrahiah: and\n"
    .string "the sons of Izrahiah; Michael, and\l"
    .string "Obadiah, and Joel, Ishiah, five:\l"
    .string "all of them chief men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_4::
    .string "And with them, by their generations,\n"
    .string "after the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "were bands of soldiers for war, six\l"
    .string "and thirty thousand men: for they had\l"
    .string "many wives and sons.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_5::
    .string "And their brethren among all the\n"
    .string "families of Issachar were valiant\l"
    .string "men of might, reckoned in all by\l"
    .string "their genealogies fourscore and\l"
    .string "seven thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_6::
    .string "The sons of Benjamin; Bela, and\n"
    .string "Becher, and Jediael, three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_7::
    .string "And the sons of Bela; Ezbon, and\n"
    .string "Uzzi, and Uzziel, and Jerimoth, and\l"
    .string "Iri, five; heads of the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers, mighty men of valour;\l"
    .string "and were reckoned by their\l"
    .string "genealogies twenty and two thousand\l"
    .string "and thirty and four.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_8::
    .string "And the sons of Becher; Zemira, and\n"
    .string "Joash, and Eliezer, and Elioenai,\l"
    .string "and Omri, and Jerimoth, and Abiah,\l"
    .string "and Anathoth, and Alameth. All\l"
    .string "these are the sons of Becher.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_9::
    .string "And the number of them, after their\n"
    .string "genealogy by their generations,\l"
    .string "heads of the house of their fathers,\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, was twenty\l"
    .string "thousand and two hundred.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_10::
    .string "The sons also of Jediael; Bilhan:\n"
    .string "and the sons of Bilhan; Jeush, and\l"
    .string "Benjamin, and Ehud, and Chenaanah,\l"
    .string "and Zethan, and Tharshish, and\l"
    .string "Ahishahar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_11::
    .string "All these the sons of Jediael, by\n"
    .string "the heads of their fathers, mighty\l"
    .string "men of valour, were seventeen\l"
    .string "thousand and two hundred soldiers,\l"
    .string "fit to go out for war and battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_12::
    .string "Shuppim also, and Huppim, the\n"
    .string "children of Ir, and Hushim, the sons\l"
    .string "of Aher.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_13::
    .string "The sons of Naphtali; Jahziel, and\n"
    .string "Guni, and Jezer, and Shallum, the\l"
    .string "sons of Bilhah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_14::
    .string "The sons of Manasseh; Ashriel, whom\n"
    .string "she bare: (but his concubine the\l"
    .string "Aramitess bare Machir the father of\l"
    .string "Gilead:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_15::
    .string "And Machir took to wife the sister\n"
    .string "of Huppim and Shuppim, whose\l"
    .string "sister’s name was Maachah;) and the\l"
    .string "name of the second was Zelophehad:\l"
    .string "and Zelophehad had daughters$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_16::
    .string "And Maachah the wife of Machir bare\n"
    .string "a son, and she called his name\l"
    .string "Peresh; and the name of his brother\l"
    .string "was Sheresh; and his sons were Ulam\l"
    .string "and Rakem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_17::
    .string "And the sons of Ulam; Bedan. These\n"
    .string "were the sons of Gilead, the son of\l"
    .string "Machir, the son of Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_18::
    .string "And his sister Hammoleketh bare\n"
    .string "Ishod, and Abiezer, and Mahalah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_19::
    .string "And the sons of Shemidah were,\n"
    .string "Ahian, and Shechem, and Likhi, and\l"
    .string "Aniam.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_20::
    .string "And the sons of Ephraim;\n"
    .string "Shuthelah, and Bered his son, and\l"
    .string "Tahath his son, and Eladah his son,\l"
    .string "and Tahath his son,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_21::
    .string "And Zabad his son, and Shuthelah\n"
    .string "his son, and Ezer, and Elead, whom\l"
    .string "the men of Gath that were born in\l"
    .string "that land slew, because they came\l"
    .string "down to take away their cattle$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_22::
    .string "And Ephraim their father mourned\n"
    .string "many days, and his brethren came to\l"
    .string "comfort him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_23::
    .string "And when he went in to his wife, she\n"
    .string "conceived, and bare a son, and he\l"
    .string "called his name Beriah, because it\l"
    .string "went evil with his house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_24::
    .string "(And his daughter was Sherah, who\n"
    .string "built Bethhoron the nether, and the\l"
    .string "upper, and Uzzensherah.)"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_25::
    .string "And Rephah was his son, also\n"
    .string "Resheph, and Telah his son, and\l"
    .string "Tahan his son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_26::
    .string "Laadan his son, Ammihud his son,\n"
    .string "Elishama his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_27::
    .string "Non his son, Jehoshuah his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_28::
    .string "And their possessions and\n"
    .string "habitations were, Bethel and the\l"
    .string "towns thereof, and eastward Naaran,\l"
    .string "and westward Gezer, with the towns\l"
    .string "thereof; Shechem also and the towns\l"
    .string "thereof, unto Gaza and the towns\l"
    .string "thereof:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_29::
    .string "And by the borders of the children\n"
    .string "of Manasseh, Bethshean and her towns,\l"
    .string "Taanach and her towns, Megiddo and\l"
    .string "her towns, Dor and her towns. In\l"
    .string "these dwelt the children of Joseph\l"
    .string "the son of Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_30::
    .string "The sons of Asher; Imnah, and Isuah,\n"
    .string "and Ishuai, and Beriah, and Serah\l"
    .string "their sister.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_31::
    .string "And the sons of Beriah; Heber, and\n"
    .string "Malchiel, who is the father of\l"
    .string "Birzavith.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_32::
    .string "And Heber begat Japhlet, and\n"
    .string "Shomer, and Hotham, and Shua their\l"
    .string "sister.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_33::
    .string "And the sons of Japhlet; Pasach,\n"
    .string "and Bimhal, and Ashvath. These are\l"
    .string "the children of Japhlet.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_34::
    .string "And the sons of Shamer; Ahi, and\n"
    .string "Rohgah, Jehubbah, and Aram.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_35::
    .string "And the sons of his brother Helem;\n"
    .string "Zophah, and Imna, and Shelesh, and\l"
    .string "Amal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_36::
    .string "The sons of Zophah; Suah, and\n"
    .string "Harnepher, and Shual, and Beri, and\l"
    .string "Imrah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_37::
    .string "Bezer, and Hod, and Shamma, and\n"
    .string "Shilshah, and Ithran, and Beera$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_38::
    .string "And the sons of Jether; Jephunneh,\n"
    .string "and Pispah, and Ara.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_39::
    .string "And the sons of Ulla; Arah, and\n"
    .string "Haniel, and Rezia.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_7_40::
    .string "All these were the children of\n"
    .string "Asher, heads of their father’s house,\l"
    .string "choice and mighty men of valour,\l"
    .string "chief of the princes. And the number\l"
    .string "throughout the genealogy of them\l"
    .string "that were apt to the war and to\l"
    .string "battle was twenty and six thousand\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_1::
    .string "Now Benjamin begat Bela his\n"
    .string "firstborn, Ashbel the second, and\l"
    .string "Aharah the third,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_2::
    .string "Nohah the fourth, and Rapha the\n"
    .string "fifth$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_3::
    .string "And the sons of Bela were, Addar,\n"
    .string "and Gera, and Abihud,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_4::
    .string "And Abishua, and Naaman, and Ahoah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_5::
    .string "And Gera, and Shephuphan, and Huram$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_6::
    .string "And these are the sons of Ehud:\n"
    .string "these are the heads of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Geba, and they\l"
    .string "removed them to Manahath:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_7::
    .string "And Naaman, and Ahiah, and Gera, he\n"
    .string "removed them, and begat Uzza, and\l"
    .string "Ahihud$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_8::
    .string "And Shaharaim begat children in the\n"
    .string "country of Moab, after he had sent\l"
    .string "them away; Hushim and Baara were his\l"
    .string "wives.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_9::
    .string "And he begat of Hodesh his wife,\n"
    .string "Jobab, and Zibia, and Mesha, and\l"
    .string "Malcham,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_10::
    .string "And Jeuz, and Shachia, and Mirma.\n"
    .string "These were his sons, heads of the\l"
    .string "fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_11::
    .string "And of Hushim he begat Abitub, and\n"
    .string "Elpaal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_12::
    .string "The sons of Elpaal; Eber, and\n"
    .string "Misham, and Shamed, who built Ono,\l"
    .string "and Lod, with the towns thereof:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_13::
    .string "Beriah also, and Shema, who were\n"
    .string "heads of the fathers of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Aijalon, who drove\l"
    .string "away the inhabitants of Gath:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_14::
    .string "And Ahio, Shashak, and Jeremoth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_15::
    .string "And Zebadiah, and Arad, and Ader,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_16::
    .string "And Michael, and Ispah, and Joha,\n"
    .string "the sons of Beriah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_17::
    .string "And Zebadiah, and Meshullam, and\n"
    .string "Hezeki, and Heber,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_18::
    .string "Ishmerai also, and Jezliah, and\n"
    .string "Jobab, the sons of Elpaal;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_19::
    .string "And Jakim, and Zichri, and Zabdi,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_20::
    .string "And Elienai, and Zilthai, and\n"
    .string "Eliel,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_21::
    .string "And Adaiah, and Beraiah, and\n"
    .string "Shimrath, the sons of Shimhi;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_22::
    .string "And Ishpan, and Heber, and Eliel,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_23::
    .string "And Abdon, and Zichri, and Hanan,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_24::
    .string "And Hananiah, and Elam, and\n"
    .string "Antothijah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_25::
    .string "And Iphedeiah, and Penuel, the\n"
    .string "sons of Shashak;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_26::
    .string "And Shamsherai, and Shehariah, and\n"
    .string "Athaliah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_27::
    .string "And Jaresiah, and Eliah, and\n"
    .string "Zichri, the sons of Jeroham$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_28::
    .string "These were heads of the fathers, by\n"
    .string "their generations, chief men. These\l"
    .string "dwelt in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_29::
    .string "And at Gibeon dwelt the father of\n"
    .string "Gibeon; whose wife’s name was\l"
    .string "Maachah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_30::
    .string "And his firstborn son Abdon, and\n"
    .string "Zur, and Kish, and Baal, and Nadab,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_31::
    .string "And Gedor, and Ahio, and Zacher$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_32::
    .string "And Mikloth begat Shimeah. And\n"
    .string "these also dwelt with their\l"
    .string "brethren in Jerusalem, over against\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_33::
    .string "And Ner begat Kish, and Kish begat\n"
    .string "Saul, and Saul begat Jonathan, and\l"
    .string "Malchishua, and Abinadab, and\l"
    .string "Eshbaal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_34::
    .string "And the son of Jonathan was\n"
    .string "Meribbaal; and Meribbaal begat\l"
    .string "Micah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_35::
    .string "And the sons of Micah were, Pithon,\n"
    .string "and Melech, and Tarea, and Ahaz.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_36::
    .string "And Ahaz begat Jehoadah; and\n"
    .string "Jehoadah begat Alemeth, and\l"
    .string "Azmaveth, and Zimri; and Zimri begat\l"
    .string "Moza,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_37::
    .string "And Moza begat Binea: Rapha was his\n"
    .string "son, Eleasah his son, Azel his son:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_38::
    .string "And Azel had six sons, whose names\n"
    .string "are these, Azrikam, Bocheru, and\l"
    .string "Ishmael, and Sheariah, and Obadiah,\l"
    .string "and Hanan. All these were the sons\l"
    .string "of Azel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_39::
    .string "And the sons of Eshek his brother\n"
    .string "were, Ulam his firstborn, Jehush the\l"
    .string "second, and Eliphelet the third.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_8_40::
    .string "And the sons of Ulam were mighty\n"
    .string "men of valour, archers, and had many\l"
    .string "sons, and sons’ sons, an hundred and\l"
    .string "fifty. All these are of the sons of\l"
    .string "Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_1::
    .string "So all Israel were reckoned by\n"
    .string "genealogies; and, behold, they were\l"
    .string "written in the book of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel and Judah, who were carried\l"
    .string "away to Babylon for their\l"
    .string "transgression.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_2::
    .string "Now the first inhabitants that\n"
    .string "dwelt in their possessions in their\l"
    .string "cities were, the Israelites, the\l"
    .string "priests, Levites, and the Nethinims.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_3::
    .string "And in Jerusalem dwelt of the\n"
    .string "children of Judah, and of the\l"
    .string "children of Benjamin, and of the\l"
    .string "children of Ephraim, and Manasseh;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_4::
    .string "Uthai the son of Ammihud, the son of\n"
    .string "Omri, the son of Imri, the son of\l"
    .string "Bani, of the children of Pharez the\l"
    .string "son of Judah$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_5::
    .string "And of the Shilonites; Asaiah the\n"
    .string "firstborn, and his sons.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_6::
    .string "And of the sons of Zerah; Jeuel, and\n"
    .string "their brethren, six hundred and\l"
    .string "ninety.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_7::
    .string "And of the sons of Benjamin; Sallu\n"
    .string "the son of Meshullam, the son of\l"
    .string "Hodaviah, the son of Hasenuah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_8::
    .string "And Ibneiah the son of Jeroham, and\n"
    .string "Elah the son of Uzzi, the son of\l"
    .string "Michri, and Meshullam the son of\l"
    .string "Shephathiah, the son of Reuel, the\l"
    .string "son of Ibnijah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_9::
    .string "And their brethren, according to\n"
    .string "their generations, nine hundred and\l"
    .string "fifty and six. All these men were\l"
    .string "chief of the fathers in the house of\l"
    .string "their fathers$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_10::
    .string "And of the priests; Jedaiah, and\n"
    .string "Jehoiarib, and Jachin,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_11::
    .string "And Azariah the son of Hilkiah, the\n"
    .string "son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok,\l"
    .string "the son of Meraioth, the son of\l"
    .string "Ahitub, the ruler of the house of\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_12::
    .string "And Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the\n"
    .string "son of Pashur, the son of Malchijah,\l"
    .string "and Maasiai the son of Adiel, the son\l"
    .string "of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam,\l"
    .string "the son of Meshillemith, the son of\l"
    .string "Immer;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_13::
    .string "And their brethren, heads of the\n"
    .string "house of their fathers, a thousand\l"
    .string "and seven hundred and threescore;\l"
    .string "very able men for the work of the\l"
    .string "service of the house of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_14::
    .string "And of the Levites; Shemaiah the son\n"
    .string "of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the\l"
    .string "son of Hashabiah, of the sons of\l"
    .string "Merari;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_15::
    .string "And Bakbakkar, Heresh, and Galal,\n"
    .string "and Mattaniah the son of Micah, the\l"
    .string "son of Zichri, the son of Asaph;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_16::
    .string "And Obadiah the son of Shemaiah, the\n"
    .string "son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun,\l"
    .string "and Berechiah the son of Asa, the son\l"
    .string "of Elkanah, that dwelt in the\l"
    .string "villages of the Netophathites$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_17::
    .string "And the porters were, Shallum, and\n"
    .string "Akkub, and Talmon, and Ahiman, and\l"
    .string "their brethren: Shallum was the\l"
    .string "chief;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_18::
    .string "Who hitherto waited in the king’s\n"
    .string "gate eastward: they were porters in\l"
    .string "the companies of the children of\l"
    .string "Levi$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_19::
    .string "And Shallum the son of Kore, the\n"
    .string "son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,\l"
    .string "and his brethren, of the house of his\l"
    .string "father, the Korahites, were over the\l"
    .string "work of the service, keepers of the\l"
    .string "gates of the tabernacle: and their\l"
    .string "fathers, being over the host of the\l"
    .string "LORD, were keepers of the entry.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_20::
    .string "And Phinehas the son of Eleazar was\n"
    .string "the ruler over them in time past,\l"
    .string "and the LORD was with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_21::
    .string "And Zechariah the son of\n"
    .string "Meshelemiah was porter of the door\l"
    .string "of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_22::
    .string "All these which were chosen to be\n"
    .string "porters in the gates were two hundred\l"
    .string "and twelve. These were reckoned by\l"
    .string "their genealogy in their villages,\l"
    .string "whom David and Samuel the seer did\l"
    .string "ordain in their set office.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_23::
    .string "So they and their children had the\n"
    .string "oversight of the gates of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, namely, the house of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle, by wards.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_24::
    .string "In four quarters were the porters,\n"
    .string "toward the east, west, north, and\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_25::
    .string "And their brethren, which were in\n"
    .string "their villages, were to come after\l"
    .string "seven days from time to time with\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_26::
    .string "For these Levites, the four chief\n"
    .string "porters, were in their set office,\l"
    .string "and were over the chambers and\l"
    .string "treasuries of the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_27::
    .string "And they lodged round about the\n"
    .string "house of God, because the charge was\l"
    .string "upon them, and the opening thereof\l"
    .string "every morning pertained to them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_28::
    .string "And certain of them had the charge\n"
    .string "of the ministering vessels, that\l"
    .string "they should bring them in and out by\l"
    .string "tale.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_29::
    .string "Some of them also were appointed\n"
    .string "to oversee the vessels, and all the\l"
    .string "instruments of the sanctuary, and the\l"
    .string "fine flour, and the wine, and the\l"
    .string "oil, and the frankincense, and the\l"
    .string "spices.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_30::
    .string "And some of the sons of the priests\n"
    .string "made the ointment of the spices.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_31::
    .string "And Mattithiah, one of the Levites,\n"
    .string "who was the firstborn of Shallum\l"
    .string "the Korahite, had the set office over\l"
    .string "the things that were made in the\l"
    .string "pans.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_32::
    .string "And other of their brethren, of the\n"
    .string "sons of the Kohathites, were over the\l"
    .string "shewbread, to prepare it every\l"
    .string "sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_33::
    .string "And these are the singers, chief of\n"
    .string "the fathers of the Levites, who\l"
    .string "remaining in the chambers were free:\l"
    .string "for they were employed in that work\l"
    .string "day and night.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_34::
    .string "These chief fathers of the Levites\n"
    .string "were chief throughout their\l"
    .string "generations; these dwelt at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_35::
    .string "And in Gibeon dwelt the father of\n"
    .string "Gibeon, Jehiel, whose wife’s name\l"
    .string "was Maachah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_36::
    .string "And his firstborn son Abdon, then\n"
    .string "Zur, and Kish, and Baal, and Ner, and\l"
    .string "Nadab$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_37::
    .string "And Gedor, and Ahio, and Zechariah,\n"
    .string "and Mikloth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_38::
    .string "And Mikloth begat Shimeam. And they\n"
    .string "also dwelt with their brethren at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, over against their\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_39::
    .string "And Ner begat Kish; and Kish begat\n"
    .string "Saul; and Saul begat Jonathan, and\l"
    .string "Malchishua, and Abinadab, and\l"
    .string "Eshbaal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_40::
    .string "And the son of Jonathan was\n"
    .string "Meribbaal: and Meribbaal begat\l"
    .string "Micah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_41::
    .string "And the sons of Micah were, Pithon,\n"
    .string "and Melech, and Tahrea, and Ahaz.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_42::
    .string "And Ahaz begat Jarah; and Jarah\n"
    .string "begat Alemeth, and Azmaveth, and\l"
    .string "Zimri; and Zimri begat Moza;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_43::
    .string "And Moza begat Binea; and Rephaiah\n"
    .string "his son, Eleasah his son, Azel his\l"
    .string "son$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_9_44::
    .string "And Azel had six sons, whose names\n"
    .string "are these, Azrikam, Bocheru, and\l"
    .string "Ishmael, and Sheariah, and Obadiah,\l"
    .string "and Hanan: these were the sons of\l"
    .string "Azel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_1::
    .string "Now the Philistines fought against\n"
    .string "Israel; and the men of Israel fled\l"
    .string "from before the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "fell down slain in mount Gilboa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_2::
    .string "And the Philistines followed hard\n"
    .string "after Saul, and after his sons; and\l"
    .string "the Philistines slew Jonathan, and\l"
    .string "Abinadab, and Malchishua, the sons\l"
    .string "of Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_3::
    .string "And the battle went sore against\n"
    .string "Saul, and the archers hit him, and he\l"
    .string "was wounded of the archers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_4::
    .string "Then said Saul to his armourbearer,\n"
    .string "Draw thy sword, and thrust me through\l"
    .string "therewith; lest these uncircumcised\l"
    .string "come and abuse me. But his\l"
    .string "armourbearer would not; for he was\l"
    .string "sore afraid. So Saul took a sword,\l"
    .string "and fell upon it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_5::
    .string "And when his armourbearer saw that\n"
    .string "Saul was dead, he fell likewise on\l"
    .string "the sword, and died.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_6::
    .string "So Saul died, and his three sons,\n"
    .string "and all his house died together.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_7::
    .string "And when all the men of Israel\n"
    .string "that were in the valley saw that\l"
    .string "they fled, and that Saul and his\l"
    .string "sons were dead, then they forsook\l"
    .string "their cities, and fled: and the\l"
    .string "Philistines came and dwelt in them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_8::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "when the Philistines came to strip\l"
    .string "the slain, that they found Saul and\l"
    .string "his sons fallen in mount Gilboa.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_9::
    .string "And when they had stripped him,\n"
    .string "they took his head, and his armour,\l"
    .string "and sent into the land of the\l"
    .string "Philistines round about, to carry\l"
    .string "tidings unto their idols, and to the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_10::
    .string "And they put his armour in the\n"
    .string "house of their gods, and fastened his\l"
    .string "head in the temple of Dagon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_11::
    .string "And when all Jabeshgilead heard\n"
    .string "all that the Philistines had done\l"
    .string "to Saul,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_12::
    .string "They arose, all the valiant men,\n"
    .string "and took away the body of Saul, and\l"
    .string "the bodies of his sons, and brought\l"
    .string "them to Jabesh, and buried their\l"
    .string "bones under the oak in Jabesh, and\l"
    .string "fasted seven days$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_13::
    .string "So Saul died for his transgression\n"
    .string "which he committed against the LORD,\l"
    .string "even against the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he kept not, and also for\l"
    .string "asking counsel of one that had a\l"
    .string "familiar spirit, to enquire of it;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_10_14::
    .string "And enquired not of the LORD:\n"
    .string "therefore he slew him, and turned\l"
    .string "the kingdom unto David the son of\l"
    .string "Jesse$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_1::
    .string "Then all Israel gathered\n"
    .string "themselves to David unto Hebron,\l"
    .string "saying, Behold, we are thy bone and\l"
    .string "thy flesh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_2::
    .string "And moreover in time past, even\n"
    .string "when Saul was king, thou wast he that\l"
    .string "leddest out and broughtest in\l"
    .string "Israel: and the LORD thy God said\l"
    .string "unto thee, Thou shalt feed my\l"
    .string "people Israel, and thou shalt be\l"
    .string "ruler over my people Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_3::
    .string "Therefore came all the elders of\n"
    .string "Israel to the king to Hebron; and\l"
    .string "David made a covenant with them in\l"
    .string "Hebron before the LORD; and they\l"
    .string "anointed David king over Israel,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD by\l"
    .string "Samuel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_4::
    .string "And David and all Israel went to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, which is Jebus; where the\l"
    .string "Jebusites were, the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_5::
    .string "And the inhabitants of Jebus said to\n"
    .string "David, Thou shalt not come hither.\l"
    .string "Nevertheless David took the castle\l"
    .string "of Zion, which is the city of David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_6::
    .string "And David said, Whosoever smiteth\n"
    .string "the Jebusites first shall be chief\l"
    .string "and captain. So Joab the son of\l"
    .string "Zeruiah went first up, and was chief.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_7::
    .string "And David dwelt in the castle;\n"
    .string "therefore they called it the city\l"
    .string "of David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_8::
    .string "And he built the city round about,\n"
    .string "even from Millo round about: and\l"
    .string "Joab repaired the rest of the city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_9::
    .string "So David waxed greater and greater:\n"
    .string "for the LORD of hosts was with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_10::
    .string "These also are the chief of the\n"
    .string "mighty men whom David had, who\l"
    .string "strengthened themselves with him in\l"
    .string "his kingdom, and with all Israel,\l"
    .string "to make him king, according to the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD concerning Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_11::
    .string "And this is the number of the mighty\n"
    .string "men whom David had; Jashobeam, an\l"
    .string "Hachmonite, the chief of the\l"
    .string "captains: he lifted up his spear\l"
    .string "against three hundred slain by him\l"
    .string "at one time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_12::
    .string "And after him was Eleazar the son\n"
    .string "of Dodo, the Ahohite, who was one of\l"
    .string "the three mighties.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_13::
    .string "He was with David at Pasdammim, and\n"
    .string "there the Philistines were gathered\l"
    .string "together to battle, where was a\l"
    .string "parcel of ground full of barley;\l"
    .string "and the people fled from before\l"
    .string "the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_14::
    .string "And they set themselves in the\n"
    .string "midst of that parcel, and delivered\l"
    .string "it, and slew the Philistines; and\l"
    .string "the LORD saved them by a great\l"
    .string "deliverance.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_15::
    .string "Now three of the thirty captains\n"
    .string "went down to the rock to David, into\l"
    .string "the cave of Adullam; and the host of\l"
    .string "the Philistines encamped in the\l"
    .string "valley of Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_16::
    .string "And David was then in the hold, and\n"
    .string "the Philistines’ garrison was then\l"
    .string "at Bethlehem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_17::
    .string "And David longed, and said, Oh that\n"
    .string "one would give me drink of the water\l"
    .string "of the well of Bethlehem, that is\l"
    .string "at the gate!"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_18::
    .string "And the three brake through the host\n"
    .string "of the Philistines, and drew water\l"
    .string "out of the well of Bethlehem, that\l"
    .string "was by the gate, and took it, and\l"
    .string "brought it to David: but David would\l"
    .string "not drink of it, but poured it out to\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_19::
    .string "And said, My God forbid it me, that I\n"
    .string "should do this thing: shall I drink\l"
    .string "the blood of these men that have put\l"
    .string "their lives in jeopardy? for with\l"
    .string "the jeopardy of their lives they\l"
    .string "brought it. Therefore he would not\l"
    .string "drink it. These things did these\l"
    .string "three mightiest.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_20::
    .string "And Abishai the brother of Joab, he\n"
    .string "was chief of the three: for lifting\l"
    .string "up his spear against three hundred,\l"
    .string "he slew them, and had a name among\l"
    .string "the three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_21::
    .string "Of the three, he was more\n"
    .string "honourable than the two; for he was\l"
    .string "their captain: howbeit he attained\l"
    .string "not to the first three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_22::
    .string "Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son\n"
    .string "of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had\l"
    .string "done many acts; he slew two\l"
    .string "lionlike men of Moab: also he went\l"
    .string "down and slew a lion in a pit in a\l"
    .string "snowy day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_23::
    .string "And he slew an Egyptian, a man of\n"
    .string "great stature, five cubits high; and\l"
    .string "in the Egyptian’s hand was a spear\l"
    .string "like a weaver’s beam; and he went\l"
    .string "down to him with a staff, and\l"
    .string "plucked the spear out of the\l"
    .string "Egyptian’s hand, and slew him with\l"
    .string "his own spear.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_24::
    .string "These things did Benaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Jehoiada, and had the name among the\l"
    .string "three mighties.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_25::
    .string "Behold, he was honourable among\n"
    .string "the thirty, but attained not to the\l"
    .string "first three: and David set him over\l"
    .string "his guard.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_26::
    .string "Also the valiant men of the armies\n"
    .string "were, Asahel the brother of Joab,\l"
    .string "Elhanan the son of Dodo of\l"
    .string "Bethlehem,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_27::
    .string "Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the\n"
    .string "Pelonite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_28::
    .string "Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite,\n"
    .string "Abiezer the Antothite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_29::
    .string "Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the\n"
    .string "Ahohite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_30::
    .string "Maharai the Netophathite, Heled\n"
    .string "the son of Baanah the Netophathite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_31::
    .string "Ithai the son of Ribai of Gibeah,\n"
    .string "that pertained to the children of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, Benaiah the Pirathonite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_32::
    .string "Hurai of the brooks of Gaash, Abiel\n"
    .string "the Arbathite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_33::
    .string "Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba\n"
    .string "the Shaalbonite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_34::
    .string "The sons of Hashem the Gizonite,\n"
    .string "Jonathan the son of Shage the\l"
    .string "Hararite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_35::
    .string "Ahiam the son of Sacar the Hararite,\n"
    .string "Eliphal the son of Ur,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_36::
    .string "Hepher the Mecherathite, Ahijah the\n"
    .string "Pelonite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_37::
    .string "Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai the son\n"
    .string "of Ezbai,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_38::
    .string "Joel the brother of Nathan, Mibhar\n"
    .string "the son of Haggeri,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_39::
    .string "Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the\n"
    .string "Berothite, the armourbearer of Joab\l"
    .string "the son of Zeruiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_40::
    .string "Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_41::
    .string "Uriah the Hittite, Zabad the son of\n"
    .string "Ahlai,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_42::
    .string "Adina the son of Shiza the\n"
    .string "Reubenite, a captain of the\l"
    .string "Reubenites, and thirty with him,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_43::
    .string "Hanan the son of Maachah, and\n"
    .string "Joshaphat the Mithnite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_44::
    .string "Uzzia the Ashterathite, Shama and\n"
    .string "Jehiel the sons of Hothan the\l"
    .string "Aroerite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_45::
    .string "Jediael the son of Shimri, and Joha\n"
    .string "his brother, the Tizite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_46::
    .string "Eliel the Mahavite, and Jeribai,\n"
    .string "and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam,\l"
    .string "and Ithmah the Moabite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_11_47::
    .string "Eliel, and Obed, and Jasiel the\n"
    .string "Mesobaite$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_1::
    .string "Now these are they that came to\n"
    .string "David to Ziklag, while he yet kept\l"
    .string "himself close because of Saul the\l"
    .string "son of Kish: and they were among the\l"
    .string "mighty men, helpers of the war.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_2::
    .string "They were armed with bows, and\n"
    .string "could use both the right hand and\l"
    .string "the left in hurling stones and\l"
    .string "shooting arrows out of a bow, even of\l"
    .string "Saul’s brethren of Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_3::
    .string "The chief was Ahiezer, then Joash,\n"
    .string "the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite;\l"
    .string "and Jeziel, and Pelet, the sons of\l"
    .string "Azmaveth; and Berachah, and Jehu the\l"
    .string "Antothite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_4::
    .string "And Ismaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty\n"
    .string "man among the thirty, and over the\l"
    .string "thirty; and Jeremiah, and Jahaziel,\l"
    .string "and Johanan, and Josabad the\l"
    .string "Gederathite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_5::
    .string "Eluzai, and Jerimoth, and Bealiah,\n"
    .string "and Shemariah, and Shephatiah the\l"
    .string "Haruphite,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_6::
    .string "Elkanah, and Jesiah, and Azareel,\n"
    .string "and Joezer, and Jashobeam, the\l"
    .string "Korhites,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_7::
    .string "And Joelah, and Zebadiah, the sons\n"
    .string "of Jeroham of Gedor$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_8::
    .string "And of the Gadites there separated\n"
    .string "themselves unto David into the hold\l"
    .string "to the wilderness men of might, and\l"
    .string "men of war fit for the battle, that\l"
    .string "could handle shield and buckler,\l"
    .string "whose faces were like the faces of\l"
    .string "lions, and were as swift as the roes\l"
    .string "upon the mountains;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_9::
    .string "Ezer the first, Obadiah the second,\n"
    .string "Eliab the third,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_10::
    .string "Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the\n"
    .string "fifth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_11::
    .string "Attai the sixth, Eliel the\n"
    .string "seventh,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_12::
    .string "Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the\n"
    .string "ninth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_13::
    .string "Jeremiah the tenth, Machbanai the\n"
    .string "eleventh$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_14::
    .string "These were of the sons of Gad,\n"
    .string "captains of the host: one of the\l"
    .string "least was over an hundred, and the\l"
    .string "greatest over a thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_15::
    .string "These are they that went over Jordan\n"
    .string "in the first month, when it had\l"
    .string "overflown all his banks; and they\l"
    .string "put to flight all them of the\l"
    .string "valleys, both toward the east, and\l"
    .string "toward the west.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_16::
    .string "And there came of the children of\n"
    .string "Benjamin and Judah to the hold unto\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_17::
    .string "And David went out to meet them, and\n"
    .string "answered and said unto them, If ye be\l"
    .string "come peaceably unto me to help me,\l"
    .string "mine heart shall be knit unto you:\l"
    .string "but if ye be come to betray me to mine\l"
    .string "enemies, seeing there is no wrong in\l"
    .string "mine hands, the God of our fathers\l"
    .string "look thereon, and rebuke it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_18::
    .string "Then the spirit came upon Amasai,\n"
    .string "who was chief of the captains, and he\l"
    .string "said, Thine are we, David, and on thy\l"
    .string "side, thou son of Jesse: peace,\l"
    .string "peace be unto thee, and peace be to\l"
    .string "thine helpers; for thy God helpeth\l"
    .string "thee. Then David received them, and\l"
    .string "made them captains of the band.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_19::
    .string "And there fell some of Manasseh to\n"
    .string "David, when he came with the\l"
    .string "Philistines against Saul to\l"
    .string "battle: but they helped them not:\l"
    .string "for the lords of the Philistines\l"
    .string "upon advisement sent him away,\l"
    .string "saying, He will fall to his master\l"
    .string "Saul to the jeopardy of our heads.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_20::
    .string "As he went to Ziklag, there fell\n"
    .string "to him of Manasseh, Adnah, and\l"
    .string "Jozabad, and Jediael, and Michael,\l"
    .string "and Jozabad, and Elihu, and Zilthai,\l"
    .string "captains of the thousands that were\l"
    .string "of Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_21::
    .string "And they helped David against the\n"
    .string "band of the rovers: for they were\l"
    .string "all mighty men of valour, and were\l"
    .string "captains in the host.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_22::
    .string "For at that time day by day there\n"
    .string "came to David to help him, until it\l"
    .string "was a great host, like the host of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_23::
    .string "And these are the numbers of the\n"
    .string "bands that were ready armed to the\l"
    .string "war, and came to David to Hebron, to\l"
    .string "turn the kingdom of Saul to him,\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_24::
    .string "The children of Judah that bare\n"
    .string "shield and spear were six thousand\l"
    .string "and eight hundred, ready armed to the\l"
    .string "war.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_25::
    .string "Of the children of Simeon, mighty\n"
    .string "men of valour for the war, seven\l"
    .string "thousand and one hundred.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_26::
    .string "Of the children of Levi four\n"
    .string "thousand and six hundred.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_27::
    .string "And Jehoiada was the leader of the\n"
    .string "Aaronites, and with him were three\l"
    .string "thousand and seven hundred;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_28::
    .string "And Zadok, a young man mighty of\n"
    .string "valour, and of his father’s house\l"
    .string "twenty and two captains$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_29::
    .string "And of the children of Benjamin,\n"
    .string "the kindred of Saul, three thousand:\l"
    .string "for hitherto the greatest part of\l"
    .string "them had kept the ward of the house\l"
    .string "of Saul.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_30::
    .string "And of the children of Ephraim\n"
    .string "twenty thousand and eight hundred,\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, famous\l"
    .string "throughout the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_31::
    .string "And of the half tribe of Manasseh\n"
    .string "eighteen thousand, which were\l"
    .string "expressed by name, to come and make\l"
    .string "David king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_32::
    .string "And of the children of Issachar,\n"
    .string "which were men that had\l"
    .string "understanding of the times, to know\l"
    .string "what Israel ought to do; the heads of\l"
    .string "them were two hundred; and all their\l"
    .string "brethren were at their commandment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_33::
    .string "Of Zebulun, such as went forth to\n"
    .string "battle, expert in war, with all\l"
    .string "instruments of war, fifty thousand,\l"
    .string "which could keep rank: they were not\l"
    .string "of double heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_34::
    .string "And of Naphtali a thousand\n"
    .string "captains, and with them with shield\l"
    .string "and spear thirty and seven thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_35::
    .string "And of the Danites expert in war\n"
    .string "twenty and eight thousand and six\l"
    .string "hundred.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_36::
    .string "And of Asher, such as went forth to\n"
    .string "battle, expert in war, forty\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_37::
    .string "And on the other side of Jordan, of\n"
    .string "the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and\l"
    .string "of the half tribe of Manasseh, with\l"
    .string "all manner of instruments of war\l"
    .string "for the battle, an hundred and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_38::
    .string "All these men of war, that could\n"
    .string "keep rank, came with a perfect heart\l"
    .string "to Hebron, to make David king over\l"
    .string "all Israel: and all the rest also\l"
    .string "of Israel were of one heart to make\l"
    .string "David king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_39::
    .string "And there they were with David three\n"
    .string "days, eating and drinking: for their\l"
    .string "brethren had prepared for them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_12_40::
    .string "Moreover they that were nigh them,\n"
    .string "even unto Issachar and Zebulun and\l"
    .string "Naphtali, brought bread on asses,\l"
    .string "and on camels, and on mules, and on\l"
    .string "oxen, and meat, meal, cakes of figs,\l"
    .string "and bunches of raisins, and wine, and\l"
    .string "oil, and oxen, and sheep\l"
    .string "abundantly: for there was joy in\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_1::
    .string "And David consulted with the\n"
    .string "captains of thousands and hundreds,\l"
    .string "and with every leader.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_2::
    .string "And David said unto all the\n"
    .string "congregation of Israel, If it seem\l"
    .string "good unto you, and that it be of the\l"
    .string "LORD our God, let us send abroad unto\l"
    .string "our brethren every where, that are\l"
    .string "left in all the land of Israel, and\l"
    .string "with them also to the priests and\l"
    .string "Levites which are in their cities and\l"
    .string "suburbs, that they may gather\l"
    .string "themselves unto us:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_3::
    .string "And let us bring again the ark of\n"
    .string "our God to us: for we enquired not at\l"
    .string "it in the days of Saul$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_4::
    .string "And all the congregation said that\n"
    .string "they would do so: for the thing was\l"
    .string "right in the eyes of all the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_5::
    .string "So David gathered all Israel\n"
    .string "together, from Shihor of Egypt even\l"
    .string "unto the entering of Hemath, to bring\l"
    .string "the ark of God from Kirjathjearim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_6::
    .string "And David went up, and all\n"
    .string "Israel, to Baalah, that is, to\l"
    .string "Kirjathjearim, which belonged to\l"
    .string "Judah, to bring up thence the ark of\l"
    .string "God the LORD, that dwelleth between\l"
    .string "the cherubims, whose name is called\l"
    .string "on it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_7::
    .string "And they carried the ark of God in a\n"
    .string "new cart out of the house of\l"
    .string "Abinadab: and Uzza and Ahio drave the\l"
    .string "cart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_8::
    .string "And David and all Israel played\n"
    .string "before God with all their might, and\l"
    .string "with singing, and with harps, and\l"
    .string "with psalteries, and with\l"
    .string "timbrels, and with cymbals, and\l"
    .string "with trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_9::
    .string "And when they came unto the\n"
    .string "threshingfloor of Chidon, Uzza put\l"
    .string "forth his hand to hold the ark; for\l"
    .string "the oxen stumbled.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_10::
    .string "And the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Uzza, and he smote\l"
    .string "him, because he put his hand to the\l"
    .string "ark: and there he died before God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_11::
    .string "And David was displeased, because\n"
    .string "the LORD had made a breach upon Uzza:\l"
    .string "wherefore that place is called\l"
    .string "Perezuzza to this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_12::
    .string "And David was afraid of God that\n"
    .string "day, saying, How shall I bring the\l"
    .string "ark of God home to me?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_13::
    .string "So David brought not the ark home to\n"
    .string "himself to the city of David, but\l"
    .string "carried it aside into the house of\l"
    .string "Obededom the Gittite$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_13_14::
    .string "And the ark of God remained with the\n"
    .string "family of Obededom in his house\l"
    .string "three months. And the LORD blessed\l"
    .string "the house of Obededom, and all that\l"
    .string "he had.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_1::
    .string "Now Hiram king of Tyre sent\n"
    .string "messengers to David, and timber of\l"
    .string "cedars, with masons and carpenters,\l"
    .string "to build him an house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_2::
    .string "And David perceived that the LORD\n"
    .string "had confirmed him king over Israel,\l"
    .string "for his kingdom was lifted up on\l"
    .string "high, because of his people Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_3::
    .string "And David took more wives at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: and David begat more sons\l"
    .string "and daughters.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_4::
    .string "Now these are the names of his\n"
    .string "children which he had in Jerusalem;\l"
    .string "Shammua, and Shobab, Nathan, and\l"
    .string "Solomon,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_5::
    .string "And Ibhar, and Elishua, and\n"
    .string "Elpalet,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_6::
    .string "And Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_7::
    .string "And Elishama, and Beeliada, and\n"
    .string "Eliphalet$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_8::
    .string "And when the Philistines heard that\n"
    .string "David was anointed king over all\l"
    .string "Israel, all the Philistines went\l"
    .string "up to seek David. And David heard of\l"
    .string "it, and went out against them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_9::
    .string "And the Philistines came and\n"
    .string "spread themselves in the valley of\l"
    .string "Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_10::
    .string "And David enquired of God, saying,\n"
    .string "Shall I go up against the\l"
    .string "Philistines? And wilt thou deliver\l"
    .string "them into mine hand? And the LORD\l"
    .string "said unto him, Go up; for I will\l"
    .string "deliver them into thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_11::
    .string "So they came up to Baalperazim;\n"
    .string "and David smote them there. Then\l"
    .string "David said, God hath broken in upon\l"
    .string "mine enemies by mine hand like the\l"
    .string "breaking forth of waters: therefore\l"
    .string "they called the name of that place\l"
    .string "Baalperazim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_12::
    .string "And when they had left their gods\n"
    .string "there, David gave a commandment, and\l"
    .string "they were burned with fire.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_13::
    .string "And the Philistines yet again\n"
    .string "spread themselves abroad in the\l"
    .string "valley.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_14::
    .string "Therefore David enquired again of\n"
    .string "God; and God said unto him, Go not up\l"
    .string "after them; turn away from them, and\l"
    .string "come upon them over against the\l"
    .string "mulberry trees.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_15::
    .string "And it shall be, when thou shalt\n"
    .string "hear a sound of going in the tops of\l"
    .string "the mulberry trees, that then thou\l"
    .string "shalt go out to battle: for God is\l"
    .string "gone forth before thee to smite the\l"
    .string "host of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_16::
    .string "David therefore did as God\n"
    .string "commanded him: and they smote the\l"
    .string "host of the Philistines from Gibeon\l"
    .string "even to Gazer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_14_17::
    .string "And the fame of David went out into\n"
    .string "all lands; and the LORD brought the\l"
    .string "fear of him upon all nations.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_1::
    .string "And David made him houses in the\n"
    .string "city of David, and prepared a\l"
    .string "place for the ark of God, and\l"
    .string "pitched for it a tent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_2::
    .string "Then David said, None ought to carry\n"
    .string "the ark of God but the Levites: for\l"
    .string "them hath the LORD chosen to carry\l"
    .string "the ark of God, and to minister unto\l"
    .string "him for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_3::
    .string "And David gathered all Israel\n"
    .string "together to Jerusalem, to bring up\l"
    .string "the ark of the LORD unto his place,\l"
    .string "which he had prepared for it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_4::
    .string "And David assembled the children\n"
    .string "of Aaron, and the Levites:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_5::
    .string "Of the sons of Kohath; Uriel the\n"
    .string "chief, and his brethren an hundred\l"
    .string "and twenty:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_6::
    .string "Of the sons of Merari; Asaiah the\n"
    .string "chief, and his brethren two hundred\l"
    .string "and twenty:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_7::
    .string "Of the sons of Gershom; Joel the\n"
    .string "chief and his brethren an hundred and\l"
    .string "thirty:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_8::
    .string "Of the sons of Elizaphan; Shemaiah\n"
    .string "the chief, and his brethren two\l"
    .string "hundred:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_9::
    .string "Of the sons of Hebron; Eliel the\n"
    .string "chief, and his brethren fourscore:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_10::
    .string "Of the sons of Uzziel; Amminadab\n"
    .string "the chief, and his brethren an\l"
    .string "hundred and twelve$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_11::
    .string "And David called for Zadok and\n"
    .string "Abiathar the priests, and for the\l"
    .string "Levites, for Uriel, Asaiah, and\l"
    .string "Joel, Shemaiah, and Eliel, and\l"
    .string "Amminadab,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_12::
    .string "And said unto them, Ye are the chief\n"
    .string "of the fathers of the Levites:\l"
    .string "sanctify yourselves, both ye and\l"
    .string "your brethren, that ye may bring up\l"
    .string "the ark of the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "unto the place that I have\l"
    .string "prepared for it$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_13::
    .string "For because ye did it not at the\n"
    .string "first, the LORD our God made a breach\l"
    .string "upon us, for that we sought him not\l"
    .string "after the due order.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_14::
    .string "So the priests and the Levites\n"
    .string "sanctified themselves to bring up\l"
    .string "the ark of the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_15::
    .string "And the children of the Levites\n"
    .string "bare the ark of God upon their\l"
    .string "shoulders with the staves thereon,\l"
    .string "as Moses commanded according to the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_16::
    .string "And David spake to the chief of the\n"
    .string "Levites to appoint their brethren\l"
    .string "to be the singers with instruments of\l"
    .string "musick, psalteries and harps and\l"
    .string "cymbals, sounding, by lifting up\l"
    .string "the voice with joy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_17::
    .string "So the Levites appointed Heman the\n"
    .string "son of Joel; and of his brethren,\l"
    .string "Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of\l"
    .string "the sons of Merari their brethren,\l"
    .string "Ethan the son of Kushaiah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_18::
    .string "And with them their brethren of the\n"
    .string "second degree, Zechariah, Ben, and\l"
    .string "Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth, and\l"
    .string "Jehiel, and Unni, Eliab, and\l"
    .string "Benaiah, and Maaseiah, and\l"
    .string "Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and\l"
    .string "Mikneiah, and Obededom, and Jeiel,\l"
    .string "the porters$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_19::
    .string "So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and\n"
    .string "Ethan, were appointed to sound with\l"
    .string "cymbals of brass;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_20::
    .string "And Zechariah, and Aziel, and\n"
    .string "Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni,\l"
    .string "and Eliab, and Maaseiah, and\l"
    .string "Benaiah, with psalteries on\l"
    .string "Alamoth;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_21::
    .string "And Mattithiah, and Elipheleh,\n"
    .string "and Mikneiah, and Obededom, and\l"
    .string "Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps on\l"
    .string "the Sheminith to excel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_22::
    .string "And Chenaniah, chief of the Levites,\n"
    .string "was for song: he instructed about the\l"
    .string "song, because he was skilful.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_23::
    .string "And Berechiah and Elkanah were\n"
    .string "doorkeepers for the ark.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_24::
    .string "And Shebaniah, and Jehoshaphat, and\n"
    .string "Nethaneel, and Amasai, and\l"
    .string "Zechariah, and Benaiah, and Eliezer,\l"
    .string "the priests, did blow with the\l"
    .string "trumpets before the ark of God: and\l"
    .string "Obededom and Jehiah were\l"
    .string "doorkeepers for the ark.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_25::
    .string "So David, and the elders of Israel,\n"
    .string "and the captains over thousands,\l"
    .string "went to bring up the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD out of the house\l"
    .string "of Obededom with joy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_26::
    .string "And it came to pass, when God\n"
    .string "helped the Levites that bare the\l"
    .string "ark of the covenant of the LORD, that\l"
    .string "they offered seven bullocks and\l"
    .string "seven rams.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_27::
    .string "And David was clothed with a robe\n"
    .string "of fine linen, and all the Levites\l"
    .string "that bare the ark, and the singers,\l"
    .string "and Chenaniah the master of the song\l"
    .string "with the singers: David also had\l"
    .string "upon him an ephod of linen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_28::
    .string "Thus all Israel brought up the\n"
    .string "ark of the covenant of the LORD with\l"
    .string "shouting, and with sound of the\l"
    .string "cornet, and with trumpets, and with\l"
    .string "cymbals, making a noise with\l"
    .string "psalteries and harps.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_15_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, as the ark of\n"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD came to the\l"
    .string "city of David, that Michal, the\l"
    .string "daughter of Saul looking out at a\l"
    .string "window saw king David dancing and\l"
    .string "playing: and she despised him in her\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_1::
    .string "So they brought the ark of God, and\n"
    .string "set it in the midst of the tent that\l"
    .string "David had pitched for it: and they\l"
    .string "offered burnt sacrifices and peace\l"
    .string "offerings before God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_2::
    .string "And when David had made an end of\n"
    .string "offering the burnt offerings and the\l"
    .string "peace offerings, he blessed the\l"
    .string "people in the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_3::
    .string "And he dealt to every one of\n"
    .string "Israel, both man and woman, to every\l"
    .string "one a loaf of bread, and a good\l"
    .string "piece of flesh, and a flagon of wine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_4::
    .string "And he appointed certain of the\n"
    .string "Levites to minister before the ark of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and to record, and to thank\l"
    .string "and praise the LORD God of Israel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_5::
    .string "Asaph the chief, and next to him\n"
    .string "Zechariah, Jeiel, and Shemiramoth,\l"
    .string "and Jehiel, and Mattithiah, and\l"
    .string "Eliab, and Benaiah, and Obededom:\l"
    .string "and Jeiel with psalteries and with\l"
    .string "harps; but Asaph made a sound with\l"
    .string "cymbals;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_6::
    .string "Benaiah also and Jahaziel the\n"
    .string "priests with trumpets continually\l"
    .string "before the ark of the covenant of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_7::
    .string "Then on that day David delivered\n"
    .string "first this psalm to thank the LORD\l"
    .string "into the hand of Asaph and his\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_8::
    .string "Give thanks unto the LORD, call\n"
    .string "upon his name, make known his deeds\l"
    .string "among the people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_9::
    .string "Sing unto him, sing psalms unto\n"
    .string "him, talk ye of all his wondrous\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_10::
    .string "Glory ye in his holy name: let the\n"
    .string "heart of them rejoice that seek the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_11::
    .string "Seek the LORD and his strength, seek\n"
    .string "his face continually.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_12::
    .string "Remember his marvellous works that\n"
    .string "he hath done, his wonders, and the\l"
    .string "judgments of his mouth;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_13::
    .string "O ye seed of Israel his servant, ye\n"
    .string "children of Jacob, his chosen ones$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_14::
    .string "He is the LORD our God; his\n"
    .string "judgments are in all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_15::
    .string "Be ye mindful always of his\n"
    .string "covenant; the word which he commanded\l"
    .string "to a thousand generations;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_16::
    .string "Even of the covenant which he made\n"
    .string "with Abraham, and of his oath unto\l"
    .string "Isaac;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_17::
    .string "And hath confirmed the same to Jacob\n"
    .string "for a law, and to Israel for an\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_18::
    .string "Saying, Unto thee will I give the\n"
    .string "land of Canaan, the lot of your\l"
    .string "inheritance;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_19::
    .string "When ye were but few, even a few, and\n"
    .string "strangers in it$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_20::
    .string "And when they went from nation to\n"
    .string "nation, and from one kingdom to\l"
    .string "another people;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_21::
    .string "He suffered no man to do them wrong:\n"
    .string "yea, he reproved kings for their\l"
    .string "sakes,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_22::
    .string "Saying, Touch not mine anointed, and\n"
    .string "do my prophets no harm$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_23::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD, all the earth;\n"
    .string "shew forth from day to day his\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_24::
    .string "Declare his glory among the\n"
    .string "heathen; his marvellous works among\l"
    .string "all nations.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_25::
    .string "For great is the LORD, and greatly\n"
    .string "to be praised: he also is to be\l"
    .string "feared above all gods.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_26::
    .string "For all the gods of the people\n"
    .string "are idols: but the LORD made the\l"
    .string "heavens.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_27::
    .string "Glory and honour are in his\n"
    .string "presence; strength and gladness are\l"
    .string "in his place.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_28::
    .string "Give unto the LORD, ye kindreds of\n"
    .string "the people, give unto the LORD\l"
    .string "glory and strength.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_29::
    .string "Give unto the LORD the glory due\n"
    .string "unto his name: bring an offering, and\l"
    .string "come before him: worship the LORD in\l"
    .string "the beauty of holiness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_30::
    .string "Fear before him, all the earth: the\n"
    .string "world also shall be stable, that\l"
    .string "it be not moved.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_31::
    .string "Let the heavens be glad, and let\n"
    .string "the earth rejoice: and let men say\l"
    .string "among the nations, The LORD reigneth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_32::
    .string "Let the sea roar, and the fulness\n"
    .string "thereof: let the fields rejoice,\l"
    .string "and all that is therein.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_33::
    .string "Then shall the trees of the wood\n"
    .string "sing out at the presence of the LORD,\l"
    .string "because he cometh to judge the earth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_34::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD; for he\n"
    .string "is good; for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_35::
    .string "And say ye, Save us, O God of our\n"
    .string "salvation, and gather us together,\l"
    .string "and deliver us from the heathen,\l"
    .string "that we may give thanks to thy holy\l"
    .string "name, and glory in thy praise.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_36::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "for ever and ever. And all the\l"
    .string "people said, Amen, and praised the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_37::
    .string "So he left there before the ark of\n"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD Asaph and\l"
    .string "his brethren, to minister before the\l"
    .string "ark continually, as every day’s\l"
    .string "work required:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_38::
    .string "And Obededom with their brethren,\n"
    .string "threescore and eight; Obededom also\l"
    .string "the son of Jeduthun and Hosah to be\l"
    .string "porters:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_39::
    .string "And Zadok the priest, and his\n"
    .string "brethren the priests, before the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the LORD in the high\l"
    .string "place that was at Gibeon,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_40::
    .string "To offer burnt offerings unto the\n"
    .string "LORD upon the altar of the burnt\l"
    .string "offering continually morning and\l"
    .string "evening, and to do according to all\l"
    .string "that is written in the law of the\l"
    .string "LORD, which he commanded Israel;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_41::
    .string "And with them Heman and Jeduthun,\n"
    .string "and the rest that were chosen, who\l"
    .string "were expressed by name, to give\l"
    .string "thanks to the LORD, because his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_42::
    .string "And with them Heman and Jeduthun\n"
    .string "with trumpets and cymbals for those\l"
    .string "that should make a sound, and with\l"
    .string "musical instruments of God. And the\l"
    .string "sons of Jeduthun were porters$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_16_43::
    .string "And all the people departed\n"
    .string "every man to his house: and David\l"
    .string "returned to bless his house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass, as David sat in\n"
    .string "his house, that David said to Nathan\l"
    .string "the prophet, Lo, I dwell in an\l"
    .string "house of cedars, but the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD remaineth under\l"
    .string "curtains.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_2::
    .string "Then Nathan said unto David, Do all\n"
    .string "that is in thine heart; for God is\l"
    .string "with thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_3::
    .string "And it came to pass the same night,\n"
    .string "that the word of God came to Nathan,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_4::
    .string "Go and tell David my servant, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, Thou shalt not build\l"
    .string "me an house to dwell in:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_5::
    .string "For I have not dwelt in an house\n"
    .string "since the day that I brought up\l"
    .string "Israel unto this day; but have gone\l"
    .string "from tent to tent, and from one\l"
    .string "tabernacle to another$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_6::
    .string "Wheresoever I have walked with\n"
    .string "all Israel, spake I a word to any\l"
    .string "of the judges of Israel, whom I\l"
    .string "commanded to feed my people,\l"
    .string "saying, Why have ye not built me an\l"
    .string "house of cedars?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_7::
    .string "Now therefore thus shalt thou say\n"
    .string "unto my servant David, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, I took thee from the\l"
    .string "sheepcote, even from following the\l"
    .string "sheep, that thou shouldest be ruler\l"
    .string "over my people Israel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_8::
    .string "And I have been with thee\n"
    .string "whithersoever thou hast walked, and\l"
    .string "have cut off all thine enemies from\l"
    .string "before thee, and have made thee a\l"
    .string "name like the name of the great men\l"
    .string "that are in the earth$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_9::
    .string "Also I will ordain a place for my\n"
    .string "people Israel, and will plant\l"
    .string "them, and they shall dwell in\l"
    .string "their place, and shall be moved no\l"
    .string "more; neither shall the children of\l"
    .string "wickedness waste them any more, as at\l"
    .string "the beginning,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_10::
    .string "And since the time that I commanded\n"
    .string "judges to be over my people\l"
    .string "Israel. Moreover I will subdue\l"
    .string "all thine enemies. Furthermore I\l"
    .string "tell thee that the LORD will\l"
    .string "build thee an house$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_11::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "thy days be expired that thou must\l"
    .string "go to be with thy fathers, that I\l"
    .string "will raise up thy seed after thee,\l"
    .string "which shall be of thy sons; and I\l"
    .string "will establish his kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_12::
    .string "He shall build me an house, and I\n"
    .string "will stablish his throne for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_13::
    .string "I will be his father, and he shall\n"
    .string "be my son: and I will not take my\l"
    .string "mercy away from him, as I took it from\l"
    .string "him that was before thee:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_14::
    .string "But I will settle him in mine\n"
    .string "house and in my kingdom for ever: and\l"
    .string "his throne shall be established\l"
    .string "for evermore$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_15::
    .string "According to all these words, and\n"
    .string "according to all this vision, so did\l"
    .string "Nathan speak unto David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_16::
    .string "And David the king came and sat\n"
    .string "before the LORD, and said, Who am I, O\l"
    .string "LORD God, and what is mine house,\l"
    .string "that thou hast brought me hitherto?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_17::
    .string "And yet this was a small thing in\n"
    .string "thine eyes, O God; for thou hast also\l"
    .string "spoken of thy servant’s house for a\l"
    .string "great while to come, and hast\l"
    .string "regarded me according to the estate\l"
    .string "of a man of high degree, O LORD God$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_18::
    .string "What can David speak more to thee\n"
    .string "for the honour of thy servant? for\l"
    .string "thou knowest thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_19::
    .string "O LORD, for thy servant’s sake, and\n"
    .string "according to thine own heart, hast\l"
    .string "thou done all this greatness, in\l"
    .string "making known all these great things.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_20::
    .string "O LORD, there is none like thee,\n"
    .string "neither is there any God beside thee,\l"
    .string "according to all that we have heard\l"
    .string "with our ears.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_21::
    .string "And what one nation in the earth is\n"
    .string "like thy people Israel, whom God\l"
    .string "went to redeem to be his own\l"
    .string "people, to make thee a name of\l"
    .string "greatness and terribleness, by\l"
    .string "driving out nations from before thy\l"
    .string "people whom thou hast redeemed out\l"
    .string "of Egypt?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_22::
    .string "For thy people Israel didst thou\n"
    .string "make thine own people for ever; and\l"
    .string "thou, LORD, becamest their God$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_23::
    .string "Therefore now, LORD, let the thing\n"
    .string "that thou hast spoken concerning thy\l"
    .string "servant and concerning his house be\l"
    .string "established for ever, and do as thou\l"
    .string "hast said.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_24::
    .string "Let it even be established, that\n"
    .string "thy name may be magnified for ever,\l"
    .string "saying, The LORD of hosts is the God\l"
    .string "of Israel, even a God to Israel: and\l"
    .string "let the house of David thy servant be\l"
    .string "established before thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_25::
    .string "For thou, O my God, hast told thy\n"
    .string "servant that thou wilt build him an\l"
    .string "house: therefore thy servant hath\l"
    .string "found in his heart to pray before\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_26::
    .string "And now, LORD, thou art God, and hast\n"
    .string "promised this goodness unto thy\l"
    .string "servant:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_17_27::
    .string "Now therefore let it please thee\n"
    .string "to bless the house of thy servant,\l"
    .string "that it may be before thee for ever:\l"
    .string "for thou blessest, O LORD, and it\l"
    .string "shall be blessed for ever$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_1::
    .string "Now after this it came to pass, that\n"
    .string "David smote the Philistines, and\l"
    .string "subdued them, and took Gath and her\l"
    .string "towns out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_2::
    .string "And he smote Moab; and the Moabites\n"
    .string "became David’s servants, and brought\l"
    .string "gifts.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_3::
    .string "And David smote Hadarezer king of\n"
    .string "Zobah unto Hamath, as he went to\l"
    .string "stablish his dominion by the river\l"
    .string "Euphrates.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_4::
    .string "And David took from him a thousand\n"
    .string "chariots, and seven thousand\l"
    .string "horsemen, and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "footmen: David also houghed all the\l"
    .string "chariot horses, but reserved of them\l"
    .string "an hundred chariots.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_5::
    .string "And when the Syrians of Damascus\n"
    .string "came to help Hadarezer king of\l"
    .string "Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two\l"
    .string "and twenty thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_6::
    .string "Then David put garrisons in\n"
    .string "Syriadamascus; and the Syrians\l"
    .string "became David’s servants, and brought\l"
    .string "gifts. Thus the LORD preserved David\l"
    .string "whithersoever he went.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_7::
    .string "And David took the shields of gold\n"
    .string "that were on the servants of\l"
    .string "Hadarezer, and brought them to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_8::
    .string "Likewise from Tibhath, and from\n"
    .string "Chun, cities of Hadarezer, brought\l"
    .string "David very much brass, wherewith\l"
    .string "Solomon made the brasen sea, and the\l"
    .string "pillars, and the vessels of brass.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_9::
    .string "Now when Tou king of Hamath heard\n"
    .string "how David had smitten all the host\l"
    .string "of Hadarezer king of Zobah;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_10::
    .string "He sent Hadoram his son to king\n"
    .string "David, to enquire of his welfare,\l"
    .string "and to congratulate him, because he\l"
    .string "had fought against Hadarezer, and\l"
    .string "smitten him; (for Hadarezer had war\l"
    .string "with Tou;) and with him all manner\l"
    .string "of vessels of gold and silver and\l"
    .string "brass$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_11::
    .string "Them also king David dedicated unto\n"
    .string "the LORD, with the silver and the\l"
    .string "gold that he brought from all these\l"
    .string "nations; from Edom, and from Moab,\l"
    .string "and from the children of Ammon, and\l"
    .string "from the Philistines, and from\l"
    .string "Amalek.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_12::
    .string "Moreover Abishai the son of Zeruiah\n"
    .string "slew of the Edomites in the valley\l"
    .string "of salt eighteen thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_13::
    .string "And he put garrisons in Edom; and\n"
    .string "all the Edomites became David’s\l"
    .string "servants. Thus the LORD preserved\l"
    .string "David whithersoever he went.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_14::
    .string "So David reigned over all Israel,\n"
    .string "and executed judgment and justice\l"
    .string "among all his people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_15::
    .string "And Joab the son of Zeruiah was over\n"
    .string "the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of\l"
    .string "Ahilud, recorder.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_16::
    .string "And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and\n"
    .string "Abimelech the son of Abiathar, were\l"
    .string "the priests; and Shavsha was scribe;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_18_17::
    .string "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was\n"
    .string "over the Cherethites and the\l"
    .string "Pelethites; and the sons of David\l"
    .string "were chief about the king$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "Nahash the king of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon died, and his son reigned in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_2::
    .string "And David said, I will shew\n"
    .string "kindness unto Hanun the son of\l"
    .string "Nahash, because his father shewed\l"
    .string "kindness to me. And David sent\l"
    .string "messengers to comfort him concerning\l"
    .string "his father. So the servants of David\l"
    .string "came into the land of the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon to Hanun, to comfort him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_3::
    .string "But the princes of the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon said to Hanun, Thinkest thou\l"
    .string "that David doth honour thy father,\l"
    .string "that he hath sent comforters unto\l"
    .string "thee? are not his servants come unto\l"
    .string "thee for to search, and to overthrow,\l"
    .string "and to spy out the land?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_4::
    .string "Wherefore Hanun took David’s\n"
    .string "servants, and shaved them, and cut\l"
    .string "off their garments in the midst hard\l"
    .string "by their buttocks, and sent them away$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_5::
    .string "Then there went certain, and told\n"
    .string "David how the men were served. And he\l"
    .string "sent to meet them: for the men were\l"
    .string "greatly ashamed. And the king said,\l"
    .string "Tarry at Jericho until your beards\l"
    .string "be grown, and then return.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_6::
    .string "And when the children of Ammon saw\n"
    .string "that they had made themselves odious\l"
    .string "to David, Hanun and the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon sent a thousand talents of\l"
    .string "silver to hire them chariots and\l"
    .string "horsemen out of Mesopotamia, and out\l"
    .string "of Syriamaachah, and out of Zobah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_7::
    .string "So they hired thirty and two\n"
    .string "thousand chariots, and the king of\l"
    .string "Maachah and his people; who came\l"
    .string "and pitched before Medeba. And the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together from their\l"
    .string "cities, and came to battle.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_8::
    .string "And when David heard of it, he sent\n"
    .string "Joab, and all the host of the mighty\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_9::
    .string "And the children of Ammon came out,\n"
    .string "and put the battle in array before\l"
    .string "the gate of the city: and the kings\l"
    .string "that were come were by themselves in\l"
    .string "the field.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_10::
    .string "Now when Joab saw that the battle\n"
    .string "was set against him before and\l"
    .string "behind, he chose out of all the\l"
    .string "choice of Israel, and put them in\l"
    .string "array against the Syrians.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_11::
    .string "And the rest of the people he\n"
    .string "delivered unto the hand of Abishai\l"
    .string "his brother, and they set themselves\l"
    .string "in array against the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_12::
    .string "And he said, If the Syrians be too\n"
    .string "strong for me, then thou shalt help\l"
    .string "me: but if the children of Ammon be\l"
    .string "too strong for thee, then I will\l"
    .string "help thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_13::
    .string "Be of good courage, and let us\n"
    .string "behave ourselves valiantly for our\l"
    .string "people, and for the cities of our\l"
    .string "God: and let the LORD do that which\l"
    .string "is good in his sight.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_14::
    .string "So Joab and the people that were\n"
    .string "with him drew nigh before the Syrians\l"
    .string "unto the battle; and they fled\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_15::
    .string "And when the children of Ammon saw\n"
    .string "that the Syrians were fled, they\l"
    .string "likewise fled before Abishai his\l"
    .string "brother, and entered into the city.\l"
    .string "Then Joab came to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_16::
    .string "And when the Syrians saw that they\n"
    .string "were put to the worse before Israel,\l"
    .string "they sent messengers, and drew forth\l"
    .string "the Syrians that were beyond the\l"
    .string "river: and Shophach the captain of\l"
    .string "the host of Hadarezer went before\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_17::
    .string "And it was told David; and he\n"
    .string "gathered all Israel, and passed\l"
    .string "over Jordan, and came upon them, and\l"
    .string "set the battle in array against\l"
    .string "them. So when David had put the\l"
    .string "battle in array against the Syrians,\l"
    .string "they fought with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_18::
    .string "But the Syrians fled before\n"
    .string "Israel; and David slew of the\l"
    .string "Syrians seven thousand men which\l"
    .string "fought in chariots, and forty\l"
    .string "thousand footmen, and killed\l"
    .string "Shophach the captain of the host.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_19_19::
    .string "And when the servants of Hadarezer\n"
    .string "saw that they were put to the worse\l"
    .string "before Israel, they made peace with\l"
    .string "David, and became his servants:\l"
    .string "neither would the Syrians help the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon any more.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that after the\n"
    .string "year was expired, at the time that\l"
    .string "kings go out to battle, Joab led\l"
    .string "forth the power of the army, and\l"
    .string "wasted the country of the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon, and came and besieged Rabbah\l"
    .string " But David tarried at Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And Joab smote Rabbah, and destroyed\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_2::
    .string "And David took the crown of their\n"
    .string "king from off his head, and found it\l"
    .string "to weigh a talent of gold, and there\l"
    .string "were precious stones in it; and it\l"
    .string "was set upon David’s head: and he\l"
    .string "brought also exceeding much spoil\l"
    .string "out of the city.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_3::
    .string "And he brought out the people that\n"
    .string "were in it, and cut them with saws,\l"
    .string "and with harrows of iron, and with\l"
    .string "axes. Even so dealt David with all\l"
    .string "the cities of the children of Ammon.\l"
    .string "And David and all the people\l"
    .string "returned to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_4::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "there arose war at Gezer with the\l"
    .string "Philistines; at which time Sibbechai\l"
    .string "the Hushathite slew Sippai, that\l"
    .string "was of the children of the giant: and\l"
    .string "they were subdued.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_5::
    .string "And there was war again with the\n"
    .string "Philistines; and Elhanan the son of\l"
    .string "Jair slew Lahmi the brother of\l"
    .string "Goliath the Gittite, whose spear\l"
    .string "staff was like a weaver’s beam.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_6::
    .string "And yet again there was war at Gath,\n"
    .string "where was a man of great stature,\l"
    .string "whose fingers and toes were four and\l"
    .string "twenty, six on each hand, and six on\l"
    .string "each foot and he also was the son of\l"
    .string "the giant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_7::
    .string "But when he defied Israel, Jonathan\n"
    .string "the son of Shimea David’s brother\l"
    .string "slew him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_20_8::
    .string "These were born unto the giant in\n"
    .string "Gath; and they fell by the hand of\l"
    .string "David, and by the hand of his\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_1::
    .string "And Satan stood up against Israel,\n"
    .string "and provoked David to number Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_2::
    .string "And David said to Joab and to the\n"
    .string "rulers of the people, Go, number\l"
    .string "Israel from Beersheba even to Dan;\l"
    .string "and bring the number of them to me,\l"
    .string "that I may know it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_3::
    .string "And Joab answered, The LORD make his\n"
    .string "people an hundred times so many\l"
    .string "more as they be: but, my lord the\l"
    .string "king, are they not all my lord’s\l"
    .string "servants? why then doth my lord\l"
    .string "require this thing? why will he be a\l"
    .string "cause of trespass to Israel?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_4::
    .string "Nevertheless the king’s word\n"
    .string "prevailed against Joab. Wherefore\l"
    .string "Joab departed, and went throughout\l"
    .string "all Israel, and came to Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_5::
    .string "And Joab gave the sum of the number\n"
    .string "of the people unto David. And all\l"
    .string "they of Israel were a thousand\l"
    .string "thousand and an hundred thousand men\l"
    .string "that drew sword: and Judah was four\l"
    .string "hundred threescore and ten thousand\l"
    .string "men that drew sword.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_6::
    .string "But Levi and Benjamin counted he not\n"
    .string "among them: for the king’s word was\l"
    .string "abominable to Joab.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_7::
    .string "And God was displeased with this\n"
    .string "thing; therefore he smote Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_8::
    .string "And David said unto God, I have\n"
    .string "sinned greatly, because I have done\l"
    .string "this thing: but now, I beseech thee,\l"
    .string "do away the iniquity of thy servant;\l"
    .string "for I have done very foolishly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_9::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto Gad,\n"
    .string "David’s seer, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_10::
    .string "Go and tell David, saying, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, I offer thee three\l"
    .string "things: choose thee one of them, that\l"
    .string "I may do it unto thee$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_11::
    .string "So Gad came to David, and said unto\n"
    .string "him, Thus saith the LORD, Choose thee"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_12::
    .string "Either three years’ famine; or three\n"
    .string "months to be destroyed before thy\l"
    .string "foes, while that the sword of thine\l"
    .string "enemies overtaketh thee; or else\l"
    .string "three days the sword of the LORD,\l"
    .string "even the pestilence, in the land,\l"
    .string "and the angel of the LORD destroying\l"
    .string "throughout all the coasts of Israel\l"
    .string " Now therefore advise thyself what\l"
    .string "word I shall bring again to him that\l"
    .string "sent me$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_13::
    .string "And David said unto Gad, I am in a\n"
    .string "great strait: let me fall now into\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD; for very great\l"
    .string "are his mercies: but let me not\l"
    .string "fall into the hand of man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_14::
    .string "So the LORD sent pestilence upon\n"
    .string "Israel: and there fell of Israel\l"
    .string "seventy thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_15::
    .string "And God sent an angel unto\n"
    .string "Jerusalem to destroy it: and as he\l"
    .string "was destroying, the LORD beheld, and\l"
    .string "he repented him of the evil, and\l"
    .string "said to the angel that destroyed, It\l"
    .string "is enough, stay now thine hand. And\l"
    .string "the angel of the LORD stood by the\l"
    .string "threshingfloor of Ornan the\l"
    .string "Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_16::
    .string "And David lifted up his eyes, and\n"
    .string "saw the angel of the LORD stand\l"
    .string "between the earth and the heaven,\l"
    .string "having a drawn sword in his hand\l"
    .string "stretched out over Jerusalem. Then\l"
    .string "David and the elders of Israel, who\l"
    .string "were clothed in sackcloth, fell\l"
    .string "upon their faces.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_17::
    .string "And David said unto God, Is it not I\n"
    .string "that commanded the people to be\l"
    .string "numbered? even I it is that have\l"
    .string "sinned and done evil indeed; but as\l"
    .string "for these sheep, what have they\l"
    .string "done? let thine hand, I pray thee, O\l"
    .string "LORD my God, be on me, and on my\l"
    .string "father’s house; but not on thy\l"
    .string "people, that they should be\l"
    .string "plagued.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_18::
    .string "Then the angel of the LORD\n"
    .string "commanded Gad to say to David, that\l"
    .string "David should go up, and set up an\l"
    .string "altar unto the LORD in the\l"
    .string "threshingfloor of Ornan the\l"
    .string "Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_19::
    .string "And David went up at the saying of\n"
    .string "Gad, which he spake in the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_20::
    .string "And Ornan turned back, and saw the\n"
    .string "angel; and his four sons with him hid\l"
    .string "themselves. Now Ornan was threshing\l"
    .string "wheat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_21::
    .string "And as David came to Ornan, Ornan\n"
    .string "looked and saw David, and went out of\l"
    .string "the threshingfloor, and bowed\l"
    .string "himself to David with his face to\l"
    .string "the ground.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_22::
    .string "Then David said to Ornan, Grant me\n"
    .string "the place of this threshingfloor,\l"
    .string "that I may build an altar therein\l"
    .string "unto the LORD: thou shalt grant it me\l"
    .string "for the full price: that the\l"
    .string "plague may be stayed from the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_23::
    .string "And Ornan said unto David, Take it\n"
    .string "to thee, and let my lord the king do\l"
    .string "that which is good in his eyes: lo, I\l"
    .string "give thee the oxen also for burnt\l"
    .string "offerings, and the threshing\l"
    .string "instruments for wood, and the wheat\l"
    .string "for the meat offering; I give it all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_24::
    .string "And king David said to Ornan, Nay;\n"
    .string "but I will verily buy it for the\l"
    .string "full price: for I will not take\l"
    .string "that which is thine for the LORD, nor\l"
    .string "offer burnt offerings without cost.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_25::
    .string "So David gave to Ornan for the\n"
    .string "place six hundred shekels of gold\l"
    .string "by weight.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_26::
    .string "And David built there an altar\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, and offered burnt\l"
    .string "offerings and peace offerings, and\l"
    .string "called upon the LORD; and he\l"
    .string "answered him from heaven by fire\l"
    .string "upon the altar of burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_27::
    .string "And the LORD commanded the angel;\n"
    .string "and he put up his sword again into\l"
    .string "the sheath thereof.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_28::
    .string "At that time when David saw that the\n"
    .string "LORD had answered him in the\l"
    .string "threshingfloor of Ornan the\l"
    .string "Jebusite, then he sacrificed there.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_29::
    .string "For the tabernacle of the LORD,\n"
    .string "which Moses made in the wilderness,\l"
    .string "and the altar of the burnt offering,\l"
    .string "were at that season in the high\l"
    .string "place at Gibeon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_21_30::
    .string "But David could not go before it to\n"
    .string "enquire of God: for he was afraid\l"
    .string "because of the sword of the angel of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_1::
    .string "Then David said, This is the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD God, and this is the\l"
    .string "altar of the burnt offering for\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_2::
    .string "And David commanded to gather\n"
    .string "together the strangers that were in\l"
    .string "the land of Israel; and he set\l"
    .string "masons to hew wrought stones to\l"
    .string "build the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_3::
    .string "And David prepared iron in\n"
    .string "abundance for the nails for the\l"
    .string "doors of the gates, and for the\l"
    .string "joinings; and brass in abundance\l"
    .string "without weight;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_4::
    .string "Also cedar trees in abundance: for\n"
    .string "the Zidonians and they of Tyre\l"
    .string "brought much cedar wood to David$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_5::
    .string "And David said, Solomon my son is\n"
    .string "young and tender, and the house that\l"
    .string "is to be builded for the LORD must be\l"
    .string "exceeding magnifical, of fame and of\l"
    .string "glory throughout all countries: I\l"
    .string "will therefore now make\l"
    .string "preparation for it. So David\l"
    .string "prepared abundantly before his\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_6::
    .string "Then he called for Solomon his\n"
    .string "son, and charged him to build an\l"
    .string "house for the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_7::
    .string "And David said to Solomon, My son,\n"
    .string "as for me, it was in my mind to build\l"
    .string "an house unto the name of the LORD my\l"
    .string "God:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_8::
    .string "But the word of the LORD came to me,\n"
    .string "saying, Thou hast shed blood\l"
    .string "abundantly, and hast made great\l"
    .string "wars: thou shalt not build an house\l"
    .string "unto my name, because thou hast shed\l"
    .string "much blood upon the earth in my\l"
    .string "sight$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_9::
    .string "Behold, a son shall be born to\n"
    .string "thee, who shall be a man of rest;\l"
    .string "and I will give him rest from all\l"
    .string "his enemies round about: for his name\l"
    .string "shall be Solomon, and I will give\l"
    .string "peace and quietness unto Israel in\l"
    .string "his days.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_10::
    .string "He shall build an house for my\n"
    .string "name; and he shall be my son, and I\l"
    .string "will be his father; and I will\l"
    .string "establish the throne of his kingdom\l"
    .string "over Israel for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_11::
    .string "Now, my son, the LORD be with thee;\n"
    .string "and prosper thou, and build the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD thy God, as he hath\l"
    .string "said of thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_12::
    .string "Only the LORD give thee wisdom and\n"
    .string "understanding, and give thee charge\l"
    .string "concerning Israel, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "keep the law of the LORD thy God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_13::
    .string "Then shalt thou prosper, if thou\n"
    .string "takest heed to fulfil the statutes\l"
    .string "and judgments which the LORD charged\l"
    .string "Moses with concerning Israel: be\l"
    .string "strong, and of good courage; dread\l"
    .string "not, nor be dismayed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_14::
    .string "Now, behold, in my trouble I have\n"
    .string "prepared for the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "an hundred thousand talents of\l"
    .string "gold, and a thousand thousand\l"
    .string "talents of silver; and of brass and\l"
    .string "iron without weight; for it is in\l"
    .string "abundance: timber also and stone\l"
    .string "have I prepared; and thou mayest add\l"
    .string "thereto.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_15::
    .string "Moreover there are workmen with\n"
    .string "thee in abundance, hewers and workers\l"
    .string "of stone and timber, and all manner\l"
    .string "of cunning men for every manner of\l"
    .string "work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_16::
    .string "Of the gold, the silver, and the\n"
    .string "brass, and the iron, there is no\l"
    .string "number. Arise therefore, and be\l"
    .string "doing, and the LORD be with thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_17::
    .string "David also commanded all the\n"
    .string "princes of Israel to help Solomon\l"
    .string "his son, saying,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_18::
    .string "Is not the LORD your God with you?\n"
    .string "and hath he not given you rest on\l"
    .string "every side? for he hath given the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land into mine\l"
    .string "hand; and the land is subdued before\l"
    .string "the LORD, and before his people$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_22_19::
    .string "Now set your heart and your soul to\n"
    .string "seek the LORD your God; arise\l"
    .string "therefore, and build ye the\l"
    .string "sanctuary of the LORD God, to bring\l"
    .string "the ark of the covenant of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the holy vessels of God, into\l"
    .string "the house that is to be built to the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_1::
    .string "So when David was old and full of\n"
    .string "days, he made Solomon his son king\l"
    .string "over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_2::
    .string "And he gathered together all the\n"
    .string "princes of Israel, with the priests\l"
    .string "and the Levites.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_3::
    .string "Now the Levites were numbered from\n"
    .string "the age of thirty years and upward:\l"
    .string "and their number by their polls,\l"
    .string "man by man, was thirty and eight\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_4::
    .string "Of which, twenty and four thousand\n"
    .string "were to set forward the work of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD; and six thousand\l"
    .string "were officers and judges:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_5::
    .string "Moreover four thousand were\n"
    .string "porters; and four thousand praised\l"
    .string "the LORD with the instruments which I\l"
    .string "made, said David, to praise therewith$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_6::
    .string "And David divided them into courses\n"
    .string "among the sons of Levi, namely,\l"
    .string "Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_7::
    .string "Of the Gershonites were, Laadan, and\n"
    .string "Shimei.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_8::
    .string "The sons of Laadan; the chief was\n"
    .string "Jehiel, and Zetham, and Joel, three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_9::
    .string "The sons of Shimei; Shelomith, and\n"
    .string "Haziel, and Haran, three. These were\l"
    .string "the chief of the fathers of Laadan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_10::
    .string "And the sons of Shimei were, Jahath,\n"
    .string "Zina, and Jeush, and Beriah. These\l"
    .string "four were the sons of Shimei.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_11::
    .string "And Jahath was the chief, and Zizah\n"
    .string "the second: but Jeush and Beriah had\l"
    .string "not many sons; therefore they were in\l"
    .string "one reckoning, according to their\l"
    .string "father’s house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_12::
    .string "The sons of Kohath; Amram, Izhar,\n"
    .string "Hebron, and Uzziel, four.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_13::
    .string "The sons of Amram; Aaron and Moses:\n"
    .string "and Aaron was separated, that he\l"
    .string "should sanctify the most holy\l"
    .string "things, he and his sons for ever, to\l"
    .string "burn incense before the LORD, to\l"
    .string "minister unto him, and to bless in\l"
    .string "his name for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_14::
    .string "Now concerning Moses the man of God,\n"
    .string "his sons were named of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Levi.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_15::
    .string "The sons of Moses were, Gershom, and\n"
    .string "Eliezer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_16::
    .string "Of the sons of Gershom, Shebuel was\n"
    .string "the chief.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_17::
    .string "And the sons of Eliezer were,\n"
    .string "Rehabiah the chief. And Eliezer had\l"
    .string "none other sons; but the sons of\l"
    .string "Rehabiah were very many.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_18::
    .string "Of the sons of Izhar; Shelomith the\n"
    .string "chief.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_19::
    .string "Of the sons of Hebron; Jeriah the\n"
    .string "first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel\l"
    .string "the third, and Jekameam the fourth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_20::
    .string "Of the sons of Uzziel; Micah the\n"
    .string "first and Jesiah the second.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_21::
    .string "The sons of Merari; Mahli, and Mushi\n"
    .string " The sons of Mahli; Eleazar, and\l"
    .string "Kish.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_22::
    .string "And Eleazar died, and had no sons,\n"
    .string "but daughters: and their brethren the\l"
    .string "sons of Kish took them.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_23::
    .string "The sons of Mushi; Mahli, and Eder,\n"
    .string "and Jeremoth, three.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_24::
    .string "These were the sons of Levi after\n"
    .string "the house of their fathers; even the\l"
    .string "chief of the fathers, as they were\l"
    .string "counted by number of names by their\l"
    .string "polls, that did the work for the\l"
    .string "service of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "from the age of twenty years and\l"
    .string "upward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_25::
    .string "For David said, The LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel hath given rest unto his\l"
    .string "people, that they may dwell in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem for ever:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_26::
    .string "And also unto the Levites; they\n"
    .string "shall no more carry the tabernacle,\l"
    .string "nor any vessels of it for the\l"
    .string "service thereof$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_27::
    .string "For by the last words of David the\n"
    .string "Levites were numbered from twenty\l"
    .string "years old and above:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_28::
    .string "Because their office was to wait on\n"
    .string "the sons of Aaron for the service of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, in the courts,\l"
    .string "and in the chambers, and in the\l"
    .string "purifying of all holy things, and\l"
    .string "the work of the service of the house\l"
    .string "of God;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_29::
    .string "Both for the shewbread, and for the\n"
    .string "fine flour for meat offering, and\l"
    .string "for the unleavened cakes, and for\l"
    .string "that which is baked in the pan, and\l"
    .string "for that which is fried, and for all\l"
    .string "manner of measure and size;"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_30::
    .string "And to stand every morning to thank\n"
    .string "and praise the LORD, and likewise at\l"
    .string "even:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_31::
    .string "And to offer all burnt sacrifices\n"
    .string "unto the LORD in the sabbaths, in the\l"
    .string "new moons, and on the set feasts, by\l"
    .string "number, according to the order\l"
    .string "commanded unto them, continually\l"
    .string "before the LORD:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_23_32::
    .string "And that they should keep the\n"
    .string "charge of the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and the charge of the\l"
    .string "holy place, and the charge of the\l"
    .string "sons of Aaron their brethren, in the\l"
    .string "service of the house of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_1::
    .string "Now these are the divisions of the\n"
    .string "sons of Aaron. The sons of Aaron;\l"
    .string "Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar, and\l"
    .string "Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_2::
    .string "But Nadab and Abihu died before\n"
    .string "their father, and had no children:\l"
    .string "therefore Eleazar and Ithamar\l"
    .string "executed the priest’s office.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_3::
    .string "And David distributed them, both\n"
    .string "Zadok of the sons of Eleazar, and\l"
    .string "Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar,\l"
    .string "according to their offices in their\l"
    .string "service.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_4::
    .string "And there were more chief men found\n"
    .string "of the sons of Eleazar than of the\l"
    .string "sons of Ithamar, and thus were they\l"
    .string "divided. Among the sons of Eleazar\l"
    .string "there were sixteen chief men of the\l"
    .string "house of their fathers, and eight\l"
    .string "among the sons of Ithamar according\l"
    .string "to the house of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_5::
    .string "Thus were they divided by lot, one\n"
    .string "sort with another; for the governors\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary, and governors of\l"
    .string "the house of God, were of the sons of\l"
    .string "Eleazar, and of the sons of Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_6::
    .string "And Shemaiah the son of Nethaneel\n"
    .string "the scribe, one of the Levites, wrote\l"
    .string "them before the king, and the\l"
    .string "princes, and Zadok the priest, and\l"
    .string "Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, and\l"
    .string "before the chief of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the priests and Levites: one\l"
    .string "principal household being taken\l"
    .string "for Eleazar, and one taken for\l"
    .string "Ithamar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_7::
    .string "Now the first lot came forth to\n"
    .string "Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_8::
    .string "The third to Harim, the fourth to\n"
    .string "Seorim,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_9::
    .string "The fifth to Malchijah, the sixth\n"
    .string "to Mijamin,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_10::
    .string "The seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to\n"
    .string "Abijah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_11::
    .string "The ninth to Jeshuah, the tenth to\n"
    .string "Shecaniah,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_12::
    .string "The eleventh to Eliashib, the\n"
    .string "twelfth to Jakim,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_13::
    .string "The thirteenth to Huppah, the\n"
    .string "fourteenth to Jeshebeab,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_14::
    .string "The fifteenth to Bilgah, the\n"
    .string "sixteenth to Immer,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_15::
    .string "The seventeenth to Hezir, the\n"
    .string "eighteenth to Aphses,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_16::
    .string "The nineteenth to Pethahiah, the\n"
    .string "twentieth to Jehezekel,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_17::
    .string "The one and twentieth to Jachin, the\n"
    .string "two and twentieth to Gamul,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_18::
    .string "The three and twentieth to Delaiah,\n"
    .string "the four and twentieth to Maaziah$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_19::
    .string "These were the orderings of them in\n"
    .string "their service to come into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, according to their\l"
    .string "manner, under Aaron their father, as\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel had commanded\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_20::
    .string "And the rest of the sons of Levi\n"
    .string "were these: Of the sons of Amram;\l"
    .string "Shubael: of the sons of Shubael;\l"
    .string "Jehdeiah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_21::
    .string "Concerning Rehabiah: of the sons of\n"
    .string "Rehabiah, the first was Isshiah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_22::
    .string "Of the Izharites; Shelomoth: of the\n"
    .string "sons of Shelomoth; Jahath.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_23::
    .string "And the sons of Hebron; Jeriah the\n"
    .string "first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel\l"
    .string "the third, Jekameam the fourth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_24::
    .string "Of the sons of Uzziel; Michah: of\n"
    .string "the sons of Michah; Shamir.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_25::
    .string "The brother of Michah was Isshiah:\n"
    .string "of the sons of Isshiah; Zechariah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_26::
    .string "The sons of Merari were Mahli and\n"
    .string "Mushi: the sons of Jaaziah; Beno.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_27::
    .string "The sons of Merari by Jaaziah; Beno,\n"
    .string "and Shoham, and Zaccur, and Ibri.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_28::
    .string "Of Mahli came Eleazar, who had no\n"
    .string "sons.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_29::
    .string "Concerning Kish: the son of Kish was\n"
    .string "Jerahmeel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_30::
    .string "The sons also of Mushi; Mahli, and\n"
    .string "Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the\l"
    .string "sons of the Levites after the house\l"
    .string "of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_24_31::
    .string "These likewise cast lots over\n"
    .string "against their brethren the sons of\l"
    .string "Aaron in the presence of David the\l"
    .string "king, and Zadok, and Ahimelech, and\l"
    .string "the chief of the fathers of the\l"
    .string "priests and Levites, even the\l"
    .string "principal fathers over against\l"
    .string "their younger brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_1::
    .string "Moreover David and the captains of\n"
    .string "the host separated to the service of\l"
    .string "the sons of Asaph, and of Heman, and\l"
    .string "of Jeduthun, who should prophesy\l"
    .string "with harps, with psalteries, and\l"
    .string "with cymbals: and the number of the\l"
    .string "workmen according to their service\l"
    .string "was:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_2::
    .string "Of the sons of Asaph; Zaccur, and\n"
    .string "Joseph, and Nethaniah, and\l"
    .string "Asarelah, the sons of Asaph under\l"
    .string "the hands of Asaph, which\l"
    .string "prophesied according to the order of\l"
    .string "the king$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_3::
    .string "Of Jeduthun: the sons of Jeduthun;\n"
    .string "Gedaliah, and Zeri, and Jeshaiah,\l"
    .string "Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six, under\l"
    .string "the hands of their father Jeduthun,\l"
    .string "who prophesied with a harp, to give\l"
    .string "thanks and to praise the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_4::
    .string "Of Heman: the sons of Heman:\n"
    .string "Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel,\l"
    .string "Shebuel, and Jerimoth, Hananiah,\l"
    .string "Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, and\l"
    .string "Romamtiezer, Joshbekashah,\l"
    .string "Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_5::
    .string "All these were the sons of Heman\n"
    .string "the king’s seer in the words of God,\l"
    .string "to lift up the horn. And God gave to\l"
    .string "Heman fourteen sons and three\l"
    .string "daughters$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_6::
    .string "All these were under the hands of\n"
    .string "their father for song in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, with cymbals, psalteries,\l"
    .string "and harps, for the service of the\l"
    .string "house of God, according to the king’s\l"
    .string "order to Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_7::
    .string "So the number of them, with their\n"
    .string "brethren that were instructed in the\l"
    .string "songs of the LORD, even all that\l"
    .string "were cunning, was two hundred\l"
    .string "fourscore and eight.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_8::
    .string "And they cast lots, ward against\n"
    .string "ward, as well the small as the\l"
    .string "great, the teacher as the scholar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_9::
    .string "Now the first lot came forth for\n"
    .string "Asaph to Joseph: the second to\l"
    .string "Gedaliah, who with his brethren and\l"
    .string "sons were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_10::
    .string "The third to Zaccur, he, his sons,\n"
    .string "and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_11::
    .string "The fourth to Izri, he, his sons, and\n"
    .string "his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_12::
    .string "The fifth to Nethaniah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_13::
    .string "The sixth to Bukkiah, he, his sons,\n"
    .string "and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_14::
    .string "The seventh to Jesharelah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_15::
    .string "The eighth to Jeshaiah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_16::
    .string "The ninth to Mattaniah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_17::
    .string "The tenth to Shimei, he, his sons,\n"
    .string "and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_18::
    .string "The eleventh to Azareel, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_19::
    .string "The twelfth to Hashabiah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_20::
    .string "The thirteenth to Shubael, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_21::
    .string "The fourteenth to Mattithiah, he,\n"
    .string "his sons, and his brethren, were\l"
    .string "twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_22::
    .string "The fifteenth to Jeremoth, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_23::
    .string "The sixteenth to Hananiah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_24::
    .string "The seventeenth to Joshbekashah,\n"
    .string "he, his sons, and his brethren, were\l"
    .string "twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_25::
    .string "The eighteenth to Hanani, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_26::
    .string "The nineteenth to Mallothi, he,\n"
    .string "his sons, and his brethren, were\l"
    .string "twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_27::
    .string "The twentieth to Eliathah, he, his\n"
    .string "sons, and his brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_28::
    .string "The one and twentieth to Hothir, he,\n"
    .string "his sons, and his brethren, were\l"
    .string "twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_29::
    .string "The two and twentieth to Giddalti,\n"
    .string "he, his sons, and his brethren, were\l"
    .string "twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_30::
    .string "The three and twentieth to\n"
    .string "Mahazioth, he, his sons, and his\l"
    .string "brethren, were twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_25_31::
    .string "The four and twentieth to\n"
    .string "Romamtiezer, he, his sons, and his\l"
    .string "brethren, were twelve$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_1::
    .string "Concerning the divisions of the\n"
    .string "porters: Of the Korhites was\l"
    .string "Meshelemiah the son of Kore, of the\l"
    .string "sons of Asaph.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_2::
    .string "And the sons of Meshelemiah were,\n"
    .string "Zechariah the firstborn, Jediael the\l"
    .string "second, Zebadiah the third, Jathniel\l"
    .string "the fourth,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_3::
    .string "Elam the fifth, Jehohanan the\n"
    .string "sixth, Elioenai the seventh$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_4::
    .string "Moreover the sons of Obededom were,\n"
    .string "Shemaiah the firstborn, Jehozabad\l"
    .string "the second, Joah the third, and Sacar\l"
    .string "the fourth, and Nethaneel the fifth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_5::
    .string "Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the\n"
    .string "seventh, Peulthai the eighth: for\l"
    .string "God blessed him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_6::
    .string "Also unto Shemaiah his son were\n"
    .string "sons born, that ruled throughout the\l"
    .string "house of their father: for they were\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_7::
    .string "The sons of Shemaiah; Othni, and\n"
    .string "Rephael, and Obed, Elzabad, whose\l"
    .string "brethren were strong men, Elihu, and\l"
    .string "Semachiah.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_8::
    .string "All these of the sons of Obededom:\n"
    .string "they and their sons and their\l"
    .string "brethren, able men for strength for\l"
    .string "the service, were threescore and two\l"
    .string "of Obededom.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_9::
    .string "And Meshelemiah had sons and\n"
    .string "brethren, strong men, eighteen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_10::
    .string "Also Hosah, of the children of\n"
    .string "Merari, had sons; Simri the chief,\l"
    .string "(for though he was not the firstborn,\l"
    .string "yet his father made him the chief;)"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_11::
    .string "Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the\n"
    .string "third, Zechariah the fourth: all\l"
    .string "the sons and brethren of Hosah were\l"
    .string "thirteen$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_12::
    .string "Among these were the divisions of\n"
    .string "the porters, even among the chief\l"
    .string "men, having wards one against\l"
    .string "another, to minister in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_13::
    .string "And they cast lots, as well the\n"
    .string "small as the great, according to the\l"
    .string "house of their fathers, for every\l"
    .string "gate.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_14::
    .string "And the lot eastward fell to\n"
    .string "Shelemiah. Then for Zechariah his\l"
    .string "son, a wise counsellor, they cast\l"
    .string "lots; and his lot came out northward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_15::
    .string "To Obededom southward; and to his\n"
    .string "sons the house of Asuppim.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_16::
    .string "To Shuppim and Hosah the lot came\n"
    .string "forth westward, with the gate\l"
    .string "Shallecheth, by the causeway of the\l"
    .string "going up, ward against ward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_17::
    .string "Eastward were six Levites,\n"
    .string "northward four a day, southward four\l"
    .string "a day, and toward Asuppim two and\l"
    .string "two.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_18::
    .string "At Parbar westward, four at the\n"
    .string "causeway, and two at Parbar.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_19::
    .string "These are the divisions of the\n"
    .string "porters among the sons of Kore, and\l"
    .string "among the sons of Merari.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_20::
    .string "And of the Levites, Ahijah was over\n"
    .string "the treasures of the house of God,\l"
    .string "and over the treasures of the\l"
    .string "dedicated things.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_21::
    .string "As concerning the sons of Laadan;\n"
    .string "the sons of the Gershonite Laadan,\l"
    .string "chief fathers, even of Laadan the\l"
    .string "Gershonite, were Jehieli.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_22::
    .string "The sons of Jehieli; Zetham, and\n"
    .string "Joel his brother, which were over\l"
    .string "the treasures of the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_23::
    .string "Of the Amramites, and the Izharites,\n"
    .string "the Hebronites, and the Uzzielites:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_24::
    .string "And Shebuel the son of Gershom, the\n"
    .string "son of Moses, was ruler of the\l"
    .string "treasures$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_25::
    .string "And his brethren by Eliezer;\n"
    .string "Rehabiah his son, and Jeshaiah his\l"
    .string "son, and Joram his son, and Zichri\l"
    .string "his son, and Shelomith his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_26::
    .string "Which Shelomith and his brethren\n"
    .string "were over all the treasures of the\l"
    .string "dedicated things, which David the\l"
    .string "king, and the chief fathers, the\l"
    .string "captains over thousands and\l"
    .string "hundreds, and the captains of the\l"
    .string "host, had dedicated.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_27::
    .string "Out of the spoils won in battles\n"
    .string "did they dedicate to maintain the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_28::
    .string "And all that Samuel the seer, and\n"
    .string "Saul the son of Kish, and Abner the\l"
    .string "son of Ner, and Joab the son of\l"
    .string "Zeruiah, had dedicated; and\l"
    .string "whosoever had dedicated any thing, it\l"
    .string "was under the hand of Shelomith, and\l"
    .string "of his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_29::
    .string "Of the Izharites, Chenaniah and his\n"
    .string "sons were for the outward business\l"
    .string "over Israel, for officers and judges.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_30::
    .string "And of the Hebronites, Hashabiah and\n"
    .string "his brethren, men of valour, a\l"
    .string "thousand and seven hundred, were\l"
    .string "officers among them of Israel on\l"
    .string "this side Jordan westward in all\l"
    .string "the business of the LORD, and in the\l"
    .string "service of the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_31::
    .string "Among the Hebronites was Jerijah\n"
    .string "the chief, even among the Hebronites,\l"
    .string "according to the generations of his\l"
    .string "fathers. In the fortieth year of the\l"
    .string "reign of David they were sought for,\l"
    .string "and there were found among them\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour at Jazer of\l"
    .string "Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_26_32::
    .string "And his brethren, men of valour,\n"
    .string "were two thousand and seven hundred\l"
    .string "chief fathers, whom king David made\l"
    .string "rulers over the Reubenites, the\l"
    .string "Gadites, and the half tribe of\l"
    .string "Manasseh, for every matter\l"
    .string "pertaining to God, and affairs of the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_1::
    .string "Now the children of Israel after\n"
    .string "their number, to wit, the chief\l"
    .string "fathers and captains of thousands\l"
    .string "and hundreds, and their officers that\l"
    .string "served the king in any matter of the\l"
    .string "courses, which came in and went out\l"
    .string "month by month throughout all the\l"
    .string "months of the year, of every course\l"
    .string "were twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_2::
    .string "Over the first course for the first\n"
    .string "month was Jashobeam the son of\l"
    .string "Zabdiel: and in his course were\l"
    .string "twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_3::
    .string "Of the children of Perez was the\n"
    .string "chief of all the captains of the\l"
    .string "host for the first month.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_4::
    .string "And over the course of the second\n"
    .string "month was Dodai an Ahohite, and of\l"
    .string "his course was Mikloth also the\l"
    .string "ruler: in his course likewise were\l"
    .string "twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_5::
    .string "The third captain of the host for\n"
    .string "the third month was Benaiah the son\l"
    .string "of Jehoiada, a chief priest: and in\l"
    .string "his course were twenty and four\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_6::
    .string "This is that Benaiah, who was mighty\n"
    .string "among the thirty, and above the\l"
    .string "thirty: and in his course was\l"
    .string "Ammizabad his son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_7::
    .string "The fourth captain for the fourth\n"
    .string "month was Asahel the brother of\l"
    .string "Joab, and Zebadiah his son after him:\l"
    .string "and in his course were twenty and\l"
    .string "four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_8::
    .string "The fifth captain for the fifth\n"
    .string "month was Shamhuth the Izrahite: and\l"
    .string "in his course were twenty and four\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_9::
    .string "The sixth captain for the sixth\n"
    .string "month was Ira the son of Ikkesh the\l"
    .string "Tekoite: and in his course were\l"
    .string "twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_10::
    .string "The seventh captain for the seventh\n"
    .string "month was Helez the Pelonite, of the\l"
    .string "children of Ephraim: and in his\l"
    .string "course were twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_11::
    .string "The eighth captain for the eighth\n"
    .string "month was Sibbecai the Hushathite, of\l"
    .string "the Zarhites: and in his course were\l"
    .string "twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_12::
    .string "The ninth captain for the ninth\n"
    .string "month was Abiezer the Anetothite, of\l"
    .string "the Benjamites: and in his course\l"
    .string "were twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_13::
    .string "The tenth captain for the tenth\n"
    .string "month was Maharai the Netophathite,\l"
    .string "of the Zarhites: and in his course\l"
    .string "were twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_14::
    .string "The eleventh captain for the\n"
    .string "eleventh month was Benaiah the\l"
    .string "Pirathonite, of the children of\l"
    .string "Ephraim: and in his course were\l"
    .string "twenty and four thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_15::
    .string "The twelfth captain for the\n"
    .string "twelfth month was Heldai the\l"
    .string "Netophathite, of Othniel: and in\l"
    .string "his course were twenty and four\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_16::
    .string "Furthermore over the tribes of\n"
    .string "Israel: the ruler of the Reubenites\l"
    .string "was Eliezer the son of Zichri: of the\l"
    .string "Simeonites, Shephatiah the son of\l"
    .string "Maachah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_17::
    .string "Of the Levites, Hashabiah the son of\n"
    .string "Kemuel: of the Aaronites, Zadok:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_18::
    .string "Of Judah, Elihu, one of the\n"
    .string "brethren of David: of Issachar, Omri\l"
    .string "the son of Michael:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_19::
    .string "Of Zebulun, Ishmaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Obadiah: of Naphtali, Jerimoth the\l"
    .string "son of Azriel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_20::
    .string "Of the children of Ephraim, Hoshea\n"
    .string "the son of Azaziah: of the half tribe\l"
    .string "of Manasseh, Joel the son of\l"
    .string "Pedaiah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_21::
    .string "Of the half tribe of Manasseh in\n"
    .string "Gilead, Iddo the son of Zechariah:\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, Jaasiel the son of\l"
    .string "Abner:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_22::
    .string "Of Dan, Azareel the son of Jeroham.\n"
    .string "These were the princes of the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_23::
    .string "But David took not the number of\n"
    .string "them from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "under: because the LORD had said he\l"
    .string "would increase Israel like to the\l"
    .string "stars of the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_24::
    .string "Joab the son of Zeruiah began to\n"
    .string "number, but he finished not, because\l"
    .string "there fell wrath for it against\l"
    .string "Israel; neither was the number put\l"
    .string "in the account of the chronicles of\l"
    .string "king David.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_25::
    .string "And over the king’s treasures was\n"
    .string "Azmaveth the son of Adiel: and over\l"
    .string "the storehouses in the fields, in\l"
    .string "the cities, and in the villages, and\l"
    .string "in the castles, was Jehonathan the\l"
    .string "son of Uzziah:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_26::
    .string "And over them that did the work of\n"
    .string "the field for tillage of the ground\l"
    .string "was Ezri the son of Chelub:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_27::
    .string "And over the vineyards was Shimei\n"
    .string "the Ramathite: over the increase of\l"
    .string "the vineyards for the wine cellars\l"
    .string "was Zabdi the Shiphmite:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_28::
    .string "And over the olive trees and the\n"
    .string "sycomore trees that were in the low\l"
    .string "plains was Baalhanan the Gederite:\l"
    .string "and over the cellars of oil was\l"
    .string "Joash:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_29::
    .string "And over the herds that fed in\n"
    .string "Sharon was Shitrai the Sharonite: and\l"
    .string "over the herds that were in the\l"
    .string "valleys was Shaphat the son of\l"
    .string "Adlai:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_30::
    .string "Over the camels also was Obil the\n"
    .string "Ishmaelite: and over the asses was\l"
    .string "Jehdeiah the Meronothite:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_31::
    .string "And over the flocks was Jaziz the\n"
    .string "Hagerite. All these were the rulers\l"
    .string "of the substance which was king\l"
    .string "David’s$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_32::
    .string "Also Jonathan David’s uncle was a\n"
    .string "counsellor, a wise man, and a\l"
    .string "scribe: and Jehiel the son of\l"
    .string "Hachmoni was with the king’s sons:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_33::
    .string "And Ahithophel was the king’s\n"
    .string "counsellor: and Hushai the Archite\l"
    .string "was the king’s companion:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_27_34::
    .string "And after Ahithophel was Jehoiada\n"
    .string "the son of Benaiah, and Abiathar: and\l"
    .string "the general of the king’s army was\l"
    .string "Joab$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_1::
    .string "And David assembled all the\n"
    .string "princes of Israel, the princes of\l"
    .string "the tribes, and the captains of the\l"
    .string "companies that ministered to the\l"
    .string "king by course, and the captains\l"
    .string "over the thousands, and captains\l"
    .string "over the hundreds, and the stewards\l"
    .string "over all the substance and\l"
    .string "possession of the king, and of his\l"
    .string "sons, with the officers, and with the\l"
    .string "mighty men, and with all the\l"
    .string "valiant men, unto Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_2::
    .string "Then David the king stood up upon\n"
    .string "his feet, and said, Hear me, my\l"
    .string "brethren, and my people: As for me,\l"
    .string "I had in mine heart to build an house\l"
    .string "of rest for the ark of the covenant\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and for the footstool of\l"
    .string "our God, and had made ready for the\l"
    .string "building:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_3::
    .string "But God said unto me, Thou shalt not\n"
    .string "build an house for my name, because\l"
    .string "thou hast been a man of war, and hast\l"
    .string "shed blood$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_4::
    .string "Howbeit the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "chose me before all the house of my\l"
    .string "father to be king over Israel for\l"
    .string "ever: for he hath chosen Judah to be\l"
    .string "the ruler; and of the house of Judah,\l"
    .string "the house of my father; and among the\l"
    .string "sons of my father he liked me to make\l"
    .string "me king over all Israel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_5::
    .string "And of all my sons, (for the LORD\n"
    .string "hath given me many sons,) he hath\l"
    .string "chosen Solomon my son to sit upon\l"
    .string "the throne of the kingdom of the LORD\l"
    .string "over Israel$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_6::
    .string "And he said unto me, Solomon thy\n"
    .string "son, he shall build my house and my\l"
    .string "courts: for I have chosen him to be my\l"
    .string "son, and I will be his father.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_7::
    .string "Moreover I will establish his\n"
    .string "kingdom for ever, if he be constant\l"
    .string "to do my commandments and my\l"
    .string "judgments, as at this day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_8::
    .string "Now therefore in the sight of all\n"
    .string "Israel the congregation of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and in the audience of our God, keep\l"
    .string "and seek for all the commandments\l"
    .string "of the LORD your God: that ye may\l"
    .string "possess this good land, and leave it\l"
    .string "for an inheritance for your children\l"
    .string "after you for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_9::
    .string "And thou, Solomon my son, know thou\n"
    .string "the God of thy father, and serve him\l"
    .string "with a perfect heart and with a\l"
    .string "willing mind: for the LORD\l"
    .string "searcheth all hearts, and\l"
    .string "understandeth all the imaginations\l"
    .string "of the thoughts: if thou seek him, he\l"
    .string "will be found of thee; but if thou\l"
    .string "forsake him, he will cast thee off\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_10::
    .string "Take heed now; for the LORD hath\n"
    .string "chosen thee to build an house for\l"
    .string "the sanctuary: be strong, and do it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_11::
    .string "Then David gave to Solomon his son\n"
    .string "the pattern of the porch, and of the\l"
    .string "houses thereof, and of the treasuries\l"
    .string "thereof, and of the upper chambers\l"
    .string "thereof, and of the inner parlours\l"
    .string "thereof, and of the place of the\l"
    .string "mercy seat,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_12::
    .string "And the pattern of all that he had\n"
    .string "by the spirit, of the courts of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and of all the\l"
    .string "chambers round about, of the\l"
    .string "treasuries of the house of God, and\l"
    .string "of the treasuries of the dedicated\l"
    .string "things:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_13::
    .string "Also for the courses of the\n"
    .string "priests and the Levites, and for all\l"
    .string "the work of the service of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and for all the\l"
    .string "vessels of service in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_14::
    .string "He gave of gold by weight for\n"
    .string "things of gold, for all instruments\l"
    .string "of all manner of service; silver\l"
    .string "also for all instruments of silver\l"
    .string "by weight, for all instruments of\l"
    .string "every kind of service:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_15::
    .string "Even the weight for the\n"
    .string "candlesticks of gold, and for their\l"
    .string "lamps of gold, by weight for every\l"
    .string "candlestick, and for the lamps\l"
    .string "thereof: and for the candlesticks of\l"
    .string "silver by weight, both for the\l"
    .string "candlestick, and also for the\l"
    .string "lamps thereof, according to the use\l"
    .string "of every candlestick$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_16::
    .string "And by weight he gave gold for the\n"
    .string "tables of shewbread, for every\l"
    .string "table; and likewise silver for the\l"
    .string "tables of silver:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_17::
    .string "Also pure gold for the\n"
    .string "fleshhooks, and the bowls, and the\l"
    .string "cups: and for the golden basons he\l"
    .string "gave gold by weight for every bason;\l"
    .string "and likewise silver by weight for\l"
    .string "every bason of silver:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_18::
    .string "And for the altar of incense\n"
    .string "refined gold by weight; and gold for\l"
    .string "the pattern of the chariot of the\l"
    .string "cherubims, that spread out their\l"
    .string "wings, and covered the ark of the\l"
    .string "covenant of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_19::
    .string "All this, said David, the LORD made\n"
    .string "me understand in writing by his hand\l"
    .string "upon me, even all the works of this\l"
    .string "pattern.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_20::
    .string "And David said to Solomon his son,\n"
    .string "Be strong and of good courage, and do\l"
    .string "it: fear not, nor be dismayed: for the\l"
    .string "LORD God, even my God, will be with\l"
    .string "thee; he will not fail thee, nor\l"
    .string "forsake thee, until thou hast\l"
    .string "finished all the work for the\l"
    .string "service of the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_28_21::
    .string "And, behold, the courses of the\n"
    .string "priests and the Levites, even they\l"
    .string "shall be with thee for all the\l"
    .string "service of the house of God: and\l"
    .string "there shall be with thee for all\l"
    .string "manner of workmanship every\l"
    .string "willing skilful man, for any\l"
    .string "manner of service: also the princes\l"
    .string "and all the people will be\l"
    .string "wholly at thy commandment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_1::
    .string "Furthermore David the king said\n"
    .string "unto all the congregation, Solomon\l"
    .string "my son, whom alone God hath chosen,\l"
    .string "is yet young and tender, and the work\l"
    .string "is great: for the palace is not for\l"
    .string "man, but for the LORD God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_2::
    .string "Now I have prepared with all my\n"
    .string "might for the house of my God the\l"
    .string "gold for things to be made of gold,\l"
    .string "and the silver for things of silver,\l"
    .string "and the brass for things of brass,\l"
    .string "the iron for things of iron, and wood\l"
    .string "for things of wood; onyx stones, and\l"
    .string "stones to be set, glistering stones,\l"
    .string "and of divers colours, and all\l"
    .string "manner of precious stones, and\l"
    .string "marble stones in abundance.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_3::
    .string "Moreover, because I have set my\n"
    .string "affection to the house of my God, I\l"
    .string "have of mine own proper good, of\l"
    .string "gold and silver, which I have given\l"
    .string "to the house of my God, over and above\l"
    .string "all that I have prepared for the\l"
    .string "holy house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_4::
    .string "Even three thousand talents of\n"
    .string "gold, of the gold of Ophir, and\l"
    .string "seven thousand talents of refined\l"
    .string "silver, to overlay the walls of\l"
    .string "the houses withal:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_5::
    .string "The gold for things of gold, and\n"
    .string "the silver for things of silver, and\l"
    .string "for all manner of work to be made by\l"
    .string "the hands of artificers. And who then\l"
    .string "is willing to consecrate his\l"
    .string "service this day unto the LORD?"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_6::
    .string "Then the chief of the fathers and\n"
    .string "princes of the tribes of Israel and\l"
    .string "the captains of thousands and of\l"
    .string "hundreds, with the rulers of the\l"
    .string "king’s work, offered willingly,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_7::
    .string "And gave for the service of the\n"
    .string "house of God of gold five thousand\l"
    .string "talents and ten thousand drams, and\l"
    .string "of silver ten thousand talents, and\l"
    .string "of brass eighteen thousand talents,\l"
    .string "and one hundred thousand talents of\l"
    .string "iron$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_8::
    .string "And they with whom precious stones\n"
    .string "were found gave them to the treasure\l"
    .string "of the house of the LORD, by the hand\l"
    .string "of Jehiel the Gershonite.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_9::
    .string "Then the people rejoiced, for that\n"
    .string "they offered willingly, because\l"
    .string "with perfect heart they offered\l"
    .string "willingly to the LORD: and David\l"
    .string "the king also rejoiced with great\l"
    .string "joy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_10::
    .string "Wherefore David blessed the LORD\n"
    .string "before all the congregation: and\l"
    .string "David said, Blessed be thou, LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel our father, for ever\l"
    .string "and ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_11::
    .string "Thine, O LORD is the greatness, and\n"
    .string "the power, and the glory, and the\l"
    .string "victory, and the majesty: for all\l"
    .string "that is in the heaven and in the\l"
    .string "earth is thine; thine is the kingdom,\l"
    .string "O LORD, and thou art exalted as head\l"
    .string "above all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_12::
    .string "Both riches and honour come of thee,\n"
    .string "and thou reignest over all; and in\l"
    .string "thine hand is power and might; and in\l"
    .string "thine hand it is to make great, and to\l"
    .string "give strength unto all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_13::
    .string "Now therefore, our God, we thank\n"
    .string "thee, and praise thy glorious name.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_14::
    .string "But who am I, and what is my\n"
    .string "people, that we should be able to\l"
    .string "offer so willingly after this sort?\l"
    .string "for all things come of thee, and of\l"
    .string "thine own have we given thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_15::
    .string "For we are strangers before thee,\n"
    .string "and sojourners, as were all our\l"
    .string "fathers: our days on the earth are as\l"
    .string "a shadow, and there is none abiding.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_16::
    .string "O LORD our God, all this store that\n"
    .string "we have prepared to build thee an\l"
    .string "house for thine holy name cometh of\l"
    .string "thine hand, and is all thine own.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_17::
    .string "I know also, my God, that thou\n"
    .string "triest the heart, and hast pleasure\l"
    .string "in uprightness. As for me, in the\l"
    .string "uprightness of mine heart I have\l"
    .string "willingly offered all these\l"
    .string "things: and now have I seen with joy\l"
    .string "thy people, which are present\l"
    .string "here, to offer willingly unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_18::
    .string "O LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and of\n"
    .string "Israel, our fathers, keep this for\l"
    .string "ever in the imagination of the\l"
    .string "thoughts of the heart of thy\l"
    .string "people, and prepare their heart\l"
    .string "unto thee:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_19::
    .string "And give unto Solomon my son a\n"
    .string "perfect heart, to keep thy\l"
    .string "commandments, thy testimonies, and\l"
    .string "thy statutes, and to do all these\l"
    .string "things, and to build the palace,\l"
    .string "for the which I have made provision$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_20::
    .string "And David said to all the\n"
    .string "congregation, Now bless the LORD\l"
    .string "your God. And all the congregation\l"
    .string "blessed the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers, and bowed down their heads,\l"
    .string "and worshipped the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_21::
    .string "And they sacrificed sacrifices unto\n"
    .string "the LORD, and offered burnt offerings\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, on the morrow after\l"
    .string "that day, even a thousand bullocks,\l"
    .string "a thousand rams, and a thousand\l"
    .string "lambs, with their drink offerings,\l"
    .string "and sacrifices in abundance for all\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_22::
    .string "And did eat and drink before the\n"
    .string "LORD on that day with great\l"
    .string "gladness. And they made Solomon the\l"
    .string "son of David king the second time,\l"
    .string "and anointed him unto the LORD to be\l"
    .string "the chief governor, and Zadok to be\l"
    .string "priest$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_23::
    .string "Then Solomon sat on the throne of\n"
    .string "the LORD as king instead of David his\l"
    .string "father, and prospered; and all\l"
    .string "Israel obeyed him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_24::
    .string "And all the princes, and the\n"
    .string "mighty men, and all the sons\l"
    .string "likewise of king David, submitted\l"
    .string "themselves unto Solomon the king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_25::
    .string "And the LORD magnified Solomon\n"
    .string "exceedingly in the sight of all\l"
    .string "Israel, and bestowed upon him such\l"
    .string "royal majesty as had not been on any\l"
    .string "king before him in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_26::
    .string "Thus David the son of Jesse reigned\n"
    .string "over all Israel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_27::
    .string "And the time that he reigned over\n"
    .string "Israel was forty years; seven years\l"
    .string "reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and\l"
    .string "three years reigned he in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_28::
    .string "And he died in a good old age, full\n"
    .string "of days, riches, and honour: and\l"
    .string "Solomon his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_29::
    .string "Now the acts of David the king,\n"
    .string "first and last, behold, they are\l"
    .string "written in the book of Samuel the\l"
    .string "seer, and in the book of Nathan the\l"
    .string "prophet, and in the book of Gad the\l"
    .string "seer,"
Bible_Text_1_Chronicles_29_30::
    .string "With all his reign and his might,\n"
    .string "and the times that went over him, and\l"
    .string "over Israel, and over all the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of the countries$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_1::
    .string "And Solomon the son of David was\n"
    .string "strengthened in his kingdom, and the\l"
    .string "LORD his God was with him, and\l"
    .string "magnified him exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_2::
    .string "Then Solomon spake unto all\n"
    .string "Israel, to the captains of\l"
    .string "thousands and of hundreds, and to the\l"
    .string "judges, and to every governor in all\l"
    .string "Israel, the chief of the fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_3::
    .string "So Solomon, and all the\n"
    .string "congregation with him, went to the\l"
    .string "high place that was at Gibeon; for\l"
    .string "there was the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation of God, which Moses the\l"
    .string "servant of the LORD had made in the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_4::
    .string "But the ark of God had David brought\n"
    .string "up from Kirjathjearim to the place\l"
    .string "which David had prepared for it: for\l"
    .string "he had pitched a tent for it at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_5::
    .string "Moreover the brasen altar, that\n"
    .string "Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of\l"
    .string "Hur, had made, he put before the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the LORD: and Solomon\l"
    .string "and the congregation sought unto it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_6::
    .string "And Solomon went up thither to the\n"
    .string "brasen altar before the LORD, which\l"
    .string "was at the tabernacle of the\l"
    .string "congregation, and offered a thousand\l"
    .string "burnt offerings upon it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_7::
    .string "In that night did God appear unto\n"
    .string "Solomon, and said unto him, Ask what\l"
    .string "I shall give thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_8::
    .string "And Solomon said unto God, Thou\n"
    .string "hast shewed great mercy unto David my\l"
    .string "father, and hast made me to reign in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_9::
    .string "Now, O LORD God, let thy promise\n"
    .string "unto David my father be established:\l"
    .string "for thou hast made me king over a\l"
    .string "people like the dust of the earth\l"
    .string "in multitude.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_10::
    .string "Give me now wisdom and knowledge,\n"
    .string "that I may go out and come in before\l"
    .string "this people: for who can judge this\l"
    .string "thy people, that is so great?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_11::
    .string "And God said to Solomon, Because\n"
    .string "this was in thine heart, and thou\l"
    .string "hast not asked riches, wealth, or\l"
    .string "honour, nor the life of thine\l"
    .string "enemies, neither yet hast asked long\l"
    .string "life; but hast asked wisdom and\l"
    .string "knowledge for thyself, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest judge my people, over whom I\l"
    .string "have made thee king:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_12::
    .string "Wisdom and knowledge is granted\n"
    .string "unto thee; and I will give thee\l"
    .string "riches, and wealth, and honour, such\l"
    .string "as none of the kings have had that\l"
    .string "have been before thee, neither\l"
    .string "shall there any after thee have the\l"
    .string "like$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_13::
    .string "Then Solomon came from his journey\n"
    .string "to the high place that was at Gibeon\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem, from before the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "reigned over Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_14::
    .string "And Solomon gathered chariots and\n"
    .string "horsemen: and he had a thousand and\l"
    .string "four hundred chariots, and twelve\l"
    .string "thousand horsemen, which he placed\l"
    .string "in the chariot cities, and with the\l"
    .string "king at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_15::
    .string "And the king made silver and gold\n"
    .string "at Jerusalem as plenteous as\l"
    .string "stones, and cedar trees made he as\l"
    .string "the sycomore trees that are in the\l"
    .string "vale for abundance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_16::
    .string "And Solomon had horses brought out\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king’s\l"
    .string "merchants received the linen yarn at\l"
    .string "a price.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_1_17::
    .string "And they fetched up, and brought\n"
    .string "forth out of Egypt a chariot for six\l"
    .string "hundred shekels of silver, and an\l"
    .string "horse for an hundred and fifty: and\l"
    .string "so brought they out horses for all\l"
    .string "the kings of the Hittites, and for\l"
    .string "the kings of Syria, by their means.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_1::
    .string "And Solomon determined to build an\n"
    .string "house for the name of the LORD, and an\l"
    .string "house for his kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_2::
    .string "And Solomon told out threescore\n"
    .string "and ten thousand men to bear burdens,\l"
    .string "and fourscore thousand to hew in the\l"
    .string "mountain, and three thousand and six\l"
    .string "hundred to oversee them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_3::
    .string "And Solomon sent to Huram the king\n"
    .string "of Tyre, saying, As thou didst deal\l"
    .string "with David my father, and didst send\l"
    .string "him cedars to build him an house to\l"
    .string "dwell therein, even so deal with me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_4::
    .string "Behold, I build an house to the\n"
    .string "name of the LORD my God, to dedicate\l"
    .string "it to him, and to burn before him\l"
    .string "sweet incense, and for the continual\l"
    .string "shewbread, and for the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings morning and evening, on the\l"
    .string "sabbaths, and on the new moons, and\l"
    .string "on the solemn feasts of the LORD our\l"
    .string "God. This is an ordinance for ever to\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_5::
    .string "And the house which I build is\n"
    .string "great: for great is our God above\l"
    .string "all gods.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_6::
    .string "But who is able to build him an\n"
    .string "house, seeing the heaven and heaven\l"
    .string "of heavens cannot contain him? who am\l"
    .string "I then, that I should build him an\l"
    .string "house, save only to burn sacrifice\l"
    .string "before him?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_7::
    .string "Send me now therefore a man cunning\n"
    .string "to work in gold, and in silver, and\l"
    .string "in brass, and in iron, and in\l"
    .string "purple, and crimson, and blue, and\l"
    .string "that can skill to grave with the\l"
    .string "cunning men that are with me in Judah\l"
    .string "and in Jerusalem, whom David my\l"
    .string "father did provide$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_8::
    .string "Send me also cedar trees, fir\n"
    .string "trees, and algum trees, out of\l"
    .string "Lebanon: for I know that thy servants\l"
    .string "can skill to cut timber in Lebanon;\l"
    .string "and, behold, my servants shall be\l"
    .string "with thy servants,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_9::
    .string "Even to prepare me timber in\n"
    .string "abundance: for the house which I am\l"
    .string "about to build shall be wonderful\l"
    .string "great$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_10::
    .string "And, behold, I will give to thy\n"
    .string "servants, the hewers that cut timber,\l"
    .string "twenty thousand measures of beaten\l"
    .string "wheat, and twenty thousand measures\l"
    .string "of barley, and twenty thousand baths\l"
    .string "of wine, and twenty thousand baths of\l"
    .string "oil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_11::
    .string "Then Huram the king of Tyre answered\n"
    .string "in writing, which he sent to\l"
    .string "Solomon, Because the LORD hath\l"
    .string "loved his people, he hath made thee\l"
    .string "king over them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_12::
    .string "Huram said moreover, Blessed be the\n"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, that made heaven\l"
    .string "and earth, who hath given to David\l"
    .string "the king a wise son, endued with\l"
    .string "prudence and understanding, that\l"
    .string "might build an house for the LORD,\l"
    .string "and an house for his kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_13::
    .string "And now I have sent a cunning man,\n"
    .string "endued with understanding, of Huram\l"
    .string "my father’s,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_14::
    .string "The son of a woman of the daughters\n"
    .string "of Dan, and his father was a man of\l"
    .string "Tyre, skilful to work in gold, and\l"
    .string "in silver, in brass, in iron, in\l"
    .string "stone, and in timber, in purple, in\l"
    .string "blue, and in fine linen, and in\l"
    .string "crimson; also to grave any manner of\l"
    .string "graving, and to find out every device\l"
    .string "which shall be put to him, with thy\l"
    .string "cunning men, and with the cunning men\l"
    .string "of my lord David thy father$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_15::
    .string "Now therefore the wheat, and the\n"
    .string "barley, the oil, and the wine, which\l"
    .string "my lord hath spoken of, let him\l"
    .string "send unto his servants:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_16::
    .string "And we will cut wood out of\n"
    .string "Lebanon, as much as thou shalt need:\l"
    .string "and we will bring it to thee in\l"
    .string "floats by sea to Joppa; and thou\l"
    .string "shalt carry it up to Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_17::
    .string "And Solomon numbered all the\n"
    .string "strangers that were in the land of\l"
    .string "Israel, after the numbering\l"
    .string "wherewith David his father had\l"
    .string "numbered them; and they were found an\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty thousand and three\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_2_18::
    .string "And he set threescore and ten\n"
    .string "thousand of them to be bearers of\l"
    .string "burdens, and fourscore thousand to be\l"
    .string "hewers in the mountain, and three\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred overseers\l"
    .string "to set the people a work.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_1::
    .string "Then Solomon began to build the\n"
    .string "house of the LORD at Jerusalem in\l"
    .string "mount Moriah, where the Lord\l"
    .string "appeared unto David his father, in\l"
    .string "the place that David had prepared\l"
    .string "in the threshingfloor of Ornan the\l"
    .string "Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_2::
    .string "And he began to build in the second\n"
    .string "day of the second month, in the\l"
    .string "fourth year of his reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_3::
    .string "Now these are the things wherein\n"
    .string "Solomon was instructed for the\l"
    .string "building of the house of God. The\l"
    .string "length by cubits after the first\l"
    .string "measure was threescore cubits, and\l"
    .string "the breadth twenty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_4::
    .string "And the porch that was in the front\n"
    .string "of the house, the length of it was\l"
    .string "according to the breadth of the\l"
    .string "house, twenty cubits, and the height\l"
    .string "was an hundred and twenty: and he\l"
    .string "overlaid it within with pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_5::
    .string "And the greater house he cieled\n"
    .string "with fir tree, which he overlaid\l"
    .string "with fine gold, and set thereon\l"
    .string "palm trees and chains.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_6::
    .string "And he garnished the house with\n"
    .string "precious stones for beauty: and the\l"
    .string "gold was gold of Parvaim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_7::
    .string "He overlaid also the house, the\n"
    .string "beams, the posts, and the walls\l"
    .string "thereof, and the doors thereof, with\l"
    .string "gold; and graved cherubims on the\l"
    .string "walls.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_8::
    .string "And he made the most holy house, the\n"
    .string "length whereof was according to the\l"
    .string "breadth of the house, twenty cubits,\l"
    .string "and the breadth thereof twenty\l"
    .string "cubits: and he overlaid it with fine\l"
    .string "gold, amounting to six hundred\l"
    .string "talents.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_9::
    .string "And the weight of the nails was\n"
    .string "fifty shekels of gold. And he\l"
    .string "overlaid the upper chambers with\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_10::
    .string "And in the most holy house he made\n"
    .string "two cherubims of image work, and\l"
    .string "overlaid them with gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_11::
    .string "And the wings of the cherubims were\n"
    .string "twenty cubits long: one wing of the\l"
    .string "one cherub was five cubits, reaching\l"
    .string "to the wall of the house: and the\l"
    .string "other wing was likewise five cubits,\l"
    .string "reaching to the wing of the other\l"
    .string "cherub.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_12::
    .string "And one wing of the other cherub was\n"
    .string "five cubits, reaching to the wall of\l"
    .string "the house: and the other wing was\l"
    .string "five cubits also, joining to the\l"
    .string "wing of the other cherub.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_13::
    .string "The wings of these cherubims spread\n"
    .string "themselves forth twenty cubits: and\l"
    .string "they stood on their feet, and their\l"
    .string "faces were inward.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_14::
    .string "And he made the vail of blue, and\n"
    .string "purple, and crimson, and fine\l"
    .string "linen, and wrought cherubims thereon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_15::
    .string "Also he made before the house two\n"
    .string "pillars of thirty and five cubits\l"
    .string "high, and the chapiter that was on\l"
    .string "the top of each of them was five\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_16::
    .string "And he made chains, as in the\n"
    .string "oracle, and put them on the heads of\l"
    .string "the pillars; and made an hundred\l"
    .string "pomegranates, and put them on the\l"
    .string "chains.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_3_17::
    .string "And he reared up the pillars\n"
    .string "before the temple, one on the right\l"
    .string "hand, and the other on the left; and\l"
    .string "called the name of that on the right\l"
    .string "hand Jachin, and the name of that on\l"
    .string "the left Boaz.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_1::
    .string "Moreover he made an altar of brass,\n"
    .string "twenty cubits the length thereof,\l"
    .string "and twenty cubits the breadth\l"
    .string "thereof, and ten cubits the height\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_2::
    .string "Also he made a molten sea of ten\n"
    .string "cubits from brim to brim, round in\l"
    .string "compass, and five cubits the height\l"
    .string "thereof; and a line of thirty cubits\l"
    .string "did compass it round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_3::
    .string "And under it was the similitude of\n"
    .string "oxen, which did compass it round\l"
    .string "about: ten in a cubit, compassing\l"
    .string "the sea round about. Two rows of oxen\l"
    .string "were cast, when it was cast.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_4::
    .string "It stood upon twelve oxen, three\n"
    .string "looking toward the north, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the west, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the south, and three\l"
    .string "looking toward the east: and the sea\l"
    .string "was set above upon them, and all\l"
    .string "their hinder parts were inward.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_5::
    .string "And the thickness of it was an\n"
    .string "handbreadth, and the brim of it like\l"
    .string "the work of the brim of a cup, with\l"
    .string "flowers of lilies; and it received\l"
    .string "and held three thousand baths.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_6::
    .string "He made also ten lavers, and put\n"
    .string "five on the right hand, and five on\l"
    .string "the left, to wash in them: such\l"
    .string "things as they offered for the burnt\l"
    .string "offering they washed in them; but the\l"
    .string "sea was for the priests to wash in.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_7::
    .string "And he made ten candlesticks of\n"
    .string "gold according to their form, and\l"
    .string "set them in the temple, five on the\l"
    .string "right hand, and five on the left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_8::
    .string "He made also ten tables, and\n"
    .string "placed them in the temple, five on\l"
    .string "the right side, and five on the left.\l"
    .string "And he made an hundred basons of\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_9::
    .string "Furthermore he made the court of the\n"
    .string "priests, and the great court, and\l"
    .string "doors for the court, and overlaid\l"
    .string "the doors of them with brass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_10::
    .string "And he set the sea on the right side\n"
    .string "of the east end, over against the\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_11::
    .string "And Huram made the pots, and the\n"
    .string "shovels, and the basons. And Huram\l"
    .string "finished the work that he was to make\l"
    .string "for king Solomon for the house of\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_12::
    .string "To wit, the two pillars, and the\n"
    .string "pommels, and the chapiters which\l"
    .string "were on the top of the two pillars,\l"
    .string "and the two wreaths to cover the two\l"
    .string "pommels of the chapiters which were\l"
    .string "on the top of the pillars;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_13::
    .string "And four hundred pomegranates on\n"
    .string "the two wreaths; two rows of\l"
    .string "pomegranates on each wreath, to cover\l"
    .string "the two pommels of the chapiters\l"
    .string "which were upon the pillars$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_14::
    .string "He made also bases, and lavers made\n"
    .string "he upon the bases;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_15::
    .string "One sea, and twelve oxen under it$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_16::
    .string "The pots also, and the shovels,\n"
    .string "and the fleshhooks, and all their\l"
    .string "instruments, did Huram his father\l"
    .string "make to king Solomon for the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD of bright brass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_17::
    .string "In the plain of Jordan did the king\n"
    .string "cast them, in the clay ground\l"
    .string "between Succoth and Zeredathah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_18::
    .string "Thus Solomon made all these\n"
    .string "vessels in great abundance: for the\l"
    .string "weight of the brass could not be\l"
    .string "found out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_19::
    .string "And Solomon made all the vessels\n"
    .string "that were for the house of God, the\l"
    .string "golden altar also, and the tables\l"
    .string "whereon the shewbread was set;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_20::
    .string "Moreover the candlesticks with\n"
    .string "their lamps, that they should burn\l"
    .string "after the manner before the oracle,\l"
    .string "of pure gold;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_21::
    .string "And the flowers, and the lamps,\n"
    .string "and the tongs, made he of gold, and\l"
    .string "that perfect gold;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_4_22::
    .string "And the snuffers, and the basons,\n"
    .string "and the spoons, and the censers, of\l"
    .string "pure gold: and the entry of the\l"
    .string "house, the inner doors thereof for\l"
    .string "the most holy place, and the doors\l"
    .string "of the house of the temple, were of\l"
    .string "gold$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_1::
    .string "Thus all the work that Solomon\n"
    .string "made for the house of the LORD was\l"
    .string "finished: and Solomon brought in\l"
    .string "all the things that David his\l"
    .string "father had dedicated; and the\l"
    .string "silver, and the gold, and all the\l"
    .string "instruments, put he among the\l"
    .string "treasures of the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_2::
    .string "Then Solomon assembled the elders\n"
    .string "of Israel, and all the heads of the\l"
    .string "tribes, the chief of the fathers of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of\l"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD out of the\l"
    .string "city of David, which is Zion.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_3::
    .string "Wherefore all the men of Israel\n"
    .string "assembled themselves unto the king\l"
    .string "in the feast which was in the seventh\l"
    .string "month.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_4::
    .string "And all the elders of Israel\n"
    .string "came; and the Levites took up the\l"
    .string "ark.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_5::
    .string "And they brought up the ark, and the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of the congregation, and\l"
    .string "all the holy vessels that were in\l"
    .string "the tabernacle, these did the\l"
    .string "priests and the Levites bring up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_6::
    .string "Also king Solomon, and all the\n"
    .string "congregation of Israel that were\l"
    .string "assembled unto him before the ark,\l"
    .string "sacrificed sheep and oxen, which\l"
    .string "could not be told nor numbered for\l"
    .string "multitude.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_7::
    .string "And the priests brought in the ark\n"
    .string "of the covenant of the LORD unto his\l"
    .string "place, to the oracle of the house,\l"
    .string "into the most holy place, even\l"
    .string "under the wings of the cherubims:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_8::
    .string "For the cherubims spread forth\n"
    .string "their wings over the place of the\l"
    .string "ark, and the cherubims covered the\l"
    .string "ark and the staves thereof above$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_9::
    .string "And they drew out the staves of the\n"
    .string "ark, that the ends of the staves were\l"
    .string "seen from the ark before the oracle;\l"
    .string "but they were not seen without. And\l"
    .string "there it is unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_10::
    .string "There was nothing in the ark save\n"
    .string "the two tables which Moses put\l"
    .string "therein at Horeb, when the LORD made\l"
    .string "a covenant with the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, when they came out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "priests were come out of the holy\l"
    .string "place: (for all the priests that\l"
    .string "were present were sanctified, and\l"
    .string "did not then wait by course:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_12::
    .string "Also the Levites which were the\n"
    .string "singers, all of them of Asaph, of\l"
    .string "Heman, of Jeduthun, with their sons\l"
    .string "and their brethren, being arrayed in\l"
    .string "white linen, having cymbals and\l"
    .string "psalteries and harps, stood at the\l"
    .string "east end of the altar, and with them\l"
    .string "an hundred and twenty priests\l"
    .string "sounding with trumpets:)"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_13::
    .string "It came even to pass, as the\n"
    .string "trumpeters and singers were as one,\l"
    .string "to make one sound to be heard in\l"
    .string "praising and thanking the LORD; and\l"
    .string "when they lifted up their voice\l"
    .string "with the trumpets and cymbals and\l"
    .string "instruments of musick, and praised\l"
    .string "the LORD, saying, For he is good; for\l"
    .string "his mercy endureth for ever: that\l"
    .string "then the house was filled with a\l"
    .string "cloud, even the house of the LORD;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_5_14::
    .string "So that the priests could not\n"
    .string "stand to minister by reason of the\l"
    .string "cloud: for the glory of the LORD had\l"
    .string "filled the house of God$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_1::
    .string "Then said Solomon, The LORD hath\n"
    .string "said that he would dwell in the\l"
    .string "thick darkness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_2::
    .string "But I have built an house of\n"
    .string "habitation for thee, and a place for\l"
    .string "thy dwelling for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_3::
    .string "And the king turned his face, and\n"
    .string "blessed the whole congregation of\l"
    .string "Israel: and all the congregation of\l"
    .string "Israel stood.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_4::
    .string "And he said, Blessed be the LORD God\n"
    .string "of Israel, who hath with his hands\l"
    .string "fulfilled that which he spake with\l"
    .string "his mouth to my father David, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_5::
    .string "Since the day that I brought forth\n"
    .string "my people out of the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "I chose no city among all the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel to build an house in, that\l"
    .string "my name might be there; neither chose\l"
    .string "I any man to be a ruler over my\l"
    .string "people Israel:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_6::
    .string "But I have chosen Jerusalem, that\n"
    .string "my name might be there; and have\l"
    .string "chosen David to be over my people\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_7::
    .string "Now it was in the heart of David my\n"
    .string "father to build an house for the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_8::
    .string "But the LORD said to David my\n"
    .string "father, Forasmuch as it was in thine\l"
    .string "heart to build an house for my name,\l"
    .string "thou didst well in that it was in\l"
    .string "thine heart:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_9::
    .string "Notwithstanding thou shalt not\n"
    .string "build the house; but thy son which\l"
    .string "shall come forth out of thy loins,\l"
    .string "he shall build the house for my name$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_10::
    .string "The LORD therefore hath performed\n"
    .string "his word that he hath spoken: for I\l"
    .string "am risen up in the room of David my\l"
    .string "father, and am set on the throne of\l"
    .string "Israel, as the LORD promised, and\l"
    .string "have built the house for the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_11::
    .string "And in it have I put the ark,\n"
    .string "wherein is the covenant of the LORD,\l"
    .string "that he made with the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_12::
    .string "And he stood before the altar of\n"
    .string "the LORD in the presence of all the\l"
    .string "congregation of Israel, and spread\l"
    .string "forth his hands:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_13::
    .string "For Solomon had made a brasen\n"
    .string "scaffold of five cubits long, and\l"
    .string "five cubits broad, and three cubits\l"
    .string "high, and had set it in the midst of\l"
    .string "the court: and upon it he stood, and\l"
    .string "kneeled down upon his knees before\l"
    .string "all the congregation of Israel, and\l"
    .string "spread forth his hands toward heaven$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_14::
    .string "And said, O LORD God of Israel,\n"
    .string "there is no God like thee in the\l"
    .string "heaven, nor in the earth; which\l"
    .string "keepest covenant, and shewest mercy\l"
    .string "unto thy servants, that walk before\l"
    .string "thee with all their hearts:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_15::
    .string "Thou which hast kept with thy\n"
    .string "servant David my father that which\l"
    .string "thou hast promised him; and spakest\l"
    .string "with thy mouth, and hast fulfilled\l"
    .string "it with thine hand, as it is this day$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_16::
    .string "Now therefore, O LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel, keep with thy servant David\l"
    .string "my father that which thou hast\l"
    .string "promised him, saying, There shall\l"
    .string "not fail thee a man in my sight to\l"
    .string "sit upon the throne of Israel; yet\l"
    .string "so that thy children take heed to\l"
    .string "their way to walk in my law, as thou\l"
    .string "hast walked before me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_17::
    .string "Now then, O LORD God of Israel, let\n"
    .string "thy word be verified, which thou hast\l"
    .string "spoken unto thy servant David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_18::
    .string "But will God in very deed dwell\n"
    .string "with men on the earth? behold,\l"
    .string "heaven and the heaven of heavens\l"
    .string "cannot contain thee; how much less\l"
    .string "this house which I have built!"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_19::
    .string "Have respect therefore to the\n"
    .string "prayer of thy servant, and to his\l"
    .string "supplication, O LORD my God, to\l"
    .string "hearken unto the cry and the prayer\l"
    .string "which thy servant prayeth before\l"
    .string "thee:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_20::
    .string "That thine eyes may be open upon\n"
    .string "this house day and night, upon the\l"
    .string "place whereof thou hast said that\l"
    .string "thou wouldest put thy name there; to\l"
    .string "hearken unto the prayer which thy\l"
    .string "servant prayeth toward this place$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_21::
    .string "Hearken therefore unto the\n"
    .string "supplications of thy servant, and\l"
    .string "of thy people Israel, which they\l"
    .string "shall make toward this place: hear\l"
    .string "thou from thy dwelling place, even\l"
    .string "from heaven; and when thou hearest,\l"
    .string "forgive.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_22::
    .string "If a man sin against his neighbour,\n"
    .string "and an oath be laid upon him to make\l"
    .string "him swear, and the oath come before\l"
    .string "thine altar in this house;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_23::
    .string "Then hear thou from heaven, and do,\n"
    .string "and judge thy servants, by requiting\l"
    .string "the wicked, by recompensing his way\l"
    .string "upon his own head; and by justifying\l"
    .string "the righteous, by giving him\l"
    .string "according to his righteousness$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_24::
    .string "And if thy people Israel be put\n"
    .string "to the worse before the enemy,\l"
    .string "because they have sinned against\l"
    .string "thee; and shall return and confess\l"
    .string "thy name, and pray and make\l"
    .string "supplication before thee in this\l"
    .string "house;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_25::
    .string "Then hear thou from the heavens, and\n"
    .string "forgive the sin of thy people\l"
    .string "Israel, and bring them again unto\l"
    .string "the land which thou gavest to them\l"
    .string "and to their fathers$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_26::
    .string "When the heaven is shut up, and\n"
    .string "there is no rain, because they have\l"
    .string "sinned against thee; yet if they\l"
    .string "pray toward this place, and confess\l"
    .string "thy name, and turn from their sin,\l"
    .string "when thou dost afflict them;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_27::
    .string "Then hear thou from heaven, and\n"
    .string "forgive the sin of thy servants, and\l"
    .string "of thy people Israel, when thou\l"
    .string "hast taught them the good way,\l"
    .string "wherein they should walk; and send\l"
    .string "rain upon thy land, which thou hast\l"
    .string "given unto thy people for an\l"
    .string "inheritance$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_28::
    .string "If there be dearth in the land, if\n"
    .string "there be pestilence, if there be\l"
    .string "blasting, or mildew, locusts, or\l"
    .string "caterpillers; if their enemies\l"
    .string "besiege them in the cities of their\l"
    .string "land; whatsoever sore or whatsoever\l"
    .string "sickness there be:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_29::
    .string "Then what prayer or what\n"
    .string "supplication soever shall be made\l"
    .string "of any man, or of all thy people\l"
    .string "Israel, when every one shall know\l"
    .string "his own sore and his own grief, and\l"
    .string "shall spread forth his hands in\l"
    .string "this house:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_30::
    .string "Then hear thou from heaven thy\n"
    .string "dwelling place, and forgive, and\l"
    .string "render unto every man according unto\l"
    .string "all his ways, whose heart thou\l"
    .string "knowest; (for thou only knowest the\l"
    .string "hearts of the children of men:)"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_31::
    .string "That they may fear thee, to walk in\n"
    .string "thy ways, so long as they live in\l"
    .string "the land which thou gavest unto our\l"
    .string "fathers$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_32::
    .string "Moreover concerning the stranger,\n"
    .string "which is not of thy people Israel,\l"
    .string "but is come from a far country for\l"
    .string "thy great name’s sake, and thy mighty\l"
    .string "hand, and thy stretched out arm; if\l"
    .string "they come and pray in this house;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_33::
    .string "Then hear thou from the heavens,\n"
    .string "even from thy dwelling place, and\l"
    .string "do according to all that the\l"
    .string "stranger calleth to thee for; that\l"
    .string "all people of the earth may know\l"
    .string "thy name, and fear thee, as doth thy\l"
    .string "people Israel, and may know that\l"
    .string "this house which I have built is\l"
    .string "called by thy name$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_34::
    .string "If thy people go out to war\n"
    .string "against their enemies by the way that\l"
    .string "thou shalt send them, and they pray\l"
    .string "unto thee toward this city which thou\l"
    .string "hast chosen, and the house which I\l"
    .string "have built for thy name;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_35::
    .string "Then hear thou from the heavens\n"
    .string "their prayer and their\l"
    .string "supplication, and maintain their\l"
    .string "cause$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_36::
    .string "If they sin against thee, (for there\n"
    .string "is no man which sinneth not,) and\l"
    .string "thou be angry with them, and deliver\l"
    .string "them over before their enemies, and\l"
    .string "they carry them away captives unto a\l"
    .string "land far off or near;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_37::
    .string "Yet if they bethink themselves in\n"
    .string "the land whither they are carried\l"
    .string "captive, and turn and pray unto thee\l"
    .string "in the land of their captivity,\l"
    .string "saying, We have sinned, we have done\l"
    .string "amiss, and have dealt wickedly;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_38::
    .string "If they return to thee with all\n"
    .string "their heart and with all their soul\l"
    .string "in the land of their captivity,\l"
    .string "whither they have carried them\l"
    .string "captives, and pray toward their\l"
    .string "land, which thou gavest unto their\l"
    .string "fathers, and toward the city which\l"
    .string "thou hast chosen, and toward the\l"
    .string "house which I have built for thy\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_39::
    .string "Then hear thou from the heavens,\n"
    .string "even from thy dwelling place,\l"
    .string "their prayer and their\l"
    .string "supplications, and maintain their\l"
    .string "cause, and forgive thy people which\l"
    .string "have sinned against thee$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_40::
    .string "Now, my God, let, I beseech thee,\n"
    .string "thine eyes be open, and let thine\l"
    .string "ears be attent unto the prayer that\l"
    .string "is made in this place.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_41::
    .string "Now therefore arise, O LORD God,\n"
    .string "into thy resting place, thou, and\l"
    .string "the ark of thy strength: let thy\l"
    .string "priests, O LORD God, be clothed with\l"
    .string "salvation, and let thy saints\l"
    .string "rejoice in goodness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_6_42::
    .string "O LORD God, turn not away the face of\n"
    .string "thine anointed: remember the mercies\l"
    .string "of David thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_1::
    .string "Now when Solomon had made an end of\n"
    .string "praying, the fire came down from\l"
    .string "heaven, and consumed the burnt\l"
    .string "offering and the sacrifices; and the\l"
    .string "glory of the LORD filled the house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_2::
    .string "And the priests could not enter\n"
    .string "into the house of the LORD, because\l"
    .string "the glory of the LORD had filled\l"
    .string "the LORD’s house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_3::
    .string "And when all the children of\n"
    .string "Israel saw how the fire came down,\l"
    .string "and the glory of the LORD upon the\l"
    .string "house, they bowed themselves with\l"
    .string "their faces to the ground upon the\l"
    .string "pavement, and worshipped, and\l"
    .string "praised the LORD, saying, For he is\l"
    .string "good; for his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_4::
    .string "Then the king and all the people\n"
    .string "offered sacrifices before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_5::
    .string "And king Solomon offered a\n"
    .string "sacrifice of twenty and two thousand\l"
    .string "oxen, and an hundred and twenty\l"
    .string "thousand sheep: so the king and all\l"
    .string "the people dedicated the house of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_6::
    .string "And the priests waited on their\n"
    .string "offices: the Levites also with\l"
    .string "instruments of musick of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which David the king had made to\l"
    .string "praise the LORD, because his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever, when David\l"
    .string "praised by their ministry; and the\l"
    .string "priests sounded trumpets before\l"
    .string "them, and all Israel stood.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_7::
    .string "Moreover Solomon hallowed the\n"
    .string "middle of the court that was before\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD: for there he\l"
    .string "offered burnt offerings, and the fat\l"
    .string "of the peace offerings, because the\l"
    .string "brasen altar which Solomon had made\l"
    .string "was not able to receive the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings, and the meat offerings,\l"
    .string "and the fat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_8::
    .string "Also at the same time Solomon kept\n"
    .string "the feast seven days, and all\l"
    .string "Israel with him, a very great\l"
    .string "congregation, from the entering in of\l"
    .string "Hamath unto the river of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_9::
    .string "And in the eighth day they made a\n"
    .string "solemn assembly: for they kept the\l"
    .string "dedication of the altar seven days,\l"
    .string "and the feast seven days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_10::
    .string "And on the three and twentieth day\n"
    .string "of the seventh month he sent the\l"
    .string "people away into their tents, glad\l"
    .string "and merry in heart for the goodness\l"
    .string "that the LORD had shewed unto David,\l"
    .string "and to Solomon, and to Israel his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_11::
    .string "Thus Solomon finished the house of\n"
    .string "the LORD, and the king’s house: and\l"
    .string "all that came into Solomon’s heart\l"
    .string "to make in the house of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "in his own house, he prosperously\l"
    .string "effected.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_12::
    .string "And the LORD appeared to Solomon\n"
    .string "by night, and said unto him, I have\l"
    .string "heard thy prayer, and have chosen\l"
    .string "this place to myself for an house\l"
    .string "of sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_13::
    .string "If I shut up heaven that there be no\n"
    .string "rain, or if I command the locusts to\l"
    .string "devour the land, or if I send\l"
    .string "pestilence among my people;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_14::
    .string "If my people, which are called by\n"
    .string "my name, shall humble themselves,\l"
    .string "and pray, and seek my face, and turn\l"
    .string "from their wicked ways; then will I\l"
    .string "hear from heaven, and will forgive\l"
    .string "their sin, and will heal their land$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_15::
    .string "Now mine eyes shall be open, and\n"
    .string "mine ears attent unto the prayer\l"
    .string "that is made in this place.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_16::
    .string "For now have I chosen and sanctified\n"
    .string "this house, that my name may be there\l"
    .string "for ever: and mine eyes and mine\l"
    .string "heart shall be there perpetually.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_17::
    .string "And as for thee, if thou wilt walk\n"
    .string "before me, as David thy father\l"
    .string "walked, and do according to all\l"
    .string "that I have commanded thee, and\l"
    .string "shalt observe my statutes and my\l"
    .string "judgments;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_18::
    .string "Then will I stablish the throne of\n"
    .string "thy kingdom, according as I have\l"
    .string "covenanted with David thy father,\l"
    .string "saying, There shall not fail thee a\l"
    .string "man to be ruler in Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_19::
    .string "But if ye turn away, and forsake my\n"
    .string "statutes and my commandments, which I\l"
    .string "have set before you, and shall go\l"
    .string "and serve other gods, and worship\l"
    .string "them;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_20::
    .string "Then will I pluck them up by the\n"
    .string "roots out of my land which I have\l"
    .string "given them; and this house, which I\l"
    .string "have sanctified for my name, will I\l"
    .string "cast out of my sight, and will make\l"
    .string "it to be a proverb and a byword among\l"
    .string "all nations$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_21::
    .string "And this house, which is high,\n"
    .string "shall be an astonishment to every\l"
    .string "one that passeth by it; so that he\l"
    .string "shall say, Why hath the LORD done\l"
    .string "thus unto this land, and unto this\l"
    .string "house?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_7_22::
    .string "And it shall be answered, Because\n"
    .string "they forsook the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers, which brought them forth out\l"
    .string "of the land of Egypt, and laid hold\l"
    .string "on other gods, and worshipped them,\l"
    .string "and served them: therefore hath he\l"
    .string "brought all this evil upon them$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_1::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "twenty years, wherein Solomon had\l"
    .string "built the house of the LORD, and his\l"
    .string "own house,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_2::
    .string "That the cities which Huram had\n"
    .string "restored to Solomon, Solomon built\l"
    .string "them, and caused the children of\l"
    .string "Israel to dwell there$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_3::
    .string "And Solomon went to Hamathzobah,\n"
    .string "and prevailed against it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_4::
    .string "And he built Tadmor in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and all the store\l"
    .string "cities, which he built in Hamath.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_5::
    .string "Also he built Bethhoron the\n"
    .string "upper, and Bethhoron the nether,\l"
    .string "fenced cities, with walls, gates,\l"
    .string "and bars;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_6::
    .string "And Baalath, and all the store\n"
    .string "cities that Solomon had, and all\l"
    .string "the chariot cities, and the cities of\l"
    .string "the horsemen, and all that Solomon\l"
    .string "desired to build in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "in Lebanon, and throughout all the\l"
    .string "land of his dominion$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_7::
    .string "As for all the people that were\n"
    .string "left of the Hittites, and the\l"
    .string "Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the\l"
    .string "Hivites, and the Jebusites, which\l"
    .string "were not of Israel,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_8::
    .string "But of their children, who were\n"
    .string "left after them in the land, whom the\l"
    .string "children of Israel consumed not,\l"
    .string "them did Solomon make to pay\l"
    .string "tribute until this day$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_9::
    .string "But of the children of Israel did\n"
    .string "Solomon make no servants for his\l"
    .string "work; but they were men of war, and\l"
    .string "chief of his captains, and captains\l"
    .string "of his chariots and horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_10::
    .string "And these were the chief of king\n"
    .string "Solomon’s officers, even two hundred\l"
    .string "and fifty, that bare rule over the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_11::
    .string "And Solomon brought up the\n"
    .string "daughter of Pharaoh out of the city\l"
    .string "of David unto the house that he had\l"
    .string "built for her: for he said, My wife\l"
    .string "shall not dwell in the house of\l"
    .string "David king of Israel, because the\l"
    .string "places are holy, whereunto the ark\l"
    .string "of the LORD hath come.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_12::
    .string "Then Solomon offered burnt\n"
    .string "offerings unto the LORD on the altar\l"
    .string "of the LORD, which he had built\l"
    .string "before the porch,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_13::
    .string "Even after a certain rate every day,\n"
    .string "offering according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of Moses, on the\l"
    .string "sabbaths, and on the new moons, and\l"
    .string "on the solemn feasts, three times in\l"
    .string "the year, even in the feast of\l"
    .string "unleavened bread, and in the feast\l"
    .string "of weeks, and in the feast of\l"
    .string "tabernacles$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_14::
    .string "And he appointed, according to the\n"
    .string "order of David his father, the\l"
    .string "courses of the priests to their\l"
    .string "service, and the Levites to their\l"
    .string "charges, to praise and minister\l"
    .string "before the priests, as the duty of\l"
    .string "every day required: the porters\l"
    .string "also by their courses at every gate:\l"
    .string "for so had David the man of God\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_15::
    .string "And they departed not from the\n"
    .string "commandment of the king unto the\l"
    .string "priests and Levites concerning any\l"
    .string "matter, or concerning the treasures.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_16::
    .string "Now all the work of Solomon was\n"
    .string "prepared unto the day of the\l"
    .string "foundation of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and until it was finished. So the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD was perfected.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_17::
    .string "Then went Solomon to Eziongeber,\n"
    .string "and to Eloth, at the sea side in the\l"
    .string "land of Edom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_8_18::
    .string "And Huram sent him by the hands of\n"
    .string "his servants ships, and servants\l"
    .string "that had knowledge of the sea; and\l"
    .string "they went with the servants of\l"
    .string "Solomon to Ophir, and took thence\l"
    .string "four hundred and fifty talents of\l"
    .string "gold, and brought them to king\l"
    .string "Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_1::
    .string "And when the queen of Sheba heard of\n"
    .string "the fame of Solomon, she came to\l"
    .string "prove Solomon with hard questions at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, with a very great\l"
    .string "company, and camels that bare\l"
    .string "spices, and gold in abundance, and\l"
    .string "precious stones: and when she was\l"
    .string "come to Solomon, she communed with\l"
    .string "him of all that was in her heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_2::
    .string "And Solomon told her all her\n"
    .string "questions: and there was nothing hid\l"
    .string "from Solomon which he told her not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_3::
    .string "And when the queen of Sheba had seen\n"
    .string "the wisdom of Solomon, and the house\l"
    .string "that he had built,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_4::
    .string "And the meat of his table, and the\n"
    .string "sitting of his servants, and the\l"
    .string "attendance of his ministers, and\l"
    .string "their apparel; his cupbearers\l"
    .string "also, and their apparel; and his\l"
    .string "ascent by which he went up into the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD; there was no more\l"
    .string "spirit in her$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_5::
    .string "And she said to the king, It was a\n"
    .string "true report which I heard in mine\l"
    .string "own land of thine acts, and of thy\l"
    .string "wisdom:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_6::
    .string "Howbeit I believed not their words,\n"
    .string "until I came, and mine eyes had seen\l"
    .string "it: and, behold, the one half of the\l"
    .string "greatness of thy wisdom was not told\l"
    .string "me: for thou exceedest the fame that\l"
    .string "I heard$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_7::
    .string "Happy are thy men, and happy are\n"
    .string "these thy servants, which stand\l"
    .string "continually before thee, and hear\l"
    .string "thy wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_8::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD thy God, which\n"
    .string "delighted in thee to set thee on his\l"
    .string "throne, to be king for the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God: because thy God loved Israel,\l"
    .string "to establish them for ever,\l"
    .string "therefore made he thee king over\l"
    .string "them, to do judgment and justice.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_9::
    .string "And she gave the king an hundred and\n"
    .string "twenty talents of gold, and of\l"
    .string "spices great abundance, and\l"
    .string "precious stones: neither was there\l"
    .string "any such spice as the queen of Sheba\l"
    .string "gave king Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_10::
    .string "And the servants also of Huram, and\n"
    .string "the servants of Solomon, which\l"
    .string "brought gold from Ophir, brought\l"
    .string "algum trees and precious stones.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_11::
    .string "And the king made of the algum\n"
    .string "trees terraces to the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and to the king’s palace, and\l"
    .string "harps and psalteries for singers:\l"
    .string "and there were none such seen before\l"
    .string "in the land of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_12::
    .string "And king Solomon gave to the queen\n"
    .string "of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever\l"
    .string "she asked, beside that which she had\l"
    .string "brought unto the king. So she turned,\l"
    .string "and went away to her own land, she\l"
    .string "and her servants.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_13::
    .string "Now the weight of gold that came to\n"
    .string "Solomon in one year was six hundred\l"
    .string "and threescore and six talents of\l"
    .string "gold;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_14::
    .string "Beside that which chapmen and\n"
    .string "merchants brought. And all the\l"
    .string "kings of Arabia and governors of the\l"
    .string "country brought gold and silver to\l"
    .string "Solomon$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_15::
    .string "And king Solomon made two hundred\n"
    .string "targets of beaten gold: six hundred\l"
    .string "shekels of beaten gold went to one\l"
    .string "target.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_16::
    .string "And three hundred shields made he\n"
    .string "of beaten gold: three hundred\l"
    .string "shekels of gold went to one shield.\l"
    .string "And the king put them in the house of\l"
    .string "the forest of Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_17::
    .string "Moreover the king made a great\n"
    .string "throne of ivory, and overlaid it\l"
    .string "with pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_18::
    .string "And there were six steps to the\n"
    .string "throne, with a footstool of gold,\l"
    .string "which were fastened to the throne,\l"
    .string "and stays on each side of the sitting\l"
    .string "place, and two lions standing by the\l"
    .string "stays:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_19::
    .string "And twelve lions stood there on\n"
    .string "the one side and on the other upon\l"
    .string "the six steps. There was not the\l"
    .string "like made in any kingdom$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_20::
    .string "And all the drinking vessels of\n"
    .string "king Solomon were of gold, and all\l"
    .string "the vessels of the house of the\l"
    .string "forest of Lebanon were of pure gold:\l"
    .string "none were of silver; it was not any\l"
    .string "thing accounted of in the days of\l"
    .string "Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_21::
    .string "For the king’s ships went to\n"
    .string "Tarshish with the servants of Huram:\l"
    .string "every three years once came the\l"
    .string "ships of Tarshish bringing gold,\l"
    .string "and silver, ivory, and apes, and\l"
    .string "peacocks.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_22::
    .string "And king Solomon passed all the\n"
    .string "kings of the earth in riches and\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_23::
    .string "And all the kings of the earth\n"
    .string "sought the presence of Solomon, to\l"
    .string "hear his wisdom, that God had put in\l"
    .string "his heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_24::
    .string "And they brought every man his\n"
    .string "present, vessels of silver, and\l"
    .string "vessels of gold, and raiment,\l"
    .string "harness, and spices, horses, and\l"
    .string "mules, a rate year by year.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_25::
    .string "And Solomon had four thousand\n"
    .string "stalls for horses and chariots, and\l"
    .string "twelve thousand horsemen; whom he\l"
    .string "bestowed in the chariot cities, and\l"
    .string "with the king at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_26::
    .string "And he reigned over all the kings\n"
    .string "from the river even unto the land of\l"
    .string "the Philistines, and to the border\l"
    .string "of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_27::
    .string "And the king made silver in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem as stones, and cedar trees\l"
    .string "made he as the sycomore trees that\l"
    .string "are in the low plains in abundance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_28::
    .string "And they brought unto Solomon\n"
    .string "horses out of Egypt, and out of all\l"
    .string "lands.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_29::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Solomon,\n"
    .string "first and last, are they not written\l"
    .string "in the book of Nathan the prophet,\l"
    .string "and in the prophecy of Ahijah the\l"
    .string "Shilonite, and in the visions of\l"
    .string "Iddo the seer against Jeroboam the\l"
    .string "son of Nebat?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_30::
    .string "And Solomon reigned in Jerusalem\n"
    .string "over all Israel forty years$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_9_31::
    .string "And Solomon slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and he was buried in the\l"
    .string "city of David his father: and\l"
    .string "Rehoboam his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_1::
    .string "And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for to\n"
    .string "Shechem were all Israel come to\l"
    .string "make him king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jeroboam\n"
    .string "the son of Nebat, who was in Egypt,\l"
    .string "whither he fled from the presence\l"
    .string "of Solomon the king, heard it, that\l"
    .string "Jeroboam returned out of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_3::
    .string "And they sent and called him. So\n"
    .string "Jeroboam and all Israel came and\l"
    .string "spake to Rehoboam, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_4::
    .string "Thy father made our yoke grievous:\n"
    .string "now therefore ease thou somewhat the\l"
    .string "grievous servitude of thy father, and\l"
    .string "his heavy yoke that he put upon us,\l"
    .string "and we will serve thee$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, Come again\n"
    .string "unto me after three days. And the\l"
    .string "people departed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_6::
    .string "And king Rehoboam took counsel with\n"
    .string "the old men that had stood before\l"
    .string "Solomon his father while he yet\l"
    .string "lived, saying, What counsel give ye\l"
    .string "me to return answer to this people?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_7::
    .string "And they spake unto him, saying, If\n"
    .string "thou be kind to this people, and\l"
    .string "please them, and speak good words to\l"
    .string "them, they will be thy servants for\l"
    .string "ever$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_8::
    .string "But he forsook the counsel which\n"
    .string "the old men gave him, and took\l"
    .string "counsel with the young men that were\l"
    .string "brought up with him, that stood\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_9::
    .string "And he said unto them, What advice\n"
    .string "give ye that we may return answer to\l"
    .string "this people, which have spoken to\l"
    .string "me, saying, Ease somewhat the yoke\l"
    .string "that thy father did put upon us?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_10::
    .string "And the young men that were brought\n"
    .string "up with him spake unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Thus shalt thou answer the people\l"
    .string "that spake unto thee, saying, Thy\l"
    .string "father made our yoke heavy, but make\l"
    .string "thou it somewhat lighter for us;\l"
    .string "thus shalt thou say unto them, My\l"
    .string "little finger shall be thicker\l"
    .string "than my father’s loins$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_11::
    .string "For whereas my father put a heavy\n"
    .string "yoke upon you, I will put more to\l"
    .string "your yoke: my father chastised you\l"
    .string "with whips, but I will chastise you\l"
    .string "with scorpions.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_12::
    .string "So Jeroboam and all the people\n"
    .string "came to Rehoboam on the third day, as\l"
    .string "the king bade, saying, Come again to\l"
    .string "me on the third day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_13::
    .string "And the king answered them roughly;\n"
    .string "and king Rehoboam forsook the\l"
    .string "counsel of the old men,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_14::
    .string "And answered them after the advice\n"
    .string "of the young men, saying, My father\l"
    .string "made your yoke heavy, but I will add\l"
    .string "thereto: my father chastised you with\l"
    .string "whips, but I will chastise you with\l"
    .string "scorpions$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_15::
    .string "So the king hearkened not unto the\n"
    .string "people: for the cause was of God,\l"
    .string "that the LORD might perform his\l"
    .string "word, which he spake by the hand of\l"
    .string "Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the\l"
    .string "son of Nebat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_16::
    .string "And when all Israel saw that the\n"
    .string "king would not hearken unto them,\l"
    .string "the people answered the king,\l"
    .string "saying, What portion have we in\l"
    .string "David? and we have none inheritance\l"
    .string "in the son of Jesse: every man to your\l"
    .string "tents, O Israel: and now, David, see\l"
    .string "to thine own house. So all Israel\l"
    .string "went to their tents.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_17::
    .string "But as for the children of Israel\n"
    .string "that dwelt in the cities of Judah,\l"
    .string "Rehoboam reigned over them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_18::
    .string "Then king Rehoboam sent Hadoram\n"
    .string "that was over the tribute; and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel stoned him with\l"
    .string "stones, that he died. But king\l"
    .string "Rehoboam made speed to get him up to\l"
    .string "his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_10_19::
    .string "And Israel rebelled against the\n"
    .string "house of David unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_1::
    .string "And when Rehoboam was come to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, he gathered of the house\l"
    .string "of Judah and Benjamin an hundred and\l"
    .string "fourscore thousand chosen men, which\l"
    .string "were warriors, to fight against\l"
    .string "Israel, that he might bring the\l"
    .string "kingdom again to Rehoboam.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_2::
    .string "But the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Shemaiah the man of God, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_3::
    .string "Speak unto Rehoboam the son of\n"
    .string "Solomon, king of Judah, and to all\l"
    .string "Israel in Judah and Benjamin,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not\n"
    .string "go up, nor fight against your\l"
    .string "brethren: return every man to his\l"
    .string "house: for this thing is done of me.\l"
    .string "And they obeyed the words of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and returned from going against\l"
    .string "Jeroboam$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_5::
    .string "And Rehoboam dwelt in Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and built cities for defence in\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_6::
    .string "He built even Bethlehem, and Etam,\n"
    .string "and Tekoa,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_7::
    .string "And Bethzur, and Shoco, and\n"
    .string "Adullam,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_8::
    .string "And Gath, and Mareshah, and Ziph,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_9::
    .string "And Adoraim, and Lachish, and\n"
    .string "Azekah,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_10::
    .string "And Zorah, and Aijalon, and Hebron,\n"
    .string "which are in Judah and in Benjamin\l"
    .string "fenced cities$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_11::
    .string "And he fortified the strong holds,\n"
    .string "and put captains in them, and store\l"
    .string "of victual, and of oil and wine.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_12::
    .string "And in every several city he put\n"
    .string "shields and spears, and made them\l"
    .string "exceeding strong, having Judah and\l"
    .string "Benjamin on his side.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_13::
    .string "And the priests and the Levites\n"
    .string "that were in all Israel resorted to\l"
    .string "him out of all their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_14::
    .string "For the Levites left their suburbs\n"
    .string "and their possession, and came to\l"
    .string "Judah and Jerusalem: for Jeroboam\l"
    .string "and his sons had cast them off from\l"
    .string "executing the priest’s office unto\l"
    .string "the LORD:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_15::
    .string "And he ordained him priests for the\n"
    .string "high places, and for the devils,\l"
    .string "and for the calves which he had made$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_16::
    .string "And after them out of all the\n"
    .string "tribes of Israel such as set their\l"
    .string "hearts to seek the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel came to Jerusalem, to\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_17::
    .string "So they strengthened the kingdom of\n"
    .string "Judah, and made Rehoboam the son of\l"
    .string "Solomon strong, three years: for\l"
    .string "three years they walked in the way\l"
    .string "of David and Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_18::
    .string "And Rehoboam took him Mahalath the\n"
    .string "daughter of Jerimoth the son of David\l"
    .string "to wife, and Abihail the daughter of\l"
    .string "Eliab the son of Jesse;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_19::
    .string "Which bare him children; Jeush, and\n"
    .string "Shamariah, and Zaham$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_20::
    .string "And after her he took Maachah the\n"
    .string "daughter of Absalom; which bare him\l"
    .string "Abijah, and Attai, and Ziza, and\l"
    .string "Shelomith.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_21::
    .string "And Rehoboam loved Maachah the\n"
    .string "daughter of Absalom above all his\l"
    .string "wives and his concubines: (for he\l"
    .string "took eighteen wives, and threescore\l"
    .string "concubines; and begat twenty and\l"
    .string "eight sons, and threescore\l"
    .string "daughters.)"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_22::
    .string "And Rehoboam made Abijah the son of\n"
    .string "Maachah the chief, to be ruler among\l"
    .string "his brethren: for he thought to make\l"
    .string "him king$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_11_23::
    .string "And he dealt wisely, and dispersed\n"
    .string "of all his children throughout\l"
    .string "all the countries of Judah and\l"
    .string "Benjamin, unto every fenced city: and\l"
    .string "he gave them victual in abundance.\l"
    .string "And he desired many wives.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Rehoboam\n"
    .string "had established the kingdom, and had\l"
    .string "strengthened himself, he forsook the\l"
    .string "law of the LORD, and all Israel\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, that in the\n"
    .string "fifth year of king Rehoboam Shishak\l"
    .string "king of Egypt came up against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, because they had\l"
    .string "transgressed against the LORD,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_3::
    .string "With twelve hundred chariots, and\n"
    .string "threescore thousand horsemen: and\l"
    .string "the people were without number\l"
    .string "that came with him out of Egypt; the\l"
    .string "Lubims, the Sukkiims, and the\l"
    .string "Ethiopians$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_4::
    .string "And he took the fenced cities which\n"
    .string "pertained to Judah, and came to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_5::
    .string "Then came Shemaiah the prophet to\n"
    .string "Rehoboam, and to the princes of\l"
    .string "Judah, that were gathered together to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem because of Shishak, and\l"
    .string "said unto them, Thus saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "Ye have forsaken me, and therefore\l"
    .string "have I also left you in the hand of\l"
    .string "Shishak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_6::
    .string "Whereupon the princes of Israel\n"
    .string "and the king humbled themselves;\l"
    .string "and they said, The LORD is righteous.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_7::
    .string "And when the LORD saw that they\n"
    .string "humbled themselves, the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, They\l"
    .string "have humbled themselves; therefore\l"
    .string "I will not destroy them, but I will\l"
    .string "grant them some deliverance; and my\l"
    .string "wrath shall not be poured out upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem by the hand of Shishak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_8::
    .string "Nevertheless they shall be his\n"
    .string "servants; that they may know my\l"
    .string "service, and the service of the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of the countries.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_9::
    .string "So Shishak king of Egypt came up\n"
    .string "against Jerusalem, and took away the\l"
    .string "treasures of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the treasures of the king’s\l"
    .string "house; he took all: he carried away\l"
    .string "also the shields of gold which\l"
    .string "Solomon had made.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_10::
    .string "Instead of which king Rehoboam made\n"
    .string "shields of brass, and committed them\l"
    .string "to the hands of the chief of the\l"
    .string "guard, that kept the entrance of the\l"
    .string "king’s house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_11::
    .string "And when the king entered into the\n"
    .string "house of the LORD, the guard came and\l"
    .string "fetched them, and brought them again\l"
    .string "into the guard chamber.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_12::
    .string "And when he humbled himself, the\n"
    .string "wrath of the LORD turned from him,\l"
    .string "that he would not destroy him\l"
    .string "altogether: and also in Judah\l"
    .string "things went well.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_13::
    .string "So king Rehoboam strengthened\n"
    .string "himself in Jerusalem, and reigned:\l"
    .string "for Rehoboam was one and forty years\l"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned seventeen years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, the city which the LORD\l"
    .string "had chosen out of all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel, to put his name there. And\l"
    .string "his mother’s name was Naamah an\l"
    .string "Ammonitess.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_14::
    .string "And he did evil, because he\n"
    .string "prepared not his heart to seek the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_15::
    .string "Now the acts of Rehoboam, first and\n"
    .string "last, are they not written in the\l"
    .string "book of Shemaiah the prophet, and of\l"
    .string "Iddo the seer concerning\l"
    .string "genealogies? And there were wars\l"
    .string "between Rehoboam and Jeroboam\l"
    .string "continually.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_12_16::
    .string "And Rehoboam slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried in the city\l"
    .string "of David: and Abijah his son reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_1::
    .string "Now in the eighteenth year of king\n"
    .string "Jeroboam began Abijah to reign over\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_2::
    .string "He reigned three years in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem. His mother’s name also\l"
    .string "was Michaiah the daughter of Uriel\l"
    .string "of Gibeah. And there was war between\l"
    .string "Abijah and Jeroboam.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_3::
    .string "And Abijah set the battle in array\n"
    .string "with an army of valiant men of war,\l"
    .string "even four hundred thousand chosen\l"
    .string "men: Jeroboam also set the battle in\l"
    .string "array against him with eight hundred\l"
    .string "thousand chosen men, being mighty men\l"
    .string "of valour.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_4::
    .string "And Abijah stood up upon mount\n"
    .string "Zemaraim, which is in mount Ephraim,\l"
    .string "and said, Hear me, thou Jeroboam, and\l"
    .string "all Israel;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_5::
    .string "Ought ye not to know that the LORD\n"
    .string "God of Israel gave the kingdom over\l"
    .string "Israel to David for ever, even to him\l"
    .string "and to his sons by a covenant of\l"
    .string "salt?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_6::
    .string "Yet Jeroboam the son of Nebat, the\n"
    .string "servant of Solomon the son of David,\l"
    .string "is risen up, and hath rebelled\l"
    .string "against his lord$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_7::
    .string "And there are gathered unto him vain\n"
    .string "men, the children of Belial, and\l"
    .string "have strengthened themselves\l"
    .string "against Rehoboam the son of Solomon,\l"
    .string "when Rehoboam was young and\l"
    .string "tenderhearted, and could not\l"
    .string "withstand them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_8::
    .string "And now ye think to withstand the\n"
    .string "kingdom of the LORD in the hand of\l"
    .string "the sons of David; and ye be a great\l"
    .string "multitude, and there are with you\l"
    .string "golden calves, which Jeroboam made\l"
    .string "you for gods.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_9::
    .string "Have ye not cast out the priests of\n"
    .string "the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the\l"
    .string "Levites, and have made you priests\l"
    .string "after the manner of the nations of\l"
    .string "other lands? so that whosoever\l"
    .string "cometh to consecrate himself with a\l"
    .string "young bullock and seven rams, the\l"
    .string "same may be a priest of them that are\l"
    .string "no gods.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_10::
    .string "But as for us, the LORD is our God,\n"
    .string "and we have not forsaken him; and the\l"
    .string "priests, which minister unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, are the sons of Aaron, and the\l"
    .string "Levites wait upon their business:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_11::
    .string "And they burn unto the LORD every\n"
    .string "morning and every evening burnt\l"
    .string "sacrifices and sweet incense: the\l"
    .string "shewbread also set they in order\l"
    .string "upon the pure table; and the\l"
    .string "candlestick of gold with the lamps\l"
    .string "thereof, to burn every evening: for\l"
    .string "we keep the charge of the LORD our\l"
    .string "God; but ye have forsaken him$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_12::
    .string "And, behold, God himself is with us\n"
    .string "for our captain, and his priests\l"
    .string "with sounding trumpets to cry alarm\l"
    .string "against you. O children of Israel,\l"
    .string "fight ye not against the LORD God of\l"
    .string "your fathers; for ye shall not\l"
    .string "prosper.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_13::
    .string "But Jeroboam caused an ambushment\n"
    .string "to come about behind them: so they\l"
    .string "were before Judah, and the ambushment\l"
    .string "was behind them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_14::
    .string "And when Judah looked back,\n"
    .string "behold, the battle was before and\l"
    .string "behind: and they cried unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the priests sounded with the\l"
    .string "trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_15::
    .string "Then the men of Judah gave a shout:\n"
    .string "and as the men of Judah shouted, it\l"
    .string "came to pass, that God smote\l"
    .string "Jeroboam and all Israel before\l"
    .string "Abijah and Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_16::
    .string "And the children of Israel fled\n"
    .string "before Judah: and God delivered them\l"
    .string "into their hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_17::
    .string "And Abijah and his people slew\n"
    .string "them with a great slaughter: so\l"
    .string "there fell down slain of Israel\l"
    .string "five hundred thousand chosen men.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_18::
    .string "Thus the children of Israel were\n"
    .string "brought under at that time, and the\l"
    .string "children of Judah prevailed,\l"
    .string "because they relied upon the LORD\l"
    .string "God of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_19::
    .string "And Abijah pursued after Jeroboam,\n"
    .string "and took cities from him, Bethel\l"
    .string "with the towns thereof, and Jeshanah\l"
    .string "with the towns thereof, and Ephraim\l"
    .string "with the towns thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_20::
    .string "Neither did Jeroboam recover\n"
    .string "strength again in the days of Abijah:\l"
    .string "and the LORD struck him, and he died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_21::
    .string "But Abijah waxed mighty, and married\n"
    .string "fourteen wives, and begat twenty and\l"
    .string "two sons, and sixteen daughters.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_13_22::
    .string "And the rest of the acts of Abijah,\n"
    .string "and his ways, and his sayings, are\l"
    .string "written in the story of the prophet\l"
    .string "Iddo.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_1::
    .string "So Abijah slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and they buried him in the city of\l"
    .string "David: and Asa his son reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead. In his days the land was quiet\l"
    .string "ten years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_2::
    .string "And Asa did that which was good and\n"
    .string "right in the eyes of the LORD his God:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_3::
    .string "For he took away the altars of the\n"
    .string "strange gods, and the high places,\l"
    .string "and brake down the images, and cut\l"
    .string "down the groves:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_4::
    .string "And commanded Judah to seek the LORD\n"
    .string "God of their fathers, and to do the\l"
    .string "law and the commandment$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_5::
    .string "Also he took away out of all the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah the high places and\l"
    .string "the images: and the kingdom was quiet\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_6::
    .string "And he built fenced cities in\n"
    .string "Judah: for the land had rest, and he\l"
    .string "had no war in those years; because\l"
    .string "the LORD had given him rest.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_7::
    .string "Therefore he said unto Judah, Let us\n"
    .string "build these cities, and make about\l"
    .string "them walls, and towers, gates, and\l"
    .string "bars, while the land is yet before\l"
    .string "us; because we have sought the LORD\l"
    .string "our God, we have sought him, and he\l"
    .string "hath given us rest on every side. So\l"
    .string "they built and prospered.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_8::
    .string "And Asa had an army of men that bare\n"
    .string "targets and spears, out of Judah\l"
    .string "three hundred thousand; and out of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, that bare shields and drew\l"
    .string "bows, two hundred and fourscore\l"
    .string "thousand: all these were mighty men\l"
    .string "of valour.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_9::
    .string "And there came out against them\n"
    .string "Zerah the Ethiopian with an host of\l"
    .string "a thousand thousand, and three\l"
    .string "hundred chariots; and came unto\l"
    .string "Mareshah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_10::
    .string "Then Asa went out against him, and\n"
    .string "they set the battle in array in the\l"
    .string "valley of Zephathah at Mareshah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_11::
    .string "And Asa cried unto the LORD his God,\n"
    .string "and said, LORD, it is nothing with\l"
    .string "thee to help, whether with many, or\l"
    .string "with them that have no power: help\l"
    .string "us, O LORD our God; for we rest on\l"
    .string "thee, and in thy name we go against\l"
    .string "this multitude. O LORD, thou art our\l"
    .string "God; let no man prevail against\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_12::
    .string "So the LORD smote the Ethiopians\n"
    .string "before Asa, and before Judah; and the\l"
    .string "Ethiopians fled.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_13::
    .string "And Asa and the people that were\n"
    .string "with him pursued them unto Gerar:\l"
    .string "and the Ethiopians were overthrown,\l"
    .string "that they could not recover\l"
    .string "themselves; for they were destroyed\l"
    .string "before the LORD, and before his host;\l"
    .string "and they carried away very much\l"
    .string "spoil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_14::
    .string "And they smote all the cities\n"
    .string "round about Gerar; for the fear of\l"
    .string "the LORD came upon them: and they\l"
    .string "spoiled all the cities; for there\l"
    .string "was exceeding much spoil in them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_14_15::
    .string "They smote also the tents of\n"
    .string "cattle, and carried away sheep and\l"
    .string "camels in abundance, and returned to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_1::
    .string "And the Spirit of God came upon\n"
    .string "Azariah the son of Oded:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_2::
    .string "And he went out to meet Asa, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Hear ye me, Asa, and all\l"
    .string "Judah and Benjamin; The LORD is with\l"
    .string "you, while ye be with him; and if ye\l"
    .string "seek him, he will be found of you;\l"
    .string "but if ye forsake him, he will\l"
    .string "forsake you$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_3::
    .string "Now for a long season Israel hath\n"
    .string "been without the true God, and\l"
    .string "without a teaching priest, and\l"
    .string "without law.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_4::
    .string "But when they in their trouble did\n"
    .string "turn unto the LORD God of Israel, and\l"
    .string "sought him, he was found of them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_5::
    .string "And in those times there was no\n"
    .string "peace to him that went out, nor to him\l"
    .string "that came in, but great vexations\l"
    .string "were upon all the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "the countries.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_6::
    .string "And nation was destroyed of nation,\n"
    .string "and city of city: for God did vex them\l"
    .string "with all adversity.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_7::
    .string "Be ye strong therefore, and let not\n"
    .string "your hands be weak: for your work\l"
    .string "shall be rewarded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_8::
    .string "And when Asa heard these words, and\n"
    .string "the prophecy of Oded the prophet,\l"
    .string "he took courage, and put away the\l"
    .string "abominable idols out of all the\l"
    .string "land of Judah and Benjamin, and out\l"
    .string "of the cities which he had taken from\l"
    .string "mount Ephraim, and renewed the\l"
    .string "altar of the LORD, that was before\l"
    .string "the porch of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_9::
    .string "And he gathered all Judah and\n"
    .string "Benjamin, and the strangers with them\l"
    .string "out of Ephraim and Manasseh, and out\l"
    .string "of Simeon: for they fell to him out\l"
    .string "of Israel in abundance, when they\l"
    .string "saw that the LORD his God was with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_10::
    .string "So they gathered themselves\n"
    .string "together at Jerusalem in the third\l"
    .string "month, in the fifteenth year of the\l"
    .string "reign of Asa.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_11::
    .string "And they offered unto the LORD the\n"
    .string "same time, of the spoil which they\l"
    .string "had brought, seven hundred oxen and\l"
    .string "seven thousand sheep.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_12::
    .string "And they entered into a covenant to\n"
    .string "seek the LORD God of their fathers\l"
    .string "with all their heart and with all\l"
    .string "their soul;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_13::
    .string "That whosoever would not seek the\n"
    .string "LORD God of Israel should be put to\l"
    .string "death, whether small or great,\l"
    .string "whether man or woman$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_14::
    .string "And they sware unto the LORD with a\n"
    .string "loud voice, and with shouting, and\l"
    .string "with trumpets, and with cornets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_15::
    .string "And all Judah rejoiced at the oath:\n"
    .string "for they had sworn with all their\l"
    .string "heart, and sought him with their\l"
    .string "whole desire; and he was found of\l"
    .string "them: and the LORD gave them rest\l"
    .string "round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_16::
    .string "And also concerning Maachah the\n"
    .string "mother of Asa the king, he removed\l"
    .string "her from being queen, because she had\l"
    .string "made an idol in a grove: and Asa cut\l"
    .string "down her idol, and stamped it, and\l"
    .string "burnt it at the brook Kidron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_17::
    .string "But the high places were not taken\n"
    .string "away out of Israel: nevertheless\l"
    .string "the heart of Asa was perfect all\l"
    .string "his days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_18::
    .string "And he brought into the house of God\n"
    .string "the things that his father had\l"
    .string "dedicated, and that he himself had\l"
    .string "dedicated, silver, and gold, and\l"
    .string "vessels.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_15_19::
    .string "And there was no more war unto the\n"
    .string "five and thirtieth year of the reign\l"
    .string "of Asa.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_1::
    .string "In the six and thirtieth year of the\n"
    .string "reign of Asa Baasha king of Israel\l"
    .string "came up against Judah, and built\l"
    .string "Ramah, to the intent that he might\l"
    .string "let none go out or come in to Asa king\l"
    .string "of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_2::
    .string "Then Asa brought out silver and\n"
    .string "gold out of the treasures of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD and of the king’s\l"
    .string "house, and sent to Benhadad king of\l"
    .string "Syria, that dwelt at Damascus,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_3::
    .string "There is a league between me and\n"
    .string "thee, as there was between my father\l"
    .string "and thy father: behold, I have sent\l"
    .string "thee silver and gold; go, break thy\l"
    .string "league with Baasha king of Israel,\l"
    .string "that he may depart from me$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_4::
    .string "And Benhadad hearkened unto king\n"
    .string "Asa, and sent the captains of his\l"
    .string "armies against the cities of Israel;\l"
    .string "and they smote Ijon, and Dan, and\l"
    .string "Abelmaim, and all the store cities\l"
    .string "of Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_5::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Baasha\n"
    .string "heard it, that he left off building\l"
    .string "of Ramah, and let his work cease.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_6::
    .string "Then Asa the king took all Judah;\n"
    .string "and they carried away the stones of\l"
    .string "Ramah, and the timber thereof,\l"
    .string "wherewith Baasha was building; and\l"
    .string "he built therewith Geba and Mizpah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_7::
    .string "And at that time Hanani the seer\n"
    .string "came to Asa king of Judah, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Because thou hast relied\l"
    .string "on the king of Syria, and not relied\l"
    .string "on the LORD thy God, therefore is the\l"
    .string "host of the king of Syria escaped\l"
    .string "out of thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_8::
    .string "Were not the Ethiopians and the\n"
    .string "Lubims a huge host, with very many\l"
    .string "chariots and horsemen? yet, because\l"
    .string "thou didst rely on the LORD, he\l"
    .string "delivered them into thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_9::
    .string "For the eyes of the LORD run to and\n"
    .string "fro throughout the whole earth, to\l"
    .string "shew himself strong in the behalf\l"
    .string "of them whose heart is perfect\l"
    .string "toward him. Herein thou hast done\l"
    .string "foolishly: therefore from\l"
    .string "henceforth thou shalt have wars.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_10::
    .string "Then Asa was wroth with the seer,\n"
    .string "and put him in a prison house; for\l"
    .string "he was in a rage with him because of\l"
    .string "this thing. And Asa oppressed some\l"
    .string "of the people the same time.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_11::
    .string "And, behold, the acts of Asa, first\n"
    .string "and last, lo, they are written in\l"
    .string "the book of the kings of Judah and\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_12::
    .string "And Asa in the thirty and ninth year\n"
    .string "of his reign was diseased in his\l"
    .string "feet, until his disease was\l"
    .string "exceeding great: yet in his disease\l"
    .string "he sought not to the LORD, but to the\l"
    .string "physicians.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_13::
    .string "And Asa slept with his fathers, and\n"
    .string "died in the one and fortieth year of\l"
    .string "his reign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_16_14::
    .string "And they buried him in his own\n"
    .string "sepulchres, which he had made for\l"
    .string "himself in the city of David, and\l"
    .string "laid him in the bed which was filled\l"
    .string "with sweet odours and divers kinds of\l"
    .string "spices prepared by the\l"
    .string "apothecaries’ art: and they made a\l"
    .string "very great burning for him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_1::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat his son reigned in\n"
    .string "his stead, and strengthened himself\l"
    .string "against Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_2::
    .string "And he placed forces in all the\n"
    .string "fenced cities of Judah, and set\l"
    .string "garrisons in the land of Judah, and\l"
    .string "in the cities of Ephraim, which Asa\l"
    .string "his father had taken.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_3::
    .string "And the LORD was with Jehoshaphat,\n"
    .string "because he walked in the first ways\l"
    .string "of his father David, and sought not\l"
    .string "unto Baalim;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_4::
    .string "But sought to the Lord God of his\n"
    .string "father, and walked in his\l"
    .string "commandments, and not after the\l"
    .string "doings of Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_5::
    .string "Therefore the LORD stablished the\n"
    .string "kingdom in his hand; and all Judah\l"
    .string "brought to Jehoshaphat presents;\l"
    .string "and he had riches and honour in\l"
    .string "abundance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_6::
    .string "And his heart was lifted up in the\n"
    .string "ways of the LORD: moreover he took\l"
    .string "away the high places and groves out\l"
    .string "of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_7::
    .string "Also in the third year of his reign\n"
    .string "he sent to his princes, even to\l"
    .string "Benhail, and to Obadiah, and to\l"
    .string "Zechariah, and to Nethaneel, and to\l"
    .string "Michaiah, to teach in the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_8::
    .string "And with them he sent Levites, even\n"
    .string "Shemaiah, and Nethaniah, and\l"
    .string "Zebadiah, and Asahel, and\l"
    .string "Shemiramoth, and Jehonathan, and\l"
    .string "Adonijah, and Tobijah, and\l"
    .string "Tobadonijah, Levites; and with them\l"
    .string "Elishama and Jehoram, priests.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_9::
    .string "And they taught in Judah, and had\n"
    .string "the book of the law of the LORD with\l"
    .string "them, and went about throughout all\l"
    .string "the cities of Judah, and taught the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_10::
    .string "And the fear of the LORD fell upon\n"
    .string "all the kingdoms of the lands that\l"
    .string "were round about Judah, so that they\l"
    .string "made no war against Jehoshaphat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_11::
    .string "Also some of the Philistines\n"
    .string "brought Jehoshaphat presents, and\l"
    .string "tribute silver; and the Arabians\l"
    .string "brought him flocks, seven thousand\l"
    .string "and seven hundred rams, and seven\l"
    .string "thousand and seven hundred he goats.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_12::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat waxed great\n"
    .string "exceedingly; and he built in Judah\l"
    .string "castles, and cities of store.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_13::
    .string "And he had much business in the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah: and the men of war,\l"
    .string "mighty men of valour, were in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_14::
    .string "And these are the numbers of them\n"
    .string "according to the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers: Of Judah, the captains of\l"
    .string "thousands; Adnah the chief, and with\l"
    .string "him mighty men of valour three\l"
    .string "hundred thousand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_15::
    .string "And next to him was Jehohanan the\n"
    .string "captain, and with him two hundred\l"
    .string "and fourscore thousand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_16::
    .string "And next him was Amasiah the son of\n"
    .string "Zichri, who willingly offered\l"
    .string "himself unto the LORD; and with him\l"
    .string "two hundred thousand mighty men of\l"
    .string "valour.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_17::
    .string "And of Benjamin; Eliada a mighty\n"
    .string "man of valour, and with him armed men\l"
    .string "with bow and shield two hundred\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_18::
    .string "And next him was Jehozabad, and with\n"
    .string "him an hundred and fourscore\l"
    .string "thousand ready prepared for the war.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_17_19::
    .string "These waited on the king, beside\n"
    .string "those whom the king put in the\l"
    .string "fenced cities throughout all Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_1::
    .string "Now Jehoshaphat had riches and\n"
    .string "honour in abundance, and joined\l"
    .string "affinity with Ahab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_2::
    .string "And after certain years he went down\n"
    .string "to Ahab to Samaria. And Ahab killed\l"
    .string "sheep and oxen for him in abundance,\l"
    .string "and for the people that he had with\l"
    .string "him, and persuaded him to go up with\l"
    .string "him to Ramothgilead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_3::
    .string "And Ahab king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat king of Judah, Wilt\l"
    .string "thou go with me to Ramothgilead? And\l"
    .string "he answered him, I am as thou art, and\l"
    .string "my people as thy people; and we\l"
    .string "will be with thee in the war.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_4::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat said unto the king\n"
    .string "of Israel, Enquire, I pray thee, at\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD to day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_5::
    .string "Therefore the king of Israel\n"
    .string "gathered together of prophets four\l"
    .string "hundred men, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Shall we go to Ramothgilead to\l"
    .string "battle, or shall I forbear? And\l"
    .string "they said, Go up; for God will\l"
    .string "deliver it into the king’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_6::
    .string "But Jehoshaphat said, Is there not\n"
    .string "here a prophet of the LORD besides,\l"
    .string "that we might enquire of him?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_7::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man,\l"
    .string "by whom we may enquire of the LORD:\l"
    .string "but I hate him; for he never\l"
    .string "prophesied good unto me, but always\l"
    .string "evil: the same is Micaiah the son of\l"
    .string "Imla. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not\l"
    .string "the king say so$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_8::
    .string "And the king of Israel called for\n"
    .string "one of his officers, and said, Fetch\l"
    .string "quickly Micaiah the son of Imla.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_9::
    .string "And the king of Israel and\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat king of Judah sat either\l"
    .string "of them on his throne, clothed in\l"
    .string "their robes, and they sat in a void\l"
    .string "place at the entering in of the gate\l"
    .string "of Samaria; and all the prophets\l"
    .string "prophesied before them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_10::
    .string "And Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah\n"
    .string "had made him horns of iron, and said,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, With these thou\l"
    .string "shalt push Syria until they be\l"
    .string "consumed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_11::
    .string "And all the prophets prophesied\n"
    .string "so, saying, Go up to Ramothgilead,\l"
    .string "and prosper: for the LORD shall\l"
    .string "deliver it into the hand of the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_12::
    .string "And the messenger that went to\n"
    .string "call Micaiah spake to him, saying,\l"
    .string "Behold, the words of the prophets\l"
    .string "declare good to the king with one\l"
    .string "assent; let thy word therefore, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, be like one of theirs, and\l"
    .string "speak thou good.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_13::
    .string "And Micaiah said, As the LORD\n"
    .string "liveth, even what my God saith, that\l"
    .string "will I speak.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_14::
    .string "And when he was come to the king, the\n"
    .string "king said unto him, Micaiah, shall\l"
    .string "we go to Ramothgilead to battle, or\l"
    .string "shall I forbear? And he said, Go ye\l"
    .string "up, and prosper, and they shall be\l"
    .string "delivered into your hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_15::
    .string "And the king said to him, How many\n"
    .string "times shall I adjure thee that thou\l"
    .string "say nothing but the truth to me in\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_16::
    .string "Then he said, I did see all Israel\n"
    .string "scattered upon the mountains, as\l"
    .string "sheep that have no shepherd: and the\l"
    .string "LORD said, These have no master; let\l"
    .string "them return therefore every man to\l"
    .string "his house in peace$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_17::
    .string "And the king of Israel said to\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, Did I not tell thee\l"
    .string "that he would not prophesy good\l"
    .string "unto me, but evil?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_18::
    .string "Again he said, Therefore hear the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD; I saw the LORD\l"
    .string "sitting upon his throne, and all\l"
    .string "the host of heaven standing on his\l"
    .string "right hand and on his left$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_19::
    .string "And the LORD said, Who shall entice\n"
    .string "Ahab king of Israel, that he may go\l"
    .string "up and fall at Ramothgilead? And\l"
    .string "one spake saying after this manner,\l"
    .string "and another saying after that manner.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_20::
    .string "Then there came out a spirit, and\n"
    .string "stood before the LORD, and said, I\l"
    .string "will entice him. And the LORD said\l"
    .string "unto him, Wherewith?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_21::
    .string "And he said, I will go out, and be a\n"
    .string "lying spirit in the mouth of all\l"
    .string "his prophets. And the Lord said,\l"
    .string "Thou shalt entice him, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt also prevail: go out, and do\l"
    .string "even so$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_22::
    .string "Now therefore, behold, the LORD\n"
    .string "hath put a lying spirit in the\l"
    .string "mouth of these thy prophets, and the\l"
    .string "LORD hath spoken evil against thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_23::
    .string "Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah\n"
    .string "came near, and smote Micaiah upon\l"
    .string "the cheek, and said, Which way went\l"
    .string "the Spirit of the LORD from me to\l"
    .string "speak unto thee?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_24::
    .string "And Micaiah said, Behold, thou\n"
    .string "shalt see on that day when thou\l"
    .string "shalt go into an inner chamber to\l"
    .string "hide thyself$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_25::
    .string "Then the king of Israel said, Take\n"
    .string "ye Micaiah, and carry him back to\l"
    .string "Amon the governor of the city, and to\l"
    .string "Joash the king’s son;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_26::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the king, Put\n"
    .string "this fellow in the prison, and feed\l"
    .string "him with bread of affliction and\l"
    .string "with water of affliction, until I\l"
    .string "return in peace$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_27::
    .string "And Micaiah said, If thou certainly\n"
    .string "return in peace, then hath not the\l"
    .string "LORD spoken by me. And he said,\l"
    .string "Hearken, all ye people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_28::
    .string "So the king of Israel and\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went\l"
    .string "up to Ramothgilead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_29::
    .string "And the king of Israel said unto\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, I will disguise\l"
    .string "myself, and I will go to the\l"
    .string "battle; but put thou on thy robes.\l"
    .string "So the king of Israel disguised\l"
    .string "himself; and they went to the\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_30::
    .string "Now the king of Syria had commanded\n"
    .string "the captains of the chariots that\l"
    .string "were with him, saying, Fight ye not\l"
    .string "with small or great, save only with\l"
    .string "the king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_31::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "captains of the chariots saw\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, that they said, It is\l"
    .string "the king of Israel. Therefore they\l"
    .string "compassed about him to fight: but\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD\l"
    .string "helped him; and God moved them to\l"
    .string "depart from him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_32::
    .string "For it came to pass, that, when the\n"
    .string "captains of the chariots perceived\l"
    .string "that it was not the king of Israel,\l"
    .string "they turned back again from pursuing\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_33::
    .string "And a certain man drew a bow at a\n"
    .string "venture, and smote the king of\l"
    .string "Israel between the joints of the\l"
    .string "harness: therefore he said to his\l"
    .string "chariot man, Turn thine hand, that\l"
    .string "thou mayest carry me out of the host;\l"
    .string "for I am wounded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_18_34::
    .string "And the battle increased that day:\n"
    .string "howbeit the king of Israel stayed\l"
    .string "himself up in his chariot against\l"
    .string "the Syrians until the even: and\l"
    .string "about the time of the sun going down\l"
    .string "he died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_1::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat the king of Judah\n"
    .string "returned to his house in peace to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_2::
    .string "And Jehu the son of Hanani the seer\n"
    .string "went out to meet him, and said to king\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, Shouldest thou help\l"
    .string "the ungodly, and love them that hate\l"
    .string "the LORD? therefore is wrath upon\l"
    .string "thee from before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_3::
    .string "Nevertheless there are good things\n"
    .string "found in thee, in that thou hast\l"
    .string "taken away the groves out of the\l"
    .string "land, and hast prepared thine heart\l"
    .string "to seek God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_4::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat dwelt at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: and he went out again\l"
    .string "through the people from Beersheba\l"
    .string "to mount Ephraim, and brought them\l"
    .string "back unto the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_5::
    .string "And he set judges in the land\n"
    .string "throughout all the fenced cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, city by city,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_6::
    .string "And said to the judges, Take heed\n"
    .string "what ye do: for ye judge not for man,\l"
    .string "but for the LORD, who is with you in\l"
    .string "the judgment$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_7::
    .string "Wherefore now let the fear of the\n"
    .string "LORD be upon you; take heed and do\l"
    .string "it: for there is no iniquity with the\l"
    .string "LORD our God, nor respect of\l"
    .string "persons, nor taking of gifts.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_8::
    .string "Moreover in Jerusalem did\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat set of the Levites, and\l"
    .string "of the priests, and of the chief of\l"
    .string "the fathers of Israel, for the\l"
    .string "judgment of the LORD, and for\l"
    .string "controversies, when they returned to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_9::
    .string "And he charged them, saying, Thus\n"
    .string "shall ye do in the fear of the LORD,\l"
    .string "faithfully, and with a perfect\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_10::
    .string "And what cause soever shall come\n"
    .string "to you of your brethren that dwell\l"
    .string "in your cities, between blood and\l"
    .string "blood, between law and commandment,\l"
    .string "statutes and judgments, ye shall\l"
    .string "even warn them that they trespass\l"
    .string "not against the LORD, and so wrath\l"
    .string "come upon you, and upon your\l"
    .string "brethren: this do, and ye shall not\l"
    .string "trespass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_19_11::
    .string "And, behold, Amariah the chief\n"
    .string "priest is over you in all matters of\l"
    .string "the LORD; and Zebadiah the son of\l"
    .string "Ishmael, the ruler of the house of\l"
    .string "Judah, for all the king’s matters:\l"
    .string "also the Levites shall be officers\l"
    .string "before you. Deal courageously, and\l"
    .string "the LORD shall be with the good.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_1::
    .string "It came to pass after this also,\n"
    .string "that the children of Moab, and the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon, and with them\l"
    .string "other beside the Ammonites, came\l"
    .string "against Jehoshaphat to battle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_2::
    .string "Then there came some that told\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, saying, There cometh a\l"
    .string "great multitude against thee from\l"
    .string "beyond the sea on this side Syria;\l"
    .string "and, behold, they be in\l"
    .string "Hazazontamar, which is Engedi.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_3::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat feared, and set\n"
    .string "himself to seek the LORD, and\l"
    .string "proclaimed a fast throughout all\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_4::
    .string "And Judah gathered themselves\n"
    .string "together, to ask help of the LORD:\l"
    .string "even out of all the cities of Judah\l"
    .string "they came to seek the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_5::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat stood in the\n"
    .string "congregation of Judah and Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "in the house of the LORD, before the\l"
    .string "new court,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_6::
    .string "And said, O LORD God of our fathers,\n"
    .string "art not thou God in heaven? and\l"
    .string "rulest not thou over all the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of the heathen? and in thine\l"
    .string "hand is there not power and might, so\l"
    .string "that none is able to withstand thee?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_7::
    .string "Art not thou our God, who didst\n"
    .string "drive out the inhabitants of this\l"
    .string "land before thy people Israel, and\l"
    .string "gavest it to the seed of Abraham thy\l"
    .string "friend for ever?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_8::
    .string "And they dwelt therein, and have\n"
    .string "built thee a sanctuary therein for\l"
    .string "thy name, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_9::
    .string "If, when evil cometh upon us, as\n"
    .string "the sword, judgment, or pestilence,\l"
    .string "or famine, we stand before this\l"
    .string "house, and in thy presence, (for thy\l"
    .string "name is in this house,) and cry unto\l"
    .string "thee in our affliction, then thou\l"
    .string "wilt hear and help$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_10::
    .string "And now, behold, the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon and Moab and mount Seir, whom\l"
    .string "thou wouldest not let Israel\l"
    .string "invade, when they came out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, but they turned from\l"
    .string "them, and destroyed them not;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_11::
    .string "Behold, I say, how they reward us,\n"
    .string "to come to cast us out of thy\l"
    .string "possession, which thou hast given us\l"
    .string "to inherit$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_12::
    .string "O our God, wilt thou not judge them?\n"
    .string "for we have no might against this\l"
    .string "great company that cometh against\l"
    .string "us; neither know we what to do: but\l"
    .string "our eyes are upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_13::
    .string "And all Judah stood before the\n"
    .string "LORD, with their little ones, their\l"
    .string "wives, and their children.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_14::
    .string "Then upon Jahaziel the son of\n"
    .string "Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the\l"
    .string "son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, a\l"
    .string "Levite of the sons of Asaph, came the\l"
    .string "Spirit of the LORD in the midst of\l"
    .string "the congregation;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_15::
    .string "And he said, Hearken ye, all Judah,\n"
    .string "and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "thou king Jehoshaphat, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD unto you, Be not afraid nor\l"
    .string "dismayed by reason of this great\l"
    .string "multitude; for the battle is not\l"
    .string "yours, but God’s$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_16::
    .string "To morrow go ye down against them:\n"
    .string "behold, they come up by the cliff\l"
    .string "of Ziz; and ye shall find them at\l"
    .string "the end of the brook, before the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Jeruel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_17::
    .string "Ye shall not need to fight in this\n"
    .string "battle: set yourselves, stand ye\l"
    .string "still, and see the salvation of the\l"
    .string "LORD with you, O Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: fear not, nor be\l"
    .string "dismayed; to morrow go out against\l"
    .string "them: for the LORD will be with you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_18::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat bowed his head with\n"
    .string "his face to the ground: and all\l"
    .string "Judah and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem fell before the LORD,\l"
    .string "worshipping the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_19::
    .string "And the Levites, of the children of\n"
    .string "the Kohathites, and of the children\l"
    .string "of the Korhites, stood up to praise\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel with a loud\l"
    .string "voice on high.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_20::
    .string "And they rose early in the morning,\n"
    .string "and went forth into the wilderness\l"
    .string "of Tekoa: and as they went forth,\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat stood and said, Hear me,\l"
    .string "O Judah, and ye inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; Believe in the LORD your\l"
    .string "God, so shall ye be established;\l"
    .string "believe his prophets, so shall ye\l"
    .string "prosper.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_21::
    .string "And when he had consulted with the\n"
    .string "people, he appointed singers unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, and that should praise the\l"
    .string "beauty of holiness, as they went out\l"
    .string "before the army, and to say, Praise\l"
    .string "the LORD; for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_22::
    .string "And when they began to sing and to\n"
    .string "praise, the LORD set ambushments\l"
    .string "against the children of Ammon, Moab,\l"
    .string "and mount Seir, which were come\l"
    .string "against Judah; and they were smitten.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_23::
    .string "For the children of Ammon and Moab\n"
    .string "stood up against the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "mount Seir, utterly to slay and\l"
    .string "destroy them: and when they had made\l"
    .string "an end of the inhabitants of Seir,\l"
    .string "every one helped to destroy another.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_24::
    .string "And when Judah came toward the watch\n"
    .string "tower in the wilderness, they\l"
    .string "looked unto the multitude, and,\l"
    .string "behold, they were dead bodies\l"
    .string "fallen to the earth, and none\l"
    .string "escaped.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_25::
    .string "And when Jehoshaphat and his\n"
    .string "people came to take away the spoil\l"
    .string "of them, they found among them in\l"
    .string "abundance both riches with the dead\l"
    .string "bodies, and precious jewels, which\l"
    .string "they stripped off for themselves,\l"
    .string "more than they could carry away: and\l"
    .string "they were three days in gathering of\l"
    .string "the spoil, it was so much.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_26::
    .string "And on the fourth day they\n"
    .string "assembled themselves in the\l"
    .string "valley of Berachah; for there they\l"
    .string "blessed the LORD: therefore the name\l"
    .string "of the same place was called, The\l"
    .string "valley of Berachah, unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_27::
    .string "Then they returned, every man of\n"
    .string "Judah and Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat in the forefront of\l"
    .string "them, to go again to Jerusalem with\l"
    .string "joy; for the LORD had made them to\l"
    .string "rejoice over their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_28::
    .string "And they came to Jerusalem with\n"
    .string "psalteries and harps and trumpets\l"
    .string "unto the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_29::
    .string "And the fear of God was on all the\n"
    .string "kingdoms of those countries, when\l"
    .string "they had heard that the LORD fought\l"
    .string "against the enemies of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_30::
    .string "So the realm of Jehoshaphat was\n"
    .string "quiet: for his God gave him rest\l"
    .string "round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_31::
    .string "And Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah:\n"
    .string "he was thirty and five years old\l"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned twenty and five years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_32::
    .string "And he walked in the way of Asa his\n"
    .string "father, and departed not from it,\l"
    .string "doing that which was right in the\l"
    .string "sight of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_33::
    .string "Howbeit the high places were not\n"
    .string "taken away: for as yet the people\l"
    .string "had not prepared their hearts unto\l"
    .string "the God of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_34::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, first and last,\l"
    .string "behold, they are written in the book\l"
    .string "of Jehu the son of Hanani, who is\l"
    .string "mentioned in the book of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_35::
    .string "And after this did Jehoshaphat king\n"
    .string "of Judah join himself with Ahaziah\l"
    .string "king of Israel, who did very\l"
    .string "wickedly:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_36::
    .string "And he joined himself with him to\n"
    .string "make ships to go to Tarshish: and\l"
    .string "they made the ships in Eziongaber$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_20_37::
    .string "Then Eliezer the son of Dodavah of\n"
    .string "Mareshah prophesied against\l"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, saying, Because thou\l"
    .string "hast joined thyself with Ahaziah,\l"
    .string "the LORD hath broken thy works. And\l"
    .string "the ships were broken, that they\l"
    .string "were not able to go to Tarshish.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_1::
    .string "Now Jehoshaphat slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and was buried with his\l"
    .string "fathers in the city of David. And\l"
    .string "Jehoram his son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_2::
    .string "And he had brethren the sons of\n"
    .string "Jehoshaphat, Azariah, and Jehiel,\l"
    .string "and Zechariah, and Azariah, and\l"
    .string "Michael, and Shephatiah: all these\l"
    .string "were the sons of Jehoshaphat king of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_3::
    .string "And their father gave them great\n"
    .string "gifts of silver, and of gold, and of\l"
    .string "precious things, with fenced cities\l"
    .string "in Judah: but the kingdom gave he to\l"
    .string "Jehoram; because he was the\l"
    .string "firstborn.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_4::
    .string "Now when Jehoram was risen up to\n"
    .string "the kingdom of his father, he\l"
    .string "strengthened himself, and slew all\l"
    .string "his brethren with the sword, and\l"
    .string "divers also of the princes of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_5::
    .string "Jehoram was thirty and two years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned eight years in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_6::
    .string "And he walked in the way of the\n"
    .string "kings of Israel, like as did the\l"
    .string "house of Ahab: for he had the\l"
    .string "daughter of Ahab to wife: and he\l"
    .string "wrought that which was evil in the\l"
    .string "eyes of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_7::
    .string "Howbeit the LORD would not destroy\n"
    .string "the house of David, because of the\l"
    .string "covenant that he had made with David,\l"
    .string "and as he promised to give a light\l"
    .string "to him and to his sons for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_8::
    .string "In his days the Edomites revolted\n"
    .string "from under the dominion of Judah, and\l"
    .string "made themselves a king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_9::
    .string "Then Jehoram went forth with his\n"
    .string "princes, and all his chariots with\l"
    .string "him: and he rose up by night, and\l"
    .string "smote the Edomites which compassed\l"
    .string "him in, and the captains of the\l"
    .string "chariots.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_10::
    .string "So the Edomites revolted from under\n"
    .string "the hand of Judah unto this day. The\l"
    .string "same time also did Libnah revolt\l"
    .string "from under his hand; because he had\l"
    .string "forsaken the LORD God of his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_11::
    .string "Moreover he made high places in\n"
    .string "the mountains of Judah and caused the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem to commit\l"
    .string "fornication, and compelled Judah\l"
    .string "thereto.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_12::
    .string "And there came a writing to him from\n"
    .string "Elijah the prophet, saying, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD God of David thy\l"
    .string "father, Because thou hast not walked\l"
    .string "in the ways of Jehoshaphat thy\l"
    .string "father, nor in the ways of Asa king of\l"
    .string "Judah,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_13::
    .string "But hast walked in the way of the\n"
    .string "kings of Israel, and hast made Judah\l"
    .string "and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to\l"
    .string "go a whoring, like to the whoredoms\l"
    .string "of the house of Ahab, and also hast\l"
    .string "slain thy brethren of thy father’s\l"
    .string "house, which were better than\l"
    .string "thyself:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_14::
    .string "Behold, with a great plague will\n"
    .string "the LORD smite thy people, and thy\l"
    .string "children, and thy wives, and all\l"
    .string "thy goods:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_15::
    .string "And thou shalt have great sickness\n"
    .string "by disease of thy bowels, until thy\l"
    .string "bowels fall out by reason of the\l"
    .string "sickness day by day$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_16::
    .string "Moreover the LORD stirred up\n"
    .string "against Jehoram the spirit of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and of the Arabians,\l"
    .string "that were near the Ethiopians:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_17::
    .string "And they came up into Judah, and\n"
    .string "brake into it, and carried away all\l"
    .string "the substance that was found in the\l"
    .string "king’s house, and his sons also, and\l"
    .string "his wives; so that there was never a\l"
    .string "son left him, save Jehoahaz, the\l"
    .string "youngest of his sons$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_18::
    .string "And after all this the LORD smote\n"
    .string "him in his bowels with an incurable\l"
    .string "disease.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, that in\n"
    .string "process of time, after the end of two\l"
    .string "years, his bowels fell out by\l"
    .string "reason of his sickness: so he died of\l"
    .string "sore diseases. And his people made\l"
    .string "no burning for him, like the burning\l"
    .string "of his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_21_20::
    .string "Thirty and two years old was he\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned in Jerusalem eight years,\l"
    .string "and departed without being desired.\l"
    .string "Howbeit they buried him in the city\l"
    .string "of David, but not in the sepulchres\l"
    .string "of the kings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_1::
    .string "And the inhabitants of Jerusalem\n"
    .string "made Ahaziah his youngest son king in\l"
    .string "his stead: for the band of men that\l"
    .string "came with the Arabians to the camp\l"
    .string "had slain all the eldest. So\l"
    .string "Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of\l"
    .string "Judah reigned.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_2::
    .string "Forty and two years old was Ahaziah\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned one year in Jerusalem. His\l"
    .string "mother’s name also was Athaliah the\l"
    .string "daughter of Omri.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_3::
    .string "He also walked in the ways of the\n"
    .string "house of Ahab: for his mother was his\l"
    .string "counsellor to do wickedly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_4::
    .string "Wherefore he did evil in the sight\n"
    .string "of the LORD like the house of Ahab:\l"
    .string "for they were his counsellors after\l"
    .string "the death of his father to his\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_5::
    .string "He walked also after their\n"
    .string "counsel, and went with Jehoram the\l"
    .string "son of Ahab king of Israel to war\l"
    .string "against Hazael king of Syria at\l"
    .string "Ramothgilead: and the Syrians smote\l"
    .string "Joram.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_6::
    .string "And he returned to be healed in\n"
    .string "Jezreel because of the wounds which\l"
    .string "were given him at Ramah, when he\l"
    .string "fought with Hazael king of Syria.\l"
    .string "And Azariah the son of Jehoram king\l"
    .string "of Judah went down to see Jehoram the\l"
    .string "son of Ahab at Jezreel, because he\l"
    .string "was sick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_7::
    .string "And the destruction of Ahaziah was\n"
    .string "of God by coming to Joram: for when he\l"
    .string "was come, he went out with Jehoram\l"
    .string "against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom\l"
    .string "the LORD had anointed to cut off the\l"
    .string "house of Ahab.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when Jehu\n"
    .string "was executing judgment upon the\l"
    .string "house of Ahab, and found the princes\l"
    .string "of Judah, and the sons of the\l"
    .string "brethren of Ahaziah, that ministered\l"
    .string "to Ahaziah, he slew them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_9::
    .string "And he sought Ahaziah: and they\n"
    .string "caught him, (for he was hid in\l"
    .string "Samaria,) and brought him to Jehu:\l"
    .string "and when they had slain him, they\l"
    .string "buried him: Because, said they, he is\l"
    .string "the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought\l"
    .string "the LORD with all his heart. So the\l"
    .string "house of Ahaziah had no power to\l"
    .string "keep still the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_10::
    .string "But when Athaliah the mother of\n"
    .string "Ahaziah saw that her son was dead,\l"
    .string "she arose and destroyed all the\l"
    .string "seed royal of the house of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_11::
    .string "But Jehoshabeath, the daughter of\n"
    .string "the king, took Joash the son of\l"
    .string "Ahaziah, and stole him from among\l"
    .string "the king’s sons that were slain, and\l"
    .string "put him and his nurse in a\l"
    .string "bedchamber. So Jehoshabeath, the\l"
    .string "daughter of king Jehoram, the wife of\l"
    .string "Jehoiada the priest, (for she was\l"
    .string "the sister of Ahaziah,) hid him from\l"
    .string "Athaliah, so that she slew him not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_22_12::
    .string "And he was with them hid in the\n"
    .string "house of God six years: and Athaliah\l"
    .string "reigned over the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_1::
    .string "And in the seventh year Jehoiada\n"
    .string "strengthened himself, and took the\l"
    .string "captains of hundreds, Azariah the\l"
    .string "son of Jeroham, and Ishmael the son\l"
    .string "of Jehohanan, and Azariah the son of\l"
    .string "Obed, and Maaseiah the son of Adaiah,\l"
    .string "and Elishaphat the son of Zichri,\l"
    .string "into covenant with him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_2::
    .string "And they went about in Judah, and\n"
    .string "gathered the Levites out of all the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah, and the chief of the\l"
    .string "fathers of Israel, and they came to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_3::
    .string "And all the congregation made a\n"
    .string "covenant with the king in the house\l"
    .string "of God. And he said unto them,\l"
    .string "Behold, the king’s son shall reign,\l"
    .string "as the LORD hath said of the sons of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_4::
    .string "This is the thing that ye shall do;\n"
    .string "A third part of you entering on the\l"
    .string "sabbath, of the priests and of the\l"
    .string "Levites, shall be porters of the\l"
    .string "doors;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_5::
    .string "And a third part shall be at the\n"
    .string "king’s house; and a third part at the\l"
    .string "gate of the foundation: and all the\l"
    .string "people shall be in the courts of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_6::
    .string "But let none come into the house of\n"
    .string "the LORD, save the priests, and they\l"
    .string "that minister of the Levites; they\l"
    .string "shall go in, for they are holy: but\l"
    .string "all the people shall keep the\l"
    .string "watch of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_7::
    .string "And the Levites shall compass the\n"
    .string "king round about, every man with his\l"
    .string "weapons in his hand; and whosoever\l"
    .string "else cometh into the house, he\l"
    .string "shall be put to death: but be ye\l"
    .string "with the king when he cometh in, and\l"
    .string "when he goeth out.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_8::
    .string "So the Levites and all Judah did\n"
    .string "according to all things that\l"
    .string "Jehoiada the priest had commanded,\l"
    .string "and took every man his men that were\l"
    .string "to come in on the sabbath, with them\l"
    .string "that were to go out on the sabbath:\l"
    .string "for Jehoiada the priest dismissed\l"
    .string "not the courses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_9::
    .string "Moreover Jehoiada the priest\n"
    .string "delivered to the captains of\l"
    .string "hundreds spears, and bucklers, and\l"
    .string "shields, that had been king David’s,\l"
    .string "which were in the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_10::
    .string "And he set all the people, every\n"
    .string "man having his weapon in his hand,\l"
    .string "from the right side of the temple to\l"
    .string "the left side of the temple, along\l"
    .string "by the altar and the temple, by the\l"
    .string "king round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_11::
    .string "Then they brought out the king’s\n"
    .string "son, and put upon him the crown, and\l"
    .string "gave him the testimony, and made him\l"
    .string "king. And Jehoiada and his sons\l"
    .string "anointed him, and said, God save the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_12::
    .string "Now when Athaliah heard the noise\n"
    .string "of the people running and praising\l"
    .string "the king, she came to the people\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_13::
    .string "And she looked, and, behold, the\n"
    .string "king stood at his pillar at the\l"
    .string "entering in, and the princes and the\l"
    .string "trumpets by the king: and all the\l"
    .string "people of the land rejoiced, and\l"
    .string "sounded with trumpets, also the\l"
    .string "singers with instruments of musick,\l"
    .string "and such as taught to sing praise.\l"
    .string "Then Athaliah rent her clothes, and\l"
    .string "said, Treason, Treason$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_14::
    .string "Then Jehoiada the priest brought\n"
    .string "out the captains of hundreds that\l"
    .string "were set over the host, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Have her forth of the ranges:\l"
    .string "and whoso followeth her, let him be\l"
    .string "slain with the sword. For the priest\l"
    .string "said, Slay her not in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_15::
    .string "So they laid hands on her; and when\n"
    .string "she was come to the entering of the\l"
    .string "horse gate by the king’s house, they\l"
    .string "slew her there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_16::
    .string "And Jehoiada made a covenant\n"
    .string "between him, and between all the\l"
    .string "people, and between the king, that\l"
    .string "they should be the LORD’s people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_17::
    .string "Then all the people went to the\n"
    .string "house of Baal, and brake it down, and\l"
    .string "brake his altars and his images in\l"
    .string "pieces, and slew Mattan the priest\l"
    .string "of Baal before the altars.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_18::
    .string "Also Jehoiada appointed the\n"
    .string "offices of the house of the LORD by\l"
    .string "the hand of the priests the Levites,\l"
    .string "whom David had distributed in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, to offer the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings of the LORD, as it is\l"
    .string "written in the law of Moses, with\l"
    .string "rejoicing and with singing, as it was\l"
    .string "ordained by David.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_19::
    .string "And he set the porters at the gates\n"
    .string "of the house of the LORD, that none\l"
    .string "which was unclean in any thing\l"
    .string "should enter in.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_20::
    .string "And he took the captains of\n"
    .string "hundreds, and the nobles, and the\l"
    .string "governors of the people, and all\l"
    .string "the people of the land, and\l"
    .string "brought down the king from the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD: and they came through\l"
    .string "the high gate into the king’s house,\l"
    .string "and set the king upon the throne of\l"
    .string "the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_23_21::
    .string "And all the people of the land\n"
    .string "rejoiced: and the city was quiet,\l"
    .string "after that they had slain Athaliah\l"
    .string "with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_1::
    .string "Joash was seven years old when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned forty\l"
    .string "years in Jerusalem. His mother’s\l"
    .string "name also was Zibiah of Beersheba.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_2::
    .string "And Joash did that which was right\n"
    .string "in the sight of the LORD all the\l"
    .string "days of Jehoiada the priest.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_3::
    .string "And Jehoiada took for him two wives;\n"
    .string "and he begat sons and daughters.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_4::
    .string "And it came to pass after this, that\n"
    .string "Joash was minded to repair the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_5::
    .string "And he gathered together the\n"
    .string "priests and the Levites, and said to\l"
    .string "them, Go out unto the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, and gather of all Israel\l"
    .string "money to repair the house of your\l"
    .string "God from year to year, and see that ye\l"
    .string "hasten the matter. Howbeit the\l"
    .string "Levites hastened it not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_6::
    .string "And the king called for Jehoiada\n"
    .string "the chief, and said unto him, Why\l"
    .string "hast thou not required of the Levites\l"
    .string "to bring in out of Judah and out of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem the collection,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "Moses the servant of the LORD, and of\l"
    .string "the congregation of Israel, for the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of witness?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_7::
    .string "For the sons of Athaliah, that\n"
    .string "wicked woman, had broken up the\l"
    .string "house of God; and also all the\l"
    .string "dedicated things of the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD did they bestow upon Baalim$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_8::
    .string "And at the king’s commandment they\n"
    .string "made a chest, and set it without at\l"
    .string "the gate of the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_9::
    .string "And they made a proclamation\n"
    .string "through Judah and Jerusalem, to\l"
    .string "bring in to the LORD the collection\l"
    .string "that Moses the servant of God laid\l"
    .string "upon Israel in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_10::
    .string "And all the princes and all the\n"
    .string "people rejoiced, and brought in,\l"
    .string "and cast into the chest, until they\l"
    .string "had made an end.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_11::
    .string "Now it came to pass, that at what\n"
    .string "time the chest was brought unto the\l"
    .string "king’s office by the hand of the\l"
    .string "Levites, and when they saw that there\l"
    .string "was much money, the king’s scribe and\l"
    .string "the high priest’s officer came and\l"
    .string "emptied the chest, and took it, and\l"
    .string "carried it to his place again. Thus\l"
    .string "they did day by day, and gathered\l"
    .string "money in abundance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_12::
    .string "And the king and Jehoiada gave it to\n"
    .string "such as did the work of the service\l"
    .string "of the house of the LORD, and hired\l"
    .string "masons and carpenters to repair the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and also such as\l"
    .string "wrought iron and brass to mend the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_13::
    .string "So the workmen wrought, and the work\n"
    .string "was perfected by them, and they set\l"
    .string "the house of God in his state, and\l"
    .string "strengthened it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_14::
    .string "And when they had finished it, they\n"
    .string "brought the rest of the money before\l"
    .string "the king and Jehoiada, whereof were\l"
    .string "made vessels for the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, even vessels to minister, and\l"
    .string "to offer withal, and spoons, and\l"
    .string "vessels of gold and silver. And\l"
    .string "they offered burnt offerings in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD continually all\l"
    .string "the days of Jehoiada.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_15::
    .string "But Jehoiada waxed old, and was\n"
    .string "full of days when he died; an\l"
    .string "hundred and thirty years old was he\l"
    .string "when he died.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_16::
    .string "And they buried him in the city of\n"
    .string "David among the kings, because he had\l"
    .string "done good in Israel, both toward\l"
    .string "God, and toward his house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_17::
    .string "Now after the death of Jehoiada came\n"
    .string "the princes of Judah, and made\l"
    .string "obeisance to the king. Then the king\l"
    .string "hearkened unto them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_18::
    .string "And they left the house of the LORD\n"
    .string "God of their fathers, and served\l"
    .string "groves and idols: and wrath came\l"
    .string "upon Judah and Jerusalem for this\l"
    .string "their trespass.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_19::
    .string "Yet he sent prophets to them, to\n"
    .string "bring them again unto the LORD; and\l"
    .string "they testified against them: but they\l"
    .string "would not give ear.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_20::
    .string "And the Spirit of God came upon\n"
    .string "Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the\l"
    .string "priest, which stood above the\l"
    .string "people, and said unto them, Thus\l"
    .string "saith God, Why transgress ye the\l"
    .string "commandments of the LORD, that ye\l"
    .string "cannot prosper? because ye have\l"
    .string "forsaken the LORD, he hath also\l"
    .string "forsaken you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_21::
    .string "And they conspired against him, and\n"
    .string "stoned him with stones at the\l"
    .string "commandment of the king in the court\l"
    .string "of the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_22::
    .string "Thus Joash the king remembered not\n"
    .string "the kindness which Jehoiada his\l"
    .string "father had done to him, but slew his\l"
    .string "son. And when he died, he said, The\l"
    .string "LORD look upon it, and require it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_23::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "the year, that the host of Syria came\l"
    .string "up against him: and they came to\l"
    .string "Judah and Jerusalem, and destroyed\l"
    .string "all the princes of the people\l"
    .string "from among the people, and sent\l"
    .string "all the spoil of them unto the\l"
    .string "king of Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_24::
    .string "For the army of the Syrians came\n"
    .string "with a small company of men, and\l"
    .string "the LORD delivered a very great host\l"
    .string "into their hand, because they had\l"
    .string "forsaken the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers. So they executed judgment\l"
    .string "against Joash.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_25::
    .string "And when they were departed from\n"
    .string "him, (for they left him in great\l"
    .string "diseases,) his own servants\l"
    .string "conspired against him for the blood\l"
    .string "of the sons of Jehoiada the priest,\l"
    .string "and slew him on his bed, and he died:\l"
    .string "and they buried him in the city of\l"
    .string "David, but they buried him not in the\l"
    .string "sepulchres of the kings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_26::
    .string "And these are they that conspired\n"
    .string "against him; Zabad the son of\l"
    .string "Shimeath an Ammonitess, and\l"
    .string "Jehozabad the son of Shimrith a\l"
    .string "Moabitess.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_24_27::
    .string "Now concerning his sons, and the\n"
    .string "greatness of the burdens laid upon\l"
    .string "him, and the repairing of the house\l"
    .string "of God, behold, they are written in\l"
    .string "the story of the book of the kings.\l"
    .string "And Amaziah his son reigned in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_1::
    .string "Amaziah was twenty and five years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned twenty and nine years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_2::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, but not with a\l"
    .string "perfect heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_3::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when the\n"
    .string "kingdom was established to him, that\l"
    .string "he slew his servants that had\l"
    .string "killed the king his father.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_4::
    .string "But he slew not their children, but\n"
    .string "did as it is written in the law in\l"
    .string "the book of Moses, where the LORD\l"
    .string "commanded, saying, The fathers\l"
    .string "shall not die for the children,\l"
    .string "neither shall the children die for\l"
    .string "the fathers, but every man shall die\l"
    .string "for his own sin.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_5::
    .string "Moreover Amaziah gathered Judah\n"
    .string "together, and made them captains\l"
    .string "over thousands, and captains over\l"
    .string "hundreds, according to the houses of\l"
    .string "their fathers, throughout all Judah\l"
    .string "and Benjamin: and he numbered them\l"
    .string "from twenty years old and above, and\l"
    .string "found them three hundred thousand\l"
    .string "choice men, able to go forth to war,\l"
    .string "that could handle spear and shield.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_6::
    .string "He hired also an hundred thousand\n"
    .string "mighty men of valour out of Israel\l"
    .string "for an hundred talents of silver.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_7::
    .string "But there came a man of God to him,\n"
    .string "saying, O king, let not the army of\l"
    .string "Israel go with thee; for the LORD is\l"
    .string "not with Israel, to wit, with all\l"
    .string "the children of Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_8::
    .string "But if thou wilt go, do it; be\n"
    .string "strong for the battle: God shall\l"
    .string "make thee fall before the enemy: for\l"
    .string "God hath power to help, and to cast\l"
    .string "down.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_9::
    .string "And Amaziah said to the man of God,\n"
    .string "But what shall we do for the hundred\l"
    .string "talents which I have given to the\l"
    .string "army of Israel? And the man of God\l"
    .string "answered, The LORD is able to give\l"
    .string "thee much more than this.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_10::
    .string "Then Amaziah separated them, to\n"
    .string "wit, the army that was come to him out\l"
    .string "of Ephraim, to go home again:\l"
    .string "wherefore their anger was greatly\l"
    .string "kindled against Judah, and they\l"
    .string "returned home in great anger.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_11::
    .string "And Amaziah strengthened himself,\n"
    .string "and led forth his people, and went\l"
    .string "to the valley of salt, and smote of\l"
    .string "the children of Seir ten thousand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_12::
    .string "And other ten thousand left alive\n"
    .string "did the children of Judah carry away\l"
    .string "captive, and brought them unto the\l"
    .string "top of the rock, and cast them down\l"
    .string "from the top of the rock, that they\l"
    .string "all were broken in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_13::
    .string "But the soldiers of the army which\n"
    .string "Amaziah sent back, that they should\l"
    .string "not go with him to battle, fell\l"
    .string "upon the cities of Judah, from\l"
    .string "Samaria even unto Bethhoron, and\l"
    .string "smote three thousand of them, and\l"
    .string "took much spoil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_14::
    .string "Now it came to pass, after that\n"
    .string "Amaziah was come from the slaughter\l"
    .string "of the Edomites, that he brought the\l"
    .string "gods of the children of Seir, and set\l"
    .string "them up to be his gods, and bowed\l"
    .string "down himself before them, and burned\l"
    .string "incense unto them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_15::
    .string "Wherefore the anger of the LORD was\n"
    .string "kindled against Amaziah, and he sent\l"
    .string "unto him a prophet, which said unto\l"
    .string "him, Why hast thou sought after the\l"
    .string "gods of the people, which could\l"
    .string "not deliver their own people out\l"
    .string "of thine hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he talked\n"
    .string "with him, that the king said unto\l"
    .string "him, Art thou made of the king’s\l"
    .string "counsel? forbear; why shouldest\l"
    .string "thou be smitten? Then the prophet\l"
    .string "forbare, and said, I know that God\l"
    .string "hath determined to destroy thee,\l"
    .string "because thou hast done this, and hast\l"
    .string "not hearkened unto my counsel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_17::
    .string "Then Amaziah king of Judah took\n"
    .string "advice, and sent to Joash, the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of\l"
    .string "Israel, saying, Come, let us see one\l"
    .string "another in the face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_18::
    .string "And Joash king of Israel sent to\n"
    .string "Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The\l"
    .string "thistle that was in Lebanon sent to\l"
    .string "the cedar that was in Lebanon,\l"
    .string "saying, Give thy daughter to my son\l"
    .string "to wife: and there passed by a wild\l"
    .string "beast that was in Lebanon, and trode\l"
    .string "down the thistle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_19::
    .string "Thou sayest, Lo, thou hast smitten\n"
    .string "the Edomites; and thine heart\l"
    .string "lifteth thee up to boast: abide now\l"
    .string "at home; why shouldest thou meddle\l"
    .string "to thine hurt, that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "fall, even thou, and Judah with\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_20::
    .string "But Amaziah would not hear; for it\n"
    .string "came of God, that he might deliver\l"
    .string "them into the hand of their enemies,\l"
    .string "because they sought after the gods of\l"
    .string "Edom$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_21::
    .string "So Joash the king of Israel went\n"
    .string "up; and they saw one another in the\l"
    .string "face, both he and Amaziah king of\l"
    .string "Judah, at Bethshemesh, which\l"
    .string "belongeth to Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_22::
    .string "And Judah was put to the worse\n"
    .string "before Israel, and they fled every\l"
    .string "man to his tent.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_23::
    .string "And Joash the king of Israel took\n"
    .string "Amaziah king of Judah, the son of\l"
    .string "Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, at\l"
    .string "Bethshemesh, and brought him to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and brake down the wall\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem from the gate of\l"
    .string "Ephraim to the corner gate, four\l"
    .string "hundred cubits.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_24::
    .string "And he took all the gold and the\n"
    .string "silver, and all the vessels that\l"
    .string "were found in the house of God with\l"
    .string "Obededom, and the treasures of the\l"
    .string "king’s house, the hostages also, and\l"
    .string "returned to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_25::
    .string "And Amaziah the son of Joash king of\n"
    .string "Judah lived after the death of Joash\l"
    .string "son of Jehoahaz king of Israel\l"
    .string "fifteen years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_26::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah,\n"
    .string "first and last, behold, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah and Israel?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_27::
    .string "Now after the time that Amaziah did\n"
    .string "turn away from following the LORD\l"
    .string "they made a conspiracy against him\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem; and he fled to\l"
    .string "Lachish: but they sent to Lachish\l"
    .string "after him, and slew him there$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_25_28::
    .string "And they brought him upon horses,\n"
    .string "and buried him with his fathers in\l"
    .string "the city of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_1::
    .string "Then all the people of Judah\n"
    .string "took Uzziah, who was sixteen years\l"
    .string "old, and made him king in the room of\l"
    .string "his father Amaziah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_2::
    .string "He built Eloth, and restored it to\n"
    .string "Judah, after that the king slept\l"
    .string "with his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_3::
    .string "Sixteen years old was Uzziah when\n"
    .string "he began to reign, and he reigned\l"
    .string "fifty and two years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "His mother’s name also was Jecoliah\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_4::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his father Amaziah did.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_5::
    .string "And he sought God in the days of\n"
    .string "Zechariah, who had understanding in\l"
    .string "the visions of God: and as long as he\l"
    .string "sought the LORD, God made him to\l"
    .string "prosper.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_6::
    .string "And he went forth and warred against\n"
    .string "the Philistines, and brake down the\l"
    .string "wall of Gath, and the wall of\l"
    .string "Jabneh, and the wall of Ashdod, and\l"
    .string "built cities about Ashdod, and among\l"
    .string "the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_7::
    .string "And God helped him against the\n"
    .string "Philistines, and against the\l"
    .string "Arabians that dwelt in Gurbaal, and\l"
    .string "the Mehunims.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_8::
    .string "And the Ammonites gave gifts to\n"
    .string "Uzziah: and his name spread abroad\l"
    .string "even to the entering in of Egypt; for\l"
    .string "he strengthened himself\l"
    .string "exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_9::
    .string "Moreover Uzziah built towers in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem at the corner gate, and at\l"
    .string "the valley gate, and at the turning\l"
    .string "of the wall, and fortified them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_10::
    .string "Also he built towers in the desert,\n"
    .string "and digged many wells: for he had\l"
    .string "much cattle, both in the low\l"
    .string "country, and in the plains:\l"
    .string "husbandmen also, and vine dressers\l"
    .string "in the mountains, and in Carmel: for\l"
    .string "he loved husbandry.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_11::
    .string "Moreover Uzziah had an host of\n"
    .string "fighting men, that went out to war by\l"
    .string "bands, according to the number of\l"
    .string "their account by the hand of Jeiel\l"
    .string "the scribe and Maaseiah the ruler,\l"
    .string "under the hand of Hananiah, one of\l"
    .string "the king’s captains.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_12::
    .string "The whole number of the chief of\n"
    .string "the fathers of the mighty men of\l"
    .string "valour were two thousand and six\l"
    .string "hundred.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_13::
    .string "And under their hand was an army,\n"
    .string "three hundred thousand and seven\l"
    .string "thousand and five hundred, that made\l"
    .string "war with mighty power, to help the\l"
    .string "king against the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_14::
    .string "And Uzziah prepared for them\n"
    .string "throughout all the host shields,\l"
    .string "and spears, and helmets, and\l"
    .string "habergeons, and bows, and slings to\l"
    .string "cast stones.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_15::
    .string "And he made in Jerusalem engines,\n"
    .string "invented by cunning men, to be on the\l"
    .string "towers and upon the bulwarks, to\l"
    .string "shoot arrows and great stones\l"
    .string "withal. And his name spread far\l"
    .string "abroad; for he was marvellously\l"
    .string "helped, till he was strong.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_16::
    .string "But when he was strong, his heart\n"
    .string "was lifted up to his destruction:\l"
    .string "for he transgressed against the LORD\l"
    .string "his God, and went into the temple of\l"
    .string "the LORD to burn incense upon the\l"
    .string "altar of incense.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_17::
    .string "And Azariah the priest went in\n"
    .string "after him, and with him fourscore\l"
    .string "priests of the LORD, that were\l"
    .string "valiant men:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_18::
    .string "And they withstood Uzziah the king,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, It appertaineth\l"
    .string "not unto thee, Uzziah, to burn\l"
    .string "incense unto the LORD, but to the\l"
    .string "priests the sons of Aaron, that are\l"
    .string "consecrated to burn incense: go out\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary; for thou hast\l"
    .string "trespassed; neither shall it be for\l"
    .string "thine honour from the LORD God$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_19::
    .string "Then Uzziah was wroth, and had a\n"
    .string "censer in his hand to burn incense:\l"
    .string "and while he was wroth with the\l"
    .string "priests, the leprosy even rose up\l"
    .string "in his forehead before the priests\l"
    .string "in the house of the LORD, from beside\l"
    .string "the incense altar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_20::
    .string "And Azariah the chief priest, and\n"
    .string "all the priests, looked upon him,\l"
    .string "and, behold, he was leprous in his\l"
    .string "forehead, and they thrust him out\l"
    .string "from thence; yea, himself hasted\l"
    .string "also to go out, because the LORD had\l"
    .string "smitten him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_21::
    .string "And Uzziah the king was a leper\n"
    .string "unto the day of his death, and dwelt\l"
    .string "in a several house, being a leper;\l"
    .string "for he was cut off from the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD: and Jotham his son was over\l"
    .string "the king’s house, judging the\l"
    .string "people of the land.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_22::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah,\n"
    .string "first and last, did Isaiah the\l"
    .string "prophet, the son of Amoz, write.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_26_23::
    .string "So Uzziah slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and they buried him with his fathers\l"
    .string "in the field of the burial which\l"
    .string "belonged to the kings; for they\l"
    .string "said, He is a leper: and Jotham his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_1::
    .string "Jotham was twenty and five years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "His mother’s name also was Jerushah,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Zadok.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_2::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that his father Uzziah did:\l"
    .string "howbeit he entered not into the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD. And the people\l"
    .string "did yet corruptly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_3::
    .string "He built the high gate of the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and on the wall of\l"
    .string "Ophel he built much.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_4::
    .string "Moreover he built cities in the\n"
    .string "mountains of Judah, and in the\l"
    .string "forests he built castles and towers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_5::
    .string "He fought also with the king of the\n"
    .string "Ammonites, and prevailed against\l"
    .string "them. And the children of Ammon gave\l"
    .string "him the same year an hundred talents\l"
    .string "of silver, and ten thousand measures\l"
    .string "of wheat, and ten thousand of\l"
    .string "barley. So much did the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon pay unto him, both the second\l"
    .string "year, and the third.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_6::
    .string "So Jotham became mighty, because he\n"
    .string "prepared his ways before the LORD\l"
    .string "his God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_7::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Jotham,\n"
    .string "and all his wars, and his ways, lo,\l"
    .string "they are written in the book of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel and Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_8::
    .string "He was five and twenty years old\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and reigned\l"
    .string "sixteen years in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_27_9::
    .string "And Jotham slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and they buried him in the city of\l"
    .string "David: and Ahaz his son reigned in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_1::
    .string "Ahaz was twenty years old when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned\l"
    .string "sixteen years in Jerusalem: but he\l"
    .string "did not that which was right in the\l"
    .string "sight of the LORD, like David his\l"
    .string "father:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_2::
    .string "For he walked in the ways of the\n"
    .string "kings of Israel, and made also\l"
    .string "molten images for Baalim$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_3::
    .string "Moreover he burnt incense in the\n"
    .string "valley of the son of Hinnom, and\l"
    .string "burnt his children in the fire,\l"
    .string "after the abominations of the\l"
    .string "heathen whom the LORD had cast out\l"
    .string "before the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_4::
    .string "He sacrificed also and burnt\n"
    .string "incense in the high places, and on\l"
    .string "the hills, and under every green\l"
    .string "tree.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_5::
    .string "Wherefore the LORD his God\n"
    .string "delivered him into the hand of the\l"
    .string "king of Syria; and they smote him,\l"
    .string "and carried away a great multitude\l"
    .string "of them captives, and brought them\l"
    .string "to Damascus. And he was also\l"
    .string "delivered into the hand of the king\l"
    .string "of Israel, who smote him with a great\l"
    .string "slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_6::
    .string "For Pekah the son of Remaliah slew\n"
    .string "in Judah an hundred and twenty\l"
    .string "thousand in one day, which were all\l"
    .string "valiant men; because they had\l"
    .string "forsaken the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_7::
    .string "And Zichri, a mighty man of\n"
    .string "Ephraim, slew Maaseiah the king’s\l"
    .string "son, and Azrikam the governor of the\l"
    .string "house, and Elkanah that was next to\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_8::
    .string "And the children of Israel carried\n"
    .string "away captive of their brethren two\l"
    .string "hundred thousand, women, sons, and\l"
    .string "daughters, and took also away much\l"
    .string "spoil from them, and brought the\l"
    .string "spoil to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_9::
    .string "But a prophet of the LORD was\n"
    .string "there, whose name was Oded: and he\l"
    .string "went out before the host that came to\l"
    .string "Samaria, and said unto them, Behold,\l"
    .string "because the LORD God of your fathers\l"
    .string "was wroth with Judah, he hath\l"
    .string "delivered them into your hand, and\l"
    .string "ye have slain them in a rage that\l"
    .string "reacheth up unto heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_10::
    .string "And now ye purpose to keep under\n"
    .string "the children of Judah and Jerusalem\l"
    .string "for bondmen and bondwomen unto you:\l"
    .string "but are there not with you, even with\l"
    .string "you, sins against the LORD your God?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_11::
    .string "Now hear me therefore, and deliver\n"
    .string "the captives again, which ye have\l"
    .string "taken captive of your brethren: for\l"
    .string "the fierce wrath of the LORD is upon\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_12::
    .string "Then certain of the heads of the\n"
    .string "children of Ephraim, Azariah the\l"
    .string "son of Johanan, Berechiah the son of\l"
    .string "Meshillemoth, and Jehizkiah the son\l"
    .string "of Shallum, and Amasa the son of\l"
    .string "Hadlai, stood up against them that\l"
    .string "came from the war,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_13::
    .string "And said unto them, Ye shall not\n"
    .string "bring in the captives hither: for\l"
    .string "whereas we have offended against the\l"
    .string "LORD already, ye intend to add more\l"
    .string "to our sins and to our trespass: for\l"
    .string "our trespass is great, and there is\l"
    .string "fierce wrath against Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_14::
    .string "So the armed men left the captives\n"
    .string "and the spoil before the princes\l"
    .string "and all the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_15::
    .string "And the men which were expressed by\n"
    .string "name rose up, and took the captives,\l"
    .string "and with the spoil clothed all\l"
    .string "that were naked among them, and\l"
    .string "arrayed them, and shod them, and gave\l"
    .string "them to eat and to drink, and\l"
    .string "anointed them, and carried all the\l"
    .string "feeble of them upon asses, and\l"
    .string "brought them to Jericho, the city of\l"
    .string "palm trees, to their brethren: then\l"
    .string "they returned to Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_16::
    .string "At that time did king Ahaz send unto\n"
    .string "the kings of Assyria to help him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_17::
    .string "For again the Edomites had come and\n"
    .string "smitten Judah, and carried away\l"
    .string "captives.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_18::
    .string "The Philistines also had invaded\n"
    .string "the cities of the low country, and of\l"
    .string "the south of Judah, and had taken\l"
    .string "Bethshemesh, and Ajalon, and\l"
    .string "Gederoth, and Shocho with the\l"
    .string "villages thereof, and Timnah with\l"
    .string "the villages thereof, Gimzo also\l"
    .string "and the villages thereof: and they\l"
    .string "dwelt there.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_19::
    .string "For the LORD brought Judah low\n"
    .string "because of Ahaz king of Israel; for\l"
    .string "he made Judah naked, and transgressed\l"
    .string "sore against the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_20::
    .string "And Tilgathpilneser king of\n"
    .string "Assyria came unto him, and distressed\l"
    .string "him, but strengthened him not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_21::
    .string "For Ahaz took away a portion out of\n"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and out of the\l"
    .string "house of the king, and of the\l"
    .string "princes, and gave it unto the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria: but he helped him not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_22::
    .string "And in the time of his distress did\n"
    .string "he trespass yet more against the\l"
    .string "LORD: this is that king Ahaz.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_23::
    .string "For he sacrificed unto the gods of\n"
    .string "Damascus, which smote him: and he\l"
    .string "said, Because the gods of the kings\l"
    .string "of Syria help them, therefore will\l"
    .string "I sacrifice to them, that they may\l"
    .string "help me. But they were the ruin of\l"
    .string "him, and of all Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_24::
    .string "And Ahaz gathered together the\n"
    .string "vessels of the house of God, and cut\l"
    .string "in pieces the vessels of the house\l"
    .string "of God, and shut up the doors of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and he made him\l"
    .string "altars in every corner of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_25::
    .string "And in every several city of Judah\n"
    .string "he made high places to burn incense\l"
    .string "unto other gods, and provoked to\l"
    .string "anger the LORD God of his fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_26::
    .string "Now the rest of his acts and of all\n"
    .string "his ways, first and last, behold,\l"
    .string "they are written in the book of the\l"
    .string "kings of Judah and Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_28_27::
    .string "And Ahaz slept with his fathers,\n"
    .string "and they buried him in the city, even\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem: but they brought him\l"
    .string "not into the sepulchres of the\l"
    .string "kings of Israel: and Hezekiah his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_1::
    .string "Hezekiah began to reign when he was\n"
    .string "five and twenty years old, and he\l"
    .string "reigned nine and twenty years in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was\l"
    .string "Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_2::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that David his father had done.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_3::
    .string "He in the first year of his reign, in\n"
    .string "the first month, opened the doors of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and repaired\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_4::
    .string "And he brought in the priests and\n"
    .string "the Levites, and gathered them\l"
    .string "together into the east street,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_5::
    .string "And said unto them, Hear me, ye\n"
    .string "Levites, sanctify now yourselves,\l"
    .string "and sanctify the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "God of your fathers, and carry forth\l"
    .string "the filthiness out of the holy\l"
    .string "place$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_6::
    .string "For our fathers have trespassed,\n"
    .string "and done that which was evil in the\l"
    .string "eyes of the LORD our God, and have\l"
    .string "forsaken him, and have turned away\l"
    .string "their faces from the habitation of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and turned their backs.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_7::
    .string "Also they have shut up the doors of\n"
    .string "the porch, and put out the lamps,\l"
    .string "and have not burned incense nor\l"
    .string "offered burnt offerings in the holy\l"
    .string "place unto the God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_8::
    .string "Wherefore the wrath of the LORD was\n"
    .string "upon Judah and Jerusalem, and he\l"
    .string "hath delivered them to trouble, to\l"
    .string "astonishment, and to hissing, as ye\l"
    .string "see with your eyes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_9::
    .string "For, lo, our fathers have fallen\n"
    .string "by the sword, and our sons and our\l"
    .string "daughters and our wives are in\l"
    .string "captivity for this.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_10::
    .string "Now it is in mine heart to make a\n"
    .string "covenant with the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel, that his fierce wrath may\l"
    .string "turn away from us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_11::
    .string "My sons, be not now negligent: for\n"
    .string "the LORD hath chosen you to stand\l"
    .string "before him, to serve him, and that ye\l"
    .string "should minister unto him, and burn\l"
    .string "incense.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_12::
    .string "Then the Levites arose, Mahath the\n"
    .string "son of Amasai, and Joel the son of\l"
    .string "Azariah, of the sons of the\l"
    .string "Kohathites: and of the sons of\l"
    .string "Merari, Kish the son of Abdi, and\l"
    .string "Azariah the son of Jehalelel: and\l"
    .string "of the Gershonites; Joah the son of\l"
    .string "Zimmah, and Eden the son of Joah:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_13::
    .string "And of the sons of Elizaphan;\n"
    .string "Shimri, and Jeiel: and of the sons of\l"
    .string "Asaph; Zechariah, and Mattaniah:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_14::
    .string "And of the sons of Heman; Jehiel,\n"
    .string "and Shimei: and of the sons of\l"
    .string "Jeduthun; Shemaiah, and Uzziel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_15::
    .string "And they gathered their brethren,\n"
    .string "and sanctified themselves, and came,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of the\l"
    .string "king, by the words of the LORD, to\l"
    .string "cleanse the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_16::
    .string "And the priests went into the inner\n"
    .string "part of the house of the LORD, to\l"
    .string "cleanse it, and brought out all the\l"
    .string "uncleanness that they found in the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD into the court of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD. And the\l"
    .string "Levites took it, to carry it out\l"
    .string "abroad into the brook Kidron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_17::
    .string "Now they began on the first day of\n"
    .string "the first month to sanctify, and on\l"
    .string "the eighth day of the month came they\l"
    .string "to the porch of the LORD: so they\l"
    .string "sanctified the house of the LORD in\l"
    .string "eight days; and in the sixteenth day\l"
    .string "of the first month they made an end.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_18::
    .string "Then they went in to Hezekiah the\n"
    .string "king, and said, We have cleansed\l"
    .string "all the house of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "altar of burnt offering, with all\l"
    .string "the vessels thereof, and the\l"
    .string "shewbread table, with all the\l"
    .string "vessels thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_19::
    .string "Moreover all the vessels, which\n"
    .string "king Ahaz in his reign did cast away\l"
    .string "in his transgression, have we\l"
    .string "prepared and sanctified, and,\l"
    .string "behold, they are before the altar of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_20::
    .string "Then Hezekiah the king rose early,\n"
    .string "and gathered the rulers of the city,\l"
    .string "and went up to the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_21::
    .string "And they brought seven bullocks,\n"
    .string "and seven rams, and seven lambs, and\l"
    .string "seven he goats, for a sin offering\l"
    .string "for the kingdom, and for the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, and for Judah. And he\l"
    .string "commanded the priests the sons of\l"
    .string "Aaron to offer them on the altar of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_22::
    .string "So they killed the bullocks, and\n"
    .string "the priests received the blood, and\l"
    .string "sprinkled it on the altar:\l"
    .string "likewise, when they had killed the\l"
    .string "rams, they sprinkled the blood\l"
    .string "upon the altar: they killed also\l"
    .string "the lambs, and they sprinkled the\l"
    .string "blood upon the altar.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_23::
    .string "And they brought forth the he goats\n"
    .string "for the sin offering before the king\l"
    .string "and the congregation; and they laid\l"
    .string "their hands upon them:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_24::
    .string "And the priests killed them, and\n"
    .string "they made reconciliation with their\l"
    .string "blood upon the altar, to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for all Israel: for the\l"
    .string "king commanded that the burnt\l"
    .string "offering and the sin offering should\l"
    .string "be made for all Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_25::
    .string "And he set the Levites in the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD with cymbals, with\l"
    .string "psalteries, and with harps,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "David, and of Gad the king’s seer,\l"
    .string "and Nathan the prophet: for so was\l"
    .string "the commandment of the LORD by his\l"
    .string "prophets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_26::
    .string "And the Levites stood with the\n"
    .string "instruments of David, and the\l"
    .string "priests with the trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_27::
    .string "And Hezekiah commanded to offer the\n"
    .string "burnt offering upon the altar. And\l"
    .string "when the burnt offering began, the\l"
    .string "song of the LORD began also with the\l"
    .string "trumpets, and with the instruments\l"
    .string "ordained by David king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_28::
    .string "And all the congregation\n"
    .string "worshipped, and the singers sang,\l"
    .string "and the trumpeters sounded: and all\l"
    .string "this continued until the burnt\l"
    .string "offering was finished.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_29::
    .string "And when they had made an end of\n"
    .string "offering, the king and all that were\l"
    .string "present with him bowed themselves,\l"
    .string "and worshipped.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_30::
    .string "Moreover Hezekiah the king and the\n"
    .string "princes commanded the Levites to\l"
    .string "sing praise unto the LORD with the\l"
    .string "words of David, and of Asaph the seer\l"
    .string " And they sang praises with\l"
    .string "gladness, and they bowed their heads\l"
    .string "and worshipped.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_31::
    .string "Then Hezekiah answered and said, Now\n"
    .string "ye have consecrated yourselves unto\l"
    .string "the LORD, come near and bring\l"
    .string "sacrifices and thank offerings into\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD. And the\l"
    .string "congregation brought in sacrifices\l"
    .string "and thank offerings; and as many as\l"
    .string "were of a free heart burnt offerings.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_32::
    .string "And the number of the burnt\n"
    .string "offerings, which the congregation\l"
    .string "brought, was threescore and ten\l"
    .string "bullocks, an hundred rams, and two\l"
    .string "hundred lambs: all these were for a\l"
    .string "burnt offering to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_33::
    .string "And the consecrated things were six\n"
    .string "hundred oxen and three thousand\l"
    .string "sheep.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_34::
    .string "But the priests were too few, so\n"
    .string "that they could not flay all the\l"
    .string "burnt offerings: wherefore their\l"
    .string "brethren the Levites did help them,\l"
    .string "till the work was ended, and until\l"
    .string "the other priests had sanctified\l"
    .string "themselves: for the Levites were\l"
    .string "more upright in heart to sanctify\l"
    .string "themselves than the priests.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_35::
    .string "And also the burnt offerings were\n"
    .string "in abundance, with the fat of the\l"
    .string "peace offerings, and the drink\l"
    .string "offerings for every burnt offering.\l"
    .string "So the service of the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD was set in order.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_29_36::
    .string "And Hezekiah rejoiced, and all the\n"
    .string "people, that God had prepared the\l"
    .string "people: for the thing was done\l"
    .string "suddenly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_1::
    .string "And Hezekiah sent to all Israel\n"
    .string "and Judah, and wrote letters also to\l"
    .string "Ephraim and Manasseh, that they\l"
    .string "should come to the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "at Jerusalem, to keep the passover\l"
    .string "unto the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_2::
    .string "For the king had taken counsel, and\n"
    .string "his princes, and all the\l"
    .string "congregation in Jerusalem, to keep\l"
    .string "the passover in the second month.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_3::
    .string "For they could not keep it at that\n"
    .string "time, because the priests had not\l"
    .string "sanctified themselves\l"
    .string "sufficiently, neither had the\l"
    .string "people gathered themselves\l"
    .string "together to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_4::
    .string "And the thing pleased the king and\n"
    .string "all the congregation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_5::
    .string "So they established a decree to\n"
    .string "make proclamation throughout all\l"
    .string "Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan,\l"
    .string "that they should come to keep the\l"
    .string "passover unto the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "at Jerusalem: for they had not done\l"
    .string "it of a long time in such sort as it\l"
    .string "was written.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_6::
    .string "So the posts went with the letters\n"
    .string "from the king and his princes\l"
    .string "throughout all Israel and Judah,\l"
    .string "and according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "the king, saying, Ye children of\l"
    .string "Israel, turn again unto the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, and he\l"
    .string "will return to the remnant of you,\l"
    .string "that are escaped out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the kings of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_7::
    .string "And be not ye like your fathers, and\n"
    .string "like your brethren, which trespassed\l"
    .string "against the LORD God of their\l"
    .string "fathers, who therefore gave them up\l"
    .string "to desolation, as ye see.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_8::
    .string "Now be ye not stiffnecked, as your\n"
    .string "fathers were, but yield yourselves\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, and enter into his\l"
    .string "sanctuary, which he hath sanctified\l"
    .string "for ever: and serve the LORD your\l"
    .string "God, that the fierceness of his wrath\l"
    .string "may turn away from you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_9::
    .string "For if ye turn again unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "your brethren and your children\l"
    .string "shall find compassion before them\l"
    .string "that lead them captive, so that they\l"
    .string "shall come again into this land:\l"
    .string "for the LORD your God is gracious and\l"
    .string "merciful, and will not turn away\l"
    .string "his face from you, if ye return unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_10::
    .string "So the posts passed from city to\n"
    .string "city through the country of Ephraim\l"
    .string "and Manasseh even unto Zebulun: but\l"
    .string "they laughed them to scorn, and\l"
    .string "mocked them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_11::
    .string "Nevertheless divers of Asher and\n"
    .string "Manasseh and of Zebulun humbled\l"
    .string "themselves, and came to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_12::
    .string "Also in Judah the hand of God was to\n"
    .string "give them one heart to do the\l"
    .string "commandment of the king and of the\l"
    .string "princes, by the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_13::
    .string "And there assembled at Jerusalem\n"
    .string "much people to keep the feast of\l"
    .string "unleavened bread in the second\l"
    .string "month, a very great congregation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_14::
    .string "And they arose and took away the\n"
    .string "altars that were in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "all the altars for incense took\l"
    .string "they away, and cast them into the\l"
    .string "brook Kidron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_15::
    .string "Then they killed the passover on\n"
    .string "the fourteenth day of the second\l"
    .string "month: and the priests and the\l"
    .string "Levites were ashamed, and sanctified\l"
    .string "themselves, and brought in the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings into the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_16::
    .string "And they stood in their place\n"
    .string "after their manner, according to the\l"
    .string "law of Moses the man of God: the\l"
    .string "priests sprinkled the blood, which\l"
    .string "they received of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Levites.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_17::
    .string "For there were many in the\n"
    .string "congregation that were not\l"
    .string "sanctified: therefore the Levites\l"
    .string "had the charge of the killing of the\l"
    .string "passovers for every one that was not\l"
    .string "clean, to sanctify them unto the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_18::
    .string "For a multitude of the people,\n"
    .string "even many of Ephraim, and Manasseh,\l"
    .string "Issachar, and Zebulun, had not\l"
    .string "cleansed themselves, yet did they\l"
    .string "eat the passover otherwise than it\l"
    .string "was written. But Hezekiah prayed for\l"
    .string "them, saying, The good LORD pardon\l"
    .string "every one"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_19::
    .string "That prepareth his heart to seek\n"
    .string "God, the LORD God of his fathers,\l"
    .string "though he be not cleansed according\l"
    .string "to the purification of the sanctuary$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_20::
    .string "And the LORD hearkened to Hezekiah,\n"
    .string "and healed the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_21::
    .string "And the children of Israel that\n"
    .string "were present at Jerusalem kept the\l"
    .string "feast of unleavened bread seven days\l"
    .string "with great gladness: and the Levites\l"
    .string "and the priests praised the LORD\l"
    .string "day by day, singing with loud\l"
    .string "instruments unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_22::
    .string "And Hezekiah spake comfortably\n"
    .string "unto all the Levites that taught\l"
    .string "the good knowledge of the LORD: and\l"
    .string "they did eat throughout the feast\l"
    .string "seven days, offering peace\l"
    .string "offerings, and making confession to\l"
    .string "the LORD God of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_23::
    .string "And the whole assembly took\n"
    .string "counsel to keep other seven days:\l"
    .string "and they kept other seven days with\l"
    .string "gladness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_24::
    .string "For Hezekiah king of Judah did give\n"
    .string "to the congregation a thousand\l"
    .string "bullocks and seven thousand sheep;\l"
    .string "and the princes gave to the\l"
    .string "congregation a thousand bullocks\l"
    .string "and ten thousand sheep: and a great\l"
    .string "number of priests sanctified\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_25::
    .string "And all the congregation of Judah,\n"
    .string "with the priests and the Levites,\l"
    .string "and all the congregation that came\l"
    .string "out of Israel, and the strangers\l"
    .string "that came out of the land of Israel,\l"
    .string "and that dwelt in Judah, rejoiced.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_26::
    .string "So there was great joy in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: for since the time of\l"
    .string "Solomon the son of David king of\l"
    .string "Israel there was not the like in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_30_27::
    .string "Then the priests the Levites arose\n"
    .string "and blessed the people: and their\l"
    .string "voice was heard, and their prayer\l"
    .string "came up to his holy dwelling\l"
    .string "place, even unto heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_1::
    .string "Now when all this was finished,\n"
    .string "all Israel that were present went\l"
    .string "out to the cities of Judah, and brake\l"
    .string "the images in pieces, and cut down\l"
    .string "the groves, and threw down the high\l"
    .string "places and the altars out of all\l"
    .string "Judah and Benjamin, in Ephraim also\l"
    .string "and Manasseh, until they had\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed them all. Then\l"
    .string "all the children of Israel\l"
    .string "returned, every man to his\l"
    .string "possession, into their own cities.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_2::
    .string "And Hezekiah appointed the courses\n"
    .string "of the priests and the Levites after\l"
    .string "their courses, every man according to\l"
    .string "his service, the priests and Levites\l"
    .string "for burnt offerings and for peace\l"
    .string "offerings, to minister, and to give\l"
    .string "thanks, and to praise in the gates of\l"
    .string "the tents of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_3::
    .string "He appointed also the king’s\n"
    .string "portion of his substance for the\l"
    .string "burnt offerings, to wit, for the\l"
    .string "morning and evening burnt offerings,\l"
    .string "and the burnt offerings for the\l"
    .string "sabbaths, and for the new moons, and\l"
    .string "for the set feasts, as it is written\l"
    .string "in the law of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_4::
    .string "Moreover he commanded the people\n"
    .string "that dwelt in Jerusalem to give the\l"
    .string "portion of the priests and the\l"
    .string "Levites, that they might be\l"
    .string "encouraged in the law of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_5::
    .string "And as soon as the commandment came\n"
    .string "abroad, the children of Israel\l"
    .string "brought in abundance the firstfruits\l"
    .string "of corn, wine, and oil, and honey,\l"
    .string "and of all the increase of the\l"
    .string "field; and the tithe of all things\l"
    .string "brought they in abundantly.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_6::
    .string "And concerning the children of\n"
    .string "Israel and Judah, that dwelt in the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah, they also brought\l"
    .string "in the tithe of oxen and sheep, and\l"
    .string "the tithe of holy things which were\l"
    .string "consecrated unto the LORD their God,\l"
    .string "and laid them by heaps.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_7::
    .string "In the third month they began to\n"
    .string "lay the foundation of the heaps, and\l"
    .string "finished them in the seventh month.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_8::
    .string "And when Hezekiah and the princes\n"
    .string "came and saw the heaps, they blessed\l"
    .string "the LORD, and his people Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_9::
    .string "Then Hezekiah questioned with the\n"
    .string "priests and the Levites concerning\l"
    .string "the heaps.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_10::
    .string "And Azariah the chief priest of the\n"
    .string "house of Zadok answered him, and\l"
    .string "said, Since the people began to\l"
    .string "bring the offerings into the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, we have had enough to eat,\l"
    .string "and have left plenty: for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath blessed his people; and that\l"
    .string "which is left is this great store.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_11::
    .string "Then Hezekiah commanded to prepare\n"
    .string "chambers in the house of the LORD;\l"
    .string "and they prepared them,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_12::
    .string "And brought in the offerings and the\n"
    .string "tithes and the dedicated things\l"
    .string "faithfully: over which Cononiah the\l"
    .string "Levite was ruler, and Shimei his\l"
    .string "brother was the next$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_13::
    .string "And Jehiel, and Azaziah, and\n"
    .string "Nahath, and Asahel, and Jerimoth,\l"
    .string "and Jozabad, and Eliel, and\l"
    .string "Ismachiah, and Mahath, and Benaiah,\l"
    .string "were overseers under the hand of\l"
    .string "Cononiah and Shimei his brother, at\l"
    .string "the commandment of Hezekiah the king,\l"
    .string "and Azariah the ruler of the house\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_14::
    .string "And Kore the son of Imnah the\n"
    .string "Levite, the porter toward the east,\l"
    .string "was over the freewill offerings of\l"
    .string "God, to distribute the oblations of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and the most holy things.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_15::
    .string "And next him were Eden, and\n"
    .string "Miniamin, and Jeshua, and Shemaiah,\l"
    .string "Amariah, and Shecaniah, in the cities\l"
    .string "of the priests, in their set office,\l"
    .string "to give to their brethren by courses,\l"
    .string "as well to the great as to the\l"
    .string "small:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_16::
    .string "Beside their genealogy of males,\n"
    .string "from three years old and upward,\l"
    .string "even unto every one that entereth\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD, his daily\l"
    .string "portion for their service in their\l"
    .string "charges according to their courses;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_17::
    .string "Both to the genealogy of the\n"
    .string "priests by the house of their\l"
    .string "fathers, and the Levites from twenty\l"
    .string "years old and upward, in their\l"
    .string "charges by their courses;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_18::
    .string "And to the genealogy of all their\n"
    .string "little ones, their wives, and their\l"
    .string "sons, and their daughters, through\l"
    .string "all the congregation: for in their\l"
    .string "set office they sanctified\l"
    .string "themselves in holiness:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_19::
    .string "Also of the sons of Aaron the\n"
    .string "priests, which were in the fields of\l"
    .string "the suburbs of their cities, in every\l"
    .string "several city, the men that were\l"
    .string "expressed by name, to give portions\l"
    .string "to all the males among the\l"
    .string "priests, and to all that were\l"
    .string "reckoned by genealogies among the\l"
    .string "Levites$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_20::
    .string "And thus did Hezekiah throughout\n"
    .string "all Judah, and wrought that which\l"
    .string "was good and right and truth before\l"
    .string "the LORD his God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_31_21::
    .string "And in every work that he began in\n"
    .string "the service of the house of God, and\l"
    .string "in the law, and in the commandments,\l"
    .string "to seek his God, he did it with all\l"
    .string "his heart, and prospered.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_1::
    .string "After these things, and the\n"
    .string "establishment thereof, Sennacherib\l"
    .string "king of Assyria came, and entered\l"
    .string "into Judah, and encamped against the\l"
    .string "fenced cities, and thought to win\l"
    .string "them for himself.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_2::
    .string "And when Hezekiah saw that\n"
    .string "Sennacherib was come, and that he was\l"
    .string "purposed to fight against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_3::
    .string "He took counsel with his princes\n"
    .string "and his mighty men to stop the\l"
    .string "waters of the fountains which were\l"
    .string "without the city: and they did help\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_4::
    .string "So there was gathered much people\n"
    .string "together, who stopped all the\l"
    .string "fountains, and the brook that ran\l"
    .string "through the midst of the land,\l"
    .string "saying, Why should the kings of\l"
    .string "Assyria come, and find much water?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_5::
    .string "Also he strengthened himself, and\n"
    .string "built up all the wall that was\l"
    .string "broken, and raised it up to the\l"
    .string "towers, and another wall without,\l"
    .string "and repaired Millo in the city of\l"
    .string "David, and made darts and shields in\l"
    .string "abundance$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_6::
    .string "And he set captains of war over the\n"
    .string "people, and gathered them together\l"
    .string "to him in the street of the gate of\l"
    .string "the city, and spake comfortably to\l"
    .string "them, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_7::
    .string "Be strong and courageous, be not\n"
    .string "afraid nor dismayed for the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, nor for all the multitude\l"
    .string "that is with him: for there be more\l"
    .string "with us than with him:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_8::
    .string "With him is an arm of flesh; but\n"
    .string "with us is the LORD our God to help\l"
    .string "us, and to fight our battles. And the\l"
    .string "people rested themselves upon the\l"
    .string "words of Hezekiah king of Judah$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_9::
    .string "After this did Sennacherib king of\n"
    .string "Assyria send his servants to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, (but he himself laid\l"
    .string "siege against Lachish, and all his\l"
    .string "power with him,) unto Hezekiah king\l"
    .string "of Judah, and unto all Judah that\l"
    .string "were at Jerusalem, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_10::
    .string "Thus saith Sennacherib king of\n"
    .string "Assyria, Whereon do ye trust, that ye\l"
    .string "abide in the siege in Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_11::
    .string "Doth not Hezekiah persuade you to\n"
    .string "give over yourselves to die by\l"
    .string "famine and by thirst, saying, The\l"
    .string "LORD our God shall deliver us out\l"
    .string "of the hand of the king of Assyria?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_12::
    .string "Hath not the same Hezekiah taken\n"
    .string "away his high places and his\l"
    .string "altars, and commanded Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, saying, Ye shall\l"
    .string "worship before one altar, and burn\l"
    .string "incense upon it?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_13::
    .string "Know ye not what I and my fathers\n"
    .string "have done unto all the people of\l"
    .string "other lands? were the gods of the\l"
    .string "nations of those lands any ways\l"
    .string "able to deliver their lands out of\l"
    .string "mine hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_14::
    .string "Who was there among all the gods of\n"
    .string "those nations that my fathers\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed, that could\l"
    .string "deliver his people out of mine\l"
    .string "hand, that your God should be able\l"
    .string "to deliver you out of mine hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_15::
    .string "Now therefore let not Hezekiah\n"
    .string "deceive you, nor persuade you on\l"
    .string "this manner, neither yet believe\l"
    .string "him: for no god of any nation or\l"
    .string "kingdom was able to deliver his\l"
    .string "people out of mine hand, and out of\l"
    .string "the hand of my fathers: how much less\l"
    .string "shall your God deliver you out of\l"
    .string "mine hand?"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_16::
    .string "And his servants spake yet more\n"
    .string "against the LORD God, and against his\l"
    .string "servant Hezekiah$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_17::
    .string "He wrote also letters to rail on\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel, and to speak\l"
    .string "against him, saying, As the gods of\l"
    .string "the nations of other lands have not\l"
    .string "delivered their people out of mine\l"
    .string "hand, so shall not the God of\l"
    .string "Hezekiah deliver his people out of\l"
    .string "mine hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_18::
    .string "Then they cried with a loud voice\n"
    .string "in the Jews’ speech unto the\l"
    .string "people of Jerusalem that were on\l"
    .string "the wall, to affright them, and to\l"
    .string "trouble them; that they might take\l"
    .string "the city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_19::
    .string "And they spake against the God of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, as against the gods of\l"
    .string "the people of the earth, which were\l"
    .string "the work of the hands of man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_20::
    .string "And for this cause Hezekiah the\n"
    .string "king, and the prophet Isaiah the son\l"
    .string "of Amoz, prayed and cried to heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_21::
    .string "And the LORD sent an angel, which\n"
    .string "cut off all the mighty men of\l"
    .string "valour, and the leaders and\l"
    .string "captains in the camp of the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria. So he returned with shame of\l"
    .string "face to his own land. And when he was\l"
    .string "come into the house of his god, they\l"
    .string "that came forth of his own bowels\l"
    .string "slew him there with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_22::
    .string "Thus the LORD saved Hezekiah and the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem from the\l"
    .string "hand of Sennacherib the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and from the hand of all\l"
    .string "other, and guided them on every side.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_23::
    .string "And many brought gifts unto the LORD\n"
    .string "to Jerusalem, and presents to\l"
    .string "Hezekiah king of Judah: so that he\l"
    .string "was magnified in the sight of all\l"
    .string "nations from thenceforth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_24::
    .string "In those days Hezekiah was sick to\n"
    .string "the death, and prayed unto the LORD:\l"
    .string "and he spake unto him, and he gave\l"
    .string "him a sign.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_25::
    .string "But Hezekiah rendered not again\n"
    .string "according to the benefit done unto\l"
    .string "him; for his heart was lifted up:\l"
    .string "therefore there was wrath upon him,\l"
    .string "and upon Judah and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_26::
    .string "Notwithstanding Hezekiah humbled\n"
    .string "himself for the pride of his heart,\l"
    .string "both he and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, so that the wrath of the\l"
    .string "LORD came not upon them in the days\l"
    .string "of Hezekiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_27::
    .string "And Hezekiah had exceeding much\n"
    .string "riches and honour: and he made\l"
    .string "himself treasuries for silver, and\l"
    .string "for gold, and for precious stones,\l"
    .string "and for spices, and for shields, and\l"
    .string "for all manner of pleasant\l"
    .string "jewels;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_28::
    .string "Storehouses also for the increase\n"
    .string "of corn, and wine, and oil; and\l"
    .string "stalls for all manner of beasts,\l"
    .string "and cotes for flocks$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_29::
    .string "Moreover he provided him cities,\n"
    .string "and possessions of flocks and herds\l"
    .string "in abundance: for God had given him\l"
    .string "substance very much.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_30::
    .string "This same Hezekiah also stopped\n"
    .string "the upper watercourse of Gihon, and\l"
    .string "brought it straight down to the west\l"
    .string "side of the city of David. And\l"
    .string "Hezekiah prospered in all his\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_31::
    .string "Howbeit in the business of the\n"
    .string "ambassadors of the princes of\l"
    .string "Babylon, who sent unto him to\l"
    .string "enquire of the wonder that was done\l"
    .string "in the land, God left him, to try\l"
    .string "him, that he might know all that was\l"
    .string "in his heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_32::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Hezekiah, and his goodness, behold,\l"
    .string "they are written in the vision of\l"
    .string "Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz,\l"
    .string "and in the book of the kings of Judah\l"
    .string "and Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_32_33::
    .string "And Hezekiah slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and they buried him in the\l"
    .string "chiefest of the sepulchres of the\l"
    .string "sons of David: and all Judah and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem did him\l"
    .string "honour at his death. And Manasseh his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_1::
    .string "Manasseh was twelve years old when\n"
    .string "he began to reign, and he reigned\l"
    .string "fifty and five years in Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_2::
    .string "But did that which was evil in the\n"
    .string "sight of the LORD, like unto the\l"
    .string "abominations of the heathen, whom the\l"
    .string "LORD had cast out before the\l"
    .string "children of Israel$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_3::
    .string "For he built again the high places\n"
    .string "which Hezekiah his father had broken\l"
    .string "down, and he reared up altars for\l"
    .string "Baalim, and made groves, and\l"
    .string "worshipped all the host of heaven,\l"
    .string "and served them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_4::
    .string "Also he built altars in the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD, whereof the LORD had\l"
    .string "said, In Jerusalem shall my name be\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_5::
    .string "And he built altars for all the\n"
    .string "host of heaven in the two courts of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_6::
    .string "And he caused his children to pass\n"
    .string "through the fire in the valley of\l"
    .string "the son of Hinnom: also he observed\l"
    .string "times, and used enchantments, and\l"
    .string "used witchcraft, and dealt with a\l"
    .string "familiar spirit, and with wizards:\l"
    .string "he wrought much evil in the sight of\l"
    .string "the LORD, to provoke him to anger.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_7::
    .string "And he set a carved image, the idol\n"
    .string "which he had made, in the house of\l"
    .string "God, of which God had said to David\l"
    .string "and to Solomon his son, In this\l"
    .string "house, and in Jerusalem, which I\l"
    .string "have chosen before all the tribes\l"
    .string "of Israel, will I put my name for\l"
    .string "ever:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_8::
    .string "Neither will I any more remove the\n"
    .string "foot of Israel from out of the land\l"
    .string "which I have appointed for your\l"
    .string "fathers; so that they will take heed\l"
    .string "to do all that I have commanded\l"
    .string "them, according to the whole law and\l"
    .string "the statutes and the ordinances by\l"
    .string "the hand of Moses$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_9::
    .string "So Manasseh made Judah and the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem to err, and\l"
    .string "to do worse than the heathen, whom\l"
    .string "the LORD had destroyed before the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_10::
    .string "And the LORD spake to Manasseh, and\n"
    .string "to his people: but they would not\l"
    .string "hearken.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_11::
    .string "Wherefore the LORD brought upon\n"
    .string "them the captains of the host of the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria, which took Manasseh\l"
    .string "among the thorns, and bound him with\l"
    .string "fetters, and carried him to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_12::
    .string "And when he was in affliction, he\n"
    .string "besought the LORD his God, and\l"
    .string "humbled himself greatly before the\l"
    .string "God of his fathers,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_13::
    .string "And prayed unto him: and he was\n"
    .string "intreated of him, and heard his\l"
    .string "supplication, and brought him\l"
    .string "again to Jerusalem into his kingdom.\l"
    .string "Then Manasseh knew that the LORD he\l"
    .string "was God$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_14::
    .string "Now after this he built a wall\n"
    .string "without the city of David, on the\l"
    .string "west side of Gihon, in the valley,\l"
    .string "even to the entering in at the fish\l"
    .string "gate, and compassed about Ophel,\l"
    .string "and raised it up a very great height,\l"
    .string "and put captains of war in all the\l"
    .string "fenced cities of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_15::
    .string "And he took away the strange gods,\n"
    .string "and the idol out of the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and all the altars that he\l"
    .string "had built in the mount of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "cast them out of the city.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_16::
    .string "And he repaired the altar of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and sacrificed thereon peace\l"
    .string "offerings and thank offerings, and\l"
    .string "commanded Judah to serve the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_17::
    .string "Nevertheless the people did\n"
    .string "sacrifice still in the high\l"
    .string "places, yet unto the LORD their God\l"
    .string "only.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_18::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Manasseh, and his prayer unto his\l"
    .string "God, and the words of the seers that\l"
    .string "spake to him in the name of the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, behold, they are\l"
    .string "written in the book of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_19::
    .string "His prayer also, and how God was\n"
    .string "intreated of him, and all his sins,\l"
    .string "and his trespass, and the places\l"
    .string "wherein he built high places, and\l"
    .string "set up groves and graven images,\l"
    .string "before he was humbled: behold, they\l"
    .string "are written among the sayings of the\l"
    .string "seers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_20::
    .string "So Manasseh slept with his\n"
    .string "fathers, and they buried him in his\l"
    .string "own house: and Amon his son reigned\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_21::
    .string "Amon was two and twenty years old\n"
    .string "when he began to reign, and reigned\l"
    .string "two years in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_22::
    .string "But he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, as did\l"
    .string "Manasseh his father: for Amon\l"
    .string "sacrificed unto all the carved\l"
    .string "images which Manasseh his father had\l"
    .string "made, and served them;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_23::
    .string "And humbled not himself before the\n"
    .string "LORD, as Manasseh his father had\l"
    .string "humbled himself; but Amon\l"
    .string "trespassed more and more$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_24::
    .string "And his servants conspired against\n"
    .string "him, and slew him in his own house.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_33_25::
    .string "But the people of the land slew\n"
    .string "all them that had conspired\l"
    .string "against king Amon; and the people\l"
    .string "of the land made Josiah his son king\l"
    .string "in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_1::
    .string "Josiah was eight years old when he\n"
    .string "began to reign, and he reigned in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem one and thirty years.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_2::
    .string "And he did that which was right in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD, and walked in\l"
    .string "the ways of David his father, and\l"
    .string "declined neither to the right hand,\l"
    .string "nor to the left.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_3::
    .string "For in the eighth year of his reign,\n"
    .string "while he was yet young, he began to\l"
    .string "seek after the God of David his\l"
    .string "father: and in the twelfth year he\l"
    .string "began to purge Judah and Jerusalem\l"
    .string "from the high places, and the\l"
    .string "groves, and the carved images, and\l"
    .string "the molten images.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_4::
    .string "And they brake down the altars of\n"
    .string "Baalim in his presence; and the\l"
    .string "images, that were on high above them,\l"
    .string "he cut down; and the groves, and the\l"
    .string "carved images, and the molten\l"
    .string "images, he brake in pieces, and made\l"
    .string "dust of them, and strowed it upon the\l"
    .string "graves of them that had sacrificed\l"
    .string "unto them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_5::
    .string "And he burnt the bones of the\n"
    .string "priests upon their altars, and\l"
    .string "cleansed Judah and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_6::
    .string "And so did he in the cities of\n"
    .string "Manasseh, and Ephraim, and Simeon,\l"
    .string "even unto Naphtali, with their\l"
    .string "mattocks round about.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_7::
    .string "And when he had broken down the\n"
    .string "altars and the groves, and had\l"
    .string "beaten the graven images into\l"
    .string "powder, and cut down all the idols\l"
    .string "throughout all the land of Israel,\l"
    .string "he returned to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_8::
    .string "Now in the eighteenth year of his\n"
    .string "reign, when he had purged the land,\l"
    .string "and the house, he sent Shaphan the\l"
    .string "son of Azaliah, and Maaseiah the\l"
    .string "governor of the city, and Joah the\l"
    .string "son of Joahaz the recorder, to\l"
    .string "repair the house of the LORD his God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_9::
    .string "And when they came to Hilkiah the\n"
    .string "high priest, they delivered the\l"
    .string "money that was brought into the house\l"
    .string "of God, which the Levites that kept\l"
    .string "the doors had gathered of the hand of\l"
    .string "Manasseh and Ephraim, and of all\l"
    .string "the remnant of Israel, and of all\l"
    .string "Judah and Benjamin; and they returned\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_10::
    .string "And they put it in the hand of the\n"
    .string "workmen that had the oversight of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, and they gave it to\l"
    .string "the workmen that wrought in the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD, to repair and amend the\l"
    .string "house:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_11::
    .string "Even to the artificers and builders\n"
    .string "gave they it, to buy hewn stone, and\l"
    .string "timber for couplings, and to floor\l"
    .string "the houses which the kings of Judah\l"
    .string "had destroyed$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_12::
    .string "And the men did the work\n"
    .string "faithfully: and the overseers of\l"
    .string "them were Jahath and Obadiah, the\l"
    .string "Levites, of the sons of Merari; and\l"
    .string "Zechariah and Meshullam, of the\l"
    .string "sons of the Kohathites, to set it\l"
    .string "forward; and other of the Levites,\l"
    .string "all that could skill of\l"
    .string "instruments of musick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_13::
    .string "Also they were over the bearers of\n"
    .string "burdens, and were overseers of all\l"
    .string "that wrought the work in any manner\l"
    .string "of service: and of the Levites there\l"
    .string "were scribes, and officers, and\l"
    .string "porters.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_14::
    .string "And when they brought out the money\n"
    .string "that was brought into the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, Hilkiah the priest found a\l"
    .string "book of the law of the LORD given by\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_15::
    .string "And Hilkiah answered and said to\n"
    .string "Shaphan the scribe, I have found the\l"
    .string "book of the law in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD. And Hilkiah delivered the\l"
    .string "book to Shaphan.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_16::
    .string "And Shaphan carried the book to the\n"
    .string "king, and brought the king word back\l"
    .string "again, saying, All that was\l"
    .string "committed to thy servants, they do it.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_17::
    .string "And they have gathered together the\n"
    .string "money that was found in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and have delivered it into\l"
    .string "the hand of the overseers, and to the\l"
    .string "hand of the workmen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_18::
    .string "Then Shaphan the scribe told the\n"
    .string "king, saying, Hilkiah the priest\l"
    .string "hath given me a book. And Shaphan\l"
    .string "read it before the king.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the king\n"
    .string "had heard the words of the law, that\l"
    .string "he rent his clothes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_20::
    .string "And the king commanded Hilkiah, and\n"
    .string "Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Abdon\l"
    .string "the son of Micah, and Shaphan the\l"
    .string "scribe, and Asaiah a servant of the\l"
    .string "king’s, saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_21::
    .string "Go, enquire of the LORD for me, and\n"
    .string "for them that are left in Israel and\l"
    .string "in Judah, concerning the words of the\l"
    .string "book that is found: for great is the\l"
    .string "wrath of the LORD that is poured out\l"
    .string "upon us, because our fathers have\l"
    .string "not kept the word of the LORD, to do\l"
    .string "after all that is written in this\l"
    .string "book$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_22::
    .string "And Hilkiah, and they that the king\n"
    .string "had appointed, went to Huldah the\l"
    .string "prophetess, the wife of Shallum the\l"
    .string "son of Tikvath, the son of Hasrah,\l"
    .string "keeper of the wardrobe; (now she\l"
    .string "dwelt in Jerusalem in the\l"
    .string "college:) and they spake to her to\l"
    .string "that effect.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_23::
    .string "And she answered them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel, Tell ye the\l"
    .string "man that sent you to me,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_24::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will bring evil upon this place,\l"
    .string "and upon the inhabitants thereof,\l"
    .string "even all the curses that are\l"
    .string "written in the book which they have\l"
    .string "read before the king of Judah:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_25::
    .string "Because they have forsaken me, and\n"
    .string "have burned incense unto other gods,\l"
    .string "that they might provoke me to anger\l"
    .string "with all the works of their hands;\l"
    .string "therefore my wrath shall be poured\l"
    .string "out upon this place, and shall not\l"
    .string "be quenched$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_26::
    .string "And as for the king of Judah, who\n"
    .string "sent you to enquire of the LORD, so\l"
    .string "shall ye say unto him, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel concerning\l"
    .string "the words which thou hast heard;"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_27::
    .string "Because thine heart was tender, and\n"
    .string "thou didst humble thyself before\l"
    .string "God, when thou heardest his words\l"
    .string "against this place, and against the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof, and humbledst\l"
    .string "thyself before me, and didst rend\l"
    .string "thy clothes, and weep before me; I\l"
    .string "have even heard thee also, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_28::
    .string "Behold, I will gather thee to thy\n"
    .string "fathers, and thou shalt be gathered\l"
    .string "to thy grave in peace, neither\l"
    .string "shall thine eyes see all the evil\l"
    .string "that I will bring upon this place,\l"
    .string "and upon the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "same. So they brought the king word\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_29::
    .string "Then the king sent and gathered\n"
    .string "together all the elders of Judah\l"
    .string "and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_30::
    .string "And the king went up into the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and all the men of\l"
    .string "Judah, and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and the priests, and the\l"
    .string "Levites, and all the people,\l"
    .string "great and small: and he read in\l"
    .string "their ears all the words of the book\l"
    .string "of the covenant that was found in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_31::
    .string "And the king stood in his place,\n"
    .string "and made a covenant before the LORD,\l"
    .string "to walk after the LORD, and to keep\l"
    .string "his commandments, and his\l"
    .string "testimonies, and his statutes, with\l"
    .string "all his heart, and with all his\l"
    .string "soul, to perform the words of the\l"
    .string "covenant which are written in this\l"
    .string "book.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_32::
    .string "And he caused all that were\n"
    .string "present in Jerusalem and Benjamin to\l"
    .string "stand to it. And the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem did according to the\l"
    .string "covenant of God, the God of their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_34_33::
    .string "And Josiah took away all the\n"
    .string "abominations out of all the\l"
    .string "countries that pertained to the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, and made all\l"
    .string "that were present in Israel to\l"
    .string "serve, even to serve the LORD their\l"
    .string "God. And all his days they departed\l"
    .string "not from following the LORD, the God\l"
    .string "of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_1::
    .string "Moreover Josiah kept a passover\n"
    .string "unto the LORD in Jerusalem: and they\l"
    .string "killed the passover on the\l"
    .string "fourteenth day of the first month.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_2::
    .string "And he set the priests in their\n"
    .string "charges, and encouraged them to the\l"
    .string "service of the house of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_3::
    .string "And said unto the Levites that\n"
    .string "taught all Israel, which were holy\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, Put the holy ark in\l"
    .string "the house which Solomon the son of\l"
    .string "David king of Israel did build; it\l"
    .string "shall not be a burden upon your\l"
    .string "shoulders: serve now the LORD your\l"
    .string "God, and his people Israel,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_4::
    .string "And prepare yourselves by the\n"
    .string "houses of your fathers, after your\l"
    .string "courses, according to the writing of\l"
    .string "David king of Israel, and according\l"
    .string "to the writing of Solomon his son$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_5::
    .string "And stand in the holy place\n"
    .string "according to the divisions of the\l"
    .string "families of the fathers of your\l"
    .string "brethren the people, and after the\l"
    .string "division of the families of the\l"
    .string "Levites.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_6::
    .string "So kill the passover, and sanctify\n"
    .string "yourselves, and prepare your\l"
    .string "brethren, that they may do according\l"
    .string "to the word of the LORD by the hand of\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_7::
    .string "And Josiah gave to the people, of\n"
    .string "the flock, lambs and kids, all for\l"
    .string "the passover offerings, for all\l"
    .string "that were present, to the number of\l"
    .string "thirty thousand, and three thousand\l"
    .string "bullocks: these were of the king’s\l"
    .string "substance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_8::
    .string "And his princes gave willingly\n"
    .string "unto the people, to the priests,\l"
    .string "and to the Levites: Hilkiah and\l"
    .string "Zechariah and Jehiel, rulers of the\l"
    .string "house of God, gave unto the priests\l"
    .string "for the passover offerings two\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred small\l"
    .string "cattle and three hundred oxen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_9::
    .string "Conaniah also, and Shemaiah and\n"
    .string "Nethaneel, his brethren, and\l"
    .string "Hashabiah and Jeiel and Jozabad,\l"
    .string "chief of the Levites, gave unto the\l"
    .string "Levites for passover offerings five\l"
    .string "thousand small cattle, and five\l"
    .string "hundred oxen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_10::
    .string "So the service was prepared, and\n"
    .string "the priests stood in their place,\l"
    .string "and the Levites in their courses,\l"
    .string "according to the king’s commandment.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_11::
    .string "And they killed the passover, and\n"
    .string "the priests sprinkled the blood\l"
    .string "from their hands, and the Levites\l"
    .string "flayed them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_12::
    .string "And they removed the burnt\n"
    .string "offerings, that they might give\l"
    .string "according to the divisions of the\l"
    .string "families of the people, to offer\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, as it is written in the\l"
    .string "book of Moses. And so did they with\l"
    .string "the oxen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_13::
    .string "And they roasted the passover with\n"
    .string "fire according to the ordinance: but\l"
    .string "the other holy offerings sod they in\l"
    .string "pots, and in caldrons, and in pans,\l"
    .string "and divided them speedily among\l"
    .string "all the people.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_14::
    .string "And afterward they made ready for\n"
    .string "themselves, and for the priests:\l"
    .string "because the priests the sons of\l"
    .string "Aaron were busied in offering of\l"
    .string "burnt offerings and the fat until\l"
    .string "night; therefore the Levites\l"
    .string "prepared for themselves, and for\l"
    .string "the priests the sons of Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_15::
    .string "And the singers the sons of Asaph\n"
    .string "were in their place, according to\l"
    .string "the commandment of David, and Asaph,\l"
    .string "and Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s\l"
    .string "seer; and the porters waited at\l"
    .string "every gate; they might not depart\l"
    .string "from their service; for their\l"
    .string "brethren the Levites prepared for\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_16::
    .string "So all the service of the LORD was\n"
    .string "prepared the same day, to keep the\l"
    .string "passover, and to offer burnt\l"
    .string "offerings upon the altar of the\l"
    .string "LORD, according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "king Josiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_17::
    .string "And the children of Israel that\n"
    .string "were present kept the passover at\l"
    .string "that time, and the feast of\l"
    .string "unleavened bread seven days.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_18::
    .string "And there was no passover like to\n"
    .string "that kept in Israel from the days of\l"
    .string "Samuel the prophet; neither did\l"
    .string "all the kings of Israel keep such\l"
    .string "a passover as Josiah kept, and the\l"
    .string "priests, and the Levites, and all\l"
    .string "Judah and Israel that were present,\l"
    .string "and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_19::
    .string "In the eighteenth year of the reign\n"
    .string "of Josiah was this passover kept.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_20::
    .string "After all this, when Josiah had\n"
    .string "prepared the temple, Necho king of\l"
    .string "Egypt came up to fight against\l"
    .string "Charchemish by Euphrates: and Josiah\l"
    .string "went out against him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_21::
    .string "But he sent ambassadors to him,\n"
    .string "saying, What have I to do with thee,\l"
    .string "thou king of Judah? I come not\l"
    .string "against thee this day, but against\l"
    .string "the house wherewith I have war: for\l"
    .string "God commanded me to make haste:\l"
    .string "forbear thee from meddling with God,\l"
    .string "who is with me, that he destroy thee\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_22::
    .string "Nevertheless Josiah would not turn\n"
    .string "his face from him, but disguised\l"
    .string "himself, that he might fight with\l"
    .string "him, and hearkened not unto the words\l"
    .string "of Necho from the mouth of God, and\l"
    .string "came to fight in the valley of\l"
    .string "Megiddo.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_23::
    .string "And the archers shot at king Josiah;\n"
    .string "and the king said to his servants,\l"
    .string "Have me away; for I am sore wounded.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_24::
    .string "His servants therefore took him out\n"
    .string "of that chariot, and put him in the\l"
    .string "second chariot that he had; and they\l"
    .string "brought him to Jerusalem, and he\l"
    .string "died, and was buried in one of the\l"
    .string "sepulchres of his fathers. And all\l"
    .string "Judah and Jerusalem mourned for\l"
    .string "Josiah.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_25::
    .string "And Jeremiah lamented for Josiah:\n"
    .string "and all the singing men and the\l"
    .string "singing women spake of Josiah in\l"
    .string "their lamentations to this day, and\l"
    .string "made them an ordinance in Israel:\l"
    .string "and, behold, they are written in the\l"
    .string "lamentations.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_26::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of Josiah,\n"
    .string "and his goodness, according to that\l"
    .string "which was written in the law of the\l"
    .string "LORD,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_35_27::
    .string "And his deeds, first and last,\n"
    .string "behold, they are written in the book\l"
    .string "of the kings of Israel and Judah$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_1::
    .string "Then the people of the land took\n"
    .string "Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and made\l"
    .string "him king in his father’s stead in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_2::
    .string "Jehoahaz was twenty and three years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned three months in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_3::
    .string "And the king of Egypt put him down\n"
    .string "at Jerusalem, and condemned the\l"
    .string "land in an hundred talents of\l"
    .string "silver and a talent of gold.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_4::
    .string "And the king of Egypt made Eliakim\n"
    .string "his brother king over Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and turned his name to\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim. And Necho took Jehoahaz\l"
    .string "his brother, and carried him to\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_5::
    .string "Jehoiakim was twenty and five years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned eleven years in Jerusalem:\l"
    .string "and he did that which was evil in the\l"
    .string "sight of the LORD his God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_6::
    .string "Against him came up Nebuchadnezzar\n"
    .string "king of Babylon, and bound him in\l"
    .string "fetters, to carry him to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_7::
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar also carried of the\n"
    .string "vessels of the house of the LORD to\l"
    .string "Babylon, and put them in his\l"
    .string "temple at Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_8::
    .string "Now the rest of the acts of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim, and his abominations\l"
    .string "which he did, and that which was\l"
    .string "found in him, behold, they are\l"
    .string "written in the book of the kings of\l"
    .string "Israel and Judah: and Jehoiachin his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_9::
    .string "Jehoiachin was eight years old when\n"
    .string "he began to reign, and he reigned\l"
    .string "three months and ten days in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: and he did that which was\l"
    .string "evil in the sight of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_10::
    .string "And when the year was expired, king\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar sent, and brought him\l"
    .string "to Babylon, with the goodly vessels\l"
    .string "of the house of the LORD, and made\l"
    .string "Zedekiah his brother king over Judah\l"
    .string "and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_11::
    .string "Zedekiah was one and twenty years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and\l"
    .string "reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_12::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the sight of the LORD his God, and\l"
    .string "humbled not himself before Jeremiah\l"
    .string "the prophet speaking from the\l"
    .string "mouth of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_13::
    .string "And he also rebelled against king\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him\l"
    .string "swear by God: but he stiffened his\l"
    .string "neck, and hardened his heart from\l"
    .string "turning unto the LORD God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_14::
    .string "Moreover all the chief of the\n"
    .string "priests, and the people,\l"
    .string "transgressed very much after all\l"
    .string "the abominations of the heathen; and\l"
    .string "polluted the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "which he had hallowed in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_15::
    .string "And the LORD God of their fathers\n"
    .string "sent to them by his messengers,\l"
    .string "rising up betimes, and sending;\l"
    .string "because he had compassion on his\l"
    .string "people, and on his dwelling\l"
    .string "place:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_16::
    .string "But they mocked the messengers of\n"
    .string "God, and despised his words, and\l"
    .string "misused his prophets, until the\l"
    .string "wrath of the LORD arose against his\l"
    .string "people, till there was no remedy$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_17::
    .string "Therefore he brought upon them the\n"
    .string "king of the Chaldees, who slew their\l"
    .string "young men with the sword in the house\l"
    .string "of their sanctuary, and had no\l"
    .string "compassion upon young man or\l"
    .string "maiden, old man, or him that stooped\l"
    .string "for age: he gave them all into his\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_18::
    .string "And all the vessels of the house\n"
    .string "of God, great and small, and the\l"
    .string "treasures of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and the treasures of the king, and of\l"
    .string "his princes; all these he brought\l"
    .string "to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_19::
    .string "And they burnt the house of God, and\n"
    .string "brake down the wall of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and burnt all the palaces thereof\l"
    .string "with fire, and destroyed all the\l"
    .string "goodly vessels thereof.$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_20::
    .string "And them that had escaped from the\n"
    .string "sword carried he away to Babylon;\l"
    .string "where they were servants to him and\l"
    .string "his sons until the reign of the\l"
    .string "kingdom of Persia:"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_21::
    .string "To fulfil the word of the LORD by\n"
    .string "the mouth of Jeremiah, until the\l"
    .string "land had enjoyed her sabbaths: for as\l"
    .string "long as she lay desolate she kept\l"
    .string "sabbath, to fulfil threescore and\l"
    .string "ten years$"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_22::
    .string "Now in the first year of Cyrus king\n"
    .string "of Persia, that the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "spoken by the mouth of Jeremiah\l"
    .string "might be accomplished, the LORD\l"
    .string "stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king\l"
    .string "of Persia, that he made a\l"
    .string "proclamation throughout all his\l"
    .string "kingdom, and put it also in writing,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_2_Chronicles_36_23::
    .string "Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia,\n"
    .string "All the kingdoms of the earth hath\l"
    .string "the LORD God of heaven given me; and\l"
    .string "he hath charged me to build him an\l"
    .string "house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah\l"
    .string " Who is there among you of all his\l"
    .string "people? The LORD his God be with\l"
    .string "him, and let him go up$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_1::
    .string "Now in the first year of Cyrus king\n"
    .string "of Persia, that the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "by the mouth of Jeremiah might be\l"
    .string "fulfilled, the LORD stirred up the\l"
    .string "spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that\l"
    .string "he made a proclamation throughout\l"
    .string "all his kingdom, and put it also in\l"
    .string "writing, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_2::
    .string "Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, The\n"
    .string "LORD God of heaven hath given me all\l"
    .string "the kingdoms of the earth; and he\l"
    .string "hath charged me to build him an\l"
    .string "house at Jerusalem, which is in Judah$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_3::
    .string "Who is there among you of all his\n"
    .string "people? his God be with him, and\l"
    .string "let him go up to Jerusalem, which is\l"
    .string "in Judah, and build the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, (he is the God,)\l"
    .string "which is in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_4::
    .string "And whosoever remaineth in any\n"
    .string "place where he sojourneth, let the\l"
    .string "men of his place help him with\l"
    .string "silver, and with gold, and with\l"
    .string "goods, and with beasts, beside the\l"
    .string "freewill offering for the house of\l"
    .string "God that is in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_5::
    .string "Then rose up the chief of the\n"
    .string "fathers of Judah and Benjamin, and\l"
    .string "the priests, and the Levites, with\l"
    .string "all them whose spirit God had\l"
    .string "raised, to go up to build the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD which is in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_6::
    .string "And all they that were about them\n"
    .string "strengthened their hands with\l"
    .string "vessels of silver, with gold, with\l"
    .string "goods, and with beasts, and with\l"
    .string "precious things, beside all that\l"
    .string "was willingly offered.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_7::
    .string "Also Cyrus the king brought forth\n"
    .string "the vessels of the house of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which Nebuchadnezzar had brought\l"
    .string "forth out of Jerusalem, and had put\l"
    .string "them in the house of his gods;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_8::
    .string "Even those did Cyrus king of Persia\n"
    .string "bring forth by the hand of Mithredath\l"
    .string "the treasurer, and numbered them unto\l"
    .string "Sheshbazzar, the prince of Judah$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_9::
    .string "And this is the number of them:\n"
    .string "thirty chargers of gold, a thousand\l"
    .string "chargers of silver, nine and twenty\l"
    .string "knives,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_10::
    .string "Thirty basons of gold, silver\n"
    .string "basons of a second sort four hundred\l"
    .string "and ten, and other vessels a thousand$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_1_11::
    .string "All the vessels of gold and of\n"
    .string "silver were five thousand and four\l"
    .string "hundred. All these did Sheshbazzar\l"
    .string "bring up with them of the captivity\l"
    .string "that were brought up from Babylon\l"
    .string "unto Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_1::
    .string "Now these are the children of the\n"
    .string "province that went up out of the\l"
    .string "captivity, of those which had been\l"
    .string "carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon had carried away\l"
    .string "unto Babylon, and came again unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem and Judah, every one unto\l"
    .string "his city;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_2::
    .string "Which came with Zerubbabel: Jeshua,\n"
    .string "Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah,\l"
    .string "Mordecai, Bilshan, Mizpar, Bigvai,\l"
    .string "Rehum, Baanah. The number of the men\l"
    .string "of the people of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_3::
    .string "The children of Parosh, two\n"
    .string "thousand an hundred seventy and two$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_4::
    .string "The children of Shephatiah, three\n"
    .string "hundred seventy and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_5::
    .string "The children of Arah, seven hundred\n"
    .string "seventy and five.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_6::
    .string "The children of Pahathmoab, of the\n"
    .string "children of Jeshua and Joab, two\l"
    .string "thousand eight hundred and twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_7::
    .string "The children of Elam, a thousand\n"
    .string "two hundred fifty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_8::
    .string "The children of Zattu, nine hundred\n"
    .string "forty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_9::
    .string "The children of Zaccai, seven\n"
    .string "hundred and threescore.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_10::
    .string "The children of Bani, six hundred\n"
    .string "forty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_11::
    .string "The children of Bebai, six hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_12::
    .string "The children of Azgad, a thousand\n"
    .string "two hundred twenty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_13::
    .string "The children of Adonikam, six\n"
    .string "hundred sixty and six.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_14::
    .string "The children of Bigvai, two\n"
    .string "thousand fifty and six.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_15::
    .string "The children of Adin, four hundred\n"
    .string "fifty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_16::
    .string "The children of Ater of Hezekiah,\n"
    .string "ninety and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_17::
    .string "The children of Bezai, three\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_18::
    .string "The children of Jorah, an hundred\n"
    .string "and twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_19::
    .string "The children of Hashum, two hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_20::
    .string "The children of Gibbar, ninety and\n"
    .string "five.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_21::
    .string "The children of Bethlehem, an\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_22::
    .string "The men of Netophah, fifty and six.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_23::
    .string "The men of Anathoth, an hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_24::
    .string "The children of Azmaveth, forty and\n"
    .string "two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_25::
    .string "The children of Kirjatharim,\n"
    .string "Chephirah, and Beeroth, seven\l"
    .string "hundred and forty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_26::
    .string "The children of Ramah and Gaba, six\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and one.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_27::
    .string "The men of Michmas, an hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_28::
    .string "The men of Bethel and Ai, two\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_29::
    .string "The children of Nebo, fifty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_30::
    .string "The children of Magbish, an hundred\n"
    .string "fifty and six.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_31::
    .string "The children of the other Elam, a\n"
    .string "thousand two hundred fifty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_32::
    .string "The children of Harim, three\n"
    .string "hundred and twenty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_33::
    .string "The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono,\n"
    .string "seven hundred twenty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_34::
    .string "The children of Jericho, three\n"
    .string "hundred forty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_35::
    .string "The children of Senaah, three\n"
    .string "thousand and six hundred and thirty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_36::
    .string "The priests: the children of\n"
    .string "Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, nine\l"
    .string "hundred seventy and three.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_37::
    .string "The children of Immer, a thousand\n"
    .string "fifty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_38::
    .string "The children of Pashur, a thousand\n"
    .string "two hundred forty and seven.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_39::
    .string "The children of Harim, a thousand\n"
    .string "and seventeen.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_40::
    .string "The Levites: the children of Jeshua\n"
    .string "and Kadmiel, of the children of\l"
    .string "Hodaviah, seventy and four.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_41::
    .string "The singers: the children of\n"
    .string "Asaph, an hundred twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_42::
    .string "The children of the porters: the\n"
    .string "children of Shallum, the children\l"
    .string "of Ater, the children of Talmon, the\l"
    .string "children of Akkub, the children of\l"
    .string "Hatita, the children of Shobai, in\l"
    .string "all an hundred thirty and nine.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_43::
    .string "The Nethinims: the children of\n"
    .string "Ziha, the children of Hasupha, the\l"
    .string "children of Tabbaoth,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_44::
    .string "The children of Keros, the\n"
    .string "children of Siaha, the children of\l"
    .string "Padon,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_45::
    .string "The children of Lebanah, the\n"
    .string "children of Hagabah, the children\l"
    .string "of Akkub,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_46::
    .string "The children of Hagab, the\n"
    .string "children of Shalmai, the children\l"
    .string "of Hanan,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_47::
    .string "The children of Giddel, the\n"
    .string "children of Gahar, the children of\l"
    .string "Reaiah,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_48::
    .string "The children of Rezin, the\n"
    .string "children of Nekoda, the children of\l"
    .string "Gazzam,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_49::
    .string "The children of Uzza, the children\n"
    .string "of Paseah, the children of Besai,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_50::
    .string "The children of Asnah, the\n"
    .string "children of Mehunim, the children\l"
    .string "of Nephusim,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_51::
    .string "The children of Bakbuk, the\n"
    .string "children of Hakupha, the children\l"
    .string "of Harhur,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_52::
    .string "The children of Bazluth, the\n"
    .string "children of Mehida, the children of\l"
    .string "Harsha,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_53::
    .string "The children of Barkos, the\n"
    .string "children of Sisera, the children of\l"
    .string "Thamah,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_54::
    .string "The children of Neziah, the\n"
    .string "children of Hatipha$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_55::
    .string "The children of Solomon’s\n"
    .string "servants: the children of Sotai, the\l"
    .string "children of Sophereth, the\l"
    .string "children of Peruda,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_56::
    .string "The children of Jaalah, the\n"
    .string "children of Darkon, the children of\l"
    .string "Giddel,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_57::
    .string "The children of Shephatiah, the\n"
    .string "children of Hattil, the children of\l"
    .string "Pochereth of Zebaim, the children of\l"
    .string "Ami$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_58::
    .string "All the Nethinims, and the\n"
    .string "children of Solomon’s servants,\l"
    .string "were three hundred ninety and two.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_59::
    .string "And these were they which went up\n"
    .string "from Telmelah, Telharsa, Cherub,\l"
    .string "Addan, and Immer: but they could not\l"
    .string "shew their father’s house, and their\l"
    .string "seed, whether they were of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_60::
    .string "The children of Delaiah, the\n"
    .string "children of Tobiah, the children of\l"
    .string "Nekoda, six hundred fifty and two$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_61::
    .string "And of the children of the priests:\n"
    .string "the children of Habaiah, the\l"
    .string "children of Koz, the children of\l"
    .string "Barzillai; which took a wife of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Barzillai the\l"
    .string "Gileadite, and was called after\l"
    .string "their name:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_62::
    .string "These sought their register among\n"
    .string "those that were reckoned by\l"
    .string "genealogy, but they were not found:\l"
    .string "therefore were they, as polluted,\l"
    .string "put from the priesthood$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_63::
    .string "And the Tirshatha said unto them,\n"
    .string "that they should not eat of the most\l"
    .string "holy things, till there stood up a\l"
    .string "priest with Urim and with Thummim.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_64::
    .string "The whole congregation together\n"
    .string "was forty and two thousand three\l"
    .string "hundred and threescore,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_65::
    .string "Beside their servants and their\n"
    .string "maids, of whom there were seven\l"
    .string "thousand three hundred thirty and\l"
    .string "seven: and there were among them two\l"
    .string "hundred singing men and singing women$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_66::
    .string "Their horses were seven hundred\n"
    .string "thirty and six; their mules, two\l"
    .string "hundred forty and five;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_67::
    .string "Their camels, four hundred thirty\n"
    .string "and five; their asses, six thousand\l"
    .string "seven hundred and twenty$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_68::
    .string "And some of the chief of the\n"
    .string "fathers, when they came to the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD which is at Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "offered freely for the house of God\l"
    .string "to set it up in his place:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_69::
    .string "They gave after their ability unto\n"
    .string "the treasure of the work threescore\l"
    .string "and one thousand drams of gold, and\l"
    .string "five thousand pound of silver, and\l"
    .string "one hundred priests’ garments$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_2_70::
    .string "So the priests, and the Levites,\n"
    .string "and some of the people, and the\l"
    .string "singers, and the porters, and the\l"
    .string "Nethinims, dwelt in their cities,\l"
    .string "and all Israel in their cities.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_1::
    .string "And when the seventh month was come,\n"
    .string "and the children of Israel were in\l"
    .string "the cities, the people gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together as one man to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_2::
    .string "Then stood up Jeshua the son of\n"
    .string "Jozadak, and his brethren the\l"
    .string "priests, and Zerubbabel the son of\l"
    .string "Shealtiel, and his brethren, and\l"
    .string "builded the altar of the God of\l"
    .string "Israel, to offer burnt offerings\l"
    .string "thereon, as it is written in the law\l"
    .string "of Moses the man of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_3::
    .string "And they set the altar upon his\n"
    .string "bases; for fear was upon them\l"
    .string "because of the people of those\l"
    .string "countries: and they offered burnt\l"
    .string "offerings thereon unto the LORD, even\l"
    .string "burnt offerings morning and evening.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_4::
    .string "They kept also the feast of\n"
    .string "tabernacles, as it is written, and\l"
    .string "offered the daily burnt offerings by\l"
    .string "number, according to the custom, as\l"
    .string "the duty of every day required;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_5::
    .string "And afterward offered the\n"
    .string "continual burnt offering, both of\l"
    .string "the new moons, and of all the set\l"
    .string "feasts of the LORD that were\l"
    .string "consecrated, and of every one that\l"
    .string "willingly offered a freewill\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_6::
    .string "From the first day of the seventh\n"
    .string "month began they to offer burnt\l"
    .string "offerings unto the LORD. But the\l"
    .string "foundation of the temple of the\l"
    .string "LORD was not yet laid.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_7::
    .string "They gave money also unto the\n"
    .string "masons, and to the carpenters; and\l"
    .string "meat, and drink, and oil, unto them\l"
    .string "of Zidon, and to them of Tyre, to\l"
    .string "bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the\l"
    .string "sea of Joppa, according to the grant\l"
    .string "that they had of Cyrus king of Persia.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_8::
    .string "Now in the second year of their\n"
    .string "coming unto the house of God at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, in the second month,\l"
    .string "began Zerubbabel the son of\l"
    .string "Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of\l"
    .string "Jozadak, and the remnant of their\l"
    .string "brethren the priests and the\l"
    .string "Levites, and all they that were come\l"
    .string "out of the captivity unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and appointed the\l"
    .string "Levites, from twenty years old and\l"
    .string "upward, to set forward the work of\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_9::
    .string "Then stood Jeshua with his sons and\n"
    .string "his brethren, Kadmiel and his sons,\l"
    .string "the sons of Judah, together, to set\l"
    .string "forward the workmen in the house of\l"
    .string "God: the sons of Henadad, with their\l"
    .string "sons and their brethren the Levites.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_10::
    .string "And when the builders laid the\n"
    .string "foundation of the temple of the\l"
    .string "LORD, they set the priests in their\l"
    .string "apparel with trumpets, and the\l"
    .string "Levites the sons of Asaph with\l"
    .string "cymbals, to praise the LORD, after\l"
    .string "the ordinance of David king of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_11::
    .string "And they sang together by course in\n"
    .string "praising and giving thanks unto the\l"
    .string "LORD; because he is good, for his\l"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever toward\l"
    .string "Israel. And all the people\l"
    .string "shouted with a great shout, when they\l"
    .string "praised the LORD, because the\l"
    .string "foundation of the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "was laid.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_12::
    .string "But many of the priests and Levites\n"
    .string "and chief of the fathers, who were\l"
    .string "ancient men, that had seen the first\l"
    .string "house, when the foundation of this\l"
    .string "house was laid before their eyes,\l"
    .string "wept with a loud voice; and many\l"
    .string "shouted aloud for joy:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_3_13::
    .string "So that the people could not\n"
    .string "discern the noise of the shout of joy\l"
    .string "from the noise of the weeping of the\l"
    .string "people: for the people shouted\l"
    .string "with a loud shout, and the noise was\l"
    .string "heard afar off$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_1::
    .string "Now when the adversaries of Judah\n"
    .string "and Benjamin heard that the children\l"
    .string "of the captivity builded the\l"
    .string "temple unto the LORD God of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_2::
    .string "Then they came to Zerubbabel, and\n"
    .string "to the chief of the fathers, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Let us build with you: for\l"
    .string "we seek your God, as ye do; and we do\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto him since the days of\l"
    .string "Esarhaddon king of Assur, which\l"
    .string "brought us up hither$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_3::
    .string "But Zerubbabel, and Jeshua, and the\n"
    .string "rest of the chief of the fathers of\l"
    .string "Israel, said unto them, Ye have\l"
    .string "nothing to do with us to build an\l"
    .string "house unto our God; but we ourselves\l"
    .string "together will build unto the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, as king Cyrus the king\l"
    .string "of Persia hath commanded us.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_4::
    .string "Then the people of the land\n"
    .string "weakened the hands of the people of\l"
    .string "Judah, and troubled them in\l"
    .string "building,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_5::
    .string "And hired counsellors against\n"
    .string "them, to frustrate their purpose,\l"
    .string "all the days of Cyrus king of\l"
    .string "Persia, even until the reign of\l"
    .string "Darius king of Persia$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_6::
    .string "And in the reign of Ahasuerus, in\n"
    .string "the beginning of his reign, wrote\l"
    .string "they unto him an accusation against\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_7::
    .string "And in the days of Artaxerxes wrote\n"
    .string "Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and\l"
    .string "the rest of their companions, unto\l"
    .string "Artaxerxes king of Persia; and the\l"
    .string "writing of the letter was written in\l"
    .string "the Syrian tongue, and interpreted\l"
    .string "in the Syrian tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_8::
    .string "Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai\n"
    .string "the scribe wrote a letter against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king in\l"
    .string "this sort:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_9::
    .string "Then wrote Rehum the chancellor,\n"
    .string "and Shimshai the scribe, and the rest\l"
    .string "of their companions; the Dinaites,\l"
    .string "the Apharsathchites, the\l"
    .string "Tarpelites, the Apharsites, the\l"
    .string "Archevites, the Babylonians, the\l"
    .string "Susanchites, the Dehavites, and the\l"
    .string "Elamites,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_10::
    .string "And the rest of the nations whom the\n"
    .string "great and noble Asnapper brought\l"
    .string "over, and set in the cities of\l"
    .string "Samaria, and the rest that are on\l"
    .string "this side the river, and at such a\l"
    .string "time$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_11::
    .string "This is the copy of the letter that\n"
    .string "they sent unto him, even unto\l"
    .string "Artaxerxes the king; Thy servants the\l"
    .string "men on this side the river, and at\l"
    .string "such a time.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_12::
    .string "Be it known unto the king, that the\n"
    .string "Jews which came up from thee to us\l"
    .string "are come unto Jerusalem, building\l"
    .string "the rebellious and the bad city, and\l"
    .string "have set up the walls thereof, and\l"
    .string "joined the foundations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_13::
    .string "Be it known now unto the king, that,\n"
    .string "if this city be builded, and the\l"
    .string "walls set up again, then will they\l"
    .string "not pay toll, tribute, and custom,\l"
    .string "and so thou shalt endamage the\l"
    .string "revenue of the kings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_14::
    .string "Now because we have maintenance\n"
    .string "from the king’s palace, and it was\l"
    .string "not meet for us to see the king’s\l"
    .string "dishonour, therefore have we sent and\l"
    .string "certified the king;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_15::
    .string "That search may be made in the book\n"
    .string "of the records of thy fathers: so\l"
    .string "shalt thou find in the book of the\l"
    .string "records, and know that this city is a\l"
    .string "rebellious city, and hurtful unto\l"
    .string "kings and provinces, and that they\l"
    .string "have moved sedition within the same\l"
    .string "of old time: for which cause was this\l"
    .string "city destroyed$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_16::
    .string "We certify the king that, if this\n"
    .string "city be builded again, and the\l"
    .string "walls thereof set up, by this means\l"
    .string "thou shalt have no portion on this\l"
    .string "side the river.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_17::
    .string "Then sent the king an answer unto\n"
    .string "Rehum the chancellor, and to\l"
    .string "Shimshai the scribe, and to the rest\l"
    .string "of their companions that dwell in\l"
    .string "Samaria, and unto the rest beyond the\l"
    .string "river, Peace, and at such a time.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_18::
    .string "The letter which ye sent unto us\n"
    .string "hath been plainly read before me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_19::
    .string "And I commanded, and search hath\n"
    .string "been made, and it is found that this\l"
    .string "city of old time hath made\l"
    .string "insurrection against kings, and that\l"
    .string "rebellion and sedition have been\l"
    .string "made therein.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_20::
    .string "There have been mighty kings also\n"
    .string "over Jerusalem, which have ruled\l"
    .string "over all countries beyond the\l"
    .string "river; and toll, tribute, and\l"
    .string "custom, was paid unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_21::
    .string "Give ye now commandment to cause\n"
    .string "these men to cease, and that this\l"
    .string "city be not builded, until another\l"
    .string "commandment shall be given from me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_22::
    .string "Take heed now that ye fail not to do\n"
    .string "this: why should damage grow to the\l"
    .string "hurt of the kings?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_23::
    .string "Now when the copy of king\n"
    .string "Artaxerxes’ letter was read before\l"
    .string "Rehum, and Shimshai the scribe, and\l"
    .string "their companions, they went up in\l"
    .string "haste to Jerusalem unto the Jews,\l"
    .string "and made them to cease by force and\l"
    .string "power$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_4_24::
    .string "Then ceased the work of the house of\n"
    .string "God which is at Jerusalem. So it\l"
    .string "ceased unto the second year of the\l"
    .string "reign of Darius king of Persia.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_1::
    .string "Then the prophets, Haggai the\n"
    .string "prophet, and Zechariah the son of\l"
    .string "Iddo, prophesied unto the Jews that\l"
    .string "were in Judah and Jerusalem in the\l"
    .string "name of the God of Israel, even unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_2::
    .string "Then rose up Zerubbabel the son of\n"
    .string "Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of\l"
    .string "Jozadak, and began to build the\l"
    .string "house of God which is at Jerusalem:\l"
    .string "and with them were the prophets of\l"
    .string "God helping them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_3::
    .string "At the same time came to them\n"
    .string "Tatnai, governor on this side the\l"
    .string "river, and Shetharboznai and their\l"
    .string "companions, and said thus unto them,\l"
    .string "Who hath commanded you to build this\l"
    .string "house, and to make up this wall?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_4::
    .string "Then said we unto them after this\n"
    .string "manner, What are the names of the men\l"
    .string "that make this building?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_5::
    .string "But the eye of their God was upon\n"
    .string "the elders of the Jews, that they\l"
    .string "could not cause them to cease, till\l"
    .string "the matter came to Darius: and then\l"
    .string "they returned answer by letter\l"
    .string "concerning this matter$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_6::
    .string "The copy of the letter that Tatnai,\n"
    .string "governor on this side the river, and\l"
    .string "Shetharboznai and his companions\l"
    .string "the Apharsachites, which were on\l"
    .string "this side the river, sent unto Darius\l"
    .string "the king:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_7::
    .string "They sent a letter unto him,\n"
    .string "wherein was written thus; Unto Darius\l"
    .string "the king, all peace$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_8::
    .string "Be it known unto the king, that we\n"
    .string "went into the province of Judea, to\l"
    .string "the house of the great God, which is\l"
    .string "builded with great stones, and\l"
    .string "timber is laid in the walls, and\l"
    .string "this work goeth fast on, and\l"
    .string "prospereth in their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_9::
    .string "Then asked we those elders, and\n"
    .string "said unto them thus, Who commanded\l"
    .string "you to build this house, and to make\l"
    .string "up these walls?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_10::
    .string "We asked their names also, to\n"
    .string "certify thee, that we might write the\l"
    .string "names of the men that were the chief\l"
    .string "of them$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_11::
    .string "And thus they returned us answer,\n"
    .string "saying, We are the servants of the\l"
    .string "God of heaven and earth, and build\l"
    .string "the house that was builded these\l"
    .string "many years ago, which a great king of\l"
    .string "Israel builded and set up.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_12::
    .string "But after that our fathers had\n"
    .string "provoked the God of heaven unto\l"
    .string "wrath, he gave them into the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "the Chaldean, who destroyed this\l"
    .string "house, and carried the people away\l"
    .string "into Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_13::
    .string "But in the first year of Cyrus the\n"
    .string "king of Babylon the same king Cyrus\l"
    .string "made a decree to build this house of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_14::
    .string "And the vessels also of gold and\n"
    .string "silver of the house of God, which\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar took out of the\l"
    .string "temple that was in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "brought them into the temple of\l"
    .string "Babylon, those did Cyrus the king\l"
    .string "take out of the temple of Babylon,\l"
    .string "and they were delivered unto one,\l"
    .string "whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he\l"
    .string "had made governor;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_15::
    .string "And said unto him, Take these\n"
    .string "vessels, go, carry them into the\l"
    .string "temple that is in Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "let the house of God be builded in\l"
    .string "his place$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_16::
    .string "Then came the same Sheshbazzar, and\n"
    .string "laid the foundation of the house of\l"
    .string "God which is in Jerusalem: and since\l"
    .string "that time even until now hath it\l"
    .string "been in building, and yet it is not\l"
    .string "finished.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_5_17::
    .string "Now therefore, if it seem good to\n"
    .string "the king, let there be search made in\l"
    .string "the king’s treasure house, which is\l"
    .string "there at Babylon, whether it be so,\l"
    .string "that a decree was made of Cyrus the\l"
    .string "king to build this house of God at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and let the king send his\l"
    .string "pleasure to us concerning this\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_1::
    .string "Then Darius the king made a decree,\n"
    .string "and search was made in the house of\l"
    .string "the rolls, where the treasures were\l"
    .string "laid up in Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_2::
    .string "And there was found at Achmetha, in\n"
    .string "the palace that is in the province\l"
    .string "of the Medes, a roll, and therein\l"
    .string "was a record thus written:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_3::
    .string "In the first year of Cyrus the king\n"
    .string "the same Cyrus the king made a decree\l"
    .string "concerning the house of God at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, Let the house be\l"
    .string "builded, the place where they\l"
    .string "offered sacrifices, and let the\l"
    .string "foundations thereof be strongly\l"
    .string "laid; the height thereof threescore\l"
    .string "cubits, and the breadth thereof\l"
    .string "threescore cubits;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_4::
    .string "With three rows of great stones, and\n"
    .string "a row of new timber: and let the\l"
    .string "expenses be given out of the king’s\l"
    .string "house:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_5::
    .string "And also let the golden and\n"
    .string "silver vessels of the house of God,\l"
    .string "which Nebuchadnezzar took forth out\l"
    .string "of the temple which is at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and brought unto\l"
    .string "Babylon, be restored, and brought\l"
    .string "again unto the temple which is at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, every one to his place,\l"
    .string "and place them in the house of God$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_6::
    .string "Now therefore, Tatnai, governor\n"
    .string "beyond the river, Shetharboznai, and\l"
    .string "your companions the Apharsachites,\l"
    .string "which are beyond the river, be ye far\l"
    .string "from thence:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_7::
    .string "Let the work of this house of God\n"
    .string "alone; let the governor of the Jews\l"
    .string "and the elders of the Jews build\l"
    .string "this house of God in his place$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_8::
    .string "Moreover I make a decree what ye\n"
    .string "shall do to the elders of these\l"
    .string "Jews for the building of this house\l"
    .string "of God: that of the king’s goods,\l"
    .string "even of the tribute beyond the river,\l"
    .string "forthwith expenses be given unto\l"
    .string "these men, that they be not hindered.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_9::
    .string "And that which they have need of,\n"
    .string "both young bullocks, and rams, and\l"
    .string "lambs, for the burnt offerings of the\l"
    .string "God of heaven, wheat, salt, wine, and\l"
    .string "oil, according to the appointment\l"
    .string "of the priests which are at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, let it be given them day\l"
    .string "by day without fail:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_10::
    .string "That they may offer sacrifices of\n"
    .string "sweet savours unto the God of heaven,\l"
    .string "and pray for the life of the king,\l"
    .string "and of his sons$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_11::
    .string "Also I have made a decree, that\n"
    .string "whosoever shall alter this word,\l"
    .string "let timber be pulled down from his\l"
    .string "house, and being set up, let him be\l"
    .string "hanged thereon; and let his house be\l"
    .string "made a dunghill for this.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_12::
    .string "And the God that hath caused his\n"
    .string "name to dwell there destroy all\l"
    .string "kings and people, that shall put\l"
    .string "to their hand to alter and to\l"
    .string "destroy this house of God which is at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem. I Darius have made a\l"
    .string "decree; let it be done with speed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_13::
    .string "Then Tatnai, governor on this side\n"
    .string "the river, Shetharboznai, and their\l"
    .string "companions, according to that which\l"
    .string "Darius the king had sent, so they did\l"
    .string "speedily.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_14::
    .string "And the elders of the Jews builded,\n"
    .string "and they prospered through the\l"
    .string "prophesying of Haggai the prophet\l"
    .string "and Zechariah the son of Iddo. And\l"
    .string "they builded, and finished it,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of the\l"
    .string "God of Israel, and according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of Cyrus, and Darius, and\l"
    .string "Artaxerxes king of Persia.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_15::
    .string "And this house was finished on the\n"
    .string "third day of the month Adar, which\l"
    .string "was in the sixth year of the reign of\l"
    .string "Darius the king.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_16::
    .string "And the children of Israel, the\n"
    .string "priests, and the Levites, and the\l"
    .string "rest of the children of the\l"
    .string "captivity, kept the dedication of\l"
    .string "this house of God with joy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_17::
    .string "And offered at the dedication of\n"
    .string "this house of God an hundred\l"
    .string "bullocks, two hundred rams, four\l"
    .string "hundred lambs; and for a sin\l"
    .string "offering for all Israel, twelve he\l"
    .string "goats, according to the number of the\l"
    .string "tribes of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_18::
    .string "And they set the priests in their\n"
    .string "divisions, and the Levites in their\l"
    .string "courses, for the service of God,\l"
    .string "which is at Jerusalem; as it is\l"
    .string "written in the book of Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_19::
    .string "And the children of the captivity\n"
    .string "kept the passover upon the\l"
    .string "fourteenth day of the first month.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_20::
    .string "For the priests and the Levites\n"
    .string "were purified together, all of them\l"
    .string "were pure, and killed the passover\l"
    .string "for all the children of the\l"
    .string "captivity, and for their brethren\l"
    .string "the priests, and for themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_21::
    .string "And the children of Israel, which\n"
    .string "were come again out of captivity,\l"
    .string "and all such as had separated\l"
    .string "themselves unto them from the\l"
    .string "filthiness of the heathen of the\l"
    .string "land, to seek the LORD God of Israel,\l"
    .string "did eat,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_6_22::
    .string "And kept the feast of unleavened\n"
    .string "bread seven days with joy: for the\l"
    .string "LORD had made them joyful, and\l"
    .string "turned the heart of the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria unto them, to strengthen\l"
    .string "their hands in the work of the house\l"
    .string "of God, the God of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_1::
    .string "Now after these things, in the reign\n"
    .string "of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra\l"
    .string "the son of Seraiah, the son of\l"
    .string "Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_2::
    .string "The son of Shallum, the son of\n"
    .string "Zadok, the son of Ahitub,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_3::
    .string "The son of Amariah, the son of\n"
    .string "Azariah, the son of Meraioth,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_4::
    .string "The son of Zerahiah, the son of\n"
    .string "Uzzi, the son of Bukki,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_5::
    .string "The son of Abishua, the son of\n"
    .string "Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the\l"
    .string "son of Aaron the chief priest:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_6::
    .string "This Ezra went up from Babylon; and\n"
    .string "he was a ready scribe in the law of\l"
    .string "Moses, which the LORD God of Israel\l"
    .string "had given: and the king granted him\l"
    .string "all his request, according to the\l"
    .string "hand of the LORD his God upon him$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_7::
    .string "And there went up some of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, and of the\l"
    .string "priests, and the Levites, and the\l"
    .string "singers, and the porters, and the\l"
    .string "Nethinims, unto Jerusalem, in the\l"
    .string "seventh year of Artaxerxes the king.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_8::
    .string "And he came to Jerusalem in the\n"
    .string "fifth month, which was in the seventh\l"
    .string "year of the king.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_9::
    .string "For upon the first day of the first\n"
    .string "month began he to go up from\l"
    .string "Babylon, and on the first day of the\l"
    .string "fifth month came he to Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "according to the good hand of his God\l"
    .string "upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_10::
    .string "For Ezra had prepared his heart to\n"
    .string "seek the law of the LORD, and to do\l"
    .string "it, and to teach in Israel statutes\l"
    .string "and judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_11::
    .string "Now this is the copy of the letter\n"
    .string "that the king Artaxerxes gave unto\l"
    .string "Ezra the priest, the scribe, even a\l"
    .string "scribe of the words of the\l"
    .string "commandments of the LORD, and of his\l"
    .string "statutes to Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_12::
    .string "Artaxerxes, king of kings, unto Ezra\n"
    .string "the priest, a scribe of the law of\l"
    .string "the God of heaven, perfect peace,\l"
    .string "and at such a time.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_13::
    .string "I make a decree, that all they of\n"
    .string "the people of Israel, and of his\l"
    .string "priests and Levites, in my realm,\l"
    .string "which are minded of their own\l"
    .string "freewill to go up to Jerusalem, go\l"
    .string "with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_14::
    .string "Forasmuch as thou art sent of the\n"
    .string "king, and of his seven counsellors,\l"
    .string "to enquire concerning Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, according to the law of\l"
    .string "thy God which is in thine hand;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_15::
    .string "And to carry the silver and gold,\n"
    .string "which the king and his counsellors\l"
    .string "have freely offered unto the God of\l"
    .string "Israel, whose habitation is in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_16::
    .string "And all the silver and gold that\n"
    .string "thou canst find in all the province\l"
    .string "of Babylon, with the freewill\l"
    .string "offering of the people, and of the\l"
    .string "priests, offering willingly for\l"
    .string "the house of their God which is in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_17::
    .string "That thou mayest buy speedily with\n"
    .string "this money bullocks, rams, lambs,\l"
    .string "with their meat offerings and their\l"
    .string "drink offerings, and offer them upon\l"
    .string "the altar of the house of your God\l"
    .string "which is in Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_18::
    .string "And whatsoever shall seem good to\n"
    .string "thee, and to thy brethren, to do with\l"
    .string "the rest of the silver and the gold,\l"
    .string "that do after the will of your God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_19::
    .string "The vessels also that are given\n"
    .string "thee for the service of the house of\l"
    .string "thy God, those deliver thou before\l"
    .string "the God of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_20::
    .string "And whatsoever more shall be\n"
    .string "needful for the house of thy God,\l"
    .string "which thou shalt have occasion to\l"
    .string "bestow, bestow it out of the king’s\l"
    .string "treasure house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_21::
    .string "And I, even I Artaxerxes the king,\n"
    .string "do make a decree to all the\l"
    .string "treasurers which are beyond the\l"
    .string "river, that whatsoever Ezra the\l"
    .string "priest, the scribe of the law of the\l"
    .string "God of heaven, shall require of you,\l"
    .string "it be done speedily,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_22::
    .string "Unto an hundred talents of silver,\n"
    .string "and to an hundred measures of wheat,\l"
    .string "and to an hundred baths of wine, and\l"
    .string "to an hundred baths of oil, and salt\l"
    .string "without prescribing how much$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_23::
    .string "Whatsoever is commanded by the God\n"
    .string "of heaven, let it be diligently\l"
    .string "done for the house of the God of\l"
    .string "heaven: for why should there be\l"
    .string "wrath against the realm of the king\l"
    .string "and his sons?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_24::
    .string "Also we certify you, that touching\n"
    .string "any of the priests and Levites,\l"
    .string "singers, porters, Nethinims, or\l"
    .string "ministers of this house of God, it\l"
    .string "shall not be lawful to impose\l"
    .string "toll, tribute, or custom, upon them$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_25::
    .string "And thou, Ezra, after the wisdom of\n"
    .string "thy God, that is in thine hand, set\l"
    .string "magistrates and judges, which may\l"
    .string "judge all the people that are\l"
    .string "beyond the river, all such as know\l"
    .string "the laws of thy God; and teach ye\l"
    .string "them that know them not.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_26::
    .string "And whosoever will not do the law\n"
    .string "of thy God, and the law of the king,\l"
    .string "let judgment be executed speedily\l"
    .string "upon him, whether it be unto death,\l"
    .string "or to banishment, or to confiscation\l"
    .string "of goods, or to imprisonment.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_27::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God of our\n"
    .string "fathers, which hath put such a thing\l"
    .string "as this in the king’s heart, to\l"
    .string "beautify the house of the LORD which\l"
    .string "is in Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_7_28::
    .string "And hath extended mercy unto me\n"
    .string "before the king, and his\l"
    .string "counsellors, and before all the\l"
    .string "king’s mighty princes. And I was\l"
    .string "strengthened as the hand of the LORD\l"
    .string "my God was upon me, and I gathered\l"
    .string "together out of Israel chief men to\l"
    .string "go up with me$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_1::
    .string "These are now the chief of their\n"
    .string "fathers, and this is the genealogy\l"
    .string "of them that went up with me from\l"
    .string "Babylon, in the reign of Artaxerxes\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_2::
    .string "Of the sons of Phinehas; Gershom: of\n"
    .string "the sons of Ithamar; Daniel: of the\l"
    .string "sons of David; Hattush.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_3::
    .string "Of the sons of Shechaniah, of the\n"
    .string "sons of Pharosh; Zechariah: and with\l"
    .string "him were reckoned by genealogy of\l"
    .string "the males an hundred and fifty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_4::
    .string "Of the sons of Pahathmoab;\n"
    .string "Elihoenai the son of Zerahiah, and\l"
    .string "with him two hundred males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_5::
    .string "Of the sons of Shechaniah; the son\n"
    .string "of Jahaziel, and with him three\l"
    .string "hundred males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_6::
    .string "Of the sons also of Adin; Ebed the\n"
    .string "son of Jonathan, and with him fifty\l"
    .string "males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_7::
    .string "And of the sons of Elam; Jeshaiah\n"
    .string "the son of Athaliah, and with him\l"
    .string "seventy males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_8::
    .string "And of the sons of Shephatiah;\n"
    .string "Zebadiah the son of Michael, and\l"
    .string "with him fourscore males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_9::
    .string "Of the sons of Joab; Obadiah the son\n"
    .string "of Jehiel, and with him two hundred\l"
    .string "and eighteen males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_10::
    .string "And of the sons of Shelomith; the\n"
    .string "son of Josiphiah, and with him an\l"
    .string "hundred and threescore males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_11::
    .string "And of the sons of Bebai; Zechariah\n"
    .string "the son of Bebai, and with him twenty\l"
    .string "and eight males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_12::
    .string "And of the sons of Azgad; Johanan\n"
    .string "the son of Hakkatan, and with him an\l"
    .string "hundred and ten males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_13::
    .string "And of the last sons of Adonikam,\n"
    .string "whose names are these, Eliphelet,\l"
    .string "Jeiel, and Shemaiah, and with them\l"
    .string "threescore males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_14::
    .string "Of the sons also of Bigvai; Uthai,\n"
    .string "and Zabbud, and with them seventy\l"
    .string "males.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_15::
    .string "And I gathered them together to the\n"
    .string "river that runneth to Ahava; and\l"
    .string "there abode we in tents three days:\l"
    .string "and I viewed the people, and the\l"
    .string "priests, and found there none of the\l"
    .string "sons of Levi.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_16::
    .string "Then sent I for Eliezer, for Ariel,\n"
    .string "for Shemaiah, and for Elnathan, and\l"
    .string "for Jarib, and for Elnathan, and for\l"
    .string "Nathan, and for Zechariah, and for\l"
    .string "Meshullam, chief men; also for\l"
    .string "Joiarib, and for Elnathan, men of\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_17::
    .string "And I sent them with commandment\n"
    .string "unto Iddo the chief at the place\l"
    .string "Casiphia, and I told them what they\l"
    .string "should say unto Iddo, and to his\l"
    .string "brethren the Nethinims, at the\l"
    .string "place Casiphia, that they should\l"
    .string "bring unto us ministers for the house\l"
    .string "of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_18::
    .string "And by the good hand of our God upon\n"
    .string "us they brought us a man of\l"
    .string "understanding, of the sons of Mahli,\l"
    .string "the son of Levi, the son of Israel;\l"
    .string "and Sherebiah, with his sons and his\l"
    .string "brethren, eighteen;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_19::
    .string "And Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah\n"
    .string "of the sons of Merari, his brethren\l"
    .string "and their sons, twenty;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_20::
    .string "Also of the Nethinims, whom David\n"
    .string "and the princes had appointed for\l"
    .string "the service of the Levites, two\l"
    .string "hundred and twenty Nethinims: all\l"
    .string "of them were expressed by name$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_21::
    .string "Then I proclaimed a fast there, at\n"
    .string "the river of Ahava, that we might\l"
    .string "afflict ourselves before our God,\l"
    .string "to seek of him a right way for us, and\l"
    .string "for our little ones, and for all\l"
    .string "our substance.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_22::
    .string "For I was ashamed to require of the\n"
    .string "king a band of soldiers and horsemen\l"
    .string "to help us against the enemy in the\l"
    .string "way: because we had spoken unto the\l"
    .string "king, saying, The hand of our God is\l"
    .string "upon all them for good that seek\l"
    .string "him; but his power and his wrath is\l"
    .string "against all them that forsake him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_23::
    .string "So we fasted and besought our God\n"
    .string "for this: and he was intreated of us.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_24::
    .string "Then I separated twelve of the\n"
    .string "chief of the priests, Sherebiah,\l"
    .string "Hashabiah, and ten of their brethren\l"
    .string "with them,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_25::
    .string "And weighed unto them the silver,\n"
    .string "and the gold, and the vessels, even\l"
    .string "the offering of the house of our God,\l"
    .string "which the king, and his\l"
    .string "counsellors, and his lords, and\l"
    .string "all Israel there present, had\l"
    .string "offered:"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_26::
    .string "I even weighed unto their hand six\n"
    .string "hundred and fifty talents of\l"
    .string "silver, and silver vessels an\l"
    .string "hundred talents, and of gold an\l"
    .string "hundred talents;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_27::
    .string "Also twenty basons of gold, of a\n"
    .string "thousand drams; and two vessels of\l"
    .string "fine copper, precious as gold$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_28::
    .string "And I said unto them, Ye are holy\n"
    .string "unto the LORD; the vessels are holy\l"
    .string "also; and the silver and the gold\l"
    .string "are a freewill offering unto the\l"
    .string "LORD God of your fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_29::
    .string "Watch ye, and keep them, until ye\n"
    .string "weigh them before the chief of the\l"
    .string "priests and the Levites, and chief of\l"
    .string "the fathers of Israel, at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, in the chambers of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_30::
    .string "So took the priests and the Levites\n"
    .string "the weight of the silver, and the\l"
    .string "gold, and the vessels, to bring them\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem unto the house of our\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_31::
    .string "Then we departed from the river of\n"
    .string "Ahava on the twelfth day of the\l"
    .string "first month, to go unto Jerusalem:\l"
    .string "and the hand of our God was upon us,\l"
    .string "and he delivered us from the hand of\l"
    .string "the enemy, and of such as lay in wait\l"
    .string "by the way.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_32::
    .string "And we came to Jerusalem, and abode\n"
    .string "there three days.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_33::
    .string "Now on the fourth day was the\n"
    .string "silver and the gold and the vessels\l"
    .string "weighed in the house of our God by\l"
    .string "the hand of Meremoth the son of Uriah\l"
    .string "the priest; and with him was Eleazar\l"
    .string "the son of Phinehas; and with them\l"
    .string "was Jozabad the son of Jeshua, and\l"
    .string "Noadiah the son of Binnui, Levites;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_34::
    .string "By number and by weight of every\n"
    .string "one: and all the weight was written\l"
    .string "at that time$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_35::
    .string "Also the children of those that\n"
    .string "had been carried away, which were\l"
    .string "come out of the captivity, offered\l"
    .string "burnt offerings unto the God of\l"
    .string "Israel, twelve bullocks for all\l"
    .string "Israel, ninety and six rams, seventy\l"
    .string "and seven lambs, twelve he goats for\l"
    .string "a sin offering: all this was a burnt\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_8_36::
    .string "And they delivered the king’s\n"
    .string "commissions unto the king’s\l"
    .string "lieutenants, and to the governors on\l"
    .string "this side the river: and they\l"
    .string "furthered the people, and the house\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_1::
    .string "Now when these things were done, the\n"
    .string "princes came to me, saying, The\l"
    .string "people of Israel, and the priests,\l"
    .string "and the Levites, have not separated\l"
    .string "themselves from the people of the\l"
    .string "lands, doing according to their\l"
    .string "abominations, even of the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, the Hittites, the\l"
    .string "Perizzites, the Jebusites, the\l"
    .string "Ammonites, the Moabites, the\l"
    .string "Egyptians, and the Amorites.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_2::
    .string "For they have taken of their\n"
    .string "daughters for themselves, and for\l"
    .string "their sons: so that the holy seed\l"
    .string "have mingled themselves with the\l"
    .string "people of those lands: yea, the\l"
    .string "hand of the princes and rulers hath\l"
    .string "been chief in this trespass.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_3::
    .string "And when I heard this thing, I rent\n"
    .string "my garment and my mantle, and\l"
    .string "plucked off the hair of my head and\l"
    .string "of my beard, and sat down astonied.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_4::
    .string "Then were assembled unto me every\n"
    .string "one that trembled at the words of\l"
    .string "the God of Israel, because of the\l"
    .string "transgression of those that had been\l"
    .string "carried away; and I sat astonied\l"
    .string "until the evening sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_5::
    .string "And at the evening sacrifice I arose\n"
    .string "up from my heaviness; and having\l"
    .string "rent my garment and my mantle, I\l"
    .string "fell upon my knees, and spread out\l"
    .string "my hands unto the LORD my God,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_6::
    .string "And said, O my God, I am ashamed and\n"
    .string "blush to lift up my face to thee, my\l"
    .string "God: for our iniquities are increased\l"
    .string "over our head, and our trespass is\l"
    .string "grown up unto the heavens$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_7::
    .string "Since the days of our fathers have\n"
    .string "we been in a great trespass unto\l"
    .string "this day; and for our iniquities have\l"
    .string "we, our kings, and our priests, been\l"
    .string "delivered into the hand of the kings\l"
    .string "of the lands, to the sword, to\l"
    .string "captivity, and to a spoil, and to\l"
    .string "confusion of face, as it is this day.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_8::
    .string "And now for a little space grace\n"
    .string "hath been shewed from the LORD our\l"
    .string "God, to leave us a remnant to\l"
    .string "escape, and to give us a nail in his\l"
    .string "holy place, that our God may\l"
    .string "lighten our eyes, and give us a\l"
    .string "little reviving in our bondage.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_9::
    .string "For we were bondmen; yet our God\n"
    .string "hath not forsaken us in our bondage,\l"
    .string "but hath extended mercy unto us in\l"
    .string "the sight of the kings of Persia, to\l"
    .string "give us a reviving, to set up the\l"
    .string "house of our God, and to repair the\l"
    .string "desolations thereof, and to give us\l"
    .string "a wall in Judah and in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_10::
    .string "And now, O our God, what shall we\n"
    .string "say after this? for we have forsaken\l"
    .string "thy commandments,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_11::
    .string "Which thou hast commanded by thy\n"
    .string "servants the prophets, saying, The\l"
    .string "land, unto which ye go to possess it,\l"
    .string "is an unclean land with the\l"
    .string "filthiness of the people of the\l"
    .string "lands, with their abominations,\l"
    .string "which have filled it from one end to\l"
    .string "another with their uncleanness$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_12::
    .string "Now therefore give not your\n"
    .string "daughters unto their sons, neither\l"
    .string "take their daughters unto your sons,\l"
    .string "nor seek their peace or their\l"
    .string "wealth for ever: that ye may be\l"
    .string "strong, and eat the good of the land,\l"
    .string "and leave it for an inheritance to\l"
    .string "your children for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_13::
    .string "And after all that is come upon us\n"
    .string "for our evil deeds, and for our great\l"
    .string "trespass, seeing that thou our God\l"
    .string "hast punished us less than our\l"
    .string "iniquities deserve, and hast given us\l"
    .string "such deliverance as this;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_14::
    .string "Should we again break thy\n"
    .string "commandments, and join in affinity\l"
    .string "with the people of these\l"
    .string "abominations? wouldest not thou be\l"
    .string "angry with us till thou hadst\l"
    .string "consumed us, so that there should be\l"
    .string "no remnant nor escaping?"
Bible_Text_Ezra_9_15::
    .string "O LORD God of Israel, thou art\n"
    .string "righteous: for we remain yet\l"
    .string "escaped, as it is this day: behold,\l"
    .string "we are before thee in our\l"
    .string "trespasses: for we cannot stand\l"
    .string "before thee because of this$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_1::
    .string "Now when Ezra had prayed, and when\n"
    .string "he had confessed, weeping and\l"
    .string "casting himself down before the\l"
    .string "house of God, there assembled unto\l"
    .string "him out of Israel a very great\l"
    .string "congregation of men and women and\l"
    .string "children: for the people wept\l"
    .string "very sore.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_2::
    .string "And Shechaniah the son of Jehiel,\n"
    .string "one of the sons of Elam, answered and\l"
    .string "said unto Ezra, We have trespassed\l"
    .string "against our God, and have taken\l"
    .string "strange wives of the people of the\l"
    .string "land: yet now there is hope in\l"
    .string "Israel concerning this thing.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_3::
    .string "Now therefore let us make a\n"
    .string "covenant with our God to put away\l"
    .string "all the wives, and such as are born\l"
    .string "of them, according to the counsel of\l"
    .string "my lord, and of those that tremble\l"
    .string "at the commandment of our God; and\l"
    .string "let it be done according to the law.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_4::
    .string "Arise; for this matter belongeth\n"
    .string "unto thee: we also will be with\l"
    .string "thee: be of good courage, and do it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_5::
    .string "Then arose Ezra, and made the chief\n"
    .string "priests, the Levites, and all\l"
    .string "Israel, to swear that they should do\l"
    .string "according to this word. And they\l"
    .string "sware.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_6::
    .string "Then Ezra rose up from before the\n"
    .string "house of God, and went into the\l"
    .string "chamber of Johanan the son of\l"
    .string "Eliashib: and when he came thither,\l"
    .string "he did eat no bread, nor drink water:\l"
    .string "for he mourned because of the\l"
    .string "transgression of them that had been\l"
    .string "carried away.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_7::
    .string "And they made proclamation\n"
    .string "throughout Judah and Jerusalem unto\l"
    .string "all the children of the captivity,\l"
    .string "that they should gather themselves\l"
    .string "together unto Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_8::
    .string "And that whosoever would not come\n"
    .string "within three days, according to the\l"
    .string "counsel of the princes and the\l"
    .string "elders, all his substance should\l"
    .string "be forfeited, and himself separated\l"
    .string "from the congregation of those that\l"
    .string "had been carried away$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_9::
    .string "Then all the men of Judah and\n"
    .string "Benjamin gathered themselves\l"
    .string "together unto Jerusalem within\l"
    .string "three days. It was the ninth month,\l"
    .string "on the twentieth day of the month;\l"
    .string "and all the people sat in the\l"
    .string "street of the house of God,\l"
    .string "trembling because of this matter,\l"
    .string "and for the great rain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_10::
    .string "And Ezra the priest stood up, and\n"
    .string "said unto them, Ye have transgressed,\l"
    .string "and have taken strange wives, to\l"
    .string "increase the trespass of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_11::
    .string "Now therefore make confession unto\n"
    .string "the LORD God of your fathers, and do\l"
    .string "his pleasure: and separate\l"
    .string "yourselves from the people of the\l"
    .string "land, and from the strange wives.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_12::
    .string "Then all the congregation answered\n"
    .string "and said with a loud voice, As thou\l"
    .string "hast said, so must we do.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_13::
    .string "But the people are many, and it is\n"
    .string "a time of much rain, and we are not\l"
    .string "able to stand without, neither is\l"
    .string "this a work of one day or two: for we\l"
    .string "are many that have transgressed in\l"
    .string "this thing.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_14::
    .string "Let now our rulers of all the\n"
    .string "congregation stand, and let all\l"
    .string "them which have taken strange wives\l"
    .string "in our cities come at appointed\l"
    .string "times, and with them the elders of\l"
    .string "every city, and the judges thereof,\l"
    .string "until the fierce wrath of our God\l"
    .string "for this matter be turned from us.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_15::
    .string "Only Jonathan the son of Asahel\n"
    .string "and Jahaziah the son of Tikvah were\l"
    .string "employed about this matter: and\l"
    .string "Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite\l"
    .string "helped them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_16::
    .string "And the children of the captivity\n"
    .string "did so. And Ezra the priest, with\l"
    .string "certain chief of the fathers, after\l"
    .string "the house of their fathers, and all\l"
    .string "of them by their names, were\l"
    .string "separated, and sat down in the first\l"
    .string "day of the tenth month to examine the\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_17::
    .string "And they made an end with all the\n"
    .string "men that had taken strange wives by\l"
    .string "the first day of the first month.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_18::
    .string "And among the sons of the priests\n"
    .string "there were found that had taken\l"
    .string "strange wives: namely, of the sons\l"
    .string "of Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his\l"
    .string "brethren; Maaseiah, and Eliezer, and\l"
    .string "Jarib, and Gedaliah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_19::
    .string "And they gave their hands that they\n"
    .string "would put away their wives; and\l"
    .string "being guilty, they offered a ram of\l"
    .string "the flock for their trespass.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_20::
    .string "And of the sons of Immer; Hanani,\n"
    .string "and Zebadiah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_21::
    .string "And of the sons of Harim; Maaseiah,\n"
    .string "and Elijah, and Shemaiah, and\l"
    .string "Jehiel, and Uzziah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_22::
    .string "And of the sons of Pashur;\n"
    .string "Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael,\l"
    .string "Nethaneel, Jozabad, and Elasah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_23::
    .string "Also of the Levites; Jozabad, and\n"
    .string "Shimei, and Kelaiah, (the same is\l"
    .string "Kelita,) Pethahiah, Judah, and\l"
    .string "Eliezer.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_24::
    .string "Of the singers also; Eliashib: and\n"
    .string "of the porters; Shallum, and\l"
    .string "Telem, and Uri.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_25::
    .string "Moreover of Israel: of the sons of\n"
    .string "Parosh; Ramiah, and Jeziah, and\l"
    .string "Malchiah, and Miamin, and Eleazar,\l"
    .string "and Malchijah, and Benaiah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_26::
    .string "And of the sons of Elam; Mattaniah,\n"
    .string "Zechariah, and Jehiel, and Abdi, and\l"
    .string "Jeremoth, and Eliah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_27::
    .string "And of the sons of Zattu; Elioenai,\n"
    .string "Eliashib, Mattaniah, and Jeremoth,\l"
    .string "and Zabad, and Aziza.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_28::
    .string "Of the sons also of Bebai;\n"
    .string "Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and\l"
    .string "Athlai.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_29::
    .string "And of the sons of Bani; Meshullam,\n"
    .string "Malluch, and Adaiah, Jashub, and\l"
    .string "Sheal, and Ramoth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_30::
    .string "And of the sons of Pahathmoab; Adna,\n"
    .string "and Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah,\l"
    .string "Mattaniah, Bezaleel, and Binnui,\l"
    .string "and Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_31::
    .string "And of the sons of Harim; Eliezer,\n"
    .string "Ishijah, Malchiah, Shemaiah,\l"
    .string "Shimeon,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_32::
    .string "Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_33::
    .string "Of the sons of Hashum; Mattenai,\n"
    .string "Mattathah, Zabad, Eliphelet,\l"
    .string "Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_34::
    .string "Of the sons of Bani; Maadai, Amram,\n"
    .string "and Uel,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_35::
    .string "Benaiah, Bedeiah, Chelluh,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_36::
    .string "Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_37::
    .string "Mattaniah, Mattenai, and Jaasau,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_38::
    .string "And Bani, and Binnui, Shimei,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_39::
    .string "And Shelemiah, and Nathan, and\n"
    .string "Adaiah,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_40::
    .string "Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_41::
    .string "Azareel, and Shelemiah, Shemariah,"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_42::
    .string "Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_43::
    .string "Of the sons of Nebo; Jeiel,\n"
    .string "Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Jadau, and\l"
    .string "Joel, Benaiah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezra_10_44::
    .string "All these had taken strange wives:\n"
    .string "and some of them had wives by whom\l"
    .string "they had children.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_1::
    .string "The words of Nehemiah the son of\n"
    .string "Hachaliah. And it came to pass in\l"
    .string "the month Chisleu, in the twentieth\l"
    .string "year, as I was in Shushan the\l"
    .string "palace,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_2::
    .string "That Hanani, one of my brethren,\n"
    .string "came, he and certain men of Judah;\l"
    .string "and I asked them concerning the Jews\l"
    .string "that had escaped, which were left of\l"
    .string "the captivity, and concerning\l"
    .string "Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_3::
    .string "And they said unto me, The remnant\n"
    .string "that are left of the captivity\l"
    .string "there in the province are in great\l"
    .string "affliction and reproach: the wall\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem also is broken down,\l"
    .string "and the gates thereof are burned with\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, when I heard\n"
    .string "these words, that I sat down and\l"
    .string "wept, and mourned certain days, and\l"
    .string "fasted, and prayed before the God of\l"
    .string "heaven,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_5::
    .string "And said, I beseech thee, O LORD God\n"
    .string "of heaven, the great and terrible\l"
    .string "God, that keepeth covenant and mercy\l"
    .string "for them that love him and observe\l"
    .string "his commandments:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_6::
    .string "Let thine ear now be attentive, and\n"
    .string "thine eyes open, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "hear the prayer of thy servant,\l"
    .string "which I pray before thee now, day and\l"
    .string "night, for the children of Israel\l"
    .string "thy servants, and confess the sins of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel, which we\l"
    .string "have sinned against thee: both I and\l"
    .string "my father’s house have sinned$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_7::
    .string "We have dealt very corruptly\n"
    .string "against thee, and have not kept the\l"
    .string "commandments, nor the statutes, nor\l"
    .string "the judgments, which thou\l"
    .string "commandedst thy servant Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_8::
    .string "Remember, I beseech thee, the word\n"
    .string "that thou commandedst thy servant\l"
    .string "Moses, saying, If ye transgress, I\l"
    .string "will scatter you abroad among the\l"
    .string "nations:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_9::
    .string "But if ye turn unto me, and keep my\n"
    .string "commandments, and do them; though\l"
    .string "there were of you cast out unto the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of the heaven, yet\l"
    .string "will I gather them from thence, and\l"
    .string "will bring them unto the place\l"
    .string "that I have chosen to set my name\l"
    .string "there$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_10::
    .string "Now these are thy servants and thy\n"
    .string "people, whom thou hast redeemed by\l"
    .string "thy great power, and by thy strong\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_1_11::
    .string "O LORD, I beseech thee, let now\n"
    .string "thine ear be attentive to the prayer\l"
    .string "of thy servant, and to the prayer of\l"
    .string "thy servants, who desire to fear thy\l"
    .string "name: and prosper, I pray thee, thy\l"
    .string "servant this day, and grant him mercy\l"
    .string "in the sight of this man. For I was\l"
    .string "the king’s cupbearer.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the month\n"
    .string "Nisan, in the twentieth year of\l"
    .string "Artaxerxes the king, that wine was\l"
    .string "before him: and I took up the wine,\l"
    .string "and gave it unto the king. Now I had\l"
    .string "not been beforetime sad in his\l"
    .string "presence.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_2::
    .string "Wherefore the king said unto me, Why\n"
    .string "is thy countenance sad, seeing thou\l"
    .string "art not sick? this is nothing else\l"
    .string "but sorrow of heart. Then I was very\l"
    .string "sore afraid,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_3::
    .string "And said unto the king, Let the king\n"
    .string "live for ever: why should not my\l"
    .string "countenance be sad, when the city,\l"
    .string "the place of my fathers’\l"
    .string "sepulchres, lieth waste, and the\l"
    .string "gates thereof are consumed with fire?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_4::
    .string "Then the king said unto me, For what\n"
    .string "dost thou make request? So I prayed\l"
    .string "to the God of heaven$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_5::
    .string "And I said unto the king, If it\n"
    .string "please the king, and if thy servant\l"
    .string "have found favour in thy sight, that\l"
    .string "thou wouldest send me unto Judah,\l"
    .string "unto the city of my fathers’\l"
    .string "sepulchres, that I may build it.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_6::
    .string "And the king said unto me, (the\n"
    .string "queen also sitting by him,) For how\l"
    .string "long shall thy journey be? and when\l"
    .string "wilt thou return? So it pleased the\l"
    .string "king to send me; and I set him a time.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_7::
    .string "Moreover I said unto the king, If it\n"
    .string "please the king, let letters be\l"
    .string "given me to the governors beyond the\l"
    .string "river, that they may convey me over\l"
    .string "till I come into Judah;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_8::
    .string "And a letter unto Asaph the keeper\n"
    .string "of the king’s forest, that he may\l"
    .string "give me timber to make beams for the\l"
    .string "gates of the palace which\l"
    .string "appertained to the house, and for\l"
    .string "the wall of the city, and for the\l"
    .string "house that I shall enter into. And\l"
    .string "the king granted me, according to the\l"
    .string "good hand of my God upon me$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_9::
    .string "Then I came to the governors beyond\n"
    .string "the river, and gave them the king’s\l"
    .string "letters. Now the king had sent\l"
    .string "captains of the army and horsemen\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_10::
    .string "When Sanballat the Horonite, and\n"
    .string "Tobiah the servant, the Ammonite,\l"
    .string "heard of it, it grieved them\l"
    .string "exceedingly that there was come a\l"
    .string "man to seek the welfare of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_11::
    .string "So I came to Jerusalem, and was\n"
    .string "there three days.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_12::
    .string "And I arose in the night, I and some\n"
    .string "few men with me; neither told I any\l"
    .string "man what my God had put in my heart\l"
    .string "to do at Jerusalem: neither was\l"
    .string "there any beast with me, save the\l"
    .string "beast that I rode upon.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_13::
    .string "And I went out by night by the gate\n"
    .string "of the valley, even before the\l"
    .string "dragon well, and to the dung port,\l"
    .string "and viewed the walls of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "which were broken down, and the gates\l"
    .string "thereof were consumed with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_14::
    .string "Then I went on to the gate of the\n"
    .string "fountain, and to the king’s pool:\l"
    .string "but there was no place for the beast\l"
    .string "that was under me to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_15::
    .string "Then went I up in the night by the\n"
    .string "brook, and viewed the wall, and\l"
    .string "turned back, and entered by the gate\l"
    .string "of the valley, and so returned.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_16::
    .string "And the rulers knew not whither I\n"
    .string "went, or what I did; neither had I as\l"
    .string "yet told it to the Jews, nor to the\l"
    .string "priests, nor to the nobles, nor to\l"
    .string "the rulers, nor to the rest that did\l"
    .string "the work.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_17::
    .string "Then said I unto them, Ye see the\n"
    .string "distress that we are in, how\l"
    .string "Jerusalem lieth waste, and the\l"
    .string "gates thereof are burned with fire:\l"
    .string "come, and let us build up the wall\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, that we be no more a\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_18::
    .string "Then I told them of the hand of my\n"
    .string "God which was good upon me; as also\l"
    .string "the king’s words that he had spoken\l"
    .string "unto me. And they said, Let us rise\l"
    .string "up and build. So they strengthened\l"
    .string "their hands for this good work.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_19::
    .string "But when Sanballat the Horonite,\n"
    .string "and Tobiah the servant, the Ammonite,\l"
    .string "and Geshem the Arabian, heard it,\l"
    .string "they laughed us to scorn, and\l"
    .string "despised us, and said, What is this\l"
    .string "thing that ye do? will ye rebel\l"
    .string "against the king?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_2_20::
    .string "Then answered I them, and said unto\n"
    .string "them, The God of heaven, he will\l"
    .string "prosper us; therefore we his\l"
    .string "servants will arise and build: but\l"
    .string "ye have no portion, nor right, nor\l"
    .string "memorial, in Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_1::
    .string "Then Eliashib the high priest rose\n"
    .string "up with his brethren the priests,\l"
    .string "and they builded the sheep gate;\l"
    .string "they sanctified it, and set up the\l"
    .string "doors of it; even unto the tower of\l"
    .string "Meah they sanctified it, unto the\l"
    .string "tower of Hananeel.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_2::
    .string "And next unto him builded the men\n"
    .string "of Jericho. And next to them builded\l"
    .string "Zaccur the son of Imri.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_3::
    .string "But the fish gate did the sons of\n"
    .string "Hassenaah build, who also laid the\l"
    .string "beams thereof, and set up the doors\l"
    .string "thereof, the locks thereof, and the\l"
    .string "bars thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_4::
    .string "And next unto them repaired\n"
    .string "Meremoth the son of Urijah, the son\l"
    .string "of Koz. And next unto them repaired\l"
    .string "Meshullam the son of Berechiah, the\l"
    .string "son of Meshezabeel. And next unto\l"
    .string "them repaired Zadok the son of Baana.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_5::
    .string "And next unto them the Tekoites\n"
    .string "repaired; but their nobles put not\l"
    .string "their necks to the work of their LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_6::
    .string "Moreover the old gate repaired\n"
    .string "Jehoiada the son of Paseah, and\l"
    .string "Meshullam the son of Besodeiah;\l"
    .string "they laid the beams thereof, and set\l"
    .string "up the doors thereof, and the locks\l"
    .string "thereof, and the bars thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_7::
    .string "And next unto them repaired\n"
    .string "Melatiah the Gibeonite, and Jadon\l"
    .string "the Meronothite, the men of Gibeon,\l"
    .string "and of Mizpah, unto the throne of the\l"
    .string "governor on this side the river.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_8::
    .string "Next unto him repaired Uzziel the\n"
    .string "son of Harhaiah, of the goldsmiths.\l"
    .string "Next unto him also repaired\l"
    .string "Hananiah the son of one of the\l"
    .string "apothecaries, and they fortified\l"
    .string "Jerusalem unto the broad wall.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_9::
    .string "And next unto them repaired\n"
    .string "Rephaiah the son of Hur, the ruler\l"
    .string "of the half part of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_10::
    .string "And next unto them repaired Jedaiah\n"
    .string "the son of Harumaph, even over\l"
    .string "against his house. And next unto him\l"
    .string "repaired Hattush the son of\l"
    .string "Hashabniah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_11::
    .string "Malchijah the son of Harim, and\n"
    .string "Hashub the son of Pahathmoab,\l"
    .string "repaired the other piece, and the\l"
    .string "tower of the furnaces.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_12::
    .string "And next unto him repaired\n"
    .string "Shallum the son of Halohesh, the\l"
    .string "ruler of the half part of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, he and his daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_13::
    .string "The valley gate repaired Hanun,\n"
    .string "and the inhabitants of Zanoah; they\l"
    .string "built it, and set up the doors\l"
    .string "thereof, the locks thereof, and the\l"
    .string "bars thereof, and a thousand cubits\l"
    .string "on the wall unto the dung gate.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_14::
    .string "But the dung gate repaired\n"
    .string "Malchiah the son of Rechab, the\l"
    .string "ruler of part of Bethhaccerem; he\l"
    .string "built it, and set up the doors\l"
    .string "thereof, the locks thereof, and the\l"
    .string "bars thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_15::
    .string "But the gate of the fountain\n"
    .string "repaired Shallun the son of\l"
    .string "Colhozeh, the ruler of part of\l"
    .string "Mizpah; he built it, and covered it,\l"
    .string "and set up the doors thereof, the\l"
    .string "locks thereof, and the bars thereof,\l"
    .string "and the wall of the pool of Siloah\l"
    .string "by the king’s garden, and unto the\l"
    .string "stairs that go down from the city of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_16::
    .string "After him repaired Nehemiah the son\n"
    .string "of Azbuk, the ruler of the half\l"
    .string "part of Bethzur, unto the place over\l"
    .string "against the sepulchres of David,\l"
    .string "and to the pool that was made, and\l"
    .string "unto the house of the mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_17::
    .string "After him repaired the Levites,\n"
    .string "Rehum the son of Bani. Next unto him\l"
    .string "repaired Hashabiah, the ruler of\l"
    .string "the half part of Keilah, in his\l"
    .string "part.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_18::
    .string "After him repaired their brethren,\n"
    .string "Bavai the son of Henadad, the ruler\l"
    .string "of the half part of Keilah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_19::
    .string "And next to him repaired Ezer the\n"
    .string "son of Jeshua, the ruler of Mizpah,\l"
    .string "another piece over against the going\l"
    .string "up to the armoury at the turning of\l"
    .string "the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_20::
    .string "After him Baruch the son of Zabbai\n"
    .string "earnestly repaired the other\l"
    .string "piece, from the turning of the wall\l"
    .string "unto the door of the house of\l"
    .string "Eliashib the high priest.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_21::
    .string "After him repaired Meremoth the son\n"
    .string "of Urijah the son of Koz another\l"
    .string "piece, from the door of the house of\l"
    .string "Eliashib even to the end of the\l"
    .string "house of Eliashib.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_22::
    .string "And after him repaired the\n"
    .string "priests, the men of the plain.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_23::
    .string "After him repaired Benjamin and\n"
    .string "Hashub over against their house.\l"
    .string "After him repaired Azariah the son\l"
    .string "of Maaseiah the son of Ananiah by his\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_24::
    .string "After him repaired Binnui the son\n"
    .string "of Henadad another piece, from the\l"
    .string "house of Azariah unto the turning of\l"
    .string "the wall, even unto the corner.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_25::
    .string "Palal the son of Uzai, over against\n"
    .string "the turning of the wall, and the\l"
    .string "tower which lieth out from the\l"
    .string "king’s high house, that was by the\l"
    .string "court of the prison. After him\l"
    .string "Pedaiah the son of Parosh.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_26::
    .string "Moreover the Nethinims dwelt in\n"
    .string "Ophel, unto the place over against\l"
    .string "the water gate toward the east, and\l"
    .string "the tower that lieth out.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_27::
    .string "After them the Tekoites repaired\n"
    .string "another piece, over against the\l"
    .string "great tower that lieth out, even\l"
    .string "unto the wall of Ophel.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_28::
    .string "From above the horse gate repaired\n"
    .string "the priests, every one over against\l"
    .string "his house.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_29::
    .string "After them repaired Zadok the son\n"
    .string "of Immer over against his house.\l"
    .string "After him repaired also Shemaiah\l"
    .string "the son of Shechaniah, the keeper of\l"
    .string "the east gate.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_30::
    .string "After him repaired Hananiah the son\n"
    .string "of Shelemiah, and Hanun the sixth\l"
    .string "son of Zalaph, another piece. After\l"
    .string "him repaired Meshullam the son of\l"
    .string "Berechiah over against his chamber.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_31::
    .string "After him repaired Malchiah the\n"
    .string "goldsmith’s son unto the place of\l"
    .string "the Nethinims, and of the merchants,\l"
    .string "over against the gate Miphkad, and\l"
    .string "to the going up of the corner.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_3_32::
    .string "And between the going up of the\n"
    .string "corner unto the sheep gate repaired\l"
    .string "the goldsmiths and the merchants.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_1::
    .string "But it came to pass, that when\n"
    .string "Sanballat heard that we builded\l"
    .string "the wall, he was wroth, and took\l"
    .string "great indignation, and mocked the\l"
    .string "Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_2::
    .string "And he spake before his brethren\n"
    .string "and the army of Samaria, and said,\l"
    .string "What do these feeble Jews? will\l"
    .string "they fortify themselves? will they\l"
    .string "sacrifice? will they make an end in\l"
    .string "a day? will they revive the stones\l"
    .string "out of the heaps of the rubbish\l"
    .string "which are burned?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_3::
    .string "Now Tobiah the Ammonite was by him,\n"
    .string "and he said, Even that which they\l"
    .string "build, if a fox go up, he shall\l"
    .string "even break down their stone wall$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_4::
    .string "Hear, O our God; for we are\n"
    .string "despised: and turn their reproach\l"
    .string "upon their own head, and give them\l"
    .string "for a prey in the land of\l"
    .string "captivity:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_5::
    .string "And cover not their iniquity, and\n"
    .string "let not their sin be blotted out\l"
    .string "from before thee: for they have\l"
    .string "provoked thee to anger before the\l"
    .string "builders$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_6::
    .string "So built we the wall; and all the\n"
    .string "wall was joined together unto the\l"
    .string "half thereof: for the people had a\l"
    .string "mind to work.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_7::
    .string "But it came to pass, that when\n"
    .string "Sanballat, and Tobiah, and the\l"
    .string "Arabians, and the Ammonites, and the\l"
    .string "Ashdodites, heard that the walls of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem were made up, and that the\l"
    .string "breaches began to be stopped, then\l"
    .string "they were very wroth,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_8::
    .string "And conspired all of them\n"
    .string "together to come and to fight against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and to hinder it$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_9::
    .string "Nevertheless we made our prayer\n"
    .string "unto our God, and set a watch against\l"
    .string "them day and night, because of them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_10::
    .string "And Judah said, The strength of the\n"
    .string "bearers of burdens is decayed, and\l"
    .string "there is much rubbish; so that we are\l"
    .string "not able to build the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_11::
    .string "And our adversaries said, They\n"
    .string "shall not know, neither see, till\l"
    .string "we come in the midst among them, and\l"
    .string "slay them, and cause the work to\l"
    .string "cease.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_12::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when the\n"
    .string "Jews which dwelt by them came, they\l"
    .string "said unto us ten times, From all\l"
    .string "places whence ye shall return unto\l"
    .string "us they will be upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_13::
    .string "Therefore set I in the lower\n"
    .string "places behind the wall, and on the\l"
    .string "higher places, I even set the\l"
    .string "people after their families with\l"
    .string "their swords, their spears, and\l"
    .string "their bows.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_14::
    .string "And I looked, and rose up, and said\n"
    .string "unto the nobles, and to the rulers,\l"
    .string "and to the rest of the people, Be\l"
    .string "not ye afraid of them: remember the\l"
    .string "LORD, which is great and terrible,\l"
    .string "and fight for your brethren, your\l"
    .string "sons, and your daughters, your wives,\l"
    .string "and your houses.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, when our\n"
    .string "enemies heard that it was known unto\l"
    .string "us, and God had brought their\l"
    .string "counsel to nought, that we returned\l"
    .string "all of us to the wall, every one\l"
    .string "unto his work.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_16::
    .string "And it came to pass from that time\n"
    .string "forth, that the half of my servants\l"
    .string "wrought in the work, and the other\l"
    .string "half of them held both the spears,\l"
    .string "the shields, and the bows, and the\l"
    .string "habergeons; and the rulers were\l"
    .string "behind all the house of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_17::
    .string "They which builded on the wall,\n"
    .string "and they that bare burdens, with\l"
    .string "those that laded, every one with one\l"
    .string "of his hands wrought in the work, and\l"
    .string "with the other hand held a weapon.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_18::
    .string "For the builders, every one had his\n"
    .string "sword girded by his side, and so\l"
    .string "builded. And he that sounded the\l"
    .string "trumpet was by me.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_19::
    .string "And I said unto the nobles, and to\n"
    .string "the rulers, and to the rest of the\l"
    .string "people, The work is great and\l"
    .string "large, and we are separated upon the\l"
    .string "wall, one far from another.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_20::
    .string "In what place therefore ye hear\n"
    .string "the sound of the trumpet, resort ye\l"
    .string "thither unto us: our God shall fight\l"
    .string "for us.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_21::
    .string "So we laboured in the work: and\n"
    .string "half of them held the spears from\l"
    .string "the rising of the morning till the\l"
    .string "stars appeared.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_22::
    .string "Likewise at the same time said I\n"
    .string "unto the people, Let every one with\l"
    .string "his servant lodge within Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "that in the night they may be a guard\l"
    .string "to us, and labour on the day.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_4_23::
    .string "So neither I, nor my brethren, nor\n"
    .string "my servants, nor the men of the guard\l"
    .string "which followed me, none of us put\l"
    .string "off our clothes, saving that every\l"
    .string "one put them off for washing.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_1::
    .string "And there was a great cry of the\n"
    .string "people and of their wives against\l"
    .string "their brethren the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_2::
    .string "For there were that said, We, our\n"
    .string "sons, and our daughters, are many:\l"
    .string "therefore we take up corn for them,\l"
    .string "that we may eat, and live.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_3::
    .string "Some also there were that said, We\n"
    .string "have mortgaged our lands, vineyards,\l"
    .string "and houses, that we might buy corn,\l"
    .string "because of the dearth.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_4::
    .string "There were also that said, We have\n"
    .string "borrowed money for the king’s\l"
    .string "tribute, and that upon our lands and\l"
    .string "vineyards.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_5::
    .string "Yet now our flesh is as the flesh\n"
    .string "of our brethren, our children as\l"
    .string "their children: and, lo, we bring\l"
    .string "into bondage our sons and our\l"
    .string "daughters to be servants, and some of\l"
    .string "our daughters are brought unto\l"
    .string "bondage already: neither is it in\l"
    .string "our power to redeem them; for other\l"
    .string "men have our lands and vineyards.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_6::
    .string "And I was very angry when I heard\n"
    .string "their cry and these words.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_7::
    .string "Then I consulted with myself, and I\n"
    .string "rebuked the nobles, and the rulers,\l"
    .string "and said unto them, Ye exact usury,\l"
    .string "every one of his brother. And I set a\l"
    .string "great assembly against them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_8::
    .string "And I said unto them, We after our\n"
    .string "ability have redeemed our brethren\l"
    .string "the Jews, which were sold unto the\l"
    .string "heathen; and will ye even sell\l"
    .string "your brethren? or shall they be\l"
    .string "sold unto us? Then held they their\l"
    .string "peace, and found nothing to answer.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_9::
    .string "Also I said, It is not good that ye\n"
    .string "do: ought ye not to walk in the fear\l"
    .string "of our God because of the reproach\l"
    .string "of the heathen our enemies?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_10::
    .string "I likewise, and my brethren, and my\n"
    .string "servants, might exact of them money\l"
    .string "and corn: I pray you, let us leave\l"
    .string "off this usury$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_11::
    .string "Restore, I pray you, to them, even\n"
    .string "this day, their lands, their\l"
    .string "vineyards, their oliveyards, and\l"
    .string "their houses, also the hundredth\l"
    .string "part of the money, and of the corn,\l"
    .string "the wine, and the oil, that ye exact\l"
    .string "of them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_12::
    .string "Then said they, We will restore\n"
    .string "them, and will require nothing of\l"
    .string "them; so will we do as thou sayest.\l"
    .string "Then I called the priests, and took\l"
    .string "an oath of them, that they should do\l"
    .string "according to this promise.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_13::
    .string "Also I shook my lap, and said, So\n"
    .string "God shake out every man from his\l"
    .string "house, and from his labour, that\l"
    .string "performeth not this promise, even\l"
    .string "thus be he shaken out, and emptied.\l"
    .string "And all the congregation said,\l"
    .string "Amen, and praised the LORD. And the\l"
    .string "people did according to this\l"
    .string "promise.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_14::
    .string "Moreover from the time that I was\n"
    .string "appointed to be their governor in\l"
    .string "the land of Judah, from the\l"
    .string "twentieth year even unto the two and\l"
    .string "thirtieth year of Artaxerxes the\l"
    .string "king, that is, twelve years, I and my\l"
    .string "brethren have not eaten the bread of\l"
    .string "the governor.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_15::
    .string "But the former governors that had\n"
    .string "been before me were chargeable unto\l"
    .string "the people, and had taken of them\l"
    .string "bread and wine, beside forty shekels\l"
    .string "of silver; yea, even their servants\l"
    .string "bare rule over the people: but so\l"
    .string "did not I, because of the fear of God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_16::
    .string "Yea, also I continued in the work of\n"
    .string "this wall, neither bought we any\l"
    .string "land: and all my servants were\l"
    .string "gathered thither unto the work.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_17::
    .string "Moreover there were at my table an\n"
    .string "hundred and fifty of the Jews and\l"
    .string "rulers, beside those that came unto\l"
    .string "us from among the heathen that are\l"
    .string "about us.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_18::
    .string "Now that which was prepared for me\n"
    .string "daily was one ox and six choice\l"
    .string "sheep; also fowls were prepared\l"
    .string "for me, and once in ten days store of\l"
    .string "all sorts of wine: yet for all this\l"
    .string "required not I the bread of the\l"
    .string "governor, because the bondage was\l"
    .string "heavy upon this people.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_5_19::
    .string "Think upon me, my God, for good,\n"
    .string "according to all that I have done\l"
    .string "for this people.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass when\n"
    .string "Sanballat, and Tobiah, and Geshem\l"
    .string "the Arabian, and the rest of our\l"
    .string "enemies, heard that I had builded\l"
    .string "the wall, and that there was no\l"
    .string "breach left therein; (though at that\l"
    .string "time I had not set up the doors upon\l"
    .string "the gates;)"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_2::
    .string "That Sanballat and Geshem sent\n"
    .string "unto me, saying, Come, let us meet\l"
    .string "together in some one of the\l"
    .string "villages in the plain of Ono. But\l"
    .string "they thought to do me mischief$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_3::
    .string "And I sent messengers unto them,\n"
    .string "saying, I am doing a great work, so\l"
    .string "that I cannot come down: why should\l"
    .string "the work cease, whilst I leave it,\l"
    .string "and come down to you?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_4::
    .string "Yet they sent unto me four times\n"
    .string "after this sort; and I answered them\l"
    .string "after the same manner$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_5::
    .string "Then sent Sanballat his servant\n"
    .string "unto me in like manner the fifth\l"
    .string "time with an open letter in his\l"
    .string "hand;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_6::
    .string "Wherein was written, It is reported\n"
    .string "among the heathen, and Gashmu saith\l"
    .string "it, that thou and the Jews think to\l"
    .string "rebel: for which cause thou\l"
    .string "buildest the wall, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "be their king, according to these\l"
    .string "words$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_7::
    .string "And thou hast also appointed\n"
    .string "prophets to preach of thee at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, saying, There is a king\l"
    .string "in Judah: and now shall it be\l"
    .string "reported to the king according to\l"
    .string "these words. Come now therefore, and\l"
    .string "let us take counsel together.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_8::
    .string "Then I sent unto him, saying, There\n"
    .string "are no such things done as thou\l"
    .string "sayest, but thou feignest them out of\l"
    .string "thine own heart.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_9::
    .string "For they all made us afraid,\n"
    .string "saying, Their hands shall be\l"
    .string "weakened from the work, that it be\l"
    .string "not done. Now therefore, O God,\l"
    .string "strengthen my hands.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_10::
    .string "Afterward I came unto the house of\n"
    .string "Shemaiah the son of Delaiah the son\l"
    .string "of Mehetabeel, who was shut up; and\l"
    .string "he said, Let us meet together in the\l"
    .string "house of God, within the temple, and\l"
    .string "let us shut the doors of the temple:\l"
    .string "for they will come to slay thee;\l"
    .string "yea, in the night will they come to\l"
    .string "slay thee.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_11::
    .string "And I said, Should such a man as I\n"
    .string "flee? and who is there, that, being\l"
    .string "as I am, would go into the temple to\l"
    .string "save his life? I will not go in.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_12::
    .string "And, lo, I perceived that God had\n"
    .string "not sent him; but that he pronounced\l"
    .string "this prophecy against me: for\l"
    .string "Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_13::
    .string "Therefore was he hired, that I\n"
    .string "should be afraid, and do so, and sin,\l"
    .string "and that they might have matter for\l"
    .string "an evil report, that they might\l"
    .string "reproach me.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_14::
    .string "My God, think thou upon Tobiah and\n"
    .string "Sanballat according to these their\l"
    .string "works, and on the prophetess\l"
    .string "Noadiah, and the rest of the\l"
    .string "prophets, that would have put me in\l"
    .string "fear.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_15::
    .string "So the wall was finished in the\n"
    .string "twenty and fifth day of the month\l"
    .string "Elul, in fifty and two days.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when all\n"
    .string "our enemies heard thereof, and all\l"
    .string "the heathen that were about us saw\l"
    .string "these things, they were much cast\l"
    .string "down in their own eyes: for they\l"
    .string "perceived that this work was wrought\l"
    .string "of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_17::
    .string "Moreover in those days the nobles\n"
    .string "of Judah sent many letters unto\l"
    .string "Tobiah, and the letters of Tobiah\l"
    .string "came unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_18::
    .string "For there were many in Judah sworn\n"
    .string "unto him, because he was the son in\l"
    .string "law of Shechaniah the son of Arah;\l"
    .string "and his son Johanan had taken the\l"
    .string "daughter of Meshullam the son of\l"
    .string "Berechiah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_6_19::
    .string "Also they reported his good deeds\n"
    .string "before me, and uttered my words to him\l"
    .string " And Tobiah sent letters to put me\l"
    .string "in fear.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when the wall\n"
    .string "was built, and I had set up the\l"
    .string "doors, and the porters and the\l"
    .string "singers and the Levites were\l"
    .string "appointed,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_2::
    .string "That I gave my brother Hanani, and\n"
    .string "Hananiah the ruler of the palace,\l"
    .string "charge over Jerusalem: for he was a\l"
    .string "faithful man, and feared God above\l"
    .string "many$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_3::
    .string "And I said unto them, Let not the\n"
    .string "gates of Jerusalem be opened until\l"
    .string "the sun be hot; and while they stand\l"
    .string "by, let them shut the doors, and bar\l"
    .string "them: and appoint watches of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, every one\l"
    .string "in his watch, and every one to be over\l"
    .string "against his house.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_4::
    .string "Now the city was large and great:\n"
    .string "but the people were few therein,\l"
    .string "and the houses were not builded.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_5::
    .string "And my God put into mine heart to\n"
    .string "gather together the nobles, and the\l"
    .string "rulers, and the people, that they\l"
    .string "might be reckoned by genealogy. And\l"
    .string "I found a register of the genealogy\l"
    .string "of them which came up at the first,\l"
    .string "and found written therein,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_6::
    .string "These are the children of the\n"
    .string "province, that went up out of the\l"
    .string "captivity, of those that had been\l"
    .string "carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon had carried\l"
    .string "away, and came again to Jerusalem\l"
    .string "and to Judah, every one unto his\l"
    .string "city;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_7::
    .string "Who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua,\n"
    .string "Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah,\l"
    .string "Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan,\l"
    .string "Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, Baanah.\l"
    .string "The number, I say, of the men of the\l"
    .string "people of Israel was this;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_8::
    .string "The children of Parosh, two\n"
    .string "thousand an hundred seventy and two$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_9::
    .string "The children of Shephatiah, three\n"
    .string "hundred seventy and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_10::
    .string "The children of Arah, six hundred\n"
    .string "fifty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_11::
    .string "The children of Pahathmoab, of the\n"
    .string "children of Jeshua and Joab, two\l"
    .string "thousand and eight hundred and\l"
    .string "eighteen.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_12::
    .string "The children of Elam, a thousand\n"
    .string "two hundred fifty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_13::
    .string "The children of Zattu, eight\n"
    .string "hundred forty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_14::
    .string "The children of Zaccai, seven\n"
    .string "hundred and threescore.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_15::
    .string "The children of Binnui, six hundred\n"
    .string "forty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_16::
    .string "The children of Bebai, six hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_17::
    .string "The children of Azgad, two thousand\n"
    .string "three hundred twenty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_18::
    .string "The children of Adonikam, six\n"
    .string "hundred threescore and seven.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_19::
    .string "The children of Bigvai, two\n"
    .string "thousand threescore and seven.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_20::
    .string "The children of Adin, six hundred\n"
    .string "fifty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_21::
    .string "The children of Ater of Hezekiah,\n"
    .string "ninety and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_22::
    .string "The children of Hashum, three\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_23::
    .string "The children of Bezai, three\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_24::
    .string "The children of Hariph, an hundred\n"
    .string "and twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_25::
    .string "The children of Gibeon, ninety and\n"
    .string "five.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_26::
    .string "The men of Bethlehem and Netophah,\n"
    .string "an hundred fourscore and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_27::
    .string "The men of Anathoth, an hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_28::
    .string "The men of Bethazmaveth, forty and\n"
    .string "two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_29::
    .string "The men of Kirjathjearim,\n"
    .string "Chephirah, and Beeroth, seven\l"
    .string "hundred forty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_30::
    .string "The men of Ramah and Gaba, six\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and one.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_31::
    .string "The men of Michmas, an hundred and\n"
    .string "twenty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_32::
    .string "The men of Bethel and Ai, an hundred\n"
    .string "twenty and three.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_33::
    .string "The men of the other Nebo, fifty and\n"
    .string "two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_34::
    .string "The children of the other Elam, a\n"
    .string "thousand two hundred fifty and four.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_35::
    .string "The children of Harim, three\n"
    .string "hundred and twenty.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_36::
    .string "The children of Jericho, three\n"
    .string "hundred forty and five.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_37::
    .string "The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono,\n"
    .string "seven hundred twenty and one.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_38::
    .string "The children of Senaah, three\n"
    .string "thousand nine hundred and thirty.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_39::
    .string "The priests: the children of\n"
    .string "Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, nine\l"
    .string "hundred seventy and three.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_40::
    .string "The children of Immer, a thousand\n"
    .string "fifty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_41::
    .string "The children of Pashur, a thousand\n"
    .string "two hundred forty and seven.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_42::
    .string "The children of Harim, a thousand\n"
    .string "and seventeen.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_43::
    .string "The Levites: the children of\n"
    .string "Jeshua, of Kadmiel, and of the\l"
    .string "children of Hodevah, seventy and\l"
    .string "four.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_44::
    .string "The singers: the children of\n"
    .string "Asaph, an hundred forty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_45::
    .string "The porters: the children of\n"
    .string "Shallum, the children of Ater, the\l"
    .string "children of Talmon, the children of\l"
    .string "Akkub, the children of Hatita, the\l"
    .string "children of Shobai, an hundred\l"
    .string "thirty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_46::
    .string "The Nethinims: the children of\n"
    .string "Ziha, the children of Hashupha, the\l"
    .string "children of Tabbaoth,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_47::
    .string "The children of Keros, the\n"
    .string "children of Sia, the children of\l"
    .string "Padon,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_48::
    .string "The children of Lebana, the\n"
    .string "children of Hagaba, the children of\l"
    .string "Shalmai,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_49::
    .string "The children of Hanan, the\n"
    .string "children of Giddel, the children of\l"
    .string "Gahar,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_50::
    .string "The children of Reaiah, the\n"
    .string "children of Rezin, the children of\l"
    .string "Nekoda,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_51::
    .string "The children of Gazzam, the\n"
    .string "children of Uzza, the children of\l"
    .string "Phaseah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_52::
    .string "The children of Besai, the\n"
    .string "children of Meunim, the children of\l"
    .string "Nephishesim,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_53::
    .string "The children of Bakbuk, the\n"
    .string "children of Hakupha, the children\l"
    .string "of Harhur,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_54::
    .string "The children of Bazlith, the\n"
    .string "children of Mehida, the children of\l"
    .string "Harsha,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_55::
    .string "The children of Barkos, the\n"
    .string "children of Sisera, the children of\l"
    .string "Tamah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_56::
    .string "The children of Neziah, the\n"
    .string "children of Hatipha$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_57::
    .string "The children of Solomon’s\n"
    .string "servants: the children of Sotai, the\l"
    .string "children of Sophereth, the\l"
    .string "children of Perida,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_58::
    .string "The children of Jaala, the\n"
    .string "children of Darkon, the children of\l"
    .string "Giddel,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_59::
    .string "The children of Shephatiah, the\n"
    .string "children of Hattil, the children of\l"
    .string "Pochereth of Zebaim, the children of\l"
    .string "Amon$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_60::
    .string "All the Nethinims, and the\n"
    .string "children of Solomon’s servants,\l"
    .string "were three hundred ninety and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_61::
    .string "And these were they which went up\n"
    .string "also from Telmelah, Telharesha,\l"
    .string "Cherub, Addon, and Immer: but they\l"
    .string "could not shew their father’s house,\l"
    .string "nor their seed, whether they were of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_62::
    .string "The children of Delaiah, the\n"
    .string "children of Tobiah, the children of\l"
    .string "Nekoda, six hundred forty and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_63::
    .string "And of the priests: the children of\n"
    .string "Habaiah, the children of Koz, the\l"
    .string "children of Barzillai, which took\l"
    .string "one of the daughters of Barzillai\l"
    .string "the Gileadite to wife, and was\l"
    .string "called after their name.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_64::
    .string "These sought their register among\n"
    .string "those that were reckoned by\l"
    .string "genealogy, but it was not found:\l"
    .string "therefore were they, as polluted,\l"
    .string "put from the priesthood.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_65::
    .string "And the Tirshatha said unto them,\n"
    .string "that they should not eat of the most\l"
    .string "holy things, till there stood up a\l"
    .string "priest with Urim and Thummim.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_66::
    .string "The whole congregation together\n"
    .string "was forty and two thousand three\l"
    .string "hundred and threescore,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_67::
    .string "Beside their manservants and their\n"
    .string "maidservants, of whom there were\l"
    .string "seven thousand three hundred thirty\l"
    .string "and seven: and they had two hundred\l"
    .string "forty and five singing men and\l"
    .string "singing women$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_68::
    .string "Their horses, seven hundred thirty\n"
    .string "and six: their mules, two hundred\l"
    .string "forty and five:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_69::
    .string "Their camels, four hundred thirty\n"
    .string "and five: six thousand seven hundred\l"
    .string "and twenty asses$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_70::
    .string "And some of the chief of the fathers\n"
    .string "gave unto the work. The Tirshatha\l"
    .string "gave to the treasure a thousand drams\l"
    .string "of gold, fifty basons, five hundred\l"
    .string "and thirty priests’ garments.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_71::
    .string "And some of the chief of the fathers\n"
    .string "gave to the treasure of the work\l"
    .string "twenty thousand drams of gold, and\l"
    .string "two thousand and two hundred pound\l"
    .string "of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_72::
    .string "And that which the rest of the\n"
    .string "people gave was twenty thousand\l"
    .string "drams of gold, and two thousand\l"
    .string "pound of silver, and threescore and\l"
    .string "seven priests’ garments.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_7_73::
    .string "So the priests, and the Levites,\n"
    .string "and the porters, and the singers,\l"
    .string "and some of the people, and the\l"
    .string "Nethinims, and all Israel, dwelt\l"
    .string "in their cities; and when the seventh\l"
    .string "month came, the children of Israel\l"
    .string "were in their cities.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_1::
    .string "And all the people gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together as one man into\l"
    .string "the street that was before the water\l"
    .string "gate; and they spake unto Ezra the\l"
    .string "scribe to bring the book of the law\l"
    .string "of Moses, which the LORD had\l"
    .string "commanded to Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_2::
    .string "And Ezra the priest brought the\n"
    .string "law before the congregation both of\l"
    .string "men and women, and all that could\l"
    .string "hear with understanding, upon the\l"
    .string "first day of the seventh month.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_3::
    .string "And he read therein before the\n"
    .string "street that was before the water gate\l"
    .string "from the morning until midday,\l"
    .string "before the men and the women, and\l"
    .string "those that could understand; and the\l"
    .string "ears of all the people were\l"
    .string "attentive unto the book of the law.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_4::
    .string "And Ezra the scribe stood upon a\n"
    .string "pulpit of wood, which they had made\l"
    .string "for the purpose; and beside him\l"
    .string "stood Mattithiah, and Shema, and\l"
    .string "Anaiah, and Urijah, and Hilkiah, and\l"
    .string "Maaseiah, on his right hand; and on\l"
    .string "his left hand, Pedaiah, and Mishael,\l"
    .string "and Malchiah, and Hashum, and\l"
    .string "Hashbadana, Zechariah, and\l"
    .string "Meshullam.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_5::
    .string "And Ezra opened the book in the\n"
    .string "sight of all the people; (for he\l"
    .string "was above all the people;) and\l"
    .string "when he opened it, all the people\l"
    .string "stood up:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_6::
    .string "And Ezra blessed the LORD, the\n"
    .string "great God. And all the people\l"
    .string "answered, Amen, Amen, with lifting\l"
    .string "up their hands: and they bowed their\l"
    .string "heads, and worshipped the LORD with\l"
    .string "their faces to the ground$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_7::
    .string "Also Jeshua, and Bani, and\n"
    .string "Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai,\l"
    .string "Hodijah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah,\l"
    .string "Jozabad, Hanan, Pelaiah, and the\l"
    .string "Levites, caused the people to\l"
    .string "understand the law: and the people\l"
    .string "stood in their place.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_8::
    .string "So they read in the book in the law\n"
    .string "of God distinctly, and gave the\l"
    .string "sense, and caused them to understand\l"
    .string "the reading.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_9::
    .string "And Nehemiah, which is the\n"
    .string "Tirshatha, and Ezra the priest the\l"
    .string "scribe, and the Levites that taught\l"
    .string "the people, said unto all the\l"
    .string "people, This day is holy unto the\l"
    .string "LORD your God; mourn not, nor weep.\l"
    .string "For all the people wept, when\l"
    .string "they heard the words of the law.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_10::
    .string "Then he said unto them, Go your way,\n"
    .string "eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and\l"
    .string "send portions unto them for whom\l"
    .string "nothing is prepared: for this day is\l"
    .string "holy unto our LORD: neither be ye\l"
    .string "sorry; for the joy of the LORD is your\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_11::
    .string "So the Levites stilled all the\n"
    .string "people, saying, Hold your peace,\l"
    .string "for the day is holy; neither be ye\l"
    .string "grieved.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_12::
    .string "And all the people went their\n"
    .string "way to eat, and to drink, and to send\l"
    .string "portions, and to make great mirth,\l"
    .string "because they had understood the\l"
    .string "words that were declared unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_13::
    .string "And on the second day were gathered\n"
    .string "together the chief of the fathers of\l"
    .string "all the people, the priests, and\l"
    .string "the Levites, unto Ezra the scribe,\l"
    .string "even to understand the words of the\l"
    .string "law.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_14::
    .string "And they found written in the law\n"
    .string "which the LORD had commanded by\l"
    .string "Moses, that the children of Israel\l"
    .string "should dwell in booths in the feast\l"
    .string "of the seventh month:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_15::
    .string "And that they should publish and\n"
    .string "proclaim in all their cities, and\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem, saying, Go forth unto\l"
    .string "the mount, and fetch olive branches,\l"
    .string "and pine branches, and myrtle\l"
    .string "branches, and palm branches, and\l"
    .string "branches of thick trees, to make\l"
    .string "booths, as it is written$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_16::
    .string "So the people went forth, and\n"
    .string "brought them, and made themselves\l"
    .string "booths, every one upon the roof of\l"
    .string "his house, and in their courts, and\l"
    .string "in the courts of the house of God, and\l"
    .string "in the street of the water gate, and\l"
    .string "in the street of the gate of Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_17::
    .string "And all the congregation of them\n"
    .string "that were come again out of the\l"
    .string "captivity made booths, and sat under\l"
    .string "the booths: for since the days of\l"
    .string "Jeshua the son of Nun unto that day\l"
    .string "had not the children of Israel done\l"
    .string "so. And there was very great\l"
    .string "gladness.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_8_18::
    .string "Also day by day, from the first day\n"
    .string "unto the last day, he read in the\l"
    .string "book of the law of God. And they\l"
    .string "kept the feast seven days; and on the\l"
    .string "eighth day was a solemn assembly,\l"
    .string "according unto the manner.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_1::
    .string "Now in the twenty and fourth day of\n"
    .string "this month the children of Israel\l"
    .string "were assembled with fasting, and\l"
    .string "with sackclothes, and earth upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_2::
    .string "And the seed of Israel separated\n"
    .string "themselves from all strangers, and\l"
    .string "stood and confessed their sins, and\l"
    .string "the iniquities of their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_3::
    .string "And they stood up in their place,\n"
    .string "and read in the book of the law of\l"
    .string "the LORD their God one fourth part\l"
    .string "of the day; and another fourth part\l"
    .string "they confessed, and worshipped the\l"
    .string "LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_4::
    .string "Then stood up upon the stairs, of\n"
    .string "the Levites, Jeshua, and Bani,\l"
    .string "Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni,\l"
    .string "Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani, and\l"
    .string "cried with a loud voice unto the\l"
    .string "LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_5::
    .string "Then the Levites, Jeshua, and\n"
    .string "Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabniah,\l"
    .string "Sherebiah, Hodijah, Shebaniah, and\l"
    .string "Pethahiah, said, Stand up and bless\l"
    .string "the LORD your God for ever and ever:\l"
    .string "and blessed be thy glorious name,\l"
    .string "which is exalted above all\l"
    .string "blessing and praise.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_6::
    .string "Thou, even thou, art LORD alone;\n"
    .string "thou hast made heaven, the heaven of\l"
    .string "heavens, with all their host, the\l"
    .string "earth, and all things that are\l"
    .string "therein, the seas, and all that is\l"
    .string "therein, and thou preservest them\l"
    .string "all; and the host of heaven\l"
    .string "worshippeth thee.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_7::
    .string "Thou art the LORD the God, who didst\n"
    .string "choose Abram, and broughtest him\l"
    .string "forth out of Ur of the Chaldees, and\l"
    .string "gavest him the name of Abraham;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_8::
    .string "And foundest his heart faithful\n"
    .string "before thee, and madest a covenant\l"
    .string "with him to give the land of the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, the Hittites, the\l"
    .string "Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the\l"
    .string "Jebusites, and the Girgashites, to\l"
    .string "give it, I say, to his seed, and hast\l"
    .string "performed thy words; for thou art\l"
    .string "righteous:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_9::
    .string "And didst see the affliction of our\n"
    .string "fathers in Egypt, and heardest their\l"
    .string "cry by the Red sea;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_10::
    .string "And shewedst signs and wonders upon\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, and on all his servants,\l"
    .string "and on all the people of his\l"
    .string "land: for thou knewest that they\l"
    .string "dealt proudly against them. So\l"
    .string "didst thou get thee a name, as it is\l"
    .string "this day$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_11::
    .string "And thou didst divide the sea before\n"
    .string "them, so that they went through the\l"
    .string "midst of the sea on the dry land; and\l"
    .string "their persecutors thou threwest\l"
    .string "into the deeps, as a stone into the\l"
    .string "mighty waters.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_12::
    .string "Moreover thou leddest them in the\n"
    .string "day by a cloudy pillar; and in the\l"
    .string "night by a pillar of fire, to give\l"
    .string "them light in the way wherein they\l"
    .string "should go.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_13::
    .string "Thou camest down also upon mount\n"
    .string "Sinai, and spakest with them from\l"
    .string "heaven, and gavest them right\l"
    .string "judgments, and true laws, good\l"
    .string "statutes and commandments:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_14::
    .string "And madest known unto them thy holy\n"
    .string "sabbath, and commandedst them\l"
    .string "precepts, statutes, and laws, by the\l"
    .string "hand of Moses thy servant:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_15::
    .string "And gavest them bread from heaven\n"
    .string "for their hunger, and broughtest\l"
    .string "forth water for them out of the rock\l"
    .string "for their thirst, and promisedst\l"
    .string "them that they should go in to\l"
    .string "possess the land which thou hadst\l"
    .string "sworn to give them$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_16::
    .string "But they and our fathers dealt\n"
    .string "proudly, and hardened their necks,\l"
    .string "and hearkened not to thy\l"
    .string "commandments,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_17::
    .string "And refused to obey, neither were\n"
    .string "mindful of thy wonders that thou\l"
    .string "didst among them; but hardened their\l"
    .string "necks, and in their rebellion\l"
    .string "appointed a captain to return to\l"
    .string "their bondage: but thou art a God\l"
    .string "ready to pardon, gracious and\l"
    .string "merciful, slow to anger, and of\l"
    .string "great kindness, and forsookest them\l"
    .string "not$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_18::
    .string "Yea, when they had made them a\n"
    .string "molten calf, and said, This is thy\l"
    .string "God that brought thee up out of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and had wrought great\l"
    .string "provocations;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_19::
    .string "Yet thou in thy manifold mercies\n"
    .string "forsookest them not in the\l"
    .string "wilderness: the pillar of the\l"
    .string "cloud departed not from them by day,\l"
    .string "to lead them in the way; neither the\l"
    .string "pillar of fire by night, to shew\l"
    .string "them light, and the way wherein they\l"
    .string "should go$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_20::
    .string "Thou gavest also thy good spirit\n"
    .string "to instruct them, and withheldest\l"
    .string "not thy manna from their mouth, and\l"
    .string "gavest them water for their thirst.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_21::
    .string "Yea, forty years didst thou sustain\n"
    .string "them in the wilderness, so that they\l"
    .string "lacked nothing; their clothes waxed\l"
    .string "not old, and their feet swelled not.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_22::
    .string "Moreover thou gavest them kingdoms\n"
    .string "and nations, and didst divide them\l"
    .string "into corners: so they possessed the\l"
    .string "land of Sihon, and the land of the\l"
    .string "king of Heshbon, and the land of Og\l"
    .string "king of Bashan.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_23::
    .string "Their children also\n"
    .string "multipliedst thou as the stars of\l"
    .string "heaven, and broughtest them into the\l"
    .string "land, concerning which thou hadst\l"
    .string "promised to their fathers, that they\l"
    .string "should go in to possess it.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_24::
    .string "So the children went in and\n"
    .string "possessed the land, and thou\l"
    .string "subduedst before them the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land, the\l"
    .string "Canaanites, and gavest them into\l"
    .string "their hands, with their kings, and\l"
    .string "the people of the land, that they\l"
    .string "might do with them as they would.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_25::
    .string "And they took strong cities, and a\n"
    .string "fat land, and possessed houses\l"
    .string "full of all goods, wells digged,\l"
    .string "vineyards, and oliveyards, and fruit\l"
    .string "trees in abundance: so they did eat,\l"
    .string "and were filled, and became fat, and\l"
    .string "delighted themselves in thy great\l"
    .string "goodness.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_26::
    .string "Nevertheless they were\n"
    .string "disobedient, and rebelled against\l"
    .string "thee, and cast thy law behind their\l"
    .string "backs, and slew thy prophets which\l"
    .string "testified against them to turn them\l"
    .string "to thee, and they wrought great\l"
    .string "provocations.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_27::
    .string "Therefore thou deliveredst them\n"
    .string "into the hand of their enemies, who\l"
    .string "vexed them: and in the time of their\l"
    .string "trouble, when they cried unto thee,\l"
    .string "thou heardest them from heaven; and\l"
    .string "according to thy manifold mercies\l"
    .string "thou gavest them saviours, who saved\l"
    .string "them out of the hand of their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_28::
    .string "But after they had rest, they did\n"
    .string "evil again before thee: therefore\l"
    .string "leftest thou them in the land of\l"
    .string "their enemies, so that they had the\l"
    .string "dominion over them: yet when they\l"
    .string "returned, and cried unto thee, thou\l"
    .string "heardest them from heaven; and many\l"
    .string "times didst thou deliver them\l"
    .string "according to thy mercies;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_29::
    .string "And testifiedst against them, that\n"
    .string "thou mightest bring them again unto\l"
    .string "thy law: yet they dealt proudly,\l"
    .string "and hearkened not unto thy\l"
    .string "commandments, but sinned against thy\l"
    .string "judgments, (which if a man do, he\l"
    .string "shall live in them;) and withdrew\l"
    .string "the shoulder, and hardened their\l"
    .string "neck, and would not hear$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_30::
    .string "Yet many years didst thou forbear\n"
    .string "them, and testifiedst against them by\l"
    .string "thy spirit in thy prophets: yet\l"
    .string "would they not give ear: therefore\l"
    .string "gavest thou them into the hand of the\l"
    .string "people of the lands.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_31::
    .string "Nevertheless for thy great\n"
    .string "mercies’ sake thou didst not utterly\l"
    .string "consume them, nor forsake them; for\l"
    .string "thou art a gracious and merciful God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_32::
    .string "Now therefore, our God, the great,\n"
    .string "the mighty, and the terrible God,\l"
    .string "who keepest covenant and mercy, let\l"
    .string "not all the trouble seem little\l"
    .string "before thee, that hath come upon us,\l"
    .string "on our kings, on our princes, and on\l"
    .string "our priests, and on our prophets,\l"
    .string "and on our fathers, and on all thy\l"
    .string "people, since the time of the kings\l"
    .string "of Assyria unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_33::
    .string "Howbeit thou art just in all that\n"
    .string "is brought upon us; for thou hast\l"
    .string "done right, but we have done\l"
    .string "wickedly:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_34::
    .string "Neither have our kings, our\n"
    .string "princes, our priests, nor our\l"
    .string "fathers, kept thy law, nor\l"
    .string "hearkened unto thy commandments and\l"
    .string "thy testimonies, wherewith thou\l"
    .string "didst testify against them$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_35::
    .string "For they have not served thee in\n"
    .string "their kingdom, and in thy great\l"
    .string "goodness that thou gavest them, and\l"
    .string "in the large and fat land which thou\l"
    .string "gavest before them, neither turned\l"
    .string "they from their wicked works.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_36::
    .string "Behold, we are servants this day,\n"
    .string "and for the land that thou gavest\l"
    .string "unto our fathers to eat the fruit\l"
    .string "thereof and the good thereof,\l"
    .string "behold, we are servants in it:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_37::
    .string "And it yieldeth much increase unto\n"
    .string "the kings whom thou hast set over us\l"
    .string "because of our sins: also they have\l"
    .string "dominion over our bodies, and over\l"
    .string "our cattle, at their pleasure, and\l"
    .string "we are in great distress$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_9_38::
    .string "And because of all this we make a\n"
    .string "sure covenant, and write it; and our\l"
    .string "princes, Levites, and priests, seal\l"
    .string "unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_1::
    .string "Now those that sealed were,\n"
    .string "Nehemiah, the Tirshatha, the son of\l"
    .string "Hachaliah, and Zidkijah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_2::
    .string "Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_3::
    .string "Pashur, Amariah, Malchijah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_4::
    .string "Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_5::
    .string "Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_6::
    .string "Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_7::
    .string "Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_8::
    .string "Maaziah, Bilgai, Shemaiah: these\n"
    .string "were the priests$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_9::
    .string "And the Levites: both Jeshua the son\n"
    .string "of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of\l"
    .string "Henadad, Kadmiel;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_10::
    .string "And their brethren, Shebaniah,\n"
    .string "Hodijah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_11::
    .string "Micha, Rehob, Hashabiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_12::
    .string "Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_13::
    .string "Hodijah, Bani, Beninu$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_14::
    .string "The chief of the people; Parosh,\n"
    .string "Pahathmoab, Elam, Zatthu, Bani,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_15::
    .string "Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_16::
    .string "Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_17::
    .string "Ater, Hizkijah, Azzur,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_18::
    .string "Hodijah, Hashum, Bezai,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_19::
    .string "Hariph, Anathoth, Nebai,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_20::
    .string "Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_21::
    .string "Meshezabeel, Zadok, Jaddua,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_22::
    .string "Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_23::
    .string "Hoshea, Hananiah, Hashub,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_24::
    .string "Hallohesh, Pileha, Shobek,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_25::
    .string "Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_26::
    .string "And Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_27::
    .string "Malluch, Harim, Baanah$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_28::
    .string "And the rest of the people, the\n"
    .string "priests, the Levites, the porters,\l"
    .string "the singers, the Nethinims, and all\l"
    .string "they that had separated themselves\l"
    .string "from the people of the lands unto\l"
    .string "the law of God, their wives, their\l"
    .string "sons, and their daughters, every one\l"
    .string "having knowledge, and having\l"
    .string "understanding;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_29::
    .string "They clave to their brethren, their\n"
    .string "nobles, and entered into a curse,\l"
    .string "and into an oath, to walk in God’s\l"
    .string "law, which was given by Moses the\l"
    .string "servant of God, and to observe and do\l"
    .string "all the commandments of the LORD\l"
    .string "our Lord, and his judgments and his\l"
    .string "statutes;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_30::
    .string "And that we would not give our\n"
    .string "daughters unto the people of the\l"
    .string "land, not take their daughters for\l"
    .string "our sons:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_31::
    .string "And if the people of the land\n"
    .string "bring ware or any victuals on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day to sell, that we would\l"
    .string "not buy it of them on the sabbath, or\l"
    .string "on the holy day: and that we would\l"
    .string "leave the seventh year, and the\l"
    .string "exaction of every debt$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_32::
    .string "Also we made ordinances for us, to\n"
    .string "charge ourselves yearly with the\l"
    .string "third part of a shekel for the\l"
    .string "service of the house of our God;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_33::
    .string "For the shewbread, and for the\n"
    .string "continual meat offering, and for the\l"
    .string "continual burnt offering, of the\l"
    .string "sabbaths, of the new moons, for the\l"
    .string "set feasts, and for the holy things,\l"
    .string "and for the sin offerings to make an\l"
    .string "atonement for Israel, and for all\l"
    .string "the work of the house of our God$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_34::
    .string "And we cast the lots among the\n"
    .string "priests, the Levites, and the\l"
    .string "people, for the wood offering, to\l"
    .string "bring it into the house of our God,\l"
    .string "after the houses of our fathers, at\l"
    .string "times appointed year by year, to\l"
    .string "burn upon the altar of the LORD our\l"
    .string "God, as it is written in the law:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_35::
    .string "And to bring the firstfruits of our\n"
    .string "ground, and the firstfruits of all\l"
    .string "fruit of all trees, year by year,\l"
    .string "unto the house of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_36::
    .string "Also the firstborn of our sons, and\n"
    .string "of our cattle, as it is written in\l"
    .string "the law, and the firstlings of our\l"
    .string "herds and of our flocks, to bring to\l"
    .string "the house of our God, unto the\l"
    .string "priests that minister in the house of\l"
    .string "our God:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_37::
    .string "And that we should bring the\n"
    .string "firstfruits of our dough, and our\l"
    .string "offerings, and the fruit of all\l"
    .string "manner of trees, of wine and of oil,\l"
    .string "unto the priests, to the chambers of\l"
    .string "the house of our God; and the tithes\l"
    .string "of our ground unto the Levites, that\l"
    .string "the same Levites might have the\l"
    .string "tithes in all the cities of our\l"
    .string "tillage$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_38::
    .string "And the priest the son of Aaron\n"
    .string "shall be with the Levites, when the\l"
    .string "Levites take tithes: and the Levites\l"
    .string "shall bring up the tithe of the\l"
    .string "tithes unto the house of our God, to\l"
    .string "the chambers, into the treasure\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_10_39::
    .string "For the children of Israel and the\n"
    .string "children of Levi shall bring the\l"
    .string "offering of the corn, of the new\l"
    .string "wine, and the oil, unto the chambers,\l"
    .string "where are the vessels of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary, and the priests that\l"
    .string "minister, and the porters, and the\l"
    .string "singers: and we will not forsake the\l"
    .string "house of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_1::
    .string "And the rulers of the people\n"
    .string "dwelt at Jerusalem: the rest of the\l"
    .string "people also cast lots, to bring\l"
    .string "one of ten to dwell in Jerusalem\l"
    .string "the holy city, and nine parts to\l"
    .string "dwell in other cities.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_2::
    .string "And the people blessed all the\n"
    .string "men, that willingly offered\l"
    .string "themselves to dwell at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_3::
    .string "Now these are the chief of the\n"
    .string "province that dwelt in Jerusalem:\l"
    .string "but in the cities of Judah dwelt\l"
    .string "every one in his possession in their\l"
    .string "cities, to wit, Israel, the priests,\l"
    .string "and the Levites, and the Nethinims,\l"
    .string "and the children of Solomon’s\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_4::
    .string "And at Jerusalem dwelt certain of\n"
    .string "the children of Judah, and of the\l"
    .string "children of Benjamin. Of the\l"
    .string "children of Judah; Athaiah the son\l"
    .string "of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the\l"
    .string "son of Amariah, the son of\l"
    .string "Shephatiah, the son of Mahalaleel,\l"
    .string "of the children of Perez;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_5::
    .string "And Maaseiah the son of Baruch, the\n"
    .string "son of Colhozeh, the son of Hazaiah,\l"
    .string "the son of Adaiah, the son of\l"
    .string "Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, the\l"
    .string "son of Shiloni$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_6::
    .string "All the sons of Perez that dwelt\n"
    .string "at Jerusalem were four hundred\l"
    .string "threescore and eight valiant men.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_7::
    .string "And these are the sons of Benjamin;\n"
    .string "Sallu the son of Meshullam, the\l"
    .string "son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the\l"
    .string "son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah,\l"
    .string "the son of Ithiel, the son of\l"
    .string "Jesaiah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_8::
    .string "And after him Gabbai, Sallai, nine\n"
    .string "hundred twenty and eight.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_9::
    .string "And Joel the son of Zichri was\n"
    .string "their overseer: and Judah the son of\l"
    .string "Senuah was second over the city.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_10::
    .string "Of the priests: Jedaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Joiarib, Jachin.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_11::
    .string "Seraiah the son of Hilkiah, the son\n"
    .string "of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the\l"
    .string "son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub,\l"
    .string "was the ruler of the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_12::
    .string "And their brethren that did the work\n"
    .string "of the house were eight hundred\l"
    .string "twenty and two: and Adaiah the son of\l"
    .string "Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the\l"
    .string "son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah,\l"
    .string "the son of Pashur, the son of\l"
    .string "Malchiah.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_13::
    .string "And his brethren, chief of the\n"
    .string "fathers, two hundred forty and two:\l"
    .string "and Amashai the son of Azareel, the\l"
    .string "son of Ahasai, the son of\l"
    .string "Meshillemoth, the son of Immer,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_14::
    .string "And their brethren, mighty men of\n"
    .string "valour, an hundred twenty and eight:\l"
    .string "and their overseer was Zabdiel, the\l"
    .string "son of one of the great men$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_15::
    .string "Also of the Levites: Shemaiah the\n"
    .string "son of Hashub, the son of Azrikam,\l"
    .string "the son of Hashabiah, the son of\l"
    .string "Bunni;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_16::
    .string "And Shabbethai and Jozabad, of the\n"
    .string "chief of the Levites, had the\l"
    .string "oversight of the outward business of\l"
    .string "the house of God$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_17::
    .string "And Mattaniah the son of Micha, the\n"
    .string "son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, was\l"
    .string "the principal to begin the\l"
    .string "thanksgiving in prayer: and\l"
    .string "Bakbukiah the second among his\l"
    .string "brethren, and Abda the son of\l"
    .string "Shammua, the son of Galal, the son\l"
    .string "of Jeduthun.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_18::
    .string "All the Levites in the holy city\n"
    .string "were two hundred fourscore and four.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_19::
    .string "Moreover the porters, Akkub,\n"
    .string "Talmon, and their brethren that\l"
    .string "kept the gates, were an hundred\l"
    .string "seventy and two.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_20::
    .string "And the residue of Israel, of the\n"
    .string "priests, and the Levites, were in\l"
    .string "all the cities of Judah, every one\l"
    .string "in his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_21::
    .string "But the Nethinims dwelt in Ophel:\n"
    .string "and Ziha and Gispa were over the\l"
    .string "Nethinims.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_22::
    .string "The overseer also of the Levites at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem was Uzzi the son of Bani,\l"
    .string "the son of Hashabiah, the son of\l"
    .string "Mattaniah, the son of Micha. Of the\l"
    .string "sons of Asaph, the singers were over\l"
    .string "the business of the house of God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_23::
    .string "For it was the king’s commandment\n"
    .string "concerning them, that a certain\l"
    .string "portion should be for the singers,\l"
    .string "due for every day.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_24::
    .string "And Pethahiah the son of\n"
    .string "Meshezabeel, of the children of\l"
    .string "Zerah the son of Judah, was at the\l"
    .string "king’s hand in all matters\l"
    .string "concerning the people.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_25::
    .string "And for the villages, with their\n"
    .string "fields, some of the children of\l"
    .string "Judah dwelt at Kirjatharba, and in\l"
    .string "the villages thereof, and at Dibon,\l"
    .string "and in the villages thereof, and at\l"
    .string "Jekabzeel, and in the villages\l"
    .string "thereof,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_26::
    .string "And at Jeshua, and at Moladah, and\n"
    .string "at Bethphelet,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_27::
    .string "And at Hazarshual, and at\n"
    .string "Beersheba, and in the villages\l"
    .string "thereof,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_28::
    .string "And at Ziklag, and at Mekonah, and\n"
    .string "in the villages thereof,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_29::
    .string "And at Enrimmon, and at Zareah, and\n"
    .string "at Jarmuth,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_30::
    .string "Zanoah, Adullam, and in their\n"
    .string "villages, at Lachish, and the\l"
    .string "fields thereof, at Azekah, and in\l"
    .string "the villages thereof. And they\l"
    .string "dwelt from Beersheba unto the\l"
    .string "valley of Hinnom$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_31::
    .string "The children also of Benjamin from\n"
    .string "Geba dwelt at Michmash, and Aija,\l"
    .string "and Bethel, and in their villages.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_32::
    .string "And at Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_33::
    .string "Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_34::
    .string "Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_35::
    .string "Lod, and Ono, the valley of\n"
    .string "craftsmen$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_11_36::
    .string "And of the Levites were divisions in\n"
    .string "Judah, and in Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_1::
    .string "Now these are the priests and the\n"
    .string "Levites that went up with\l"
    .string "Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel,\l"
    .string "and Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_2::
    .string "Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_3::
    .string "Shechaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_4::
    .string "Iddo, Ginnetho, Abijah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_5::
    .string "Miamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_6::
    .string "Shemaiah, and Joiarib, Jedaiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_7::
    .string "Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, Jedaiah.\n"
    .string "These were the chief of the priests\l"
    .string "and of their brethren in the days of\l"
    .string "Jeshua$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_8::
    .string "Moreover the Levites: Jeshua,\n"
    .string "Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah,\l"
    .string "and Mattaniah, which was over the\l"
    .string "thanksgiving, he and his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_9::
    .string "Also Bakbukiah and Unni, their\n"
    .string "brethren, were over against them in\l"
    .string "the watches.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_10::
    .string "And Jeshua begat Joiakim, Joiakim\n"
    .string "also begat Eliashib, and Eliashib\l"
    .string "begat Joiada,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_11::
    .string "And Joiada begat Jonathan, and\n"
    .string "Jonathan begat Jaddua$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_12::
    .string "And in the days of Joiakim were\n"
    .string "priests, the chief of the fathers: of\l"
    .string "Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah,\l"
    .string "Hananiah;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_13::
    .string "Of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah,\n"
    .string "Jehohanan;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_14::
    .string "Of Melicu, Jonathan; of Shebaniah,\n"
    .string "Joseph;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_15::
    .string "Of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth,\n"
    .string "Helkai;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_16::
    .string "Of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon,\n"
    .string "Meshullam;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_17::
    .string "Of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of\n"
    .string "Moadiah, Piltai:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_18::
    .string "Of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah,\n"
    .string "Jehonathan;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_19::
    .string "And of Joiarib, Mattenai; of\n"
    .string "Jedaiah, Uzzi;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_20::
    .string "Of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_21::
    .string "Of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah,\n"
    .string "Nethaneel$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_22::
    .string "The Levites in the days of\n"
    .string "Eliashib, Joiada, and Johanan, and\l"
    .string "Jaddua, were recorded chief of the\l"
    .string "fathers: also the priests, to the\l"
    .string "reign of Darius the Persian.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_23::
    .string "The sons of Levi, the chief of the\n"
    .string "fathers, were written in the book of\l"
    .string "the chronicles, even until the days\l"
    .string "of Johanan the son of Eliashib.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_24::
    .string "And the chief of the Levites:\n"
    .string "Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the\l"
    .string "son of Kadmiel, with their brethren\l"
    .string "over against them, to praise and to\l"
    .string "give thanks, according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of David the man of God,\l"
    .string "ward over against ward.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_25::
    .string "Mattaniah, and Bakbukiah, Obadiah,\n"
    .string "Meshullam, Talmon, Akkub, were\l"
    .string "porters keeping the ward at the\l"
    .string "thresholds of the gates.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_26::
    .string "These were in the days of Joiakim\n"
    .string "the son of Jeshua, the son of\l"
    .string "Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah\l"
    .string "the governor, and of Ezra the\l"
    .string "priest, the scribe.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_27::
    .string "And at the dedication of the wall\n"
    .string "of Jerusalem they sought the Levites\l"
    .string "out of all their places, to bring\l"
    .string "them to Jerusalem, to keep the\l"
    .string "dedication with gladness, both with\l"
    .string "thanksgivings, and with singing,\l"
    .string "with cymbals, psalteries, and with\l"
    .string "harps.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_28::
    .string "And the sons of the singers gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together, both out of the\l"
    .string "plain country round about\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and from the villages of\l"
    .string "Netophathi;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_29::
    .string "Also from the house of Gilgal, and\n"
    .string "out of the fields of Geba and\l"
    .string "Azmaveth: for the singers had\l"
    .string "builded them villages round about\l"
    .string "Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_30::
    .string "And the priests and the Levites\n"
    .string "purified themselves, and purified\l"
    .string "the people, and the gates, and the\l"
    .string "wall.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_31::
    .string "Then I brought up the princes of\n"
    .string "Judah upon the wall, and\l"
    .string "appointed two great companies of\l"
    .string "them that gave thanks, whereof one\l"
    .string "went on the right hand upon the\l"
    .string "wall toward the dung gate:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_32::
    .string "And after them went Hoshaiah, and\n"
    .string "half of the princes of Judah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_33::
    .string "And Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_34::
    .string "Judah, and Benjamin, and Shemaiah,\n"
    .string "and Jeremiah,"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_35::
    .string "And certain of the priests’ sons\n"
    .string "with trumpets; namely, Zechariah\l"
    .string "the son of Jonathan, the son of\l"
    .string "Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the\l"
    .string "son of Michaiah, the son of Zaccur,\l"
    .string "the son of Asaph:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_36::
    .string "And his brethren, Shemaiah, and\n"
    .string "Azarael, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai,\l"
    .string "Nethaneel, and Judah, Hanani, with\l"
    .string "the musical instruments of David the\l"
    .string "man of God, and Ezra the scribe\l"
    .string "before them$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_37::
    .string "And at the fountain gate, which was\n"
    .string "over against them, they went up by\l"
    .string "the stairs of the city of David, at\l"
    .string "the going up of the wall, above the\l"
    .string "house of David, even unto the water\l"
    .string "gate eastward.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_38::
    .string "And the other company of them that\n"
    .string "gave thanks went over against them,\l"
    .string "and I after them, and the half of the\l"
    .string "people upon the wall, from beyond\l"
    .string "the tower of the furnaces even unto\l"
    .string "the broad wall;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_39::
    .string "And from above the gate of Ephraim,\n"
    .string "and above the old gate, and above the\l"
    .string "fish gate, and the tower of\l"
    .string "Hananeel, and the tower of Meah,\l"
    .string "even unto the sheep gate: and they\l"
    .string "stood still in the prison gate$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_40::
    .string "So stood the two companies of them\n"
    .string "that gave thanks in the house of God,\l"
    .string "and I, and the half of the rulers\l"
    .string "with me:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_41::
    .string "And the priests; Eliakim,\n"
    .string "Maaseiah, Miniamin, Michaiah,\l"
    .string "Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah,\l"
    .string "with trumpets;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_42::
    .string "And Maaseiah, and Shemaiah, and\n"
    .string "Eleazar, and Uzzi, and Jehohanan,\l"
    .string "and Malchijah, and Elam, and Ezer.\l"
    .string "And the singers sang loud, with\l"
    .string "Jezrahiah their overseer$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_43::
    .string "Also that day they offered great\n"
    .string "sacrifices, and rejoiced: for God had\l"
    .string "made them rejoice with great joy: the\l"
    .string "wives also and the children\l"
    .string "rejoiced: so that the joy of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem was heard even afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_44::
    .string "And at that time were some\n"
    .string "appointed over the chambers for the\l"
    .string "treasures, for the offerings, for the\l"
    .string "firstfruits, and for the tithes, to\l"
    .string "gather into them out of the fields\l"
    .string "of the cities the portions of the\l"
    .string "law for the priests and Levites: for\l"
    .string "Judah rejoiced for the priests and\l"
    .string "for the Levites that waited.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_45::
    .string "And both the singers and the\n"
    .string "porters kept the ward of their God,\l"
    .string "and the ward of the purification,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of\l"
    .string "David, and of Solomon his son.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_46::
    .string "For in the days of David and Asaph\n"
    .string "of old there were chief of the\l"
    .string "singers, and songs of praise and\l"
    .string "thanksgiving unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_12_47::
    .string "And all Israel in the days of\n"
    .string "Zerubbabel, and in the days of\l"
    .string "Nehemiah, gave the portions of the\l"
    .string "singers and the porters, every day\l"
    .string "his portion: and they sanctified\l"
    .string "holy things unto the Levites; and\l"
    .string "the Levites sanctified them unto the\l"
    .string "children of Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_1::
    .string "On that day they read in the book of\n"
    .string "Moses in the audience of the\l"
    .string "people; and therein was found\l"
    .string "written, that the Ammonite and the\l"
    .string "Moabite should not come into the\l"
    .string "congregation of God for ever;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_2::
    .string "Because they met not the children\n"
    .string "of Israel with bread and with water,\l"
    .string "but hired Balaam against them, that\l"
    .string "he should curse them: howbeit our\l"
    .string "God turned the curse into a blessing$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_3::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when they had\n"
    .string "heard the law, that they separated\l"
    .string "from Israel all the mixed\l"
    .string "multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_4::
    .string "And before this, Eliashib the\n"
    .string "priest, having the oversight of the\l"
    .string "chamber of the house of our God, was\l"
    .string "allied unto Tobiah:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_5::
    .string "And he had prepared for him a great\n"
    .string "chamber, where aforetime they laid\l"
    .string "the meat offerings, the\l"
    .string "frankincense, and the vessels, and\l"
    .string "the tithes of the corn, the new wine,\l"
    .string "and the oil, which was commanded to\l"
    .string "be given to the Levites, and the\l"
    .string "singers, and the porters; and the\l"
    .string "offerings of the priests$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_6::
    .string "But in all this time was not I at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: for in the two and\l"
    .string "thirtieth year of Artaxerxes king of\l"
    .string "Babylon came I unto the king, and\l"
    .string "after certain days obtained I leave\l"
    .string "of the king:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_7::
    .string "And I came to Jerusalem, and\n"
    .string "understood of the evil that\l"
    .string "Eliashib did for Tobiah, in\l"
    .string "preparing him a chamber in the\l"
    .string "courts of the house of God$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_8::
    .string "And it grieved me sore: therefore I\n"
    .string "cast forth all the household stuff\l"
    .string "to Tobiah out of the chamber.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_9::
    .string "Then I commanded, and they cleansed\n"
    .string "the chambers: and thither brought I\l"
    .string "again the vessels of the house of\l"
    .string "God, with the meat offering and the\l"
    .string "frankincense.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_10::
    .string "And I perceived that the portions\n"
    .string "of the Levites had not been given\l"
    .string "them: for the Levites and the\l"
    .string "singers, that did the work, were\l"
    .string "fled every one to his field.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_11::
    .string "Then contended I with the rulers,\n"
    .string "and said, Why is the house of God\l"
    .string "forsaken? And I gathered them\l"
    .string "together, and set them in their\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_12::
    .string "Then brought all Judah the tithe\n"
    .string "of the corn and the new wine and the\l"
    .string "oil unto the treasuries.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_13::
    .string "And I made treasurers over the\n"
    .string "treasuries, Shelemiah the priest,\l"
    .string "and Zadok the scribe, and of the\l"
    .string "Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them\l"
    .string "was Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son\l"
    .string "of Mattaniah: for they were counted\l"
    .string "faithful, and their office was to\l"
    .string "distribute unto their brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_14::
    .string "Remember me, O my God, concerning\n"
    .string "this, and wipe not out my good deeds\l"
    .string "that I have done for the house of my\l"
    .string "God, and for the offices thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_15::
    .string "In those days saw I in Judah some\n"
    .string "treading wine presses on the\l"
    .string "sabbath, and bringing in sheaves, and\l"
    .string "lading asses; as also wine, grapes,\l"
    .string "and figs, and all manner of burdens,\l"
    .string "which they brought into Jerusalem on\l"
    .string "the sabbath day: and I testified\l"
    .string "against them in the day wherein they\l"
    .string "sold victuals.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_16::
    .string "There dwelt men of Tyre also\n"
    .string "therein, which brought fish, and\l"
    .string "all manner of ware, and sold on the\l"
    .string "sabbath unto the children of Judah,\l"
    .string "and in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_17::
    .string "Then I contended with the nobles of\n"
    .string "Judah, and said unto them, What evil\l"
    .string "thing is this that ye do, and profane\l"
    .string "the sabbath day?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_18::
    .string "Did not your fathers thus, and did\n"
    .string "not our God bring all this evil\l"
    .string "upon us, and upon this city? yet ye\l"
    .string "bring more wrath upon Israel by\l"
    .string "profaning the sabbath$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_19::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when the\n"
    .string "gates of Jerusalem began to be dark\l"
    .string "before the sabbath, I commanded that\l"
    .string "the gates should be shut, and\l"
    .string "charged that they should not be\l"
    .string "opened till after the sabbath: and\l"
    .string "some of my servants set I at the\l"
    .string "gates, that there should no burden\l"
    .string "be brought in on the sabbath day.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_20::
    .string "So the merchants and sellers of\n"
    .string "all kind of ware lodged without\l"
    .string "Jerusalem once or twice.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_21::
    .string "Then I testified against them, and\n"
    .string "said unto them, Why lodge ye about\l"
    .string "the wall? if ye do so again, I will\l"
    .string "lay hands on you. From that time\l"
    .string "forth came they no more on the\l"
    .string "sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_22::
    .string "And I commanded the Levites that\n"
    .string "they should cleanse themselves,\l"
    .string "and that they should come and keep\l"
    .string "the gates, to sanctify the sabbath day\l"
    .string " Remember me, O my God, concerning\l"
    .string "this also, and spare me according to\l"
    .string "the greatness of thy mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_23::
    .string "In those days also saw I Jews that\n"
    .string "had married wives of Ashdod, of\l"
    .string "Ammon, and of Moab:"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_24::
    .string "And their children spake half in\n"
    .string "the speech of Ashdod, and could not\l"
    .string "speak in the Jews’ language, but\l"
    .string "according to the language of each\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_25::
    .string "And I contended with them, and\n"
    .string "cursed them, and smote certain of\l"
    .string "them, and plucked off their hair,\l"
    .string "and made them swear by God, saying,\l"
    .string "Ye shall not give your daughters\l"
    .string "unto their sons, nor take their\l"
    .string "daughters unto your sons, or for\l"
    .string "yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_26::
    .string "Did not Solomon king of Israel sin\n"
    .string "by these things? yet among many\l"
    .string "nations was there no king like him,\l"
    .string "who was beloved of his God, and God\l"
    .string "made him king over all Israel:\l"
    .string "nevertheless even him did\l"
    .string "outlandish women cause to sin.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_27::
    .string "Shall we then hearken unto you to\n"
    .string "do all this great evil, to\l"
    .string "transgress against our God in\l"
    .string "marrying strange wives?"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_28::
    .string "And one of the sons of Joiada, the\n"
    .string "son of Eliashib the high priest, was\l"
    .string "son in law to Sanballat the\l"
    .string "Horonite: therefore I chased him from\l"
    .string "me$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_29::
    .string "Remember them, O my God, because\n"
    .string "they have defiled the priesthood,\l"
    .string "and the covenant of the priesthood,\l"
    .string "and of the Levites.$"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_30::
    .string "Thus cleansed I them from all\n"
    .string "strangers, and appointed the wards\l"
    .string "of the priests and the Levites,\l"
    .string "every one in his business;"
Bible_Text_Nehemiah_13_31::
    .string "And for the wood offering, at times\n"
    .string "appointed, and for the firstfruits.\l"
    .string "Remember me, O my God, for good$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the days of\n"
    .string "Ahasuerus, (this is Ahasuerus which\l"
    .string "reigned, from India even unto\l"
    .string "Ethiopia, over an hundred and seven\l"
    .string "and twenty provinces:)"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_2::
    .string "That in those days, when the king\n"
    .string "Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his\l"
    .string "kingdom, which was in Shushan the\l"
    .string "palace,"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_3::
    .string "In the third year of his reign, he\n"
    .string "made a feast unto all his princes\l"
    .string "and his servants; the power of\l"
    .string "Persia and Media, the nobles and\l"
    .string "princes of the provinces, being\l"
    .string "before him:"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_4::
    .string "When he shewed the riches of his\n"
    .string "glorious kingdom and the honour of\l"
    .string "his excellent majesty many days,\l"
    .string "even an hundred and fourscore days$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_5::
    .string "And when these days were expired,\n"
    .string "the king made a feast unto all the\l"
    .string "people that were present in\l"
    .string "Shushan the palace, both unto great\l"
    .string "and small, seven days, in the court\l"
    .string "of the garden of the king’s palace;"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_6::
    .string "Where were white, green, and blue,\n"
    .string "hangings, fastened with cords of fine\l"
    .string "linen and purple to silver rings\l"
    .string "and pillars of marble: the beds\l"
    .string "were of gold and silver, upon a\l"
    .string "pavement of red, and blue, and white,\l"
    .string "and black, marble$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_7::
    .string "And they gave them drink in vessels\n"
    .string "of gold, (the vessels being diverse\l"
    .string "one from another,) and royal wine in\l"
    .string "abundance, according to the state of\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_8::
    .string "And the drinking was according to\n"
    .string "the law; none did compel: for so\l"
    .string "the king had appointed to all the\l"
    .string "officers of his house, that they\l"
    .string "should do according to every man’s\l"
    .string "pleasure.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_9::
    .string "Also Vashti the queen made a feast\n"
    .string "for the women in the royal house\l"
    .string "which belonged to king Ahasuerus.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_10::
    .string "On the seventh day, when the heart\n"
    .string "of the king was merry with wine, he\l"
    .string "commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona,\l"
    .string "Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and\l"
    .string "Carcas, the seven chamberlains that\l"
    .string "served in the presence of Ahasuerus\l"
    .string "the king,"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_11::
    .string "To bring Vashti the queen before the\n"
    .string "king with the crown royal, to shew\l"
    .string "the people and the princes her\l"
    .string "beauty: for she was fair to look on$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_12::
    .string "But the queen Vashti refused to come\n"
    .string "at the king’s commandment by his\l"
    .string "chamberlains: therefore was the king\l"
    .string "very wroth, and his anger burned in\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_13::
    .string "Then the king said to the wise men,\n"
    .string "which knew the times, (for so was the\l"
    .string "king’s manner toward all that knew\l"
    .string "law and judgment:"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_14::
    .string "And the next unto him was Carshena,\n"
    .string "Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres,\l"
    .string "Marsena, and Memucan, the seven\l"
    .string "princes of Persia and Media, which\l"
    .string "saw the king’s face, and which sat\l"
    .string "the first in the kingdom;)"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_15::
    .string "What shall we do unto the queen\n"
    .string "Vashti according to law, because she\l"
    .string "hath not performed the commandment\l"
    .string "of the king Ahasuerus by the\l"
    .string "chamberlains?"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_16::
    .string "And Memucan answered before the\n"
    .string "king and the princes, Vashti the\l"
    .string "queen hath not done wrong to the king\l"
    .string "only, but also to all the princes,\l"
    .string "and to all the people that are in\l"
    .string "all the provinces of the king\l"
    .string "Ahasuerus$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_17::
    .string "For this deed of the queen shall\n"
    .string "come abroad unto all women, so that\l"
    .string "they shall despise their husbands\l"
    .string "in their eyes, when it shall be\l"
    .string "reported, The king Ahasuerus\l"
    .string "commanded Vashti the queen to be\l"
    .string "brought in before him, but she came\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_18::
    .string "Likewise shall the ladies of\n"
    .string "Persia and Media say this day unto\l"
    .string "all the king’s princes, which have\l"
    .string "heard of the deed of the queen. Thus\l"
    .string "shall there arise too much\l"
    .string "contempt and wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_19::
    .string "If it please the king, let there\n"
    .string "go a royal commandment from him, and\l"
    .string "let it be written among the laws of\l"
    .string "the Persians and the Medes, that it\l"
    .string "be not altered, That Vashti come no\l"
    .string "more before king Ahasuerus; and let\l"
    .string "the king give her royal estate unto\l"
    .string "another that is better than she.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_20::
    .string "And when the king’s decree which he\n"
    .string "shall make shall be published\l"
    .string "throughout all his empire, (for it\l"
    .string "is great,) all the wives shall\l"
    .string "give to their husbands honour, both\l"
    .string "to great and small.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_21::
    .string "And the saying pleased the king\n"
    .string "and the princes; and the king did\l"
    .string "according to the word of Memucan:"
Bible_Text_Esther_1_22::
    .string "For he sent letters into all the\n"
    .string "king’s provinces, into every\l"
    .string "province according to the writing\l"
    .string "thereof, and to every people after\l"
    .string "their language, that every man\l"
    .string "should bear rule in his own house,\l"
    .string "and that it should be published\l"
    .string "according to the language of every\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_1::
    .string "After these things, when the wrath\n"
    .string "of king Ahasuerus was appeased, he\l"
    .string "remembered Vashti, and what she had\l"
    .string "done, and what was decreed against\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_2::
    .string "Then said the king’s servants that\n"
    .string "ministered unto him, Let there be\l"
    .string "fair young virgins sought for the\l"
    .string "king:"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_3::
    .string "And let the king appoint officers\n"
    .string "in all the provinces of his\l"
    .string "kingdom, that they may gather\l"
    .string "together all the fair young virgins\l"
    .string "unto Shushan the palace, to the\l"
    .string "house of the women, unto the custody\l"
    .string "of Hege the king’s chamberlain,\l"
    .string "keeper of the women; and let their\l"
    .string "things for purification be given\l"
    .string "them:"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_4::
    .string "And let the maiden which pleaseth\n"
    .string "the king be queen instead of Vashti\l"
    .string "And the thing pleased the king; and\l"
    .string "he did so.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_5::
    .string "Now in Shushan the palace there\n"
    .string "was a certain Jew, whose name was\l"
    .string "Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of\l"
    .string "Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite;"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_6::
    .string "Who had been carried away from\n"
    .string "Jerusalem with the captivity which\l"
    .string "had been carried away with Jeconiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon had carried away$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_7::
    .string "And he brought up Hadassah, that\n"
    .string "is, Esther, his uncle’s daughter:\l"
    .string "for she had neither father nor\l"
    .string "mother, and the maid was fair and\l"
    .string "beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her\l"
    .string "father and mother were dead, took for\l"
    .string "his own daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_8::
    .string "So it came to pass, when the king’s\n"
    .string "commandment and his decree was heard,\l"
    .string "and when many maidens were gathered\l"
    .string "together unto Shushan the palace,\l"
    .string "to the custody of Hegai, that Esther\l"
    .string "was brought also unto the king’s\l"
    .string "house, to the custody of Hegai,\l"
    .string "keeper of the women.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_9::
    .string "And the maiden pleased him, and she\n"
    .string "obtained kindness of him; and he\l"
    .string "speedily gave her her things for\l"
    .string "purification, with such things as\l"
    .string "belonged to her, and seven maidens,\l"
    .string "which were meet to be given her, out\l"
    .string "of the king’s house: and he\l"
    .string "preferred her and her maids unto the\l"
    .string "best place of the house of the women.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_10::
    .string "Esther had not shewed her people\n"
    .string "nor her kindred: for Mordecai had\l"
    .string "charged her that she should not shew\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_11::
    .string "And Mordecai walked every day\n"
    .string "before the court of the women’s\l"
    .string "house, to know how Esther did, and\l"
    .string "what should become of her.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_12::
    .string "Now when every maid’s turn was come\n"
    .string "to go in to king Ahasuerus, after\l"
    .string "that she had been twelve months,\l"
    .string "according to the manner of the women,\l"
    .string "(for so were the days of their\l"
    .string "purifications accomplished, to wit,\l"
    .string "six months with oil of myrrh, and six\l"
    .string "months with sweet odours, and with\l"
    .string "other things for the purifying of\l"
    .string "the women;)"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_13::
    .string "Then thus came every maiden unto the\n"
    .string "king; whatsoever she desired was\l"
    .string "given her to go with her out of the\l"
    .string "house of the women unto the king’s\l"
    .string "house$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_14::
    .string "In the evening she went, and on the\n"
    .string "morrow she returned into the second\l"
    .string "house of the women, to the custody of\l"
    .string "Shaashgaz, the king’s chamberlain,\l"
    .string "which kept the concubines: she came\l"
    .string "in unto the king no more, except the\l"
    .string "king delighted in her, and that she\l"
    .string "were called by name.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_15::
    .string "Now when the turn of Esther, the\n"
    .string "daughter of Abihail the uncle of\l"
    .string "Mordecai, who had taken her for his\l"
    .string "daughter, was come to go in unto the\l"
    .string "king, she required nothing but what\l"
    .string "Hegai the king’s chamberlain, the\l"
    .string "keeper of the women, appointed. And\l"
    .string "Esther obtained favour in the sight\l"
    .string "of all them that looked upon her.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_16::
    .string "So Esther was taken unto king\n"
    .string "Ahasuerus into his house royal in\l"
    .string "the tenth month, which is the month\l"
    .string "Tebeth, in the seventh year of his\l"
    .string "reign.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_17::
    .string "And the king loved Esther above\n"
    .string "all the women, and she obtained\l"
    .string "grace and favour in his sight more\l"
    .string "than all the virgins; so that he set\l"
    .string "the royal crown upon her head, and\l"
    .string "made her queen instead of Vashti.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_18::
    .string "Then the king made a great feast\n"
    .string "unto all his princes and his\l"
    .string "servants, even Esther’s feast; and he\l"
    .string "made a release to the provinces, and\l"
    .string "gave gifts, according to the state of\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_19::
    .string "And when the virgins were gathered\n"
    .string "together the second time, then\l"
    .string "Mordecai sat in the king’s gate.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_20::
    .string "Esther had not yet shewed her\n"
    .string "kindred nor her people; as Mordecai\l"
    .string "had charged her: for Esther did the\l"
    .string "commandment of Mordecai, like as\l"
    .string "when she was brought up with him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_21::
    .string "In those days, while Mordecai sat\n"
    .string "in the king’s gate, two of the king’s\l"
    .string "chamberlains, Bigthan and Teresh, of\l"
    .string "those which kept the door, were\l"
    .string "wroth, and sought to lay hands on the\l"
    .string "king Ahasuerus.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_22::
    .string "And the thing was known to Mordecai,\n"
    .string "who told it unto Esther the queen;\l"
    .string "and Esther certified the king\l"
    .string "thereof in Mordecai’s name.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_2_23::
    .string "And when inquisition was made of the\n"
    .string "matter, it was found out; therefore\l"
    .string "they were both hanged on a tree: and\l"
    .string "it was written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_1::
    .string "After these things did king\n"
    .string "Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of\l"
    .string "Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced\l"
    .string "him, and set his seat above all the\l"
    .string "princes that were with him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_2::
    .string "And all the king’s servants, that\n"
    .string "were in the king’s gate, bowed, and\l"
    .string "reverenced Haman: for the king had so\l"
    .string "commanded concerning him. But\l"
    .string "Mordecai bowed not, nor did him\l"
    .string "reverence.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_3::
    .string "Then the king’s servants, which were\n"
    .string "in the king’s gate, said unto\l"
    .string "Mordecai, Why transgressest thou the\l"
    .string "king’s commandment?"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_4::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when they\n"
    .string "spake daily unto him, and he\l"
    .string "hearkened not unto them, that they\l"
    .string "told Haman, to see whether\l"
    .string "Mordecai’s matters would stand: for\l"
    .string "he had told them that he was a Jew$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_5::
    .string "And when Haman saw that Mordecai\n"
    .string "bowed not, nor did him reverence,\l"
    .string "then was Haman full of wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_6::
    .string "And he thought scorn to lay hands\n"
    .string "on Mordecai alone; for they had\l"
    .string "shewed him the people of Mordecai:\l"
    .string "wherefore Haman sought to destroy\l"
    .string "all the Jews that were throughout\l"
    .string "the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even\l"
    .string "the people of Mordecai.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_7::
    .string "In the first month, that is, the\n"
    .string "month Nisan, in the twelfth year of\l"
    .string "king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that\l"
    .string "is, the lot, before Haman from day to\l"
    .string "day, and from month to month, to the\l"
    .string "twelfth month, that is, the month\l"
    .string "Adar.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_8::
    .string "And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus,\n"
    .string "There is a certain people\l"
    .string "scattered abroad and dispersed\l"
    .string "among the people in all the\l"
    .string "provinces of thy kingdom; and their\l"
    .string "laws are diverse from all people;\l"
    .string "neither keep they the king’s laws:\l"
    .string "therefore it is not for the king’s\l"
    .string "profit to suffer them.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_9::
    .string "If it please the king, let it be\n"
    .string "written that they may be destroyed:\l"
    .string "and I will pay ten thousand\l"
    .string "talents of silver to the hands of\l"
    .string "those that have the charge of the\l"
    .string "business, to bring it into the king’s\l"
    .string "treasuries.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_10::
    .string "And the king took his ring from his\n"
    .string "hand, and gave it unto Haman the son\l"
    .string "of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews’\l"
    .string "enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_11::
    .string "And the king said unto Haman, The\n"
    .string "silver is given to thee, the\l"
    .string "people also, to do with them as it\l"
    .string "seemeth good to thee.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_12::
    .string "Then were the king’s scribes\n"
    .string "called on the thirteenth day of the\l"
    .string "first month, and there was written\l"
    .string "according to all that Haman had\l"
    .string "commanded unto the king’s\l"
    .string "lieutenants, and to the governors\l"
    .string "that were over every province, and\l"
    .string "to the rulers of every people of\l"
    .string "every province according to the\l"
    .string "writing thereof, and to every\l"
    .string "people after their language; in the\l"
    .string "name of king Ahasuerus was it\l"
    .string "written, and sealed with the king’s\l"
    .string "ring.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_13::
    .string "And the letters were sent by posts\n"
    .string "into all the king’s provinces, to\l"
    .string "destroy, to kill, and to cause to\l"
    .string "perish, all Jews, both young and\l"
    .string "old, little children and women, in\l"
    .string "one day, even upon the thirteenth\l"
    .string "day of the twelfth month, which is\l"
    .string "the month Adar, and to take the\l"
    .string "spoil of them for a prey.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_14::
    .string "The copy of the writing for a\n"
    .string "commandment to be given in every\l"
    .string "province was published unto all\l"
    .string "people, that they should be ready\l"
    .string "against that day.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_3_15::
    .string "The posts went out, being hastened\n"
    .string "by the king’s commandment, and the\l"
    .string "decree was given in Shushan the\l"
    .string "palace. And the king and Haman sat\l"
    .string "down to drink; but the city Shushan\l"
    .string "was perplexed.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_1::
    .string "When Mordecai perceived all that\n"
    .string "was done, Mordecai rent his clothes,\l"
    .string "and put on sackcloth with ashes, and\l"
    .string "went out into the midst of the city,\l"
    .string "and cried with a loud and a bitter\l"
    .string "cry;"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_2::
    .string "And came even before the king’s\n"
    .string "gate: for none might enter into the\l"
    .string "king’s gate clothed with sackcloth$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_3::
    .string "And in every province,\n"
    .string "whithersoever the king’s commandment\l"
    .string "and his decree came, there was great\l"
    .string "mourning among the Jews, and fasting,\l"
    .string "and weeping, and wailing; and many\l"
    .string "lay in sackcloth and ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_4::
    .string "So Esther’s maids and her\n"
    .string "chamberlains came and told it her.\l"
    .string "Then was the queen exceedingly\l"
    .string "grieved; and she sent raiment to\l"
    .string "clothe Mordecai, and to take away\l"
    .string "his sackcloth from him: but he\l"
    .string "received it not.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_5::
    .string "Then called Esther for Hatach, one\n"
    .string "of the king’s chamberlains, whom he\l"
    .string "had appointed to attend upon her,\l"
    .string "and gave him a commandment to\l"
    .string "Mordecai, to know what it was, and\l"
    .string "why it was.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_6::
    .string "So Hatach went forth to Mordecai\n"
    .string "unto the street of the city, which\l"
    .string "was before the king’s gate.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_7::
    .string "And Mordecai told him of all that\n"
    .string "had happened unto him, and of the\l"
    .string "sum of the money that Haman had\l"
    .string "promised to pay to the king’s\l"
    .string "treasuries for the Jews, to destroy\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_8::
    .string "Also he gave him the copy of the\n"
    .string "writing of the decree that was given\l"
    .string "at Shushan to destroy them, to shew\l"
    .string "it unto Esther, and to declare it\l"
    .string "unto her, and to charge her that she\l"
    .string "should go in unto the king, to make\l"
    .string "supplication unto him, and to make\l"
    .string "request before him for her people.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_9::
    .string "And Hatach came and told Esther the\n"
    .string "words of Mordecai.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_10::
    .string "Again Esther spake unto Hatach, and\n"
    .string "gave him commandment unto Mordecai;"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_11::
    .string "All the king’s servants, and the\n"
    .string "people of the king’s provinces, do\l"
    .string "know, that whosoever, whether man or\l"
    .string "woman, shall come unto the king into\l"
    .string "the inner court, who is not called,\l"
    .string "there is one law of his to put him\l"
    .string "to death, except such to whom the\l"
    .string "king shall hold out the golden\l"
    .string "sceptre, that he may live: but I\l"
    .string "have not been called to come in unto\l"
    .string "the king these thirty days$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_12::
    .string "And they told to Mordecai Esther’s\n"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_13::
    .string "Then Mordecai commanded to answer\n"
    .string "Esther, Think not with thyself that\l"
    .string "thou shalt escape in the king’s\l"
    .string "house, more than all the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_14::
    .string "For if thou altogether holdest thy\n"
    .string "peace at this time, then shall there\l"
    .string "enlargement and deliverance arise\l"
    .string "to the Jews from another place; but\l"
    .string "thou and thy father’s house shall\l"
    .string "be destroyed: and who knoweth whether\l"
    .string "thou art come to the kingdom for such\l"
    .string "a time as this?"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_15::
    .string "Then Esther bade them return\n"
    .string "Mordecai this answer,"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_16::
    .string "Go, gather together all the Jews\n"
    .string "that are present in Shushan, and\l"
    .string "fast ye for me, and neither eat nor\l"
    .string "drink three days, night or day: I\l"
    .string "also and my maidens will fast\l"
    .string "likewise; and so will I go in unto\l"
    .string "the king, which is not according to\l"
    .string "the law: and if I perish, I perish$"
Bible_Text_Esther_4_17::
    .string "So Mordecai went his way, and did\n"
    .string "according to all that Esther had\l"
    .string "commanded him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass on the third\n"
    .string "day, that Esther put on her royal\l"
    .string "apparel, and stood in the inner\l"
    .string "court of the king’s house, over\l"
    .string "against the king’s house: and the\l"
    .string "king sat upon his royal throne in\l"
    .string "the royal house, over against the\l"
    .string "gate of the house.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_2::
    .string "And it was so, when the king saw\n"
    .string "Esther the queen standing in the\l"
    .string "court, that she obtained favour in\l"
    .string "his sight: and the king held out to\l"
    .string "Esther the golden sceptre that was\l"
    .string "in his hand. So Esther drew near, and\l"
    .string "touched the top of the sceptre.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_3::
    .string "Then said the king unto her, What\n"
    .string "wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is\l"
    .string "thy request? it shall be even given\l"
    .string "thee to the half of the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_4::
    .string "And Esther answered, If it seem good\n"
    .string "unto the king, let the king and Haman\l"
    .string "come this day unto the banquet that I\l"
    .string "have prepared for him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_5::
    .string "Then the king said, Cause Haman to\n"
    .string "make haste, that he may do as Esther\l"
    .string "hath said. So the king and Haman came\l"
    .string "to the banquet that Esther had\l"
    .string "prepared.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_6::
    .string "And the king said unto Esther at the\n"
    .string "banquet of wine, What is thy\l"
    .string "petition? and it shall be granted\l"
    .string "thee: and what is thy request? even\l"
    .string "to the half of the kingdom it shall\l"
    .string "be performed.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_7::
    .string "Then answered Esther, and said, My\n"
    .string "petition and my request is;"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_8::
    .string "If I have found favour in the sight\n"
    .string "of the king, and if it please the\l"
    .string "king to grant my petition, and to\l"
    .string "perform my request, let the king and\l"
    .string "Haman come to the banquet that I\l"
    .string "shall prepare for them, and I\l"
    .string "will do to morrow as the king hath\l"
    .string "said$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_9::
    .string "Then went Haman forth that day\n"
    .string "joyful and with a glad heart: but\l"
    .string "when Haman saw Mordecai in the king’s\l"
    .string "gate, that he stood not up, nor moved\l"
    .string "for him, he was full of indignation\l"
    .string "against Mordecai.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_10::
    .string "Nevertheless Haman refrained\n"
    .string "himself: and when he came home, he\l"
    .string "sent and called for his friends, and\l"
    .string "Zeresh his wife.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_11::
    .string "And Haman told them of the glory of\n"
    .string "his riches, and the multitude of his\l"
    .string "children, and all the things\l"
    .string "wherein the king had promoted him,\l"
    .string "and how he had advanced him above the\l"
    .string "princes and servants of the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_12::
    .string "Haman said moreover, Yea, Esther the\n"
    .string "queen did let no man come in with the\l"
    .string "king unto the banquet that she had\l"
    .string "prepared but myself; and to morrow\l"
    .string "am I invited unto her also with the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_13::
    .string "Yet all this availeth me nothing,\n"
    .string "so long as I see Mordecai the Jew\l"
    .string "sitting at the king’s gate.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_5_14::
    .string "Then said Zeresh his wife and all\n"
    .string "his friends unto him, Let a gallows\l"
    .string "be made of fifty cubits high, and to\l"
    .string "morrow speak thou unto the king that\l"
    .string "Mordecai may be hanged thereon: then\l"
    .string "go thou in merrily with the king\l"
    .string "unto the banquet. And the thing\l"
    .string "pleased Haman; and he caused the\l"
    .string "gallows to be made.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_1::
    .string "On that night could not the king\n"
    .string "sleep, and he commanded to bring the\l"
    .string "book of records of the chronicles;\l"
    .string "and they were read before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_2::
    .string "And it was found written, that\n"
    .string "Mordecai had told of Bigthana and\l"
    .string "Teresh, two of the king’s\l"
    .string "chamberlains, the keepers of the\l"
    .string "door, who sought to lay hand on the\l"
    .string "king Ahasuerus.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_3::
    .string "And the king said, What honour and\n"
    .string "dignity hath been done to Mordecai\l"
    .string "for this? Then said the king’s\l"
    .string "servants that ministered unto him,\l"
    .string "There is nothing done for him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_4::
    .string "And the king said, Who is in the\n"
    .string "court? Now Haman was come into the\l"
    .string "outward court of the king’s house, to\l"
    .string "speak unto the king to hang Mordecai\l"
    .string "on the gallows that he had\l"
    .string "prepared for him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_5::
    .string "And the king’s servants said unto\n"
    .string "him, Behold, Haman standeth in the\l"
    .string "court. And the king said, Let him\l"
    .string "come in.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_6::
    .string "So Haman came in. And the king said\n"
    .string "unto him, What shall be done unto\l"
    .string "the man whom the king delighteth to\l"
    .string "honour? Now Haman thought in his\l"
    .string "heart, To whom would the king\l"
    .string "delight to do honour more than to\l"
    .string "myself?"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_7::
    .string "And Haman answered the king, For the\n"
    .string "man whom the king delighteth to\l"
    .string "honour,"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_8::
    .string "Let the royal apparel be brought\n"
    .string "which the king useth to wear, and the\l"
    .string "horse that the king rideth upon, and\l"
    .string "the crown royal which is set upon\l"
    .string "his head:"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_9::
    .string "And let this apparel and horse be\n"
    .string "delivered to the hand of one of the\l"
    .string "king’s most noble princes, that\l"
    .string "they may array the man withal whom\l"
    .string "the king delighteth to honour, and\l"
    .string "bring him on horseback through the\l"
    .string "street of the city, and proclaim\l"
    .string "before him, Thus shall it be done to\l"
    .string "the man whom the king delighteth to\l"
    .string "honour$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_10::
    .string "Then the king said to Haman, Make\n"
    .string "haste, and take the apparel and the\l"
    .string "horse, as thou hast said, and do even\l"
    .string "so to Mordecai the Jew, that sitteth\l"
    .string "at the king’s gate: let nothing fail\l"
    .string "of all that thou hast spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_11::
    .string "Then took Haman the apparel and\n"
    .string "the horse, and arrayed Mordecai, and\l"
    .string "brought him on horseback through the\l"
    .string "street of the city, and proclaimed\l"
    .string "before him, Thus shall it be done\l"
    .string "unto the man whom the king\l"
    .string "delighteth to honour.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_12::
    .string "And Mordecai came again to the\n"
    .string "king’s gate. But Haman hasted to his\l"
    .string "house mourning, and having his head\l"
    .string "covered.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_13::
    .string "And Haman told Zeresh his wife and\n"
    .string "all his friends every thing that\l"
    .string "had befallen him. Then said his wise\l"
    .string "men and Zeresh his wife unto him, If\l"
    .string "Mordecai be of the seed of the Jews,\l"
    .string "before whom thou hast begun to fall,\l"
    .string "thou shalt not prevail against him,\l"
    .string "but shalt surely fall before him.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_6_14::
    .string "And while they were yet talking\n"
    .string "with him, came the king’s\l"
    .string "chamberlains, and hasted to bring\l"
    .string "Haman unto the banquet that Esther\l"
    .string "had prepared.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_1::
    .string "So the king and Haman came to\n"
    .string "banquet with Esther the queen.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_2::
    .string "And the king said again unto Esther\n"
    .string "on the second day at the banquet of\l"
    .string "wine, What is thy petition, queen\l"
    .string "Esther? and it shall be granted\l"
    .string "thee: and what is thy request? and it\l"
    .string "shall be performed, even to the\l"
    .string "half of the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_3::
    .string "Then Esther the queen answered and\n"
    .string "said, If I have found favour in thy\l"
    .string "sight, O king, and if it please the\l"
    .string "king, let my life be given me at my\l"
    .string "petition, and my people at my\l"
    .string "request:"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_4::
    .string "For we are sold, I and my people,\n"
    .string "to be destroyed, to be slain, and to\l"
    .string "perish. But if we had been sold for\l"
    .string "bondmen and bondwomen, I had held my\l"
    .string "tongue, although the enemy could\l"
    .string "not countervail the king’s damage$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_5::
    .string "Then the king Ahasuerus answered\n"
    .string "and said unto Esther the queen, Who\l"
    .string "is he, and where is he, that durst\l"
    .string "presume in his heart to do so?"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_6::
    .string "And Esther said, The adversary and\n"
    .string "enemy is this wicked Haman. Then\l"
    .string "Haman was afraid before the king and\l"
    .string "the queen$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_7::
    .string "And the king arising from the\n"
    .string "banquet of wine in his wrath went\l"
    .string "into the palace garden: and Haman\l"
    .string "stood up to make request for his\l"
    .string "life to Esther the queen; for he saw\l"
    .string "that there was evil determined\l"
    .string "against him by the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_8::
    .string "Then the king returned out of the\n"
    .string "palace garden into the place of the\l"
    .string "banquet of wine; and Haman was\l"
    .string "fallen upon the bed whereon Esther\l"
    .string "was. Then said the king, Will he\l"
    .string "force the queen also before me in\l"
    .string "the house? As the word went out of the\l"
    .string "king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s\l"
    .string "face.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_9::
    .string "And Harbonah, one of the\n"
    .string "chamberlains, said before the king,\l"
    .string "Behold also, the gallows fifty\l"
    .string "cubits high, which Haman had made for\l"
    .string "Mordecai, who had spoken good for\l"
    .string "the king, standeth in the house of\l"
    .string "Haman. Then the king said, Hang him\l"
    .string "thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_7_10::
    .string "So they hanged Haman on the\n"
    .string "gallows that he had prepared for\l"
    .string "Mordecai. Then was the king’s wrath\l"
    .string "pacified.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_1::
    .string "On that day did the king Ahasuerus\n"
    .string "give the house of Haman the Jews’\l"
    .string "enemy unto Esther the queen. And\l"
    .string "Mordecai came before the king; for\l"
    .string "Esther had told what he was unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_2::
    .string "And the king took off his ring,\n"
    .string "which he had taken from Haman, and\l"
    .string "gave it unto Mordecai. And Esther set\l"
    .string "Mordecai over the house of Haman.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_3::
    .string "And Esther spake yet again before\n"
    .string "the king, and fell down at his feet,\l"
    .string "and besought him with tears to put\l"
    .string "away the mischief of Haman the\l"
    .string "Agagite, and his device that he had\l"
    .string "devised against the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_4::
    .string "Then the king held out the golden\n"
    .string "sceptre toward Esther. So Esther\l"
    .string "arose, and stood before the king,"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_5::
    .string "And said, If it please the king,\n"
    .string "and if I have favour in his sight, and\l"
    .string "the thing seem right before the king,\l"
    .string "and I be pleasing in his eyes, let\l"
    .string "it be written to reverse the letters\l"
    .string "devised by Haman the son of\l"
    .string "Hammedatha the Agagite, which he\l"
    .string "wrote to destroy the Jews which are\l"
    .string "in all the king’s provinces:"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_6::
    .string "For how can I endure to see the evil\n"
    .string "that shall come unto my people? or\l"
    .string "how can I endure to see the\l"
    .string "destruction of my kindred?"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_7::
    .string "Then the king Ahasuerus said unto\n"
    .string "Esther the queen and to Mordecai the\l"
    .string "Jew, Behold, I have given Esther the\l"
    .string "house of Haman, and him they have\l"
    .string "hanged upon the gallows, because he\l"
    .string "laid his hand upon the Jews$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_8::
    .string "Write ye also for the Jews, as it\n"
    .string "liketh you, in the king’s name, and\l"
    .string "seal it with the king’s ring: for the\l"
    .string "writing which is written in the\l"
    .string "king’s name, and sealed with the\l"
    .string "king’s ring, may no man reverse.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_9::
    .string "Then were the king’s scribes\n"
    .string "called at that time in the third\l"
    .string "month, that is, the month Sivan, on\l"
    .string "the three and twentieth day thereof;\l"
    .string "and it was written according to all\l"
    .string "that Mordecai commanded unto the\l"
    .string "Jews, and to the lieutenants, and\l"
    .string "the deputies and rulers of the\l"
    .string "provinces which are from India unto\l"
    .string "Ethiopia, an hundred twenty and\l"
    .string "seven provinces, unto every\l"
    .string "province according to the writing\l"
    .string "thereof, and unto every people\l"
    .string "after their language, and to the\l"
    .string "Jews according to their writing, and\l"
    .string "according to their language.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_10::
    .string "And he wrote in the king Ahasuerus’\n"
    .string "name, and sealed it with the king’s\l"
    .string "ring, and sent letters by posts on\l"
    .string "horseback, and riders on mules,\l"
    .string "camels, and young dromedaries:"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_11::
    .string "Wherein the king granted the Jews\n"
    .string "which were in every city to gather\l"
    .string "themselves together, and to stand\l"
    .string "for their life, to destroy, to slay\l"
    .string "and to cause to perish, all the\l"
    .string "power of the people and province\l"
    .string "that would assault them, both\l"
    .string "little ones and women, and to take\l"
    .string "the spoil of them for a prey,"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_12::
    .string "Upon one day in all the provinces\n"
    .string "of king Ahasuerus, namely, upon the\l"
    .string "thirteenth day of the twelfth month,\l"
    .string "which is the month Adar$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_13::
    .string "The copy of the writing for a\n"
    .string "commandment to be given in every\l"
    .string "province was published unto all\l"
    .string "people, and that the Jews should be\l"
    .string "ready against that day to avenge\l"
    .string "themselves on their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_14::
    .string "So the posts that rode upon mules\n"
    .string "and camels went out, being hastened\l"
    .string "and pressed on by the king’s\l"
    .string "commandment. And the decree was given\l"
    .string "at Shushan the palace.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_15::
    .string "And Mordecai went out from the\n"
    .string "presence of the king in royal\l"
    .string "apparel of blue and white, and\l"
    .string "with a great crown of gold, and with\l"
    .string "a garment of fine linen and\l"
    .string "purple: and the city of Shushan\l"
    .string "rejoiced and was glad.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_16::
    .string "The Jews had light, and gladness,\n"
    .string "and joy, and honour.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_8_17::
    .string "And in every province, and in every\n"
    .string "city, whithersoever the king’s\l"
    .string "commandment and his decree came, the\l"
    .string "Jews had joy and gladness, a feast\l"
    .string "and a good day. And many of the\l"
    .string "people of the land became Jews; for\l"
    .string "the fear of the Jews fell upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_1::
    .string "Now in the twelfth month, that is,\n"
    .string "the month Adar, on the thirteenth day\l"
    .string "of the same, when the king’s\l"
    .string "commandment and his decree drew near\l"
    .string "to be put in execution, in the day\l"
    .string "that the enemies of the Jews hoped\l"
    .string "to have power over them, (though it\l"
    .string "was turned to the contrary, that the\l"
    .string "Jews had rule over them that hated\l"
    .string "them;)"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_2::
    .string "The Jews gathered themselves\n"
    .string "together in their cities throughout\l"
    .string "all the provinces of the king\l"
    .string "Ahasuerus, to lay hand on such as\l"
    .string "sought their hurt: and no man could\l"
    .string "withstand them; for the fear of them\l"
    .string "fell upon all people$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_3::
    .string "And all the rulers of the\n"
    .string "provinces, and the lieutenants, and\l"
    .string "the deputies, and officers of the\l"
    .string "king, helped the Jews; because the\l"
    .string "fear of Mordecai fell upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_4::
    .string "For Mordecai was great in the king’s\n"
    .string "house, and his fame went out\l"
    .string "throughout all the provinces: for\l"
    .string "this man Mordecai waxed greater and\l"
    .string "greater.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_5::
    .string "Thus the Jews smote all their\n"
    .string "enemies with the stroke of the sword,\l"
    .string "and slaughter, and destruction, and\l"
    .string "did what they would unto those that\l"
    .string "hated them.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_6::
    .string "And in Shushan the palace the Jews\n"
    .string "slew and destroyed five hundred men.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_7::
    .string "And Parshandatha, and Dalphon, and\n"
    .string "Aspatha,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_8::
    .string "And Poratha, and Adalia, and\n"
    .string "Aridatha,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_9::
    .string "And Parmashta, and Arisai, and\n"
    .string "Aridai, and Vajezatha,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_10::
    .string "The ten sons of Haman the son of\n"
    .string "Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews,\l"
    .string "slew they; but on the spoil laid\l"
    .string "they not their hand$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_11::
    .string "On that day the number of those that\n"
    .string "were slain in Shushan the palace\l"
    .string "was brought before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_12::
    .string "And the king said unto Esther the\n"
    .string "queen, The Jews have slain and\l"
    .string "destroyed five hundred men in\l"
    .string "Shushan the palace, and the ten sons\l"
    .string "of Haman; what have they done in the\l"
    .string "rest of the king’s provinces? now\l"
    .string "what is thy petition? and it shall\l"
    .string "be granted thee: or what is thy\l"
    .string "request further? and it shall be\l"
    .string "done.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_13::
    .string "Then said Esther, If it please the\n"
    .string "king, let it be granted to the Jews\l"
    .string "which are in Shushan to do to morrow\l"
    .string "also according unto this day’s\l"
    .string "decree, and let Haman’s ten sons be\l"
    .string "hanged upon the gallows.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_14::
    .string "And the king commanded it so to be\n"
    .string "done: and the decree was given at\l"
    .string "Shushan; and they hanged Haman’s ten\l"
    .string "sons.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_15::
    .string "For the Jews that were in Shushan\n"
    .string "gathered themselves together on the\l"
    .string "fourteenth day also of the month\l"
    .string "Adar, and slew three hundred men at\l"
    .string "Shushan; but on the prey they laid\l"
    .string "not their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_16::
    .string "But the other Jews that were in the\n"
    .string "king’s provinces gathered\l"
    .string "themselves together, and stood for\l"
    .string "their lives, and had rest from their\l"
    .string "enemies, and slew of their foes\l"
    .string "seventy and five thousand, but they\l"
    .string "laid not their hands on the prey,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_17::
    .string "On the thirteenth day of the month\n"
    .string "Adar; and on the fourteenth day of\l"
    .string "the same rested they, and made it a\l"
    .string "day of feasting and gladness$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_18::
    .string "But the Jews that were at Shushan\n"
    .string "assembled together on the\l"
    .string "thirteenth day thereof, and on the\l"
    .string "fourteenth thereof; and on the\l"
    .string "fifteenth day of the same they\l"
    .string "rested, and made it a day of feasting\l"
    .string "and gladness.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_19::
    .string "Therefore the Jews of the\n"
    .string "villages, that dwelt in the\l"
    .string "unwalled towns, made the fourteenth\l"
    .string "day of the month Adar a day of\l"
    .string "gladness and feasting, and a good\l"
    .string "day, and of sending portions one to\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_20::
    .string "And Mordecai wrote these things, and\n"
    .string "sent letters unto all the Jews that\l"
    .string "were in all the provinces of the\l"
    .string "king Ahasuerus, both nigh and far,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_21::
    .string "To stablish this among them, that\n"
    .string "they should keep the fourteenth day\l"
    .string "of the month Adar, and the fifteenth\l"
    .string "day of the same, yearly,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_22::
    .string "As the days wherein the Jews rested\n"
    .string "from their enemies, and the month\l"
    .string "which was turned unto them from\l"
    .string "sorrow to joy, and from mourning into\l"
    .string "a good day: that they should make\l"
    .string "them days of feasting and joy, and of\l"
    .string "sending portions one to another, and\l"
    .string "gifts to the poor$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_23::
    .string "And the Jews undertook to do as they\n"
    .string "had begun, and as Mordecai had\l"
    .string "written unto them;"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_24::
    .string "Because Haman the son of Hammedatha,\n"
    .string "the Agagite, the enemy of all the\l"
    .string "Jews, had devised against the Jews to\l"
    .string "destroy them, and had cast Pur, that\l"
    .string "is, the lot, to consume them, and to\l"
    .string "destroy them;"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_25::
    .string "But when Esther came before the\n"
    .string "king, he commanded by letters that\l"
    .string "his wicked device, which he devised\l"
    .string "against the Jews, should return\l"
    .string "upon his own head, and that he and\l"
    .string "his sons should be hanged on the\l"
    .string "gallows$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_26::
    .string "Wherefore they called these days\n"
    .string "Purim after the name of Pur.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_27::
    .string "The Jews ordained, and took upon\n"
    .string "them, and upon their seed, and upon\l"
    .string "all such as joined themselves unto\l"
    .string "them, so as it should not fail, that\l"
    .string "they would keep these two days\l"
    .string "according to their writing, and\l"
    .string "according to their appointed time\l"
    .string "every year;"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_28::
    .string "And that these days should be\n"
    .string "remembered and kept throughout\l"
    .string "every generation, every family,\l"
    .string "every province, and every city; and\l"
    .string "that these days of Purim should not\l"
    .string "fail from among the Jews, nor the\l"
    .string "memorial of them perish from their\l"
    .string "seed$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_29::
    .string "Then Esther the queen, the daughter\n"
    .string "of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew,\l"
    .string "wrote with all authority, to\l"
    .string "confirm this second letter of Purim.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_30::
    .string "And he sent the letters unto all\n"
    .string "the Jews, to the hundred twenty and\l"
    .string "seven provinces of the kingdom of\l"
    .string "Ahasuerus, with words of peace and\l"
    .string "truth,"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_31::
    .string "To confirm these days of Purim in\n"
    .string "their times appointed, according as\l"
    .string "Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen\l"
    .string "had enjoined them, and as they had\l"
    .string "decreed for themselves and for their\l"
    .string "seed, the matters of the fastings and\l"
    .string "their cry$"
Bible_Text_Esther_9_32::
    .string "And the decree of Esther confirmed\n"
    .string "these matters of Purim; and it was\l"
    .string "written in the book.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_10_1::
    .string "And the king Ahasuerus laid a\n"
    .string "tribute upon the land, and upon the\l"
    .string "isles of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Esther_10_2::
    .string "And all the acts of his power and\n"
    .string "of his might, and the declaration of\l"
    .string "the greatness of Mordecai, whereunto\l"
    .string "the king advanced him, are they not\l"
    .string "written in the book of the\l"
    .string "chronicles of the kings of Media and\l"
    .string "Persia?"
Bible_Text_Esther_10_3::
    .string "For Mordecai the Jew was next unto\n"
    .string "king Ahasuerus, and great among the\l"
    .string "Jews, and accepted of the multitude\l"
    .string "of his brethren, seeking the wealth\l"
    .string "of his people, and speaking peace\l"
    .string "to all his seed$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_1::
    .string "There was a man in the land of Uz,\n"
    .string "whose name was Job; and that man was\l"
    .string "perfect and upright, and one that\l"
    .string "feared God, and eschewed evil.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_2::
    .string "And there were born unto him seven\n"
    .string "sons and three daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_3::
    .string "His substance also was seven\n"
    .string "thousand sheep, and three thousand\l"
    .string "camels, and five hundred yoke of\l"
    .string "oxen, and five hundred she asses, and\l"
    .string "a very great household; so that this\l"
    .string "man was the greatest of all the men\l"
    .string "of the east.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_4::
    .string "And his sons went and feasted in\n"
    .string "their houses, every one his day; and\l"
    .string "sent and called for their three\l"
    .string "sisters to eat and to drink with them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_5::
    .string "And it was so, when the days of their\n"
    .string "feasting were gone about, that Job\l"
    .string "sent and sanctified them, and rose\l"
    .string "up early in the morning, and offered\l"
    .string "burnt offerings according to the\l"
    .string "number of them all: for Job said, It\l"
    .string "may be that my sons have sinned, and\l"
    .string "cursed God in their hearts. Thus did\l"
    .string "Job continually.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_6::
    .string "Now there was a day when the sons of\n"
    .string "God came to present themselves\l"
    .string "before the LORD, and Satan came also\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_7::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan, Whence\n"
    .string "comest thou? Then Satan answered the\l"
    .string "LORD, and said, From going to and fro\l"
    .string "in the earth, and from walking up\l"
    .string "and down in it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_8::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast\n"
    .string "thou considered my servant Job, that\l"
    .string "there is none like him in the earth,\l"
    .string "a perfect and an upright man, one\l"
    .string "that feareth God, and escheweth\l"
    .string "evil?"
Bible_Text_Job_1_9::
    .string "Then Satan answered the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, Doth Job fear God for nought?"
Bible_Text_Job_1_10::
    .string "Hast not thou made an hedge about\n"
    .string "him, and about his house, and about\l"
    .string "all that he hath on every side? thou\l"
    .string "hast blessed the work of his hands,\l"
    .string "and his substance is increased in the\l"
    .string "land$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_11::
    .string "But put forth thine hand now, and\n"
    .string "touch all that he hath, and he will\l"
    .string "curse thee to thy face.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_12::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan,\n"
    .string "Behold, all that he hath is in thy\l"
    .string "power; only upon himself put not\l"
    .string "forth thine hand. So Satan went forth\l"
    .string "from the presence of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_13::
    .string "And there was a day when his sons\n"
    .string "and his daughters were eating and\l"
    .string "drinking wine in their eldest\l"
    .string "brother’s house:"
Bible_Text_Job_1_14::
    .string "And there came a messenger unto Job,\n"
    .string "and said, The oxen were plowing, and\l"
    .string "the asses feeding beside them:"
Bible_Text_Job_1_15::
    .string "And the Sabeans fell upon them,\n"
    .string "and took them away; yea, they have\l"
    .string "slain the servants with the edge of\l"
    .string "the sword; and I only am escaped\l"
    .string "alone to tell thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_16::
    .string "While he was yet speaking, there\n"
    .string "came also another, and said, The\l"
    .string "fire of God is fallen from heaven,\l"
    .string "and hath burned up the sheep, and\l"
    .string "the servants, and consumed them; and\l"
    .string "I only am escaped alone to tell\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_17::
    .string "While he was yet speaking, there\n"
    .string "came also another, and said, The\l"
    .string "Chaldeans made out three bands, and\l"
    .string "fell upon the camels, and have\l"
    .string "carried them away, yea, and slain\l"
    .string "the servants with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword; and I only am escaped alone\l"
    .string "to tell thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_18::
    .string "While he was yet speaking, there\n"
    .string "came also another, and said, Thy\l"
    .string "sons and thy daughters were eating\l"
    .string "and drinking wine in their eldest\l"
    .string "brother’s house:"
Bible_Text_Job_1_19::
    .string "And, behold, there came a great\n"
    .string "wind from the wilderness, and smote\l"
    .string "the four corners of the house, and it\l"
    .string "fell upon the young men, and they\l"
    .string "are dead; and I only am escaped\l"
    .string "alone to tell thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_20::
    .string "Then Job arose, and rent his\n"
    .string "mantle, and shaved his head, and\l"
    .string "fell down upon the ground, and\l"
    .string "worshipped,"
Bible_Text_Job_1_21::
    .string "And said, Naked came I out of my\n"
    .string "mother’s womb, and naked shall I\l"
    .string "return thither: the LORD gave, and\l"
    .string "the LORD hath taken away; blessed be\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Job_1_22::
    .string "In all this Job sinned not, nor\n"
    .string "charged God foolishly.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_1::
    .string "Again there was a day when the sons\n"
    .string "of God came to present themselves\l"
    .string "before the LORD, and Satan came also\l"
    .string "among them to present himself\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan, From\n"
    .string "whence comest thou? And Satan\l"
    .string "answered the LORD, and said, From\l"
    .string "going to and fro in the earth, and\l"
    .string "from walking up and down in it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_3::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast\n"
    .string "thou considered my servant Job, that\l"
    .string "there is none like him in the earth,\l"
    .string "a perfect and an upright man, one\l"
    .string "that feareth God, and escheweth\l"
    .string "evil? and still he holdeth fast\l"
    .string "his integrity, although thou movedst\l"
    .string "me against him, to destroy him\l"
    .string "without cause.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_4::
    .string "And Satan answered the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, Skin for skin, yea, all that a\l"
    .string "man hath will he give for his life.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_5::
    .string "But put forth thine hand now, and\n"
    .string "touch his bone and his flesh, and he\l"
    .string "will curse thee to thy face.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_6::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan,\n"
    .string "Behold, he is in thine hand; but save\l"
    .string "his life.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_7::
    .string "So went Satan forth from the\n"
    .string "presence of the LORD, and smote Job\l"
    .string "with sore boils from the sole of his\l"
    .string "foot unto his crown.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_8::
    .string "And he took him a potsherd to\n"
    .string "scrape himself withal; and he sat\l"
    .string "down among the ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_9::
    .string "Then said his wife unto him, Dost\n"
    .string "thou still retain thine integrity?\l"
    .string "curse God, and die.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_10::
    .string "But he said unto her, Thou speakest\n"
    .string "as one of the foolish women speaketh\l"
    .string " What? shall we receive good at the\l"
    .string "hand of God, and shall we not\l"
    .string "receive evil? In all this did not\l"
    .string "Job sin with his lips.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_11::
    .string "Now when Job’s three friends heard\n"
    .string "of all this evil that was come\l"
    .string "upon him, they came every one from\l"
    .string "his own place; Eliphaz the\l"
    .string "Temanite, and Bildad the Shuhite,\l"
    .string "and Zophar the Naamathite: for they\l"
    .string "had made an appointment together to\l"
    .string "come to mourn with him and to comfort\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_12::
    .string "And when they lifted up their eyes\n"
    .string "afar off, and knew him not, they\l"
    .string "lifted up their voice, and wept; and\l"
    .string "they rent every one his mantle, and\l"
    .string "sprinkled dust upon their heads\l"
    .string "toward heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Job_2_13::
    .string "So they sat down with him upon the\n"
    .string "ground seven days and seven nights,\l"
    .string "and none spake a word unto him: for\l"
    .string "they saw that his grief was very\l"
    .string "great.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_1::
    .string "After this opened Job his mouth,\n"
    .string "and cursed his day.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_2::
    .string "And Job spake, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_3_3::
    .string "Let the day perish wherein I was\n"
    .string "born, and the night in which it was\l"
    .string "said, There is a man child conceived$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_4::
    .string "Let that day be darkness; let not\n"
    .string "God regard it from above, neither\l"
    .string "let the light shine upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_5::
    .string "Let darkness and the shadow of death\n"
    .string "stain it; let a cloud dwell upon\l"
    .string "it; let the blackness of the day\l"
    .string "terrify it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_6::
    .string "As for that night, let darkness\n"
    .string "seize upon it; let it not be joined\l"
    .string "unto the days of the year, let it not\l"
    .string "come into the number of the months.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_7::
    .string "Lo, let that night be solitary,\n"
    .string "let no joyful voice come therein.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_8::
    .string "Let them curse it that curse the\n"
    .string "day, who are ready to raise up their\l"
    .string "mourning.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_9::
    .string "Let the stars of the twilight\n"
    .string "thereof be dark; let it look for\l"
    .string "light, but have none; neither let it\l"
    .string "see the dawning of the day:"
Bible_Text_Job_3_10::
    .string "Because it shut not up the doors of\n"
    .string "my mother’s womb, nor hid sorrow from\l"
    .string "mine eyes$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_11::
    .string "Why died I not from the womb? why did\n"
    .string "I not give up the ghost when I came\l"
    .string "out of the belly?"
Bible_Text_Job_3_12::
    .string "Why did the knees prevent me? or why\n"
    .string "the breasts that I should suck?"
Bible_Text_Job_3_13::
    .string "For now should I have lain still\n"
    .string "and been quiet, I should have\l"
    .string "slept: then had I been at rest,"
Bible_Text_Job_3_14::
    .string "With kings and counsellors of the\n"
    .string "earth, which build desolate places\l"
    .string "for themselves;"
Bible_Text_Job_3_15::
    .string "Or with princes that had gold, who\n"
    .string "filled their houses with silver:"
Bible_Text_Job_3_16::
    .string "Or as an hidden untimely birth I\n"
    .string "had not been; as infants which never\l"
    .string "saw light$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_17::
    .string "There the wicked cease from\n"
    .string "troubling; and there the weary be at\l"
    .string "rest.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_18::
    .string "There the prisoners rest together;\n"
    .string "they hear not the voice of the\l"
    .string "oppressor.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_19::
    .string "The small and great are there; and\n"
    .string "the servant is free from his master.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_20::
    .string "Wherefore is light given to him\n"
    .string "that is in misery, and life unto the\l"
    .string "bitter in soul;"
Bible_Text_Job_3_21::
    .string "Which long for death, but it cometh\n"
    .string "not; and dig for it more than for hid\l"
    .string "treasures;"
Bible_Text_Job_3_22::
    .string "Which rejoice exceedingly, and are\n"
    .string "glad, when they can find the grave?"
Bible_Text_Job_3_23::
    .string "Why is light given to a man whose\n"
    .string "way is hid, and whom God hath hedged\l"
    .string "in?"
Bible_Text_Job_3_24::
    .string "For my sighing cometh before I eat,\n"
    .string "and my roarings are poured out like\l"
    .string "the waters$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_25::
    .string "For the thing which I greatly\n"
    .string "feared is come upon me, and that\l"
    .string "which I was afraid of is come unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_3_26::
    .string "I was not in safety, neither had I\n"
    .string "rest, neither was I quiet; yet\l"
    .string "trouble came.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_1::
    .string "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered\n"
    .string "and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_4_2::
    .string "If we assay to commune with thee,\n"
    .string "wilt thou be grieved? but who can\l"
    .string "withhold himself from speaking?"
Bible_Text_Job_4_3::
    .string "Behold, thou hast instructed many,\n"
    .string "and thou hast strengthened the weak\l"
    .string "hands$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_4::
    .string "Thy words have upholden him that\n"
    .string "was falling, and thou hast\l"
    .string "strengthened the feeble knees.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_5::
    .string "But now it is come upon thee, and\n"
    .string "thou faintest; it toucheth thee, and\l"
    .string "thou art troubled.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_6::
    .string "Is not this thy fear, thy\n"
    .string "confidence, thy hope, and the\l"
    .string "uprightness of thy ways?"
Bible_Text_Job_4_7::
    .string "Remember, I pray thee, who ever\n"
    .string "perished, being innocent? or where\l"
    .string "were the righteous cut off?"
Bible_Text_Job_4_8::
    .string "Even as I have seen, they that plow\n"
    .string "iniquity, and sow wickedness, reap\l"
    .string "the same$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_9::
    .string "By the blast of God they perish,\n"
    .string "and by the breath of his nostrils\l"
    .string "are they consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_10::
    .string "The roaring of the lion, and the\n"
    .string "voice of the fierce lion, and the\l"
    .string "teeth of the young lions, are broken.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_11::
    .string "The old lion perisheth for lack\n"
    .string "of prey, and the stout lion’s\l"
    .string "whelps are scattered abroad.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_12::
    .string "Now a thing was secretly brought to\n"
    .string "me, and mine ear received a little\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_13::
    .string "In thoughts from the visions of the\n"
    .string "night, when deep sleep falleth on\l"
    .string "men,"
Bible_Text_Job_4_14::
    .string "Fear came upon me, and trembling,\n"
    .string "which made all my bones to shake$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_15::
    .string "Then a spirit passed before my\n"
    .string "face; the hair of my flesh stood up:"
Bible_Text_Job_4_16::
    .string "It stood still, but I could not\n"
    .string "discern the form thereof: an image\l"
    .string "was before mine eyes, there was\l"
    .string "silence, and I heard a voice, saying,"
Bible_Text_Job_4_17::
    .string "Shall mortal man be more just than\n"
    .string "God? shall a man be more pure than\l"
    .string "his maker?"
Bible_Text_Job_4_18::
    .string "Behold, he put no trust in his\n"
    .string "servants; and his angels he charged\l"
    .string "with folly:"
Bible_Text_Job_4_19::
    .string "How much less in them that dwell\n"
    .string "in houses of clay, whose foundation\l"
    .string "is in the dust, which are crushed\l"
    .string "before the moth?"
Bible_Text_Job_4_20::
    .string "They are destroyed from morning to\n"
    .string "evening: they perish for ever\l"
    .string "without any regarding it$"
Bible_Text_Job_4_21::
    .string "Doth not their excellency which is\n"
    .string "in them go away? they die, even\l"
    .string "without wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_1::
    .string "Call now, if there be any that\n"
    .string "will answer thee; and to which of\l"
    .string "the saints wilt thou turn?"
Bible_Text_Job_5_2::
    .string "For wrath killeth the foolish man,\n"
    .string "and envy slayeth the silly one$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_3::
    .string "I have seen the foolish taking\n"
    .string "root: but suddenly I cursed his\l"
    .string "habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_4::
    .string "His children are far from safety,\n"
    .string "and they are crushed in the gate,\l"
    .string "neither is there any to deliver them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_5::
    .string "Whose harvest the hungry eateth up,\n"
    .string "and taketh it even out of the thorns,\l"
    .string "and the robber swalloweth up their\l"
    .string "substance.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_6::
    .string "Although affliction cometh not\n"
    .string "forth of the dust, neither doth\l"
    .string "trouble spring out of the ground;"
Bible_Text_Job_5_7::
    .string "Yet man is born unto trouble, as the\n"
    .string "sparks fly upward$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_8::
    .string "I would seek unto God, and unto God\n"
    .string "would I commit my cause:"
Bible_Text_Job_5_9::
    .string "Which doeth great things and\n"
    .string "unsearchable; marvellous things\l"
    .string "without number:"
Bible_Text_Job_5_10::
    .string "Who giveth rain upon the earth, and\n"
    .string "sendeth waters upon the fields:"
Bible_Text_Job_5_11::
    .string "To set up on high those that be\n"
    .string "low; that those which mourn may be\l"
    .string "exalted to safety$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_12::
    .string "He disappointeth the devices of\n"
    .string "the crafty, so that their hands\l"
    .string "cannot perform their enterprise.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_13::
    .string "He taketh the wise in their own\n"
    .string "craftiness: and the counsel of the\l"
    .string "froward is carried headlong.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_14::
    .string "They meet with darkness in the day\n"
    .string "time, and grope in the noonday as in\l"
    .string "the night.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_15::
    .string "But he saveth the poor from the\n"
    .string "sword, from their mouth, and from the\l"
    .string "hand of the mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_16::
    .string "So the poor hath hope, and iniquity\n"
    .string "stoppeth her mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_17::
    .string "Behold, happy is the man whom God\n"
    .string "correcteth: therefore despise not\l"
    .string "thou the chastening of the Almighty:"
Bible_Text_Job_5_18::
    .string "For he maketh sore, and bindeth up:\n"
    .string "he woundeth, and his hands make whole$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_19::
    .string "He shall deliver thee in six\n"
    .string "troubles: yea, in seven there shall\l"
    .string "no evil touch thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_20::
    .string "In famine he shall redeem thee\n"
    .string "from death: and in war from the power\l"
    .string "of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_21::
    .string "Thou shalt be hid from the scourge\n"
    .string "of the tongue: neither shalt thou be\l"
    .string "afraid of destruction when it cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_22::
    .string "At destruction and famine thou\n"
    .string "shalt laugh: neither shalt thou be\l"
    .string "afraid of the beasts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_23::
    .string "For thou shalt be in league with\n"
    .string "the stones of the field: and the\l"
    .string "beasts of the field shall be at\l"
    .string "peace with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_24::
    .string "And thou shalt know that thy\n"
    .string "tabernacle shall be in peace; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt visit thy habitation, and\l"
    .string "shalt not sin.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_25::
    .string "Thou shalt know also that thy seed\n"
    .string "shall be great, and thine offspring\l"
    .string "as the grass of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_26::
    .string "Thou shalt come to thy grave in a\n"
    .string "full age, like as a shock of corn\l"
    .string "cometh in in his season.$"
Bible_Text_Job_5_27::
    .string "Lo this, we have searched it, so it\n"
    .string "is; hear it, and know thou it for thy\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_1::
    .string "But Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_6_2::
    .string "Oh that my grief were throughly\n"
    .string "weighed, and my calamity laid in the\l"
    .string "balances together!"
Bible_Text_Job_6_3::
    .string "For now it would be heavier than\n"
    .string "the sand of the sea: therefore my\l"
    .string "words are swallowed up$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_4::
    .string "For the arrows of the Almighty are\n"
    .string "within me, the poison whereof\l"
    .string "drinketh up my spirit: the terrors\l"
    .string "of God do set themselves in array\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_5::
    .string "Doth the wild ass bray when he hath\n"
    .string "grass? or loweth the ox over his\l"
    .string "fodder?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_6::
    .string "Can that which is unsavoury be eaten\n"
    .string "without salt? or is there any taste\l"
    .string "in the white of an egg?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_7::
    .string "The things that my soul refused to\n"
    .string "touch are as my sorrowful meat$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_8::
    .string "Oh that I might have my request; and\n"
    .string "that God would grant me the thing\l"
    .string "that I long for!"
Bible_Text_Job_6_9::
    .string "Even that it would please God to\n"
    .string "destroy me; that he would let loose\l"
    .string "his hand, and cut me off!"
Bible_Text_Job_6_10::
    .string "Then should I yet have comfort;\n"
    .string "yea, I would harden myself in\l"
    .string "sorrow: let him not spare; for I\l"
    .string "have not concealed the words of the\l"
    .string "Holy One$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_11::
    .string "What is my strength, that I should\n"
    .string "hope? and what is mine end, that I\l"
    .string "should prolong my life?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_12::
    .string "Is my strength the strength of\n"
    .string "stones? or is my flesh of brass?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_13::
    .string "Is not my help in me? and is wisdom\n"
    .string "driven quite from me?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_14::
    .string "To him that is afflicted pity\n"
    .string "should be shewed from his friend;\l"
    .string "but he forsaketh the fear of the\l"
    .string "Almighty$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_15::
    .string "My brethren have dealt\n"
    .string "deceitfully as a brook, and as the\l"
    .string "stream of brooks they pass away;"
Bible_Text_Job_6_16::
    .string "Which are blackish by reason of the\n"
    .string "ice, and wherein the snow is hid:"
Bible_Text_Job_6_17::
    .string "What time they wax warm, they\n"
    .string "vanish: when it is hot, they are\l"
    .string "consumed out of their place$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_18::
    .string "The paths of their way are turned\n"
    .string "aside; they go to nothing, and\l"
    .string "perish.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_19::
    .string "The troops of Tema looked, the\n"
    .string "companies of Sheba waited for them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_20::
    .string "They were confounded because they\n"
    .string "had hoped; they came thither, and\l"
    .string "were ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_21::
    .string "For now ye are nothing; ye see my\n"
    .string "casting down, and are afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_22::
    .string "Did I say, Bring unto me? or, Give a\n"
    .string "reward for me of your substance?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_23::
    .string "Or, Deliver me from the enemy’s\n"
    .string "hand? or, Redeem me from the hand of\l"
    .string "the mighty?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_24::
    .string "Teach me, and I will hold my\n"
    .string "tongue: and cause me to understand\l"
    .string "wherein I have erred$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_25::
    .string "How forcible are right words! but\n"
    .string "what doth your arguing reprove?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_26::
    .string "Do ye imagine to reprove words, and\n"
    .string "the speeches of one that is\l"
    .string "desperate, which are as wind?"
Bible_Text_Job_6_27::
    .string "Yea, ye overwhelm the fatherless,\n"
    .string "and ye dig a pit for your friend$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_28::
    .string "Now therefore be content, look\n"
    .string "upon me; for it is evident unto you\l"
    .string "if I lie.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_29::
    .string "Return, I pray you, let it not be\n"
    .string "iniquity; yea, return again, my\l"
    .string "righteousness is in it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_6_30::
    .string "Is there iniquity in my tongue?\n"
    .string "cannot my taste discern perverse\l"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_1::
    .string "Is there not an appointed time to\n"
    .string "man upon earth? are not his days\l"
    .string "also like the days of an hireling?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_2::
    .string "As a servant earnestly desireth the\n"
    .string "shadow, and as an hireling looketh\l"
    .string "for the reward of his work:"
Bible_Text_Job_7_3::
    .string "So am I made to possess months of\n"
    .string "vanity, and wearisome nights are\l"
    .string "appointed to me$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_4::
    .string "When I lie down, I say, When shall\n"
    .string "I arise, and the night be gone? and I\l"
    .string "am full of tossings to and fro unto\l"
    .string "the dawning of the day.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_5::
    .string "My flesh is clothed with worms and\n"
    .string "clods of dust; my skin is broken, and\l"
    .string "become loathsome.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_6::
    .string "My days are swifter than a weaver’s\n"
    .string "shuttle, and are spent without\l"
    .string "hope.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_7::
    .string "O remember that my life is wind:\n"
    .string "mine eye shall no more see good.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_8::
    .string "The eye of him that hath seen me\n"
    .string "shall see me no more: thine eyes are\l"
    .string "upon me, and I am not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_9::
    .string "As the cloud is consumed and\n"
    .string "vanisheth away: so he that goeth down\l"
    .string "to the grave shall come up no more.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_10::
    .string "He shall return no more to his\n"
    .string "house, neither shall his place\l"
    .string "know him any more.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_11::
    .string "Therefore I will not refrain my\n"
    .string "mouth; I will speak in the anguish\l"
    .string "of my spirit; I will complain in\l"
    .string "the bitterness of my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_12::
    .string "Am I a sea, or a whale, that thou\n"
    .string "settest a watch over me?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_13::
    .string "When I say, My bed shall comfort\n"
    .string "me, my couch shall ease my\l"
    .string "complaints;"
Bible_Text_Job_7_14::
    .string "Then thou scarest me with dreams,\n"
    .string "and terrifiest me through visions:"
Bible_Text_Job_7_15::
    .string "So that my soul chooseth\n"
    .string "strangling, and death rather than my\l"
    .string "life$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_16::
    .string "I loathe it; I would not live\n"
    .string "alway: let me alone; for my days\l"
    .string "are vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Job_7_17::
    .string "What is man, that thou shouldest\n"
    .string "magnify him? and that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "set thine heart upon him?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_18::
    .string "And that thou shouldest visit him\n"
    .string "every morning, and try him every\l"
    .string "moment?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_19::
    .string "How long wilt thou not depart from\n"
    .string "me, nor let me alone till I\l"
    .string "swallow down my spittle?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_20::
    .string "I have sinned; what shall I do unto\n"
    .string "thee, O thou preserver of men? why\l"
    .string "hast thou set me as a mark against\l"
    .string "thee, so that I am a burden to\l"
    .string "myself?"
Bible_Text_Job_7_21::
    .string "And why dost thou not pardon my\n"
    .string "transgression, and take away my\l"
    .string "iniquity? for now shall I sleep in\l"
    .string "the dust; and thou shalt seek me in\l"
    .string "the morning, but I shall not be$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_1::
    .string "Then answered Bildad the Shuhite,\n"
    .string "and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_8_2::
    .string "How long wilt thou speak these\n"
    .string "things? and how long shall the\l"
    .string "words of thy mouth be like a strong\l"
    .string "wind?"
Bible_Text_Job_8_3::
    .string "Doth God pervert judgment? or doth\n"
    .string "the Almighty pervert justice?"
Bible_Text_Job_8_4::
    .string "If thy children have sinned against\n"
    .string "him, and he have cast them away for\l"
    .string "their transgression;"
Bible_Text_Job_8_5::
    .string "If thou wouldest seek unto God\n"
    .string "betimes, and make thy supplication\l"
    .string "to the Almighty;"
Bible_Text_Job_8_6::
    .string "If thou wert pure and upright;\n"
    .string "surely now he would awake for thee,\l"
    .string "and make the habitation of thy\l"
    .string "righteousness prosperous$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_7::
    .string "Though thy beginning was small,\n"
    .string "yet thy latter end should greatly\l"
    .string "increase.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_8::
    .string "For enquire, I pray thee, of the\n"
    .string "former age, and prepare thyself to\l"
    .string "the search of their fathers:"
Bible_Text_Job_8_9::
    .string "(For we are but of yesterday, and\n"
    .string "know nothing, because our days upon\l"
    .string "earth are a shadow:)"
Bible_Text_Job_8_10::
    .string "Shall not they teach thee, and\n"
    .string "tell thee, and utter words out of\l"
    .string "their heart?"
Bible_Text_Job_8_11::
    .string "Can the rush grow up without mire?\n"
    .string "can the flag grow without water?"
Bible_Text_Job_8_12::
    .string "Whilst it is yet in his greenness,\n"
    .string "and not cut down, it withereth before\l"
    .string "any other herb$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_13::
    .string "So are the paths of all that\n"
    .string "forget God; and the hypocrite’s\l"
    .string "hope shall perish:"
Bible_Text_Job_8_14::
    .string "Whose hope shall be cut off, and\n"
    .string "whose trust shall be a spider’s web$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_15::
    .string "He shall lean upon his house, but\n"
    .string "it shall not stand: he shall hold\l"
    .string "it fast, but it shall not endure.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_16::
    .string "He is green before the sun, and his\n"
    .string "branch shooteth forth in his garden.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_17::
    .string "His roots are wrapped about the\n"
    .string "heap, and seeth the place of stones.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_18::
    .string "If he destroy him from his place,\n"
    .string "then it shall deny him, saying, I\l"
    .string "have not seen thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_19::
    .string "Behold, this is the joy of his way,\n"
    .string "and out of the earth shall others\l"
    .string "grow.$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_20::
    .string "Behold, God will not cast away a\n"
    .string "perfect man, neither will he help\l"
    .string "the evil doers:"
Bible_Text_Job_8_21::
    .string "Till he fill thy mouth with\n"
    .string "laughing, and thy lips with\l"
    .string "rejoicing$"
Bible_Text_Job_8_22::
    .string "They that hate thee shall be\n"
    .string "clothed with shame; and the\l"
    .string "dwelling place of the wicked\l"
    .string "shall come to nought.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_1::
    .string "Then Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_9_2::
    .string "I know it is so of a truth: but how\n"
    .string "should man be just with God?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_3::
    .string "If he will contend with him, he\n"
    .string "cannot answer him one of a thousand$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_4::
    .string "He is wise in heart, and mighty in\n"
    .string "strength: who hath hardened himself\l"
    .string "against him, and hath prospered?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_5::
    .string "Which removeth the mountains, and\n"
    .string "they know not: which overturneth them\l"
    .string "in his anger$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_6::
    .string "Which shaketh the earth out of her\n"
    .string "place, and the pillars thereof\l"
    .string "tremble.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_7::
    .string "Which commandeth the sun, and it\n"
    .string "riseth not; and sealeth up the\l"
    .string "stars.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_8::
    .string "Which alone spreadeth out the\n"
    .string "heavens, and treadeth upon the waves\l"
    .string "of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_9::
    .string "Which maketh Arcturus, Orion, and\n"
    .string "Pleiades, and the chambers of the\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_10::
    .string "Which doeth great things past\n"
    .string "finding out; yea, and wonders without\l"
    .string "number.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_11::
    .string "Lo, he goeth by me, and I see him\n"
    .string "not: he passeth on also, but I\l"
    .string "perceive him not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_12::
    .string "Behold, he taketh away, who can\n"
    .string "hinder him? who will say unto him,\l"
    .string "What doest thou?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_13::
    .string "If God will not withdraw his anger,\n"
    .string "the proud helpers do stoop under\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_14::
    .string "How much less shall I answer him,\n"
    .string "and choose out my words to reason\l"
    .string "with him?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_15::
    .string "Whom, though I were righteous, yet\n"
    .string "would I not answer, but I would make\l"
    .string "supplication to my judge$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_16::
    .string "If I had called, and he had\n"
    .string "answered me; yet would I not believe\l"
    .string "that he had hearkened unto my voice.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_17::
    .string "For he breaketh me with a tempest,\n"
    .string "and multiplieth my wounds without\l"
    .string "cause.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_18::
    .string "He will not suffer me to take my\n"
    .string "breath, but filleth me with\l"
    .string "bitterness.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_19::
    .string "If I speak of strength, lo, he is\n"
    .string "strong: and if of judgment, who\l"
    .string "shall set me a time to plead?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_20::
    .string "If I justify myself, mine own mouth\n"
    .string "shall condemn me: if I say, I am\l"
    .string "perfect, it shall also prove me\l"
    .string "perverse$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_21::
    .string "Though I were perfect, yet would I\n"
    .string "not know my soul: I would despise\l"
    .string "my life.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_22::
    .string "This is one thing, therefore I said\n"
    .string "it, He destroyeth the perfect and\l"
    .string "the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_23::
    .string "If the scourge slay suddenly, he\n"
    .string "will laugh at the trial of the\l"
    .string "innocent.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_24::
    .string "The earth is given into the hand of\n"
    .string "the wicked: he covereth the faces of\l"
    .string "the judges thereof; if not, where,\l"
    .string "and who is he?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_25::
    .string "Now my days are swifter than a post:\n"
    .string "they flee away, they see no good$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_26::
    .string "They are passed away as the swift\n"
    .string "ships: as the eagle that hasteth to\l"
    .string "the prey.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_27::
    .string "If I say, I will forget my\n"
    .string "complaint, I will leave off my\l"
    .string "heaviness, and comfort myself:"
Bible_Text_Job_9_28::
    .string "I am afraid of all my sorrows, I\n"
    .string "know that thou wilt not hold me\l"
    .string "innocent$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_29::
    .string "If I be wicked, why then labour I in\n"
    .string "vain?"
Bible_Text_Job_9_30::
    .string "If I wash myself with snow water,\n"
    .string "and make my hands never so clean;"
Bible_Text_Job_9_31::
    .string "Yet shalt thou plunge me in the\n"
    .string "ditch, and mine own clothes shall\l"
    .string "abhor me$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_32::
    .string "For he is not a man, as I am, that I\n"
    .string "should answer him, and we should\l"
    .string "come together in judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_33::
    .string "Neither is there any daysman\n"
    .string "betwixt us, that might lay his hand\l"
    .string "upon us both.$"
Bible_Text_Job_9_34::
    .string "Let him take his rod away from me,\n"
    .string "and let not his fear terrify me:"
Bible_Text_Job_9_35::
    .string "Then would I speak, and not fear\n"
    .string "him; but it is not so with me$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_1::
    .string "My soul is weary of my life; I\n"
    .string "will leave my complaint upon\l"
    .string "myself; I will speak in the\l"
    .string "bitterness of my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_2::
    .string "I will say unto God, Do not condemn\n"
    .string "me; shew me wherefore thou contendest\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_3::
    .string "Is it good unto thee that thou\n"
    .string "shouldest oppress, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest despise the work of thine\l"
    .string "hands, and shine upon the counsel of\l"
    .string "the wicked?"
Bible_Text_Job_10_4::
    .string "Hast thou eyes of flesh? or seest\n"
    .string "thou as man seeth?"
Bible_Text_Job_10_5::
    .string "Are thy days as the days of man? are\n"
    .string "thy years as man’s days,"
Bible_Text_Job_10_6::
    .string "That thou enquirest after mine\n"
    .string "iniquity, and searchest after my sin?"
Bible_Text_Job_10_7::
    .string "Thou knowest that I am not wicked;\n"
    .string "and there is none that can deliver\l"
    .string "out of thine hand$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_8::
    .string "Thine hands have made me and\n"
    .string "fashioned me together round about;\l"
    .string "yet thou dost destroy me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_9::
    .string "Remember, I beseech thee, that thou\n"
    .string "hast made me as the clay; and wilt\l"
    .string "thou bring me into dust again?"
Bible_Text_Job_10_10::
    .string "Hast thou not poured me out as\n"
    .string "milk, and curdled me like cheese?"
Bible_Text_Job_10_11::
    .string "Thou hast clothed me with skin and\n"
    .string "flesh, and hast fenced me with bones\l"
    .string "and sinews$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_12::
    .string "Thou hast granted me life and\n"
    .string "favour, and thy visitation hath\l"
    .string "preserved my spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_13::
    .string "And these things hast thou hid in\n"
    .string "thine heart: I know that this is with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_14::
    .string "If I sin, then thou markest me, and\n"
    .string "thou wilt not acquit me from mine\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_15::
    .string "If I be wicked, woe unto me; and if I\n"
    .string "be righteous, yet will I not lift\l"
    .string "up my head. I am full of confusion;\l"
    .string "therefore see thou mine affliction;"
Bible_Text_Job_10_16::
    .string "For it increaseth. Thou huntest me\n"
    .string "as a fierce lion: and again thou\l"
    .string "shewest thyself marvellous upon me$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_17::
    .string "Thou renewest thy witnesses against\n"
    .string "me, and increasest thine indignation\l"
    .string "upon me; changes and war are against\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_18::
    .string "Wherefore then hast thou brought me\n"
    .string "forth out of the womb? Oh that I had\l"
    .string "given up the ghost, and no eye had\l"
    .string "seen me!"
Bible_Text_Job_10_19::
    .string "I should have been as though I had\n"
    .string "not been; I should have been carried\l"
    .string "from the womb to the grave$"
Bible_Text_Job_10_20::
    .string "Are not my days few? cease then, and\n"
    .string "let me alone, that I may take comfort\l"
    .string "a little,"
Bible_Text_Job_10_21::
    .string "Before I go whence I shall not\n"
    .string "return, even to the land of darkness\l"
    .string "and the shadow of death;"
Bible_Text_Job_10_22::
    .string "A land of darkness, as darkness\n"
    .string "itself; and of the shadow of death,\l"
    .string "without any order, and where the\l"
    .string "light is as darkness$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_1::
    .string "Then answered Zophar the\n"
    .string "Naamathite, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_11_2::
    .string "Should not the multitude of words\n"
    .string "be answered? and should a man full\l"
    .string "of talk be justified?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_3::
    .string "Should thy lies make men hold\n"
    .string "their peace? and when thou mockest,\l"
    .string "shall no man make thee ashamed?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_4::
    .string "For thou hast said, My doctrine is\n"
    .string "pure, and I am clean in thine eyes$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_5::
    .string "But oh that God would speak, and\n"
    .string "open his lips against thee;"
Bible_Text_Job_11_6::
    .string "And that he would shew thee the\n"
    .string "secrets of wisdom, that they are\l"
    .string "double to that which is! Know\l"
    .string "therefore that God exacteth of thee\l"
    .string "less than thine iniquity deserveth$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_7::
    .string "Canst thou by searching find out\n"
    .string "God? canst thou find out the\l"
    .string "Almighty unto perfection?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_8::
    .string "It is as high as heaven; what canst\n"
    .string "thou do? deeper than hell; what\l"
    .string "canst thou know?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_9::
    .string "The measure thereof is longer than\n"
    .string "the earth, and broader than the sea$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_10::
    .string "If he cut off, and shut up, or\n"
    .string "gather together, then who can hinder\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_11::
    .string "For he knoweth vain men: he seeth\n"
    .string "wickedness also; will he not then\l"
    .string "consider it?"
Bible_Text_Job_11_12::
    .string "For vain men would be wise, though\n"
    .string "man be born like a wild ass’s colt$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_13::
    .string "If thou prepare thine heart, and\n"
    .string "stretch out thine hands toward him;"
Bible_Text_Job_11_14::
    .string "If iniquity be in thine hand, put it\n"
    .string "far away, and let not wickedness\l"
    .string "dwell in thy tabernacles$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_15::
    .string "For then shalt thou lift up thy\n"
    .string "face without spot; yea, thou shalt\l"
    .string "be stedfast, and shalt not fear:"
Bible_Text_Job_11_16::
    .string "Because thou shalt forget thy\n"
    .string "misery, and remember it as waters\l"
    .string "that pass away:"
Bible_Text_Job_11_17::
    .string "And thine age shall be clearer\n"
    .string "than the noonday: thou shalt shine\l"
    .string "forth, thou shalt be as the morning$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_18::
    .string "And thou shalt be secure, because\n"
    .string "there is hope; yea, thou shalt dig\l"
    .string "about thee, and thou shalt take thy\l"
    .string "rest in safety.$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_19::
    .string "Also thou shalt lie down, and none\n"
    .string "shall make thee afraid; yea, many\l"
    .string "shall make suit unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_11_20::
    .string "But the eyes of the wicked shall\n"
    .string "fail, and they shall not escape,\l"
    .string "and their hope shall be as the\l"
    .string "giving up of the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_1::
    .string "And Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_12_2::
    .string "No doubt but ye are the people,\n"
    .string "and wisdom shall die with you$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_3::
    .string "But I have understanding as well\n"
    .string "as you; I am not inferior to you: yea,\l"
    .string "who knoweth not such things as these?"
Bible_Text_Job_12_4::
    .string "I am as one mocked of his neighbour,\n"
    .string "who calleth upon God, and he\l"
    .string "answereth him: the just upright man\l"
    .string "is laughed to scorn$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_5::
    .string "He that is ready to slip with his\n"
    .string "feet is as a lamp despised in the\l"
    .string "thought of him that is at ease.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_6::
    .string "The tabernacles of robbers\n"
    .string "prosper, and they that provoke God\l"
    .string "are secure; into whose hand God\l"
    .string "bringeth abundantly.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_7::
    .string "But ask now the beasts, and they\n"
    .string "shall teach thee; and the fowls of\l"
    .string "the air, and they shall tell thee:"
Bible_Text_Job_12_8::
    .string "Or speak to the earth, and it\n"
    .string "shall teach thee: and the fishes of\l"
    .string "the sea shall declare unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_9::
    .string "Who knoweth not in all these that\n"
    .string "the hand of the LORD hath wrought\l"
    .string "this?"
Bible_Text_Job_12_10::
    .string "In whose hand is the soul of every\n"
    .string "living thing, and the breath of all\l"
    .string "mankind$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_11::
    .string "Doth not the ear try words? and the\n"
    .string "mouth taste his meat?"
Bible_Text_Job_12_12::
    .string "With the ancient is wisdom; and in\n"
    .string "length of days understanding$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_13::
    .string "With him is wisdom and strength, he\n"
    .string "hath counsel and understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_14::
    .string "Behold, he breaketh down, and it\n"
    .string "cannot be built again: he shutteth\l"
    .string "up a man, and there can be no\l"
    .string "opening.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_15::
    .string "Behold, he withholdeth the waters,\n"
    .string "and they dry up: also he sendeth\l"
    .string "them out, and they overturn the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_16::
    .string "With him is strength and wisdom: the\n"
    .string "deceived and the deceiver are his.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_17::
    .string "He leadeth counsellors away\n"
    .string "spoiled, and maketh the judges\l"
    .string "fools.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_18::
    .string "He looseth the bond of kings, and\n"
    .string "girdeth their loins with a girdle.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_19::
    .string "He leadeth princes away spoiled,\n"
    .string "and overthroweth the mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_20::
    .string "He removeth away the speech of the\n"
    .string "trusty, and taketh away the\l"
    .string "understanding of the aged.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_21::
    .string "He poureth contempt upon princes,\n"
    .string "and weakeneth the strength of the\l"
    .string "mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_22::
    .string "He discovereth deep things out of\n"
    .string "darkness, and bringeth out to light\l"
    .string "the shadow of death.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_23::
    .string "He increaseth the nations, and\n"
    .string "destroyeth them: he enlargeth the\l"
    .string "nations, and straiteneth them again.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_24::
    .string "He taketh away the heart of the\n"
    .string "chief of the people of the earth,\l"
    .string "and causeth them to wander in a\l"
    .string "wilderness where there is no way.$"
Bible_Text_Job_12_25::
    .string "They grope in the dark without\n"
    .string "light, and he maketh them to stagger\l"
    .string "like a drunken man.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_1::
    .string "Lo, mine eye hath seen all this,\n"
    .string "mine ear hath heard and understood it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_2::
    .string "What ye know, the same do I know\n"
    .string "also: I am not inferior unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_3::
    .string "Surely I would speak to the\n"
    .string "Almighty, and I desire to reason\l"
    .string "with God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_4::
    .string "But ye are forgers of lies, ye are\n"
    .string "all physicians of no value.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_5::
    .string "O that ye would altogether hold\n"
    .string "your peace! and it should be your\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_6::
    .string "Hear now my reasoning, and hearken\n"
    .string "to the pleadings of my lips.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_7::
    .string "Will ye speak wickedly for God?\n"
    .string "and talk deceitfully for him?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_8::
    .string "Will ye accept his person? will\n"
    .string "ye contend for God?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_9::
    .string "Is it good that he should search\n"
    .string "you out? or as one man mocketh\l"
    .string "another, do ye so mock him?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_10::
    .string "He will surely reprove you, if ye\n"
    .string "do secretly accept persons$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_11::
    .string "Shall not his excellency make you\n"
    .string "afraid? and his dread fall upon\l"
    .string "you?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_12::
    .string "Your remembrances are like unto\n"
    .string "ashes, your bodies to bodies of clay$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_13::
    .string "Hold your peace, let me alone,\n"
    .string "that I may speak, and let come on me\l"
    .string "what will.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_14::
    .string "Wherefore do I take my flesh in my\n"
    .string "teeth, and put my life in mine hand?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_15::
    .string "Though he slay me, yet will I\n"
    .string "trust in him: but I will maintain\l"
    .string "mine own ways before him$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_16::
    .string "He also shall be my salvation:\n"
    .string "for an hypocrite shall not come\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_17::
    .string "Hear diligently my speech, and my\n"
    .string "declaration with your ears.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_18::
    .string "Behold now, I have ordered my\n"
    .string "cause; I know that I shall be\l"
    .string "justified.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_19::
    .string "Who is he that will plead with me?\n"
    .string "for now, if I hold my tongue, I\l"
    .string "shall give up the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_20::
    .string "Only do not two things unto me: then\n"
    .string "will I not hide myself from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_21::
    .string "Withdraw thine hand far from me: and\n"
    .string "let not thy dread make me afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_22::
    .string "Then call thou, and I will\n"
    .string "answer: or let me speak, and answer\l"
    .string "thou me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_23::
    .string "How many are mine iniquities and\n"
    .string "sins? make me to know my\l"
    .string "transgression and my sin.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_24::
    .string "Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and\n"
    .string "holdest me for thine enemy?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_25::
    .string "Wilt thou break a leaf driven to\n"
    .string "and fro? and wilt thou pursue the\l"
    .string "dry stubble?"
Bible_Text_Job_13_26::
    .string "For thou writest bitter things\n"
    .string "against me, and makest me to possess\l"
    .string "the iniquities of my youth$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_27::
    .string "Thou puttest my feet also in the\n"
    .string "stocks, and lookest narrowly unto\l"
    .string "all my paths; thou settest a print\l"
    .string "upon the heels of my feet.$"
Bible_Text_Job_13_28::
    .string "And he, as a rotten thing,\n"
    .string "consumeth, as a garment that is moth\l"
    .string "eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_1::
    .string "Man that is born of a woman is of few\n"
    .string "days and full of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_2::
    .string "He cometh forth like a flower, and\n"
    .string "is cut down: he fleeth also as a\l"
    .string "shadow, and continueth not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_3::
    .string "And doth thou open thine eyes upon\n"
    .string "such an one, and bringest me into\l"
    .string "judgment with thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_14_4::
    .string "Who can bring a clean thing out of\n"
    .string "an unclean? not one$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_5::
    .string "Seeing his days are determined, the\n"
    .string "number of his months are with thee,\l"
    .string "thou hast appointed his bounds that\l"
    .string "he cannot pass;"
Bible_Text_Job_14_6::
    .string "Turn from him, that he may rest,\n"
    .string "till he shall accomplish, as an\l"
    .string "hireling, his day$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_7::
    .string "For there is hope of a tree, if it\n"
    .string "be cut down, that it will sprout\l"
    .string "again, and that the tender branch\l"
    .string "thereof will not cease.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_8::
    .string "Though the root thereof wax old in\n"
    .string "the earth, and the stock thereof die\l"
    .string "in the ground;"
Bible_Text_Job_14_9::
    .string "Yet through the scent of water it\n"
    .string "will bud, and bring forth boughs\l"
    .string "like a plant$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_10::
    .string "But man dieth, and wasteth away:\n"
    .string "yea, man giveth up the ghost, and\l"
    .string "where is he?"
Bible_Text_Job_14_11::
    .string "As the waters fail from the sea, and\n"
    .string "the flood decayeth and drieth up:"
Bible_Text_Job_14_12::
    .string "So man lieth down, and riseth not:\n"
    .string "till the heavens be no more, they\l"
    .string "shall not awake, nor be raised out\l"
    .string "of their sleep$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_13::
    .string "O that thou wouldest hide me in the\n"
    .string "grave, that thou wouldest keep me\l"
    .string "secret, until thy wrath be past,\l"
    .string "that thou wouldest appoint me a set\l"
    .string "time, and remember me!"
Bible_Text_Job_14_14::
    .string "If a man die, shall he live again?\n"
    .string "all the days of my appointed time\l"
    .string "will I wait, till my change come$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_15::
    .string "Thou shalt call, and I will\n"
    .string "answer thee: thou wilt have a desire\l"
    .string "to the work of thine hands.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_16::
    .string "For now thou numberest my steps:\n"
    .string "dost thou not watch over my sin?"
Bible_Text_Job_14_17::
    .string "My transgression is sealed up in a\n"
    .string "bag, and thou sewest up mine iniquity$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_18::
    .string "And surely the mountains falling\n"
    .string "cometh to nought, and the rock is\l"
    .string "removed out of his place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_19::
    .string "The waters wear the stones: thou\n"
    .string "washest away the things which grow\l"
    .string "out of the dust of the earth; and thou\l"
    .string "destroyest the hope of man.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_20::
    .string "Thou prevailest for ever against\n"
    .string "him, and he passeth: thou changest\l"
    .string "his countenance, and sendest him\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_21::
    .string "His sons come to honour, and he\n"
    .string "knoweth it not; and they are brought\l"
    .string "low, but he perceiveth it not of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_14_22::
    .string "But his flesh upon him shall have\n"
    .string "pain, and his soul within him shall\l"
    .string "mourn.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_1::
    .string "Then answered Eliphaz the\n"
    .string "Temanite, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_15_2::
    .string "Should a wise man utter vain\n"
    .string "knowledge, and fill his belly\l"
    .string "with the east wind?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_3::
    .string "Should he reason with\n"
    .string "unprofitable talk? or with\l"
    .string "speeches wherewith he can do no\l"
    .string "good?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_4::
    .string "Yea, thou castest off fear, and\n"
    .string "restrainest prayer before God$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_5::
    .string "For thy mouth uttereth thine\n"
    .string "iniquity, and thou choosest the\l"
    .string "tongue of the crafty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_6::
    .string "Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and\n"
    .string "not I: yea, thine own lips testify\l"
    .string "against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_7::
    .string "Art thou the first man that was\n"
    .string "born? or wast thou made before the\l"
    .string "hills?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_8::
    .string "Hast thou heard the secret of God?\n"
    .string "and dost thou restrain wisdom to\l"
    .string "thyself?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_9::
    .string "What knowest thou, that we know not?\n"
    .string "what understandest thou, which is not\l"
    .string "in us?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_10::
    .string "With us are both the grayheaded and\n"
    .string "very aged men, much elder than thy\l"
    .string "father$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_11::
    .string "Are the consolations of God small\n"
    .string "with thee? is there any secret thing\l"
    .string "with thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_12::
    .string "Why doth thine heart carry thee\n"
    .string "away? and what do thy eyes wink at,"
Bible_Text_Job_15_13::
    .string "That thou turnest thy spirit\n"
    .string "against God, and lettest such words\l"
    .string "go out of thy mouth?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_14::
    .string "What is man, that he should be\n"
    .string "clean? and he which is born of a\l"
    .string "woman, that he should be righteous?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_15::
    .string "Behold, he putteth no trust in his\n"
    .string "saints; yea, the heavens are not\l"
    .string "clean in his sight$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_16::
    .string "How much more abominable and\n"
    .string "filthy is man, which drinketh\l"
    .string "iniquity like water?"
Bible_Text_Job_15_17::
    .string "I will shew thee, hear me; and that\n"
    .string "which I have seen I will declare;"
Bible_Text_Job_15_18::
    .string "Which wise men have told from their\n"
    .string "fathers, and have not hid it:"
Bible_Text_Job_15_19::
    .string "Unto whom alone the earth was\n"
    .string "given, and no stranger passed among\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_20::
    .string "The wicked man travaileth with\n"
    .string "pain all his days, and the number of\l"
    .string "years is hidden to the oppressor.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_21::
    .string "A dreadful sound is in his ears: in\n"
    .string "prosperity the destroyer shall\l"
    .string "come upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_22::
    .string "He believeth not that he shall\n"
    .string "return out of darkness, and he is\l"
    .string "waited for of the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_23::
    .string "He wandereth abroad for bread,\n"
    .string "saying, Where is it? he knoweth that\l"
    .string "the day of darkness is ready at his\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_24::
    .string "Trouble and anguish shall make\n"
    .string "him afraid; they shall prevail\l"
    .string "against him, as a king ready to the\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_25::
    .string "For he stretcheth out his hand\n"
    .string "against God, and strengtheneth\l"
    .string "himself against the Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_26::
    .string "He runneth upon him, even on his\n"
    .string "neck, upon the thick bosses of his\l"
    .string "bucklers:"
Bible_Text_Job_15_27::
    .string "Because he covereth his face with\n"
    .string "his fatness, and maketh collops of\l"
    .string "fat on his flanks$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_28::
    .string "And he dwelleth in desolate\n"
    .string "cities, and in houses which no man\l"
    .string "inhabiteth, which are ready to become\l"
    .string "heaps.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_29::
    .string "He shall not be rich, neither\n"
    .string "shall his substance continue,\l"
    .string "neither shall he prolong the\l"
    .string "perfection thereof upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_30::
    .string "He shall not depart out of\n"
    .string "darkness; the flame shall dry up\l"
    .string "his branches, and by the breath of\l"
    .string "his mouth shall he go away.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_31::
    .string "Let not him that is deceived trust\n"
    .string "in vanity: for vanity shall be his\l"
    .string "recompence.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_32::
    .string "It shall be accomplished before\n"
    .string "his time, and his branch shall not\l"
    .string "be green.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_33::
    .string "He shall shake off his unripe\n"
    .string "grape as the vine, and shall cast\l"
    .string "off his flower as the olive.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_34::
    .string "For the congregation of hypocrites\n"
    .string "shall be desolate, and fire shall\l"
    .string "consume the tabernacles of bribery.$"
Bible_Text_Job_15_35::
    .string "They conceive mischief, and bring\n"
    .string "forth vanity, and their belly\l"
    .string "prepareth deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_1::
    .string "Then Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_16_2::
    .string "I have heard many such things:\n"
    .string "miserable comforters are ye all$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_3::
    .string "Shall vain words have an end? or\n"
    .string "what emboldeneth thee that thou\l"
    .string "answerest?"
Bible_Text_Job_16_4::
    .string "I also could speak as ye do: if\n"
    .string "your soul were in my soul’s stead, I\l"
    .string "could heap up words against you,\l"
    .string "and shake mine head at you$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_5::
    .string "But I would strengthen you with my\n"
    .string "mouth, and the moving of my lips\l"
    .string "should asswage your grief.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_6::
    .string "Though I speak, my grief is not\n"
    .string "asswaged: and though I forbear, what\l"
    .string "am I eased?"
Bible_Text_Job_16_7::
    .string "But now he hath made me weary: thou\n"
    .string "hast made desolate all my company$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_8::
    .string "And thou hast filled me with\n"
    .string "wrinkles, which is a witness against\l"
    .string "me: and my leanness rising up in me\l"
    .string "beareth witness to my face.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_9::
    .string "He teareth me in his wrath, who\n"
    .string "hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with\l"
    .string "his teeth; mine enemy sharpeneth his\l"
    .string "eyes upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_10::
    .string "They have gaped upon me with their\n"
    .string "mouth; they have smitten me upon the\l"
    .string "cheek reproachfully; they have\l"
    .string "gathered themselves together\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_11::
    .string "God hath delivered me to the\n"
    .string "ungodly, and turned me over into the\l"
    .string "hands of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_12::
    .string "I was at ease, but he hath broken me\n"
    .string "asunder: he hath also taken me by my\l"
    .string "neck, and shaken me to pieces, and\l"
    .string "set me up for his mark.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_13::
    .string "His archers compass me round about,\n"
    .string "he cleaveth my reins asunder, and\l"
    .string "doth not spare; he poureth out my\l"
    .string "gall upon the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_14::
    .string "He breaketh me with breach upon\n"
    .string "breach, he runneth upon me like a\l"
    .string "giant.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_15::
    .string "I have sewed sackcloth upon my\n"
    .string "skin, and defiled my horn in the\l"
    .string "dust.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_16::
    .string "My face is foul with weeping, and\n"
    .string "on my eyelids is the shadow of death;"
Bible_Text_Job_16_17::
    .string "Not for any injustice in mine hands:\n"
    .string "also my prayer is pure$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_18::
    .string "O earth, cover not thou my blood,\n"
    .string "and let my cry have no place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_19::
    .string "Also now, behold, my witness is in\n"
    .string "heaven, and my record is on high.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_20::
    .string "My friends scorn me: but mine eye\n"
    .string "poureth out tears unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_16_21::
    .string "O that one might plead for a man\n"
    .string "with God, as a man pleadeth for his\l"
    .string "neighbour!"
Bible_Text_Job_16_22::
    .string "When a few years are come, then I\n"
    .string "shall go the way whence I shall\l"
    .string "not return$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_1::
    .string "My breath is corrupt, my days are\n"
    .string "extinct, the graves are ready for me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_2::
    .string "Are there not mockers with me? and\n"
    .string "doth not mine eye continue in their\l"
    .string "provocation?"
Bible_Text_Job_17_3::
    .string "Lay down now, put me in a surety\n"
    .string "with thee; who is he that will\l"
    .string "strike hands with me?"
Bible_Text_Job_17_4::
    .string "For thou hast hid their heart from\n"
    .string "understanding: therefore shalt thou\l"
    .string "not exalt them$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_5::
    .string "He that speaketh flattery to his\n"
    .string "friends, even the eyes of his\l"
    .string "children shall fail.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_6::
    .string "He hath made me also a byword of the\n"
    .string "people; and aforetime I was as a\l"
    .string "tabret.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_7::
    .string "Mine eye also is dim by reason of\n"
    .string "sorrow, and all my members are as a\l"
    .string "shadow.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_8::
    .string "Upright men shall be astonied at\n"
    .string "this, and the innocent shall stir\l"
    .string "up himself against the hypocrite.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_9::
    .string "The righteous also shall hold on\n"
    .string "his way, and he that hath clean hands\l"
    .string "shall be stronger and stronger.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_10::
    .string "But as for you all, do ye return,\n"
    .string "and come now: for I cannot find one\l"
    .string "wise man among you.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_11::
    .string "My days are past, my purposes are\n"
    .string "broken off, even the thoughts of my\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_12::
    .string "They change the night into day: the\n"
    .string "light is short because of darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_13::
    .string "If I wait, the grave is mine house: I\n"
    .string "have made my bed in the darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_14::
    .string "I have said to corruption, Thou art\n"
    .string "my father: to the worm, Thou art my\l"
    .string "mother, and my sister.$"
Bible_Text_Job_17_15::
    .string "And where is now my hope? as for my\n"
    .string "hope, who shall see it?"
Bible_Text_Job_17_16::
    .string "They shall go down to the bars of\n"
    .string "the pit, when our rest together is in\l"
    .string "the dust$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_1::
    .string "Then answered Bildad the Shuhite,\n"
    .string "and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_18_2::
    .string "How long will it be ere ye make an\n"
    .string "end of words? mark, and afterwards we\l"
    .string "will speak$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_3::
    .string "Wherefore are we counted as beasts,\n"
    .string "and reputed vile in your sight?"
Bible_Text_Job_18_4::
    .string "He teareth himself in his anger:\n"
    .string "shall the earth be forsaken for\l"
    .string "thee? and shall the rock be removed\l"
    .string "out of his place?"
Bible_Text_Job_18_5::
    .string "Yea, the light of the wicked shall\n"
    .string "be put out, and the spark of his\l"
    .string "fire shall not shine$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_6::
    .string "The light shall be dark in his\n"
    .string "tabernacle, and his candle shall\l"
    .string "be put out with him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_7::
    .string "The steps of his strength shall be\n"
    .string "straitened, and his own counsel\l"
    .string "shall cast him down.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_8::
    .string "For he is cast into a net by his own\n"
    .string "feet, and he walketh upon a snare.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_9::
    .string "The gin shall take him by the\n"
    .string "heel, and the robber shall\l"
    .string "prevail against him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_10::
    .string "The snare is laid for him in the\n"
    .string "ground, and a trap for him in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_11::
    .string "Terrors shall make him afraid on\n"
    .string "every side, and shall drive him to\l"
    .string "his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_12::
    .string "His strength shall be\n"
    .string "hungerbitten, and destruction shall\l"
    .string "be ready at his side.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_13::
    .string "It shall devour the strength of\n"
    .string "his skin: even the firstborn of death\l"
    .string "shall devour his strength.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_14::
    .string "His confidence shall be rooted out\n"
    .string "of his tabernacle, and it shall\l"
    .string "bring him to the king of terrors.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_15::
    .string "It shall dwell in his\n"
    .string "tabernacle, because it is none of\l"
    .string "his: brimstone shall be scattered\l"
    .string "upon his habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_16::
    .string "His roots shall be dried up\n"
    .string "beneath, and above shall his branch\l"
    .string "be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_17::
    .string "His remembrance shall perish from\n"
    .string "the earth, and he shall have no name\l"
    .string "in the street.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_18::
    .string "He shall be driven from light into\n"
    .string "darkness, and chased out of the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_19::
    .string "He shall neither have son nor\n"
    .string "nephew among his people, nor any\l"
    .string "remaining in his dwellings.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_20::
    .string "They that come after him shall be\n"
    .string "astonied at his day, as they that\l"
    .string "went before were affrighted.$"
Bible_Text_Job_18_21::
    .string "Surely such are the dwellings of\n"
    .string "the wicked, and this is the place of\l"
    .string "him that knoweth not God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_1::
    .string "Then Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_19_2::
    .string "How long will ye vex my soul, and\n"
    .string "break me in pieces with words?"
Bible_Text_Job_19_3::
    .string "These ten times have ye reproached\n"
    .string "me: ye are not ashamed that ye make\l"
    .string "yourselves strange to me$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_4::
    .string "And be it indeed that I have erred,\n"
    .string "mine error remaineth with myself.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_5::
    .string "If indeed ye will magnify\n"
    .string "yourselves against me, and plead\l"
    .string "against me my reproach:"
Bible_Text_Job_19_6::
    .string "Know now that God hath overthrown\n"
    .string "me, and hath compassed me with his\l"
    .string "net$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_7::
    .string "Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am\n"
    .string "not heard: I cry aloud, but there is\l"
    .string "no judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_8::
    .string "He hath fenced up my way that I\n"
    .string "cannot pass, and he hath set\l"
    .string "darkness in my paths.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_9::
    .string "He hath stripped me of my glory,\n"
    .string "and taken the crown from my head.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_10::
    .string "He hath destroyed me on every side,\n"
    .string "and I am gone: and mine hope hath he\l"
    .string "removed like a tree.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_11::
    .string "He hath also kindled his wrath\n"
    .string "against me, and he counteth me unto\l"
    .string "him as one of his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_12::
    .string "His troops come together, and raise\n"
    .string "up their way against me, and encamp\l"
    .string "round about my tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_13::
    .string "He hath put my brethren far from me,\n"
    .string "and mine acquaintance are verily\l"
    .string "estranged from me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_14::
    .string "My kinsfolk have failed, and my\n"
    .string "familiar friends have forgotten me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_15::
    .string "They that dwell in mine house, and\n"
    .string "my maids, count me for a stranger: I\l"
    .string "am an alien in their sight.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_16::
    .string "I called my servant, and he gave me\n"
    .string "no answer; I intreated him with my\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_17::
    .string "My breath is strange to my wife,\n"
    .string "though I intreated for the\l"
    .string "children’s sake of mine own body.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_18::
    .string "Yea, young children despised me; I\n"
    .string "arose, and they spake against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_19::
    .string "All my inward friends abhorred me:\n"
    .string "and they whom I loved are turned\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_20::
    .string "My bone cleaveth to my skin and to\n"
    .string "my flesh, and I am escaped with the\l"
    .string "skin of my teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_21::
    .string "Have pity upon me, have pity upon\n"
    .string "me, O ye my friends; for the hand of\l"
    .string "God hath touched me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_22::
    .string "Why do ye persecute me as God, and\n"
    .string "are not satisfied with my flesh?"
Bible_Text_Job_19_23::
    .string "Oh that my words were now written!\n"
    .string "oh that they were printed in a book!"
Bible_Text_Job_19_24::
    .string "That they were graven with an iron\n"
    .string "pen and lead in the rock for ever!"
Bible_Text_Job_19_25::
    .string "For I know that my redeemer liveth,\n"
    .string "and that he shall stand at the\l"
    .string "latter day upon the earth:"
Bible_Text_Job_19_26::
    .string "And though after my skin worms\n"
    .string "destroy this body, yet in my flesh\l"
    .string "shall I see God:"
Bible_Text_Job_19_27::
    .string "Whom I shall see for myself, and\n"
    .string "mine eyes shall behold, and not\l"
    .string "another; though my reins be consumed\l"
    .string "within me$"
Bible_Text_Job_19_28::
    .string "But ye should say, Why persecute we\n"
    .string "him, seeing the root of the matter is\l"
    .string "found in me?"
Bible_Text_Job_19_29::
    .string "Be ye afraid of the sword: for wrath\n"
    .string "bringeth the punishments of the\l"
    .string "sword, that ye may know there is a\l"
    .string "judgment$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_1::
    .string "Then answered Zophar the\n"
    .string "Naamathite, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_20_2::
    .string "Therefore do my thoughts cause me to\n"
    .string "answer, and for this I make haste$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_3::
    .string "I have heard the check of my\n"
    .string "reproach, and the spirit of my\l"
    .string "understanding causeth me to answer.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_4::
    .string "Knowest thou not this of old, since\n"
    .string "man was placed upon earth,"
Bible_Text_Job_20_5::
    .string "That the triumphing of the wicked\n"
    .string "is short, and the joy of the\l"
    .string "hypocrite but for a moment?"
Bible_Text_Job_20_6::
    .string "Though his excellency mount up to\n"
    .string "the heavens, and his head reach unto\l"
    .string "the clouds;"
Bible_Text_Job_20_7::
    .string "Yet he shall perish for ever like\n"
    .string "his own dung: they which have seen\l"
    .string "him shall say, Where is he?"
Bible_Text_Job_20_8::
    .string "He shall fly away as a dream, and\n"
    .string "shall not be found: yea, he shall\l"
    .string "be chased away as a vision of the\l"
    .string "night$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_9::
    .string "The eye also which saw him shall\n"
    .string "see him no more; neither shall his\l"
    .string "place any more behold him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_10::
    .string "His children shall seek to\n"
    .string "please the poor, and his hands\l"
    .string "shall restore their goods.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_11::
    .string "His bones are full of the sin of\n"
    .string "his youth, which shall lie down\l"
    .string "with him in the dust.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_12::
    .string "Though wickedness be sweet in his\n"
    .string "mouth, though he hide it under his\l"
    .string "tongue;"
Bible_Text_Job_20_13::
    .string "Though he spare it, and forsake it\n"
    .string "not; but keep it still within his\l"
    .string "mouth:"
Bible_Text_Job_20_14::
    .string "Yet his meat in his bowels is\n"
    .string "turned, it is the gall of asps\l"
    .string "within him$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_15::
    .string "He hath swallowed down riches, and\n"
    .string "he shall vomit them up again: God\l"
    .string "shall cast them out of his belly.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_16::
    .string "He shall suck the poison of asps:\n"
    .string "the viper’s tongue shall slay him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_17::
    .string "He shall not see the rivers, the\n"
    .string "floods, the brooks of honey and\l"
    .string "butter.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_18::
    .string "That which he laboured for shall\n"
    .string "he restore, and shall not swallow\l"
    .string "it down: according to his substance\l"
    .string "shall the restitution be, and he\l"
    .string "shall not rejoice therein.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_19::
    .string "Because he hath oppressed and hath\n"
    .string "forsaken the poor; because he hath\l"
    .string "violently taken away an house which\l"
    .string "he builded not;"
Bible_Text_Job_20_20::
    .string "Surely he shall not feel\n"
    .string "quietness in his belly, he shall\l"
    .string "not save of that which he desired$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_21::
    .string "There shall none of his meat be\n"
    .string "left; therefore shall no man look\l"
    .string "for his goods.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_22::
    .string "In the fulness of his sufficiency\n"
    .string "he shall be in straits: every hand\l"
    .string "of the wicked shall come upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_23::
    .string "When he is about to fill his\n"
    .string "belly, God shall cast the fury of\l"
    .string "his wrath upon him, and shall rain\l"
    .string "it upon him while he is eating.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_24::
    .string "He shall flee from the iron\n"
    .string "weapon, and the bow of steel shall\l"
    .string "strike him through.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_25::
    .string "It is drawn, and cometh out of the\n"
    .string "body; yea, the glittering sword\l"
    .string "cometh out of his gall: terrors are\l"
    .string "upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_26::
    .string "All darkness shall be hid in his\n"
    .string "secret places: a fire not blown\l"
    .string "shall consume him; it shall go\l"
    .string "ill with him that is left in his\l"
    .string "tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_27::
    .string "The heaven shall reveal his\n"
    .string "iniquity; and the earth shall rise\l"
    .string "up against him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_28::
    .string "The increase of his house shall\n"
    .string "depart, and his goods shall flow\l"
    .string "away in the day of his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Job_20_29::
    .string "This is the portion of a wicked man\n"
    .string "from God, and the heritage\l"
    .string "appointed unto him by God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_1::
    .string "But Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_21_2::
    .string "Hear diligently my speech, and\n"
    .string "let this be your consolations$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_3::
    .string "Suffer me that I may speak; and\n"
    .string "after that I have spoken, mock on.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_4::
    .string "As for me, is my complaint to man?\n"
    .string "and if it were so, why should not my\l"
    .string "spirit be troubled?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_5::
    .string "Mark me, and be astonished, and lay\n"
    .string "your hand upon your mouth$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_6::
    .string "Even when I remember I am afraid,\n"
    .string "and trembling taketh hold on my\l"
    .string "flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_7::
    .string "Wherefore do the wicked live,\n"
    .string "become old, yea, are mighty in\l"
    .string "power?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_8::
    .string "Their seed is established in their\n"
    .string "sight with them, and their offspring\l"
    .string "before their eyes$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_9::
    .string "Their houses are safe from fear,\n"
    .string "neither is the rod of God upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_10::
    .string "Their bull gendereth, and faileth\n"
    .string "not; their cow calveth, and casteth\l"
    .string "not her calf.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_11::
    .string "They send forth their little ones\n"
    .string "like a flock, and their children\l"
    .string "dance.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_12::
    .string "They take the timbrel and harp, and\n"
    .string "rejoice at the sound of the organ.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_13::
    .string "They spend their days in wealth,\n"
    .string "and in a moment go down to the grave.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_14::
    .string "Therefore they say unto God, Depart\n"
    .string "from us; for we desire not the\l"
    .string "knowledge of thy ways.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_15::
    .string "What is the Almighty, that we\n"
    .string "should serve him? and what profit\l"
    .string "should we have, if we pray unto him?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_16::
    .string "Lo, their good is not in their hand:\n"
    .string "the counsel of the wicked is far\l"
    .string "from me$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_17::
    .string "How oft is the candle of the wicked\n"
    .string "put out! and how oft cometh their\l"
    .string "destruction upon them! God\l"
    .string "distributeth sorrows in his anger.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_18::
    .string "They are as stubble before the\n"
    .string "wind, and as chaff that the storm\l"
    .string "carrieth away.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_19::
    .string "God layeth up his iniquity for his\n"
    .string "children: he rewardeth him, and he\l"
    .string "shall know it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_20::
    .string "His eyes shall see his\n"
    .string "destruction, and he shall drink of\l"
    .string "the wrath of the Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_21::
    .string "For what pleasure hath he in his\n"
    .string "house after him, when the number of\l"
    .string "his months is cut off in the midst?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_22::
    .string "Shall any teach God knowledge?\n"
    .string "seeing he judgeth those that are high$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_23::
    .string "One dieth in his full strength,\n"
    .string "being wholly at ease and quiet.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_24::
    .string "His breasts are full of milk, and\n"
    .string "his bones are moistened with marrow.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_25::
    .string "And another dieth in the bitterness\n"
    .string "of his soul, and never eateth with\l"
    .string "pleasure.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_26::
    .string "They shall lie down alike in the\n"
    .string "dust, and the worms shall cover\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_27::
    .string "Behold, I know your thoughts, and\n"
    .string "the devices which ye wrongfully\l"
    .string "imagine against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_28::
    .string "For ye say, Where is the house of the\n"
    .string "prince? and where are the dwelling\l"
    .string "places of the wicked?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_29::
    .string "Have ye not asked them that go by\n"
    .string "the way? and do ye not know their\l"
    .string "tokens,"
Bible_Text_Job_21_30::
    .string "That the wicked is reserved to the\n"
    .string "day of destruction? they shall be\l"
    .string "brought forth to the day of wrath$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_31::
    .string "Who shall declare his way to his\n"
    .string "face? and who shall repay him what\l"
    .string "he hath done?"
Bible_Text_Job_21_32::
    .string "Yet shall he be brought to the\n"
    .string "grave, and shall remain in the tomb$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_33::
    .string "The clods of the valley shall be\n"
    .string "sweet unto him, and every man shall\l"
    .string "draw after him, as there are\l"
    .string "innumerable before him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_21_34::
    .string "How then comfort ye me in vain,\n"
    .string "seeing in your answers there\l"
    .string "remaineth falsehood?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_1::
    .string "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered\n"
    .string "and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_22_2::
    .string "Can a man be profitable unto God,\n"
    .string "as he that is wise may be profitable\l"
    .string "unto himself?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_3::
    .string "Is it any pleasure to the\n"
    .string "Almighty, that thou art righteous?\l"
    .string "or is it gain to him, that thou makest\l"
    .string "thy ways perfect?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_4::
    .string "Will he reprove thee for fear of\n"
    .string "thee? will he enter with thee into\l"
    .string "judgment?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_5::
    .string "Is not thy wickedness great? and\n"
    .string "thine iniquities infinite?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_6::
    .string "For thou hast taken a pledge from\n"
    .string "thy brother for nought, and\l"
    .string "stripped the naked of their\l"
    .string "clothing$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_7::
    .string "Thou hast not given water to the\n"
    .string "weary to drink, and thou hast\l"
    .string "withholden bread from the hungry.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_8::
    .string "But as for the mighty man, he had the\n"
    .string "earth; and the honourable man dwelt\l"
    .string "in it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_9::
    .string "Thou hast sent widows away empty,\n"
    .string "and the arms of the fatherless have\l"
    .string "been broken.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_10::
    .string "Therefore snares are round about\n"
    .string "thee, and sudden fear troubleth\l"
    .string "thee;"
Bible_Text_Job_22_11::
    .string "Or darkness, that thou canst not\n"
    .string "see; and abundance of waters cover\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_12::
    .string "Is not God in the height of heaven?\n"
    .string "and behold the height of the stars,\l"
    .string "how high they are!"
Bible_Text_Job_22_13::
    .string "And thou sayest, How doth God know?\n"
    .string "can he judge through the dark cloud?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_14::
    .string "Thick clouds are a covering to him,\n"
    .string "that he seeth not; and he walketh in\l"
    .string "the circuit of heaven$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_15::
    .string "Hast thou marked the old way which\n"
    .string "wicked men have trodden?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_16::
    .string "Which were cut down out of time,\n"
    .string "whose foundation was overflown with\l"
    .string "a flood:"
Bible_Text_Job_22_17::
    .string "Which said unto God, Depart from\n"
    .string "us: and what can the Almighty do for\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_Job_22_18::
    .string "Yet he filled their houses with\n"
    .string "good things: but the counsel of the\l"
    .string "wicked is far from me$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_19::
    .string "The righteous see it, and are glad:\n"
    .string "and the innocent laugh them to scorn.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_20::
    .string "Whereas our substance is not cut\n"
    .string "down, but the remnant of them the\l"
    .string "fire consumeth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_21::
    .string "Acquaint now thyself with him, and\n"
    .string "be at peace: thereby good shall\l"
    .string "come unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_22::
    .string "Receive, I pray thee, the law from\n"
    .string "his mouth, and lay up his words in\l"
    .string "thine heart.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_23::
    .string "If thou return to the Almighty,\n"
    .string "thou shalt be built up, thou shalt\l"
    .string "put away iniquity far from thy\l"
    .string "tabernacles.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_24::
    .string "Then shalt thou lay up gold as\n"
    .string "dust, and the gold of Ophir as the\l"
    .string "stones of the brooks.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_25::
    .string "Yea, the Almighty shall be thy\n"
    .string "defence, and thou shalt have plenty\l"
    .string "of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_26::
    .string "For then shalt thou have thy\n"
    .string "delight in the Almighty, and shalt\l"
    .string "lift up thy face unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_27::
    .string "Thou shalt make thy prayer unto\n"
    .string "him, and he shall hear thee, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt pay thy vows.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_28::
    .string "Thou shalt also decree a thing, and\n"
    .string "it shall be established unto thee:\l"
    .string "and the light shall shine upon thy\l"
    .string "ways.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_29::
    .string "When men are cast down, then thou\n"
    .string "shalt say, There is lifting up; and\l"
    .string "he shall save the humble person.$"
Bible_Text_Job_22_30::
    .string "He shall deliver the island of\n"
    .string "the innocent: and it is delivered by\l"
    .string "the pureness of thine hands.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_1::
    .string "Then Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_23_2::
    .string "Even to day is my complaint bitter:\n"
    .string "my stroke is heavier than my groaning$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_3::
    .string "Oh that I knew where I might find\n"
    .string "him! that I might come even to his\l"
    .string "seat!"
Bible_Text_Job_23_4::
    .string "I would order my cause before him,\n"
    .string "and fill my mouth with arguments$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_5::
    .string "I would know the words which he\n"
    .string "would answer me, and understand what\l"
    .string "he would say unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_6::
    .string "Will he plead against me with his\n"
    .string "great power? No; but he would put\l"
    .string "strength in me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_7::
    .string "There the righteous might dispute\n"
    .string "with him; so should I be delivered\l"
    .string "for ever from my judge.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_8::
    .string "Behold, I go forward, but he is not\n"
    .string "there; and backward, but I cannot\l"
    .string "perceive him:"
Bible_Text_Job_23_9::
    .string "On the left hand, where he doth\n"
    .string "work, but I cannot behold him: he\l"
    .string "hideth himself on the right hand,\l"
    .string "that I cannot see him:"
Bible_Text_Job_23_10::
    .string "But he knoweth the way that I take:\n"
    .string "when he hath tried me, I shall come\l"
    .string "forth as gold$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_11::
    .string "My foot hath held his steps, his\n"
    .string "way have I kept, and not declined.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_12::
    .string "Neither have I gone back from the\n"
    .string "commandment of his lips; I have\l"
    .string "esteemed the words of his mouth more\l"
    .string "than my necessary food.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_13::
    .string "But he is in one mind, and who can\n"
    .string "turn him? and what his soul\l"
    .string "desireth, even that he doeth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_14::
    .string "For he performeth the thing that is\n"
    .string "appointed for me: and many such\l"
    .string "things are with him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_15::
    .string "Therefore am I troubled at his\n"
    .string "presence: when I consider, I am\l"
    .string "afraid of him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_23_16::
    .string "For God maketh my heart soft, and\n"
    .string "the Almighty troubleth me:"
Bible_Text_Job_23_17::
    .string "Because I was not cut off before the\n"
    .string "darkness, neither hath he covered the\l"
    .string "darkness from my face$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_1::
    .string "Why, seeing times are not hidden\n"
    .string "from the Almighty, do they that know\l"
    .string "him not see his days?"
Bible_Text_Job_24_2::
    .string "Some remove the landmarks; they\n"
    .string "violently take away flocks, and\l"
    .string "feed thereof$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_3::
    .string "They drive away the ass of the\n"
    .string "fatherless, they take the widow’s ox\l"
    .string "for a pledge.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_4::
    .string "They turn the needy out of the way:\n"
    .string "the poor of the earth hide\l"
    .string "themselves together.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_5::
    .string "Behold, as wild asses in the\n"
    .string "desert, go they forth to their work;\l"
    .string "rising betimes for a prey: the\l"
    .string "wilderness yieldeth food for them\l"
    .string "and for their children.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_6::
    .string "They reap every one his corn in the\n"
    .string "field: and they gather the vintage\l"
    .string "of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_7::
    .string "They cause the naked to lodge\n"
    .string "without clothing, that they have no\l"
    .string "covering in the cold.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_8::
    .string "They are wet with the showers of the\n"
    .string "mountains, and embrace the rock for\l"
    .string "want of a shelter.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_9::
    .string "They pluck the fatherless from\n"
    .string "the breast, and take a pledge of the\l"
    .string "poor.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_10::
    .string "They cause him to go naked without\n"
    .string "clothing, and they take away the\l"
    .string "sheaf from the hungry;"
Bible_Text_Job_24_11::
    .string "Which make oil within their walls,\n"
    .string "and tread their winepresses, and\l"
    .string "suffer thirst$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_12::
    .string "Men groan from out of the city, and\n"
    .string "the soul of the wounded crieth out:\l"
    .string "yet God layeth not folly to them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_13::
    .string "They are of those that rebel\n"
    .string "against the light; they know not the\l"
    .string "ways thereof, nor abide in the paths\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_14::
    .string "The murderer rising with the light\n"
    .string "killeth the poor and needy, and in\l"
    .string "the night is as a thief.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_15::
    .string "The eye also of the adulterer\n"
    .string "waiteth for the twilight, saying, No\l"
    .string "eye shall see me: and disguiseth his\l"
    .string "face.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_16::
    .string "In the dark they dig through houses,\n"
    .string "which they had marked for themselves\l"
    .string "in the daytime: they know not the\l"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_17::
    .string "For the morning is to them even as\n"
    .string "the shadow of death: if one know\l"
    .string "them, they are in the terrors of the\l"
    .string "shadow of death.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_18::
    .string "He is swift as the waters; their\n"
    .string "portion is cursed in the earth: he\l"
    .string "beholdeth not the way of the\l"
    .string "vineyards.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_19::
    .string "Drought and heat consume the snow\n"
    .string "waters: so doth the grave those which\l"
    .string "have sinned.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_20::
    .string "The womb shall forget him; the worm\n"
    .string "shall feed sweetly on him; he\l"
    .string "shall be no more remembered; and\l"
    .string "wickedness shall be broken as a\l"
    .string "tree.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_21::
    .string "He evil entreateth the barren that\n"
    .string "beareth not: and doeth not good to\l"
    .string "the widow.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_22::
    .string "He draweth also the mighty with his\n"
    .string "power: he riseth up, and no man is\l"
    .string "sure of life.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_23::
    .string "Though it be given him to be in\n"
    .string "safety, whereon he resteth; yet his\l"
    .string "eyes are upon their ways.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_24::
    .string "They are exalted for a little\n"
    .string "while, but are gone and brought low;\l"
    .string "they are taken out of the way as all\l"
    .string "other, and cut off as the tops of the\l"
    .string "ears of corn.$"
Bible_Text_Job_24_25::
    .string "And if it be not so now, who will\n"
    .string "make me a liar, and make my speech\l"
    .string "nothing worth?"
Bible_Text_Job_25_1::
    .string "Then answered Bildad the Shuhite,\n"
    .string "and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_25_2::
    .string "Dominion and fear are with him, he\n"
    .string "maketh peace in his high places$"
Bible_Text_Job_25_3::
    .string "Is there any number of his armies?\n"
    .string "and upon whom doth not his light\l"
    .string "arise?"
Bible_Text_Job_25_4::
    .string "How then can man be justified with\n"
    .string "God? or how can he be clean that is\l"
    .string "born of a woman?"
Bible_Text_Job_25_5::
    .string "Behold even to the moon, and it\n"
    .string "shineth not; yea, the stars are not\l"
    .string "pure in his sight$"
Bible_Text_Job_25_6::
    .string "How much less man, that is a worm?\n"
    .string "and the son of man, which is a worm?"
Bible_Text_Job_26_1::
    .string "But Job answered and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_26_2::
    .string "How hast thou helped him that is\n"
    .string "without power? how savest thou the\l"
    .string "arm that hath no strength?"
Bible_Text_Job_26_3::
    .string "How hast thou counselled him that\n"
    .string "hath no wisdom? and how hast thou\l"
    .string "plentifully declared the thing as\l"
    .string "it is?"
Bible_Text_Job_26_4::
    .string "To whom hast thou uttered words? and\n"
    .string "whose spirit came from thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_26_5::
    .string "Dead things are formed from under\n"
    .string "the waters, and the inhabitants\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_6::
    .string "Hell is naked before him, and\n"
    .string "destruction hath no covering.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_7::
    .string "He stretcheth out the north over the\n"
    .string "empty place, and hangeth the earth\l"
    .string "upon nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_8::
    .string "He bindeth up the waters in his\n"
    .string "thick clouds; and the cloud is not\l"
    .string "rent under them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_9::
    .string "He holdeth back the face of his\n"
    .string "throne, and spreadeth his cloud\l"
    .string "upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_10::
    .string "He hath compassed the waters with\n"
    .string "bounds, until the day and night come\l"
    .string "to an end.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_11::
    .string "The pillars of heaven tremble and\n"
    .string "are astonished at his reproof.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_12::
    .string "He divideth the sea with his power,\n"
    .string "and by his understanding he smiteth\l"
    .string "through the proud.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_13::
    .string "By his spirit he hath garnished the\n"
    .string "heavens; his hand hath formed the\l"
    .string "crooked serpent.$"
Bible_Text_Job_26_14::
    .string "Lo, these are parts of his ways: but\n"
    .string "how little a portion is heard of\l"
    .string "him? but the thunder of his power who\l"
    .string "can understand?"
Bible_Text_Job_27_1::
    .string "Moreover Job continued his\n"
    .string "parable, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_27_2::
    .string "As God liveth, who hath taken away\n"
    .string "my judgment; and the Almighty, who\l"
    .string "hath vexed my soul;"
Bible_Text_Job_27_3::
    .string "All the while my breath is in me,\n"
    .string "and the spirit of God is in my\l"
    .string "nostrils;"
Bible_Text_Job_27_4::
    .string "My lips shall not speak\n"
    .string "wickedness, nor my tongue utter\l"
    .string "deceit$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_5::
    .string "God forbid that I should justify\n"
    .string "you: till I die I will not remove\l"
    .string "mine integrity from me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_6::
    .string "My righteousness I hold fast, and\n"
    .string "will not let it go: my heart shall\l"
    .string "not reproach me so long as I live.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_7::
    .string "Let mine enemy be as the wicked, and\n"
    .string "he that riseth up against me as the\l"
    .string "unrighteous.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_8::
    .string "For what is the hope of the\n"
    .string "hypocrite, though he hath gained,\l"
    .string "when God taketh away his soul?"
Bible_Text_Job_27_9::
    .string "Will God hear his cry when trouble\n"
    .string "cometh upon him?"
Bible_Text_Job_27_10::
    .string "Will he delight himself in the\n"
    .string "Almighty? will he always call\l"
    .string "upon God?"
Bible_Text_Job_27_11::
    .string "I will teach you by the hand of\n"
    .string "God: that which is with the Almighty\l"
    .string "will I not conceal$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_12::
    .string "Behold, all ye yourselves have\n"
    .string "seen it; why then are ye thus\l"
    .string "altogether vain?"
Bible_Text_Job_27_13::
    .string "This is the portion of a wicked man\n"
    .string "with God, and the heritage of\l"
    .string "oppressors, which they shall\l"
    .string "receive of the Almighty$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_14::
    .string "If his children be multiplied, it\n"
    .string "is for the sword: and his offspring\l"
    .string "shall not be satisfied with bread.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_15::
    .string "Those that remain of him shall be\n"
    .string "buried in death: and his widows\l"
    .string "shall not weep.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_16::
    .string "Though he heap up silver as the\n"
    .string "dust, and prepare raiment as the\l"
    .string "clay;"
Bible_Text_Job_27_17::
    .string "He may prepare it, but the just\n"
    .string "shall put it on, and the innocent\l"
    .string "shall divide the silver$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_18::
    .string "He buildeth his house as a moth, and\n"
    .string "as a booth that the keeper maketh.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_19::
    .string "The rich man shall lie down, but\n"
    .string "he shall not be gathered: he\l"
    .string "openeth his eyes, and he is not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_20::
    .string "Terrors take hold on him as waters,\n"
    .string "a tempest stealeth him away in the\l"
    .string "night.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_21::
    .string "The east wind carrieth him away, and\n"
    .string "he departeth: and as a storm hurleth\l"
    .string "him out of his place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_22::
    .string "For God shall cast upon him, and\n"
    .string "not spare: he would fain flee out\l"
    .string "of his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Job_27_23::
    .string "Men shall clap their hands at\n"
    .string "him, and shall hiss him out of his\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_1::
    .string "Surely there is a vein for the\n"
    .string "silver, and a place for gold where\l"
    .string "they fine it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_2::
    .string "Iron is taken out of the earth, and\n"
    .string "brass is molten out of the stone.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_3::
    .string "He setteth an end to darkness, and\n"
    .string "searcheth out all perfection: the\l"
    .string "stones of darkness, and the shadow of\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_4::
    .string "The flood breaketh out from the\n"
    .string "inhabitant; even the waters\l"
    .string "forgotten of the foot: they are dried\l"
    .string "up, they are gone away from men.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_5::
    .string "As for the earth, out of it cometh\n"
    .string "bread: and under it is turned up as\l"
    .string "it were fire.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_6::
    .string "The stones of it are the place of\n"
    .string "sapphires: and it hath dust of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_7::
    .string "There is a path which no fowl\n"
    .string "knoweth, and which the vulture’s eye\l"
    .string "hath not seen:"
Bible_Text_Job_28_8::
    .string "The lion’s whelps have not\n"
    .string "trodden it, nor the fierce lion\l"
    .string "passed by it$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_9::
    .string "He putteth forth his hand upon the\n"
    .string "rock; he overturneth the mountains by\l"
    .string "the roots.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_10::
    .string "He cutteth out rivers among the\n"
    .string "rocks; and his eye seeth every\l"
    .string "precious thing.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_11::
    .string "He bindeth the floods from\n"
    .string "overflowing; and the thing that is\l"
    .string "hid bringeth he forth to light.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_12::
    .string "But where shall wisdom be found?\n"
    .string "and where is the place of\l"
    .string "understanding?"
Bible_Text_Job_28_13::
    .string "Man knoweth not the price thereof;\n"
    .string "neither is it found in the land of\l"
    .string "the living$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_14::
    .string "The depth saith, It is not in me:\n"
    .string "and the sea saith, It is not with me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_15::
    .string "It cannot be gotten for gold,\n"
    .string "neither shall silver be weighed\l"
    .string "for the price thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_16::
    .string "It cannot be valued with the gold\n"
    .string "of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or\l"
    .string "the sapphire.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_17::
    .string "The gold and the crystal cannot\n"
    .string "equal it: and the exchange of it\l"
    .string "shall not be for jewels of fine\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_18::
    .string "No mention shall be made of coral,\n"
    .string "or of pearls: for the price of\l"
    .string "wisdom is above rubies.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_19::
    .string "The topaz of Ethiopia shall not\n"
    .string "equal it, neither shall it be\l"
    .string "valued with pure gold.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_20::
    .string "Whence then cometh wisdom? and where\n"
    .string "is the place of understanding?"
Bible_Text_Job_28_21::
    .string "Seeing it is hid from the eyes of\n"
    .string "all living, and kept close from\l"
    .string "the fowls of the air$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_22::
    .string "Destruction and death say, We have\n"
    .string "heard the fame thereof with our ears.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_23::
    .string "God understandeth the way thereof,\n"
    .string "and he knoweth the place thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_24::
    .string "For he looketh to the ends of the\n"
    .string "earth, and seeth under the whole\l"
    .string "heaven;"
Bible_Text_Job_28_25::
    .string "To make the weight for the winds;\n"
    .string "and he weigheth the waters by measure$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_26::
    .string "When he made a decree for the rain,\n"
    .string "and a way for the lightning of the\l"
    .string "thunder:"
Bible_Text_Job_28_27::
    .string "Then did he see it, and declare it;\n"
    .string "he prepared it, yea, and searched it\l"
    .string "out$"
Bible_Text_Job_28_28::
    .string "And unto man he said, Behold, the\n"
    .string "fear of the LORD, that is wisdom; and\l"
    .string "to depart from evil is\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_1::
    .string "Moreover Job continued his\n"
    .string "parable, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_29_2::
    .string "Oh that I were as in months past, as\n"
    .string "in the days when God preserved me;"
Bible_Text_Job_29_3::
    .string "When his candle shined upon my\n"
    .string "head, and when by his light I walked\l"
    .string "through darkness;"
Bible_Text_Job_29_4::
    .string "As I was in the days of my youth,\n"
    .string "when the secret of God was upon my\l"
    .string "tabernacle;"
Bible_Text_Job_29_5::
    .string "When the Almighty was yet with me,\n"
    .string "when my children were about me;"
Bible_Text_Job_29_6::
    .string "When I washed my steps with butter,\n"
    .string "and the rock poured me out rivers of\l"
    .string "oil;"
Bible_Text_Job_29_7::
    .string "When I went out to the gate through\n"
    .string "the city, when I prepared my seat in\l"
    .string "the street!"
Bible_Text_Job_29_8::
    .string "The young men saw me, and hid\n"
    .string "themselves: and the aged arose, and\l"
    .string "stood up$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_9::
    .string "The princes refrained talking, and\n"
    .string "laid their hand on their mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_10::
    .string "The nobles held their peace, and\n"
    .string "their tongue cleaved to the roof of\l"
    .string "their mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_11::
    .string "When the ear heard me, then it\n"
    .string "blessed me; and when the eye saw me,\l"
    .string "it gave witness to me:"
Bible_Text_Job_29_12::
    .string "Because I delivered the poor that\n"
    .string "cried, and the fatherless, and him\l"
    .string "that had none to help him$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_13::
    .string "The blessing of him that was ready\n"
    .string "to perish came upon me: and I caused\l"
    .string "the widow’s heart to sing for joy.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_14::
    .string "I put on righteousness, and it\n"
    .string "clothed me: my judgment was as a robe\l"
    .string "and a diadem.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_15::
    .string "I was eyes to the blind, and feet\n"
    .string "was I to the lame.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_16::
    .string "I was a father to the poor: and the\n"
    .string "cause which I knew not I searched out.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_17::
    .string "And I brake the jaws of the wicked,\n"
    .string "and plucked the spoil out of his\l"
    .string "teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_18::
    .string "Then I said, I shall die in my\n"
    .string "nest, and I shall multiply my days\l"
    .string "as the sand.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_19::
    .string "My root was spread out by the\n"
    .string "waters, and the dew lay all night\l"
    .string "upon my branch.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_20::
    .string "My glory was fresh in me, and my bow\n"
    .string "was renewed in my hand.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_21::
    .string "Unto me men gave ear, and waited,\n"
    .string "and kept silence at my counsel.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_22::
    .string "After my words they spake not\n"
    .string "again; and my speech dropped upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_23::
    .string "And they waited for me as for the\n"
    .string "rain; and they opened their mouth\l"
    .string "wide as for the latter rain.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_24::
    .string "If I laughed on them, they believed\n"
    .string "it not; and the light of my\l"
    .string "countenance they cast not down.$"
Bible_Text_Job_29_25::
    .string "I chose out their way, and sat\n"
    .string "chief, and dwelt as a king in the\l"
    .string "army, as one that comforteth the\l"
    .string "mourners.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_1::
    .string "But now they that are younger than I\n"
    .string "have me in derision, whose fathers I\l"
    .string "would have disdained to have set\l"
    .string "with the dogs of my flock.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_2::
    .string "Yea, whereto might the strength of\n"
    .string "their hands profit me, in whom old\l"
    .string "age was perished?"
Bible_Text_Job_30_3::
    .string "For want and famine they were\n"
    .string "solitary; fleeing into the\l"
    .string "wilderness in former time desolate\l"
    .string "and waste$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_4::
    .string "Who cut up mallows by the bushes,\n"
    .string "and juniper roots for their meat.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_5::
    .string "They were driven forth from among\n"
    .string "men, (they cried after them as after\l"
    .string "a thief;)"
Bible_Text_Job_30_6::
    .string "To dwell in the cliffs of the\n"
    .string "valleys, in caves of the earth, and\l"
    .string "in the rocks$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_7::
    .string "Among the bushes they brayed; under\n"
    .string "the nettles they were gathered\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_8::
    .string "They were children of fools, yea,\n"
    .string "children of base men: they were\l"
    .string "viler than the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_9::
    .string "And now am I their song, yea, I am\n"
    .string "their byword.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_10::
    .string "They abhor me, they flee far from\n"
    .string "me, and spare not to spit in my face.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_11::
    .string "Because he hath loosed my cord, and\n"
    .string "afflicted me, they have also let\l"
    .string "loose the bridle before me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_12::
    .string "Upon my right hand rise the youth;\n"
    .string "they push away my feet, and they\l"
    .string "raise up against me the ways of\l"
    .string "their destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_13::
    .string "They mar my path, they set forward\n"
    .string "my calamity, they have no helper.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_14::
    .string "They came upon me as a wide\n"
    .string "breaking in of waters: in the\l"
    .string "desolation they rolled themselves\l"
    .string "upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_15::
    .string "Terrors are turned upon me: they\n"
    .string "pursue my soul as the wind: and my\l"
    .string "welfare passeth away as a cloud.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_16::
    .string "And now my soul is poured out upon\n"
    .string "me; the days of affliction have\l"
    .string "taken hold upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_17::
    .string "My bones are pierced in me in the\n"
    .string "night season: and my sinews take no\l"
    .string "rest.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_18::
    .string "By the great force of my disease is\n"
    .string "my garment changed: it bindeth me\l"
    .string "about as the collar of my coat.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_19::
    .string "He hath cast me into the mire, and I\n"
    .string "am become like dust and ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_20::
    .string "I cry unto thee, and thou dost not\n"
    .string "hear me: I stand up, and thou\l"
    .string "regardest me not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_21::
    .string "Thou art become cruel to me: with\n"
    .string "thy strong hand thou opposest\l"
    .string "thyself against me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_22::
    .string "Thou liftest me up to the wind;\n"
    .string "thou causest me to ride upon it, and\l"
    .string "dissolvest my substance.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_23::
    .string "For I know that thou wilt bring me\n"
    .string "to death, and to the house appointed\l"
    .string "for all living.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_24::
    .string "Howbeit he will not stretch out\n"
    .string "his hand to the grave, though they\l"
    .string "cry in his destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_25::
    .string "Did not I weep for him that was in\n"
    .string "trouble? was not my soul grieved for\l"
    .string "the poor?"
Bible_Text_Job_30_26::
    .string "When I looked for good, then evil\n"
    .string "came unto me: and when I waited for\l"
    .string "light, there came darkness$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_27::
    .string "My bowels boiled, and rested not:\n"
    .string "the days of affliction prevented me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_28::
    .string "I went mourning without the sun: I\n"
    .string "stood up, and I cried in the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_29::
    .string "I am a brother to dragons, and a\n"
    .string "companion to owls.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_30::
    .string "My skin is black upon me, and my\n"
    .string "bones are burned with heat.$"
Bible_Text_Job_30_31::
    .string "My harp also is turned to mourning,\n"
    .string "and my organ into the voice of them\l"
    .string "that weep.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_1::
    .string "I made a covenant with mine eyes;\n"
    .string "why then should I think upon a maid?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_2::
    .string "For what portion of God is there\n"
    .string "from above? and what inheritance of\l"
    .string "the Almighty from on high?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_3::
    .string "Is not destruction to the wicked?\n"
    .string "and a strange punishment to the\l"
    .string "workers of iniquity?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_4::
    .string "Doth not he see my ways, and count\n"
    .string "all my steps?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_5::
    .string "If I have walked with vanity, or if\n"
    .string "my foot hath hasted to deceit;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_6::
    .string "Let me be weighed in an even\n"
    .string "balance that God may know mine\l"
    .string "integrity$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_7::
    .string "If my step hath turned out of the\n"
    .string "way, and mine heart walked after\l"
    .string "mine eyes, and if any blot hath\l"
    .string "cleaved to mine hands;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_8::
    .string "Then let me sow, and let another\n"
    .string "eat; yea, let my offspring be rooted\l"
    .string "out$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_9::
    .string "If mine heart have been deceived by\n"
    .string "a woman, or if I have laid wait at my\l"
    .string "neighbour’s door;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_10::
    .string "Then let my wife grind unto\n"
    .string "another, and let others bow down\l"
    .string "upon her$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_11::
    .string "For this is an heinous crime; yea,\n"
    .string "it is an iniquity to be punished by\l"
    .string "the judges.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_12::
    .string "For it is a fire that consumeth to\n"
    .string "destruction, and would root out all\l"
    .string "mine increase.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_13::
    .string "If I did despise the cause of my\n"
    .string "manservant or of my maidservant, when\l"
    .string "they contended with me;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_14::
    .string "What then shall I do when God\n"
    .string "riseth up? and when he visiteth,\l"
    .string "what shall I answer him?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_15::
    .string "Did not he that made me in the womb\n"
    .string "make him? and did not one fashion us\l"
    .string "in the womb?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_16::
    .string "If I have withheld the poor from\n"
    .string "their desire, or have caused the eyes\l"
    .string "of the widow to fail;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_17::
    .string "Or have eaten my morsel myself\n"
    .string "alone, and the fatherless hath not\l"
    .string "eaten thereof;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_18::
    .string "(For from my youth he was brought\n"
    .string "up with me, as with a father, and I\l"
    .string "have guided her from my mother’s\l"
    .string "womb;)"
Bible_Text_Job_31_19::
    .string "If I have seen any perish for want\n"
    .string "of clothing, or any poor without\l"
    .string "covering;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_20::
    .string "If his loins have not blessed me,\n"
    .string "and if he were not warmed with the\l"
    .string "fleece of my sheep;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_21::
    .string "If I have lifted up my hand against\n"
    .string "the fatherless, when I saw my help\l"
    .string "in the gate:"
Bible_Text_Job_31_22::
    .string "Then let mine arm fall from my\n"
    .string "shoulder blade, and mine arm be\l"
    .string "broken from the bone$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_23::
    .string "For destruction from God was a\n"
    .string "terror to me, and by reason of his\l"
    .string "highness I could not endure.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_24::
    .string "If I have made gold my hope, or\n"
    .string "have said to the fine gold, Thou art\l"
    .string "my confidence;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_25::
    .string "If I rejoice because my wealth was\n"
    .string "great, and because mine hand had\l"
    .string "gotten much;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_26::
    .string "If I beheld the sun when it shined,\n"
    .string "or the moon walking in brightness;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_27::
    .string "And my heart hath been secretly\n"
    .string "enticed, or my mouth hath kissed my\l"
    .string "hand:"
Bible_Text_Job_31_28::
    .string "This also were an iniquity to be\n"
    .string "punished by the judge: for I should\l"
    .string "have denied the God that is above$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_29::
    .string "If I rejoice at the destruction of\n"
    .string "him that hated me, or lifted up\l"
    .string "myself when evil found him:"
Bible_Text_Job_31_30::
    .string "Neither have I suffered my mouth to\n"
    .string "sin by wishing a curse to his soul$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_31::
    .string "If the men of my tabernacle said\n"
    .string "not, Oh that we had of his flesh! we\l"
    .string "cannot be satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_32::
    .string "The stranger did not lodge in the\n"
    .string "street: but I opened my doors to the\l"
    .string "traveller.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_33::
    .string "If I covered my transgressions as\n"
    .string "Adam, by hiding mine iniquity in my\l"
    .string "bosom:"
Bible_Text_Job_31_34::
    .string "Did I fear a great multitude, or did\n"
    .string "the contempt of families terrify\l"
    .string "me, that I kept silence, and went\l"
    .string "not out of the door?"
Bible_Text_Job_31_35::
    .string "Oh that one would hear me! behold,\n"
    .string "my desire is, that the Almighty\l"
    .string "would answer me, and that mine\l"
    .string "adversary had written a book$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_36::
    .string "Surely I would take it upon my\n"
    .string "shoulder, and bind it as a crown to\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_37::
    .string "I would declare unto him the\n"
    .string "number of my steps; as a prince\l"
    .string "would I go near unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_31_38::
    .string "If my land cry against me, or that\n"
    .string "the furrows likewise thereof\l"
    .string "complain;"
Bible_Text_Job_31_39::
    .string "If I have eaten the fruits thereof\n"
    .string "without money, or have caused the\l"
    .string "owners thereof to lose their life:"
Bible_Text_Job_31_40::
    .string "Let thistles grow instead of wheat,\n"
    .string "and cockle instead of barley The\l"
    .string "words of Job are ended.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_1::
    .string "So these three men ceased to answer\n"
    .string "Job, because he was righteous in his\l"
    .string "own eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_2::
    .string "Then was kindled the wrath of\n"
    .string "Elihu the son of Barachel the\l"
    .string "Buzite, of the kindred of Ram:\l"
    .string "against Job was his wrath kindled,\l"
    .string "because he justified himself rather\l"
    .string "than God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_3::
    .string "Also against his three friends was\n"
    .string "his wrath kindled, because they had\l"
    .string "found no answer, and yet had\l"
    .string "condemned Job.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_4::
    .string "Now Elihu had waited till Job had\n"
    .string "spoken, because they were elder\l"
    .string "than he.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_5::
    .string "When Elihu saw that there was no\n"
    .string "answer in the mouth of these three\l"
    .string "men, then his wrath was kindled.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_6::
    .string "And Elihu the son of Barachel the\n"
    .string "Buzite answered and said, I am young,\l"
    .string "and ye are very old; wherefore I was\l"
    .string "afraid, and durst not shew you mine\l"
    .string "opinion.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_7::
    .string "I said, Days should speak, and\n"
    .string "multitude of years should teach\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_8::
    .string "But there is a spirit in man: and\n"
    .string "the inspiration of the Almighty\l"
    .string "giveth them understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_9::
    .string "Great men are not always wise:\n"
    .string "neither do the aged understand\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_10::
    .string "Therefore I said, Hearken to me; I\n"
    .string "also will shew mine opinion.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_11::
    .string "Behold, I waited for your words; I\n"
    .string "gave ear to your reasons, whilst ye\l"
    .string "searched out what to say.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_12::
    .string "Yea, I attended unto you, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there was none of you that\l"
    .string "convinced Job, or that answered his\l"
    .string "words:"
Bible_Text_Job_32_13::
    .string "Lest ye should say, We have found\n"
    .string "out wisdom: God thrusteth him down,\l"
    .string "not man$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_14::
    .string "Now he hath not directed his words\n"
    .string "against me: neither will I answer\l"
    .string "him with your speeches.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_15::
    .string "They were amazed, they answered no\n"
    .string "more: they left off speaking.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_16::
    .string "When I had waited, (for they spake\n"
    .string "not, but stood still, and answered\l"
    .string "no more;)"
Bible_Text_Job_32_17::
    .string "I said, I will answer also my\n"
    .string "part, I also will shew mine opinion$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_18::
    .string "For I am full of matter, the\n"
    .string "spirit within me constraineth me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_19::
    .string "Behold, my belly is as wine which\n"
    .string "hath no vent; it is ready to burst\l"
    .string "like new bottles.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_20::
    .string "I will speak, that I may be\n"
    .string "refreshed: I will open my lips and\l"
    .string "answer.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_21::
    .string "Let me not, I pray you, accept any\n"
    .string "man’s person, neither let me give\l"
    .string "flattering titles unto man.$"
Bible_Text_Job_32_22::
    .string "For I know not to give flattering\n"
    .string "titles; in so doing my maker would\l"
    .string "soon take me away.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_1::
    .string "Wherefore, Job, I pray thee, hear my\n"
    .string "speeches, and hearken to all my\l"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_2::
    .string "Behold, now I have opened my mouth,\n"
    .string "my tongue hath spoken in my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_3::
    .string "My words shall be of the\n"
    .string "uprightness of my heart: and my\l"
    .string "lips shall utter knowledge\l"
    .string "clearly.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_4::
    .string "The spirit of God hath made me, and\n"
    .string "the breath of the Almighty hath\l"
    .string "given me life.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_5::
    .string "If thou canst answer me, set thy\n"
    .string "words in order before me, stand up.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_6::
    .string "Behold, I am according to thy wish\n"
    .string "in God’s stead: I also am formed out\l"
    .string "of the clay.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_7::
    .string "Behold, my terror shall not make\n"
    .string "thee afraid, neither shall my hand\l"
    .string "be heavy upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_8::
    .string "Surely thou hast spoken in mine\n"
    .string "hearing, and I have heard the voice\l"
    .string "of thy words, saying,"
Bible_Text_Job_33_9::
    .string "I am clean without transgression, I\n"
    .string "am innocent; neither is there\l"
    .string "iniquity in me$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_10::
    .string "Behold, he findeth occasions\n"
    .string "against me, he counteth me for his\l"
    .string "enemy,"
Bible_Text_Job_33_11::
    .string "He putteth my feet in the stocks, he\n"
    .string "marketh all my paths$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_12::
    .string "Behold, in this thou art not just: I\n"
    .string "will answer thee, that God is\l"
    .string "greater than man.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_13::
    .string "Why dost thou strive against him?\n"
    .string "for he giveth not account of any of\l"
    .string "his matters.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_14::
    .string "For God speaketh once, yea twice,\n"
    .string "yet man perceiveth it not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_15::
    .string "In a dream, in a vision of the night,\n"
    .string "when deep sleep falleth upon men,\l"
    .string "in slumberings upon the bed;"
Bible_Text_Job_33_16::
    .string "Then he openeth the ears of men, and\n"
    .string "sealeth their instruction,"
Bible_Text_Job_33_17::
    .string "That he may withdraw man from his\n"
    .string "purpose, and hide pride from man$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_18::
    .string "He keepeth back his soul from the\n"
    .string "pit, and his life from perishing by\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_19::
    .string "He is chastened also with pain\n"
    .string "upon his bed, and the multitude of\l"
    .string "his bones with strong pain:"
Bible_Text_Job_33_20::
    .string "So that his life abhorreth bread,\n"
    .string "and his soul dainty meat$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_21::
    .string "His flesh is consumed away, that it\n"
    .string "cannot be seen; and his bones that\l"
    .string "were not seen stick out.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_22::
    .string "Yea, his soul draweth near unto the\n"
    .string "grave, and his life to the\l"
    .string "destroyers.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_23::
    .string "If there be a messenger with him, an\n"
    .string "interpreter, one among a thousand,\l"
    .string "to shew unto man his uprightness:"
Bible_Text_Job_33_24::
    .string "Then he is gracious unto him, and\n"
    .string "saith, Deliver him from going down\l"
    .string "to the pit: I have found a ransom$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_25::
    .string "His flesh shall be fresher than a\n"
    .string "child’s: he shall return to the\l"
    .string "days of his youth:"
Bible_Text_Job_33_26::
    .string "He shall pray unto God, and he\n"
    .string "will be favourable unto him: and he\l"
    .string "shall see his face with joy: for he\l"
    .string "will render unto man his\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_27::
    .string "He looketh upon men, and if any\n"
    .string "say, I have sinned, and perverted\l"
    .string "that which was right, and it\l"
    .string "profited me not;"
Bible_Text_Job_33_28::
    .string "He will deliver his soul from\n"
    .string "going into the pit, and his life\l"
    .string "shall see the light$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_29::
    .string "Lo, all these things worketh God\n"
    .string "oftentimes with man,"
Bible_Text_Job_33_30::
    .string "To bring back his soul from the\n"
    .string "pit, to be enlightened with the\l"
    .string "light of the living$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_31::
    .string "Mark well, O Job, hearken unto me:\n"
    .string "hold thy peace, and I will speak.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_32::
    .string "If thou hast anything to say, answer\n"
    .string "me: speak, for I desire to justify\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_33_33::
    .string "If not, hearken unto me: hold thy\n"
    .string "peace, and I shall teach thee\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_1::
    .string "Furthermore Elihu answered and\n"
    .string "said,"
Bible_Text_Job_34_2::
    .string "Hear my words, O ye wise men; and\n"
    .string "give ear unto me, ye that have\l"
    .string "knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_3::
    .string "For the ear trieth words, as the\n"
    .string "mouth tasteth meat.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_4::
    .string "Let us choose to us judgment: let us\n"
    .string "know among ourselves what is good.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_5::
    .string "For Job hath said, I am righteous:\n"
    .string "and God hath taken away my judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_6::
    .string "Should I lie against my right? my\n"
    .string "wound is incurable without\l"
    .string "transgression.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_7::
    .string "What man is like Job, who drinketh\n"
    .string "up scorning like water?"
Bible_Text_Job_34_8::
    .string "Which goeth in company with the\n"
    .string "workers of iniquity, and walketh\l"
    .string "with wicked men$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_9::
    .string "For he hath said, It profiteth a man\n"
    .string "nothing that he should delight\l"
    .string "himself with God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_10::
    .string "Therefore hearken unto me ye men of\n"
    .string "understanding: far be it from God,\l"
    .string "that he should do wickedness; and\l"
    .string "from the Almighty, that he should\l"
    .string "commit iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_11::
    .string "For the work of a man shall he\n"
    .string "render unto him, and cause every man\l"
    .string "to find according to his ways.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_12::
    .string "Yea, surely God will not do\n"
    .string "wickedly, neither will the\l"
    .string "Almighty pervert judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_13::
    .string "Who hath given him a charge over the\n"
    .string "earth? or who hath disposed the\l"
    .string "whole world?"
Bible_Text_Job_34_14::
    .string "If he set his heart upon man, if he\n"
    .string "gather unto himself his spirit and\l"
    .string "his breath;"
Bible_Text_Job_34_15::
    .string "All flesh shall perish\n"
    .string "together, and man shall turn again\l"
    .string "unto dust$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_16::
    .string "If now thou hast understanding, hear\n"
    .string "this: hearken to the voice of my\l"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_17::
    .string "Shall even he that hateth right\n"
    .string "govern? and wilt thou condemn him\l"
    .string "that is most just?"
Bible_Text_Job_34_18::
    .string "Is it fit to say to a king, Thou art\n"
    .string "wicked? and to princes, Ye are\l"
    .string "ungodly?"
Bible_Text_Job_34_19::
    .string "How much less to him that\n"
    .string "accepteth not the persons of\l"
    .string "princes, nor regardeth the rich more\l"
    .string "than the poor? for they all are the\l"
    .string "work of his hands$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_20::
    .string "In a moment shall they die, and the\n"
    .string "people shall be troubled at\l"
    .string "midnight, and pass away: and the\l"
    .string "mighty shall be taken away without\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_21::
    .string "For his eyes are upon the ways of\n"
    .string "man, and he seeth all his goings.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_22::
    .string "There is no darkness, nor shadow of\n"
    .string "death, where the workers of iniquity\l"
    .string "may hide themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_23::
    .string "For he will not lay upon man more\n"
    .string "than right; that he should enter\l"
    .string "into judgment with God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_24::
    .string "He shall break in pieces mighty\n"
    .string "men without number, and set others in\l"
    .string "their stead.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_25::
    .string "Therefore he knoweth their works,\n"
    .string "and he overturneth them in the night,\l"
    .string "so that they are destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_26::
    .string "He striketh them as wicked men in\n"
    .string "the open sight of others;"
Bible_Text_Job_34_27::
    .string "Because they turned back from him,\n"
    .string "and would not consider any of his\l"
    .string "ways:"
Bible_Text_Job_34_28::
    .string "So that they cause the cry of the\n"
    .string "poor to come unto him, and he heareth\l"
    .string "the cry of the afflicted$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_29::
    .string "When he giveth quietness, who then\n"
    .string "can make trouble? and when he hideth\l"
    .string "his face, who then can behold him?\l"
    .string "whether it be done against a nation,\l"
    .string "or against a man only:"
Bible_Text_Job_34_30::
    .string "That the hypocrite reign not, lest\n"
    .string "the people be ensnared$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_31::
    .string "Surely it is meet to be said unto\n"
    .string "God, I have borne chastisement, I\l"
    .string "will not offend any more:"
Bible_Text_Job_34_32::
    .string "That which I see not teach thou me:\n"
    .string "if I have done iniquity, I will do\l"
    .string "no more$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_33::
    .string "Should it be according to thy mind?\n"
    .string "he will recompense it, whether thou\l"
    .string "refuse, or whether thou choose; and\l"
    .string "not I: therefore speak what thou\l"
    .string "knowest.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_34::
    .string "Let men of understanding tell me,\n"
    .string "and let a wise man hearken unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_35::
    .string "Job hath spoken without knowledge,\n"
    .string "and his words were without wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_36::
    .string "My desire is that Job may be tried\n"
    .string "unto the end because of his answers\l"
    .string "for wicked men.$"
Bible_Text_Job_34_37::
    .string "For he addeth rebellion unto his\n"
    .string "sin, he clappeth his hands among\l"
    .string "us, and multiplieth his words\l"
    .string "against God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_1::
    .string "Elihu spake moreover, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_35_2::
    .string "Thinkest thou this to be right, that\n"
    .string "thou saidst, My righteousness is more\l"
    .string "than God’s?"
Bible_Text_Job_35_3::
    .string "For thou saidst, What advantage\n"
    .string "will it be unto thee? and, What\l"
    .string "profit shall I have, if I be\l"
    .string "cleansed from my sin?"
Bible_Text_Job_35_4::
    .string "I will answer thee, and thy\n"
    .string "companions with thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_5::
    .string "Look unto the heavens, and see; and\n"
    .string "behold the clouds which are higher\l"
    .string "than thou.$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_6::
    .string "If thou sinnest, what doest thou\n"
    .string "against him? or if thy transgressions\l"
    .string "be multiplied, what doest thou unto\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_Job_35_7::
    .string "If thou be righteous, what givest\n"
    .string "thou him? or what receiveth he of\l"
    .string "thine hand?"
Bible_Text_Job_35_8::
    .string "Thy wickedness may hurt a man as\n"
    .string "thou art; and thy righteousness may\l"
    .string "profit the son of man$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_9::
    .string "By reason of the multitude of\n"
    .string "oppressions they make the\l"
    .string "oppressed to cry: they cry out by\l"
    .string "reason of the arm of the mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_10::
    .string "But none saith, Where is God my\n"
    .string "maker, who giveth songs in the night;"
Bible_Text_Job_35_11::
    .string "Who teacheth us more than the beasts\n"
    .string "of the earth, and maketh us wiser\l"
    .string "than the fowls of heaven?"
Bible_Text_Job_35_12::
    .string "There they cry, but none giveth\n"
    .string "answer, because of the pride of evil\l"
    .string "men$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_13::
    .string "Surely God will not hear vanity,\n"
    .string "neither will the Almighty regard\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_14::
    .string "Although thou sayest thou shalt\n"
    .string "not see him, yet judgment is before\l"
    .string "him; therefore trust thou in him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_35_15::
    .string "But now, because it is not so, he\n"
    .string "hath visited in his anger; yet he\l"
    .string "knoweth it not in great extremity:"
Bible_Text_Job_35_16::
    .string "Therefore doth Job open his mouth\n"
    .string "in vain; he multiplieth words\l"
    .string "without knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_1::
    .string "Elihu also proceeded, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_36_2::
    .string "Suffer me a little, and I will\n"
    .string "shew thee that I have yet to speak on\l"
    .string "God’s behalf$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_3::
    .string "I will fetch my knowledge from\n"
    .string "afar, and will ascribe\l"
    .string "righteousness to my Maker.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_4::
    .string "For truly my words shall not be\n"
    .string "false: he that is perfect in\l"
    .string "knowledge is with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_5::
    .string "Behold, God is mighty, and\n"
    .string "despiseth not any: he is mighty in\l"
    .string "strength and wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_6::
    .string "He preserveth not the life of the\n"
    .string "wicked: but giveth right to the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_7::
    .string "He withdraweth not his eyes from the\n"
    .string "righteous: but with kings are they on\l"
    .string "the throne; yea, he doth establish\l"
    .string "them for ever, and they are exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_8::
    .string "And if they be bound in fetters, and\n"
    .string "be holden in cords of affliction;"
Bible_Text_Job_36_9::
    .string "Then he sheweth them their work, and\n"
    .string "their transgressions that they have\l"
    .string "exceeded$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_10::
    .string "He openeth also their ear to\n"
    .string "discipline, and commandeth that\l"
    .string "they return from iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_11::
    .string "If they obey and serve him, they\n"
    .string "shall spend their days in\l"
    .string "prosperity, and their years in\l"
    .string "pleasures.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_12::
    .string "But if they obey not, they shall\n"
    .string "perish by the sword, and they shall\l"
    .string "die without knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_13::
    .string "But the hypocrites in heart heap\n"
    .string "up wrath: they cry not when he\l"
    .string "bindeth them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_14::
    .string "They die in youth, and their life is\n"
    .string "among the unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_15::
    .string "He delivereth the poor in his\n"
    .string "affliction, and openeth their ears\l"
    .string "in oppression.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_16::
    .string "Even so would he have removed thee\n"
    .string "out of the strait into a broad\l"
    .string "place, where there is no straitness;\l"
    .string "and that which should be set on thy\l"
    .string "table should be full of fatness.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_17::
    .string "But thou hast fulfilled the\n"
    .string "judgment of the wicked: judgment and\l"
    .string "justice take hold on thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_18::
    .string "Because there is wrath, beware lest\n"
    .string "he take thee away with his stroke:\l"
    .string "then a great ransom cannot deliver\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_19::
    .string "Will he esteem thy riches? no, not\n"
    .string "gold, nor all the forces of\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_20::
    .string "Desire not the night, when people\n"
    .string "are cut off in their place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_21::
    .string "Take heed, regard not iniquity: for\n"
    .string "this hast thou chosen rather than\l"
    .string "affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_22::
    .string "Behold, God exalteth by his power:\n"
    .string "who teacheth like him?"
Bible_Text_Job_36_23::
    .string "Who hath enjoined him his way? or\n"
    .string "who can say, Thou hast wrought\l"
    .string "iniquity?"
Bible_Text_Job_36_24::
    .string "Remember that thou magnify his work,\n"
    .string "which men behold$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_25::
    .string "Every man may see it; man may behold\n"
    .string "it afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_26::
    .string "Behold, God is great, and we know\n"
    .string "him not, neither can the number of\l"
    .string "his years be searched out.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_27::
    .string "For he maketh small the drops of\n"
    .string "water: they pour down rain according\l"
    .string "to the vapour thereof:"
Bible_Text_Job_36_28::
    .string "Which the clouds do drop and\n"
    .string "distil upon man abundantly$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_29::
    .string "Also can any understand the\n"
    .string "spreadings of the clouds, or the\l"
    .string "noise of his tabernacle?"
Bible_Text_Job_36_30::
    .string "Behold, he spreadeth his light\n"
    .string "upon it, and covereth the bottom of\l"
    .string "the sea$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_31::
    .string "For by them judgeth he the people;\n"
    .string "he giveth meat in abundance.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_32::
    .string "With clouds he covereth the light;\n"
    .string "and commandeth it not to shine by the\l"
    .string "cloud that cometh betwixt.$"
Bible_Text_Job_36_33::
    .string "The noise thereof sheweth\n"
    .string "concerning it, the cattle also\l"
    .string "concerning the vapour.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_1::
    .string "At this also my heart trembleth,\n"
    .string "and is moved out of his place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_2::
    .string "Hear attentively the noise of his\n"
    .string "voice, and the sound that goeth out\l"
    .string "of his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_3::
    .string "He directeth it under the whole\n"
    .string "heaven, and his lightning unto the\l"
    .string "ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_4::
    .string "After it a voice roareth: he\n"
    .string "thundereth with the voice of his\l"
    .string "excellency; and he will not stay\l"
    .string "them when his voice is heard.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_5::
    .string "God thundereth marvellously with\n"
    .string "his voice; great things doeth he,\l"
    .string "which we cannot comprehend.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_6::
    .string "For he saith to the snow, Be thou on\n"
    .string "the earth; likewise to the small\l"
    .string "rain, and to the great rain of his\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_7::
    .string "He sealeth up the hand of every\n"
    .string "man; that all men may know his work.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_8::
    .string "Then the beasts go into dens, and\n"
    .string "remain in their places.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_9::
    .string "Out of the south cometh the\n"
    .string "whirlwind: and cold out of the\l"
    .string "north.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_10::
    .string "By the breath of God frost is given:\n"
    .string "and the breadth of the waters is\l"
    .string "straitened.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_11::
    .string "Also by watering he wearieth the\n"
    .string "thick cloud: he scattereth his\l"
    .string "bright cloud:"
Bible_Text_Job_37_12::
    .string "And it is turned round about by his\n"
    .string "counsels: that they may do\l"
    .string "whatsoever he commandeth them upon\l"
    .string "the face of the world in the earth$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_13::
    .string "He causeth it to come, whether for\n"
    .string "correction, or for his land, or for\l"
    .string "mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_14::
    .string "Hearken unto this, O Job: stand\n"
    .string "still, and consider the wondrous\l"
    .string "works of God.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_15::
    .string "Dost thou know when God disposed\n"
    .string "them, and caused the light of his\l"
    .string "cloud to shine?"
Bible_Text_Job_37_16::
    .string "Dost thou know the balancings of\n"
    .string "the clouds, the wondrous works of\l"
    .string "him which is perfect in knowledge?"
Bible_Text_Job_37_17::
    .string "How thy garments are warm, when he\n"
    .string "quieteth the earth by the south wind?"
Bible_Text_Job_37_18::
    .string "Hast thou with him spread out the\n"
    .string "sky, which is strong, and as a molten\l"
    .string "looking glass?"
Bible_Text_Job_37_19::
    .string "Teach us what we shall say unto\n"
    .string "him; for we cannot order our speech\l"
    .string "by reason of darkness$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_20::
    .string "Shall it be told him that I speak?\n"
    .string "if a man speak, surely he shall be\l"
    .string "swallowed up.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_21::
    .string "And now men see not the bright\n"
    .string "light which is in the clouds: but the\l"
    .string "wind passeth, and cleanseth them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_22::
    .string "Fair weather cometh out of the\n"
    .string "north: with God is terrible majesty.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_23::
    .string "Touching the Almighty, we cannot\n"
    .string "find him out: he is excellent in\l"
    .string "power, and in judgment, and in\l"
    .string "plenty of justice: he will not\l"
    .string "afflict.$"
Bible_Text_Job_37_24::
    .string "Men do therefore fear him: he\n"
    .string "respecteth not any that are wise of\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_1::
    .string "Then the LORD answered Job out of\n"
    .string "the whirlwind, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_2::
    .string "Who is this that darkeneth counsel\n"
    .string "by words without knowledge?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_3::
    .string "Gird up now thy loins like a man;\n"
    .string "for I will demand of thee, and\l"
    .string "answer thou me$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_4::
    .string "Where wast thou when I laid the\n"
    .string "foundations of the earth? declare,\l"
    .string "if thou hast understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_5::
    .string "Who hath laid the measures thereof,\n"
    .string "if thou knowest? or who hath\l"
    .string "stretched the line upon it?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_6::
    .string "Whereupon are the foundations\n"
    .string "thereof fastened? or who laid the\l"
    .string "corner stone thereof;"
Bible_Text_Job_38_7::
    .string "When the morning stars sang\n"
    .string "together, and all the sons of God\l"
    .string "shouted for joy?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_8::
    .string "Or who shut up the sea with doors,\n"
    .string "when it brake forth, as if it had\l"
    .string "issued out of the womb?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_9::
    .string "When I made the cloud the garment\n"
    .string "thereof, and thick darkness a\l"
    .string "swaddlingband for it,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_10::
    .string "And brake up for it my decreed\n"
    .string "place, and set bars and doors,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_11::
    .string "And said, Hitherto shalt thou come,\n"
    .string "but no further: and here shall thy\l"
    .string "proud waves be stayed?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_12::
    .string "Hast thou commanded the morning\n"
    .string "since thy days; and caused the\l"
    .string "dayspring to know his place;"
Bible_Text_Job_38_13::
    .string "That it might take hold of the ends\n"
    .string "of the earth, that the wicked might\l"
    .string "be shaken out of it?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_14::
    .string "It is turned as clay to the seal;\n"
    .string "and they stand as a garment$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_15::
    .string "And from the wicked their light is\n"
    .string "withholden, and the high arm shall\l"
    .string "be broken.$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_16::
    .string "Hast thou entered into the springs\n"
    .string "of the sea? or hast thou walked in\l"
    .string "the search of the depth?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_17::
    .string "Have the gates of death been opened\n"
    .string "unto thee? or hast thou seen the\l"
    .string "doors of the shadow of death?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_18::
    .string "Hast thou perceived the breadth of\n"
    .string "the earth? declare if thou knowest\l"
    .string "it all$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_19::
    .string "Where is the way where light\n"
    .string "dwelleth? and as for darkness,\l"
    .string "where is the place thereof,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_20::
    .string "That thou shouldest take it to the\n"
    .string "bound thereof, and that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest know the paths to the\l"
    .string "house thereof?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_21::
    .string "Knowest thou it, because thou wast\n"
    .string "then born? or because the number of\l"
    .string "thy days is great?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_22::
    .string "Hast thou entered into the\n"
    .string "treasures of the snow? or hast thou\l"
    .string "seen the treasures of the hail,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_23::
    .string "Which I have reserved against the\n"
    .string "time of trouble, against the day of\l"
    .string "battle and war?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_24::
    .string "By what way is the light parted,\n"
    .string "which scattereth the east wind upon\l"
    .string "the earth?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_25::
    .string "Who hath divided a watercourse for\n"
    .string "the overflowing of waters, or a way\l"
    .string "for the lightning of thunder;"
Bible_Text_Job_38_26::
    .string "To cause it to rain on the earth,\n"
    .string "where no man is; on the wilderness,\l"
    .string "wherein there is no man;"
Bible_Text_Job_38_27::
    .string "To satisfy the desolate and waste\n"
    .string "ground; and to cause the bud of the\l"
    .string "tender herb to spring forth?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_28::
    .string "Hath the rain a father? or who hath\n"
    .string "begotten the drops of dew?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_29::
    .string "Out of whose womb came the ice? and\n"
    .string "the hoary frost of heaven, who hath\l"
    .string "gendered it?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_30::
    .string "The waters are hid as with a stone,\n"
    .string "and the face of the deep is frozen$"
Bible_Text_Job_38_31::
    .string "Canst thou bind the sweet\n"
    .string "influences of Pleiades, or loose\l"
    .string "the bands of Orion?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_32::
    .string "Canst thou bring forth Mazzaroth in\n"
    .string "his season? or canst thou guide\l"
    .string "Arcturus with his sons?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_33::
    .string "Knowest thou the ordinances of\n"
    .string "heaven? canst thou set the dominion\l"
    .string "thereof in the earth?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_34::
    .string "Canst thou lift up thy voice to the\n"
    .string "clouds, that abundance of waters may\l"
    .string "cover thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_35::
    .string "Canst thou send lightnings, that\n"
    .string "they may go and say unto thee, Here we\l"
    .string "are?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_36::
    .string "Who hath put wisdom in the inward\n"
    .string "parts? or who hath given\l"
    .string "understanding to the heart?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_37::
    .string "Who can number the clouds in\n"
    .string "wisdom? or who can stay the bottles\l"
    .string "of heaven,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_38::
    .string "When the dust groweth into hardness,\n"
    .string "and the clods cleave fast together?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_39::
    .string "Wilt thou hunt the prey for the\n"
    .string "lion? or fill the appetite of the\l"
    .string "young lions,"
Bible_Text_Job_38_40::
    .string "When they couch in their dens, and\n"
    .string "abide in the covert to lie in wait?"
Bible_Text_Job_38_41::
    .string "Who provideth for the raven his\n"
    .string "food? when his young ones cry unto\l"
    .string "God, they wander for lack of meat$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_1::
    .string "Knowest thou the time when the wild\n"
    .string "goats of the rock bring forth? or\l"
    .string "canst thou mark when the hinds do\l"
    .string "calve?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_2::
    .string "Canst thou number the months that\n"
    .string "they fulfil? or knowest thou the\l"
    .string "time when they bring forth?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_3::
    .string "They bow themselves, they bring\n"
    .string "forth their young ones, they cast out\l"
    .string "their sorrows$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_4::
    .string "Their young ones are in good\n"
    .string "liking, they grow up with corn; they\l"
    .string "go forth, and return not unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_5::
    .string "Who hath sent out the wild ass free?\n"
    .string "or who hath loosed the bands of the\l"
    .string "wild ass?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_6::
    .string "Whose house I have made the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and the barren land his\l"
    .string "dwellings$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_7::
    .string "He scorneth the multitude of the\n"
    .string "city, neither regardeth he the crying\l"
    .string "of the driver.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_8::
    .string "The range of the mountains is his\n"
    .string "pasture, and he searcheth after every\l"
    .string "green thing.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_9::
    .string "Will the unicorn be willing to\n"
    .string "serve thee, or abide by thy crib?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_10::
    .string "Canst thou bind the unicorn with his\n"
    .string "band in the furrow? or will he\l"
    .string "harrow the valleys after thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_11::
    .string "Wilt thou trust him, because his\n"
    .string "strength is great? or wilt thou\l"
    .string "leave thy labour to him?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_12::
    .string "Wilt thou believe him, that he\n"
    .string "will bring home thy seed, and gather\l"
    .string "it into thy barn?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_13::
    .string "Gavest thou the goodly wings unto\n"
    .string "the peacocks? or wings and feathers\l"
    .string "unto the ostrich?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_14::
    .string "Which leaveth her eggs in the\n"
    .string "earth, and warmeth them in dust,"
Bible_Text_Job_39_15::
    .string "And forgetteth that the foot may\n"
    .string "crush them, or that the wild beast\l"
    .string "may break them$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_16::
    .string "She is hardened against her young\n"
    .string "ones, as though they were not hers:\l"
    .string "her labour is in vain without fear;"
Bible_Text_Job_39_17::
    .string "Because God hath deprived her of\n"
    .string "wisdom, neither hath he imparted to\l"
    .string "her understanding$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_18::
    .string "What time she lifteth up herself\n"
    .string "on high, she scorneth the horse and\l"
    .string "his rider.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_19::
    .string "Hast thou given the horse strength?\n"
    .string "hast thou clothed his neck with\l"
    .string "thunder?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_20::
    .string "Canst thou make him afraid as a\n"
    .string "grasshopper? the glory of his\l"
    .string "nostrils is terrible$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_21::
    .string "He paweth in the valley, and\n"
    .string "rejoiceth in his strength: he goeth\l"
    .string "on to meet the armed men.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_22::
    .string "He mocketh at fear, and is not\n"
    .string "affrighted; neither turneth he back\l"
    .string "from the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_23::
    .string "The quiver rattleth against him,\n"
    .string "the glittering spear and the\l"
    .string "shield.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_24::
    .string "He swalloweth the ground with\n"
    .string "fierceness and rage: neither\l"
    .string "believeth he that it is the sound of\l"
    .string "the trumpet.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_25::
    .string "He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha;\n"
    .string "and he smelleth the battle afar\l"
    .string "off, the thunder of the captains,\l"
    .string "and the shouting.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_26::
    .string "Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, and\n"
    .string "stretch her wings toward the south?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_27::
    .string "Doth the eagle mount up at thy\n"
    .string "command, and make her nest on high?"
Bible_Text_Job_39_28::
    .string "She dwelleth and abideth on the\n"
    .string "rock, upon the crag of the rock, and\l"
    .string "the strong place$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_29::
    .string "From thence she seeketh the prey,\n"
    .string "and her eyes behold afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Job_39_30::
    .string "Her young ones also suck up blood:\n"
    .string "and where the slain are, there is\l"
    .string "she.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_1::
    .string "Moreover the LORD answered Job, and\n"
    .string "said,"
Bible_Text_Job_40_2::
    .string "Shall he that contendeth with the\n"
    .string "Almighty instruct him? he that\l"
    .string "reproveth God, let him answer it$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_3::
    .string "Then Job answered the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said,"
Bible_Text_Job_40_4::
    .string "Behold, I am vile; what shall I\n"
    .string "answer thee? I will lay mine hand\l"
    .string "upon my mouth$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_5::
    .string "Once have I spoken; but I will not\n"
    .string "answer: yea, twice; but I will\l"
    .string "proceed no further.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_6::
    .string "Then answered the LORD unto Job out\n"
    .string "of the whirlwind, and said,"
Bible_Text_Job_40_7::
    .string "Gird up thy loins now like a man: I\n"
    .string "will demand of thee, and declare\l"
    .string "thou unto me$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_8::
    .string "Wilt thou also disannul my\n"
    .string "judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that\l"
    .string "thou mayest be righteous?"
Bible_Text_Job_40_9::
    .string "Hast thou an arm like God? or canst\n"
    .string "thou thunder with a voice like him?"
Bible_Text_Job_40_10::
    .string "Deck thyself now with majesty and\n"
    .string "excellency; and array thyself with\l"
    .string "glory and beauty$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_11::
    .string "Cast abroad the rage of thy wrath:\n"
    .string "and behold every one that is proud,\l"
    .string "and abase him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_12::
    .string "Look on every one that is proud, and\n"
    .string "bring him low; and tread down the\l"
    .string "wicked in their place.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_13::
    .string "Hide them in the dust together; and\n"
    .string "bind their faces in secret.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_14::
    .string "Then will I also confess unto thee\n"
    .string "that thine own right hand can save\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_15::
    .string "Behold now behemoth, which I made\n"
    .string "with thee; he eateth grass as an ox.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_16::
    .string "Lo now, his strength is in his\n"
    .string "loins, and his force is in the navel\l"
    .string "of his belly.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_17::
    .string "He moveth his tail like a cedar:\n"
    .string "the sinews of his stones are\l"
    .string "wrapped together.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_18::
    .string "His bones are as strong pieces of\n"
    .string "brass; his bones are like bars of\l"
    .string "iron.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_19::
    .string "He is the chief of the ways of God:\n"
    .string "he that made him can make his sword\l"
    .string "to approach unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_20::
    .string "Surely the mountains bring him\n"
    .string "forth food, where all the beasts of\l"
    .string "the field play.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_21::
    .string "He lieth under the shady trees, in\n"
    .string "the covert of the reed, and fens.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_22::
    .string "The shady trees cover him with their\n"
    .string "shadow; the willows of the brook\l"
    .string "compass him about.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_23::
    .string "Behold, he drinketh up a river, and\n"
    .string "hasteth not: he trusteth that he can\l"
    .string "draw up Jordan into his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_40_24::
    .string "He taketh it with his eyes: his nose\n"
    .string "pierceth through snares.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_1::
    .string "Canst thou draw out leviathan with\n"
    .string "an hook? or his tongue with a cord\l"
    .string "which thou lettest down?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_2::
    .string "Canst thou put an hook into his\n"
    .string "nose? or bore his jaw through with a\l"
    .string "thorn?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_3::
    .string "Will he make many supplications\n"
    .string "unto thee? will he speak soft words\l"
    .string "unto thee?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_4::
    .string "Will he make a covenant with thee?\n"
    .string "wilt thou take him for a servant for\l"
    .string "ever?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_5::
    .string "Wilt thou play with him as with a\n"
    .string "bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy\l"
    .string "maidens?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_6::
    .string "Shall the companions make a\n"
    .string "banquet of him? shall they part him\l"
    .string "among the merchants?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_7::
    .string "Canst thou fill his skin with\n"
    .string "barbed irons? or his head with fish\l"
    .string "spears?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_8::
    .string "Lay thine hand upon him, remember\n"
    .string "the battle, do no more$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_9::
    .string "Behold, the hope of him is in vain:\n"
    .string "shall not one be cast down even at\l"
    .string "the sight of him?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_10::
    .string "None is so fierce that dare stir him\n"
    .string "up: who then is able to stand before\l"
    .string "me?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_11::
    .string "Who hath prevented me, that I\n"
    .string "should repay him? whatsoever is\l"
    .string "under the whole heaven is mine$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_12::
    .string "I will not conceal his parts, nor\n"
    .string "his power, nor his comely\l"
    .string "proportion.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_13::
    .string "Who can discover the face of his\n"
    .string "garment? or who can come to him with\l"
    .string "his double bridle?"
Bible_Text_Job_41_14::
    .string "Who can open the doors of his face?\n"
    .string "his teeth are terrible round about$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_15::
    .string "His scales are his pride, shut up\n"
    .string "together as with a close seal.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_16::
    .string "One is so near to another, that no\n"
    .string "air can come between them.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_17::
    .string "They are joined one to another, they\n"
    .string "stick together, that they cannot be\l"
    .string "sundered.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_18::
    .string "By his neesings a light doth shine,\n"
    .string "and his eyes are like the eyelids of\l"
    .string "the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_19::
    .string "Out of his mouth go burning lamps,\n"
    .string "and sparks of fire leap out.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_20::
    .string "Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as\n"
    .string "out of a seething pot or caldron.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_21::
    .string "His breath kindleth coals, and a\n"
    .string "flame goeth out of his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_22::
    .string "In his neck remaineth strength, and\n"
    .string "sorrow is turned into joy before him.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_23::
    .string "The flakes of his flesh are joined\n"
    .string "together: they are firm in\l"
    .string "themselves; they cannot be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_24::
    .string "His heart is as firm as a stone; yea,\n"
    .string "as hard as a piece of the nether\l"
    .string "millstone.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_25::
    .string "When he raiseth up himself, the\n"
    .string "mighty are afraid: by reason of\l"
    .string "breakings they purify themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_26::
    .string "The sword of him that layeth at him\n"
    .string "cannot hold: the spear, the dart,\l"
    .string "nor the habergeon.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_27::
    .string "He esteemeth iron as straw, and\n"
    .string "brass as rotten wood.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_28::
    .string "The arrow cannot make him flee:\n"
    .string "slingstones are turned with him into\l"
    .string "stubble.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_29::
    .string "Darts are counted as stubble: he\n"
    .string "laugheth at the shaking of a spear.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_30::
    .string "Sharp stones are under him: he\n"
    .string "spreadeth sharp pointed things\l"
    .string "upon the mire.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_31::
    .string "He maketh the deep to boil like a\n"
    .string "pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of\l"
    .string "ointment.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_32::
    .string "He maketh a path to shine after him;\n"
    .string "one would think the deep to be hoary.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_33::
    .string "Upon earth there is not his like,\n"
    .string "who is made without fear.$"
Bible_Text_Job_41_34::
    .string "He beholdeth all high things: he\n"
    .string "is a king over all the children of\l"
    .string "pride.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_1::
    .string "Then Job answered the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said,"
Bible_Text_Job_42_2::
    .string "I know that thou canst do every\n"
    .string "thing, and that no thought can be\l"
    .string "withholden from thee$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_3::
    .string "Who is he that hideth counsel\n"
    .string "without knowledge? therefore have I\l"
    .string "uttered that I understood not; things\l"
    .string "too wonderful for me, which I knew\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_4::
    .string "Hear, I beseech thee, and I will\n"
    .string "speak: I will demand of thee, and\l"
    .string "declare thou unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_5::
    .string "I have heard of thee by the hearing\n"
    .string "of the ear: but now mine eye seeth\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_6::
    .string "Wherefore I abhor myself, and\n"
    .string "repent in dust and ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_7::
    .string "And it was so, that after the LORD\n"
    .string "had spoken these words unto Job, the\l"
    .string "LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite,\l"
    .string "My wrath is kindled against thee,\l"
    .string "and against thy two friends: for ye\l"
    .string "have not spoken of me the thing that\l"
    .string "is right, as my servant Job hath.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_8::
    .string "Therefore take unto you now seven\n"
    .string "bullocks and seven rams, and go to\l"
    .string "my servant Job, and offer up for\l"
    .string "yourselves a burnt offering; and my\l"
    .string "servant Job shall pray for you: for\l"
    .string "him will I accept: lest I deal\l"
    .string "with you after your folly, in that\l"
    .string "ye have not spoken of me the thing\l"
    .string "which is right, like my servant Job.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_9::
    .string "So Eliphaz the Temanite and\n"
    .string "Bildad the Shuhite and Zophar the\l"
    .string "Naamathite went, and did according as\l"
    .string "the LORD commanded them: the LORD\l"
    .string "also accepted Job.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_10::
    .string "And the LORD turned the captivity\n"
    .string "of Job, when he prayed for his\l"
    .string "friends: also the LORD gave Job\l"
    .string "twice as much as he had before.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_11::
    .string "Then came there unto him all his\n"
    .string "brethren, and all his sisters, and\l"
    .string "all they that had been of his\l"
    .string "acquaintance before, and did eat\l"
    .string "bread with him in his house: and they\l"
    .string "bemoaned him, and comforted him over\l"
    .string "all the evil that the LORD had\l"
    .string "brought upon him: every man also\l"
    .string "gave him a piece of money, and every\l"
    .string "one an earring of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_12::
    .string "So the LORD blessed the latter end\n"
    .string "of Job more than his beginning: for\l"
    .string "he had fourteen thousand sheep, and\l"
    .string "six thousand camels, and a thousand\l"
    .string "yoke of oxen, and a thousand she\l"
    .string "asses.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_13::
    .string "He had also seven sons and three\n"
    .string "daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_14::
    .string "And he called the name of the\n"
    .string "first, Jemima; and the name of the\l"
    .string "second, Kezia; and the name of the\l"
    .string "third, Kerenhappuch.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_15::
    .string "And in all the land were no women\n"
    .string "found so fair as the daughters of\l"
    .string "Job: and their father gave them\l"
    .string "inheritance among their brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_16::
    .string "After this lived Job an hundred and\n"
    .string "forty years, and saw his sons, and\l"
    .string "his sons’ sons, even four\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Job_42_17::
    .string "So Job died, being old and full of\n"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_1::
    .string "Blessed is the man that walketh\n"
    .string "not in the counsel of the ungodly,\l"
    .string "nor standeth in the way of sinners,\l"
    .string "nor sitteth in the seat of the\l"
    .string "scornful.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_2::
    .string "But his delight is in the law of\n"
    .string "the LORD; and in his law doth he\l"
    .string "meditate day and night.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_3::
    .string "And he shall be like a tree\n"
    .string "planted by the rivers of water, that\l"
    .string "bringeth forth his fruit in his\l"
    .string "season; his leaf also shall not\l"
    .string "wither; and whatsoever he doeth\l"
    .string "shall prosper.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_4::
    .string "The ungodly are not so: but are\n"
    .string "like the chaff which the wind driveth\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_5::
    .string "Therefore the ungodly shall not\n"
    .string "stand in the judgment, nor sinners in\l"
    .string "the congregation of the righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_1_6::
    .string "For the LORD knoweth the way of the\n"
    .string "righteous: but the way of the\l"
    .string "ungodly shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_1::
    .string "Why do the heathen rage, and the\n"
    .string "people imagine a vain thing?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_2::
    .string "The kings of the earth set\n"
    .string "themselves, and the rulers take\l"
    .string "counsel together, against the LORD,\l"
    .string "and against his anointed, saying,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_3::
    .string "Let us break their bands asunder,\n"
    .string "and cast away their cords from us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_4::
    .string "He that sitteth in the heavens\n"
    .string "shall laugh: the LORD shall have\l"
    .string "them in derision.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_5::
    .string "Then shall he speak unto them in\n"
    .string "his wrath, and vex them in his sore\l"
    .string "displeasure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_6::
    .string "Yet have I set my king upon my holy\n"
    .string "hill of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_7::
    .string "I will declare the decree: the\n"
    .string "LORD hath said unto me, Thou art my\l"
    .string "Son; this day have I begotten thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_8::
    .string "Ask of me, and I shall give thee\n"
    .string "the heathen for thine inheritance,\l"
    .string "and the uttermost parts of the earth\l"
    .string "for thy possession.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_9::
    .string "Thou shalt break them with a rod of\n"
    .string "iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces\l"
    .string "like a potter’s vessel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_10::
    .string "Be wise now therefore, O ye kings:\n"
    .string "be instructed, ye judges of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_11::
    .string "Serve the LORD with fear, and\n"
    .string "rejoice with trembling.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_2_12::
    .string "Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and\n"
    .string "ye perish from the way, when his\l"
    .string "wrath is kindled but a little.\l"
    .string "Blessed are all they that put\l"
    .string "their trust in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_1::
    .string "Lord, how are they increased that\n"
    .string "trouble me! many are they that rise\l"
    .string "up against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_2::
    .string "Many there be which say of my soul,\n"
    .string "There is no help for him in God.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_3::
    .string "But thou, O LORD, art a shield for\n"
    .string "me; my glory, and the lifter up of\l"
    .string "mine head.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_4::
    .string "I cried unto the LORD with my voice,\n"
    .string "and he heard me out of his holy hill\l"
    .string " Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_5::
    .string "I laid me down and slept; I\n"
    .string "awaked; for the LORD sustained me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_6::
    .string "I will not be afraid of ten\n"
    .string "thousands of people, that have set\l"
    .string "themselves against me round about.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_7::
    .string "Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for\n"
    .string "thou hast smitten all mine enemies\l"
    .string "upon the cheek bone; thou hast\l"
    .string "broken the teeth of the ungodly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_3_8::
    .string "Salvation belongeth unto the LORD:\n"
    .string "thy blessing is upon thy people.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_1::
    .string "Hear me when I call, O God of my\n"
    .string "righteousness: thou hast enlarged me\l"
    .string "when I was in distress; have mercy\l"
    .string "upon me, and hear my prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_2::
    .string "O ye sons of men, how long will ye\n"
    .string "turn my glory into shame? how long\l"
    .string "will ye love vanity, and seek after\l"
    .string "leasing? Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_3::
    .string "But know that the LORD hath set\n"
    .string "apart him that is godly for\l"
    .string "himself: the LORD will hear when I\l"
    .string "call unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_4::
    .string "Stand in awe, and sin not: commune\n"
    .string "with your own heart upon your bed,\l"
    .string "and be still. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_5::
    .string "Offer the sacrifices of\n"
    .string "righteousness, and put your trust in\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_6::
    .string "There be many that say, Who will\n"
    .string "shew us any good? LORD, lift thou up\l"
    .string "the light of thy countenance upon\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_7::
    .string "Thou hast put gladness in my heart,\n"
    .string "more than in the time that their corn\l"
    .string "and their wine increased.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_4_8::
    .string "I will both lay me down in peace,\n"
    .string "and sleep: for thou, LORD, only\l"
    .string "makest me dwell in safety.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_1::
    .string "Give ear to my words, O LORD,\n"
    .string "consider my meditation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_2::
    .string "Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my\n"
    .string "King, and my God: for unto thee will\l"
    .string "I pray.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_3::
    .string "My voice shalt thou hear in the\n"
    .string "morning, O LORD; in the morning will\l"
    .string "I direct my prayer unto thee, and\l"
    .string "will look up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_4::
    .string "For thou art not a God that hath\n"
    .string "pleasure in wickedness: neither\l"
    .string "shall evil dwell with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_5::
    .string "The foolish shall not stand in thy\n"
    .string "sight: thou hatest all workers of\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_6::
    .string "Thou shalt destroy them that speak\n"
    .string "leasing: the LORD will abhor the\l"
    .string "bloody and deceitful man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_7::
    .string "But as for me, I will come into thy\n"
    .string "house in the multitude of thy mercy:\l"
    .string "and in thy fear will I worship\l"
    .string "toward thy holy temple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_8::
    .string "Lead me, O LORD, in thy\n"
    .string "righteousness because of mine\l"
    .string "enemies; make thy way straight before\l"
    .string "my face.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_9::
    .string "For there is no faithfulness in\n"
    .string "their mouth; their inward part is\l"
    .string "very wickedness; their throat is an\l"
    .string "open sepulchre; they flatter with\l"
    .string "their tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_10::
    .string "Destroy thou them, O God; let them\n"
    .string "fall by their own counsels; cast\l"
    .string "them out in the multitude of their\l"
    .string "transgressions; for they have\l"
    .string "rebelled against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_11::
    .string "But let all those that put their\n"
    .string "trust in thee rejoice: let them ever\l"
    .string "shout for joy, because thou defendest\l"
    .string "them: let them also that love thy\l"
    .string "name be joyful in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_5_12::
    .string "For thou, LORD, wilt bless the\n"
    .string "righteous; with favour wilt thou\l"
    .string "compass him as with a shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_1::
    .string "O LORD, rebuke me not in thine\n"
    .string "anger, neither chasten me in thy hot\l"
    .string "displeasure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_2::
    .string "Have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I am\n"
    .string "weak: O LORD, heal me; for my bones\l"
    .string "are vexed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_3::
    .string "My soul is also sore vexed: but\n"
    .string "thou, O LORD, how long?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_4::
    .string "Return, O LORD, deliver my soul: oh\n"
    .string "save me for thy mercies’ sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_5::
    .string "For in death there is no remembrance\n"
    .string "of thee: in the grave who shall give\l"
    .string "thee thanks?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_6::
    .string "I am weary with my groaning; all\n"
    .string "the night make I my bed to swim; I\l"
    .string "water my couch with my tears.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_7::
    .string "Mine eye is consumed because of\n"
    .string "grief; it waxeth old because of all\l"
    .string "mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_8::
    .string "Depart from me, all ye workers of\n"
    .string "iniquity; for the LORD hath heard the\l"
    .string "voice of my weeping.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_9::
    .string "The LORD hath heard my\n"
    .string "supplication; the LORD will\l"
    .string "receive my prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_6_10::
    .string "Let all mine enemies be ashamed\n"
    .string "and sore vexed: let them return and\l"
    .string "be ashamed suddenly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_1::
    .string "O LORD my God, in thee do I put my\n"
    .string "trust: save me from all them that\l"
    .string "persecute me, and deliver me:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_2::
    .string "Lest he tear my soul like a lion,\n"
    .string "rending it in pieces, while there is\l"
    .string "none to deliver.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_3::
    .string "O LORD my God, If I have done this;\n"
    .string "if there be iniquity in my hands;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_4::
    .string "If I have rewarded evil unto him\n"
    .string "that was at peace with me; (yea, I\l"
    .string "have delivered him that without\l"
    .string "cause is mine enemy:)$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_5::
    .string "Let the enemy persecute my soul,\n"
    .string "and take it; yea, let him tread down\l"
    .string "my life upon the earth, and lay\l"
    .string "mine honour in the dust. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_6::
    .string "Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift\n"
    .string "up thyself because of the rage of\l"
    .string "mine enemies: and awake for me to the\l"
    .string "judgment that thou hast commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_7::
    .string "So shall the congregation of the\n"
    .string "people compass thee about: for\l"
    .string "their sakes therefore return thou on\l"
    .string "high.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_8::
    .string "The LORD shall judge the people:\n"
    .string "judge me, O LORD, according to my\l"
    .string "righteousness, and according to mine\l"
    .string "integrity that is in me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_9::
    .string "Oh let the wickedness of the wicked\n"
    .string "come to an end; but establish the\l"
    .string "just: for the righteous God trieth\l"
    .string "the hearts and reins.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_10::
    .string "My defence is of God, which saveth\n"
    .string "the upright in heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_11::
    .string "God judgeth the righteous, and God\n"
    .string "is angry with the wicked every day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_12::
    .string "If he turn not, he will whet his\n"
    .string "sword; he hath bent his bow, and made\l"
    .string "it ready.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_13::
    .string "He hath also prepared for him the\n"
    .string "instruments of death; he ordaineth\l"
    .string "his arrows against the persecutors.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_14::
    .string "Behold, he travaileth with\n"
    .string "iniquity, and hath conceived\l"
    .string "mischief, and brought forth\l"
    .string "falsehood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_15::
    .string "He made a pit, and digged it, and is\n"
    .string "fallen into the ditch which he made.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_16::
    .string "His mischief shall return upon\n"
    .string "his own head, and his violent\l"
    .string "dealing shall come down upon his\l"
    .string "own pate.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_7_17::
    .string "I will praise the LORD according\n"
    .string "to his righteousness: and will sing\l"
    .string "praise to the name of the LORD most\l"
    .string "high.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_1::
    .string "O LORD, our Lord, how excellent is\n"
    .string "thy name in all the earth! who hast\l"
    .string "set thy glory above the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_2::
    .string "Out of the mouth of babes and\n"
    .string "sucklings hast thou ordained\l"
    .string "strength because of thine enemies,\l"
    .string "that thou mightest still the enemy\l"
    .string "and the avenger.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_3::
    .string "When I consider thy heavens, the\n"
    .string "work of thy fingers, the moon and the\l"
    .string "stars, which thou hast ordained;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_4::
    .string "What is man, that thou art mindful\n"
    .string "of him? and the son of man, that thou\l"
    .string "visitest him?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_5::
    .string "For thou hast made him a little\n"
    .string "lower than the angels, and hast\l"
    .string "crowned him with glory and honour.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_6::
    .string "Thou madest him to have dominion\n"
    .string "over the works of thy hands; thou\l"
    .string "hast put all things under his feet:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_7::
    .string "All sheep and oxen, yea, and the\n"
    .string "beasts of the field;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_8::
    .string "The fowl of the air, and the fish of\n"
    .string "the sea, and whatsoever passeth\l"
    .string "through the paths of the seas.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_8_9::
    .string "O LORD our Lord, how excellent is\n"
    .string "thy name in all the earth!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_1::
    .string "I will praise thee, O LORD, with\n"
    .string "my whole heart; I will shew forth\l"
    .string "all thy marvellous works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_2::
    .string "I will be glad and rejoice in\n"
    .string "thee: I will sing praise to thy\l"
    .string "name, O thou most High.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_3::
    .string "When mine enemies are turned back,\n"
    .string "they shall fall and perish at thy\l"
    .string "presence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_4::
    .string "For thou hast maintained my right\n"
    .string "and my cause; thou satest in the\l"
    .string "throne judging right.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_5::
    .string "Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou\n"
    .string "hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast\l"
    .string "put out their name for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_6::
    .string "O thou enemy, destructions are come\n"
    .string "to a perpetual end: and thou hast\l"
    .string "destroyed cities; their memorial is\l"
    .string "perished with them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_7::
    .string "But the LORD shall endure for ever:\n"
    .string "he hath prepared his throne for\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_8::
    .string "And he shall judge the world in\n"
    .string "righteousness, he shall minister\l"
    .string "judgment to the people in\l"
    .string "uprightness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_9::
    .string "The LORD also will be a refuge for\n"
    .string "the oppressed, a refuge in times of\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_10::
    .string "And they that know thy name will\n"
    .string "put their trust in thee: for thou,\l"
    .string "LORD, hast not forsaken them that\l"
    .string "seek thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_11::
    .string "Sing praises to the LORD, which\n"
    .string "dwelleth in Zion: declare among the\l"
    .string "people his doings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_12::
    .string "When he maketh inquisition for\n"
    .string "blood, he remembereth them: he\l"
    .string "forgetteth not the cry of the humble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_13::
    .string "Have mercy upon me, O LORD;\n"
    .string "consider my trouble which I suffer\l"
    .string "of them that hate me, thou that\l"
    .string "liftest me up from the gates of\l"
    .string "death:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_14::
    .string "That I may shew forth all thy\n"
    .string "praise in the gates of the daughter\l"
    .string "of Zion: I will rejoice in thy\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_15::
    .string "The heathen are sunk down in the\n"
    .string "pit that they made: in the net which\l"
    .string "they hid is their own foot taken.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_16::
    .string "The LORD is known by the judgment\n"
    .string "which he executeth: the wicked is\l"
    .string "snared in the work of his own hands.\l"
    .string "Higgaion. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_17::
    .string "The wicked shall be turned into\n"
    .string "hell, and all the nations that\l"
    .string "forget God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_18::
    .string "For the needy shall not alway be\n"
    .string "forgotten: the expectation of the\l"
    .string "poor shall not perish for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_19::
    .string "Arise, O LORD; let not man\n"
    .string "prevail: let the heathen be judged\l"
    .string "in thy sight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_9_20::
    .string "Put them in fear, O LORD: that the\n"
    .string "nations may know themselves to be\l"
    .string "but men. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_1::
    .string "Why standest thou afar off, O LORD?\n"
    .string "why hidest thou thyself in times of\l"
    .string "trouble?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_2::
    .string "The wicked in his pride doth\n"
    .string "persecute the poor: let them be\l"
    .string "taken in the devices that they have\l"
    .string "imagined.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_3::
    .string "For the wicked boasteth of his\n"
    .string "heart’s desire, and blesseth the\l"
    .string "covetous, whom the LORD abhorreth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_4::
    .string "The wicked, through the pride of\n"
    .string "his countenance, will not seek\l"
    .string "after God: God is not in all his\l"
    .string "thoughts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_5::
    .string "His ways are always grievous; thy\n"
    .string "judgments are far above out of his\l"
    .string "sight: as for all his enemies, he\l"
    .string "puffeth at them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_6::
    .string "He hath said in his heart, I shall\n"
    .string "not be moved: for I shall never be\l"
    .string "in adversity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_7::
    .string "His mouth is full of cursing and\n"
    .string "deceit and fraud: under his tongue is\l"
    .string "mischief and vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_8::
    .string "He sitteth in the lurking places\n"
    .string "of the villages: in the secret\l"
    .string "places doth he murder the innocent:\l"
    .string "his eyes are privily set against\l"
    .string "the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_9::
    .string "He lieth in wait secretly as a\n"
    .string "lion in his den: he lieth in wait to\l"
    .string "catch the poor: he doth catch the\l"
    .string "poor, when he draweth him into his\l"
    .string "net.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_10::
    .string "He croucheth, and humbleth\n"
    .string "himself, that the poor may fall by\l"
    .string "his strong ones.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_11::
    .string "He hath said in his heart, God hath\n"
    .string "forgotten: he hideth his face; he\l"
    .string "will never see it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_12::
    .string "Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine\n"
    .string "hand: forget not the humble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_13::
    .string "Wherefore doth the wicked contemn\n"
    .string "God? he hath said in his heart, Thou\l"
    .string "wilt not require it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_14::
    .string "Thou hast seen it; for thou\n"
    .string "beholdest mischief and spite, to\l"
    .string "requite it with thy hand: the poor\l"
    .string "committeth himself unto thee; thou\l"
    .string "art the helper of the fatherless.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_15::
    .string "Break thou the arm of the wicked and\n"
    .string "the evil man: seek out his\l"
    .string "wickedness till thou find none.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_16::
    .string "The LORD is King for ever and ever:\n"
    .string "the heathen are perished out of his\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_17::
    .string "LORD, thou hast heard the desire of\n"
    .string "the humble: thou wilt prepare\l"
    .string "their heart, thou wilt cause thine\l"
    .string "ear to hear:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_10_18::
    .string "To judge the fatherless and the\n"
    .string "oppressed, that the man of the earth\l"
    .string "may no more oppress.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_1::
    .string "In the LORD put I my trust: how say\n"
    .string "ye to my soul, Flee as a bird to your\l"
    .string "mountain?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_2::
    .string "For, lo, the wicked bend their bow,\n"
    .string "they make ready their arrow upon the\l"
    .string "string, that they may privily shoot\l"
    .string "at the upright in heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_3::
    .string "If the foundations be destroyed,\n"
    .string "what can the righteous do?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_4::
    .string "The LORD is in his holy temple,\n"
    .string "the LORD’s throne is in heaven: his\l"
    .string "eyes behold, his eyelids try, the\l"
    .string "children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_5::
    .string "The LORD trieth the righteous: but\n"
    .string "the wicked and him that loveth\l"
    .string "violence his soul hateth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_6::
    .string "Upon the wicked he shall rain\n"
    .string "snares, fire and brimstone, and an\l"
    .string "horrible tempest: this shall be\l"
    .string "the portion of their cup.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_11_7::
    .string "For the righteous LORD loveth\n"
    .string "righteousness; his countenance doth\l"
    .string "behold the upright.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_1::
    .string "Help, LORD; for the godly man\n"
    .string "ceaseth; for the faithful fail from\l"
    .string "among the children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_2::
    .string "They speak vanity every one with\n"
    .string "his neighbour: with flattering\l"
    .string "lips and with a double heart do they\l"
    .string "speak.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_3::
    .string "The LORD shall cut off all\n"
    .string "flattering lips, and the tongue\l"
    .string "that speaketh proud things:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_4::
    .string "Who have said, With our tongue will\n"
    .string "we prevail; our lips are our own:\l"
    .string "who is lord over us?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_5::
    .string "For the oppression of the poor,\n"
    .string "for the sighing of the needy, now\l"
    .string "will I arise, saith the LORD; I\l"
    .string "will set him in safety from him that\l"
    .string "puffeth at him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_6::
    .string "The words of the LORD are pure\n"
    .string "words: as silver tried in a furnace\l"
    .string "of earth, purified seven times.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_7::
    .string "Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou\n"
    .string "shalt preserve them from this\l"
    .string "generation for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_12_8::
    .string "The wicked walk on every side, when\n"
    .string "the vilest men are exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_1::
    .string "How long wilt thou forget me, O\n"
    .string "LORD? for ever? how long wilt thou\l"
    .string "hide thy face from me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_2::
    .string "How long shall I take counsel in\n"
    .string "my soul, having sorrow in my heart\l"
    .string "daily? how long shall mine enemy\l"
    .string "be exalted over me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_3::
    .string "Consider and hear me, O LORD my God:\n"
    .string "lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the\l"
    .string "sleep of death;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_4::
    .string "Lest mine enemy say, I have\n"
    .string "prevailed against him; and those\l"
    .string "that trouble me rejoice when I am\l"
    .string "moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_5::
    .string "But I have trusted in thy mercy; my\n"
    .string "heart shall rejoice in thy\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_13_6::
    .string "I will sing unto the LORD, because\n"
    .string "he hath dealt bountifully with me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_1::
    .string "The fool hath said in his heart,\n"
    .string "There is no God. They are corrupt,\l"
    .string "they have done abominable works,\l"
    .string "there is none that doeth good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_2::
    .string "The LORD looked down from heaven\n"
    .string "upon the children of men, to see if\l"
    .string "there were any that did understand,\l"
    .string "and seek God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_3::
    .string "They are all gone aside, they are\n"
    .string "all together become filthy: there\l"
    .string "is none that doeth good, no, not one.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_4::
    .string "Have all the workers of iniquity\n"
    .string "no knowledge? who eat up my people\l"
    .string "as they eat bread, and call not\l"
    .string "upon the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_5::
    .string "There were they in great fear: for\n"
    .string "God is in the generation of the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_6::
    .string "Ye have shamed the counsel of the\n"
    .string "poor, because the LORD is his refuge.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_14_7::
    .string "Oh that the salvation of Israel\n"
    .string "were come out of Zion! when the LORD\l"
    .string "bringeth back the captivity of his\l"
    .string "people, Jacob shall rejoice, and\l"
    .string "Israel shall be glad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_15_1::
    .string "Lord, who shall abide in thy\n"
    .string "tabernacle? who shall dwell in\l"
    .string "thy holy hill?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_15_2::
    .string "He that walketh uprightly, and\n"
    .string "worketh righteousness, and speaketh\l"
    .string "the truth in his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_15_3::
    .string "He that backbiteth not with his\n"
    .string "tongue, nor doeth evil to his\l"
    .string "neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach\l"
    .string "against his neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_15_4::
    .string "In whose eyes a vile person is\n"
    .string "contemned; but he honoureth them that\l"
    .string "fear the LORD. He that sweareth to\l"
    .string "his own hurt, and changeth not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_15_5::
    .string "He that putteth not out his money\n"
    .string "to usury, nor taketh reward against\l"
    .string "the innocent. He that doeth these\l"
    .string "things shall never be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_1::
    .string "Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I\n"
    .string "put my trust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_2::
    .string "O my soul, thou hast said unto the\n"
    .string "LORD, Thou art my Lord: my goodness\l"
    .string "extendeth not to thee;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_3::
    .string "But to the saints that are in the\n"
    .string "earth, and to the excellent, in whom\l"
    .string "is all my delight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_4::
    .string "Their sorrows shall be\n"
    .string "multiplied that hasten after\l"
    .string "another god: their drink offerings of\l"
    .string "blood will I not offer, nor take up\l"
    .string "their names into my lips.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_5::
    .string "The LORD is the portion of mine\n"
    .string "inheritance and of my cup: thou\l"
    .string "maintainest my lot.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_6::
    .string "The lines are fallen unto me in\n"
    .string "pleasant places; yea, I have a\l"
    .string "goodly heritage.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_7::
    .string "I will bless the LORD, who hath\n"
    .string "given me counsel: my reins also\l"
    .string "instruct me in the night seasons.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_8::
    .string "I have set the LORD always before\n"
    .string "me: because he is at my right hand, I\l"
    .string "shall not be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_9::
    .string "Therefore my heart is glad, and my\n"
    .string "glory rejoiceth: my flesh also\l"
    .string "shall rest in hope.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_10::
    .string "For thou wilt not leave my soul in\n"
    .string "hell; neither wilt thou suffer\l"
    .string "thine Holy One to see corruption.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_16_11::
    .string "Thou wilt shew me the path of\n"
    .string "life: in thy presence is fulness of\l"
    .string "joy; at thy right hand there are\l"
    .string "pleasures for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_1::
    .string "Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto\n"
    .string "my cry, give ear unto my prayer, that\l"
    .string "goeth not out of feigned lips.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_2::
    .string "Let my sentence come forth from thy\n"
    .string "presence; let thine eyes behold the\l"
    .string "things that are equal.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_3::
    .string "Thou hast proved mine heart; thou\n"
    .string "hast visited me in the night; thou\l"
    .string "hast tried me, and shalt find\l"
    .string "nothing; I am purposed that my mouth\l"
    .string "shall not transgress.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_4::
    .string "Concerning the works of men, by the\n"
    .string "word of thy lips I have kept me\l"
    .string "from the paths of the destroyer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_5::
    .string "Hold up my goings in thy paths,\n"
    .string "that my footsteps slip not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_6::
    .string "I have called upon thee, for thou\n"
    .string "wilt hear me, O God: incline thine\l"
    .string "ear unto me, and hear my speech.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_7::
    .string "Shew thy marvellous\n"
    .string "lovingkindness, O thou that savest by\l"
    .string "thy right hand them which put their\l"
    .string "trust in thee from those that rise\l"
    .string "up against them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_8::
    .string "Keep me as the apple of the eye,\n"
    .string "hide me under the shadow of thy wings,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_9::
    .string "From the wicked that oppress me,\n"
    .string "from my deadly enemies, who compass\l"
    .string "me about.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_10::
    .string "They are inclosed in their own fat:\n"
    .string "with their mouth they speak\l"
    .string "proudly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_11::
    .string "They have now compassed us in our\n"
    .string "steps: they have set their eyes\l"
    .string "bowing down to the earth;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_12::
    .string "Like as a lion that is greedy of his\n"
    .string "prey, and as it were a young lion\l"
    .string "lurking in secret places.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_13::
    .string "Arise, O LORD, disappoint him, cast\n"
    .string "him down: deliver my soul from the\l"
    .string "wicked, which is thy sword:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_14::
    .string "From men which are thy hand, O LORD,\n"
    .string "from men of the world, which have\l"
    .string "their portion in this life, and\l"
    .string "whose belly thou fillest with thy\l"
    .string "hid treasure: they are full of\l"
    .string "children, and leave the rest of\l"
    .string "their substance to their babes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_17_15::
    .string "As for me, I will behold thy face\n"
    .string "in righteousness: I shall be\l"
    .string "satisfied, when I awake, with thy\l"
    .string "likeness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_1::
    .string "I will love thee, O LORD, my\n"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_2::
    .string "The LORD is my rock, and my\n"
    .string "fortress, and my deliverer; my God,\l"
    .string "my strength, in whom I will trust;\l"
    .string "my buckler, and the horn of my\l"
    .string "salvation, and my high tower.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_3::
    .string "I will call upon the LORD, who is\n"
    .string "worthy to be praised: so shall I be\l"
    .string "saved from mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_4::
    .string "The sorrows of death compassed me,\n"
    .string "and the floods of ungodly men made\l"
    .string "me afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_5::
    .string "The sorrows of hell compassed me\n"
    .string "about: the snares of death prevented\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_6::
    .string "In my distress I called upon the\n"
    .string "LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard\l"
    .string "my voice out of his temple, and my\l"
    .string "cry came before him, even into his\l"
    .string "ears.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_7::
    .string "Then the earth shook and trembled;\n"
    .string "the foundations also of the hills\l"
    .string "moved and were shaken, because he was\l"
    .string "wroth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_8::
    .string "There went up a smoke out of his\n"
    .string "nostrils, and fire out of his mouth\l"
    .string "devoured: coals were kindled by it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_9::
    .string "He bowed the heavens also, and came\n"
    .string "down: and darkness was under his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_10::
    .string "And he rode upon a cherub, and did\n"
    .string "fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings\l"
    .string "of the wind.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_11::
    .string "He made darkness his secret place;\n"
    .string "his pavilion round about him were\l"
    .string "dark waters and thick clouds of the\l"
    .string "skies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_12::
    .string "At the brightness that was before\n"
    .string "him his thick clouds passed, hail\l"
    .string "stones and coals of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_13::
    .string "The LORD also thundered in the\n"
    .string "heavens, and the Highest gave his\l"
    .string "voice; hail stones and coals of\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_14::
    .string "Yea, he sent out his arrows, and\n"
    .string "scattered them; and he shot out\l"
    .string "lightnings, and discomfited them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_15::
    .string "Then the channels of waters were\n"
    .string "seen, and the foundations of the\l"
    .string "world were discovered at thy rebuke,\l"
    .string "O LORD, at the blast of the breath of\l"
    .string "thy nostrils.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_16::
    .string "He sent from above, he took me, he\n"
    .string "drew me out of many waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_17::
    .string "He delivered me from my strong\n"
    .string "enemy, and from them which hated me:\l"
    .string "for they were too strong for me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_18::
    .string "They prevented me in the day of my\n"
    .string "calamity: but the LORD was my stay.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_19::
    .string "He brought me forth also into a\n"
    .string "large place; he delivered me,\l"
    .string "because he delighted in me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_20::
    .string "The LORD rewarded me according to my\n"
    .string "righteousness; according to the\l"
    .string "cleanness of my hands hath he\l"
    .string "recompensed me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_21::
    .string "For I have kept the ways of the\n"
    .string "LORD, and have not wickedly\l"
    .string "departed from my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_22::
    .string "For all his judgments were before\n"
    .string "me, and I did not put away his\l"
    .string "statutes from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_23::
    .string "I was also upright before him, and\n"
    .string "I kept myself from mine iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_24::
    .string "Therefore hath the LORD\n"
    .string "recompensed me according to my\l"
    .string "righteousness, according to the\l"
    .string "cleanness of my hands in his\l"
    .string "eyesight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_25::
    .string "With the merciful thou wilt shew\n"
    .string "thyself merciful; with an upright\l"
    .string "man thou wilt shew thyself upright;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_26::
    .string "With the pure thou wilt shew\n"
    .string "thyself pure; and with the froward\l"
    .string "thou wilt shew thyself froward.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_27::
    .string "For thou wilt save the afflicted\n"
    .string "people; but wilt bring down high\l"
    .string "looks.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_28::
    .string "For thou wilt light my candle: the\n"
    .string "LORD my God will enlighten my\l"
    .string "darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_29::
    .string "For by thee I have run through a\n"
    .string "troop; and by my God have I leaped\l"
    .string "over a wall.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_30::
    .string "As for God, his way is perfect: the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD is tried: he is a\l"
    .string "buckler to all those that trust in\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_31::
    .string "For who is God save the LORD? or who\n"
    .string "is a rock save our God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_32::
    .string "It is God that girdeth me with\n"
    .string "strength, and maketh my way perfect.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_33::
    .string "He maketh my feet like hinds’ feet,\n"
    .string "and setteth me upon my high places.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_34::
    .string "He teacheth my hands to war, so that\n"
    .string "a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_35::
    .string "Thou hast also given me the shield\n"
    .string "of thy salvation: and thy right hand\l"
    .string "hath holden me up, and thy\l"
    .string "gentleness hath made me great.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_36::
    .string "Thou hast enlarged my steps under\n"
    .string "me, that my feet did not slip.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_37::
    .string "I have pursued mine enemies, and\n"
    .string "overtaken them: neither did I turn\l"
    .string "again till they were consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_38::
    .string "I have wounded them that they were\n"
    .string "not able to rise: they are fallen\l"
    .string "under my feet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_39::
    .string "For thou hast girded me with\n"
    .string "strength unto the battle: thou hast\l"
    .string "subdued under me those that rose up\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_40::
    .string "Thou hast also given me the necks\n"
    .string "of mine enemies; that I might destroy\l"
    .string "them that hate me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_41::
    .string "They cried, but there was none to\n"
    .string "save them: even unto the LORD, but he\l"
    .string "answered them not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_42::
    .string "Then did I beat them small as the\n"
    .string "dust before the wind: I did cast them\l"
    .string "out as the dirt in the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_43::
    .string "Thou hast delivered me from the\n"
    .string "strivings of the people; and thou\l"
    .string "hast made me the head of the heathen:\l"
    .string "a people whom I have not known\l"
    .string "shall serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_44::
    .string "As soon as they hear of me, they\n"
    .string "shall obey me: the strangers shall\l"
    .string "submit themselves unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_45::
    .string "The strangers shall fade away, and\n"
    .string "be afraid out of their close places.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_46::
    .string "The LORD liveth; and blessed be my\n"
    .string "rock; and let the God of my\l"
    .string "salvation be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_47::
    .string "It is God that avengeth me, and\n"
    .string "subdueth the people under me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_48::
    .string "He delivereth me from mine enemies:\n"
    .string "yea, thou liftest me up above those\l"
    .string "that rise up against me: thou hast\l"
    .string "delivered me from the violent man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_49::
    .string "Therefore will I give thanks unto\n"
    .string "thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and\l"
    .string "sing praises unto thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_18_50::
    .string "Great deliverance giveth he to his\n"
    .string "king; and sheweth mercy to his\l"
    .string "anointed, to David, and to his seed\l"
    .string "for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_1::
    .string "The heavens declare the glory of\n"
    .string "God; and the firmament sheweth his\l"
    .string "handywork.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_2::
    .string "Day unto day uttereth speech, and\n"
    .string "night unto night sheweth knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_3::
    .string "There is no speech nor language,\n"
    .string "where their voice is not heard.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_4::
    .string "Their line is gone out through all\n"
    .string "the earth, and their words to the end\l"
    .string "of the world. In them hath he set a\l"
    .string "tabernacle for the sun,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_5::
    .string "Which is as a bridegroom coming out\n"
    .string "of his chamber, and rejoiceth as a\l"
    .string "strong man to run a race.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_6::
    .string "His going forth is from the end of\n"
    .string "the heaven, and his circuit unto the\l"
    .string "ends of it: and there is nothing hid\l"
    .string "from the heat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_7::
    .string "The law of the LORD is perfect,\n"
    .string "converting the soul: the testimony\l"
    .string "of the LORD is sure, making wise the\l"
    .string "simple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_8::
    .string "The statutes of the LORD are right,\n"
    .string "rejoicing the heart: the commandment\l"
    .string "of the LORD is pure, enlightening\l"
    .string "the eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_9::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is clean,\n"
    .string "enduring for ever: the judgments of\l"
    .string "the LORD are true and righteous\l"
    .string "altogether.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_10::
    .string "More to be desired are they than\n"
    .string "gold, yea, than much fine gold:\l"
    .string "sweeter also than honey and the\l"
    .string "honeycomb.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_11::
    .string "Moreover by them is thy servant\n"
    .string "warned: and in keeping of them there\l"
    .string "is great reward.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_12::
    .string "Who can understand his errors?\n"
    .string "cleanse thou me from secret faults.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_13::
    .string "Keep back thy servant also from\n"
    .string "presumptuous sins; let them not\l"
    .string "have dominion over me: then shall I\l"
    .string "be upright, and I shall be innocent\l"
    .string "from the great transgression.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_19_14::
    .string "Let the words of my mouth, and the\n"
    .string "meditation of my heart, be\l"
    .string "acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my\l"
    .string "strength, and my redeemer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_1::
    .string "The LORD hear thee in the day of\n"
    .string "trouble; the name of the God of Jacob\l"
    .string "defend thee;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_2::
    .string "Send thee help from the sanctuary,\n"
    .string "and strengthen thee out of Zion;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_3::
    .string "Remember all thy offerings, and\n"
    .string "accept thy burnt sacrifice; Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_4::
    .string "Grant thee according to thine own\n"
    .string "heart, and fulfil all thy counsel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_5::
    .string "We will rejoice in thy salvation,\n"
    .string "and in the name of our God we will\l"
    .string "set up our banners: the LORD fulfil\l"
    .string "all thy petitions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_6::
    .string "Now know I that the LORD saveth his\n"
    .string "anointed; he will hear him from his\l"
    .string "holy heaven with the saving strength\l"
    .string "of his right hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_7::
    .string "Some trust in chariots, and some in\n"
    .string "horses: but we will remember the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_8::
    .string "They are brought down and fallen:\n"
    .string "but we are risen, and stand upright.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_20_9::
    .string "Save, LORD: let the king hear us\n"
    .string "when we call.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_1::
    .string "The king shall joy in thy strength,\n"
    .string "O LORD; and in thy salvation how\l"
    .string "greatly shall he rejoice!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_2::
    .string "Thou hast given him his heart’s\n"
    .string "desire, and hast not withholden the\l"
    .string "request of his lips. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_3::
    .string "For thou preventest him with the\n"
    .string "blessings of goodness: thou settest\l"
    .string "a crown of pure gold on his head.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_4::
    .string "He asked life of thee, and thou\n"
    .string "gavest it him, even length of days\l"
    .string "for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_5::
    .string "His glory is great in thy\n"
    .string "salvation: honour and majesty hast\l"
    .string "thou laid upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_6::
    .string "For thou hast made him most blessed\n"
    .string "for ever: thou hast made him\l"
    .string "exceeding glad with thy countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_7::
    .string "For the king trusteth in the LORD,\n"
    .string "and through the mercy of the most\l"
    .string "High he shall not be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_8::
    .string "Thine hand shall find out all\n"
    .string "thine enemies: thy right hand shall\l"
    .string "find out those that hate thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_9::
    .string "Thou shalt make them as a fiery\n"
    .string "oven in the time of thine anger: the\l"
    .string "LORD shall swallow them up in his\l"
    .string "wrath, and the fire shall devour\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_10::
    .string "Their fruit shalt thou destroy from\n"
    .string "the earth, and their seed from among\l"
    .string "the children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_11::
    .string "For they intended evil against\n"
    .string "thee: they imagined a mischievous\l"
    .string "device, which they are not able to\l"
    .string "perform.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_12::
    .string "Therefore shalt thou make them turn\n"
    .string "their back, when thou shalt make\l"
    .string "ready thine arrows upon thy strings\l"
    .string "against the face of them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_21_13::
    .string "Be thou exalted, LORD, in thine own\n"
    .string "strength: so will we sing and\l"
    .string "praise thy power.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_1::
    .string "My God, my God, why hast thou\n"
    .string "forsaken me? why art thou so far from\l"
    .string "helping me, and from the words of my\l"
    .string "roaring?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_2::
    .string "O my God, I cry in the day time, but\n"
    .string "thou hearest not; and in the night\l"
    .string "season, and am not silent.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_3::
    .string "But thou art holy, O thou that\n"
    .string "inhabitest the praises of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_4::
    .string "Our fathers trusted in thee: they\n"
    .string "trusted, and thou didst deliver them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_5::
    .string "They cried unto thee, and were\n"
    .string "delivered: they trusted in thee, and\l"
    .string "were not confounded.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_6::
    .string "But I am a worm, and no man; a\n"
    .string "reproach of men, and despised of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_7::
    .string "All they that see me laugh me to\n"
    .string "scorn: they shoot out the lip, they\l"
    .string "shake the head, saying,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_8::
    .string "He trusted on the LORD that he\n"
    .string "would deliver him: let him deliver\l"
    .string "him, seeing he delighted in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_9::
    .string "But thou art he that took me out of\n"
    .string "the womb: thou didst make me hope\l"
    .string "when I was upon my mother’s breasts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_10::
    .string "I was cast upon thee from the womb:\n"
    .string "thou art my God from my mother’s\l"
    .string "belly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_11::
    .string "Be not far from me; for trouble is\n"
    .string "near; for there is none to help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_12::
    .string "Many bulls have compassed me:\n"
    .string "strong bulls of Bashan have beset\l"
    .string "me round.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_13::
    .string "They gaped upon me with their\n"
    .string "mouths, as a ravening and a roaring\l"
    .string "lion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_14::
    .string "I am poured out like water, and\n"
    .string "all my bones are out of joint: my\l"
    .string "heart is like wax; it is melted in\l"
    .string "the midst of my bowels.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_15::
    .string "My strength is dried up like a\n"
    .string "potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to\l"
    .string "my jaws; and thou hast brought me\l"
    .string "into the dust of death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_16::
    .string "For dogs have compassed me: the\n"
    .string "assembly of the wicked have\l"
    .string "inclosed me: they pierced my hands\l"
    .string "and my feet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_17::
    .string "I may tell all my bones: they\n"
    .string "look and stare upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_18::
    .string "They part my garments among them,\n"
    .string "and cast lots upon my vesture.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_19::
    .string "But be not thou far from me, O LORD:\n"
    .string "O my strength, haste thee to help me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_20::
    .string "Deliver my soul from the sword; my\n"
    .string "darling from the power of the dog.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_21::
    .string "Save me from the lion’s mouth: for\n"
    .string "thou hast heard me from the horns of\l"
    .string "the unicorns.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_22::
    .string "I will declare thy name unto my\n"
    .string "brethren: in the midst of the\l"
    .string "congregation will I praise thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_23::
    .string "Ye that fear the LORD, praise him;\n"
    .string "all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify\l"
    .string "him; and fear him, all ye the seed\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_24::
    .string "For he hath not despised nor\n"
    .string "abhorred the affliction of the\l"
    .string "afflicted; neither hath he hid his\l"
    .string "face from him; but when he cried unto\l"
    .string "him, he heard.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_25::
    .string "My praise shall be of thee in the\n"
    .string "great congregation: I will pay my\l"
    .string "vows before them that fear him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_26::
    .string "The meek shall eat and be\n"
    .string "satisfied: they shall praise the\l"
    .string "LORD that seek him: your heart shall\l"
    .string "live for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_27::
    .string "All the ends of the world shall\n"
    .string "remember and turn unto the LORD: and\l"
    .string "all the kindreds of the nations\l"
    .string "shall worship before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_28::
    .string "For the kingdom is the LORD’s: and\n"
    .string "he is the governor among the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_29::
    .string "All they that be fat upon earth\n"
    .string "shall eat and worship: all they\l"
    .string "that go down to the dust shall bow\l"
    .string "before him: and none can keep alive\l"
    .string "his own soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_30::
    .string "A seed shall serve him; it shall\n"
    .string "be accounted to the Lord for a\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_22_31::
    .string "They shall come, and shall\n"
    .string "declare his righteousness unto a\l"
    .string "people that shall be born, that he\l"
    .string "hath done this.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_1::
    .string "The LORD is my shepherd; I shall\n"
    .string "not want.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_2::
    .string "He maketh me to lie down in green\n"
    .string "pastures: he leadeth me beside the\l"
    .string "still waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_3::
    .string "He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me\n"
    .string "in the paths of righteousness for\l"
    .string "his name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_4::
    .string "Yea, though I walk through the\n"
    .string "valley of the shadow of death, I\l"
    .string "will fear no evil: for thou art\l"
    .string "with me; thy rod and thy staff they\l"
    .string "comfort me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_5::
    .string "Thou preparest a table before me\n"
    .string "in the presence of mine enemies:\l"
    .string "thou anointest my head with oil; my\l"
    .string "cup runneth over.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_23_6::
    .string "Surely goodness and mercy shall\n"
    .string "follow me all the days of my life:\l"
    .string "and I will dwell in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_1::
    .string "The earth is the LORD’s, and the\n"
    .string "fulness thereof; the world, and\l"
    .string "they that dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_2::
    .string "For he hath founded it upon the\n"
    .string "seas, and established it upon the\l"
    .string "floods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_3::
    .string "Who shall ascend into the hill of\n"
    .string "the LORD? or who shall stand in his\l"
    .string "holy place?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_4::
    .string "He that hath clean hands, and a\n"
    .string "pure heart; who hath not lifted up\l"
    .string "his soul unto vanity, nor sworn\l"
    .string "deceitfully.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_5::
    .string "He shall receive the blessing\n"
    .string "from the LORD, and righteousness from\l"
    .string "the God of his salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_6::
    .string "This is the generation of them that\n"
    .string "seek him, that seek thy face, O Jacob.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_7::
    .string "Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and\n"
    .string "be ye lift up, ye everlasting\l"
    .string "doors; and the King of glory shall\l"
    .string "come in.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_8::
    .string "Who is this King of glory? The LORD\n"
    .string "strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_9::
    .string "Lift up your heads, O ye gates; even\n"
    .string "lift them up, ye everlasting doors;\l"
    .string "and the King of glory shall come in.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_24_10::
    .string "Who is this King of glory? The LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts, he is the King of glory.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_1::
    .string "Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my\n"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_2::
    .string "O my God, I trust in thee: let me\n"
    .string "not be ashamed, let not mine enemies\l"
    .string "triumph over me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_3::
    .string "Yea, let none that wait on thee be\n"
    .string "ashamed: let them be ashamed which\l"
    .string "transgress without cause.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_4::
    .string "Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me\n"
    .string "thy paths.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_5::
    .string "Lead me in thy truth, and teach me:\n"
    .string "for thou art the God of my salvation;\l"
    .string "on thee do I wait all the day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_6::
    .string "Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies\n"
    .string "and thy lovingkindnesses; for they\l"
    .string "have been ever of old.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_7::
    .string "Remember not the sins of my youth,\n"
    .string "nor my transgressions: according to\l"
    .string "thy mercy remember thou me for thy\l"
    .string "goodness’ sake, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_8::
    .string "Good and upright is the LORD:\n"
    .string "therefore will he teach sinners in\l"
    .string "the way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_9::
    .string "The meek will he guide in judgment:\n"
    .string "and the meek will he teach his way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_10::
    .string "All the paths of the LORD are\n"
    .string "mercy and truth unto such as keep\l"
    .string "his covenant and his testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_11::
    .string "For thy name’s sake, O LORD, pardon\n"
    .string "mine iniquity; for it is great.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_12::
    .string "What man is he that feareth the\n"
    .string "LORD? him shall he teach in the way\l"
    .string "that he shall choose.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_13::
    .string "His soul shall dwell at ease; and\n"
    .string "his seed shall inherit the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_14::
    .string "The secret of the LORD is with them\n"
    .string "that fear him; and he will shew them\l"
    .string "his covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_15::
    .string "Mine eyes are ever toward the LORD;\n"
    .string "for he shall pluck my feet out of\l"
    .string "the net.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_16::
    .string "Turn thee unto me, and have mercy\n"
    .string "upon me; for I am desolate and\l"
    .string "afflicted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_17::
    .string "The troubles of my heart are\n"
    .string "enlarged: O bring thou me out of my\l"
    .string "distresses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_18::
    .string "Look upon mine affliction and my\n"
    .string "pain; and forgive all my sins.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_19::
    .string "Consider mine enemies; for they are\n"
    .string "many; and they hate me with cruel\l"
    .string "hatred.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_20::
    .string "O keep my soul, and deliver me:\n"
    .string "let me not be ashamed; for I put my\l"
    .string "trust in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_21::
    .string "Let integrity and uprightness\n"
    .string "preserve me; for I wait on thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_25_22::
    .string "Redeem Israel, O God, out of all\n"
    .string "his troubles.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_1::
    .string "Judge me, O LORD; for I have walked\n"
    .string "in mine integrity: I have trusted\l"
    .string "also in the LORD; therefore I shall\l"
    .string "not slide.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_2::
    .string "Examine me, O LORD, and prove me;\n"
    .string "try my reins and my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_3::
    .string "For thy lovingkindness is before\n"
    .string "mine eyes: and I have walked in thy\l"
    .string "truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_4::
    .string "I have not sat with vain persons,\n"
    .string "neither will I go in with\l"
    .string "dissemblers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_5::
    .string "I have hated the congregation of\n"
    .string "evil doers; and will not sit with\l"
    .string "the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_6::
    .string "I will wash mine hands in\n"
    .string "innocency: so will I compass thine\l"
    .string "altar, O LORD:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_7::
    .string "That I may publish with the voice\n"
    .string "of thanksgiving, and tell of all\l"
    .string "thy wondrous works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_8::
    .string "LORD, I have loved the habitation\n"
    .string "of thy house, and the place where\l"
    .string "thine honour dwelleth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_9::
    .string "Gather not my soul with sinners,\n"
    .string "nor my life with bloody men:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_10::
    .string "In whose hands is mischief, and\n"
    .string "their right hand is full of bribes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_11::
    .string "But as for me, I will walk in mine\n"
    .string "integrity: redeem me, and be\l"
    .string "merciful unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_26_12::
    .string "My foot standeth in an even place:\n"
    .string "in the congregations will I bless\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_1::
    .string "The LORD is my light and my\n"
    .string "salvation; whom shall I fear? the\l"
    .string "LORD is the strength of my life; of\l"
    .string "whom shall I be afraid?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_2::
    .string "When the wicked, even mine enemies\n"
    .string "and my foes, came upon me to eat up\l"
    .string "my flesh, they stumbled and fell.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_3::
    .string "Though an host should encamp\n"
    .string "against me, my heart shall not fear:\l"
    .string "though war should rise against me,\l"
    .string "in this will I be confident.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_4::
    .string "One thing have I desired of the\n"
    .string "LORD, that will I seek after; that I\l"
    .string "may dwell in the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "all the days of my life, to behold\l"
    .string "the beauty of the LORD, and to\l"
    .string "enquire in his temple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_5::
    .string "For in the time of trouble he\n"
    .string "shall hide me in his pavilion: in\l"
    .string "the secret of his tabernacle shall\l"
    .string "he hide me; he shall set me up upon\l"
    .string "a rock.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_6::
    .string "And now shall mine head be lifted\n"
    .string "up above mine enemies round about\l"
    .string "me: therefore will I offer in his\l"
    .string "tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I\l"
    .string "will sing, yea, I will sing\l"
    .string "praises unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_7::
    .string "Hear, O LORD, when I cry with my\n"
    .string "voice: have mercy also upon me, and\l"
    .string "answer me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_8::
    .string "When thou saidst, Seek ye my face;\n"
    .string "my heart said unto thee, Thy face,\l"
    .string "LORD, will I seek.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_9::
    .string "Hide not thy face far from me; put\n"
    .string "not thy servant away in anger: thou\l"
    .string "hast been my help; leave me not,\l"
    .string "neither forsake me, O God of my\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_10::
    .string "When my father and my mother forsake\n"
    .string "me, then the LORD will take me up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_11::
    .string "Teach me thy way, O LORD, and lead\n"
    .string "me in a plain path, because of mine\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_12::
    .string "Deliver me not over unto the will\n"
    .string "of mine enemies: for false witnesses\l"
    .string "are risen up against me, and such as\l"
    .string "breathe out cruelty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_13::
    .string "I had fainted, unless I had\n"
    .string "believed to see the goodness of the\l"
    .string "LORD in the land of the living.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_27_14::
    .string "Wait on the LORD: be of good\n"
    .string "courage, and he shall strengthen\l"
    .string "thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_1::
    .string "Unto thee will I cry, O LORD my\n"
    .string "rock; be not silent to me: lest, if\l"
    .string "thou be silent to me, I become like\l"
    .string "them that go down into the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_2::
    .string "Hear the voice of my\n"
    .string "supplications, when I cry unto\l"
    .string "thee, when I lift up my hands toward\l"
    .string "thy holy oracle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_3::
    .string "Draw me not away with the wicked,\n"
    .string "and with the workers of iniquity,\l"
    .string "which speak peace to their\l"
    .string "neighbours, but mischief is in their\l"
    .string "hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_4::
    .string "Give them according to their deeds,\n"
    .string "and according to the wickedness of\l"
    .string "their endeavours: give them after the\l"
    .string "work of their hands; render to them\l"
    .string "their desert.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_5::
    .string "Because they regard not the works of\n"
    .string "the LORD, nor the operation of his\l"
    .string "hands, he shall destroy them, and\l"
    .string "not build them up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_6::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD, because he\n"
    .string "hath heard the voice of my\l"
    .string "supplications.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_7::
    .string "The LORD is my strength and my\n"
    .string "shield; my heart trusted in him, and\l"
    .string "I am helped: therefore my heart\l"
    .string "greatly rejoiceth; and with my song\l"
    .string "will I praise him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_8::
    .string "The LORD is their strength, and he\n"
    .string "is the saving strength of his\l"
    .string "anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_28_9::
    .string "Save thy people, and bless thine\n"
    .string "inheritance: feed them also, and\l"
    .string "lift them up for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_1::
    .string "Give unto the LORD, O ye mighty,\n"
    .string "give unto the LORD glory and\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_2::
    .string "Give unto the LORD the glory due\n"
    .string "unto his name; worship the LORD in\l"
    .string "the beauty of holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_3::
    .string "The voice of the LORD is upon the\n"
    .string "waters: the God of glory thundereth:\l"
    .string "the LORD is upon many waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_4::
    .string "The voice of the LORD is powerful;\n"
    .string "the voice of the LORD is full of\l"
    .string "majesty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_5::
    .string "The voice of the LORD breaketh the\n"
    .string "cedars; yea, the LORD breaketh the\l"
    .string "cedars of Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_6::
    .string "He maketh them also to skip like a\n"
    .string "calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a\l"
    .string "young unicorn.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_7::
    .string "The voice of the LORD divideth the\n"
    .string "flames of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_8::
    .string "The voice of the LORD shaketh the\n"
    .string "wilderness; the LORD shaketh the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Kadesh.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_9::
    .string "The voice of the LORD maketh the\n"
    .string "hinds to calve, and discovereth the\l"
    .string "forests: and in his temple doth\l"
    .string "every one speak of his glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_10::
    .string "The LORD sitteth upon the flood;\n"
    .string "yea, the LORD sitteth King for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_29_11::
    .string "The LORD will give strength unto\n"
    .string "his people; the LORD will bless\l"
    .string "his people with peace.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_1::
    .string "I will extol thee, O LORD; for\n"
    .string "thou hast lifted me up, and hast not\l"
    .string "made my foes to rejoice over me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_2::
    .string "O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and\n"
    .string "thou hast healed me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_3::
    .string "O LORD, thou hast brought up my\n"
    .string "soul from the grave: thou hast kept\l"
    .string "me alive, that I should not go down\l"
    .string "to the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_4::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD, O ye saints of\n"
    .string "his, and give thanks at the\l"
    .string "remembrance of his holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_5::
    .string "For his anger endureth but a moment;\n"
    .string "in his favour is life: weeping may\l"
    .string "endure for a night, but joy cometh in\l"
    .string "the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_6::
    .string "And in my prosperity I said, I\n"
    .string "shall never be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_7::
    .string "LORD, by thy favour thou hast made\n"
    .string "my mountain to stand strong: thou\l"
    .string "didst hide thy face, and I was\l"
    .string "troubled.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_8::
    .string "I cried to thee, O LORD; and unto the\n"
    .string "LORD I made supplication.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_9::
    .string "What profit is there in my blood,\n"
    .string "when I go down to the pit? Shall the\l"
    .string "dust praise thee? shall it declare\l"
    .string "thy truth?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_10::
    .string "Hear, O LORD, and have mercy upon\n"
    .string "me: LORD, be thou my helper.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_11::
    .string "Thou hast turned for me my mourning\n"
    .string "into dancing: thou hast put off my\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and girded me with\l"
    .string "gladness;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_30_12::
    .string "To the end that my glory may sing\n"
    .string "praise to thee, and not be silent. O\l"
    .string "LORD my God, I will give thanks unto\l"
    .string "thee for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_1::
    .string "In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust;\n"
    .string "let me never be ashamed: deliver me\l"
    .string "in thy righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_2::
    .string "Bow down thine ear to me; deliver me\n"
    .string "speedily: be thou my strong rock,\l"
    .string "for an house of defence to save me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_3::
    .string "For thou art my rock and my\n"
    .string "fortress; therefore for thy name’s\l"
    .string "sake lead me, and guide me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_4::
    .string "Pull me out of the net that they\n"
    .string "have laid privily for me: for thou\l"
    .string "art my strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_5::
    .string "Into thine hand I commit my spirit:\n"
    .string "thou hast redeemed me, O LORD God of\l"
    .string "truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_6::
    .string "I have hated them that regard lying\n"
    .string "vanities: but I trust in the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_7::
    .string "I will be glad and rejoice in thy\n"
    .string "mercy: for thou hast considered my\l"
    .string "trouble; thou hast known my soul in\l"
    .string "adversities;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_8::
    .string "And hast not shut me up into the\n"
    .string "hand of the enemy: thou hast set my\l"
    .string "feet in a large room.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_9::
    .string "Have mercy upon me, O LORD, for I am\n"
    .string "in trouble: mine eye is consumed\l"
    .string "with grief, yea, my soul and my\l"
    .string "belly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_10::
    .string "For my life is spent with grief,\n"
    .string "and my years with sighing: my\l"
    .string "strength faileth because of mine\l"
    .string "iniquity, and my bones are consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_11::
    .string "I was a reproach among all mine\n"
    .string "enemies, but especially among my\l"
    .string "neighbours, and a fear to mine\l"
    .string "acquaintance: they that did see me\l"
    .string "without fled from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_12::
    .string "I am forgotten as a dead man out of\n"
    .string "mind: I am like a broken vessel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_13::
    .string "For I have heard the slander of\n"
    .string "many: fear was on every side: while\l"
    .string "they took counsel together against\l"
    .string "me, they devised to take away my\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_14::
    .string "But I trusted in thee, O LORD: I\n"
    .string "said, Thou art my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_15::
    .string "My times are in thy hand: deliver me\n"
    .string "from the hand of mine enemies, and\l"
    .string "from them that persecute me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_16::
    .string "Make thy face to shine upon thy\n"
    .string "servant: save me for thy mercies’\l"
    .string "sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_17::
    .string "Let me not be ashamed, O LORD; for I\n"
    .string "have called upon thee: let the\l"
    .string "wicked be ashamed, and let them be\l"
    .string "silent in the grave.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_18::
    .string "Let the lying lips be put to\n"
    .string "silence; which speak grievous\l"
    .string "things proudly and contemptuously\l"
    .string "against the righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_19::
    .string "Oh how great is thy goodness, which\n"
    .string "thou hast laid up for them that fear\l"
    .string "thee; which thou hast wrought for\l"
    .string "them that trust in thee before the\l"
    .string "sons of men!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_20::
    .string "Thou shalt hide them in the secret\n"
    .string "of thy presence from the pride of\l"
    .string "man: thou shalt keep them secretly\l"
    .string "in a pavilion from the strife of\l"
    .string "tongues.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_21::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD: for he hath\n"
    .string "shewed me his marvellous kindness\l"
    .string "in a strong city.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_22::
    .string "For I said in my haste, I am cut off\n"
    .string "from before thine eyes: nevertheless\l"
    .string "thou heardest the voice of my\l"
    .string "supplications when I cried unto\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_23::
    .string "O love the LORD, all ye his\n"
    .string "saints: for the LORD preserveth the\l"
    .string "faithful, and plentifully\l"
    .string "rewardeth the proud doer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_31_24::
    .string "Be of good courage, and he shall\n"
    .string "strengthen your heart, all ye that\l"
    .string "hope in the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_1::
    .string "Blessed is he whose transgression\n"
    .string "is forgiven, whose sin is covered.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_2::
    .string "Blessed is the man unto whom the\n"
    .string "LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in\l"
    .string "whose spirit there is no guile.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_3::
    .string "When I kept silence, my bones waxed\n"
    .string "old through my roaring all the day\l"
    .string "long.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_4::
    .string "For day and night thy hand was heavy\n"
    .string "upon me: my moisture is turned into\l"
    .string "the drought of summer. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_5::
    .string "I acknowledge my sin unto thee, and\n"
    .string "mine iniquity have I not hid. I said,\l"
    .string "I will confess my transgressions\l"
    .string "unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the\l"
    .string "iniquity of my sin. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_6::
    .string "For this shall every one that is\n"
    .string "godly pray unto thee in a time when\l"
    .string "thou mayest be found: surely in the\l"
    .string "floods of great waters they shall\l"
    .string "not come nigh unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_7::
    .string "Thou art my hiding place; thou\n"
    .string "shalt preserve me from trouble;\l"
    .string "thou shalt compass me about with\l"
    .string "songs of deliverance. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_8::
    .string "I will instruct thee and teach\n"
    .string "thee in the way which thou shalt go:\l"
    .string "I will guide thee with mine eye.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_9::
    .string "Be ye not as the horse, or as the\n"
    .string "mule, which have no understanding:\l"
    .string "whose mouth must be held in with bit\l"
    .string "and bridle, lest they come near unto\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_10::
    .string "Many sorrows shall be to the\n"
    .string "wicked: but he that trusteth in the\l"
    .string "LORD, mercy shall compass him\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_32_11::
    .string "Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye\n"
    .string "righteous: and shout for joy, all ye\l"
    .string "that are upright in heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_1::
    .string "Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous:\n"
    .string "for praise is comely for the\l"
    .string "upright.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_2::
    .string "Praise the LORD with harp: sing\n"
    .string "unto him with the psaltery and an\l"
    .string "instrument of ten strings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_3::
    .string "Sing unto him a new song; play\n"
    .string "skilfully with a loud noise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_4::
    .string "For the word of the LORD is right;\n"
    .string "and all his works are done in truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_5::
    .string "He loveth righteousness and\n"
    .string "judgment: the earth is full of the\l"
    .string "goodness of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_6::
    .string "By the word of the LORD were the\n"
    .string "heavens made; and all the host of\l"
    .string "them by the breath of his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_7::
    .string "He gathereth the waters of the sea\n"
    .string "together as an heap: he layeth up\l"
    .string "the depth in storehouses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_8::
    .string "Let all the earth fear the LORD:\n"
    .string "let all the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "world stand in awe of him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_9::
    .string "For he spake, and it was done; he\n"
    .string "commanded, and it stood fast.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_10::
    .string "The LORD bringeth the counsel of\n"
    .string "the heathen to nought: he maketh the\l"
    .string "devices of the people of none\l"
    .string "effect.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_11::
    .string "The counsel of the LORD standeth\n"
    .string "for ever, the thoughts of his heart\l"
    .string "to all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_12::
    .string "Blessed is the nation whose God is\n"
    .string "the LORD; and the people whom he\l"
    .string "hath chosen for his own inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_13::
    .string "The LORD looketh from heaven; he\n"
    .string "beholdeth all the sons of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_14::
    .string "From the place of his habitation\n"
    .string "he looketh upon all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_15::
    .string "He fashioneth their hearts alike;\n"
    .string "he considereth all their works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_16::
    .string "There is no king saved by the\n"
    .string "multitude of an host: a mighty man is\l"
    .string "not delivered by much strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_17::
    .string "An horse is a vain thing for safety:\n"
    .string "neither shall he deliver any by his\l"
    .string "great strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_18::
    .string "Behold, the eye of the LORD is upon\n"
    .string "them that fear him, upon them that\l"
    .string "hope in his mercy;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_19::
    .string "To deliver their soul from death,\n"
    .string "and to keep them alive in famine.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_20::
    .string "Our soul waiteth for the LORD: he is\n"
    .string "our help and our shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_21::
    .string "For our heart shall rejoice in him,\n"
    .string "because we have trusted in his holy\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_33_22::
    .string "Let thy mercy, O LORD, be upon us,\n"
    .string "according as we hope in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_1::
    .string "I will bless the LORD at all\n"
    .string "times: his praise shall\l"
    .string "continually be in my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_2::
    .string "My soul shall make her boast in\n"
    .string "the LORD: the humble shall hear\l"
    .string "thereof, and be glad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_3::
    .string "O magnify the LORD with me, and let\n"
    .string "us exalt his name together.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_4::
    .string "I sought the LORD, and he heard me,\n"
    .string "and delivered me from all my fears.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_5::
    .string "They looked unto him, and were\n"
    .string "lightened: and their faces were not\l"
    .string "ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_6::
    .string "This poor man cried, and the LORD\n"
    .string "heard him, and saved him out of all\l"
    .string "his troubles.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_7::
    .string "The angel of the LORD encampeth\n"
    .string "round about them that fear him, and\l"
    .string "delivereth them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_8::
    .string "O taste and see that the LORD is\n"
    .string "good: blessed is the man that\l"
    .string "trusteth in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_9::
    .string "O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for\n"
    .string "there is no want to them that fear\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_10::
    .string "The young lions do lack, and suffer\n"
    .string "hunger: but they that seek the LORD\l"
    .string "shall not want any good thing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_11::
    .string "Come, ye children, hearken unto me:\n"
    .string "I will teach you the fear of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_12::
    .string "What man is he that desireth life,\n"
    .string "and loveth many days, that he may see\l"
    .string "good?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_13::
    .string "Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy\n"
    .string "lips from speaking guile.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_14::
    .string "Depart from evil, and do good; seek\n"
    .string "peace, and pursue it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_15::
    .string "The eyes of the LORD are upon the\n"
    .string "righteous, and his ears are open\l"
    .string "unto their cry.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_16::
    .string "The face of the LORD is against them\n"
    .string "that do evil, to cut off the\l"
    .string "remembrance of them from the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_17::
    .string "The righteous cry, and the LORD\n"
    .string "heareth, and delivereth them out of\l"
    .string "all their troubles.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_18::
    .string "The LORD is nigh unto them that are\n"
    .string "of a broken heart; and saveth such as\l"
    .string "be of a contrite spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_19::
    .string "Many are the afflictions of the\n"
    .string "righteous: but the LORD delivereth\l"
    .string "him out of them all.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_20::
    .string "He keepeth all his bones: not one\n"
    .string "of them is broken.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_21::
    .string "Evil shall slay the wicked: and\n"
    .string "they that hate the righteous shall\l"
    .string "be desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_34_22::
    .string "The LORD redeemeth the soul of his\n"
    .string "servants: and none of them that trust\l"
    .string "in him shall be desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_1::
    .string "Plead my cause, O LORD, with them\n"
    .string "that strive with me: fight against\l"
    .string "them that fight against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_2::
    .string "Take hold of shield and buckler,\n"
    .string "and stand up for mine help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_3::
    .string "Draw out also the spear, and stop\n"
    .string "the way against them that persecute\l"
    .string "me: say unto my soul, I am thy\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_4::
    .string "Let them be confounded and put to\n"
    .string "shame that seek after my soul: let\l"
    .string "them be turned back and brought to\l"
    .string "confusion that devise my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_5::
    .string "Let them be as chaff before the\n"
    .string "wind: and let the angel of the LORD\l"
    .string "chase them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_6::
    .string "Let their way be dark and\n"
    .string "slippery: and let the angel of the\l"
    .string "LORD persecute them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_7::
    .string "For without cause have they hid for\n"
    .string "me their net in a pit, which without\l"
    .string "cause they have digged for my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_8::
    .string "Let destruction come upon him at\n"
    .string "unawares; and let his net that he\l"
    .string "hath hid catch himself: into that\l"
    .string "very destruction let him fall.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_9::
    .string "And my soul shall be joyful in\n"
    .string "the LORD: it shall rejoice in his\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_10::
    .string "All my bones shall say, LORD, who\n"
    .string "is like unto thee, which deliverest\l"
    .string "the poor from him that is too strong\l"
    .string "for him, yea, the poor and the needy\l"
    .string "from him that spoileth him?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_11::
    .string "False witnesses did rise up; they\n"
    .string "laid to my charge things that I knew\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_12::
    .string "They rewarded me evil for good to\n"
    .string "the spoiling of my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_13::
    .string "But as for me, when they were sick,\n"
    .string "my clothing was sackcloth: I\l"
    .string "humbled my soul with fasting; and my\l"
    .string "prayer returned into mine own bosom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_14::
    .string "I behaved myself as though he had\n"
    .string "been my friend or brother: I bowed\l"
    .string "down heavily, as one that mourneth\l"
    .string "for his mother.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_15::
    .string "But in mine adversity they rejoiced,\n"
    .string "and gathered themselves together:\l"
    .string "yea, the abjects gathered themselves\l"
    .string "together against me, and I knew it\l"
    .string "not; they did tear me, and ceased not:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_16::
    .string "With hypocritical mockers in\n"
    .string "feasts, they gnashed upon me with\l"
    .string "their teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_17::
    .string "Lord, how long wilt thou look on?\n"
    .string "rescue my soul from their\l"
    .string "destructions, my darling from the\l"
    .string "lions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_18::
    .string "I will give thee thanks in the\n"
    .string "great congregation: I will praise\l"
    .string "thee among much people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_19::
    .string "Let not them that are mine enemies\n"
    .string "wrongfully rejoice over me: neither\l"
    .string "let them wink with the eye that hate\l"
    .string "me without a cause.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_20::
    .string "For they speak not peace: but they\n"
    .string "devise deceitful matters against\l"
    .string "them that are quiet in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_21::
    .string "Yea, they opened their mouth wide\n"
    .string "against me, and said, Aha, aha, our\l"
    .string "eye hath seen it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_22::
    .string "This thou hast seen, O LORD: keep\n"
    .string "not silence: O Lord, be not far from\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_23::
    .string "Stir up thyself, and awake to my\n"
    .string "judgment, even unto my cause, my God\l"
    .string "and my Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_24::
    .string "Judge me, O LORD my God, according\n"
    .string "to thy righteousness; and let them\l"
    .string "not rejoice over me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_25::
    .string "Let them not say in their hearts,\n"
    .string "Ah, so would we have it: let them\l"
    .string "not say, We have swallowed him up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_26::
    .string "Let them be ashamed and brought to\n"
    .string "confusion together that rejoice at\l"
    .string "mine hurt: let them be clothed with\l"
    .string "shame and dishonour that magnify\l"
    .string "themselves against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_27::
    .string "Let them shout for joy, and be glad,\n"
    .string "that favour my righteous cause: yea,\l"
    .string "let them say continually, Let the\l"
    .string "LORD be magnified, which hath\l"
    .string "pleasure in the prosperity of his\l"
    .string "servant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_35_28::
    .string "And my tongue shall speak of thy\n"
    .string "righteousness and of thy praise\l"
    .string "all the day long.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_1::
    .string "The transgression of the wicked\n"
    .string "saith within my heart, that there is\l"
    .string "no fear of God before his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_2::
    .string "For he flattereth himself in his\n"
    .string "own eyes, until his iniquity be\l"
    .string "found to be hateful.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_3::
    .string "The words of his mouth are iniquity\n"
    .string "and deceit: he hath left off to be\l"
    .string "wise, and to do good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_4::
    .string "He deviseth mischief upon his bed;\n"
    .string "he setteth himself in a way that is\l"
    .string "not good; he abhorreth not evil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_5::
    .string "Thy mercy, O LORD, is in the heavens;\n"
    .string "and thy faithfulness reacheth unto\l"
    .string "the clouds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_6::
    .string "Thy righteousness is like the great\n"
    .string "mountains; thy judgments are a great\l"
    .string "deep: O LORD, thou preservest man\l"
    .string "and beast.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_7::
    .string "How excellent is thy\n"
    .string "lovingkindness, O God! therefore the\l"
    .string "children of men put their trust\l"
    .string "under the shadow of thy wings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_8::
    .string "They shall be abundantly\n"
    .string "satisfied with the fatness of thy\l"
    .string "house; and thou shalt make them\l"
    .string "drink of the river of thy pleasures.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_9::
    .string "For with thee is the fountain of\n"
    .string "life: in thy light shall we see\l"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_10::
    .string "O continue thy lovingkindness unto\n"
    .string "them that know thee; and thy\l"
    .string "righteousness to the upright in\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_11::
    .string "Let not the foot of pride come\n"
    .string "against me, and let not the hand of\l"
    .string "the wicked remove me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_36_12::
    .string "There are the workers of iniquity\n"
    .string "fallen: they are cast down, and\l"
    .string "shall not be able to rise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_1::
    .string "Fret not thyself because of\n"
    .string "evildoers, neither be thou envious\l"
    .string "against the workers of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_2::
    .string "For they shall soon be cut down\n"
    .string "like the grass, and wither as the\l"
    .string "green herb.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_3::
    .string "Trust in the LORD, and do good; so\n"
    .string "shalt thou dwell in the land, and\l"
    .string "verily thou shalt be fed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_4::
    .string "Delight thyself also in the LORD:\n"
    .string "and he shall give thee the desires\l"
    .string "of thine heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_5::
    .string "Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust\n"
    .string "also in him; and he shall bring it\l"
    .string "to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_6::
    .string "And he shall bring forth thy\n"
    .string "righteousness as the light, and thy\l"
    .string "judgment as the noonday.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_7::
    .string "Rest in the LORD, and wait\n"
    .string "patiently for him: fret not thyself\l"
    .string "because of him who prospereth in\l"
    .string "his way, because of the man who\l"
    .string "bringeth wicked devices to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_8::
    .string "Cease from anger, and forsake wrath:\n"
    .string "fret not thyself in any wise to do\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_9::
    .string "For evildoers shall be cut off:\n"
    .string "but those that wait upon the LORD,\l"
    .string "they shall inherit the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_10::
    .string "For yet a little while, and the\n"
    .string "wicked shall not be: yea, thou\l"
    .string "shalt diligently consider his\l"
    .string "place, and it shall not be.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_11::
    .string "But the meek shall inherit the\n"
    .string "earth; and shall delight\l"
    .string "themselves in the abundance of\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_12::
    .string "The wicked plotteth against the\n"
    .string "just, and gnasheth upon him with his\l"
    .string "teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_13::
    .string "The LORD shall laugh at him: for\n"
    .string "he seeth that his day is coming.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_14::
    .string "The wicked have drawn out the sword,\n"
    .string "and have bent their bow, to cast down\l"
    .string "the poor and needy, and to slay such\l"
    .string "as be of upright conversation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_15::
    .string "Their sword shall enter into their\n"
    .string "own heart, and their bows shall be\l"
    .string "broken.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_16::
    .string "A little that a righteous man hath\n"
    .string "is better than the riches of many\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_17::
    .string "For the arms of the wicked shall be\n"
    .string "broken: but the LORD upholdeth the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_18::
    .string "The LORD knoweth the days of the\n"
    .string "upright: and their inheritance\l"
    .string "shall be for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_19::
    .string "They shall not be ashamed in the\n"
    .string "evil time: and in the days of famine\l"
    .string "they shall be satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_20::
    .string "But the wicked shall perish, and\n"
    .string "the enemies of the LORD shall be as\l"
    .string "the fat of lambs: they shall\l"
    .string "consume; into smoke shall they\l"
    .string "consume away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_21::
    .string "The wicked borroweth, and payeth\n"
    .string "not again: but the righteous sheweth\l"
    .string "mercy, and giveth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_22::
    .string "For such as be blessed of him\n"
    .string "shall inherit the earth; and they\l"
    .string "that be cursed of him shall be cut\l"
    .string "off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_23::
    .string "The steps of a good man are ordered\n"
    .string "by the LORD: and he delighteth in his\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_24::
    .string "Though he fall, he shall not be\n"
    .string "utterly cast down: for the LORD\l"
    .string "upholdeth him with his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_25::
    .string "I have been young, and now am old;\n"
    .string "yet have I not seen the righteous\l"
    .string "forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_26::
    .string "He is ever merciful, and lendeth;\n"
    .string "and his seed is blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_27::
    .string "Depart from evil, and do good; and\n"
    .string "dwell for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_28::
    .string "For the LORD loveth judgment, and\n"
    .string "forsaketh not his saints; they are\l"
    .string "preserved for ever: but the seed of\l"
    .string "the wicked shall be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_29::
    .string "The righteous shall inherit the\n"
    .string "land, and dwell therein for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_30::
    .string "The mouth of the righteous speaketh\n"
    .string "wisdom, and his tongue talketh of\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_31::
    .string "The law of his God is in his heart;\n"
    .string "none of his steps shall slide.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_32::
    .string "The wicked watcheth the righteous,\n"
    .string "and seeketh to slay him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_33::
    .string "The LORD will not leave him in his\n"
    .string "hand, nor condemn him when he is\l"
    .string "judged.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_34::
    .string "Wait on the LORD, and keep his way,\n"
    .string "and he shall exalt thee to inherit\l"
    .string "the land: when the wicked are cut\l"
    .string "off, thou shalt see it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_35::
    .string "I have seen the wicked in great\n"
    .string "power, and spreading himself like a\l"
    .string "green bay tree.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_36::
    .string "Yet he passed away, and, lo, he was\n"
    .string "not: yea, I sought him, but he could\l"
    .string "not be found.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_37::
    .string "Mark the perfect man, and behold\n"
    .string "the upright: for the end of that man\l"
    .string "is peace.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_38::
    .string "But the transgressors shall be\n"
    .string "destroyed together: the end of the\l"
    .string "wicked shall be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_39::
    .string "But the salvation of the righteous\n"
    .string "is of the LORD: he is their strength\l"
    .string "in the time of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_37_40::
    .string "And the LORD shall help them, and\n"
    .string "deliver them: he shall deliver\l"
    .string "them from the wicked, and save them,\l"
    .string "because they trust in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_1::
    .string "O lord, rebuke me not in thy wrath:\n"
    .string "neither chasten me in thy hot\l"
    .string "displeasure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_2::
    .string "For thine arrows stick fast in me,\n"
    .string "and thy hand presseth me sore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_3::
    .string "There is no soundness in my flesh\n"
    .string "because of thine anger; neither is\l"
    .string "there any rest in my bones because of\l"
    .string "my sin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_4::
    .string "For mine iniquities are gone over\n"
    .string "mine head: as an heavy burden they\l"
    .string "are too heavy for me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_5::
    .string "My wounds stink and are corrupt\n"
    .string "because of my foolishness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_6::
    .string "I am troubled; I am bowed down\n"
    .string "greatly; I go mourning all the day\l"
    .string "long.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_7::
    .string "For my loins are filled with a\n"
    .string "loathsome disease: and there is no\l"
    .string "soundness in my flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_8::
    .string "I am feeble and sore broken: I have\n"
    .string "roared by reason of the disquietness\l"
    .string "of my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_9::
    .string "Lord, all my desire is before thee;\n"
    .string "and my groaning is not hid from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_10::
    .string "My heart panteth, my strength\n"
    .string "faileth me: as for the light of mine\l"
    .string "eyes, it also is gone from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_11::
    .string "My lovers and my friends stand\n"
    .string "aloof from my sore; and my kinsmen\l"
    .string "stand afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_12::
    .string "They also that seek after my life\n"
    .string "lay snares for me: and they that seek\l"
    .string "my hurt speak mischievous things,\l"
    .string "and imagine deceits all the day\l"
    .string "long.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_13::
    .string "But I, as a deaf man, heard not; and\n"
    .string "I was as a dumb man that openeth not\l"
    .string "his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_14::
    .string "Thus I was as a man that heareth not,\n"
    .string "and in whose mouth are no reproofs.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_15::
    .string "For in thee, O LORD, do I hope: thou\n"
    .string "wilt hear, O Lord my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_16::
    .string "For I said, Hear me, lest otherwise\n"
    .string "they should rejoice over me: when my\l"
    .string "foot slippeth, they magnify\l"
    .string "themselves against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_17::
    .string "For I am ready to halt, and my\n"
    .string "sorrow is continually before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_18::
    .string "For I will declare mine iniquity;\n"
    .string "I will be sorry for my sin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_19::
    .string "But mine enemies are lively, and\n"
    .string "they are strong: and they that hate\l"
    .string "me wrongfully are multiplied.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_20::
    .string "They also that render evil for\n"
    .string "good are mine adversaries; because I\l"
    .string "follow the thing that good is.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_21::
    .string "Forsake me not, O LORD: O my God, be\n"
    .string "not far from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_38_22::
    .string "Make haste to help me, O Lord my\n"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_1::
    .string "I said, I will take heed to my\n"
    .string "ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I\l"
    .string "will keep my mouth with a bridle,\l"
    .string "while the wicked is before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_2::
    .string "I was dumb with silence, I held my\n"
    .string "peace, even from good; and my sorrow\l"
    .string "was stirred.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_3::
    .string "My heart was hot within me, while I\n"
    .string "was musing the fire burned: then\l"
    .string "spake I with my tongue,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_4::
    .string "LORD, make me to know mine end, and\n"
    .string "the measure of my days, what it is:\l"
    .string "that I may know how frail I am.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_5::
    .string "Behold, thou hast made my days as an\n"
    .string "handbreadth; and mine age is as\l"
    .string "nothing before thee: verily every\l"
    .string "man at his best state is altogether\l"
    .string "vanity. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_6::
    .string "Surely every man walketh in a vain\n"
    .string "shew: surely they are disquieted in\l"
    .string "vain: he heapeth up riches, and\l"
    .string "knoweth not who shall gather them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_7::
    .string "And now, Lord, what wait I for? my\n"
    .string "hope is in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_8::
    .string "Deliver me from all my\n"
    .string "transgressions: make me not the\l"
    .string "reproach of the foolish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_9::
    .string "I was dumb, I opened not my mouth;\n"
    .string "because thou didst it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_10::
    .string "Remove thy stroke away from me: I am\n"
    .string "consumed by the blow of thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_11::
    .string "When thou with rebukes dost correct\n"
    .string "man for iniquity, thou makest his\l"
    .string "beauty to consume away like a moth:\l"
    .string "surely every man is vanity. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_12::
    .string "Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear\n"
    .string "unto my cry; hold not thy peace at\l"
    .string "my tears: for I am a stranger with\l"
    .string "thee, and a sojourner, as all my\l"
    .string "fathers were.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_39_13::
    .string "O spare me, that I may recover\n"
    .string "strength, before I go hence, and be\l"
    .string "no more.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_1::
    .string "I waited patiently for the LORD;\n"
    .string "and he inclined unto me, and heard my\l"
    .string "cry.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_2::
    .string "He brought me up also out of an\n"
    .string "horrible pit, out of the miry clay,\l"
    .string "and set my feet upon a rock, and\l"
    .string "established my goings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_3::
    .string "And he hath put a new song in my\n"
    .string "mouth, even praise unto our God:\l"
    .string "many shall see it, and fear, and\l"
    .string "shall trust in the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_4::
    .string "Blessed is that man that maketh the\n"
    .string "LORD his trust, and respecteth not\l"
    .string "the proud, nor such as turn aside to\l"
    .string "lies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_5::
    .string "Many, O LORD my God, are thy\n"
    .string "wonderful works which thou hast\l"
    .string "done, and thy thoughts which are to\l"
    .string "us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up\l"
    .string "in order unto thee: if I would\l"
    .string "declare and speak of them, they are\l"
    .string "more than can be numbered.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_6::
    .string "Sacrifice and offering thou didst\n"
    .string "not desire; mine ears hast thou\l"
    .string "opened: burnt offering and sin\l"
    .string "offering hast thou not required.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_7::
    .string "Then said I, Lo, I come: in the\n"
    .string "volume of the book it is written of\l"
    .string "me,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_8::
    .string "I delight to do thy will, O my God:\n"
    .string "yea, thy law is within my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_9::
    .string "I have preached righteousness in\n"
    .string "the great congregation: lo, I have\l"
    .string "not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou\l"
    .string "knowest.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_10::
    .string "I have not hid thy righteousness\n"
    .string "within my heart; I have declared thy\l"
    .string "faithfulness and thy salvation: I\l"
    .string "have not concealed thy\l"
    .string "lovingkindness and thy truth from\l"
    .string "the great congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_11::
    .string "Withhold not thou thy tender\n"
    .string "mercies from me, O LORD: let thy\l"
    .string "lovingkindness and thy truth\l"
    .string "continually preserve me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_12::
    .string "For innumerable evils have\n"
    .string "compassed me about: mine iniquities\l"
    .string "have taken hold upon me, so that I\l"
    .string "am not able to look up; they are\l"
    .string "more than the hairs of mine head:\l"
    .string "therefore my heart faileth me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_13::
    .string "Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me:\n"
    .string "O LORD, make haste to help me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_14::
    .string "Let them be ashamed and confounded\n"
    .string "together that seek after my soul to\l"
    .string "destroy it; let them be driven\l"
    .string "backward and put to shame that wish\l"
    .string "me evil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_15::
    .string "Let them be desolate for a reward\n"
    .string "of their shame that say unto me, Aha,\l"
    .string "aha.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_16::
    .string "Let all those that seek thee\n"
    .string "rejoice and be glad in thee: let\l"
    .string "such as love thy salvation say\l"
    .string "continually, The LORD be magnified.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_40_17::
    .string "But I am poor and needy; yet the\n"
    .string "Lord thinketh upon me: thou art my\l"
    .string "help and my deliverer; make no\l"
    .string "tarrying, O my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_1::
    .string "Blessed is he that considereth the\n"
    .string "poor: the LORD will deliver him in\l"
    .string "time of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_2::
    .string "The LORD will preserve him, and\n"
    .string "keep him alive; and he shall be\l"
    .string "blessed upon the earth: and thou\l"
    .string "wilt not deliver him unto the will\l"
    .string "of his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_3::
    .string "The LORD will strengthen him upon\n"
    .string "the bed of languishing: thou wilt\l"
    .string "make all his bed in his sickness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_4::
    .string "I said, LORD, be merciful unto me:\n"
    .string "heal my soul; for I have sinned\l"
    .string "against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_5::
    .string "Mine enemies speak evil of me, When\n"
    .string "shall he die, and his name perish?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_6::
    .string "And if he come to see me, he\n"
    .string "speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth\l"
    .string "iniquity to itself; when he goeth\l"
    .string "abroad, he telleth it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_7::
    .string "All that hate me whisper together\n"
    .string "against me: against me do they devise\l"
    .string "my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_8::
    .string "An evil disease, say they,\n"
    .string "cleaveth fast unto him: and now that\l"
    .string "he lieth he shall rise up no more.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_9::
    .string "Yea, mine own familiar friend, in\n"
    .string "whom I trusted, which did eat of my\l"
    .string "bread, hath lifted up his heel\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_10::
    .string "But thou, O LORD, be merciful unto\n"
    .string "me, and raise me up, that I may\l"
    .string "requite them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_11::
    .string "By this I know that thou favourest\n"
    .string "me, because mine enemy doth not\l"
    .string "triumph over me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_12::
    .string "And as for me, thou upholdest me in\n"
    .string "mine integrity, and settest me before\l"
    .string "thy face for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_41_13::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "from everlasting, and to everlasting\l"
    .string " Amen, and Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_1::
    .string "As the hart panteth after the water\n"
    .string "brooks, so panteth my soul after\l"
    .string "thee, O God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_2::
    .string "My soul thirsteth for God, for the\n"
    .string "living God: when shall I come and\l"
    .string "appear before God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_3::
    .string "My tears have been my meat day and\n"
    .string "night, while they continually say\l"
    .string "unto me, Where is thy God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_4::
    .string "When I remember these things, I\n"
    .string "pour out my soul in me: for I had\l"
    .string "gone with the multitude, I went with\l"
    .string "them to the house of God, with the\l"
    .string "voice of joy and praise, with a\l"
    .string "multitude that kept holyday.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_5::
    .string "Why art thou cast down, O my soul?\n"
    .string "and why art thou disquieted in me?\l"
    .string "hope thou in God: for I shall yet\l"
    .string "praise him for the help of his\l"
    .string "countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_6::
    .string "O my God, my soul is cast down\n"
    .string "within me: therefore will I\l"
    .string "remember thee from the land of\l"
    .string "Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from\l"
    .string "the hill Mizar.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_7::
    .string "Deep calleth unto deep at the\n"
    .string "noise of thy waterspouts: all thy\l"
    .string "waves and thy billows are gone over\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_8::
    .string "Yet the LORD will command his\n"
    .string "lovingkindness in the day time, and\l"
    .string "in the night his song shall be with\l"
    .string "me, and my prayer unto the God of my\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_9::
    .string "I will say unto God my rock, Why\n"
    .string "hast thou forgotten me? why go I\l"
    .string "mourning because of the oppression\l"
    .string "of the enemy?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_10::
    .string "As with a sword in my bones, mine\n"
    .string "enemies reproach me; while they say\l"
    .string "daily unto me, Where is thy God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_42_11::
    .string "Why art thou cast down, O my soul?\n"
    .string "and why art thou disquieted within\l"
    .string "me? hope thou in God: for I shall\l"
    .string "yet praise him, who is the health of\l"
    .string "my countenance, and my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_43_1::
    .string "Judge me, O God, and plead my cause\n"
    .string "against an ungodly nation: O\l"
    .string "deliver me from the deceitful and\l"
    .string "unjust man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_43_2::
    .string "For thou art the God of my strength:\n"
    .string "why dost thou cast me off? why go I\l"
    .string "mourning because of the oppression\l"
    .string "of the enemy?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_43_3::
    .string "O send out thy light and thy truth:\n"
    .string "let them lead me; let them bring me\l"
    .string "unto thy holy hill, and to thy\l"
    .string "tabernacles.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_43_4::
    .string "Then will I go unto the altar of\n"
    .string "God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea,\l"
    .string "upon the harp will I praise thee,\l"
    .string "O God my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_43_5::
    .string "Why art thou cast down, O my soul?\n"
    .string "and why art thou disquieted within\l"
    .string "me? hope in God: for I shall yet\l"
    .string "praise him, who is the health of my\l"
    .string "countenance, and my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_1::
    .string "We have heard with our ears, O God,\n"
    .string "our fathers have told us, what work\l"
    .string "thou didst in their days, in the\l"
    .string "times of old.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_2::
    .string "How thou didst drive out the heathen\n"
    .string "with thy hand, and plantedst them;\l"
    .string "how thou didst afflict the people,\l"
    .string "and cast them out.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_3::
    .string "For they got not the land in\n"
    .string "possession by their own sword,\l"
    .string "neither did their own arm save them:\l"
    .string "but thy right hand, and thine arm,\l"
    .string "and the light of thy countenance,\l"
    .string "because thou hadst a favour unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_4::
    .string "Thou art my King, O God: command\n"
    .string "deliverances for Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_5::
    .string "Through thee will we push down our\n"
    .string "enemies: through thy name will we\l"
    .string "tread them under that rise up\l"
    .string "against us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_6::
    .string "For I will not trust in my bow,\n"
    .string "neither shall my sword save me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_7::
    .string "But thou hast saved us from our\n"
    .string "enemies, and hast put them to shame\l"
    .string "that hated us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_8::
    .string "In God we boast all the day long,\n"
    .string "and praise thy name for ever. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_9::
    .string "But thou hast cast off, and put us\n"
    .string "to shame; and goest not forth with\l"
    .string "our armies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_10::
    .string "Thou makest us to turn back from the\n"
    .string "enemy: and they which hate us spoil\l"
    .string "for themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_11::
    .string "Thou hast given us like sheep\n"
    .string "appointed for meat; and hast\l"
    .string "scattered us among the heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_12::
    .string "Thou sellest thy people for\n"
    .string "nought, and dost not increase thy\l"
    .string "wealth by their price.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_13::
    .string "Thou makest us a reproach to our\n"
    .string "neighbours, a scorn and a derision to\l"
    .string "them that are round about us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_14::
    .string "Thou makest us a byword among the\n"
    .string "heathen, a shaking of the head among\l"
    .string "the people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_15::
    .string "My confusion is continually before\n"
    .string "me, and the shame of my face hath\l"
    .string "covered me,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_16::
    .string "For the voice of him that\n"
    .string "reproacheth and blasphemeth; by\l"
    .string "reason of the enemy and avenger.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_17::
    .string "All this is come upon us; yet have\n"
    .string "we not forgotten thee, neither have\l"
    .string "we dealt falsely in thy covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_18::
    .string "Our heart is not turned back,\n"
    .string "neither have our steps declined\l"
    .string "from thy way;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_19::
    .string "Though thou hast sore broken us in\n"
    .string "the place of dragons, and covered us\l"
    .string "with the shadow of death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_20::
    .string "If we have forgotten the name of our\n"
    .string "God, or stretched out our hands to a\l"
    .string "strange god;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_21::
    .string "Shall not God search this out? for\n"
    .string "he knoweth the secrets of the heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_22::
    .string "Yea, for thy sake are we killed\n"
    .string "all the day long; we are counted as\l"
    .string "sheep for the slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_23::
    .string "Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord?\n"
    .string "arise, cast us not off for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_24::
    .string "Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and\n"
    .string "forgettest our affliction and our\l"
    .string "oppression?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_25::
    .string "For our soul is bowed down to the\n"
    .string "dust: our belly cleaveth unto the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_44_26::
    .string "Arise for our help, and redeem us\n"
    .string "for thy mercies’ sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_1::
    .string "My heart is inditing a good matter:\n"
    .string "I speak of the things which I have\l"
    .string "made touching the king: my tongue is\l"
    .string "the pen of a ready writer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_2::
    .string "Thou art fairer than the children\n"
    .string "of men: grace is poured into thy\l"
    .string "lips: therefore God hath blessed\l"
    .string "thee for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_3::
    .string "Gird thy sword upon thy thigh, O\n"
    .string "most mighty, with thy glory and thy\l"
    .string "majesty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_4::
    .string "And in thy majesty ride\n"
    .string "prosperously because of truth and\l"
    .string "meekness and righteousness; and thy\l"
    .string "right hand shall teach thee\l"
    .string "terrible things.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_5::
    .string "Thine arrows are sharp in the heart\n"
    .string "of the king’s enemies; whereby the\l"
    .string "people fall under thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_6::
    .string "Thy throne, O God, is for ever and\n"
    .string "ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom is a\l"
    .string "right sceptre.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_7::
    .string "Thou lovest righteousness, and\n"
    .string "hatest wickedness: therefore God,\l"
    .string "thy God, hath anointed thee with the\l"
    .string "oil of gladness above thy fellows.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_8::
    .string "All thy garments smell of myrrh,\n"
    .string "and aloes, and cassia, out of the\l"
    .string "ivory palaces, whereby they have\l"
    .string "made thee glad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_9::
    .string "Kings’ daughters were among thy\n"
    .string "honourable women: upon thy right\l"
    .string "hand did stand the queen in gold of\l"
    .string "Ophir.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_10::
    .string "Hearken, O daughter, and consider,\n"
    .string "and incline thine ear; forget also\l"
    .string "thine own people, and thy father’s\l"
    .string "house;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_11::
    .string "So shall the king greatly desire\n"
    .string "thy beauty: for he is thy Lord; and\l"
    .string "worship thou him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_12::
    .string "And the daughter of Tyre shall be\n"
    .string "there with a gift; even the rich\l"
    .string "among the people shall intreat\l"
    .string "thy favour.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_13::
    .string "The king’s daughter is all\n"
    .string "glorious within: her clothing is of\l"
    .string "wrought gold.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_14::
    .string "She shall be brought unto the king\n"
    .string "in raiment of needlework: the\l"
    .string "virgins her companions that follow\l"
    .string "her shall be brought unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_15::
    .string "With gladness and rejoicing shall\n"
    .string "they be brought: they shall enter\l"
    .string "into the king’s palace.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_16::
    .string "Instead of thy fathers shall be\n"
    .string "thy children, whom thou mayest make\l"
    .string "princes in all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_45_17::
    .string "I will make thy name to be\n"
    .string "remembered in all generations:\l"
    .string "therefore shall the people\l"
    .string "praise thee for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_1::
    .string "God is our refuge and strength, a\n"
    .string "very present help in trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_2::
    .string "Therefore will not we fear, though\n"
    .string "the earth be removed, and though the\l"
    .string "mountains be carried into the midst\l"
    .string "of the sea;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_3::
    .string "Though the waters thereof roar and\n"
    .string "be troubled, though the mountains\l"
    .string "shake with the swelling thereof.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_4::
    .string "There is a river, the streams\n"
    .string "whereof shall make glad the city of\l"
    .string "God, the holy place of the\l"
    .string "tabernacles of the most High.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_5::
    .string "God is in the midst of her; she\n"
    .string "shall not be moved: God shall\l"
    .string "help her, and that right early.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_6::
    .string "The heathen raged, the kingdoms were\n"
    .string "moved: he uttered his voice, the\l"
    .string "earth melted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_7::
    .string "The LORD of hosts is with us; the God\n"
    .string "of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_8::
    .string "Come, behold the works of the LORD,\n"
    .string "what desolations he hath made in the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_9::
    .string "He maketh wars to cease unto the end\n"
    .string "of the earth; he breaketh the bow,\l"
    .string "and cutteth the spear in sunder; he\l"
    .string "burneth the chariot in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_10::
    .string "Be still, and know that I am God: I\n"
    .string "will be exalted among the heathen,\l"
    .string "I will be exalted in the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_46_11::
    .string "The LORD of hosts is with us; the God\n"
    .string "of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_1::
    .string "O clap your hands, all ye\n"
    .string "people; shout unto God with the\l"
    .string "voice of triumph.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_2::
    .string "For the LORD most high is terrible;\n"
    .string "he is a great King over all the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_3::
    .string "He shall subdue the people under\n"
    .string "us, and the nations under our feet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_4::
    .string "He shall choose our inheritance\n"
    .string "for us, the excellency of Jacob whom\l"
    .string "he loved. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_5::
    .string "God is gone up with a shout, the\n"
    .string "LORD with the sound of a trumpet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_6::
    .string "Sing praises to God, sing praises:\n"
    .string "sing praises unto our King, sing\l"
    .string "praises.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_7::
    .string "For God is the King of all the\n"
    .string "earth: sing ye praises with\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_8::
    .string "God reigneth over the heathen: God\n"
    .string "sitteth upon the throne of his\l"
    .string "holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_47_9::
    .string "The princes of the people are\n"
    .string "gathered together, even the people\l"
    .string "of the God of Abraham: for the\l"
    .string "shields of the earth belong unto\l"
    .string "God: he is greatly exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_1::
    .string "Great is the LORD, and greatly to be\n"
    .string "praised in the city of our God, in the\l"
    .string "mountain of his holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_2::
    .string "Beautiful for situation, the joy of\n"
    .string "the whole earth, is mount Zion, on\l"
    .string "the sides of the north, the city of\l"
    .string "the great King.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_3::
    .string "God is known in her palaces for a\n"
    .string "refuge.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_4::
    .string "For, lo, the kings were assembled,\n"
    .string "they passed by together.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_5::
    .string "They saw it, and so they marvelled;\n"
    .string "they were troubled, and hasted away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_6::
    .string "Fear took hold upon them there, and\n"
    .string "pain, as of a woman in travail.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_7::
    .string "Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish\n"
    .string "with an east wind.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_8::
    .string "As we have heard, so have we seen in\n"
    .string "the city of the LORD of hosts, in the\l"
    .string "city of our God: God will establish\l"
    .string "it for ever. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_9::
    .string "We have thought of thy\n"
    .string "lovingkindness, O God, in the midst\l"
    .string "of thy temple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_10::
    .string "According to thy name, O God, so is\n"
    .string "thy praise unto the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth: thy right hand is full of\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_11::
    .string "Let mount Zion rejoice, let the\n"
    .string "daughters of Judah be glad, because\l"
    .string "of thy judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_12::
    .string "Walk about Zion, and go round about\n"
    .string "her: tell the towers thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_13::
    .string "Mark ye well her bulwarks,\n"
    .string "consider her palaces; that ye may\l"
    .string "tell it to the generation\l"
    .string "following.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_48_14::
    .string "For this God is our God for ever and\n"
    .string "ever: he will be our guide even unto\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_1::
    .string "Hear this, all ye people; give\n"
    .string "ear, all ye inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "world:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_2::
    .string "Both low and high, rich and poor,\n"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_3::
    .string "My mouth shall speak of wisdom;\n"
    .string "and the meditation of my heart\l"
    .string "shall be of understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_4::
    .string "I will incline mine ear to a\n"
    .string "parable: I will open my dark\l"
    .string "saying upon the harp.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_5::
    .string "Wherefore should I fear in the days\n"
    .string "of evil, when the iniquity of my\l"
    .string "heels shall compass me about?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_6::
    .string "They that trust in their wealth,\n"
    .string "and boast themselves in the\l"
    .string "multitude of their riches;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_7::
    .string "None of them can by any means redeem\n"
    .string "his brother, nor give to God a ransom\l"
    .string "for him:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_8::
    .string "(For the redemption of their soul\n"
    .string "is precious, and it ceaseth for\l"
    .string "ever:)$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_9::
    .string "That he should still live for\n"
    .string "ever, and not see corruption.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_10::
    .string "For he seeth that wise men die,\n"
    .string "likewise the fool and the brutish\l"
    .string "person perish, and leave their\l"
    .string "wealth to others.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_11::
    .string "Their inward thought is, that their\n"
    .string "houses shall continue for ever, and\l"
    .string "their dwelling places to all\l"
    .string "generations; they call their lands\l"
    .string "after their own names.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_12::
    .string "Nevertheless man being in honour\n"
    .string "abideth not: he is like the beasts\l"
    .string "that perish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_13::
    .string "This their way is their folly: yet\n"
    .string "their posterity approve their\l"
    .string "sayings. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_14::
    .string "Like sheep they are laid in the\n"
    .string "grave; death shall feed on them; and\l"
    .string "the upright shall have dominion\l"
    .string "over them in the morning; and their\l"
    .string "beauty shall consume in the grave\l"
    .string "from their dwelling.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_15::
    .string "But God will redeem my soul from\n"
    .string "the power of the grave: for he\l"
    .string "shall receive me. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_16::
    .string "Be not thou afraid when one is made\n"
    .string "rich, when the glory of his house is\l"
    .string "increased;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_17::
    .string "For when he dieth he shall carry\n"
    .string "nothing away: his glory shall not\l"
    .string "descend after him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_18::
    .string "Though while he lived he blessed\n"
    .string "his soul: and men will praise\l"
    .string "thee, when thou doest well to\l"
    .string "thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_19::
    .string "He shall go to the generation of\n"
    .string "his fathers; they shall never see\l"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_49_20::
    .string "Man that is in honour, and\n"
    .string "understandeth not, is like the\l"
    .string "beasts that perish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_1::
    .string "The mighty God, even the LORD, hath\n"
    .string "spoken, and called the earth from\l"
    .string "the rising of the sun unto the going\l"
    .string "down thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_2::
    .string "Out of Zion, the perfection of\n"
    .string "beauty, God hath shined.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_3::
    .string "Our God shall come, and shall not\n"
    .string "keep silence: a fire shall devour\l"
    .string "before him, and it shall be very\l"
    .string "tempestuous round about him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_4::
    .string "He shall call to the heavens from\n"
    .string "above, and to the earth, that he may\l"
    .string "judge his people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_5::
    .string "Gather my saints together unto me;\n"
    .string "those that have made a covenant with\l"
    .string "me by sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_6::
    .string "And the heavens shall declare his\n"
    .string "righteousness: for God is judge\l"
    .string "himself. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_7::
    .string "Hear, O my people, and I will\n"
    .string "speak; O Israel, and I will\l"
    .string "testify against thee: I am God, even\l"
    .string "thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_8::
    .string "I will not reprove thee for thy\n"
    .string "sacrifices or thy burnt offerings, to\l"
    .string "have been continually before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_9::
    .string "I will take no bullock out of thy\n"
    .string "house, nor he goats out of thy folds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_10::
    .string "For every beast of the forest is\n"
    .string "mine, and the cattle upon a thousand\l"
    .string "hills.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_11::
    .string "I know all the fowls of the\n"
    .string "mountains: and the wild beasts of\l"
    .string "the field are mine.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_12::
    .string "If I were hungry, I would not tell\n"
    .string "thee: for the world is mine, and the\l"
    .string "fulness thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_13::
    .string "Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or\n"
    .string "drink the blood of goats?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_14::
    .string "Offer unto God thanksgiving; and\n"
    .string "pay thy vows unto the most High:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_15::
    .string "And call upon me in the day of\n"
    .string "trouble: I will deliver thee, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt glorify me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_16::
    .string "But unto the wicked God saith, What\n"
    .string "hast thou to do to declare my\l"
    .string "statutes, or that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "take my covenant in thy mouth?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_17::
    .string "Seeing thou hatest instruction, and\n"
    .string "casteth my words behind thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_18::
    .string "When thou sawest a thief, then thou\n"
    .string "consentedst with him, and hast been\l"
    .string "partaker with adulterers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_19::
    .string "Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and\n"
    .string "thy tongue frameth deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_20::
    .string "Thou sittest and speakest against\n"
    .string "thy brother; thou slanderest thine\l"
    .string "own mother’s son.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_21::
    .string "These things hast thou done, and I\n"
    .string "kept silence; thou thoughtest that\l"
    .string "I was altogether such an one as\l"
    .string "thyself: but I will reprove thee,\l"
    .string "and set them in order before thine\l"
    .string "eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_22::
    .string "Now consider this, ye that forget\n"
    .string "God, lest I tear you in pieces, and\l"
    .string "there be none to deliver.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_50_23::
    .string "Whoso offereth praise glorifieth\n"
    .string "me: and to him that ordereth his\l"
    .string "conversation aright will I shew the\l"
    .string "salvation of God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_1::
    .string "Have mercy upon me, O God,\n"
    .string "according to thy lovingkindness:\l"
    .string "according unto the multitude of thy\l"
    .string "tender mercies blot out my\l"
    .string "transgressions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_2::
    .string "Wash me throughly from mine\n"
    .string "iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_3::
    .string "For I acknowledge my\n"
    .string "transgressions: and my sin is ever\l"
    .string "before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_4::
    .string "Against thee, thee only, have I\n"
    .string "sinned, and done this evil in thy\l"
    .string "sight: that thou mightest be\l"
    .string "justified when thou speakest, and be\l"
    .string "clear when thou judgest.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_5::
    .string "Behold, I was shapen in iniquity;\n"
    .string "and in sin did my mother conceive me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_6::
    .string "Behold, thou desirest truth in the\n"
    .string "inward parts: and in the hidden part\l"
    .string "thou shalt make me to know wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_7::
    .string "Purge me with hyssop, and I shall\n"
    .string "be clean: wash me, and I shall be\l"
    .string "whiter than snow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_8::
    .string "Make me to hear joy and gladness;\n"
    .string "that the bones which thou hast broken\l"
    .string "may rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_9::
    .string "Hide thy face from my sins, and blot\n"
    .string "out all mine iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_10::
    .string "Create in me a clean heart, O God;\n"
    .string "and renew a right spirit within me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_11::
    .string "Cast me not away from thy presence;\n"
    .string "and take not thy holy spirit from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_12::
    .string "Restore unto me the joy of thy\n"
    .string "salvation; and uphold me with thy\l"
    .string "free spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_13::
    .string "Then will I teach transgressors\n"
    .string "thy ways; and sinners shall be\l"
    .string "converted unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_14::
    .string "Deliver me from bloodguiltiness,\n"
    .string "O God, thou God of my salvation: and\l"
    .string "my tongue shall sing aloud of thy\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_15::
    .string "O Lord, open thou my lips; and my\n"
    .string "mouth shall shew forth thy praise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_16::
    .string "For thou desirest not sacrifice;\n"
    .string "else would I give it: thou\l"
    .string "delightest not in burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_17::
    .string "The sacrifices of God are a broken\n"
    .string "spirit: a broken and a contrite\l"
    .string "heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_18::
    .string "Do good in thy good pleasure unto\n"
    .string "Zion: build thou the walls of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_51_19::
    .string "Then shalt thou be pleased with\n"
    .string "the sacrifices of righteousness,\l"
    .string "with burnt offering and whole burnt\l"
    .string "offering: then shall they offer\l"
    .string "bullocks upon thine altar.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_1::
    .string "Why boastest thou thyself in\n"
    .string "mischief, O mighty man? the goodness\l"
    .string "of God endureth continually.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_2::
    .string "The tongue deviseth mischiefs; like\n"
    .string "a sharp razor, working deceitfully.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_3::
    .string "Thou lovest evil more than good;\n"
    .string "and lying rather than to speak\l"
    .string "righteousness. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_4::
    .string "Thou lovest all devouring words, O\n"
    .string "thou deceitful tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_5::
    .string "God shall likewise destroy thee\n"
    .string "for ever, he shall take thee away,\l"
    .string "and pluck thee out of thy dwelling\l"
    .string "place, and root thee out of the land\l"
    .string "of the living. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_6::
    .string "The righteous also shall see, and\n"
    .string "fear, and shall laugh at him:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_7::
    .string "Lo, this is the man that made not God\n"
    .string "his strength; but trusted in the\l"
    .string "abundance of his riches, and\l"
    .string "strengthened himself in his\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_8::
    .string "But I am like a green olive tree in\n"
    .string "the house of God: I trust in the mercy\l"
    .string "of God for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_52_9::
    .string "I will praise thee for ever,\n"
    .string "because thou hast done it: and I\l"
    .string "will wait on thy name; for it is\l"
    .string "good before thy saints.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_1::
    .string "The fool hath said in his heart,\n"
    .string "There is no God. Corrupt are they,\l"
    .string "and have done abominable iniquity:\l"
    .string "there is none that doeth good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_2::
    .string "God looked down from heaven upon\n"
    .string "the children of men, to see if there\l"
    .string "were any that did understand, that\l"
    .string "did seek God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_3::
    .string "Every one of them is gone back: they\n"
    .string "are altogether become filthy; there\l"
    .string "is none that doeth good, no, not one.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_4::
    .string "Have the workers of iniquity no\n"
    .string "knowledge? who eat up my people as\l"
    .string "they eat bread: they have not called\l"
    .string "upon God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_5::
    .string "There were they in great fear, where\n"
    .string "no fear was: for God hath scattered\l"
    .string "the bones of him that encampeth\l"
    .string "against thee: thou hast put them to\l"
    .string "shame, because God hath despised\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_53_6::
    .string "Oh that the salvation of Israel\n"
    .string "were come out of Zion! When God\l"
    .string "bringeth back the captivity of his\l"
    .string "people, Jacob shall rejoice, and\l"
    .string "Israel shall be glad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_1::
    .string "Save me, O God, by thy name, and\n"
    .string "judge me by thy strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_2::
    .string "Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to\n"
    .string "the words of my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_3::
    .string "For strangers are risen up against\n"
    .string "me, and oppressors seek after my\l"
    .string "soul: they have not set God before\l"
    .string "them. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_4::
    .string "Behold, God is mine helper: the\n"
    .string "Lord is with them that uphold my\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_5::
    .string "He shall reward evil unto mine\n"
    .string "enemies: cut them off in thy truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_6::
    .string "I will freely sacrifice unto thee:\n"
    .string "I will praise thy name, O LORD; for\l"
    .string "it is good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_54_7::
    .string "For he hath delivered me out of\n"
    .string "all trouble: and mine eye hath seen\l"
    .string "his desire upon mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_1::
    .string "Give ear to my prayer, O God; and\n"
    .string "hide not thyself from my\l"
    .string "supplication.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_2::
    .string "Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn\n"
    .string "in my complaint, and make a noise;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_3::
    .string "Because of the voice of the enemy,\n"
    .string "because of the oppression of the\l"
    .string "wicked: for they cast iniquity upon\l"
    .string "me, and in wrath they hate me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_4::
    .string "My heart is sore pained within me:\n"
    .string "and the terrors of death are fallen\l"
    .string "upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_5::
    .string "Fearfulness and trembling are come\n"
    .string "upon me, and horror hath\l"
    .string "overwhelmed me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_6::
    .string "And I said, Oh that I had wings like\n"
    .string "a dove! for then would I fly away,\l"
    .string "and be at rest.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_7::
    .string "Lo, then would I wander far off, and\n"
    .string "remain in the wilderness. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_8::
    .string "I would hasten my escape from the\n"
    .string "windy storm and tempest.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_9::
    .string "Destroy, O Lord, and divide their\n"
    .string "tongues: for I have seen violence\l"
    .string "and strife in the city.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_10::
    .string "Day and night they go about it upon\n"
    .string "the walls thereof: mischief also\l"
    .string "and sorrow are in the midst of it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_11::
    .string "Wickedness is in the midst thereof:\n"
    .string "deceit and guile depart not from\l"
    .string "her streets.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_12::
    .string "For it was not an enemy that\n"
    .string "reproached me; then I could have\l"
    .string "borne it: neither was it he that\l"
    .string "hated me that did magnify himself\l"
    .string "against me; then I would have hid\l"
    .string "myself from him:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_13::
    .string "But it was thou, a man mine equal,\n"
    .string "my guide, and mine acquaintance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_14::
    .string "We took sweet counsel together, and\n"
    .string "walked unto the house of God in\l"
    .string "company.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_15::
    .string "Let death seize upon them, and let\n"
    .string "them go down quick into hell: for\l"
    .string "wickedness is in their dwellings,\l"
    .string "and among them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_16::
    .string "As for me, I will call upon God;\n"
    .string "and the LORD shall save me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_17::
    .string "Evening, and morning, and at noon,\n"
    .string "will I pray, and cry aloud: and he\l"
    .string "shall hear my voice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_18::
    .string "He hath delivered my soul in peace\n"
    .string "from the battle that was against me:\l"
    .string "for there were many with me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_19::
    .string "God shall hear, and afflict them,\n"
    .string "even he that abideth of old. Selah.\l"
    .string "Because they have no changes,\l"
    .string "therefore they fear not God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_20::
    .string "He hath put forth his hands against\n"
    .string "such as be at peace with him: he hath\l"
    .string "broken his covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_21::
    .string "The words of his mouth were smoother\n"
    .string "than butter, but war was in his\l"
    .string "heart: his words were softer than\l"
    .string "oil, yet were they drawn swords.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_22::
    .string "Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and\n"
    .string "he shall sustain thee: he shall\l"
    .string "never suffer the righteous to be\l"
    .string "moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_55_23::
    .string "But thou, O God, shalt bring them\n"
    .string "down into the pit of destruction:\l"
    .string "bloody and deceitful men shall not\l"
    .string "live out half their days; but I\l"
    .string "will trust in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_1::
    .string "Be merciful unto me, O God: for man\n"
    .string "would swallow me up; he fighting\l"
    .string "daily oppresseth me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_2::
    .string "Mine enemies would daily swallow\n"
    .string "me up: for they be many that fight\l"
    .string "against me, O thou most High.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_3::
    .string "What time I am afraid, I will trust\n"
    .string "in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_4::
    .string "In God I will praise his word, in\n"
    .string "God I have put my trust; I will not\l"
    .string "fear what flesh can do unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_5::
    .string "Every day they wrest my words: all\n"
    .string "their thoughts are against me for\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_6::
    .string "They gather themselves together,\n"
    .string "they hide themselves, they mark my\l"
    .string "steps, when they wait for my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_7::
    .string "Shall they escape by iniquity? in\n"
    .string "thine anger cast down the people, O\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_8::
    .string "Thou tellest my wanderings: put\n"
    .string "thou my tears into thy bottle: are\l"
    .string "they not in thy book?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_9::
    .string "When I cry unto thee, then shall\n"
    .string "mine enemies turn back: this I know;\l"
    .string "for God is for me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_10::
    .string "In God will I praise his word: in\n"
    .string "the LORD will I praise his word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_11::
    .string "In God have I put my trust: I will\n"
    .string "not be afraid what man can do unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_12::
    .string "Thy vows are upon me, O God: I will\n"
    .string "render praises unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_56_13::
    .string "For thou hast delivered my soul\n"
    .string "from death: wilt not thou deliver my\l"
    .string "feet from falling, that I may walk\l"
    .string "before God in the light of the\l"
    .string "living?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_1::
    .string "Be merciful unto me, O God, be\n"
    .string "merciful unto me: for my soul\l"
    .string "trusteth in thee: yea, in the shadow\l"
    .string "of thy wings will I make my refuge,\l"
    .string "until these calamities be overpast.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_2::
    .string "I will cry unto God most high; unto\n"
    .string "God that performeth all things for\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_3::
    .string "He shall send from heaven, and save\n"
    .string "me from the reproach of him that\l"
    .string "would swallow me up. Selah. God\l"
    .string "shall send forth his mercy and his\l"
    .string "truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_4::
    .string "My soul is among lions: and I lie\n"
    .string "even among them that are set on fire,\l"
    .string "even the sons of men, whose teeth are\l"
    .string "spears and arrows, and their tongue\l"
    .string "a sharp sword.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_5::
    .string "Be thou exalted, O God, above the\n"
    .string "heavens; let thy glory be above\l"
    .string "all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_6::
    .string "They have prepared a net for my\n"
    .string "steps; my soul is bowed down: they\l"
    .string "have digged a pit before me, into the\l"
    .string "midst whereof they are fallen\l"
    .string "themselves. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_7::
    .string "My heart is fixed, O God, my heart is\n"
    .string "fixed: I will sing and give praise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_8::
    .string "Awake up, my glory; awake,\n"
    .string "psaltery and harp: I myself will\l"
    .string "awake early.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_9::
    .string "I will praise thee, O Lord, among\n"
    .string "the people: I will sing unto thee\l"
    .string "among the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_10::
    .string "For thy mercy is great unto the\n"
    .string "heavens, and thy truth unto the\l"
    .string "clouds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_57_11::
    .string "Be thou exalted, O God, above the\n"
    .string "heavens: let thy glory be above\l"
    .string "all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_1::
    .string "Do ye indeed speak righteousness, O\n"
    .string "congregation? do ye judge\l"
    .string "uprightly, O ye sons of men?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_2::
    .string "Yea, in heart ye work wickedness; ye\n"
    .string "weigh the violence of your hands in\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_3::
    .string "The wicked are estranged from the\n"
    .string "womb: they go astray as soon as they\l"
    .string "be born, speaking lies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_4::
    .string "Their poison is like the poison of\n"
    .string "a serpent: they are like the deaf\l"
    .string "adder that stoppeth her ear;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_5::
    .string "Which will not hearken to the\n"
    .string "voice of charmers, charming never so\l"
    .string "wisely.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_6::
    .string "Break their teeth, O God, in their\n"
    .string "mouth: break out the great teeth of\l"
    .string "the young lions, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_7::
    .string "Let them melt away as waters which\n"
    .string "run continually: when he bendeth\l"
    .string "his bow to shoot his arrows, let them\l"
    .string "be as cut in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_8::
    .string "As a snail which melteth, let\n"
    .string "every one of them pass away: like\l"
    .string "the untimely birth of a woman, that\l"
    .string "they may not see the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_9::
    .string "Before your pots can feel the\n"
    .string "thorns, he shall take them away as\l"
    .string "with a whirlwind, both living, and\l"
    .string "in his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_10::
    .string "The righteous shall rejoice when\n"
    .string "he seeth the vengeance: he shall\l"
    .string "wash his feet in the blood of the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_58_11::
    .string "So that a man shall say, Verily\n"
    .string "there is a reward for the righteous:\l"
    .string "verily he is a God that judgeth in\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_1::
    .string "Deliver me from mine enemies, O my\n"
    .string "God: defend me from them that rise up\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_2::
    .string "Deliver me from the workers of\n"
    .string "iniquity, and save me from bloody\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_3::
    .string "For, lo, they lie in wait for my\n"
    .string "soul: the mighty are gathered\l"
    .string "against me; not for my transgression,\l"
    .string "nor for my sin, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_4::
    .string "They run and prepare themselves\n"
    .string "without my fault: awake to help me,\l"
    .string "and behold.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_5::
    .string "Thou therefore, O LORD God of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel, awake to visit\l"
    .string "all the heathen: be not merciful to\l"
    .string "any wicked transgressors. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_6::
    .string "They return at evening: they make a\n"
    .string "noise like a dog, and go round about\l"
    .string "the city.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_7::
    .string "Behold, they belch out with their\n"
    .string "mouth: swords are in their lips: for\l"
    .string "who, say they, doth hear?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_8::
    .string "But thou, O LORD, shalt laugh at\n"
    .string "them; thou shalt have all the\l"
    .string "heathen in derision.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_9::
    .string "Because of his strength will I\n"
    .string "wait upon thee: for God is my\l"
    .string "defence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_10::
    .string "The God of my mercy shall prevent\n"
    .string "me: God shall let me see my desire\l"
    .string "upon mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_11::
    .string "Slay them not, lest my people\n"
    .string "forget: scatter them by thy power;\l"
    .string "and bring them down, O Lord our\l"
    .string "shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_12::
    .string "For the sin of their mouth and the\n"
    .string "words of their lips let them even\l"
    .string "be taken in their pride: and for\l"
    .string "cursing and lying which they speak.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_13::
    .string "Consume them in wrath, consume them,\n"
    .string "that they may not be: and let them\l"
    .string "know that God ruleth in Jacob unto\l"
    .string "the ends of the earth. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_14::
    .string "And at evening let them return; and\n"
    .string "let them make a noise like a dog, and\l"
    .string "go round about the city.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_15::
    .string "Let them wander up and down for\n"
    .string "meat, and grudge if they be not\l"
    .string "satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_16::
    .string "But I will sing of thy power; yea,\n"
    .string "I will sing aloud of thy mercy in\l"
    .string "the morning: for thou hast been my\l"
    .string "defence and refuge in the day of my\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_59_17::
    .string "Unto thee, O my strength, will I\n"
    .string "sing: for God is my defence, and the\l"
    .string "God of my mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_1::
    .string "O God, thou hast cast us off, thou\n"
    .string "hast scattered us, thou hast been\l"
    .string "displeased; O turn thyself to us\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_2::
    .string "Thou hast made the earth to\n"
    .string "tremble; thou hast broken it: heal\l"
    .string "the breaches thereof; for it shaketh.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_3::
    .string "Thou hast shewed thy people hard\n"
    .string "things: thou hast made us to drink\l"
    .string "the wine of astonishment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_4::
    .string "Thou hast given a banner to them\n"
    .string "that fear thee, that it may be\l"
    .string "displayed because of the truth.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_5::
    .string "That thy beloved may be delivered;\n"
    .string "save with thy right hand, and hear me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_6::
    .string "God hath spoken in his holiness; I\n"
    .string "will rejoice, I will divide\l"
    .string "Shechem, and mete out the valley of\l"
    .string "Succoth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_7::
    .string "Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is\n"
    .string "mine; Ephraim also is the strength\l"
    .string "of mine head; Judah is my lawgiver;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_8::
    .string "Moab is my washpot; over Edom will\n"
    .string "I cast out my shoe: Philistia,\l"
    .string "triumph thou because of me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_9::
    .string "Who will bring me into the strong\n"
    .string "city? who will lead me into Edom?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_10::
    .string "Wilt not thou, O God, which hadst\n"
    .string "cast us off? and thou, O God, which\l"
    .string "didst not go out with our armies?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_11::
    .string "Give us help from trouble: for\n"
    .string "vain is the help of man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_60_12::
    .string "Through God we shall do\n"
    .string "valiantly: for he it is that shall\l"
    .string "tread down our enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_1::
    .string "Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my\n"
    .string "prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_2::
    .string "From the end of the earth will I\n"
    .string "cry unto thee, when my heart is\l"
    .string "overwhelmed: lead me to the rock\l"
    .string "that is higher than I.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_3::
    .string "For thou hast been a shelter for me,\n"
    .string "and a strong tower from the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_4::
    .string "I will abide in thy tabernacle for\n"
    .string "ever: I will trust in the covert of\l"
    .string "thy wings. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_5::
    .string "For thou, O God, hast heard my vows:\n"
    .string "thou hast given me the heritage of\l"
    .string "those that fear thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_6::
    .string "Thou wilt prolong the king’s\n"
    .string "life: and his years as many\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_7::
    .string "He shall abide before God for ever:\n"
    .string "O prepare mercy and truth, which may\l"
    .string "preserve him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_61_8::
    .string "So will I sing praise unto thy\n"
    .string "name for ever, that I may daily\l"
    .string "perform my vows.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_1::
    .string "Truly my soul waiteth upon God:\n"
    .string "from him cometh my salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_2::
    .string "He only is my rock and my\n"
    .string "salvation; he is my defence; I\l"
    .string "shall not be greatly moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_3::
    .string "How long will ye imagine mischief\n"
    .string "against a man? ye shall be slain\l"
    .string "all of you: as a bowing wall\l"
    .string "shall ye be, and as a tottering\l"
    .string "fence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_4::
    .string "They only consult to cast him down\n"
    .string "from his excellency: they delight\l"
    .string "in lies: they bless with their\l"
    .string "mouth, but they curse inwardly.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_5::
    .string "My soul, wait thou only upon God;\n"
    .string "for my expectation is from him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_6::
    .string "He only is my rock and my\n"
    .string "salvation: he is my defence; I\l"
    .string "shall not be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_7::
    .string "In God is my salvation and my\n"
    .string "glory: the rock of my strength, and\l"
    .string "my refuge, is in God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_8::
    .string "Trust in him at all times; ye\n"
    .string "people, pour out your heart before\l"
    .string "him: God is a refuge for us. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_9::
    .string "Surely men of low degree are\n"
    .string "vanity, and men of high degree are a\l"
    .string "lie: to be laid in the balance, they\l"
    .string "are altogether lighter than vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_10::
    .string "Trust not in oppression, and\n"
    .string "become not vain in robbery: if riches\l"
    .string "increase, set not your heart upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_11::
    .string "God hath spoken once; twice have I\n"
    .string "heard this; that power belongeth\l"
    .string "unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_62_12::
    .string "Also unto thee, O Lord, belongeth\n"
    .string "mercy: for thou renderest to every\l"
    .string "man according to his work.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_1::
    .string "O God, thou art my God; early will\n"
    .string "I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for\l"
    .string "thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a\l"
    .string "dry and thirsty land, where no water\l"
    .string "is;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_2::
    .string "To see thy power and thy glory, so\n"
    .string "as I have seen thee in the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_3::
    .string "Because thy lovingkindness is\n"
    .string "better than life, my lips shall\l"
    .string "praise thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_4::
    .string "Thus will I bless thee while I\n"
    .string "live: I will lift up my hands in\l"
    .string "thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_5::
    .string "My soul shall be satisfied as with\n"
    .string "marrow and fatness; and my mouth\l"
    .string "shall praise thee with joyful\l"
    .string "lips:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_6::
    .string "When I remember thee upon my bed,\n"
    .string "and meditate on thee in the night\l"
    .string "watches.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_7::
    .string "Because thou hast been my help,\n"
    .string "therefore in the shadow of thy wings\l"
    .string "will I rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_8::
    .string "My soul followeth hard after thee:\n"
    .string "thy right hand upholdeth me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_9::
    .string "But those that seek my soul, to\n"
    .string "destroy it, shall go into the lower\l"
    .string "parts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_10::
    .string "They shall fall by the sword:\n"
    .string "they shall be a portion for foxes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_63_11::
    .string "But the king shall rejoice in God;\n"
    .string "every one that sweareth by him\l"
    .string "shall glory: but the mouth of them\l"
    .string "that speak lies shall be stopped.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_1::
    .string "Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer:\n"
    .string "preserve my life from fear of the\l"
    .string "enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_2::
    .string "Hide me from the secret counsel of\n"
    .string "the wicked; from the insurrection of\l"
    .string "the workers of iniquity:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_3::
    .string "Who whet their tongue like a sword,\n"
    .string "and bend their bows to shoot their\l"
    .string "arrows, even bitter words:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_4::
    .string "That they may shoot in secret at the\n"
    .string "perfect: suddenly do they shoot at\l"
    .string "him, and fear not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_5::
    .string "They encourage themselves in an\n"
    .string "evil matter: they commune of laying\l"
    .string "snares privily; they say, Who\l"
    .string "shall see them?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_6::
    .string "They search out iniquities; they\n"
    .string "accomplish a diligent search: both\l"
    .string "the inward thought of every one of\l"
    .string "them, and the heart, is deep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_7::
    .string "But God shall shoot at them with an\n"
    .string "arrow; suddenly shall they be\l"
    .string "wounded.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_8::
    .string "So they shall make their own\n"
    .string "tongue to fall upon themselves:\l"
    .string "all that see them shall flee away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_9::
    .string "And all men shall fear, and\n"
    .string "shall declare the work of God; for\l"
    .string "they shall wisely consider of his\l"
    .string "doing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_64_10::
    .string "The righteous shall be glad in the\n"
    .string "LORD, and shall trust in him; and\l"
    .string "all the upright in heart shall\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_1::
    .string "Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in\n"
    .string "Sion: and unto thee shall the vow be\l"
    .string "performed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_2::
    .string "O thou that hearest prayer, unto\n"
    .string "thee shall all flesh come.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_3::
    .string "Iniquities prevail against me: as\n"
    .string "for our transgressions, thou shalt\l"
    .string "purge them away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_4::
    .string "Blessed is the man whom thou\n"
    .string "choosest, and causest to approach\l"
    .string "unto thee, that he may dwell in thy\l"
    .string "courts: we shall be satisfied with\l"
    .string "the goodness of thy house, even of\l"
    .string "thy holy temple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_5::
    .string "By terrible things in\n"
    .string "righteousness wilt thou answer us, O\l"
    .string "God of our salvation; who art the\l"
    .string "confidence of all the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth, and of them that are afar off\l"
    .string "upon the sea:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_6::
    .string "Which by his strength setteth fast\n"
    .string "the mountains; being girded with\l"
    .string "power:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_7::
    .string "Which stilleth the noise of the\n"
    .string "seas, the noise of their waves, and\l"
    .string "the tumult of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_8::
    .string "They also that dwell in the\n"
    .string "uttermost parts are afraid at thy\l"
    .string "tokens: thou makest the outgoings of\l"
    .string "the morning and evening to rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_9::
    .string "Thou visitest the earth, and\n"
    .string "waterest it: thou greatly enrichest\l"
    .string "it with the river of God, which is\l"
    .string "full of water: thou preparest them\l"
    .string "corn, when thou hast so provided for\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_10::
    .string "Thou waterest the ridges thereof\n"
    .string "abundantly: thou settlest the\l"
    .string "furrows thereof: thou makest it soft\l"
    .string "with showers: thou blessest the\l"
    .string "springing thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_11::
    .string "Thou crownest the year with thy\n"
    .string "goodness; and thy paths drop\l"
    .string "fatness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_12::
    .string "They drop upon the pastures of the\n"
    .string "wilderness: and the little hills\l"
    .string "rejoice on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_65_13::
    .string "The pastures are clothed with\n"
    .string "flocks; the valleys also are\l"
    .string "covered over with corn; they shout\l"
    .string "for joy, they also sing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_1::
    .string "Make a joyful noise unto God, all\n"
    .string "ye lands:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_2::
    .string "Sing forth the honour of his name:\n"
    .string "make his praise glorious.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_3::
    .string "Say unto God, How terrible art thou\n"
    .string "in thy works! through the greatness\l"
    .string "of thy power shall thine enemies\l"
    .string "submit themselves unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_4::
    .string "All the earth shall worship\n"
    .string "thee, and shall sing unto thee; they\l"
    .string "shall sing to thy name. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_5::
    .string "Come and see the works of God: he is\n"
    .string "terrible in his doing toward the\l"
    .string "children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_6::
    .string "He turned the sea into dry land:\n"
    .string "they went through the flood on foot:\l"
    .string "there did we rejoice in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_7::
    .string "He ruleth by his power for ever;\n"
    .string "his eyes behold the nations: let not\l"
    .string "the rebellious exalt themselves.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_8::
    .string "O bless our God, ye people, and\n"
    .string "make the voice of his praise to be\l"
    .string "heard:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_9::
    .string "Which holdeth our soul in life,\n"
    .string "and suffereth not our feet to be\l"
    .string "moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_10::
    .string "For thou, O God, hast proved us:\n"
    .string "thou hast tried us, as silver is\l"
    .string "tried.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_11::
    .string "Thou broughtest us into the net;\n"
    .string "thou laidst affliction upon our\l"
    .string "loins.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_12::
    .string "Thou hast caused men to ride over\n"
    .string "our heads; we went through fire and\l"
    .string "through water: but thou broughtest us\l"
    .string "out into a wealthy place.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_13::
    .string "I will go into thy house with burnt\n"
    .string "offerings: I will pay thee my vows,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_14::
    .string "Which my lips have uttered, and my\n"
    .string "mouth hath spoken, when I was in\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_15::
    .string "I will offer unto thee burnt\n"
    .string "sacrifices of fatlings, with the\l"
    .string "incense of rams; I will offer\l"
    .string "bullocks with goats. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_16::
    .string "Come and hear, all ye that fear\n"
    .string "God, and I will declare what he\l"
    .string "hath done for my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_17::
    .string "I cried unto him with my mouth, and\n"
    .string "he was extolled with my tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_18::
    .string "If I regard iniquity in my heart,\n"
    .string "the Lord will not hear me:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_19::
    .string "But verily God hath heard me; he\n"
    .string "hath attended to the voice of my\l"
    .string "prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_66_20::
    .string "Blessed be God, which hath not\n"
    .string "turned away my prayer, nor his mercy\l"
    .string "from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_1::
    .string "God be merciful unto us, and bless\n"
    .string "us; and cause his face to shine upon\l"
    .string "us; Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_2::
    .string "That thy way may be known upon\n"
    .string "earth, thy saving health among all\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_3::
    .string "Let the people praise thee, O\n"
    .string "God; let all the people praise\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_4::
    .string "O let the nations be glad and sing\n"
    .string "for joy: for thou shalt judge the\l"
    .string "people righteously, and govern the\l"
    .string "nations upon earth. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_5::
    .string "Let the people praise thee, O\n"
    .string "God; let all the people praise\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_6::
    .string "Then shall the earth yield her\n"
    .string "increase; and God, even our own God,\l"
    .string "shall bless us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_67_7::
    .string "God shall bless us; and all the\n"
    .string "ends of the earth shall fear him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_1::
    .string "Let God arise, let his enemies be\n"
    .string "scattered: let them also that hate\l"
    .string "him flee before him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_2::
    .string "As smoke is driven away, so drive\n"
    .string "them away: as wax melteth before the\l"
    .string "fire, so let the wicked perish at\l"
    .string "the presence of God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_3::
    .string "But let the righteous be glad; let\n"
    .string "them rejoice before God: yea, let\l"
    .string "them exceedingly rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_4::
    .string "Sing unto God, sing praises to his\n"
    .string "name: extol him that rideth upon the\l"
    .string "heavens by his name JAH, and rejoice\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_5::
    .string "A father of the fatherless, and a\n"
    .string "judge of the widows, is God in his\l"
    .string "holy habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_6::
    .string "God setteth the solitary in\n"
    .string "families: he bringeth out those\l"
    .string "which are bound with chains: but the\l"
    .string "rebellious dwell in a dry land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_7::
    .string "O God, when thou wentest forth\n"
    .string "before thy people, when thou didst\l"
    .string "march through the wilderness; Selah:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_8::
    .string "The earth shook, the heavens also\n"
    .string "dropped at the presence of God:\l"
    .string "even Sinai itself was moved at the\l"
    .string "presence of God, the God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_9::
    .string "Thou, O God, didst send a\n"
    .string "plentiful rain, whereby thou didst\l"
    .string "confirm thine inheritance, when it\l"
    .string "was weary.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_10::
    .string "Thy congregation hath dwelt\n"
    .string "therein: thou, O God, hast prepared\l"
    .string "of thy goodness for the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_11::
    .string "The Lord gave the word: great was\n"
    .string "the company of those that\l"
    .string "published it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_12::
    .string "Kings of armies did flee apace: and\n"
    .string "she that tarried at home divided the\l"
    .string "spoil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_13::
    .string "Though ye have lien among the pots,\n"
    .string "yet shall ye be as the wings of a\l"
    .string "dove covered with silver, and her\l"
    .string "feathers with yellow gold.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_14::
    .string "When the Almighty scattered kings\n"
    .string "in it, it was white as snow in Salmon.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_15::
    .string "The hill of God is as the hill of\n"
    .string "Bashan; an high hill as the hill of\l"
    .string "Bashan.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_16::
    .string "Why leap ye, ye high hills? this\n"
    .string "is the hill which God desireth to\l"
    .string "dwell in; yea, the LORD will\l"
    .string "dwell in it for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_17::
    .string "The chariots of God are twenty\n"
    .string "thousand, even thousands of angels:\l"
    .string "the Lord is among them, as in Sinai,\l"
    .string "in the holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_18::
    .string "Thou hast ascended on high, thou\n"
    .string "hast led captivity captive: thou\l"
    .string "hast received gifts for men; yea, for\l"
    .string "the rebellious also, that the LORD\l"
    .string "God might dwell among them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_19::
    .string "Blessed be the Lord, who daily\n"
    .string "loadeth us with benefits, even the\l"
    .string "God of our salvation. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_20::
    .string "He that is our God is the God of\n"
    .string "salvation; and unto GOD the Lord\l"
    .string "belong the issues from death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_21::
    .string "But God shall wound the head of his\n"
    .string "enemies, and the hairy scalp of such\l"
    .string "an one as goeth on still in his\l"
    .string "trespasses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_22::
    .string "The Lord said, I will bring again\n"
    .string "from Bashan, I will bring my\l"
    .string "people again from the depths of the\l"
    .string "sea:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_23::
    .string "That thy foot may be dipped in the\n"
    .string "blood of thine enemies, and the\l"
    .string "tongue of thy dogs in the same.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_24::
    .string "They have seen thy goings, O God;\n"
    .string "even the goings of my God, my King, in\l"
    .string "the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_25::
    .string "The singers went before, the\n"
    .string "players on instruments followed\l"
    .string "after; among them were the damsels\l"
    .string "playing with timbrels.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_26::
    .string "Bless ye God in the congregations,\n"
    .string "even the Lord, from the fountain of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_27::
    .string "There is little Benjamin with\n"
    .string "their ruler, the princes of Judah\l"
    .string "and their council, the princes of\l"
    .string "Zebulun, and the princes of\l"
    .string "Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_28::
    .string "Thy God hath commanded thy strength:\n"
    .string "strengthen, O God, that which thou\l"
    .string "hast wrought for us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_29::
    .string "Because of thy temple at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem shall kings bring\l"
    .string "presents unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_30::
    .string "Rebuke the company of spearmen,\n"
    .string "the multitude of the bulls, with\l"
    .string "the calves of the people, till\l"
    .string "every one submit himself with\l"
    .string "pieces of silver: scatter thou the\l"
    .string "people that delight in war.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_31::
    .string "Princes shall come out of Egypt;\n"
    .string "Ethiopia shall soon stretch out\l"
    .string "her hands unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_32::
    .string "Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the\n"
    .string "earth; O sing praises unto the Lord;\l"
    .string "Selah:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_33::
    .string "To him that rideth upon the heavens\n"
    .string "of heavens, which were of old; lo,\l"
    .string "he doth send out his voice, and that a\l"
    .string "mighty voice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_34::
    .string "Ascribe ye strength unto God: his\n"
    .string "excellency is over Israel, and his\l"
    .string "strength is in the clouds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_68_35::
    .string "O God, thou art terrible out of thy\n"
    .string "holy places: the God of Israel is\l"
    .string "he that giveth strength and power\l"
    .string "unto his people. Blessed be God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_1::
    .string "Save me, O God; for the waters are\n"
    .string "come in unto my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_2::
    .string "I sink in deep mire, where there is\n"
    .string "no standing: I am come into deep\l"
    .string "waters, where the floods overflow\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_3::
    .string "I am weary of my crying: my throat is\n"
    .string "dried: mine eyes fail while I wait\l"
    .string "for my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_4::
    .string "They that hate me without a cause\n"
    .string "are more than the hairs of mine head:\l"
    .string "they that would destroy me, being\l"
    .string "mine enemies wrongfully, are\l"
    .string "mighty: then I restored that which I\l"
    .string "took not away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_5::
    .string "O God, thou knowest my foolishness;\n"
    .string "and my sins are not hid from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_6::
    .string "Let not them that wait on thee, O\n"
    .string "Lord GOD of hosts, be ashamed for my\l"
    .string "sake: let not those that seek thee be\l"
    .string "confounded for my sake, O God of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_7::
    .string "Because for thy sake I have borne\n"
    .string "reproach; shame hath covered my face.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_8::
    .string "I am become a stranger unto my\n"
    .string "brethren, and an alien unto my\l"
    .string "mother’s children.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_9::
    .string "For the zeal of thine house hath\n"
    .string "eaten me up; and the reproaches of\l"
    .string "them that reproached thee are\l"
    .string "fallen upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_10::
    .string "When I wept, and chastened my soul\n"
    .string "with fasting, that was to my\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_11::
    .string "I made sackcloth also my garment;\n"
    .string "and I became a proverb to them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_12::
    .string "They that sit in the gate speak\n"
    .string "against me; and I was the song of the\l"
    .string "drunkards.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_13::
    .string "But as for me, my prayer is unto\n"
    .string "thee, O LORD, in an acceptable time:\l"
    .string "O God, in the multitude of thy mercy\l"
    .string "hear me, in the truth of thy\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_14::
    .string "Deliver me out of the mire, and let\n"
    .string "me not sink: let me be delivered\l"
    .string "from them that hate me, and out of the\l"
    .string "deep waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_15::
    .string "Let not the waterflood overflow\n"
    .string "me, neither let the deep swallow\l"
    .string "me up, and let not the pit shut her\l"
    .string "mouth upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_16::
    .string "Hear me, O LORD; for thy\n"
    .string "lovingkindness is good: turn unto me\l"
    .string "according to the multitude of thy\l"
    .string "tender mercies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_17::
    .string "And hide not thy face from thy\n"
    .string "servant; for I am in trouble: hear me\l"
    .string "speedily.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_18::
    .string "Draw nigh unto my soul, and redeem\n"
    .string "it: deliver me because of mine\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_19::
    .string "Thou hast known my reproach, and my\n"
    .string "shame, and my dishonour: mine\l"
    .string "adversaries are all before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_20::
    .string "Reproach hath broken my heart; and\n"
    .string "I am full of heaviness: and I\l"
    .string "looked for some to take pity, but\l"
    .string "there was none; and for comforters,\l"
    .string "but I found none.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_21::
    .string "They gave me also gall for my\n"
    .string "meat; and in my thirst they gave me\l"
    .string "vinegar to drink.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_22::
    .string "Let their table become a snare\n"
    .string "before them: and that which should\l"
    .string "have been for their welfare, let it\l"
    .string "become a trap.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_23::
    .string "Let their eyes be darkened, that\n"
    .string "they see not; and make their loins\l"
    .string "continually to shake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_24::
    .string "Pour out thine indignation upon\n"
    .string "them, and let thy wrathful anger\l"
    .string "take hold of them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_25::
    .string "Let their habitation be desolate;\n"
    .string "and let none dwell in their tents.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_26::
    .string "For they persecute him whom thou\n"
    .string "hast smitten; and they talk to the\l"
    .string "grief of those whom thou hast wounded.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_27::
    .string "Add iniquity unto their iniquity:\n"
    .string "and let them not come into thy\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_28::
    .string "Let them be blotted out of the book\n"
    .string "of the living, and not be written\l"
    .string "with the righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_29::
    .string "But I am poor and sorrowful: let\n"
    .string "thy salvation, O God, set me up on\l"
    .string "high.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_30::
    .string "I will praise the name of God with\n"
    .string "a song, and will magnify him with\l"
    .string "thanksgiving.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_31::
    .string "This also shall please the LORD\n"
    .string "better than an ox or bullock that\l"
    .string "hath horns and hoofs.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_32::
    .string "The humble shall see this, and be\n"
    .string "glad: and your heart shall live\l"
    .string "that seek God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_33::
    .string "For the LORD heareth the poor, and\n"
    .string "despiseth not his prisoners.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_34::
    .string "Let the heaven and earth praise\n"
    .string "him, the seas, and every thing that\l"
    .string "moveth therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_35::
    .string "For God will save Zion, and will\n"
    .string "build the cities of Judah: that they\l"
    .string "may dwell there, and have it in\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_69_36::
    .string "The seed also of his servants\n"
    .string "shall inherit it: and they that\l"
    .string "love his name shall dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_70_1::
    .string "Make haste, O God, to deliver me;\n"
    .string "make haste to help me, O Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_70_2::
    .string "Let them be ashamed and confounded\n"
    .string "that seek after my soul: let them be\l"
    .string "turned backward, and put to\l"
    .string "confusion, that desire my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_70_3::
    .string "Let them be turned back for a reward\n"
    .string "of their shame that say, Aha, aha.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_70_4::
    .string "Let all those that seek thee\n"
    .string "rejoice and be glad in thee: and let\l"
    .string "such as love thy salvation say\l"
    .string "continually, Let God be magnified.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_70_5::
    .string "But I am poor and needy: make haste\n"
    .string "unto me, O God: thou art my help and\l"
    .string "my deliverer; O LORD, make no\l"
    .string "tarrying.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_1::
    .string "In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust:\n"
    .string "let me never be put to confusion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_2::
    .string "Deliver me in thy righteousness,\n"
    .string "and cause me to escape: incline\l"
    .string "thine ear unto me, and save me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_3::
    .string "Be thou my strong habitation,\n"
    .string "whereunto I may continually resort:\l"
    .string "thou hast given commandment to save\l"
    .string "me; for thou art my rock and my\l"
    .string "fortress.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_4::
    .string "Deliver me, O my God, out of the\n"
    .string "hand of the wicked, out of the hand of\l"
    .string "the unrighteous and cruel man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_5::
    .string "For thou art my hope, O Lord GOD:\n"
    .string "thou art my trust from my youth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_6::
    .string "By thee have I been holden up from\n"
    .string "the womb: thou art he that took me out\l"
    .string "of my mother’s bowels: my praise\l"
    .string "shall be continually of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_7::
    .string "I am as a wonder unto many; but thou\n"
    .string "art my strong refuge.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_8::
    .string "Let my mouth be filled with thy\n"
    .string "praise and with thy honour all the\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_9::
    .string "Cast me not off in the time of old\n"
    .string "age; forsake me not when my strength\l"
    .string "faileth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_10::
    .string "For mine enemies speak against me;\n"
    .string "and they that lay wait for my soul\l"
    .string "take counsel together,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_11::
    .string "Saying, God hath forsaken him:\n"
    .string "persecute and take him; for there is\l"
    .string "none to deliver him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_12::
    .string "O God, be not far from me: O my God,\n"
    .string "make haste for my help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_13::
    .string "Let them be confounded and consumed\n"
    .string "that are adversaries to my soul; let\l"
    .string "them be covered with reproach and\l"
    .string "dishonour that seek my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_14::
    .string "But I will hope continually, and\n"
    .string "will yet praise thee more and more.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_15::
    .string "My mouth shall shew forth thy\n"
    .string "righteousness and thy salvation\l"
    .string "all the day; for I know not the\l"
    .string "numbers thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_16::
    .string "I will go in the strength of the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD: I will make mention of thy\l"
    .string "righteousness, even of thine only.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_17::
    .string "O God, thou hast taught me from my\n"
    .string "youth: and hitherto have I declared\l"
    .string "thy wondrous works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_18::
    .string "Now also when I am old and\n"
    .string "greyheaded, O God, forsake me not;\l"
    .string "until I have shewed thy strength\l"
    .string "unto this generation, and thy power\l"
    .string "to every one that is to come.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_19::
    .string "Thy righteousness also, O God, is\n"
    .string "very high, who hast done great\l"
    .string "things: O God, who is like unto thee!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_20::
    .string "Thou, which hast shewed me great and\n"
    .string "sore troubles, shalt quicken me\l"
    .string "again, and shalt bring me up again\l"
    .string "from the depths of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_21::
    .string "Thou shalt increase my greatness,\n"
    .string "and comfort me on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_22::
    .string "I will also praise thee with the\n"
    .string "psaltery, even thy truth, O my God:\l"
    .string "unto thee will I sing with the\l"
    .string "harp, O thou Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_23::
    .string "My lips shall greatly rejoice\n"
    .string "when I sing unto thee; and my soul,\l"
    .string "which thou hast redeemed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_71_24::
    .string "My tongue also shall talk of thy\n"
    .string "righteousness all the day long: for\l"
    .string "they are confounded, for they are\l"
    .string "brought unto shame, that seek my hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_1::
    .string "Give the king thy judgments, O God,\n"
    .string "and thy righteousness unto the\l"
    .string "king’s son.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_2::
    .string "He shall judge thy people with\n"
    .string "righteousness, and thy poor with\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_3::
    .string "The mountains shall bring peace\n"
    .string "to the people, and the little\l"
    .string "hills, by righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_4::
    .string "He shall judge the poor of the\n"
    .string "people, he shall save the\l"
    .string "children of the needy, and shall\l"
    .string "break in pieces the oppressor.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_5::
    .string "They shall fear thee as long as\n"
    .string "the sun and moon endure, throughout\l"
    .string "all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_6::
    .string "He shall come down like rain upon\n"
    .string "the mown grass: as showers that water\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_7::
    .string "In his days shall the righteous\n"
    .string "flourish; and abundance of peace so\l"
    .string "long as the moon endureth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_8::
    .string "He shall have dominion also from\n"
    .string "sea to sea, and from the river unto\l"
    .string "the ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_9::
    .string "They that dwell in the wilderness\n"
    .string "shall bow before him; and his\l"
    .string "enemies shall lick the dust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_10::
    .string "The kings of Tarshish and of the\n"
    .string "isles shall bring presents: the\l"
    .string "kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer\l"
    .string "gifts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_11::
    .string "Yea, all kings shall fall down\n"
    .string "before him: all nations shall\l"
    .string "serve him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_12::
    .string "For he shall deliver the needy\n"
    .string "when he crieth; the poor also, and\l"
    .string "him that hath no helper.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_13::
    .string "He shall spare the poor and\n"
    .string "needy, and shall save the souls of\l"
    .string "the needy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_14::
    .string "He shall redeem their soul from\n"
    .string "deceit and violence: and precious\l"
    .string "shall their blood be in his sight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_15::
    .string "And he shall live, and to him\n"
    .string "shall be given of the gold of\l"
    .string "Sheba: prayer also shall be made\l"
    .string "for him continually; and daily\l"
    .string "shall he be praised.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_16::
    .string "There shall be an handful of corn\n"
    .string "in the earth upon the top of the\l"
    .string "mountains; the fruit thereof shall\l"
    .string "shake like Lebanon: and they of the\l"
    .string "city shall flourish like grass of\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_17::
    .string "His name shall endure for ever: his\n"
    .string "name shall be continued as long as\l"
    .string "the sun: and men shall be blessed\l"
    .string "in him: all nations shall call\l"
    .string "him blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_18::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel, who only doeth wondrous\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_19::
    .string "And blessed be his glorious name\n"
    .string "for ever: and let the whole earth be\l"
    .string "filled with his glory; Amen, and\l"
    .string "Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_72_20::
    .string "The prayers of David the son of\n"
    .string "Jesse are ended.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_1::
    .string "Truly God is good to Israel, even\n"
    .string "to such as are of a clean heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_2::
    .string "But as for me, my feet were almost\n"
    .string "gone; my steps had well nigh\l"
    .string "slipped.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_3::
    .string "For I was envious at the foolish,\n"
    .string "when I saw the prosperity of the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_4::
    .string "For there are no bands in their\n"
    .string "death: but their strength is firm.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_5::
    .string "They are not in trouble as other\n"
    .string "men; neither are they plagued like\l"
    .string "other men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_6::
    .string "Therefore pride compasseth them\n"
    .string "about as a chain; violence covereth\l"
    .string "them as a garment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_7::
    .string "Their eyes stand out with fatness:\n"
    .string "they have more than heart could wish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_8::
    .string "They are corrupt, and speak\n"
    .string "wickedly concerning oppression:\l"
    .string "they speak loftily.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_9::
    .string "They set their mouth against the\n"
    .string "heavens, and their tongue walketh\l"
    .string "through the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_10::
    .string "Therefore his people return\n"
    .string "hither: and waters of a full cup\l"
    .string "are wrung out to them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_11::
    .string "And they say, How doth God know? and\n"
    .string "is there knowledge in the most High?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_12::
    .string "Behold, these are the ungodly, who\n"
    .string "prosper in the world; they increase\l"
    .string "in riches.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_13::
    .string "Verily I have cleansed my heart in\n"
    .string "vain, and washed my hands in\l"
    .string "innocency.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_14::
    .string "For all the day long have I been\n"
    .string "plagued, and chastened every\l"
    .string "morning.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_15::
    .string "If I say, I will speak thus;\n"
    .string "behold, I should offend against the\l"
    .string "generation of thy children.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_16::
    .string "When I thought to know this, it was\n"
    .string "too painful for me;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_17::
    .string "Until I went into the sanctuary of\n"
    .string "God; then understood I their end.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_18::
    .string "Surely thou didst set them in\n"
    .string "slippery places: thou castedst\l"
    .string "them down into destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_19::
    .string "How are they brought into\n"
    .string "desolation, as in a moment! they are\l"
    .string "utterly consumed with terrors.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_20::
    .string "As a dream when one awaketh; so, O\n"
    .string "Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt\l"
    .string "despise their image.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_21::
    .string "Thus my heart was grieved, and I was\n"
    .string "pricked in my reins.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_22::
    .string "So foolish was I, and ignorant: I\n"
    .string "was as a beast before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_23::
    .string "Nevertheless I am continually\n"
    .string "with thee: thou hast holden me by my\l"
    .string "right hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_24::
    .string "Thou shalt guide me with thy\n"
    .string "counsel, and afterward receive me to\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_25::
    .string "Whom have I in heaven but thee? and\n"
    .string "there is none upon earth that I\l"
    .string "desire beside thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_26::
    .string "My flesh and my heart faileth: but\n"
    .string "God is the strength of my heart, and\l"
    .string "my portion for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_27::
    .string "For, lo, they that are far from thee\n"
    .string "shall perish: thou hast destroyed\l"
    .string "all them that go a whoring from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_73_28::
    .string "But it is good for me to draw near to\n"
    .string "God: I have put my trust in the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD, that I may declare all thy\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_1::
    .string "O God, why hast thou cast us off for\n"
    .string "ever? why doth thine anger smoke\l"
    .string "against the sheep of thy pasture?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_2::
    .string "Remember thy congregation, which\n"
    .string "thou hast purchased of old; the rod\l"
    .string "of thine inheritance, which thou hast\l"
    .string "redeemed; this mount Zion, wherein\l"
    .string "thou hast dwelt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_3::
    .string "Lift up thy feet unto the\n"
    .string "perpetual desolations; even all\l"
    .string "that the enemy hath done wickedly in\l"
    .string "the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_4::
    .string "Thine enemies roar in the midst of\n"
    .string "thy congregations; they set up their\l"
    .string "ensigns for signs.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_5::
    .string "A man was famous according as he had\n"
    .string "lifted up axes upon the thick trees.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_6::
    .string "But now they break down the carved\n"
    .string "work thereof at once with axes and\l"
    .string "hammers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_7::
    .string "They have cast fire into thy\n"
    .string "sanctuary, they have defiled by\l"
    .string "casting down the dwelling place of\l"
    .string "thy name to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_8::
    .string "They said in their hearts, Let us\n"
    .string "destroy them together: they have\l"
    .string "burned up all the synagogues of God\l"
    .string "in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_9::
    .string "We see not our signs: there is no\n"
    .string "more any prophet: neither is there\l"
    .string "among us any that knoweth how long.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_10::
    .string "O God, how long shall the\n"
    .string "adversary reproach? shall the\l"
    .string "enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_11::
    .string "Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even\n"
    .string "thy right hand? pluck it out of thy\l"
    .string "bosom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_12::
    .string "For God is my King of old, working\n"
    .string "salvation in the midst of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_13::
    .string "Thou didst divide the sea by thy\n"
    .string "strength: thou brakest the heads of\l"
    .string "the dragons in the waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_14::
    .string "Thou brakest the heads of leviathan\n"
    .string "in pieces, and gavest him to be meat\l"
    .string "to the people inhabiting the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_15::
    .string "Thou didst cleave the fountain and\n"
    .string "the flood: thou driedst up mighty\l"
    .string "rivers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_16::
    .string "The day is thine, the night also is\n"
    .string "thine: thou hast prepared the light\l"
    .string "and the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_17::
    .string "Thou hast set all the borders of\n"
    .string "the earth: thou hast made summer and\l"
    .string "winter.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_18::
    .string "Remember this, that the enemy hath\n"
    .string "reproached, O LORD, and that the\l"
    .string "foolish people have blasphemed\l"
    .string "thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_19::
    .string "O deliver not the soul of thy\n"
    .string "turtledove unto the multitude of\l"
    .string "the wicked: forget not the\l"
    .string "congregation of thy poor for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_20::
    .string "Have respect unto the covenant: for\n"
    .string "the dark places of the earth are\l"
    .string "full of the habitations of cruelty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_21::
    .string "O let not the oppressed return\n"
    .string "ashamed: let the poor and needy\l"
    .string "praise thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_22::
    .string "Arise, O God, plead thine own\n"
    .string "cause: remember how the foolish man\l"
    .string "reproacheth thee daily.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_74_23::
    .string "Forget not the voice of thine\n"
    .string "enemies: the tumult of those that\l"
    .string "rise up against thee increaseth\l"
    .string "continually.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_1::
    .string "Unto thee, O God, do we give thanks,\n"
    .string "unto thee do we give thanks: for that\l"
    .string "thy name is near thy wondrous works\l"
    .string "declare.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_2::
    .string "When I shall receive the\n"
    .string "congregation I will judge\l"
    .string "uprightly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_3::
    .string "The earth and all the inhabitants\n"
    .string "thereof are dissolved: I bear up the\l"
    .string "pillars of it. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_4::
    .string "I said unto the fools, Deal not\n"
    .string "foolishly: and to the wicked, Lift\l"
    .string "not up the horn:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_5::
    .string "Lift not up your horn on high:\n"
    .string "speak not with a stiff neck.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_6::
    .string "For promotion cometh neither from\n"
    .string "the east, nor from the west, nor from\l"
    .string "the south.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_7::
    .string "But God is the judge: he putteth\n"
    .string "down one, and setteth up another.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_8::
    .string "For in the hand of the LORD there is\n"
    .string "a cup, and the wine is red; it is\l"
    .string "full of mixture; and he poureth out\l"
    .string "of the same: but the dregs thereof,\l"
    .string "all the wicked of the earth shall\l"
    .string "wring them out, and drink them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_9::
    .string "But I will declare for ever; I\n"
    .string "will sing praises to the God of\l"
    .string "Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_75_10::
    .string "All the horns of the wicked also\n"
    .string "will I cut off; but the horns of the\l"
    .string "righteous shall be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_1::
    .string "In Judah is God known: his name is\n"
    .string "great in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_2::
    .string "In Salem also is his tabernacle,\n"
    .string "and his dwelling place in Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_3::
    .string "There brake he the arrows of the\n"
    .string "bow, the shield, and the sword, and\l"
    .string "the battle. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_4::
    .string "Thou art more glorious and\n"
    .string "excellent than the mountains of\l"
    .string "prey.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_5::
    .string "The stouthearted are spoiled, they\n"
    .string "have slept their sleep: and none\l"
    .string "of the men of might have found their\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_6::
    .string "At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both\n"
    .string "the chariot and horse are cast into a\l"
    .string "dead sleep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_7::
    .string "Thou, even thou, art to be feared:\n"
    .string "and who may stand in thy sight when\l"
    .string "once thou art angry?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_8::
    .string "Thou didst cause judgment to be\n"
    .string "heard from heaven; the earth feared,\l"
    .string "and was still,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_9::
    .string "When God arose to judgment, to save\n"
    .string "all the meek of the earth. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_10::
    .string "Surely the wrath of man shall\n"
    .string "praise thee: the remainder of wrath\l"
    .string "shalt thou restrain.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_11::
    .string "Vow, and pay unto the LORD your God:\n"
    .string "let all that be round about him\l"
    .string "bring presents unto him that ought\l"
    .string "to be feared.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_76_12::
    .string "He shall cut off the spirit of\n"
    .string "princes: he is terrible to the kings\l"
    .string "of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_1::
    .string "I cried unto God with my voice, even\n"
    .string "unto God with my voice; and he gave\l"
    .string "ear unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_2::
    .string "In the day of my trouble I sought\n"
    .string "the Lord: my sore ran in the night,\l"
    .string "and ceased not: my soul refused to be\l"
    .string "comforted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_3::
    .string "I remembered God, and was troubled:\n"
    .string "I complained, and my spirit was\l"
    .string "overwhelmed. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_4::
    .string "Thou holdest mine eyes waking: I am\n"
    .string "so troubled that I cannot speak.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_5::
    .string "I have considered the days of old,\n"
    .string "the years of ancient times.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_6::
    .string "I call to remembrance my song in\n"
    .string "the night: I commune with mine own\l"
    .string "heart: and my spirit made diligent\l"
    .string "search.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_7::
    .string "Will the Lord cast off for ever?\n"
    .string "and will he be favourable no more?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_8::
    .string "Is his mercy clean gone for ever?\n"
    .string "doth his promise fail for evermore?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_9::
    .string "Hath God forgotten to be gracious?\n"
    .string "hath he in anger shut up his tender\l"
    .string "mercies? Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_10::
    .string "And I said, This is my infirmity:\n"
    .string "but I will remember the years of the\l"
    .string "right hand of the most High.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_11::
    .string "I will remember the works of the\n"
    .string "LORD: surely I will remember thy\l"
    .string "wonders of old.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_12::
    .string "I will meditate also of all thy\n"
    .string "work, and talk of thy doings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_13::
    .string "Thy way, O God, is in the sanctuary:\n"
    .string "who is so great a God as our God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_14::
    .string "Thou art the God that doest wonders:\n"
    .string "thou hast declared thy strength\l"
    .string "among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_15::
    .string "Thou hast with thine arm redeemed\n"
    .string "thy people, the sons of Jacob and\l"
    .string "Joseph. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_16::
    .string "The waters saw thee, O God, the\n"
    .string "waters saw thee; they were afraid:\l"
    .string "the depths also were troubled.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_17::
    .string "The clouds poured out water: the\n"
    .string "skies sent out a sound: thine arrows\l"
    .string "also went abroad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_18::
    .string "The voice of thy thunder was in the\n"
    .string "heaven: the lightnings lightened\l"
    .string "the world: the earth trembled and\l"
    .string "shook.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_19::
    .string "Thy way is in the sea, and thy path\n"
    .string "in the great waters, and thy\l"
    .string "footsteps are not known.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_77_20::
    .string "Thou leddest thy people like a\n"
    .string "flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_1::
    .string "Give ear, O my people, to my law:\n"
    .string "incline your ears to the words of my\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_2::
    .string "I will open my mouth in a\n"
    .string "parable: I will utter dark sayings\l"
    .string "of old:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_3::
    .string "Which we have heard and known, and\n"
    .string "our fathers have told us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_4::
    .string "We will not hide them from their\n"
    .string "children, shewing to the generation\l"
    .string "to come the praises of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "his strength, and his wonderful\l"
    .string "works that he hath done.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_5::
    .string "For he established a testimony in\n"
    .string "Jacob, and appointed a law in\l"
    .string "Israel, which he commanded our\l"
    .string "fathers, that they should make them\l"
    .string "known to their children:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_6::
    .string "That the generation to come might\n"
    .string "know them, even the children which\l"
    .string "should be born; who should arise and\l"
    .string "declare them to their children:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_7::
    .string "That they might set their hope in\n"
    .string "God, and not forget the works of God,\l"
    .string "but keep his commandments:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_8::
    .string "And might not be as their fathers, a\n"
    .string "stubborn and rebellious generation;\l"
    .string "a generation that set not their heart\l"
    .string "aright, and whose spirit was not\l"
    .string "stedfast with God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_9::
    .string "The children of Ephraim, being\n"
    .string "armed, and carrying bows, turned back\l"
    .string "in the day of battle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_10::
    .string "They kept not the covenant of God,\n"
    .string "and refused to walk in his law;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_11::
    .string "And forgat his works, and his\n"
    .string "wonders that he had shewed them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_12::
    .string "Marvellous things did he in the\n"
    .string "sight of their fathers, in the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, in the field of Zoan.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_13::
    .string "He divided the sea, and caused them\n"
    .string "to pass through; and he made the\l"
    .string "waters to stand as an heap.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_14::
    .string "In the daytime also he led them\n"
    .string "with a cloud, and all the night\l"
    .string "with a light of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_15::
    .string "He clave the rocks in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and gave them drink as\l"
    .string "out of the great depths.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_16::
    .string "He brought streams also out of the\n"
    .string "rock, and caused waters to run down\l"
    .string "like rivers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_17::
    .string "And they sinned yet more against him\n"
    .string "by provoking the most High in the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_18::
    .string "And they tempted God in their heart\n"
    .string "by asking meat for their lust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_19::
    .string "Yea, they spake against God; they\n"
    .string "said, Can God furnish a table in the\l"
    .string "wilderness?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_20::
    .string "Behold, he smote the rock, that the\n"
    .string "waters gushed out, and the streams\l"
    .string "overflowed; can he give bread also?\l"
    .string "can he provide flesh for his\l"
    .string "people?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_21::
    .string "Therefore the LORD heard this, and\n"
    .string "was wroth: so a fire was kindled\l"
    .string "against Jacob, and anger also came\l"
    .string "up against Israel;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_22::
    .string "Because they believed not in God,\n"
    .string "and trusted not in his salvation:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_23::
    .string "Though he had commanded the clouds\n"
    .string "from above, and opened the doors of\l"
    .string "heaven,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_24::
    .string "And had rained down manna upon them\n"
    .string "to eat, and had given them of the corn\l"
    .string "of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_25::
    .string "Man did eat angels’ food: he sent\n"
    .string "them meat to the full.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_26::
    .string "He caused an east wind to blow in\n"
    .string "the heaven: and by his power he\l"
    .string "brought in the south wind.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_27::
    .string "He rained flesh also upon them as\n"
    .string "dust, and feathered fowls like as\l"
    .string "the sand of the sea:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_28::
    .string "And he let it fall in the midst of\n"
    .string "their camp, round about their\l"
    .string "habitations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_29::
    .string "So they did eat, and were well\n"
    .string "filled: for he gave them their own\l"
    .string "desire;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_30::
    .string "They were not estranged from their\n"
    .string "lust. But while their meat was yet in\l"
    .string "their mouths,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_31::
    .string "The wrath of God came upon them, and\n"
    .string "slew the fattest of them, and smote\l"
    .string "down the chosen men of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_32::
    .string "For all this they sinned still,\n"
    .string "and believed not for his wondrous\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_33::
    .string "Therefore their days did he consume\n"
    .string "in vanity, and their years in\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_34::
    .string "When he slew them, then they sought\n"
    .string "him: and they returned and enquired\l"
    .string "early after God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_35::
    .string "And they remembered that God was\n"
    .string "their rock, and the high God their\l"
    .string "redeemer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_36::
    .string "Nevertheless they did flatter him\n"
    .string "with their mouth, and they lied unto\l"
    .string "him with their tongues.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_37::
    .string "For their heart was not right with\n"
    .string "him, neither were they stedfast in\l"
    .string "his covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_38::
    .string "But he, being full of compassion,\n"
    .string "forgave their iniquity, and\l"
    .string "destroyed them not: yea, many a time\l"
    .string "turned he his anger away, and did not\l"
    .string "stir up all his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_39::
    .string "For he remembered that they were but\n"
    .string "flesh; a wind that passeth away, and\l"
    .string "cometh not again.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_40::
    .string "How oft did they provoke him in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and grieve him in the\l"
    .string "desert!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_41::
    .string "Yea, they turned back and tempted\n"
    .string "God, and limited the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_42::
    .string "They remembered not his hand, nor\n"
    .string "the day when he delivered them from\l"
    .string "the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_43::
    .string "How he had wrought his signs in\n"
    .string "Egypt, and his wonders in the field\l"
    .string "of Zoan.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_44::
    .string "And had turned their rivers into\n"
    .string "blood; and their floods, that they\l"
    .string "could not drink.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_45::
    .string "He sent divers sorts of flies among\n"
    .string "them, which devoured them; and frogs,\l"
    .string "which destroyed them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_46::
    .string "He gave also their increase unto\n"
    .string "the caterpiller, and their labour\l"
    .string "unto the locust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_47::
    .string "He destroyed their vines with hail,\n"
    .string "and their sycomore trees with frost.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_48::
    .string "He gave up their cattle also to\n"
    .string "the hail, and their flocks to hot\l"
    .string "thunderbolts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_49::
    .string "He cast upon them the fierceness of\n"
    .string "his anger, wrath, and indignation,\l"
    .string "and trouble, by sending evil angels\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_50::
    .string "He made a way to his anger; he\n"
    .string "spared not their soul from death,\l"
    .string "but gave their life over to the\l"
    .string "pestilence;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_51::
    .string "And smote all the firstborn in\n"
    .string "Egypt; the chief of their strength\l"
    .string "in the tabernacles of Ham:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_52::
    .string "But made his own people to go\n"
    .string "forth like sheep, and guided them in\l"
    .string "the wilderness like a flock.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_53::
    .string "And he led them on safely, so that\n"
    .string "they feared not: but the sea\l"
    .string "overwhelmed their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_54::
    .string "And he brought them to the border of\n"
    .string "his sanctuary, even to this mountain,\l"
    .string "which his right hand had purchased.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_55::
    .string "He cast out the heathen also before\n"
    .string "them, and divided them an inheritance\l"
    .string "by line, and made the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel to dwell in their tents.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_56::
    .string "Yet they tempted and provoked the\n"
    .string "most high God, and kept not his\l"
    .string "testimonies:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_57::
    .string "But turned back, and dealt\n"
    .string "unfaithfully like their fathers:\l"
    .string "they were turned aside like a\l"
    .string "deceitful bow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_58::
    .string "For they provoked him to anger with\n"
    .string "their high places, and moved him to\l"
    .string "jealousy with their graven images.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_59::
    .string "When God heard this, he was wroth,\n"
    .string "and greatly abhorred Israel:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_60::
    .string "So that he forsook the tabernacle\n"
    .string "of Shiloh, the tent which he placed\l"
    .string "among men;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_61::
    .string "And delivered his strength into\n"
    .string "captivity, and his glory into the\l"
    .string "enemy’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_62::
    .string "He gave his people over also unto\n"
    .string "the sword; and was wroth with his\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_63::
    .string "The fire consumed their young men;\n"
    .string "and their maidens were not given to\l"
    .string "marriage.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_64::
    .string "Their priests fell by the sword;\n"
    .string "and their widows made no lamentation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_65::
    .string "Then the LORD awaked as one out of\n"
    .string "sleep, and like a mighty man that\l"
    .string "shouteth by reason of wine.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_66::
    .string "And he smote his enemies in the\n"
    .string "hinder parts: he put them to a\l"
    .string "perpetual reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_67::
    .string "Moreover he refused the tabernacle\n"
    .string "of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of\l"
    .string "Ephraim:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_68::
    .string "But chose the tribe of Judah, the\n"
    .string "mount Zion which he loved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_69::
    .string "And he built his sanctuary like\n"
    .string "high palaces, like the earth which\l"
    .string "he hath established for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_70::
    .string "He chose David also his servant,\n"
    .string "and took him from the sheepfolds:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_71::
    .string "From following the ewes great with\n"
    .string "young he brought him to feed Jacob\l"
    .string "his people, and Israel his\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_78_72::
    .string "So he fed them according to the\n"
    .string "integrity of his heart; and guided\l"
    .string "them by the skilfulness of his\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_1::
    .string "O God, the heathen are come into\n"
    .string "thine inheritance; thy holy temple\l"
    .string "have they defiled; they have laid\l"
    .string "Jerusalem on heaps.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_2::
    .string "The dead bodies of thy servants have\n"
    .string "they given to be meat unto the fowls\l"
    .string "of the heaven, the flesh of thy\l"
    .string "saints unto the beasts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_3::
    .string "Their blood have they shed like\n"
    .string "water round about Jerusalem; and\l"
    .string "there was none to bury them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_4::
    .string "We are become a reproach to our\n"
    .string "neighbours, a scorn and derision to\l"
    .string "them that are round about us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_5::
    .string "How long, LORD? wilt thou be angry\n"
    .string "for ever? shall thy jealousy burn\l"
    .string "like fire?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_6::
    .string "Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen\n"
    .string "that have not known thee, and upon\l"
    .string "the kingdoms that have not called\l"
    .string "upon thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_7::
    .string "For they have devoured Jacob, and\n"
    .string "laid waste his dwelling place.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_8::
    .string "O remember not against us former\n"
    .string "iniquities: let thy tender mercies\l"
    .string "speedily prevent us: for we are\l"
    .string "brought very low.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_9::
    .string "Help us, O God of our salvation,\n"
    .string "for the glory of thy name: and\l"
    .string "deliver us, and purge away our sins,\l"
    .string "for thy name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_10::
    .string "Wherefore should the heathen say,\n"
    .string "Where is their God? let him be known\l"
    .string "among the heathen in our sight by the\l"
    .string "revenging of the blood of thy\l"
    .string "servants which is shed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_11::
    .string "Let the sighing of the prisoner\n"
    .string "come before thee; according to the\l"
    .string "greatness of thy power preserve\l"
    .string "thou those that are appointed to\l"
    .string "die;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_12::
    .string "And render unto our neighbours\n"
    .string "sevenfold into their bosom their\l"
    .string "reproach, wherewith they have\l"
    .string "reproached thee, O Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_79_13::
    .string "So we thy people and sheep of thy\n"
    .string "pasture will give thee thanks for\l"
    .string "ever: we will shew forth thy praise\l"
    .string "to all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_1::
    .string "Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel,\n"
    .string "thou that leadest Joseph like a\l"
    .string "flock; thou that dwellest between\l"
    .string "the cherubims, shine forth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_2::
    .string "Before Ephraim and Benjamin and\n"
    .string "Manasseh stir up thy strength, and\l"
    .string "come and save us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_3::
    .string "Turn us again, O God, and cause thy\n"
    .string "face to shine; and we shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_4::
    .string "O LORD God of hosts, how long wilt\n"
    .string "thou be angry against the prayer of\l"
    .string "thy people?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_5::
    .string "Thou feedest them with the bread of\n"
    .string "tears; and givest them tears to drink\l"
    .string "in great measure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_6::
    .string "Thou makest us a strife unto our\n"
    .string "neighbours: and our enemies laugh\l"
    .string "among themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_7::
    .string "Turn us again, O God of hosts, and\n"
    .string "cause thy face to shine; and we\l"
    .string "shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_8::
    .string "Thou hast brought a vine out of\n"
    .string "Egypt: thou hast cast out the\l"
    .string "heathen, and planted it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_9::
    .string "Thou preparedst room before it,\n"
    .string "and didst cause it to take deep root,\l"
    .string "and it filled the land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_10::
    .string "The hills were covered with the\n"
    .string "shadow of it, and the boughs thereof\l"
    .string "were like the goodly cedars.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_11::
    .string "She sent out her boughs unto the\n"
    .string "sea, and her branches unto the river.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_12::
    .string "Why hast thou then broken down her\n"
    .string "hedges, so that all they which pass\l"
    .string "by the way do pluck her?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_13::
    .string "The boar out of the wood doth waste\n"
    .string "it, and the wild beast of the field\l"
    .string "doth devour it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_14::
    .string "Return, we beseech thee, O God of\n"
    .string "hosts: look down from heaven, and\l"
    .string "behold, and visit this vine;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_15::
    .string "And the vineyard which thy right\n"
    .string "hand hath planted, and the branch\l"
    .string "that thou madest strong for thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_16::
    .string "It is burned with fire, it is cut\n"
    .string "down: they perish at the rebuke of\l"
    .string "thy countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_17::
    .string "Let thy hand be upon the man of thy\n"
    .string "right hand, upon the son of man whom\l"
    .string "thou madest strong for thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_18::
    .string "So will not we go back from thee:\n"
    .string "quicken us, and we will call upon\l"
    .string "thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_80_19::
    .string "Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts,\n"
    .string "cause thy face to shine; and we\l"
    .string "shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_1::
    .string "Sing aloud unto God our strength:\n"
    .string "make a joyful noise unto the God of\l"
    .string "Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_2::
    .string "Take a psalm, and bring hither the\n"
    .string "timbrel, the pleasant harp with\l"
    .string "the psaltery.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_3::
    .string "Blow up the trumpet in the new\n"
    .string "moon, in the time appointed, on our\l"
    .string "solemn feast day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_4::
    .string "For this was a statute for Israel,\n"
    .string "and a law of the God of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_5::
    .string "This he ordained in Joseph for a\n"
    .string "testimony, when he went out through\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt: where I heard a\l"
    .string "language that I understood not.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_6::
    .string "I removed his shoulder from the\n"
    .string "burden: his hands were delivered\l"
    .string "from the pots.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_7::
    .string "Thou calledst in trouble, and I\n"
    .string "delivered thee; I answered thee in\l"
    .string "the secret place of thunder: I\l"
    .string "proved thee at the waters of Meribah.\l"
    .string "Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_8::
    .string "Hear, O my people, and I will\n"
    .string "testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou\l"
    .string "wilt hearken unto me;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_9::
    .string "There shall no strange god be in\n"
    .string "thee; neither shalt thou worship\l"
    .string "any strange god.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_10::
    .string "I am the LORD thy God, which brought\n"
    .string "thee out of the land of Egypt: open\l"
    .string "thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_11::
    .string "But my people would not hearken\n"
    .string "to my voice; and Israel would none\l"
    .string "of me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_12::
    .string "So I gave them up unto their own\n"
    .string "hearts’ lust: and they walked in\l"
    .string "their own counsels.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_13::
    .string "Oh that my people had hearkened\n"
    .string "unto me, and Israel had walked in my\l"
    .string "ways!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_14::
    .string "I should soon have subdued their\n"
    .string "enemies, and turned my hand against\l"
    .string "their adversaries.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_15::
    .string "The haters of the LORD should have\n"
    .string "submitted themselves unto him: but\l"
    .string "their time should have endured for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_81_16::
    .string "He should have fed them also with\n"
    .string "the finest of the wheat: and with\l"
    .string "honey out of the rock should I have\l"
    .string "satisfied thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_1::
    .string "God standeth in the congregation of\n"
    .string "the mighty; he judgeth among the gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_2::
    .string "How long will ye judge unjustly,\n"
    .string "and accept the persons of the\l"
    .string "wicked? Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_3::
    .string "Defend the poor and fatherless: do\n"
    .string "justice to the afflicted and needy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_4::
    .string "Deliver the poor and needy: rid\n"
    .string "them out of the hand of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_5::
    .string "They know not, neither will they\n"
    .string "understand; they walk on in\l"
    .string "darkness: all the foundations of\l"
    .string "the earth are out of course.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_6::
    .string "I have said, Ye are gods; and all\n"
    .string "of you are children of the most High.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_7::
    .string "But ye shall die like men, and\n"
    .string "fall like one of the princes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_82_8::
    .string "Arise, O God, judge the earth: for\n"
    .string "thou shalt inherit all nations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_1::
    .string "Keep not thou silence, O God: hold\n"
    .string "not thy peace, and be not still, O\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_2::
    .string "For, lo, thine enemies make a\n"
    .string "tumult: and they that hate thee have\l"
    .string "lifted up the head.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_3::
    .string "They have taken crafty counsel\n"
    .string "against thy people, and consulted\l"
    .string "against thy hidden ones.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_4::
    .string "They have said, Come, and let us cut\n"
    .string "them off from being a nation; that\l"
    .string "the name of Israel may be no more in\l"
    .string "remembrance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_5::
    .string "For they have consulted together\n"
    .string "with one consent: they are\l"
    .string "confederate against thee:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_6::
    .string "The tabernacles of Edom, and the\n"
    .string "Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the\l"
    .string "Hagarenes;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_7::
    .string "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the\n"
    .string "Philistines with the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Tyre;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_8::
    .string "Assur also is joined with them:\n"
    .string "they have holpen the children of\l"
    .string "Lot. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_9::
    .string "Do unto them as unto the Midianites;\n"
    .string "as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the\l"
    .string "brook of Kison:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_10::
    .string "Which perished at Endor: they\n"
    .string "became as dung for the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_11::
    .string "Make their nobles like Oreb, and\n"
    .string "like Zeeb: yea, all their princes\l"
    .string "as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_12::
    .string "Who said, Let us take to ourselves\n"
    .string "the houses of God in possession.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_13::
    .string "O my God, make them like a wheel;\n"
    .string "as the stubble before the wind.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_14::
    .string "As the fire burneth a wood, and as\n"
    .string "the flame setteth the mountains on\l"
    .string "fire;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_15::
    .string "So persecute them with thy\n"
    .string "tempest, and make them afraid with\l"
    .string "thy storm.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_16::
    .string "Fill their faces with shame; that\n"
    .string "they may seek thy name, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_17::
    .string "Let them be confounded and troubled\n"
    .string "for ever; yea, let them be put to\l"
    .string "shame, and perish:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_83_18::
    .string "That men may know that thou, whose\n"
    .string "name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most\l"
    .string "high over all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_1::
    .string "How amiable are thy tabernacles, O\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_2::
    .string "My soul longeth, yea, even\n"
    .string "fainteth for the courts of the LORD:\l"
    .string "my heart and my flesh crieth out for\l"
    .string "the living God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_3::
    .string "Yea, the sparrow hath found an\n"
    .string "house, and the swallow a nest for\l"
    .string "herself, where she may lay her\l"
    .string "young, even thine altars, O LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, my King, and my God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_4::
    .string "Blessed are they that dwell in thy\n"
    .string "house: they will be still\l"
    .string "praising thee. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_5::
    .string "Blessed is the man whose strength\n"
    .string "is in thee; in whose heart are the\l"
    .string "ways of them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_6::
    .string "Who passing through the valley of\n"
    .string "Baca make it a well; the rain also\l"
    .string "filleth the pools.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_7::
    .string "They go from strength to strength,\n"
    .string "every one of them in Zion appeareth\l"
    .string "before God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_8::
    .string "O LORD God of hosts, hear my prayer:\n"
    .string "give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_9::
    .string "Behold, O God our shield, and look\n"
    .string "upon the face of thine anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_10::
    .string "For a day in thy courts is better\n"
    .string "than a thousand. I had rather be a\l"
    .string "doorkeeper in the house of my God,\l"
    .string "than to dwell in the tents of\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_11::
    .string "For the LORD God is a sun and\n"
    .string "shield: the LORD will give grace\l"
    .string "and glory: no good thing will he\l"
    .string "withhold from them that walk\l"
    .string "uprightly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_84_12::
    .string "O LORD of hosts, blessed is the man\n"
    .string "that trusteth in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_1::
    .string "Lord, thou hast been favourable\n"
    .string "unto thy land: thou hast brought\l"
    .string "back the captivity of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_2::
    .string "Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of\n"
    .string "thy people, thou hast covered all\l"
    .string "their sin. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_3::
    .string "Thou hast taken away all thy wrath:\n"
    .string "thou hast turned thyself from the\l"
    .string "fierceness of thine anger.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_4::
    .string "Turn us, O God of our salvation, and\n"
    .string "cause thine anger toward us to cease.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_5::
    .string "Wilt thou be angry with us for ever?\n"
    .string "wilt thou draw out thine anger to\l"
    .string "all generations?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_6::
    .string "Wilt thou not revive us again: that\n"
    .string "thy people may rejoice in thee?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_7::
    .string "Shew us thy mercy, O LORD, and grant\n"
    .string "us thy salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_8::
    .string "I will hear what God the LORD\n"
    .string "will speak: for he will speak\l"
    .string "peace unto his people, and to his\l"
    .string "saints: but let them not turn again\l"
    .string "to folly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_9::
    .string "Surely his salvation is nigh them\n"
    .string "that fear him; that glory may dwell\l"
    .string "in our land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_10::
    .string "Mercy and truth are met together;\n"
    .string "righteousness and peace have kissed\l"
    .string "each other.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_11::
    .string "Truth shall spring out of the\n"
    .string "earth; and righteousness shall\l"
    .string "look down from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_12::
    .string "Yea, the LORD shall give that which\n"
    .string "is good; and our land shall yield\l"
    .string "her increase.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_85_13::
    .string "Righteousness shall go before him;\n"
    .string "and shall set us in the way of his\l"
    .string "steps.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_1::
    .string "Bow down thine ear, O LORD, hear me:\n"
    .string "for I am poor and needy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_2::
    .string "Preserve my soul; for I am holy: O\n"
    .string "thou my God, save thy servant that\l"
    .string "trusteth in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_3::
    .string "Be merciful unto me, O Lord: for I\n"
    .string "cry unto thee daily.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_4::
    .string "Rejoice the soul of thy servant:\n"
    .string "for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up\l"
    .string "my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_5::
    .string "For thou, Lord, art good, and ready\n"
    .string "to forgive; and plenteous in mercy\l"
    .string "unto all them that call upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_6::
    .string "Give ear, O LORD, unto my prayer;\n"
    .string "and attend to the voice of my\l"
    .string "supplications.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_7::
    .string "In the day of my trouble I will\n"
    .string "call upon thee: for thou wilt\l"
    .string "answer me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_8::
    .string "Among the gods there is none like\n"
    .string "unto thee, O Lord; neither are there\l"
    .string "any works like unto thy works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_9::
    .string "All nations whom thou hast made\n"
    .string "shall come and worship before thee,\l"
    .string "O Lord; and shall glorify thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_10::
    .string "For thou art great, and doest\n"
    .string "wondrous things: thou art God alone.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_11::
    .string "Teach me thy way, O LORD; I will\n"
    .string "walk in thy truth: unite my heart to\l"
    .string "fear thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_12::
    .string "I will praise thee, O Lord my God,\n"
    .string "with all my heart: and I will\l"
    .string "glorify thy name for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_13::
    .string "For great is thy mercy toward me:\n"
    .string "and thou hast delivered my soul\l"
    .string "from the lowest hell.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_14::
    .string "O God, the proud are risen against\n"
    .string "me, and the assemblies of violent\l"
    .string "men have sought after my soul; and\l"
    .string "have not set thee before them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_15::
    .string "But thou, O Lord, art a God full of\n"
    .string "compassion, and gracious,\l"
    .string "longsuffering, and plenteous in\l"
    .string "mercy and truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_16::
    .string "O turn unto me, and have mercy upon\n"
    .string "me; give thy strength unto thy\l"
    .string "servant, and save the son of thine\l"
    .string "handmaid.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_86_17::
    .string "Shew me a token for good; that they\n"
    .string "which hate me may see it, and be\l"
    .string "ashamed: because thou, LORD, hast\l"
    .string "holpen me, and comforted me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_1::
    .string "His foundation is in the holy\n"
    .string "mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_2::
    .string "The LORD loveth the gates of Zion\n"
    .string "more than all the dwellings of\l"
    .string "Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_3::
    .string "Glorious things are spoken of\n"
    .string "thee, O city of God. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_4::
    .string "I will make mention of Rahab and\n"
    .string "Babylon to them that know me: behold\l"
    .string "Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia;\l"
    .string "this man was born there.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_5::
    .string "And of Zion it shall be said, This\n"
    .string "and that man was born in her: and the\l"
    .string "highest himself shall establish\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_6::
    .string "The LORD shall count, when he\n"
    .string "writeth up the people, that this\l"
    .string "man was born there. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_87_7::
    .string "As well the singers as the\n"
    .string "players on instruments shall be\l"
    .string "there: all my springs are in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_1::
    .string "O lord God of my salvation, I have\n"
    .string "cried day and night before thee:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_2::
    .string "Let my prayer come before thee:\n"
    .string "incline thine ear unto my cry;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_3::
    .string "For my soul is full of troubles:\n"
    .string "and my life draweth nigh unto the\l"
    .string "grave.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_4::
    .string "I am counted with them that go down\n"
    .string "into the pit: I am as a man that hath\l"
    .string "no strength:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_5::
    .string "Free among the dead, like the slain\n"
    .string "that lie in the grave, whom thou\l"
    .string "rememberest no more: and they are cut\l"
    .string "off from thy hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_6::
    .string "Thou hast laid me in the lowest\n"
    .string "pit, in darkness, in the deeps.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_7::
    .string "Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and\n"
    .string "thou hast afflicted me with all thy\l"
    .string "waves. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_8::
    .string "Thou hast put away mine\n"
    .string "acquaintance far from me; thou hast\l"
    .string "made me an abomination unto them: I\l"
    .string "am shut up, and I cannot come forth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_9::
    .string "Mine eye mourneth by reason of\n"
    .string "affliction: LORD, I have called\l"
    .string "daily upon thee, I have stretched\l"
    .string "out my hands unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_10::
    .string "Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead?\n"
    .string "shall the dead arise and praise\l"
    .string "thee? Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_11::
    .string "Shall thy lovingkindness be\n"
    .string "declared in the grave? or thy\l"
    .string "faithfulness in destruction?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_12::
    .string "Shall thy wonders be known in the\n"
    .string "dark? and thy righteousness in the\l"
    .string "land of forgetfulness?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_13::
    .string "But unto thee have I cried, O LORD;\n"
    .string "and in the morning shall my prayer\l"
    .string "prevent thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_14::
    .string "LORD, why castest thou off my soul?\n"
    .string "why hidest thou thy face from me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_15::
    .string "I am afflicted and ready to die\n"
    .string "from my youth up: while I suffer thy\l"
    .string "terrors I am distracted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_16::
    .string "Thy fierce wrath goeth over me; thy\n"
    .string "terrors have cut me off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_17::
    .string "They came round about me daily\n"
    .string "like water; they compassed me about\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_88_18::
    .string "Lover and friend hast thou put far\n"
    .string "from me, and mine acquaintance into\l"
    .string "darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_1::
    .string "I will sing of the mercies of the\n"
    .string "LORD for ever: with my mouth will I\l"
    .string "make known thy faithfulness to all\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_2::
    .string "For I have said, Mercy shall be\n"
    .string "built up for ever: thy faithfulness\l"
    .string "shalt thou establish in the very\l"
    .string "heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_3::
    .string "I have made a covenant with my\n"
    .string "chosen, I have sworn unto David my\l"
    .string "servant,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_4::
    .string "Thy seed will I establish for\n"
    .string "ever, and build up thy throne to\l"
    .string "all generations. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_5::
    .string "And the heavens shall praise thy\n"
    .string "wonders, O LORD: thy faithfulness\l"
    .string "also in the congregation of the\l"
    .string "saints.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_6::
    .string "For who in the heaven can be\n"
    .string "compared unto the LORD? who among\l"
    .string "the sons of the mighty can be\l"
    .string "likened unto the LORD?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_7::
    .string "God is greatly to be feared in the\n"
    .string "assembly of the saints, and to be had\l"
    .string "in reverence of all them that are\l"
    .string "about him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_8::
    .string "O LORD God of hosts, who is a strong\n"
    .string "LORD like unto thee? or to thy\l"
    .string "faithfulness round about thee?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_9::
    .string "Thou rulest the raging of the sea:\n"
    .string "when the waves thereof arise, thou\l"
    .string "stillest them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_10::
    .string "Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces,\n"
    .string "as one that is slain; thou hast\l"
    .string "scattered thine enemies with thy\l"
    .string "strong arm.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_11::
    .string "The heavens are thine, the earth\n"
    .string "also is thine: as for the world and\l"
    .string "the fulness thereof, thou hast\l"
    .string "founded them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_12::
    .string "The north and the south thou hast\n"
    .string "created them: Tabor and Hermon\l"
    .string "shall rejoice in thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_13::
    .string "Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is\n"
    .string "thy hand, and high is thy right hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_14::
    .string "Justice and judgment are the\n"
    .string "habitation of thy throne: mercy and\l"
    .string "truth shall go before thy face.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_15::
    .string "Blessed is the people that know\n"
    .string "the joyful sound: they shall walk,\l"
    .string "O LORD, in the light of thy\l"
    .string "countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_16::
    .string "In thy name shall they rejoice\n"
    .string "all the day: and in thy\l"
    .string "righteousness shall they be\l"
    .string "exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_17::
    .string "For thou art the glory of their\n"
    .string "strength: and in thy favour our horn\l"
    .string "shall be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_18::
    .string "For the LORD is our defence; and the\n"
    .string "Holy One of Israel is our king.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_19::
    .string "Then thou spakest in vision to thy\n"
    .string "holy one, and saidst, I have laid\l"
    .string "help upon one that is mighty; I\l"
    .string "have exalted one chosen out of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_20::
    .string "I have found David my servant; with\n"
    .string "my holy oil have I anointed him:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_21::
    .string "With whom my hand shall be\n"
    .string "established: mine arm also shall\l"
    .string "strengthen him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_22::
    .string "The enemy shall not exact upon\n"
    .string "him; nor the son of wickedness\l"
    .string "afflict him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_23::
    .string "And I will beat down his foes\n"
    .string "before his face, and plague them\l"
    .string "that hate him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_24::
    .string "But my faithfulness and my mercy\n"
    .string "shall be with him: and in my name\l"
    .string "shall his horn be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_25::
    .string "I will set his hand also in the\n"
    .string "sea, and his right hand in the rivers.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_26::
    .string "He shall cry unto me, Thou art my\n"
    .string "father, my God, and the rock of my\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_27::
    .string "Also I will make him my firstborn,\n"
    .string "higher than the kings of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_28::
    .string "My mercy will I keep for him for\n"
    .string "evermore, and my covenant shall\l"
    .string "stand fast with him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_29::
    .string "His seed also will I make to\n"
    .string "endure for ever, and his throne as\l"
    .string "the days of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_30::
    .string "If his children forsake my law, and\n"
    .string "walk not in my judgments;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_31::
    .string "If they break my statutes, and keep\n"
    .string "not my commandments;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_32::
    .string "Then will I visit their\n"
    .string "transgression with the rod, and their\l"
    .string "iniquity with stripes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_33::
    .string "Nevertheless my lovingkindness\n"
    .string "will I not utterly take from him,\l"
    .string "nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_34::
    .string "My covenant will I not break, nor\n"
    .string "alter the thing that is gone out of\l"
    .string "my lips.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_35::
    .string "Once have I sworn by my holiness\n"
    .string "that I will not lie unto David.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_36::
    .string "His seed shall endure for ever, and\n"
    .string "his throne as the sun before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_37::
    .string "It shall be established for ever\n"
    .string "as the moon, and as a faithful\l"
    .string "witness in heaven. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_38::
    .string "But thou hast cast off and abhorred,\n"
    .string "thou hast been wroth with thine\l"
    .string "anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_39::
    .string "Thou hast made void the covenant of\n"
    .string "thy servant: thou hast profaned his\l"
    .string "crown by casting it to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_40::
    .string "Thou hast broken down all his\n"
    .string "hedges; thou hast brought his strong\l"
    .string "holds to ruin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_41::
    .string "All that pass by the way spoil\n"
    .string "him: he is a reproach to his\l"
    .string "neighbours.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_42::
    .string "Thou hast set up the right hand of\n"
    .string "his adversaries; thou hast made all\l"
    .string "his enemies to rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_43::
    .string "Thou hast also turned the edge of\n"
    .string "his sword, and hast not made him to\l"
    .string "stand in the battle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_44::
    .string "Thou hast made his glory to cease,\n"
    .string "and cast his throne down to the\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_45::
    .string "The days of his youth hast thou\n"
    .string "shortened: thou hast covered him with\l"
    .string "shame. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_46::
    .string "How long, LORD? wilt thou hide\n"
    .string "thyself for ever? shall thy wrath\l"
    .string "burn like fire?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_47::
    .string "Remember how short my time is:\n"
    .string "wherefore hast thou made all men in\l"
    .string "vain?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_48::
    .string "What man is he that liveth, and\n"
    .string "shall not see death? shall he\l"
    .string "deliver his soul from the hand of\l"
    .string "the grave? Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_49::
    .string "Lord, where are thy former\n"
    .string "lovingkindnesses, which thou swarest\l"
    .string "unto David in thy truth?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_50::
    .string "Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy\n"
    .string "servants; how I do bear in my bosom\l"
    .string "the reproach of all the mighty\l"
    .string "people;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_51::
    .string "Wherewith thine enemies have\n"
    .string "reproached, O LORD; wherewith they\l"
    .string "have reproached the footsteps of\l"
    .string "thine anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_89_52::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD for evermore.\n"
    .string "Amen, and Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_1::
    .string "Lord, thou hast been our dwelling\n"
    .string "place in all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_2::
    .string "Before the mountains were brought\n"
    .string "forth, or ever thou hadst formed the\l"
    .string "earth and the world, even from\l"
    .string "everlasting to everlasting, thou\l"
    .string "art God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_3::
    .string "Thou turnest man to destruction; and\n"
    .string "sayest, Return, ye children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_4::
    .string "For a thousand years in thy sight\n"
    .string "are but as yesterday when it is past,\l"
    .string "and as a watch in the night.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_5::
    .string "Thou carriest them away as with a\n"
    .string "flood; they are as a sleep: in the\l"
    .string "morning they are like grass which\l"
    .string "groweth up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_6::
    .string "In the morning it flourisheth, and\n"
    .string "groweth up; in the evening it is cut\l"
    .string "down, and withereth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_7::
    .string "For we are consumed by thine anger,\n"
    .string "and by thy wrath are we troubled.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_8::
    .string "Thou hast set our iniquities before\n"
    .string "thee, our secret sins in the light of\l"
    .string "thy countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_9::
    .string "For all our days are passed away\n"
    .string "in thy wrath: we spend our years as a\l"
    .string "tale that is told.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_10::
    .string "The days of our years are threescore\n"
    .string "years and ten; and if by reason of\l"
    .string "strength they be fourscore years, yet\l"
    .string "is their strength labour and sorrow;\l"
    .string "for it is soon cut off, and we fly\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_11::
    .string "Who knoweth the power of thine\n"
    .string "anger? even according to thy fear, so\l"
    .string "is thy wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_12::
    .string "So teach us to number our days, that\n"
    .string "we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_13::
    .string "Return, O LORD, how long? and let\n"
    .string "it repent thee concerning thy\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_14::
    .string "O satisfy us early with thy mercy;\n"
    .string "that we may rejoice and be glad all\l"
    .string "our days.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_15::
    .string "Make us glad according to the days\n"
    .string "wherein thou hast afflicted us, and\l"
    .string "the years wherein we have seen evil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_16::
    .string "Let thy work appear unto thy\n"
    .string "servants, and thy glory unto their\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_90_17::
    .string "And let the beauty of the LORD our\n"
    .string "God be upon us: and establish thou\l"
    .string "the work of our hands upon us; yea,\l"
    .string "the work of our hands establish thou\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_1::
    .string "He that dwelleth in the secret\n"
    .string "place of the most High shall abide\l"
    .string "under the shadow of the Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_2::
    .string "I will say of the LORD, He is my\n"
    .string "refuge and my fortress: my God; in\l"
    .string "him will I trust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_3::
    .string "Surely he shall deliver thee from\n"
    .string "the snare of the fowler, and from the\l"
    .string "noisome pestilence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_4::
    .string "He shall cover thee with his\n"
    .string "feathers, and under his wings shalt\l"
    .string "thou trust: his truth shall be thy\l"
    .string "shield and buckler.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_5::
    .string "Thou shalt not be afraid for the\n"
    .string "terror by night; nor for the arrow\l"
    .string "that flieth by day;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_6::
    .string "Nor for the pestilence that\n"
    .string "walketh in darkness; nor for the\l"
    .string "destruction that wasteth at noonday.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_7::
    .string "A thousand shall fall at thy\n"
    .string "side, and ten thousand at thy right\l"
    .string "hand; but it shall not come nigh\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_8::
    .string "Only with thine eyes shalt thou\n"
    .string "behold and see the reward of the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_9::
    .string "Because thou hast made the LORD,\n"
    .string "which is my refuge, even the most\l"
    .string "High, thy habitation;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_10::
    .string "There shall no evil befall thee,\n"
    .string "neither shall any plague come nigh\l"
    .string "thy dwelling.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_11::
    .string "For he shall give his angels\n"
    .string "charge over thee, to keep thee in\l"
    .string "all thy ways.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_12::
    .string "They shall bear thee up in their\n"
    .string "hands, lest thou dash thy foot\l"
    .string "against a stone.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_13::
    .string "Thou shalt tread upon the lion and\n"
    .string "adder: the young lion and the dragon\l"
    .string "shalt thou trample under feet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_14::
    .string "Because he hath set his love upon\n"
    .string "me, therefore will I deliver him: I\l"
    .string "will set him on high, because he\l"
    .string "hath known my name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_15::
    .string "He shall call upon me, and I\n"
    .string "will answer him: I will be with him\l"
    .string "in trouble; I will deliver him,\l"
    .string "and honour him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_91_16::
    .string "With long life will I satisfy\n"
    .string "him, and shew him my salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_1::
    .string "It is a good thing to give thanks\n"
    .string "unto the Lord, and to sing praises\l"
    .string "unto thy name, O most High:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_2::
    .string "To shew forth thy lovingkindness in\n"
    .string "the morning, and thy faithfulness\l"
    .string "every night,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_3::
    .string "Upon an instrument of ten strings,\n"
    .string "and upon the psaltery; upon the\l"
    .string "harp with a solemn sound.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_4::
    .string "For thou, LORD, hast made me glad\n"
    .string "through thy work: I will triumph in\l"
    .string "the works of thy hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_5::
    .string "O LORD, how great are thy works! and\n"
    .string "thy thoughts are very deep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_6::
    .string "A brutish man knoweth not; neither\n"
    .string "doth a fool understand this.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_7::
    .string "When the wicked spring as the\n"
    .string "grass, and when all the workers of\l"
    .string "iniquity do flourish; it is that\l"
    .string "they shall be destroyed for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_8::
    .string "But thou, LORD, art most high for\n"
    .string "evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_9::
    .string "For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for,\n"
    .string "lo, thine enemies shall perish;\l"
    .string "all the workers of iniquity shall\l"
    .string "be scattered.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_10::
    .string "But my horn shalt thou exalt like\n"
    .string "the horn of an unicorn: I shall be\l"
    .string "anointed with fresh oil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_11::
    .string "Mine eye also shall see my desire\n"
    .string "on mine enemies, and mine ears shall\l"
    .string "hear my desire of the wicked that\l"
    .string "rise up against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_12::
    .string "The righteous shall flourish\n"
    .string "like the palm tree: he shall grow\l"
    .string "like a cedar in Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_13::
    .string "Those that be planted in the house\n"
    .string "of the LORD shall flourish in the\l"
    .string "courts of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_14::
    .string "They shall still bring forth\n"
    .string "fruit in old age; they shall be fat\l"
    .string "and flourishing;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_92_15::
    .string "To shew that the LORD is upright: he\n"
    .string "is my rock, and there is no\l"
    .string "unrighteousness in him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_93_1::
    .string "The LORD reigneth, he is clothed\n"
    .string "with majesty; the LORD is clothed\l"
    .string "with strength, wherewith he hath\l"
    .string "girded himself: the world also is\l"
    .string "stablished, that it cannot be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_93_2::
    .string "Thy throne is established of old:\n"
    .string "thou art from everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_93_3::
    .string "The floods have lifted up, O LORD,\n"
    .string "the floods have lifted up their\l"
    .string "voice; the floods lift up their\l"
    .string "waves.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_93_4::
    .string "The LORD on high is mightier than\n"
    .string "the noise of many waters, yea, than\l"
    .string "the mighty waves of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_93_5::
    .string "Thy testimonies are very sure:\n"
    .string "holiness becometh thine house, O\l"
    .string "LORD, for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_1::
    .string "O Lord God, to whom vengeance\n"
    .string "belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance\l"
    .string "belongeth, shew thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_2::
    .string "Lift up thyself, thou judge of the\n"
    .string "earth: render a reward to the proud.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_3::
    .string "LORD, how long shall the wicked,\n"
    .string "how long shall the wicked triumph?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_4::
    .string "How long shall they utter and\n"
    .string "speak hard things? and all the\l"
    .string "workers of iniquity boast\l"
    .string "themselves?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_5::
    .string "They break in pieces thy people,\n"
    .string "O LORD, and afflict thine heritage.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_6::
    .string "They slay the widow and the\n"
    .string "stranger, and murder the fatherless.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_7::
    .string "Yet they say, The LORD shall not\n"
    .string "see, neither shall the God of Jacob\l"
    .string "regard it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_8::
    .string "Understand, ye brutish among the\n"
    .string "people: and ye fools, when will ye\l"
    .string "be wise?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_9::
    .string "He that planted the ear, shall he\n"
    .string "not hear? he that formed the eye,\l"
    .string "shall he not see?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_10::
    .string "He that chastiseth the heathen,\n"
    .string "shall not he correct? he that\l"
    .string "teacheth man knowledge, shall not\l"
    .string "he know?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_11::
    .string "The LORD knoweth the thoughts of\n"
    .string "man, that they are vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_12::
    .string "Blessed is the man whom thou\n"
    .string "chastenest, O LORD, and teachest him\l"
    .string "out of thy law;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_13::
    .string "That thou mayest give him rest from\n"
    .string "the days of adversity, until the pit\l"
    .string "be digged for the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_14::
    .string "For the LORD will not cast off his\n"
    .string "people, neither will he forsake\l"
    .string "his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_15::
    .string "But judgment shall return unto\n"
    .string "righteousness: and all the upright\l"
    .string "in heart shall follow it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_16::
    .string "Who will rise up for me against\n"
    .string "the evildoers? or who will stand\l"
    .string "up for me against the workers of\l"
    .string "iniquity?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_17::
    .string "Unless the LORD had been my help,\n"
    .string "my soul had almost dwelt in\l"
    .string "silence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_18::
    .string "When I said, My foot slippeth; thy\n"
    .string "mercy, O LORD, held me up.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_19::
    .string "In the multitude of my thoughts\n"
    .string "within me thy comforts delight my\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_20::
    .string "Shall the throne of iniquity have\n"
    .string "fellowship with thee, which\l"
    .string "frameth mischief by a law?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_21::
    .string "They gather themselves together\n"
    .string "against the soul of the righteous,\l"
    .string "and condemn the innocent blood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_22::
    .string "But the LORD is my defence; and my\n"
    .string "God is the rock of my refuge.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_94_23::
    .string "And he shall bring upon them their\n"
    .string "own iniquity, and shall cut them off\l"
    .string "in their own wickedness; yea, the\l"
    .string "LORD our God shall cut them off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_1::
    .string "O come, let us sing unto the LORD:\n"
    .string "let us make a joyful noise to the\l"
    .string "rock of our salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_2::
    .string "Let us come before his presence\n"
    .string "with thanksgiving, and make a joyful\l"
    .string "noise unto him with psalms.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_3::
    .string "For the LORD is a great God, and a\n"
    .string "great King above all gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_4::
    .string "In his hand are the deep places of\n"
    .string "the earth: the strength of the hills\l"
    .string "is his also.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_5::
    .string "The sea is his, and he made it: and\n"
    .string "his hands formed the dry land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_6::
    .string "O come, let us worship and bow\n"
    .string "down: let us kneel before the LORD\l"
    .string "our maker.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_7::
    .string "For he is our God; and we are the\n"
    .string "people of his pasture, and the\l"
    .string "sheep of his hand. To day if ye will\l"
    .string "hear his voice,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_8::
    .string "Harden not your heart, as in the\n"
    .string "provocation, and as in the day of\l"
    .string "temptation in the wilderness:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_9::
    .string "When your fathers tempted me,\n"
    .string "proved me, and saw my work.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_10::
    .string "Forty years long was I grieved with\n"
    .string "this generation, and said, It is a\l"
    .string "people that do err in their heart,\l"
    .string "and they have not known my ways:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_95_11::
    .string "Unto whom I sware in my wrath that\n"
    .string "they should not enter into my rest.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_1::
    .string "O sing unto the LORD a new song: sing\n"
    .string "unto the LORD, all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_2::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD, bless his name;\n"
    .string "shew forth his salvation from day to\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_3::
    .string "Declare his glory among the\n"
    .string "heathen, his wonders among all\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_4::
    .string "For the LORD is great, and greatly\n"
    .string "to be praised: he is to be feared\l"
    .string "above all gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_5::
    .string "For all the gods of the nations are\n"
    .string "idols: but the LORD made the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_6::
    .string "Honour and majesty are before him:\n"
    .string "strength and beauty are in his\l"
    .string "sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_7::
    .string "Give unto the LORD, O ye kindreds of\n"
    .string "the people, give unto the LORD\l"
    .string "glory and strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_8::
    .string "Give unto the LORD the glory due\n"
    .string "unto his name: bring an offering, and\l"
    .string "come into his courts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_9::
    .string "O worship the LORD in the beauty of\n"
    .string "holiness: fear before him, all the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_10::
    .string "Say among the heathen that the LORD\n"
    .string "reigneth: the world also shall be\l"
    .string "established that it shall not be\l"
    .string "moved: he shall judge the people\l"
    .string "righteously.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_11::
    .string "Let the heavens rejoice, and let\n"
    .string "the earth be glad; let the sea roar,\l"
    .string "and the fulness thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_12::
    .string "Let the field be joyful, and all\n"
    .string "that is therein: then shall all\l"
    .string "the trees of the wood rejoice$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_96_13::
    .string "Before the LORD: for he cometh, for\n"
    .string "he cometh to judge the earth: he\l"
    .string "shall judge the world with\l"
    .string "righteousness, and the people with\l"
    .string "his truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_1::
    .string "The LORD reigneth; let the earth\n"
    .string "rejoice; let the multitude of isles\l"
    .string "be glad thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_2::
    .string "Clouds and darkness are round about\n"
    .string "him: righteousness and judgment are\l"
    .string "the habitation of his throne.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_3::
    .string "A fire goeth before him, and burneth\n"
    .string "up his enemies round about.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_4::
    .string "His lightnings enlightened the\n"
    .string "world: the earth saw, and trembled.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_5::
    .string "The hills melted like wax at the\n"
    .string "presence of the LORD, at the\l"
    .string "presence of the Lord of the whole\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_6::
    .string "The heavens declare his\n"
    .string "righteousness, and all the people\l"
    .string "see his glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_7::
    .string "Confounded be all they that serve\n"
    .string "graven images, that boast themselves\l"
    .string "of idols: worship him, all ye gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_8::
    .string "Zion heard, and was glad; and the\n"
    .string "daughters of Judah rejoiced because\l"
    .string "of thy judgments, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_9::
    .string "For thou, LORD, art high above all\n"
    .string "the earth: thou art exalted far\l"
    .string "above all gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_10::
    .string "Ye that love the LORD, hate evil:\n"
    .string "he preserveth the souls of his\l"
    .string "saints; he delivereth them out of\l"
    .string "the hand of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_11::
    .string "Light is sown for the righteous, and\n"
    .string "gladness for the upright in heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_97_12::
    .string "Rejoice in the LORD, ye righteous;\n"
    .string "and give thanks at the remembrance of\l"
    .string "his holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_1::
    .string "O sing unto the LORD a new song; for\n"
    .string "he hath done marvellous things: his\l"
    .string "right hand, and his holy arm, hath\l"
    .string "gotten him the victory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_2::
    .string "The LORD hath made known his\n"
    .string "salvation: his righteousness hath he\l"
    .string "openly shewed in the sight of the\l"
    .string "heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_3::
    .string "He hath remembered his mercy and his\n"
    .string "truth toward the house of Israel:\l"
    .string "all the ends of the earth have seen\l"
    .string "the salvation of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_4::
    .string "Make a joyful noise unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "all the earth: make a loud noise,\l"
    .string "and rejoice, and sing praise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_5::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD with the harp;\n"
    .string "with the harp, and the voice of a\l"
    .string "psalm.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_6::
    .string "With trumpets and sound of cornet\n"
    .string "make a joyful noise before the LORD,\l"
    .string "the King.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_7::
    .string "Let the sea roar, and the fulness\n"
    .string "thereof; the world, and they that\l"
    .string "dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_8::
    .string "Let the floods clap their hands:\n"
    .string "let the hills be joyful together$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_98_9::
    .string "Before the LORD; for he cometh to\n"
    .string "judge the earth: with righteousness\l"
    .string "shall he judge the world, and the\l"
    .string "people with equity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_1::
    .string "The LORD reigneth; let the people\n"
    .string "tremble: he sitteth between the\l"
    .string "cherubims; let the earth be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_2::
    .string "The LORD is great in Zion; and he is\n"
    .string "high above all the people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_3::
    .string "Let them praise thy great and\n"
    .string "terrible name; for it is holy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_4::
    .string "The king’s strength also loveth\n"
    .string "judgment; thou dost establish\l"
    .string "equity, thou executest judgment and\l"
    .string "righteousness in Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_5::
    .string "Exalt ye the LORD our God, and\n"
    .string "worship at his footstool; for he is\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_6::
    .string "Moses and Aaron among his priests,\n"
    .string "and Samuel among them that call\l"
    .string "upon his name; they called upon\l"
    .string "the LORD, and he answered them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_7::
    .string "He spake unto them in the cloudy\n"
    .string "pillar: they kept his testimonies,\l"
    .string "and the ordinance that he gave them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_8::
    .string "Thou answeredst them, O LORD our\n"
    .string "God: thou wast a God that forgavest\l"
    .string "them, though thou tookest vengeance\l"
    .string "of their inventions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_99_9::
    .string "Exalt the LORD our God, and worship\n"
    .string "at his holy hill; for the LORD our\l"
    .string "God is holy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_100_1::
    .string "Make a joyful noise unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "all ye lands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_100_2::
    .string "Serve the LORD with gladness: come\n"
    .string "before his presence with singing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_100_3::
    .string "Know ye that the LORD he is God: it\n"
    .string "is he that hath made us, and not we\l"
    .string "ourselves; we are his people, and\l"
    .string "the sheep of his pasture.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_100_4::
    .string "Enter into his gates with\n"
    .string "thanksgiving, and into his courts\l"
    .string "with praise: be thankful unto him,\l"
    .string "and bless his name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_100_5::
    .string "For the LORD is good; his mercy is\n"
    .string "everlasting; and his truth endureth\l"
    .string "to all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_1::
    .string "I will sing of mercy and judgment:\n"
    .string "unto thee, O LORD, will I sing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_2::
    .string "I will behave myself wisely in a\n"
    .string "perfect way. O when wilt thou come\l"
    .string "unto me? I will walk within my\l"
    .string "house with a perfect heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_3::
    .string "I will set no wicked thing before\n"
    .string "mine eyes: I hate the work of them\l"
    .string "that turn aside; it shall not\l"
    .string "cleave to me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_4::
    .string "A froward heart shall depart from\n"
    .string "me: I will not know a wicked person.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_5::
    .string "Whoso privily slandereth his\n"
    .string "neighbour, him will I cut off: him\l"
    .string "that hath an high look and a proud\l"
    .string "heart will not I suffer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_6::
    .string "Mine eyes shall be upon the\n"
    .string "faithful of the land, that they may\l"
    .string "dwell with me: he that walketh in a\l"
    .string "perfect way, he shall serve me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_7::
    .string "He that worketh deceit shall not\n"
    .string "dwell within my house: he that\l"
    .string "telleth lies shall not tarry in\l"
    .string "my sight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_101_8::
    .string "I will early destroy all the\n"
    .string "wicked of the land; that I may cut\l"
    .string "off all wicked doers from the city\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_1::
    .string "Hear my prayer, O LORD, and let my\n"
    .string "cry come unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_2::
    .string "Hide not thy face from me in the day\n"
    .string "when I am in trouble; incline thine\l"
    .string "ear unto me: in the day when I call\l"
    .string "answer me speedily.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_3::
    .string "For my days are consumed like\n"
    .string "smoke, and my bones are burned as an\l"
    .string "hearth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_4::
    .string "My heart is smitten, and withered\n"
    .string "like grass; so that I forget to eat my\l"
    .string "bread.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_5::
    .string "By reason of the voice of my\n"
    .string "groaning my bones cleave to my skin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_6::
    .string "I am like a pelican of the\n"
    .string "wilderness: I am like an owl of the\l"
    .string "desert.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_7::
    .string "I watch, and am as a sparrow alone\n"
    .string "upon the house top.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_8::
    .string "Mine enemies reproach me all the\n"
    .string "day; and they that are mad against me\l"
    .string "are sworn against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_9::
    .string "For I have eaten ashes like bread,\n"
    .string "and mingled my drink with weeping.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_10::
    .string "Because of thine indignation and\n"
    .string "thy wrath: for thou hast lifted me\l"
    .string "up, and cast me down.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_11::
    .string "My days are like a shadow that\n"
    .string "declineth; and I am withered like\l"
    .string "grass.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_12::
    .string "But thou, O LORD, shall endure for\n"
    .string "ever; and thy remembrance unto all\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_13::
    .string "Thou shalt arise, and have mercy\n"
    .string "upon Zion: for the time to favour\l"
    .string "her, yea, the set time, is come.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_14::
    .string "For thy servants take pleasure in\n"
    .string "her stones, and favour the dust\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_15::
    .string "So the heathen shall fear the name\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and all the kings of\l"
    .string "the earth thy glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_16::
    .string "When the LORD shall build up\n"
    .string "Zion, he shall appear in his\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_17::
    .string "He will regard the prayer of the\n"
    .string "destitute, and not despise their\l"
    .string "prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_18::
    .string "This shall be written for the\n"
    .string "generation to come: and the people\l"
    .string "which shall be created shall\l"
    .string "praise the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_19::
    .string "For he hath looked down from the\n"
    .string "height of his sanctuary; from heaven\l"
    .string "did the LORD behold the earth;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_20::
    .string "To hear the groaning of the\n"
    .string "prisoner; to loose those that are\l"
    .string "appointed to death;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_21::
    .string "To declare the name of the LORD in\n"
    .string "Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_22::
    .string "When the people are gathered\n"
    .string "together, and the kingdoms, to serve\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_23::
    .string "He weakened my strength in the way;\n"
    .string "he shortened my days.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_24::
    .string "I said, O my God, take me not away in\n"
    .string "the midst of my days: thy years are\l"
    .string "throughout all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_25::
    .string "Of old hast thou laid the\n"
    .string "foundation of the earth: and the\l"
    .string "heavens are the work of thy hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_26::
    .string "They shall perish, but thou shalt\n"
    .string "endure: yea, all of them shall wax\l"
    .string "old like a garment; as a vesture\l"
    .string "shalt thou change them, and they\l"
    .string "shall be changed:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_27::
    .string "But thou art the same, and thy years\n"
    .string "shall have no end.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_102_28::
    .string "The children of thy servants\n"
    .string "shall continue, and their seed\l"
    .string "shall be established before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_1::
    .string "Bless the LORD, O my soul: and all\n"
    .string "that is within me, bless his holy\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_2::
    .string "Bless the LORD, O my soul, and\n"
    .string "forget not all his benefits:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_3::
    .string "Who forgiveth all thine\n"
    .string "iniquities; who healeth all thy\l"
    .string "diseases;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_4::
    .string "Who redeemeth thy life from\n"
    .string "destruction; who crowneth thee with\l"
    .string "lovingkindness and tender mercies;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_5::
    .string "Who satisfieth thy mouth with good\n"
    .string "things; so that thy youth is renewed\l"
    .string "like the eagle’s.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_6::
    .string "The LORD executeth righteousness\n"
    .string "and judgment for all that are\l"
    .string "oppressed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_7::
    .string "He made known his ways unto Moses,\n"
    .string "his acts unto the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_8::
    .string "The LORD is merciful and gracious,\n"
    .string "slow to anger, and plenteous in\l"
    .string "mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_9::
    .string "He will not always chide: neither\n"
    .string "will he keep his anger for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_10::
    .string "He hath not dealt with us after our\n"
    .string "sins; nor rewarded us according to\l"
    .string "our iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_11::
    .string "For as the heaven is high above the\n"
    .string "earth, so great is his mercy toward\l"
    .string "them that fear him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_12::
    .string "As far as the east is from the west,\n"
    .string "so far hath he removed our\l"
    .string "transgressions from us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_13::
    .string "Like as a father pitieth his\n"
    .string "children, so the LORD pitieth them\l"
    .string "that fear him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_14::
    .string "For he knoweth our frame; he\n"
    .string "remembereth that we are dust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_15::
    .string "As for man, his days are as grass: as\n"
    .string "a flower of the field, so he\l"
    .string "flourisheth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_16::
    .string "For the wind passeth over it, and it\n"
    .string "is gone; and the place thereof\l"
    .string "shall know it no more.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_17::
    .string "But the mercy of the LORD is from\n"
    .string "everlasting to everlasting upon\l"
    .string "them that fear him, and his\l"
    .string "righteousness unto children’s\l"
    .string "children;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_18::
    .string "To such as keep his covenant, and to\n"
    .string "those that remember his commandments\l"
    .string "to do them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_19::
    .string "The LORD hath prepared his throne\n"
    .string "in the heavens; and his kingdom\l"
    .string "ruleth over all.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_20::
    .string "Bless the LORD, ye his angels, that\n"
    .string "excel in strength, that do his\l"
    .string "commandments, hearkening unto the\l"
    .string "voice of his word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_21::
    .string "Bless ye the LORD, all ye his\n"
    .string "hosts; ye ministers of his, that do\l"
    .string "his pleasure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_103_22::
    .string "Bless the LORD, all his works in\n"
    .string "all places of his dominion: bless\l"
    .string "the LORD, O my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_1::
    .string "Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD\n"
    .string "my God, thou art very great; thou art\l"
    .string "clothed with honour and majesty.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_2::
    .string "Who coverest thyself with light as\n"
    .string "with a garment: who stretchest out\l"
    .string "the heavens like a curtain:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_3::
    .string "Who layeth the beams of his\n"
    .string "chambers in the waters: who maketh\l"
    .string "the clouds his chariot: who walketh\l"
    .string "upon the wings of the wind:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_4::
    .string "Who maketh his angels spirits; his\n"
    .string "ministers a flaming fire:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_5::
    .string "Who laid the foundations of the\n"
    .string "earth, that it should not be removed\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_6::
    .string "Thou coveredst it with the deep as\n"
    .string "with a garment: the waters stood\l"
    .string "above the mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_7::
    .string "At thy rebuke they fled; at the\n"
    .string "voice of thy thunder they hasted away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_8::
    .string "They go up by the mountains; they go\n"
    .string "down by the valleys unto the place\l"
    .string "which thou hast founded for them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_9::
    .string "Thou hast set a bound that they may\n"
    .string "not pass over; that they turn not\l"
    .string "again to cover the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_10::
    .string "He sendeth the springs into the\n"
    .string "valleys, which run among the hills.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_11::
    .string "They give drink to every beast of\n"
    .string "the field: the wild asses quench\l"
    .string "their thirst.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_12::
    .string "By them shall the fowls of the\n"
    .string "heaven have their habitation, which\l"
    .string "sing among the branches.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_13::
    .string "He watereth the hills from his\n"
    .string "chambers: the earth is satisfied with\l"
    .string "the fruit of thy works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_14::
    .string "He causeth the grass to grow for the\n"
    .string "cattle, and herb for the service of\l"
    .string "man: that he may bring forth food out\l"
    .string "of the earth;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_15::
    .string "And wine that maketh glad the heart\n"
    .string "of man, and oil to make his face to\l"
    .string "shine, and bread which strengtheneth\l"
    .string "man’s heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_16::
    .string "The trees of the LORD are full of\n"
    .string "sap; the cedars of Lebanon, which he\l"
    .string "hath planted;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_17::
    .string "Where the birds make their nests: as\n"
    .string "for the stork, the fir trees are her\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_18::
    .string "The high hills are a refuge for the\n"
    .string "wild goats; and the rocks for the\l"
    .string "conies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_19::
    .string "He appointed the moon for seasons:\n"
    .string "the sun knoweth his going down.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_20::
    .string "Thou makest darkness, and it is\n"
    .string "night: wherein all the beasts of the\l"
    .string "forest do creep forth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_21::
    .string "The young lions roar after their\n"
    .string "prey, and seek their meat from God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_22::
    .string "The sun ariseth, they gather\n"
    .string "themselves together, and lay them\l"
    .string "down in their dens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_23::
    .string "Man goeth forth unto his work and to\n"
    .string "his labour until the evening.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_24::
    .string "O LORD, how manifold are thy works!\n"
    .string "in wisdom hast thou made them all:\l"
    .string "the earth is full of thy riches.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_25::
    .string "So is this great and wide sea,\n"
    .string "wherein are things creeping\l"
    .string "innumerable, both small and great\l"
    .string "beasts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_26::
    .string "There go the ships: there is that\n"
    .string "leviathan, whom thou hast made to\l"
    .string "play therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_27::
    .string "These wait all upon thee; that\n"
    .string "thou mayest give them their meat in\l"
    .string "due season.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_28::
    .string "That thou givest them they gather:\n"
    .string "thou openest thine hand, they are\l"
    .string "filled with good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_29::
    .string "Thou hidest thy face, they are\n"
    .string "troubled: thou takest away their\l"
    .string "breath, they die, and return to their\l"
    .string "dust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_30::
    .string "Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they\n"
    .string "are created: and thou renewest the\l"
    .string "face of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_31::
    .string "The glory of the LORD shall endure\n"
    .string "for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in\l"
    .string "his works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_32::
    .string "He looketh on the earth, and it\n"
    .string "trembleth: he toucheth the hills,\l"
    .string "and they smoke.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_33::
    .string "I will sing unto the LORD as long\n"
    .string "as I live: I will sing praise to my\l"
    .string "God while I have my being.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_34::
    .string "My meditation of him shall be\n"
    .string "sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_104_35::
    .string "Let the sinners be consumed out of\n"
    .string "the earth, and let the wicked be no\l"
    .string "more. Bless thou the LORD, O my\l"
    .string "soul. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_1::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD; call\n"
    .string "upon his name: make known his deeds\l"
    .string "among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_2::
    .string "Sing unto him, sing psalms unto\n"
    .string "him: talk ye of all his wondrous\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_3::
    .string "Glory ye in his holy name: let the\n"
    .string "heart of them rejoice that seek the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_4::
    .string "Seek the LORD, and his strength:\n"
    .string "seek his face evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_5::
    .string "Remember his marvellous works that\n"
    .string "he hath done; his wonders, and the\l"
    .string "judgments of his mouth;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_6::
    .string "O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye\n"
    .string "children of Jacob his chosen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_7::
    .string "He is the LORD our God: his\n"
    .string "judgments are in all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_8::
    .string "He hath remembered his covenant for\n"
    .string "ever, the word which he commanded to\l"
    .string "a thousand generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_9::
    .string "Which covenant he made with Abraham,\n"
    .string "and his oath unto Isaac;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_10::
    .string "And confirmed the same unto Jacob\n"
    .string "for a law, and to Israel for an\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_11::
    .string "Saying, Unto thee will I give the\n"
    .string "land of Canaan, the lot of your\l"
    .string "inheritance:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_12::
    .string "When they were but a few men in\n"
    .string "number; yea, very few, and strangers\l"
    .string "in it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_13::
    .string "When they went from one nation to\n"
    .string "another, from one kingdom to another\l"
    .string "people;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_14::
    .string "He suffered no man to do them wrong:\n"
    .string "yea, he reproved kings for their\l"
    .string "sakes;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_15::
    .string "Saying, Touch not mine anointed, and\n"
    .string "do my prophets no harm.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_16::
    .string "Moreover he called for a famine\n"
    .string "upon the land: he brake the whole\l"
    .string "staff of bread.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_17::
    .string "He sent a man before them, even\n"
    .string "Joseph, who was sold for a servant:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_18::
    .string "Whose feet they hurt with fetters:\n"
    .string "he was laid in iron:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_19::
    .string "Until the time that his word came:\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD tried him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_20::
    .string "The king sent and loosed him; even\n"
    .string "the ruler of the people, and let\l"
    .string "him go free.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_21::
    .string "He made him lord of his house, and\n"
    .string "ruler of all his substance:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_22::
    .string "To bind his princes at his\n"
    .string "pleasure; and teach his senators\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_23::
    .string "Israel also came into Egypt; and\n"
    .string "Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_24::
    .string "And he increased his people\n"
    .string "greatly; and made them stronger than\l"
    .string "their enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_25::
    .string "He turned their heart to hate his\n"
    .string "people, to deal subtilly with his\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_26::
    .string "He sent Moses his servant; and Aaron\n"
    .string "whom he had chosen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_27::
    .string "They shewed his signs among them,\n"
    .string "and wonders in the land of Ham.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_28::
    .string "He sent darkness, and made it dark;\n"
    .string "and they rebelled not against his\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_29::
    .string "He turned their waters into blood,\n"
    .string "and slew their fish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_30::
    .string "Their land brought forth frogs in\n"
    .string "abundance, in the chambers of their\l"
    .string "kings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_31::
    .string "He spake, and there came divers\n"
    .string "sorts of flies, and lice in all\l"
    .string "their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_32::
    .string "He gave them hail for rain, and\n"
    .string "flaming fire in their land.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_33::
    .string "He smote their vines also and their\n"
    .string "fig trees; and brake the trees of\l"
    .string "their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_34::
    .string "He spake, and the locusts came, and\n"
    .string "caterpillers, and that without\l"
    .string "number,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_35::
    .string "And did eat up all the herbs in\n"
    .string "their land, and devoured the fruit\l"
    .string "of their ground.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_36::
    .string "He smote also all the firstborn in\n"
    .string "their land, the chief of all their\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_37::
    .string "He brought them forth also with\n"
    .string "silver and gold: and there was not\l"
    .string "one feeble person among their\l"
    .string "tribes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_38::
    .string "Egypt was glad when they departed:\n"
    .string "for the fear of them fell upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_39::
    .string "He spread a cloud for a covering;\n"
    .string "and fire to give light in the night.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_40::
    .string "The people asked, and he brought\n"
    .string "quails, and satisfied them with the\l"
    .string "bread of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_41::
    .string "He opened the rock, and the waters\n"
    .string "gushed out; they ran in the dry\l"
    .string "places like a river.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_42::
    .string "For he remembered his holy\n"
    .string "promise, and Abraham his servant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_43::
    .string "And he brought forth his people\n"
    .string "with joy, and his chosen with\l"
    .string "gladness:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_44::
    .string "And gave them the lands of the\n"
    .string "heathen: and they inherited the\l"
    .string "labour of the people;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_105_45::
    .string "That they might observe his\n"
    .string "statutes, and keep his laws. Praise\l"
    .string "ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks\n"
    .string "unto the LORD; for he is good: for his\l"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_2::
    .string "Who can utter the mighty acts of the\n"
    .string "LORD? who can shew forth all his\l"
    .string "praise?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_3::
    .string "Blessed are they that keep\n"
    .string "judgment, and he that doeth\l"
    .string "righteousness at all times.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_4::
    .string "Remember me, O LORD, with the favour\n"
    .string "that thou bearest unto thy people:\l"
    .string "O visit me with thy salvation;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_5::
    .string "That I may see the good of thy\n"
    .string "chosen, that I may rejoice in the\l"
    .string "gladness of thy nation, that I may\l"
    .string "glory with thine inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_6::
    .string "We have sinned with our fathers, we\n"
    .string "have committed iniquity, we have done\l"
    .string "wickedly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_7::
    .string "Our fathers understood not thy\n"
    .string "wonders in Egypt; they remembered\l"
    .string "not the multitude of thy mercies;\l"
    .string "but provoked him at the sea, even at\l"
    .string "the Red sea.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_8::
    .string "Nevertheless he saved them for his\n"
    .string "name’s sake, that he might make his\l"
    .string "mighty power to be known.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_9::
    .string "He rebuked the Red sea also, and it\n"
    .string "was dried up: so he led them through\l"
    .string "the depths, as through the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_10::
    .string "And he saved them from the hand of\n"
    .string "him that hated them, and redeemed\l"
    .string "them from the hand of the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_11::
    .string "And the waters covered their\n"
    .string "enemies: there was not one of them\l"
    .string "left.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_12::
    .string "Then believed they his words; they\n"
    .string "sang his praise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_13::
    .string "They soon forgat his works; they\n"
    .string "waited not for his counsel:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_14::
    .string "But lusted exceedingly in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and tempted God in the\l"
    .string "desert.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_15::
    .string "And he gave them their request; but\n"
    .string "sent leanness into their soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_16::
    .string "They envied Moses also in the camp,\n"
    .string "and Aaron the saint of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_17::
    .string "The earth opened and swallowed up\n"
    .string "Dathan and covered the company of\l"
    .string "Abiram.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_18::
    .string "And a fire was kindled in their\n"
    .string "company; the flame burned up the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_19::
    .string "They made a calf in Horeb, and\n"
    .string "worshipped the molten image.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_20::
    .string "Thus they changed their glory into\n"
    .string "the similitude of an ox that eateth\l"
    .string "grass.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_21::
    .string "They forgat God their saviour, which\n"
    .string "had done great things in Egypt;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_22::
    .string "Wondrous works in the land of Ham,\n"
    .string "and terrible things by the Red sea.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_23::
    .string "Therefore he said that he would\n"
    .string "destroy them, had not Moses his\l"
    .string "chosen stood before him in the\l"
    .string "breach, to turn away his wrath, lest\l"
    .string "he should destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_24::
    .string "Yea, they despised the pleasant\n"
    .string "land, they believed not his word:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_25::
    .string "But murmured in their tents, and\n"
    .string "hearkened not unto the voice of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_26::
    .string "Therefore he lifted up his hand\n"
    .string "against them, to overthrow them in\l"
    .string "the wilderness:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_27::
    .string "To overthrow their seed also among\n"
    .string "the nations, and to scatter them in\l"
    .string "the lands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_28::
    .string "They joined themselves also unto\n"
    .string "Baalpeor, and ate the sacrifices of\l"
    .string "the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_29::
    .string "Thus they provoked him to anger\n"
    .string "with their inventions: and the\l"
    .string "plague brake in upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_30::
    .string "Then stood up Phinehas, and\n"
    .string "executed judgment: and so the\l"
    .string "plague was stayed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_31::
    .string "And that was counted unto him for\n"
    .string "righteousness unto all generations\l"
    .string "for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_32::
    .string "They angered him also at the waters\n"
    .string "of strife, so that it went ill with\l"
    .string "Moses for their sakes:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_33::
    .string "Because they provoked his spirit,\n"
    .string "so that he spake unadvisedly with\l"
    .string "his lips.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_34::
    .string "They did not destroy the nations,\n"
    .string "concerning whom the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "them:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_35::
    .string "But were mingled among the heathen,\n"
    .string "and learned their works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_36::
    .string "And they served their idols: which\n"
    .string "were a snare unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_37::
    .string "Yea, they sacrificed their sons and\n"
    .string "their daughters unto devils,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_38::
    .string "And shed innocent blood, even the\n"
    .string "blood of their sons and of their\l"
    .string "daughters, whom they sacrificed unto\l"
    .string "the idols of Canaan: and the land\l"
    .string "was polluted with blood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_39::
    .string "Thus were they defiled with their\n"
    .string "own works, and went a whoring with\l"
    .string "their own inventions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_40::
    .string "Therefore was the wrath of the LORD\n"
    .string "kindled against his people,\l"
    .string "insomuch that he abhorred his own\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_41::
    .string "And he gave them into the hand of\n"
    .string "the heathen; and they that hated them\l"
    .string "ruled over them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_42::
    .string "Their enemies also oppressed\n"
    .string "them, and they were brought into\l"
    .string "subjection under their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_43::
    .string "Many times did he deliver them; but\n"
    .string "they provoked him with their\l"
    .string "counsel, and were brought low for\l"
    .string "their iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_44::
    .string "Nevertheless he regarded their\n"
    .string "affliction, when he heard their cry:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_45::
    .string "And he remembered for them his\n"
    .string "covenant, and repented according to\l"
    .string "the multitude of his mercies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_46::
    .string "He made them also to be pitied of\n"
    .string "all those that carried them\l"
    .string "captives.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_47::
    .string "Save us, O LORD our God, and gather\n"
    .string "us from among the heathen, to give\l"
    .string "thanks unto thy holy name, and to\l"
    .string "triumph in thy praise.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_106_48::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD God of Israel\n"
    .string "from everlasting to everlasting:\l"
    .string "and let all the people say, Amen.\l"
    .string "Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_1::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD, for he\n"
    .string "is good: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_2::
    .string "Let the redeemed of the LORD say so,\n"
    .string "whom he hath redeemed from the hand\l"
    .string "of the enemy;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_3::
    .string "And gathered them out of the lands,\n"
    .string "from the east, and from the west,\l"
    .string "from the north, and from the south.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_4::
    .string "They wandered in the wilderness in\n"
    .string "a solitary way; they found no city to\l"
    .string "dwell in.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_5::
    .string "Hungry and thirsty, their soul\n"
    .string "fainted in them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_6::
    .string "Then they cried unto the LORD in\n"
    .string "their trouble, and he delivered\l"
    .string "them out of their distresses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_7::
    .string "And he led them forth by the right\n"
    .string "way, that they might go to a city of\l"
    .string "habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_8::
    .string "Oh that men would praise the LORD\n"
    .string "for his goodness, and for his\l"
    .string "wonderful works to the children of\l"
    .string "men!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_9::
    .string "For he satisfieth the longing\n"
    .string "soul, and filleth the hungry soul\l"
    .string "with goodness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_10::
    .string "Such as sit in darkness and in the\n"
    .string "shadow of death, being bound in\l"
    .string "affliction and iron;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_11::
    .string "Because they rebelled against the\n"
    .string "words of God, and contemned the\l"
    .string "counsel of the most High:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_12::
    .string "Therefore he brought down their\n"
    .string "heart with labour; they fell down,\l"
    .string "and there was none to help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_13::
    .string "Then they cried unto the LORD in\n"
    .string "their trouble, and he saved them out\l"
    .string "of their distresses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_14::
    .string "He brought them out of darkness and\n"
    .string "the shadow of death, and brake their\l"
    .string "bands in sunder.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_15::
    .string "Oh that men would praise the LORD\n"
    .string "for his goodness, and for his\l"
    .string "wonderful works to the children of\l"
    .string "men!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_16::
    .string "For he hath broken the gates of\n"
    .string "brass, and cut the bars of iron in\l"
    .string "sunder.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_17::
    .string "Fools because of their\n"
    .string "transgression, and because of their\l"
    .string "iniquities, are afflicted.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_18::
    .string "Their soul abhorreth all manner\n"
    .string "of meat; and they draw near unto the\l"
    .string "gates of death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_19::
    .string "Then they cry unto the LORD in their\n"
    .string "trouble, and he saveth them out of\l"
    .string "their distresses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_20::
    .string "He sent his word, and healed them,\n"
    .string "and delivered them from their\l"
    .string "destructions.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_21::
    .string "Oh that men would praise the LORD\n"
    .string "for his goodness, and for his\l"
    .string "wonderful works to the children of\l"
    .string "men!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_22::
    .string "And let them sacrifice the\n"
    .string "sacrifices of thanksgiving, and\l"
    .string "declare his works with rejoicing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_23::
    .string "They that go down to the sea in\n"
    .string "ships, that do business in great\l"
    .string "waters;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_24::
    .string "These see the works of the LORD, and\n"
    .string "his wonders in the deep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_25::
    .string "For he commandeth, and raiseth the\n"
    .string "stormy wind, which lifteth up the\l"
    .string "waves thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_26::
    .string "They mount up to the heaven, they go\n"
    .string "down again to the depths: their soul\l"
    .string "is melted because of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_27::
    .string "They reel to and fro, and stagger\n"
    .string "like a drunken man, and are at their\l"
    .string "wit’s end.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_28::
    .string "Then they cry unto the LORD in their\n"
    .string "trouble, and he bringeth them out of\l"
    .string "their distresses.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_29::
    .string "He maketh the storm a calm, so that\n"
    .string "the waves thereof are still.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_30::
    .string "Then are they glad because they be\n"
    .string "quiet; so he bringeth them unto their\l"
    .string "desired haven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_31::
    .string "Oh that men would praise the LORD\n"
    .string "for his goodness, and for his\l"
    .string "wonderful works to the children of\l"
    .string "men!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_32::
    .string "Let them exalt him also in the\n"
    .string "congregation of the people, and\l"
    .string "praise him in the assembly of the\l"
    .string "elders.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_33::
    .string "He turneth rivers into a\n"
    .string "wilderness, and the watersprings\l"
    .string "into dry ground;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_34::
    .string "A fruitful land into barrenness,\n"
    .string "for the wickedness of them that\l"
    .string "dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_35::
    .string "He turneth the wilderness into a\n"
    .string "standing water, and dry ground into\l"
    .string "watersprings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_36::
    .string "And there he maketh the hungry to\n"
    .string "dwell, that they may prepare a\l"
    .string "city for habitation;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_37::
    .string "And sow the fields, and plant\n"
    .string "vineyards, which may yield fruits of\l"
    .string "increase.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_38::
    .string "He blesseth them also, so that they\n"
    .string "are multiplied greatly; and\l"
    .string "suffereth not their cattle to\l"
    .string "decrease.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_39::
    .string "Again, they are minished and brought\n"
    .string "low through oppression,\l"
    .string "affliction, and sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_40::
    .string "He poureth contempt upon princes,\n"
    .string "and causeth them to wander in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, where there is no way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_41::
    .string "Yet setteth he the poor on high\n"
    .string "from affliction, and maketh him\l"
    .string "families like a flock.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_42::
    .string "The righteous shall see it, and\n"
    .string "rejoice: and all iniquity shall\l"
    .string "stop her mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_107_43::
    .string "Whoso is wise, and will observe\n"
    .string "these things, even they shall\l"
    .string "understand the lovingkindness of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_1::
    .string "O god, my heart is fixed; I will\n"
    .string "sing and give praise, even with my\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_2::
    .string "Awake, psaltery and harp: I\n"
    .string "myself will awake early.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_3::
    .string "I will praise thee, O LORD, among\n"
    .string "the people: and I will sing\l"
    .string "praises unto thee among the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_4::
    .string "For thy mercy is great above the\n"
    .string "heavens: and thy truth reacheth unto\l"
    .string "the clouds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_5::
    .string "Be thou exalted, O God, above the\n"
    .string "heavens: and thy glory above all\l"
    .string "the earth;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_6::
    .string "That thy beloved may be delivered:\n"
    .string "save with thy right hand, and answer\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_7::
    .string "God hath spoken in his holiness; I\n"
    .string "will rejoice, I will divide\l"
    .string "Shechem, and mete out the valley of\l"
    .string "Succoth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_8::
    .string "Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine;\n"
    .string "Ephraim also is the strength of\l"
    .string "mine head; Judah is my lawgiver;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_9::
    .string "Moab is my washpot; over Edom will\n"
    .string "I cast out my shoe; over Philistia\l"
    .string "will I triumph.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_10::
    .string "Who will bring me into the strong\n"
    .string "city? who will lead me into Edom?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_11::
    .string "Wilt not thou, O God, who hast cast\n"
    .string "us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go\l"
    .string "forth with our hosts?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_12::
    .string "Give us help from trouble: for\n"
    .string "vain is the help of man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_108_13::
    .string "Through God we shall do\n"
    .string "valiantly: for he it is that shall\l"
    .string "tread down our enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_1::
    .string "Hold not thy peace, O God of my\n"
    .string "praise;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_2::
    .string "For the mouth of the wicked and the\n"
    .string "mouth of the deceitful are opened\l"
    .string "against me: they have spoken against\l"
    .string "me with a lying tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_3::
    .string "They compassed me about also with\n"
    .string "words of hatred; and fought against\l"
    .string "me without a cause.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_4::
    .string "For my love they are my\n"
    .string "adversaries: but I give myself unto\l"
    .string "prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_5::
    .string "And they have rewarded me evil for\n"
    .string "good, and hatred for my love.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_6::
    .string "Set thou a wicked man over him: and\n"
    .string "let Satan stand at his right hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_7::
    .string "When he shall be judged, let him\n"
    .string "be condemned: and let his prayer\l"
    .string "become sin.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_8::
    .string "Let his days be few; and let another\n"
    .string "take his office.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_9::
    .string "Let his children be fatherless,\n"
    .string "and his wife a widow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_10::
    .string "Let his children be continually\n"
    .string "vagabonds, and beg: let them seek\l"
    .string "their bread also out of their\l"
    .string "desolate places.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_11::
    .string "Let the extortioner catch all that\n"
    .string "he hath; and let the strangers\l"
    .string "spoil his labour.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_12::
    .string "Let there be none to extend mercy\n"
    .string "unto him: neither let there be any to\l"
    .string "favour his fatherless children.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_13::
    .string "Let his posterity be cut off; and in\n"
    .string "the generation following let their\l"
    .string "name be blotted out.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_14::
    .string "Let the iniquity of his fathers be\n"
    .string "remembered with the LORD; and let\l"
    .string "not the sin of his mother be blotted\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_15::
    .string "Let them be before the LORD\n"
    .string "continually, that he may cut off the\l"
    .string "memory of them from the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_16::
    .string "Because that he remembered not to\n"
    .string "shew mercy, but persecuted the poor\l"
    .string "and needy man, that he might even\l"
    .string "slay the broken in heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_17::
    .string "As he loved cursing, so let it come\n"
    .string "unto him: as he delighted not in\l"
    .string "blessing, so let it be far from him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_18::
    .string "As he clothed himself with cursing\n"
    .string "like as with his garment, so let it\l"
    .string "come into his bowels like water, and\l"
    .string "like oil into his bones.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_19::
    .string "Let it be unto him as the garment\n"
    .string "which covereth him, and for a girdle\l"
    .string "wherewith he is girded continually.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_20::
    .string "Let this be the reward of mine\n"
    .string "adversaries from the LORD, and of\l"
    .string "them that speak evil against my\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_21::
    .string "But do thou for me, O GOD the Lord,\n"
    .string "for thy name’s sake: because thy\l"
    .string "mercy is good, deliver thou me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_22::
    .string "For I am poor and needy, and my\n"
    .string "heart is wounded within me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_23::
    .string "I am gone like the shadow when it\n"
    .string "declineth: I am tossed up and down\l"
    .string "as the locust.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_24::
    .string "My knees are weak through fasting;\n"
    .string "and my flesh faileth of fatness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_25::
    .string "I became also a reproach unto them:\n"
    .string "when they looked upon me they\l"
    .string "shaked their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_26::
    .string "Help me, O LORD my God: O save me\n"
    .string "according to thy mercy:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_27::
    .string "That they may know that this is thy\n"
    .string "hand; that thou, LORD, hast done it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_28::
    .string "Let them curse, but bless thou:\n"
    .string "when they arise, let them be\l"
    .string "ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_29::
    .string "Let mine adversaries be clothed\n"
    .string "with shame, and let them cover\l"
    .string "themselves with their own confusion,\l"
    .string "as with a mantle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_30::
    .string "I will greatly praise the LORD\n"
    .string "with my mouth; yea, I will praise\l"
    .string "him among the multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_109_31::
    .string "For he shall stand at the right\n"
    .string "hand of the poor, to save him from\l"
    .string "those that condemn his soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_1::
    .string "The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou\n"
    .string "at my right hand, until I make thine\l"
    .string "enemies thy footstool.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_2::
    .string "The LORD shall send the rod of thy\n"
    .string "strength out of Zion: rule thou in\l"
    .string "the midst of thine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_3::
    .string "Thy people shall be willing in\n"
    .string "the day of thy power, in the beauties\l"
    .string "of holiness from the womb of the\l"
    .string "morning: thou hast the dew of thy\l"
    .string "youth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_4::
    .string "The LORD hath sworn, and will not\n"
    .string "repent, Thou art a priest for ever\l"
    .string "after the order of Melchizedek.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_5::
    .string "The Lord at thy right hand shall\n"
    .string "strike through kings in the day of\l"
    .string "his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_6::
    .string "He shall judge among the heathen,\n"
    .string "he shall fill the places with the\l"
    .string "dead bodies; he shall wound the\l"
    .string "heads over many countries.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_110_7::
    .string "He shall drink of the brook in the\n"
    .string "way: therefore shall he lift up\l"
    .string "the head.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. I will praise\n"
    .string "the LORD with my whole heart, in the\l"
    .string "assembly of the upright, and in the\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_2::
    .string "The works of the LORD are great,\n"
    .string "sought out of all them that have\l"
    .string "pleasure therein.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_3::
    .string "His work is honourable and\n"
    .string "glorious: and his righteousness\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_4::
    .string "He hath made his wonderful works to\n"
    .string "be remembered: the LORD is gracious\l"
    .string "and full of compassion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_5::
    .string "He hath given meat unto them that\n"
    .string "fear him: he will ever be mindful\l"
    .string "of his covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_6::
    .string "He hath shewed his people the\n"
    .string "power of his works, that he may give\l"
    .string "them the heritage of the heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_7::
    .string "The works of his hands are verity\n"
    .string "and judgment; all his commandments\l"
    .string "are sure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_8::
    .string "They stand fast for ever and ever,\n"
    .string "and are done in truth and\l"
    .string "uprightness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_9::
    .string "He sent redemption unto his\n"
    .string "people: he hath commanded his\l"
    .string "covenant for ever: holy and reverend\l"
    .string "is his name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_111_10::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is the\n"
    .string "beginning of wisdom: a good\l"
    .string "understanding have all they that do\l"
    .string "his commandments: his praise\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Blessed is the\n"
    .string "man that feareth the LORD, that\l"
    .string "delighteth greatly in his\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_2::
    .string "His seed shall be mighty upon\n"
    .string "earth: the generation of the upright\l"
    .string "shall be blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_3::
    .string "Wealth and riches shall be in his\n"
    .string "house: and his righteousness\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_4::
    .string "Unto the upright there ariseth\n"
    .string "light in the darkness: he is\l"
    .string "gracious, and full of compassion,\l"
    .string "and righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_5::
    .string "A good man sheweth favour, and\n"
    .string "lendeth: he will guide his affairs\l"
    .string "with discretion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_6::
    .string "Surely he shall not be moved for\n"
    .string "ever: the righteous shall be in\l"
    .string "everlasting remembrance.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_7::
    .string "He shall not be afraid of evil\n"
    .string "tidings: his heart is fixed, trusting\l"
    .string "in the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_8::
    .string "His heart is established, he shall\n"
    .string "not be afraid, until he see his\l"
    .string "desire upon his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_9::
    .string "He hath dispersed, he hath given to\n"
    .string "the poor; his righteousness endureth\l"
    .string "for ever; his horn shall be exalted\l"
    .string "with honour.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_112_10::
    .string "The wicked shall see it, and be\n"
    .string "grieved; he shall gnash with his\l"
    .string "teeth, and melt away: the desire of\l"
    .string "the wicked shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Praise, O ye\n"
    .string "servants of the LORD, praise the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_2::
    .string "Blessed be the name of the LORD\n"
    .string "from this time forth and for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_3::
    .string "From the rising of the sun unto the\n"
    .string "going down of the same the LORD’s\l"
    .string "name is to be praised.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_4::
    .string "The LORD is high above all nations,\n"
    .string "and his glory above the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_5::
    .string "Who is like unto the LORD our God,\n"
    .string "who dwelleth on high,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_6::
    .string "Who humbleth himself to behold\n"
    .string "the things that are in heaven, and in\l"
    .string "the earth!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_7::
    .string "He raiseth up the poor out of the\n"
    .string "dust, and lifteth the needy out of\l"
    .string "the dunghill;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_8::
    .string "That he may set him with princes,\n"
    .string "even with the princes of his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_113_9::
    .string "He maketh the barren woman to keep\n"
    .string "house, and to be a joyful mother of\l"
    .string "children. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_1::
    .string "When Israel went out of Egypt, the\n"
    .string "house of Jacob from a people of\l"
    .string "strange language;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_2::
    .string "Judah was his sanctuary, and Israel\n"
    .string "his dominion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_3::
    .string "The sea saw it, and fled: Jordan was\n"
    .string "driven back.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_4::
    .string "The mountains skipped like rams,\n"
    .string "and the little hills like lambs.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_5::
    .string "What ailed thee, O thou sea, that\n"
    .string "thou fleddest? thou Jordan, that\l"
    .string "thou wast driven back?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_6::
    .string "Ye mountains, that ye skipped like\n"
    .string "rams; and ye little hills, like\l"
    .string "lambs?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_7::
    .string "Tremble, thou earth, at the\n"
    .string "presence of the Lord, at the\l"
    .string "presence of the God of Jacob;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_114_8::
    .string "Which turned the rock into a\n"
    .string "standing water, the flint into a\l"
    .string "fountain of waters.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_1::
    .string "Not unto us, O LORD, not unto us, but\n"
    .string "unto thy name give glory, for thy\l"
    .string "mercy, and for thy truth’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_2::
    .string "Wherefore should the heathen say,\n"
    .string "Where is now their God?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_3::
    .string "But our God is in the heavens: he\n"
    .string "hath done whatsoever he hath\l"
    .string "pleased.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_4::
    .string "Their idols are silver and gold,\n"
    .string "the work of men’s hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_5::
    .string "They have mouths, but they speak\n"
    .string "not: eyes have they, but they see not:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_6::
    .string "They have ears, but they hear not:\n"
    .string "noses have they, but they smell not:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_7::
    .string "They have hands, but they handle\n"
    .string "not: feet have they, but they walk\l"
    .string "not: neither speak they through\l"
    .string "their throat.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_8::
    .string "They that make them are like unto\n"
    .string "them; so is every one that trusteth\l"
    .string "in them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_9::
    .string "O Israel, trust thou in the LORD: he\n"
    .string "is their help and their shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_10::
    .string "O house of Aaron, trust in the LORD:\n"
    .string "he is their help and their shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_11::
    .string "Ye that fear the LORD, trust in the\n"
    .string "LORD: he is their help and their\l"
    .string "shield.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_12::
    .string "The LORD hath been mindful of us: he\n"
    .string "will bless us; he will bless the\l"
    .string "house of Israel; he will bless the\l"
    .string "house of Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_13::
    .string "He will bless them that fear the\n"
    .string "LORD, both small and great.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_14::
    .string "The LORD shall increase you more\n"
    .string "and more, you and your children.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_15::
    .string "Ye are blessed of the LORD which\n"
    .string "made heaven and earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_16::
    .string "The heaven, even the heavens, are\n"
    .string "the LORD’s: but the earth hath he\l"
    .string "given to the children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_17::
    .string "The dead praise not the LORD,\n"
    .string "neither any that go down into\l"
    .string "silence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_115_18::
    .string "But we will bless the LORD from\n"
    .string "this time forth and for evermore.\l"
    .string "Praise the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_1::
    .string "I love the LORD, because he hath\n"
    .string "heard my voice and my\l"
    .string "supplications.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_2::
    .string "Because he hath inclined his ear\n"
    .string "unto me, therefore will I call\l"
    .string "upon him as long as I live.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_3::
    .string "The sorrows of death compassed me,\n"
    .string "and the pains of hell gat hold\l"
    .string "upon me: I found trouble and sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_4::
    .string "Then called I upon the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD; O LORD, I beseech thee, deliver\l"
    .string "my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_5::
    .string "Gracious is the LORD, and righteous;\n"
    .string "yea, our God is merciful.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_6::
    .string "The LORD preserveth the simple: I\n"
    .string "was brought low, and he helped me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_7::
    .string "Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for\n"
    .string "the LORD hath dealt bountifully\l"
    .string "with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_8::
    .string "For thou hast delivered my soul\n"
    .string "from death, mine eyes from tears, and\l"
    .string "my feet from falling.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_9::
    .string "I will walk before the LORD in the\n"
    .string "land of the living.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_10::
    .string "I believed, therefore have I\n"
    .string "spoken: I was greatly afflicted:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_11::
    .string "I said in my haste, All men are\n"
    .string "liars.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_12::
    .string "What shall I render unto the LORD\n"
    .string "for all his benefits toward me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_13::
    .string "I will take the cup of salvation,\n"
    .string "and call upon the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_14::
    .string "I will pay my vows unto the LORD\n"
    .string "now in the presence of all his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_15::
    .string "Precious in the sight of the LORD is\n"
    .string "the death of his saints.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_16::
    .string "O LORD, truly I am thy servant; I am\n"
    .string "thy servant, and the son of thine\l"
    .string "handmaid: thou hast loosed my bonds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_17::
    .string "I will offer to thee the sacrifice\n"
    .string "of thanksgiving, and will call\l"
    .string "upon the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_18::
    .string "I will pay my vows unto the LORD\n"
    .string "now in the presence of all his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_116_19::
    .string "In the courts of the LORD’s house,\n"
    .string "in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_117_1::
    .string "O praise the LORD, all ye nations:\n"
    .string "praise him, all ye people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_117_2::
    .string "For his merciful kindness is great\n"
    .string "toward us: and the truth of the LORD\l"
    .string "endureth for ever. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_1::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD; for he\n"
    .string "is good: because his mercy endureth\l"
    .string "for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_2::
    .string "Let Israel now say, that his mercy\n"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_3::
    .string "Let the house of Aaron now say, that\n"
    .string "his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_4::
    .string "Let them now that fear the LORD say,\n"
    .string "that his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_5::
    .string "I called upon the LORD in\n"
    .string "distress: the LORD answered me, and\l"
    .string "set me in a large place.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_6::
    .string "The LORD is on my side; I will not\n"
    .string "fear: what can man do unto me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_7::
    .string "The LORD taketh my part with them\n"
    .string "that help me: therefore shall I\l"
    .string "see my desire upon them that hate me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_8::
    .string "It is better to trust in the LORD\n"
    .string "than to put confidence in man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_9::
    .string "It is better to trust in the LORD\n"
    .string "than to put confidence in princes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_10::
    .string "All nations compassed me about:\n"
    .string "but in the name of the LORD will I\l"
    .string "destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_11::
    .string "They compassed me about; yea, they\n"
    .string "compassed me about: but in the name\l"
    .string "of the LORD I will destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_12::
    .string "They compassed me about like bees:\n"
    .string "they are quenched as the fire of\l"
    .string "thorns: for in the name of the LORD I\l"
    .string "will destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_13::
    .string "Thou hast thrust sore at me that I\n"
    .string "might fall: but the LORD helped me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_14::
    .string "The LORD is my strength and song,\n"
    .string "and is become my salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_15::
    .string "The voice of rejoicing and\n"
    .string "salvation is in the tabernacles of\l"
    .string "the righteous: the right hand of the\l"
    .string "LORD doeth valiantly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_16::
    .string "The right hand of the LORD is\n"
    .string "exalted: the right hand of the LORD\l"
    .string "doeth valiantly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_17::
    .string "I shall not die, but live, and\n"
    .string "declare the works of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_18::
    .string "The LORD hath chastened me sore: but\n"
    .string "he hath not given me over unto death.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_19::
    .string "Open to me the gates of\n"
    .string "righteousness: I will go into them,\l"
    .string "and I will praise the LORD:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_20::
    .string "This gate of the LORD, into which\n"
    .string "the righteous shall enter.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_21::
    .string "I will praise thee: for thou hast\n"
    .string "heard me, and art become my\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_22::
    .string "The stone which the builders\n"
    .string "refused is become the head stone of\l"
    .string "the corner.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_23::
    .string "This is the LORD’s doing; it is\n"
    .string "marvellous in our eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_24::
    .string "This is the day which the LORD hath\n"
    .string "made; we will rejoice and be glad\l"
    .string "in it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_25::
    .string "Save now, I beseech thee, O LORD: O\n"
    .string "LORD, I beseech thee, send now\l"
    .string "prosperity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_26::
    .string "Blessed be he that cometh in the\n"
    .string "name of the LORD: we have blessed you\l"
    .string "out of the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_27::
    .string "God is the LORD, which hath shewed\n"
    .string "us light: bind the sacrifice with\l"
    .string "cords, even unto the horns of the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_28::
    .string "Thou art my God, and I will praise\n"
    .string "thee: thou art my God, I will exalt\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_118_29::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD; for he\n"
    .string "is good: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_1::
    .string "Blessed are the undefiled in the\n"
    .string "way, who walk in the law of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_2::
    .string "Blessed are they that keep his\n"
    .string "testimonies, and that seek him with\l"
    .string "the whole heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_3::
    .string "They also do no iniquity: they walk\n"
    .string "in his ways.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_4::
    .string "Thou hast commanded us to keep thy\n"
    .string "precepts diligently.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_5::
    .string "O that my ways were directed to\n"
    .string "keep thy statutes!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_6::
    .string "Then shall I not be ashamed, when I\n"
    .string "have respect unto all thy\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_7::
    .string "I will praise thee with\n"
    .string "uprightness of heart, when I shall\l"
    .string "have learned thy righteous\l"
    .string "judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_8::
    .string "I will keep thy statutes: O\n"
    .string "forsake me not utterly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_9::
    .string "Wherewithal shall a young man\n"
    .string "cleanse his way? by taking heed\l"
    .string "thereto according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_10::
    .string "With my whole heart have I sought\n"
    .string "thee: O let me not wander from thy\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_11::
    .string "Thy word have I hid in mine heart,\n"
    .string "that I might not sin against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_12::
    .string "Blessed art thou, O LORD: teach me\n"
    .string "thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_13::
    .string "With my lips have I declared all\n"
    .string "the judgments of thy mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_14::
    .string "I have rejoiced in the way of thy\n"
    .string "testimonies, as much as in all\l"
    .string "riches.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_15::
    .string "I will meditate in thy precepts,\n"
    .string "and have respect unto thy ways.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_16::
    .string "I will delight myself in thy\n"
    .string "statutes: I will not forget thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_17::
    .string "Deal bountifully with thy\n"
    .string "servant, that I may live, and keep\l"
    .string "thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_18::
    .string "Open thou mine eyes, that I may\n"
    .string "behold wondrous things out of thy\l"
    .string "law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_19::
    .string "I am a stranger in the earth: hide\n"
    .string "not thy commandments from me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_20::
    .string "My soul breaketh for the longing\n"
    .string "that it hath unto thy judgments at\l"
    .string "all times.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_21::
    .string "Thou hast rebuked the proud that\n"
    .string "are cursed, which do err from thy\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_22::
    .string "Remove from me reproach and\n"
    .string "contempt; for I have kept thy\l"
    .string "testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_23::
    .string "Princes also did sit and speak\n"
    .string "against me: but thy servant did\l"
    .string "meditate in thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_24::
    .string "Thy testimonies also are my\n"
    .string "delight and my counsellors.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_25::
    .string "My soul cleaveth unto the dust:\n"
    .string "quicken thou me according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_26::
    .string "I have declared my ways, and thou\n"
    .string "heardest me: teach me thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_27::
    .string "Make me to understand the way of thy\n"
    .string "precepts: so shall I talk of thy\l"
    .string "wondrous works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_28::
    .string "My soul melteth for heaviness:\n"
    .string "strengthen thou me according unto\l"
    .string "thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_29::
    .string "Remove from me the way of lying: and\n"
    .string "grant me thy law graciously.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_30::
    .string "I have chosen the way of truth: thy\n"
    .string "judgments have I laid before me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_31::
    .string "I have stuck unto thy testimonies: O\n"
    .string "LORD, put me not to shame.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_32::
    .string "I will run the way of thy\n"
    .string "commandments, when thou shalt\l"
    .string "enlarge my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_33::
    .string "Teach me, O LORD, the way of thy\n"
    .string "statutes; and I shall keep it unto\l"
    .string "the end.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_34::
    .string "Give me understanding, and I shall\n"
    .string "keep thy law; yea, I shall observe\l"
    .string "it with my whole heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_35::
    .string "Make me to go in the path of thy\n"
    .string "commandments; for therein do I\l"
    .string "delight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_36::
    .string "Incline my heart unto thy\n"
    .string "testimonies, and not to covetousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_37::
    .string "Turn away mine eyes from beholding\n"
    .string "vanity; and quicken thou me in thy\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_38::
    .string "Stablish thy word unto thy servant,\n"
    .string "who is devoted to thy fear.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_39::
    .string "Turn away my reproach which I fear:\n"
    .string "for thy judgments are good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_40::
    .string "Behold, I have longed after thy\n"
    .string "precepts: quicken me in thy\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_41::
    .string "Let thy mercies come also unto me, O\n"
    .string "LORD, even thy salvation, according\l"
    .string "to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_42::
    .string "So shall I have wherewith to\n"
    .string "answer him that reproacheth me: for\l"
    .string "I trust in thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_43::
    .string "And take not the word of truth\n"
    .string "utterly out of my mouth; for I have\l"
    .string "hoped in thy judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_44::
    .string "So shall I keep thy law\n"
    .string "continually for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_45::
    .string "And I will walk at liberty: for I\n"
    .string "seek thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_46::
    .string "I will speak of thy testimonies\n"
    .string "also before kings, and will not be\l"
    .string "ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_47::
    .string "And I will delight myself in thy\n"
    .string "commandments, which I have loved.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_48::
    .string "My hands also will I lift up unto\n"
    .string "thy commandments, which I have\l"
    .string "loved; and I will meditate in thy\l"
    .string "statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_49::
    .string "Remember the word unto thy servant,\n"
    .string "upon which thou hast caused me to\l"
    .string "hope.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_50::
    .string "This is my comfort in my\n"
    .string "affliction: for thy word hath\l"
    .string "quickened me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_51::
    .string "The proud have had me greatly in\n"
    .string "derision: yet have I not declined\l"
    .string "from thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_52::
    .string "I remembered thy judgments of old,\n"
    .string "O LORD; and have comforted myself.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_53::
    .string "Horror hath taken hold upon me\n"
    .string "because of the wicked that forsake\l"
    .string "thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_54::
    .string "Thy statutes have been my songs in\n"
    .string "the house of my pilgrimage.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_55::
    .string "I have remembered thy name, O LORD,\n"
    .string "in the night, and have kept thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_56::
    .string "This I had, because I kept thy\n"
    .string "precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_57::
    .string "Thou art my portion, O LORD: I have\n"
    .string "said that I would keep thy words.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_58::
    .string "I intreated thy favour with my\n"
    .string "whole heart: be merciful unto me\l"
    .string "according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_59::
    .string "I thought on my ways, and turned my\n"
    .string "feet unto thy testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_60::
    .string "I made haste, and delayed not to\n"
    .string "keep thy commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_61::
    .string "The bands of the wicked have robbed\n"
    .string "me: but I have not forgotten thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_62::
    .string "At midnight I will rise to give\n"
    .string "thanks unto thee because of thy\l"
    .string "righteous judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_63::
    .string "I am a companion of all them that\n"
    .string "fear thee, and of them that keep thy\l"
    .string "precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_64::
    .string "The earth, O LORD, is full of thy\n"
    .string "mercy: teach me thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_65::
    .string "Thou hast dealt well with thy\n"
    .string "servant, O LORD, according unto thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_66::
    .string "Teach me good judgment and\n"
    .string "knowledge: for I have believed thy\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_67::
    .string "Before I was afflicted I went\n"
    .string "astray: but now have I kept thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_68::
    .string "Thou art good, and doest good; teach\n"
    .string "me thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_69::
    .string "The proud have forged a lie\n"
    .string "against me: but I will keep thy\l"
    .string "precepts with my whole heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_70::
    .string "Their heart is as fat as grease; but\n"
    .string "I delight in thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_71::
    .string "It is good for me that I have been\n"
    .string "afflicted; that I might learn thy\l"
    .string "statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_72::
    .string "The law of thy mouth is better unto\n"
    .string "me than thousands of gold and\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_73::
    .string "Thy hands have made me and fashioned\n"
    .string "me: give me understanding, that I may\l"
    .string "learn thy commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_74::
    .string "They that fear thee will be glad\n"
    .string "when they see me; because I have\l"
    .string "hoped in thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_75::
    .string "I know, O LORD, that thy judgments\n"
    .string "are right, and that thou in\l"
    .string "faithfulness hast afflicted me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_76::
    .string "Let, I pray thee, thy merciful\n"
    .string "kindness be for my comfort, according\l"
    .string "to thy word unto thy servant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_77::
    .string "Let thy tender mercies come unto me,\n"
    .string "that I may live: for thy law is my\l"
    .string "delight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_78::
    .string "Let the proud be ashamed; for they\n"
    .string "dealt perversely with me without a\l"
    .string "cause: but I will meditate in thy\l"
    .string "precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_79::
    .string "Let those that fear thee turn unto\n"
    .string "me, and those that have known thy\l"
    .string "testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_80::
    .string "Let my heart be sound in thy\n"
    .string "statutes; that I be not ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_81::
    .string "My soul fainteth for thy\n"
    .string "salvation: but I hope in thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_82::
    .string "Mine eyes fail for thy word,\n"
    .string "saying, When wilt thou comfort me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_83::
    .string "For I am become like a bottle in\n"
    .string "the smoke; yet do I not forget thy\l"
    .string "statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_84::
    .string "How many are the days of thy\n"
    .string "servant? when wilt thou execute\l"
    .string "judgment on them that persecute me?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_85::
    .string "The proud have digged pits for me,\n"
    .string "which are not after thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_86::
    .string "All thy commandments are\n"
    .string "faithful: they persecute me\l"
    .string "wrongfully; help thou me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_87::
    .string "They had almost consumed me upon\n"
    .string "earth; but I forsook not thy\l"
    .string "precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_88::
    .string "Quicken me after thy\n"
    .string "lovingkindness; so shall I keep the\l"
    .string "testimony of thy mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_89::
    .string "For ever, O LORD, thy word is\n"
    .string "settled in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_90::
    .string "Thy faithfulness is unto all\n"
    .string "generations: thou hast established\l"
    .string "the earth, and it abideth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_91::
    .string "They continue this day according to\n"
    .string "thine ordinances: for all are thy\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_92::
    .string "Unless thy law had been my\n"
    .string "delights, I should then have\l"
    .string "perished in mine affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_93::
    .string "I will never forget thy precepts:\n"
    .string "for with them thou hast quickened me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_94::
    .string "I am thine, save me: for I have\n"
    .string "sought thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_95::
    .string "The wicked have waited for me to\n"
    .string "destroy me: but I will consider thy\l"
    .string "testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_96::
    .string "I have seen an end of all\n"
    .string "perfection: but thy commandment is\l"
    .string "exceeding broad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_97::
    .string "O how I love thy law! it is my\n"
    .string "meditation all the day.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_98::
    .string "Thou through thy commandments hast\n"
    .string "made me wiser than mine enemies: for\l"
    .string "they are ever with me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_99::
    .string "I have more understanding than all\n"
    .string "my teachers: for thy testimonies are\l"
    .string "my meditation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_100::
    .string "I understand more than the ancients,\n"
    .string "because I keep thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_101::
    .string "I have refrained my feet from every\n"
    .string "evil way, that I might keep thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_102::
    .string "I have not departed from thy\n"
    .string "judgments: for thou hast taught me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_103::
    .string "How sweet are thy words unto my\n"
    .string "taste! yea, sweeter than honey to my\l"
    .string "mouth!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_104::
    .string "Through thy precepts I get\n"
    .string "understanding: therefore I hate\l"
    .string "every false way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_105::
    .string "Thy word is a lamp unto my feet,\n"
    .string "and a light unto my path.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_106::
    .string "I have sworn, and I will perform\n"
    .string "it, that I will keep thy righteous\l"
    .string "judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_107::
    .string "I am afflicted very much: quicken\n"
    .string "me, O LORD, according unto thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_108::
    .string "Accept, I beseech thee, the\n"
    .string "freewill offerings of my mouth, O\l"
    .string "LORD, and teach me thy judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_109::
    .string "My soul is continually in my hand:\n"
    .string "yet do I not forget thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_110::
    .string "The wicked have laid a snare for me:\n"
    .string "yet I erred not from thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_111::
    .string "Thy testimonies have I taken as an\n"
    .string "heritage for ever: for they are the\l"
    .string "rejoicing of my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_112::
    .string "I have inclined mine heart to\n"
    .string "perform thy statutes alway, even\l"
    .string "unto the end.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_113::
    .string "I hate vain thoughts: but thy law do\n"
    .string "I love.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_114::
    .string "Thou art my hiding place and my\n"
    .string "shield: I hope in thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_115::
    .string "Depart from me, ye evildoers: for I\n"
    .string "will keep the commandments of my\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_116::
    .string "Uphold me according unto thy word,\n"
    .string "that I may live: and let me not be\l"
    .string "ashamed of my hope.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_117::
    .string "Hold thou me up, and I shall be\n"
    .string "safe: and I will have respect unto\l"
    .string "thy statutes continually.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_118::
    .string "Thou hast trodden down all them\n"
    .string "that err from thy statutes: for their\l"
    .string "deceit is falsehood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_119::
    .string "Thou puttest away all the wicked\n"
    .string "of the earth like dross: therefore I\l"
    .string "love thy testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_120::
    .string "My flesh trembleth for fear of\n"
    .string "thee; and I am afraid of thy\l"
    .string "judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_121::
    .string "I have done judgment and justice:\n"
    .string "leave me not to mine oppressors.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_122::
    .string "Be surety for thy servant for good:\n"
    .string "let not the proud oppress me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_123::
    .string "Mine eyes fail for thy salvation,\n"
    .string "and for the word of thy righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_124::
    .string "Deal with thy servant according\n"
    .string "unto thy mercy, and teach me thy\l"
    .string "statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_125::
    .string "I am thy servant; give me\n"
    .string "understanding, that I may know thy\l"
    .string "testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_126::
    .string "It is time for thee, LORD, to work:\n"
    .string "for they have made void thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_127::
    .string "Therefore I love thy commandments\n"
    .string "above gold; yea, above fine gold.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_128::
    .string "Therefore I esteem all thy\n"
    .string "precepts concerning all things to\l"
    .string "be right; and I hate every false way.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_129::
    .string "Thy testimonies are wonderful:\n"
    .string "therefore doth my soul keep them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_130::
    .string "The entrance of thy words giveth\n"
    .string "light; it giveth understanding unto\l"
    .string "the simple.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_131::
    .string "I opened my mouth, and panted: for\n"
    .string "I longed for thy commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_132::
    .string "Look thou upon me, and be merciful\n"
    .string "unto me, as thou usest to do unto\l"
    .string "those that love thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_133::
    .string "Order my steps in thy word: and let\n"
    .string "not any iniquity have dominion over\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_134::
    .string "Deliver me from the oppression of\n"
    .string "man: so will I keep thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_135::
    .string "Make thy face to shine upon thy\n"
    .string "servant; and teach me thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_136::
    .string "Rivers of waters run down mine eyes,\n"
    .string "because they keep not thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_137::
    .string "Righteous art thou, O LORD, and\n"
    .string "upright are thy judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_138::
    .string "Thy testimonies that thou hast\n"
    .string "commanded are righteous and very\l"
    .string "faithful.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_139::
    .string "My zeal hath consumed me, because\n"
    .string "mine enemies have forgotten thy\l"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_140::
    .string "Thy word is very pure: therefore\n"
    .string "thy servant loveth it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_141::
    .string "I am small and despised: yet do\n"
    .string "not I forget thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_142::
    .string "Thy righteousness is an\n"
    .string "everlasting righteousness, and thy\l"
    .string "law is the truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_143::
    .string "Trouble and anguish have taken\n"
    .string "hold on me: yet thy commandments are\l"
    .string "my delights.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_144::
    .string "The righteousness of thy\n"
    .string "testimonies is everlasting: give me\l"
    .string "understanding, and I shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_145::
    .string "I cried with my whole heart; hear\n"
    .string "me, O LORD: I will keep thy\l"
    .string "statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_146::
    .string "I cried unto thee; save me, and I\n"
    .string "shall keep thy testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_147::
    .string "I prevented the dawning of the\n"
    .string "morning, and cried: I hoped in thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_148::
    .string "Mine eyes prevent the night\n"
    .string "watches, that I might meditate in thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_149::
    .string "Hear my voice according unto thy\n"
    .string "lovingkindness: O LORD, quicken me\l"
    .string "according to thy judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_150::
    .string "They draw nigh that follow after\n"
    .string "mischief: they are far from thy law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_151::
    .string "Thou art near, O LORD; and all thy\n"
    .string "commandments are truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_152::
    .string "Concerning thy testimonies, I have\n"
    .string "known of old that thou hast founded\l"
    .string "them for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_153::
    .string "Consider mine affliction, and\n"
    .string "deliver me: for I do not forget thy\l"
    .string "law.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_154::
    .string "Plead my cause, and deliver me:\n"
    .string "quicken me according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_155::
    .string "Salvation is far from the wicked:\n"
    .string "for they seek not thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_156::
    .string "Great are thy tender mercies, O\n"
    .string "LORD: quicken me according to thy\l"
    .string "judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_157::
    .string "Many are my persecutors and mine\n"
    .string "enemies; yet do I not decline from\l"
    .string "thy testimonies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_158::
    .string "I beheld the transgressors, and was\n"
    .string "grieved; because they kept not thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_159::
    .string "Consider how I love thy precepts:\n"
    .string "quicken me, O LORD, according to thy\l"
    .string "lovingkindness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_160::
    .string "Thy word is true from the beginning:\n"
    .string "and every one of thy righteous\l"
    .string "judgments endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_161::
    .string "Princes have persecuted me without\n"
    .string "a cause: but my heart standeth in awe\l"
    .string "of thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_162::
    .string "I rejoice at thy word, as one that\n"
    .string "findeth great spoil.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_163::
    .string "I hate and abhor lying: but thy law\n"
    .string "do I love.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_164::
    .string "Seven times a day do I praise thee\n"
    .string "because of thy righteous judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_165::
    .string "Great peace have they which love\n"
    .string "thy law: and nothing shall offend\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_166::
    .string "LORD, I have hoped for thy\n"
    .string "salvation, and done thy\l"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_167::
    .string "My soul hath kept thy testimonies;\n"
    .string "and I love them exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_168::
    .string "I have kept thy precepts and thy\n"
    .string "testimonies: for all my ways are\l"
    .string "before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_169::
    .string "Let my cry come near before thee, O\n"
    .string "LORD: give me understanding\l"
    .string "according to thy word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_170::
    .string "Let my supplication come before\n"
    .string "thee: deliver me according to thy\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_171::
    .string "My lips shall utter praise, when\n"
    .string "thou hast taught me thy statutes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_172::
    .string "My tongue shall speak of thy word:\n"
    .string "for all thy commandments are\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_173::
    .string "Let thine hand help me; for I have\n"
    .string "chosen thy precepts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_174::
    .string "I have longed for thy salvation, O\n"
    .string "LORD; and thy law is my delight.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_175::
    .string "Let my soul live, and it shall\n"
    .string "praise thee; and let thy judgments\l"
    .string "help me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_119_176::
    .string "I have gone astray like a lost\n"
    .string "sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not\l"
    .string "forget thy commandments.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_1::
    .string "In my distress I cried unto the\n"
    .string "LORD, and he heard me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_2::
    .string "Deliver my soul, O LORD, from\n"
    .string "lying lips, and from a deceitful\l"
    .string "tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_3::
    .string "What shall be given unto thee? or\n"
    .string "what shall be done unto thee, thou\l"
    .string "false tongue?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_4::
    .string "Sharp arrows of the mighty, with\n"
    .string "coals of juniper.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_5::
    .string "Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech,\n"
    .string "that I dwell in the tents of Kedar!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_6::
    .string "My soul hath long dwelt with him\n"
    .string "that hateth peace.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_120_7::
    .string "I am for peace: but when I speak,\n"
    .string "they are for war.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_1::
    .string "I will lift up mine eyes unto the\n"
    .string "hills, from whence cometh my help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_2::
    .string "My help cometh from the LORD, which\n"
    .string "made heaven and earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_3::
    .string "He will not suffer thy foot to be\n"
    .string "moved: he that keepeth thee will\l"
    .string "not slumber.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_4::
    .string "Behold, he that keepeth Israel\n"
    .string "shall neither slumber nor sleep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_5::
    .string "The LORD is thy keeper: the LORD is\n"
    .string "thy shade upon thy right hand.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_6::
    .string "The sun shall not smite thee by\n"
    .string "day, nor the moon by night.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_7::
    .string "The LORD shall preserve thee from\n"
    .string "all evil: he shall preserve thy\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_121_8::
    .string "The LORD shall preserve thy going\n"
    .string "out and thy coming in from this time\l"
    .string "forth, and even for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_1::
    .string "I was glad when they said unto me,\n"
    .string "Let us go into the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_2::
    .string "Our feet shall stand within thy\n"
    .string "gates, O Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_3::
    .string "Jerusalem is builded as a city\n"
    .string "that is compact together:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_4::
    .string "Whither the tribes go up, the\n"
    .string "tribes of the LORD, unto the\l"
    .string "testimony of Israel, to give thanks\l"
    .string "unto the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_5::
    .string "For there are set thrones of\n"
    .string "judgment, the thrones of the house of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_6::
    .string "Pray for the peace of Jerusalem:\n"
    .string "they shall prosper that love thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_7::
    .string "Peace be within thy walls, and\n"
    .string "prosperity within thy palaces.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_8::
    .string "For my brethren and companions’\n"
    .string "sakes, I will now say, Peace be\l"
    .string "within thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_122_9::
    .string "Because of the house of the LORD our\n"
    .string "God I will seek thy good.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_123_1::
    .string "Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O\n"
    .string "thou that dwellest in the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_123_2::
    .string "Behold, as the eyes of servants\n"
    .string "look unto the hand of their masters,\l"
    .string "and as the eyes of a maiden unto the\l"
    .string "hand of her mistress; so our eyes\l"
    .string "wait upon the LORD our God, until\l"
    .string "that he have mercy upon us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_123_3::
    .string "Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have\n"
    .string "mercy upon us: for we are\l"
    .string "exceedingly filled with contempt.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_123_4::
    .string "Our soul is exceedingly filled\n"
    .string "with the scorning of those that are\l"
    .string "at ease, and with the contempt of the\l"
    .string "proud.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_1::
    .string "If it had not been the LORD who was\n"
    .string "on our side, now may Israel say;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_2::
    .string "If it had not been the LORD who was\n"
    .string "on our side, when men rose up against\l"
    .string "us:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_3::
    .string "Then they had swallowed us up\n"
    .string "quick, when their wrath was kindled\l"
    .string "against us:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_4::
    .string "Then the waters had overwhelmed us,\n"
    .string "the stream had gone over our soul:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_5::
    .string "Then the proud waters had gone over\n"
    .string "our soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_6::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD, who hath not\n"
    .string "given us as a prey to their teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_7::
    .string "Our soul is escaped as a bird out\n"
    .string "of the snare of the fowlers: the\l"
    .string "snare is broken, and we are escaped.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_124_8::
    .string "Our help is in the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD, who made heaven and earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_125_1::
    .string "They that trust in the LORD shall\n"
    .string "be as mount Zion, which cannot be\l"
    .string "removed, but abideth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_125_2::
    .string "As the mountains are round about\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, so the LORD is round\l"
    .string "about his people from henceforth\l"
    .string "even for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_125_3::
    .string "For the rod of the wicked shall not\n"
    .string "rest upon the lot of the righteous;\l"
    .string "lest the righteous put forth their\l"
    .string "hands unto iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_125_4::
    .string "Do good, O LORD, unto those that be\n"
    .string "good, and to them that are upright in\l"
    .string "their hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_125_5::
    .string "As for such as turn aside unto their\n"
    .string "crooked ways, the LORD shall lead\l"
    .string "them forth with the workers of\l"
    .string "iniquity: but peace shall be upon\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_1::
    .string "When the LORD turned again the\n"
    .string "captivity of Zion, we were like them\l"
    .string "that dream.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_2::
    .string "Then was our mouth filled with\n"
    .string "laughter, and our tongue with\l"
    .string "singing: then said they among the\l"
    .string "heathen, The LORD hath done great\l"
    .string "things for them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_3::
    .string "The LORD hath done great things for\n"
    .string "us; whereof we are glad.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_4::
    .string "Turn again our captivity, O LORD,\n"
    .string "as the streams in the south.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_5::
    .string "They that sow in tears shall reap\n"
    .string "in joy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_126_6::
    .string "He that goeth forth and weepeth,\n"
    .string "bearing precious seed, shall\l"
    .string "doubtless come again with rejoicing,\l"
    .string "bringing his sheaves with him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_127_1::
    .string "Except the LORD build the house,\n"
    .string "they labour in vain that build it:\l"
    .string "except the LORD keep the city, the\l"
    .string "watchman waketh but in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_127_2::
    .string "It is vain for you to rise up\n"
    .string "early, to sit up late, to eat the\l"
    .string "bread of sorrows: for so he giveth\l"
    .string "his beloved sleep.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_127_3::
    .string "Lo, children are an heritage of the\n"
    .string "LORD: and the fruit of the womb is his\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_127_4::
    .string "As arrows are in the hand of a\n"
    .string "mighty man; so are children of the\l"
    .string "youth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_127_5::
    .string "Happy is the man that hath his\n"
    .string "quiver full of them: they shall\l"
    .string "not be ashamed, but they shall\l"
    .string "speak with the enemies in the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_1::
    .string "Blessed is every one that feareth\n"
    .string "the LORD; that walketh in his ways.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_2::
    .string "For thou shalt eat the labour of\n"
    .string "thine hands: happy shalt thou be,\l"
    .string "and it shall be well with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_3::
    .string "Thy wife shall be as a fruitful\n"
    .string "vine by the sides of thine house: thy\l"
    .string "children like olive plants round\l"
    .string "about thy table.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_4::
    .string "Behold, that thus shall the man be\n"
    .string "blessed that feareth the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_5::
    .string "The LORD shall bless thee out of\n"
    .string "Zion: and thou shalt see the good of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem all the days of thy life.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_128_6::
    .string "Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s\n"
    .string "children, and peace upon Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_1::
    .string "Many a time have they afflicted me\n"
    .string "from my youth, may Israel now say:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_2::
    .string "Many a time have they afflicted me\n"
    .string "from my youth: yet they have not\l"
    .string "prevailed against me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_3::
    .string "The plowers plowed upon my back:\n"
    .string "they made long their furrows.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_4::
    .string "The LORD is righteous: he hath cut\n"
    .string "asunder the cords of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_5::
    .string "Let them all be confounded and\n"
    .string "turned back that hate Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_6::
    .string "Let them be as the grass upon the\n"
    .string "housetops, which withereth afore it\l"
    .string "groweth up:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_7::
    .string "Wherewith the mower filleth not\n"
    .string "his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves\l"
    .string "his bosom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_129_8::
    .string "Neither do they which go by say, The\n"
    .string "blessing of the LORD be upon you: we\l"
    .string "bless you in the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_1::
    .string "Out of the depths have I cried unto\n"
    .string "thee, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_2::
    .string "Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears\n"
    .string "be attentive to the voice of my\l"
    .string "supplications.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_3::
    .string "If thou, LORD, shouldest mark\n"
    .string "iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_4::
    .string "But there is forgiveness with thee,\n"
    .string "that thou mayest be feared.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_5::
    .string "I wait for the LORD, my soul doth\n"
    .string "wait, and in his word do I hope.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_6::
    .string "My soul waiteth for the Lord more\n"
    .string "than they that watch for the morning:\l"
    .string "I say, more than they that watch for\l"
    .string "the morning.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_7::
    .string "Let Israel hope in the LORD: for\n"
    .string "with the LORD there is mercy, and\l"
    .string "with him is plenteous redemption.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_130_8::
    .string "And he shall redeem Israel from\n"
    .string "all his iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_131_1::
    .string "Lord, my heart is not haughty, nor\n"
    .string "mine eyes lofty: neither do I\l"
    .string "exercise myself in great matters, or\l"
    .string "in things too high for me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_131_2::
    .string "Surely I have behaved and quieted\n"
    .string "myself, as a child that is weaned of\l"
    .string "his mother: my soul is even as a\l"
    .string "weaned child.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_131_3::
    .string "Let Israel hope in the LORD from\n"
    .string "henceforth and for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_1::
    .string "Lord, remember David, and all his\n"
    .string "afflictions:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_2::
    .string "How he sware unto the LORD, and\n"
    .string "vowed unto the mighty God of Jacob;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_3::
    .string "Surely I will not come into the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of my house, nor go up\l"
    .string "into my bed;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_4::
    .string "I will not give sleep to mine\n"
    .string "eyes, or slumber to mine eyelids,$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_5::
    .string "Until I find out a place for the\n"
    .string "LORD, an habitation for the mighty\l"
    .string "God of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_6::
    .string "Lo, we heard of it at Ephratah: we\n"
    .string "found it in the fields of the wood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_7::
    .string "We will go into his tabernacles:\n"
    .string "we will worship at his footstool.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_8::
    .string "Arise, O LORD, into thy rest; thou,\n"
    .string "and the ark of thy strength.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_9::
    .string "Let thy priests be clothed with\n"
    .string "righteousness; and let thy saints\l"
    .string "shout for joy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_10::
    .string "For thy servant David’s sake turn\n"
    .string "not away the face of thine anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_11::
    .string "The LORD hath sworn in truth unto\n"
    .string "David; he will not turn from it; Of\l"
    .string "the fruit of thy body will I set\l"
    .string "upon thy throne.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_12::
    .string "If thy children will keep my\n"
    .string "covenant and my testimony that I\l"
    .string "shall teach them, their children\l"
    .string "shall also sit upon thy throne for\l"
    .string "evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_13::
    .string "For the LORD hath chosen Zion; he\n"
    .string "hath desired it for his habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_14::
    .string "This is my rest for ever: here will\n"
    .string "I dwell; for I have desired it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_15::
    .string "I will abundantly bless her\n"
    .string "provision: I will satisfy her poor\l"
    .string "with bread.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_16::
    .string "I will also clothe her priests\n"
    .string "with salvation: and her saints\l"
    .string "shall shout aloud for joy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_17::
    .string "There will I make the horn of David\n"
    .string "to bud: I have ordained a lamp for\l"
    .string "mine anointed.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_132_18::
    .string "His enemies will I clothe with\n"
    .string "shame: but upon himself shall his\l"
    .string "crown flourish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_133_1::
    .string "Behold, how good and how pleasant\n"
    .string "it is for brethren to dwell\l"
    .string "together in unity!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_133_2::
    .string "It is like the precious ointment\n"
    .string "upon the head, that ran down upon\l"
    .string "the beard, even Aaron’s beard: that\l"
    .string "went down to the skirts of his\l"
    .string "garments;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_133_3::
    .string "As the dew of Hermon, and as the dew\n"
    .string "that descended upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Zion: for there the LORD commanded\l"
    .string "the blessing, even life for\l"
    .string "evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_134_1::
    .string "Behold, bless ye the LORD, all ye\n"
    .string "servants of the LORD, which by night\l"
    .string "stand in the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_134_2::
    .string "Lift up your hands in the\n"
    .string "sanctuary, and bless the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_134_3::
    .string "The LORD that made heaven and earth\n"
    .string "bless thee out of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the\n"
    .string "name of the LORD; praise him, O ye\l"
    .string "servants of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_2::
    .string "Ye that stand in the house of the\n"
    .string "LORD, in the courts of the house of\l"
    .string "our God.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_3::
    .string "Praise the LORD; for the LORD is\n"
    .string "good: sing praises unto his name;\l"
    .string "for it is pleasant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_4::
    .string "For the LORD hath chosen Jacob unto\n"
    .string "himself, and Israel for his\l"
    .string "peculiar treasure.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_5::
    .string "For I know that the LORD is great,\n"
    .string "and that our Lord is above all gods.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_6::
    .string "Whatsoever the LORD pleased, that\n"
    .string "did he in heaven, and in earth, in the\l"
    .string "seas, and all deep places.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_7::
    .string "He causeth the vapours to ascend\n"
    .string "from the ends of the earth; he maketh\l"
    .string "lightnings for the rain; he bringeth\l"
    .string "the wind out of his treasuries.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_8::
    .string "Who smote the firstborn of Egypt,\n"
    .string "both of man and beast.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_9::
    .string "Who sent tokens and wonders into the\n"
    .string "midst of thee, O Egypt, upon\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_10::
    .string "Who smote great nations, and slew\n"
    .string "mighty kings;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_11::
    .string "Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og\n"
    .string "king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms\l"
    .string "of Canaan:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_12::
    .string "And gave their land for an\n"
    .string "heritage, an heritage unto Israel\l"
    .string "his people.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_13::
    .string "Thy name, O LORD, endureth for ever;\n"
    .string "and thy memorial, O LORD, throughout\l"
    .string "all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_14::
    .string "For the LORD will judge his\n"
    .string "people, and he will repent\l"
    .string "himself concerning his servants.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_15::
    .string "The idols of the heathen are\n"
    .string "silver and gold, the work of men’s\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_16::
    .string "They have mouths, but they speak\n"
    .string "not; eyes have they, but they see not;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_17::
    .string "They have ears, but they hear not;\n"
    .string "neither is there any breath in their\l"
    .string "mouths.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_18::
    .string "They that make them are like unto\n"
    .string "them: so is every one that trusteth\l"
    .string "in them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_19::
    .string "Bless the LORD, O house of Israel:\n"
    .string "bless the LORD, O house of Aaron:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_20::
    .string "Bless the LORD, O house of Levi: ye\n"
    .string "that fear the LORD, bless the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_135_21::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD out of Zion,\n"
    .string "which dwelleth at Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_1::
    .string "O give thanks unto the LORD; for he\n"
    .string "is good: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_2::
    .string "O give thanks unto the God of gods:\n"
    .string "for his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_3::
    .string "O give thanks to the Lord of lords:\n"
    .string "for his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_4::
    .string "To him who alone doeth great\n"
    .string "wonders: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_5::
    .string "To him that by wisdom made the\n"
    .string "heavens: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_6::
    .string "To him that stretched out the earth\n"
    .string "above the waters: for his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_7::
    .string "To him that made great lights: for\n"
    .string "his mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_8::
    .string "The sun to rule by day: for his\n"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_9::
    .string "The moon and stars to rule by night:\n"
    .string "for his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_10::
    .string "To him that smote Egypt in their\n"
    .string "firstborn: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_11::
    .string "And brought out Israel from among\n"
    .string "them: for his mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_12::
    .string "With a strong hand, and with a\n"
    .string "stretched out arm: for his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_13::
    .string "To him which divided the Red sea\n"
    .string "into parts: for his mercy endureth\l"
    .string "for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_14::
    .string "And made Israel to pass through\n"
    .string "the midst of it: for his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_15::
    .string "But overthrew Pharaoh and his host\n"
    .string "in the Red sea: for his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_16::
    .string "To him which led his people\n"
    .string "through the wilderness: for his\l"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_17::
    .string "To him which smote great kings: for\n"
    .string "his mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_18::
    .string "And slew famous kings: for his\n"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_19::
    .string "Sihon king of the Amorites: for his\n"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_20::
    .string "And Og the king of Bashan: for his\n"
    .string "mercy endureth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_21::
    .string "And gave their land for an\n"
    .string "heritage: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_22::
    .string "Even an heritage unto Israel his\n"
    .string "servant: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_23::
    .string "Who remembered us in our low\n"
    .string "estate: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_24::
    .string "And hath redeemed us from our\n"
    .string "enemies: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_25::
    .string "Who giveth food to all flesh: for\n"
    .string "his mercy endureth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_136_26::
    .string "O give thanks unto the God of\n"
    .string "heaven: for his mercy endureth for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_1::
    .string "By the rivers of Babylon, there we\n"
    .string "sat down, yea, we wept, when we\l"
    .string "remembered Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_2::
    .string "We hanged our harps upon the\n"
    .string "willows in the midst thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_3::
    .string "For there they that carried us away\n"
    .string "captive required of us a song; and\l"
    .string "they that wasted us required of us\l"
    .string "mirth, saying, Sing us one of the\l"
    .string "songs of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_4::
    .string "How shall we sing the LORD’s song\n"
    .string "in a strange land?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_5::
    .string "If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let\n"
    .string "my right hand forget her cunning.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_6::
    .string "If I do not remember thee, let my\n"
    .string "tongue cleave to the roof of my\l"
    .string "mouth; if I prefer not Jerusalem\l"
    .string "above my chief joy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_7::
    .string "Remember, O LORD, the children of\n"
    .string "Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who\l"
    .string "said, Rase it, rase it, even to the\l"
    .string "foundation thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_8::
    .string "O daughter of Babylon, who art to be\n"
    .string "destroyed; happy shall he be, that\l"
    .string "rewardeth thee as thou hast served us.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_137_9::
    .string "Happy shall he be, that taketh\n"
    .string "and dasheth thy little ones against\l"
    .string "the stones.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_1::
    .string "I will praise thee with my whole\n"
    .string "heart: before the gods will I sing\l"
    .string "praise unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_2::
    .string "I will worship toward thy holy\n"
    .string "temple, and praise thy name for thy\l"
    .string "lovingkindness and for thy truth: for\l"
    .string "thou hast magnified thy word above\l"
    .string "all thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_3::
    .string "In the day when I cried thou\n"
    .string "answeredst me, and strengthenedst me\l"
    .string "with strength in my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_4::
    .string "All the kings of the earth shall\n"
    .string "praise thee, O LORD, when they hear\l"
    .string "the words of thy mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_5::
    .string "Yea, they shall sing in the ways of\n"
    .string "the LORD: for great is the glory of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_6::
    .string "Though the LORD be high, yet hath he\n"
    .string "respect unto the lowly: but the\l"
    .string "proud he knoweth afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_7::
    .string "Though I walk in the midst of\n"
    .string "trouble, thou wilt revive me: thou\l"
    .string "shalt stretch forth thine hand\l"
    .string "against the wrath of mine enemies,\l"
    .string "and thy right hand shall save me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_138_8::
    .string "The LORD will perfect that which\n"
    .string "concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD,\l"
    .string "endureth for ever: forsake not the\l"
    .string "works of thine own hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_1::
    .string "O lord, thou hast searched me, and\n"
    .string "known me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_2::
    .string "Thou knowest my downsitting and\n"
    .string "mine uprising, thou understandest my\l"
    .string "thought afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_3::
    .string "Thou compassest my path and my\n"
    .string "lying down, and art acquainted with\l"
    .string "all my ways.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_4::
    .string "For there is not a word in my tongue,\n"
    .string "but, lo, O LORD, thou knowest it\l"
    .string "altogether.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_5::
    .string "Thou hast beset me behind and\n"
    .string "before, and laid thine hand upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_6::
    .string "Such knowledge is too wonderful\n"
    .string "for me; it is high, I cannot attain\l"
    .string "unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_7::
    .string "Whither shall I go from thy\n"
    .string "spirit? or whither shall I flee\l"
    .string "from thy presence?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_8::
    .string "If I ascend up into heaven, thou art\n"
    .string "there: if I make my bed in hell,\l"
    .string "behold, thou art there.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_9::
    .string "If I take the wings of the morning,\n"
    .string "and dwell in the uttermost parts of\l"
    .string "the sea;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_10::
    .string "Even there shall thy hand lead me,\n"
    .string "and thy right hand shall hold me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_11::
    .string "If I say, Surely the darkness\n"
    .string "shall cover me; even the night\l"
    .string "shall be light about me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_12::
    .string "Yea, the darkness hideth not from\n"
    .string "thee; but the night shineth as the\l"
    .string "day: the darkness and the light are\l"
    .string "both alike to thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_13::
    .string "For thou hast possessed my reins:\n"
    .string "thou hast covered me in my mother’s\l"
    .string "womb.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_14::
    .string "I will praise thee; for I am\n"
    .string "fearfully and wonderfully made:\l"
    .string "marvellous are thy works; and that\l"
    .string "my soul knoweth right well.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_15::
    .string "My substance was not hid from thee,\n"
    .string "when I was made in secret, and\l"
    .string "curiously wrought in the lowest\l"
    .string "parts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_16::
    .string "Thine eyes did see my substance, yet\n"
    .string "being unperfect; and in thy book\l"
    .string "all my members were written, which\l"
    .string "in continuance were fashioned, when\l"
    .string "as yet there was none of them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_17::
    .string "How precious also are thy thoughts\n"
    .string "unto me, O God! how great is the sum\l"
    .string "of them!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_18::
    .string "If I should count them, they are\n"
    .string "more in number than the sand: when I\l"
    .string "awake, I am still with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_19::
    .string "Surely thou wilt slay the wicked,\n"
    .string "O God: depart from me therefore, ye\l"
    .string "bloody men.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_20::
    .string "For they speak against thee\n"
    .string "wickedly, and thine enemies take thy\l"
    .string "name in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_21::
    .string "Do not I hate them, O LORD, that hate\n"
    .string "thee? and am not I grieved with those\l"
    .string "that rise up against thee?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_22::
    .string "I hate them with perfect hatred: I\n"
    .string "count them mine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_23::
    .string "Search me, O God, and know my heart:\n"
    .string "try me, and know my thoughts:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_139_24::
    .string "And see if there be any wicked way\n"
    .string "in me, and lead me in the way\l"
    .string "everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_1::
    .string "Deliver me, O LORD, from the evil\n"
    .string "man: preserve me from the violent\l"
    .string "man;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_2::
    .string "Which imagine mischiefs in their\n"
    .string "heart; continually are they\l"
    .string "gathered together for war.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_3::
    .string "They have sharpened their tongues\n"
    .string "like a serpent; adders’ poison is\l"
    .string "under their lips. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_4::
    .string "Keep me, O LORD, from the hands of\n"
    .string "the wicked; preserve me from the\l"
    .string "violent man; who have purposed to\l"
    .string "overthrow my goings.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_5::
    .string "The proud have hid a snare for me,\n"
    .string "and cords; they have spread a net by\l"
    .string "the wayside; they have set gins for me\l"
    .string " Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_6::
    .string "I said unto the LORD, Thou art my\n"
    .string "God: hear the voice of my\l"
    .string "supplications, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_7::
    .string "O GOD the Lord, the strength of my\n"
    .string "salvation, thou hast covered my head\l"
    .string "in the day of battle.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_8::
    .string "Grant not, O LORD, the desires of\n"
    .string "the wicked: further not his wicked\l"
    .string "device; lest they exalt\l"
    .string "themselves. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_9::
    .string "As for the head of those that\n"
    .string "compass me about, let the mischief\l"
    .string "of their own lips cover them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_10::
    .string "Let burning coals fall upon them:\n"
    .string "let them be cast into the fire; into\l"
    .string "deep pits, that they rise not up\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_11::
    .string "Let not an evil speaker be\n"
    .string "established in the earth: evil\l"
    .string "shall hunt the violent man to\l"
    .string "overthrow him.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_12::
    .string "I know that the LORD will maintain\n"
    .string "the cause of the afflicted, and the\l"
    .string "right of the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_140_13::
    .string "Surely the righteous shall give\n"
    .string "thanks unto thy name: the upright\l"
    .string "shall dwell in thy presence.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_1::
    .string "Lord, I cry unto thee: make haste\n"
    .string "unto me; give ear unto my voice, when\l"
    .string "I cry unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_2::
    .string "Let my prayer be set forth before\n"
    .string "thee as incense; and the lifting up\l"
    .string "of my hands as the evening sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_3::
    .string "Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth;\n"
    .string "keep the door of my lips.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_4::
    .string "Incline not my heart to any evil\n"
    .string "thing, to practise wicked works with\l"
    .string "men that work iniquity: and let me\l"
    .string "not eat of their dainties.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_5::
    .string "Let the righteous smite me; it\n"
    .string "shall be a kindness: and let him\l"
    .string "reprove me; it shall be an\l"
    .string "excellent oil, which shall not\l"
    .string "break my head: for yet my prayer\l"
    .string "also shall be in their calamities.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_6::
    .string "When their judges are overthrown in\n"
    .string "stony places, they shall hear my\l"
    .string "words; for they are sweet.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_7::
    .string "Our bones are scattered at the\n"
    .string "grave’s mouth, as when one cutteth\l"
    .string "and cleaveth wood upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_8::
    .string "But mine eyes are unto thee, O GOD\n"
    .string "the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave\l"
    .string "not my soul destitute.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_9::
    .string "Keep me from the snares which they\n"
    .string "have laid for me, and the gins of the\l"
    .string "workers of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_141_10::
    .string "Let the wicked fall into their own\n"
    .string "nets, whilst that I withal escape.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_1::
    .string "I cried unto the LORD with my voice;\n"
    .string "with my voice unto the LORD did I\l"
    .string "make my supplication.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_2::
    .string "I poured out my complaint before\n"
    .string "him; I shewed before him my trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_3::
    .string "When my spirit was overwhelmed\n"
    .string "within me, then thou knewest my\l"
    .string "path. In the way wherein I walked\l"
    .string "have they privily laid a snare for\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_4::
    .string "I looked on my right hand, and\n"
    .string "beheld, but there was no man that\l"
    .string "would know me: refuge failed me; no\l"
    .string "man cared for my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_5::
    .string "I cried unto thee, O LORD: I said,\n"
    .string "Thou art my refuge and my portion in\l"
    .string "the land of the living.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_6::
    .string "Attend unto my cry; for I am brought\n"
    .string "very low: deliver me from my\l"
    .string "persecutors; for they are stronger\l"
    .string "than I.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_142_7::
    .string "Bring my soul out of prison, that I\n"
    .string "may praise thy name: the righteous\l"
    .string "shall compass me about; for thou\l"
    .string "shalt deal bountifully with me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_1::
    .string "Hear my prayer, O LORD, give ear to\n"
    .string "my supplications: in thy\l"
    .string "faithfulness answer me, and in thy\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_2::
    .string "And enter not into judgment with thy\n"
    .string "servant: for in thy sight shall no\l"
    .string "man living be justified.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_3::
    .string "For the enemy hath persecuted my\n"
    .string "soul; he hath smitten my life down\l"
    .string "to the ground; he hath made me to\l"
    .string "dwell in darkness, as those that\l"
    .string "have been long dead.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_4::
    .string "Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed\n"
    .string "within me; my heart within me is\l"
    .string "desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_5::
    .string "I remember the days of old; I\n"
    .string "meditate on all thy works; I muse on\l"
    .string "the work of thy hands.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_6::
    .string "I stretch forth my hands unto thee:\n"
    .string "my soul thirsteth after thee, as a\l"
    .string "thirsty land. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_7::
    .string "Hear me speedily, O LORD: my\n"
    .string "spirit faileth: hide not thy face\l"
    .string "from me, lest I be like unto them\l"
    .string "that go down into the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_8::
    .string "Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness\n"
    .string "in the morning; for in thee do I\l"
    .string "trust: cause me to know the way\l"
    .string "wherein I should walk; for I lift\l"
    .string "up my soul unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_9::
    .string "Deliver me, O LORD, from mine\n"
    .string "enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_10::
    .string "Teach me to do thy will; for thou\n"
    .string "art my God: thy spirit is good; lead\l"
    .string "me into the land of uprightness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_11::
    .string "Quicken me, O LORD, for thy name’s\n"
    .string "sake: for thy righteousness’ sake\l"
    .string "bring my soul out of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_143_12::
    .string "And of thy mercy cut off mine\n"
    .string "enemies, and destroy all them that\l"
    .string "afflict my soul: for I am thy\l"
    .string "servant.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_1::
    .string "Blessed be the LORD my strength,\n"
    .string "which teacheth my hands to war, and\l"
    .string "my fingers to fight:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_2::
    .string "My goodness, and my fortress; my\n"
    .string "high tower, and my deliverer; my\l"
    .string "shield, and he in whom I trust; who\l"
    .string "subdueth my people under me.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_3::
    .string "LORD, what is man, that thou takest\n"
    .string "knowledge of him! or the son of man,\l"
    .string "that thou makest account of him!$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_4::
    .string "Man is like to vanity: his days are\n"
    .string "as a shadow that passeth away.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_5::
    .string "Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come\n"
    .string "down: touch the mountains, and they\l"
    .string "shall smoke.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_6::
    .string "Cast forth lightning, and scatter\n"
    .string "them: shoot out thine arrows, and\l"
    .string "destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_7::
    .string "Send thine hand from above; rid me,\n"
    .string "and deliver me out of great waters,\l"
    .string "from the hand of strange children;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_8::
    .string "Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and\n"
    .string "their right hand is a right hand of\l"
    .string "falsehood.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_9::
    .string "I will sing a new song unto thee, O\n"
    .string "God: upon a psaltery and an\l"
    .string "instrument of ten strings will I\l"
    .string "sing praises unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_10::
    .string "It is he that giveth salvation unto\n"
    .string "kings: who delivereth David his\l"
    .string "servant from the hurtful sword.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_11::
    .string "Rid me, and deliver me from the hand\n"
    .string "of strange children, whose mouth\l"
    .string "speaketh vanity, and their right\l"
    .string "hand is a right hand of falsehood:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_12::
    .string "That our sons may be as plants\n"
    .string "grown up in their youth; that our\l"
    .string "daughters may be as corner stones,\l"
    .string "polished after the similitude of a\l"
    .string "palace:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_13::
    .string "That our garners may be full,\n"
    .string "affording all manner of store: that\l"
    .string "our sheep may bring forth thousands\l"
    .string "and ten thousands in our streets:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_14::
    .string "That our oxen may be strong to\n"
    .string "labour; that there be no breaking in,\l"
    .string "nor going out; that there be no\l"
    .string "complaining in our streets.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_144_15::
    .string "Happy is that people, that is in\n"
    .string "such a case: yea, happy is that\l"
    .string "people, whose God is the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_1::
    .string "I will extol thee, my God, O king;\n"
    .string "and I will bless thy name for ever\l"
    .string "and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_2::
    .string "Every day will I bless thee; and I\n"
    .string "will praise thy name for ever and\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_3::
    .string "Great is the LORD, and greatly to be\n"
    .string "praised; and his greatness is\l"
    .string "unsearchable.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_4::
    .string "One generation shall praise thy\n"
    .string "works to another, and shall declare\l"
    .string "thy mighty acts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_5::
    .string "I will speak of the glorious\n"
    .string "honour of thy majesty, and of thy\l"
    .string "wondrous works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_6::
    .string "And men shall speak of the might\n"
    .string "of thy terrible acts: and I will\l"
    .string "declare thy greatness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_7::
    .string "They shall abundantly utter the\n"
    .string "memory of thy great goodness, and\l"
    .string "shall sing of thy righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_8::
    .string "The LORD is gracious, and full of\n"
    .string "compassion; slow to anger, and of\l"
    .string "great mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_9::
    .string "The LORD is good to all: and his\n"
    .string "tender mercies are over all his\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_10::
    .string "All thy works shall praise thee,\n"
    .string "O LORD; and thy saints shall bless\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_11::
    .string "They shall speak of the glory of\n"
    .string "thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_12::
    .string "To make known to the sons of men his\n"
    .string "mighty acts, and the glorious\l"
    .string "majesty of his kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_13::
    .string "Thy kingdom is an everlasting\n"
    .string "kingdom, and thy dominion endureth\l"
    .string "throughout all generations.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_14::
    .string "The LORD upholdeth all that\n"
    .string "fall, and raiseth up all those\l"
    .string "that be bowed down.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_15::
    .string "The eyes of all wait upon thee;\n"
    .string "and thou givest them their meat in\l"
    .string "due season.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_16::
    .string "Thou openest thine hand, and\n"
    .string "satisfiest the desire of every\l"
    .string "living thing.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_17::
    .string "The LORD is righteous in all his\n"
    .string "ways, and holy in all his works.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_18::
    .string "The LORD is nigh unto all them that\n"
    .string "call upon him, to all that call\l"
    .string "upon him in truth.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_19::
    .string "He will fulfil the desire of them\n"
    .string "that fear him: he also will hear\l"
    .string "their cry, and will save them.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_20::
    .string "The LORD preserveth all them that\n"
    .string "love him: but all the wicked will\l"
    .string "he destroy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_145_21::
    .string "My mouth shall speak the praise\n"
    .string "of the LORD: and let all flesh\l"
    .string "bless his holy name for ever and\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Praise the LORD,\n"
    .string "O my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_2::
    .string "While I live will I praise the\n"
    .string "LORD: I will sing praises unto my\l"
    .string "God while I have any being.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_3::
    .string "Put not your trust in princes, nor\n"
    .string "in the son of man, in whom there is no\l"
    .string "help.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_4::
    .string "His breath goeth forth, he returneth\n"
    .string "to his earth; in that very day his\l"
    .string "thoughts perish.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_5::
    .string "Happy is he that hath the God of\n"
    .string "Jacob for his help, whose hope is\l"
    .string "in the LORD his God:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_6::
    .string "Which made heaven, and earth, the\n"
    .string "sea, and all that therein is: which\l"
    .string "keepeth truth for ever:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_7::
    .string "Which executeth judgment for the\n"
    .string "oppressed: which giveth food to the\l"
    .string "hungry. The LORD looseth the\l"
    .string "prisoners:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_8::
    .string "The LORD openeth the eyes of the\n"
    .string "blind: the LORD raiseth them that\l"
    .string "are bowed down: the LORD loveth the\l"
    .string "righteous:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_9::
    .string "The LORD preserveth the strangers;\n"
    .string "he relieveth the fatherless and\l"
    .string "widow: but the way of the wicked he\l"
    .string "turneth upside down.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_146_10::
    .string "The LORD shall reign for ever, even\n"
    .string "thy God, O Zion, unto all\l"
    .string "generations. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD: for it is good to\n"
    .string "sing praises unto our God; for it is\l"
    .string "pleasant; and praise is comely.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_2::
    .string "The LORD doth build up Jerusalem:\n"
    .string "he gathereth together the outcasts\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_3::
    .string "He healeth the broken in heart, and\n"
    .string "bindeth up their wounds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_4::
    .string "He telleth the number of the stars;\n"
    .string "he calleth them all by their names.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_5::
    .string "Great is our Lord, and of great\n"
    .string "power: his understanding is infinite.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_6::
    .string "The LORD lifteth up the meek: he\n"
    .string "casteth the wicked down to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_7::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD with\n"
    .string "thanksgiving; sing praise upon the\l"
    .string "harp unto our God:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_8::
    .string "Who covereth the heaven with\n"
    .string "clouds, who prepareth rain for the\l"
    .string "earth, who maketh grass to grow upon\l"
    .string "the mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_9::
    .string "He giveth to the beast his food, and\n"
    .string "to the young ravens which cry.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_10::
    .string "He delighteth not in the strength\n"
    .string "of the horse: he taketh not pleasure\l"
    .string "in the legs of a man.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_11::
    .string "The LORD taketh pleasure in them\n"
    .string "that fear him, in those that hope in\l"
    .string "his mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_12::
    .string "Praise the LORD, O Jerusalem;\n"
    .string "praise thy God, O Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_13::
    .string "For he hath strengthened the bars of\n"
    .string "thy gates; he hath blessed thy\l"
    .string "children within thee.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_14::
    .string "He maketh peace in thy borders, and\n"
    .string "filleth thee with the finest of the\l"
    .string "wheat.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_15::
    .string "He sendeth forth his commandment\n"
    .string "upon earth: his word runneth very\l"
    .string "swiftly.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_16::
    .string "He giveth snow like wool: he\n"
    .string "scattereth the hoarfrost like ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_17::
    .string "He casteth forth his ice like\n"
    .string "morsels: who can stand before his\l"
    .string "cold?$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_18::
    .string "He sendeth out his word, and\n"
    .string "melteth them: he causeth his wind to\l"
    .string "blow, and the waters flow.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_19::
    .string "He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his\n"
    .string "statutes and his judgments unto\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_147_20::
    .string "He hath not dealt so with any\n"
    .string "nation: and as for his judgments,\l"
    .string "they have not known them. Praise ye\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the\n"
    .string "LORD from the heavens: praise him in\l"
    .string "the heights.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_2::
    .string "Praise ye him, all his angels:\n"
    .string "praise ye him, all his hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_3::
    .string "Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise\n"
    .string "him, all ye stars of light.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_4::
    .string "Praise him, ye heavens of heavens,\n"
    .string "and ye waters that be above the\l"
    .string "heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_5::
    .string "Let them praise the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD: for he commanded, and they were\l"
    .string "created.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_6::
    .string "He hath also stablished them for\n"
    .string "ever and ever: he hath made a decree\l"
    .string "which shall not pass.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_7::
    .string "Praise the LORD from the earth, ye\n"
    .string "dragons, and all deeps:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_8::
    .string "Fire, and hail; snow, and vapours;\n"
    .string "stormy wind fulfilling his word:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_9::
    .string "Mountains, and all hills;\n"
    .string "fruitful trees, and all cedars:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_10::
    .string "Beasts, and all cattle; creeping\n"
    .string "things, and flying fowl:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_11::
    .string "Kings of the earth, and all\n"
    .string "people; princes, and all judges\l"
    .string "of the earth:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_12::
    .string "Both young men, and maidens; old\n"
    .string "men, and children:$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_13::
    .string "Let them praise the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD: for his name alone is\l"
    .string "excellent; his glory is above the\l"
    .string "earth and heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_148_14::
    .string "He also exalteth the horn of his\n"
    .string "people, the praise of all his\l"
    .string "saints; even of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel, a people near unto him.\l"
    .string "Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the\n"
    .string "LORD a new song, and his praise in\l"
    .string "the congregation of saints.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_2::
    .string "Let Israel rejoice in him that made\n"
    .string "him: let the children of Zion be\l"
    .string "joyful in their King.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_3::
    .string "Let them praise his name in the\n"
    .string "dance: let them sing praises unto\l"
    .string "him with the timbrel and harp.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_4::
    .string "For the LORD taketh pleasure in\n"
    .string "his people: he will beautify the\l"
    .string "meek with salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_5::
    .string "Let the saints be joyful in glory:\n"
    .string "let them sing aloud upon their beds.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_6::
    .string "Let the high praises of God be in\n"
    .string "their mouth, and a two-edged sword in\l"
    .string "their hand;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_7::
    .string "To execute vengeance upon the\n"
    .string "heathen, and punishments upon the\l"
    .string "people;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_8::
    .string "To bind their kings with chains, and\n"
    .string "their nobles with fetters of iron;$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_149_9::
    .string "To execute upon them the judgment\n"
    .string "written: this honour have all his\l"
    .string "saints. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_1::
    .string "Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in\n"
    .string "his sanctuary: praise him in the\l"
    .string "firmament of his power.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_2::
    .string "Praise him for his mighty acts:\n"
    .string "praise him according to his\l"
    .string "excellent greatness.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_3::
    .string "Praise him with the sound of the\n"
    .string "trumpet: praise him with the\l"
    .string "psaltery and harp.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_4::
    .string "Praise him with the timbrel and\n"
    .string "dance: praise him with stringed\l"
    .string "instruments and organs.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_5::
    .string "Praise him upon the loud cymbals:\n"
    .string "praise him upon the high sounding\l"
    .string "cymbals.$"
Bible_Text_Psalms_150_6::
    .string "Let every thing that hath breath\n"
    .string "praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_1::
    .string "The proverbs of Solomon the son of\n"
    .string "David, king of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_2::
    .string "To know wisdom and instruction; to\n"
    .string "perceive the words of understanding;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_3::
    .string "To receive the instruction of\n"
    .string "wisdom, justice, and judgment, and\l"
    .string "equity;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_4::
    .string "To give subtilty to the simple, to\n"
    .string "the young man knowledge and\l"
    .string "discretion$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_5::
    .string "A wise man will hear, and will\n"
    .string "increase learning; and a man of\l"
    .string "understanding shall attain unto\l"
    .string "wise counsels:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_6::
    .string "To understand a proverb, and the\n"
    .string "interpretation; the words of the\l"
    .string "wise, and their dark sayings$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_7::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is the\n"
    .string "beginning of knowledge: but fools\l"
    .string "despise wisdom and instruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_8::
    .string "My son, hear the instruction of thy\n"
    .string "father, and forsake not the law of\l"
    .string "thy mother:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_9::
    .string "For they shall be an ornament of\n"
    .string "grace unto thy head, and chains about\l"
    .string "thy neck$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_10::
    .string "My son, if sinners entice thee,\n"
    .string "consent thou not.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_11::
    .string "If they say, Come with us, let us\n"
    .string "lay wait for blood, let us lurk\l"
    .string "privily for the innocent without\l"
    .string "cause:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_12::
    .string "Let us swallow them up alive as\n"
    .string "the grave; and whole, as those that\l"
    .string "go down into the pit:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_13::
    .string "We shall find all precious\n"
    .string "substance, we shall fill our\l"
    .string "houses with spoil:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_14::
    .string "Cast in thy lot among us; let us\n"
    .string "all have one purse:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_15::
    .string "My son, walk not thou in the way\n"
    .string "with them; refrain thy foot from\l"
    .string "their path:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_16::
    .string "For their feet run to evil, and make\n"
    .string "haste to shed blood$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_17::
    .string "Surely in vain the net is spread in\n"
    .string "the sight of any bird.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_18::
    .string "And they lay wait for their own\n"
    .string "blood; they lurk privily for their\l"
    .string "own lives.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_19::
    .string "So are the ways of every one that is\n"
    .string "greedy of gain; which taketh away the\l"
    .string "life of the owners thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_20::
    .string "Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth\n"
    .string "her voice in the streets:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_21::
    .string "She crieth in the chief place of\n"
    .string "concourse, in the openings of the\l"
    .string "gates: in the city she uttereth her\l"
    .string "words, saying,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_22::
    .string "How long, ye simple ones, will ye\n"
    .string "love simplicity? and the scorners\l"
    .string "delight in their scorning, and\l"
    .string "fools hate knowledge?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_23::
    .string "Turn you at my reproof: behold, I\n"
    .string "will pour out my spirit unto you, I\l"
    .string "will make known my words unto you$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_24::
    .string "Because I have called, and ye\n"
    .string "refused; I have stretched out my\l"
    .string "hand, and no man regarded;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_25::
    .string "But ye have set at nought all my\n"
    .string "counsel, and would none of my\l"
    .string "reproof:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_26::
    .string "I also will laugh at your\n"
    .string "calamity; I will mock when your\l"
    .string "fear cometh;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_27::
    .string "When your fear cometh as\n"
    .string "desolation, and your destruction\l"
    .string "cometh as a whirlwind; when distress\l"
    .string "and anguish cometh upon you$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_28::
    .string "Then shall they call upon me, but\n"
    .string "I will not answer; they shall seek\l"
    .string "me early, but they shall not find\l"
    .string "me:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_29::
    .string "For that they hated knowledge, and\n"
    .string "did not choose the fear of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_30::
    .string "They would none of my counsel: they\n"
    .string "despised all my reproof$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_31::
    .string "Therefore shall they eat of the\n"
    .string "fruit of their own way, and be\l"
    .string "filled with their own devices.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_32::
    .string "For the turning away of the simple\n"
    .string "shall slay them, and the\l"
    .string "prosperity of fools shall destroy\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_1_33::
    .string "But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall\n"
    .string "dwell safely, and shall be quiet\l"
    .string "from fear of evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_1::
    .string "My son, if thou wilt receive my\n"
    .string "words, and hide my commandments with\l"
    .string "thee;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_2::
    .string "So that thou incline thine ear unto\n"
    .string "wisdom, and apply thine heart to\l"
    .string "understanding;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_3::
    .string "Yea, if thou criest after\n"
    .string "knowledge, and liftest up thy voice\l"
    .string "for understanding;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_4::
    .string "If thou seekest her as silver, and\n"
    .string "searchest for her as for hid\l"
    .string "treasures;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_5::
    .string "Then shalt thou understand the fear\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and find the knowledge\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_6::
    .string "For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of\n"
    .string "his mouth cometh knowledge and\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_7::
    .string "He layeth up sound wisdom for the\n"
    .string "righteous: he is a buckler to them\l"
    .string "that walk uprightly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_8::
    .string "He keepeth the paths of judgment,\n"
    .string "and preserveth the way of his saints.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_9::
    .string "Then shalt thou understand\n"
    .string "righteousness, and judgment, and\l"
    .string "equity; yea, every good path.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_10::
    .string "When wisdom entereth into thine\n"
    .string "heart, and knowledge is pleasant\l"
    .string "unto thy soul;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_11::
    .string "Discretion shall preserve thee,\n"
    .string "understanding shall keep thee:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_12::
    .string "To deliver thee from the way of the\n"
    .string "evil man, from the man that speaketh\l"
    .string "froward things;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_13::
    .string "Who leave the paths of\n"
    .string "uprightness, to walk in the ways of\l"
    .string "darkness;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_14::
    .string "Who rejoice to do evil, and delight\n"
    .string "in the frowardness of the wicked;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_15::
    .string "Whose ways are crooked, and they\n"
    .string "froward in their paths:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_16::
    .string "To deliver thee from the strange\n"
    .string "woman, even from the stranger which\l"
    .string "flattereth with her words;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_17::
    .string "Which forsaketh the guide of her\n"
    .string "youth, and forgetteth the covenant of\l"
    .string "her God$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_18::
    .string "For her house inclineth unto death,\n"
    .string "and her paths unto the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_19::
    .string "None that go unto her return again,\n"
    .string "neither take they hold of the paths\l"
    .string "of life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_20::
    .string "That thou mayest walk in the way of\n"
    .string "good men, and keep the paths of the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_21::
    .string "For the upright shall dwell in\n"
    .string "the land, and the perfect shall\l"
    .string "remain in it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_2_22::
    .string "But the wicked shall be cut off\n"
    .string "from the earth, and the transgressors\l"
    .string "shall be rooted out of it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_1::
    .string "My son, forget not my law; but let\n"
    .string "thine heart keep my commandments:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_2::
    .string "For length of days, and long life,\n"
    .string "and peace, shall they add to thee$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_3::
    .string "Let not mercy and truth forsake\n"
    .string "thee: bind them about thy neck; write\l"
    .string "them upon the table of thine heart:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_4::
    .string "So shalt thou find favour and good\n"
    .string "understanding in the sight of God and\l"
    .string "man$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_5::
    .string "Trust in the LORD with all thine\n"
    .string "heart; and lean not unto thine own\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_6::
    .string "In all thy ways acknowledge him,\n"
    .string "and he shall direct thy paths.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_7::
    .string "Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear\n"
    .string "the LORD, and depart from evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_8::
    .string "It shall be health to thy navel,\n"
    .string "and marrow to thy bones.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_9::
    .string "Honour the LORD with thy substance,\n"
    .string "and with the firstfruits of all\l"
    .string "thine increase:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_10::
    .string "So shall thy barns be filled with\n"
    .string "plenty, and thy presses shall\l"
    .string "burst out with new wine$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_11::
    .string "My son, despise not the chastening\n"
    .string "of the LORD; neither be weary of his\l"
    .string "correction:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_12::
    .string "For whom the LORD loveth he\n"
    .string "correcteth; even as a father the son\l"
    .string "in whom he delighteth$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_13::
    .string "Happy is the man that findeth\n"
    .string "wisdom, and the man that getteth\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_14::
    .string "For the merchandise of it is better\n"
    .string "than the merchandise of silver, and\l"
    .string "the gain thereof than fine gold.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_15::
    .string "She is more precious than rubies:\n"
    .string "and all the things thou canst\l"
    .string "desire are not to be compared unto\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_16::
    .string "Length of days is in her right hand;\n"
    .string "and in her left hand riches and\l"
    .string "honour.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_17::
    .string "Her ways are ways of pleasantness,\n"
    .string "and all her paths are peace.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_18::
    .string "She is a tree of life to them that\n"
    .string "lay hold upon her: and happy is\l"
    .string "every one that retaineth her.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_19::
    .string "The LORD by wisdom hath founded the\n"
    .string "earth; by understanding hath he\l"
    .string "established the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_20::
    .string "By his knowledge the depths are\n"
    .string "broken up, and the clouds drop down\l"
    .string "the dew.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_21::
    .string "My son, let not them depart from\n"
    .string "thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and\l"
    .string "discretion:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_22::
    .string "So shall they be life unto thy\n"
    .string "soul, and grace to thy neck$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_23::
    .string "Then shalt thou walk in thy way\n"
    .string "safely, and thy foot shall not\l"
    .string "stumble.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_24::
    .string "When thou liest down, thou shalt\n"
    .string "not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie\l"
    .string "down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_25::
    .string "Be not afraid of sudden fear,\n"
    .string "neither of the desolation of the\l"
    .string "wicked, when it cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_26::
    .string "For the LORD shall be thy\n"
    .string "confidence, and shall keep thy foot\l"
    .string "from being taken.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_27::
    .string "Withhold not good from them to whom\n"
    .string "it is due, when it is in the power of\l"
    .string "thine hand to do it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_28::
    .string "Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and\n"
    .string "come again, and to morrow I will\l"
    .string "give; when thou hast it by thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_29::
    .string "Devise not evil against thy\n"
    .string "neighbour, seeing he dwelleth\l"
    .string "securely by thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_30::
    .string "Strive not with a man without cause,\n"
    .string "if he have done thee no harm.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_31::
    .string "Envy thou not the oppressor, and\n"
    .string "choose none of his ways.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_32::
    .string "For the froward is abomination to\n"
    .string "the LORD: but his secret is with the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_33::
    .string "The curse of the LORD is in the\n"
    .string "house of the wicked: but he blesseth\l"
    .string "the habitation of the just.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_34::
    .string "Surely he scorneth the scorners:\n"
    .string "but he giveth grace unto the lowly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_3_35::
    .string "The wise shall inherit glory: but\n"
    .string "shame shall be the promotion of\l"
    .string "fools.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_1::
    .string "Hear, ye children, the instruction\n"
    .string "of a father, and attend to know\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_2::
    .string "For I give you good doctrine,\n"
    .string "forsake ye not my law.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_3::
    .string "For I was my father’s son, tender\n"
    .string "and only beloved in the sight of my\l"
    .string "mother.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_4::
    .string "He taught me also, and said unto me,\n"
    .string "Let thine heart retain my words:\l"
    .string "keep my commandments, and live.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_5::
    .string "Get wisdom, get understanding:\n"
    .string "forget it not; neither decline from\l"
    .string "the words of my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_6::
    .string "Forsake her not, and she shall\n"
    .string "preserve thee: love her, and she\l"
    .string "shall keep thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_7::
    .string "Wisdom is the principal thing;\n"
    .string "therefore get wisdom: and with all\l"
    .string "thy getting get understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_8::
    .string "Exalt her, and she shall promote\n"
    .string "thee: she shall bring thee to\l"
    .string "honour, when thou dost embrace her.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_9::
    .string "She shall give to thine head an\n"
    .string "ornament of grace: a crown of glory\l"
    .string "shall she deliver to thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_10::
    .string "Hear, O my son, and receive my\n"
    .string "sayings; and the years of thy life\l"
    .string "shall be many.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_11::
    .string "I have taught thee in the way of\n"
    .string "wisdom; I have led thee in right\l"
    .string "paths.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_12::
    .string "When thou goest, thy steps shall\n"
    .string "not be straitened; and when thou\l"
    .string "runnest, thou shalt not stumble.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_13::
    .string "Take fast hold of instruction; let\n"
    .string "her not go: keep her; for she is thy\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_14::
    .string "Enter not into the path of the\n"
    .string "wicked, and go not in the way of evil\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_15::
    .string "Avoid it, pass not by it, turn from\n"
    .string "it, and pass away.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_16::
    .string "For they sleep not, except they\n"
    .string "have done mischief; and their sleep\l"
    .string "is taken away, unless they cause\l"
    .string "some to fall.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_17::
    .string "For they eat the bread of\n"
    .string "wickedness, and drink the wine of\l"
    .string "violence.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_18::
    .string "But the path of the just is as the\n"
    .string "shining light, that shineth more and\l"
    .string "more unto the perfect day.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_19::
    .string "The way of the wicked is as\n"
    .string "darkness: they know not at what they\l"
    .string "stumble.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_20::
    .string "My son, attend to my words; incline\n"
    .string "thine ear unto my sayings.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_21::
    .string "Let them not depart from thine\n"
    .string "eyes; keep them in the midst of thine\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_22::
    .string "For they are life unto those that\n"
    .string "find them, and health to all their\l"
    .string "flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_23::
    .string "Keep thy heart with all\n"
    .string "diligence; for out of it are the\l"
    .string "issues of life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_24::
    .string "Put away from thee a froward mouth,\n"
    .string "and perverse lips put far from\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_25::
    .string "Let thine eyes look right on, and\n"
    .string "let thine eyelids look straight\l"
    .string "before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_26::
    .string "Ponder the path of thy feet, and\n"
    .string "let all thy ways be established.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_4_27::
    .string "Turn not to the right hand nor to\n"
    .string "the left: remove thy foot from evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_1::
    .string "My son, attend unto my wisdom, and\n"
    .string "bow thine ear to my understanding:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_2::
    .string "That thou mayest regard discretion,\n"
    .string "and that thy lips may keep\l"
    .string "knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_3::
    .string "For the lips of a strange woman\n"
    .string "drop as an honeycomb, and her mouth\l"
    .string "is smoother than oil:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_4::
    .string "But her end is bitter as wormwood,\n"
    .string "sharp as a two-edged sword$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_5::
    .string "Her feet go down to death; her steps\n"
    .string "take hold on hell.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_6::
    .string "Lest thou shouldest ponder the\n"
    .string "path of life, her ways are moveable,\l"
    .string "that thou canst not know them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_7::
    .string "Hear me now therefore, O ye\n"
    .string "children, and depart not from the\l"
    .string "words of my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_8::
    .string "Remove thy way far from her, and\n"
    .string "come not nigh the door of her house:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_9::
    .string "Lest thou give thine honour unto\n"
    .string "others, and thy years unto the\l"
    .string "cruel:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_10::
    .string "Lest strangers be filled with thy\n"
    .string "wealth; and thy labours be in the\l"
    .string "house of a stranger;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_11::
    .string "And thou mourn at the last, when thy\n"
    .string "flesh and thy body are consumed,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_12::
    .string "And say, How have I hated\n"
    .string "instruction, and my heart despised\l"
    .string "reproof;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_13::
    .string "And have not obeyed the voice of my\n"
    .string "teachers, nor inclined mine ear to\l"
    .string "them that instructed me!"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_14::
    .string "I was almost in all evil in the\n"
    .string "midst of the congregation and\l"
    .string "assembly$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_15::
    .string "Drink waters out of thine own\n"
    .string "cistern, and running waters out of\l"
    .string "thine own well.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_16::
    .string "Let thy fountains be dispersed\n"
    .string "abroad, and rivers of waters in the\l"
    .string "streets.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_17::
    .string "Let them be only thine own, and not\n"
    .string "strangers’ with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_18::
    .string "Let thy fountain be blessed: and\n"
    .string "rejoice with the wife of thy youth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_19::
    .string "Let her be as the loving hind and\n"
    .string "pleasant roe; let her breasts\l"
    .string "satisfy thee at all times; and be\l"
    .string "thou ravished always with her love.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_20::
    .string "And why wilt thou, my son, be\n"
    .string "ravished with a strange woman, and\l"
    .string "embrace the bosom of a stranger?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_21::
    .string "For the ways of man are before the\n"
    .string "eyes of the LORD, and he pondereth\l"
    .string "all his goings$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_22::
    .string "His own iniquities shall take the\n"
    .string "wicked himself, and he shall be\l"
    .string "holden with the cords of his sins.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_5_23::
    .string "He shall die without instruction;\n"
    .string "and in the greatness of his folly he\l"
    .string "shall go astray.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_1::
    .string "My son, if thou be surety for thy\n"
    .string "friend, if thou hast stricken thy\l"
    .string "hand with a stranger,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_2::
    .string "Thou art snared with the words of\n"
    .string "thy mouth, thou art taken with the\l"
    .string "words of thy mouth$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_3::
    .string "Do this now, my son, and deliver\n"
    .string "thyself, when thou art come into the\l"
    .string "hand of thy friend; go, humble\l"
    .string "thyself, and make sure thy friend.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_4::
    .string "Give not sleep to thine eyes, nor\n"
    .string "slumber to thine eyelids.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_5::
    .string "Deliver thyself as a roe from the\n"
    .string "hand of the hunter, and as a bird from\l"
    .string "the hand of the fowler.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_6::
    .string "Go to the ant, thou sluggard;\n"
    .string "consider her ways, and be wise:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_7::
    .string "Which having no guide, overseer, or\n"
    .string "ruler,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_8::
    .string "Provideth her meat in the summer,\n"
    .string "and gathereth her food in the harvest$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_9::
    .string "How long wilt thou sleep, O\n"
    .string "sluggard? when wilt thou arise out\l"
    .string "of thy sleep?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_10::
    .string "Yet a little sleep, a little\n"
    .string "slumber, a little folding of the\l"
    .string "hands to sleep:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_11::
    .string "So shall thy poverty come as one\n"
    .string "that travelleth, and thy want as an\l"
    .string "armed man$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_12::
    .string "A naughty person, a wicked man,\n"
    .string "walketh with a froward mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_13::
    .string "He winketh with his eyes, he\n"
    .string "speaketh with his feet, he teacheth\l"
    .string "with his fingers;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_14::
    .string "Frowardness is in his heart, he\n"
    .string "deviseth mischief continually; he\l"
    .string "soweth discord$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_15::
    .string "Therefore shall his calamity come\n"
    .string "suddenly; suddenly shall he be\l"
    .string "broken without remedy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_16::
    .string "These six things doth the LORD hate:\n"
    .string "yea, seven are an abomination unto\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_17::
    .string "A proud look, a lying tongue, and\n"
    .string "hands that shed innocent blood,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_18::
    .string "An heart that deviseth wicked\n"
    .string "imaginations, feet that be swift in\l"
    .string "running to mischief,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_19::
    .string "A false witness that speaketh\n"
    .string "lies, and he that soweth discord\l"
    .string "among brethren$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_20::
    .string "My son, keep thy father’s\n"
    .string "commandment, and forsake not the law\l"
    .string "of thy mother:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_21::
    .string "Bind them continually upon thine\n"
    .string "heart, and tie them about thy neck$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_22::
    .string "When thou goest, it shall lead\n"
    .string "thee; when thou sleepest, it shall\l"
    .string "keep thee; and when thou awakest, it\l"
    .string "shall talk with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_23::
    .string "For the commandment is a lamp; and\n"
    .string "the law is light; and reproofs of\l"
    .string "instruction are the way of life:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_24::
    .string "To keep thee from the evil woman,\n"
    .string "from the flattery of the tongue of a\l"
    .string "strange woman$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_25::
    .string "Lust not after her beauty in thine\n"
    .string "heart; neither let her take thee\l"
    .string "with her eyelids.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_26::
    .string "For by means of a whorish woman a\n"
    .string "man is brought to a piece of bread:\l"
    .string "and the adultress will hunt for the\l"
    .string "precious life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_27::
    .string "Can a man take fire in his bosom, and\n"
    .string "his clothes not be burned?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_28::
    .string "Can one go upon hot coals, and his\n"
    .string "feet not be burned?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_29::
    .string "So he that goeth in to his\n"
    .string "neighbour’s wife; whosoever toucheth\l"
    .string "her shall not be innocent$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_30::
    .string "Men do not despise a thief, if he\n"
    .string "steal to satisfy his soul when he is\l"
    .string "hungry;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_31::
    .string "But if he be found, he shall\n"
    .string "restore sevenfold; he shall give\l"
    .string "all the substance of his house$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_32::
    .string "But whoso committeth adultery with\n"
    .string "a woman lacketh understanding: he\l"
    .string "that doeth it destroyeth his own\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_33::
    .string "A wound and dishonour shall he get;\n"
    .string "and his reproach shall not be\l"
    .string "wiped away.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_34::
    .string "For jealousy is the rage of a man:\n"
    .string "therefore he will not spare in the\l"
    .string "day of vengeance.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_6_35::
    .string "He will not regard any ransom;\n"
    .string "neither will he rest content,\l"
    .string "though thou givest many gifts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_1::
    .string "My son, keep my words, and lay up\n"
    .string "my commandments with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_2::
    .string "Keep my commandments, and live;\n"
    .string "and my law as the apple of thine\l"
    .string "eye.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_3::
    .string "Bind them upon thy fingers, write\n"
    .string "them upon the table of thine heart.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_4::
    .string "Say unto wisdom, Thou art my sister;\n"
    .string "and call understanding thy\l"
    .string "kinswoman:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_5::
    .string "That they may keep thee from the\n"
    .string "strange woman, from the stranger\l"
    .string "which flattereth with her words$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_6::
    .string "For at the window of my house I\n"
    .string "looked through my casement,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_7::
    .string "And beheld among the simple ones,\n"
    .string "I discerned among the youths, a young\l"
    .string "man void of understanding,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_8::
    .string "Passing through the street near her\n"
    .string "corner; and he went the way to her\l"
    .string "house,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_9::
    .string "In the twilight, in the evening, in\n"
    .string "the black and dark night:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_10::
    .string "And, behold, there met him a woman\n"
    .string "with the attire of an harlot, and\l"
    .string "subtil of heart$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_11::
    .string "(She is loud and stubborn; her feet\n"
    .string "abide not in her house:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_12::
    .string "Now is she without, now in the\n"
    .string "streets, and lieth in wait at every\l"
    .string "corner.)"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_13::
    .string "So she caught him, and kissed him,\n"
    .string "and with an impudent face said unto\l"
    .string "him,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_14::
    .string "I have peace offerings with me;\n"
    .string "this day have I payed my vows$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_15::
    .string "Therefore came I forth to meet thee,\n"
    .string "diligently to seek thy face, and I\l"
    .string "have found thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_16::
    .string "I have decked my bed with coverings\n"
    .string "of tapestry, with carved works, with\l"
    .string "fine linen of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_17::
    .string "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh,\n"
    .string "aloes, and cinnamon.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_18::
    .string "Come, let us take our fill of love\n"
    .string "until the morning: let us solace\l"
    .string "ourselves with loves.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_19::
    .string "For the goodman is not at home, he is\n"
    .string "gone a long journey:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_20::
    .string "He hath taken a bag of money with\n"
    .string "him, and will come home at the day\l"
    .string "appointed$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_21::
    .string "With her much fair speech she\n"
    .string "caused him to yield, with the\l"
    .string "flattering of her lips she forced\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_22::
    .string "He goeth after her straightway, as\n"
    .string "an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a\l"
    .string "fool to the correction of the\l"
    .string "stocks;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_23::
    .string "Till a dart strike through his\n"
    .string "liver; as a bird hasteth to the\l"
    .string "snare, and knoweth not that it is for\l"
    .string "his life$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_24::
    .string "Hearken unto me now therefore, O ye\n"
    .string "children, and attend to the words of\l"
    .string "my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_25::
    .string "Let not thine heart decline to her\n"
    .string "ways, go not astray in her paths.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_26::
    .string "For she hath cast down many wounded:\n"
    .string "yea, many strong men have been slain\l"
    .string "by her.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_7_27::
    .string "Her house is the way to hell, going\n"
    .string "down to the chambers of death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_1::
    .string "Doth not wisdom cry? and\n"
    .string "understanding put forth her voice?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_2::
    .string "She standeth in the top of high\n"
    .string "places, by the way in the places of\l"
    .string "the paths$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_3::
    .string "She crieth at the gates, at the\n"
    .string "entry of the city, at the coming in at\l"
    .string "the doors.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_4::
    .string "Unto you, O men, I call; and my\n"
    .string "voice is to the sons of man.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_5::
    .string "O ye simple, understand wisdom:\n"
    .string "and, ye fools, be ye of an\l"
    .string "understanding heart.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_6::
    .string "Hear; for I will speak of\n"
    .string "excellent things; and the opening\l"
    .string "of my lips shall be right things.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_7::
    .string "For my mouth shall speak truth;\n"
    .string "and wickedness is an abomination to\l"
    .string "my lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_8::
    .string "All the words of my mouth are in\n"
    .string "righteousness; there is nothing\l"
    .string "froward or perverse in them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_9::
    .string "They are all plain to him that\n"
    .string "understandeth, and right to them that\l"
    .string "find knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_10::
    .string "Receive my instruction, and not\n"
    .string "silver; and knowledge rather than\l"
    .string "choice gold.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_11::
    .string "For wisdom is better than rubies;\n"
    .string "and all the things that may be\l"
    .string "desired are not to be compared to it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_12::
    .string "I wisdom dwell with prudence, and\n"
    .string "find out knowledge of witty\l"
    .string "inventions.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_13::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is to hate\n"
    .string "evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the\l"
    .string "evil way, and the froward mouth, do I\l"
    .string "hate.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_14::
    .string "Counsel is mine, and sound wisdom:\n"
    .string "I am understanding; I have strength.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_15::
    .string "By me kings reign, and princes\n"
    .string "decree justice.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_16::
    .string "By me princes rule, and nobles,\n"
    .string "even all the judges of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_17::
    .string "I love them that love me; and those\n"
    .string "that seek me early shall find me.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_18::
    .string "Riches and honour are with me; yea,\n"
    .string "durable riches and righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_19::
    .string "My fruit is better than gold, yea,\n"
    .string "than fine gold; and my revenue than\l"
    .string "choice silver.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_20::
    .string "I lead in the way of righteousness,\n"
    .string "in the midst of the paths of\l"
    .string "judgment:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_21::
    .string "That I may cause those that love me\n"
    .string "to inherit substance; and I will\l"
    .string "fill their treasures$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_22::
    .string "The LORD possessed me in the\n"
    .string "beginning of his way, before his\l"
    .string "works of old.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_23::
    .string "I was set up from everlasting, from\n"
    .string "the beginning, or ever the earth was.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_24::
    .string "When there were no depths, I was\n"
    .string "brought forth; when there were no\l"
    .string "fountains abounding with water.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_25::
    .string "Before the mountains were settled,\n"
    .string "before the hills was I brought\l"
    .string "forth:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_26::
    .string "While as yet he had not made the\n"
    .string "earth, nor the fields, nor the\l"
    .string "highest part of the dust of the\l"
    .string "world$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_27::
    .string "When he prepared the heavens, I was\n"
    .string "there: when he set a compass upon\l"
    .string "the face of the depth:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_28::
    .string "When he established the clouds\n"
    .string "above: when he strengthened the\l"
    .string "fountains of the deep:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_29::
    .string "When he gave to the sea his decree,\n"
    .string "that the waters should not pass his\l"
    .string "commandment: when he appointed the\l"
    .string "foundations of the earth:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_30::
    .string "Then I was by him, as one brought up\n"
    .string "with him: and I was daily his\l"
    .string "delight, rejoicing always before\l"
    .string "him;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_31::
    .string "Rejoicing in the habitable part of\n"
    .string "his earth; and my delights were with\l"
    .string "the sons of men$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_32::
    .string "Now therefore hearken unto me, O ye\n"
    .string "children: for blessed are they that\l"
    .string "keep my ways.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_33::
    .string "Hear instruction, and be wise, and\n"
    .string "refuse it not.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_34::
    .string "Blessed is the man that heareth me,\n"
    .string "watching daily at my gates, waiting\l"
    .string "at the posts of my doors.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_35::
    .string "For whoso findeth me findeth life,\n"
    .string "and shall obtain favour of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_8_36::
    .string "But he that sinneth against me\n"
    .string "wrongeth his own soul: all they\l"
    .string "that hate me love death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_1::
    .string "Wisdom hath builded her house, she\n"
    .string "hath hewn out her seven pillars:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_2::
    .string "She hath killed her beasts; she\n"
    .string "hath mingled her wine; she hath also\l"
    .string "furnished her table$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_3::
    .string "She hath sent forth her maidens: she\n"
    .string "crieth upon the highest places of\l"
    .string "the city,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_4::
    .string "Whoso is simple, let him turn in\n"
    .string "hither: as for him that wanteth\l"
    .string "understanding, she saith to him,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_5::
    .string "Come, eat of my bread, and drink of\n"
    .string "the wine which I have mingled$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_6::
    .string "Forsake the foolish, and live; and\n"
    .string "go in the way of understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_7::
    .string "He that reproveth a scorner getteth\n"
    .string "to himself shame: and he that\l"
    .string "rebuketh a wicked man getteth\l"
    .string "himself a blot.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_8::
    .string "Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate\n"
    .string "thee: rebuke a wise man, and he will\l"
    .string "love thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_9::
    .string "Give instruction to a wise man, and\n"
    .string "he will be yet wiser: teach a just\l"
    .string "man, and he will increase in\l"
    .string "learning.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_10::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is the\n"
    .string "beginning of wisdom: and the\l"
    .string "knowledge of the holy is\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_11::
    .string "For by me thy days shall be\n"
    .string "multiplied, and the years of thy\l"
    .string "life shall be increased.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_12::
    .string "If thou be wise, thou shalt be wise\n"
    .string "for thyself: but if thou scornest,\l"
    .string "thou alone shalt bear it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_13::
    .string "A foolish woman is clamorous: she\n"
    .string "is simple, and knoweth nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_14::
    .string "For she sitteth at the door of her\n"
    .string "house, on a seat in the high places\l"
    .string "of the city,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_15::
    .string "To call passengers who go right on\n"
    .string "their ways:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_16::
    .string "Whoso is simple, let him turn in\n"
    .string "hither: and as for him that wanteth\l"
    .string "understanding, she saith to him,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_17::
    .string "Stolen waters are sweet, and bread\n"
    .string "eaten in secret is pleasant$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_9_18::
    .string "But he knoweth not that the dead are\n"
    .string "there; and that her guests are in the\l"
    .string "depths of hell.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_1::
    .string "The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son\n"
    .string "maketh a glad father: but a foolish\l"
    .string "son is the heaviness of his mother.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_2::
    .string "Treasures of wickedness profit\n"
    .string "nothing: but righteousness\l"
    .string "delivereth from death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_3::
    .string "The LORD will not suffer the soul\n"
    .string "of the righteous to famish: but he\l"
    .string "casteth away the substance of the\l"
    .string "wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_4::
    .string "He becometh poor that dealeth with\n"
    .string "a slack hand: but the hand of the\l"
    .string "diligent maketh rich.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_5::
    .string "He that gathereth in summer is a\n"
    .string "wise son: but he that sleepeth in\l"
    .string "harvest is a son that causeth shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_6::
    .string "Blessings are upon the head of the\n"
    .string "just: but violence covereth the\l"
    .string "mouth of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_7::
    .string "The memory of the just is blessed:\n"
    .string "but the name of the wicked shall rot.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_8::
    .string "The wise in heart will receive\n"
    .string "commandments: but a prating fool\l"
    .string "shall fall.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_9::
    .string "He that walketh uprightly\n"
    .string "walketh surely: but he that\l"
    .string "perverteth his ways shall be known.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_10::
    .string "He that winketh with the eye causeth\n"
    .string "sorrow: but a prating fool shall\l"
    .string "fall.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_11::
    .string "The mouth of a righteous man is a\n"
    .string "well of life: but violence\l"
    .string "covereth the mouth of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_12::
    .string "Hatred stirreth up strifes: but\n"
    .string "love covereth all sins.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_13::
    .string "In the lips of him that hath\n"
    .string "understanding wisdom is found: but a\l"
    .string "rod is for the back of him that is\l"
    .string "void of understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_14::
    .string "Wise men lay up knowledge: but the\n"
    .string "mouth of the foolish is near\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_15::
    .string "The rich man’s wealth is his strong\n"
    .string "city: the destruction of the poor is\l"
    .string "their poverty.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_16::
    .string "The labour of the righteous tendeth\n"
    .string "to life: the fruit of the wicked to\l"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_17::
    .string "He is in the way of life that\n"
    .string "keepeth instruction: but he that\l"
    .string "refuseth reproof erreth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_18::
    .string "He that hideth hatred with lying\n"
    .string "lips, and he that uttereth a\l"
    .string "slander, is a fool.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_19::
    .string "In the multitude of words there\n"
    .string "wanteth not sin: but he that\l"
    .string "refraineth his lips is wise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_20::
    .string "The tongue of the just is as choice\n"
    .string "silver: the heart of the wicked is\l"
    .string "little worth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_21::
    .string "The lips of the righteous feed\n"
    .string "many: but fools die for want of\l"
    .string "wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_22::
    .string "The blessing of the LORD, it maketh\n"
    .string "rich, and he addeth no sorrow with it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_23::
    .string "It is as sport to a fool to do\n"
    .string "mischief: but a man of understanding\l"
    .string "hath wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_24::
    .string "The fear of the wicked, it shall\n"
    .string "come upon him: but the desire of the\l"
    .string "righteous shall be granted.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_25::
    .string "As the whirlwind passeth, so is the\n"
    .string "wicked no more: but the righteous is\l"
    .string "an everlasting foundation.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_26::
    .string "As vinegar to the teeth, and as\n"
    .string "smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard\l"
    .string "to them that send him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_27::
    .string "The fear of the LORD prolongeth\n"
    .string "days: but the years of the wicked\l"
    .string "shall be shortened.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_28::
    .string "The hope of the righteous shall be\n"
    .string "gladness: but the expectation of\l"
    .string "the wicked shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_29::
    .string "The way of the LORD is strength to\n"
    .string "the upright: but destruction shall\l"
    .string "be to the workers of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_30::
    .string "The righteous shall never be\n"
    .string "removed: but the wicked shall not\l"
    .string "inhabit the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_31::
    .string "The mouth of the just bringeth forth\n"
    .string "wisdom: but the froward tongue\l"
    .string "shall be cut out.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_10_32::
    .string "The lips of the righteous know\n"
    .string "what is acceptable: but the mouth of\l"
    .string "the wicked speaketh frowardness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_1::
    .string "A false balance is abomination to\n"
    .string "the LORD: but a just weight is his\l"
    .string "delight.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_2::
    .string "When pride cometh, then cometh\n"
    .string "shame: but with the lowly is wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_3::
    .string "The integrity of the upright\n"
    .string "shall guide them: but the\l"
    .string "perverseness of transgressors\l"
    .string "shall destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_4::
    .string "Riches profit not in the day of\n"
    .string "wrath: but righteousness delivereth\l"
    .string "from death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_5::
    .string "The righteousness of the perfect\n"
    .string "shall direct his way: but the wicked\l"
    .string "shall fall by his own wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_6::
    .string "The righteousness of the upright\n"
    .string "shall deliver them: but\l"
    .string "transgressors shall be taken in\l"
    .string "their own naughtiness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_7::
    .string "When a wicked man dieth, his\n"
    .string "expectation shall perish: and the\l"
    .string "hope of unjust men perisheth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_8::
    .string "The righteous is delivered out of\n"
    .string "trouble, and the wicked cometh in\l"
    .string "his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_9::
    .string "An hypocrite with his mouth\n"
    .string "destroyeth his neighbour: but\l"
    .string "through knowledge shall the just\l"
    .string "be delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_10::
    .string "When it goeth well with the\n"
    .string "righteous, the city rejoiceth: and\l"
    .string "when the wicked perish, there is\l"
    .string "shouting.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_11::
    .string "By the blessing of the upright the\n"
    .string "city is exalted: but it is\l"
    .string "overthrown by the mouth of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_12::
    .string "He that is void of wisdom despiseth\n"
    .string "his neighbour: but a man of\l"
    .string "understanding holdeth his peace.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_13::
    .string "A talebearer revealeth secrets:\n"
    .string "but he that is of a faithful spirit\l"
    .string "concealeth the matter.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_14::
    .string "Where no counsel is, the people\n"
    .string "fall: but in the multitude of\l"
    .string "counsellors there is safety.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_15::
    .string "He that is surety for a stranger\n"
    .string "shall smart for it: and he that\l"
    .string "hateth suretiship is sure.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_16::
    .string "A gracious woman retaineth honour:\n"
    .string "and strong men retain riches.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_17::
    .string "The merciful man doeth good to his\n"
    .string "own soul: but he that is cruel\l"
    .string "troubleth his own flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_18::
    .string "The wicked worketh a deceitful\n"
    .string "work: but to him that soweth\l"
    .string "righteousness shall be a sure\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_19::
    .string "As righteousness tendeth to life:\n"
    .string "so he that pursueth evil pursueth\l"
    .string "it to his own death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_20::
    .string "They that are of a froward heart are\n"
    .string "abomination to the LORD: but such as\l"
    .string "are upright in their way are his\l"
    .string "delight.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_21::
    .string "Though hand join in hand, the wicked\n"
    .string "shall not be unpunished: but the\l"
    .string "seed of the righteous shall be\l"
    .string "delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_22::
    .string "As a jewel of gold in a swine’s\n"
    .string "snout, so is a fair woman which is\l"
    .string "without discretion.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_23::
    .string "The desire of the righteous is only\n"
    .string "good: but the expectation of the\l"
    .string "wicked is wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_24::
    .string "There is that scattereth, and yet\n"
    .string "increaseth; and there is that\l"
    .string "withholdeth more than is meet, but\l"
    .string "it tendeth to poverty.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_25::
    .string "The liberal soul shall be made\n"
    .string "fat: and he that watereth shall be\l"
    .string "watered also himself.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_26::
    .string "He that withholdeth corn, the\n"
    .string "people shall curse him: but\l"
    .string "blessing shall be upon the head of\l"
    .string "him that selleth it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_27::
    .string "He that diligently seeketh good\n"
    .string "procureth favour: but he that seeketh\l"
    .string "mischief, it shall come unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_28::
    .string "He that trusteth in his riches\n"
    .string "shall fall; but the righteous\l"
    .string "shall flourish as a branch.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_29::
    .string "He that troubleth his own house\n"
    .string "shall inherit the wind: and the\l"
    .string "fool shall be servant to the wise\l"
    .string "of heart.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_30::
    .string "The fruit of the righteous is a tree\n"
    .string "of life; and he that winneth souls\l"
    .string "is wise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_11_31::
    .string "Behold, the righteous shall be\n"
    .string "recompensed in the earth: much more\l"
    .string "the wicked and the sinner.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_1::
    .string "Whoso loveth instruction loveth\n"
    .string "knowledge: but he that hateth\l"
    .string "reproof is brutish.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_2::
    .string "A good man obtaineth favour of the\n"
    .string "LORD: but a man of wicked devices\l"
    .string "will he condemn.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_3::
    .string "A man shall not be established by\n"
    .string "wickedness: but the root of the\l"
    .string "righteous shall not be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_4::
    .string "A virtuous woman is a crown to her\n"
    .string "husband: but she that maketh ashamed\l"
    .string "is as rottenness in his bones.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_5::
    .string "The thoughts of the righteous are\n"
    .string "right: but the counsels of the\l"
    .string "wicked are deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_6::
    .string "The words of the wicked are to lie\n"
    .string "in wait for blood: but the mouth of\l"
    .string "the upright shall deliver them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_7::
    .string "The wicked are overthrown, and are\n"
    .string "not: but the house of the righteous\l"
    .string "shall stand.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_8::
    .string "A man shall be commended according\n"
    .string "to his wisdom: but he that is of a\l"
    .string "perverse heart shall be despised.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_9::
    .string "He that is despised, and hath a\n"
    .string "servant, is better than he that\l"
    .string "honoureth himself, and lacketh\l"
    .string "bread.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_10::
    .string "A righteous man regardeth the life\n"
    .string "of his beast: but the tender mercies\l"
    .string "of the wicked are cruel.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_11::
    .string "He that tilleth his land shall\n"
    .string "be satisfied with bread: but he that\l"
    .string "followeth vain persons is void of\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_12::
    .string "The wicked desireth the net of evil\n"
    .string "men: but the root of the righteous\l"
    .string "yieldeth fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_13::
    .string "The wicked is snared by the\n"
    .string "transgression of his lips: but the\l"
    .string "just shall come out of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_14::
    .string "A man shall be satisfied with good\n"
    .string "by the fruit of his mouth: and the\l"
    .string "recompence of a man’s hands shall\l"
    .string "be rendered unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_15::
    .string "The way of a fool is right in his\n"
    .string "own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto\l"
    .string "counsel is wise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_16::
    .string "A fool’s wrath is presently known:\n"
    .string "but a prudent man covereth shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_17::
    .string "He that speaketh truth sheweth\n"
    .string "forth righteousness: but a false\l"
    .string "witness deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_18::
    .string "There is that speaketh like the\n"
    .string "piercings of a sword: but the tongue\l"
    .string "of the wise is health.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_19::
    .string "The lip of truth shall be\n"
    .string "established for ever: but a lying\l"
    .string "tongue is but for a moment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_20::
    .string "Deceit is in the heart of them that\n"
    .string "imagine evil: but to the\l"
    .string "counsellors of peace is joy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_21::
    .string "There shall no evil happen to\n"
    .string "the just: but the wicked shall be\l"
    .string "filled with mischief.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_22::
    .string "Lying lips are abomination to the\n"
    .string "LORD: but they that deal truly are\l"
    .string "his delight.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_23::
    .string "A prudent man concealeth\n"
    .string "knowledge: but the heart of fools\l"
    .string "proclaimeth foolishness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_24::
    .string "The hand of the diligent shall\n"
    .string "bear rule: but the slothful shall\l"
    .string "be under tribute.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_25::
    .string "Heaviness in the heart of man maketh\n"
    .string "it stoop: but a good word maketh it\l"
    .string "glad.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_26::
    .string "The righteous is more excellent\n"
    .string "than his neighbour: but the way of\l"
    .string "the wicked seduceth them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_27::
    .string "The slothful man roasteth not that\n"
    .string "which he took in hunting: but the\l"
    .string "substance of a diligent man is\l"
    .string "precious.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_12_28::
    .string "In the way of righteousness is\n"
    .string "life: and in the pathway thereof\l"
    .string "there is no death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_1::
    .string "A wise son heareth his father’s\n"
    .string "instruction: but a scorner heareth\l"
    .string "not rebuke.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_2::
    .string "A man shall eat good by the fruit\n"
    .string "of his mouth: but the soul of the\l"
    .string "transgressors shall eat violence.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_3::
    .string "He that keepeth his mouth keepeth\n"
    .string "his life: but he that openeth wide\l"
    .string "his lips shall have destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_4::
    .string "The soul of the sluggard desireth,\n"
    .string "and hath nothing: but the soul of the\l"
    .string "diligent shall be made fat.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_5::
    .string "A righteous man hateth lying: but a\n"
    .string "wicked man is loathsome, and cometh\l"
    .string "to shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_6::
    .string "Righteousness keepeth him that is\n"
    .string "upright in the way: but wickedness\l"
    .string "overthroweth the sinner.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_7::
    .string "There is that maketh himself rich,\n"
    .string "yet hath nothing: there is that\l"
    .string "maketh himself poor, yet hath great\l"
    .string "riches.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_8::
    .string "The ransom of a man’s life are his\n"
    .string "riches: but the poor heareth not\l"
    .string "rebuke.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_9::
    .string "The light of the righteous\n"
    .string "rejoiceth: but the lamp of the\l"
    .string "wicked shall be put out.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_10::
    .string "Only by pride cometh contention:\n"
    .string "but with the well advised is wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_11::
    .string "Wealth gotten by vanity shall be\n"
    .string "diminished: but he that gathereth by\l"
    .string "labour shall increase.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_12::
    .string "Hope deferred maketh the heart\n"
    .string "sick: but when the desire cometh, it\l"
    .string "is a tree of life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_13::
    .string "Whoso despiseth the word shall be\n"
    .string "destroyed: but he that feareth the\l"
    .string "commandment shall be rewarded.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_14::
    .string "The law of the wise is a fountain of\n"
    .string "life, to depart from the snares of\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_15::
    .string "Good understanding giveth favour:\n"
    .string "but the way of transgressors is hard.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_16::
    .string "Every prudent man dealeth with\n"
    .string "knowledge: but a fool layeth open\l"
    .string "his folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_17::
    .string "A wicked messenger falleth into\n"
    .string "mischief: but a faithful ambassador\l"
    .string "is health.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_18::
    .string "Poverty and shame shall be to him\n"
    .string "that refuseth instruction: but he\l"
    .string "that regardeth reproof shall be\l"
    .string "honoured.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_19::
    .string "The desire accomplished is sweet\n"
    .string "to the soul: but it is abomination to\l"
    .string "fools to depart from evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_20::
    .string "He that walketh with wise men\n"
    .string "shall be wise: but a companion of\l"
    .string "fools shall be destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_21::
    .string "Evil pursueth sinners: but to the\n"
    .string "righteous good shall be repayed.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_22::
    .string "A good man leaveth an inheritance\n"
    .string "to his children’s children: and the\l"
    .string "wealth of the sinner is laid up for\l"
    .string "the just.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_23::
    .string "Much food is in the tillage of the\n"
    .string "poor: but there is that is destroyed\l"
    .string "for want of judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_24::
    .string "He that spareth his rod hateth his\n"
    .string "son: but he that loveth him\l"
    .string "chasteneth him betimes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_13_25::
    .string "The righteous eateth to the\n"
    .string "satisfying of his soul: but the\l"
    .string "belly of the wicked shall want.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_1::
    .string "Every wise woman buildeth her\n"
    .string "house: but the foolish plucketh it\l"
    .string "down with her hands.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_2::
    .string "He that walketh in his uprightness\n"
    .string "feareth the LORD: but he that is\l"
    .string "perverse in his ways despiseth him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_3::
    .string "In the mouth of the foolish is a rod\n"
    .string "of pride: but the lips of the wise\l"
    .string "shall preserve them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_4::
    .string "Where no oxen are, the crib is\n"
    .string "clean: but much increase is by the\l"
    .string "strength of the ox.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_5::
    .string "A faithful witness will not lie:\n"
    .string "but a false witness will utter\l"
    .string "lies.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_6::
    .string "A scorner seeketh wisdom, and\n"
    .string "findeth it not: but knowledge is\l"
    .string "easy unto him that understandeth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_7::
    .string "Go from the presence of a foolish\n"
    .string "man, when thou perceivest not in him\l"
    .string "the lips of knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_8::
    .string "The wisdom of the prudent is to\n"
    .string "understand his way: but the folly of\l"
    .string "fools is deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_9::
    .string "Fools make a mock at sin: but among\n"
    .string "the righteous there is favour.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_10::
    .string "The heart knoweth his own\n"
    .string "bitterness; and a stranger doth not\l"
    .string "intermeddle with his joy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_11::
    .string "The house of the wicked shall be\n"
    .string "overthrown: but the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "the upright shall flourish.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_12::
    .string "There is a way which seemeth right\n"
    .string "unto a man, but the end thereof are\l"
    .string "the ways of death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_13::
    .string "Even in laughter the heart is\n"
    .string "sorrowful; and the end of that mirth\l"
    .string "is heaviness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_14::
    .string "The backslider in heart shall be\n"
    .string "filled with his own ways: and a good\l"
    .string "man shall be satisfied from\l"
    .string "himself.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_15::
    .string "The simple believeth every word:\n"
    .string "but the prudent man looketh well\l"
    .string "to his going.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_16::
    .string "A wise man feareth, and departeth\n"
    .string "from evil: but the fool rageth, and\l"
    .string "is confident.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_17::
    .string "He that is soon angry dealeth\n"
    .string "foolishly: and a man of wicked\l"
    .string "devices is hated.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_18::
    .string "The simple inherit folly: but the\n"
    .string "prudent are crowned with knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_19::
    .string "The evil bow before the good; and\n"
    .string "the wicked at the gates of the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_20::
    .string "The poor is hated even of his own\n"
    .string "neighbour: but the rich hath many\l"
    .string "friends.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_21::
    .string "He that despiseth his neighbour\n"
    .string "sinneth: but he that hath mercy on\l"
    .string "the poor, happy is he.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_22::
    .string "Do they not err that devise evil?\n"
    .string "but mercy and truth shall be to them\l"
    .string "that devise good.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_23::
    .string "In all labour there is profit:\n"
    .string "but the talk of the lips tendeth\l"
    .string "only to penury.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_24::
    .string "The crown of the wise is their\n"
    .string "riches: but the foolishness of\l"
    .string "fools is folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_25::
    .string "A true witness delivereth souls:\n"
    .string "but a deceitful witness speaketh\l"
    .string "lies.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_26::
    .string "In the fear of the LORD is strong\n"
    .string "confidence: and his children shall\l"
    .string "have a place of refuge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_27::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is a fountain\n"
    .string "of life, to depart from the snares\l"
    .string "of death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_28::
    .string "In the multitude of people is the\n"
    .string "king’s honour: but in the want of\l"
    .string "people is the destruction of the\l"
    .string "prince.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_29::
    .string "He that is slow to wrath is of great\n"
    .string "understanding: but he that is hasty\l"
    .string "of spirit exalteth folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_30::
    .string "A sound heart is the life of the\n"
    .string "flesh: but envy the rottenness of\l"
    .string "the bones.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_31::
    .string "He that oppresseth the poor\n"
    .string "reproacheth his Maker: but he that\l"
    .string "honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_32::
    .string "The wicked is driven away in his\n"
    .string "wickedness: but the righteous hath\l"
    .string "hope in his death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_33::
    .string "Wisdom resteth in the heart of him\n"
    .string "that hath understanding: but that\l"
    .string "which is in the midst of fools is\l"
    .string "made known.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_34::
    .string "Righteousness exalteth a nation:\n"
    .string "but sin is a reproach to any\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_14_35::
    .string "The king’s favour is toward a wise\n"
    .string "servant: but his wrath is against him\l"
    .string "that causeth shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_1::
    .string "A soft answer turneth away wrath:\n"
    .string "but grievous words stir up anger.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_2::
    .string "The tongue of the wise useth\n"
    .string "knowledge aright: but the mouth of\l"
    .string "fools poureth out foolishness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_3::
    .string "The eyes of the LORD are in every\n"
    .string "place, beholding the evil and the\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_4::
    .string "A wholesome tongue is a tree of\n"
    .string "life: but perverseness therein is a\l"
    .string "breach in the spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_5::
    .string "A fool despiseth his father’s\n"
    .string "instruction: but he that regardeth\l"
    .string "reproof is prudent.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_6::
    .string "In the house of the righteous is\n"
    .string "much treasure: but in the revenues of\l"
    .string "the wicked is trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_7::
    .string "The lips of the wise disperse\n"
    .string "knowledge: but the heart of the\l"
    .string "foolish doeth not so.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_8::
    .string "The sacrifice of the wicked is an\n"
    .string "abomination to the LORD: but the\l"
    .string "prayer of the upright is his\l"
    .string "delight.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_9::
    .string "The way of the wicked is an\n"
    .string "abomination unto the LORD: but he\l"
    .string "loveth him that followeth after\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_10::
    .string "Correction is grievous unto him\n"
    .string "that forsaketh the way: and he that\l"
    .string "hateth reproof shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_11::
    .string "Hell and destruction are before\n"
    .string "the LORD: how much more then the\l"
    .string "hearts of the children of men?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_12::
    .string "A scorner loveth not one that\n"
    .string "reproveth him: neither will he go\l"
    .string "unto the wise$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_13::
    .string "A merry heart maketh a cheerful\n"
    .string "countenance: but by sorrow of the\l"
    .string "heart the spirit is broken.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_14::
    .string "The heart of him that hath\n"
    .string "understanding seeketh knowledge:\l"
    .string "but the mouth of fools feedeth on\l"
    .string "foolishness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_15::
    .string "All the days of the afflicted are\n"
    .string "evil: but he that is of a merry heart\l"
    .string "hath a continual feast.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_16::
    .string "Better is little with the fear of\n"
    .string "the LORD than great treasure and\l"
    .string "trouble therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_17::
    .string "Better is a dinner of herbs where\n"
    .string "love is, than a stalled ox and\l"
    .string "hatred therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_18::
    .string "A wrathful man stirreth up strife:\n"
    .string "but he that is slow to anger\l"
    .string "appeaseth strife.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_19::
    .string "The way of the slothful man is as\n"
    .string "an hedge of thorns: but the way of the\l"
    .string "righteous is made plain.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_20::
    .string "A wise son maketh a glad father: but\n"
    .string "a foolish man despiseth his mother.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_21::
    .string "Folly is joy to him that is\n"
    .string "destitute of wisdom: but a man of\l"
    .string "understanding walketh uprightly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_22::
    .string "Without counsel purposes are\n"
    .string "disappointed: but in the multitude\l"
    .string "of counsellors they are\l"
    .string "established.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_23::
    .string "A man hath joy by the answer of his\n"
    .string "mouth: and a word spoken in due\l"
    .string "season, how good is it!"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_24::
    .string "The way of life is above to the\n"
    .string "wise, that he may depart from hell\l"
    .string "beneath$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_25::
    .string "The LORD will destroy the house of\n"
    .string "the proud: but he will establish\l"
    .string "the border of the widow.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_26::
    .string "The thoughts of the wicked are an\n"
    .string "abomination to the LORD: but the\l"
    .string "words of the pure are pleasant\l"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_27::
    .string "He that is greedy of gain troubleth\n"
    .string "his own house; but he that hateth\l"
    .string "gifts shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_28::
    .string "The heart of the righteous studieth\n"
    .string "to answer: but the mouth of the\l"
    .string "wicked poureth out evil things.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_29::
    .string "The LORD is far from the wicked: but\n"
    .string "he heareth the prayer of the\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_30::
    .string "The light of the eyes rejoiceth the\n"
    .string "heart: and a good report maketh the\l"
    .string "bones fat.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_31::
    .string "The ear that heareth the reproof of\n"
    .string "life abideth among the wise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_32::
    .string "He that refuseth instruction\n"
    .string "despiseth his own soul: but he that\l"
    .string "heareth reproof getteth\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_15_33::
    .string "The fear of the LORD is the\n"
    .string "instruction of wisdom; and before\l"
    .string "honour is humility.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_1::
    .string "The preparations of the heart in\n"
    .string "man, and the answer of the tongue, is\l"
    .string "from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_2::
    .string "All the ways of a man are clean in\n"
    .string "his own eyes; but the LORD weigheth\l"
    .string "the spirits.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_3::
    .string "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and\n"
    .string "thy thoughts shall be established.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_4::
    .string "The LORD hath made all things for\n"
    .string "himself: yea, even the wicked for\l"
    .string "the day of evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_5::
    .string "Every one that is proud in heart is\n"
    .string "an abomination to the LORD: though\l"
    .string "hand join in hand, he shall not be\l"
    .string "unpunished.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_6::
    .string "By mercy and truth iniquity is\n"
    .string "purged: and by the fear of the LORD\l"
    .string "men depart from evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_7::
    .string "When a man’s ways please the LORD,\n"
    .string "he maketh even his enemies to be at\l"
    .string "peace with him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_8::
    .string "Better is a little with\n"
    .string "righteousness than great revenues\l"
    .string "without right.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_9::
    .string "A man’s heart deviseth his way: but\n"
    .string "the LORD directeth his steps.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_10::
    .string "A divine sentence is in the lips of\n"
    .string "the king: his mouth transgresseth not\l"
    .string "in judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_11::
    .string "A just weight and balance are the\n"
    .string "LORD’s: all the weights of the bag\l"
    .string "are his work.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_12::
    .string "It is an abomination to kings to\n"
    .string "commit wickedness: for the throne is\l"
    .string "established by righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_13::
    .string "Righteous lips are the delight of\n"
    .string "kings; and they love him that\l"
    .string "speaketh right.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_14::
    .string "The wrath of a king is as messengers\n"
    .string "of death: but a wise man will\l"
    .string "pacify it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_15::
    .string "In the light of the king’s\n"
    .string "countenance is life; and his favour\l"
    .string "is as a cloud of the latter rain.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_16::
    .string "How much better is it to get wisdom\n"
    .string "than gold! and to get understanding\l"
    .string "rather to be chosen than silver!"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_17::
    .string "The highway of the upright is to\n"
    .string "depart from evil: he that keepeth\l"
    .string "his way preserveth his soul$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_18::
    .string "Pride goeth before destruction, and\n"
    .string "an haughty spirit before a fall.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_19::
    .string "Better it is to be of an humble\n"
    .string "spirit with the lowly, than to\l"
    .string "divide the spoil with the proud.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_20::
    .string "He that handleth a matter wisely\n"
    .string "shall find good: and whoso trusteth\l"
    .string "in the LORD, happy is he.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_21::
    .string "The wise in heart shall be called\n"
    .string "prudent: and the sweetness of the\l"
    .string "lips increaseth learning.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_22::
    .string "Understanding is a wellspring of\n"
    .string "life unto him that hath it: but the\l"
    .string "instruction of fools is folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_23::
    .string "The heart of the wise teacheth his\n"
    .string "mouth, and addeth learning to his\l"
    .string "lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_24::
    .string "Pleasant words are as an honeycomb,\n"
    .string "sweet to the soul, and health to the\l"
    .string "bones.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_25::
    .string "There is a way that seemeth right\n"
    .string "unto a man, but the end thereof are\l"
    .string "the ways of death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_26::
    .string "He that laboureth laboureth for\n"
    .string "himself; for his mouth craveth it of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_27::
    .string "An ungodly man diggeth up evil:\n"
    .string "and in his lips there is as a\l"
    .string "burning fire.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_28::
    .string "A froward man soweth strife: and a\n"
    .string "whisperer separateth chief friends.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_29::
    .string "A violent man enticeth his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and leadeth him into the\l"
    .string "way that is not good.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_30::
    .string "He shutteth his eyes to devise\n"
    .string "froward things: moving his lips he\l"
    .string "bringeth evil to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_31::
    .string "The hoary head is a crown of glory,\n"
    .string "if it be found in the way of\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_32::
    .string "He that is slow to anger is better\n"
    .string "than the mighty; and he that ruleth\l"
    .string "his spirit than he that taketh a\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_16_33::
    .string "The lot is cast into the lap; but\n"
    .string "the whole disposing thereof is of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_1::
    .string "Better is a dry morsel, and\n"
    .string "quietness therewith, than an house\l"
    .string "full of sacrifices with strife.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_2::
    .string "A wise servant shall have rule\n"
    .string "over a son that causeth shame, and\l"
    .string "shall have part of the inheritance\l"
    .string "among the brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_3::
    .string "The fining pot is for silver, and\n"
    .string "the furnace for gold: but the LORD\l"
    .string "trieth the hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_4::
    .string "A wicked doer giveth heed to false\n"
    .string "lips; and a liar giveth ear to a\l"
    .string "naughty tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_5::
    .string "Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth\n"
    .string "his Maker: and he that is glad at\l"
    .string "calamities shall not be\l"
    .string "unpunished.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_6::
    .string "Children’s children are the crown\n"
    .string "of old men; and the glory of\l"
    .string "children are their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_7::
    .string "Excellent speech becometh not a\n"
    .string "fool: much less do lying lips a\l"
    .string "prince.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_8::
    .string "A gift is as a precious stone in the\n"
    .string "eyes of him that hath it:\l"
    .string "whithersoever it turneth, it\l"
    .string "prospereth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_9::
    .string "He that covereth a transgression\n"
    .string "seeketh love; but he that repeateth\l"
    .string "a matter separateth very friends.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_10::
    .string "A reproof entereth more into a wise\n"
    .string "man than an hundred stripes into a\l"
    .string "fool.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_11::
    .string "An evil man seeketh only\n"
    .string "rebellion: therefore a cruel\l"
    .string "messenger shall be sent against him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_12::
    .string "Let a bear robbed of her whelps\n"
    .string "meet a man, rather than a fool in his\l"
    .string "folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_13::
    .string "Whoso rewardeth evil for good,\n"
    .string "evil shall not depart from his\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_14::
    .string "The beginning of strife is as when\n"
    .string "one letteth out water: therefore\l"
    .string "leave off contention, before it be\l"
    .string "meddled with.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_15::
    .string "He that justifieth the wicked, and\n"
    .string "he that condemneth the just, even\l"
    .string "they both are abomination to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_16::
    .string "Wherefore is there a price in the\n"
    .string "hand of a fool to get wisdom, seeing\l"
    .string "he hath no heart to it?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_17::
    .string "A friend loveth at all times, and\n"
    .string "a brother is born for adversity$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_18::
    .string "A man void of understanding\n"
    .string "striketh hands, and becometh surety\l"
    .string "in the presence of his friend.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_19::
    .string "He loveth transgression that\n"
    .string "loveth strife: and he that exalteth\l"
    .string "his gate seeketh destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_20::
    .string "He that hath a froward heart findeth\n"
    .string "no good: and he that hath a perverse\l"
    .string "tongue falleth into mischief.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_21::
    .string "He that begetteth a fool doeth it\n"
    .string "to his sorrow: and the father of a\l"
    .string "fool hath no joy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_22::
    .string "A merry heart doeth good like a\n"
    .string "medicine: but a broken spirit drieth\l"
    .string "the bones.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_23::
    .string "A wicked man taketh a gift out of\n"
    .string "the bosom to pervert the ways of\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_24::
    .string "Wisdom is before him that hath\n"
    .string "understanding; but the eyes of a\l"
    .string "fool are in the ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_25::
    .string "A foolish son is a grief to his\n"
    .string "father, and bitterness to her that\l"
    .string "bare him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_26::
    .string "Also to punish the just is not\n"
    .string "good, nor to strike princes for\l"
    .string "equity.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_27::
    .string "He that hath knowledge spareth his\n"
    .string "words: and a man of understanding is\l"
    .string "of an excellent spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_17_28::
    .string "Even a fool, when he holdeth his\n"
    .string "peace, is counted wise: and he that\l"
    .string "shutteth his lips is esteemed a man\l"
    .string "of understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_1::
    .string "Through desire a man, having\n"
    .string "separated himself, seeketh and\l"
    .string "intermeddleth with all wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_2::
    .string "A fool hath no delight in\n"
    .string "understanding, but that his heart may\l"
    .string "discover itself.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_3::
    .string "When the wicked cometh, then cometh\n"
    .string "also contempt, and with ignominy\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_4::
    .string "The words of a man’s mouth are as\n"
    .string "deep waters, and the wellspring of\l"
    .string "wisdom as a flowing brook.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_5::
    .string "It is not good to accept the person\n"
    .string "of the wicked, to overthrow the\l"
    .string "righteous in judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_6::
    .string "A fool’s lips enter into\n"
    .string "contention, and his mouth calleth\l"
    .string "for strokes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_7::
    .string "A fool’s mouth is his destruction,\n"
    .string "and his lips are the snare of his\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_8::
    .string "The words of a talebearer are as\n"
    .string "wounds, and they go down into the\l"
    .string "innermost parts of the belly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_9::
    .string "He also that is slothful in his\n"
    .string "work is brother to him that is a\l"
    .string "great waster.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_10::
    .string "The name of the LORD is a strong\n"
    .string "tower: the righteous runneth into it,\l"
    .string "and is safe.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_11::
    .string "The rich man’s wealth is his strong\n"
    .string "city, and as an high wall in his own\l"
    .string "conceit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_12::
    .string "Before destruction the heart of man\n"
    .string "is haughty, and before honour is\l"
    .string "humility.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_13::
    .string "He that answereth a matter before he\n"
    .string "heareth it, it is folly and shame\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_14::
    .string "The spirit of a man will sustain\n"
    .string "his infirmity; but a wounded spirit\l"
    .string "who can bear?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_15::
    .string "The heart of the prudent getteth\n"
    .string "knowledge; and the ear of the wise\l"
    .string "seeketh knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_16::
    .string "A man’s gift maketh room for him,\n"
    .string "and bringeth him before great men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_17::
    .string "He that is first in his own cause\n"
    .string "seemeth just; but his neighbour\l"
    .string "cometh and searcheth him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_18::
    .string "The lot causeth contentions to\n"
    .string "cease, and parteth between the\l"
    .string "mighty.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_19::
    .string "A brother offended is harder to be\n"
    .string "won than a strong city: and their\l"
    .string "contentions are like the bars of a\l"
    .string "castle.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_20::
    .string "A man’s belly shall be satisfied\n"
    .string "with the fruit of his mouth; and with\l"
    .string "the increase of his lips shall he\l"
    .string "be filled.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_21::
    .string "Death and life are in the power of\n"
    .string "the tongue: and they that love it\l"
    .string "shall eat the fruit thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_22::
    .string "Whoso findeth a wife findeth a good\n"
    .string "thing, and obtaineth favour of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_23::
    .string "The poor useth intreaties; but the\n"
    .string "rich answereth roughly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_18_24::
    .string "A man that hath friends must shew\n"
    .string "himself friendly: and there is a\l"
    .string "friend that sticketh closer than a\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_1::
    .string "Better is the poor that walketh in\n"
    .string "his integrity, than he that is\l"
    .string "perverse in his lips, and is a fool.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_2::
    .string "Also, that the soul be without\n"
    .string "knowledge, it is not good; and he\l"
    .string "that hasteth with his feet sinneth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_3::
    .string "The foolishness of man perverteth\n"
    .string "his way: and his heart fretteth\l"
    .string "against the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_4::
    .string "Wealth maketh many friends; but the\n"
    .string "poor is separated from his neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_5::
    .string "A false witness shall not be\n"
    .string "unpunished, and he that speaketh\l"
    .string "lies shall not escape.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_6::
    .string "Many will intreat the favour of\n"
    .string "the prince: and every man is a friend\l"
    .string "to him that giveth gifts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_7::
    .string "All the brethren of the poor do\n"
    .string "hate him: how much more do his\l"
    .string "friends go far from him? he pursueth\l"
    .string "them with words, yet they are wanting\l"
    .string "to him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_8::
    .string "He that getteth wisdom loveth his\n"
    .string "own soul: he that keepeth\l"
    .string "understanding shall find good.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_9::
    .string "A false witness shall not be\n"
    .string "unpunished, and he that speaketh\l"
    .string "lies shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_10::
    .string "Delight is not seemly for a fool;\n"
    .string "much less for a servant to have rule\l"
    .string "over princes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_11::
    .string "The discretion of a man deferreth\n"
    .string "his anger; and it is his glory to\l"
    .string "pass over a transgression.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_12::
    .string "The king’s wrath is as the roaring\n"
    .string "of a lion; but his favour is as dew\l"
    .string "upon the grass.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_13::
    .string "A foolish son is the calamity of\n"
    .string "his father: and the contentions of a\l"
    .string "wife are a continual dropping.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_14::
    .string "House and riches are the\n"
    .string "inheritance of fathers: and a\l"
    .string "prudent wife is from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_15::
    .string "Slothfulness casteth into a deep\n"
    .string "sleep; and an idle soul shall\l"
    .string "suffer hunger.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_16::
    .string "He that keepeth the commandment\n"
    .string "keepeth his own soul; but he that\l"
    .string "despiseth his ways shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_17::
    .string "He that hath pity upon the poor\n"
    .string "lendeth unto the LORD; and that which\l"
    .string "he hath given will he pay him again.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_18::
    .string "Chasten thy son while there is\n"
    .string "hope, and let not thy soul spare\l"
    .string "for his crying.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_19::
    .string "A man of great wrath shall suffer\n"
    .string "punishment: for if thou deliver him,\l"
    .string "yet thou must do it again.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_20::
    .string "Hear counsel, and receive\n"
    .string "instruction, that thou mayest be wise\l"
    .string "in thy latter end.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_21::
    .string "There are many devices in a man’s\n"
    .string "heart; nevertheless the counsel of\l"
    .string "the LORD, that shall stand.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_22::
    .string "The desire of a man is his kindness:\n"
    .string "and a poor man is better than a liar.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_23::
    .string "The fear of the LORD tendeth to\n"
    .string "life: and he that hath it shall\l"
    .string "abide satisfied; he shall not be\l"
    .string "visited with evil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_24::
    .string "A slothful man hideth his hand in\n"
    .string "his bosom, and will not so much as\l"
    .string "bring it to his mouth again.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_25::
    .string "Smite a scorner, and the simple\n"
    .string "will beware: and reprove one that\l"
    .string "hath understanding, and he will\l"
    .string "understand knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_26::
    .string "He that wasteth his father, and\n"
    .string "chaseth away his mother, is a son\l"
    .string "that causeth shame, and bringeth\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_27::
    .string "Cease, my son, to hear the\n"
    .string "instruction that causeth to err from\l"
    .string "the words of knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_28::
    .string "An ungodly witness scorneth\n"
    .string "judgment: and the mouth of the wicked\l"
    .string "devoureth iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_19_29::
    .string "Judgments are prepared for\n"
    .string "scorners, and stripes for the back\l"
    .string "of fools.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_1::
    .string "Wine is a mocker, strong drink is\n"
    .string "raging: and whosoever is deceived\l"
    .string "thereby is not wise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_2::
    .string "The fear of a king is as the roaring\n"
    .string "of a lion: whoso provoketh him to\l"
    .string "anger sinneth against his own soul.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_3::
    .string "It is an honour for a man to cease\n"
    .string "from strife: but every fool will be\l"
    .string "meddling.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_4::
    .string "The sluggard will not plow by\n"
    .string "reason of the cold; therefore shall\l"
    .string "he beg in harvest, and have nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_5::
    .string "Counsel in the heart of man is like\n"
    .string "deep water; but a man of\l"
    .string "understanding will draw it out.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_6::
    .string "Most men will proclaim every one\n"
    .string "his own goodness: but a faithful man\l"
    .string "who can find?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_7::
    .string "The just man walketh in his\n"
    .string "integrity: his children are blessed\l"
    .string "after him$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_8::
    .string "A king that sitteth in the throne of\n"
    .string "judgment scattereth away all evil\l"
    .string "with his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_9::
    .string "Who can say, I have made my heart\n"
    .string "clean, I am pure from my sin?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_10::
    .string "Divers weights, and divers\n"
    .string "measures, both of them are alike\l"
    .string "abomination to the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_11::
    .string "Even a child is known by his doings,\n"
    .string "whether his work be pure, and\l"
    .string "whether it be right.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_12::
    .string "The hearing ear, and the seeing eye,\n"
    .string "the LORD hath made even both of them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_13::
    .string "Love not sleep, lest thou come to\n"
    .string "poverty; open thine eyes, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be satisfied with bread.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_14::
    .string "It is naught, it is naught, saith\n"
    .string "the buyer: but when he is gone his\l"
    .string "way, then he boasteth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_15::
    .string "There is gold, and a multitude of\n"
    .string "rubies: but the lips of knowledge\l"
    .string "are a precious jewel.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_16::
    .string "Take his garment that is surety for\n"
    .string "a stranger: and take a pledge of him\l"
    .string "for a strange woman.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_17::
    .string "Bread of deceit is sweet to a man;\n"
    .string "but afterwards his mouth shall be\l"
    .string "filled with gravel.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_18::
    .string "Every purpose is established by\n"
    .string "counsel: and with good advice make\l"
    .string "war.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_19::
    .string "He that goeth about as a talebearer\n"
    .string "revealeth secrets: therefore meddle\l"
    .string "not with him that flattereth with\l"
    .string "his lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_20::
    .string "Whoso curseth his father or his\n"
    .string "mother, his lamp shall be put out\l"
    .string "in obscure darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_21::
    .string "An inheritance may be gotten\n"
    .string "hastily at the beginning; but the\l"
    .string "end thereof shall not be blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_22::
    .string "Say not thou, I will recompense\n"
    .string "evil; but wait on the LORD, and he\l"
    .string "shall save thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_23::
    .string "Divers weights are an abomination\n"
    .string "unto the LORD; and a false balance\l"
    .string "is not good.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_24::
    .string "Man’s goings are of the LORD; how\n"
    .string "can a man then understand his own\l"
    .string "way?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_25::
    .string "It is a snare to the man who\n"
    .string "devoureth that which is holy, and\l"
    .string "after vows to make enquiry$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_26::
    .string "A wise king scattereth the wicked,\n"
    .string "and bringeth the wheel over them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_27::
    .string "The spirit of man is the candle of\n"
    .string "the LORD, searching all the inward\l"
    .string "parts of the belly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_28::
    .string "Mercy and truth preserve the king:\n"
    .string "and his throne is upholden by mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_29::
    .string "The glory of young men is their\n"
    .string "strength: and the beauty of old men\l"
    .string "is the grey head.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_20_30::
    .string "The blueness of a wound cleanseth\n"
    .string "away evil: so do stripes the inward\l"
    .string "parts of the belly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_1::
    .string "The king’s heart is in the hand of\n"
    .string "the LORD, as the rivers of water: he\l"
    .string "turneth it whithersoever he will.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_2::
    .string "Every way of a man is right in his\n"
    .string "own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the\l"
    .string "hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_3::
    .string "To do justice and judgment is more\n"
    .string "acceptable to the LORD than\l"
    .string "sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_4::
    .string "An high look, and a proud heart,\n"
    .string "and the plowing of the wicked, is\l"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_5::
    .string "The thoughts of the diligent tend\n"
    .string "only to plenteousness; but of every\l"
    .string "one that is hasty only to want.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_6::
    .string "The getting of treasures by a lying\n"
    .string "tongue is a vanity tossed to and fro\l"
    .string "of them that seek death.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_7::
    .string "The robbery of the wicked shall\n"
    .string "destroy them; because they refuse to\l"
    .string "do judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_8::
    .string "The way of man is froward and\n"
    .string "strange: but as for the pure, his\l"
    .string "work is right.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_9::
    .string "It is better to dwell in a corner\n"
    .string "of the housetop, than with a\l"
    .string "brawling woman in a wide house.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_10::
    .string "The soul of the wicked desireth\n"
    .string "evil: his neighbour findeth no\l"
    .string "favour in his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_11::
    .string "When the scorner is punished, the\n"
    .string "simple is made wise: and when the\l"
    .string "wise is instructed, he receiveth\l"
    .string "knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_12::
    .string "The righteous man wisely\n"
    .string "considereth the house of the wicked:\l"
    .string "but God overthroweth the wicked for\l"
    .string "their wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_13::
    .string "Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry\n"
    .string "of the poor, he also shall cry\l"
    .string "himself, but shall not be heard.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_14::
    .string "A gift in secret pacifieth anger:\n"
    .string "and a reward in the bosom strong\l"
    .string "wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_15::
    .string "It is joy to the just to do judgment:\n"
    .string "but destruction shall be to the\l"
    .string "workers of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_16::
    .string "The man that wandereth out of the\n"
    .string "way of understanding shall remain\l"
    .string "in the congregation of the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_17::
    .string "He that loveth pleasure shall be\n"
    .string "a poor man: he that loveth wine and\l"
    .string "oil shall not be rich.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_18::
    .string "The wicked shall be a ransom for\n"
    .string "the righteous, and the transgressor\l"
    .string "for the upright.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_19::
    .string "It is better to dwell in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, than with a contentious\l"
    .string "and an angry woman.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_20::
    .string "There is treasure to be desired and\n"
    .string "oil in the dwelling of the wise;\l"
    .string "but a foolish man spendeth it up.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_21::
    .string "He that followeth after\n"
    .string "righteousness and mercy findeth\l"
    .string "life, righteousness, and honour.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_22::
    .string "A wise man scaleth the city of the\n"
    .string "mighty, and casteth down the strength\l"
    .string "of the confidence thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_23::
    .string "Whoso keepeth his mouth and his\n"
    .string "tongue keepeth his soul from\l"
    .string "troubles.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_24::
    .string "Proud and haughty scorner is his\n"
    .string "name, who dealeth in proud wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_25::
    .string "The desire of the slothful\n"
    .string "killeth him; for his hands refuse to\l"
    .string "labour.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_26::
    .string "He coveteth greedily all the day\n"
    .string "long: but the righteous giveth and\l"
    .string "spareth not.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_27::
    .string "The sacrifice of the wicked is\n"
    .string "abomination: how much more, when he\l"
    .string "bringeth it with a wicked mind?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_28::
    .string "A false witness shall perish: but\n"
    .string "the man that heareth speaketh\l"
    .string "constantly$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_29::
    .string "A wicked man hardeneth his face: but\n"
    .string "as for the upright, he directeth his\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_30::
    .string "There is no wisdom nor\n"
    .string "understanding nor counsel against\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_21_31::
    .string "The horse is prepared against the\n"
    .string "day of battle: but safety is of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_1::
    .string "A good name is rather to be chosen\n"
    .string "than great riches, and loving favour\l"
    .string "rather than silver and gold.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_2::
    .string "The rich and poor meet together:\n"
    .string "the LORD is the maker of them all.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_3::
    .string "A prudent man foreseeth the evil,\n"
    .string "and hideth himself: but the simple\l"
    .string "pass on, and are punished.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_4::
    .string "By humility and the fear of the\n"
    .string "LORD are riches, and honour, and\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_5::
    .string "Thorns and snares are in the way of\n"
    .string "the froward: he that doth keep his\l"
    .string "soul shall be far from them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_6::
    .string "Train up a child in the way he\n"
    .string "should go: and when he is old, he\l"
    .string "will not depart from it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_7::
    .string "The rich ruleth over the poor, and\n"
    .string "the borrower is servant to the\l"
    .string "lender.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_8::
    .string "He that soweth iniquity shall\n"
    .string "reap vanity: and the rod of his anger\l"
    .string "shall fail.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_9::
    .string "He that hath a bountiful eye shall\n"
    .string "be blessed; for he giveth of his\l"
    .string "bread to the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_10::
    .string "Cast out the scorner, and contention\n"
    .string "shall go out; yea, strife and\l"
    .string "reproach shall cease.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_11::
    .string "He that loveth pureness of heart,\n"
    .string "for the grace of his lips the king\l"
    .string "shall be his friend.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_12::
    .string "The eyes of the LORD preserve\n"
    .string "knowledge, and he overthroweth the\l"
    .string "words of the transgressor.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_13::
    .string "The slothful man saith, There is a\n"
    .string "lion without, I shall be slain in\l"
    .string "the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_14::
    .string "The mouth of strange women is a\n"
    .string "deep pit: he that is abhorred of the\l"
    .string "LORD shall fall therein.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_15::
    .string "Foolishness is bound in the heart\n"
    .string "of a child; but the rod of correction\l"
    .string "shall drive it far from him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_16::
    .string "He that oppresseth the poor to\n"
    .string "increase his riches, and he that\l"
    .string "giveth to the rich, shall surely\l"
    .string "come to want.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_17::
    .string "Bow down thine ear, and hear the\n"
    .string "words of the wise, and apply thine\l"
    .string "heart unto my knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_18::
    .string "For it is a pleasant thing if thou\n"
    .string "keep them within thee; they shall\l"
    .string "withal be fitted in thy lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_19::
    .string "That thy trust may be in the LORD, I\n"
    .string "have made known to thee this day,\l"
    .string "even to thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_20::
    .string "Have not I written to thee\n"
    .string "excellent things in counsels and\l"
    .string "knowledge,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_21::
    .string "That I might make thee know the\n"
    .string "certainty of the words of truth; that\l"
    .string "thou mightest answer the words of\l"
    .string "truth to them that send unto thee?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_22::
    .string "Rob not the poor, because he is\n"
    .string "poor: neither oppress the\l"
    .string "afflicted in the gate:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_23::
    .string "For the LORD will plead their\n"
    .string "cause, and spoil the soul of those\l"
    .string "that spoiled them$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_24::
    .string "Make no friendship with an angry\n"
    .string "man; and with a furious man thou\l"
    .string "shalt not go:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_25::
    .string "Lest thou learn his ways, and get a\n"
    .string "snare to thy soul$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_26::
    .string "Be not thou one of them that strike\n"
    .string "hands, or of them that are sureties\l"
    .string "for debts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_27::
    .string "If thou hast nothing to pay, why\n"
    .string "should he take away thy bed from\l"
    .string "under thee?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_28::
    .string "Remove not the ancient landmark,\n"
    .string "which thy fathers have set$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_22_29::
    .string "Seest thou a man diligent in his\n"
    .string "business? he shall stand before\l"
    .string "kings; he shall not stand before\l"
    .string "mean men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_1::
    .string "When thou sittest to eat with a\n"
    .string "ruler, consider diligently what is\l"
    .string "before thee:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_2::
    .string "And put a knife to thy throat, if\n"
    .string "thou be a man given to appetite$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_3::
    .string "Be not desirous of his dainties: for\n"
    .string "they are deceitful meat.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_4::
    .string "Labour not to be rich: cease from\n"
    .string "thine own wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_5::
    .string "Wilt thou set thine eyes upon that\n"
    .string "which is not? for riches certainly\l"
    .string "make themselves wings; they fly\l"
    .string "away as an eagle toward heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_6::
    .string "Eat thou not the bread of him that\n"
    .string "hath an evil eye, neither desire\l"
    .string "thou his dainty meats:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_7::
    .string "For as he thinketh in his heart, so\n"
    .string "is he: Eat and drink, saith he to\l"
    .string "thee; but his heart is not with thee$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_8::
    .string "The morsel which thou hast eaten\n"
    .string "shalt thou vomit up, and lose thy\l"
    .string "sweet words.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_9::
    .string "Speak not in the ears of a fool:\n"
    .string "for he will despise the wisdom of\l"
    .string "thy words.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_10::
    .string "Remove not the old landmark; and\n"
    .string "enter not into the fields of the\l"
    .string "fatherless:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_11::
    .string "For their redeemer is mighty; he\n"
    .string "shall plead their cause with thee$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_12::
    .string "Apply thine heart unto\n"
    .string "instruction, and thine ears to the\l"
    .string "words of knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_13::
    .string "Withhold not correction from the\n"
    .string "child: for if thou beatest him with\l"
    .string "the rod, he shall not die.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_14::
    .string "Thou shalt beat him with the rod,\n"
    .string "and shalt deliver his soul from\l"
    .string "hell.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_15::
    .string "My son, if thine heart be wise, my\n"
    .string "heart shall rejoice, even mine.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_16::
    .string "Yea, my reins shall rejoice, when\n"
    .string "thy lips speak right things.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_17::
    .string "Let not thine heart envy sinners:\n"
    .string "but be thou in the fear of the LORD\l"
    .string "all the day long.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_18::
    .string "For surely there is an end; and\n"
    .string "thine expectation shall not be cut\l"
    .string "off.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_19::
    .string "Hear thou, my son, and be wise, and\n"
    .string "guide thine heart in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_20::
    .string "Be not among winebibbers; among\n"
    .string "riotous eaters of flesh:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_21::
    .string "For the drunkard and the glutton\n"
    .string "shall come to poverty: and\l"
    .string "drowsiness shall clothe a man with\l"
    .string "rags$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_22::
    .string "Hearken unto thy father that begat\n"
    .string "thee, and despise not thy mother\l"
    .string "when she is old.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_23::
    .string "Buy the truth, and sell it not;\n"
    .string "also wisdom, and instruction, and\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_24::
    .string "The father of the righteous shall\n"
    .string "greatly rejoice: and he that\l"
    .string "begetteth a wise child shall have\l"
    .string "joy of him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_25::
    .string "Thy father and thy mother shall be\n"
    .string "glad, and she that bare thee shall\l"
    .string "rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_26::
    .string "My son, give me thine heart, and let\n"
    .string "thine eyes observe my ways.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_27::
    .string "For a whore is a deep ditch; and a\n"
    .string "strange woman is a narrow pit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_28::
    .string "She also lieth in wait as for a\n"
    .string "prey, and increaseth the\l"
    .string "transgressors among men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_29::
    .string "Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who\n"
    .string "hath contentions? who hath babbling?\l"
    .string "who hath wounds without cause? who\l"
    .string "hath redness of eyes?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_30::
    .string "They that tarry long at the wine;\n"
    .string "they that go to seek mixed wine$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_31::
    .string "Look not thou upon the wine when it\n"
    .string "is red, when it giveth his colour in\l"
    .string "the cup, when it moveth itself\l"
    .string "aright.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_32::
    .string "At the last it biteth like a\n"
    .string "serpent, and stingeth like an adder.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_33::
    .string "Thine eyes shall behold strange\n"
    .string "women, and thine heart shall utter\l"
    .string "perverse things.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_34::
    .string "Yea, thou shalt be as he that lieth\n"
    .string "down in the midst of the sea, or as he\l"
    .string "that lieth upon the top of a mast.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_23_35::
    .string "They have stricken me, shalt thou\n"
    .string "say, and I was not sick; they have\l"
    .string "beaten me, and I felt it not: when\l"
    .string "shall I awake? I will seek it yet\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_1::
    .string "Be not thou envious against evil\n"
    .string "men, neither desire to be with them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_2::
    .string "For their heart studieth\n"
    .string "destruction, and their lips talk of\l"
    .string "mischief.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_3::
    .string "Through wisdom is an house builded;\n"
    .string "and by understanding it is\l"
    .string "established:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_4::
    .string "And by knowledge shall the\n"
    .string "chambers be filled with all\l"
    .string "precious and pleasant riches$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_5::
    .string "A wise man is strong; yea, a man of\n"
    .string "knowledge increaseth strength.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_6::
    .string "For by wise counsel thou shalt\n"
    .string "make thy war: and in multitude of\l"
    .string "counsellors there is safety.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_7::
    .string "Wisdom is too high for a fool: he\n"
    .string "openeth not his mouth in the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_8::
    .string "He that deviseth to do evil shall\n"
    .string "be called a mischievous person.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_9::
    .string "The thought of foolishness is sin:\n"
    .string "and the scorner is an abomination to\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_10::
    .string "If thou faint in the day of\n"
    .string "adversity, thy strength is small.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_11::
    .string "If thou forbear to deliver them\n"
    .string "that are drawn unto death, and those\l"
    .string "that are ready to be slain;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_12::
    .string "If thou sayest, Behold, we knew it\n"
    .string "not; doth not he that pondereth the\l"
    .string "heart consider it? and he that\l"
    .string "keepeth thy soul, doth not he know\l"
    .string "it? and shall not he render to every\l"
    .string "man according to his works?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_13::
    .string "My son, eat thou honey, because it\n"
    .string "is good; and the honeycomb, which is\l"
    .string "sweet to thy taste:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_14::
    .string "So shall the knowledge of wisdom\n"
    .string "be unto thy soul: when thou hast\l"
    .string "found it, then there shall be a\l"
    .string "reward, and thy expectation shall\l"
    .string "not be cut off$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_15::
    .string "Lay not wait, O wicked man, against\n"
    .string "the dwelling of the righteous;\l"
    .string "spoil not his resting place:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_16::
    .string "For a just man falleth seven times,\n"
    .string "and riseth up again: but the wicked\l"
    .string "shall fall into mischief$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_17::
    .string "Rejoice not when thine enemy\n"
    .string "falleth, and let not thine heart be\l"
    .string "glad when he stumbleth:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_18::
    .string "Lest the LORD see it, and it\n"
    .string "displease him, and he turn away his\l"
    .string "wrath from him$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_19::
    .string "Fret not thyself because of evil\n"
    .string "men, neither be thou envious at the\l"
    .string "wicked:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_20::
    .string "For there shall be no reward to the\n"
    .string "evil man; the candle of the wicked\l"
    .string "shall be put out$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_21::
    .string "My son, fear thou the LORD and the\n"
    .string "king: and meddle not with them that\l"
    .string "are given to change:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_22::
    .string "For their calamity shall rise\n"
    .string "suddenly; and who knoweth the ruin\l"
    .string "of them both?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_23::
    .string "These things also belong to the\n"
    .string "wise. It is not good to have respect\l"
    .string "of persons in judgment$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_24::
    .string "He that saith unto the wicked, Thou\n"
    .string "are righteous; him shall the\l"
    .string "people curse, nations shall abhor\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_25::
    .string "But to them that rebuke him shall\n"
    .string "be delight, and a good blessing\l"
    .string "shall come upon them$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_26::
    .string "Every man shall kiss his lips\n"
    .string "that giveth a right answer.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_27::
    .string "Prepare thy work without, and make\n"
    .string "it fit for thyself in the field; and\l"
    .string "afterwards build thine house.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_28::
    .string "Be not a witness against thy\n"
    .string "neighbour without cause; and deceive\l"
    .string "not with thy lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_29::
    .string "Say not, I will do so to him as he\n"
    .string "hath done to me: I will render to\l"
    .string "the man according to his work.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_30::
    .string "I went by the field of the\n"
    .string "slothful, and by the vineyard of the\l"
    .string "man void of understanding;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_31::
    .string "And, lo, it was all grown over\n"
    .string "with thorns, and nettles had covered\l"
    .string "the face thereof, and the stone wall\l"
    .string "thereof was broken down$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_32::
    .string "Then I saw, and considered it well:\n"
    .string "I looked upon it, and received\l"
    .string "instruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_33::
    .string "Yet a little sleep, a little\n"
    .string "slumber, a little folding of the\l"
    .string "hands to sleep:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_24_34::
    .string "So shall thy poverty come as one\n"
    .string "that travelleth; and thy want as an\l"
    .string "armed man$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_1::
    .string "These are also proverbs of\n"
    .string "Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah copied out.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_2::
    .string "It is the glory of God to conceal a\n"
    .string "thing: but the honour of kings is to\l"
    .string "search out a matter.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_3::
    .string "The heaven for height, and the earth\n"
    .string "for depth, and the heart of kings is\l"
    .string "unsearchable.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_4::
    .string "Take away the dross from the\n"
    .string "silver, and there shall come forth\l"
    .string "a vessel for the finer.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_5::
    .string "Take away the wicked from before the\n"
    .string "king, and his throne shall be\l"
    .string "established in righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_6::
    .string "Put not forth thyself in the\n"
    .string "presence of the king, and stand not\l"
    .string "in the place of great men:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_7::
    .string "For better it is that it be said\n"
    .string "unto thee, Come up hither; than that\l"
    .string "thou shouldest be put lower in the\l"
    .string "presence of the prince whom thine\l"
    .string "eyes have seen$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_8::
    .string "Go not forth hastily to strive,\n"
    .string "lest thou know not what to do in the\l"
    .string "end thereof, when thy neighbour hath\l"
    .string "put thee to shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_9::
    .string "Debate thy cause with thy neighbour\n"
    .string "himself; and discover not a secret\l"
    .string "to another:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_10::
    .string "Lest he that heareth it put thee to\n"
    .string "shame, and thine infamy turn not away$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_11::
    .string "A word fitly spoken is like\n"
    .string "apples of gold in pictures of\l"
    .string "silver.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_12::
    .string "As an earring of gold, and an\n"
    .string "ornament of fine gold, so is a wise\l"
    .string "reprover upon an obedient ear.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_13::
    .string "As the cold of snow in the time of\n"
    .string "harvest, so is a faithful messenger\l"
    .string "to them that send him: for he\l"
    .string "refresheth the soul of his masters.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_14::
    .string "Whoso boasteth himself of a false\n"
    .string "gift is like clouds and wind\l"
    .string "without rain.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_15::
    .string "By long forbearing is a prince\n"
    .string "persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh\l"
    .string "the bone.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_16::
    .string "Hast thou found honey? eat so much\n"
    .string "as is sufficient for thee, lest thou\l"
    .string "be filled therewith, and vomit it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_17::
    .string "Withdraw thy foot from thy\n"
    .string "neighbour’s house; lest he be weary\l"
    .string "of thee, and so hate thee.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_18::
    .string "A man that beareth false witness\n"
    .string "against his neighbour is a maul, and\l"
    .string "a sword, and a sharp arrow.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_19::
    .string "Confidence in an unfaithful man in\n"
    .string "time of trouble is like a broken\l"
    .string "tooth, and a foot out of joint.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_20::
    .string "As he that taketh away a garment in\n"
    .string "cold weather, and as vinegar upon\l"
    .string "nitre, so is he that singeth songs to\l"
    .string "an heavy heart.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_21::
    .string "If thine enemy be hungry, give him\n"
    .string "bread to eat; and if he be thirsty,\l"
    .string "give him water to drink:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_22::
    .string "For thou shalt heap coals of fire\n"
    .string "upon his head, and the LORD shall\l"
    .string "reward thee$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_23::
    .string "The north wind driveth away rain: so\n"
    .string "doth an angry countenance a\l"
    .string "backbiting tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_24::
    .string "It is better to dwell in the corner\n"
    .string "of the housetop, than with a\l"
    .string "brawling woman and in a wide house.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_25::
    .string "As cold waters to a thirsty soul,\n"
    .string "so is good news from a far country.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_26::
    .string "A righteous man falling down\n"
    .string "before the wicked is as a troubled\l"
    .string "fountain, and a corrupt spring.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_27::
    .string "It is not good to eat much honey: so\n"
    .string "for men to search their own glory is\l"
    .string "not glory.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_25_28::
    .string "He that hath no rule over his own\n"
    .string "spirit is like a city that is broken\l"
    .string "down, and without walls.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_1::
    .string "As snow in summer, and as rain in\n"
    .string "harvest, so honour is not seemly for\l"
    .string "a fool.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_2::
    .string "As the bird by wandering, as the\n"
    .string "swallow by flying, so the curse\l"
    .string "causeless shall not come.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_3::
    .string "A whip for the horse, a bridle for\n"
    .string "the ass, and a rod for the fool’s\l"
    .string "back.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_4::
    .string "Answer not a fool according to his\n"
    .string "folly, lest thou also be like unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_5::
    .string "Answer a fool according to his\n"
    .string "folly, lest he be wise in his own\l"
    .string "conceit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_6::
    .string "He that sendeth a message by the\n"
    .string "hand of a fool cutteth off the feet,\l"
    .string "and drinketh damage.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_7::
    .string "The legs of the lame are not\n"
    .string "equal: so is a parable in the mouth\l"
    .string "of fools.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_8::
    .string "As he that bindeth a stone in a\n"
    .string "sling, so is he that giveth honour to\l"
    .string "a fool.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_9::
    .string "As a thorn goeth up into the hand of\n"
    .string "a drunkard, so is a parable in the\l"
    .string "mouths of fools.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_10::
    .string "The great God that formed all\n"
    .string "things both rewardeth the fool, and\l"
    .string "rewardeth transgressors.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_11::
    .string "As a dog returneth to his vomit, so a\n"
    .string "fool returneth to his folly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_12::
    .string "Seest thou a man wise in his own\n"
    .string "conceit? there is more hope of a\l"
    .string "fool than of him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_13::
    .string "The slothful man saith, There is a\n"
    .string "lion in the way; a lion is in the\l"
    .string "streets.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_14::
    .string "As the door turneth upon his\n"
    .string "hinges, so doth the slothful upon\l"
    .string "his bed.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_15::
    .string "The slothful hideth his hand in\n"
    .string "his bosom; it grieveth him to bring\l"
    .string "it again to his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_16::
    .string "The sluggard is wiser in his own\n"
    .string "conceit than seven men that can\l"
    .string "render a reason.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_17::
    .string "He that passeth by, and meddleth\n"
    .string "with strife belonging not to him, is\l"
    .string "like one that taketh a dog by the\l"
    .string "ears.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_18::
    .string "As a mad man who casteth firebrands,\n"
    .string "arrows, and death,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_19::
    .string "So is the man that deceiveth his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and saith, Am not I in\l"
    .string "sport?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_20::
    .string "Where no wood is, there the fire\n"
    .string "goeth out: so where there is no\l"
    .string "talebearer, the strife ceaseth$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_21::
    .string "As coals are to burning coals, and\n"
    .string "wood to fire; so is a contentious man\l"
    .string "to kindle strife.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_22::
    .string "The words of a talebearer are as\n"
    .string "wounds, and they go down into the\l"
    .string "innermost parts of the belly.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_23::
    .string "Burning lips and a wicked heart\n"
    .string "are like a potsherd covered with\l"
    .string "silver dross.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_24::
    .string "He that hateth dissembleth with his\n"
    .string "lips, and layeth up deceit within\l"
    .string "him;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_25::
    .string "When he speaketh fair, believe him\n"
    .string "not: for there are seven abominations\l"
    .string "in his heart$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_26::
    .string "Whose hatred is covered by deceit,\n"
    .string "his wickedness shall be shewed\l"
    .string "before the whole congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_27::
    .string "Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall\n"
    .string "therein: and he that rolleth a\l"
    .string "stone, it will return upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_26_28::
    .string "A lying tongue hateth those that\n"
    .string "are afflicted by it; and a\l"
    .string "flattering mouth worketh ruin.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_1::
    .string "Boast not thyself of to morrow; for\n"
    .string "thou knowest not what a day may bring\l"
    .string "forth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_2::
    .string "Let another man praise thee, and\n"
    .string "not thine own mouth; a stranger, and\l"
    .string "not thine own lips.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_3::
    .string "A stone is heavy, and the sand\n"
    .string "weighty; but a fool’s wrath is\l"
    .string "heavier than them both.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_4::
    .string "Wrath is cruel, and anger is\n"
    .string "outrageous; but who is able to stand\l"
    .string "before envy?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_5::
    .string "Open rebuke is better than secret\n"
    .string "love$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_6::
    .string "Faithful are the wounds of a\n"
    .string "friend; but the kisses of an enemy\l"
    .string "are deceitful.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_7::
    .string "The full soul loatheth an\n"
    .string "honeycomb; but to the hungry soul\l"
    .string "every bitter thing is sweet.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_8::
    .string "As a bird that wandereth from her\n"
    .string "nest, so is a man that wandereth from\l"
    .string "his place.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_9::
    .string "Ointment and perfume rejoice the\n"
    .string "heart: so doth the sweetness of a\l"
    .string "man’s friend by hearty counsel.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_10::
    .string "Thine own friend, and thy father’s\n"
    .string "friend, forsake not; neither go into\l"
    .string "thy brother’s house in the day of thy\l"
    .string "calamity: for better is a neighbour\l"
    .string "that is near than a brother far off.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_11::
    .string "My son, be wise, and make my heart\n"
    .string "glad, that I may answer him that\l"
    .string "reproacheth me.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_12::
    .string "A prudent man foreseeth the evil,\n"
    .string "and hideth himself; but the simple\l"
    .string "pass on, and are punished.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_13::
    .string "Take his garment that is surety for\n"
    .string "a stranger, and take a pledge of him\l"
    .string "for a strange woman.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_14::
    .string "He that blesseth his friend with a\n"
    .string "loud voice, rising early in the\l"
    .string "morning, it shall be counted a curse\l"
    .string "to him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_15::
    .string "A continual dropping in a very\n"
    .string "rainy day and a contentious woman are\l"
    .string "alike.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_16::
    .string "Whosoever hideth her hideth the\n"
    .string "wind, and the ointment of his right\l"
    .string "hand, which bewrayeth itself.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_17::
    .string "Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man\n"
    .string "sharpeneth the countenance of his\l"
    .string "friend.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_18::
    .string "Whoso keepeth the fig tree shall\n"
    .string "eat the fruit thereof: so he that\l"
    .string "waiteth on his master shall be\l"
    .string "honoured.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_19::
    .string "As in water face answereth to face,\n"
    .string "so the heart of man to man.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_20::
    .string "Hell and destruction are never\n"
    .string "full; so the eyes of man are never\l"
    .string "satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_21::
    .string "As the fining pot for silver, and\n"
    .string "the furnace for gold; so is a man to\l"
    .string "his praise.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_22::
    .string "Though thou shouldest bray a fool\n"
    .string "in a mortar among wheat with a\l"
    .string "pestle, yet will not his\l"
    .string "foolishness depart from him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_23::
    .string "Be thou diligent to know the state\n"
    .string "of thy flocks, and look well to thy\l"
    .string "herds.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_24::
    .string "For riches are not for ever: and\n"
    .string "doth the crown endure to every\l"
    .string "generation?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_25::
    .string "The hay appeareth, and the tender\n"
    .string "grass sheweth itself, and herbs of\l"
    .string "the mountains are gathered$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_26::
    .string "The lambs are for thy clothing, and\n"
    .string "the goats are the price of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_27_27::
    .string "And thou shalt have goats’ milk\n"
    .string "enough for thy food, for the food of\l"
    .string "thy household, and for the\l"
    .string "maintenance for thy maidens.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_1::
    .string "The wicked flee when no man\n"
    .string "pursueth: but the righteous are bold\l"
    .string "as a lion.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_2::
    .string "For the transgression of a land\n"
    .string "many are the princes thereof: but by\l"
    .string "a man of understanding and knowledge\l"
    .string "the state thereof shall be\l"
    .string "prolonged.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_3::
    .string "A poor man that oppresseth the\n"
    .string "poor is like a sweeping rain which\l"
    .string "leaveth no food.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_4::
    .string "They that forsake the law praise\n"
    .string "the wicked: but such as keep the law\l"
    .string "contend with them.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_5::
    .string "Evil men understand not judgment:\n"
    .string "but they that seek the LORD\l"
    .string "understand all things.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_6::
    .string "Better is the poor that walketh in\n"
    .string "his uprightness, than he that is\l"
    .string "perverse in his ways, though he be\l"
    .string "rich.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_7::
    .string "Whoso keepeth the law is a wise\n"
    .string "son: but he that is a companion of\l"
    .string "riotous men shameth his father.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_8::
    .string "He that by usury and unjust gain\n"
    .string "increaseth his substance, he shall\l"
    .string "gather it for him that will pity\l"
    .string "the poor.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_9::
    .string "He that turneth away his ear from\n"
    .string "hearing the law, even his prayer\l"
    .string "shall be abomination.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_10::
    .string "Whoso causeth the righteous to go\n"
    .string "astray in an evil way, he shall\l"
    .string "fall himself into his own pit: but\l"
    .string "the upright shall have good things\l"
    .string "in possession.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_11::
    .string "The rich man is wise in his own\n"
    .string "conceit; but the poor that hath\l"
    .string "understanding searcheth him out.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_12::
    .string "When righteous men do rejoice, there\n"
    .string "is great glory: but when the wicked\l"
    .string "rise, a man is hidden.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_13::
    .string "He that covereth his sins shall\n"
    .string "not prosper: but whoso confesseth\l"
    .string "and forsaketh them shall have mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_14::
    .string "Happy is the man that feareth\n"
    .string "alway: but he that hardeneth his\l"
    .string "heart shall fall into mischief.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_15::
    .string "As a roaring lion, and a ranging\n"
    .string "bear; so is a wicked ruler over the\l"
    .string "poor people.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_16::
    .string "The prince that wanteth\n"
    .string "understanding is also a great\l"
    .string "oppressor: but he that hateth\l"
    .string "covetousness shall prolong his\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_17::
    .string "A man that doeth violence to the\n"
    .string "blood of any person shall flee to\l"
    .string "the pit; let no man stay him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_18::
    .string "Whoso walketh uprightly shall be\n"
    .string "saved: but he that is perverse in his\l"
    .string "ways shall fall at once.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_19::
    .string "He that tilleth his land shall\n"
    .string "have plenty of bread: but he that\l"
    .string "followeth after vain persons\l"
    .string "shall have poverty enough.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_20::
    .string "A faithful man shall abound with\n"
    .string "blessings: but he that maketh haste\l"
    .string "to be rich shall not be innocent.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_21::
    .string "To have respect of persons is not\n"
    .string "good: for for a piece of bread that\l"
    .string "man will transgress.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_22::
    .string "He that hasteth to be rich hath an\n"
    .string "evil eye, and considereth not that\l"
    .string "poverty shall come upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_23::
    .string "He that rebuketh a man afterwards\n"
    .string "shall find more favour than he that\l"
    .string "flattereth with the tongue.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_24::
    .string "Whoso robbeth his father or his\n"
    .string "mother, and saith, It is no\l"
    .string "transgression; the same is the\l"
    .string "companion of a destroyer.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_25::
    .string "He that is of a proud heart\n"
    .string "stirreth up strife: but he that\l"
    .string "putteth his trust in the LORD shall\l"
    .string "be made fat.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_26::
    .string "He that trusteth in his own heart is\n"
    .string "a fool: but whoso walketh wisely,\l"
    .string "he shall be delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_27::
    .string "He that giveth unto the poor shall\n"
    .string "not lack: but he that hideth his eyes\l"
    .string "shall have many a curse.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_28_28::
    .string "When the wicked rise, men hide\n"
    .string "themselves: but when they perish,\l"
    .string "the righteous increase.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_1::
    .string "He, that being often reproved\n"
    .string "hardeneth his neck, shall suddenly\l"
    .string "be destroyed, and that without\l"
    .string "remedy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_2::
    .string "When the righteous are in authority,\n"
    .string "the people rejoice: but when the\l"
    .string "wicked beareth rule, the people\l"
    .string "mourn.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_3::
    .string "Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his\n"
    .string "father: but he that keepeth company\l"
    .string "with harlots spendeth his substance.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_4::
    .string "The king by judgment establisheth\n"
    .string "the land: but he that receiveth\l"
    .string "gifts overthroweth it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_5::
    .string "A man that flattereth his neighbour\n"
    .string "spreadeth a net for his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_6::
    .string "In the transgression of an evil man\n"
    .string "there is a snare: but the righteous\l"
    .string "doth sing and rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_7::
    .string "The righteous considereth the cause\n"
    .string "of the poor: but the wicked\l"
    .string "regardeth not to know it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_8::
    .string "Scornful men bring a city into a\n"
    .string "snare: but wise men turn away wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_9::
    .string "If a wise man contendeth with a\n"
    .string "foolish man, whether he rage or\l"
    .string "laugh, there is no rest.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_10::
    .string "The bloodthirsty hate the upright:\n"
    .string "but the just seek his soul.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_11::
    .string "A fool uttereth all his mind: but\n"
    .string "a wise man keepeth it in till\l"
    .string "afterwards.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_12::
    .string "If a ruler hearken to lies, all\n"
    .string "his servants are wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_13::
    .string "The poor and the deceitful man\n"
    .string "meet together: the LORD lighteneth\l"
    .string "both their eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_14::
    .string "The king that faithfully judgeth\n"
    .string "the poor, his throne shall be\l"
    .string "established for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_15::
    .string "The rod and reproof give wisdom:\n"
    .string "but a child left to himself\l"
    .string "bringeth his mother to shame.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_16::
    .string "When the wicked are multiplied,\n"
    .string "transgression increaseth: but the\l"
    .string "righteous shall see their fall.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_17::
    .string "Correct thy son, and he shall give\n"
    .string "thee rest; yea, he shall give\l"
    .string "delight unto thy soul.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_18::
    .string "Where there is no vision, the\n"
    .string "people perish: but he that keepeth\l"
    .string "the law, happy is he.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_19::
    .string "A servant will not be corrected by\n"
    .string "words: for though he understand he\l"
    .string "will not answer.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_20::
    .string "Seest thou a man that is hasty in\n"
    .string "his words? there is more hope of a\l"
    .string "fool than of him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_21::
    .string "He that delicately bringeth up\n"
    .string "his servant from a child shall have\l"
    .string "him become his son at the length.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_22::
    .string "An angry man stirreth up strife,\n"
    .string "and a furious man aboundeth in\l"
    .string "transgression.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_23::
    .string "A man’s pride shall bring him\n"
    .string "low: but honour shall uphold the\l"
    .string "humble in spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_24::
    .string "Whoso is partner with a thief\n"
    .string "hateth his own soul: he heareth\l"
    .string "cursing, and bewrayeth it not.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_25::
    .string "The fear of man bringeth a snare:\n"
    .string "but whoso putteth his trust in the\l"
    .string "LORD shall be safe.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_26::
    .string "Many seek the ruler’s favour; but\n"
    .string "every man’s judgment cometh from the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_29_27::
    .string "An unjust man is an abomination to\n"
    .string "the just: and he that is upright in\l"
    .string "the way is abomination to the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_1::
    .string "The words of Agur the son of Jakeh,\n"
    .string "even the prophecy: the man spake\l"
    .string "unto Ithiel, even unto Ithiel and\l"
    .string "Ucal,"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_2::
    .string "Surely I am more brutish than any\n"
    .string "man, and have not the understanding\l"
    .string "of a man$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_3::
    .string "I neither learned wisdom, nor have\n"
    .string "the knowledge of the holy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_4::
    .string "Who hath ascended up into heaven,\n"
    .string "or descended? who hath gathered the\l"
    .string "wind in his fists? who hath bound the\l"
    .string "waters in a garment? who hath\l"
    .string "established all the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth? what is his name, and what is\l"
    .string "his son’s name, if thou canst tell?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_5::
    .string "Every word of God is pure: he is a\n"
    .string "shield unto them that put their\l"
    .string "trust in him$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_6::
    .string "Add thou not unto his words, lest he\n"
    .string "reprove thee, and thou be found a\l"
    .string "liar.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_7::
    .string "Two things have I required of thee;\n"
    .string "deny me them not before I die:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_8::
    .string "Remove far from me vanity and lies:\n"
    .string "give me neither poverty nor riches;\l"
    .string "feed me with food convenient for me:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_9::
    .string "Lest I be full, and deny thee, and\n"
    .string "say, Who is the LORD? or lest I be\l"
    .string "poor, and steal, and take the name of\l"
    .string "my God in vain$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_10::
    .string "Accuse not a servant unto his\n"
    .string "master, lest he curse thee, and thou\l"
    .string "be found guilty.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_11::
    .string "There is a generation that curseth\n"
    .string "their father, and doth not bless\l"
    .string "their mother.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_12::
    .string "There is a generation that are pure\n"
    .string "in their own eyes, and yet is not\l"
    .string "washed from their filthiness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_13::
    .string "There is a generation, O how lofty\n"
    .string "are their eyes! and their eyelids\l"
    .string "are lifted up.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_14::
    .string "There is a generation, whose teeth\n"
    .string "are as swords, and their jaw teeth as\l"
    .string "knives, to devour the poor from off\l"
    .string "the earth, and the needy from among\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_15::
    .string "The horseleach hath two daughters,\n"
    .string "crying, Give, give. There are three\l"
    .string "things that are never satisfied, yea,\l"
    .string "four things say not, It is enough:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_16::
    .string "The grave; and the barren womb; the\n"
    .string "earth that is not filled with water;\l"
    .string "and the fire that saith not, It is\l"
    .string "enough$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_17::
    .string "The eye that mocketh at his father,\n"
    .string "and despiseth to obey his mother,\l"
    .string "the ravens of the valley shall\l"
    .string "pick it out, and the young eagles\l"
    .string "shall eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_18::
    .string "There be three things which are too\n"
    .string "wonderful for me, yea, four which I\l"
    .string "know not:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_19::
    .string "The way of an eagle in the air; the\n"
    .string "way of a serpent upon a rock; the\l"
    .string "way of a ship in the midst of the\l"
    .string "sea; and the way of a man with a maid$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_20::
    .string "Such is the way of an adulterous\n"
    .string "woman; she eateth, and wipeth her\l"
    .string "mouth, and saith, I have done no\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_21::
    .string "For three things the earth is\n"
    .string "disquieted, and for four which it\l"
    .string "cannot bear:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_22::
    .string "For a servant when he reigneth; and\n"
    .string "a fool when he is filled with meat;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_23::
    .string "For an odious woman when she is\n"
    .string "married; and an handmaid that is heir\l"
    .string "to her mistress$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_24::
    .string "There be four things which are\n"
    .string "little upon the earth, but they are\l"
    .string "exceeding wise:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_25::
    .string "The ants are a people not strong,\n"
    .string "yet they prepare their meat in the\l"
    .string "summer;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_26::
    .string "The conies are but a feeble folk,\n"
    .string "yet make they their houses in the\l"
    .string "rocks;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_27::
    .string "The locusts have no king, yet go\n"
    .string "they forth all of them by bands;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_28::
    .string "The spider taketh hold with her\n"
    .string "hands, and is in kings’ palaces$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_29::
    .string "There be three things which go\n"
    .string "well, yea, four are comely in\l"
    .string "going:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_30::
    .string "A lion which is strongest among\n"
    .string "beasts, and turneth not away for any;"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_31::
    .string "A greyhound; an he goat also; and a\n"
    .string "king, against whom there is no rising\l"
    .string "up$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_32::
    .string "If thou hast done foolishly in\n"
    .string "lifting up thyself, or if thou hast\l"
    .string "thought evil, lay thine hand upon\l"
    .string "thy mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_30_33::
    .string "Surely the churning of milk\n"
    .string "bringeth forth butter, and the\l"
    .string "wringing of the nose bringeth forth\l"
    .string "blood: so the forcing of wrath\l"
    .string "bringeth forth strife.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_1::
    .string "The words of king Lemuel, the\n"
    .string "prophecy that his mother taught him.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_2::
    .string "What, my son? and what, the son of my\n"
    .string "womb? and what, the son of my vows?"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_3::
    .string "Give not thy strength unto women,\n"
    .string "nor thy ways to that which destroyeth\l"
    .string "kings$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_4::
    .string "It is not for kings, O Lemuel, it is\n"
    .string "not for kings to drink wine; nor for\l"
    .string "princes strong drink:"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_5::
    .string "Lest they drink, and forget the\n"
    .string "law, and pervert the judgment of any\l"
    .string "of the afflicted$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_6::
    .string "Give strong drink unto him that is\n"
    .string "ready to perish, and wine unto those\l"
    .string "that be of heavy hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_7::
    .string "Let him drink, and forget his\n"
    .string "poverty, and remember his misery no\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_8::
    .string "Open thy mouth for the dumb in the\n"
    .string "cause of all such as are appointed\l"
    .string "to destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_9::
    .string "Open thy mouth, judge righteously,\n"
    .string "and plead the cause of the poor and\l"
    .string "needy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_10::
    .string "Who can find a virtuous woman? for\n"
    .string "her price is far above rubies.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_11::
    .string "The heart of her husband doth\n"
    .string "safely trust in her, so that he\l"
    .string "shall have no need of spoil.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_12::
    .string "She will do him good and not evil\n"
    .string "all the days of her life.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_13::
    .string "She seeketh wool, and flax, and\n"
    .string "worketh willingly with her hands.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_14::
    .string "She is like the merchants’ ships;\n"
    .string "she bringeth her food from afar.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_15::
    .string "She riseth also while it is yet\n"
    .string "night, and giveth meat to her\l"
    .string "household, and a portion to her\l"
    .string "maidens.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_16::
    .string "She considereth a field, and buyeth\n"
    .string "it: with the fruit of her hands she\l"
    .string "planteth a vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_17::
    .string "She girdeth her loins with\n"
    .string "strength, and strengtheneth her arms.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_18::
    .string "She perceiveth that her\n"
    .string "merchandise is good: her candle\l"
    .string "goeth not out by night.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_19::
    .string "She layeth her hands to the\n"
    .string "spindle, and her hands hold the\l"
    .string "distaff.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_20::
    .string "She stretcheth out her hand to the\n"
    .string "poor; yea, she reacheth forth her\l"
    .string "hands to the needy.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_21::
    .string "She is not afraid of the snow for\n"
    .string "her household: for all her\l"
    .string "household are clothed with scarlet.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_22::
    .string "She maketh herself coverings of\n"
    .string "tapestry; her clothing is silk and\l"
    .string "purple.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_23::
    .string "Her husband is known in the gates,\n"
    .string "when he sitteth among the elders of\l"
    .string "the land.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_24::
    .string "She maketh fine linen, and selleth\n"
    .string "it; and delivereth girdles unto the\l"
    .string "merchant.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_25::
    .string "Strength and honour are her\n"
    .string "clothing; and she shall rejoice in\l"
    .string "time to come.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_26::
    .string "She openeth her mouth with wisdom;\n"
    .string "and in her tongue is the law of\l"
    .string "kindness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_27::
    .string "She looketh well to the ways of\n"
    .string "her household, and eateth not the\l"
    .string "bread of idleness.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_28::
    .string "Her children arise up, and call\n"
    .string "her blessed; her husband also, and\l"
    .string "he praiseth her.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_29::
    .string "Many daughters have done\n"
    .string "virtuously, but thou excellest\l"
    .string "them all.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_30::
    .string "Favour is deceitful, and beauty is\n"
    .string "vain: but a woman that feareth the\l"
    .string "LORD, she shall be praised.$"
Bible_Text_Proverbs_31_31::
    .string "Give her of the fruit of her hands;\n"
    .string "and let her own works praise her in\l"
    .string "the gates.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_1::
    .string "The words of the Preacher, the son\n"
    .string "of David, king in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_2::
    .string "Vanity of vanities, saith the\n"
    .string "Preacher, vanity of vanities; all\l"
    .string "is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_3::
    .string "What profit hath a man of all his\n"
    .string "labour which he taketh under the sun?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_4::
    .string "One generation passeth away, and\n"
    .string "another generation cometh: but the\l"
    .string "earth abideth for ever$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_5::
    .string "The sun also ariseth, and the sun\n"
    .string "goeth down, and hasteth to his place\l"
    .string "where he arose.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_6::
    .string "The wind goeth toward the south, and\n"
    .string "turneth about unto the north; it\l"
    .string "whirleth about continually, and\l"
    .string "the wind returneth again according\l"
    .string "to his circuits.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_7::
    .string "All the rivers run into the sea;\n"
    .string "yet the sea is not full; unto the\l"
    .string "place from whence the rivers come,\l"
    .string "thither they return again.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_8::
    .string "All things are full of labour;\n"
    .string "man cannot utter it: the eye is not\l"
    .string "satisfied with seeing, nor the ear\l"
    .string "filled with hearing.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_9::
    .string "The thing that hath been, it is that\n"
    .string "which shall be; and that which is\l"
    .string "done is that which shall be done:\l"
    .string "and there is no new thing under the\l"
    .string "sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_10::
    .string "Is there any thing whereof it may be\n"
    .string "said, See, this is new? it hath been\l"
    .string "already of old time, which was\l"
    .string "before us.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_11::
    .string "There is no remembrance of former\n"
    .string "things; neither shall there be any\l"
    .string "remembrance of things that are to\l"
    .string "come with those that shall come\l"
    .string "after.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_12::
    .string "I the Preacher was king over Israel\n"
    .string "in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_13::
    .string "And I gave my heart to seek and\n"
    .string "search out by wisdom concerning all\l"
    .string "things that are done under heaven:\l"
    .string "this sore travail hath God given to\l"
    .string "the sons of man to be exercised\l"
    .string "therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_14::
    .string "I have seen all the works that are\n"
    .string "done under the sun; and, behold,\l"
    .string "all is vanity and vexation of\l"
    .string "spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_15::
    .string "That which is crooked cannot be made\n"
    .string "straight: and that which is wanting\l"
    .string "cannot be numbered.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_16::
    .string "I communed with mine own heart,\n"
    .string "saying, Lo, I am come to great estate,\l"
    .string "and have gotten more wisdom than\l"
    .string "all they that have been before me in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: yea, my heart had great\l"
    .string "experience of wisdom and knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_17::
    .string "And I gave my heart to know wisdom,\n"
    .string "and to know madness and folly: I\l"
    .string "perceived that this also is vexation\l"
    .string "of spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_1_18::
    .string "For in much wisdom is much grief:\n"
    .string "and he that increaseth knowledge\l"
    .string "increaseth sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_1::
    .string "I said in mine heart, Go to now, I\n"
    .string "will prove thee with mirth,\l"
    .string "therefore enjoy pleasure: and,\l"
    .string "behold, this also is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_2::
    .string "I said of laughter, It is mad: and\n"
    .string "of mirth, What doeth it?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_3::
    .string "I sought in mine heart to give\n"
    .string "myself unto wine, yet acquainting\l"
    .string "mine heart with wisdom; and to lay\l"
    .string "hold on folly, till I might see\l"
    .string "what was that good for the sons of\l"
    .string "men, which they should do under the\l"
    .string "heaven all the days of their life$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_4::
    .string "I made me great works; I builded me\n"
    .string "houses; I planted me vineyards:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_5::
    .string "I made me gardens and orchards, and\n"
    .string "I planted trees in them of all\l"
    .string "kind of fruits:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_6::
    .string "I made me pools of water, to water\n"
    .string "therewith the wood that bringeth\l"
    .string "forth trees:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_7::
    .string "I got me servants and maidens, and\n"
    .string "had servants born in my house; also I\l"
    .string "had great possessions of great and\l"
    .string "small cattle above all that were\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem before me:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_8::
    .string "I gathered me also silver and\n"
    .string "gold, and the peculiar treasure of\l"
    .string "kings and of the provinces: I gat me\l"
    .string "men singers and women singers, and\l"
    .string "the delights of the sons of men, as\l"
    .string "musical instruments, and that of\l"
    .string "all sorts$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_9::
    .string "So I was great, and increased more\n"
    .string "than all that were before me in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_10::
    .string "And whatsoever mine eyes desired I\n"
    .string "kept not from them, I withheld not\l"
    .string "my heart from any joy; for my heart\l"
    .string "rejoiced in all my labour: and this\l"
    .string "was my portion of all my labour.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_11::
    .string "Then I looked on all the works\n"
    .string "that my hands had wrought, and on the\l"
    .string "labour that I had laboured to do:\l"
    .string "and, behold, all was vanity and\l"
    .string "vexation of spirit, and there was no\l"
    .string "profit under the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_12::
    .string "And I turned myself to behold\n"
    .string "wisdom, and madness, and folly: for\l"
    .string "what can the man do that cometh after\l"
    .string "the king? even that which hath been\l"
    .string "already done.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_13::
    .string "Then I saw that wisdom excelleth\n"
    .string "folly, as far as light excelleth\l"
    .string "darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_14::
    .string "The wise man’s eyes are in his head;\n"
    .string "but the fool walketh in darkness:\l"
    .string "and I myself perceived also that\l"
    .string "one event happeneth to them all.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_15::
    .string "Then said I in my heart, As it\n"
    .string "happeneth to the fool, so it\l"
    .string "happeneth even to me; and why was I\l"
    .string "then more wise? Then I said in my\l"
    .string "heart, that this also is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_16::
    .string "For there is no remembrance of the\n"
    .string "wise more than of the fool for ever;\l"
    .string "seeing that which now is in the days\l"
    .string "to come shall all be forgotten.\l"
    .string "And how dieth the wise man? as the\l"
    .string "fool.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_17::
    .string "Therefore I hated life; because the\n"
    .string "work that is wrought under the sun is\l"
    .string "grievous unto me: for all is vanity\l"
    .string "and vexation of spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_18::
    .string "Yea, I hated all my labour which I\n"
    .string "had taken under the sun: because I\l"
    .string "should leave it unto the man that\l"
    .string "shall be after me.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_19::
    .string "And who knoweth whether he shall\n"
    .string "be a wise man or a fool? yet shall\l"
    .string "he have rule over all my labour\l"
    .string "wherein I have laboured, and wherein\l"
    .string "I have shewed myself wise under the\l"
    .string "sun. This is also vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_20::
    .string "Therefore I went about to cause my\n"
    .string "heart to despair of all the labour\l"
    .string "which I took under the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_21::
    .string "For there is a man whose labour is\n"
    .string "in wisdom, and in knowledge, and in\l"
    .string "equity; yet to a man that hath not\l"
    .string "laboured therein shall he leave it\l"
    .string "for his portion. This also is vanity\l"
    .string "and a great evil.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_22::
    .string "For what hath man of all his\n"
    .string "labour, and of the vexation of his\l"
    .string "heart, wherein he hath laboured\l"
    .string "under the sun?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_23::
    .string "For all his days are sorrows, and\n"
    .string "his travail grief; yea, his heart\l"
    .string "taketh not rest in the night. This is\l"
    .string "also vanity$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_24::
    .string "There is nothing better for a man,\n"
    .string "than that he should eat and drink,\l"
    .string "and that he should make his soul\l"
    .string "enjoy good in his labour. This also\l"
    .string "I saw, that it was from the hand of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_25::
    .string "For who can eat, or who else can\n"
    .string "hasten hereunto, more than I?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_2_26::
    .string "For God giveth to a man that is good\n"
    .string "in his sight wisdom, and knowledge,\l"
    .string "and joy: but to the sinner he giveth\l"
    .string "travail, to gather and to heap up,\l"
    .string "that he may give to him that is good\l"
    .string "before God. This also is vanity and\l"
    .string "vexation of spirit$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_1::
    .string "To every thing there is a season,\n"
    .string "and a time to every purpose under\l"
    .string "the heaven:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_2::
    .string "A time to be born, and a time to die;\n"
    .string "a time to plant, and a time to\l"
    .string "pluck up that which is planted;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_3::
    .string "A time to kill, and a time to heal;\n"
    .string "a time to break down, and a time to\l"
    .string "build up;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_4::
    .string "A time to weep, and a time to\n"
    .string "laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to\l"
    .string "dance;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_5::
    .string "A time to cast away stones, and a\n"
    .string "time to gather stones together; a\l"
    .string "time to embrace, and a time to\l"
    .string "refrain from embracing;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_6::
    .string "A time to get, and a time to lose; a\n"
    .string "time to keep, and a time to cast\l"
    .string "away;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_7::
    .string "A time to rend, and a time to sew; a\n"
    .string "time to keep silence, and a time to\l"
    .string "speak;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_8::
    .string "A time to love, and a time to hate;\n"
    .string "a time of war, and a time of peace$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_9::
    .string "What profit hath he that worketh in\n"
    .string "that wherein he laboureth?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_10::
    .string "I have seen the travail, which God\n"
    .string "hath given to the sons of men to be\l"
    .string "exercised in it$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_11::
    .string "He hath made every thing beautiful\n"
    .string "in his time: also he hath set the\l"
    .string "world in their heart, so that no man\l"
    .string "can find out the work that God maketh\l"
    .string "from the beginning to the end.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_12::
    .string "I know that there is no good in them,\n"
    .string "but for a man to rejoice, and to do\l"
    .string "good in his life.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_13::
    .string "And also that every man should eat\n"
    .string "and drink, and enjoy the good of all\l"
    .string "his labour, it is the gift of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_14::
    .string "I know that, whatsoever God doeth,\n"
    .string "it shall be for ever: nothing can be\l"
    .string "put to it, nor any thing taken from\l"
    .string "it: and God doeth it, that men should\l"
    .string "fear before him.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_15::
    .string "That which hath been is now; and\n"
    .string "that which is to be hath already\l"
    .string "been; and God requireth that which is\l"
    .string "past.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_16::
    .string "And moreover I saw under the sun the\n"
    .string "place of judgment, that wickedness\l"
    .string "was there; and the place of\l"
    .string "righteousness, that iniquity was\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_17::
    .string "I said in mine heart, God shall\n"
    .string "judge the righteous and the wicked:\l"
    .string "for there is a time there for every\l"
    .string "purpose and for every work.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_18::
    .string "I said in mine heart concerning the\n"
    .string "estate of the sons of men, that God\l"
    .string "might manifest them, and that they\l"
    .string "might see that they themselves are\l"
    .string "beasts.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_19::
    .string "For that which befalleth the sons\n"
    .string "of men befalleth beasts; even one\l"
    .string "thing befalleth them: as the one\l"
    .string "dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they\l"
    .string "have all one breath; so that a man\l"
    .string "hath no preeminence above a beast:\l"
    .string "for all is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_20::
    .string "All go unto one place; all are\n"
    .string "of the dust, and all turn to dust\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_21::
    .string "Who knoweth the spirit of man that\n"
    .string "goeth upward, and the spirit of the\l"
    .string "beast that goeth downward to the\l"
    .string "earth?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_3_22::
    .string "Wherefore I perceive that there is\n"
    .string "nothing better, than that a man\l"
    .string "should rejoice in his own works; for\l"
    .string "that is his portion: for who shall\l"
    .string "bring him to see what shall be after\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_1::
    .string "So I returned, and considered all\n"
    .string "the oppressions that are done under\l"
    .string "the sun: and behold the tears of such\l"
    .string "as were oppressed, and they had no\l"
    .string "comforter; and on the side of their\l"
    .string "oppressors there was power; but\l"
    .string "they had no comforter$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_2::
    .string "Wherefore I praised the dead which\n"
    .string "are already dead more than the\l"
    .string "living which are yet alive.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_3::
    .string "Yea, better is he than both they,\n"
    .string "which hath not yet been, who hath not\l"
    .string "seen the evil work that is done\l"
    .string "under the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_4::
    .string "Again, I considered all travail,\n"
    .string "and every right work, that for this a\l"
    .string "man is envied of his neighbour. This\l"
    .string "is also vanity and vexation of\l"
    .string "spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_5::
    .string "The fool foldeth his hands\n"
    .string "together, and eateth his own flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_6::
    .string "Better is an handful with\n"
    .string "quietness, than both the hands full\l"
    .string "with travail and vexation of spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_7::
    .string "Then I returned, and I saw vanity\n"
    .string "under the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_8::
    .string "There is one alone, and there is not\n"
    .string "a second; yea, he hath neither child\l"
    .string "nor brother: yet is there no end of\l"
    .string "all his labour; neither is his eye\l"
    .string "satisfied with riches; neither saith\l"
    .string "he, For whom do I labour, and bereave\l"
    .string "my soul of good? This is also\l"
    .string "vanity, yea, it is a sore travail.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_9::
    .string "Two are better than one; because\n"
    .string "they have a good reward for their\l"
    .string "labour.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_10::
    .string "For if they fall, the one will\n"
    .string "lift up his fellow: but woe to him\l"
    .string "that is alone when he falleth; for\l"
    .string "he hath not another to help him up.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_11::
    .string "Again, if two lie together, then\n"
    .string "they have heat: but how can one be\l"
    .string "warm alone?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_12::
    .string "And if one prevail against him, two\n"
    .string "shall withstand him; and a\l"
    .string "threefold cord is not quickly broken$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_13::
    .string "Better is a poor and a wise child\n"
    .string "than an old and foolish king, who\l"
    .string "will no more be admonished.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_14::
    .string "For out of prison he cometh to\n"
    .string "reign; whereas also he that is born\l"
    .string "in his kingdom becometh poor.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_15::
    .string "I considered all the living which\n"
    .string "walk under the sun, with the second\l"
    .string "child that shall stand up in his\l"
    .string "stead.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_4_16::
    .string "There is no end of all the\n"
    .string "people, even of all that have been\l"
    .string "before them: they also that come\l"
    .string "after shall not rejoice in him.\l"
    .string "Surely this also is vanity and\l"
    .string "vexation of spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_1::
    .string "Keep thy foot when thou goest to\n"
    .string "the house of God, and be more ready to\l"
    .string "hear, than to give the sacrifice of\l"
    .string "fools: for they consider not that\l"
    .string "they do evil.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_2::
    .string "Be not rash with thy mouth, and let\n"
    .string "not thine heart be hasty to utter any\l"
    .string "thing before God: for God is in\l"
    .string "heaven, and thou upon earth:\l"
    .string "therefore let thy words be few.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_3::
    .string "For a dream cometh through the\n"
    .string "multitude of business; and a fool’s\l"
    .string "voice is known by multitude of words.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_4::
    .string "When thou vowest a vow unto God,\n"
    .string "defer not to pay it; for he hath no\l"
    .string "pleasure in fools: pay that which\l"
    .string "thou hast vowed.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_5::
    .string "Better is it that thou shouldest\n"
    .string "not vow, than that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "vow and not pay.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_6::
    .string "Suffer not thy mouth to cause thy\n"
    .string "flesh to sin; neither say thou\l"
    .string "before the angel, that it was an\l"
    .string "error: wherefore should God be angry\l"
    .string "at thy voice, and destroy the work of\l"
    .string "thine hands?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_7::
    .string "For in the multitude of dreams and\n"
    .string "many words there are also divers\l"
    .string "vanities: but fear thou God$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_8::
    .string "If thou seest the oppression of\n"
    .string "the poor, and violent perverting of\l"
    .string "judgment and justice in a province,\l"
    .string "marvel not at the matter: for he that\l"
    .string "is higher than the highest regardeth;\l"
    .string "and there be higher than they.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_9::
    .string "Moreover the profit of the earth is\n"
    .string "for all: the king himself is served\l"
    .string "by the field.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_10::
    .string "He that loveth silver shall not\n"
    .string "be satisfied with silver; nor he\l"
    .string "that loveth abundance with increase:\l"
    .string "this is also vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_11::
    .string "When goods increase, they are\n"
    .string "increased that eat them: and what\l"
    .string "good is there to the owners thereof,\l"
    .string "saving the beholding of them with\l"
    .string "their eyes?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_12::
    .string "The sleep of a labouring man is\n"
    .string "sweet, whether he eat little or\l"
    .string "much: but the abundance of the rich\l"
    .string "will not suffer him to sleep$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_13::
    .string "There is a sore evil which I have\n"
    .string "seen under the sun, namely, riches\l"
    .string "kept for the owners thereof to their\l"
    .string "hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_14::
    .string "But those riches perish by evil\n"
    .string "travail: and he begetteth a son, and\l"
    .string "there is nothing in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_15::
    .string "As he came forth of his mother’s\n"
    .string "womb, naked shall he return to go as\l"
    .string "he came, and shall take nothing of\l"
    .string "his labour, which he may carry away\l"
    .string "in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_16::
    .string "And this also is a sore evil, that\n"
    .string "in all points as he came, so shall\l"
    .string "he go: and what profit hath he that\l"
    .string "hath laboured for the wind?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_17::
    .string "All his days also he eateth in\n"
    .string "darkness, and he hath much sorrow and\l"
    .string "wrath with his sickness$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_18::
    .string "Behold that which I have seen: it is\n"
    .string "good and comely for one to eat and to\l"
    .string "drink, and to enjoy the good of all\l"
    .string "his labour that he taketh under the\l"
    .string "sun all the days of his life, which\l"
    .string "God giveth him: for it is his\l"
    .string "portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_19::
    .string "Every man also to whom God hath\n"
    .string "given riches and wealth, and hath\l"
    .string "given him power to eat thereof, and\l"
    .string "to take his portion, and to rejoice\l"
    .string "in his labour; this is the gift of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_5_20::
    .string "For he shall not much remember the\n"
    .string "days of his life; because God\l"
    .string "answereth him in the joy of his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_1::
    .string "There is an evil which I have seen\n"
    .string "under the sun, and it is common among\l"
    .string "men:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_2::
    .string "A man to whom God hath given riches,\n"
    .string "wealth, and honour, so that he\l"
    .string "wanteth nothing for his soul of all\l"
    .string "that he desireth, yet God giveth him\l"
    .string "not power to eat thereof, but a\l"
    .string "stranger eateth it: this is vanity,\l"
    .string "and it is an evil disease$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_3::
    .string "If a man beget an hundred children,\n"
    .string "and live many years, so that the days\l"
    .string "of his years be many, and his soul be\l"
    .string "not filled with good, and also that\l"
    .string "he have no burial; I say, that an\l"
    .string "untimely birth is better than he.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_4::
    .string "For he cometh in with vanity, and\n"
    .string "departeth in darkness, and his name\l"
    .string "shall be covered with darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_5::
    .string "Moreover he hath not seen the sun,\n"
    .string "nor known any thing: this hath more\l"
    .string "rest than the other.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_6::
    .string "Yea, though he live a thousand\n"
    .string "years twice told, yet hath he seen no\l"
    .string "good: do not all go to one place?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_7::
    .string "All the labour of man is for his\n"
    .string "mouth, and yet the appetite is not\l"
    .string "filled$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_8::
    .string "For what hath the wise more than the\n"
    .string "fool? what hath the poor, that\l"
    .string "knoweth to walk before the living?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_9::
    .string "Better is the sight of the eyes than\n"
    .string "the wandering of the desire: this is\l"
    .string "also vanity and vexation of spirit$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_10::
    .string "That which hath been is named\n"
    .string "already, and it is known that it is\l"
    .string "man: neither may he contend with him\l"
    .string "that is mightier than he.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_11::
    .string "Seeing there be many things that\n"
    .string "increase vanity, what is man the\l"
    .string "better?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_6_12::
    .string "For who knoweth what is good for man\n"
    .string "in this life, all the days of his\l"
    .string "vain life which he spendeth as a\l"
    .string "shadow? for who can tell a man what\l"
    .string "shall be after him under the sun?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_1::
    .string "A good name is better than precious\n"
    .string "ointment; and the day of death than\l"
    .string "the day of one’s birth$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_2::
    .string "It is better to go to the house of\n"
    .string "mourning, than to go to the house of\l"
    .string "feasting: for that is the end of all\l"
    .string "men; and the living will lay it to\l"
    .string "his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_3::
    .string "Sorrow is better than laughter: for\n"
    .string "by the sadness of the countenance the\l"
    .string "heart is made better.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_4::
    .string "The heart of the wise is in the\n"
    .string "house of mourning; but the heart of\l"
    .string "fools is in the house of mirth.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_5::
    .string "It is better to hear the rebuke of\n"
    .string "the wise, than for a man to hear the\l"
    .string "song of fools.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_6::
    .string "For as the crackling of thorns\n"
    .string "under a pot, so is the laughter of\l"
    .string "the fool: this also is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_7::
    .string "Surely oppression maketh a wise\n"
    .string "man mad; and a gift destroyeth the\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_8::
    .string "Better is the end of a thing than\n"
    .string "the beginning thereof: and the\l"
    .string "patient in spirit is better than the\l"
    .string "proud in spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_9::
    .string "Be not hasty in thy spirit to be\n"
    .string "angry: for anger resteth in the bosom\l"
    .string "of fools.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_10::
    .string "Say not thou, What is the cause that\n"
    .string "the former days were better than\l"
    .string "these? for thou dost not enquire\l"
    .string "wisely concerning this.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_11::
    .string "Wisdom is good with an inheritance:\n"
    .string "and by it there is profit to them\l"
    .string "that see the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_12::
    .string "For wisdom is a defence, and money\n"
    .string "is a defence: but the excellency of\l"
    .string "knowledge is, that wisdom giveth\l"
    .string "life to them that have it.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_13::
    .string "Consider the work of God: for who\n"
    .string "can make that straight, which he hath\l"
    .string "made crooked?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_14::
    .string "In the day of prosperity be\n"
    .string "joyful, but in the day of adversity\l"
    .string "consider: God also hath set the one\l"
    .string "over against the other, to the end\l"
    .string "that man should find nothing after\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_15::
    .string "All things have I seen in the days\n"
    .string "of my vanity: there is a just man that\l"
    .string "perisheth in his righteousness, and\l"
    .string "there is a wicked man that\l"
    .string "prolongeth his life in his\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_16::
    .string "Be not righteous over much; neither\n"
    .string "make thyself over wise: why\l"
    .string "shouldest thou destroy thyself?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_17::
    .string "Be not over much wicked, neither be\n"
    .string "thou foolish: why shouldest thou\l"
    .string "die before thy time?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_18::
    .string "It is good that thou shouldest take\n"
    .string "hold of this; yea, also from this\l"
    .string "withdraw not thine hand: for he that\l"
    .string "feareth God shall come forth of\l"
    .string "them all$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_19::
    .string "Wisdom strengtheneth the wise more\n"
    .string "than ten mighty men which are in the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_20::
    .string "For there is not a just man upon\n"
    .string "earth, that doeth good, and sinneth\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_21::
    .string "Also take no heed unto all words\n"
    .string "that are spoken; lest thou hear thy\l"
    .string "servant curse thee:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_22::
    .string "For oftentimes also thine own heart\n"
    .string "knoweth that thou thyself likewise\l"
    .string "hast cursed others$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_23::
    .string "All this have I proved by wisdom:\n"
    .string "I said, I will be wise; but it was\l"
    .string "far from me.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_24::
    .string "That which is far off, and exceeding\n"
    .string "deep, who can find it out?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_25::
    .string "I applied mine heart to know, and\n"
    .string "to search, and to seek out wisdom,\l"
    .string "and the reason of things, and to know\l"
    .string "the wickedness of folly, even of\l"
    .string "foolishness and madness:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_26::
    .string "And I find more bitter than death\n"
    .string "the woman, whose heart is snares and\l"
    .string "nets, and her hands as bands: whoso\l"
    .string "pleaseth God shall escape from\l"
    .string "her; but the sinner shall be taken\l"
    .string "by her$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_27::
    .string "Behold, this have I found, saith\n"
    .string "the preacher, counting one by one,\l"
    .string "to find out the account:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_28::
    .string "Which yet my soul seeketh, but I\n"
    .string "find not: one man among a thousand\l"
    .string "have I found; but a woman among all\l"
    .string "those have I not found$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_7_29::
    .string "Lo, this only have I found, that God\n"
    .string "hath made man upright; but they have\l"
    .string "sought out many inventions.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_1::
    .string "Who is as the wise man? and who\n"
    .string "knoweth the interpretation of a\l"
    .string "thing? a man’s wisdom maketh his face\l"
    .string "to shine, and the boldness of his\l"
    .string "face shall be changed.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_2::
    .string "I counsel thee to keep the king’s\n"
    .string "commandment, and that in regard of\l"
    .string "the oath of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_3::
    .string "Be not hasty to go out of his sight:\n"
    .string "stand not in an evil thing; for he\l"
    .string "doeth whatsoever pleaseth him.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_4::
    .string "Where the word of a king is, there is\n"
    .string "power: and who may say unto him, What\l"
    .string "doest thou?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_5::
    .string "Whoso keepeth the commandment\n"
    .string "shall feel no evil thing: and a\l"
    .string "wise man’s heart discerneth both\l"
    .string "time and judgment$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_6::
    .string "Because to every purpose there is\n"
    .string "time and judgment, therefore the\l"
    .string "misery of man is great upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_7::
    .string "For he knoweth not that which\n"
    .string "shall be: for who can tell him when\l"
    .string "it shall be?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_8::
    .string "There is no man that hath power\n"
    .string "over the spirit to retain the\l"
    .string "spirit; neither hath he power in the\l"
    .string "day of death: and there is no\l"
    .string "discharge in that war; neither\l"
    .string "shall wickedness deliver those\l"
    .string "that are given to it$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_9::
    .string "All this have I seen, and applied\n"
    .string "my heart unto every work that is done\l"
    .string "under the sun: there is a time\l"
    .string "wherein one man ruleth over another\l"
    .string "to his own hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_10::
    .string "And so I saw the wicked buried, who\n"
    .string "had come and gone from the place of\l"
    .string "the holy, and they were forgotten in\l"
    .string "the city where they had so done: this\l"
    .string "is also vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_11::
    .string "Because sentence against an evil\n"
    .string "work is not executed speedily,\l"
    .string "therefore the heart of the sons of\l"
    .string "men is fully set in them to do evil.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_12::
    .string "Though a sinner do evil an hundred\n"
    .string "times, and his days be prolonged,\l"
    .string "yet surely I know that it shall be\l"
    .string "well with them that fear God, which\l"
    .string "fear before him:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_13::
    .string "But it shall not be well with the\n"
    .string "wicked, neither shall he prolong\l"
    .string "his days, which are as a shadow;\l"
    .string "because he feareth not before God$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_14::
    .string "There is a vanity which is done\n"
    .string "upon the earth; that there be just\l"
    .string "men, unto whom it happeneth\l"
    .string "according to the work of the wicked;\l"
    .string "again, there be wicked men, to whom\l"
    .string "it happeneth according to the work\l"
    .string "of the righteous: I said that this\l"
    .string "also is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_15::
    .string "Then I commended mirth, because a\n"
    .string "man hath no better thing under the\l"
    .string "sun, than to eat, and to drink, and to\l"
    .string "be merry: for that shall abide with\l"
    .string "him of his labour the days of his\l"
    .string "life, which God giveth him under the\l"
    .string "sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_16::
    .string "When I applied mine heart to know\n"
    .string "wisdom, and to see the business that\l"
    .string "is done upon the earth: (for also\l"
    .string "there is that neither day nor night\l"
    .string "seeth sleep with his eyes:)"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_8_17::
    .string "Then I beheld all the work of God,\n"
    .string "that a man cannot find out the work\l"
    .string "that is done under the sun: because\l"
    .string "though a man labour to seek it out,\l"
    .string "yet he shall not find it; yea\l"
    .string "farther; though a wise man think to\l"
    .string "know it, yet shall he not be able to\l"
    .string "find it$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_1::
    .string "For all this I considered in my\n"
    .string "heart even to declare all this,\l"
    .string "that the righteous, and the wise, and\l"
    .string "their works, are in the hand of God:\l"
    .string "no man knoweth either love or hatred\l"
    .string "by all that is before them.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_2::
    .string "All things come alike to all:\n"
    .string "there is one event to the righteous,\l"
    .string "and to the wicked; to the good and to\l"
    .string "the clean, and to the unclean; to\l"
    .string "him that sacrificeth, and to him that\l"
    .string "sacrificeth not: as is the good, so\l"
    .string "is the sinner; and he that sweareth,\l"
    .string "as he that feareth an oath.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_3::
    .string "This is an evil among all things\n"
    .string "that are done under the sun, that\l"
    .string "there is one event unto all: yea,\l"
    .string "also the heart of the sons of men is\l"
    .string "full of evil, and madness is in\l"
    .string "their heart while they live, and\l"
    .string "after that they go to the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_4::
    .string "For to him that is joined to all\n"
    .string "the living there is hope: for a\l"
    .string "living dog is better than a dead\l"
    .string "lion.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_5::
    .string "For the living know that they\n"
    .string "shall die: but the dead know not any\l"
    .string "thing, neither have they any more a\l"
    .string "reward; for the memory of them is\l"
    .string "forgotten.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_6::
    .string "Also their love, and their hatred,\n"
    .string "and their envy, is now perished;\l"
    .string "neither have they any more a portion\l"
    .string "for ever in any thing that is done\l"
    .string "under the sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_7::
    .string "Go thy way, eat thy bread with joy,\n"
    .string "and drink thy wine with a merry\l"
    .string "heart; for God now accepteth thy\l"
    .string "works.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_8::
    .string "Let thy garments be always white;\n"
    .string "and let thy head lack no ointment.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_9::
    .string "Live joyfully with the wife whom\n"
    .string "thou lovest all the days of the\l"
    .string "life of thy vanity, which he hath\l"
    .string "given thee under the sun, all the\l"
    .string "days of thy vanity: for that is thy\l"
    .string "portion in this life, and in thy\l"
    .string "labour which thou takest under the\l"
    .string "sun.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_10::
    .string "Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do,\n"
    .string "do it with thy might; for there is no\l"
    .string "work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor\l"
    .string "wisdom, in the grave, whither thou\l"
    .string "goest.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_11::
    .string "I returned, and saw under the sun,\n"
    .string "that the race is not to the swift, nor\l"
    .string "the battle to the strong, neither\l"
    .string "yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches\l"
    .string "to men of understanding, nor yet\l"
    .string "favour to men of skill; but time and\l"
    .string "chance happeneth to them all.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_12::
    .string "For man also knoweth not his time:\n"
    .string "as the fishes that are taken in an\l"
    .string "evil net, and as the birds that are\l"
    .string "caught in the snare; so are the sons\l"
    .string "of men snared in an evil time, when\l"
    .string "it falleth suddenly upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_13::
    .string "This wisdom have I seen also under\n"
    .string "the sun, and it seemed great unto me:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_14::
    .string "There was a little city, and few\n"
    .string "men within it; and there came a great\l"
    .string "king against it, and besieged it, and\l"
    .string "built great bulwarks against it:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_15::
    .string "Now there was found in it a poor\n"
    .string "wise man, and he by his wisdom\l"
    .string "delivered the city; yet no man\l"
    .string "remembered that same poor man$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_16::
    .string "Then said I, Wisdom is better than\n"
    .string "strength: nevertheless the poor\l"
    .string "man’s wisdom is despised, and his\l"
    .string "words are not heard.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_17::
    .string "The words of wise men are heard in\n"
    .string "quiet more than the cry of him that\l"
    .string "ruleth among fools.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_9_18::
    .string "Wisdom is better than weapons of\n"
    .string "war: but one sinner destroyeth much\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_1::
    .string "Dead flies cause the ointment of\n"
    .string "the apothecary to send forth a\l"
    .string "stinking savour: so doth a little\l"
    .string "folly him that is in reputation for\l"
    .string "wisdom and honour.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_2::
    .string "A wise man’s heart is at his right\n"
    .string "hand; but a fool’s heart at his left.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_3::
    .string "Yea also, when he that is a fool\n"
    .string "walketh by the way, his wisdom\l"
    .string "faileth him, and he saith to every\l"
    .string "one that he is a fool.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_4::
    .string "If the spirit of the ruler rise up\n"
    .string "against thee, leave not thy place;\l"
    .string "for yielding pacifieth great\l"
    .string "offences.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_5::
    .string "There is an evil which I have seen\n"
    .string "under the sun, as an error which\l"
    .string "proceedeth from the ruler:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_6::
    .string "Folly is set in great dignity, and\n"
    .string "the rich sit in low place$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_7::
    .string "I have seen servants upon horses,\n"
    .string "and princes walking as servants\l"
    .string "upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_8::
    .string "He that diggeth a pit shall fall\n"
    .string "into it; and whoso breaketh an hedge,\l"
    .string "a serpent shall bite him.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_9::
    .string "Whoso removeth stones shall be\n"
    .string "hurt therewith; and he that cleaveth\l"
    .string "wood shall be endangered thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_10::
    .string "If the iron be blunt, and he do not\n"
    .string "whet the edge, then must he put to\l"
    .string "more strength: but wisdom is\l"
    .string "profitable to direct.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_11::
    .string "Surely the serpent will bite\n"
    .string "without enchantment; and a babbler\l"
    .string "is no better.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_12::
    .string "The words of a wise man’s mouth are\n"
    .string "gracious; but the lips of a fool\l"
    .string "will swallow up himself.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_13::
    .string "The beginning of the words of his\n"
    .string "mouth is foolishness: and the end of\l"
    .string "his talk is mischievous madness.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_14::
    .string "A fool also is full of words: a\n"
    .string "man cannot tell what shall be; and\l"
    .string "what shall be after him, who can\l"
    .string "tell him?"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_15::
    .string "The labour of the foolish wearieth\n"
    .string "every one of them, because he knoweth\l"
    .string "not how to go to the city$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_16::
    .string "Woe to thee, O land, when thy king\n"
    .string "is a child, and thy princes eat in\l"
    .string "the morning!"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_17::
    .string "Blessed art thou, O land, when thy\n"
    .string "king is the son of nobles, and thy\l"
    .string "princes eat in due season, for\l"
    .string "strength, and not for drunkenness!"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_18::
    .string "By much slothfulness the building\n"
    .string "decayeth; and through idleness of\l"
    .string "the hands the house droppeth through$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_19::
    .string "A feast is made for laughter, and\n"
    .string "wine maketh merry: but money\l"
    .string "answereth all things.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_10_20::
    .string "Curse not the king, no not in thy\n"
    .string "thought; and curse not the rich in\l"
    .string "thy bedchamber: for a bird of the air\l"
    .string "shall carry the voice, and that\l"
    .string "which hath wings shall tell the\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_1::
    .string "Cast thy bread upon the waters: for\n"
    .string "thou shalt find it after many days.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_2::
    .string "Give a portion to seven, and also\n"
    .string "to eight; for thou knowest not what\l"
    .string "evil shall be upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_3::
    .string "If the clouds be full of rain,\n"
    .string "they empty themselves upon the\l"
    .string "earth: and if the tree fall toward\l"
    .string "the south, or toward the north, in\l"
    .string "the place where the tree falleth,\l"
    .string "there it shall be.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_4::
    .string "He that observeth the wind shall\n"
    .string "not sow; and he that regardeth the\l"
    .string "clouds shall not reap.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_5::
    .string "As thou knowest not what is the way\n"
    .string "of the spirit, nor how the bones do\l"
    .string "grow in the womb of her that is with\l"
    .string "child: even so thou knowest not the\l"
    .string "works of God who maketh all.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_6::
    .string "In the morning sow thy seed, and in\n"
    .string "the evening withhold not thine hand:\l"
    .string "for thou knowest not whether shall\l"
    .string "prosper, either this or that, or\l"
    .string "whether they both shall be alike\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_7::
    .string "Truly the light is sweet, and a\n"
    .string "pleasant thing it is for the eyes to\l"
    .string "behold the sun:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_8::
    .string "But if a man live many years, and\n"
    .string "rejoice in them all; yet let him\l"
    .string "remember the days of darkness; for\l"
    .string "they shall be many. All that\l"
    .string "cometh is vanity$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_9::
    .string "Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth;\n"
    .string "and let thy heart cheer thee in the\l"
    .string "days of thy youth, and walk in the\l"
    .string "ways of thine heart, and in the sight\l"
    .string "of thine eyes: but know thou, that\l"
    .string "for all these things God will\l"
    .string "bring thee into judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_11_10::
    .string "Therefore remove sorrow from thy\n"
    .string "heart, and put away evil from thy\l"
    .string "flesh: for childhood and youth are\l"
    .string "vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_1::
    .string "Remember now thy Creator in the days\n"
    .string "of thy youth, while the evil days\l"
    .string "come not, nor the years draw nigh,\l"
    .string "when thou shalt say, I have no\l"
    .string "pleasure in them;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_2::
    .string "While the sun, or the light, or the\n"
    .string "moon, or the stars, be not darkened,\l"
    .string "nor the clouds return after the\l"
    .string "rain:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_3::
    .string "In the day when the keepers of the\n"
    .string "house shall tremble, and the strong\l"
    .string "men shall bow themselves, and the\l"
    .string "grinders cease because they are few,\l"
    .string "and those that look out of the\l"
    .string "windows be darkened,"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_4::
    .string "And the doors shall be shut in the\n"
    .string "streets, when the sound of the\l"
    .string "grinding is low, and he shall rise\l"
    .string "up at the voice of the bird, and all\l"
    .string "the daughters of musick shall be\l"
    .string "brought low;"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_5::
    .string "Also when they shall be afraid of\n"
    .string "that which is high, and fears shall\l"
    .string "be in the way, and the almond tree\l"
    .string "shall flourish, and the\l"
    .string "grasshopper shall be a burden, and\l"
    .string "desire shall fail: because man\l"
    .string "goeth to his long home, and the\l"
    .string "mourners go about the streets:"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_6::
    .string "Or ever the silver cord be loosed,\n"
    .string "or the golden bowl be broken, or the\l"
    .string "pitcher be broken at the fountain, or\l"
    .string "the wheel broken at the cistern$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_7::
    .string "Then shall the dust return to the\n"
    .string "earth as it was: and the spirit\l"
    .string "shall return unto God who gave it.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_8::
    .string "Vanity of vanities, saith the\n"
    .string "preacher; all is vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_9::
    .string "And moreover, because the preacher\n"
    .string "was wise, he still taught the\l"
    .string "people knowledge; yea, he gave good\l"
    .string "heed, and sought out, and set in\l"
    .string "order many proverbs.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_10::
    .string "The preacher sought to find out\n"
    .string "acceptable words: and that which\l"
    .string "was written was upright, even words\l"
    .string "of truth.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_11::
    .string "The words of the wise are as goads,\n"
    .string "and as nails fastened by the masters\l"
    .string "of assemblies, which are given from\l"
    .string "one shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_12::
    .string "And further, by these, my son, be\n"
    .string "admonished: of making many books\l"
    .string "there is no end; and much study is a\l"
    .string "weariness of the flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_13::
    .string "Let us hear the conclusion of the\n"
    .string "whole matter: Fear God, and keep his\l"
    .string "commandments: for this is the whole\l"
    .string "duty of man.$"
Bible_Text_Ecclesiastes_12_14::
    .string "For God shall bring every work\n"
    .string "into judgment, with every secret\l"
    .string "thing, whether it be good, or whether\l"
    .string "it be evil.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_1::
    .string "The song of songs, which is\n"
    .string "Solomon’s.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_2::
    .string "Let him kiss me with the kisses of\n"
    .string "his mouth: for thy love is better\l"
    .string "than wine.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_3::
    .string "Because of the savour of thy good\n"
    .string "ointments thy name is as ointment\l"
    .string "poured forth, therefore do the\l"
    .string "virgins love thee.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_4::
    .string "Draw me, we will run after thee:\n"
    .string "the king hath brought me into his\l"
    .string "chambers: we will be glad and\l"
    .string "rejoice in thee, we will remember\l"
    .string "thy love more than wine: the upright\l"
    .string "love thee.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_5::
    .string "I am black, but comely, O ye\n"
    .string "daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents\l"
    .string "of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_6::
    .string "Look not upon me, because I am\n"
    .string "black, because the sun hath looked\l"
    .string "upon me: my mother’s children were\l"
    .string "angry with me; they made me the\l"
    .string "keeper of the vineyards; but mine\l"
    .string "own vineyard have I not kept.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_7::
    .string "Tell me, O thou whom my soul\n"
    .string "loveth, where thou feedest, where\l"
    .string "thou makest thy flock to rest at\l"
    .string "noon: for why should I be as one that\l"
    .string "turneth aside by the flocks of thy\l"
    .string "companions?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_8::
    .string "If thou know not, O thou fairest\n"
    .string "among women, go thy way forth by the\l"
    .string "footsteps of the flock, and feed thy\l"
    .string "kids beside the shepherds’ tents$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_9::
    .string "I have compared thee, O my love, to\n"
    .string "a company of horses in Pharaoh’s\l"
    .string "chariots.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_10::
    .string "Thy cheeks are comely with rows of\n"
    .string "jewels, thy neck with chains of\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_11::
    .string "We will make thee borders of gold\n"
    .string "with studs of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_12::
    .string "While the king sitteth at his\n"
    .string "table, my spikenard sendeth forth\l"
    .string "the smell thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_13::
    .string "A bundle of myrrh is my\n"
    .string "well-beloved unto me; he shall\l"
    .string "lie all night betwixt my breasts.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_14::
    .string "My beloved is unto me as a cluster\n"
    .string "of camphire in the vineyards of\l"
    .string "Engedi.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_15::
    .string "Behold, thou art fair, my love;\n"
    .string "behold, thou art fair; thou hast\l"
    .string "doves’ eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_16::
    .string "Behold, thou art fair, my beloved,\n"
    .string "yea, pleasant: also our bed is\l"
    .string "green.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_1_17::
    .string "The beams of our house are cedar,\n"
    .string "and our rafters of fir.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_1::
    .string "I am the rose of Sharon, and the\n"
    .string "lily of the valleys.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_2::
    .string "As the lily among thorns, so is my\n"
    .string "love among the daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_3::
    .string "As the apple tree among the trees\n"
    .string "of the wood, so is my beloved among\l"
    .string "the sons. I sat down under his shadow\l"
    .string "with great delight, and his fruit\l"
    .string "was sweet to my taste.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_4::
    .string "He brought me to the banqueting\n"
    .string "house, and his banner over me was\l"
    .string "love.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_5::
    .string "Stay me with flagons, comfort me\n"
    .string "with apples: for I am sick of love.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_6::
    .string "His left hand is under my head, and\n"
    .string "his right hand doth embrace me.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_7::
    .string "I charge you, O ye daughters of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the\l"
    .string "hinds of the field, that ye stir not\l"
    .string "up, nor awake my love, till he\l"
    .string "please.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_8::
    .string "The voice of my beloved! behold, he\n"
    .string "cometh leaping upon the mountains,\l"
    .string "skipping upon the hills.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_9::
    .string "My beloved is like a roe or a young\n"
    .string "hart: behold, he standeth behind our\l"
    .string "wall, he looketh forth at the\l"
    .string "windows, shewing himself through the\l"
    .string "lattice.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_10::
    .string "My beloved spake, and said unto me,\n"
    .string "Rise up, my love, my fair one, and\l"
    .string "come away.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_11::
    .string "For, lo, the winter is past, the\n"
    .string "rain is over and gone;"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_12::
    .string "The flowers appear on the earth;\n"
    .string "the time of the singing of birds is\l"
    .string "come, and the voice of the turtle is\l"
    .string "heard in our land;"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_13::
    .string "The fig tree putteth forth her\n"
    .string "green figs, and the vines with the\l"
    .string "tender grape give a good smell.\l"
    .string "Arise, my love, my fair one, and come\l"
    .string "away$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_14::
    .string "O my dove, that art in the clefts of\n"
    .string "the rock, in the secret places of\l"
    .string "the stairs, let me see thy\l"
    .string "countenance, let me hear thy voice;\l"
    .string "for sweet is thy voice, and thy\l"
    .string "countenance is comely.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_15::
    .string "Take us the foxes, the little\n"
    .string "foxes, that spoil the vines: for our\l"
    .string "vines have tender grapes.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_16::
    .string "My beloved is mine, and I am his: he\n"
    .string "feedeth among the lilies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_2_17::
    .string "Until the day break, and the\n"
    .string "shadows flee away, turn, my beloved,\l"
    .string "and be thou like a roe or a young\l"
    .string "hart upon the mountains of Bether.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_1::
    .string "By night on my bed I sought him whom\n"
    .string "my soul loveth: I sought him, but I\l"
    .string "found him not.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_2::
    .string "I will rise now, and go about the\n"
    .string "city in the streets, and in the broad\l"
    .string "ways I will seek him whom my soul\l"
    .string "loveth: I sought him, but I found him\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_3::
    .string "The watchmen that go about the city\n"
    .string "found me: to whom I said, Saw ye him\l"
    .string "whom my soul loveth?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_4::
    .string "It was but a little that I passed\n"
    .string "from them, but I found him whom my\l"
    .string "soul loveth: I held him, and would\l"
    .string "not let him go, until I had brought\l"
    .string "him into my mother’s house, and into\l"
    .string "the chamber of her that conceived me$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_5::
    .string "I charge you, O ye daughters of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the\l"
    .string "hinds of the field, that ye stir not\l"
    .string "up, nor awake my love, till he\l"
    .string "please.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_6::
    .string "Who is this that cometh out of the\n"
    .string "wilderness like pillars of smoke,\l"
    .string "perfumed with myrrh and\l"
    .string "frankincense, with all powders of\l"
    .string "the merchant?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_7::
    .string "Behold his bed, which is\n"
    .string "Solomon’s; threescore valiant men\l"
    .string "are about it, of the valiant of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_8::
    .string "They all hold swords, being\n"
    .string "expert in war: every man hath his\l"
    .string "sword upon his thigh because of fear\l"
    .string "in the night.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_9::
    .string "King Solomon made himself a\n"
    .string "chariot of the wood of Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_10::
    .string "He made the pillars thereof of\n"
    .string "silver, the bottom thereof of gold,\l"
    .string "the covering of it of purple, the\l"
    .string "midst thereof being paved with\l"
    .string "love, for the daughters of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_3_11::
    .string "Go forth, O ye daughters of Zion,\n"
    .string "and behold king Solomon with the\l"
    .string "crown wherewith his mother crowned\l"
    .string "him in the day of his espousals, and\l"
    .string "in the day of the gladness of his\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_1::
    .string "Behold, thou art fair, my love;\n"
    .string "behold, thou art fair; thou hast\l"
    .string "doves’ eyes within thy locks: thy\l"
    .string "hair is as a flock of goats, that\l"
    .string "appear from mount Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_2::
    .string "Thy teeth are like a flock of\n"
    .string "sheep that are even shorn, which\l"
    .string "came up from the washing; whereof\l"
    .string "every one bear twins, and none is\l"
    .string "barren among them.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_3::
    .string "Thy lips are like a thread of\n"
    .string "scarlet, and thy speech is comely:\l"
    .string "thy temples are like a piece of a\l"
    .string "pomegranate within thy locks.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_4::
    .string "Thy neck is like the tower of David\n"
    .string "builded for an armoury, whereon\l"
    .string "there hang a thousand bucklers, all\l"
    .string "shields of mighty men.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_5::
    .string "Thy two breasts are like two young\n"
    .string "roes that are twins, which feed among\l"
    .string "the lilies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_6::
    .string "Until the day break, and the\n"
    .string "shadows flee away, I will get me to\l"
    .string "the mountain of myrrh, and to the\l"
    .string "hill of frankincense.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_7::
    .string "Thou art all fair, my love; there\n"
    .string "is no spot in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_8::
    .string "Come with me from Lebanon, my\n"
    .string "spouse, with me from Lebanon: look\l"
    .string "from the top of Amana, from the top\l"
    .string "of Shenir and Hermon, from the\l"
    .string "lions’ dens, from the mountains of\l"
    .string "the leopards.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_9::
    .string "Thou hast ravished my heart, my\n"
    .string "sister, my spouse; thou hast\l"
    .string "ravished my heart with one of thine\l"
    .string "eyes, with one chain of thy neck.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_10::
    .string "How fair is thy love, my sister, my\n"
    .string "spouse! how much better is thy love\l"
    .string "than wine! and the smell of thine\l"
    .string "ointments than all spices!"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_11::
    .string "Thy lips, O my spouse, drop as the\n"
    .string "honeycomb: honey and milk are under\l"
    .string "thy tongue; and the smell of thy\l"
    .string "garments is like the smell of\l"
    .string "Lebanon$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_12::
    .string "A garden inclosed is my sister, my\n"
    .string "spouse; a spring shut up, a\l"
    .string "fountain sealed.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_13::
    .string "Thy plants are an orchard of\n"
    .string "pomegranates, with pleasant fruits;\l"
    .string "camphire, with spikenard,"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_14::
    .string "Spikenard and saffron; calamus and\n"
    .string "cinnamon, with all trees of\l"
    .string "frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with\l"
    .string "all the chief spices:"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_15::
    .string "A fountain of gardens, a well of\n"
    .string "living waters, and streams from\l"
    .string "Lebanon$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_4_16::
    .string "Awake, O north wind; and come, thou\n"
    .string "south; blow upon my garden, that the\l"
    .string "spices thereof may flow out. Let my\l"
    .string "beloved come into his garden, and\l"
    .string "eat his pleasant fruits.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_1::
    .string "I am come into my garden, my sister,\n"
    .string "my spouse: I have gathered my myrrh\l"
    .string "with my spice; I have eaten my\l"
    .string "honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk\l"
    .string "my wine with my milk: eat, O friends;\l"
    .string "drink, yea, drink abundantly, O\l"
    .string "beloved.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_2::
    .string "I sleep, but my heart waketh: it is\n"
    .string "the voice of my beloved that\l"
    .string "knocketh, saying, Open to me, my\l"
    .string "sister, my love, my dove, my\l"
    .string "undefiled: for my head is filled\l"
    .string "with dew, and my locks with the\l"
    .string "drops of the night.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_3::
    .string "I have put off my coat; how shall I\n"
    .string "put it on? I have washed my feet; how\l"
    .string "shall I defile them?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_4::
    .string "My beloved put in his hand by the\n"
    .string "hole of the door, and my bowels were\l"
    .string "moved for him$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_5::
    .string "I rose up to open to my beloved;\n"
    .string "and my hands dropped with myrrh, and\l"
    .string "my fingers with sweet smelling\l"
    .string "myrrh, upon the handles of the lock.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_6::
    .string "I opened to my beloved; but my\n"
    .string "beloved had withdrawn himself, and\l"
    .string "was gone: my soul failed when he\l"
    .string "spake: I sought him, but I could not\l"
    .string "find him; I called him, but he gave\l"
    .string "me no answer.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_7::
    .string "The watchmen that went about the\n"
    .string "city found me, they smote me, they\l"
    .string "wounded me; the keepers of the\l"
    .string "walls took away my veil from me.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_8::
    .string "I charge you, O daughters of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved,\l"
    .string "that ye tell him, that I am sick of\l"
    .string "love.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_9::
    .string "What is thy beloved more than\n"
    .string "another beloved, O thou fairest\l"
    .string "among women? what is thy beloved\l"
    .string "more than another beloved, that thou\l"
    .string "dost so charge us?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_10::
    .string "My beloved is white and ruddy, the\n"
    .string "chiefest among ten thousand$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_11::
    .string "His head is as the most fine gold,\n"
    .string "his locks are bushy, and black as a\l"
    .string "raven.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_12::
    .string "His eyes are as the eyes of doves by\n"
    .string "the rivers of waters, washed with\l"
    .string "milk, and fitly set.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_13::
    .string "His cheeks are as a bed of spices,\n"
    .string "as sweet flowers: his lips like\l"
    .string "lilies, dropping sweet smelling\l"
    .string "myrrh.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_14::
    .string "His hands are as gold rings set\n"
    .string "with the beryl: his belly is as\l"
    .string "bright ivory overlaid with\l"
    .string "sapphires.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_15::
    .string "His legs are as pillars of\n"
    .string "marble, set upon sockets of fine\l"
    .string "gold: his countenance is as Lebanon,\l"
    .string "excellent as the cedars.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_5_16::
    .string "His mouth is most sweet: yea, he is\n"
    .string "altogether lovely. This is my\l"
    .string "beloved, and this is my friend, O\l"
    .string "daughters of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_1::
    .string "Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou\n"
    .string "fairest among women? whither is thy\l"
    .string "beloved turned aside? that we may\l"
    .string "seek him with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_2::
    .string "My beloved is gone down into his\n"
    .string "garden, to the beds of spices, to\l"
    .string "feed in the gardens, and to gather\l"
    .string "lilies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_3::
    .string "I am my beloved’s, and my beloved\n"
    .string "is mine: he feedeth among the\l"
    .string "lilies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_4::
    .string "Thou art beautiful, O my love, as\n"
    .string "Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "terrible as an army with banners.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_5::
    .string "Turn away thine eyes from me, for\n"
    .string "they have overcome me: thy hair is as\l"
    .string "a flock of goats that appear from\l"
    .string "Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_6::
    .string "Thy teeth are as a flock of sheep\n"
    .string "which go up from the washing,\l"
    .string "whereof every one beareth twins, and\l"
    .string "there is not one barren among them.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_7::
    .string "As a piece of a pomegranate are thy\n"
    .string "temples within thy locks.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_8::
    .string "There are threescore queens, and\n"
    .string "fourscore concubines, and virgins\l"
    .string "without number.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_9::
    .string "My dove, my undefiled is but one;\n"
    .string "she is the only one of her mother,\l"
    .string "she is the choice one of her that\l"
    .string "bare her. The daughters saw her, and\l"
    .string "blessed her; yea, the queens and the\l"
    .string "concubines, and they praised her.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_10::
    .string "Who is she that looketh forth as\n"
    .string "the morning, fair as the moon, clear\l"
    .string "as the sun, and terrible as an army\l"
    .string "with banners?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_11::
    .string "I went down into the garden of nuts\n"
    .string "to see the fruits of the valley, and\l"
    .string "to see whether the vine flourished\l"
    .string "and the pomegranates budded$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_12::
    .string "Or ever I was aware, my soul made me\n"
    .string "like the chariots of Amminadib.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_6_13::
    .string "Return, return, O Shulamite;\n"
    .string "return, return, that we may look\l"
    .string "upon thee. What will ye see in the\l"
    .string "Shulamite? As it were the company of\l"
    .string "two armies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_1::
    .string "How beautiful are thy feet with\n"
    .string "shoes, O prince’s daughter! the\l"
    .string "joints of thy thighs are like\l"
    .string "jewels, the work of the hands of a\l"
    .string "cunning workman.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_2::
    .string "Thy navel is like a round goblet,\n"
    .string "which wanteth not liquor: thy belly\l"
    .string "is like an heap of wheat set about\l"
    .string "with lilies.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_3::
    .string "Thy two breasts are like two young\n"
    .string "roes that are twins.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_4::
    .string "Thy neck is as a tower of ivory;\n"
    .string "thine eyes like the fishpools in\l"
    .string "Heshbon, by the gate of Bathrabbim:\l"
    .string "thy nose is as the tower of Lebanon\l"
    .string "which looketh toward Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_5::
    .string "Thine head upon thee is like\n"
    .string "Carmel, and the hair of thine head\l"
    .string "like purple; the king is held in\l"
    .string "the galleries.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_6::
    .string "How fair and how pleasant art thou,\n"
    .string "O love, for delights!"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_7::
    .string "This thy stature is like to a palm\n"
    .string "tree, and thy breasts to clusters of\l"
    .string "grapes$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_8::
    .string "I said, I will go up to the palm\n"
    .string "tree, I will take hold of the\l"
    .string "boughs thereof: now also thy breasts\l"
    .string "shall be as clusters of the vine,\l"
    .string "and the smell of thy nose like\l"
    .string "apples;"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_9::
    .string "And the roof of thy mouth like the\n"
    .string "best wine for my beloved, that goeth\l"
    .string "down sweetly, causing the lips of\l"
    .string "those that are asleep to speak$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_10::
    .string "I am my beloved’s, and his desire is\n"
    .string "toward me.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_11::
    .string "Come, my beloved, let us go forth\n"
    .string "into the field; let us lodge in the\l"
    .string "villages.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_12::
    .string "Let us get up early to the\n"
    .string "vineyards; let us see if the vine\l"
    .string "flourish, whether the tender grape\l"
    .string "appear, and the pomegranates bud\l"
    .string "forth: there will I give thee my\l"
    .string "loves.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_7_13::
    .string "The mandrakes give a smell, and at\n"
    .string "our gates are all manner of\l"
    .string "pleasant fruits, new and old, which\l"
    .string "I have laid up for thee, O my\l"
    .string "beloved.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_1::
    .string "O that thou wert as my brother, that\n"
    .string "sucked the breasts of my mother! when\l"
    .string "I should find thee without, I would\l"
    .string "kiss thee; yea, I should not be\l"
    .string "despised.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_2::
    .string "I would lead thee, and bring thee\n"
    .string "into my mother’s house, who would\l"
    .string "instruct me: I would cause thee to\l"
    .string "drink of spiced wine of the juice of\l"
    .string "my pomegranate.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_3::
    .string "His left hand should be under my\n"
    .string "head, and his right hand should\l"
    .string "embrace me.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_4::
    .string "I charge you, O daughters of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, that ye stir not up, nor\l"
    .string "awake my love, until he please.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_5::
    .string "Who is this that cometh up from the\n"
    .string "wilderness, leaning upon her\l"
    .string "beloved? I raised thee up under the\l"
    .string "apple tree: there thy mother\l"
    .string "brought thee forth: there she brought\l"
    .string "thee forth that bare thee.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_6::
    .string "Set me as a seal upon thine heart,\n"
    .string "as a seal upon thine arm: for love\l"
    .string "is strong as death; jealousy is\l"
    .string "cruel as the grave: the coals\l"
    .string "thereof are coals of fire, which\l"
    .string "hath a most vehement flame.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_7::
    .string "Many waters cannot quench love,\n"
    .string "neither can the floods drown it: if a\l"
    .string "man would give all the substance of\l"
    .string "his house for love, it would\l"
    .string "utterly be contemned.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_8::
    .string "We have a little sister, and she\n"
    .string "hath no breasts: what shall we do\l"
    .string "for our sister in the day when she\l"
    .string "shall be spoken for?"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_9::
    .string "If she be a wall, we will build\n"
    .string "upon her a palace of silver: and if\l"
    .string "she be a door, we will inclose her\l"
    .string "with boards of cedar$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_10::
    .string "I am a wall, and my breasts like\n"
    .string "towers: then was I in his eyes as one\l"
    .string "that found favour.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_11::
    .string "Solomon had a vineyard at\n"
    .string "Baalhamon; he let out the vineyard\l"
    .string "unto keepers; every one for the\l"
    .string "fruit thereof was to bring a thousand\l"
    .string "pieces of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_12::
    .string "My vineyard, which is mine, is\n"
    .string "before me: thou, O Solomon, must have\l"
    .string "a thousand, and those that keep the\l"
    .string "fruit thereof two hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_13::
    .string "Thou that dwellest in the gardens,\n"
    .string "the companions hearken to thy voice:\l"
    .string "cause me to hear it.$"
Bible_Text_Song_of_Solomon_8_14::
    .string "Make haste, my beloved, and be thou\n"
    .string "like to a roe or to a young hart upon\l"
    .string "the mountains of spices.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_1::
    .string "The vision of Isaiah the son of\n"
    .string "Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah\l"
    .string "and Jerusalem in the days of Uzziah,\l"
    .string "Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_2::
    .string "Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O\n"
    .string "earth: for the LORD hath spoken, I\l"
    .string "have nourished and brought up\l"
    .string "children, and they have rebelled\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_3::
    .string "The ox knoweth his owner, and the\n"
    .string "ass his master’s crib: but Israel\l"
    .string "doth not know, my people doth not\l"
    .string "consider.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_4::
    .string "Ah sinful nation, a people laden\n"
    .string "with iniquity, a seed of evildoers,\l"
    .string "children that are corrupters: they\l"
    .string "have forsaken the LORD, they have\l"
    .string "provoked the Holy One of Israel\l"
    .string "unto anger, they are gone away\l"
    .string "backward.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_5::
    .string "Why should ye be stricken any more?\n"
    .string "ye will revolt more and more: the\l"
    .string "whole head is sick, and the whole\l"
    .string "heart faint.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_6::
    .string "From the sole of the foot even unto\n"
    .string "the head there is no soundness in it;\l"
    .string "but wounds, and bruises, and\l"
    .string "putrifying sores: they have not been\l"
    .string "closed, neither bound up, neither\l"
    .string "mollified with ointment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_7::
    .string "Your country is desolate, your\n"
    .string "cities are burned with fire: your\l"
    .string "land, strangers devour it in your\l"
    .string "presence, and it is desolate, as\l"
    .string "overthrown by strangers.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_8::
    .string "And the daughter of Zion is left as\n"
    .string "a cottage in a vineyard, as a lodge\l"
    .string "in a garden of cucumbers, as a\l"
    .string "besieged city.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_9::
    .string "Except the LORD of hosts had left\n"
    .string "unto us a very small remnant, we\l"
    .string "should have been as Sodom, and we\l"
    .string "should have been like unto Gomorrah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_10::
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD, ye rulers\n"
    .string "of Sodom; give ear unto the law of\l"
    .string "our God, ye people of Gomorrah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_11::
    .string "To what purpose is the multitude\n"
    .string "of your sacrifices unto me? saith the\l"
    .string "LORD: I am full of the burnt\l"
    .string "offerings of rams, and the fat of fed\l"
    .string "beasts; and I delight not in the\l"
    .string "blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or\l"
    .string "of he goats.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_12::
    .string "When ye come to appear before me,\n"
    .string "who hath required this at your hand,\l"
    .string "to tread my courts?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_13::
    .string "Bring no more vain oblations;\n"
    .string "incense is an abomination unto me;\l"
    .string "the new moons and sabbaths, the\l"
    .string "calling of assemblies, I cannot\l"
    .string "away with; it is iniquity, even the\l"
    .string "solemn meeting$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_14::
    .string "Your new moons and your appointed\n"
    .string "feasts my soul hateth: they are a\l"
    .string "trouble unto me; I am weary to bear\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_15::
    .string "And when ye spread forth your\n"
    .string "hands, I will hide mine eyes from\l"
    .string "you: yea, when ye make many prayers,\l"
    .string "I will not hear: your hands are\l"
    .string "full of blood.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_16::
    .string "Wash you, make you clean; put away\n"
    .string "the evil of your doings from before\l"
    .string "mine eyes; cease to do evil;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_17::
    .string "Learn to do well; seek judgment,\n"
    .string "relieve the oppressed, judge the\l"
    .string "fatherless, plead for the widow$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_18::
    .string "Come now, and let us reason\n"
    .string "together, saith the LORD: though your\l"
    .string "sins be as scarlet, they shall be\l"
    .string "as white as snow; though they be red\l"
    .string "like crimson, they shall be as wool.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_19::
    .string "If ye be willing and obedient, ye\n"
    .string "shall eat the good of the land:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_20::
    .string "But if ye refuse and rebel, ye\n"
    .string "shall be devoured with the sword:\l"
    .string "for the mouth of the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_21::
    .string "How is the faithful city become an\n"
    .string "harlot! it was full of judgment;\l"
    .string "righteousness lodged in it; but now\l"
    .string "murderers.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_22::
    .string "Thy silver is become dross, thy\n"
    .string "wine mixed with water:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_23::
    .string "Thy princes are rebellious, and\n"
    .string "companions of thieves: every one\l"
    .string "loveth gifts, and followeth after\l"
    .string "rewards: they judge not the\l"
    .string "fatherless, neither doth the cause\l"
    .string "of the widow come unto them$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_24::
    .string "Therefore saith the LORD, the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts, the mighty One of Israel,\l"
    .string "Ah, I will ease me of mine\l"
    .string "adversaries, and avenge me of mine\l"
    .string "enemies:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_25::
    .string "And I will turn my hand upon thee,\n"
    .string "and purely purge away thy dross,\l"
    .string "and take away all thy tin:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_26::
    .string "And I will restore thy judges as at\n"
    .string "the first, and thy counsellors as at\l"
    .string "the beginning: afterward thou shalt\l"
    .string "be called, The city of\l"
    .string "righteousness, the faithful city$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_27::
    .string "Zion shall be redeemed with\n"
    .string "judgment, and her converts with\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_28::
    .string "And the destruction of the\n"
    .string "transgressors and of the sinners\l"
    .string "shall be together, and they that\l"
    .string "forsake the LORD shall be consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_29::
    .string "For they shall be ashamed of the\n"
    .string "oaks which ye have desired, and ye\l"
    .string "shall be confounded for the gardens\l"
    .string "that ye have chosen.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_30::
    .string "For ye shall be as an oak whose\n"
    .string "leaf fadeth, and as a garden that\l"
    .string "hath no water.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_1_31::
    .string "And the strong shall be as tow, and\n"
    .string "the maker of it as a spark, and they\l"
    .string "shall both burn together, and none\l"
    .string "shall quench them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_1::
    .string "The word that Isaiah the son of Amoz\n"
    .string "saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_2::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "last days, that the mountain of the\l"
    .string "LORD’s house shall be established\l"
    .string "in the top of the mountains, and\l"
    .string "shall be exalted above the hills;\l"
    .string "and all nations shall flow unto\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_3::
    .string "And many people shall go and say,\n"
    .string "Come ye, and let us go up to the\l"
    .string "mountain of the LORD, to the house of\l"
    .string "the God of Jacob; and he will teach\l"
    .string "us of his ways, and we will walk in\l"
    .string "his paths: for out of Zion shall go\l"
    .string "forth the law, and the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD from Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_4::
    .string "And he shall judge among the\n"
    .string "nations, and shall rebuke many\l"
    .string "people: and they shall beat their\l"
    .string "swords into plowshares, and their\l"
    .string "spears into pruninghooks: nation\l"
    .string "shall not lift up sword against\l"
    .string "nation, neither shall they learn\l"
    .string "war any more.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_5::
    .string "O house of Jacob, come ye, and let\n"
    .string "us walk in the light of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_6::
    .string "Therefore thou hast forsaken thy\n"
    .string "people the house of Jacob, because\l"
    .string "they be replenished from the east,\l"
    .string "and are soothsayers like the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and they please\l"
    .string "themselves in the children of\l"
    .string "strangers.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_7::
    .string "Their land also is full of\n"
    .string "silver and gold, neither is there\l"
    .string "any end of their treasures; their\l"
    .string "land is also full of horses,\l"
    .string "neither is there any end of their\l"
    .string "chariots:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_8::
    .string "Their land also is full of idols;\n"
    .string "they worship the work of their own\l"
    .string "hands, that which their own fingers\l"
    .string "have made:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_9::
    .string "And the mean man boweth down, and\n"
    .string "the great man humbleth himself:\l"
    .string "therefore forgive them not$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_10::
    .string "Enter into the rock, and hide thee\n"
    .string "in the dust, for fear of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "for the glory of his majesty.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_11::
    .string "The lofty looks of man shall be\n"
    .string "humbled, and the haughtiness of men\l"
    .string "shall be bowed down, and the LORD\l"
    .string "alone shall be exalted in that day.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_12::
    .string "For the day of the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "shall be upon every one that is\l"
    .string "proud and lofty, and upon every one\l"
    .string "that is lifted up; and he shall be\l"
    .string "brought low:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_13::
    .string "And upon all the cedars of\n"
    .string "Lebanon, that are high and lifted\l"
    .string "up, and upon all the oaks of\l"
    .string "Bashan,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_14::
    .string "And upon all the high mountains,\n"
    .string "and upon all the hills that are\l"
    .string "lifted up,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_15::
    .string "And upon every high tower, and upon\n"
    .string "every fenced wall,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_16::
    .string "And upon all the ships of\n"
    .string "Tarshish, and upon all pleasant\l"
    .string "pictures$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_17::
    .string "And the loftiness of man shall be\n"
    .string "bowed down, and the haughtiness of\l"
    .string "men shall be made low: and the LORD\l"
    .string "alone shall be exalted in that day.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_18::
    .string "And the idols he shall utterly\n"
    .string "abolish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_19::
    .string "And they shall go into the holes\n"
    .string "of the rocks, and into the caves of\l"
    .string "the earth, for fear of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "for the glory of his majesty, when he\l"
    .string "ariseth to shake terribly the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_20::
    .string "In that day a man shall cast his\n"
    .string "idols of silver, and his idols of\l"
    .string "gold, which they made each one for\l"
    .string "himself to worship, to the moles\l"
    .string "and to the bats;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_21::
    .string "To go into the clefts of the rocks,\n"
    .string "and into the tops of the ragged\l"
    .string "rocks, for fear of the LORD, and for\l"
    .string "the glory of his majesty, when he\l"
    .string "ariseth to shake terribly the earth$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_2_22::
    .string "Cease ye from man, whose breath is\n"
    .string "in his nostrils: for wherein is he to\l"
    .string "be accounted of?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_1::
    .string "For, behold, the Lord, the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, doth take away from Jerusalem\l"
    .string "and from Judah the stay and the\l"
    .string "staff, the whole stay of bread, and\l"
    .string "the whole stay of water$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_2::
    .string "The mighty man, and the man of war,\n"
    .string "the judge, and the prophet, and the\l"
    .string "prudent, and the ancient,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_3::
    .string "The captain of fifty, and the\n"
    .string "honourable man, and the\l"
    .string "counsellor, and the cunning\l"
    .string "artificer, and the eloquent orator$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_4::
    .string "And I will give children to be\n"
    .string "their princes, and babes shall\l"
    .string "rule over them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_5::
    .string "And the people shall be\n"
    .string "oppressed, every one by another,\l"
    .string "and every one by his neighbour: the\l"
    .string "child shall behave himself\l"
    .string "proudly against the ancient, and the\l"
    .string "base against the honourable.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_6::
    .string "When a man shall take hold of his\n"
    .string "brother of the house of his father,\l"
    .string "saying, Thou hast clothing, be thou\l"
    .string "our ruler, and let this ruin be\l"
    .string "under thy hand:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_7::
    .string "In that day shall he swear, saying,\n"
    .string "I will not be an healer; for in my\l"
    .string "house is neither bread nor clothing:\l"
    .string "make me not a ruler of the people$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_8::
    .string "For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah\n"
    .string "is fallen: because their tongue and\l"
    .string "their doings are against the LORD, to\l"
    .string "provoke the eyes of his glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_9::
    .string "The shew of their countenance doth\n"
    .string "witness against them; and they\l"
    .string "declare their sin as Sodom, they\l"
    .string "hide it not. Woe unto their soul! for\l"
    .string "they have rewarded evil unto\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_10::
    .string "Say ye to the righteous, that it\n"
    .string "shall be well with him: for they\l"
    .string "shall eat the fruit of their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_11::
    .string "Woe unto the wicked! it shall be\n"
    .string "ill with him: for the reward of his\l"
    .string "hands shall be given him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_12::
    .string "As for my people, children are\n"
    .string "their oppressors, and women rule\l"
    .string "over them. O my people, they which\l"
    .string "lead thee cause thee to err, and\l"
    .string "destroy the way of thy paths.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_13::
    .string "The LORD standeth up to plead, and\n"
    .string "standeth to judge the people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_14::
    .string "The LORD will enter into judgment\n"
    .string "with the ancients of his people,\l"
    .string "and the princes thereof: for ye have\l"
    .string "eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of\l"
    .string "the poor is in your houses.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_15::
    .string "What mean ye that ye beat my\n"
    .string "people to pieces, and grind the\l"
    .string "faces of the poor? saith the Lord GOD\l"
    .string "of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_16::
    .string "Moreover the LORD saith, Because the\n"
    .string "daughters of Zion are haughty, and\l"
    .string "walk with stretched forth necks and\l"
    .string "wanton eyes, walking and mincing as\l"
    .string "they go, and making a tinkling with\l"
    .string "their feet:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_17::
    .string "Therefore the LORD will smite with\n"
    .string "a scab the crown of the head of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Zion, and the LORD will\l"
    .string "discover their secret parts$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_18::
    .string "In that day the Lord will take away\n"
    .string "the bravery of their tinkling\l"
    .string "ornaments about their feet, and their\l"
    .string "cauls, and their round tires like\l"
    .string "the moon,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_19::
    .string "The chains, and the bracelets, and\n"
    .string "the mufflers,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_20::
    .string "The bonnets, and the ornaments of\n"
    .string "the legs, and the headbands, and the\l"
    .string "tablets, and the earrings,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_21::
    .string "The rings, and nose jewels,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_22::
    .string "The changeable suits of apparel,\n"
    .string "and the mantles, and the wimples,\l"
    .string "and the crisping pins,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_23::
    .string "The glasses, and the fine linen,\n"
    .string "and the hoods, and the vails$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_24::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "instead of sweet smell there shall\l"
    .string "be stink; and instead of a girdle a\l"
    .string "rent; and instead of well set hair\l"
    .string "baldness; and instead of a stomacher\l"
    .string "a girding of sackcloth; and burning\l"
    .string "instead of beauty.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_25::
    .string "Thy men shall fall by the sword,\n"
    .string "and thy mighty in the war.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_3_26::
    .string "And her gates shall lament and\n"
    .string "mourn; and she being desolate shall\l"
    .string "sit upon the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_1::
    .string "And in that day seven women shall\n"
    .string "take hold of one man, saying, We\l"
    .string "will eat our own bread, and wear our\l"
    .string "own apparel: only let us be\l"
    .string "called by thy name, to take away our\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_2::
    .string "In that day shall the branch of the\n"
    .string "LORD be beautiful and glorious, and\l"
    .string "the fruit of the earth shall be\l"
    .string "excellent and comely for them that\l"
    .string "are escaped of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_3::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that he\n"
    .string "that is left in Zion, and he that\l"
    .string "remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be\l"
    .string "called holy, even every one that is\l"
    .string "written among the living in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_4::
    .string "When the Lord shall have washed\n"
    .string "away the filth of the daughters of\l"
    .string "Zion, and shall have purged the\l"
    .string "blood of Jerusalem from the midst\l"
    .string "thereof by the spirit of judgment,\l"
    .string "and by the spirit of burning$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_5::
    .string "And the LORD will create upon\n"
    .string "every dwelling place of mount\l"
    .string "Zion, and upon her assemblies, a\l"
    .string "cloud and smoke by day, and the\l"
    .string "shining of a flaming fire by night:\l"
    .string "for upon all the glory shall be a\l"
    .string "defence.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_4_6::
    .string "And there shall be a tabernacle\n"
    .string "for a shadow in the day time from the\l"
    .string "heat, and for a place of refuge, and\l"
    .string "for a covert from storm and from rain.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_1::
    .string "Now will I sing to my\n"
    .string "wellbeloved a song of my beloved\l"
    .string "touching his vineyard. My\l"
    .string "wellbeloved hath a vineyard in a\l"
    .string "very fruitful hill:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_2::
    .string "And he fenced it, and gathered out\n"
    .string "the stones thereof, and planted it\l"
    .string "with the choicest vine, and built a\l"
    .string "tower in the midst of it, and also\l"
    .string "made a winepress therein: and he\l"
    .string "looked that it should bring forth\l"
    .string "grapes, and it brought forth wild\l"
    .string "grapes$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_3::
    .string "And now, O inhabitants of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, and men of Judah, judge, I\l"
    .string "pray you, betwixt me and my vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_4::
    .string "What could have been done more to\n"
    .string "my vineyard, that I have not done in\l"
    .string "it? wherefore, when I looked that it\l"
    .string "should bring forth grapes, brought\l"
    .string "it forth wild grapes?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_5::
    .string "And now go to; I will tell you\n"
    .string "what I will do to my vineyard: I\l"
    .string "will take away the hedge thereof,\l"
    .string "and it shall be eaten up; and break\l"
    .string "down the wall thereof, and it\l"
    .string "shall be trodden down:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_6::
    .string "And I will lay it waste: it shall\n"
    .string "not be pruned, nor digged; but there\l"
    .string "shall come up briers and thorns: I\l"
    .string "will also command the clouds that\l"
    .string "they rain no rain upon it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_7::
    .string "For the vineyard of the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts is the house of Israel, and the\l"
    .string "men of Judah his pleasant plant:\l"
    .string "and he looked for judgment, but\l"
    .string "behold oppression; for\l"
    .string "righteousness, but behold a cry.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_8::
    .string "Woe unto them that join house to\n"
    .string "house, that lay field to field,\l"
    .string "till there be no place, that they\l"
    .string "may be placed alone in the midst of\l"
    .string "the earth!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_9::
    .string "In mine ears said the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "Of a truth many houses shall be\l"
    .string "desolate, even great and fair,\l"
    .string "without inhabitant$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_10::
    .string "Yea, ten acres of vineyard shall\n"
    .string "yield one bath, and the seed of an\l"
    .string "homer shall yield an ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_11::
    .string "Woe unto them that rise up early in\n"
    .string "the morning, that they may follow\l"
    .string "strong drink; that continue until\l"
    .string "night, till wine inflame them!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_12::
    .string "And the harp, and the viol, the\n"
    .string "tabret, and pipe, and wine, are in\l"
    .string "their feasts: but they regard not the\l"
    .string "work of the LORD, neither consider\l"
    .string "the operation of his hands$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_13::
    .string "Therefore my people are gone into\n"
    .string "captivity, because they have no\l"
    .string "knowledge: and their honourable men\l"
    .string "are famished, and their multitude\l"
    .string "dried up with thirst.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_14::
    .string "Therefore hell hath enlarged\n"
    .string "herself, and opened her mouth\l"
    .string "without measure: and their glory,\l"
    .string "and their multitude, and their\l"
    .string "pomp, and he that rejoiceth, shall\l"
    .string "descend into it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_15::
    .string "And the mean man shall be brought\n"
    .string "down, and the mighty man shall be\l"
    .string "humbled, and the eyes of the lofty\l"
    .string "shall be humbled:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_16::
    .string "But the LORD of hosts shall be\n"
    .string "exalted in judgment, and God that is\l"
    .string "holy shall be sanctified in\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_17::
    .string "Then shall the lambs feed after\n"
    .string "their manner, and the waste places\l"
    .string "of the fat ones shall strangers eat.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_18::
    .string "Woe unto them that draw iniquity\n"
    .string "with cords of vanity, and sin as it\l"
    .string "were with a cart rope:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_19::
    .string "That say, Let him make speed, and\n"
    .string "hasten his work, that we may see it:\l"
    .string "and let the counsel of the Holy One\l"
    .string "of Israel draw nigh and come, that we\l"
    .string "may know it!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_20::
    .string "Woe unto them that call evil good,\n"
    .string "and good evil; that put darkness for\l"
    .string "light, and light for darkness; that\l"
    .string "put bitter for sweet, and sweet for\l"
    .string "bitter!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_21::
    .string "Woe unto them that are wise in their\n"
    .string "own eyes, and prudent in their own\l"
    .string "sight!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_22::
    .string "Woe unto them that are mighty to\n"
    .string "drink wine, and men of strength to\l"
    .string "mingle strong drink:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_23::
    .string "Which justify the wicked for reward,\n"
    .string "and take away the righteousness of\l"
    .string "the righteous from him!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_24::
    .string "Therefore as the fire devoureth the\n"
    .string "stubble, and the flame consumeth\l"
    .string "the chaff, so their root shall be as\l"
    .string "rottenness, and their blossom\l"
    .string "shall go up as dust: because they\l"
    .string "have cast away the law of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, and despised the word of the\l"
    .string "Holy One of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_25::
    .string "Therefore is the anger of the LORD\n"
    .string "kindled against his people, and he\l"
    .string "hath stretched forth his hand\l"
    .string "against them, and hath smitten them:\l"
    .string "and the hills did tremble, and\l"
    .string "their carcases were torn in the midst\l"
    .string "of the streets. For all this his\l"
    .string "anger is not turned away, but his\l"
    .string "hand is stretched out still.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_26::
    .string "And he will lift up an ensign to\n"
    .string "the nations from far, and will hiss\l"
    .string "unto them from the end of the earth:\l"
    .string "and, behold, they shall come with\l"
    .string "speed swiftly:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_27::
    .string "None shall be weary nor stumble\n"
    .string "among them; none shall slumber nor\l"
    .string "sleep; neither shall the girdle\l"
    .string "of their loins be loosed, nor the\l"
    .string "latchet of their shoes be broken:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_28::
    .string "Whose arrows are sharp, and all\n"
    .string "their bows bent, their horses’ hoofs\l"
    .string "shall be counted like flint, and\l"
    .string "their wheels like a whirlwind:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_29::
    .string "Their roaring shall be like a\n"
    .string "lion, they shall roar like young\l"
    .string "lions: yea, they shall roar, and\l"
    .string "lay hold of the prey, and shall\l"
    .string "carry it away safe, and none shall\l"
    .string "deliver it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_5_30::
    .string "And in that day they shall roar\n"
    .string "against them like the roaring of the\l"
    .string "sea: and if one look unto the land,\l"
    .string "behold darkness and sorrow, and the\l"
    .string "light is darkened in the heavens\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_1::
    .string "In the year that king Uzziah died I\n"
    .string "saw also the LORD sitting upon a\l"
    .string "throne, high and lifted up, and his\l"
    .string "train filled the temple.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_2::
    .string "Above it stood the seraphims: each\n"
    .string "one had six wings; with twain he\l"
    .string "covered his face, and with twain he\l"
    .string "covered his feet, and with twain he\l"
    .string "did fly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_3::
    .string "And one cried unto another, and\n"
    .string "said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts: the whole earth is full\l"
    .string "of his glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_4::
    .string "And the posts of the door moved at\n"
    .string "the voice of him that cried, and the\l"
    .string "house was filled with smoke.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_5::
    .string "Then said I, Woe is me! for I am\n"
    .string "undone; because I am a man of unclean\l"
    .string "lips, and I dwell in the midst of a\l"
    .string "people of unclean lips: for mine\l"
    .string "eyes have seen the King, the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_6::
    .string "Then flew one of the seraphims\n"
    .string "unto me, having a live coal in his\l"
    .string "hand, which he had taken with the\l"
    .string "tongs from off the altar:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_7::
    .string "And he laid it upon my mouth, and\n"
    .string "said, Lo, this hath touched thy\l"
    .string "lips; and thine iniquity is taken\l"
    .string "away, and thy sin purged$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_8::
    .string "Also I heard the voice of the Lord,\n"
    .string "saying, Whom shall I send, and who\l"
    .string "will go for us? Then said I, Here am\l"
    .string "I; send me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_9::
    .string "And he said, Go, and tell this\n"
    .string "people, Hear ye indeed, but\l"
    .string "understand not; and see ye indeed,\l"
    .string "but perceive not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_10::
    .string "Make the heart of this people fat,\n"
    .string "and make their ears heavy, and shut\l"
    .string "their eyes; lest they see with their\l"
    .string "eyes, and hear with their ears, and\l"
    .string "understand with their heart, and\l"
    .string "convert, and be healed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_11::
    .string "Then said I, Lord, how long? And he\n"
    .string "answered, Until the cities be wasted\l"
    .string "without inhabitant, and the houses\l"
    .string "without man, and the land be utterly\l"
    .string "desolate,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_12::
    .string "And the LORD have removed men far\n"
    .string "away, and there be a great forsaking\l"
    .string "in the midst of the land$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_6_13::
    .string "But yet in it shall be a tenth, and\n"
    .string "it shall return, and shall be\l"
    .string "eaten: as a teil tree, and as an oak,\l"
    .string "whose substance is in them, when they\l"
    .string "cast their leaves: so the holy seed\l"
    .string "shall be the substance thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the days of\n"
    .string "Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of\l"
    .string "Uzziah, king of Judah, that Rezin the\l"
    .string "king of Syria, and Pekah the son of\l"
    .string "Remaliah, king of Israel, went up\l"
    .string "toward Jerusalem to war against it,\l"
    .string "but could not prevail against it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_2::
    .string "And it was told the house of David,\n"
    .string "saying, Syria is confederate with\l"
    .string "Ephraim. And his heart was moved,\l"
    .string "and the heart of his people, as the\l"
    .string "trees of the wood are moved with the\l"
    .string "wind.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_3::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go\n"
    .string "forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and\l"
    .string "Shearjashub thy son, at the end of\l"
    .string "the conduit of the upper pool in\l"
    .string "the highway of the fuller’s field;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_4::
    .string "And say unto him, Take heed, and be\n"
    .string "quiet; fear not, neither be\l"
    .string "fainthearted for the two tails of\l"
    .string "these smoking firebrands, for the\l"
    .string "fierce anger of Rezin with Syria, and\l"
    .string "of the son of Remaliah$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_5::
    .string "Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son\n"
    .string "of Remaliah, have taken evil\l"
    .string "counsel against thee, saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_6::
    .string "Let us go up against Judah, and vex\n"
    .string "it, and let us make a breach therein\l"
    .string "for us, and set a king in the midst of\l"
    .string "it, even the son of Tabeal:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_7::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD, It shall\n"
    .string "not stand, neither shall it come to\l"
    .string "pass$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_8::
    .string "For the head of Syria is Damascus,\n"
    .string "and the head of Damascus is Rezin;\l"
    .string "and within threescore and five years\l"
    .string "shall Ephraim be broken, that it be\l"
    .string "not a people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_9::
    .string "And the head of Ephraim is Samaria,\n"
    .string "and the head of Samaria is\l"
    .string "Remaliah’s son. If ye will not\l"
    .string "believe, surely ye shall not be\l"
    .string "established.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_10::
    .string "Moreover the LORD spake again unto\n"
    .string "Ahaz, saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_11::
    .string "Ask thee a sign of the LORD thy God;\n"
    .string "ask it either in the depth, or in the\l"
    .string "height above$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_12::
    .string "But Ahaz said, I will not ask,\n"
    .string "neither will I tempt the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_13::
    .string "And he said, Hear ye now, O house of\n"
    .string "David; Is it a small thing for you\l"
    .string "to weary men, but will ye weary my\l"
    .string "God also?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_14::
    .string "Therefore the Lord himself shall\n"
    .string "give you a sign; Behold, a virgin\l"
    .string "shall conceive, and bear a son, and\l"
    .string "shall call his name Immanuel$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_15::
    .string "Butter and honey shall he eat, that\n"
    .string "he may know to refuse the evil, and\l"
    .string "choose the good.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_16::
    .string "For before the child shall know to\n"
    .string "refuse the evil, and choose the\l"
    .string "good, the land that thou abhorrest\l"
    .string "shall be forsaken of both her kings.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_17::
    .string "The LORD shall bring upon thee,\n"
    .string "and upon thy people, and upon thy\l"
    .string "father’s house, days that have not\l"
    .string "come, from the day that Ephraim\l"
    .string "departed from Judah; even the king\l"
    .string "of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_18::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the LORD shall hiss for\l"
    .string "the fly that is in the uttermost\l"
    .string "part of the rivers of Egypt, and for\l"
    .string "the bee that is in the land of\l"
    .string "Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_19::
    .string "And they shall come, and shall\n"
    .string "rest all of them in the desolate\l"
    .string "valleys, and in the holes of the\l"
    .string "rocks, and upon all thorns, and\l"
    .string "upon all bushes.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_20::
    .string "In the same day shall the Lord\n"
    .string "shave with a razor that is hired,\l"
    .string "namely, by them beyond the river, by\l"
    .string "the king of Assyria, the head, and\l"
    .string "the hair of the feet: and it shall\l"
    .string "also consume the beard.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_21::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that a man shall nourish a\l"
    .string "young cow, and two sheep;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_22::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, for the\n"
    .string "abundance of milk that they shall\l"
    .string "give he shall eat butter: for butter\l"
    .string "and honey shall every one eat that\l"
    .string "is left in the land$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_23::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that every place shall be,\l"
    .string "where there were a thousand vines at\l"
    .string "a thousand silverlings, it shall\l"
    .string "even be for briers and thorns.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_24::
    .string "With arrows and with bows shall\n"
    .string "men come thither; because all the\l"
    .string "land shall become briers and thorns.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_7_25::
    .string "And on all hills that shall be\n"
    .string "digged with the mattock, there\l"
    .string "shall not come thither the fear of\l"
    .string "briers and thorns: but it shall be\l"
    .string "for the sending forth of oxen, and\l"
    .string "for the treading of lesser cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_1::
    .string "Moreover the LORD said unto me, Take\n"
    .string "thee a great roll, and write in it\l"
    .string "with a man’s pen concerning\l"
    .string "Mahershalalhashbaz.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_2::
    .string "And I took unto me faithful\n"
    .string "witnesses to record, Uriah the\l"
    .string "priest, and Zechariah the son of\l"
    .string "Jeberechiah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_3::
    .string "And I went unto the prophetess; and\n"
    .string "she conceived, and bare a son. Then\l"
    .string "said the LORD to me, Call his name\l"
    .string "Mahershalalhashbaz.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_4::
    .string "For before the child shall have\n"
    .string "knowledge to cry, My father, and my\l"
    .string "mother, the riches of Damascus and\l"
    .string "the spoil of Samaria shall be\l"
    .string "taken away before the king of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_5::
    .string "The LORD spake also unto me again,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_6::
    .string "Forasmuch as this people refuseth\n"
    .string "the waters of Shiloah that go\l"
    .string "softly, and rejoice in Rezin and\l"
    .string "Remaliah’s son;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_7::
    .string "Now therefore, behold, the Lord\n"
    .string "bringeth up upon them the waters of\l"
    .string "the river, strong and many, even the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria, and all his glory:\l"
    .string "and he shall come up over all his\l"
    .string "channels, and go over all his\l"
    .string "banks:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_8::
    .string "And he shall pass through Judah;\n"
    .string "he shall overflow and go over, he\l"
    .string "shall reach even to the neck; and\l"
    .string "the stretching out of his wings\l"
    .string "shall fill the breadth of thy\l"
    .string "land, O Immanuel$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_9::
    .string "Associate yourselves, O ye\n"
    .string "people, and ye shall be broken in\l"
    .string "pieces; and give ear, all ye of far\l"
    .string "countries: gird yourselves, and ye\l"
    .string "shall be broken in pieces; gird\l"
    .string "yourselves, and ye shall be broken\l"
    .string "in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_10::
    .string "Take counsel together, and it\n"
    .string "shall come to nought; speak the\l"
    .string "word, and it shall not stand: for\l"
    .string "God is with us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_11::
    .string "For the LORD spake thus to me with a\n"
    .string "strong hand, and instructed me that I\l"
    .string "should not walk in the way of this\l"
    .string "people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_12::
    .string "Say ye not, A confederacy, to all\n"
    .string "them to whom this people shall\l"
    .string "say, A confederacy; neither fear ye\l"
    .string "their fear, nor be afraid$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_13::
    .string "Sanctify the LORD of hosts himself;\n"
    .string "and let him be your fear, and let\l"
    .string "him be your dread.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_14::
    .string "And he shall be for a sanctuary;\n"
    .string "but for a stone of stumbling and for\l"
    .string "a rock of offence to both the houses\l"
    .string "of Israel, for a gin and for a snare\l"
    .string "to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_15::
    .string "And many among them shall stumble,\n"
    .string "and fall, and be broken, and be\l"
    .string "snared, and be taken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_16::
    .string "Bind up the testimony, seal the\n"
    .string "law among my disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_17::
    .string "And I will wait upon the LORD,\n"
    .string "that hideth his face from the house\l"
    .string "of Jacob, and I will look for him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_18::
    .string "Behold, I and the children whom the\n"
    .string "LORD hath given me are for signs and\l"
    .string "for wonders in Israel from the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts, which dwelleth in mount\l"
    .string "Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_19::
    .string "And when they shall say unto you,\n"
    .string "Seek unto them that have familiar\l"
    .string "spirits, and unto wizards that\l"
    .string "peep, and that mutter: should not a\l"
    .string "people seek unto their God? for the\l"
    .string "living to the dead?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_20::
    .string "To the law and to the testimony: if\n"
    .string "they speak not according to this\l"
    .string "word, it is because there is no light\l"
    .string "in them$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_21::
    .string "And they shall pass through it,\n"
    .string "hardly bestead and hungry: and it\l"
    .string "shall come to pass, that when they\l"
    .string "shall be hungry, they shall fret\l"
    .string "themselves, and curse their king and\l"
    .string "their God, and look upward.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_8_22::
    .string "And they shall look unto the\n"
    .string "earth; and behold trouble and\l"
    .string "darkness, dimness of anguish; and\l"
    .string "they shall be driven to darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_1::
    .string "Nevertheless the dimness shall\n"
    .string "not be such as was in her vexation,\l"
    .string "when at the first he lightly\l"
    .string "afflicted the land of Zebulun and\l"
    .string "the land of Naphtali, and afterward\l"
    .string "did more grievously afflict her by\l"
    .string "the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, in\l"
    .string "Galilee of the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_2::
    .string "The people that walked in\n"
    .string "darkness have seen a great light:\l"
    .string "they that dwell in the land of the\l"
    .string "shadow of death, upon them hath the\l"
    .string "light shined.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_3::
    .string "Thou hast multiplied the nation,\n"
    .string "and not increased the joy: they joy\l"
    .string "before thee according to the joy in\l"
    .string "harvest, and as men rejoice when they\l"
    .string "divide the spoil.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_4::
    .string "For thou hast broken the yoke of his\n"
    .string "burden, and the staff of his\l"
    .string "shoulder, the rod of his oppressor,\l"
    .string "as in the day of Midian.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_5::
    .string "For every battle of the warrior is\n"
    .string "with confused noise, and garments\l"
    .string "rolled in blood; but this shall be\l"
    .string "with burning and fuel of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_6::
    .string "For unto us a child is born, unto us\n"
    .string "a son is given: and the government\l"
    .string "shall be upon his shoulder: and\l"
    .string "his name shall be called\l"
    .string "Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty\l"
    .string "God, The everlasting Father, The\l"
    .string "Prince of Peace.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_7::
    .string "Of the increase of his government\n"
    .string "and peace there shall be no end,\l"
    .string "upon the throne of David, and upon\l"
    .string "his kingdom, to order it, and to\l"
    .string "establish it with judgment and with\l"
    .string "justice from henceforth even for ever\l"
    .string " The zeal of the LORD of hosts\l"
    .string "will perform this.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_8::
    .string "The Lord sent a word into Jacob, and\n"
    .string "it hath lighted upon Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_9::
    .string "And all the people shall know,\n"
    .string "even Ephraim and the inhabitant of\l"
    .string "Samaria, that say in the pride and\l"
    .string "stoutness of heart,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_10::
    .string "The bricks are fallen down, but we\n"
    .string "will build with hewn stones: the\l"
    .string "sycomores are cut down, but we will\l"
    .string "change them into cedars$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_11::
    .string "Therefore the LORD shall set up\n"
    .string "the adversaries of Rezin against him,\l"
    .string "and join his enemies together;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_12::
    .string "The Syrians before, and the\n"
    .string "Philistines behind; and they shall\l"
    .string "devour Israel with open mouth. For\l"
    .string "all this his anger is not turned\l"
    .string "away, but his hand is stretched out\l"
    .string "still$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_13::
    .string "For the people turneth not unto\n"
    .string "him that smiteth them, neither do\l"
    .string "they seek the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_14::
    .string "Therefore the LORD will cut off\n"
    .string "from Israel head and tail, branch\l"
    .string "and rush, in one day.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_15::
    .string "The ancient and honourable, he is\n"
    .string "the head; and the prophet that\l"
    .string "teacheth lies, he is the tail.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_16::
    .string "For the leaders of this people\n"
    .string "cause them to err; and they that are\l"
    .string "led of them are destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_17::
    .string "Therefore the LORD shall have no\n"
    .string "joy in their young men, neither\l"
    .string "shall have mercy on their\l"
    .string "fatherless and widows: for every one\l"
    .string "is an hypocrite and an evildoer, and\l"
    .string "every mouth speaketh folly. For\l"
    .string "all this his anger is not turned\l"
    .string "away, but his hand is stretched out\l"
    .string "still.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_18::
    .string "For wickedness burneth as the fire:\n"
    .string "it shall devour the briers and\l"
    .string "thorns, and shall kindle in the\l"
    .string "thickets of the forest, and they\l"
    .string "shall mount up like the lifting\l"
    .string "up of smoke.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_19::
    .string "Through the wrath of the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts is the land darkened, and the\l"
    .string "people shall be as the fuel of the\l"
    .string "fire: no man shall spare his\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_20::
    .string "And he shall snatch on the right\n"
    .string "hand, and be hungry; and he shall\l"
    .string "eat on the left hand, and they\l"
    .string "shall not be satisfied: they shall\l"
    .string "eat every man the flesh of his own\l"
    .string "arm:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_9_21::
    .string "Manasseh, Ephraim; and Ephraim,\n"
    .string "Manasseh: and they together shall\l"
    .string "be against Judah. For all this his\l"
    .string "anger is not turned away, but his\l"
    .string "hand is stretched out still$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_1::
    .string "Woe unto them that decree\n"
    .string "unrighteous decrees, and that write\l"
    .string "grievousness which they have\l"
    .string "prescribed;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_2::
    .string "To turn aside the needy from\n"
    .string "judgment, and to take away the right\l"
    .string "from the poor of my people, that\l"
    .string "widows may be their prey, and that\l"
    .string "they may rob the fatherless!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_3::
    .string "And what will ye do in the day of\n"
    .string "visitation, and in the desolation\l"
    .string "which shall come from far? to whom\l"
    .string "will ye flee for help? and where\l"
    .string "will ye leave your glory?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_4::
    .string "Without me they shall bow down\n"
    .string "under the prisoners, and they shall\l"
    .string "fall under the slain. For all this\l"
    .string "his anger is not turned away, but his\l"
    .string "hand is stretched out still$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_5::
    .string "O Assyrian, the rod of mine anger,\n"
    .string "and the staff in their hand is mine\l"
    .string "indignation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_6::
    .string "I will send him against an\n"
    .string "hypocritical nation, and against\l"
    .string "the people of my wrath will I give\l"
    .string "him a charge, to take the spoil, and\l"
    .string "to take the prey, and to tread them\l"
    .string "down like the mire of the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_7::
    .string "Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither\n"
    .string "doth his heart think so; but it is in\l"
    .string "his heart to destroy and cut off\l"
    .string "nations not a few.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_8::
    .string "For he saith, Are not my princes\n"
    .string "altogether kings?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_9::
    .string "Is not Calno as Carchemish? is not\n"
    .string "Hamath as Arpad? is not Samaria as\l"
    .string "Damascus?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_10::
    .string "As my hand hath found the kingdoms\n"
    .string "of the idols, and whose graven\l"
    .string "images did excel them of Jerusalem\l"
    .string "and of Samaria;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_11::
    .string "Shall I not, as I have done unto\n"
    .string "Samaria and her idols, so do to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem and her idols?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_12::
    .string "Wherefore it shall come to pass,\n"
    .string "that when the Lord hath performed\l"
    .string "his whole work upon mount Zion and\l"
    .string "on Jerusalem, I will punish the\l"
    .string "fruit of the stout heart of the king\l"
    .string "of Assyria, and the glory of his high\l"
    .string "looks$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_13::
    .string "For he saith, By the strength of my\n"
    .string "hand I have done it, and by my wisdom;\l"
    .string "for I am prudent: and I have removed\l"
    .string "the bounds of the people, and have\l"
    .string "robbed their treasures, and I have\l"
    .string "put down the inhabitants like a\l"
    .string "valiant man:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_14::
    .string "And my hand hath found as a nest the\n"
    .string "riches of the people: and as one\l"
    .string "gathereth eggs that are left, have I\l"
    .string "gathered all the earth; and there\l"
    .string "was none that moved the wing, or\l"
    .string "opened the mouth, or peeped$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_15::
    .string "Shall the axe boast itself\n"
    .string "against him that heweth therewith? or\l"
    .string "shall the saw magnify itself\l"
    .string "against him that shaketh it? as if\l"
    .string "the rod should shake itself against\l"
    .string "them that lift it up, or as if the\l"
    .string "staff should lift up itself, as if\l"
    .string "it were no wood.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_16::
    .string "Therefore shall the Lord, the Lord\n"
    .string "of hosts, send among his fat ones\l"
    .string "leanness; and under his glory he\l"
    .string "shall kindle a burning like the\l"
    .string "burning of a fire.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_17::
    .string "And the light of Israel shall be\n"
    .string "for a fire, and his Holy One for a\l"
    .string "flame: and it shall burn and devour\l"
    .string "his thorns and his briers in one day;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_18::
    .string "And shall consume the glory of his\n"
    .string "forest, and of his fruitful field,\l"
    .string "both soul and body: and they shall\l"
    .string "be as when a standard-bearer fainteth$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_19::
    .string "And the rest of the trees of his\n"
    .string "forest shall be few, that a child\l"
    .string "may write them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_20::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the remnant of Israel, and\l"
    .string "such as are escaped of the house of\l"
    .string "Jacob, shall no more again stay\l"
    .string "upon him that smote them; but shall\l"
    .string "stay upon the LORD, the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel, in truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_21::
    .string "The remnant shall return, even the\n"
    .string "remnant of Jacob, unto the mighty God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_22::
    .string "For though thy people Israel be\n"
    .string "as the sand of the sea, yet a remnant\l"
    .string "of them shall return: the\l"
    .string "consumption decreed shall\l"
    .string "overflow with righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_23::
    .string "For the Lord GOD of hosts shall\n"
    .string "make a consumption, even determined,\l"
    .string "in the midst of all the land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_24::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD of\n"
    .string "hosts, O my people that dwellest\l"
    .string "in Zion, be not afraid of the\l"
    .string "Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a\l"
    .string "rod, and shall lift up his staff\l"
    .string "against thee, after the manner of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_25::
    .string "For yet a very little while, and\n"
    .string "the indignation shall cease, and\l"
    .string "mine anger in their destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_26::
    .string "And the LORD of hosts shall stir\n"
    .string "up a scourge for him according to\l"
    .string "the slaughter of Midian at the rock\l"
    .string "of Oreb: and as his rod was upon the\l"
    .string "sea, so shall he lift it up after\l"
    .string "the manner of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_27::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that his burden shall be taken\l"
    .string "away from off thy shoulder, and his\l"
    .string "yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke\l"
    .string "shall be destroyed because of the\l"
    .string "anointing.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_28::
    .string "He is come to Aiath, he is passed to\n"
    .string "Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up\l"
    .string "his carriages:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_29::
    .string "They are gone over the passage:\n"
    .string "they have taken up their lodging at\l"
    .string "Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of\l"
    .string "Saul is fled$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_30::
    .string "Lift up thy voice, O daughter of\n"
    .string "Gallim: cause it to be heard unto\l"
    .string "Laish, O poor Anathoth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_31::
    .string "Madmenah is removed; the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Gebim gather\l"
    .string "themselves to flee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_32::
    .string "As yet shall he remain at Nob that\n"
    .string "day: he shall shake his hand against\l"
    .string "the mount of the daughter of Zion,\l"
    .string "the hill of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_33::
    .string "Behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "shall lop the bough with terror:\l"
    .string "and the high ones of stature shall\l"
    .string "be hewn down, and the haughty shall\l"
    .string "be humbled.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_10_34::
    .string "And he shall cut down the thickets\n"
    .string "of the forest with iron, and Lebanon\l"
    .string "shall fall by a mighty one.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_1::
    .string "And there shall come forth a rod\n"
    .string "out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch\l"
    .string "shall grow out of his roots:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_2::
    .string "And the spirit of the LORD shall\n"
    .string "rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom\l"
    .string "and understanding, the spirit of\l"
    .string "counsel and might, the spirit of\l"
    .string "knowledge and of the fear of the\l"
    .string "LORD;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_3::
    .string "And shall make him of quick\n"
    .string "understanding in the fear of the\l"
    .string "LORD: and he shall not judge after\l"
    .string "the sight of his eyes, neither\l"
    .string "reprove after the hearing of his\l"
    .string "ears:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_4::
    .string "But with righteousness shall he\n"
    .string "judge the poor, and reprove with\l"
    .string "equity for the meek of the earth: and\l"
    .string "he shall smite the earth: with the\l"
    .string "rod of his mouth, and with the breath\l"
    .string "of his lips shall he slay the\l"
    .string "wicked$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_5::
    .string "And righteousness shall be the\n"
    .string "girdle of his loins, and\l"
    .string "faithfulness the girdle of his\l"
    .string "reins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_6::
    .string "The wolf also shall dwell with\n"
    .string "the lamb, and the leopard shall\l"
    .string "lie down with the kid; and the calf\l"
    .string "and the young lion and the fatling\l"
    .string "together; and a little child\l"
    .string "shall lead them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_7::
    .string "And the cow and the bear shall\n"
    .string "feed; their young ones shall lie\l"
    .string "down together: and the lion shall\l"
    .string "eat straw like the ox.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_8::
    .string "And the sucking child shall play\n"
    .string "on the hole of the asp, and the\l"
    .string "weaned child shall put his hand on\l"
    .string "the cockatrice’ den.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_9::
    .string "They shall not hurt nor destroy in\n"
    .string "all my holy mountain: for the earth\l"
    .string "shall be full of the knowledge of\l"
    .string "the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_10::
    .string "And in that day there shall be a\n"
    .string "root of Jesse, which shall stand for\l"
    .string "an ensign of the people; to it\l"
    .string "shall the Gentiles seek: and his\l"
    .string "rest shall be glorious.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_11::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the Lord shall set his\l"
    .string "hand again the second time to recover\l"
    .string "the remnant of his people, which\l"
    .string "shall be left, from Assyria, and\l"
    .string "from Egypt, and from Pathros, and\l"
    .string "from Cush, and from Elam, and from\l"
    .string "Shinar, and from Hamath, and from the\l"
    .string "islands of the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_12::
    .string "And he shall set up an ensign for\n"
    .string "the nations, and shall assemble the\l"
    .string "outcasts of Israel, and gather\l"
    .string "together the dispersed of Judah from\l"
    .string "the four corners of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_13::
    .string "The envy also of Ephraim shall\n"
    .string "depart, and the adversaries of Judah\l"
    .string "shall be cut off: Ephraim shall\l"
    .string "not envy Judah, and Judah shall not\l"
    .string "vex Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_14::
    .string "But they shall fly upon the\n"
    .string "shoulders of the Philistines toward\l"
    .string "the west; they shall spoil them of\l"
    .string "the east together: they shall lay\l"
    .string "their hand upon Edom and Moab; and\l"
    .string "the children of Ammon shall obey\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_15::
    .string "And the LORD shall utterly\n"
    .string "destroy the tongue of the Egyptian\l"
    .string "sea; and with his mighty wind shall\l"
    .string "he shake his hand over the river, and\l"
    .string "shall smite it in the seven streams,\l"
    .string "and make men go over dryshod.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_11_16::
    .string "And there shall be an highway for\n"
    .string "the remnant of his people, which\l"
    .string "shall be left, from Assyria; like\l"
    .string "as it was to Israel in the day that\l"
    .string "he came up out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_1::
    .string "And in that day thou shalt say, O\n"
    .string "LORD, I will praise thee: though\l"
    .string "thou wast angry with me, thine anger\l"
    .string "is turned away, and thou comfortedst\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_2::
    .string "Behold, God is my salvation; I\n"
    .string "will trust, and not be afraid: for\l"
    .string "the LORD JEHOVAH is my strength and\l"
    .string "my song; he also is become my\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_3::
    .string "Therefore with joy shall ye draw\n"
    .string "water out of the wells of salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_4::
    .string "And in that day shall ye say,\n"
    .string "Praise the LORD, call upon his\l"
    .string "name, declare his doings among the\l"
    .string "people, make mention that his name\l"
    .string "is exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_5::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD; for he hath done\n"
    .string "excellent things: this is known in\l"
    .string "all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_12_6::
    .string "Cry out and shout, thou inhabitant\n"
    .string "of Zion: for great is the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel in the midst of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_1::
    .string "The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah\n"
    .string "the son of Amoz did see.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_2::
    .string "Lift ye up a banner upon the high\n"
    .string "mountain, exalt the voice unto them,\l"
    .string "shake the hand, that they may go into\l"
    .string "the gates of the nobles.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_3::
    .string "I have commanded my sanctified ones,\n"
    .string "I have also called my mighty ones\l"
    .string "for mine anger, even them that\l"
    .string "rejoice in my highness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_4::
    .string "The noise of a multitude in the\n"
    .string "mountains, like as of a great\l"
    .string "people; a tumultuous noise of the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of nations gathered\l"
    .string "together: the LORD of hosts mustereth\l"
    .string "the host of the battle.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_5::
    .string "They come from a far country, from\n"
    .string "the end of heaven, even the LORD, and\l"
    .string "the weapons of his indignation, to\l"
    .string "destroy the whole land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_6::
    .string "Howl ye; for the day of the LORD is\n"
    .string "at hand; it shall come as a\l"
    .string "destruction from the Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_7::
    .string "Therefore shall all hands be\n"
    .string "faint, and every man’s heart shall\l"
    .string "melt:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_8::
    .string "And they shall be afraid: pangs\n"
    .string "and sorrows shall take hold of\l"
    .string "them; they shall be in pain as a\l"
    .string "woman that travaileth: they shall\l"
    .string "be amazed one at another; their faces\l"
    .string "shall be as flames$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_9::
    .string "Behold, the day of the LORD cometh,\n"
    .string "cruel both with wrath and fierce\l"
    .string "anger, to lay the land desolate:\l"
    .string "and he shall destroy the sinners\l"
    .string "thereof out of it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_10::
    .string "For the stars of heaven and the\n"
    .string "constellations thereof shall not\l"
    .string "give their light: the sun shall be\l"
    .string "darkened in his going forth, and the\l"
    .string "moon shall not cause her light to\l"
    .string "shine.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_11::
    .string "And I will punish the world for\n"
    .string "their evil, and the wicked for their\l"
    .string "iniquity; and I will cause the\l"
    .string "arrogancy of the proud to cease, and\l"
    .string "will lay low the haughtiness of\l"
    .string "the terrible.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_12::
    .string "I will make a man more precious\n"
    .string "than fine gold; even a man than the\l"
    .string "golden wedge of Ophir.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_13::
    .string "Therefore I will shake the\n"
    .string "heavens, and the earth shall remove\l"
    .string "out of her place, in the wrath of\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts, and in the day of\l"
    .string "his fierce anger.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_14::
    .string "And it shall be as the chased roe,\n"
    .string "and as a sheep that no man taketh\l"
    .string "up: they shall every man turn to\l"
    .string "his own people, and flee every one\l"
    .string "into his own land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_15::
    .string "Every one that is found shall be\n"
    .string "thrust through; and every one that is\l"
    .string "joined unto them shall fall by the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_16::
    .string "Their children also shall be\n"
    .string "dashed to pieces before their eyes;\l"
    .string "their houses shall be spoiled, and\l"
    .string "their wives ravished.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_17::
    .string "Behold, I will stir up the Medes\n"
    .string "against them, which shall not\l"
    .string "regard silver; and as for gold, they\l"
    .string "shall not delight in it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_18::
    .string "Their bows also shall dash the\n"
    .string "young men to pieces; and they shall\l"
    .string "have no pity on the fruit of the\l"
    .string "womb; their eyes shall not spare\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_19::
    .string "And Babylon, the glory of\n"
    .string "kingdoms, the beauty of the\l"
    .string "Chaldees’ excellency, shall be as\l"
    .string "when God overthrew Sodom and\l"
    .string "Gomorrah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_20::
    .string "It shall never be inhabited,\n"
    .string "neither shall it be dwelt in from\l"
    .string "generation to generation: neither\l"
    .string "shall the Arabian pitch tent there;\l"
    .string "neither shall the shepherds make\l"
    .string "their fold there.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_21::
    .string "But wild beasts of the desert\n"
    .string "shall lie there; and their houses\l"
    .string "shall be full of doleful\l"
    .string "creatures; and owls shall dwell\l"
    .string "there, and satyrs shall dance there.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_13_22::
    .string "And the wild beasts of the islands\n"
    .string "shall cry in their desolate houses,\l"
    .string "and dragons in their pleasant\l"
    .string "palaces: and her time is near to\l"
    .string "come, and her days shall not be\l"
    .string "prolonged.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_1::
    .string "For the LORD will have mercy on\n"
    .string "Jacob, and will yet choose Israel,\l"
    .string "and set them in their own land: and\l"
    .string "the strangers shall be joined with\l"
    .string "them, and they shall cleave to the\l"
    .string "house of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_2::
    .string "And the people shall take them,\n"
    .string "and bring them to their place: and\l"
    .string "the house of Israel shall possess\l"
    .string "them in the land of the LORD for\l"
    .string "servants and handmaids: and they\l"
    .string "shall take them captives, whose\l"
    .string "captives they were; and they shall\l"
    .string "rule over their oppressors.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_3::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "day that the LORD shall give thee\l"
    .string "rest from thy sorrow, and from thy\l"
    .string "fear, and from the hard bondage\l"
    .string "wherein thou wast made to serve,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_4::
    .string "That thou shalt take up this\n"
    .string "proverb against the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "and say, How hath the oppressor\l"
    .string "ceased! the golden city ceased!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_5::
    .string "The LORD hath broken the staff of\n"
    .string "the wicked, and the sceptre of the\l"
    .string "rulers$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_6::
    .string "He who smote the people in wrath\n"
    .string "with a continual stroke, he that\l"
    .string "ruled the nations in anger, is\l"
    .string "persecuted, and none hindereth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_7::
    .string "The whole earth is at rest, and is\n"
    .string "quiet: they break forth into singing.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_8::
    .string "Yea, the fir trees rejoice at thee,\n"
    .string "and the cedars of Lebanon, saying,\l"
    .string "Since thou art laid down, no feller\l"
    .string "is come up against us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_9::
    .string "Hell from beneath is moved for\n"
    .string "thee to meet thee at thy coming: it\l"
    .string "stirreth up the dead for thee, even\l"
    .string "all the chief ones of the earth; it\l"
    .string "hath raised up from their thrones\l"
    .string "all the kings of the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_10::
    .string "All they shall speak and say\n"
    .string "unto thee, Art thou also become weak\l"
    .string "as we? art thou become like unto us?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_11::
    .string "Thy pomp is brought down to the\n"
    .string "grave, and the noise of thy viols:\l"
    .string "the worm is spread under thee, and\l"
    .string "the worms cover thee$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_12::
    .string "How art thou fallen from heaven, O\n"
    .string "Lucifer, son of the morning! how art\l"
    .string "thou cut down to the ground, which\l"
    .string "didst weaken the nations!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_13::
    .string "For thou hast said in thine heart, I\n"
    .string "will ascend into heaven, I will\l"
    .string "exalt my throne above the stars of\l"
    .string "God: I will sit also upon the mount\l"
    .string "of the congregation, in the sides of\l"
    .string "the north:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_14::
    .string "I will ascend above the heights of\n"
    .string "the clouds; I will be like the most\l"
    .string "High$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_15::
    .string "Yet thou shalt be brought down to\n"
    .string "hell, to the sides of the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_16::
    .string "They that see thee shall narrowly\n"
    .string "look upon thee, and consider thee,\l"
    .string "saying, Is this the man that made the\l"
    .string "earth to tremble, that did shake\l"
    .string "kingdoms;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_17::
    .string "That made the world as a\n"
    .string "wilderness, and destroyed the cities\l"
    .string "thereof; that opened not the house\l"
    .string "of his prisoners?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_18::
    .string "All the kings of the nations, even\n"
    .string "all of them, lie in glory, every\l"
    .string "one in his own house$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_19::
    .string "But thou art cast out of thy grave\n"
    .string "like an abominable branch, and as\l"
    .string "the raiment of those that are slain,\l"
    .string "thrust through with a sword, that go\l"
    .string "down to the stones of the pit; as a\l"
    .string "carcase trodden under feet.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_20::
    .string "Thou shalt not be joined with them\n"
    .string "in burial, because thou hast\l"
    .string "destroyed thy land, and slain thy\l"
    .string "people: the seed of evildoers\l"
    .string "shall never be renowned.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_21::
    .string "Prepare slaughter for his\n"
    .string "children for the iniquity of their\l"
    .string "fathers; that they do not rise, nor\l"
    .string "possess the land, nor fill the face\l"
    .string "of the world with cities.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_22::
    .string "For I will rise up against them,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts, and cut off\l"
    .string "from Babylon the name, and remnant,\l"
    .string "and son, and nephew, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_23::
    .string "I will also make it a possession\n"
    .string "for the bittern, and pools of water:\l"
    .string "and I will sweep it with the besom\l"
    .string "of destruction, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_24::
    .string "The LORD of hosts hath sworn,\n"
    .string "saying, Surely as I have thought, so\l"
    .string "shall it come to pass; and as I have\l"
    .string "purposed, so shall it stand:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_25::
    .string "That I will break the Assyrian in\n"
    .string "my land, and upon my mountains tread\l"
    .string "him under foot: then shall his yoke\l"
    .string "depart from off them, and his burden\l"
    .string "depart from off their shoulders$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_26::
    .string "This is the purpose that is\n"
    .string "purposed upon the whole earth: and\l"
    .string "this is the hand that is stretched\l"
    .string "out upon all the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_27::
    .string "For the LORD of hosts hath\n"
    .string "purposed, and who shall disannul\l"
    .string "it? and his hand is stretched out,\l"
    .string "and who shall turn it back?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_28::
    .string "In the year that king Ahaz died was\n"
    .string "this burden$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_29::
    .string "Rejoice not thou, whole Palestina,\n"
    .string "because the rod of him that smote\l"
    .string "thee is broken: for out of the\l"
    .string "serpent’s root shall come forth a\l"
    .string "cockatrice, and his fruit shall be a\l"
    .string "fiery flying serpent.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_30::
    .string "And the firstborn of the poor\n"
    .string "shall feed, and the needy shall\l"
    .string "lie down in safety: and I will kill\l"
    .string "thy root with famine, and he shall\l"
    .string "slay thy remnant.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_31::
    .string "Howl, O gate; cry, O city; thou,\n"
    .string "whole Palestina, art dissolved:\l"
    .string "for there shall come from the north\l"
    .string "a smoke, and none shall be alone in\l"
    .string "his appointed times.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_14_32::
    .string "What shall one then answer the\n"
    .string "messengers of the nation? That the\l"
    .string "LORD hath founded Zion, and the poor\l"
    .string "of his people shall trust in it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_1::
    .string "The burden of Moab. Because in the\n"
    .string "night Ar of Moab is laid waste, and\l"
    .string "brought to silence; because in the\l"
    .string "night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and\l"
    .string "brought to silence;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_2::
    .string "He is gone up to Bajith, and to\n"
    .string "Dibon, the high places, to weep:\l"
    .string "Moab shall howl over Nebo, and over\l"
    .string "Medeba: on all their heads shall\l"
    .string "be baldness, and every beard cut off$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_3::
    .string "In their streets they shall gird\n"
    .string "themselves with sackcloth: on the\l"
    .string "tops of their houses, and in their\l"
    .string "streets, every one shall howl,\l"
    .string "weeping abundantly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_4::
    .string "And Heshbon shall cry, and\n"
    .string "Elealeh: their voice shall be\l"
    .string "heard even unto Jahaz: therefore the\l"
    .string "armed soldiers of Moab shall cry\l"
    .string "out; his life shall be grievous\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_5::
    .string "My heart shall cry out for Moab;\n"
    .string "his fugitives shall flee unto Zoar,\l"
    .string "an heifer of three years old: for by\l"
    .string "the mounting up of Luhith with\l"
    .string "weeping shall they go it up; for in\l"
    .string "the way of Horonaim they shall\l"
    .string "raise up a cry of destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_6::
    .string "For the waters of Nimrim shall be\n"
    .string "desolate: for the hay is withered\l"
    .string "away, the grass faileth, there is no\l"
    .string "green thing.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_7::
    .string "Therefore the abundance they have\n"
    .string "gotten, and that which they have\l"
    .string "laid up, shall they carry away to\l"
    .string "the brook of the willows.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_8::
    .string "For the cry is gone round about the\n"
    .string "borders of Moab; the howling thereof\l"
    .string "unto Eglaim, and the howling\l"
    .string "thereof unto Beerelim.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_15_9::
    .string "For the waters of Dimon shall be\n"
    .string "full of blood: for I will bring\l"
    .string "more upon Dimon, lions upon him\l"
    .string "that escapeth of Moab, and upon the\l"
    .string "remnant of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_1::
    .string "Send ye the lamb to the ruler of\n"
    .string "the land from Sela to the\l"
    .string "wilderness, unto the mount of the\l"
    .string "daughter of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_2::
    .string "For it shall be, that, as a\n"
    .string "wandering bird cast out of the nest,\l"
    .string "so the daughters of Moab shall be at\l"
    .string "the fords of Arnon.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_3::
    .string "Take counsel, execute judgment;\n"
    .string "make thy shadow as the night in the\l"
    .string "midst of the noonday; hide the\l"
    .string "outcasts; bewray not him that\l"
    .string "wandereth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_4::
    .string "Let mine outcasts dwell with thee,\n"
    .string "Moab; be thou a covert to them from\l"
    .string "the face of the spoiler: for the\l"
    .string "extortioner is at an end, the\l"
    .string "spoiler ceaseth, the oppressors\l"
    .string "are consumed out of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_5::
    .string "And in mercy shall the throne be\n"
    .string "established: and he shall sit upon\l"
    .string "it in truth in the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "David, judging, and seeking judgment,\l"
    .string "and hasting righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_6::
    .string "We have heard of the pride of Moab;\n"
    .string "he is very proud: even of his\l"
    .string "haughtiness, and his pride, and his\l"
    .string "wrath: but his lies shall not be so.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_7::
    .string "Therefore shall Moab howl for\n"
    .string "Moab, every one shall howl: for the\l"
    .string "foundations of Kirhareseth shall ye\l"
    .string "mourn; surely they are stricken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_8::
    .string "For the fields of Heshbon\n"
    .string "languish, and the vine of Sibmah: the\l"
    .string "lords of the heathen have broken down\l"
    .string "the principal plants thereof,\l"
    .string "they are come even unto Jazer, they\l"
    .string "wandered through the wilderness: her\l"
    .string "branches are stretched out, they are\l"
    .string "gone over the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_9::
    .string "Therefore I will bewail with the\n"
    .string "weeping of Jazer the vine of Sibmah:\l"
    .string "I will water thee with my tears, O\l"
    .string "Heshbon, and Elealeh: for the\l"
    .string "shouting for thy summer fruits and\l"
    .string "for thy harvest is fallen.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_10::
    .string "And gladness is taken away, and joy\n"
    .string "out of the plentiful field; and in\l"
    .string "the vineyards there shall be no\l"
    .string "singing, neither shall there be\l"
    .string "shouting: the treaders shall tread\l"
    .string "out no wine in their presses; I have\l"
    .string "made their vintage shouting to cease.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_11::
    .string "Wherefore my bowels shall sound\n"
    .string "like an harp for Moab, and mine\l"
    .string "inward parts for Kirharesh.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_12::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when it\n"
    .string "is seen that Moab is weary on the\l"
    .string "high place, that he shall come to\l"
    .string "his sanctuary to pray; but he shall\l"
    .string "not prevail.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_13::
    .string "This is the word that the LORD hath\n"
    .string "spoken concerning Moab since that\l"
    .string "time.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_16_14::
    .string "But now the LORD hath spoken,\n"
    .string "saying, Within three years, as the\l"
    .string "years of an hireling, and the glory\l"
    .string "of Moab shall be contemned, with\l"
    .string "all that great multitude; and the\l"
    .string "remnant shall be very small and\l"
    .string "feeble.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_1::
    .string "The burden of Damascus. Behold,\n"
    .string "Damascus is taken away from being a\l"
    .string "city, and it shall be a ruinous\l"
    .string "heap.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_2::
    .string "The cities of Aroer are forsaken:\n"
    .string "they shall be for flocks, which\l"
    .string "shall lie down, and none shall\l"
    .string "make them afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_3::
    .string "The fortress also shall cease\n"
    .string "from Ephraim, and the kingdom from\l"
    .string "Damascus, and the remnant of Syria:\l"
    .string "they shall be as the glory of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, saith the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_4::
    .string "And in that day it shall come to\n"
    .string "pass, that the glory of Jacob shall\l"
    .string "be made thin, and the fatness of his\l"
    .string "flesh shall wax lean.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_5::
    .string "And it shall be as when the\n"
    .string "harvestman gathereth the corn, and\l"
    .string "reapeth the ears with his arm; and it\l"
    .string "shall be as he that gathereth ears\l"
    .string "in the valley of Rephaim.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_6::
    .string "Yet gleaning grapes shall be\n"
    .string "left in it, as the shaking of an\l"
    .string "olive tree, two or three berries in\l"
    .string "the top of the uppermost bough,\l"
    .string "four or five in the outmost fruitful\l"
    .string "branches thereof, saith the LORD God\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_7::
    .string "At that day shall a man look to\n"
    .string "his Maker, and his eyes shall have\l"
    .string "respect to the Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_8::
    .string "And he shall not look to the\n"
    .string "altars, the work of his hands,\l"
    .string "neither shall respect that which\l"
    .string "his fingers have made, either the\l"
    .string "groves, or the images.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_9::
    .string "In that day shall his strong\n"
    .string "cities be as a forsaken bough, and an\l"
    .string "uppermost branch, which they left\l"
    .string "because of the children of Israel:\l"
    .string "and there shall be desolation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_10::
    .string "Because thou hast forgotten the God\n"
    .string "of thy salvation, and hast not been\l"
    .string "mindful of the rock of thy strength,\l"
    .string "therefore shalt thou plant\l"
    .string "pleasant plants, and shalt set it\l"
    .string "with strange slips:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_11::
    .string "In the day shalt thou make thy\n"
    .string "plant to grow, and in the morning\l"
    .string "shalt thou make thy seed to\l"
    .string "flourish: but the harvest shall be\l"
    .string "a heap in the day of grief and of\l"
    .string "desperate sorrow$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_12::
    .string "Woe to the multitude of many\n"
    .string "people, which make a noise like the\l"
    .string "noise of the seas; and to the rushing\l"
    .string "of nations, that make a rushing like\l"
    .string "the rushing of mighty waters!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_13::
    .string "The nations shall rush like the\n"
    .string "rushing of many waters: but God\l"
    .string "shall rebuke them, and they shall\l"
    .string "flee far off, and shall be chased\l"
    .string "as the chaff of the mountains before\l"
    .string "the wind, and like a rolling thing\l"
    .string "before the whirlwind$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_17_14::
    .string "And behold at eveningtide trouble;\n"
    .string "and before the morning he is not.\l"
    .string "This is the portion of them that\l"
    .string "spoil us, and the lot of them that\l"
    .string "rob us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_1::
    .string "Woe to the land shadowing with\n"
    .string "wings, which is beyond the rivers of\l"
    .string "Ethiopia:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_2::
    .string "That sendeth ambassadors by the sea,\n"
    .string "even in vessels of bulrushes upon\l"
    .string "the waters, saying, Go, ye swift\l"
    .string "messengers, to a nation scattered and\l"
    .string "peeled, to a people terrible from\l"
    .string "their beginning hitherto; a nation\l"
    .string "meted out and trodden down, whose\l"
    .string "land the rivers have spoiled!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_3::
    .string "All ye inhabitants of the world,\n"
    .string "and dwellers on the earth, see ye,\l"
    .string "when he lifteth up an ensign on the\l"
    .string "mountains; and when he bloweth a\l"
    .string "trumpet, hear ye$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_4::
    .string "For so the LORD said unto me, I\n"
    .string "will take my rest, and I will\l"
    .string "consider in my dwelling place\l"
    .string "like a clear heat upon herbs, and\l"
    .string "like a cloud of dew in the heat of\l"
    .string "harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_5::
    .string "For afore the harvest, when the bud\n"
    .string "is perfect, and the sour grape is\l"
    .string "ripening in the flower, he shall\l"
    .string "both cut off the sprigs with\l"
    .string "pruning hooks, and take away and cut\l"
    .string "down the branches.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_6::
    .string "They shall be left together unto\n"
    .string "the fowls of the mountains, and to\l"
    .string "the beasts of the earth: and the\l"
    .string "fowls shall summer upon them, and\l"
    .string "all the beasts of the earth shall\l"
    .string "winter upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_18_7::
    .string "In that time shall the present be\n"
    .string "brought unto the LORD of hosts of a\l"
    .string "people scattered and peeled, and\l"
    .string "from a people terrible from their\l"
    .string "beginning hitherto; a nation meted\l"
    .string "out and trodden under foot, whose\l"
    .string "land the rivers have spoiled, to the\l"
    .string "place of the name of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, the mount Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_1::
    .string "The burden of Egypt. Behold, the\n"
    .string "LORD rideth upon a swift cloud, and\l"
    .string "shall come into Egypt: and the\l"
    .string "idols of Egypt shall be moved at\l"
    .string "his presence, and the heart of Egypt\l"
    .string "shall melt in the midst of it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_2::
    .string "And I will set the Egyptians\n"
    .string "against the Egyptians: and they\l"
    .string "shall fight every one against his\l"
    .string "brother, and every one against his\l"
    .string "neighbour; city against city, and\l"
    .string "kingdom against kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_3::
    .string "And the spirit of Egypt shall\n"
    .string "fail in the midst thereof; and I\l"
    .string "will destroy the counsel thereof:\l"
    .string "and they shall seek to the idols,\l"
    .string "and to the charmers, and to them that\l"
    .string "have familiar spirits, and to the\l"
    .string "wizards.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_4::
    .string "And the Egyptians will I give over\n"
    .string "into the hand of a cruel lord; and a\l"
    .string "fierce king shall rule over them,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_5::
    .string "And the waters shall fail from the\n"
    .string "sea, and the river shall be wasted\l"
    .string "and dried up.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_6::
    .string "And they shall turn the rivers far\n"
    .string "away; and the brooks of defence\l"
    .string "shall be emptied and dried up: the\l"
    .string "reeds and flags shall wither.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_7::
    .string "The paper reeds by the brooks, by\n"
    .string "the mouth of the brooks, and every\l"
    .string "thing sown by the brooks, shall\l"
    .string "wither, be driven away, and be no\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_8::
    .string "The fishers also shall mourn, and\n"
    .string "all they that cast angle into the\l"
    .string "brooks shall lament, and they that\l"
    .string "spread nets upon the waters shall\l"
    .string "languish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_9::
    .string "Moreover they that work in fine\n"
    .string "flax, and they that weave networks,\l"
    .string "shall be confounded.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_10::
    .string "And they shall be broken in the\n"
    .string "purposes thereof, all that make\l"
    .string "sluices and ponds for fish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_11::
    .string "Surely the princes of Zoan are\n"
    .string "fools, the counsel of the wise\l"
    .string "counsellors of Pharaoh is become\l"
    .string "brutish: how say ye unto Pharaoh, I\l"
    .string "am the son of the wise, the son of\l"
    .string "ancient kings?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_12::
    .string "Where are they? where are thy wise\n"
    .string "men? and let them tell thee now,\l"
    .string "and let them know what the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts hath purposed upon Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_13::
    .string "The princes of Zoan are become\n"
    .string "fools, the princes of Noph are\l"
    .string "deceived; they have also seduced\l"
    .string "Egypt, even they that are the stay of\l"
    .string "the tribes thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_14::
    .string "The LORD hath mingled a perverse\n"
    .string "spirit in the midst thereof: and\l"
    .string "they have caused Egypt to err in\l"
    .string "every work thereof, as a drunken man\l"
    .string "staggereth in his vomit.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_15::
    .string "Neither shall there be any work\n"
    .string "for Egypt, which the head or tail,\l"
    .string "branch or rush, may do.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_16::
    .string "In that day shall Egypt be like\n"
    .string "unto women: and it shall be afraid\l"
    .string "and fear because of the shaking of\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD of hosts, which\l"
    .string "he shaketh over it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_17::
    .string "And the land of Judah shall be a\n"
    .string "terror unto Egypt, every one that\l"
    .string "maketh mention thereof shall be\l"
    .string "afraid in himself, because of the\l"
    .string "counsel of the LORD of hosts, which\l"
    .string "he hath determined against it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_18::
    .string "In that day shall five cities in\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt speak the\l"
    .string "language of Canaan, and swear to the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts; one shall be\l"
    .string "called, The city of destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_19::
    .string "In that day shall there be an\n"
    .string "altar to the LORD in the midst of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, and a pillar at the\l"
    .string "border thereof to the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_20::
    .string "And it shall be for a sign and for\n"
    .string "a witness unto the LORD of hosts in\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt: for they shall\l"
    .string "cry unto the LORD because of the\l"
    .string "oppressors, and he shall send them\l"
    .string "a saviour, and a great one, and he\l"
    .string "shall deliver them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_21::
    .string "And the LORD shall be known to\n"
    .string "Egypt, and the Egyptians shall\l"
    .string "know the LORD in that day, and shall\l"
    .string "do sacrifice and oblation; yea, they\l"
    .string "shall vow a vow unto the LORD, and\l"
    .string "perform it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_22::
    .string "And the LORD shall smite Egypt: he\n"
    .string "shall smite and heal it: and they\l"
    .string "shall return even to the LORD, and\l"
    .string "he shall be intreated of them, and\l"
    .string "shall heal them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_23::
    .string "In that day shall there be a\n"
    .string "highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and\l"
    .string "the Assyrian shall come into Egypt,\l"
    .string "and the Egyptian into Assyria, and\l"
    .string "the Egyptians shall serve with the\l"
    .string "Assyrians.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_24::
    .string "In that day shall Israel be the\n"
    .string "third with Egypt and with Assyria,\l"
    .string "even a blessing in the midst of the\l"
    .string "land:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_19_25::
    .string "Whom the LORD of hosts shall\n"
    .string "bless, saying, Blessed be Egypt my\l"
    .string "people, and Assyria the work of my\l"
    .string "hands, and Israel mine inheritance$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_1::
    .string "In the year that Tartan came unto\n"
    .string "Ashdod, (when Sargon the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria sent him,) and fought against\l"
    .string "Ashdod, and took it;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_2::
    .string "At the same time spake the LORD by\n"
    .string "Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go\l"
    .string "and loose the sackcloth from off\l"
    .string "thy loins, and put off thy shoe from\l"
    .string "thy foot. And he did so, walking\l"
    .string "naked and barefoot$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_3::
    .string "And the LORD said, Like as my\n"
    .string "servant Isaiah hath walked naked and\l"
    .string "barefoot three years for a sign and\l"
    .string "wonder upon Egypt and upon\l"
    .string "Ethiopia;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_4::
    .string "So shall the king of Assyria lead\n"
    .string "away the Egyptians prisoners, and\l"
    .string "the Ethiopians captives, young and\l"
    .string "old, naked and barefoot, even with\l"
    .string "their buttocks uncovered, to the\l"
    .string "shame of Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_5::
    .string "And they shall be afraid and\n"
    .string "ashamed of Ethiopia their\l"
    .string "expectation, and of Egypt their\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_20_6::
    .string "And the inhabitant of this isle\n"
    .string "shall say in that day, Behold, such\l"
    .string "is our expectation, whither we flee\l"
    .string "for help to be delivered from the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria: and how shall we\l"
    .string "escape?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_1::
    .string "The burden of the desert of the sea.\n"
    .string "As whirlwinds in the south pass\l"
    .string "through; so it cometh from the\l"
    .string "desert, from a terrible land$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_2::
    .string "A grievous vision is declared unto\n"
    .string "me; the treacherous dealer dealeth\l"
    .string "treacherously, and the spoiler\l"
    .string "spoileth. Go up, O Elam: besiege, O\l"
    .string "Media; all the sighing thereof have\l"
    .string "I made to cease.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_3::
    .string "Therefore are my loins filled\n"
    .string "with pain: pangs have taken hold\l"
    .string "upon me, as the pangs of a woman\l"
    .string "that travaileth: I was bowed down at\l"
    .string "the hearing of it; I was dismayed at\l"
    .string "the seeing of it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_4::
    .string "My heart panted, fearfulness\n"
    .string "affrighted me: the night of my\l"
    .string "pleasure hath he turned into fear\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_5::
    .string "Prepare the table, watch in the\n"
    .string "watchtower, eat, drink: arise, ye\l"
    .string "princes, and anoint the shield.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_6::
    .string "For thus hath the LORD said unto me,\n"
    .string "Go, set a watchman, let him declare\l"
    .string "what he seeth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_7::
    .string "And he saw a chariot with a couple\n"
    .string "of horsemen, a chariot of asses, and\l"
    .string "a chariot of camels; and he\l"
    .string "hearkened diligently with much\l"
    .string "heed:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_8::
    .string "And he cried, A lion: My lord, I\n"
    .string "stand continually upon the\l"
    .string "watchtower in the daytime, and I am\l"
    .string "set in my ward whole nights:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_9::
    .string "And, behold, here cometh a chariot\n"
    .string "of men, with a couple of horsemen.\l"
    .string "And he answered and said, Babylon is\l"
    .string "fallen, is fallen; and all the\l"
    .string "graven images of her gods he hath\l"
    .string "broken unto the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_10::
    .string "O my threshing, and the corn of my\n"
    .string "floor: that which I have heard of the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, the God of Israel,\l"
    .string "have I declared unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_11::
    .string "The burden of Dumah. He calleth to\n"
    .string "me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the\l"
    .string "night? Watchman, what of the night?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_12::
    .string "The watchman said, The morning\n"
    .string "cometh, and also the night: if ye\l"
    .string "will enquire, enquire ye: return,\l"
    .string "come$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_13::
    .string "The burden upon Arabia. In the\n"
    .string "forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O\l"
    .string "ye travelling companies of Dedanim.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_14::
    .string "The inhabitants of the land of Tema\n"
    .string "brought water to him that was\l"
    .string "thirsty, they prevented with their\l"
    .string "bread him that fled.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_15::
    .string "For they fled from the swords, from\n"
    .string "the drawn sword, and from the bent\l"
    .string "bow, and from the grievousness of war.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_16::
    .string "For thus hath the LORD said unto me,\n"
    .string "Within a year, according to the years\l"
    .string "of an hireling, and all the glory\l"
    .string "of Kedar shall fail:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_21_17::
    .string "And the residue of the number of\n"
    .string "archers, the mighty men of the\l"
    .string "children of Kedar, shall be\l"
    .string "diminished: for the LORD God of\l"
    .string "Israel hath spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_1::
    .string "The burden of the valley of vision.\n"
    .string "What aileth thee now, that thou art\l"
    .string "wholly gone up to the housetops?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_2::
    .string "Thou that art full of stirs, a\n"
    .string "tumultuous city, joyous city: thy\l"
    .string "slain men are not slain with the\l"
    .string "sword, nor dead in battle$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_3::
    .string "All thy rulers are fled together,\n"
    .string "they are bound by the archers: all\l"
    .string "that are found in thee are bound\l"
    .string "together, which have fled from far.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_4::
    .string "Therefore said I, Look away from me;\n"
    .string "I will weep bitterly, labour not\l"
    .string "to comfort me, because of the\l"
    .string "spoiling of the daughter of my\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_5::
    .string "For it is a day of trouble, and of\n"
    .string "treading down, and of perplexity by\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD of hosts in the valley\l"
    .string "of vision, breaking down the walls,\l"
    .string "and of crying to the mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_6::
    .string "And Elam bare the quiver with\n"
    .string "chariots of men and horsemen, and Kir\l"
    .string "uncovered the shield.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_7::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "thy choicest valleys shall be\l"
    .string "full of chariots, and the horsemen\l"
    .string "shall set themselves in array at\l"
    .string "the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_8::
    .string "And he discovered the covering of\n"
    .string "Judah, and thou didst look in that\l"
    .string "day to the armour of the house of the\l"
    .string "forest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_9::
    .string "Ye have seen also the breaches of\n"
    .string "the city of David, that they are\l"
    .string "many: and ye gathered together the\l"
    .string "waters of the lower pool.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_10::
    .string "And ye have numbered the houses of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, and the houses have ye\l"
    .string "broken down to fortify the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_11::
    .string "Ye made also a ditch between the\n"
    .string "two walls for the water of the old\l"
    .string "pool: but ye have not looked unto\l"
    .string "the maker thereof, neither had\l"
    .string "respect unto him that fashioned it\l"
    .string "long ago.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_12::
    .string "And in that day did the Lord GOD of\n"
    .string "hosts call to weeping, and to\l"
    .string "mourning, and to baldness, and to\l"
    .string "girding with sackcloth:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_13::
    .string "And behold joy and gladness,\n"
    .string "slaying oxen, and killing sheep,\l"
    .string "eating flesh, and drinking wine:\l"
    .string "let us eat and drink; for to morrow we\l"
    .string "shall die$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_14::
    .string "And it was revealed in mine ears by\n"
    .string "the LORD of hosts, Surely this\l"
    .string "iniquity shall not be purged from\l"
    .string "you till ye die, saith the Lord GOD\l"
    .string "of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_15::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts,\n"
    .string "Go, get thee unto this treasurer,\l"
    .string "even unto Shebna, which is over the\l"
    .string "house, and say,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_16::
    .string "What hast thou here? and whom hast\n"
    .string "thou here, that thou hast hewed thee\l"
    .string "out a sepulchre here, as he that\l"
    .string "heweth him out a sepulchre on high,\l"
    .string "and that graveth an habitation for\l"
    .string "himself in a rock?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_17::
    .string "Behold, the LORD will carry thee\n"
    .string "away with a mighty captivity, and\l"
    .string "will surely cover thee$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_18::
    .string "He will surely violently turn\n"
    .string "and toss thee like a ball into a\l"
    .string "large country: there shalt thou die,\l"
    .string "and there the chariots of thy glory\l"
    .string "shall be the shame of thy lord’s\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_19::
    .string "And I will drive thee from thy\n"
    .string "station, and from thy state shall he\l"
    .string "pull thee down.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_20::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that I will call my servant\l"
    .string "Eliakim the son of Hilkiah:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_21::
    .string "And I will clothe him with thy\n"
    .string "robe, and strengthen him with thy\l"
    .string "girdle, and I will commit thy\l"
    .string "government into his hand: and he\l"
    .string "shall be a father to the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the\l"
    .string "house of Judah$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_22::
    .string "And the key of the house of David\n"
    .string "will I lay upon his shoulder; so\l"
    .string "he shall open, and none shall\l"
    .string "shut; and he shall shut, and none\l"
    .string "shall open.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_23::
    .string "And I will fasten him as a nail in\n"
    .string "a sure place; and he shall be for a\l"
    .string "glorious throne to his father’s\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_24::
    .string "And they shall hang upon him all\n"
    .string "the glory of his father’s house, the\l"
    .string "offspring and the issue, all\l"
    .string "vessels of small quantity, from the\l"
    .string "vessels of cups, even to all the\l"
    .string "vessels of flagons.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_22_25::
    .string "In that day, saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, shall the nail that is\l"
    .string "fastened in the sure place be\l"
    .string "removed, and be cut down, and fall;\l"
    .string "and the burden that was upon it\l"
    .string "shall be cut off: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_1::
    .string "The burden of Tyre. Howl, ye ships\n"
    .string "of Tarshish; for it is laid waste, so\l"
    .string "that there is no house, no entering\l"
    .string "in: from the land of Chittim it is\l"
    .string "revealed to them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_2::
    .string "Be still, ye inhabitants of the\n"
    .string "isle; thou whom the merchants of\l"
    .string "Zidon, that pass over the sea, have\l"
    .string "replenished.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_3::
    .string "And by great waters the seed of\n"
    .string "Sihor, the harvest of the river, is\l"
    .string "her revenue; and she is a mart of\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_4::
    .string "Be thou ashamed, O Zidon: for the\n"
    .string "sea hath spoken, even the strength\l"
    .string "of the sea, saying, I travail not,\l"
    .string "nor bring forth children, neither do\l"
    .string "I nourish up young men, nor bring up\l"
    .string "virgins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_5::
    .string "As at the report concerning Egypt,\n"
    .string "so shall they be sorely pained at\l"
    .string "the report of Tyre.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_6::
    .string "Pass ye over to Tarshish; howl, ye\n"
    .string "inhabitants of the isle.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_7::
    .string "Is this your joyous city, whose\n"
    .string "antiquity is of ancient days? her own\l"
    .string "feet shall carry her afar off to\l"
    .string "sojourn.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_8::
    .string "Who hath taken this counsel against\n"
    .string "Tyre, the crowning city, whose\l"
    .string "merchants are princes, whose\l"
    .string "traffickers are the honourable of\l"
    .string "the earth?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_9::
    .string "The LORD of hosts hath purposed it,\n"
    .string "to stain the pride of all glory,\l"
    .string "and to bring into contempt all the\l"
    .string "honourable of the earth$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_10::
    .string "Pass through thy land as a river, O\n"
    .string "daughter of Tarshish: there is no\l"
    .string "more strength.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_11::
    .string "He stretched out his hand over the\n"
    .string "sea, he shook the kingdoms: the LORD\l"
    .string "hath given a commandment against the\l"
    .string "merchant city, to destroy the strong\l"
    .string "holds thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_12::
    .string "And he said, Thou shalt no more\n"
    .string "rejoice, O thou oppressed virgin,\l"
    .string "daughter of Zidon: arise, pass over\l"
    .string "to Chittim; there also shalt thou\l"
    .string "have no rest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_13::
    .string "Behold the land of the Chaldeans;\n"
    .string "this people was not, till the\l"
    .string "Assyrian founded it for them that\l"
    .string "dwell in the wilderness: they set\l"
    .string "up the towers thereof, they raised\l"
    .string "up the palaces thereof; and he\l"
    .string "brought it to ruin.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_14::
    .string "Howl, ye ships of Tarshish: for\n"
    .string "your strength is laid waste.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_15::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that Tyre shall be forgotten\l"
    .string "seventy years, according to the days\l"
    .string "of one king: after the end of seventy\l"
    .string "years shall Tyre sing as an harlot.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_16::
    .string "Take an harp, go about the city,\n"
    .string "thou harlot that hast been\l"
    .string "forgotten; make sweet melody, sing\l"
    .string "many songs, that thou mayest be\l"
    .string "remembered.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_17::
    .string "And it shall come to pass after\n"
    .string "the end of seventy years, that the\l"
    .string "LORD will visit Tyre, and she\l"
    .string "shall turn to her hire, and shall\l"
    .string "commit fornication with all the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of the world upon the face\l"
    .string "of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_23_18::
    .string "And her merchandise and her hire\n"
    .string "shall be holiness to the LORD: it\l"
    .string "shall not be treasured nor laid\l"
    .string "up; for her merchandise shall be\l"
    .string "for them that dwell before the LORD,\l"
    .string "to eat sufficiently, and for\l"
    .string "durable clothing.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_1::
    .string "Behold, the LORD maketh the earth\n"
    .string "empty, and maketh it waste, and\l"
    .string "turneth it upside down, and\l"
    .string "scattereth abroad the inhabitants\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_2::
    .string "And it shall be, as with the\n"
    .string "people, so with the priest; as with\l"
    .string "the servant, so with his master; as\l"
    .string "with the maid, so with her mistress;\l"
    .string "as with the buyer, so with the\l"
    .string "seller; as with the lender, so with\l"
    .string "the borrower; as with the taker of\l"
    .string "usury, so with the giver of usury to\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_3::
    .string "The land shall be utterly\n"
    .string "emptied, and utterly spoiled: for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath spoken this word.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_4::
    .string "The earth mourneth and fadeth away,\n"
    .string "the world languisheth and fadeth\l"
    .string "away, the haughty people of the\l"
    .string "earth do languish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_5::
    .string "The earth also is defiled under\n"
    .string "the inhabitants thereof; because\l"
    .string "they have transgressed the laws,\l"
    .string "changed the ordinance, broken the\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_6::
    .string "Therefore hath the curse devoured\n"
    .string "the earth, and they that dwell\l"
    .string "therein are desolate: therefore the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth are burned,\l"
    .string "and few men left.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_7::
    .string "The new wine mourneth, the vine\n"
    .string "languisheth, all the merryhearted\l"
    .string "do sigh.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_8::
    .string "The mirth of tabrets ceaseth, the\n"
    .string "noise of them that rejoice endeth,\l"
    .string "the joy of the harp ceaseth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_9::
    .string "They shall not drink wine with a\n"
    .string "song; strong drink shall be bitter\l"
    .string "to them that drink it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_10::
    .string "The city of confusion is broken\n"
    .string "down: every house is shut up, that no\l"
    .string "man may come in.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_11::
    .string "There is a crying for wine in the\n"
    .string "streets; all joy is darkened, the\l"
    .string "mirth of the land is gone.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_12::
    .string "In the city is left desolation, and\n"
    .string "the gate is smitten with destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_13::
    .string "When thus it shall be in the midst\n"
    .string "of the land among the people,\l"
    .string "there shall be as the shaking of an\l"
    .string "olive tree, and as the gleaning\l"
    .string "grapes when the vintage is done.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_14::
    .string "They shall lift up their voice,\n"
    .string "they shall sing for the majesty of\l"
    .string "the LORD, they shall cry aloud from\l"
    .string "the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_15::
    .string "Wherefore glorify ye the LORD in\n"
    .string "the fires, even the name of the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel in the isles of the\l"
    .string "sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_16::
    .string "From the uttermost part of the\n"
    .string "earth have we heard songs, even\l"
    .string "glory to the righteous. But I said,\l"
    .string "My leanness, my leanness, woe unto\l"
    .string "me! the treacherous dealers have\l"
    .string "dealt treacherously; yea, the\l"
    .string "treacherous dealers have dealt very\l"
    .string "treacherously.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_17::
    .string "Fear, and the pit, and the snare,\n"
    .string "are upon thee, O inhabitant of the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_18::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that he\n"
    .string "who fleeth from the noise of the\l"
    .string "fear shall fall into the pit; and\l"
    .string "he that cometh up out of the midst of\l"
    .string "the pit shall be taken in the\l"
    .string "snare: for the windows from on high\l"
    .string "are open, and the foundations of the\l"
    .string "earth do shake.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_19::
    .string "The earth is utterly broken down,\n"
    .string "the earth is clean dissolved, the\l"
    .string "earth is moved exceedingly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_20::
    .string "The earth shall reel to and fro\n"
    .string "like a drunkard, and shall be\l"
    .string "removed like a cottage; and the\l"
    .string "transgression thereof shall be\l"
    .string "heavy upon it; and it shall fall,\l"
    .string "and not rise again.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_21::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the LORD shall punish the\l"
    .string "host of the high ones that are on\l"
    .string "high, and the kings of the earth upon\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_22::
    .string "And they shall be gathered\n"
    .string "together, as prisoners are gathered\l"
    .string "in the pit, and shall be shut up in\l"
    .string "the prison, and after many days\l"
    .string "shall they be visited.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_24_23::
    .string "Then the moon shall be confounded,\n"
    .string "and the sun ashamed, when the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts shall reign in mount Zion, and\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem, and before his\l"
    .string "ancients gloriously.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_1::
    .string "O Lord, thou art my God; I will\n"
    .string "exalt thee, I will praise thy\l"
    .string "name; for thou hast done wonderful\l"
    .string "things; thy counsels of old are\l"
    .string "faithfulness and truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_2::
    .string "For thou hast made of a city an\n"
    .string "heap; of a defenced city a ruin: a\l"
    .string "palace of strangers to be no city; it\l"
    .string "shall never be built.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_3::
    .string "Therefore shall the strong\n"
    .string "people glorify thee, the city of\l"
    .string "the terrible nations shall fear\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_4::
    .string "For thou hast been a strength to the\n"
    .string "poor, a strength to the needy in his\l"
    .string "distress, a refuge from the storm, a\l"
    .string "shadow from the heat, when the blast\l"
    .string "of the terrible ones is as a storm\l"
    .string "against the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_5::
    .string "Thou shalt bring down the noise of\n"
    .string "strangers, as the heat in a dry\l"
    .string "place; even the heat with the shadow\l"
    .string "of a cloud: the branch of the\l"
    .string "terrible ones shall be brought low.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_6::
    .string "And in this mountain shall the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts make unto all\l"
    .string "people a feast of fat things, a\l"
    .string "feast of wines on the lees, of fat\l"
    .string "things full of marrow, of wines on\l"
    .string "the lees well refined.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_7::
    .string "And he will destroy in this\n"
    .string "mountain the face of the covering\l"
    .string "cast over all people, and the\l"
    .string "vail that is spread over all\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_8::
    .string "He will swallow up death in\n"
    .string "victory; and the Lord GOD will wipe\l"
    .string "away tears from off all faces; and\l"
    .string "the rebuke of his people shall he\l"
    .string "take away from off all the earth:\l"
    .string "for the LORD hath spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_9::
    .string "And it shall be said in that day,\n"
    .string "Lo, this is our God; we have waited\l"
    .string "for him, and he will save us: this\l"
    .string "is the LORD; we have waited for him,\l"
    .string "we will be glad and rejoice in his\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_10::
    .string "For in this mountain shall the\n"
    .string "hand of the LORD rest, and Moab\l"
    .string "shall be trodden down under him,\l"
    .string "even as straw is trodden down for the\l"
    .string "dunghill.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_11::
    .string "And he shall spread forth his\n"
    .string "hands in the midst of them, as he that\l"
    .string "swimmeth spreadeth forth his hands\l"
    .string "to swim: and he shall bring down\l"
    .string "their pride together with the\l"
    .string "spoils of their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_25_12::
    .string "And the fortress of the high fort of\n"
    .string "thy walls shall he bring down, lay\l"
    .string "low, and bring to the ground, even to\l"
    .string "the dust.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_1::
    .string "In that day shall this song be sung\n"
    .string "in the land of Judah; We have a\l"
    .string "strong city; salvation will God\l"
    .string "appoint for walls and bulwarks.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_2::
    .string "Open ye the gates, that the\n"
    .string "righteous nation which keepeth the\l"
    .string "truth may enter in.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_3::
    .string "Thou wilt keep him in perfect\n"
    .string "peace, whose mind is stayed on thee:\l"
    .string "because he trusteth in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_4::
    .string "Trust ye in the LORD for ever: for in\n"
    .string "the LORD JEHOVAH is everlasting\l"
    .string "strength:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_5::
    .string "For he bringeth down them that\n"
    .string "dwell on high; the lofty city, he\l"
    .string "layeth it low; he layeth it low,\l"
    .string "even to the ground; he bringeth it\l"
    .string "even to the dust$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_6::
    .string "The foot shall tread it down, even\n"
    .string "the feet of the poor, and the steps\l"
    .string "of the needy.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_7::
    .string "The way of the just is uprightness:\n"
    .string "thou, most upright, dost weigh the\l"
    .string "path of the just.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_8::
    .string "Yea, in the way of thy judgments, O\n"
    .string "LORD, have we waited for thee; the\l"
    .string "desire of our soul is to thy name,\l"
    .string "and to the remembrance of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_9::
    .string "With my soul have I desired thee in\n"
    .string "the night; yea, with my spirit\l"
    .string "within me will I seek thee early:\l"
    .string "for when thy judgments are in the\l"
    .string "earth, the inhabitants of the world\l"
    .string "will learn righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_10::
    .string "Let favour be shewed to the wicked,\n"
    .string "yet will he not learn\l"
    .string "righteousness: in the land of\l"
    .string "uprightness will he deal\l"
    .string "unjustly, and will not behold the\l"
    .string "majesty of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_11::
    .string "LORD, when thy hand is lifted up,\n"
    .string "they will not see: but they shall\l"
    .string "see, and be ashamed for their envy at\l"
    .string "the people; yea, the fire of thine\l"
    .string "enemies shall devour them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_12::
    .string "LORD, thou wilt ordain peace for\n"
    .string "us: for thou also hast wrought all\l"
    .string "our works in us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_13::
    .string "O LORD our God, other lords beside\n"
    .string "thee have had dominion over us: but\l"
    .string "by thee only will we make mention\l"
    .string "of thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_14::
    .string "They are dead, they shall not\n"
    .string "live; they are deceased, they shall\l"
    .string "not rise: therefore hast thou visited\l"
    .string "and destroyed them, and made all\l"
    .string "their memory to perish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_15::
    .string "Thou hast increased the nation, O\n"
    .string "LORD, thou hast increased the nation:\l"
    .string "thou art glorified: thou hadst\l"
    .string "removed it far unto all the ends of\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_16::
    .string "LORD, in trouble have they visited\n"
    .string "thee, they poured out a prayer when\l"
    .string "thy chastening was upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_17::
    .string "Like as a woman with child, that\n"
    .string "draweth near the time of her\l"
    .string "delivery, is in pain, and crieth out\l"
    .string "in her pangs; so have we been in thy\l"
    .string "sight, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_18::
    .string "We have been with child, we have\n"
    .string "been in pain, we have as it were\l"
    .string "brought forth wind; we have not\l"
    .string "wrought any deliverance in the\l"
    .string "earth; neither have the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of the world fallen.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_19::
    .string "Thy dead men shall live, together\n"
    .string "with my dead body shall they arise.\l"
    .string "Awake and sing, ye that dwell in\l"
    .string "dust: for thy dew is as the dew of\l"
    .string "herbs, and the earth shall cast out\l"
    .string "the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_20::
    .string "Come, my people, enter thou into\n"
    .string "thy chambers, and shut thy doors\l"
    .string "about thee: hide thyself as it were\l"
    .string "for a little moment, until the\l"
    .string "indignation be overpast.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_26_21::
    .string "For, behold, the LORD cometh out of\n"
    .string "his place to punish the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth for their\l"
    .string "iniquity: the earth also shall\l"
    .string "disclose her blood, and shall no\l"
    .string "more cover her slain.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_1::
    .string "In that day the LORD with his sore\n"
    .string "and great and strong sword shall\l"
    .string "punish leviathan the piercing\l"
    .string "serpent, even leviathan that\l"
    .string "crooked serpent; and he shall slay\l"
    .string "the dragon that is in the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_2::
    .string "In that day sing ye unto her, A\n"
    .string "vineyard of red wine.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_3::
    .string "I the LORD do keep it; I will water\n"
    .string "it every moment: lest any hurt it, I\l"
    .string "will keep it night and day.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_4::
    .string "Fury is not in me: who would set the\n"
    .string "briers and thorns against me in\l"
    .string "battle? I would go through them, I\l"
    .string "would burn them together.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_5::
    .string "Or let him take hold of my\n"
    .string "strength, that he may make peace\l"
    .string "with me; and he shall make peace\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_6::
    .string "He shall cause them that come of\n"
    .string "Jacob to take root: Israel shall\l"
    .string "blossom and bud, and fill the face\l"
    .string "of the world with fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_7::
    .string "Hath he smitten him, as he smote\n"
    .string "those that smote him? or is he slain\l"
    .string "according to the slaughter of them\l"
    .string "that are slain by him?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_8::
    .string "In measure, when it shooteth forth,\n"
    .string "thou wilt debate with it: he stayeth\l"
    .string "his rough wind in the day of the east\l"
    .string "wind$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_9::
    .string "By this therefore shall the\n"
    .string "iniquity of Jacob be purged; and\l"
    .string "this is all the fruit to take away\l"
    .string "his sin; when he maketh all the\l"
    .string "stones of the altar as chalkstones\l"
    .string "that are beaten in sunder, the groves\l"
    .string "and images shall not stand up.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_10::
    .string "Yet the defenced city shall be\n"
    .string "desolate, and the habitation\l"
    .string "forsaken, and left like a\l"
    .string "wilderness: there shall the calf\l"
    .string "feed, and there shall he lie down,\l"
    .string "and consume the branches thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_11::
    .string "When the boughs thereof are\n"
    .string "withered, they shall be broken off:\l"
    .string "the women come, and set them on fire:\l"
    .string "for it is a people of no\l"
    .string "understanding: therefore he that\l"
    .string "made them will not have mercy on\l"
    .string "them, and he that formed them will\l"
    .string "shew them no favour.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_12::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the LORD shall beat off\l"
    .string "from the channel of the river unto\l"
    .string "the stream of Egypt, and ye shall\l"
    .string "be gathered one by one, O ye children\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_27_13::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the great trumpet shall\l"
    .string "be blown, and they shall come which\l"
    .string "were ready to perish in the land of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and the outcasts in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, and shall worship\l"
    .string "the LORD in the holy mount at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_1::
    .string "Woe to the crown of pride, to the\n"
    .string "drunkards of Ephraim, whose\l"
    .string "glorious beauty is a fading flower,\l"
    .string "which are on the head of the fat\l"
    .string "valleys of them that are overcome\l"
    .string "with wine!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_2::
    .string "Behold, the Lord hath a mighty and\n"
    .string "strong one, which as a tempest of\l"
    .string "hail and a destroying storm, as a\l"
    .string "flood of mighty waters overflowing,\l"
    .string "shall cast down to the earth with\l"
    .string "the hand$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_3::
    .string "The crown of pride, the drunkards\n"
    .string "of Ephraim, shall be trodden under\l"
    .string "feet:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_4::
    .string "And the glorious beauty, which is\n"
    .string "on the head of the fat valley,\l"
    .string "shall be a fading flower, and as\l"
    .string "the hasty fruit before the summer;\l"
    .string "which when he that looketh upon it\l"
    .string "seeth, while it is yet in his hand he\l"
    .string "eateth it up$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_5::
    .string "In that day shall the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "be for a crown of glory, and for a\l"
    .string "diadem of beauty, unto the residue of\l"
    .string "his people,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_6::
    .string "And for a spirit of judgment to him\n"
    .string "that sitteth in judgment, and for\l"
    .string "strength to them that turn the\l"
    .string "battle to the gate$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_7::
    .string "But they also have erred through\n"
    .string "wine, and through strong drink are\l"
    .string "out of the way; the priest and the\l"
    .string "prophet have erred through strong\l"
    .string "drink, they are swallowed up of\l"
    .string "wine, they are out of the way through\l"
    .string "strong drink; they err in vision,\l"
    .string "they stumble in judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_8::
    .string "For all tables are full of vomit\n"
    .string "and filthiness, so that there is no\l"
    .string "place clean.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_9::
    .string "Whom shall he teach knowledge? and\n"
    .string "whom shall he make to understand\l"
    .string "doctrine? them that are weaned from\l"
    .string "the milk, and drawn from the breasts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_10::
    .string "For precept must be upon\n"
    .string "precept, precept upon precept;\l"
    .string "line upon line, line upon line;\l"
    .string "here a little, and there a little:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_11::
    .string "For with stammering lips and\n"
    .string "another tongue will he speak to\l"
    .string "this people$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_12::
    .string "To whom he said, This is the rest\n"
    .string "wherewith ye may cause the weary to\l"
    .string "rest; and this is the refreshing: yet\l"
    .string "they would not hear.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_13::
    .string "But the word of the LORD was unto\n"
    .string "them precept upon precept,\l"
    .string "precept upon precept; line upon\l"
    .string "line, line upon line; here a\l"
    .string "little, and there a little; that\l"
    .string "they might go, and fall backward,\l"
    .string "and be broken, and snared, and taken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_14::
    .string "Wherefore hear the word of the LORD,\n"
    .string "ye scornful men, that rule this\l"
    .string "people which is in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_15::
    .string "Because ye have said, We have made a\n"
    .string "covenant with death, and with hell\l"
    .string "are we at agreement; when the\l"
    .string "overflowing scourge shall pass\l"
    .string "through, it shall not come unto us:\l"
    .string "for we have made lies our refuge, and\l"
    .string "under falsehood have we hid\l"
    .string "ourselves:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_16::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD,\n"
    .string "Behold, I lay in Zion for a\l"
    .string "foundation a stone, a tried stone, a\l"
    .string "precious corner stone, a sure\l"
    .string "foundation: he that believeth\l"
    .string "shall not make haste$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_17::
    .string "Judgment also will I lay to the\n"
    .string "line, and righteousness to the\l"
    .string "plummet: and the hail shall sweep\l"
    .string "away the refuge of lies, and the\l"
    .string "waters shall overflow the hiding\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_18::
    .string "And your covenant with death shall\n"
    .string "be disannulled, and your agreement\l"
    .string "with hell shall not stand; when\l"
    .string "the overflowing scourge shall\l"
    .string "pass through, then ye shall be\l"
    .string "trodden down by it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_19::
    .string "From the time that it goeth forth it\n"
    .string "shall take you: for morning by\l"
    .string "morning shall it pass over, by day\l"
    .string "and by night: and it shall be a\l"
    .string "vexation only to understand the\l"
    .string "report.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_20::
    .string "For the bed is shorter than that a\n"
    .string "man can stretch himself on it: and\l"
    .string "the covering narrower than that he\l"
    .string "can wrap himself in it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_21::
    .string "For the LORD shall rise up as in\n"
    .string "mount Perazim, he shall be wroth as\l"
    .string "in the valley of Gibeon, that he may\l"
    .string "do his work, his strange work; and\l"
    .string "bring to pass his act, his strange\l"
    .string "act.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_22::
    .string "Now therefore be ye not mockers,\n"
    .string "lest your bands be made strong: for I\l"
    .string "have heard from the Lord GOD of hosts\l"
    .string "a consumption, even determined upon\l"
    .string "the whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_23::
    .string "Give ye ear, and hear my voice;\n"
    .string "hearken, and hear my speech.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_24::
    .string "Doth the plowman plow all day to\n"
    .string "sow? doth he open and break the\l"
    .string "clods of his ground?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_25::
    .string "When he hath made plain the face\n"
    .string "thereof, doth he not cast abroad the\l"
    .string "fitches, and scatter the cummin, and\l"
    .string "cast in the principal wheat and the\l"
    .string "appointed barley and the rie in\l"
    .string "their place?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_26::
    .string "For his God doth instruct him to\n"
    .string "discretion, and doth teach him$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_27::
    .string "For the fitches are not threshed\n"
    .string "with a threshing instrument, neither\l"
    .string "is a cart wheel turned about upon\l"
    .string "the cummin; but the fitches are\l"
    .string "beaten out with a staff, and the\l"
    .string "cummin with a rod.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_28::
    .string "Bread corn is bruised; because he\n"
    .string "will not ever be threshing it, nor\l"
    .string "break it with the wheel of his cart,\l"
    .string "nor bruise it with his horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_28_29::
    .string "This also cometh forth from the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts, which is wonderful in\l"
    .string "counsel, and excellent in working.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_1::
    .string "Woe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city\n"
    .string "where David dwelt! add ye year to\l"
    .string "year; let them kill sacrifices.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_2::
    .string "Yet I will distress Ariel, and\n"
    .string "there shall be heaviness and\l"
    .string "sorrow: and it shall be unto me as\l"
    .string "Ariel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_3::
    .string "And I will camp against thee round\n"
    .string "about, and will lay siege against\l"
    .string "thee with a mount, and I will raise\l"
    .string "forts against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_4::
    .string "And thou shalt be brought down, and\n"
    .string "shalt speak out of the ground, and\l"
    .string "thy speech shall be low out of the\l"
    .string "dust, and thy voice shall be, as of\l"
    .string "one that hath a familiar spirit, out\l"
    .string "of the ground, and thy speech shall\l"
    .string "whisper out of the dust.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_5::
    .string "Moreover the multitude of thy\n"
    .string "strangers shall be like small\l"
    .string "dust, and the multitude of the\l"
    .string "terrible ones shall be as chaff\l"
    .string "that passeth away: yea, it shall be\l"
    .string "at an instant suddenly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_6::
    .string "Thou shalt be visited of the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts with thunder, and with\l"
    .string "earthquake, and great noise, with\l"
    .string "storm and tempest, and the flame of\l"
    .string "devouring fire.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_7::
    .string "And the multitude of all the\n"
    .string "nations that fight against Ariel,\l"
    .string "even all that fight against her and\l"
    .string "her munition, and that distress her,\l"
    .string "shall be as a dream of a night\l"
    .string "vision.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_8::
    .string "It shall even be as when an hungry\n"
    .string "man dreameth, and, behold, he\l"
    .string "eateth; but he awaketh, and his soul\l"
    .string "is empty: or as when a thirsty man\l"
    .string "dreameth, and, behold, he drinketh;\l"
    .string "but he awaketh, and, behold, he is\l"
    .string "faint, and his soul hath appetite:\l"
    .string "so shall the multitude of all the\l"
    .string "nations be, that fight against mount\l"
    .string "Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_9::
    .string "Stay yourselves, and wonder; cry ye\n"
    .string "out, and cry: they are drunken, but\l"
    .string "not with wine; they stagger, but not\l"
    .string "with strong drink.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_10::
    .string "For the LORD hath poured out upon\n"
    .string "you the spirit of deep sleep, and\l"
    .string "hath closed your eyes: the prophets\l"
    .string "and your rulers, the seers hath he\l"
    .string "covered.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_11::
    .string "And the vision of all is become\n"
    .string "unto you as the words of a book that\l"
    .string "is sealed, which men deliver to one\l"
    .string "that is learned, saying, Read this, I\l"
    .string "pray thee: and he saith, I cannot; for\l"
    .string "it is sealed:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_12::
    .string "And the book is delivered to him\n"
    .string "that is not learned, saying, Read\l"
    .string "this, I pray thee: and he saith, I am\l"
    .string "not learned$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_13::
    .string "Wherefore the Lord said, Forasmuch\n"
    .string "as this people draw near me with\l"
    .string "their mouth, and with their lips do\l"
    .string "honour me, but have removed their\l"
    .string "heart far from me, and their fear\l"
    .string "toward me is taught by the precept\l"
    .string "of men:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_14::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will proceed\n"
    .string "to do a marvellous work among this\l"
    .string "people, even a marvellous work and\l"
    .string "a wonder: for the wisdom of their\l"
    .string "wise men shall perish, and the\l"
    .string "understanding of their prudent men\l"
    .string "shall be hid$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_15::
    .string "Woe unto them that seek deep to\n"
    .string "hide their counsel from the LORD,\l"
    .string "and their works are in the dark, and\l"
    .string "they say, Who seeth us? and who\l"
    .string "knoweth us?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_16::
    .string "Surely your turning of things\n"
    .string "upside down shall be esteemed as\l"
    .string "the potter’s clay: for shall the\l"
    .string "work say of him that made it, He made\l"
    .string "me not? or shall the thing framed\l"
    .string "say of him that framed it, He had no\l"
    .string "understanding?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_17::
    .string "Is it not yet a very little while,\n"
    .string "and Lebanon shall be turned into a\l"
    .string "fruitful field, and the fruitful\l"
    .string "field shall be esteemed as a\l"
    .string "forest?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_18::
    .string "And in that day shall the deaf hear\n"
    .string "the words of the book, and the eyes of\l"
    .string "the blind shall see out of\l"
    .string "obscurity, and out of darkness$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_19::
    .string "The meek also shall increase\n"
    .string "their joy in the LORD, and the poor\l"
    .string "among men shall rejoice in the Holy\l"
    .string "One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_20::
    .string "For the terrible one is brought to\n"
    .string "nought, and the scorner is consumed,\l"
    .string "and all that watch for iniquity are\l"
    .string "cut off:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_21::
    .string "That make a man an offender for a\n"
    .string "word, and lay a snare for him that\l"
    .string "reproveth in the gate, and turn\l"
    .string "aside the just for a thing of nought$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_22::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD, who\n"
    .string "redeemed Abraham, concerning the\l"
    .string "house of Jacob, Jacob shall not now\l"
    .string "be ashamed, neither shall his face\l"
    .string "now wax pale.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_23::
    .string "But when he seeth his children, the\n"
    .string "work of mine hands, in the midst of\l"
    .string "him, they shall sanctify my name,\l"
    .string "and sanctify the Holy One of Jacob,\l"
    .string "and shall fear the God of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_29_24::
    .string "They also that erred in spirit\n"
    .string "shall come to understanding, and\l"
    .string "they that murmured shall learn\l"
    .string "doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_1::
    .string "Woe to the rebellious children,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that take counsel,\l"
    .string "but not of me; and that cover with a\l"
    .string "covering, but not of my spirit, that\l"
    .string "they may add sin to sin:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_2::
    .string "That walk to go down into Egypt,\n"
    .string "and have not asked at my mouth; to\l"
    .string "strengthen themselves in the\l"
    .string "strength of Pharaoh, and to trust in\l"
    .string "the shadow of Egypt!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_3::
    .string "Therefore shall the strength of\n"
    .string "Pharaoh be your shame, and the trust\l"
    .string "in the shadow of Egypt your confusion$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_4::
    .string "For his princes were at Zoan, and\n"
    .string "his ambassadors came to Hanes.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_5::
    .string "They were all ashamed of a\n"
    .string "people that could not profit them,\l"
    .string "nor be an help nor profit, but a\l"
    .string "shame, and also a reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_6::
    .string "The burden of the beasts of the\n"
    .string "south: into the land of trouble and\l"
    .string "anguish, from whence come the young\l"
    .string "and old lion, the viper and fiery\l"
    .string "flying serpent, they will carry\l"
    .string "their riches upon the shoulders of\l"
    .string "young asses, and their treasures\l"
    .string "upon the bunches of camels, to a\l"
    .string "people that shall not profit them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_7::
    .string "For the Egyptians shall help in\n"
    .string "vain, and to no purpose: therefore\l"
    .string "have I cried concerning this, Their\l"
    .string "strength is to sit still.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_8::
    .string "Now go, write it before them in a\n"
    .string "table, and note it in a book, that it\l"
    .string "may be for the time to come for ever\l"
    .string "and ever:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_9::
    .string "That this is a rebellious\n"
    .string "people, lying children, children\l"
    .string "that will not hear the law of the\l"
    .string "LORD:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_10::
    .string "Which say to the seers, See not; and\n"
    .string "to the prophets, Prophesy not unto\l"
    .string "us right things, speak unto us\l"
    .string "smooth things, prophesy deceits:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_11::
    .string "Get you out of the way, turn aside\n"
    .string "out of the path, cause the Holy One\l"
    .string "of Israel to cease from before us$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_12::
    .string "Wherefore thus saith the Holy One\n"
    .string "of Israel, Because ye despise this\l"
    .string "word, and trust in oppression and\l"
    .string "perverseness, and stay thereon:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_13::
    .string "Therefore this iniquity shall be\n"
    .string "to you as a breach ready to fall,\l"
    .string "swelling out in a high wall, whose\l"
    .string "breaking cometh suddenly at an\l"
    .string "instant$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_14::
    .string "And he shall break it as the\n"
    .string "breaking of the potters’ vessel\l"
    .string "that is broken in pieces; he shall\l"
    .string "not spare: so that there shall not\l"
    .string "be found in the bursting of it a\l"
    .string "sherd to take fire from the hearth,\l"
    .string "or to take water withal out of the\l"
    .string "pit.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_15::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD, the\n"
    .string "Holy One of Israel; In returning and\l"
    .string "rest shall ye be saved; in quietness\l"
    .string "and in confidence shall be your\l"
    .string "strength: and ye would not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_16::
    .string "But ye said, No; for we will flee\n"
    .string "upon horses; therefore shall ye\l"
    .string "flee: and, We will ride upon the\l"
    .string "swift; therefore shall they that\l"
    .string "pursue you be swift.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_17::
    .string "One thousand shall flee at the\n"
    .string "rebuke of one; at the rebuke of five\l"
    .string "shall ye flee: till ye be left as\l"
    .string "a beacon upon the top of a mountain,\l"
    .string "and as an ensign on an hill.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_18::
    .string "And therefore will the LORD wait,\n"
    .string "that he may be gracious unto you, and\l"
    .string "therefore will he be exalted, that\l"
    .string "he may have mercy upon you: for the\l"
    .string "LORD is a God of judgment: blessed\l"
    .string "are all they that wait for him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_19::
    .string "For the people shall dwell in\n"
    .string "Zion at Jerusalem: thou shalt weep\l"
    .string "no more: he will be very gracious\l"
    .string "unto thee at the voice of thy cry;\l"
    .string "when he shall hear it, he will\l"
    .string "answer thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_20::
    .string "And though the Lord give you the\n"
    .string "bread of adversity, and the water of\l"
    .string "affliction, yet shall not thy\l"
    .string "teachers be removed into a corner any\l"
    .string "more, but thine eyes shall see thy\l"
    .string "teachers:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_21::
    .string "And thine ears shall hear a word\n"
    .string "behind thee, saying, This is the way,\l"
    .string "walk ye in it, when ye turn to the\l"
    .string "right hand, and when ye turn to the\l"
    .string "left$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_22::
    .string "Ye shall defile also the covering\n"
    .string "of thy graven images of silver, and\l"
    .string "the ornament of thy molten images of\l"
    .string "gold: thou shalt cast them away as a\l"
    .string "menstruous cloth; thou shalt say\l"
    .string "unto it, Get thee hence.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_23::
    .string "Then shall he give the rain of thy\n"
    .string "seed, that thou shalt sow the ground\l"
    .string "withal; and bread of the increase of\l"
    .string "the earth, and it shall be fat and\l"
    .string "plenteous: in that day shall thy\l"
    .string "cattle feed in large pastures.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_24::
    .string "The oxen likewise and the young\n"
    .string "asses that ear the ground shall eat\l"
    .string "clean provender, which hath been\l"
    .string "winnowed with the shovel and with\l"
    .string "the fan.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_25::
    .string "And there shall be upon every high\n"
    .string "mountain, and upon every high hill,\l"
    .string "rivers and streams of waters in the\l"
    .string "day of the great slaughter, when the\l"
    .string "towers fall.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_26::
    .string "Moreover the light of the moon\n"
    .string "shall be as the light of the sun,\l"
    .string "and the light of the sun shall be\l"
    .string "sevenfold, as the light of seven\l"
    .string "days, in the day that the LORD\l"
    .string "bindeth up the breach of his\l"
    .string "people, and healeth the stroke of\l"
    .string "their wound.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_27::
    .string "Behold, the name of the LORD cometh\n"
    .string "from far, burning with his anger, and\l"
    .string "the burden thereof is heavy: his\l"
    .string "lips are full of indignation, and\l"
    .string "his tongue as a devouring fire:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_28::
    .string "And his breath, as an overflowing\n"
    .string "stream, shall reach to the midst of\l"
    .string "the neck, to sift the nations with\l"
    .string "the sieve of vanity: and there shall\l"
    .string "be a bridle in the jaws of the\l"
    .string "people, causing them to err$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_29::
    .string "Ye shall have a song, as in the\n"
    .string "night when a holy solemnity is\l"
    .string "kept; and gladness of heart, as when\l"
    .string "one goeth with a pipe to come into\l"
    .string "the mountain of the LORD, to the\l"
    .string "mighty One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_30::
    .string "And the LORD shall cause his\n"
    .string "glorious voice to be heard, and\l"
    .string "shall shew the lighting down of his\l"
    .string "arm, with the indignation of his\l"
    .string "anger, and with the flame of a\l"
    .string "devouring fire, with scattering, and\l"
    .string "tempest, and hailstones.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_31::
    .string "For through the voice of the LORD\n"
    .string "shall the Assyrian be beaten down,\l"
    .string "which smote with a rod.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_32::
    .string "And in every place where the\n"
    .string "grounded staff shall pass, which\l"
    .string "the LORD shall lay upon him, it\l"
    .string "shall be with tabrets and harps:\l"
    .string "and in battles of shaking will he\l"
    .string "fight with it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_30_33::
    .string "For Tophet is ordained of old; yea,\n"
    .string "for the king it is prepared; he hath\l"
    .string "made it deep and large: the pile\l"
    .string "thereof is fire and much wood; the\l"
    .string "breath of the LORD, like a stream of\l"
    .string "brimstone, doth kindle it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_1::
    .string "Woe to them that go down to Egypt\n"
    .string "for help; and stay on horses, and\l"
    .string "trust in chariots, because they are\l"
    .string "many; and in horsemen, because they\l"
    .string "are very strong; but they look not\l"
    .string "unto the Holy One of Israel, neither\l"
    .string "seek the LORD!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_2::
    .string "Yet he also is wise, and will\n"
    .string "bring evil, and will not call back\l"
    .string "his words: but will arise against\l"
    .string "the house of the evildoers, and\l"
    .string "against the help of them that work\l"
    .string "iniquity$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_3::
    .string "Now the Egyptians are men, and not\n"
    .string "God; and their horses flesh, and not\l"
    .string "spirit. When the LORD shall stretch\l"
    .string "out his hand, both he that helpeth\l"
    .string "shall fall, and he that is holpen\l"
    .string "shall fall down, and they all\l"
    .string "shall fail together.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_4::
    .string "For thus hath the LORD spoken unto\n"
    .string "me, Like as the lion and the young\l"
    .string "lion roaring on his prey, when a\l"
    .string "multitude of shepherds is called\l"
    .string "forth against him, he will not be\l"
    .string "afraid of their voice, nor abase\l"
    .string "himself for the noise of them: so\l"
    .string "shall the LORD of hosts come down to\l"
    .string "fight for mount Zion, and for the\l"
    .string "hill thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_5::
    .string "As birds flying, so will the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts defend Jerusalem; defending\l"
    .string "also he will deliver it; and\l"
    .string "passing over he will preserve it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_6::
    .string "Turn ye unto him from whom the\n"
    .string "children of Israel have deeply\l"
    .string "revolted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_7::
    .string "For in that day every man shall\n"
    .string "cast away his idols of silver, and\l"
    .string "his idols of gold, which your own\l"
    .string "hands have made unto you for a sin.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_8::
    .string "Then shall the Assyrian fall with\n"
    .string "the sword, not of a mighty man; and\l"
    .string "the sword, not of a mean man, shall\l"
    .string "devour him: but he shall flee from\l"
    .string "the sword, and his young men shall\l"
    .string "be discomfited.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_31_9::
    .string "And he shall pass over to his\n"
    .string "strong hold for fear, and his\l"
    .string "princes shall be afraid of the\l"
    .string "ensign, saith the LORD, whose fire is\l"
    .string "in Zion, and his furnace in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_1::
    .string "Behold, a king shall reign in\n"
    .string "righteousness, and princes shall\l"
    .string "rule in judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_2::
    .string "And a man shall be as an hiding\n"
    .string "place from the wind, and a covert\l"
    .string "from the tempest; as rivers of water\l"
    .string "in a dry place, as the shadow of a\l"
    .string "great rock in a weary land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_3::
    .string "And the eyes of them that see shall\n"
    .string "not be dim, and the ears of them that\l"
    .string "hear shall hearken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_4::
    .string "The heart also of the rash shall\n"
    .string "understand knowledge, and the tongue\l"
    .string "of the stammerers shall be ready to\l"
    .string "speak plainly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_5::
    .string "The vile person shall be no more\n"
    .string "called liberal, nor the churl\l"
    .string "said to be bountiful.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_6::
    .string "For the vile person will speak\n"
    .string "villany, and his heart will work\l"
    .string "iniquity, to practise hypocrisy,\l"
    .string "and to utter error against the LORD,\l"
    .string "to make empty the soul of the\l"
    .string "hungry, and he will cause the drink\l"
    .string "of the thirsty to fail.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_7::
    .string "The instruments also of the churl\n"
    .string "are evil: he deviseth wicked devices\l"
    .string "to destroy the poor with lying\l"
    .string "words, even when the needy speaketh\l"
    .string "right.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_8::
    .string "But the liberal deviseth liberal\n"
    .string "things; and by liberal things\l"
    .string "shall he stand.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_9::
    .string "Rise up, ye women that are at ease;\n"
    .string "hear my voice, ye careless\l"
    .string "daughters; give ear unto my speech.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_10::
    .string "Many days and years shall ye be\n"
    .string "troubled, ye careless women: for\l"
    .string "the vintage shall fail, the\l"
    .string "gathering shall not come.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_11::
    .string "Tremble, ye women that are at ease;\n"
    .string "be troubled, ye careless ones:\l"
    .string "strip you, and make you bare, and\l"
    .string "gird sackcloth upon your loins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_12::
    .string "They shall lament for the teats,\n"
    .string "for the pleasant fields, for the\l"
    .string "fruitful vine.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_13::
    .string "Upon the land of my people\n"
    .string "shall come up thorns and briers;\l"
    .string "yea, upon all the houses of joy in\l"
    .string "the joyous city:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_14::
    .string "Because the palaces shall be\n"
    .string "forsaken; the multitude of the city\l"
    .string "shall be left; the forts and towers\l"
    .string "shall be for dens for ever, a joy of\l"
    .string "wild asses, a pasture of flocks;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_15::
    .string "Until the spirit be poured upon\n"
    .string "us from on high, and the wilderness\l"
    .string "be a fruitful field, and the\l"
    .string "fruitful field be counted for a\l"
    .string "forest$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_16::
    .string "Then judgment shall dwell in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and righteousness\l"
    .string "remain in the fruitful field.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_17::
    .string "And the work of righteousness\n"
    .string "shall be peace; and the effect of\l"
    .string "righteousness quietness and\l"
    .string "assurance for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_18::
    .string "And my people shall dwell in a\n"
    .string "peaceable habitation, and in sure\l"
    .string "dwellings, and in quiet resting\l"
    .string "places;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_19::
    .string "When it shall hail, coming down on\n"
    .string "the forest; and the city shall be\l"
    .string "low in a low place$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_32_20::
    .string "Blessed are ye that sow beside all\n"
    .string "waters, that send forth thither the\l"
    .string "feet of the ox and the ass.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_1::
    .string "Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou\n"
    .string "wast not spoiled; and dealest\l"
    .string "treacherously, and they dealt not\l"
    .string "treacherously with thee! when thou\l"
    .string "shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt\l"
    .string "be spoiled; and when thou shalt\l"
    .string "make an end to deal treacherously,\l"
    .string "they shall deal treacherously\l"
    .string "with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_2::
    .string "O LORD, be gracious unto us; we have\n"
    .string "waited for thee: be thou their arm\l"
    .string "every morning, our salvation also\l"
    .string "in the time of trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_3::
    .string "At the noise of the tumult the\n"
    .string "people fled; at the lifting up of\l"
    .string "thyself the nations were scattered.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_4::
    .string "And your spoil shall be gathered\n"
    .string "like the gathering of the\l"
    .string "caterpiller: as the running to and\l"
    .string "fro of locusts shall he run upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_5::
    .string "The LORD is exalted; for he\n"
    .string "dwelleth on high: he hath filled\l"
    .string "Zion with judgment and righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_6::
    .string "And wisdom and knowledge shall be\n"
    .string "the stability of thy times, and\l"
    .string "strength of salvation: the fear of\l"
    .string "the LORD is his treasure.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_7::
    .string "Behold, their valiant ones shall\n"
    .string "cry without: the ambassadors of\l"
    .string "peace shall weep bitterly.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_8::
    .string "The highways lie waste, the\n"
    .string "wayfaring man ceaseth: he hath broken\l"
    .string "the covenant, he hath despised the\l"
    .string "cities, he regardeth no man.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_9::
    .string "The earth mourneth and languisheth:\n"
    .string "Lebanon is ashamed and hewn down:\l"
    .string "Sharon is like a wilderness; and\l"
    .string "Bashan and Carmel shake off their\l"
    .string "fruits.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_10::
    .string "Now will I rise, saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "now will I be exalted; now will I\l"
    .string "lift up myself.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_11::
    .string "Ye shall conceive chaff, ye shall\n"
    .string "bring forth stubble: your breath, as\l"
    .string "fire, shall devour you.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_12::
    .string "And the people shall be as the\n"
    .string "burnings of lime: as thorns cut up\l"
    .string "shall they be burned in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_13::
    .string "Hear, ye that are far off, what I\n"
    .string "have done; and, ye that are near,\l"
    .string "acknowledge my might.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_14::
    .string "The sinners in Zion are afraid;\n"
    .string "fearfulness hath surprised the\l"
    .string "hypocrites. Who among us shall\l"
    .string "dwell with the devouring fire? who\l"
    .string "among us shall dwell with\l"
    .string "everlasting burnings?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_15::
    .string "He that walketh righteously, and\n"
    .string "speaketh uprightly; he that\l"
    .string "despiseth the gain of oppressions,\l"
    .string "that shaketh his hands from holding\l"
    .string "of bribes, that stoppeth his ears\l"
    .string "from hearing of blood, and shutteth\l"
    .string "his eyes from seeing evil;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_16::
    .string "He shall dwell on high: his\n"
    .string "place of defence shall be the\l"
    .string "munitions of rocks: bread shall be\l"
    .string "given him; his waters shall be sure$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_17::
    .string "Thine eyes shall see the king in\n"
    .string "his beauty: they shall behold the\l"
    .string "land that is very far off.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_18::
    .string "Thine heart shall meditate terror.\n"
    .string "Where is the scribe? where is the\l"
    .string "receiver? where is he that counted\l"
    .string "the towers?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_19::
    .string "Thou shalt not see a fierce\n"
    .string "people, a people of a deeper\l"
    .string "speech than thou canst perceive; of\l"
    .string "a stammering tongue, that thou canst\l"
    .string "not understand$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_20::
    .string "Look upon Zion, the city of our\n"
    .string "solemnities: thine eyes shall see\l"
    .string "Jerusalem a quiet habitation, a\l"
    .string "tabernacle that shall not be taken\l"
    .string "down; not one of the stakes thereof\l"
    .string "shall ever be removed, neither\l"
    .string "shall any of the cords thereof be\l"
    .string "broken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_21::
    .string "But there the glorious LORD will\n"
    .string "be unto us a place of broad rivers\l"
    .string "and streams; wherein shall go no\l"
    .string "galley with oars, neither shall\l"
    .string "gallant ship pass thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_22::
    .string "For the LORD is our judge, the LORD\n"
    .string "is our lawgiver, the LORD is our\l"
    .string "king; he will save us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_23::
    .string "Thy tacklings are loosed; they\n"
    .string "could not well strengthen their\l"
    .string "mast, they could not spread the\l"
    .string "sail: then is the prey of a great\l"
    .string "spoil divided; the lame take the\l"
    .string "prey.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_33_24::
    .string "And the inhabitant shall not say, I\n"
    .string "am sick: the people that dwell\l"
    .string "therein shall be forgiven their\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_1::
    .string "Come near, ye nations, to hear; and\n"
    .string "hearken, ye people: let the earth\l"
    .string "hear, and all that is therein; the\l"
    .string "world, and all things that come\l"
    .string "forth of it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_2::
    .string "For the indignation of the LORD is\n"
    .string "upon all nations, and his fury\l"
    .string "upon all their armies: he hath\l"
    .string "utterly destroyed them, he hath\l"
    .string "delivered them to the slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_3::
    .string "Their slain also shall be cast\n"
    .string "out, and their stink shall come up\l"
    .string "out of their carcases, and the\l"
    .string "mountains shall be melted with\l"
    .string "their blood.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_4::
    .string "And all the host of heaven shall\n"
    .string "be dissolved, and the heavens shall\l"
    .string "be rolled together as a scroll:\l"
    .string "and all their host shall fall\l"
    .string "down, as the leaf falleth off from\l"
    .string "the vine, and as a falling fig from\l"
    .string "the fig tree.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_5::
    .string "For my sword shall be bathed in\n"
    .string "heaven: behold, it shall come down\l"
    .string "upon Idumea, and upon the people\l"
    .string "of my curse, to judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_6::
    .string "The sword of the LORD is filled\n"
    .string "with blood, it is made fat with\l"
    .string "fatness, and with the blood of lambs\l"
    .string "and goats, with the fat of the\l"
    .string "kidneys of rams: for the LORD hath a\l"
    .string "sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great\l"
    .string "slaughter in the land of Idumea.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_7::
    .string "And the unicorns shall come down\n"
    .string "with them, and the bullocks with the\l"
    .string "bulls; and their land shall be\l"
    .string "soaked with blood, and their dust\l"
    .string "made fat with fatness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_8::
    .string "For it is the day of the LORD’s\n"
    .string "vengeance, and the year of\l"
    .string "recompences for the controversy of\l"
    .string "Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_9::
    .string "And the streams thereof shall be\n"
    .string "turned into pitch, and the dust\l"
    .string "thereof into brimstone, and the land\l"
    .string "thereof shall become burning pitch.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_10::
    .string "It shall not be quenched night nor\n"
    .string "day; the smoke thereof shall go up\l"
    .string "for ever: from generation to\l"
    .string "generation it shall lie waste; none\l"
    .string "shall pass through it for ever and\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_11::
    .string "But the cormorant and the bittern\n"
    .string "shall possess it; the owl also and\l"
    .string "the raven shall dwell in it: and he\l"
    .string "shall stretch out upon it the line\l"
    .string "of confusion, and the stones of\l"
    .string "emptiness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_12::
    .string "They shall call the nobles\n"
    .string "thereof to the kingdom, but none\l"
    .string "shall be there, and all her\l"
    .string "princes shall be nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_13::
    .string "And thorns shall come up in her\n"
    .string "palaces, nettles and brambles in\l"
    .string "the fortresses thereof: and it\l"
    .string "shall be an habitation of dragons,\l"
    .string "and a court for owls.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_14::
    .string "The wild beasts of the desert\n"
    .string "shall also meet with the wild\l"
    .string "beasts of the island, and the satyr\l"
    .string "shall cry to his fellow; the\l"
    .string "screech owl also shall rest there,\l"
    .string "and find for herself a place of\l"
    .string "rest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_15::
    .string "There shall the great owl make her\n"
    .string "nest, and lay, and hatch, and gather\l"
    .string "under her shadow: there shall the\l"
    .string "vultures also be gathered, every\l"
    .string "one with her mate.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_16::
    .string "Seek ye out of the book of the LORD,\n"
    .string "and read: no one of these shall\l"
    .string "fail, none shall want her mate: for\l"
    .string "my mouth it hath commanded, and his\l"
    .string "spirit it hath gathered them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_34_17::
    .string "And he hath cast the lot for them,\n"
    .string "and his hand hath divided it unto\l"
    .string "them by line: they shall possess\l"
    .string "it for ever, from generation to\l"
    .string "generation shall they dwell\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_1::
    .string "The wilderness and the solitary\n"
    .string "place shall be glad for them; and\l"
    .string "the desert shall rejoice, and\l"
    .string "blossom as the rose.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_2::
    .string "It shall blossom abundantly, and\n"
    .string "rejoice even with joy and singing:\l"
    .string "the glory of Lebanon shall be given\l"
    .string "unto it, the excellency of Carmel\l"
    .string "and Sharon, they shall see the\l"
    .string "glory of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "excellency of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_3::
    .string "Strengthen ye the weak hands, and\n"
    .string "confirm the feeble knees.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_4::
    .string "Say to them that are of a fearful\n"
    .string "heart, Be strong, fear not: behold,\l"
    .string "your God will come with vengeance,\l"
    .string "even God with a recompence; he will\l"
    .string "come and save you.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_5::
    .string "Then the eyes of the blind shall\n"
    .string "be opened, and the ears of the deaf\l"
    .string "shall be unstopped.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_6::
    .string "Then shall the lame man leap as\n"
    .string "an hart, and the tongue of the dumb\l"
    .string "sing: for in the wilderness shall\l"
    .string "waters break out, and streams in the\l"
    .string "desert.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_7::
    .string "And the parched ground shall\n"
    .string "become a pool, and the thirsty land\l"
    .string "springs of water: in the habitation\l"
    .string "of dragons, where each lay, shall\l"
    .string "be grass with reeds and rushes.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_8::
    .string "And an highway shall be there, and\n"
    .string "a way, and it shall be called The\l"
    .string "way of holiness; the unclean shall\l"
    .string "not pass over it; but it shall be\l"
    .string "for those: the wayfaring men, though\l"
    .string "fools, shall not err therein.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_9::
    .string "No lion shall be there, nor any\n"
    .string "ravenous beast shall go up thereon,\l"
    .string "it shall not be found there; but the\l"
    .string "redeemed shall walk there:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_35_10::
    .string "And the ransomed of the LORD shall\n"
    .string "return, and come to Zion with songs\l"
    .string "and everlasting joy upon their\l"
    .string "heads: they shall obtain joy and\l"
    .string "gladness, and sorrow and sighing\l"
    .string "shall flee away$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the\n"
    .string "fourteenth year of king Hezekiah,\l"
    .string "that Sennacherib king of Assyria\l"
    .string "came up against all the defenced\l"
    .string "cities of Judah, and took them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_2::
    .string "And the king of Assyria sent\n"
    .string "Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem\l"
    .string "unto king Hezekiah with a great army.\l"
    .string "And he stood by the conduit of the\l"
    .string "upper pool in the highway of the\l"
    .string "fuller’s field.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_3::
    .string "Then came forth unto him Eliakim,\n"
    .string "Hilkiah’s son, which was over the\l"
    .string "house, and Shebna the scribe, and\l"
    .string "Joah, Asaph’s son, the recorder.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_4::
    .string "And Rabshakeh said unto them, Say ye\n"
    .string "now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great\l"
    .string "king, the king of Assyria, What\l"
    .string "confidence is this wherein thou\l"
    .string "trustest?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_5::
    .string "I say, sayest thou, (but they are\n"
    .string "but vain words) I have counsel and\l"
    .string "strength for war: now on whom dost\l"
    .string "thou trust, that thou rebellest\l"
    .string "against me?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_6::
    .string "Lo, thou trustest in the staff of\n"
    .string "this broken reed, on Egypt; whereon\l"
    .string "if a man lean, it will go into his\l"
    .string "hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh\l"
    .string "king of Egypt to all that trust in\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_7::
    .string "But if thou say to me, We trust in\n"
    .string "the LORD our God: is it not he, whose\l"
    .string "high places and whose altars\l"
    .string "Hezekiah hath taken away, and said to\l"
    .string "Judah and to Jerusalem, Ye shall\l"
    .string "worship before this altar?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_8::
    .string "Now therefore give pledges, I pray\n"
    .string "thee, to my master the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria, and I will give thee two\l"
    .string "thousand horses, if thou be able on\l"
    .string "thy part to set riders upon them$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_9::
    .string "How then wilt thou turn away the\n"
    .string "face of one captain of the least of\l"
    .string "my master’s servants, and put thy\l"
    .string "trust on Egypt for chariots and for\l"
    .string "horsemen?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_10::
    .string "And am I now come up without the\n"
    .string "LORD against this land to destroy\l"
    .string "it? the LORD said unto me, Go up\l"
    .string "against this land, and destroy it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_11::
    .string "Then said Eliakim and Shebna and\n"
    .string "Joah unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, unto thy servants in the Syrian\l"
    .string "language; for we understand it: and\l"
    .string "speak not to us in the Jews’\l"
    .string "language, in the ears of the people\l"
    .string "that are on the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_12::
    .string "But Rabshakeh said, Hath my master\n"
    .string "sent me to thy master and to thee to\l"
    .string "speak these words? hath he not sent\l"
    .string "me to the men that sit upon the\l"
    .string "wall, that they may eat their own\l"
    .string "dung, and drink their own piss with\l"
    .string "you?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_13::
    .string "Then Rabshakeh stood, and cried with\n"
    .string "a loud voice in the Jews’ language,\l"
    .string "and said, Hear ye the words of the\l"
    .string "great king, the king of Assyria$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_14::
    .string "Thus saith the king, Let not\n"
    .string "Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall\l"
    .string "not be able to deliver you.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_15::
    .string "Neither let Hezekiah make you trust\n"
    .string "in the LORD, saying, The LORD will\l"
    .string "surely deliver us: this city shall\l"
    .string "not be delivered into the hand of\l"
    .string "the king of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_16::
    .string "Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus\n"
    .string "saith the king of Assyria, Make an\l"
    .string "agreement with me by a present, and\l"
    .string "come out to me: and eat ye every one\l"
    .string "of his vine, and every one of his fig\l"
    .string "tree, and drink ye every one the\l"
    .string "waters of his own cistern;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_17::
    .string "Until I come and take you away to a\n"
    .string "land like your own land, a land of\l"
    .string "corn and wine, a land of bread and\l"
    .string "vineyards$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_18::
    .string "Beware lest Hezekiah persuade you,\n"
    .string "saying, the LORD will deliver us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_19::
    .string "Where are the gods of Hamath and\n"
    .string "Arphad? where are the gods of\l"
    .string "Sepharvaim? and have they delivered\l"
    .string "Samaria out of my hand?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_20::
    .string "Who are they among all the gods of\n"
    .string "these lands, that have delivered\l"
    .string "their land out of my hand, that the\l"
    .string "LORD should deliver Jerusalem out\l"
    .string "of my hand?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_21::
    .string "But they held their peace, and\n"
    .string "answered him not a word: for the\l"
    .string "king’s commandment was, saying,\l"
    .string "Answer him not$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_36_22::
    .string "Then came Eliakim, the son of\n"
    .string "Hilkiah, that was over the\l"
    .string "household, and Shebna the scribe,\l"
    .string "and Joah, the son of Asaph, the\l"
    .string "recorder, to Hezekiah with their\l"
    .string "clothes rent, and told him the words\l"
    .string "of Rabshakeh.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when king\n"
    .string "Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his\l"
    .string "clothes, and covered himself with\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and went into the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_2::
    .string "And he sent Eliakim, who was over\n"
    .string "the household, and Shebna the\l"
    .string "scribe, and the elders of the\l"
    .string "priests covered with sackcloth, unto\l"
    .string "Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_3::
    .string "And they said unto him, Thus saith\n"
    .string "Hezekiah, This day is a day of\l"
    .string "trouble, and of rebuke, and of\l"
    .string "blasphemy: for the children are\l"
    .string "come to the birth, and there is not\l"
    .string "strength to bring forth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_4::
    .string "It may be the LORD thy God will\n"
    .string "hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria his master hath sent\l"
    .string "to reproach the living God, and\l"
    .string "will reprove the words which the\l"
    .string "LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore\l"
    .string "lift up thy prayer for the remnant\l"
    .string "that is left.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_5::
    .string "So the servants of king Hezekiah\n"
    .string "came to Isaiah.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_6::
    .string "And Isaiah said unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "shall ye say unto your master, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the\l"
    .string "words that thou hast heard, wherewith\l"
    .string "the servants of the king of Assyria\l"
    .string "have blasphemed me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_7::
    .string "Behold, I will send a blast upon\n"
    .string "him, and he shall hear a rumour, and\l"
    .string "return to his own land; and I will\l"
    .string "cause him to fall by the sword in\l"
    .string "his own land.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_8::
    .string "So Rabshakeh returned, and found the\n"
    .string "king of Assyria warring against\l"
    .string "Libnah: for he had heard that he was\l"
    .string "departed from Lachish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_9::
    .string "And he heard say concerning\n"
    .string "Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, He is\l"
    .string "come forth to make war with thee. And\l"
    .string "when he heard it, he sent messengers\l"
    .string "to Hezekiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_10::
    .string "Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah\n"
    .string "king of Judah, saying, Let not thy\l"
    .string "God, in whom thou trustest, deceive\l"
    .string "thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not\l"
    .string "be given into the hand of the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_11::
    .string "Behold, thou hast heard what the\n"
    .string "kings of Assyria have done to all\l"
    .string "lands by destroying them utterly;\l"
    .string "and shalt thou be delivered?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_12::
    .string "Have the gods of the nations\n"
    .string "delivered them which my fathers have\l"
    .string "destroyed, as Gozan, and Haran, and\l"
    .string "Rezeph, and the children of Eden\l"
    .string "which were in Telassar?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_13::
    .string "Where is the king of Hamath, and the\n"
    .string "king of Arphad, and the king of the\l"
    .string "city of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_14::
    .string "And Hezekiah received the letter\n"
    .string "from the hand of the messengers, and\l"
    .string "read it: and Hezekiah went up unto\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, and spread it\l"
    .string "before the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_15::
    .string "And Hezekiah prayed unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_16::
    .string "O LORD of hosts, God of Israel, that\n"
    .string "dwellest between the cherubims,\l"
    .string "thou art the God, even thou alone, of\l"
    .string "all the kingdoms of the earth: thou\l"
    .string "hast made heaven and earth$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_17::
    .string "Incline thine ear, O LORD, and hear;\n"
    .string "open thine eyes, O LORD, and see: and\l"
    .string "hear all the words of Sennacherib,\l"
    .string "which hath sent to reproach the\l"
    .string "living God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_18::
    .string "Of a truth, LORD, the kings of\n"
    .string "Assyria have laid waste all the\l"
    .string "nations, and their countries,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_19::
    .string "And have cast their gods into the\n"
    .string "fire: for they were no gods, but the\l"
    .string "work of men’s hands, wood and stone:\l"
    .string "therefore they have destroyed them$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_20::
    .string "Now therefore, O LORD our God, save\n"
    .string "us from his hand, that all the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of the earth may know that\l"
    .string "thou art the LORD, even thou only.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_21::
    .string "Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent\n"
    .string "unto Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD God of Israel, Whereas thou\l"
    .string "hast prayed to me against\l"
    .string "Sennacherib king of Assyria:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_22::
    .string "This is the word which the LORD hath\n"
    .string "spoken concerning him; The virgin,\l"
    .string "the daughter of Zion, hath despised\l"
    .string "thee, and laughed thee to scorn; the\l"
    .string "daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken\l"
    .string "her head at thee$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_23::
    .string "Whom hast thou reproached and\n"
    .string "blasphemed? and against whom hast\l"
    .string "thou exalted thy voice, and lifted\l"
    .string "up thine eyes on high? even against\l"
    .string "the Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_24::
    .string "By thy servants hast thou\n"
    .string "reproached the Lord, and hast said,\l"
    .string "By the multitude of my chariots am I\l"
    .string "come up to the height of the\l"
    .string "mountains, to the sides of Lebanon;\l"
    .string "and I will cut down the tall\l"
    .string "cedars thereof, and the choice fir\l"
    .string "trees thereof: and I will enter into\l"
    .string "the height of his border, and the\l"
    .string "forest of his Carmel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_25::
    .string "I have digged, and drunk water; and\n"
    .string "with the sole of my feet have I dried\l"
    .string "up all the rivers of the besieged\l"
    .string "places.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_26::
    .string "Hast thou not heard long ago, how I\n"
    .string "have done it; and of ancient times,\l"
    .string "that I have formed it? now have I\l"
    .string "brought it to pass, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest be to lay waste defenced\l"
    .string "cities into ruinous heaps.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_27::
    .string "Therefore their inhabitants were of\n"
    .string "small power, they were dismayed and\l"
    .string "confounded: they were as the grass of\l"
    .string "the field, and as the green herb, as\l"
    .string "the grass on the housetops, and as\l"
    .string "corn blasted before it be grown up.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_28::
    .string "But I know thy abode, and thy going\n"
    .string "out, and thy coming in, and thy rage\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_29::
    .string "Because thy rage against me, and thy\n"
    .string "tumult, is come up into mine ears,\l"
    .string "therefore will I put my hook in thy\l"
    .string "nose, and my bridle in thy lips,\l"
    .string "and I will turn thee back by the way\l"
    .string "by which thou camest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_30::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto thee,\n"
    .string "Ye shall eat this year such as\l"
    .string "groweth of itself; and the second\l"
    .string "year that which springeth of the\l"
    .string "same: and in the third year sow ye,\l"
    .string "and reap, and plant vineyards, and\l"
    .string "eat the fruit thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_31::
    .string "And the remnant that is escaped of\n"
    .string "the house of Judah shall again take\l"
    .string "root downward, and bear fruit\l"
    .string "upward:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_32::
    .string "For out of Jerusalem shall go\n"
    .string "forth a remnant, and they that\l"
    .string "escape out of mount Zion: the zeal\l"
    .string "of the LORD of hosts shall do this$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_33::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "concerning the king of Assyria, He\l"
    .string "shall not come into this city, nor\l"
    .string "shoot an arrow there, nor come before\l"
    .string "it with shields, nor cast a bank\l"
    .string "against it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_34::
    .string "By the way that he came, by the same\n"
    .string "shall he return, and shall not\l"
    .string "come into this city, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_35::
    .string "For I will defend this city to save\n"
    .string "it for mine own sake, and for my\l"
    .string "servant David’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_36::
    .string "Then the angel of the LORD went\n"
    .string "forth, and smote in the camp of the\l"
    .string "Assyrians a hundred and fourscore\l"
    .string "and five thousand: and when they\l"
    .string "arose early in the morning, behold,\l"
    .string "they were all dead corpses.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_37::
    .string "So Sennacherib king of Assyria\n"
    .string "departed, and went and returned, and\l"
    .string "dwelt at Nineveh.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_37_38::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he was\n"
    .string "worshipping in the house of Nisroch\l"
    .string "his god, that Adrammelech and\l"
    .string "Sharezer his sons smote him with the\l"
    .string "sword; and they escaped into the\l"
    .string "land of Armenia: and Esarhaddon his\l"
    .string "son reigned in his stead.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_1::
    .string "In those days was Hezekiah sick unto\n"
    .string "death. And Isaiah the prophet the\l"
    .string "son of Amoz came unto him, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set\l"
    .string "thine house in order: for thou shalt\l"
    .string "die, and not live.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_2::
    .string "Then Hezekiah turned his face\n"
    .string "toward the wall, and prayed unto\l"
    .string "the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_3::
    .string "And said, Remember now, O LORD, I\n"
    .string "beseech thee, how I have walked\l"
    .string "before thee in truth and with a\l"
    .string "perfect heart, and have done that\l"
    .string "which is good in thy sight. And\l"
    .string "Hezekiah wept sore$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_4::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD to\n"
    .string "Isaiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_5::
    .string "Go, and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, the God of David thy\l"
    .string "father, I have heard thy prayer, I\l"
    .string "have seen thy tears: behold, I will\l"
    .string "add unto thy days fifteen years$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_6::
    .string "And I will deliver thee and this\n"
    .string "city out of the hand of the king of\l"
    .string "Assyria: and I will defend this\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_7::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto thee\n"
    .string "from the LORD, that the LORD will do\l"
    .string "this thing that he hath spoken;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_8::
    .string "Behold, I will bring again the\n"
    .string "shadow of the degrees, which is gone\l"
    .string "down in the sun dial of Ahaz, ten\l"
    .string "degrees backward. So the sun returned\l"
    .string "ten degrees, by which degrees it was\l"
    .string "gone down$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_9::
    .string "The writing of Hezekiah king of\n"
    .string "Judah, when he had been sick, and was\l"
    .string "recovered of his sickness:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_10::
    .string "I said in the cutting off of my days,\n"
    .string "I shall go to the gates of the\l"
    .string "grave: I am deprived of the residue\l"
    .string "of my years$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_11::
    .string "I said, I shall not see the LORD,\n"
    .string "even the LORD, in the land of the\l"
    .string "living: I shall behold man no more\l"
    .string "with the inhabitants of the world.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_12::
    .string "Mine age is departed, and is\n"
    .string "removed from me as a shepherd’s\l"
    .string "tent: I have cut off like a weaver my\l"
    .string "life: he will cut me off with\l"
    .string "pining sickness: from day even to\l"
    .string "night wilt thou make an end of me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_13::
    .string "I reckoned till morning, that, as a\n"
    .string "lion, so will he break all my\l"
    .string "bones: from day even to night wilt\l"
    .string "thou make an end of me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_14::
    .string "Like a crane or a swallow, so did I\n"
    .string "chatter: I did mourn as a dove: mine\l"
    .string "eyes fail with looking upward: O\l"
    .string "LORD, I am oppressed; undertake for\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_15::
    .string "What shall I say? he hath both\n"
    .string "spoken unto me, and himself hath\l"
    .string "done it: I shall go softly all my\l"
    .string "years in the bitterness of my soul.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_16::
    .string "O LORD, by these things men live,\n"
    .string "and in all these things is the life\l"
    .string "of my spirit: so wilt thou recover\l"
    .string "me, and make me to live.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_17::
    .string "Behold, for peace I had great\n"
    .string "bitterness: but thou hast in love to\l"
    .string "my soul delivered it from the pit\l"
    .string "of corruption: for thou hast cast\l"
    .string "all my sins behind thy back.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_18::
    .string "For the grave cannot praise thee,\n"
    .string "death can not celebrate thee: they\l"
    .string "that go down into the pit cannot\l"
    .string "hope for thy truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_19::
    .string "The living, the living, he shall\n"
    .string "praise thee, as I do this day: the\l"
    .string "father to the children shall make\l"
    .string "known thy truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_20::
    .string "The LORD was ready to save me:\n"
    .string "therefore we will sing my songs to\l"
    .string "the stringed instruments all the\l"
    .string "days of our life in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_21::
    .string "For Isaiah had said, Let them take a\n"
    .string "lump of figs, and lay it for a\l"
    .string "plaister upon the boil, and he\l"
    .string "shall recover.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_38_22::
    .string "Hezekiah also had said, What is the\n"
    .string "sign that I shall go up to the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_1::
    .string "At that time Merodachbaladan, the\n"
    .string "son of Baladan, king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "sent letters and a present to\l"
    .string "Hezekiah: for he had heard that he\l"
    .string "had been sick, and was recovered$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_2::
    .string "And Hezekiah was glad of them, and\n"
    .string "shewed them the house of his\l"
    .string "precious things, the silver, and the\l"
    .string "gold, and the spices, and the\l"
    .string "precious ointment, and all the\l"
    .string "house of his armour, and all that\l"
    .string "was found in his treasures: there was\l"
    .string "nothing in his house, nor in all his\l"
    .string "dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_3::
    .string "Then came Isaiah the prophet unto\n"
    .string "king Hezekiah, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "What said these men? and from whence\l"
    .string "came they unto thee? And Hezekiah\l"
    .string "said, They are come from a far\l"
    .string "country unto me, even from Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_4::
    .string "Then said he, What have they seen in\n"
    .string "thine house? And Hezekiah answered,\l"
    .string "All that is in mine house have they\l"
    .string "seen: there is nothing among my\l"
    .string "treasures that I have not shewed them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_5::
    .string "Then said Isaiah to Hezekiah, Hear\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD of hosts:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_6::
    .string "Behold, the days come, that all\n"
    .string "that is in thine house, and that\l"
    .string "which thy fathers have laid up in\l"
    .string "store until this day, shall be\l"
    .string "carried to Babylon: nothing shall\l"
    .string "be left, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_7::
    .string "And of thy sons that shall issue\n"
    .string "from thee, which thou shalt beget,\l"
    .string "shall they take away; and they\l"
    .string "shall be eunuchs in the palace of\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_39_8::
    .string "Then said Hezekiah to Isaiah, Good\n"
    .string "is the word of the LORD which thou\l"
    .string "hast spoken. He said moreover, For\l"
    .string "there shall be peace and truth in\l"
    .string "my days.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_1::
    .string "Comfort ye, comfort ye my people,\n"
    .string "saith your God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_2::
    .string "Speak ye comfortably to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, and cry unto her, that\l"
    .string "her warfare is accomplished, that\l"
    .string "her iniquity is pardoned: for she\l"
    .string "hath received of the LORD’s hand\l"
    .string "double for all her sins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_3::
    .string "The voice of him that crieth in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, Prepare ye the way of\l"
    .string "the LORD, make straight in the desert\l"
    .string "a highway for our God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_4::
    .string "Every valley shall be exalted,\n"
    .string "and every mountain and hill shall\l"
    .string "be made low: and the crooked shall\l"
    .string "be made straight, and the rough\l"
    .string "places plain:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_5::
    .string "And the glory of the LORD shall be\n"
    .string "revealed, and all flesh shall see\l"
    .string "it together: for the mouth of the\l"
    .string "LORD hath spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_6::
    .string "The voice said, Cry. And he said,\n"
    .string "What shall I cry? All flesh is\l"
    .string "grass, and all the goodliness\l"
    .string "thereof is as the flower of the\l"
    .string "field:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_7::
    .string "The grass withereth, the flower\n"
    .string "fadeth: because the spirit of the\l"
    .string "LORD bloweth upon it: surely the\l"
    .string "people is grass$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_8::
    .string "The grass withereth, the flower\n"
    .string "fadeth: but the word of our God\l"
    .string "shall stand for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_9::
    .string "O Zion, that bringest good tidings,\n"
    .string "get thee up into the high mountain; O\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, that bringest good\l"
    .string "tidings, lift up thy voice with\l"
    .string "strength; lift it up, be not afraid;\l"
    .string "say unto the cities of Judah, Behold\l"
    .string "your God!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_10::
    .string "Behold, the Lord GOD will come\n"
    .string "with strong hand, and his arm shall\l"
    .string "rule for him: behold, his reward is\l"
    .string "with him, and his work before him$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_11::
    .string "He shall feed his flock like a\n"
    .string "shepherd: he shall gather the\l"
    .string "lambs with his arm, and carry them in\l"
    .string "his bosom, and shall gently lead\l"
    .string "those that are with young.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_12::
    .string "Who hath measured the waters in the\n"
    .string "hollow of his hand, and meted out\l"
    .string "heaven with the span, and\l"
    .string "comprehended the dust of the earth\l"
    .string "in a measure, and weighed the\l"
    .string "mountains in scales, and the hills\l"
    .string "in a balance?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_13::
    .string "Who hath directed the Spirit of the\n"
    .string "LORD, or being his counsellor hath\l"
    .string "taught him?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_14::
    .string "With whom took he counsel, and who\n"
    .string "instructed him, and taught him in the\l"
    .string "path of judgment, and taught him\l"
    .string "knowledge, and shewed to him the way\l"
    .string "of understanding?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_15::
    .string "Behold, the nations are as a drop\n"
    .string "of a bucket, and are counted as the\l"
    .string "small dust of the balance: behold,\l"
    .string "he taketh up the isles as a very\l"
    .string "little thing$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_16::
    .string "And Lebanon is not sufficient to\n"
    .string "burn, nor the beasts thereof\l"
    .string "sufficient for a burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_17::
    .string "All nations before him are as\n"
    .string "nothing; and they are counted to him\l"
    .string "less than nothing, and vanity.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_18::
    .string "To whom then will ye liken God? or\n"
    .string "what likeness will ye compare unto\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_19::
    .string "The workman melteth a graven image,\n"
    .string "and the goldsmith spreadeth it over\l"
    .string "with gold, and casteth silver chains$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_20::
    .string "He that is so impoverished that he\n"
    .string "hath no oblation chooseth a tree\l"
    .string "that will not rot; he seeketh unto\l"
    .string "him a cunning workman to prepare a\l"
    .string "graven image, that shall not be\l"
    .string "moved.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_21::
    .string "Have ye not known? have ye not\n"
    .string "heard? hath it not been told you from\l"
    .string "the beginning? have ye not understood\l"
    .string "from the foundations of the earth?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_22::
    .string "It is he that sitteth upon the\n"
    .string "circle of the earth, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof are as\l"
    .string "grasshoppers; that stretcheth out\l"
    .string "the heavens as a curtain, and\l"
    .string "spreadeth them out as a tent to\l"
    .string "dwell in:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_23::
    .string "That bringeth the princes to\n"
    .string "nothing; he maketh the judges of the\l"
    .string "earth as vanity$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_24::
    .string "Yea, they shall not be planted;\n"
    .string "yea, they shall not be sown: yea,\l"
    .string "their stock shall not take root in\l"
    .string "the earth: and he shall also blow\l"
    .string "upon them, and they shall wither,\l"
    .string "and the whirlwind shall take them\l"
    .string "away as stubble.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_25::
    .string "To whom then will ye liken me, or\n"
    .string "shall I be equal? saith the Holy\l"
    .string "One.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_26::
    .string "Lift up your eyes on high, and\n"
    .string "behold who hath created these\l"
    .string "things, that bringeth out their host\l"
    .string "by number: he calleth them all by\l"
    .string "names by the greatness of his might,\l"
    .string "for that he is strong in power; not\l"
    .string "one faileth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_27::
    .string "Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and\n"
    .string "speakest, O Israel, My way is hid\l"
    .string "from the LORD, and my judgment is\l"
    .string "passed over from my God?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_28::
    .string "Hast thou not known? hast thou not\n"
    .string "heard, that the everlasting God, the\l"
    .string "LORD, the Creator of the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth, fainteth not, neither is\l"
    .string "weary? there is no searching of his\l"
    .string "understanding$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_29::
    .string "He giveth power to the faint; and to\n"
    .string "them that have no might he increaseth\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_30::
    .string "Even the youths shall faint and be\n"
    .string "weary, and the young men shall\l"
    .string "utterly fall:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_40_31::
    .string "But they that wait upon the LORD\n"
    .string "shall renew their strength; they\l"
    .string "shall mount up with wings as\l"
    .string "eagles; they shall run, and not be\l"
    .string "weary; and they shall walk, and not\l"
    .string "faint$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_1::
    .string "Keep silence before me, O islands;\n"
    .string "and let the people renew their\l"
    .string "strength: let them come near; then\l"
    .string "let them speak: let us come near\l"
    .string "together to judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_2::
    .string "Who raised up the righteous man\n"
    .string "from the east, called him to his\l"
    .string "foot, gave the nations before him,\l"
    .string "and made him rule over kings? he gave\l"
    .string "them as the dust to his sword, and as\l"
    .string "driven stubble to his bow.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_3::
    .string "He pursued them, and passed\n"
    .string "safely; even by the way that he had\l"
    .string "not gone with his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_4::
    .string "Who hath wrought and done it,\n"
    .string "calling the generations from the\l"
    .string "beginning? I the LORD, the first, and\l"
    .string "with the last; I am he.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_5::
    .string "The isles saw it, and feared; the\n"
    .string "ends of the earth were afraid, drew\l"
    .string "near, and came.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_6::
    .string "They helped every one his\n"
    .string "neighbour; and every one said to his\l"
    .string "brother, Be of good courage.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_7::
    .string "So the carpenter encouraged the\n"
    .string "goldsmith, and he that smootheth\l"
    .string "with the hammer him that smote the\l"
    .string "anvil, saying, It is ready for the\l"
    .string "sodering: and he fastened it with\l"
    .string "nails, that it should not be moved.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_8::
    .string "But thou, Israel, art my servant,\n"
    .string "Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of\l"
    .string "Abraham my friend.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_9::
    .string "Thou whom I have taken from the ends\n"
    .string "of the earth, and called thee from\l"
    .string "the chief men thereof, and said unto\l"
    .string "thee, Thou art my servant; I have\l"
    .string "chosen thee, and not cast thee away.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_10::
    .string "Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be\n"
    .string "not dismayed; for I am thy God: I\l"
    .string "will strengthen thee; yea, I will\l"
    .string "help thee; yea, I will uphold\l"
    .string "thee with the right hand of my\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_11::
    .string "Behold, all they that were\n"
    .string "incensed against thee shall be\l"
    .string "ashamed and confounded: they shall\l"
    .string "be as nothing; and they that strive\l"
    .string "with thee shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_12::
    .string "Thou shalt seek them, and shalt not\n"
    .string "find them, even them that contended\l"
    .string "with thee: they that war against thee\l"
    .string "shall be as nothing, and as a thing\l"
    .string "of nought.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_13::
    .string "For I the LORD thy God will hold\n"
    .string "thy right hand, saying unto thee,\l"
    .string "Fear not; I will help thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_14::
    .string "Fear not, thou worm Jacob, and ye\n"
    .string "men of Israel; I will help thee,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, and thy redeemer, the\l"
    .string "Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_15::
    .string "Behold, I will make thee a new\n"
    .string "sharp threshing instrument having\l"
    .string "teeth: thou shalt thresh the\l"
    .string "mountains, and beat them small, and\l"
    .string "shalt make the hills as chaff.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_16::
    .string "Thou shalt fan them, and the wind\n"
    .string "shall carry them away, and the\l"
    .string "whirlwind shall scatter them: and\l"
    .string "thou shalt rejoice in the LORD, and\l"
    .string "shalt glory in the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_17::
    .string "When the poor and needy seek water,\n"
    .string "and there is none, and their tongue\l"
    .string "faileth for thirst, I the LORD will\l"
    .string "hear them, I the God of Israel will\l"
    .string "not forsake them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_18::
    .string "I will open rivers in high\n"
    .string "places, and fountains in the midst\l"
    .string "of the valleys: I will make the\l"
    .string "wilderness a pool of water, and the\l"
    .string "dry land springs of water.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_19::
    .string "I will plant in the wilderness\n"
    .string "the cedar, the shittah tree, and the\l"
    .string "myrtle, and the oil tree; I will\l"
    .string "set in the desert the fir tree, and\l"
    .string "the pine, and the box tree together:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_20::
    .string "That they may see, and know, and\n"
    .string "consider, and understand together,\l"
    .string "that the hand of the LORD hath done\l"
    .string "this, and the Holy One of Israel\l"
    .string "hath created it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_21::
    .string "Produce your cause, saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "bring forth your strong reasons,\l"
    .string "saith the King of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_22::
    .string "Let them bring them forth, and shew\n"
    .string "us what shall happen: let them\l"
    .string "shew the former things, what they be,\l"
    .string "that we may consider them, and know\l"
    .string "the latter end of them; or declare\l"
    .string "us things for to come.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_23::
    .string "Shew the things that are to come\n"
    .string "hereafter, that we may know that ye\l"
    .string "are gods: yea, do good, or do evil,\l"
    .string "that we may be dismayed, and behold\l"
    .string "it together.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_24::
    .string "Behold, ye are of nothing, and your\n"
    .string "work of nought: an abomination is he\l"
    .string "that chooseth you.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_25::
    .string "I have raised up one from the north,\n"
    .string "and he shall come: from the rising\l"
    .string "of the sun shall he call upon my\l"
    .string "name: and he shall come upon\l"
    .string "princes as upon morter, and as the\l"
    .string "potter treadeth clay.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_26::
    .string "Who hath declared from the\n"
    .string "beginning, that we may know? and\l"
    .string "beforetime, that we may say, He is\l"
    .string "righteous? yea, there is none that\l"
    .string "sheweth, yea, there is none that\l"
    .string "declareth, yea, there is none that\l"
    .string "heareth your words.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_27::
    .string "The first shall say to Zion,\n"
    .string "Behold, behold them: and I will\l"
    .string "give to Jerusalem one that bringeth\l"
    .string "good tidings.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_28::
    .string "For I beheld, and there was no man;\n"
    .string "even among them, and there was no\l"
    .string "counsellor, that, when I asked of\l"
    .string "them, could answer a word.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_41_29::
    .string "Behold, they are all vanity; their\n"
    .string "works are nothing: their molten\l"
    .string "images are wind and confusion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_1::
    .string "Behold my servant, whom I uphold;\n"
    .string "mine elect, in whom my soul\l"
    .string "delighteth; I have put my spirit\l"
    .string "upon him: he shall bring forth\l"
    .string "judgment to the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_2::
    .string "He shall not cry, nor lift up, nor\n"
    .string "cause his voice to be heard in the\l"
    .string "street.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_3::
    .string "A bruised reed shall he not break,\n"
    .string "and the smoking flax shall he not\l"
    .string "quench: he shall bring forth\l"
    .string "judgment unto truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_4::
    .string "He shall not fail nor be\n"
    .string "discouraged, till he have set\l"
    .string "judgment in the earth: and the isles\l"
    .string "shall wait for his law.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_5::
    .string "Thus saith God the LORD, he that\n"
    .string "created the heavens, and stretched\l"
    .string "them out; he that spread forth the\l"
    .string "earth, and that which cometh out of\l"
    .string "it; he that giveth breath unto the\l"
    .string "people upon it, and spirit to them\l"
    .string "that walk therein:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_6::
    .string "I the LORD have called thee in\n"
    .string "righteousness, and will hold thine\l"
    .string "hand, and will keep thee, and give\l"
    .string "thee for a covenant of the people,\l"
    .string "for a light of the Gentiles;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_7::
    .string "To open the blind eyes, to bring\n"
    .string "out the prisoners from the prison,\l"
    .string "and them that sit in darkness out of\l"
    .string "the prison house$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_8::
    .string "I am the LORD: that is my name: and\n"
    .string "my glory will I not give to\l"
    .string "another, neither my praise to graven\l"
    .string "images.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_9::
    .string "Behold, the former things are come\n"
    .string "to pass, and new things do I\l"
    .string "declare: before they spring forth I\l"
    .string "tell you of them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_10::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD a new song, and\n"
    .string "his praise from the end of the earth,\l"
    .string "ye that go down to the sea, and all\l"
    .string "that is therein; the isles, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_11::
    .string "Let the wilderness and the cities\n"
    .string "thereof lift up their voice, the\l"
    .string "villages that Kedar doth inhabit:\l"
    .string "let the inhabitants of the rock sing,\l"
    .string "let them shout from the top of the\l"
    .string "mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_12::
    .string "Let them give glory unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and declare his praise in the\l"
    .string "islands.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_13::
    .string "The LORD shall go forth as a mighty\n"
    .string "man, he shall stir up jealousy\l"
    .string "like a man of war: he shall cry, yea,\l"
    .string "roar; he shall prevail against his\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_14::
    .string "I have long time holden my peace;\n"
    .string "I have been still, and refrained\l"
    .string "myself: now will I cry like a\l"
    .string "travailing woman; I will destroy\l"
    .string "and devour at once.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_15::
    .string "I will make waste mountains and\n"
    .string "hills, and dry up all their herbs;\l"
    .string "and I will make the rivers islands,\l"
    .string "and I will dry up the pools.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_16::
    .string "And I will bring the blind by a\n"
    .string "way that they knew not; I will lead\l"
    .string "them in paths that they have not\l"
    .string "known: I will make darkness light\l"
    .string "before them, and crooked things\l"
    .string "straight. These things will I do\l"
    .string "unto them, and not forsake them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_17::
    .string "They shall be turned back, they\n"
    .string "shall be greatly ashamed, that\l"
    .string "trust in graven images, that say to\l"
    .string "the molten images, Ye are our gods.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_18::
    .string "Hear, ye deaf; and look, ye blind,\n"
    .string "that ye may see.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_19::
    .string "Who is blind, but my servant? or\n"
    .string "deaf, as my messenger that I sent?\l"
    .string "who is blind as he that is perfect,\l"
    .string "and blind as the LORD’s servant?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_20::
    .string "Seeing many things, but thou\n"
    .string "observest not; opening the ears, but\l"
    .string "he heareth not$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_21::
    .string "The LORD is well pleased for his\n"
    .string "righteousness’ sake; he will\l"
    .string "magnify the law, and make it\l"
    .string "honourable.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_22::
    .string "But this is a people robbed and\n"
    .string "spoiled; they are all of them\l"
    .string "snared in holes, and they are hid in\l"
    .string "prison houses: they are for a prey,\l"
    .string "and none delivereth; for a spoil,\l"
    .string "and none saith, Restore.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_23::
    .string "Who among you will give ear to\n"
    .string "this? who will hearken and hear for\l"
    .string "the time to come?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_24::
    .string "Who gave Jacob for a spoil, and\n"
    .string "Israel to the robbers? did not the\l"
    .string "LORD, he against whom we have sinned?\l"
    .string "for they would not walk in his ways,\l"
    .string "neither were they obedient unto his\l"
    .string "law$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_42_25::
    .string "Therefore he hath poured upon him\n"
    .string "the fury of his anger, and the\l"
    .string "strength of battle: and it hath set\l"
    .string "him on fire round about, yet he knew\l"
    .string "not; and it burned him, yet he laid\l"
    .string "it not to heart.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_1::
    .string "But now thus saith the LORD that\n"
    .string "created thee, O Jacob, and he that\l"
    .string "formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for\l"
    .string "I have redeemed thee, I have called\l"
    .string "thee by thy name; thou art mine.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_2::
    .string "When thou passest through the\n"
    .string "waters, I will be with thee; and\l"
    .string "through the rivers, they shall not\l"
    .string "overflow thee: when thou walkest\l"
    .string "through the fire, thou shalt not be\l"
    .string "burned; neither shall the flame\l"
    .string "kindle upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_3::
    .string "For I am the LORD thy God, the Holy\n"
    .string "One of Israel, thy Saviour: I gave\l"
    .string "Egypt for thy ransom, Ethiopia and\l"
    .string "Seba for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_4::
    .string "Since thou wast precious in my\n"
    .string "sight, thou hast been honourable,\l"
    .string "and I have loved thee: therefore\l"
    .string "will I give men for thee, and\l"
    .string "people for thy life.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_5::
    .string "Fear not: for I am with thee: I\n"
    .string "will bring thy seed from the east,\l"
    .string "and gather thee from the west;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_6::
    .string "I will say to the north, Give up;\n"
    .string "and to the south, Keep not back:\l"
    .string "bring my sons from far, and my\l"
    .string "daughters from the ends of the earth;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_7::
    .string "Even every one that is called by my\n"
    .string "name: for I have created him for my\l"
    .string "glory, I have formed him; yea, I have\l"
    .string "made him$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_8::
    .string "Bring forth the blind people that\n"
    .string "have eyes, and the deaf that have\l"
    .string "ears.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_9::
    .string "Let all the nations be gathered\n"
    .string "together, and let the people be\l"
    .string "assembled: who among them can\l"
    .string "declare this, and shew us former\l"
    .string "things? let them bring forth their\l"
    .string "witnesses, that they may be\l"
    .string "justified: or let them hear, and say,\l"
    .string "It is truth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_10::
    .string "Ye are my witnesses, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "and my servant whom I have chosen:\l"
    .string "that ye may know and believe me, and\l"
    .string "understand that I am he: before me\l"
    .string "there was no God formed, neither\l"
    .string "shall there be after me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_11::
    .string "I, even I, am the LORD; and beside me\n"
    .string "there is no saviour.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_12::
    .string "I have declared, and have saved,\n"
    .string "and I have shewed, when there was no\l"
    .string "strange god among you: therefore ye\l"
    .string "are my witnesses, saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "that I am God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_13::
    .string "Yea, before the day was I am he; and\n"
    .string "there is none that can deliver out\l"
    .string "of my hand: I will work, and who\l"
    .string "shall let it?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_14::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, your redeemer,\n"
    .string "the Holy One of Israel; For your\l"
    .string "sake I have sent to Babylon, and have\l"
    .string "brought down all their nobles, and\l"
    .string "the Chaldeans, whose cry is in the\l"
    .string "ships$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_15::
    .string "I am the LORD, your Holy One, the\n"
    .string "creator of Israel, your King.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_16::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, which maketh a\n"
    .string "way in the sea, and a path in the\l"
    .string "mighty waters;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_17::
    .string "Which bringeth forth the chariot\n"
    .string "and horse, the army and the power;\l"
    .string "they shall lie down together, they\l"
    .string "shall not rise: they are extinct,\l"
    .string "they are quenched as tow$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_18::
    .string "Remember ye not the former things,\n"
    .string "neither consider the things of old.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_19::
    .string "Behold, I will do a new thing; now\n"
    .string "it shall spring forth; shall ye\l"
    .string "not know it? I will even make a way\l"
    .string "in the wilderness, and rivers in the\l"
    .string "desert.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_20::
    .string "The beast of the field shall\n"
    .string "honour me, the dragons and the owls:\l"
    .string "because I give waters in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, and rivers in the\l"
    .string "desert, to give drink to my people,\l"
    .string "my chosen.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_21::
    .string "This people have I formed for\n"
    .string "myself; they shall shew forth my\l"
    .string "praise.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_22::
    .string "But thou hast not called upon me,\n"
    .string "O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of\l"
    .string "me, O Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_23::
    .string "Thou hast not brought me the small\n"
    .string "cattle of thy burnt offerings;\l"
    .string "neither hast thou honoured me with\l"
    .string "thy sacrifices. I have not caused\l"
    .string "thee to serve with an offering, nor\l"
    .string "wearied thee with incense.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_24::
    .string "Thou hast bought me no sweet cane\n"
    .string "with money, neither hast thou\l"
    .string "filled me with the fat of thy\l"
    .string "sacrifices: but thou hast made me to\l"
    .string "serve with thy sins, thou hast\l"
    .string "wearied me with thine iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_25::
    .string "I, even I, am he that blotteth out\n"
    .string "thy transgressions for mine own sake,\l"
    .string "and will not remember thy sins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_26::
    .string "Put me in remembrance: let us\n"
    .string "plead together: declare thou, that\l"
    .string "thou mayest be justified.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_27::
    .string "Thy first father hath sinned, and\n"
    .string "thy teachers have transgressed\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_43_28::
    .string "Therefore I have profaned the\n"
    .string "princes of the sanctuary, and have\l"
    .string "given Jacob to the curse, and Israel\l"
    .string "to reproaches.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_1::
    .string "Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant;\n"
    .string "and Israel, whom I have chosen:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD that made thee,\n"
    .string "and formed thee from the womb, which\l"
    .string "will help thee; Fear not, O Jacob,\l"
    .string "my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I\l"
    .string "have chosen$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_3::
    .string "For I will pour water upon him\n"
    .string "that is thirsty, and floods upon the\l"
    .string "dry ground: I will pour my spirit\l"
    .string "upon thy seed, and my blessing upon\l"
    .string "thine offspring:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_4::
    .string "And they shall spring up as among\n"
    .string "the grass, as willows by the water\l"
    .string "courses$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_5::
    .string "One shall say, I am the LORD’s; and\n"
    .string "another shall call himself by the\l"
    .string "name of Jacob; and another shall\l"
    .string "subscribe with his hand unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, and surname himself by the\l"
    .string "name of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_6::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD the King of\n"
    .string "Israel, and his redeemer the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts; I am the first, and I am the\l"
    .string "last; and beside me there is no God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_7::
    .string "And who, as I, shall call, and\n"
    .string "shall declare it, and set it in\l"
    .string "order for me, since I appointed the\l"
    .string "ancient people? and the things that\l"
    .string "are coming, and shall come, let\l"
    .string "them shew unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_8::
    .string "Fear ye not, neither be afraid: have\n"
    .string "not I told thee from that time, and\l"
    .string "have declared it? ye are even my\l"
    .string "witnesses. Is there a God beside me?\l"
    .string "yea, there is no God; I know not any.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_9::
    .string "They that make a graven image are\n"
    .string "all of them vanity; and their\l"
    .string "delectable things shall not\l"
    .string "profit; and they are their own\l"
    .string "witnesses; they see not, nor know;\l"
    .string "that they may be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_10::
    .string "Who hath formed a god, or molten a\n"
    .string "graven image that is profitable for\l"
    .string "nothing?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_11::
    .string "Behold, all his fellows shall\n"
    .string "be ashamed: and the workmen, they are\l"
    .string "of men: let them all be gathered\l"
    .string "together, let them stand up; yet\l"
    .string "they shall fear, and they shall be\l"
    .string "ashamed together$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_12::
    .string "The smith with the tongs both\n"
    .string "worketh in the coals, and fashioneth\l"
    .string "it with hammers, and worketh it with\l"
    .string "the strength of his arms: yea, he is\l"
    .string "hungry, and his strength faileth: he\l"
    .string "drinketh no water, and is faint.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_13::
    .string "The carpenter stretcheth out his\n"
    .string "rule; he marketh it out with a line;\l"
    .string "he fitteth it with planes, and he\l"
    .string "marketh it out with the compass, and\l"
    .string "maketh it after the figure of a man,\l"
    .string "according to the beauty of a man;\l"
    .string "that it may remain in the house.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_14::
    .string "He heweth him down cedars, and\n"
    .string "taketh the cypress and the oak,\l"
    .string "which he strengtheneth for himself\l"
    .string "among the trees of the forest: he\l"
    .string "planteth an ash, and the rain doth\l"
    .string "nourish it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_15::
    .string "Then shall it be for a man to burn:\n"
    .string "for he will take thereof, and warm\l"
    .string "himself; yea, he kindleth it, and\l"
    .string "baketh bread; yea, he maketh a god,\l"
    .string "and worshippeth it; he maketh it a\l"
    .string "graven image, and falleth down\l"
    .string "thereto.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_16::
    .string "He burneth part thereof in the\n"
    .string "fire; with part thereof he eateth\l"
    .string "flesh; he roasteth roast, and is\l"
    .string "satisfied: yea, he warmeth himself,\l"
    .string "and saith, Aha, I am warm, I have seen\l"
    .string "the fire:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_17::
    .string "And the residue thereof he maketh a\n"
    .string "god, even his graven image: he\l"
    .string "falleth down unto it, and\l"
    .string "worshippeth it, and prayeth unto\l"
    .string "it, and saith, Deliver me; for thou\l"
    .string "art my god$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_18::
    .string "They have not known nor understood:\n"
    .string "for he hath shut their eyes, that\l"
    .string "they cannot see; and their hearts,\l"
    .string "that they cannot understand.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_19::
    .string "And none considereth in his heart,\n"
    .string "neither is there knowledge nor\l"
    .string "understanding to say, I have burned\l"
    .string "part of it in the fire; yea, also I\l"
    .string "have baked bread upon the coals\l"
    .string "thereof; I have roasted flesh, and\l"
    .string "eaten it: and shall I make the\l"
    .string "residue thereof an abomination?\l"
    .string "shall I fall down to the stock of a\l"
    .string "tree?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_20::
    .string "He feedeth on ashes: a deceived\n"
    .string "heart hath turned him aside, that he\l"
    .string "cannot deliver his soul, nor say, Is\l"
    .string "there not a lie in my right hand?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_21::
    .string "Remember these, O Jacob and Israel;\n"
    .string "for thou art my servant: I have\l"
    .string "formed thee; thou art my servant: O\l"
    .string "Israel, thou shalt not be forgotten\l"
    .string "of me$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_22::
    .string "I have blotted out, as a thick\n"
    .string "cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a\l"
    .string "cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for\l"
    .string "I have redeemed thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_23::
    .string "Sing, O ye heavens; for the LORD\n"
    .string "hath done it: shout, ye lower parts\l"
    .string "of the earth: break forth into\l"
    .string "singing, ye mountains, O forest, and\l"
    .string "every tree therein: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "redeemed Jacob, and glorified\l"
    .string "himself in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_24::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, thy redeemer,\n"
    .string "and he that formed thee from the\l"
    .string "womb, I am the LORD that maketh all\l"
    .string "things; that stretcheth forth the\l"
    .string "heavens alone; that spreadeth\l"
    .string "abroad the earth by myself;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_25::
    .string "That frustrateth the tokens of the\n"
    .string "liars, and maketh diviners mad; that\l"
    .string "turneth wise men backward, and maketh\l"
    .string "their knowledge foolish;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_26::
    .string "That confirmeth the word of his\n"
    .string "servant, and performeth the counsel\l"
    .string "of his messengers; that saith to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, Thou shalt be inhabited;\l"
    .string "and to the cities of Judah, Ye shall\l"
    .string "be built, and I will raise up the\l"
    .string "decayed places thereof:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_27::
    .string "That saith to the deep, Be dry, and\n"
    .string "I will dry up thy rivers:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_44_28::
    .string "That saith of Cyrus, He is my\n"
    .string "shepherd, and shall perform all\l"
    .string "my pleasure: even saying to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and\l"
    .string "to the temple, Thy foundation\l"
    .string "shall be laid$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD to his anointed,\n"
    .string "to Cyrus, whose right hand I have\l"
    .string "holden, to subdue nations before\l"
    .string "him; and I will loose the loins of\l"
    .string "kings, to open before him the two\l"
    .string "leaved gates; and the gates shall\l"
    .string "not be shut;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_2::
    .string "I will go before thee, and make the\n"
    .string "crooked places straight: I will\l"
    .string "break in pieces the gates of brass,\l"
    .string "and cut in sunder the bars of iron:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_3::
    .string "And I will give thee the treasures\n"
    .string "of darkness, and hidden riches of\l"
    .string "secret places, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "know that I, the LORD, which call\l"
    .string "thee by thy name, am the God of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_4::
    .string "For Jacob my servant’s sake, and\n"
    .string "Israel mine elect, I have even\l"
    .string "called thee by thy name: I have\l"
    .string "surnamed thee, though thou hast not\l"
    .string "known me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_5::
    .string "I am the LORD, and there is none\n"
    .string "else, there is no God beside me: I\l"
    .string "girded thee, though thou hast not\l"
    .string "known me:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_6::
    .string "That they may know from the rising\n"
    .string "of the sun, and from the west, that\l"
    .string "there is none beside me. I am the\l"
    .string "LORD, and there is none else$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_7::
    .string "I form the light, and create\n"
    .string "darkness: I make peace, and create\l"
    .string "evil: I the LORD do all these\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_8::
    .string "Drop down, ye heavens, from above,\n"
    .string "and let the skies pour down\l"
    .string "righteousness: let the earth open,\l"
    .string "and let them bring forth salvation,\l"
    .string "and let righteousness spring up\l"
    .string "together; I the LORD have created it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_9::
    .string "Woe unto him that striveth with his\n"
    .string "Maker! Let the potsherd strive with\l"
    .string "the potsherds of the earth. Shall\l"
    .string "the clay say to him that fashioneth\l"
    .string "it, What makest thou? or thy work, He\l"
    .string "hath no hands?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_10::
    .string "Woe unto him that saith unto his\n"
    .string "father, What begettest thou? or to\l"
    .string "the woman, What hast thou brought\l"
    .string "forth?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_11::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the Holy One of\n"
    .string "Israel, and his Maker, Ask me of\l"
    .string "things to come concerning my sons,\l"
    .string "and concerning the work of my hands\l"
    .string "command ye me$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_12::
    .string "I have made the earth, and created\n"
    .string "man upon it: I, even my hands, have\l"
    .string "stretched out the heavens, and all\l"
    .string "their host have I commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_13::
    .string "I have raised him up in\n"
    .string "righteousness, and I will direct\l"
    .string "all his ways: he shall build my\l"
    .string "city, and he shall let go my\l"
    .string "captives, not for price nor reward,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_14::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, The labour of\n"
    .string "Egypt, and merchandise of Ethiopia\l"
    .string "and of the Sabeans, men of stature,\l"
    .string "shall come over unto thee, and they\l"
    .string "shall be thine: they shall come\l"
    .string "after thee; in chains they shall\l"
    .string "come over, and they shall fall\l"
    .string "down unto thee, they shall make\l"
    .string "supplication unto thee, saying,\l"
    .string "Surely God is in thee; and there is\l"
    .string "none else, there is no God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_15::
    .string "Verily thou art a God that hidest\n"
    .string "thyself, O God of Israel, the\l"
    .string "Saviour.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_16::
    .string "They shall be ashamed, and also\n"
    .string "confounded, all of them: they\l"
    .string "shall go to confusion together that\l"
    .string "are makers of idols.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_17::
    .string "But Israel shall be saved in the\n"
    .string "LORD with an everlasting salvation:\l"
    .string "ye shall not be ashamed nor\l"
    .string "confounded world without end.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_18::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD that created\n"
    .string "the heavens; God himself that formed\l"
    .string "the earth and made it; he hath\l"
    .string "established it, he created it not in\l"
    .string "vain, he formed it to be inhabited: I\l"
    .string "am the LORD; and there is none else.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_19::
    .string "I have not spoken in secret, in a\n"
    .string "dark place of the earth: I said not\l"
    .string "unto the seed of Jacob, Seek ye me in\l"
    .string "vain: I the LORD speak\l"
    .string "righteousness, I declare things that\l"
    .string "are right.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_20::
    .string "Assemble yourselves and come; draw\n"
    .string "near together, ye that are escaped\l"
    .string "of the nations: they have no\l"
    .string "knowledge that set up the wood of\l"
    .string "their graven image, and pray unto a\l"
    .string "god that cannot save.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_21::
    .string "Tell ye, and bring them near; yea,\n"
    .string "let them take counsel together: who\l"
    .string "hath declared this from ancient\l"
    .string "time? who hath told it from that\l"
    .string "time? have not I the LORD? and there\l"
    .string "is no God else beside me; a just God\l"
    .string "and a Saviour; there is none beside\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_22::
    .string "Look unto me, and be ye saved, all\n"
    .string "the ends of the earth: for I am God,\l"
    .string "and there is none else.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_23::
    .string "I have sworn by myself, the word is\n"
    .string "gone out of my mouth in\l"
    .string "righteousness, and shall not\l"
    .string "return, That unto me every knee\l"
    .string "shall bow, every tongue shall\l"
    .string "swear.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_24::
    .string "Surely, shall one say, in the LORD\n"
    .string "have I righteousness and strength:\l"
    .string "even to him shall men come; and all\l"
    .string "that are incensed against him shall\l"
    .string "be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_45_25::
    .string "In the LORD shall all the seed of\n"
    .string "Israel be justified, and shall\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_1::
    .string "Bel boweth down, Nebo stoopeth,\n"
    .string "their idols were upon the beasts,\l"
    .string "and upon the cattle: your carriages\l"
    .string "were heavy loaden; they are a burden\l"
    .string "to the weary beast.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_2::
    .string "They stoop, they bow down together;\n"
    .string "they could not deliver the burden,\l"
    .string "but themselves are gone into\l"
    .string "captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_3::
    .string "Hearken unto me, O house of Jacob,\n"
    .string "and all the remnant of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, which are borne by me from\l"
    .string "the belly, which are carried from\l"
    .string "the womb:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_4::
    .string "And even to your old age I am he;\n"
    .string "and even to hoar hairs will I carry\l"
    .string "you: I have made, and I will bear;\l"
    .string "even I will carry, and will\l"
    .string "deliver you$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_5::
    .string "To whom will ye liken me, and make\n"
    .string "me equal, and compare me, that we\l"
    .string "may be like?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_6::
    .string "They lavish gold out of the bag,\n"
    .string "and weigh silver in the balance, and\l"
    .string "hire a goldsmith; and he maketh it a\l"
    .string "god: they fall down, yea, they\l"
    .string "worship$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_7::
    .string "They bear him upon the shoulder,\n"
    .string "they carry him, and set him in his\l"
    .string "place, and he standeth; from his\l"
    .string "place shall he not remove: yea, one\l"
    .string "shall cry unto him, yet can he not\l"
    .string "answer, nor save him out of his\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_8::
    .string "Remember this, and shew yourselves\n"
    .string "men: bring it again to mind, O ye\l"
    .string "transgressors.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_9::
    .string "Remember the former things of old:\n"
    .string "for I am God, and there is none else;\l"
    .string "I am God, and there is none like me,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_10::
    .string "Declaring the end from the\n"
    .string "beginning, and from ancient times the\l"
    .string "things that are not yet done, saying,\l"
    .string "My counsel shall stand, and I will\l"
    .string "do all my pleasure:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_11::
    .string "Calling a ravenous bird from the\n"
    .string "east, the man that executeth my\l"
    .string "counsel from a far country: yea, I\l"
    .string "have spoken it, I will also bring\l"
    .string "it to pass; I have purposed it, I\l"
    .string "will also do it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_12::
    .string "Hearken unto me, ye stouthearted,\n"
    .string "that are far from righteousness:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_46_13::
    .string "I bring near my righteousness; it\n"
    .string "shall not be far off, and my\l"
    .string "salvation shall not tarry: and I\l"
    .string "will place salvation in Zion for\l"
    .string "Israel my glory$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_1::
    .string "Come down, and sit in the dust, O\n"
    .string "virgin daughter of Babylon, sit on\l"
    .string "the ground: there is no throne, O\l"
    .string "daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou\l"
    .string "shalt no more be called tender and\l"
    .string "delicate.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_2::
    .string "Take the millstones, and grind\n"
    .string "meal: uncover thy locks, make bare\l"
    .string "the leg, uncover the thigh, pass\l"
    .string "over the rivers.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_3::
    .string "Thy nakedness shall be uncovered,\n"
    .string "yea, thy shame shall be seen: I\l"
    .string "will take vengeance, and I will\l"
    .string "not meet thee as a man.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_4::
    .string "As for our redeemer, the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts is his name, the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_5::
    .string "Sit thou silent, and get thee into\n"
    .string "darkness, O daughter of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be\l"
    .string "called, The lady of kingdoms.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_6::
    .string "I was wroth with my people, I have\n"
    .string "polluted mine inheritance, and\l"
    .string "given them into thine hand: thou\l"
    .string "didst shew them no mercy; upon the\l"
    .string "ancient hast thou very heavily laid\l"
    .string "thy yoke.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_7::
    .string "And thou saidst, I shall be a lady\n"
    .string "for ever: so that thou didst not lay\l"
    .string "these things to thy heart, neither\l"
    .string "didst remember the latter end of it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_8::
    .string "Therefore hear now this, thou that\n"
    .string "art given to pleasures, that\l"
    .string "dwellest carelessly, that sayest\l"
    .string "in thine heart, I am, and none else\l"
    .string "beside me; I shall not sit as a\l"
    .string "widow, neither shall I know the\l"
    .string "loss of children:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_9::
    .string "But these two things shall come to\n"
    .string "thee in a moment in one day, the loss\l"
    .string "of children, and widowhood: they\l"
    .string "shall come upon thee in their\l"
    .string "perfection for the multitude of thy\l"
    .string "sorceries, and for the great\l"
    .string "abundance of thine enchantments$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_10::
    .string "For thou hast trusted in thy\n"
    .string "wickedness: thou hast said, None\l"
    .string "seeth me. Thy wisdom and thy\l"
    .string "knowledge, it hath perverted thee;\l"
    .string "and thou hast said in thine heart, I\l"
    .string "am, and none else beside me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_11::
    .string "Therefore shall evil come upon\n"
    .string "thee; thou shalt not know from\l"
    .string "whence it riseth: and mischief\l"
    .string "shall fall upon thee; thou shalt\l"
    .string "not be able to put it off: and\l"
    .string "desolation shall come upon thee\l"
    .string "suddenly, which thou shalt not know.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_12::
    .string "Stand now with thine enchantments,\n"
    .string "and with the multitude of thy\l"
    .string "sorceries, wherein thou hast\l"
    .string "laboured from thy youth; if so be\l"
    .string "thou shalt be able to profit, if so\l"
    .string "be thou mayest prevail.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_13::
    .string "Thou art wearied in the multitude\n"
    .string "of thy counsels. Let now the\l"
    .string "astrologers, the stargazers, the\l"
    .string "monthly prognosticators, stand up,\l"
    .string "and save thee from these things that\l"
    .string "shall come upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_14::
    .string "Behold, they shall be as stubble;\n"
    .string "the fire shall burn them; they\l"
    .string "shall not deliver themselves from\l"
    .string "the power of the flame: there\l"
    .string "shall not be a coal to warm at, nor\l"
    .string "fire to sit before it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_47_15::
    .string "Thus shall they be unto thee with\n"
    .string "whom thou hast laboured, even thy\l"
    .string "merchants, from thy youth: they\l"
    .string "shall wander every one to his\l"
    .string "quarter; none shall save thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_1::
    .string "Hear ye this, O house of Jacob,\n"
    .string "which are called by the name of\l"
    .string "Israel, and are come forth out of the\l"
    .string "waters of Judah, which swear by the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD, and make mention of\l"
    .string "the God of Israel, but not in truth,\l"
    .string "nor in righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_2::
    .string "For they call themselves of the\n"
    .string "holy city, and stay themselves upon\l"
    .string "the God of Israel; The LORD of hosts\l"
    .string "is his name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_3::
    .string "I have declared the former things\n"
    .string "from the beginning; and they went\l"
    .string "forth out of my mouth, and I shewed\l"
    .string "them; I did them suddenly, and they\l"
    .string "came to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_4::
    .string "Because I knew that thou art\n"
    .string "obstinate, and thy neck is an iron\l"
    .string "sinew, and thy brow brass;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_5::
    .string "I have even from the beginning\n"
    .string "declared it to thee; before it came\l"
    .string "to pass I shewed it thee: lest thou\l"
    .string "shouldest say, Mine idol hath done\l"
    .string "them, and my graven image, and my\l"
    .string "molten image, hath commanded them$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_6::
    .string "Thou hast heard, see all this; and\n"
    .string "will not ye declare it? I have\l"
    .string "shewed thee new things from this\l"
    .string "time, even hidden things, and thou\l"
    .string "didst not know them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_7::
    .string "They are created now, and not from\n"
    .string "the beginning; even before the day\l"
    .string "when thou heardest them not; lest\l"
    .string "thou shouldest say, Behold, I knew\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_8::
    .string "Yea, thou heardest not; yea, thou\n"
    .string "knewest not; yea, from that time that\l"
    .string "thine ear was not opened: for I knew\l"
    .string "that thou wouldest deal very\l"
    .string "treacherously, and wast called a\l"
    .string "transgressor from the womb.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_9::
    .string "For my name’s sake will I defer\n"
    .string "mine anger, and for my praise will\l"
    .string "I refrain for thee, that I cut thee\l"
    .string "not off.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_10::
    .string "Behold, I have refined thee, but\n"
    .string "not with silver; I have chosen thee\l"
    .string "in the furnace of affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_11::
    .string "For mine own sake, even for mine own\n"
    .string "sake, will I do it: for how should\l"
    .string "my name be polluted? and I will\l"
    .string "not give my glory unto another.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_12::
    .string "Hearken unto me, O Jacob and\n"
    .string "Israel, my called; I am he; I am the\l"
    .string "first, I also am the last.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_13::
    .string "Mine hand also hath laid the\n"
    .string "foundation of the earth, and my right\l"
    .string "hand hath spanned the heavens: when\l"
    .string "I call unto them, they stand up\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_14::
    .string "All ye, assemble yourselves, and\n"
    .string "hear; which among them hath declared\l"
    .string "these things? The LORD hath loved\l"
    .string "him: he will do his pleasure on\l"
    .string "Babylon, and his arm shall be on\l"
    .string "the Chaldeans.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_15::
    .string "I, even I, have spoken; yea, I have\n"
    .string "called him: I have brought him, and\l"
    .string "he shall make his way prosperous.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_16::
    .string "Come ye near unto me, hear ye this; I\n"
    .string "have not spoken in secret from the\l"
    .string "beginning; from the time that it was,\l"
    .string "there am I: and now the Lord GOD, and\l"
    .string "his Spirit, hath sent me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_17::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, thy Redeemer,\n"
    .string "the Holy One of Israel; I am the\l"
    .string "LORD thy God which teacheth thee to\l"
    .string "profit, which leadeth thee by the\l"
    .string "way that thou shouldest go.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_18::
    .string "O that thou hadst hearkened to my\n"
    .string "commandments! then had thy peace\l"
    .string "been as a river, and thy\l"
    .string "righteousness as the waves of the\l"
    .string "sea:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_19::
    .string "Thy seed also had been as the sand,\n"
    .string "and the offspring of thy bowels\l"
    .string "like the gravel thereof; his name\l"
    .string "should not have been cut off nor\l"
    .string "destroyed from before me$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_20::
    .string "Go ye forth of Babylon, flee ye\n"
    .string "from the Chaldeans, with a voice of\l"
    .string "singing declare ye, tell this,\l"
    .string "utter it even to the end of the earth;\l"
    .string "say ye, The LORD hath redeemed his\l"
    .string "servant Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_21::
    .string "And they thirsted not when he led\n"
    .string "them through the deserts: he caused\l"
    .string "the waters to flow out of the rock\l"
    .string "for them: he clave the rock also,\l"
    .string "and the waters gushed out.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_48_22::
    .string "There is no peace, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "unto the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_1::
    .string "Listen, O isles, unto me; and\n"
    .string "hearken, ye people, from far; The\l"
    .string "LORD hath called me from the womb;\l"
    .string "from the bowels of my mother hath he\l"
    .string "made mention of my name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_2::
    .string "And he hath made my mouth like a\n"
    .string "sharp sword; in the shadow of his\l"
    .string "hand hath he hid me, and made me a\l"
    .string "polished shaft; in his quiver hath\l"
    .string "he hid me;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_3::
    .string "And said unto me, Thou art my\n"
    .string "servant, O Israel, in whom I will\l"
    .string "be glorified$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_4::
    .string "Then I said, I have laboured in\n"
    .string "vain, I have spent my strength for\l"
    .string "nought, and in vain: yet surely my\l"
    .string "judgment is with the LORD, and my\l"
    .string "work with my God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_5::
    .string "And now, saith the LORD that formed\n"
    .string "me from the womb to be his servant, to\l"
    .string "bring Jacob again to him, Though\l"
    .string "Israel be not gathered, yet shall I\l"
    .string "be glorious in the eyes of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and my God shall be my strength.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_6::
    .string "And he said, It is a light thing\n"
    .string "that thou shouldest be my servant to\l"
    .string "raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to\l"
    .string "restore the preserved of Israel: I\l"
    .string "will also give thee for a light to\l"
    .string "the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my\l"
    .string "salvation unto the end of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_7::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the Redeemer of\n"
    .string "Israel, and his Holy One, to him\l"
    .string "whom man despiseth, to him whom the\l"
    .string "nation abhorreth, to a servant of\l"
    .string "rulers, Kings shall see and arise,\l"
    .string "princes also shall worship,\l"
    .string "because of the LORD that is\l"
    .string "faithful, and the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel, and he shall choose thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_8::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, In an\n"
    .string "acceptable time have I heard thee,\l"
    .string "and in a day of salvation have I\l"
    .string "helped thee: and I will preserve\l"
    .string "thee, and give thee for a covenant of\l"
    .string "the people, to establish the\l"
    .string "earth, to cause to inherit the\l"
    .string "desolate heritages;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_9::
    .string "That thou mayest say to the\n"
    .string "prisoners, Go forth; to them that are\l"
    .string "in darkness, Shew yourselves. They\l"
    .string "shall feed in the ways, and their\l"
    .string "pastures shall be in all high\l"
    .string "places$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_10::
    .string "They shall not hunger nor thirst;\n"
    .string "neither shall the heat nor sun\l"
    .string "smite them: for he that hath mercy on\l"
    .string "them shall lead them, even by the\l"
    .string "springs of water shall he guide\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_11::
    .string "And I will make all my mountains\n"
    .string "a way, and my highways shall be\l"
    .string "exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_12::
    .string "Behold, these shall come from far:\n"
    .string "and, lo, these from the north and\l"
    .string "from the west; and these from the\l"
    .string "land of Sinim.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_13::
    .string "Sing, O heavens; and be joyful, O\n"
    .string "earth; and break forth into singing,\l"
    .string "O mountains: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "comforted his people, and will\l"
    .string "have mercy upon his afflicted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_14::
    .string "But Zion said, The LORD hath\n"
    .string "forsaken me, and my Lord hath\l"
    .string "forgotten me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_15::
    .string "Can a woman forget her sucking\n"
    .string "child, that she should not have\l"
    .string "compassion on the son of her womb?\l"
    .string "yea, they may forget, yet will I not\l"
    .string "forget thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_16::
    .string "Behold, I have graven thee upon the\n"
    .string "palms of my hands; thy walls are\l"
    .string "continually before me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_17::
    .string "Thy children shall make haste; thy\n"
    .string "destroyers and they that made thee\l"
    .string "waste shall go forth of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_18::
    .string "Lift up thine eyes round about, and\n"
    .string "behold: all these gather\l"
    .string "themselves together, and come to thee\l"
    .string " As I live, saith the LORD, thou\l"
    .string "shalt surely clothe thee with them\l"
    .string "all, as with an ornament, and bind\l"
    .string "them on thee, as a bride doeth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_19::
    .string "For thy waste and thy desolate\n"
    .string "places, and the land of thy\l"
    .string "destruction, shall even now be too\l"
    .string "narrow by reason of the inhabitants,\l"
    .string "and they that swallowed thee up\l"
    .string "shall be far away.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_20::
    .string "The children which thou shalt\n"
    .string "have, after thou hast lost the\l"
    .string "other, shall say again in thine\l"
    .string "ears, The place is too strait for\l"
    .string "me: give place to me that I may\l"
    .string "dwell.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_21::
    .string "Then shalt thou say in thine heart,\n"
    .string "Who hath begotten me these, seeing I\l"
    .string "have lost my children, and am\l"
    .string "desolate, a captive, and removing\l"
    .string "to and fro? and who hath brought up\l"
    .string "these? Behold, I was left alone;\l"
    .string "these, where had they been?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_22::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will lift up mine hand to the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, and set up my standard to\l"
    .string "the people: and they shall bring\l"
    .string "thy sons in their arms, and thy\l"
    .string "daughters shall be carried upon\l"
    .string "their shoulders$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_23::
    .string "And kings shall be thy nursing\n"
    .string "fathers, and their queens thy nursing\l"
    .string "mothers: they shall bow down to thee\l"
    .string "with their face toward the earth, and\l"
    .string "lick up the dust of thy feet; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt know that I am the LORD:\l"
    .string "for they shall not be ashamed that\l"
    .string "wait for me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_24::
    .string "Shall the prey be taken from the\n"
    .string "mighty, or the lawful captive\l"
    .string "delivered?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_25::
    .string "But thus saith the LORD, Even the\n"
    .string "captives of the mighty shall be\l"
    .string "taken away, and the prey of the\l"
    .string "terrible shall be delivered: for I\l"
    .string "will contend with him that\l"
    .string "contendeth with thee, and I will\l"
    .string "save thy children$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_49_26::
    .string "And I will feed them that oppress\n"
    .string "thee with their own flesh; and they\l"
    .string "shall be drunken with their own\l"
    .string "blood, as with sweet wine: and all\l"
    .string "flesh shall know that I the LORD am\l"
    .string "thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the\l"
    .string "mighty One of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Where is the\n"
    .string "bill of your mother’s divorcement,\l"
    .string "whom I have put away? or which of my\l"
    .string "creditors is it to whom I have sold\l"
    .string "you? Behold, for your iniquities\l"
    .string "have ye sold yourselves, and for\l"
    .string "your transgressions is your mother\l"
    .string "put away.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_2::
    .string "Wherefore, when I came, was there no\n"
    .string "man? when I called, was there none\l"
    .string "to answer? Is my hand shortened at\l"
    .string "all, that it cannot redeem? or have\l"
    .string "I no power to deliver? behold, at\l"
    .string "my rebuke I dry up the sea, I make\l"
    .string "the rivers a wilderness: their fish\l"
    .string "stinketh, because there is no water,\l"
    .string "and dieth for thirst.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_3::
    .string "I clothe the heavens with\n"
    .string "blackness, and I make sackcloth\l"
    .string "their covering.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_4::
    .string "The Lord GOD hath given me the\n"
    .string "tongue of the learned, that I should\l"
    .string "know how to speak a word in season to\l"
    .string "him that is weary: he wakeneth\l"
    .string "morning by morning, he wakeneth mine\l"
    .string "ear to hear as the learned.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_5::
    .string "The Lord GOD hath opened mine ear,\n"
    .string "and I was not rebellious, neither\l"
    .string "turned away back.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_6::
    .string "I gave my back to the smiters, and my\n"
    .string "cheeks to them that plucked off the\l"
    .string "hair: I hid not my face from shame and\l"
    .string "spitting.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_7::
    .string "For the Lord GOD will help me;\n"
    .string "therefore shall I not be\l"
    .string "confounded: therefore have I set my\l"
    .string "face like a flint, and I know that I\l"
    .string "shall not be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_8::
    .string "He is near that justifieth me; who\n"
    .string "will contend with me? let us stand\l"
    .string "together: who is mine adversary? let\l"
    .string "him come near to me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_9::
    .string "Behold, the Lord GOD will help\n"
    .string "me; who is he that shall condemn me?\l"
    .string "lo, they all shall wax old as a\l"
    .string "garment; the moth shall eat them up.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_10::
    .string "Who is among you that feareth the\n"
    .string "LORD, that obeyeth the voice of his\l"
    .string "servant, that walketh in darkness,\l"
    .string "and hath no light? let him trust in\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD, and stay upon\l"
    .string "his God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_50_11::
    .string "Behold, all ye that kindle a\n"
    .string "fire, that compass yourselves about\l"
    .string "with sparks: walk in the light of\l"
    .string "your fire, and in the sparks that ye\l"
    .string "have kindled. This shall ye have of\l"
    .string "mine hand; ye shall lie down in\l"
    .string "sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_1::
    .string "Hearken to me, ye that follow after\n"
    .string "righteousness, ye that seek the LORD:\l"
    .string "look unto the rock whence ye are\l"
    .string "hewn, and to the hole of the pit\l"
    .string "whence ye are digged.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_2::
    .string "Look unto Abraham your father, and\n"
    .string "unto Sarah that bare you: for I\l"
    .string "called him alone, and blessed him,\l"
    .string "and increased him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_3::
    .string "For the LORD shall comfort Zion: he\n"
    .string "will comfort all her waste\l"
    .string "places; and he will make her\l"
    .string "wilderness like Eden, and her\l"
    .string "desert like the garden of the LORD;\l"
    .string "joy and gladness shall be found\l"
    .string "therein, thanksgiving, and the voice\l"
    .string "of melody.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_4::
    .string "Hearken unto me, my people; and\n"
    .string "give ear unto me, O my nation: for a\l"
    .string "law shall proceed from me, and I\l"
    .string "will make my judgment to rest for a\l"
    .string "light of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_5::
    .string "My righteousness is near; my\n"
    .string "salvation is gone forth, and mine\l"
    .string "arms shall judge the people; the\l"
    .string "isles shall wait upon me, and on\l"
    .string "mine arm shall they trust.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_6::
    .string "Lift up your eyes to the heavens,\n"
    .string "and look upon the earth beneath: for\l"
    .string "the heavens shall vanish away like\l"
    .string "smoke, and the earth shall wax old\l"
    .string "like a garment, and they that dwell\l"
    .string "therein shall die in like manner:\l"
    .string "but my salvation shall be for ever,\l"
    .string "and my righteousness shall not be\l"
    .string "abolished.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_7::
    .string "Hearken unto me, ye that know\n"
    .string "righteousness, the people in whose\l"
    .string "heart is my law; fear ye not the\l"
    .string "reproach of men, neither be ye\l"
    .string "afraid of their revilings.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_8::
    .string "For the moth shall eat them up\n"
    .string "like a garment, and the worm shall\l"
    .string "eat them like wool: but my\l"
    .string "righteousness shall be for ever,\l"
    .string "and my salvation from generation to\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_9::
    .string "Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm\n"
    .string "of the LORD; awake, as in the ancient\l"
    .string "days, in the generations of old. Art\l"
    .string "thou not it that hath cut Rahab, and\l"
    .string "wounded the dragon?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_10::
    .string "Art thou not it which hath dried the\n"
    .string "sea, the waters of the great deep;\l"
    .string "that hath made the depths of the sea\l"
    .string "a way for the ransomed to pass over?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_11::
    .string "Therefore the redeemed of the LORD\n"
    .string "shall return, and come with singing\l"
    .string "unto Zion; and everlasting joy\l"
    .string "shall be upon their head: they\l"
    .string "shall obtain gladness and joy; and\l"
    .string "sorrow and mourning shall flee away$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_12::
    .string "I, even I, am he that comforteth you:\n"
    .string "who art thou, that thou shouldest be\l"
    .string "afraid of a man that shall die, and\l"
    .string "of the son of man which shall be\l"
    .string "made as grass;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_13::
    .string "And forgettest the LORD thy maker,\n"
    .string "that hath stretched forth the\l"
    .string "heavens, and laid the foundations of\l"
    .string "the earth; and hast feared\l"
    .string "continually every day because of\l"
    .string "the fury of the oppressor, as if he\l"
    .string "were ready to destroy? and where is\l"
    .string "the fury of the oppressor?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_14::
    .string "The captive exile hasteneth that\n"
    .string "he may be loosed, and that he should\l"
    .string "not die in the pit, nor that his\l"
    .string "bread should fail$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_15::
    .string "But I am the LORD thy God, that\n"
    .string "divided the sea, whose waves roared:\l"
    .string "The LORD of hosts is his name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_16::
    .string "And I have put my words in thy\n"
    .string "mouth, and I have covered thee in the\l"
    .string "shadow of mine hand, that I may\l"
    .string "plant the heavens, and lay the\l"
    .string "foundations of the earth, and say\l"
    .string "unto Zion, Thou art my people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_17::
    .string "Awake, awake, stand up, O\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, which hast drunk at the\l"
    .string "hand of the LORD the cup of his fury;\l"
    .string "thou hast drunken the dregs of the\l"
    .string "cup of trembling, and wrung them\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_18::
    .string "There is none to guide her among\n"
    .string "all the sons whom she hath brought\l"
    .string "forth; neither is there any that\l"
    .string "taketh her by the hand of all the\l"
    .string "sons that she hath brought up.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_19::
    .string "These two things are come unto thee;\n"
    .string "who shall be sorry for thee?\l"
    .string "desolation, and destruction, and the\l"
    .string "famine, and the sword: by whom shall\l"
    .string "I comfort thee?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_20::
    .string "Thy sons have fainted, they lie at\n"
    .string "the head of all the streets, as a\l"
    .string "wild bull in a net: they are full\l"
    .string "of the fury of the LORD, the rebuke of\l"
    .string "thy God$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_21::
    .string "Therefore hear now this, thou\n"
    .string "afflicted, and drunken, but not with\l"
    .string "wine:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_22::
    .string "Thus saith thy Lord the LORD, and\n"
    .string "thy God that pleadeth the cause of\l"
    .string "his people, Behold, I have taken\l"
    .string "out of thine hand the cup of\l"
    .string "trembling, even the dregs of the cup\l"
    .string "of my fury; thou shalt no more drink\l"
    .string "it again:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_51_23::
    .string "But I will put it into the hand of\n"
    .string "them that afflict thee; which have\l"
    .string "said to thy soul, Bow down, that we\l"
    .string "may go over: and thou hast laid thy\l"
    .string "body as the ground, and as the\l"
    .string "street, to them that went over$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_1::
    .string "Awake, awake; put on thy strength, O\n"
    .string "Zion; put on thy beautiful\l"
    .string "garments, O Jerusalem, the holy\l"
    .string "city: for henceforth there shall no\l"
    .string "more come into thee the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised and the unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_2::
    .string "Shake thyself from the dust; arise,\n"
    .string "and sit down, O Jerusalem: loose\l"
    .string "thyself from the bands of thy neck, O\l"
    .string "captive daughter of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_3::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Ye have\n"
    .string "sold yourselves for nought; and ye\l"
    .string "shall be redeemed without money.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_4::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD, My\n"
    .string "people went down aforetime into\l"
    .string "Egypt to sojourn there; and the\l"
    .string "Assyrian oppressed them without\l"
    .string "cause.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_5::
    .string "Now therefore, what have I here,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that my people is\l"
    .string "taken away for nought? they that\l"
    .string "rule over them make them to howl,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; and my name\l"
    .string "continually every day is\l"
    .string "blasphemed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_6::
    .string "Therefore my people shall know\n"
    .string "my name: therefore they shall know\l"
    .string "in that day that I am he that doth\l"
    .string "speak: behold, it is I.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_7::
    .string "How beautiful upon the mountains\n"
    .string "are the feet of him that bringeth\l"
    .string "good tidings, that publisheth\l"
    .string "peace; that bringeth good tidings of\l"
    .string "good, that publisheth salvation;\l"
    .string "that saith unto Zion, Thy God\l"
    .string "reigneth!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_8::
    .string "Thy watchmen shall lift up the\n"
    .string "voice; with the voice together\l"
    .string "shall they sing: for they shall\l"
    .string "see eye to eye, when the LORD shall\l"
    .string "bring again Zion$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_9::
    .string "Break forth into joy, sing together,\n"
    .string "ye waste places of Jerusalem: for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath comforted his people,\l"
    .string "he hath redeemed Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_10::
    .string "The LORD hath made bare his holy\n"
    .string "arm in the eyes of all the nations;\l"
    .string "and all the ends of the earth\l"
    .string "shall see the salvation of our God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_11::
    .string "Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out\n"
    .string "from thence, touch no unclean thing;\l"
    .string "go ye out of the midst of her; be ye\l"
    .string "clean, that bear the vessels of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_12::
    .string "For ye shall not go out with haste,\n"
    .string "nor go by flight: for the LORD will\l"
    .string "go before you; and the God of Israel\l"
    .string "will be your rereward.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_13::
    .string "Behold, my servant shall deal\n"
    .string "prudently, he shall be exalted and\l"
    .string "extolled, and be very high.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_14::
    .string "As many were astonied at thee; his\n"
    .string "visage was so marred more than any\l"
    .string "man, and his form more than the sons\l"
    .string "of men:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_52_15::
    .string "So shall he sprinkle many\n"
    .string "nations; the kings shall shut their\l"
    .string "mouths at him: for that which had not\l"
    .string "been told them shall they see; and\l"
    .string "that which they had not heard shall\l"
    .string "they consider$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_1::
    .string "Who hath believed our report? and\n"
    .string "to whom is the arm of the LORD\l"
    .string "revealed?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_2::
    .string "For he shall grow up before him as\n"
    .string "a tender plant, and as a root out of\l"
    .string "a dry ground: he hath no form nor\l"
    .string "comeliness; and when we shall see\l"
    .string "him, there is no beauty that we\l"
    .string "should desire him$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_3::
    .string "He is despised and rejected of men;\n"
    .string "a man of sorrows, and acquainted with\l"
    .string "grief: and we hid as it were our faces\l"
    .string "from him; he was despised, and we\l"
    .string "esteemed him not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_4::
    .string "Surely he hath borne our griefs,\n"
    .string "and carried our sorrows: yet we did\l"
    .string "esteem him stricken, smitten of God,\l"
    .string "and afflicted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_5::
    .string "But he was wounded for our\n"
    .string "transgressions, he was bruised for\l"
    .string "our iniquities: the chastisement of\l"
    .string "our peace was upon him; and with his\l"
    .string "stripes we are healed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_6::
    .string "All we like sheep have gone\n"
    .string "astray; we have turned every one to\l"
    .string "his own way; and the LORD hath laid\l"
    .string "on him the iniquity of us all.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_7::
    .string "He was oppressed, and he was\n"
    .string "afflicted, yet he opened not his\l"
    .string "mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the\l"
    .string "slaughter, and as a sheep before her\l"
    .string "shearers is dumb, so he openeth not\l"
    .string "his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_8::
    .string "He was taken from prison and from\n"
    .string "judgment: and who shall declare his\l"
    .string "generation? for he was cut off out of\l"
    .string "the land of the living: for the\l"
    .string "transgression of my people was he\l"
    .string "stricken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_9::
    .string "And he made his grave with the\n"
    .string "wicked, and with the rich in his\l"
    .string "death; because he had done no\l"
    .string "violence, neither was any deceit in\l"
    .string "his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_10::
    .string "Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise\n"
    .string "him; he hath put him to grief: when\l"
    .string "thou shalt make his soul an\l"
    .string "offering for sin, he shall see his\l"
    .string "seed, he shall prolong his days,\l"
    .string "and the pleasure of the LORD shall\l"
    .string "prosper in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_11::
    .string "He shall see of the travail of his\n"
    .string "soul, and shall be satisfied: by\l"
    .string "his knowledge shall my righteous\l"
    .string "servant justify many; for he shall\l"
    .string "bear their iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_53_12::
    .string "Therefore will I divide him a\n"
    .string "portion with the great, and he shall\l"
    .string "divide the spoil with the strong;\l"
    .string "because he hath poured out his soul\l"
    .string "unto death: and he was numbered with\l"
    .string "the transgressors; and he bare the\l"
    .string "sin of many, and made intercession\l"
    .string "for the transgressors.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_1::
    .string "Sing, O barren, thou that didst not\n"
    .string "bear; break forth into singing, and\l"
    .string "cry aloud, thou that didst not\l"
    .string "travail with child: for more are the\l"
    .string "children of the desolate than the\l"
    .string "children of the married wife, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_2::
    .string "Enlarge the place of thy tent, and\n"
    .string "let them stretch forth the curtains\l"
    .string "of thine habitations: spare not,\l"
    .string "lengthen thy cords, and strengthen\l"
    .string "thy stakes;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_3::
    .string "For thou shalt break forth on the\n"
    .string "right hand and on the left; and thy\l"
    .string "seed shall inherit the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "and make the desolate cities to be\l"
    .string "inhabited$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_4::
    .string "Fear not; for thou shalt not be\n"
    .string "ashamed: neither be thou confounded;\l"
    .string "for thou shalt not be put to shame:\l"
    .string "for thou shalt forget the shame of\l"
    .string "thy youth, and shalt not remember\l"
    .string "the reproach of thy widowhood any\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_5::
    .string "For thy Maker is thine husband; the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts is his name; and thy\l"
    .string "Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The\l"
    .string "God of the whole earth shall he be\l"
    .string "called.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_6::
    .string "For the LORD hath called thee as a\n"
    .string "woman forsaken and grieved in\l"
    .string "spirit, and a wife of youth, when\l"
    .string "thou wast refused, saith thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_7::
    .string "For a small moment have I forsaken\n"
    .string "thee; but with great mercies will I\l"
    .string "gather thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_8::
    .string "In a little wrath I hid my face\n"
    .string "from thee for a moment; but with\l"
    .string "everlasting kindness will I have\l"
    .string "mercy on thee, saith the LORD thy\l"
    .string "Redeemer.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_9::
    .string "For this is as the waters of Noah\n"
    .string "unto me: for as I have sworn that the\l"
    .string "waters of Noah should no more go\l"
    .string "over the earth; so have I sworn that I\l"
    .string "would not be wroth with thee, nor\l"
    .string "rebuke thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_10::
    .string "For the mountains shall depart,\n"
    .string "and the hills be removed; but my\l"
    .string "kindness shall not depart from\l"
    .string "thee, neither shall the covenant of\l"
    .string "my peace be removed, saith the LORD\l"
    .string "that hath mercy on thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_11::
    .string "O thou afflicted, tossed with\n"
    .string "tempest, and not comforted, behold,\l"
    .string "I will lay thy stones with fair\l"
    .string "colours, and lay thy foundations\l"
    .string "with sapphires.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_12::
    .string "And I will make thy windows of\n"
    .string "agates, and thy gates of carbuncles,\l"
    .string "and all thy borders of pleasant\l"
    .string "stones.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_13::
    .string "And all thy children shall be\n"
    .string "taught of the LORD; and great shall\l"
    .string "be the peace of thy children.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_14::
    .string "In righteousness shalt thou be\n"
    .string "established: thou shalt be far from\l"
    .string "oppression; for thou shalt not\l"
    .string "fear: and from terror; for it shall\l"
    .string "not come near thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_15::
    .string "Behold, they shall surely gather\n"
    .string "together, but not by me: whosoever\l"
    .string "shall gather together against thee\l"
    .string "shall fall for thy sake.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_16::
    .string "Behold, I have created the smith\n"
    .string "that bloweth the coals in the fire,\l"
    .string "and that bringeth forth an\l"
    .string "instrument for his work; and I have\l"
    .string "created the waster to destroy.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_54_17::
    .string "No weapon that is formed against\n"
    .string "thee shall prosper; and every\l"
    .string "tongue that shall rise against thee\l"
    .string "in judgment thou shalt condemn. This\l"
    .string "is the heritage of the servants of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and their righteousness is\l"
    .string "of me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_1::
    .string "Ho, every one that thirsteth, come\n"
    .string "ye to the waters, and he that hath no\l"
    .string "money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea,\l"
    .string "come, buy wine and milk without\l"
    .string "money and without price.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_2::
    .string "Wherefore do ye spend money for\n"
    .string "that which is not bread? and your\l"
    .string "labour for that which satisfieth not?\l"
    .string "hearken diligently unto me, and eat\l"
    .string "ye that which is good, and let your\l"
    .string "soul delight itself in fatness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_3::
    .string "Incline your ear, and come unto me:\n"
    .string "hear, and your soul shall live;\l"
    .string "and I will make an everlasting\l"
    .string "covenant with you, even the sure\l"
    .string "mercies of David.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_4::
    .string "Behold, I have given him for a\n"
    .string "witness to the people, a leader\l"
    .string "and commander to the people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_5::
    .string "Behold, thou shalt call a nation\n"
    .string "that thou knowest not, and nations\l"
    .string "that knew not thee shall run unto\l"
    .string "thee because of the LORD thy God, and\l"
    .string "for the Holy One of Israel; for he\l"
    .string "hath glorified thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_6::
    .string "Seek ye the LORD while he may be\n"
    .string "found, call ye upon him while he is\l"
    .string "near:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_7::
    .string "Let the wicked forsake his way, and\n"
    .string "the unrighteous man his thoughts: and\l"
    .string "let him return unto the LORD, and he\l"
    .string "will have mercy upon him; and to\l"
    .string "our God, for he will abundantly\l"
    .string "pardon$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_8::
    .string "For my thoughts are not your\n"
    .string "thoughts, neither are your ways my\l"
    .string "ways, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_9::
    .string "For as the heavens are higher than\n"
    .string "the earth, so are my ways higher than\l"
    .string "your ways, and my thoughts than your\l"
    .string "thoughts.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_10::
    .string "For as the rain cometh down, and the\n"
    .string "snow from heaven, and returneth not\l"
    .string "thither, but watereth the earth, and\l"
    .string "maketh it bring forth and bud, that\l"
    .string "it may give seed to the sower, and\l"
    .string "bread to the eater:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_11::
    .string "So shall my word be that goeth\n"
    .string "forth out of my mouth: it shall not\l"
    .string "return unto me void, but it shall\l"
    .string "accomplish that which I please,\l"
    .string "and it shall prosper in the thing\l"
    .string "whereto I sent it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_12::
    .string "For ye shall go out with joy, and\n"
    .string "be led forth with peace: the\l"
    .string "mountains and the hills shall\l"
    .string "break forth before you into singing,\l"
    .string "and all the trees of the field\l"
    .string "shall clap their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_55_13::
    .string "Instead of the thorn shall come up\n"
    .string "the fir tree, and instead of the\l"
    .string "brier shall come up the myrtle\l"
    .string "tree: and it shall be to the LORD\l"
    .string "for a name, for an everlasting sign\l"
    .string "that shall not be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Keep ye\n"
    .string "judgment, and do justice: for my\l"
    .string "salvation is near to come, and my\l"
    .string "righteousness to be revealed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_2::
    .string "Blessed is the man that doeth this,\n"
    .string "and the son of man that layeth hold\l"
    .string "on it; that keepeth the sabbath from\l"
    .string "polluting it, and keepeth his hand\l"
    .string "from doing any evil.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_3::
    .string "Neither let the son of the\n"
    .string "stranger, that hath joined himself\l"
    .string "to the LORD, speak, saying, The LORD\l"
    .string "hath utterly separated me from his\l"
    .string "people: neither let the eunuch say,\l"
    .string "Behold, I am a dry tree.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_4::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD unto the\n"
    .string "eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and\l"
    .string "choose the things that please me,\l"
    .string "and take hold of my covenant;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_5::
    .string "Even unto them will I give in mine\n"
    .string "house and within my walls a place\l"
    .string "and a name better than of sons and of\l"
    .string "daughters: I will give them an\l"
    .string "everlasting name, that shall not be\l"
    .string "cut off$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_6::
    .string "Also the sons of the stranger, that\n"
    .string "join themselves to the LORD, to\l"
    .string "serve him, and to love the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD, to be his servants, every\l"
    .string "one that keepeth the sabbath from\l"
    .string "polluting it, and taketh hold of my\l"
    .string "covenant;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_7::
    .string "Even them will I bring to my holy\n"
    .string "mountain, and make them joyful in my\l"
    .string "house of prayer: their burnt\l"
    .string "offerings and their sacrifices\l"
    .string "shall be accepted upon mine\l"
    .string "altar; for mine house shall be\l"
    .string "called an house of prayer for all\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_8::
    .string "The Lord GOD, which gathereth the\n"
    .string "outcasts of Israel saith, Yet will\l"
    .string "I gather others to him, beside those\l"
    .string "that are gathered unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_9::
    .string "All ye beasts of the field, come\n"
    .string "to devour, yea, all ye beasts in the\l"
    .string "forest.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_10::
    .string "His watchmen are blind: they are\n"
    .string "all ignorant, they are all dumb\l"
    .string "dogs, they cannot bark; sleeping,\l"
    .string "lying down, loving to slumber.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_11::
    .string "Yea, they are greedy dogs which can\n"
    .string "never have enough, and they are\l"
    .string "shepherds that cannot understand:\l"
    .string "they all look to their own way,\l"
    .string "every one for his gain, from his\l"
    .string "quarter.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_56_12::
    .string "Come ye, say they, I will fetch\n"
    .string "wine, and we will fill ourselves\l"
    .string "with strong drink; and to morrow\l"
    .string "shall be as this day, and much more\l"
    .string "abundant.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_1::
    .string "The righteous perisheth, and no man\n"
    .string "layeth it to heart: and merciful men\l"
    .string "are taken away, none considering that\l"
    .string "the righteous is taken away from the\l"
    .string "evil to come.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_2::
    .string "He shall enter into peace: they\n"
    .string "shall rest in their beds, each one\l"
    .string "walking in his uprightness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_3::
    .string "But draw near hither, ye sons of the\n"
    .string "sorceress, the seed of the adulterer\l"
    .string "and the whore.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_4::
    .string "Against whom do ye sport\n"
    .string "yourselves? against whom make ye a\l"
    .string "wide mouth, and draw out the tongue?\l"
    .string "are ye not children of\l"
    .string "transgression, a seed of falsehood,$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_5::
    .string "Enflaming yourselves with idols\n"
    .string "under every green tree, slaying the\l"
    .string "children in the valleys under the\l"
    .string "clifts of the rocks?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_6::
    .string "Among the smooth stones of the\n"
    .string "stream is thy portion; they, they\l"
    .string "are thy lot: even to them hast thou\l"
    .string "poured a drink offering, thou hast\l"
    .string "offered a meat offering. Should I\l"
    .string "receive comfort in these?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_7::
    .string "Upon a lofty and high mountain\n"
    .string "hast thou set thy bed: even thither\l"
    .string "wentest thou up to offer sacrifice$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_8::
    .string "Behind the doors also and the\n"
    .string "posts hast thou set up thy\l"
    .string "remembrance: for thou hast\l"
    .string "discovered thyself to another than\l"
    .string "me, and art gone up; thou hast\l"
    .string "enlarged thy bed, and made thee a\l"
    .string "covenant with them; thou lovedst\l"
    .string "their bed where thou sawest it.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_9::
    .string "And thou wentest to the king with\n"
    .string "ointment, and didst increase thy\l"
    .string "perfumes, and didst send thy\l"
    .string "messengers far off, and didst debase\l"
    .string "thyself even unto hell.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_10::
    .string "Thou art wearied in the greatness of\n"
    .string "thy way; yet saidst thou not, There\l"
    .string "is no hope: thou hast found the life\l"
    .string "of thine hand; therefore thou wast\l"
    .string "not grieved.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_11::
    .string "And of whom hast thou been afraid or\n"
    .string "feared, that thou hast lied, and\l"
    .string "hast not remembered me, nor laid it\l"
    .string "to thy heart? have not I held my\l"
    .string "peace even of old, and thou fearest\l"
    .string "me not?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_12::
    .string "I will declare thy righteousness,\n"
    .string "and thy works; for they shall not\l"
    .string "profit thee$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_13::
    .string "When thou criest, let thy\n"
    .string "companies deliver thee; but the\l"
    .string "wind shall carry them all away;\l"
    .string "vanity shall take them: but he that\l"
    .string "putteth his trust in me shall\l"
    .string "possess the land, and shall inherit\l"
    .string "my holy mountain;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_14::
    .string "And shall say, Cast ye up, cast ye\n"
    .string "up, prepare the way, take up the\l"
    .string "stumblingblock out of the way of my\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_15::
    .string "For thus saith the high and lofty\n"
    .string "One that inhabiteth eternity, whose\l"
    .string "name is Holy; I dwell in the high\l"
    .string "and holy place, with him also that\l"
    .string "is of a contrite and humble spirit,\l"
    .string "to revive the spirit of the humble,\l"
    .string "and to revive the heart of the\l"
    .string "contrite ones.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_16::
    .string "For I will not contend for ever,\n"
    .string "neither will I be always wroth: for\l"
    .string "the spirit should fail before me,\l"
    .string "and the souls which I have made.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_17::
    .string "For the iniquity of his\n"
    .string "covetousness was I wroth, and smote\l"
    .string "him: I hid me, and was wroth, and he\l"
    .string "went on frowardly in the way of his\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_18::
    .string "I have seen his ways, and will\n"
    .string "heal him: I will lead him also,\l"
    .string "and restore comforts unto him and to\l"
    .string "his mourners.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_19::
    .string "I create the fruit of the lips;\n"
    .string "Peace, peace to him that is far off,\l"
    .string "and to him that is near, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD; and I will heal him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_20::
    .string "But the wicked are like the\n"
    .string "troubled sea, when it cannot rest,\l"
    .string "whose waters cast up mire and dirt.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_57_21::
    .string "There is no peace, saith my God, to\n"
    .string "the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_1::
    .string "Cry aloud, spare not, lift up thy\n"
    .string "voice like a trumpet, and shew my\l"
    .string "people their transgression, and the\l"
    .string "house of Jacob their sins.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_2::
    .string "Yet they seek me daily, and delight\n"
    .string "to know my ways, as a nation that did\l"
    .string "righteousness, and forsook not the\l"
    .string "ordinance of their God: they ask of\l"
    .string "me the ordinances of justice; they\l"
    .string "take delight in approaching to God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_3::
    .string "Wherefore have we fasted, say they,\n"
    .string "and thou seest not? wherefore have we\l"
    .string "afflicted our soul, and thou takest\l"
    .string "no knowledge? Behold, in the day of\l"
    .string "your fast ye find pleasure, and\l"
    .string "exact all your labours.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_4::
    .string "Behold, ye fast for strife and\n"
    .string "debate, and to smite with the fist of\l"
    .string "wickedness: ye shall not fast as ye\l"
    .string "do this day, to make your voice to be\l"
    .string "heard on high.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_5::
    .string "Is it such a fast that I have chosen?\n"
    .string "a day for a man to afflict his soul?\l"
    .string "is it to bow down his head as a\l"
    .string "bulrush, and to spread sackcloth\l"
    .string "and ashes under him? wilt thou call\l"
    .string "this a fast, and an acceptable day\l"
    .string "to the LORD?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_6::
    .string "Is not this the fast that I have\n"
    .string "chosen? to loose the bands of\l"
    .string "wickedness, to undo the heavy\l"
    .string "burdens, and to let the oppressed\l"
    .string "go free, and that ye break every\l"
    .string "yoke?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_7::
    .string "Is it not to deal thy bread to the\n"
    .string "hungry, and that thou bring the poor\l"
    .string "that are cast out to thy house? when\l"
    .string "thou seest the naked, that thou cover\l"
    .string "him; and that thou hide not thyself\l"
    .string "from thine own flesh?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_8::
    .string "Then shall thy light break forth\n"
    .string "as the morning, and thine health\l"
    .string "shall spring forth speedily: and\l"
    .string "thy righteousness shall go before\l"
    .string "thee; the glory of the LORD shall\l"
    .string "be thy rereward$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_9::
    .string "Then shalt thou call, and the LORD\n"
    .string "shall answer; thou shalt cry, and\l"
    .string "he shall say, Here I am. If thou\l"
    .string "take away from the midst of thee the\l"
    .string "yoke, the putting forth of the\l"
    .string "finger, and speaking vanity;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_10::
    .string "And if thou draw out thy soul to the\n"
    .string "hungry, and satisfy the afflicted\l"
    .string "soul; then shall thy light rise in\l"
    .string "obscurity, and thy darkness be as the\l"
    .string "noon day:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_11::
    .string "And the LORD shall guide thee\n"
    .string "continually, and satisfy thy soul\l"
    .string "in drought, and make fat thy bones:\l"
    .string "and thou shalt be like a watered\l"
    .string "garden, and like a spring of water,\l"
    .string "whose waters fail not$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_12::
    .string "And they that shall be of thee\n"
    .string "shall build the old waste places:\l"
    .string "thou shalt raise up the foundations\l"
    .string "of many generations; and thou shalt\l"
    .string "be called, The repairer of the\l"
    .string "breach, The restorer of paths to\l"
    .string "dwell in.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_13::
    .string "If thou turn away thy foot from the\n"
    .string "sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on\l"
    .string "my holy day; and call the sabbath a\l"
    .string "delight, the holy of the LORD,\l"
    .string "honourable; and shalt honour him,\l"
    .string "not doing thine own ways, nor finding\l"
    .string "thine own pleasure, nor speaking\l"
    .string "thine own words:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_58_14::
    .string "Then shalt thou delight thyself\n"
    .string "in the LORD; and I will cause thee\l"
    .string "to ride upon the high places of the\l"
    .string "earth, and feed thee with the\l"
    .string "heritage of Jacob thy father: for the\l"
    .string "mouth of the LORD hath spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_1::
    .string "Behold, the LORD’s hand is not\n"
    .string "shortened, that it cannot save;\l"
    .string "neither his ear heavy, that it cannot\l"
    .string "hear:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_2::
    .string "But your iniquities have separated\n"
    .string "between you and your God, and your\l"
    .string "sins have hid his face from you, that\l"
    .string "he will not hear$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_3::
    .string "For your hands are defiled with\n"
    .string "blood, and your fingers with\l"
    .string "iniquity; your lips have spoken\l"
    .string "lies, your tongue hath muttered\l"
    .string "perverseness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_4::
    .string "None calleth for justice, nor any\n"
    .string "pleadeth for truth: they trust in\l"
    .string "vanity, and speak lies; they\l"
    .string "conceive mischief, and bring forth\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_5::
    .string "They hatch cockatrice’ eggs, and\n"
    .string "weave the spider’s web: he that\l"
    .string "eateth of their eggs dieth, and that\l"
    .string "which is crushed breaketh out into a\l"
    .string "viper.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_6::
    .string "Their webs shall not become\n"
    .string "garments, neither shall they cover\l"
    .string "themselves with their works: their\l"
    .string "works are works of iniquity, and the\l"
    .string "act of violence is in their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_7::
    .string "Their feet run to evil, and they\n"
    .string "make haste to shed innocent blood:\l"
    .string "their thoughts are thoughts of\l"
    .string "iniquity; wasting and destruction\l"
    .string "are in their paths.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_8::
    .string "The way of peace they know not; and\n"
    .string "there is no judgment in their goings:\l"
    .string "they have made them crooked paths:\l"
    .string "whosoever goeth therein shall not\l"
    .string "know peace.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_9::
    .string "Therefore is judgment far from us,\n"
    .string "neither doth justice overtake us: we\l"
    .string "wait for light, but behold\l"
    .string "obscurity; for brightness, but we\l"
    .string "walk in darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_10::
    .string "We grope for the wall like the\n"
    .string "blind, and we grope as if we had no\l"
    .string "eyes: we stumble at noon day as in\l"
    .string "the night; we are in desolate\l"
    .string "places as dead men.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_11::
    .string "We roar all like bears, and mourn\n"
    .string "sore like doves: we look for\l"
    .string "judgment, but there is none; for\l"
    .string "salvation, but it is far off from us.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_12::
    .string "For our transgressions are\n"
    .string "multiplied before thee, and our\l"
    .string "sins testify against us: for our\l"
    .string "transgressions are with us; and as\l"
    .string "for our iniquities, we know them;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_13::
    .string "In transgressing and lying against\n"
    .string "the LORD, and departing away from\l"
    .string "our God, speaking oppression and\l"
    .string "revolt, conceiving and uttering from\l"
    .string "the heart words of falsehood$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_14::
    .string "And judgment is turned away\n"
    .string "backward, and justice standeth afar\l"
    .string "off: for truth is fallen in the\l"
    .string "street, and equity cannot enter.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_15::
    .string "Yea, truth faileth; and he that\n"
    .string "departeth from evil maketh himself\l"
    .string "a prey: and the LORD saw it, and it\l"
    .string "displeased him that there was no\l"
    .string "judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_16::
    .string "And he saw that there was no man, and\n"
    .string "wondered that there was no\l"
    .string "intercessor: therefore his arm\l"
    .string "brought salvation unto him; and his\l"
    .string "righteousness, it sustained him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_17::
    .string "For he put on righteousness as a\n"
    .string "breastplate, and an helmet of\l"
    .string "salvation upon his head; and he put\l"
    .string "on the garments of vengeance for\l"
    .string "clothing, and was clad with zeal as\l"
    .string "a cloak.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_18::
    .string "According to their deeds,\n"
    .string "accordingly he will repay, fury to\l"
    .string "his adversaries, recompence to his\l"
    .string "enemies; to the islands he will\l"
    .string "repay recompence.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_19::
    .string "So shall they fear the name of the\n"
    .string "LORD from the west, and his glory\l"
    .string "from the rising of the sun. When the\l"
    .string "enemy shall come in like a flood,\l"
    .string "the Spirit of the LORD shall lift\l"
    .string "up a standard against him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_20::
    .string "And the Redeemer shall come to\n"
    .string "Zion, and unto them that turn from\l"
    .string "transgression in Jacob, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_59_21::
    .string "As for me, this is my covenant with\n"
    .string "them, saith the LORD; My spirit that\l"
    .string "is upon thee, and my words which I\l"
    .string "have put in thy mouth, shall not\l"
    .string "depart out of thy mouth, nor out of\l"
    .string "the mouth of thy seed, nor out of the\l"
    .string "mouth of thy seed’s seed, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, from henceforth and for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_1::
    .string "Arise, shine; for thy light is come,\n"
    .string "and the glory of the LORD is risen\l"
    .string "upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_2::
    .string "For, behold, the darkness shall\n"
    .string "cover the earth, and gross darkness\l"
    .string "the people: but the LORD shall\l"
    .string "arise upon thee, and his glory\l"
    .string "shall be seen upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_3::
    .string "And the Gentiles shall come to thy\n"
    .string "light, and kings to the brightness of\l"
    .string "thy rising.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_4::
    .string "Lift up thine eyes round about, and\n"
    .string "see: all they gather themselves\l"
    .string "together, they come to thee: thy sons\l"
    .string "shall come from far, and thy\l"
    .string "daughters shall be nursed at thy\l"
    .string "side.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_5::
    .string "Then thou shalt see, and flow\n"
    .string "together, and thine heart shall\l"
    .string "fear, and be enlarged; because the\l"
    .string "abundance of the sea shall be\l"
    .string "converted unto thee, the forces of\l"
    .string "the Gentiles shall come unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_6::
    .string "The multitude of camels shall\n"
    .string "cover thee, the dromedaries of Midian\l"
    .string "and Ephah; all they from Sheba\l"
    .string "shall come: they shall bring gold\l"
    .string "and incense; and they shall shew\l"
    .string "forth the praises of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_7::
    .string "All the flocks of Kedar shall be\n"
    .string "gathered together unto thee, the rams\l"
    .string "of Nebaioth shall minister unto\l"
    .string "thee: they shall come up with\l"
    .string "acceptance on mine altar, and I\l"
    .string "will glorify the house of my glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_8::
    .string "Who are these that fly as a cloud,\n"
    .string "and as the doves to their windows?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_9::
    .string "Surely the isles shall wait for\n"
    .string "me, and the ships of Tarshish first,\l"
    .string "to bring thy sons from far, their\l"
    .string "silver and their gold with them,\l"
    .string "unto the name of the LORD thy God, and\l"
    .string "to the Holy One of Israel, because\l"
    .string "he hath glorified thee$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_10::
    .string "And the sons of strangers shall\n"
    .string "build up thy walls, and their\l"
    .string "kings shall minister unto thee: for\l"
    .string "in my wrath I smote thee, but in my\l"
    .string "favour have I had mercy on thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_11::
    .string "Therefore thy gates shall be open\n"
    .string "continually; they shall not be\l"
    .string "shut day nor night; that men may\l"
    .string "bring unto thee the forces of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, and that their kings may\l"
    .string "be brought.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_12::
    .string "For the nation and kingdom that\n"
    .string "will not serve thee shall perish;\l"
    .string "yea, those nations shall be utterly\l"
    .string "wasted.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_13::
    .string "The glory of Lebanon shall come\n"
    .string "unto thee, the fir tree, the pine\l"
    .string "tree, and the box together, to\l"
    .string "beautify the place of my sanctuary;\l"
    .string "and I will make the place of my\l"
    .string "feet glorious.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_14::
    .string "The sons also of them that\n"
    .string "afflicted thee shall come bending\l"
    .string "unto thee; and all they that\l"
    .string "despised thee shall bow\l"
    .string "themselves down at the soles of thy\l"
    .string "feet; and they shall call thee;\l"
    .string "The city of the LORD, The Zion of the\l"
    .string "Holy One of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_15::
    .string "Whereas thou hast been forsaken and\n"
    .string "hated, so that no man went through\l"
    .string "thee, I will make thee an eternal\l"
    .string "excellency, a joy of many\l"
    .string "generations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_16::
    .string "Thou shalt also suck the milk of\n"
    .string "the Gentiles, and shalt suck the\l"
    .string "breast of kings: and thou shalt know\l"
    .string "that I the LORD am thy Saviour and\l"
    .string "thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_17::
    .string "For brass I will bring gold, and\n"
    .string "for iron I will bring silver, and\l"
    .string "for wood brass, and for stones iron:\l"
    .string "I will also make thy officers\l"
    .string "peace, and thine exactors\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_18::
    .string "Violence shall no more be heard in\n"
    .string "thy land, wasting nor destruction\l"
    .string "within thy borders; but thou shalt\l"
    .string "call thy walls Salvation, and thy\l"
    .string "gates Praise.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_19::
    .string "The sun shall be no more thy light\n"
    .string "by day; neither for brightness\l"
    .string "shall the moon give light unto\l"
    .string "thee: but the LORD shall be unto\l"
    .string "thee an everlasting light, and thy\l"
    .string "God thy glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_20::
    .string "Thy sun shall no more go down;\n"
    .string "neither shall thy moon withdraw\l"
    .string "itself: for the LORD shall be thine\l"
    .string "everlasting light, and the days of\l"
    .string "thy mourning shall be ended.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_21::
    .string "Thy people also shall be all\n"
    .string "righteous: they shall inherit the\l"
    .string "land for ever, the branch of my\l"
    .string "planting, the work of my hands, that\l"
    .string "I may be glorified.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_60_22::
    .string "A little one shall become a\n"
    .string "thousand, and a small one a strong\l"
    .string "nation: I the LORD will hasten it in\l"
    .string "his time.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_1::
    .string "The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon\n"
    .string "me; because the LORD hath anointed me\l"
    .string "to preach good tidings unto the\l"
    .string "meek; he hath sent me to bind up the\l"
    .string "brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty\l"
    .string "to the captives, and the opening of\l"
    .string "the prison to them that are bound;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_2::
    .string "To proclaim the acceptable year\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and the day of vengeance\l"
    .string "of our God; to comfort all that\l"
    .string "mourn;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_3::
    .string "To appoint unto them that mourn in\n"
    .string "Zion, to give unto them beauty for\l"
    .string "ashes, the oil of joy for mourning,\l"
    .string "the garment of praise for the\l"
    .string "spirit of heaviness; that they might\l"
    .string "be called trees of righteousness,\l"
    .string "the planting of the LORD, that he\l"
    .string "might be glorified$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_4::
    .string "And they shall build the old\n"
    .string "wastes, they shall raise up the\l"
    .string "former desolations, and they shall\l"
    .string "repair the waste cities, the\l"
    .string "desolations of many generations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_5::
    .string "And strangers shall stand and feed\n"
    .string "your flocks, and the sons of the\l"
    .string "alien shall be your plowmen and\l"
    .string "your vinedressers.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_6::
    .string "But ye shall be named the Priests\n"
    .string "of the LORD: men shall call you the\l"
    .string "Ministers of our God: ye shall eat\l"
    .string "the riches of the Gentiles, and in\l"
    .string "their glory shall ye boast\l"
    .string "yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_7::
    .string "For your shame ye shall have\n"
    .string "double; and for confusion they\l"
    .string "shall rejoice in their portion:\l"
    .string "therefore in their land they shall\l"
    .string "possess the double: everlasting joy\l"
    .string "shall be unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_8::
    .string "For I the LORD love judgment, I hate\n"
    .string "robbery for burnt offering; and I\l"
    .string "will direct their work in truth, and\l"
    .string "I will make an everlasting\l"
    .string "covenant with them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_9::
    .string "And their seed shall be known\n"
    .string "among the Gentiles, and their\l"
    .string "offspring among the people: all\l"
    .string "that see them shall acknowledge\l"
    .string "them, that they are the seed which\l"
    .string "the LORD hath blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_10::
    .string "I will greatly rejoice in the\n"
    .string "LORD, my soul shall be joyful in my\l"
    .string "God; for he hath clothed me with the\l"
    .string "garments of salvation, he hath\l"
    .string "covered me with the robe of\l"
    .string "righteousness, as a bridegroom\l"
    .string "decketh himself with ornaments, and\l"
    .string "as a bride adorneth herself with her\l"
    .string "jewels.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_61_11::
    .string "For as the earth bringeth forth her\n"
    .string "bud, and as the garden causeth the\l"
    .string "things that are sown in it to spring\l"
    .string "forth; so the Lord GOD will cause\l"
    .string "righteousness and praise to spring\l"
    .string "forth before all the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_1::
    .string "For Zion’s sake will I not hold my\n"
    .string "peace, and for Jerusalem’s sake I\l"
    .string "will not rest, until the\l"
    .string "righteousness thereof go forth as\l"
    .string "brightness, and the salvation\l"
    .string "thereof as a lamp that burneth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_2::
    .string "And the Gentiles shall see thy\n"
    .string "righteousness, and all kings thy\l"
    .string "glory: and thou shalt be called by\l"
    .string "a new name, which the mouth of the\l"
    .string "LORD shall name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_3::
    .string "Thou shalt also be a crown of\n"
    .string "glory in the hand of the LORD, and a\l"
    .string "royal diadem in the hand of thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_4::
    .string "Thou shalt no more be termed\n"
    .string "Forsaken; neither shall thy land\l"
    .string "any more be termed Desolate: but\l"
    .string "thou shalt be called Hephzibah,\l"
    .string "and thy land Beulah: for the LORD\l"
    .string "delighteth in thee, and thy land\l"
    .string "shall be married.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_5::
    .string "For as a young man marrieth a\n"
    .string "virgin, so shall thy sons marry\l"
    .string "thee: and as the bridegroom rejoiceth\l"
    .string "over the bride, so shall thy God\l"
    .string "rejoice over thee.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_6::
    .string "I have set watchmen upon thy\n"
    .string "walls, O Jerusalem, which shall\l"
    .string "never hold their peace day nor\l"
    .string "night: ye that make mention of the\l"
    .string "LORD, keep not silence,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_7::
    .string "And give him no rest, till he\n"
    .string "establish, and till he make\l"
    .string "Jerusalem a praise in the earth$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_8::
    .string "The LORD hath sworn by his right\n"
    .string "hand, and by the arm of his strength,\l"
    .string "Surely I will no more give thy corn\l"
    .string "to be meat for thine enemies; and the\l"
    .string "sons of the stranger shall not\l"
    .string "drink thy wine, for the which thou\l"
    .string "hast laboured:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_9::
    .string "But they that have gathered it\n"
    .string "shall eat it, and praise the LORD;\l"
    .string "and they that have brought it\l"
    .string "together shall drink it in the\l"
    .string "courts of my holiness$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_10::
    .string "Go through, go through the gates;\n"
    .string "prepare ye the way of the people;\l"
    .string "cast up, cast up the highway; gather\l"
    .string "out the stones; lift up a standard\l"
    .string "for the people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_11::
    .string "Behold, the LORD hath proclaimed\n"
    .string "unto the end of the world, Say ye to\l"
    .string "the daughter of Zion, Behold, thy\l"
    .string "salvation cometh; behold, his\l"
    .string "reward is with him, and his work\l"
    .string "before him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_62_12::
    .string "And they shall call them, The\n"
    .string "holy people, The redeemed of the\l"
    .string "LORD: and thou shalt be called,\l"
    .string "Sought out, A city not forsaken.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_1::
    .string "Who is this that cometh from Edom,\n"
    .string "with dyed garments from Bozrah? this\l"
    .string "that is glorious in his apparel,\l"
    .string "travelling in the greatness of his\l"
    .string "strength? I that speak in\l"
    .string "righteousness, mighty to save.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_2::
    .string "Wherefore art thou red in thine\n"
    .string "apparel, and thy garments like him\l"
    .string "that treadeth in the winefat?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_3::
    .string "I have trodden the winepress\n"
    .string "alone; and of the people there was\l"
    .string "none with me: for I will tread them\l"
    .string "in mine anger, and trample them in\l"
    .string "my fury; and their blood shall be\l"
    .string "sprinkled upon my garments, and I\l"
    .string "will stain all my raiment$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_4::
    .string "For the day of vengeance is in mine\n"
    .string "heart, and the year of my redeemed is\l"
    .string "come.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_5::
    .string "And I looked, and there was none to\n"
    .string "help; and I wondered that there was\l"
    .string "none to uphold: therefore mine own\l"
    .string "arm brought salvation unto me; and\l"
    .string "my fury, it upheld me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_6::
    .string "And I will tread down the people\n"
    .string "in mine anger, and make them drunk in\l"
    .string "my fury, and I will bring down their\l"
    .string "strength to the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_7::
    .string "I will mention the\n"
    .string "lovingkindnesses of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "praises of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that the LORD hath bestowed on\l"
    .string "us, and the great goodness toward the\l"
    .string "house of Israel, which he hath\l"
    .string "bestowed on them according to his\l"
    .string "mercies, and according to the\l"
    .string "multitude of his lovingkindnesses.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_8::
    .string "For he said, Surely they are my\n"
    .string "people, children that will not\l"
    .string "lie: so he was their Saviour.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_9::
    .string "In all their affliction he was\n"
    .string "afflicted, and the angel of his\l"
    .string "presence saved them: in his love and\l"
    .string "in his pity he redeemed them; and he\l"
    .string "bare them, and carried them all the\l"
    .string "days of old.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_10::
    .string "But they rebelled, and vexed his\n"
    .string "holy Spirit: therefore he was\l"
    .string "turned to be their enemy, and he\l"
    .string "fought against them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_11::
    .string "Then he remembered the days of old,\n"
    .string "Moses, and his people, saying,\l"
    .string "Where is he that brought them up out\l"
    .string "of the sea with the shepherd of his\l"
    .string "flock? where is he that put his\l"
    .string "holy Spirit within him?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_12::
    .string "That led them by the right hand of\n"
    .string "Moses with his glorious arm,\l"
    .string "dividing the water before them, to\l"
    .string "make himself an everlasting name?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_13::
    .string "That led them through the deep, as\n"
    .string "an horse in the wilderness, that\l"
    .string "they should not stumble?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_14::
    .string "As a beast goeth down into the\n"
    .string "valley, the Spirit of the LORD\l"
    .string "caused him to rest: so didst thou\l"
    .string "lead thy people, to make thyself a\l"
    .string "glorious name$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_15::
    .string "Look down from heaven, and behold\n"
    .string "from the habitation of thy holiness\l"
    .string "and of thy glory: where is thy zeal\l"
    .string "and thy strength, the sounding of thy\l"
    .string "bowels and of thy mercies toward me?\l"
    .string "are they restrained?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_16::
    .string "Doubtless thou art our father,\n"
    .string "though Abraham be ignorant of us, and\l"
    .string "Israel acknowledge us not: thou, O\l"
    .string "LORD, art our father, our redeemer;\l"
    .string "thy name is from everlasting$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_17::
    .string "O LORD, why hast thou made us to err\n"
    .string "from thy ways, and hardened our heart\l"
    .string "from thy fear? Return for thy\l"
    .string "servants’ sake, the tribes of thine\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_18::
    .string "The people of thy holiness have\n"
    .string "possessed it but a little while:\l"
    .string "our adversaries have trodden down\l"
    .string "thy sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_63_19::
    .string "We are thine: thou never barest\n"
    .string "rule over them; they were not\l"
    .string "called by thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_1::
    .string "Oh that thou wouldest rend the\n"
    .string "heavens, that thou wouldest come\l"
    .string "down, that the mountains might flow\l"
    .string "down at thy presence,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_2::
    .string "As when the melting fire burneth,\n"
    .string "the fire causeth the waters to boil,\l"
    .string "to make thy name known to thine\l"
    .string "adversaries, that the nations may\l"
    .string "tremble at thy presence!"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_3::
    .string "When thou didst terrible things\n"
    .string "which we looked not for, thou camest\l"
    .string "down, the mountains flowed down at\l"
    .string "thy presence$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_4::
    .string "For since the beginning of the\n"
    .string "world men have not heard, nor\l"
    .string "perceived by the ear, neither hath\l"
    .string "the eye seen, O God, beside thee, what\l"
    .string "he hath prepared for him that\l"
    .string "waiteth for him.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_5::
    .string "Thou meetest him that rejoiceth and\n"
    .string "worketh righteousness, those that\l"
    .string "remember thee in thy ways: behold,\l"
    .string "thou art wroth; for we have sinned:\l"
    .string "in those is continuance, and we\l"
    .string "shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_6::
    .string "But we are all as an unclean\n"
    .string "thing, and all our righteousnesses\l"
    .string "are as filthy rags; and we all do\l"
    .string "fade as a leaf; and our iniquities,\l"
    .string "like the wind, have taken us away.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_7::
    .string "And there is none that calleth\n"
    .string "upon thy name, that stirreth up\l"
    .string "himself to take hold of thee: for\l"
    .string "thou hast hid thy face from us, and\l"
    .string "hast consumed us, because of our\l"
    .string "iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_8::
    .string "But now, O LORD, thou art our father;\n"
    .string "we are the clay, and thou our\l"
    .string "potter; and we all are the work of\l"
    .string "thy hand.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_9::
    .string "Be not wroth very sore, O LORD,\n"
    .string "neither remember iniquity for ever:\l"
    .string "behold, see, we beseech thee, we are\l"
    .string "all thy people.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_10::
    .string "Thy holy cities are a wilderness,\n"
    .string "Zion is a wilderness, Jerusalem a\l"
    .string "desolation.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_11::
    .string "Our holy and our beautiful house,\n"
    .string "where our fathers praised thee, is\l"
    .string "burned up with fire: and all our\l"
    .string "pleasant things are laid waste.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_64_12::
    .string "Wilt thou refrain thyself for\n"
    .string "these things, O LORD? wilt thou hold\l"
    .string "thy peace, and afflict us very sore?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_1::
    .string "I am sought of them that asked not\n"
    .string "for me; I am found of them that sought\l"
    .string "me not: I said, Behold me, behold\l"
    .string "me, unto a nation that was not\l"
    .string "called by my name$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_2::
    .string "I have spread out my hands all the\n"
    .string "day unto a rebellious people,\l"
    .string "which walketh in a way that was not\l"
    .string "good, after their own thoughts;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_3::
    .string "A people that provoketh me to\n"
    .string "anger continually to my face; that\l"
    .string "sacrificeth in gardens, and burneth\l"
    .string "incense upon altars of brick;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_4::
    .string "Which remain among the graves, and\n"
    .string "lodge in the monuments, which eat\l"
    .string "swine’s flesh, and broth of\l"
    .string "abominable things is in their\l"
    .string "vessels;"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_5::
    .string "Which say, Stand by thyself, come\n"
    .string "not near to me; for I am holier than\l"
    .string "thou. These are a smoke in my nose, a\l"
    .string "fire that burneth all the day$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_6::
    .string "Behold, it is written before me: I\n"
    .string "will not keep silence, but will\l"
    .string "recompense, even recompense into\l"
    .string "their bosom,"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_7::
    .string "Your iniquities, and the iniquities\n"
    .string "of your fathers together, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, which have burned incense upon\l"
    .string "the mountains, and blasphemed me\l"
    .string "upon the hills: therefore will I\l"
    .string "measure their former work into their\l"
    .string "bosom$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_8::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, As the new wine\n"
    .string "is found in the cluster, and one\l"
    .string "saith, Destroy it not; for a\l"
    .string "blessing is in it: so will I do for\l"
    .string "my servants’ sakes, that I may not\l"
    .string "destroy them all.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_9::
    .string "And I will bring forth a seed out\n"
    .string "of Jacob, and out of Judah an\l"
    .string "inheritor of my mountains: and mine\l"
    .string "elect shall inherit it, and my\l"
    .string "servants shall dwell there.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_10::
    .string "And Sharon shall be a fold of\n"
    .string "flocks, and the valley of Achor a\l"
    .string "place for the herds to lie down in,\l"
    .string "for my people that have sought me.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_11::
    .string "But ye are they that forsake the\n"
    .string "LORD, that forget my holy mountain,\l"
    .string "that prepare a table for that\l"
    .string "troop, and that furnish the drink\l"
    .string "offering unto that number.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_12::
    .string "Therefore will I number you to the\n"
    .string "sword, and ye shall all bow down to\l"
    .string "the slaughter: because when I\l"
    .string "called, ye did not answer; when I\l"
    .string "spake, ye did not hear; but did evil\l"
    .string "before mine eyes, and did choose that\l"
    .string "wherein I delighted not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_13::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD,\n"
    .string "Behold, my servants shall eat, but\l"
    .string "ye shall be hungry: behold, my\l"
    .string "servants shall drink, but ye shall\l"
    .string "be thirsty: behold, my servants\l"
    .string "shall rejoice, but ye shall be\l"
    .string "ashamed:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_14::
    .string "Behold, my servants shall sing for\n"
    .string "joy of heart, but ye shall cry for\l"
    .string "sorrow of heart, and shall howl for\l"
    .string "vexation of spirit$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_15::
    .string "And ye shall leave your name for a\n"
    .string "curse unto my chosen: for the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD shall slay thee, and call his\l"
    .string "servants by another name:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_16::
    .string "That he who blesseth himself in\n"
    .string "the earth shall bless himself in\l"
    .string "the God of truth; and he that\l"
    .string "sweareth in the earth shall swear\l"
    .string "by the God of truth; because the\l"
    .string "former troubles are forgotten, and\l"
    .string "because they are hid from mine eyes$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_17::
    .string "For, behold, I create new heavens\n"
    .string "and a new earth: and the former\l"
    .string "shall not be remembered, nor come\l"
    .string "into mind.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_18::
    .string "But be ye glad and rejoice for ever\n"
    .string "in that which I create: for, behold,\l"
    .string "I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and\l"
    .string "her people a joy.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_19::
    .string "And I will rejoice in Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and joy in my people: and the voice\l"
    .string "of weeping shall be no more heard\l"
    .string "in her, nor the voice of crying.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_20::
    .string "There shall be no more thence an\n"
    .string "infant of days, nor an old man that\l"
    .string "hath not filled his days: for the\l"
    .string "child shall die an hundred years\l"
    .string "old; but the sinner being an hundred\l"
    .string "years old shall be accursed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_21::
    .string "And they shall build houses, and\n"
    .string "inhabit them; and they shall plant\l"
    .string "vineyards, and eat the fruit of them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_22::
    .string "They shall not build, and another\n"
    .string "inhabit; they shall not plant, and\l"
    .string "another eat: for as the days of a tree\l"
    .string "are the days of my people, and mine\l"
    .string "elect shall long enjoy the work of\l"
    .string "their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_23::
    .string "They shall not labour in vain, nor\n"
    .string "bring forth for trouble; for they\l"
    .string "are the seed of the blessed of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and their offspring with them.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_24::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "before they call, I will answer;\l"
    .string "and while they are yet speaking, I\l"
    .string "will hear.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_65_25::
    .string "The wolf and the lamb shall feed\n"
    .string "together, and the lion shall eat\l"
    .string "straw like the bullock: and dust\l"
    .string "shall be the serpent’s meat. They\l"
    .string "shall not hurt nor destroy in all\l"
    .string "my holy mountain, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, The heaven is\n"
    .string "my throne, and the earth is my\l"
    .string "footstool: where is the house that\l"
    .string "ye build unto me? and where is the\l"
    .string "place of my rest?"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_2::
    .string "For all those things hath mine\n"
    .string "hand made, and all those things have\l"
    .string "been, saith the LORD: but to this man\l"
    .string "will I look, even to him that is\l"
    .string "poor and of a contrite spirit, and\l"
    .string "trembleth at my word$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_3::
    .string "He that killeth an ox is as if he\n"
    .string "slew a man; he that sacrificeth a\l"
    .string "lamb, as if he cut off a dog’s neck;\l"
    .string "he that offereth an oblation, as if\l"
    .string "he offered swine’s blood; he that\l"
    .string "burneth incense, as if he blessed an\l"
    .string "idol. Yea, they have chosen their\l"
    .string "own ways, and their soul delighteth\l"
    .string "in their abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_4::
    .string "I also will choose their\n"
    .string "delusions, and will bring their\l"
    .string "fears upon them; because when I\l"
    .string "called, none did answer; when I\l"
    .string "spake, they did not hear: but they\l"
    .string "did evil before mine eyes, and chose\l"
    .string "that in which I delighted not.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_5::
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD, ye that\n"
    .string "tremble at his word; Your brethren\l"
    .string "that hated you, that cast you out for\l"
    .string "my name’s sake, said, Let the LORD be\l"
    .string "glorified: but he shall appear to\l"
    .string "your joy, and they shall be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_6::
    .string "A voice of noise from the city, a\n"
    .string "voice from the temple, a voice of\l"
    .string "the LORD that rendereth recompence\l"
    .string "to his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_7::
    .string "Before she travailed, she brought\n"
    .string "forth; before her pain came, she was\l"
    .string "delivered of a man child.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_8::
    .string "Who hath heard such a thing? who\n"
    .string "hath seen such things? Shall the\l"
    .string "earth be made to bring forth in one\l"
    .string "day? or shall a nation be born at\l"
    .string "once? for as soon as Zion travailed,\l"
    .string "she brought forth her children.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_9::
    .string "Shall I bring to the birth, and not\n"
    .string "cause to bring forth? saith the LORD:\l"
    .string "shall I cause to bring forth, and\l"
    .string "shut the womb? saith thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_10::
    .string "Rejoice ye with Jerusalem, and be\n"
    .string "glad with her, all ye that love\l"
    .string "her: rejoice for joy with her, all\l"
    .string "ye that mourn for her:"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_11::
    .string "That ye may suck, and be satisfied\n"
    .string "with the breasts of her\l"
    .string "consolations; that ye may milk out,\l"
    .string "and be delighted with the abundance\l"
    .string "of her glory$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_12::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will extend peace to her like a\l"
    .string "river, and the glory of the Gentiles\l"
    .string "like a flowing stream: then shall\l"
    .string "ye suck, ye shall be borne upon her\l"
    .string "sides, and be dandled upon her\l"
    .string "knees.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_13::
    .string "As one whom his mother comforteth,\n"
    .string "so will I comfort you; and ye shall\l"
    .string "be comforted in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_14::
    .string "And when ye see this, your heart\n"
    .string "shall rejoice, and your bones\l"
    .string "shall flourish like an herb: and\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD shall be known\l"
    .string "toward his servants, and his\l"
    .string "indignation toward his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_15::
    .string "For, behold, the LORD will come\n"
    .string "with fire, and with his chariots\l"
    .string "like a whirlwind, to render his\l"
    .string "anger with fury, and his rebuke with\l"
    .string "flames of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_16::
    .string "For by fire and by his sword will\n"
    .string "the LORD plead with all flesh: and\l"
    .string "the slain of the LORD shall be many.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_17::
    .string "They that sanctify themselves, and\n"
    .string "purify themselves in the gardens\l"
    .string "behind one tree in the midst, eating\l"
    .string "swine’s flesh, and the abomination,\l"
    .string "and the mouse, shall be consumed\l"
    .string "together, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_18::
    .string "For I know their works and their\n"
    .string "thoughts: it shall come, that I\l"
    .string "will gather all nations and\l"
    .string "tongues; and they shall come, and\l"
    .string "see my glory.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_19::
    .string "And I will set a sign among them,\n"
    .string "and I will send those that escape\l"
    .string "of them unto the nations, to\l"
    .string "Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, that draw the\l"
    .string "bow, to Tubal, and Javan, to the\l"
    .string "isles afar off, that have not heard\l"
    .string "my fame, neither have seen my glory;\l"
    .string "and they shall declare my glory\l"
    .string "among the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_20::
    .string "And they shall bring all your\n"
    .string "brethren for an offering unto the\l"
    .string "LORD out of all nations upon\l"
    .string "horses, and in chariots, and in\l"
    .string "litters, and upon mules, and upon\l"
    .string "swift beasts, to my holy mountain\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, saith the LORD, as the\l"
    .string "children of Israel bring an\l"
    .string "offering in a clean vessel into the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_21::
    .string "And I will also take of them for\n"
    .string "priests and for Levites, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_22::
    .string "For as the new heavens and the new\n"
    .string "earth, which I will make, shall\l"
    .string "remain before me, saith the LORD, so\l"
    .string "shall your seed and your name\l"
    .string "remain.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_23::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "from one new moon to another, and\l"
    .string "from one sabbath to another, shall\l"
    .string "all flesh come to worship before\l"
    .string "me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Isaiah_66_24::
    .string "And they shall go forth, and look\n"
    .string "upon the carcases of the men that\l"
    .string "have transgressed against me: for\l"
    .string "their worm shall not die, neither\l"
    .string "shall their fire be quenched; and\l"
    .string "they shall be an abhorring unto\l"
    .string "all flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_1::
    .string "The words of Jeremiah the son of\n"
    .string "Hilkiah, of the priests that were in\l"
    .string "Anathoth in the land of Benjamin:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_2::
    .string "To whom the word of the LORD came in\n"
    .string "the days of Josiah the son of Amon\l"
    .string "king of Judah, in the thirteenth year\l"
    .string "of his reign$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_3::
    .string "It came also in the days of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah, unto the end of the eleventh\l"
    .string "year of Zedekiah the son of Josiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, unto the carrying away\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem captive in the fifth\l"
    .string "month.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_4::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_5::
    .string "Before I formed thee in the belly I\n"
    .string "knew thee; and before thou camest\l"
    .string "forth out of the womb I sanctified\l"
    .string "thee, and I ordained thee a prophet\l"
    .string "unto the nations$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_6::
    .string "Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! behold, I\n"
    .string "cannot speak: for I am a child.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_7::
    .string "But the LORD said unto me, Say not, I\n"
    .string "am a child: for thou shalt go to\l"
    .string "all that I shall send thee, and\l"
    .string "whatsoever I command thee thou shalt\l"
    .string "speak.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_8::
    .string "Be not afraid of their faces: for I\n"
    .string "am with thee to deliver thee, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_9::
    .string "Then the LORD put forth his hand,\n"
    .string "and touched my mouth. And the LORD\l"
    .string "said unto me, Behold, I have put my\l"
    .string "words in thy mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_10::
    .string "See, I have this day set thee over\n"
    .string "the nations and over the kingdoms, to\l"
    .string "root out, and to pull down, and to\l"
    .string "destroy, and to throw down, to build,\l"
    .string "and to plant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_11::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying, Jeremiah, what seest\l"
    .string "thou? And I said, I see a rod of an\l"
    .string "almond tree.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_12::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, Thou\n"
    .string "hast well seen: for I will hasten\l"
    .string "my word to perform it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_13::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me the second time, saying, What\l"
    .string "seest thou? And I said, I see a\l"
    .string "seething pot; and the face thereof\l"
    .string "is toward the north.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_14::
    .string "Then the LORD said unto me, Out of\n"
    .string "the north an evil shall break forth\l"
    .string "upon all the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_15::
    .string "For, lo, I will call all the\n"
    .string "families of the kingdoms of the\l"
    .string "north, saith the LORD; and they\l"
    .string "shall come, and they shall set\l"
    .string "every one his throne at the entering\l"
    .string "of the gates of Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "against all the walls thereof\l"
    .string "round about, and against all the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_16::
    .string "And I will utter my judgments\n"
    .string "against them touching all their\l"
    .string "wickedness, who have forsaken me, and\l"
    .string "have burned incense unto other gods,\l"
    .string "and worshipped the works of their\l"
    .string "own hands.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_17::
    .string "Thou therefore gird up thy loins,\n"
    .string "and arise, and speak unto them all\l"
    .string "that I command thee: be not dismayed\l"
    .string "at their faces, lest I confound thee\l"
    .string "before them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_18::
    .string "For, behold, I have made thee this\n"
    .string "day a defenced city, and an iron\l"
    .string "pillar, and brasen walls against\l"
    .string "the whole land, against the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah, against the princes thereof,\l"
    .string "against the priests thereof, and\l"
    .string "against the people of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_1_19::
    .string "And they shall fight against thee;\n"
    .string "but they shall not prevail against\l"
    .string "thee; for I am with thee, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, to deliver thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_1::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "to me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_2::
    .string "Go and cry in the ears of Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "saying, Thus saith the LORD; I\l"
    .string "remember thee, the kindness of thy\l"
    .string "youth, the love of thine espousals,\l"
    .string "when thou wentest after me in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, in a land that was not\l"
    .string "sown$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_3::
    .string "Israel was holiness unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and the firstfruits of his increase:\l"
    .string "all that devour him shall offend;\l"
    .string "evil shall come upon them, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_4::
    .string "Hear ye the word of the LORD, O house\n"
    .string "of Jacob, and all the families of\l"
    .string "the house of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_5::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, What iniquity\n"
    .string "have your fathers found in me, that\l"
    .string "they are gone far from me, and have\l"
    .string "walked after vanity, and are become\l"
    .string "vain?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_6::
    .string "Neither said they, Where is the LORD\n"
    .string "that brought us up out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, that led us through the\l"
    .string "wilderness, through a land of\l"
    .string "deserts and of pits, through a land\l"
    .string "of drought, and of the shadow of\l"
    .string "death, through a land that no man\l"
    .string "passed through, and where no man\l"
    .string "dwelt?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_7::
    .string "And I brought you into a plentiful\n"
    .string "country, to eat the fruit thereof and\l"
    .string "the goodness thereof; but when ye\l"
    .string "entered, ye defiled my land, and\l"
    .string "made mine heritage an abomination$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_8::
    .string "The priests said not, Where is the\n"
    .string "LORD? and they that handle the law\l"
    .string "knew me not: the pastors also\l"
    .string "transgressed against me, and the\l"
    .string "prophets prophesied by Baal, and\l"
    .string "walked after things that do not\l"
    .string "profit.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_9::
    .string "Wherefore I will yet plead with\n"
    .string "you, saith the LORD, and with your\l"
    .string "children’s children will I plead.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_10::
    .string "For pass over the isles of Chittim,\n"
    .string "and see; and send unto Kedar, and\l"
    .string "consider diligently, and see if\l"
    .string "there be such a thing.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_11::
    .string "Hath a nation changed their gods,\n"
    .string "which are yet no gods? but my\l"
    .string "people have changed their glory\l"
    .string "for that which doth not profit.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_12::
    .string "Be astonished, O ye heavens, at\n"
    .string "this, and be horribly afraid, be ye\l"
    .string "very desolate, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_13::
    .string "For my people have committed two\n"
    .string "evils; they have forsaken me the\l"
    .string "fountain of living waters, and hewed\l"
    .string "them out cisterns, broken cisterns,\l"
    .string "that can hold no water.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_14::
    .string "Is Israel a servant? is he a\n"
    .string "homeborn slave? why is he spoiled?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_15::
    .string "The young lions roared upon him,\n"
    .string "and yelled, and they made his land\l"
    .string "waste: his cities are burned without\l"
    .string "inhabitant$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_16::
    .string "Also the children of Noph and\n"
    .string "Tahapanes have broken the crown of\l"
    .string "thy head.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_17::
    .string "Hast thou not procured this unto\n"
    .string "thyself, in that thou hast forsaken\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God, when he led thee by\l"
    .string "the way?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_18::
    .string "And now what hast thou to do in the\n"
    .string "way of Egypt, to drink the waters of\l"
    .string "Sihor? or what hast thou to do in the\l"
    .string "way of Assyria, to drink the waters\l"
    .string "of the river?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_19::
    .string "Thine own wickedness shall correct\n"
    .string "thee, and thy backslidings shall\l"
    .string "reprove thee: know therefore and see\l"
    .string "that it is an evil thing and bitter,\l"
    .string "that thou hast forsaken the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God, and that my fear is not in thee,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD of hosts$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_20::
    .string "For of old time I have broken thy\n"
    .string "yoke, and burst thy bands; and thou\l"
    .string "saidst, I will not transgress; when\l"
    .string "upon every high hill and under\l"
    .string "every green tree thou wanderest,\l"
    .string "playing the harlot.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_21::
    .string "Yet I had planted thee a noble\n"
    .string "vine, wholly a right seed: how then\l"
    .string "art thou turned into the degenerate\l"
    .string "plant of a strange vine unto me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_22::
    .string "For though thou wash thee with\n"
    .string "nitre, and take thee much soap, yet\l"
    .string "thine iniquity is marked before me,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_23::
    .string "How canst thou say, I am not\n"
    .string "polluted, I have not gone after\l"
    .string "Baalim? see thy way in the valley,\l"
    .string "know what thou hast done: thou art a\l"
    .string "swift dromedary traversing her ways;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_24::
    .string "A wild ass used to the wilderness,\n"
    .string "that snuffeth up the wind at her\l"
    .string "pleasure; in her occasion who can\l"
    .string "turn her away? all they that seek\l"
    .string "her will not weary themselves; in\l"
    .string "her month they shall find her$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_25::
    .string "Withhold thy foot from being\n"
    .string "unshod, and thy throat from thirst:\l"
    .string "but thou saidst, There is no hope:\l"
    .string "no; for I have loved strangers, and\l"
    .string "after them will I go.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_26::
    .string "As the thief is ashamed when he is\n"
    .string "found, so is the house of Israel\l"
    .string "ashamed; they, their kings, their\l"
    .string "princes, and their priests, and\l"
    .string "their prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_27::
    .string "Saying to a stock, Thou art my\n"
    .string "father; and to a stone, Thou hast\l"
    .string "brought me forth: for they have\l"
    .string "turned their back unto me, and not\l"
    .string "their face: but in the time of their\l"
    .string "trouble they will say, Arise, and\l"
    .string "save us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_28::
    .string "But where are thy gods that thou\n"
    .string "hast made thee? let them arise, if\l"
    .string "they can save thee in the time of thy\l"
    .string "trouble: for according to the number\l"
    .string "of thy cities are thy gods, O Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_29::
    .string "Wherefore will ye plead with me?\n"
    .string "ye all have transgressed against\l"
    .string "me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_30::
    .string "In vain have I smitten your\n"
    .string "children; they received no\l"
    .string "correction: your own sword hath\l"
    .string "devoured your prophets, like a\l"
    .string "destroying lion.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_31::
    .string "O generation, see ye the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD. Have I been a wilderness unto\l"
    .string "Israel? a land of darkness?\l"
    .string "wherefore say my people, We are\l"
    .string "lords; we will come no more unto\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_32::
    .string "Can a maid forget her ornaments, or\n"
    .string "a bride her attire? yet my people\l"
    .string "have forgotten me days without number$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_33::
    .string "Why trimmest thou thy way to seek\n"
    .string "love? therefore hast thou also\l"
    .string "taught the wicked ones thy ways.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_34::
    .string "Also in thy skirts is found the\n"
    .string "blood of the souls of the poor\l"
    .string "innocents: I have not found it by\l"
    .string "secret search, but upon all these.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_35::
    .string "Yet thou sayest, Because I am\n"
    .string "innocent, surely his anger shall\l"
    .string "turn from me. Behold, I will plead\l"
    .string "with thee, because thou sayest, I\l"
    .string "have not sinned.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_36::
    .string "Why gaddest thou about so much to\n"
    .string "change thy way? thou also shalt be\l"
    .string "ashamed of Egypt, as thou wast\l"
    .string "ashamed of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_2_37::
    .string "Yea, thou shalt go forth from him,\n"
    .string "and thine hands upon thine head: for\l"
    .string "the LORD hath rejected thy\l"
    .string "confidences, and thou shalt not\l"
    .string "prosper in them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_1::
    .string "They say, If a man put away his\n"
    .string "wife, and she go from him, and become\l"
    .string "another man’s, shall he return unto\l"
    .string "her again? shall not that land be\l"
    .string "greatly polluted? but thou hast\l"
    .string "played the harlot with many lovers;\l"
    .string "yet return again to me, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_2::
    .string "Lift up thine eyes unto the high\n"
    .string "places, and see where thou hast not\l"
    .string "been lien with. In the ways hast thou\l"
    .string "sat for them, as the Arabian in the\l"
    .string "wilderness; and thou hast polluted\l"
    .string "the land with thy whoredoms and with\l"
    .string "thy wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_3::
    .string "Therefore the showers have been\n"
    .string "withholden, and there hath been no\l"
    .string "latter rain; and thou hadst a whore’s\l"
    .string "forehead, thou refusedst to be\l"
    .string "ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_4::
    .string "Wilt thou not from this time cry\n"
    .string "unto me, My father, thou art the\l"
    .string "guide of my youth?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_5::
    .string "Will he reserve his anger for ever?\n"
    .string "will he keep it to the end? Behold,\l"
    .string "thou hast spoken and done evil\l"
    .string "things as thou couldest$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_6::
    .string "The LORD said also unto me in the\n"
    .string "days of Josiah the king, Hast thou\l"
    .string "seen that which backsliding Israel\l"
    .string "hath done? she is gone up upon every\l"
    .string "high mountain and under every green\l"
    .string "tree, and there hath played the\l"
    .string "harlot.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_7::
    .string "And I said after she had done all\n"
    .string "these things, Turn thou unto me. But\l"
    .string "she returned not. And her treacherous\l"
    .string "sister Judah saw it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_8::
    .string "And I saw, when for all the causes\n"
    .string "whereby backsliding Israel\l"
    .string "committed adultery I had put her\l"
    .string "away, and given her a bill of\l"
    .string "divorce; yet her treacherous sister\l"
    .string "Judah feared not, but went and\l"
    .string "played the harlot also.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_9::
    .string "And it came to pass through the\n"
    .string "lightness of her whoredom, that she\l"
    .string "defiled the land, and committed\l"
    .string "adultery with stones and with stocks.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_10::
    .string "And yet for all this her\n"
    .string "treacherous sister Judah hath not\l"
    .string "turned unto me with her whole heart,\l"
    .string "but feignedly, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_11::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, The\n"
    .string "backsliding Israel hath justified\l"
    .string "herself more than treacherous Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_12::
    .string "Go and proclaim these words toward\n"
    .string "the north, and say, Return, thou\l"
    .string "backsliding Israel, saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "and I will not cause mine anger to\l"
    .string "fall upon you: for I am merciful,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, and I will not keep\l"
    .string "anger for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_13::
    .string "Only acknowledge thine iniquity,\n"
    .string "that thou hast transgressed against\l"
    .string "the LORD thy God, and hast scattered\l"
    .string "thy ways to the strangers under every\l"
    .string "green tree, and ye have not obeyed my\l"
    .string "voice, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_14::
    .string "Turn, O backsliding children,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; for I am married unto\l"
    .string "you: and I will take you one of a\l"
    .string "city, and two of a family, and I\l"
    .string "will bring you to Zion:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_15::
    .string "And I will give you pastors\n"
    .string "according to mine heart, which\l"
    .string "shall feed you with knowledge and\l"
    .string "understanding$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_16::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when ye\n"
    .string "be multiplied and increased in the\l"
    .string "land, in those days, saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "they shall say no more, The ark of\l"
    .string "the covenant of the LORD: neither\l"
    .string "shall it come to mind: neither\l"
    .string "shall they remember it; neither\l"
    .string "shall they visit it; neither shall\l"
    .string "that be done any more.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_17::
    .string "At that time they shall call\n"
    .string "Jerusalem the throne of the LORD;\l"
    .string "and all the nations shall be\l"
    .string "gathered unto it, to the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD, to Jerusalem: neither shall\l"
    .string "they walk any more after the\l"
    .string "imagination of their evil heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_18::
    .string "In those days the house of Judah\n"
    .string "shall walk with the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, and they shall come\l"
    .string "together out of the land of the\l"
    .string "north to the land that I have given\l"
    .string "for an inheritance unto your fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_19::
    .string "But I said, How shall I put thee\n"
    .string "among the children, and give thee a\l"
    .string "pleasant land, a goodly heritage of\l"
    .string "the hosts of nations? and I said,\l"
    .string "Thou shalt call me, My father; and\l"
    .string "shalt not turn away from me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_20::
    .string "Surely as a wife treacherously\n"
    .string "departeth from her husband, so have\l"
    .string "ye dealt treacherously with me, O\l"
    .string "house of Israel, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_21::
    .string "A voice was heard upon the high\n"
    .string "places, weeping and supplications\l"
    .string "of the children of Israel: for they\l"
    .string "have perverted their way, and they\l"
    .string "have forgotten the LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_22::
    .string "Return, ye backsliding children,\n"
    .string "and I will heal your backslidings.\l"
    .string "Behold, we come unto thee; for thou\l"
    .string "art the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_23::
    .string "Truly in vain is salvation hoped\n"
    .string "for from the hills, and from the\l"
    .string "multitude of mountains: truly in\l"
    .string "the LORD our God is the salvation of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_24::
    .string "For shame hath devoured the labour\n"
    .string "of our fathers from our youth; their\l"
    .string "flocks and their herds, their sons\l"
    .string "and their daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_3_25::
    .string "We lie down in our shame, and our\n"
    .string "confusion covereth us: for we have\l"
    .string "sinned against the LORD our God, we\l"
    .string "and our fathers, from our youth even\l"
    .string "unto this day, and have not obeyed\l"
    .string "the voice of the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_1::
    .string "If thou wilt return, O Israel,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, return unto me: and\l"
    .string "if thou wilt put away thine\l"
    .string "abominations out of my sight, then\l"
    .string "shalt thou not remove.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_2::
    .string "And thou shalt swear, The LORD\n"
    .string "liveth, in truth, in judgment, and in\l"
    .string "righteousness; and the nations\l"
    .string "shall bless themselves in him, and\l"
    .string "in him shall they glory.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_3::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD to the men\n"
    .string "of Judah and Jerusalem, Break up\l"
    .string "your fallow ground, and sow not\l"
    .string "among thorns.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_4::
    .string "Circumcise yourselves to the LORD,\n"
    .string "and take away the foreskins of your\l"
    .string "heart, ye men of Judah and\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem: lest my\l"
    .string "fury come forth like fire, and burn\l"
    .string "that none can quench it, because of\l"
    .string "the evil of your doings.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_5::
    .string "Declare ye in Judah, and publish\n"
    .string "in Jerusalem; and say, Blow ye the\l"
    .string "trumpet in the land: cry, gather\l"
    .string "together, and say, Assemble\l"
    .string "yourselves, and let us go into the\l"
    .string "defenced cities.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_6::
    .string "Set up the standard toward Zion:\n"
    .string "retire, stay not: for I will bring\l"
    .string "evil from the north, and a great\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_7::
    .string "The lion is come up from his\n"
    .string "thicket, and the destroyer of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles is on his way; he is gone\l"
    .string "forth from his place to make thy\l"
    .string "land desolate; and thy cities shall\l"
    .string "be laid waste, without an inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_8::
    .string "For this gird you with sackcloth,\n"
    .string "lament and howl: for the fierce\l"
    .string "anger of the LORD is not turned back\l"
    .string "from us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass at that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD, that the heart\l"
    .string "of the king shall perish, and the\l"
    .string "heart of the princes; and the\l"
    .string "priests shall be astonished, and\l"
    .string "the prophets shall wonder.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_10::
    .string "Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! surely\n"
    .string "thou hast greatly deceived this\l"
    .string "people and Jerusalem, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "shall have peace; whereas the sword\l"
    .string "reacheth unto the soul.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_11::
    .string "At that time shall it be said to\n"
    .string "this people and to Jerusalem, A\l"
    .string "dry wind of the high places in the\l"
    .string "wilderness toward the daughter of my\l"
    .string "people, not to fan, nor to cleanse,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_12::
    .string "Even a full wind from those\n"
    .string "places shall come unto me: now\l"
    .string "also will I give sentence against\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_13::
    .string "Behold, he shall come up as\n"
    .string "clouds, and his chariots shall be\l"
    .string "as a whirlwind: his horses are\l"
    .string "swifter than eagles. Woe unto us!\l"
    .string "for we are spoiled.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_14::
    .string "O Jerusalem, wash thine heart from\n"
    .string "wickedness, that thou mayest be saved\l"
    .string " How long shall thy vain thoughts\l"
    .string "lodge within thee?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_15::
    .string "For a voice declareth from Dan, and\n"
    .string "publisheth affliction from mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_16::
    .string "Make ye mention to the nations;\n"
    .string "behold, publish against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, that watchers come from a\l"
    .string "far country, and give out their voice\l"
    .string "against the cities of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_17::
    .string "As keepers of a field, are they\n"
    .string "against her round about; because she\l"
    .string "hath been rebellious against me,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_18::
    .string "Thy way and thy doings have\n"
    .string "procured these things unto thee; this\l"
    .string "is thy wickedness, because it is\l"
    .string "bitter, because it reacheth unto\l"
    .string "thine heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_19::
    .string "My bowels, my bowels! I am pained\n"
    .string "at my very heart; my heart maketh a\l"
    .string "noise in me; I cannot hold my peace,\l"
    .string "because thou hast heard, O my soul,\l"
    .string "the sound of the trumpet, the alarm\l"
    .string "of war.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_20::
    .string "Destruction upon destruction is\n"
    .string "cried; for the whole land is\l"
    .string "spoiled: suddenly are my tents\l"
    .string "spoiled, and my curtains in a\l"
    .string "moment.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_21::
    .string "How long shall I see the standard,\n"
    .string "and hear the sound of the trumpet?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_22::
    .string "For my people is foolish, they\n"
    .string "have not known me; they are sottish\l"
    .string "children, and they have none\l"
    .string "understanding: they are wise to do\l"
    .string "evil, but to do good they have no\l"
    .string "knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_23::
    .string "I beheld the earth, and, lo, it was\n"
    .string "without form, and void; and the\l"
    .string "heavens, and they had no light.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_24::
    .string "I beheld the mountains, and, lo,\n"
    .string "they trembled, and all the hills\l"
    .string "moved lightly.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_25::
    .string "I beheld, and, lo, there was no\n"
    .string "man, and all the birds of the\l"
    .string "heavens were fled.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_26::
    .string "I beheld, and, lo, the fruitful\n"
    .string "place was a wilderness, and all\l"
    .string "the cities thereof were broken down\l"
    .string "at the presence of the LORD, and by\l"
    .string "his fierce anger.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_27::
    .string "For thus hath the LORD said, The\n"
    .string "whole land shall be desolate; yet\l"
    .string "will I not make a full end.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_28::
    .string "For this shall the earth mourn, and\n"
    .string "the heavens above be black; because\l"
    .string "I have spoken it, I have purposed\l"
    .string "it, and will not repent, neither\l"
    .string "will I turn back from it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_29::
    .string "The whole city shall flee for the\n"
    .string "noise of the horsemen and bowmen;\l"
    .string "they shall go into thickets, and\l"
    .string "climb up upon the rocks: every city\l"
    .string "shall be forsaken, and not a man\l"
    .string "dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_30::
    .string "And when thou art spoiled, what\n"
    .string "wilt thou do? Though thou clothest\l"
    .string "thyself with crimson, though thou\l"
    .string "deckest thee with ornaments of gold,\l"
    .string "though thou rentest thy face with\l"
    .string "painting, in vain shalt thou make\l"
    .string "thyself fair; thy lovers will\l"
    .string "despise thee, they will seek thy\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_4_31::
    .string "For I have heard a voice as of a\n"
    .string "woman in travail, and the anguish as\l"
    .string "of her that bringeth forth her first\l"
    .string "child, the voice of the daughter of\l"
    .string "Zion, that bewaileth herself, that\l"
    .string "spreadeth her hands, saying, Woe is\l"
    .string "me now! for my soul is wearied\l"
    .string "because of murderers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_1::
    .string "Run ye to and fro through the\n"
    .string "streets of Jerusalem, and see now,\l"
    .string "and know, and seek in the broad\l"
    .string "places thereof, if ye can find a man,\l"
    .string "if there be any that executeth\l"
    .string "judgment, that seeketh the truth; and\l"
    .string "I will pardon it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_2::
    .string "And though they say, The LORD\n"
    .string "liveth; surely they swear falsely.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_3::
    .string "O LORD, are not thine eyes upon the\n"
    .string "truth? thou hast stricken them, but\l"
    .string "they have not grieved; thou hast\l"
    .string "consumed them, but they have refused\l"
    .string "to receive correction: they have made\l"
    .string "their faces harder than a rock; they\l"
    .string "have refused to return.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_4::
    .string "Therefore I said, Surely these are\n"
    .string "poor; they are foolish: for they\l"
    .string "know not the way of the LORD, nor the\l"
    .string "judgment of their God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_5::
    .string "I will get me unto the great men,\n"
    .string "and will speak unto them; for they\l"
    .string "have known the way of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "the judgment of their God: but these\l"
    .string "have altogether broken the yoke, and\l"
    .string "burst the bonds.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_6::
    .string "Wherefore a lion out of the forest\n"
    .string "shall slay them, and a wolf of the\l"
    .string "evenings shall spoil them, a\l"
    .string "leopard shall watch over their\l"
    .string "cities: every one that goeth out\l"
    .string "thence shall be torn in pieces:\l"
    .string "because their transgressions are\l"
    .string "many, and their backslidings are\l"
    .string "increased.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_7::
    .string "How shall I pardon thee for this?\n"
    .string "thy children have forsaken me, and\l"
    .string "sworn by them that are no gods: when I\l"
    .string "had fed them to the full, they then\l"
    .string "committed adultery, and assembled\l"
    .string "themselves by troops in the\l"
    .string "harlots’ houses.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_8::
    .string "They were as fed horses in the\n"
    .string "morning: every one neighed after his\l"
    .string "neighbour’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_9::
    .string "Shall I not visit for these things?\n"
    .string "saith the LORD: and shall not my\l"
    .string "soul be avenged on such a nation as\l"
    .string "this?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_10::
    .string "Go ye up upon her walls, and\n"
    .string "destroy; but make not a full end:\l"
    .string "take away her battlements; for they\l"
    .string "are not the LORD’s$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_11::
    .string "For the house of Israel and the\n"
    .string "house of Judah have dealt very\l"
    .string "treacherously against me, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_12::
    .string "They have belied the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, It is not he; neither shall\l"
    .string "evil come upon us; neither shall\l"
    .string "we see sword nor famine:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_13::
    .string "And the prophets shall become\n"
    .string "wind, and the word is not in them:\l"
    .string "thus shall it be done unto them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_14::
    .string "Wherefore thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "hosts, Because ye speak this word,\l"
    .string "behold, I will make my words in thy\l"
    .string "mouth fire, and this people wood,\l"
    .string "and it shall devour them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_15::
    .string "Lo, I will bring a nation upon you\n"
    .string "from far, O house of Israel, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD: it is a mighty nation, it is\l"
    .string "an ancient nation, a nation whose\l"
    .string "language thou knowest not, neither\l"
    .string "understandest what they say.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_16::
    .string "Their quiver is as an open\n"
    .string "sepulchre, they are all mighty men.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_17::
    .string "And they shall eat up thine\n"
    .string "harvest, and thy bread, which thy\l"
    .string "sons and thy daughters should eat:\l"
    .string "they shall eat up thy flocks and\l"
    .string "thine herds: they shall eat up thy\l"
    .string "vines and thy fig trees: they shall\l"
    .string "impoverish thy fenced cities,\l"
    .string "wherein thou trustedst, with the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_18::
    .string "Nevertheless in those days, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, I will not make a full\l"
    .string "end with you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_19::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when ye\n"
    .string "shall say, Wherefore doeth the LORD\l"
    .string "our God all these things unto us?\l"
    .string "then shalt thou answer them, Like as\l"
    .string "ye have forsaken me, and served\l"
    .string "strange gods in your land, so shall\l"
    .string "ye serve strangers in a land that is\l"
    .string "not yours.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_20::
    .string "Declare this in the house of Jacob,\n"
    .string "and publish it in Judah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_21::
    .string "Hear now this, O foolish people,\n"
    .string "and without understanding; which\l"
    .string "have eyes, and see not; which have\l"
    .string "ears, and hear not:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_22::
    .string "Fear ye not me? saith the LORD:\n"
    .string "will ye not tremble at my\l"
    .string "presence, which have placed the\l"
    .string "sand for the bound of the sea by a\l"
    .string "perpetual decree, that it cannot\l"
    .string "pass it: and though the waves thereof\l"
    .string "toss themselves, yet can they not\l"
    .string "prevail; though they roar, yet can\l"
    .string "they not pass over it?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_23::
    .string "But this people hath a revolting\n"
    .string "and a rebellious heart; they are\l"
    .string "revolted and gone$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_24::
    .string "Neither say they in their heart, Let\n"
    .string "us now fear the LORD our God, that\l"
    .string "giveth rain, both the former and the\l"
    .string "latter, in his season: he reserveth\l"
    .string "unto us the appointed weeks of the\l"
    .string "harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_25::
    .string "Your iniquities have turned away\n"
    .string "these things, and your sins have\l"
    .string "withholden good things from you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_26::
    .string "For among my people are found\n"
    .string "wicked men: they lay wait, as he that\l"
    .string "setteth snares; they set a trap,\l"
    .string "they catch men.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_27::
    .string "As a cage is full of birds, so are\n"
    .string "their houses full of deceit:\l"
    .string "therefore they are become great, and\l"
    .string "waxen rich.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_28::
    .string "They are waxen fat, they shine: yea,\n"
    .string "they overpass the deeds of the\l"
    .string "wicked: they judge not the cause, the\l"
    .string "cause of the fatherless, yet they\l"
    .string "prosper; and the right of the needy\l"
    .string "do they not judge.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_29::
    .string "Shall I not visit for these things?\n"
    .string "saith the LORD: shall not my soul\l"
    .string "be avenged on such a nation as this?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_30::
    .string "A wonderful and horrible thing is\n"
    .string "committed in the land;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_5_31::
    .string "The prophets prophesy falsely,\n"
    .string "and the priests bear rule by their\l"
    .string "means; and my people love to have\l"
    .string "it so: and what will ye do in the end\l"
    .string "thereof?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_1::
    .string "O ye children of Benjamin, gather\n"
    .string "yourselves to flee out of the midst\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, and blow the trumpet\l"
    .string "in Tekoa, and set up a sign of fire\l"
    .string "in Bethhaccerem: for evil\l"
    .string "appeareth out of the north, and\l"
    .string "great destruction$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_2::
    .string "I have likened the daughter of Zion\n"
    .string "to a comely and delicate woman.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_3::
    .string "The shepherds with their flocks\n"
    .string "shall come unto her; they shall\l"
    .string "pitch their tents against her round\l"
    .string "about; they shall feed every one in\l"
    .string "his place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_4::
    .string "Prepare ye war against her; arise,\n"
    .string "and let us go up at noon. Woe unto\l"
    .string "us! for the day goeth away, for the\l"
    .string "shadows of the evening are stretched\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_5::
    .string "Arise, and let us go by night, and\n"
    .string "let us destroy her palaces.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_6::
    .string "For thus hath the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "said, Hew ye down trees, and cast a\l"
    .string "mount against Jerusalem: this is the\l"
    .string "city to be visited; she is wholly\l"
    .string "oppression in the midst of her.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_7::
    .string "As a fountain casteth out her\n"
    .string "waters, so she casteth out her\l"
    .string "wickedness: violence and spoil is\l"
    .string "heard in her; before me continually\l"
    .string "is grief and wounds.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_8::
    .string "Be thou instructed, O Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "lest my soul depart from thee; lest\l"
    .string "I make thee desolate, a land not\l"
    .string "inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_9::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, They\n"
    .string "shall throughly glean the remnant\l"
    .string "of Israel as a vine: turn back thine\l"
    .string "hand as a grapegatherer into the\l"
    .string "baskets.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_10::
    .string "To whom shall I speak, and give\n"
    .string "warning, that they may hear? behold,\l"
    .string "their ear is uncircumcised, and they\l"
    .string "cannot hearken: behold, the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD is unto them a reproach;\l"
    .string "they have no delight in it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_11::
    .string "Therefore I am full of the fury of\n"
    .string "the LORD; I am weary with holding in:\l"
    .string "I will pour it out upon the\l"
    .string "children abroad, and upon the\l"
    .string "assembly of young men together: for\l"
    .string "even the husband with the wife\l"
    .string "shall be taken, the aged with him\l"
    .string "that is full of days.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_12::
    .string "And their houses shall be turned\n"
    .string "unto others, with their fields and\l"
    .string "wives together: for I will stretch\l"
    .string "out my hand upon the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "the land, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_13::
    .string "For from the least of them even\n"
    .string "unto the greatest of them every one\l"
    .string "is given to covetousness; and from\l"
    .string "the prophet even unto the priest\l"
    .string "every one dealeth falsely.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_14::
    .string "They have healed also the hurt of\n"
    .string "the daughter of my people\l"
    .string "slightly, saying, Peace, peace;\l"
    .string "when there is no peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_15::
    .string "Were they ashamed when they had\n"
    .string "committed abomination? nay, they\l"
    .string "were not at all ashamed, neither\l"
    .string "could they blush: therefore they\l"
    .string "shall fall among them that fall:\l"
    .string "at the time that I visit them they\l"
    .string "shall be cast down, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_16::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Stand ye in the\n"
    .string "ways, and see, and ask for the old\l"
    .string "paths, where is the good way, and\l"
    .string "walk therein, and ye shall find\l"
    .string "rest for your souls. But they said,\l"
    .string "We will not walk therein.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_17::
    .string "Also I set watchmen over you,\n"
    .string "saying, Hearken to the sound of the\l"
    .string "trumpet. But they said, We will not\l"
    .string "hearken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_18::
    .string "Therefore hear, ye nations, and\n"
    .string "know, O congregation, what is among\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_19::
    .string "Hear, O earth: behold, I will\n"
    .string "bring evil upon this people, even\l"
    .string "the fruit of their thoughts, because\l"
    .string "they have not hearkened unto my\l"
    .string "words, nor to my law, but rejected it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_20::
    .string "To what purpose cometh there to me\n"
    .string "incense from Sheba, and the sweet\l"
    .string "cane from a far country? your burnt\l"
    .string "offerings are not acceptable, nor\l"
    .string "your sacrifices sweet unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_21::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "Behold, I will lay\l"
    .string "stumblingblocks before this\l"
    .string "people, and the fathers and the sons\l"
    .string "together shall fall upon them;\l"
    .string "the neighbour and his friend shall\l"
    .string "perish.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_22::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Behold, a\n"
    .string "people cometh from the north\l"
    .string "country, and a great nation shall be\l"
    .string "raised from the sides of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_23::
    .string "They shall lay hold on bow and\n"
    .string "spear; they are cruel, and have no\l"
    .string "mercy; their voice roareth like the\l"
    .string "sea; and they ride upon horses, set\l"
    .string "in array as men for war against thee,\l"
    .string "O daughter of Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_24::
    .string "We have heard the fame thereof: our\n"
    .string "hands wax feeble: anguish hath taken\l"
    .string "hold of us, and pain, as of a woman\l"
    .string "in travail.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_25::
    .string "Go not forth into the field, nor\n"
    .string "walk by the way; for the sword of the\l"
    .string "enemy and fear is on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_26::
    .string "O daughter of my people, gird thee\n"
    .string "with sackcloth, and wallow thyself\l"
    .string "in ashes: make thee mourning, as for\l"
    .string "an only son, most bitter\l"
    .string "lamentation: for the spoiler shall\l"
    .string "suddenly come upon us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_27::
    .string "I have set thee for a tower and a\n"
    .string "fortress among my people, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest know and try their way.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_28::
    .string "They are all grievous revolters,\n"
    .string "walking with slanders: they are\l"
    .string "brass and iron; they are all\l"
    .string "corrupters.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_29::
    .string "The bellows are burned, the lead\n"
    .string "is consumed of the fire; the founder\l"
    .string "melteth in vain: for the wicked are\l"
    .string "not plucked away.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_6_30::
    .string "Reprobate silver shall men call\n"
    .string "them, because the LORD hath rejected\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_2::
    .string "Stand in the gate of the LORD’s\n"
    .string "house, and proclaim there this\l"
    .string "word, and say, Hear the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD, all ye of Judah, that enter in\l"
    .string "at these gates to worship the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_3::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel, Amend your ways and\l"
    .string "your doings, and I will cause you to\l"
    .string "dwell in this place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_4::
    .string "Trust ye not in lying words,\n"
    .string "saying, The temple of the LORD, The\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD, The temple of\l"
    .string "the LORD, are these.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_5::
    .string "For if ye throughly amend your ways\n"
    .string "and your doings; if ye throughly\l"
    .string "execute judgment between a man and\l"
    .string "his neighbour;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_6::
    .string "If ye oppress not the stranger, the\n"
    .string "fatherless, and the widow, and shed\l"
    .string "not innocent blood in this place,\l"
    .string "neither walk after other gods to\l"
    .string "your hurt:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_7::
    .string "Then will I cause you to dwell in\n"
    .string "this place, in the land that I gave\l"
    .string "to your fathers, for ever and ever$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_8::
    .string "Behold, ye trust in lying words,\n"
    .string "that cannot profit.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_9::
    .string "Will ye steal, murder, and commit\n"
    .string "adultery, and swear falsely, and\l"
    .string "burn incense unto Baal, and walk\l"
    .string "after other gods whom ye know not;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_10::
    .string "And come and stand before me in this\n"
    .string "house, which is called by my name,\l"
    .string "and say, We are delivered to do all\l"
    .string "these abominations?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_11::
    .string "Is this house, which is called by\n"
    .string "my name, become a den of robbers in\l"
    .string "your eyes? Behold, even I have seen\l"
    .string "it, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_12::
    .string "But go ye now unto my place which\n"
    .string "was in Shiloh, where I set my name at\l"
    .string "the first, and see what I did to it\l"
    .string "for the wickedness of my people\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_13::
    .string "And now, because ye have done all\n"
    .string "these works, saith the LORD, and I\l"
    .string "spake unto you, rising up early and\l"
    .string "speaking, but ye heard not; and I\l"
    .string "called you, but ye answered not;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_14::
    .string "Therefore will I do unto this\n"
    .string "house, which is called by my name,\l"
    .string "wherein ye trust, and unto the place\l"
    .string "which I gave to you and to your\l"
    .string "fathers, as I have done to Shiloh$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_15::
    .string "And I will cast you out of my\n"
    .string "sight, as I have cast out all your\l"
    .string "brethren, even the whole seed of\l"
    .string "Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_16::
    .string "Therefore pray not thou for this\n"
    .string "people, neither lift up cry nor\l"
    .string "prayer for them, neither make\l"
    .string "intercession to me: for I will not\l"
    .string "hear thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_17::
    .string "Seest thou not what they do in the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah and in the streets of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_18::
    .string "The children gather wood, and the\n"
    .string "fathers kindle the fire, and the\l"
    .string "women knead their dough, to make\l"
    .string "cakes to the queen of heaven, and to\l"
    .string "pour out drink offerings unto other\l"
    .string "gods, that they may provoke me to\l"
    .string "anger$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_19::
    .string "Do they provoke me to anger? saith\n"
    .string "the LORD: do they not provoke\l"
    .string "themselves to the confusion of their\l"
    .string "own faces?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_20::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, mine anger and my fury\l"
    .string "shall be poured out upon this\l"
    .string "place, upon man, and upon beast,\l"
    .string "and upon the trees of the field, and\l"
    .string "upon the fruit of the ground; and it\l"
    .string "shall burn, and shall not be\l"
    .string "quenched$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_21::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; Put your burnt\l"
    .string "offerings unto your sacrifices, and\l"
    .string "eat flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_22::
    .string "For I spake not unto your fathers,\n"
    .string "nor commanded them in the day that I\l"
    .string "brought them out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, concerning burnt offerings or\l"
    .string "sacrifices:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_23::
    .string "But this thing commanded I them,\n"
    .string "saying, Obey my voice, and I will be\l"
    .string "your God, and ye shall be my\l"
    .string "people: and walk ye in all the\l"
    .string "ways that I have commanded you, that\l"
    .string "it may be well unto you$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_24::
    .string "But they hearkened not, nor\n"
    .string "inclined their ear, but walked in\l"
    .string "the counsels and in the imagination\l"
    .string "of their evil heart, and went\l"
    .string "backward, and not forward.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_25::
    .string "Since the day that your fathers came\n"
    .string "forth out of the land of Egypt unto\l"
    .string "this day I have even sent unto you\l"
    .string "all my servants the prophets,\l"
    .string "daily rising up early and sending\l"
    .string "them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_26::
    .string "Yet they hearkened not unto me, nor\n"
    .string "inclined their ear, but hardened\l"
    .string "their neck: they did worse than their\l"
    .string "fathers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_27::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt speak all\n"
    .string "these words unto them; but they will\l"
    .string "not hearken to thee: thou shalt also\l"
    .string "call unto them; but they will not\l"
    .string "answer thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_28::
    .string "But thou shalt say unto them, This\n"
    .string "is a nation that obeyeth not the\l"
    .string "voice of the LORD their God, nor\l"
    .string "receiveth correction: truth is\l"
    .string "perished, and is cut off from their\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_29::
    .string "Cut off thine hair, O Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and cast it away, and take up a\l"
    .string "lamentation on high places; for the\l"
    .string "LORD hath rejected and forsaken the\l"
    .string "generation of his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_30::
    .string "For the children of Judah have done\n"
    .string "evil in my sight, saith the LORD:\l"
    .string "they have set their abominations in\l"
    .string "the house which is called by my\l"
    .string "name, to pollute it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_31::
    .string "And they have built the high\n"
    .string "places of Tophet, which is in the\l"
    .string "valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn\l"
    .string "their sons and their daughters in the\l"
    .string "fire; which I commanded them not,\l"
    .string "neither came it into my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_32::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that it shall no\l"
    .string "more be called Tophet, nor the\l"
    .string "valley of the son of Hinnom, but the\l"
    .string "valley of slaughter: for they\l"
    .string "shall bury in Tophet, till there\l"
    .string "be no place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_33::
    .string "And the carcases of this people\n"
    .string "shall be meat for the fowls of the\l"
    .string "heaven, and for the beasts of the\l"
    .string "earth; and none shall fray them\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_7_34::
    .string "Then will I cause to cease from the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah, and from the streets\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, the voice of mirth,\l"
    .string "and the voice of gladness, the voice\l"
    .string "of the bridegroom, and the voice of\l"
    .string "the bride: for the land shall be\l"
    .string "desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_1::
    .string "At that time, saith the LORD, they\n"
    .string "shall bring out the bones of the\l"
    .string "kings of Judah, and the bones of his\l"
    .string "princes, and the bones of the\l"
    .string "priests, and the bones of the\l"
    .string "prophets, and the bones of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, out of\l"
    .string "their graves:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_2::
    .string "And they shall spread them before\n"
    .string "the sun, and the moon, and all the\l"
    .string "host of heaven, whom they have\l"
    .string "loved, and whom they have served, and\l"
    .string "after whom they have walked, and\l"
    .string "whom they have sought, and whom they\l"
    .string "have worshipped: they shall not be\l"
    .string "gathered, nor be buried; they shall\l"
    .string "be for dung upon the face of the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_3::
    .string "And death shall be chosen rather\n"
    .string "than life by all the residue of\l"
    .string "them that remain of this evil\l"
    .string "family, which remain in all the\l"
    .string "places whither I have driven them,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_4::
    .string "Moreover thou shalt say unto them,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Shall they\l"
    .string "fall, and not arise? shall he turn\l"
    .string "away, and not return?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_5::
    .string "Why then is this people of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem slidden back by a\l"
    .string "perpetual backsliding? they hold\l"
    .string "fast deceit, they refuse to return$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_6::
    .string "I hearkened and heard, but they\n"
    .string "spake not aright: no man repented\l"
    .string "him of his wickedness, saying, What\l"
    .string "have I done? every one turned to his\l"
    .string "course, as the horse rusheth into the\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_7::
    .string "Yea, the stork in the heaven knoweth\n"
    .string "her appointed times; and the turtle\l"
    .string "and the crane and the swallow\l"
    .string "observe the time of their coming; but\l"
    .string "my people know not the judgment of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_8::
    .string "How do ye say, We are wise, and the\n"
    .string "law of the LORD is with us? Lo,\l"
    .string "certainly in vain made he it; the\l"
    .string "pen of the scribes is in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_9::
    .string "The wise men are ashamed, they are\n"
    .string "dismayed and taken: lo, they have\l"
    .string "rejected the word of the LORD; and\l"
    .string "what wisdom is in them?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_10::
    .string "Therefore will I give their wives\n"
    .string "unto others, and their fields to\l"
    .string "them that shall inherit them: for\l"
    .string "every one from the least even unto\l"
    .string "the greatest is given to\l"
    .string "covetousness, from the prophet even\l"
    .string "unto the priest every one dealeth\l"
    .string "falsely$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_11::
    .string "For they have healed the hurt of\n"
    .string "the daughter of my people\l"
    .string "slightly, saying, Peace, peace;\l"
    .string "when there is no peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_12::
    .string "Were they ashamed when they had\n"
    .string "committed abomination? nay, they\l"
    .string "were not at all ashamed, neither\l"
    .string "could they blush: therefore shall\l"
    .string "they fall among them that fall: in\l"
    .string "the time of their visitation they\l"
    .string "shall be cast down, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_13::
    .string "I will surely consume them, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD: there shall be no grapes\l"
    .string "on the vine, nor figs on the fig tree,\l"
    .string "and the leaf shall fade; and the\l"
    .string "things that I have given them shall\l"
    .string "pass away from them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_14::
    .string "Why do we sit still? assemble\n"
    .string "yourselves, and let us enter into\l"
    .string "the defenced cities, and let us be\l"
    .string "silent there: for the LORD our God\l"
    .string "hath put us to silence, and given us\l"
    .string "water of gall to drink, because we\l"
    .string "have sinned against the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_15::
    .string "We looked for peace, but no good\n"
    .string "came; and for a time of health, and\l"
    .string "behold trouble!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_16::
    .string "The snorting of his horses was heard\n"
    .string "from Dan: the whole land trembled\l"
    .string "at the sound of the neighing of his\l"
    .string "strong ones; for they are come, and\l"
    .string "have devoured the land, and all\l"
    .string "that is in it; the city, and those\l"
    .string "that dwell therein$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_17::
    .string "For, behold, I will send\n"
    .string "serpents, cockatrices, among you,\l"
    .string "which will not be charmed, and they\l"
    .string "shall bite you, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_18::
    .string "When I would comfort myself\n"
    .string "against sorrow, my heart is faint in\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_19::
    .string "Behold the voice of the cry of the\n"
    .string "daughter of my people because of\l"
    .string "them that dwell in a far country: Is\l"
    .string "not the LORD in Zion? is not her king\l"
    .string "in her? Why have they provoked me to\l"
    .string "anger with their graven images, and\l"
    .string "with strange vanities?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_20::
    .string "The harvest is past, the summer is\n"
    .string "ended, and we are not saved$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_21::
    .string "For the hurt of the daughter of my\n"
    .string "people am I hurt; I am black;\l"
    .string "astonishment hath taken hold on me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_8_22::
    .string "Is there no balm in Gilead; is\n"
    .string "there no physician there? why then\l"
    .string "is not the health of the daughter of\l"
    .string "my people recovered?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_1::
    .string "Oh that my head were waters, and\n"
    .string "mine eyes a fountain of tears, that I\l"
    .string "might weep day and night for the\l"
    .string "slain of the daughter of my\l"
    .string "people!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_2::
    .string "Oh that I had in the wilderness a\n"
    .string "lodging place of wayfaring men;\l"
    .string "that I might leave my people, and\l"
    .string "go from them! for they be all\l"
    .string "adulterers, an assembly of\l"
    .string "treacherous men$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_3::
    .string "And they bend their tongues like\n"
    .string "their bow for lies: but they are not\l"
    .string "valiant for the truth upon the\l"
    .string "earth; for they proceed from evil to\l"
    .string "evil, and they know not me, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_4::
    .string "Take ye heed every one of his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and trust ye not in any\l"
    .string "brother: for every brother will\l"
    .string "utterly supplant, and every\l"
    .string "neighbour will walk with slanders.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_5::
    .string "And they will deceive every one\n"
    .string "his neighbour, and will not speak\l"
    .string "the truth: they have taught their\l"
    .string "tongue to speak lies, and weary\l"
    .string "themselves to commit iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_6::
    .string "Thine habitation is in the midst of\n"
    .string "deceit; through deceit they refuse to\l"
    .string "know me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_7::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, Behold, I will melt them,\l"
    .string "and try them; for how shall I do for\l"
    .string "the daughter of my people?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_8::
    .string "Their tongue is as an arrow shot\n"
    .string "out; it speaketh deceit: one\l"
    .string "speaketh peaceably to his\l"
    .string "neighbour with his mouth, but in\l"
    .string "heart he layeth his wait$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_9::
    .string "Shall I not visit them for these\n"
    .string "things? saith the LORD: shall not my\l"
    .string "soul be avenged on such a nation as\l"
    .string "this?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_10::
    .string "For the mountains will I take up a\n"
    .string "weeping and wailing, and for the\l"
    .string "habitations of the wilderness a\l"
    .string "lamentation, because they are burned\l"
    .string "up, so that none can pass through\l"
    .string "them; neither can men hear the voice\l"
    .string "of the cattle; both the fowl of the\l"
    .string "heavens and the beast are fled; they\l"
    .string "are gone$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_11::
    .string "And I will make Jerusalem heaps,\n"
    .string "and a den of dragons; and I will\l"
    .string "make the cities of Judah desolate,\l"
    .string "without an inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_12::
    .string "Who is the wise man, that may\n"
    .string "understand this? and who is he to\l"
    .string "whom the mouth of the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken, that he may declare it, for\l"
    .string "what the land perisheth and is\l"
    .string "burned up like a wilderness, that\l"
    .string "none passeth through?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_13::
    .string "And the LORD saith, Because they\n"
    .string "have forsaken my law which I set\l"
    .string "before them, and have not obeyed my\l"
    .string "voice, neither walked therein;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_14::
    .string "But have walked after the\n"
    .string "imagination of their own heart, and\l"
    .string "after Baalim, which their fathers\l"
    .string "taught them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_15::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I\l"
    .string "will feed them, even this people,\l"
    .string "with wormwood, and give them water of\l"
    .string "gall to drink$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_16::
    .string "I will scatter them also among the\n"
    .string "heathen, whom neither they nor their\l"
    .string "fathers have known: and I will send\l"
    .string "a sword after them, till I have\l"
    .string "consumed them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_17::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "Consider ye, and call for the\l"
    .string "mourning women, that they may come;\l"
    .string "and send for cunning women, that they\l"
    .string "may come:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_18::
    .string "And let them make haste, and take\n"
    .string "up a wailing for us, that our eyes\l"
    .string "may run down with tears, and our\l"
    .string "eyelids gush out with waters$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_19::
    .string "For a voice of wailing is heard out\n"
    .string "of Zion, How are we spoiled! we are\l"
    .string "greatly confounded, because we have\l"
    .string "forsaken the land, because our\l"
    .string "dwellings have cast us out.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_20::
    .string "Yet hear the word of the LORD, O ye\n"
    .string "women, and let your ear receive the\l"
    .string "word of his mouth, and teach your\l"
    .string "daughters wailing, and every one her\l"
    .string "neighbour lamentation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_21::
    .string "For death is come up into our\n"
    .string "windows, and is entered into our\l"
    .string "palaces, to cut off the children\l"
    .string "from without, and the young men from\l"
    .string "the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_22::
    .string "Speak, Thus saith the LORD, Even\n"
    .string "the carcases of men shall fall as\l"
    .string "dung upon the open field, and as\l"
    .string "the handful after the harvestman,\l"
    .string "and none shall gather them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_23::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Let not the\n"
    .string "wise man glory in his wisdom,\l"
    .string "neither let the mighty man glory in\l"
    .string "his might, let not the rich man\l"
    .string "glory in his riches:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_24::
    .string "But let him that glorieth glory in\n"
    .string "this, that he understandeth and\l"
    .string "knoweth me, that I am the LORD which\l"
    .string "exercise lovingkindness, judgment,\l"
    .string "and righteousness, in the earth: for\l"
    .string "in these things I delight, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_25::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will punish all them\l"
    .string "which are circumcised with the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_9_26::
    .string "Egypt, and Judah, and Edom, and the\n"
    .string "children of Ammon, and Moab, and\l"
    .string "all that are in the utmost corners,\l"
    .string "that dwell in the wilderness: for\l"
    .string "all these nations are\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, and all the house of\l"
    .string "Israel are uncircumcised in the\l"
    .string "heart$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_1::
    .string "Hear ye the word which the LORD\n"
    .string "speaketh unto you, O house of\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Learn not the\n"
    .string "way of the heathen, and be not\l"
    .string "dismayed at the signs of heaven; for\l"
    .string "the heathen are dismayed at them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_3::
    .string "For the customs of the people are\n"
    .string "vain: for one cutteth a tree out of\l"
    .string "the forest, the work of the hands of\l"
    .string "the workman, with the axe.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_4::
    .string "They deck it with silver and with\n"
    .string "gold; they fasten it with nails and\l"
    .string "with hammers, that it move not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_5::
    .string "They are upright as the palm tree,\n"
    .string "but speak not: they must needs be\l"
    .string "borne, because they cannot go. Be not\l"
    .string "afraid of them; for they cannot do\l"
    .string "evil, neither also is it in them to\l"
    .string "do good.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_6::
    .string "Forasmuch as there is none like\n"
    .string "unto thee, O LORD; thou art great, and\l"
    .string "thy name is great in might.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_7::
    .string "Who would not fear thee, O King of\n"
    .string "nations? for to thee doth it\l"
    .string "appertain: forasmuch as among all\l"
    .string "the wise men of the nations, and in\l"
    .string "all their kingdoms, there is none\l"
    .string "like unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_8::
    .string "But they are altogether brutish and\n"
    .string "foolish: the stock is a doctrine of\l"
    .string "vanities.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_9::
    .string "Silver spread into plates is\n"
    .string "brought from Tarshish, and gold from\l"
    .string "Uphaz, the work of the workman, and\l"
    .string "of the hands of the founder: blue and\l"
    .string "purple is their clothing: they are\l"
    .string "all the work of cunning men.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_10::
    .string "But the LORD is the true God, he is\n"
    .string "the living God, and an everlasting\l"
    .string "king: at his wrath the earth shall\l"
    .string "tremble, and the nations shall not\l"
    .string "be able to abide his indignation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_11::
    .string "Thus shall ye say unto them, The\n"
    .string "gods that have not made the heavens\l"
    .string "and the earth, even they shall\l"
    .string "perish from the earth, and from under\l"
    .string "these heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_12::
    .string "He hath made the earth by his power,\n"
    .string "he hath established the world by\l"
    .string "his wisdom, and hath stretched out\l"
    .string "the heavens by his discretion.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_13::
    .string "When he uttereth his voice, there is\n"
    .string "a multitude of waters in the\l"
    .string "heavens, and he causeth the vapours\l"
    .string "to ascend from the ends of the earth;\l"
    .string "he maketh lightnings with rain, and\l"
    .string "bringeth forth the wind out of his\l"
    .string "treasures.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_14::
    .string "Every man is brutish in his\n"
    .string "knowledge: every founder is\l"
    .string "confounded by the graven image: for\l"
    .string "his molten image is falsehood, and\l"
    .string "there is no breath in them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_15::
    .string "They are vanity, and the work of\n"
    .string "errors: in the time of their\l"
    .string "visitation they shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_16::
    .string "The portion of Jacob is not like\n"
    .string "them: for he is the former of all\l"
    .string "things; and Israel is the rod of his\l"
    .string "inheritance: The LORD of hosts is his\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_17::
    .string "Gather up thy wares out of the\n"
    .string "land, O inhabitant of the fortress.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_18::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will sling out the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "the land at this once, and will\l"
    .string "distress them, that they may find it\l"
    .string "so.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_19::
    .string "Woe is me for my hurt! my wound is\n"
    .string "grievous; but I said, Truly this is a\l"
    .string "grief, and I must bear it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_20::
    .string "My tabernacle is spoiled, and\n"
    .string "all my cords are broken: my\l"
    .string "children are gone forth of me, and\l"
    .string "they are not: there is none to\l"
    .string "stretch forth my tent any more, and\l"
    .string "to set up my curtains.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_21::
    .string "For the pastors are become brutish,\n"
    .string "and have not sought the LORD:\l"
    .string "therefore they shall not prosper,\l"
    .string "and all their flocks shall be\l"
    .string "scattered.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_22::
    .string "Behold, the noise of the bruit is\n"
    .string "come, and a great commotion out of\l"
    .string "the north country, to make the cities\l"
    .string "of Judah desolate, and a den of\l"
    .string "dragons.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_23::
    .string "O LORD, I know that the way of man is\n"
    .string "not in himself: it is not in man that\l"
    .string "walketh to direct his steps.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_24::
    .string "O LORD, correct me, but with\n"
    .string "judgment; not in thine anger, lest\l"
    .string "thou bring me to nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_10_25::
    .string "Pour out thy fury upon the heathen\n"
    .string "that know thee not, and upon the\l"
    .string "families that call not on thy name:\l"
    .string "for they have eaten up Jacob, and\l"
    .string "devoured him, and consumed him, and\l"
    .string "have made his habitation desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_2::
    .string "Hear ye the words of this covenant,\n"
    .string "and speak unto the men of Judah, and\l"
    .string "to the inhabitants of Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_3::
    .string "And say thou unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD God of Israel; Cursed be the\l"
    .string "man that obeyeth not the words of\l"
    .string "this covenant,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_4::
    .string "Which I commanded your fathers in\n"
    .string "the day that I brought them forth out\l"
    .string "of the land of Egypt, from the iron\l"
    .string "furnace, saying, Obey my voice, and\l"
    .string "do them, according to all which I\l"
    .string "command you: so shall ye be my\l"
    .string "people, and I will be your God:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_5::
    .string "That I may perform the oath which I\n"
    .string "have sworn unto your fathers, to give\l"
    .string "them a land flowing with milk and\l"
    .string "honey, as it is this day. Then\l"
    .string "answered I, and said, So be it, O LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_6::
    .string "Then the LORD said unto me,\n"
    .string "Proclaim all these words in the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah, and in the streets\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, saying, Hear ye the\l"
    .string "words of this covenant, and do them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_7::
    .string "For I earnestly protested unto\n"
    .string "your fathers in the day that I\l"
    .string "brought them up out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, even unto this day, rising\l"
    .string "early and protesting, saying, Obey\l"
    .string "my voice.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_8::
    .string "Yet they obeyed not, nor inclined\n"
    .string "their ear, but walked every one in\l"
    .string "the imagination of their evil heart:\l"
    .string "therefore I will bring upon them\l"
    .string "all the words of this covenant,\l"
    .string "which I commanded them to do: but\l"
    .string "they did them not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_9::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, A\n"
    .string "conspiracy is found among the men of\l"
    .string "Judah, and among the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_10::
    .string "They are turned back to the\n"
    .string "iniquities of their forefathers,\l"
    .string "which refused to hear my words; and\l"
    .string "they went after other gods to serve\l"
    .string "them: the house of Israel and the\l"
    .string "house of Judah have broken my\l"
    .string "covenant which I made with their\l"
    .string "fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_11::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "Behold, I will bring evil upon\l"
    .string "them, which they shall not be able\l"
    .string "to escape; and though they shall\l"
    .string "cry unto me, I will not hearken unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_12::
    .string "Then shall the cities of Judah and\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem go, and cry\l"
    .string "unto the gods unto whom they offer\l"
    .string "incense: but they shall not save\l"
    .string "them at all in the time of their\l"
    .string "trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_13::
    .string "For according to the number of thy\n"
    .string "cities were thy gods, O Judah; and\l"
    .string "according to the number of the\l"
    .string "streets of Jerusalem have ye set up\l"
    .string "altars to that shameful thing, even\l"
    .string "altars to burn incense unto Baal.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_14::
    .string "Therefore pray not thou for this\n"
    .string "people, neither lift up a cry or\l"
    .string "prayer for them: for I will not hear\l"
    .string "them in the time that they cry unto\l"
    .string "me for their trouble.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_15::
    .string "What hath my beloved to do in mine\n"
    .string "house, seeing she hath wrought\l"
    .string "lewdness with many, and the holy\l"
    .string "flesh is passed from thee? when thou\l"
    .string "doest evil, then thou rejoicest.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_16::
    .string "The LORD called thy name, A green\n"
    .string "olive tree, fair, and of goodly\l"
    .string "fruit: with the noise of a great\l"
    .string "tumult he hath kindled fire upon\l"
    .string "it, and the branches of it are broken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_17::
    .string "For the LORD of hosts, that planted\n"
    .string "thee, hath pronounced evil against\l"
    .string "thee, for the evil of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel and of the house of Judah,\l"
    .string "which they have done against\l"
    .string "themselves to provoke me to anger\l"
    .string "in offering incense unto Baal.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_18::
    .string "And the LORD hath given me\n"
    .string "knowledge of it, and I know it: then\l"
    .string "thou shewedst me their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_19::
    .string "But I was like a lamb or an ox that\n"
    .string "is brought to the slaughter; and I\l"
    .string "knew not that they had devised\l"
    .string "devices against me, saying, Let us\l"
    .string "destroy the tree with the fruit\l"
    .string "thereof, and let us cut him off from\l"
    .string "the land of the living, that his\l"
    .string "name may be no more remembered.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_20::
    .string "But, O LORD of hosts, that judgest\n"
    .string "righteously, that triest the reins\l"
    .string "and the heart, let me see thy\l"
    .string "vengeance on them: for unto thee have\l"
    .string "I revealed my cause.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_21::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of the\n"
    .string "men of Anathoth, that seek thy life,\l"
    .string "saying, Prophesy not in the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD, that thou die not by our\l"
    .string "hand:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_22::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, Behold, I will punish them:\l"
    .string "the young men shall die by the\l"
    .string "sword; their sons and their daughters\l"
    .string "shall die by famine:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_11_23::
    .string "And there shall be no remnant of\n"
    .string "them: for I will bring evil upon\l"
    .string "the men of Anathoth, even the year of\l"
    .string "their visitation$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_1::
    .string "Righteous art thou, O LORD, when I\n"
    .string "plead with thee: yet let me talk\l"
    .string "with thee of thy judgments: Wherefore\l"
    .string "doth the way of the wicked prosper?\l"
    .string "wherefore are all they happy that\l"
    .string "deal very treacherously?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_2::
    .string "Thou hast planted them, yea, they\n"
    .string "have taken root: they grow, yea, they\l"
    .string "bring forth fruit: thou art near in\l"
    .string "their mouth, and far from their reins$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_3::
    .string "But thou, O LORD, knowest me: thou\n"
    .string "hast seen me, and tried mine heart\l"
    .string "toward thee: pull them out like\l"
    .string "sheep for the slaughter, and\l"
    .string "prepare them for the day of\l"
    .string "slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_4::
    .string "How long shall the land mourn,\n"
    .string "and the herbs of every field wither,\l"
    .string "for the wickedness of them that\l"
    .string "dwell therein? the beasts are\l"
    .string "consumed, and the birds; because they\l"
    .string "said, He shall not see our last end.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_5::
    .string "If thou hast run with the footmen,\n"
    .string "and they have wearied thee, then how\l"
    .string "canst thou contend with horses? and\l"
    .string "if in the land of peace, wherein\l"
    .string "thou trustedst, they wearied thee,\l"
    .string "then how wilt thou do in the\l"
    .string "swelling of Jordan?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_6::
    .string "For even thy brethren, and the house\n"
    .string "of thy father, even they have dealt\l"
    .string "treacherously with thee; yea, they\l"
    .string "have called a multitude after thee:\l"
    .string "believe them not, though they speak\l"
    .string "fair words unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_7::
    .string "I have forsaken mine house, I have\n"
    .string "left mine heritage; I have given the\l"
    .string "dearly beloved of my soul into the\l"
    .string "hand of her enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_8::
    .string "Mine heritage is unto me as a lion\n"
    .string "in the forest; it crieth out against\l"
    .string "me: therefore have I hated it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_9::
    .string "Mine heritage is unto me as a\n"
    .string "speckled bird, the birds round\l"
    .string "about are against her; come ye,\l"
    .string "assemble all the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field, come to devour.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_10::
    .string "Many pastors have destroyed my\n"
    .string "vineyard, they have trodden my\l"
    .string "portion under foot, they have made my\l"
    .string "pleasant portion a desolate\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_11::
    .string "They have made it desolate, and\n"
    .string "being desolate it mourneth unto me;\l"
    .string "the whole land is made desolate,\l"
    .string "because no man layeth it to heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_12::
    .string "The spoilers are come upon all\n"
    .string "high places through the\l"
    .string "wilderness: for the sword of the\l"
    .string "LORD shall devour from the one end\l"
    .string "of the land even to the other end of\l"
    .string "the land: no flesh shall have\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_13::
    .string "They have sown wheat, but shall\n"
    .string "reap thorns: they have put\l"
    .string "themselves to pain, but shall not\l"
    .string "profit: and they shall be ashamed of\l"
    .string "your revenues because of the fierce\l"
    .string "anger of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_14::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD against all\n"
    .string "mine evil neighbours, that touch the\l"
    .string "inheritance which I have caused my\l"
    .string "people Israel to inherit; Behold,\l"
    .string "I will pluck them out of their\l"
    .string "land, and pluck out the house of\l"
    .string "Judah from among them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_15::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, after\n"
    .string "that I have plucked them out I\l"
    .string "will return, and have compassion on\l"
    .string "them, and will bring them again,\l"
    .string "every man to his heritage, and every\l"
    .string "man to his land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_16::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if they\n"
    .string "will diligently learn the ways of\l"
    .string "my people, to swear by my name, The\l"
    .string "LORD liveth; as they taught my\l"
    .string "people to swear by Baal; then\l"
    .string "shall they be built in the midst of\l"
    .string "my people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_12_17::
    .string "But if they will not obey, I will\n"
    .string "utterly pluck up and destroy that\l"
    .string "nation, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD unto me, Go and\n"
    .string "get thee a linen girdle, and put it\l"
    .string "upon thy loins, and put it not in\l"
    .string "water.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_2::
    .string "So I got a girdle according to the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD, and put it on my\l"
    .string "loins.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_3::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me the second time, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_4::
    .string "Take the girdle that thou hast got,\n"
    .string "which is upon thy loins, and arise,\l"
    .string "go to Euphrates, and hide it there in\l"
    .string "a hole of the rock$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_5::
    .string "So I went, and hid it by Euphrates,\n"
    .string "as the LORD commanded me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_6::
    .string "And it came to pass after many days,\n"
    .string "that the LORD said unto me, Arise, go\l"
    .string "to Euphrates, and take the girdle\l"
    .string "from thence, which I commanded thee\l"
    .string "to hide there.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_7::
    .string "Then I went to Euphrates, and\n"
    .string "digged, and took the girdle from the\l"
    .string "place where I had hid it: and,\l"
    .string "behold, the girdle was marred, it\l"
    .string "was profitable for nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_8::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_9::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, After this\n"
    .string "manner will I mar the pride of\l"
    .string "Judah, and the great pride of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_10::
    .string "This evil people, which refuse to\n"
    .string "hear my words, which walk in the\l"
    .string "imagination of their heart, and walk\l"
    .string "after other gods, to serve them, and\l"
    .string "to worship them, shall even be as\l"
    .string "this girdle, which is good for\l"
    .string "nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_11::
    .string "For as the girdle cleaveth to the\n"
    .string "loins of a man, so have I caused to\l"
    .string "cleave unto me the whole house of\l"
    .string "Israel and the whole house of Judah,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; that they might be\l"
    .string "unto me for a people, and for a\l"
    .string "name, and for a praise, and for a\l"
    .string "glory: but they would not hear.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_12::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt speak unto\n"
    .string "them this word; Thus saith the LORD\l"
    .string "God of Israel, Every bottle shall\l"
    .string "be filled with wine: and they\l"
    .string "shall say unto thee, Do we not\l"
    .string "certainly know that every bottle\l"
    .string "shall be filled with wine?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_13::
    .string "Then shalt thou say unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, Behold, I will\l"
    .string "fill all the inhabitants of this\l"
    .string "land, even the kings that sit upon\l"
    .string "David’s throne, and the priests, and\l"
    .string "the prophets, and all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, with\l"
    .string "drunkenness$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_14::
    .string "And I will dash them one against\n"
    .string "another, even the fathers and the\l"
    .string "sons together, saith the LORD: I\l"
    .string "will not pity, nor spare, nor have\l"
    .string "mercy, but destroy them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_15::
    .string "Hear ye, and give ear; be not proud:\n"
    .string "for the LORD hath spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_16::
    .string "Give glory to the LORD your God,\n"
    .string "before he cause darkness, and before\l"
    .string "your feet stumble upon the dark\l"
    .string "mountains, and, while ye look for\l"
    .string "light, he turn it into the shadow of\l"
    .string "death, and make it gross darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_17::
    .string "But if ye will not hear it, my soul\n"
    .string "shall weep in secret places for\l"
    .string "your pride; and mine eye shall\l"
    .string "weep sore, and run down with tears,\l"
    .string "because the LORD’s flock is carried\l"
    .string "away captive.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_18::
    .string "Say unto the king and to the queen,\n"
    .string "Humble yourselves, sit down: for\l"
    .string "your principalities shall come\l"
    .string "down, even the crown of your glory.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_19::
    .string "The cities of the south shall be\n"
    .string "shut up, and none shall open them:\l"
    .string "Judah shall be carried away\l"
    .string "captive all of it, it shall be\l"
    .string "wholly carried away captive.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_20::
    .string "Lift up your eyes, and behold them\n"
    .string "that come from the north: where is\l"
    .string "the flock that was given thee, thy\l"
    .string "beautiful flock?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_21::
    .string "What wilt thou say when he shall\n"
    .string "punish thee? for thou hast taught\l"
    .string "them to be captains, and as chief\l"
    .string "over thee: shall not sorrows take\l"
    .string "thee, as a woman in travail?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_22::
    .string "And if thou say in thine heart,\n"
    .string "Wherefore come these things upon me?\l"
    .string "For the greatness of thine iniquity\l"
    .string "are thy skirts discovered, and thy\l"
    .string "heels made bare$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_23::
    .string "Can the Ethiopian change his skin,\n"
    .string "or the leopard his spots? then may\l"
    .string "ye also do good, that are accustomed\l"
    .string "to do evil.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_24::
    .string "Therefore will I scatter them as\n"
    .string "the stubble that passeth away by\l"
    .string "the wind of the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_25::
    .string "This is thy lot, the portion of thy\n"
    .string "measures from me, saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "because thou hast forgotten me, and\l"
    .string "trusted in falsehood.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_26::
    .string "Therefore will I discover thy\n"
    .string "skirts upon thy face, that thy shame\l"
    .string "may appear.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_13_27::
    .string "I have seen thine adulteries, and\n"
    .string "thy neighings, the lewdness of thy\l"
    .string "whoredom, and thine abominations on\l"
    .string "the hills in the fields. Woe unto\l"
    .string "thee, O Jerusalem! wilt thou not be\l"
    .string "made clean? when shall it once be?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah concerning the dearth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_2::
    .string "Judah mourneth, and the gates\n"
    .string "thereof languish; they are black\l"
    .string "unto the ground; and the cry of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem is gone up.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_3::
    .string "And their nobles have sent their\n"
    .string "little ones to the waters: they came\l"
    .string "to the pits, and found no water; they\l"
    .string "returned with their vessels empty;\l"
    .string "they were ashamed and confounded, and\l"
    .string "covered their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_4::
    .string "Because the ground is chapt, for\n"
    .string "there was no rain in the earth, the\l"
    .string "plowmen were ashamed, they covered\l"
    .string "their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_5::
    .string "Yea, the hind also calved in the\n"
    .string "field, and forsook it, because there\l"
    .string "was no grass.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_6::
    .string "And the wild asses did stand in the\n"
    .string "high places, they snuffed up the\l"
    .string "wind like dragons; their eyes did\l"
    .string "fail, because there was no grass.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_7::
    .string "O LORD, though our iniquities\n"
    .string "testify against us, do thou it for\l"
    .string "thy name’s sake: for our\l"
    .string "backslidings are many; we have\l"
    .string "sinned against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_8::
    .string "O the hope of Israel, the saviour\n"
    .string "thereof in time of trouble, why\l"
    .string "shouldest thou be as a stranger in\l"
    .string "the land, and as a wayfaring man that\l"
    .string "turneth aside to tarry for a night?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_9::
    .string "Why shouldest thou be as a man\n"
    .string "astonied, as a mighty man that cannot\l"
    .string "save? yet thou, O LORD, art in the\l"
    .string "midst of us, and we are called by\l"
    .string "thy name; leave us not$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_10::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD unto this\n"
    .string "people, Thus have they loved to\l"
    .string "wander, they have not refrained their\l"
    .string "feet, therefore the LORD doth not\l"
    .string "accept them; he will now remember\l"
    .string "their iniquity, and visit their sins.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_11::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, Pray not\n"
    .string "for this people for their good.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_12::
    .string "When they fast, I will not hear\n"
    .string "their cry; and when they offer burnt\l"
    .string "offering and an oblation, I will\l"
    .string "not accept them: but I will consume\l"
    .string "them by the sword, and by the famine,\l"
    .string "and by the pestilence.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_13::
    .string "Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! behold,\n"
    .string "the prophets say unto them, Ye\l"
    .string "shall not see the sword, neither\l"
    .string "shall ye have famine; but I will\l"
    .string "give you assured peace in this\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_14::
    .string "Then the LORD said unto me, The\n"
    .string "prophets prophesy lies in my name:\l"
    .string "I sent them not, neither have I\l"
    .string "commanded them, neither spake unto\l"
    .string "them: they prophesy unto you a\l"
    .string "false vision and divination, and a\l"
    .string "thing of nought, and the deceit of\l"
    .string "their heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_15::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "concerning the prophets that\l"
    .string "prophesy in my name, and I sent them\l"
    .string "not, yet they say, Sword and famine\l"
    .string "shall not be in this land; By sword\l"
    .string "and famine shall those prophets be\l"
    .string "consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_16::
    .string "And the people to whom they\n"
    .string "prophesy shall be cast out in the\l"
    .string "streets of Jerusalem because of the\l"
    .string "famine and the sword; and they shall\l"
    .string "have none to bury them, them, their\l"
    .string "wives, nor their sons, nor their\l"
    .string "daughters: for I will pour their\l"
    .string "wickedness upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_17::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt say this word\n"
    .string "unto them; Let mine eyes run down\l"
    .string "with tears night and day, and let\l"
    .string "them not cease: for the virgin\l"
    .string "daughter of my people is broken\l"
    .string "with a great breach, with a very\l"
    .string "grievous blow.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_18::
    .string "If I go forth into the field, then\n"
    .string "behold the slain with the sword! and\l"
    .string "if I enter into the city, then behold\l"
    .string "them that are sick with famine! yea,\l"
    .string "both the prophet and the priest go\l"
    .string "about into a land that they know not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_19::
    .string "Hast thou utterly rejected Judah?\n"
    .string "hath thy soul lothed Zion? why hast\l"
    .string "thou smitten us, and there is no\l"
    .string "healing for us? we looked for\l"
    .string "peace, and there is no good; and for\l"
    .string "the time of healing, and behold\l"
    .string "trouble!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_20::
    .string "We acknowledge, O LORD, our\n"
    .string "wickedness, and the iniquity of our\l"
    .string "fathers: for we have sinned against\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_21::
    .string "Do not abhor us, for thy name’s\n"
    .string "sake, do not disgrace the throne of\l"
    .string "thy glory: remember, break not thy\l"
    .string "covenant with us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_14_22::
    .string "Are there any among the vanities of\n"
    .string "the Gentiles that can cause rain? or\l"
    .string "can the heavens give showers? art not\l"
    .string "thou he, O LORD our God? therefore we\l"
    .string "will wait upon thee: for thou hast\l"
    .string "made all these things.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_1::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, Though\n"
    .string "Moses and Samuel stood before me,\l"
    .string "yet my mind could not be toward this\l"
    .string "people: cast them out of my sight,\l"
    .string "and let them go forth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_2::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if they\n"
    .string "say unto thee, Whither shall we go\l"
    .string "forth? then thou shalt tell them,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Such as are for\l"
    .string "death, to death; and such as are for\l"
    .string "the sword, to the sword; and such as\l"
    .string "are for the famine, to the famine;\l"
    .string "and such as are for the captivity, to\l"
    .string "the captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_3::
    .string "And I will appoint over them four\n"
    .string "kinds, saith the LORD: the sword to\l"
    .string "slay, and the dogs to tear, and the\l"
    .string "fowls of the heaven, and the beasts\l"
    .string "of the earth, to devour and destroy.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_4::
    .string "And I will cause them to be removed\n"
    .string "into all kingdoms of the earth,\l"
    .string "because of Manasseh the son of\l"
    .string "Hezekiah king of Judah, for that\l"
    .string "which he did in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_5::
    .string "For who shall have pity upon\n"
    .string "thee, O Jerusalem? or who shall\l"
    .string "bemoan thee? or who shall go aside\l"
    .string "to ask how thou doest?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_6::
    .string "Thou hast forsaken me, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, thou art gone backward:\l"
    .string "therefore will I stretch out my\l"
    .string "hand against thee, and destroy thee;\l"
    .string "I am weary with repenting$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_7::
    .string "And I will fan them with a fan in\n"
    .string "the gates of the land; I will\l"
    .string "bereave them of children, I will\l"
    .string "destroy my people since they\l"
    .string "return not from their ways.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_8::
    .string "Their widows are increased to me\n"
    .string "above the sand of the seas: I have\l"
    .string "brought upon them against the mother\l"
    .string "of the young men a spoiler at\l"
    .string "noonday: I have caused him to fall\l"
    .string "upon it suddenly, and terrors upon\l"
    .string "the city.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_9::
    .string "She that hath borne seven\n"
    .string "languisheth: she hath given up the\l"
    .string "ghost; her sun is gone down while it\l"
    .string "was yet day: she hath been ashamed\l"
    .string "and confounded: and the residue of\l"
    .string "them will I deliver to the sword\l"
    .string "before their enemies, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_10::
    .string "Woe is me, my mother, that thou hast\n"
    .string "borne me a man of strife and a man of\l"
    .string "contention to the whole earth! I\l"
    .string "have neither lent on usury, nor men\l"
    .string "have lent to me on usury; yet every\l"
    .string "one of them doth curse me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_11::
    .string "The LORD said, Verily it shall be\n"
    .string "well with thy remnant; verily I\l"
    .string "will cause the enemy to entreat\l"
    .string "thee well in the time of evil and\l"
    .string "in the time of affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_12::
    .string "Shall iron break the northern iron\n"
    .string "and the steel?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_13::
    .string "Thy substance and thy treasures\n"
    .string "will I give to the spoil without\l"
    .string "price, and that for all thy sins,\l"
    .string "even in all thy borders$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_14::
    .string "And I will make thee to pass with\n"
    .string "thine enemies into a land which thou\l"
    .string "knowest not: for a fire is kindled in\l"
    .string "mine anger, which shall burn upon\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_15::
    .string "O LORD, thou knowest: remember me,\n"
    .string "and visit me, and revenge me of my\l"
    .string "persecutors; take me not away in thy\l"
    .string "longsuffering: know that for thy sake\l"
    .string "I have suffered rebuke.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_16::
    .string "Thy words were found, and I did eat\n"
    .string "them; and thy word was unto me the joy\l"
    .string "and rejoicing of mine heart: for I am\l"
    .string "called by thy name, O LORD God of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_17::
    .string "I sat not in the assembly of the\n"
    .string "mockers, nor rejoiced; I sat alone\l"
    .string "because of thy hand: for thou hast\l"
    .string "filled me with indignation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_18::
    .string "Why is my pain perpetual, and my\n"
    .string "wound incurable, which refuseth to\l"
    .string "be healed? wilt thou be altogether\l"
    .string "unto me as a liar, and as waters that\l"
    .string "fail?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_19::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD, If\n"
    .string "thou return, then will I bring thee\l"
    .string "again, and thou shalt stand before\l"
    .string "me: and if thou take forth the\l"
    .string "precious from the vile, thou shalt\l"
    .string "be as my mouth: let them return unto\l"
    .string "thee; but return not thou unto them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_20::
    .string "And I will make thee unto this\n"
    .string "people a fenced brasen wall: and\l"
    .string "they shall fight against thee, but\l"
    .string "they shall not prevail against\l"
    .string "thee: for I am with thee to save thee\l"
    .string "and to deliver thee, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_15_21::
    .string "And I will deliver thee out of the\n"
    .string "hand of the wicked, and I will\l"
    .string "redeem thee out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "terrible.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came also unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_2::
    .string "Thou shalt not take thee a wife,\n"
    .string "neither shalt thou have sons or\l"
    .string "daughters in this place$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_3::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD concerning\n"
    .string "the sons and concerning the\l"
    .string "daughters that are born in this\l"
    .string "place, and concerning their mothers\l"
    .string "that bare them, and concerning their\l"
    .string "fathers that begat them in this\l"
    .string "land;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_4::
    .string "They shall die of grievous deaths;\n"
    .string "they shall not be lamented; neither\l"
    .string "shall they be buried; but they\l"
    .string "shall be as dung upon the face of\l"
    .string "the earth: and they shall be\l"
    .string "consumed by the sword, and by famine;\l"
    .string "and their carcases shall be meat\l"
    .string "for the fowls of heaven, and for the\l"
    .string "beasts of the earth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_5::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Enter not\n"
    .string "into the house of mourning, neither\l"
    .string "go to lament nor bemoan them: for I\l"
    .string "have taken away my peace from this\l"
    .string "people, saith the LORD, even\l"
    .string "lovingkindness and mercies.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_6::
    .string "Both the great and the small\n"
    .string "shall die in this land: they shall\l"
    .string "not be buried, neither shall men\l"
    .string "lament for them, nor cut themselves,\l"
    .string "nor make themselves bald for them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_7::
    .string "Neither shall men tear themselves\n"
    .string "for them in mourning, to comfort them\l"
    .string "for the dead; neither shall men give\l"
    .string "them the cup of consolation to\l"
    .string "drink for their father or for their\l"
    .string "mother$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_8::
    .string "Thou shalt not also go into the\n"
    .string "house of feasting, to sit with them\l"
    .string "to eat and to drink.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_9::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; Behold, I will\l"
    .string "cause to cease out of this place in\l"
    .string "your eyes, and in your days, the\l"
    .string "voice of mirth, and the voice of\l"
    .string "gladness, the voice of the\l"
    .string "bridegroom, and the voice of the\l"
    .string "bride.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_10::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "thou shalt shew this people all\l"
    .string "these words, and they shall say unto\l"
    .string "thee, Wherefore hath the LORD\l"
    .string "pronounced all this great evil\l"
    .string "against us? or what is our iniquity?\l"
    .string "or what is our sin that we have\l"
    .string "committed against the LORD our God?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_11::
    .string "Then shalt thou say unto them,\n"
    .string "Because your fathers have forsaken\l"
    .string "me, saith the LORD, and have walked\l"
    .string "after other gods, and have served\l"
    .string "them, and have worshipped them, and\l"
    .string "have forsaken me, and have not kept\l"
    .string "my law;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_12::
    .string "And ye have done worse than your\n"
    .string "fathers; for, behold, ye walk every\l"
    .string "one after the imagination of his\l"
    .string "evil heart, that they may not\l"
    .string "hearken unto me:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_13::
    .string "Therefore will I cast you out of\n"
    .string "this land into a land that ye know\l"
    .string "not, neither ye nor your fathers; and\l"
    .string "there shall ye serve other gods day\l"
    .string "and night; where I will not shew you\l"
    .string "favour$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_14::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that it shall no\l"
    .string "more be said, The LORD liveth, that\l"
    .string "brought up the children of Israel\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_15::
    .string "But, The LORD liveth, that brought\n"
    .string "up the children of Israel from the\l"
    .string "land of the north, and from all the\l"
    .string "lands whither he had driven them: and\l"
    .string "I will bring them again into their\l"
    .string "land that I gave unto their fathers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_16::
    .string "Behold, I will send for many\n"
    .string "fishers, saith the LORD, and they\l"
    .string "shall fish them; and after will I\l"
    .string "send for many hunters, and they\l"
    .string "shall hunt them from every\l"
    .string "mountain, and from every hill, and\l"
    .string "out of the holes of the rocks.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_17::
    .string "For mine eyes are upon all their\n"
    .string "ways: they are not hid from my face,\l"
    .string "neither is their iniquity hid from\l"
    .string "mine eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_18::
    .string "And first I will recompense their\n"
    .string "iniquity and their sin double;\l"
    .string "because they have defiled my land,\l"
    .string "they have filled mine inheritance\l"
    .string "with the carcases of their\l"
    .string "detestable and abominable things.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_19::
    .string "O LORD, my strength, and my\n"
    .string "fortress, and my refuge in the day of\l"
    .string "affliction, the Gentiles shall\l"
    .string "come unto thee from the ends of the\l"
    .string "earth, and shall say, Surely our\l"
    .string "fathers have inherited lies, vanity,\l"
    .string "and things wherein there is no\l"
    .string "profit.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_20::
    .string "Shall a man make gods unto\n"
    .string "himself, and they are no gods?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_16_21::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will this\n"
    .string "once cause them to know, I will\l"
    .string "cause them to know mine hand and my\l"
    .string "might; and they shall know that my\l"
    .string "name is The LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_1::
    .string "The sin of Judah is written with a\n"
    .string "pen of iron, and with the point of a\l"
    .string "diamond: it is graven upon the table\l"
    .string "of their heart, and upon the horns of\l"
    .string "your altars;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_2::
    .string "Whilst their children remember\n"
    .string "their altars and their groves by the\l"
    .string "green trees upon the high hills$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_3::
    .string "O my mountain in the field, I will\n"
    .string "give thy substance and all thy\l"
    .string "treasures to the spoil, and thy high\l"
    .string "places for sin, throughout all thy\l"
    .string "borders.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_4::
    .string "And thou, even thyself, shalt\n"
    .string "discontinue from thine heritage that\l"
    .string "I gave thee; and I will cause thee\l"
    .string "to serve thine enemies in the land\l"
    .string "which thou knowest not: for ye have\l"
    .string "kindled a fire in mine anger, which\l"
    .string "shall burn for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_5::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Cursed be the\n"
    .string "man that trusteth in man, and maketh\l"
    .string "flesh his arm, and whose heart\l"
    .string "departeth from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_6::
    .string "For he shall be like the heath in\n"
    .string "the desert, and shall not see when\l"
    .string "good cometh; but shall inhabit the\l"
    .string "parched places in the wilderness,\l"
    .string "in a salt land and not inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_7::
    .string "Blessed is the man that trusteth in\n"
    .string "the LORD, and whose hope the LORD is.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_8::
    .string "For he shall be as a tree planted\n"
    .string "by the waters, and that spreadeth\l"
    .string "out her roots by the river, and\l"
    .string "shall not see when heat cometh, but\l"
    .string "her leaf shall be green; and shall\l"
    .string "not be careful in the year of\l"
    .string "drought, neither shall cease from\l"
    .string "yielding fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_9::
    .string "The heart is deceitful above all\n"
    .string "things, and desperately wicked: who\l"
    .string "can know it?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_10::
    .string "I the LORD search the heart, I try\n"
    .string "the reins, even to give every man\l"
    .string "according to his ways, and according\l"
    .string "to the fruit of his doings$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_11::
    .string "As the partridge sitteth on eggs,\n"
    .string "and hatcheth them not; so he that\l"
    .string "getteth riches, and not by right,\l"
    .string "shall leave them in the midst of\l"
    .string "his days, and at his end shall be a\l"
    .string "fool.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_12::
    .string "A glorious high throne from the\n"
    .string "beginning is the place of our\l"
    .string "sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_13::
    .string "O LORD, the hope of Israel, all\n"
    .string "that forsake thee shall be ashamed,\l"
    .string "and they that depart from me shall\l"
    .string "be written in the earth, because they\l"
    .string "have forsaken the LORD, the fountain\l"
    .string "of living waters.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_14::
    .string "Heal me, O LORD, and I shall be\n"
    .string "healed; save me, and I shall be\l"
    .string "saved: for thou art my praise.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_15::
    .string "Behold, they say unto me, Where is\n"
    .string "the word of the LORD? let it come now.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_16::
    .string "As for me, I have not hastened from\n"
    .string "being a pastor to follow thee:\l"
    .string "neither have I desired the woeful\l"
    .string "day; thou knowest: that which came\l"
    .string "out of my lips was right before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_17::
    .string "Be not a terror unto me: thou art my\n"
    .string "hope in the day of evil.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_18::
    .string "Let them be confounded that\n"
    .string "persecute me, but let not me be\l"
    .string "confounded: let them be dismayed,\l"
    .string "but let not me be dismayed: bring\l"
    .string "upon them the day of evil, and\l"
    .string "destroy them with double\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_19::
    .string "Thus said the LORD unto me; Go and\n"
    .string "stand in the gate of the children of\l"
    .string "the people, whereby the kings of\l"
    .string "Judah come in, and by the which they\l"
    .string "go out, and in all the gates of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_20::
    .string "And say unto them, Hear ye the word\n"
    .string "of the LORD, ye kings of Judah, and\l"
    .string "all Judah, and all the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, that enter in by these\l"
    .string "gates:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_21::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Take heed to\n"
    .string "yourselves, and bear no burden on\l"
    .string "the sabbath day, nor bring it in by\l"
    .string "the gates of Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_22::
    .string "Neither carry forth a burden out of\n"
    .string "your houses on the sabbath day,\l"
    .string "neither do ye any work, but hallow\l"
    .string "ye the sabbath day, as I commanded\l"
    .string "your fathers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_23::
    .string "But they obeyed not, neither\n"
    .string "inclined their ear, but made their\l"
    .string "neck stiff, that they might not hear,\l"
    .string "nor receive instruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_24::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if ye\n"
    .string "diligently hearken unto me, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD, to bring in no burden\l"
    .string "through the gates of this city on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day, but hallow the sabbath\l"
    .string "day, to do no work therein;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_25::
    .string "Then shall there enter into the\n"
    .string "gates of this city kings and princes\l"
    .string "sitting upon the throne of David,\l"
    .string "riding in chariots and on horses,\l"
    .string "they, and their princes, the men of\l"
    .string "Judah, and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: and this city shall\l"
    .string "remain for ever$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_26::
    .string "And they shall come from the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah, and from the places\l"
    .string "about Jerusalem, and from the land\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, and from the plain, and\l"
    .string "from the mountains, and from the\l"
    .string "south, bringing burnt offerings, and\l"
    .string "sacrifices, and meat offerings, and\l"
    .string "incense, and bringing sacrifices of\l"
    .string "praise, unto the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_17_27::
    .string "But if ye will not hearken unto me\n"
    .string "to hallow the sabbath day, and not\l"
    .string "to bear a burden, even entering in at\l"
    .string "the gates of Jerusalem on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day; then will I kindle a\l"
    .string "fire in the gates thereof, and it\l"
    .string "shall devour the palaces of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and it shall not be\l"
    .string "quenched.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_1::
    .string "The word which came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_2::
    .string "Arise, and go down to the potter’s\n"
    .string "house, and there I will cause thee\l"
    .string "to hear my words$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_3::
    .string "Then I went down to the potter’s\n"
    .string "house, and, behold, he wrought a work\l"
    .string "on the wheels.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_4::
    .string "And the vessel that he made of clay\n"
    .string "was marred in the hand of the potter:\l"
    .string "so he made it again another vessel,\l"
    .string "as seemed good to the potter to make\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_5::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came to me,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_6::
    .string "O house of Israel, cannot I do with\n"
    .string "you as this potter? saith the LORD.\l"
    .string "Behold, as the clay is in the\l"
    .string "potter’s hand, so are ye in mine\l"
    .string "hand, O house of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_7::
    .string "At what instant I shall speak\n"
    .string "concerning a nation, and concerning a\l"
    .string "kingdom, to pluck up, and to pull\l"
    .string "down, and to destroy it;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_8::
    .string "If that nation, against whom I have\n"
    .string "pronounced, turn from their evil, I\l"
    .string "will repent of the evil that I\l"
    .string "thought to do unto them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_9::
    .string "And at what instant I shall speak\n"
    .string "concerning a nation, and concerning a\l"
    .string "kingdom, to build and to plant it;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_10::
    .string "If it do evil in my sight, that it\n"
    .string "obey not my voice, then I will\l"
    .string "repent of the good, wherewith I said\l"
    .string "I would benefit them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_11::
    .string "Now therefore go to, speak to the\n"
    .string "men of Judah, and to the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, saying, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD; Behold, I frame evil against\l"
    .string "you, and devise a device against you:\l"
    .string "return ye now every one from his\l"
    .string "evil way, and make your ways and your\l"
    .string "doings good.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_12::
    .string "And they said, There is no hope: but\n"
    .string "we will walk after our own devices,\l"
    .string "and we will every one do the\l"
    .string "imagination of his evil heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_13::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD; Ask\n"
    .string "ye now among the heathen, who hath\l"
    .string "heard such things: the virgin of\l"
    .string "Israel hath done a very horrible\l"
    .string "thing.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_14::
    .string "Will a man leave the snow of\n"
    .string "Lebanon which cometh from the rock of\l"
    .string "the field? or shall the cold\l"
    .string "flowing waters that come from\l"
    .string "another place be forsaken?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_15::
    .string "Because my people hath forgotten\n"
    .string "me, they have burned incense to\l"
    .string "vanity, and they have caused them to\l"
    .string "stumble in their ways from the\l"
    .string "ancient paths, to walk in paths, in\l"
    .string "a way not cast up;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_16::
    .string "To make their land desolate, and a\n"
    .string "perpetual hissing; every one that\l"
    .string "passeth thereby shall be\l"
    .string "astonished, and wag his head$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_17::
    .string "I will scatter them as with an east\n"
    .string "wind before the enemy; I will shew\l"
    .string "them the back, and not the face, in\l"
    .string "the day of their calamity.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_18::
    .string "Then said they, Come and let us\n"
    .string "devise devices against Jeremiah; for\l"
    .string "the law shall not perish from the\l"
    .string "priest, nor counsel from the wise,\l"
    .string "nor the word from the prophet. Come,\l"
    .string "and let us smite him with the tongue,\l"
    .string "and let us not give heed to any of\l"
    .string "his words.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_19::
    .string "Give heed to me, O LORD, and hearken\n"
    .string "to the voice of them that contend\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_20::
    .string "Shall evil be recompensed for\n"
    .string "good? for they have digged a pit for\l"
    .string "my soul. Remember that I stood\l"
    .string "before thee to speak good for them,\l"
    .string "and to turn away thy wrath from them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_21::
    .string "Therefore deliver up their\n"
    .string "children to the famine, and pour out\l"
    .string "their blood by the force of the\l"
    .string "sword; and let their wives be\l"
    .string "bereaved of their children, and be\l"
    .string "widows; and let their men be put to\l"
    .string "death; let their young men be slain\l"
    .string "by the sword in battle.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_22::
    .string "Let a cry be heard from their\n"
    .string "houses, when thou shalt bring a\l"
    .string "troop suddenly upon them: for they\l"
    .string "have digged a pit to take me, and hid\l"
    .string "snares for my feet.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_18_23::
    .string "Yet, LORD, thou knowest all their\n"
    .string "counsel against me to slay me:\l"
    .string "forgive not their iniquity, neither\l"
    .string "blot out their sin from thy sight,\l"
    .string "but let them be overthrown before\l"
    .string "thee; deal thus with them in the time\l"
    .string "of thine anger.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Go and get a\n"
    .string "potter’s earthen bottle, and take of\l"
    .string "the ancients of the people, and of\l"
    .string "the ancients of the priests;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_2::
    .string "And go forth unto the valley of the\n"
    .string "son of Hinnom, which is by the entry\l"
    .string "of the east gate, and proclaim there\l"
    .string "the words that I shall tell thee,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_3::
    .string "And say, Hear ye the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD, O kings of Judah, and\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem; Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel;\l"
    .string "Behold, I will bring evil upon\l"
    .string "this place, the which whosoever\l"
    .string "heareth, his ears shall tingle$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_4::
    .string "Because they have forsaken me, and\n"
    .string "have estranged this place, and have\l"
    .string "burned incense in it unto other gods,\l"
    .string "whom neither they nor their fathers\l"
    .string "have known, nor the kings of Judah,\l"
    .string "and have filled this place with\l"
    .string "the blood of innocents;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_5::
    .string "They have built also the high\n"
    .string "places of Baal, to burn their sons\l"
    .string "with fire for burnt offerings unto\l"
    .string "Baal, which I commanded not, nor\l"
    .string "spake it, neither came it into my\l"
    .string "mind:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_6::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that this place\l"
    .string "shall no more be called Tophet,\l"
    .string "nor The valley of the son of Hinnom,\l"
    .string "but The valley of slaughter$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_7::
    .string "And I will make void the counsel\n"
    .string "of Judah and Jerusalem in this\l"
    .string "place; and I will cause them to\l"
    .string "fall by the sword before their\l"
    .string "enemies, and by the hands of them\l"
    .string "that seek their lives: and their\l"
    .string "carcases will I give to be meat for\l"
    .string "the fowls of the heaven, and for the\l"
    .string "beasts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_8::
    .string "And I will make this city\n"
    .string "desolate, and an hissing; every one\l"
    .string "that passeth thereby shall be\l"
    .string "astonished and hiss because of all\l"
    .string "the plagues thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_9::
    .string "And I will cause them to eat the\n"
    .string "flesh of their sons and the flesh of\l"
    .string "their daughters, and they shall eat\l"
    .string "every one the flesh of his friend in\l"
    .string "the siege and straitness, wherewith\l"
    .string "their enemies, and they that seek\l"
    .string "their lives, shall straiten them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_10::
    .string "Then shalt thou break the bottle\n"
    .string "in the sight of the men that go with\l"
    .string "thee,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_11::
    .string "And shalt say unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the LORD of hosts; Even so will I\l"
    .string "break this people and this city, as\l"
    .string "one breaketh a potter’s vessel,\l"
    .string "that cannot be made whole again: and\l"
    .string "they shall bury them in Tophet,\l"
    .string "till there be no place to bury$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_12::
    .string "Thus will I do unto this place,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, and to the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof, and even make\l"
    .string "this city as Tophet:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_13::
    .string "And the houses of Jerusalem, and\n"
    .string "the houses of the kings of Judah,\l"
    .string "shall be defiled as the place of\l"
    .string "Tophet, because of all the houses\l"
    .string "upon whose roofs they have burned\l"
    .string "incense unto all the host of heaven,\l"
    .string "and have poured out drink offerings\l"
    .string "unto other gods$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_14::
    .string "Then came Jeremiah from Tophet,\n"
    .string "whither the LORD had sent him to\l"
    .string "prophesy; and he stood in the court\l"
    .string "of the LORD’s house; and said to all\l"
    .string "the people,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_19_15::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; Behold, I will\l"
    .string "bring upon this city and upon all\l"
    .string "her towns all the evil that I have\l"
    .string "pronounced against it, because they\l"
    .string "have hardened their necks, that they\l"
    .string "might not hear my words$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_1::
    .string "Now Pashur the son of Immer the\n"
    .string "priest, who was also chief governor\l"
    .string "in the house of the LORD, heard that\l"
    .string "Jeremiah prophesied these things.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_2::
    .string "Then Pashur smote Jeremiah the\n"
    .string "prophet, and put him in the stocks\l"
    .string "that were in the high gate of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, which was by the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_3::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that Pashur brought forth Jeremiah\l"
    .string "out of the stocks. Then said Jeremiah\l"
    .string "unto him, The LORD hath not called\l"
    .string "thy name Pashur, but Magormissabib.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_4::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I\n"
    .string "will make thee a terror to thyself,\l"
    .string "and to all thy friends: and they\l"
    .string "shall fall by the sword of their\l"
    .string "enemies, and thine eyes shall\l"
    .string "behold it: and I will give all\l"
    .string "Judah into the hand of the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and he shall carry them\l"
    .string "captive into Babylon, and shall\l"
    .string "slay them with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_5::
    .string "Moreover I will deliver all the\n"
    .string "strength of this city, and all the\l"
    .string "labours thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "precious things thereof, and all\l"
    .string "the treasures of the kings of Judah\l"
    .string "will I give into the hand of their\l"
    .string "enemies, which shall spoil them,\l"
    .string "and take them, and carry them to\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_6::
    .string "And thou, Pashur, and all that\n"
    .string "dwell in thine house shall go into\l"
    .string "captivity: and thou shalt come to\l"
    .string "Babylon, and there thou shalt die,\l"
    .string "and shalt be buried there, thou, and\l"
    .string "all thy friends, to whom thou hast\l"
    .string "prophesied lies.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_7::
    .string "O LORD, thou hast deceived me, and I\n"
    .string "was deceived; thou art stronger than\l"
    .string "I, and hast prevailed: I am in\l"
    .string "derision daily, every one mocketh me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_8::
    .string "For since I spake, I cried out, I\n"
    .string "cried violence and spoil; because\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD was made a\l"
    .string "reproach unto me, and a derision,\l"
    .string "daily.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_9::
    .string "Then I said, I will not make\n"
    .string "mention of him, nor speak any more in\l"
    .string "his name. But his word was in mine\l"
    .string "heart as a burning fire shut up in my\l"
    .string "bones, and I was weary with\l"
    .string "forbearing, and I could not stay.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_10::
    .string "For I heard the defaming of many,\n"
    .string "fear on every side. Report, say they,\l"
    .string "and we will report it. All my\l"
    .string "familiars watched for my halting,\l"
    .string "saying, Peradventure he will be\l"
    .string "enticed, and we shall prevail\l"
    .string "against him, and we shall take our\l"
    .string "revenge on him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_11::
    .string "But the LORD is with me as a mighty\n"
    .string "terrible one: therefore my\l"
    .string "persecutors shall stumble, and\l"
    .string "they shall not prevail: they\l"
    .string "shall be greatly ashamed; for they\l"
    .string "shall not prosper: their\l"
    .string "everlasting confusion shall never\l"
    .string "be forgotten.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_12::
    .string "But, O LORD of hosts, that triest\n"
    .string "the righteous, and seest the reins\l"
    .string "and the heart, let me see thy\l"
    .string "vengeance on them: for unto thee have\l"
    .string "I opened my cause.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_13::
    .string "Sing unto the LORD, praise ye the\n"
    .string "LORD: for he hath delivered the soul\l"
    .string "of the poor from the hand of\l"
    .string "evildoers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_14::
    .string "Cursed be the day wherein I was\n"
    .string "born: let not the day wherein my\l"
    .string "mother bare me be blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_15::
    .string "Cursed be the man who brought\n"
    .string "tidings to my father, saying, A man\l"
    .string "child is born unto thee; making him\l"
    .string "very glad.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_16::
    .string "And let that man be as the cities\n"
    .string "which the LORD overthrew, and\l"
    .string "repented not: and let him hear the\l"
    .string "cry in the morning, and the shouting\l"
    .string "at noontide;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_17::
    .string "Because he slew me not from the\n"
    .string "womb; or that my mother might have\l"
    .string "been my grave, and her womb to be\l"
    .string "always great with me$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_20_18::
    .string "Wherefore came I forth out of the\n"
    .string "womb to see labour and sorrow, that\l"
    .string "my days should be consumed with\l"
    .string "shame?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_1::
    .string "The word which came unto Jeremiah\n"
    .string "from the LORD, when king Zedekiah\l"
    .string "sent unto him Pashur the son of\l"
    .string "Melchiah, and Zephaniah the son of\l"
    .string "Maaseiah the priest, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_2::
    .string "Enquire, I pray thee, of the LORD\n"
    .string "for us; for Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon maketh war against us; if so\l"
    .string "be that the LORD will deal with us\l"
    .string "according to all his wondrous\l"
    .string "works, that he may go up from us$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_3::
    .string "Then said Jeremiah unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "shall ye say to Zedekiah:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD God of Israel;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will turn back the\l"
    .string "weapons of war that are in your\l"
    .string "hands, wherewith ye fight against the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon, and against the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans, which besiege you without\l"
    .string "the walls, and I will assemble\l"
    .string "them into the midst of this city$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_5::
    .string "And I myself will fight against\n"
    .string "you with an outstretched hand and\l"
    .string "with a strong arm, even in anger, and\l"
    .string "in fury, and in great wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_6::
    .string "And I will smite the inhabitants\n"
    .string "of this city, both man and beast:\l"
    .string "they shall die of a great\l"
    .string "pestilence.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_7::
    .string "And afterward, saith the LORD, I\n"
    .string "will deliver Zedekiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah, and his servants, and the\l"
    .string "people, and such as are left in\l"
    .string "this city from the pestilence, from\l"
    .string "the sword, and from the famine, into\l"
    .string "the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and into the hand of their\l"
    .string "enemies, and into the hand of those\l"
    .string "that seek their life: and he shall\l"
    .string "smite them with the edge of the\l"
    .string "sword; he shall not spare them,\l"
    .string "neither have pity, nor have mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_8::
    .string "And unto this people thou shalt\n"
    .string "say, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I\l"
    .string "set before you the way of life, and\l"
    .string "the way of death.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_9::
    .string "He that abideth in this city shall\n"
    .string "die by the sword, and by the famine,\l"
    .string "and by the pestilence: but he that\l"
    .string "goeth out, and falleth to the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans that besiege you, he\l"
    .string "shall live, and his life shall be\l"
    .string "unto him for a prey.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_10::
    .string "For I have set my face against this\n"
    .string "city for evil, and not for good,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD: it shall be given\l"
    .string "into the hand of the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "and he shall burn it with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_11::
    .string "And touching the house of the king\n"
    .string "of Judah, say, Hear ye the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_12::
    .string "O house of David, thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD; Execute judgment in the\l"
    .string "morning, and deliver him that is\l"
    .string "spoiled out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "oppressor, lest my fury go out\l"
    .string "like fire, and burn that none can\l"
    .string "quench it, because of the evil of\l"
    .string "your doings$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_13::
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O\n"
    .string "inhabitant of the valley, and rock\l"
    .string "of the plain, saith the LORD; which\l"
    .string "say, Who shall come down against us?\l"
    .string "or who shall enter into our\l"
    .string "habitations?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_21_14::
    .string "But I will punish you according to\n"
    .string "the fruit of your doings, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD: and I will kindle a fire in\l"
    .string "the forest thereof, and it shall\l"
    .string "devour all things round about it$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Go down to the\n"
    .string "house of the king of Judah, and speak\l"
    .string "there this word,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_2::
    .string "And say, Hear the word of the LORD, O\n"
    .string "king of Judah, that sittest upon the\l"
    .string "throne of David, thou, and thy\l"
    .string "servants, and thy people that enter\l"
    .string "in by these gates:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_3::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Execute ye\n"
    .string "judgment and righteousness, and\l"
    .string "deliver the spoiled out of the hand\l"
    .string "of the oppressor: and do no wrong,\l"
    .string "do no violence to the stranger, the\l"
    .string "fatherless, nor the widow, neither\l"
    .string "shed innocent blood in this place$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_4::
    .string "For if ye do this thing indeed, then\n"
    .string "shall there enter in by the gates of\l"
    .string "this house kings sitting upon the\l"
    .string "throne of David, riding in chariots\l"
    .string "and on horses, he, and his servants,\l"
    .string "and his people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_5::
    .string "But if ye will not hear these\n"
    .string "words, I swear by myself, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, that this house shall become a\l"
    .string "desolation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_6::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD unto the\n"
    .string "king’s house of Judah; Thou art\l"
    .string "Gilead unto me, and the head of\l"
    .string "Lebanon: yet surely I will make\l"
    .string "thee a wilderness, and cities which\l"
    .string "are not inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_7::
    .string "And I will prepare destroyers\n"
    .string "against thee, every one with his\l"
    .string "weapons: and they shall cut down\l"
    .string "thy choice cedars, and cast them into\l"
    .string "the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_8::
    .string "And many nations shall pass by\n"
    .string "this city, and they shall say every\l"
    .string "man to his neighbour, Wherefore hath\l"
    .string "the LORD done thus unto this great\l"
    .string "city?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_9::
    .string "Then they shall answer, Because\n"
    .string "they have forsaken the covenant of\l"
    .string "the LORD their God, and worshipped\l"
    .string "other gods, and served them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_10::
    .string "Weep ye not for the dead, neither\n"
    .string "bemoan him: but weep sore for him\l"
    .string "that goeth away: for he shall return\l"
    .string "no more, nor see his native country.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_11::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD touching\n"
    .string "Shallum the son of Josiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah, which reigned instead of\l"
    .string "Josiah his father, which went forth\l"
    .string "out of this place; He shall not\l"
    .string "return thither any more:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_12::
    .string "But he shall die in the place\n"
    .string "whither they have led him captive,\l"
    .string "and shall see this land no more$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_13::
    .string "Woe unto him that buildeth his\n"
    .string "house by unrighteousness, and his\l"
    .string "chambers by wrong; that useth his\l"
    .string "neighbour’s service without wages,\l"
    .string "and giveth him not for his work;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_14::
    .string "That saith, I will build me a wide\n"
    .string "house and large chambers, and\l"
    .string "cutteth him out windows; and it is\l"
    .string "cieled with cedar, and painted with\l"
    .string "vermilion$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_15::
    .string "Shalt thou reign, because thou\n"
    .string "closest thyself in cedar? did not\l"
    .string "thy father eat and drink, and do\l"
    .string "judgment and justice, and then it was\l"
    .string "well with him?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_16::
    .string "He judged the cause of the poor and\n"
    .string "needy; then it was well with him:\l"
    .string "was not this to know me? saith the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_17::
    .string "But thine eyes and thine heart are\n"
    .string "not but for thy covetousness, and for\l"
    .string "to shed innocent blood, and for\l"
    .string "oppression, and for violence, to do\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_18::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "concerning Jehoiakim the son of\l"
    .string "Josiah king of Judah; They shall not\l"
    .string "lament for him, saying, Ah my\l"
    .string "brother! or, Ah sister! they shall\l"
    .string "not lament for him, saying, Ah lord!\l"
    .string "or, Ah his glory!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_19::
    .string "He shall be buried with the burial\n"
    .string "of an ass, drawn and cast forth\l"
    .string "beyond the gates of Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_20::
    .string "Go up to Lebanon, and cry; and lift\n"
    .string "up thy voice in Bashan, and cry from\l"
    .string "the passages: for all thy lovers\l"
    .string "are destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_21::
    .string "I spake unto thee in thy\n"
    .string "prosperity; but thou saidst, I will\l"
    .string "not hear. This hath been thy manner\l"
    .string "from thy youth, that thou obeyedst\l"
    .string "not my voice.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_22::
    .string "The wind shall eat up all thy\n"
    .string "pastors, and thy lovers shall go\l"
    .string "into captivity: surely then shalt\l"
    .string "thou be ashamed and confounded for\l"
    .string "all thy wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_23::
    .string "O inhabitant of Lebanon, that makest\n"
    .string "thy nest in the cedars, how gracious\l"
    .string "shalt thou be when pangs come upon\l"
    .string "thee, the pain as of a woman in\l"
    .string "travail!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_24::
    .string "As I live, saith the LORD, though\n"
    .string "Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of\l"
    .string "Judah were the signet upon my right\l"
    .string "hand, yet would I pluck thee\l"
    .string "thence;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_25::
    .string "And I will give thee into the hand\n"
    .string "of them that seek thy life, and into\l"
    .string "the hand of them whose face thou\l"
    .string "fearest, even into the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and\l"
    .string "into the hand of the Chaldeans$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_26::
    .string "And I will cast thee out, and thy\n"
    .string "mother that bare thee, into another\l"
    .string "country, where ye were not born; and\l"
    .string "there shall ye die.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_27::
    .string "But to the land whereunto they\n"
    .string "desire to return, thither shall\l"
    .string "they not return.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_28::
    .string "Is this man Coniah a despised\n"
    .string "broken idol? is he a vessel wherein\l"
    .string "is no pleasure? wherefore are they\l"
    .string "cast out, he and his seed, and are\l"
    .string "cast into a land which they know not?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_29::
    .string "O earth, earth, earth, hear the word\n"
    .string "of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_22_30::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, Write ye this\n"
    .string "man childless, a man that shall\l"
    .string "not prosper in his days: for no man\l"
    .string "of his seed shall prosper, sitting\l"
    .string "upon the throne of David, and ruling\l"
    .string "any more in Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_1::
    .string "Woe be unto the pastors that\n"
    .string "destroy and scatter the sheep of my\l"
    .string "pasture! saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_2::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel against the pastors that\l"
    .string "feed my people; Ye have scattered\l"
    .string "my flock, and driven them away, and\l"
    .string "have not visited them: behold, I\l"
    .string "will visit upon you the evil of\l"
    .string "your doings, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_3::
    .string "And I will gather the remnant of my\n"
    .string "flock out of all countries whither\l"
    .string "I have driven them, and will bring\l"
    .string "them again to their folds; and they\l"
    .string "shall be fruitful and increase.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_4::
    .string "And I will set up shepherds over\n"
    .string "them which shall feed them: and they\l"
    .string "shall fear no more, nor be dismayed,\l"
    .string "neither shall they be lacking,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_5::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will raise unto David a\l"
    .string "righteous Branch, and a King shall\l"
    .string "reign and prosper, and shall\l"
    .string "execute judgment and justice in the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_6::
    .string "In his days Judah shall be saved,\n"
    .string "and Israel shall dwell safely:\l"
    .string "and this is his name whereby he\l"
    .string "shall be called, THE LORD OUR\l"
    .string "RIGHTEOUSNESS.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_7::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that they shall no\l"
    .string "more say, The LORD liveth, which\l"
    .string "brought up the children of Israel\l"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_8::
    .string "But, The LORD liveth, which brought\n"
    .string "up and which led the seed of the\l"
    .string "house of Israel out of the north\l"
    .string "country, and from all countries\l"
    .string "whither I had driven them; and they\l"
    .string "shall dwell in their own land$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_9::
    .string "Mine heart within me is broken\n"
    .string "because of the prophets; all my\l"
    .string "bones shake; I am like a drunken man,\l"
    .string "and like a man whom wine hath\l"
    .string "overcome, because of the LORD, and\l"
    .string "because of the words of his holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_10::
    .string "For the land is full of\n"
    .string "adulterers; for because of swearing\l"
    .string "the land mourneth; the pleasant\l"
    .string "places of the wilderness are dried\l"
    .string "up, and their course is evil, and\l"
    .string "their force is not right.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_11::
    .string "For both prophet and priest are\n"
    .string "profane; yea, in my house have I\l"
    .string "found their wickedness, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_12::
    .string "Wherefore their way shall be unto\n"
    .string "them as slippery ways in the\l"
    .string "darkness: they shall be driven on,\l"
    .string "and fall therein: for I will bring\l"
    .string "evil upon them, even the year of\l"
    .string "their visitation, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_13::
    .string "And I have seen folly in the\n"
    .string "prophets of Samaria; they\l"
    .string "prophesied in Baal, and caused my\l"
    .string "people Israel to err.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_14::
    .string "I have seen also in the prophets\n"
    .string "of Jerusalem an horrible thing:\l"
    .string "they commit adultery, and walk in\l"
    .string "lies: they strengthen also the hands\l"
    .string "of evildoers, that none doth return\l"
    .string "from his wickedness; they are all of\l"
    .string "them unto me as Sodom, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants thereof as Gomorrah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_15::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts concerning the prophets;\l"
    .string "Behold, I will feed them with\l"
    .string "wormwood, and make them drink the\l"
    .string "water of gall: for from the\l"
    .string "prophets of Jerusalem is\l"
    .string "profaneness gone forth into all the\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_16::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "Hearken not unto the words of the\l"
    .string "prophets that prophesy unto you:\l"
    .string "they make you vain: they speak a\l"
    .string "vision of their own heart, and not\l"
    .string "out of the mouth of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_17::
    .string "They say still unto them that\n"
    .string "despise me, The LORD hath said, Ye\l"
    .string "shall have peace; and they say unto\l"
    .string "every one that walketh after the\l"
    .string "imagination of his own heart, No\l"
    .string "evil shall come upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_18::
    .string "For who hath stood in the counsel\n"
    .string "of the LORD, and hath perceived and\l"
    .string "heard his word? who hath marked his\l"
    .string "word, and heard it?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_19::
    .string "Behold, a whirlwind of the LORD is\n"
    .string "gone forth in fury, even a grievous\l"
    .string "whirlwind: it shall fall\l"
    .string "grievously upon the head of the\l"
    .string "wicked$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_20::
    .string "The anger of the LORD shall not\n"
    .string "return, until he have executed, and\l"
    .string "till he have performed the\l"
    .string "thoughts of his heart: in the latter\l"
    .string "days ye shall consider it\l"
    .string "perfectly.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_21::
    .string "I have not sent these prophets, yet\n"
    .string "they ran: I have not spoken to them,\l"
    .string "yet they prophesied.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_22::
    .string "But if they had stood in my counsel,\n"
    .string "and had caused my people to hear my\l"
    .string "words, then they should have turned\l"
    .string "them from their evil way, and from\l"
    .string "the evil of their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_23::
    .string "Am I a God at hand, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "and not a God afar off?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_24::
    .string "Can any hide himself in secret\n"
    .string "places that I shall not see him?\l"
    .string "saith the LORD. Do not I fill heaven\l"
    .string "and earth? saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_25::
    .string "I have heard what the prophets\n"
    .string "said, that prophesy lies in my\l"
    .string "name, saying, I have dreamed, I have\l"
    .string "dreamed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_26::
    .string "How long shall this be in the\n"
    .string "heart of the prophets that\l"
    .string "prophesy lies? yea, they are\l"
    .string "prophets of the deceit of their own\l"
    .string "heart;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_27::
    .string "Which think to cause my people to\n"
    .string "forget my name by their dreams which\l"
    .string "they tell every man to his\l"
    .string "neighbour, as their fathers have\l"
    .string "forgotten my name for Baal$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_28::
    .string "The prophet that hath a dream, let\n"
    .string "him tell a dream; and he that hath\l"
    .string "my word, let him speak my word\l"
    .string "faithfully. What is the chaff to the\l"
    .string "wheat? saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_29::
    .string "Is not my word like as a fire? saith\n"
    .string "the LORD; and like a hammer that\l"
    .string "breaketh the rock in pieces?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_30::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I am against the\n"
    .string "prophets, saith the LORD, that\l"
    .string "steal my words every one from his\l"
    .string "neighbour$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_31::
    .string "Behold, I am against the prophets,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that use their\l"
    .string "tongues, and say, He saith.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_32::
    .string "Behold, I am against them that\n"
    .string "prophesy false dreams, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, and do tell them, and cause my\l"
    .string "people to err by their lies, and by\l"
    .string "their lightness; yet I sent them\l"
    .string "not, nor commanded them: therefore\l"
    .string "they shall not profit this\l"
    .string "people at all, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_33::
    .string "And when this people, or the\n"
    .string "prophet, or a priest, shall ask\l"
    .string "thee, saying, What is the burden of\l"
    .string "the LORD? thou shalt then say unto\l"
    .string "them, What burden? I will even\l"
    .string "forsake you, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_34::
    .string "And as for the prophet, and the\n"
    .string "priest, and the people, that\l"
    .string "shall say, The burden of the LORD, I\l"
    .string "will even punish that man and his\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_35::
    .string "Thus shall ye say every one to his\n"
    .string "neighbour, and every one to his\l"
    .string "brother, What hath the LORD answered?\l"
    .string "and, What hath the LORD spoken?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_36::
    .string "And the burden of the LORD shall ye\n"
    .string "mention no more: for every man’s word\l"
    .string "shall be his burden; for ye have\l"
    .string "perverted the words of the living\l"
    .string "God, of the LORD of hosts our God$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_37::
    .string "Thus shalt thou say to the\n"
    .string "prophet, What hath the LORD answered\l"
    .string "thee? and, What hath the LORD spoken?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_38::
    .string "But since ye say, The burden of the\n"
    .string "LORD; therefore thus saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "Because ye say this word, The burden\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and I have sent unto you,\l"
    .string "saying, Ye shall not say, The burden\l"
    .string "of the LORD;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_39::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I, even I, will\n"
    .string "utterly forget you, and I will\l"
    .string "forsake you, and the city that I gave\l"
    .string "you and your fathers, and cast you\l"
    .string "out of my presence:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_23_40::
    .string "And I will bring an everlasting\n"
    .string "reproach upon you, and a\l"
    .string "perpetual shame, which shall not\l"
    .string "be forgotten$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_1::
    .string "The LORD shewed me, and, behold, two\n"
    .string "baskets of figs were set before the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD, after that\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon had\l"
    .string "carried away captive Jeconiah the\l"
    .string "son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, and\l"
    .string "the princes of Judah, with the\l"
    .string "carpenters and smiths, from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and had brought them to\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_2::
    .string "One basket had very good figs, even\n"
    .string "like the figs that are first ripe:\l"
    .string "and the other basket had very naughty\l"
    .string "figs, which could not be eaten, they\l"
    .string "were so bad.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_3::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, What\n"
    .string "seest thou, Jeremiah? And I said,\l"
    .string "Figs; the good figs, very good; and\l"
    .string "the evil, very evil, that cannot be\l"
    .string "eaten, they are so evil.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_4::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_5::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel; Like these good figs, so\l"
    .string "will I acknowledge them that are\l"
    .string "carried away captive of Judah, whom\l"
    .string "I have sent out of this place into\l"
    .string "the land of the Chaldeans for their\l"
    .string "good$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_6::
    .string "For I will set mine eyes upon them\n"
    .string "for good, and I will bring them\l"
    .string "again to this land: and I will\l"
    .string "build them, and not pull them\l"
    .string "down; and I will plant them, and\l"
    .string "not pluck them up.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_7::
    .string "And I will give them an heart to\n"
    .string "know me, that I am the LORD: and they\l"
    .string "shall be my people, and I will be\l"
    .string "their God: for they shall return\l"
    .string "unto me with their whole heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_8::
    .string "And as the evil figs, which cannot\n"
    .string "be eaten, they are so evil; surely\l"
    .string "thus saith the LORD, So will I give\l"
    .string "Zedekiah the king of Judah, and his\l"
    .string "princes, and the residue of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, that remain in this\l"
    .string "land, and them that dwell in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_9::
    .string "And I will deliver them to be\n"
    .string "removed into all the kingdoms of\l"
    .string "the earth for their hurt, to be a\l"
    .string "reproach and a proverb, a taunt and\l"
    .string "a curse, in all places whither I\l"
    .string "shall drive them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_24_10::
    .string "And I will send the sword, the\n"
    .string "famine, and the pestilence, among\l"
    .string "them, till they be consumed from off\l"
    .string "the land that I gave unto them and to\l"
    .string "their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah\n"
    .string "concerning all the people of\l"
    .string "Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim\l"
    .string "the son of Josiah king of Judah, that\l"
    .string "was the first year of Nebuchadrezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_2::
    .string "The which Jeremiah the prophet\n"
    .string "spake unto all the people of\l"
    .string "Judah, and to all the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_3::
    .string "From the thirteenth year of Josiah\n"
    .string "the son of Amon king of Judah, even\l"
    .string "unto this day, that is the three and\l"
    .string "twentieth year, the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "hath come unto me, and I have spoken\l"
    .string "unto you, rising early and\l"
    .string "speaking; but ye have not hearkened$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_4::
    .string "And the LORD hath sent unto you all\n"
    .string "his servants the prophets, rising\l"
    .string "early and sending them; but ye have\l"
    .string "not hearkened, nor inclined your ear\l"
    .string "to hear.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_5::
    .string "They said, Turn ye again now every\n"
    .string "one from his evil way, and from the\l"
    .string "evil of your doings, and dwell in\l"
    .string "the land that the LORD hath given\l"
    .string "unto you and to your fathers for ever\l"
    .string "and ever:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_6::
    .string "And go not after other gods to serve\n"
    .string "them, and to worship them, and\l"
    .string "provoke me not to anger with the\l"
    .string "works of your hands; and I will do\l"
    .string "you no hurt$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_7::
    .string "Yet ye have not hearkened unto me,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; that ye might\l"
    .string "provoke me to anger with the works of\l"
    .string "your hands to your own hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_8::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts; Because ye have not heard my\l"
    .string "words,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_9::
    .string "Behold, I will send and take all\n"
    .string "the families of the north, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, and Nebuchadrezzar the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, my servant, and will bring\l"
    .string "them against this land, and against\l"
    .string "the inhabitants thereof, and against\l"
    .string "all these nations round about, and\l"
    .string "will utterly destroy them, and make\l"
    .string "them an astonishment, and an hissing,\l"
    .string "and perpetual desolations$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_10::
    .string "Moreover I will take from them the\n"
    .string "voice of mirth, and the voice of\l"
    .string "gladness, the voice of the\l"
    .string "bridegroom, and the voice of the\l"
    .string "bride, the sound of the millstones,\l"
    .string "and the light of the candle.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_11::
    .string "And this whole land shall be a\n"
    .string "desolation, and an astonishment; and\l"
    .string "these nations shall serve the king\l"
    .string "of Babylon seventy years.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_12::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, when\n"
    .string "seventy years are accomplished,\l"
    .string "that I will punish the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and that nation, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, for their iniquity, and the\l"
    .string "land of the Chaldeans, and will\l"
    .string "make it perpetual desolations.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_13::
    .string "And I will bring upon that land\n"
    .string "all my words which I have\l"
    .string "pronounced against it, even all\l"
    .string "that is written in this book, which\l"
    .string "Jeremiah hath prophesied against\l"
    .string "all the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_14::
    .string "For many nations and great kings\n"
    .string "shall serve themselves of them\l"
    .string "also: and I will recompense them\l"
    .string "according to their deeds, and\l"
    .string "according to the works of their own\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_15::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel unto me; Take the wine cup of\l"
    .string "this fury at my hand, and cause all\l"
    .string "the nations, to whom I send thee, to\l"
    .string "drink it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_16::
    .string "And they shall drink, and be moved,\n"
    .string "and be mad, because of the sword that\l"
    .string "I will send among them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_17::
    .string "Then took I the cup at the LORD’s\n"
    .string "hand, and made all the nations to\l"
    .string "drink, unto whom the LORD had sent\l"
    .string "me:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_18::
    .string "To wit, Jerusalem, and the cities\n"
    .string "of Judah, and the kings thereof, and\l"
    .string "the princes thereof, to make them a\l"
    .string "desolation, an astonishment, an\l"
    .string "hissing, and a curse; as it is this\l"
    .string "day;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_19::
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, and his\n"
    .string "servants, and his princes, and all\l"
    .string "his people;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_20::
    .string "And all the mingled people, and\n"
    .string "all the kings of the land of Uz, and\l"
    .string "all the kings of the land of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, and Ashkelon, and\l"
    .string "Azzah, and Ekron, and the remnant of\l"
    .string "Ashdod,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_21::
    .string "Edom, and Moab, and the children of\n"
    .string "Ammon,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_22::
    .string "And all the kings of Tyrus, and\n"
    .string "all the kings of Zidon, and the\l"
    .string "kings of the isles which are beyond\l"
    .string "the sea,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_23::
    .string "Dedan, and Tema, and Buz, and all\n"
    .string "that are in the utmost corners,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_24::
    .string "And all the kings of Arabia, and\n"
    .string "all the kings of the mingled\l"
    .string "people that dwell in the desert,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_25::
    .string "And all the kings of Zimri, and\n"
    .string "all the kings of Elam, and all the\l"
    .string "kings of the Medes,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_26::
    .string "And all the kings of the north, far\n"
    .string "and near, one with another, and all\l"
    .string "the kingdoms of the world, which are\l"
    .string "upon the face of the earth: and the\l"
    .string "king of Sheshach shall drink after\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_27::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt say unto them,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God\l"
    .string "of Israel; Drink ye, and be drunken,\l"
    .string "and spue, and fall, and rise no\l"
    .string "more, because of the sword which I\l"
    .string "will send among you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_28::
    .string "And it shall be, if they refuse to\n"
    .string "take the cup at thine hand to drink,\l"
    .string "then shalt thou say unto them, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts; Ye shall\l"
    .string "certainly drink.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_29::
    .string "For, lo, I begin to bring evil on\n"
    .string "the city which is called by my name,\l"
    .string "and should ye be utterly\l"
    .string "unpunished? Ye shall not be\l"
    .string "unpunished: for I will call for a\l"
    .string "sword upon all the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "the earth, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_30::
    .string "Therefore prophesy thou against\n"
    .string "them all these words, and say unto\l"
    .string "them, The LORD shall roar from on\l"
    .string "high, and utter his voice from his\l"
    .string "holy habitation; he shall mightily\l"
    .string "roar upon his habitation; he shall\l"
    .string "give a shout, as they that tread the\l"
    .string "grapes, against all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_31::
    .string "A noise shall come even to the ends\n"
    .string "of the earth; for the LORD hath a\l"
    .string "controversy with the nations, he\l"
    .string "will plead with all flesh; he\l"
    .string "will give them that are wicked to\l"
    .string "the sword, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_32::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "Behold, evil shall go forth from\l"
    .string "nation to nation, and a great\l"
    .string "whirlwind shall be raised up from\l"
    .string "the coasts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_33::
    .string "And the slain of the LORD shall be\n"
    .string "at that day from one end of the earth\l"
    .string "even unto the other end of the earth:\l"
    .string "they shall not be lamented, neither\l"
    .string "gathered, nor buried; they shall be\l"
    .string "dung upon the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_34::
    .string "Howl, ye shepherds, and cry; and\n"
    .string "wallow yourselves in the ashes, ye\l"
    .string "principal of the flock: for the\l"
    .string "days of your slaughter and of your\l"
    .string "dispersions are accomplished; and\l"
    .string "ye shall fall like a pleasant\l"
    .string "vessel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_35::
    .string "And the shepherds shall have no\n"
    .string "way to flee, nor the principal of\l"
    .string "the flock to escape.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_36::
    .string "A voice of the cry of the shepherds,\n"
    .string "and an howling of the principal of\l"
    .string "the flock, shall be heard: for the\l"
    .string "LORD hath spoiled their pasture.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_37::
    .string "And the peaceable habitations are\n"
    .string "cut down because of the fierce anger\l"
    .string "of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_25_38::
    .string "He hath forsaken his covert, as the\n"
    .string "lion: for their land is desolate\l"
    .string "because of the fierceness of the\l"
    .string "oppressor, and because of his\l"
    .string "fierce anger.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_1::
    .string "In the beginning of the reign of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah came this word from the LORD,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Stand in the\n"
    .string "court of the LORD’s house, and speak\l"
    .string "unto all the cities of Judah, which\l"
    .string "come to worship in the LORD’s house,\l"
    .string "all the words that I command thee to\l"
    .string "speak unto them; diminish not a\l"
    .string "word:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_3::
    .string "If so be they will hearken, and\n"
    .string "turn every man from his evil way,\l"
    .string "that I may repent me of the evil,\l"
    .string "which I purpose to do unto them\l"
    .string "because of the evil of their doings$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_4::
    .string "And thou shalt say unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; If ye will not\l"
    .string "hearken to me, to walk in my law,\l"
    .string "which I have set before you,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_5::
    .string "To hearken to the words of my\n"
    .string "servants the prophets, whom I sent\l"
    .string "unto you, both rising up early, and\l"
    .string "sending them, but ye have not\l"
    .string "hearkened;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_6::
    .string "Then will I make this house like\n"
    .string "Shiloh, and will make this city a\l"
    .string "curse to all the nations of the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_7::
    .string "So the priests and the prophets\n"
    .string "and all the people heard Jeremiah\l"
    .string "speaking these words in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_8::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when Jeremiah\n"
    .string "had made an end of speaking all\l"
    .string "that the LORD had commanded him to\l"
    .string "speak unto all the people, that\l"
    .string "the priests and the prophets and\l"
    .string "all the people took him, saying,\l"
    .string "Thou shalt surely die.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_9::
    .string "Why hast thou prophesied in the\n"
    .string "name of the LORD, saying, This house\l"
    .string "shall be like Shiloh, and this\l"
    .string "city shall be desolate without an\l"
    .string "inhabitant? And all the people\l"
    .string "were gathered against Jeremiah in\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_10::
    .string "When the princes of Judah heard\n"
    .string "these things, then they came up from\l"
    .string "the king’s house unto the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and sat down in the entry of\l"
    .string "the new gate of the LORD’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_11::
    .string "Then spake the priests and the\n"
    .string "prophets unto the princes and to\l"
    .string "all the people, saying, This man\l"
    .string "is worthy to die; for he hath\l"
    .string "prophesied against this city, as ye\l"
    .string "have heard with your ears.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_12::
    .string "Then spake Jeremiah unto all the\n"
    .string "princes and to all the people,\l"
    .string "saying, The LORD sent me to prophesy\l"
    .string "against this house and against this\l"
    .string "city all the words that ye have\l"
    .string "heard.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_13::
    .string "Therefore now amend your ways and\n"
    .string "your doings, and obey the voice of\l"
    .string "the LORD your God; and the LORD will\l"
    .string "repent him of the evil that he hath\l"
    .string "pronounced against you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_14::
    .string "As for me, behold, I am in your\n"
    .string "hand: do with me as seemeth good and\l"
    .string "meet unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_15::
    .string "But know ye for certain, that if ye\n"
    .string "put me to death, ye shall surely\l"
    .string "bring innocent blood upon\l"
    .string "yourselves, and upon this city, and\l"
    .string "upon the inhabitants thereof: for of\l"
    .string "a truth the LORD hath sent me unto\l"
    .string "you to speak all these words in\l"
    .string "your ears.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_16::
    .string "Then said the princes and all the\n"
    .string "people unto the priests and to the\l"
    .string "prophets; This man is not worthy to\l"
    .string "die: for he hath spoken to us in the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_17::
    .string "Then rose up certain of the elders\n"
    .string "of the land, and spake to all the\l"
    .string "assembly of the people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_18::
    .string "Micah the Morasthite prophesied in\n"
    .string "the days of Hezekiah king of Judah,\l"
    .string "and spake to all the people of\l"
    .string "Judah, saying, Thus saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts; Zion shall be plowed like a\l"
    .string "field, and Jerusalem shall become\l"
    .string "heaps, and the mountain of the house\l"
    .string "as the high places of a forest$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_19::
    .string "Did Hezekiah king of Judah and all\n"
    .string "Judah put him at all to death? did\l"
    .string "he not fear the LORD, and besought\l"
    .string "the LORD, and the LORD repented him\l"
    .string "of the evil which he had pronounced\l"
    .string "against them? Thus might we procure\l"
    .string "great evil against our souls.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_20::
    .string "And there was also a man that\n"
    .string "prophesied in the name of the LORD,\l"
    .string "Urijah the son of Shemaiah of\l"
    .string "Kirjathjearim, who prophesied\l"
    .string "against this city and against this\l"
    .string "land according to all the words of\l"
    .string "Jeremiah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_21::
    .string "And when Jehoiakim the king, with\n"
    .string "all his mighty men, and all the\l"
    .string "princes, heard his words, the king\l"
    .string "sought to put him to death: but when\l"
    .string "Urijah heard it, he was afraid, and\l"
    .string "fled, and went into Egypt;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_22::
    .string "And Jehoiakim the king sent men into\n"
    .string "Egypt, namely, Elnathan the son of\l"
    .string "Achbor, and certain men with him into\l"
    .string "Egypt$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_23::
    .string "And they fetched forth Urijah out of\n"
    .string "Egypt, and brought him unto\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim the king; who slew him\l"
    .string "with the sword, and cast his dead\l"
    .string "body into the graves of the common\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_26_24::
    .string "Nevertheless the hand of Ahikam the\n"
    .string "son of Shaphan was with Jeremiah,\l"
    .string "that they should not give him into\l"
    .string "the hand of the people to put him\l"
    .string "to death.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_1::
    .string "In the beginning of the reign of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah came this word unto Jeremiah\l"
    .string "from the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD to me; Make thee\n"
    .string "bonds and yokes, and put them upon\l"
    .string "thy neck,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_3::
    .string "And send them to the king of Edom,\n"
    .string "and to the king of Moab, and to the\l"
    .string "king of the Ammonites, and to the\l"
    .string "king of Tyrus, and to the king of\l"
    .string "Zidon, by the hand of the messengers\l"
    .string "which come to Jerusalem unto\l"
    .string "Zedekiah king of Judah;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_4::
    .string "And command them to say unto their\n"
    .string "masters, Thus saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Thus\l"
    .string "shall ye say unto your masters;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_5::
    .string "I have made the earth, the man and\n"
    .string "the beast that are upon the ground,\l"
    .string "by my great power and by my\l"
    .string "outstretched arm, and have given it\l"
    .string "unto whom it seemed meet unto me$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_6::
    .string "And now have I given all these\n"
    .string "lands into the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "my servant; and the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field have I given him also to serve\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_7::
    .string "And all nations shall serve him,\n"
    .string "and his son, and his son’s son, until\l"
    .string "the very time of his land come: and\l"
    .string "then many nations and great kings\l"
    .string "shall serve themselves of him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_8::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "the nation and kingdom which will\l"
    .string "not serve the same Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon, and that will\l"
    .string "not put their neck under the yoke of\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon, that nation\l"
    .string "will I punish, saith the LORD, with\l"
    .string "the sword, and with the famine, and\l"
    .string "with the pestilence, until I have\l"
    .string "consumed them by his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_9::
    .string "Therefore hearken not ye to your\n"
    .string "prophets, nor to your diviners, nor\l"
    .string "to your dreamers, nor to your\l"
    .string "enchanters, nor to your sorcerers,\l"
    .string "which speak unto you, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "shall not serve the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_10::
    .string "For they prophesy a lie unto you,\n"
    .string "to remove you far from your land; and\l"
    .string "that I should drive you out, and ye\l"
    .string "should perish$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_11::
    .string "But the nations that bring their\n"
    .string "neck under the yoke of the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and serve him, those will\l"
    .string "I let remain still in their own\l"
    .string "land, saith the LORD; and they shall\l"
    .string "till it, and dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_12::
    .string "I spake also to Zedekiah king of\n"
    .string "Judah according to all these words,\l"
    .string "saying, Bring your necks under the\l"
    .string "yoke of the king of Babylon, and\l"
    .string "serve him and his people, and live.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_13::
    .string "Why will ye die, thou and thy\n"
    .string "people, by the sword, by the famine,\l"
    .string "and by the pestilence, as the LORD\l"
    .string "hath spoken against the nation that\l"
    .string "will not serve the king of Babylon?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_14::
    .string "Therefore hearken not unto the\n"
    .string "words of the prophets that speak\l"
    .string "unto you, saying, Ye shall not serve\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon: for they\l"
    .string "prophesy a lie unto you$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_15::
    .string "For I have not sent them, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, yet they prophesy a lie in my\l"
    .string "name; that I might drive you out, and\l"
    .string "that ye might perish, ye, and the\l"
    .string "prophets that prophesy unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_16::
    .string "Also I spake to the priests and to\n"
    .string "all this people, saying, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; Hearken not to the\l"
    .string "words of your prophets that\l"
    .string "prophesy unto you, saying, Behold,\l"
    .string "the vessels of the LORD’s house\l"
    .string "shall now shortly be brought again\l"
    .string "from Babylon: for they prophesy a\l"
    .string "lie unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_17::
    .string "Hearken not unto them; serve the\n"
    .string "king of Babylon, and live:\l"
    .string "wherefore should this city be laid\l"
    .string "waste?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_18::
    .string "But if they be prophets, and if the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD be with them, let\l"
    .string "them now make intercession to the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, that the vessels\l"
    .string "which are left in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and in the house of the king of\l"
    .string "Judah, and at Jerusalem, go not to\l"
    .string "Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_19::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "concerning the pillars, and\l"
    .string "concerning the sea, and concerning\l"
    .string "the bases, and concerning the residue\l"
    .string "of the vessels that remain in this\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_20::
    .string "Which Nebuchadnezzar king of\n"
    .string "Babylon took not, when he carried\l"
    .string "away captive Jeconiah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim king of Judah from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem to Babylon, and all the\l"
    .string "nobles of Judah and Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_21::
    .string "Yea, thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel, concerning the\l"
    .string "vessels that remain in the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and in the house of the king\l"
    .string "of Judah and of Jerusalem;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_27_22::
    .string "They shall be carried to Babylon,\n"
    .string "and there shall they be until the\l"
    .string "day that I visit them, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD; then will I bring them up,\l"
    .string "and restore them to this place$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_1::
    .string "And it came to pass the same year,\n"
    .string "in the beginning of the reign of\l"
    .string "Zedekiah king of Judah, in the fourth\l"
    .string "year, and in the fifth month, that\l"
    .string "Hananiah the son of Azur the\l"
    .string "prophet, which was of Gibeon, spake\l"
    .string "unto me in the house of the LORD, in\l"
    .string "the presence of the priests and of\l"
    .string "all the people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_2::
    .string "Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel, saying, I have\l"
    .string "broken the yoke of the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_3::
    .string "Within two full years will I\n"
    .string "bring again into this place all\l"
    .string "the vessels of the LORD’s house,\l"
    .string "that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon\l"
    .string "took away from this place, and\l"
    .string "carried them to Babylon:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_4::
    .string "And I will bring again to this\n"
    .string "place Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim\l"
    .string "king of Judah, with all the\l"
    .string "captives of Judah, that went into\l"
    .string "Babylon, saith the LORD: for I will\l"
    .string "break the yoke of the king of Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_5::
    .string "Then the prophet Jeremiah said\n"
    .string "unto the prophet Hananiah in the\l"
    .string "presence of the priests, and in the\l"
    .string "presence of all the people that\l"
    .string "stood in the house of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_6::
    .string "Even the prophet Jeremiah said,\n"
    .string "Amen: the LORD do so: the LORD\l"
    .string "perform thy words which thou hast\l"
    .string "prophesied, to bring again the\l"
    .string "vessels of the LORD’s house, and\l"
    .string "all that is carried away captive,\l"
    .string "from Babylon into this place$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_7::
    .string "Nevertheless hear thou now this\n"
    .string "word that I speak in thine ears, and\l"
    .string "in the ears of all the people;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_8::
    .string "The prophets that have been before\n"
    .string "me and before thee of old\l"
    .string "prophesied both against many\l"
    .string "countries, and against great\l"
    .string "kingdoms, of war, and of evil, and of\l"
    .string "pestilence$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_9::
    .string "The prophet which prophesieth of\n"
    .string "peace, when the word of the prophet\l"
    .string "shall come to pass, then shall the\l"
    .string "prophet be known, that the LORD hath\l"
    .string "truly sent him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_10::
    .string "Then Hananiah the prophet took the\n"
    .string "yoke from off the prophet\l"
    .string "Jeremiah’s neck, and brake it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_11::
    .string "And Hananiah spake in the presence\n"
    .string "of all the people, saying, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; Even so will I break\l"
    .string "the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon from the neck of all\l"
    .string "nations within the space of two\l"
    .string "full years. And the prophet\l"
    .string "Jeremiah went his way.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_12::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah the prophet, after that\l"
    .string "Hananiah the prophet had broken the\l"
    .string "yoke from off the neck of the\l"
    .string "prophet Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_13::
    .string "Go and tell Hananiah, saying, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; Thou hast broken the\l"
    .string "yokes of wood; but thou shalt make\l"
    .string "for them yokes of iron$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_14::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; I have put a yoke\l"
    .string "of iron upon the neck of all these\l"
    .string "nations, that they may serve\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and\l"
    .string "they shall serve him: and I have\l"
    .string "given him the beasts of the field\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_15::
    .string "Then said the prophet Jeremiah\n"
    .string "unto Hananiah the prophet, Hear\l"
    .string "now, Hananiah; The LORD hath not sent\l"
    .string "thee; but thou makest this people\l"
    .string "to trust in a lie.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_16::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will cast thee from off\l"
    .string "the face of the earth: this year thou\l"
    .string "shalt die, because thou hast taught\l"
    .string "rebellion against the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_28_17::
    .string "So Hananiah the prophet died the\n"
    .string "same year in the seventh month.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_1::
    .string "Now these are the words of the\n"
    .string "letter that Jeremiah the prophet\l"
    .string "sent from Jerusalem unto the residue\l"
    .string "of the elders which were carried\l"
    .string "away captives, and to the priests,\l"
    .string "and to the prophets, and to all the\l"
    .string "people whom Nebuchadnezzar had\l"
    .string "carried away captive from Jerusalem\l"
    .string "to Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_2::
    .string "(After that Jeconiah the king, and\n"
    .string "the queen, and the eunuchs, the\l"
    .string "princes of Judah and Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "the carpenters, and the smiths, were\l"
    .string "departed from Jerusalem;)"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_3::
    .string "By the hand of Elasah the son of\n"
    .string "Shaphan, and Gemariah the son of\l"
    .string "Hilkiah, (whom Zedekiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah sent unto Babylon to\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon)\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel, unto all that are\l"
    .string "carried away captives, whom I have\l"
    .string "caused to be carried away from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem unto Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_5::
    .string "Build ye houses, and dwell in\n"
    .string "them; and plant gardens, and eat the\l"
    .string "fruit of them;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_6::
    .string "Take ye wives, and beget sons and\n"
    .string "daughters; and take wives for your\l"
    .string "sons, and give your daughters to\l"
    .string "husbands, that they may bear sons and\l"
    .string "daughters; that ye may be increased\l"
    .string "there, and not diminished$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_7::
    .string "And seek the peace of the city\n"
    .string "whither I have caused you to be\l"
    .string "carried away captives, and pray\l"
    .string "unto the LORD for it: for in the\l"
    .string "peace thereof shall ye have peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_8::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; Let not your\l"
    .string "prophets and your diviners, that be\l"
    .string "in the midst of you, deceive you,\l"
    .string "neither hearken to your dreams which\l"
    .string "ye cause to be dreamed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_9::
    .string "For they prophesy falsely unto\n"
    .string "you in my name: I have not sent them,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_10::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, That after\n"
    .string "seventy years be accomplished at\l"
    .string "Babylon I will visit you, and\l"
    .string "perform my good word toward you, in\l"
    .string "causing you to return to this place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_11::
    .string "For I know the thoughts that I think\n"
    .string "toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts\l"
    .string "of peace, and not of evil, to give\l"
    .string "you an expected end.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_12::
    .string "Then shall ye call upon me, and\n"
    .string "ye shall go and pray unto me, and I\l"
    .string "will hearken unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_13::
    .string "And ye shall seek me, and find me,\n"
    .string "when ye shall search for me with\l"
    .string "all your heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_14::
    .string "And I will be found of you, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD: and I will turn away your\l"
    .string "captivity, and I will gather you\l"
    .string "from all the nations, and from all\l"
    .string "the places whither I have driven\l"
    .string "you, saith the LORD; and I will\l"
    .string "bring you again into the place\l"
    .string "whence I caused you to be carried\l"
    .string "away captive.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_15::
    .string "Because ye have said, The LORD hath\n"
    .string "raised us up prophets in Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_16::
    .string "Know that thus saith the LORD of the\n"
    .string "king that sitteth upon the throne of\l"
    .string "David, and of all the people that\l"
    .string "dwelleth in this city, and of your\l"
    .string "brethren that are not gone forth with\l"
    .string "you into captivity;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_17::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will send upon them the\l"
    .string "sword, the famine, and the\l"
    .string "pestilence, and will make them\l"
    .string "like vile figs, that cannot be\l"
    .string "eaten, they are so evil$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_18::
    .string "And I will persecute them with the\n"
    .string "sword, with the famine, and with the\l"
    .string "pestilence, and will deliver them\l"
    .string "to be removed to all the kingdoms of\l"
    .string "the earth, to be a curse, and an\l"
    .string "astonishment, and an hissing, and a\l"
    .string "reproach, among all the nations\l"
    .string "whither I have driven them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_19::
    .string "Because they have not hearkened to\n"
    .string "my words, saith the LORD, which I\l"
    .string "sent unto them by my servants the\l"
    .string "prophets, rising up early and\l"
    .string "sending them; but ye would not hear,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_20::
    .string "Hear ye therefore the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD, all ye of the captivity, whom\l"
    .string "I have sent from Jerusalem to\l"
    .string "Babylon:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_21::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel, of Ahab the son of\l"
    .string "Kolaiah, and of Zedekiah the son of\l"
    .string "Maaseiah, which prophesy a lie unto\l"
    .string "you in my name; Behold, I will\l"
    .string "deliver them into the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon; and\l"
    .string "he shall slay them before your\l"
    .string "eyes;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_22::
    .string "And of them shall be taken up a\n"
    .string "curse by all the captivity of Judah\l"
    .string "which are in Babylon, saying, The\l"
    .string "LORD make thee like Zedekiah and\l"
    .string "like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon\l"
    .string "roasted in the fire;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_23::
    .string "Because they have committed\n"
    .string "villany in Israel, and have\l"
    .string "committed adultery with their\l"
    .string "neighbours’ wives, and have spoken\l"
    .string "lying words in my name, which I have\l"
    .string "not commanded them; even I know, and\l"
    .string "am a witness, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_24::
    .string "Thus shalt thou also speak to\n"
    .string "Shemaiah the Nehelamite, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_25::
    .string "Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel, saying, Because\l"
    .string "thou hast sent letters in thy name\l"
    .string "unto all the people that are at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and to Zephaniah the son\l"
    .string "of Maaseiah the priest, and to all\l"
    .string "the priests, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_26::
    .string "The LORD hath made thee priest in\n"
    .string "the stead of Jehoiada the priest,\l"
    .string "that ye should be officers in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, for every man that\l"
    .string "is mad, and maketh himself a\l"
    .string "prophet, that thou shouldest put\l"
    .string "him in prison, and in the stocks$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_27::
    .string "Now therefore why hast thou not\n"
    .string "reproved Jeremiah of Anathoth, which\l"
    .string "maketh himself a prophet to you?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_28::
    .string "For therefore he sent unto us in\n"
    .string "Babylon, saying, This captivity is\l"
    .string "long: build ye houses, and dwell in\l"
    .string "them; and plant gardens, and eat the\l"
    .string "fruit of them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_29::
    .string "And Zephaniah the priest read this\n"
    .string "letter in the ears of Jeremiah the\l"
    .string "prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_30::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_31::
    .string "Send to all them of the captivity,\n"
    .string "saying, Thus saith the LORD\l"
    .string "concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite;\l"
    .string "Because that Shemaiah hath\l"
    .string "prophesied unto you, and I sent him\l"
    .string "not, and he caused you to trust in a\l"
    .string "lie:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_29_32::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will punish Shemaiah the\l"
    .string "Nehelamite, and his seed: he shall\l"
    .string "not have a man to dwell among this\l"
    .string "people; neither shall he behold\l"
    .string "the good that I will do for my\l"
    .string "people, saith the LORD; because he\l"
    .string "hath taught rebellion against the\l"
    .string "LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_2::
    .string "Thus speaketh the LORD God of\n"
    .string "Israel, saying, Write thee all the\l"
    .string "words that I have spoken unto thee\l"
    .string "in a book$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_3::
    .string "For, lo, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will bring again the\l"
    .string "captivity of my people Israel and\l"
    .string "Judah, saith the LORD: and I will\l"
    .string "cause them to return to the land\l"
    .string "that I gave to their fathers, and\l"
    .string "they shall possess it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_4::
    .string "And these are the words that the\n"
    .string "LORD spake concerning Israel and\l"
    .string "concerning Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_5::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; We have\n"
    .string "heard a voice of trembling, of fear,\l"
    .string "and not of peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_6::
    .string "Ask ye now, and see whether a man\n"
    .string "doth travail with child? wherefore\l"
    .string "do I see every man with his hands on\l"
    .string "his loins, as a woman in travail,\l"
    .string "and all faces are turned into\l"
    .string "paleness?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_7::
    .string "Alas! for that day is great, so that\n"
    .string "none is like it: it is even the time\l"
    .string "of Jacob’s trouble, but he shall be\l"
    .string "saved out of it$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_8::
    .string "For it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD of hosts, that I\l"
    .string "will break his yoke from off thy\l"
    .string "neck, and will burst thy bonds, and\l"
    .string "strangers shall no more serve\l"
    .string "themselves of him:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_9::
    .string "But they shall serve the LORD\n"
    .string "their God, and David their king, whom\l"
    .string "I will raise up unto them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_10::
    .string "Therefore fear thou not, O my\n"
    .string "servant Jacob, saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "neither be dismayed, O Israel: for,\l"
    .string "lo, I will save thee from afar, and\l"
    .string "thy seed from the land of their\l"
    .string "captivity; and Jacob shall return,\l"
    .string "and shall be in rest, and be quiet,\l"
    .string "and none shall make him afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_11::
    .string "For I am with thee, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "to save thee: though I make a full\l"
    .string "end of all nations whither I have\l"
    .string "scattered thee, yet I will not make\l"
    .string "a full end of thee: but I will\l"
    .string "correct thee in measure, and will\l"
    .string "not leave thee altogether\l"
    .string "unpunished.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_12::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, Thy bruise\n"
    .string "is incurable, and thy wound is\l"
    .string "grievous.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_13::
    .string "There is none to plead thy cause,\n"
    .string "that thou mayest be bound up: thou\l"
    .string "hast no healing medicines.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_14::
    .string "All thy lovers have forgotten\n"
    .string "thee; they seek thee not; for I have\l"
    .string "wounded thee with the wound of an\l"
    .string "enemy, with the chastisement of a\l"
    .string "cruel one, for the multitude of\l"
    .string "thine iniquity; because thy sins were\l"
    .string "increased.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_15::
    .string "Why criest thou for thine\n"
    .string "affliction? thy sorrow is incurable\l"
    .string "for the multitude of thine iniquity:\l"
    .string "because thy sins were increased, I\l"
    .string "have done these things unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_16::
    .string "Therefore all they that devour\n"
    .string "thee shall be devoured; and all\l"
    .string "thine adversaries, every one of them,\l"
    .string "shall go into captivity; and they\l"
    .string "that spoil thee shall be a spoil,\l"
    .string "and all that prey upon thee will\l"
    .string "I give for a prey.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_17::
    .string "For I will restore health unto\n"
    .string "thee, and I will heal thee of thy\l"
    .string "wounds, saith the LORD; because they\l"
    .string "called thee an Outcast, saying,\l"
    .string "This is Zion, whom no man seeketh\l"
    .string "after.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_18::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I\n"
    .string "will bring again the captivity of\l"
    .string "Jacob’s tents, and have mercy on his\l"
    .string "dwellingplaces; and the city\l"
    .string "shall be builded upon her own\l"
    .string "heap, and the palace shall remain\l"
    .string "after the manner thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_19::
    .string "And out of them shall proceed\n"
    .string "thanksgiving and the voice of them\l"
    .string "that make merry: and I will\l"
    .string "multiply them, and they shall not\l"
    .string "be few; I will also glorify them,\l"
    .string "and they shall not be small.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_20::
    .string "Their children also shall be as\n"
    .string "aforetime, and their congregation\l"
    .string "shall be established before me, and\l"
    .string "I will punish all that oppress\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_21::
    .string "And their nobles shall be of\n"
    .string "themselves, and their governor\l"
    .string "shall proceed from the midst of\l"
    .string "them; and I will cause him to draw\l"
    .string "near, and he shall approach unto\l"
    .string "me: for who is this that engaged his\l"
    .string "heart to approach unto me? saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_22::
    .string "And ye shall be my people, and I\n"
    .string "will be your God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_23::
    .string "Behold, the whirlwind of the LORD\n"
    .string "goeth forth with fury, a continuing\l"
    .string "whirlwind: it shall fall with\l"
    .string "pain upon the head of the wicked.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_30_24::
    .string "The fierce anger of the LORD shall\n"
    .string "not return, until he hath done it,\l"
    .string "and until he have performed the\l"
    .string "intents of his heart: in the latter\l"
    .string "days ye shall consider it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_1::
    .string "At the same time, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "will I be the God of all the\l"
    .string "families of Israel, and they shall\l"
    .string "be my people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, The people\n"
    .string "which were left of the sword found\l"
    .string "grace in the wilderness; even\l"
    .string "Israel, when I went to cause him to\l"
    .string "rest.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_3::
    .string "The LORD hath appeared of old unto\n"
    .string "me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee\l"
    .string "with an everlasting love: therefore\l"
    .string "with lovingkindness have I drawn\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_4::
    .string "Again I will build thee, and thou\n"
    .string "shalt be built, O virgin of Israel:\l"
    .string "thou shalt again be adorned with thy\l"
    .string "tabrets, and shalt go forth in the\l"
    .string "dances of them that make merry.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_5::
    .string "Thou shalt yet plant vines upon\n"
    .string "the mountains of Samaria: the\l"
    .string "planters shall plant, and shall\l"
    .string "eat them as common things.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_6::
    .string "For there shall be a day, that the\n"
    .string "watchmen upon the mount Ephraim\l"
    .string "shall cry, Arise ye, and let us go\l"
    .string "up to Zion unto the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_7::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; Sing with\n"
    .string "gladness for Jacob, and shout among\l"
    .string "the chief of the nations: publish\l"
    .string "ye, praise ye, and say, O LORD, save\l"
    .string "thy people, the remnant of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_8::
    .string "Behold, I will bring them from the\n"
    .string "north country, and gather them from\l"
    .string "the coasts of the earth, and with\l"
    .string "them the blind and the lame, the\l"
    .string "woman with child and her that\l"
    .string "travaileth with child together: a\l"
    .string "great company shall return thither.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_9::
    .string "They shall come with weeping, and\n"
    .string "with supplications will I lead\l"
    .string "them: I will cause them to walk by\l"
    .string "the rivers of waters in a straight\l"
    .string "way, wherein they shall not\l"
    .string "stumble: for I am a father to\l"
    .string "Israel, and Ephraim is my firstborn.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_10::
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD, O ye\n"
    .string "nations, and declare it in the isles\l"
    .string "afar off, and say, He that scattered\l"
    .string "Israel will gather him, and keep\l"
    .string "him, as a shepherd doth his flock.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_11::
    .string "For the LORD hath redeemed Jacob,\n"
    .string "and ransomed him from the hand of him\l"
    .string "that was stronger than he.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_12::
    .string "Therefore they shall come and sing\n"
    .string "in the height of Zion, and shall\l"
    .string "flow together to the goodness of the\l"
    .string "LORD, for wheat, and for wine, and for\l"
    .string "oil, and for the young of the flock\l"
    .string "and of the herd: and their soul\l"
    .string "shall be as a watered garden; and\l"
    .string "they shall not sorrow any more at\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_13::
    .string "Then shall the virgin rejoice in\n"
    .string "the dance, both young men and old\l"
    .string "together: for I will turn their\l"
    .string "mourning into joy, and will comfort\l"
    .string "them, and make them rejoice from\l"
    .string "their sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_14::
    .string "And I will satiate the soul of the\n"
    .string "priests with fatness, and my people\l"
    .string "shall be satisfied with my\l"
    .string "goodness, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_15::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; A voice was\n"
    .string "heard in Ramah, lamentation, and\l"
    .string "bitter weeping; Rahel weeping for\l"
    .string "her children refused to be comforted\l"
    .string "for her children, because they were\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_16::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Refrain thy\n"
    .string "voice from weeping, and thine eyes\l"
    .string "from tears: for thy work shall be\l"
    .string "rewarded, saith the LORD; and they\l"
    .string "shall come again from the land of\l"
    .string "the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_17::
    .string "And there is hope in thine end,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that thy children\l"
    .string "shall come again to their own\l"
    .string "border.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_18::
    .string "I have surely heard Ephraim\n"
    .string "bemoaning himself thus; Thou hast\l"
    .string "chastised me, and I was chastised, as\l"
    .string "a bullock unaccustomed to the yoke:\l"
    .string "turn thou me, and I shall be turned;\l"
    .string "for thou art the LORD my God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_19::
    .string "Surely after that I was turned, I\n"
    .string "repented; and after that I was\l"
    .string "instructed, I smote upon my thigh: I\l"
    .string "was ashamed, yea, even confounded,\l"
    .string "because I did bear the reproach of\l"
    .string "my youth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_20::
    .string "Is Ephraim my dear son? is he a\n"
    .string "pleasant child? for since I spake\l"
    .string "against him, I do earnestly remember\l"
    .string "him still: therefore my bowels are\l"
    .string "troubled for him; I will surely\l"
    .string "have mercy upon him, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_21::
    .string "Set thee up waymarks, make thee\n"
    .string "high heaps: set thine heart toward\l"
    .string "the highway, even the way which thou\l"
    .string "wentest: turn again, O virgin of\l"
    .string "Israel, turn again to these thy\l"
    .string "cities.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_22::
    .string "How long wilt thou go about, O thou\n"
    .string "backsliding daughter? for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath created a new thing in the\l"
    .string "earth, A woman shall compass a man.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_23::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; As yet they shall\l"
    .string "use this speech in the land of Judah\l"
    .string "and in the cities thereof, when I\l"
    .string "shall bring again their captivity;\l"
    .string "The LORD bless thee, O habitation of\l"
    .string "justice, and mountain of holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_24::
    .string "And there shall dwell in Judah\n"
    .string "itself, and in all the cities\l"
    .string "thereof together, husbandmen, and\l"
    .string "they that go forth with flocks.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_25::
    .string "For I have satiated the weary soul,\n"
    .string "and I have replenished every\l"
    .string "sorrowful soul.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_26::
    .string "Upon this I awaked, and beheld; and\n"
    .string "my sleep was sweet unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_27::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will sow the house of\l"
    .string "Israel and the house of Judah with\l"
    .string "the seed of man, and with the seed of\l"
    .string "beast.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_28::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "like as I have watched over them, to\l"
    .string "pluck up, and to break down, and to\l"
    .string "throw down, and to destroy, and to\l"
    .string "afflict; so will I watch over them,\l"
    .string "to build, and to plant, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_29::
    .string "In those days they shall say no\n"
    .string "more, The fathers have eaten a sour\l"
    .string "grape, and the children’s teeth are\l"
    .string "set on edge.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_30::
    .string "But every one shall die for his own\n"
    .string "iniquity: every man that eateth the\l"
    .string "sour grape, his teeth shall be set\l"
    .string "on edge.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_31::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will make a new\l"
    .string "covenant with the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "and with the house of Judah:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_32::
    .string "Not according to the covenant that I\n"
    .string "made with their fathers in the day\l"
    .string "that I took them by the hand to bring\l"
    .string "them out of the land of Egypt; which\l"
    .string "my covenant they brake, although I\l"
    .string "was an husband unto them, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_33::
    .string "But this shall be the covenant\n"
    .string "that I will make with the house of\l"
    .string "Israel; After those days, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, I will put my law in their\l"
    .string "inward parts, and write it in their\l"
    .string "hearts; and will be their God, and\l"
    .string "they shall be my people$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_34::
    .string "And they shall teach no more every\n"
    .string "man his neighbour, and every man his\l"
    .string "brother, saying, Know the LORD: for\l"
    .string "they shall all know me, from the\l"
    .string "least of them unto the greatest of\l"
    .string "them, saith the LORD: for I will\l"
    .string "forgive their iniquity, and I will\l"
    .string "remember their sin no more.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_35::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, which giveth\n"
    .string "the sun for a light by day, and the\l"
    .string "ordinances of the moon and of the\l"
    .string "stars for a light by night, which\l"
    .string "divideth the sea when the waves\l"
    .string "thereof roar; The LORD of hosts is\l"
    .string "his name:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_36::
    .string "If those ordinances depart from\n"
    .string "before me, saith the LORD, then the\l"
    .string "seed of Israel also shall cease\l"
    .string "from being a nation before me for ever$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_37::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; If heaven above\n"
    .string "can be measured, and the foundations\l"
    .string "of the earth searched out beneath, I\l"
    .string "will also cast off all the seed of\l"
    .string "Israel for all that they have done,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_38::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that the city shall be built\l"
    .string "to the LORD from the tower of\l"
    .string "Hananeel unto the gate of the corner.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_39::
    .string "And the measuring line shall yet\n"
    .string "go forth over against it upon the\l"
    .string "hill Gareb, and shall compass\l"
    .string "about to Goath.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_31_40::
    .string "And the whole valley of the dead\n"
    .string "bodies, and of the ashes, and all\l"
    .string "the fields unto the brook of Kidron,\l"
    .string "unto the corner of the horse gate\l"
    .string "toward the east, shall be holy unto\l"
    .string "the LORD; it shall not be plucked\l"
    .string "up, nor thrown down any more for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD in the tenth year of\l"
    .string "Zedekiah king of Judah, which was the\l"
    .string "eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_2::
    .string "For then the king of Babylon’s army\n"
    .string "besieged Jerusalem: and Jeremiah the\l"
    .string "prophet was shut up in the court of\l"
    .string "the prison, which was in the king of\l"
    .string "Judah’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_3::
    .string "For Zedekiah king of Judah had shut\n"
    .string "him up, saying, Wherefore dost thou\l"
    .string "prophesy, and say, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD, Behold, I will give this city\l"
    .string "into the hand of the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "and he shall take it;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_4::
    .string "And Zedekiah king of Judah shall\n"
    .string "not escape out of the hand of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans, but shall surely be\l"
    .string "delivered into the hand of the king\l"
    .string "of Babylon, and shall speak with\l"
    .string "him mouth to mouth, and his eyes\l"
    .string "shall behold his eyes;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_5::
    .string "And he shall lead Zedekiah to\n"
    .string "Babylon, and there shall he be\l"
    .string "until I visit him, saith the LORD:\l"
    .string "though ye fight with the Chaldeans,\l"
    .string "ye shall not prosper$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_6::
    .string "And Jeremiah said, The word of the\n"
    .string "LORD came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_7::
    .string "Behold, Hanameel the son of\n"
    .string "Shallum thine uncle shall come\l"
    .string "unto thee saying, Buy thee my field\l"
    .string "that is in Anathoth: for the right of\l"
    .string "redemption is thine to buy it$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_8::
    .string "So Hanameel mine uncle’s son came\n"
    .string "to me in the court of the prison\l"
    .string "according to the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and said unto me, Buy my field, I\l"
    .string "pray thee, that is in Anathoth, which\l"
    .string "is in the country of Benjamin: for\l"
    .string "the right of inheritance is thine,\l"
    .string "and the redemption is thine; buy it\l"
    .string "for thyself. Then I knew that this\l"
    .string "was the word of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_9::
    .string "And I bought the field of Hanameel\n"
    .string "my uncle’s son, that was in\l"
    .string "Anathoth, and weighed him the money,\l"
    .string "even seventeen shekels of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_10::
    .string "And I subscribed the evidence, and\n"
    .string "sealed it, and took witnesses, and\l"
    .string "weighed him the money in the\l"
    .string "balances.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_11::
    .string "So I took the evidence of the\n"
    .string "purchase, both that which was sealed\l"
    .string "according to the law and custom, and\l"
    .string "that which was open:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_12::
    .string "And I gave the evidence of the\n"
    .string "purchase unto Baruch the son of\l"
    .string "Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, in the\l"
    .string "sight of Hanameel mine uncle’s son,\l"
    .string "and in the presence of the witnesses\l"
    .string "that subscribed the book of the\l"
    .string "purchase, before all the Jews that\l"
    .string "sat in the court of the prison$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_13::
    .string "And I charged Baruch before them,\n"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_14::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; Take these evidences,\l"
    .string "this evidence of the purchase, both\l"
    .string "which is sealed, and this evidence\l"
    .string "which is open; and put them in an\l"
    .string "earthen vessel, that they may\l"
    .string "continue many days$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_15::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; Houses and fields\l"
    .string "and vineyards shall be possessed\l"
    .string "again in this land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_16::
    .string "Now when I had delivered the\n"
    .string "evidence of the purchase unto Baruch\l"
    .string "the son of Neriah, I prayed unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_17::
    .string "Ah Lord GOD! behold, thou hast made\n"
    .string "the heaven and the earth by thy great\l"
    .string "power and stretched out arm, and\l"
    .string "there is nothing too hard for thee:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_18::
    .string "Thou shewest lovingkindness unto\n"
    .string "thousands, and recompensest the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the fathers into the\l"
    .string "bosom of their children after them:\l"
    .string "the Great, the Mighty God, the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts, is his name,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_19::
    .string "Great in counsel, and mighty in\n"
    .string "work: for thine eyes are open upon\l"
    .string "all the ways of the sons of men: to\l"
    .string "give every one according to his ways,\l"
    .string "and according to the fruit of his\l"
    .string "doings:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_20::
    .string "Which hast set signs and wonders in\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt, even unto this\l"
    .string "day, and in Israel, and among other\l"
    .string "men; and hast made thee a name, as at\l"
    .string "this day;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_21::
    .string "And hast brought forth thy people\n"
    .string "Israel out of the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "with signs, and with wonders, and\l"
    .string "with a strong hand, and with a\l"
    .string "stretched out arm, and with great\l"
    .string "terror;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_22::
    .string "And hast given them this land,\n"
    .string "which thou didst swear to their\l"
    .string "fathers to give them, a land flowing\l"
    .string "with milk and honey;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_23::
    .string "And they came in, and possessed it;\n"
    .string "but they obeyed not thy voice,\l"
    .string "neither walked in thy law; they have\l"
    .string "done nothing of all that thou\l"
    .string "commandedst them to do: therefore\l"
    .string "thou hast caused all this evil to\l"
    .string "come upon them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_24::
    .string "Behold the mounts, they are come\n"
    .string "unto the city to take it; and the city\l"
    .string "is given into the hand of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans, that fight against it,\l"
    .string "because of the sword, and of the\l"
    .string "famine, and of the pestilence: and\l"
    .string "what thou hast spoken is come to\l"
    .string "pass; and, behold, thou seest it$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_25::
    .string "And thou hast said unto me, O Lord\n"
    .string "GOD, Buy thee the field for money,\l"
    .string "and take witnesses; for the city is\l"
    .string "given into the hand of the Chaldeans.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_26::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_27::
    .string "Behold, I am the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "all flesh: is there any thing too\l"
    .string "hard for me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_28::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will give this city into\l"
    .string "the hand of the Chaldeans, and into\l"
    .string "the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and he shall take it:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_29::
    .string "And the Chaldeans, that fight\n"
    .string "against this city, shall come and\l"
    .string "set fire on this city, and burn it\l"
    .string "with the houses, upon whose roofs\l"
    .string "they have offered incense unto Baal,\l"
    .string "and poured out drink offerings unto\l"
    .string "other gods, to provoke me to anger$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_30::
    .string "For the children of Israel and the\n"
    .string "children of Judah have only done\l"
    .string "evil before me from their youth: for\l"
    .string "the children of Israel have only\l"
    .string "provoked me to anger with the work of\l"
    .string "their hands, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_31::
    .string "For this city hath been to me as a\n"
    .string "provocation of mine anger and of my\l"
    .string "fury from the day that they built it\l"
    .string "even unto this day; that I should\l"
    .string "remove it from before my face,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_32::
    .string "Because of all the evil of the\n"
    .string "children of Israel and of the\l"
    .string "children of Judah, which they have\l"
    .string "done to provoke me to anger, they,\l"
    .string "their kings, their princes, their\l"
    .string "priests, and their prophets, and\l"
    .string "the men of Judah, and the inhabitants\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_33::
    .string "And they have turned unto me the\n"
    .string "back, and not the face: though I\l"
    .string "taught them, rising up early and\l"
    .string "teaching them, yet they have not\l"
    .string "hearkened to receive instruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_34::
    .string "But they set their abominations in\n"
    .string "the house, which is called by my\l"
    .string "name, to defile it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_35::
    .string "And they built the high places of\n"
    .string "Baal, which are in the valley of\l"
    .string "the son of Hinnom, to cause their\l"
    .string "sons and their daughters to pass\l"
    .string "through the fire unto Molech; which\l"
    .string "I commanded them not, neither came it\l"
    .string "into my mind, that they should do\l"
    .string "this abomination, to cause Judah to\l"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_36::
    .string "And now therefore thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, the God of Israel, concerning\l"
    .string "this city, whereof ye say, It shall\l"
    .string "be delivered into the hand of the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon by the sword, and by\l"
    .string "the famine, and by the pestilence;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_37::
    .string "Behold, I will gather them out of\n"
    .string "all countries, whither I have\l"
    .string "driven them in mine anger, and in my\l"
    .string "fury, and in great wrath; and I will\l"
    .string "bring them again unto this place,\l"
    .string "and I will cause them to dwell\l"
    .string "safely:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_38::
    .string "And they shall be my people, and\n"
    .string "I will be their God:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_39::
    .string "And I will give them one heart, and\n"
    .string "one way, that they may fear me for\l"
    .string "ever, for the good of them, and of\l"
    .string "their children after them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_40::
    .string "And I will make an everlasting\n"
    .string "covenant with them, that I will not\l"
    .string "turn away from them, to do them good;\l"
    .string "but I will put my fear in their\l"
    .string "hearts, that they shall not depart\l"
    .string "from me$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_41::
    .string "Yea, I will rejoice over them to do\n"
    .string "them good, and I will plant them in\l"
    .string "this land assuredly with my whole\l"
    .string "heart and with my whole soul.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_42::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; Like as I\n"
    .string "have brought all this great evil\l"
    .string "upon this people, so will I bring\l"
    .string "upon them all the good that I have\l"
    .string "promised them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_43::
    .string "And fields shall be bought in this\n"
    .string "land, whereof ye say, It is desolate\l"
    .string "without man or beast; it is given\l"
    .string "into the hand of the Chaldeans.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_32_44::
    .string "Men shall buy fields for money,\n"
    .string "and subscribe evidences, and seal\l"
    .string "them, and take witnesses in the land\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, and in the places about\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and in the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, and in the cities of the\l"
    .string "mountains, and in the cities of the\l"
    .string "valley, and in the cities of the\l"
    .string "south: for I will cause their\l"
    .string "captivity to return, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_1::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto Jeremiah the second time, while\l"
    .string "he was yet shut up in the court of\l"
    .string "the prison, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD the maker\n"
    .string "thereof, the LORD that formed it, to\l"
    .string "establish it; the LORD is his name;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_3::
    .string "Call unto me, and I will answer\n"
    .string "thee, and shew thee great and mighty\l"
    .string "things, which thou knowest not$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_4::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel, concerning the houses of\l"
    .string "this city, and concerning the houses\l"
    .string "of the kings of Judah, which are\l"
    .string "thrown down by the mounts, and by the\l"
    .string "sword;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_5::
    .string "They come to fight with the\n"
    .string "Chaldeans, but it is to fill them\l"
    .string "with the dead bodies of men, whom I\l"
    .string "have slain in mine anger and in my\l"
    .string "fury, and for all whose wickedness I\l"
    .string "have hid my face from this city$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_6::
    .string "Behold, I will bring it health\n"
    .string "and cure, and I will cure them, and\l"
    .string "will reveal unto them the\l"
    .string "abundance of peace and truth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_7::
    .string "And I will cause the captivity of\n"
    .string "Judah and the captivity of Israel\l"
    .string "to return, and will build them, as\l"
    .string "at the first.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_8::
    .string "And I will cleanse them from all\n"
    .string "their iniquity, whereby they have\l"
    .string "sinned against me; and I will\l"
    .string "pardon all their iniquities,\l"
    .string "whereby they have sinned, and whereby\l"
    .string "they have transgressed against me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_9::
    .string "And it shall be to me a name of joy,\n"
    .string "a praise and an honour before all\l"
    .string "the nations of the earth, which\l"
    .string "shall hear all the good that I do\l"
    .string "unto them: and they shall fear and\l"
    .string "tremble for all the goodness and\l"
    .string "for all the prosperity that I\l"
    .string "procure unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_10::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Again there\n"
    .string "shall be heard in this place,\l"
    .string "which ye say shall be desolate\l"
    .string "without man and without beast, even\l"
    .string "in the cities of Judah, and in the\l"
    .string "streets of Jerusalem, that are\l"
    .string "desolate, without man, and without\l"
    .string "inhabitant, and without beast,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_11::
    .string "The voice of joy, and the voice of\n"
    .string "gladness, the voice of the\l"
    .string "bridegroom, and the voice of the\l"
    .string "bride, the voice of them that shall\l"
    .string "say, Praise the LORD of hosts: for\l"
    .string "the LORD is good; for his mercy\l"
    .string "endureth for ever: and of them that\l"
    .string "shall bring the sacrifice of\l"
    .string "praise into the house of the LORD.\l"
    .string "For I will cause to return the\l"
    .string "captivity of the land, as at the\l"
    .string "first, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_12::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Again\n"
    .string "in this place, which is desolate\l"
    .string "without man and without beast, and in\l"
    .string "all the cities thereof, shall be\l"
    .string "an habitation of shepherds causing\l"
    .string "their flocks to lie down.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_13::
    .string "In the cities of the mountains, in\n"
    .string "the cities of the vale, and in the\l"
    .string "cities of the south, and in the land\l"
    .string "of Benjamin, and in the places about\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and in the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, shall the flocks pass again\l"
    .string "under the hands of him that telleth\l"
    .string "them, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_14::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that I will perform that good\l"
    .string "thing which I have promised unto the\l"
    .string "house of Israel and to the house of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_15::
    .string "In those days, and at that time,\n"
    .string "will I cause the Branch of\l"
    .string "righteousness to grow up unto David;\l"
    .string "and he shall execute judgment and\l"
    .string "righteousness in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_16::
    .string "In those days shall Judah be saved,\n"
    .string "and Jerusalem shall dwell\l"
    .string "safely: and this is the name\l"
    .string "wherewith she shall be called, The\l"
    .string "LORD our righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_17::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; David\n"
    .string "shall never want a man to sit upon\l"
    .string "the throne of the house of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_18::
    .string "Neither shall the priests the\n"
    .string "Levites want a man before me to offer\l"
    .string "burnt offerings, and to kindle meat\l"
    .string "offerings, and to do sacrifice\l"
    .string "continually$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_19::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_20::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; If ye can break\n"
    .string "my covenant of the day, and my\l"
    .string "covenant of the night, and that there\l"
    .string "should not be day and night in their\l"
    .string "season;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_21::
    .string "Then may also my covenant be broken\n"
    .string "with David my servant, that he\l"
    .string "should not have a son to reign upon\l"
    .string "his throne; and with the Levites the\l"
    .string "priests, my ministers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_22::
    .string "As the host of heaven cannot be\n"
    .string "numbered, neither the sand of the sea\l"
    .string "measured: so will I multiply the\l"
    .string "seed of David my servant, and the\l"
    .string "Levites that minister unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_23::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "to Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_24::
    .string "Considerest thou not what this\n"
    .string "people have spoken, saying, The two\l"
    .string "families which the LORD hath chosen,\l"
    .string "he hath even cast them off? thus they\l"
    .string "have despised my people, that they\l"
    .string "should be no more a nation before\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_25::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; If my covenant\n"
    .string "be not with day and night, and if I\l"
    .string "have not appointed the ordinances\l"
    .string "of heaven and earth;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_33_26::
    .string "Then will I cast away the seed of\n"
    .string "Jacob and David my servant, so that I\l"
    .string "will not take any of his seed to be\l"
    .string "rulers over the seed of Abraham,\l"
    .string "Isaac, and Jacob: for I will cause\l"
    .string "their captivity to return, and have\l"
    .string "mercy on them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_1::
    .string "The word which came unto Jeremiah\n"
    .string "from the LORD, when Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon, and all his army,\l"
    .string "and all the kingdoms of the earth of\l"
    .string "his dominion, and all the people,\l"
    .string "fought against Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "against all the cities thereof,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel; Go and speak to Zedekiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, and tell him, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; Behold, I will give\l"
    .string "this city into the hand of the king\l"
    .string "of Babylon, and he shall burn it\l"
    .string "with fire:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_3::
    .string "And thou shalt not escape out of\n"
    .string "his hand, but shalt surely be taken,\l"
    .string "and delivered into his hand; and\l"
    .string "thine eyes shall behold the eyes of\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon, and he shall\l"
    .string "speak with thee mouth to mouth, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt go to Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_4::
    .string "Yet hear the word of the LORD, O\n"
    .string "Zedekiah king of Judah; Thus saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of thee, Thou shalt not die\l"
    .string "by the sword:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_5::
    .string "But thou shalt die in peace: and\n"
    .string "with the burnings of thy fathers, the\l"
    .string "former kings which were before thee,\l"
    .string "so shall they burn odours for thee;\l"
    .string "and they will lament thee, saying,\l"
    .string "Ah lord! for I have pronounced the\l"
    .string "word, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_6::
    .string "Then Jeremiah the prophet spake\n"
    .string "all these words unto Zedekiah king\l"
    .string "of Judah in Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_7::
    .string "When the king of Babylon’s army\n"
    .string "fought against Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "against all the cities of Judah\l"
    .string "that were left, against Lachish, and\l"
    .string "against Azekah: for these defenced\l"
    .string "cities remained of the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_8::
    .string "This is the word that came unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah from the LORD, after that\l"
    .string "the king Zedekiah had made a covenant\l"
    .string "with all the people which were at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, to proclaim liberty\l"
    .string "unto them;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_9::
    .string "That every man should let his\n"
    .string "manservant, and every man his\l"
    .string "maidservant, being an Hebrew or an\l"
    .string "Hebrewess, go free; that none should\l"
    .string "serve himself of them, to wit, of a\l"
    .string "Jew his brother$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_10::
    .string "Now when all the princes, and all\n"
    .string "the people, which had entered into\l"
    .string "the covenant, heard that every one\l"
    .string "should let his manservant, and\l"
    .string "every one his maidservant, go free,\l"
    .string "that none should serve themselves\l"
    .string "of them any more, then they obeyed,\l"
    .string "and let them go.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_11::
    .string "But afterward they turned, and\n"
    .string "caused the servants and the\l"
    .string "handmaids, whom they had let go\l"
    .string "free, to return, and brought them\l"
    .string "into subjection for servants and for\l"
    .string "handmaids.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_12::
    .string "Therefore the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_13::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel; I made a covenant with your\l"
    .string "fathers in the day that I brought\l"
    .string "them forth out of the land of Egypt,\l"
    .string "out of the house of bondmen, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_14::
    .string "At the end of seven years let ye go\n"
    .string "every man his brother an Hebrew,\l"
    .string "which hath been sold unto thee; and\l"
    .string "when he hath served thee six years,\l"
    .string "thou shalt let him go free from\l"
    .string "thee: but your fathers hearkened not\l"
    .string "unto me, neither inclined their ear$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_15::
    .string "And ye were now turned, and had done\n"
    .string "right in my sight, in proclaiming\l"
    .string "liberty every man to his neighbour;\l"
    .string "and ye had made a covenant before me\l"
    .string "in the house which is called by my\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_16::
    .string "But ye turned and polluted my\n"
    .string "name, and caused every man his\l"
    .string "servant, and every man his handmaid,\l"
    .string "whom ye had set at liberty at their\l"
    .string "pleasure, to return, and brought\l"
    .string "them into subjection, to be unto you\l"
    .string "for servants and for handmaids$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_17::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD; Ye\n"
    .string "have not hearkened unto me, in\l"
    .string "proclaiming liberty, every one to\l"
    .string "his brother, and every man to his\l"
    .string "neighbour: behold, I proclaim a\l"
    .string "liberty for you, saith the LORD, to\l"
    .string "the sword, to the pestilence, and to\l"
    .string "the famine; and I will make you to\l"
    .string "be removed into all the kingdoms of\l"
    .string "the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_18::
    .string "And I will give the men that have\n"
    .string "transgressed my covenant, which have\l"
    .string "not performed the words of the\l"
    .string "covenant which they had made before\l"
    .string "me, when they cut the calf in twain,\l"
    .string "and passed between the parts\l"
    .string "thereof,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_19::
    .string "The princes of Judah, and the\n"
    .string "princes of Jerusalem, the eunuchs,\l"
    .string "and the priests, and all the\l"
    .string "people of the land, which passed\l"
    .string "between the parts of the calf;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_20::
    .string "I will even give them into the hand\n"
    .string "of their enemies, and into the hand\l"
    .string "of them that seek their life: and\l"
    .string "their dead bodies shall be for meat\l"
    .string "unto the fowls of the heaven, and to\l"
    .string "the beasts of the earth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_21::
    .string "And Zedekiah king of Judah and his\n"
    .string "princes will I give into the hand of\l"
    .string "their enemies, and into the hand of\l"
    .string "them that seek their life, and into\l"
    .string "the hand of the king of Babylon’s\l"
    .string "army, which are gone up from you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_34_22::
    .string "Behold, I will command, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, and cause them to return to\l"
    .string "this city; and they shall fight\l"
    .string "against it, and take it, and burn it\l"
    .string "with fire: and I will make the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah a desolation without\l"
    .string "an inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_1::
    .string "The word which came unto Jeremiah\n"
    .string "from the LORD in the days of\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_2::
    .string "Go unto the house of the Rechabites,\n"
    .string "and speak unto them, and bring them\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD, into one\l"
    .string "of the chambers, and give them wine\l"
    .string "to drink$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_3::
    .string "Then I took Jaazaniah the son of\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, the son of Habaziniah, and\l"
    .string "his brethren, and all his sons, and\l"
    .string "the whole house of the Rechabites;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_4::
    .string "And I brought them into the house of\n"
    .string "the LORD, into the chamber of the\l"
    .string "sons of Hanan, the son of Igdaliah, a\l"
    .string "man of God, which was by the chamber\l"
    .string "of the princes, which was above the\l"
    .string "chamber of Maaseiah the son of\l"
    .string "Shallum, the keeper of the door:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_5::
    .string "And I set before the sons of the\n"
    .string "house of the Rechabites pots full\l"
    .string "of wine, and cups, and I said unto\l"
    .string "them, Drink ye wine$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_6::
    .string "But they said, We will drink no\n"
    .string "wine: for Jonadab the son of Rechab\l"
    .string "our father commanded us, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "shall drink no wine, neither ye, nor\l"
    .string "your sons for ever:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_7::
    .string "Neither shall ye build house, nor\n"
    .string "sow seed, nor plant vineyard, nor\l"
    .string "have any: but all your days ye\l"
    .string "shall dwell in tents; that ye may\l"
    .string "live many days in the land where ye\l"
    .string "be strangers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_8::
    .string "Thus have we obeyed the voice of\n"
    .string "Jonadab the son of Rechab our father\l"
    .string "in all that he hath charged us, to\l"
    .string "drink no wine all our days, we, our\l"
    .string "wives, our sons, nor our daughters;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_9::
    .string "Nor to build houses for us to\n"
    .string "dwell in: neither have we vineyard,\l"
    .string "nor field, nor seed:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_10::
    .string "But we have dwelt in tents, and have\n"
    .string "obeyed, and done according to all\l"
    .string "that Jonadab our father commanded us$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_11::
    .string "But it came to pass, when\n"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon came\l"
    .string "up into the land, that we said,\l"
    .string "Come, and let us go to Jerusalem for\l"
    .string "fear of the army of the Chaldeans,\l"
    .string "and for fear of the army of the\l"
    .string "Syrians: so we dwell at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_12::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_13::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; Go and tell the men\l"
    .string "of Judah and the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, Will ye not receive\l"
    .string "instruction to hearken to my words?\l"
    .string "saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_14::
    .string "The words of Jonadab the son of\n"
    .string "Rechab, that he commanded his sons\l"
    .string "not to drink wine, are performed;\l"
    .string "for unto this day they drink none,\l"
    .string "but obey their father’s commandment:\l"
    .string "notwithstanding I have spoken unto\l"
    .string "you, rising early and speaking; but\l"
    .string "ye hearkened not unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_15::
    .string "I have sent also unto you all my\n"
    .string "servants the prophets, rising up\l"
    .string "early and sending them, saying,\l"
    .string "Return ye now every man from his\l"
    .string "evil way, and amend your doings, and\l"
    .string "go not after other gods to serve\l"
    .string "them, and ye shall dwell in the\l"
    .string "land which I have given to you and to\l"
    .string "your fathers: but ye have not\l"
    .string "inclined your ear, nor hearkened\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_16::
    .string "Because the sons of Jonadab the son\n"
    .string "of Rechab have performed the\l"
    .string "commandment of their father, which he\l"
    .string "commanded them; but this people\l"
    .string "hath not hearkened unto me:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_17::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD God of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I\l"
    .string "will bring upon Judah and upon\l"
    .string "all the inhabitants of Jerusalem\l"
    .string "all the evil that I have\l"
    .string "pronounced against them: because I\l"
    .string "have spoken unto them, but they have\l"
    .string "not heard; and I have called unto\l"
    .string "them, but they have not answered$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_18::
    .string "And Jeremiah said unto the house of\n"
    .string "the Rechabites, Thus saith the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts, the God of Israel; Because\l"
    .string "ye have obeyed the commandment of\l"
    .string "Jonadab your father, and kept all\l"
    .string "his precepts, and done according\l"
    .string "unto all that he hath commanded you:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_35_19::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Jonadab\l"
    .string "the son of Rechab shall not want a\l"
    .string "man to stand before me for ever$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the fourth\n"
    .string "year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, that this word came\l"
    .string "unto Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_2::
    .string "Take thee a roll of a book, and\n"
    .string "write therein all the words that I\l"
    .string "have spoken unto thee against\l"
    .string "Israel, and against Judah, and\l"
    .string "against all the nations, from the\l"
    .string "day I spake unto thee, from the days\l"
    .string "of Josiah, even unto this day$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_3::
    .string "It may be that the house of Judah\n"
    .string "will hear all the evil which I\l"
    .string "purpose to do unto them; that they\l"
    .string "may return every man from his evil\l"
    .string "way; that I may forgive their\l"
    .string "iniquity and their sin.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_4::
    .string "Then Jeremiah called Baruch the\n"
    .string "son of Neriah: and Baruch wrote from\l"
    .string "the mouth of Jeremiah all the words\l"
    .string "of the LORD, which he had spoken unto\l"
    .string "him, upon a roll of a book.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_5::
    .string "And Jeremiah commanded Baruch,\n"
    .string "saying, I am shut up; I cannot go\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_6::
    .string "Therefore go thou, and read in the\n"
    .string "roll, which thou hast written from\l"
    .string "my mouth, the words of the LORD in the\l"
    .string "ears of the people in the LORD’s\l"
    .string "house upon the fasting day: and also\l"
    .string "thou shalt read them in the ears of\l"
    .string "all Judah that come out of their\l"
    .string "cities$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_7::
    .string "It may be they will present their\n"
    .string "supplication before the LORD, and\l"
    .string "will return every one from his evil\l"
    .string "way: for great is the anger and the\l"
    .string "fury that the LORD hath pronounced\l"
    .string "against this people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_8::
    .string "And Baruch the son of Neriah did\n"
    .string "according to all that Jeremiah the\l"
    .string "prophet commanded him, reading in\l"
    .string "the book the words of the LORD in the\l"
    .string "LORD’s house.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_9::
    .string "And it came to pass in the fifth\n"
    .string "year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah, in the ninth month,\l"
    .string "that they proclaimed a fast before\l"
    .string "the LORD to all the people in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and to all the people\l"
    .string "that came from the cities of Judah\l"
    .string "unto Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_10::
    .string "Then read Baruch in the book the\n"
    .string "words of Jeremiah in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, in the chamber of Gemariah the\l"
    .string "son of Shaphan the scribe, in the\l"
    .string "higher court, at the entry of the new\l"
    .string "gate of the LORD’s house, in the ears\l"
    .string "of all the people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_11::
    .string "When Michaiah the son of Gemariah,\n"
    .string "the son of Shaphan, had heard out of\l"
    .string "the book all the words of the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_12::
    .string "Then he went down into the king’s\n"
    .string "house, into the scribe’s chamber:\l"
    .string "and, lo, all the princes sat there,\l"
    .string "even Elishama the scribe, and\l"
    .string "Delaiah the son of Shemaiah, and\l"
    .string "Elnathan the son of Achbor, and\l"
    .string "Gemariah the son of Shaphan, and\l"
    .string "Zedekiah the son of Hananiah, and\l"
    .string "all the princes$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_13::
    .string "Then Michaiah declared unto them\n"
    .string "all the words that he had heard,\l"
    .string "when Baruch read the book in the ears\l"
    .string "of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_14::
    .string "Therefore all the princes sent\n"
    .string "Jehudi the son of Nethaniah, the son\l"
    .string "of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, unto\l"
    .string "Baruch, saying, Take in thine hand\l"
    .string "the roll wherein thou hast read in\l"
    .string "the ears of the people, and come.\l"
    .string "So Baruch the son of Neriah took the\l"
    .string "roll in his hand, and came unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_15::
    .string "And they said unto him, Sit down\n"
    .string "now, and read it in our ears. So\l"
    .string "Baruch read it in their ears.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_16::
    .string "Now it came to pass, when they had\n"
    .string "heard all the words, they were\l"
    .string "afraid both one and other, and said\l"
    .string "unto Baruch, We will surely tell\l"
    .string "the king of all these words.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_17::
    .string "And they asked Baruch, saying,\n"
    .string "Tell us now, How didst thou write\l"
    .string "all these words at his mouth?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_18::
    .string "Then Baruch answered them, He\n"
    .string "pronounced all these words unto me\l"
    .string "with his mouth, and I wrote them with\l"
    .string "ink in the book$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_19::
    .string "Then said the princes unto Baruch,\n"
    .string "Go, hide thee, thou and Jeremiah; and\l"
    .string "let no man know where ye be.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_20::
    .string "And they went in to the king into\n"
    .string "the court, but they laid up the\l"
    .string "roll in the chamber of Elishama the\l"
    .string "scribe, and told all the words in\l"
    .string "the ears of the king.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_21::
    .string "So the king sent Jehudi to fetch the\n"
    .string "roll: and he took it out of\l"
    .string "Elishama the scribe’s chamber. And\l"
    .string "Jehudi read it in the ears of the\l"
    .string "king, and in the ears of all the\l"
    .string "princes which stood beside the king.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_22::
    .string "Now the king sat in the winterhouse\n"
    .string "in the ninth month: and there was a\l"
    .string "fire on the hearth burning before him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when\n"
    .string "Jehudi had read three or four\l"
    .string "leaves, he cut it with the penknife,\l"
    .string "and cast it into the fire that was on\l"
    .string "the hearth, until all the roll was\l"
    .string "consumed in the fire that was on the\l"
    .string "hearth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_24::
    .string "Yet they were not afraid, nor rent\n"
    .string "their garments, neither the king, nor\l"
    .string "any of his servants that heard all\l"
    .string "these words.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_25::
    .string "Nevertheless Elnathan and Delaiah\n"
    .string "and Gemariah had made intercession\l"
    .string "to the king that he would not burn\l"
    .string "the roll: but he would not hear\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_26::
    .string "But the king commanded Jerahmeel\n"
    .string "the son of Hammelech, and Seraiah\l"
    .string "the son of Azriel, and Shelemiah the\l"
    .string "son of Abdeel, to take Baruch the\l"
    .string "scribe and Jeremiah the prophet:\l"
    .string "but the LORD hid them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_27::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, after that the king had\l"
    .string "burned the roll, and the words which\l"
    .string "Baruch wrote at the mouth of\l"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_28::
    .string "Take thee again another roll, and\n"
    .string "write in it all the former words\l"
    .string "that were in the first roll, which\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim the king of Judah hath\l"
    .string "burned$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_29::
    .string "And thou shalt say to Jehoiakim\n"
    .string "king of Judah, Thus saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "Thou hast burned this roll, saying,\l"
    .string "Why hast thou written therein,\l"
    .string "saying, The king of Babylon shall\l"
    .string "certainly come and destroy this\l"
    .string "land, and shall cause to cease from\l"
    .string "thence man and beast?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_30::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim king of Judah; He shall\l"
    .string "have none to sit upon the throne of\l"
    .string "David: and his dead body shall be\l"
    .string "cast out in the day to the heat, and\l"
    .string "in the night to the frost$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_31::
    .string "And I will punish him and his seed\n"
    .string "and his servants for their iniquity;\l"
    .string "and I will bring upon them, and\l"
    .string "upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and upon the men of Judah, all the\l"
    .string "evil that I have pronounced against\l"
    .string "them; but they hearkened not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_36_32::
    .string "Then took Jeremiah another roll,\n"
    .string "and gave it to Baruch the scribe, the\l"
    .string "son of Neriah; who wrote therein from\l"
    .string "the mouth of Jeremiah all the words\l"
    .string "of the book which Jehoiakim king of\l"
    .string "Judah had burned in the fire: and\l"
    .string "there were added besides unto them\l"
    .string "many like words.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_1::
    .string "And king Zedekiah the son of Josiah\n"
    .string "reigned instead of Coniah the son of\l"
    .string "Jehoiakim, whom Nebuchadrezzar king\l"
    .string "of Babylon made king in the land of\l"
    .string "Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_2::
    .string "But neither he, nor his servants,\n"
    .string "nor the people of the land, did\l"
    .string "hearken unto the words of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which he spake by the prophet\l"
    .string "Jeremiah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_3::
    .string "And Zedekiah the king sent Jehucal\n"
    .string "the son of Shelemiah and Zephaniah\l"
    .string "the son of Maaseiah the priest to\l"
    .string "the prophet Jeremiah, saying, Pray\l"
    .string "now unto the LORD our God for us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_4::
    .string "Now Jeremiah came in and went out\n"
    .string "among the people: for they had not\l"
    .string "put him into prison.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_5::
    .string "Then Pharaoh’s army was come forth\n"
    .string "out of Egypt: and when the Chaldeans\l"
    .string "that besieged Jerusalem heard\l"
    .string "tidings of them, they departed from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_6::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "the prophet Jeremiah saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_7::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel; Thus shall ye say to the\l"
    .string "king of Judah, that sent you unto me\l"
    .string "to enquire of me; Behold, Pharaoh’s\l"
    .string "army, which is come forth to help\l"
    .string "you, shall return to Egypt into\l"
    .string "their own land$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_8::
    .string "And the Chaldeans shall come\n"
    .string "again, and fight against this city,\l"
    .string "and take it, and burn it with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_9::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Deceive not\n"
    .string "yourselves, saying, The Chaldeans\l"
    .string "shall surely depart from us: for\l"
    .string "they shall not depart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_10::
    .string "For though ye had smitten the whole\n"
    .string "army of the Chaldeans that fight\l"
    .string "against you, and there remained but\l"
    .string "wounded men among them, yet should\l"
    .string "they rise up every man in his tent,\l"
    .string "and burn this city with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when the\n"
    .string "army of the Chaldeans was broken up\l"
    .string "from Jerusalem for fear of Pharaoh’s\l"
    .string "army,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_12::
    .string "Then Jeremiah went forth out of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem to go into the land of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, to separate himself\l"
    .string "thence in the midst of the people$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_13::
    .string "And when he was in the gate of\n"
    .string "Benjamin, a captain of the ward was\l"
    .string "there, whose name was Irijah, the son\l"
    .string "of Shelemiah, the son of Hananiah;\l"
    .string "and he took Jeremiah the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying, Thou fallest away to the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_14::
    .string "Then said Jeremiah, It is false; I\n"
    .string "fall not away to the Chaldeans. But\l"
    .string "he hearkened not to him: so Irijah\l"
    .string "took Jeremiah, and brought him to the\l"
    .string "princes.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_15::
    .string "Wherefore the princes were wroth\n"
    .string "with Jeremiah, and smote him, and\l"
    .string "put him in prison in the house of\l"
    .string "Jonathan the scribe: for they had\l"
    .string "made that the prison.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_16::
    .string "When Jeremiah was entered into the\n"
    .string "dungeon, and into the cabins, and\l"
    .string "Jeremiah had remained there many\l"
    .string "days;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_17::
    .string "Then Zedekiah the king sent, and\n"
    .string "took him out: and the king asked him\l"
    .string "secretly in his house, and said, Is\l"
    .string "there any word from the LORD? And\l"
    .string "Jeremiah said, There is: for, said\l"
    .string "he, thou shalt be delivered into the\l"
    .string "hand of the king of Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_18::
    .string "Moreover Jeremiah said unto king\n"
    .string "Zedekiah, What have I offended\l"
    .string "against thee, or against thy\l"
    .string "servants, or against this people,\l"
    .string "that ye have put me in prison?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_19::
    .string "Where are now your prophets which\n"
    .string "prophesied unto you, saying, The\l"
    .string "king of Babylon shall not come\l"
    .string "against you, nor against this land?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_20::
    .string "Therefore hear now, I pray thee, O\n"
    .string "my lord the king: let my\l"
    .string "supplication, I pray thee, be\l"
    .string "accepted before thee; that thou\l"
    .string "cause me not to return to the house\l"
    .string "of Jonathan the scribe, lest I die\l"
    .string "there$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_37_21::
    .string "Then Zedekiah the king commanded\n"
    .string "that they should commit Jeremiah\l"
    .string "into the court of the prison, and\l"
    .string "that they should give him daily a\l"
    .string "piece of bread out of the bakers’\l"
    .string "street, until all the bread in the\l"
    .string "city were spent. Thus Jeremiah\l"
    .string "remained in the court of the prison.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_1::
    .string "Then Shephatiah the son of Mattan,\n"
    .string "and Gedaliah the son of Pashur, and\l"
    .string "Jucal the son of Shelemiah, and\l"
    .string "Pashur the son of Malchiah, heard\l"
    .string "the words that Jeremiah had spoken\l"
    .string "unto all the people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, He that\n"
    .string "remaineth in this city shall die by\l"
    .string "the sword, by the famine, and by the\l"
    .string "pestilence: but he that goeth forth\l"
    .string "to the Chaldeans shall live; for\l"
    .string "he shall have his life for a prey,\l"
    .string "and shall live$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_3::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, This city\n"
    .string "shall surely be given into the hand\l"
    .string "of the king of Babylon’s army, which\l"
    .string "shall take it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_4::
    .string "Therefore the princes said unto the\n"
    .string "king, We beseech thee, let this man\l"
    .string "be put to death: for thus he\l"
    .string "weakeneth the hands of the men of war\l"
    .string "that remain in this city, and the\l"
    .string "hands of all the people, in\l"
    .string "speaking such words unto them: for\l"
    .string "this man seeketh not the welfare of\l"
    .string "this people, but the hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_5::
    .string "Then Zedekiah the king said,\n"
    .string "Behold, he is in your hand: for the\l"
    .string "king is not he that can do any thing\l"
    .string "against you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_6::
    .string "Then took they Jeremiah, and cast\n"
    .string "him into the dungeon of Malchiah the\l"
    .string "son of Hammelech, that was in the\l"
    .string "court of the prison: and they let\l"
    .string "down Jeremiah with cords. And in the\l"
    .string "dungeon there was no water, but mire:\l"
    .string "so Jeremiah sunk in the mire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_7::
    .string "Now when Ebedmelech the Ethiopian,\n"
    .string "one of the eunuchs which was in the\l"
    .string "king’s house, heard that they had\l"
    .string "put Jeremiah in the dungeon; the king\l"
    .string "then sitting in the gate of Benjamin;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_8::
    .string "Ebedmelech went forth out of the\n"
    .string "king’s house, and spake to the king\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_9::
    .string "My lord the king, these men have\n"
    .string "done evil in all that they have\l"
    .string "done to Jeremiah the prophet, whom\l"
    .string "they have cast into the dungeon; and\l"
    .string "he is like to die for hunger in the\l"
    .string "place where he is: for there is no\l"
    .string "more bread in the city$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_10::
    .string "Then the king commanded Ebedmelech\n"
    .string "the Ethiopian, saying, Take from\l"
    .string "hence thirty men with thee, and take\l"
    .string "up Jeremiah the prophet out of the\l"
    .string "dungeon, before he die.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_11::
    .string "So Ebedmelech took the men with\n"
    .string "him, and went into the house of the\l"
    .string "king under the treasury, and took\l"
    .string "thence old cast clouts and old\l"
    .string "rotten rags, and let them down by\l"
    .string "cords into the dungeon to Jeremiah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_12::
    .string "And Ebedmelech the Ethiopian said\n"
    .string "unto Jeremiah, Put now these old\l"
    .string "cast clouts and rotten rags under\l"
    .string "thine armholes under the cords. And\l"
    .string "Jeremiah did so.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_13::
    .string "So they drew up Jeremiah with\n"
    .string "cords, and took him up out of the\l"
    .string "dungeon: and Jeremiah remained in the\l"
    .string "court of the prison.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_14::
    .string "Then Zedekiah the king sent, and\n"
    .string "took Jeremiah the prophet unto him\l"
    .string "into the third entry that is in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD: and the king said\l"
    .string "unto Jeremiah, I will ask thee a\l"
    .string "thing; hide nothing from me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_15::
    .string "Then Jeremiah said unto Zedekiah, If\n"
    .string "I declare it unto thee, wilt thou\l"
    .string "not surely put me to death? and if I\l"
    .string "give thee counsel, wilt thou not\l"
    .string "hearken unto me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_16::
    .string "So Zedekiah the king sware secretly\n"
    .string "unto Jeremiah, saying, As the LORD\l"
    .string "liveth, that made us this soul, I\l"
    .string "will not put thee to death, neither\l"
    .string "will I give thee into the hand of\l"
    .string "these men that seek thy life$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_17::
    .string "Then said Jeremiah unto Zedekiah,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\l"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; If thou\l"
    .string "wilt assuredly go forth unto the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon’s princes, then thy\l"
    .string "soul shall live, and this city\l"
    .string "shall not be burned with fire; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt live, and thine house:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_18::
    .string "But if thou wilt not go forth to the\n"
    .string "king of Babylon’s princes, then\l"
    .string "shall this city be given into the\l"
    .string "hand of the Chaldeans, and they\l"
    .string "shall burn it with fire, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt not escape out of their hand$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_19::
    .string "And Zedekiah the king said unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, I am afraid of the Jews\l"
    .string "that are fallen to the Chaldeans,\l"
    .string "lest they deliver me into their\l"
    .string "hand, and they mock me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_20::
    .string "But Jeremiah said, They shall not\n"
    .string "deliver thee. Obey, I beseech thee,\l"
    .string "the voice of the LORD, which I speak\l"
    .string "unto thee: so it shall be well unto\l"
    .string "thee, and thy soul shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_21::
    .string "But if thou refuse to go forth, this\n"
    .string "is the word that the LORD hath shewed\l"
    .string "me:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_22::
    .string "And, behold, all the women that\n"
    .string "are left in the king of Judah’s\l"
    .string "house shall be brought forth to the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon’s princes, and\l"
    .string "those women shall say, Thy friends\l"
    .string "have set thee on, and have prevailed\l"
    .string "against thee: thy feet are sunk in\l"
    .string "the mire, and they are turned away\l"
    .string "back$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_23::
    .string "So they shall bring out all thy\n"
    .string "wives and thy children to the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans: and thou shalt not\l"
    .string "escape out of their hand, but shalt\l"
    .string "be taken by the hand of the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon: and thou shalt cause this\l"
    .string "city to be burned with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_24::
    .string "Then said Zedekiah unto Jeremiah,\n"
    .string "Let no man know of these words, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt not die.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_25::
    .string "But if the princes hear that I have\n"
    .string "talked with thee, and they come unto\l"
    .string "thee, and say unto thee, Declare\l"
    .string "unto us now what thou hast said unto\l"
    .string "the king, hide it not from us, and we\l"
    .string "will not put thee to death; also\l"
    .string "what the king said unto thee:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_26::
    .string "Then thou shalt say unto them, I\n"
    .string "presented my supplication before\l"
    .string "the king, that he would not cause me\l"
    .string "to return to Jonathan’s house, to die\l"
    .string "there$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_27::
    .string "Then came all the princes unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, and asked him: and he told\l"
    .string "them according to all these words\l"
    .string "that the king had commanded. So they\l"
    .string "left off speaking with him; for the\l"
    .string "matter was not perceived.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_38_28::
    .string "So Jeremiah abode in the court of\n"
    .string "the prison until the day that\l"
    .string "Jerusalem was taken: and he was\l"
    .string "there when Jerusalem was taken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_1::
    .string "In the ninth year of Zedekiah king\n"
    .string "of Judah, in the tenth month, came\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon and\l"
    .string "all his army against Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "they besieged it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_2::
    .string "And in the eleventh year of\n"
    .string "Zedekiah, in the fourth month, the\l"
    .string "ninth day of the month, the city was\l"
    .string "broken up.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_3::
    .string "And all the princes of the king of\n"
    .string "Babylon came in, and sat in the\l"
    .string "middle gate, even Nergalsharezer,\l"
    .string "Samgarnebo, Sarsechim, Rabsaris,\l"
    .string "Nergalsharezer, Rabmag, with all\l"
    .string "the residue of the princes of the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when\n"
    .string "Zedekiah the king of Judah saw them,\l"
    .string "and all the men of war, then they\l"
    .string "fled, and went forth out of the city\l"
    .string "by night, by the way of the king’s\l"
    .string "garden, by the gate betwixt the two\l"
    .string "walls: and he went out the way of\l"
    .string "the plain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_5::
    .string "But the Chaldeans’ army pursued\n"
    .string "after them, and overtook Zedekiah in\l"
    .string "the plains of Jericho: and when they\l"
    .string "had taken him, they brought him up to\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon to\l"
    .string "Riblah in the land of Hamath, where\l"
    .string "he gave judgment upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_6::
    .string "Then the king of Babylon slew the\n"
    .string "sons of Zedekiah in Riblah before\l"
    .string "his eyes: also the king of Babylon\l"
    .string "slew all the nobles of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_7::
    .string "Moreover he put out Zedekiah’s\n"
    .string "eyes, and bound him with chains, to\l"
    .string "carry him to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_8::
    .string "And the Chaldeans burned the king’s\n"
    .string "house, and the houses of the\l"
    .string "people, with fire, and brake down\l"
    .string "the walls of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_9::
    .string "Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard carried away captive into\l"
    .string "Babylon the remnant of the people\l"
    .string "that remained in the city, and those\l"
    .string "that fell away, that fell to him,\l"
    .string "with the rest of the people that\l"
    .string "remained.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_10::
    .string "But Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard left of the poor of the\l"
    .string "people, which had nothing, in the\l"
    .string "land of Judah, and gave them\l"
    .string "vineyards and fields at the same\l"
    .string "time.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_11::
    .string "Now Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon\n"
    .string "gave charge concerning Jeremiah to\l"
    .string "Nebuzaradan the captain of the\l"
    .string "guard, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_12::
    .string "Take him, and look well to him,\n"
    .string "and do him no harm; but do unto him\l"
    .string "even as he shall say unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_13::
    .string "So Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard sent, and Nebushasban,\l"
    .string "Rabsaris, and Nergalsharezer,\l"
    .string "Rabmag, and all the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon’s princes;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_14::
    .string "Even they sent, and took Jeremiah\n"
    .string "out of the court of the prison, and\l"
    .string "committed him unto Gedaliah the son\l"
    .string "of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, that he\l"
    .string "should carry him home: so he dwelt\l"
    .string "among the people$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_15::
    .string "Now the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, while he was shut up in\l"
    .string "the court of the prison, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_16::
    .string "Go and speak to Ebedmelech the\n"
    .string "Ethiopian, saying, Thus saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, the God of Israel;\l"
    .string "Behold, I will bring my words upon\l"
    .string "this city for evil, and not for good;\l"
    .string "and they shall be accomplished in\l"
    .string "that day before thee$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_17::
    .string "But I will deliver thee in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD: and thou shalt\l"
    .string "not be given into the hand of the men\l"
    .string "of whom thou art afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_39_18::
    .string "For I will surely deliver thee,\n"
    .string "and thou shalt not fall by the\l"
    .string "sword, but thy life shall be for a\l"
    .string "prey unto thee: because thou hast\l"
    .string "put thy trust in me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah from\n"
    .string "the LORD, after that Nebuzaradan the\l"
    .string "captain of the guard had let him go\l"
    .string "from Ramah, when he had taken him\l"
    .string "being bound in chains among all\l"
    .string "that were carried away captive of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem and Judah, which were\l"
    .string "carried away captive unto Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_2::
    .string "And the captain of the guard took\n"
    .string "Jeremiah, and said unto him, The LORD\l"
    .string "thy God hath pronounced this evil\l"
    .string "upon this place.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_3::
    .string "Now the LORD hath brought it, and\n"
    .string "done according as he hath said:\l"
    .string "because ye have sinned against the\l"
    .string "LORD, and have not obeyed his voice,\l"
    .string "therefore this thing is come upon\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_4::
    .string "And now, behold, I loose thee this\n"
    .string "day from the chains which were upon\l"
    .string "thine hand. If it seem good unto thee\l"
    .string "to come with me into Babylon, come;\l"
    .string "and I will look well unto thee:\l"
    .string "but if it seem ill unto thee to come\l"
    .string "with me into Babylon, forbear:\l"
    .string "behold, all the land is before\l"
    .string "thee: whither it seemeth good and\l"
    .string "convenient for thee to go, thither go.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_5::
    .string "Now while he was not yet gone back,\n"
    .string "he said, Go back also to Gedaliah\l"
    .string "the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan,\l"
    .string "whom the king of Babylon hath made\l"
    .string "governor over the cities of Judah,\l"
    .string "and dwell with him among the\l"
    .string "people: or go wheresoever it\l"
    .string "seemeth convenient unto thee to go.\l"
    .string "So the captain of the guard gave him\l"
    .string "victuals and a reward, and let him\l"
    .string "go.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_6::
    .string "Then went Jeremiah unto Gedaliah\n"
    .string "the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and\l"
    .string "dwelt with him among the people\l"
    .string "that were left in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_7::
    .string "Now when all the captains of the\n"
    .string "forces which were in the fields,\l"
    .string "even they and their men, heard that\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon had made\l"
    .string "Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor\l"
    .string "in the land, and had committed unto\l"
    .string "him men, and women, and children, and\l"
    .string "of the poor of the land, of them\l"
    .string "that were not carried away captive\l"
    .string "to Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_8::
    .string "Then they came to Gedaliah to\n"
    .string "Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah, and Johanan and Jonathan\l"
    .string "the sons of Kareah, and Seraiah the\l"
    .string "son of Tanhumeth, and the sons of\l"
    .string "Ephai the Netophathite, and\l"
    .string "Jezaniah the son of a Maachathite,\l"
    .string "they and their men$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_9::
    .string "And Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the\n"
    .string "son of Shaphan sware unto them and\l"
    .string "to their men, saying, Fear not to\l"
    .string "serve the Chaldeans: dwell in the\l"
    .string "land, and serve the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "and it shall be well with you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_10::
    .string "As for me, behold, I will dwell\n"
    .string "at Mizpah, to serve the Chaldeans,\l"
    .string "which will come unto us: but ye,\l"
    .string "gather ye wine, and summer fruits,\l"
    .string "and oil, and put them in your\l"
    .string "vessels, and dwell in your cities\l"
    .string "that ye have taken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_11::
    .string "Likewise when all the Jews that\n"
    .string "were in Moab, and among the\l"
    .string "Ammonites, and in Edom, and that were\l"
    .string "in all the countries, heard that the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon had left a remnant\l"
    .string "of Judah, and that he had set over\l"
    .string "them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the\l"
    .string "son of Shaphan;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_12::
    .string "Even all the Jews returned out of\n"
    .string "all places whither they were\l"
    .string "driven, and came to the land of\l"
    .string "Judah, to Gedaliah, unto Mizpah, and\l"
    .string "gathered wine and summer fruits very\l"
    .string "much$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_13::
    .string "Moreover Johanan the son of Kareah,\n"
    .string "and all the captains of the forces\l"
    .string "that were in the fields, came to\l"
    .string "Gedaliah to Mizpah,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_14::
    .string "And said unto him, Dost thou\n"
    .string "certainly know that Baalis the king\l"
    .string "of the Ammonites hath sent Ishmael\l"
    .string "the son of Nethaniah to slay thee?\l"
    .string "But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam\l"
    .string "believed them not$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_15::
    .string "Then Johanan the son of Kareah\n"
    .string "spake to Gedaliah in Mizpah\l"
    .string "secretly saying, Let me go, I pray\l"
    .string "thee, and I will slay Ishmael the\l"
    .string "son of Nethaniah, and no man shall\l"
    .string "know it: wherefore should he slay\l"
    .string "thee, that all the Jews which are\l"
    .string "gathered unto thee should be\l"
    .string "scattered, and the remnant in Judah\l"
    .string "perish?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_40_16::
    .string "But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam said\n"
    .string "unto Johanan the son of Kareah, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt not do this thing: for thou\l"
    .string "speakest falsely of Ishmael$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the seventh\n"
    .string "month, that Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah the son of Elishama, of\l"
    .string "the seed royal, and the princes of\l"
    .string "the king, even ten men with him, came\l"
    .string "unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to\l"
    .string "Mizpah; and there they did eat bread\l"
    .string "together in Mizpah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_2::
    .string "Then arose Ishmael the son of\n"
    .string "Nethaniah, and the ten men that were\l"
    .string "with him, and smote Gedaliah the son\l"
    .string "of Ahikam the son of Shaphan with\l"
    .string "the sword, and slew him, whom the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon had made governor\l"
    .string "over the land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_3::
    .string "Ishmael also slew all the Jews\n"
    .string "that were with him, even with\l"
    .string "Gedaliah, at Mizpah, and the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans that were found there, and\l"
    .string "the men of war.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_4::
    .string "And it came to pass the second day\n"
    .string "after he had slain Gedaliah, and no\l"
    .string "man knew it,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_5::
    .string "That there came certain from\n"
    .string "Shechem, from Shiloh, and from\l"
    .string "Samaria, even fourscore men, having\l"
    .string "their beards shaven, and their\l"
    .string "clothes rent, and having cut\l"
    .string "themselves, with offerings and\l"
    .string "incense in their hand, to bring them\l"
    .string "to the house of the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_6::
    .string "And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah\n"
    .string "went forth from Mizpah to meet them,\l"
    .string "weeping all along as he went: and\l"
    .string "it came to pass, as he met them, he\l"
    .string "said unto them, Come to Gedaliah the\l"
    .string "son of Ahikam.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_7::
    .string "And it was so, when they came into\n"
    .string "the midst of the city, that Ishmael\l"
    .string "the son of Nethaniah slew them, and\l"
    .string "cast them into the midst of the pit,\l"
    .string "he, and the men that were with him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_8::
    .string "But ten men were found among them\n"
    .string "that said unto Ishmael, Slay us not:\l"
    .string "for we have treasures in the field,\l"
    .string "of wheat, and of barley, and of oil,\l"
    .string "and of honey. So he forbare, and slew\l"
    .string "them not among their brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_9::
    .string "Now the pit wherein Ishmael had\n"
    .string "cast all the dead bodies of the men,\l"
    .string "whom he had slain because of\l"
    .string "Gedaliah, was it which Asa the king\l"
    .string "had made for fear of Baasha king of\l"
    .string "Israel: and Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah filled it with them that\l"
    .string "were slain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_10::
    .string "Then Ishmael carried away captive\n"
    .string "all the residue of the people\l"
    .string "that were in Mizpah, even the king’s\l"
    .string "daughters, and all the people\l"
    .string "that remained in Mizpah, whom\l"
    .string "Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard\l"
    .string "had committed to Gedaliah the son of\l"
    .string "Ahikam: and Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah carried them away captive,\l"
    .string "and departed to go over to the\l"
    .string "Ammonites.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_11::
    .string "But when Johanan the son of Kareah,\n"
    .string "and all the captains of the forces\l"
    .string "that were with him, heard of all the\l"
    .string "evil that Ishmael the son of\l"
    .string "Nethaniah had done,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_12::
    .string "Then they took all the men, and\n"
    .string "went to fight with Ishmael the son\l"
    .string "of Nethaniah, and found him by the\l"
    .string "great waters that are in Gibeon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_13::
    .string "Now it came to pass, that when all\n"
    .string "the people which were with Ishmael\l"
    .string "saw Johanan the son of Kareah, and\l"
    .string "all the captains of the forces that\l"
    .string "were with him, then they were glad.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_14::
    .string "So all the people that Ishmael\n"
    .string "had carried away captive from\l"
    .string "Mizpah cast about and returned, and\l"
    .string "went unto Johanan the son of Kareah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_15::
    .string "But Ishmael the son of Nethaniah\n"
    .string "escaped from Johanan with eight men,\l"
    .string "and went to the Ammonites.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_16::
    .string "Then took Johanan the son of Kareah,\n"
    .string "and all the captains of the forces\l"
    .string "that were with him, all the remnant\l"
    .string "of the people whom he had recovered\l"
    .string "from Ishmael the son of Nethaniah,\l"
    .string "from Mizpah, after that he had slain\l"
    .string "Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, even\l"
    .string "mighty men of war, and the women, and\l"
    .string "the children, and the eunuchs, whom\l"
    .string "he had brought again from Gibeon:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_17::
    .string "And they departed, and dwelt in the\n"
    .string "habitation of Chimham, which is by\l"
    .string "Bethlehem, to go to enter into\l"
    .string "Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_41_18::
    .string "Because of the Chaldeans: for they\n"
    .string "were afraid of them, because Ishmael\l"
    .string "the son of Nethaniah had slain\l"
    .string "Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, whom the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon made governor in the\l"
    .string "land$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_1::
    .string "Then all the captains of the\n"
    .string "forces, and Johanan the son of\l"
    .string "Kareah, and Jezaniah the son of\l"
    .string "Hoshaiah, and all the people from\l"
    .string "the least even unto the greatest,\l"
    .string "came near,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_2::
    .string "And said unto Jeremiah the\n"
    .string "prophet, Let, we beseech thee, our\l"
    .string "supplication be accepted before\l"
    .string "thee, and pray for us unto the LORD\l"
    .string "thy God, even for all this remnant;\l"
    .string "(for we are left but a few of many,\l"
    .string "as thine eyes do behold us:)"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_3::
    .string "That the LORD thy God may shew us\n"
    .string "the way wherein we may walk, and the\l"
    .string "thing that we may do$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_4::
    .string "Then Jeremiah the prophet said\n"
    .string "unto them, I have heard you; behold,\l"
    .string "I will pray unto the LORD your God\l"
    .string "according to your words; and it\l"
    .string "shall come to pass, that whatsoever\l"
    .string "thing the LORD shall answer you, I\l"
    .string "will declare it unto you; I will\l"
    .string "keep nothing back from you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_5::
    .string "Then they said to Jeremiah, The LORD\n"
    .string "be a true and faithful witness\l"
    .string "between us, if we do not even\l"
    .string "according to all things for the\l"
    .string "which the LORD thy God shall send\l"
    .string "thee to us.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_6::
    .string "Whether it be good, or whether it be\n"
    .string "evil, we will obey the voice of the\l"
    .string "LORD our God, to whom we send thee;\l"
    .string "that it may be well with us, when we\l"
    .string "obey the voice of the LORD our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_7::
    .string "And it came to pass after ten days,\n"
    .string "that the word of the LORD came unto\l"
    .string "Jeremiah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_8::
    .string "Then called he Johanan the son of\n"
    .string "Kareah, and all the captains of the\l"
    .string "forces which were with him, and all\l"
    .string "the people from the least even to\l"
    .string "the greatest,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_9::
    .string "And said unto them, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, the God of Israel, unto whom ye\l"
    .string "sent me to present your\l"
    .string "supplication before him;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_10::
    .string "If ye will still abide in this\n"
    .string "land, then will I build you, and\l"
    .string "not pull you down, and I will\l"
    .string "plant you, and not pluck you up:\l"
    .string "for I repent me of the evil that I\l"
    .string "have done unto you$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_11::
    .string "Be not afraid of the king of\n"
    .string "Babylon, of whom ye are afraid; be\l"
    .string "not afraid of him, saith the LORD:\l"
    .string "for I am with you to save you, and to\l"
    .string "deliver you from his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_12::
    .string "And I will shew mercies unto you,\n"
    .string "that he may have mercy upon you, and\l"
    .string "cause you to return to your own land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_13::
    .string "But if ye say, We will not dwell\n"
    .string "in this land, neither obey the voice\l"
    .string "of the LORD your God,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_14::
    .string "Saying, No; but we will go into the\n"
    .string "land of Egypt, where we shall see\l"
    .string "no war, nor hear the sound of the\l"
    .string "trumpet, nor have hunger of bread;\l"
    .string "and there will we dwell:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_15::
    .string "And now therefore hear the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD, ye remnant of Judah; Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts, the God of\l"
    .string "Israel; If ye wholly set your faces\l"
    .string "to enter into Egypt, and go to\l"
    .string "sojourn there;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_16::
    .string "Then it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "the sword, which ye feared, shall\l"
    .string "overtake you there in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and the famine, whereof ye\l"
    .string "were afraid, shall follow close\l"
    .string "after you there in Egypt; and there\l"
    .string "ye shall die$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_17::
    .string "So shall it be with all the men\n"
    .string "that set their faces to go into\l"
    .string "Egypt to sojourn there; they shall\l"
    .string "die by the sword, by the famine, and\l"
    .string "by the pestilence: and none of them\l"
    .string "shall remain or escape from the\l"
    .string "evil that I will bring upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_18::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; As mine anger and\l"
    .string "my fury hath been poured forth upon\l"
    .string "the inhabitants of Jerusalem; so\l"
    .string "shall my fury be poured forth upon\l"
    .string "you, when ye shall enter into\l"
    .string "Egypt: and ye shall be an\l"
    .string "execration, and an astonishment, and\l"
    .string "a curse, and a reproach; and ye\l"
    .string "shall see this place no more.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_19::
    .string "The LORD hath said concerning you, O\n"
    .string "ye remnant of Judah; Go ye not into\l"
    .string "Egypt: know certainly that I have\l"
    .string "admonished you this day.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_20::
    .string "For ye dissembled in your hearts,\n"
    .string "when ye sent me unto the LORD your\l"
    .string "God, saying, Pray for us unto the\l"
    .string "LORD our God; and according unto all\l"
    .string "that the LORD our God shall say, so\l"
    .string "declare unto us, and we will do it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_21::
    .string "And now I have this day declared it\n"
    .string "to you; but ye have not obeyed the\l"
    .string "voice of the LORD your God, nor any\l"
    .string "thing for the which he hath sent me\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_42_22::
    .string "Now therefore know certainly that\n"
    .string "ye shall die by the sword, by the\l"
    .string "famine, and by the pestilence, in\l"
    .string "the place whither ye desire to go\l"
    .string "and to sojourn.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when\n"
    .string "Jeremiah had made an end of speaking\l"
    .string "unto all the people all the\l"
    .string "words of the LORD their God, for\l"
    .string "which the LORD their God had sent him\l"
    .string "to them, even all these words,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_2::
    .string "Then spake Azariah the son of\n"
    .string "Hoshaiah, and Johanan the son of\l"
    .string "Kareah, and all the proud men,\l"
    .string "saying unto Jeremiah, Thou speakest\l"
    .string "falsely: the LORD our God hath not\l"
    .string "sent thee to say, Go not into Egypt\l"
    .string "to sojourn there:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_3::
    .string "But Baruch the son of Neriah setteth\n"
    .string "thee on against us, for to deliver us\l"
    .string "into the hand of the Chaldeans, that\l"
    .string "they might put us to death, and carry\l"
    .string "us away captives into Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_4::
    .string "So Johanan the son of Kareah, and\n"
    .string "all the captains of the forces, and\l"
    .string "all the people, obeyed not the\l"
    .string "voice of the LORD, to dwell in the\l"
    .string "land of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_5::
    .string "But Johanan the son of Kareah, and\n"
    .string "all the captains of the forces,\l"
    .string "took all the remnant of Judah, that\l"
    .string "were returned from all nations,\l"
    .string "whither they had been driven, to\l"
    .string "dwell in the land of Judah;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_6::
    .string "Even men, and women, and children,\n"
    .string "and the king’s daughters, and every\l"
    .string "person that Nebuzaradan the captain\l"
    .string "of the guard had left with Gedaliah\l"
    .string "the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan,\l"
    .string "and Jeremiah the prophet, and\l"
    .string "Baruch the son of Neriah$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_7::
    .string "So they came into the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt: for they obeyed not the voice\l"
    .string "of the LORD: thus came they even to\l"
    .string "Tahpanhes.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_8::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "Jeremiah in Tahpanhes, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_9::
    .string "Take great stones in thine hand, and\n"
    .string "hide them in the clay in the\l"
    .string "brickkiln, which is at the entry of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s house in Tahpanhes, in the\l"
    .string "sight of the men of Judah;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_10::
    .string "And say unto them, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts, the God of Israel;\l"
    .string "Behold, I will send and take\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon,\l"
    .string "my servant, and will set his throne\l"
    .string "upon these stones that I have hid;\l"
    .string "and he shall spread his royal\l"
    .string "pavilion over them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_11::
    .string "And when he cometh, he shall smite\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt, and deliver such\l"
    .string "as are for death to death; and such as\l"
    .string "are for captivity to captivity; and\l"
    .string "such as are for the sword to the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_12::
    .string "And I will kindle a fire in the\n"
    .string "houses of the gods of Egypt; and he\l"
    .string "shall burn them, and carry them away\l"
    .string "captives: and he shall array\l"
    .string "himself with the land of Egypt, as\l"
    .string "a shepherd putteth on his garment;\l"
    .string "and he shall go forth from thence in\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_43_13::
    .string "He shall break also the images of\n"
    .string "Bethshemesh, that is in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt; and the houses of the gods of\l"
    .string "the Egyptians shall he burn with\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_1::
    .string "The word that came to Jeremiah\n"
    .string "concerning all the Jews which\l"
    .string "dwell in the land of Egypt, which\l"
    .string "dwell at Migdol, and at Tahpanhes,\l"
    .string "and at Noph, and in the country of\l"
    .string "Pathros, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel; Ye have seen all the\l"
    .string "evil that I have brought upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and upon all the cities\l"
    .string "of Judah; and, behold, this day they\l"
    .string "are a desolation, and no man\l"
    .string "dwelleth therein,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_3::
    .string "Because of their wickedness which\n"
    .string "they have committed to provoke me to\l"
    .string "anger, in that they went to burn\l"
    .string "incense, and to serve other gods,\l"
    .string "whom they knew not, neither they, ye,\l"
    .string "nor your fathers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_4::
    .string "Howbeit I sent unto you all my\n"
    .string "servants the prophets, rising\l"
    .string "early and sending them, saying, Oh,\l"
    .string "do not this abominable thing that I\l"
    .string "hate.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_5::
    .string "But they hearkened not, nor\n"
    .string "inclined their ear to turn from\l"
    .string "their wickedness, to burn no incense\l"
    .string "unto other gods.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_6::
    .string "Wherefore my fury and mine anger was\n"
    .string "poured forth, and was kindled in the\l"
    .string "cities of Judah and in the streets of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and they are wasted and\l"
    .string "desolate, as at this day.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_7::
    .string "Therefore now thus saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "the God of hosts, the God of Israel;\l"
    .string "Wherefore commit ye this great evil\l"
    .string "against your souls, to cut off from\l"
    .string "you man and woman, child and\l"
    .string "suckling, out of Judah, to leave you\l"
    .string "none to remain;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_8::
    .string "In that ye provoke me unto wrath\n"
    .string "with the works of your hands, burning\l"
    .string "incense unto other gods in the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt, whither ye be gone to\l"
    .string "dwell, that ye might cut yourselves\l"
    .string "off, and that ye might be a curse and\l"
    .string "a reproach among all the nations of\l"
    .string "the earth?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_9::
    .string "Have ye forgotten the wickedness of\n"
    .string "your fathers, and the wickedness of\l"
    .string "the kings of Judah, and the\l"
    .string "wickedness of their wives, and your\l"
    .string "own wickedness, and the wickedness of\l"
    .string "your wives, which they have committed\l"
    .string "in the land of Judah, and in the\l"
    .string "streets of Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_10::
    .string "They are not humbled even unto this\n"
    .string "day, neither have they feared, nor\l"
    .string "walked in my law, nor in my\l"
    .string "statutes, that I set before you and\l"
    .string "before your fathers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_11::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I\l"
    .string "will set my face against you for\l"
    .string "evil, and to cut off all Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_12::
    .string "And I will take the remnant of\n"
    .string "Judah, that have set their faces to\l"
    .string "go into the land of Egypt to sojourn\l"
    .string "there, and they shall all be\l"
    .string "consumed, and fall in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt; they shall even be consumed\l"
    .string "by the sword and by the famine: they\l"
    .string "shall die, from the least even unto\l"
    .string "the greatest, by the sword and by the\l"
    .string "famine: and they shall be an\l"
    .string "execration, and an astonishment, and\l"
    .string "a curse, and a reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_13::
    .string "For I will punish them that\n"
    .string "dwell in the land of Egypt, as I\l"
    .string "have punished Jerusalem, by the\l"
    .string "sword, by the famine, and by the\l"
    .string "pestilence:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_14::
    .string "So that none of the remnant of\n"
    .string "Judah, which are gone into the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt to sojourn there, shall\l"
    .string "escape or remain, that they should\l"
    .string "return into the land of Judah, to the\l"
    .string "which they have a desire to return to\l"
    .string "dwell there: for none shall return\l"
    .string "but such as shall escape$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_15::
    .string "Then all the men which knew that\n"
    .string "their wives had burned incense unto\l"
    .string "other gods, and all the women that\l"
    .string "stood by, a great multitude, even\l"
    .string "all the people that dwelt in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, in Pathros, answered\l"
    .string "Jeremiah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_16::
    .string "As for the word that thou hast\n"
    .string "spoken unto us in the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD, we will not hearken unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_17::
    .string "But we will certainly do\n"
    .string "whatsoever thing goeth forth out of\l"
    .string "our own mouth, to burn incense unto\l"
    .string "the queen of heaven, and to pour out\l"
    .string "drink offerings unto her, as we have\l"
    .string "done, we, and our fathers, our kings,\l"
    .string "and our princes, in the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, and in the streets of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: for then had we plenty\l"
    .string "of victuals, and were well, and saw\l"
    .string "no evil.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_18::
    .string "But since we left off to burn\n"
    .string "incense to the queen of heaven, and\l"
    .string "to pour out drink offerings unto\l"
    .string "her, we have wanted all things, and\l"
    .string "have been consumed by the sword and\l"
    .string "by the famine.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_19::
    .string "And when we burned incense to the\n"
    .string "queen of heaven, and poured out\l"
    .string "drink offerings unto her, did we make\l"
    .string "her cakes to worship her, and pour\l"
    .string "out drink offerings unto her, without\l"
    .string "our men?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_20::
    .string "Then Jeremiah said unto all the\n"
    .string "people, to the men, and to the\l"
    .string "women, and to all the people which\l"
    .string "had given him that answer, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_21::
    .string "The incense that ye burned in the\n"
    .string "cities of Judah, and in the streets\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, ye, and your fathers,\l"
    .string "your kings, and your princes, and\l"
    .string "the people of the land, did not the\l"
    .string "LORD remember them, and came it not\l"
    .string "into his mind?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_22::
    .string "So that the LORD could no longer\n"
    .string "bear, because of the evil of your\l"
    .string "doings, and because of the\l"
    .string "abominations which ye have\l"
    .string "committed; therefore is your land a\l"
    .string "desolation, and an astonishment, and\l"
    .string "a curse, without an inhabitant, as at\l"
    .string "this day$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_23::
    .string "Because ye have burned incense, and\n"
    .string "because ye have sinned against the\l"
    .string "LORD, and have not obeyed the voice\l"
    .string "of the LORD, nor walked in his law,\l"
    .string "nor in his statutes, nor in his\l"
    .string "testimonies; therefore this evil is\l"
    .string "happened unto you, as at this day.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_24::
    .string "Moreover Jeremiah said unto all\n"
    .string "the people, and to all the women,\l"
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD, all Judah\l"
    .string "that are in the land of Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_25::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the\n"
    .string "God of Israel, saying; Ye and your\l"
    .string "wives have both spoken with your\l"
    .string "mouths, and fulfilled with your\l"
    .string "hand, saying, We will surely\l"
    .string "perform our vows that we have vowed,\l"
    .string "to burn incense to the queen of\l"
    .string "heaven, and to pour out drink\l"
    .string "offerings unto her: ye will surely\l"
    .string "accomplish your vows, and surely\l"
    .string "perform your vows$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_26::
    .string "Therefore hear ye the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD, all Judah that dwell in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt; Behold, I have sworn\l"
    .string "by my great name, saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "that my name shall no more be named\l"
    .string "in the mouth of any man of Judah in\l"
    .string "all the land of Egypt, saying, The\l"
    .string "Lord GOD liveth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_27::
    .string "Behold, I will watch over them for\n"
    .string "evil, and not for good: and all the\l"
    .string "men of Judah that are in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt shall be consumed by the\l"
    .string "sword and by the famine, until there\l"
    .string "be an end of them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_28::
    .string "Yet a small number that escape the\n"
    .string "sword shall return out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt into the land of Judah, and\l"
    .string "all the remnant of Judah, that are\l"
    .string "gone into the land of Egypt to\l"
    .string "sojourn there, shall know whose\l"
    .string "words shall stand, mine, or theirs.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_29::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto you,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that I will punish\l"
    .string "you in this place, that ye may know\l"
    .string "that my words shall surely stand\l"
    .string "against you for evil:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_44_30::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I\n"
    .string "will give Pharaohhophra king of\l"
    .string "Egypt into the hand of his enemies,\l"
    .string "and into the hand of them that seek\l"
    .string "his life; as I gave Zedekiah king of\l"
    .string "Judah into the hand of\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, his\l"
    .string "enemy, and that sought his life$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_45_1::
    .string "The word that Jeremiah the prophet\n"
    .string "spake unto Baruch the son of Neriah,\l"
    .string "when he had written these words in a\l"
    .string "book at the mouth of Jeremiah, in the\l"
    .string "fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of\l"
    .string "Josiah king of Judah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_45_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel, unto thee, O Baruch:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_45_3::
    .string "Thou didst say, Woe is me now! for\n"
    .string "the LORD hath added grief to my\l"
    .string "sorrow; I fainted in my sighing, and\l"
    .string "I find no rest$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_45_4::
    .string "Thus shalt thou say unto him, The\n"
    .string "LORD saith thus; Behold, that which\l"
    .string "I have built will I break down, and\l"
    .string "that which I have planted I will\l"
    .string "pluck up, even this whole land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_45_5::
    .string "And seekest thou great things for\n"
    .string "thyself? seek them not: for, behold,\l"
    .string "I will bring evil upon all\l"
    .string "flesh, saith the LORD: but thy life\l"
    .string "will I give unto thee for a prey in\l"
    .string "all places whither thou goest.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD which came to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah the prophet against the\l"
    .string "Gentiles;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_2::
    .string "Against Egypt, against the army of\n"
    .string "Pharaohnecho king of Egypt, which\l"
    .string "was by the river Euphrates in\l"
    .string "Carchemish, which Nebuchadrezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon smote in the fourth\l"
    .string "year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah\l"
    .string "king of Judah$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_3::
    .string "Order ye the buckler and shield,\n"
    .string "and draw near to battle.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_4::
    .string "Harness the horses; and get up, ye\n"
    .string "horsemen, and stand forth with your\l"
    .string "helmets; furbish the spears, and\l"
    .string "put on the brigandines.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_5::
    .string "Wherefore have I seen them dismayed\n"
    .string "and turned away back? and their\l"
    .string "mighty ones are beaten down, and are\l"
    .string "fled apace, and look not back: for\l"
    .string "fear was round about, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_6::
    .string "Let not the swift flee away, nor the\n"
    .string "mighty man escape; they shall\l"
    .string "stumble, and fall toward the north\l"
    .string "by the river Euphrates.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_7::
    .string "Who is this that cometh up as a\n"
    .string "flood, whose waters are moved as the\l"
    .string "rivers?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_8::
    .string "Egypt riseth up like a flood, and\n"
    .string "his waters are moved like the\l"
    .string "rivers; and he saith, I will go up,\l"
    .string "and will cover the earth; I will\l"
    .string "destroy the city and the inhabitants\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_9::
    .string "Come up, ye horses; and rage, ye\n"
    .string "chariots; and let the mighty men\l"
    .string "come forth; the Ethiopians and the\l"
    .string "Libyans, that handle the shield;\l"
    .string "and the Lydians, that handle and\l"
    .string "bend the bow.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_10::
    .string "For this is the day of the Lord GOD\n"
    .string "of hosts, a day of vengeance, that he\l"
    .string "may avenge him of his adversaries:\l"
    .string "and the sword shall devour, and it\l"
    .string "shall be satiate and made drunk\l"
    .string "with their blood: for the Lord GOD of\l"
    .string "hosts hath a sacrifice in the north\l"
    .string "country by the river Euphrates.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_11::
    .string "Go up into Gilead, and take balm,\n"
    .string "O virgin, the daughter of Egypt: in\l"
    .string "vain shalt thou use many medicines;\l"
    .string "for thou shalt not be cured.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_12::
    .string "The nations have heard of thy shame,\n"
    .string "and thy cry hath filled the land:\l"
    .string "for the mighty man hath stumbled\l"
    .string "against the mighty, and they are\l"
    .string "fallen both together.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_13::
    .string "The word that the LORD spake to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah the prophet, how\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon\l"
    .string "should come and smite the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_14::
    .string "Declare ye in Egypt, and publish\n"
    .string "in Migdol, and publish in Noph and\l"
    .string "in Tahpanhes: say ye, Stand fast, and\l"
    .string "prepare thee; for the sword shall\l"
    .string "devour round about thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_15::
    .string "Why are thy valiant men swept away?\n"
    .string "they stood not, because the LORD did\l"
    .string "drive them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_16::
    .string "He made many to fall, yea, one\n"
    .string "fell upon another: and they said,\l"
    .string "Arise, and let us go again to our own\l"
    .string "people, and to the land of our\l"
    .string "nativity, from the oppressing sword.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_17::
    .string "They did cry there, Pharaoh king of\n"
    .string "Egypt is but a noise; he hath passed\l"
    .string "the time appointed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_18::
    .string "As I live, saith the King, whose\n"
    .string "name is the LORD of hosts, Surely as\l"
    .string "Tabor is among the mountains, and as\l"
    .string "Carmel by the sea, so shall he come.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_19::
    .string "O thou daughter dwelling in Egypt,\n"
    .string "furnish thyself to go into\l"
    .string "captivity: for Noph shall be waste\l"
    .string "and desolate without an inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_20::
    .string "Egypt is like a very fair heifer,\n"
    .string "but destruction cometh; it cometh out\l"
    .string "of the north.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_21::
    .string "Also her hired men are in the midst\n"
    .string "of her like fatted bullocks; for\l"
    .string "they also are turned back, and are\l"
    .string "fled away together: they did not\l"
    .string "stand, because the day of their\l"
    .string "calamity was come upon them, and the\l"
    .string "time of their visitation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_22::
    .string "The voice thereof shall go like a\n"
    .string "serpent; for they shall march with\l"
    .string "an army, and come against her with\l"
    .string "axes, as hewers of wood.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_23::
    .string "They shall cut down her forest,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, though it cannot be\l"
    .string "searched; because they are more than\l"
    .string "the grasshoppers, and are\l"
    .string "innumerable.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_24::
    .string "The daughter of Egypt shall be\n"
    .string "confounded; she shall be delivered\l"
    .string "into the hand of the people of the\l"
    .string "north.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_25::
    .string "The LORD of hosts, the God of\n"
    .string "Israel, saith; Behold, I will\l"
    .string "punish the multitude of No, and\l"
    .string "Pharaoh, and Egypt, with their gods,\l"
    .string "and their kings; even Pharaoh, and\l"
    .string "all them that trust in him:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_26::
    .string "And I will deliver them into the\n"
    .string "hand of those that seek their lives,\l"
    .string "and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon, and into the hand of\l"
    .string "his servants: and afterward it\l"
    .string "shall be inhabited, as in the days\l"
    .string "of old, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_27::
    .string "But fear not thou, O my servant\n"
    .string "Jacob, and be not dismayed, O Israel:\l"
    .string "for, behold, I will save thee from\l"
    .string "afar off, and thy seed from the land\l"
    .string "of their captivity; and Jacob shall\l"
    .string "return, and be in rest and at ease,\l"
    .string "and none shall make him afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_46_28::
    .string "Fear thou not, O Jacob my servant,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD: for I am with thee;\l"
    .string "for I will make a full end of all\l"
    .string "the nations whither I have driven\l"
    .string "thee: but I will not make a full\l"
    .string "end of thee, but correct thee in\l"
    .string "measure; yet will I not leave thee\l"
    .string "wholly unpunished.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah the prophet against the\l"
    .string "Philistines, before that Pharaoh\l"
    .string "smote Gaza.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Behold, waters\n"
    .string "rise up out of the north, and shall\l"
    .string "be an overflowing flood, and shall\l"
    .string "overflow the land, and all that is\l"
    .string "therein; the city, and them that\l"
    .string "dwell therein: then the men shall\l"
    .string "cry, and all the inhabitants of the\l"
    .string "land shall howl.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_3::
    .string "At the noise of the stamping of the\n"
    .string "hoofs of his strong horses, at the\l"
    .string "rushing of his chariots, and at the\l"
    .string "rumbling of his wheels, the fathers\l"
    .string "shall not look back to their\l"
    .string "children for feebleness of hands;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_4::
    .string "Because of the day that cometh to\n"
    .string "spoil all the Philistines, and to\l"
    .string "cut off from Tyrus and Zidon every\l"
    .string "helper that remaineth: for the LORD\l"
    .string "will spoil the Philistines, the\l"
    .string "remnant of the country of Caphtor$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_5::
    .string "Baldness is come upon Gaza;\n"
    .string "Ashkelon is cut off with the remnant\l"
    .string "of their valley: how long wilt\l"
    .string "thou cut thyself?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_6::
    .string "O thou sword of the LORD, how long\n"
    .string "will it be ere thou be quiet? put\l"
    .string "up thyself into thy scabbard, rest,\l"
    .string "and be still$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_47_7::
    .string "How can it be quiet, seeing the LORD\n"
    .string "hath given it a charge against\l"
    .string "Ashkelon, and against the sea shore?\l"
    .string "there hath he appointed it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_1::
    .string "Against Moab thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Woe unto\l"
    .string "Nebo! for it is spoiled: Kiriathaim\l"
    .string "is confounded and taken: Misgab is\l"
    .string "confounded and dismayed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_2::
    .string "There shall be no more praise of\n"
    .string "Moab: in Heshbon they have devised\l"
    .string "evil against it; come, and let us\l"
    .string "cut it off from being a nation. Also\l"
    .string "thou shalt be cut down, O Madmen; the\l"
    .string "sword shall pursue thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_3::
    .string "A voice of crying shall be from\n"
    .string "Horonaim, spoiling and great\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_4::
    .string "Moab is destroyed; her little ones\n"
    .string "have caused a cry to be heard.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_5::
    .string "For in the going up of Luhith\n"
    .string "continual weeping shall go up;\l"
    .string "for in the going down of Horonaim the\l"
    .string "enemies have heard a cry of\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_6::
    .string "Flee, save your lives, and be like\n"
    .string "the heath in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_7::
    .string "For because thou hast trusted in thy\n"
    .string "works and in thy treasures, thou\l"
    .string "shalt also be taken: and Chemosh\l"
    .string "shall go forth into captivity with\l"
    .string "his priests and his princes\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_8::
    .string "And the spoiler shall come upon\n"
    .string "every city, and no city shall\l"
    .string "escape: the valley also shall\l"
    .string "perish, and the plain shall be\l"
    .string "destroyed, as the LORD hath spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_9::
    .string "Give wings unto Moab, that it may\n"
    .string "flee and get away: for the cities\l"
    .string "thereof shall be desolate, without\l"
    .string "any to dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_10::
    .string "Cursed be he that doeth the work of\n"
    .string "the LORD deceitfully, and cursed be\l"
    .string "he that keepeth back his sword from\l"
    .string "blood.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_11::
    .string "Moab hath been at ease from his\n"
    .string "youth, and he hath settled on his\l"
    .string "lees, and hath not been emptied from\l"
    .string "vessel to vessel, neither hath he\l"
    .string "gone into captivity: therefore his\l"
    .string "taste remained in him, and his scent\l"
    .string "is not changed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_12::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that I will send\l"
    .string "unto him wanderers, that shall\l"
    .string "cause him to wander, and shall\l"
    .string "empty his vessels, and break their\l"
    .string "bottles.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_13::
    .string "And Moab shall be ashamed of\n"
    .string "Chemosh, as the house of Israel was\l"
    .string "ashamed of Bethel their confidence.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_14::
    .string "How say ye, We are mighty and strong\n"
    .string "men for the war?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_15::
    .string "Moab is spoiled, and gone up out\n"
    .string "of her cities, and his chosen young\l"
    .string "men are gone down to the slaughter,\l"
    .string "saith the King, whose name is the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_16::
    .string "The calamity of Moab is near to\n"
    .string "come, and his affliction hasteth\l"
    .string "fast.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_17::
    .string "All ye that are about him, bemoan\n"
    .string "him; and all ye that know his name,\l"
    .string "say, How is the strong staff broken,\l"
    .string "and the beautiful rod!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_18::
    .string "Thou daughter that dost inhabit\n"
    .string "Dibon, come down from thy glory, and\l"
    .string "sit in thirst; for the spoiler of\l"
    .string "Moab shall come upon thee, and he\l"
    .string "shall destroy thy strong holds$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_19::
    .string "O inhabitant of Aroer, stand by the\n"
    .string "way, and espy; ask him that fleeth,\l"
    .string "and her that escapeth, and say, What\l"
    .string "is done?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_20::
    .string "Moab is confounded; for it is broken\n"
    .string "down: howl and cry; tell ye it in\l"
    .string "Arnon, that Moab is spoiled,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_21::
    .string "And judgment is come upon the\n"
    .string "plain country; upon Holon, and\l"
    .string "upon Jahazah, and upon Mephaath,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_22::
    .string "And upon Dibon, and upon Nebo, and\n"
    .string "upon Bethdiblathaim,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_23::
    .string "And upon Kiriathaim, and upon\n"
    .string "Bethgamul, and upon Bethmeon,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_24::
    .string "And upon Kerioth, and upon Bozrah,\n"
    .string "and upon all the cities of the\l"
    .string "land of Moab, far or near$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_25::
    .string "The horn of Moab is cut off, and his\n"
    .string "arm is broken, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_26::
    .string "Make ye him drunken: for he\n"
    .string "magnified himself against the LORD:\l"
    .string "Moab also shall wallow in his\l"
    .string "vomit, and he also shall be in\l"
    .string "derision.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_27::
    .string "For was not Israel a derision unto\n"
    .string "thee? was he found among thieves? for\l"
    .string "since thou spakest of him, thou\l"
    .string "skippedst for joy.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_28::
    .string "O ye that dwell in Moab, leave the\n"
    .string "cities, and dwell in the rock, and\l"
    .string "be like the dove that maketh her\l"
    .string "nest in the sides of the hole’s\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_29::
    .string "We have heard the pride of Moab, (he\n"
    .string "is exceeding proud) his loftiness,\l"
    .string "and his arrogancy, and his pride,\l"
    .string "and the haughtiness of his heart.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_30::
    .string "I know his wrath, saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "but it shall not be so; his lies\l"
    .string "shall not so effect it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_31::
    .string "Therefore will I howl for Moab,\n"
    .string "and I will cry out for all Moab;\l"
    .string "mine heart shall mourn for the men\l"
    .string "of Kirheres.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_32::
    .string "O vine of Sibmah, I will weep for\n"
    .string "thee with the weeping of Jazer: thy\l"
    .string "plants are gone over the sea, they\l"
    .string "reach even to the sea of Jazer: the\l"
    .string "spoiler is fallen upon thy summer\l"
    .string "fruits and upon thy vintage.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_33::
    .string "And joy and gladness is taken from\n"
    .string "the plentiful field, and from the\l"
    .string "land of Moab, and I have caused wine\l"
    .string "to fail from the winepresses: none\l"
    .string "shall tread with shouting; their\l"
    .string "shouting shall be no shouting.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_34::
    .string "From the cry of Heshbon even unto\n"
    .string "Elealeh, and even unto Jahaz, have\l"
    .string "they uttered their voice, from Zoar\l"
    .string "even unto Horonaim, as an heifer of\l"
    .string "three years old: for the waters also\l"
    .string "of Nimrim shall be desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_35::
    .string "Moreover I will cause to cease in\n"
    .string "Moab, saith the LORD, him that\l"
    .string "offereth in the high places, and him\l"
    .string "that burneth incense to his gods.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_36::
    .string "Therefore mine heart shall sound\n"
    .string "for Moab like pipes, and mine heart\l"
    .string "shall sound like pipes for the\l"
    .string "men of Kirheres: because the riches\l"
    .string "that he hath gotten are perished.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_37::
    .string "For every head shall be bald, and\n"
    .string "every beard clipped: upon all the\l"
    .string "hands shall be cuttings, and upon\l"
    .string "the loins sackcloth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_38::
    .string "There shall be lamentation\n"
    .string "generally upon all the housetops\l"
    .string "of Moab, and in the streets thereof:\l"
    .string "for I have broken Moab like a vessel\l"
    .string "wherein is no pleasure, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_39::
    .string "They shall howl, saying, How is it\n"
    .string "broken down! how hath Moab turned the\l"
    .string "back with shame! so shall Moab be a\l"
    .string "derision and a dismaying to all\l"
    .string "them about him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_40::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; Behold, he\n"
    .string "shall fly as an eagle, and shall\l"
    .string "spread his wings over Moab.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_41::
    .string "Kerioth is taken, and the strong\n"
    .string "holds are surprised, and the mighty\l"
    .string "men’s hearts in Moab at that day\l"
    .string "shall be as the heart of a woman in\l"
    .string "her pangs.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_42::
    .string "And Moab shall be destroyed from\n"
    .string "being a people, because he hath\l"
    .string "magnified himself against the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_43::
    .string "Fear, and the pit, and the snare,\n"
    .string "shall be upon thee, O inhabitant of\l"
    .string "Moab, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_44::
    .string "He that fleeth from the fear shall\n"
    .string "fall into the pit; and he that\l"
    .string "getteth up out of the pit shall be\l"
    .string "taken in the snare: for I will bring\l"
    .string "upon it, even upon Moab, the year of\l"
    .string "their visitation, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_45::
    .string "They that fled stood under the\n"
    .string "shadow of Heshbon because of the\l"
    .string "force: but a fire shall come forth\l"
    .string "out of Heshbon, and a flame from the\l"
    .string "midst of Sihon, and shall devour the\l"
    .string "corner of Moab, and the crown of the\l"
    .string "head of the tumultuous ones.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_46::
    .string "Woe be unto thee, O Moab! the\n"
    .string "people of Chemosh perisheth: for\l"
    .string "thy sons are taken captives, and thy\l"
    .string "daughters captives.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_48_47::
    .string "Yet will I bring again the\n"
    .string "captivity of Moab in the latter\l"
    .string "days, saith the LORD. Thus far is the\l"
    .string "judgment of Moab.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_1::
    .string "Concerning the Ammonites, thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; Hath Israel no sons?\l"
    .string "hath he no heir? why then doth their\l"
    .string "king inherit Gad, and his people\l"
    .string "dwell in his cities?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_2::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that I will cause an\l"
    .string "alarm of war to be heard in Rabbah of\l"
    .string "the Ammonites; and it shall be a\l"
    .string "desolate heap, and her daughters\l"
    .string "shall be burned with fire: then\l"
    .string "shall Israel be heir unto them that\l"
    .string "were his heirs, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_3::
    .string "Howl, O Heshbon, for Ai is\n"
    .string "spoiled: cry, ye daughters of\l"
    .string "Rabbah, gird you with sackcloth;\l"
    .string "lament, and run to and fro by the\l"
    .string "hedges; for their king shall go into\l"
    .string "captivity, and his priests and his\l"
    .string "princes together.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_4::
    .string "Wherefore gloriest thou in the\n"
    .string "valleys, thy flowing valley, O\l"
    .string "backsliding daughter? that trusted\l"
    .string "in her treasures, saying, Who shall\l"
    .string "come unto me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_5::
    .string "Behold, I will bring a fear upon\n"
    .string "thee, saith the Lord GOD of hosts,\l"
    .string "from all those that be about thee;\l"
    .string "and ye shall be driven out every man\l"
    .string "right forth; and none shall gather\l"
    .string "up him that wandereth$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_6::
    .string "And afterward I will bring again\n"
    .string "the captivity of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_7::
    .string "Concerning Edom, thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts; Is wisdom no more in Teman?\l"
    .string "is counsel perished from the\l"
    .string "prudent? is their wisdom vanished?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_8::
    .string "Flee ye, turn back, dwell deep, O\n"
    .string "inhabitants of Dedan; for I will\l"
    .string "bring the calamity of Esau upon him,\l"
    .string "the time that I will visit him$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_9::
    .string "If grapegatherers come to thee,\n"
    .string "would they not leave some gleaning\l"
    .string "grapes? if thieves by night, they\l"
    .string "will destroy till they have enough.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_10::
    .string "But I have made Esau bare, I have\n"
    .string "uncovered his secret places, and he\l"
    .string "shall not be able to hide himself:\l"
    .string "his seed is spoiled, and his\l"
    .string "brethren, and his neighbours, and he\l"
    .string "is not.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_11::
    .string "Leave thy fatherless children, I\n"
    .string "will preserve them alive; and let\l"
    .string "thy widows trust in me.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_12::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD; Behold,\n"
    .string "they whose judgment was not to drink\l"
    .string "of the cup have assuredly drunken;\l"
    .string "and art thou he that shall\l"
    .string "altogether go unpunished? thou\l"
    .string "shalt not go unpunished, but thou\l"
    .string "shalt surely drink of it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_13::
    .string "For I have sworn by myself, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, that Bozrah shall become a\l"
    .string "desolation, a reproach, a waste, and\l"
    .string "a curse; and all the cities thereof\l"
    .string "shall be perpetual wastes.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_14::
    .string "I have heard a rumour from the LORD,\n"
    .string "and an ambassador is sent unto the\l"
    .string "heathen, saying, Gather ye together,\l"
    .string "and come against her, and rise up to\l"
    .string "the battle.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_15::
    .string "For, lo, I will make thee small\n"
    .string "among the heathen, and despised\l"
    .string "among men.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_16::
    .string "Thy terribleness hath deceived\n"
    .string "thee, and the pride of thine heart, O\l"
    .string "thou that dwellest in the clefts of\l"
    .string "the rock, that holdest the height of\l"
    .string "the hill: though thou shouldest\l"
    .string "make thy nest as high as the eagle, I\l"
    .string "will bring thee down from thence,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_17::
    .string "Also Edom shall be a desolation:\n"
    .string "every one that goeth by it shall be\l"
    .string "astonished, and shall hiss at all\l"
    .string "the plagues thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_18::
    .string "As in the overthrow of Sodom and\n"
    .string "Gomorrah and the neighbour cities\l"
    .string "thereof, saith the LORD, no man\l"
    .string "shall abide there, neither shall a\l"
    .string "son of man dwell in it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_19::
    .string "Behold, he shall come up like a\n"
    .string "lion from the swelling of Jordan\l"
    .string "against the habitation of the strong:\l"
    .string "but I will suddenly make him run\l"
    .string "away from her: and who is a chosen\l"
    .string "man, that I may appoint over her?\l"
    .string "for who is like me? and who will\l"
    .string "appoint me the time? and who is that\l"
    .string "shepherd that will stand before me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_20::
    .string "Therefore hear the counsel of the\n"
    .string "LORD, that he hath taken against\l"
    .string "Edom; and his purposes, that he hath\l"
    .string "purposed against the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Teman: Surely the least of the\l"
    .string "flock shall draw them out: surely\l"
    .string "he shall make their habitations\l"
    .string "desolate with them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_21::
    .string "The earth is moved at the noise of\n"
    .string "their fall, at the cry the noise\l"
    .string "thereof was heard in the Red sea.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_22::
    .string "Behold, he shall come up and fly\n"
    .string "as the eagle, and spread his wings\l"
    .string "over Bozrah: and at that day shall\l"
    .string "the heart of the mighty men of Edom\l"
    .string "be as the heart of a woman in her\l"
    .string "pangs.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_23::
    .string "Concerning Damascus. Hamath is\n"
    .string "confounded, and Arpad: for they have\l"
    .string "heard evil tidings: they are\l"
    .string "fainthearted; there is sorrow on the\l"
    .string "sea; it cannot be quiet.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_24::
    .string "Damascus is waxed feeble, and\n"
    .string "turneth herself to flee, and fear\l"
    .string "hath seized on her: anguish and\l"
    .string "sorrows have taken her, as a woman in\l"
    .string "travail.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_25::
    .string "How is the city of praise not left,\n"
    .string "the city of my joy!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_26::
    .string "Therefore her young men shall\n"
    .string "fall in her streets, and all the\l"
    .string "men of war shall be cut off in that\l"
    .string "day, saith the LORD of hosts$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_27::
    .string "And I will kindle a fire in the\n"
    .string "wall of Damascus, and it shall\l"
    .string "consume the palaces of Benhadad.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_28::
    .string "Concerning Kedar, and concerning\n"
    .string "the kingdoms of Hazor, which\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon\l"
    .string "shall smite, thus saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "Arise ye, go up to Kedar, and spoil\l"
    .string "the men of the east.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_29::
    .string "Their tents and their flocks\n"
    .string "shall they take away: they shall\l"
    .string "take to themselves their curtains,\l"
    .string "and all their vessels, and their\l"
    .string "camels; and they shall cry unto\l"
    .string "them, Fear is on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_30::
    .string "Flee, get you far off, dwell deep,\n"
    .string "O ye inhabitants of Hazor, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD; for Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon hath taken counsel against\l"
    .string "you, and hath conceived a purpose\l"
    .string "against you.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_31::
    .string "Arise, get you up unto the wealthy\n"
    .string "nation, that dwelleth without care,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, which have neither\l"
    .string "gates nor bars, which dwell alone.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_32::
    .string "And their camels shall be a booty,\n"
    .string "and the multitude of their cattle a\l"
    .string "spoil: and I will scatter into\l"
    .string "all winds them that are in the\l"
    .string "utmost corners; and I will bring\l"
    .string "their calamity from all sides\l"
    .string "thereof, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_33::
    .string "And Hazor shall be a dwelling for\n"
    .string "dragons, and a desolation for ever:\l"
    .string "there shall no man abide there, nor\l"
    .string "any son of man dwell in it.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_34::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came to\n"
    .string "Jeremiah the prophet against Elam\l"
    .string "in the beginning of the reign of\l"
    .string "Zedekiah king of Judah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_35::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will break the bow of\l"
    .string "Elam, the chief of their might$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_36::
    .string "And upon Elam will I bring the\n"
    .string "four winds from the four quarters of\l"
    .string "heaven, and will scatter them\l"
    .string "toward all those winds; and there\l"
    .string "shall be no nation whither the\l"
    .string "outcasts of Elam shall not come.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_37::
    .string "For I will cause Elam to be\n"
    .string "dismayed before their enemies, and\l"
    .string "before them that seek their life:\l"
    .string "and I will bring evil upon them,\l"
    .string "even my fierce anger, saith the LORD;\l"
    .string "and I will send the sword after\l"
    .string "them, till I have consumed them:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_38::
    .string "And I will set my throne in Elam,\n"
    .string "and will destroy from thence the\l"
    .string "king and the princes, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_49_39::
    .string "But it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "latter days, that I will bring again\l"
    .string "the captivity of Elam, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_1::
    .string "The word that the LORD spake\n"
    .string "against Babylon and against the\l"
    .string "land of the Chaldeans by Jeremiah\l"
    .string "the prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_2::
    .string "Declare ye among the nations, and\n"
    .string "publish, and set up a standard;\l"
    .string "publish, and conceal not: say,\l"
    .string "Babylon is taken, Bel is\l"
    .string "confounded, Merodach is broken in\l"
    .string "pieces; her idols are confounded,\l"
    .string "her images are broken in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_3::
    .string "For out of the north there cometh\n"
    .string "up a nation against her, which\l"
    .string "shall make her land desolate, and\l"
    .string "none shall dwell therein: they\l"
    .string "shall remove, they shall depart,\l"
    .string "both man and beast.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_4::
    .string "In those days, and in that time,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, the children of\l"
    .string "Israel shall come, they and the\l"
    .string "children of Judah together, going\l"
    .string "and weeping: they shall go, and\l"
    .string "seek the LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_5::
    .string "They shall ask the way to Zion with\n"
    .string "their faces thitherward, saying,\l"
    .string "Come, and let us join ourselves to\l"
    .string "the LORD in a perpetual covenant\l"
    .string "that shall not be forgotten.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_6::
    .string "My people hath been lost sheep:\n"
    .string "their shepherds have caused them to\l"
    .string "go astray, they have turned them away\l"
    .string "on the mountains: they have gone from\l"
    .string "mountain to hill, they have\l"
    .string "forgotten their restingplace.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_7::
    .string "All that found them have devoured\n"
    .string "them: and their adversaries said, We\l"
    .string "offend not, because they have sinned\l"
    .string "against the LORD, the habitation of\l"
    .string "justice, even the LORD, the hope of\l"
    .string "their fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_8::
    .string "Remove out of the midst of Babylon,\n"
    .string "and go forth out of the land of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans, and be as the he goats\l"
    .string "before the flocks.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_9::
    .string "For, lo, I will raise and cause to\n"
    .string "come up against Babylon an\l"
    .string "assembly of great nations from the\l"
    .string "north country: and they shall set\l"
    .string "themselves in array against her;\l"
    .string "from thence she shall be taken:\l"
    .string "their arrows shall be as of a mighty\l"
    .string "expert man; none shall return in\l"
    .string "vain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_10::
    .string "And Chaldea shall be a spoil:\n"
    .string "all that spoil her shall be\l"
    .string "satisfied, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_11::
    .string "Because ye were glad, because ye\n"
    .string "rejoiced, O ye destroyers of mine\l"
    .string "heritage, because ye are grown fat as\l"
    .string "the heifer at grass, and bellow as\l"
    .string "bulls;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_12::
    .string "Your mother shall be sore\n"
    .string "confounded; she that bare you shall\l"
    .string "be ashamed: behold, the hindermost\l"
    .string "of the nations shall be a\l"
    .string "wilderness, a dry land, and a desert$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_13::
    .string "Because of the wrath of the LORD it\n"
    .string "shall not be inhabited, but it\l"
    .string "shall be wholly desolate: every\l"
    .string "one that goeth by Babylon shall be\l"
    .string "astonished, and hiss at all her\l"
    .string "plagues.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_14::
    .string "Put yourselves in array against\n"
    .string "Babylon round about: all ye that\l"
    .string "bend the bow, shoot at her, spare no\l"
    .string "arrows: for she hath sinned against\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_15::
    .string "Shout against her round about: she\n"
    .string "hath given her hand: her foundations\l"
    .string "are fallen, her walls are thrown\l"
    .string "down: for it is the vengeance of the\l"
    .string "LORD: take vengeance upon her; as\l"
    .string "she hath done, do unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_16::
    .string "Cut off the sower from Babylon, and\n"
    .string "him that handleth the sickle in the\l"
    .string "time of harvest: for fear of the\l"
    .string "oppressing sword they shall turn\l"
    .string "every one to his people, and they\l"
    .string "shall flee every one to his own\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_17::
    .string "Israel is a scattered sheep; the\n"
    .string "lions have driven him away: first the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria hath devoured him;\l"
    .string "and last this Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon hath broken his bones.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_18::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I\l"
    .string "will punish the king of Babylon\l"
    .string "and his land, as I have punished the\l"
    .string "king of Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_19::
    .string "And I will bring Israel again to\n"
    .string "his habitation, and he shall feed on\l"
    .string "Carmel and Bashan, and his soul\l"
    .string "shall be satisfied upon mount\l"
    .string "Ephraim and Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_20::
    .string "In those days, and in that time,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, the iniquity of\l"
    .string "Israel shall be sought for, and\l"
    .string "there shall be none; and the sins of\l"
    .string "Judah, and they shall not be found:\l"
    .string "for I will pardon them whom I\l"
    .string "reserve.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_21::
    .string "Go up against the land of\n"
    .string "Merathaim, even against it, and\l"
    .string "against the inhabitants of Pekod:\l"
    .string "waste and utterly destroy after\l"
    .string "them, saith the LORD, and do\l"
    .string "according to all that I have\l"
    .string "commanded thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_22::
    .string "A sound of battle is in the land,\n"
    .string "and of great destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_23::
    .string "How is the hammer of the whole\n"
    .string "earth cut asunder and broken! how is\l"
    .string "Babylon become a desolation among\l"
    .string "the nations!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_24::
    .string "I have laid a snare for thee, and\n"
    .string "thou art also taken, O Babylon, and\l"
    .string "thou wast not aware: thou art found,\l"
    .string "and also caught, because thou hast\l"
    .string "striven against the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_25::
    .string "The LORD hath opened his armoury,\n"
    .string "and hath brought forth the weapons\l"
    .string "of his indignation: for this is the\l"
    .string "work of the Lord GOD of hosts in the\l"
    .string "land of the Chaldeans.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_26::
    .string "Come against her from the utmost\n"
    .string "border, open her storehouses: cast\l"
    .string "her up as heaps, and destroy her\l"
    .string "utterly: let nothing of her be left.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_27::
    .string "Slay all her bullocks; let them\n"
    .string "go down to the slaughter: woe unto\l"
    .string "them! for their day is come, the time\l"
    .string "of their visitation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_28::
    .string "The voice of them that flee and\n"
    .string "escape out of the land of Babylon,\l"
    .string "to declare in Zion the vengeance of\l"
    .string "the LORD our God, the vengeance of\l"
    .string "his temple.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_29::
    .string "Call together the archers against\n"
    .string "Babylon: all ye that bend the bow,\l"
    .string "camp against it round about; let\l"
    .string "none thereof escape: recompense her\l"
    .string "according to her work; according to\l"
    .string "all that she hath done, do unto her:\l"
    .string "for she hath been proud against the\l"
    .string "LORD, against the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_30::
    .string "Therefore shall her young men\n"
    .string "fall in the streets, and all her\l"
    .string "men of war shall be cut off in that\l"
    .string "day, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_31::
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O thou\n"
    .string "most proud, saith the Lord GOD of\l"
    .string "hosts: for thy day is come, the time\l"
    .string "that I will visit thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_32::
    .string "And the most proud shall stumble\n"
    .string "and fall, and none shall raise him\l"
    .string "up: and I will kindle a fire in his\l"
    .string "cities, and it shall devour all\l"
    .string "round about him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_33::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The\n"
    .string "children of Israel and the\l"
    .string "children of Judah were oppressed\l"
    .string "together: and all that took them\l"
    .string "captives held them fast; they\l"
    .string "refused to let them go.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_34::
    .string "Their Redeemer is strong; the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts is his name: he shall\l"
    .string "throughly plead their cause, that\l"
    .string "he may give rest to the land, and\l"
    .string "disquiet the inhabitants of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_35::
    .string "A sword is upon the Chaldeans,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, and upon the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Babylon, and upon\l"
    .string "her princes, and upon her wise men.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_36::
    .string "A sword is upon the liars; and they\n"
    .string "shall dote: a sword is upon her\l"
    .string "mighty men; and they shall be\l"
    .string "dismayed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_37::
    .string "A sword is upon their horses, and\n"
    .string "upon their chariots, and upon all\l"
    .string "the mingled people that are in the\l"
    .string "midst of her; and they shall become\l"
    .string "as women: a sword is upon her\l"
    .string "treasures; and they shall be robbed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_38::
    .string "A drought is upon her waters; and\n"
    .string "they shall be dried up: for it is\l"
    .string "the land of graven images, and they\l"
    .string "are mad upon their idols.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_39::
    .string "Therefore the wild beasts of the\n"
    .string "desert with the wild beasts of the\l"
    .string "islands shall dwell there, and\l"
    .string "the owls shall dwell therein: and\l"
    .string "it shall be no more inhabited for\l"
    .string "ever; neither shall it be dwelt in\l"
    .string "from generation to generation.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_40::
    .string "As God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah\n"
    .string "and the neighbour cities thereof,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD; so shall no man\l"
    .string "abide there, neither shall any son\l"
    .string "of man dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_41::
    .string "Behold, a people shall come from\n"
    .string "the north, and a great nation, and\l"
    .string "many kings shall be raised up from\l"
    .string "the coasts of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_42::
    .string "They shall hold the bow and the\n"
    .string "lance: they are cruel, and will not\l"
    .string "shew mercy: their voice shall roar\l"
    .string "like the sea, and they shall ride\l"
    .string "upon horses, every one put in array,\l"
    .string "like a man to the battle, against\l"
    .string "thee, O daughter of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_43::
    .string "The king of Babylon hath heard the\n"
    .string "report of them, and his hands waxed\l"
    .string "feeble: anguish took hold of him,\l"
    .string "and pangs as of a woman in travail.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_44::
    .string "Behold, he shall come up like a\n"
    .string "lion from the swelling of Jordan\l"
    .string "unto the habitation of the strong:\l"
    .string "but I will make them suddenly run\l"
    .string "away from her: and who is a chosen\l"
    .string "man, that I may appoint over her?\l"
    .string "for who is like me? and who will\l"
    .string "appoint me the time? and who is that\l"
    .string "shepherd that will stand before me?"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_45::
    .string "Therefore hear ye the counsel of\n"
    .string "the LORD, that he hath taken against\l"
    .string "Babylon; and his purposes, that he\l"
    .string "hath purposed against the land of\l"
    .string "the Chaldeans: Surely the least of\l"
    .string "the flock shall draw them out:\l"
    .string "surely he shall make their\l"
    .string "habitation desolate with them$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_50_46::
    .string "At the noise of the taking of\n"
    .string "Babylon the earth is moved, and the\l"
    .string "cry is heard among the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I\n"
    .string "will raise up against Babylon, and\l"
    .string "against them that dwell in the\l"
    .string "midst of them that rise up against\l"
    .string "me, a destroying wind;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_2::
    .string "And will send unto Babylon\n"
    .string "fanners, that shall fan her, and\l"
    .string "shall empty her land: for in the\l"
    .string "day of trouble they shall be\l"
    .string "against her round about$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_3::
    .string "Against him that bendeth let the\n"
    .string "archer bend his bow, and against him\l"
    .string "that lifteth himself up in his\l"
    .string "brigandine: and spare ye not her\l"
    .string "young men; destroy ye utterly all\l"
    .string "her host.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_4::
    .string "Thus the slain shall fall in the\n"
    .string "land of the Chaldeans, and they that\l"
    .string "are thrust through in her streets.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_5::
    .string "For Israel hath not been forsaken,\n"
    .string "nor Judah of his God, of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts; though their land was filled\l"
    .string "with sin against the Holy One of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_6::
    .string "Flee out of the midst of Babylon,\n"
    .string "and deliver every man his soul: be\l"
    .string "not cut off in her iniquity; for this\l"
    .string "is the time of the LORD’s vengeance;\l"
    .string "he will render unto her a\l"
    .string "recompence.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_7::
    .string "Babylon hath been a golden cup in\n"
    .string "the LORD’s hand, that made all the\l"
    .string "earth drunken: the nations have\l"
    .string "drunken of her wine; therefore the\l"
    .string "nations are mad.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_8::
    .string "Babylon is suddenly fallen and\n"
    .string "destroyed: howl for her; take balm\l"
    .string "for her pain, if so be she may be\l"
    .string "healed.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_9::
    .string "We would have healed Babylon, but\n"
    .string "she is not healed: forsake her, and\l"
    .string "let us go every one into his own\l"
    .string "country: for her judgment reacheth\l"
    .string "unto heaven, and is lifted up even\l"
    .string "to the skies.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_10::
    .string "The LORD hath brought forth our\n"
    .string "righteousness: come, and let us\l"
    .string "declare in Zion the work of the LORD\l"
    .string "our God.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_11::
    .string "Make bright the arrows; gather the\n"
    .string "shields: the LORD hath raised up the\l"
    .string "spirit of the kings of the Medes: for\l"
    .string "his device is against Babylon, to\l"
    .string "destroy it; because it is the\l"
    .string "vengeance of the LORD, the vengeance\l"
    .string "of his temple.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_12::
    .string "Set up the standard upon the\n"
    .string "walls of Babylon, make the watch\l"
    .string "strong, set up the watchmen,\l"
    .string "prepare the ambushes: for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath both devised and done that which\l"
    .string "he spake against the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_13::
    .string "O thou that dwellest upon many\n"
    .string "waters, abundant in treasures, thine\l"
    .string "end is come, and the measure of thy\l"
    .string "covetousness.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_14::
    .string "The LORD of hosts hath sworn by\n"
    .string "himself, saying, Surely I will\l"
    .string "fill thee with men, as with\l"
    .string "caterpillers; and they shall\l"
    .string "lift up a shout against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_15::
    .string "He hath made the earth by his power,\n"
    .string "he hath established the world by\l"
    .string "his wisdom, and hath stretched out\l"
    .string "the heaven by his understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_16::
    .string "When he uttereth his voice, there is\n"
    .string "a multitude of waters in the\l"
    .string "heavens; and he causeth the vapours\l"
    .string "to ascend from the ends of the earth:\l"
    .string "he maketh lightnings with rain, and\l"
    .string "bringeth forth the wind out of his\l"
    .string "treasures.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_17::
    .string "Every man is brutish by his\n"
    .string "knowledge; every founder is\l"
    .string "confounded by the graven image: for\l"
    .string "his molten image is falsehood, and\l"
    .string "there is no breath in them.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_18::
    .string "They are vanity, the work of errors:\n"
    .string "in the time of their visitation they\l"
    .string "shall perish.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_19::
    .string "The portion of Jacob is not like\n"
    .string "them; for he is the former of all\l"
    .string "things: and Israel is the rod of his\l"
    .string "inheritance: the LORD of hosts is his\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_20::
    .string "Thou art my battle axe and weapons\n"
    .string "of war: for with thee will I break\l"
    .string "in pieces the nations, and with thee\l"
    .string "will I destroy kingdoms;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_21::
    .string "And with thee will I break in\n"
    .string "pieces the horse and his rider; and\l"
    .string "with thee will I break in pieces\l"
    .string "the chariot and his rider;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_22::
    .string "With thee also will I break in\n"
    .string "pieces man and woman; and with thee\l"
    .string "will I break in pieces old and\l"
    .string "young; and with thee will I break in\l"
    .string "pieces the young man and the maid;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_23::
    .string "I will also break in pieces with\n"
    .string "thee the shepherd and his flock; and\l"
    .string "with thee will I break in pieces\l"
    .string "the husbandman and his yoke of oxen;\l"
    .string "and with thee will I break in\l"
    .string "pieces captains and rulers$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_24::
    .string "And I will render unto Babylon and\n"
    .string "to all the inhabitants of Chaldea\l"
    .string "all their evil that they have done\l"
    .string "in Zion in your sight, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_25::
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O\n"
    .string "destroying mountain, saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "which destroyest all the earth: and\l"
    .string "I will stretch out mine hand upon\l"
    .string "thee, and roll thee down from the\l"
    .string "rocks, and will make thee a burnt\l"
    .string "mountain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_26::
    .string "And they shall not take of thee a\n"
    .string "stone for a corner, nor a stone for\l"
    .string "foundations; but thou shalt be\l"
    .string "desolate for ever, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_27::
    .string "Set ye up a standard in the land,\n"
    .string "blow the trumpet among the nations,\l"
    .string "prepare the nations against her,\l"
    .string "call together against her the\l"
    .string "kingdoms of Ararat, Minni, and\l"
    .string "Ashchenaz; appoint a captain\l"
    .string "against her; cause the horses to come\l"
    .string "up as the rough caterpillers.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_28::
    .string "Prepare against her the nations\n"
    .string "with the kings of the Medes, the\l"
    .string "captains thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "rulers thereof, and all the land\l"
    .string "of his dominion.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_29::
    .string "And the land shall tremble and\n"
    .string "sorrow: for every purpose of the\l"
    .string "LORD shall be performed against\l"
    .string "Babylon, to make the land of\l"
    .string "Babylon a desolation without an\l"
    .string "inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_30::
    .string "The mighty men of Babylon have\n"
    .string "forborn to fight, they have remained\l"
    .string "in their holds: their might hath\l"
    .string "failed; they became as women: they\l"
    .string "have burned her dwellingplaces;\l"
    .string "her bars are broken.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_31::
    .string "One post shall run to meet\n"
    .string "another, and one messenger to meet\l"
    .string "another, to shew the king of Babylon\l"
    .string "that his city is taken at one end,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_32::
    .string "And that the passages are stopped,\n"
    .string "and the reeds they have burned with\l"
    .string "fire, and the men of war are\l"
    .string "affrighted$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_33::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "the God of Israel; The daughter of\l"
    .string "Babylon is like a threshingfloor,\l"
    .string "it is time to thresh her: yet a\l"
    .string "little while, and the time of her\l"
    .string "harvest shall come.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_34::
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon\n"
    .string "hath devoured me, he hath crushed me,\l"
    .string "he hath made me an empty vessel, he\l"
    .string "hath swallowed me up like a\l"
    .string "dragon, he hath filled his belly\l"
    .string "with my delicates, he hath cast me\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_35::
    .string "The violence done to me and to my\n"
    .string "flesh be upon Babylon, shall the\l"
    .string "inhabitant of Zion say; and my blood\l"
    .string "upon the inhabitants of Chaldea,\l"
    .string "shall Jerusalem say.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_36::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will plead thy cause,\l"
    .string "and take vengeance for thee; and I\l"
    .string "will dry up her sea, and make her\l"
    .string "springs dry.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_37::
    .string "And Babylon shall become heaps, a\n"
    .string "dwellingplace for dragons, an\l"
    .string "astonishment, and an hissing,\l"
    .string "without an inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_38::
    .string "They shall roar together like\n"
    .string "lions: they shall yell as lions’\l"
    .string "whelps.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_39::
    .string "In their heat I will make their\n"
    .string "feasts, and I will make them\l"
    .string "drunken, that they may rejoice, and\l"
    .string "sleep a perpetual sleep, and not\l"
    .string "wake, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_40::
    .string "I will bring them down like lambs\n"
    .string "to the slaughter, like rams with he\l"
    .string "goats.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_41::
    .string "How is Sheshach taken! and how is\n"
    .string "the praise of the whole earth\l"
    .string "surprised! how is Babylon become an\l"
    .string "astonishment among the nations!"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_42::
    .string "The sea is come up upon Babylon:\n"
    .string "she is covered with the multitude of\l"
    .string "the waves thereof$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_43::
    .string "Her cities are a desolation, a dry\n"
    .string "land, and a wilderness, a land\l"
    .string "wherein no man dwelleth, neither\l"
    .string "doth any son of man pass thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_44::
    .string "And I will punish Bel in Babylon,\n"
    .string "and I will bring forth out of his\l"
    .string "mouth that which he hath swallowed\l"
    .string "up: and the nations shall not flow\l"
    .string "together any more unto him: yea, the\l"
    .string "wall of Babylon shall fall.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_45::
    .string "My people, go ye out of the midst\n"
    .string "of her, and deliver ye every man his\l"
    .string "soul from the fierce anger of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_46::
    .string "And lest your heart faint, and ye\n"
    .string "fear for the rumour that shall be\l"
    .string "heard in the land; a rumour shall\l"
    .string "both come one year, and after that in\l"
    .string "another year shall come a rumour,\l"
    .string "and violence in the land, ruler\l"
    .string "against ruler.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_47::
    .string "Therefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "that I will do judgment upon the\l"
    .string "graven images of Babylon: and her\l"
    .string "whole land shall be confounded,\l"
    .string "and all her slain shall fall in\l"
    .string "the midst of her.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_48::
    .string "Then the heaven and the earth, and\n"
    .string "all that is therein, shall sing\l"
    .string "for Babylon: for the spoilers\l"
    .string "shall come unto her from the north,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_49::
    .string "As Babylon hath caused the slain\n"
    .string "of Israel to fall, so at Babylon\l"
    .string "shall fall the slain of all the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_50::
    .string "Ye that have escaped the sword, go\n"
    .string "away, stand not still: remember the\l"
    .string "LORD afar off, and let Jerusalem\l"
    .string "come into your mind.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_51::
    .string "We are confounded, because we have\n"
    .string "heard reproach: shame hath covered\l"
    .string "our faces: for strangers are come\l"
    .string "into the sanctuaries of the LORD’s\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_52::
    .string "Wherefore, behold, the days come,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD, that I will do\l"
    .string "judgment upon her graven images: and\l"
    .string "through all her land the wounded\l"
    .string "shall groan.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_53::
    .string "Though Babylon should mount up to\n"
    .string "heaven, and though she should\l"
    .string "fortify the height of her strength,\l"
    .string "yet from me shall spoilers come\l"
    .string "unto her, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_54::
    .string "A sound of a cry cometh from\n"
    .string "Babylon, and great destruction from\l"
    .string "the land of the Chaldeans:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_55::
    .string "Because the LORD hath spoiled\n"
    .string "Babylon, and destroyed out of her\l"
    .string "the great voice; when her waves do\l"
    .string "roar like great waters, a noise of\l"
    .string "their voice is uttered:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_56::
    .string "Because the spoiler is come upon\n"
    .string "her, even upon Babylon, and her\l"
    .string "mighty men are taken, every one of\l"
    .string "their bows is broken: for the LORD\l"
    .string "God of recompences shall surely\l"
    .string "requite$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_57::
    .string "And I will make drunk her princes,\n"
    .string "and her wise men, her captains, and\l"
    .string "her rulers, and her mighty men: and\l"
    .string "they shall sleep a perpetual\l"
    .string "sleep, and not wake, saith the King,\l"
    .string "whose name is the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_58::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The\n"
    .string "broad walls of Babylon shall be\l"
    .string "utterly broken, and her high gates\l"
    .string "shall be burned with fire; and the\l"
    .string "people shall labour in vain, and\l"
    .string "the folk in the fire, and they\l"
    .string "shall be weary.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_59::
    .string "The word which Jeremiah the\n"
    .string "prophet commanded Seraiah the son of\l"
    .string "Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, when he\l"
    .string "went with Zedekiah the king of Judah\l"
    .string "into Babylon in the fourth year of\l"
    .string "his reign. And this Seraiah was a\l"
    .string "quiet prince.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_60::
    .string "So Jeremiah wrote in a book all the\n"
    .string "evil that should come upon\l"
    .string "Babylon, even all these words that\l"
    .string "are written against Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_61::
    .string "And Jeremiah said to Seraiah, When\n"
    .string "thou comest to Babylon, and shalt\l"
    .string "see, and shalt read all these\l"
    .string "words;"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_62::
    .string "Then shalt thou say, O LORD, thou\n"
    .string "hast spoken against this place, to\l"
    .string "cut it off, that none shall remain\l"
    .string "in it, neither man nor beast, but\l"
    .string "that it shall be desolate for ever$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_63::
    .string "And it shall be, when thou hast\n"
    .string "made an end of reading this book,\l"
    .string "that thou shalt bind a stone to it,\l"
    .string "and cast it into the midst of\l"
    .string "Euphrates:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_51_64::
    .string "And thou shalt say, Thus shall\n"
    .string "Babylon sink, and shall not rise\l"
    .string "from the evil that I will bring\l"
    .string "upon her: and they shall be weary.\l"
    .string "Thus far are the words of Jeremiah$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_1::
    .string "Zedekiah was one and twenty years\n"
    .string "old when he began to reign, and he\l"
    .string "reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.\l"
    .string "And his mother’s name was Hamutal\l"
    .string "the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_2::
    .string "And he did that which was evil in\n"
    .string "the eyes of the LORD, according to\l"
    .string "all that Jehoiakim had done.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_3::
    .string "For through the anger of the LORD it\n"
    .string "came to pass in Jerusalem and Judah,\l"
    .string "till he had cast them out from his\l"
    .string "presence, that Zedekiah rebelled\l"
    .string "against the king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_4::
    .string "And it came to pass in the ninth\n"
    .string "year of his reign, in the tenth\l"
    .string "month, in the tenth day of the month,\l"
    .string "that Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon\l"
    .string "came, he and all his army, against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and pitched against it,\l"
    .string "and built forts against it round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_5::
    .string "So the city was besieged unto the\n"
    .string "eleventh year of king Zedekiah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_6::
    .string "And in the fourth month, in the\n"
    .string "ninth day of the month, the famine\l"
    .string "was sore in the city, so that there\l"
    .string "was no bread for the people of the\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_7::
    .string "Then the city was broken up, and\n"
    .string "all the men of war fled, and went\l"
    .string "forth out of the city by night by the\l"
    .string "way of the gate between the two\l"
    .string "walls, which was by the king’s\l"
    .string "garden; (now the Chaldeans were by\l"
    .string "the city round about:) and they went\l"
    .string "by the way of the plain.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_8::
    .string "But the army of the Chaldeans\n"
    .string "pursued after the king, and overtook\l"
    .string "Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho;\l"
    .string "and all his army was scattered from\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_9::
    .string "Then they took the king, and carried\n"
    .string "him up unto the king of Babylon to\l"
    .string "Riblah in the land of Hamath; where\l"
    .string "he gave judgment upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_10::
    .string "And the king of Babylon slew the\n"
    .string "sons of Zedekiah before his eyes: he\l"
    .string "slew also all the princes of\l"
    .string "Judah in Riblah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_11::
    .string "Then he put out the eyes of\n"
    .string "Zedekiah; and the king of Babylon\l"
    .string "bound him in chains, and carried him\l"
    .string "to Babylon, and put him in prison\l"
    .string "till the day of his death.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_12::
    .string "Now in the fifth month, in the tenth\n"
    .string "day of the month, which was the\l"
    .string "nineteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon, came Nebuzaradan,\l"
    .string "captain of the guard, which served\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon, into\l"
    .string "Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_13::
    .string "And burned the house of the LORD,\n"
    .string "and the king’s house; and all the\l"
    .string "houses of Jerusalem, and all the\l"
    .string "houses of the great men, burned he\l"
    .string "with fire:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_14::
    .string "And all the army of the Chaldeans,\n"
    .string "that were with the captain of the\l"
    .string "guard, brake down all the walls of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem round about$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_15::
    .string "Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard carried away captive certain\l"
    .string "of the poor of the people, and the\l"
    .string "residue of the people that\l"
    .string "remained in the city, and those that\l"
    .string "fell away, that fell to the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon, and the rest of the\l"
    .string "multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_16::
    .string "But Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard left certain of the poor of\l"
    .string "the land for vinedressers and for\l"
    .string "husbandmen.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_17::
    .string "Also the pillars of brass that\n"
    .string "were in the house of the LORD, and the\l"
    .string "bases, and the brasen sea that was in\l"
    .string "the house of the LORD, the Chaldeans\l"
    .string "brake, and carried all the brass of\l"
    .string "them to Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_18::
    .string "The caldrons also, and the\n"
    .string "shovels, and the snuffers, and the\l"
    .string "bowls, and the spoons, and all the\l"
    .string "vessels of brass wherewith they\l"
    .string "ministered, took they away.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_19::
    .string "And the basons, and the firepans,\n"
    .string "and the bowls, and the caldrons, and\l"
    .string "the candlesticks, and the spoons,\l"
    .string "and the cups; that which was of gold\l"
    .string "in gold, and that which was of\l"
    .string "silver in silver, took the captain\l"
    .string "of the guard away.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_20::
    .string "The two pillars, one sea, and\n"
    .string "twelve brasen bulls that were\l"
    .string "under the bases, which king Solomon\l"
    .string "had made in the house of the LORD: the\l"
    .string "brass of all these vessels was\l"
    .string "without weight.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_21::
    .string "And concerning the pillars, the\n"
    .string "height of one pillar was eighteen\l"
    .string "cubits; and a fillet of twelve\l"
    .string "cubits did compass it; and the\l"
    .string "thickness thereof was four fingers:\l"
    .string "it was hollow.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_22::
    .string "And a chapiter of brass was upon\n"
    .string "it; and the height of one chapiter\l"
    .string "was five cubits, with network and\l"
    .string "pomegranates upon the chapiters\l"
    .string "round about, all of brass. The\l"
    .string "second pillar also and the\l"
    .string "pomegranates were like unto these.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_23::
    .string "And there were ninety and six\n"
    .string "pomegranates on a side; and all the\l"
    .string "pomegranates upon the network were\l"
    .string "an hundred round about.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_24::
    .string "And the captain of the guard took\n"
    .string "Seraiah the chief priest, and\l"
    .string "Zephaniah the second priest, and\l"
    .string "the three keepers of the door:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_25::
    .string "He took also out of the city an\n"
    .string "eunuch, which had the charge of the\l"
    .string "men of war; and seven men of them that\l"
    .string "were near the king’s person, which\l"
    .string "were found in the city; and the\l"
    .string "principal scribe of the host, who\l"
    .string "mustered the people of the land;\l"
    .string "and threescore men of the people of\l"
    .string "the land, that were found in the\l"
    .string "midst of the city$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_26::
    .string "So Nebuzaradan the captain of the\n"
    .string "guard took them, and brought them to\l"
    .string "the king of Babylon to Riblah.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_27::
    .string "And the king of Babylon smote them,\n"
    .string "and put them to death in Riblah in\l"
    .string "the land of Hamath. Thus Judah was\l"
    .string "carried away captive out of his own\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_28::
    .string "This is the people whom\n"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar carried away\l"
    .string "captive: in the seventh year three\l"
    .string "thousand Jews and three and twenty:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_29::
    .string "In the eighteenth year of\n"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar he carried away\l"
    .string "captive from Jerusalem eight\l"
    .string "hundred thirty and two persons:"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_30::
    .string "In the three and twentieth year of\n"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar Nebuzaradan the\l"
    .string "captain of the guard carried away\l"
    .string "captive of the Jews seven hundred\l"
    .string "forty and five persons: all the\l"
    .string "persons were four thousand and six\l"
    .string "hundred$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_31::
    .string "And it came to pass in the seven and\n"
    .string "thirtieth year of the captivity of\l"
    .string "Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the\l"
    .string "twelfth month, in the five and\l"
    .string "twentieth day of the month, that\l"
    .string "Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the\l"
    .string "first year of his reign lifted up\l"
    .string "the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah,\l"
    .string "and brought him forth out of prison.$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_32::
    .string "And spake kindly unto him, and set\n"
    .string "his throne above the throne of the\l"
    .string "kings that were with him in Babylon,"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_33::
    .string "And changed his prison garments:\n"
    .string "and he did continually eat bread\l"
    .string "before him all the days of his life$"
Bible_Text_Jeremiah_52_34::
    .string "And for his diet, there was a\n"
    .string "continual diet given him of the king\l"
    .string "of Babylon, every day a portion\l"
    .string "until the day of his death, all the\l"
    .string "days of his life.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_1::
    .string "How doth the city sit solitary,\n"
    .string "that was full of people! how is\l"
    .string "she become as a widow! she that was\l"
    .string "great among the nations, and\l"
    .string "princess among the provinces, how is\l"
    .string "she become tributary!"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_2::
    .string "She weepeth sore in the night, and\n"
    .string "her tears are on her cheeks: among\l"
    .string "all her lovers she hath none to\l"
    .string "comfort her: all her friends have\l"
    .string "dealt treacherously with her, they\l"
    .string "are become her enemies$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_3::
    .string "Judah is gone into captivity\n"
    .string "because of affliction, and because\l"
    .string "of great servitude: she dwelleth\l"
    .string "among the heathen, she findeth no\l"
    .string "rest: all her persecutors overtook\l"
    .string "her between the straits.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_4::
    .string "The ways of Zion do mourn, because\n"
    .string "none come to the solemn feasts: all\l"
    .string "her gates are desolate: her priests\l"
    .string "sigh, her virgins are afflicted, and\l"
    .string "she is in bitterness.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_5::
    .string "Her adversaries are the chief, her\n"
    .string "enemies prosper; for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "afflicted her for the multitude of\l"
    .string "her transgressions: her children are\l"
    .string "gone into captivity before the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_6::
    .string "And from the daughter of Zion all\n"
    .string "her beauty is departed: her princes\l"
    .string "are become like harts that find no\l"
    .string "pasture, and they are gone without\l"
    .string "strength before the pursuer.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_7::
    .string "Jerusalem remembered in the days of\n"
    .string "her affliction and of her miseries\l"
    .string "all her pleasant things that she\l"
    .string "had in the days of old, when her\l"
    .string "people fell into the hand of the\l"
    .string "enemy, and none did help her: the\l"
    .string "adversaries saw her, and did mock at\l"
    .string "her sabbaths.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_8::
    .string "Jerusalem hath grievously sinned;\n"
    .string "therefore she is removed: all that\l"
    .string "honoured her despise her, because\l"
    .string "they have seen her nakedness: yea,\l"
    .string "she sigheth, and turneth backward.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_9::
    .string "Her filthiness is in her skirts;\n"
    .string "she remembereth not her last end;\l"
    .string "therefore she came down\l"
    .string "wonderfully: she had no comforter.\l"
    .string "O LORD, behold my affliction: for\l"
    .string "the enemy hath magnified himself.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_10::
    .string "The adversary hath spread out his\n"
    .string "hand upon all her pleasant\l"
    .string "things: for she hath seen that the\l"
    .string "heathen entered into her sanctuary,\l"
    .string "whom thou didst command that they\l"
    .string "should not enter into thy\l"
    .string "congregation.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_11::
    .string "All her people sigh, they seek\n"
    .string "bread; they have given their\l"
    .string "pleasant things for meat to relieve\l"
    .string "the soul: see, O LORD, and consider;\l"
    .string "for I am become vile.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_12::
    .string "Is it nothing to you, all ye that\n"
    .string "pass by? behold, and see if there be\l"
    .string "any sorrow like unto my sorrow,\l"
    .string "which is done unto me, wherewith the\l"
    .string "LORD hath afflicted me in the day of\l"
    .string "his fierce anger.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_13::
    .string "From above hath he sent fire into my\n"
    .string "bones, and it prevaileth against\l"
    .string "them: he hath spread a net for my\l"
    .string "feet, he hath turned me back: he hath\l"
    .string "made me desolate and faint all the\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_14::
    .string "The yoke of my transgressions is\n"
    .string "bound by his hand: they are wreathed,\l"
    .string "and come up upon my neck: he hath\l"
    .string "made my strength to fall, the LORD\l"
    .string "hath delivered me into their hands,\l"
    .string "from whom I am not able to rise up.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_15::
    .string "The LORD hath trodden under foot\n"
    .string "all my mighty men in the midst of\l"
    .string "me: he hath called an assembly\l"
    .string "against me to crush my young men: the\l"
    .string "LORD hath trodden the virgin, the\l"
    .string "daughter of Judah, as in a winepress.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_16::
    .string "For these things I weep; mine eye,\n"
    .string "mine eye runneth down with water,\l"
    .string "because the comforter that should\l"
    .string "relieve my soul is far from me: my\l"
    .string "children are desolate, because the\l"
    .string "enemy prevailed.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_17::
    .string "Zion spreadeth forth her hands, and\n"
    .string "there is none to comfort her: the\l"
    .string "LORD hath commanded concerning\l"
    .string "Jacob, that his adversaries should\l"
    .string "be round about him: Jerusalem is as a\l"
    .string "menstruous woman among them.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_18::
    .string "The LORD is righteous; for I have\n"
    .string "rebelled against his commandment:\l"
    .string "hear, I pray you, all people, and\l"
    .string "behold my sorrow: my virgins and my\l"
    .string "young men are gone into captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_19::
    .string "I called for my lovers, but they\n"
    .string "deceived me: my priests and mine\l"
    .string "elders gave up the ghost in the\l"
    .string "city, while they sought their meat\l"
    .string "to relieve their souls.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_20::
    .string "Behold, O LORD; for I am in\n"
    .string "distress: my bowels are troubled;\l"
    .string "mine heart is turned within me; for I\l"
    .string "have grievously rebelled: abroad\l"
    .string "the sword bereaveth, at home there is\l"
    .string "as death.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_21::
    .string "They have heard that I sigh: there\n"
    .string "is none to comfort me: all mine\l"
    .string "enemies have heard of my trouble;\l"
    .string "they are glad that thou hast done it:\l"
    .string "thou wilt bring the day that thou\l"
    .string "hast called, and they shall be\l"
    .string "like unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_1_22::
    .string "Let all their wickedness come\n"
    .string "before thee; and do unto them, as\l"
    .string "thou hast done unto me for all my\l"
    .string "transgressions: for my sighs are\l"
    .string "many, and my heart is faint.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_1::
    .string "How hath the LORD covered the\n"
    .string "daughter of Zion with a cloud in his\l"
    .string "anger, and cast down from heaven unto\l"
    .string "the earth the beauty of Israel, and\l"
    .string "remembered not his footstool in the\l"
    .string "day of his anger!"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_2::
    .string "The LORD hath swallowed up all\n"
    .string "the habitations of Jacob, and hath\l"
    .string "not pitied: he hath thrown down in\l"
    .string "his wrath the strong holds of the\l"
    .string "daughter of Judah; he hath brought\l"
    .string "them down to the ground: he hath\l"
    .string "polluted the kingdom and the\l"
    .string "princes thereof$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_3::
    .string "He hath cut off in his fierce anger\n"
    .string "all the horn of Israel: he hath\l"
    .string "drawn back his right hand from before\l"
    .string "the enemy, and he burned against\l"
    .string "Jacob like a flaming fire, which\l"
    .string "devoureth round about.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_4::
    .string "He hath bent his bow like an enemy:\n"
    .string "he stood with his right hand as an\l"
    .string "adversary, and slew all that were\l"
    .string "pleasant to the eye in the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the daughter of Zion:\l"
    .string "he poured out his fury like fire.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_5::
    .string "The LORD was as an enemy: he hath\n"
    .string "swallowed up Israel, he hath\l"
    .string "swallowed up all her palaces: he\l"
    .string "hath destroyed his strong holds, and\l"
    .string "hath increased in the daughter of\l"
    .string "Judah mourning and lamentation.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_6::
    .string "And he hath violently taken away\n"
    .string "his tabernacle, as if it were of a\l"
    .string "garden: he hath destroyed his\l"
    .string "places of the assembly: the LORD\l"
    .string "hath caused the solemn feasts and\l"
    .string "sabbaths to be forgotten in Zion, and\l"
    .string "hath despised in the indignation of\l"
    .string "his anger the king and the priest.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_7::
    .string "The LORD hath cast off his altar, he\n"
    .string "hath abhorred his sanctuary, he hath\l"
    .string "given up into the hand of the enemy\l"
    .string "the walls of her palaces; they\l"
    .string "have made a noise in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD, as in the day of a solemn feast.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_8::
    .string "The LORD hath purposed to destroy\n"
    .string "the wall of the daughter of Zion: he\l"
    .string "hath stretched out a line, he hath\l"
    .string "not withdrawn his hand from\l"
    .string "destroying: therefore he made the\l"
    .string "rampart and the wall to lament;\l"
    .string "they languished together.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_9::
    .string "Her gates are sunk into the ground;\n"
    .string "he hath destroyed and broken her\l"
    .string "bars: her king and her princes are\l"
    .string "among the Gentiles: the law is no\l"
    .string "more; her prophets also find no\l"
    .string "vision from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_10::
    .string "The elders of the daughter of Zion\n"
    .string "sit upon the ground, and keep\l"
    .string "silence: they have cast up dust\l"
    .string "upon their heads; they have girded\l"
    .string "themselves with sackcloth: the\l"
    .string "virgins of Jerusalem hang down their\l"
    .string "heads to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_11::
    .string "Mine eyes do fail with tears, my\n"
    .string "bowels are troubled, my liver is\l"
    .string "poured upon the earth, for the\l"
    .string "destruction of the daughter of my\l"
    .string "people; because the children and\l"
    .string "the sucklings swoon in the streets\l"
    .string "of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_12::
    .string "They say to their mothers, Where is\n"
    .string "corn and wine? when they swooned as\l"
    .string "the wounded in the streets of the\l"
    .string "city, when their soul was poured out\l"
    .string "into their mothers’ bosom.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_13::
    .string "What thing shall I take to witness\n"
    .string "for thee? what thing shall I liken\l"
    .string "to thee, O daughter of Jerusalem?\l"
    .string "what shall I equal to thee, that I\l"
    .string "may comfort thee, O virgin daughter\l"
    .string "of Zion? for thy breach is great like\l"
    .string "the sea: who can heal thee?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_14::
    .string "Thy prophets have seen vain and\n"
    .string "foolish things for thee: and they\l"
    .string "have not discovered thine iniquity,\l"
    .string "to turn away thy captivity; but have\l"
    .string "seen for thee false burdens and\l"
    .string "causes of banishment$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_15::
    .string "All that pass by clap their\n"
    .string "hands at thee; they hiss and wag\l"
    .string "their head at the daughter of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, saying, Is this the city\l"
    .string "that men call The perfection of\l"
    .string "beauty, The joy of the whole earth?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_16::
    .string "All thine enemies have opened\n"
    .string "their mouth against thee: they hiss\l"
    .string "and gnash the teeth: they say, We\l"
    .string "have swallowed her up: certainly\l"
    .string "this is the day that we looked for;\l"
    .string "we have found, we have seen it$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_17::
    .string "The LORD hath done that which he had\n"
    .string "devised; he hath fulfilled his word\l"
    .string "that he had commanded in the days of\l"
    .string "old: he hath thrown down, and hath\l"
    .string "not pitied: and he hath caused thine\l"
    .string "enemy to rejoice over thee, he hath\l"
    .string "set up the horn of thine adversaries.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_18::
    .string "Their heart cried unto the LORD, O\n"
    .string "wall of the daughter of Zion, let\l"
    .string "tears run down like a river day and\l"
    .string "night: give thyself no rest; let not\l"
    .string "the apple of thine eye cease.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_19::
    .string "Arise, cry out in the night: in the\n"
    .string "beginning of the watches pour out\l"
    .string "thine heart like water before the\l"
    .string "face of the LORD: lift up thy hands\l"
    .string "toward him for the life of thy young\l"
    .string "children, that faint for hunger in\l"
    .string "the top of every street.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_20::
    .string "Behold, O LORD, and consider to\n"
    .string "whom thou hast done this. Shall the\l"
    .string "women eat their fruit, and children\l"
    .string "of a span long? shall the priest\l"
    .string "and the prophet be slain in the\l"
    .string "sanctuary of the Lord?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_21::
    .string "The young and the old lie on the\n"
    .string "ground in the streets: my virgins and\l"
    .string "my young men are fallen by the\l"
    .string "sword; thou hast slain them in the\l"
    .string "day of thine anger; thou hast\l"
    .string "killed, and not pitied$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_2_22::
    .string "Thou hast called as in a solemn\n"
    .string "day my terrors round about, so that\l"
    .string "in the day of the LORD’s anger none\l"
    .string "escaped nor remained: those that I\l"
    .string "have swaddled and brought up hath\l"
    .string "mine enemy consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_1::
    .string "I am the man that hath seen\n"
    .string "affliction by the rod of his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_2::
    .string "He hath led me, and brought me into\n"
    .string "darkness, but not into light.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_3::
    .string "Surely against me is he turned; he\n"
    .string "turneth his hand against me all the\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_4::
    .string "My flesh and my skin hath he made\n"
    .string "old; he hath broken my bones.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_5::
    .string "He hath builded against me, and\n"
    .string "compassed me with gall and travail.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_6::
    .string "He hath set me in dark places, as\n"
    .string "they that be dead of old.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_7::
    .string "He hath hedged me about, that I\n"
    .string "cannot get out: he hath made my chain\l"
    .string "heavy.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_8::
    .string "Also when I cry and shout, he\n"
    .string "shutteth out my prayer.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_9::
    .string "He hath inclosed my ways with hewn\n"
    .string "stone, he hath made my paths crooked.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_10::
    .string "He was unto me as a bear lying in\n"
    .string "wait, and as a lion in secret\l"
    .string "places.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_11::
    .string "He hath turned aside my ways, and\n"
    .string "pulled me in pieces: he hath made\l"
    .string "me desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_12::
    .string "He hath bent his bow, and set me as a\n"
    .string "mark for the arrow.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_13::
    .string "He hath caused the arrows of his\n"
    .string "quiver to enter into my reins.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_14::
    .string "I was a derision to all my\n"
    .string "people; and their song all the day.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_15::
    .string "He hath filled me with bitterness,\n"
    .string "he hath made me drunken with wormwood.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_16::
    .string "He hath also broken my teeth with\n"
    .string "gravel stones, he hath covered me\l"
    .string "with ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_17::
    .string "And thou hast removed my soul far\n"
    .string "off from peace: I forgat\l"
    .string "prosperity.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_18::
    .string "And I said, My strength and my hope\n"
    .string "is perished from the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_19::
    .string "Remembering mine affliction and my\n"
    .string "misery, the wormwood and the gall$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_20::
    .string "My soul hath them still in\n"
    .string "remembrance, and is humbled in me.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_21::
    .string "This I recall to my mind, therefore\n"
    .string "have I hope.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_22::
    .string "It is of the LORD’s mercies that we\n"
    .string "are not consumed, because his\l"
    .string "compassions fail not.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_23::
    .string "They are new every morning: great is\n"
    .string "thy faithfulness.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_24::
    .string "The LORD is my portion, saith my\n"
    .string "soul; therefore will I hope in him.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_25::
    .string "The LORD is good unto them that wait\n"
    .string "for him, to the soul that seeketh\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_26::
    .string "It is good that a man should both\n"
    .string "hope and quietly wait for the\l"
    .string "salvation of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_27::
    .string "It is good for a man that he bear the\n"
    .string "yoke of his youth.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_28::
    .string "He sitteth alone and keepeth\n"
    .string "silence, because he hath borne it\l"
    .string "upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_29::
    .string "He putteth his mouth in the dust; if\n"
    .string "so be there may be hope.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_30::
    .string "He giveth his cheek to him that\n"
    .string "smiteth him: he is filled full\l"
    .string "with reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_31::
    .string "For the LORD will not cast off for\n"
    .string "ever:"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_32::
    .string "But though he cause grief, yet will\n"
    .string "he have compassion according to the\l"
    .string "multitude of his mercies$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_33::
    .string "For he doth not afflict willingly\n"
    .string "nor grieve the children of men.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_34::
    .string "To crush under his feet all the\n"
    .string "prisoners of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_35::
    .string "To turn aside the right of a man\n"
    .string "before the face of the most High,"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_36::
    .string "To subvert a man in his cause, the\n"
    .string "LORD approveth not$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_37::
    .string "Who is he that saith, and it cometh\n"
    .string "to pass, when the Lord commandeth it\l"
    .string "not?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_38::
    .string "Out of the mouth of the most High\n"
    .string "proceedeth not evil and good?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_39::
    .string "Wherefore doth a living man\n"
    .string "complain, a man for the punishment\l"
    .string "of his sins?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_40::
    .string "Let us search and try our ways, and\n"
    .string "turn again to the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_41::
    .string "Let us lift up our heart with our\n"
    .string "hands unto God in the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_42::
    .string "We have transgressed and have\n"
    .string "rebelled: thou hast not pardoned.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_43::
    .string "Thou hast covered with anger, and\n"
    .string "persecuted us: thou hast slain, thou\l"
    .string "hast not pitied.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_44::
    .string "Thou hast covered thyself with a\n"
    .string "cloud, that our prayer should not\l"
    .string "pass through.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_45::
    .string "Thou hast made us as the offscouring\n"
    .string "and refuse in the midst of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_46::
    .string "All our enemies have opened their\n"
    .string "mouths against us.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_47::
    .string "Fear and a snare is come upon us,\n"
    .string "desolation and destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_48::
    .string "Mine eye runneth down with rivers of\n"
    .string "water for the destruction of the\l"
    .string "daughter of my people.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_49::
    .string "Mine eye trickleth down, and\n"
    .string "ceaseth not, without any\l"
    .string "intermission.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_50::
    .string "Till the LORD look down, and\n"
    .string "behold from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_51::
    .string "Mine eye affecteth mine heart\n"
    .string "because of all the daughters of my\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_52::
    .string "Mine enemies chased me sore, like a\n"
    .string "bird, without cause.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_53::
    .string "They have cut off my life in the\n"
    .string "dungeon, and cast a stone upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_54::
    .string "Waters flowed over mine head; then\n"
    .string "I said, I am cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_55::
    .string "I called upon thy name, O LORD,\n"
    .string "out of the low dungeon.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_56::
    .string "Thou hast heard my voice: hide not\n"
    .string "thine ear at my breathing, at my cry.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_57::
    .string "Thou drewest near in the day that I\n"
    .string "called upon thee: thou saidst, Fear\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_58::
    .string "O LORD, thou hast pleaded the\n"
    .string "causes of my soul; thou hast\l"
    .string "redeemed my life.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_59::
    .string "O LORD, thou hast seen my wrong:\n"
    .string "judge thou my cause.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_60::
    .string "Thou hast seen all their vengeance\n"
    .string "and all their imaginations against\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_61::
    .string "Thou hast heard their reproach, O\n"
    .string "LORD, and all their imaginations\l"
    .string "against me;"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_62::
    .string "The lips of those that rose up\n"
    .string "against me, and their device against\l"
    .string "me all the day$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_63::
    .string "Behold their sitting down, and\n"
    .string "their rising up; I am their musick.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_64::
    .string "Render unto them a recompence, O\n"
    .string "LORD, according to the work of their\l"
    .string "hands.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_65::
    .string "Give them sorrow of heart, thy curse\n"
    .string "unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_3_66::
    .string "Persecute and destroy them in anger\n"
    .string "from under the heavens of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_1::
    .string "How is the gold become dim! how is\n"
    .string "the most fine gold changed! the\l"
    .string "stones of the sanctuary are poured\l"
    .string "out in the top of every street.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_2::
    .string "The precious sons of Zion,\n"
    .string "comparable to fine gold, how are\l"
    .string "they esteemed as earthen pitchers,\l"
    .string "the work of the hands of the potter!"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_3::
    .string "Even the sea monsters draw out the\n"
    .string "breast, they give suck to their young\l"
    .string "ones: the daughter of my people is\l"
    .string "become cruel, like the ostriches in\l"
    .string "the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_4::
    .string "The tongue of the sucking child\n"
    .string "cleaveth to the roof of his mouth\l"
    .string "for thirst: the young children ask\l"
    .string "bread, and no man breaketh it unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_5::
    .string "They that did feed delicately are\n"
    .string "desolate in the streets: they that\l"
    .string "were brought up in scarlet embrace\l"
    .string "dunghills.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_6::
    .string "For the punishment of the iniquity\n"
    .string "of the daughter of my people is\l"
    .string "greater than the punishment of the\l"
    .string "sin of Sodom, that was overthrown as\l"
    .string "in a moment, and no hands stayed on\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_7::
    .string "Her Nazarites were purer than snow,\n"
    .string "they were whiter than milk, they\l"
    .string "were more ruddy in body than rubies,\l"
    .string "their polishing was of sapphire:"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_8::
    .string "Their visage is blacker than a\n"
    .string "coal; they are not known in the\l"
    .string "streets: their skin cleaveth to\l"
    .string "their bones; it is withered, it is\l"
    .string "become like a stick$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_9::
    .string "They that be slain with the sword\n"
    .string "are better than they that be slain\l"
    .string "with hunger: for these pine away,\l"
    .string "stricken through for want of the\l"
    .string "fruits of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_10::
    .string "The hands of the pitiful women\n"
    .string "have sodden their own children: they\l"
    .string "were their meat in the destruction of\l"
    .string "the daughter of my people.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_11::
    .string "The LORD hath accomplished his\n"
    .string "fury; he hath poured out his fierce\l"
    .string "anger, and hath kindled a fire in\l"
    .string "Zion, and it hath devoured the\l"
    .string "foundations thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_12::
    .string "The kings of the earth, and all the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of the world, would not\l"
    .string "have believed that the adversary and\l"
    .string "the enemy should have entered into\l"
    .string "the gates of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_13::
    .string "For the sins of her prophets, and\n"
    .string "the iniquities of her priests, that\l"
    .string "have shed the blood of the just in\l"
    .string "the midst of her,"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_14::
    .string "They have wandered as blind men in\n"
    .string "the streets, they have polluted\l"
    .string "themselves with blood, so that men\l"
    .string "could not touch their garments$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_15::
    .string "They cried unto them, Depart ye; it\n"
    .string "is unclean; depart, depart, touch\l"
    .string "not: when they fled away and\l"
    .string "wandered, they said among the\l"
    .string "heathen, They shall no more sojourn\l"
    .string "there.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_16::
    .string "The anger of the LORD hath divided\n"
    .string "them; he will no more regard them:\l"
    .string "they respected not the persons of\l"
    .string "the priests, they favoured not the\l"
    .string "elders.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_17::
    .string "As for us, our eyes as yet failed\n"
    .string "for our vain help: in our watching\l"
    .string "we have watched for a nation that\l"
    .string "could not save us.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_18::
    .string "They hunt our steps, that we cannot\n"
    .string "go in our streets: our end is near,\l"
    .string "our days are fulfilled; for our end\l"
    .string "is come.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_19::
    .string "Our persecutors are swifter than\n"
    .string "the eagles of the heaven: they\l"
    .string "pursued us upon the mountains, they\l"
    .string "laid wait for us in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_20::
    .string "The breath of our nostrils, the\n"
    .string "anointed of the LORD, was taken in\l"
    .string "their pits, of whom we said, Under\l"
    .string "his shadow we shall live among the\l"
    .string "heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_21::
    .string "Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of\n"
    .string "Edom, that dwellest in the land of\l"
    .string "Uz; the cup also shall pass\l"
    .string "through unto thee: thou shalt be\l"
    .string "drunken, and shalt make thyself\l"
    .string "naked.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_4_22::
    .string "The punishment of thine iniquity is\n"
    .string "accomplished, O daughter of Zion;\l"
    .string "he will no more carry thee away into\l"
    .string "captivity: he will visit thine\l"
    .string "iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he\l"
    .string "will discover thy sins.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_1::
    .string "Remember, O LORD, what is come upon\n"
    .string "us: consider, and behold our\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_2::
    .string "Our inheritance is turned to\n"
    .string "strangers, our houses to aliens.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_3::
    .string "We are orphans and fatherless, our\n"
    .string "mothers are as widows.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_4::
    .string "We have drunken our water for money;\n"
    .string "our wood is sold unto us.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_5::
    .string "Our necks are under persecution: we\n"
    .string "labour, and have no rest.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_6::
    .string "We have given the hand to the\n"
    .string "Egyptians, and to the Assyrians, to\l"
    .string "be satisfied with bread.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_7::
    .string "Our fathers have sinned, and are\n"
    .string "not; and we have borne their\l"
    .string "iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_8::
    .string "Servants have ruled over us: there\n"
    .string "is none that doth deliver us out of\l"
    .string "their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_9::
    .string "We gat our bread with the peril of\n"
    .string "our lives because of the sword of\l"
    .string "the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_10::
    .string "Our skin was black like an oven\n"
    .string "because of the terrible famine.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_11::
    .string "They ravished the women in Zion, and\n"
    .string "the maids in the cities of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_12::
    .string "Princes are hanged up by their\n"
    .string "hand: the faces of elders were not\l"
    .string "honoured.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_13::
    .string "They took the young men to grind,\n"
    .string "and the children fell under the\l"
    .string "wood.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_14::
    .string "The elders have ceased from the\n"
    .string "gate, the young men from their musick.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_15::
    .string "The joy of our heart is ceased; our\n"
    .string "dance is turned into mourning.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_16::
    .string "The crown is fallen from our head:\n"
    .string "woe unto us, that we have sinned!"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_17::
    .string "For this our heart is faint; for\n"
    .string "these things our eyes are dim$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_18::
    .string "Because of the mountain of Zion,\n"
    .string "which is desolate, the foxes walk\l"
    .string "upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_19::
    .string "Thou, O LORD, remainest for ever;\n"
    .string "thy throne from generation to\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_20::
    .string "Wherefore dost thou forget us for\n"
    .string "ever, and forsake us so long time?"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_21::
    .string "Turn thou us unto thee, O LORD, and\n"
    .string "we shall be turned; renew our days\l"
    .string "as of old$"
Bible_Text_Lamentations_5_22::
    .string "But thou hast utterly rejected us;\n"
    .string "thou art very wroth against us.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_1::
    .string "Now it came to pass in the\n"
    .string "thirtieth year, in the fourth month,\l"
    .string "in the fifth day of the month, as I\l"
    .string "was among the captives by the river\l"
    .string "of Chebar, that the heavens were\l"
    .string "opened, and I saw visions of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_2::
    .string "In the fifth day of the month, which\n"
    .string "was the fifth year of king\l"
    .string "Jehoiachin’s captivity,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_3::
    .string "The word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "expressly unto Ezekiel the priest,\l"
    .string "the son of Buzi, in the land of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans by the river Chebar; and\l"
    .string "the hand of the LORD was there upon\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_4::
    .string "And I looked, and, behold, a\n"
    .string "whirlwind came out of the north, a\l"
    .string "great cloud, and a fire infolding\l"
    .string "itself, and a brightness was about\l"
    .string "it, and out of the midst thereof as\l"
    .string "the colour of amber, out of the midst\l"
    .string "of the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_5::
    .string "Also out of the midst thereof came\n"
    .string "the likeness of four living\l"
    .string "creatures. And this was their\l"
    .string "appearance; they had the likeness\l"
    .string "of a man.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_6::
    .string "And every one had four faces, and\n"
    .string "every one had four wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_7::
    .string "And their feet were straight feet;\n"
    .string "and the sole of their feet was like\l"
    .string "the sole of a calf’s foot: and they\l"
    .string "sparkled like the colour of\l"
    .string "burnished brass.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_8::
    .string "And they had the hands of a man\n"
    .string "under their wings on their four\l"
    .string "sides; and they four had their faces\l"
    .string "and their wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_9::
    .string "Their wings were joined one to\n"
    .string "another; they turned not when they\l"
    .string "went; they went every one straight\l"
    .string "forward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_10::
    .string "As for the likeness of their faces,\n"
    .string "they four had the face of a man, and\l"
    .string "the face of a lion, on the right\l"
    .string "side: and they four had the face of an\l"
    .string "ox on the left side; they four also\l"
    .string "had the face of an eagle.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_11::
    .string "Thus were their faces: and their\n"
    .string "wings were stretched upward; two\l"
    .string "wings of every one were joined one to\l"
    .string "another, and two covered their\l"
    .string "bodies.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_12::
    .string "And they went every one straight\n"
    .string "forward: whither the spirit was to\l"
    .string "go, they went; and they turned not\l"
    .string "when they went.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_13::
    .string "As for the likeness of the living\n"
    .string "creatures, their appearance was\l"
    .string "like burning coals of fire, and like\l"
    .string "the appearance of lamps: it went\l"
    .string "up and down among the living\l"
    .string "creatures; and the fire was bright,\l"
    .string "and out of the fire went forth\l"
    .string "lightning.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_14::
    .string "And the living creatures ran and\n"
    .string "returned as the appearance of a\l"
    .string "flash of lightning.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_15::
    .string "Now as I beheld the living\n"
    .string "creatures, behold one wheel upon\l"
    .string "the earth by the living creatures,\l"
    .string "with his four faces.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_16::
    .string "The appearance of the wheels and\n"
    .string "their work was like unto the colour\l"
    .string "of a beryl: and they four had one\l"
    .string "likeness: and their appearance and\l"
    .string "their work was as it were a wheel in\l"
    .string "the middle of a wheel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_17::
    .string "When they went, they went upon\n"
    .string "their four sides: and they turned not\l"
    .string "when they went.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_18::
    .string "As for their rings, they were so\n"
    .string "high that they were dreadful; and\l"
    .string "their rings were full of eyes round\l"
    .string "about them four.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_19::
    .string "And when the living creatures went,\n"
    .string "the wheels went by them: and when the\l"
    .string "living creatures were lifted up\l"
    .string "from the earth, the wheels were\l"
    .string "lifted up.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_20::
    .string "Whithersoever the spirit was to go,\n"
    .string "they went, thither was their spirit\l"
    .string "to go; and the wheels were lifted\l"
    .string "up over against them: for the spirit\l"
    .string "of the living creature was in the\l"
    .string "wheels.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_21::
    .string "When those went, these went; and\n"
    .string "when those stood, these stood; and\l"
    .string "when those were lifted up from the\l"
    .string "earth, the wheels were lifted up\l"
    .string "over against them: for the spirit of\l"
    .string "the living creature was in the\l"
    .string "wheels.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_22::
    .string "And the likeness of the firmament\n"
    .string "upon the heads of the living\l"
    .string "creature was as the colour of the\l"
    .string "terrible crystal, stretched forth\l"
    .string "over their heads above.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_23::
    .string "And under the firmament were their\n"
    .string "wings straight, the one toward the\l"
    .string "other: every one had two, which\l"
    .string "covered on this side, and every one\l"
    .string "had two, which covered on that side,\l"
    .string "their bodies.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_24::
    .string "And when they went, I heard the\n"
    .string "noise of their wings, like the noise\l"
    .string "of great waters, as the voice of the\l"
    .string "Almighty, the voice of speech, as\l"
    .string "the noise of an host: when they\l"
    .string "stood, they let down their wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_25::
    .string "And there was a voice from the\n"
    .string "firmament that was over their heads,\l"
    .string "when they stood, and had let down\l"
    .string "their wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_26::
    .string "And above the firmament that was\n"
    .string "over their heads was the likeness of\l"
    .string "a throne, as the appearance of a\l"
    .string "sapphire stone: and upon the\l"
    .string "likeness of the throne was the\l"
    .string "likeness as the appearance of a man\l"
    .string "above upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_27::
    .string "And I saw as the colour of amber, as\n"
    .string "the appearance of fire round about\l"
    .string "within it, from the appearance of\l"
    .string "his loins even upward, and from the\l"
    .string "appearance of his loins even\l"
    .string "downward, I saw as it were the\l"
    .string "appearance of fire, and it had\l"
    .string "brightness round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_1_28::
    .string "As the appearance of the bow that\n"
    .string "is in the cloud in the day of rain,\l"
    .string "so was the appearance of the\l"
    .string "brightness round about. This was the\l"
    .string "appearance of the likeness of the\l"
    .string "glory of the LORD. And when I saw it,\l"
    .string "I fell upon my face, and I heard a\l"
    .string "voice of one that spake.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_1::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "stand upon thy feet, and I will\l"
    .string "speak unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_2::
    .string "And the spirit entered into me when\n"
    .string "he spake unto me, and set me upon my\l"
    .string "feet, that I heard him that spake\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_3::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, I\n"
    .string "send thee to the children of Israel,\l"
    .string "to a rebellious nation that hath\l"
    .string "rebelled against me: they and their\l"
    .string "fathers have transgressed against\l"
    .string "me, even unto this very day.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_4::
    .string "For they are impudent children and\n"
    .string "stiffhearted. I do send thee unto\l"
    .string "them; and thou shalt say unto them,\l"
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_5::
    .string "And they, whether they will hear,\n"
    .string "or whether they will forbear, (for\l"
    .string "they are a rebellious house,) yet\l"
    .string "shall know that there hath been a\l"
    .string "prophet among them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_6::
    .string "And thou, son of man, be not afraid\n"
    .string "of them, neither be afraid of their\l"
    .string "words, though briers and thorns be\l"
    .string "with thee, and thou dost dwell among\l"
    .string "scorpions: be not afraid of their\l"
    .string "words, nor be dismayed at their\l"
    .string "looks, though they be a rebellious\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_7::
    .string "And thou shalt speak my words unto\n"
    .string "them, whether they will hear, or\l"
    .string "whether they will forbear: for they\l"
    .string "are most rebellious.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_8::
    .string "But thou, son of man, hear what I say\n"
    .string "unto thee; Be not thou rebellious\l"
    .string "like that rebellious house: open\l"
    .string "thy mouth, and eat that I give thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_9::
    .string "And when I looked, behold, an hand\n"
    .string "was sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of\l"
    .string "a book was therein;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_2_10::
    .string "And he spread it before me; and it\n"
    .string "was written within and without: and\l"
    .string "there was written therein\l"
    .string "lamentations, and mourning, and woe$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_1::
    .string "Moreover he said unto me, Son of\n"
    .string "man, eat that thou findest; eat this\l"
    .string "roll, and go speak unto the house\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_2::
    .string "So I opened my mouth, and he caused\n"
    .string "me to eat that roll.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_3::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "cause thy belly to eat, and fill\l"
    .string "thy bowels with this roll that I\l"
    .string "give thee. Then did I eat it; and it\l"
    .string "was in my mouth as honey for\l"
    .string "sweetness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_4::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, go,\n"
    .string "get thee unto the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "and speak with my words unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_5::
    .string "For thou art not sent to a people\n"
    .string "of a strange speech and of an hard\l"
    .string "language, but to the house of\l"
    .string "Israel;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_6::
    .string "Not to many people of a strange\n"
    .string "speech and of an hard language,\l"
    .string "whose words thou canst not understand\l"
    .string " Surely, had I sent thee to them,\l"
    .string "they would have hearkened unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_7::
    .string "But the house of Israel will not\n"
    .string "hearken unto thee; for they will not\l"
    .string "hearken unto me: for all the house\l"
    .string "of Israel are impudent and\l"
    .string "hardhearted.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_8::
    .string "Behold, I have made thy face strong\n"
    .string "against their faces, and thy forehead\l"
    .string "strong against their foreheads.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_9::
    .string "As an adamant harder than flint\n"
    .string "have I made thy forehead: fear them\l"
    .string "not, neither be dismayed at their\l"
    .string "looks, though they be a rebellious\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_10::
    .string "Moreover he said unto me, Son of\n"
    .string "man, all my words that I shall\l"
    .string "speak unto thee receive in thine\l"
    .string "heart, and hear with thine ears.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_11::
    .string "And go, get thee to them of the\n"
    .string "captivity, unto the children of thy\l"
    .string "people, and speak unto them, and\l"
    .string "tell them, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "whether they will hear, or whether\l"
    .string "they will forbear.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_12::
    .string "Then the spirit took me up, and I\n"
    .string "heard behind me a voice of a great\l"
    .string "rushing, saying, Blessed be the\l"
    .string "glory of the LORD from his place.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_13::
    .string "I heard also the noise of the wings\n"
    .string "of the living creatures that touched\l"
    .string "one another, and the noise of the\l"
    .string "wheels over against them, and a\l"
    .string "noise of a great rushing.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_14::
    .string "So the spirit lifted me up, and\n"
    .string "took me away, and I went in\l"
    .string "bitterness, in the heat of my\l"
    .string "spirit; but the hand of the LORD was\l"
    .string "strong upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_15::
    .string "Then I came to them of the\n"
    .string "captivity at Telabib, that dwelt by\l"
    .string "the river of Chebar, and I sat where\l"
    .string "they sat, and remained there\l"
    .string "astonished among them seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_16::
    .string "And it came to pass at the end of\n"
    .string "seven days, that the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_17::
    .string "Son of man, I have made thee a\n"
    .string "watchman unto the house of Israel:\l"
    .string "therefore hear the word at my mouth,\l"
    .string "and give them warning from me$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_18::
    .string "When I say unto the wicked, Thou\n"
    .string "shalt surely die; and thou givest\l"
    .string "him not warning, nor speakest to\l"
    .string "warn the wicked from his wicked way,\l"
    .string "to save his life; the same wicked man\l"
    .string "shall die in his iniquity; but his\l"
    .string "blood will I require at thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_19::
    .string "Yet if thou warn the wicked, and he\n"
    .string "turn not from his wickedness, nor\l"
    .string "from his wicked way, he shall die in\l"
    .string "his iniquity; but thou hast\l"
    .string "delivered thy soul.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_20::
    .string "Again, When a righteous man doth\n"
    .string "turn from his righteousness, and\l"
    .string "commit iniquity, and I lay a\l"
    .string "stumbling-block before him, he\l"
    .string "shall die: because thou hast not\l"
    .string "given him warning, he shall die in\l"
    .string "his sin, and his righteousness which\l"
    .string "he hath done shall not be\l"
    .string "remembered; but his blood will I\l"
    .string "require at thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_21::
    .string "Nevertheless if thou warn the\n"
    .string "righteous man, that the righteous sin\l"
    .string "not, and he doth not sin, he shall\l"
    .string "surely live, because he is warned;\l"
    .string "also thou hast delivered thy soul.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_22::
    .string "And the hand of the LORD was there\n"
    .string "upon me; and he said unto me, Arise,\l"
    .string "go forth into the plain, and I will\l"
    .string "there talk with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_23::
    .string "Then I arose, and went forth into\n"
    .string "the plain: and, behold, the glory\l"
    .string "of the LORD stood there, as the glory\l"
    .string "which I saw by the river of Chebar:\l"
    .string "and I fell on my face.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_24::
    .string "Then the spirit entered into me,\n"
    .string "and set me upon my feet, and spake\l"
    .string "with me, and said unto me, Go, shut\l"
    .string "thyself within thine house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_25::
    .string "But thou, O son of man, behold, they\n"
    .string "shall put bands upon thee, and\l"
    .string "shall bind thee with them, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt not go out among them:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_26::
    .string "And I will make thy tongue cleave\n"
    .string "to the roof of thy mouth, that thou\l"
    .string "shalt be dumb, and shalt not be to\l"
    .string "them a reprover: for they are a\l"
    .string "rebellious house$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_3_27::
    .string "But when I speak with thee, I will\n"
    .string "open thy mouth, and thou shalt say\l"
    .string "unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "He that heareth, let him hear; and he\l"
    .string "that forbeareth, let him forbear:\l"
    .string "for they are a rebellious house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_1::
    .string "Thou also, son of man, take thee a\n"
    .string "tile, and lay it before thee, and\l"
    .string "pourtray upon it the city, even\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_2::
    .string "And lay siege against it, and build\n"
    .string "a fort against it, and cast a mount\l"
    .string "against it; set the camp also\l"
    .string "against it, and set battering rams\l"
    .string "against it round about$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_3::
    .string "Moreover take thou unto thee an iron\n"
    .string "pan, and set it for a wall of iron\l"
    .string "between thee and the city: and set\l"
    .string "thy face against it, and it shall be\l"
    .string "besieged, and thou shalt lay siege\l"
    .string "against it. This shall be a sign to\l"
    .string "the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_4::
    .string "Lie thou also upon thy left side,\n"
    .string "and lay the iniquity of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel upon it: according to the\l"
    .string "number of the days that thou shalt\l"
    .string "lie upon it thou shalt bear their\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_5::
    .string "For I have laid upon thee the years\n"
    .string "of their iniquity, according to the\l"
    .string "number of the days, three hundred and\l"
    .string "ninety days: so shalt thou bear the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_6::
    .string "And when thou hast accomplished\n"
    .string "them, lie again on thy right side,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt bear the iniquity of\l"
    .string "the house of Judah forty days: I have\l"
    .string "appointed thee each day for a year.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_7::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt set thy face\n"
    .string "toward the siege of Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "thine arm shall be uncovered, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt prophesy against it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_8::
    .string "And, behold, I will lay bands\n"
    .string "upon thee, and thou shalt not turn\l"
    .string "thee from one side to another, till\l"
    .string "thou hast ended the days of thy siege.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_9::
    .string "Take thou also unto thee wheat, and\n"
    .string "barley, and beans, and lentiles,\l"
    .string "and millet, and fitches, and put\l"
    .string "them in one vessel, and make thee\l"
    .string "bread thereof, according to the\l"
    .string "number of the days that thou shalt\l"
    .string "lie upon thy side, three hundred and\l"
    .string "ninety days shalt thou eat thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_10::
    .string "And thy meat which thou shalt eat\n"
    .string "shall be by weight, twenty shekels\l"
    .string "a day: from time to time shalt thou\l"
    .string "eat it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_11::
    .string "Thou shalt drink also water by\n"
    .string "measure, the sixth part of an hin:\l"
    .string "from time to time shalt thou drink.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_12::
    .string "And thou shalt eat it as barley\n"
    .string "cakes, and thou shalt bake it with\l"
    .string "dung that cometh out of man, in their\l"
    .string "sight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_13::
    .string "And the LORD said, Even thus shall\n"
    .string "the children of Israel eat their\l"
    .string "defiled bread among the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "whither I will drive them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_14::
    .string "Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! behold, my\n"
    .string "soul hath not been polluted: for\l"
    .string "from my youth up even till now have\l"
    .string "I not eaten of that which dieth of\l"
    .string "itself, or is torn in pieces;\l"
    .string "neither came there abominable flesh\l"
    .string "into my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_15::
    .string "Then he said unto me, Lo, I have\n"
    .string "given thee cow’s dung for man’s dung,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt prepare thy bread\l"
    .string "therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_16::
    .string "Moreover he said unto me, Son of\n"
    .string "man, behold, I will break the staff\l"
    .string "of bread in Jerusalem: and they\l"
    .string "shall eat bread by weight, and with\l"
    .string "care; and they shall drink water by\l"
    .string "measure, and with astonishment:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_4_17::
    .string "That they may want bread and water,\n"
    .string "and be astonied one with another, and\l"
    .string "consume away for their iniquity$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_1::
    .string "And thou, son of man, take thee a\n"
    .string "sharp knife, take thee a barber’s\l"
    .string "razor, and cause it to pass upon\l"
    .string "thine head and upon thy beard: then\l"
    .string "take thee balances to weigh, and\l"
    .string "divide the hair.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_2::
    .string "Thou shalt burn with fire a third\n"
    .string "part in the midst of the city, when\l"
    .string "the days of the siege are\l"
    .string "fulfilled: and thou shalt take a\l"
    .string "third part, and smite about it with a\l"
    .string "knife: and a third part thou shalt\l"
    .string "scatter in the wind; and I will draw\l"
    .string "out a sword after them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_3::
    .string "Thou shalt also take thereof a few\n"
    .string "in number, and bind them in thy\l"
    .string "skirts.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_4::
    .string "Then take of them again, and cast\n"
    .string "them into the midst of the fire, and\l"
    .string "burn them in the fire; for thereof\l"
    .string "shall a fire come forth into all\l"
    .string "the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_5::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; This is\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: I have set it in the midst\l"
    .string "of the nations and countries that are\l"
    .string "round about her.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_6::
    .string "And she hath changed my judgments\n"
    .string "into wickedness more than the\l"
    .string "nations, and my statutes more than\l"
    .string "the countries that are round about\l"
    .string "her: for they have refused my\l"
    .string "judgments and my statutes, they have\l"
    .string "not walked in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_7::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because ye multiplied more than\l"
    .string "the nations that are round about you,\l"
    .string "and have not walked in my statutes,\l"
    .string "neither have kept my judgments,\l"
    .string "neither have done according to the\l"
    .string "judgments of the nations that are\l"
    .string "round about you;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_8::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I, even I, am against thee,\l"
    .string "and will execute judgments in the\l"
    .string "midst of thee in the sight of the\l"
    .string "nations$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_9::
    .string "And I will do in thee that which I\n"
    .string "have not done, and whereunto I will\l"
    .string "not do any more the like, because of\l"
    .string "all thine abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_10::
    .string "Therefore the fathers shall eat\n"
    .string "the sons in the midst of thee, and the\l"
    .string "sons shall eat their fathers; and I\l"
    .string "will execute judgments in thee, and\l"
    .string "the whole remnant of thee will I\l"
    .string "scatter into all the winds.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_11::
    .string "Wherefore, as I live, saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD; Surely, because thou hast\l"
    .string "defiled my sanctuary with all thy\l"
    .string "detestable things, and with all\l"
    .string "thine abominations, therefore will\l"
    .string "I also diminish thee; neither shall\l"
    .string "mine eye spare, neither will I have\l"
    .string "any pity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_12::
    .string "A third part of thee shall die\n"
    .string "with the pestilence, and with\l"
    .string "famine shall they be consumed in\l"
    .string "the midst of thee: and a third part\l"
    .string "shall fall by the sword round\l"
    .string "about thee; and I will scatter a\l"
    .string "third part into all the winds, and\l"
    .string "I will draw out a sword after them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_13::
    .string "Thus shall mine anger be\n"
    .string "accomplished, and I will cause my\l"
    .string "fury to rest upon them, and I will\l"
    .string "be comforted: and they shall know\l"
    .string "that I the LORD have spoken it in my\l"
    .string "zeal, when I have accomplished my\l"
    .string "fury in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_14::
    .string "Moreover I will make thee waste,\n"
    .string "and a reproach among the nations\l"
    .string "that are round about thee, in the\l"
    .string "sight of all that pass by.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_15::
    .string "So it shall be a reproach and a\n"
    .string "taunt, an instruction and an\l"
    .string "astonishment unto the nations that\l"
    .string "are round about thee, when I shall\l"
    .string "execute judgments in thee in anger\l"
    .string "and in fury and in furious rebukes. I\l"
    .string "the LORD have spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_16::
    .string "When I shall send upon them the\n"
    .string "evil arrows of famine, which shall\l"
    .string "be for their destruction, and which I\l"
    .string "will send to destroy you: and I\l"
    .string "will increase the famine upon you,\l"
    .string "and will break your staff of bread:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_5_17::
    .string "So will I send upon you famine and\n"
    .string "evil beasts, and they shall bereave\l"
    .string "thee: and pestilence and blood\l"
    .string "shall pass through thee; and I\l"
    .string "will bring the sword upon thee. I\l"
    .string "the LORD have spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face toward the\n"
    .string "mountains of Israel, and prophesy\l"
    .string "against them,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_3::
    .string "And say, Ye mountains of Israel,\n"
    .string "hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD to the mountains,\l"
    .string "and to the hills, to the rivers, and\l"
    .string "to the valleys; Behold, I, even I,\l"
    .string "will bring a sword upon you, and I\l"
    .string "will destroy your high places$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_4::
    .string "And your altars shall be\n"
    .string "desolate, and your images shall be\l"
    .string "broken: and I will cast down your\l"
    .string "slain men before your idols.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_5::
    .string "And I will lay the dead carcases\n"
    .string "of the children of Israel before\l"
    .string "their idols; and I will scatter\l"
    .string "your bones round about your altars.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_6::
    .string "In all your dwellingplaces the\n"
    .string "cities shall be laid waste, and the\l"
    .string "high places shall be desolate;\l"
    .string "that your altars may be laid waste\l"
    .string "and made desolate, and your idols\l"
    .string "may be broken and cease, and your\l"
    .string "images may be cut down, and your\l"
    .string "works may be abolished.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_7::
    .string "And the slain shall fall in the\n"
    .string "midst of you, and ye shall know that\l"
    .string "I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_8::
    .string "Yet will I leave a remnant, that\n"
    .string "ye may have some that shall escape\l"
    .string "the sword among the nations, when ye\l"
    .string "shall be scattered through the\l"
    .string "countries.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_9::
    .string "And they that escape of you shall\n"
    .string "remember me among the nations\l"
    .string "whither they shall be carried\l"
    .string "captives, because I am broken with\l"
    .string "their whorish heart, which hath\l"
    .string "departed from me, and with their\l"
    .string "eyes, which go a whoring after their\l"
    .string "idols: and they shall lothe\l"
    .string "themselves for the evils which they\l"
    .string "have committed in all their\l"
    .string "abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_10::
    .string "And they shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, and that I have not said in vain\l"
    .string "that I would do this evil unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_11::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Smite with\n"
    .string "thine hand, and stamp with thy foot,\l"
    .string "and say, Alas for all the evil\l"
    .string "abominations of the house of Israel!\l"
    .string "for they shall fall by the sword,\l"
    .string "by the famine, and by the\l"
    .string "pestilence.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_12::
    .string "He that is far off shall die of the\n"
    .string "pestilence; and he that is near\l"
    .string "shall fall by the sword; and he\l"
    .string "that remaineth and is besieged\l"
    .string "shall die by the famine: thus will\l"
    .string "I accomplish my fury upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_13::
    .string "Then shall ye know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when their slain men shall be\l"
    .string "among their idols round about their\l"
    .string "altars, upon every high hill, in\l"
    .string "all the tops of the mountains, and\l"
    .string "under every green tree, and under\l"
    .string "every thick oak, the place where\l"
    .string "they did offer sweet savour to all\l"
    .string "their idols.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_6_14::
    .string "So will I stretch out my hand upon\n"
    .string "them, and make the land desolate,\l"
    .string "yea, more desolate than the\l"
    .string "wilderness toward Diblath, in all\l"
    .string "their habitations: and they shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_1::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_2::
    .string "Also, thou son of man, thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD unto the land of\l"
    .string "Israel; An end, the end is come upon\l"
    .string "the four corners of the land$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_3::
    .string "Now is the end come upon thee, and I\n"
    .string "will send mine anger upon thee, and\l"
    .string "will judge thee according to thy\l"
    .string "ways, and will recompense upon\l"
    .string "thee all thine abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_4::
    .string "And mine eye shall not spare thee,\n"
    .string "neither will I have pity: but I\l"
    .string "will recompense thy ways upon\l"
    .string "thee, and thine abominations shall\l"
    .string "be in the midst of thee: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_5::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; An evil, an\n"
    .string "only evil, behold, is come.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_6::
    .string "An end is come, the end is come: it\n"
    .string "watcheth for thee; behold, it is\l"
    .string "come.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_7::
    .string "The morning is come unto thee, O\n"
    .string "thou that dwellest in the land: the\l"
    .string "time is come, the day of trouble is\l"
    .string "near, and not the sounding again of\l"
    .string "the mountains.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_8::
    .string "Now will I shortly pour out my\n"
    .string "fury upon thee, and accomplish mine\l"
    .string "anger upon thee: and I will judge\l"
    .string "thee according to thy ways, and will\l"
    .string "recompense thee for all thine\l"
    .string "abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_9::
    .string "And mine eye shall not spare,\n"
    .string "neither will I have pity: I will\l"
    .string "recompense thee according to thy\l"
    .string "ways and thine abominations that are\l"
    .string "in the midst of thee; and ye shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD that smiteth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_10::
    .string "Behold the day, behold, it is come:\n"
    .string "the morning is gone forth; the rod\l"
    .string "hath blossomed, pride hath budded.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_11::
    .string "Violence is risen up into a rod of\n"
    .string "wickedness: none of them shall\l"
    .string "remain, nor of their multitude, nor\l"
    .string "of any of theirs: neither shall\l"
    .string "there be wailing for them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_12::
    .string "The time is come, the day draweth\n"
    .string "near: let not the buyer rejoice, nor\l"
    .string "the seller mourn: for wrath is upon\l"
    .string "all the multitude thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_13::
    .string "For the seller shall not return\n"
    .string "to that which is sold, although they\l"
    .string "were yet alive: for the vision is\l"
    .string "touching the whole multitude\l"
    .string "thereof, which shall not return;\l"
    .string "neither shall any strengthen\l"
    .string "himself in the iniquity of his life.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_14::
    .string "They have blown the trumpet, even\n"
    .string "to make all ready; but none goeth to\l"
    .string "the battle: for my wrath is upon\l"
    .string "all the multitude thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_15::
    .string "The sword is without, and the\n"
    .string "pestilence and the famine within: he\l"
    .string "that is in the field shall die with\l"
    .string "the sword; and he that is in the city,\l"
    .string "famine and pestilence shall\l"
    .string "devour him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_16::
    .string "But they that escape of them shall\n"
    .string "escape, and shall be on the\l"
    .string "mountains like doves of the\l"
    .string "valleys, all of them mourning,\l"
    .string "every one for his iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_17::
    .string "All hands shall be feeble, and\n"
    .string "all knees shall be weak as water.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_18::
    .string "They shall also gird themselves\n"
    .string "with sackcloth, and horror shall\l"
    .string "cover them; and shame shall be upon\l"
    .string "all faces, and baldness upon all\l"
    .string "their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_19::
    .string "They shall cast their silver in\n"
    .string "the streets, and their gold shall\l"
    .string "be removed: their silver and their\l"
    .string "gold shall not be able to deliver\l"
    .string "them in the day of the wrath of the\l"
    .string "LORD: they shall not satisfy their\l"
    .string "souls, neither fill their bowels:\l"
    .string "because it is the stumblingblock of\l"
    .string "their iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_20::
    .string "As for the beauty of his ornament,\n"
    .string "he set it in majesty: but they made\l"
    .string "the images of their abominations and\l"
    .string "of their detestable things therein:\l"
    .string "therefore have I set it far from them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_21::
    .string "And I will give it into the hands\n"
    .string "of the strangers for a prey, and to\l"
    .string "the wicked of the earth for a spoil;\l"
    .string "and they shall pollute it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_22::
    .string "My face will I turn also from\n"
    .string "them, and they shall pollute my\l"
    .string "secret place: for the robbers\l"
    .string "shall enter into it, and defile it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_23::
    .string "Make a chain: for the land is full\n"
    .string "of bloody crimes, and the city is\l"
    .string "full of violence.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_24::
    .string "Wherefore I will bring the worst\n"
    .string "of the heathen, and they shall\l"
    .string "possess their houses: I will also\l"
    .string "make the pomp of the strong to\l"
    .string "cease; and their holy places\l"
    .string "shall be defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_25::
    .string "Destruction cometh; and they shall\n"
    .string "seek peace, and there shall be none.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_26::
    .string "Mischief shall come upon\n"
    .string "mischief, and rumour shall be upon\l"
    .string "rumour; then shall they seek a\l"
    .string "vision of the prophet; but the law\l"
    .string "shall perish from the priest, and\l"
    .string "counsel from the ancients.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_7_27::
    .string "The king shall mourn, and the\n"
    .string "prince shall be clothed with\l"
    .string "desolation, and the hands of the\l"
    .string "people of the land shall be\l"
    .string "troubled: I will do unto them after\l"
    .string "their way, and according to their\l"
    .string "deserts will I judge them; and they\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the sixth\n"
    .string "year, in the sixth month, in the\l"
    .string "fifth day of the month, as I sat in\l"
    .string "mine house, and the elders of Judah\l"
    .string "sat before me, that the hand of the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD fell there upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_2::
    .string "Then I beheld, and lo a likeness\n"
    .string "as the appearance of fire: from the\l"
    .string "appearance of his loins even\l"
    .string "downward, fire; and from his loins\l"
    .string "even upward, as the appearance of\l"
    .string "brightness, as the colour of amber.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_3::
    .string "And he put forth the form of an\n"
    .string "hand, and took me by a lock of mine\l"
    .string "head; and the spirit lifted me up\l"
    .string "between the earth and the heaven, and\l"
    .string "brought me in the visions of God to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, to the door of the inner\l"
    .string "gate that looketh toward the north;\l"
    .string "where was the seat of the image of\l"
    .string "jealousy, which provoketh to\l"
    .string "jealousy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_4::
    .string "And, behold, the glory of the God\n"
    .string "of Israel was there, according to\l"
    .string "the vision that I saw in the plain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_5::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "lift up thine eyes now the way\l"
    .string "toward the north. So I lifted up\l"
    .string "mine eyes the way toward the north,\l"
    .string "and behold northward at the gate of\l"
    .string "the altar this image of jealousy in\l"
    .string "the entry.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_6::
    .string "He said furthermore unto me, Son of\n"
    .string "man, seest thou what they do? even\l"
    .string "the great abominations that the\l"
    .string "house of Israel committeth here,\l"
    .string "that I should go far off from my\l"
    .string "sanctuary? but turn thee yet again,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt see greater\l"
    .string "abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_7::
    .string "And he brought me to the door of the\n"
    .string "court; and when I looked, behold a\l"
    .string "hole in the wall.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_8::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Son of man, dig\n"
    .string "now in the wall: and when I had\l"
    .string "digged in the wall, behold a door.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_9::
    .string "And he said unto me, Go in, and\n"
    .string "behold the wicked abominations that\l"
    .string "they do here.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_10::
    .string "So I went in and saw; and behold\n"
    .string "every form of creeping things, and\l"
    .string "abominable beasts, and all the\l"
    .string "idols of the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "pourtrayed upon the wall round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_11::
    .string "And there stood before them seventy\n"
    .string "men of the ancients of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, and in the midst of them\l"
    .string "stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan,\l"
    .string "with every man his censer in his\l"
    .string "hand; and a thick cloud of incense\l"
    .string "went up.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_12::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "hast thou seen what the ancients of\l"
    .string "the house of Israel do in the dark,\l"
    .string "every man in the chambers of his\l"
    .string "imagery? for they say, the LORD seeth\l"
    .string "us not; the LORD hath forsaken the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_13::
    .string "He said also unto me, Turn thee yet\n"
    .string "again, and thou shalt see greater\l"
    .string "abominations that they do.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_14::
    .string "Then he brought me to the door of\n"
    .string "the gate of the LORD’s house which\l"
    .string "was toward the north; and, behold,\l"
    .string "there sat women weeping for Tammuz.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_15::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Hast thou seen\n"
    .string "this, O son of man? turn thee yet\l"
    .string "again, and thou shalt see greater\l"
    .string "abominations than these.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_16::
    .string "And he brought me into the inner\n"
    .string "court of the LORD’s house, and,\l"
    .string "behold, at the door of the temple\l"
    .string "of the LORD, between the porch and\l"
    .string "the altar, were about five and\l"
    .string "twenty men, with their backs toward\l"
    .string "the temple of the LORD, and their\l"
    .string "faces toward the east; and they\l"
    .string "worshipped the sun toward the east.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_17::
    .string "Then he said unto me, Hast thou seen\n"
    .string "this, O son of man? Is it a light\l"
    .string "thing to the house of Judah that they\l"
    .string "commit the abominations which they\l"
    .string "commit here? for they have filled\l"
    .string "the land with violence, and have\l"
    .string "returned to provoke me to anger:\l"
    .string "and, lo, they put the branch to\l"
    .string "their nose.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_8_18::
    .string "Therefore will I also deal in\n"
    .string "fury: mine eye shall not spare,\l"
    .string "neither will I have pity: and\l"
    .string "though they cry in mine ears with a\l"
    .string "loud voice, yet will I not hear them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_1::
    .string "He cried also in mine ears with a\n"
    .string "loud voice, saying, Cause them that\l"
    .string "have charge over the city to draw\l"
    .string "near, even every man with his\l"
    .string "destroying weapon in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_2::
    .string "And, behold, six men came from the\n"
    .string "way of the higher gate, which lieth\l"
    .string "toward the north, and every man a\l"
    .string "slaughter weapon in his hand; and\l"
    .string "one man among them was clothed with\l"
    .string "linen, with a writer’s inkhorn by his\l"
    .string "side: and they went in, and stood\l"
    .string "beside the brasen altar.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_3::
    .string "And the glory of the God of Israel\n"
    .string "was gone up from the cherub,\l"
    .string "whereupon he was, to the threshold\l"
    .string "of the house. And he called to the\l"
    .string "man clothed with linen, which had\l"
    .string "the writer’s inkhorn by his side;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_4::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Go\n"
    .string "through the midst of the city,\l"
    .string "through the midst of Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "set a mark upon the foreheads of the\l"
    .string "men that sigh and that cry for all\l"
    .string "the abominations that be done in the\l"
    .string "midst thereof$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_5::
    .string "And to the others he said in mine\n"
    .string "hearing, Go ye after him through the\l"
    .string "city, and smite: let not your eye\l"
    .string "spare, neither have ye pity:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_6::
    .string "Slay utterly old and young, both\n"
    .string "maids, and little children, and\l"
    .string "women: but come not near any man upon\l"
    .string "whom is the mark; and begin at my\l"
    .string "sanctuary. Then they began at the\l"
    .string "ancient men which were before the\l"
    .string "house$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_7::
    .string "And he said unto them, Defile the\n"
    .string "house, and fill the courts with the\l"
    .string "slain: go ye forth. And they went\l"
    .string "forth, and slew in the city.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, while they\n"
    .string "were slaying them, and I was left,\l"
    .string "that I fell upon my face, and\l"
    .string "cried, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt\l"
    .string "thou destroy all the residue of\l"
    .string "Israel in thy pouring out of thy\l"
    .string "fury upon Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_9::
    .string "Then said he unto me, The iniquity\n"
    .string "of the house of Israel and Judah is\l"
    .string "exceeding great, and the land is\l"
    .string "full of blood, and the city full\l"
    .string "of perverseness: for they say, The\l"
    .string "LORD hath forsaken the earth, and the\l"
    .string "LORD seeth not$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_10::
    .string "And as for me also, mine eye shall\n"
    .string "not spare, neither will I have\l"
    .string "pity, but I will recompense their\l"
    .string "way upon their head.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_9_11::
    .string "And, behold, the man clothed with\n"
    .string "linen, which had the inkhorn by his\l"
    .string "side, reported the matter, saying, I\l"
    .string "have done as thou hast commanded me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_1::
    .string "Then I looked, and, behold, in the\n"
    .string "firmament that was above the head of\l"
    .string "the cherubims there appeared over\l"
    .string "them as it were a sapphire stone, as\l"
    .string "the appearance of the likeness of a\l"
    .string "throne.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_2::
    .string "And he spake unto the man clothed\n"
    .string "with linen, and said, Go in between\l"
    .string "the wheels, even under the cherub,\l"
    .string "and fill thine hand with coals of\l"
    .string "fire from between the cherubims, and\l"
    .string "scatter them over the city. And he\l"
    .string "went in in my sight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_3::
    .string "Now the cherubims stood on the right\n"
    .string "side of the house, when the man went\l"
    .string "in; and the cloud filled the inner\l"
    .string "court.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_4::
    .string "Then the glory of the LORD went up\n"
    .string "from the cherub, and stood over the\l"
    .string "threshold of the house; and the\l"
    .string "house was filled with the cloud,\l"
    .string "and the court was full of the\l"
    .string "brightness of the LORD’s glory.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_5::
    .string "And the sound of the cherubims’\n"
    .string "wings was heard even to the outer\l"
    .string "court, as the voice of the Almighty\l"
    .string "God when he speaketh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when he\n"
    .string "had commanded the man clothed with\l"
    .string "linen, saying, Take fire from between\l"
    .string "the wheels, from between the\l"
    .string "cherubims; then he went in, and stood\l"
    .string "beside the wheels.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_7::
    .string "And one cherub stretched forth his\n"
    .string "hand from between the cherubims unto\l"
    .string "the fire that was between the\l"
    .string "cherubims, and took thereof, and put\l"
    .string "it into the hands of him that was\l"
    .string "clothed with linen: who took it, and\l"
    .string "went out.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_8::
    .string "And there appeared in the\n"
    .string "cherubims the form of a man’s hand\l"
    .string "under their wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_9::
    .string "And when I looked, behold the four\n"
    .string "wheels by the cherubims, one wheel\l"
    .string "by one cherub, and another wheel by\l"
    .string "another cherub: and the appearance\l"
    .string "of the wheels was as the colour of a\l"
    .string "beryl stone.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_10::
    .string "And as for their appearances, they\n"
    .string "four had one likeness, as if a wheel\l"
    .string "had been in the midst of a wheel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_11::
    .string "When they went, they went upon\n"
    .string "their four sides; they turned not as\l"
    .string "they went, but to the place whither\l"
    .string "the head looked they followed it;\l"
    .string "they turned not as they went.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_12::
    .string "And their whole body, and their\n"
    .string "backs, and their hands, and their\l"
    .string "wings, and the wheels, were full of\l"
    .string "eyes round about, even the wheels\l"
    .string "that they four had.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_13::
    .string "As for the wheels, it was cried unto\n"
    .string "them in my hearing, O wheel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_14::
    .string "And every one had four faces: the\n"
    .string "first face was the face of a cherub,\l"
    .string "and the second face was the face of a\l"
    .string "man, and the third the face of a\l"
    .string "lion, and the fourth the face of an\l"
    .string "eagle.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_15::
    .string "And the cherubims were lifted up.\n"
    .string "This is the living creature that I\l"
    .string "saw by the river of Chebar.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_16::
    .string "And when the cherubims went, the\n"
    .string "wheels went by them: and when the\l"
    .string "cherubims lifted up their wings to\l"
    .string "mount up from the earth, the same\l"
    .string "wheels also turned not from beside\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_17::
    .string "When they stood, these stood; and\n"
    .string "when they were lifted up, these\l"
    .string "lifted up themselves also: for the\l"
    .string "spirit of the living creature was\l"
    .string "in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_18::
    .string "Then the glory of the LORD\n"
    .string "departed from off the threshold of\l"
    .string "the house, and stood over the\l"
    .string "cherubims.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_19::
    .string "And the cherubims lifted up their\n"
    .string "wings, and mounted up from the earth\l"
    .string "in my sight: when they went out, the\l"
    .string "wheels also were beside them, and\l"
    .string "every one stood at the door of the\l"
    .string "east gate of the LORD’s house; and\l"
    .string "the glory of the God of Israel was\l"
    .string "over them above.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_20::
    .string "This is the living creature that I\n"
    .string "saw under the God of Israel by the\l"
    .string "river of Chebar; and I knew that they\l"
    .string "were the cherubims.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_21::
    .string "Every one had four faces apiece,\n"
    .string "and every one four wings; and the\l"
    .string "likeness of the hands of a man was\l"
    .string "under their wings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_10_22::
    .string "And the likeness of their faces was\n"
    .string "the same faces which I saw by the\l"
    .string "river of Chebar, their appearances\l"
    .string "and themselves: they went every one\l"
    .string "straight forward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_1::
    .string "Moreover the spirit lifted me up,\n"
    .string "and brought me unto the east gate of\l"
    .string "the LORD’s house, which looketh\l"
    .string "eastward: and behold at the door of\l"
    .string "the gate five and twenty men; among\l"
    .string "whom I saw Jaazaniah the son of Azur,\l"
    .string "and Pelatiah the son of Benaiah,\l"
    .string "princes of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_2::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "these are the men that devise\l"
    .string "mischief, and give wicked counsel in\l"
    .string "this city:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_3::
    .string "Which say, It is not near; let us\n"
    .string "build houses: this city is the\l"
    .string "caldron, and we be the flesh$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_4::
    .string "Therefore prophesy against them,\n"
    .string "prophesy, O son of man.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_5::
    .string "And the Spirit of the LORD fell\n"
    .string "upon me, and said unto me, Speak;\l"
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Thus have ye\l"
    .string "said, O house of Israel: for I know\l"
    .string "the things that come into your mind,\l"
    .string "every one of them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_6::
    .string "Ye have multiplied your slain in\n"
    .string "this city, and ye have filled the\l"
    .string "streets thereof with the slain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_7::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Your slain whom ye have laid in the\l"
    .string "midst of it, they are the flesh, and\l"
    .string "this city is the caldron: but I\l"
    .string "will bring you forth out of the\l"
    .string "midst of it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_8::
    .string "Ye have feared the sword; and I\n"
    .string "will bring a sword upon you, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_9::
    .string "And I will bring you out of the\n"
    .string "midst thereof, and deliver you into\l"
    .string "the hands of strangers, and will\l"
    .string "execute judgments among you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_10::
    .string "Ye shall fall by the sword; I\n"
    .string "will judge you in the border of\l"
    .string "Israel; and ye shall know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_11::
    .string "This city shall not be your\n"
    .string "caldron, neither shall ye be the\l"
    .string "flesh in the midst thereof; but I\l"
    .string "will judge you in the border of\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_12::
    .string "And ye shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD: for ye have not walked in my\l"
    .string "statutes, neither executed my\l"
    .string "judgments, but have done after the\l"
    .string "manners of the heathen that are round\l"
    .string "about you$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_13::
    .string "And it came to pass, when I\n"
    .string "prophesied, that Pelatiah the son\l"
    .string "of Benaiah died. Then fell I down\l"
    .string "upon my face, and cried with a loud\l"
    .string "voice, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt\l"
    .string "thou make a full end of the remnant\l"
    .string "of Israel?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_14::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_15::
    .string "Son of man, thy brethren, even thy\n"
    .string "brethren, the men of thy kindred, and\l"
    .string "all the house of Israel wholly,\l"
    .string "are they unto whom the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem have said, Get you far\l"
    .string "from the LORD: unto us is this land\l"
    .string "given in possession$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_16::
    .string "Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD; Although I have cast them far\l"
    .string "off among the heathen, and although\l"
    .string "I have scattered them among the\l"
    .string "countries, yet will I be to them as\l"
    .string "a little sanctuary in the countries\l"
    .string "where they shall come.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_17::
    .string "Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD; I will even gather you from the\l"
    .string "people, and assemble you out of the\l"
    .string "countries where ye have been\l"
    .string "scattered, and I will give you the\l"
    .string "land of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_18::
    .string "And they shall come thither, and\n"
    .string "they shall take away all the\l"
    .string "detestable things thereof and all\l"
    .string "the abominations thereof from thence.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_19::
    .string "And I will give them one heart, and\n"
    .string "I will put a new spirit within you;\l"
    .string "and I will take the stony heart out\l"
    .string "of their flesh, and will give them\l"
    .string "an heart of flesh:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_20::
    .string "That they may walk in my statutes,\n"
    .string "and keep mine ordinances, and do\l"
    .string "them: and they shall be my people,\l"
    .string "and I will be their God$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_21::
    .string "But as for them whose heart walketh\n"
    .string "after the heart of their detestable\l"
    .string "things and their abominations, I\l"
    .string "will recompense their way upon\l"
    .string "their own heads, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_22::
    .string "Then did the cherubims lift up\n"
    .string "their wings, and the wheels beside\l"
    .string "them; and the glory of the God of\l"
    .string "Israel was over them above.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_23::
    .string "And the glory of the LORD went up\n"
    .string "from the midst of the city, and stood\l"
    .string "upon the mountain which is on the\l"
    .string "east side of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_24::
    .string "Afterwards the spirit took me up,\n"
    .string "and brought me in a vision by the\l"
    .string "Spirit of God into Chaldea, to them\l"
    .string "of the captivity. So the vision that\l"
    .string "I had seen went up from me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_11_25::
    .string "Then I spake unto them of the\n"
    .string "captivity all the things that the\l"
    .string "LORD had shewed me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD also came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_2::
    .string "Son of man, thou dwellest in the\n"
    .string "midst of a rebellious house, which\l"
    .string "have eyes to see, and see not; they\l"
    .string "have ears to hear, and hear not: for\l"
    .string "they are a rebellious house$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_3::
    .string "Therefore, thou son of man,\n"
    .string "prepare thee stuff for removing, and\l"
    .string "remove by day in their sight; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt remove from thy place to\l"
    .string "another place in their sight: it may\l"
    .string "be they will consider, though they\l"
    .string "be a rebellious house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_4::
    .string "Then shalt thou bring forth thy\n"
    .string "stuff by day in their sight, as stuff\l"
    .string "for removing: and thou shalt go\l"
    .string "forth at even in their sight, as they\l"
    .string "that go forth into captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_5::
    .string "Dig thou through the wall in their\n"
    .string "sight, and carry out thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_6::
    .string "In their sight shalt thou bear it\n"
    .string "upon thy shoulders, and carry it\l"
    .string "forth in the twilight: thou shalt\l"
    .string "cover thy face, that thou see not the\l"
    .string "ground: for I have set thee for a sign\l"
    .string "unto the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_7::
    .string "And I did so as I was commanded: I\n"
    .string "brought forth my stuff by day, as\l"
    .string "stuff for captivity, and in the even\l"
    .string "I digged through the wall with mine\l"
    .string "hand; I brought it forth in the\l"
    .string "twilight, and I bare it upon my\l"
    .string "shoulder in their sight.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_8::
    .string "And in the morning came the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_9::
    .string "Son of man, hath not the house of\n"
    .string "Israel, the rebellious house, said\l"
    .string "unto thee, What doest thou?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_10::
    .string "Say thou unto them, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD; This burden concerneth the\l"
    .string "prince in Jerusalem, and all the\l"
    .string "house of Israel that are among them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_11::
    .string "Say, I am your sign: like as I have\n"
    .string "done, so shall it be done unto them:\l"
    .string "they shall remove and go into\l"
    .string "captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_12::
    .string "And the prince that is among them\n"
    .string "shall bear upon his shoulder in\l"
    .string "the twilight, and shall go forth:\l"
    .string "they shall dig through the wall to\l"
    .string "carry out thereby: he shall cover\l"
    .string "his face, that he see not the ground\l"
    .string "with his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_13::
    .string "My net also will I spread upon\n"
    .string "him, and he shall be taken in my\l"
    .string "snare: and I will bring him to\l"
    .string "Babylon to the land of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans; yet shall he not see it,\l"
    .string "though he shall die there.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_14::
    .string "And I will scatter toward every\n"
    .string "wind all that are about him to\l"
    .string "help him, and all his bands; and I\l"
    .string "will draw out the sword after them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_15::
    .string "And they shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when I shall scatter them\l"
    .string "among the nations, and disperse them\l"
    .string "in the countries.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_16::
    .string "But I will leave a few men of them\n"
    .string "from the sword, from the famine, and\l"
    .string "from the pestilence; that they may\l"
    .string "declare all their abominations\l"
    .string "among the heathen whither they come;\l"
    .string "and they shall know that I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_17::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "to me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_18::
    .string "Son of man, eat thy bread with\n"
    .string "quaking, and drink thy water with\l"
    .string "trembling and with carefulness;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_19::
    .string "And say unto the people of the\n"
    .string "land, Thus saith the Lord GOD of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem, and of the\l"
    .string "land of Israel; They shall eat\l"
    .string "their bread with carefulness, and\l"
    .string "drink their water with astonishment,\l"
    .string "that her land may be desolate from\l"
    .string "all that is therein, because of the\l"
    .string "violence of all them that dwell\l"
    .string "therein$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_20::
    .string "And the cities that are inhabited\n"
    .string "shall be laid waste, and the land\l"
    .string "shall be desolate; and ye shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_21::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_22::
    .string "Son of man, what is that proverb\n"
    .string "that ye have in the land of Israel,\l"
    .string "saying, The days are prolonged, and\l"
    .string "every vision faileth?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_23::
    .string "Tell them therefore, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD; I will make this\l"
    .string "proverb to cease, and they shall no\l"
    .string "more use it as a proverb in Israel;\l"
    .string "but say unto them, The days are at\l"
    .string "hand, and the effect of every vision$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_24::
    .string "For there shall be no more any vain\n"
    .string "vision nor flattering divination\l"
    .string "within the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_25::
    .string "For I am the LORD: I will speak,\n"
    .string "and the word that I shall speak\l"
    .string "shall come to pass; it shall be no\l"
    .string "more prolonged: for in your days, O\l"
    .string "rebellious house, will I say the\l"
    .string "word, and will perform it, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_26::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came to\n"
    .string "me, saying.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_27::
    .string "Son of man, behold, they of the\n"
    .string "house of Israel say, The vision that\l"
    .string "he seeth is for many days to come, and\l"
    .string "he prophesieth of the times that\l"
    .string "are far off.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_12_28::
    .string "Therefore say unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD; There shall none of my\l"
    .string "words be prolonged any more, but the\l"
    .string "word which I have spoken shall be\l"
    .string "done, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_2::
    .string "Son of man, prophesy against the\n"
    .string "prophets of Israel that prophesy,\l"
    .string "and say thou unto them that\l"
    .string "prophesy out of their own hearts,\l"
    .string "Hear ye the word of the LORD;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_3::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe unto\n"
    .string "the foolish prophets, that follow\l"
    .string "their own spirit, and have seen\l"
    .string "nothing!"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_4::
    .string "O Israel, thy prophets are like\n"
    .string "the foxes in the deserts$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_5::
    .string "Ye have not gone up into the gaps,\n"
    .string "neither made up the hedge for the\l"
    .string "house of Israel to stand in the\l"
    .string "battle in the day of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_6::
    .string "They have seen vanity and lying\n"
    .string "divination, saying, The LORD saith:\l"
    .string "and the LORD hath not sent them: and\l"
    .string "they have made others to hope that\l"
    .string "they would confirm the word.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_7::
    .string "Have ye not seen a vain vision, and\n"
    .string "have ye not spoken a lying\l"
    .string "divination, whereas ye say, The LORD\l"
    .string "saith it; albeit I have not spoken?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_8::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because ye have spoken vanity, and\l"
    .string "seen lies, therefore, behold, I am\l"
    .string "against you, saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_9::
    .string "And mine hand shall be upon the\n"
    .string "prophets that see vanity, and that\l"
    .string "divine lies: they shall not be in\l"
    .string "the assembly of my people, neither\l"
    .string "shall they be written in the\l"
    .string "writing of the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "neither shall they enter into the\l"
    .string "land of Israel; and ye shall know\l"
    .string "that I am the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_10::
    .string "Because, even because they have\n"
    .string "seduced my people, saying, Peace;\l"
    .string "and there was no peace; and one\l"
    .string "built up a wall, and, lo, others\l"
    .string "daubed it with untempered morter:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_11::
    .string "Say unto them which daub it with\n"
    .string "untempered morter, that it shall\l"
    .string "fall: there shall be an\l"
    .string "overflowing shower; and ye, O great\l"
    .string "hailstones, shall fall; and a\l"
    .string "stormy wind shall rend it$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_12::
    .string "Lo, when the wall is fallen,\n"
    .string "shall it not be said unto you, Where\l"
    .string "is the daubing wherewith ye have\l"
    .string "daubed it?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_13::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I\n"
    .string "will even rend it with a stormy wind\l"
    .string "in my fury; and there shall be an\l"
    .string "overflowing shower in mine anger,\l"
    .string "and great hailstones in my fury to\l"
    .string "consume it$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_14::
    .string "So will I break down the wall\n"
    .string "that ye have daubed with untempered\l"
    .string "morter, and bring it down to the\l"
    .string "ground, so that the foundation\l"
    .string "thereof shall be discovered, and it\l"
    .string "shall fall, and ye shall be\l"
    .string "consumed in the midst thereof: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_15::
    .string "Thus will I accomplish my wrath\n"
    .string "upon the wall, and upon them that\l"
    .string "have daubed it with untempered\l"
    .string "morter, and will say unto you, The\l"
    .string "wall is no more, neither they that\l"
    .string "daubed it;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_16::
    .string "To wit, the prophets of Israel\n"
    .string "which prophesy concerning\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and which see visions of\l"
    .string "peace for her, and there is no peace,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_17::
    .string "Likewise, thou son of man, set thy\n"
    .string "face against the daughters of thy\l"
    .string "people, which prophesy out of\l"
    .string "their own heart; and prophesy thou\l"
    .string "against them,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_18::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Woe to the women that sew pillows\l"
    .string "to all armholes, and make kerchiefs\l"
    .string "upon the head of every stature to\l"
    .string "hunt souls! Will ye hunt the souls\l"
    .string "of my people, and will ye save the\l"
    .string "souls alive that come unto you?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_19::
    .string "And will ye pollute me among my\n"
    .string "people for handfuls of barley and\l"
    .string "for pieces of bread, to slay the\l"
    .string "souls that should not die, and to\l"
    .string "save the souls alive that should\l"
    .string "not live, by your lying to my\l"
    .string "people that hear your lies?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_20::
    .string "Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I am against your pillows,\l"
    .string "wherewith ye there hunt the souls to\l"
    .string "make them fly, and I will tear them\l"
    .string "from your arms, and will let the\l"
    .string "souls go, even the souls that ye\l"
    .string "hunt to make them fly$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_21::
    .string "Your kerchiefs also will I tear,\n"
    .string "and deliver my people out of your\l"
    .string "hand, and they shall be no more in\l"
    .string "your hand to be hunted; and ye shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_22::
    .string "Because with lies ye have made the\n"
    .string "heart of the righteous sad, whom I\l"
    .string "have not made sad; and strengthened\l"
    .string "the hands of the wicked, that he\l"
    .string "should not return from his wicked\l"
    .string "way, by promising him life:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_13_23::
    .string "Therefore ye shall see no more\n"
    .string "vanity, nor divine divinations: for I\l"
    .string "will deliver my people out of\l"
    .string "your hand: and ye shall know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_1::
    .string "Then came certain of the elders of\n"
    .string "Israel unto me, and sat before me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_2::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_3::
    .string "Son of man, these men have set up\n"
    .string "their idols in their heart, and put\l"
    .string "the stumblingblock of their\l"
    .string "iniquity before their face: should I\l"
    .string "be enquired of at all by them?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_4::
    .string "Therefore speak unto them, and say\n"
    .string "unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "Every man of the house of Israel\l"
    .string "that setteth up his idols in his\l"
    .string "heart, and putteth the\l"
    .string "stumblingblock of his iniquity\l"
    .string "before his face, and cometh to the\l"
    .string "prophet; I the LORD will answer him\l"
    .string "that cometh according to the\l"
    .string "multitude of his idols;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_5::
    .string "That I may take the house of Israel\n"
    .string "in their own heart, because they are\l"
    .string "all estranged from me through their\l"
    .string "idols$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_6::
    .string "Therefore say unto the house of\n"
    .string "Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "Repent, and turn yourselves from\l"
    .string "your idols; and turn away your faces\l"
    .string "from all your abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_7::
    .string "For every one of the house of\n"
    .string "Israel, or of the stranger that\l"
    .string "sojourneth in Israel, which\l"
    .string "separateth himself from me, and\l"
    .string "setteth up his idols in his heart,\l"
    .string "and putteth the stumblingblock of\l"
    .string "his iniquity before his face, and\l"
    .string "cometh to a prophet to enquire of\l"
    .string "him concerning me; I the LORD will\l"
    .string "answer him by myself:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_8::
    .string "And I will set my face against that\n"
    .string "man, and will make him a sign and a\l"
    .string "proverb, and I will cut him off from\l"
    .string "the midst of my people; and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_9::
    .string "And if the prophet be deceived\n"
    .string "when he hath spoken a thing, I the\l"
    .string "LORD have deceived that prophet,\l"
    .string "and I will stretch out my hand upon\l"
    .string "him, and will destroy him from the\l"
    .string "midst of my people Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_10::
    .string "And they shall bear the\n"
    .string "punishment of their iniquity: the\l"
    .string "punishment of the prophet shall be\l"
    .string "even as the punishment of him that\l"
    .string "seeketh unto him;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_11::
    .string "That the house of Israel may go no\n"
    .string "more astray from me, neither be\l"
    .string "polluted any more with all their\l"
    .string "transgressions; but that they may be\l"
    .string "my people, and I may be their God,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_12::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again to\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_13::
    .string "Son of man, when the land sinneth\n"
    .string "against me by trespassing\l"
    .string "grievously, then will I stretch out\l"
    .string "mine hand upon it, and will break\l"
    .string "the staff of the bread thereof, and\l"
    .string "will send famine upon it, and will\l"
    .string "cut off man and beast from it:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_14::
    .string "Though these three men, Noah,\n"
    .string "Daniel, and Job, were in it, they\l"
    .string "should deliver but their own souls\l"
    .string "by their righteousness, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_15::
    .string "If I cause noisome beasts to pass\n"
    .string "through the land, and they spoil\l"
    .string "it, so that it be desolate, that no\l"
    .string "man may pass through because of the\l"
    .string "beasts:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_16::
    .string "Though these three men were in it,\n"
    .string "as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they\l"
    .string "shall deliver neither sons nor\l"
    .string "daughters; they only shall be\l"
    .string "delivered, but the land shall be\l"
    .string "desolate$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_17::
    .string "Or if I bring a sword upon that\n"
    .string "land, and say, Sword, go through the\l"
    .string "land; so that I cut off man and beast\l"
    .string "from it:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_18::
    .string "Though these three men were in it,\n"
    .string "as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they\l"
    .string "shall deliver neither sons nor\l"
    .string "daughters, but they only shall be\l"
    .string "delivered themselves$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_19::
    .string "Or if I send a pestilence into that\n"
    .string "land, and pour out my fury upon it\l"
    .string "in blood, to cut off from it man and\l"
    .string "beast:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_20::
    .string "Though Noah, Daniel, and Job were\n"
    .string "in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD,\l"
    .string "they shall deliver neither son nor\l"
    .string "daughter; they shall but deliver\l"
    .string "their own souls by their\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_21::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; How\n"
    .string "much more when I send my four sore\l"
    .string "judgments upon Jerusalem, the\l"
    .string "sword, and the famine, and the\l"
    .string "noisome beast, and the pestilence,\l"
    .string "to cut off from it man and beast?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_22::
    .string "Yet, behold, therein shall be\n"
    .string "left a remnant that shall be\l"
    .string "brought forth, both sons and\l"
    .string "daughters: behold, they shall come\l"
    .string "forth unto you, and ye shall see\l"
    .string "their way and their doings: and ye\l"
    .string "shall be comforted concerning the\l"
    .string "evil that I have brought upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, even concerning all\l"
    .string "that I have brought upon it$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_14_23::
    .string "And they shall comfort you, when ye\n"
    .string "see their ways and their doings: and\l"
    .string "ye shall know that I have not done\l"
    .string "without cause all that I have done\l"
    .string "in it, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_2::
    .string "Son of man, what is the vine tree\n"
    .string "more than any tree, or than a branch\l"
    .string "which is among the trees of the\l"
    .string "forest?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_3::
    .string "Shall wood be taken thereof to do\n"
    .string "any work? or will men take a pin of\l"
    .string "it to hang any vessel thereon?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_4::
    .string "Behold, it is cast into the fire for\n"
    .string "fuel; the fire devoureth both the\l"
    .string "ends of it, and the midst of it is\l"
    .string "burned. Is it meet for any work?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_5::
    .string "Behold, when it was whole, it was\n"
    .string "meet for no work: how much less\l"
    .string "shall it be meet yet for any work,\l"
    .string "when the fire hath devoured it, and\l"
    .string "it is burned?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_6::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "As the vine tree among the trees of\l"
    .string "the forest, which I have given to the\l"
    .string "fire for fuel, so will I give the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_7::
    .string "And I will set my face against\n"
    .string "them; they shall go out from one\l"
    .string "fire, and another fire shall devour\l"
    .string "them; and ye shall know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD, when I set my face against\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_15_8::
    .string "And I will make the land\n"
    .string "desolate, because they have\l"
    .string "committed a trespass, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_1::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_2::
    .string "Son of man, cause Jerusalem to know\n"
    .string "her abominations,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_3::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD\n"
    .string "unto Jerusalem; Thy birth and thy\l"
    .string "nativity is of the land of Canaan;\l"
    .string "thy father was an Amorite, and thy\l"
    .string "mother an Hittite$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_4::
    .string "And as for thy nativity, in the day\n"
    .string "thou wast born thy navel was not cut,\l"
    .string "neither wast thou washed in water to\l"
    .string "supple thee; thou wast not salted\l"
    .string "at all, nor swaddled at all.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_5::
    .string "None eye pitied thee, to do any of\n"
    .string "these unto thee, to have compassion\l"
    .string "upon thee; but thou wast cast out in\l"
    .string "the open field, to the lothing of\l"
    .string "thy person, in the day that thou wast\l"
    .string "born.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_6::
    .string "And when I passed by thee, and saw\n"
    .string "thee polluted in thine own blood,\l"
    .string "I said unto thee when thou wast in\l"
    .string "thy blood, Live; yea, I said unto\l"
    .string "thee when thou wast in thy blood,\l"
    .string "Live.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_7::
    .string "I have caused thee to multiply as\n"
    .string "the bud of the field, and thou hast\l"
    .string "increased and waxen great, and thou\l"
    .string "art come to excellent ornaments:\l"
    .string "thy breasts are fashioned, and thine\l"
    .string "hair is grown, whereas thou wast\l"
    .string "naked and bare.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_8::
    .string "Now when I passed by thee, and\n"
    .string "looked upon thee, behold, thy time\l"
    .string "was the time of love; and I spread\l"
    .string "my skirt over thee, and covered thy\l"
    .string "nakedness: yea, I sware unto thee,\l"
    .string "and entered into a covenant with\l"
    .string "thee, saith the Lord GOD, and thou\l"
    .string "becamest mine.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_9::
    .string "Then washed I thee with water; yea,\n"
    .string "I throughly washed away thy blood\l"
    .string "from thee, and I anointed thee with\l"
    .string "oil.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_10::
    .string "I clothed thee also with broidered\n"
    .string "work, and shod thee with badgers’\l"
    .string "skin, and I girded thee about with\l"
    .string "fine linen, and I covered thee with\l"
    .string "silk.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_11::
    .string "I decked thee also with ornaments,\n"
    .string "and I put bracelets upon thy hands,\l"
    .string "and a chain on thy neck.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_12::
    .string "And I put a jewel on thy forehead,\n"
    .string "and earrings in thine ears, and a\l"
    .string "beautiful crown upon thine head.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_13::
    .string "Thus wast thou decked with gold and\n"
    .string "silver; and thy raiment was of fine\l"
    .string "linen, and silk, and broidered work;\l"
    .string "thou didst eat fine flour, and\l"
    .string "honey, and oil: and thou wast\l"
    .string "exceeding beautiful, and thou didst\l"
    .string "prosper into a kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_14::
    .string "And thy renown went forth among the\n"
    .string "heathen for thy beauty: for it was\l"
    .string "perfect through my comeliness, which\l"
    .string "I had put upon thee, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_15::
    .string "But thou didst trust in thine own\n"
    .string "beauty, and playedst the harlot\l"
    .string "because of thy renown, and pouredst\l"
    .string "out thy fornications on every one\l"
    .string "that passed by; his it was.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_16::
    .string "And of thy garments thou didst take,\n"
    .string "and deckedst thy high places with\l"
    .string "divers colours, and playedst the\l"
    .string "harlot thereupon: the like things\l"
    .string "shall not come, neither shall it\l"
    .string "be so.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_17::
    .string "Thou hast also taken thy fair\n"
    .string "jewels of my gold and of my silver,\l"
    .string "which I had given thee, and madest to\l"
    .string "thyself images of men, and didst\l"
    .string "commit whoredom with them,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_18::
    .string "And tookest thy broidered garments,\n"
    .string "and coveredst them: and thou hast set\l"
    .string "mine oil and mine incense before them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_19::
    .string "My meat also which I gave thee, fine\n"
    .string "flour, and oil, and honey, wherewith\l"
    .string "I fed thee, thou hast even set it\l"
    .string "before them for a sweet savour: and\l"
    .string "thus it was, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_20::
    .string "Moreover thou hast taken thy sons\n"
    .string "and thy daughters, whom thou hast\l"
    .string "borne unto me, and these hast thou\l"
    .string "sacrificed unto them to be devoured.\l"
    .string "Is this of thy whoredoms a small\l"
    .string "matter,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_21::
    .string "That thou hast slain my children,\n"
    .string "and delivered them to cause them to\l"
    .string "pass through the fire for them?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_22::
    .string "And in all thine abominations and\n"
    .string "thy whoredoms thou hast not\l"
    .string "remembered the days of thy youth,\l"
    .string "when thou wast naked and bare, and\l"
    .string "wast polluted in thy blood$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_23::
    .string "And it came to pass after all thy\n"
    .string "wickedness, (woe, woe unto thee!\l"
    .string "saith the LORD GOD;)"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_24::
    .string "That thou hast also built unto\n"
    .string "thee an eminent place, and hast made\l"
    .string "thee an high place in every street$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_25::
    .string "Thou hast built thy high place at\n"
    .string "every head of the way, and hast made\l"
    .string "thy beauty to be abhorred, and hast\l"
    .string "opened thy feet to every one that\l"
    .string "passed by, and multiplied thy\l"
    .string "whoredoms.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_26::
    .string "Thou hast also committed\n"
    .string "fornication with the Egyptians thy\l"
    .string "neighbours, great of flesh; and hast\l"
    .string "increased thy whoredoms, to provoke\l"
    .string "me to anger.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_27::
    .string "Behold, therefore I have stretched\n"
    .string "out my hand over thee, and have\l"
    .string "diminished thine ordinary food, and\l"
    .string "delivered thee unto the will of\l"
    .string "them that hate thee, the daughters of\l"
    .string "the Philistines, which are ashamed\l"
    .string "of thy lewd way.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_28::
    .string "Thou hast played the whore also\n"
    .string "with the Assyrians, because thou wast\l"
    .string "unsatiable; yea, thou hast played\l"
    .string "the harlot with them, and yet\l"
    .string "couldest not be satisfied.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_29::
    .string "Thou hast moreover multiplied thy\n"
    .string "fornication in the land of Canaan\l"
    .string "unto Chaldea; and yet thou wast not\l"
    .string "satisfied therewith.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_30::
    .string "How weak is thine heart, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD GOD, seeing thou doest all\l"
    .string "these things, the work of an\l"
    .string "imperious whorish woman;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_31::
    .string "In that thou buildest thine eminent\n"
    .string "place in the head of every way, and\l"
    .string "makest thine high place in every\l"
    .string "street; and hast not been as an\l"
    .string "harlot, in that thou scornest hire;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_32::
    .string "But as a wife that committeth\n"
    .string "adultery, which taketh strangers\l"
    .string "instead of her husband!"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_33::
    .string "They give gifts to all whores: but\n"
    .string "thou givest thy gifts to all thy\l"
    .string "lovers, and hirest them, that they\l"
    .string "may come unto thee on every side for\l"
    .string "thy whoredom$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_34::
    .string "And the contrary is in thee from\n"
    .string "other women in thy whoredoms, whereas\l"
    .string "none followeth thee to commit\l"
    .string "whoredoms: and in that thou givest a\l"
    .string "reward, and no reward is given unto\l"
    .string "thee, therefore thou art contrary.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_35::
    .string "Wherefore, O harlot, hear the word\n"
    .string "of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_36::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thy\n"
    .string "filthiness was poured out, and thy\l"
    .string "nakedness discovered through thy\l"
    .string "whoredoms with thy lovers, and with\l"
    .string "all the idols of thy abominations,\l"
    .string "and by the blood of thy children,\l"
    .string "which thou didst give unto them;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_37::
    .string "Behold, therefore I will gather\n"
    .string "all thy lovers, with whom thou hast\l"
    .string "taken pleasure, and all them that\l"
    .string "thou hast loved, with all them that\l"
    .string "thou hast hated; I will even gather\l"
    .string "them round about against thee, and\l"
    .string "will discover thy nakedness unto\l"
    .string "them, that they may see all thy\l"
    .string "nakedness$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_38::
    .string "And I will judge thee, as women\n"
    .string "that break wedlock and shed blood\l"
    .string "are judged; and I will give thee\l"
    .string "blood in fury and jealousy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_39::
    .string "And I will also give thee into\n"
    .string "their hand, and they shall throw\l"
    .string "down thine eminent place, and\l"
    .string "shall break down thy high places:\l"
    .string "they shall strip thee also of thy\l"
    .string "clothes, and shall take thy fair\l"
    .string "jewels, and leave thee naked and\l"
    .string "bare.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_40::
    .string "They shall also bring up a\n"
    .string "company against thee, and they\l"
    .string "shall stone thee with stones, and\l"
    .string "thrust thee through with their\l"
    .string "swords.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_41::
    .string "And they shall burn thine houses\n"
    .string "with fire, and execute judgments\l"
    .string "upon thee in the sight of many women:\l"
    .string "and I will cause thee to cease from\l"
    .string "playing the harlot, and thou also\l"
    .string "shalt give no hire any more.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_42::
    .string "So will I make my fury toward thee\n"
    .string "to rest, and my jealousy shall\l"
    .string "depart from thee, and I will be\l"
    .string "quiet, and will be no more angry.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_43::
    .string "Because thou hast not remembered\n"
    .string "the days of thy youth, but hast\l"
    .string "fretted me in all these things;\l"
    .string "behold, therefore I also will\l"
    .string "recompense thy way upon thine head,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD: and thou shalt\l"
    .string "not commit this lewdness above all\l"
    .string "thine abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_44::
    .string "Behold, every one that useth\n"
    .string "proverbs shall use this proverb\l"
    .string "against thee, saying, As is the\l"
    .string "mother, so is her daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_45::
    .string "Thou art thy mother’s daughter, that\n"
    .string "lotheth her husband and her\l"
    .string "children; and thou art the sister of\l"
    .string "thy sisters, which lothed their\l"
    .string "husbands and their children: your\l"
    .string "mother was an Hittite, and your\l"
    .string "father an Amorite.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_46::
    .string "And thine elder sister is Samaria,\n"
    .string "she and her daughters that dwell at\l"
    .string "thy left hand: and thy younger\l"
    .string "sister, that dwelleth at thy right\l"
    .string "hand, is Sodom and her daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_47::
    .string "Yet hast thou not walked after\n"
    .string "their ways, nor done after their\l"
    .string "abominations: but, as if that were a\l"
    .string "very little thing, thou wast\l"
    .string "corrupted more than they in all thy\l"
    .string "ways.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_48::
    .string "As I live, saith the Lord GOD, Sodom\n"
    .string "thy sister hath not done, she nor her\l"
    .string "daughters, as thou hast done, thou\l"
    .string "and thy daughters.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_49::
    .string "Behold, this was the iniquity of\n"
    .string "thy sister Sodom, pride, fulness of\l"
    .string "bread, and abundance of idleness was\l"
    .string "in her and in her daughters, neither\l"
    .string "did she strengthen the hand of the\l"
    .string "poor and needy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_50::
    .string "And they were haughty, and committed\n"
    .string "abomination before me: therefore I\l"
    .string "took them away as I saw good.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_51::
    .string "Neither hath Samaria committed\n"
    .string "half of thy sins; but thou hast\l"
    .string "multiplied thine abominations more\l"
    .string "than they, and hast justified thy\l"
    .string "sisters in all thine abominations\l"
    .string "which thou hast done.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_52::
    .string "Thou also, which hast judged thy\n"
    .string "sisters, bear thine own shame for thy\l"
    .string "sins that thou hast committed more\l"
    .string "abominable than they: they are more\l"
    .string "righteous than thou: yea, be thou\l"
    .string "confounded also, and bear thy shame,\l"
    .string "in that thou hast justified thy\l"
    .string "sisters.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_53::
    .string "When I shall bring again their\n"
    .string "captivity, the captivity of Sodom\l"
    .string "and her daughters, and the captivity\l"
    .string "of Samaria and her daughters, then\l"
    .string "will I bring again the captivity of\l"
    .string "thy captives in the midst of them:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_54::
    .string "That thou mayest bear thine own\n"
    .string "shame, and mayest be confounded in\l"
    .string "all that thou hast done, in that\l"
    .string "thou art a comfort unto them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_55::
    .string "When thy sisters, Sodom and her\n"
    .string "daughters, shall return to their\l"
    .string "former estate, and Samaria and her\l"
    .string "daughters shall return to their\l"
    .string "former estate, then thou and thy\l"
    .string "daughters shall return to your\l"
    .string "former estate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_56::
    .string "For thy sister Sodom was not\n"
    .string "mentioned by thy mouth in the day of\l"
    .string "thy pride,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_57::
    .string "Before thy wickedness was\n"
    .string "discovered, as at the time of thy\l"
    .string "reproach of the daughters of Syria,\l"
    .string "and all that are round about her,\l"
    .string "the daughters of the Philistines,\l"
    .string "which despise thee round about$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_58::
    .string "Thou hast borne thy lewdness and\n"
    .string "thine abominations, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_59::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "even deal with thee as thou hast\l"
    .string "done, which hast despised the oath\l"
    .string "in breaking the covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_60::
    .string "Nevertheless I will remember my\n"
    .string "covenant with thee in the days of thy\l"
    .string "youth, and I will establish unto\l"
    .string "thee an everlasting covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_61::
    .string "Then thou shalt remember thy ways,\n"
    .string "and be ashamed, when thou shalt\l"
    .string "receive thy sisters, thine elder and\l"
    .string "thy younger: and I will give them\l"
    .string "unto thee for daughters, but not by\l"
    .string "thy covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_62::
    .string "And I will establish my covenant\n"
    .string "with thee; and thou shalt know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_16_63::
    .string "That thou mayest remember, and be\n"
    .string "confounded, and never open thy mouth\l"
    .string "any more because of thy shame, when I\l"
    .string "am pacified toward thee for all\l"
    .string "that thou hast done, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_2::
    .string "Son of man, put forth a riddle, and\n"
    .string "speak a parable unto the house of\l"
    .string "Israel;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_3::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; A\n"
    .string "great eagle with great wings,\l"
    .string "longwinged, full of feathers, which\l"
    .string "had divers colours, came unto\l"
    .string "Lebanon, and took the highest branch\l"
    .string "of the cedar:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_4::
    .string "He cropped off the top of his\n"
    .string "young twigs, and carried it into a\l"
    .string "land of traffick; he set it in a city\l"
    .string "of merchants$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_5::
    .string "He took also of the seed of the\n"
    .string "land, and planted it in a fruitful\l"
    .string "field; he placed it by great\l"
    .string "waters, and set it as a willow tree.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_6::
    .string "And it grew, and became a spreading\n"
    .string "vine of low stature, whose branches\l"
    .string "turned toward him, and the roots\l"
    .string "thereof were under him: so it became\l"
    .string "a vine, and brought forth branches,\l"
    .string "and shot forth sprigs.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_7::
    .string "There was also another great eagle\n"
    .string "with great wings and many feathers:\l"
    .string "and, behold, this vine did bend her\l"
    .string "roots toward him, and shot forth her\l"
    .string "branches toward him, that he might\l"
    .string "water it by the furrows of her\l"
    .string "plantation.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_8::
    .string "It was planted in a good soil by\n"
    .string "great waters, that it might bring\l"
    .string "forth branches, and that it might\l"
    .string "bear fruit, that it might be a goodly\l"
    .string "vine.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_9::
    .string "Say thou, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Shall it prosper? shall he not\l"
    .string "pull up the roots thereof, and cut\l"
    .string "off the fruit thereof, that it\l"
    .string "wither? it shall wither in all the\l"
    .string "leaves of her spring, even without\l"
    .string "great power or many people to\l"
    .string "pluck it up by the roots thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_10::
    .string "Yea, behold, being planted,\n"
    .string "shall it prosper? shall it not\l"
    .string "utterly wither, when the east wind\l"
    .string "toucheth it? it shall wither in the\l"
    .string "furrows where it grew.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_11::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_12::
    .string "Say now to the rebellious house,\n"
    .string "Know ye not what these things mean?\l"
    .string "tell them, Behold, the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon is come to Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "hath taken the king thereof, and the\l"
    .string "princes thereof, and led them with\l"
    .string "him to Babylon;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_13::
    .string "And hath taken of the king’s seed,\n"
    .string "and made a covenant with him, and\l"
    .string "hath taken an oath of him: he hath\l"
    .string "also taken the mighty of the land:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_14::
    .string "That the kingdom might be base, that\n"
    .string "it might not lift itself up, but\l"
    .string "that by keeping of his covenant it\l"
    .string "might stand$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_15::
    .string "But he rebelled against him in\n"
    .string "sending his ambassadors into Egypt,\l"
    .string "that they might give him horses and\l"
    .string "much people. Shall he prosper?\l"
    .string "shall he escape that doeth such\l"
    .string "things? or shall he break the\l"
    .string "covenant, and be delivered?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_16::
    .string "As I live, saith the Lord GOD,\n"
    .string "surely in the place where the king\l"
    .string "dwelleth that made him king, whose\l"
    .string "oath he despised, and whose covenant\l"
    .string "he brake, even with him in the midst\l"
    .string "of Babylon he shall die$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_17::
    .string "Neither shall Pharaoh with his\n"
    .string "mighty army and great company make\l"
    .string "for him in the war, by casting up\l"
    .string "mounts, and building forts, to cut\l"
    .string "off many persons:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_18::
    .string "Seeing he despised the oath by\n"
    .string "breaking the covenant, when, lo, he\l"
    .string "had given his hand, and hath done\l"
    .string "all these things, he shall not\l"
    .string "escape$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_19::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "As I live, surely mine oath that he\l"
    .string "hath despised, and my covenant that\l"
    .string "he hath broken, even it will I\l"
    .string "recompense upon his own head.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_20::
    .string "And I will spread my net upon him,\n"
    .string "and he shall be taken in my snare,\l"
    .string "and I will bring him to Babylon,\l"
    .string "and will plead with him there for\l"
    .string "his trespass that he hath\l"
    .string "trespassed against me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_21::
    .string "And all his fugitives with all\n"
    .string "his bands shall fall by the sword,\l"
    .string "and they that remain shall be\l"
    .string "scattered toward all winds: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I the LORD have\l"
    .string "spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_22::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "also take of the highest branch of\l"
    .string "the high cedar, and will set it; I\l"
    .string "will crop off from the top of his\l"
    .string "young twigs a tender one, and will\l"
    .string "plant it upon an high mountain and\l"
    .string "eminent:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_23::
    .string "In the mountain of the height of\n"
    .string "Israel will I plant it: and it\l"
    .string "shall bring forth boughs, and bear\l"
    .string "fruit, and be a goodly cedar: and\l"
    .string "under it shall dwell all fowl of\l"
    .string "every wing; in the shadow of the\l"
    .string "branches thereof shall they dwell$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_17_24::
    .string "And all the trees of the field\n"
    .string "shall know that I the LORD have\l"
    .string "brought down the high tree, have\l"
    .string "exalted the low tree, have dried up\l"
    .string "the green tree, and have made the dry\l"
    .string "tree to flourish: I the LORD have\l"
    .string "spoken and have done it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came unto me\n"
    .string "again, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_2::
    .string "What mean ye, that ye use this\n"
    .string "proverb concerning the land of\l"
    .string "Israel, saying, The fathers have\l"
    .string "eaten sour grapes, and the\l"
    .string "children’s teeth are set on edge?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_3::
    .string "As I live, saith the Lord GOD, ye\n"
    .string "shall not have occasion any more to\l"
    .string "use this proverb in Israel$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_4::
    .string "Behold, all souls are mine; as\n"
    .string "the soul of the father, so also the\l"
    .string "soul of the son is mine: the soul\l"
    .string "that sinneth, it shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_5::
    .string "But if a man be just, and do that\n"
    .string "which is lawful and right,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_6::
    .string "And hath not eaten upon the\n"
    .string "mountains, neither hath lifted up\l"
    .string "his eyes to the idols of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, neither hath defiled his\l"
    .string "neighbour’s wife, neither hath come\l"
    .string "near to a menstruous woman,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_7::
    .string "And hath not oppressed any, but\n"
    .string "hath restored to the debtor his\l"
    .string "pledge, hath spoiled none by\l"
    .string "violence, hath given his bread to\l"
    .string "the hungry, and hath covered the\l"
    .string "naked with a garment;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_8::
    .string "He that hath not given forth upon\n"
    .string "usury, neither hath taken any\l"
    .string "increase, that hath withdrawn his\l"
    .string "hand from iniquity, hath executed\l"
    .string "true judgment between man and man,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_9::
    .string "Hath walked in my statutes, and\n"
    .string "hath kept my judgments, to deal\l"
    .string "truly; he is just, he shall surely\l"
    .string "live, saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_10::
    .string "If he beget a son that is a robber, a\n"
    .string "shedder of blood, and that doeth the\l"
    .string "like to any one of these things,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_11::
    .string "And that doeth not any of those\n"
    .string "duties, but even hath eaten upon the\l"
    .string "mountains, and defiled his\l"
    .string "neighbour’s wife,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_12::
    .string "Hath oppressed the poor and needy,\n"
    .string "hath spoiled by violence, hath not\l"
    .string "restored the pledge, and hath\l"
    .string "lifted up his eyes to the idols,\l"
    .string "hath committed abomination,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_13::
    .string "Hath given forth upon usury, and\n"
    .string "hath taken increase: shall he then\l"
    .string "live? he shall not live: he hath\l"
    .string "done all these abominations; he\l"
    .string "shall surely die; his blood shall\l"
    .string "be upon him$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_14::
    .string "Now, lo, if he beget a son, that\n"
    .string "seeth all his father’s sins which\l"
    .string "he hath done, and considereth, and\l"
    .string "doeth not such like,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_15::
    .string "That hath not eaten upon the\n"
    .string "mountains, neither hath lifted up\l"
    .string "his eyes to the idols of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, hath not defiled his\l"
    .string "neighbour’s wife,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_16::
    .string "Neither hath oppressed any, hath\n"
    .string "not withholden the pledge, neither\l"
    .string "hath spoiled by violence, but hath\l"
    .string "given his bread to the hungry, and\l"
    .string "hath covered the naked with a\l"
    .string "garment,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_17::
    .string "That hath taken off his hand from\n"
    .string "the poor, that hath not received\l"
    .string "usury nor increase, hath executed my\l"
    .string "judgments, hath walked in my\l"
    .string "statutes; he shall not die for the\l"
    .string "iniquity of his father, he shall\l"
    .string "surely live$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_18::
    .string "As for his father, because he\n"
    .string "cruelly oppressed, spoiled his\l"
    .string "brother by violence, and did that\l"
    .string "which is not good among his people,\l"
    .string "lo, even he shall die in his\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_19::
    .string "Yet say ye, Why? doth not the son\n"
    .string "bear the iniquity of the father? When\l"
    .string "the son hath done that which is\l"
    .string "lawful and right, and hath kept\l"
    .string "all my statutes, and hath done them,\l"
    .string "he shall surely live.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_20::
    .string "The soul that sinneth, it shall die\n"
    .string " The son shall not bear the\l"
    .string "iniquity of the father, neither\l"
    .string "shall the father bear the iniquity\l"
    .string "of the son: the righteousness of the\l"
    .string "righteous shall be upon him, and\l"
    .string "the wickedness of the wicked shall\l"
    .string "be upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_21::
    .string "But if the wicked will turn from\n"
    .string "all his sins that he hath committed,\l"
    .string "and keep all my statutes, and do\l"
    .string "that which is lawful and right, he\l"
    .string "shall surely live, he shall not\l"
    .string "die.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_22::
    .string "All his transgressions that he\n"
    .string "hath committed, they shall not be\l"
    .string "mentioned unto him: in his\l"
    .string "righteousness that he hath done he\l"
    .string "shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_23::
    .string "Have I any pleasure at all that\n"
    .string "the wicked should die? saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD: and not that he should\l"
    .string "return from his ways, and live?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_24::
    .string "But when the righteous turneth away\n"
    .string "from his righteousness, and\l"
    .string "committeth iniquity, and doeth\l"
    .string "according to all the abominations\l"
    .string "that the wicked man doeth, shall he\l"
    .string "live? All his righteousness that he\l"
    .string "hath done shall not be mentioned: in\l"
    .string "his trespass that he hath\l"
    .string "trespassed, and in his sin that he\l"
    .string "hath sinned, in them shall he die$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_25::
    .string "Yet ye say, The way of the LORD is\n"
    .string "not equal. Hear now, O house of\l"
    .string "Israel; Is not my way equal? are not\l"
    .string "your ways unequal?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_26::
    .string "When a righteous man turneth away\n"
    .string "from his righteousness, and\l"
    .string "committeth iniquity, and dieth in\l"
    .string "them; for his iniquity that he hath\l"
    .string "done shall he die$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_27::
    .string "Again, when the wicked man turneth\n"
    .string "away from his wickedness that he hath\l"
    .string "committed, and doeth that which is\l"
    .string "lawful and right, he shall save his\l"
    .string "soul alive.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_28::
    .string "Because he considereth, and turneth\n"
    .string "away from all his transgressions\l"
    .string "that he hath committed, he shall\l"
    .string "surely live, he shall not die.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_29::
    .string "Yet saith the house of Israel, The\n"
    .string "way of the LORD is not equal. O house\l"
    .string "of Israel, are not my ways equal?\l"
    .string "are not your ways unequal?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_30::
    .string "Therefore I will judge you, O house\n"
    .string "of Israel, every one according to\l"
    .string "his ways, saith the Lord GOD. Repent,\l"
    .string "and turn yourselves from all your\l"
    .string "transgressions; so iniquity shall\l"
    .string "not be your ruin$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_31::
    .string "Cast away from you all your\n"
    .string "transgressions, whereby ye have\l"
    .string "transgressed; and make you a new\l"
    .string "heart and a new spirit: for why\l"
    .string "will ye die, O house of Israel?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_18_32::
    .string "For I have no pleasure in the death\n"
    .string "of him that dieth, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD: wherefore turn yourselves, and\l"
    .string "live ye$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_1::
    .string "Moreover take thou up a\n"
    .string "lamentation for the princes of\l"
    .string "Israel,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_2::
    .string "And say, What is thy mother? A\n"
    .string "lioness: she lay down among lions,\l"
    .string "she nourished her whelps among\l"
    .string "young lions$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_3::
    .string "And she brought up one of her\n"
    .string "whelps: it became a young lion, and\l"
    .string "it learned to catch the prey; it\l"
    .string "devoured men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_4::
    .string "The nations also heard of him; he\n"
    .string "was taken in their pit, and they\l"
    .string "brought him with chains unto the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_5::
    .string "Now when she saw that she had\n"
    .string "waited, and her hope was lost, then\l"
    .string "she took another of her whelps, and\l"
    .string "made him a young lion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_6::
    .string "And he went up and down among the\n"
    .string "lions, he became a young lion, and\l"
    .string "learned to catch the prey, and\l"
    .string "devoured men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_7::
    .string "And he knew their desolate\n"
    .string "palaces, and he laid waste their\l"
    .string "cities; and the land was desolate,\l"
    .string "and the fulness thereof, by the\l"
    .string "noise of his roaring.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_8::
    .string "Then the nations set against him on\n"
    .string "every side from the provinces, and\l"
    .string "spread their net over him: he was\l"
    .string "taken in their pit.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_9::
    .string "And they put him in ward in chains,\n"
    .string "and brought him to the king of\l"
    .string "Babylon: they brought him into\l"
    .string "holds, that his voice should no more\l"
    .string "be heard upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_10::
    .string "Thy mother is like a vine in thy\n"
    .string "blood, planted by the waters: she\l"
    .string "was fruitful and full of branches\l"
    .string "by reason of many waters.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_11::
    .string "And she had strong rods for the\n"
    .string "sceptres of them that bare rule, and\l"
    .string "her stature was exalted among the\l"
    .string "thick branches, and she appeared in\l"
    .string "her height with the multitude of her\l"
    .string "branches.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_12::
    .string "But she was plucked up in fury,\n"
    .string "she was cast down to the ground, and\l"
    .string "the east wind dried up her fruit: her\l"
    .string "strong rods were broken and withered;\l"
    .string "the fire consumed them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_13::
    .string "And now she is planted in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, in a dry and thirsty\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_19_14::
    .string "And fire is gone out of a rod of her\n"
    .string "branches, which hath devoured her\l"
    .string "fruit, so that she hath no strong rod\l"
    .string "to be a sceptre to rule. This is a\l"
    .string "lamentation, and shall be for a\l"
    .string "lamentation.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the seventh\n"
    .string "year, in the fifth month, the tenth\l"
    .string "day of the month, that certain of the\l"
    .string "elders of Israel came to enquire of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and sat before me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_2::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_3::
    .string "Son of man, speak unto the elders\n"
    .string "of Israel, and say unto them, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Are ye come to\l"
    .string "enquire of me? As I live, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD, I will not be enquired of\l"
    .string "by you$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_4::
    .string "Wilt thou judge them, son of man,\n"
    .string "wilt thou judge them? cause them to\l"
    .string "know the abominations of their\l"
    .string "fathers:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_5::
    .string "And say unto them, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD; In the day when I chose\l"
    .string "Israel, and lifted up mine hand\l"
    .string "unto the seed of the house of Jacob,\l"
    .string "and made myself known unto them in\l"
    .string "the land of Egypt, when I lifted up\l"
    .string "mine hand unto them, saying, I am the\l"
    .string "LORD your God;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_6::
    .string "In the day that I lifted up mine\n"
    .string "hand unto them, to bring them forth\l"
    .string "of the land of Egypt into a land\l"
    .string "that I had espied for them, flowing\l"
    .string "with milk and honey, which is the\l"
    .string "glory of all lands:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_7::
    .string "Then said I unto them, Cast ye away\n"
    .string "every man the abominations of his\l"
    .string "eyes, and defile not yourselves\l"
    .string "with the idols of Egypt: I am the\l"
    .string "LORD your God$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_8::
    .string "But they rebelled against me, and\n"
    .string "would not hearken unto me: they did\l"
    .string "not every man cast away the\l"
    .string "abominations of their eyes, neither\l"
    .string "did they forsake the idols of Egypt:\l"
    .string "then I said, I will pour out my fury\l"
    .string "upon them, to accomplish my anger\l"
    .string "against them in the midst of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_9::
    .string "But I wrought for my name’s sake,\n"
    .string "that it should not be polluted\l"
    .string "before the heathen, among whom they\l"
    .string "were, in whose sight I made myself\l"
    .string "known unto them, in bringing them\l"
    .string "forth out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_10::
    .string "Wherefore I caused them to go forth\n"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt, and\l"
    .string "brought them into the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_11::
    .string "And I gave them my statutes, and\n"
    .string "shewed them my judgments, which if a\l"
    .string "man do, he shall even live in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_12::
    .string "Moreover also I gave them my\n"
    .string "sabbaths, to be a sign between me and\l"
    .string "them, that they might know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD that sanctify them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_13::
    .string "But the house of Israel rebelled\n"
    .string "against me in the wilderness: they\l"
    .string "walked not in my statutes, and they\l"
    .string "despised my judgments, which if a\l"
    .string "man do, he shall even live in them;\l"
    .string "and my sabbaths they greatly\l"
    .string "polluted: then I said, I would\l"
    .string "pour out my fury upon them in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, to consume them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_14::
    .string "But I wrought for my name’s sake,\n"
    .string "that it should not be polluted\l"
    .string "before the heathen, in whose sight I\l"
    .string "brought them out.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_15::
    .string "Yet also I lifted up my hand unto\n"
    .string "them in the wilderness, that I would\l"
    .string "not bring them into the land which I\l"
    .string "had given them, flowing with milk\l"
    .string "and honey, which is the glory of\l"
    .string "all lands;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_16::
    .string "Because they despised my judgments,\n"
    .string "and walked not in my statutes, but\l"
    .string "polluted my sabbaths: for their\l"
    .string "heart went after their idols$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_17::
    .string "Nevertheless mine eye spared them\n"
    .string "from destroying them, neither did I\l"
    .string "make an end of them in the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_18::
    .string "But I said unto their children in\n"
    .string "the wilderness, Walk ye not in the\l"
    .string "statutes of your fathers, neither\l"
    .string "observe their judgments, nor defile\l"
    .string "yourselves with their idols:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_19::
    .string "I am the LORD your God; walk in my\n"
    .string "statutes, and keep my judgments, and\l"
    .string "do them;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_20::
    .string "And hallow my sabbaths; and they\n"
    .string "shall be a sign between me and you,\l"
    .string "that ye may know that I am the LORD\l"
    .string "your God$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_21::
    .string "Notwithstanding the children\n"
    .string "rebelled against me: they walked\l"
    .string "not in my statutes, neither kept my\l"
    .string "judgments to do them, which if a man\l"
    .string "do, he shall even live in them;\l"
    .string "they polluted my sabbaths: then I\l"
    .string "said, I would pour out my fury upon\l"
    .string "them, to accomplish my anger\l"
    .string "against them in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_22::
    .string "Nevertheless I withdrew mine hand,\n"
    .string "and wrought for my name’s sake, that\l"
    .string "it should not be polluted in the\l"
    .string "sight of the heathen, in whose sight\l"
    .string "I brought them forth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_23::
    .string "I lifted up mine hand unto them\n"
    .string "also in the wilderness, that I\l"
    .string "would scatter them among the\l"
    .string "heathen, and disperse them through\l"
    .string "the countries;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_24::
    .string "Because they had not executed my\n"
    .string "judgments, but had despised my\l"
    .string "statutes, and had polluted my\l"
    .string "sabbaths, and their eyes were after\l"
    .string "their fathers’ idols$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_25::
    .string "Wherefore I gave them also statutes\n"
    .string "that were not good, and judgments\l"
    .string "whereby they should not live;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_26::
    .string "And I polluted them in their own\n"
    .string "gifts, in that they caused to pass\l"
    .string "through the fire all that openeth\l"
    .string "the womb, that I might make them\l"
    .string "desolate, to the end that they might\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_27::
    .string "Therefore, son of man, speak unto\n"
    .string "the house of Israel, and say unto\l"
    .string "them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Yet in\l"
    .string "this your fathers have blasphemed\l"
    .string "me, in that they have committed a\l"
    .string "trespass against me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_28::
    .string "For when I had brought them into the\n"
    .string "land, for the which I lifted up mine\l"
    .string "hand to give it to them, then they saw\l"
    .string "every high hill, and all the thick\l"
    .string "trees, and they offered there their\l"
    .string "sacrifices, and there they presented\l"
    .string "the provocation of their offering:\l"
    .string "there also they made their sweet\l"
    .string "savour, and poured out there their\l"
    .string "drink offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_29::
    .string "Then I said unto them, What is the\n"
    .string "high place whereunto ye go? And the\l"
    .string "name whereof is called Bamah unto\l"
    .string "this day.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_30::
    .string "Wherefore say unto the house of\n"
    .string "Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Are\l"
    .string "ye polluted after the manner of\l"
    .string "your fathers? and commit ye whoredom\l"
    .string "after their abominations?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_31::
    .string "For when ye offer your gifts, when\n"
    .string "ye make your sons to pass through\l"
    .string "the fire, ye pollute yourselves\l"
    .string "with all your idols, even unto this\l"
    .string "day: and shall I be enquired of by\l"
    .string "you, O house of Israel? As I live,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD, I will not be\l"
    .string "enquired of by you$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_32::
    .string "And that which cometh into your mind\n"
    .string "shall not be at all, that ye say,\l"
    .string "We will be as the heathen, as the\l"
    .string "families of the countries, to serve\l"
    .string "wood and stone.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_33::
    .string "As I live, saith the Lord GOD,\n"
    .string "surely with a mighty hand, and with a\l"
    .string "stretched out arm, and with fury\l"
    .string "poured out, will I rule over you:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_34::
    .string "And I will bring you out from the\n"
    .string "people, and will gather you out of\l"
    .string "the countries wherein ye are\l"
    .string "scattered, with a mighty hand, and\l"
    .string "with a stretched out arm, and with\l"
    .string "fury poured out$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_35::
    .string "And I will bring you into the\n"
    .string "wilderness of the people, and\l"
    .string "there will I plead with you face\l"
    .string "to face.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_36::
    .string "Like as I pleaded with your\n"
    .string "fathers in the wilderness of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, so will I plead\l"
    .string "with you, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_37::
    .string "And I will cause you to pass under\n"
    .string "the rod, and I will bring you into\l"
    .string "the bond of the covenant:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_38::
    .string "And I will purge out from among\n"
    .string "you the rebels, and them that\l"
    .string "transgress against me: I will bring\l"
    .string "them forth out of the country where\l"
    .string "they sojourn, and they shall not\l"
    .string "enter into the land of Israel: and\l"
    .string "ye shall know that I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_39::
    .string "As for you, O house of Israel, thus\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Go ye, serve ye\l"
    .string "every one his idols, and hereafter\l"
    .string "also, if ye will not hearken unto\l"
    .string "me: but pollute ye my holy name no\l"
    .string "more with your gifts, and with your\l"
    .string "idols.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_40::
    .string "For in mine holy mountain, in the\n"
    .string "mountain of the height of Israel,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD, there shall\l"
    .string "all the house of Israel, all of\l"
    .string "them in the land, serve me: there\l"
    .string "will I accept them, and there will\l"
    .string "I require your offerings, and the\l"
    .string "firstfruits of your oblations, with\l"
    .string "all your holy things.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_41::
    .string "I will accept you with your sweet\n"
    .string "savour, when I bring you out from the\l"
    .string "people, and gather you out of the\l"
    .string "countries wherein ye have been\l"
    .string "scattered; and I will be sanctified\l"
    .string "in you before the heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_42::
    .string "And ye shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when I shall bring you into\l"
    .string "the land of Israel, into the country\l"
    .string "for the which I lifted up mine hand\l"
    .string "to give it to your fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_43::
    .string "And there shall ye remember your\n"
    .string "ways, and all your doings, wherein\l"
    .string "ye have been defiled; and ye shall\l"
    .string "lothe yourselves in your own sight\l"
    .string "for all your evils that ye have\l"
    .string "committed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_44::
    .string "And ye shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD when I have wrought with you for\l"
    .string "my name’s sake, not according to your\l"
    .string "wicked ways, nor according to your\l"
    .string "corrupt doings, O ye house of\l"
    .string "Israel, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_45::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_46::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face toward the\n"
    .string "south, and drop thy word toward the\l"
    .string "south, and prophesy against the\l"
    .string "forest of the south field;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_47::
    .string "And say to the forest of the south,\n"
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD; Thus saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD; Behold, I will\l"
    .string "kindle a fire in thee, and it shall\l"
    .string "devour every green tree in thee, and\l"
    .string "every dry tree: the flaming flame\l"
    .string "shall not be quenched, and all\l"
    .string "faces from the south to the north\l"
    .string "shall be burned therein$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_48::
    .string "And all flesh shall see that I\n"
    .string "the LORD have kindled it: it shall\l"
    .string "not be quenched.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_20_49::
    .string "Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! they say of\n"
    .string "me, Doth he not speak parables?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face toward\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, and drop thy word toward\l"
    .string "the holy places, and prophesy\l"
    .string "against the land of Israel,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_3::
    .string "And say to the land of Israel, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; Behold, I am against\l"
    .string "thee, and will draw forth my sword\l"
    .string "out of his sheath, and will cut off\l"
    .string "from thee the righteous and the\l"
    .string "wicked$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_4::
    .string "Seeing then that I will cut off\n"
    .string "from thee the righteous and the\l"
    .string "wicked, therefore shall my sword go\l"
    .string "forth out of his sheath against all\l"
    .string "flesh from the south to the north:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_5::
    .string "That all flesh may know that I the\n"
    .string "LORD have drawn forth my sword out of\l"
    .string "his sheath: it shall not return any\l"
    .string "more$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_6::
    .string "Sigh therefore, thou son of man,\n"
    .string "with the breaking of thy loins; and\l"
    .string "with bitterness sigh before their\l"
    .string "eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_7::
    .string "And it shall be, when they say unto\n"
    .string "thee, Wherefore sighest thou? that\l"
    .string "thou shalt answer, For the tidings;\l"
    .string "because it cometh: and every heart\l"
    .string "shall melt, and all hands shall\l"
    .string "be feeble, and every spirit shall\l"
    .string "faint, and all knees shall be weak\l"
    .string "as water: behold, it cometh, and\l"
    .string "shall be brought to pass, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_8::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_9::
    .string "Son of man, prophesy, and say, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; Say, A sword, a sword\l"
    .string "is sharpened, and also furbished:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_10::
    .string "It is sharpened to make a sore\n"
    .string "slaughter; it is furbished that it\l"
    .string "may glitter: should we then make\l"
    .string "mirth? it contemneth the rod of my\l"
    .string "son, as every tree$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_11::
    .string "And he hath given it to be\n"
    .string "furbished, that it may be handled:\l"
    .string "this sword is sharpened, and it is\l"
    .string "furbished, to give it into the hand\l"
    .string "of the slayer.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_12::
    .string "Cry and howl, son of man: for it\n"
    .string "shall be upon my people, it\l"
    .string "shall be upon all the princes of\l"
    .string "Israel: terrors by reason of the\l"
    .string "sword shall be upon my people:\l"
    .string "smite therefore upon thy thigh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_13::
    .string "Because it is a trial, and what if\n"
    .string "the sword contemn even the rod? it\l"
    .string "shall be no more, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_14::
    .string "Thou therefore, son of man,\n"
    .string "prophesy, and smite thine hands\l"
    .string "together, and let the sword be\l"
    .string "doubled the third time, the sword of\l"
    .string "the slain: it is the sword of the\l"
    .string "great men that are slain, which\l"
    .string "entereth into their privy chambers.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_15::
    .string "I have set the point of the sword\n"
    .string "against all their gates, that their\l"
    .string "heart may faint, and their ruins be\l"
    .string "multiplied: ah! it is made bright,\l"
    .string "it is wrapped up for the slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_16::
    .string "Go thee one way or other, either on\n"
    .string "the right hand, or on the left,\l"
    .string "whithersoever thy face is set.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_17::
    .string "I will also smite mine hands\n"
    .string "together, and I will cause my fury\l"
    .string "to rest: I the LORD have said it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_18::
    .string "The word of the LORD came unto me\n"
    .string "again, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_19::
    .string "Also, thou son of man, appoint\n"
    .string "thee two ways, that the sword of the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon may come: both twain\l"
    .string "shall come forth out of one land:\l"
    .string "and choose thou a place, choose it\l"
    .string "at the head of the way to the city$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_20::
    .string "Appoint a way, that the sword may\n"
    .string "come to Rabbath of the Ammonites, and\l"
    .string "to Judah in Jerusalem the defenced.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_21::
    .string "For the king of Babylon stood at\n"
    .string "the parting of the way, at the head\l"
    .string "of the two ways, to use divination:\l"
    .string "he made his arrows bright, he\l"
    .string "consulted with images, he looked in\l"
    .string "the liver.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_22::
    .string "At his right hand was the divination\n"
    .string "for Jerusalem, to appoint\l"
    .string "captains, to open the mouth in the\l"
    .string "slaughter, to lift up the voice\l"
    .string "with shouting, to appoint battering\l"
    .string "rams against the gates, to cast a\l"
    .string "mount, and to build a fort.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_23::
    .string "And it shall be unto them as a\n"
    .string "false divination in their sight, to\l"
    .string "them that have sworn oaths: but he\l"
    .string "will call to remembrance the\l"
    .string "iniquity, that they may be taken.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_24::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because ye have made your iniquity to\l"
    .string "be remembered, in that your\l"
    .string "transgressions are discovered, so\l"
    .string "that in all your doings your sins do\l"
    .string "appear; because, I say, that ye are\l"
    .string "come to remembrance, ye shall be\l"
    .string "taken with the hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_25::
    .string "And thou, profane wicked prince of\n"
    .string "Israel, whose day is come, when\l"
    .string "iniquity shall have an end,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_26::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Remove the\n"
    .string "diadem, and take off the crown: this\l"
    .string "shall not be the same: exalt him\l"
    .string "that is low, and abase him that is\l"
    .string "high$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_27::
    .string "I will overturn, overturn,\n"
    .string "overturn, it: and it shall be no\l"
    .string "more, until he come whose right it\l"
    .string "is; and I will give it him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_28::
    .string "And thou, son of man, prophesy and\n"
    .string "say, Thus saith the Lord GOD\l"
    .string "concerning the Ammonites, and\l"
    .string "concerning their reproach; even say\l"
    .string "thou, The sword, the sword is drawn:\l"
    .string "for the slaughter it is furbished,\l"
    .string "to consume because of the\l"
    .string "glittering:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_29::
    .string "Whiles they see vanity unto thee,\n"
    .string "whiles they divine a lie unto thee,\l"
    .string "to bring thee upon the necks of them\l"
    .string "that are slain, of the wicked, whose\l"
    .string "day is come, when their iniquity\l"
    .string "shall have an end$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_30::
    .string "Shall I cause it to return into his\n"
    .string "sheath? I will judge thee in the\l"
    .string "place where thou wast created, in\l"
    .string "the land of thy nativity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_31::
    .string "And I will pour out mine\n"
    .string "indignation upon thee, I will blow\l"
    .string "against thee in the fire of my wrath,\l"
    .string "and deliver thee into the hand of\l"
    .string "brutish men, and skilful to destroy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_21_32::
    .string "Thou shalt be for fuel to the fire;\n"
    .string "thy blood shall be in the midst of\l"
    .string "the land; thou shalt be no more\l"
    .string "remembered: for I the LORD have\l"
    .string "spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_1::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_2::
    .string "Now, thou son of man, wilt thou\n"
    .string "judge, wilt thou judge the bloody\l"
    .string "city? yea, thou shalt shew her all\l"
    .string "her abominations$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_3::
    .string "Then say thou, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD, The city sheddeth blood in the\l"
    .string "midst of it, that her time may come,\l"
    .string "and maketh idols against herself to\l"
    .string "defile herself.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_4::
    .string "Thou art become guilty in thy\n"
    .string "blood that thou hast shed; and hast\l"
    .string "defiled thyself in thine idols\l"
    .string "which thou hast made; and thou hast\l"
    .string "caused thy days to draw near, and art\l"
    .string "come even unto thy years: therefore\l"
    .string "have I made thee a reproach unto the\l"
    .string "heathen, and a mocking to all\l"
    .string "countries.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_5::
    .string "Those that be near, and those that\n"
    .string "be far from thee, shall mock thee,\l"
    .string "which art infamous and much vexed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_6::
    .string "Behold, the princes of Israel,\n"
    .string "every one were in thee to their\l"
    .string "power to shed blood.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_7::
    .string "In thee have they set light by\n"
    .string "father and mother: in the midst of\l"
    .string "thee have they dealt by oppression\l"
    .string "with the stranger: in thee have they\l"
    .string "vexed the fatherless and the widow.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_8::
    .string "Thou hast despised mine holy\n"
    .string "things, and hast profaned my\l"
    .string "sabbaths.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_9::
    .string "In thee are men that carry tales to\n"
    .string "shed blood: and in thee they eat\l"
    .string "upon the mountains: in the midst of\l"
    .string "thee they commit lewdness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_10::
    .string "In thee have they discovered their\n"
    .string "fathers’ nakedness: in thee have they\l"
    .string "humbled her that was set apart for\l"
    .string "pollution.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_11::
    .string "And one hath committed abomination\n"
    .string "with his neighbour’s wife; and\l"
    .string "another hath lewdly defiled his\l"
    .string "daughter in law; and another in thee\l"
    .string "hath humbled his sister, his\l"
    .string "father’s daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_12::
    .string "In thee have they taken gifts to\n"
    .string "shed blood; thou hast taken usury\l"
    .string "and increase, and thou hast greedily\l"
    .string "gained of thy neighbours by\l"
    .string "extortion, and hast forgotten me,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_13::
    .string "Behold, therefore I have smitten\n"
    .string "mine hand at thy dishonest gain which\l"
    .string "thou hast made, and at thy blood\l"
    .string "which hath been in the midst of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_14::
    .string "Can thine heart endure, or can thine\n"
    .string "hands be strong, in the days that I\l"
    .string "shall deal with thee? I the LORD\l"
    .string "have spoken it, and will do it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_15::
    .string "And I will scatter thee among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and disperse thee in the\l"
    .string "countries, and will consume thy\l"
    .string "filthiness out of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_16::
    .string "And thou shalt take thine\n"
    .string "inheritance in thyself in the sight\l"
    .string "of the heathen, and thou shalt know\l"
    .string "that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_17::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_18::
    .string "Son of man, the house of Israel is\n"
    .string "to me become dross: all they are\l"
    .string "brass, and tin, and iron, and lead,\l"
    .string "in the midst of the furnace; they are\l"
    .string "even the dross of silver$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_19::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because ye are all become dross,\l"
    .string "behold, therefore I will gather you\l"
    .string "into the midst of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_20::
    .string "As they gather silver, and brass,\n"
    .string "and iron, and lead, and tin, into the\l"
    .string "midst of the furnace, to blow the\l"
    .string "fire upon it, to melt it; so will I\l"
    .string "gather you in mine anger and in my\l"
    .string "fury, and I will leave you there,\l"
    .string "and melt you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_21::
    .string "Yea, I will gather you, and blow\n"
    .string "upon you in the fire of my wrath, and\l"
    .string "ye shall be melted in the midst\l"
    .string "therof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_22::
    .string "As silver is melted in the midst of\n"
    .string "the furnace, so shall ye be melted\l"
    .string "in the midst thereof; and ye shall\l"
    .string "know that I the LORD have poured out\l"
    .string "my fury upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_23::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_24::
    .string "Son of man, say unto her, Thou art\n"
    .string "the land that is not cleansed, nor\l"
    .string "rained upon in the day of indignation$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_25::
    .string "There is a conspiracy of her\n"
    .string "prophets in the midst thereof, like\l"
    .string "a roaring lion ravening the prey;\l"
    .string "they have devoured souls; they have\l"
    .string "taken the treasure and precious\l"
    .string "things; they have made her many\l"
    .string "widows in the midst thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_26::
    .string "Her priests have violated my law,\n"
    .string "and have profaned mine holy things:\l"
    .string "they have put no difference between\l"
    .string "the holy and profane, neither have\l"
    .string "they shewed difference between the\l"
    .string "unclean and the clean, and have hid\l"
    .string "their eyes from my sabbaths, and I am\l"
    .string "profaned among them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_27::
    .string "Her princes in the midst thereof\n"
    .string "are like wolves ravening the prey,\l"
    .string "to shed blood, and to destroy souls,\l"
    .string "to get dishonest gain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_28::
    .string "And her prophets have daubed them\n"
    .string "with untempered morter, seeing\l"
    .string "vanity, and divining lies unto them,\l"
    .string "saying, Thus saith the Lord GOD, when\l"
    .string "the LORD hath not spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_29::
    .string "The people of the land have used\n"
    .string "oppression, and exercised robbery,\l"
    .string "and have vexed the poor and needy:\l"
    .string "yea, they have oppressed the\l"
    .string "stranger wrongfully.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_30::
    .string "And I sought for a man among them,\n"
    .string "that should make up the hedge, and\l"
    .string "stand in the gap before me for the\l"
    .string "land, that I should not destroy it:\l"
    .string "but I found none.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_22_31::
    .string "Therefore have I poured out mine\n"
    .string "indignation upon them; I have\l"
    .string "consumed them with the fire of my\l"
    .string "wrath: their own way have I\l"
    .string "recompensed upon their heads, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_2::
    .string "Son of man, there were two women,\n"
    .string "the daughters of one mother:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_3::
    .string "And they committed whoredoms in\n"
    .string "Egypt; they committed whoredoms in\l"
    .string "their youth: there were their breasts\l"
    .string "pressed, and there they bruised the\l"
    .string "teats of their virginity$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_4::
    .string "And the names of them were Aholah\n"
    .string "the elder, and Aholibah her sister:\l"
    .string "and they were mine, and they bare\l"
    .string "sons and daughters. Thus were their\l"
    .string "names; Samaria is Aholah, and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem Aholibah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_5::
    .string "And Aholah played the harlot when\n"
    .string "she was mine; and she doted on her\l"
    .string "lovers, on the Assyrians her\l"
    .string "neighbours,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_6::
    .string "Which were clothed with blue,\n"
    .string "captains and rulers, all of them\l"
    .string "desirable young men, horsemen riding\l"
    .string "upon horses$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_7::
    .string "Thus she committed her whoredoms\n"
    .string "with them, with all them that were\l"
    .string "the chosen men of Assyria, and with\l"
    .string "all on whom she doted: with all\l"
    .string "their idols she defiled herself.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_8::
    .string "Neither left she her whoredoms\n"
    .string "brought from Egypt: for in her youth\l"
    .string "they lay with her, and they bruised\l"
    .string "the breasts of her virginity, and\l"
    .string "poured their whoredom upon her.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_9::
    .string "Wherefore I have delivered her into\n"
    .string "the hand of her lovers, into the hand\l"
    .string "of the Assyrians, upon whom she\l"
    .string "doted.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_10::
    .string "These discovered her nakedness:\n"
    .string "they took her sons and her daughters,\l"
    .string "and slew her with the sword: and she\l"
    .string "became famous among women; for they\l"
    .string "had executed judgment upon her.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_11::
    .string "And when her sister Aholibah saw\n"
    .string "this, she was more corrupt in her\l"
    .string "inordinate love than she, and in her\l"
    .string "whoredoms more than her sister in her\l"
    .string "whoredoms.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_12::
    .string "She doted upon the Assyrians her\n"
    .string "neighbours, captains and rulers\l"
    .string "clothed most gorgeously, horsemen\l"
    .string "riding upon horses, all of them\l"
    .string "desirable young men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_13::
    .string "Then I saw that she was defiled,\n"
    .string "that they took both one way,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_14::
    .string "And that she increased her\n"
    .string "whoredoms: for when she saw men\l"
    .string "pourtrayed upon the wall, the\l"
    .string "images of the Chaldeans pourtrayed\l"
    .string "with vermilion,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_15::
    .string "Girded with girdles upon their\n"
    .string "loins, exceeding in dyed attire upon\l"
    .string "their heads, all of them princes to\l"
    .string "look to, after the manner of the\l"
    .string "Babylonians of Chaldea, the land of\l"
    .string "their nativity:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_16::
    .string "And as soon as she saw them with her\n"
    .string "eyes, she doted upon them, and sent\l"
    .string "messengers unto them into Chaldea$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_17::
    .string "And the Babylonians came to her\n"
    .string "into the bed of love, and they\l"
    .string "defiled her with their whoredom, and\l"
    .string "she was polluted with them, and her\l"
    .string "mind was alienated from them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_18::
    .string "So she discovered her whoredoms, and\n"
    .string "discovered her nakedness: then my\l"
    .string "mind was alienated from her, like as\l"
    .string "my mind was alienated from her\l"
    .string "sister.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_19::
    .string "Yet she multiplied her whoredoms,\n"
    .string "in calling to remembrance the days\l"
    .string "of her youth, wherein she had played\l"
    .string "the harlot in the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_20::
    .string "For she doted upon their\n"
    .string "paramours, whose flesh is as the\l"
    .string "flesh of asses, and whose issue is\l"
    .string "like the issue of horses.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_21::
    .string "Thus thou calledst to remembrance\n"
    .string "the lewdness of thy youth, in\l"
    .string "bruising thy teats by the Egyptians\l"
    .string "for the paps of thy youth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_22::
    .string "Therefore, O Aholibah, thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD; Behold, I will raise\l"
    .string "up thy lovers against thee, from\l"
    .string "whom thy mind is alienated, and I\l"
    .string "will bring them against thee on\l"
    .string "every side;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_23::
    .string "The Babylonians, and all the\n"
    .string "Chaldeans, Pekod, and Shoa, and Koa,\l"
    .string "and all the Assyrians with them:\l"
    .string "all of them desirable young men,\l"
    .string "captains and rulers, great lords\l"
    .string "and renowned, all of them riding\l"
    .string "upon horses$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_24::
    .string "And they shall come against thee\n"
    .string "with chariots, wagons, and wheels,\l"
    .string "and with an assembly of people,\l"
    .string "which shall set against thee\l"
    .string "buckler and shield and helmet\l"
    .string "round about: and I will set judgment\l"
    .string "before them, and they shall judge\l"
    .string "thee according to their judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_25::
    .string "And I will set my jealousy against\n"
    .string "thee, and they shall deal\l"
    .string "furiously with thee: they shall\l"
    .string "take away thy nose and thine ears;\l"
    .string "and thy remnant shall fall by the\l"
    .string "sword: they shall take thy sons and\l"
    .string "thy daughters; and thy residue\l"
    .string "shall be devoured by the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_26::
    .string "They shall also strip thee out of\n"
    .string "thy clothes, and take away thy fair\l"
    .string "jewels.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_27::
    .string "Thus will I make thy lewdness to\n"
    .string "cease from thee, and thy whoredom\l"
    .string "brought from the land of Egypt: so\l"
    .string "that thou shalt not lift up thine\l"
    .string "eyes unto them, nor remember Egypt\l"
    .string "any more.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_28::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will deliver thee into\l"
    .string "the hand of them whom thou hatest,\l"
    .string "into the hand of them from whom thy\l"
    .string "mind is alienated:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_29::
    .string "And they shall deal with thee\n"
    .string "hatefully, and shall take away\l"
    .string "all thy labour, and shall leave\l"
    .string "thee naked and bare: and the\l"
    .string "nakedness of thy whoredoms shall be\l"
    .string "discovered, both thy lewdness and\l"
    .string "thy whoredoms$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_30::
    .string "I will do these things unto thee,\n"
    .string "because thou hast gone a whoring\l"
    .string "after the heathen, and because thou\l"
    .string "art polluted with their idols.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_31::
    .string "Thou hast walked in the way of thy\n"
    .string "sister; therefore will I give her\l"
    .string "cup into thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_32::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou shalt\n"
    .string "drink of thy sister’s cup deep and\l"
    .string "large: thou shalt be laughed to\l"
    .string "scorn and had in derision; it\l"
    .string "containeth much.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_33::
    .string "Thou shalt be filled with\n"
    .string "drunkenness and sorrow, with the cup\l"
    .string "of astonishment and desolation, with\l"
    .string "the cup of thy sister Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_34::
    .string "Thou shalt even drink it and suck\n"
    .string "it out, and thou shalt break the\l"
    .string "sherds thereof, and pluck off thine\l"
    .string "own breasts: for I have spoken it,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_35::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because thou hast forgotten me, and\l"
    .string "cast me behind thy back, therefore\l"
    .string "bear thou also thy lewdness and thy\l"
    .string "whoredoms.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_36::
    .string "The LORD said moreover unto me; Son\n"
    .string "of man, wilt thou judge Aholah and\l"
    .string "Aholibah? yea, declare unto them\l"
    .string "their abominations;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_37::
    .string "That they have committed adultery,\n"
    .string "and blood is in their hands, and with\l"
    .string "their idols have they committed\l"
    .string "adultery, and have also caused\l"
    .string "their sons, whom they bare unto me,\l"
    .string "to pass for them through the fire, to\l"
    .string "devour them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_38::
    .string "Moreover this they have done unto\n"
    .string "me: they have defiled my sanctuary\l"
    .string "in the same day, and have profaned my\l"
    .string "sabbaths.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_39::
    .string "For when they had slain their\n"
    .string "children to their idols, then they\l"
    .string "came the same day into my sanctuary\l"
    .string "to profane it; and, lo, thus have\l"
    .string "they done in the midst of mine house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_40::
    .string "And furthermore, that ye have sent\n"
    .string "for men to come from far, unto whom a\l"
    .string "messenger was sent; and, lo, they\l"
    .string "came: for whom thou didst wash\l"
    .string "thyself, paintedst thy eyes, and\l"
    .string "deckedst thyself with ornaments,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_41::
    .string "And satest upon a stately bed, and\n"
    .string "a table prepared before it,\l"
    .string "whereupon thou hast set mine incense\l"
    .string "and mine oil$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_42::
    .string "And a voice of a multitude being at\n"
    .string "ease was with her: and with the men of\l"
    .string "the common sort were brought Sabeans\l"
    .string "from the wilderness, which put\l"
    .string "bracelets upon their hands, and\l"
    .string "beautiful crowns upon their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_43::
    .string "Then said I unto her that was old in\n"
    .string "adulteries, Will they now commit\l"
    .string "whoredoms with her, and she with\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_44::
    .string "Yet they went in unto her, as they go\n"
    .string "in unto a woman that playeth the\l"
    .string "harlot: so went they in unto Aholah\l"
    .string "and unto Aholibah, the lewd women$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_45::
    .string "And the righteous men, they shall\n"
    .string "judge them after the manner of\l"
    .string "adulteresses, and after the manner\l"
    .string "of women that shed blood; because\l"
    .string "they are adulteresses, and blood is\l"
    .string "in their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_46::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "bring up a company upon them, and\l"
    .string "will give them to be removed and\l"
    .string "spoiled.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_47::
    .string "And the company shall stone them\n"
    .string "with stones, and dispatch them with\l"
    .string "their swords; they shall slay their\l"
    .string "sons and their daughters, and burn\l"
    .string "up their houses with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_48::
    .string "Thus will I cause lewdness to\n"
    .string "cease out of the land, that all\l"
    .string "women may be taught not to do after\l"
    .string "your lewdness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_23_49::
    .string "And they shall recompense your\n"
    .string "lewdness upon you, and ye shall\l"
    .string "bear the sins of your idols: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_1::
    .string "Again in the ninth year, in the\n"
    .string "tenth month, in the tenth day of the\l"
    .string "month, the word of the LORD came unto\l"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_2::
    .string "Son of man, write thee the name of\n"
    .string "the day, even of this same day: the\l"
    .string "king of Babylon set himself against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem this same day$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_3::
    .string "And utter a parable unto the\n"
    .string "rebellious house, and say unto\l"
    .string "them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Set on\l"
    .string "a pot, set it on, and also pour\l"
    .string "water into it:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_4::
    .string "Gather the pieces thereof into it,\n"
    .string "even every good piece, the thigh,\l"
    .string "and the shoulder; fill it with the\l"
    .string "choice bones$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_5::
    .string "Take the choice of the flock, and\n"
    .string "burn also the bones under it, and\l"
    .string "make it boil well, and let them\l"
    .string "seethe the bones of it therein.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_6::
    .string "Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Woe to the bloody city, to the pot\l"
    .string "whose scum is therein, and whose scum\l"
    .string "is not gone out of it! bring it out\l"
    .string "piece by piece; let no lot fall\l"
    .string "upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_7::
    .string "For her blood is in the midst of\n"
    .string "her; she set it upon the top of a\l"
    .string "rock; she poured it not upon the\l"
    .string "ground, to cover it with dust;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_8::
    .string "That it might cause fury to come up\n"
    .string "to take vengeance; I have set her\l"
    .string "blood upon the top of a rock, that\l"
    .string "it should not be covered$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_9::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Woe to the bloody city! I will even\l"
    .string "make the pile for fire great.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_10::
    .string "Heap on wood, kindle the fire,\n"
    .string "consume the flesh, and spice it\l"
    .string "well, and let the bones be burned.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_11::
    .string "Then set it empty upon the coals\n"
    .string "thereof, that the brass of it may be\l"
    .string "hot, and may burn, and that the\l"
    .string "filthiness of it may be molten in\l"
    .string "it, that the scum of it may be\l"
    .string "consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_12::
    .string "She hath wearied herself with\n"
    .string "lies, and her great scum went not\l"
    .string "forth out of her: her scum shall be\l"
    .string "in the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_13::
    .string "In thy filthiness is lewdness:\n"
    .string "because I have purged thee, and thou\l"
    .string "wast not purged, thou shalt not be\l"
    .string "purged from thy filthiness any more,\l"
    .string "till I have caused my fury to rest\l"
    .string "upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_14::
    .string "I the LORD have spoken it: it\n"
    .string "shall come to pass, and I will do\l"
    .string "it; I will not go back, neither\l"
    .string "will I spare, neither will I\l"
    .string "repent; according to thy ways, and\l"
    .string "according to thy doings, shall they\l"
    .string "judge thee, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_15::
    .string "Also the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_16::
    .string "Son of man, behold, I take away from\n"
    .string "thee the desire of thine eyes with a\l"
    .string "stroke: yet neither shalt thou mourn\l"
    .string "nor weep, neither shall thy tears\l"
    .string "run down$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_17::
    .string "Forbear to cry, make no mourning for\n"
    .string "the dead, bind the tire of thine head\l"
    .string "upon thee, and put on thy shoes\l"
    .string "upon thy feet, and cover not thy\l"
    .string "lips, and eat not the bread of men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_18::
    .string "So I spake unto the people in the\n"
    .string "morning: and at even my wife died;\l"
    .string "and I did in the morning as I was\l"
    .string "commanded.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_19::
    .string "And the people said unto me, Wilt\n"
    .string "thou not tell us what these things\l"
    .string "are to us, that thou doest so?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_20::
    .string "Then I answered them, The word of\n"
    .string "the LORD came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_21::
    .string "Speak unto the house of Israel,\n"
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I\l"
    .string "will profane my sanctuary, the\l"
    .string "excellency of your strength, the\l"
    .string "desire of your eyes, and that which\l"
    .string "your soul pitieth; and your sons and\l"
    .string "your daughters whom ye have left\l"
    .string "shall fall by the sword$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_22::
    .string "And ye shall do as I have done: ye\n"
    .string "shall not cover your lips, nor eat\l"
    .string "the bread of men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_23::
    .string "And your tires shall be upon your\n"
    .string "heads, and your shoes upon your\l"
    .string "feet: ye shall not mourn nor weep;\l"
    .string "but ye shall pine away for your\l"
    .string "iniquities, and mourn one toward\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_24::
    .string "Thus Ezekiel is unto you a sign:\n"
    .string "according to all that he hath done\l"
    .string "shall ye do: and when this cometh,\l"
    .string "ye shall know that I am the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_25::
    .string "Also, thou son of man, shall it\n"
    .string "not be in the day when I take from\l"
    .string "them their strength, the joy of their\l"
    .string "glory, the desire of their eyes, and\l"
    .string "that whereupon they set their minds,\l"
    .string "their sons and their daughters,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_26::
    .string "That he that escapeth in that day\n"
    .string "shall come unto thee, to cause thee\l"
    .string "to hear it with thine ears?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_24_27::
    .string "In that day shall thy mouth be\n"
    .string "opened to him which is escaped, and\l"
    .string "thou shalt speak, and be no more\l"
    .string "dumb: and thou shalt be a sign unto\l"
    .string "them; and they shall know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face against the\n"
    .string "Ammonites, and prophesy against\l"
    .string "them;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_3::
    .string "And say unto the Ammonites, Hear the\n"
    .string "word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD; Because thou saidst, Aha,\l"
    .string "against my sanctuary, when it was\l"
    .string "profaned; and against the land of\l"
    .string "Israel, when it was desolate; and\l"
    .string "against the house of Judah, when they\l"
    .string "went into captivity;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_4::
    .string "Behold, therefore I will deliver\n"
    .string "thee to the men of the east for a\l"
    .string "possession, and they shall set\l"
    .string "their palaces in thee, and make\l"
    .string "their dwellings in thee: they\l"
    .string "shall eat thy fruit, and they\l"
    .string "shall drink thy milk$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_5::
    .string "And I will make Rabbah a stable\n"
    .string "for camels, and the Ammonites a\l"
    .string "couching place for flocks: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_6::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; Because\n"
    .string "thou hast clapped thine hands, and\l"
    .string "stamped with the feet, and rejoiced\l"
    .string "in heart with all thy despite\l"
    .string "against the land of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_7::
    .string "Behold, therefore I will stretch\n"
    .string "out mine hand upon thee, and will\l"
    .string "deliver thee for a spoil to the\l"
    .string "heathen; and I will cut thee off\l"
    .string "from the people, and I will cause\l"
    .string "thee to perish out of the countries:\l"
    .string "I will destroy thee; and thou shalt\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_8::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because\n"
    .string "that Moab and Seir do say, Behold,\l"
    .string "the house of Judah is like unto all\l"
    .string "the heathen;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_9::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will open\n"
    .string "the side of Moab from the cities,\l"
    .string "from his cities which are on his\l"
    .string "frontiers, the glory of the country,\l"
    .string "Bethjeshimoth, Baalmeon, and\l"
    .string "Kiriathaim,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_10::
    .string "Unto the men of the east with the\n"
    .string "Ammonites, and will give them in\l"
    .string "possession, that the Ammonites may\l"
    .string "not be remembered among the nations$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_11::
    .string "And I will execute judgments upon\n"
    .string "Moab; and they shall know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_12::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because\n"
    .string "that Edom hath dealt against the\l"
    .string "house of Judah by taking vengeance,\l"
    .string "and hath greatly offended, and\l"
    .string "revenged himself upon them;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_13::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I\n"
    .string "will also stretch out mine hand\l"
    .string "upon Edom, and will cut off man and\l"
    .string "beast from it; and I will make it\l"
    .string "desolate from Teman; and they of\l"
    .string "Dedan shall fall by the sword$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_14::
    .string "And I will lay my vengeance upon\n"
    .string "Edom by the hand of my people\l"
    .string "Israel: and they shall do in Edom\l"
    .string "according to mine anger and\l"
    .string "according to my fury; and they shall\l"
    .string "know my vengeance, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_15::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the\n"
    .string "Philistines have dealt by revenge,\l"
    .string "and have taken vengeance with a\l"
    .string "despiteful heart, to destroy it for\l"
    .string "the old hatred;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_16::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will stretch out mine\l"
    .string "hand upon the Philistines, and I\l"
    .string "will cut off the Cherethims, and\l"
    .string "destroy the remnant of the sea coast$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_25_17::
    .string "And I will execute great vengeance\n"
    .string "upon them with furious rebukes; and\l"
    .string "they shall know that I am the LORD,\l"
    .string "when I shall lay my vengeance upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the eleventh\n"
    .string "year, in the first day of the month,\l"
    .string "that the word of the LORD came unto\l"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_2::
    .string "Son of man, because that Tyrus hath\n"
    .string "said against Jerusalem, Aha, she is\l"
    .string "broken that was the gates of the\l"
    .string "people: she is turned unto me: I\l"
    .string "shall be replenished, now she is\l"
    .string "laid waste:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_3::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O Tyrus,\l"
    .string "and will cause many nations to come\l"
    .string "up against thee, as the sea causeth\l"
    .string "his waves to come up$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_4::
    .string "And they shall destroy the walls\n"
    .string "of Tyrus, and break down her towers:\l"
    .string "I will also scrape her dust from\l"
    .string "her, and make her like the top of a\l"
    .string "rock.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_5::
    .string "It shall be a place for the\n"
    .string "spreading of nets in the midst of\l"
    .string "the sea: for I have spoken it, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD: and it shall become a\l"
    .string "spoil to the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_6::
    .string "And her daughters which are in the\n"
    .string "field shall be slain by the sword;\l"
    .string "and they shall know that I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_7::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will bring upon Tyrus\l"
    .string "Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, a\l"
    .string "king of kings, from the north, with\l"
    .string "horses, and with chariots, and with\l"
    .string "horsemen, and companies, and much\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_8::
    .string "He shall slay with the sword thy\n"
    .string "daughters in the field: and he\l"
    .string "shall make a fort against thee, and\l"
    .string "cast a mount against thee, and lift\l"
    .string "up the buckler against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_9::
    .string "And he shall set engines of war\n"
    .string "against thy walls, and with his axes\l"
    .string "he shall break down thy towers.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_10::
    .string "By reason of the abundance of his\n"
    .string "horses their dust shall cover thee:\l"
    .string "thy walls shall shake at the noise\l"
    .string "of the horsemen, and of the wheels,\l"
    .string "and of the chariots, when he shall\l"
    .string "enter into thy gates, as men enter\l"
    .string "into a city wherein is made a breach.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_11::
    .string "With the hoofs of his horses shall\n"
    .string "he tread down all thy streets: he\l"
    .string "shall slay thy people by the\l"
    .string "sword, and thy strong garrisons\l"
    .string "shall go down to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_12::
    .string "And they shall make a spoil of\n"
    .string "thy riches, and make a prey of thy\l"
    .string "merchandise: and they shall break\l"
    .string "down thy walls, and destroy thy\l"
    .string "pleasant houses: and they shall\l"
    .string "lay thy stones and thy timber and thy\l"
    .string "dust in the midst of the water.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_13::
    .string "And I will cause the noise of thy\n"
    .string "songs to cease; and the sound of thy\l"
    .string "harps shall be no more heard.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_14::
    .string "And I will make thee like the top\n"
    .string "of a rock: thou shalt be a place to\l"
    .string "spread nets upon; thou shalt be\l"
    .string "built no more: for I the LORD have\l"
    .string "spoken it, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_15::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD to Tyrus;\n"
    .string "Shall not the isles shake at the\l"
    .string "sound of thy fall, when the wounded\l"
    .string "cry, when the slaughter is made in\l"
    .string "the midst of thee?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_16::
    .string "Then all the princes of the sea\n"
    .string "shall come down from their thrones,\l"
    .string "and lay away their robes, and put\l"
    .string "off their broidered garments: they\l"
    .string "shall clothe themselves with\l"
    .string "trembling; they shall sit upon the\l"
    .string "ground, and shall tremble at every\l"
    .string "moment, and be astonished at thee$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_17::
    .string "And they shall take up a\n"
    .string "lamentation for thee, and say to\l"
    .string "thee, How art thou destroyed, that\l"
    .string "wast inhabited of seafaring men, the\l"
    .string "renowned city, which wast strong in\l"
    .string "the sea, she and her inhabitants,\l"
    .string "which cause their terror to be on\l"
    .string "all that haunt it!"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_18::
    .string "Now shall the isles tremble in\n"
    .string "the day of thy fall; yea, the isles\l"
    .string "that are in the sea shall be\l"
    .string "troubled at thy departure$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_19::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; When I\n"
    .string "shall make thee a desolate city,\l"
    .string "like the cities that are not\l"
    .string "inhabited; when I shall bring up\l"
    .string "the deep upon thee, and great waters\l"
    .string "shall cover thee;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_20::
    .string "When I shall bring thee down with\n"
    .string "them that descend into the pit, with\l"
    .string "the people of old time, and shall\l"
    .string "set thee in the low parts of the\l"
    .string "earth, in places desolate of old,\l"
    .string "with them that go down to the pit,\l"
    .string "that thou be not inhabited; and I\l"
    .string "shall set glory in the land of the\l"
    .string "living;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_26_21::
    .string "I will make thee a terror, and thou\n"
    .string "shalt be no more: though thou be\l"
    .string "sought for, yet shalt thou never be\l"
    .string "found again, saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_2::
    .string "Now, thou son of man, take up a\n"
    .string "lamentation for Tyrus;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_3::
    .string "And say unto Tyrus, O thou that art\n"
    .string "situate at the entry of the sea,\l"
    .string "which art a merchant of the people\l"
    .string "for many isles, Thus saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD; O Tyrus, thou hast said, I am of\l"
    .string "perfect beauty$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_4::
    .string "Thy borders are in the midst of the\n"
    .string "seas, thy builders have perfected\l"
    .string "thy beauty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_5::
    .string "They have made all thy ship boards\n"
    .string "of fir trees of Senir: they have\l"
    .string "taken cedars from Lebanon to make\l"
    .string "masts for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_6::
    .string "Of the oaks of Bashan have they made\n"
    .string "thine oars; the company of the\l"
    .string "Ashurites have made thy benches of\l"
    .string "ivory, brought out of the isles of\l"
    .string "Chittim.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_7::
    .string "Fine linen with broidered work from\n"
    .string "Egypt was that which thou spreadest\l"
    .string "forth to be thy sail; blue and\l"
    .string "purple from the isles of Elishah\l"
    .string "was that which covered thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_8::
    .string "The inhabitants of Zidon and Arvad\n"
    .string "were thy mariners: thy wise men, O\l"
    .string "Tyrus, that were in thee, were thy\l"
    .string "pilots.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_9::
    .string "The ancients of Gebal and the wise\n"
    .string "men thereof were in thee thy\l"
    .string "calkers: all the ships of the sea\l"
    .string "with their mariners were in thee to\l"
    .string "occupy thy merchandise.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_10::
    .string "They of Persia and of Lud and of\n"
    .string "Phut were in thine army, thy men of\l"
    .string "war: they hanged the shield and\l"
    .string "helmet in thee; they set forth thy\l"
    .string "comeliness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_11::
    .string "The men of Arvad with thine army\n"
    .string "were upon thy walls round about,\l"
    .string "and the Gammadims were in thy towers:\l"
    .string "they hanged their shields upon thy\l"
    .string "walls round about; they have made\l"
    .string "thy beauty perfect.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_12::
    .string "Tarshish was thy merchant by reason\n"
    .string "of the multitude of all kind of\l"
    .string "riches; with silver, iron, tin, and\l"
    .string "lead, they traded in thy fairs.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_13::
    .string "Javan, Tubal, and Meshech, they\n"
    .string "were thy merchants: they traded the\l"
    .string "persons of men and vessels of brass\l"
    .string "in thy market.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_14::
    .string "They of the house of Togarmah traded\n"
    .string "in thy fairs with horses and horsemen\l"
    .string "and mules.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_15::
    .string "The men of Dedan were thy merchants;\n"
    .string "many isles were the merchandise of\l"
    .string "thine hand: they brought thee for a\l"
    .string "present horns of ivory and ebony.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_16::
    .string "Syria was thy merchant by reason of\n"
    .string "the multitude of the wares of thy\l"
    .string "making: they occupied in thy fairs\l"
    .string "with emeralds, purple, and\l"
    .string "broidered work, and fine linen, and\l"
    .string "coral, and agate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_17::
    .string "Judah, and the land of Israel, they\n"
    .string "were thy merchants: they traded in\l"
    .string "thy market wheat of Minnith, and\l"
    .string "Pannag, and honey, and oil, and balm.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_18::
    .string "Damascus was thy merchant in the\n"
    .string "multitude of the wares of thy\l"
    .string "making, for the multitude of all\l"
    .string "riches; in the wine of Helbon, and\l"
    .string "white wool.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_19::
    .string "Dan also and Javan going to and fro\n"
    .string "occupied in thy fairs: bright iron,\l"
    .string "cassia, and calamus, were in thy\l"
    .string "market.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_20::
    .string "Dedan was thy merchant in precious\n"
    .string "clothes for chariots.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_21::
    .string "Arabia, and all the princes of\n"
    .string "Kedar, they occupied with thee in\l"
    .string "lambs, and rams, and goats: in these\l"
    .string "were they thy merchants.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_22::
    .string "The merchants of Sheba and Raamah,\n"
    .string "they were thy merchants: they\l"
    .string "occupied in thy fairs with chief of\l"
    .string "all spices, and with all precious\l"
    .string "stones, and gold.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_23::
    .string "Haran, and Canneh, and Eden, the\n"
    .string "merchants of Sheba, Asshur, and\l"
    .string "Chilmad, were thy merchants.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_24::
    .string "These were thy merchants in all\n"
    .string "sorts of things, in blue clothes,\l"
    .string "and broidered work, and in chests of\l"
    .string "rich apparel, bound with cords, and\l"
    .string "made of cedar, among thy merchandise.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_25::
    .string "The ships of Tarshish did sing of\n"
    .string "thee in thy market: and thou wast\l"
    .string "replenished, and made very\l"
    .string "glorious in the midst of the seas.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_26::
    .string "Thy rowers have brought thee into\n"
    .string "great waters: the east wind hath\l"
    .string "broken thee in the midst of the seas.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_27::
    .string "Thy riches, and thy fairs, thy\n"
    .string "merchandise, thy mariners, and thy\l"
    .string "pilots, thy calkers, and the\l"
    .string "occupiers of thy merchandise, and\l"
    .string "all thy men of war, that are in\l"
    .string "thee, and in all thy company which\l"
    .string "is in the midst of thee, shall fall\l"
    .string "into the midst of the seas in the day\l"
    .string "of thy ruin.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_28::
    .string "The suburbs shall shake at the\n"
    .string "sound of the cry of thy pilots.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_29::
    .string "And all that handle the oar, the\n"
    .string "mariners, and all the pilots of\l"
    .string "the sea, shall come down from their\l"
    .string "ships, they shall stand upon the\l"
    .string "land;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_30::
    .string "And shall cause their voice to be\n"
    .string "heard against thee, and shall cry\l"
    .string "bitterly, and shall cast up dust\l"
    .string "upon their heads, they shall\l"
    .string "wallow themselves in the ashes:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_31::
    .string "And they shall make themselves\n"
    .string "utterly bald for thee, and gird them\l"
    .string "with sackcloth, and they shall\l"
    .string "weep for thee with bitterness of\l"
    .string "heart and bitter wailing$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_32::
    .string "And in their wailing they shall\n"
    .string "take up a lamentation for thee, and\l"
    .string "lament over thee, saying, What city\l"
    .string "is like Tyrus, like the destroyed in\l"
    .string "the midst of the sea?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_33::
    .string "When thy wares went forth out of the\n"
    .string "seas, thou filledst many people;\l"
    .string "thou didst enrich the kings of the\l"
    .string "earth with the multitude of thy\l"
    .string "riches and of thy merchandise$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_34::
    .string "In the time when thou shalt be\n"
    .string "broken by the seas in the depths of\l"
    .string "the waters thy merchandise and all\l"
    .string "thy company in the midst of thee\l"
    .string "shall fall.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_35::
    .string "All the inhabitants of the isles\n"
    .string "shall be astonished at thee, and\l"
    .string "their kings shall be sore afraid,\l"
    .string "they shall be troubled in their\l"
    .string "countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_27_36::
    .string "The merchants among the people\n"
    .string "shall hiss at thee; thou shalt be a\l"
    .string "terror, and never shalt be any more.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_2::
    .string "Son of man, say unto the prince of\n"
    .string "Tyrus, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "Because thine heart is lifted up,\l"
    .string "and thou hast said, I am a God, I sit\l"
    .string "in the seat of God, in the midst of\l"
    .string "the seas; yet thou art a man, and not\l"
    .string "God, though thou set thine heart as\l"
    .string "the heart of God:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_3::
    .string "Behold, thou art wiser than\n"
    .string "Daniel; there is no secret that they\l"
    .string "can hide from thee:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_4::
    .string "With thy wisdom and with thine\n"
    .string "understanding thou hast gotten thee\l"
    .string "riches, and hast gotten gold and\l"
    .string "silver into thy treasures:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_5::
    .string "By thy great wisdom and by thy\n"
    .string "traffick hast thou increased thy\l"
    .string "riches, and thine heart is lifted up\l"
    .string "because of thy riches:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_6::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because thou hast set thine heart as\l"
    .string "the heart of God;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_7::
    .string "Behold, therefore I will bring\n"
    .string "strangers upon thee, the terrible\l"
    .string "of the nations: and they shall draw\l"
    .string "their swords against the beauty of\l"
    .string "thy wisdom, and they shall defile\l"
    .string "thy brightness$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_8::
    .string "They shall bring thee down to the\n"
    .string "pit, and thou shalt die the deaths of\l"
    .string "them that are slain in the midst of\l"
    .string "the seas.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_9::
    .string "Wilt thou yet say before him that\n"
    .string "slayeth thee, I am God? but thou\l"
    .string "shalt be a man, and no God, in the\l"
    .string "hand of him that slayeth thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_10::
    .string "Thou shalt die the deaths of the\n"
    .string "uncircumcised by the hand of\l"
    .string "strangers: for I have spoken it,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_11::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_12::
    .string "Son of man, take up a lamentation\n"
    .string "upon the king of Tyrus, and say unto\l"
    .string "him, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou\l"
    .string "sealest up the sum, full of\l"
    .string "wisdom, and perfect in beauty$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_13::
    .string "Thou hast been in Eden the garden of\n"
    .string "God; every precious stone was thy\l"
    .string "covering, the sardius, topaz, and\l"
    .string "the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and\l"
    .string "the jasper, the sapphire, the\l"
    .string "emerald, and the carbuncle, and\l"
    .string "gold: the workmanship of thy\l"
    .string "tabrets and of thy pipes was\l"
    .string "prepared in thee in the day that\l"
    .string "thou wast created.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_14::
    .string "Thou art the anointed cherub that\n"
    .string "covereth; and I have set thee so:\l"
    .string "thou wast upon the holy mountain of\l"
    .string "God; thou hast walked up and down in\l"
    .string "the midst of the stones of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_15::
    .string "Thou wast perfect in thy ways from\n"
    .string "the day that thou wast created, till\l"
    .string "iniquity was found in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_16::
    .string "By the multitude of thy merchandise\n"
    .string "they have filled the midst of thee\l"
    .string "with violence, and thou hast sinned:\l"
    .string "therefore I will cast thee as\l"
    .string "profane out of the mountain of God:\l"
    .string "and I will destroy thee, O covering\l"
    .string "cherub, from the midst of the stones\l"
    .string "of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_17::
    .string "Thine heart was lifted up because\n"
    .string "of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted\l"
    .string "thy wisdom by reason of thy\l"
    .string "brightness: I will cast thee to the\l"
    .string "ground, I will lay thee before\l"
    .string "kings, that they may behold thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_18::
    .string "Thou hast defiled thy sanctuaries\n"
    .string "by the multitude of thine\l"
    .string "iniquities, by the iniquity of thy\l"
    .string "traffick; therefore will I bring\l"
    .string "forth a fire from the midst of thee,\l"
    .string "it shall devour thee, and I will\l"
    .string "bring thee to ashes upon the earth\l"
    .string "in the sight of all them that\l"
    .string "behold thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_19::
    .string "All they that know thee among the\n"
    .string "people shall be astonished at\l"
    .string "thee: thou shalt be a terror, and\l"
    .string "never shalt thou be any more.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_20::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_21::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face against\n"
    .string "Zidon, and prophesy against it,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_22::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O Zidon;\l"
    .string "and I will be glorified in the\l"
    .string "midst of thee: and they shall know\l"
    .string "that I am the LORD, when I shall\l"
    .string "have executed judgments in her, and\l"
    .string "shall be sanctified in her$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_23::
    .string "For I will send into her\n"
    .string "pestilence, and blood into her\l"
    .string "streets; and the wounded shall be\l"
    .string "judged in the midst of her by the\l"
    .string "sword upon her on every side; and\l"
    .string "they shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_24::
    .string "And there shall be no more a\n"
    .string "pricking brier unto the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, nor any grieving thorn of\l"
    .string "all that are round about them, that\l"
    .string "despised them; and they shall know\l"
    .string "that I am the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_25::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; When I\n"
    .string "shall have gathered the house of\l"
    .string "Israel from the people among whom\l"
    .string "they are scattered, and shall be\l"
    .string "sanctified in them in the sight of\l"
    .string "the heathen, then shall they dwell\l"
    .string "in their land that I have given to my\l"
    .string "servant Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_28_26::
    .string "And they shall dwell safely\n"
    .string "therein, and shall build houses,\l"
    .string "and plant vineyards; yea, they\l"
    .string "shall dwell with confidence, when\l"
    .string "I have executed judgments upon all\l"
    .string "those that despise them round about\l"
    .string "them; and they shall know that I am\l"
    .string "the LORD their God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_1::
    .string "In the tenth year, in the tenth\n"
    .string "month, in the twelfth day of the\l"
    .string "month, the word of the LORD came unto\l"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face against\n"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy\l"
    .string "against him, and against all Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_3::
    .string "Speak, and say, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD; Behold, I am against thee,\l"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt, the great\l"
    .string "dragon that lieth in the midst of\l"
    .string "his rivers, which hath said, My river\l"
    .string "is mine own, and I have made it for\l"
    .string "myself$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_4::
    .string "But I will put hooks in thy jaws,\n"
    .string "and I will cause the fish of thy\l"
    .string "rivers to stick unto thy scales, and\l"
    .string "I will bring thee up out of the\l"
    .string "midst of thy rivers, and all the\l"
    .string "fish of thy rivers shall stick unto\l"
    .string "thy scales.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_5::
    .string "And I will leave thee thrown into\n"
    .string "the wilderness, thee and all the\l"
    .string "fish of thy rivers: thou shalt fall\l"
    .string "upon the open fields; thou shalt\l"
    .string "not be brought together, nor\l"
    .string "gathered: I have given thee for meat\l"
    .string "to the beasts of the field and to the\l"
    .string "fowls of the heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_6::
    .string "And all the inhabitants of Egypt\n"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD,\l"
    .string "because they have been a staff of\l"
    .string "reed to the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_7::
    .string "When they took hold of thee by thy\n"
    .string "hand, thou didst break, and rend all\l"
    .string "their shoulder: and when they\l"
    .string "leaned upon thee, thou brakest, and\l"
    .string "madest all their loins to be at a\l"
    .string "stand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_8::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will bring a sword upon\l"
    .string "thee, and cut off man and beast out of\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_9::
    .string "And the land of Egypt shall be\n"
    .string "desolate and waste; and they shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD: because he\l"
    .string "hath said, The river is mine, and I\l"
    .string "have made it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_10::
    .string "Behold, therefore I am against\n"
    .string "thee, and against thy rivers, and I\l"
    .string "will make the land of Egypt\l"
    .string "utterly waste and desolate, from\l"
    .string "the tower of Syene even unto the\l"
    .string "border of Ethiopia.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_11::
    .string "No foot of man shall pass through\n"
    .string "it, nor foot of beast shall pass\l"
    .string "through it, neither shall it be\l"
    .string "inhabited forty years.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_12::
    .string "And I will make the land of Egypt\n"
    .string "desolate in the midst of the\l"
    .string "countries that are desolate, and her\l"
    .string "cities among the cities that are\l"
    .string "laid waste shall be desolate forty\l"
    .string "years: and I will scatter the\l"
    .string "Egyptians among the nations, and\l"
    .string "will disperse them through the\l"
    .string "countries.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_13::
    .string "Yet thus saith the Lord GOD; At the\n"
    .string "end of forty years will I gather the\l"
    .string "Egyptians from the people whither\l"
    .string "they were scattered:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_14::
    .string "And I will bring again the\n"
    .string "captivity of Egypt, and will cause\l"
    .string "them to return into the land of\l"
    .string "Pathros, into the land of their\l"
    .string "habitation; and they shall be there\l"
    .string "a base kingdom$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_15::
    .string "It shall be the basest of the\n"
    .string "kingdoms; neither shall it exalt\l"
    .string "itself any more above the nations:\l"
    .string "for I will diminish them, that they\l"
    .string "shall no more rule over the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_16::
    .string "And it shall be no more the\n"
    .string "confidence of the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "which bringeth their iniquity to\l"
    .string "remembrance, when they shall look\l"
    .string "after them: but they shall know that\l"
    .string "I am the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_17::
    .string "And it came to pass in the seven and\n"
    .string "twentieth year, in the first month,\l"
    .string "in the first day of the month, the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD came unto me,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_18::
    .string "Son of man, Nebuchadrezzar king of\n"
    .string "Babylon caused his army to serve a\l"
    .string "great service against Tyrus: every\l"
    .string "head was made bald, and every\l"
    .string "shoulder was peeled: yet had he no\l"
    .string "wages, nor his army, for Tyrus, for\l"
    .string "the service that he had served\l"
    .string "against it:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_19::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will give the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt unto Nebuchadrezzar king of\l"
    .string "Babylon; and he shall take her\l"
    .string "multitude, and take her spoil, and\l"
    .string "take her prey; and it shall be the\l"
    .string "wages for his army$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_20::
    .string "I have given him the land of Egypt\n"
    .string "for his labour wherewith he served\l"
    .string "against it, because they wrought for\l"
    .string "me, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_29_21::
    .string "In that day will I cause the horn\n"
    .string "of the house of Israel to bud forth,\l"
    .string "and I will give thee the opening of\l"
    .string "the mouth in the midst of them; and\l"
    .string "they shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_2::
    .string "Son of man, prophesy and say, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Howl ye, Woe\l"
    .string "worth the day!"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_3::
    .string "For the day is near, even the day of\n"
    .string "the LORD is near, a cloudy day; it\l"
    .string "shall be the time of the heathen$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_4::
    .string "And the sword shall come upon\n"
    .string "Egypt, and great pain shall be in\l"
    .string "Ethiopia, when the slain shall\l"
    .string "fall in Egypt, and they shall take\l"
    .string "away her multitude, and her\l"
    .string "foundations shall be broken down.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_5::
    .string "Ethiopia, and Libya, and Lydia, and\n"
    .string "all the mingled people, and Chub,\l"
    .string "and the men of the land that is in\l"
    .string "league, shall fall with them by\l"
    .string "the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_6::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; They also that\n"
    .string "uphold Egypt shall fall; and the\l"
    .string "pride of her power shall come down:\l"
    .string "from the tower of Syene shall they\l"
    .string "fall in it by the sword, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_7::
    .string "And they shall be desolate in the\n"
    .string "midst of the countries that are\l"
    .string "desolate, and her cities shall be\l"
    .string "in the midst of the cities that are\l"
    .string "wasted.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_8::
    .string "And they shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when I have set a fire in\l"
    .string "Egypt, and when all her helpers\l"
    .string "shall be destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_9::
    .string "In that day shall messengers go\n"
    .string "forth from me in ships to make the\l"
    .string "careless Ethiopians afraid, and\l"
    .string "great pain shall come upon them,\l"
    .string "as in the day of Egypt: for, lo, it\l"
    .string "cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_10::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "also make the multitude of Egypt to\l"
    .string "cease by the hand of Nebuchadrezzar\l"
    .string "king of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_11::
    .string "He and his people with him, the\n"
    .string "terrible of the nations, shall be\l"
    .string "brought to destroy the land: and\l"
    .string "they shall draw their swords\l"
    .string "against Egypt, and fill the land\l"
    .string "with the slain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_12::
    .string "And I will make the rivers dry, and\n"
    .string "sell the land into the hand of the\l"
    .string "wicked: and I will make the land\l"
    .string "waste, and all that is therein, by\l"
    .string "the hand of strangers: I the LORD\l"
    .string "have spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_13::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "also destroy the idols, and I will\l"
    .string "cause their images to cease out of\l"
    .string "Noph; and there shall be no more a\l"
    .string "prince of the land of Egypt: and I\l"
    .string "will put a fear in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_14::
    .string "And I will make Pathros desolate,\n"
    .string "and will set fire in Zoan, and will\l"
    .string "execute judgments in No.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_15::
    .string "And I will pour my fury upon Sin,\n"
    .string "the strength of Egypt; and I will\l"
    .string "cut off the multitude of No.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_16::
    .string "And I will set fire in Egypt: Sin\n"
    .string "shall have great pain, and No\l"
    .string "shall be rent asunder, and Noph\l"
    .string "shall have distresses daily.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_17::
    .string "The young men of Aven and of\n"
    .string "Pibeseth shall fall by the sword:\l"
    .string "and these cities shall go into\l"
    .string "captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_18::
    .string "At Tehaphnehes also the day shall\n"
    .string "be darkened, when I shall break\l"
    .string "there the yokes of Egypt: and the\l"
    .string "pomp of her strength shall cease in\l"
    .string "her: as for her, a cloud shall\l"
    .string "cover her, and her daughters shall\l"
    .string "go into captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_19::
    .string "Thus will I execute judgments in\n"
    .string "Egypt: and they shall know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_20::
    .string "And it came to pass in the eleventh\n"
    .string "year, in the first month, in the\l"
    .string "seventh day of the month, that the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD came unto me,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_21::
    .string "Son of man, I have broken the arm of\n"
    .string "Pharaoh king of Egypt; and, lo, it\l"
    .string "shall not be bound up to be healed,\l"
    .string "to put a roller to bind it, to make\l"
    .string "it strong to hold the sword$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_22::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and will break his arms, the\l"
    .string "strong, and that which was broken;\l"
    .string "and I will cause the sword to fall\l"
    .string "out of his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_23::
    .string "And I will scatter the Egyptians\n"
    .string "among the nations, and will\l"
    .string "disperse them through the countries.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_24::
    .string "And I will strengthen the arms of\n"
    .string "the king of Babylon, and put my\l"
    .string "sword in his hand: but I will break\l"
    .string "Pharaoh’s arms, and he shall groan\l"
    .string "before him with the groanings of a\l"
    .string "deadly wounded man.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_25::
    .string "But I will strengthen the arms of\n"
    .string "the king of Babylon, and the arms of\l"
    .string "Pharaoh shall fall down; and they\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD, when\l"
    .string "I shall put my sword into the hand\l"
    .string "of the king of Babylon, and he\l"
    .string "shall stretch it out upon the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_30_26::
    .string "And I will scatter the Egyptians\n"
    .string "among the nations, and disperse them\l"
    .string "among the countries; and they shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the eleventh\n"
    .string "year, in the third month, in the\l"
    .string "first day of the month, that the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_2::
    .string "Son of man, speak unto Pharaoh king\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and to his multitude; Whom\l"
    .string "art thou like in thy greatness?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_3::
    .string "Behold, the Assyrian was a cedar in\n"
    .string "Lebanon with fair branches, and with\l"
    .string "a shadowing shroud, and of an high\l"
    .string "stature; and his top was among the\l"
    .string "thick boughs$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_4::
    .string "The waters made him great, the deep\n"
    .string "set him up on high with her rivers\l"
    .string "running round about his plants, and\l"
    .string "sent her little rivers unto all\l"
    .string "the trees of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_5::
    .string "Therefore his height was exalted\n"
    .string "above all the trees of the field,\l"
    .string "and his boughs were multiplied, and\l"
    .string "his branches became long because of\l"
    .string "the multitude of waters, when he\l"
    .string "shot forth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_6::
    .string "All the fowls of heaven made their\n"
    .string "nests in his boughs, and under his\l"
    .string "branches did all the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field bring forth their young, and\l"
    .string "under his shadow dwelt all great\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_7::
    .string "Thus was he fair in his greatness,\n"
    .string "in the length of his branches: for\l"
    .string "his root was by great waters.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_8::
    .string "The cedars in the garden of God\n"
    .string "could not hide him: the fir trees\l"
    .string "were not like his boughs, and the\l"
    .string "chestnut trees were not like his\l"
    .string "branches; nor any tree in the garden\l"
    .string "of God was like unto him in his\l"
    .string "beauty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_9::
    .string "I have made him fair by the\n"
    .string "multitude of his branches: so that\l"
    .string "all the trees of Eden, that were in\l"
    .string "the garden of God, envied him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_10::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Because thou hast lifted up\l"
    .string "thyself in height, and he hath shot\l"
    .string "up his top among the thick boughs,\l"
    .string "and his heart is lifted up in his\l"
    .string "height;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_11::
    .string "I have therefore delivered him into\n"
    .string "the hand of the mighty one of the\l"
    .string "heathen; he shall surely deal with\l"
    .string "him: I have driven him out for his\l"
    .string "wickedness$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_12::
    .string "And strangers, the terrible of the\n"
    .string "nations, have cut him off, and have\l"
    .string "left him: upon the mountains and in\l"
    .string "all the valleys his branches are\l"
    .string "fallen, and his boughs are broken by\l"
    .string "all the rivers of the land; and\l"
    .string "all the people of the earth are\l"
    .string "gone down from his shadow, and have\l"
    .string "left him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_13::
    .string "Upon his ruin shall all the\n"
    .string "fowls of the heaven remain, and all\l"
    .string "the beasts of the field shall be\l"
    .string "upon his branches:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_14::
    .string "To the end that none of all the\n"
    .string "trees by the waters exalt\l"
    .string "themselves for their height, neither\l"
    .string "shoot up their top among the thick\l"
    .string "boughs, neither their trees stand up\l"
    .string "in their height, all that drink\l"
    .string "water: for they are all delivered\l"
    .string "unto death, to the nether parts of\l"
    .string "the earth, in the midst of the\l"
    .string "children of men, with them that go\l"
    .string "down to the pit$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_15::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day\n"
    .string "when he went down to the grave I\l"
    .string "caused a mourning: I covered the\l"
    .string "deep for him, and I restrained the\l"
    .string "floods thereof, and the great waters\l"
    .string "were stayed: and I caused Lebanon to\l"
    .string "mourn for him, and all the trees of\l"
    .string "the field fainted for him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_16::
    .string "I made the nations to shake at the\n"
    .string "sound of his fall, when I cast him\l"
    .string "down to hell with them that descend\l"
    .string "into the pit: and all the trees of\l"
    .string "Eden, the choice and best of Lebanon,\l"
    .string "all that drink water, shall be\l"
    .string "comforted in the nether parts of the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_17::
    .string "They also went down into hell with\n"
    .string "him unto them that be slain with the\l"
    .string "sword; and they that were his arm,\l"
    .string "that dwelt under his shadow in the\l"
    .string "midst of the heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_31_18::
    .string "To whom art thou thus like in glory\n"
    .string "and in greatness among the trees of\l"
    .string "Eden? yet shalt thou be brought down\l"
    .string "with the trees of Eden unto the\l"
    .string "nether parts of the earth: thou\l"
    .string "shalt lie in the midst of the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised with them that be\l"
    .string "slain by the sword. This is Pharaoh\l"
    .string "and all his multitude, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the twelfth\n"
    .string "year, in the twelfth month, in the\l"
    .string "first day of the month, that the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_2::
    .string "Son of man, take up a lamentation\n"
    .string "for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say\l"
    .string "unto him, Thou art like a young lion\l"
    .string "of the nations, and thou art as a\l"
    .string "whale in the seas: and thou camest\l"
    .string "forth with thy rivers, and\l"
    .string "troubledst the waters with thy feet,\l"
    .string "and fouledst their rivers$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_3::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will\n"
    .string "therefore spread out my net over\l"
    .string "thee with a company of many\l"
    .string "people; and they shall bring thee\l"
    .string "up in my net.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_4::
    .string "Then will I leave thee upon the\n"
    .string "land, I will cast thee forth upon\l"
    .string "the open field, and will cause\l"
    .string "all the fowls of the heaven to\l"
    .string "remain upon thee, and I will fill\l"
    .string "the beasts of the whole earth with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_5::
    .string "And I will lay thy flesh upon the\n"
    .string "mountains, and fill the valleys\l"
    .string "with thy height.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_6::
    .string "I will also water with thy blood\n"
    .string "the land wherein thou swimmest, even\l"
    .string "to the mountains; and the rivers\l"
    .string "shall be full of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_7::
    .string "And when I shall put thee out, I\n"
    .string "will cover the heaven, and make the\l"
    .string "stars thereof dark; I will cover the\l"
    .string "sun with a cloud, and the moon\l"
    .string "shall not give her light.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_8::
    .string "All the bright lights of heaven\n"
    .string "will I make dark over thee, and set\l"
    .string "darkness upon thy land, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_9::
    .string "I will also vex the hearts of many\n"
    .string "people, when I shall bring thy\l"
    .string "destruction among the nations, into\l"
    .string "the countries which thou hast not\l"
    .string "known.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_10::
    .string "Yea, I will make many people\n"
    .string "amazed at thee, and their kings\l"
    .string "shall be horribly afraid for thee,\l"
    .string "when I shall brandish my sword\l"
    .string "before them; and they shall tremble\l"
    .string "at every moment, every man for his\l"
    .string "own life, in the day of thy fall.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_11::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; The\n"
    .string "sword of the king of Babylon shall\l"
    .string "come upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_12::
    .string "By the swords of the mighty will I\n"
    .string "cause thy multitude to fall, the\l"
    .string "terrible of the nations, all of\l"
    .string "them: and they shall spoil the\l"
    .string "pomp of Egypt, and all the\l"
    .string "multitude thereof shall be\l"
    .string "destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_13::
    .string "I will destroy also all the\n"
    .string "beasts thereof from beside the great\l"
    .string "waters; neither shall the foot of\l"
    .string "man trouble them any more, nor the\l"
    .string "hoofs of beasts trouble them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_14::
    .string "Then will I make their waters\n"
    .string "deep, and cause their rivers to run\l"
    .string "like oil, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_15::
    .string "When I shall make the land of\n"
    .string "Egypt desolate, and the country\l"
    .string "shall be destitute of that whereof\l"
    .string "it was full, when I shall smite\l"
    .string "all them that dwell therein, then\l"
    .string "shall they know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_16::
    .string "This is the lamentation wherewith\n"
    .string "they shall lament her: the\l"
    .string "daughters of the nations shall\l"
    .string "lament her: they shall lament for\l"
    .string "her, even for Egypt, and for all\l"
    .string "her multitude, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_17::
    .string "It came to pass also in the\n"
    .string "twelfth year, in the fifteenth day\l"
    .string "of the month, that the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_18::
    .string "Son of man, wail for the multitude\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and cast them down, even\l"
    .string "her, and the daughters of the famous\l"
    .string "nations, unto the nether parts of\l"
    .string "the earth, with them that go down\l"
    .string "into the pit$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_19::
    .string "Whom dost thou pass in beauty? go\n"
    .string "down, and be thou laid with the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_20::
    .string "They shall fall in the midst of\n"
    .string "them that are slain by the sword: she\l"
    .string "is delivered to the sword: draw her\l"
    .string "and all her multitudes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_21::
    .string "The strong among the mighty shall\n"
    .string "speak to him out of the midst of\l"
    .string "hell with them that help him: they\l"
    .string "are gone down, they lie\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, slain by the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_22::
    .string "Asshur is there and all her\n"
    .string "company: his graves are about him:\l"
    .string "all of them slain, fallen by the\l"
    .string "sword:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_23::
    .string "Whose graves are set in the sides of\n"
    .string "the pit, and her company is round\l"
    .string "about her grave: all of them slain,\l"
    .string "fallen by the sword, which caused\l"
    .string "terror in the land of the living$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_24::
    .string "There is Elam and all her\n"
    .string "multitude round about her grave,\l"
    .string "all of them slain, fallen by the\l"
    .string "sword, which are gone down\l"
    .string "uncircumcised into the nether parts\l"
    .string "of the earth, which caused their\l"
    .string "terror in the land of the living;\l"
    .string "yet have they borne their shame with\l"
    .string "them that go down to the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_25::
    .string "They have set her a bed in the midst\n"
    .string "of the slain with all her\l"
    .string "multitude: her graves are round\l"
    .string "about him: all of them\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, slain by the sword:\l"
    .string "though their terror was caused in the\l"
    .string "land of the living, yet have they\l"
    .string "borne their shame with them that go\l"
    .string "down to the pit: he is put in the\l"
    .string "midst of them that be slain.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_26::
    .string "There is Meshech, Tubal, and all\n"
    .string "her multitude: her graves are round\l"
    .string "about him: all of them\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, slain by the sword,\l"
    .string "though they caused their terror in\l"
    .string "the land of the living.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_27::
    .string "And they shall not lie with the\n"
    .string "mighty that are fallen of the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, which are gone down to\l"
    .string "hell with their weapons of war: and\l"
    .string "they have laid their swords under\l"
    .string "their heads, but their iniquities\l"
    .string "shall be upon their bones, though\l"
    .string "they were the terror of the mighty in\l"
    .string "the land of the living.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_28::
    .string "Yea, thou shalt be broken in the\n"
    .string "midst of the uncircumcised, and\l"
    .string "shalt lie with them that are slain\l"
    .string "with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_29::
    .string "There is Edom, her kings, and all\n"
    .string "her princes, which with their might\l"
    .string "are laid by them that were slain by\l"
    .string "the sword: they shall lie with the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised, and with them that go\l"
    .string "down to the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_30::
    .string "There be the princes of the north,\n"
    .string "all of them, and all the\l"
    .string "Zidonians, which are gone down with\l"
    .string "the slain; with their terror they\l"
    .string "are ashamed of their might; and they\l"
    .string "lie uncircumcised with them that be\l"
    .string "slain by the sword, and bear their\l"
    .string "shame with them that go down to the\l"
    .string "pit.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_31::
    .string "Pharaoh shall see them, and shall\n"
    .string "be comforted over all his\l"
    .string "multitude, even Pharaoh and all his\l"
    .string "army slain by the sword, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_32_32::
    .string "For I have caused my terror in the\n"
    .string "land of the living: and he shall be\l"
    .string "laid in the midst of the\l"
    .string "uncircumcised with them that are\l"
    .string "slain with the sword, even Pharaoh\l"
    .string "and all his multitude, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_1::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_2::
    .string "Son of man, speak to the children\n"
    .string "of thy people, and say unto them,\l"
    .string "When I bring the sword upon a land,\l"
    .string "if the people of the land take a\l"
    .string "man of their coasts, and set him for\l"
    .string "their watchman:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_3::
    .string "If when he seeth the sword come\n"
    .string "upon the land, he blow the\l"
    .string "trumpet, and warn the people;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_4::
    .string "Then whosoever heareth the sound of\n"
    .string "the trumpet, and taketh not warning;\l"
    .string "if the sword come, and take him away,\l"
    .string "his blood shall be upon his own\l"
    .string "head$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_5::
    .string "He heard the sound of the trumpet,\n"
    .string "and took not warning; his blood\l"
    .string "shall be upon him. But he that\l"
    .string "taketh warning shall deliver his\l"
    .string "soul.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_6::
    .string "But if the watchman see the sword\n"
    .string "come, and blow not the trumpet, and\l"
    .string "the people be not warned; if the\l"
    .string "sword come, and take any person from\l"
    .string "among them, he is taken away in his\l"
    .string "iniquity; but his blood will I\l"
    .string "require at the watchman’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_7::
    .string "So thou, O son of man, I have set\n"
    .string "thee a watchman unto the house of\l"
    .string "Israel; therefore thou shalt hear\l"
    .string "the word at my mouth, and warn them\l"
    .string "from me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_8::
    .string "When I say unto the wicked, O wicked\n"
    .string "man, thou shalt surely die; if thou\l"
    .string "dost not speak to warn the wicked\l"
    .string "from his way, that wicked man shall\l"
    .string "die in his iniquity; but his blood\l"
    .string "will I require at thine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_9::
    .string "Nevertheless, if thou warn the\n"
    .string "wicked of his way to turn from it; if\l"
    .string "he do not turn from his way, he\l"
    .string "shall die in his iniquity; but thou\l"
    .string "hast delivered thy soul.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_10::
    .string "Therefore, O thou son of man, speak\n"
    .string "unto the house of Israel; Thus ye\l"
    .string "speak, saying, If our transgressions\l"
    .string "and our sins be upon us, and we pine\l"
    .string "away in them, how should we then\l"
    .string "live?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_11::
    .string "Say unto them, As I live, saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the\l"
    .string "death of the wicked; but that the\l"
    .string "wicked turn from his way and live:\l"
    .string "turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways;\l"
    .string "for why will ye die, O house of\l"
    .string "Israel?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_12::
    .string "Therefore, thou son of man, say unto\n"
    .string "the children of thy people, The\l"
    .string "righteousness of the righteous\l"
    .string "shall not deliver him in the day of\l"
    .string "his transgression: as for the\l"
    .string "wickedness of the wicked, he shall\l"
    .string "not fall thereby in the day that he\l"
    .string "turneth from his wickedness; neither\l"
    .string "shall the righteous be able to\l"
    .string "live for his righteousness in the day\l"
    .string "that he sinneth$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_13::
    .string "When I shall say to the righteous,\n"
    .string "that he shall surely live; if he\l"
    .string "trust to his own righteousness, and\l"
    .string "commit iniquity, all his\l"
    .string "righteousnesses shall not be\l"
    .string "remembered; but for his iniquity that\l"
    .string "he hath committed, he shall die for\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_14::
    .string "Again, when I say unto the wicked,\n"
    .string "Thou shalt surely die; if he turn\l"
    .string "from his sin, and do that which is\l"
    .string "lawful and right;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_15::
    .string "If the wicked restore the pledge,\n"
    .string "give again that he had robbed, walk\l"
    .string "in the statutes of life, without\l"
    .string "committing iniquity; he shall\l"
    .string "surely live, he shall not die$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_16::
    .string "None of his sins that he hath\n"
    .string "committed shall be mentioned unto\l"
    .string "him: he hath done that which is\l"
    .string "lawful and right; he shall surely\l"
    .string "live.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_17::
    .string "Yet the children of thy people\n"
    .string "say, The way of the Lord is not\l"
    .string "equal: but as for them, their way is\l"
    .string "not equal.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_18::
    .string "When the righteous turneth from his\n"
    .string "righteousness, and committeth\l"
    .string "iniquity, he shall even die thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_19::
    .string "But if the wicked turn from his\n"
    .string "wickedness, and do that which is\l"
    .string "lawful and right, he shall live\l"
    .string "thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_20::
    .string "Yet ye say, The way of the Lord is\n"
    .string "not equal. O ye house of Israel, I\l"
    .string "will judge you every one after his\l"
    .string "ways.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_21::
    .string "And it came to pass in the twelfth\n"
    .string "year of our captivity, in the tenth\l"
    .string "month, in the fifth day of the month,\l"
    .string "that one that had escaped out of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem came unto me, saying, The\l"
    .string "city is smitten.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_22::
    .string "Now the hand of the LORD was upon me\n"
    .string "in the evening, afore he that was\l"
    .string "escaped came; and had opened my\l"
    .string "mouth, until he came to me in the\l"
    .string "morning; and my mouth was opened,\l"
    .string "and I was no more dumb.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_23::
    .string "Then the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_24::
    .string "Son of man, they that inhabit those\n"
    .string "wastes of the land of Israel speak,\l"
    .string "saying, Abraham was one, and he\l"
    .string "inherited the land: but we are many;\l"
    .string "the land is given us for inheritance$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_25::
    .string "Wherefore say unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD; Ye eat with the blood,\l"
    .string "and lift up your eyes toward your\l"
    .string "idols, and shed blood: and shall\l"
    .string "ye possess the land?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_26::
    .string "Ye stand upon your sword, ye work\n"
    .string "abomination, and ye defile every one\l"
    .string "his neighbour’s wife: and shall ye\l"
    .string "possess the land?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_27::
    .string "Say thou thus unto them, Thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD; As I live, surely they\l"
    .string "that are in the wastes shall fall\l"
    .string "by the sword, and him that is in the\l"
    .string "open field will I give to the\l"
    .string "beasts to be devoured, and they that\l"
    .string "be in the forts and in the caves\l"
    .string "shall die of the pestilence$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_28::
    .string "For I will lay the land most\n"
    .string "desolate, and the pomp of her\l"
    .string "strength shall cease; and the\l"
    .string "mountains of Israel shall be\l"
    .string "desolate, that none shall pass\l"
    .string "through.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_29::
    .string "Then shall they know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when I have laid the land most\l"
    .string "desolate because of all their\l"
    .string "abominations which they have\l"
    .string "committed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_30::
    .string "Also, thou son of man, the children\n"
    .string "of thy people still are talking\l"
    .string "against thee by the walls and in the\l"
    .string "doors of the houses, and speak one to\l"
    .string "another, every one to his brother,\l"
    .string "saying, Come, I pray you, and hear\l"
    .string "what is the word that cometh forth\l"
    .string "from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_31::
    .string "And they come unto thee as the\n"
    .string "people cometh, and they sit before\l"
    .string "thee as my people, and they hear\l"
    .string "thy words, but they will not do\l"
    .string "them: for with their mouth they shew\l"
    .string "much love, but their heart goeth\l"
    .string "after their covetousness.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_32::
    .string "And, lo, thou art unto them as a\n"
    .string "very lovely song of one that hath a\l"
    .string "pleasant voice, and can play well\l"
    .string "on an instrument: for they hear thy\l"
    .string "words, but they do them not.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_33_33::
    .string "And when this cometh to pass, (lo,\n"
    .string "it will come,) then shall they\l"
    .string "know that a prophet hath been among\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_2::
    .string "Son of man, prophesy against the\n"
    .string "shepherds of Israel, prophesy, and\l"
    .string "say unto them, Thus saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD unto the shepherds; Woe be to the\l"
    .string "shepherds of Israel that do feed\l"
    .string "themselves! should not the\l"
    .string "shepherds feed the flocks?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_3::
    .string "Ye eat the fat, and ye clothe you\n"
    .string "with the wool, ye kill them that\l"
    .string "are fed: but ye feed not the flock$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_4::
    .string "The diseased have ye not\n"
    .string "strengthened, neither have ye healed\l"
    .string "that which was sick, neither have ye\l"
    .string "bound up that which was broken,\l"
    .string "neither have ye brought again that\l"
    .string "which was driven away, neither have\l"
    .string "ye sought that which was lost; but\l"
    .string "with force and with cruelty have ye\l"
    .string "ruled them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_5::
    .string "And they were scattered, because\n"
    .string "there is no shepherd: and they\l"
    .string "became meat to all the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field, when they were scattered.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_6::
    .string "My sheep wandered through all the\n"
    .string "mountains, and upon every high\l"
    .string "hill: yea, my flock was scattered\l"
    .string "upon all the face of the earth, and\l"
    .string "none did search or seek after them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_7::
    .string "Therefore, ye shepherds, hear the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_8::
    .string "As I live, saith the Lord GOD,\n"
    .string "surely because my flock became a\l"
    .string "prey, and my flock became meat to\l"
    .string "every beast of the field, because\l"
    .string "there was no shepherd, neither did\l"
    .string "my shepherds search for my flock,\l"
    .string "but the shepherds fed themselves,\l"
    .string "and fed not my flock;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_9::
    .string "Therefore, O ye shepherds, hear the\n"
    .string "word of the LORD;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_10::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I\n"
    .string "am against the shepherds; and I\l"
    .string "will require my flock at their\l"
    .string "hand, and cause them to cease from\l"
    .string "feeding the flock; neither shall\l"
    .string "the shepherds feed themselves any\l"
    .string "more; for I will deliver my flock\l"
    .string "from their mouth, that they may not\l"
    .string "be meat for them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_11::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I, even I, will both search\l"
    .string "my sheep, and seek them out.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_12::
    .string "As a shepherd seeketh out his\n"
    .string "flock in the day that he is among his\l"
    .string "sheep that are scattered; so will I\l"
    .string "seek out my sheep, and will\l"
    .string "deliver them out of all places\l"
    .string "where they have been scattered in the\l"
    .string "cloudy and dark day.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_13::
    .string "And I will bring them out from the\n"
    .string "people, and gather them from the\l"
    .string "countries, and will bring them to\l"
    .string "their own land, and feed them upon\l"
    .string "the mountains of Israel by the\l"
    .string "rivers, and in all the inhabited\l"
    .string "places of the country.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_14::
    .string "I will feed them in a good\n"
    .string "pasture, and upon the high mountains\l"
    .string "of Israel shall their fold be:\l"
    .string "there shall they lie in a good\l"
    .string "fold, and in a fat pasture shall\l"
    .string "they feed upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_15::
    .string "I will feed my flock, and I will\n"
    .string "cause them to lie down, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_16::
    .string "I will seek that which was lost,\n"
    .string "and bring again that which was driven\l"
    .string "away, and will bind up that which\l"
    .string "was broken, and will strengthen\l"
    .string "that which was sick: but I will\l"
    .string "destroy the fat and the strong; I\l"
    .string "will feed them with judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_17::
    .string "And as for you, O my flock, thus\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I judge\l"
    .string "between cattle and cattle, between\l"
    .string "the rams and the he goats.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_18::
    .string "Seemeth it a small thing unto you\n"
    .string "to have eaten up the good pasture,\l"
    .string "but ye must tread down with your feet\l"
    .string "the residue of your pastures? and to\l"
    .string "have drunk of the deep waters, but ye\l"
    .string "must foul the residue with your\l"
    .string "feet?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_19::
    .string "And as for my flock, they eat that\n"
    .string "which ye have trodden with your feet;\l"
    .string "and they drink that which ye have\l"
    .string "fouled with your feet$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_20::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD\n"
    .string "unto them; Behold, I, even I, will\l"
    .string "judge between the fat cattle and\l"
    .string "between the lean cattle.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_21::
    .string "Because ye have thrust with side and\n"
    .string "with shoulder, and pushed all the\l"
    .string "diseased with your horns, till ye\l"
    .string "have scattered them abroad;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_22::
    .string "Therefore will I save my flock,\n"
    .string "and they shall no more be a prey;\l"
    .string "and I will judge between cattle and\l"
    .string "cattle$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_23::
    .string "And I will set up one shepherd\n"
    .string "over them, and he shall feed them,\l"
    .string "even my servant David; he shall feed\l"
    .string "them, and he shall be their\l"
    .string "shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_24::
    .string "And I the LORD will be their God,\n"
    .string "and my servant David a prince among\l"
    .string "them; I the LORD have spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_25::
    .string "And I will make with them a\n"
    .string "covenant of peace, and will cause\l"
    .string "the evil beasts to cease out of the\l"
    .string "land: and they shall dwell safely\l"
    .string "in the wilderness, and sleep in the\l"
    .string "woods.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_26::
    .string "And I will make them and the\n"
    .string "places round about my hill a\l"
    .string "blessing; and I will cause the\l"
    .string "shower to come down in his season;\l"
    .string "there shall be showers of blessing.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_27::
    .string "And the tree of the field shall\n"
    .string "yield her fruit, and the earth\l"
    .string "shall yield her increase, and they\l"
    .string "shall be safe in their land, and\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD, when\l"
    .string "I have broken the bands of their\l"
    .string "yoke, and delivered them out of the\l"
    .string "hand of those that served themselves\l"
    .string "of them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_28::
    .string "And they shall no more be a prey\n"
    .string "to the heathen, neither shall the\l"
    .string "beast of the land devour them; but\l"
    .string "they shall dwell safely, and none\l"
    .string "shall make them afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_29::
    .string "And I will raise up for them a\n"
    .string "plant of renown, and they shall be\l"
    .string "no more consumed with hunger in the\l"
    .string "land, neither bear the shame of the\l"
    .string "heathen any more.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_30::
    .string "Thus shall they know that I the\n"
    .string "LORD their God am with them, and that\l"
    .string "they, even the house of Israel, are\l"
    .string "my people, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_34_31::
    .string "And ye my flock, the flock of my\n"
    .string "pasture, are men, and I am your God,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_1::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face against\n"
    .string "mount Seir, and prophesy against\l"
    .string "it,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_3::
    .string "And say unto it, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD; Behold, O mount Seir, I am\l"
    .string "against thee, and I will stretch out\l"
    .string "mine hand against thee, and I will\l"
    .string "make thee most desolate$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_4::
    .string "I will lay thy cities waste, and\n"
    .string "thou shalt be desolate, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_5::
    .string "Because thou hast had a perpetual\n"
    .string "hatred, and hast shed the blood of\l"
    .string "the children of Israel by the force\l"
    .string "of the sword in the time of their\l"
    .string "calamity, in the time that their\l"
    .string "iniquity had an end:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_6::
    .string "Therefore, as I live, saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD, I will prepare thee unto\l"
    .string "blood, and blood shall pursue\l"
    .string "thee: sith thou hast not hated\l"
    .string "blood, even blood shall pursue\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_7::
    .string "Thus will I make mount Seir most\n"
    .string "desolate, and cut off from it him\l"
    .string "that passeth out and him that\l"
    .string "returneth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_8::
    .string "And I will fill his mountains\n"
    .string "with his slain men: in thy hills,\l"
    .string "and in thy valleys, and in all thy\l"
    .string "rivers, shall they fall that are\l"
    .string "slain with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_9::
    .string "I will make thee perpetual\n"
    .string "desolations, and thy cities shall\l"
    .string "not return: and ye shall know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_10::
    .string "Because thou hast said, These two\n"
    .string "nations and these two countries\l"
    .string "shall be mine, and we will possess\l"
    .string "it; whereas the LORD was there:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_11::
    .string "Therefore, as I live, saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD, I will even do according\l"
    .string "to thine anger, and according to\l"
    .string "thine envy which thou hast used out\l"
    .string "of thy hatred against them; and I\l"
    .string "will make myself known among them,\l"
    .string "when I have judged thee$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_12::
    .string "And thou shalt know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, and that I have heard all thy\l"
    .string "blasphemies which thou hast spoken\l"
    .string "against the mountains of Israel,\l"
    .string "saying, They are laid desolate,\l"
    .string "they are given us to consume.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_13::
    .string "Thus with your mouth ye have boasted\n"
    .string "against me, and have multiplied\l"
    .string "your words against me: I have heard\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_14::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; When the\n"
    .string "whole earth rejoiceth, I will make\l"
    .string "thee desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_35_15::
    .string "As thou didst rejoice at the\n"
    .string "inheritance of the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "because it was desolate, so will I\l"
    .string "do unto thee: thou shalt be\l"
    .string "desolate, O mount Seir, and all\l"
    .string "Idumea, even all of it: and they\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_1::
    .string "Also, thou son of man, prophesy\n"
    .string "unto the mountains of Israel, and\l"
    .string "say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_2::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the\n"
    .string "enemy hath said against you, Aha,\l"
    .string "even the ancient high places are\l"
    .string "ours in possession:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_3::
    .string "Therefore prophesy and say, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Because they have\l"
    .string "made you desolate, and swallowed\l"
    .string "you up on every side, that ye might\l"
    .string "be a possession unto the residue of\l"
    .string "the heathen, and ye are taken up in\l"
    .string "the lips of talkers, and are an\l"
    .string "infamy of the people:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_4::
    .string "Therefore, ye mountains of Israel,\n"
    .string "hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD to the mountains,\l"
    .string "and to the hills, to the rivers, and\l"
    .string "to the valleys, to the desolate\l"
    .string "wastes, and to the cities that are\l"
    .string "forsaken, which became a prey and\l"
    .string "derision to the residue of the\l"
    .string "heathen that are round about;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_5::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Surely in the fire of my jealousy\l"
    .string "have I spoken against the residue of\l"
    .string "the heathen, and against all\l"
    .string "Idumea, which have appointed my\l"
    .string "land into their possession with the\l"
    .string "joy of all their heart, with\l"
    .string "despiteful minds, to cast it out for\l"
    .string "a prey$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_6::
    .string "Prophesy therefore concerning the\n"
    .string "land of Israel, and say unto the\l"
    .string "mountains, and to the hills, to the\l"
    .string "rivers, and to the valleys, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I have\l"
    .string "spoken in my jealousy and in my\l"
    .string "fury, because ye have borne the shame\l"
    .string "of the heathen:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_7::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I\n"
    .string "have lifted up mine hand, Surely\l"
    .string "the heathen that are about you, they\l"
    .string "shall bear their shame$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_8::
    .string "But ye, O mountains of Israel, ye\n"
    .string "shall shoot forth your branches,\l"
    .string "and yield your fruit to my people\l"
    .string "of Israel; for they are at hand to\l"
    .string "come.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_9::
    .string "For, behold, I am for you, and I\n"
    .string "will turn unto you, and ye shall be\l"
    .string "tilled and sown:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_10::
    .string "And I will multiply men upon\n"
    .string "you, all the house of Israel, even\l"
    .string "all of it: and the cities shall be\l"
    .string "inhabited, and the wastes shall be\l"
    .string "builded:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_11::
    .string "And I will multiply upon you man\n"
    .string "and beast; and they shall increase\l"
    .string "and bring fruit: and I will settle\l"
    .string "you after your old estates, and\l"
    .string "will do better unto you than at your\l"
    .string "beginnings: and ye shall know that I\l"
    .string "am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_12::
    .string "Yea, I will cause men to walk upon\n"
    .string "you, even my people Israel; and\l"
    .string "they shall possess thee, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt be their inheritance, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt no more henceforth bereave\l"
    .string "them of men.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_13::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because\n"
    .string "they say unto you, Thou land\l"
    .string "devourest up men, and hast bereaved\l"
    .string "thy nations:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_14::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt devour men no\n"
    .string "more, neither bereave thy nations any\l"
    .string "more, saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_15::
    .string "Neither will I cause men to hear in\n"
    .string "thee the shame of the heathen any\l"
    .string "more, neither shalt thou bear the\l"
    .string "reproach of the people any more,\l"
    .string "neither shalt thou cause thy nations\l"
    .string "to fall any more, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_16::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_17::
    .string "Son of man, when the house of Israel\n"
    .string "dwelt in their own land, they\l"
    .string "defiled it by their own way and by\l"
    .string "their doings: their way was before me\l"
    .string "as the uncleanness of a removed woman$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_18::
    .string "Wherefore I poured my fury upon\n"
    .string "them for the blood that they had\l"
    .string "shed upon the land, and for their\l"
    .string "idols wherewith they had polluted\l"
    .string "it:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_19::
    .string "And I scattered them among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and they were dispersed\l"
    .string "through the countries: according to\l"
    .string "their way and according to their\l"
    .string "doings I judged them$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_20::
    .string "And when they entered unto the\n"
    .string "heathen, whither they went, they\l"
    .string "profaned my holy name, when they\l"
    .string "said to them, These are the people\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and are gone forth out of\l"
    .string "his land.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_21::
    .string "But I had pity for mine holy name,\n"
    .string "which the house of Israel had\l"
    .string "profaned among the heathen, whither\l"
    .string "they went.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_22::
    .string "Therefore say unto the house of\n"
    .string "Israel, thus saith the Lord GOD; I do\l"
    .string "not this for your sakes, O house of\l"
    .string "Israel, but for mine holy name’s\l"
    .string "sake, which ye have profaned among\l"
    .string "the heathen, whither ye went.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_23::
    .string "And I will sanctify my great name,\n"
    .string "which was profaned among the\l"
    .string "heathen, which ye have profaned in\l"
    .string "the midst of them; and the heathen\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD, when I shall be\l"
    .string "sanctified in you before their eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_24::
    .string "For I will take you from among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and gather you out of all\l"
    .string "countries, and will bring you into\l"
    .string "your own land.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_25::
    .string "Then will I sprinkle clean water\n"
    .string "upon you, and ye shall be clean:\l"
    .string "from all your filthiness, and from\l"
    .string "all your idols, will I cleanse\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_26::
    .string "A new heart also will I give you,\n"
    .string "and a new spirit will I put within\l"
    .string "you: and I will take away the stony\l"
    .string "heart out of your flesh, and I will\l"
    .string "give you an heart of flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_27::
    .string "And I will put my spirit within\n"
    .string "you, and cause you to walk in my\l"
    .string "statutes, and ye shall keep my\l"
    .string "judgments, and do them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_28::
    .string "And ye shall dwell in the land\n"
    .string "that I gave to your fathers; and ye\l"
    .string "shall be my people, and I will be\l"
    .string "your God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_29::
    .string "I will also save you from all\n"
    .string "your uncleannesses: and I will\l"
    .string "call for the corn, and will\l"
    .string "increase it, and lay no famine upon\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_30::
    .string "And I will multiply the fruit of\n"
    .string "the tree, and the increase of the\l"
    .string "field, that ye shall receive no\l"
    .string "more reproach of famine among the\l"
    .string "heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_31::
    .string "Then shall ye remember your own\n"
    .string "evil ways, and your doings that were\l"
    .string "not good, and shall lothe\l"
    .string "yourselves in your own sight for\l"
    .string "your iniquities and for your\l"
    .string "abominations.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_32::
    .string "Not for your sakes do I this, saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD, be it known unto you: be\l"
    .string "ashamed and confounded for your own\l"
    .string "ways, O house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_33::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day\n"
    .string "that I shall have cleansed you from\l"
    .string "all your iniquities I will also\l"
    .string "cause you to dwell in the cities,\l"
    .string "and the wastes shall be builded.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_34::
    .string "And the desolate land shall be\n"
    .string "tilled, whereas it lay desolate in\l"
    .string "the sight of all that passed by.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_35::
    .string "And they shall say, This land that\n"
    .string "was desolate is become like the\l"
    .string "garden of Eden; and the waste and\l"
    .string "desolate and ruined cities are\l"
    .string "become fenced, and are inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_36::
    .string "Then the heathen that are left\n"
    .string "round about you shall know that I\l"
    .string "the LORD build the ruined places,\l"
    .string "and plant that that was desolate: I\l"
    .string "the LORD have spoken it, and I will\l"
    .string "do it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_37::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will yet\n"
    .string "for this be enquired of by the house\l"
    .string "of Israel, to do it for them; I will\l"
    .string "increase them with men like a flock.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_36_38::
    .string "As the holy flock, as the flock of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem in her solemn feasts; so\l"
    .string "shall the waste cities be filled\l"
    .string "with flocks of men: and they shall\l"
    .string "know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_1::
    .string "The hand of the LORD was upon me,\n"
    .string "and carried me out in the spirit of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and set me down in the midst\l"
    .string "of the valley which was full of\l"
    .string "bones,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_2::
    .string "And caused me to pass by them round\n"
    .string "about: and, behold, there were very\l"
    .string "many in the open valley; and, lo,\l"
    .string "they were very dry$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_3::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, can\n"
    .string "these bones live? And I answered, O\l"
    .string "Lord GOD, thou knowest.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_4::
    .string "Again he said unto me, Prophesy\n"
    .string "upon these bones, and say unto them,\l"
    .string "O ye dry bones, hear the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_5::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD unto these\n"
    .string "bones; Behold, I will cause breath\l"
    .string "to enter into you, and ye shall\l"
    .string "live:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_6::
    .string "And I will lay sinews upon you,\n"
    .string "and will bring up flesh upon you,\l"
    .string "and cover you with skin, and put\l"
    .string "breath in you, and ye shall live;\l"
    .string "and ye shall know that I am the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_7::
    .string "So I prophesied as I was commanded:\n"
    .string "and as I prophesied, there was a\l"
    .string "noise, and behold a shaking, and the\l"
    .string "bones came together, bone to his bone.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_8::
    .string "And when I beheld, lo, the sinews\n"
    .string "and the flesh came up upon them,\l"
    .string "and the skin covered them above: but\l"
    .string "there was no breath in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_9::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Prophesy unto\n"
    .string "the wind, prophesy, son of man, and\l"
    .string "say to the wind, Thus saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD; Come from the four winds, O\l"
    .string "breath, and breathe upon these\l"
    .string "slain, that they may live.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_10::
    .string "So I prophesied as he commanded me,\n"
    .string "and the breath came into them, and\l"
    .string "they lived, and stood up upon their\l"
    .string "feet, an exceeding great army.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_11::
    .string "Then he said unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "these bones are the whole house of\l"
    .string "Israel: behold, they say, Our bones\l"
    .string "are dried, and our hope is lost: we\l"
    .string "are cut off for our parts.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_12::
    .string "Therefore prophesy and say unto\n"
    .string "them, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\l"
    .string "Behold, O my people, I will open\l"
    .string "your graves, and cause you to come up\l"
    .string "out of your graves, and bring you\l"
    .string "into the land of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_13::
    .string "And ye shall know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD, when I have opened your\l"
    .string "graves, O my people, and brought\l"
    .string "you up out of your graves,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_14::
    .string "And shall put my spirit in you,\n"
    .string "and ye shall live, and I shall\l"
    .string "place you in your own land: then\l"
    .string "shall ye know that I the LORD have\l"
    .string "spoken it, and performed it, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_15::
    .string "The word of the LORD came again unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_16::
    .string "Moreover, thou son of man, take thee\n"
    .string "one stick, and write upon it, For\l"
    .string "Judah, and for the children of\l"
    .string "Israel his companions: then take\l"
    .string "another stick, and write upon it,\l"
    .string "For Joseph, the stick of Ephraim and\l"
    .string "for all the house of Israel his\l"
    .string "companions:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_17::
    .string "And join them one to another into\n"
    .string "one stick; and they shall become one\l"
    .string "in thine hand$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_18::
    .string "And when the children of thy\n"
    .string "people shall speak unto thee,\l"
    .string "saying, Wilt thou not shew us what\l"
    .string "thou meanest by these?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_19::
    .string "Say unto them, Thus saith the Lord\n"
    .string "GOD; Behold, I will take the stick\l"
    .string "of Joseph, which is in the hand of\l"
    .string "Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel\l"
    .string "his fellows, and will put them\l"
    .string "with him, even with the stick of\l"
    .string "Judah, and make them one stick, and\l"
    .string "they shall be one in mine hand$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_20::
    .string "And the sticks whereon thou writest\n"
    .string "shall be in thine hand before their\l"
    .string "eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_21::
    .string "And say unto them, Thus saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD; Behold, I will take the\l"
    .string "children of Israel from among the\l"
    .string "heathen, whither they be gone, and\l"
    .string "will gather them on every side, and\l"
    .string "bring them into their own land:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_22::
    .string "And I will make them one nation in\n"
    .string "the land upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Israel; and one king shall be king\l"
    .string "to them all: and they shall be no\l"
    .string "more two nations, neither shall\l"
    .string "they be divided into two kingdoms any\l"
    .string "more at all$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_23::
    .string "Neither shall they defile\n"
    .string "themselves any more with their\l"
    .string "idols, nor with their detestable\l"
    .string "things, nor with any of their\l"
    .string "transgressions: but I will save\l"
    .string "them out of all their\l"
    .string "dwellingplaces, wherein they have\l"
    .string "sinned, and will cleanse them: so\l"
    .string "shall they be my people, and I\l"
    .string "will be their God.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_24::
    .string "And David my servant shall be king\n"
    .string "over them; and they all shall have\l"
    .string "one shepherd: they shall also\l"
    .string "walk in my judgments, and observe my\l"
    .string "statutes, and do them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_25::
    .string "And they shall dwell in the land\n"
    .string "that I have given unto Jacob my\l"
    .string "servant, wherein your fathers have\l"
    .string "dwelt; and they shall dwell\l"
    .string "therein, even they, and their\l"
    .string "children, and their children’s\l"
    .string "children for ever: and my servant\l"
    .string "David shall be their prince for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_26::
    .string "Moreover I will make a covenant of\n"
    .string "peace with them; it shall be an\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant with them: and\l"
    .string "I will place them, and multiply\l"
    .string "them, and will set my sanctuary in\l"
    .string "the midst of them for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_27::
    .string "My tabernacle also shall be with\n"
    .string "them: yea, I will be their God, and\l"
    .string "they shall be my people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_37_28::
    .string "And the heathen shall know that I\n"
    .string "the LORD do sanctify Israel, when my\l"
    .string "sanctuary shall be in the midst of\l"
    .string "them for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_2::
    .string "Son of man, set thy face against\n"
    .string "Gog, the land of Magog, the chief\l"
    .string "prince of Meshech and Tubal, and\l"
    .string "prophesy against him,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_3::
    .string "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, O Gog, the\l"
    .string "chief prince of Meshech and Tubal:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_4::
    .string "And I will turn thee back, and put\n"
    .string "hooks into thy jaws, and I will\l"
    .string "bring thee forth, and all thine\l"
    .string "army, horses and horsemen, all of\l"
    .string "them clothed with all sorts of\l"
    .string "armour, even a great company with\l"
    .string "bucklers and shields, all of them\l"
    .string "handling swords:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_5::
    .string "Persia, Ethiopia, and Libya with\n"
    .string "them; all of them with shield and\l"
    .string "helmet:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_6::
    .string "Gomer, and all his bands; the house\n"
    .string "of Togarmah of the north quarters,\l"
    .string "and all his bands: and many people\l"
    .string "with thee$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_7::
    .string "Be thou prepared, and prepare for\n"
    .string "thyself, thou, and all thy company\l"
    .string "that are assembled unto thee, and be\l"
    .string "thou a guard unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_8::
    .string "After many days thou shalt be\n"
    .string "visited: in the latter years thou\l"
    .string "shalt come into the land that is\l"
    .string "brought back from the sword, and is\l"
    .string "gathered out of many people,\l"
    .string "against the mountains of Israel,\l"
    .string "which have been always waste: but it\l"
    .string "is brought forth out of the nations,\l"
    .string "and they shall dwell safely all\l"
    .string "of them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_9::
    .string "Thou shalt ascend and come like a\n"
    .string "storm, thou shalt be like a cloud\l"
    .string "to cover the land, thou, and all\l"
    .string "thy bands, and many people with\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_10::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; It shall\n"
    .string "also come to pass, that at the same\l"
    .string "time shall things come into thy\l"
    .string "mind, and thou shalt think an evil\l"
    .string "thought:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_11::
    .string "And thou shalt say, I will go up\n"
    .string "to the land of unwalled villages;\l"
    .string "I will go to them that are at rest,\l"
    .string "that dwell safely, all of them\l"
    .string "dwelling without walls, and having\l"
    .string "neither bars nor gates,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_12::
    .string "To take a spoil, and to take a\n"
    .string "prey; to turn thine hand upon the\l"
    .string "desolate places that are now\l"
    .string "inhabited, and upon the people\l"
    .string "that are gathered out of the nations,\l"
    .string "which have gotten cattle and goods,\l"
    .string "that dwell in the midst of the land$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_13::
    .string "Sheba, and Dedan, and the merchants\n"
    .string "of Tarshish, with all the young\l"
    .string "lions thereof, shall say unto thee,\l"
    .string "Art thou come to take a spoil? hast\l"
    .string "thou gathered thy company to take a\l"
    .string "prey? to carry away silver and gold,\l"
    .string "to take away cattle and goods, to\l"
    .string "take a great spoil?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_14::
    .string "Therefore, son of man, prophesy\n"
    .string "and say unto Gog, Thus saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD; In that day when my people of\l"
    .string "Israel dwelleth safely, shalt\l"
    .string "thou not know it?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_15::
    .string "And thou shalt come from thy place\n"
    .string "out of the north parts, thou, and\l"
    .string "many people with thee, all of them\l"
    .string "riding upon horses, a great\l"
    .string "company, and a mighty army:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_16::
    .string "And thou shalt come up against my\n"
    .string "people of Israel, as a cloud to\l"
    .string "cover the land; it shall be in the\l"
    .string "latter days, and I will bring thee\l"
    .string "against my land, that the heathen\l"
    .string "may know me, when I shall be\l"
    .string "sanctified in thee, O Gog, before\l"
    .string "their eyes$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_17::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Art thou he\n"
    .string "of whom I have spoken in old time by\l"
    .string "my servants the prophets of Israel,\l"
    .string "which prophesied in those days many\l"
    .string "years that I would bring thee\l"
    .string "against them?"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_18::
    .string "And it shall come to pass at the\n"
    .string "same time when Gog shall come\l"
    .string "against the land of Israel, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD, that my fury shall\l"
    .string "come up in my face$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_19::
    .string "For in my jealousy and in the fire\n"
    .string "of my wrath have I spoken, Surely in\l"
    .string "that day there shall be a great\l"
    .string "shaking in the land of Israel;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_20::
    .string "So that the fishes of the sea, and\n"
    .string "the fowls of the heaven, and the\l"
    .string "beasts of the field, and all\l"
    .string "creeping things that creep upon\l"
    .string "the earth, and all the men that are\l"
    .string "upon the face of the earth, shall\l"
    .string "shake at my presence, and the\l"
    .string "mountains shall be thrown down, and\l"
    .string "the steep places shall fall, and\l"
    .string "every wall shall fall to the\l"
    .string "ground$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_21::
    .string "And I will call for a sword\n"
    .string "against him throughout all my\l"
    .string "mountains, saith the Lord GOD: every\l"
    .string "man’s sword shall be against his\l"
    .string "brother.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_22::
    .string "And I will plead against him with\n"
    .string "pestilence and with blood; and I\l"
    .string "will rain upon him, and upon his\l"
    .string "bands, and upon the many people\l"
    .string "that are with him, an overflowing\l"
    .string "rain, and great hailstones, fire,\l"
    .string "and brimstone.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_38_23::
    .string "Thus will I magnify myself, and\n"
    .string "sanctify myself; and I will be\l"
    .string "known in the eyes of many nations,\l"
    .string "and they shall know that I am the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_1::
    .string "Therefore, thou son of man,\n"
    .string "prophesy against Gog, and say, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am\l"
    .string "against thee, O Gog, the chief\l"
    .string "prince of Meshech and Tubal:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_2::
    .string "And I will turn thee back, and\n"
    .string "leave but the sixth part of thee, and\l"
    .string "will cause thee to come up from the\l"
    .string "north parts, and will bring thee\l"
    .string "upon the mountains of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_3::
    .string "And I will smite thy bow out of thy\n"
    .string "left hand, and will cause thine\l"
    .string "arrows to fall out of thy right hand$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_4::
    .string "Thou shalt fall upon the\n"
    .string "mountains of Israel, thou, and all\l"
    .string "thy bands, and the people that is\l"
    .string "with thee: I will give thee unto the\l"
    .string "ravenous birds of every sort, and to\l"
    .string "the beasts of the field to be\l"
    .string "devoured.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_5::
    .string "Thou shalt fall upon the open\n"
    .string "field: for I have spoken it, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_6::
    .string "And I will send a fire on Magog,\n"
    .string "and among them that dwell\l"
    .string "carelessly in the isles: and they\l"
    .string "shall know that I am the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_7::
    .string "So will I make my holy name known\n"
    .string "in the midst of my people Israel;\l"
    .string "and I will not let them pollute\l"
    .string "my holy name any more: and the\l"
    .string "heathen shall know that I am the\l"
    .string "LORD, the Holy One in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_8::
    .string "Behold, it is come, and it is done,\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; this is the day\l"
    .string "whereof I have spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_9::
    .string "And they that dwell in the cities\n"
    .string "of Israel shall go forth, and\l"
    .string "shall set on fire and burn the\l"
    .string "weapons, both the shields and the\l"
    .string "bucklers, the bows and the arrows,\l"
    .string "and the handstaves, and the spears,\l"
    .string "and they shall burn them with fire\l"
    .string "seven years:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_10::
    .string "So that they shall take no wood out\n"
    .string "of the field, neither cut down any\l"
    .string "out of the forests; for they shall\l"
    .string "burn the weapons with fire: and they\l"
    .string "shall spoil those that spoiled\l"
    .string "them, and rob those that robbed them,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_11::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that I will give unto Gog a\l"
    .string "place there of graves in Israel, the\l"
    .string "valley of the passengers on the\l"
    .string "east of the sea: and it shall stop\l"
    .string "the noses of the passengers: and\l"
    .string "there shall they bury Gog and all\l"
    .string "his multitude: and they shall\l"
    .string "call it The valley of Hamongog.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_12::
    .string "And seven months shall the house\n"
    .string "of Israel be burying of them, that\l"
    .string "they may cleanse the land.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_13::
    .string "Yea, all the people of the land\n"
    .string "shall bury them; and it shall be to\l"
    .string "them a renown the day that I shall\l"
    .string "be glorified, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_14::
    .string "And they shall sever out men of\n"
    .string "continual employment, passing\l"
    .string "through the land to bury with the\l"
    .string "passengers those that remain upon\l"
    .string "the face of the earth, to cleanse it:\l"
    .string "after the end of seven months shall\l"
    .string "they search.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_15::
    .string "And the passengers that pass\n"
    .string "through the land, when any seeth a\l"
    .string "man’s bone, then shall he set up a\l"
    .string "sign by it, till the buriers have\l"
    .string "buried it in the valley of Hamongog.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_16::
    .string "And also the name of the city\n"
    .string "shall be Hamonah. Thus shall they\l"
    .string "cleanse the land.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_17::
    .string "And, thou son of man, thus saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD; Speak unto every feathered\l"
    .string "fowl, and to every beast of the\l"
    .string "field, Assemble yourselves, and\l"
    .string "come; gather yourselves on every\l"
    .string "side to my sacrifice that I do\l"
    .string "sacrifice for you, even a great\l"
    .string "sacrifice upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Israel, that ye may eat flesh, and\l"
    .string "drink blood.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_18::
    .string "Ye shall eat the flesh of the\n"
    .string "mighty, and drink the blood of the\l"
    .string "princes of the earth, of rams, of\l"
    .string "lambs, and of goats, of bullocks,\l"
    .string "all of them fatlings of Bashan.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_19::
    .string "And ye shall eat fat till ye be\n"
    .string "full, and drink blood till ye be\l"
    .string "drunken, of my sacrifice which I have\l"
    .string "sacrificed for you.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_20::
    .string "Thus ye shall be filled at my\n"
    .string "table with horses and chariots, with\l"
    .string "mighty men, and with all men of war,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_21::
    .string "And I will set my glory among the\n"
    .string "heathen, and all the heathen shall\l"
    .string "see my judgment that I have executed,\l"
    .string "and my hand that I have laid upon\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_22::
    .string "So the house of Israel shall know\n"
    .string "that I am the LORD their God from\l"
    .string "that day and forward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_23::
    .string "And the heathen shall know that\n"
    .string "the house of Israel went into\l"
    .string "captivity for their iniquity:\l"
    .string "because they trespassed against me,\l"
    .string "therefore hid I my face from them,\l"
    .string "and gave them into the hand of their\l"
    .string "enemies: so fell they all by the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_24::
    .string "According to their uncleanness and\n"
    .string "according to their transgressions\l"
    .string "have I done unto them, and hid my face\l"
    .string "from them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_25::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "Now will I bring again the\l"
    .string "captivity of Jacob, and have mercy\l"
    .string "upon the whole house of Israel, and\l"
    .string "will be jealous for my holy name;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_26::
    .string "After that they have borne their\n"
    .string "shame, and all their trespasses\l"
    .string "whereby they have trespassed\l"
    .string "against me, when they dwelt safely\l"
    .string "in their land, and none made them\l"
    .string "afraid$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_27::
    .string "When I have brought them again from\n"
    .string "the people, and gathered them out\l"
    .string "of their enemies’ lands, and am\l"
    .string "sanctified in them in the sight of\l"
    .string "many nations;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_28::
    .string "Then shall they know that I am the\n"
    .string "LORD their God, which caused them to\l"
    .string "be led into captivity among the\l"
    .string "heathen: but I have gathered them\l"
    .string "unto their own land, and have left\l"
    .string "none of them any more there$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_39_29::
    .string "Neither will I hide my face any\n"
    .string "more from them: for I have poured out\l"
    .string "my spirit upon the house of Israel,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_1::
    .string "In the five and twentieth year of\n"
    .string "our captivity, in the beginning of\l"
    .string "the year, in the tenth day of the\l"
    .string "month, in the fourteenth year after\l"
    .string "that the city was smitten, in the\l"
    .string "selfsame day the hand of the LORD\l"
    .string "was upon me, and brought me thither.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_2::
    .string "In the visions of God brought he me\n"
    .string "into the land of Israel, and set me\l"
    .string "upon a very high mountain, by which\l"
    .string "was as the frame of a city on the\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_3::
    .string "And he brought me thither, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there was a man, whose\l"
    .string "appearance was like the\l"
    .string "appearance of brass, with a line of\l"
    .string "flax in his hand, and a measuring\l"
    .string "reed; and he stood in the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_4::
    .string "And the man said unto me, Son of man,\n"
    .string "behold with thine eyes, and hear\l"
    .string "with thine ears, and set thine heart\l"
    .string "upon all that I shall shew thee;\l"
    .string "for to the intent that I might shew\l"
    .string "them unto thee art thou brought\l"
    .string "hither: declare all that thou seest\l"
    .string "to the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_5::
    .string "And behold a wall on the outside\n"
    .string "of the house round about, and in the\l"
    .string "man’s hand a measuring reed of six\l"
    .string "cubits long by the cubit and an hand\l"
    .string "breadth: so he measured the breadth\l"
    .string "of the building, one reed; and the\l"
    .string "height, one reed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_6::
    .string "Then came he unto the gate which\n"
    .string "looketh toward the east, and went up\l"
    .string "the stairs thereof, and measured the\l"
    .string "threshold of the gate, which was one\l"
    .string "reed broad; and the other threshold\l"
    .string "of the gate, which was one reed broad.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_7::
    .string "And every little chamber was one\n"
    .string "reed long, and one reed broad; and\l"
    .string "between the little chambers were\l"
    .string "five cubits; and the threshold of\l"
    .string "the gate by the porch of the gate\l"
    .string "within was one reed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_8::
    .string "He measured also the porch of the\n"
    .string "gate within, one reed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_9::
    .string "Then measured he the porch of the\n"
    .string "gate, eight cubits; and the posts\l"
    .string "thereof, two cubits; and the porch\l"
    .string "of the gate was inward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_10::
    .string "And the little chambers of the\n"
    .string "gate eastward were three on this\l"
    .string "side, and three on that side; they\l"
    .string "three were of one measure: and the\l"
    .string "posts had one measure on this side\l"
    .string "and on that side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_11::
    .string "And he measured the breadth of the\n"
    .string "entry of the gate, ten cubits; and\l"
    .string "the length of the gate, thirteen\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_12::
    .string "The space also before the little\n"
    .string "chambers was one cubit on this side,\l"
    .string "and the space was one cubit on that\l"
    .string "side: and the little chambers were\l"
    .string "six cubits on this side, and six\l"
    .string "cubits on that side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_13::
    .string "He measured then the gate from the\n"
    .string "roof of one little chamber to the\l"
    .string "roof of another: the breadth was five\l"
    .string "and twenty cubits, door against door.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_14::
    .string "He made also posts of threescore\n"
    .string "cubits, even unto the post of the\l"
    .string "court round about the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_15::
    .string "And from the face of the gate of the\n"
    .string "entrance unto the face of the porch\l"
    .string "of the inner gate were fifty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_16::
    .string "And there were narrow windows to the\n"
    .string "little chambers, and to their posts\l"
    .string "within the gate round about, and\l"
    .string "likewise to the arches: and windows\l"
    .string "were round about inward: and upon\l"
    .string "each post were palm trees.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_17::
    .string "Then brought he me into the outward\n"
    .string "court, and, lo, there were chambers,\l"
    .string "and a pavement made for the court\l"
    .string "round about: thirty chambers were\l"
    .string "upon the pavement.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_18::
    .string "And the pavement by the side of the\n"
    .string "gates over against the length of the\l"
    .string "gates was the lower pavement.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_19::
    .string "Then he measured the breadth from\n"
    .string "the forefront of the lower gate unto\l"
    .string "the forefront of the inner court\l"
    .string "without, an hundred cubits eastward\l"
    .string "and northward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_20::
    .string "And the gate of the outward court\n"
    .string "that looked toward the north, he\l"
    .string "measured the length thereof, and the\l"
    .string "breadth thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_21::
    .string "And the little chambers thereof\n"
    .string "were three on this side and three on\l"
    .string "that side; and the posts thereof and\l"
    .string "the arches thereof were after the\l"
    .string "measure of the first gate: the\l"
    .string "length thereof was fifty cubits, and\l"
    .string "the breadth five and twenty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_22::
    .string "And their windows, and their arches,\n"
    .string "and their palm trees, were after the\l"
    .string "measure of the gate that looketh\l"
    .string "toward the east; and they went up\l"
    .string "unto it by seven steps; and the\l"
    .string "arches thereof were before them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_23::
    .string "And the gate of the inner court was\n"
    .string "over against the gate toward the\l"
    .string "north, and toward the east; and he\l"
    .string "measured from gate to gate an hundred\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_24::
    .string "After that he brought me toward the\n"
    .string "south, and behold a gate toward the\l"
    .string "south: and he measured the posts\l"
    .string "thereof and the arches thereof\l"
    .string "according to these measures.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_25::
    .string "And there were windows in it and in\n"
    .string "the arches thereof round about, like\l"
    .string "those windows: the length was fifty\l"
    .string "cubits, and the breadth five and\l"
    .string "twenty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_26::
    .string "And there were seven steps to go up\n"
    .string "to it, and the arches thereof were\l"
    .string "before them: and it had palm trees,\l"
    .string "one on this side, and another on that\l"
    .string "side, upon the posts thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_27::
    .string "And there was a gate in the inner\n"
    .string "court toward the south: and he\l"
    .string "measured from gate to gate toward the\l"
    .string "south an hundred cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_28::
    .string "And he brought me to the inner court\n"
    .string "by the south gate: and he measured\l"
    .string "the south gate according to these\l"
    .string "measures;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_29::
    .string "And the little chambers thereof,\n"
    .string "and the posts thereof, and the\l"
    .string "arches thereof, according to these\l"
    .string "measures: and there were windows in\l"
    .string "it and in the arches thereof round\l"
    .string "about: it was fifty cubits long, and\l"
    .string "five and twenty cubits broad$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_30::
    .string "And the arches round about were five\n"
    .string "and twenty cubits long, and five\l"
    .string "cubits broad.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_31::
    .string "And the arches thereof were toward\n"
    .string "the utter court; and palm trees were\l"
    .string "upon the posts thereof: and the\l"
    .string "going up to it had eight steps.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_32::
    .string "And he brought me into the inner\n"
    .string "court toward the east: and he\l"
    .string "measured the gate according to these\l"
    .string "measures.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_33::
    .string "And the little chambers thereof,\n"
    .string "and the posts thereof, and the\l"
    .string "arches thereof, were according to\l"
    .string "these measures: and there were\l"
    .string "windows therein and in the arches\l"
    .string "thereof round about: it was fifty\l"
    .string "cubits long, and five and twenty\l"
    .string "cubits broad.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_34::
    .string "And the arches thereof were toward\n"
    .string "the outward court; and palm trees\l"
    .string "were upon the posts thereof, on this\l"
    .string "side, and on that side: and the going\l"
    .string "up to it had eight steps.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_35::
    .string "And he brought me to the north gate,\n"
    .string "and measured it according to these\l"
    .string "measures;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_36::
    .string "The little chambers thereof, the\n"
    .string "posts thereof, and the arches\l"
    .string "thereof, and the windows to it round\l"
    .string "about: the length was fifty cubits,\l"
    .string "and the breadth five and twenty\l"
    .string "cubits$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_37::
    .string "And the posts thereof were toward\n"
    .string "the utter court; and palm trees were\l"
    .string "upon the posts thereof, on this\l"
    .string "side, and on that side: and the going\l"
    .string "up to it had eight steps.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_38::
    .string "And the chambers and the entries\n"
    .string "thereof were by the posts of the\l"
    .string "gates, where they washed the burnt\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_39::
    .string "And in the porch of the gate were\n"
    .string "two tables on this side, and two\l"
    .string "tables on that side, to slay thereon\l"
    .string "the burnt offering and the sin\l"
    .string "offering and the trespass offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_40::
    .string "And at the side without, as one\n"
    .string "goeth up to the entry of the north\l"
    .string "gate, were two tables; and on the\l"
    .string "other side, which was at the porch of\l"
    .string "the gate, were two tables.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_41::
    .string "Four tables were on this side, and\n"
    .string "four tables on that side, by the side\l"
    .string "of the gate; eight tables,\l"
    .string "whereupon they slew their\l"
    .string "sacrifices.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_42::
    .string "And the four tables were of hewn\n"
    .string "stone for the burnt offering, of a\l"
    .string "cubit and an half long, and a cubit\l"
    .string "and an half broad, and one cubit\l"
    .string "high: whereupon also they laid the\l"
    .string "instruments wherewith they slew the\l"
    .string "burnt offering and the sacrifice.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_43::
    .string "And within were hooks, an hand\n"
    .string "broad, fastened round about: and\l"
    .string "upon the tables was the flesh of\l"
    .string "the offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_44::
    .string "And without the inner gate were the\n"
    .string "chambers of the singers in the inner\l"
    .string "court, which was at the side of the\l"
    .string "north gate; and their prospect was\l"
    .string "toward the south: one at the side of\l"
    .string "the east gate having the prospect\l"
    .string "toward the north.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_45::
    .string "And he said unto me, This chamber,\n"
    .string "whose prospect is toward the south,\l"
    .string "is for the priests, the keepers of\l"
    .string "the charge of the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_46::
    .string "And the chamber whose prospect is\n"
    .string "toward the north is for the priests,\l"
    .string "the keepers of the charge of the\l"
    .string "altar: these are the sons of Zadok\l"
    .string "among the sons of Levi, which come\l"
    .string "near to the LORD to minister unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_47::
    .string "So he measured the court, an hundred\n"
    .string "cubits long, and an hundred cubits\l"
    .string "broad, foursquare; and the altar\l"
    .string "that was before the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_48::
    .string "And he brought me to the porch of\n"
    .string "the house, and measured each post of\l"
    .string "the porch, five cubits on this side,\l"
    .string "and five cubits on that side: and the\l"
    .string "breadth of the gate was three cubits\l"
    .string "on this side, and three cubits on\l"
    .string "that side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_40_49::
    .string "The length of the porch was twenty\n"
    .string "cubits, and the breadth eleven\l"
    .string "cubits, and he brought me by the\l"
    .string "steps whereby they went up to it:\l"
    .string "and there were pillars by the\l"
    .string "posts, one on this side, and another\l"
    .string "on that side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_1::
    .string "Afterward he brought me to the\n"
    .string "temple, and measured the posts, six\l"
    .string "cubits broad on the one side, and six\l"
    .string "cubits broad on the other side, which\l"
    .string "was the breadth of the tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_2::
    .string "And the breadth of the door was ten\n"
    .string "cubits; and the sides of the door\l"
    .string "were five cubits on the one side, and\l"
    .string "five cubits on the other side: and he\l"
    .string "measured the length thereof, forty\l"
    .string "cubits: and the breadth, twenty\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_3::
    .string "Then went he inward, and measured\n"
    .string "the post of the door, two cubits; and\l"
    .string "the door, six cubits; and the breadth\l"
    .string "of the door, seven cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_4::
    .string "So he measured the length thereof,\n"
    .string "twenty cubits; and the breadth,\l"
    .string "twenty cubits, before the temple:\l"
    .string "and he said unto me, This is the most\l"
    .string "holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_5::
    .string "After he measured the wall of the\n"
    .string "house, six cubits; and the breadth of\l"
    .string "every side chamber, four cubits,\l"
    .string "round about the house on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_6::
    .string "And the side chambers were three,\n"
    .string "one over another, and thirty in\l"
    .string "order; and they entered into the\l"
    .string "wall which was of the house for the\l"
    .string "side chambers round about, that they\l"
    .string "might have hold, but they had not\l"
    .string "hold in the wall of the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_7::
    .string "And there was an enlarging, and a\n"
    .string "winding about still upward to the\l"
    .string "side chambers: for the winding about\l"
    .string "of the house went still upward\l"
    .string "round about the house: therefore the\l"
    .string "breadth of the house was still\l"
    .string "upward, and so increased from the\l"
    .string "lowest chamber to the highest by the\l"
    .string "midst.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_8::
    .string "I saw also the height of the house\n"
    .string "round about: the foundations of the\l"
    .string "side chambers were a full reed of\l"
    .string "six great cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_9::
    .string "The thickness of the wall, which\n"
    .string "was for the side chamber without, was\l"
    .string "five cubits: and that which was left\l"
    .string "was the place of the side chambers\l"
    .string "that were within.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_10::
    .string "And between the chambers was the\n"
    .string "wideness of twenty cubits round\l"
    .string "about the house on every side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_11::
    .string "And the doors of the side chambers\n"
    .string "were toward the place that was\l"
    .string "left, one door toward the north, and\l"
    .string "another door toward the south: and\l"
    .string "the breadth of the place that was\l"
    .string "left was five cubits round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_12::
    .string "Now the building that was before\n"
    .string "the separate place at the end\l"
    .string "toward the west was seventy cubits\l"
    .string "broad; and the wall of the building\l"
    .string "was five cubits thick round about,\l"
    .string "and the length thereof ninety cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_13::
    .string "So he measured the house, an hundred\n"
    .string "cubits long; and the separate\l"
    .string "place, and the building, with the\l"
    .string "walls thereof, an hundred cubits\l"
    .string "long;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_14::
    .string "Also the breadth of the face of the\n"
    .string "house, and of the separate place\l"
    .string "toward the east, an hundred cubits$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_15::
    .string "And he measured the length of the\n"
    .string "building over against the separate\l"
    .string "place which was behind it, and the\l"
    .string "galleries thereof on the one side\l"
    .string "and on the other side, an hundred\l"
    .string "cubits, with the inner temple, and\l"
    .string "the porches of the court;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_16::
    .string "The door posts, and the narrow\n"
    .string "windows, and the galleries round\l"
    .string "about on their three stories, over\l"
    .string "against the door, cieled with wood\l"
    .string "round about, and from the ground up\l"
    .string "to the windows, and the windows were\l"
    .string "covered;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_17::
    .string "To that above the door, even unto\n"
    .string "the inner house, and without, and by\l"
    .string "all the wall round about within\l"
    .string "and without, by measure$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_18::
    .string "And it was made with cherubims and\n"
    .string "palm trees, so that a palm tree was\l"
    .string "between a cherub and a cherub; and\l"
    .string "every cherub had two faces;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_19::
    .string "So that the face of a man was toward\n"
    .string "the palm tree on the one side, and\l"
    .string "the face of a young lion toward the\l"
    .string "palm tree on the other side: it was\l"
    .string "made through all the house round\l"
    .string "about$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_20::
    .string "From the ground unto above the door\n"
    .string "were cherubims and palm trees made,\l"
    .string "and on the wall of the temple.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_21::
    .string "The posts of the temple were\n"
    .string "squared, and the face of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary; the appearance of the\l"
    .string "one as the appearance of the other.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_22::
    .string "The altar of wood was three cubits\n"
    .string "high, and the length thereof two\l"
    .string "cubits; and the corners thereof, and\l"
    .string "the length thereof, and the walls\l"
    .string "thereof, were of wood: and he said\l"
    .string "unto me, This is the table that is\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_23::
    .string "And the temple and the sanctuary\n"
    .string "had two doors.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_24::
    .string "And the doors had two leaves\n"
    .string "apiece, two turning leaves; two\l"
    .string "leaves for the one door, and two\l"
    .string "leaves for the other door.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_25::
    .string "And there were made on them, on the\n"
    .string "doors of the temple, cherubims and\l"
    .string "palm trees, like as were made upon\l"
    .string "the walls; and there were thick\l"
    .string "planks upon the face of the porch\l"
    .string "without.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_41_26::
    .string "And there were narrow windows and\n"
    .string "palm trees on the one side and on the\l"
    .string "other side, on the sides of the\l"
    .string "porch, and upon the side chambers of\l"
    .string "the house, and thick planks.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_1::
    .string "Then he brought me forth into the\n"
    .string "utter court, the way toward the\l"
    .string "north: and he brought me into the\l"
    .string "chamber that was over against the\l"
    .string "separate place, and which was\l"
    .string "before the building toward the north.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_2::
    .string "Before the length of an hundred\n"
    .string "cubits was the north door, and the\l"
    .string "breadth was fifty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_3::
    .string "Over against the twenty cubits\n"
    .string "which were for the inner court, and\l"
    .string "over against the pavement which was\l"
    .string "for the utter court, was gallery\l"
    .string "against gallery in three stories.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_4::
    .string "And before the chambers was a walk\n"
    .string "to ten cubits breadth inward, a way\l"
    .string "of one cubit; and their doors toward\l"
    .string "the north.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_5::
    .string "Now the upper chambers were\n"
    .string "shorter: for the galleries were\l"
    .string "higher than these, than the lower,\l"
    .string "and than the middlemost of the\l"
    .string "building.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_6::
    .string "For they were in three stories, but\n"
    .string "had not pillars as the pillars of\l"
    .string "the courts: therefore the building\l"
    .string "was straitened more than the lowest\l"
    .string "and the middlemost from the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_7::
    .string "And the wall that was without over\n"
    .string "against the chambers, toward the\l"
    .string "utter court on the forepart of the\l"
    .string "chambers, the length thereof was\l"
    .string "fifty cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_8::
    .string "For the length of the chambers that\n"
    .string "were in the utter court was fifty\l"
    .string "cubits: and, lo, before the temple\l"
    .string "were an hundred cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_9::
    .string "And from under these chambers was\n"
    .string "the entry on the east side, as one\l"
    .string "goeth into them from the utter court.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_10::
    .string "The chambers were in the thickness\n"
    .string "of the wall of the court toward the\l"
    .string "east, over against the separate\l"
    .string "place, and over against the\l"
    .string "building.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_11::
    .string "And the way before them was like\n"
    .string "the appearance of the chambers\l"
    .string "which were toward the north, as long\l"
    .string "as they, and as broad as they: and\l"
    .string "all their goings out were both\l"
    .string "according to their fashions, and\l"
    .string "according to their doors.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_12::
    .string "And according to the doors of the\n"
    .string "chambers that were toward the south\l"
    .string "was a door in the head of the way,\l"
    .string "even the way directly before the\l"
    .string "wall toward the east, as one\l"
    .string "entereth into them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_13::
    .string "Then said he unto me, The north\n"
    .string "chambers and the south chambers,\l"
    .string "which are before the separate\l"
    .string "place, they be holy chambers, where\l"
    .string "the priests that approach unto the\l"
    .string "LORD shall eat the most holy\l"
    .string "things: there shall they lay the\l"
    .string "most holy things, and the meat\l"
    .string "offering, and the sin offering, and\l"
    .string "the trespass offering; for the\l"
    .string "place is holy.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_14::
    .string "When the priests enter therein,\n"
    .string "then shall they not go out of the\l"
    .string "holy place into the utter court,\l"
    .string "but there they shall lay their\l"
    .string "garments wherein they minister; for\l"
    .string "they are holy; and shall put on\l"
    .string "other garments, and shall approach\l"
    .string "to those things which are for the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_15::
    .string "Now when he had made an end of\n"
    .string "measuring the inner house, he brought\l"
    .string "me forth toward the gate whose\l"
    .string "prospect is toward the east, and\l"
    .string "measured it round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_16::
    .string "He measured the east side with the\n"
    .string "measuring reed, five hundred reeds,\l"
    .string "with the measuring reed round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_17::
    .string "He measured the north side, five\n"
    .string "hundred reeds, with the measuring\l"
    .string "reed round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_18::
    .string "He measured the south side, five\n"
    .string "hundred reeds, with the measuring\l"
    .string "reed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_19::
    .string "He turned about to the west side,\n"
    .string "and measured five hundred reeds with\l"
    .string "the measuring reed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_42_20::
    .string "He measured it by the four sides: it\n"
    .string "had a wall round about, five hundred\l"
    .string "reeds long, and five hundred broad,\l"
    .string "to make a separation between the\l"
    .string "sanctuary and the profane place.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_1::
    .string "Afterward he brought me to the gate,\n"
    .string "even the gate that looketh toward\l"
    .string "the east:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_2::
    .string "And, behold, the glory of the God\n"
    .string "of Israel came from the way of the\l"
    .string "east: and his voice was like a noise\l"
    .string "of many waters: and the earth shined\l"
    .string "with his glory$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_3::
    .string "And it was according to the\n"
    .string "appearance of the vision which I\l"
    .string "saw, even according to the vision\l"
    .string "that I saw when I came to destroy the\l"
    .string "city: and the visions were like the\l"
    .string "vision that I saw by the river\l"
    .string "Chebar; and I fell upon my face.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_4::
    .string "And the glory of the LORD came into\n"
    .string "the house by the way of the gate\l"
    .string "whose prospect is toward the east.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_5::
    .string "So the spirit took me up, and\n"
    .string "brought me into the inner court; and,\l"
    .string "behold, the glory of the LORD\l"
    .string "filled the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_6::
    .string "And I heard him speaking unto me\n"
    .string "out of the house; and the man stood by\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_7::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, the\n"
    .string "place of my throne, and the place\l"
    .string "of the soles of my feet, where I\l"
    .string "will dwell in the midst of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel for ever, and my\l"
    .string "holy name, shall the house of\l"
    .string "Israel no more defile, neither\l"
    .string "they, nor their kings, by their\l"
    .string "whoredom, nor by the carcases of\l"
    .string "their kings in their high places.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_8::
    .string "In their setting of their threshold\n"
    .string "by my thresholds, and their post by\l"
    .string "my posts, and the wall between me\l"
    .string "and them, they have even defiled my\l"
    .string "holy name by their abominations that\l"
    .string "they have committed: wherefore I have\l"
    .string "consumed them in mine anger.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_9::
    .string "Now let them put away their\n"
    .string "whoredom, and the carcases of their\l"
    .string "kings, far from me, and I will\l"
    .string "dwell in the midst of them for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_10::
    .string "Thou son of man, shew the house to\n"
    .string "the house of Israel, that they may be\l"
    .string "ashamed of their iniquities: and let\l"
    .string "them measure the pattern.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_11::
    .string "And if they be ashamed of all that\n"
    .string "they have done, shew them the form of\l"
    .string "the house, and the fashion thereof,\l"
    .string "and the goings out thereof, and the\l"
    .string "comings in thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "forms thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "ordinances thereof, and all the\l"
    .string "forms thereof, and all the laws\l"
    .string "thereof: and write it in their sight,\l"
    .string "that they may keep the whole form\l"
    .string "thereof, and all the ordinances\l"
    .string "thereof, and do them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_12::
    .string "This is the law of the house; Upon\n"
    .string "the top of the mountain the whole\l"
    .string "limit thereof round about shall be\l"
    .string "most holy. Behold, this is the law\l"
    .string "of the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_13::
    .string "And these are the measures of the\n"
    .string "altar after the cubits: The cubit is\l"
    .string "a cubit and an hand breadth; even the\l"
    .string "bottom shall be a cubit, and the\l"
    .string "breadth a cubit, and the border\l"
    .string "thereof by the edge thereof round\l"
    .string "about shall be a span: and this\l"
    .string "shall be the higher place of the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_14::
    .string "And from the bottom upon the ground\n"
    .string "even to the lower settle shall be\l"
    .string "two cubits, and the breadth one\l"
    .string "cubit; and from the lesser settle\l"
    .string "even to the greater settle shall be\l"
    .string "four cubits, and the breadth one\l"
    .string "cubit.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_15::
    .string "So the altar shall be four cubits;\n"
    .string "and from the altar and upward\l"
    .string "shall be four horns.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_16::
    .string "And the altar shall be twelve\n"
    .string "cubits long, twelve broad, square\l"
    .string "in the four squares thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_17::
    .string "And the settle shall be fourteen\n"
    .string "cubits long and fourteen broad in\l"
    .string "the four squares thereof; and the\l"
    .string "border about it shall be half a\l"
    .string "cubit; and the bottom thereof shall\l"
    .string "be a cubit about; and his stairs\l"
    .string "shall look toward the east.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_18::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, thus\n"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD; These are the\l"
    .string "ordinances of the altar in the day\l"
    .string "when they shall make it, to offer\l"
    .string "burnt offerings thereon, and to\l"
    .string "sprinkle blood thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_19::
    .string "And thou shalt give to the priests\n"
    .string "the Levites that be of the seed of\l"
    .string "Zadok, which approach unto me, to\l"
    .string "minister unto me, saith the Lord GOD,\l"
    .string "a young bullock for a sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_20::
    .string "And thou shalt take of the blood\n"
    .string "thereof, and put it on the four horns\l"
    .string "of it, and on the four corners of the\l"
    .string "settle, and upon the border round\l"
    .string "about: thus shalt thou cleanse and\l"
    .string "purge it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_21::
    .string "Thou shalt take the bullock also\n"
    .string "of the sin offering, and he shall\l"
    .string "burn it in the appointed place of\l"
    .string "the house, without the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_22::
    .string "And on the second day thou shalt\n"
    .string "offer a kid of the goats without\l"
    .string "blemish for a sin offering; and they\l"
    .string "shall cleanse the altar, as they\l"
    .string "did cleanse it with the bullock.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_23::
    .string "When thou hast made an end of\n"
    .string "cleansing it, thou shalt offer a\l"
    .string "young bullock without blemish, and\l"
    .string "a ram out of the flock without\l"
    .string "blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_24::
    .string "And thou shalt offer them before\n"
    .string "the LORD, and the priests shall\l"
    .string "cast salt upon them, and they\l"
    .string "shall offer them up for a burnt\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_25::
    .string "Seven days shalt thou prepare\n"
    .string "every day a goat for a sin offering:\l"
    .string "they shall also prepare a young\l"
    .string "bullock, and a ram out of the\l"
    .string "flock, without blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_26::
    .string "Seven days shall they purge the\n"
    .string "altar and purify it; and they\l"
    .string "shall consecrate themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_43_27::
    .string "And when these days are expired, it\n"
    .string "shall be, that upon the eighth day,\l"
    .string "and so forward, the priests shall\l"
    .string "make your burnt offerings upon the\l"
    .string "altar, and your peace offerings;\l"
    .string "and I will accept you, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_1::
    .string "Then he brought me back the way of\n"
    .string "the gate of the outward sanctuary\l"
    .string "which looketh toward the east; and\l"
    .string "it was shut.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_2::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me; This\n"
    .string "gate shall be shut, it shall not be\l"
    .string "opened, and no man shall enter in\l"
    .string "by it; because the LORD, the God of\l"
    .string "Israel, hath entered in by it,\l"
    .string "therefore it shall be shut.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_3::
    .string "It is for the prince; the prince,\n"
    .string "he shall sit in it to eat bread\l"
    .string "before the LORD; he shall enter by\l"
    .string "the way of the porch of that gate,\l"
    .string "and shall go out by the way of the\l"
    .string "same.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_4::
    .string "Then brought he me the way of the\n"
    .string "north gate before the house: and I\l"
    .string "looked, and, behold, the glory of\l"
    .string "the LORD filled the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD: and I fell upon my face.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_5::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, Son of\n"
    .string "man, mark well, and behold with\l"
    .string "thine eyes, and hear with thine ears\l"
    .string "all that I say unto thee concerning\l"
    .string "all the ordinances of the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and all the laws thereof;\l"
    .string "and mark well the entering in of the\l"
    .string "house, with every going forth of the\l"
    .string "sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_6::
    .string "And thou shalt say to the\n"
    .string "rebellious, even to the house of\l"
    .string "Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O ye\l"
    .string "house of Israel, let it suffice you\l"
    .string "of all your abominations,"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_7::
    .string "In that ye have brought into my\n"
    .string "sanctuary strangers, uncircumcised\l"
    .string "in heart, and uncircumcised in\l"
    .string "flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to\l"
    .string "pollute it, even my house, when ye\l"
    .string "offer my bread, the fat and the\l"
    .string "blood, and they have broken my\l"
    .string "covenant because of all your\l"
    .string "abominations$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_8::
    .string "And ye have not kept the charge of\n"
    .string "mine holy things: but ye have set\l"
    .string "keepers of my charge in my sanctuary\l"
    .string "for yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_9::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; No\n"
    .string "stranger, uncircumcised in heart,\l"
    .string "nor uncircumcised in flesh, shall\l"
    .string "enter into my sanctuary, of any\l"
    .string "stranger that is among the children\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_10::
    .string "And the Levites that are gone away\n"
    .string "far from me, when Israel went\l"
    .string "astray, which went astray away from\l"
    .string "me after their idols; they shall\l"
    .string "even bear their iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_11::
    .string "Yet they shall be ministers in my\n"
    .string "sanctuary, having charge at the gates\l"
    .string "of the house, and ministering to the\l"
    .string "house: they shall slay the burnt\l"
    .string "offering and the sacrifice for the\l"
    .string "people, and they shall stand\l"
    .string "before them to minister unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_12::
    .string "Because they ministered unto them\n"
    .string "before their idols, and caused the\l"
    .string "house of Israel to fall into\l"
    .string "iniquity; therefore have I lifted\l"
    .string "up mine hand against them, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD, and they shall bear their\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_13::
    .string "And they shall not come near unto\n"
    .string "me, to do the office of a priest unto\l"
    .string "me, nor to come near to any of my\l"
    .string "holy things, in the most holy\l"
    .string "place: but they shall bear their\l"
    .string "shame, and their abominations which\l"
    .string "they have committed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_14::
    .string "But I will make them keepers of\n"
    .string "the charge of the house, for all the\l"
    .string "service thereof, and for all that\l"
    .string "shall be done therein.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_15::
    .string "But the priests the Levites, the\n"
    .string "sons of Zadok, that kept the charge\l"
    .string "of my sanctuary when the children of\l"
    .string "Israel went astray from me, they\l"
    .string "shall come near to me to minister\l"
    .string "unto me, and they shall stand before\l"
    .string "me to offer unto me the fat and the\l"
    .string "blood, saith the Lord GOD:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_16::
    .string "They shall enter into my\n"
    .string "sanctuary, and they shall come near\l"
    .string "to my table, to minister unto me, and\l"
    .string "they shall keep my charge$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_17::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "when they enter in at the gates of\l"
    .string "the inner court, they shall be\l"
    .string "clothed with linen garments; and no\l"
    .string "wool shall come upon them, whiles\l"
    .string "they minister in the gates of the\l"
    .string "inner court, and within.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_18::
    .string "They shall have linen bonnets\n"
    .string "upon their heads, and shall have\l"
    .string "linen breeches upon their loins;\l"
    .string "they shall not gird themselves\l"
    .string "with any thing that causeth sweat.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_19::
    .string "And when they go forth into the\n"
    .string "utter court, even into the utter\l"
    .string "court to the people, they shall\l"
    .string "put off their garments wherein they\l"
    .string "ministered, and lay them in the holy\l"
    .string "chambers, and they shall put on\l"
    .string "other garments; and they shall not\l"
    .string "sanctify the people with their\l"
    .string "garments.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_20::
    .string "Neither shall they shave their\n"
    .string "heads, nor suffer their locks to\l"
    .string "grow long; they shall only poll\l"
    .string "their heads.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_21::
    .string "Neither shall any priest drink\n"
    .string "wine, when they enter into the inner\l"
    .string "court.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_22::
    .string "Neither shall they take for their\n"
    .string "wives a widow, nor her that is put\l"
    .string "away: but they shall take maidens of\l"
    .string "the seed of the house of Israel, or a\l"
    .string "widow that had a priest before.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_23::
    .string "And they shall teach my people\n"
    .string "the difference between the holy and\l"
    .string "profane, and cause them to discern\l"
    .string "between the unclean and the clean.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_24::
    .string "And in controversy they shall\n"
    .string "stand in judgment; and they shall\l"
    .string "judge it according to my judgments:\l"
    .string "and they shall keep my laws and my\l"
    .string "statutes in all mine assemblies;\l"
    .string "and they shall hallow my sabbaths.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_25::
    .string "And they shall come at no dead\n"
    .string "person to defile themselves: but\l"
    .string "for father, or for mother, or for son,\l"
    .string "or for daughter, for brother, or for\l"
    .string "sister that hath had no husband, they\l"
    .string "may defile themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_26::
    .string "And after he is cleansed, they\n"
    .string "shall reckon unto him seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_27::
    .string "And in the day that he goeth into\n"
    .string "the sanctuary, unto the inner court,\l"
    .string "to minister in the sanctuary, he\l"
    .string "shall offer his sin offering, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_28::
    .string "And it shall be unto them for an\n"
    .string "inheritance: I am their inheritance:\l"
    .string "and ye shall give them no\l"
    .string "possession in Israel: I am their\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_29::
    .string "They shall eat the meat offering,\n"
    .string "and the sin offering, and the\l"
    .string "trespass offering: and every\l"
    .string "dedicated thing in Israel shall be\l"
    .string "theirs.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_30::
    .string "And the first of all the\n"
    .string "firstfruits of all things, and\l"
    .string "every oblation of all, of every\l"
    .string "sort of your oblations, shall be\l"
    .string "the priest’s: ye shall also give\l"
    .string "unto the priest the first of your\l"
    .string "dough, that he may cause the\l"
    .string "blessing to rest in thine house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_44_31::
    .string "The priests shall not eat of any\n"
    .string "thing that is dead of itself, or\l"
    .string "torn, whether it be fowl or beast.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_1::
    .string "Moreover, when ye shall divide by\n"
    .string "lot the land for inheritance, ye\l"
    .string "shall offer an oblation unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, an holy portion of the land:\l"
    .string "the length shall be the length of\l"
    .string "five and twenty thousand reeds, and\l"
    .string "the breadth shall be ten thousand.\l"
    .string "This shall be holy in all the\l"
    .string "borders thereof round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_2::
    .string "Of this there shall be for the\n"
    .string "sanctuary five hundred in length,\l"
    .string "with five hundred in breadth, square\l"
    .string "round about; and fifty cubits round\l"
    .string "about for the suburbs thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_3::
    .string "And of this measure shalt thou\n"
    .string "measure the length of five and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand, and the breadth of\l"
    .string "ten thousand: and in it shall be the\l"
    .string "sanctuary and the most holy place.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_4::
    .string "The holy portion of the land\n"
    .string "shall be for the priests the\l"
    .string "ministers of the sanctuary, which\l"
    .string "shall come near to minister unto\l"
    .string "the LORD: and it shall be a place\l"
    .string "for their houses, and an holy place\l"
    .string "for the sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_5::
    .string "And the five and twenty thousand of\n"
    .string "length, and the ten thousand of\l"
    .string "breadth shall also the Levites, the\l"
    .string "ministers of the house, have for\l"
    .string "themselves, for a possession for\l"
    .string "twenty chambers.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_6::
    .string "And ye shall appoint the\n"
    .string "possession of the city five thousand\l"
    .string "broad, and five and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "long, over against the oblation of\l"
    .string "the holy portion: it shall be for\l"
    .string "the whole house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_7::
    .string "And a portion shall be for the\n"
    .string "prince on the one side and on the\l"
    .string "other side of the oblation of the\l"
    .string "holy portion, and of the possession\l"
    .string "of the city, before the oblation of\l"
    .string "the holy portion, and before the\l"
    .string "possession of the city, from the west\l"
    .string "side westward, and from the east side\l"
    .string "eastward: and the length shall be\l"
    .string "over against one of the portions,\l"
    .string "from the west border unto the east\l"
    .string "border.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_8::
    .string "In the land shall be his\n"
    .string "possession in Israel: and my\l"
    .string "princes shall no more oppress my\l"
    .string "people; and the rest of the land\l"
    .string "shall they give to the house of\l"
    .string "Israel according to their tribes.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_9::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Let it\n"
    .string "suffice you, O princes of Israel:\l"
    .string "remove violence and spoil, and\l"
    .string "execute judgment and justice, take\l"
    .string "away your exactions from my people,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_10::
    .string "Ye shall have just balances, and a\n"
    .string "just ephah, and a just bath.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_11::
    .string "The ephah and the bath shall be of\n"
    .string "one measure, that the bath may\l"
    .string "contain the tenth part of an homer,\l"
    .string "and the ephah the tenth part of an\l"
    .string "homer: the measure thereof shall be\l"
    .string "after the homer.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_12::
    .string "And the shekel shall be twenty\n"
    .string "gerahs: twenty shekels, five and\l"
    .string "twenty shekels, fifteen shekels,\l"
    .string "shall be your maneh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_13::
    .string "This is the oblation that ye shall\n"
    .string "offer; the sixth part of an ephah of\l"
    .string "an homer of wheat, and ye shall give\l"
    .string "the sixth part of an ephah of an\l"
    .string "homer of barley:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_14::
    .string "Concerning the ordinance of oil,\n"
    .string "the bath of oil, ye shall offer the\l"
    .string "tenth part of a bath out of the cor,\l"
    .string "which is an homer of ten baths; for\l"
    .string "ten baths are an homer:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_15::
    .string "And one lamb out of the flock, out\n"
    .string "of two hundred, out of the fat\l"
    .string "pastures of Israel; for a meat\l"
    .string "offering, and for a burnt offering,\l"
    .string "and for peace offerings, to make\l"
    .string "reconciliation for them, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_16::
    .string "All the people of the land\n"
    .string "shall give this oblation for the\l"
    .string "prince in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_17::
    .string "And it shall be the prince’s part\n"
    .string "to give burnt offerings, and meat\l"
    .string "offerings, and drink offerings, in\l"
    .string "the feasts, and in the new moons, and\l"
    .string "in the sabbaths, in all solemnities\l"
    .string "of the house of Israel: he shall\l"
    .string "prepare the sin offering, and the\l"
    .string "meat offering, and the burnt\l"
    .string "offering, and the peace offerings,\l"
    .string "to make reconciliation for the house\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_18::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the\n"
    .string "first month, in the first day of the\l"
    .string "month, thou shalt take a young\l"
    .string "bullock without blemish, and\l"
    .string "cleanse the sanctuary:"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_19::
    .string "And the priest shall take of the\n"
    .string "blood of the sin offering, and put\l"
    .string "it upon the posts of the house, and\l"
    .string "upon the four corners of the settle\l"
    .string "of the altar, and upon the posts of\l"
    .string "the gate of the inner court$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_20::
    .string "And so thou shalt do the seventh\n"
    .string "day of the month for every one that\l"
    .string "erreth, and for him that is simple:\l"
    .string "so shall ye reconcile the house.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_21::
    .string "In the first month, in the\n"
    .string "fourteenth day of the month, ye\l"
    .string "shall have the passover, a feast of\l"
    .string "seven days; unleavened bread shall\l"
    .string "be eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_22::
    .string "And upon that day shall the\n"
    .string "prince prepare for himself and for\l"
    .string "all the people of the land a\l"
    .string "bullock for a sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_23::
    .string "And seven days of the feast he\n"
    .string "shall prepare a burnt offering to\l"
    .string "the LORD, seven bullocks and seven\l"
    .string "rams without blemish daily the\l"
    .string "seven days; and a kid of the goats\l"
    .string "daily for a sin offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_24::
    .string "And he shall prepare a meat\n"
    .string "offering of an ephah for a bullock,\l"
    .string "and an ephah for a ram, and an hin of\l"
    .string "oil for an ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_45_25::
    .string "In the seventh month, in the\n"
    .string "fifteenth day of the month, shall he\l"
    .string "do the like in the feast of the seven\l"
    .string "days, according to the sin offering,\l"
    .string "according to the burnt offering, and\l"
    .string "according to the meat offering, and\l"
    .string "according to the oil.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_1::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; The gate of\n"
    .string "the inner court that looketh toward\l"
    .string "the east shall be shut the six\l"
    .string "working days; but on the sabbath it\l"
    .string "shall be opened, and in the day of\l"
    .string "the new moon it shall be opened.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_2::
    .string "And the prince shall enter by the\n"
    .string "way of the porch of that gate\l"
    .string "without, and shall stand by the\l"
    .string "post of the gate, and the priests\l"
    .string "shall prepare his burnt offering\l"
    .string "and his peace offerings, and he\l"
    .string "shall worship at the threshold of\l"
    .string "the gate: then he shall go forth;\l"
    .string "but the gate shall not be shut\l"
    .string "until the evening.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_3::
    .string "Likewise the people of the land\n"
    .string "shall worship at the door of this\l"
    .string "gate before the LORD in the sabbaths\l"
    .string "and in the new moons.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_4::
    .string "And the burnt offering that the\n"
    .string "prince shall offer unto the LORD in\l"
    .string "the sabbath day shall be six lambs\l"
    .string "without blemish, and a ram without\l"
    .string "blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_5::
    .string "And the meat offering shall be an\n"
    .string "ephah for a ram, and the meat\l"
    .string "offering for the lambs as he shall\l"
    .string "be able to give, and an hin of oil to\l"
    .string "an ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_6::
    .string "And in the day of the new moon it\n"
    .string "shall be a young bullock without\l"
    .string "blemish, and six lambs, and a ram:\l"
    .string "they shall be without blemish.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_7::
    .string "And he shall prepare a meat\n"
    .string "offering, an ephah for a bullock,\l"
    .string "and an ephah for a ram, and for the\l"
    .string "lambs according as his hand shall\l"
    .string "attain unto, and an hin of oil to an\l"
    .string "ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_8::
    .string "And when the prince shall enter,\n"
    .string "he shall go in by the way of the\l"
    .string "porch of that gate, and he shall go\l"
    .string "forth by the way thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_9::
    .string "But when the people of the land\n"
    .string "shall come before the LORD in the\l"
    .string "solemn feasts, he that entereth in\l"
    .string "by the way of the north gate to\l"
    .string "worship shall go out by the way of\l"
    .string "the south gate; and he that entereth\l"
    .string "by the way of the south gate shall\l"
    .string "go forth by the way of the north gate:\l"
    .string "he shall not return by the way of\l"
    .string "the gate whereby he came in, but\l"
    .string "shall go forth over against it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_10::
    .string "And the prince in the midst of them,\n"
    .string "when they go in, shall go in; and\l"
    .string "when they go forth, shall go forth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_11::
    .string "And in the feasts and in the\n"
    .string "solemnities the meat offering\l"
    .string "shall be an ephah to a bullock,\l"
    .string "and an ephah to a ram, and to the\l"
    .string "lambs as he is able to give, and an\l"
    .string "hin of oil to an ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_12::
    .string "Now when the prince shall\n"
    .string "prepare a voluntary burnt offering\l"
    .string "or peace offerings voluntarily\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, one shall then open\l"
    .string "him the gate that looketh toward the\l"
    .string "east, and he shall prepare his\l"
    .string "burnt offering and his peace\l"
    .string "offerings, as he did on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day: then he shall go forth; and\l"
    .string "after his going forth one shall\l"
    .string "shut the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_13::
    .string "Thou shalt daily prepare a burnt\n"
    .string "offering unto the LORD of a lamb of\l"
    .string "the first year without blemish: thou\l"
    .string "shalt prepare it every morning.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_14::
    .string "And thou shalt prepare a meat\n"
    .string "offering for it every morning, the\l"
    .string "sixth part of an ephah, and the\l"
    .string "third part of an hin of oil, to\l"
    .string "temper with the fine flour; a meat\l"
    .string "offering continually by a\l"
    .string "perpetual ordinance unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_15::
    .string "Thus shall they prepare the\n"
    .string "lamb, and the meat offering, and the\l"
    .string "oil, every morning for a continual\l"
    .string "burnt offering.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_16::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; If the\n"
    .string "prince give a gift unto any of his\l"
    .string "sons, the inheritance thereof shall\l"
    .string "be his sons’; it shall be their\l"
    .string "possession by inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_17::
    .string "But if he give a gift of his\n"
    .string "inheritance to one of his servants,\l"
    .string "then it shall be his to the year of\l"
    .string "liberty; after it shall return to\l"
    .string "the prince: but his inheritance\l"
    .string "shall be his sons’ for them.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_18::
    .string "Moreover the prince shall not\n"
    .string "take of the people’s inheritance\l"
    .string "by oppression, to thrust them out of\l"
    .string "their possession; but he shall give\l"
    .string "his sons inheritance out of his own\l"
    .string "possession: that my people be not\l"
    .string "scattered every man from his\l"
    .string "possession.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_19::
    .string "After he brought me through the\n"
    .string "entry, which was at the side of the\l"
    .string "gate, into the holy chambers of the\l"
    .string "priests, which looked toward the\l"
    .string "north: and, behold, there was a\l"
    .string "place on the two sides westward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_20::
    .string "Then said he unto me, This is the\n"
    .string "place where the priests shall\l"
    .string "boil the trespass offering and the\l"
    .string "sin offering, where they shall bake\l"
    .string "the meat offering; that they bear\l"
    .string "them not out into the utter court, to\l"
    .string "sanctify the people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_21::
    .string "Then he brought me forth into the\n"
    .string "utter court, and caused me to pass by\l"
    .string "the four corners of the court; and,\l"
    .string "behold, in every corner of the court\l"
    .string "there was a court.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_22::
    .string "In the four corners of the court\n"
    .string "there were courts joined of forty\l"
    .string "cubits long and thirty broad: these\l"
    .string "four corners were of one measure.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_23::
    .string "And there was a row of building\n"
    .string "round about in them, round about them\l"
    .string "four, and it was made with boiling\l"
    .string "places under the rows round about.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_46_24::
    .string "Then said he unto me, These are the\n"
    .string "places of them that boil, where the\l"
    .string "ministers of the house shall boil\l"
    .string "the sacrifice of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_1::
    .string "Afterward he brought me again unto\n"
    .string "the door of the house; and, behold,\l"
    .string "waters issued out from under the\l"
    .string "threshold of the house eastward: for\l"
    .string "the forefront of the house stood\l"
    .string "toward the east, and the waters came\l"
    .string "down from under from the right side\l"
    .string "of the house, at the south side of the\l"
    .string "altar.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_2::
    .string "Then brought he me out of the way of\n"
    .string "the gate northward, and led me about\l"
    .string "the way without unto the utter gate\l"
    .string "by the way that looketh eastward;\l"
    .string "and, behold, there ran out waters on\l"
    .string "the right side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_3::
    .string "And when the man that had the line\n"
    .string "in his hand went forth eastward, he\l"
    .string "measured a thousand cubits, and he\l"
    .string "brought me through the waters; the\l"
    .string "waters were to the ankles.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_4::
    .string "Again he measured a thousand, and\n"
    .string "brought me through the waters; the\l"
    .string "waters were to the knees. Again he\l"
    .string "measured a thousand, and brought me\l"
    .string "through; the waters were to the\l"
    .string "loins.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_5::
    .string "Afterward he measured a thousand;\n"
    .string "and it was a river that I could not\l"
    .string "pass over: for the waters were risen,\l"
    .string "waters to swim in, a river that could\l"
    .string "not be passed over.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_6::
    .string "And he said unto me, Son of man, hast\n"
    .string "thou seen this? Then he brought me,\l"
    .string "and caused me to return to the brink\l"
    .string "of the river.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_7::
    .string "Now when I had returned, behold, at\n"
    .string "the bank of the river were very many\l"
    .string "trees on the one side and on the\l"
    .string "other.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_8::
    .string "Then said he unto me, These waters\n"
    .string "issue out toward the east country,\l"
    .string "and go down into the desert, and go\l"
    .string "into the sea: which being brought\l"
    .string "forth into the sea, the waters shall\l"
    .string "be healed.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "every thing that liveth, which\l"
    .string "moveth, whithersoever the rivers\l"
    .string "shall come, shall live: and there\l"
    .string "shall be a very great multitude of\l"
    .string "fish, because these waters shall\l"
    .string "come thither: for they shall be\l"
    .string "healed; and every thing shall live\l"
    .string "whither the river cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_10::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "the fishers shall stand upon it\l"
    .string "from Engedi even unto Eneglaim; they\l"
    .string "shall be a place to spread forth\l"
    .string "nets; their fish shall be according\l"
    .string "to their kinds, as the fish of the\l"
    .string "great sea, exceeding many.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_11::
    .string "But the miry places thereof and\n"
    .string "the marishes thereof shall not be\l"
    .string "healed; they shall be given to\l"
    .string "salt.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_12::
    .string "And by the river upon the bank\n"
    .string "thereof, on this side and on that\l"
    .string "side, shall grow all trees for\l"
    .string "meat, whose leaf shall not fade,\l"
    .string "neither shall the fruit thereof be\l"
    .string "consumed: it shall bring forth new\l"
    .string "fruit according to his months,\l"
    .string "because their waters they issued out\l"
    .string "of the sanctuary: and the fruit\l"
    .string "thereof shall be for meat, and the\l"
    .string "leaf thereof for medicine.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_13::
    .string "Thus saith the Lord GOD; This shall\n"
    .string "be the border, whereby ye shall\l"
    .string "inherit the land according to the\l"
    .string "twelve tribes of Israel: Joseph\l"
    .string "shall have two portions.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_14::
    .string "And ye shall inherit it, one as\n"
    .string "well as another: concerning the\l"
    .string "which I lifted up mine hand to give\l"
    .string "it unto your fathers: and this land\l"
    .string "shall fall unto you for\l"
    .string "inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_15::
    .string "And this shall be the border of the\n"
    .string "land toward the north side, from the\l"
    .string "great sea, the way of Hethlon, as men\l"
    .string "go to Zedad;"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_16::
    .string "Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim, which is\n"
    .string "between the border of Damascus and\l"
    .string "the border of Hamath; Hazarhatticon,\l"
    .string "which is by the coast of Hauran$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_17::
    .string "And the border from the sea shall\n"
    .string "be Hazarenan, the border of Damascus,\l"
    .string "and the north northward, and the\l"
    .string "border of Hamath. And this is the\l"
    .string "north side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_18::
    .string "And the east side ye shall measure\n"
    .string "from Hauran, and from Damascus, and\l"
    .string "from Gilead, and from the land of\l"
    .string "Israel by Jordan, from the border\l"
    .string "unto the east sea. And this is the\l"
    .string "east side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_19::
    .string "And the south side southward, from\n"
    .string "Tamar even to the waters of strife in\l"
    .string "Kadesh, the river to the great sea.\l"
    .string "And this is the south side southward.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_20::
    .string "The west side also shall be the\n"
    .string "great sea from the border, till a\l"
    .string "man come over against Hamath. This is\l"
    .string "the west side.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_21::
    .string "So shall ye divide this land unto\n"
    .string "you according to the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_22::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that ye\n"
    .string "shall divide it by lot for an\l"
    .string "inheritance unto you, and to the\l"
    .string "strangers that sojourn among you,\l"
    .string "which shall beget children among\l"
    .string "you: and they shall be unto you as\l"
    .string "born in the country among the\l"
    .string "children of Israel; they shall\l"
    .string "have inheritance with you among the\l"
    .string "tribes of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_47_23::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that in\n"
    .string "what tribe the stranger sojourneth,\l"
    .string "there shall ye give him his\l"
    .string "inheritance, saith the Lord GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_1::
    .string "Now these are the names of the tribes\n"
    .string " From the north end to the coast of\l"
    .string "the way of Hethlon, as one goeth to\l"
    .string "Hamath, Hazarenan, the border of\l"
    .string "Damascus northward, to the coast of\l"
    .string "Hamath; for these are his sides east\l"
    .string "and west; a portion for Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_2::
    .string "And by the border of Dan, from the\n"
    .string "east side unto the west side, a\l"
    .string "portion for Asher.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_3::
    .string "And by the border of Asher, from the\n"
    .string "east side even unto the west side, a\l"
    .string "portion for Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_4::
    .string "And by the border of Naphtali, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side, a\l"
    .string "portion for Manasseh.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_5::
    .string "And by the border of Manasseh, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side, a\l"
    .string "portion for Ephraim.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_6::
    .string "And by the border of Ephraim, from\n"
    .string "the east side even unto the west\l"
    .string "side, a portion for Reuben.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_7::
    .string "And by the border of Reuben, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side, a\l"
    .string "portion for Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_8::
    .string "And by the border of Judah, from the\n"
    .string "east side unto the west side, shall\l"
    .string "be the offering which ye shall\l"
    .string "offer of five and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "reeds in breadth, and in length as\l"
    .string "one of the other parts, from the east\l"
    .string "side unto the west side: and the\l"
    .string "sanctuary shall be in the midst of\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_9::
    .string "The oblation that ye shall offer\n"
    .string "unto the LORD shall be of five and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand in length, and of\l"
    .string "ten thousand in breadth.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_10::
    .string "And for them, even for the priests,\n"
    .string "shall be this holy oblation;\l"
    .string "toward the north five and twenty\l"
    .string "thousand in length, and toward the\l"
    .string "west ten thousand in breadth, and\l"
    .string "toward the east ten thousand in\l"
    .string "breadth, and toward the south five\l"
    .string "and twenty thousand in length: and\l"
    .string "the sanctuary of the LORD shall be\l"
    .string "in the midst thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_11::
    .string "It shall be for the priests that\n"
    .string "are sanctified of the sons of Zadok;\l"
    .string "which have kept my charge, which\l"
    .string "went not astray when the children of\l"
    .string "Israel went astray, as the Levites\l"
    .string "went astray.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_12::
    .string "And this oblation of the land that\n"
    .string "is offered shall be unto them a\l"
    .string "thing most holy by the border of the\l"
    .string "Levites.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_13::
    .string "And over against the border of the\n"
    .string "priests the Levites shall have five\l"
    .string "and twenty thousand in length, and\l"
    .string "ten thousand in breadth: all the\l"
    .string "length shall be five and twenty\l"
    .string "thousand, and the breadth ten\l"
    .string "thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_14::
    .string "And they shall not sell of it,\n"
    .string "neither exchange, nor alienate the\l"
    .string "firstfruits of the land: for it is\l"
    .string "holy unto the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_15::
    .string "And the five thousand, that are\n"
    .string "left in the breadth over against the\l"
    .string "five and twenty thousand, shall be a\l"
    .string "profane place for the city, for\l"
    .string "dwelling, and for suburbs: and the\l"
    .string "city shall be in the midst thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_16::
    .string "And these shall be the measures\n"
    .string "thereof; the north side four thousand\l"
    .string "and five hundred, and the south side\l"
    .string "four thousand and five hundred, and\l"
    .string "on the east side four thousand and\l"
    .string "five hundred, and the west side four\l"
    .string "thousand and five hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_17::
    .string "And the suburbs of the city shall\n"
    .string "be toward the north two hundred and\l"
    .string "fifty, and toward the south two\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty, and toward the\l"
    .string "east two hundred and fifty, and\l"
    .string "toward the west two hundred and fifty.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_18::
    .string "And the residue in length over\n"
    .string "against the oblation of the holy\l"
    .string "portion shall be ten thousand\l"
    .string "eastward, and ten thousand westward:\l"
    .string "and it shall be over against the\l"
    .string "oblation of the holy portion; and\l"
    .string "the increase thereof shall be for\l"
    .string "food unto them that serve the city.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_19::
    .string "And they that serve the city shall\n"
    .string "serve it out of all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_20::
    .string "All the oblation shall be five\n"
    .string "and twenty thousand by five and\l"
    .string "twenty thousand: ye shall offer the\l"
    .string "holy oblation foursquare, with the\l"
    .string "possession of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_21::
    .string "And the residue shall be for the\n"
    .string "prince, on the one side and on the\l"
    .string "other of the holy oblation, and of\l"
    .string "the possession of the city, over\l"
    .string "against the five and twenty thousand\l"
    .string "of the oblation toward the east\l"
    .string "border, and westward over against the\l"
    .string "five and twenty thousand toward the\l"
    .string "west border, over against the\l"
    .string "portions for the prince: and it\l"
    .string "shall be the holy oblation; and\l"
    .string "the sanctuary of the house shall be\l"
    .string "in the midst thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_22::
    .string "Moreover from the possession of the\n"
    .string "Levites, and from the possession of\l"
    .string "the city, being in the midst of that\l"
    .string "which is the prince’s, between the\l"
    .string "border of Judah and the border of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, shall be for the prince.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_23::
    .string "As for the rest of the tribes, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side,\l"
    .string "Benjamin shall have a portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_24::
    .string "And by the border of Benjamin, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side,\l"
    .string "Simeon shall have a portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_25::
    .string "And by the border of Simeon, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side,\l"
    .string "Issachar a portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_26::
    .string "And by the border of Issachar, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side,\l"
    .string "Zebulun a portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_27::
    .string "And by the border of Zebulun, from\n"
    .string "the east side unto the west side, Gad\l"
    .string "a portion.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_28::
    .string "And by the border of Gad, at the\n"
    .string "south side southward, the border\l"
    .string "shall be even from Tamar unto the\l"
    .string "waters of strife in Kadesh, and to\l"
    .string "the river toward the great sea.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_29::
    .string "This is the land which ye shall\n"
    .string "divide by lot unto the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel for inheritance, and these\l"
    .string "are their portions, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_30::
    .string "And these are the goings out of the\n"
    .string "city on the north side, four thousand\l"
    .string "and five hundred measures.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_31::
    .string "And the gates of the city shall be\n"
    .string "after the names of the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel: three gates northward; one\l"
    .string "gate of Reuben, one gate of Judah,\l"
    .string "one gate of Levi.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_32::
    .string "And at the east side four thousand\n"
    .string "and five hundred: and three gates;\l"
    .string "and one gate of Joseph, one gate of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, one gate of Dan.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_33::
    .string "And at the south side four thousand\n"
    .string "and five hundred measures: and three\l"
    .string "gates; one gate of Simeon, one gate\l"
    .string "of Issachar, one gate of Zebulun.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_34::
    .string "At the west side four thousand and\n"
    .string "five hundred, with their three gates;\l"
    .string "one gate of Gad, one gate of Asher,\l"
    .string "one gate of Naphtali.$"
Bible_Text_Ezekiel_48_35::
    .string "It was round about eighteen\n"
    .string "thousand measures: and the name of\l"
    .string "the city from that day shall be, The\l"
    .string "LORD is there.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_1::
    .string "In the third year of the reign of\n"
    .string "Jehoiakim king of Judah came\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and besieged it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_2::
    .string "And the Lord gave Jehoiakim king of\n"
    .string "Judah into his hand, with part of the\l"
    .string "vessels of the house of God: which he\l"
    .string "carried into the land of Shinar to\l"
    .string "the house of his god; and he brought\l"
    .string "the vessels into the treasure house\l"
    .string "of his god.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_3::
    .string "And the king spake unto Ashpenaz\n"
    .string "the master of his eunuchs, that he\l"
    .string "should bring certain of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, and of the\l"
    .string "king’s seed, and of the princes;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_4::
    .string "Children in whom was no blemish,\n"
    .string "but well favoured, and skilful in\l"
    .string "all wisdom, and cunning in\l"
    .string "knowledge, and understanding\l"
    .string "science, and such as had ability in\l"
    .string "them to stand in the king’s palace,\l"
    .string "and whom they might teach the\l"
    .string "learning and the tongue of the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_5::
    .string "And the king appointed them a\n"
    .string "daily provision of the king’s meat,\l"
    .string "and of the wine which he drank: so\l"
    .string "nourishing them three years, that at\l"
    .string "the end thereof they might stand\l"
    .string "before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_6::
    .string "Now among these were of the\n"
    .string "children of Judah, Daniel,\l"
    .string "Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_7::
    .string "Unto whom the prince of the eunuchs\n"
    .string "gave names: for he gave unto Daniel\l"
    .string "the name of Belteshazzar; and to\l"
    .string "Hananiah, of Shadrach; and to\l"
    .string "Mishael, of Meshach; and to Azariah,\l"
    .string "of Abednego$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_8::
    .string "But Daniel purposed in his heart\n"
    .string "that he would not defile himself\l"
    .string "with the portion of the king’s meat,\l"
    .string "nor with the wine which he drank:\l"
    .string "therefore he requested of the prince\l"
    .string "of the eunuchs that he might not\l"
    .string "defile himself.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_9::
    .string "Now God had brought Daniel into\n"
    .string "favour and tender love with the\l"
    .string "prince of the eunuchs.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_10::
    .string "And the prince of the eunuchs said\n"
    .string "unto Daniel, I fear my lord the\l"
    .string "king, who hath appointed your meat\l"
    .string "and your drink: for why should he see\l"
    .string "your faces worse liking than the\l"
    .string "children which are of your sort?\l"
    .string "then shall ye make me endanger my\l"
    .string "head to the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_11::
    .string "Then said Daniel to Melzar, whom\n"
    .string "the prince of the eunuchs had set\l"
    .string "over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and\l"
    .string "Azariah,"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_12::
    .string "Prove thy servants, I beseech thee,\n"
    .string "ten days; and let them give us\l"
    .string "pulse to eat, and water to drink$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_13::
    .string "Then let our countenances be\n"
    .string "looked upon before thee, and the\l"
    .string "countenance of the children that eat\l"
    .string "of the portion of the king’s meat:\l"
    .string "and as thou seest, deal with thy\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_14::
    .string "So he consented to them in this\n"
    .string "matter, and proved them ten days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_15::
    .string "And at the end of ten days their\n"
    .string "countenances appeared fairer and\l"
    .string "fatter in flesh than all the\l"
    .string "children which did eat the portion\l"
    .string "of the king’s meat.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_16::
    .string "Thus Melzar took away the portion\n"
    .string "of their meat, and the wine that they\l"
    .string "should drink; and gave them pulse.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_17::
    .string "As for these four children, God\n"
    .string "gave them knowledge and skill in\l"
    .string "all learning and wisdom: and\l"
    .string "Daniel had understanding in all\l"
    .string "visions and dreams.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_18::
    .string "Now at the end of the days that the\n"
    .string "king had said he should bring them\l"
    .string "in, then the prince of the eunuchs\l"
    .string "brought them in before\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_19::
    .string "And the king communed with them; and\n"
    .string "among them all was found none like\l"
    .string "Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and\l"
    .string "Azariah: therefore stood they before\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_20::
    .string "And in all matters of wisdom and\n"
    .string "understanding, that the king\l"
    .string "enquired of them, he found them ten\l"
    .string "times better than all the magicians\l"
    .string "and astrologers that were in all\l"
    .string "his realm.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_1_21::
    .string "And Daniel continued even unto the\n"
    .string "first year of king Cyrus.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_1::
    .string "And in the second year of the reign\n"
    .string "of Nebuchadnezzar Nebuchadnezzar\l"
    .string "dreamed dreams, wherewith his spirit\l"
    .string "was troubled, and his sleep brake\l"
    .string "from him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_2::
    .string "Then the king commanded to call\n"
    .string "the magicians, and the astrologers,\l"
    .string "and the sorcerers, and the\l"
    .string "Chaldeans, for to shew the king his\l"
    .string "dreams. So they came and stood before\l"
    .string "the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_3::
    .string "And the king said unto them, I have\n"
    .string "dreamed a dream, and my spirit was\l"
    .string "troubled to know the dream.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_4::
    .string "Then spake the Chaldeans to the\n"
    .string "king in Syriack, O king, live for\l"
    .string "ever: tell thy servants the dream,\l"
    .string "and we will shew the\l"
    .string "interpretation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_5::
    .string "The king answered and said to the\n"
    .string "Chaldeans, The thing is gone from\l"
    .string "me: if ye will not make known unto\l"
    .string "me the dream, with the\l"
    .string "interpretation thereof, ye shall\l"
    .string "be cut in pieces, and your houses\l"
    .string "shall be made a dunghill.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_6::
    .string "But if ye shew the dream, and the\n"
    .string "interpretation thereof, ye shall\l"
    .string "receive of me gifts and rewards and\l"
    .string "great honour: therefore shew me the\l"
    .string "dream, and the interpretation\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_7::
    .string "They answered again and said, Let\n"
    .string "the king tell his servants the\l"
    .string "dream, and we will shew the\l"
    .string "interpretation of it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_8::
    .string "The king answered and said, I know\n"
    .string "of certainty that ye would gain the\l"
    .string "time, because ye see the thing is\l"
    .string "gone from me.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_9::
    .string "But if ye will not make known unto\n"
    .string "me the dream, there is but one decree\l"
    .string "for you: for ye have prepared lying\l"
    .string "and corrupt words to speak before\l"
    .string "me, till the time be changed:\l"
    .string "therefore tell me the dream, and I\l"
    .string "shall know that ye can shew me the\l"
    .string "interpretation thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_10::
    .string "The Chaldeans answered before the\n"
    .string "king, and said, There is not a man\l"
    .string "upon the earth that can shew the\l"
    .string "king’s matter: therefore there is no\l"
    .string "king, lord, nor ruler, that asked\l"
    .string "such things at any magician, or\l"
    .string "astrologer, or Chaldean.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_11::
    .string "And it is a rare thing that the king\n"
    .string "requireth, and there is none other\l"
    .string "that can shew it before the king,\l"
    .string "except the gods, whose dwelling is\l"
    .string "not with flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_12::
    .string "For this cause the king was angry\n"
    .string "and very furious, and commanded to\l"
    .string "destroy all the wise men of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_13::
    .string "And the decree went forth that the\n"
    .string "wise men should be slain; and they\l"
    .string "sought Daniel and his fellows to be\l"
    .string "slain.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_14::
    .string "Then Daniel answered with counsel\n"
    .string "and wisdom to Arioch the captain of\l"
    .string "the king’s guard, which was gone\l"
    .string "forth to slay the wise men of\l"
    .string "Babylon:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_15::
    .string "He answered and said to Arioch the\n"
    .string "king’s captain, Why is the decree so\l"
    .string "hasty from the king? Then Arioch made\l"
    .string "the thing known to Daniel$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_16::
    .string "Then Daniel went in, and desired of\n"
    .string "the king that he would give him time,\l"
    .string "and that he would shew the king the\l"
    .string "interpretation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_17::
    .string "Then Daniel went to his house, and\n"
    .string "made the thing known to Hananiah,\l"
    .string "Mishael, and Azariah, his\l"
    .string "companions:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_18::
    .string "That they would desire mercies of\n"
    .string "the God of heaven concerning this\l"
    .string "secret; that Daniel and his fellows\l"
    .string "should not perish with the rest of\l"
    .string "the wise men of Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_19::
    .string "Then was the secret revealed unto\n"
    .string "Daniel in a night vision. Then\l"
    .string "Daniel blessed the God of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_20::
    .string "Daniel answered and said, Blessed\n"
    .string "be the name of God for ever and ever:\l"
    .string "for wisdom and might are his:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_21::
    .string "And he changeth the times and the\n"
    .string "seasons: he removeth kings, and\l"
    .string "setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom\l"
    .string "unto the wise, and knowledge to them\l"
    .string "that know understanding:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_22::
    .string "He revealeth the deep and secret\n"
    .string "things: he knoweth what is in the\l"
    .string "darkness, and the light dwelleth\l"
    .string "with him$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_23::
    .string "I thank thee, and praise thee, O\n"
    .string "thou God of my fathers, who hast\l"
    .string "given me wisdom and might, and hast\l"
    .string "made known unto me now what we\l"
    .string "desired of thee: for thou hast now\l"
    .string "made known unto us the king’s matter.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_24::
    .string "Therefore Daniel went in unto\n"
    .string "Arioch, whom the king had ordained to\l"
    .string "destroy the wise men of Babylon: he\l"
    .string "went and said thus unto him; Destroy\l"
    .string "not the wise men of Babylon: bring me\l"
    .string "in before the king, and I will shew\l"
    .string "unto the king the interpretation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_25::
    .string "Then Arioch brought in Daniel\n"
    .string "before the king in haste, and said\l"
    .string "thus unto him, I have found a man of\l"
    .string "the captives of Judah, that will\l"
    .string "make known unto the king the\l"
    .string "interpretation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_26::
    .string "The king answered and said to\n"
    .string "Daniel, whose name was\l"
    .string "Belteshazzar, Art thou able to make\l"
    .string "known unto me the dream which I have\l"
    .string "seen, and the interpretation\l"
    .string "thereof?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_27::
    .string "Daniel answered in the presence of\n"
    .string "the king, and said, The secret which\l"
    .string "the king hath demanded cannot the\l"
    .string "wise men, the astrologers, the\l"
    .string "magicians, the soothsayers, shew\l"
    .string "unto the king;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_28::
    .string "But there is a God in heaven that\n"
    .string "revealeth secrets, and maketh known\l"
    .string "to the king Nebuchadnezzar what\l"
    .string "shall be in the latter days. Thy\l"
    .string "dream, and the visions of thy head\l"
    .string "upon thy bed, are these;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_29::
    .string "As for thee, O king, thy thoughts\n"
    .string "came into thy mind upon thy bed, what\l"
    .string "should come to pass hereafter: and\l"
    .string "he that revealeth secrets maketh\l"
    .string "known to thee what shall come to\l"
    .string "pass$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_30::
    .string "But as for me, this secret is not\n"
    .string "revealed to me for any wisdom that I\l"
    .string "have more than any living, but for\l"
    .string "their sakes that shall make known\l"
    .string "the interpretation to the king, and\l"
    .string "that thou mightest know the thoughts\l"
    .string "of thy heart.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_31::
    .string "Thou, O king, sawest, and behold a\n"
    .string "great image. This great image, whose\l"
    .string "brightness was excellent, stood\l"
    .string "before thee; and the form thereof was\l"
    .string "terrible.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_32::
    .string "This image’s head was of fine gold,\n"
    .string "his breast and his arms of silver,\l"
    .string "his belly and his thighs of brass,"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_33::
    .string "His legs of iron, his feet part of\n"
    .string "iron and part of clay$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_34::
    .string "Thou sawest till that a stone was\n"
    .string "cut out without hands, which smote\l"
    .string "the image upon his feet that were of\l"
    .string "iron and clay, and brake them to\l"
    .string "pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_35::
    .string "Then was the iron, the clay, the\n"
    .string "brass, the silver, and the gold,\l"
    .string "broken to pieces together, and\l"
    .string "became like the chaff of the summer\l"
    .string "threshingfloors; and the wind\l"
    .string "carried them away, that no place was\l"
    .string "found for them: and the stone that\l"
    .string "smote the image became a great\l"
    .string "mountain, and filled the whole\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_36::
    .string "This is the dream; and we will\n"
    .string "tell the interpretation thereof\l"
    .string "before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_37::
    .string "Thou, O king, art a king of kings:\n"
    .string "for the God of heaven hath given thee\l"
    .string "a kingdom, power, and strength, and\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_38::
    .string "And wheresoever the children of men\n"
    .string "dwell, the beasts of the field and\l"
    .string "the fowls of the heaven hath he\l"
    .string "given into thine hand, and hath made\l"
    .string "thee ruler over them all. Thou art\l"
    .string "this head of gold.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_39::
    .string "And after thee shall arise another\n"
    .string "kingdom inferior to thee, and another\l"
    .string "third kingdom of brass, which shall\l"
    .string "bear rule over all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_40::
    .string "And the fourth kingdom shall be\n"
    .string "strong as iron: forasmuch as iron\l"
    .string "breaketh in pieces and subdueth\l"
    .string "all things: and as iron that\l"
    .string "breaketh all these, shall it break\l"
    .string "in pieces and bruise.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_41::
    .string "And whereas thou sawest the feet and\n"
    .string "toes, part of potters’ clay, and\l"
    .string "part of iron, the kingdom shall be\l"
    .string "divided; but there shall be in it of\l"
    .string "the strength of the iron, forasmuch\l"
    .string "as thou sawest the iron mixed with\l"
    .string "miry clay.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_42::
    .string "And as the toes of the feet were\n"
    .string "part of iron, and part of clay, so\l"
    .string "the kingdom shall be partly\l"
    .string "strong, and partly broken.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_43::
    .string "And whereas thou sawest iron mixed\n"
    .string "with miry clay, they shall mingle\l"
    .string "themselves with the seed of men: but\l"
    .string "they shall not cleave one to\l"
    .string "another, even as iron is not mixed\l"
    .string "with clay.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_44::
    .string "And in the days of these kings\n"
    .string "shall the God of heaven set up a\l"
    .string "kingdom, which shall never be\l"
    .string "destroyed: and the kingdom shall\l"
    .string "not be left to other people, but it\l"
    .string "shall break in pieces and consume\l"
    .string "all these kingdoms, and it shall\l"
    .string "stand for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_45::
    .string "Forasmuch as thou sawest that the\n"
    .string "stone was cut out of the mountain\l"
    .string "without hands, and that it brake in\l"
    .string "pieces the iron, the brass, the clay,\l"
    .string "the silver, and the gold; the great\l"
    .string "God hath made known to the king what\l"
    .string "shall come to pass hereafter: and\l"
    .string "the dream is certain, and the\l"
    .string "interpretation thereof sure.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_46::
    .string "Then the king Nebuchadnezzar fell\n"
    .string "upon his face, and worshipped\l"
    .string "Daniel, and commanded that they\l"
    .string "should offer an oblation and sweet\l"
    .string "odours unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_47::
    .string "The king answered unto Daniel, and\n"
    .string "said, Of a truth it is, that your God\l"
    .string "is a God of gods, and a Lord of kings,\l"
    .string "and a revealer of secrets, seeing\l"
    .string "thou couldest reveal this secret.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_48::
    .string "Then the king made Daniel a great\n"
    .string "man, and gave him many great gifts,\l"
    .string "and made him ruler over the whole\l"
    .string "province of Babylon, and chief of\l"
    .string "the governors over all the wise men\l"
    .string "of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_2_49::
    .string "Then Daniel requested of the king,\n"
    .string "and he set Shadrach, Meshach, and\l"
    .string "Abednego, over the affairs of the\l"
    .string "province of Babylon: but Daniel sat\l"
    .string "in the gate of the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_1::
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king made an\n"
    .string "image of gold, whose height was\l"
    .string "threescore cubits, and the breadth\l"
    .string "thereof six cubits: he set it up in\l"
    .string "the plain of Dura, in the province\l"
    .string "of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_2::
    .string "Then Nebuchadnezzar the king sent\n"
    .string "to gather together the princes, the\l"
    .string "governors, and the captains, the\l"
    .string "judges, the treasurers, the\l"
    .string "counsellors, the sheriffs, and all\l"
    .string "the rulers of the provinces, to come\l"
    .string "to the dedication of the image which\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_3::
    .string "Then the princes, the governors,\n"
    .string "and captains, the judges, the\l"
    .string "treasurers, the counsellors, the\l"
    .string "sheriffs, and all the rulers of the\l"
    .string "provinces, were gathered together\l"
    .string "unto the dedication of the image that\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up;\l"
    .string "and they stood before the image that\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar had set up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_4::
    .string "Then an herald cried aloud, To you\n"
    .string "it is commanded, O people, nations,\l"
    .string "and languages,"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_5::
    .string "That at what time ye hear the sound\n"
    .string "of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut,\l"
    .string "psaltery, dulcimer, and all kinds\l"
    .string "of musick, ye fall down and worship\l"
    .string "the golden image that\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king hath set up:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_6::
    .string "And whoso falleth not down and\n"
    .string "worshippeth shall the same hour be\l"
    .string "cast into the midst of a burning\l"
    .string "fiery furnace$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_7::
    .string "Therefore at that time, when all\n"
    .string "the people heard the sound of the\l"
    .string "cornet, flute, harp, sackbut,\l"
    .string "psaltery, and all kinds of musick,\l"
    .string "all the people, the nations, and\l"
    .string "the languages, fell down and\l"
    .string "worshipped the golden image that\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_8::
    .string "Wherefore at that time certain\n"
    .string "Chaldeans came near, and accused the\l"
    .string "Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_9::
    .string "They spake and said to the king\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar, O king, live for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_10::
    .string "Thou, O king, hast made a decree,\n"
    .string "that every man that shall hear the\l"
    .string "sound of the cornet, flute, harp,\l"
    .string "sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer,\l"
    .string "and all kinds of musick, shall\l"
    .string "fall down and worship the golden\l"
    .string "image:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_11::
    .string "And whoso falleth not down and\n"
    .string "worshippeth, that he should be cast\l"
    .string "into the midst of a burning fiery\l"
    .string "furnace$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_12::
    .string "There are certain Jews whom thou\n"
    .string "hast set over the affairs of the\l"
    .string "province of Babylon, Shadrach,\l"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego; these men, O\l"
    .string "king, have not regarded thee: they\l"
    .string "serve not thy gods, nor worship the\l"
    .string "golden image which thou hast set up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_13::
    .string "Then Nebuchadnezzar in his rage and\n"
    .string "fury commanded to bring Shadrach,\l"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego. Then they\l"
    .string "brought these men before the king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_14::
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar spake and said unto\n"
    .string "them, Is it true, O Shadrach,\l"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego, do not ye\l"
    .string "serve my gods, nor worship the\l"
    .string "golden image which I have set up?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_15::
    .string "Now if ye be ready that at what time\n"
    .string "ye hear the sound of the cornet,\l"
    .string "flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery,\l"
    .string "and dulcimer, and all kinds of\l"
    .string "musick, ye fall down and worship\l"
    .string "the image which I have made; well:\l"
    .string "but if ye worship not, ye shall be\l"
    .string "cast the same hour into the midst of\l"
    .string "a burning fiery furnace; and who is\l"
    .string "that God that shall deliver you out\l"
    .string "of my hands?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_16::
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego,\n"
    .string "answered and said to the king, O\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar, we are not careful\l"
    .string "to answer thee in this matter$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_17::
    .string "If it be so, our God whom we serve is\n"
    .string "able to deliver us from the burning\l"
    .string "fiery furnace, and he will deliver\l"
    .string "us out of thine hand, O king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_18::
    .string "But if not, be it known unto thee, O\n"
    .string "king, that we will not serve thy\l"
    .string "gods, nor worship the golden image\l"
    .string "which thou hast set up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_19::
    .string "Then was Nebuchadnezzar full of\n"
    .string "fury, and the form of his visage was\l"
    .string "changed against Shadrach, Meshach,\l"
    .string "and Abednego: therefore he spake,\l"
    .string "and commanded that they should heat\l"
    .string "the furnace one seven times more than\l"
    .string "it was wont to be heated.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_20::
    .string "And he commanded the most mighty men\n"
    .string "that were in his army to bind\l"
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, and\l"
    .string "to cast them into the burning fiery\l"
    .string "furnace.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_21::
    .string "Then these men were bound in their\n"
    .string "coats, their hosen, and their hats,\l"
    .string "and their other garments, and were\l"
    .string "cast into the midst of the burning\l"
    .string "fiery furnace.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_22::
    .string "Therefore because the king’s\n"
    .string "commandment was urgent, and the\l"
    .string "furnace exceeding hot, the flames of\l"
    .string "the fire slew those men that took up\l"
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_23::
    .string "And these three men, Shadrach,\n"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego, fell down\l"
    .string "bound into the midst of the burning\l"
    .string "fiery furnace.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_24::
    .string "Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was\n"
    .string "astonied, and rose up in haste, and\l"
    .string "spake, and said unto his\l"
    .string "counsellors, Did not we cast three\l"
    .string "men bound into the midst of the fire?\l"
    .string "They answered and said unto the king,\l"
    .string "True, O king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_25::
    .string "He answered and said, Lo, I see four\n"
    .string "men loose, walking in the midst of\l"
    .string "the fire, and they have no hurt; and\l"
    .string "the form of the fourth is like the\l"
    .string "Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_26::
    .string "Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to\n"
    .string "the mouth of the burning fiery\l"
    .string "furnace, and spake, and said,\l"
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, ye\l"
    .string "servants of the most high God, come\l"
    .string "forth, and come hither. Then\l"
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, came\l"
    .string "forth of the midst of the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_27::
    .string "And the princes, governors, and\n"
    .string "captains, and the king’s\l"
    .string "counsellors, being gathered\l"
    .string "together, saw these men, upon whose\l"
    .string "bodies the fire had no power, nor was\l"
    .string "an hair of their head singed, neither\l"
    .string "were their coats changed, nor the\l"
    .string "smell of fire had passed on them.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_28::
    .string "Then Nebuchadnezzar spake, and\n"
    .string "said, Blessed be the God of\l"
    .string "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, who\l"
    .string "hath sent his angel, and delivered\l"
    .string "his servants that trusted in him, and\l"
    .string "have changed the king’s word, and\l"
    .string "yielded their bodies, that they\l"
    .string "might not serve nor worship any god,\l"
    .string "except their own God.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_29::
    .string "Therefore I make a decree, That\n"
    .string "every people, nation, and\l"
    .string "language, which speak any thing\l"
    .string "amiss against the God of Shadrach,\l"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego, shall be cut\l"
    .string "in pieces, and their houses shall\l"
    .string "be made a dunghill: because there is\l"
    .string "no other God that can deliver after\l"
    .string "this sort.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_3_30::
    .string "Then the king promoted Shadrach,\n"
    .string "Meshach, and Abednego, in the\l"
    .string "province of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_1::
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar the king, unto all\n"
    .string "people, nations, and languages,\l"
    .string "that dwell in all the earth; Peace\l"
    .string "be multiplied unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_2::
    .string "I thought it good to shew the signs\n"
    .string "and wonders that the high God hath\l"
    .string "wrought toward me.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_3::
    .string "How great are his signs! and how\n"
    .string "mighty are his wonders! his kingdom\l"
    .string "is an everlasting kingdom, and his\l"
    .string "dominion is from generation to\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_4::
    .string "I Nebuchadnezzar was at rest in mine\n"
    .string "house, and flourishing in my\l"
    .string "palace:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_5::
    .string "I saw a dream which made me afraid,\n"
    .string "and the thoughts upon my bed and the\l"
    .string "visions of my head troubled me$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_6::
    .string "Therefore made I a decree to bring\n"
    .string "in all the wise men of Babylon\l"
    .string "before me, that they might make known\l"
    .string "unto me the interpretation of the\l"
    .string "dream.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_7::
    .string "Then came in the magicians, the\n"
    .string "astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the\l"
    .string "soothsayers: and I told the dream\l"
    .string "before them; but they did not make\l"
    .string "known unto me the interpretation\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_8::
    .string "But at the last Daniel came in\n"
    .string "before me, whose name was\l"
    .string "Belteshazzar, according to the name\l"
    .string "of my God, and in whom is the spirit\l"
    .string "of the holy gods: and before him I\l"
    .string "told the dream, saying,"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_9::
    .string "O Belteshazzar, master of the\n"
    .string "magicians, because I know that the\l"
    .string "spirit of the holy gods is in thee,\l"
    .string "and no secret troubleth thee, tell\l"
    .string "me the visions of my dream that I\l"
    .string "have seen, and the interpretation\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_10::
    .string "Thus were the visions of mine head\n"
    .string "in my bed; I saw, and behold a tree\l"
    .string "in the midst of the earth, and the\l"
    .string "height thereof was great.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_11::
    .string "The tree grew, and was strong, and\n"
    .string "the height thereof reached unto\l"
    .string "heaven, and the sight thereof to the\l"
    .string "end of all the earth:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_12::
    .string "The leaves thereof were fair, and\n"
    .string "the fruit thereof much, and in it was\l"
    .string "meat for all: the beasts of the\l"
    .string "field had shadow under it, and the\l"
    .string "fowls of the heaven dwelt in the\l"
    .string "boughs thereof, and all flesh was\l"
    .string "fed of it$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_13::
    .string "I saw in the visions of my head upon\n"
    .string "my bed, and, behold, a watcher and an\l"
    .string "holy one came down from heaven;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_14::
    .string "He cried aloud, and said thus, Hew\n"
    .string "down the tree, and cut off his\l"
    .string "branches, shake off his leaves, and\l"
    .string "scatter his fruit: let the beasts\l"
    .string "get away from under it, and the fowls\l"
    .string "from his branches:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_15::
    .string "Nevertheless leave the stump of\n"
    .string "his roots in the earth, even with a\l"
    .string "band of iron and brass, in the tender\l"
    .string "grass of the field; and let it be\l"
    .string "wet with the dew of heaven, and let\l"
    .string "his portion be with the beasts in\l"
    .string "the grass of the earth:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_16::
    .string "Let his heart be changed from man’s,\n"
    .string "and let a beast’s heart be given\l"
    .string "unto him; and let seven times pass\l"
    .string "over him$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_17::
    .string "This matter is by the decree of the\n"
    .string "watchers, and the demand by the word\l"
    .string "of the holy ones: to the intent that\l"
    .string "the living may know that the most\l"
    .string "High ruleth in the kingdom of men,\l"
    .string "and giveth it to whomsoever he will,\l"
    .string "and setteth up over it the basest of\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_18::
    .string "This dream I king Nebuchadnezzar\n"
    .string "have seen. Now thou, O Belteshazzar,\l"
    .string "declare the interpretation thereof,\l"
    .string "forasmuch as all the wise men of my\l"
    .string "kingdom are not able to make known\l"
    .string "unto me the interpretation: but thou\l"
    .string "art able; for the spirit of the\l"
    .string "holy gods is in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_19::
    .string "Then Daniel, whose name was\n"
    .string "Belteshazzar, was astonied for one\l"
    .string "hour, and his thoughts troubled him.\l"
    .string "The king spake, and said,\l"
    .string "Belteshazzar, let not the dream, or\l"
    .string "the interpretation thereof, trouble\l"
    .string "thee. Belteshazzar answered and\l"
    .string "said, My lord, the dream be to them\l"
    .string "that hate thee, and the\l"
    .string "interpretation thereof to thine\l"
    .string "enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_20::
    .string "The tree that thou sawest, which\n"
    .string "grew, and was strong, whose height\l"
    .string "reached unto the heaven, and the\l"
    .string "sight thereof to all the earth;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_21::
    .string "Whose leaves were fair, and the\n"
    .string "fruit thereof much, and in it was\l"
    .string "meat for all; under which the beasts\l"
    .string "of the field dwelt, and upon whose\l"
    .string "branches the fowls of the heaven had\l"
    .string "their habitation:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_22::
    .string "It is thou, O king, that art grown\n"
    .string "and become strong: for thy greatness\l"
    .string "is grown, and reacheth unto heaven,\l"
    .string "and thy dominion to the end of the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_23::
    .string "And whereas the king saw a watcher\n"
    .string "and an holy one coming down from\l"
    .string "heaven, and saying, Hew the tree\l"
    .string "down, and destroy it; yet leave the\l"
    .string "stump of the roots thereof in the\l"
    .string "earth, even with a band of iron and\l"
    .string "brass, in the tender grass of the\l"
    .string "field; and let it be wet with the\l"
    .string "dew of heaven, and let his portion\l"
    .string "be with the beasts of the field,\l"
    .string "till seven times pass over him;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_24::
    .string "This is the interpretation, O king,\n"
    .string "and this is the decree of the most\l"
    .string "High, which is come upon my lord the\l"
    .string "king:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_25::
    .string "That they shall drive thee from\n"
    .string "men, and thy dwelling shall be\l"
    .string "with the beasts of the field, and\l"
    .string "they shall make thee to eat grass as\l"
    .string "oxen, and they shall wet thee with\l"
    .string "the dew of heaven, and seven times\l"
    .string "shall pass over thee, till thou\l"
    .string "know that the most High ruleth in\l"
    .string "the kingdom of men, and giveth it to\l"
    .string "whomsoever he will$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_26::
    .string "And whereas they commanded to leave\n"
    .string "the stump of the tree roots; thy\l"
    .string "kingdom shall be sure unto thee,\l"
    .string "after that thou shalt have known\l"
    .string "that the heavens do rule.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_27::
    .string "Wherefore, O king, let my counsel\n"
    .string "be acceptable unto thee, and break\l"
    .string "off thy sins by righteousness, and\l"
    .string "thine iniquities by shewing mercy to\l"
    .string "the poor; if it may be a lengthening\l"
    .string "of thy tranquillity.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_28::
    .string "All this came upon the king\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_29::
    .string "At the end of twelve months he\n"
    .string "walked in the palace of the kingdom\l"
    .string "of Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_30::
    .string "The king spake, and said, Is not\n"
    .string "this great Babylon, that I have\l"
    .string "built for the house of the kingdom\l"
    .string "by the might of my power, and for the\l"
    .string "honour of my majesty?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_31::
    .string "While the word was in the king’s\n"
    .string "mouth, there fell a voice from\l"
    .string "heaven, saying, O king\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar, to thee it is\l"
    .string "spoken; The kingdom is departed\l"
    .string "from thee$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_32::
    .string "And they shall drive thee from men,\n"
    .string "and thy dwelling shall be with the\l"
    .string "beasts of the field: they shall\l"
    .string "make thee to eat grass as oxen, and\l"
    .string "seven times shall pass over thee,\l"
    .string "until thou know that the most High\l"
    .string "ruleth in the kingdom of men, and\l"
    .string "giveth it to whomsoever he will.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_33::
    .string "The same hour was the thing\n"
    .string "fulfilled upon Nebuchadnezzar:\l"
    .string "and he was driven from men, and did\l"
    .string "eat grass as oxen, and his body was\l"
    .string "wet with the dew of heaven, till his\l"
    .string "hairs were grown like eagles’\l"
    .string "feathers, and his nails like birds’\l"
    .string "claws.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_34::
    .string "And at the end of the days I\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar lifted up mine eyes\l"
    .string "unto heaven, and mine understanding\l"
    .string "returned unto me, and I blessed the\l"
    .string "most High, and I praised and\l"
    .string "honoured him that liveth for ever,\l"
    .string "whose dominion is an everlasting\l"
    .string "dominion, and his kingdom is from\l"
    .string "generation to generation:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_35::
    .string "And all the inhabitants of the\n"
    .string "earth are reputed as nothing: and he\l"
    .string "doeth according to his will in the\l"
    .string "army of heaven, and among the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth: and none\l"
    .string "can stay his hand, or say unto him,\l"
    .string "What doest thou?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_36::
    .string "At the same time my reason returned\n"
    .string "unto me; and for the glory of my\l"
    .string "kingdom, mine honour and brightness\l"
    .string "returned unto me; and my\l"
    .string "counsellors and my lords sought\l"
    .string "unto me; and I was established in my\l"
    .string "kingdom, and excellent majesty was\l"
    .string "added unto me$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_4_37::
    .string "Now I Nebuchadnezzar praise and\n"
    .string "extol and honour the King of heaven,\l"
    .string "all whose works are truth, and his\l"
    .string "ways judgment: and those that walk\l"
    .string "in pride he is able to abase.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_1::
    .string "Belshazzar the king made a great\n"
    .string "feast to a thousand of his lords, and\l"
    .string "drank wine before the thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_2::
    .string "Belshazzar, whiles he tasted the\n"
    .string "wine, commanded to bring the golden\l"
    .string "and silver vessels which his father\l"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar had taken out of the\l"
    .string "temple which was in Jerusalem; that\l"
    .string "the king, and his princes, his wives,\l"
    .string "and his concubines, might drink\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_3::
    .string "Then they brought the golden\n"
    .string "vessels that were taken out of the\l"
    .string "temple of the house of God which was\l"
    .string "at Jerusalem; and the king, and his\l"
    .string "princes, his wives, and his\l"
    .string "concubines, drank in them.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_4::
    .string "They drank wine, and praised the\n"
    .string "gods of gold, and of silver, of\l"
    .string "brass, of iron, of wood, and of stone.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_5::
    .string "In the same hour came forth fingers\n"
    .string "of a man’s hand, and wrote over\l"
    .string "against the candlestick upon the\l"
    .string "plaister of the wall of the king’s\l"
    .string "palace: and the king saw the part of\l"
    .string "the hand that wrote.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_6::
    .string "Then the king’s countenance was\n"
    .string "changed, and his thoughts troubled\l"
    .string "him, so that the joints of his loins\l"
    .string "were loosed, and his knees smote one\l"
    .string "against another.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_7::
    .string "The king cried aloud to bring in\n"
    .string "the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and\l"
    .string "the soothsayers. And the king spake,\l"
    .string "and said to the wise men of Babylon,\l"
    .string "Whosoever shall read this writing,\l"
    .string "and shew me the interpretation\l"
    .string "thereof, shall be clothed with\l"
    .string "scarlet, and have a chain of gold\l"
    .string "about his neck, and shall be the\l"
    .string "third ruler in the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_8::
    .string "Then came in all the king’s wise\n"
    .string "men: but they could not read the\l"
    .string "writing, nor make known to the king\l"
    .string "the interpretation thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_9::
    .string "Then was king Belshazzar greatly\n"
    .string "troubled, and his countenance was\l"
    .string "changed in him, and his lords were\l"
    .string "astonied.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_10::
    .string "Now the queen by reason of the words\n"
    .string "of the king and his lords came into\l"
    .string "the banquet house: and the queen\l"
    .string "spake and said, O king, live for\l"
    .string "ever: let not thy thoughts trouble\l"
    .string "thee, nor let thy countenance be\l"
    .string "changed:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_11::
    .string "There is a man in thy kingdom, in\n"
    .string "whom is the spirit of the holy gods;\l"
    .string "and in the days of thy father light\l"
    .string "and understanding and wisdom, like\l"
    .string "the wisdom of the gods, was found in\l"
    .string "him; whom the king Nebuchadnezzar thy\l"
    .string "father, the king, I say, thy father,\l"
    .string "made master of the magicians,\l"
    .string "astrologers, Chaldeans, and\l"
    .string "soothsayers;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_12::
    .string "Forasmuch as an excellent spirit,\n"
    .string "and knowledge, and understanding,\l"
    .string "interpreting of dreams, and shewing\l"
    .string "of hard sentences, and dissolving of\l"
    .string "doubts, were found in the same\l"
    .string "Daniel, whom the king named\l"
    .string "Belteshazzar: now let Daniel be\l"
    .string "called, and he will shew the\l"
    .string "interpretation$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_13::
    .string "Then was Daniel brought in before\n"
    .string "the king. And the king spake and said\l"
    .string "unto Daniel, Art thou that Daniel,\l"
    .string "which art of the children of the\l"
    .string "captivity of Judah, whom the king my\l"
    .string "father brought out of Jewry?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_14::
    .string "I have even heard of thee, that the\n"
    .string "spirit of the gods is in thee, and\l"
    .string "that light and understanding and\l"
    .string "excellent wisdom is found in thee$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_15::
    .string "And now the wise men, the\n"
    .string "astrologers, have been brought in\l"
    .string "before me, that they should read\l"
    .string "this writing, and make known unto me\l"
    .string "the interpretation thereof: but they\l"
    .string "could not shew the interpretation\l"
    .string "of the thing:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_16::
    .string "And I have heard of thee, that thou\n"
    .string "canst make interpretations, and\l"
    .string "dissolve doubts: now if thou canst\l"
    .string "read the writing, and make known to\l"
    .string "me the interpretation thereof, thou\l"
    .string "shalt be clothed with scarlet, and\l"
    .string "have a chain of gold about thy neck,\l"
    .string "and shalt be the third ruler in the\l"
    .string "kingdom$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_17::
    .string "Then Daniel answered and said\n"
    .string "before the king, Let thy gifts be to\l"
    .string "thyself, and give thy rewards to\l"
    .string "another; yet I will read the writing\l"
    .string "unto the king, and make known to him\l"
    .string "the interpretation.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_18::
    .string "O thou king, the most high God gave\n"
    .string "Nebuchadnezzar thy father a kingdom,\l"
    .string "and majesty, and glory, and honour:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_19::
    .string "And for the majesty that he gave\n"
    .string "him, all people, nations, and\l"
    .string "languages, trembled and feared\l"
    .string "before him: whom he would he slew;\l"
    .string "and whom he would he kept alive;\l"
    .string "and whom he would he set up; and\l"
    .string "whom he would he put down$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_20::
    .string "But when his heart was lifted up,\n"
    .string "and his mind hardened in pride, he\l"
    .string "was deposed from his kingly throne,\l"
    .string "and they took his glory from him:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_21::
    .string "And he was driven from the sons of\n"
    .string "men; and his heart was made like the\l"
    .string "beasts, and his dwelling was with\l"
    .string "the wild asses: they fed him with\l"
    .string "grass like oxen, and his body was wet\l"
    .string "with the dew of heaven; till he knew\l"
    .string "that the most high God ruled in the\l"
    .string "kingdom of men, and that he\l"
    .string "appointeth over it whomsoever he\l"
    .string "will$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_22::
    .string "And thou his son, O Belshazzar,\n"
    .string "hast not humbled thine heart, though\l"
    .string "thou knewest all this;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_23::
    .string "But hast lifted up thyself\n"
    .string "against the Lord of heaven; and they\l"
    .string "have brought the vessels of his\l"
    .string "house before thee, and thou, and thy\l"
    .string "lords, thy wives, and thy concubines,\l"
    .string "have drunk wine in them; and thou\l"
    .string "hast praised the gods of silver, and\l"
    .string "gold, of brass, iron, wood, and\l"
    .string "stone, which see not, nor hear, nor\l"
    .string "know: and the God in whose hand thy\l"
    .string "breath is, and whose are all thy\l"
    .string "ways, hast thou not glorified:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_24::
    .string "Then was the part of the hand sent\n"
    .string "from him; and this writing was written$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_25::
    .string "And this is the writing that was\n"
    .string "written, MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_26::
    .string "This is the interpretation of the\n"
    .string "thing: MENE; God hath numbered thy\l"
    .string "kingdom, and finished it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_27::
    .string "TEKEL; Thou art weighed in the\n"
    .string "balances, and art found wanting.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_28::
    .string "PERES; Thy kingdom is divided, and\n"
    .string "given to the Medes and Persians.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_29::
    .string "Then commanded Belshazzar, and they\n"
    .string "clothed Daniel with scarlet, and\l"
    .string "put a chain of gold about his neck,\l"
    .string "and made a proclamation concerning\l"
    .string "him, that he should be the third\l"
    .string "ruler in the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_30::
    .string "In that night was Belshazzar the\n"
    .string "king of the Chaldeans slain.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_5_31::
    .string "And Darius the Median took the\n"
    .string "kingdom, being about threescore and\l"
    .string "two years old.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_1::
    .string "It pleased Darius to set over the\n"
    .string "kingdom an hundred and twenty\l"
    .string "princes, which should be over the\l"
    .string "whole kingdom;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_2::
    .string "And over these three presidents; of\n"
    .string "whom Daniel was first: that the\l"
    .string "princes might give accounts unto\l"
    .string "them, and the king should have no\l"
    .string "damage$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_3::
    .string "Then this Daniel was preferred\n"
    .string "above the presidents and princes,\l"
    .string "because an excellent spirit was in\l"
    .string "him; and the king thought to set him\l"
    .string "over the whole realm.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_4::
    .string "Then the presidents and princes\n"
    .string "sought to find occasion against\l"
    .string "Daniel concerning the kingdom; but\l"
    .string "they could find none occasion nor\l"
    .string "fault; forasmuch as he was\l"
    .string "faithful, neither was there any\l"
    .string "error or fault found in him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_5::
    .string "Then said these men, We shall not\n"
    .string "find any occasion against this\l"
    .string "Daniel, except we find it against\l"
    .string "him concerning the law of his God.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_6::
    .string "Then these presidents and princes\n"
    .string "assembled together to the king, and\l"
    .string "said thus unto him, King Darius,\l"
    .string "live for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_7::
    .string "All the presidents of the kingdom,\n"
    .string "the governors, and the princes, the\l"
    .string "counsellors, and the captains,\l"
    .string "have consulted together to\l"
    .string "establish a royal statute, and to\l"
    .string "make a firm decree, that whosoever\l"
    .string "shall ask a petition of any God or\l"
    .string "man for thirty days, save of thee, O\l"
    .string "king, he shall be cast into the den\l"
    .string "of lions.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_8::
    .string "Now, O king, establish the decree,\n"
    .string "and sign the writing, that it be not\l"
    .string "changed, according to the law of the\l"
    .string "Medes and Persians, which altereth\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_9::
    .string "Wherefore king Darius signed the\n"
    .string "writing and the decree.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_10::
    .string "Now when Daniel knew that the\n"
    .string "writing was signed, he went into his\l"
    .string "house; and his windows being open in\l"
    .string "his chamber toward Jerusalem, he\l"
    .string "kneeled upon his knees three times\l"
    .string "a day, and prayed, and gave thanks\l"
    .string "before his God, as he did aforetime.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_11::
    .string "Then these men assembled, and found\n"
    .string "Daniel praying and making\l"
    .string "supplication before his God.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_12::
    .string "Then they came near, and spake\n"
    .string "before the king concerning the\l"
    .string "king’s decree; Hast thou not signed a\l"
    .string "decree, that every man that shall\l"
    .string "ask a petition of any God or man\l"
    .string "within thirty days, save of thee, O\l"
    .string "king, shall be cast into the den of\l"
    .string "lions? The king answered and said,\l"
    .string "The thing is true, according to the\l"
    .string "law of the Medes and Persians, which\l"
    .string "altereth not.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_13::
    .string "Then answered they and said before\n"
    .string "the king, That Daniel, which is of\l"
    .string "the children of the captivity of\l"
    .string "Judah, regardeth not thee, O king,\l"
    .string "nor the decree that thou hast signed,\l"
    .string "but maketh his petition three times\l"
    .string "a day.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_14::
    .string "Then the king, when he heard these\n"
    .string "words, was sore displeased with\l"
    .string "himself, and set his heart on Daniel\l"
    .string "to deliver him: and he laboured\l"
    .string "till the going down of the sun to\l"
    .string "deliver him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_15::
    .string "Then these men assembled unto the\n"
    .string "king, and said unto the king, Know, O\l"
    .string "king, that the law of the Medes and\l"
    .string "Persians is, That no decree nor\l"
    .string "statute which the king establisheth\l"
    .string "may be changed.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_16::
    .string "Then the king commanded, and they\n"
    .string "brought Daniel, and cast him into\l"
    .string "the den of lions. Now the king spake\l"
    .string "and said unto Daniel, Thy God whom\l"
    .string "thou servest continually, he will\l"
    .string "deliver thee.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_17::
    .string "And a stone was brought, and laid\n"
    .string "upon the mouth of the den; and the\l"
    .string "king sealed it with his own signet,\l"
    .string "and with the signet of his lords;\l"
    .string "that the purpose might not be\l"
    .string "changed concerning Daniel.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_18::
    .string "Then the king went to his palace,\n"
    .string "and passed the night fasting:\l"
    .string "neither were instruments of musick\l"
    .string "brought before him: and his sleep\l"
    .string "went from him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_19::
    .string "Then the king arose very early in\n"
    .string "the morning, and went in haste unto\l"
    .string "the den of lions.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_20::
    .string "And when he came to the den, he cried\n"
    .string "with a lamentable voice unto\l"
    .string "Daniel: and the king spake and said\l"
    .string "to Daniel, O Daniel, servant of the\l"
    .string "living God, is thy God, whom thou\l"
    .string "servest continually, able to\l"
    .string "deliver thee from the lions?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_21::
    .string "Then said Daniel unto the king, O\n"
    .string "king, live for ever$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_22::
    .string "My God hath sent his angel, and hath\n"
    .string "shut the lions’ mouths, that they\l"
    .string "have not hurt me: forasmuch as before\l"
    .string "him innocency was found in me; and\l"
    .string "also before thee, O king, have I done\l"
    .string "no hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_23::
    .string "Then was the king exceedingly glad\n"
    .string "for him, and commanded that they\l"
    .string "should take Daniel up out of the den\l"
    .string " So Daniel was taken up out of the\l"
    .string "den, and no manner of hurt was found\l"
    .string "upon him, because he believed in his\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_24::
    .string "And the king commanded, and they\n"
    .string "brought those men which had accused\l"
    .string "Daniel, and they cast them into the\l"
    .string "den of lions, them, their children,\l"
    .string "and their wives; and the lions had\l"
    .string "the mastery of them, and brake all\l"
    .string "their bones in pieces or ever they\l"
    .string "came at the bottom of the den.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_25::
    .string "Then king Darius wrote unto all\n"
    .string "people, nations, and languages,\l"
    .string "that dwell in all the earth; Peace\l"
    .string "be multiplied unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_26::
    .string "I make a decree, That in every\n"
    .string "dominion of my kingdom men tremble\l"
    .string "and fear before the God of Daniel:\l"
    .string "for he is the living God, and\l"
    .string "stedfast for ever, and his kingdom\l"
    .string "that which shall not be destroyed,\l"
    .string "and his dominion shall be even unto\l"
    .string "the end.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_27::
    .string "He delivereth and rescueth, and he\n"
    .string "worketh signs and wonders in heaven\l"
    .string "and in earth, who hath delivered\l"
    .string "Daniel from the power of the lions.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_6_28::
    .string "So this Daniel prospered in the\n"
    .string "reign of Darius, and in the reign of\l"
    .string "Cyrus the Persian.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_1::
    .string "In the first year of Belshazzar\n"
    .string "king of Babylon Daniel had a dream\l"
    .string "and visions of his head upon his bed:\l"
    .string "then he wrote the dream, and told the\l"
    .string "sum of the matters.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_2::
    .string "Daniel spake and said, I saw in my\n"
    .string "vision by night, and, behold, the\l"
    .string "four winds of the heaven strove upon\l"
    .string "the great sea.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_3::
    .string "And four great beasts came up from\n"
    .string "the sea, diverse one from another.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_4::
    .string "The first was like a lion, and had\n"
    .string "eagle’s wings: I beheld till the\l"
    .string "wings thereof were plucked, and it\l"
    .string "was lifted up from the earth, and\l"
    .string "made stand upon the feet as a man,\l"
    .string "and a man’s heart was given to it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_5::
    .string "And behold another beast, a second,\n"
    .string "like to a bear, and it raised up\l"
    .string "itself on one side, and it had three\l"
    .string "ribs in the mouth of it between the\l"
    .string "teeth of it: and they said thus unto\l"
    .string "it, Arise, devour much flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_6::
    .string "After this I beheld, and lo\n"
    .string "another, like a leopard, which had\l"
    .string "upon the back of it four wings of a\l"
    .string "fowl; the beast had also four heads;\l"
    .string "and dominion was given to it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_7::
    .string "After this I saw in the night\n"
    .string "visions, and behold a fourth beast,\l"
    .string "dreadful and terrible, and strong\l"
    .string "exceedingly; and it had great iron\l"
    .string "teeth: it devoured and brake in\l"
    .string "pieces, and stamped the residue with\l"
    .string "the feet of it: and it was diverse\l"
    .string "from all the beasts that were\l"
    .string "before it; and it had ten horns.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_8::
    .string "I considered the horns, and,\n"
    .string "behold, there came up among them\l"
    .string "another little horn, before whom\l"
    .string "there were three of the first horns\l"
    .string "plucked up by the roots: and,\l"
    .string "behold, in this horn were eyes like\l"
    .string "the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking\l"
    .string "great things.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_9::
    .string "I beheld till the thrones were\n"
    .string "cast down, and the Ancient of days\l"
    .string "did sit, whose garment was white as\l"
    .string "snow, and the hair of his head like\l"
    .string "the pure wool: his throne was like\l"
    .string "the fiery flame, and his wheels as\l"
    .string "burning fire.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_10::
    .string "A fiery stream issued and came forth\n"
    .string "from before him: thousand thousands\l"
    .string "ministered unto him, and ten thousand\l"
    .string "times ten thousand stood before him:\l"
    .string "the judgment was set, and the books\l"
    .string "were opened.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_11::
    .string "I beheld then because of the voice\n"
    .string "of the great words which the horn\l"
    .string "spake: I beheld even till the\l"
    .string "beast was slain, and his body\l"
    .string "destroyed, and given to the burning\l"
    .string "flame.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_12::
    .string "As concerning the rest of the\n"
    .string "beasts, they had their dominion taken\l"
    .string "away: yet their lives were\l"
    .string "prolonged for a season and time.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_13::
    .string "I saw in the night visions, and,\n"
    .string "behold, one like the Son of man came\l"
    .string "with the clouds of heaven, and came\l"
    .string "to the Ancient of days, and they\l"
    .string "brought him near before him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_14::
    .string "And there was given him dominion,\n"
    .string "and glory, and a kingdom, that all\l"
    .string "people, nations, and languages,\l"
    .string "should serve him: his dominion is an\l"
    .string "everlasting dominion, which shall\l"
    .string "not pass away, and his kingdom that\l"
    .string "which shall not be destroyed.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_15::
    .string "I Daniel was grieved in my spirit\n"
    .string "in the midst of my body, and the\l"
    .string "visions of my head troubled me.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_16::
    .string "I came near unto one of them that\n"
    .string "stood by, and asked him the truth of\l"
    .string "all this. So he told me, and made me\l"
    .string "know the interpretation of the\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_17::
    .string "These great beasts, which are four,\n"
    .string "are four kings, which shall arise\l"
    .string "out of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_18::
    .string "But the saints of the most High\n"
    .string "shall take the kingdom, and possess\l"
    .string "the kingdom for ever, even for ever\l"
    .string "and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_19::
    .string "Then I would know the truth of the\n"
    .string "fourth beast, which was diverse from\l"
    .string "all the others, exceeding\l"
    .string "dreadful, whose teeth were of iron,\l"
    .string "and his nails of brass; which\l"
    .string "devoured, brake in pieces, and\l"
    .string "stamped the residue with his feet;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_20::
    .string "And of the ten horns that were in\n"
    .string "his head, and of the other which came\l"
    .string "up, and before whom three fell;\l"
    .string "even of that horn that had eyes, and a\l"
    .string "mouth that spake very great things,\l"
    .string "whose look was more stout than his\l"
    .string "fellows$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_21::
    .string "I beheld, and the same horn made war\n"
    .string "with the saints, and prevailed\l"
    .string "against them;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_22::
    .string "Until the Ancient of days came, and\n"
    .string "judgment was given to the saints of\l"
    .string "the most High; and the time came that\l"
    .string "the saints possessed the kingdom$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_23::
    .string "Thus he said, The fourth beast\n"
    .string "shall be the fourth kingdom upon\l"
    .string "earth, which shall be diverse from\l"
    .string "all kingdoms, and shall devour the\l"
    .string "whole earth, and shall tread it\l"
    .string "down, and break it in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_24::
    .string "And the ten horns out of this\n"
    .string "kingdom are ten kings that shall\l"
    .string "arise: and another shall rise after\l"
    .string "them; and he shall be diverse from\l"
    .string "the first, and he shall subdue three\l"
    .string "kings.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_25::
    .string "And he shall speak great words\n"
    .string "against the most High, and shall\l"
    .string "wear out the saints of the most High,\l"
    .string "and think to change times and laws:\l"
    .string "and they shall be given into his\l"
    .string "hand until a time and times and the\l"
    .string "dividing of time.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_26::
    .string "But the judgment shall sit, and\n"
    .string "they shall take away his dominion,\l"
    .string "to consume and to destroy it unto the\l"
    .string "end.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_27::
    .string "And the kingdom and dominion, and\n"
    .string "the greatness of the kingdom under\l"
    .string "the whole heaven, shall be given to\l"
    .string "the people of the saints of the\l"
    .string "most High, whose kingdom is an\l"
    .string "everlasting kingdom, and all\l"
    .string "dominions shall serve and obey him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_7_28::
    .string "Hitherto is the end of the matter.\n"
    .string "As for me Daniel, my cogitations\l"
    .string "much troubled me, and my countenance\l"
    .string "changed in me: but I kept the matter\l"
    .string "in my heart.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_1::
    .string "In the third year of the reign of\n"
    .string "king Belshazzar a vision appeared\l"
    .string "unto me, even unto me Daniel, after\l"
    .string "that which appeared unto me at the\l"
    .string "first.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_2::
    .string "And I saw in a vision; and it came to\n"
    .string "pass, when I saw, that I was at\l"
    .string "Shushan in the palace, which is in\l"
    .string "the province of Elam; and I saw in a\l"
    .string "vision, and I was by the river of\l"
    .string "Ulai.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_3::
    .string "Then I lifted up mine eyes, and\n"
    .string "saw, and, behold, there stood before\l"
    .string "the river a ram which had two horns:\l"
    .string "and the two horns were high; but one\l"
    .string "was higher than the other, and the\l"
    .string "higher came up last.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_4::
    .string "I saw the ram pushing westward, and\n"
    .string "northward, and southward; so that no\l"
    .string "beasts might stand before him,\l"
    .string "neither was there any that could\l"
    .string "deliver out of his hand; but he did\l"
    .string "according to his will, and became\l"
    .string "great.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_5::
    .string "And as I was considering, behold,\n"
    .string "an he goat came from the west on the\l"
    .string "face of the whole earth, and touched\l"
    .string "not the ground: and the goat had a\l"
    .string "notable horn between his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_6::
    .string "And he came to the ram that had two\n"
    .string "horns, which I had seen standing\l"
    .string "before the river, and ran unto him in\l"
    .string "the fury of his power.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_7::
    .string "And I saw him come close unto the\n"
    .string "ram, and he was moved with choler\l"
    .string "against him, and smote the ram, and\l"
    .string "brake his two horns: and there was no\l"
    .string "power in the ram to stand before him,\l"
    .string "but he cast him down to the ground,\l"
    .string "and stamped upon him: and there was\l"
    .string "none that could deliver the ram out\l"
    .string "of his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_8::
    .string "Therefore the he goat waxed very\n"
    .string "great: and when he was strong, the\l"
    .string "great horn was broken; and for it\l"
    .string "came up four notable ones toward\l"
    .string "the four winds of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_9::
    .string "And out of one of them came forth a\n"
    .string "little horn, which waxed exceeding\l"
    .string "great, toward the south, and toward\l"
    .string "the east, and toward the pleasant\l"
    .string "land.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_10::
    .string "And it waxed great, even to the host\n"
    .string "of heaven; and it cast down some of\l"
    .string "the host and of the stars to the\l"
    .string "ground, and stamped upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_11::
    .string "Yea, he magnified himself even to\n"
    .string "the prince of the host, and by him\l"
    .string "the daily sacrifice was taken away,\l"
    .string "and the place of the sanctuary was\l"
    .string "cast down.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_12::
    .string "And an host was given him against\n"
    .string "the daily sacrifice by reason of\l"
    .string "transgression, and it cast down the\l"
    .string "truth to the ground; and it\l"
    .string "practised, and prospered.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_13::
    .string "Then I heard one saint speaking,\n"
    .string "and another saint said unto that\l"
    .string "certain saint which spake, How long\l"
    .string "shall be the vision concerning the\l"
    .string "daily sacrifice, and the\l"
    .string "transgression of desolation, to give\l"
    .string "both the sanctuary and the host to be\l"
    .string "trodden under foot?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_14::
    .string "And he said unto me, Unto two\n"
    .string "thousand and three hundred days; then\l"
    .string "shall the sanctuary be cleansed$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, when I, even I\n"
    .string "Daniel, had seen the vision, and\l"
    .string "sought for the meaning, then,\l"
    .string "behold, there stood before me as the\l"
    .string "appearance of a man.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_16::
    .string "And I heard a man’s voice between\n"
    .string "the banks of Ulai, which called,\l"
    .string "and said, Gabriel, make this man to\l"
    .string "understand the vision.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_17::
    .string "So he came near where I stood: and\n"
    .string "when he came, I was afraid, and fell\l"
    .string "upon my face: but he said unto me,\l"
    .string "Understand, O son of man: for at the\l"
    .string "time of the end shall be the vision.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_18::
    .string "Now as he was speaking with me, I\n"
    .string "was in a deep sleep on my face\l"
    .string "toward the ground: but he touched me,\l"
    .string "and set me upright.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_19::
    .string "And he said, Behold, I will make\n"
    .string "thee know what shall be in the last\l"
    .string "end of the indignation: for at the\l"
    .string "time appointed the end shall be.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_20::
    .string "The ram which thou sawest having two\n"
    .string "horns are the kings of Media and\l"
    .string "Persia.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_21::
    .string "And the rough goat is the king of\n"
    .string "Grecia: and the great horn that is\l"
    .string "between his eyes is the first king.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_22::
    .string "Now that being broken, whereas four\n"
    .string "stood up for it, four kingdoms\l"
    .string "shall stand up out of the nation,\l"
    .string "but not in his power.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_23::
    .string "And in the latter time of their\n"
    .string "kingdom, when the transgressors are\l"
    .string "come to the full, a king of fierce\l"
    .string "countenance, and understanding dark\l"
    .string "sentences, shall stand up.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_24::
    .string "And his power shall be mighty, but\n"
    .string "not by his own power: and he shall\l"
    .string "destroy wonderfully, and shall\l"
    .string "prosper, and practise, and shall\l"
    .string "destroy the mighty and the holy\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_25::
    .string "And through his policy also he\n"
    .string "shall cause craft to prosper in\l"
    .string "his hand; and he shall magnify\l"
    .string "himself in his heart, and by peace\l"
    .string "shall destroy many: he shall also\l"
    .string "stand up against the Prince of\l"
    .string "princes; but he shall be broken\l"
    .string "without hand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_26::
    .string "And the vision of the evening and\n"
    .string "the morning which was told is true:\l"
    .string "wherefore shut thou up the vision;\l"
    .string "for it shall be for many days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_8_27::
    .string "And I Daniel fainted, and was sick\n"
    .string "certain days; afterward I rose up,\l"
    .string "and did the king’s business; and I\l"
    .string "was astonished at the vision, but\l"
    .string "none understood it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_1::
    .string "In the first year of Darius the son\n"
    .string "of Ahasuerus, of the seed of the\l"
    .string "Medes, which was made king over the\l"
    .string "realm of the Chaldeans;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_2::
    .string "In the first year of his reign I\n"
    .string "Daniel understood by books the\l"
    .string "number of the years, whereof the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD came to Jeremiah the\l"
    .string "prophet, that he would accomplish\l"
    .string "seventy years in the desolations of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_3::
    .string "And I set my face unto the Lord God,\n"
    .string "to seek by prayer and\l"
    .string "supplications, with fasting, and\l"
    .string "sackcloth, and ashes:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_4::
    .string "And I prayed unto the LORD my God,\n"
    .string "and made my confession, and said, O\l"
    .string "Lord, the great and dreadful God,\l"
    .string "keeping the covenant and mercy to\l"
    .string "them that love him, and to them that\l"
    .string "keep his commandments;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_5::
    .string "We have sinned, and have committed\n"
    .string "iniquity, and have done wickedly,\l"
    .string "and have rebelled, even by\l"
    .string "departing from thy precepts and\l"
    .string "from thy judgments:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_6::
    .string "Neither have we hearkened unto thy\n"
    .string "servants the prophets, which spake\l"
    .string "in thy name to our kings, our\l"
    .string "princes, and our fathers, and to all\l"
    .string "the people of the land$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_7::
    .string "O LORD, righteousness belongeth\n"
    .string "unto thee, but unto us confusion of\l"
    .string "faces, as at this day; to the men of\l"
    .string "Judah, and to the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and unto all Israel,\l"
    .string "that are near, and that are far off,\l"
    .string "through all the countries whither\l"
    .string "thou hast driven them, because of\l"
    .string "their trespass that they have\l"
    .string "trespassed against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_8::
    .string "O Lord, to us belongeth confusion\n"
    .string "of face, to our kings, to our\l"
    .string "princes, and to our fathers, because\l"
    .string "we have sinned against thee.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_9::
    .string "To the Lord our God belong mercies\n"
    .string "and forgivenesses, though we have\l"
    .string "rebelled against him;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_10::
    .string "Neither have we obeyed the voice of\n"
    .string "the LORD our God, to walk in his\l"
    .string "laws, which he set before us by his\l"
    .string "servants the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_11::
    .string "Yea, all Israel have transgressed\n"
    .string "thy law, even by departing, that\l"
    .string "they might not obey thy voice;\l"
    .string "therefore the curse is poured upon\l"
    .string "us, and the oath that is written in\l"
    .string "the law of Moses the servant of God,\l"
    .string "because we have sinned against him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_12::
    .string "And he hath confirmed his words,\n"
    .string "which he spake against us, and\l"
    .string "against our judges that judged us, by\l"
    .string "bringing upon us a great evil: for\l"
    .string "under the whole heaven hath not been\l"
    .string "done as hath been done upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_13::
    .string "As it is written in the law of\n"
    .string "Moses, all this evil is come upon\l"
    .string "us: yet made we not our prayer before\l"
    .string "the LORD our God, that we might turn\l"
    .string "from our iniquities, and understand\l"
    .string "thy truth.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_14::
    .string "Therefore hath the LORD watched\n"
    .string "upon the evil, and brought it upon\l"
    .string "us: for the LORD our God is righteous\l"
    .string "in all his works which he doeth: for\l"
    .string "we obeyed not his voice.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_15::
    .string "And now, O Lord our God, that hast\n"
    .string "brought thy people forth out of the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and\l"
    .string "hast gotten thee renown, as at this\l"
    .string "day; we have sinned, we have done\l"
    .string "wickedly.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_16::
    .string "O LORD, according to all thy\n"
    .string "righteousness, I beseech thee, let\l"
    .string "thine anger and thy fury be turned\l"
    .string "away from thy city Jerusalem, thy\l"
    .string "holy mountain: because for our sins,\l"
    .string "and for the iniquities of our\l"
    .string "fathers, Jerusalem and thy people\l"
    .string "are become a reproach to all that\l"
    .string "are about us.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_17::
    .string "Now therefore, O our God, hear the\n"
    .string "prayer of thy servant, and his\l"
    .string "supplications, and cause thy face\l"
    .string "to shine upon thy sanctuary that is\l"
    .string "desolate, for the Lord’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_18::
    .string "O my God, incline thine ear, and\n"
    .string "hear; open thine eyes, and behold\l"
    .string "our desolations, and the city which\l"
    .string "is called by thy name: for we do not\l"
    .string "present our supplications before\l"
    .string "thee for our righteousnesses, but for\l"
    .string "thy great mercies.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_19::
    .string "O Lord, hear; O Lord, forgive; O\n"
    .string "Lord, hearken and do; defer not, for\l"
    .string "thine own sake, O my God: for thy city\l"
    .string "and thy people are called by thy\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_20::
    .string "And whiles I was speaking, and\n"
    .string "praying, and confessing my sin and\l"
    .string "the sin of my people Israel, and\l"
    .string "presenting my supplication before\l"
    .string "the LORD my God for the holy\l"
    .string "mountain of my God;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_21::
    .string "Yea, whiles I was speaking in\n"
    .string "prayer, even the man Gabriel, whom I\l"
    .string "had seen in the vision at the\l"
    .string "beginning, being caused to fly\l"
    .string "swiftly, touched me about the time\l"
    .string "of the evening oblation$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_22::
    .string "And he informed me, and talked with\n"
    .string "me, and said, O Daniel, I am now come\l"
    .string "forth to give thee skill and\l"
    .string "understanding.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_23::
    .string "At the beginning of thy\n"
    .string "supplications the commandment came\l"
    .string "forth, and I am come to shew thee; for\l"
    .string "thou art greatly beloved: therefore\l"
    .string "understand the matter, and consider\l"
    .string "the vision.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_24::
    .string "Seventy weeks are determined upon\n"
    .string "thy people and upon thy holy city,\l"
    .string "to finish the transgression, and to\l"
    .string "make an end of sins, and to make\l"
    .string "reconciliation for iniquity, and to\l"
    .string "bring in everlasting righteousness,\l"
    .string "and to seal up the vision and\l"
    .string "prophecy, and to anoint the most\l"
    .string "Holy.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_25::
    .string "Know therefore and understand, that\n"
    .string "from the going forth of the\l"
    .string "commandment to restore and to build\l"
    .string "Jerusalem unto the Messiah the\l"
    .string "Prince shall be seven weeks, and\l"
    .string "threescore and two weeks: the street\l"
    .string "shall be built again, and the\l"
    .string "wall, even in troublous times.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_26::
    .string "And after threescore and two weeks\n"
    .string "shall Messiah be cut off, but not\l"
    .string "for himself: and the people of the\l"
    .string "prince that shall come shall\l"
    .string "destroy the city and the sanctuary;\l"
    .string "and the end thereof shall be with a\l"
    .string "flood, and unto the end of the war\l"
    .string "desolations are determined.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_9_27::
    .string "And he shall confirm the covenant\n"
    .string "with many for one week: and in the\l"
    .string "midst of the week he shall cause the\l"
    .string "sacrifice and the oblation to cease,\l"
    .string "and for the overspreading of\l"
    .string "abominations he shall make it\l"
    .string "desolate, even until the\l"
    .string "consummation, and that determined\l"
    .string "shall be poured upon the desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_1::
    .string "In the third year of Cyrus king of\n"
    .string "Persia a thing was revealed unto\l"
    .string "Daniel, whose name was called\l"
    .string "Belteshazzar; and the thing was\l"
    .string "true, but the time appointed was\l"
    .string "long: and he understood the thing,\l"
    .string "and had understanding of the vision.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_2::
    .string "In those days I Daniel was mourning\n"
    .string "three full weeks.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_3::
    .string "I ate no pleasant bread, neither\n"
    .string "came flesh nor wine in my mouth,\l"
    .string "neither did I anoint myself at all,\l"
    .string "till three whole weeks were\l"
    .string "fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_4::
    .string "And in the four and twentieth day of\n"
    .string "the first month, as I was by the side\l"
    .string "of the great river, which is\l"
    .string "Hiddekel;"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_5::
    .string "Then I lifted up mine eyes, and\n"
    .string "looked, and behold a certain man\l"
    .string "clothed in linen, whose loins were\l"
    .string "girded with fine gold of Uphaz:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_6::
    .string "His body also was like the beryl,\n"
    .string "and his face as the appearance of\l"
    .string "lightning, and his eyes as lamps of\l"
    .string "fire, and his arms and his feet like\l"
    .string "in colour to polished brass, and\l"
    .string "the voice of his words like the\l"
    .string "voice of a multitude$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_7::
    .string "And I Daniel alone saw the vision:\n"
    .string "for the men that were with me saw not\l"
    .string "the vision; but a great quaking fell\l"
    .string "upon them, so that they fled to hide\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_8::
    .string "Therefore I was left alone, and saw\n"
    .string "this great vision, and there remained\l"
    .string "no strength in me: for my comeliness\l"
    .string "was turned in me into corruption,\l"
    .string "and I retained no strength.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_9::
    .string "Yet heard I the voice of his words:\n"
    .string "and when I heard the voice of his\l"
    .string "words, then was I in a deep sleep on\l"
    .string "my face, and my face toward the\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_10::
    .string "And, behold, an hand touched me,\n"
    .string "which set me upon my knees and upon\l"
    .string "the palms of my hands.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_11::
    .string "And he said unto me, O Daniel, a man\n"
    .string "greatly beloved, understand the\l"
    .string "words that I speak unto thee, and\l"
    .string "stand upright: for unto thee am I now\l"
    .string "sent. And when he had spoken this\l"
    .string "word unto me, I stood trembling.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_12::
    .string "Then said he unto me, Fear not,\n"
    .string "Daniel: for from the first day that\l"
    .string "thou didst set thine heart to\l"
    .string "understand, and to chasten thyself\l"
    .string "before thy God, thy words were heard,\l"
    .string "and I am come for thy words.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_13::
    .string "But the prince of the kingdom of\n"
    .string "Persia withstood me one and twenty\l"
    .string "days: but, lo, Michael, one of the\l"
    .string "chief princes, came to help me; and\l"
    .string "I remained there with the kings of\l"
    .string "Persia.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_14::
    .string "Now I am come to make thee\n"
    .string "understand what shall befall thy\l"
    .string "people in the latter days: for yet\l"
    .string "the vision is for many days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_15::
    .string "And when he had spoken such words\n"
    .string "unto me, I set my face toward the\l"
    .string "ground, and I became dumb.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_16::
    .string "And, behold, one like the\n"
    .string "similitude of the sons of men\l"
    .string "touched my lips: then I opened my\l"
    .string "mouth, and spake, and said unto him\l"
    .string "that stood before me, O my lord, by\l"
    .string "the vision my sorrows are turned\l"
    .string "upon me, and I have retained no\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_17::
    .string "For how can the servant of this my\n"
    .string "lord talk with this my lord? for as\l"
    .string "for me, straightway there remained no\l"
    .string "strength in me, neither is there\l"
    .string "breath left in me.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_18::
    .string "Then there came again and touched me\n"
    .string "one like the appearance of a man,\l"
    .string "and he strengthened me,"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_19::
    .string "And said, O man greatly beloved,\n"
    .string "fear not: peace be unto thee, be\l"
    .string "strong, yea, be strong. And when he\l"
    .string "had spoken unto me, I was\l"
    .string "strengthened, and said, Let my lord\l"
    .string "speak; for thou hast strengthened me$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_20::
    .string "Then said he, Knowest thou wherefore\n"
    .string "I come unto thee? and now will I\l"
    .string "return to fight with the prince of\l"
    .string "Persia: and when I am gone forth, lo,\l"
    .string "the prince of Grecia shall come.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_10_21::
    .string "But I will shew thee that which is\n"
    .string "noted in the scripture of truth: and\l"
    .string "there is none that holdeth with me\l"
    .string "in these things, but Michael your\l"
    .string "prince.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_1::
    .string "Also I in the first year of Darius\n"
    .string "the Mede, even I, stood to confirm\l"
    .string "and to strengthen him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_2::
    .string "And now will I shew thee the truth.\n"
    .string "Behold, there shall stand up yet\l"
    .string "three kings in Persia; and the fourth\l"
    .string "shall be far richer than they all:\l"
    .string "and by his strength through his\l"
    .string "riches he shall stir up all\l"
    .string "against the realm of Grecia.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_3::
    .string "And a mighty king shall stand up,\n"
    .string "that shall rule with great\l"
    .string "dominion, and do according to his\l"
    .string "will.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_4::
    .string "And when he shall stand up, his\n"
    .string "kingdom shall be broken, and shall\l"
    .string "be divided toward the four winds of\l"
    .string "heaven; and not to his posterity,\l"
    .string "nor according to his dominion which\l"
    .string "he ruled: for his kingdom shall be\l"
    .string "plucked up, even for others beside\l"
    .string "those.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_5::
    .string "And the king of the south shall be\n"
    .string "strong, and one of his princes; and\l"
    .string "he shall be strong above him, and\l"
    .string "have dominion; his dominion shall\l"
    .string "be a great dominion.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_6::
    .string "And in the end of years they shall\n"
    .string "join themselves together; for the\l"
    .string "king’s daughter of the south shall\l"
    .string "come to the king of the north to make\l"
    .string "an agreement: but she shall not\l"
    .string "retain the power of the arm; neither\l"
    .string "shall he stand, nor his arm: but she\l"
    .string "shall be given up, and they that\l"
    .string "brought her, and he that begat her,\l"
    .string "and he that strengthened her in these\l"
    .string "times.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_7::
    .string "But out of a branch of her roots\n"
    .string "shall one stand up in his estate,\l"
    .string "which shall come with an army, and\l"
    .string "shall enter into the fortress of\l"
    .string "the king of the north, and shall\l"
    .string "deal against them, and shall\l"
    .string "prevail:"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_8::
    .string "And shall also carry captives\n"
    .string "into Egypt their gods, with their\l"
    .string "princes, and with their precious\l"
    .string "vessels of silver and of gold; and\l"
    .string "he shall continue more years than\l"
    .string "the king of the north$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_9::
    .string "So the king of the south shall come\n"
    .string "into his kingdom, and shall return\l"
    .string "into his own land.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_10::
    .string "But his sons shall be stirred up,\n"
    .string "and shall assemble a multitude of\l"
    .string "great forces: and one shall\l"
    .string "certainly come, and overflow, and\l"
    .string "pass through: then shall he return,\l"
    .string "and be stirred up, even to his\l"
    .string "fortress.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_11::
    .string "And the king of the south shall be\n"
    .string "moved with choler, and shall come\l"
    .string "forth and fight with him, even with\l"
    .string "the king of the north: and he shall\l"
    .string "set forth a great multitude; but the\l"
    .string "multitude shall be given into his\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_12::
    .string "And when he hath taken away the\n"
    .string "multitude, his heart shall be\l"
    .string "lifted up; and he shall cast down\l"
    .string "many ten thousands: but he shall not\l"
    .string "be strengthened by it.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_13::
    .string "For the king of the north shall\n"
    .string "return, and shall set forth a\l"
    .string "multitude greater than the former,\l"
    .string "and shall certainly come after\l"
    .string "certain years with a great army and\l"
    .string "with much riches.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_14::
    .string "And in those times there shall\n"
    .string "many stand up against the king of\l"
    .string "the south: also the robbers of thy\l"
    .string "people shall exalt themselves to\l"
    .string "establish the vision; but they\l"
    .string "shall fall.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_15::
    .string "So the king of the north shall\n"
    .string "come, and cast up a mount, and take\l"
    .string "the most fenced cities: and the arms\l"
    .string "of the south shall not withstand,\l"
    .string "neither his chosen people, neither\l"
    .string "shall there be any strength to\l"
    .string "withstand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_16::
    .string "But he that cometh against him\n"
    .string "shall do according to his own\l"
    .string "will, and none shall stand before\l"
    .string "him: and he shall stand in the\l"
    .string "glorious land, which by his hand\l"
    .string "shall be consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_17::
    .string "He shall also set his face to\n"
    .string "enter with the strength of his whole\l"
    .string "kingdom, and upright ones with him;\l"
    .string "thus shall he do: and he shall give\l"
    .string "him the daughter of women,\l"
    .string "corrupting her: but she shall not\l"
    .string "stand on his side, neither be for him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_18::
    .string "After this shall he turn his face\n"
    .string "unto the isles, and shall take\l"
    .string "many: but a prince for his own\l"
    .string "behalf shall cause the reproach\l"
    .string "offered by him to cease; without his\l"
    .string "own reproach he shall cause it to\l"
    .string "turn upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_19::
    .string "Then he shall turn his face toward\n"
    .string "the fort of his own land: but he\l"
    .string "shall stumble and fall, and not be\l"
    .string "found.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_20::
    .string "Then shall stand up in his estate\n"
    .string "a raiser of taxes in the glory of the\l"
    .string "kingdom: but within few days he\l"
    .string "shall be destroyed, neither in\l"
    .string "anger, nor in battle.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_21::
    .string "And in his estate shall stand up a\n"
    .string "vile person, to whom they shall\l"
    .string "not give the honour of the kingdom:\l"
    .string "but he shall come in peaceably,\l"
    .string "and obtain the kingdom by flatteries.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_22::
    .string "And with the arms of a flood shall\n"
    .string "they be overflown from before him,\l"
    .string "and shall be broken; yea, also the\l"
    .string "prince of the covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_23::
    .string "And after the league made with him\n"
    .string "he shall work deceitfully: for he\l"
    .string "shall come up, and shall become\l"
    .string "strong with a small people.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_24::
    .string "He shall enter peaceably even\n"
    .string "upon the fattest places of the\l"
    .string "province; and he shall do that which\l"
    .string "his fathers have not done, nor his\l"
    .string "fathers’ fathers; he shall scatter\l"
    .string "among them the prey, and spoil, and\l"
    .string "riches: yea, and he shall forecast\l"
    .string "his devices against the strong\l"
    .string "holds, even for a time.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_25::
    .string "And he shall stir up his power\n"
    .string "and his courage against the king of\l"
    .string "the south with a great army; and the\l"
    .string "king of the south shall be stirred\l"
    .string "up to battle with a very great and\l"
    .string "mighty army; but he shall not stand:\l"
    .string "for they shall forecast devices\l"
    .string "against him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_26::
    .string "Yea, they that feed of the portion\n"
    .string "of his meat shall destroy him, and\l"
    .string "his army shall overflow: and many\l"
    .string "shall fall down slain.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_27::
    .string "And both of these kings’ hearts\n"
    .string "shall be to do mischief, and they\l"
    .string "shall speak lies at one table; but\l"
    .string "it shall not prosper: for yet the\l"
    .string "end shall be at the time appointed.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_28::
    .string "Then shall he return into his land\n"
    .string "with great riches; and his heart\l"
    .string "shall be against the holy covenant;\l"
    .string "and he shall do exploits, and\l"
    .string "return to his own land.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_29::
    .string "At the time appointed he shall\n"
    .string "return, and come toward the south;\l"
    .string "but it shall not be as the former,\l"
    .string "or as the latter.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_30::
    .string "For the ships of Chittim shall\n"
    .string "come against him: therefore he\l"
    .string "shall be grieved, and return, and\l"
    .string "have indignation against the holy\l"
    .string "covenant: so shall he do; he shall\l"
    .string "even return, and have intelligence\l"
    .string "with them that forsake the holy\l"
    .string "covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_31::
    .string "And arms shall stand on his part,\n"
    .string "and they shall pollute the\l"
    .string "sanctuary of strength, and shall\l"
    .string "take away the daily sacrifice, and\l"
    .string "they shall place the abomination\l"
    .string "that maketh desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_32::
    .string "And such as do wickedly against the\n"
    .string "covenant shall he corrupt by\l"
    .string "flatteries: but the people that do\l"
    .string "know their God shall be strong, and\l"
    .string "do exploits.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_33::
    .string "And they that understand among the\n"
    .string "people shall instruct many: yet\l"
    .string "they shall fall by the sword, and\l"
    .string "by flame, by captivity, and by\l"
    .string "spoil, many days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_34::
    .string "Now when they shall fall, they\n"
    .string "shall be holpen with a little\l"
    .string "help: but many shall cleave to\l"
    .string "them with flatteries.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_35::
    .string "And some of them of understanding\n"
    .string "shall fall, to try them, and to\l"
    .string "purge, and to make them white, even\l"
    .string "to the time of the end: because it is\l"
    .string "yet for a time appointed.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_36::
    .string "And the king shall do according to\n"
    .string "his will; and he shall exalt\l"
    .string "himself, and magnify himself above\l"
    .string "every god, and shall speak\l"
    .string "marvellous things against the God\l"
    .string "of gods, and shall prosper till\l"
    .string "the indignation be accomplished:\l"
    .string "for that that is determined shall\l"
    .string "be done.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_37::
    .string "Neither shall he regard the God of\n"
    .string "his fathers, nor the desire of women,\l"
    .string "nor regard any god: for he shall\l"
    .string "magnify himself above all.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_38::
    .string "But in his estate shall he honour\n"
    .string "the God of forces: and a god whom his\l"
    .string "fathers knew not shall he honour\l"
    .string "with gold, and silver, and with\l"
    .string "precious stones, and pleasant\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_39::
    .string "Thus shall he do in the most strong\n"
    .string "holds with a strange god, whom he\l"
    .string "shall acknowledge and increase\l"
    .string "with glory: and he shall cause them\l"
    .string "to rule over many, and shall divide\l"
    .string "the land for gain.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_40::
    .string "And at the time of the end shall\n"
    .string "the king of the south push at him:\l"
    .string "and the king of the north shall come\l"
    .string "against him like a whirlwind, with\l"
    .string "chariots, and with horsemen, and with\l"
    .string "many ships; and he shall enter into\l"
    .string "the countries, and shall overflow\l"
    .string "and pass over.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_41::
    .string "He shall enter also into the\n"
    .string "glorious land, and many countries\l"
    .string "shall be overthrown: but these\l"
    .string "shall escape out of his hand, even\l"
    .string "Edom, and Moab, and the chief of the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_42::
    .string "He shall stretch forth his hand\n"
    .string "also upon the countries: and the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt shall not escape.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_43::
    .string "But he shall have power over the\n"
    .string "treasures of gold and of silver, and\l"
    .string "over all the precious things of\l"
    .string "Egypt: and the Libyans and the\l"
    .string "Ethiopians shall be at his steps.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_44::
    .string "But tidings out of the east and out\n"
    .string "of the north shall trouble him:\l"
    .string "therefore he shall go forth with\l"
    .string "great fury to destroy, and utterly\l"
    .string "to make away many.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_11_45::
    .string "And he shall plant the\n"
    .string "tabernacles of his palace between\l"
    .string "the seas in the glorious holy\l"
    .string "mountain; yet he shall come to his\l"
    .string "end, and none shall help him.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_1::
    .string "And at that time shall Michael\n"
    .string "stand up, the great prince which\l"
    .string "standeth for the children of thy\l"
    .string "people: and there shall be a time\l"
    .string "of trouble, such as never was since\l"
    .string "there was a nation even to that same\l"
    .string "time: and at that time thy people\l"
    .string "shall be delivered, every one that\l"
    .string "shall be found written in the book.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_2::
    .string "And many of them that sleep in the\n"
    .string "dust of the earth shall awake, some\l"
    .string "to everlasting life, and some to\l"
    .string "shame and everlasting contempt.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_3::
    .string "And they that be wise shall shine\n"
    .string "as the brightness of the firmament;\l"
    .string "and they that turn many to\l"
    .string "righteousness as the stars for ever\l"
    .string "and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_4::
    .string "But thou, O Daniel, shut up the\n"
    .string "words, and seal the book, even to the\l"
    .string "time of the end: many shall run to\l"
    .string "and fro, and knowledge shall be\l"
    .string "increased.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_5::
    .string "Then I Daniel looked, and, behold,\n"
    .string "there stood other two, the one on\l"
    .string "this side of the bank of the river,\l"
    .string "and the other on that side of the\l"
    .string "bank of the river.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_6::
    .string "And one said to the man clothed in\n"
    .string "linen, which was upon the waters of\l"
    .string "the river, How long shall it be to\l"
    .string "the end of these wonders?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_7::
    .string "And I heard the man clothed in\n"
    .string "linen, which was upon the waters of\l"
    .string "the river, when he held up his right\l"
    .string "hand and his left hand unto heaven,\l"
    .string "and sware by him that liveth for\l"
    .string "ever that it shall be for a time,\l"
    .string "times, and an half; and when he\l"
    .string "shall have accomplished to\l"
    .string "scatter the power of the holy\l"
    .string "people, all these things shall be\l"
    .string "finished$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_8::
    .string "And I heard, but I understood not:\n"
    .string "then said I, O my Lord, what shall\l"
    .string "be the end of these things?"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_9::
    .string "And he said, Go thy way, Daniel: for\n"
    .string "the words are closed up and sealed\l"
    .string "till the time of the end$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_10::
    .string "Many shall be purified, and made\n"
    .string "white, and tried; but the wicked\l"
    .string "shall do wickedly: and none of the\l"
    .string "wicked shall understand; but the\l"
    .string "wise shall understand.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_11::
    .string "And from the time that the daily\n"
    .string "sacrifice shall be taken away, and\l"
    .string "the abomination that maketh\l"
    .string "desolate set up, there shall be a\l"
    .string "thousand two hundred and ninety days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_12::
    .string "Blessed is he that waiteth, and\n"
    .string "cometh to the thousand three hundred\l"
    .string "and five and thirty days.$"
Bible_Text_Daniel_12_13::
    .string "But go thou thy way till the end\n"
    .string "be: for thou shalt rest, and stand in\l"
    .string "thy lot at the end of the days.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came unto\n"
    .string "Hosea, the son of Beeri, in the days\l"
    .string "of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and\l"
    .string "Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and in the\l"
    .string "days of Jeroboam the son of Joash,\l"
    .string "king of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_2::
    .string "The beginning of the word of the\n"
    .string "LORD by Hosea. And the LORD said to\l"
    .string "Hosea, Go, take unto thee a wife of\l"
    .string "whoredoms and children of whoredoms:\l"
    .string "for the land hath committed great\l"
    .string "whoredom, departing from the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_3::
    .string "So he went and took Gomer the\n"
    .string "daughter of Diblaim; which\l"
    .string "conceived, and bare him a son.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_4::
    .string "And the LORD said unto him, Call\n"
    .string "his name Jezreel; for yet a little\l"
    .string "while, and I will avenge the blood\l"
    .string "of Jezreel upon the house of Jehu,\l"
    .string "and will cause to cease the kingdom\l"
    .string "of the house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_5::
    .string "And it shall come to pass at that\n"
    .string "day, that I will break the bow of\l"
    .string "Israel, in the valley of Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_6::
    .string "And she conceived again, and bare a\n"
    .string "daughter. And God said unto him,\l"
    .string "Call her name Loruhamah: for I\l"
    .string "will no more have mercy upon the\l"
    .string "house of Israel; but I will\l"
    .string "utterly take them away.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_7::
    .string "But I will have mercy upon the\n"
    .string "house of Judah, and will save them\l"
    .string "by the LORD their God, and will not\l"
    .string "save them by bow, nor by sword, nor by\l"
    .string "battle, by horses, nor by horsemen.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_8::
    .string "Now when she had weaned Loruhamah,\n"
    .string "she conceived, and bare a son.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_9::
    .string "Then said God, Call his name\n"
    .string "Loammi: for ye are not my people,\l"
    .string "and I will not be your God.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_10::
    .string "Yet the number of the children of\n"
    .string "Israel shall be as the sand of the\l"
    .string "sea, which cannot be measured nor\l"
    .string "numbered; and it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, that in the place where it was\l"
    .string "said unto them, Ye are not my\l"
    .string "people, there it shall be said\l"
    .string "unto them, Ye are the sons of the\l"
    .string "living God.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_1_11::
    .string "Then shall the children of Judah\n"
    .string "and the children of Israel be\l"
    .string "gathered together, and appoint\l"
    .string "themselves one head, and they shall\l"
    .string "come up out of the land: for great\l"
    .string "shall be the day of Jezreel.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_1::
    .string "Say ye unto your brethren, Ammi; and\n"
    .string "to your sisters, Ruhamah.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_2::
    .string "Plead with your mother, plead: for\n"
    .string "she is not my wife, neither am I her\l"
    .string "husband: let her therefore put away\l"
    .string "her whoredoms out of her sight, and\l"
    .string "her adulteries from between her\l"
    .string "breasts;"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_3::
    .string "Lest I strip her naked, and set her\n"
    .string "as in the day that she was born, and\l"
    .string "make her as a wilderness, and set her\l"
    .string "like a dry land, and slay her with\l"
    .string "thirst$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_4::
    .string "And I will not have mercy upon her\n"
    .string "children; for they be the children\l"
    .string "of whoredoms.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_5::
    .string "For their mother hath played the\n"
    .string "harlot: she that conceived them hath\l"
    .string "done shamefully: for she said, I\l"
    .string "will go after my lovers, that give\l"
    .string "me my bread and my water, my wool and\l"
    .string "my flax, mine oil and my drink.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_6::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will hedge\n"
    .string "up thy way with thorns, and make a\l"
    .string "wall, that she shall not find her\l"
    .string "paths.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_7::
    .string "And she shall follow after her\n"
    .string "lovers, but she shall not overtake\l"
    .string "them; and she shall seek them, but\l"
    .string "shall not find them: then shall\l"
    .string "she say, I will go and return to my\l"
    .string "first husband; for then was it better\l"
    .string "with me than now.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_8::
    .string "For she did not know that I gave her\n"
    .string "corn, and wine, and oil, and\l"
    .string "multiplied her silver and gold,\l"
    .string "which they prepared for Baal.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_9::
    .string "Therefore will I return, and take\n"
    .string "away my corn in the time thereof, and\l"
    .string "my wine in the season thereof, and\l"
    .string "will recover my wool and my flax\l"
    .string "given to cover her nakedness.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_10::
    .string "And now will I discover her\n"
    .string "lewdness in the sight of her lovers,\l"
    .string "and none shall deliver her out of\l"
    .string "mine hand.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_11::
    .string "I will also cause all her mirth\n"
    .string "to cease, her feast days, her new\l"
    .string "moons, and her sabbaths, and all her\l"
    .string "solemn feasts.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_12::
    .string "And I will destroy her vines and\n"
    .string "her fig trees, whereof she hath said,\l"
    .string "These are my rewards that my lovers\l"
    .string "have given me: and I will make them\l"
    .string "a forest, and the beasts of the field\l"
    .string "shall eat them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_13::
    .string "And I will visit upon her the days\n"
    .string "of Baalim, wherein she burned\l"
    .string "incense to them, and she decked\l"
    .string "herself with her earrings and her\l"
    .string "jewels, and she went after her\l"
    .string "lovers, and forgat me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_14::
    .string "Therefore, behold, I will allure\n"
    .string "her, and bring her into the\l"
    .string "wilderness, and speak comfortably\l"
    .string "unto her.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_15::
    .string "And I will give her her vineyards\n"
    .string "from thence, and the valley of Achor\l"
    .string "for a door of hope: and she shall\l"
    .string "sing there, as in the days of her\l"
    .string "youth, and as in the day when she came\l"
    .string "up out of the land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_16::
    .string "And it shall be at that day, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, that thou shalt call me\l"
    .string "Ishi; and shalt call me no more\l"
    .string "Baali.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_17::
    .string "For I will take away the names of\n"
    .string "Baalim out of her mouth, and they\l"
    .string "shall no more be remembered by\l"
    .string "their name.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_18::
    .string "And in that day will I make a\n"
    .string "covenant for them with the beasts of\l"
    .string "the field and with the fowls of\l"
    .string "heaven, and with the creeping things\l"
    .string "of the ground: and I will break the\l"
    .string "bow and the sword and the battle out\l"
    .string "of the earth, and will make them to\l"
    .string "lie down safely.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_19::
    .string "And I will betroth thee unto me for\n"
    .string "ever; yea, I will betroth thee unto\l"
    .string "me in righteousness, and in judgment,\l"
    .string "and in lovingkindness, and in\l"
    .string "mercies.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_20::
    .string "I will even betroth thee unto me in\n"
    .string "faithfulness: and thou shalt know\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_21::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, I will hear, saith the LORD, I\l"
    .string "will hear the heavens, and they\l"
    .string "shall hear the earth;"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_22::
    .string "And the earth shall hear the corn,\n"
    .string "and the wine, and the oil; and they\l"
    .string "shall hear Jezreel$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_2_23::
    .string "And I will sow her unto me in the\n"
    .string "earth; and I will have mercy upon\l"
    .string "her that had not obtained mercy; and\l"
    .string "I will say to them which were not my\l"
    .string "people, Thou art my people; and\l"
    .string "they shall say, Thou art my God.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_3_1::
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, Go yet,\n"
    .string "love a woman beloved of her friend,\l"
    .string "yet an adulteress, according to the\l"
    .string "love of the LORD toward the children\l"
    .string "of Israel, who look to other gods,\l"
    .string "and love flagons of wine.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_3_2::
    .string "So I bought her to me for fifteen\n"
    .string "pieces of silver, and for an homer of\l"
    .string "barley, and an half homer of\l"
    .string "barley:"
Bible_Text_Hosea_3_3::
    .string "And I said unto her, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "abide for me many days; thou shalt\l"
    .string "not play the harlot, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt not be for another man: so\l"
    .string "will I also be for thee$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_3_4::
    .string "For the children of Israel shall\n"
    .string "abide many days without a king, and\l"
    .string "without a prince, and without a\l"
    .string "sacrifice, and without an image, and\l"
    .string "without an ephod, and without\l"
    .string "teraphim:"
Bible_Text_Hosea_3_5::
    .string "Afterward shall the children of\n"
    .string "Israel return, and seek the LORD\l"
    .string "their God, and David their king; and\l"
    .string "shall fear the LORD and his\l"
    .string "goodness in the latter days$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_1::
    .string "Hear the word of the LORD, ye\n"
    .string "children of Israel: for the LORD\l"
    .string "hath a controversy with the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the land, because\l"
    .string "there is no truth, nor mercy, nor\l"
    .string "knowledge of God in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_2::
    .string "By swearing, and lying, and\n"
    .string "killing, and stealing, and\l"
    .string "committing adultery, they break out,\l"
    .string "and blood toucheth blood.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_3::
    .string "Therefore shall the land mourn,\n"
    .string "and every one that dwelleth therein\l"
    .string "shall languish, with the beasts of\l"
    .string "the field, and with the fowls of\l"
    .string "heaven; yea, the fishes of the sea\l"
    .string "also shall be taken away.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_4::
    .string "Yet let no man strive, nor reprove\n"
    .string "another: for thy people are as they\l"
    .string "that strive with the priest.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_5::
    .string "Therefore shalt thou fall in the\n"
    .string "day, and the prophet also shall\l"
    .string "fall with thee in the night, and I\l"
    .string "will destroy thy mother.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_6::
    .string "My people are destroyed for lack\n"
    .string "of knowledge: because thou hast\l"
    .string "rejected knowledge, I will also\l"
    .string "reject thee, that thou shalt be no\l"
    .string "priest to me: seeing thou hast\l"
    .string "forgotten the law of thy God, I\l"
    .string "will also forget thy children.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_7::
    .string "As they were increased, so they\n"
    .string "sinned against me: therefore will I\l"
    .string "change their glory into shame.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_8::
    .string "They eat up the sin of my people,\n"
    .string "and they set their heart on their\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_9::
    .string "And there shall be, like people,\n"
    .string "like priest: and I will punish\l"
    .string "them for their ways, and reward them\l"
    .string "their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_10::
    .string "For they shall eat, and not have\n"
    .string "enough: they shall commit whoredom,\l"
    .string "and shall not increase: because\l"
    .string "they have left off to take heed to\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_11::
    .string "Whoredom and wine and new wine take\n"
    .string "away the heart.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_12::
    .string "My people ask counsel at their\n"
    .string "stocks, and their staff declareth\l"
    .string "unto them: for the spirit of\l"
    .string "whoredoms hath caused them to err,\l"
    .string "and they have gone a whoring from\l"
    .string "under their God.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_13::
    .string "They sacrifice upon the tops of\n"
    .string "the mountains, and burn incense upon\l"
    .string "the hills, under oaks and poplars\l"
    .string "and elms, because the shadow thereof\l"
    .string "is good: therefore your daughters\l"
    .string "shall commit whoredom, and your\l"
    .string "spouses shall commit adultery.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_14::
    .string "I will not punish your daughters\n"
    .string "when they commit whoredom, nor your\l"
    .string "spouses when they commit adultery:\l"
    .string "for themselves are separated with\l"
    .string "whores, and they sacrifice with\l"
    .string "harlots: therefore the people that\l"
    .string "doth not understand shall fall.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_15::
    .string "Though thou, Israel, play the\n"
    .string "harlot, yet let not Judah offend;\l"
    .string "and come not ye unto Gilgal, neither\l"
    .string "go ye up to Bethaven, nor swear, The\l"
    .string "LORD liveth.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_16::
    .string "For Israel slideth back as a\n"
    .string "backsliding heifer: now the LORD\l"
    .string "will feed them as a lamb in a large\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_17::
    .string "Ephraim is joined to idols: let\n"
    .string "him alone.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_18::
    .string "Their drink is sour: they have\n"
    .string "committed whoredom continually: her\l"
    .string "rulers with shame do love, Give ye.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_4_19::
    .string "The wind hath bound her up in her\n"
    .string "wings, and they shall be ashamed\l"
    .string "because of their sacrifices.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_1::
    .string "Hear ye this, O priests; and\n"
    .string "hearken, ye house of Israel; and\l"
    .string "give ye ear, O house of the king; for\l"
    .string "judgment is toward you, because ye\l"
    .string "have been a snare on Mizpah, and a\l"
    .string "net spread upon Tabor.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_2::
    .string "And the revolters are profound to\n"
    .string "make slaughter, though I have been a\l"
    .string "rebuker of them all.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_3::
    .string "I know Ephraim, and Israel is not\n"
    .string "hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, thou\l"
    .string "committest whoredom, and Israel is\l"
    .string "defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_4::
    .string "They will not frame their doings\n"
    .string "to turn unto their God: for the\l"
    .string "spirit of whoredoms is in the midst\l"
    .string "of them, and they have not known the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_5::
    .string "And the pride of Israel doth\n"
    .string "testify to his face: therefore\l"
    .string "shall Israel and Ephraim fall in\l"
    .string "their iniquity: Judah also shall\l"
    .string "fall with them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_6::
    .string "They shall go with their flocks\n"
    .string "and with their herds to seek the\l"
    .string "LORD; but they shall not find him;\l"
    .string "he hath withdrawn himself from them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_7::
    .string "They have dealt treacherously\n"
    .string "against the LORD: for they have\l"
    .string "begotten strange children: now\l"
    .string "shall a month devour them with\l"
    .string "their portions.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_8::
    .string "Blow ye the cornet in Gibeah, and\n"
    .string "the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud at\l"
    .string "Bethaven, after thee, O Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_9::
    .string "Ephraim shall be desolate in the\n"
    .string "day of rebuke: among the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel have I made known that which\l"
    .string "shall surely be.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_10::
    .string "The princes of Judah were like\n"
    .string "them that remove the bound: therefore\l"
    .string "I will pour out my wrath upon them\l"
    .string "like water.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_11::
    .string "Ephraim is oppressed and broken\n"
    .string "in judgment, because he willingly\l"
    .string "walked after the commandment.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_12::
    .string "Therefore will I be unto Ephraim\n"
    .string "as a moth, and to the house of Judah\l"
    .string "as rottenness.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_13::
    .string "When Ephraim saw his sickness, and\n"
    .string "Judah saw his wound, then went\l"
    .string "Ephraim to the Assyrian, and sent to\l"
    .string "king Jareb: yet could he not heal\l"
    .string "you, nor cure you of your wound.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_14::
    .string "For I will be unto Ephraim as a\n"
    .string "lion, and as a young lion to the\l"
    .string "house of Judah: I, even I, will tear\l"
    .string "and go away; I will take away, and\l"
    .string "none shall rescue him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_5_15::
    .string "I will go and return to my place,\n"
    .string "till they acknowledge their\l"
    .string "offence, and seek my face: in their\l"
    .string "affliction they will seek me early.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_1::
    .string "Come, and let us return unto the\n"
    .string "LORD: for he hath torn, and he will\l"
    .string "heal us; he hath smitten, and he\l"
    .string "will bind us up.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_2::
    .string "After two days will he revive us:\n"
    .string "in the third day he will raise us\l"
    .string "up, and we shall live in his sight.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_3::
    .string "Then shall we know, if we follow\n"
    .string "on to know the LORD: his going forth\l"
    .string "is prepared as the morning; and he\l"
    .string "shall come unto us as the rain, as\l"
    .string "the latter and former rain unto the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_4::
    .string "O Ephraim, what shall I do unto\n"
    .string "thee? O Judah, what shall I do unto\l"
    .string "thee? for your goodness is as a\l"
    .string "morning cloud, and as the early dew\l"
    .string "it goeth away.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_5::
    .string "Therefore have I hewed them by the\n"
    .string "prophets; I have slain them by the\l"
    .string "words of my mouth: and thy judgments\l"
    .string "are as the light that goeth forth.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_6::
    .string "For I desired mercy, and not\n"
    .string "sacrifice; and the knowledge of God\l"
    .string "more than burnt offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_7::
    .string "But they like men have transgressed\n"
    .string "the covenant: there have they dealt\l"
    .string "treacherously against me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_8::
    .string "Gilead is a city of them that work\n"
    .string "iniquity, and is polluted with\l"
    .string "blood.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_9::
    .string "And as troops of robbers wait for a\n"
    .string "man, so the company of priests\l"
    .string "murder in the way by consent: for\l"
    .string "they commit lewdness.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_10::
    .string "I have seen an horrible thing in\n"
    .string "the house of Israel: there is the\l"
    .string "whoredom of Ephraim, Israel is\l"
    .string "defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_6_11::
    .string "Also, O Judah, he hath set an\n"
    .string "harvest for thee, when I returned the\l"
    .string "captivity of my people.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_1::
    .string "When I would have healed Israel,\n"
    .string "then the iniquity of Ephraim was\l"
    .string "discovered, and the wickedness of\l"
    .string "Samaria: for they commit falsehood;\l"
    .string "and the thief cometh in, and the\l"
    .string "troop of robbers spoileth without.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_2::
    .string "And they consider not in their\n"
    .string "hearts that I remember all their\l"
    .string "wickedness: now their own doings have\l"
    .string "beset them about; they are before my\l"
    .string "face.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_3::
    .string "They make the king glad with their\n"
    .string "wickedness, and the princes with\l"
    .string "their lies.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_4::
    .string "They are all adulterers, as an\n"
    .string "oven heated by the baker, who ceaseth\l"
    .string "from raising after he hath kneaded\l"
    .string "the dough, until it be leavened.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_5::
    .string "In the day of our king the princes\n"
    .string "have made him sick with bottles of\l"
    .string "wine; he stretched out his hand with\l"
    .string "scorners.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_6::
    .string "For they have made ready their heart\n"
    .string "like an oven, whiles they lie in\l"
    .string "wait: their baker sleepeth all the\l"
    .string "night; in the morning it burneth as a\l"
    .string "flaming fire.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_7::
    .string "They are all hot as an oven, and\n"
    .string "have devoured their judges; all\l"
    .string "their kings are fallen: there is\l"
    .string "none among them that calleth unto\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_8::
    .string "Ephraim, he hath mixed himself\n"
    .string "among the people; Ephraim is a\l"
    .string "cake not turned.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_9::
    .string "Strangers have devoured his\n"
    .string "strength, and he knoweth it not: yea,\l"
    .string "gray hairs are here and there upon\l"
    .string "him, yet he knoweth not.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_10::
    .string "And the pride of Israel testifieth\n"
    .string "to his face: and they do not return to\l"
    .string "the LORD their God, nor seek him for\l"
    .string "all this.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_11::
    .string "Ephraim also is like a silly\n"
    .string "dove without heart: they call to\l"
    .string "Egypt, they go to Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_12::
    .string "When they shall go, I will spread\n"
    .string "my net upon them; I will bring them\l"
    .string "down as the fowls of the heaven; I\l"
    .string "will chastise them, as their\l"
    .string "congregation hath heard.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_13::
    .string "Woe unto them! for they have fled\n"
    .string "from me: destruction unto them!\l"
    .string "because they have transgressed\l"
    .string "against me: though I have redeemed\l"
    .string "them, yet they have spoken lies\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_14::
    .string "And they have not cried unto me with\n"
    .string "their heart, when they howled upon\l"
    .string "their beds: they assemble\l"
    .string "themselves for corn and wine, and\l"
    .string "they rebel against me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_15::
    .string "Though I have bound and\n"
    .string "strengthened their arms, yet do they\l"
    .string "imagine mischief against me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_7_16::
    .string "They return, but not to the most\n"
    .string "High: they are like a deceitful bow:\l"
    .string "their princes shall fall by the\l"
    .string "sword for the rage of their tongue:\l"
    .string "this shall be their derision in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_1::
    .string "Set the trumpet to thy mouth. He\n"
    .string "shall come as an eagle against the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD, because they have\l"
    .string "transgressed my covenant, and\l"
    .string "trespassed against my law.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_2::
    .string "Israel shall cry unto me, My God,\n"
    .string "we know thee.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_3::
    .string "Israel hath cast off the thing that\n"
    .string "is good: the enemy shall pursue him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_4::
    .string "They have set up kings, but not by\n"
    .string "me: they have made princes, and I\l"
    .string "knew it not: of their silver and\l"
    .string "their gold have they made them\l"
    .string "idols, that they may be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_5::
    .string "Thy calf, O Samaria, hath cast thee\n"
    .string "off; mine anger is kindled against\l"
    .string "them: how long will it be ere they\l"
    .string "attain to innocency?"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_6::
    .string "For from Israel was it also: the\n"
    .string "workman made it; therefore it is not\l"
    .string "God: but the calf of Samaria shall\l"
    .string "be broken in pieces$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_7::
    .string "For they have sown the wind, and\n"
    .string "they shall reap the whirlwind: it\l"
    .string "hath no stalk; the bud shall yield\l"
    .string "no meal: if so be it yield, the\l"
    .string "strangers shall swallow it up.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_8::
    .string "Israel is swallowed up: now\n"
    .string "shall they be among the Gentiles as\l"
    .string "a vessel wherein is no pleasure.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_9::
    .string "For they are gone up to Assyria, a\n"
    .string "wild ass alone by himself: Ephraim\l"
    .string "hath hired lovers.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_10::
    .string "Yea, though they have hired among\n"
    .string "the nations, now will I gather them,\l"
    .string "and they shall sorrow a little for\l"
    .string "the burden of the king of princes.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_11::
    .string "Because Ephraim hath made many\n"
    .string "altars to sin, altars shall be\l"
    .string "unto him to sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_12::
    .string "I have written to him the great\n"
    .string "things of my law, but they were\l"
    .string "counted as a strange thing.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_13::
    .string "They sacrifice flesh for the\n"
    .string "sacrifices of mine offerings, and eat\l"
    .string "it; but the LORD accepteth them not;\l"
    .string "now will he remember their\l"
    .string "iniquity, and visit their sins: they\l"
    .string "shall return to Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_8_14::
    .string "For Israel hath forgotten his\n"
    .string "Maker, and buildeth temples; and\l"
    .string "Judah hath multiplied fenced\l"
    .string "cities: but I will send a fire upon\l"
    .string "his cities, and it shall devour the\l"
    .string "palaces thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_1::
    .string "Rejoice not, O Israel, for joy, as\n"
    .string "other people: for thou hast gone a\l"
    .string "whoring from thy God, thou hast\l"
    .string "loved a reward upon every cornfloor.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_2::
    .string "The floor and the winepress shall\n"
    .string "not feed them, and the new wine\l"
    .string "shall fail in her.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_3::
    .string "They shall not dwell in the\n"
    .string "LORD’s land; but Ephraim shall\l"
    .string "return to Egypt, and they shall eat\l"
    .string "unclean things in Assyria.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_4::
    .string "They shall not offer wine\n"
    .string "offerings to the LORD, neither\l"
    .string "shall they be pleasing unto him:\l"
    .string "their sacrifices shall be unto them\l"
    .string "as the bread of mourners; all that\l"
    .string "eat thereof shall be polluted:\l"
    .string "for their bread for their soul\l"
    .string "shall not come into the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_5::
    .string "What will ye do in the solemn day,\n"
    .string "and in the day of the feast of the\l"
    .string "LORD?"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_6::
    .string "For, lo, they are gone because of\n"
    .string "destruction: Egypt shall gather\l"
    .string "them up, Memphis shall bury them:\l"
    .string "the pleasant places for their\l"
    .string "silver, nettles shall possess\l"
    .string "them: thorns shall be in their\l"
    .string "tabernacles$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_7::
    .string "The days of visitation are come, the\n"
    .string "days of recompence are come; Israel\l"
    .string "shall know it: the prophet is a\l"
    .string "fool, the spiritual man is mad, for\l"
    .string "the multitude of thine iniquity, and\l"
    .string "the great hatred.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_8::
    .string "The watchman of Ephraim was with my\n"
    .string "God: but the prophet is a snare of a\l"
    .string "fowler in all his ways, and hatred\l"
    .string "in the house of his God.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_9::
    .string "They have deeply corrupted\n"
    .string "themselves, as in the days of\l"
    .string "Gibeah: therefore he will remember\l"
    .string "their iniquity, he will visit their\l"
    .string "sins.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_10::
    .string "I found Israel like grapes in the\n"
    .string "wilderness; I saw your fathers as\l"
    .string "the firstripe in the fig tree at her\l"
    .string "first time: but they went to\l"
    .string "Baalpeor, and separated\l"
    .string "themselves unto that shame; and\l"
    .string "their abominations were according as\l"
    .string "they loved.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_11::
    .string "As for Ephraim, their glory shall\n"
    .string "fly away like a bird, from the\l"
    .string "birth, and from the womb, and from\l"
    .string "the conception.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_12::
    .string "Though they bring up their\n"
    .string "children, yet will I bereave them,\l"
    .string "that there shall not be a man left:\l"
    .string "yea, woe also to them when I depart\l"
    .string "from them!"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_13::
    .string "Ephraim, as I saw Tyrus, is\n"
    .string "planted in a pleasant place: but\l"
    .string "Ephraim shall bring forth his\l"
    .string "children to the murderer$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_14::
    .string "Give them, O LORD: what wilt thou\n"
    .string "give? give them a miscarrying womb\l"
    .string "and dry breasts.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_15::
    .string "All their wickedness is in\n"
    .string "Gilgal: for there I hated them: for\l"
    .string "the wickedness of their doings I\l"
    .string "will drive them out of mine house, I\l"
    .string "will love them no more: all their\l"
    .string "princes are revolters.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_16::
    .string "Ephraim is smitten, their root is\n"
    .string "dried up, they shall bear no fruit:\l"
    .string "yea, though they bring forth, yet\l"
    .string "will I slay even the beloved fruit\l"
    .string "of their womb.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_9_17::
    .string "My God will cast them away, because\n"
    .string "they did not hearken unto him: and\l"
    .string "they shall be wanderers among the\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_1::
    .string "Israel is an empty vine, he\n"
    .string "bringeth forth fruit unto himself:\l"
    .string "according to the multitude of his\l"
    .string "fruit he hath increased the altars;\l"
    .string "according to the goodness of his\l"
    .string "land they have made goodly images.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_2::
    .string "Their heart is divided; now shall\n"
    .string "they be found faulty: he shall\l"
    .string "break down their altars, he shall\l"
    .string "spoil their images.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_3::
    .string "For now they shall say, We have no\n"
    .string "king, because we feared not the LORD;\l"
    .string "what then should a king do to us?"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_4::
    .string "They have spoken words, swearing\n"
    .string "falsely in making a covenant: thus\l"
    .string "judgment springeth up as hemlock\l"
    .string "in the furrows of the field$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_5::
    .string "The inhabitants of Samaria shall\n"
    .string "fear because of the calves of\l"
    .string "Bethaven: for the people thereof\l"
    .string "shall mourn over it, and the\l"
    .string "priests thereof that rejoiced on it,\l"
    .string "for the glory thereof, because it is\l"
    .string "departed from it.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_6::
    .string "It shall be also carried unto\n"
    .string "Assyria for a present to king Jareb:\l"
    .string "Ephraim shall receive shame, and\l"
    .string "Israel shall be ashamed of his own\l"
    .string "counsel.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_7::
    .string "As for Samaria, her king is cut off\n"
    .string "as the foam upon the water.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_8::
    .string "The high places also of Aven, the\n"
    .string "sin of Israel, shall be destroyed:\l"
    .string "the thorn and the thistle shall\l"
    .string "come up on their altars; and they\l"
    .string "shall say to the mountains, Cover\l"
    .string "us; and to the hills, Fall on us.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_9::
    .string "O Israel, thou hast sinned from the\n"
    .string "days of Gibeah: there they stood: the\l"
    .string "battle in Gibeah against the\l"
    .string "children of iniquity did not\l"
    .string "overtake them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_10::
    .string "It is in my desire that I should\n"
    .string "chastise them; and the people\l"
    .string "shall be gathered against them,\l"
    .string "when they shall bind themselves in\l"
    .string "their two furrows.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_11::
    .string "And Ephraim is as an heifer that is\n"
    .string "taught, and loveth to tread out the\l"
    .string "corn; but I passed over upon her\l"
    .string "fair neck: I will make Ephraim to\l"
    .string "ride; Judah shall plow, and Jacob\l"
    .string "shall break his clods.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_12::
    .string "Sow to yourselves in righteousness,\n"
    .string "reap in mercy; break up your\l"
    .string "fallow ground: for it is time to\l"
    .string "seek the LORD, till he come and rain\l"
    .string "righteousness upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_13::
    .string "Ye have plowed wickedness, ye have\n"
    .string "reaped iniquity; ye have eaten the\l"
    .string "fruit of lies: because thou didst\l"
    .string "trust in thy way, in the multitude of\l"
    .string "thy mighty men.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_14::
    .string "Therefore shall a tumult arise\n"
    .string "among thy people, and all thy\l"
    .string "fortresses shall be spoiled, as\l"
    .string "Shalman spoiled Betharbel in the\l"
    .string "day of battle: the mother was dashed\l"
    .string "in pieces upon her children.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_10_15::
    .string "So shall Bethel do unto you\n"
    .string "because of your great wickedness: in\l"
    .string "a morning shall the king of Israel\l"
    .string "utterly be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_1::
    .string "When Israel was a child, then I\n"
    .string "loved him, and called my son out of\l"
    .string "Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_2::
    .string "As they called them, so they went\n"
    .string "from them: they sacrificed unto\l"
    .string "Baalim, and burned incense to graven\l"
    .string "images.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_3::
    .string "I taught Ephraim also to go, taking\n"
    .string "them by their arms; but they knew not\l"
    .string "that I healed them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_4::
    .string "I drew them with cords of a man, with\n"
    .string "bands of love: and I was to them as\l"
    .string "they that take off the yoke on their\l"
    .string "jaws, and I laid meat unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_5::
    .string "He shall not return into the land\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and the Assyrian shall be\l"
    .string "his king, because they refused to\l"
    .string "return.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_6::
    .string "And the sword shall abide on his\n"
    .string "cities, and shall consume his\l"
    .string "branches, and devour them, because of\l"
    .string "their own counsels.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_7::
    .string "And my people are bent to\n"
    .string "backsliding from me: though they\l"
    .string "called them to the most High, none\l"
    .string "at all would exalt him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_8::
    .string "How shall I give thee up,\n"
    .string "Ephraim? how shall I deliver thee,\l"
    .string "Israel? how shall I make thee as\l"
    .string "Admah? how shall I set thee as\l"
    .string "Zeboim? mine heart is turned within\l"
    .string "me, my repentings are kindled\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_9::
    .string "I will not execute the fierceness\n"
    .string "of mine anger, I will not return to\l"
    .string "destroy Ephraim: for I am God, and\l"
    .string "not man; the Holy One in the midst of\l"
    .string "thee: and I will not enter into the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_10::
    .string "They shall walk after the LORD: he\n"
    .string "shall roar like a lion: when he\l"
    .string "shall roar, then the children\l"
    .string "shall tremble from the west.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_11::
    .string "They shall tremble as a bird out\n"
    .string "of Egypt, and as a dove out of the\l"
    .string "land of Assyria: and I will place\l"
    .string "them in their houses, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_11_12::
    .string "Ephraim compasseth me about with\n"
    .string "lies, and the house of Israel with\l"
    .string "deceit: but Judah yet ruleth with\l"
    .string "God, and is faithful with the saints.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_1::
    .string "Ephraim feedeth on wind, and\n"
    .string "followeth after the east wind: he\l"
    .string "daily increaseth lies and\l"
    .string "desolation; and they do make a\l"
    .string "covenant with the Assyrians, and oil\l"
    .string "is carried into Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_2::
    .string "The LORD hath also a controversy\n"
    .string "with Judah, and will punish Jacob\l"
    .string "according to his ways; according to\l"
    .string "his doings will he recompense him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_3::
    .string "He took his brother by the heel in\n"
    .string "the womb, and by his strength he had\l"
    .string "power with God:"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_4::
    .string "Yea, he had power over the angel,\n"
    .string "and prevailed: he wept, and made\l"
    .string "supplication unto him: he found him\l"
    .string "in Bethel, and there he spake with\l"
    .string "us;"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_5::
    .string "Even the LORD God of hosts; the LORD\n"
    .string "is his memorial$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_6::
    .string "Therefore turn thou to thy God:\n"
    .string "keep mercy and judgment and wait on\l"
    .string "thy God continually.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_7::
    .string "He is a merchant, the balances of\n"
    .string "deceit are in his hand: he loveth to\l"
    .string "oppress.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_8::
    .string "And Ephraim said, Yet I am become\n"
    .string "rich, I have found me out substance:\l"
    .string "in all my labours they shall find\l"
    .string "none iniquity in me that were sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_9::
    .string "And I that am the LORD thy God from\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt will yet make\l"
    .string "thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in\l"
    .string "the days of the solemn feast.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_10::
    .string "I have also spoken by the\n"
    .string "prophets, and I have multiplied\l"
    .string "visions, and used similitudes, by\l"
    .string "the ministry of the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_11::
    .string "Is there iniquity in Gilead?\n"
    .string "surely they are vanity: they\l"
    .string "sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yea,\l"
    .string "their altars are as heaps in the\l"
    .string "furrows of the fields.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_12::
    .string "And Jacob fled into the country of\n"
    .string "Syria, and Israel served for a wife,\l"
    .string "and for a wife he kept sheep.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_13::
    .string "And by a prophet the LORD brought\n"
    .string "Israel out of Egypt, and by a\l"
    .string "prophet was he preserved.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_12_14::
    .string "Ephraim provoked him to anger most\n"
    .string "bitterly: therefore shall he leave\l"
    .string "his blood upon him, and his\l"
    .string "reproach shall his LORD return\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_1::
    .string "When Ephraim spake trembling, he\n"
    .string "exalted himself in Israel; but when\l"
    .string "he offended in Baal, he died.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_2::
    .string "And now they sin more and more, and\n"
    .string "have made them molten images of\l"
    .string "their silver, and idols according\l"
    .string "to their own understanding, all of\l"
    .string "it the work of the craftsmen: they\l"
    .string "say of them, Let the men that\l"
    .string "sacrifice kiss the calves.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_3::
    .string "Therefore they shall be as the\n"
    .string "morning cloud and as the early dew\l"
    .string "that passeth away, as the chaff that\l"
    .string "is driven with the whirlwind out of\l"
    .string "the floor, and as the smoke out of\l"
    .string "the chimney.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_4::
    .string "Yet I am the LORD thy God from the\n"
    .string "land of Egypt, and thou shalt know\l"
    .string "no god but me: for there is no saviour\l"
    .string "beside me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_5::
    .string "I did know thee in the wilderness,\n"
    .string "in the land of great drought.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_6::
    .string "According to their pasture, so were\n"
    .string "they filled; they were filled, and\l"
    .string "their heart was exalted; therefore\l"
    .string "have they forgotten me.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_7::
    .string "Therefore I will be unto them as a\n"
    .string "lion: as a leopard by the way will\l"
    .string "I observe them:"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_8::
    .string "I will meet them as a bear that is\n"
    .string "bereaved of her whelps, and will\l"
    .string "rend the caul of their heart, and\l"
    .string "there will I devour them like a\l"
    .string "lion: the wild beast shall tear them$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_9::
    .string "O Israel, thou hast destroyed\n"
    .string "thyself; but in me is thine help.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_10::
    .string "I will be thy king: where is any\n"
    .string "other that may save thee in all thy\l"
    .string "cities? and thy judges of whom thou\l"
    .string "saidst, Give me a king and princes?"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_11::
    .string "I gave thee a king in mine anger, and\n"
    .string "took him away in my wrath$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_12::
    .string "The iniquity of Ephraim is bound\n"
    .string "up; his sin is hid.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_13::
    .string "The sorrows of a travailing woman\n"
    .string "shall come upon him: he is an\l"
    .string "unwise son; for he should not stay\l"
    .string "long in the place of the breaking\l"
    .string "forth of children.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_14::
    .string "I will ransom them from the power\n"
    .string "of the grave; I will redeem them\l"
    .string "from death: O death, I will be thy\l"
    .string "plagues; O grave, I will be thy\l"
    .string "destruction: repentance shall be\l"
    .string "hid from mine eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_15::
    .string "Though he be fruitful among his\n"
    .string "brethren, an east wind shall come,\l"
    .string "the wind of the LORD shall come up\l"
    .string "from the wilderness, and his spring\l"
    .string "shall become dry, and his fountain\l"
    .string "shall be dried up: he shall\l"
    .string "spoil the treasure of all\l"
    .string "pleasant vessels.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_13_16::
    .string "Samaria shall become desolate;\n"
    .string "for she hath rebelled against her\l"
    .string "God: they shall fall by the sword:\l"
    .string "their infants shall be dashed in\l"
    .string "pieces, and their women with child\l"
    .string "shall be ripped up.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_1::
    .string "O israel, return unto the LORD thy\n"
    .string "God; for thou hast fallen by thine\l"
    .string "iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_2::
    .string "Take with you words, and turn to the\n"
    .string "LORD: say unto him, Take away all\l"
    .string "iniquity, and receive us graciously:\l"
    .string "so will we render the calves of our\l"
    .string "lips.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_3::
    .string "Asshur shall not save us; we will\n"
    .string "not ride upon horses: neither will\l"
    .string "we say any more to the work of our\l"
    .string "hands, Ye are our gods: for in thee\l"
    .string "the fatherless findeth mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_4::
    .string "I will heal their backsliding, I\n"
    .string "will love them freely: for mine\l"
    .string "anger is turned away from him.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_5::
    .string "I will be as the dew unto Israel:\n"
    .string "he shall grow as the lily, and cast\l"
    .string "forth his roots as Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_6::
    .string "His branches shall spread, and his\n"
    .string "beauty shall be as the olive tree,\l"
    .string "and his smell as Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_7::
    .string "They that dwell under his shadow\n"
    .string "shall return; they shall revive as\l"
    .string "the corn, and grow as the vine: the\l"
    .string "scent thereof shall be as the wine\l"
    .string "of Lebanon.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_8::
    .string "Ephraim shall say, What have I to\n"
    .string "do any more with idols? I have heard\l"
    .string "him, and observed him: I am like a\l"
    .string "green fir tree. From me is thy fruit\l"
    .string "found.$"
Bible_Text_Hosea_14_9::
    .string "Who is wise, and he shall\n"
    .string "understand these things? prudent,\l"
    .string "and he shall know them? for the ways\l"
    .string "of the LORD are right, and the just\l"
    .string "shall walk in them: but the\l"
    .string "transgressors shall fall therein.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came to\n"
    .string "Joel the son of Pethuel.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_2::
    .string "Hear this, ye old men, and give ear,\n"
    .string "all ye inhabitants of the land.\l"
    .string "Hath this been in your days, or even\l"
    .string "in the days of your fathers?$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_3::
    .string "Tell ye your children of it, and\n"
    .string "let your children tell their\l"
    .string "children, and their children\l"
    .string "another generation.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_4::
    .string "That which the palmerworm hath\n"
    .string "left hath the locust eaten; and that\l"
    .string "which the locust hath left hath the\l"
    .string "cankerworm eaten; and that which the\l"
    .string "cankerworm hath left hath the\l"
    .string "caterpiller eaten.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_5::
    .string "Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and\n"
    .string "howl, all ye drinkers of wine,\l"
    .string "because of the new wine; for it is cut\l"
    .string "off from your mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_6::
    .string "For a nation is come up upon my\n"
    .string "land, strong, and without number,\l"
    .string "whose teeth are the teeth of a lion,\l"
    .string "and he hath the cheek teeth of a\l"
    .string "great lion.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_7::
    .string "He hath laid my vine waste, and\n"
    .string "barked my fig tree: he hath made it\l"
    .string "clean bare, and cast it away; the\l"
    .string "branches thereof are made white.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_8::
    .string "Lament like a virgin girded with\n"
    .string "sackcloth for the husband of her\l"
    .string "youth.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_9::
    .string "The meat offering and the drink\n"
    .string "offering is cut off from the house of\l"
    .string "the LORD; the priests, the LORD’s\l"
    .string "ministers, mourn.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_10::
    .string "The field is wasted, the land\n"
    .string "mourneth; for the corn is wasted: the\l"
    .string "new wine is dried up, the oil\l"
    .string "languisheth.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_11::
    .string "Be ye ashamed, O ye husbandmen;\n"
    .string "howl, O ye vinedressers, for the\l"
    .string "wheat and for the barley; because\l"
    .string "the harvest of the field is\l"
    .string "perished.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_12::
    .string "The vine is dried up, and the fig\n"
    .string "tree languisheth; the pomegranate\l"
    .string "tree, the palm tree also, and the\l"
    .string "apple tree, even all the trees of\l"
    .string "the field, are withered: because joy\l"
    .string "is withered away from the sons of men.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_13::
    .string "Gird yourselves, and lament, ye\n"
    .string "priests: howl, ye ministers of the\l"
    .string "altar: come, lie all night in\l"
    .string "sackcloth, ye ministers of my God:\l"
    .string "for the meat offering and the drink\l"
    .string "offering is withholden from the\l"
    .string "house of your God.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_14::
    .string "Sanctify ye a fast, call a solemn\n"
    .string "assembly, gather the elders and\l"
    .string "all the inhabitants of the land\l"
    .string "into the house of the LORD your God,\l"
    .string "and cry unto the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_15::
    .string "Alas for the day! for the day of the\n"
    .string "LORD is at hand, and as a destruction\l"
    .string "from the Almighty shall it come$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_16::
    .string "Is not the meat cut off before our\n"
    .string "eyes, yea, joy and gladness from the\l"
    .string "house of our God?"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_17::
    .string "The seed is rotten under their\n"
    .string "clods, the garners are laid\l"
    .string "desolate, the barns are broken down;\l"
    .string "for the corn is withered$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_18::
    .string "How do the beasts groan! the herds\n"
    .string "of cattle are perplexed, because\l"
    .string "they have no pasture; yea, the\l"
    .string "flocks of sheep are made desolate.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_19::
    .string "O LORD, to thee will I cry: for the\n"
    .string "fire hath devoured the pastures of\l"
    .string "the wilderness, and the flame hath\l"
    .string "burned all the trees of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_1_20::
    .string "The beasts of the field cry also\n"
    .string "unto thee: for the rivers of waters\l"
    .string "are dried up, and the fire hath\l"
    .string "devoured the pastures of the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_1::
    .string "Blow ye the trumpet in Zion, and\n"
    .string "sound an alarm in my holy mountain:\l"
    .string "let all the inhabitants of the land\l"
    .string "tremble: for the day of the LORD\l"
    .string "cometh, for it is nigh at hand;"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_2::
    .string "A day of darkness and of\n"
    .string "gloominess, a day of clouds and of\l"
    .string "thick darkness, as the morning\l"
    .string "spread upon the mountains: a great\l"
    .string "people and a strong; there hath not\l"
    .string "been ever the like, neither shall\l"
    .string "be any more after it, even to the\l"
    .string "years of many generations$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_3::
    .string "A fire devoureth before them; and\n"
    .string "behind them a flame burneth: the\l"
    .string "land is as the garden of Eden before\l"
    .string "them, and behind them a desolate\l"
    .string "wilderness; yea, and nothing shall\l"
    .string "escape them.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_4::
    .string "The appearance of them is as the\n"
    .string "appearance of horses; and as\l"
    .string "horsemen, so shall they run.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_5::
    .string "Like the noise of chariots on the\n"
    .string "tops of mountains shall they\l"
    .string "leap, like the noise of a flame of\l"
    .string "fire that devoureth the stubble, as\l"
    .string "a strong people set in battle\l"
    .string "array.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_6::
    .string "Before their face the people\n"
    .string "shall be much pained: all faces\l"
    .string "shall gather blackness.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_7::
    .string "They shall run like mighty men;\n"
    .string "they shall climb the wall like\l"
    .string "men of war; and they shall march\l"
    .string "every one on his ways, and they\l"
    .string "shall not break their ranks:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_8::
    .string "Neither shall one thrust another;\n"
    .string "they shall walk every one in his\l"
    .string "path: and when they fall upon the\l"
    .string "sword, they shall not be wounded$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_9::
    .string "They shall run to and fro in the\n"
    .string "city; they shall run upon the\l"
    .string "wall, they shall climb up upon\l"
    .string "the houses; they shall enter in at\l"
    .string "the windows like a thief.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_10::
    .string "The earth shall quake before them;\n"
    .string "the heavens shall tremble: the sun\l"
    .string "and the moon shall be dark, and the\l"
    .string "stars shall withdraw their shining:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_11::
    .string "And the LORD shall utter his voice\n"
    .string "before his army: for his camp is very\l"
    .string "great: for he is strong that\l"
    .string "executeth his word: for the day of\l"
    .string "the LORD is great and very terrible;\l"
    .string "and who can abide it?"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_12::
    .string "Therefore also now, saith the LORD,\n"
    .string "turn ye even to me with all your\l"
    .string "heart, and with fasting, and with\l"
    .string "weeping, and with mourning:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_13::
    .string "And rend your heart, and not your\n"
    .string "garments, and turn unto the LORD your\l"
    .string "God: for he is gracious and\l"
    .string "merciful, slow to anger, and of\l"
    .string "great kindness, and repenteth him of\l"
    .string "the evil$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_14::
    .string "Who knoweth if he will return and\n"
    .string "repent, and leave a blessing behind\l"
    .string "him; even a meat offering and a drink\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD your God?"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_15::
    .string "Blow the trumpet in Zion, sanctify\n"
    .string "a fast, call a solemn assembly:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_16::
    .string "Gather the people, sanctify the\n"
    .string "congregation, assemble the elders,\l"
    .string "gather the children, and those that\l"
    .string "suck the breasts: let the bridegroom\l"
    .string "go forth of his chamber, and the\l"
    .string "bride out of her closet$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_17::
    .string "Let the priests, the ministers of\n"
    .string "the LORD, weep between the porch and\l"
    .string "the altar, and let them say, Spare\l"
    .string "thy people, O LORD, and give not\l"
    .string "thine heritage to reproach, that the\l"
    .string "heathen should rule over them:\l"
    .string "wherefore should they say among the\l"
    .string "people, Where is their God?"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_18::
    .string "Then will the LORD be jealous for\n"
    .string "his land, and pity his people$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_19::
    .string "Yea, the LORD will answer and say\n"
    .string "unto his people, Behold, I will\l"
    .string "send you corn, and wine, and oil, and\l"
    .string "ye shall be satisfied therewith:\l"
    .string "and I will no more make you a\l"
    .string "reproach among the heathen:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_20::
    .string "But I will remove far off from you\n"
    .string "the northern army, and will drive\l"
    .string "him into a land barren and desolate,\l"
    .string "with his face toward the east sea,\l"
    .string "and his hinder part toward the\l"
    .string "utmost sea, and his stink shall come\l"
    .string "up, and his ill savour shall come\l"
    .string "up, because he hath done great things$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_21::
    .string "Fear not, O land; be glad and\n"
    .string "rejoice: for the LORD will do great\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_22::
    .string "Be not afraid, ye beasts of the\n"
    .string "field: for the pastures of the\l"
    .string "wilderness do spring, for the tree\l"
    .string "beareth her fruit, the fig tree and\l"
    .string "the vine do yield their strength.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_23::
    .string "Be glad then, ye children of Zion,\n"
    .string "and rejoice in the LORD your God: for\l"
    .string "he hath given you the former rain\l"
    .string "moderately, and he will cause to\l"
    .string "come down for you the rain, the\l"
    .string "former rain, and the latter rain in\l"
    .string "the first month.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_24::
    .string "And the floors shall be full of\n"
    .string "wheat, and the vats shall overflow\l"
    .string "with wine and oil.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_25::
    .string "And I will restore to you the years\n"
    .string "that the locust hath eaten, the\l"
    .string "cankerworm, and the caterpiller,\l"
    .string "and the palmerworm, my great army\l"
    .string "which I sent among you.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_26::
    .string "And ye shall eat in plenty, and be\n"
    .string "satisfied, and praise the name of\l"
    .string "the LORD your God, that hath dealt\l"
    .string "wondrously with you: and my people\l"
    .string "shall never be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_27::
    .string "And ye shall know that I am in the\n"
    .string "midst of Israel, and that I am the\l"
    .string "LORD your God, and none else: and my\l"
    .string "people shall never be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_28::
    .string "And it shall come to pass\n"
    .string "afterward, that I will pour out my\l"
    .string "spirit upon all flesh; and your\l"
    .string "sons and your daughters shall\l"
    .string "prophesy, your old men shall dream\l"
    .string "dreams, your young men shall see\l"
    .string "visions:"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_29::
    .string "And also upon the servants and\n"
    .string "upon the handmaids in those days\l"
    .string "will I pour out my spirit$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_30::
    .string "And I will shew wonders in the\n"
    .string "heavens and in the earth, blood, and\l"
    .string "fire, and pillars of smoke.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_31::
    .string "The sun shall be turned into\n"
    .string "darkness, and the moon into blood,\l"
    .string "before the great and terrible day of\l"
    .string "the LORD come.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_2_32::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "whosoever shall call on the name\l"
    .string "of the LORD shall be delivered: for\l"
    .string "in mount Zion and in Jerusalem\l"
    .string "shall be deliverance, as the LORD\l"
    .string "hath said, and in the remnant whom\l"
    .string "the LORD shall call.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_1::
    .string "For, behold, in those days, and in\n"
    .string "that time, when I shall bring again\l"
    .string "the captivity of Judah and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_2::
    .string "I will also gather all nations,\n"
    .string "and will bring them down into the\l"
    .string "valley of Jehoshaphat, and will\l"
    .string "plead with them there for my\l"
    .string "people and for my heritage Israel,\l"
    .string "whom they have scattered among the\l"
    .string "nations, and parted my land$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_3::
    .string "And they have cast lots for my\n"
    .string "people; and have given a boy for an\l"
    .string "harlot, and sold a girl for wine,\l"
    .string "that they might drink.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_4::
    .string "Yea, and what have ye to do with me,\n"
    .string "O Tyre, and Zidon, and all the\l"
    .string "coasts of Palestine? will ye render\l"
    .string "me a recompence? and if ye\l"
    .string "recompense me, swiftly and\l"
    .string "speedily will I return your\l"
    .string "recompence upon your own head;"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_5::
    .string "Because ye have taken my silver and\n"
    .string "my gold, and have carried into your\l"
    .string "temples my goodly pleasant\l"
    .string "things:"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_6::
    .string "The children also of Judah and the\n"
    .string "children of Jerusalem have ye sold\l"
    .string "unto the Grecians, that ye might\l"
    .string "remove them far from their border$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_7::
    .string "Behold, I will raise them out of\n"
    .string "the place whither ye have sold\l"
    .string "them, and will return your\l"
    .string "recompence upon your own head:"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_8::
    .string "And I will sell your sons and\n"
    .string "your daughters into the hand of the\l"
    .string "children of Judah, and they shall\l"
    .string "sell them to the Sabeans, to a\l"
    .string "people far off: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken it$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_9::
    .string "Proclaim ye this among the\n"
    .string "Gentiles; Prepare war, wake up the\l"
    .string "mighty men, let all the men of war\l"
    .string "draw near; let them come up:"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_10::
    .string "Beat your plowshares into swords\n"
    .string "and your pruninghooks into spears:\l"
    .string "let the weak say, I am strong$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_11::
    .string "Assemble yourselves, and come,\n"
    .string "all ye heathen, and gather\l"
    .string "yourselves together round about:\l"
    .string "thither cause thy mighty ones to come\l"
    .string "down, O LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_12::
    .string "Let the heathen be wakened, and come\n"
    .string "up to the valley of Jehoshaphat:\l"
    .string "for there will I sit to judge all\l"
    .string "the heathen round about.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_13::
    .string "Put ye in the sickle, for the\n"
    .string "harvest is ripe: come, get you down;\l"
    .string "for the press is full, the fats\l"
    .string "overflow; for their wickedness is\l"
    .string "great.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_14::
    .string "Multitudes, multitudes in the\n"
    .string "valley of decision: for the day of\l"
    .string "the LORD is near in the valley of\l"
    .string "decision.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_15::
    .string "The sun and the moon shall be\n"
    .string "darkened, and the stars shall\l"
    .string "withdraw their shining.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_16::
    .string "The LORD also shall roar out of\n"
    .string "Zion, and utter his voice from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and the heavens and the\l"
    .string "earth shall shake: but the LORD\l"
    .string "will be the hope of his people,\l"
    .string "and the strength of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_17::
    .string "So shall ye know that I am the LORD\n"
    .string "your God dwelling in Zion, my holy\l"
    .string "mountain: then shall Jerusalem be\l"
    .string "holy, and there shall no strangers\l"
    .string "pass through her any more.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_18::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the mountains shall drop\l"
    .string "down new wine, and the hills shall\l"
    .string "flow with milk, and all the rivers\l"
    .string "of Judah shall flow with waters,\l"
    .string "and a fountain shall come forth out\l"
    .string "of the house of the LORD, and shall\l"
    .string "water the valley of Shittim.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_19::
    .string "Egypt shall be a desolation, and\n"
    .string "Edom shall be a desolate\l"
    .string "wilderness, for the violence\l"
    .string "against the children of Judah,\l"
    .string "because they have shed innocent\l"
    .string "blood in their land.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_20::
    .string "But Judah shall dwell for ever,\n"
    .string "and Jerusalem from generation to\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Joel_3_21::
    .string "For I will cleanse their blood\n"
    .string "that I have not cleansed: for the\l"
    .string "LORD dwelleth in Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_1::
    .string "The words of Amos, who was among the\n"
    .string "herdmen of Tekoa, which he saw\l"
    .string "concerning Israel in the days of\l"
    .string "Uzziah king of Judah, and in the days\l"
    .string "of Jeroboam the son of Joash king of\l"
    .string "Israel, two years before the\l"
    .string "earthquake.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_2::
    .string "And he said, The LORD will roar\n"
    .string "from Zion, and utter his voice from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and the habitations of\l"
    .string "the shepherds shall mourn, and the\l"
    .string "top of Carmel shall wither.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_3::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Damascus, and for\l"
    .string "four, I will not turn away the\l"
    .string "punishment thereof; because they\l"
    .string "have threshed Gilead with threshing\l"
    .string "instruments of iron:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_4::
    .string "But I will send a fire into the\n"
    .string "house of Hazael, which shall devour\l"
    .string "the palaces of Benhadad$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_5::
    .string "I will break also the bar of\n"
    .string "Damascus, and cut off the inhabitant\l"
    .string "from the plain of Aven, and him that\l"
    .string "holdeth the sceptre from the house\l"
    .string "of Eden: and the people of Syria\l"
    .string "shall go into captivity unto Kir,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_6::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Gaza, and for four,\l"
    .string "I will not turn away the punishment\l"
    .string "thereof; because they carried away\l"
    .string "captive the whole captivity, to\l"
    .string "deliver them up to Edom:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_7::
    .string "But I will send a fire on the wall\n"
    .string "of Gaza, which shall devour the\l"
    .string "palaces thereof:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_8::
    .string "And I will cut off the inhabitant\n"
    .string "from Ashdod, and him that holdeth\l"
    .string "the sceptre from Ashkelon, and I\l"
    .string "will turn mine hand against Ekron:\l"
    .string "and the remnant of the Philistines\l"
    .string "shall perish, saith the Lord GOD$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_9::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Tyrus, and for\l"
    .string "four, I will not turn away the\l"
    .string "punishment thereof; because they\l"
    .string "delivered up the whole captivity\l"
    .string "to Edom, and remembered not the\l"
    .string "brotherly covenant:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_10::
    .string "But I will send a fire on the wall\n"
    .string "of Tyrus, which shall devour the\l"
    .string "palaces thereof$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_11::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Edom, and for four,\l"
    .string "I will not turn away the punishment\l"
    .string "thereof; because he did pursue his\l"
    .string "brother with the sword, and did cast\l"
    .string "off all pity, and his anger did\l"
    .string "tear perpetually, and he kept his\l"
    .string "wrath for ever:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_12::
    .string "But I will send a fire upon Teman,\n"
    .string "which shall devour the palaces of\l"
    .string "Bozrah$"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_13::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of the children of\l"
    .string "Ammon, and for four, I will not turn\l"
    .string "away the punishment thereof; because\l"
    .string "they have ripped up the women with\l"
    .string "child of Gilead, that they might\l"
    .string "enlarge their border:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_14::
    .string "But I will kindle a fire in the\n"
    .string "wall of Rabbah, and it shall\l"
    .string "devour the palaces thereof, with\l"
    .string "shouting in the day of battle, with a\l"
    .string "tempest in the day of the whirlwind:"
Bible_Text_Amos_1_15::
    .string "And their king shall go into\n"
    .string "captivity, he and his princes\l"
    .string "together, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_1::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Moab, and for four,\l"
    .string "I will not turn away the punishment\l"
    .string "thereof; because he burned the bones\l"
    .string "of the king of Edom into lime:"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_2::
    .string "But I will send a fire upon Moab,\n"
    .string "and it shall devour the palaces of\l"
    .string "Kirioth: and Moab shall die with\l"
    .string "tumult, with shouting, and with the\l"
    .string "sound of the trumpet:"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_3::
    .string "And I will cut off the judge from\n"
    .string "the midst thereof, and will slay\l"
    .string "all the princes thereof with him,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Judah, and for\l"
    .string "four, I will not turn away the\l"
    .string "punishment thereof; because they\l"
    .string "have despised the law of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and have not kept his commandments,\l"
    .string "and their lies caused them to err,\l"
    .string "after the which their fathers have\l"
    .string "walked:"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_5::
    .string "But I will send a fire upon Judah,\n"
    .string "and it shall devour the palaces of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_6::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; For three\n"
    .string "transgressions of Israel, and for\l"
    .string "four, I will not turn away the\l"
    .string "punishment thereof; because they\l"
    .string "sold the righteous for silver, and\l"
    .string "the poor for a pair of shoes;"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_7::
    .string "That pant after the dust of the\n"
    .string "earth on the head of the poor, and\l"
    .string "turn aside the way of the meek: and a\l"
    .string "man and his father will go in unto\l"
    .string "the same maid, to profane my holy\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_8::
    .string "And they lay themselves down upon\n"
    .string "clothes laid to pledge by every\l"
    .string "altar, and they drink the wine of the\l"
    .string "condemned in the house of their god$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_9::
    .string "Yet destroyed I the Amorite before\n"
    .string "them, whose height was like the\l"
    .string "height of the cedars, and he was\l"
    .string "strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed\l"
    .string "his fruit from above, and his roots\l"
    .string "from beneath.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_10::
    .string "Also I brought you up from the\n"
    .string "land of Egypt, and led you forty\l"
    .string "years through the wilderness, to\l"
    .string "possess the land of the Amorite.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_11::
    .string "And I raised up of your sons for\n"
    .string "prophets, and of your young men for\l"
    .string "Nazarites. Is it not even thus, O ye\l"
    .string "children of Israel? saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_12::
    .string "But ye gave the Nazarites wine to\n"
    .string "drink; and commanded the prophets,\l"
    .string "saying, Prophesy not.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_13::
    .string "Behold, I am pressed under you, as\n"
    .string "a cart is pressed that is full of\l"
    .string "sheaves.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_14::
    .string "Therefore the flight shall\n"
    .string "perish from the swift, and the strong\l"
    .string "shall not strengthen his force,\l"
    .string "neither shall the mighty deliver\l"
    .string "himself:"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_15::
    .string "Neither shall he stand that\n"
    .string "handleth the bow; and he that is\l"
    .string "swift of foot shall not deliver\l"
    .string "himself: neither shall he that\l"
    .string "rideth the horse deliver himself$"
Bible_Text_Amos_2_16::
    .string "And he that is courageous among the\n"
    .string "mighty shall flee away naked in\l"
    .string "that day, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_1::
    .string "Hear this word that the LORD hath\n"
    .string "spoken against you, O children of\l"
    .string "Israel, against the whole family\l"
    .string "which I brought up from the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, saying,"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_2::
    .string "You only have I known of all the\n"
    .string "families of the earth: therefore I\l"
    .string "will punish you for all your\l"
    .string "iniquities$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_3::
    .string "Can two walk together, except they\n"
    .string "be agreed?"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_4::
    .string "Will a lion roar in the forest,\n"
    .string "when he hath no prey? will a young\l"
    .string "lion cry out of his den, if he have\l"
    .string "taken nothing?"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_5::
    .string "Can a bird fall in a snare upon\n"
    .string "the earth, where no gin is for him?\l"
    .string "shall one take up a snare from the\l"
    .string "earth, and have taken nothing at\l"
    .string "all?"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_6::
    .string "Shall a trumpet be blown in the\n"
    .string "city, and the people not be afraid?\l"
    .string "shall there be evil in a city, and\l"
    .string "the LORD hath not done it?"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_7::
    .string "Surely the Lord GOD will do\n"
    .string "nothing, but he revealeth his secret\l"
    .string "unto his servants the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_8::
    .string "The lion hath roared, who will not\n"
    .string "fear? the Lord GOD hath spoken, who\l"
    .string "can but prophesy?"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_9::
    .string "Publish in the palaces at Ashdod,\n"
    .string "and in the palaces in the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, and say, Assemble\l"
    .string "yourselves upon the mountains of\l"
    .string "Samaria, and behold the great\l"
    .string "tumults in the midst thereof, and\l"
    .string "the oppressed in the midst thereof$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_10::
    .string "For they know not to do right, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, who store up violence and\l"
    .string "robbery in their palaces.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_11::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD;\n"
    .string "An adversary there shall be even\l"
    .string "round about the land; and he shall\l"
    .string "bring down thy strength from thee,\l"
    .string "and thy palaces shall be spoiled.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_12::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; As the\n"
    .string "shepherd taketh out of the mouth of\l"
    .string "the lion two legs, or a piece of an\l"
    .string "ear; so shall the children of\l"
    .string "Israel be taken out that dwell in\l"
    .string "Samaria in the corner of a bed, and in\l"
    .string "Damascus in a couch.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_13::
    .string "Hear ye, and testify in the house of\n"
    .string "Jacob, saith the Lord GOD, the God of\l"
    .string "hosts,"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_14::
    .string "That in the day that I shall visit\n"
    .string "the transgressions of Israel upon\l"
    .string "him I will also visit the altars\l"
    .string "of Bethel: and the horns of the\l"
    .string "altar shall be cut off, and fall\l"
    .string "to the ground$"
Bible_Text_Amos_3_15::
    .string "And I will smite the winter house\n"
    .string "with the summer house; and the houses\l"
    .string "of ivory shall perish, and the\l"
    .string "great houses shall have an end,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_1::
    .string "Hear this word, ye kine of Bashan,\n"
    .string "that are in the mountain of Samaria,\l"
    .string "which oppress the poor, which crush\l"
    .string "the needy, which say to their\l"
    .string "masters, Bring, and let us drink.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_2::
    .string "The Lord GOD hath sworn by his\n"
    .string "holiness, that, lo, the days shall\l"
    .string "come upon you, that he will take\l"
    .string "you away with hooks, and your\l"
    .string "posterity with fishhooks.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_3::
    .string "And ye shall go out at the\n"
    .string "breaches, every cow at that which is\l"
    .string "before her; and ye shall cast them\l"
    .string "into the palace, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_4::
    .string "Come to Bethel, and transgress; at\n"
    .string "Gilgal multiply transgression;\l"
    .string "and bring your sacrifices every\l"
    .string "morning, and your tithes after three\l"
    .string "years:"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_5::
    .string "And offer a sacrifice of\n"
    .string "thanksgiving with leaven, and\l"
    .string "proclaim and publish the free\l"
    .string "offerings: for this liketh you, O ye\l"
    .string "children of Israel, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_6::
    .string "And I also have given you\n"
    .string "cleanness of teeth in all your\l"
    .string "cities, and want of bread in all\l"
    .string "your places: yet have ye not\l"
    .string "returned unto me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_7::
    .string "And also I have withholden the\n"
    .string "rain from you, when there were yet\l"
    .string "three months to the harvest: and I\l"
    .string "caused it to rain upon one city, and\l"
    .string "caused it not to rain upon another\l"
    .string "city: one piece was rained upon, and\l"
    .string "the piece whereupon it rained not\l"
    .string "withered.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_8::
    .string "So two or three cities wandered unto\n"
    .string "one city, to drink water; but they\l"
    .string "were not satisfied: yet have ye not\l"
    .string "returned unto me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_9::
    .string "I have smitten you with blasting\n"
    .string "and mildew: when your gardens and\l"
    .string "your vineyards and your fig trees and\l"
    .string "your olive trees increased, the\l"
    .string "palmerworm devoured them: yet have\l"
    .string "ye not returned unto me, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_10::
    .string "I have sent among you the\n"
    .string "pestilence after the manner of\l"
    .string "Egypt: your young men have I slain\l"
    .string "with the sword, and have taken away\l"
    .string "your horses; and I have made the\l"
    .string "stink of your camps to come up unto\l"
    .string "your nostrils: yet have ye not\l"
    .string "returned unto me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_11::
    .string "I have overthrown some of you, as\n"
    .string "God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah, and\l"
    .string "ye were as a firebrand plucked out\l"
    .string "of the burning: yet have ye not\l"
    .string "returned unto me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_12::
    .string "Therefore thus will I do unto thee,\n"
    .string "O Israel: and because I will do\l"
    .string "this unto thee, prepare to meet thy\l"
    .string "God, O Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_4_13::
    .string "For, lo, he that formeth the\n"
    .string "mountains, and createth the wind, and\l"
    .string "declareth unto man what is his\l"
    .string "thought, that maketh the morning\l"
    .string "darkness, and treadeth upon the high\l"
    .string "places of the earth, The LORD, The\l"
    .string "God of hosts, is his name.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_1::
    .string "Hear ye this word which I take up\n"
    .string "against you, even a lamentation, O\l"
    .string "house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_2::
    .string "The virgin of Israel is fallen;\n"
    .string "she shall no more rise: she is\l"
    .string "forsaken upon her land; there is\l"
    .string "none to raise her up.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_3::
    .string "For thus saith the Lord GOD; The\n"
    .string "city that went out by a thousand\l"
    .string "shall leave an hundred, and that\l"
    .string "which went forth by an hundred\l"
    .string "shall leave ten, to the house of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_4::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD unto the\n"
    .string "house of Israel, Seek ye me, and ye\l"
    .string "shall live:"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_5::
    .string "But seek not Bethel, nor enter into\n"
    .string "Gilgal, and pass not to Beersheba:\l"
    .string "for Gilgal shall surely go into\l"
    .string "captivity, and Bethel shall come\l"
    .string "to nought$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_6::
    .string "Seek the LORD, and ye shall live;\n"
    .string "lest he break out like fire in the\l"
    .string "house of Joseph, and devour it, and\l"
    .string "there be none to quench it in Bethel.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_7::
    .string "Ye who turn judgment to wormwood,\n"
    .string "and leave off righteousness in the\l"
    .string "earth,"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_8::
    .string "Seek him that maketh the seven stars\n"
    .string "and Orion, and turneth the shadow of\l"
    .string "death into the morning, and maketh\l"
    .string "the day dark with night: that\l"
    .string "calleth for the waters of the sea,\l"
    .string "and poureth them out upon the face\l"
    .string "of the earth: The LORD is his name:"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_9::
    .string "That strengtheneth the spoiled\n"
    .string "against the strong, so that the\l"
    .string "spoiled shall come against the\l"
    .string "fortress$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_10::
    .string "They hate him that rebuketh in the\n"
    .string "gate, and they abhor him that\l"
    .string "speaketh uprightly.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_11::
    .string "Forasmuch therefore as your\n"
    .string "treading is upon the poor, and ye\l"
    .string "take from him burdens of wheat: ye\l"
    .string "have built houses of hewn stone, but\l"
    .string "ye shall not dwell in them; ye have\l"
    .string "planted pleasant vineyards, but ye\l"
    .string "shall not drink wine of them.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_12::
    .string "For I know your manifold\n"
    .string "transgressions and your mighty sins:\l"
    .string "they afflict the just, they take a\l"
    .string "bribe, and they turn aside the poor\l"
    .string "in the gate from their right.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_13::
    .string "Therefore the prudent shall keep\n"
    .string "silence in that time; for it is an\l"
    .string "evil time.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_14::
    .string "Seek good, and not evil, that ye may\n"
    .string "live: and so the LORD, the God of\l"
    .string "hosts, shall be with you, as ye have\l"
    .string "spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_15::
    .string "Hate the evil, and love the good,\n"
    .string "and establish judgment in the gate:\l"
    .string "it may be that the LORD God of hosts\l"
    .string "will be gracious unto the remnant\l"
    .string "of Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_16::
    .string "Therefore the LORD, the God of\n"
    .string "hosts, the LORD, saith thus; Wailing\l"
    .string "shall be in all streets; and they\l"
    .string "shall say in all the highways,\l"
    .string "Alas! alas! and they shall call\l"
    .string "the husbandman to mourning, and such\l"
    .string "as are skilful of lamentation to\l"
    .string "wailing.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_17::
    .string "And in all vineyards shall be\n"
    .string "wailing: for I will pass through\l"
    .string "thee, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_18::
    .string "Woe unto you that desire the day of\n"
    .string "the LORD! to what end is it for you?\l"
    .string "the day of the LORD is darkness, and\l"
    .string "not light.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_19::
    .string "As if a man did flee from a lion,\n"
    .string "and a bear met him; or went into the\l"
    .string "house, and leaned his hand on the\l"
    .string "wall, and a serpent bit him.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_20::
    .string "Shall not the day of the LORD be\n"
    .string "darkness, and not light? even very\l"
    .string "dark, and no brightness in it?"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_21::
    .string "I hate, I despise your feast days,\n"
    .string "and I will not smell in your\l"
    .string "solemn assemblies$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_22::
    .string "Though ye offer me burnt offerings\n"
    .string "and your meat offerings, I will not\l"
    .string "accept them: neither will I regard\l"
    .string "the peace offerings of your fat\l"
    .string "beasts.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_23::
    .string "Take thou away from me the noise of\n"
    .string "thy songs; for I will not hear the\l"
    .string "melody of thy viols.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_24::
    .string "But let judgment run down as\n"
    .string "waters, and righteousness as a mighty\l"
    .string "stream.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_25::
    .string "Have ye offered unto me sacrifices\n"
    .string "and offerings in the wilderness\l"
    .string "forty years, O house of Israel?"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_26::
    .string "But ye have borne the tabernacle of\n"
    .string "your Moloch and Chiun your images,\l"
    .string "the star of your god, which ye made to\l"
    .string "yourselves$"
Bible_Text_Amos_5_27::
    .string "Therefore will I cause you to go\n"
    .string "into captivity beyond Damascus,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD, whose name is The God\l"
    .string "of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_1::
    .string "Woe to them that are at ease in Zion,\n"
    .string "and trust in the mountain of Samaria,\l"
    .string "which are named chief of the nations,\l"
    .string "to whom the house of Israel came!"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_2::
    .string "Pass ye unto Calneh, and see; and\n"
    .string "from thence go ye to Hamath the\l"
    .string "great: then go down to Gath of the\l"
    .string "Philistines: be they better than\l"
    .string "these kingdoms? or their border\l"
    .string "greater than your border?"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_3::
    .string "Ye that put far away the evil day,\n"
    .string "and cause the seat of violence to\l"
    .string "come near;"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_4::
    .string "That lie upon beds of ivory, and\n"
    .string "stretch themselves upon their\l"
    .string "couches, and eat the lambs out of the\l"
    .string "flock, and the calves out of the\l"
    .string "midst of the stall;"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_5::
    .string "That chant to the sound of the viol,\n"
    .string "and invent to themselves\l"
    .string "instruments of musick, like David;"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_6::
    .string "That drink wine in bowls, and\n"
    .string "anoint themselves with the chief\l"
    .string "ointments: but they are not grieved\l"
    .string "for the affliction of Joseph$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_7::
    .string "Therefore now shall they go\n"
    .string "captive with the first that go\l"
    .string "captive, and the banquet of them\l"
    .string "that stretched themselves shall be\l"
    .string "removed.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_8::
    .string "The Lord GOD hath sworn by himself,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD the God of hosts, I\l"
    .string "abhor the excellency of Jacob, and\l"
    .string "hate his palaces: therefore will I\l"
    .string "deliver up the city with all that\l"
    .string "is therein.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, if\n"
    .string "there remain ten men in one house,\l"
    .string "that they shall die.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_10::
    .string "And a man’s uncle shall take him\n"
    .string "up, and he that burneth him, to bring\l"
    .string "out the bones out of the house, and\l"
    .string "shall say unto him that is by the\l"
    .string "sides of the house, Is there yet any\l"
    .string "with thee? and he shall say, No.\l"
    .string "Then shall he say, Hold thy tongue:\l"
    .string "for we may not make mention of the\l"
    .string "name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_11::
    .string "For, behold, the LORD commandeth,\n"
    .string "and he will smite the great house\l"
    .string "with breaches, and the little house\l"
    .string "with clefts.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_12::
    .string "Shall horses run upon the rock?\n"
    .string "will one plow there with oxen? for\l"
    .string "ye have turned judgment into gall,\l"
    .string "and the fruit of righteousness into\l"
    .string "hemlock:"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_13::
    .string "Ye which rejoice in a thing of\n"
    .string "nought, which say, Have we not taken\l"
    .string "to us horns by our own strength?"
Bible_Text_Amos_6_14::
    .string "But, behold, I will raise up\n"
    .string "against you a nation, O house of\l"
    .string "Israel, saith the LORD the God of\l"
    .string "hosts; and they shall afflict you\l"
    .string "from the entering in of Hemath unto\l"
    .string "the river of the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_1::
    .string "Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto\n"
    .string "me; and, behold, he formed\l"
    .string "grasshoppers in the beginning of\l"
    .string "the shooting up of the latter\l"
    .string "growth; and, lo, it was the latter\l"
    .string "growth after the king’s mowings.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_2::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when they\n"
    .string "had made an end of eating the grass\l"
    .string "of the land, then I said, O Lord GOD,\l"
    .string "forgive, I beseech thee: by whom\l"
    .string "shall Jacob arise? for he is small.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_3::
    .string "The LORD repented for this: It\n"
    .string "shall not be, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_4::
    .string "Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto\n"
    .string "me: and, behold, the Lord GOD\l"
    .string "called to contend by fire, and it\l"
    .string "devoured the great deep, and did eat\l"
    .string "up a part.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_5::
    .string "Then said I, O Lord GOD, cease, I\n"
    .string "beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob\l"
    .string "arise? for he is small.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_6::
    .string "The LORD repented for this: This\n"
    .string "also shall not be, saith the Lord\l"
    .string "GOD.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_7::
    .string "Thus he shewed me: and, behold, the\n"
    .string "LORD stood upon a wall made by a\l"
    .string "plumbline, with a plumbline in\l"
    .string "his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_8::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, Amos,\n"
    .string "what seest thou? And I said, A\l"
    .string "plumbline. Then said the LORD,\l"
    .string "Behold, I will set a plumbline in\l"
    .string "the midst of my people Israel: I\l"
    .string "will not again pass by them any\l"
    .string "more:"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_9::
    .string "And the high places of Isaac\n"
    .string "shall be desolate, and the\l"
    .string "sanctuaries of Israel shall be\l"
    .string "laid waste; and I will rise against\l"
    .string "the house of Jeroboam with the sword$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_10::
    .string "Then Amaziah the priest of Bethel\n"
    .string "sent to Jeroboam king of Israel,\l"
    .string "saying, Amos hath conspired against\l"
    .string "thee in the midst of the house of\l"
    .string "Israel: the land is not able to\l"
    .string "bear all his words.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_11::
    .string "For thus Amos saith, Jeroboam\n"
    .string "shall die by the sword, and Israel\l"
    .string "shall surely be led away captive\l"
    .string "out of their own land.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_12::
    .string "Also Amaziah said unto Amos, O thou\n"
    .string "seer, go, flee thee away into the\l"
    .string "land of Judah, and there eat bread,\l"
    .string "and prophesy there:"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_13::
    .string "But prophesy not again any more at\n"
    .string "Bethel: for it is the king’s\l"
    .string "chapel, and it is the king’s court$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_14::
    .string "Then answered Amos, and said to\n"
    .string "Amaziah, I was no prophet, neither\l"
    .string "was I a prophet’s son; but I was an\l"
    .string "herdman, and a gatherer of sycomore\l"
    .string "fruit:"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_15::
    .string "And the LORD took me as I followed\n"
    .string "the flock, and the LORD said unto me,\l"
    .string "Go, prophesy unto my people\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_16::
    .string "Now therefore hear thou the word of\n"
    .string "the LORD: Thou sayest, Prophesy not\l"
    .string "against Israel, and drop not thy\l"
    .string "word against the house of Isaac.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_7_17::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD; Thy\n"
    .string "wife shall be an harlot in the\l"
    .string "city, and thy sons and thy daughters\l"
    .string "shall fall by the sword, and thy\l"
    .string "land shall be divided by line; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt die in a polluted land:\l"
    .string "and Israel shall surely go into\l"
    .string "captivity forth of his land.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_1::
    .string "Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto\n"
    .string "me: and behold a basket of summer\l"
    .string "fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_2::
    .string "And he said, Amos, what seest thou?\n"
    .string "And I said, A basket of summer fruit.\l"
    .string "Then said the LORD unto me, The end is\l"
    .string "come upon my people of Israel; I\l"
    .string "will not again pass by them any\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_3::
    .string "And the songs of the temple shall\n"
    .string "be howlings in that day, saith the\l"
    .string "Lord GOD: there shall be many dead\l"
    .string "bodies in every place; they shall\l"
    .string "cast them forth with silence.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_4::
    .string "Hear this, O ye that swallow up\n"
    .string "the needy, even to make the poor of\l"
    .string "the land to fail,"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_5::
    .string "Saying, When will the new moon be\n"
    .string "gone, that we may sell corn? and the\l"
    .string "sabbath, that we may set forth wheat,\l"
    .string "making the ephah small, and the\l"
    .string "shekel great, and falsifying the\l"
    .string "balances by deceit?"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_6::
    .string "That we may buy the poor for\n"
    .string "silver, and the needy for a pair of\l"
    .string "shoes; yea, and sell the refuse of\l"
    .string "the wheat?"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_7::
    .string "The LORD hath sworn by the\n"
    .string "excellency of Jacob, Surely I\l"
    .string "will never forget any of their works$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_8::
    .string "Shall not the land tremble for\n"
    .string "this, and every one mourn that\l"
    .string "dwelleth therein? and it shall\l"
    .string "rise up wholly as a flood; and it\l"
    .string "shall be cast out and drowned, as by\l"
    .string "the flood of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the Lord GOD, that I will\l"
    .string "cause the sun to go down at noon, and\l"
    .string "I will darken the earth in the\l"
    .string "clear day:"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_10::
    .string "And I will turn your feasts into\n"
    .string "mourning, and all your songs into\l"
    .string "lamentation; and I will bring up\l"
    .string "sackcloth upon all loins, and\l"
    .string "baldness upon every head; and I\l"
    .string "will make it as the mourning of an\l"
    .string "only son, and the end thereof as a\l"
    .string "bitter day$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_11::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "Lord GOD, that I will send a famine\l"
    .string "in the land, not a famine of bread,\l"
    .string "nor a thirst for water, but of\l"
    .string "hearing the words of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_12::
    .string "And they shall wander from sea to\n"
    .string "sea, and from the north even to the\l"
    .string "east, they shall run to and fro to\l"
    .string "seek the word of the LORD, and shall\l"
    .string "not find it$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_13::
    .string "In that day shall the fair virgins\n"
    .string "and young men faint for thirst.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_8_14::
    .string "They that swear by the sin of\n"
    .string "Samaria, and say, Thy god, O Dan,\l"
    .string "liveth; and, The manner of Beersheba\l"
    .string "liveth; even they shall fall, and\l"
    .string "never rise up again.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_1::
    .string "I saw the LORD standing upon the\n"
    .string "altar: and he said, Smite the\l"
    .string "lintel of the door, that the posts\l"
    .string "may shake: and cut them in the head,\l"
    .string "all of them; and I will slay the\l"
    .string "last of them with the sword: he that\l"
    .string "fleeth of them shall not flee\l"
    .string "away, and he that escapeth of them\l"
    .string "shall not be delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_2::
    .string "Though they dig into hell, thence\n"
    .string "shall mine hand take them; though\l"
    .string "they climb up to heaven, thence\l"
    .string "will I bring them down:"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_3::
    .string "And though they hide themselves in\n"
    .string "the top of Carmel, I will search\l"
    .string "and take them out thence; and though\l"
    .string "they be hid from my sight in the\l"
    .string "bottom of the sea, thence will I\l"
    .string "command the serpent, and he shall\l"
    .string "bite them:"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_4::
    .string "And though they go into captivity\n"
    .string "before their enemies, thence will I\l"
    .string "command the sword, and it shall\l"
    .string "slay them: and I will set mine eyes\l"
    .string "upon them for evil, and not for good$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_5::
    .string "And the Lord GOD of hosts is he that\n"
    .string "toucheth the land, and it shall\l"
    .string "melt, and all that dwell therein\l"
    .string "shall mourn: and it shall rise up\l"
    .string "wholly like a flood; and shall be\l"
    .string "drowned, as by the flood of Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_6::
    .string "It is he that buildeth his stories\n"
    .string "in the heaven, and hath founded his\l"
    .string "troop in the earth; he that calleth\l"
    .string "for the waters of the sea, and\l"
    .string "poureth them out upon the face of\l"
    .string "the earth: The LORD is his name.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_7::
    .string "Are ye not as children of the\n"
    .string "Ethiopians unto me, O children of\l"
    .string "Israel? saith the LORD. Have not I\l"
    .string "brought up Israel out of the land\l"
    .string "of Egypt? and the Philistines from\l"
    .string "Caphtor, and the Syrians from Kir?"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_8::
    .string "Behold, the eyes of the Lord GOD are\n"
    .string "upon the sinful kingdom, and I\l"
    .string "will destroy it from off the face of\l"
    .string "the earth; saving that I will not\l"
    .string "utterly destroy the house of Jacob,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_9::
    .string "For, lo, I will command, and I\n"
    .string "will sift the house of Israel among\l"
    .string "all nations, like as corn is sifted\l"
    .string "in a sieve, yet shall not the least\l"
    .string "grain fall upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_10::
    .string "All the sinners of my people\n"
    .string "shall die by the sword, which say,\l"
    .string "The evil shall not overtake nor\l"
    .string "prevent us.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_11::
    .string "In that day will I raise up the\n"
    .string "tabernacle of David that is fallen,\l"
    .string "and close up the breaches thereof;\l"
    .string "and I will raise up his ruins, and I\l"
    .string "will build it as in the days of\l"
    .string "old:"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_12::
    .string "That they may possess the remnant\n"
    .string "of Edom, and of all the heathen,\l"
    .string "which are called by my name, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD that doeth this$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_13::
    .string "Behold, the days come, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, that the plowman shall\l"
    .string "overtake the reaper, and the treader\l"
    .string "of grapes him that soweth seed; and\l"
    .string "the mountains shall drop sweet\l"
    .string "wine, and all the hills shall\l"
    .string "melt.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_14::
    .string "And I will bring again the\n"
    .string "captivity of my people of Israel,\l"
    .string "and they shall build the waste\l"
    .string "cities, and inhabit them; and they\l"
    .string "shall plant vineyards, and drink\l"
    .string "the wine thereof; they shall also\l"
    .string "make gardens, and eat the fruit of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Amos_9_15::
    .string "And I will plant them upon their\n"
    .string "land, and they shall no more be\l"
    .string "pulled up out of their land which\l"
    .string "I have given them, saith the LORD thy\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_1::
    .string "The vision of Obadiah. Thus saith\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD concerning Edom; We have\l"
    .string "heard a rumour from the LORD, and an\l"
    .string "ambassador is sent among the heathen,\l"
    .string "Arise ye, and let us rise up against\l"
    .string "her in battle.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_2::
    .string "Behold, I have made thee small\n"
    .string "among the heathen: thou art greatly\l"
    .string "despised.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_3::
    .string "The pride of thine heart hath\n"
    .string "deceived thee, thou that dwellest\l"
    .string "in the clefts of the rock, whose\l"
    .string "habitation is high; that saith in his\l"
    .string "heart, Who shall bring me down to\l"
    .string "the ground?"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_4::
    .string "Though thou exalt thyself as the\n"
    .string "eagle, and though thou set thy nest\l"
    .string "among the stars, thence will I bring\l"
    .string "thee down, saith the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_5::
    .string "If thieves came to thee, if robbers\n"
    .string "by night, (how art thou cut off!)\l"
    .string "would they not have stolen till\l"
    .string "they had enough? if the\l"
    .string "grapegatherers came to thee, would\l"
    .string "they not leave some grapes?"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_6::
    .string "How are the things of Esau searched\n"
    .string "out! how are his hidden things sought\l"
    .string "up!"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_7::
    .string "All the men of thy confederacy\n"
    .string "have brought thee even to the border:\l"
    .string "the men that were at peace with thee\l"
    .string "have deceived thee, and prevailed\l"
    .string "against thee; they that eat thy bread\l"
    .string "have laid a wound under thee: there\l"
    .string "is none understanding in him$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_8::
    .string "Shall I not in that day, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD, even destroy the wise men out\l"
    .string "of Edom, and understanding out of the\l"
    .string "mount of Esau?"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_9::
    .string "And thy mighty men, O Teman, shall\n"
    .string "be dismayed, to the end that every\l"
    .string "one of the mount of Esau may be cut\l"
    .string "off by slaughter$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_10::
    .string "For thy violence against thy\n"
    .string "brother Jacob shame shall cover\l"
    .string "thee, and thou shalt be cut off for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_11::
    .string "In the day that thou stoodest on the\n"
    .string "other side, in the day that the\l"
    .string "strangers carried away captive his\l"
    .string "forces, and foreigners entered into\l"
    .string "his gates, and cast lots upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, even thou wast as one of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_12::
    .string "But thou shouldest not have looked\n"
    .string "on the day of thy brother in the day\l"
    .string "that he became a stranger; neither\l"
    .string "shouldest thou have rejoiced over\l"
    .string "the children of Judah in the day of\l"
    .string "their destruction; neither\l"
    .string "shouldest thou have spoken\l"
    .string "proudly in the day of distress.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_13::
    .string "Thou shouldest not have entered\n"
    .string "into the gate of my people in the\l"
    .string "day of their calamity; yea, thou\l"
    .string "shouldest not have looked on their\l"
    .string "affliction in the day of their\l"
    .string "calamity, nor have laid hands on\l"
    .string "their substance in the day of their\l"
    .string "calamity;"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_14::
    .string "Neither shouldest thou have stood\n"
    .string "in the crossway, to cut off those of\l"
    .string "his that did escape; neither\l"
    .string "shouldest thou have delivered up\l"
    .string "those of his that did remain in the\l"
    .string "day of distress$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_15::
    .string "For the day of the LORD is near upon\n"
    .string "all the heathen: as thou hast done,\l"
    .string "it shall be done unto thee: thy\l"
    .string "reward shall return upon thine own\l"
    .string "head.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_16::
    .string "For as ye have drunk upon my holy\n"
    .string "mountain, so shall all the heathen\l"
    .string "drink continually, yea, they shall\l"
    .string "drink, and they shall swallow\l"
    .string "down, and they shall be as though\l"
    .string "they had not been.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_17::
    .string "But upon mount Zion shall be\n"
    .string "deliverance, and there shall be\l"
    .string "holiness; and the house of Jacob\l"
    .string "shall possess their possessions.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_18::
    .string "And the house of Jacob shall be a\n"
    .string "fire, and the house of Joseph a\l"
    .string "flame, and the house of Esau for\l"
    .string "stubble, and they shall kindle in\l"
    .string "them, and devour them; and there\l"
    .string "shall not be any remaining of the\l"
    .string "house of Esau; for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_19::
    .string "And they of the south shall\n"
    .string "possess the mount of Esau; and they\l"
    .string "of the plain the Philistines: and\l"
    .string "they shall possess the fields of\l"
    .string "Ephraim, and the fields of Samaria:\l"
    .string "and Benjamin shall possess Gilead.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_20::
    .string "And the captivity of this host of\n"
    .string "the children of Israel shall\l"
    .string "possess that of the Canaanites, even\l"
    .string "unto Zarephath; and the captivity\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem, which is in Sepharad,\l"
    .string "shall possess the cities of the\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_Obadiah_1_21::
    .string "And saviours shall come up on\n"
    .string "mount Zion to judge the mount of\l"
    .string "Esau; and the kingdom shall be the\l"
    .string "LORD’s.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_1::
    .string "Now the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Jonah the son of Amittai, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_2::
    .string "Arise, go to Nineveh, that great\n"
    .string "city, and cry against it; for their\l"
    .string "wickedness is come up before me$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_3::
    .string "But Jonah rose up to flee unto\n"
    .string "Tarshish from the presence of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and went down to Joppa; and he\l"
    .string "found a ship going to Tarshish: so he\l"
    .string "paid the fare thereof, and went down\l"
    .string "into it, to go with them unto\l"
    .string "Tarshish from the presence of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_4::
    .string "But the LORD sent out a great wind\n"
    .string "into the sea, and there was a mighty\l"
    .string "tempest in the sea, so that the ship\l"
    .string "was like to be broken.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_5::
    .string "Then the mariners were afraid, and\n"
    .string "cried every man unto his god, and\l"
    .string "cast forth the wares that were in the\l"
    .string "ship into the sea, to lighten it of\l"
    .string "them. But Jonah was gone down into\l"
    .string "the sides of the ship; and he lay,\l"
    .string "and was fast asleep.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_6::
    .string "So the shipmaster came to him, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, What meanest thou, O\l"
    .string "sleeper? arise, call upon thy God,\l"
    .string "if so be that God will think upon\l"
    .string "us, that we perish not.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_7::
    .string "And they said every one to his\n"
    .string "fellow, Come, and let us cast lots,\l"
    .string "that we may know for whose cause this\l"
    .string "evil is upon us. So they cast lots,\l"
    .string "and the lot fell upon Jonah.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_8::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Tell us,\n"
    .string "we pray thee, for whose cause this\l"
    .string "evil is upon us; What is thine\l"
    .string "occupation? and whence comest thou?\l"
    .string "what is thy country? and of what\l"
    .string "people art thou?"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_9::
    .string "And he said unto them, I am an\n"
    .string "Hebrew; and I fear the LORD, the God\l"
    .string "of heaven, which hath made the sea\l"
    .string "and the dry land$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_10::
    .string "Then were the men exceedingly\n"
    .string "afraid, and said unto him. Why hast\l"
    .string "thou done this? For the men knew that\l"
    .string "he fled from the presence of the\l"
    .string "LORD, because he had told them.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_11::
    .string "Then said they unto him, What shall\n"
    .string "we do unto thee, that the sea may be\l"
    .string "calm unto us? for the sea wrought,\l"
    .string "and was tempestuous.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_12::
    .string "And he said unto them, Take me up,\n"
    .string "and cast me forth into the sea; so\l"
    .string "shall the sea be calm unto you: for\l"
    .string "I know that for my sake this great\l"
    .string "tempest is upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_13::
    .string "Nevertheless the men rowed hard to\n"
    .string "bring it to the land; but they could\l"
    .string "not: for the sea wrought, and was\l"
    .string "tempestuous against them.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_14::
    .string "Wherefore they cried unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "and said, We beseech thee, O LORD, we\l"
    .string "beseech thee, let us not perish for\l"
    .string "this man’s life, and lay not upon\l"
    .string "us innocent blood: for thou, O LORD,\l"
    .string "hast done as it pleased thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_15::
    .string "So they look up Jonah, and cast him\n"
    .string "forth into the sea: and the sea\l"
    .string "ceased from her raging.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_16::
    .string "Then the men feared the LORD\n"
    .string "exceedingly, and offered a sacrifice\l"
    .string "unto the LORD, and made vows.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_1_17::
    .string "Now the LORD had prepared a great\n"
    .string "fish to swallow up Jonah. And Jonah\l"
    .string "was in the belly of the fish three\l"
    .string "days and three nights.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_1::
    .string "Then Jonah prayed unto the LORD his\n"
    .string "God out of the fish’s belly,"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_2::
    .string "And said, I cried by reason of mine\n"
    .string "affliction unto the LORD, and he\l"
    .string "heard me; out of the belly of hell\l"
    .string "cried I, and thou heardest my voice$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_3::
    .string "For thou hadst cast me into the\n"
    .string "deep, in the midst of the seas; and\l"
    .string "the floods compassed me about: all\l"
    .string "thy billows and thy waves passed\l"
    .string "over me.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_4::
    .string "Then I said, I am cast out of thy\n"
    .string "sight; yet I will look again toward\l"
    .string "thy holy temple.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_5::
    .string "The waters compassed me about, even\n"
    .string "to the soul: the depth closed me\l"
    .string "round about, the weeds were wrapped\l"
    .string "about my head.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_6::
    .string "I went down to the bottoms of the\n"
    .string "mountains; the earth with her bars\l"
    .string "was about me for ever: yet hast thou\l"
    .string "brought up my life from corruption,\l"
    .string "O LORD my God.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_7::
    .string "When my soul fainted within me I\n"
    .string "remembered the LORD: and my prayer\l"
    .string "came in unto thee, into thine holy\l"
    .string "temple.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_8::
    .string "They that observe lying vanities\n"
    .string "forsake their own mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_9::
    .string "But I will sacrifice unto thee\n"
    .string "with the voice of thanksgiving; I\l"
    .string "will pay that that I have vowed.\l"
    .string "Salvation is of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_2_10::
    .string "And the LORD spake unto the fish,\n"
    .string "and it vomited out Jonah upon the\l"
    .string "dry land.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_1::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Jonah the second time, saying,"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_2::
    .string "Arise, go unto Nineveh, that great\n"
    .string "city, and preach unto it the\l"
    .string "preaching that I bid thee$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_3::
    .string "So Jonah arose, and went unto\n"
    .string "Nineveh, according to the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD. Now Nineveh was an exceeding\l"
    .string "great city of three days’ journey.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_4::
    .string "And Jonah began to enter into the\n"
    .string "city a day’s journey, and he cried,\l"
    .string "and said, Yet forty days, and Nineveh\l"
    .string "shall be overthrown.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_5::
    .string "So the people of Nineveh believed\n"
    .string "God, and proclaimed a fast, and put\l"
    .string "on sackcloth, from the greatest of\l"
    .string "them even to the least of them.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_6::
    .string "For word came unto the king of\n"
    .string "Nineveh, and he arose from his\l"
    .string "throne, and he laid his robe from\l"
    .string "him, and covered him with sackcloth,\l"
    .string "and sat in ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_7::
    .string "And he caused it to be proclaimed\n"
    .string "and published through Nineveh by\l"
    .string "the decree of the king and his\l"
    .string "nobles, saying, Let neither man nor\l"
    .string "beast, herd nor flock, taste any\l"
    .string "thing: let them not feed, nor drink\l"
    .string "water:"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_8::
    .string "But let man and beast be covered\n"
    .string "with sackcloth, and cry mightily\l"
    .string "unto God: yea, let them turn every\l"
    .string "one from his evil way, and from the\l"
    .string "violence that is in their hands$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_9::
    .string "Who can tell if God will turn and\n"
    .string "repent, and turn away from his\l"
    .string "fierce anger, that we perish not?"
Bible_Text_Jonah_3_10::
    .string "And God saw their works, that they\n"
    .string "turned from their evil way; and God\l"
    .string "repented of the evil, that he had\l"
    .string "said that he would do unto them; and\l"
    .string "he did it not$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_1::
    .string "But it displeased Jonah\n"
    .string "exceedingly, and he was very angry.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_2::
    .string "And he prayed unto the LORD, and\n"
    .string "said, I pray thee, O LORD, was not\l"
    .string "this my saying, when I was yet in my\l"
    .string "country? Therefore I fled before\l"
    .string "unto Tarshish: for I knew that thou\l"
    .string "art a gracious God, and merciful,\l"
    .string "slow to anger, and of great\l"
    .string "kindness, and repentest thee of the\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_3::
    .string "Therefore now, O LORD, take, I\n"
    .string "beseech thee, my life from me; for it\l"
    .string "is better for me to die than to live.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_4::
    .string "Then said the LORD, Doest thou well\n"
    .string "to be angry?"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_5::
    .string "So Jonah went out of the city, and\n"
    .string "sat on the east side of the city, and\l"
    .string "there made him a booth, and sat under\l"
    .string "it in the shadow, till he might see\l"
    .string "what would become of the city$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_6::
    .string "And the LORD God prepared a gourd,\n"
    .string "and made it to come up over Jonah,\l"
    .string "that it might be a shadow over his\l"
    .string "head, to deliver him from his grief.\l"
    .string "So Jonah was exceeding glad of the\l"
    .string "gourd.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_7::
    .string "But God prepared a worm when the\n"
    .string "morning rose the next day, and it\l"
    .string "smote the gourd that it withered.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the sun\n"
    .string "did arise, that God prepared a\l"
    .string "vehement east wind; and the sun beat\l"
    .string "upon the head of Jonah, that he\l"
    .string "fainted, and wished in himself to\l"
    .string "die, and said, It is better for me to\l"
    .string "die than to live.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_9::
    .string "And God said to Jonah, Doest thou\n"
    .string "well to be angry for the gourd? And\l"
    .string "he said, I do well to be angry, even\l"
    .string "unto death.$"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_10::
    .string "Then said the LORD, Thou hast had\n"
    .string "pity on the gourd, for the which thou\l"
    .string "hast not laboured, neither madest it\l"
    .string "grow; which came up in a night, and\l"
    .string "perished in a night:"
Bible_Text_Jonah_4_11::
    .string "And should not I spare Nineveh,\n"
    .string "that great city, wherein are more\l"
    .string "than sixscore thousand persons that\l"
    .string "cannot discern between their right\l"
    .string "hand and their left hand; and also\l"
    .string "much cattle$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD that came to\n"
    .string "Micah the Morasthite in the days of\l"
    .string "Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of\l"
    .string "Judah, which he saw concerning\l"
    .string "Samaria and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_2::
    .string "Hear, all ye people; hearken, O\n"
    .string "earth, and all that therein is: and\l"
    .string "let the Lord GOD be witness against\l"
    .string "you, the LORD from his holy temple.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_3::
    .string "For, behold, the LORD cometh forth\n"
    .string "out of his place, and will come\l"
    .string "down, and tread upon the high\l"
    .string "places of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_4::
    .string "And the mountains shall be molten\n"
    .string "under him, and the valleys shall\l"
    .string "be cleft, as wax before the fire, and\l"
    .string "as the waters that are poured down a\l"
    .string "steep place.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_5::
    .string "For the transgression of Jacob is\n"
    .string "all this, and for the sins of the\l"
    .string "house of Israel. What is the\l"
    .string "transgression of Jacob? is it not\l"
    .string "Samaria? and what are the high\l"
    .string "places of Judah? are they not\l"
    .string "Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_6::
    .string "Therefore I will make Samaria as\n"
    .string "an heap of the field, and as\l"
    .string "plantings of a vineyard: and I will\l"
    .string "pour down the stones thereof into the\l"
    .string "valley, and I will discover the\l"
    .string "foundations thereof$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_7::
    .string "And all the graven images thereof\n"
    .string "shall be beaten to pieces, and all\l"
    .string "the hires thereof shall be burned\l"
    .string "with the fire, and all the idols\l"
    .string "thereof will I lay desolate: for\l"
    .string "she gathered it of the hire of an\l"
    .string "harlot, and they shall return to\l"
    .string "the hire of an harlot.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_8::
    .string "Therefore I will wail and howl, I\n"
    .string "will go stripped and naked: I\l"
    .string "will make a wailing like the\l"
    .string "dragons, and mourning as the owls.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_9::
    .string "For her wound is incurable; for it\n"
    .string "is come unto Judah; he is come unto\l"
    .string "the gate of my people, even to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_10::
    .string "Declare ye it not at Gath, weep ye\n"
    .string "not at all: in the house of Aphrah\l"
    .string "roll thyself in the dust.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_11::
    .string "Pass ye away, thou inhabitant of\n"
    .string "Saphir, having thy shame naked: the\l"
    .string "inhabitant of Zaanan came not forth\l"
    .string "in the mourning of Bethezel; he\l"
    .string "shall receive of you his standing.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_12::
    .string "For the inhabitant of Maroth waited\n"
    .string "carefully for good: but evil came\l"
    .string "down from the LORD unto the gate of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_13::
    .string "O thou inhabitant of Lachish, bind\n"
    .string "the chariot to the swift beast: she\l"
    .string "is the beginning of the sin to the\l"
    .string "daughter of Zion: for the\l"
    .string "transgressions of Israel were found\l"
    .string "in thee.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_14::
    .string "Therefore shalt thou give presents\n"
    .string "to Moreshethgath: the houses of\l"
    .string "Achzib shall be a lie to the kings\l"
    .string "of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_15::
    .string "Yet will I bring an heir unto thee,\n"
    .string "O inhabitant of Mareshah: he shall\l"
    .string "come unto Adullam the glory of\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_1_16::
    .string "Make thee bald, and poll thee for\n"
    .string "thy delicate children; enlarge thy\l"
    .string "baldness as the eagle; for they are\l"
    .string "gone into captivity from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_1::
    .string "Woe to them that devise iniquity,\n"
    .string "and work evil upon their beds! when\l"
    .string "the morning is light, they practise\l"
    .string "it, because it is in the power of\l"
    .string "their hand.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_2::
    .string "And they covet fields, and take\n"
    .string "them by violence; and houses, and\l"
    .string "take them away: so they oppress a\l"
    .string "man and his house, even a man and his\l"
    .string "heritage.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_3::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD;\n"
    .string "Behold, against this family do I\l"
    .string "devise an evil, from which ye shall\l"
    .string "not remove your necks; neither\l"
    .string "shall ye go haughtily: for this\l"
    .string "time is evil.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_4::
    .string "In that day shall one take up a\n"
    .string "parable against you, and lament\l"
    .string "with a doleful lamentation, and\l"
    .string "say, We be utterly spoiled: he hath\l"
    .string "changed the portion of my people:\l"
    .string "how hath he removed it from me!\l"
    .string "turning away he hath divided our\l"
    .string "fields.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_5::
    .string "Therefore thou shalt have none that\n"
    .string "shall cast a cord by lot in the\l"
    .string "congregation of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_6::
    .string "Prophesy ye not, say they to them\n"
    .string "that prophesy: they shall not\l"
    .string "prophesy to them, that they shall\l"
    .string "not take shame.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_7::
    .string "O thou that art named the house of\n"
    .string "Jacob, is the spirit of the LORD\l"
    .string "straitened? are these his doings? do\l"
    .string "not my words do good to him that\l"
    .string "walketh uprightly?"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_8::
    .string "Even of late my people is risen\n"
    .string "up as an enemy: ye pull off the\l"
    .string "robe with the garment from them that\l"
    .string "pass by securely as men averse from\l"
    .string "war$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_9::
    .string "The women of my people have ye\n"
    .string "cast out from their pleasant\l"
    .string "houses; from their children have ye\l"
    .string "taken away my glory for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_10::
    .string "Arise ye, and depart; for this is\n"
    .string "not your rest: because it is\l"
    .string "polluted, it shall destroy you,\l"
    .string "even with a sore destruction.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_11::
    .string "If a man walking in the spirit and\n"
    .string "falsehood do lie, saying, I will\l"
    .string "prophesy unto thee of wine and of\l"
    .string "strong drink; he shall even be the\l"
    .string "prophet of this people.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_12::
    .string "I will surely assemble, O Jacob,\n"
    .string "all of thee; I will surely gather\l"
    .string "the remnant of Israel; I will put\l"
    .string "them together as the sheep of\l"
    .string "Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of\l"
    .string "their fold: they shall make great\l"
    .string "noise by reason of the multitude of\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_2_13::
    .string "The breaker is come up before them:\n"
    .string "they have broken up, and have passed\l"
    .string "through the gate, and are gone out by\l"
    .string "it: and their king shall pass\l"
    .string "before them, and the LORD on the head\l"
    .string "of them.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_1::
    .string "And I said, Hear, I pray you, O\n"
    .string "heads of Jacob, and ye princes of the\l"
    .string "house of Israel; Is it not for you to\l"
    .string "know judgment?"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_2::
    .string "Who hate the good, and love the\n"
    .string "evil; who pluck off their skin from\l"
    .string "off them, and their flesh from off\l"
    .string "their bones;"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_3::
    .string "Who also eat the flesh of my\n"
    .string "people, and flay their skin from\l"
    .string "off them; and they break their bones,\l"
    .string "and chop them in pieces, as for the\l"
    .string "pot, and as flesh within the caldron$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_4::
    .string "Then shall they cry unto the LORD,\n"
    .string "but he will not hear them: he will\l"
    .string "even hide his face from them at that\l"
    .string "time, as they have behaved\l"
    .string "themselves ill in their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_5::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD concerning the\n"
    .string "prophets that make my people err,\l"
    .string "that bite with their teeth, and cry,\l"
    .string "Peace; and he that putteth not into\l"
    .string "their mouths, they even prepare war\l"
    .string "against him.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_6::
    .string "Therefore night shall be unto you,\n"
    .string "that ye shall not have a vision; and\l"
    .string "it shall be dark unto you, that ye\l"
    .string "shall not divine; and the sun\l"
    .string "shall go down over the prophets,\l"
    .string "and the day shall be dark over them.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_7::
    .string "Then shall the seers be ashamed,\n"
    .string "and the diviners confounded: yea,\l"
    .string "they shall all cover their lips;\l"
    .string "for there is no answer of God.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_8::
    .string "But truly I am full of power by\n"
    .string "the spirit of the LORD, and of\l"
    .string "judgment, and of might, to declare\l"
    .string "unto Jacob his transgression, and to\l"
    .string "Israel his sin.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_9::
    .string "Hear this, I pray you, ye heads of\n"
    .string "the house of Jacob, and princes of\l"
    .string "the house of Israel, that abhor\l"
    .string "judgment, and pervert all equity.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_10::
    .string "They build up Zion with blood, and\n"
    .string "Jerusalem with iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_11::
    .string "The heads thereof judge for reward,\n"
    .string "and the priests thereof teach for\l"
    .string "hire, and the prophets thereof\l"
    .string "divine for money: yet will they\l"
    .string "lean upon the LORD, and say, Is not\l"
    .string "the LORD among us? none evil can come\l"
    .string "upon us.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_3_12::
    .string "Therefore shall Zion for your sake\n"
    .string "be plowed as a field, and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem shall become heaps, and\l"
    .string "the mountain of the house as the high\l"
    .string "places of the forest.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_1::
    .string "But in the last days it shall come\n"
    .string "to pass, that the mountain of the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD shall be\l"
    .string "established in the top of the\l"
    .string "mountains, and it shall be exalted\l"
    .string "above the hills; and people\l"
    .string "shall flow unto it.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_2::
    .string "And many nations shall come, and\n"
    .string "say, Come, and let us go up to the\l"
    .string "mountain of the LORD, and to the\l"
    .string "house of the God of Jacob; and he\l"
    .string "will teach us of his ways, and we\l"
    .string "will walk in his paths: for the\l"
    .string "law shall go forth of Zion, and the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD from Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_3::
    .string "And he shall judge among many\n"
    .string "people, and rebuke strong nations\l"
    .string "afar off; and they shall beat their\l"
    .string "swords into plowshares, and their\l"
    .string "spears into pruninghooks: nation\l"
    .string "shall not lift up a sword against\l"
    .string "nation, neither shall they learn\l"
    .string "war any more.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_4::
    .string "But they shall sit every man under\n"
    .string "his vine and under his fig tree; and\l"
    .string "none shall make them afraid: for the\l"
    .string "mouth of the LORD of hosts hath\l"
    .string "spoken it.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_5::
    .string "For all people will walk every\n"
    .string "one in the name of his god, and we\l"
    .string "will walk in the name of the LORD\l"
    .string "our God for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_6::
    .string "In that day, saith the LORD, will I\n"
    .string "assemble her that halteth, and I\l"
    .string "will gather her that is driven out,\l"
    .string "and her that I have afflicted;"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_7::
    .string "And I will make her that halted a\n"
    .string "remnant, and her that was cast far\l"
    .string "off a strong nation: and the LORD\l"
    .string "shall reign over them in mount Zion\l"
    .string "from henceforth, even for ever$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_8::
    .string "And thou, O tower of the flock, the\n"
    .string "strong hold of the daughter of Zion,\l"
    .string "unto thee shall it come, even the\l"
    .string "first dominion; the kingdom shall\l"
    .string "come to the daughter of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_9::
    .string "Now why dost thou cry out aloud? is\n"
    .string "there no king in thee? is thy\l"
    .string "counsellor perished? for pangs\l"
    .string "have taken thee as a woman in\l"
    .string "travail.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_10::
    .string "Be in pain, and labour to bring\n"
    .string "forth, O daughter of Zion, like a\l"
    .string "woman in travail: for now shalt thou\l"
    .string "go forth out of the city, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt dwell in the field, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt go even to Babylon; there\l"
    .string "shalt thou be delivered; there the\l"
    .string "LORD shall redeem thee from the\l"
    .string "hand of thine enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_11::
    .string "Now also many nations are gathered\n"
    .string "against thee, that say, Let her be\l"
    .string "defiled, and let our eye look upon\l"
    .string "Zion.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_12::
    .string "But they know not the thoughts of\n"
    .string "the LORD, neither understand they his\l"
    .string "counsel: for he shall gather them\l"
    .string "as the sheaves into the floor.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_4_13::
    .string "Arise and thresh, O daughter of\n"
    .string "Zion: for I will make thine horn\l"
    .string "iron, and I will make thy hoofs\l"
    .string "brass: and thou shalt beat in pieces\l"
    .string "many people: and I will\l"
    .string "consecrate their gain unto the LORD,\l"
    .string "and their substance unto the Lord of\l"
    .string "the whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_1::
    .string "Now gather thyself in troops, O\n"
    .string "daughter of troops: he hath laid\l"
    .string "siege against us: they shall smite\l"
    .string "the judge of Israel with a rod upon\l"
    .string "the cheek.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_2::
    .string "But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah,\n"
    .string "though thou be little among the\l"
    .string "thousands of Judah, yet out of thee\l"
    .string "shall he come forth unto me that is\l"
    .string "to be ruler in Israel; whose goings\l"
    .string "forth have been from of old, from\l"
    .string "everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_3::
    .string "Therefore will he give them up,\n"
    .string "until the time that she which\l"
    .string "travaileth hath brought forth: then\l"
    .string "the remnant of his brethren shall\l"
    .string "return unto the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_4::
    .string "And he shall stand and feed in the\n"
    .string "strength of the LORD, in the majesty\l"
    .string "of the name of the LORD his God; and\l"
    .string "they shall abide: for now shall he\l"
    .string "be great unto the ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_5::
    .string "And this man shall be the peace,\n"
    .string "when the Assyrian shall come into\l"
    .string "our land: and when he shall tread\l"
    .string "in our palaces, then shall we\l"
    .string "raise against him seven shepherds,\l"
    .string "and eight principal men.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_6::
    .string "And they shall waste the land of\n"
    .string "Assyria with the sword, and the land\l"
    .string "of Nimrod in the entrances thereof:\l"
    .string "thus shall he deliver us from the\l"
    .string "Assyrian, when he cometh into our\l"
    .string "land, and when he treadeth within our\l"
    .string "borders.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_7::
    .string "And the remnant of Jacob shall be\n"
    .string "in the midst of many people as a\l"
    .string "dew from the LORD, as the showers\l"
    .string "upon the grass, that tarrieth not\l"
    .string "for man, nor waiteth for the sons of\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_8::
    .string "And the remnant of Jacob shall be\n"
    .string "among the Gentiles in the midst of\l"
    .string "many people as a lion among the\l"
    .string "beasts of the forest, as a young lion\l"
    .string "among the flocks of sheep: who, if\l"
    .string "he go through, both treadeth down,\l"
    .string "and teareth in pieces, and none can\l"
    .string "deliver.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_9::
    .string "Thine hand shall be lifted up\n"
    .string "upon thine adversaries, and all\l"
    .string "thine enemies shall be cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_10::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD, that I will cut\l"
    .string "off thy horses out of the midst of\l"
    .string "thee, and I will destroy thy\l"
    .string "chariots:"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_11::
    .string "And I will cut off the cities of\n"
    .string "thy land, and throw down all thy\l"
    .string "strong holds:"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_12::
    .string "And I will cut off witchcrafts out\n"
    .string "of thine hand; and thou shalt have no\l"
    .string "more soothsayers:"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_13::
    .string "Thy graven images also will I cut\n"
    .string "off, and thy standing images out of\l"
    .string "the midst of thee; and thou shalt no\l"
    .string "more worship the work of thine hands$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_14::
    .string "And I will pluck up thy groves\n"
    .string "out of the midst of thee: so will I\l"
    .string "destroy thy cities.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_5_15::
    .string "And I will execute vengeance in\n"
    .string "anger and fury upon the heathen,\l"
    .string "such as they have not heard.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_1::
    .string "Hear ye now what the LORD saith;\n"
    .string "Arise, contend thou before the\l"
    .string "mountains, and let the hills hear\l"
    .string "thy voice.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_2::
    .string "Hear ye, O mountains, the LORD’s\n"
    .string "controversy, and ye strong\l"
    .string "foundations of the earth: for the\l"
    .string "LORD hath a controversy with his\l"
    .string "people, and he will plead with\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_3::
    .string "O my people, what have I done unto\n"
    .string "thee? and wherein have I wearied\l"
    .string "thee? testify against me.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_4::
    .string "For I brought thee up out of the\n"
    .string "land of Egypt, and redeemed thee out\l"
    .string "of the house of servants; and I sent\l"
    .string "before thee Moses, Aaron, and Miriam.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_5::
    .string "O my people, remember now what\n"
    .string "Balak king of Moab consulted, and\l"
    .string "what Balaam the son of Beor answered\l"
    .string "him from Shittim unto Gilgal; that\l"
    .string "ye may know the righteousness of the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_6::
    .string "Wherewith shall I come before the\n"
    .string "LORD, and bow myself before the high\l"
    .string "God? shall I come before him with\l"
    .string "burnt offerings, with calves of a\l"
    .string "year old?"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_7::
    .string "Will the LORD be pleased with\n"
    .string "thousands of rams, or with ten\l"
    .string "thousands of rivers of oil? shall I\l"
    .string "give my firstborn for my\l"
    .string "transgression, the fruit of my body\l"
    .string "for the sin of my soul?"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_8::
    .string "He hath shewed thee, O man, what is\n"
    .string "good; and what doth the LORD require\l"
    .string "of thee, but to do justly, and to\l"
    .string "love mercy, and to walk humbly with\l"
    .string "thy God?"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_9::
    .string "The LORD’s voice crieth unto the\n"
    .string "city, and the man of wisdom shall\l"
    .string "see thy name: hear ye the rod, and who\l"
    .string "hath appointed it$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_10::
    .string "Are there yet the treasures of\n"
    .string "wickedness in the house of the\l"
    .string "wicked, and the scant measure that is\l"
    .string "abominable?"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_11::
    .string "Shall I count them pure with the\n"
    .string "wicked balances, and with the bag of\l"
    .string "deceitful weights?"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_12::
    .string "For the rich men thereof are full\n"
    .string "of violence, and the inhabitants\l"
    .string "thereof have spoken lies, and their\l"
    .string "tongue is deceitful in their mouth$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_13::
    .string "Therefore also will I make thee\n"
    .string "sick in smiting thee, in making thee\l"
    .string "desolate because of thy sins.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_14::
    .string "Thou shalt eat, but not be\n"
    .string "satisfied; and thy casting down\l"
    .string "shall be in the midst of thee; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt take hold, but shalt not\l"
    .string "deliver; and that which thou\l"
    .string "deliverest will I give up to the\l"
    .string "sword.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_15::
    .string "Thou shalt sow, but thou shalt not\n"
    .string "reap; thou shalt tread the olives,\l"
    .string "but thou shalt not anoint thee with\l"
    .string "oil; and sweet wine, but shalt not\l"
    .string "drink wine.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_6_16::
    .string "For the statutes of Omri are kept,\n"
    .string "and all the works of the house of\l"
    .string "Ahab, and ye walk in their counsels;\l"
    .string "that I should make thee a\l"
    .string "desolation, and the inhabitants\l"
    .string "thereof an hissing: therefore ye\l"
    .string "shall bear the reproach of my\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_1::
    .string "Woe is me! for I am as when they have\n"
    .string "gathered the summer fruits, as the\l"
    .string "grapegleanings of the vintage:\l"
    .string "there is no cluster to eat: my soul\l"
    .string "desired the firstripe fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_2::
    .string "The good man is perished out of the\n"
    .string "earth: and there is none upright\l"
    .string "among men: they all lie in wait for\l"
    .string "blood; they hunt every man his\l"
    .string "brother with a net.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_3::
    .string "That they may do evil with both\n"
    .string "hands earnestly, the prince asketh,\l"
    .string "and the judge asketh for a reward;\l"
    .string "and the great man, he uttereth his\l"
    .string "mischievous desire: so they wrap it\l"
    .string "up.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_4::
    .string "The best of them is as a brier: the\n"
    .string "most upright is sharper than a\l"
    .string "thorn hedge: the day of thy watchmen\l"
    .string "and thy visitation cometh; now\l"
    .string "shall be their perplexity.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_5::
    .string "Trust ye not in a friend, put ye not\n"
    .string "confidence in a guide: keep the\l"
    .string "doors of thy mouth from her that\l"
    .string "lieth in thy bosom.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_6::
    .string "For the son dishonoureth the father,\n"
    .string "the daughter riseth up against her\l"
    .string "mother, the daughter in law against\l"
    .string "her mother in law; a man’s enemies\l"
    .string "are the men of his own house.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_7::
    .string "Therefore I will look unto the\n"
    .string "LORD; I will wait for the God of my\l"
    .string "salvation: my God will hear me.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_8::
    .string "Rejoice not against me, O mine\n"
    .string "enemy: when I fall, I shall arise;\l"
    .string "when I sit in darkness, the LORD\l"
    .string "shall be a light unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_9::
    .string "I will bear the indignation of the\n"
    .string "LORD, because I have sinned against\l"
    .string "him, until he plead my cause, and\l"
    .string "execute judgment for me: he will\l"
    .string "bring me forth to the light, and I\l"
    .string "shall behold his righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_10::
    .string "Then she that is mine enemy shall\n"
    .string "see it, and shame shall cover her\l"
    .string "which said unto me, Where is the LORD\l"
    .string "thy God? mine eyes shall behold\l"
    .string "her: now shall she be trodden down\l"
    .string "as the mire of the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_11::
    .string "In the day that thy walls are to be\n"
    .string "built, in that day shall the decree\l"
    .string "be far removed.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_12::
    .string "In that day also he shall come\n"
    .string "even to thee from Assyria, and from\l"
    .string "the fortified cities, and from the\l"
    .string "fortress even to the river, and from\l"
    .string "sea to sea, and from mountain to\l"
    .string "mountain.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_13::
    .string "Notwithstanding the land shall be\n"
    .string "desolate because of them that\l"
    .string "dwell therein, for the fruit of\l"
    .string "their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_14::
    .string "Feed thy people with thy rod, the\n"
    .string "flock of thine heritage, which\l"
    .string "dwell solitarily in the wood, in\l"
    .string "the midst of Carmel: let them feed\l"
    .string "in Bashan and Gilead, as in the days\l"
    .string "of old.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_15::
    .string "According to the days of thy coming\n"
    .string "out of the land of Egypt will I\l"
    .string "shew unto him marvellous things.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_16::
    .string "The nations shall see and be\n"
    .string "confounded at all their might: they\l"
    .string "shall lay their hand upon their\l"
    .string "mouth, their ears shall be deaf.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_17::
    .string "They shall lick the dust like a\n"
    .string "serpent, they shall move out of\l"
    .string "their holes like worms of the earth:\l"
    .string "they shall be afraid of the LORD our\l"
    .string "God, and shall fear because of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_18::
    .string "Who is a God like unto thee, that\n"
    .string "pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by\l"
    .string "the transgression of the remnant of\l"
    .string "his heritage? he retaineth not his\l"
    .string "anger for ever, because he\l"
    .string "delighteth in mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_19::
    .string "He will turn again, he will have\n"
    .string "compassion upon us; he will subdue\l"
    .string "our iniquities; and thou wilt cast\l"
    .string "all their sins into the depths of\l"
    .string "the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Micah_7_20::
    .string "Thou wilt perform the truth to\n"
    .string "Jacob, and the mercy to Abraham,\l"
    .string "which thou hast sworn unto our\l"
    .string "fathers from the days of old.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_1::
    .string "The burden of Nineveh. The book of\n"
    .string "the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_2::
    .string "God is jealous, and the LORD\n"
    .string "revengeth; the LORD revengeth, and is\l"
    .string "furious; the LORD will take\l"
    .string "vengeance on his adversaries, and he\l"
    .string "reserveth wrath for his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_3::
    .string "The LORD is slow to anger, and great\n"
    .string "in power, and will not at all\l"
    .string "acquit the wicked: the LORD hath his\l"
    .string "way in the whirlwind and in the\l"
    .string "storm, and the clouds are the dust of\l"
    .string "his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_4::
    .string "He rebuketh the sea, and maketh it\n"
    .string "dry, and drieth up all the rivers:\l"
    .string "Bashan languisheth, and Carmel, and\l"
    .string "the flower of Lebanon languisheth.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_5::
    .string "The mountains quake at him, and the\n"
    .string "hills melt, and the earth is burned\l"
    .string "at his presence, yea, the world, and\l"
    .string "all that dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_6::
    .string "Who can stand before his\n"
    .string "indignation? and who can abide in the\l"
    .string "fierceness of his anger? his fury is\l"
    .string "poured out like fire, and the rocks\l"
    .string "are thrown down by him.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_7::
    .string "The LORD is good, a strong hold in\n"
    .string "the day of trouble; and he knoweth\l"
    .string "them that trust in him.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_8::
    .string "But with an overrunning flood he\n"
    .string "will make an utter end of the\l"
    .string "place thereof, and darkness shall\l"
    .string "pursue his enemies.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_9::
    .string "What do ye imagine against the LORD?\n"
    .string "he will make an utter end:\l"
    .string "affliction shall not rise up the\l"
    .string "second time.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_10::
    .string "For while they be folden together\n"
    .string "as thorns, and while they are\l"
    .string "drunken as drunkards, they shall be\l"
    .string "devoured as stubble fully dry.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_11::
    .string "There is one come out of thee, that\n"
    .string "imagineth evil against the LORD, a\l"
    .string "wicked counsellor.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_12::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; Though they be\n"
    .string "quiet, and likewise many, yet thus\l"
    .string "shall they be cut down, when he\l"
    .string "shall pass through. Though I have\l"
    .string "afflicted thee, I will afflict\l"
    .string "thee no more.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_13::
    .string "For now will I break his yoke from\n"
    .string "off thee, and will burst thy bonds\l"
    .string "in sunder.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_14::
    .string "And the LORD hath given a\n"
    .string "commandment concerning thee, that no\l"
    .string "more of thy name be sown: out of the\l"
    .string "house of thy gods will I cut off the\l"
    .string "graven image and the molten image: I\l"
    .string "will make thy grave; for thou art\l"
    .string "vile.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_1_15::
    .string "Behold upon the mountains the feet\n"
    .string "of him that bringeth good tidings,\l"
    .string "that publisheth peace! O Judah,\l"
    .string "keep thy solemn feasts, perform thy\l"
    .string "vows: for the wicked shall no more\l"
    .string "pass through thee; he is utterly cut\l"
    .string "off.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_1::
    .string "He that dasheth in pieces is come\n"
    .string "up before thy face: keep the\l"
    .string "munition, watch the way, make thy\l"
    .string "loins strong, fortify thy power\l"
    .string "mightily.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_2::
    .string "For the LORD hath turned away the\n"
    .string "excellency of Jacob, as the\l"
    .string "excellency of Israel: for the\l"
    .string "emptiers have emptied them out, and\l"
    .string "marred their vine branches.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_3::
    .string "The shield of his mighty men is\n"
    .string "made red, the valiant men are in\l"
    .string "scarlet: the chariots shall be with\l"
    .string "flaming torches in the day of his\l"
    .string "preparation, and the fir trees\l"
    .string "shall be terribly shaken.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_4::
    .string "The chariots shall rage in the\n"
    .string "streets, they shall justle one\l"
    .string "against another in the broad ways:\l"
    .string "they shall seem like torches, they\l"
    .string "shall run like the lightnings.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_5::
    .string "He shall recount his worthies:\n"
    .string "they shall stumble in their walk;\l"
    .string "they shall make haste to the wall\l"
    .string "thereof, and the defence shall be\l"
    .string "prepared.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_6::
    .string "The gates of the rivers shall be\n"
    .string "opened, and the palace shall be\l"
    .string "dissolved.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_7::
    .string "And Huzzab shall be led away\n"
    .string "captive, she shall be brought up,\l"
    .string "and her maids shall lead her as\l"
    .string "with the voice of doves, tabering\l"
    .string "upon their breasts.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_8::
    .string "But Nineveh is of old like a pool\n"
    .string "of water: yet they shall flee away.\l"
    .string "Stand, stand, shall they cry; but\l"
    .string "none shall look back.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_9::
    .string "Take ye the spoil of silver, take\n"
    .string "the spoil of gold: for there is\l"
    .string "none end of the store and glory out\l"
    .string "of all the pleasant furniture.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_10::
    .string "She is empty, and void, and waste:\n"
    .string "and the heart melteth, and the knees\l"
    .string "smite together, and much pain is in\l"
    .string "all loins, and the faces of them\l"
    .string "all gather blackness.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_11::
    .string "Where is the dwelling of the\n"
    .string "lions, and the feedingplace of the\l"
    .string "young lions, where the lion, even\l"
    .string "the old lion, walked, and the\l"
    .string "lion’s whelp, and none made them\l"
    .string "afraid?"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_12::
    .string "The lion did tear in pieces enough\n"
    .string "for his whelps, and strangled for\l"
    .string "his lionesses, and filled his\l"
    .string "holes with prey, and his dens with\l"
    .string "ravin$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_2_13::
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD of hosts, and I will burn\l"
    .string "her chariots in the smoke, and the\l"
    .string "sword shall devour thy young lions:\l"
    .string "and I will cut off thy prey from\l"
    .string "the earth, and the voice of thy\l"
    .string "messengers shall no more be heard.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_1::
    .string "Woe to the bloody city! it is all\n"
    .string "full of lies and robbery; the prey\l"
    .string "departeth not;"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_2::
    .string "The noise of a whip, and the noise\n"
    .string "of the rattling of the wheels, and\l"
    .string "of the pransing horses, and of the\l"
    .string "jumping chariots$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_3::
    .string "The horseman lifteth up both the\n"
    .string "bright sword and the glittering\l"
    .string "spear: and there is a multitude of\l"
    .string "slain, and a great number of\l"
    .string "carcases; and there is none end of\l"
    .string "their corpses; they stumble upon\l"
    .string "their corpses:"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_4::
    .string "Because of the multitude of the\n"
    .string "whoredoms of the wellfavoured\l"
    .string "harlot, the mistress of witchcrafts,\l"
    .string "that selleth nations through her\l"
    .string "whoredoms, and families through her\l"
    .string "witchcrafts$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_5::
    .string "Behold, I am against thee, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD of hosts; and I will\l"
    .string "discover thy skirts upon thy face,\l"
    .string "and I will shew the nations thy\l"
    .string "nakedness, and the kingdoms thy\l"
    .string "shame.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_6::
    .string "And I will cast abominable filth\n"
    .string "upon thee, and make thee vile, and\l"
    .string "will set thee as a gazingstock.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_7::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "all they that look upon thee\l"
    .string "shall flee from thee, and say,\l"
    .string "Nineveh is laid waste: who will\l"
    .string "bemoan her? whence shall I seek\l"
    .string "comforters for thee?"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_8::
    .string "Art thou better than populous No,\n"
    .string "that was situate among the rivers,\l"
    .string "that had the waters round about it,\l"
    .string "whose rampart was the sea, and her\l"
    .string "wall was from the sea?"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_9::
    .string "Ethiopia and Egypt were her\n"
    .string "strength, and it was infinite; Put\l"
    .string "and Lubim were thy helpers$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_10::
    .string "Yet was she carried away, she went\n"
    .string "into captivity: her young children\l"
    .string "also were dashed in pieces at the\l"
    .string "top of all the streets: and they\l"
    .string "cast lots for her honourable men,\l"
    .string "and all her great men were bound in\l"
    .string "chains.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_11::
    .string "Thou also shalt be drunken: thou\n"
    .string "shalt be hid, thou also shalt seek\l"
    .string "strength because of the enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_12::
    .string "All thy strong holds shall be\n"
    .string "like fig trees with the firstripe\l"
    .string "figs: if they be shaken, they shall\l"
    .string "even fall into the mouth of the\l"
    .string "eater.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_13::
    .string "Behold, thy people in the midst\n"
    .string "of thee are women: the gates of thy\l"
    .string "land shall be set wide open unto\l"
    .string "thine enemies: the fire shall\l"
    .string "devour thy bars.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_14::
    .string "Draw thee waters for the siege,\n"
    .string "fortify thy strong holds: go into\l"
    .string "clay, and tread the morter, make\l"
    .string "strong the brickkiln.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_15::
    .string "There shall the fire devour thee;\n"
    .string "the sword shall cut thee off, it\l"
    .string "shall eat thee up like the\l"
    .string "cankerworm: make thyself many as the\l"
    .string "cankerworm, make thyself many as the\l"
    .string "locusts.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_16::
    .string "Thou hast multiplied thy\n"
    .string "merchants above the stars of heaven:\l"
    .string "the cankerworm spoileth, and\l"
    .string "fleeth away.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_17::
    .string "Thy crowned are as the locusts, and\n"
    .string "thy captains as the great\l"
    .string "grasshoppers, which camp in the\l"
    .string "hedges in the cold day, but when the\l"
    .string "sun ariseth they flee away, and\l"
    .string "their place is not known where they\l"
    .string "are.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_18::
    .string "Thy shepherds slumber, O king of\n"
    .string "Assyria: thy nobles shall dwell\l"
    .string "in the dust: thy people is\l"
    .string "scattered upon the mountains, and no\l"
    .string "man gathereth them.$"
Bible_Text_Nahum_3_19::
    .string "There is no healing of thy bruise;\n"
    .string "thy wound is grievous: all that hear\l"
    .string "the bruit of thee shall clap the\l"
    .string "hands over thee: for upon whom hath\l"
    .string "not thy wickedness passed\l"
    .string "continually?$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_1::
    .string "The burden which Habakkuk the\n"
    .string "prophet did see.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_2::
    .string "O LORD, how long shall I cry, and\n"
    .string "thou wilt not hear! even cry out unto\l"
    .string "thee of violence, and thou wilt not\l"
    .string "save!"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_3::
    .string "Why dost thou shew me iniquity, and\n"
    .string "cause me to behold grievance? for\l"
    .string "spoiling and violence are before\l"
    .string "me: and there are that raise up\l"
    .string "strife and contention$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_4::
    .string "Therefore the law is slacked, and\n"
    .string "judgment doth never go forth: for the\l"
    .string "wicked doth compass about the\l"
    .string "righteous; therefore wrong judgment\l"
    .string "proceedeth.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_5::
    .string "Behold ye among the heathen, and\n"
    .string "regard, and wonder marvelously: for\l"
    .string "I will work a work in your days\l"
    .string "which ye will not believe, though\l"
    .string "it be told you.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_6::
    .string "For, lo, I raise up the Chaldeans,\n"
    .string "that bitter and hasty nation, which\l"
    .string "shall march through the breadth of\l"
    .string "the land, to possess the\l"
    .string "dwellingplaces that are not\l"
    .string "theirs.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_7::
    .string "They are terrible and dreadful:\n"
    .string "their judgment and their dignity\l"
    .string "shall proceed of themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_8::
    .string "Their horses also are swifter than\n"
    .string "the leopards, and are more fierce\l"
    .string "than the evening wolves: and their\l"
    .string "horsemen shall spread themselves,\l"
    .string "and their horsemen shall come from\l"
    .string "far; they shall fly as the eagle\l"
    .string "that hasteth to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_9::
    .string "They shall come all for\n"
    .string "violence: their faces shall sup\l"
    .string "up as the east wind, and they shall\l"
    .string "gather the captivity as the sand.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_10::
    .string "And they shall scoff at the kings,\n"
    .string "and the princes shall be a scorn\l"
    .string "unto them: they shall deride every\l"
    .string "strong hold; for they shall heap\l"
    .string "dust, and take it.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_11::
    .string "Then shall his mind change, and he\n"
    .string "shall pass over, and offend,\l"
    .string "imputing this his power unto his\l"
    .string "god.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_12::
    .string "Art thou not from everlasting, O\n"
    .string "LORD my God, mine Holy One? we\l"
    .string "shall not die. O LORD, thou hast\l"
    .string "ordained them for judgment; and, O\l"
    .string "mighty God, thou hast established\l"
    .string "them for correction.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_13::
    .string "Thou art of purer eyes than to\n"
    .string "behold evil, and canst not look on\l"
    .string "iniquity: wherefore lookest thou\l"
    .string "upon them that deal treacherously,\l"
    .string "and holdest thy tongue when the\l"
    .string "wicked devoureth the man that is more\l"
    .string "righteous than he?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_14::
    .string "And makest men as the fishes of the\n"
    .string "sea, as the creeping things, that\l"
    .string "have no ruler over them?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_15::
    .string "They take up all of them with the\n"
    .string "angle, they catch them in their net,\l"
    .string "and gather them in their drag:\l"
    .string "therefore they rejoice and are glad$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_16::
    .string "Therefore they sacrifice unto their\n"
    .string "net, and burn incense unto their\l"
    .string "drag; because by them their portion\l"
    .string "is fat, and their meat plenteous.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_1_17::
    .string "Shall they therefore empty their\n"
    .string "net, and not spare continually to\l"
    .string "slay the nations?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_1::
    .string "I will stand upon my watch, and\n"
    .string "set me upon the tower, and will\l"
    .string "watch to see what he will say unto\l"
    .string "me, and what I shall answer when I\l"
    .string "am reproved$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_2::
    .string "And the LORD answered me, and said,\n"
    .string "Write the vision, and make it plain\l"
    .string "upon tables, that he may run that\l"
    .string "readeth it.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_3::
    .string "For the vision is yet for an\n"
    .string "appointed time, but at the end it\l"
    .string "shall speak, and not lie: though\l"
    .string "it tarry, wait for it; because it\l"
    .string "will surely come, it will not\l"
    .string "tarry.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_4::
    .string "Behold, his soul which is lifted\n"
    .string "up is not upright in him: but the\l"
    .string "just shall live by his faith.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_5::
    .string "Yea also, because he transgresseth\n"
    .string "by wine, he is a proud man, neither\l"
    .string "keepeth at home, who enlargeth his\l"
    .string "desire as hell, and is as death, and\l"
    .string "cannot be satisfied, but gathereth\l"
    .string "unto him all nations, and heapeth\l"
    .string "unto him all people:"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_6::
    .string "Shall not all these take up a\n"
    .string "parable against him, and a taunting\l"
    .string "proverb against him, and say, Woe to\l"
    .string "him that increaseth that which is not\l"
    .string "his! how long? and to him that\l"
    .string "ladeth himself with thick clay!"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_7::
    .string "Shall they not rise up suddenly\n"
    .string "that shall bite thee, and awake that\l"
    .string "shall vex thee, and thou shalt be\l"
    .string "for booties unto them?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_8::
    .string "Because thou hast spoiled many\n"
    .string "nations, all the remnant of the\l"
    .string "people shall spoil thee; because\l"
    .string "of men’s blood, and for the violence\l"
    .string "of the land, of the city, and of all\l"
    .string "that dwell therein$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_9::
    .string "Woe to him that coveteth an evil\n"
    .string "covetousness to his house, that he\l"
    .string "may set his nest on high, that he may\l"
    .string "be delivered from the power of\l"
    .string "evil!"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_10::
    .string "Thou hast consulted shame to thy\n"
    .string "house by cutting off many people,\l"
    .string "and hast sinned against thy soul$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_11::
    .string "For the stone shall cry out of the\n"
    .string "wall, and the beam out of the timber\l"
    .string "shall answer it.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_12::
    .string "Woe to him that buildeth a town\n"
    .string "with blood, and stablisheth a city\l"
    .string "by iniquity!"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_13::
    .string "Behold, is it not of the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts that the people shall\l"
    .string "labour in the very fire, and the\l"
    .string "people shall weary themselves for\l"
    .string "very vanity?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_14::
    .string "For the earth shall be filled\n"
    .string "with the knowledge of the glory of\l"
    .string "the LORD, as the waters cover the sea$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_15::
    .string "Woe unto him that giveth his\n"
    .string "neighbour drink, that puttest thy\l"
    .string "bottle to him, and makest him\l"
    .string "drunken also, that thou mayest look\l"
    .string "on their nakedness!"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_16::
    .string "Thou art filled with shame for\n"
    .string "glory: drink thou also, and let thy\l"
    .string "foreskin be uncovered: the cup of\l"
    .string "the LORD’s right hand shall be\l"
    .string "turned unto thee, and shameful\l"
    .string "spewing shall be on thy glory$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_17::
    .string "For the violence of Lebanon shall\n"
    .string "cover thee, and the spoil of beasts,\l"
    .string "which made them afraid, because of\l"
    .string "men’s blood, and for the violence of\l"
    .string "the land, of the city, and of all\l"
    .string "that dwell therein.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_18::
    .string "What profiteth the graven image\n"
    .string "that the maker thereof hath graven\l"
    .string "it; the molten image, and a teacher\l"
    .string "of lies, that the maker of his work\l"
    .string "trusteth therein, to make dumb\l"
    .string "idols?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_19::
    .string "Woe unto him that saith to the wood,\n"
    .string "Awake; to the dumb stone, Arise, it\l"
    .string "shall teach! Behold, it is laid\l"
    .string "over with gold and silver, and there\l"
    .string "is no breath at all in the midst of\l"
    .string "it$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_2_20::
    .string "But the LORD is in his holy\n"
    .string "temple: let all the earth keep\l"
    .string "silence before him.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_1::
    .string "A prayer of Habakkuk the prophet\n"
    .string "upon Shigionoth.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_2::
    .string "O LORD, I have heard thy speech, and\n"
    .string "was afraid: O LORD, revive thy work\l"
    .string "in the midst of the years, in the\l"
    .string "midst of the years make known; in\l"
    .string "wrath remember mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_3::
    .string "God came from Teman, and the Holy\n"
    .string "One from mount Paran. Selah. His\l"
    .string "glory covered the heavens, and the\l"
    .string "earth was full of his praise.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_4::
    .string "And his brightness was as the\n"
    .string "light; he had horns coming out of his\l"
    .string "hand: and there was the hiding of his\l"
    .string "power.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_5::
    .string "Before him went the pestilence,\n"
    .string "and burning coals went forth at his\l"
    .string "feet.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_6::
    .string "He stood, and measured the earth: he\n"
    .string "beheld, and drove asunder the\l"
    .string "nations; and the everlasting\l"
    .string "mountains were scattered, the\l"
    .string "perpetual hills did bow: his ways\l"
    .string "are everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_7::
    .string "I saw the tents of Cushan in\n"
    .string "affliction: and the curtains of the\l"
    .string "land of Midian did tremble.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_8::
    .string "Was the LORD displeased against\n"
    .string "the rivers? was thine anger against\l"
    .string "the rivers? was thy wrath against the\l"
    .string "sea, that thou didst ride upon thine\l"
    .string "horses and thy chariots of\l"
    .string "salvation?"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_9::
    .string "Thy bow was made quite naked,\n"
    .string "according to the oaths of the tribes,\l"
    .string "even thy word. Selah. Thou didst\l"
    .string "cleave the earth with rivers$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_10::
    .string "The mountains saw thee, and they\n"
    .string "trembled: the overflowing of the\l"
    .string "water passed by: the deep uttered\l"
    .string "his voice, and lifted up his hands\l"
    .string "on high.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_11::
    .string "The sun and moon stood still in\n"
    .string "their habitation: at the light of\l"
    .string "thine arrows they went, and at the\l"
    .string "shining of thy glittering spear.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_12::
    .string "Thou didst march through the land\n"
    .string "in indignation, thou didst thresh the\l"
    .string "heathen in anger.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_13::
    .string "Thou wentest forth for the\n"
    .string "salvation of thy people, even for\l"
    .string "salvation with thine anointed; thou\l"
    .string "woundedst the head out of the house\l"
    .string "of the wicked, by discovering the\l"
    .string "foundation unto the neck. Selah.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_14::
    .string "Thou didst strike through with his\n"
    .string "staves the head of his villages:\l"
    .string "they came out as a whirlwind to\l"
    .string "scatter me: their rejoicing was as to\l"
    .string "devour the poor secretly.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_15::
    .string "Thou didst walk through the sea\n"
    .string "with thine horses, through the heap\l"
    .string "of great waters.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_16::
    .string "When I heard, my belly trembled;\n"
    .string "my lips quivered at the voice:\l"
    .string "rottenness entered into my bones, and\l"
    .string "I trembled in myself, that I might\l"
    .string "rest in the day of trouble: when he\l"
    .string "cometh up unto the people, he\l"
    .string "will invade them with his troops.$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_17::
    .string "Although the fig tree shall not\n"
    .string "blossom, neither shall fruit be in\l"
    .string "the vines; the labour of the olive\l"
    .string "shall fail, and the fields shall\l"
    .string "yield no meat; the flock shall be\l"
    .string "cut off from the fold, and there\l"
    .string "shall be no herd in the stalls:"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_18::
    .string "Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I\n"
    .string "will joy in the God of my salvation$"
Bible_Text_Habakkuk_3_19::
    .string "The LORD God is my strength, and he\n"
    .string "will make my feet like hinds’ feet,\l"
    .string "and he will make me to walk upon\l"
    .string "mine high places. To the chief\l"
    .string "singer on my stringed instruments.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_1::
    .string "The word of the LORD which came unto\n"
    .string "Zephaniah the son of Cushi, the son\l"
    .string "of Gedaliah, the son of Amariah, the\l"
    .string "son of Hizkiah, in the days of Josiah\l"
    .string "the son of Amon, king of Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_2::
    .string "I will utterly consume all\n"
    .string "things from off the land, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_3::
    .string "I will consume man and beast; I\n"
    .string "will consume the fowls of the\l"
    .string "heaven, and the fishes of the sea,\l"
    .string "and the stumblingblocks with the\l"
    .string "wicked: and I will cut off man from\l"
    .string "off the land, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_4::
    .string "I will also stretch out mine hand\n"
    .string "upon Judah, and upon all the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem; and I\l"
    .string "will cut off the remnant of Baal\l"
    .string "from this place, and the name of the\l"
    .string "Chemarims with the priests;"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_5::
    .string "And them that worship the host of\n"
    .string "heaven upon the housetops; and them\l"
    .string "that worship and that swear by the\l"
    .string "LORD, and that swear by Malcham;"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_6::
    .string "And them that are turned back from\n"
    .string "the LORD; and those that have not\l"
    .string "sought the LORD, nor enquired for him$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_7::
    .string "Hold thy peace at the presence of\n"
    .string "the Lord GOD: for the day of the LORD\l"
    .string "is at hand: for the LORD hath\l"
    .string "prepared a sacrifice, he hath bid\l"
    .string "his guests.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_8::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "day of the LORD’s sacrifice, that I\l"
    .string "will punish the princes, and the\l"
    .string "king’s children, and all such as\l"
    .string "are clothed with strange apparel.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_9::
    .string "In the same day also will I\n"
    .string "punish all those that leap on the\l"
    .string "threshold, which fill their\l"
    .string "masters’ houses with violence and\l"
    .string "deceit.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_10::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD, that there\l"
    .string "shall be the noise of a cry from the\l"
    .string "fish gate, and an howling from the\l"
    .string "second, and a great crashing from the\l"
    .string "hills.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_11::
    .string "Howl, ye inhabitants of Maktesh,\n"
    .string "for all the merchant people are\l"
    .string "cut down; all they that bear silver\l"
    .string "are cut off.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_12::
    .string "And it shall come to pass at that\n"
    .string "time, that I will search Jerusalem\l"
    .string "with candles, and punish the men\l"
    .string "that are settled on their lees: that\l"
    .string "say in their heart, The LORD will\l"
    .string "not do good, neither will he do\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_13::
    .string "Therefore their goods shall become\n"
    .string "a booty, and their houses a\l"
    .string "desolation: they shall also build\l"
    .string "houses, but not inhabit them; and\l"
    .string "they shall plant vineyards, but\l"
    .string "not drink the wine thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_14::
    .string "The great day of the LORD is near, it\n"
    .string "is near, and hasteth greatly, even\l"
    .string "the voice of the day of the LORD: the\l"
    .string "mighty man shall cry there\l"
    .string "bitterly.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_15::
    .string "That day is a day of wrath, a day of\n"
    .string "trouble and distress, a day of\l"
    .string "wasteness and desolation, a day of\l"
    .string "darkness and gloominess, a day of\l"
    .string "clouds and thick darkness,"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_16::
    .string "A day of the trumpet and alarm\n"
    .string "against the fenced cities, and\l"
    .string "against the high towers$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_17::
    .string "And I will bring distress upon\n"
    .string "men, that they shall walk like\l"
    .string "blind men, because they have sinned\l"
    .string "against the LORD: and their blood\l"
    .string "shall be poured out as dust, and\l"
    .string "their flesh as the dung.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_1_18::
    .string "Neither their silver nor their\n"
    .string "gold shall be able to deliver\l"
    .string "them in the day of the LORD’s wrath;\l"
    .string "but the whole land shall be\l"
    .string "devoured by the fire of his\l"
    .string "jealousy: for he shall make even a\l"
    .string "speedy riddance of all them that\l"
    .string "dwell in the land.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_1::
    .string "Gather yourselves together, yea,\n"
    .string "gather together, O nation not\l"
    .string "desired;"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_2::
    .string "Before the decree bring forth,\n"
    .string "before the day pass as the chaff,\l"
    .string "before the fierce anger of the LORD\l"
    .string "come upon you, before the day of the\l"
    .string "LORD’s anger come upon you$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_3::
    .string "Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of\n"
    .string "the earth, which have wrought his\l"
    .string "judgment; seek righteousness, seek\l"
    .string "meekness: it may be ye shall be hid\l"
    .string "in the day of the LORD’s anger.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_4::
    .string "For Gaza shall be forsaken, and\n"
    .string "Ashkelon a desolation: they shall\l"
    .string "drive out Ashdod at the noon day, and\l"
    .string "Ekron shall be rooted up.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_5::
    .string "Woe unto the inhabitants of the sea\n"
    .string "coast, the nation of the Cherethites!\l"
    .string "the word of the LORD is against you; O\l"
    .string "Canaan, the land of the\l"
    .string "Philistines, I will even destroy\l"
    .string "thee, that there shall be no\l"
    .string "inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_6::
    .string "And the sea coast shall be\n"
    .string "dwellings and cottages for\l"
    .string "shepherds, and folds for flocks.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_7::
    .string "And the coast shall be for the\n"
    .string "remnant of the house of Judah; they\l"
    .string "shall feed thereupon: in the houses\l"
    .string "of Ashkelon shall they lie down in\l"
    .string "the evening: for the LORD their God\l"
    .string "shall visit them, and turn away\l"
    .string "their captivity.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_8::
    .string "I have heard the reproach of Moab,\n"
    .string "and the revilings of the children\l"
    .string "of Ammon, whereby they have\l"
    .string "reproached my people, and\l"
    .string "magnified themselves against their\l"
    .string "border.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_9::
    .string "Therefore as I live, saith the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts, the God of Israel, Surely\l"
    .string "Moab shall be as Sodom, and the\l"
    .string "children of Ammon as Gomorrah, even\l"
    .string "the breeding of nettles, and\l"
    .string "saltpits, and a perpetual\l"
    .string "desolation: the residue of my\l"
    .string "people shall spoil them, and the\l"
    .string "remnant of my people shall\l"
    .string "possess them.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_10::
    .string "This shall they have for their\n"
    .string "pride, because they have reproached\l"
    .string "and magnified themselves against\l"
    .string "the people of the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_11::
    .string "The LORD will be terrible unto\n"
    .string "them: for he will famish all the\l"
    .string "gods of the earth; and men shall\l"
    .string "worship him, every one from his\l"
    .string "place, even all the isles of the\l"
    .string "heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_12::
    .string "Ye Ethiopians also, ye shall be\n"
    .string "slain by my sword.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_13::
    .string "And he will stretch out his hand\n"
    .string "against the north, and destroy\l"
    .string "Assyria; and will make Nineveh a\l"
    .string "desolation, and dry like a\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_14::
    .string "And flocks shall lie down in the\n"
    .string "midst of her, all the beasts of the\l"
    .string "nations: both the cormorant and the\l"
    .string "bittern shall lodge in the upper\l"
    .string "lintels of it; their voice shall\l"
    .string "sing in the windows; desolation\l"
    .string "shall be in the thresholds; for he\l"
    .string "shall uncover the cedar work.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_2_15::
    .string "This is the rejoicing city that\n"
    .string "dwelt carelessly, that said in her\l"
    .string "heart, I am, and there is none beside\l"
    .string "me: how is she become a desolation, a\l"
    .string "place for beasts to lie down in!\l"
    .string "every one that passeth by her shall\l"
    .string "hiss, and wag his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_1::
    .string "Woe to her that is filthy and\n"
    .string "polluted, to the oppressing city!"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_2::
    .string "She obeyed not the voice; she\n"
    .string "received not correction; she trusted\l"
    .string "not in the LORD; she drew not near to\l"
    .string "her God$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_3::
    .string "Her princes within her are roaring\n"
    .string "lions; her judges are evening\l"
    .string "wolves; they gnaw not the bones\l"
    .string "till the morrow.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_4::
    .string "Her prophets are light and\n"
    .string "treacherous persons: her priests\l"
    .string "have polluted the sanctuary, they\l"
    .string "have done violence to the law.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_5::
    .string "The just LORD is in the midst\n"
    .string "thereof; he will not do iniquity:\l"
    .string "every morning doth he bring his\l"
    .string "judgment to light, he faileth not;\l"
    .string "but the unjust knoweth no shame.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_6::
    .string "I have cut off the nations: their\n"
    .string "towers are desolate; I made their\l"
    .string "streets waste, that none passeth by:\l"
    .string "their cities are destroyed, so that\l"
    .string "there is no man, that there is none\l"
    .string "inhabitant.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_7::
    .string "I said, Surely thou wilt fear me,\n"
    .string "thou wilt receive instruction; so\l"
    .string "their dwelling should not be cut\l"
    .string "off, howsoever I punished them: but\l"
    .string "they rose early, and corrupted all\l"
    .string "their doings.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_8::
    .string "Therefore wait ye upon me, saith\n"
    .string "the LORD, until the day that I rise\l"
    .string "up to the prey: for my determination\l"
    .string "is to gather the nations, that I may\l"
    .string "assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon\l"
    .string "them mine indignation, even all my\l"
    .string "fierce anger: for all the earth\l"
    .string "shall be devoured with the fire of\l"
    .string "my jealousy.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_9::
    .string "For then will I turn to the\n"
    .string "people a pure language, that they\l"
    .string "may all call upon the name of the\l"
    .string "LORD, to serve him with one consent.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_10::
    .string "From beyond the rivers of Ethiopia\n"
    .string "my suppliants, even the daughter of\l"
    .string "my dispersed, shall bring mine\l"
    .string "offering.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_11::
    .string "In that day shalt thou not be\n"
    .string "ashamed for all thy doings, wherein\l"
    .string "thou hast transgressed against me:\l"
    .string "for then I will take away out of the\l"
    .string "midst of thee them that rejoice in\l"
    .string "thy pride, and thou shalt no more be\l"
    .string "haughty because of my holy mountain.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_12::
    .string "I will also leave in the midst of\n"
    .string "thee an afflicted and poor\l"
    .string "people, and they shall trust in\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_13::
    .string "The remnant of Israel shall not do\n"
    .string "iniquity, nor speak lies; neither\l"
    .string "shall a deceitful tongue be found\l"
    .string "in their mouth: for they shall feed\l"
    .string "and lie down, and none shall make\l"
    .string "them afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_14::
    .string "Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O\n"
    .string "Israel; be glad and rejoice with\l"
    .string "all the heart, O daughter of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_15::
    .string "The LORD hath taken away thy\n"
    .string "judgments, he hath cast out thine\l"
    .string "enemy: the king of Israel, even the\l"
    .string "LORD, is in the midst of thee: thou\l"
    .string "shalt not see evil any more.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_16::
    .string "In that day it shall be said to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, Fear thou not: and to\l"
    .string "Zion, Let not thine hands be slack.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_17::
    .string "The LORD thy God in the midst of\n"
    .string "thee is mighty; he will save, he\l"
    .string "will rejoice over thee with joy; he\l"
    .string "will rest in his love, he will joy\l"
    .string "over thee with singing.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_18::
    .string "I will gather them that are\n"
    .string "sorrowful for the solemn assembly,\l"
    .string "who are of thee, to whom the reproach\l"
    .string "of it was a burden.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_19::
    .string "Behold, at that time I will undo\n"
    .string "all that afflict thee: and I will\l"
    .string "save her that halteth, and gather\l"
    .string "her that was driven out; and I will\l"
    .string "get them praise and fame in every\l"
    .string "land where they have been put to\l"
    .string "shame.$"
Bible_Text_Zephaniah_3_20::
    .string "At that time will I bring you\n"
    .string "again, even in the time that I gather\l"
    .string "you: for I will make you a name and a\l"
    .string "praise among all people of the\l"
    .string "earth, when I turn back your\l"
    .string "captivity before your eyes, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_1::
    .string "In the second year of Darius the\n"
    .string "king, in the sixth month, in the\l"
    .string "first day of the month, came the word\l"
    .string "of the LORD by Haggai the prophet\l"
    .string "unto Zerubbabel the son of\l"
    .string "Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and\l"
    .string "to Joshua the son of Josedech, the\l"
    .string "high priest, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_2::
    .string "Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "saying, This people say, The time\l"
    .string "is not come, the time that the LORD’s\l"
    .string "house should be built$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_3::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD by\n"
    .string "Haggai the prophet, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_4::
    .string "Is it time for you, O ye, to dwell\n"
    .string "in your cieled houses, and this\l"
    .string "house lie waste?"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_5::
    .string "Now therefore thus saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts; Consider your ways$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_6::
    .string "Ye have sown much, and bring in\n"
    .string "little; ye eat, but ye have not\l"
    .string "enough; ye drink, but ye are not\l"
    .string "filled with drink; ye clothe you,\l"
    .string "but there is none warm; and he that\l"
    .string "earneth wages earneth wages to put\l"
    .string "it into a bag with holes.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_7::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "Consider your ways.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_8::
    .string "Go up to the mountain, and bring\n"
    .string "wood, and build the house; and I\l"
    .string "will take pleasure in it, and I\l"
    .string "will be glorified, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_9::
    .string "Ye looked for much, and, lo it came\n"
    .string "to little; and when ye brought it\l"
    .string "home, I did blow upon it. Why? saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts. Because of mine\l"
    .string "house that is waste, and ye run every\l"
    .string "man unto his own house.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_10::
    .string "Therefore the heaven over you is\n"
    .string "stayed from dew, and the earth is\l"
    .string "stayed from her fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_11::
    .string "And I called for a drought upon\n"
    .string "the land, and upon the mountains,\l"
    .string "and upon the corn, and upon the new\l"
    .string "wine, and upon the oil, and upon\l"
    .string "that which the ground bringeth forth,\l"
    .string "and upon men, and upon cattle, and\l"
    .string "upon all the labour of the hands.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_12::
    .string "Then Zerubbabel the son of\n"
    .string "Shealtiel, and Joshua the son of\l"
    .string "Josedech, the high priest, with all\l"
    .string "the remnant of the people, obeyed\l"
    .string "the voice of the LORD their God, and\l"
    .string "the words of Haggai the prophet, as\l"
    .string "the LORD their God had sent him, and\l"
    .string "the people did fear before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_13::
    .string "Then spake Haggai the LORD’s\n"
    .string "messenger in the LORD’s message unto\l"
    .string "the people, saying, I am with you,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_14::
    .string "And the LORD stirred up the spirit\n"
    .string "of Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel,\l"
    .string "governor of Judah, and the spirit of\l"
    .string "Joshua the son of Josedech, the high\l"
    .string "priest, and the spirit of all the\l"
    .string "remnant of the people; and they\l"
    .string "came and did work in the house of the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, their God,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_1_15::
    .string "In the four and twentieth day of the\n"
    .string "sixth month, in the second year of\l"
    .string "Darius the king$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_1::
    .string "In the seventh month, in the one and\n"
    .string "twentieth day of the month, came the\l"
    .string "word of the LORD by the prophet\l"
    .string "Haggai, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_2::
    .string "Speak now to Zerubbabel the son of\n"
    .string "Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and\l"
    .string "to Joshua the son of Josedech, the\l"
    .string "high priest, and to the residue of\l"
    .string "the people, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_3::
    .string "Who is left among you that saw this\n"
    .string "house in her first glory? and how do\l"
    .string "ye see it now? is it not in your eyes\l"
    .string "in comparison of it as nothing?"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_4::
    .string "Yet now be strong, O Zerubbabel,\n"
    .string "saith the LORD; and be strong, O\l"
    .string "Joshua, son of Josedech, the high\l"
    .string "priest; and be strong, all ye\l"
    .string "people of the land, saith the LORD,\l"
    .string "and work: for I am with you, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts:"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_5::
    .string "According to the word that I\n"
    .string "covenanted with you when ye came out\l"
    .string "of Egypt, so my spirit remaineth\l"
    .string "among you: fear ye not$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_6::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "Yet once, it is a little while, and\l"
    .string "I will shake the heavens, and the\l"
    .string "earth, and the sea, and the dry land;"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_7::
    .string "And I will shake all nations, and\n"
    .string "the desire of all nations shall\l"
    .string "come: and I will fill this house\l"
    .string "with glory, saith the LORD of hosts$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_8::
    .string "The silver is mine, and the gold is\n"
    .string "mine, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_9::
    .string "The glory of this latter house\n"
    .string "shall be greater than of the former,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts: and in this\l"
    .string "place will I give peace, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_10::
    .string "In the four and twentieth day of the\n"
    .string "ninth month, in the second year of\l"
    .string "Darius, came the word of the LORD by\l"
    .string "Haggai the prophet, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_11::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Ask\n"
    .string "now the priests concerning the law,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_12::
    .string "If one bear holy flesh in the skirt\n"
    .string "of his garment, and with his skirt do\l"
    .string "touch bread, or pottage, or wine, or\l"
    .string "oil, or any meat, shall it be holy?\l"
    .string "And the priests answered and said, No$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_13::
    .string "Then said Haggai, If one that is\n"
    .string "unclean by a dead body touch any of\l"
    .string "these, shall it be unclean? And the\l"
    .string "priests answered and said, It shall\l"
    .string "be unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_14::
    .string "Then answered Haggai, and said, So\n"
    .string "is this people, and so is this\l"
    .string "nation before me, saith the LORD; and\l"
    .string "so is every work of their hands; and\l"
    .string "that which they offer there is\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_15::
    .string "And now, I pray you, consider from\n"
    .string "this day and upward, from before a\l"
    .string "stone was laid upon a stone in the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_16::
    .string "Since those days were, when one came\n"
    .string "to an heap of twenty measures, there\l"
    .string "were but ten: when one came to the\l"
    .string "pressfat for to draw out fifty\l"
    .string "vessels out of the press, there were\l"
    .string "but twenty$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_17::
    .string "I smote you with blasting and with\n"
    .string "mildew and with hail in all the\l"
    .string "labours of your hands; yet ye turned\l"
    .string "not to me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_18::
    .string "Consider now from this day and\n"
    .string "upward, from the four and twentieth\l"
    .string "day of the ninth month, even from the\l"
    .string "day that the foundation of the LORD’s\l"
    .string "temple was laid, consider it.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_19::
    .string "Is the seed yet in the barn? yea, as\n"
    .string "yet the vine, and the fig tree, and\l"
    .string "the pomegranate, and the olive\l"
    .string "tree, hath not brought forth: from\l"
    .string "this day will I bless you.$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_20::
    .string "And again the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto Haggai in the four and twentieth\l"
    .string "day of the month, saying,"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_21::
    .string "Speak to Zerubbabel, governor of\n"
    .string "Judah, saying, I will shake the\l"
    .string "heavens and the earth;"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_22::
    .string "And I will overthrow the throne of\n"
    .string "kingdoms, and I will destroy the\l"
    .string "strength of the kingdoms of the\l"
    .string "heathen; and I will overthrow the\l"
    .string "chariots, and those that ride in\l"
    .string "them; and the horses and their riders\l"
    .string "shall come down, every one by the\l"
    .string "sword of his brother$"
Bible_Text_Haggai_2_23::
    .string "In that day, saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, will I take thee, O\l"
    .string "Zerubbabel, my servant, the son of\l"
    .string "Shealtiel, saith the LORD, and\l"
    .string "will make thee as a signet: for I\l"
    .string "have chosen thee, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_1::
    .string "In the eighth month, in the second\n"
    .string "year of Darius, came the word of the\l"
    .string "LORD unto Zechariah, the son of\l"
    .string "Berechiah, the son of Iddo the\l"
    .string "prophet, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_2::
    .string "The LORD hath been sore displeased\n"
    .string "with your fathers$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_3::
    .string "Therefore say thou unto them, Thus\n"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto\l"
    .string "me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I\l"
    .string "will turn unto you, saith the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_4::
    .string "Be ye not as your fathers, unto whom\n"
    .string "the former prophets have cried,\l"
    .string "saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts;\l"
    .string "Turn ye now from your evil ways, and\l"
    .string "from your evil doings: but they did\l"
    .string "not hear, nor hearken unto me, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_5::
    .string "Your fathers, where are they? and\n"
    .string "the prophets, do they live for\l"
    .string "ever?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_6::
    .string "But my words and my statutes, which\n"
    .string "I commanded my servants the\l"
    .string "prophets, did they not take hold of\l"
    .string "your fathers? and they returned and\l"
    .string "said, Like as the LORD of hosts\l"
    .string "thought to do unto us, according to\l"
    .string "our ways, and according to our\l"
    .string "doings, so hath he dealt with us$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_7::
    .string "Upon the four and twentieth day of\n"
    .string "the eleventh month, which is the\l"
    .string "month Sebat, in the second year of\l"
    .string "Darius, came the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah,\l"
    .string "the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_8::
    .string "I saw by night, and behold a man\n"
    .string "riding upon a red horse, and he stood\l"
    .string "among the myrtle trees that were in\l"
    .string "the bottom; and behind him were there\l"
    .string "red horses, speckled, and white$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_9::
    .string "Then said I, O my lord, what are\n"
    .string "these? And the angel that talked\l"
    .string "with me said unto me, I will shew\l"
    .string "thee what these be.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_10::
    .string "And the man that stood among the\n"
    .string "myrtle trees answered and said,\l"
    .string "These are they whom the LORD hath\l"
    .string "sent to walk to and fro through the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_11::
    .string "And they answered the angel of the\n"
    .string "LORD that stood among the myrtle\l"
    .string "trees, and said, We have walked to\l"
    .string "and fro through the earth, and,\l"
    .string "behold, all the earth sitteth\l"
    .string "still, and is at rest.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_12::
    .string "Then the angel of the LORD answered\n"
    .string "and said, O LORD of hosts, how long\l"
    .string "wilt thou not have mercy on\l"
    .string "Jerusalem and on the cities of\l"
    .string "Judah, against which thou hast had\l"
    .string "indignation these threescore and ten\l"
    .string "years?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_13::
    .string "And the LORD answered the angel\n"
    .string "that talked with me with good words\l"
    .string "and comfortable words$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_14::
    .string "So the angel that communed with me\n"
    .string "said unto me, Cry thou, saying, Thus\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts; I am jealous\l"
    .string "for Jerusalem and for Zion with a\l"
    .string "great jealousy.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_15::
    .string "And I am very sore displeased with\n"
    .string "the heathen that are at ease: for I\l"
    .string "was but a little displeased, and\l"
    .string "they helped forward the affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_16::
    .string "Therefore thus saith the LORD; I am\n"
    .string "returned to Jerusalem with mercies:\l"
    .string "my house shall be built in it,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts, and a line\l"
    .string "shall be stretched forth upon\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_17::
    .string "Cry yet, saying, Thus saith the LORD\n"
    .string "of hosts; My cities through\l"
    .string "prosperity shall yet be spread\l"
    .string "abroad; and the LORD shall yet\l"
    .string "comfort Zion, and shall yet choose\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_18::
    .string "Then lifted I up mine eyes, and\n"
    .string "saw, and behold four horns.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_19::
    .string "And I said unto the angel that\n"
    .string "talked with me, What be these? And he\l"
    .string "answered me, These are the horns\l"
    .string "which have scattered Judah, Israel,\l"
    .string "and Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_20::
    .string "And the LORD shewed me four\n"
    .string "carpenters.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_1_21::
    .string "Then said I, What come these to do?\n"
    .string "And he spake, saying, These are the\l"
    .string "horns which have scattered Judah, so\l"
    .string "that no man did lift up his head:\l"
    .string "but these are come to fray them, to\l"
    .string "cast out the horns of the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "which lifted up their horn over the\l"
    .string "land of Judah to scatter it.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_1::
    .string "I lifted up mine eyes again, and\n"
    .string "looked, and behold a man with a\l"
    .string "measuring line in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_2::
    .string "Then said I, Whither goest thou? And\n"
    .string "he said unto me, To measure\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, to see what is the\l"
    .string "breadth thereof, and what is the\l"
    .string "length thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_3::
    .string "And, behold, the angel that talked\n"
    .string "with me went forth, and another\l"
    .string "angel went out to meet him,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_4::
    .string "And said unto him, Run, speak to\n"
    .string "this young man, saying, Jerusalem\l"
    .string "shall be inhabited as towns without\l"
    .string "walls for the multitude of men and\l"
    .string "cattle therein:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_5::
    .string "For I, saith the LORD, will be unto\n"
    .string "her a wall of fire round about, and\l"
    .string "will be the glory in the midst of\l"
    .string "her$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_6::
    .string "Ho, ho, come forth, and flee from\n"
    .string "the land of the north, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD: for I have spread you abroad as\l"
    .string "the four winds of the heaven, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_7::
    .string "Deliver thyself, O Zion, that\n"
    .string "dwellest with the daughter of\l"
    .string "Babylon.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_8::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "After the glory hath he sent me unto\l"
    .string "the nations which spoiled you: for\l"
    .string "he that toucheth you toucheth the\l"
    .string "apple of his eye.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_9::
    .string "For, behold, I will shake mine\n"
    .string "hand upon them, and they shall be a\l"
    .string "spoil to their servants: and ye\l"
    .string "shall know that the LORD of hosts\l"
    .string "hath sent me.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_10::
    .string "Sing and rejoice, O daughter of\n"
    .string "Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will\l"
    .string "dwell in the midst of thee, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_11::
    .string "And many nations shall be joined\n"
    .string "to the LORD in that day, and shall\l"
    .string "be my people: and I will dwell in\l"
    .string "the midst of thee, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "know that the LORD of hosts hath sent\l"
    .string "me unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_12::
    .string "And the LORD shall inherit Judah\n"
    .string "his portion in the holy land, and\l"
    .string "shall choose Jerusalem again.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_2_13::
    .string "Be silent, O all flesh, before\n"
    .string "the LORD: for he is raised up out of\l"
    .string "his holy habitation.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_1::
    .string "And he shewed me Joshua the high\n"
    .string "priest standing before the angel of\l"
    .string "the LORD, and Satan standing at his\l"
    .string "right hand to resist him.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_2::
    .string "And the LORD said unto Satan, The\n"
    .string "LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the\l"
    .string "LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem\l"
    .string "rebuke thee: is not this a brand\l"
    .string "plucked out of the fire?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_3::
    .string "Now Joshua was clothed with filthy\n"
    .string "garments, and stood before the angel$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_4::
    .string "And he answered and spake unto\n"
    .string "those that stood before him, saying,\l"
    .string "Take away the filthy garments from\l"
    .string "him. And unto him he said, Behold, I\l"
    .string "have caused thine iniquity to pass\l"
    .string "from thee, and I will clothe thee\l"
    .string "with change of raiment.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_5::
    .string "And I said, Let them set a fair mitre\n"
    .string "upon his head. So they set a fair\l"
    .string "mitre upon his head, and clothed him\l"
    .string "with garments. And the angel of the\l"
    .string "LORD stood by.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_6::
    .string "And the angel of the LORD\n"
    .string "protested unto Joshua, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_7::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If\n"
    .string "thou wilt walk in my ways, and if\l"
    .string "thou wilt keep my charge, then thou\l"
    .string "shalt also judge my house, and\l"
    .string "shalt also keep my courts, and I\l"
    .string "will give thee places to walk\l"
    .string "among these that stand by$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_8::
    .string "Hear now, O Joshua the high priest,\n"
    .string "thou, and thy fellows that sit\l"
    .string "before thee: for they are men\l"
    .string "wondered at: for, behold, I will\l"
    .string "bring forth my servant the BRANCH.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_9::
    .string "For behold the stone that I have\n"
    .string "laid before Joshua; upon one stone\l"
    .string "shall be seven eyes: behold, I\l"
    .string "will engrave the graving thereof,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts, and I will\l"
    .string "remove the iniquity of that land in\l"
    .string "one day.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_3_10::
    .string "In that day, saith the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts, shall ye call every man his\l"
    .string "neighbour under the vine and under\l"
    .string "the fig tree.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_1::
    .string "And the angel that talked with me\n"
    .string "came again, and waked me, as a man\l"
    .string "that is wakened out of his sleep.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_2::
    .string "And said unto me, What seest thou?\n"
    .string "And I said, I have looked, and\l"
    .string "behold a candlestick all of gold,\l"
    .string "with a bowl upon the top of it, and\l"
    .string "his seven lamps thereon, and seven\l"
    .string "pipes to the seven lamps, which are\l"
    .string "upon the top thereof:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_3::
    .string "And two olive trees by it, one upon\n"
    .string "the right side of the bowl, and the\l"
    .string "other upon the left side thereof$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_4::
    .string "So I answered and spake to the\n"
    .string "angel that talked with me, saying,\l"
    .string "What are these, my lord?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_5::
    .string "Then the angel that talked with me\n"
    .string "answered and said unto me, Knowest\l"
    .string "thou not what these be? And I said,\l"
    .string "No, my lord$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_6::
    .string "Then he answered and spake unto me,\n"
    .string "saying, This is the word of the LORD\l"
    .string "unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by\l"
    .string "might, nor by power, but by my\l"
    .string "spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_7::
    .string "Who art thou, O great mountain?\n"
    .string "before Zerubbabel thou shalt become\l"
    .string "a plain: and he shall bring forth\l"
    .string "the headstone thereof with\l"
    .string "shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_8::
    .string "Moreover the word of the LORD came\n"
    .string "unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_9::
    .string "The hands of Zerubbabel have laid\n"
    .string "the foundation of this house; his\l"
    .string "hands shall also finish it; and\l"
    .string "thou shalt know that the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts hath sent me unto you$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_10::
    .string "For who hath despised the day of\n"
    .string "small things? for they shall\l"
    .string "rejoice, and shall see the plummet\l"
    .string "in the hand of Zerubbabel with those\l"
    .string "seven; they are the eyes of the LORD,\l"
    .string "which run to and fro through the\l"
    .string "whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_11::
    .string "Then answered I, and said unto him,\n"
    .string "What are these two olive trees upon\l"
    .string "the right side of the candlestick\l"
    .string "and upon the left side thereof?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_12::
    .string "And I answered again, and said unto\n"
    .string "him, What be these two olive\l"
    .string "branches which through the two\l"
    .string "golden pipes empty the golden\l"
    .string "oil out of themselves?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_13::
    .string "And he answered me and said, Knowest\n"
    .string "thou not what these be? And I said,\l"
    .string "No, my lord$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_4_14::
    .string "Then said he, These are the two\n"
    .string "anointed ones, that stand by the LORD\l"
    .string "of the whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_1::
    .string "Then I turned, and lifted up mine\n"
    .string "eyes, and looked, and behold a\l"
    .string "flying roll.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_2::
    .string "And he said unto me, What seest\n"
    .string "thou? And I answered, I see a flying\l"
    .string "roll; the length thereof is twenty\l"
    .string "cubits, and the breadth thereof ten\l"
    .string "cubits.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_3::
    .string "Then said he unto me, This is the\n"
    .string "curse that goeth forth over the face\l"
    .string "of the whole earth: for every one\l"
    .string "that stealeth shall be cut off as\l"
    .string "on this side according to it; and\l"
    .string "every one that sweareth shall be\l"
    .string "cut off as on that side according to\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_4::
    .string "I will bring it forth, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts, and it shall enter\l"
    .string "into the house of the thief, and into\l"
    .string "the house of him that sweareth\l"
    .string "falsely by my name: and it shall\l"
    .string "remain in the midst of his house, and\l"
    .string "shall consume it with the timber\l"
    .string "thereof and the stones thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_5::
    .string "Then the angel that talked with me\n"
    .string "went forth, and said unto me, Lift up\l"
    .string "now thine eyes, and see what is this\l"
    .string "that goeth forth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_6::
    .string "And I said, What is it? And he said,\n"
    .string "This is an ephah that goeth forth. He\l"
    .string "said moreover, This is their\l"
    .string "resemblance through all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_7::
    .string "And, behold, there was lifted up a\n"
    .string "talent of lead: and this is a woman\l"
    .string "that sitteth in the midst of the\l"
    .string "ephah.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_8::
    .string "And he said, This is wickedness. And\n"
    .string "he cast it into the midst of the\l"
    .string "ephah; and he cast the weight of\l"
    .string "lead upon the mouth thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_9::
    .string "Then lifted I up mine eyes, and\n"
    .string "looked, and, behold, there came out\l"
    .string "two women, and the wind was in their\l"
    .string "wings; for they had wings like the\l"
    .string "wings of a stork: and they lifted up\l"
    .string "the ephah between the earth and the\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_10::
    .string "Then said I to the angel that\n"
    .string "talked with me, Whither do these\l"
    .string "bear the ephah?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_5_11::
    .string "And he said unto me, To build it an\n"
    .string "house in the land of Shinar: and it\l"
    .string "shall be established, and set there\l"
    .string "upon her own base$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_1::
    .string "And I turned, and lifted up mine\n"
    .string "eyes, and looked, and, behold, there\l"
    .string "came four chariots out from between\l"
    .string "two mountains; and the mountains were\l"
    .string "mountains of brass.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_2::
    .string "In the first chariot were red\n"
    .string "horses; and in the second chariot\l"
    .string "black horses;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_3::
    .string "And in the third chariot white\n"
    .string "horses; and in the fourth chariot\l"
    .string "grisled and bay horses$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_4::
    .string "Then I answered and said unto the\n"
    .string "angel that talked with me, What are\l"
    .string "these, my lord?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_5::
    .string "And the angel answered and said\n"
    .string "unto me, These are the four spirits\l"
    .string "of the heavens, which go forth from\l"
    .string "standing before the LORD of all the\l"
    .string "earth$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_6::
    .string "The black horses which are therein\n"
    .string "go forth into the north country; and\l"
    .string "the white go forth after them; and\l"
    .string "the grisled go forth toward the\l"
    .string "south country.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_7::
    .string "And the bay went forth, and sought\n"
    .string "to go that they might walk to and fro\l"
    .string "through the earth: and he said, Get\l"
    .string "you hence, walk to and fro through\l"
    .string "the earth. So they walked to and fro\l"
    .string "through the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_8::
    .string "Then cried he upon me, and spake\n"
    .string "unto me, saying, Behold, these that\l"
    .string "go toward the north country have\l"
    .string "quieted my spirit in the north\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_9::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_10::
    .string "Take of them of the captivity, even\n"
    .string "of Heldai, of Tobijah, and of\l"
    .string "Jedaiah, which are come from\l"
    .string "Babylon, and come thou the same day,\l"
    .string "and go into the house of Josiah the\l"
    .string "son of Zephaniah;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_11::
    .string "Then take silver and gold, and make\n"
    .string "crowns, and set them upon the head of\l"
    .string "Joshua the son of Josedech, the high\l"
    .string "priest;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_12::
    .string "And speak unto him, saying, Thus\n"
    .string "speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying,\l"
    .string "Behold the man whose name is The\l"
    .string "BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of\l"
    .string "his place, and he shall build the\l"
    .string "temple of the LORD:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_13::
    .string "Even he shall build the temple\n"
    .string "of the LORD; and he shall bear the\l"
    .string "glory, and shall sit and rule upon\l"
    .string "his throne; and he shall be a\l"
    .string "priest upon his throne: and the\l"
    .string "counsel of peace shall be between\l"
    .string "them both$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_14::
    .string "And the crowns shall be to Helem,\n"
    .string "and to Tobijah, and to Jedaiah, and\l"
    .string "to Hen the son of Zephaniah, for a\l"
    .string "memorial in the temple of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_6_15::
    .string "And they that are far off shall\n"
    .string "come and build in the temple of the\l"
    .string "LORD, and ye shall know that the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you.\l"
    .string "And this shall come to pass, if ye\l"
    .string "will diligently obey the voice of\l"
    .string "the LORD your God.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in the fourth\n"
    .string "year of king Darius, that the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD came unto Zechariah in the\l"
    .string "fourth day of the ninth month, even\l"
    .string "in Chisleu;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_2::
    .string "When they had sent unto the house of\n"
    .string "God Sherezer and Regemmelech, and\l"
    .string "their men, to pray before the LORD,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_3::
    .string "And to speak unto the priests\n"
    .string "which were in the house of the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts, and to the prophets,\l"
    .string "saying, Should I weep in the fifth\l"
    .string "month, separating myself, as I have\l"
    .string "done these so many years?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_4::
    .string "Then came the word of the LORD of\n"
    .string "hosts unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_5::
    .string "Speak unto all the people of the\n"
    .string "land, and to the priests, saying,\l"
    .string "When ye fasted and mourned in the\l"
    .string "fifth and seventh month, even those\l"
    .string "seventy years, did ye at all fast\l"
    .string "unto me, even to me?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_6::
    .string "And when ye did eat, and when ye did\n"
    .string "drink, did not ye eat for\l"
    .string "yourselves, and drink for\l"
    .string "yourselves?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_7::
    .string "Should ye not hear the words which\n"
    .string "the LORD hath cried by the former\l"
    .string "prophets, when Jerusalem was\l"
    .string "inhabited and in prosperity, and\l"
    .string "the cities thereof round about her,\l"
    .string "when men inhabited the south and the\l"
    .string "plain?"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_8::
    .string "And the word of the LORD came unto\n"
    .string "Zechariah, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_9::
    .string "Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts,\n"
    .string "saying, Execute true judgment, and\l"
    .string "shew mercy and compassions every man\l"
    .string "to his brother:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_10::
    .string "And oppress not the widow, nor the\n"
    .string "fatherless, the stranger, nor the\l"
    .string "poor; and let none of you imagine\l"
    .string "evil against his brother in your\l"
    .string "heart$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_11::
    .string "But they refused to hearken, and\n"
    .string "pulled away the shoulder, and\l"
    .string "stopped their ears, that they\l"
    .string "should not hear.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_12::
    .string "Yea, they made their hearts as an\n"
    .string "adamant stone, lest they should\l"
    .string "hear the law, and the words which the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts hath sent in his\l"
    .string "spirit by the former prophets:\l"
    .string "therefore came a great wrath from the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_13::
    .string "Therefore it is come to pass, that\n"
    .string "as he cried, and they would not hear;\l"
    .string "so they cried, and I would not hear,\l"
    .string "saith the LORD of hosts:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_7_14::
    .string "But I scattered them with a\n"
    .string "whirlwind among all the nations\l"
    .string "whom they knew not. Thus the land was\l"
    .string "desolate after them, that no man\l"
    .string "passed through nor returned: for they\l"
    .string "laid the pleasant land desolate$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_1::
    .string "Again the word of the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "came to me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_2::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I was\n"
    .string "jealous for Zion with great\l"
    .string "jealousy, and I was jealous for her\l"
    .string "with great fury$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_3::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD; I am returned\n"
    .string "unto Zion, and will dwell in the\l"
    .string "midst of Jerusalem: and Jerusalem\l"
    .string "shall be called a city of truth;\l"
    .string "and the mountain of the LORD of hosts\l"
    .string "the holy mountain.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; There\n"
    .string "shall yet old men and old women\l"
    .string "dwell in the streets of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and every man with his staff in his\l"
    .string "hand for very age.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_5::
    .string "And the streets of the city shall\n"
    .string "be full of boys and girls playing\l"
    .string "in the streets thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_6::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If it\n"
    .string "be marvellous in the eyes of the\l"
    .string "remnant of this people in these\l"
    .string "days, should it also be marvellous\l"
    .string "in mine eyes? saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_7::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts;\n"
    .string "Behold, I will save my people\l"
    .string "from the east country, and from the\l"
    .string "west country;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_8::
    .string "And I will bring them, and they\n"
    .string "shall dwell in the midst of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: and they shall be my\l"
    .string "people, and I will be their God, in\l"
    .string "truth and in righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_9::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Let\n"
    .string "your hands be strong, ye that hear in\l"
    .string "these days these words by the mouth\l"
    .string "of the prophets, which were in the\l"
    .string "day that the foundation of the house\l"
    .string "of the LORD of hosts was laid, that\l"
    .string "the temple might be built.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_10::
    .string "For before these days there was no\n"
    .string "hire for man, nor any hire for beast;\l"
    .string "neither was there any peace to him\l"
    .string "that went out or came in because of\l"
    .string "the affliction: for I set all men\l"
    .string "every one against his neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_11::
    .string "But now I will not be unto the\n"
    .string "residue of this people as in the\l"
    .string "former days, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_12::
    .string "For the seed shall be prosperous;\n"
    .string "the vine shall give her fruit, and\l"
    .string "the ground shall give her increase,\l"
    .string "and the heavens shall give their\l"
    .string "dew; and I will cause the remnant of\l"
    .string "this people to possess all these\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_13::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that as\n"
    .string "ye were a curse among the heathen, O\l"
    .string "house of Judah, and house of Israel;\l"
    .string "so will I save you, and ye shall be\l"
    .string "a blessing: fear not, but let your\l"
    .string "hands be strong.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_14::
    .string "For thus saith the LORD of hosts; As\n"
    .string "I thought to punish you, when your\l"
    .string "fathers provoked me to wrath, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts, and I repented\l"
    .string "not:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_15::
    .string "So again have I thought in these\n"
    .string "days to do well unto Jerusalem and\l"
    .string "to the house of Judah: fear ye not$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_16::
    .string "These are the things that ye shall\n"
    .string "do; Speak ye every man the truth to\l"
    .string "his neighbour; execute the judgment\l"
    .string "of truth and peace in your gates:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_17::
    .string "And let none of you imagine evil in\n"
    .string "your hearts against his neighbour;\l"
    .string "and love no false oath: for all\l"
    .string "these are things that I hate, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_18::
    .string "And the word of the LORD of hosts\n"
    .string "came unto me, saying,"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_19::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The\n"
    .string "fast of the fourth month, and the\l"
    .string "fast of the fifth, and the fast of the\l"
    .string "seventh, and the fast of the tenth,\l"
    .string "shall be to the house of Judah joy\l"
    .string "and gladness, and cheerful feasts;\l"
    .string "therefore love the truth and peace$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_20::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; It\n"
    .string "shall yet come to pass, that there\l"
    .string "shall come people, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of many cities:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_21::
    .string "And the inhabitants of one city\n"
    .string "shall go to another, saying, Let us\l"
    .string "go speedily to pray before the\l"
    .string "LORD, and to seek the LORD of hosts: I\l"
    .string "will go also$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_22::
    .string "Yea, many people and strong\n"
    .string "nations shall come to seek the LORD\l"
    .string "of hosts in Jerusalem, and to pray\l"
    .string "before the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_8_23::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD of hosts; In\n"
    .string "those days it shall come to pass,\l"
    .string "that ten men shall take hold out of\l"
    .string "all languages of the nations, even\l"
    .string "shall take hold of the skirt of him\l"
    .string "that is a Jew, saying, We will go\l"
    .string "with you: for we have heard that God\l"
    .string "is with you.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_1::
    .string "The burden of the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "in the land of Hadrach, and Damascus\l"
    .string "shall be the rest thereof: when the\l"
    .string "eyes of man, as of all the tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel, shall be toward the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_2::
    .string "And Hamath also shall border\n"
    .string "thereby; Tyrus, and Zidon, though it\l"
    .string "be very wise.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_3::
    .string "And Tyrus did build herself a\n"
    .string "strong hold, and heaped up silver\l"
    .string "as the dust, and fine gold as the\l"
    .string "mire of the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_4::
    .string "Behold, the LORD will cast her\n"
    .string "out, and he will smite her power in\l"
    .string "the sea; and she shall be devoured\l"
    .string "with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_5::
    .string "Ashkelon shall see it, and fear;\n"
    .string "Gaza also shall see it, and be very\l"
    .string "sorrowful, and Ekron; for her\l"
    .string "expectation shall be ashamed; and\l"
    .string "the king shall perish from Gaza,\l"
    .string "and Ashkelon shall not be\l"
    .string "inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_6::
    .string "And a bastard shall dwell in\n"
    .string "Ashdod, and I will cut off the\l"
    .string "pride of the Philistines.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_7::
    .string "And I will take away his blood out\n"
    .string "of his mouth, and his abominations\l"
    .string "from between his teeth: but he that\l"
    .string "remaineth, even he, shall be for our\l"
    .string "God, and he shall be as a governor\l"
    .string "in Judah, and Ekron as a Jebusite.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_8::
    .string "And I will encamp about mine house\n"
    .string "because of the army, because of him\l"
    .string "that passeth by, and because of him\l"
    .string "that returneth: and no oppressor\l"
    .string "shall pass through them any more:\l"
    .string "for now have I seen with mine eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_9::
    .string "Rejoice greatly, O daughter of\n"
    .string "Zion; shout, O daughter of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: behold, thy King cometh\l"
    .string "unto thee: he is just, and having\l"
    .string "salvation; lowly, and riding upon\l"
    .string "an ass, and upon a colt the foal of\l"
    .string "an ass.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_10::
    .string "And I will cut off the chariot from\n"
    .string "Ephraim, and the horse from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and the battle bow\l"
    .string "shall be cut off: and he shall\l"
    .string "speak peace unto the heathen: and\l"
    .string "his dominion shall be from sea even\l"
    .string "to sea, and from the river even to the\l"
    .string "ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_11::
    .string "As for thee also, by the blood of\n"
    .string "thy covenant I have sent forth thy\l"
    .string "prisoners out of the pit wherein is\l"
    .string "no water.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_12::
    .string "Turn you to the strong hold, ye\n"
    .string "prisoners of hope: even to day do I\l"
    .string "declare that I will render double\l"
    .string "unto thee;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_13::
    .string "When I have bent Judah for me,\n"
    .string "filled the bow with Ephraim, and\l"
    .string "raised up thy sons, O Zion, against\l"
    .string "thy sons, O Greece, and made thee as\l"
    .string "the sword of a mighty man$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_14::
    .string "And the LORD shall be seen over\n"
    .string "them, and his arrow shall go forth\l"
    .string "as the lightning: and the LORD God\l"
    .string "shall blow the trumpet, and shall\l"
    .string "go with whirlwinds of the south.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_15::
    .string "The LORD of hosts shall defend\n"
    .string "them; and they shall devour, and\l"
    .string "subdue with sling stones; and they\l"
    .string "shall drink, and make a noise as\l"
    .string "through wine; and they shall be\l"
    .string "filled like bowls, and as the\l"
    .string "corners of the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_16::
    .string "And the LORD their God shall save\n"
    .string "them in that day as the flock of his\l"
    .string "people: for they shall be as the\l"
    .string "stones of a crown, lifted up as an\l"
    .string "ensign upon his land.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_9_17::
    .string "For how great is his goodness, and\n"
    .string "how great is his beauty! corn shall\l"
    .string "make the young men cheerful, and new\l"
    .string "wine the maids.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_1::
    .string "Ask ye of the LORD rain in the time\n"
    .string "of the latter rain; so the LORD\l"
    .string "shall make bright clouds, and give\l"
    .string "them showers of rain, to every one\l"
    .string "grass in the field.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_2::
    .string "For the idols have spoken vanity,\n"
    .string "and the diviners have seen a lie, and\l"
    .string "have told false dreams; they\l"
    .string "comfort in vain: therefore they went\l"
    .string "their way as a flock, they were\l"
    .string "troubled, because there was no\l"
    .string "shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_3::
    .string "Mine anger was kindled against the\n"
    .string "shepherds, and I punished the\l"
    .string "goats: for the LORD of hosts hath\l"
    .string "visited his flock the house of\l"
    .string "Judah, and hath made them as his\l"
    .string "goodly horse in the battle.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_4::
    .string "Out of him came forth the corner,\n"
    .string "out of him the nail, out of him the\l"
    .string "battle bow, out of him every\l"
    .string "oppressor together.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_5::
    .string "And they shall be as mighty men,\n"
    .string "which tread down their enemies in the\l"
    .string "mire of the streets in the battle:\l"
    .string "and they shall fight, because the\l"
    .string "LORD is with them, and the riders on\l"
    .string "horses shall be confounded.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_6::
    .string "And I will strengthen the house of\n"
    .string "Judah, and I will save the house of\l"
    .string "Joseph, and I will bring them again\l"
    .string "to place them; for I have mercy\l"
    .string "upon them: and they shall be as\l"
    .string "though I had not cast them off: for I\l"
    .string "am the LORD their God, and will hear\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_7::
    .string "And they of Ephraim shall be like\n"
    .string "a mighty man, and their heart shall\l"
    .string "rejoice as through wine: yea, their\l"
    .string "children shall see it, and be\l"
    .string "glad; their heart shall rejoice in\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_8::
    .string "I will hiss for them, and gather\n"
    .string "them; for I have redeemed them: and\l"
    .string "they shall increase as they have\l"
    .string "increased.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_9::
    .string "And I will sow them among the\n"
    .string "people: and they shall remember me\l"
    .string "in far countries; and they shall\l"
    .string "live with their children, and turn\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_10::
    .string "I will bring them again also out\n"
    .string "of the land of Egypt, and gather\l"
    .string "them out of Assyria; and I will\l"
    .string "bring them into the land of Gilead\l"
    .string "and Lebanon; and place shall not\l"
    .string "be found for them.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_11::
    .string "And he shall pass through the sea\n"
    .string "with affliction, and shall smite\l"
    .string "the waves in the sea, and all the\l"
    .string "deeps of the river shall dry up:\l"
    .string "and the pride of Assyria shall be\l"
    .string "brought down, and the sceptre of\l"
    .string "Egypt shall depart away.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_10_12::
    .string "And I will strengthen them in the\n"
    .string "LORD; and they shall walk up and\l"
    .string "down in his name, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_1::
    .string "Open thy doors, O Lebanon, that the\n"
    .string "fire may devour thy cedars.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_2::
    .string "Howl, fir tree; for the cedar is\n"
    .string "fallen; because the mighty are\l"
    .string "spoiled: howl, O ye oaks of Bashan;\l"
    .string "for the forest of the vintage is come\l"
    .string "down.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_3::
    .string "There is a voice of the howling of\n"
    .string "the shepherds; for their glory is\l"
    .string "spoiled: a voice of the roaring of\l"
    .string "young lions; for the pride of Jordan\l"
    .string "is spoiled.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_4::
    .string "Thus saith the LORD my God; Feed the\n"
    .string "flock of the slaughter;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_5::
    .string "Whose possessors slay them, and\n"
    .string "hold themselves not guilty: and\l"
    .string "they that sell them say, Blessed be\l"
    .string "the LORD; for I am rich: and their own\l"
    .string "shepherds pity them not$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_6::
    .string "For I will no more pity the\n"
    .string "inhabitants of the land, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD: but, lo, I will deliver the\l"
    .string "men every one into his neighbour’s\l"
    .string "hand, and into the hand of his king:\l"
    .string "and they shall smite the land, and\l"
    .string "out of their hand I will not\l"
    .string "deliver them.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_7::
    .string "And I will feed the flock of\n"
    .string "slaughter, even you, O poor of the\l"
    .string "flock. And I took unto me two staves;\l"
    .string "the one I called Beauty, and the\l"
    .string "other I called Bands; and I fed the\l"
    .string "flock.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_8::
    .string "Three shepherds also I cut off in\n"
    .string "one month; and my soul lothed them,\l"
    .string "and their soul also abhorred me.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_9::
    .string "Then said I, I will not feed you:\n"
    .string "that that dieth, let it die; and that\l"
    .string "that is to be cut off, let it be cut\l"
    .string "off; and let the rest eat every one\l"
    .string "the flesh of another.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_10::
    .string "And I took my staff, even Beauty,\n"
    .string "and cut it asunder, that I might\l"
    .string "break my covenant which I had made\l"
    .string "with all the people.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_11::
    .string "And it was broken in that day: and so\n"
    .string "the poor of the flock that waited\l"
    .string "upon me knew that it was the word of\l"
    .string "the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_12::
    .string "And I said unto them, If ye think\n"
    .string "good, give me my price; and if not,\l"
    .string "forbear. So they weighed for my\l"
    .string "price thirty pieces of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_13::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, Cast it\n"
    .string "unto the potter: a goodly price\l"
    .string "that I was prised at of them. And I\l"
    .string "took the thirty pieces of silver,\l"
    .string "and cast them to the potter in the\l"
    .string "house of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_14::
    .string "Then I cut asunder mine other staff,\n"
    .string "even Bands, that I might break the\l"
    .string "brotherhood between Judah and\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_15::
    .string "And the LORD said unto me, Take unto\n"
    .string "thee yet the instruments of a\l"
    .string "foolish shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_16::
    .string "For, lo, I will raise up a\n"
    .string "shepherd in the land, which shall\l"
    .string "not visit those that be cut off,\l"
    .string "neither shall seek the young one,\l"
    .string "nor heal that that is broken, nor\l"
    .string "feed that that standeth still: but\l"
    .string "he shall eat the flesh of the fat,\l"
    .string "and tear their claws in pieces.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_11_17::
    .string "Woe to the idol shepherd that\n"
    .string "leaveth the flock! the sword shall\l"
    .string "be upon his arm, and upon his right\l"
    .string "eye: his arm shall be clean dried\l"
    .string "up, and his right eye shall be\l"
    .string "utterly darkened.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_1::
    .string "The burden of the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "for Israel, saith the LORD, which\l"
    .string "stretcheth forth the heavens, and\l"
    .string "layeth the foundation of the earth,\l"
    .string "and formeth the spirit of man within\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_2::
    .string "Behold, I will make Jerusalem a\n"
    .string "cup of trembling unto all the\l"
    .string "people round about, when they\l"
    .string "shall be in the siege both against\l"
    .string "Judah and against Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_3::
    .string "And in that day will I make\n"
    .string "Jerusalem a burdensome stone for\l"
    .string "all people: all that burden\l"
    .string "themselves with it shall be cut in\l"
    .string "pieces, though all the people of\l"
    .string "the earth be gathered together\l"
    .string "against it.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_4::
    .string "In that day, saith the LORD, I will\n"
    .string "smite every horse with astonishment,\l"
    .string "and his rider with madness: and I\l"
    .string "will open mine eyes upon the house\l"
    .string "of Judah, and will smite every horse\l"
    .string "of the people with blindness.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_5::
    .string "And the governors of Judah shall\n"
    .string "say in their heart, The inhabitants\l"
    .string "of Jerusalem shall be my strength\l"
    .string "in the LORD of hosts their God.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_6::
    .string "In that day will I make the\n"
    .string "governors of Judah like an hearth of\l"
    .string "fire among the wood, and like a torch\l"
    .string "of fire in a sheaf; and they shall\l"
    .string "devour all the people round\l"
    .string "about, on the right hand and on the\l"
    .string "left: and Jerusalem shall be\l"
    .string "inhabited again in her own place,\l"
    .string "even in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_7::
    .string "The LORD also shall save the tents\n"
    .string "of Judah first, that the glory of the\l"
    .string "house of David and the glory of the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of Jerusalem do not\l"
    .string "magnify themselves against Judah.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_8::
    .string "In that day shall the LORD defend\n"
    .string "the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and he\l"
    .string "that is feeble among them at that\l"
    .string "day shall be as David; and the house\l"
    .string "of David shall be as God, as the\l"
    .string "angel of the LORD before them.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_9::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that I will seek to destroy\l"
    .string "all the nations that come against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_10::
    .string "And I will pour upon the house of\n"
    .string "David, and upon the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and\l"
    .string "of supplications: and they shall\l"
    .string "look upon me whom they have pierced,\l"
    .string "and they shall mourn for him, as one\l"
    .string "mourneth for his only son, and\l"
    .string "shall be in bitterness for him, as\l"
    .string "one that is in bitterness for his\l"
    .string "firstborn.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_11::
    .string "In that day shall there be a great\n"
    .string "mourning in Jerusalem, as the\l"
    .string "mourning of Hadadrimmon in the\l"
    .string "valley of Megiddon.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_12::
    .string "And the land shall mourn, every\n"
    .string "family apart; the family of the\l"
    .string "house of David apart, and their\l"
    .string "wives apart; the family of the house\l"
    .string "of Nathan apart, and their wives\l"
    .string "apart;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_13::
    .string "The family of the house of Levi\n"
    .string "apart, and their wives apart; the\l"
    .string "family of Shimei apart, and their\l"
    .string "wives apart;"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_12_14::
    .string "All the families that remain,\n"
    .string "every family apart, and their wives\l"
    .string "apart$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_1::
    .string "In that day there shall be a\n"
    .string "fountain opened to the house of\l"
    .string "David and to the inhabitants of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem for sin and for\l"
    .string "uncleanness.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_2::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, saith the LORD of hosts, that I\l"
    .string "will cut off the names of the idols\l"
    .string "out of the land, and they shall no\l"
    .string "more be remembered: and also I will\l"
    .string "cause the prophets and the unclean\l"
    .string "spirit to pass out of the land.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_3::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "when any shall yet prophesy, then\l"
    .string "his father and his mother that begat\l"
    .string "him shall say unto him, Thou shalt\l"
    .string "not live; for thou speakest lies in\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD: and his father\l"
    .string "and his mother that begat him shall\l"
    .string "thrust him through when he\l"
    .string "prophesieth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_4::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the prophets shall be\l"
    .string "ashamed every one of his vision, when\l"
    .string "he hath prophesied; neither shall\l"
    .string "they wear a rough garment to deceive:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_5::
    .string "But he shall say, I am no prophet,\n"
    .string "I am an husbandman; for man taught me\l"
    .string "to keep cattle from my youth$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_6::
    .string "And one shall say unto him, What\n"
    .string "are these wounds in thine hands? Then\l"
    .string "he shall answer, Those with which I\l"
    .string "was wounded in the house of my\l"
    .string "friends.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_7::
    .string "Awake, O sword, against my\n"
    .string "shepherd, and against the man that\l"
    .string "is my fellow, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts: smite the shepherd, and the\l"
    .string "sheep shall be scattered: and I\l"
    .string "will turn mine hand upon the\l"
    .string "little ones.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_8::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that in\n"
    .string "all the land, saith the LORD, two\l"
    .string "parts therein shall be cut off and\l"
    .string "die; but the third shall be left\l"
    .string "therein.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_13_9::
    .string "And I will bring the third part\n"
    .string "through the fire, and will refine\l"
    .string "them as silver is refined, and will\l"
    .string "try them as gold is tried: they\l"
    .string "shall call on my name, and I will\l"
    .string "hear them: I will say, It is my\l"
    .string "people: and they shall say, The\l"
    .string "LORD is my God.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_1::
    .string "Behold, the day of the LORD cometh,\n"
    .string "and thy spoil shall be divided in\l"
    .string "the midst of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_2::
    .string "For I will gather all nations\n"
    .string "against Jerusalem to battle; and\l"
    .string "the city shall be taken, and the\l"
    .string "houses rifled, and the women\l"
    .string "ravished; and half of the city\l"
    .string "shall go forth into captivity, and\l"
    .string "the residue of the people shall\l"
    .string "not be cut off from the city.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_3::
    .string "Then shall the LORD go forth, and\n"
    .string "fight against those nations, as when\l"
    .string "he fought in the day of battle.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_4::
    .string "And his feet shall stand in that\n"
    .string "day upon the mount of Olives, which\l"
    .string "is before Jerusalem on the east, and\l"
    .string "the mount of Olives shall cleave\l"
    .string "in the midst thereof toward the east\l"
    .string "and toward the west, and there shall\l"
    .string "be a very great valley; and half of\l"
    .string "the mountain shall remove toward\l"
    .string "the north, and half of it toward the\l"
    .string "south.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_5::
    .string "And ye shall flee to the valley\n"
    .string "of the mountains; for the valley of\l"
    .string "the mountains shall reach unto\l"
    .string "Azal: yea, ye shall flee, like as\l"
    .string "ye fled from before the earthquake\l"
    .string "in the days of Uzziah king of Judah:\l"
    .string "and the LORD my God shall come, and\l"
    .string "all the saints with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_6::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that the light shall not be\l"
    .string "clear, nor dark:"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_7::
    .string "But it shall be one day which\n"
    .string "shall be known to the LORD, not day,\l"
    .string "nor night: but it shall come to\l"
    .string "pass, that at evening time it shall\l"
    .string "be light$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_8::
    .string "And it shall be in that day, that\n"
    .string "living waters shall go out from\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; half of them toward the\l"
    .string "former sea, and half of them toward\l"
    .string "the hinder sea: in summer and in\l"
    .string "winter shall it be.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_9::
    .string "And the LORD shall be king over\n"
    .string "all the earth: in that day shall\l"
    .string "there be one LORD, and his name one.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_10::
    .string "All the land shall be turned as a\n"
    .string "plain from Geba to Rimmon south of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: and it shall be lifted\l"
    .string "up, and inhabited in her place,\l"
    .string "from Benjamin’s gate unto the place\l"
    .string "of the first gate, unto the corner\l"
    .string "gate, and from the tower of Hananeel\l"
    .string "unto the king’s winepresses.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_11::
    .string "And men shall dwell in it, and\n"
    .string "there shall be no more utter\l"
    .string "destruction; but Jerusalem shall\l"
    .string "be safely inhabited.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_12::
    .string "And this shall be the plague\n"
    .string "wherewith the LORD will smite all\l"
    .string "the people that have fought\l"
    .string "against Jerusalem; Their flesh\l"
    .string "shall consume away while they\l"
    .string "stand upon their feet, and their\l"
    .string "eyes shall consume away in their\l"
    .string "holes, and their tongue shall\l"
    .string "consume away in their mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_13::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in that\n"
    .string "day, that a great tumult from the\l"
    .string "LORD shall be among them; and they\l"
    .string "shall lay hold every one on the\l"
    .string "hand of his neighbour, and his hand\l"
    .string "shall rise up against the hand of\l"
    .string "his neighbour.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_14::
    .string "And Judah also shall fight at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem; and the wealth of all\l"
    .string "the heathen round about shall be\l"
    .string "gathered together, gold, and\l"
    .string "silver, and apparel, in great\l"
    .string "abundance.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_15::
    .string "And so shall be the plague of the\n"
    .string "horse, of the mule, of the camel,\l"
    .string "and of the ass, and of all the\l"
    .string "beasts that shall be in these tents,\l"
    .string "as this plague.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_16::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "every one that is left of all the\l"
    .string "nations which came against\l"
    .string "Jerusalem shall even go up from\l"
    .string "year to year to worship the King, the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts, and to keep the feast\l"
    .string "of tabernacles.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_17::
    .string "And it shall be, that whoso will\n"
    .string "not come up of all the families of\l"
    .string "the earth unto Jerusalem to worship\l"
    .string "the King, the LORD of hosts, even\l"
    .string "upon them shall be no rain.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_18::
    .string "And if the family of Egypt go not\n"
    .string "up, and come not, that have no rain;\l"
    .string "there shall be the plague,\l"
    .string "wherewith the LORD will smite the\l"
    .string "heathen that come not up to keep the\l"
    .string "feast of tabernacles.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_19::
    .string "This shall be the punishment of\n"
    .string "Egypt, and the punishment of all\l"
    .string "nations that come not up to keep the\l"
    .string "feast of tabernacles.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_20::
    .string "In that day shall there be upon\n"
    .string "the bells of the horses, HOLINESS\l"
    .string "UNTO THE LORD; and the pots in the\l"
    .string "LORD’s house shall be like the\l"
    .string "bowls before the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Zechariah_14_21::
    .string "Yea, every pot in Jerusalem and in\n"
    .string "Judah shall be holiness unto the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts: and all they that\l"
    .string "sacrifice shall come and take of\l"
    .string "them, and seethe therein: and in that\l"
    .string "day there shall be no more the\l"
    .string "Canaanite in the house of the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_1::
    .string "The burden of the word of the LORD\n"
    .string "to Israel by Malachi.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_2::
    .string "I have loved you, saith the LORD.\n"
    .string "Yet ye say, Wherein hast thou loved\l"
    .string "us? Was not Esau Jacob’s brother?\l"
    .string "saith the LORD: yet I loved Jacob,"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_3::
    .string "And I hated Esau, and laid his\n"
    .string "mountains and his heritage waste for\l"
    .string "the dragons of the wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_4::
    .string "Whereas Edom saith, We are\n"
    .string "impoverished, but we will return\l"
    .string "and build the desolate places;\l"
    .string "thus saith the LORD of hosts, They\l"
    .string "shall build, but I will throw\l"
    .string "down; and they shall call them,\l"
    .string "The border of wickedness, and, The\l"
    .string "people against whom the LORD hath\l"
    .string "indignation for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_5::
    .string "And your eyes shall see, and ye\n"
    .string "shall say, The LORD will be\l"
    .string "magnified from the border of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_6::
    .string "A son honoureth his father, and a\n"
    .string "servant his master: if then I be a\l"
    .string "father, where is mine honour? and if\l"
    .string "I be a master, where is my fear? saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts unto you, O\l"
    .string "priests, that despise my name. And\l"
    .string "ye say, Wherein have we despised thy\l"
    .string "name?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_7::
    .string "Ye offer polluted bread upon mine\n"
    .string "altar; and ye say, Wherein have we\l"
    .string "polluted thee? In that ye say, The\l"
    .string "table of the LORD is contemptible$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_8::
    .string "And if ye offer the blind for\n"
    .string "sacrifice, is it not evil? and if ye\l"
    .string "offer the lame and sick, is it not\l"
    .string "evil? offer it now unto thy\l"
    .string "governor; will he be pleased with\l"
    .string "thee, or accept thy person? saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_9::
    .string "And now, I pray you, beseech God\n"
    .string "that he will be gracious unto us:\l"
    .string "this hath been by your means: will\l"
    .string "he regard your persons? saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_10::
    .string "Who is there even among you that\n"
    .string "would shut the doors for nought?\l"
    .string "neither do ye kindle fire on mine\l"
    .string "altar for nought. I have no\l"
    .string "pleasure in you, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, neither will I accept an\l"
    .string "offering at your hand.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_11::
    .string "For from the rising of the sun even\n"
    .string "unto the going down of the same my\l"
    .string "name shall be great among the\l"
    .string "Gentiles; and in every place\l"
    .string "incense shall be offered unto my\l"
    .string "name, and a pure offering: for my\l"
    .string "name shall be great among the\l"
    .string "heathen, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_12::
    .string "But ye have profaned it, in that ye\n"
    .string "say, The table of the LORD is\l"
    .string "polluted; and the fruit thereof,\l"
    .string "even his meat, is contemptible.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_13::
    .string "Ye said also, Behold, what a\n"
    .string "weariness is it! and ye have snuffed\l"
    .string "at it, saith the LORD of hosts; and ye\l"
    .string "brought that which was torn, and the\l"
    .string "lame, and the sick; thus ye brought\l"
    .string "an offering: should I accept this of\l"
    .string "your hand? saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_1_14::
    .string "But cursed be the deceiver, which\n"
    .string "hath in his flock a male, and\l"
    .string "voweth, and sacrificeth unto the LORD\l"
    .string "a corrupt thing: for I am a great\l"
    .string "King, saith the LORD of hosts, and my\l"
    .string "name is dreadful among the heathen.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_1::
    .string "And now, O ye priests, this\n"
    .string "commandment is for you.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_2::
    .string "If ye will not hear, and if ye\n"
    .string "will not lay it to heart, to give\l"
    .string "glory unto my name, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts, I will even send a curse\l"
    .string "upon you, and I will curse your\l"
    .string "blessings: yea, I have cursed them\l"
    .string "already, because ye do not lay it to\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_3::
    .string "Behold, I will corrupt your seed,\n"
    .string "and spread dung upon your faces,\l"
    .string "even the dung of your solemn feasts;\l"
    .string "and one shall take you away with it.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_4::
    .string "And ye shall know that I have sent\n"
    .string "this commandment unto you, that my\l"
    .string "covenant might be with Levi, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_5::
    .string "My covenant was with him of life\n"
    .string "and peace; and I gave them to him for\l"
    .string "the fear wherewith he feared me, and\l"
    .string "was afraid before my name.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_6::
    .string "The law of truth was in his mouth,\n"
    .string "and iniquity was not found in his\l"
    .string "lips: he walked with me in peace\l"
    .string "and equity, and did turn many away\l"
    .string "from iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_7::
    .string "For the priest’s lips should\n"
    .string "keep knowledge, and they should\l"
    .string "seek the law at his mouth: for he is\l"
    .string "the messenger of the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_8::
    .string "But ye are departed out of the way;\n"
    .string "ye have caused many to stumble at\l"
    .string "the law; ye have corrupted the\l"
    .string "covenant of Levi, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_9::
    .string "Therefore have I also made you\n"
    .string "contemptible and base before all\l"
    .string "the people, according as ye have\l"
    .string "not kept my ways, but have been\l"
    .string "partial in the law.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_10::
    .string "Have we not all one father? hath\n"
    .string "not one God created us? why do we\l"
    .string "deal treacherously every man\l"
    .string "against his brother, by profaning\l"
    .string "the covenant of our fathers?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_11::
    .string "Judah hath dealt treacherously,\n"
    .string "and an abomination is committed in\l"
    .string "Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah\l"
    .string "hath profaned the holiness of the\l"
    .string "LORD which he loved, and hath\l"
    .string "married the daughter of a strange god$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_12::
    .string "The LORD will cut off the man that\n"
    .string "doeth this, the master and the\l"
    .string "scholar, out of the tabernacles of\l"
    .string "Jacob, and him that offereth an\l"
    .string "offering unto the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_13::
    .string "And this have ye done again,\n"
    .string "covering the altar of the LORD with\l"
    .string "tears, with weeping, and with crying\l"
    .string "out, insomuch that he regardeth not\l"
    .string "the offering any more, or receiveth\l"
    .string "it with good will at your hand.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_14::
    .string "Yet ye say, Wherefore? Because the\n"
    .string "LORD hath been witness between thee\l"
    .string "and the wife of thy youth, against\l"
    .string "whom thou hast dealt treacherously:\l"
    .string "yet is she thy companion, and the\l"
    .string "wife of thy covenant.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_15::
    .string "And did not he make one? Yet had he\n"
    .string "the residue of the spirit. And\l"
    .string "wherefore one? That he might seek a\l"
    .string "godly seed. Therefore take heed to\l"
    .string "your spirit, and let none deal\l"
    .string "treacherously against the wife of\l"
    .string "his youth.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_16::
    .string "For the LORD, the God of Israel,\n"
    .string "saith that he hateth putting away:\l"
    .string "for one covereth violence with his\l"
    .string "garment, saith the LORD of hosts:\l"
    .string "therefore take heed to your spirit,\l"
    .string "that ye deal not treacherously.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_2_17::
    .string "Ye have wearied the LORD with your\n"
    .string "words. Yet ye say, Wherein have we\l"
    .string "wearied him? When ye say, Every one\l"
    .string "that doeth evil is good in the sight\l"
    .string "of the LORD, and he delighteth in\l"
    .string "them; or, Where is the God of\l"
    .string "judgment?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_1::
    .string "Behold, I will send my messenger,\n"
    .string "and he shall prepare the way\l"
    .string "before me: and the LORD, whom ye seek,\l"
    .string "shall suddenly come to his\l"
    .string "temple, even the messenger of the\l"
    .string "covenant, whom ye delight in:\l"
    .string "behold, he shall come, saith the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_2::
    .string "But who may abide the day of his\n"
    .string "coming? and who shall stand when he\l"
    .string "appeareth? for he is like a\l"
    .string "refiner’s fire, and like fullers’\l"
    .string "soap:"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_3::
    .string "And he shall sit as a refiner and\n"
    .string "purifier of silver: and he shall\l"
    .string "purify the sons of Levi, and purge\l"
    .string "them as gold and silver, that they\l"
    .string "may offer unto the LORD an offering\l"
    .string "in righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_4::
    .string "Then shall the offering of Judah\n"
    .string "and Jerusalem be pleasant unto the\l"
    .string "LORD, as in the days of old, and as\l"
    .string "in former years.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_5::
    .string "And I will come near to you to\n"
    .string "judgment; and I will be a swift\l"
    .string "witness against the sorcerers, and\l"
    .string "against the adulterers, and against\l"
    .string "false swearers, and against those\l"
    .string "that oppress the hireling in his\l"
    .string "wages, the widow, and the\l"
    .string "fatherless, and that turn aside the\l"
    .string "stranger from his right, and fear not\l"
    .string "me, saith the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_6::
    .string "For I am the LORD, I change not;\n"
    .string "therefore ye sons of Jacob are not\l"
    .string "consumed.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_7::
    .string "Even from the days of your fathers\n"
    .string "ye are gone away from mine\l"
    .string "ordinances, and have not kept them.\l"
    .string "Return unto me, and I will return\l"
    .string "unto you, saith the LORD of hosts.\l"
    .string "But ye said, Wherein shall we\l"
    .string "return?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_8::
    .string "Will a man rob God? Yet ye have\n"
    .string "robbed me. But ye say, Wherein have\l"
    .string "we robbed thee? In tithes and\l"
    .string "offerings$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_9::
    .string "Ye are cursed with a curse: for ye\n"
    .string "have robbed me, even this whole\l"
    .string "nation.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_10::
    .string "Bring ye all the tithes into the\n"
    .string "storehouse, that there may be meat in\l"
    .string "mine house, and prove me now\l"
    .string "herewith, saith the LORD of hosts, if\l"
    .string "I will not open you the windows of\l"
    .string "heaven, and pour you out a blessing,\l"
    .string "that there shall not be room enough\l"
    .string "to receive it.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_11::
    .string "And I will rebuke the devourer for\n"
    .string "your sakes, and he shall not destroy\l"
    .string "the fruits of your ground; neither\l"
    .string "shall your vine cast her fruit\l"
    .string "before the time in the field, saith\l"
    .string "the LORD of hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_12::
    .string "And all nations shall call you\n"
    .string "blessed: for ye shall be a\l"
    .string "delightsome land, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_13::
    .string "Your words have been stout against\n"
    .string "me, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, What\l"
    .string "have we spoken so much against thee?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_14::
    .string "Ye have said, It is vain to serve\n"
    .string "God: and what profit is it that we\l"
    .string "have kept his ordinance, and that we\l"
    .string "have walked mournfully before the\l"
    .string "LORD of hosts?"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_15::
    .string "And now we call the proud happy;\n"
    .string "yea, they that work wickedness are\l"
    .string "set up; yea, they that tempt God are\l"
    .string "even delivered$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_16::
    .string "Then they that feared the LORD\n"
    .string "spake often one to another: and the\l"
    .string "LORD hearkened, and heard it, and a\l"
    .string "book of remembrance was written\l"
    .string "before him for them that feared the\l"
    .string "LORD, and that thought upon his name.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_17::
    .string "And they shall be mine, saith the\n"
    .string "LORD of hosts, in that day when I make\l"
    .string "up my jewels; and I will spare\l"
    .string "them, as a man spareth his own son\l"
    .string "that serveth him.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_3_18::
    .string "Then shall ye return, and discern\n"
    .string "between the righteous and the wicked,\l"
    .string "between him that serveth God and him\l"
    .string "that serveth him not.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_1::
    .string "For, behold, the day cometh, that\n"
    .string "shall burn as an oven; and all the\l"
    .string "proud, yea, and all that do\l"
    .string "wickedly, shall be stubble: and\l"
    .string "the day that cometh shall burn them\l"
    .string "up, saith the LORD of hosts, that it\l"
    .string "shall leave them neither root nor\l"
    .string "branch.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_2::
    .string "But unto you that fear my name\n"
    .string "shall the Sun of righteousness\l"
    .string "arise with healing in his wings; and\l"
    .string "ye shall go forth, and grow up as\l"
    .string "calves of the stall.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_3::
    .string "And ye shall tread down the wicked;\n"
    .string "for they shall be ashes under the\l"
    .string "soles of your feet in the day that I\l"
    .string "shall do this, saith the LORD of\l"
    .string "hosts.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_4::
    .string "Remember ye the law of Moses my\n"
    .string "servant, which I commanded unto him\l"
    .string "in Horeb for all Israel, with the\l"
    .string "statutes and judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_5::
    .string "Behold, I will send you Elijah\n"
    .string "the prophet before the coming of\l"
    .string "the great and dreadful day of the\l"
    .string "LORD:"
Bible_Text_Malachi_4_6::
    .string "And he shall turn the heart of the\n"
    .string "fathers to the children, and the\l"
    .string "heart of the children to their\l"
    .string "fathers, lest I come and smite the\l"
    .string "earth with a curse$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_1::
    .string "The book of the generation of Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ, the son of David, the son of\l"
    .string "Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_2::
    .string "Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat\n"
    .string "Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his\l"
    .string "brethren;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_3::
    .string "And Judas begat Phares and Zara of\n"
    .string "Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and\l"
    .string "Esrom begat Aram;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_4::
    .string "And Aram begat Aminadab; and\n"
    .string "Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson\l"
    .string "begat Salmon;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_5::
    .string "And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab;\n"
    .string "and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed\l"
    .string "begat Jesse;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_6::
    .string "And Jesse begat David the king; and\n"
    .string "David the king begat Solomon of her\l"
    .string "that had been the wife of Urias;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_7::
    .string "And Solomon begat Roboam; and\n"
    .string "Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat\l"
    .string "Asa;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_8::
    .string "And Asa begat Josaphat; and\n"
    .string "Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram\l"
    .string "begat Ozias;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_9::
    .string "And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham\n"
    .string "begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_10::
    .string "And Ezekias begat Manasses; and\n"
    .string "Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat\l"
    .string "Josias;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_11::
    .string "And Josias begat Jechonias and his\n"
    .string "brethren, about the time they were\l"
    .string "carried away to Babylon:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_12::
    .string "And after they were brought to\n"
    .string "Babylon, Jechonias begat\l"
    .string "Salathiel; and Salathiel begat\l"
    .string "Zorobabel;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_13::
    .string "And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and\n"
    .string "Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim\l"
    .string "begat Azor;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_14::
    .string "And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc\n"
    .string "begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_15::
    .string "And Eliud begat Eleazar; and\n"
    .string "Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan\l"
    .string "begat Jacob;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_16::
    .string "And Jacob begat Joseph the husband\n"
    .string "of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who\l"
    .string "is called Christ$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_17::
    .string "So all the generations from\n"
    .string "Abraham to David are fourteen\l"
    .string "generations; and from David until\l"
    .string "the carrying away into Babylon are\l"
    .string "fourteen generations; and from the\l"
    .string "carrying away into Babylon unto\l"
    .string "Christ are fourteen generations.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_18::
    .string "Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on\n"
    .string "this wise: When as his mother Mary\l"
    .string "was espoused to Joseph, before they\l"
    .string "came together, she was found with\l"
    .string "child of the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_19::
    .string "Then Joseph her husband, being a\n"
    .string "just man, and not willing to make\l"
    .string "her a publick example, was minded\l"
    .string "to put her away privily.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_20::
    .string "But while he thought on these\n"
    .string "things, behold, the angel of the\l"
    .string "LORD appeared unto him in a dream,\l"
    .string "saying, Joseph, thou son of David,\l"
    .string "fear not to take unto thee Mary thy\l"
    .string "wife: for that which is conceived in\l"
    .string "her is of the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_21::
    .string "And she shall bring forth a son,\n"
    .string "and thou shalt call his name JESUS:\l"
    .string "for he shall save his people from\l"
    .string "their sins.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_22::
    .string "Now all this was done, that it\n"
    .string "might be fulfilled which was\l"
    .string "spoken of the Lord by the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_23::
    .string "Behold, a virgin shall be with\n"
    .string "child, and shall bring forth a son,\l"
    .string "and they shall call his name\l"
    .string "Emmanuel, which being interpreted\l"
    .string "is, God with us$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_24::
    .string "Then Joseph being raised from\n"
    .string "sleep did as the angel of the Lord\l"
    .string "had bidden him, and took unto him his\l"
    .string "wife:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_1_25::
    .string "And knew her not till she had\n"
    .string "brought forth her firstborn son: and\l"
    .string "he called his name JESUS$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_1::
    .string "Now when Jesus was born in\n"
    .string "Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of\l"
    .string "Herod the king, behold, there came\l"
    .string "wise men from the east to Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_2::
    .string "Saying, Where is he that is born\n"
    .string "King of the Jews? for we have seen his\l"
    .string "star in the east, and are come to\l"
    .string "worship him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_3::
    .string "When Herod the king had heard these\n"
    .string "things, he was troubled, and all\l"
    .string "Jerusalem with him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_4::
    .string "And when he had gathered all the\n"
    .string "chief priests and scribes of the\l"
    .string "people together, he demanded of\l"
    .string "them where Christ should be born.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_5::
    .string "And they said unto him, In\n"
    .string "Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is\l"
    .string "written by the prophet,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_6::
    .string "And thou Bethlehem, in the land of\n"
    .string "Juda, art not the least among the\l"
    .string "princes of Juda: for out of thee\l"
    .string "shall come a Governor, that shall\l"
    .string "rule my people Israel$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_7::
    .string "Then Herod, when he had privily\n"
    .string "called the wise men, enquired of\l"
    .string "them diligently what time the star\l"
    .string "appeared.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_8::
    .string "And he sent them to Bethlehem, and\n"
    .string "said, Go and search diligently for\l"
    .string "the young child; and when ye have\l"
    .string "found him, bring me word again, that\l"
    .string "I may come and worship him also.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_9::
    .string "When they had heard the king, they\n"
    .string "departed; and, lo, the star, which\l"
    .string "they saw in the east, went before\l"
    .string "them, till it came and stood over\l"
    .string "where the young child was.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_10::
    .string "When they saw the star, they\n"
    .string "rejoiced with exceeding great joy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_11::
    .string "And when they were come into the\n"
    .string "house, they saw the young child with\l"
    .string "Mary his mother, and fell down, and\l"
    .string "worshipped him: and when they had\l"
    .string "opened their treasures, they\l"
    .string "presented unto him gifts; gold, and\l"
    .string "frankincense and myrrh.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_12::
    .string "And being warned of God in a dream\n"
    .string "that they should not return to\l"
    .string "Herod, they departed into their own\l"
    .string "country another way.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_13::
    .string "And when they were departed,\n"
    .string "behold, the angel of the Lord\l"
    .string "appeareth to Joseph in a dream,\l"
    .string "saying, Arise, and take the young\l"
    .string "child and his mother, and flee into\l"
    .string "Egypt, and be thou there until I\l"
    .string "bring thee word: for Herod will seek\l"
    .string "the young child to destroy him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_14::
    .string "When he arose, he took the young\n"
    .string "child and his mother by night, and\l"
    .string "departed into Egypt:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_15::
    .string "And was there until the death of\n"
    .string "Herod: that it might be fulfilled\l"
    .string "which was spoken of the Lord by the\l"
    .string "prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I\l"
    .string "called my son$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_16::
    .string "Then Herod, when he saw that he was\n"
    .string "mocked of the wise men, was exceeding\l"
    .string "wroth, and sent forth, and slew all\l"
    .string "the children that were in\l"
    .string "Bethlehem, and in all the coasts\l"
    .string "thereof, from two years old and\l"
    .string "under, according to the time which he\l"
    .string "had diligently enquired of the wise\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_17::
    .string "Then was fulfilled that which was\n"
    .string "spoken by Jeremy the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_18::
    .string "In Rama was there a voice heard,\n"
    .string "lamentation, and weeping, and great\l"
    .string "mourning, Rachel weeping for her\l"
    .string "children, and would not be\l"
    .string "comforted, because they are not$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_19::
    .string "But when Herod was dead, behold, an\n"
    .string "angel of the Lord appeareth in a\l"
    .string "dream to Joseph in Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_20::
    .string "Saying, Arise, and take the young\n"
    .string "child and his mother, and go into the\l"
    .string "land of Israel: for they are dead\l"
    .string "which sought the young child’s life$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_21::
    .string "And he arose, and took the young\n"
    .string "child and his mother, and came into\l"
    .string "the land of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_22::
    .string "But when he heard that Archelaus\n"
    .string "did reign in Judaea in the room of\l"
    .string "his father Herod, he was afraid to go\l"
    .string "thither: notwithstanding, being\l"
    .string "warned of God in a dream, he turned\l"
    .string "aside into the parts of Galilee:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_2_23::
    .string "And he came and dwelt in a city\n"
    .string "called Nazareth: that it might be\l"
    .string "fulfilled which was spoken by the\l"
    .string "prophets, He shall be called a\l"
    .string "Nazarene$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_1::
    .string "In those days came John the\n"
    .string "Baptist, preaching in the\l"
    .string "wilderness of Judaea,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_2::
    .string "And saying, Repent ye: for the\n"
    .string "kingdom of heaven is at hand$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_3::
    .string "For this is he that was spoken of by\n"
    .string "the prophet Esaias, saying, The\l"
    .string "voice of one crying in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, Prepare ye the way of\l"
    .string "the Lord, make his paths straight.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_4::
    .string "And the same John had his raiment of\n"
    .string "camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle\l"
    .string "about his loins; and his meat was\l"
    .string "locusts and wild honey.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_5::
    .string "Then went out to him Jerusalem, and\n"
    .string "all Judaea, and all the region\l"
    .string "round about Jordan,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_6::
    .string "And were baptized of him in Jordan,\n"
    .string "confessing their sins$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_7::
    .string "But when he saw many of the\n"
    .string "Pharisees and Sadducees come to his\l"
    .string "baptism, he said unto them, O\l"
    .string "generation of vipers, who hath\l"
    .string "warned you to flee from the wrath to\l"
    .string "come?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_8::
    .string "Bring forth therefore fruits meet\n"
    .string "for repentance:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_9::
    .string "And think not to say within\n"
    .string "yourselves, We have Abraham to our\l"
    .string "father: for I say unto you, that God\l"
    .string "is able of these stones to raise up\l"
    .string "children unto Abraham$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_10::
    .string "And now also the axe is laid unto\n"
    .string "the root of the trees: therefore\l"
    .string "every tree which bringeth not forth\l"
    .string "good fruit is hewn down, and cast\l"
    .string "into the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_11::
    .string "I indeed baptize you with water\n"
    .string "unto repentance. but he that cometh\l"
    .string "after me is mightier than I, whose\l"
    .string "shoes I am not worthy to bear: he\l"
    .string "shall baptize you with the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost, and with fire:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_12::
    .string "Whose fan is in his hand, and he\n"
    .string "will throughly purge his floor,\l"
    .string "and gather his wheat into the garner;\l"
    .string "but he will burn up the chaff with\l"
    .string "unquenchable fire$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_13::
    .string "Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to\n"
    .string "Jordan unto John, to be baptized of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_14::
    .string "But John forbad him, saying, I have\n"
    .string "need to be baptized of thee, and\l"
    .string "comest thou to me?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_15::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "Suffer it to be so now: for thus it\l"
    .string "becometh us to fulfil all\l"
    .string "righteousness. Then he suffered him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_16::
    .string "And Jesus, when he was baptized,\n"
    .string "went up straightway out of the\l"
    .string "water: and, lo, the heavens were\l"
    .string "opened unto him, and he saw the\l"
    .string "Spirit of God descending like a\l"
    .string "dove, and lighting upon him:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_3_17::
    .string "And lo a voice from heaven, saying,\n"
    .string "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am\l"
    .string "well pleased$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_1::
    .string "Then was Jesus led up of the\n"
    .string "spirit into the wilderness to be\l"
    .string "tempted of the devil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_2::
    .string "And when he had fasted forty days\n"
    .string "and forty nights, he was afterward an\l"
    .string "hungred.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_3::
    .string "And when the tempter came to him, he\n"
    .string "said, If thou be the Son of God,\l"
    .string "command that these stones be made\l"
    .string "bread.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_4::
    .string "But he answered and said, It is\n"
    .string "written, Man shall not live by\l"
    .string "bread alone, but by every word that\l"
    .string "proceedeth out of the mouth of God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_5::
    .string "Then the devil taketh him up into\n"
    .string "the holy city, and setteth him on a\l"
    .string "pinnacle of the temple,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_6::
    .string "And saith unto him, If thou be the\n"
    .string "Son of God, cast thyself down: for it\l"
    .string "is written, He shall give his\l"
    .string "angels charge concerning thee: and\l"
    .string "in their hands they shall bear thee\l"
    .string "up, lest at any time thou dash thy\l"
    .string "foot against a stone$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_7::
    .string "Jesus said unto him, It is written\n"
    .string "again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord\l"
    .string "thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_8::
    .string "Again, the devil taketh him up into\n"
    .string "an exceeding high mountain, and\l"
    .string "sheweth him all the kingdoms of the\l"
    .string "world, and the glory of them;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_9::
    .string "And saith unto him, All these\n"
    .string "things will I give thee, if thou\l"
    .string "wilt fall down and worship me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_10::
    .string "Then saith Jesus unto him, Get thee\n"
    .string "hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt worship the Lord thy God, and\l"
    .string "him only shalt thou serve.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_11::
    .string "Then the devil leaveth him, and,\n"
    .string "behold, angels came and ministered\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_12::
    .string "Now when Jesus had heard that John\n"
    .string "was cast into prison, he departed\l"
    .string "into Galilee;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_13::
    .string "And leaving Nazareth, he came and\n"
    .string "dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon\l"
    .string "the sea coast, in the borders of\l"
    .string "Zabulon and Nephthalim:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_14::
    .string "That it might be fulfilled which\n"
    .string "was spoken by Esaias the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_15::
    .string "The land of Zabulon, and the land\n"
    .string "of Nephthalim, by the way of the\l"
    .string "sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_16::
    .string "The people which sat in darkness\n"
    .string "saw great light; and to them which\l"
    .string "sat in the region and shadow of death\l"
    .string "light is sprung up$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_17::
    .string "From that time Jesus began to\n"
    .string "preach, and to say, Repent: for the\l"
    .string "kingdom of heaven is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_18::
    .string "And Jesus, walking by the sea of\n"
    .string "Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon\l"
    .string "called Peter, and Andrew his\l"
    .string "brother, casting a net into the sea:\l"
    .string "for they were fishers.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_19::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Follow me,\n"
    .string "and I will make you fishers of men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_20::
    .string "And they straightway left their\n"
    .string "nets, and followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_21::
    .string "And going on from thence, he saw\n"
    .string "other two brethren, James the son of\l"
    .string "Zebedee, and John his brother, in a\l"
    .string "ship with Zebedee their father,\l"
    .string "mending their nets; and he called\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_22::
    .string "And they immediately left the\n"
    .string "ship and their father, and followed\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_23::
    .string "And Jesus went about all Galilee,\n"
    .string "teaching in their synagogues, and\l"
    .string "preaching the gospel of the\l"
    .string "kingdom, and healing all manner of\l"
    .string "sickness and all manner of disease\l"
    .string "among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_24::
    .string "And his fame went throughout all\n"
    .string "Syria: and they brought unto him all\l"
    .string "sick people that were taken with\l"
    .string "divers diseases and torments, and\l"
    .string "those which were possessed with\l"
    .string "devils, and those which were\l"
    .string "lunatick, and those that had the\l"
    .string "palsy; and he healed them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_4_25::
    .string "And there followed him great\n"
    .string "multitudes of people from\l"
    .string "Galilee, and from Decapolis, and\l"
    .string "from Jerusalem, and from Judaea, and\l"
    .string "from beyond Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_1::
    .string "And seeing the multitudes, he went\n"
    .string "up into a mountain: and when he was\l"
    .string "set, his disciples came unto him:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_2::
    .string "And he opened his mouth, and taught\n"
    .string "them, saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_3::
    .string "Blessed are the poor in spirit:\n"
    .string "for theirs is the kingdom of heaven$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_4::
    .string "Blessed are they that mourn: for\n"
    .string "they shall be comforted.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_5::
    .string "Blessed are the meek: for they\n"
    .string "shall inherit the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_6::
    .string "Blessed are they which do hunger\n"
    .string "and thirst after righteousness: for\l"
    .string "they shall be filled.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_7::
    .string "Blessed are the merciful: for they\n"
    .string "shall obtain mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_8::
    .string "Blessed are the pure in heart: for\n"
    .string "they shall see God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_9::
    .string "Blessed are the peacemakers: for\n"
    .string "they shall be called the children\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_10::
    .string "Blessed are they which are\n"
    .string "persecuted for righteousness’ sake:\l"
    .string "for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_11::
    .string "Blessed are ye, when men shall\n"
    .string "revile you, and persecute you, and\l"
    .string "shall say all manner of evil\l"
    .string "against you falsely, for my sake.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_12::
    .string "Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for\n"
    .string "great is your reward in heaven: for\l"
    .string "so persecuted they the prophets\l"
    .string "which were before you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_13::
    .string "Ye are the salt of the earth: but if\n"
    .string "the salt have lost his savour,\l"
    .string "wherewith shall it be salted? it is\l"
    .string "thenceforth good for nothing, but to\l"
    .string "be cast out, and to be trodden under\l"
    .string "foot of men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_14::
    .string "Ye are the light of the world. A\n"
    .string "city that is set on an hill cannot\l"
    .string "be hid.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_15::
    .string "Neither do men light a candle, and\n"
    .string "put it under a bushel, but on a\l"
    .string "candlestick; and it giveth light\l"
    .string "unto all that are in the house.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_16::
    .string "Let your light so shine before men,\n"
    .string "that they may see your good works,\l"
    .string "and glorify your Father which is in\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_17::
    .string "Think not that I am come to destroy\n"
    .string "the law, or the prophets: I am not\l"
    .string "come to destroy, but to fulfil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_18::
    .string "For verily I say unto you, Till\n"
    .string "heaven and earth pass, one jot or one\l"
    .string "tittle shall in no wise pass from\l"
    .string "the law, till all be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_19::
    .string "Whosoever therefore shall break\n"
    .string "one of these least commandments, and\l"
    .string "shall teach men so, he shall be\l"
    .string "called the least in the kingdom of\l"
    .string "heaven: but whosoever shall do and\l"
    .string "teach them, the same shall be\l"
    .string "called great in the kingdom of\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_20::
    .string "For I say unto you, That except your\n"
    .string "righteousness shall exceed the\l"
    .string "righteousness of the scribes and\l"
    .string "Pharisees, ye shall in no case enter\l"
    .string "into the kingdom of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_21::
    .string "Ye have heard that it was said by\n"
    .string "them of old time, Thou shalt not\l"
    .string "kill; and whosoever shall kill\l"
    .string "shall be in danger of the judgment:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_22::
    .string "But I say unto you, That whosoever\n"
    .string "is angry with his brother without a\l"
    .string "cause shall be in danger of the\l"
    .string "judgment: and whosoever shall say\l"
    .string "to his brother, Raca, shall be in\l"
    .string "danger of the council: but whosoever\l"
    .string "shall say, Thou fool, shall be in\l"
    .string "danger of hell fire$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_23::
    .string "Therefore if thou bring thy gift to\n"
    .string "the altar, and there rememberest\l"
    .string "that thy brother hath ought against\l"
    .string "thee;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_24::
    .string "Leave there thy gift before the\n"
    .string "altar, and go thy way; first be\l"
    .string "reconciled to thy brother, and then\l"
    .string "come and offer thy gift$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_25::
    .string "Agree with thine adversary quickly,\n"
    .string "whiles thou art in the way with him;\l"
    .string "lest at any time the adversary\l"
    .string "deliver thee to the judge, and the\l"
    .string "judge deliver thee to the officer,\l"
    .string "and thou be cast into prison.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_26::
    .string "Verily I say unto thee, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "by no means come out thence, till\l"
    .string "thou hast paid the uttermost\l"
    .string "farthing.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_27::
    .string "Ye have heard that it was said by\n"
    .string "them of old time, Thou shalt not\l"
    .string "commit adultery:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_28::
    .string "But I say unto you, That whosoever\n"
    .string "looketh on a woman to lust after her\l"
    .string "hath committed adultery with her\l"
    .string "already in his heart$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_29::
    .string "And if thy right eye offend thee,\n"
    .string "pluck it out, and cast it from thee:\l"
    .string "for it is profitable for thee that\l"
    .string "one of thy members should perish,\l"
    .string "and not that thy whole body should\l"
    .string "be cast into hell.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_30::
    .string "And if thy right hand offend thee,\n"
    .string "cut it off, and cast it from thee: for\l"
    .string "it is profitable for thee that one\l"
    .string "of thy members should perish, and\l"
    .string "not that thy whole body should be\l"
    .string "cast into hell.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_31::
    .string "It hath been said, Whosoever shall\n"
    .string "put away his wife, let him give her a\l"
    .string "writing of divorcement:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_32::
    .string "But I say unto you, That whosoever\n"
    .string "shall put away his wife, saving for\l"
    .string "the cause of fornication, causeth her\l"
    .string "to commit adultery: and whosoever\l"
    .string "shall marry her that is divorced\l"
    .string "committeth adultery$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_33::
    .string "Again, ye have heard that it hath\n"
    .string "been said by them of old time, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt not forswear thyself, but\l"
    .string "shalt perform unto the Lord thine\l"
    .string "oaths:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_34::
    .string "But I say unto you, Swear not at\n"
    .string "all; neither by heaven; for it is\l"
    .string "God’s throne:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_35::
    .string "Nor by the earth; for it is his\n"
    .string "footstool: neither by Jerusalem;\l"
    .string "for it is the city of the great King$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_36::
    .string "Neither shalt thou swear by thy\n"
    .string "head, because thou canst not make one\l"
    .string "hair white or black.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_37::
    .string "But let your communication be, Yea,\n"
    .string "yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more\l"
    .string "than these cometh of evil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_38::
    .string "Ye have heard that it hath been\n"
    .string "said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth\l"
    .string "for a tooth:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_39::
    .string "But I say unto you, That ye resist\n"
    .string "not evil: but whosoever shall smite\l"
    .string "thee on thy right cheek, turn to him\l"
    .string "the other also$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_40::
    .string "And if any man will sue thee at the\n"
    .string "law, and take away thy coat, let him\l"
    .string "have thy cloak also.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_41::
    .string "And whosoever shall compel thee\n"
    .string "to go a mile, go with him twain.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_42::
    .string "Give to him that asketh thee, and\n"
    .string "from him that would borrow of thee\l"
    .string "turn not thou away.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_43::
    .string "Ye have heard that it hath been\n"
    .string "said, Thou shalt love thy\l"
    .string "neighbour, and hate thine enemy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_44::
    .string "But I say unto you, Love your\n"
    .string "enemies, bless them that curse you,\l"
    .string "do good to them that hate you, and\l"
    .string "pray for them which despitefully\l"
    .string "use you, and persecute you;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_45::
    .string "That ye may be the children of your\n"
    .string "Father which is in heaven: for he\l"
    .string "maketh his sun to rise on the evil\l"
    .string "and on the good, and sendeth rain on\l"
    .string "the just and on the unjust$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_46::
    .string "For if ye love them which love you,\n"
    .string "what reward have ye? do not even the\l"
    .string "publicans the same?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_47::
    .string "And if ye salute your brethren\n"
    .string "only, what do ye more than others? do\l"
    .string "not even the publicans so?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_5_48::
    .string "Be ye therefore perfect, even as\n"
    .string "your Father which is in heaven is\l"
    .string "perfect$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_1::
    .string "Take heed that ye do not your alms\n"
    .string "before men, to be seen of them:\l"
    .string "otherwise ye have no reward of your\l"
    .string "Father which is in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_2::
    .string "Therefore when thou doest thine\n"
    .string "alms, do not sound a trumpet before\l"
    .string "thee, as the hypocrites do in the\l"
    .string "synagogues and in the streets, that\l"
    .string "they may have glory of men. Verily I\l"
    .string "say unto you, They have their reward.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_3::
    .string "But when thou doest alms, let not\n"
    .string "thy left hand know what thy right\l"
    .string "hand doeth:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_4::
    .string "That thine alms may be in secret:\n"
    .string "and thy Father which seeth in secret\l"
    .string "himself shall reward thee openly$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_5::
    .string "And when thou prayest, thou shalt\n"
    .string "not be as the hypocrites are: for\l"
    .string "they love to pray standing in the\l"
    .string "synagogues and in the corners of the\l"
    .string "streets, that they may be seen of\l"
    .string "men. Verily I say unto you, They have\l"
    .string "their reward.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_6::
    .string "But thou, when thou prayest, enter\n"
    .string "into thy closet, and when thou hast\l"
    .string "shut thy door, pray to thy Father\l"
    .string "which is in secret; and thy Father\l"
    .string "which seeth in secret shall reward\l"
    .string "thee openly.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_7::
    .string "But when ye pray, use not vain\n"
    .string "repetitions, as the heathen do: for\l"
    .string "they think that they shall be heard\l"
    .string "for their much speaking.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_8::
    .string "Be not ye therefore like unto them:\n"
    .string "for your Father knoweth what things\l"
    .string "ye have need of, before ye ask him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_9::
    .string "After this manner therefore pray\n"
    .string "ye: Our Father which art in heaven,\l"
    .string "Hallowed be thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_10::
    .string "Thy kingdom come, Thy will be done\n"
    .string "in earth, as it is in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_11::
    .string "Give us this day our daily bread.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_12::
    .string "And forgive us our debts, as we\n"
    .string "forgive our debtors.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_13::
    .string "And lead us not into temptation,\n"
    .string "but deliver us from evil: For thine\l"
    .string "is the kingdom, and the power, and\l"
    .string "the glory, for ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_14::
    .string "For if ye forgive men their\n"
    .string "trespasses, your heavenly Father\l"
    .string "will also forgive you:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_15::
    .string "But if ye forgive not men their\n"
    .string "trespasses, neither will your\l"
    .string "Father forgive your trespasses$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_16::
    .string "Moreover when ye fast, be not, as\n"
    .string "the hypocrites, of a sad\l"
    .string "countenance: for they disfigure\l"
    .string "their faces, that they may appear\l"
    .string "unto men to fast. Verily I say unto\l"
    .string "you, They have their reward.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_17::
    .string "But thou, when thou fastest, anoint\n"
    .string "thine head, and wash thy face;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_18::
    .string "That thou appear not unto men to\n"
    .string "fast, but unto thy Father which is in\l"
    .string "secret: and thy Father, which seeth\l"
    .string "in secret, shall reward thee openly$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_19::
    .string "Lay not up for yourselves\n"
    .string "treasures upon earth, where moth and\l"
    .string "rust doth corrupt, and where thieves\l"
    .string "break through and steal:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_20::
    .string "But lay up for yourselves\n"
    .string "treasures in heaven, where neither\l"
    .string "moth nor rust doth corrupt, and\l"
    .string "where thieves do not break through\l"
    .string "nor steal:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_21::
    .string "For where your treasure is, there\n"
    .string "will your heart be also$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_22::
    .string "The light of the body is the eye: if\n"
    .string "therefore thine eye be single, thy\l"
    .string "whole body shall be full of light.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_23::
    .string "But if thine eye be evil, thy whole\n"
    .string "body shall be full of darkness. If\l"
    .string "therefore the light that is in thee\l"
    .string "be darkness, how great is that\l"
    .string "darkness!$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_24::
    .string "No man can serve two masters: for\n"
    .string "either he will hate the one, and\l"
    .string "love the other; or else he will\l"
    .string "hold to the one, and despise the\l"
    .string "other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_25::
    .string "Therefore I say unto you, Take no\n"
    .string "thought for your life, what ye\l"
    .string "shall eat, or what ye shall drink;\l"
    .string "nor yet for your body, what ye shall\l"
    .string "put on. Is not the life more than\l"
    .string "meat, and the body than raiment?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_26::
    .string "Behold the fowls of the air: for\n"
    .string "they sow not, neither do they reap,\l"
    .string "nor gather into barns; yet your\l"
    .string "heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye\l"
    .string "not much better than they?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_27::
    .string "Which of you by taking thought can\n"
    .string "add one cubit unto his stature?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_28::
    .string "And why take ye thought for raiment?\n"
    .string "Consider the lilies of the field,\l"
    .string "how they grow; they toil not,\l"
    .string "neither do they spin:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_29::
    .string "And yet I say unto you, That even\n"
    .string "Solomon in all his glory was not\l"
    .string "arrayed like one of these$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_30::
    .string "Wherefore, if God so clothe the\n"
    .string "grass of the field, which to day is,\l"
    .string "and to morrow is cast into the oven,\l"
    .string "shall he not much more clothe you,\l"
    .string "O ye of little faith?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_31::
    .string "Therefore take no thought, saying,\n"
    .string "What shall we eat? or, What shall\l"
    .string "we drink? or, Wherewithal shall we\l"
    .string "be clothed?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_32::
    .string "(For after all these things do the\n"
    .string "Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly\l"
    .string "Father knoweth that ye have need of\l"
    .string "all these things$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_33::
    .string "But seek ye first the kingdom of\n"
    .string "God, and his righteousness; and all\l"
    .string "these things shall be added unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_6_34::
    .string "Take therefore no thought for the\n"
    .string "morrow: for the morrow shall take\l"
    .string "thought for the things of itself.\l"
    .string "Sufficient unto the day is the evil\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_1::
    .string "Judge not, that ye be not judged.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_2::
    .string "For with what judgment ye judge, ye\n"
    .string "shall be judged: and with what\l"
    .string "measure ye mete, it shall be\l"
    .string "measured to you again.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_3::
    .string "And why beholdest thou the mote\n"
    .string "that is in thy brother’s eye, but\l"
    .string "considerest not the beam that is in\l"
    .string "thine own eye?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_4::
    .string "Or how wilt thou say to thy brother,\n"
    .string "Let me pull out the mote out of\l"
    .string "thine eye; and, behold, a beam is in\l"
    .string "thine own eye?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_5::
    .string "Thou hypocrite, first cast out the\n"
    .string "beam out of thine own eye; and then\l"
    .string "shalt thou see clearly to cast out\l"
    .string "the mote out of thy brother’s eye$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_6::
    .string "Give not that which is holy unto\n"
    .string "the dogs, neither cast ye your\l"
    .string "pearls before swine, lest they\l"
    .string "trample them under their feet, and\l"
    .string "turn again and rend you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_7::
    .string "Ask, and it shall be given you;\n"
    .string "seek, and ye shall find; knock, and\l"
    .string "it shall be opened unto you:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_8::
    .string "For every one that asketh receiveth;\n"
    .string "and he that seeketh findeth; and to\l"
    .string "him that knocketh it shall be\l"
    .string "opened$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_9::
    .string "Or what man is there of you, whom if\n"
    .string "his son ask bread, will he give him\l"
    .string "a stone?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_10::
    .string "Or if he ask a fish, will he give\n"
    .string "him a serpent?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_11::
    .string "If ye then, being evil, know how to\n"
    .string "give good gifts unto your children,\l"
    .string "how much more shall your Father\l"
    .string "which is in heaven give good things\l"
    .string "to them that ask him?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_12::
    .string "Therefore all things whatsoever ye\n"
    .string "would that men should do to you, do\l"
    .string "ye even so to them: for this is the\l"
    .string "law and the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_13::
    .string "Enter ye in at the strait gate: for\n"
    .string "wide is the gate, and broad is the\l"
    .string "way, that leadeth to destruction,\l"
    .string "and many there be which go in\l"
    .string "thereat:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_14::
    .string "Because strait is the gate, and\n"
    .string "narrow is the way, which leadeth\l"
    .string "unto life, and few there be that find\l"
    .string "it$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_15::
    .string "Beware of false prophets, which\n"
    .string "come to you in sheep’s clothing, but\l"
    .string "inwardly they are ravening wolves.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_16::
    .string "Ye shall know them by their fruits.\n"
    .string "Do men gather grapes of thorns, or\l"
    .string "figs of thistles?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_17::
    .string "Even so every good tree bringeth\n"
    .string "forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree\l"
    .string "bringeth forth evil fruit$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_18::
    .string "A good tree cannot bring forth evil\n"
    .string "fruit, neither can a corrupt tree\l"
    .string "bring forth good fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_19::
    .string "Every tree that bringeth not forth\n"
    .string "good fruit is hewn down, and cast\l"
    .string "into the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_20::
    .string "Wherefore by their fruits ye shall\n"
    .string "know them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_21::
    .string "Not every one that saith unto me,\n"
    .string "Lord, Lord, shall enter into the\l"
    .string "kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth\l"
    .string "the will of my Father which is in\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_22::
    .string "Many will say to me in that day,\n"
    .string "Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied\l"
    .string "in thy name? and in thy name have cast\l"
    .string "out devils? and in thy name done many\l"
    .string "wonderful works?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_23::
    .string "And then will I profess unto them,\n"
    .string "I never knew you: depart from me, ye\l"
    .string "that work iniquity$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_24::
    .string "Therefore whosoever heareth these\n"
    .string "sayings of mine, and doeth them, I\l"
    .string "will liken him unto a wise man,\l"
    .string "which built his house upon a rock:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_25::
    .string "And the rain descended, and the\n"
    .string "floods came, and the winds blew, and\l"
    .string "beat upon that house; and it fell\l"
    .string "not: for it was founded upon a rock$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_26::
    .string "And every one that heareth these\n"
    .string "sayings of mine, and doeth them not,\l"
    .string "shall be likened unto a foolish\l"
    .string "man, which built his house upon the\l"
    .string "sand:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_27::
    .string "And the rain descended, and the\n"
    .string "floods came, and the winds blew, and\l"
    .string "beat upon that house; and it fell:\l"
    .string "and great was the fall of it$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_28::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jesus had\n"
    .string "ended these sayings, the people\l"
    .string "were astonished at his doctrine:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_7_29::
    .string "For he taught them as one having\n"
    .string "authority, and not as the scribes$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_1::
    .string "When he was come down from the\n"
    .string "mountain, great multitudes\l"
    .string "followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_2::
    .string "And, behold, there came a leper\n"
    .string "and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if\l"
    .string "thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_3::
    .string "And Jesus put forth his hand, and\n"
    .string "touched him, saying, I will; be thou\l"
    .string "clean. And immediately his leprosy\l"
    .string "was cleansed.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_4::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto him, See thou\n"
    .string "tell no man; but go thy way, shew\l"
    .string "thyself to the priest, and offer the\l"
    .string "gift that Moses commanded, for a\l"
    .string "testimony unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_5::
    .string "And when Jesus was entered into\n"
    .string "Capernaum, there came unto him a\l"
    .string "centurion, beseeching him,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_6::
    .string "And saying, Lord, my servant lieth\n"
    .string "at home sick of the palsy,\l"
    .string "grievously tormented$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_7::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto him, I will\n"
    .string "come and heal him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_8::
    .string "The centurion answered and said,\n"
    .string "Lord, I am not worthy that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest come under my roof: but\l"
    .string "speak the word only, and my servant\l"
    .string "shall be healed.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_9::
    .string "For I am a man under authority,\n"
    .string "having soldiers under me: and I say\l"
    .string "to this man, Go, and he goeth; and to\l"
    .string "another, Come, and he cometh; and to\l"
    .string "my servant, Do this, and he doeth it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_10::
    .string "When Jesus heard it, he marvelled,\n"
    .string "and said to them that followed,\l"
    .string "Verily I say unto you, I have not\l"
    .string "found so great faith, no, not in\l"
    .string "Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_11::
    .string "And I say unto you, That many shall\n"
    .string "come from the east and west, and\l"
    .string "shall sit down with Abraham, and\l"
    .string "Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_12::
    .string "But the children of the kingdom\n"
    .string "shall be cast out into outer\l"
    .string "darkness: there shall be weeping\l"
    .string "and gnashing of teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_13::
    .string "And Jesus said unto the centurion,\n"
    .string "Go thy way; and as thou hast\l"
    .string "believed, so be it done unto thee.\l"
    .string "And his servant was healed in the\l"
    .string "selfsame hour.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_14::
    .string "And when Jesus was come into Peter’s\n"
    .string "house, he saw his wife’s mother\l"
    .string "laid, and sick of a fever.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_15::
    .string "And he touched her hand, and the\n"
    .string "fever left her: and she arose, and\l"
    .string "ministered unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_16::
    .string "When the even was come, they brought\n"
    .string "unto him many that were possessed\l"
    .string "with devils: and he cast out the\l"
    .string "spirits with his word, and healed\l"
    .string "all that were sick:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_17::
    .string "That it might be fulfilled which\n"
    .string "was spoken by Esaias the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying, Himself took our\l"
    .string "infirmities, and bare our sicknesses$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_18::
    .string "Now when Jesus saw great multitudes\n"
    .string "about him, he gave commandment to\l"
    .string "depart unto the other side.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_19::
    .string "And a certain scribe came, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Master, I will follow\l"
    .string "thee whithersoever thou goest.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_20::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto him, The foxes\n"
    .string "have holes, and the birds of the air\l"
    .string "have nests; but the Son of man hath\l"
    .string "not where to lay his head.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_21::
    .string "And another of his disciples said\n"
    .string "unto him, Lord, suffer me first to go\l"
    .string "and bury my father.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_22::
    .string "But Jesus said unto him, Follow me;\n"
    .string "and let the dead bury their dead.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_23::
    .string "And when he was entered into a ship,\n"
    .string "his disciples followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_24::
    .string "And, behold, there arose a great\n"
    .string "tempest in the sea, insomuch that\l"
    .string "the ship was covered with the waves:\l"
    .string "but he was asleep.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_25::
    .string "And his disciples came to him, and\n"
    .string "awoke him, saying, Lord, save us: we\l"
    .string "perish.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_26::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Why are ye\n"
    .string "fearful, O ye of little faith? Then\l"
    .string "he arose, and rebuked the winds and\l"
    .string "the sea; and there was a great calm.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_27::
    .string "But the men marvelled, saying,\n"
    .string "What manner of man is this, that even\l"
    .string "the winds and the sea obey him!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_28::
    .string "And when he was come to the other\n"
    .string "side into the country of the\l"
    .string "Gergesenes, there met him two\l"
    .string "possessed with devils, coming out of\l"
    .string "the tombs, exceeding fierce, so that\l"
    .string "no man might pass by that way$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_29::
    .string "And, behold, they cried out,\n"
    .string "saying, What have we to do with thee,\l"
    .string "Jesus, thou Son of God? art thou come\l"
    .string "hither to torment us before the time?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_30::
    .string "And there was a good way off from\n"
    .string "them an herd of many swine feeding$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_31::
    .string "So the devils besought him, saying,\n"
    .string "If thou cast us out, suffer us to go\l"
    .string "away into the herd of swine.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_32::
    .string "And he said unto them, Go. And when\n"
    .string "they were come out, they went into\l"
    .string "the herd of swine: and, behold, the\l"
    .string "whole herd of swine ran violently\l"
    .string "down a steep place into the sea,\l"
    .string "and perished in the waters.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_33::
    .string "And they that kept them fled, and\n"
    .string "went their ways into the city, and\l"
    .string "told every thing, and what was\l"
    .string "befallen to the possessed of the\l"
    .string "devils.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_8_34::
    .string "And, behold, the whole city came\n"
    .string "out to meet Jesus: and when they saw\l"
    .string "him, they besought him that he would\l"
    .string "depart out of their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_1::
    .string "And he entered into a ship, and\n"
    .string "passed over, and came into his own\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_2::
    .string "And, behold, they brought to him a\n"
    .string "man sick of the palsy, lying on a\l"
    .string "bed: and Jesus seeing their faith\l"
    .string "said unto the sick of the palsy;\l"
    .string "Son, be of good cheer; thy sins be\l"
    .string "forgiven thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_3::
    .string "And, behold, certain of the scribes\n"
    .string "said within themselves, This man\l"
    .string "blasphemeth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_4::
    .string "And Jesus knowing their thoughts\n"
    .string "said, Wherefore think ye evil in\l"
    .string "your hearts?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_5::
    .string "For whether is easier, to say, Thy\n"
    .string "sins be forgiven thee; or to say,\l"
    .string "Arise, and walk?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_6::
    .string "But that ye may know that the Son of\n"
    .string "man hath power on earth to forgive\l"
    .string "sins, (then saith he to the sick of\l"
    .string "the palsy,) Arise, take up thy bed,\l"
    .string "and go unto thine house$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_7::
    .string "And he arose, and departed to his\n"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_8::
    .string "But when the multitudes saw it,\n"
    .string "they marvelled, and glorified God,\l"
    .string "which had given such power unto men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_9::
    .string "And as Jesus passed forth from\n"
    .string "thence, he saw a man, named Matthew,\l"
    .string "sitting at the receipt of custom:\l"
    .string "and he saith unto him, Follow me.\l"
    .string "And he arose, and followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_10::
    .string "And it came to pass, as Jesus sat at\n"
    .string "meat in the house, behold, many\l"
    .string "publicans and sinners came and sat\l"
    .string "down with him and his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_11::
    .string "And when the Pharisees saw it, they\n"
    .string "said unto his disciples, Why eateth\l"
    .string "your Master with publicans and\l"
    .string "sinners?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_12::
    .string "But when Jesus heard that, he said\n"
    .string "unto them, They that be whole need\l"
    .string "not a physician, but they that are\l"
    .string "sick$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_13::
    .string "But go ye and learn what that\n"
    .string "meaneth, I will have mercy, and not\l"
    .string "sacrifice: for I am not come to call\l"
    .string "the righteous, but sinners to\l"
    .string "repentance.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_14::
    .string "Then came to him the disciples of\n"
    .string "John, saying, Why do we and the\l"
    .string "Pharisees fast oft, but thy\l"
    .string "disciples fast not?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_15::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, Can the\n"
    .string "children of the bridechamber mourn,\l"
    .string "as long as the bridegroom is with\l"
    .string "them? but the days will come, when\l"
    .string "the bridegroom shall be taken from\l"
    .string "them, and then shall they fast$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_16::
    .string "No man putteth a piece of new\n"
    .string "cloth unto an old garment, for that\l"
    .string "which is put in to fill it up\l"
    .string "taketh from the garment, and the rent\l"
    .string "is made worse.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_17::
    .string "Neither do men put new wine into\n"
    .string "old bottles: else the bottles\l"
    .string "break, and the wine runneth out, and\l"
    .string "the bottles perish: but they put\l"
    .string "new wine into new bottles, and both\l"
    .string "are preserved.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_18::
    .string "While he spake these things unto\n"
    .string "them, behold, there came a certain\l"
    .string "ruler, and worshipped him, saying,\l"
    .string "My daughter is even now dead: but\l"
    .string "come and lay thy hand upon her, and\l"
    .string "she shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_19::
    .string "And Jesus arose, and followed him,\n"
    .string "and so did his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_20::
    .string "And, behold, a woman, which was\n"
    .string "diseased with an issue of blood\l"
    .string "twelve years, came behind him, and\l"
    .string "touched the hem of his garment:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_21::
    .string "For she said within herself, If I\n"
    .string "may but touch his garment, I shall\l"
    .string "be whole$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_22::
    .string "But Jesus turned him about, and when\n"
    .string "he saw her, he said, Daughter, be of\l"
    .string "good comfort; thy faith hath made\l"
    .string "thee whole. And the woman was made\l"
    .string "whole from that hour.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_23::
    .string "And when Jesus came into the\n"
    .string "ruler’s house, and saw the\l"
    .string "minstrels and the people making a\l"
    .string "noise,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_24::
    .string "He said unto them, Give place: for\n"
    .string "the maid is not dead, but sleepeth.\l"
    .string "And they laughed him to scorn$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_25::
    .string "But when the people were put\n"
    .string "forth, he went in, and took her by the\l"
    .string "hand, and the maid arose.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_26::
    .string "And the fame hereof went abroad into\n"
    .string "all that land.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_27::
    .string "And when Jesus departed thence, two\n"
    .string "blind men followed him, crying, and\l"
    .string "saying, Thou son of David, have mercy\l"
    .string "on us.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_28::
    .string "And when he was come into the house,\n"
    .string "the blind men came to him: and Jesus\l"
    .string "saith unto them, Believe ye that I am\l"
    .string "able to do this? They said unto him,\l"
    .string "Yea, Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_29::
    .string "Then touched he their eyes, saying,\n"
    .string "According to your faith be it unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_30::
    .string "And their eyes were opened; and\n"
    .string "Jesus straitly charged them, saying,\l"
    .string "See that no man know it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_31::
    .string "But they, when they were departed,\n"
    .string "spread abroad his fame in all that\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_32::
    .string "As they went out, behold, they\n"
    .string "brought to him a dumb man possessed\l"
    .string "with a devil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_33::
    .string "And when the devil was cast out, the\n"
    .string "dumb spake: and the multitudes\l"
    .string "marvelled, saying, It was never so\l"
    .string "seen in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_34::
    .string "But the Pharisees said, He casteth\n"
    .string "out devils through the prince of\l"
    .string "the devils.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_35::
    .string "And Jesus went about all the\n"
    .string "cities and villages, teaching in\l"
    .string "their synagogues, and preaching the\l"
    .string "gospel of the kingdom, and healing\l"
    .string "every sickness and every disease\l"
    .string "among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_36::
    .string "But when he saw the multitudes, he\n"
    .string "was moved with compassion on them,\l"
    .string "because they fainted, and were\l"
    .string "scattered abroad, as sheep having no\l"
    .string "shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_37::
    .string "Then saith he unto his disciples,\n"
    .string "The harvest truly is plenteous, but\l"
    .string "the labourers are few;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_9_38::
    .string "Pray ye therefore the Lord of the\n"
    .string "harvest, that he will send forth\l"
    .string "labourers into his harvest$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_1::
    .string "And when he had called unto him his\n"
    .string "twelve disciples, he gave them\l"
    .string "power against unclean spirits, to\l"
    .string "cast them out, and to heal all\l"
    .string "manner of sickness and all manner\l"
    .string "of disease.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_2::
    .string "Now the names of the twelve\n"
    .string "apostles are these; The first,\l"
    .string "Simon, who is called Peter, and\l"
    .string "Andrew his brother; James the son of\l"
    .string "Zebedee, and John his brother;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_3::
    .string "Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas,\n"
    .string "and Matthew the publican; James the\l"
    .string "son of Alphaeus, and Lebbaeus,\l"
    .string "whose surname was Thaddaeus;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_4::
    .string "Simon the Canaanite, and Judas\n"
    .string "Iscariot, who also betrayed him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_5::
    .string "These twelve Jesus sent forth, and\n"
    .string "commanded them, saying, Go not into\l"
    .string "the way of the Gentiles, and into any\l"
    .string "city of the Samaritans enter ye not:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_6::
    .string "But go rather to the lost sheep of\n"
    .string "the house of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_7::
    .string "And as ye go, preach, saying, The\n"
    .string "kingdom of heaven is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_8::
    .string "Heal the sick, cleanse the\n"
    .string "lepers, raise the dead, cast out\l"
    .string "devils: freely ye have received,\l"
    .string "freely give.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_9::
    .string "Provide neither gold, nor silver,\n"
    .string "nor brass in your purses,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_10::
    .string "Nor scrip for your journey, neither\n"
    .string "two coats, neither shoes, nor yet\l"
    .string "staves: for the workman is worthy of\l"
    .string "his meat$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_11::
    .string "And into whatsoever city or town ye\n"
    .string "shall enter, enquire who in it is\l"
    .string "worthy; and there abide till ye go\l"
    .string "thence.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_12::
    .string "And when ye come into an house,\n"
    .string "salute it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_13::
    .string "And if the house be worthy, let your\n"
    .string "peace come upon it: but if it be not\l"
    .string "worthy, let your peace return to\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_14::
    .string "And whosoever shall not receive\n"
    .string "you, nor hear your words, when ye\l"
    .string "depart out of that house or city,\l"
    .string "shake off the dust of your feet.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_15::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, It shall be\n"
    .string "more tolerable for the land of\l"
    .string "Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of\l"
    .string "judgment, than for that city.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_16::
    .string "Behold, I send you forth as sheep\n"
    .string "in the midst of wolves: be ye\l"
    .string "therefore wise as serpents, and\l"
    .string "harmless as doves.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_17::
    .string "But beware of men: for they will\n"
    .string "deliver you up to the councils, and\l"
    .string "they will scourge you in their\l"
    .string "synagogues;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_18::
    .string "And ye shall be brought before\n"
    .string "governors and kings for my sake, for\l"
    .string "a testimony against them and the\l"
    .string "Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_19::
    .string "But when they deliver you up, take\n"
    .string "no thought how or what ye shall\l"
    .string "speak: for it shall be given you in\l"
    .string "that same hour what ye shall speak.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_20::
    .string "For it is not ye that speak, but the\n"
    .string "Spirit of your Father which\l"
    .string "speaketh in you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_21::
    .string "And the brother shall deliver up\n"
    .string "the brother to death, and the father\l"
    .string "the child: and the children shall\l"
    .string "rise up against their parents, and\l"
    .string "cause them to be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_22::
    .string "And ye shall be hated of all men\n"
    .string "for my name’s sake: but he that\l"
    .string "endureth to the end shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_23::
    .string "But when they persecute you in this\n"
    .string "city, flee ye into another: for\l"
    .string "verily I say unto you, Ye shall not\l"
    .string "have gone over the cities of Israel,\l"
    .string "till the Son of man be come.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_24::
    .string "The disciple is not above his\n"
    .string "master, nor the servant above his\l"
    .string "lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_25::
    .string "It is enough for the disciple that\n"
    .string "he be as his master, and the servant\l"
    .string "as his lord. If they have called\l"
    .string "the master of the house Beelzebub,\l"
    .string "how much more shall they call them\l"
    .string "of his household?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_26::
    .string "Fear them not therefore: for there\n"
    .string "is nothing covered, that shall not\l"
    .string "be revealed; and hid, that shall\l"
    .string "not be known$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_27::
    .string "What I tell you in darkness, that\n"
    .string "speak ye in light: and what ye hear\l"
    .string "in the ear, that preach ye upon the\l"
    .string "housetops.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_28::
    .string "And fear not them which kill the\n"
    .string "body, but are not able to kill the\l"
    .string "soul: but rather fear him which is\l"
    .string "able to destroy both soul and body\l"
    .string "in hell.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_29::
    .string "Are not two sparrows sold for a\n"
    .string "farthing? and one of them shall not\l"
    .string "fall on the ground without your\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_30::
    .string "But the very hairs of your head are\n"
    .string "all numbered.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_31::
    .string "Fear ye not therefore, ye are of\n"
    .string "more value than many sparrows.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_32::
    .string "Whosoever therefore shall confess\n"
    .string "me before men, him will I confess\l"
    .string "also before my Father which is in\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_33::
    .string "But whosoever shall deny me before\n"
    .string "men, him will I also deny before my\l"
    .string "Father which is in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_34::
    .string "Think not that I am come to send\n"
    .string "peace on earth: I came not to send\l"
    .string "peace, but a sword.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_35::
    .string "For I am come to set a man at\n"
    .string "variance against his father, and the\l"
    .string "daughter against her mother, and the\l"
    .string "daughter in law against her mother\l"
    .string "in law.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_36::
    .string "And a man’s foes shall be they of\n"
    .string "his own household.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_37::
    .string "He that loveth father or mother\n"
    .string "more than me is not worthy of me: and\l"
    .string "he that loveth son or daughter more\l"
    .string "than me is not worthy of me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_38::
    .string "And he that taketh not his cross,\n"
    .string "and followeth after me, is not\l"
    .string "worthy of me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_39::
    .string "He that findeth his life shall\n"
    .string "lose it: and he that loseth his life\l"
    .string "for my sake shall find it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_40::
    .string "He that receiveth you receiveth me,\n"
    .string "and he that receiveth me receiveth\l"
    .string "him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_41::
    .string "He that receiveth a prophet in the\n"
    .string "name of a prophet shall receive a\l"
    .string "prophet’s reward; and he that\l"
    .string "receiveth a righteous man in the name\l"
    .string "of a righteous man shall receive a\l"
    .string "righteous man’s reward.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_10_42::
    .string "And whosoever shall give to drink\n"
    .string "unto one of these little ones a cup\l"
    .string "of cold water only in the name of a\l"
    .string "disciple, verily I say unto you, he\l"
    .string "shall in no wise lose his reward.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jesus had\n"
    .string "made an end of commanding his twelve\l"
    .string "disciples, he departed thence to\l"
    .string "teach and to preach in their cities.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_2::
    .string "Now when John had heard in the\n"
    .string "prison the works of Christ, he sent\l"
    .string "two of his disciples,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_3::
    .string "And said unto him, Art thou he that\n"
    .string "should come, or do we look for\l"
    .string "another?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_4::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Go and shew John again those things\l"
    .string "which ye do hear and see:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_5::
    .string "The blind receive their sight, and\n"
    .string "the lame walk, the lepers are\l"
    .string "cleansed, and the deaf hear, the\l"
    .string "dead are raised up, and the poor\l"
    .string "have the gospel preached to them$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_6::
    .string "And blessed is he, whosoever shall\n"
    .string "not be offended in me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_7::
    .string "And as they departed, Jesus began\n"
    .string "to say unto the multitudes\l"
    .string "concerning John, What went ye out\l"
    .string "into the wilderness to see? A reed\l"
    .string "shaken with the wind?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_8::
    .string "But what went ye out for to see? A\n"
    .string "man clothed in soft raiment?\l"
    .string "behold, they that wear soft\l"
    .string "clothing are in kings’ houses$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_9::
    .string "But what went ye out for to see? A\n"
    .string "prophet? yea, I say unto you, and\l"
    .string "more than a prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_10::
    .string "For this is he, of whom it is\n"
    .string "written, Behold, I send my messenger\l"
    .string "before thy face, which shall\l"
    .string "prepare thy way before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_11::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Among them\n"
    .string "that are born of women there hath not\l"
    .string "risen a greater than John the\l"
    .string "Baptist: notwithstanding he that is\l"
    .string "least in the kingdom of heaven is\l"
    .string "greater than he.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_12::
    .string "And from the days of John the\n"
    .string "Baptist until now the kingdom of\l"
    .string "heaven suffereth violence, and the\l"
    .string "violent take it by force.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_13::
    .string "For all the prophets and the law\n"
    .string "prophesied until John.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_14::
    .string "And if ye will receive it, this is\n"
    .string "Elias, which was for to come.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_15::
    .string "He that hath ears to hear, let him\n"
    .string "hear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_16::
    .string "But whereunto shall I liken this\n"
    .string "generation? It is like unto\l"
    .string "children sitting in the markets, and\l"
    .string "calling unto their fellows,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_17::
    .string "And saying, We have piped unto you,\n"
    .string "and ye have not danced; we have\l"
    .string "mourned unto you, and ye have not\l"
    .string "lamented$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_18::
    .string "For John came neither eating nor\n"
    .string "drinking, and they say, He hath a\l"
    .string "devil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_19::
    .string "The Son of man came eating and\n"
    .string "drinking, and they say, Behold a man\l"
    .string "gluttonous, and a winebibber, a\l"
    .string "friend of publicans and sinners.\l"
    .string "But wisdom is justified of her\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_20::
    .string "Then began he to upbraid the cities\n"
    .string "wherein most of his mighty works were\l"
    .string "done, because they repented not:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_21::
    .string "Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto\n"
    .string "thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty\l"
    .string "works, which were done in you, had\l"
    .string "been done in Tyre and Sidon, they\l"
    .string "would have repented long ago in\l"
    .string "sackcloth and ashes$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_22::
    .string "But I say unto you, It shall be\n"
    .string "more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon\l"
    .string "at the day of judgment, than for you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_23::
    .string "And thou, Capernaum, which art\n"
    .string "exalted unto heaven, shalt be\l"
    .string "brought down to hell: for if the\l"
    .string "mighty works, which have been done in\l"
    .string "thee, had been done in Sodom, it\l"
    .string "would have remained until this day.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_24::
    .string "But I say unto you, That it shall\n"
    .string "be more tolerable for the land of\l"
    .string "Sodom in the day of judgment, than\l"
    .string "for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_25::
    .string "At that time Jesus answered and\n"
    .string "said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of\l"
    .string "heaven and earth, because thou hast\l"
    .string "hid these things from the wise and\l"
    .string "prudent, and hast revealed them unto\l"
    .string "babes.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_26::
    .string "Even so, Father: for so it seemed\n"
    .string "good in thy sight.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_27::
    .string "All things are delivered unto me\n"
    .string "of my Father: and no man knoweth the\l"
    .string "Son, but the Father; neither knoweth\l"
    .string "any man the Father, save the Son, and\l"
    .string "he to whomsoever the Son will\l"
    .string "reveal him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_28::
    .string "Come unto me, all ye that labour\n"
    .string "and are heavy laden, and I will\l"
    .string "give you rest.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_29::
    .string "Take my yoke upon you, and learn of\n"
    .string "me; for I am meek and lowly in\l"
    .string "heart: and ye shall find rest unto\l"
    .string "your souls.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_11_30::
    .string "For my yoke is easy, and my burden is\n"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_1::
    .string "At that time Jesus went on the\n"
    .string "sabbath day through the corn; and his\l"
    .string "disciples were an hungred, and\l"
    .string "began to pluck the ears of corn and\l"
    .string "to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_2::
    .string "But when the Pharisees saw it, they\n"
    .string "said unto him, Behold, thy\l"
    .string "disciples do that which is not\l"
    .string "lawful to do upon the sabbath day.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_3::
    .string "But he said unto them, Have ye not\n"
    .string "read what David did, when he was an\l"
    .string "hungred, and they that were with him;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_4::
    .string "How he entered into the house of\n"
    .string "God, and did eat the shewbread, which\l"
    .string "was not lawful for him to eat,\l"
    .string "neither for them which were with him,\l"
    .string "but only for the priests?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_5::
    .string "Or have ye not read in the law, how\n"
    .string "that on the sabbath days the priests\l"
    .string "in the temple profane the sabbath,\l"
    .string "and are blameless?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_6::
    .string "But I say unto you, That in this\n"
    .string "place is one greater than the\l"
    .string "temple$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_7::
    .string "But if ye had known what this\n"
    .string "meaneth, I will have mercy, and not\l"
    .string "sacrifice, ye would not have\l"
    .string "condemned the guiltless.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_8::
    .string "For the Son of man is Lord even of\n"
    .string "the sabbath day.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_9::
    .string "And when he was departed thence, he\n"
    .string "went into their synagogue:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_10::
    .string "And, behold, there was a man which\n"
    .string "had his hand withered. And they asked\l"
    .string "him, saying, Is it lawful to heal\l"
    .string "on the sabbath days? that they might\l"
    .string "accuse him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_11::
    .string "And he said unto them, What man\n"
    .string "shall there be among you, that\l"
    .string "shall have one sheep, and if it\l"
    .string "fall into a pit on the sabbath day,\l"
    .string "will he not lay hold on it, and\l"
    .string "lift it out?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_12::
    .string "How much then is a man better than a\n"
    .string "sheep? Wherefore it is lawful to do\l"
    .string "well on the sabbath days$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_13::
    .string "Then saith he to the man, Stretch\n"
    .string "forth thine hand. And he stretched it\l"
    .string "forth; and it was restored whole,\l"
    .string "like as the other.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_14::
    .string "Then the Pharisees went out, and\n"
    .string "held a council against him, how they\l"
    .string "might destroy him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_15::
    .string "But when Jesus knew it, he withdrew\n"
    .string "himself from thence: and great\l"
    .string "multitudes followed him, and he\l"
    .string "healed them all;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_16::
    .string "And charged them that they should\n"
    .string "not make him known:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_17::
    .string "That it might be fulfilled which\n"
    .string "was spoken by Esaias the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_18::
    .string "Behold my servant, whom I have\n"
    .string "chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul\l"
    .string "is well pleased: I will put my\l"
    .string "spirit upon him, and he shall shew\l"
    .string "judgment to the Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_19::
    .string "He shall not strive, nor cry;\n"
    .string "neither shall any man hear his\l"
    .string "voice in the streets.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_20::
    .string "A bruised reed shall he not break,\n"
    .string "and smoking flax shall he not\l"
    .string "quench, till he send forth judgment\l"
    .string "unto victory.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_21::
    .string "And in his name shall the Gentiles\n"
    .string "trust.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_22::
    .string "Then was brought unto him one\n"
    .string "possessed with a devil, blind, and\l"
    .string "dumb: and he healed him, insomuch\l"
    .string "that the blind and dumb both spake\l"
    .string "and saw.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_23::
    .string "And all the people were amazed,\n"
    .string "and said, Is not this the son of\l"
    .string "David?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_24::
    .string "But when the Pharisees heard it,\n"
    .string "they said, This fellow doth not cast\l"
    .string "out devils, but by Beelzebub the\l"
    .string "prince of the devils$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_25::
    .string "And Jesus knew their thoughts, and\n"
    .string "said unto them, Every kingdom divided\l"
    .string "against itself is brought to\l"
    .string "desolation; and every city or house\l"
    .string "divided against itself shall not\l"
    .string "stand:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_26::
    .string "And if Satan cast out Satan, he is\n"
    .string "divided against himself; how shall\l"
    .string "then his kingdom stand?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_27::
    .string "And if I by Beelzebub cast out\n"
    .string "devils, by whom do your children\l"
    .string "cast them out? therefore they shall\l"
    .string "be your judges$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_28::
    .string "But if I cast out devils by the\n"
    .string "Spirit of God, then the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God is come unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_29::
    .string "Or else how can one enter into a\n"
    .string "strong man’s house, and spoil his\l"
    .string "goods, except he first bind the\l"
    .string "strong man? and then he will spoil\l"
    .string "his house.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_30::
    .string "He that is not with me is against me;\n"
    .string "and he that gathereth not with me\l"
    .string "scattereth abroad.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_31::
    .string "Wherefore I say unto you, All\n"
    .string "manner of sin and blasphemy shall\l"
    .string "be forgiven unto men: but the\l"
    .string "blasphemy against the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "shall not be forgiven unto men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_32::
    .string "And whosoever speaketh a word\n"
    .string "against the Son of man, it shall be\l"
    .string "forgiven him: but whosoever speaketh\l"
    .string "against the Holy Ghost, it shall\l"
    .string "not be forgiven him, neither in this\l"
    .string "world, neither in the world to come.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_33::
    .string "Either make the tree good, and his\n"
    .string "fruit good; or else make the tree\l"
    .string "corrupt, and his fruit corrupt: for\l"
    .string "the tree is known by his fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_34::
    .string "O generation of vipers, how can ye,\n"
    .string "being evil, speak good things? for\l"
    .string "out of the abundance of the heart the\l"
    .string "mouth speaketh.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_35::
    .string "A good man out of the good treasure\n"
    .string "of the heart bringeth forth good\l"
    .string "things: and an evil man out of the\l"
    .string "evil treasure bringeth forth evil\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_36::
    .string "But I say unto you, That every idle\n"
    .string "word that men shall speak, they\l"
    .string "shall give account thereof in the\l"
    .string "day of judgment.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_37::
    .string "For by thy words thou shalt be\n"
    .string "justified, and by thy words thou\l"
    .string "shalt be condemned.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_38::
    .string "Then certain of the scribes and of\n"
    .string "the Pharisees answered, saying,\l"
    .string "Master, we would see a sign from\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_39::
    .string "But he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "An evil and adulterous generation\l"
    .string "seeketh after a sign; and there\l"
    .string "shall no sign be given to it, but\l"
    .string "the sign of the prophet Jonas:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_40::
    .string "For as Jonas was three days and\n"
    .string "three nights in the whale’s belly;\l"
    .string "so shall the Son of man be three\l"
    .string "days and three nights in the heart of\l"
    .string "the earth$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_41::
    .string "The men of Nineveh shall rise in\n"
    .string "judgment with this generation, and\l"
    .string "shall condemn it: because they\l"
    .string "repented at the preaching of Jonas;\l"
    .string "and, behold, a greater than Jonas is\l"
    .string "here.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_42::
    .string "The queen of the south shall rise\n"
    .string "up in the judgment with this\l"
    .string "generation, and shall condemn it:\l"
    .string "for she came from the uttermost\l"
    .string "parts of the earth to hear the wisdom\l"
    .string "of Solomon; and, behold, a greater\l"
    .string "than Solomon is here.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_43::
    .string "When the unclean spirit is gone\n"
    .string "out of a man, he walketh through dry\l"
    .string "places, seeking rest, and findeth\l"
    .string "none.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_44::
    .string "Then he saith, I will return into\n"
    .string "my house from whence I came out; and\l"
    .string "when he is come, he findeth it empty,\l"
    .string "swept, and garnished.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_45::
    .string "Then goeth he, and taketh with\n"
    .string "himself seven other spirits more\l"
    .string "wicked than himself, and they enter\l"
    .string "in and dwell there: and the last\l"
    .string "state of that man is worse than the\l"
    .string "first. Even so shall it be also\l"
    .string "unto this wicked generation.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_46::
    .string "While he yet talked to the\n"
    .string "people, behold, his mother and his\l"
    .string "brethren stood without, desiring to\l"
    .string "speak with him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_47::
    .string "Then one said unto him, Behold, thy\n"
    .string "mother and thy brethren stand\l"
    .string "without, desiring to speak with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_48::
    .string "But he answered and said unto him\n"
    .string "that told him, Who is my mother? and\l"
    .string "who are my brethren?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_49::
    .string "And he stretched forth his hand\n"
    .string "toward his disciples, and said,\l"
    .string "Behold my mother and my brethren!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_12_50::
    .string "For whosoever shall do the will\n"
    .string "of my Father which is in heaven, the\l"
    .string "same is my brother, and sister, and\l"
    .string "mother$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_1::
    .string "The same day went Jesus out of the\n"
    .string "house, and sat by the sea side.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_2::
    .string "And great multitudes were gathered\n"
    .string "together unto him, so that he went\l"
    .string "into a ship, and sat; and the whole\l"
    .string "multitude stood on the shore.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_3::
    .string "And he spake many things unto them\n"
    .string "in parables, saying, Behold, a\l"
    .string "sower went forth to sow;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_4::
    .string "And when he sowed, some seeds fell\n"
    .string "by the way side, and the fowls came\l"
    .string "and devoured them up:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_5::
    .string "Some fell upon stony places,\n"
    .string "where they had not much earth: and\l"
    .string "forthwith they sprung up, because\l"
    .string "they had no deepness of earth:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_6::
    .string "And when the sun was up, they were\n"
    .string "scorched; and because they had no\l"
    .string "root, they withered away$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_7::
    .string "And some fell among thorns; and the\n"
    .string "thorns sprung up, and choked them:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_8::
    .string "But other fell into good ground,\n"
    .string "and brought forth fruit, some an\l"
    .string "hundredfold, some sixtyfold, some\l"
    .string "thirtyfold$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_9::
    .string "Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_10::
    .string "And the disciples came, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Why speakest thou unto\l"
    .string "them in parables?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_11::
    .string "He answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Because it is given unto you to know\l"
    .string "the mysteries of the kingdom of\l"
    .string "heaven, but to them it is not given$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_12::
    .string "For whosoever hath, to him shall be\n"
    .string "given, and he shall have more\l"
    .string "abundance: but whosoever hath not,\l"
    .string "from him shall be taken away even\l"
    .string "that he hath.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_13::
    .string "Therefore speak I to them in\n"
    .string "parables: because they seeing see\l"
    .string "not; and hearing they hear not,\l"
    .string "neither do they understand.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_14::
    .string "And in them is fulfilled the\n"
    .string "prophecy of Esaias, which saith, By\l"
    .string "hearing ye shall hear, and shall\l"
    .string "not understand; and seeing ye shall\l"
    .string "see, and shall not perceive:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_15::
    .string "For this people’s heart is waxed\n"
    .string "gross, and their ears are dull of\l"
    .string "hearing, and their eyes they have\l"
    .string "closed; lest at any time they\l"
    .string "should see with their eyes and hear\l"
    .string "with their ears, and should\l"
    .string "understand with their heart, and\l"
    .string "should be converted, and I should\l"
    .string "heal them$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_16::
    .string "But blessed are your eyes, for they\n"
    .string "see: and your ears, for they hear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_17::
    .string "For verily I say unto you, That many\n"
    .string "prophets and righteous men have\l"
    .string "desired to see those things which ye\l"
    .string "see, and have not seen them; and to\l"
    .string "hear those things which ye hear, and\l"
    .string "have not heard them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_18::
    .string "Hear ye therefore the parable of\n"
    .string "the sower.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_19::
    .string "When any one heareth the word of the\n"
    .string "kingdom, and understandeth it not,\l"
    .string "then cometh the wicked one, and\l"
    .string "catcheth away that which was sown in\l"
    .string "his heart. This is he which received\l"
    .string "seed by the way side.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_20::
    .string "But he that received the seed into\n"
    .string "stony places, the same is he that\l"
    .string "heareth the word, and anon with joy\l"
    .string "receiveth it;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_21::
    .string "Yet hath he not root in himself, but\n"
    .string "dureth for a while: for when\l"
    .string "tribulation or persecution ariseth\l"
    .string "because of the word, by and by he is\l"
    .string "offended$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_22::
    .string "He also that received seed among\n"
    .string "the thorns is he that heareth the\l"
    .string "word; and the care of this world, and\l"
    .string "the deceitfulness of riches, choke\l"
    .string "the word, and he becometh unfruitful.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_23::
    .string "But he that received seed into the\n"
    .string "good ground is he that heareth the\l"
    .string "word, and understandeth it; which\l"
    .string "also beareth fruit, and bringeth\l"
    .string "forth, some an hundredfold, some\l"
    .string "sixty, some thirty.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_24::
    .string "Another parable put he forth unto\n"
    .string "them, saying, The kingdom of heaven\l"
    .string "is likened unto a man which sowed\l"
    .string "good seed in his field:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_25::
    .string "But while men slept, his enemy\n"
    .string "came and sowed tares among the wheat,\l"
    .string "and went his way$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_26::
    .string "But when the blade was sprung up,\n"
    .string "and brought forth fruit, then\l"
    .string "appeared the tares also.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_27::
    .string "So the servants of the householder\n"
    .string "came and said unto him, Sir, didst\l"
    .string "not thou sow good seed in thy field?\l"
    .string "from whence then hath it tares?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_28::
    .string "He said unto them, An enemy hath\n"
    .string "done this. The servants said unto\l"
    .string "him, Wilt thou then that we go and\l"
    .string "gather them up?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_29::
    .string "But he said, Nay; lest while ye\n"
    .string "gather up the tares, ye root up\l"
    .string "also the wheat with them$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_30::
    .string "Let both grow together until the\n"
    .string "harvest: and in the time of harvest I\l"
    .string "will say to the reapers, Gather ye\l"
    .string "together first the tares, and bind\l"
    .string "them in bundles to burn them: but\l"
    .string "gather the wheat into my barn.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_31::
    .string "Another parable put he forth unto\n"
    .string "them, saying, The kingdom of heaven\l"
    .string "is like to a grain of mustard seed,\l"
    .string "which a man took, and sowed in his\l"
    .string "field:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_32::
    .string "Which indeed is the least of all\n"
    .string "seeds: but when it is grown, it is the\l"
    .string "greatest among herbs, and becometh a\l"
    .string "tree, so that the birds of the air\l"
    .string "come and lodge in the branches\l"
    .string "thereof$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_33::
    .string "Another parable spake he unto\n"
    .string "them; The kingdom of heaven is like\l"
    .string "unto leaven, which a woman took, and\l"
    .string "hid in three measures of meal, till\l"
    .string "the whole was leavened.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_34::
    .string "All these things spake Jesus unto\n"
    .string "the multitude in parables; and\l"
    .string "without a parable spake he not unto\l"
    .string "them:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_35::
    .string "That it might be fulfilled which\n"
    .string "was spoken by the prophet, saying,\l"
    .string "I will open my mouth in parables;\l"
    .string "I will utter things which have been\l"
    .string "kept secret from the foundation of\l"
    .string "the world$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_36::
    .string "Then Jesus sent the multitude away,\n"
    .string "and went into the house: and his\l"
    .string "disciples came unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Declare unto us the parable of the\l"
    .string "tares of the field.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_37::
    .string "He answered and said unto them, He\n"
    .string "that soweth the good seed is the Son\l"
    .string "of man;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_38::
    .string "The field is the world; the good\n"
    .string "seed are the children of the\l"
    .string "kingdom; but the tares are the\l"
    .string "children of the wicked one;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_39::
    .string "The enemy that sowed them is the\n"
    .string "devil; the harvest is the end of the\l"
    .string "world; and the reapers are the\l"
    .string "angels$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_40::
    .string "As therefore the tares are gathered\n"
    .string "and burned in the fire; so shall it\l"
    .string "be in the end of this world.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_41::
    .string "The Son of man shall send forth his\n"
    .string "angels, and they shall gather out\l"
    .string "of his kingdom all things that\l"
    .string "offend, and them which do iniquity;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_42::
    .string "And shall cast them into a furnace\n"
    .string "of fire: there shall be wailing and\l"
    .string "gnashing of teeth$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_43::
    .string "Then shall the righteous shine\n"
    .string "forth as the sun in the kingdom of\l"
    .string "their Father. Who hath ears to hear,\l"
    .string "let him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_44::
    .string "Again, the kingdom of heaven is\n"
    .string "like unto treasure hid in a field;\l"
    .string "the which when a man hath found, he\l"
    .string "hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and\l"
    .string "selleth all that he hath, and\l"
    .string "buyeth that field.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_45::
    .string "Again, the kingdom of heaven is\n"
    .string "like unto a merchant man, seeking\l"
    .string "goodly pearls:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_46::
    .string "Who, when he had found one pearl of\n"
    .string "great price, went and sold all\l"
    .string "that he had, and bought it$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_47::
    .string "Again, the kingdom of heaven is\n"
    .string "like unto a net, that was cast into\l"
    .string "the sea, and gathered of every kind:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_48::
    .string "Which, when it was full, they drew\n"
    .string "to shore, and sat down, and gathered\l"
    .string "the good into vessels, but cast the\l"
    .string "bad away$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_49::
    .string "So shall it be at the end of the\n"
    .string "world: the angels shall come\l"
    .string "forth, and sever the wicked from\l"
    .string "among the just,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_50::
    .string "And shall cast them into the\n"
    .string "furnace of fire: there shall be\l"
    .string "wailing and gnashing of teeth$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_51::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, Have ye\n"
    .string "understood all these things? They\l"
    .string "say unto him, Yea, Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_52::
    .string "Then said he unto them, Therefore\n"
    .string "every scribe which is instructed\l"
    .string "unto the kingdom of heaven is like\l"
    .string "unto a man that is an householder,\l"
    .string "which bringeth forth out of his\l"
    .string "treasure things new and old.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_53::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when Jesus\n"
    .string "had finished these parables, he\l"
    .string "departed thence.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_54::
    .string "And when he was come into his own\n"
    .string "country, he taught them in their\l"
    .string "synagogue, insomuch that they were\l"
    .string "astonished, and said, Whence hath\l"
    .string "this man this wisdom, and these\l"
    .string "mighty works?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_55::
    .string "Is not this the carpenter’s son? is\n"
    .string "not his mother called Mary? and his\l"
    .string "brethren, James, and Joses, and\l"
    .string "Simon, and Judas?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_56::
    .string "And his sisters, are they not all\n"
    .string "with us? Whence then hath this man\l"
    .string "all these things?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_57::
    .string "And they were offended in him. But\n"
    .string "Jesus said unto them, A prophet is\l"
    .string "not without honour, save in his own\l"
    .string "country, and in his own house$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_13_58::
    .string "And he did not many mighty works\n"
    .string "there because of their unbelief.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_1::
    .string "At that time Herod the tetrarch\n"
    .string "heard of the fame of Jesus,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_2::
    .string "And said unto his servants, This is\n"
    .string "John the Baptist; he is risen from\l"
    .string "the dead; and therefore mighty works\l"
    .string "do shew forth themselves in him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_3::
    .string "For Herod had laid hold on John,\n"
    .string "and bound him, and put him in prison\l"
    .string "for Herodias’ sake, his brother\l"
    .string "Philip’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_4::
    .string "For John said unto him, It is not\n"
    .string "lawful for thee to have her.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_5::
    .string "And when he would have put him to\n"
    .string "death, he feared the multitude,\l"
    .string "because they counted him as a\l"
    .string "prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_6::
    .string "But when Herod’s birthday was kept,\n"
    .string "the daughter of Herodias danced\l"
    .string "before them, and pleased Herod.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_7::
    .string "Whereupon he promised with an oath\n"
    .string "to give her whatsoever she would ask.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_8::
    .string "And she, being before instructed of\n"
    .string "her mother, said, Give me here John\l"
    .string "Baptist’s head in a charger.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_9::
    .string "And the king was sorry:\n"
    .string "nevertheless for the oath’s sake,\l"
    .string "and them which sat with him at meat,\l"
    .string "he commanded it to be given her.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_10::
    .string "And he sent, and beheaded John in\n"
    .string "the prison.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_11::
    .string "And his head was brought in a\n"
    .string "charger, and given to the damsel:\l"
    .string "and she brought it to her mother.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_12::
    .string "And his disciples came, and took\n"
    .string "up the body, and buried it, and went\l"
    .string "and told Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_13::
    .string "When Jesus heard of it, he departed\n"
    .string "thence by ship into a desert place\l"
    .string "apart: and when the people had\l"
    .string "heard thereof, they followed him on\l"
    .string "foot out of the cities.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_14::
    .string "And Jesus went forth, and saw a\n"
    .string "great multitude, and was moved with\l"
    .string "compassion toward them, and he\l"
    .string "healed their sick.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_15::
    .string "And when it was evening, his\n"
    .string "disciples came to him, saying, This\l"
    .string "is a desert place, and the time is\l"
    .string "now past; send the multitude away,\l"
    .string "that they may go into the villages,\l"
    .string "and buy themselves victuals.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_16::
    .string "But Jesus said unto them, They need\n"
    .string "not depart; give ye them to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_17::
    .string "And they say unto him, We have here\n"
    .string "but five loaves, and two fishes.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_18::
    .string "He said, Bring them hither to me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_19::
    .string "And he commanded the multitude to\n"
    .string "sit down on the grass, and took the\l"
    .string "five loaves, and the two fishes, and\l"
    .string "looking up to heaven, he blessed,\l"
    .string "and brake, and gave the loaves to his\l"
    .string "disciples, and the disciples to\l"
    .string "the multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_20::
    .string "And they did all eat, and were\n"
    .string "filled: and they took up of the\l"
    .string "fragments that remained twelve\l"
    .string "baskets full.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_21::
    .string "And they that had eaten were about\n"
    .string "five thousand men, beside women and\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_22::
    .string "And straightway Jesus constrained\n"
    .string "his disciples to get into a ship,\l"
    .string "and to go before him unto the other\l"
    .string "side, while he sent the multitudes\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_23::
    .string "And when he had sent the multitudes\n"
    .string "away, he went up into a mountain\l"
    .string "apart to pray: and when the evening\l"
    .string "was come, he was there alone.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_24::
    .string "But the ship was now in the midst of\n"
    .string "the sea, tossed with waves: for the\l"
    .string "wind was contrary.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_25::
    .string "And in the fourth watch of the night\n"
    .string "Jesus went unto them, walking on the\l"
    .string "sea.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_26::
    .string "And when the disciples saw him\n"
    .string "walking on the sea, they were\l"
    .string "troubled, saying, It is a spirit;\l"
    .string "and they cried out for fear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_27::
    .string "But straightway Jesus spake unto\n"
    .string "them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is\l"
    .string "I; be not afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_28::
    .string "And Peter answered him and said,\n"
    .string "Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto\l"
    .string "thee on the water.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_29::
    .string "And he said, Come. And when Peter\n"
    .string "was come down out of the ship, he\l"
    .string "walked on the water, to go to Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_30::
    .string "But when he saw the wind boisterous,\n"
    .string "he was afraid; and beginning to sink,\l"
    .string "he cried, saying, Lord, save me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_31::
    .string "And immediately Jesus stretched\n"
    .string "forth his hand, and caught him, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, O thou of little\l"
    .string "faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_32::
    .string "And when they were come into the\n"
    .string "ship, the wind ceased$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_33::
    .string "Then they that were in the ship\n"
    .string "came and worshipped him, saying, Of\l"
    .string "a truth thou art the Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_34::
    .string "And when they were gone over, they\n"
    .string "came into the land of Gennesaret.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_35::
    .string "And when the men of that place had\n"
    .string "knowledge of him, they sent out into\l"
    .string "all that country round about, and\l"
    .string "brought unto him all that were\l"
    .string "diseased;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_14_36::
    .string "And besought him that they might\n"
    .string "only touch the hem of his garment:\l"
    .string "and as many as touched were made\l"
    .string "perfectly whole$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_1::
    .string "Then came to Jesus scribes and\n"
    .string "Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_2::
    .string "Why do thy disciples transgress\n"
    .string "the tradition of the elders? for\l"
    .string "they wash not their hands when they\l"
    .string "eat bread$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_3::
    .string "But he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Why do ye also transgress the\l"
    .string "commandment of God by your tradition?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_4::
    .string "For God commanded, saying, Honour\n"
    .string "thy father and mother: and, He that\l"
    .string "curseth father or mother, let him\l"
    .string "die the death$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_5::
    .string "But ye say, Whosoever shall say to\n"
    .string "his father or his mother, It is a\l"
    .string "gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be\l"
    .string "profited by me;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_6::
    .string "And honour not his father or his\n"
    .string "mother, he shall be free. Thus have\l"
    .string "ye made the commandment of God of\l"
    .string "none effect by your tradition$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_7::
    .string "Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias\n"
    .string "prophesy of you, saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_8::
    .string "This people draweth nigh unto me\n"
    .string "with their mouth, and honoureth me\l"
    .string "with their lips; but their heart is\l"
    .string "far from me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_9::
    .string "But in vain they do worship me,\n"
    .string "teaching for doctrines the\l"
    .string "commandments of men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_10::
    .string "And he called the multitude, and\n"
    .string "said unto them, Hear, and understand:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_11::
    .string "Not that which goeth into the mouth\n"
    .string "defileth a man; but that which\l"
    .string "cometh out of the mouth, this\l"
    .string "defileth a man$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_12::
    .string "Then came his disciples, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Knowest thou that the\l"
    .string "Pharisees were offended, after they\l"
    .string "heard this saying?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_13::
    .string "But he answered and said, Every\n"
    .string "plant, which my heavenly Father\l"
    .string "hath not planted, shall be rooted\l"
    .string "up$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_14::
    .string "Let them alone: they be blind\n"
    .string "leaders of the blind. And if the\l"
    .string "blind lead the blind, both shall\l"
    .string "fall into the ditch.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_15::
    .string "Then answered Peter and said unto\n"
    .string "him, Declare unto us this parable.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_16::
    .string "And Jesus said, Are ye also yet\n"
    .string "without understanding?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_17::
    .string "Do not ye yet understand, that\n"
    .string "whatsoever entereth in at the mouth\l"
    .string "goeth into the belly, and is cast\l"
    .string "out into the draught?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_18::
    .string "But those things which proceed out\n"
    .string "of the mouth come forth from the\l"
    .string "heart; and they defile the man$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_19::
    .string "For out of the heart proceed evil\n"
    .string "thoughts, murders, adulteries,\l"
    .string "fornications, thefts, false witness,\l"
    .string "blasphemies:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_20::
    .string "These are the things which defile a\n"
    .string "man: but to eat with unwashen hands\l"
    .string "defileth not a man$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_21::
    .string "Then Jesus went thence, and\n"
    .string "departed into the coasts of Tyre and\l"
    .string "Sidon.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_22::
    .string "And, behold, a woman of Canaan came\n"
    .string "out of the same coasts, and cried\l"
    .string "unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O\l"
    .string "Lord, thou son of David; my daughter\l"
    .string "is grievously vexed with a devil.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_23::
    .string "But he answered her not a word. And\n"
    .string "his disciples came and besought\l"
    .string "him, saying, Send her away; for she\l"
    .string "crieth after us.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_24::
    .string "But he answered and said, I am not\n"
    .string "sent but unto the lost sheep of the\l"
    .string "house of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_25::
    .string "Then came she and worshipped him,\n"
    .string "saying, Lord, help me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_26::
    .string "But he answered and said, It is not\n"
    .string "meet to take the children’s bread,\l"
    .string "and to cast it to dogs.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_27::
    .string "And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the\n"
    .string "dogs eat of the crumbs which fall\l"
    .string "from their masters’ table.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_28::
    .string "Then Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "her, O woman, great is thy faith: be\l"
    .string "it unto thee even as thou wilt. And\l"
    .string "her daughter was made whole from\l"
    .string "that very hour.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_29::
    .string "And Jesus departed from thence, and\n"
    .string "came nigh unto the sea of Galilee;\l"
    .string "and went up into a mountain, and sat\l"
    .string "down there.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_30::
    .string "And great multitudes came unto him,\n"
    .string "having with them those that were\l"
    .string "lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many\l"
    .string "others, and cast them down at Jesus’\l"
    .string "feet; and he healed them:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_31::
    .string "Insomuch that the multitude\n"
    .string "wondered, when they saw the dumb to\l"
    .string "speak, the maimed to be whole, the\l"
    .string "lame to walk, and the blind to see:\l"
    .string "and they glorified the God of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_32::
    .string "Then Jesus called his disciples\n"
    .string "unto him, and said, I have\l"
    .string "compassion on the multitude,\l"
    .string "because they continue with me now\l"
    .string "three days, and have nothing to eat:\l"
    .string "and I will not send them away\l"
    .string "fasting, lest they faint in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_33::
    .string "And his disciples say unto him,\n"
    .string "Whence should we have so much bread\l"
    .string "in the wilderness, as to fill so\l"
    .string "great a multitude?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_34::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto them, How many\n"
    .string "loaves have ye? And they said, Seven,\l"
    .string "and a few little fishes$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_35::
    .string "And he commanded the multitude to\n"
    .string "sit down on the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_36::
    .string "And he took the seven loaves and\n"
    .string "the fishes, and gave thanks, and\l"
    .string "brake them, and gave to his\l"
    .string "disciples, and the disciples to\l"
    .string "the multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_37::
    .string "And they did all eat, and were\n"
    .string "filled: and they took up of the\l"
    .string "broken meat that was left seven\l"
    .string "baskets full.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_38::
    .string "And they that did eat were four\n"
    .string "thousand men, beside women and\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_15_39::
    .string "And he sent away the multitude, and\n"
    .string "took ship, and came into the coasts\l"
    .string "of Magdala.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_1::
    .string "The Pharisees also with the\n"
    .string "Sadducees came, and tempting desired\l"
    .string "him that he would shew them a sign\l"
    .string "from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_2::
    .string "He answered and said unto them, When\n"
    .string "it is evening, ye say, It will be\l"
    .string "fair weather: for the sky is red.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_3::
    .string "And in the morning, It will be\n"
    .string "foul weather to day: for the sky is\l"
    .string "red and lowering. O ye hypocrites,\l"
    .string "ye can discern the face of the sky;\l"
    .string "but can ye not discern the signs of\l"
    .string "the times?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_4::
    .string "A wicked and adulterous generation\n"
    .string "seeketh after a sign; and there\l"
    .string "shall no sign be given unto it, but\l"
    .string "the sign of the prophet Jonas. And\l"
    .string "he left them, and departed$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_5::
    .string "And when his disciples were come\n"
    .string "to the other side, they had forgotten\l"
    .string "to take bread.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_6::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto them, Take heed\n"
    .string "and beware of the leaven of the\l"
    .string "Pharisees and of the Sadducees.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_7::
    .string "And they reasoned among themselves,\n"
    .string "saying, It is because we have taken\l"
    .string "no bread.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_8::
    .string "Which when Jesus perceived, he said\n"
    .string "unto them, O ye of little faith, why\l"
    .string "reason ye among yourselves, because\l"
    .string "ye have brought no bread?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_9::
    .string "Do ye not yet understand, neither\n"
    .string "remember the five loaves of the five\l"
    .string "thousand, and how many baskets ye\l"
    .string "took up?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_10::
    .string "Neither the seven loaves of the\n"
    .string "four thousand, and how many baskets\l"
    .string "ye took up?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_11::
    .string "How is it that ye do not understand\n"
    .string "that I spake it not to you\l"
    .string "concerning bread, that ye should\l"
    .string "beware of the leaven of the\l"
    .string "Pharisees and of the Sadducees?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_12::
    .string "Then understood they how that he\n"
    .string "bade them not beware of the leaven\l"
    .string "of bread, but of the doctrine of the\l"
    .string "Pharisees and of the Sadducees$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_13::
    .string "When Jesus came into the coasts of\n"
    .string "Caesarea Philippi, he asked his\l"
    .string "disciples, saying, Whom do men say\l"
    .string "that I the Son of man am?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_14::
    .string "And they said, Some say that thou\n"
    .string "art John the Baptist: some, Elias;\l"
    .string "and others, Jeremias, or one of the\l"
    .string "prophets$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_15::
    .string "He saith unto them, But whom say ye\n"
    .string "that I am?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_16::
    .string "And Simon Peter answered and said,\n"
    .string "Thou art the Christ, the Son of the\l"
    .string "living God$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_16_17::
