    .string "the twelve tribes of Israel$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_19_29::
    .string "And every one that hath forsaken\n"
    .string "houses, or brethren, or sisters, or\l"
    .string "father, or mother, or wife, or\l"
    .string "children, or lands, for my name’s\l"
    .string "sake, shall receive an\l"
    .string "hundredfold, and shall inherit\l"
    .string "everlasting life.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_19_30::
    .string "But many that are first shall be\n"
    .string "last; and the last shall be first.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_1::
    .string "For the kingdom of heaven is like\n"
    .string "unto a man that is an householder,\l"
    .string "which went out early in the morning\l"
    .string "to hire labourers into his vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_2::
    .string "And when he had agreed with the\n"
    .string "labourers for a penny a day, he sent\l"
    .string "them into his vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_3::
    .string "And he went out about the third\n"
    .string "hour, and saw others standing idle\l"
    .string "in the marketplace,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_4::
    .string "And said unto them; Go ye also into\n"
    .string "the vineyard, and whatsoever is right\l"
    .string "I will give you. And they went their\l"
    .string "way$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_5::
    .string "Again he went out about the sixth\n"
    .string "and ninth hour, and did likewise.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_6::
    .string "And about the eleventh hour he went\n"
    .string "out, and found others standing idle,\l"
    .string "and saith unto them, Why stand ye\l"
    .string "here all the day idle?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_7::
    .string "They say unto him, Because no man\n"
    .string "hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go\l"
    .string "ye also into the vineyard; and\l"
    .string "whatsoever is right, that shall ye\l"
    .string "receive$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_8::
    .string "So when even was come, the lord of\n"
    .string "the vineyard saith unto his steward,\l"
    .string "Call the labourers, and give them\l"
    .string "their hire, beginning from the last\l"
    .string "unto the first.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_9::
    .string "And when they came that were hired\n"
    .string "about the eleventh hour, they\l"
    .string "received every man a penny.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_10::
    .string "But when the first came, they\n"
    .string "supposed that they should have\l"
    .string "received more; and they likewise\l"
    .string "received every man a penny.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_11::
    .string "And when they had received it, they\n"
    .string "murmured against the goodman of the\l"
    .string "house,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_12::
    .string "Saying, These last have wrought but\n"
    .string "one hour, and thou hast made them\l"
    .string "equal unto us, which have borne the\l"
    .string "burden and heat of the day$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_13::
    .string "But he answered one of them, and\n"
    .string "said, Friend, I do thee no wrong:\l"
    .string "didst not thou agree with me for a\l"
    .string "penny?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_14::
    .string "Take that thine is, and go thy way: I\n"
    .string "will give unto this last, even as\l"
    .string "unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_15::
    .string "Is it not lawful for me to do what\n"
    .string "I will with mine own? Is thine eye\l"
    .string "evil, because I am good?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_16::
    .string "So the last shall be first, and\n"
    .string "the first last: for many be called,\l"
    .string "but few chosen$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_17::
    .string "And Jesus going up to Jerusalem\n"
    .string "took the twelve disciples apart in\l"
    .string "the way, and said unto them,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_18::
    .string "Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and\n"
    .string "the Son of man shall be betrayed\l"
    .string "unto the chief priests and unto the\l"
    .string "scribes, and they shall condemn him\l"
    .string "to death,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_19::
    .string "And shall deliver him to the\n"
    .string "Gentiles to mock, and to scourge,\l"
    .string "and to crucify him: and the third day\l"
    .string "he shall rise again$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_20::
    .string "Then came to him the mother of\n"
    .string "Zebedee’s children with her sons,\l"
    .string "worshipping him, and desiring a\l"
    .string "certain thing of him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_21::
    .string "And he said unto her, What wilt\n"
    .string "thou? She saith unto him, Grant that\l"
    .string "these my two sons may sit, the one on\l"
    .string "thy right hand, and the other on the\l"
    .string "left, in thy kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_22::
    .string "But Jesus answered and said, Ye know\n"
    .string "not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink\l"
    .string "of the cup that I shall drink of,\l"
    .string "and to be baptized with the baptism\l"
    .string "that I am baptized with? They say\l"
    .string "unto him, We are able.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_23::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Ye shall\n"
    .string "drink indeed of my cup, and be\l"
    .string "baptized with the baptism that I am\l"
    .string "baptized with: but to sit on my right\l"
    .string "hand, and on my left, is not mine to\l"
    .string "give, but it shall be given to them\l"
    .string "for whom it is prepared of my Father.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_24::
    .string "And when the ten heard it, they were\n"
    .string "moved with indignation against the\l"
    .string "two brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_25::
    .string "But Jesus called them unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, Ye know that the princes of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles exercise dominion over\l"
    .string "them, and they that are great\l"
    .string "exercise authority upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_26::
    .string "But it shall not be so among you:\n"
    .string "but whosoever will be great among\l"
    .string "you, let him be your minister;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_27::
    .string "And whosoever will be chief among\n"
    .string "you, let him be your servant:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_28::
    .string "Even as the Son of man came not to be\n"
    .string "ministered unto, but to minister, and\l"
    .string "to give his life a ransom for many$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_29::
    .string "And as they departed from Jericho,\n"
    .string "a great multitude followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_30::
    .string "And, behold, two blind men sitting\n"
    .string "by the way side, when they heard that\l"
    .string "Jesus passed by, cried out, saying,\l"
    .string "Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou son of\l"
    .string "David.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_31::
    .string "And the multitude rebuked them,\n"
    .string "because they should hold their\l"
    .string "peace: but they cried the more,\l"
    .string "saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou\l"
    .string "son of David.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_32::
    .string "And Jesus stood still, and called\n"
    .string "them, and said, What will ye that I\l"
    .string "shall do unto you?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_33::
    .string "They say unto him, Lord, that our\n"
    .string "eyes may be opened$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_20_34::
    .string "So Jesus had compassion on them,\n"
    .string "and touched their eyes: and\l"
    .string "immediately their eyes received\l"
    .string "sight, and they followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_1::
    .string "And when they drew nigh unto\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, and were come to\l"
    .string "Bethphage, unto the mount of\l"
    .string "Olives, then sent Jesus two\l"
    .string "disciples,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_2::
    .string "Saying unto them, Go into the\n"
    .string "village over against you, and\l"
    .string "straightway ye shall find an ass\l"
    .string "tied, and a colt with her: loose\l"
    .string "them, and bring them unto me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_3::
    .string "And if any man say ought unto you, ye\n"
    .string "shall say, The Lord hath need of\l"
    .string "them; and straightway he will send\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_4::
    .string "All this was done, that it might be\n"
    .string "fulfilled which was spoken by the\l"
    .string "prophet, saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_5::
    .string "Tell ye the daughter of Sion,\n"
    .string "Behold, thy King cometh unto thee,\l"
    .string "meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a\l"
    .string "colt the foal of an ass$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_6::
    .string "And the disciples went, and did as\n"
    .string "Jesus commanded them,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_7::
    .string "And brought the ass, and the colt,\n"
    .string "and put on them their clothes, and\l"
    .string "they set him thereon$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_8::
    .string "And a very great multitude spread\n"
    .string "their garments in the way; others cut\l"
    .string "down branches from the trees, and\l"
    .string "strawed them in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_9::
    .string "And the multitudes that went\n"
    .string "before, and that followed, cried,\l"
    .string "saying, Hosanna to the son of David:\l"
    .string "Blessed is he that cometh in the\l"
    .string "name of the Lord; Hosanna in the\l"
    .string "highest.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_10::
    .string "And when he was come into\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, all the city was moved,\l"
    .string "saying, Who is this?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_11::
    .string "And the multitude said, This is\n"
    .string "Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of\l"
    .string "Galilee$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_12::
    .string "And Jesus went into the temple of\n"
    .string "God, and cast out all them that\l"
    .string "sold and bought in the temple, and\l"
    .string "overthrew the tables of the\l"
    .string "moneychangers, and the seats of them\l"
    .string "that sold doves,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_13::
    .string "And said unto them, It is written,\n"
    .string "My house shall be called the house\l"
    .string "of prayer; but ye have made it a den\l"
    .string "of thieves$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_14::
    .string "And the blind and the lame came to\n"
    .string "him in the temple; and he healed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_15::
    .string "And when the chief priests and\n"
    .string "scribes saw the wonderful things\l"
    .string "that he did, and the children crying\l"
    .string "in the temple, and saying, Hosanna\l"
    .string "to the son of David; they were sore\l"
    .string "displeased,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_16::
    .string "And said unto him, Hearest thou what\n"
    .string "these say? And Jesus saith unto them,\l"
    .string "Yea; have ye never read, Out of the\l"
    .string "mouth of babes and sucklings thou\l"
    .string "hast perfected praise?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_17::
    .string "And he left them, and went out of\n"
    .string "the city into Bethany; and he lodged\l"
    .string "there$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_18::
    .string "Now in the morning as he returned\n"
    .string "into the city, he hungered.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_19::
    .string "And when he saw a fig tree in the\n"
    .string "way, he came to it, and found nothing\l"
    .string "thereon, but leaves only, and said\l"
    .string "unto it, Let no fruit grow on thee\l"
    .string "henceforward for ever. And\l"
    .string "presently the fig tree withered away.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_20::
    .string "And when the disciples saw it, they\n"
    .string "marvelled, saying, How soon is the\l"
    .string "fig tree withered away!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_21::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Verily I say unto you, If ye have\l"
    .string "faith, and doubt not, ye shall not\l"
    .string "only do this which is done to the fig\l"
    .string "tree, but also if ye shall say unto\l"
    .string "this mountain, Be thou removed, and\l"
    .string "be thou cast into the sea; it shall\l"
    .string "be done$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_22::
    .string "And all things, whatsoever ye\n"
    .string "shall ask in prayer, believing, ye\l"
    .string "shall receive.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_23::
    .string "And when he was come into the\n"
    .string "temple, the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "elders of the people came unto him\l"
    .string "as he was teaching, and said, By what\l"
    .string "authority doest thou these things?\l"
    .string "and who gave thee this authority?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_24::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, I also will ask you one\l"
    .string "thing, which if ye tell me, I in\l"
    .string "like wise will tell you by what\l"
    .string "authority I do these things$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_25::
    .string "The baptism of John, whence was it?\n"
    .string "from heaven, or of men? And they\l"
    .string "reasoned with themselves, saying, If\l"
    .string "we shall say, From heaven; he will\l"
    .string "say unto us, Why did ye not then\l"
    .string "believe him?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_26::
    .string "But if we shall say, Of men; we\n"
    .string "fear the people; for all hold\l"
    .string "John as a prophet$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_27::
    .string "And they answered Jesus, and said,\n"
    .string "We cannot tell. And he said unto\l"
    .string "them, Neither tell I you by what\l"
    .string "authority I do these things.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_28::
    .string "But what think ye? A certain man had\n"
    .string "two sons; and he came to the first,\l"
    .string "and said, Son, go work to day in my\l"
    .string "vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_29::
    .string "He answered and said, I will not:\n"
    .string "but afterward he repented, and went.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_30::
    .string "And he came to the second, and said\n"
    .string "likewise. And he answered and said, I\l"
    .string "go, sir: and went not.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_31::
    .string "Whether of them twain did the will\n"
    .string "of his father? They say unto him, The\l"
    .string "first. Jesus saith unto them, Verily\l"
    .string "I say unto you, That the publicans\l"
    .string "and the harlots go into the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God before you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_32::
    .string "For John came unto you in the way of\n"
    .string "righteousness, and ye believed him\l"
    .string "not: but the publicans and the\l"
    .string "harlots believed him: and ye, when\l"
    .string "ye had seen it, repented not\l"
    .string "afterward, that ye might believe him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_33::
    .string "Hear another parable: There was a\n"
    .string "certain householder, which planted\l"
    .string "a vineyard, and hedged it round\l"
    .string "about, and digged a winepress in it,\l"
    .string "and built a tower, and let it out to\l"
    .string "husbandmen, and went into a far\l"
    .string "country:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_34::
    .string "And when the time of the fruit drew\n"
    .string "near, he sent his servants to the\l"
    .string "husbandmen, that they might receive\l"
    .string "the fruits of it$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_35::
    .string "And the husbandmen took his\n"
    .string "servants, and beat one, and killed\l"
    .string "another, and stoned another.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_36::
    .string "Again, he sent other servants more\n"
    .string "than the first: and they did unto\l"
    .string "them likewise.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_37::
    .string "But last of all he sent unto them\n"
    .string "his son, saying, They will\l"
    .string "reverence my son.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_38::
    .string "But when the husbandmen saw the son,\n"
    .string "they said among themselves, This is\l"
    .string "the heir; come, let us kill him, and\l"
    .string "let us seize on his inheritance.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_39::
    .string "And they caught him, and cast him\n"
    .string "out of the vineyard, and slew him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_40::
    .string "When the lord therefore of the\n"
    .string "vineyard cometh, what will he do\l"
    .string "unto those husbandmen?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_41::
    .string "They say unto him, He will\n"
    .string "miserably destroy those wicked men,\l"
    .string "and will let out his vineyard unto\l"
    .string "other husbandmen, which shall\l"
    .string "render him the fruits in their\l"
    .string "seasons$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_42::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, Did ye never\n"
    .string "read in the scriptures, The stone\l"
    .string "which the builders rejected, the\l"
    .string "same is become the head of the\l"
    .string "corner: this is the Lord’s doing, and\l"
    .string "it is marvellous in our eyes?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_43::
    .string "Therefore say I unto you, The\n"
    .string "kingdom of God shall be taken from\l"
    .string "you, and given to a nation bringing\l"
    .string "forth the fruits thereof$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_44::
    .string "And whosoever shall fall on this\n"
    .string "stone shall be broken: but on\l"
    .string "whomsoever it shall fall, it will\l"
    .string "grind him to powder.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_45::
    .string "And when the chief priests and\n"
    .string "Pharisees had heard his parables,\l"
    .string "they perceived that he spake of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_21_46::
    .string "But when they sought to lay hands\n"
    .string "on him, they feared the multitude,\l"
    .string "because they took him for a prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_1::
    .string "And Jesus answered and spake unto\n"
    .string "them again by parables, and said,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_2::
    .string "The kingdom of heaven is like unto\n"
    .string "a certain king, which made a marriage\l"
    .string "for his son,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_3::
    .string "And sent forth his servants to\n"
    .string "call them that were bidden to the\l"
    .string "wedding: and they would not come$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_4::
    .string "Again, he sent forth other servants,\n"
    .string "saying, Tell them which are bidden,\l"
    .string "Behold, I have prepared my dinner:\l"
    .string "my oxen and my fatlings are killed,\l"
    .string "and all things are ready: come unto\l"
    .string "the marriage.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_5::
    .string "But they made light of it, and went\n"
    .string "their ways, one to his farm, another\l"
    .string "to his merchandise:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_6::
    .string "And the remnant took his servants,\n"
    .string "and entreated them spitefully, and\l"
    .string "slew them$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_7::
    .string "But when the king heard thereof, he\n"
    .string "was wroth: and he sent forth his\l"
    .string "armies, and destroyed those\l"
    .string "murderers, and burned up their city.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_8::
    .string "Then saith he to his servants, The\n"
    .string "wedding is ready, but they which were\l"
    .string "bidden were not worthy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_9::
    .string "Go ye therefore into the highways,\n"
    .string "and as many as ye shall find, bid to\l"
    .string "the marriage.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_10::
    .string "So those servants went out into the\n"
    .string "highways, and gathered together all\l"
    .string "as many as they found, both bad and\l"
    .string "good: and the wedding was furnished\l"
    .string "with guests.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_11::
    .string "And when the king came in to see the\n"
    .string "guests, he saw there a man which had\l"
    .string "not on a wedding garment:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_12::
    .string "And he saith unto him, Friend, how\n"
    .string "camest thou in hither not having a\l"
    .string "wedding garment? And he was\l"
    .string "speechless$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_13::
    .string "Then said the king to the servants,\n"
    .string "Bind him hand and foot, and take him\l"
    .string "away, and cast him into outer\l"
    .string "darkness, there shall be weeping\l"
    .string "and gnashing of teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_14::
    .string "For many are called, but few are\n"
    .string "chosen.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_15::
    .string "Then went the Pharisees, and took\n"
    .string "counsel how they might entangle him\l"
    .string "in his talk.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_16::
    .string "And they sent out unto him their\n"
    .string "disciples with the Herodians,\l"
    .string "saying, Master, we know that thou art\l"
    .string "true, and teachest the way of God in\l"
    .string "truth, neither carest thou for any\l"
    .string "man: for thou regardest not the\l"
    .string "person of men.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_17::
    .string "Tell us therefore, What thinkest\n"
    .string "thou? Is it lawful to give tribute\l"
    .string "unto Caesar, or not?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_18::
    .string "But Jesus perceived their\n"
    .string "wickedness, and said, Why tempt ye\l"
    .string "me, ye hypocrites?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_19::
    .string "Shew me the tribute money. And they\n"
    .string "brought unto him a penny$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_20::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Whose is\n"
    .string "this image and superscription?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_21::
    .string "They say unto him, Caesar’s. Then\n"
    .string "saith he unto them, Render therefore\l"
    .string "unto Caesar the things which are\l"
    .string "Caesar’s; and unto God the things\l"
    .string "that are God’s$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_22::
    .string "When they had heard these words,\n"
    .string "they marvelled, and left him, and\l"
    .string "went their way.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_23::
    .string "The same day came to him the\n"
    .string "Sadducees, which say that there is no\l"
    .string "resurrection, and asked him,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_24::
    .string "Saying, Master, Moses said, If a man\n"
    .string "die, having no children, his brother\l"
    .string "shall marry his wife, and raise up\l"
    .string "seed unto his brother$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_25::
    .string "Now there were with us seven\n"
    .string "brethren: and the first, when he had\l"
    .string "married a wife, deceased, and, having\l"
    .string "no issue, left his wife unto his\l"
    .string "brother:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_26::
    .string "Likewise the second also, and the\n"
    .string "third, unto the seventh$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_27::
    .string "And last of all the woman died\n"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_28::
    .string "Therefore in the resurrection whose\n"
    .string "wife shall she be of the seven? for\l"
    .string "they all had her.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_29::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Ye do err, not knowing the\l"
    .string "scriptures, nor the power of God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_30::
    .string "For in the resurrection they\n"
    .string "neither marry, nor are given in\l"
    .string "marriage, but are as the angels of\l"
    .string "God in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_31::
    .string "But as touching the resurrection of\n"
    .string "the dead, have ye not read that which\l"
    .string "was spoken unto you by God, saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_32::
    .string "I am the God of Abraham, and the God\n"
    .string "of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is\l"
    .string "not the God of the dead, but of the\l"
    .string "living$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_33::
    .string "And when the multitude heard this,\n"
    .string "they were astonished at his doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_34::
    .string "But when the Pharisees had heard\n"
    .string "that he had put the Sadducees to\l"
    .string "silence, they were gathered\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_35::
    .string "Then one of them, which was a\n"
    .string "lawyer, asked him a question,\l"
    .string "tempting him, and saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_36::
    .string "Master, which is the great\n"
    .string "commandment in the law?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_37::
    .string "Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "love the Lord thy God with all thy\l"
    .string "heart, and with all thy soul, and\l"
    .string "with all thy mind$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_38::
    .string "This is the first and great\n"
    .string "commandment.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_39::
    .string "And the second is like unto it, Thou\n"
    .string "shalt love thy neighbour as\l"
    .string "thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_40::
    .string "On these two commandments hang all\n"
    .string "the law and the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_41::
    .string "While the Pharisees were gathered\n"
    .string "together, Jesus asked them,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_42::
    .string "Saying, What think ye of Christ?\n"
    .string "whose son is he? They say unto him,\l"
    .string "The son of David$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_43::
    .string "He saith unto them, How then doth\n"
    .string "David in spirit call him Lord,\l"
    .string "saying,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_44::
    .string "The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou\n"
    .string "on my right hand, till I make thine\l"
    .string "enemies thy footstool?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_45::
    .string "If David then call him Lord, how is\n"
    .string "he his son?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_22_46::
    .string "And no man was able to answer him a\n"
    .string "word, neither durst any man from that\l"
    .string "day forth ask him any more questions$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_1::
    .string "Then spake Jesus to the multitude,\n"
    .string "and to his disciples,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_2::
    .string "Saying, The scribes and the\n"
    .string "Pharisees sit in Moses’ seat:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_3::
    .string "All therefore whatsoever they bid\n"
    .string "you observe, that observe and do; but\l"
    .string "do not ye after their works: for they\l"
    .string "say, and do not$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_4::
    .string "For they bind heavy burdens and\n"
    .string "grievous to be borne, and lay them on\l"
    .string "men’s shoulders; but they\l"
    .string "themselves will not move them with\l"
    .string "one of their fingers.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_5::
    .string "But all their works they do for to\n"
    .string "be seen of men: they make broad their\l"
    .string "phylacteries, and enlarge the\l"
    .string "borders of their garments,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_6::
    .string "And love the uppermost rooms at\n"
    .string "feasts, and the chief seats in the\l"
    .string "synagogues,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_7::
    .string "And greetings in the markets, and to\n"
    .string "be called of men, Rabbi, Rabbi$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_8::
    .string "But be not ye called Rabbi: for one\n"
    .string "is your Master, even Christ; and all\l"
    .string "ye are brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_9::
    .string "And call no man your father upon\n"
    .string "the earth: for one is your Father,\l"
    .string "which is in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_10::
    .string "Neither be ye called masters: for\n"
    .string "one is your Master, even Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_11::
    .string "But he that is greatest among you\n"
    .string "shall be your servant.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_12::
    .string "And whosoever shall exalt\n"
    .string "himself shall be abased; and he\l"
    .string "that shall humble himself shall\l"
    .string "be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_13::
    .string "But woe unto you, scribes and\n"
    .string "Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut\l"
    .string "up the kingdom of heaven against\l"
    .string "men: for ye neither go in\l"
    .string "yourselves, neither suffer ye them\l"
    .string "that are entering to go in.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_14::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye devour widows’\l"
    .string "houses, and for a pretence make long\l"
    .string "prayer: therefore ye shall receive\l"
    .string "the greater damnation.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_15::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye compass sea and\l"
    .string "land to make one proselyte, and when\l"
    .string "he is made, ye make him twofold more\l"
    .string "the child of hell than yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_16::
    .string "Woe unto you, ye blind guides,\n"
    .string "which say, Whosoever shall swear by\l"
    .string "the temple, it is nothing; but\l"
    .string "whosoever shall swear by the gold\l"
    .string "of the temple, he is a debtor!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_17::
    .string "Ye fools and blind: for whether is\n"
    .string "greater, the gold, or the temple\l"
    .string "that sanctifieth the gold?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_18::
    .string "And, Whosoever shall swear by the\n"
    .string "altar, it is nothing; but whosoever\l"
    .string "sweareth by the gift that is upon it,\l"
    .string "he is guilty$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_19::
    .string "Ye fools and blind: for whether is\n"
    .string "greater, the gift, or the altar that\l"
    .string "sanctifieth the gift?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_20::
    .string "Whoso therefore shall swear by the\n"
    .string "altar, sweareth by it, and by all\l"
    .string "things thereon$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_21::
    .string "And whoso shall swear by the\n"
    .string "temple, sweareth by it, and by him\l"
    .string "that dwelleth therein.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_22::
    .string "And he that shall swear by heaven,\n"
    .string "sweareth by the throne of God, and by\l"
    .string "him that sitteth thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_23::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint\l"
    .string "and anise and cummin, and have\l"
    .string "omitted the weightier matters of the\l"
    .string "law, judgment, mercy, and faith:\l"
    .string "these ought ye to have done, and not\l"
    .string "to leave the other undone.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_24::
    .string "Ye blind guides, which strain at a\n"
    .string "gnat, and swallow a camel.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_25::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye make clean the\l"
    .string "outside of the cup and of the\l"
    .string "platter, but within they are full\l"
    .string "of extortion and excess.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_26::
    .string "Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first\n"
    .string "that which is within the cup and\l"
    .string "platter, that the outside of them\l"
    .string "may be clean also.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_27::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye are like unto\l"
    .string "whited sepulchres, which indeed\l"
    .string "appear beautiful outward, but are\l"
    .string "within full of dead men’s bones, and\l"
    .string "of all uncleanness.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_28::
    .string "Even so ye also outwardly appear\n"
    .string "righteous unto men, but within ye are\l"
    .string "full of hypocrisy and iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_29::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! because ye build the\l"
    .string "tombs of the prophets, and garnish\l"
    .string "the sepulchres of the righteous,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_30::
    .string "And say, If we had been in the days\n"
    .string "of our fathers, we would not have\l"
    .string "been partakers with them in the\l"
    .string "blood of the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_31::
    .string "Wherefore ye be witnesses unto\n"
    .string "yourselves, that ye are the\l"
    .string "children of them which killed the\l"
    .string "prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_32::
    .string "Fill ye up then the measure of\n"
    .string "your fathers.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_33::
    .string "Ye serpents, ye generation of\n"
    .string "vipers, how can ye escape the\l"
    .string "damnation of hell?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_34::
    .string "Wherefore, behold, I send unto you\n"
    .string "prophets, and wise men, and scribes:\l"
    .string "and some of them ye shall kill and\l"
    .string "crucify; and some of them shall ye\l"
    .string "scourge in your synagogues, and\l"
    .string "persecute them from city to city:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_35::
    .string "That upon you may come all the\n"
    .string "righteous blood shed upon the\l"
    .string "earth, from the blood of righteous\l"
    .string "Abel unto the blood of Zacharias\l"
    .string "son of Barachias, whom ye slew\l"
    .string "between the temple and the altar$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_36::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, All these\n"
    .string "things shall come upon this\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_37::
    .string "O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that\n"
    .string "killest the prophets, and stonest\l"
    .string "them which are sent unto thee, how\l"
    .string "often would I have gathered thy\l"
    .string "children together, even as a hen\l"
    .string "gathereth her chickens under her\l"
    .string "wings, and ye would not!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_38::
    .string "Behold, your house is left unto you\n"
    .string "desolate$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_23_39::
    .string "For I say unto you, Ye shall not\n"
    .string "see me henceforth, till ye shall\l"
    .string "say, Blessed is he that cometh in the\l"
    .string "name of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_1::
    .string "And Jesus went out, and departed\n"
    .string "from the temple: and his disciples\l"
    .string "came to him for to shew him the\l"
    .string "buildings of the temple.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_2::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, See ye not\n"
    .string "all these things? verily I say unto\l"
    .string "you, There shall not be left here\l"
    .string "one stone upon another, that shall\l"
    .string "not be thrown down.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_3::
    .string "And as he sat upon the mount of\n"
    .string "Olives, the disciples came unto him\l"
    .string "privately, saying, Tell us, when\l"
    .string "shall these things be? and what\l"
    .string "shall be the sign of thy coming, and\l"
    .string "of the end of the world?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_4::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, Take heed that no man deceive\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_5::
    .string "For many shall come in my name,\n"
    .string "saying, I am Christ; and shall\l"
    .string "deceive many.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_6::
    .string "And ye shall hear of wars and\n"
    .string "rumours of wars: see that ye be not\l"
    .string "troubled: for all these things must\l"
    .string "come to pass, but the end is not yet.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_7::
    .string "For nation shall rise against\n"
    .string "nation, and kingdom against kingdom:\l"
    .string "and there shall be famines, and\l"
    .string "pestilences, and earthquakes, in\l"
    .string "divers places.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_8::
    .string "All these are the beginning of\n"
    .string "sorrows.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_9::
    .string "Then shall they deliver you up to\n"
    .string "be afflicted, and shall kill you:\l"
    .string "and ye shall be hated of all\l"
    .string "nations for my name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_10::
    .string "And then shall many be offended,\n"
    .string "and shall betray one another, and\l"
    .string "shall hate one another.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_11::
    .string "And many false prophets shall\n"
    .string "rise, and shall deceive many.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_12::
    .string "And because iniquity shall abound,\n"
    .string "the love of many shall wax cold.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_13::
    .string "But he that shall endure unto the\n"
    .string "end, the same shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_14::
    .string "And this gospel of the kingdom\n"
    .string "shall be preached in all the\l"
    .string "world for a witness unto all\l"
    .string "nations; and then shall the end\l"
    .string "come.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_15::
    .string "When ye therefore shall see the\n"
    .string "abomination of desolation, spoken\l"
    .string "of by Daniel the prophet, stand in\l"
    .string "the holy place, (whoso readeth,\l"
    .string "let him understand:)"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_16::
    .string "Then let them which be in Judaea\n"
    .string "flee into the mountains:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_17::
    .string "Let him which is on the housetop\n"
    .string "not come down to take any thing out\l"
    .string "of his house:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_18::
    .string "Neither let him which is in the\n"
    .string "field return back to take his\l"
    .string "clothes$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_19::
    .string "And woe unto them that are with\n"
    .string "child, and to them that give suck in\l"
    .string "those days!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_20::
    .string "But pray ye that your flight be not\n"
    .string "in the winter, neither on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_21::
    .string "For then shall be great\n"
    .string "tribulation, such as was not since\l"
    .string "the beginning of the world to this\l"
    .string "time, no, nor ever shall be$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_22::
    .string "And except those days should be\n"
    .string "shortened, there should no flesh be\l"
    .string "saved: but for the elect’s sake\l"
    .string "those days shall be shortened.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_23::
    .string "Then if any man shall say unto you,\n"
    .string "Lo, here is Christ, or there; believe\l"
    .string "it not.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_24::
    .string "For there shall arise false\n"
    .string "Christs, and false prophets, and\l"
    .string "shall shew great signs and wonders;\l"
    .string "insomuch that, if it were possible,\l"
    .string "they shall deceive the very elect.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_25::
    .string "Behold, I have told you before.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_26::
    .string "Wherefore if they shall say unto\n"
    .string "you, Behold, he is in the desert; go\l"
    .string "not forth: behold, he is in the\l"
    .string "secret chambers; believe it not.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_27::
    .string "For as the lightning cometh out of\n"
    .string "the east, and shineth even unto the\l"
    .string "west; so shall also the coming of\l"
    .string "the Son of man be.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_28::
    .string "For wheresoever the carcase is,\n"
    .string "there will the eagles be gathered\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_29::
    .string "Immediately after the tribulation\n"
    .string "of those days shall the sun be\l"
    .string "darkened, and the moon shall not\l"
    .string "give her light, and the stars shall\l"
    .string "fall from heaven, and the powers of\l"
    .string "the heavens shall be shaken:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_30::
    .string "And then shall appear the sign of\n"
    .string "the Son of man in heaven: and then\l"
    .string "shall all the tribes of the earth\l"
    .string "mourn, and they shall see the Son of\l"
    .string "man coming in the clouds of heaven\l"
    .string "with power and great glory$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_31::
    .string "And he shall send his angels with\n"
    .string "a great sound of a trumpet, and they\l"
    .string "shall gather together his elect\l"
    .string "from the four winds, from one end of\l"
    .string "heaven to the other.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_32::
    .string "Now learn a parable of the fig\n"
    .string "tree; When his branch is yet tender,\l"
    .string "and putteth forth leaves, ye know\l"
    .string "that summer is nigh:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_33::
    .string "So likewise ye, when ye shall see\n"
    .string "all these things, know that it is\l"
    .string "near, even at the doors$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_34::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, This\n"
    .string "generation shall not pass, till\l"
    .string "all these things be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_35::
    .string "Heaven and earth shall pass away,\n"
    .string "but my words shall not pass away.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_36::
    .string "But of that day and hour knoweth no\n"
    .string "man, no, not the angels of heaven,\l"
    .string "but my Father only.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_37::
    .string "But as the days of Noe were, so\n"
    .string "shall also the coming of the Son of\l"
    .string "man be.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_38::
    .string "For as in the days that were before\n"
    .string "the flood they were eating and\l"
    .string "drinking, marrying and giving in\l"
    .string "marriage, until the day that Noe\l"
    .string "entered into the ark,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_39::
    .string "And knew not until the flood came,\n"
    .string "and took them all away; so shall\l"
    .string "also the coming of the Son of man be$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_40::
    .string "Then shall two be in the field;\n"
    .string "the one shall be taken, and the\l"
    .string "other left.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_41::
    .string "Two women shall be grinding at the\n"
    .string "mill; the one shall be taken, and\l"
    .string "the other left.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_42::
    .string "Watch therefore: for ye know not\n"
    .string "what hour your Lord doth come.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_43::
    .string "But know this, that if the goodman\n"
    .string "of the house had known in what watch\l"
    .string "the thief would come, he would have\l"
    .string "watched, and would not have suffered\l"
    .string "his house to be broken up.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_44::
    .string "Therefore be ye also ready: for in\n"
    .string "such an hour as ye think not the Son\l"
    .string "of man cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_45::
    .string "Who then is a faithful and wise\n"
    .string "servant, whom his lord hath made\l"
    .string "ruler over his household, to give\l"
    .string "them meat in due season?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_46::
    .string "Blessed is that servant, whom his\n"
    .string "lord when he cometh shall find so\l"
    .string "doing$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_47::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, That he\n"
    .string "shall make him ruler over all his\l"
    .string "goods.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_48::
    .string "But and if that evil servant shall\n"
    .string "say in his heart, My lord delayeth\l"
    .string "his coming;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_49::
    .string "And shall begin to smite his\n"
    .string "fellowservants, and to eat and\l"
    .string "drink with the drunken;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_50::
    .string "The lord of that servant shall\n"
    .string "come in a day when he looketh not for\l"
    .string "him, and in an hour that he is not\l"
    .string "aware of,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_24_51::
    .string "And shall cut him asunder, and\n"
    .string "appoint him his portion with the\l"
    .string "hypocrites: there shall be weeping\l"
    .string "and gnashing of teeth$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_1::
    .string "Then shall the kingdom of heaven\n"
    .string "be likened unto ten virgins, which\l"
    .string "took their lamps, and went forth to\l"
    .string "meet the bridegroom.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_2::
    .string "And five of them were wise, and five\n"
    .string "were foolish.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_3::
    .string "They that were foolish took their\n"
    .string "lamps, and took no oil with them:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_4::
    .string "But the wise took oil in their\n"
    .string "vessels with their lamps$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_5::
    .string "While the bridegroom tarried, they\n"
    .string "all slumbered and slept.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_6::
    .string "And at midnight there was a cry\n"
    .string "made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh;\l"
    .string "go ye out to meet him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_7::
    .string "Then all those virgins arose, and\n"
    .string "trimmed their lamps.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_8::
    .string "And the foolish said unto the wise,\n"
    .string "Give us of your oil; for our lamps\l"
    .string "are gone out.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_9::
    .string "But the wise answered, saying, Not\n"
    .string "so; lest there be not enough for us\l"
    .string "and you: but go ye rather to them that\l"
    .string "sell, and buy for yourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_10::
    .string "And while they went to buy, the\n"
    .string "bridegroom came; and they that were\l"
    .string "ready went in with him to the\l"
    .string "marriage: and the door was shut.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_11::
    .string "Afterward came also the other\n"
    .string "virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_12::
    .string "But he answered and said, Verily I\n"
    .string "say unto you, I know you not.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_13::
    .string "Watch therefore, for ye know neither\n"
    .string "the day nor the hour wherein the Son\l"
    .string "of man cometh.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_14::
    .string "For the kingdom of heaven is as a\n"
    .string "man travelling into a far country,\l"
    .string "who called his own servants, and\l"
    .string "delivered unto them his goods.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_15::
    .string "And unto one he gave five talents,\n"
    .string "to another two, and to another one;\l"
    .string "to every man according to his\l"
    .string "several ability; and straightway\l"
    .string "took his journey.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_16::
    .string "Then he that had received the five\n"
    .string "talents went and traded with the\l"
    .string "same, and made them other five\l"
    .string "talents.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_17::
    .string "And likewise he that had received\n"
    .string "two, he also gained other two.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_18::
    .string "But he that had received one went\n"
    .string "and digged in the earth, and hid his\l"
    .string "lord’s money.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_19::
    .string "After a long time the lord of those\n"
    .string "servants cometh, and reckoneth with\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_20::
    .string "And so he that had received five\n"
    .string "talents came and brought other five\l"
    .string "talents, saying, Lord, thou\l"
    .string "deliveredst unto me five talents:\l"
    .string "behold, I have gained beside them\l"
    .string "five talents more.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_21::
    .string "His lord said unto him, Well done,\n"
    .string "thou good and faithful servant: thou\l"
    .string "hast been faithful over a few\l"
    .string "things, I will make thee ruler over\l"
    .string "many things: enter thou into the joy\l"
    .string "of thy lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_22::
    .string "He also that had received two\n"
    .string "talents came and said, Lord, thou\l"
    .string "deliveredst unto me two talents:\l"
    .string "behold, I have gained two other\l"
    .string "talents beside them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_23::
    .string "His lord said unto him, Well done,\n"
    .string "good and faithful servant; thou hast\l"
    .string "been faithful over a few things, I\l"
    .string "will make thee ruler over many\l"
    .string "things: enter thou into the joy of\l"
    .string "thy lord.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_24::
    .string "Then he which had received the one\n"
    .string "talent came and said, Lord, I knew\l"
    .string "thee that thou art an hard man,\l"
    .string "reaping where thou hast not sown,\l"
    .string "and gathering where thou hast not\l"
    .string "strawed:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_25::
    .string "And I was afraid, and went and hid\n"
    .string "thy talent in the earth: lo, there\l"
    .string "thou hast that is thine$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_26::
    .string "His lord answered and said unto\n"
    .string "him, Thou wicked and slothful\l"
    .string "servant, thou knewest that I reap\l"
    .string "where I sowed not, and gather where I\l"
    .string "have not strawed:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_27::
    .string "Thou oughtest therefore to have put\n"
    .string "my money to the exchangers, and then\l"
    .string "at my coming I should have received\l"
    .string "mine own with usury$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_28::
    .string "Take therefore the talent from him,\n"
    .string "and give it unto him which hath ten\l"
    .string "talents.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_29::
    .string "For unto every one that hath shall\n"
    .string "be given, and he shall have\l"
    .string "abundance: but from him that hath not\l"
    .string "shall be taken away even that which\l"
    .string "he hath.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_30::
    .string "And cast ye the unprofitable\n"
    .string "servant into outer darkness: there\l"
    .string "shall be weeping and gnashing of\l"
    .string "teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_31::
    .string "When the Son of man shall come in\n"
    .string "his glory, and all the holy angels\l"
    .string "with him, then shall he sit upon\l"
    .string "the throne of his glory:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_32::
    .string "And before him shall be gathered\n"
    .string "all nations: and he shall\l"
    .string "separate them one from another, as a\l"
    .string "shepherd divideth his sheep from\l"
    .string "the goats:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_33::
    .string "And he shall set the sheep on his\n"
    .string "right hand, but the goats on the left$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_34::
    .string "Then shall the King say unto them\n"
    .string "on his right hand, Come, ye blessed\l"
    .string "of my Father, inherit the kingdom\l"
    .string "prepared for you from the foundation\l"
    .string "of the world:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_35::
    .string "For I was an hungred, and ye gave me\n"
    .string "meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me\l"
    .string "drink: I was a stranger, and ye took\l"
    .string "me in:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_36::
    .string "Naked, and ye clothed me: I was\n"
    .string "sick, and ye visited me: I was in\l"
    .string "prison, and ye came unto me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_37::
    .string "Then shall the righteous answer\n"
    .string "him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an\l"
    .string "hungred, and fed thee? or thirsty,\l"
    .string "and gave thee drink?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_38::
    .string "When saw we thee a stranger, and\n"
    .string "took thee in? or naked, and clothed\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_39::
    .string "Or when saw we thee sick, or in\n"
    .string "prison, and came unto thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_40::
    .string "And the King shall answer and say\n"
    .string "unto them, Verily I say unto you,\l"
    .string "Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one\l"
    .string "of the least of these my brethren, ye\l"
    .string "have done it unto me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_41::
    .string "Then shall he say also unto them\n"
    .string "on the left hand, Depart from me, ye\l"
    .string "cursed, into everlasting fire,\l"
    .string "prepared for the devil and his\l"
    .string "angels:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_42::
    .string "For I was an hungred, and ye gave me\n"
    .string "no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me\l"
    .string "no drink:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_43::
    .string "I was a stranger, and ye took me not\n"
    .string "in: naked, and ye clothed me not:\l"
    .string "sick, and in prison, and ye visited\l"
    .string "me not$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_44::
    .string "Then shall they also answer him,\n"
    .string "saying, Lord, when saw we thee an\l"
    .string "hungred, or athirst, or a stranger,\l"
    .string "or naked, or sick, or in prison, and\l"
    .string "did not minister unto thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_45::
    .string "Then shall he answer them, saying,\n"
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye\l"
    .string "did it not to one of the least of\l"
    .string "these, ye did it not to me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_25_46::
    .string "And these shall go away into\n"
    .string "everlasting punishment: but the\l"
    .string "righteous into life eternal.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, when Jesus had\n"
    .string "finished all these sayings, he said\l"
    .string "unto his disciples,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_2::
    .string "Ye know that after two days is the\n"
    .string "feast of the passover, and the Son of\l"
    .string "man is betrayed to be crucified$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_3::
    .string "Then assembled together the chief\n"
    .string "priests, and the scribes, and the\l"
    .string "elders of the people, unto the\l"
    .string "palace of the high priest, who was\l"
    .string "called Caiaphas,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_4::
    .string "And consulted that they might take\n"
    .string "Jesus by subtilty, and kill him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_5::
    .string "But they said, Not on the feast day,\n"
    .string "lest there be an uproar among the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_6::
    .string "Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in\n"
    .string "the house of Simon the leper,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_7::
    .string "There came unto him a woman having\n"
    .string "an alabaster box of very precious\l"
    .string "ointment, and poured it on his head,\l"
    .string "as he sat at meat$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_8::
    .string "But when his disciples saw it, they\n"
    .string "had indignation, saying, To what\l"
    .string "purpose is this waste?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_9::
    .string "For this ointment might have been\n"
    .string "sold for much, and given to the poor$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_10::
    .string "When Jesus understood it, he said\n"
    .string "unto them, Why trouble ye the woman?\l"
    .string "for she hath wrought a good work\l"
    .string "upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_11::
    .string "For ye have the poor always with\n"
    .string "you; but me ye have not always.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_12::
    .string "For in that she hath poured this\n"
    .string "ointment on my body, she did it for my\l"
    .string "burial.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_13::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever\n"
    .string "this gospel shall be preached in\l"
    .string "the whole world, there shall also\l"
    .string "this, that this woman hath done, be\l"
    .string "told for a memorial of her.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_14::
    .string "Then one of the twelve, called\n"
    .string "Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief\l"
    .string "priests,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_15::
    .string "And said unto them, What will ye\n"
    .string "give me, and I will deliver him\l"
    .string "unto you? And they covenanted with\l"
    .string "him for thirty pieces of silver$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_16::
    .string "And from that time he sought\n"
    .string "opportunity to betray him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_17::
    .string "Now the first day of the feast of\n"
    .string "unleavened bread the disciples\l"
    .string "came to Jesus, saying unto him, Where\l"
    .string "wilt thou that we prepare for thee\l"
    .string "to eat the passover?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_18::
    .string "And he said, Go into the city to such\n"
    .string "a man, and say unto him, The Master\l"
    .string "saith, My time is at hand; I will\l"
    .string "keep the passover at thy house with\l"
    .string "my disciples$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_19::
    .string "And the disciples did as Jesus had\n"
    .string "appointed them; and they made ready\l"
    .string "the passover.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_20::
    .string "Now when the even was come, he sat\n"
    .string "down with the twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_21::
    .string "And as they did eat, he said, Verily\n"
    .string "I say unto you, that one of you\l"
    .string "shall betray me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_22::
    .string "And they were exceeding sorrowful,\n"
    .string "and began every one of them to say\l"
    .string "unto him, Lord, is it I?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_23::
    .string "And he answered and said, He that\n"
    .string "dippeth his hand with me in the\l"
    .string "dish, the same shall betray me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_24::
    .string "The Son of man goeth as it is\n"
    .string "written of him: but woe unto that man\l"
    .string "by whom the Son of man is betrayed! it\l"
    .string "had been good for that man if he had\l"
    .string "not been born.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_25::
    .string "Then Judas, which betrayed him,\n"
    .string "answered and said, Master, is it I? He\l"
    .string "said unto him, Thou hast said.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_26::
    .string "And as they were eating, Jesus took\n"
    .string "bread, and blessed it, and brake it,\l"
    .string "and gave it to the disciples, and\l"
    .string "said, Take, eat; this is my body.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_27::
    .string "And he took the cup, and gave\n"
    .string "thanks, and gave it to them, saying,\l"
    .string "Drink ye all of it;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_28::
    .string "For this is my blood of the new\n"
    .string "testament, which is shed for many for\l"
    .string "the remission of sins$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_29::
    .string "But I say unto you, I will not\n"
    .string "drink henceforth of this fruit of the\l"
    .string "vine, until that day when I drink it\l"
    .string "new with you in my Father’s kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_30::
    .string "And when they had sung an hymn, they\n"
    .string "went out into the mount of Olives.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_31::
    .string "Then saith Jesus unto them, All ye\n"
    .string "shall be offended because of me\l"
    .string "this night: for it is written, I\l"
    .string "will smite the shepherd, and the\l"
    .string "sheep of the flock shall be\l"
    .string "scattered abroad.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_32::
    .string "But after I am risen again, I will\n"
    .string "go before you into Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_33::
    .string "Peter answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Though all men shall be offended\l"
    .string "because of thee, yet will I never be\l"
    .string "offended.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_34::
    .string "Jesus said unto him, Verily I say\n"
    .string "unto thee, That this night, before\l"
    .string "the cock crow, thou shalt deny me\l"
    .string "thrice.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_35::
    .string "Peter said unto him, Though I\n"
    .string "should die with thee, yet will I\l"
    .string "not deny thee. Likewise also said\l"
    .string "all the disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_36::
    .string "Then cometh Jesus with them unto a\n"
    .string "place called Gethsemane, and saith\l"
    .string "unto the disciples, Sit ye here,\l"
    .string "while I go and pray yonder.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_37::
    .string "And he took with him Peter and the\n"
    .string "two sons of Zebedee, and began to be\l"
    .string "sorrowful and very heavy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_38::
    .string "Then saith he unto them, My soul is\n"
    .string "exceeding sorrowful, even unto\l"
    .string "death: tarry ye here, and watch with\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_39::
    .string "And he went a little farther, and\n"
    .string "fell on his face, and prayed,\l"
    .string "saying, O my Father, if it be\l"
    .string "possible, let this cup pass from\l"
    .string "me: nevertheless not as I will, but\l"
    .string "as thou wilt.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_40::
    .string "And he cometh unto the disciples,\n"
    .string "and findeth them asleep, and saith\l"
    .string "unto Peter, What, could ye not watch\l"
    .string "with me one hour?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_41::
    .string "Watch and pray, that ye enter not\n"
    .string "into temptation: the spirit indeed\l"
    .string "is willing, but the flesh is weak$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_42::
    .string "He went away again the second time,\n"
    .string "and prayed, saying, O my Father, if\l"
    .string "this cup may not pass away from me,\l"
    .string "except I drink it, thy will be done.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_43::
    .string "And he came and found them asleep\n"
    .string "again: for their eyes were heavy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_44::
    .string "And he left them, and went away\n"
    .string "again, and prayed the third time,\l"
    .string "saying the same words.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_45::
    .string "Then cometh he to his disciples,\n"
    .string "and saith unto them, Sleep on now,\l"
    .string "and take your rest: behold, the hour\l"
    .string "is at hand, and the Son of man is\l"
    .string "betrayed into the hands of sinners.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_46::
    .string "Rise, let us be going: behold, he\n"
    .string "is at hand that doth betray me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_47::
    .string "And while he yet spake, lo, Judas,\n"
    .string "one of the twelve, came, and with him\l"
    .string "a great multitude with swords and\l"
    .string "staves, from the chief priests and\l"
    .string "elders of the people.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_48::
    .string "Now he that betrayed him gave them a\n"
    .string "sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall\l"
    .string "kiss, that same is he: hold him fast.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_49::
    .string "And forthwith he came to Jesus, and\n"
    .string "said, Hail, master; and kissed him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_50::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Friend,\n"
    .string "wherefore art thou come? Then came\l"
    .string "they, and laid hands on Jesus and\l"
    .string "took him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_51::
    .string "And, behold, one of them which were\n"
    .string "with Jesus stretched out his hand,\l"
    .string "and drew his sword, and struck a\l"
    .string "servant of the high priest’s, and\l"
    .string "smote off his ear.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_52::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto him, Put up\n"
    .string "again thy sword into his place: for\l"
    .string "all they that take the sword shall\l"
    .string "perish with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_53::
    .string "Thinkest thou that I cannot now\n"
    .string "pray to my Father, and he shall\l"
    .string "presently give me more than twelve\l"
    .string "legions of angels?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_54::
    .string "But how then shall the scriptures\n"
    .string "be fulfilled, that thus it must be?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_55::
    .string "In that same hour said Jesus to the\n"
    .string "multitudes, Are ye come out as\l"
    .string "against a thief with swords and\l"
    .string "staves for to take me? I sat daily\l"
    .string "with you teaching in the temple, and\l"
    .string "ye laid no hold on me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_56::
    .string "But all this was done, that the\n"
    .string "scriptures of the prophets might\l"
    .string "be fulfilled. Then all the\l"
    .string "disciples forsook him, and fled.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_57::
    .string "And they that had laid hold on\n"
    .string "Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the\l"
    .string "high priest, where the scribes and\l"
    .string "the elders were assembled.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_58::
    .string "But Peter followed him afar off\n"
    .string "unto the high priest’s palace, and\l"
    .string "went in, and sat with the servants,\l"
    .string "to see the end.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_59::
    .string "Now the chief priests, and elders,\n"
    .string "and all the council, sought false\l"
    .string "witness against Jesus, to put him to\l"
    .string "death;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_60::
    .string "But found none: yea, though many\n"
    .string "false witnesses came, yet found they\l"
    .string "none. At the last came two false\l"
    .string "witnesses,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_61::
    .string "And said, This fellow said, I am\n"
    .string "able to destroy the temple of God,\l"
    .string "and to build it in three days$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_62::
    .string "And the high priest arose, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Answerest thou nothing?\l"
    .string "what is it which these witness\l"
    .string "against thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_63::
    .string "But Jesus held his peace, And the\n"
    .string "high priest answered and said unto\l"
    .string "him, I adjure thee by the living God,\l"
    .string "that thou tell us whether thou be\l"
    .string "the Christ, the Son of God$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_64::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, Thou hast\n"
    .string "said: nevertheless I say unto you,\l"
    .string "Hereafter shall ye see the Son of\l"
    .string "man sitting on the right hand of\l"
    .string "power, and coming in the clouds of\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_65::
    .string "Then the high priest rent his\n"
    .string "clothes, saying, He hath spoken\l"
    .string "blasphemy; what further need have\l"
    .string "we of witnesses? behold, now ye have\l"
    .string "heard his blasphemy.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_66::
    .string "What think ye? They answered and\n"
    .string "said, He is guilty of death.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_67::
    .string "Then did they spit in his face, and\n"
    .string "buffeted him; and others smote him\l"
    .string "with the palms of their hands,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_68::
    .string "Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou\n"
    .string "Christ, Who is he that smote thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_69::
    .string "Now Peter sat without in the\n"
    .string "palace: and a damsel came unto him,\l"
    .string "saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of\l"
    .string "Galilee$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_70::
    .string "But he denied before them all,\n"
    .string "saying, I know not what thou sayest.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_71::
    .string "And when he was gone out into the\n"
    .string "porch, another maid saw him, and said\l"
    .string "unto them that were there, This\l"
    .string "fellow was also with Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_72::
    .string "And again he denied with an oath, I\n"
    .string "do not know the man.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_73::
    .string "And after a while came unto him\n"
    .string "they that stood by, and said to\l"
    .string "Peter, Surely thou also art one of\l"
    .string "them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_74::
    .string "Then began he to curse and to swear,\n"
    .string "saying, I know not the man. And\l"
    .string "immediately the cock crew.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_26_75::
    .string "And Peter remembered the word of\n"
    .string "Jesus, which said unto him, Before\l"
    .string "the cock crow, thou shalt deny me\l"
    .string "thrice. And he went out, and wept\l"
    .string "bitterly.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_1::
    .string "When the morning was come, all the\n"
    .string "chief priests and elders of the\l"
    .string "people took counsel against Jesus\l"
    .string "to put him to death:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_2::
    .string "And when they had bound him, they\n"
    .string "led him away, and delivered him to\l"
    .string "Pontius Pilate the governor$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_3::
    .string "Then Judas, which had betrayed him,\n"
    .string "when he saw that he was condemned,\l"
    .string "repented himself, and brought again\l"
    .string "the thirty pieces of silver to the\l"
    .string "chief priests and elders,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_4::
    .string "Saying, I have sinned in that I have\n"
    .string "betrayed the innocent blood. And\l"
    .string "they said, What is that to us? see\l"
    .string "thou to that$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_5::
    .string "And he cast down the pieces of\n"
    .string "silver in the temple, and\l"
    .string "departed, and went and hanged\l"
    .string "himself.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_6::
    .string "And the chief priests took the\n"
    .string "silver pieces, and said, It is not\l"
    .string "lawful for to put them into the\l"
    .string "treasury, because it is the price of\l"
    .string "blood.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_7::
    .string "And they took counsel, and bought\n"
    .string "with them the potter’s field, to\l"
    .string "bury strangers in.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_8::
    .string "Wherefore that field was called,\n"
    .string "The field of blood, unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_9::
    .string "Then was fulfilled that which was\n"
    .string "spoken by Jeremy the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying, And they took the thirty\l"
    .string "pieces of silver, the price of him\l"
    .string "that was valued, whom they of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel did value;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_10::
    .string "And gave them for the potter’s\n"
    .string "field, as the Lord appointed me$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_11::
    .string "And Jesus stood before the governor:\n"
    .string "and the governor asked him, saying,\l"
    .string "Art thou the King of the Jews? And\l"
    .string "Jesus said unto him, Thou sayest.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_12::
    .string "And when he was accused of the chief\n"
    .string "priests and elders, he answered\l"
    .string "nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_13::
    .string "Then said Pilate unto him, Hearest\n"
    .string "thou not how many things they witness\l"
    .string "against thee?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_14::
    .string "And he answered him to never a word;\n"
    .string "insomuch that the governor\l"
    .string "marvelled greatly$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_15::
    .string "Now at that feast the governor was\n"
    .string "wont to release unto the people a\l"
    .string "prisoner, whom they would.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_16::
    .string "And they had then a notable\n"
    .string "prisoner, called Barabbas.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_17::
    .string "Therefore when they were gathered\n"
    .string "together, Pilate said unto them,\l"
    .string "Whom will ye that I release unto\l"
    .string "you? Barabbas, or Jesus which is\l"
    .string "called Christ?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_18::
    .string "For he knew that for envy they had\n"
    .string "delivered him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_19::
    .string "When he was set down on the judgment\n"
    .string "seat, his wife sent unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Have thou nothing to do with that\l"
    .string "just man: for I have suffered many\l"
    .string "things this day in a dream because of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_20::
    .string "But the chief priests and elders\n"
    .string "persuaded the multitude that they\l"
    .string "should ask Barabbas, and destroy\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_21::
    .string "The governor answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, Whether of the twain will ye\l"
    .string "that I release unto you? They said,\l"
    .string "Barabbas.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_22::
    .string "Pilate saith unto them, What shall\n"
    .string "I do then with Jesus which is called\l"
    .string "Christ? They all say unto him, Let\l"
    .string "him be crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_23::
    .string "And the governor said, Why, what\n"
    .string "evil hath he done? But they cried out\l"
    .string "the more, saying, Let him be\l"
    .string "crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_24::
    .string "When Pilate saw that he could\n"
    .string "prevail nothing, but that rather a\l"
    .string "tumult was made, he took water, and\l"
    .string "washed his hands before the\l"
    .string "multitude, saying, I am innocent of\l"
    .string "the blood of this just person: see\l"
    .string "ye to it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_25::
    .string "Then answered all the people,\n"
    .string "and said, His blood be on us, and on\l"
    .string "our children.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_26::
    .string "Then released he Barabbas unto\n"
    .string "them: and when he had scourged Jesus,\l"
    .string "he delivered him to be crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_27::
    .string "Then the soldiers of the governor\n"
    .string "took Jesus into the common hall, and\l"
    .string "gathered unto him the whole band of\l"
    .string "soldiers.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_28::
    .string "And they stripped him, and put on\n"
    .string "him a scarlet robe.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_29::
    .string "And when they had platted a crown\n"
    .string "of thorns, they put it upon his\l"
    .string "head, and a reed in his right hand:\l"
    .string "and they bowed the knee before him,\l"
    .string "and mocked him, saying, Hail, King of\l"
    .string "the Jews!"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_30::
    .string "And they spit upon him, and took\n"
    .string "the reed, and smote him on the head$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_31::
    .string "And after that they had mocked him,\n"
    .string "they took the robe off from him, and\l"
    .string "put his own raiment on him, and led\l"
    .string "him away to crucify him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_32::
    .string "And as they came out, they found a\n"
    .string "man of Cyrene, Simon by name: him\l"
    .string "they compelled to bear his cross.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_33::
    .string "And when they were come unto a\n"
    .string "place called Golgotha, that is to\l"
    .string "say, a place of a skull,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_34::
    .string "They gave him vinegar to drink\n"
    .string "mingled with gall: and when he had\l"
    .string "tasted thereof, he would not drink$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_35::
    .string "And they crucified him, and parted\n"
    .string "his garments, casting lots: that it\l"
    .string "might be fulfilled which was\l"
    .string "spoken by the prophet, They parted\l"
    .string "my garments among them, and upon my\l"
    .string "vesture did they cast lots.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_36::
    .string "And sitting down they watched him\n"
    .string "there;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_37::
    .string "And set up over his head his\n"
    .string "accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE\l"
    .string "KING OF THE JEWS$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_38::
    .string "Then were there two thieves\n"
    .string "crucified with him, one on the right\l"
    .string "hand, and another on the left.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_39::
    .string "And they that passed by reviled\n"
    .string "him, wagging their heads,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_40::
    .string "And saying, Thou that destroyest the\n"
    .string "temple, and buildest it in three\l"
    .string "days, save thyself. If thou be the\l"
    .string "Son of God, come down from the cross$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_41::
    .string "Likewise also the chief priests\n"
    .string "mocking him, with the scribes and\l"
    .string "elders, said,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_42::
    .string "He saved others; himself he cannot\n"
    .string "save. If he be the King of Israel,\l"
    .string "let him now come down from the cross,\l"
    .string "and we will believe him$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_43::
    .string "He trusted in God; let him deliver\n"
    .string "him now, if he will have him: for he\l"
    .string "said, I am the Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_44::
    .string "The thieves also, which were\n"
    .string "crucified with him, cast the same in\l"
    .string "his teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_45::
    .string "Now from the sixth hour there was\n"
    .string "darkness over all the land unto the\l"
    .string "ninth hour.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_46::
    .string "And about the ninth hour Jesus cried\n"
    .string "with a loud voice, saying, Eli,\l"
    .string "Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to\l"
    .string "say, My God, my God, why hast thou\l"
    .string "forsaken me?"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_47::
    .string "Some of them that stood there, when\n"
    .string "they heard that, said, This man\l"
    .string "calleth for Elias$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_48::
    .string "And straightway one of them ran, and\n"
    .string "took a spunge, and filled it with\l"
    .string "vinegar, and put it on a reed, and\l"
    .string "gave him to drink.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_49::
    .string "The rest said, Let be, let us see\n"
    .string "whether Elias will come to save him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_50::
    .string "Jesus, when he had cried again with\n"
    .string "a loud voice, yielded up the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_51::
    .string "And, behold, the veil of the\n"
    .string "temple was rent in twain from the\l"
    .string "top to the bottom; and the earth did\l"
    .string "quake, and the rocks rent;"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_52::
    .string "And the graves were opened; and\n"
    .string "many bodies of the saints which\l"
    .string "slept arose,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_53::
    .string "And came out of the graves after his\n"
    .string "resurrection, and went into the holy\l"
    .string "city, and appeared unto many$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_54::
    .string "Now when the centurion, and they\n"
    .string "that were with him, watching Jesus,\l"
    .string "saw the earthquake, and those things\l"
    .string "that were done, they feared greatly,\l"
    .string "saying, Truly this was the Son of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_55::
    .string "And many women were there beholding\n"
    .string "afar off, which followed Jesus from\l"
    .string "Galilee, ministering unto him:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_56::
    .string "Among which was Mary Magdalene, and\n"
    .string "Mary the mother of James and Joses,\l"
    .string "and the mother of Zebedee’s children$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_57::
    .string "When the even was come, there came a\n"
    .string "rich man of Arimathaea, named\l"
    .string "Joseph, who also himself was Jesus’\l"
    .string "disciple:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_58::
    .string "He went to Pilate, and begged the\n"
    .string "body of Jesus. Then Pilate commanded\l"
    .string "the body to be delivered$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_59::
    .string "And when Joseph had taken the body,\n"
    .string "he wrapped it in a clean linen\l"
    .string "cloth,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_60::
    .string "And laid it in his own new tomb,\n"
    .string "which he had hewn out in the rock: and\l"
    .string "he rolled a great stone to the door\l"
    .string "of the sepulchre, and departed$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_61::
    .string "And there was Mary Magdalene, and\n"
    .string "the other Mary, sitting over against\l"
    .string "the sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_62::
    .string "Now the next day, that followed the\n"
    .string "day of the preparation, the chief\l"
    .string "priests and Pharisees came together\l"
    .string "unto Pilate,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_63::
    .string "Saying, Sir, we remember that that\n"
    .string "deceiver said, while he was yet\l"
    .string "alive, After three days I will rise\l"
    .string "again$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_64::
    .string "Command therefore that the\n"
    .string "sepulchre be made sure until the\l"
    .string "third day, lest his disciples come\l"
    .string "by night, and steal him away, and say\l"
    .string "unto the people, He is risen from\l"
    .string "the dead: so the last error shall\l"
    .string "be worse than the first.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_65::
    .string "Pilate said unto them, Ye have a\n"
    .string "watch: go your way, make it as sure as\l"
    .string "ye can.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_27_66::
    .string "So they went, and made the\n"
    .string "sepulchre sure, sealing the stone,\l"
    .string "and setting a watch.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_1::
    .string "In the end of the sabbath, as it\n"
    .string "began to dawn toward the first day of\l"
    .string "the week, came Mary Magdalene and\l"
    .string "the other Mary to see the sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_2::
    .string "And, behold, there was a great\n"
    .string "earthquake: for the angel of the\l"
    .string "Lord descended from heaven, and came\l"
    .string "and rolled back the stone from the\l"
    .string "door, and sat upon it.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_3::
    .string "His countenance was like\n"
    .string "lightning, and his raiment white as\l"
    .string "snow:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_4::
    .string "And for fear of him the keepers did\n"
    .string "shake, and became as dead men$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_5::
    .string "And the angel answered and said\n"
    .string "unto the women, Fear not ye: for I\l"
    .string "know that ye seek Jesus, which was\l"
    .string "crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_6::
    .string "He is not here: for he is risen, as\n"
    .string "he said. Come, see the place where\l"
    .string "the Lord lay.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_7::
    .string "And go quickly, and tell his\n"
    .string "disciples that he is risen from the\l"
    .string "dead; and, behold, he goeth before\l"
    .string "you into Galilee; there shall ye\l"
    .string "see him: lo, I have told you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_8::
    .string "And they departed quickly from the\n"
    .string "sepulchre with fear and great joy;\l"
    .string "and did run to bring his disciples\l"
    .string "word.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_9::
    .string "And as they went to tell his\n"
    .string "disciples, behold, Jesus met them,\l"
    .string "saying, All hail. And they came and\l"
    .string "held him by the feet, and\l"
    .string "worshipped him.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_10::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them, Be not\n"
    .string "afraid: go tell my brethren that\l"
    .string "they go into Galilee, and there\l"
    .string "shall they see me.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_11::
    .string "Now when they were going, behold,\n"
    .string "some of the watch came into the city,\l"
    .string "and shewed unto the chief priests\l"
    .string "all the things that were done.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_12::
    .string "And when they were assembled with\n"
    .string "the elders, and had taken counsel,\l"
    .string "they gave large money unto the\l"
    .string "soldiers,"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_13::
    .string "Saying, Say ye, His disciples came\n"
    .string "by night, and stole him away while\l"
    .string "we slept$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_14::
    .string "And if this come to the governor’s\n"
    .string "ears, we will persuade him, and\l"
    .string "secure you.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_15::
    .string "So they took the money, and did as\n"
    .string "they were taught: and this saying is\l"
    .string "commonly reported among the Jews\l"
    .string "until this day.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_16::
    .string "Then the eleven disciples went\n"
    .string "away into Galilee, into a mountain\l"
    .string "where Jesus had appointed them.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_17::
    .string "And when they saw him, they\n"
    .string "worshipped him: but some doubted.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_18::
    .string "And Jesus came and spake unto them,\n"
    .string "saying, All power is given unto me\l"
    .string "in heaven and in earth.$"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_19::
    .string "Go ye therefore, and teach all\n"
    .string "nations, baptizing them in the name\l"
    .string "of the Father, and of the Son, and of\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost:"
Bible_Text_Matthew_28_20::
    .string "Teaching them to observe all\n"
    .string "things whatsoever I have commanded\l"
    .string "you: and, lo, I am with you alway,\l"
    .string "even unto the end of the world. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_1::
    .string "The beginning of the gospel of\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ, the Son of God;"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_2::
    .string "As it is written in the prophets,\n"
    .string "Behold, I send my messenger before\l"
    .string "thy face, which shall prepare thy\l"
    .string "way before thee$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_3::
    .string "The voice of one crying in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, Prepare ye the way of\l"
    .string "the Lord, make his paths straight.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_4::
    .string "John did baptize in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and preach the baptism\l"
    .string "of repentance for the remission of\l"
    .string "sins.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_5::
    .string "And there went out unto him all the\n"
    .string "land of Judaea, and they of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and were all baptized\l"
    .string "of him in the river of Jordan,\l"
    .string "confessing their sins.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_6::
    .string "And John was clothed with camel’s\n"
    .string "hair, and with a girdle of a skin\l"
    .string "about his loins; and he did eat\l"
    .string "locusts and wild honey;"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_7::
    .string "And preached, saying, There cometh\n"
    .string "one mightier than I after me, the\l"
    .string "latchet of whose shoes I am not\l"
    .string "worthy to stoop down and unloose$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_8::
    .string "I indeed have baptized you with\n"
    .string "water: but he shall baptize you\l"
    .string "with the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_9::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "that Jesus came from Nazareth of\l"
    .string "Galilee, and was baptized of John\l"
    .string "in Jordan.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_10::
    .string "And straightway coming up out of\n"
    .string "the water, he saw the heavens\l"
    .string "opened, and the Spirit like a dove\l"
    .string "descending upon him:"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_11::
    .string "And there came a voice from heaven,\n"
    .string "saying, Thou art my beloved Son, in\l"
    .string "whom I am well pleased$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_12::
    .string "And immediately the spirit driveth\n"
    .string "him into the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_13::
    .string "And he was there in the wilderness\n"
    .string "forty days, tempted of Satan; and\l"
    .string "was with the wild beasts; and the\l"
    .string "angels ministered unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_14::
    .string "Now after that John was put in\n"
    .string "prison, Jesus came into Galilee,\l"
    .string "preaching the gospel of the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God,"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_15::
    .string "And saying, The time is fulfilled,\n"
    .string "and the kingdom of God is at hand:\l"
    .string "repent ye, and believe the gospel$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_16::
    .string "Now as he walked by the sea of\n"
    .string "Galilee, he saw Simon and Andrew his\l"
    .string "brother casting a net into the sea:\l"
    .string "for they were fishers.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_17::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, Come ye\n"
    .string "after me, and I will make you to\l"
    .string "become fishers of men.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_18::
    .string "And straightway they forsook their\n"
    .string "nets, and followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_19::
    .string "And when he had gone a little\n"
    .string "farther thence, he saw James the son\l"
    .string "of Zebedee, and John his brother, who\l"
    .string "also were in the ship mending their\l"
    .string "nets.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_20::
    .string "And straightway he called them:\n"
    .string "and they left their father Zebedee\l"
    .string "in the ship with the hired servants,\l"
    .string "and went after him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_21::
    .string "And they went into Capernaum; and\n"
    .string "straightway on the sabbath day he\l"
    .string "entered into the synagogue, and\l"
    .string "taught.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_22::
    .string "And they were astonished at his\n"
    .string "doctrine: for he taught them as one\l"
    .string "that had authority, and not as the\l"
    .string "scribes.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_23::
    .string "And there was in their synagogue a\n"
    .string "man with an unclean spirit; and he\l"
    .string "cried out,"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_24::
    .string "Saying, Let us alone; what have we\n"
    .string "to do with thee, thou Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth? art thou come to destroy\l"
    .string "us? I know thee who thou art, the\l"
    .string "Holy One of God$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_25::
    .string "And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold\n"
    .string "thy peace, and come out of him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_26::
    .string "And when the unclean spirit had\n"
    .string "torn him, and cried with a loud\l"
    .string "voice, he came out of him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_27::
    .string "And they were all amazed, insomuch\n"
    .string "that they questioned among\l"
    .string "themselves, saying, What thing is\l"
    .string "this? what new doctrine is this? for\l"
    .string "with authority commandeth he even\l"
    .string "the unclean spirits, and they do\l"
    .string "obey him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_28::
    .string "And immediately his fame spread\n"
    .string "abroad throughout all the region\l"
    .string "round about Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_29::
    .string "And forthwith, when they were come\n"
    .string "out of the synagogue, they entered\l"
    .string "into the house of Simon and Andrew,\l"
    .string "with James and John.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_30::
    .string "But Simon’s wife’s mother lay sick\n"
    .string "of a fever, and anon they tell him\l"
    .string "of her.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_31::
    .string "And he came and took her by the hand,\n"
    .string "and lifted her up; and immediately\l"
    .string "the fever left her, and she\l"
    .string "ministered unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_32::
    .string "And at even, when the sun did set,\n"
    .string "they brought unto him all that were\l"
    .string "diseased, and them that were\l"
    .string "possessed with devils.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_33::
    .string "And all the city was gathered\n"
    .string "together at the door.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_34::
    .string "And he healed many that were sick\n"
    .string "of divers diseases, and cast out many\l"
    .string "devils; and suffered not the devils\l"
    .string "to speak, because they knew him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_35::
    .string "And in the morning, rising up a\n"
    .string "great while before day, he went out,\l"
    .string "and departed into a solitary\l"
    .string "place, and there prayed.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_36::
    .string "And Simon and they that were with\n"
    .string "him followed after him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_37::
    .string "And when they had found him, they\n"
    .string "said unto him, All men seek for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_38::
    .string "And he said unto them, Let us go into\n"
    .string "the next towns, that I may preach\l"
    .string "there also: for therefore came I\l"
    .string "forth.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_39::
    .string "And he preached in their synagogues\n"
    .string "throughout all Galilee, and cast\l"
    .string "out devils.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_40::
    .string "And there came a leper to him,\n"
    .string "beseeching him, and kneeling down to\l"
    .string "him, and saying unto him, If thou\l"
    .string "wilt, thou canst make me clean.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_41::
    .string "And Jesus, moved with compassion,\n"
    .string "put forth his hand, and touched him,\l"
    .string "and saith unto him, I will; be thou\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_42::
    .string "And as soon as he had spoken,\n"
    .string "immediately the leprosy departed\l"
    .string "from him, and he was cleansed.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_43::
    .string "And he straitly charged him, and\n"
    .string "forthwith sent him away;"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_44::
    .string "And saith unto him, See thou say\n"
    .string "nothing to any man: but go thy way,\l"
    .string "shew thyself to the priest, and\l"
    .string "offer for thy cleansing those things\l"
    .string "which Moses commanded, for a\l"
    .string "testimony unto them$"
Bible_Text_Mark_1_45::
    .string "But he went out, and began to\n"
    .string "publish it much, and to blaze abroad\l"
    .string "the matter, insomuch that Jesus\l"
    .string "could no more openly enter into the\l"
    .string "city, but was without in desert\l"
    .string "places: and they came to him from\l"
    .string "every quarter.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_1::
    .string "And again he entered into Capernaum\n"
    .string "after some days; and it was noised\l"
    .string "that he was in the house.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_2::
    .string "And straightway many were gathered\n"
    .string "together, insomuch that there was no\l"
    .string "room to receive them, no, not so much\l"
    .string "as about the door: and he preached\l"
    .string "the word unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_3::
    .string "And they come unto him, bringing one\n"
    .string "sick of the palsy, which was borne\l"
    .string "of four.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_4::
    .string "And when they could not come nigh\n"
    .string "unto him for the press, they\l"
    .string "uncovered the roof where he was: and\l"
    .string "when they had broken it up, they let\l"
    .string "down the bed wherein the sick of the\l"
    .string "palsy lay.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_5::
    .string "When Jesus saw their faith, he said\n"
    .string "unto the sick of the palsy, Son, thy\l"
    .string "sins be forgiven thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_6::
    .string "But there was certain of the scribes\n"
    .string "sitting there, and reasoning in their\l"
    .string "hearts,"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_7::
    .string "Why doth this man thus speak\n"
    .string "blasphemies? who can forgive sins\l"
    .string "but God only?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_8::
    .string "And immediately when Jesus\n"
    .string "perceived in his spirit that they so\l"
    .string "reasoned within themselves, he said\l"
    .string "unto them, Why reason ye these things\l"
    .string "in your hearts?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_9::
    .string "Whether is it easier to say to the\n"
    .string "sick of the palsy, Thy sins be\l"
    .string "forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and\l"
    .string "take up thy bed, and walk?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_10::
    .string "But that ye may know that the Son of\n"
    .string "man hath power on earth to forgive\l"
    .string "sins, (he saith to the sick of the\l"
    .string "palsy,)"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_11::
    .string "I say unto thee, Arise, and take up\n"
    .string "thy bed, and go thy way into thine\l"
    .string "house$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_12::
    .string "And immediately he arose, took up\n"
    .string "the bed, and went forth before them\l"
    .string "all; insomuch that they were all\l"
    .string "amazed, and glorified God, saying,\l"
    .string "We never saw it on this fashion.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_13::
    .string "And he went forth again by the sea\n"
    .string "side; and all the multitude\l"
    .string "resorted unto him, and he taught them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_14::
    .string "And as he passed by, he saw Levi the\n"
    .string "son of Alphaeus sitting at the\l"
    .string "receipt of custom, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Follow me. And he arose and\l"
    .string "followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as Jesus\n"
    .string "sat at meat in his house, many\l"
    .string "publicans and sinners sat also\l"
    .string "together with Jesus and his\l"
    .string "disciples: for there were many, and\l"
    .string "they followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_16::
    .string "And when the scribes and Pharisees\n"
    .string "saw him eat with publicans and\l"
    .string "sinners, they said unto his\l"
    .string "disciples, How is it that he eateth\l"
    .string "and drinketh with publicans and\l"
    .string "sinners?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_17::
    .string "When Jesus heard it, he saith unto\n"
    .string "them, They that are whole have no\l"
    .string "need of the physician, but they that\l"
    .string "are sick: I came not to call the\l"
    .string "righteous, but sinners to repentance$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_18::
    .string "And the disciples of John and of\n"
    .string "the Pharisees used to fast: and they\l"
    .string "come and say unto him, Why do the\l"
    .string "disciples of John and of the\l"
    .string "Pharisees fast, but thy disciples\l"
    .string "fast not?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_19::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, Can the\n"
    .string "children of the bridechamber fast,\l"
    .string "while the bridegroom is with them?\l"
    .string "as long as they have the bridegroom\l"
    .string "with them, they cannot fast$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_20::
    .string "But the days will come, when the\n"
    .string "bridegroom shall be taken away from\l"
    .string "them, and then shall they fast in\l"
    .string "those days.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_21::
    .string "No man also seweth a piece of new\n"
    .string "cloth on an old garment: else the\l"
    .string "new piece that filled it up taketh\l"
    .string "away from the old, and the rent is\l"
    .string "made worse.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_22::
    .string "And no man putteth new wine into\n"
    .string "old bottles: else the new wine doth\l"
    .string "burst the bottles, and the wine is\l"
    .string "spilled, and the bottles will be\l"
    .string "marred: but new wine must be put into\l"
    .string "new bottles.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, that he went\n"
    .string "through the corn fields on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day; and his disciples\l"
    .string "began, as they went, to pluck the\l"
    .string "ears of corn.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_24::
    .string "And the Pharisees said unto him,\n"
    .string "Behold, why do they on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day that which is not lawful?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_25::
    .string "And he said unto them, Have ye never\n"
    .string "read what David did, when he had\l"
    .string "need, and was an hungred, he, and they\l"
    .string "that were with him?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_26::
    .string "How he went into the house of God in\n"
    .string "the days of Abiathar the high\l"
    .string "priest, and did eat the shewbread,\l"
    .string "which is not lawful to eat but for\l"
    .string "the priests, and gave also to them\l"
    .string "which were with him?"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_27::
    .string "And he said unto them, The sabbath\n"
    .string "was made for man, and not man for the\l"
    .string "sabbath:"
Bible_Text_Mark_2_28::
    .string "Therefore the Son of man is Lord\n"
    .string "also of the sabbath$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_1::
    .string "And he entered again into the\n"
    .string "synagogue; and there was a man there\l"
    .string "which had a withered hand.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_2::
    .string "And they watched him, whether he\n"
    .string "would heal him on the sabbath day;\l"
    .string "that they might accuse him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_3::
    .string "And he saith unto the man which had\n"
    .string "the withered hand, Stand forth.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_4::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Is it\n"
    .string "lawful to do good on the sabbath\l"
    .string "days, or to do evil? to save life, or\l"
    .string "to kill? But they held their peace.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_5::
    .string "And when he had looked round about\n"
    .string "on them with anger, being grieved for\l"
    .string "the hardness of their hearts, he\l"
    .string "saith unto the man, Stretch forth\l"
    .string "thine hand. And he stretched it out:\l"
    .string "and his hand was restored whole as\l"
    .string "the other.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_6::
    .string "And the Pharisees went forth, and\n"
    .string "straightway took counsel with the\l"
    .string "Herodians against him, how they might\l"
    .string "destroy him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_7::
    .string "But Jesus withdrew himself with his\n"
    .string "disciples to the sea: and a great\l"
    .string "multitude from Galilee followed\l"
    .string "him, and from Judaea,"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_8::
    .string "And from Jerusalem, and from\n"
    .string "Idumaea, and from beyond Jordan; and\l"
    .string "they about Tyre and Sidon, a great\l"
    .string "multitude, when they had heard what\l"
    .string "great things he did, came unto him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_9::
    .string "And he spake to his disciples,\n"
    .string "that a small ship should wait on\l"
    .string "him because of the multitude, lest\l"
    .string "they should throng him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_10::
    .string "For he had healed many; insomuch\n"
    .string "that they pressed upon him for to\l"
    .string "touch him, as many as had plagues.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_11::
    .string "And unclean spirits, when they saw\n"
    .string "him, fell down before him, and\l"
    .string "cried, saying, Thou art the Son of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_12::
    .string "And he straitly charged them that\n"
    .string "they should not make him known.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_13::
    .string "And he goeth up into a mountain, and\n"
    .string "calleth unto him whom he would: and\l"
    .string "they came unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_14::
    .string "And he ordained twelve, that they\n"
    .string "should be with him, and that he might\l"
    .string "send them forth to preach,"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_15::
    .string "And to have power to heal\n"
    .string "sicknesses, and to cast out devils:"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_16::
    .string "And Simon he surnamed Peter;"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_17::
    .string "And James the son of Zebedee, and\n"
    .string "John the brother of James; and he\l"
    .string "surnamed them Boanerges, which is,\l"
    .string "The sons of thunder:"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_18::
    .string "And Andrew, and Philip, and\n"
    .string "Bartholomew, and Matthew, and\l"
    .string "Thomas, and James the son of\l"
    .string "Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus, and Simon\l"
    .string "the Canaanite,"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_19::
    .string "And Judas Iscariot, which also\n"
    .string "betrayed him: and they went into an\l"
    .string "house$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_20::
    .string "And the multitude cometh together\n"
    .string "again, so that they could not so much\l"
    .string "as eat bread.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_21::
    .string "And when his friends heard of it,\n"
    .string "they went out to lay hold on him:\l"
    .string "for they said, He is beside himself.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_22::
    .string "And the scribes which came down from\n"
    .string "Jerusalem said, He hath Beelzebub,\l"
    .string "and by the prince of the devils\l"
    .string "casteth he out devils.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_23::
    .string "And he called them unto him, and\n"
    .string "said unto them in parables, How can\l"
    .string "Satan cast out Satan?"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_24::
    .string "And if a kingdom be divided against\n"
    .string "itself, that kingdom cannot stand$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_25::
    .string "And if a house be divided against\n"
    .string "itself, that house cannot stand.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_26::
    .string "And if Satan rise up against\n"
    .string "himself, and be divided, he cannot\l"
    .string "stand, but hath an end.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_27::
    .string "No man can enter into a strong man’s\n"
    .string "house, and spoil his goods, except\l"
    .string "he will first bind the strong man;\l"
    .string "and then he will spoil his house.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_28::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, All sins\n"
    .string "shall be forgiven unto the sons of\l"
    .string "men, and blasphemies wherewith\l"
    .string "soever they shall blaspheme:"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_29::
    .string "But he that shall blaspheme\n"
    .string "against the Holy Ghost hath never\l"
    .string "forgiveness, but is in danger of\l"
    .string "eternal damnation$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_30::
    .string "Because they said, He hath an\n"
    .string "unclean spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_31::
    .string "There came then his brethren and his\n"
    .string "mother, and, standing without, sent\l"
    .string "unto him, calling him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_32::
    .string "And the multitude sat about him,\n"
    .string "and they said unto him, Behold, thy\l"
    .string "mother and thy brethren without seek\l"
    .string "for thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_33::
    .string "And he answered them, saying, Who is\n"
    .string "my mother, or my brethren?"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_34::
    .string "And he looked round about on them\n"
    .string "which sat about him, and said,\l"
    .string "Behold my mother and my brethren!"
Bible_Text_Mark_3_35::
    .string "For whosoever shall do the will\n"
    .string "of God, the same is my brother, and my\l"
    .string "sister, and mother$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_1::
    .string "And he began again to teach by the\n"
    .string "sea side: and there was gathered unto\l"
    .string "him a great multitude, so that he\l"
    .string "entered into a ship, and sat in the\l"
    .string "sea; and the whole multitude was by\l"
    .string "the sea on the land.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_2::
    .string "And he taught them many things by\n"
    .string "parables, and said unto them in his\l"
    .string "doctrine,"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_3::
    .string "Hearken; Behold, there went out a\n"
    .string "sower to sow:"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he sowed,\n"
    .string "some fell by the way side, and the\l"
    .string "fowls of the air came and devoured\l"
    .string "it up$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_5::
    .string "And some fell on stony ground,\n"
    .string "where it had not much earth; and\l"
    .string "immediately it sprang up, because\l"
    .string "it had no depth of earth:"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_6::
    .string "But when the sun was up, it was\n"
    .string "scorched; and because it had no root,\l"
    .string "it withered away$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_7::
    .string "And some fell among thorns, and the\n"
    .string "thorns grew up, and choked it, and it\l"
    .string "yielded no fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_8::
    .string "And other fell on good ground, and\n"
    .string "did yield fruit that sprang up and\l"
    .string "increased; and brought forth, some\l"
    .string "thirty, and some sixty, and some an\l"
    .string "hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_9::
    .string "And he said unto them, He that hath\n"
    .string "ears to hear, let him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_10::
    .string "And when he was alone, they that\n"
    .string "were about him with the twelve asked\l"
    .string "of him the parable.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_11::
    .string "And he said unto them, Unto you it is\n"
    .string "given to know the mystery of the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God: but unto them that\l"
    .string "are without, all these things are\l"
    .string "done in parables:"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_12::
    .string "That seeing they may see, and not\n"
    .string "perceive; and hearing they may hear,\l"
    .string "and not understand; lest at any time\l"
    .string "they should be converted, and their\l"
    .string "sins should be forgiven them$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_13::
    .string "And he said unto them, Know ye not\n"
    .string "this parable? and how then will ye\l"
    .string "know all parables?"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_14::
    .string "The sower soweth the word$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_15::
    .string "And these are they by the way side,\n"
    .string "where the word is sown; but when they\l"
    .string "have heard, Satan cometh\l"
    .string "immediately, and taketh away the\l"
    .string "word that was sown in their hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_16::
    .string "And these are they likewise which\n"
    .string "are sown on stony ground; who, when\l"
    .string "they have heard the word,\l"
    .string "immediately receive it with\l"
    .string "gladness;"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_17::
    .string "And have no root in themselves, and\n"
    .string "so endure but for a time: afterward,\l"
    .string "when affliction or persecution\l"
    .string "ariseth for the word’s sake,\l"
    .string "immediately they are offended$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_18::
    .string "And these are they which are sown\n"
    .string "among thorns; such as hear the word,"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_19::
    .string "And the cares of this world, and the\n"
    .string "deceitfulness of riches, and the\l"
    .string "lusts of other things entering in,\l"
    .string "choke the word, and it becometh\l"
    .string "unfruitful$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_20::
    .string "And these are they which are sown on\n"
    .string "good ground; such as hear the word,\l"
    .string "and receive it, and bring forth\l"
    .string "fruit, some thirtyfold, some sixty,\l"
    .string "and some an hundred.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_21::
    .string "And he said unto them, Is a candle\n"
    .string "brought to be put under a bushel, or\l"
    .string "under a bed? and not to be set on a\l"
    .string "candlestick?"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_22::
    .string "For there is nothing hid, which\n"
    .string "shall not be manifested; neither\l"
    .string "was any thing kept secret, but that\l"
    .string "it should come abroad$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_23::
    .string "If any man have ears to hear, let\n"
    .string "him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_24::
    .string "And he said unto them, Take heed\n"
    .string "what ye hear: with what measure ye\l"
    .string "mete, it shall be measured to you:\l"
    .string "and unto you that hear shall more be\l"
    .string "given.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_25::
    .string "For he that hath, to him shall be\n"
    .string "given: and he that hath not, from him\l"
    .string "shall be taken even that which he\l"
    .string "hath.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_26::
    .string "And he said, So is the kingdom of\n"
    .string "God, as if a man should cast seed\l"
    .string "into the ground;"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_27::
    .string "And should sleep, and rise night\n"
    .string "and day, and the seed should spring\l"
    .string "and grow up, he knoweth not how$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_28::
    .string "For the earth bringeth forth fruit\n"
    .string "of herself; first the blade, then\l"
    .string "the ear, after that the full corn in\l"
    .string "the ear.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_29::
    .string "But when the fruit is brought forth,\n"
    .string "immediately he putteth in the\l"
    .string "sickle, because the harvest is come.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_30::
    .string "And he said, Whereunto shall we\n"
    .string "liken the kingdom of God? or with\l"
    .string "what comparison shall we compare\l"
    .string "it?"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_31::
    .string "It is like a grain of mustard seed,\n"
    .string "which, when it is sown in the earth,\l"
    .string "is less than all the seeds that be\l"
    .string "in the earth:"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_32::
    .string "But when it is sown, it groweth up,\n"
    .string "and becometh greater than all\l"
    .string "herbs, and shooteth out great\l"
    .string "branches; so that the fowls of the\l"
    .string "air may lodge under the shadow of it$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_33::
    .string "And with many such parables spake\n"
    .string "he the word unto them, as they were\l"
    .string "able to hear it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_34::
    .string "But without a parable spake he not\n"
    .string "unto them: and when they were alone,\l"
    .string "he expounded all things to his\l"
    .string "disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_35::
    .string "And the same day, when the even was\n"
    .string "come, he saith unto them, Let us pass\l"
    .string "over unto the other side.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_36::
    .string "And when they had sent away the\n"
    .string "multitude, they took him even as he\l"
    .string "was in the ship. And there were also\l"
    .string "with him other little ships.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_37::
    .string "And there arose a great storm of\n"
    .string "wind, and the waves beat into the\l"
    .string "ship, so that it was now full.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_38::
    .string "And he was in the hinder part of the\n"
    .string "ship, asleep on a pillow: and\l"
    .string "they awake him, and say unto him,\l"
    .string "Master, carest thou not that we\l"
    .string "perish?"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_39::
    .string "And he arose, and rebuked the wind,\n"
    .string "and said unto the sea, Peace, be\l"
    .string "still. And the wind ceased, and\l"
    .string "there was a great calm$"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_40::
    .string "And he said unto them, Why are ye so\n"
    .string "fearful? how is it that ye have no\l"
    .string "faith?"
Bible_Text_Mark_4_41::
    .string "And they feared exceedingly, and\n"
    .string "said one to another, What manner of\l"
    .string "man is this, that even the wind and\l"
    .string "the sea obey him?"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_1::
    .string "And they came over unto the other\n"
    .string "side of the sea, into the country of\l"
    .string "the Gadarenes$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_2::
    .string "And when he was come out of the\n"
    .string "ship, immediately there met him out\l"
    .string "of the tombs a man with an unclean\l"
    .string "spirit,"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_3::
    .string "Who had his dwelling among the\n"
    .string "tombs; and no man could bind him, no,\l"
    .string "not with chains:"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_4::
    .string "Because that he had been often bound\n"
    .string "with fetters and chains, and the\l"
    .string "chains had been plucked asunder by\l"
    .string "him, and the fetters broken in\l"
    .string "pieces: neither could any man tame\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_5::
    .string "And always, night and day, he was in\n"
    .string "the mountains, and in the tombs,\l"
    .string "crying, and cutting himself with\l"
    .string "stones.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_6::
    .string "But when he saw Jesus afar off, he\n"
    .string "ran and worshipped him,"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_7::
    .string "And cried with a loud voice, and\n"
    .string "said, What have I to do with thee,\l"
    .string "Jesus, thou Son of the most high God?\l"
    .string "I adjure thee by God, that thou\l"
    .string "torment me not$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_8::
    .string "For he said unto him, Come out of the\n"
    .string "man, thou unclean spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_9::
    .string "And he asked him, What is thy name?\n"
    .string "And he answered, saying, My name is\l"
    .string "Legion: for we are many.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_10::
    .string "And he besought him much that he\n"
    .string "would not send them away out of the\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_11::
    .string "Now there was there nigh unto the\n"
    .string "mountains a great herd of swine\l"
    .string "feeding.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_12::
    .string "And all the devils besought him,\n"
    .string "saying, Send us into the swine, that\l"
    .string "we may enter into them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_13::
    .string "And forthwith Jesus gave them\n"
    .string "leave. And the unclean spirits went\l"
    .string "out, and entered into the swine: and\l"
    .string "the herd ran violently down a steep\l"
    .string "place into the sea, (they were about\l"
    .string "two thousand;) and were choked in the\l"
    .string "sea.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_14::
    .string "And they that fed the swine fled,\n"
    .string "and told it in the city, and in the\l"
    .string "country. And they went out to see\l"
    .string "what it was that was done.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_15::
    .string "And they come to Jesus, and see him\n"
    .string "that was possessed with the devil,\l"
    .string "and had the legion, sitting, and\l"
    .string "clothed, and in his right mind: and\l"
    .string "they were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_16::
    .string "And they that saw it told them how\n"
    .string "it befell to him that was possessed\l"
    .string "with the devil, and also concerning\l"
    .string "the swine.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_17::
    .string "And they began to pray him to\n"
    .string "depart out of their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_18::
    .string "And when he was come into the ship,\n"
    .string "he that had been possessed with the\l"
    .string "devil prayed him that he might be\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_19::
    .string "Howbeit Jesus suffered him not, but\n"
    .string "saith unto him, Go home to thy\l"
    .string "friends, and tell them how great\l"
    .string "things the Lord hath done for thee,\l"
    .string "and hath had compassion on thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_20::
    .string "And he departed, and began to\n"
    .string "publish in Decapolis how great\l"
    .string "things Jesus had done for him: and\l"
    .string "all men did marvel.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_21::
    .string "And when Jesus was passed over\n"
    .string "again by ship unto the other side,\l"
    .string "much people gathered unto him: and\l"
    .string "he was nigh unto the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_22::
    .string "And, behold, there cometh one of\n"
    .string "the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus\l"
    .string "by name; and when he saw him, he\l"
    .string "fell at his feet,"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_23::
    .string "And besought him greatly, saying,\n"
    .string "My little daughter lieth at the\l"
    .string "point of death: I pray thee, come and\l"
    .string "lay thy hands on her, that she may be\l"
    .string "healed; and she shall live$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_24::
    .string "And Jesus went with him; and much\n"
    .string "people followed him, and thronged\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_25::
    .string "And a certain woman, which had an\n"
    .string "issue of blood twelve years,"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_26::
    .string "And had suffered many things of many\n"
    .string "physicians, and had spent all that\l"
    .string "she had, and was nothing bettered,\l"
    .string "but rather grew worse,"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_27::
    .string "When she had heard of Jesus, came in\n"
    .string "the press behind, and touched his\l"
    .string "garment$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_28::
    .string "For she said, If I may touch but his\n"
    .string "clothes, I shall be whole.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_29::
    .string "And straightway the fountain of her\n"
    .string "blood was dried up; and she felt in\l"
    .string "her body that she was healed of that\l"
    .string "plague.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_30::
    .string "And Jesus, immediately knowing in\n"
    .string "himself that virtue had gone out of\l"
    .string "him, turned him about in the press,\l"
    .string "and said, Who touched my clothes?"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_31::
    .string "And his disciples said unto him,\n"
    .string "Thou seest the multitude thronging\l"
    .string "thee, and sayest thou, Who touched\l"
    .string "me?"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_32::
    .string "And he looked round about to see\n"
    .string "her that had done this thing$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_33::
    .string "But the woman fearing and\n"
    .string "trembling, knowing what was done in\l"
    .string "her, came and fell down before him,\l"
    .string "and told him all the truth.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_34::
    .string "And he said unto her, Daughter, thy\n"
    .string "faith hath made thee whole; go in\l"
    .string "peace, and be whole of thy plague.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_35::
    .string "While he yet spake, there came from\n"
    .string "the ruler of the synagogue’s house\l"
    .string "certain which said, Thy daughter is\l"
    .string "dead: why troublest thou the Master\l"
    .string "any further?"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_36::
    .string "As soon as Jesus heard the word that\n"
    .string "was spoken, he saith unto the ruler\l"
    .string "of the synagogue, Be not afraid,\l"
    .string "only believe$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_37::
    .string "And he suffered no man to follow\n"
    .string "him, save Peter, and James, and John\l"
    .string "the brother of James.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_38::
    .string "And he cometh to the house of the\n"
    .string "ruler of the synagogue, and seeth\l"
    .string "the tumult, and them that wept and\l"
    .string "wailed greatly.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_39::
    .string "And when he was come in, he saith\n"
    .string "unto them, Why make ye this ado, and\l"
    .string "weep? the damsel is not dead, but\l"
    .string "sleepeth.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_40::
    .string "And they laughed him to scorn. But\n"
    .string "when he had put them all out, he\l"
    .string "taketh the father and the mother of\l"
    .string "the damsel, and them that were with\l"
    .string "him, and entereth in where the\l"
    .string "damsel was lying.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_41::
    .string "And he took the damsel by the hand,\n"
    .string "and said unto her, Talitha cumi;\l"
    .string "which is, being interpreted,\l"
    .string "Damsel, I say unto thee, arise.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_42::
    .string "And straightway the damsel arose,\n"
    .string "and walked; for she was of the age of\l"
    .string "twelve years. And they were\l"
    .string "astonished with a great astonishment.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_5_43::
    .string "And he charged them straitly that\n"
    .string "no man should know it; and commanded\l"
    .string "that something should be given her\l"
    .string "to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_1::
    .string "And he went out from thence, and\n"
    .string "came into his own country; and his\l"
    .string "disciples follow him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_2::
    .string "And when the sabbath day was come,\n"
    .string "he began to teach in the synagogue:\l"
    .string "and many hearing him were astonished,\l"
    .string "saying, From whence hath this man\l"
    .string "these things? and what wisdom is this\l"
    .string "which is given unto him, that even\l"
    .string "such mighty works are wrought by his\l"
    .string "hands?"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_3::
    .string "Is not this the carpenter, the son\n"
    .string "of Mary, the brother of James, and\l"
    .string "Joses, and of Juda, and Simon? and are\l"
    .string "not his sisters here with us? And\l"
    .string "they were offended at him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_4::
    .string "But Jesus said unto them, A prophet\n"
    .string "is not without honour, but in his own\l"
    .string "country, and among his own kin, and\l"
    .string "in his own house.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_5::
    .string "And he could there do no mighty\n"
    .string "work, save that he laid his hands\l"
    .string "upon a few sick folk, and healed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_6::
    .string "And he marvelled because of their\n"
    .string "unbelief. And he went round about\l"
    .string "the villages, teaching.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_7::
    .string "And he called unto him the twelve,\n"
    .string "and began to send them forth by two\l"
    .string "and two; and gave them power over\l"
    .string "unclean spirits;"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_8::
    .string "And commanded them that they should\n"
    .string "take nothing for their journey, save\l"
    .string "a staff only; no scrip, no bread, no\l"
    .string "money in their purse:"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_9::
    .string "But be shod with sandals; and not\n"
    .string "put on two coats$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_10::
    .string "And he said unto them, In what\n"
    .string "place soever ye enter into an house,\l"
    .string "there abide till ye depart from\l"
    .string "that place.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_11::
    .string "And whosoever shall not receive\n"
    .string "you, nor hear you, when ye depart\l"
    .string "thence, shake off the dust under your\l"
    .string "feet for a testimony against them.\l"
    .string "Verily I say unto you, It shall be\l"
    .string "more tolerable for Sodom and\l"
    .string "Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than\l"
    .string "for that city.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_12::
    .string "And they went out, and preached\n"
    .string "that men should repent.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_13::
    .string "And they cast out many devils, and\n"
    .string "anointed with oil many that were\l"
    .string "sick, and healed them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_14::
    .string "And king Herod heard of him; (for\n"
    .string "his name was spread abroad:) and he\l"
    .string "said, That John the Baptist was\l"
    .string "risen from the dead, and therefore\l"
    .string "mighty works do shew forth\l"
    .string "themselves in him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_15::
    .string "Others said, That it is Elias. And\n"
    .string "others said, That it is a prophet,\l"
    .string "or as one of the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_16::
    .string "But when Herod heard thereof, he\n"
    .string "said, It is John, whom I beheaded: he\l"
    .string "is risen from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_17::
    .string "For Herod himself had sent forth\n"
    .string "and laid hold upon John, and bound\l"
    .string "him in prison for Herodias’ sake,\l"
    .string "his brother Philip’s wife: for he\l"
    .string "had married her.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_18::
    .string "For John had said unto Herod, It is\n"
    .string "not lawful for thee to have thy\l"
    .string "brother’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_19::
    .string "Therefore Herodias had a quarrel\n"
    .string "against him, and would have killed\l"
    .string "him; but she could not:"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_20::
    .string "For Herod feared John, knowing that\n"
    .string "he was a just man and an holy, and\l"
    .string "observed him; and when he heard him,\l"
    .string "he did many things, and heard him\l"
    .string "gladly$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_21::
    .string "And when a convenient day was come,\n"
    .string "that Herod on his birthday made a\l"
    .string "supper to his lords, high\l"
    .string "captains, and chief estates of\l"
    .string "Galilee;"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_22::
    .string "And when the daughter of the said\n"
    .string "Herodias came in, and danced, and\l"
    .string "pleased Herod and them that sat with\l"
    .string "him, the king said unto the damsel,\l"
    .string "Ask of me whatsoever thou wilt, and I\l"
    .string "will give it thee$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_23::
    .string "And he sware unto her, Whatsoever\n"
    .string "thou shalt ask of me, I will give it\l"
    .string "thee, unto the half of my kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_24::
    .string "And she went forth, and said unto\n"
    .string "her mother, What shall I ask? And\l"
    .string "she said, The head of John the\l"
    .string "Baptist.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_25::
    .string "And she came in straightway with\n"
    .string "haste unto the king, and asked,\l"
    .string "saying, I will that thou give me by\l"
    .string "and by in a charger the head of John\l"
    .string "the Baptist.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_26::
    .string "And the king was exceeding sorry;\n"
    .string "yet for his oath’s sake, and for\l"
    .string "their sakes which sat with him, he\l"
    .string "would not reject her.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_27::
    .string "And immediately the king sent an\n"
    .string "executioner, and commanded his head\l"
    .string "to be brought: and he went and\l"
    .string "beheaded him in the prison,"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_28::
    .string "And brought his head in a charger,\n"
    .string "and gave it to the damsel: and the\l"
    .string "damsel gave it to her mother$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_29::
    .string "And when his disciples heard of it,\n"
    .string "they came and took up his corpse,\l"
    .string "and laid it in a tomb.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_30::
    .string "And the apostles gathered\n"
    .string "themselves together unto Jesus, and\l"
    .string "told him all things, both what they\l"
    .string "had done, and what they had taught.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_31::
    .string "And he said unto them, Come ye\n"
    .string "yourselves apart into a desert\l"
    .string "place, and rest a while: for there\l"
    .string "were many coming and going, and they\l"
    .string "had no leisure so much as to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_32::
    .string "And they departed into a desert\n"
    .string "place by ship privately.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_33::
    .string "And the people saw them\n"
    .string "departing, and many knew him, and\l"
    .string "ran afoot thither out of all cities,\l"
    .string "and outwent them, and came together\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_34::
    .string "And Jesus, when he came out, saw\n"
    .string "much people, and was moved with\l"
    .string "compassion toward them, because they\l"
    .string "were as sheep not having a shepherd:\l"
    .string "and he began to teach them many\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_35::
    .string "And when the day was now far spent,\n"
    .string "his disciples came unto him, and\l"
    .string "said, This is a desert place, and\l"
    .string "now the time is far passed:"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_36::
    .string "Send them away, that they may go\n"
    .string "into the country round about, and\l"
    .string "into the villages, and buy\l"
    .string "themselves bread: for they have\l"
    .string "nothing to eat$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_37::
    .string "He answered and said unto them, Give\n"
    .string "ye them to eat. And they say unto him,\l"
    .string "Shall we go and buy two hundred\l"
    .string "pennyworth of bread, and give them to\l"
    .string "eat?"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_38::
    .string "He saith unto them, How many loaves\n"
    .string "have ye? go and see. And when they\l"
    .string "knew, they say, Five, and two fishes$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_39::
    .string "And he commanded them to make all\n"
    .string "sit down by companies upon the\l"
    .string "green grass.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_40::
    .string "And they sat down in ranks, by\n"
    .string "hundreds, and by fifties.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_41::
    .string "And when he had taken the five\n"
    .string "loaves and the two fishes, he looked\l"
    .string "up to heaven, and blessed, and brake\l"
    .string "the loaves, and gave them to his\l"
    .string "disciples to set before them; and\l"
    .string "the two fishes divided he among them\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_42::
    .string "And they did all eat, and were\n"
    .string "filled.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_43::
    .string "And they took up twelve baskets\n"
    .string "full of the fragments, and of the\l"
    .string "fishes.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_44::
    .string "And they that did eat of the loaves\n"
    .string "were about five thousand men.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_45::
    .string "And straightway he constrained his\n"
    .string "disciples to get into the ship, and\l"
    .string "to go to the other side before unto\l"
    .string "Bethsaida, while he sent away the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_46::
    .string "And when he had sent them away, he\n"
    .string "departed into a mountain to pray.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_47::
    .string "And when even was come, the ship was\n"
    .string "in the midst of the sea, and he alone\l"
    .string "on the land.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_48::
    .string "And he saw them toiling in rowing;\n"
    .string "for the wind was contrary unto them:\l"
    .string "and about the fourth watch of the\l"
    .string "night he cometh unto them, walking\l"
    .string "upon the sea, and would have passed\l"
    .string "by them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_49::
    .string "But when they saw him walking upon\n"
    .string "the sea, they supposed it had been a\l"
    .string "spirit, and cried out:"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_50::
    .string "For they all saw him, and were\n"
    .string "troubled. And immediately he\l"
    .string "talked with them, and saith unto\l"
    .string "them, Be of good cheer: it is I; be\l"
    .string "not afraid$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_51::
    .string "And he went up unto them into the\n"
    .string "ship; and the wind ceased: and they\l"
    .string "were sore amazed in themselves\l"
    .string "beyond measure, and wondered.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_52::
    .string "For they considered not the miracle\n"
    .string "of the loaves: for their heart was\l"
    .string "hardened.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_53::
    .string "And when they had passed over, they\n"
    .string "came into the land of Gennesaret,\l"
    .string "and drew to the shore.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_54::
    .string "And when they were come out of the\n"
    .string "ship, straightway they knew him,"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_55::
    .string "And ran through that whole region\n"
    .string "round about, and began to carry about\l"
    .string "in beds those that were sick, where\l"
    .string "they heard he was$"
Bible_Text_Mark_6_56::
    .string "And whithersoever he entered, into\n"
    .string "villages, or cities, or country,\l"
    .string "they laid the sick in the streets,\l"
    .string "and besought him that they might\l"
    .string "touch if it were but the border of\l"
    .string "his garment: and as many as touched\l"
    .string "him were made whole.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_1::
    .string "Then came together unto him the\n"
    .string "Pharisees, and certain of the\l"
    .string "scribes, which came from Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_2::
    .string "And when they saw some of his\n"
    .string "disciples eat bread with defiled,\l"
    .string "that is to say, with unwashen, hands,\l"
    .string "they found fault.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_3::
    .string "For the Pharisees, and all the\n"
    .string "Jews, except they wash their hands\l"
    .string "oft, eat not, holding the tradition\l"
    .string "of the elders.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_4::
    .string "And when they come from the market,\n"
    .string "except they wash, they eat not. And\l"
    .string "many other things there be, which\l"
    .string "they have received to hold, as the\l"
    .string "washing of cups, and pots, brasen\l"
    .string "vessels, and of tables.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_5::
    .string "Then the Pharisees and scribes\n"
    .string "asked him, Why walk not thy\l"
    .string "disciples according to the\l"
    .string "tradition of the elders, but eat\l"
    .string "bread with unwashen hands?"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_6::
    .string "He answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Well hath Esaias prophesied of you\l"
    .string "hypocrites, as it is written, This\l"
    .string "people honoureth me with their\l"
    .string "lips, but their heart is far from me$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_7::
    .string "Howbeit in vain do they worship me,\n"
    .string "teaching for doctrines the\l"
    .string "commandments of men.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_8::
    .string "For laying aside the commandment of\n"
    .string "God, ye hold the tradition of men, as\l"
    .string "the washing of pots and cups: and\l"
    .string "many other such like things ye do.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_9::
    .string "And he said unto them, Full well\n"
    .string "ye reject the commandment of God,\l"
    .string "that ye may keep your own tradition.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_10::
    .string "For Moses said, Honour thy father\n"
    .string "and thy mother; and, Whoso curseth\l"
    .string "father or mother, let him die the\l"
    .string "death:"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_11::
    .string "But ye say, If a man shall say to\n"
    .string "his father or mother, It is Corban,\l"
    .string "that is to say, a gift, by whatsoever\l"
    .string "thou mightest be profited by me; he\l"
    .string "shall be free$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_12::
    .string "And ye suffer him no more to do\n"
    .string "ought for his father or his mother;"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_13::
    .string "Making the word of God of none\n"
    .string "effect through your tradition, which\l"
    .string "ye have delivered: and many such\l"
    .string "like things do ye$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_14::
    .string "And when he had called all the\n"
    .string "people unto him, he said unto them,\l"
    .string "Hearken unto me every one of you, and\l"
    .string "understand:"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_15::
    .string "There is nothing from without a man,\n"
    .string "that entering into him can defile\l"
    .string "him: but the things which come out of\l"
    .string "him, those are they that defile the\l"
    .string "man$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_16::
    .string "If any man have ears to hear, let\n"
    .string "him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_17::
    .string "And when he was entered into the\n"
    .string "house from the people, his\l"
    .string "disciples asked him concerning the\l"
    .string "parable.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_18::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Are ye so\n"
    .string "without understanding also? Do ye\l"
    .string "not perceive, that whatsoever thing\l"
    .string "from without entereth into the man,\l"
    .string "it cannot defile him;"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_19::
    .string "Because it entereth not into his\n"
    .string "heart, but into the belly, and goeth\l"
    .string "out into the draught, purging all\l"
    .string "meats?"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_20::
    .string "And he said, That which cometh out\n"
    .string "of the man, that defileth the man$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_21::
    .string "For from within, out of the heart of\n"
    .string "men, proceed evil thoughts,\l"
    .string "adulteries, fornications, murders,"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_22::
    .string "Thefts, covetousness, wickedness,\n"
    .string "deceit, lasciviousness, an evil\l"
    .string "eye, blasphemy, pride,\l"
    .string "foolishness:"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_23::
    .string "All these evil things come from\n"
    .string "within, and defile the man$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_24::
    .string "And from thence he arose, and went\n"
    .string "into the borders of Tyre and Sidon,\l"
    .string "and entered into an house, and would\l"
    .string "have no man know it: but he could not\l"
    .string "be hid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_25::
    .string "For a certain woman, whose young\n"
    .string "daughter had an unclean spirit,\l"
    .string "heard of him, and came and fell at\l"
    .string "his feet:"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_26::
    .string "The woman was a Greek, a\n"
    .string "Syrophenician by nation; and she\l"
    .string "besought him that he would cast\l"
    .string "forth the devil out of her daughter$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_27::
    .string "But Jesus said unto her, Let the\n"
    .string "children first be filled: for it is\l"
    .string "not meet to take the children’s\l"
    .string "bread, and to cast it unto the dogs.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_28::
    .string "And she answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Yes, Lord: yet the dogs under the\l"
    .string "table eat of the children’s crumbs.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_29::
    .string "And he said unto her, For this\n"
    .string "saying go thy way; the devil is gone\l"
    .string "out of thy daughter.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_30::
    .string "And when she was come to her house,\n"
    .string "she found the devil gone out, and her\l"
    .string "daughter laid upon the bed.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_31::
    .string "And again, departing from the\n"
    .string "coasts of Tyre and Sidon, he came\l"
    .string "unto the sea of Galilee, through the\l"
    .string "midst of the coasts of Decapolis.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_32::
    .string "And they bring unto him one that was\n"
    .string "deaf, and had an impediment in his\l"
    .string "speech; and they beseech him to put\l"
    .string "his hand upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_33::
    .string "And he took him aside from the\n"
    .string "multitude, and put his fingers into\l"
    .string "his ears, and he spit, and touched\l"
    .string "his tongue;"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_34::
    .string "And looking up to heaven, he\n"
    .string "sighed, and saith unto him,\l"
    .string "Ephphatha, that is, Be opened$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_35::
    .string "And straightway his ears were\n"
    .string "opened, and the string of his tongue\l"
    .string "was loosed, and he spake plain.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_36::
    .string "And he charged them that they\n"
    .string "should tell no man: but the more he\l"
    .string "charged them, so much the more a\l"
    .string "great deal they published it;"
Bible_Text_Mark_7_37::
    .string "And were beyond measure astonished,\n"
    .string "saying, He hath done all things\l"
    .string "well: he maketh both the deaf to\l"
    .string "hear, and the dumb to speak$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_1::
    .string "In those days the multitude being\n"
    .string "very great, and having nothing to\l"
    .string "eat, Jesus called his disciples\l"
    .string "unto him, and saith unto them,"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_2::
    .string "I have compassion on the\n"
    .string "multitude, because they have now\l"
    .string "been with me three days, and have\l"
    .string "nothing to eat:"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_3::
    .string "And if I send them away fasting to\n"
    .string "their own houses, they will faint by\l"
    .string "the way: for divers of them came from\l"
    .string "far$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_4::
    .string "And his disciples answered him,\n"
    .string "From whence can a man satisfy these\l"
    .string "men with bread here in the\l"
    .string "wilderness?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_5::
    .string "And he asked them, How many loaves\n"
    .string "have ye? And they said, Seven$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_6::
    .string "And he commanded the people to sit\n"
    .string "down on the ground: and he took the\l"
    .string "seven loaves, and gave thanks, and\l"
    .string "brake, and gave to his disciples to\l"
    .string "set before them; and they did set\l"
    .string "them before the people.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_7::
    .string "And they had a few small fishes:\n"
    .string "and he blessed, and commanded to set\l"
    .string "them also before them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_8::
    .string "So they did eat, and were filled:\n"
    .string "and they took up of the broken meat\l"
    .string "that was left seven baskets.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_9::
    .string "And they that had eaten were about\n"
    .string "four thousand: and he sent them away.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_10::
    .string "And straightway he entered into a\n"
    .string "ship with his disciples, and came\l"
    .string "into the parts of Dalmanutha.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_11::
    .string "And the Pharisees came forth, and\n"
    .string "began to question with him, seeking\l"
    .string "of him a sign from heaven, tempting\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_12::
    .string "And he sighed deeply in his\n"
    .string "spirit, and saith, Why doth this\l"
    .string "generation seek after a sign? verily\l"
    .string "I say unto you, There shall no sign\l"
    .string "be given unto this generation.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_13::
    .string "And he left them, and entering into\n"
    .string "the ship again departed to the\l"
    .string "other side.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_14::
    .string "Now the disciples had forgotten to\n"
    .string "take bread, neither had they in the\l"
    .string "ship with them more than one loaf.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_15::
    .string "And he charged them, saying, Take\n"
    .string "heed, beware of the leaven of the\l"
    .string "Pharisees, and of the leaven of\l"
    .string "Herod.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_16::
    .string "And they reasoned among themselves,\n"
    .string "saying, It is because we have no\l"
    .string "bread.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_17::
    .string "And when Jesus knew it, he saith\n"
    .string "unto them, Why reason ye, because ye\l"
    .string "have no bread? perceive ye not yet,\l"
    .string "neither understand? have ye your\l"
    .string "heart yet hardened?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_18::
    .string "Having eyes, see ye not? and having\n"
    .string "ears, hear ye not? and do ye not\l"
    .string "remember?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_19::
    .string "When I brake the five loaves among\n"
    .string "five thousand, how many baskets\l"
    .string "full of fragments took ye up? They\l"
    .string "say unto him, Twelve$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_20::
    .string "And when the seven among four\n"
    .string "thousand, how many baskets full of\l"
    .string "fragments took ye up? And they said,\l"
    .string "Seven.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_21::
    .string "And he said unto them, How is it that\n"
    .string "ye do not understand?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_22::
    .string "And he cometh to Bethsaida; and they\n"
    .string "bring a blind man unto him, and\l"
    .string "besought him to touch him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_23::
    .string "And he took the blind man by the\n"
    .string "hand, and led him out of the town;\l"
    .string "and when he had spit on his eyes, and\l"
    .string "put his hands upon him, he asked him\l"
    .string "if he saw ought.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_24::
    .string "And he looked up, and said, I see\n"
    .string "men as trees, walking.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_25::
    .string "After that he put his hands again\n"
    .string "upon his eyes, and made him look\l"
    .string "up: and he was restored, and saw\l"
    .string "every man clearly.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_26::
    .string "And he sent him away to his house,\n"
    .string "saying, Neither go into the town, nor\l"
    .string "tell it to any in the town.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_27::
    .string "And Jesus went out, and his\n"
    .string "disciples, into the towns of\l"
    .string "Caesarea Philippi: and by the way\l"
    .string "he asked his disciples, saying unto\l"
    .string "them, Whom do men say that I am?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_28::
    .string "And they answered, John the\n"
    .string "Baptist; but some say, Elias; and\l"
    .string "others, One of the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_29::
    .string "And he saith unto them, But whom say\n"
    .string "ye that I am? And Peter answereth and\l"
    .string "saith unto him, Thou art the Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_30::
    .string "And he charged them that they\n"
    .string "should tell no man of him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_31::
    .string "And he began to teach them, that the\n"
    .string "Son of man must suffer many things,\l"
    .string "and be rejected of the elders, and of\l"
    .string "the chief priests, and scribes, and\l"
    .string "be killed, and after three days rise\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_32::
    .string "And he spake that saying openly.\n"
    .string "And Peter took him, and began to\l"
    .string "rebuke him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_33::
    .string "But when he had turned about and\n"
    .string "looked on his disciples, he rebuked\l"
    .string "Peter, saying, Get thee behind me,\l"
    .string "Satan: for thou savourest not the\l"
    .string "things that be of God, but the things\l"
    .string "that be of men.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_34::
    .string "And when he had called the\n"
    .string "people unto him with his disciples\l"
    .string "also, he said unto them, Whosoever\l"
    .string "will come after me, let him deny\l"
    .string "himself, and take up his cross, and\l"
    .string "follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_35::
    .string "For whosoever will save his life\n"
    .string "shall lose it; but whosoever\l"
    .string "shall lose his life for my sake\l"
    .string "and the gospel’s, the same shall\l"
    .string "save it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_36::
    .string "For what shall it profit a man, if\n"
    .string "he shall gain the whole world, and\l"
    .string "lose his own soul?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_37::
    .string "Or what shall a man give in\n"
    .string "exchange for his soul?"
Bible_Text_Mark_8_38::
    .string "Whosoever therefore shall be\n"
    .string "ashamed of me and of my words in this\l"
    .string "adulterous and sinful generation;\l"
    .string "of him also shall the Son of man be\l"
    .string "ashamed, when he cometh in the glory\l"
    .string "of his Father with the holy angels$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_1::
    .string "And he said unto them, Verily I say\n"
    .string "unto you, That there be some of them\l"
    .string "that stand here, which shall not\l"
    .string "taste of death, till they have seen\l"
    .string "the kingdom of God come with power.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_2::
    .string "And after six days Jesus taketh with\n"
    .string "him Peter, and James, and John, and\l"
    .string "leadeth them up into an high\l"
    .string "mountain apart by themselves: and\l"
    .string "he was transfigured before them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_3::
    .string "And his raiment became shining,\n"
    .string "exceeding white as snow; so as no\l"
    .string "fuller on earth can white them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_4::
    .string "And there appeared unto them\n"
    .string "Elias with Moses: and they were\l"
    .string "talking with Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_5::
    .string "And Peter answered and said to\n"
    .string "Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be\l"
    .string "here: and let us make three\l"
    .string "tabernacles; one for thee, and one\l"
    .string "for Moses, and one for Elias.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_6::
    .string "For he wist not what to say; for they\n"
    .string "were sore afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_7::
    .string "And there was a cloud that\n"
    .string "overshadowed them: and a voice came\l"
    .string "out of the cloud, saying, This is my\l"
    .string "beloved Son: hear him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_8::
    .string "And suddenly, when they had looked\n"
    .string "round about, they saw no man any\l"
    .string "more, save Jesus only with\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_9::
    .string "And as they came down from the\n"
    .string "mountain, he charged them that they\l"
    .string "should tell no man what things they\l"
    .string "had seen, till the Son of man were\l"
    .string "risen from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_10::
    .string "And they kept that saying with\n"
    .string "themselves, questioning one with\l"
    .string "another what the rising from the dead\l"
    .string "should mean.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_11::
    .string "And they asked him, saying, Why say\n"
    .string "the scribes that Elias must first\l"
    .string "come?"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_12::
    .string "And he answered and told them,\n"
    .string "Elias verily cometh first, and\l"
    .string "restoreth all things; and how it is\l"
    .string "written of the Son of man, that he\l"
    .string "must suffer many things, and be set\l"
    .string "at nought$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_13::
    .string "But I say unto you, That Elias is\n"
    .string "indeed come, and they have done unto\l"
    .string "him whatsoever they listed, as it is\l"
    .string "written of him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_14::
    .string "And when he came to his disciples,\n"
    .string "he saw a great multitude about them,\l"
    .string "and the scribes questioning with\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_15::
    .string "And straightway all the people,\n"
    .string "when they beheld him, were greatly\l"
    .string "amazed, and running to him saluted\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_16::
    .string "And he asked the scribes, What\n"
    .string "question ye with them?"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_17::
    .string "And one of the multitude answered\n"
    .string "and said, Master, I have brought unto\l"
    .string "thee my son, which hath a dumb\l"
    .string "spirit;"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_18::
    .string "And wheresoever he taketh him, he\n"
    .string "teareth him: and he foameth, and\l"
    .string "gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth\l"
    .string "away: and I spake to thy disciples\l"
    .string "that they should cast him out; and\l"
    .string "they could not$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_19::
    .string "He answereth him, and saith, O\n"
    .string "faithless generation, how long\l"
    .string "shall I be with you? how long\l"
    .string "shall I suffer you? bring him unto\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_20::
    .string "And they brought him unto him: and\n"
    .string "when he saw him, straightway the\l"
    .string "spirit tare him; and he fell on the\l"
    .string "ground, and wallowed foaming.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_21::
    .string "And he asked his father, How long is\n"
    .string "it ago since this came unto him? And\l"
    .string "he said, Of a child.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_22::
    .string "And ofttimes it hath cast him into\n"
    .string "the fire, and into the waters, to\l"
    .string "destroy him: but if thou canst do any\l"
    .string "thing, have compassion on us, and\l"
    .string "help us.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_23::
    .string "Jesus said unto him, If thou canst\n"
    .string "believe, all things are possible\l"
    .string "to him that believeth.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_24::
    .string "And straightway the father of the\n"
    .string "child cried out, and said with\l"
    .string "tears, Lord, I believe; help thou\l"
    .string "mine unbelief.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_25::
    .string "When Jesus saw that the people\n"
    .string "came running together, he rebuked the\l"
    .string "foul spirit, saying unto him, Thou\l"
    .string "dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee,\l"
    .string "come out of him, and enter no more\l"
    .string "into him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_26::
    .string "And the spirit cried, and rent him\n"
    .string "sore, and came out of him: and he was\l"
    .string "as one dead; insomuch that many said,\l"
    .string "He is dead.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_27::
    .string "But Jesus took him by the hand, and\n"
    .string "lifted him up; and he arose.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_28::
    .string "And when he was come into the house,\n"
    .string "his disciples asked him privately,\l"
    .string "Why could not we cast him out?"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_29::
    .string "And he said unto them, This kind can\n"
    .string "come forth by nothing, but by prayer\l"
    .string "and fasting$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_30::
    .string "And they departed thence, and\n"
    .string "passed through Galilee; and he\l"
    .string "would not that any man should know\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_31::
    .string "For he taught his disciples, and\n"
    .string "said unto them, The Son of man is\l"
    .string "delivered into the hands of men, and\l"
    .string "they shall kill him; and after\l"
    .string "that he is killed, he shall rise\l"
    .string "the third day.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_32::
    .string "But they understood not that saying,\n"
    .string "and were afraid to ask him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_33::
    .string "And he came to Capernaum: and being\n"
    .string "in the house he asked them, What was\l"
    .string "it that ye disputed among\l"
    .string "yourselves by the way?"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_34::
    .string "But they held their peace: for by\n"
    .string "the way they had disputed among\l"
    .string "themselves, who should be the\l"
    .string "greatest$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_35::
    .string "And he sat down, and called the\n"
    .string "twelve, and saith unto them, If any\l"
    .string "man desire to be first, the same\l"
    .string "shall be last of all, and servant\l"
    .string "of all.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_36::
    .string "And he took a child, and set him in\n"
    .string "the midst of them: and when he had\l"
    .string "taken him in his arms, he said unto\l"
    .string "them,"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_37::
    .string "Whosoever shall receive one of\n"
    .string "such children in my name, receiveth\l"
    .string "me: and whosoever shall receive me,\l"
    .string "receiveth not me, but him that sent me$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_38::
    .string "And John answered him, saying,\n"
    .string "Master, we saw one casting out\l"
    .string "devils in thy name, and he\l"
    .string "followeth not us: and we forbad him,\l"
    .string "because he followeth not us.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_39::
    .string "But Jesus said, Forbid him not: for\n"
    .string "there is no man which shall do a\l"
    .string "miracle in my name, that can\l"
    .string "lightly speak evil of me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_40::
    .string "For he that is not against us is on\n"
    .string "our part.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_41::
    .string "For whosoever shall give you a cup\n"
    .string "of water to drink in my name, because\l"
    .string "ye belong to Christ, verily I say\l"
    .string "unto you, he shall not lose his\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_42::
    .string "And whosoever shall offend one of\n"
    .string "these little ones that believe in\l"
    .string "me, it is better for him that a\l"
    .string "millstone were hanged about his\l"
    .string "neck, and he were cast into the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_43::
    .string "And if thy hand offend thee, cut it\n"
    .string "off: it is better for thee to enter\l"
    .string "into life maimed, than having two\l"
    .string "hands to go into hell, into the fire\l"
    .string "that never shall be quenched:"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_44::
    .string "Where their worm dieth not, and the\n"
    .string "fire is not quenched$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_45::
    .string "And if thy foot offend thee, cut it\n"
    .string "off: it is better for thee to enter\l"
    .string "halt into life, than having two feet\l"
    .string "to be cast into hell, into the fire\l"
    .string "that never shall be quenched:"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_46::
    .string "Where their worm dieth not, and the\n"
    .string "fire is not quenched$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_47::
    .string "And if thine eye offend thee, pluck\n"
    .string "it out: it is better for thee to enter\l"
    .string "into the kingdom of God with one eye,\l"
    .string "than having two eyes to be cast into\l"
    .string "hell fire:"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_48::
    .string "Where their worm dieth not, and the\n"
    .string "fire is not quenched$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_49::
    .string "For every one shall be salted with\n"
    .string "fire, and every sacrifice shall be\l"
    .string "salted with salt.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_9_50::
    .string "Salt is good: but if the salt have\n"
    .string "lost his saltness, wherewith will\l"
    .string "ye season it? Have salt in\l"
    .string "yourselves, and have peace one with\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_1::
    .string "And he arose from thence, and cometh\n"
    .string "into the coasts of Judaea by the\l"
    .string "farther side of Jordan: and the\l"
    .string "people resort unto him again; and,\l"
    .string "as he was wont, he taught them again.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_2::
    .string "And the Pharisees came to him, and\n"
    .string "asked him, Is it lawful for a man to\l"
    .string "put away his wife? tempting him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_3::
    .string "And he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "What did Moses command you?"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_4::
    .string "And they said, Moses suffered to\n"
    .string "write a bill of divorcement, and to\l"
    .string "put her away$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_5::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, For the hardness of your heart\l"
    .string "he wrote you this precept.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_6::
    .string "But from the beginning of the\n"
    .string "creation God made them male and\l"
    .string "female.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_7::
    .string "For this cause shall a man leave\n"
    .string "his father and mother, and cleave to\l"
    .string "his wife;"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_8::
    .string "And they twain shall be one flesh:\n"
    .string "so then they are no more twain, but\l"
    .string "one flesh$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_9::
    .string "What therefore God hath joined\n"
    .string "together, let not man put asunder.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_10::
    .string "And in the house his disciples\n"
    .string "asked him again of the same matter.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_11::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Whosoever\n"
    .string "shall put away his wife, and marry\l"
    .string "another, committeth adultery\l"
    .string "against her.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_12::
    .string "And if a woman shall put away her\n"
    .string "husband, and be married to another,\l"
    .string "she committeth adultery.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_13::
    .string "And they brought young children to\n"
    .string "him, that he should touch them: and\l"
    .string "his disciples rebuked those that\l"
    .string "brought them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_14::
    .string "But when Jesus saw it, he was much\n"
    .string "displeased, and said unto them,\l"
    .string "Suffer the little children to come\l"
    .string "unto me, and forbid them not: for of\l"
    .string "such is the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_15::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Whosoever\n"
    .string "shall not receive the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God as a little child, he shall\l"
    .string "not enter therein.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_16::
    .string "And he took them up in his arms,\n"
    .string "put his hands upon them, and blessed\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_17::
    .string "And when he was gone forth into the\n"
    .string "way, there came one running, and\l"
    .string "kneeled to him, and asked him, Good\l"
    .string "Master, what shall I do that I may\l"
    .string "inherit eternal life?"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_18::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Why\n"
    .string "callest thou me good? there is none\l"
    .string "good but one, that is, God$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_19::
    .string "Thou knowest the commandments, Do\n"
    .string "not commit adultery, Do not kill,\l"
    .string "Do not steal, Do not bear false\l"
    .string "witness, Defraud not, Honour thy\l"
    .string "father and mother."
Bible_Text_Mark_10_20::
    .string "And he answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Master, all these have I observed\l"
    .string "from my youth$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_21::
    .string "Then Jesus beholding him loved\n"
    .string "him, and said unto him, One thing\l"
    .string "thou lackest: go thy way, sell\l"
    .string "whatsoever thou hast, and give to the\l"
    .string "poor, and thou shalt have treasure\l"
    .string "in heaven: and come, take up the\l"
    .string "cross, and follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_22::
    .string "And he was sad at that saying, and\n"
    .string "went away grieved: for he had great\l"
    .string "possessions.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_23::
    .string "And Jesus looked round about, and\n"
    .string "saith unto his disciples, How\l"
    .string "hardly shall they that have riches\l"
    .string "enter into the kingdom of God!"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_24::
    .string "And the disciples were astonished\n"
    .string "at his words. But Jesus answereth\l"
    .string "again, and saith unto them,\l"
    .string "Children, how hard is it for them\l"
    .string "that trust in riches to enter into\l"
    .string "the kingdom of God!"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_25::
    .string "It is easier for a camel to go\n"
    .string "through the eye of a needle, than for\l"
    .string "a rich man to enter into the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_26::
    .string "And they were astonished out of\n"
    .string "measure, saying among themselves,\l"
    .string "Who then can be saved?"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_27::
    .string "And Jesus looking upon them saith,\n"
    .string "With men it is impossible, but not\l"
    .string "with God: for with God all things\l"
    .string "are possible$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_28::
    .string "Then Peter began to say unto him,\n"
    .string "Lo, we have left all, and have\l"
    .string "followed thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_29::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said, Verily\n"
    .string "I say unto you, There is no man that\l"
    .string "hath left house, or brethren, or\l"
    .string "sisters, or father, or mother, or\l"
    .string "wife, or children, or lands, for my\l"
    .string "sake, and the gospel’s,"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_30::
    .string "But he shall receive an\n"
    .string "hundredfold now in this time,\l"
    .string "houses, and brethren, and sisters,\l"
    .string "and mothers, and children, and\l"
    .string "lands, with persecutions; and in the\l"
    .string "world to come eternal life$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_31::
    .string "But many that are first shall be\n"
    .string "last; and the last first.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_32::
    .string "And they were in the way going up to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem; and Jesus went before\l"
    .string "them: and they were amazed; and as\l"
    .string "they followed, they were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_33::
    .string "Saying, Behold, we go up to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall\l"
    .string "be delivered unto the chief\l"
    .string "priests, and unto the scribes; and\l"
    .string "they shall condemn him to death, and\l"
    .string "shall deliver him to the Gentiles:"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_34::
    .string "And they shall mock him, and\n"
    .string "shall scourge him, and shall spit\l"
    .string "upon him, and shall kill him: and\l"
    .string "the third day he shall rise again$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_35::
    .string "And James and John, the sons of\n"
    .string "Zebedee, come unto him, saying,\l"
    .string "Master, we would that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest do for us whatsoever we\l"
    .string "shall desire.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_36::
    .string "And he said unto them, What would ye\n"
    .string "that I should do for you?"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_37::
    .string "They said unto him, Grant unto us\n"
    .string "that we may sit, one on thy right\l"
    .string "hand, and the other on thy left hand,\l"
    .string "in thy glory$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_38::
    .string "But Jesus said unto them, Ye know\n"
    .string "not what ye ask: can ye drink of the\l"
    .string "cup that I drink of? and be baptized\l"
    .string "with the baptism that I am baptized\l"
    .string "with?"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_39::
    .string "And they said unto him, We can. And\n"
    .string "Jesus said unto them, Ye shall\l"
    .string "indeed drink of the cup that I drink\l"
    .string "of; and with the baptism that I am\l"
    .string "baptized withal shall ye be\l"
    .string "baptized:"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_40::
    .string "But to sit on my right hand and on my\n"
    .string "left hand is not mine to give; but it\l"
    .string "shall be given to them for whom it\l"
    .string "is prepared$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_41::
    .string "And when the ten heard it, they\n"
    .string "began to be much displeased with\l"
    .string "James and John.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_42::
    .string "But Jesus called them to him, and\n"
    .string "saith unto them, Ye know that they\l"
    .string "which are accounted to rule over the\l"
    .string "Gentiles exercise lordship over\l"
    .string "them; and their great ones exercise\l"
    .string "authority upon them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_43::
    .string "But so shall it not be among you:\n"
    .string "but whosoever will be great among\l"
    .string "you, shall be your minister:"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_44::
    .string "And whosoever of you will be the\n"
    .string "chiefest, shall be servant of all$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_45::
    .string "For even the Son of man came not to\n"
    .string "be ministered unto, but to minister,\l"
    .string "and to give his life a ransom for\l"
    .string "many.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_46::
    .string "And they came to Jericho: and as he\n"
    .string "went out of Jericho with his\l"
    .string "disciples and a great number of\l"
    .string "people, blind Bartimaeus, the son\l"
    .string "of Timaeus, sat by the highway side\l"
    .string "begging.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_47::
    .string "And when he heard that it was Jesus\n"
    .string "of Nazareth, he began to cry out, and\l"
    .string "say, Jesus, thou son of David, have\l"
    .string "mercy on me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_48::
    .string "And many charged him that he should\n"
    .string "hold his peace: but he cried the\l"
    .string "more a great deal, Thou son of David,\l"
    .string "have mercy on me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_49::
    .string "And Jesus stood still, and\n"
    .string "commanded him to be called. And they\l"
    .string "call the blind man, saying unto\l"
    .string "him, Be of good comfort, rise; he\l"
    .string "calleth thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_50::
    .string "And he, casting away his garment,\n"
    .string "rose, and came to Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_51::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "him, What wilt thou that I should do\l"
    .string "unto thee? The blind man said unto\l"
    .string "him, Lord, that I might receive my\l"
    .string "sight.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_10_52::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Go thy way;\n"
    .string "thy faith hath made thee whole. And\l"
    .string "immediately he received his sight,\l"
    .string "and followed Jesus in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_1::
    .string "And when they came nigh to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, unto Bethphage and\l"
    .string "Bethany, at the mount of Olives, he\l"
    .string "sendeth forth two of his disciples,"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_2::
    .string "And saith unto them, Go your way\n"
    .string "into the village over against you:\l"
    .string "and as soon as ye be entered into it,\l"
    .string "ye shall find a colt tied, whereon\l"
    .string "never man sat; loose him, and bring\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_3::
    .string "And if any man say unto you, Why do\n"
    .string "ye this? say ye that the Lord hath\l"
    .string "need of him; and straightway he will\l"
    .string "send him hither.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_4::
    .string "And they went their way, and found\n"
    .string "the colt tied by the door without in\l"
    .string "a place where two ways met; and they\l"
    .string "loose him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_5::
    .string "And certain of them that stood there\n"
    .string "said unto them, What do ye, loosing\l"
    .string "the colt?"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_6::
    .string "And they said unto them even as\n"
    .string "Jesus had commanded: and they let\l"
    .string "them go$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_7::
    .string "And they brought the colt to Jesus,\n"
    .string "and cast their garments on him; and\l"
    .string "he sat upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_8::
    .string "And many spread their garments in\n"
    .string "the way: and others cut down branches\l"
    .string "off the trees, and strawed them in\l"
    .string "the way.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_9::
    .string "And they that went before, and they\n"
    .string "that followed, cried, saying,\l"
    .string "Hosanna; Blessed is he that cometh\l"
    .string "in the name of the Lord:"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_10::
    .string "Blessed be the kingdom of our\n"
    .string "father David, that cometh in the name\l"
    .string "of the Lord: Hosanna in the highest$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_11::
    .string "And Jesus entered into Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and into the temple: and when he had\l"
    .string "looked round about upon all things,\l"
    .string "and now the eventide was come, he\l"
    .string "went out unto Bethany with the\l"
    .string "twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_12::
    .string "And on the morrow, when they were\n"
    .string "come from Bethany, he was hungry:"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_13::
    .string "And seeing a fig tree afar off\n"
    .string "having leaves, he came, if haply he\l"
    .string "might find any thing thereon: and\l"
    .string "when he came to it, he found nothing\l"
    .string "but leaves; for the time of figs was\l"
    .string "not yet$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_14::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto it,\n"
    .string "No man eat fruit of thee hereafter\l"
    .string "for ever. And his disciples heard\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_15::
    .string "And they come to Jerusalem: and\n"
    .string "Jesus went into the temple, and\l"
    .string "began to cast out them that sold and\l"
    .string "bought in the temple, and overthrew\l"
    .string "the tables of the moneychangers, and\l"
    .string "the seats of them that sold doves;"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_16::
    .string "And would not suffer that any man\n"
    .string "should carry any vessel through the\l"
    .string "temple$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_17::
    .string "And he taught, saying unto them, Is\n"
    .string "it not written, My house shall be\l"
    .string "called of all nations the house of\l"
    .string "prayer? but ye have made it a den of\l"
    .string "thieves.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_18::
    .string "And the scribes and chief priests\n"
    .string "heard it, and sought how they might\l"
    .string "destroy him: for they feared him,\l"
    .string "because all the people was\l"
    .string "astonished at his doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_19::
    .string "And when even was come, he went out\n"
    .string "of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_20::
    .string "And in the morning, as they passed\n"
    .string "by, they saw the fig tree dried up\l"
    .string "from the roots.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_21::
    .string "And Peter calling to remembrance\n"
    .string "saith unto him, Master, behold, the\l"
    .string "fig tree which thou cursedst is\l"
    .string "withered away.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_22::
    .string "And Jesus answering saith unto them,\n"
    .string "Have faith in God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_23::
    .string "For verily I say unto you, That\n"
    .string "whosoever shall say unto this\l"
    .string "mountain, Be thou removed, and be\l"
    .string "thou cast into the sea; and shall\l"
    .string "not doubt in his heart, but shall\l"
    .string "believe that those things which he\l"
    .string "saith shall come to pass; he shall\l"
    .string "have whatsoever he saith.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_24::
    .string "Therefore I say unto you, What\n"
    .string "things soever ye desire, when ye\l"
    .string "pray, believe that ye receive them,\l"
    .string "and ye shall have them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_25::
    .string "And when ye stand praying, forgive,\n"
    .string "if ye have ought against any: that\l"
    .string "your Father also which is in heaven\l"
    .string "may forgive you your trespasses.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_26::
    .string "But if ye do not forgive, neither\n"
    .string "will your Father which is in heaven\l"
    .string "forgive your trespasses.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_27::
    .string "And they come again to Jerusalem:\n"
    .string "and as he was walking in the\l"
    .string "temple, there come to him the chief\l"
    .string "priests, and the scribes, and the\l"
    .string "elders,"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_28::
    .string "And say unto him, By what authority\n"
    .string "doest thou these things? and who gave\l"
    .string "thee this authority to do these\l"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_29::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, I will also ask of you one\l"
    .string "question, and answer me, and I will\l"
    .string "tell you by what authority I do\l"
    .string "these things$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_30::
    .string "The baptism of John, was it from\n"
    .string "heaven, or of men? answer me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_31::
    .string "And they reasoned with themselves,\n"
    .string "saying, If we shall say, From\l"
    .string "heaven; he will say, Why then did ye\l"
    .string "not believe him?"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_32::
    .string "But if we shall say, Of men; they\n"
    .string "feared the people: for all men\l"
    .string "counted John, that he was a prophet\l"
    .string "indeed$"
Bible_Text_Mark_11_33::
    .string "And they answered and said unto\n"
    .string "Jesus, We cannot tell. And Jesus\l"
    .string "answering saith unto them, Neither do\l"
    .string "I tell you by what authority I do\l"
    .string "these things.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_1::
    .string "And he began to speak unto them by\n"
    .string "parables. A certain man planted a\l"
    .string "vineyard, and set an hedge about it,\l"
    .string "and digged a place for the winefat,\l"
    .string "and built a tower, and let it out to\l"
    .string "husbandmen, and went into a far\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_2::
    .string "And at the season he sent to the\n"
    .string "husbandmen a servant, that he might\l"
    .string "receive from the husbandmen of the\l"
    .string "fruit of the vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_3::
    .string "And they caught him, and beat him,\n"
    .string "and sent him away empty.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_4::
    .string "And again he sent unto them another\n"
    .string "servant; and at him they cast stones,\l"
    .string "and wounded him in the head, and sent\l"
    .string "him away shamefully handled.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_5::
    .string "And again he sent another; and him\n"
    .string "they killed, and many others;\l"
    .string "beating some, and killing some.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_6::
    .string "Having yet therefore one son, his\n"
    .string "wellbeloved, he sent him also\l"
    .string "last unto them, saying, They will\l"
    .string "reverence my son.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_7::
    .string "But those husbandmen said among\n"
    .string "themselves, This is the heir; come,\l"
    .string "let us kill him, and the inheritance\l"
    .string "shall be ours.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_8::
    .string "And they took him, and killed him,\n"
    .string "and cast him out of the vineyard.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_9::
    .string "What shall therefore the lord of\n"
    .string "the vineyard do? he will come and\l"
    .string "destroy the husbandmen, and will\l"
    .string "give the vineyard unto others.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_10::
    .string "And have ye not read this\n"
    .string "scripture; The stone which the\l"
    .string "builders rejected is become the head\l"
    .string "of the corner:"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_11::
    .string "This was the Lord’s doing, and it is\n"
    .string "marvellous in our eyes?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_12::
    .string "And they sought to lay hold on him,\n"
    .string "but feared the people: for they\l"
    .string "knew that he had spoken the parable\l"
    .string "against them: and they left him, and\l"
    .string "went their way$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_13::
    .string "And they send unto him certain of\n"
    .string "the Pharisees and of the Herodians,\l"
    .string "to catch him in his words.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_14::
    .string "And when they were come, they say\n"
    .string "unto him, Master, we know that thou\l"
    .string "art true, and carest for no man: for\l"
    .string "thou regardest not the person of\l"
    .string "men, but teachest the way of God in\l"
    .string "truth: Is it lawful to give tribute\l"
    .string "to Caesar, or not?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_15::
    .string "Shall we give, or shall we not\n"
    .string "give? But he, knowing their\l"
    .string "hypocrisy, said unto them, Why\l"
    .string "tempt ye me? bring me a penny, that\l"
    .string "I may see it$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_16::
    .string "And they brought it. And he saith\n"
    .string "unto them, Whose is this image and\l"
    .string "superscription? And they said unto\l"
    .string "him, Caesar’s.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_17::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "Render to Caesar the things that are\l"
    .string "Caesar’s, and to God the things that\l"
    .string "are God’s. And they marvelled at\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_18::
    .string "Then come unto him the Sadducees,\n"
    .string "which say there is no resurrection;\l"
    .string "and they asked him, saying,"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_19::
    .string "Master, Moses wrote unto us, If a\n"
    .string "man’s brother die, and leave his\l"
    .string "wife behind him, and leave no\l"
    .string "children, that his brother should\l"
    .string "take his wife, and raise up seed unto\l"
    .string "his brother$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_20::
    .string "Now there were seven brethren: and\n"
    .string "the first took a wife, and dying left\l"
    .string "no seed.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_21::
    .string "And the second took her, and died,\n"
    .string "neither left he any seed: and the\l"
    .string "third likewise.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_22::
    .string "And the seven had her, and left no\n"
    .string "seed: last of all the woman died\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_23::
    .string "In the resurrection therefore, when\n"
    .string "they shall rise, whose wife shall\l"
    .string "she be of them? for the seven had her\l"
    .string "to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_24::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "Do ye not therefore err, because ye\l"
    .string "know not the scriptures, neither the\l"
    .string "power of God?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_25::
    .string "For when they shall rise from the\n"
    .string "dead, they neither marry, nor are\l"
    .string "given in marriage; but are as the\l"
    .string "angels which are in heaven$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_26::
    .string "And as touching the dead, that they\n"
    .string "rise: have ye not read in the book of\l"
    .string "Moses, how in the bush God spake unto\l"
    .string "him, saying, I am the God of Abraham,\l"
    .string "and the God of Isaac, and the God of\l"
    .string "Jacob?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_27::
    .string "He is not the God of the dead, but\n"
    .string "the God of the living: ye therefore\l"
    .string "do greatly err$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_28::
    .string "And one of the scribes came, and\n"
    .string "having heard them reasoning\l"
    .string "together, and perceiving that he had\l"
    .string "answered them well, asked him,\l"
    .string "Which is the first commandment of\l"
    .string "all?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_29::
    .string "And Jesus answered him, The first of\n"
    .string "all the commandments is, Hear, O\l"
    .string "Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord:"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_30::
    .string "And thou shalt love the Lord thy\n"
    .string "God with all thy heart, and with\l"
    .string "all thy soul, and with all thy\l"
    .string "mind, and with all thy strength:\l"
    .string "this is the first commandment$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_31::
    .string "And the second is like, namely\n"
    .string "this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour\l"
    .string "as thyself. There is none other\l"
    .string "commandment greater than these.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_32::
    .string "And the scribe said unto him, Well,\n"
    .string "Master, thou hast said the truth: for\l"
    .string "there is one God; and there is none\l"
    .string "other but he:"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_33::
    .string "And to love him with all the\n"
    .string "heart, and with all the\l"
    .string "understanding, and with all the\l"
    .string "soul, and with all the strength,\l"
    .string "and to love his neighbour as\l"
    .string "himself, is more than all whole\l"
    .string "burnt offerings and sacrifices$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_34::
    .string "And when Jesus saw that he answered\n"
    .string "discreetly, he said unto him, Thou\l"
    .string "art not far from the kingdom of God.\l"
    .string "And no man after that durst ask him\l"
    .string "any question.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_35::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said, while\n"
    .string "he taught in the temple, How say the\l"
    .string "scribes that Christ is the son of\l"
    .string "David?"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_36::
    .string "For David himself said by the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost, The LORD said to my Lord, Sit\l"
    .string "thou on my right hand, till I make\l"
    .string "thine enemies thy footstool$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_37::
    .string "David therefore himself calleth\n"
    .string "him Lord; and whence is he then his\l"
    .string "son? And the common people heard\l"
    .string "him gladly.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_38::
    .string "And he said unto them in his\n"
    .string "doctrine, Beware of the scribes,\l"
    .string "which love to go in long clothing,\l"
    .string "and love salutations in the\l"
    .string "marketplaces,"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_39::
    .string "And the chief seats in the\n"
    .string "synagogues, and the uppermost rooms\l"
    .string "at feasts:"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_40::
    .string "Which devour widows’ houses, and for\n"
    .string "a pretence make long prayers: these\l"
    .string "shall receive greater damnation$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_41::
    .string "And Jesus sat over against the\n"
    .string "treasury, and beheld how the\l"
    .string "people cast money into the\l"
    .string "treasury: and many that were rich\l"
    .string "cast in much.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_42::
    .string "And there came a certain poor\n"
    .string "widow, and she threw in two mites,\l"
    .string "which make a farthing.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_43::
    .string "And he called unto him his\n"
    .string "disciples, and saith unto them,\l"
    .string "Verily I say unto you, That this\l"
    .string "poor widow hath cast more in, than\l"
    .string "all they which have cast into the\l"
    .string "treasury:"
Bible_Text_Mark_12_44::
    .string "For all they did cast in of their\n"
    .string "abundance; but she of her want did\l"
    .string "cast in all that she had, even all\l"
    .string "her living$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_1::
    .string "And as he went out of the temple,\n"
    .string "one of his disciples saith unto him,\l"
    .string "Master, see what manner of stones and\l"
    .string "what buildings are here!"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_2::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "Seest thou these great buildings?\l"
    .string "there shall not be left one stone\l"
    .string "upon another, that shall not be\l"
    .string "thrown down$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_3::
    .string "And as he sat upon the mount of\n"
    .string "Olives over against the temple,\l"
    .string "Peter and James and John and Andrew\l"
    .string "asked him privately,"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_4::
    .string "Tell us, when shall these things\n"
    .string "be? and what shall be the sign when\l"
    .string "all these things shall be\l"
    .string "fulfilled?"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_5::
    .string "And Jesus answering them began to\n"
    .string "say, Take heed lest any man deceive\l"
    .string "you:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_6::
    .string "For many shall come in my name,\n"
    .string "saying, I am Christ; and shall\l"
    .string "deceive many$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_7::
    .string "And when ye shall hear of wars and\n"
    .string "rumours of wars, be ye not troubled:\l"
    .string "for such things must needs be; but\l"
    .string "the end shall not be yet.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_8::
    .string "For nation shall rise against\n"
    .string "nation, and kingdom against kingdom:\l"
    .string "and there shall be earthquakes in\l"
    .string "divers places, and there shall be\l"
    .string "famines and troubles: these are the\l"
    .string "beginnings of sorrows.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_9::
    .string "But take heed to yourselves: for\n"
    .string "they shall deliver you up to\l"
    .string "councils; and in the synagogues ye\l"
    .string "shall be beaten: and ye shall be\l"
    .string "brought before rulers and kings for\l"
    .string "my sake, for a testimony against them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_10::
    .string "And the gospel must first be\n"
    .string "published among all nations.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_11::
    .string "But when they shall lead you, and\n"
    .string "deliver you up, take no thought\l"
    .string "beforehand what ye shall speak,\l"
    .string "neither do ye premeditate: but\l"
    .string "whatsoever shall be given you in\l"
    .string "that hour, that speak ye: for it is\l"
    .string "not ye that speak, but the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_12::
    .string "Now the brother shall betray the\n"
    .string "brother to death, and the father the\l"
    .string "son; and children shall rise up\l"
    .string "against their parents, and shall\l"
    .string "cause them to be put to death.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_13::
    .string "And ye shall be hated of all men\n"
    .string "for my name’s sake: but he that\l"
    .string "shall endure unto the end, the same\l"
    .string "shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_14::
    .string "But when ye shall see the\n"
    .string "abomination of desolation, spoken\l"
    .string "of by Daniel the prophet, standing\l"
    .string "where it ought not, (let him that\l"
    .string "readeth understand,) then let them\l"
    .string "that be in Judaea flee to the\l"
    .string "mountains:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_15::
    .string "And let him that is on the housetop\n"
    .string "not go down into the house, neither\l"
    .string "enter therein, to take any thing out\l"
    .string "of his house:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_16::
    .string "And let him that is in the field\n"
    .string "not turn back again for to take up\l"
    .string "his garment$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_17::
    .string "But woe to them that are with child,\n"
    .string "and to them that give suck in those\l"
    .string "days!"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_18::
    .string "And pray ye that your flight be not\n"
    .string "in the winter$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_19::
    .string "For in those days shall be\n"
    .string "affliction, such as was not from the\l"
    .string "beginning of the creation which God\l"
    .string "created unto this time, neither\l"
    .string "shall be.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_20::
    .string "And except that the Lord had\n"
    .string "shortened those days, no flesh\l"
    .string "should be saved: but for the elect’s\l"
    .string "sake, whom he hath chosen, he hath\l"
    .string "shortened the days.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_21::
    .string "And then if any man shall say to\n"
    .string "you, Lo, here is Christ; or, lo, he is\l"
    .string "there; believe him not:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_22::
    .string "For false Christs and false\n"
    .string "prophets shall rise, and shall\l"
    .string "shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if\l"
    .string "it were possible, even the elect$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_23::
    .string "But take ye heed: behold, I have\n"
    .string "foretold you all things.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_24::
    .string "But in those days, after that\n"
    .string "tribulation, the sun shall be\l"
    .string "darkened, and the moon shall not\l"
    .string "give her light,"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_25::
    .string "And the stars of heaven shall\n"
    .string "fall, and the powers that are in\l"
    .string "heaven shall be shaken$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_26::
    .string "And then shall they see the Son of\n"
    .string "man coming in the clouds with great\l"
    .string "power and glory.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_27::
    .string "And then shall he send his angels,\n"
    .string "and shall gather together his\l"
    .string "elect from the four winds, from the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of the earth to the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_28::
    .string "Now learn a parable of the fig\n"
    .string "tree; When her branch is yet tender,\l"
    .string "and putteth forth leaves, ye know\l"
    .string "that summer is near:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_29::
    .string "So ye in like manner, when ye\n"
    .string "shall see these things come to\l"
    .string "pass, know that it is nigh, even at\l"
    .string "the doors$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_30::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, that this\n"
    .string "generation shall not pass, till\l"
    .string "all these things be done.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_31::
    .string "Heaven and earth shall pass away:\n"
    .string "but my words shall not pass away.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_32::
    .string "But of that day and that hour\n"
    .string "knoweth no man, no, not the angels\l"
    .string "which are in heaven, neither the Son,\l"
    .string "but the Father.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_33::
    .string "Take ye heed, watch and pray: for ye\n"
    .string "know not when the time is.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_34::
    .string "For the Son of Man is as a man taking\n"
    .string "a far journey, who left his house,\l"
    .string "and gave authority to his servants,\l"
    .string "and to every man his work, and\l"
    .string "commanded the porter to watch.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_35::
    .string "Watch ye therefore: for ye know not\n"
    .string "when the master of the house cometh,\l"
    .string "at even, or at midnight, or at the\l"
    .string "cockcrowing, or in the morning:"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_36::
    .string "Lest coming suddenly he find you\n"
    .string "sleeping$"
Bible_Text_Mark_13_37::
    .string "And what I say unto you I say unto\n"
    .string "all, Watch.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_1::
    .string "After two days was the feast of the\n"
    .string "passover, and of unleavened bread:\l"
    .string "and the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "scribes sought how they might take\l"
    .string "him by craft, and put him to death.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_2::
    .string "But they said, Not on the feast day,\n"
    .string "lest there be an uproar of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_3::
    .string "And being in Bethany in the house of\n"
    .string "Simon the leper, as he sat at meat,\l"
    .string "there came a woman having an\l"
    .string "alabaster box of ointment of\l"
    .string "spikenard very precious; and she\l"
    .string "brake the box, and poured it on his\l"
    .string "head.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_4::
    .string "And there were some that had\n"
    .string "indignation within themselves, and\l"
    .string "said, Why was this waste of the\l"
    .string "ointment made?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_5::
    .string "For it might have been sold for\n"
    .string "more than three hundred pence, and\l"
    .string "have been given to the poor. And they\l"
    .string "murmured against her$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_6::
    .string "And Jesus said, Let her alone; why\n"
    .string "trouble ye her? she hath wrought a\l"
    .string "good work on me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_7::
    .string "For ye have the poor with you\n"
    .string "always, and whensoever ye will ye\l"
    .string "may do them good: but me ye have not\l"
    .string "always.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_8::
    .string "She hath done what she could: she is\n"
    .string "come aforehand to anoint my body to\l"
    .string "the burying.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_9::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever\n"
    .string "this gospel shall be preached\l"
    .string "throughout the whole world, this\l"
    .string "also that she hath done shall be\l"
    .string "spoken of for a memorial of her.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_10::
    .string "And Judas Iscariot, one of the\n"
    .string "twelve, went unto the chief\l"
    .string "priests, to betray him unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_11::
    .string "And when they heard it, they were\n"
    .string "glad, and promised to give him money\l"
    .string " And he sought how he might\l"
    .string "conveniently betray him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_12::
    .string "And the first day of unleavened\n"
    .string "bread, when they killed the\l"
    .string "passover, his disciples said unto\l"
    .string "him, Where wilt thou that we go and\l"
    .string "prepare that thou mayest eat the\l"
    .string "passover?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_13::
    .string "And he sendeth forth two of his\n"
    .string "disciples, and saith unto them, Go\l"
    .string "ye into the city, and there shall\l"
    .string "meet you a man bearing a pitcher of\l"
    .string "water: follow him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_14::
    .string "And wheresoever he shall go in, say\n"
    .string "ye to the goodman of the house, The\l"
    .string "Master saith, Where is the\l"
    .string "guestchamber, where I shall eat the\l"
    .string "passover with my disciples?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_15::
    .string "And he will shew you a large\n"
    .string "upper room furnished and prepared:\l"
    .string "there make ready for us$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_16::
    .string "And his disciples went forth, and\n"
    .string "came into the city, and found as he\l"
    .string "had said unto them: and they made\l"
    .string "ready the passover.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_17::
    .string "And in the evening he cometh with\n"
    .string "the twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_18::
    .string "And as they sat and did eat, Jesus\n"
    .string "said, Verily I say unto you, One of\l"
    .string "you which eateth with me shall\l"
    .string "betray me.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_19::
    .string "And they began to be sorrowful, and\n"
    .string "to say unto him one by one, Is it I?\l"
    .string "and another said, Is it I?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_20::
    .string "And he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "It is one of the twelve, that\l"
    .string "dippeth with me in the dish$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_21::
    .string "The Son of man indeed goeth, as it is\n"
    .string "written of him: but woe to that man by\l"
    .string "whom the Son of man is betrayed! good\l"
    .string "were it for that man if he had never\l"
    .string "been born.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_22::
    .string "And as they did eat, Jesus took\n"
    .string "bread, and blessed, and brake it, and\l"
    .string "gave to them, and said, Take, eat:\l"
    .string "this is my body.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_23::
    .string "And he took the cup, and when he had\n"
    .string "given thanks, he gave it to them: and\l"
    .string "they all drank of it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_24::
    .string "And he said unto them, This is my\n"
    .string "blood of the new testament, which is\l"
    .string "shed for many.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_25::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, I will\n"
    .string "drink no more of the fruit of the\l"
    .string "vine, until that day that I drink it\l"
    .string "new in the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_26::
    .string "And when they had sung an hymn, they\n"
    .string "went out into the mount of Olives.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_27::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto them, All ye\n"
    .string "shall be offended because of me\l"
    .string "this night: for it is written, I\l"
    .string "will smite the shepherd, and the\l"
    .string "sheep shall be scattered.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_28::
    .string "But after that I am risen, I will\n"
    .string "go before you into Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_29::
    .string "But Peter said unto him, Although\n"
    .string "all shall be offended, yet will\l"
    .string "not I.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_30::
    .string "And Jesus saith unto him, Verily I\n"
    .string "say unto thee, That this day, even in\l"
    .string "this night, before the cock crow\l"
    .string "twice, thou shalt deny me thrice.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_31::
    .string "But he spake the more vehemently,\n"
    .string "If I should die with thee, I will\l"
    .string "not deny thee in any wise. Likewise\l"
    .string "also said they all.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_32::
    .string "And they came to a place which was\n"
    .string "named Gethsemane: and he saith to his\l"
    .string "disciples, Sit ye here, while I\l"
    .string "shall pray.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_33::
    .string "And he taketh with him Peter and\n"
    .string "James and John, and began to be sore\l"
    .string "amazed, and to be very heavy;"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_34::
    .string "And saith unto them, My soul is\n"
    .string "exceeding sorrowful unto death:\l"
    .string "tarry ye here, and watch$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_35::
    .string "And he went forward a little, and\n"
    .string "fell on the ground, and prayed\l"
    .string "that, if it were possible, the hour\l"
    .string "might pass from him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_36::
    .string "And he said, Abba, Father, all\n"
    .string "things are possible unto thee; take\l"
    .string "away this cup from me: nevertheless\l"
    .string "not what I will, but what thou wilt.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_37::
    .string "And he cometh, and findeth them\n"
    .string "sleeping, and saith unto Peter,\l"
    .string "Simon, sleepest thou? couldest not\l"
    .string "thou watch one hour?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_38::
    .string "Watch ye and pray, lest ye enter\n"
    .string "into temptation. The spirit truly\l"
    .string "is ready, but the flesh is weak$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_39::
    .string "And again he went away, and prayed,\n"
    .string "and spake the same words.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_40::
    .string "And when he returned, he found them\n"
    .string "asleep again, (for their eyes were\l"
    .string "heavy,) neither wist they what to\l"
    .string "answer him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_41::
    .string "And he cometh the third time, and\n"
    .string "saith unto them, Sleep on now, and\l"
    .string "take your rest: it is enough, the\l"
    .string "hour is come; behold, the Son of man\l"
    .string "is betrayed into the hands of sinners.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_42::
    .string "Rise up, let us go; lo, he that\n"
    .string "betrayeth me is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_43::
    .string "And immediately, while he yet\n"
    .string "spake, cometh Judas, one of the\l"
    .string "twelve, and with him a great\l"
    .string "multitude with swords and staves,\l"
    .string "from the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "scribes and the elders.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_44::
    .string "And he that betrayed him had given\n"
    .string "them a token, saying, Whomsoever I\l"
    .string "shall kiss, that same is he; take\l"
    .string "him, and lead him away safely.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_45::
    .string "And as soon as he was come, he goeth\n"
    .string "straightway to him, and saith,\l"
    .string "Master, master; and kissed him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_46::
    .string "And they laid their hands on him,\n"
    .string "and took him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_47::
    .string "And one of them that stood by drew a\n"
    .string "sword, and smote a servant of the\l"
    .string "high priest, and cut off his ear.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_48::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "them, Are ye come out, as against a\l"
    .string "thief, with swords and with staves to\l"
    .string "take me?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_49::
    .string "I was daily with you in the temple\n"
    .string "teaching, and ye took me not: but the\l"
    .string "scriptures must be fulfilled$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_50::
    .string "And they all forsook him, and fled.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_51::
    .string "And there followed him a certain\n"
    .string "young man, having a linen cloth cast\l"
    .string "about his naked body; and the young\l"
    .string "men laid hold on him:"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_52::
    .string "And he left the linen cloth, and\n"
    .string "fled from them naked$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_53::
    .string "And they led Jesus away to the high\n"
    .string "priest: and with him were assembled\l"
    .string "all the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "elders and the scribes.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_54::
    .string "And Peter followed him afar off,\n"
    .string "even into the palace of the high\l"
    .string "priest: and he sat with the servants,\l"
    .string "and warmed himself at the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_55::
    .string "And the chief priests and all the\n"
    .string "council sought for witness against\l"
    .string "Jesus to put him to death; and found\l"
    .string "none.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_56::
    .string "For many bare false witness against\n"
    .string "him, but their witness agreed not\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_57::
    .string "And there arose certain, and bare\n"
    .string "false witness against him, saying,"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_58::
    .string "We heard him say, I will destroy\n"
    .string "this temple that is made with hands,\l"
    .string "and within three days I will build\l"
    .string "another made without hands$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_59::
    .string "But neither so did their witness\n"
    .string "agree together.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_60::
    .string "And the high priest stood up in the\n"
    .string "midst, and asked Jesus, saying,\l"
    .string "Answerest thou nothing? what is it\l"
    .string "which these witness against thee?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_61::
    .string "But he held his peace, and answered\n"
    .string "nothing. Again the high priest asked\l"
    .string "him, and said unto him, Art thou the\l"
    .string "Christ, the Son of the Blessed?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_62::
    .string "And Jesus said, I am: and ye shall\n"
    .string "see the Son of man sitting on the\l"
    .string "right hand of power, and coming in\l"
    .string "the clouds of heaven$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_63::
    .string "Then the high priest rent his\n"
    .string "clothes, and saith, What need we any\l"
    .string "further witnesses?"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_64::
    .string "Ye have heard the blasphemy: what\n"
    .string "think ye? And they all condemned him\l"
    .string "to be guilty of death$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_65::
    .string "And some began to spit on him, and\n"
    .string "to cover his face, and to buffet him,\l"
    .string "and to say unto him, Prophesy: and\l"
    .string "the servants did strike him with the\l"
    .string "palms of their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_66::
    .string "And as Peter was beneath in the\n"
    .string "palace, there cometh one of the\l"
    .string "maids of the high priest:"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_67::
    .string "And when she saw Peter warming\n"
    .string "himself, she looked upon him, and\l"
    .string "said, And thou also wast with Jesus\l"
    .string "of Nazareth$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_68::
    .string "But he denied, saying, I know not,\n"
    .string "neither understand I what thou sayest\l"
    .string " And he went out into the porch; and\l"
    .string "the cock crew.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_69::
    .string "And a maid saw him again, and began\n"
    .string "to say to them that stood by, This is\l"
    .string "one of them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_70::
    .string "And he denied it again. And a\n"
    .string "little after, they that stood by\l"
    .string "said again to Peter, Surely thou art\l"
    .string "one of them: for thou art a\l"
    .string "Galilaean, and thy speech agreeth\l"
    .string "thereto.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_71::
    .string "But he began to curse and to swear,\n"
    .string "saying, I know not this man of whom ye\l"
    .string "speak.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_14_72::
    .string "And the second time the cock crew.\n"
    .string "And Peter called to mind the word\l"
    .string "that Jesus said unto him, Before the\l"
    .string "cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me\l"
    .string "thrice. And when he thought thereon,\l"
    .string "he wept.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_1::
    .string "And straightway in the morning the\n"
    .string "chief priests held a consultation\l"
    .string "with the elders and scribes and the\l"
    .string "whole council, and bound Jesus, and\l"
    .string "carried him away, and delivered him\l"
    .string "to Pilate.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_2::
    .string "And Pilate asked him, Art thou the\n"
    .string "King of the Jews? And he answering\l"
    .string "said unto them, Thou sayest it.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_3::
    .string "And the chief priests accused him\n"
    .string "of many things: but he answered\l"
    .string "nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_4::
    .string "And Pilate asked him again, saying,\n"
    .string "Answerest thou nothing? behold how\l"
    .string "many things they witness against\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_5::
    .string "But Jesus yet answered nothing; so\n"
    .string "that Pilate marvelled.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_6::
    .string "Now at that feast he released unto\n"
    .string "them one prisoner, whomsoever they\l"
    .string "desired.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_7::
    .string "And there was one named Barabbas,\n"
    .string "which lay bound with them that had\l"
    .string "made insurrection with him, who had\l"
    .string "committed murder in the insurrection.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_8::
    .string "And the multitude crying aloud\n"
    .string "began to desire him to do as he had\l"
    .string "ever done unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_9::
    .string "But Pilate answered them, saying,\n"
    .string "Will ye that I release unto you the\l"
    .string "King of the Jews?"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_10::
    .string "For he knew that the chief priests\n"
    .string "had delivered him for envy$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_11::
    .string "But the chief priests moved the\n"
    .string "people, that he should rather\l"
    .string "release Barabbas unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_12::
    .string "And Pilate answered and said again\n"
    .string "unto them, What will ye then that I\l"
    .string "shall do unto him whom ye call the\l"
    .string "King of the Jews?"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_13::
    .string "And they cried out again, Crucify him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_14::
    .string "Then Pilate said unto them, Why,\n"
    .string "what evil hath he done? And they\l"
    .string "cried out the more exceedingly,\l"
    .string "Crucify him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_15::
    .string "And so Pilate, willing to content\n"
    .string "the people, released Barabbas unto\l"
    .string "them, and delivered Jesus, when he\l"
    .string "had scourged him, to be crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_16::
    .string "And the soldiers led him away into\n"
    .string "the hall, called Praetorium; and\l"
    .string "they call together the whole band.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_17::
    .string "And they clothed him with purple,\n"
    .string "and platted a crown of thorns, and\l"
    .string "put it about his head,"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_18::
    .string "And began to salute him, Hail, King\n"
    .string "of the Jews!"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_19::
    .string "And they smote him on the head with\n"
    .string "a reed, and did spit upon him, and\l"
    .string "bowing their knees worshipped him$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_20::
    .string "And when they had mocked him, they\n"
    .string "took off the purple from him, and\l"
    .string "put his own clothes on him, and led\l"
    .string "him out to crucify him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_21::
    .string "And they compel one Simon a\n"
    .string "Cyrenian, who passed by, coming out\l"
    .string "of the country, the father of\l"
    .string "Alexander and Rufus, to bear his\l"
    .string "cross.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_22::
    .string "And they bring him unto the place\n"
    .string "Golgotha, which is, being\l"
    .string "interpreted, The place of a skull.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_23::
    .string "And they gave him to drink wine\n"
    .string "mingled with myrrh: but he received\l"
    .string "it not.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_24::
    .string "And when they had crucified him,\n"
    .string "they parted his garments, casting\l"
    .string "lots upon them, what every man\l"
    .string "should take.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_25::
    .string "And it was the third hour, and they\n"
    .string "crucified him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_26::
    .string "And the superscription of his\n"
    .string "accusation was written over, THE KING\l"
    .string "OF THE JEWS.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_27::
    .string "And with him they crucify two\n"
    .string "thieves; the one on his right hand,\l"
    .string "and the other on his left.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_28::
    .string "And the scripture was fulfilled,\n"
    .string "which saith, And he was numbered with\l"
    .string "the transgressors.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_29::
    .string "And they that passed by railed on\n"
    .string "him, wagging their heads, and saying,\l"
    .string "Ah, thou that destroyest the\l"
    .string "temple, and buildest it in three\l"
    .string "days,"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_30::
    .string "Save thyself, and come down from\n"
    .string "the cross$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_31::
    .string "Likewise also the chief priests\n"
    .string "mocking said among themselves with\l"
    .string "the scribes, He saved others;\l"
    .string "himself he cannot save.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_32::
    .string "Let Christ the King of Israel\n"
    .string "descend now from the cross, that we\l"
    .string "may see and believe. And they that\l"
    .string "were crucified with him reviled him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_33::
    .string "And when the sixth hour was come,\n"
    .string "there was darkness over the whole\l"
    .string "land until the ninth hour.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_34::
    .string "And at the ninth hour Jesus cried\n"
    .string "with a loud voice, saying, Eloi,\l"
    .string "Eloi, lama sabachthani? which is,\l"
    .string "being interpreted, My God, my God,\l"
    .string "why hast thou forsaken me?"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_35::
    .string "And some of them that stood by, when\n"
    .string "they heard it, said, Behold, he\l"
    .string "calleth Elias$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_36::
    .string "And one ran and filled a spunge\n"
    .string "full of vinegar, and put it on a\l"
    .string "reed, and gave him to drink, saying,\l"
    .string "Let alone; let us see whether Elias\l"
    .string "will come to take him down.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_37::
    .string "And Jesus cried with a loud voice,\n"
    .string "and gave up the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_38::
    .string "And the veil of the temple was\n"
    .string "rent in twain from the top to the\l"
    .string "bottom.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_39::
    .string "And when the centurion, which stood\n"
    .string "over against him, saw that he so\l"
    .string "cried out, and gave up the ghost, he\l"
    .string "said, Truly this man was the Son of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_40::
    .string "There were also women looking on\n"
    .string "afar off: among whom was Mary\l"
    .string "Magdalene, and Mary the mother of\l"
    .string "James the less and of Joses, and\l"
    .string "Salome;"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_41::
    .string "(Who also, when he was in Galilee,\n"
    .string "followed him, and ministered unto\l"
    .string "him;) and many other women which came\l"
    .string "up with him unto Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_42::
    .string "And now when the even was come,\n"
    .string "because it was the preparation,\l"
    .string "that is, the day before the sabbath,"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_43::
    .string "Joseph of Arimathaea, an\n"
    .string "honourable counsellor, which also\l"
    .string "waited for the kingdom of God, came,\l"
    .string "and went in boldly unto Pilate, and\l"
    .string "craved the body of Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_44::
    .string "And Pilate marvelled if he were\n"
    .string "already dead: and calling unto him\l"
    .string "the centurion, he asked him whether\l"
    .string "he had been any while dead.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_45::
    .string "And when he knew it of the\n"
    .string "centurion, he gave the body to\l"
    .string "Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_46::
    .string "And he bought fine linen, and took\n"
    .string "him down, and wrapped him in the\l"
    .string "linen, and laid him in a sepulchre\l"
    .string "which was hewn out of a rock, and\l"
    .string "rolled a stone unto the door of the\l"
    .string "sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_15_47::
    .string "And Mary Magdalene and Mary the\n"
    .string "mother of Joses beheld where he was\l"
    .string "laid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_1::
    .string "And when the sabbath was past, Mary\n"
    .string "Magdalene, and Mary the mother of\l"
    .string "James, and Salome, had bought sweet\l"
    .string "spices, that they might come and\l"
    .string "anoint him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_2::
    .string "And very early in the morning the\n"
    .string "first day of the week, they came unto\l"
    .string "the sepulchre at the rising of the\l"
    .string "sun.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_3::
    .string "And they said among themselves, Who\n"
    .string "shall roll us away the stone from\l"
    .string "the door of the sepulchre?"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_4::
    .string "And when they looked, they saw that\n"
    .string "the stone was rolled away: for it\l"
    .string "was very great$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_5::
    .string "And entering into the sepulchre,\n"
    .string "they saw a young man sitting on the\l"
    .string "right side, clothed in a long white\l"
    .string "garment; and they were affrighted.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_6::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Be not\n"
    .string "affrighted: Ye seek Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth, which was crucified: he is\l"
    .string "risen; he is not here: behold the\l"
    .string "place where they laid him.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_7::
    .string "But go your way, tell his\n"
    .string "disciples and Peter that he goeth\l"
    .string "before you into Galilee: there\l"
    .string "shall ye see him, as he said unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_8::
    .string "And they went out quickly, and fled\n"
    .string "from the sepulchre; for they\l"
    .string "trembled and were amazed: neither\l"
    .string "said they any thing to any man; for\l"
    .string "they were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_9::
    .string "Now when Jesus was risen early the\n"
    .string "first day of the week, he appeared\l"
    .string "first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom\l"
    .string "he had cast seven devils.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_10::
    .string "And she went and told them that had\n"
    .string "been with him, as they mourned and\l"
    .string "wept.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_11::
    .string "And they, when they had heard that\n"
    .string "he was alive, and had been seen of\l"
    .string "her, believed not.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_12::
    .string "After that he appeared in another\n"
    .string "form unto two of them, as they\l"
    .string "walked, and went into the country.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_13::
    .string "And they went and told it unto the\n"
    .string "residue: neither believed they them.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_14::
    .string "Afterward he appeared unto the\n"
    .string "eleven as they sat at meat, and\l"
    .string "upbraided them with their unbelief\l"
    .string "and hardness of heart, because they\l"
    .string "believed not them which had seen him\l"
    .string "after he was risen.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_15::
    .string "And he said unto them, Go ye into\n"
    .string "all the world, and preach the\l"
    .string "gospel to every creature.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_16::
    .string "He that believeth and is baptized\n"
    .string "shall be saved; but he that\l"
    .string "believeth not shall be damned.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_17::
    .string "And these signs shall follow them\n"
    .string "that believe; In my name shall they\l"
    .string "cast out devils; they shall speak\l"
    .string "with new tongues;"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_18::
    .string "They shall take up serpents; and\n"
    .string "if they drink any deadly thing, it\l"
    .string "shall not hurt them; they shall\l"
    .string "lay hands on the sick, and they\l"
    .string "shall recover$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_19::
    .string "So then after the Lord had spoken\n"
    .string "unto them, he was received up into\l"
    .string "heaven, and sat on the right hand of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Mark_16_20::
    .string "And they went forth, and preached\n"
    .string "every where, the Lord working with\l"
    .string "them, and confirming the word with\l"
    .string "signs following. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_1::
    .string "Forasmuch as many have taken in hand\n"
    .string "to set forth in order a declaration\l"
    .string "of those things which are most\l"
    .string "surely believed among us,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_2::
    .string "Even as they delivered them unto\n"
    .string "us, which from the beginning were\l"
    .string "eyewitnesses, and ministers of the\l"
    .string "word;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_3::
    .string "It seemed good to me also, having\n"
    .string "had perfect understanding of all\l"
    .string "things from the very first, to write\l"
    .string "unto thee in order, most excellent\l"
    .string "Theophilus,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_4::
    .string "That thou mightest know the\n"
    .string "certainty of those things, wherein\l"
    .string "thou hast been instructed$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_5::
    .string "THERE was in the days of Herod, the\n"
    .string "king of Judaea, a certain priest\l"
    .string "named Zacharias, of the course of\l"
    .string "Abia: and his wife was of the\l"
    .string "daughters of Aaron, and her name was\l"
    .string "Elisabeth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_6::
    .string "And they were both righteous before\n"
    .string "God, walking in all the\l"
    .string "commandments and ordinances of the\l"
    .string "Lord blameless.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_7::
    .string "And they had no child, because that\n"
    .string "Elisabeth was barren, and they both\l"
    .string "were now well stricken in years.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, that while he\n"
    .string "executed the priest’s office before\l"
    .string "God in the order of his course,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_9::
    .string "According to the custom of the\n"
    .string "priest’s office, his lot was to burn\l"
    .string "incense when he went into the\l"
    .string "temple of the Lord$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_10::
    .string "And the whole multitude of the\n"
    .string "people were praying without at the\l"
    .string "time of incense.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_11::
    .string "And there appeared unto him an\n"
    .string "angel of the Lord standing on the\l"
    .string "right side of the altar of incense.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_12::
    .string "And when Zacharias saw him, he was\n"
    .string "troubled, and fear fell upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_13::
    .string "But the angel said unto him, Fear\n"
    .string "not, Zacharias: for thy prayer is\l"
    .string "heard; and thy wife Elisabeth shall\l"
    .string "bear thee a son, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "call his name John.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_14::
    .string "And thou shalt have joy and\n"
    .string "gladness; and many shall rejoice at\l"
    .string "his birth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_15::
    .string "For he shall be great in the sight\n"
    .string "of the Lord, and shall drink neither\l"
    .string "wine nor strong drink; and he shall\l"
    .string "be filled with the Holy Ghost, even\l"
    .string "from his mother’s womb.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_16::
    .string "And many of the children of Israel\n"
    .string "shall he turn to the Lord their God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_17::
    .string "And he shall go before him in the\n"
    .string "spirit and power of Elias, to turn\l"
    .string "the hearts of the fathers to the\l"
    .string "children, and the disobedient to the\l"
    .string "wisdom of the just; to make ready a\l"
    .string "people prepared for the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_18::
    .string "And Zacharias said unto the angel,\n"
    .string "Whereby shall I know this? for I am\l"
    .string "an old man, and my wife well\l"
    .string "stricken in years.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_19::
    .string "And the angel answering said unto\n"
    .string "him, I am Gabriel, that stand in the\l"
    .string "presence of God; and am sent to speak\l"
    .string "unto thee, and to shew thee these\l"
    .string "glad tidings.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_20::
    .string "And, behold, thou shalt be dumb,\n"
    .string "and not able to speak, until the\l"
    .string "day that these things shall be\l"
    .string "performed, because thou believest\l"
    .string "not my words, which shall be\l"
    .string "fulfilled in their season.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_21::
    .string "And the people waited for\n"
    .string "Zacharias, and marvelled that he\l"
    .string "tarried so long in the temple.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_22::
    .string "And when he came out, he could not\n"
    .string "speak unto them: and they perceived\l"
    .string "that he had seen a vision in the\l"
    .string "temple: for he beckoned unto them,\l"
    .string "and remained speechless.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_23::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as soon\n"
    .string "as the days of his ministration were\l"
    .string "accomplished, he departed to his\l"
    .string "own house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_24::
    .string "And after those days his wife\n"
    .string "Elisabeth conceived, and hid\l"
    .string "herself five months, saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_25::
    .string "Thus hath the Lord dealt with me in\n"
    .string "the days wherein he looked on me, to\l"
    .string "take away my reproach among men$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_26::
    .string "And in the sixth month the angel\n"
    .string "Gabriel was sent from God unto a\l"
    .string "city of Galilee, named Nazareth,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_27::
    .string "To a virgin espoused to a man whose\n"
    .string "name was Joseph, of the house of\l"
    .string "David; and the virgin’s name was Mary$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_28::
    .string "And the angel came in unto her, and\n"
    .string "said, Hail, thou that art highly\l"
    .string "favoured, the Lord is with thee:\l"
    .string "blessed art thou among women.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_29::
    .string "And when she saw him, she was\n"
    .string "troubled at his saying, and cast in\l"
    .string "her mind what manner of salutation\l"
    .string "this should be.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_30::
    .string "And the angel said unto her, Fear\n"
    .string "not, Mary: for thou hast found favour\l"
    .string "with God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_31::
    .string "And, behold, thou shalt conceive\n"
    .string "in thy womb, and bring forth a son,\l"
    .string "and shalt call his name JESUS.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_32::
    .string "He shall be great, and shall be\n"
    .string "called the Son of the Highest: and\l"
    .string "the Lord God shall give unto him the\l"
    .string "throne of his father David:"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_33::
    .string "And he shall reign over the house\n"
    .string "of Jacob for ever; and of his kingdom\l"
    .string "there shall be no end$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_34::
    .string "Then said Mary unto the angel, How\n"
    .string "shall this be, seeing I know not a\l"
    .string "man?"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_35::
    .string "And the angel answered and said\n"
    .string "unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come\l"
    .string "upon thee, and the power of the\l"
    .string "Highest shall overshadow thee:\l"
    .string "therefore also that holy thing\l"
    .string "which shall be born of thee shall\l"
    .string "be called the Son of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_36::
    .string "And, behold, thy cousin Elisabeth,\n"
    .string "she hath also conceived a son in her\l"
    .string "old age: and this is the sixth month\l"
    .string "with her, who was called barren.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_37::
    .string "For with God nothing shall be\n"
    .string "impossible.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_38::
    .string "And Mary said, Behold the handmaid\n"
    .string "of the Lord; be it unto me according\l"
    .string "to thy word. And the angel departed\l"
    .string "from her.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_39::
    .string "And Mary arose in those days, and\n"
    .string "went into the hill country with\l"
    .string "haste, into a city of Juda;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_40::
    .string "And entered into the house of\n"
    .string "Zacharias, and saluted Elisabeth$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_41::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when\n"
    .string "Elisabeth heard the salutation of\l"
    .string "Mary, the babe leaped in her womb;\l"
    .string "and Elisabeth was filled with the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost:"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_42::
    .string "And she spake out with a loud\n"
    .string "voice, and said, Blessed art thou\l"
    .string "among women, and blessed is the\l"
    .string "fruit of thy womb$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_43::
    .string "And whence is this to me, that the\n"
    .string "mother of my Lord should come to me?"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_44::
    .string "For, lo, as soon as the voice of thy\n"
    .string "salutation sounded in mine ears, the\l"
    .string "babe leaped in my womb for joy$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_45::
    .string "And blessed is she that believed:\n"
    .string "for there shall be a performance of\l"
    .string "those things which were told her\l"
    .string "from the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_46::
    .string "And Mary said, My soul doth magnify\n"
    .string "the Lord,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_47::
    .string "And my spirit hath rejoiced in God\n"
    .string "my Saviour$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_48::
    .string "For he hath regarded the low estate\n"
    .string "of his handmaiden: for, behold, from\l"
    .string "henceforth all generations shall\l"
    .string "call me blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_49::
    .string "For he that is mighty hath done to\n"
    .string "me great things; and holy is his\l"
    .string "name.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_50::
    .string "And his mercy is on them that fear\n"
    .string "him from generation to generation.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_51::
    .string "He hath shewed strength with his\n"
    .string "arm; he hath scattered the proud in\l"
    .string "the imagination of their hearts.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_52::
    .string "He hath put down the mighty from\n"
    .string "their seats, and exalted them of low\l"
    .string "degree.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_53::
    .string "He hath filled the hungry with\n"
    .string "good things; and the rich he hath\l"
    .string "sent empty away.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_54::
    .string "He hath holpen his servant Israel,\n"
    .string "in remembrance of his mercy;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_55::
    .string "As he spake to our fathers, to\n"
    .string "Abraham, and to his seed for ever$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_56::
    .string "And Mary abode with her about three\n"
    .string "months, and returned to her own house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_57::
    .string "Now Elisabeth’s full time came\n"
    .string "that she should be delivered; and\l"
    .string "she brought forth a son.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_58::
    .string "And her neighbours and her cousins\n"
    .string "heard how the Lord had shewed great\l"
    .string "mercy upon her; and they rejoiced\l"
    .string "with her.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_59::
    .string "And it came to pass, that on the\n"
    .string "eighth day they came to circumcise\l"
    .string "the child; and they called him\l"
    .string "Zacharias, after the name of his\l"
    .string "father.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_60::
    .string "And his mother answered and said,\n"
    .string "Not so; but he shall be called\l"
    .string "John.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_61::
    .string "And they said unto her, There is\n"
    .string "none of thy kindred that is called\l"
    .string "by this name.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_62::
    .string "And they made signs to his father,\n"
    .string "how he would have him called.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_63::
    .string "And he asked for a writing table,\n"
    .string "and wrote, saying, His name is John.\l"
    .string "And they marvelled all.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_64::
    .string "And his mouth was opened\n"
    .string "immediately, and his tongue loosed,\l"
    .string "and he spake, and praised God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_65::
    .string "And fear came on all that dwelt\n"
    .string "round about them: and all these\l"
    .string "sayings were noised abroad\l"
    .string "throughout all the hill country of\l"
    .string "Judaea.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_66::
    .string "And all they that heard them laid\n"
    .string "them up in their hearts, saying,\l"
    .string "What manner of child shall this be!\l"
    .string "And the hand of the Lord was with him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_67::
    .string "And his father Zacharias was\n"
    .string "filled with the Holy Ghost, and\l"
    .string "prophesied, saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_68::
    .string "Blessed be the Lord God of Israel;\n"
    .string "for he hath visited and redeemed his\l"
    .string "people,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_69::
    .string "And hath raised up an horn of\n"
    .string "salvation for us in the house of his\l"
    .string "servant David;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_70::
    .string "As he spake by the mouth of his\n"
    .string "holy prophets, which have been\l"
    .string "since the world began:"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_71::
    .string "That we should be saved from our\n"
    .string "enemies, and from the hand of all\l"
    .string "that hate us;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_72::
    .string "To perform the mercy promised to\n"
    .string "our fathers, and to remember his\l"
    .string "holy covenant;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_73::
    .string "The oath which he sware to our\n"
    .string "father Abraham,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_74::
    .string "That he would grant unto us, that we\n"
    .string "being delivered out of the hand of\l"
    .string "our enemies might serve him without\l"
    .string "fear,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_75::
    .string "In holiness and righteousness\n"
    .string "before him, all the days of our life$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_76::
    .string "And thou, child, shalt be called\n"
    .string "the prophet of the Highest: for thou\l"
    .string "shalt go before the face of the Lord\l"
    .string "to prepare his ways;"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_77::
    .string "To give knowledge of salvation\n"
    .string "unto his people by the remission of\l"
    .string "their sins,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_78::
    .string "Through the tender mercy of our God;\n"
    .string "whereby the dayspring from on high\l"
    .string "hath visited us,"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_79::
    .string "To give light to them that sit in\n"
    .string "darkness and in the shadow of death,\l"
    .string "to guide our feet into the way of\l"
    .string "peace$"
Bible_Text_Luke_1_80::
    .string "And the child grew, and waxed\n"
    .string "strong in spirit, and was in the\l"
    .string "deserts till the day of his shewing\l"
    .string "unto Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "that there went out a decree from\l"
    .string "Caesar Augustus that all the world\l"
    .string "should be taxed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_2::
    .string "(And this taxing was first made when\n"
    .string "Cyrenius was governor of Syria.)"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_3::
    .string "And all went to be taxed, every one\n"
    .string "into his own city$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_4::
    .string "And Joseph also went up from\n"
    .string "Galilee, out of the city of\l"
    .string "Nazareth, into Judaea, unto the city\l"
    .string "of David, which is called\l"
    .string "Bethlehem; (because he was of the\l"
    .string "house and lineage of David:)"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_5::
    .string "To be taxed with Mary his espoused\n"
    .string "wife, being great with child$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_6::
    .string "And so it was, that, while they were\n"
    .string "there, the days were accomplished\l"
    .string "that she should be delivered.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_7::
    .string "And she brought forth her firstborn\n"
    .string "son, and wrapped him in swaddling\l"
    .string "clothes, and laid him in a manger;\l"
    .string "because there was no room for them in\l"
    .string "the inn.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_8::
    .string "And there were in the same country\n"
    .string "shepherds abiding in the field,\l"
    .string "keeping watch over their flock by\l"
    .string "night.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_9::
    .string "And, lo, the angel of the Lord came\n"
    .string "upon them, and the glory of the Lord\l"
    .string "shone round about them: and they were\l"
    .string "sore afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_10::
    .string "And the angel said unto them, Fear\n"
    .string "not: for, behold, I bring you good\l"
    .string "tidings of great joy, which shall be\l"
    .string "to all people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_11::
    .string "For unto you is born this day in the\n"
    .string "city of David a Saviour, which is\l"
    .string "Christ the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_12::
    .string "And this shall be a sign unto you;\n"
    .string "Ye shall find the babe wrapped in\l"
    .string "swaddling clothes, lying in a\l"
    .string "manger.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_13::
    .string "And suddenly there was with the\n"
    .string "angel a multitude of the heavenly\l"
    .string "host praising God, and saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_14::
    .string "Glory to God in the highest, and on\n"
    .string "earth peace, good will toward men$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, as the angels\n"
    .string "were gone away from them into heaven,\l"
    .string "the shepherds said one to another,\l"
    .string "Let us now go even unto Bethlehem,\l"
    .string "and see this thing which is come to\l"
    .string "pass, which the Lord hath made known\l"
    .string "unto us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_16::
    .string "And they came with haste, and found\n"
    .string "Mary, and Joseph, and the babe lying\l"
    .string "in a manger.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_17::
    .string "And when they had seen it, they made\n"
    .string "known abroad the saying which was\l"
    .string "told them concerning this child.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_18::
    .string "And all they that heard it\n"
    .string "wondered at those things which were\l"
    .string "told them by the shepherds.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_19::
    .string "But Mary kept all these things,\n"
    .string "and pondered them in her heart.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_20::
    .string "And the shepherds returned,\n"
    .string "glorifying and praising God for\l"
    .string "all the things that they had heard\l"
    .string "and seen, as it was told unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_21::
    .string "And when eight days were\n"
    .string "accomplished for the circumcising\l"
    .string "of the child, his name was called\l"
    .string "JESUS, which was so named of the\l"
    .string "angel before he was conceived in the\l"
    .string "womb.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_22::
    .string "And when the days of her\n"
    .string "purification according to the law of\l"
    .string "Moses were accomplished, they\l"
    .string "brought him to Jerusalem, to\l"
    .string "present him to the Lord;"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_23::
    .string "(As it is written in the law of the\n"
    .string "LORD, Every male that openeth the\l"
    .string "womb shall be called holy to the\l"
    .string "Lord;)"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_24::
    .string "And to offer a sacrifice according\n"
    .string "to that which is said in the law of\l"
    .string "the Lord, A pair of turtledoves, or\l"
    .string "two young pigeons$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_25::
    .string "And, behold, there was a man in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, whose name was Simeon;\l"
    .string "and the same man was just and devout,\l"
    .string "waiting for the consolation of\l"
    .string "Israel: and the Holy Ghost was upon\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_26::
    .string "And it was revealed unto him by the\n"
    .string "Holy Ghost, that he should not see\l"
    .string "death, before he had seen the Lord’s\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_27::
    .string "And he came by the Spirit into the\n"
    .string "temple: and when the parents\l"
    .string "brought in the child Jesus, to do for\l"
    .string "him after the custom of the law,"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_28::
    .string "Then took he him up in his arms, and\n"
    .string "blessed God, and said,"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_29::
    .string "Lord, now lettest thou thy servant\n"
    .string "depart in peace, according to thy\l"
    .string "word:"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_30::
    .string "For mine eyes have seen thy\n"
    .string "salvation,"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_31::
    .string "Which thou hast prepared before\n"
    .string "the face of all people;"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_32::
    .string "A light to lighten the Gentiles,\n"
    .string "and the glory of thy people Israel$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_33::
    .string "And Joseph and his mother\n"
    .string "marvelled at those things which\l"
    .string "were spoken of him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_34::
    .string "And Simeon blessed them, and said\n"
    .string "unto Mary his mother, Behold, this\l"
    .string "child is set for the fall and\l"
    .string "rising again of many in Israel; and\l"
    .string "for a sign which shall be spoken\l"
    .string "against;"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_35::
    .string "(Yea, a sword shall pierce through\n"
    .string "thy own soul also,) that the\l"
    .string "thoughts of many hearts may be\l"
    .string "revealed$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_36::
    .string "And there was one Anna, a\n"
    .string "prophetess, the daughter of\l"
    .string "Phanuel, of the tribe of Aser: she\l"
    .string "was of a great age, and had lived\l"
    .string "with an husband seven years from her\l"
    .string "virginity;"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_37::
    .string "And she was a widow of about\n"
    .string "fourscore and four years, which\l"
    .string "departed not from the temple, but\l"
    .string "served God with fastings and prayers\l"
    .string "night and day$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_38::
    .string "And she coming in that instant gave\n"
    .string "thanks likewise unto the Lord, and\l"
    .string "spake of him to all them that\l"
    .string "looked for redemption in Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_39::
    .string "And when they had performed all\n"
    .string "things according to the law of the\l"
    .string "Lord, they returned into Galilee,\l"
    .string "to their own city Nazareth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_40::
    .string "And the child grew, and waxed\n"
    .string "strong in spirit, filled with\l"
    .string "wisdom: and the grace of God was upon\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_41::
    .string "Now his parents went to Jerusalem\n"
    .string "every year at the feast of the\l"
    .string "passover.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_42::
    .string "And when he was twelve years old,\n"
    .string "they went up to Jerusalem after the\l"
    .string "custom of the feast.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_43::
    .string "And when they had fulfilled the\n"
    .string "days, as they returned, the child\l"
    .string "Jesus tarried behind in Jerusalem;\l"
    .string "and Joseph and his mother knew not\l"
    .string "of it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_44::
    .string "But they, supposing him to have\n"
    .string "been in the company, went a day’s\l"
    .string "journey; and they sought him among\l"
    .string "their kinsfolk and acquaintance.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_45::
    .string "And when they found him not, they\n"
    .string "turned back again to Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "seeking him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_46::
    .string "And it came to pass, that after\n"
    .string "three days they found him in the\l"
    .string "temple, sitting in the midst of the\l"
    .string "doctors, both hearing them, and\l"
    .string "asking them questions.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_47::
    .string "And all that heard him were\n"
    .string "astonished at his understanding and\l"
    .string "answers.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_48::
    .string "And when they saw him, they were\n"
    .string "amazed: and his mother said unto him,\l"
    .string "Son, why hast thou thus dealt with\l"
    .string "us? behold, thy father and I have\l"
    .string "sought thee sorrowing.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_49::
    .string "And he said unto them, How is it that\n"
    .string "ye sought me? wist ye not that I must\l"
    .string "be about my Father’s business?"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_50::
    .string "And they understood not the saying\n"
    .string "which he spake unto them$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_51::
    .string "And he went down with them, and came\n"
    .string "to Nazareth, and was subject unto\l"
    .string "them: but his mother kept all these\l"
    .string "sayings in her heart.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_2_52::
    .string "And Jesus increased in wisdom and\n"
    .string "stature, and in favour with God and\l"
    .string "man.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_1::
    .string "Now in the fifteenth year of the\n"
    .string "reign of Tiberius Caesar, Pontius\l"
    .string "Pilate being governor of Judaea, and\l"
    .string "Herod being tetrarch of Galilee,\l"
    .string "and his brother Philip tetrarch of\l"
    .string "Ituraea and of the region of\l"
    .string "Trachonitis, and Lysanias the\l"
    .string "tetrarch of Abilene,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_2::
    .string "Annas and Caiaphas being the high\n"
    .string "priests, the word of God came unto\l"
    .string "John the son of Zacharias in the\l"
    .string "wilderness$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_3::
    .string "And he came into all the country\n"
    .string "about Jordan, preaching the baptism\l"
    .string "of repentance for the remission of\l"
    .string "sins;"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_4::
    .string "As it is written in the book of the\n"
    .string "words of Esaias the prophet,\l"
    .string "saying, The voice of one crying in\l"
    .string "the wilderness, Prepare ye the way\l"
    .string "of the Lord, make his paths straight$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_5::
    .string "Every valley shall be filled,\n"
    .string "and every mountain and hill shall\l"
    .string "be brought low; and the crooked\l"
    .string "shall be made straight, and the\l"
    .string "rough ways shall be made smooth;"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_6::
    .string "And all flesh shall see the\n"
    .string "salvation of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_7::
    .string "Then said he to the multitude that\n"
    .string "came forth to be baptized of him, O\l"
    .string "generation of vipers, who hath\l"
    .string "warned you to flee from the wrath to\l"
    .string "come?"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_8::
    .string "Bring forth therefore fruits worthy\n"
    .string "of repentance, and begin not to say\l"
    .string "within yourselves, We have Abraham\l"
    .string "to our father: for I say unto you,\l"
    .string "That God is able of these stones to\l"
    .string "raise up children unto Abraham$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_9::
    .string "And now also the axe is laid unto\n"
    .string "the root of the trees: every tree\l"
    .string "therefore which bringeth not forth\l"
    .string "good fruit is hewn down, and cast\l"
    .string "into the fire.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_10::
    .string "And the people asked him, saying,\n"
    .string "What shall we do then?"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_11::
    .string "He answereth and saith unto them, He\n"
    .string "that hath two coats, let him impart\l"
    .string "to him that hath none; and he that\l"
    .string "hath meat, let him do likewise$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_12::
    .string "Then came also publicans to be\n"
    .string "baptized, and said unto him, Master,\l"
    .string "what shall we do?"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_13::
    .string "And he said unto them, Exact no more\n"
    .string "than that which is appointed you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_14::
    .string "And the soldiers likewise demanded\n"
    .string "of him, saying, And what shall we\l"
    .string "do? And he said unto them, Do\l"
    .string "violence to no man, neither accuse\l"
    .string "any falsely; and be content with\l"
    .string "your wages.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_15::
    .string "And as the people were in\n"
    .string "expectation, and all men mused in\l"
    .string "their hearts of John, whether he were\l"
    .string "the Christ, or not;"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_16::
    .string "John answered, saying unto them\n"
    .string "all, I indeed baptize you with\l"
    .string "water; but one mightier than I\l"
    .string "cometh, the latchet of whose shoes I\l"
    .string "am not worthy to unloose: he shall\l"
    .string "baptize you with the Holy Ghost and\l"
    .string "with fire:"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_17::
    .string "Whose fan is in his hand, and he\n"
    .string "will throughly purge his floor,\l"
    .string "and will gather the wheat into his\l"
    .string "garner; but the chaff he will burn\l"
    .string "with fire unquenchable$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_18::
    .string "And many other things in his\n"
    .string "exhortation preached he unto the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_19::
    .string "But Herod the tetrarch, being\n"
    .string "reproved by him for Herodias his\l"
    .string "brother Philip’s wife, and for all\l"
    .string "the evils which Herod had done,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_20::
    .string "Added yet this above all, that he\n"
    .string "shut up John in prison$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_21::
    .string "Now when all the people were\n"
    .string "baptized, it came to pass, that\l"
    .string "Jesus also being baptized, and\l"
    .string "praying, the heaven was opened,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_22::
    .string "And the Holy Ghost descended in a\n"
    .string "bodily shape like a dove upon him,\l"
    .string "and a voice came from heaven, which\l"
    .string "said, Thou art my beloved Son; in\l"
    .string "thee I am well pleased$"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_23::
    .string "And Jesus himself began to be about\n"
    .string "thirty years of age, being (as was\l"
    .string "supposed) the son of Joseph, which\l"
    .string "was the son of Heli,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_24::
    .string "Which was the son of Matthat, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Levi, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Melchi, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Janna, which was the son of Joseph,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_25::
    .string "Which was the son of Mattathias,\n"
    .string "which was the son of Amos, which was\l"
    .string "the son of Naum, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Esli, which was the son of Nagge,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_26::
    .string "Which was the son of Maath, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Mattathias, which was\l"
    .string "the son of Semei, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Joseph, which was the son of Juda,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_27::
    .string "Which was the son of Joanna, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Rhesa, which was the\l"
    .string "son of Zorobabel, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Salathiel, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Neri,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_28::
    .string "Which was the son of Melchi, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Addi, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Cosam, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Elmodam, which was the son of Er,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_29::
    .string "Which was the son of Jose, which was\n"
    .string "the son of Eliezer, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Jorim, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Matthat, which was the son of Levi,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_30::
    .string "Which was the son of Simeon, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Juda, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Joseph, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Jonan, which was the son of Eliakim,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_31::
    .string "Which was the son of Melea, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Menan, which was the\l"
    .string "son of Mattatha, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Nathan, which was the son of David,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_32::
    .string "Which was the son of Jesse, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Obed, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Booz, which was the son of Salmon,\l"
    .string "which was the son of Naasson,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_33::
    .string "Which was the son of Aminadab, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Aram, which was the son\l"
    .string "of Esrom, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Phares, which was the son of Juda,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_34::
    .string "Which was the son of Jacob, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Isaac, which was the\l"
    .string "son of Abraham, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Thara, which was the son of Nachor,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_35::
    .string "Which was the son of Saruch, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Ragau, which was the\l"
    .string "son of Phalec, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Heber, which was the son of Sala,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_36::
    .string "Which was the son of Cainan, which\n"
    .string "was the son of Arphaxad, which was\l"
    .string "the son of Sem, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Noe, which was the son of Lamech,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_37::
    .string "Which was the son of Mathusala,\n"
    .string "which was the son of Enoch, which was\l"
    .string "the son of Jared, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Maleleel, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Cainan,"
Bible_Text_Luke_3_38::
    .string "Which was the son of Enos, which was\n"
    .string "the son of Seth, which was the son of\l"
    .string "Adam, which was the son of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_1::
    .string "And Jesus being full of the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost returned from Jordan, and was\l"
    .string "led by the Spirit into the\l"
    .string "wilderness,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_2::
    .string "Being forty days tempted of the\n"
    .string "devil. And in those days he did eat\l"
    .string "nothing: and when they were ended, he\l"
    .string "afterward hungered$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_3::
    .string "And the devil said unto him, If thou\n"
    .string "be the Son of God, command this stone\l"
    .string "that it be made bread.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_4::
    .string "And Jesus answered him, saying, It\n"
    .string "is written, That man shall not live\l"
    .string "by bread alone, but by every word of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_5::
    .string "And the devil, taking him up into\n"
    .string "an high mountain, shewed unto him\l"
    .string "all the kingdoms of the world in a\l"
    .string "moment of time.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_6::
    .string "And the devil said unto him, All\n"
    .string "this power will I give thee, and\l"
    .string "the glory of them: for that is\l"
    .string "delivered unto me; and to whomsoever\l"
    .string "I will I give it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_7::
    .string "If thou therefore wilt worship me,\n"
    .string "all shall be thine.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_8::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "him, Get thee behind me, Satan: for it\l"
    .string "is written, Thou shalt worship the\l"
    .string "Lord thy God, and him only shalt\l"
    .string "thou serve.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_9::
    .string "And he brought him to Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and set him on a pinnacle of the\l"
    .string "temple, and said unto him, If thou\l"
    .string "be the Son of God, cast thyself down\l"
    .string "from hence:"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_10::
    .string "For it is written, He shall give\n"
    .string "his angels charge over thee, to keep\l"
    .string "thee:"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_11::
    .string "And in their hands they shall bear\n"
    .string "thee up, lest at any time thou dash\l"
    .string "thy foot against a stone$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_12::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "It is said, Thou shalt not tempt the\l"
    .string "Lord thy God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_13::
    .string "And when the devil had ended all\n"
    .string "the temptation, he departed from\l"
    .string "him for a season.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_14::
    .string "And Jesus returned in the power of\n"
    .string "the Spirit into Galilee: and there\l"
    .string "went out a fame of him through all\l"
    .string "the region round about.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_15::
    .string "And he taught in their synagogues,\n"
    .string "being glorified of all.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_16::
    .string "And he came to Nazareth, where he\n"
    .string "had been brought up: and, as his\l"
    .string "custom was, he went into the\l"
    .string "synagogue on the sabbath day, and\l"
    .string "stood up for to read.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_17::
    .string "And there was delivered unto him\n"
    .string "the book of the prophet Esaias. And\l"
    .string "when he had opened the book, he found\l"
    .string "the place where it was written,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_18::
    .string "The Spirit of the Lord is upon me,\n"
    .string "because he hath anointed me to\l"
    .string "preach the gospel to the poor; he\l"
    .string "hath sent me to heal the\l"
    .string "brokenhearted, to preach\l"
    .string "deliverance to the captives, and\l"
    .string "recovering of sight to the blind, to\l"
    .string "set at liberty them that are\l"
    .string "bruised,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_19::
    .string "To preach the acceptable year of\n"
    .string "the Lord$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_20::
    .string "And he closed the book, and he gave\n"
    .string "it again to the minister, and sat down\l"
    .string " And the eyes of all them that were\l"
    .string "in the synagogue were fastened on him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_21::
    .string "And he began to say unto them, This\n"
    .string "day is this scripture fulfilled in\l"
    .string "your ears.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_22::
    .string "And all bare him witness, and\n"
    .string "wondered at the gracious words which\l"
    .string "proceeded out of his mouth. And they\l"
    .string "said, Is not this Joseph’s son?"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_23::
    .string "And he said unto them, Ye will\n"
    .string "surely say unto me this proverb,\l"
    .string "Physician, heal thyself: whatsoever\l"
    .string "we have heard done in Capernaum, do\l"
    .string "also here in thy country$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_24::
    .string "And he said, Verily I say unto you,\n"
    .string "No prophet is accepted in his own\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_25::
    .string "But I tell you of a truth, many\n"
    .string "widows were in Israel in the days of\l"
    .string "Elias, when the heaven was shut up\l"
    .string "three years and six months, when\l"
    .string "great famine was throughout all the\l"
    .string "land;"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_26::
    .string "But unto none of them was Elias\n"
    .string "sent, save unto Sarepta, a city of\l"
    .string "Sidon, unto a woman that was a widow$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_27::
    .string "And many lepers were in Israel in\n"
    .string "the time of Eliseus the prophet;\l"
    .string "and none of them was cleansed,\l"
    .string "saving Naaman the Syrian.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_28::
    .string "And all they in the synagogue, when\n"
    .string "they heard these things, were\l"
    .string "filled with wrath,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_29::
    .string "And rose up, and thrust him out of\n"
    .string "the city, and led him unto the brow\l"
    .string "of the hill whereon their city was\l"
    .string "built, that they might cast him down\l"
    .string "headlong$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_30::
    .string "But he passing through the midst of\n"
    .string "them went his way,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_31::
    .string "And came down to Capernaum, a city\n"
    .string "of Galilee, and taught them on the\l"
    .string "sabbath days$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_32::
    .string "And they were astonished at his\n"
    .string "doctrine: for his word was with\l"
    .string "power.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_33::
    .string "And in the synagogue there was a\n"
    .string "man, which had a spirit of an\l"
    .string "unclean devil, and cried out with a\l"
    .string "loud voice,"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_34::
    .string "Saying, Let us alone; what have we\n"
    .string "to do with thee, thou Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth? art thou come to destroy\l"
    .string "us? I know thee who thou art; the\l"
    .string "Holy One of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_35::
    .string "And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold\n"
    .string "thy peace, and come out of him. And\l"
    .string "when the devil had thrown him in the\l"
    .string "midst, he came out of him, and hurt\l"
    .string "him not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_36::
    .string "And they were all amazed, and\n"
    .string "spake among themselves, saying,\l"
    .string "What a word is this! for with\l"
    .string "authority and power he commandeth\l"
    .string "the unclean spirits, and they come\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_37::
    .string "And the fame of him went out into\n"
    .string "every place of the country round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_38::
    .string "And he arose out of the synagogue,\n"
    .string "and entered into Simon’s house. And\l"
    .string "Simon’s wife’s mother was taken with\l"
    .string "a great fever; and they besought him\l"
    .string "for her.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_39::
    .string "And he stood over her, and rebuked\n"
    .string "the fever; and it left her: and\l"
    .string "immediately she arose and\l"
    .string "ministered unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_40::
    .string "Now when the sun was setting, all\n"
    .string "they that had any sick with divers\l"
    .string "diseases brought them unto him; and\l"
    .string "he laid his hands on every one of\l"
    .string "them, and healed them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_41::
    .string "And devils also came out of many,\n"
    .string "crying out, and saying, Thou art\l"
    .string "Christ the Son of God. And he\l"
    .string "rebuking them suffered them not to\l"
    .string "speak: for they knew that he was\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_42::
    .string "And when it was day, he departed and\n"
    .string "went into a desert place: and the\l"
    .string "people sought him, and came unto\l"
    .string "him, and stayed him, that he should\l"
    .string "not depart from them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_43::
    .string "And he said unto them, I must preach\n"
    .string "the kingdom of God to other cities\l"
    .string "also: for therefore am I sent.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_4_44::
    .string "And he preached in the synagogues\n"
    .string "of Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as the\n"
    .string "people pressed upon him to hear\l"
    .string "the word of God, he stood by the lake\l"
    .string "of Gennesaret,"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_2::
    .string "And saw two ships standing by the\n"
    .string "lake: but the fishermen were gone out\l"
    .string "of them, and were washing their nets$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_3::
    .string "And he entered into one of the\n"
    .string "ships, which was Simon’s, and\l"
    .string "prayed him that he would thrust out\l"
    .string "a little from the land. And he sat\l"
    .string "down, and taught the people out of\l"
    .string "the ship.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_4::
    .string "Now when he had left speaking, he\n"
    .string "said unto Simon, Launch out into the\l"
    .string "deep, and let down your nets for a\l"
    .string "draught.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_5::
    .string "And Simon answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "Master, we have toiled all the\l"
    .string "night, and have taken nothing:\l"
    .string "nevertheless at thy word I will\l"
    .string "let down the net.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_6::
    .string "And when they had this done, they\n"
    .string "inclosed a great multitude of\l"
    .string "fishes: and their net brake.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_7::
    .string "And they beckoned unto their\n"
    .string "partners, which were in the other\l"
    .string "ship, that they should come and\l"
    .string "help them. And they came, and\l"
    .string "filled both the ships, so that they\l"
    .string "began to sink.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_8::
    .string "When Simon Peter saw it, he fell\n"
    .string "down at Jesus’ knees, saying, Depart\l"
    .string "from me; for I am a sinful man, O\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_9::
    .string "For he was astonished, and all that\n"
    .string "were with him, at the draught of the\l"
    .string "fishes which they had taken:"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_10::
    .string "And so was also James, and John, the\n"
    .string "sons of Zebedee, which were partners\l"
    .string "with Simon. And Jesus said unto\l"
    .string "Simon, Fear not; from henceforth thou\l"
    .string "shalt catch men$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_11::
    .string "And when they had brought their\n"
    .string "ships to land, they forsook all,\l"
    .string "and followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_12::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he was in\n"
    .string "a certain city, behold a man full\l"
    .string "of leprosy: who seeing Jesus fell\l"
    .string "on his face, and besought him,\l"
    .string "saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou\l"
    .string "canst make me clean.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_13::
    .string "And he put forth his hand, and\n"
    .string "touched him, saying, I will: be thou\l"
    .string "clean. And immediately the leprosy\l"
    .string "departed from him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_14::
    .string "And he charged him to tell no man:\n"
    .string "but go, and shew thyself to the\l"
    .string "priest, and offer for thy cleansing,\l"
    .string "according as Moses commanded, for a\l"
    .string "testimony unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_15::
    .string "But so much the more went there a\n"
    .string "fame abroad of him: and great\l"
    .string "multitudes came together to hear,\l"
    .string "and to be healed by him of their\l"
    .string "infirmities.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_16::
    .string "And he withdrew himself into the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and prayed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_17::
    .string "And it came to pass on a certain\n"
    .string "day, as he was teaching, that there\l"
    .string "were Pharisees and doctors of the\l"
    .string "law sitting by, which were come out\l"
    .string "of every town of Galilee, and\l"
    .string "Judaea, and Jerusalem: and the\l"
    .string "power of the Lord was present to\l"
    .string "heal them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_18::
    .string "And, behold, men brought in a bed a\n"
    .string "man which was taken with a palsy:\l"
    .string "and they sought means to bring him\l"
    .string "in, and to lay him before him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_19::
    .string "And when they could not find by\n"
    .string "what way they might bring him in\l"
    .string "because of the multitude, they went\l"
    .string "upon the housetop, and let him down\l"
    .string "through the tiling with his couch\l"
    .string "into the midst before Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_20::
    .string "And when he saw their faith, he said\n"
    .string "unto him, Man, thy sins are forgiven\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_21::
    .string "And the scribes and the Pharisees\n"
    .string "began to reason, saying, Who is this\l"
    .string "which speaketh blasphemies? Who\l"
    .string "can forgive sins, but God alone?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_22::
    .string "But when Jesus perceived their\n"
    .string "thoughts, he answering said unto\l"
    .string "them, What reason ye in your hearts?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_23::
    .string "Whether is easier, to say, Thy sins\n"
    .string "be forgiven thee; or to say, Rise up\l"
    .string "and walk?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_24::
    .string "But that ye may know that the Son of\n"
    .string "man hath power upon earth to\l"
    .string "forgive sins, (he said unto the sick\l"
    .string "of the palsy,) I say unto thee,\l"
    .string "Arise, and take up thy couch, and go\l"
    .string "into thine house$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_25::
    .string "And immediately he rose up before\n"
    .string "them, and took up that whereon he\l"
    .string "lay, and departed to his own house,\l"
    .string "glorifying God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_26::
    .string "And they were all amazed, and they\n"
    .string "glorified God, and were filled with\l"
    .string "fear, saying, We have seen strange\l"
    .string "things to day.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_27::
    .string "And after these things he went\n"
    .string "forth, and saw a publican, named\l"
    .string "Levi, sitting at the receipt of\l"
    .string "custom: and he said unto him, Follow\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_28::
    .string "And he left all, rose up, and\n"
    .string "followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_29::
    .string "And Levi made him a great feast in\n"
    .string "his own house: and there was a great\l"
    .string "company of publicans and of others\l"
    .string "that sat down with them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_30::
    .string "But their scribes and Pharisees\n"
    .string "murmured against his disciples,\l"
    .string "saying, Why do ye eat and drink with\l"
    .string "publicans and sinners?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_31::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "They that are whole need not a\l"
    .string "physician; but they that are sick$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_32::
    .string "I came not to call the righteous,\n"
    .string "but sinners to repentance.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_33::
    .string "And they said unto him, Why do the\n"
    .string "disciples of John fast often, and\l"
    .string "make prayers, and likewise the\l"
    .string "disciples of the Pharisees; but\l"
    .string "thine eat and drink?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_34::
    .string "And he said unto them, Can ye make\n"
    .string "the children of the bridechamber\l"
    .string "fast, while the bridegroom is with\l"
    .string "them?"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_35::
    .string "But the days will come, when the\n"
    .string "bridegroom shall be taken away from\l"
    .string "them, and then shall they fast in\l"
    .string "those days$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_36::
    .string "And he spake also a parable unto\n"
    .string "them; No man putteth a piece of a\l"
    .string "new garment upon an old; if\l"
    .string "otherwise, then both the new maketh a\l"
    .string "rent, and the piece that was taken\l"
    .string "out of the new agreeth not with the\l"
    .string "old.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_37::
    .string "And no man putteth new wine into\n"
    .string "old bottles; else the new wine\l"
    .string "will burst the bottles, and be\l"
    .string "spilled, and the bottles shall\l"
    .string "perish.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_38::
    .string "But new wine must be put into new\n"
    .string "bottles; and both are preserved.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_5_39::
    .string "No man also having drunk old wine\n"
    .string "straightway desireth new: for he\l"
    .string "saith, The old is better.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_1::
    .string "And it came to pass on the second\n"
    .string "sabbath after the first, that he went\l"
    .string "through the corn fields; and his\l"
    .string "disciples plucked the ears of\l"
    .string "corn, and did eat, rubbing them in\l"
    .string "their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_2::
    .string "And certain of the Pharisees said\n"
    .string "unto them, Why do ye that which is not\l"
    .string "lawful to do on the sabbath days?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_3::
    .string "And Jesus answering them said, Have\n"
    .string "ye not read so much as this, what\l"
    .string "David did, when himself was an\l"
    .string "hungred, and they which were with\l"
    .string "him;"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_4::
    .string "How he went into the house of God,\n"
    .string "and did take and eat the shewbread,\l"
    .string "and gave also to them that were with\l"
    .string "him; which it is not lawful to eat\l"
    .string "but for the priests alone?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, That the Son\n"
    .string "of man is Lord also of the sabbath$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_6::
    .string "And it came to pass also on another\n"
    .string "sabbath, that he entered into the\l"
    .string "synagogue and taught: and there was a\l"
    .string "man whose right hand was withered.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_7::
    .string "And the scribes and Pharisees\n"
    .string "watched him, whether he would heal\l"
    .string "on the sabbath day; that they might\l"
    .string "find an accusation against him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_8::
    .string "But he knew their thoughts, and said\n"
    .string "to the man which had the withered\l"
    .string "hand, Rise up, and stand forth in the\l"
    .string "midst. And he arose and stood forth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_9::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them, I will\n"
    .string "ask you one thing; Is it lawful on\l"
    .string "the sabbath days to do good, or to do\l"
    .string "evil? to save life, or to destroy\l"
    .string "it?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_10::
    .string "And looking round about upon them\n"
    .string "all, he said unto the man, Stretch\l"
    .string "forth thy hand. And he did so: and his\l"
    .string "hand was restored whole as the other$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_11::
    .string "And they were filled with madness;\n"
    .string "and communed one with another what\l"
    .string "they might do to Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_12::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "that he went out into a mountain to\l"
    .string "pray, and continued all night in\l"
    .string "prayer to God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_13::
    .string "And when it was day, he called unto\n"
    .string "him his disciples: and of them he\l"
    .string "chose twelve, whom also he named\l"
    .string "apostles;"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_14::
    .string "Simon, (whom he also named Peter,)\n"
    .string "and Andrew his brother, James and\l"
    .string "John, Philip and Bartholomew,"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_15::
    .string "Matthew and Thomas, James the son of\n"
    .string "Alphaeus, and Simon called\l"
    .string "Zelotes,"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_16::
    .string "And Judas the brother of James, and\n"
    .string "Judas Iscariot, which also was the\l"
    .string "traitor$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_17::
    .string "And he came down with them, and\n"
    .string "stood in the plain, and the company\l"
    .string "of his disciples, and a great\l"
    .string "multitude of people out of all\l"
    .string "Judaea and Jerusalem, and from the\l"
    .string "sea coast of Tyre and Sidon, which\l"
    .string "came to hear him, and to be healed of\l"
    .string "their diseases;"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_18::
    .string "And they that were vexed with\n"
    .string "unclean spirits: and they were\l"
    .string "healed$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_19::
    .string "And the whole multitude sought to\n"
    .string "touch him: for there went virtue out\l"
    .string "of him, and healed them all.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_20::
    .string "And he lifted up his eyes on his\n"
    .string "disciples, and said, Blessed be ye\l"
    .string "poor: for yours is the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_21::
    .string "Blessed are ye that hunger now: for\n"
    .string "ye shall be filled. Blessed are ye\l"
    .string "that weep now: for ye shall laugh.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_22::
    .string "Blessed are ye, when men shall\n"
    .string "hate you, and when they shall\l"
    .string "separate you from their company,\l"
    .string "and shall reproach you, and cast\l"
    .string "out your name as evil, for the Son of\l"
    .string "man’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_23::
    .string "Rejoice ye in that day, and leap\n"
    .string "for joy: for, behold, your reward is\l"
    .string "great in heaven: for in the like\l"
    .string "manner did their fathers unto the\l"
    .string "prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_24::
    .string "But woe unto you that are rich! for\n"
    .string "ye have received your consolation.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_25::
    .string "Woe unto you that are full! for ye\n"
    .string "shall hunger. Woe unto you that\l"
    .string "laugh now! for ye shall mourn and\l"
    .string "weep.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_26::
    .string "Woe unto you, when all men shall\n"
    .string "speak well of you! for so did their\l"
    .string "fathers to the false prophets.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_27::
    .string "But I say unto you which hear, Love\n"
    .string "your enemies, do good to them which\l"
    .string "hate you,"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_28::
    .string "Bless them that curse you, and pray\n"
    .string "for them which despitefully use you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_29::
    .string "And unto him that smiteth thee on\n"
    .string "the one cheek offer also the other;\l"
    .string "and him that taketh away thy cloak\l"
    .string "forbid not to take thy coat also.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_30::
    .string "Give to every man that asketh of\n"
    .string "thee; and of him that taketh away thy\l"
    .string "goods ask them not again.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_31::
    .string "And as ye would that men should do\n"
    .string "to you, do ye also to them likewise.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_32::
    .string "For if ye love them which love you,\n"
    .string "what thank have ye? for sinners also\l"
    .string "love those that love them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_33::
    .string "And if ye do good to them which do\n"
    .string "good to you, what thank have ye? for\l"
    .string "sinners also do even the same.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_34::
    .string "And if ye lend to them of whom ye\n"
    .string "hope to receive, what thank have ye?\l"
    .string "for sinners also lend to sinners, to\l"
    .string "receive as much again.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_35::
    .string "But love ye your enemies, and do\n"
    .string "good, and lend, hoping for nothing\l"
    .string "again; and your reward shall be\l"
    .string "great, and ye shall be the children\l"
    .string "of the Highest: for he is kind unto\l"
    .string "the unthankful and to the evil.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_36::
    .string "Be ye therefore merciful, as your\n"
    .string "Father also is merciful.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_37::
    .string "Judge not, and ye shall not be\n"
    .string "judged: condemn not, and ye shall\l"
    .string "not be condemned: forgive, and ye\l"
    .string "shall be forgiven:"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_38::
    .string "Give, and it shall be given unto\n"
    .string "you; good measure, pressed down, and\l"
    .string "shaken together, and running over,\l"
    .string "shall men give into your bosom. For\l"
    .string "with the same measure that ye mete\l"
    .string "withal it shall be measured to you\l"
    .string "again$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_39::
    .string "And he spake a parable unto them,\n"
    .string "Can the blind lead the blind?\l"
    .string "shall they not both fall into the\l"
    .string "ditch?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_40::
    .string "The disciple is not above his\n"
    .string "master: but every one that is\l"
    .string "perfect shall be as his master$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_41::
    .string "And why beholdest thou the mote\n"
    .string "that is in thy brother’s eye, but\l"
    .string "perceivest not the beam that is in\l"
    .string "thine own eye?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_42::
    .string "Either how canst thou say to thy\n"
    .string "brother, Brother, let me pull out\l"
    .string "the mote that is in thine eye, when\l"
    .string "thou thyself beholdest not the beam\l"
    .string "that is in thine own eye? Thou\l"
    .string "hypocrite, cast out first the beam\l"
    .string "out of thine own eye, and then shalt\l"
    .string "thou see clearly to pull out the\l"
    .string "mote that is in thy brother’s eye$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_43::
    .string "For a good tree bringeth not forth\n"
    .string "corrupt fruit; neither doth a\l"
    .string "corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_44::
    .string "For every tree is known by his own\n"
    .string "fruit. For of thorns men do not\l"
    .string "gather figs, nor of a bramble bush\l"
    .string "gather they grapes.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_45::
    .string "A good man out of the good treasure\n"
    .string "of his heart bringeth forth that\l"
    .string "which is good; and an evil man out of\l"
    .string "the evil treasure of his heart\l"
    .string "bringeth forth that which is evil:\l"
    .string "for of the abundance of the heart his\l"
    .string "mouth speaketh.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_46::
    .string "And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and\n"
    .string "do not the things which I say?"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_47::
    .string "Whosoever cometh to me, and heareth\n"
    .string "my sayings, and doeth them, I will\l"
    .string "shew you to whom he is like:"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_48::
    .string "He is like a man which built an\n"
    .string "house, and digged deep, and laid the\l"
    .string "foundation on a rock: and when the\l"
    .string "flood arose, the stream beat\l"
    .string "vehemently upon that house, and\l"
    .string "could not shake it: for it was\l"
    .string "founded upon a rock$"
Bible_Text_Luke_6_49::
    .string "But he that heareth, and doeth not,\n"
    .string "is like a man that without a\l"
    .string "foundation built an house upon the\l"
    .string "earth; against which the stream did\l"
    .string "beat vehemently, and immediately it\l"
    .string "fell; and the ruin of that house was\l"
    .string "great.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_1::
    .string "Now when he had ended all his\n"
    .string "sayings in the audience of the\l"
    .string "people, he entered into Capernaum.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_2::
    .string "And a certain centurion’s servant,\n"
    .string "who was dear unto him, was sick, and\l"
    .string "ready to die.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_3::
    .string "And when he heard of Jesus, he sent\n"
    .string "unto him the elders of the Jews,\l"
    .string "beseeching him that he would come\l"
    .string "and heal his servant.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_4::
    .string "And when they came to Jesus, they\n"
    .string "besought him instantly, saying, That\l"
    .string "he was worthy for whom he should do\l"
    .string "this:"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_5::
    .string "For he loveth our nation, and he\n"
    .string "hath built us a synagogue$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_6::
    .string "Then Jesus went with them. And when\n"
    .string "he was now not far from the house, the\l"
    .string "centurion sent friends to him, saying\l"
    .string "unto him, Lord, trouble not thyself:\l"
    .string "for I am not worthy that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest enter under my roof:"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_7::
    .string "Wherefore neither thought I myself\n"
    .string "worthy to come unto thee: but say in a\l"
    .string "word, and my servant shall be healed$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_8::
    .string "For I also am a man set under\n"
    .string "authority, having under me soldiers,\l"
    .string "and I say unto one, Go, and he goeth;\l"
    .string "and to another, Come, and he cometh;\l"
    .string "and to my servant, Do this, and he\l"
    .string "doeth it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_9::
    .string "When Jesus heard these things, he\n"
    .string "marvelled at him, and turned him\l"
    .string "about, and said unto the people\l"
    .string "that followed him, I say unto you, I\l"
    .string "have not found so great faith, no,\l"
    .string "not in Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_10::
    .string "And they that were sent, returning\n"
    .string "to the house, found the servant\l"
    .string "whole that had been sick.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_11::
    .string "And it came to pass the day after,\n"
    .string "that he went into a city called\l"
    .string "Nain; and many of his disciples went\l"
    .string "with him, and much people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_12::
    .string "Now when he came nigh to the gate of\n"
    .string "the city, behold, there was a dead\l"
    .string "man carried out, the only son of his\l"
    .string "mother, and she was a widow: and much\l"
    .string "people of the city was with her.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_13::
    .string "And when the Lord saw her, he had\n"
    .string "compassion on her, and said unto\l"
    .string "her, Weep not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_14::
    .string "And he came and touched the bier:\n"
    .string "and they that bare him stood still.\l"
    .string "And he said, Young man, I say unto\l"
    .string "thee, Arise.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_15::
    .string "And he that was dead sat up, and\n"
    .string "began to speak. And he delivered him\l"
    .string "to his mother.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_16::
    .string "And there came a fear on all: and\n"
    .string "they glorified God, saying, That a\l"
    .string "great prophet is risen up among us;\l"
    .string "and, That God hath visited his\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_17::
    .string "And this rumour of him went forth\n"
    .string "throughout all Judaea, and\l"
    .string "throughout all the region round\l"
    .string "about.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_18::
    .string "And the disciples of John shewed\n"
    .string "him of all these things.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_19::
    .string "And John calling unto him two of\n"
    .string "his disciples sent them to Jesus,\l"
    .string "saying, Art thou he that should\l"
    .string "come? or look we for another?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_20::
    .string "When the men were come unto him,\n"
    .string "they said, John Baptist hath sent us\l"
    .string "unto thee, saying, Art thou he that\l"
    .string "should come? or look we for another?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_21::
    .string "And in that same hour he cured many\n"
    .string "of their infirmities and plagues,\l"
    .string "and of evil spirits; and unto many\l"
    .string "that were blind he gave sight$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_22::
    .string "Then Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "Go your way, and tell John what\l"
    .string "things ye have seen and heard; how\l"
    .string "that the blind see, the lame walk,\l"
    .string "the lepers are cleansed, the deaf\l"
    .string "hear, the dead are raised, to the\l"
    .string "poor the gospel is preached.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_23::
    .string "And blessed is he, whosoever shall\n"
    .string "not be offended in me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_24::
    .string "And when the messengers of John were\n"
    .string "departed, he began to speak unto the\l"
    .string "people concerning John, What went\l"
    .string "ye out into the wilderness for to\l"
    .string "see? A reed shaken with the wind?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_25::
    .string "But what went ye out for to see? A\n"
    .string "man clothed in soft raiment?\l"
    .string "Behold, they which are gorgeously\l"
    .string "apparelled, and live\l"
    .string "delicately, are in kings’ courts$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_26::
    .string "But what went ye out for to see? A\n"
    .string "prophet? Yea, I say unto you, and\l"
    .string "much more than a prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_27::
    .string "This is he, of whom it is written,\n"
    .string "Behold, I send my messenger before\l"
    .string "thy face, which shall prepare thy\l"
    .string "way before thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_28::
    .string "For I say unto you, Among those that\n"
    .string "are born of women there is not a\l"
    .string "greater prophet than John the\l"
    .string "Baptist: but he that is least in the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God is greater than he.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_29::
    .string "And all the people that heard\n"
    .string "him, and the publicans, justified\l"
    .string "God, being baptized with the\l"
    .string "baptism of John.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_30::
    .string "But the Pharisees and lawyers\n"
    .string "rejected the counsel of God against\l"
    .string "themselves, being not baptized of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_31::
    .string "And the Lord said, Whereunto then\n"
    .string "shall I liken the men of this\l"
    .string "generation? and to what are they\l"
    .string "like?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_32::
    .string "They are like unto children\n"
    .string "sitting in the marketplace, and\l"
    .string "calling one to another, and saying,\l"
    .string "We have piped unto you, and ye have\l"
    .string "not danced; we have mourned to you,\l"
    .string "and ye have not wept$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_33::
    .string "For John the Baptist came neither\n"
    .string "eating bread nor drinking wine; and\l"
    .string "ye say, He hath a devil.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_34::
    .string "The Son of man is come eating and\n"
    .string "drinking; and ye say, Behold a\l"
    .string "gluttonous man, and a winebibber, a\l"
    .string "friend of publicans and sinners!"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_35::
    .string "But wisdom is justified of all her\n"
    .string "children$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_36::
    .string "And one of the Pharisees desired him\n"
    .string "that he would eat with him. And he\l"
    .string "went into the Pharisee’s house, and\l"
    .string "sat down to meat.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_37::
    .string "And, behold, a woman in the city,\n"
    .string "which was a sinner, when she knew\l"
    .string "that Jesus sat at meat in the\l"
    .string "Pharisee’s house, brought an\l"
    .string "alabaster box of ointment,"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_38::
    .string "And stood at his feet behind him\n"
    .string "weeping, and began to wash his feet\l"
    .string "with tears, and did wipe them with\l"
    .string "the hairs of her head, and kissed his\l"
    .string "feet, and anointed them with the\l"
    .string "ointment$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_39::
    .string "Now when the Pharisee which had\n"
    .string "bidden him saw it, he spake within\l"
    .string "himself, saying, This man, if he were\l"
    .string "a prophet, would have known who and\l"
    .string "what manner of woman this is that\l"
    .string "toucheth him: for she is a sinner.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_40::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "Simon, I have somewhat to say unto\l"
    .string "thee. And he saith, Master, say on.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_41::
    .string "There was a certain creditor which\n"
    .string "had two debtors: the one owed five\l"
    .string "hundred pence, and the other fifty.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_42::
    .string "And when they had nothing to pay, he\n"
    .string "frankly forgave them both. Tell me\l"
    .string "therefore, which of them will love\l"
    .string "him most?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_43::
    .string "Simon answered and said, I suppose\n"
    .string "that he, to whom he forgave most And\l"
    .string "he said unto him, Thou hast rightly\l"
    .string "judged.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_44::
    .string "And he turned to the woman, and said\n"
    .string "unto Simon, Seest thou this woman? I\l"
    .string "entered into thine house, thou gavest\l"
    .string "me no water for my feet: but she hath\l"
    .string "washed my feet with tears, and wiped\l"
    .string "them with the hairs of her head.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_45::
    .string "Thou gavest me no kiss: but this\n"
    .string "woman since the time I came in hath\l"
    .string "not ceased to kiss my feet.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_46::
    .string "My head with oil thou didst not\n"
    .string "anoint: but this woman hath anointed\l"
    .string "my feet with ointment.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_47::
    .string "Wherefore I say unto thee, Her sins,\n"
    .string "which are many, are forgiven; for she\l"
    .string "loved much: but to whom little is\l"
    .string "forgiven, the same loveth little.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_48::
    .string "And he said unto her, Thy sins are\n"
    .string "forgiven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_49::
    .string "And they that sat at meat with him\n"
    .string "began to say within themselves, Who\l"
    .string "is this that forgiveth sins also?"
Bible_Text_Luke_7_50::
    .string "And he said to the woman, Thy faith\n"
    .string "hath saved thee; go in peace$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_1::
    .string "And it came to pass afterward, that\n"
    .string "he went throughout every city and\l"
    .string "village, preaching and shewing the\l"
    .string "glad tidings of the kingdom of God:\l"
    .string "and the twelve were with him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_2::
    .string "And certain women, which had been\n"
    .string "healed of evil spirits and\l"
    .string "infirmities, Mary called\l"
    .string "Magdalene, out of whom went seven\l"
    .string "devils,"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_3::
    .string "And Joanna the wife of Chuza Herod’s\n"
    .string "steward, and Susanna, and many\l"
    .string "others, which ministered unto him of\l"
    .string "their substance$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_4::
    .string "And when much people were\n"
    .string "gathered together, and were come to\l"
    .string "him out of every city, he spake by a\l"
    .string "parable:"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_5::
    .string "A sower went out to sow his seed: and\n"
    .string "as he sowed, some fell by the way\l"
    .string "side; and it was trodden down, and\l"
    .string "the fowls of the air devoured it$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_6::
    .string "And some fell upon a rock; and as\n"
    .string "soon as it was sprung up, it\l"
    .string "withered away, because it lacked\l"
    .string "moisture.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_7::
    .string "And some fell among thorns; and the\n"
    .string "thorns sprang up with it, and choked\l"
    .string "it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_8::
    .string "And other fell on good ground, and\n"
    .string "sprang up, and bare fruit an\l"
    .string "hundredfold. And when he had said\l"
    .string "these things, he cried, He that hath\l"
    .string "ears to hear, let him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_9::
    .string "And his disciples asked him,\n"
    .string "saying, What might this parable be?"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_10::
    .string "And he said, Unto you it is given to\n"
    .string "know the mysteries of the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God: but to others in parables; that\l"
    .string "seeing they might not see, and\l"
    .string "hearing they might not understand$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_11::
    .string "Now the parable is this: The seed\n"
    .string "is the word of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_12::
    .string "Those by the way side are they that\n"
    .string "hear; then cometh the devil, and\l"
    .string "taketh away the word out of their\l"
    .string "hearts, lest they should believe\l"
    .string "and be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_13::
    .string "They on the rock are they, which,\n"
    .string "when they hear, receive the word with\l"
    .string "joy; and these have no root, which\l"
    .string "for a while believe, and in time of\l"
    .string "temptation fall away.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_14::
    .string "And that which fell among thorns\n"
    .string "are they, which, when they have\l"
    .string "heard, go forth, and are choked with\l"
    .string "cares and riches and pleasures of\l"
    .string "this life, and bring no fruit to\l"
    .string "perfection.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_15::
    .string "But that on the good ground are\n"
    .string "they, which in an honest and good\l"
    .string "heart, having heard the word, keep\l"
    .string "it, and bring forth fruit with\l"
    .string "patience.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_16::
    .string "No man, when he hath lighted a\n"
    .string "candle, covereth it with a vessel,\l"
    .string "or putteth it under a bed; but\l"
    .string "setteth it on a candlestick, that\l"
    .string "they which enter in may see the\l"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_17::
    .string "For nothing is secret, that shall\n"
    .string "not be made manifest; neither any\l"
    .string "thing hid, that shall not be known\l"
    .string "and come abroad.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_18::
    .string "Take heed therefore how ye hear: for\n"
    .string "whosoever hath, to him shall be\l"
    .string "given; and whosoever hath not, from\l"
    .string "him shall be taken even that which\l"
    .string "he seemeth to have.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_19::
    .string "Then came to him his mother and his\n"
    .string "brethren, and could not come at him\l"
    .string "for the press.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_20::
    .string "And it was told him by certain\n"
    .string "which said, Thy mother and thy\l"
    .string "brethren stand without, desiring to\l"
    .string "see thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_21::
    .string "And he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "My mother and my brethren are these\l"
    .string "which hear the word of God, and do it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_22::
    .string "Now it came to pass on a certain\n"
    .string "day, that he went into a ship with\l"
    .string "his disciples: and he said unto\l"
    .string "them, Let us go over unto the other\l"
    .string "side of the lake. And they launched\l"
    .string "forth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_23::
    .string "But as they sailed he fell\n"
    .string "asleep: and there came down a storm\l"
    .string "of wind on the lake; and they were\l"
    .string "filled with water, and were in\l"
    .string "jeopardy.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_24::
    .string "And they came to him, and awoke him,\n"
    .string "saying, Master, master, we perish.\l"
    .string "Then he arose, and rebuked the wind\l"
    .string "and the raging of the water: and they\l"
    .string "ceased, and there was a calm.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_25::
    .string "And he said unto them, Where is your\n"
    .string "faith? And they being afraid\l"
    .string "wondered, saying one to another, What\l"
    .string "manner of man is this! for he\l"
    .string "commandeth even the winds and water,\l"
    .string "and they obey him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_26::
    .string "And they arrived at the country of\n"
    .string "the Gadarenes, which is over against\l"
    .string "Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_27::
    .string "And when he went forth to land,\n"
    .string "there met him out of the city a\l"
    .string "certain man, which had devils long\l"
    .string "time, and ware no clothes, neither\l"
    .string "abode in any house, but in the tombs.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_28::
    .string "When he saw Jesus, he cried out, and\n"
    .string "fell down before him, and with a\l"
    .string "loud voice said, What have I to do\l"
    .string "with thee, Jesus, thou Son of God\l"
    .string "most high? I beseech thee, torment me\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_29::
    .string "(For he had commanded the unclean\n"
    .string "spirit to come out of the man. For\l"
    .string "oftentimes it had caught him: and he\l"
    .string "was kept bound with chains and in\l"
    .string "fetters; and he brake the bands, and\l"
    .string "was driven of the devil into the\l"
    .string "wilderness.)"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_30::
    .string "And Jesus asked him, saying, What is\n"
    .string "thy name? And he said, Legion:\l"
    .string "because many devils were entered\l"
    .string "into him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_31::
    .string "And they besought him that he would\n"
    .string "not command them to go out into the\l"
    .string "deep.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_32::
    .string "And there was there an herd of many\n"
    .string "swine feeding on the mountain: and\l"
    .string "they besought him that he would\l"
    .string "suffer them to enter into them. And\l"
    .string "he suffered them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_33::
    .string "Then went the devils out of the man,\n"
    .string "and entered into the swine: and the\l"
    .string "herd ran violently down a steep\l"
    .string "place into the lake, and were\l"
    .string "choked.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_34::
    .string "When they that fed them saw what was\n"
    .string "done, they fled, and went and told\l"
    .string "it in the city and in the country.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_35::
    .string "Then they went out to see what was\n"
    .string "done; and came to Jesus, and found\l"
    .string "the man, out of whom the devils were\l"
    .string "departed, sitting at the feet of\l"
    .string "Jesus, clothed, and in his right\l"
    .string "mind: and they were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_36::
    .string "They also which saw it told them by\n"
    .string "what means he that was possessed of\l"
    .string "the devils was healed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_37::
    .string "Then the whole multitude of the\n"
    .string "country of the Gadarenes round about\l"
    .string "besought him to depart from them;\l"
    .string "for they were taken with great fear:\l"
    .string "and he went up into the ship, and\l"
    .string "returned back again.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_38::
    .string "Now the man out of whom the devils\n"
    .string "were departed besought him that he\l"
    .string "might be with him: but Jesus sent him\l"
    .string "away, saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_39::
    .string "Return to thine own house, and shew\n"
    .string "how great things God hath done unto\l"
    .string "thee. And he went his way, and\l"
    .string "published throughout the whole city\l"
    .string "how great things Jesus had done unto\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_40::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when\n"
    .string "Jesus was returned, the people\l"
    .string "gladly received him: for they were\l"
    .string "all waiting for him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_41::
    .string "And, behold, there came a man named\n"
    .string "Jairus, and he was a ruler of the\l"
    .string "synagogue: and he fell down at\l"
    .string "Jesus’ feet, and besought him that he\l"
    .string "would come into his house:"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_42::
    .string "For he had one only daughter, about\n"
    .string "twelve years of age, and she lay a\l"
    .string "dying. But as he went the people\l"
    .string "thronged him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_43::
    .string "And a woman having an issue of\n"
    .string "blood twelve years, which had spent\l"
    .string "all her living upon physicians,\l"
    .string "neither could be healed of any,"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_44::
    .string "Came behind him, and touched the\n"
    .string "border of his garment: and\l"
    .string "immediately her issue of blood\l"
    .string "stanched$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_45::
    .string "And Jesus said, Who touched me? When\n"
    .string "all denied, Peter and they that were\l"
    .string "with him said, Master, the multitude\l"
    .string "throng thee and press thee, and\l"
    .string "sayest thou, Who touched me?"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_46::
    .string "And Jesus said, Somebody hath\n"
    .string "touched me: for I perceive that\l"
    .string "virtue is gone out of me$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_47::
    .string "And when the woman saw that she was\n"
    .string "not hid, she came trembling, and\l"
    .string "falling down before him, she\l"
    .string "declared unto him before all the\l"
    .string "people for what cause she had\l"
    .string "touched him, and how she was healed\l"
    .string "immediately.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_48::
    .string "And he said unto her, Daughter, be\n"
    .string "of good comfort: thy faith hath made\l"
    .string "thee whole; go in peace.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_49::
    .string "While he yet spake, there cometh\n"
    .string "one from the ruler of the\l"
    .string "synagogue’s house, saying to him, Thy\l"
    .string "daughter is dead; trouble not the\l"
    .string "Master.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_50::
    .string "But when Jesus heard it, he answered\n"
    .string "him, saying, Fear not: believe only,\l"
    .string "and she shall be made whole.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_51::
    .string "And when he came into the house, he\n"
    .string "suffered no man to go in, save Peter,\l"
    .string "and James, and John, and the father\l"
    .string "and the mother of the maiden.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_52::
    .string "And all wept, and bewailed her:\n"
    .string "but he said, Weep not; she is not\l"
    .string "dead, but sleepeth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_53::
    .string "And they laughed him to scorn,\n"
    .string "knowing that she was dead.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_54::
    .string "And he put them all out, and took\n"
    .string "her by the hand, and called, saying,\l"
    .string "Maid, arise.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_55::
    .string "And her spirit came again, and she\n"
    .string "arose straightway: and he commanded\l"
    .string "to give her meat.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_8_56::
    .string "And her parents were astonished:\n"
    .string "but he charged them that they should\l"
    .string "tell no man what was done.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_1::
    .string "Then he called his twelve\n"
    .string "disciples together, and gave them\l"
    .string "power and authority over all\l"
    .string "devils, and to cure diseases.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_2::
    .string "And he sent them to preach the\n"
    .string "kingdom of God, and to heal the sick.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_3::
    .string "And he said unto them, Take nothing\n"
    .string "for your journey, neither staves, nor\l"
    .string "scrip, neither bread, neither money;\l"
    .string "neither have two coats apiece.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_4::
    .string "And whatsoever house ye enter into,\n"
    .string "there abide, and thence depart.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_5::
    .string "And whosoever will not receive\n"
    .string "you, when ye go out of that city,\l"
    .string "shake off the very dust from your\l"
    .string "feet for a testimony against them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_6::
    .string "And they departed, and went through\n"
    .string "the towns, preaching the gospel,\l"
    .string "and healing every where.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_7::
    .string "Now Herod the tetrarch heard of\n"
    .string "all that was done by him: and he was\l"
    .string "perplexed, because that it was said\l"
    .string "of some, that John was risen from the\l"
    .string "dead;"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_8::
    .string "And of some, that Elias had\n"
    .string "appeared; and of others, that one of\l"
    .string "the old prophets was risen again$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_9::
    .string "And Herod said, John have I\n"
    .string "beheaded: but who is this, of whom I\l"
    .string "hear such things? And he desired to\l"
    .string "see him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_10::
    .string "And the apostles, when they were\n"
    .string "returned, told him all that they\l"
    .string "had done. And he took them, and went\l"
    .string "aside privately into a desert\l"
    .string "place belonging to the city called\l"
    .string "Bethsaida.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_11::
    .string "And the people, when they knew it,\n"
    .string "followed him: and he received them,\l"
    .string "and spake unto them of the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God, and healed them that had need\l"
    .string "of healing.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_12::
    .string "And when the day began to wear away,\n"
    .string "then came the twelve, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Send the multitude away, that\l"
    .string "they may go into the towns and\l"
    .string "country round about, and lodge, and\l"
    .string "get victuals: for we are here in a\l"
    .string "desert place.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_13::
    .string "But he said unto them, Give ye them\n"
    .string "to eat. And they said, We have no more\l"
    .string "but five loaves and two fishes;\l"
    .string "except we should go and buy meat for\l"
    .string "all this people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_14::
    .string "For they were about five thousand\n"
    .string "men. And he said to his disciples,\l"
    .string "Make them sit down by fifties in a\l"
    .string "company.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_15::
    .string "And they did so, and made them all\n"
    .string "sit down.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_16::
    .string "Then he took the five loaves and\n"
    .string "the two fishes, and looking up to\l"
    .string "heaven, he blessed them, and brake,\l"
    .string "and gave to the disciples to set\l"
    .string "before the multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_17::
    .string "And they did eat, and were all\n"
    .string "filled: and there was taken up of\l"
    .string "fragments that remained to them\l"
    .string "twelve baskets.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_18::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he was\n"
    .string "alone praying, his disciples were\l"
    .string "with him: and he asked them, saying,\l"
    .string "Whom say the people that I am?"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_19::
    .string "They answering said, John the\n"
    .string "Baptist; but some say, Elias; and\l"
    .string "others say, that one of the old\l"
    .string "prophets is risen again$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_20::
    .string "He said unto them, But whom say ye\n"
    .string "that I am? Peter answering said, The\l"
    .string "Christ of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_21::
    .string "And he straitly charged them, and\n"
    .string "commanded them to tell no man that\l"
    .string "thing;"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_22::
    .string "Saying, The Son of man must suffer\n"
    .string "many things, and be rejected of the\l"
    .string "elders and chief priests and\l"
    .string "scribes, and be slain, and be raised\l"
    .string "the third day$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_23::
    .string "And he said to them all, If any man\n"
    .string "will come after me, let him deny\l"
    .string "himself, and take up his cross\l"
    .string "daily, and follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_24::
    .string "For whosoever will save his life\n"
    .string "shall lose it: but whosoever will\l"
    .string "lose his life for my sake, the same\l"
    .string "shall save it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_25::
    .string "For what is a man advantaged, if he\n"
    .string "gain the whole world, and lose\l"
    .string "himself, or be cast away?"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_26::
    .string "For whosoever shall be ashamed of\n"
    .string "me and of my words, of him shall the\l"
    .string "Son of man be ashamed, when he shall\l"
    .string "come in his own glory, and in his\l"
    .string "Father’s, and of the holy angels$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_27::
    .string "But I tell you of a truth, there be\n"
    .string "some standing here, which shall not\l"
    .string "taste of death, till they see the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_28::
    .string "And it came to pass about an eight\n"
    .string "days after these sayings, he took\l"
    .string "Peter and John and James, and went up\l"
    .string "into a mountain to pray.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_29::
    .string "And as he prayed, the fashion of his\n"
    .string "countenance was altered, and his\l"
    .string "raiment was white and glistering.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_30::
    .string "And, behold, there talked with him\n"
    .string "two men, which were Moses and Elias:"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_31::
    .string "Who appeared in glory, and spake\n"
    .string "of his decease which he should\l"
    .string "accomplish at Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_32::
    .string "But Peter and they that were with\n"
    .string "him were heavy with sleep: and when\l"
    .string "they were awake, they saw his glory,\l"
    .string "and the two men that stood with him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_33::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they\n"
    .string "departed from him, Peter said unto\l"
    .string "Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be\l"
    .string "here: and let us make three\l"
    .string "tabernacles; one for thee, and one\l"
    .string "for Moses, and one for Elias: not\l"
    .string "knowing what he said.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_34::
    .string "While he thus spake, there came a\n"
    .string "cloud, and overshadowed them: and\l"
    .string "they feared as they entered into the\l"
    .string "cloud.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_35::
    .string "And there came a voice out of the\n"
    .string "cloud, saying, This is my beloved\l"
    .string "Son: hear him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_36::
    .string "And when the voice was past, Jesus\n"
    .string "was found alone. And they kept it\l"
    .string "close, and told no man in those days\l"
    .string "any of those things which they had\l"
    .string "seen.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_37::
    .string "And it came to pass, that on the\n"
    .string "next day, when they were come down\l"
    .string "from the hill, much people met\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_38::
    .string "And, behold, a man of the company\n"
    .string "cried out, saying, Master, I beseech\l"
    .string "thee, look upon my son: for he is\l"
    .string "mine only child.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_39::
    .string "And, lo, a spirit taketh him, and\n"
    .string "he suddenly crieth out; and it\l"
    .string "teareth him that he foameth again,\l"
    .string "and bruising him hardly departeth\l"
    .string "from him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_40::
    .string "And I besought thy disciples to\n"
    .string "cast him out; and they could not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_41::
    .string "And Jesus answering said, O\n"
    .string "faithless and perverse generation,\l"
    .string "how long shall I be with you, and\l"
    .string "suffer you? Bring thy son hither.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_42::
    .string "And as he was yet a coming, the\n"
    .string "devil threw him down, and tare him.\l"
    .string "And Jesus rebuked the unclean\l"
    .string "spirit, and healed the child, and\l"
    .string "delivered him again to his father.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_43::
    .string "And they were all amazed at the\n"
    .string "mighty power of God. But while they\l"
    .string "wondered every one at all things\l"
    .string "which Jesus did, he said unto his\l"
    .string "disciples,"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_44::
    .string "Let these sayings sink down into\n"
    .string "your ears: for the Son of man shall\l"
    .string "be delivered into the hands of men$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_45::
    .string "But they understood not this saying,\n"
    .string "and it was hid from them, that they\l"
    .string "perceived it not: and they feared to\l"
    .string "ask him of that saying.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_46::
    .string "Then there arose a reasoning among\n"
    .string "them, which of them should be\l"
    .string "greatest.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_47::
    .string "And Jesus, perceiving the thought\n"
    .string "of their heart, took a child, and set\l"
    .string "him by him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_48::
    .string "And said unto them, Whosoever\n"
    .string "shall receive this child in my name\l"
    .string "receiveth me: and whosoever shall\l"
    .string "receive me receiveth him that sent\l"
    .string "me: for he that is least among you\l"
    .string "all, the same shall be great$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_49::
    .string "And John answered and said, Master,\n"
    .string "we saw one casting out devils in thy\l"
    .string "name; and we forbad him, because he\l"
    .string "followeth not with us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_50::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Forbid him\n"
    .string "not: for he that is not against us is\l"
    .string "for us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_51::
    .string "And it came to pass, when the time\n"
    .string "was come that he should be received\l"
    .string "up, he stedfastly set his face to go\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_52::
    .string "And sent messengers before his face:\n"
    .string "and they went, and entered into a\l"
    .string "village of the Samaritans, to make\l"
    .string "ready for him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_53::
    .string "And they did not receive him,\n"
    .string "because his face was as though he\l"
    .string "would go to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_54::
    .string "And when his disciples James and\n"
    .string "John saw this, they said, Lord, wilt\l"
    .string "thou that we command fire to come\l"
    .string "down from heaven, and consume them,\l"
    .string "even as Elias did?"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_55::
    .string "But he turned, and rebuked them, and\n"
    .string "said, Ye know not what manner of\l"
    .string "spirit ye are of$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_56::
    .string "For the Son of man is not come to\n"
    .string "destroy men’s lives, but to save them\l"
    .string " And they went to another village.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_57::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as they\n"
    .string "went in the way, a certain man said\l"
    .string "unto him, Lord, I will follow thee\l"
    .string "whithersoever thou goest.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_58::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Foxes have\n"
    .string "holes, and birds of the air have\l"
    .string "nests; but the Son of man hath not\l"
    .string "where to lay his head.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_59::
    .string "And he said unto another, Follow me\n"
    .string " But he said, Lord, suffer me first\l"
    .string "to go and bury my father.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_60::
    .string "Jesus said unto him, Let the dead\n"
    .string "bury their dead: but go thou and\l"
    .string "preach the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_61::
    .string "And another also said, Lord, I\n"
    .string "will follow thee; but let me first\l"
    .string "go bid them farewell, which are at\l"
    .string "home at my house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_9_62::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, No man,\n"
    .string "having put his hand to the plough,\l"
    .string "and looking back, is fit for the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_1::
    .string "After these things the LORD\n"
    .string "appointed other seventy also, and\l"
    .string "sent them two and two before his face\l"
    .string "into every city and place, whither\l"
    .string "he himself would come.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_2::
    .string "Therefore said he unto them, The\n"
    .string "harvest truly is great, but the\l"
    .string "labourers are few: pray ye therefore\l"
    .string "the Lord of the harvest, that he\l"
    .string "would send forth labourers into his\l"
    .string "harvest.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_3::
    .string "Go your ways: behold, I send you\n"
    .string "forth as lambs among wolves.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_4::
    .string "Carry neither purse, nor scrip,\n"
    .string "nor shoes: and salute no man by the\l"
    .string "way.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_5::
    .string "And into whatsoever house ye enter,\n"
    .string "first say, Peace be to this house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_6::
    .string "And if the son of peace be there,\n"
    .string "your peace shall rest upon it: if\l"
    .string "not, it shall turn to you again.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_7::
    .string "And in the same house remain, eating\n"
    .string "and drinking such things as they\l"
    .string "give: for the labourer is worthy of\l"
    .string "his hire. Go not from house to house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_8::
    .string "And into whatsoever city ye enter,\n"
    .string "and they receive you, eat such things\l"
    .string "as are set before you:"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_9::
    .string "And heal the sick that are therein,\n"
    .string "and say unto them, The kingdom of God\l"
    .string "is come nigh unto you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_10::
    .string "But into whatsoever city ye enter,\n"
    .string "and they receive you not, go your\l"
    .string "ways out into the streets of the\l"
    .string "same, and say,"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_11::
    .string "Even the very dust of your city,\n"
    .string "which cleaveth on us, we do wipe off\l"
    .string "against you: notwithstanding be ye\l"
    .string "sure of this, that the kingdom of God\l"
    .string "is come nigh unto you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_12::
    .string "But I say unto you, that it shall\n"
    .string "be more tolerable in that day for\l"
    .string "Sodom, than for that city.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_13::
    .string "Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto\n"
    .string "thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty\l"
    .string "works had been done in Tyre and\l"
    .string "Sidon, which have been done in you,\l"
    .string "they had a great while ago repented,\l"
    .string "sitting in sackcloth and ashes.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_14::
    .string "But it shall be more tolerable\n"
    .string "for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment,\l"
    .string "than for you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_15::
    .string "And thou, Capernaum, which art\n"
    .string "exalted to heaven, shalt be thrust\l"
    .string "down to hell.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_16::
    .string "He that heareth you heareth me; and\n"
    .string "he that despiseth you despiseth me;\l"
    .string "and he that despiseth me despiseth\l"
    .string "him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_17::
    .string "And the seventy returned again with\n"
    .string "joy, saying, Lord, even the devils\l"
    .string "are subject unto us through thy name.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_18::
    .string "And he said unto them, I beheld\n"
    .string "Satan as lightning fall from\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_19::
    .string "Behold, I give unto you power to\n"
    .string "tread on serpents and scorpions,\l"
    .string "and over all the power of the\l"
    .string "enemy: and nothing shall by any\l"
    .string "means hurt you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_20::
    .string "Notwithstanding in this rejoice\n"
    .string "not, that the spirits are subject\l"
    .string "unto you; but rather rejoice, because\l"
    .string "your names are written in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_21::
    .string "In that hour Jesus rejoiced in\n"
    .string "spirit, and said, I thank thee, O\l"
    .string "Father, Lord of heaven and earth,\l"
    .string "that thou hast hid these things from\l"
    .string "the wise and prudent, and hast\l"
    .string "revealed them unto babes: even so,\l"
    .string "Father; for so it seemed good in thy\l"
    .string "sight.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_22::
    .string "All things are delivered to me of\n"
    .string "my Father: and no man knoweth who the\l"
    .string "Son is, but the Father; and who the\l"
    .string "Father is, but the Son, and he to whom\l"
    .string "the Son will reveal him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_23::
    .string "And he turned him unto his\n"
    .string "disciples, and said privately,\l"
    .string "Blessed are the eyes which see the\l"
    .string "things that ye see:"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_24::
    .string "For I tell you, that many\n"
    .string "prophets and kings have desired to\l"
    .string "see those things which ye see, and\l"
    .string "have not seen them; and to hear those\l"
    .string "things which ye hear, and have not\l"
    .string "heard them$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_25::
    .string "And, behold, a certain lawyer\n"
    .string "stood up, and tempted him, saying,\l"
    .string "Master, what shall I do to inherit\l"
    .string "eternal life?"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_26::
    .string "He said unto him, What is written in\n"
    .string "the law? how readest thou?"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_27::
    .string "And he answering said, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "love the Lord thy God with all thy\l"
    .string "heart, and with all thy soul, and\l"
    .string "with all thy strength, and with\l"
    .string "all thy mind; and thy neighbour as\l"
    .string "thyself$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_28::
    .string "And he said unto him, Thou hast\n"
    .string "answered right: this do, and thou\l"
    .string "shalt live.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_29::
    .string "But he, willing to justify\n"
    .string "himself, said unto Jesus, And who is\l"
    .string "my neighbour?"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_30::
    .string "And Jesus answering said, A certain\n"
    .string "man went down from Jerusalem to\l"
    .string "Jericho, and fell among thieves,\l"
    .string "which stripped him of his raiment,\l"
    .string "and wounded him, and departed,\l"
    .string "leaving him half dead$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_31::
    .string "And by chance there came down a\n"
    .string "certain priest that way: and when he\l"
    .string "saw him, he passed by on the other\l"
    .string "side.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_32::
    .string "And likewise a Levite, when he was\n"
    .string "at the place, came and looked on\l"
    .string "him, and passed by on the other side.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_33::
    .string "But a certain Samaritan, as he\n"
    .string "journeyed, came where he was: and\l"
    .string "when he saw him, he had compassion on\l"
    .string "him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_34::
    .string "And went to him, and bound up his\n"
    .string "wounds, pouring in oil and wine, and\l"
    .string "set him on his own beast, and brought\l"
    .string "him to an inn, and took care of him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_35::
    .string "And on the morrow when he departed,\n"
    .string "he took out two pence, and gave them\l"
    .string "to the host, and said unto him, Take\l"
    .string "care of him; and whatsoever thou\l"
    .string "spendest more, when I come again, I\l"
    .string "will repay thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_36::
    .string "Which now of these three, thinkest\n"
    .string "thou, was neighbour unto him that\l"
    .string "fell among the thieves?"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_37::
    .string "And he said, He that shewed mercy on\n"
    .string "him. Then said Jesus unto him, Go, and\l"
    .string "do thou likewise$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_38::
    .string "Now it came to pass, as they went,\n"
    .string "that he entered into a certain\l"
    .string "village: and a certain woman named\l"
    .string "Martha received him into her house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_39::
    .string "And she had a sister called Mary,\n"
    .string "which also sat at Jesus’ feet, and\l"
    .string "heard his word.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_40::
    .string "But Martha was cumbered about much\n"
    .string "serving, and came to him, and said,\l"
    .string "Lord, dost thou not care that my\l"
    .string "sister hath left me to serve alone?\l"
    .string "bid her therefore that she help me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_41::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "her, Martha, Martha, thou art\l"
    .string "careful and troubled about many\l"
    .string "things:"
Bible_Text_Luke_10_42::
    .string "But one thing is needful: and Mary\n"
    .string "hath chosen that good part, which\l"
    .string "shall not be taken away from her$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as he was\n"
    .string "praying in a certain place, when he\l"
    .string "ceased, one of his disciples said\l"
    .string "unto him, Lord, teach us to pray, as\l"
    .string "John also taught his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_2::
    .string "And he said unto them, When ye pray,\n"
    .string "say, Our Father which art in heaven,\l"
    .string "Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom\l"
    .string "come. Thy will be done, as in\l"
    .string "heaven, so in earth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_3::
    .string "Give us day by day our daily bread.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_4::
    .string "And forgive us our sins; for we also\n"
    .string "forgive every one that is indebted to\l"
    .string "us. And lead us not into temptation;\l"
    .string "but deliver us from evil.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_5::
    .string "And he said unto them, Which of you\n"
    .string "shall have a friend, and shall go\l"
    .string "unto him at midnight, and say unto\l"
    .string "him, Friend, lend me three loaves;"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_6::
    .string "For a friend of mine in his journey\n"
    .string "is come to me, and I have nothing to\l"
    .string "set before him?"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_7::
    .string "And he from within shall answer\n"
    .string "and say, Trouble me not: the door is\l"
    .string "now shut, and my children are with me\l"
    .string "in bed; I cannot rise and give thee$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_8::
    .string "I say unto you, Though he will not\n"
    .string "rise and give him, because he is his\l"
    .string "friend, yet because of his\l"
    .string "importunity he will rise and give\l"
    .string "him as many as he needeth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_9::
    .string "And I say unto you, Ask, and it\n"
    .string "shall be given you; seek, and ye\l"
    .string "shall find; knock, and it shall be\l"
    .string "opened unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_10::
    .string "For every one that asketh receiveth;\n"
    .string "and he that seeketh findeth; and to\l"
    .string "him that knocketh it shall be\l"
    .string "opened.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_11::
    .string "If a son shall ask bread of any of\n"
    .string "you that is a father, will he give\l"
    .string "him a stone? or if he ask a fish,\l"
    .string "will he for a fish give him a\l"
    .string "serpent?"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_12::
    .string "Or if he shall ask an egg, will he\n"
    .string "offer him a scorpion?"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_13::
    .string "If ye then, being evil, know how to\n"
    .string "give good gifts unto your children:\l"
    .string "how much more shall your heavenly\l"
    .string "Father give the Holy Spirit to them\l"
    .string "that ask him?"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_14::
    .string "And he was casting out a devil, and\n"
    .string "it was dumb. And it came to pass,\l"
    .string "when the devil was gone out, the dumb\l"
    .string "spake; and the people wondered$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_15::
    .string "But some of them said, He casteth\n"
    .string "out devils through Beelzebub the\l"
    .string "chief of the devils.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_16::
    .string "And others, tempting him, sought of\n"
    .string "him a sign from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_17::
    .string "But he, knowing their thoughts, said\n"
    .string "unto them, Every kingdom divided\l"
    .string "against itself is brought to\l"
    .string "desolation; and a house divided\l"
    .string "against a house falleth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_18::
    .string "If Satan also be divided against\n"
    .string "himself, how shall his kingdom\l"
    .string "stand? because ye say that I cast out\l"
    .string "devils through Beelzebub.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_19::
    .string "And if I by Beelzebub cast out\n"
    .string "devils, by whom do your sons cast\l"
    .string "them out? therefore shall they be\l"
    .string "your judges.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_20::
    .string "But if I with the finger of God cast\n"
    .string "out devils, no doubt the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God is come upon you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_21::
    .string "When a strong man armed keepeth his\n"
    .string "palace, his goods are in peace:"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_22::
    .string "But when a stronger than he shall\n"
    .string "come upon him, and overcome him, he\l"
    .string "taketh from him all his armour\l"
    .string "wherein he trusted, and divideth his\l"
    .string "spoils$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_23::
    .string "He that is not with me is against me:\n"
    .string "and he that gathereth not with me\l"
    .string "scattereth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_24::
    .string "When the unclean spirit is gone\n"
    .string "out of a man, he walketh through dry\l"
    .string "places, seeking rest; and finding\l"
    .string "none, he saith, I will return unto\l"
    .string "my house whence I came out.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_25::
    .string "And when he cometh, he findeth it\n"
    .string "swept and garnished.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_26::
    .string "Then goeth he, and taketh to him\n"
    .string "seven other spirits more wicked than\l"
    .string "himself; and they enter in, and\l"
    .string "dwell there: and the last state of\l"
    .string "that man is worse than the first.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_27::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he spake\n"
    .string "these things, a certain woman of the\l"
    .string "company lifted up her voice, and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Blessed is the womb\l"
    .string "that bare thee, and the paps which\l"
    .string "thou hast sucked.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_28::
    .string "But he said, Yea rather, blessed\n"
    .string "are they that hear the word of God,\l"
    .string "and keep it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_29::
    .string "And when the people were gathered\n"
    .string "thick together, he began to say, This\l"
    .string "is an evil generation: they seek a\l"
    .string "sign; and there shall no sign be\l"
    .string "given it, but the sign of Jonas the\l"
    .string "prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_30::
    .string "For as Jonas was a sign unto the\n"
    .string "Ninevites, so shall also the Son of\l"
    .string "man be to this generation.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_31::
    .string "The queen of the south shall rise\n"
    .string "up in the judgment with the men of\l"
    .string "this generation, and condemn them:\l"
    .string "for she came from the utmost parts\l"
    .string "of the earth to hear the wisdom of\l"
    .string "Solomon; and, behold, a greater than\l"
    .string "Solomon is here.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_32::
    .string "The men of Nineve shall rise up in\n"
    .string "the judgment with this generation,\l"
    .string "and shall condemn it: for they\l"
    .string "repented at the preaching of Jonas;\l"
    .string "and, behold, a greater than Jonas is\l"
    .string "here.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_33::
    .string "No man, when he hath lighted a\n"
    .string "candle, putteth it in a secret\l"
    .string "place, neither under a bushel, but\l"
    .string "on a candlestick, that they which\l"
    .string "come in may see the light.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_34::
    .string "The light of the body is the eye:\n"
    .string "therefore when thine eye is single,\l"
    .string "thy whole body also is full of\l"
    .string "light; but when thine eye is evil,\l"
    .string "thy body also is full of darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_35::
    .string "Take heed therefore that the light\n"
    .string "which is in thee be not darkness.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_36::
    .string "If thy whole body therefore be\n"
    .string "full of light, having no part\l"
    .string "dark, the whole shall be full of\l"
    .string "light, as when the bright shining of\l"
    .string "a candle doth give thee light.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_37::
    .string "And as he spake, a certain Pharisee\n"
    .string "besought him to dine with him: and he\l"
    .string "went in, and sat down to meat.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_38::
    .string "And when the Pharisee saw it, he\n"
    .string "marvelled that he had not first\l"
    .string "washed before dinner.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_39::
    .string "And the Lord said unto him, Now do ye\n"
    .string "Pharisees make clean the outside of\l"
    .string "the cup and the platter; but your\l"
    .string "inward part is full of ravening and\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_40::
    .string "Ye fools, did not he that made that\n"
    .string "which is without make that which is\l"
    .string "within also?"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_41::
    .string "But rather give alms of such things\n"
    .string "as ye have; and, behold, all things\l"
    .string "are clean unto you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_42::
    .string "But woe unto you, Pharisees! for ye\n"
    .string "tithe mint and rue and all manner of\l"
    .string "herbs, and pass over judgment and\l"
    .string "the love of God: these ought ye to\l"
    .string "have done, and not to leave the other\l"
    .string "undone.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_43::
    .string "Woe unto you, Pharisees! for ye\n"
    .string "love the uppermost seats in the\l"
    .string "synagogues, and greetings in the\l"
    .string "markets.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_44::
    .string "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees,\n"
    .string "hypocrites! for ye are as graves\l"
    .string "which appear not, and the men that\l"
    .string "walk over them are not aware of them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_45::
    .string "Then answered one of the lawyers,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, Master, thus\l"
    .string "saying thou reproachest us also.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_46::
    .string "And he said, Woe unto you also, ye\n"
    .string "lawyers! for ye lade men with\l"
    .string "burdens grievous to be borne, and ye\l"
    .string "yourselves touch not the burdens\l"
    .string "with one of your fingers.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_47::
    .string "Woe unto you! for ye build the\n"
    .string "sepulchres of the prophets, and\l"
    .string "your fathers killed them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_48::
    .string "Truly ye bear witness that ye\n"
    .string "allow the deeds of your fathers: for\l"
    .string "they indeed killed them, and ye\l"
    .string "build their sepulchres.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_49::
    .string "Therefore also said the wisdom of\n"
    .string "God, I will send them prophets and\l"
    .string "apostles, and some of them they\l"
    .string "shall slay and persecute:"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_50::
    .string "That the blood of all the\n"
    .string "prophets, which was shed from the\l"
    .string "foundation of the world, may be\l"
    .string "required of this generation;"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_51::
    .string "From the blood of Abel unto the\n"
    .string "blood of Zacharias which perished\l"
    .string "between the altar and the temple:\l"
    .string "verily I say unto you, It shall be\l"
    .string "required of this generation$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_52::
    .string "Woe unto you, lawyers! for ye have\n"
    .string "taken away the key of knowledge: ye\l"
    .string "entered not in yourselves, and them\l"
    .string "that were entering in ye hindered.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_53::
    .string "And as he said these things unto\n"
    .string "them, the scribes and the Pharisees\l"
    .string "began to urge him vehemently, and to\l"
    .string "provoke him to speak of many things:"
Bible_Text_Luke_11_54::
    .string "Laying wait for him, and seeking to\n"
    .string "catch something out of his mouth,\l"
    .string "that they might accuse him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_1::
    .string "In the mean time, when there were\n"
    .string "gathered together an innumerable\l"
    .string "multitude of people, insomuch that\l"
    .string "they trode one upon another, he\l"
    .string "began to say unto his disciples\l"
    .string "first of all, Beware ye of the\l"
    .string "leaven of the Pharisees, which is\l"
    .string "hypocrisy.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_2::
    .string "For there is nothing covered, that\n"
    .string "shall not be revealed; neither hid,\l"
    .string "that shall not be known.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_3::
    .string "Therefore whatsoever ye have\n"
    .string "spoken in darkness shall be heard\l"
    .string "in the light; and that which ye have\l"
    .string "spoken in the ear in closets shall\l"
    .string "be proclaimed upon the housetops.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_4::
    .string "And I say unto you my friends, Be not\n"
    .string "afraid of them that kill the body,\l"
    .string "and after that have no more that they\l"
    .string "can do.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_5::
    .string "But I will forewarn you whom ye\n"
    .string "shall fear: Fear him, which after he\l"
    .string "hath killed hath power to cast into\l"
    .string "hell; yea, I say unto you, Fear him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_6::
    .string "Are not five sparrows sold for two\n"
    .string "farthings, and not one of them is\l"
    .string "forgotten before God?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_7::
    .string "But even the very hairs of your head\n"
    .string "are all numbered. Fear not\l"
    .string "therefore: ye are of more value than\l"
    .string "many sparrows$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_8::
    .string "Also I say unto you, Whosoever\n"
    .string "shall confess me before men, him\l"
    .string "shall the Son of man also confess\l"
    .string "before the angels of God:"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_9::
    .string "But he that denieth me before men\n"
    .string "shall be denied before the angels\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_10::
    .string "And whosoever shall speak a word\n"
    .string "against the Son of man, it shall be\l"
    .string "forgiven him: but unto him that\l"
    .string "blasphemeth against the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "it shall not be forgiven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_11::
    .string "And when they bring you unto the\n"
    .string "synagogues, and unto magistrates,\l"
    .string "and powers, take ye no thought how or\l"
    .string "what thing ye shall answer, or what\l"
    .string "ye shall say:"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_12::
    .string "For the Holy Ghost shall teach you\n"
    .string "in the same hour what ye ought to say$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_13::
    .string "And one of the company said unto\n"
    .string "him, Master, speak to my brother,\l"
    .string "that he divide the inheritance with\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_14::
    .string "And he said unto him, Man, who made\n"
    .string "me a judge or a divider over you?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_15::
    .string "And he said unto them, Take heed,\n"
    .string "and beware of covetousness: for a\l"
    .string "man’s life consisteth not in the\l"
    .string "abundance of the things which he\l"
    .string "possesseth$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_16::
    .string "And he spake a parable unto them,\n"
    .string "saying, The ground of a certain rich\l"
    .string "man brought forth plentifully:"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_17::
    .string "And he thought within himself,\n"
    .string "saying, What shall I do, because I\l"
    .string "have no room where to bestow my\l"
    .string "fruits?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_18::
    .string "And he said, This will I do: I\n"
    .string "will pull down my barns, and\l"
    .string "build greater; and there will I\l"
    .string "bestow all my fruits and my goods$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_19::
    .string "And I will say to my soul, Soul,\n"
    .string "thou hast much goods laid up for\l"
    .string "many years; take thine ease, eat,\l"
    .string "drink, and be merry.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_20::
    .string "But God said unto him, Thou fool,\n"
    .string "this night thy soul shall be\l"
    .string "required of thee: then whose shall\l"
    .string "those things be, which thou hast\l"
    .string "provided?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_21::
    .string "So is he that layeth up treasure\n"
    .string "for himself, and is not rich toward\l"
    .string "God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_22::
    .string "And he said unto his disciples,\n"
    .string "Therefore I say unto you, Take no\l"
    .string "thought for your life, what ye\l"
    .string "shall eat; neither for the body,\l"
    .string "what ye shall put on.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_23::
    .string "The life is more than meat, and the\n"
    .string "body is more than raiment.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_24::
    .string "Consider the ravens: for they\n"
    .string "neither sow nor reap; which neither\l"
    .string "have storehouse nor barn; and God\l"
    .string "feedeth them: how much more are ye\l"
    .string "better than the fowls?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_25::
    .string "And which of you with taking thought\n"
    .string "can add to his stature one cubit?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_26::
    .string "If ye then be not able to do that\n"
    .string "thing which is least, why take ye\l"
    .string "thought for the rest?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_27::
    .string "Consider the lilies how they grow:\n"
    .string "they toil not, they spin not; and\l"
    .string "yet I say unto you, that Solomon in\l"
    .string "all his glory was not arrayed like\l"
    .string "one of these$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_28::
    .string "If then God so clothe the grass,\n"
    .string "which is to day in the field, and to\l"
    .string "morrow is cast into the oven; how\l"
    .string "much more will he clothe you, O ye\l"
    .string "of little faith?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_29::
    .string "And seek not ye what ye shall eat,\n"
    .string "or what ye shall drink, neither be\l"
    .string "ye of doubtful mind$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_30::
    .string "For all these things do the\n"
    .string "nations of the world seek after: and\l"
    .string "your Father knoweth that ye have need\l"
    .string "of these things.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_31::
    .string "But rather seek ye the kingdom of\n"
    .string "God; and all these things shall be\l"
    .string "added unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_32::
    .string "Fear not, little flock; for it is\n"
    .string "your Father’s good pleasure to give\l"
    .string "you the kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_33::
    .string "Sell that ye have, and give alms;\n"
    .string "provide yourselves bags which wax\l"
    .string "not old, a treasure in the heavens\l"
    .string "that faileth not, where no thief\l"
    .string "approacheth, neither moth\l"
    .string "corrupteth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_34::
    .string "For where your treasure is, there\n"
    .string "will your heart be also.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_35::
    .string "Let your loins be girded about, and\n"
    .string "your lights burning;"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_36::
    .string "And ye yourselves like unto men\n"
    .string "that wait for their lord, when he\l"
    .string "will return from the wedding; that\l"
    .string "when he cometh and knocketh, they may\l"
    .string "open unto him immediately$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_37::
    .string "Blessed are those servants, whom\n"
    .string "the lord when he cometh shall find\l"
    .string "watching: verily I say unto you,\l"
    .string "that he shall gird himself, and\l"
    .string "make them to sit down to meat, and\l"
    .string "will come forth and serve them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_38::
    .string "And if he shall come in the second\n"
    .string "watch, or come in the third watch,\l"
    .string "and find them so, blessed are those\l"
    .string "servants.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_39::
    .string "And this know, that if the goodman\n"
    .string "of the house had known what hour the\l"
    .string "thief would come, he would have\l"
    .string "watched, and not have suffered his\l"
    .string "house to be broken through.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_40::
    .string "Be ye therefore ready also: for the\n"
    .string "Son of man cometh at an hour when ye\l"
    .string "think not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_41::
    .string "Then Peter said unto him, Lord,\n"
    .string "speakest thou this parable unto us,\l"
    .string "or even to all?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_42::
    .string "And the Lord said, Who then is that\n"
    .string "faithful and wise steward, whom his\l"
    .string "lord shall make ruler over his\l"
    .string "household, to give them their\l"
    .string "portion of meat in due season?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_43::
    .string "Blessed is that servant, whom his\n"
    .string "lord when he cometh shall find so\l"
    .string "doing$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_44::
    .string "Of a truth I say unto you, that he\n"
    .string "will make him ruler over all that\l"
    .string "he hath.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_45::
    .string "But and if that servant say in his\n"
    .string "heart, My lord delayeth his coming;\l"
    .string "and shall begin to beat the\l"
    .string "menservants and maidens, and to eat\l"
    .string "and drink, and to be drunken;"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_46::
    .string "The lord of that servant will come\n"
    .string "in a day when he looketh not for him,\l"
    .string "and at an hour when he is not aware,\l"
    .string "and will cut him in sunder, and\l"
    .string "will appoint him his portion with\l"
    .string "the unbelievers$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_47::
    .string "And that servant, which knew his\n"
    .string "lord’s will, and prepared not\l"
    .string "himself, neither did according to\l"
    .string "his will, shall be beaten with\l"
    .string "many stripes.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_48::
    .string "But he that knew not, and did commit\n"
    .string "things worthy of stripes, shall be\l"
    .string "beaten with few stripes. For unto\l"
    .string "whomsoever much is given, of him\l"
    .string "shall be much required: and to whom\l"
    .string "men have committed much, of him they\l"
    .string "will ask the more.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_49::
    .string "I am come to send fire on the earth;\n"
    .string "and what will I, if it be already\l"
    .string "kindled?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_50::
    .string "But I have a baptism to be baptized\n"
    .string "with; and how am I straitened till\l"
    .string "it be accomplished!"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_51::
    .string "Suppose ye that I am come to give\n"
    .string "peace on earth? I tell you, Nay; but\l"
    .string "rather division:"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_52::
    .string "For from henceforth there shall be\n"
    .string "five in one house divided, three\l"
    .string "against two, and two against three$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_53::
    .string "The father shall be divided\n"
    .string "against the son, and the son against\l"
    .string "the father; the mother against the\l"
    .string "daughter, and the daughter against\l"
    .string "the mother; the mother in law\l"
    .string "against her daughter in law, and the\l"
    .string "daughter in law against her mother\l"
    .string "in law.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_54::
    .string "And he said also to the people,\n"
    .string "When ye see a cloud rise out of the\l"
    .string "west, straightway ye say, There\l"
    .string "cometh a shower; and so it is.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_55::
    .string "And when ye see the south wind blow,\n"
    .string "ye say, There will be heat; and it\l"
    .string "cometh to pass.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_56::
    .string "Ye hypocrites, ye can discern the\n"
    .string "face of the sky and of the earth; but\l"
    .string "how is it that ye do not discern this\l"
    .string "time?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_57::
    .string "Yea, and why even of yourselves\n"
    .string "judge ye not what is right?"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_58::
    .string "When thou goest with thine\n"
    .string "adversary to the magistrate, as thou\l"
    .string "art in the way, give diligence that\l"
    .string "thou mayest be delivered from him;\l"
    .string "lest he hale thee to the judge, and\l"
    .string "the judge deliver thee to the\l"
    .string "officer, and the officer cast thee\l"
    .string "into prison$"
Bible_Text_Luke_12_59::
    .string "I tell thee, thou shalt not\n"
    .string "depart thence, till thou hast paid\l"
    .string "the very last mite.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_1::
    .string "There were present at that season\n"
    .string "some that told him of the\l"
    .string "Galilaeans, whose blood Pilate had\l"
    .string "mingled with their sacrifices.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_2::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "Suppose ye that these Galilaeans\l"
    .string "were sinners above all the\l"
    .string "Galilaeans, because they suffered\l"
    .string "such things?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_3::
    .string "I tell you, Nay: but, except ye\n"
    .string "repent, ye shall all likewise\l"
    .string "perish$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_4::
    .string "Or those eighteen, upon whom the\n"
    .string "tower in Siloam fell, and slew\l"
    .string "them, think ye that they were sinners\l"
    .string "above all men that dwelt in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_5::
    .string "I tell you, Nay: but, except ye\n"
    .string "repent, ye shall all likewise\l"
    .string "perish$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_6::
    .string "He spake also this parable; A\n"
    .string "certain man had a fig tree planted\l"
    .string "in his vineyard; and he came and\l"
    .string "sought fruit thereon, and found none.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_7::
    .string "Then said he unto the dresser of his\n"
    .string "vineyard, Behold, these three years\l"
    .string "I come seeking fruit on this fig\l"
    .string "tree, and find none: cut it down; why\l"
    .string "cumbereth it the ground?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_8::
    .string "And he answering said unto him,\n"
    .string "Lord, let it alone this year also,\l"
    .string "till I shall dig about it, and dung\l"
    .string "it:"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_9::
    .string "And if it bear fruit, well: and if\n"
    .string "not, then after that thou shalt cut\l"
    .string "it down$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_10::
    .string "And he was teaching in one of the\n"
    .string "synagogues on the sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_11::
    .string "And, behold, there was a woman\n"
    .string "which had a spirit of infirmity\l"
    .string "eighteen years, and was bowed\l"
    .string "together, and could in no wise lift\l"
    .string "up herself.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_12::
    .string "And when Jesus saw her, he called\n"
    .string "her to him, and said unto her, Woman,\l"
    .string "thou art loosed from thine infirmity.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_13::
    .string "And he laid his hands on her: and\n"
    .string "immediately she was made straight,\l"
    .string "and glorified God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_14::
    .string "And the ruler of the synagogue\n"
    .string "answered with indignation, because\l"
    .string "that Jesus had healed on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day, and said unto the people,\l"
    .string "There are six days in which men ought\l"
    .string "to work: in them therefore come and\l"
    .string "be healed, and not on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_15::
    .string "The Lord then answered him, and\n"
    .string "said, Thou hypocrite, doth not each\l"
    .string "one of you on the sabbath loose his\l"
    .string "ox or his ass from the stall, and\l"
    .string "lead him away to watering?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_16::
    .string "And ought not this woman, being a\n"
    .string "daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath\l"
    .string "bound, lo, these eighteen years, be\l"
    .string "loosed from this bond on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_17::
    .string "And when he had said these things,\n"
    .string "all his adversaries were ashamed:\l"
    .string "and all the people rejoiced for\l"
    .string "all the glorious things that were\l"
    .string "done by him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_18::
    .string "Then said he, Unto what is the\n"
    .string "kingdom of God like? and whereunto\l"
    .string "shall I resemble it?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_19::
    .string "It is like a grain of mustard seed,\n"
    .string "which a man took, and cast into his\l"
    .string "garden; and it grew, and waxed a\l"
    .string "great tree; and the fowls of the air\l"
    .string "lodged in the branches of it$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_20::
    .string "And again he said, Whereunto shall\n"
    .string "I liken the kingdom of God?"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_21::
    .string "It is like leaven, which a woman\n"
    .string "took and hid in three measures of\l"
    .string "meal, till the whole was leavened$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_22::
    .string "And he went through the cities and\n"
    .string "villages, teaching, and journeying\l"
    .string "toward Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_23::
    .string "Then said one unto him, Lord, are\n"
    .string "there few that be saved? And he said\l"
    .string "unto them,"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_24::
    .string "Strive to enter in at the strait\n"
    .string "gate: for many, I say unto you, will\l"
    .string "seek to enter in, and shall not be\l"
    .string "able$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_25::
    .string "When once the master of the house is\n"
    .string "risen up, and hath shut to the door,\l"
    .string "and ye begin to stand without, and to\l"
    .string "knock at the door, saying, Lord,\l"
    .string "Lord, open unto us; and he shall\l"
    .string "answer and say unto you, I know you\l"
    .string "not whence ye are:"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_26::
    .string "Then shall ye begin to say, We have\n"
    .string "eaten and drunk in thy presence, and\l"
    .string "thou hast taught in our streets$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_27::
    .string "But he shall say, I tell you, I\n"
    .string "know you not whence ye are; depart\l"
    .string "from me, all ye workers of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_28::
    .string "There shall be weeping and\n"
    .string "gnashing of teeth, when ye shall see\l"
    .string "Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, and\l"
    .string "all the prophets, in the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God, and you yourselves thrust\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_29::
    .string "And they shall come from the east,\n"
    .string "and from the west, and from the\l"
    .string "north, and from the south, and shall\l"
    .string "sit down in the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_30::
    .string "And, behold, there are last which\n"
    .string "shall be first, and there are first\l"
    .string "which shall be last.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_31::
    .string "The same day there came certain of\n"
    .string "the Pharisees, saying unto him, Get\l"
    .string "thee out, and depart hence: for\l"
    .string "Herod will kill thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_32::
    .string "And he said unto them, Go ye, and\n"
    .string "tell that fox, Behold, I cast out\l"
    .string "devils, and I do cures to day and to\l"
    .string "morrow, and the third day I shall be\l"
    .string "perfected.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_33::
    .string "Nevertheless I must walk to day,\n"
    .string "and to morrow, and the day\l"
    .string "following: for it cannot be that a\l"
    .string "prophet perish out of Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_34::
    .string "O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, which\n"
    .string "killest the prophets, and stonest\l"
    .string "them that are sent unto thee; how\l"
    .string "often would I have gathered thy\l"
    .string "children together, as a hen doth\l"
    .string "gather her brood under her wings, and\l"
    .string "ye would not!"
Bible_Text_Luke_13_35::
    .string "Behold, your house is left unto you\n"
    .string "desolate: and verily I say unto you,\l"
    .string "Ye shall not see me, until the time\l"
    .string "come when ye shall say, Blessed is\l"
    .string "he that cometh in the name of the Lord$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he went into\n"
    .string "the house of one of the chief\l"
    .string "Pharisees to eat bread on the sabbath\l"
    .string "day, that they watched him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_2::
    .string "And, behold, there was a certain\n"
    .string "man before him which had the dropsy.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_3::
    .string "And Jesus answering spake unto the\n"
    .string "lawyers and Pharisees, saying, Is it\l"
    .string "lawful to heal on the sabbath day?"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_4::
    .string "And they held their peace. And he\n"
    .string "took him, and healed him, and let\l"
    .string "him go;"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_5::
    .string "And answered them, saying, Which of\n"
    .string "you shall have an ass or an ox\l"
    .string "fallen into a pit, and will not\l"
    .string "straightway pull him out on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day?"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_6::
    .string "And they could not answer him again\n"
    .string "to these things$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_7::
    .string "And he put forth a parable to\n"
    .string "those which were bidden, when he\l"
    .string "marked how they chose out the chief\l"
    .string "rooms; saying unto them,$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_8::
    .string "When thou art bidden of any man to a\n"
    .string "wedding, sit not down in the highest\l"
    .string "room; lest a more honourable man\l"
    .string "than thou be bidden of him;"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_9::
    .string "And he that bade thee and him come\n"
    .string "and say to thee, Give this man\l"
    .string "place; and thou begin with shame to\l"
    .string "take the lowest room$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_10::
    .string "But when thou art bidden, go and sit\n"
    .string "down in the lowest room; that when he\l"
    .string "that bade thee cometh, he may say\l"
    .string "unto thee, Friend, go up higher: then\l"
    .string "shalt thou have worship in the\l"
    .string "presence of them that sit at meat\l"
    .string "with thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_11::
    .string "For whosoever exalteth himself\n"
    .string "shall be abased; and he that\l"
    .string "humbleth himself shall be exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_12::
    .string "Then said he also to him that bade\n"
    .string "him, When thou makest a dinner or a\l"
    .string "supper, call not thy friends, nor\l"
    .string "thy brethren, neither thy kinsmen,\l"
    .string "nor thy rich neighbours; lest they\l"
    .string "also bid thee again, and a\l"
    .string "recompence be made thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_13::
    .string "But when thou makest a feast, call\n"
    .string "the poor, the maimed, the lame, the\l"
    .string "blind:"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_14::
    .string "And thou shalt be blessed; for they\n"
    .string "cannot recompense thee: for thou\l"
    .string "shalt be recompensed at the\l"
    .string "resurrection of the just$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_15::
    .string "And when one of them that sat at\n"
    .string "meat with him heard these things, he\l"
    .string "said unto him, Blessed is he that\l"
    .string "shall eat bread in the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_16::
    .string "Then said he unto him, A certain man\n"
    .string "made a great supper, and bade many:"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_17::
    .string "And sent his servant at supper\n"
    .string "time to say to them that were bidden,\l"
    .string "Come; for all things are now ready$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_18::
    .string "And they all with one consent\n"
    .string "began to make excuse. The first said\l"
    .string "unto him, I have bought a piece of\l"
    .string "ground, and I must needs go and see\l"
    .string "it: I pray thee have me excused.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_19::
    .string "And another said, I have bought five\n"
    .string "yoke of oxen, and I go to prove them:\l"
    .string "I pray thee have me excused.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_20::
    .string "And another said, I have married a\n"
    .string "wife, and therefore I cannot come.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_21::
    .string "So that servant came, and shewed his\n"
    .string "lord these things. Then the master of\l"
    .string "the house being angry said to his\l"
    .string "servant, Go out quickly into the\l"
    .string "streets and lanes of the city, and\l"
    .string "bring in hither the poor, and the\l"
    .string "maimed, and the halt, and the blind.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_22::
    .string "And the servant said, Lord, it is\n"
    .string "done as thou hast commanded, and yet\l"
    .string "there is room.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_23::
    .string "And the lord said unto the servant,\n"
    .string "Go out into the highways and hedges,\l"
    .string "and compel them to come in, that my\l"
    .string "house may be filled.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_24::
    .string "For I say unto you, That none of\n"
    .string "those men which were bidden shall\l"
    .string "taste of my supper.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_25::
    .string "And there went great multitudes\n"
    .string "with him: and he turned, and said\l"
    .string "unto them,"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_26::
    .string "If any man come to me, and hate not\n"
    .string "his father, and mother, and wife, and\l"
    .string "children, and brethren, and sisters,\l"
    .string "yea, and his own life also, he\l"
    .string "cannot be my disciple$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_27::
    .string "And whosoever doth not bear his\n"
    .string "cross, and come after me, cannot be\l"
    .string "my disciple.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_28::
    .string "For which of you, intending to\n"
    .string "build a tower, sitteth not down\l"
    .string "first, and counteth the cost, whether\l"
    .string "he have sufficient to finish it?"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_29::
    .string "Lest haply, after he hath laid the\n"
    .string "foundation, and is not able to\l"
    .string "finish it, all that behold it begin\l"
    .string "to mock him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_30::
    .string "Saying, This man began to build,\n"
    .string "and was not able to finish$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_31::
    .string "Or what king, going to make war\n"
    .string "against another king, sitteth not\l"
    .string "down first, and consulteth whether\l"
    .string "he be able with ten thousand to meet\l"
    .string "him that cometh against him with\l"
    .string "twenty thousand?"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_32::
    .string "Or else, while the other is yet a\n"
    .string "great way off, he sendeth an\l"
    .string "ambassage, and desireth conditions\l"
    .string "of peace$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_33::
    .string "So likewise, whosoever he be of you\n"
    .string "that forsaketh not all that he hath,\l"
    .string "he cannot be my disciple.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_34::
    .string "Salt is good: but if the salt have\n"
    .string "lost his savour, wherewith shall it\l"
    .string "be seasoned?"
Bible_Text_Luke_14_35::
    .string "It is neither fit for the land, nor\n"
    .string "yet for the dunghill; but men cast\l"
    .string "it out. He that hath ears to hear,\l"
    .string "let him hear$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_1::
    .string "Then drew near unto him all the\n"
    .string "publicans and sinners for to hear\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_2::
    .string "And the Pharisees and scribes\n"
    .string "murmured, saying, This man receiveth\l"
    .string "sinners, and eateth with them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_3::
    .string "And he spake this parable unto\n"
    .string "them, saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_4::
    .string "What man of you, having an hundred\n"
    .string "sheep, if he lose one of them, doth\l"
    .string "not leave the ninety and nine in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, and go after that which\l"
    .string "is lost, until he find it?"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_5::
    .string "And when he hath found it, he layeth\n"
    .string "it on his shoulders, rejoicing$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_6::
    .string "And when he cometh home, he calleth\n"
    .string "together his friends and neighbours,\l"
    .string "saying unto them, Rejoice with me;\l"
    .string "for I have found my sheep which was\l"
    .string "lost.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_7::
    .string "I say unto you, that likewise joy\n"
    .string "shall be in heaven over one sinner\l"
    .string "that repenteth, more than over\l"
    .string "ninety and nine just persons, which\l"
    .string "need no repentance.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_8::
    .string "Either what woman having ten pieces\n"
    .string "of silver, if she lose one piece,\l"
    .string "doth not light a candle, and sweep\l"
    .string "the house, and seek diligently\l"
    .string "till she find it?"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_9::
    .string "And when she hath found it, she\n"
    .string "calleth her friends and her\l"
    .string "neighbours together, saying, Rejoice\l"
    .string "with me; for I have found the piece\l"
    .string "which I had lost$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_10::
    .string "Likewise, I say unto you, there is\n"
    .string "joy in the presence of the angels of\l"
    .string "God over one sinner that repenteth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_11::
    .string "And he said, A certain man had two\n"
    .string "sons:"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_12::
    .string "And the younger of them said to his\n"
    .string "father, Father, give me the portion\l"
    .string "of goods that falleth to me. And he\l"
    .string "divided unto them his living$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_13::
    .string "And not many days after the younger\n"
    .string "son gathered all together, and took\l"
    .string "his journey into a far country, and\l"
    .string "there wasted his substance with\l"
    .string "riotous living.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_14::
    .string "And when he had spent all, there\n"
    .string "arose a mighty famine in that land;\l"
    .string "and he began to be in want.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_15::
    .string "And he went and joined himself to a\n"
    .string "citizen of that country; and he sent\l"
    .string "him into his fields to feed swine.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_16::
    .string "And he would fain have filled his\n"
    .string "belly with the husks that the swine\l"
    .string "did eat: and no man gave unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_17::
    .string "And when he came to himself, he\n"
    .string "said, How many hired servants of my\l"
    .string "father’s have bread enough and to\l"
    .string "spare, and I perish with hunger!"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_18::
    .string "I will arise and go to my father,\n"
    .string "and will say unto him, Father, I\l"
    .string "have sinned against heaven, and\l"
    .string "before thee,"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_19::
    .string "And am no more worthy to be called\n"
    .string "thy son: make me as one of thy hired\l"
    .string "servants$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_20::
    .string "And he arose, and came to his\n"
    .string "father. But when he was yet a great\l"
    .string "way off, his father saw him, and had\l"
    .string "compassion, and ran, and fell on\l"
    .string "his neck, and kissed him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_21::
    .string "And the son said unto him, Father, I\n"
    .string "have sinned against heaven, and in\l"
    .string "thy sight, and am no more worthy to be\l"
    .string "called thy son.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_22::
    .string "But the father said to his servants,\n"
    .string "Bring forth the best robe, and put it\l"
    .string "on him; and put a ring on his hand,\l"
    .string "and shoes on his feet:"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_23::
    .string "And bring hither the fatted calf,\n"
    .string "and kill it; and let us eat, and be\l"
    .string "merry:"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_24::
    .string "For this my son was dead, and is\n"
    .string "alive again; he was lost, and is\l"
    .string "found. And they began to be merry$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_25::
    .string "Now his elder son was in the field:\n"
    .string "and as he came and drew nigh to the\l"
    .string "house, he heard musick and dancing.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_26::
    .string "And he called one of the servants,\n"
    .string "and asked what these things meant.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_27::
    .string "And he said unto him, Thy brother is\n"
    .string "come; and thy father hath killed the\l"
    .string "fatted calf, because he hath\l"
    .string "received him safe and sound.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_28::
    .string "And he was angry, and would not go\n"
    .string "in: therefore came his father out,\l"
    .string "and intreated him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_29::
    .string "And he answering said to his father,\n"
    .string "Lo, these many years do I serve thee,\l"
    .string "neither transgressed I at any time\l"
    .string "thy commandment: and yet thou never\l"
    .string "gavest me a kid, that I might make\l"
    .string "merry with my friends:"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_30::
    .string "But as soon as this thy son was come,\n"
    .string "which hath devoured thy living with\l"
    .string "harlots, thou hast killed for him\l"
    .string "the fatted calf$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_31::
    .string "And he said unto him, Son, thou art\n"
    .string "ever with me, and all that I have is\l"
    .string "thine.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_15_32::
    .string "It was meet that we should make\n"
    .string "merry, and be glad: for this thy\l"
    .string "brother was dead, and is alive\l"
    .string "again; and was lost, and is found.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_1::
    .string "And he said also unto his\n"
    .string "disciples, There was a certain rich\l"
    .string "man, which had a steward; and the\l"
    .string "same was accused unto him that he had\l"
    .string "wasted his goods.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_2::
    .string "And he called him, and said unto\n"
    .string "him, How is it that I hear this of\l"
    .string "thee? give an account of thy\l"
    .string "stewardship; for thou mayest be no\l"
    .string "longer steward.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_3::
    .string "Then the steward said within\n"
    .string "himself, What shall I do? for my\l"
    .string "lord taketh away from me the\l"
    .string "stewardship: I cannot dig; to beg I\l"
    .string "am ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_4::
    .string "I am resolved what to do, that, when\n"
    .string "I am put out of the stewardship,\l"
    .string "they may receive me into their houses.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_5::
    .string "So he called every one of his\n"
    .string "lord’s debtors unto him, and said\l"
    .string "unto the first, How much owest thou\l"
    .string "unto my lord?"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_6::
    .string "And he said, An hundred measures of\n"
    .string "oil. And he said unto him, Take thy\l"
    .string "bill, and sit down quickly, and\l"
    .string "write fifty$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_7::
    .string "Then said he to another, And how\n"
    .string "much owest thou? And he said, An\l"
    .string "hundred measures of wheat. And he\l"
    .string "said unto him, Take thy bill, and\l"
    .string "write fourscore.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_8::
    .string "And the lord commended the unjust\n"
    .string "steward, because he had done wisely:\l"
    .string "for the children of this world are\l"
    .string "in their generation wiser than the\l"
    .string "children of light.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_9::
    .string "And I say unto you, Make to\n"
    .string "yourselves friends of the mammon of\l"
    .string "unrighteousness; that, when ye fail,\l"
    .string "they may receive you into\l"
    .string "everlasting habitations.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_10::
    .string "He that is faithful in that which\n"
    .string "is least is faithful also in much:\l"
    .string "and he that is unjust in the least is\l"
    .string "unjust also in much.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_11::
    .string "If therefore ye have not been\n"
    .string "faithful in the unrighteous mammon,\l"
    .string "who will commit to your trust the\l"
    .string "true riches?"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_12::
    .string "And if ye have not been faithful in\n"
    .string "that which is another man’s, who\l"
    .string "shall give you that which is your\l"
    .string "own?"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_13::
    .string "No servant can serve two masters:\n"
    .string "for either he will hate the one, and\l"
    .string "love the other; or else he will\l"
    .string "hold to the one, and despise the\l"
    .string "other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_14::
    .string "And the Pharisees also, who were\n"
    .string "covetous, heard all these things:\l"
    .string "and they derided him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_15::
    .string "And he said unto them, Ye are they\n"
    .string "which justify yourselves before men;\l"
    .string "but God knoweth your hearts: for that\l"
    .string "which is highly esteemed among men\l"
    .string "is abomination in the sight of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_16::
    .string "The law and the prophets were\n"
    .string "until John: since that time the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God is preached, and\l"
    .string "every man presseth into it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_17::
    .string "And it is easier for heaven and\n"
    .string "earth to pass, than one tittle of\l"
    .string "the law to fail.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_18::
    .string "Whosoever putteth away his wife,\n"
    .string "and marrieth another, committeth\l"
    .string "adultery: and whosoever marrieth her\l"
    .string "that is put away from her husband\l"
    .string "committeth adultery.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_19::
    .string "There was a certain rich man, which\n"
    .string "was clothed in purple and fine\l"
    .string "linen, and fared sumptuously every\l"
    .string "day:"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_20::
    .string "And there was a certain beggar named\n"
    .string "Lazarus, which was laid at his gate,\l"
    .string "full of sores,"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_21::
    .string "And desiring to be fed with the\n"
    .string "crumbs which fell from the rich\l"
    .string "man’s table: moreover the dogs came\l"
    .string "and licked his sores$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_22::
    .string "And it came to pass, that the beggar\n"
    .string "died, and was carried by the angels\l"
    .string "into Abraham’s bosom: the rich man\l"
    .string "also died, and was buried;"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_23::
    .string "And in hell he lift up his eyes,\n"
    .string "being in torments, and seeth Abraham\l"
    .string "afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_24::
    .string "And he cried and said, Father\n"
    .string "Abraham, have mercy on me, and send\l"
    .string "Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of\l"
    .string "his finger in water, and cool my\l"
    .string "tongue; for I am tormented in this\l"
    .string "flame.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_25::
    .string "But Abraham said, Son, remember that\n"
    .string "thou in thy lifetime receivedst thy\l"
    .string "good things, and likewise Lazarus\l"
    .string "evil things: but now he is\l"
    .string "comforted, and thou art tormented.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_26::
    .string "And beside all this, between us and\n"
    .string "you there is a great gulf fixed: so\l"
    .string "that they which would pass from\l"
    .string "hence to you cannot; neither can they\l"
    .string "pass to us, that would come from\l"
    .string "thence.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_27::
    .string "Then he said, I pray thee\n"
    .string "therefore, father, that thou\l"
    .string "wouldest send him to my father’s\l"
    .string "house:"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_28::
    .string "For I have five brethren; that he\n"
    .string "may testify unto them, lest they\l"
    .string "also come into this place of\l"
    .string "torment$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_29::
    .string "Abraham saith unto him, They have\n"
    .string "Moses and the prophets; let them\l"
    .string "hear them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_30::
    .string "And he said, Nay, father Abraham:\n"
    .string "but if one went unto them from the\l"
    .string "dead, they will repent.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_16_31::
    .string "And he said unto him, If they hear\n"
    .string "not Moses and the prophets, neither\l"
    .string "will they be persuaded, though one\l"
    .string "rose from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_1::
    .string "Then said he unto the disciples, It\n"
    .string "is impossible but that offences\l"
    .string "will come: but woe unto him, through\l"
    .string "whom they come!"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_2::
    .string "It were better for him that a\n"
    .string "millstone were hanged about his\l"
    .string "neck, and he cast into the sea, than\l"
    .string "that he should offend one of these\l"
    .string "little ones$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_3::
    .string "Take heed to yourselves: If thy\n"
    .string "brother trespass against thee,\l"
    .string "rebuke him; and if he repent,\l"
    .string "forgive him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_4::
    .string "And if he trespass against thee\n"
    .string "seven times in a day, and seven times\l"
    .string "in a day turn again to thee, saying, I\l"
    .string "repent; thou shalt forgive him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_5::
    .string "And the apostles said unto the\n"
    .string "Lord, Increase our faith.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_6::
    .string "And the Lord said, If ye had faith as\n"
    .string "a grain of mustard seed, ye might say\l"
    .string "unto this sycamine tree, Be thou\l"
    .string "plucked up by the root, and be thou\l"
    .string "planted in the sea; and it should\l"
    .string "obey you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_7::
    .string "But which of you, having a servant\n"
    .string "plowing or feeding cattle, will\l"
    .string "say unto him by and by, when he is\l"
    .string "come from the field, Go and sit down\l"
    .string "to meat?"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_8::
    .string "And will not rather say unto him,\n"
    .string "Make ready wherewith I may sup, and\l"
    .string "gird thyself, and serve me, till I\l"
    .string "have eaten and drunken; and afterward\l"
    .string "thou shalt eat and drink?"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_9::
    .string "Doth he thank that servant because\n"
    .string "he did the things that were commanded\l"
    .string "him? I trow not$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_10::
    .string "So likewise ye, when ye shall have\n"
    .string "done all those things which are\l"
    .string "commanded you, say, We are\l"
    .string "unprofitable servants: we have done\l"
    .string "that which was our duty to do.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_11::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he went to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, that he passed through\l"
    .string "the midst of Samaria and Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_12::
    .string "And as he entered into a certain\n"
    .string "village, there met him ten men that\l"
    .string "were lepers, which stood afar off:"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_13::
    .string "And they lifted up their voices,\n"
    .string "and said, Jesus, Master, have mercy\l"
    .string "on us$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_14::
    .string "And when he saw them, he said unto\n"
    .string "them, Go shew yourselves unto the\l"
    .string "priests. And it came to pass, that,\l"
    .string "as they went, they were cleansed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_15::
    .string "And one of them, when he saw that he\n"
    .string "was healed, turned back, and with a\l"
    .string "loud voice glorified God,"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_16::
    .string "And fell down on his face at his\n"
    .string "feet, giving him thanks: and he was a\l"
    .string "Samaritan$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_17::
    .string "And Jesus answering said, Were there\n"
    .string "not ten cleansed? but where are the\l"
    .string "nine?"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_18::
    .string "There are not found that returned to\n"
    .string "give glory to God, save this stranger$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_19::
    .string "And he said unto him, Arise, go thy\n"
    .string "way: thy faith hath made thee whole.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_20::
    .string "And when he was demanded of the\n"
    .string "Pharisees, when the kingdom of God\l"
    .string "should come, he answered them and\l"
    .string "said, The kingdom of God cometh not\l"
    .string "with observation:"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_21::
    .string "Neither shall they say, Lo here!\n"
    .string "or, lo there! for, behold, the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God is within you$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_22::
    .string "And he said unto the disciples, The\n"
    .string "days will come, when ye shall\l"
    .string "desire to see one of the days of the\l"
    .string "Son of man, and ye shall not see it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_23::
    .string "And they shall say to you, See\n"
    .string "here; or, see there: go not after\l"
    .string "them, nor follow them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_24::
    .string "For as the lightning, that\n"
    .string "lighteneth out of the one part under\l"
    .string "heaven, shineth unto the other part\l"
    .string "under heaven; so shall also the Son\l"
    .string "of man be in his day.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_25::
    .string "But first must he suffer many\n"
    .string "things, and be rejected of this\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_26::
    .string "And as it was in the days of Noe, so\n"
    .string "shall it be also in the days of the\l"
    .string "Son of man.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_27::
    .string "They did eat, they drank, they\n"
    .string "married wives, they were given in\l"
    .string "marriage, until the day that Noe\l"
    .string "entered into the ark, and the flood\l"
    .string "came, and destroyed them all.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_28::
    .string "Likewise also as it was in the days\n"
    .string "of Lot; they did eat, they drank, they\l"
    .string "bought, they sold, they planted,\l"
    .string "they builded;"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_29::
    .string "But the same day that Lot went out\n"
    .string "of Sodom it rained fire and brimstone\l"
    .string "from heaven, and destroyed them all$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_30::
    .string "Even thus shall it be in the day\n"
    .string "when the Son of man is revealed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_31::
    .string "In that day, he which shall be\n"
    .string "upon the housetop, and his stuff in\l"
    .string "the house, let him not come down to\l"
    .string "take it away: and he that is in the\l"
    .string "field, let him likewise not return\l"
    .string "back.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_32::
    .string "Remember Lot’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_33::
    .string "Whosoever shall seek to save his\n"
    .string "life shall lose it; and whosoever\l"
    .string "shall lose his life shall\l"
    .string "preserve it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_34::
    .string "I tell you, in that night there\n"
    .string "shall be two men in one bed; the one\l"
    .string "shall be taken, and the other\l"
    .string "shall be left.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_35::
    .string "Two women shall be grinding\n"
    .string "together; the one shall be taken,\l"
    .string "and the other left.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_36::
    .string "Two men shall be in the field; the\n"
    .string "one shall be taken, and the other\l"
    .string "left.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_17_37::
    .string "And they answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Where, Lord? And he said unto them,\l"
    .string "Wheresoever the body is, thither\l"
    .string "will the eagles be gathered\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_1::
    .string "And he spake a parable unto them\n"
    .string "to this end, that men ought always to\l"
    .string "pray, and not to faint;"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_2::
    .string "Saying, There was in a city a judge,\n"
    .string "which feared not God, neither\l"
    .string "regarded man:"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_3::
    .string "And there was a widow in that city;\n"
    .string "and she came unto him, saying, Avenge\l"
    .string "me of mine adversary$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_4::
    .string "And he would not for a while: but\n"
    .string "afterward he said within himself,\l"
    .string "Though I fear not God, nor regard\l"
    .string "man;"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_5::
    .string "Yet because this widow troubleth\n"
    .string "me, I will avenge her, lest by her\l"
    .string "continual coming she weary me$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_6::
    .string "And the Lord said, Hear what the\n"
    .string "unjust judge saith.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_7::
    .string "And shall not God avenge his own\n"
    .string "elect, which cry day and night unto\l"
    .string "him, though he bear long with them?"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_8::
    .string "I tell you that he will avenge\n"
    .string "them speedily. Nevertheless when\l"
    .string "the Son of man cometh, shall he find\l"
    .string "faith on the earth?"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_9::
    .string "And he spake this parable unto\n"
    .string "certain which trusted in themselves\l"
    .string "that they were righteous, and\l"
    .string "despised others:"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_10::
    .string "Two men went up into the temple to\n"
    .string "pray; the one a Pharisee, and the\l"
    .string "other a publican$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_11::
    .string "The Pharisee stood and prayed thus\n"
    .string "with himself, God, I thank thee, that\l"
    .string "I am not as other men are,\l"
    .string "extortioners, unjust, adulterers, or\l"
    .string "even as this publican.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_12::
    .string "I fast twice in the week, I give\n"
    .string "tithes of all that I possess.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_13::
    .string "And the publican, standing afar\n"
    .string "off, would not lift up so much as\l"
    .string "his eyes unto heaven, but smote upon\l"
    .string "his breast, saying, God be merciful\l"
    .string "to me a sinner.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_14::
    .string "I tell you, this man went down to\n"
    .string "his house justified rather than the\l"
    .string "other: for every one that exalteth\l"
    .string "himself shall be abased; and he\l"
    .string "that humbleth himself shall be\l"
    .string "exalted.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_15::
    .string "And they brought unto him also\n"
    .string "infants, that he would touch them:\l"
    .string "but when his disciples saw it, they\l"
    .string "rebuked them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_16::
    .string "But Jesus called them unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, Suffer little children to\l"
    .string "come unto me, and forbid them not:\l"
    .string "for of such is the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_17::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, Whosoever\n"
    .string "shall not receive the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God as a little child shall in no\l"
    .string "wise enter therein.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_18::
    .string "And a certain ruler asked him,\n"
    .string "saying, Good Master, what shall I do\l"
    .string "to inherit eternal life?"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_19::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Why\n"
    .string "callest thou me good? none is good,\l"
    .string "save one, that is, God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_20::
    .string "Thou knowest the commandments, Do\n"
    .string "not commit adultery, Do not kill,\l"
    .string "Do not steal, Do not bear false\l"
    .string "witness, Honour thy father and thy\l"
    .string "mother.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_21::
    .string "And he said, All these have I kept\n"
    .string "from my youth up.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_22::
    .string "Now when Jesus heard these things,\n"
    .string "he said unto him, Yet lackest thou\l"
    .string "one thing: sell all that thou\l"
    .string "hast, and distribute unto the poor,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt have treasure in\l"
    .string "heaven: and come, follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_23::
    .string "And when he heard this, he was very\n"
    .string "sorrowful: for he was very rich.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_24::
    .string "And when Jesus saw that he was very\n"
    .string "sorrowful, he said, How hardly\l"
    .string "shall they that have riches enter\l"
    .string "into the kingdom of God!"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_25::
    .string "For it is easier for a camel to go\n"
    .string "through a needle’s eye, than for a\l"
    .string "rich man to enter into the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_26::
    .string "And they that heard it said, Who\n"
    .string "then can be saved?"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_27::
    .string "And he said, The things which are\n"
    .string "impossible with men are possible\l"
    .string "with God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_28::
    .string "Then Peter said, Lo, we have left\n"
    .string "all, and followed thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_29::
    .string "And he said unto them, Verily I say\n"
    .string "unto you, There is no man that hath\l"
    .string "left house, or parents, or brethren,\l"
    .string "or wife, or children, for the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God’s sake,"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_30::
    .string "Who shall not receive manifold\n"
    .string "more in this present time, and in the\l"
    .string "world to come life everlasting$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_31::
    .string "Then he took unto him the twelve,\n"
    .string "and said unto them, Behold, we go up\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem, and all things that\l"
    .string "are written by the prophets\l"
    .string "concerning the Son of man shall be\l"
    .string "accomplished.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_32::
    .string "For he shall be delivered unto the\n"
    .string "Gentiles, and shall be mocked, and\l"
    .string "spitefully entreated, and spitted\l"
    .string "on:"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_33::
    .string "And they shall scourge him, and\n"
    .string "put him to death: and the third day he\l"
    .string "shall rise again$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_34::
    .string "And they understood none of these\n"
    .string "things: and this saying was hid from\l"
    .string "them, neither knew they the things\l"
    .string "which were spoken.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_35::
    .string "And it came to pass, that as he was\n"
    .string "come nigh unto Jericho, a certain\l"
    .string "blind man sat by the way side\l"
    .string "begging:"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_36::
    .string "And hearing the multitude pass by,\n"
    .string "he asked what it meant$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_37::
    .string "And they told him, that Jesus of\n"
    .string "Nazareth passeth by.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_38::
    .string "And he cried, saying, Jesus, thou\n"
    .string "son of David, have mercy on me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_39::
    .string "And they which went before rebuked\n"
    .string "him, that he should hold his peace:\l"
    .string "but he cried so much the more, Thou\l"
    .string "son of David, have mercy on me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_40::
    .string "And Jesus stood, and commanded him\n"
    .string "to be brought unto him: and when he\l"
    .string "was come near, he asked him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_41::
    .string "Saying, What wilt thou that I\n"
    .string "shall do unto thee? And he said,\l"
    .string "Lord, that I may receive my sight$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_42::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Receive thy\n"
    .string "sight: thy faith hath saved thee.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_18_43::
    .string "And immediately he received his\n"
    .string "sight, and followed him,\l"
    .string "glorifying God: and all the\l"
    .string "people, when they saw it, gave\l"
    .string "praise unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_1::
    .string "And Jesus entered and passed\n"
    .string "through Jericho.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_2::
    .string "And, behold, there was a man named\n"
    .string "Zacchaeus, which was the chief among\l"
    .string "the publicans, and he was rich.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_3::
    .string "And he sought to see Jesus who he\n"
    .string "was; and could not for the press,\l"
    .string "because he was little of stature.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_4::
    .string "And he ran before, and climbed up\n"
    .string "into a sycomore tree to see him: for\l"
    .string "he was to pass that way.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_5::
    .string "And when Jesus came to the place,\n"
    .string "he looked up, and saw him, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Zacchaeus, make haste, and\l"
    .string "come down; for to day I must abide at\l"
    .string "thy house.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_6::
    .string "And he made haste, and came down,\n"
    .string "and received him joyfully.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_7::
    .string "And when they saw it, they all\n"
    .string "murmured, saying, That he was gone to\l"
    .string "be guest with a man that is a sinner.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_8::
    .string "And Zacchaeus stood, and said unto\n"
    .string "the Lord: Behold, Lord, the half of\l"
    .string "my goods I give to the poor; and if I\l"
    .string "have taken any thing from any man by\l"
    .string "false accusation, I restore him\l"
    .string "fourfold.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_9::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, This day is\n"
    .string "salvation come to this house,\l"
    .string "forsomuch as he also is a son of\l"
    .string "Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_10::
    .string "For the Son of man is come to seek\n"
    .string "and to save that which was lost.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_11::
    .string "And as they heard these things, he\n"
    .string "added and spake a parable, because\l"
    .string "he was nigh to Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "because they thought that the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God should immediately\l"
    .string "appear.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_12::
    .string "He said therefore, A certain\n"
    .string "nobleman went into a far country to\l"
    .string "receive for himself a kingdom, and\l"
    .string "to return.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_13::
    .string "And he called his ten servants, and\n"
    .string "delivered them ten pounds, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Occupy till I come.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_14::
    .string "But his citizens hated him, and sent\n"
    .string "a message after him, saying, We will\l"
    .string "not have this man to reign over us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, that when he\n"
    .string "was returned, having received the\l"
    .string "kingdom, then he commanded these\l"
    .string "servants to be called unto him, to\l"
    .string "whom he had given the money, that he\l"
    .string "might know how much every man had\l"
    .string "gained by trading.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_16::
    .string "Then came the first, saying, Lord,\n"
    .string "thy pound hath gained ten pounds.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_17::
    .string "And he said unto him, Well, thou\n"
    .string "good servant: because thou hast been\l"
    .string "faithful in a very little, have\l"
    .string "thou authority over ten cities.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_18::
    .string "And the second came, saying, Lord,\n"
    .string "thy pound hath gained five pounds.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_19::
    .string "And he said likewise to him, Be thou\n"
    .string "also over five cities.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_20::
    .string "And another came, saying, Lord,\n"
    .string "behold, here is thy pound, which I\l"
    .string "have kept laid up in a napkin:"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_21::
    .string "For I feared thee, because thou art\n"
    .string "an austere man: thou takest up that\l"
    .string "thou layedst not down, and reapest\l"
    .string "that thou didst not sow$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_22::
    .string "And he saith unto him, Out of thine\n"
    .string "own mouth will I judge thee, thou\l"
    .string "wicked servant. Thou knewest that I\l"
    .string "was an austere man, taking up that I\l"
    .string "laid not down, and reaping that I did\l"
    .string "not sow:"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_23::
    .string "Wherefore then gavest not thou my\n"
    .string "money into the bank, that at my\l"
    .string "coming I might have required mine own\l"
    .string "with usury?"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_24::
    .string "And he said unto them that stood by,\n"
    .string "Take from him the pound, and give it\l"
    .string "to him that hath ten pounds$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_25::
    .string "(And they said unto him, Lord, he\n"
    .string "hath ten pounds.)"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_26::
    .string "For I say unto you, That unto every\n"
    .string "one which hath shall be given; and\l"
    .string "from him that hath not, even that he\l"
    .string "hath shall be taken away from him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_27::
    .string "But those mine enemies, which would\n"
    .string "not that I should reign over them,\l"
    .string "bring hither, and slay them before\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_28::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, he went\n"
    .string "before, ascending up to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_29::
    .string "And it came to pass, when he was\n"
    .string "come nigh to Bethphage and Bethany,\l"
    .string "at the mount called the mount of\l"
    .string "Olives, he sent two of his\l"
    .string "disciples,"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_30::
    .string "Saying, Go ye into the village over\n"
    .string "against you; in the which at your\l"
    .string "entering ye shall find a colt tied,\l"
    .string "whereon yet never man sat: loose\l"
    .string "him, and bring him hither$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_31::
    .string "And if any man ask you, Why do ye\n"
    .string "loose him? thus shall ye say unto\l"
    .string "him, Because the Lord hath need of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_32::
    .string "And they that were sent went their\n"
    .string "way, and found even as he had said\l"
    .string "unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_33::
    .string "And as they were loosing the colt,\n"
    .string "the owners thereof said unto them,\l"
    .string "Why loose ye the colt?"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_34::
    .string "And they said, The Lord hath need of\n"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_35::
    .string "And they brought him to Jesus: and\n"
    .string "they cast their garments upon the\l"
    .string "colt, and they set Jesus thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_36::
    .string "And as he went, they spread their\n"
    .string "clothes in the way.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_37::
    .string "And when he was come nigh, even now\n"
    .string "at the descent of the mount of\l"
    .string "Olives, the whole multitude of the\l"
    .string "disciples began to rejoice and\l"
    .string "praise God with a loud voice for\l"
    .string "all the mighty works that they had\l"
    .string "seen;"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_38::
    .string "Saying, Blessed be the King that\n"
    .string "cometh in the name of the Lord: peace\l"
    .string "in heaven, and glory in the highest$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_39::
    .string "And some of the Pharisees from among\n"
    .string "the multitude said unto him, Master,\l"
    .string "rebuke thy disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_40::
    .string "And he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "I tell you that, if these should\l"
    .string "hold their peace, the stones would\l"
    .string "immediately cry out.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_41::
    .string "And when he was come near, he beheld\n"
    .string "the city, and wept over it,"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_42::
    .string "Saying, If thou hadst known, even\n"
    .string "thou, at least in this thy day, the\l"
    .string "things which belong unto thy peace!\l"
    .string "but now they are hid from thine eyes$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_43::
    .string "For the days shall come upon thee,\n"
    .string "that thine enemies shall cast a\l"
    .string "trench about thee, and compass thee\l"
    .string "round, and keep thee in on every\l"
    .string "side,"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_44::
    .string "And shall lay thee even with the\n"
    .string "ground, and thy children within\l"
    .string "thee; and they shall not leave in\l"
    .string "thee one stone upon another; because\l"
    .string "thou knewest not the time of thy\l"
    .string "visitation$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_45::
    .string "And he went into the temple, and\n"
    .string "began to cast out them that sold\l"
    .string "therein, and them that bought;"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_46::
    .string "Saying unto them, It is written, My\n"
    .string "house is the house of prayer: but ye\l"
    .string "have made it a den of thieves$"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_47::
    .string "And he taught daily in the temple.\n"
    .string "But the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "scribes and the chief of the people\l"
    .string "sought to destroy him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_19_48::
    .string "And could not find what they might\n"
    .string "do: for all the people were very\l"
    .string "attentive to hear him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that on one of\n"
    .string "those days, as he taught the people\l"
    .string "in the temple, and preached the\l"
    .string "gospel, the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "scribes came upon him with the\l"
    .string "elders,"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_2::
    .string "And spake unto him, saying, Tell\n"
    .string "us, by what authority doest thou\l"
    .string "these things? or who is he that gave\l"
    .string "thee this authority?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_3::
    .string "And he answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "I will also ask you one thing; and\l"
    .string "answer me:"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_4::
    .string "The baptism of John, was it from\n"
    .string "heaven, or of men?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_5::
    .string "And they reasoned with themselves,\n"
    .string "saying, If we shall say, From\l"
    .string "heaven; he will say, Why then\l"
    .string "believed ye him not?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_6::
    .string "But and if we say, Of men; all the\n"
    .string "people will stone us: for they be\l"
    .string "persuaded that John was a prophet$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_7::
    .string "And they answered, that they could\n"
    .string "not tell whence it was.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_8::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, Neither\n"
    .string "tell I you by what authority I do\l"
    .string "these things.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_9::
    .string "Then began he to speak to the\n"
    .string "people this parable; A certain man\l"
    .string "planted a vineyard, and let it forth\l"
    .string "to husbandmen, and went into a far\l"
    .string "country for a long time.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_10::
    .string "And at the season he sent a servant\n"
    .string "to the husbandmen, that they should\l"
    .string "give him of the fruit of the\l"
    .string "vineyard: but the husbandmen beat\l"
    .string "him, and sent him away empty.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_11::
    .string "And again he sent another servant:\n"
    .string "and they beat him also, and\l"
    .string "entreated him shamefully, and sent\l"
    .string "him away empty.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_12::
    .string "And again he sent a third: and they\n"
    .string "wounded him also, and cast him out.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_13::
    .string "Then said the lord of the vineyard,\n"
    .string "What shall I do? I will send my\l"
    .string "beloved son: it may be they will\l"
    .string "reverence him when they see him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_14::
    .string "But when the husbandmen saw him,\n"
    .string "they reasoned among themselves,\l"
    .string "saying, This is the heir: come, let\l"
    .string "us kill him, that the inheritance\l"
    .string "may be ours.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_15::
    .string "So they cast him out of the\n"
    .string "vineyard, and killed him. What\l"
    .string "therefore shall the lord of the\l"
    .string "vineyard do unto them?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_16::
    .string "He shall come and destroy these\n"
    .string "husbandmen, and shall give the\l"
    .string "vineyard to others. And when they\l"
    .string "heard it, they said, God forbid$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_17::
    .string "And he beheld them, and said, What\n"
    .string "is this then that is written, The\l"
    .string "stone which the builders rejected,\l"
    .string "the same is become the head of the\l"
    .string "corner?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_18::
    .string "Whosoever shall fall upon that\n"
    .string "stone shall be broken; but on\l"
    .string "whomsoever it shall fall, it will\l"
    .string "grind him to powder$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_19::
    .string "And the chief priests and the\n"
    .string "scribes the same hour sought to lay\l"
    .string "hands on him; and they feared the\l"
    .string "people: for they perceived that he\l"
    .string "had spoken this parable against\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_20::
    .string "And they watched him, and sent forth\n"
    .string "spies, which should feign\l"
    .string "themselves just men, that they might\l"
    .string "take hold of his words, that so they\l"
    .string "might deliver him unto the power\l"
    .string "and authority of the governor.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_21::
    .string "And they asked him, saying, Master,\n"
    .string "we know that thou sayest and teachest\l"
    .string "rightly, neither acceptest thou the\l"
    .string "person of any, but teachest the way\l"
    .string "of God truly:"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_22::
    .string "Is it lawful for us to give tribute\n"
    .string "unto Caesar, or no?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_23::
    .string "But he perceived their craftiness,\n"
    .string "and said unto them, Why tempt ye me?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_24::
    .string "Shew me a penny. Whose image and\n"
    .string "superscription hath it? They\l"
    .string "answered and said, Caesar’s$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_25::
    .string "And he said unto them, Render\n"
    .string "therefore unto Caesar the things\l"
    .string "which be Caesar’s, and unto God the\l"
    .string "things which be God’s.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_26::
    .string "And they could not take hold of his\n"
    .string "words before the people: and they\l"
    .string "marvelled at his answer, and held\l"
    .string "their peace.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_27::
    .string "Then came to him certain of the\n"
    .string "Sadducees, which deny that there is\l"
    .string "any resurrection; and they asked him,"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_28::
    .string "Saying, Master, Moses wrote unto us,\n"
    .string "If any man’s brother die, having a\l"
    .string "wife, and he die without children,\l"
    .string "that his brother should take his\l"
    .string "wife, and raise up seed unto his\l"
    .string "brother$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_29::
    .string "There were therefore seven\n"
    .string "brethren: and the first took a wife,\l"
    .string "and died without children.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_30::
    .string "And the second took her to wife, and\n"
    .string "he died childless.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_31::
    .string "And the third took her; and in like\n"
    .string "manner the seven also: and they left\l"
    .string "no children, and died.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_32::
    .string "Last of all the woman died also.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_33::
    .string "Therefore in the resurrection whose\n"
    .string "wife of them is she? for seven had her\l"
    .string "to wife.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_34::
    .string "And Jesus answering said unto them,\n"
    .string "The children of this world marry,\l"
    .string "and are given in marriage:"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_35::
    .string "But they which shall be accounted\n"
    .string "worthy to obtain that world, and the\l"
    .string "resurrection from the dead, neither\l"
    .string "marry, nor are given in marriage:"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_36::
    .string "Neither can they die any more: for\n"
    .string "they are equal unto the angels; and\l"
    .string "are the children of God, being the\l"
    .string "children of the resurrection$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_37::
    .string "Now that the dead are raised, even\n"
    .string "Moses shewed at the bush, when he\l"
    .string "calleth the Lord the God of Abraham,\l"
    .string "and the God of Isaac, and the God of\l"
    .string "Jacob.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_38::
    .string "For he is not a God of the dead, but\n"
    .string "of the living: for all live unto\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_39::
    .string "Then certain of the scribes\n"
    .string "answering said, Master, thou hast\l"
    .string "well said.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_40::
    .string "And after that they durst not ask\n"
    .string "him any question at all.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_41::
    .string "And he said unto them, How say they\n"
    .string "that Christ is David’s son?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_42::
    .string "And David himself saith in the book\n"
    .string "of Psalms, The LORD said unto my\l"
    .string "Lord, Sit thou on my right hand,"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_43::
    .string "Till I make thine enemies thy\n"
    .string "footstool$"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_44::
    .string "David therefore calleth him Lord,\n"
    .string "how is he then his son?"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_45::
    .string "Then in the audience of all the\n"
    .string "people he said unto his disciples,"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_46::
    .string "Beware of the scribes, which desire\n"
    .string "to walk in long robes, and love\l"
    .string "greetings in the markets, and the\l"
    .string "highest seats in the synagogues, and\l"
    .string "the chief rooms at feasts;"
Bible_Text_Luke_20_47::
    .string "Which devour widows’ houses, and for\n"
    .string "a shew make long prayers: the same\l"
    .string "shall receive greater damnation$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_1::
    .string "And he looked up, and saw the rich\n"
    .string "men casting their gifts into the\l"
    .string "treasury.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_2::
    .string "And he saw also a certain poor\n"
    .string "widow casting in thither two mites.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_3::
    .string "And he said, Of a truth I say unto\n"
    .string "you, that this poor widow hath cast\l"
    .string "in more than they all:"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_4::
    .string "For all these have of their\n"
    .string "abundance cast in unto the offerings\l"
    .string "of God: but she of her penury hath\l"
    .string "cast in all the living that she had$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_5::
    .string "And as some spake of the temple,\n"
    .string "how it was adorned with goodly\l"
    .string "stones and gifts, he said,"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_6::
    .string "As for these things which ye\n"
    .string "behold, the days will come, in the\l"
    .string "which there shall not be left one\l"
    .string "stone upon another, that shall not\l"
    .string "be thrown down$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_7::
    .string "And they asked him, saying, Master,\n"
    .string "but when shall these things be? and\l"
    .string "what sign will there be when these\l"
    .string "things shall come to pass?"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_8::
    .string "And he said, Take heed that ye be not\n"
    .string "deceived: for many shall come in my\l"
    .string "name, saying, I am Christ; and the\l"
    .string "time draweth near: go ye not\l"
    .string "therefore after them$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_9::
    .string "But when ye shall hear of wars and\n"
    .string "commotions, be not terrified: for\l"
    .string "these things must first come to\l"
    .string "pass; but the end is not by and by.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_10::
    .string "Then said he unto them, Nation\n"
    .string "shall rise against nation, and\l"
    .string "kingdom against kingdom:"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_11::
    .string "And great earthquakes shall be in\n"
    .string "divers places, and famines, and\l"
    .string "pestilences; and fearful sights and\l"
    .string "great signs shall there be from\l"
    .string "heaven$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_12::
    .string "But before all these, they shall\n"
    .string "lay their hands on you, and\l"
    .string "persecute you, delivering you up to\l"
    .string "the synagogues, and into prisons,\l"
    .string "being brought before kings and\l"
    .string "rulers for my name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_13::
    .string "And it shall turn to you for a\n"
    .string "testimony.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_14::
    .string "Settle it therefore in your hearts,\n"
    .string "not to meditate before what ye\l"
    .string "shall answer:"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_15::
    .string "For I will give you a mouth and\n"
    .string "wisdom, which all your adversaries\l"
    .string "shall not be able to gainsay nor\l"
    .string "resist$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_16::
    .string "And ye shall be betrayed both by\n"
    .string "parents, and brethren, and\l"
    .string "kinsfolks, and friends; and some of\l"
    .string "you shall they cause to be put to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_17::
    .string "And ye shall be hated of all men\n"
    .string "for my name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_18::
    .string "But there shall not an hair of your\n"
    .string "head perish.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_19::
    .string "In your patience possess ye your\n"
    .string "souls.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_20::
    .string "And when ye shall see Jerusalem\n"
    .string "compassed with armies, then know\l"
    .string "that the desolation thereof is nigh.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_21::
    .string "Then let them which are in Judaea\n"
    .string "flee to the mountains; and let them\l"
    .string "which are in the midst of it depart\l"
    .string "out; and let not them that are in the\l"
    .string "countries enter thereinto.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_22::
    .string "For these be the days of vengeance,\n"
    .string "that all things which are written\l"
    .string "may be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_23::
    .string "But woe unto them that are with\n"
    .string "child, and to them that give suck, in\l"
    .string "those days! for there shall be great\l"
    .string "distress in the land, and wrath upon\l"
    .string "this people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_24::
    .string "And they shall fall by the edge\n"
    .string "of the sword, and shall be led away\l"
    .string "captive into all nations: and\l"
    .string "Jerusalem shall be trodden down of\l"
    .string "the Gentiles, until the times of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_25::
    .string "And there shall be signs in the\n"
    .string "sun, and in the moon, and in the\l"
    .string "stars; and upon the earth distress\l"
    .string "of nations, with perplexity; the\l"
    .string "sea and the waves roaring;"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_26::
    .string "Men’s hearts failing them for fear,\n"
    .string "and for looking after those things\l"
    .string "which are coming on the earth: for\l"
    .string "the powers of heaven shall be\l"
    .string "shaken$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_27::
    .string "And then shall they see the Son of\n"
    .string "man coming in a cloud with power and\l"
    .string "great glory.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_28::
    .string "And when these things begin to come\n"
    .string "to pass, then look up, and lift up\l"
    .string "your heads; for your redemption\l"
    .string "draweth nigh.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_29::
    .string "And he spake to them a parable;\n"
    .string "Behold the fig tree, and all the\l"
    .string "trees;"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_30::
    .string "When they now shoot forth, ye see\n"
    .string "and know of your own selves that\l"
    .string "summer is now nigh at hand$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_31::
    .string "So likewise ye, when ye see these\n"
    .string "things come to pass, know ye that the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God is nigh at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_32::
    .string "Verily I say unto you, This\n"
    .string "generation shall not pass away,\l"
    .string "till all be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_33::
    .string "Heaven and earth shall pass away:\n"
    .string "but my words shall not pass away.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_34::
    .string "And take heed to yourselves, lest\n"
    .string "at any time your hearts be\l"
    .string "overcharged with surfeiting, and\l"
    .string "drunkenness, and cares of this life,\l"
    .string "and so that day come upon you\l"
    .string "unawares.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_35::
    .string "For as a snare shall it come on\n"
    .string "all them that dwell on the face of\l"
    .string "the whole earth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_36::
    .string "Watch ye therefore, and pray\n"
    .string "always, that ye may be accounted\l"
    .string "worthy to escape all these things\l"
    .string "that shall come to pass, and to\l"
    .string "stand before the Son of man.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_37::
    .string "And in the day time he was teaching\n"
    .string "in the temple; and at night he went\l"
    .string "out, and abode in the mount that is\l"
    .string "called the mount of Olives.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_21_38::
    .string "And all the people came early in\n"
    .string "the morning to him in the temple,\l"
    .string "for to hear him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_1::
    .string "Now the feast of unleavened bread\n"
    .string "drew nigh, which is called the\l"
    .string "Passover.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_2::
    .string "And the chief priests and scribes\n"
    .string "sought how they might kill him; for\l"
    .string "they feared the people.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_3::
    .string "Then entered Satan into Judas\n"
    .string "surnamed Iscariot, being of the\l"
    .string "number of the twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_4::
    .string "And he went his way, and communed\n"
    .string "with the chief priests and\l"
    .string "captains, how he might betray him\l"
    .string "unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_5::
    .string "And they were glad, and covenanted\n"
    .string "to give him money.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_6::
    .string "And he promised, and sought\n"
    .string "opportunity to betray him unto them\l"
    .string "in the absence of the multitude.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_7::
    .string "Then came the day of unleavened\n"
    .string "bread, when the passover must be\l"
    .string "killed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_8::
    .string "And he sent Peter and John, saying,\n"
    .string "Go and prepare us the passover,\l"
    .string "that we may eat.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_9::
    .string "And they said unto him, Where wilt\n"
    .string "thou that we prepare?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_10::
    .string "And he said unto them, Behold, when\n"
    .string "ye are entered into the city, there\l"
    .string "shall a man meet you, bearing a\l"
    .string "pitcher of water; follow him into\l"
    .string "the house where he entereth in$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_11::
    .string "And ye shall say unto the goodman\n"
    .string "of the house, The Master saith unto\l"
    .string "thee, Where is the guestchamber,\l"
    .string "where I shall eat the passover with\l"
    .string "my disciples?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_12::
    .string "And he shall shew you a large\n"
    .string "upper room furnished: there make\l"
    .string "ready$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_13::
    .string "And they went, and found as he had\n"
    .string "said unto them: and they made ready\l"
    .string "the passover.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_14::
    .string "And when the hour was come, he sat\n"
    .string "down, and the twelve apostles with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_15::
    .string "And he said unto them, With desire I\n"
    .string "have desired to eat this passover\l"
    .string "with you before I suffer:"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_16::
    .string "For I say unto you, I will not any\n"
    .string "more eat thereof, until it be\l"
    .string "fulfilled in the kingdom of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_17::
    .string "And he took the cup, and gave\n"
    .string "thanks, and said, Take this, and\l"
    .string "divide it among yourselves:"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_18::
    .string "For I say unto you, I will not\n"
    .string "drink of the fruit of the vine, until\l"
    .string "the kingdom of God shall come$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_19::
    .string "And he took bread, and gave thanks,\n"
    .string "and brake it, and gave unto them,\l"
    .string "saying, This is my body which is\l"
    .string "given for you: this do in remembrance\l"
    .string "of me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_20::
    .string "Likewise also the cup after\n"
    .string "supper, saying, This cup is the new\l"
    .string "testament in my blood, which is shed\l"
    .string "for you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_21::
    .string "But, behold, the hand of him that\n"
    .string "betrayeth me is with me on the table.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_22::
    .string "And truly the Son of man goeth, as\n"
    .string "it was determined: but woe unto that\l"
    .string "man by whom he is betrayed!"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_23::
    .string "And they began to enquire among\n"
    .string "themselves, which of them it was\l"
    .string "that should do this thing$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_24::
    .string "And there was also a strife among\n"
    .string "them, which of them should be\l"
    .string "accounted the greatest.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_25::
    .string "And he said unto them, The kings of\n"
    .string "the Gentiles exercise lordship\l"
    .string "over them; and they that exercise\l"
    .string "authority upon them are called\l"
    .string "benefactors.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_26::
    .string "But ye shall not be so: but he that\n"
    .string "is greatest among you, let him be as\l"
    .string "the younger; and he that is chief, as\l"
    .string "he that doth serve.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_27::
    .string "For whether is greater, he that\n"
    .string "sitteth at meat, or he that serveth?\l"
    .string "is not he that sitteth at meat? but I\l"
    .string "am among you as he that serveth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_28::
    .string "Ye are they which have continued\n"
    .string "with me in my temptations.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_29::
    .string "And I appoint unto you a kingdom,\n"
    .string "as my Father hath appointed unto me;"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_30::
    .string "That ye may eat and drink at my\n"
    .string "table in my kingdom, and sit on\l"
    .string "thrones judging the twelve tribes of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_31::
    .string "And the Lord said, Simon, Simon,\n"
    .string "behold, Satan hath desired to have\l"
    .string "you, that he may sift you as wheat:"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_32::
    .string "But I have prayed for thee, that thy\n"
    .string "faith fail not: and when thou art\l"
    .string "converted, strengthen thy brethren$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_33::
    .string "And he said unto him, Lord, I am\n"
    .string "ready to go with thee, both into\l"
    .string "prison, and to death.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_34::
    .string "And he said, I tell thee, Peter,\n"
    .string "the cock shall not crow this day,\l"
    .string "before that thou shalt thrice deny\l"
    .string "that thou knowest me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_35::
    .string "And he said unto them, When I sent\n"
    .string "you without purse, and scrip, and\l"
    .string "shoes, lacked ye any thing? And they\l"
    .string "said, Nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_36::
    .string "Then said he unto them, But now, he\n"
    .string "that hath a purse, let him take it,\l"
    .string "and likewise his scrip: and he that\l"
    .string "hath no sword, let him sell his\l"
    .string "garment, and buy one.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_37::
    .string "For I say unto you, that this that is\n"
    .string "written must yet be accomplished in\l"
    .string "me, And he was reckoned among the\l"
    .string "transgressors: for the things\l"
    .string "concerning me have an end.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_38::
    .string "And they said, Lord, behold, here\n"
    .string "are two swords. And he said unto\l"
    .string "them, It is enough.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_39::
    .string "And he came out, and went, as he was\n"
    .string "wont, to the mount of Olives; and his\l"
    .string "disciples also followed him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_40::
    .string "And when he was at the place, he\n"
    .string "said unto them, Pray that ye enter\l"
    .string "not into temptation.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_41::
    .string "And he was withdrawn from them about\n"
    .string "a stone’s cast, and kneeled down,\l"
    .string "and prayed,"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_42::
    .string "Saying, Father, if thou be willing,\n"
    .string "remove this cup from me:\l"
    .string "nevertheless not my will, but\l"
    .string "thine, be done$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_43::
    .string "And there appeared an angel unto\n"
    .string "him from heaven, strengthening him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_44::
    .string "And being in an agony he prayed\n"
    .string "more earnestly: and his sweat was as\l"
    .string "it were great drops of blood\l"
    .string "falling down to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_45::
    .string "And when he rose up from prayer,\n"
    .string "and was come to his disciples, he\l"
    .string "found them sleeping for sorrow,"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_46::
    .string "And said unto them, Why sleep ye?\n"
    .string "rise and pray, lest ye enter into\l"
    .string "temptation$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_47::
    .string "And while he yet spake, behold a\n"
    .string "multitude, and he that was called\l"
    .string "Judas, one of the twelve, went\l"
    .string "before them, and drew near unto Jesus\l"
    .string "to kiss him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_48::
    .string "But Jesus said unto him, Judas,\n"
    .string "betrayest thou the Son of man with a\l"
    .string "kiss?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_49::
    .string "When they which were about him saw\n"
    .string "what would follow, they said unto\l"
    .string "him, Lord, shall we smite with the\l"
    .string "sword?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_50::
    .string "And one of them smote the servant of\n"
    .string "the high priest, and cut off his\l"
    .string "right ear$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_51::
    .string "And Jesus answered and said, Suffer\n"
    .string "ye thus far. And he touched his ear,\l"
    .string "and healed him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_52::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto the chief\n"
    .string "priests, and captains of the\l"
    .string "temple, and the elders, which were\l"
    .string "come to him, Be ye come out, as\l"
    .string "against a thief, with swords and\l"
    .string "staves?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_53::
    .string "When I was daily with you in the\n"
    .string "temple, ye stretched forth no hands\l"
    .string "against me: but this is your hour,\l"
    .string "and the power of darkness$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_54::
    .string "Then took they him, and led him, and\n"
    .string "brought him into the high priest’s\l"
    .string "house. And Peter followed afar off.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_55::
    .string "And when they had kindled a fire in\n"
    .string "the midst of the hall, and were set\l"
    .string "down together, Peter sat down among\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_56::
    .string "But a certain maid beheld him as he\n"
    .string "sat by the fire, and earnestly\l"
    .string "looked upon him, and said, This man\l"
    .string "was also with him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_57::
    .string "And he denied him, saying, Woman, I\n"
    .string "know him not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_58::
    .string "And after a little while another\n"
    .string "saw him, and said, Thou art also of\l"
    .string "them. And Peter said, Man, I am not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_59::
    .string "And about the space of one hour\n"
    .string "after another confidently affirmed,\l"
    .string "saying, Of a truth this fellow also\l"
    .string "was with him: for he is a Galilaean.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_60::
    .string "And Peter said, Man, I know not what\n"
    .string "thou sayest. And immediately, while\l"
    .string "he yet spake, the cock crew.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_61::
    .string "And the Lord turned, and looked\n"
    .string "upon Peter. And Peter remembered the\l"
    .string "word of the Lord, how he had said unto\l"
    .string "him, Before the cock crow, thou\l"
    .string "shalt deny me thrice.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_62::
    .string "And Peter went out, and wept\n"
    .string "bitterly.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_63::
    .string "And the men that held Jesus mocked\n"
    .string "him, and smote him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_64::
    .string "And when they had blindfolded him,\n"
    .string "they struck him on the face, and\l"
    .string "asked him, saying, Prophesy, who is\l"
    .string "it that smote thee?"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_65::
    .string "And many other things\n"
    .string "blasphemously spake they against\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_66::
    .string "And as soon as it was day, the\n"
    .string "elders of the people and the chief\l"
    .string "priests and the scribes came\l"
    .string "together, and led him into their\l"
    .string "council, saying,"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_67::
    .string "Art thou the Christ? tell us. And\n"
    .string "he said unto them, If I tell you, ye\l"
    .string "will not believe:"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_68::
    .string "And if I also ask you, ye will not\n"
    .string "answer me, nor let me go$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_69::
    .string "Hereafter shall the Son of man sit\n"
    .string "on the right hand of the power of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_70::
    .string "Then said they all, Art thou then\n"
    .string "the Son of God? And he said unto them,\l"
    .string "Ye say that I am.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_22_71::
    .string "And they said, What need we any\n"
    .string "further witness? for we ourselves\l"
    .string "have heard of his own mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_1::
    .string "And the whole multitude of them\n"
    .string "arose, and led him unto Pilate.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_2::
    .string "And they began to accuse him,\n"
    .string "saying, We found this fellow\l"
    .string "perverting the nation, and\l"
    .string "forbidding to give tribute to Caesar,\l"
    .string "saying that he himself is Christ a\l"
    .string "King.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_3::
    .string "And Pilate asked him, saying, Art\n"
    .string "thou the King of the Jews? And he\l"
    .string "answered him and said, Thou sayest it.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_4::
    .string "Then said Pilate to the chief\n"
    .string "priests and to the people, I find\l"
    .string "no fault in this man.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_5::
    .string "And they were the more fierce,\n"
    .string "saying, He stirreth up the people,\l"
    .string "teaching throughout all Jewry,\l"
    .string "beginning from Galilee to this\l"
    .string "place.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_6::
    .string "When Pilate heard of Galilee, he\n"
    .string "asked whether the man were a\l"
    .string "Galilaean.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_7::
    .string "And as soon as he knew that he\n"
    .string "belonged unto Herod’s jurisdiction,\l"
    .string "he sent him to Herod, who himself\l"
    .string "also was at Jerusalem at that time.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_8::
    .string "And when Herod saw Jesus, he was\n"
    .string "exceeding glad: for he was desirous\l"
    .string "to see him of a long season, because\l"
    .string "he had heard many things of him; and\l"
    .string "he hoped to have seen some miracle\l"
    .string "done by him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_9::
    .string "Then he questioned with him in many\n"
    .string "words; but he answered him nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_10::
    .string "And the chief priests and scribes\n"
    .string "stood and vehemently accused him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_11::
    .string "And Herod with his men of war set\n"
    .string "him at nought, and mocked him, and\l"
    .string "arrayed him in a gorgeous robe, and\l"
    .string "sent him again to Pilate.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_12::
    .string "And the same day Pilate and Herod\n"
    .string "were made friends together: for\l"
    .string "before they were at enmity between\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_13::
    .string "And Pilate, when he had called\n"
    .string "together the chief priests and the\l"
    .string "rulers and the people,"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_14::
    .string "Said unto them, Ye have brought this\n"
    .string "man unto me, as one that perverteth\l"
    .string "the people: and, behold, I, having\l"
    .string "examined him before you, have found\l"
    .string "no fault in this man touching those\l"
    .string "things whereof ye accuse him:"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_15::
    .string "No, nor yet Herod: for I sent you to\n"
    .string "him; and, lo, nothing worthy of death\l"
    .string "is done unto him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_16::
    .string "I will therefore chastise him, and\n"
    .string "release him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_17::
    .string "(For of necessity he must release\n"
    .string "one unto them at the feast.)"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_18::
    .string "And they cried out all at once,\n"
    .string "saying, Away with this man, and\l"
    .string "release unto us Barabbas:"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_19::
    .string "(Who for a certain sedition made in\n"
    .string "the city, and for murder, was cast\l"
    .string "into prison.)"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_20::
    .string "Pilate therefore, willing to\n"
    .string "release Jesus, spake again to them$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_21::
    .string "But they cried, saying, Crucify him,\n"
    .string "crucify him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_22::
    .string "And he said unto them the third\n"
    .string "time, Why, what evil hath he done? I\l"
    .string "have found no cause of death in him: I\l"
    .string "will therefore chastise him, and\l"
    .string "let him go.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_23::
    .string "And they were instant with loud\n"
    .string "voices, requiring that he might be\l"
    .string "crucified. And the voices of them and\l"
    .string "of the chief priests prevailed.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_24::
    .string "And Pilate gave sentence that it\n"
    .string "should be as they required.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_25::
    .string "And he released unto them him that\n"
    .string "for sedition and murder was cast into\l"
    .string "prison, whom they had desired; but he\l"
    .string "delivered Jesus to their will.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_26::
    .string "And as they led him away, they laid\n"
    .string "hold upon one Simon, a Cyrenian,\l"
    .string "coming out of the country, and on him\l"
    .string "they laid the cross, that he might\l"
    .string "bear it after Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_27::
    .string "And there followed him a great\n"
    .string "company of people, and of women,\l"
    .string "which also bewailed and lamented\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_28::
    .string "But Jesus turning unto them said,\n"
    .string "Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not\l"
    .string "for me, but weep for yourselves, and\l"
    .string "for your children.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_29::
    .string "For, behold, the days are coming, in\n"
    .string "the which they shall say, Blessed\l"
    .string "are the barren, and the wombs that\l"
    .string "never bare, and the paps which never\l"
    .string "gave suck.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_30::
    .string "Then shall they begin to say to the\n"
    .string "mountains, Fall on us; and to the\l"
    .string "hills, Cover us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_31::
    .string "For if they do these things in a\n"
    .string "green tree, what shall be done in\l"
    .string "the dry?"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_32::
    .string "And there were also two other,\n"
    .string "malefactors, led with him to be put\l"
    .string "to death$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_33::
    .string "And when they were come to the\n"
    .string "place, which is called Calvary,\l"
    .string "there they crucified him, and the\l"
    .string "malefactors, one on the right hand,\l"
    .string "and the other on the left.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_34::
    .string "Then said Jesus, Father, forgive\n"
    .string "them; for they know not what they do.\l"
    .string "And they parted his raiment, and\l"
    .string "cast lots.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_35::
    .string "And the people stood beholding.\n"
    .string "And the rulers also with them\l"
    .string "derided him, saying, He saved others;\l"
    .string "let him save himself, if he be\l"
    .string "Christ, the chosen of God.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_36::
    .string "And the soldiers also mocked him,\n"
    .string "coming to him, and offering him\l"
    .string "vinegar,"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_37::
    .string "And saying, If thou be the king of\n"
    .string "the Jews, save thyself$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_38::
    .string "And a superscription also was\n"
    .string "written over him in letters of\l"
    .string "Greek, and Latin, and Hebrew, THIS IS\l"
    .string "THE KING OF THE JEWS.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_39::
    .string "And one of the malefactors which\n"
    .string "were hanged railed on him, saying,\l"
    .string "If thou be Christ, save thyself and\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_40::
    .string "But the other answering rebuked him,\n"
    .string "saying, Dost not thou fear God,\l"
    .string "seeing thou art in the same\l"
    .string "condemnation?"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_41::
    .string "And we indeed justly; for we\n"
    .string "receive the due reward of our deeds:\l"
    .string "but this man hath done nothing amiss$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_42::
    .string "And he said unto Jesus, Lord,\n"
    .string "remember me when thou comest into thy\l"
    .string "kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_43::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Verily I\n"
    .string "say unto thee, To day shalt thou be\l"
    .string "with me in paradise.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_44::
    .string "And it was about the sixth hour, and\n"
    .string "there was a darkness over all the\l"
    .string "earth until the ninth hour.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_45::
    .string "And the sun was darkened, and the\n"
    .string "veil of the temple was rent in the\l"
    .string "midst.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_46::
    .string "And when Jesus had cried with a\n"
    .string "loud voice, he said, Father, into thy\l"
    .string "hands I commend my spirit: and\l"
    .string "having said thus, he gave up the\l"
    .string "ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_47::
    .string "Now when the centurion saw what was\n"
    .string "done, he glorified God, saying,\l"
    .string "Certainly this was a righteous man.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_48::
    .string "And all the people that came\n"
    .string "together to that sight, beholding\l"
    .string "the things which were done, smote\l"
    .string "their breasts, and returned.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_49::
    .string "And all his acquaintance, and the\n"
    .string "women that followed him from\l"
    .string "Galilee, stood afar off, beholding\l"
    .string "these things.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_50::
    .string "And, behold, there was a man named\n"
    .string "Joseph, a counsellor; and he was a\l"
    .string "good man, and a just:"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_51::
    .string "(The same had not consented to the\n"
    .string "counsel and deed of them;) he was of\l"
    .string "Arimathaea, a city of the Jews: who\l"
    .string "also himself waited for the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_52::
    .string "This man went unto Pilate, and\n"
    .string "begged the body of Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_53::
    .string "And he took it down, and wrapped it\n"
    .string "in linen, and laid it in a\l"
    .string "sepulchre that was hewn in stone,\l"
    .string "wherein never man before was laid.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_54::
    .string "And that day was the preparation,\n"
    .string "and the sabbath drew on.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_55::
    .string "And the women also, which came with\n"
    .string "him from Galilee, followed after,\l"
    .string "and beheld the sepulchre, and how\l"
    .string "his body was laid.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_23_56::
    .string "And they returned, and prepared\n"
    .string "spices and ointments; and rested the\l"
    .string "sabbath day according to the\l"
    .string "commandment.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_1::
    .string "Now upon the first day of the week,\n"
    .string "very early in the morning, they came\l"
    .string "unto the sepulchre, bringing the\l"
    .string "spices which they had prepared, and\l"
    .string "certain others with them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_2::
    .string "And they found the stone rolled\n"
    .string "away from the sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_3::
    .string "And they entered in, and found not\n"
    .string "the body of the Lord Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_4::
    .string "And it came to pass, as they were\n"
    .string "much perplexed thereabout,\l"
    .string "behold, two men stood by them in\l"
    .string "shining garments:"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_5::
    .string "And as they were afraid, and bowed\n"
    .string "down their faces to the earth, they\l"
    .string "said unto them, Why seek ye the\l"
    .string "living among the dead?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_6::
    .string "He is not here, but is risen:\n"
    .string "remember how he spake unto you when\l"
    .string "he was yet in Galilee,"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_7::
    .string "Saying, The Son of man must be\n"
    .string "delivered into the hands of sinful\l"
    .string "men, and be crucified, and the third\l"
    .string "day rise again$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_8::
    .string "And they remembered his words,"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_9::
    .string "And returned from the sepulchre,\n"
    .string "and told all these things unto the\l"
    .string "eleven, and to all the rest$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_10::
    .string "It was Mary Magdalene and Joanna,\n"
    .string "and Mary the mother of James, and\l"
    .string "other women that were with them,\l"
    .string "which told these things unto the\l"
    .string "apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_11::
    .string "And their words seemed to them as\n"
    .string "idle tales, and they believed them\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_12::
    .string "Then arose Peter, and ran unto the\n"
    .string "sepulchre; and stooping down, he\l"
    .string "beheld the linen clothes laid by\l"
    .string "themselves, and departed, wondering\l"
    .string "in himself at that which was come to\l"
    .string "pass.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_13::
    .string "And, behold, two of them went that\n"
    .string "same day to a village called\l"
    .string "Emmaus, which was from Jerusalem\l"
    .string "about threescore furlongs.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_14::
    .string "And they talked together of all\n"
    .string "these things which had happened.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_15::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, while\n"
    .string "they communed together and reasoned,\l"
    .string "Jesus himself drew near, and went\l"
    .string "with them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_16::
    .string "But their eyes were holden that\n"
    .string "they should not know him.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_17::
    .string "And he said unto them, What manner\n"
    .string "of communications are these that ye\l"
    .string "have one to another, as ye walk, and\l"
    .string "are sad?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_18::
    .string "And the one of them, whose name was\n"
    .string "Cleopas, answering said unto him,\l"
    .string "Art thou only a stranger in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, and hast not known the\l"
    .string "things which are come to pass there\l"
    .string "in these days?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_19::
    .string "And he said unto them, What things?\n"
    .string "And they said unto him, Concerning\l"
    .string "Jesus of Nazareth, which was a\l"
    .string "prophet mighty in deed and word\l"
    .string "before God and all the people:"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_20::
    .string "And how the chief priests and our\n"
    .string "rulers delivered him to be\l"
    .string "condemned to death, and have\l"
    .string "crucified him$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_21::
    .string "But we trusted that it had been he\n"
    .string "which should have redeemed Israel:\l"
    .string "and beside all this, to day is the\l"
    .string "third day since these things were\l"
    .string "done.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_22::
    .string "Yea, and certain women also of our\n"
    .string "company made us astonished, which\l"
    .string "were early at the sepulchre;"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_23::
    .string "And when they found not his body,\n"
    .string "they came, saying, that they had\l"
    .string "also seen a vision of angels, which\l"
    .string "said that he was alive$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_24::
    .string "And certain of them which were with\n"
    .string "us went to the sepulchre, and found\l"
    .string "it even so as the women had said: but\l"
    .string "him they saw not.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_25::
    .string "Then he said unto them, O fools, and\n"
    .string "slow of heart to believe all that\l"
    .string "the prophets have spoken:"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_26::
    .string "Ought not Christ to have suffered\n"
    .string "these things, and to enter into his\l"
    .string "glory?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_27::
    .string "And beginning at Moses and all the\n"
    .string "prophets, he expounded unto them in\l"
    .string "all the scriptures the things\l"
    .string "concerning himself$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_28::
    .string "And they drew nigh unto the\n"
    .string "village, whither they went: and he\l"
    .string "made as though he would have gone\l"
    .string "further.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_29::
    .string "But they constrained him, saying,\n"
    .string "Abide with us: for it is toward\l"
    .string "evening, and the day is far spent.\l"
    .string "And he went in to tarry with them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_30::
    .string "And it came to pass, as he sat at\n"
    .string "meat with them, he took bread, and\l"
    .string "blessed it, and brake, and gave to\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_31::
    .string "And their eyes were opened, and\n"
    .string "they knew him; and he vanished out of\l"
    .string "their sight.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_32::
    .string "And they said one to another, Did\n"
    .string "not our heart burn within us, while\l"
    .string "he talked with us by the way, and\l"
    .string "while he opened to us the\l"
    .string "scriptures?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_33::
    .string "And they rose up the same hour, and\n"
    .string "returned to Jerusalem, and found the\l"
    .string "eleven gathered together, and them\l"
    .string "that were with them,"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_34::
    .string "Saying, The Lord is risen indeed,\n"
    .string "and hath appeared to Simon$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_35::
    .string "And they told what things were done\n"
    .string "in the way, and how he was known of\l"
    .string "them in breaking of bread.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_36::
    .string "And as they thus spake, Jesus\n"
    .string "himself stood in the midst of them,\l"
    .string "and saith unto them, Peace be unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_37::
    .string "But they were terrified and\n"
    .string "affrighted, and supposed that they\l"
    .string "had seen a spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_38::
    .string "And he said unto them, Why are ye\n"
    .string "troubled? and why do thoughts arise\l"
    .string "in your hearts?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_39::
    .string "Behold my hands and my feet, that it\n"
    .string "is I myself: handle me, and see; for\l"
    .string "a spirit hath not flesh and bones,\l"
    .string "as ye see me have$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_40::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, he\n"
    .string "shewed them his hands and his feet.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_41::
    .string "And while they yet believed not\n"
    .string "for joy, and wondered, he said unto\l"
    .string "them, Have ye here any meat?"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_42::
    .string "And they gave him a piece of a\n"
    .string "broiled fish, and of an honeycomb$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_43::
    .string "And he took it, and did eat before\n"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_44::
    .string "And he said unto them, These are the\n"
    .string "words which I spake unto you, while\l"
    .string "I was yet with you, that all things\l"
    .string "must be fulfilled, which were\l"
    .string "written in the law of Moses, and in\l"
    .string "the prophets, and in the psalms,\l"
    .string "concerning me.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_45::
    .string "Then opened he their understanding,\n"
    .string "that they might understand the\l"
    .string "scriptures,"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_46::
    .string "And said unto them, Thus it is\n"
    .string "written, and thus it behoved Christ\l"
    .string "to suffer, and to rise from the dead\l"
    .string "the third day:"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_47::
    .string "And that repentance and remission\n"
    .string "of sins should be preached in his\l"
    .string "name among all nations, beginning\l"
    .string "at Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_48::
    .string "And ye are witnesses of these things.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_49::
    .string "And, behold, I send the promise of\n"
    .string "my Father upon you: but tarry ye in\l"
    .string "the city of Jerusalem, until ye be\l"
    .string "endued with power from on high.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_50::
    .string "And he led them out as far as to\n"
    .string "Bethany, and he lifted up his hands,\l"
    .string "and blessed them.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_51::
    .string "And it came to pass, while he\n"
    .string "blessed them, he was parted from\l"
    .string "them, and carried up into heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_52::
    .string "And they worshipped him, and\n"
    .string "returned to Jerusalem with great\l"
    .string "joy:"
Bible_Text_Luke_24_53::
    .string "And were continually in the\n"
    .string "temple, praising and blessing God.\l"
    .string "Amen$"
Bible_Text_John_1_1::
    .string "In the beginning was the Word, and\n"
    .string "the Word was with God, and the Word\l"
    .string "was God.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_2::
    .string "The same was in the beginning with\n"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_3::
    .string "All things were made by him; and\n"
    .string "without him was not any thing made\l"
    .string "that was made.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_4::
    .string "In him was life; and the life was\n"
    .string "the light of men.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_5::
    .string "And the light shineth in darkness;\n"
    .string "and the darkness comprehended it not.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_6::
    .string "There was a man sent from God, whose\n"
    .string "name was John.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_7::
    .string "The same came for a witness, to bear\n"
    .string "witness of the Light, that all men\l"
    .string "through him might believe.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_8::
    .string "He was not that Light, but was sent\n"
    .string "to bear witness of that Light.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_9::
    .string "That was the true Light, which\n"
    .string "lighteth every man that cometh into\l"
    .string "the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_10::
    .string "He was in the world, and the world\n"
    .string "was made by him, and the world knew\l"
    .string "him not.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_11::
    .string "He came unto his own, and his own\n"
    .string "received him not.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_12::
    .string "But as many as received him, to them\n"
    .string "gave he power to become the sons of\l"
    .string "God, even to them that believe on his\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_John_1_13::
    .string "Which were born, not of blood, nor\n"
    .string "of the will of the flesh, nor of the\l"
    .string "will of man, but of God$"
Bible_Text_John_1_14::
    .string "And the Word was made flesh, and\n"
    .string "dwelt among us, (and we beheld his\l"
    .string "glory, the glory as of the only\l"
    .string "begotten of the Father,) full of\l"
    .string "grace and truth.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_15::
    .string "John bare witness of him, and cried,\n"
    .string "saying, This was he of whom I spake,\l"
    .string "He that cometh after me is preferred\l"
    .string "before me: for he was before me.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_16::
    .string "And of his fulness have all we\n"
    .string "received, and grace for grace.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_17::
    .string "For the law was given by Moses, but\n"
    .string "grace and truth came by Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_18::
    .string "No man hath seen God at any time, the\n"
    .string "only begotten Son, which is in the\l"
    .string "bosom of the Father, he hath\l"
    .string "declared him.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_19::
    .string "And this is the record of John, when\n"
    .string "the Jews sent priests and Levites\l"
    .string "from Jerusalem to ask him, Who art\l"
    .string "thou?"
Bible_Text_John_1_20::
    .string "And he confessed, and denied not;\n"
    .string "but confessed, I am not the Christ$"
Bible_Text_John_1_21::
    .string "And they asked him, What then? Art\n"
    .string "thou Elias? And he saith, I am not.\l"
    .string "Art thou that prophet? And he\l"
    .string "answered, No.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_22::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Who art\n"
    .string "thou? that we may give an answer to\l"
    .string "them that sent us. What sayest thou\l"
    .string "of thyself?"
Bible_Text_John_1_23::
    .string "He said, I am the voice of one crying\n"
    .string "in the wilderness, Make straight the\l"
    .string "way of the Lord, as said the prophet\l"
    .string "Esaias$"
Bible_Text_John_1_24::
    .string "And they which were sent were of the\n"
    .string "Pharisees.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_25::
    .string "And they asked him, and said unto\n"
    .string "him, Why baptizest thou then, if\l"
    .string "thou be not that Christ, nor Elias,\l"
    .string "neither that prophet?"
Bible_Text_John_1_26::
    .string "John answered them, saying, I\n"
    .string "baptize with water: but there\l"
    .string "standeth one among you, whom ye know\l"
    .string "not;"
Bible_Text_John_1_27::
    .string "He it is, who coming after me is\n"
    .string "preferred before me, whose shoe’s\l"
    .string "latchet I am not worthy to unloose$"
Bible_Text_John_1_28::
    .string "These things were done in Bethabara\n"
    .string "beyond Jordan, where John was\l"
    .string "baptizing.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_29::
    .string "The next day John seeth Jesus coming\n"
    .string "unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb\l"
    .string "of God, which taketh away the sin of\l"
    .string "the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_30::
    .string "This is he of whom I said, After me\n"
    .string "cometh a man which is preferred\l"
    .string "before me: for he was before me.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_31::
    .string "And I knew him not: but that he\n"
    .string "should be made manifest to Israel,\l"
    .string "therefore am I come baptizing with\l"
    .string "water.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_32::
    .string "And John bare record, saying, I saw\n"
    .string "the Spirit descending from heaven\l"
    .string "like a dove, and it abode upon him.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_33::
    .string "And I knew him not: but he that sent\n"
    .string "me to baptize with water, the same\l"
    .string "said unto me, Upon whom thou shalt\l"
    .string "see the Spirit descending, and\l"
    .string "remaining on him, the same is he\l"
    .string "which baptizeth with the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_34::
    .string "And I saw, and bare record that this\n"
    .string "is the Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_35::
    .string "Again the next day after John stood,\n"
    .string "and two of his disciples;"
Bible_Text_John_1_36::
    .string "And looking upon Jesus as he\n"
    .string "walked, he saith, Behold the Lamb of\l"
    .string "God!"
Bible_Text_John_1_37::
    .string "And the two disciples heard him\n"
    .string "speak, and they followed Jesus$"
Bible_Text_John_1_38::
    .string "Then Jesus turned, and saw them\n"
    .string "following, and saith unto them,\l"
    .string "What seek ye? They said unto him,\l"
    .string "Rabbi, (which is to say, being\l"
    .string "interpreted, Master,) where\l"
    .string "dwellest thou?"
Bible_Text_John_1_39::
    .string "He saith unto them, Come and see.\n"
    .string "They came and saw where he dwelt, and\l"
    .string "abode with him that day: for it was\l"
    .string "about the tenth hour$"
Bible_Text_John_1_40::
    .string "One of the two which heard John\n"
    .string "speak, and followed him, was\l"
    .string "Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_41::
    .string "He first findeth his own brother\n"
    .string "Simon, and saith unto him, We have\l"
    .string "found the Messias, which is, being\l"
    .string "interpreted, the Christ.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_42::
    .string "And he brought him to Jesus. And\n"
    .string "when Jesus beheld him, he said, Thou\l"
    .string "art Simon the son of Jona: thou shalt\l"
    .string "be called Cephas, which is by\l"
    .string "interpretation, A stone.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_43::
    .string "The day following Jesus would go\n"
    .string "forth into Galilee, and findeth\l"
    .string "Philip, and saith unto him, Follow\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_44::
    .string "Now Philip was of Bethsaida, the\n"
    .string "city of Andrew and Peter.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_45::
    .string "Philip findeth Nathanael, and\n"
    .string "saith unto him, We have found him, of\l"
    .string "whom Moses in the law, and the\l"
    .string "prophets, did write, Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth, the son of Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_46::
    .string "And Nathanael said unto him, Can\n"
    .string "there any good thing come out of\l"
    .string "Nazareth? Philip saith unto him,\l"
    .string "Come and see.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_47::
    .string "Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him,\n"
    .string "and saith of him, Behold an\l"
    .string "Israelite indeed, in whom is no\l"
    .string "guile!"
Bible_Text_John_1_48::
    .string "Nathanael saith unto him, Whence\n"
    .string "knowest thou me? Jesus answered and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Before that Philip\l"
    .string "called thee, when thou wast under\l"
    .string "the fig tree, I saw thee$"
Bible_Text_John_1_49::
    .string "Nathanael answered and saith unto\n"
    .string "him, Rabbi, thou art the Son of God;\l"
    .string "thou art the King of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_50::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Because I said unto thee, I saw thee\l"
    .string "under the fig tree, believest thou?\l"
    .string "thou shalt see greater things than\l"
    .string "these.$"
Bible_Text_John_1_51::
    .string "And he saith unto him, Verily,\n"
    .string "verily, I say unto you, Hereafter ye\l"
    .string "shall see heaven open, and the\l"
    .string "angels of God ascending and\l"
    .string "descending upon the Son of man.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_1::
    .string "And the third day there was a\n"
    .string "marriage in Cana of Galilee; and the\l"
    .string "mother of Jesus was there:"
Bible_Text_John_2_2::
    .string "And both Jesus was called, and his\n"
    .string "disciples, to the marriage$"
Bible_Text_John_2_3::
    .string "And when they wanted wine, the\n"
    .string "mother of Jesus saith unto him, They\l"
    .string "have no wine.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_4::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Woman, what\n"
    .string "have I to do with thee? mine hour is\l"
    .string "not yet come.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_5::
    .string "His mother saith unto the servants,\n"
    .string "Whatsoever he saith unto you, do it.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_6::
    .string "And there were set there six\n"
    .string "waterpots of stone, after the manner\l"
    .string "of the purifying of the Jews,\l"
    .string "containing two or three firkins\l"
    .string "apiece.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_7::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, Fill the\n"
    .string "waterpots with water. And they\l"
    .string "filled them up to the brim.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_8::
    .string "And he saith unto them, Draw out\n"
    .string "now, and bear unto the governor of\l"
    .string "the feast. And they bare it.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_9::
    .string "When the ruler of the feast had\n"
    .string "tasted the water that was made wine,\l"
    .string "and knew not whence it was: (but the\l"
    .string "servants which drew the water knew;)\l"
    .string "the governor of the feast called\l"
    .string "the bridegroom,"
Bible_Text_John_2_10::
    .string "And saith unto him, Every man at the\n"
    .string "beginning doth set forth good wine;\l"
    .string "and when men have well drunk, then\l"
    .string "that which is worse: but thou hast\l"
    .string "kept the good wine until now$"
Bible_Text_John_2_11::
    .string "This beginning of miracles did\n"
    .string "Jesus in Cana of Galilee, and\l"
    .string "manifested forth his glory; and his\l"
    .string "disciples believed on him.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_12::
    .string "After this he went down to\n"
    .string "Capernaum, he, and his mother, and\l"
    .string "his brethren, and his disciples:\l"
    .string "and they continued there not many\l"
    .string "days.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_13::
    .string "And the Jews’ passover was at hand,\n"
    .string "and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_14::
    .string "And found in the temple those that\n"
    .string "sold oxen and sheep and doves, and\l"
    .string "the changers of money sitting:"
Bible_Text_John_2_15::
    .string "And when he had made a scourge of\n"
    .string "small cords, he drove them all out\l"
    .string "of the temple, and the sheep, and\l"
    .string "the oxen; and poured out the\l"
    .string "changers’ money, and overthrew the\l"
    .string "tables;"
Bible_Text_John_2_16::
    .string "And said unto them that sold doves,\n"
    .string "Take these things hence; make not my\l"
    .string "Father’s house an house of\l"
    .string "merchandise$"
Bible_Text_John_2_17::
    .string "And his disciples remembered that\n"
    .string "it was written, The zeal of thine\l"
    .string "house hath eaten me up.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_18::
    .string "Then answered the Jews and said unto\n"
    .string "him, What sign shewest thou unto us,\l"
    .string "seeing that thou doest these things?"
Bible_Text_John_2_19::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Destroy this temple, and in three\l"
    .string "days I will raise it up$"
Bible_Text_John_2_20::
    .string "Then said the Jews, Forty and six\n"
    .string "years was this temple in building,\l"
    .string "and wilt thou rear it up in three\l"
    .string "days?"
Bible_Text_John_2_21::
    .string "But he spake of the temple of his\n"
    .string "body$"
Bible_Text_John_2_22::
    .string "When therefore he was risen from the\n"
    .string "dead, his disciples remembered that\l"
    .string "he had said this unto them; and they\l"
    .string "believed the scripture, and the\l"
    .string "word which Jesus had said.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_23::
    .string "Now when he was in Jerusalem at the\n"
    .string "passover, in the feast day, many\l"
    .string "believed in his name, when they saw\l"
    .string "the miracles which he did.$"
Bible_Text_John_2_24::
    .string "But Jesus did not commit himself\n"
    .string "unto them, because he knew all men,"
Bible_Text_John_2_25::
    .string "And needed not that any should\n"
    .string "testify of man: for he knew what was\l"
    .string "in man$"
Bible_Text_John_3_1::
    .string "There was a man of the Pharisees,\n"
    .string "named Nicodemus, a ruler of the\l"
    .string "Jews:"
Bible_Text_John_3_2::
    .string "The same came to Jesus by night, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Rabbi, we know that\l"
    .string "thou art a teacher come from God: for\l"
    .string "no man can do these miracles that\l"
    .string "thou doest, except God be with him$"
Bible_Text_John_3_3::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto thee,\l"
    .string "Except a man be born again, he cannot\l"
    .string "see the kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_4::
    .string "Nicodemus saith unto him, How can a\n"
    .string "man be born when he is old? can he\l"
    .string "enter the second time into his\l"
    .string "mother’s womb, and be born?"
Bible_Text_John_3_5::
    .string "Jesus answered, Verily, verily, I\n"
    .string "say unto thee, Except a man be born\l"
    .string "of water and of the Spirit, he cannot\l"
    .string "enter into the kingdom of God$"
Bible_Text_John_3_6::
    .string "That which is born of the flesh is\n"
    .string "flesh; and that which is born of the\l"
    .string "Spirit is spirit.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_7::
    .string "Marvel not that I said unto thee, Ye\n"
    .string "must be born again.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_8::
    .string "The wind bloweth where it listeth,\n"
    .string "and thou hearest the sound thereof,\l"
    .string "but canst not tell whence it cometh,\l"
    .string "and whither it goeth: so is every one\l"
    .string "that is born of the Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_9::
    .string "Nicodemus answered and said unto\n"
    .string "him, How can these things be?"
Bible_Text_John_3_10::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Art thou a master of Israel, and\l"
    .string "knowest not these things?"
Bible_Text_John_3_11::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto thee, We\n"
    .string "speak that we do know, and testify\l"
    .string "that we have seen; and ye receive not\l"
    .string "our witness$"
Bible_Text_John_3_12::
    .string "If I have told you earthly things,\n"
    .string "and ye believe not, how shall ye\l"
    .string "believe, if I tell you of heavenly\l"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_John_3_13::
    .string "And no man hath ascended up to\n"
    .string "heaven, but he that came down from\l"
    .string "heaven, even the Son of man which is\l"
    .string "in heaven$"
Bible_Text_John_3_14::
    .string "And as Moses lifted up the serpent\n"
    .string "in the wilderness, even so must the\l"
    .string "Son of man be lifted up:"
Bible_Text_John_3_15::
    .string "That whosoever believeth in him\n"
    .string "should not perish, but have eternal\l"
    .string "life$"
Bible_Text_John_3_16::
    .string "For God so loved the world, that he\n"
    .string "gave his only begotten Son, that\l"
    .string "whosoever believeth in him should\l"
    .string "not perish, but have everlasting\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_17::
    .string "For God sent not his Son into the\n"
    .string "world to condemn the world; but that\l"
    .string "the world through him might be saved.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_18::
    .string "He that believeth on him is not\n"
    .string "condemned: but he that believeth not\l"
    .string "is condemned already, because he\l"
    .string "hath not believed in the name of the\l"
    .string "only begotten Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_19::
    .string "And this is the condemnation, that\n"
    .string "light is come into the world, and men\l"
    .string "loved darkness rather than light,\l"
    .string "because their deeds were evil.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_20::
    .string "For every one that doeth evil\n"
    .string "hateth the light, neither cometh to\l"
    .string "the light, lest his deeds should be\l"
    .string "reproved.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_21::
    .string "But he that doeth truth cometh to\n"
    .string "the light, that his deeds may be made\l"
    .string "manifest, that they are wrought in\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_22::
    .string "After these things came Jesus and\n"
    .string "his disciples into the land of\l"
    .string "Judaea; and there he tarried with\l"
    .string "them, and baptized.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_23::
    .string "And John also was baptizing in\n"
    .string "Aenon near to Salim, because there\l"
    .string "was much water there: and they came,\l"
    .string "and were baptized.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_24::
    .string "For John was not yet cast into\n"
    .string "prison.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_25::
    .string "Then there arose a question between\n"
    .string "some of John’s disciples and the\l"
    .string "Jews about purifying.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_26::
    .string "And they came unto John, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Rabbi, he that was with\l"
    .string "thee beyond Jordan, to whom thou\l"
    .string "barest witness, behold, the same\l"
    .string "baptizeth, and all men come to him.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_27::
    .string "John answered and said, A man can\n"
    .string "receive nothing, except it be given\l"
    .string "him from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_28::
    .string "Ye yourselves bear me witness, that\n"
    .string "I said, I am not the Christ, but that\l"
    .string "I am sent before him.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_29::
    .string "He that hath the bride is the\n"
    .string "bridegroom: but the friend of the\l"
    .string "bridegroom, which standeth and\l"
    .string "heareth him, rejoiceth greatly\l"
    .string "because of the bridegroom’s voice:\l"
    .string "this my joy therefore is fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_30::
    .string "He must increase, but I must\n"
    .string "decrease.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_31::
    .string "He that cometh from above is above\n"
    .string "all: he that is of the earth is\l"
    .string "earthly, and speaketh of the earth:\l"
    .string "he that cometh from heaven is above\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_32::
    .string "And what he hath seen and heard,\n"
    .string "that he testifieth; and no man\l"
    .string "receiveth his testimony.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_33::
    .string "He that hath received his testimony\n"
    .string "hath set to his seal that God is true.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_34::
    .string "For he whom God hath sent speaketh\n"
    .string "the words of God: for God giveth not\l"
    .string "the Spirit by measure unto him.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_35::
    .string "The Father loveth the Son, and hath\n"
    .string "given all things into his hand.$"
Bible_Text_John_3_36::
    .string "He that believeth on the Son hath\n"
    .string "everlasting life: and he that\l"
    .string "believeth not the Son shall not see\l"
    .string "life; but the wrath of God abideth on\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_1::
    .string "When therefore the LORD knew how the\n"
    .string "Pharisees had heard that Jesus made\l"
    .string "and baptized more disciples than\l"
    .string "John,"
Bible_Text_John_4_2::
    .string "(Though Jesus himself baptized\n"
    .string "not, but his disciples,)"
Bible_Text_John_4_3::
    .string "He left Judaea, and departed again\n"
    .string "into Galilee$"
Bible_Text_John_4_4::
    .string "And he must needs go through Samaria.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_5::
    .string "Then cometh he to a city of Samaria,\n"
    .string "which is called Sychar, near to the\l"
    .string "parcel of ground that Jacob gave to\l"
    .string "his son Joseph.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_6::
    .string "Now Jacob’s well was there. Jesus\n"
    .string "therefore, being wearied with his\l"
    .string "journey, sat thus on the well: and\l"
    .string "it was about the sixth hour.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_7::
    .string "There cometh a woman of Samaria to\n"
    .string "draw water: Jesus saith unto her,\l"
    .string "Give me to drink.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_8::
    .string "(For his disciples were gone away\n"
    .string "unto the city to buy meat.)"
Bible_Text_John_4_9::
    .string "Then saith the woman of Samaria unto\n"
    .string "him, How is it that thou, being a Jew,\l"
    .string "askest drink of me, which am a woman\l"
    .string "of Samaria? for the Jews have no\l"
    .string "dealings with the Samaritans$"
Bible_Text_John_4_10::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto her, If\n"
    .string "thou knewest the gift of God, and who\l"
    .string "it is that saith to thee, Give me to\l"
    .string "drink; thou wouldest have asked of\l"
    .string "him, and he would have given thee\l"
    .string "living water.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_11::
    .string "The woman saith unto him, Sir, thou\n"
    .string "hast nothing to draw with, and the\l"
    .string "well is deep: from whence then hast\l"
    .string "thou that living water?"
Bible_Text_John_4_12::
    .string "Art thou greater than our father\n"
    .string "Jacob, which gave us the well, and\l"
    .string "drank thereof himself, and his\l"
    .string "children, and his cattle?"
Bible_Text_John_4_13::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto her,\n"
    .string "Whosoever drinketh of this water\l"
    .string "shall thirst again:"
Bible_Text_John_4_14::
    .string "But whosoever drinketh of the water\n"
    .string "that I shall give him shall never\l"
    .string "thirst; but the water that I shall\l"
    .string "give him shall be in him a well of\l"
    .string "water springing up into\l"
    .string "everlasting life$"
Bible_Text_John_4_15::
    .string "The woman saith unto him, Sir, give\n"
    .string "me this water, that I thirst not,\l"
    .string "neither come hither to draw.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_16::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Go, call thy\n"
    .string "husband, and come hither.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_17::
    .string "The woman answered and said, I have\n"
    .string "no husband. Jesus said unto her, Thou\l"
    .string "hast well said, I have no husband:"
Bible_Text_John_4_18::
    .string "For thou hast had five husbands; and\n"
    .string "he whom thou now hast is not thy\l"
    .string "husband: in that saidst thou truly$"
Bible_Text_John_4_19::
    .string "The woman saith unto him, Sir, I\n"
    .string "perceive that thou art a prophet.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_20::
    .string "Our fathers worshipped in this\n"
    .string "mountain; and ye say, that in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem is the place where men\l"
    .string "ought to worship.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_21::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Woman,\n"
    .string "believe me, the hour cometh, when ye\l"
    .string "shall neither in this mountain, nor\l"
    .string "yet at Jerusalem, worship the\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_22::
    .string "Ye worship ye know not what: we know\n"
    .string "what we worship: for salvation is of\l"
    .string "the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_23::
    .string "But the hour cometh, and now is,\n"
    .string "when the true worshippers shall\l"
    .string "worship the Father in spirit and in\l"
    .string "truth: for the Father seeketh such to\l"
    .string "worship him.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_24::
    .string "God is a Spirit: and they that\n"
    .string "worship him must worship him in\l"
    .string "spirit and in truth.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_25::
    .string "The woman saith unto him, I know\n"
    .string "that Messias cometh, which is\l"
    .string "called Christ: when he is come, he\l"
    .string "will tell us all things.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_26::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, I that speak\n"
    .string "unto thee am he.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_27::
    .string "And upon this came his disciples,\n"
    .string "and marvelled that he talked with\l"
    .string "the woman: yet no man said, What\l"
    .string "seekest thou? or, Why talkest thou\l"
    .string "with her?"
Bible_Text_John_4_28::
    .string "The woman then left her waterpot,\n"
    .string "and went her way into the city, and\l"
    .string "saith to the men,"
Bible_Text_John_4_29::
    .string "Come, see a man, which told me all\n"
    .string "things that ever I did: is not this\l"
    .string "the Christ?"
Bible_Text_John_4_30::
    .string "Then they went out of the city, and\n"
    .string "came unto him$"
Bible_Text_John_4_31::
    .string "In the mean while his disciples\n"
    .string "prayed him, saying, Master, eat.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_32::
    .string "But he said unto them, I have meat to\n"
    .string "eat that ye know not of.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_33::
    .string "Therefore said the disciples one\n"
    .string "to another, Hath any man brought him\l"
    .string "ought to eat?"
Bible_Text_John_4_34::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, My meat is to\n"
    .string "do the will of him that sent me, and\l"
    .string "to finish his work$"
Bible_Text_John_4_35::
    .string "Say not ye, There are yet four\n"
    .string "months, and then cometh harvest?\l"
    .string "behold, I say unto you, Lift up your\l"
    .string "eyes, and look on the fields; for\l"
    .string "they are white already to harvest.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_36::
    .string "And he that reapeth receiveth\n"
    .string "wages, and gathereth fruit unto life\l"
    .string "eternal: that both he that soweth\l"
    .string "and he that reapeth may rejoice\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_37::
    .string "And herein is that saying true, One\n"
    .string "soweth, and another reapeth.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_38::
    .string "I sent you to reap that whereon ye\n"
    .string "bestowed no labour: other men\l"
    .string "laboured, and ye are entered into\l"
    .string "their labours.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_39::
    .string "And many of the Samaritans of that\n"
    .string "city believed on him for the saying\l"
    .string "of the woman, which testified, He\l"
    .string "told me all that ever I did.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_40::
    .string "So when the Samaritans were come\n"
    .string "unto him, they besought him that he\l"
    .string "would tarry with them: and he abode\l"
    .string "there two days.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_41::
    .string "And many more believed because of\n"
    .string "his own word;"
Bible_Text_John_4_42::
    .string "And said unto the woman, Now we\n"
    .string "believe, not because of thy saying:\l"
    .string "for we have heard him ourselves, and\l"
    .string "know that this is indeed the Christ,\l"
    .string "the Saviour of the world$"
Bible_Text_John_4_43::
    .string "Now after two days he departed\n"
    .string "thence, and went into Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_44::
    .string "For Jesus himself testified, that a\n"
    .string "prophet hath no honour in his own\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_45::
    .string "Then when he was come into Galilee,\n"
    .string "the Galilaeans received him, having\l"
    .string "seen all the things that he did at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem at the feast: for they\l"
    .string "also went unto the feast.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_46::
    .string "So Jesus came again into Cana of\n"
    .string "Galilee, where he made the water\l"
    .string "wine. And there was a certain\l"
    .string "nobleman, whose son was sick at\l"
    .string "Capernaum.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_47::
    .string "When he heard that Jesus was come\n"
    .string "out of Judaea into Galilee, he went\l"
    .string "unto him, and besought him that he\l"
    .string "would come down, and heal his son:\l"
    .string "for he was at the point of death.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_48::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto him, Except ye\n"
    .string "see signs and wonders, ye will not\l"
    .string "believe.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_49::
    .string "The nobleman saith unto him, Sir,\n"
    .string "come down ere my child die.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_50::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, Go thy way;\n"
    .string "thy son liveth. And the man believed\l"
    .string "the word that Jesus had spoken unto\l"
    .string "him, and he went his way.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_51::
    .string "And as he was now going down, his\n"
    .string "servants met him, and told him,\l"
    .string "saying, Thy son liveth.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_52::
    .string "Then enquired he of them the hour\n"
    .string "when he began to amend. And they said\l"
    .string "unto him, Yesterday at the seventh\l"
    .string "hour the fever left him.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_53::
    .string "So the father knew that it was at\n"
    .string "the same hour, in the which Jesus\l"
    .string "said unto him, Thy son liveth: and\l"
    .string "himself believed, and his whole\l"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_John_4_54::
    .string "This is again the second miracle\n"
    .string "that Jesus did, when he was come out\l"
    .string "of Judaea into Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_1::
    .string "After this there was a feast of the\n"
    .string "Jews; and Jesus went up to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_2::
    .string "Now there is at Jerusalem by the\n"
    .string "sheep market a pool, which is\l"
    .string "called in the Hebrew tongue\l"
    .string "Bethesda, having five porches.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_3::
    .string "In these lay a great multitude of\n"
    .string "impotent folk, of blind, halt,\l"
    .string "withered, waiting for the moving of\l"
    .string "the water.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_4::
    .string "For an angel went down at a certain\n"
    .string "season into the pool, and troubled\l"
    .string "the water: whosoever then first after\l"
    .string "the troubling of the water stepped\l"
    .string "in was made whole of whatsoever\l"
    .string "disease he had.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_5::
    .string "And a certain man was there, which\n"
    .string "had an infirmity thirty and eight\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_6::
    .string "When Jesus saw him lie, and knew\n"
    .string "that he had been now a long time in\l"
    .string "that case, he saith unto him, Wilt\l"
    .string "thou be made whole?"
Bible_Text_John_5_7::
    .string "The impotent man answered him, Sir,\n"
    .string "I have no man, when the water is\l"
    .string "troubled, to put me into the pool:\l"
    .string "but while I am coming, another\l"
    .string "steppeth down before me$"
Bible_Text_John_5_8::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, Rise, take up\n"
    .string "thy bed, and walk.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_9::
    .string "And immediately the man was made\n"
    .string "whole, and took up his bed, and\l"
    .string "walked: and on the same day was the\l"
    .string "sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_10::
    .string "The Jews therefore said unto him\n"
    .string "that was cured, It is the sabbath\l"
    .string "day: it is not lawful for thee to\l"
    .string "carry thy bed.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_11::
    .string "He answered them, He that made me\n"
    .string "whole, the same said unto me, Take\l"
    .string "up thy bed, and walk.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_12::
    .string "Then asked they him, What man is\n"
    .string "that which said unto thee, Take up\l"
    .string "thy bed, and walk?"
Bible_Text_John_5_13::
    .string "And he that was healed wist not who\n"
    .string "it was: for Jesus had conveyed\l"
    .string "himself away, a multitude being in\l"
    .string "that place$"
Bible_Text_John_5_14::
    .string "Afterward Jesus findeth him in the\n"
    .string "temple, and said unto him, Behold,\l"
    .string "thou art made whole: sin no more,\l"
    .string "lest a worse thing come unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_15::
    .string "The man departed, and told the Jews\n"
    .string "that it was Jesus, which had made him\l"
    .string "whole.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_16::
    .string "And therefore did the Jews\n"
    .string "persecute Jesus, and sought to slay\l"
    .string "him, because he had done these things\l"
    .string "on the sabbath day.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_17::
    .string "But Jesus answered them, My Father\n"
    .string "worketh hitherto, and I work.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_18::
    .string "Therefore the Jews sought the more\n"
    .string "to kill him, because he not only\l"
    .string "had broken the sabbath, but said\l"
    .string "also that God was his Father, making\l"
    .string "himself equal with God.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_19::
    .string "Then answered Jesus and said unto\n"
    .string "them, Verily, verily, I say unto\l"
    .string "you, The Son can do nothing of\l"
    .string "himself, but what he seeth the\l"
    .string "Father do: for what things soever he\l"
    .string "doeth, these also doeth the Son\l"
    .string "likewise.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_20::
    .string "For the Father loveth the Son, and\n"
    .string "sheweth him all things that\l"
    .string "himself doeth: and he will shew him\l"
    .string "greater works than these, that ye may\l"
    .string "marvel.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_21::
    .string "For as the Father raiseth up the\n"
    .string "dead, and quickeneth them; even so\l"
    .string "the Son quickeneth whom he will.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_22::
    .string "For the Father judgeth no man, but\n"
    .string "hath committed all judgment unto\l"
    .string "the Son:"
Bible_Text_John_5_23::
    .string "That all men should honour the\n"
    .string "Son, even as they honour the Father\l"
    .string "He that honoureth not the Son\l"
    .string "honoureth not the Father which hath\l"
    .string "sent him.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_24::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, He\n"
    .string "that heareth my word, and believeth\l"
    .string "on him that sent me, hath\l"
    .string "everlasting life, and shall not\l"
    .string "come into condemnation; but is\l"
    .string "passed from death unto life.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_25::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, The\n"
    .string "hour is coming, and now is, when the\l"
    .string "dead shall hear the voice of the Son\l"
    .string "of God: and they that hear shall\l"
    .string "live.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_26::
    .string "For as the Father hath life in\n"
    .string "himself; so hath he given to the Son\l"
    .string "to have life in himself;"
Bible_Text_John_5_27::
    .string "And hath given him authority to\n"
    .string "execute judgment also, because he is\l"
    .string "the Son of man$"
Bible_Text_John_5_28::
    .string "Marvel not at this: for the hour is\n"
    .string "coming, in the which all that are in\l"
    .string "the graves shall hear his voice,"
Bible_Text_John_5_29::
    .string "And shall come forth; they that\n"
    .string "have done good, unto the resurrection\l"
    .string "of life; and they that have done\l"
    .string "evil, unto the resurrection of\l"
    .string "damnation$"
Bible_Text_John_5_30::
    .string "I can of mine own self do nothing:\n"
    .string "as I hear, I judge: and my judgment is\l"
    .string "just; because I seek not mine own\l"
    .string "will, but the will of the Father\l"
    .string "which hath sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_31::
    .string "If I bear witness of myself, my\n"
    .string "witness is not true.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_32::
    .string "There is another that beareth\n"
    .string "witness of me; and I know that the\l"
    .string "witness which he witnesseth of me is\l"
    .string "true.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_33::
    .string "Ye sent unto John, and he bare\n"
    .string "witness unto the truth.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_34::
    .string "But I receive not testimony from\n"
    .string "man: but these things I say, that ye\l"
    .string "might be saved.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_35::
    .string "He was a burning and a shining\n"
    .string "light: and ye were willing for a\l"
    .string "season to rejoice in his light.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_36::
    .string "But I have greater witness than that\n"
    .string "of John: for the works which the\l"
    .string "Father hath given me to finish, the\l"
    .string "same works that I do, bear witness of\l"
    .string "me, that the Father hath sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_37::
    .string "And the Father himself, which hath\n"
    .string "sent me, hath borne witness of me. Ye\l"
    .string "have neither heard his voice at any\l"
    .string "time, nor seen his shape.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_38::
    .string "And ye have not his word abiding in\n"
    .string "you: for whom he hath sent, him ye\l"
    .string "believe not.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_39::
    .string "Search the scriptures; for in them\n"
    .string "ye think ye have eternal life: and\l"
    .string "they are they which testify of me.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_40::
    .string "And ye will not come to me, that ye\n"
    .string "might have life.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_41::
    .string "I receive not honour from men.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_42::
    .string "But I know you, that ye have not the\n"
    .string "love of God in you.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_43::
    .string "I am come in my Father’s name, and ye\n"
    .string "receive me not: if another shall\l"
    .string "come in his own name, him ye will\l"
    .string "receive.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_44::
    .string "How can ye believe, which receive\n"
    .string "honour one of another, and seek not\l"
    .string "the honour that cometh from God\l"
    .string "only?"
Bible_Text_John_5_45::
    .string "Do not think that I will accuse you\n"
    .string "to the Father: there is one that\l"
    .string "accuseth you, even Moses, in whom ye\l"
    .string "trust$"
Bible_Text_John_5_46::
    .string "For had ye believed Moses, ye would\n"
    .string "have believed me; for he wrote of me.$"
Bible_Text_John_5_47::
    .string "But if ye believe not his writings,\n"
    .string "how shall ye believe my words?"
Bible_Text_John_6_1::
    .string "After these things Jesus went over\n"
    .string "the sea of Galilee, which is the sea\l"
    .string "of Tiberias$"
Bible_Text_John_6_2::
    .string "And a great multitude followed\n"
    .string "him, because they saw his miracles\l"
    .string "which he did on them that were\l"
    .string "diseased.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_3::
    .string "And Jesus went up into a mountain,\n"
    .string "and there he sat with his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_4::
    .string "And the passover, a feast of the\n"
    .string "Jews, was nigh.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_5::
    .string "When Jesus then lifted up his eyes,\n"
    .string "and saw a great company come unto\l"
    .string "him, he saith unto Philip, Whence\l"
    .string "shall we buy bread, that these may\l"
    .string "eat?"
Bible_Text_John_6_6::
    .string "And this he said to prove him: for\n"
    .string "he himself knew what he would do$"
Bible_Text_John_6_7::
    .string "Philip answered him, Two hundred\n"
    .string "pennyworth of bread is not\l"
    .string "sufficient for them, that every one\l"
    .string "of them may take a little.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_8::
    .string "One of his disciples, Andrew,\n"
    .string "Simon Peter’s brother, saith unto\l"
    .string "him,"
Bible_Text_John_6_9::
    .string "There is a lad here, which hath five\n"
    .string "barley loaves, and two small\l"
    .string "fishes: but what are they among so\l"
    .string "many?"
Bible_Text_John_6_10::
    .string "And Jesus said, Make the men sit down\n"
    .string " Now there was much grass in the\l"
    .string "place. So the men sat down, in number\l"
    .string "about five thousand$"
Bible_Text_John_6_11::
    .string "And Jesus took the loaves; and when\n"
    .string "he had given thanks, he distributed\l"
    .string "to the disciples, and the\l"
    .string "disciples to them that were set\l"
    .string "down; and likewise of the fishes as\l"
    .string "much as they would.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_12::
    .string "When they were filled, he said unto\n"
    .string "his disciples, Gather up the\l"
    .string "fragments that remain, that nothing\l"
    .string "be lost.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_13::
    .string "Therefore they gathered them\n"
    .string "together, and filled twelve\l"
    .string "baskets with the fragments of the\l"
    .string "five barley loaves, which remained\l"
    .string "over and above unto them that had\l"
    .string "eaten.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_14::
    .string "Then those men, when they had seen\n"
    .string "the miracle that Jesus did, said,\l"
    .string "This is of a truth that prophet that\l"
    .string "should come into the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_15::
    .string "When Jesus therefore perceived\n"
    .string "that they would come and take him by\l"
    .string "force, to make him a king, he\l"
    .string "departed again into a mountain\l"
    .string "himself alone.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_16::
    .string "And when even was now come, his\n"
    .string "disciples went down unto the sea,"
Bible_Text_John_6_17::
    .string "And entered into a ship, and went\n"
    .string "over the sea toward Capernaum. And\l"
    .string "it was now dark, and Jesus was not\l"
    .string "come to them$"
Bible_Text_John_6_18::
    .string "And the sea arose by reason of a\n"
    .string "great wind that blew.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_19::
    .string "So when they had rowed about five\n"
    .string "and twenty or thirty furlongs, they\l"
    .string "see Jesus walking on the sea, and\l"
    .string "drawing nigh unto the ship: and they\l"
    .string "were afraid.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_20::
    .string "But he saith unto them, It is I; be\n"
    .string "not afraid.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_21::
    .string "Then they willingly received him\n"
    .string "into the ship: and immediately the\l"
    .string "ship was at the land whither they\l"
    .string "went.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_22::
    .string "The day following, when the\n"
    .string "people which stood on the other\l"
    .string "side of the sea saw that there was\l"
    .string "none other boat there, save that one\l"
    .string "whereinto his disciples were\l"
    .string "entered, and that Jesus went not with\l"
    .string "his disciples into the boat, but\l"
    .string "that his disciples were gone away\l"
    .string "alone;"
Bible_Text_John_6_23::
    .string "(Howbeit there came other boats\n"
    .string "from Tiberias nigh unto the place\l"
    .string "where they did eat bread, after that\l"
    .string "the Lord had given thanks:)"
Bible_Text_John_6_24::
    .string "When the people therefore saw\n"
    .string "that Jesus was not there, neither his\l"
    .string "disciples, they also took\l"
    .string "shipping, and came to Capernaum,\l"
    .string "seeking for Jesus$"
Bible_Text_John_6_25::
    .string "And when they had found him on the\n"
    .string "other side of the sea, they said unto\l"
    .string "him, Rabbi, when camest thou hither?"
Bible_Text_John_6_26::
    .string "Jesus answered them and said,\n"
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, Ye\l"
    .string "seek me, not because ye saw the\l"
    .string "miracles, but because ye did eat of\l"
    .string "the loaves, and were filled$"
Bible_Text_John_6_27::
    .string "Labour not for the meat which\n"
    .string "perisheth, but for that meat which\l"
    .string "endureth unto everlasting life,\l"
    .string "which the Son of man shall give unto\l"
    .string "you: for him hath God the Father\l"
    .string "sealed.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_28::
    .string "Then said they unto him, What shall\n"
    .string "we do, that we might work the works of\l"
    .string "God?"
Bible_Text_John_6_29::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "This is the work of God, that ye\l"
    .string "believe on him whom he hath sent$"
Bible_Text_John_6_30::
    .string "They said therefore unto him, What\n"
    .string "sign shewest thou then, that we may\l"
    .string "see, and believe thee? what dost\l"
    .string "thou work?"
Bible_Text_John_6_31::
    .string "Our fathers did eat manna in the\n"
    .string "desert; as it is written, He gave\l"
    .string "them bread from heaven to eat$"
Bible_Text_John_6_32::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto them, Verily,\n"
    .string "verily, I say unto you, Moses gave\l"
    .string "you not that bread from heaven; but\l"
    .string "my Father giveth you the true bread\l"
    .string "from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_33::
    .string "For the bread of God is he which\n"
    .string "cometh down from heaven, and giveth\l"
    .string "life unto the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_34::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Lord,\n"
    .string "evermore give us this bread.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_35::
    .string "And Jesus said unto them, I am the\n"
    .string "bread of life: he that cometh to me\l"
    .string "shall never hunger; and he that\l"
    .string "believeth on me shall never thirst.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_36::
    .string "But I said unto you, That ye also\n"
    .string "have seen me, and believe not.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_37::
    .string "All that the Father giveth me\n"
    .string "shall come to me; and him that\l"
    .string "cometh to me I will in no wise cast\l"
    .string "out.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_38::
    .string "For I came down from heaven, not to\n"
    .string "do mine own will, but the will of\l"
    .string "him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_39::
    .string "And this is the Father’s will\n"
    .string "which hath sent me, that of all\l"
    .string "which he hath given me I should lose\l"
    .string "nothing, but should raise it up\l"
    .string "again at the last day.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_40::
    .string "And this is the will of him that\n"
    .string "sent me, that every one which seeth\l"
    .string "the Son, and believeth on him, may\l"
    .string "have everlasting life: and I will\l"
    .string "raise him up at the last day.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_41::
    .string "The Jews then murmured at him,\n"
    .string "because he said, I am the bread which\l"
    .string "came down from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_42::
    .string "And they said, Is not this Jesus,\n"
    .string "the son of Joseph, whose father and\l"
    .string "mother we know? how is it then that he\l"
    .string "saith, I came down from heaven?"
Bible_Text_John_6_43::
    .string "Jesus therefore answered and said\n"
    .string "unto them, Murmur not among\l"
    .string "yourselves$"
Bible_Text_John_6_44::
    .string "No man can come to me, except the\n"
    .string "Father which hath sent me draw him:\l"
    .string "and I will raise him up at the last\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_45::
    .string "It is written in the prophets, And\n"
    .string "they shall be all taught of God.\l"
    .string "Every man therefore that hath heard,\l"
    .string "and hath learned of the Father,\l"
    .string "cometh unto me.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_46::
    .string "Not that any man hath seen the\n"
    .string "Father, save he which is of God, he\l"
    .string "hath seen the Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_47::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, He\n"
    .string "that believeth on me hath\l"
    .string "everlasting life.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_48::
    .string "I am that bread of life.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_49::
    .string "Your fathers did eat manna in the\n"
    .string "wilderness, and are dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_50::
    .string "This is the bread which cometh down\n"
    .string "from heaven, that a man may eat\l"
    .string "thereof, and not die.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_51::
    .string "I am the living bread which came\n"
    .string "down from heaven: if any man eat of\l"
    .string "this bread, he shall live for ever:\l"
    .string "and the bread that I will give is my\l"
    .string "flesh, which I will give for the\l"
    .string "life of the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_52::
    .string "The Jews therefore strove among\n"
    .string "themselves, saying, How can this man\l"
    .string "give us his flesh to eat?"
Bible_Text_John_6_53::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto them, Verily,\n"
    .string "verily, I say unto you, Except ye\l"
    .string "eat the flesh of the Son of man, and\l"
    .string "drink his blood, ye have no life in\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_John_6_54::
    .string "Whoso eateth my flesh, and drinketh\n"
    .string "my blood, hath eternal life; and I\l"
    .string "will raise him up at the last day.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_55::
    .string "For my flesh is meat indeed, and my\n"
    .string "blood is drink indeed.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_56::
    .string "He that eateth my flesh, and\n"
    .string "drinketh my blood, dwelleth in me,\l"
    .string "and I in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_57::
    .string "As the living Father hath sent me,\n"
    .string "and I live by the Father: so he that\l"
    .string "eateth me, even he shall live by me.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_58::
    .string "This is that bread which came down\n"
    .string "from heaven: not as your fathers did\l"
    .string "eat manna, and are dead: he that\l"
    .string "eateth of this bread shall live for\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_59::
    .string "These things said he in the\n"
    .string "synagogue, as he taught in Capernaum.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_60::
    .string "Many therefore of his disciples,\n"
    .string "when they had heard this, said, This\l"
    .string "is an hard saying; who can hear it?"
Bible_Text_John_6_61::
    .string "When Jesus knew in himself that his\n"
    .string "disciples murmured at it, he said\l"
    .string "unto them, Doth this offend you?"
Bible_Text_John_6_62::
    .string "What and if ye shall see the Son of\n"
    .string "man ascend up where he was before?"
Bible_Text_John_6_63::
    .string "It is the spirit that quickeneth;\n"
    .string "the flesh profiteth nothing: the\l"
    .string "words that I speak unto you, they are\l"
    .string "spirit, and they are life$"
Bible_Text_John_6_64::
    .string "But there are some of you that\n"
    .string "believe not. For Jesus knew from the\l"
    .string "beginning who they were that\l"
    .string "believed not, and who should betray\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_65::
    .string "And he said, Therefore said I unto\n"
    .string "you, that no man can come unto me,\l"
    .string "except it were given unto him of my\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_66::
    .string "From that time many of his\n"
    .string "disciples went back, and walked no\l"
    .string "more with him.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_67::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto the twelve,\n"
    .string "Will ye also go away?"
Bible_Text_John_6_68::
    .string "Then Simon Peter answered him, Lord,\n"
    .string "to whom shall we go? thou hast the\l"
    .string "words of eternal life$"
Bible_Text_John_6_69::
    .string "And we believe and are sure that\n"
    .string "thou art that Christ, the Son of the\l"
    .string "living God.$"
Bible_Text_John_6_70::
    .string "Jesus answered them, Have not I\n"
    .string "chosen you twelve, and one of you is\l"
    .string "a devil?"
Bible_Text_John_6_71::
    .string "He spake of Judas Iscariot the son\n"
    .string "of Simon: for he it was that should\l"
    .string "betray him, being one of the twelve$"
Bible_Text_John_7_1::
    .string "After these things Jesus walked in\n"
    .string "Galilee: for he would not walk in\l"
    .string "Jewry, because the Jews sought to\l"
    .string "kill him.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_2::
    .string "Now the Jew’s feast of tabernacles\n"
    .string "was at hand.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_3::
    .string "His brethren therefore said unto\n"
    .string "him, Depart hence, and go into\l"
    .string "Judaea, that thy disciples also may\l"
    .string "see the works that thou doest.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_4::
    .string "For there is no man that doeth any\n"
    .string "thing in secret, and he himself\l"
    .string "seeketh to be known openly. If thou\l"
    .string "do these things, shew thyself to the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_5::
    .string "For neither did his brethren\n"
    .string "believe in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_6::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto them, My time\n"
    .string "is not yet come: but your time is\l"
    .string "alway ready.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_7::
    .string "The world cannot hate you; but me it\n"
    .string "hateth, because I testify of it, that\l"
    .string "the works thereof are evil.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_8::
    .string "Go ye up unto this feast: I go not\n"
    .string "up yet unto this feast: for my time\l"
    .string "is not yet full come.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_9::
    .string "When he had said these words unto\n"
    .string "them, he abode still in Galilee.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_10::
    .string "But when his brethren were gone up,\n"
    .string "then went he also up unto the feast,\l"
    .string "not openly, but as it were in secret.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_11::
    .string "Then the Jews sought him at the\n"
    .string "feast, and said, Where is he?"
Bible_Text_John_7_12::
    .string "And there was much murmuring among\n"
    .string "the people concerning him: for some\l"
    .string "said, He is a good man: others said,\l"
    .string "Nay; but he deceiveth the people$"
Bible_Text_John_7_13::
    .string "Howbeit no man spake openly of him\n"
    .string "for fear of the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_14::
    .string "Now about the midst of the feast\n"
    .string "Jesus went up into the temple, and\l"
    .string "taught.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_15::
    .string "And the Jews marvelled, saying,\n"
    .string "How knoweth this man letters, having\l"
    .string "never learned?"
Bible_Text_John_7_16::
    .string "Jesus answered them, and said, My\n"
    .string "doctrine is not mine, but his that\l"
    .string "sent me$"
Bible_Text_John_7_17::
    .string "If any man will do his will, he\n"
    .string "shall know of the doctrine, whether\l"
    .string "it be of God, or whether I speak of\l"
    .string "myself.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_18::
    .string "He that speaketh of himself\n"
    .string "seeketh his own glory: but he that\l"
    .string "seeketh his glory that sent him, the\l"
    .string "same is true, and no unrighteousness\l"
    .string "is in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_19::
    .string "Did not Moses give you the law, and\n"
    .string "yet none of you keepeth the law? Why\l"
    .string "go ye about to kill me?"
Bible_Text_John_7_20::
    .string "The people answered and said, Thou\n"
    .string "hast a devil: who goeth about to\l"
    .string "kill thee?"
Bible_Text_John_7_21::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them, I\n"
    .string "have done one work, and ye all\l"
    .string "marvel$"
Bible_Text_John_7_22::
    .string "Moses therefore gave unto you\n"
    .string "circumcision; (not because it is of\l"
    .string "Moses, but of the fathers;) and ye on\l"
    .string "the sabbath day circumcise a man.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_23::
    .string "If a man on the sabbath day receive\n"
    .string "circumcision, that the law of Moses\l"
    .string "should not be broken; are ye angry at\l"
    .string "me, because I have made a man every\l"
    .string "whit whole on the sabbath day?"
Bible_Text_John_7_24::
    .string "Judge not according to the\n"
    .string "appearance, but judge righteous\l"
    .string "judgment$"
Bible_Text_John_7_25::
    .string "Then said some of them of\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, Is not this he, whom they\l"
    .string "seek to kill?"
Bible_Text_John_7_26::
    .string "But, lo, he speaketh boldly, and\n"
    .string "they say nothing unto him. Do the\l"
    .string "rulers know indeed that this is the\l"
    .string "very Christ?"
Bible_Text_John_7_27::
    .string "Howbeit we know this man whence he\n"
    .string "is: but when Christ cometh, no man\l"
    .string "knoweth whence he is$"
Bible_Text_John_7_28::
    .string "Then cried Jesus in the temple as\n"
    .string "he taught, saying, Ye both know me,\l"
    .string "and ye know whence I am: and I am not\l"
    .string "come of myself, but he that sent me\l"
    .string "is true, whom ye know not.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_29::
    .string "But I know him: for I am from him,\n"
    .string "and he hath sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_30::
    .string "Then they sought to take him: but no\n"
    .string "man laid hands on him, because his\l"
    .string "hour was not yet come.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_31::
    .string "And many of the people believed\n"
    .string "on him, and said, When Christ cometh,\l"
    .string "will he do more miracles than these\l"
    .string "which this man hath done?"
Bible_Text_John_7_32::
    .string "The Pharisees heard that the\n"
    .string "people murmured such things\l"
    .string "concerning him; and the Pharisees and\l"
    .string "the chief priests sent officers to\l"
    .string "take him$"
Bible_Text_John_7_33::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them, Yet a\n"
    .string "little while am I with you, and then\l"
    .string "I go unto him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_34::
    .string "Ye shall seek me, and shall not\n"
    .string "find me: and where I am, thither ye\l"
    .string "cannot come.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_35::
    .string "Then said the Jews among\n"
    .string "themselves, Whither will he go,\l"
    .string "that we shall not find him? will he\l"
    .string "go unto the dispersed among the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, and teach the Gentiles?"
Bible_Text_John_7_36::
    .string "What manner of saying is this that\n"
    .string "he said, Ye shall seek me, and\l"
    .string "shall not find me: and where I am,\l"
    .string "thither ye cannot come?"
Bible_Text_John_7_37::
    .string "In the last day, that great day of\n"
    .string "the feast, Jesus stood and cried,\l"
    .string "saying, If any man thirst, let him\l"
    .string "come unto me, and drink$"
Bible_Text_John_7_38::
    .string "He that believeth on me, as the\n"
    .string "scripture hath said, out of his\l"
    .string "belly shall flow rivers of\l"
    .string "living water.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_39::
    .string "(But this spake he of the Spirit,\n"
    .string "which they that believe on him\l"
    .string "should receive: for the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "was not yet given; because that Jesus\l"
    .string "was not yet glorified.)"
Bible_Text_John_7_40::
    .string "Many of the people therefore, when\n"
    .string "they heard this saying, said, Of a\l"
    .string "truth this is the Prophet$"
Bible_Text_John_7_41::
    .string "Others said, This is the Christ. But\n"
    .string "some said, Shall Christ come out of\l"
    .string "Galilee?"
Bible_Text_John_7_42::
    .string "Hath not the scripture said, That\n"
    .string "Christ cometh of the seed of David,\l"
    .string "and out of the town of Bethlehem,\l"
    .string "where David was?"
Bible_Text_John_7_43::
    .string "So there was a division among the\n"
    .string "people because of him$"
Bible_Text_John_7_44::
    .string "And some of them would have taken\n"
    .string "him; but no man laid hands on him.$"
Bible_Text_John_7_45::
    .string "Then came the officers to the chief\n"
    .string "priests and Pharisees; and they said\l"
    .string "unto them, Why have ye not brought\l"
    .string "him?"
Bible_Text_John_7_46::
    .string "The officers answered, Never man\n"
    .string "spake like this man$"
Bible_Text_John_7_47::
    .string "Then answered them the Pharisees,\n"
    .string "Are ye also deceived?"
Bible_Text_John_7_48::
    .string "Have any of the rulers or of the\n"
    .string "Pharisees believed on him?"
Bible_Text_John_7_49::
    .string "But this people who knoweth not\n"
    .string "the law are cursed$"
Bible_Text_John_7_50::
    .string "Nicodemus saith unto them, (he that\n"
    .string "came to Jesus by night, being one of\l"
    .string "them,)"
Bible_Text_John_7_51::
    .string "Doth our law judge any man, before\n"
    .string "it hear him, and know what he doeth?"
Bible_Text_John_7_52::
    .string "They answered and said unto him, Art\n"
    .string "thou also of Galilee? Search, and\l"
    .string "look: for out of Galilee ariseth no\l"
    .string "prophet$"
Bible_Text_John_7_53::
    .string "And every man went unto his own\n"
    .string "house.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_1::
    .string "Jesus went unto the mount of Olives.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_2::
    .string "And early in the morning he came\n"
    .string "again into the temple, and all the\l"
    .string "people came unto him; and he sat\l"
    .string "down, and taught them.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_3::
    .string "And the scribes and Pharisees\n"
    .string "brought unto him a woman taken in\l"
    .string "adultery; and when they had set her\l"
    .string "in the midst,"
Bible_Text_John_8_4::
    .string "They say unto him, Master, this\n"
    .string "woman was taken in adultery, in the\l"
    .string "very act$"
Bible_Text_John_8_5::
    .string "Now Moses in the law commanded us,\n"
    .string "that such should be stoned: but what\l"
    .string "sayest thou?"
Bible_Text_John_8_6::
    .string "This they said, tempting him, that\n"
    .string "they might have to accuse him. But\l"
    .string "Jesus stooped down, and with his\l"
    .string "finger wrote on the ground, as though\l"
    .string "he heard them not$"
Bible_Text_John_8_7::
    .string "So when they continued asking him,\n"
    .string "he lifted up himself, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, He that is without sin among\l"
    .string "you, let him first cast a stone at\l"
    .string "her.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_8::
    .string "And again he stooped down, and\n"
    .string "wrote on the ground.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_9::
    .string "And they which heard it, being\n"
    .string "convicted by their own conscience,\l"
    .string "went out one by one, beginning at the\l"
    .string "eldest, even unto the last: and\l"
    .string "Jesus was left alone, and the woman\l"
    .string "standing in the midst.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_10::
    .string "When Jesus had lifted up himself,\n"
    .string "and saw none but the woman, he said\l"
    .string "unto her, Woman, where are those\l"
    .string "thine accusers? hath no man condemned\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_John_8_11::
    .string "She said, No man, Lord. And Jesus\n"
    .string "said unto her, Neither do I condemn\l"
    .string "thee: go, and sin no more$"
Bible_Text_John_8_12::
    .string "Then spake Jesus again unto them,\n"
    .string "saying, I am the light of the world:\l"
    .string "he that followeth me shall not\l"
    .string "walk in darkness, but shall have\l"
    .string "the light of life.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_13::
    .string "The Pharisees therefore said unto\n"
    .string "him, Thou bearest record of thyself;\l"
    .string "thy record is not true.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_14::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Though I bear record of myself, yet\l"
    .string "my record is true: for I know whence I\l"
    .string "came, and whither I go; but ye cannot\l"
    .string "tell whence I come, and whither I go.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_15::
    .string "Ye judge after the flesh; I judge no\n"
    .string "man.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_16::
    .string "And yet if I judge, my judgment is\n"
    .string "true: for I am not alone, but I and\l"
    .string "the Father that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_17::
    .string "It is also written in your law,\n"
    .string "that the testimony of two men is true.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_18::
    .string "I am one that bear witness of\n"
    .string "myself, and the Father that sent me\l"
    .string "beareth witness of me.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_19::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Where is\n"
    .string "thy Father? Jesus answered, Ye\l"
    .string "neither know me, nor my Father: if ye\l"
    .string "had known me, ye should have known my\l"
    .string "Father also.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_20::
    .string "These words spake Jesus in the\n"
    .string "treasury, as he taught in the\l"
    .string "temple: and no man laid hands on\l"
    .string "him; for his hour was not yet come.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_21::
    .string "Then said Jesus again unto them, I\n"
    .string "go my way, and ye shall seek me, and\l"
    .string "shall die in your sins: whither I\l"
    .string "go, ye cannot come.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_22::
    .string "Then said the Jews, Will he kill\n"
    .string "himself? because he saith, Whither I\l"
    .string "go, ye cannot come.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_23::
    .string "And he said unto them, Ye are from\n"
    .string "beneath; I am from above: ye are of\l"
    .string "this world; I am not of this world.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_24::
    .string "I said therefore unto you, that ye\n"
    .string "shall die in your sins: for if ye\l"
    .string "believe not that I am he, ye shall\l"
    .string "die in your sins.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_25::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Who art\n"
    .string "thou? And Jesus saith unto them, Even\l"
    .string "the same that I said unto you from\l"
    .string "the beginning.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_26::
    .string "I have many things to say and to\n"
    .string "judge of you: but he that sent me is\l"
    .string "true; and I speak to the world those\l"
    .string "things which I have heard of him.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_27::
    .string "They understood not that he spake\n"
    .string "to them of the Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_28::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them, When ye\n"
    .string "have lifted up the Son of man, then\l"
    .string "shall ye know that I am he, and that\l"
    .string "I do nothing of myself; but as my\l"
    .string "Father hath taught me, I speak these\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_29::
    .string "And he that sent me is with me: the\n"
    .string "Father hath not left me alone; for I\l"
    .string "do always those things that please\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_30::
    .string "As he spake these words, many\n"
    .string "believed on him.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_31::
    .string "Then said Jesus to those Jews which\n"
    .string "believed on him, If ye continue in my\l"
    .string "word, then are ye my disciples\l"
    .string "indeed;"
Bible_Text_John_8_32::
    .string "And ye shall know the truth, and\n"
    .string "the truth shall make you free$"
Bible_Text_John_8_33::
    .string "They answered him, We be Abraham’s\n"
    .string "seed, and were never in bondage to\l"
    .string "any man: how sayest thou, Ye shall\l"
    .string "be made free?"
Bible_Text_John_8_34::
    .string "Jesus answered them, Verily,\n"
    .string "verily, I say unto you, Whosoever\l"
    .string "committeth sin is the servant of sin$"
Bible_Text_John_8_35::
    .string "And the servant abideth not in the\n"
    .string "house for ever: but the Son abideth\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_36::
    .string "If the Son therefore shall make\n"
    .string "you free, ye shall be free indeed.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_37::
    .string "I know that ye are Abraham’s seed;\n"
    .string "but ye seek to kill me, because my\l"
    .string "word hath no place in you.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_38::
    .string "I speak that which I have seen with\n"
    .string "my Father: and ye do that which ye\l"
    .string "have seen with your father.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_39::
    .string "They answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Abraham is our father. Jesus saith\l"
    .string "unto them, If ye were Abraham’s\l"
    .string "children, ye would do the works of\l"
    .string "Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_40::
    .string "But now ye seek to kill me, a man\n"
    .string "that hath told you the truth, which I\l"
    .string "have heard of God: this did not\l"
    .string "Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_41::
    .string "Ye do the deeds of your father. Then\n"
    .string "said they to him, We be not born of\l"
    .string "fornication; we have one Father, even\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_42::
    .string "Jesus said unto them, If God were\n"
    .string "your Father, ye would love me: for I\l"
    .string "proceeded forth and came from God;\l"
    .string "neither came I of myself, but he sent\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_43::
    .string "Why do ye not understand my speech?\n"
    .string "even because ye cannot hear my word.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_44::
    .string "Ye are of your father the devil, and\n"
    .string "the lusts of your father ye will\l"
    .string "do. He was a murderer from the\l"
    .string "beginning, and abode not in the\l"
    .string "truth, because there is no truth in\l"
    .string "him. When he speaketh a lie, he\l"
    .string "speaketh of his own: for he is a\l"
    .string "liar, and the father of it.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_45::
    .string "And because I tell you the truth,\n"
    .string "ye believe me not.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_46::
    .string "Which of you convinceth me of sin?\n"
    .string "And if I say the truth, why do ye not\l"
    .string "believe me?"
Bible_Text_John_8_47::
    .string "He that is of God heareth God’s\n"
    .string "words: ye therefore hear them not,\l"
    .string "because ye are not of God$"
Bible_Text_John_8_48::
    .string "Then answered the Jews, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Say we not well that thou\l"
    .string "art a Samaritan, and hast a devil?"
Bible_Text_John_8_49::
    .string "Jesus answered, I have not a devil;\n"
    .string "but I honour my Father, and ye do\l"
    .string "dishonour me$"
Bible_Text_John_8_50::
    .string "And I seek not mine own glory: there\n"
    .string "is one that seeketh and judgeth.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_51::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, If\n"
    .string "a man keep my saying, he shall\l"
    .string "never see death.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_52::
    .string "Then said the Jews unto him, Now we\n"
    .string "know that thou hast a devil. Abraham\l"
    .string "is dead, and the prophets; and thou\l"
    .string "sayest, If a man keep my saying, he\l"
    .string "shall never taste of death.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_53::
    .string "Art thou greater than our father\n"
    .string "Abraham, which is dead? and the\l"
    .string "prophets are dead: whom makest thou\l"
    .string "thyself?"
Bible_Text_John_8_54::
    .string "Jesus answered, If I honour myself,\n"
    .string "my honour is nothing: it is my Father\l"
    .string "that honoureth me; of whom ye say,\l"
    .string "that he is your God:"
Bible_Text_John_8_55::
    .string "Yet ye have not known him; but I know\n"
    .string "him: and if I should say, I know him\l"
    .string "not, I shall be a liar like unto\l"
    .string "you: but I know him, and keep his\l"
    .string "saying$"
Bible_Text_John_8_56::
    .string "Your father Abraham rejoiced to see\n"
    .string "my day: and he saw it, and was glad.$"
Bible_Text_John_8_57::
    .string "Then said the Jews unto him, Thou\n"
    .string "art not yet fifty years old, and hast\l"
    .string "thou seen Abraham?"
Bible_Text_John_8_58::
    .string "Jesus said unto them, Verily,\n"
    .string "verily, I say unto you, Before\l"
    .string "Abraham was, I am$"
Bible_Text_John_8_59::
    .string "Then took they up stones to cast at\n"
    .string "him: but Jesus hid himself, and went\l"
    .string "out of the temple, going through the\l"
    .string "midst of them, and so passed by.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_1::
    .string "And as Jesus passed by, he saw a man\n"
    .string "which was blind from his birth.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_2::
    .string "And his disciples asked him,\n"
    .string "saying, Master, who did sin, this\l"
    .string "man, or his parents, that he was born\l"
    .string "blind?"
Bible_Text_John_9_3::
    .string "Jesus answered, Neither hath this\n"
    .string "man sinned, nor his parents: but\l"
    .string "that the works of God should be made\l"
    .string "manifest in him$"
Bible_Text_John_9_4::
    .string "I must work the works of him that\n"
    .string "sent me, while it is day: the night\l"
    .string "cometh, when no man can work.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_5::
    .string "As long as I am in the world, I am\n"
    .string "the light of the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_6::
    .string "When he had thus spoken, he spat on\n"
    .string "the ground, and made clay of the\l"
    .string "spittle, and he anointed the eyes of\l"
    .string "the blind man with the clay,"
Bible_Text_John_9_7::
    .string "And said unto him, Go, wash in the\n"
    .string "pool of Siloam, (which is by\l"
    .string "interpretation, Sent.) He went his\l"
    .string "way therefore, and washed, and came\l"
    .string "seeing$"
Bible_Text_John_9_8::
    .string "The neighbours therefore, and they\n"
    .string "which before had seen him that he was\l"
    .string "blind, said, Is not this he that sat\l"
    .string "and begged?"
Bible_Text_John_9_9::
    .string "Some said, This is he: others said,\n"
    .string "He is like him: but he said, I am he$"
Bible_Text_John_9_10::
    .string "Therefore said they unto him, How\n"
    .string "were thine eyes opened?"
Bible_Text_John_9_11::
    .string "He answered and said, A man that is\n"
    .string "called Jesus made clay, and\l"
    .string "anointed mine eyes, and said unto me,\l"
    .string "Go to the pool of Siloam, and wash:\l"
    .string "and I went and washed, and I received\l"
    .string "sight$"
Bible_Text_John_9_12::
    .string "Then said they unto him, Where is\n"
    .string "he? He said, I know not.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_13::
    .string "They brought to the Pharisees him\n"
    .string "that aforetime was blind.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_14::
    .string "And it was the sabbath day when\n"
    .string "Jesus made the clay, and opened his\l"
    .string "eyes.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_15::
    .string "Then again the Pharisees also asked\n"
    .string "him how he had received his sight. He\l"
    .string "said unto them, He put clay upon\l"
    .string "mine eyes, and I washed, and do see.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_16::
    .string "Therefore said some of the\n"
    .string "Pharisees, This man is not of God,\l"
    .string "because he keepeth not the sabbath\l"
    .string "day. Others said, How can a man that\l"
    .string "is a sinner do such miracles? And\l"
    .string "there was a division among them.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_17::
    .string "They say unto the blind man again,\n"
    .string "What sayest thou of him, that he hath\l"
    .string "opened thine eyes? He said, He is a\l"
    .string "prophet.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_18::
    .string "But the Jews did not believe\n"
    .string "concerning him, that he had been\l"
    .string "blind, and received his sight,\l"
    .string "until they called the parents of\l"
    .string "him that had received his sight.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_19::
    .string "And they asked them, saying, Is this\n"
    .string "your son, who ye say was born blind?\l"
    .string "how then doth he now see?"
Bible_Text_John_9_20::
    .string "His parents answered them and said,\n"
    .string "We know that this is our son, and that\l"
    .string "he was born blind:"
Bible_Text_John_9_21::
    .string "But by what means he now seeth, we\n"
    .string "know not; or who hath opened his\l"
    .string "eyes, we know not: he is of age; ask\l"
    .string "him: he shall speak for himself$"
Bible_Text_John_9_22::
    .string "These words spake his parents,\n"
    .string "because they feared the Jews: for the\l"
    .string "Jews had agreed already, that if any\l"
    .string "man did confess that he was Christ,\l"
    .string "he should be put out of the\l"
    .string "synagogue.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_23::
    .string "Therefore said his parents, He is\n"
    .string "of age; ask him.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_24::
    .string "Then again called they the man\n"
    .string "that was blind, and said unto him,\l"
    .string "Give God the praise: we know that\l"
    .string "this man is a sinner.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_25::
    .string "He answered and said, Whether he be\n"
    .string "a sinner or no, I know not: one thing\l"
    .string "I know, that, whereas I was blind,\l"
    .string "now I see.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_26::
    .string "Then said they to him again, What\n"
    .string "did he to thee? how opened he thine\l"
    .string "eyes?"
Bible_Text_John_9_27::
    .string "He answered them, I have told you\n"
    .string "already, and ye did not hear:\l"
    .string "wherefore would ye hear it again?\l"
    .string "will ye also be his disciples?"
Bible_Text_John_9_28::
    .string "Then they reviled him, and said,\n"
    .string "Thou art his disciple; but we are\l"
    .string "Moses’ disciples$"
Bible_Text_John_9_29::
    .string "We know that God spake unto Moses:\n"
    .string "as for this fellow, we know not from\l"
    .string "whence he is.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_30::
    .string "The man answered and said unto them,\n"
    .string "Why herein is a marvellous thing,\l"
    .string "that ye know not from whence he is,\l"
    .string "and yet he hath opened mine eyes.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_31::
    .string "Now we know that God heareth not\n"
    .string "sinners: but if any man be a\l"
    .string "worshipper of God, and doeth his\l"
    .string "will, him he heareth.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_32::
    .string "Since the world began was it not\n"
    .string "heard that any man opened the eyes\l"
    .string "of one that was born blind.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_33::
    .string "If this man were not of God, he\n"
    .string "could do nothing.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_34::
    .string "They answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "Thou wast altogether born in sins,\l"
    .string "and dost thou teach us? And they cast\l"
    .string "him out.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_35::
    .string "Jesus heard that they had cast him\n"
    .string "out; and when he had found him, he\l"
    .string "said unto him, Dost thou believe on\l"
    .string "the Son of God?"
Bible_Text_John_9_36::
    .string "He answered and said, Who is he,\n"
    .string "Lord, that I might believe on him?"
Bible_Text_John_9_37::
    .string "And Jesus said unto him, Thou hast\n"
    .string "both seen him, and it is he that\l"
    .string "talketh with thee$"
Bible_Text_John_9_38::
    .string "And he said, Lord, I believe. And he\n"
    .string "worshipped him.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_39::
    .string "And Jesus said, For judgment I am\n"
    .string "come into this world, that they\l"
    .string "which see not might see; and that\l"
    .string "they which see might be made blind.$"
Bible_Text_John_9_40::
    .string "And some of the Pharisees which were\n"
    .string "with him heard these words, and said\l"
    .string "unto him, Are we blind also?"
Bible_Text_John_9_41::
    .string "Jesus said unto them, If ye were\n"
    .string "blind, ye should have no sin: but\l"
    .string "now ye say, We see; therefore your\l"
    .string "sin remaineth$"
Bible_Text_John_10_1::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, He\n"
    .string "that entereth not by the door into\l"
    .string "the sheepfold, but climbeth up\l"
    .string "some other way, the same is a thief\l"
    .string "and a robber.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_2::
    .string "But he that entereth in by the door\n"
    .string "is the shepherd of the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_3::
    .string "To him the porter openeth; and the\n"
    .string "sheep hear his voice: and he\l"
    .string "calleth his own sheep by name, and\l"
    .string "leadeth them out.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_4::
    .string "And when he putteth forth his own\n"
    .string "sheep, he goeth before them, and the\l"
    .string "sheep follow him: for they know his\l"
    .string "voice.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_5::
    .string "And a stranger will they not\n"
    .string "follow, but will flee from him:\l"
    .string "for they know not the voice of\l"
    .string "strangers.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_6::
    .string "This parable spake Jesus unto\n"
    .string "them: but they understood not what\l"
    .string "things they were which he spake unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_7::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them again,\n"
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, I am\l"
    .string "the door of the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_8::
    .string "All that ever came before me are\n"
    .string "thieves and robbers: but the sheep\l"
    .string "did not hear them.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_9::
    .string "I am the door: by me if any man enter\n"
    .string "in, he shall be saved, and shall go\l"
    .string "in and out, and find pasture.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_10::
    .string "The thief cometh not, but for to\n"
    .string "steal, and to kill, and to destroy:\l"
    .string "I am come that they might have life,\l"
    .string "and that they might have it more\l"
    .string "abundantly.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_11::
    .string "I am the good shepherd: the good\n"
    .string "shepherd giveth his life for the\l"
    .string "sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_12::
    .string "But he that is an hireling, and not\n"
    .string "the shepherd, whose own the sheep\l"
    .string "are not, seeth the wolf coming, and\l"
    .string "leaveth the sheep, and fleeth: and\l"
    .string "the wolf catcheth them, and\l"
    .string "scattereth the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_13::
    .string "The hireling fleeth, because he is\n"
    .string "an hireling, and careth not for the\l"
    .string "sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_14::
    .string "I am the good shepherd, and know my\n"
    .string "sheep, and am known of mine.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_15::
    .string "As the Father knoweth me, even so\n"
    .string "know I the Father: and I lay down my\l"
    .string "life for the sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_16::
    .string "And other sheep I have, which are\n"
    .string "not of this fold: them also I must\l"
    .string "bring, and they shall hear my voice;\l"
    .string "and there shall be one fold, and\l"
    .string "one shepherd.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_17::
    .string "Therefore doth my Father love me,\n"
    .string "because I lay down my life, that I\l"
    .string "might take it again.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_18::
    .string "No man taketh it from me, but I lay\n"
    .string "it down of myself. I have power to\l"
    .string "lay it down, and I have power to take\l"
    .string "it again. This commandment have I\l"
    .string "received of my Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_19::
    .string "There was a division therefore\n"
    .string "again among the Jews for these\l"
    .string "sayings.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_20::
    .string "And many of them said, He hath a\n"
    .string "devil, and is mad; why hear ye him?"
Bible_Text_John_10_21::
    .string "Others said, These are not the words\n"
    .string "of him that hath a devil. Can a\l"
    .string "devil open the eyes of the blind?"
Bible_Text_John_10_22::
    .string "And it was at Jerusalem the feast\n"
    .string "of the dedication, and it was winter$"
Bible_Text_John_10_23::
    .string "And Jesus walked in the temple in\n"
    .string "Solomon’s porch.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_24::
    .string "Then came the Jews round about him,\n"
    .string "and said unto him, How long dost thou\l"
    .string "make us to doubt? If thou be the\l"
    .string "Christ, tell us plainly.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_25::
    .string "Jesus answered them, I told you,\n"
    .string "and ye believed not: the works that I\l"
    .string "do in my Father’s name, they bear\l"
    .string "witness of me.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_26::
    .string "But ye believe not, because ye are\n"
    .string "not of my sheep, as I said unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_27::
    .string "My sheep hear my voice, and I know\n"
    .string "them, and they follow me:"
Bible_Text_John_10_28::
    .string "And I give unto them eternal life;\n"
    .string "and they shall never perish,\l"
    .string "neither shall any man pluck them\l"
    .string "out of my hand$"
Bible_Text_John_10_29::
    .string "My Father, which gave them me, is\n"
    .string "greater than all; and no man is\l"
    .string "able to pluck them out of my\l"
    .string "Father’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_30::
    .string "I and my Father are one.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_31::
    .string "Then the Jews took up stones again\n"
    .string "to stone him.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_32::
    .string "Jesus answered them, Many good works\n"
    .string "have I shewed you from my Father; for\l"
    .string "which of those works do ye stone me?"
Bible_Text_John_10_33::
    .string "The Jews answered him, saying, For a\n"
    .string "good work we stone thee not; but for\l"
    .string "blasphemy; and because that thou,\l"
    .string "being a man, makest thyself God$"
Bible_Text_John_10_34::
    .string "Jesus answered them, Is it not\n"
    .string "written in your law, I said, Ye are\l"
    .string "gods?"
Bible_Text_John_10_35::
    .string "If he called them gods, unto whom\n"
    .string "the word of God came, and the\l"
    .string "scripture cannot be broken;"
Bible_Text_John_10_36::
    .string "Say ye of him, whom the Father hath\n"
    .string "sanctified, and sent into the world,\l"
    .string "Thou blasphemest; because I said, I\l"
    .string "am the Son of God?"
Bible_Text_John_10_37::
    .string "If I do not the works of my Father,\n"
    .string "believe me not$"
Bible_Text_John_10_38::
    .string "But if I do, though ye believe not\n"
    .string "me, believe the works: that ye may\l"
    .string "know, and believe, that the Father\l"
    .string "is in me, and I in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_39::
    .string "Therefore they sought again to take\n"
    .string "him: but he escaped out of their\l"
    .string "hand,"
Bible_Text_John_10_40::
    .string "And went away again beyond Jordan\n"
    .string "into the place where John at first\l"
    .string "baptized; and there he abode$"
Bible_Text_John_10_41::
    .string "And many resorted unto him, and\n"
    .string "said, John did no miracle: but all\l"
    .string "things that John spake of this man\l"
    .string "were true.$"
Bible_Text_John_10_42::
    .string "And many believed on him there.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_1::
    .string "Now a certain man was sick, named\n"
    .string "Lazarus, of Bethany, the town of Mary\l"
    .string "and her sister Martha.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_2::
    .string "(It was that Mary which anointed the\n"
    .string "Lord with ointment, and wiped his\l"
    .string "feet with her hair, whose brother\l"
    .string "Lazarus was sick.)"
Bible_Text_John_11_3::
    .string "Therefore his sisters sent unto him,\n"
    .string "saying, Lord, behold, he whom thou\l"
    .string "lovest is sick$"
Bible_Text_John_11_4::
    .string "When Jesus heard that, he said, This\n"
    .string "sickness is not unto death, but for\l"
    .string "the glory of God, that the Son of God\l"
    .string "might be glorified thereby.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_5::
    .string "Now Jesus loved Martha, and her\n"
    .string "sister, and Lazarus.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_6::
    .string "When he had heard therefore that he\n"
    .string "was sick, he abode two days still in\l"
    .string "the same place where he was.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_7::
    .string "Then after that saith he to his\n"
    .string "disciples, Let us go into Judaea\l"
    .string "again.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_8::
    .string "His disciples say unto him,\n"
    .string "Master, the Jews of late sought to\l"
    .string "stone thee; and goest thou thither\l"
    .string "again?"
Bible_Text_John_11_9::
    .string "Jesus answered, Are there not\n"
    .string "twelve hours in the day? If any man\l"
    .string "walk in the day, he stumbleth not,\l"
    .string "because he seeth the light of this\l"
    .string "world$"
Bible_Text_John_11_10::
    .string "But if a man walk in the night, he\n"
    .string "stumbleth, because there is no\l"
    .string "light in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_11::
    .string "These things said he: and after that\n"
    .string "he saith unto them, Our friend\l"
    .string "Lazarus sleepeth; but I go, that I\l"
    .string "may awake him out of sleep.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_12::
    .string "Then said his disciples, Lord, if\n"
    .string "he sleep, he shall do well.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_13::
    .string "Howbeit Jesus spake of his death:\n"
    .string "but they thought that he had spoken\l"
    .string "of taking of rest in sleep.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_14::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto them plainly,\n"
    .string "Lazarus is dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_15::
    .string "And I am glad for your sakes that I\n"
    .string "was not there, to the intent ye may\l"
    .string "believe; nevertheless let us go\l"
    .string "unto him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_16::
    .string "Then said Thomas, which is called\n"
    .string "Didymus, unto his fellow\l"
    .string "disciples, Let us also go, that we\l"
    .string "may die with him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_17::
    .string "Then when Jesus came, he found that\n"
    .string "he had lain in the grave four days\l"
    .string "already.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_18::
    .string "Now Bethany was nigh unto\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, about fifteen furlongs\l"
    .string "off:"
Bible_Text_John_11_19::
    .string "And many of the Jews came to Martha\n"
    .string "and Mary, to comfort them concerning\l"
    .string "their brother$"
Bible_Text_John_11_20::
    .string "Then Martha, as soon as she heard\n"
    .string "that Jesus was coming, went and met\l"
    .string "him: but Mary sat still in the house.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_21::
    .string "Then said Martha unto Jesus, Lord,\n"
    .string "if thou hadst been here, my brother\l"
    .string "had not died.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_22::
    .string "But I know, that even now,\n"
    .string "whatsoever thou wilt ask of God, God\l"
    .string "will give it thee.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_23::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Thy brother\n"
    .string "shall rise again.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_24::
    .string "Martha saith unto him, I know that\n"
    .string "he shall rise again in the\l"
    .string "resurrection at the last day.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_25::
    .string "Jesus said unto her, I am the\n"
    .string "resurrection, and the life: he that\l"
    .string "believeth in me, though he were\l"
    .string "dead, yet shall he live:"
Bible_Text_John_11_26::
    .string "And whosoever liveth and believeth\n"
    .string "in me shall never die. Believest\l"
    .string "thou this?"
Bible_Text_John_11_27::
    .string "She saith unto him, Yea, Lord: I\n"
    .string "believe that thou art the Christ,\l"
    .string "the Son of God, which should come\l"
    .string "into the world$"
Bible_Text_John_11_28::
    .string "And when she had so said, she went\n"
    .string "her way, and called Mary her sister\l"
    .string "secretly, saying, The Master is\l"
    .string "come, and calleth for thee.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_29::
    .string "As soon as she heard that, she arose\n"
    .string "quickly, and came unto him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_30::
    .string "Now Jesus was not yet come into the\n"
    .string "town, but was in that place where\l"
    .string "Martha met him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_31::
    .string "The Jews then which were with her in\n"
    .string "the house, and comforted her, when\l"
    .string "they saw Mary, that she rose up\l"
    .string "hastily and went out, followed her,\l"
    .string "saying, She goeth unto the grave to\l"
    .string "weep there.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_32::
    .string "Then when Mary was come where Jesus\n"
    .string "was, and saw him, she fell down at\l"
    .string "his feet, saying unto him, Lord, if\l"
    .string "thou hadst been here, my brother had\l"
    .string "not died.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_33::
    .string "When Jesus therefore saw her\n"
    .string "weeping, and the Jews also weeping\l"
    .string "which came with her, he groaned in\l"
    .string "the spirit, and was troubled.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_34::
    .string "And said, Where have ye laid him?\n"
    .string "They said unto him, Lord, come and\l"
    .string "see.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_35::
    .string "Jesus wept.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_36::
    .string "Then said the Jews, Behold how he\n"
    .string "loved him!"
Bible_Text_John_11_37::
    .string "And some of them said, Could not\n"
    .string "this man, which opened the eyes of\l"
    .string "the blind, have caused that even\l"
    .string "this man should not have died?"
Bible_Text_John_11_38::
    .string "Jesus therefore again groaning in\n"
    .string "himself cometh to the grave. It was a\l"
    .string "cave, and a stone lay upon it$"
Bible_Text_John_11_39::
    .string "Jesus said, Take ye away the stone.\n"
    .string "Martha, the sister of him that was\l"
    .string "dead, saith unto him, Lord, by this\l"
    .string "time he stinketh: for he hath been\l"
    .string "dead four days.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_40::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Said I not\n"
    .string "unto thee, that, if thou wouldest\l"
    .string "believe, thou shouldest see the\l"
    .string "glory of God?"
Bible_Text_John_11_41::
    .string "Then they took away the stone from\n"
    .string "the place where the dead was laid.\l"
    .string "And Jesus lifted up his eyes, and\l"
    .string "said, Father, I thank thee that thou\l"
    .string "hast heard me$"
Bible_Text_John_11_42::
    .string "And I knew that thou hearest me\n"
    .string "always: but because of the people\l"
    .string "which stand by I said it, that they\l"
    .string "may believe that thou hast sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_43::
    .string "And when he thus had spoken, he\n"
    .string "cried with a loud voice, Lazarus,\l"
    .string "come forth.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_44::
    .string "And he that was dead came forth,\n"
    .string "bound hand and foot with\l"
    .string "graveclothes: and his face was bound\l"
    .string "about with a napkin. Jesus saith\l"
    .string "unto them, Loose him, and let him go.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_45::
    .string "Then many of the Jews which came to\n"
    .string "Mary, and had seen the things which\l"
    .string "Jesus did, believed on him.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_46::
    .string "But some of them went their ways to\n"
    .string "the Pharisees, and told them what\l"
    .string "things Jesus had done.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_47::
    .string "Then gathered the chief priests and\n"
    .string "the Pharisees a council, and said,\l"
    .string "What do we? for this man doeth many\l"
    .string "miracles.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_48::
    .string "If we let him thus alone, all men\n"
    .string "will believe on him: and the Romans\l"
    .string "shall come and take away both our\l"
    .string "place and nation.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_49::
    .string "And one of them, named Caiaphas,\n"
    .string "being the high priest that same\l"
    .string "year, said unto them, Ye know nothing\l"
    .string "at all,"
Bible_Text_John_11_50::
    .string "Nor consider that it is expedient\n"
    .string "for us, that one man should die for\l"
    .string "the people, and that the whole\l"
    .string "nation perish not$"
Bible_Text_John_11_51::
    .string "And this spake he not of himself:\n"
    .string "but being high priest that year, he\l"
    .string "prophesied that Jesus should die\l"
    .string "for that nation;"
Bible_Text_John_11_52::
    .string "And not for that nation only, but\n"
    .string "that also he should gather together\l"
    .string "in one the children of God that were\l"
    .string "scattered abroad$"
Bible_Text_John_11_53::
    .string "Then from that day forth they took\n"
    .string "counsel together for to put him to\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_54::
    .string "Jesus therefore walked no more\n"
    .string "openly among the Jews; but went\l"
    .string "thence unto a country near to the\l"
    .string "wilderness, into a city called\l"
    .string "Ephraim, and there continued with\l"
    .string "his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_55::
    .string "And the Jews’ passover was nigh at\n"
    .string "hand: and many went out of the\l"
    .string "country up to Jerusalem before the\l"
    .string "passover, to purify themselves.$"
Bible_Text_John_11_56::
    .string "Then sought they for Jesus, and\n"
    .string "spake among themselves, as they\l"
    .string "stood in the temple, What think ye,\l"
    .string "that he will not come to the feast?"
Bible_Text_John_11_57::
    .string "Now both the chief priests and the\n"
    .string "Pharisees had given a commandment,\l"
    .string "that, if any man knew where he were,\l"
    .string "he should shew it, that they might\l"
    .string "take him$"
Bible_Text_John_12_1::
    .string "Then Jesus six days before the\n"
    .string "passover came to Bethany, where\l"
    .string "Lazarus was, which had been dead,\l"
    .string "whom he raised from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_2::
    .string "There they made him a supper; and\n"
    .string "Martha served: but Lazarus was one of\l"
    .string "them that sat at the table with him.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_3::
    .string "Then took Mary a pound of ointment\n"
    .string "of spikenard, very costly, and\l"
    .string "anointed the feet of Jesus, and\l"
    .string "wiped his feet with her hair: and the\l"
    .string "house was filled with the odour of\l"
    .string "the ointment.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_4::
    .string "Then saith one of his disciples,\n"
    .string "Judas Iscariot, Simon’s son, which\l"
    .string "should betray him,"
Bible_Text_John_12_5::
    .string "Why was not this ointment sold for\n"
    .string "three hundred pence, and given to\l"
    .string "the poor?"
Bible_Text_John_12_6::
    .string "This he said, not that he cared for\n"
    .string "the poor; but because he was a thief,\l"
    .string "and had the bag, and bare what was\l"
    .string "put therein$"
Bible_Text_John_12_7::
    .string "Then said Jesus, Let her alone:\n"
    .string "against the day of my burying hath\l"
    .string "she kept this.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_8::
    .string "For the poor always ye have with\n"
    .string "you; but me ye have not always.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_9::
    .string "Much people of the Jews therefore\n"
    .string "knew that he was there: and they came\l"
    .string "not for Jesus’ sake only, but that\l"
    .string "they might see Lazarus also, whom he\l"
    .string "had raised from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_10::
    .string "But the chief priests consulted\n"
    .string "that they might put Lazarus also to\l"
    .string "death;"
Bible_Text_John_12_11::
    .string "Because that by reason of him many\n"
    .string "of the Jews went away, and believed\l"
    .string "on Jesus$"
Bible_Text_John_12_12::
    .string "On the next day much people that\n"
    .string "were come to the feast, when they\l"
    .string "heard that Jesus was coming to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem,"
Bible_Text_John_12_13::
    .string "Took branches of palm trees, and\n"
    .string "went forth to meet him, and cried,\l"
    .string "Hosanna: Blessed is the King of\l"
    .string "Israel that cometh in the name of\l"
    .string "the Lord$"
Bible_Text_John_12_14::
    .string "And Jesus, when he had found a young\n"
    .string "ass, sat thereon; as it is written,"
Bible_Text_John_12_15::
    .string "Fear not, daughter of Sion: behold,\n"
    .string "thy King cometh, sitting on an ass’s\l"
    .string "colt$"
Bible_Text_John_12_16::
    .string "These things understood not his\n"
    .string "disciples at the first: but when\l"
    .string "Jesus was glorified, then remembered\l"
    .string "they that these things were written\l"
    .string "of him, and that they had done these\l"
    .string "things unto him.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_17::
    .string "The people therefore that was\n"
    .string "with him when he called Lazarus out\l"
    .string "of his grave, and raised him from the\l"
    .string "dead, bare record.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_18::
    .string "For this cause the people also\n"
    .string "met him, for that they heard that he\l"
    .string "had done this miracle.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_19::
    .string "The Pharisees therefore said among\n"
    .string "themselves, Perceive ye how ye\l"
    .string "prevail nothing? behold, the world\l"
    .string "is gone after him.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_20::
    .string "And there were certain Greeks among\n"
    .string "them that came up to worship at the\l"
    .string "feast:"
Bible_Text_John_12_21::
    .string "The same came therefore to Philip,\n"
    .string "which was of Bethsaida of Galilee,\l"
    .string "and desired him, saying, Sir, we\l"
    .string "would see Jesus$"
Bible_Text_John_12_22::
    .string "Philip cometh and telleth Andrew:\n"
    .string "and again Andrew and Philip tell\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_23::
    .string "And Jesus answered them, saying, The\n"
    .string "hour is come, that the Son of man\l"
    .string "should be glorified.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_24::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you,\n"
    .string "Except a corn of wheat fall into\l"
    .string "the ground and die, it abideth\l"
    .string "alone: but if it die, it bringeth\l"
    .string "forth much fruit.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_25::
    .string "He that loveth his life shall\n"
    .string "lose it; and he that hateth his life\l"
    .string "in this world shall keep it unto\l"
    .string "life eternal.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_26::
    .string "If any man serve me, let him\n"
    .string "follow me; and where I am, there\l"
    .string "shall also my servant be: if any\l"
    .string "man serve me, him will my Father\l"
    .string "honour.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_27::
    .string "Now is my soul troubled; and what\n"
    .string "shall I say? Father, save me from\l"
    .string "this hour: but for this cause came I\l"
    .string "unto this hour.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_28::
    .string "Father, glorify thy name. Then came\n"
    .string "there a voice from heaven, saying, I\l"
    .string "have both glorified it, and will\l"
    .string "glorify it again.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_29::
    .string "The people therefore, that stood\n"
    .string "by, and heard it, said that it\l"
    .string "thundered: others said, An angel\l"
    .string "spake to him.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_30::
    .string "Jesus answered and said, This voice\n"
    .string "came not because of me, but for your\l"
    .string "sakes.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_31::
    .string "Now is the judgment of this world:\n"
    .string "now shall the prince of this world\l"
    .string "be cast out.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_32::
    .string "And I, if I be lifted up from the\n"
    .string "earth, will draw all men unto me.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_33::
    .string "This he said, signifying what death\n"
    .string "he should die.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_34::
    .string "The people answered him, We have\n"
    .string "heard out of the law that Christ\l"
    .string "abideth for ever: and how sayest\l"
    .string "thou, The Son of man must be lifted\l"
    .string "up? who is this Son of man?"
Bible_Text_John_12_35::
    .string "Then Jesus said unto them, Yet a\n"
    .string "little while is the light with you\l"
    .string "Walk while ye have the light, lest\l"
    .string "darkness come upon you: for he that\l"
    .string "walketh in darkness knoweth not\l"
    .string "whither he goeth.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_36::
    .string "While ye have light, believe in\n"
    .string "the light, that ye may be the\l"
    .string "children of light. These things\l"
    .string "spake Jesus, and departed, and did\l"
    .string "hide himself from them.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_37::
    .string "But though he had done so many\n"
    .string "miracles before them, yet they\l"
    .string "believed not on him:"
Bible_Text_John_12_38::
    .string "That the saying of Esaias the\n"
    .string "prophet might be fulfilled, which\l"
    .string "he spake, Lord, who hath believed\l"
    .string "our report? and to whom hath the arm\l"
    .string "of the Lord been revealed?"
Bible_Text_John_12_39::
    .string "Therefore they could not believe,\n"
    .string "because that Esaias said again,"
Bible_Text_John_12_40::
    .string "He hath blinded their eyes, and\n"
    .string "hardened their heart; that they\l"
    .string "should not see with their eyes, nor\l"
    .string "understand with their heart, and be\l"
    .string "converted, and I should heal them$"
Bible_Text_John_12_41::
    .string "These things said Esaias, when he\n"
    .string "saw his glory, and spake of him.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_42::
    .string "Nevertheless among the chief\n"
    .string "rulers also many believed on him;\l"
    .string "but because of the Pharisees they did\l"
    .string "not confess him, lest they should be\l"
    .string "put out of the synagogue:"
Bible_Text_John_12_43::
    .string "For they loved the praise of men\n"
    .string "more than the praise of God$"
Bible_Text_John_12_44::
    .string "Jesus cried and said, He that\n"
    .string "believeth on me, believeth not on\l"
    .string "me, but on him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_45::
    .string "And he that seeth me seeth him that\n"
    .string "sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_46::
    .string "I am come a light into the world,\n"
    .string "that whosoever believeth on me\l"
    .string "should not abide in darkness.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_47::
    .string "And if any man hear my words, and\n"
    .string "believe not, I judge him not: for I\l"
    .string "came not to judge the world, but to\l"
    .string "save the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_48::
    .string "He that rejecteth me, and receiveth\n"
    .string "not my words, hath one that judgeth\l"
    .string "him: the word that I have spoken, the\l"
    .string "same shall judge him in the last\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_49::
    .string "For I have not spoken of myself;\n"
    .string "but the Father which sent me, he gave\l"
    .string "me a commandment, what I should say,\l"
    .string "and what I should speak.$"
Bible_Text_John_12_50::
    .string "And I know that his commandment is\n"
    .string "life everlasting: whatsoever I\l"
    .string "speak therefore, even as the Father\l"
    .string "said unto me, so I speak.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_1::
    .string "Now before the feast of the\n"
    .string "passover, when Jesus knew that his\l"
    .string "hour was come that he should depart\l"
    .string "out of this world unto the Father,\l"
    .string "having loved his own which were in\l"
    .string "the world, he loved them unto the\l"
    .string "end.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_2::
    .string "And supper being ended, the devil\n"
    .string "having now put into the heart of\l"
    .string "Judas Iscariot, Simon’s son, to\l"
    .string "betray him;"
Bible_Text_John_13_3::
    .string "Jesus knowing that the Father had\n"
    .string "given all things into his hands, and\l"
    .string "that he was come from God, and went to\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_John_13_4::
    .string "He riseth from supper, and laid\n"
    .string "aside his garments; and took a\l"
    .string "towel, and girded himself$"
Bible_Text_John_13_5::
    .string "After that he poureth water into a\n"
    .string "bason, and began to wash the\l"
    .string "disciples’ feet, and to wipe them\l"
    .string "with the towel wherewith he was\l"
    .string "girded.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_6::
    .string "Then cometh he to Simon Peter: and\n"
    .string "Peter saith unto him, Lord, dost thou\l"
    .string "wash my feet?"
Bible_Text_John_13_7::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto him,\n"
    .string "What I do thou knowest not now; but\l"
    .string "thou shalt know hereafter$"
Bible_Text_John_13_8::
    .string "Peter saith unto him, Thou shalt\n"
    .string "never wash my feet. Jesus answered\l"
    .string "him, If I wash thee not, thou hast no\l"
    .string "part with me.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_9::
    .string "Simon Peter saith unto him, Lord,\n"
    .string "not my feet only, but also my hands\l"
    .string "and my head.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_10::
    .string "Jesus saith to him, He that is\n"
    .string "washed needeth not save to wash his\l"
    .string "feet, but is clean every whit: and ye\l"
    .string "are clean, but not all.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_11::
    .string "For he knew who should betray him;\n"
    .string "therefore said he, Ye are not all\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_12::
    .string "So after he had washed their feet,\n"
    .string "and had taken his garments, and was\l"
    .string "set down again, he said unto them,\l"
    .string "Know ye what I have done to you?"
Bible_Text_John_13_13::
    .string "Ye call me Master and Lord: and ye\n"
    .string "say well; for so I am$"
Bible_Text_John_13_14::
    .string "If I then, your Lord and Master,\n"
    .string "have washed your feet; ye also ought\l"
    .string "to wash one another’s feet.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_15::
    .string "For I have given you an example,\n"
    .string "that ye should do as I have done to\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_16::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, The\n"
    .string "servant is not greater than his\l"
    .string "lord; neither he that is sent greater\l"
    .string "than he that sent him.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_17::
    .string "If ye know these things, happy are\n"
    .string "ye if ye do them.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_18::
    .string "I speak not of you all: I know whom\n"
    .string "I have chosen: but that the\l"
    .string "scripture may be fulfilled, He\l"
    .string "that eateth bread with me hath\l"
    .string "lifted up his heel against me.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_19::
    .string "Now I tell you before it come,\n"
    .string "that, when it is come to pass, ye may\l"
    .string "believe that I am he.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_20::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, He\n"
    .string "that receiveth whomsoever I send\l"
    .string "receiveth me; and he that receiveth\l"
    .string "me receiveth him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_21::
    .string "When Jesus had thus said, he was\n"
    .string "troubled in spirit, and testified,\l"
    .string "and said, Verily, verily, I say unto\l"
    .string "you, that one of you shall betray me.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_22::
    .string "Then the disciples looked one on\n"
    .string "another, doubting of whom he spake.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_23::
    .string "Now there was leaning on Jesus’\n"
    .string "bosom one of his disciples, whom\l"
    .string "Jesus loved.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_24::
    .string "Simon Peter therefore beckoned to\n"
    .string "him, that he should ask who it\l"
    .string "should be of whom he spake.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_25::
    .string "He then lying on Jesus’ breast\n"
    .string "saith unto him, Lord, who is it?"
Bible_Text_John_13_26::
    .string "Jesus answered, He it is, to whom I\n"
    .string "shall give a sop, when I have\l"
    .string "dipped it. And when he had dipped\l"
    .string "the sop, he gave it to Judas\l"
    .string "Iscariot, the son of Simon$"
Bible_Text_John_13_27::
    .string "And after the sop Satan entered\n"
    .string "into him. Then said Jesus unto him,\l"
    .string "That thou doest, do quickly.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_28::
    .string "Now no man at the table knew for\n"
    .string "what intent he spake this unto him.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_29::
    .string "For some of them thought, because\n"
    .string "Judas had the bag, that Jesus had\l"
    .string "said unto him, Buy those things that\l"
    .string "we have need of against the feast;\l"
    .string "or, that he should give something to\l"
    .string "the poor.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_30::
    .string "He then having received the sop\n"
    .string "went immediately out: and it was\l"
    .string "night.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_31::
    .string "Therefore, when he was gone out,\n"
    .string "Jesus said, Now is the Son of man\l"
    .string "glorified, and God is glorified in\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_32::
    .string "If God be glorified in him, God\n"
    .string "shall also glorify him in\l"
    .string "himself, and shall straightway\l"
    .string "glorify him.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_33::
    .string "Little children, yet a little\n"
    .string "while I am with you. Ye shall seek\l"
    .string "me: and as I said unto the Jews,\l"
    .string "Whither I go, ye cannot come; so now I\l"
    .string "say to you.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_34::
    .string "A new commandment I give unto you,\n"
    .string "That ye love one another; as I have\l"
    .string "loved you, that ye also love one\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_35::
    .string "By this shall all men know that\n"
    .string "ye are my disciples, if ye have\l"
    .string "love one to another.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_36::
    .string "Simon Peter said unto him, Lord,\n"
    .string "whither goest thou? Jesus answered\l"
    .string "him, Whither I go, thou canst not\l"
    .string "follow me now; but thou shalt\l"
    .string "follow me afterwards.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_37::
    .string "Peter said unto him, Lord, why\n"
    .string "cannot I follow thee now? I will\l"
    .string "lay down my life for thy sake.$"
Bible_Text_John_13_38::
    .string "Jesus answered him, Wilt thou lay\n"
    .string "down thy life for my sake? Verily,\l"
    .string "verily, I say unto thee, The cock\l"
    .string "shall not crow, till thou hast\l"
    .string "denied me thrice.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_1::
    .string "Let not your heart be troubled: ye\n"
    .string "believe in God, believe also in me.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_2::
    .string "In my Father’s house are many\n"
    .string "mansions: if it were not so, I would\l"
    .string "have told you. I go to prepare a\l"
    .string "place for you.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_3::
    .string "And if I go and prepare a place\n"
    .string "for you, I will come again, and\l"
    .string "receive you unto myself; that where\l"
    .string "I am, there ye may be also.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_4::
    .string "And whither I go ye know, and the way\n"
    .string "ye know.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_5::
    .string "Thomas saith unto him, Lord, we know\n"
    .string "not whither thou goest; and how can\l"
    .string "we know the way?"
Bible_Text_John_14_6::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, I am the way,\n"
    .string "the truth, and the life: no man\l"
    .string "cometh unto the Father, but by me$"
Bible_Text_John_14_7::
    .string "If ye had known me, ye should have\n"
    .string "known my Father also: and from\l"
    .string "henceforth ye know him, and have seen\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_8::
    .string "Philip saith unto him, Lord, shew\n"
    .string "us the Father, and it sufficeth us.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_9::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, Have I been so\n"
    .string "long time with you, and yet hast thou\l"
    .string "not known me, Philip? he that hath\l"
    .string "seen me hath seen the Father; and how\l"
    .string "sayest thou then, Shew us the Father?"
Bible_Text_John_14_10::
    .string "Believest thou not that I am in the\n"
    .string "Father, and the Father in me? the\l"
    .string "words that I speak unto you I speak\l"
    .string "not of myself: but the Father that\l"
    .string "dwelleth in me, he doeth the works$"
Bible_Text_John_14_11::
    .string "Believe me that I am in the Father,\n"
    .string "and the Father in me: or else\l"
    .string "believe me for the very works’ sake.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_12::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you, He\n"
    .string "that believeth on me, the works that\l"
    .string "I do shall he do also; and greater\l"
    .string "works than these shall he do;\l"
    .string "because I go unto my Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_13::
    .string "And whatsoever ye shall ask in my\n"
    .string "name, that will I do, that the\l"
    .string "Father may be glorified in the Son.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_14::
    .string "If ye shall ask any thing in my\n"
    .string "name, I will do it.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_15::
    .string "If ye love me, keep my\n"
    .string "commandments.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_16::
    .string "And I will pray the Father, and he\n"
    .string "shall give you another Comforter,\l"
    .string "that he may abide with you for ever;"
Bible_Text_John_14_17::
    .string "Even the Spirit of truth; whom the\n"
    .string "world cannot receive, because it\l"
    .string "seeth him not, neither knoweth him:\l"
    .string "but ye know him; for he dwelleth\l"
    .string "with you, and shall be in you$"
Bible_Text_John_14_18::
    .string "I will not leave you comfortless:\n"
    .string "I will come to you.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_19::
    .string "Yet a little while, and the world\n"
    .string "seeth me no more; but ye see me:\l"
    .string "because I live, ye shall live\l"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_20::
    .string "At that day ye shall know that I am\n"
    .string "in my Father, and ye in me, and I in\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_21::
    .string "He that hath my commandments, and\n"
    .string "keepeth them, he it is that loveth\l"
    .string "me: and he that loveth me shall be\l"
    .string "loved of my Father, and I will love\l"
    .string "him, and will manifest myself to\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_22::
    .string "Judas saith unto him, not Iscariot,\n"
    .string "Lord, how is it that thou wilt\l"
    .string "manifest thyself unto us, and not\l"
    .string "unto the world?"
Bible_Text_John_14_23::
    .string "Jesus answered and said unto him, If\n"
    .string "a man love me, he will keep my\l"
    .string "words: and my Father will love him,\l"
    .string "and we will come unto him, and make\l"
    .string "our abode with him$"
Bible_Text_John_14_24::
    .string "He that loveth me not keepeth not\n"
    .string "my sayings: and the word which ye\l"
    .string "hear is not mine, but the Father’s\l"
    .string "which sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_25::
    .string "These things have I spoken unto\n"
    .string "you, being yet present with you.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_26::
    .string "But the Comforter, which is the\n"
    .string "Holy Ghost, whom the Father will\l"
    .string "send in my name, he shall teach you\l"
    .string "all things, and bring all things\l"
    .string "to your remembrance, whatsoever I\l"
    .string "have said unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_27::
    .string "Peace I leave with you, my peace I\n"
    .string "give unto you: not as the world\l"
    .string "giveth, give I unto you. Let not your\l"
    .string "heart be troubled, neither let it be\l"
    .string "afraid.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_28::
    .string "Ye have heard how I said unto you, I\n"
    .string "go away, and come again unto you. If\l"
    .string "ye loved me, ye would rejoice,\l"
    .string "because I said, I go unto the Father:\l"
    .string "for my Father is greater than I.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_29::
    .string "And now I have told you before it\n"
    .string "come to pass, that, when it is come\l"
    .string "to pass, ye might believe.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_30::
    .string "Hereafter I will not talk much\n"
    .string "with you: for the prince of this\l"
    .string "world cometh, and hath nothing in me.$"
Bible_Text_John_14_31::
    .string "But that the world may know that I\n"
    .string "love the Father; and as the Father\l"
    .string "gave me commandment, even so I do.\l"
    .string "Arise, let us go hence.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_1::
    .string "I am the true vine, and my Father is\n"
    .string "the husbandman.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_2::
    .string "Every branch in me that beareth not\n"
    .string "fruit he taketh away: and every\l"
    .string "branch that beareth fruit, he\l"
    .string "purgeth it, that it may bring forth\l"
    .string "more fruit.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_3::
    .string "Now ye are clean through the word\n"
    .string "which I have spoken unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_4::
    .string "Abide in me, and I in you. As the\n"
    .string "branch cannot bear fruit of itself,\l"
    .string "except it abide in the vine; no more\l"
    .string "can ye, except ye abide in me.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_5::
    .string "I am the vine, ye are the branches:\n"
    .string "He that abideth in me, and I in him,\l"
    .string "the same bringeth forth much fruit:\l"
    .string "for without me ye can do nothing.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_6::
    .string "If a man abide not in me, he is cast\n"
    .string "forth as a branch, and is withered;\l"
    .string "and men gather them, and cast them\l"
    .string "into the fire, and they are burned.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_7::
    .string "If ye abide in me, and my words abide\n"
    .string "in you, ye shall ask what ye will,\l"
    .string "and it shall be done unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_8::
    .string "Herein is my Father glorified, that\n"
    .string "ye bear much fruit; so shall ye be\l"
    .string "my disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_9::
    .string "As the Father hath loved me, so have\n"
    .string "I loved you: continue ye in my love.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_10::
    .string "If ye keep my commandments, ye\n"
    .string "shall abide in my love; even as I\l"
    .string "have kept my Father’s commandments,\l"
    .string "and abide in his love.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_11::
    .string "These things have I spoken unto\n"
    .string "you, that my joy might remain in you,\l"
    .string "and that your joy might be full.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_12::
    .string "This is my commandment, That ye\n"
    .string "love one another, as I have loved\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_13::
    .string "Greater love hath no man than this,\n"
    .string "that a man lay down his life for his\l"
    .string "friends.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_14::
    .string "Ye are my friends, if ye do\n"
    .string "whatsoever I command you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_15::
    .string "Henceforth I call you not\n"
    .string "servants; for the servant knoweth not\l"
    .string "what his lord doeth: but I have\l"
    .string "called you friends; for all things\l"
    .string "that I have heard of my Father I have\l"
    .string "made known unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_16::
    .string "Ye have not chosen me, but I have\n"
    .string "chosen you, and ordained you, that ye\l"
    .string "should go and bring forth fruit, and\l"
    .string "that your fruit should remain: that\l"
    .string "whatsoever ye shall ask of the\l"
    .string "Father in my name, he may give it you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_17::
    .string "These things I command you, that ye\n"
    .string "love one another.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_18::
    .string "If the world hate you, ye know that\n"
    .string "it hated me before it hated you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_19::
    .string "If ye were of the world, the world\n"
    .string "would love his own: but because ye\l"
    .string "are not of the world, but I have\l"
    .string "chosen you out of the world,\l"
    .string "therefore the world hateth you.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_20::
    .string "Remember the word that I said unto\n"
    .string "you, The servant is not greater than\l"
    .string "his lord. If they have persecuted\l"
    .string "me, they will also persecute you;\l"
    .string "if they have kept my saying, they\l"
    .string "will keep yours also.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_21::
    .string "But all these things will they do\n"
    .string "unto you for my name’s sake, because\l"
    .string "they know not him that sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_22::
    .string "If I had not come and spoken unto\n"
    .string "them, they had not had sin: but now\l"
    .string "they have no cloak for their sin.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_23::
    .string "He that hateth me hateth my Father\n"
    .string "also.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_24::
    .string "If I had not done among them the\n"
    .string "works which none other man did, they\l"
    .string "had not had sin: but now have they\l"
    .string "both seen and hated both me and my\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_25::
    .string "But this cometh to pass, that the\n"
    .string "word might be fulfilled that is\l"
    .string "written in their law, They hated me\l"
    .string "without a cause.$"
Bible_Text_John_15_26::
    .string "But when the Comforter is come, whom\n"
    .string "I will send unto you from the\l"
    .string "Father, even the Spirit of truth,\l"
    .string "which proceedeth from the Father, he\l"
    .string "shall testify of me:"
Bible_Text_John_15_27::
    .string "And ye also shall bear witness,\n"
    .string "because ye have been with me from the\l"
    .string "beginning$"
Bible_Text_John_16_1::
    .string "These things have I spoken unto\n"
    .string "you, that ye should not be offended.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_2::
    .string "They shall put you out of the\n"
    .string "synagogues: yea, the time cometh,\l"
    .string "that whosoever killeth you will\l"
    .string "think that he doeth God service.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_3::
    .string "And these things will they do unto\n"
    .string "you, because they have not known the\l"
    .string "Father, nor me.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_4::
    .string "But these things have I told you,\n"
    .string "that when the time shall come, ye\l"
    .string "may remember that I told you of them.\l"
    .string "And these things I said not unto you\l"
    .string "at the beginning, because I was with\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_5::
    .string "But now I go my way to him that sent\n"
    .string "me; and none of you asketh me,\l"
    .string "Whither goest thou?"
Bible_Text_John_16_6::
    .string "But because I have said these things\n"
    .string "unto you, sorrow hath filled your\l"
    .string "heart$"
Bible_Text_John_16_7::
    .string "Nevertheless I tell you the truth;\n"
    .string "It is expedient for you that I go\l"
    .string "away: for if I go not away, the\l"
    .string "Comforter will not come unto you;\l"
    .string "but if I depart, I will send him\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_8::
    .string "And when he is come, he will\n"
    .string "reprove the world of sin, and of\l"
    .string "righteousness, and of judgment:"
Bible_Text_John_16_9::
    .string "Of sin, because they believe not on\n"
    .string "me;"
Bible_Text_John_16_10::
    .string "Of righteousness, because I go to my\n"
    .string "Father, and ye see me no more;"
Bible_Text_John_16_11::
    .string "Of judgment, because the prince of\n"
    .string "this world is judged$"
Bible_Text_John_16_12::
    .string "I have yet many things to say unto\n"
    .string "you, but ye cannot bear them now.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_13::
    .string "Howbeit when he, the Spirit of\n"
    .string "truth, is come, he will guide you\l"
    .string "into all truth: for he shall not\l"
    .string "speak of himself; but whatsoever he\l"
    .string "shall hear, that shall he speak:\l"
    .string "and he will shew you things to come.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_14::
    .string "He shall glorify me: for he shall\n"
    .string "receive of mine, and shall shew it\l"
    .string "unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_15::
    .string "All things that the Father hath\n"
    .string "are mine: therefore said I, that he\l"
    .string "shall take of mine, and shall shew\l"
    .string "it unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_16::
    .string "A little while, and ye shall not\n"
    .string "see me: and again, a little while,\l"
    .string "and ye shall see me, because I go to\l"
    .string "the Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_17::
    .string "Then said some of his disciples\n"
    .string "among themselves, What is this that\l"
    .string "he saith unto us, A little while,\l"
    .string "and ye shall not see me: and again,\l"
    .string "a little while, and ye shall see\l"
    .string "me: and, Because I go to the Father?"
Bible_Text_John_16_18::
    .string "They said therefore, What is this\n"
    .string "that he saith, A little while? we\l"
    .string "cannot tell what he saith$"
Bible_Text_John_16_19::
    .string "Now Jesus knew that they were\n"
    .string "desirous to ask him, and said unto\l"
    .string "them, Do ye enquire among yourselves\l"
    .string "of that I said, A little while, and\l"
    .string "ye shall not see me: and again, a\l"
    .string "little while, and ye shall see me?"
Bible_Text_John_16_20::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto you,\n"
    .string "That ye shall weep and lament, but\l"
    .string "the world shall rejoice: and ye\l"
    .string "shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow\l"
    .string "shall be turned into joy$"
Bible_Text_John_16_21::
    .string "A woman when she is in travail hath\n"
    .string "sorrow, because her hour is come: but\l"
    .string "as soon as she is delivered of the\l"
    .string "child, she remembereth no more the\l"
    .string "anguish, for joy that a man is born\l"
    .string "into the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_22::
    .string "And ye now therefore have sorrow:\n"
    .string "but I will see you again, and your\l"
    .string "heart shall rejoice, and your joy no\l"
    .string "man taketh from you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_23::
    .string "And in that day ye shall ask me\n"
    .string "nothing. Verily, verily, I say unto\l"
    .string "you, Whatsoever ye shall ask the\l"
    .string "Father in my name, he will give it\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_24::
    .string "Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my\n"
    .string "name: ask, and ye shall receive,\l"
    .string "that your joy may be full.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_25::
    .string "These things have I spoken unto you\n"
    .string "in proverbs: but the time cometh,\l"
    .string "when I shall no more speak unto you\l"
    .string "in proverbs, but I shall shew you\l"
    .string "plainly of the Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_26::
    .string "At that day ye shall ask in my\n"
    .string "name: and I say not unto you, that I\l"
    .string "will pray the Father for you:"
Bible_Text_John_16_27::
    .string "For the Father himself loveth you,\n"
    .string "because ye have loved me, and have\l"
    .string "believed that I came out from God$"
Bible_Text_John_16_28::
    .string "I came forth from the Father, and am\n"
    .string "come into the world: again, I leave\l"
    .string "the world, and go to the Father.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_29::
    .string "His disciples said unto him, Lo,\n"
    .string "now speakest thou plainly, and\l"
    .string "speakest no proverb.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_30::
    .string "Now are we sure that thou knowest\n"
    .string "all things, and needest not that any\l"
    .string "man should ask thee: by this we\l"
    .string "believe that thou camest forth from\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_John_16_31::
    .string "Jesus answered them, Do ye now\n"
    .string "believe?"
Bible_Text_John_16_32::
    .string "Behold, the hour cometh, yea, is now\n"
    .string "come, that ye shall be scattered,\l"
    .string "every man to his own, and shall\l"
    .string "leave me alone: and yet I am not\l"
    .string "alone, because the Father is with me$"
Bible_Text_John_16_33::
    .string "These things I have spoken unto\n"
    .string "you, that in me ye might have peace.\l"
    .string "In the world ye shall have\l"
    .string "tribulation: but be of good cheer; I\l"
    .string "have overcome the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_1::
    .string "These words spake Jesus, and\n"
    .string "lifted up his eyes to heaven, and\l"
    .string "said, Father, the hour is come;\l"
    .string "glorify thy Son, that thy Son also\l"
    .string "may glorify thee:"
Bible_Text_John_17_2::
    .string "As thou hast given him power over\n"
    .string "all flesh, that he should give\l"
    .string "eternal life to as many as thou hast\l"
    .string "given him$"
Bible_Text_John_17_3::
    .string "And this is life eternal, that they\n"
    .string "might know thee the only true God,\l"
    .string "and Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_4::
    .string "I have glorified thee on the earth:\n"
    .string "I have finished the work which thou\l"
    .string "gavest me to do.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_5::
    .string "And now, O Father, glorify thou me\n"
    .string "with thine own self with the glory\l"
    .string "which I had with thee before the\l"
    .string "world was.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_6::
    .string "I have manifested thy name unto the\n"
    .string "men which thou gavest me out of the\l"
    .string "world: thine they were, and thou\l"
    .string "gavest them me; and they have kept\l"
    .string "thy word.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_7::
    .string "Now they have known that all\n"
    .string "things whatsoever thou hast given me\l"
    .string "are of thee.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_8::
    .string "For I have given unto them the words\n"
    .string "which thou gavest me; and they have\l"
    .string "received them, and have known surely\l"
    .string "that I came out from thee, and they\l"
    .string "have believed that thou didst send\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_9::
    .string "I pray for them: I pray not for the\n"
    .string "world, but for them which thou hast\l"
    .string "given me; for they are thine.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_10::
    .string "And all mine are thine, and thine\n"
    .string "are mine; and I am glorified in them.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_11::
    .string "And now I am no more in the world,\n"
    .string "but these are in the world, and I\l"
    .string "come to thee. Holy Father, keep\l"
    .string "through thine own name those whom\l"
    .string "thou hast given me, that they may be\l"
    .string "one, as we are.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_12::
    .string "While I was with them in the world,\n"
    .string "I kept them in thy name: those that\l"
    .string "thou gavest me I have kept, and none\l"
    .string "of them is lost, but the son of\l"
    .string "perdition; that the scripture might\l"
    .string "be fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_13::
    .string "And now come I to thee; and these\n"
    .string "things I speak in the world, that\l"
    .string "they might have my joy fulfilled in\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_14::
    .string "I have given them thy word; and the\n"
    .string "world hath hated them, because they\l"
    .string "are not of the world, even as I am\l"
    .string "not of the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_15::
    .string "I pray not that thou shouldest\n"
    .string "take them out of the world, but that\l"
    .string "thou shouldest keep them from the\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_16::
    .string "They are not of the world, even as I\n"
    .string "am not of the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_17::
    .string "Sanctify them through thy truth: thy\n"
    .string "word is truth.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_18::
    .string "As thou hast sent me into the world,\n"
    .string "even so have I also sent them into\l"
    .string "the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_19::
    .string "And for their sakes I sanctify\n"
    .string "myself, that they also might be\l"
    .string "sanctified through the truth.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_20::
    .string "Neither pray I for these alone, but\n"
    .string "for them also which shall believe\l"
    .string "on me through their word;"
Bible_Text_John_17_21::
    .string "That they all may be one; as thou,\n"
    .string "Father, art in me, and I in thee, that\l"
    .string "they also may be one in us: that the\l"
    .string "world may believe that thou hast\l"
    .string "sent me$"
Bible_Text_John_17_22::
    .string "And the glory which thou gavest me\n"
    .string "I have given them; that they may be\l"
    .string "one, even as we are one:"
Bible_Text_John_17_23::
    .string "I in them, and thou in me, that they\n"
    .string "may be made perfect in one; and that\l"
    .string "the world may know that thou hast\l"
    .string "sent me, and hast loved them, as thou\l"
    .string "hast loved me$"
Bible_Text_John_17_24::
    .string "Father, I will that they also,\n"
    .string "whom thou hast given me, be with me\l"
    .string "where I am; that they may behold my\l"
    .string "glory, which thou hast given me: for\l"
    .string "thou lovedst me before the\l"
    .string "foundation of the world.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_25::
    .string "O righteous Father, the world hath\n"
    .string "not known thee: but I have known\l"
    .string "thee, and these have known that thou\l"
    .string "hast sent me.$"
Bible_Text_John_17_26::
    .string "And I have declared unto them thy\n"
    .string "name, and will declare it: that the\l"
    .string "love wherewith thou hast loved me\l"
    .string "may be in them, and I in them.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_1::
    .string "When Jesus had spoken these words,\n"
    .string "he went forth with his disciples\l"
    .string "over the brook Cedron, where was a\l"
    .string "garden, into the which he entered,\l"
    .string "and his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_2::
    .string "And Judas also, which betrayed him,\n"
    .string "knew the place: for Jesus ofttimes\l"
    .string "resorted thither with his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_3::
    .string "Judas then, having received a band\n"
    .string "of men and officers from the chief\l"
    .string "priests and Pharisees, cometh\l"
    .string "thither with lanterns and torches\l"
    .string "and weapons.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_4::
    .string "Jesus therefore, knowing all\n"
    .string "things that should come upon him,\l"
    .string "went forth, and said unto them, Whom\l"
    .string "seek ye?"
Bible_Text_John_18_5::
    .string "They answered him, Jesus of Nazareth\n"
    .string " Jesus saith unto them, I am he And\l"
    .string "Judas also, which betrayed him,\l"
    .string "stood with them.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_6::
    .string "As soon then as he had said unto\n"
    .string "them, I am he, they went backward, and\l"
    .string "fell to the ground.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_7::
    .string "Then asked he them again, Whom seek\n"
    .string "ye? And they said, Jesus of Nazareth.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_8::
    .string "Jesus answered, I have told you\n"
    .string "that I am he: if therefore ye seek me,\l"
    .string "let these go their way:"
Bible_Text_John_18_9::
    .string "That the saying might be\n"
    .string "fulfilled, which he spake, Of them\l"
    .string "which thou gavest me have I lost none$"
Bible_Text_John_18_10::
    .string "Then Simon Peter having a sword drew\n"
    .string "it, and smote the high priest’s\l"
    .string "servant, and cut off his right ear.\l"
    .string "The servant’s name was Malchus.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_11::
    .string "Then said Jesus unto Peter, Put up\n"
    .string "thy sword into the sheath: the cup\l"
    .string "which my Father hath given me, shall\l"
    .string "I not drink it?"
Bible_Text_John_18_12::
    .string "Then the band and the captain and\n"
    .string "officers of the Jews took Jesus, and\l"
    .string "bound him,"
Bible_Text_John_18_13::
    .string "And led him away to Annas first; for\n"
    .string "he was father in law to Caiaphas,\l"
    .string "which was the high priest that same\l"
    .string "year$"
Bible_Text_John_18_14::
    .string "Now Caiaphas was he, which gave\n"
    .string "counsel to the Jews, that it was\l"
    .string "expedient that one man should die\l"
    .string "for the people.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_15::
    .string "And Simon Peter followed Jesus,\n"
    .string "and so did another disciple: that\l"
    .string "disciple was known unto the high\l"
    .string "priest, and went in with Jesus into\l"
    .string "the palace of the high priest.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_16::
    .string "But Peter stood at the door without.\n"
    .string "Then went out that other disciple,\l"
    .string "which was known unto the high\l"
    .string "priest, and spake unto her that kept\l"
    .string "the door, and brought in Peter.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_17::
    .string "Then saith the damsel that kept\n"
    .string "the door unto Peter, Art not thou\l"
    .string "also one of this man’s disciples?\l"
    .string "He saith, I am not.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_18::
    .string "And the servants and officers stood\n"
    .string "there, who had made a fire of coals;\l"
    .string "for it was cold: and they warmed\l"
    .string "themselves: and Peter stood with\l"
    .string "them, and warmed himself.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_19::
    .string "The high priest then asked Jesus of\n"
    .string "his disciples, and of his doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_20::
    .string "Jesus answered him, I spake openly\n"
    .string "to the world; I ever taught in the\l"
    .string "synagogue, and in the temple,\l"
    .string "whither the Jews always resort; and\l"
    .string "in secret have I said nothing.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_21::
    .string "Why askest thou me? ask them which\n"
    .string "heard me, what I have said unto them:\l"
    .string "behold, they know what I said.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_22::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, one of\n"
    .string "the officers which stood by struck\l"
    .string "Jesus with the palm of his hand,\l"
    .string "saying, Answerest thou the high\l"
    .string "priest so?"
Bible_Text_John_18_23::
    .string "Jesus answered him, If I have\n"
    .string "spoken evil, bear witness of the\l"
    .string "evil: but if well, why smitest thou\l"
    .string "me?"
Bible_Text_John_18_24::
    .string "Now Annas had sent him bound unto\n"
    .string "Caiaphas the high priest$"
Bible_Text_John_18_25::
    .string "And Simon Peter stood and warmed\n"
    .string "himself. They said therefore unto\l"
    .string "him, Art not thou also one of his\l"
    .string "disciples? He denied it, and said, I\l"
    .string "am not.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_26::
    .string "One of the servants of the high\n"
    .string "priest, being his kinsman whose ear\l"
    .string "Peter cut off, saith, Did not I see\l"
    .string "thee in the garden with him?"
Bible_Text_John_18_27::
    .string "Peter then denied again: and\n"
    .string "immediately the cock crew$"
Bible_Text_John_18_28::
    .string "Then led they Jesus from Caiaphas\n"
    .string "unto the hall of judgment: and it\l"
    .string "was early; and they themselves went\l"
    .string "not into the judgment hall, lest\l"
    .string "they should be defiled; but that\l"
    .string "they might eat the passover.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_29::
    .string "Pilate then went out unto them, and\n"
    .string "said, What accusation bring ye\l"
    .string "against this man?"
Bible_Text_John_18_30::
    .string "They answered and said unto him, If\n"
    .string "he were not a malefactor, we would\l"
    .string "not have delivered him up unto thee$"
Bible_Text_John_18_31::
    .string "Then said Pilate unto them, Take ye\n"
    .string "him, and judge him according to your\l"
    .string "law. The Jews therefore said unto\l"
    .string "him, It is not lawful for us to put\l"
    .string "any man to death:"
Bible_Text_John_18_32::
    .string "That the saying of Jesus might be\n"
    .string "fulfilled, which he spake,\l"
    .string "signifying what death he should die$"
Bible_Text_John_18_33::
    .string "Then Pilate entered into the\n"
    .string "judgment hall again, and called\l"
    .string "Jesus, and said unto him, Art thou\l"
    .string "the King of the Jews?"
Bible_Text_John_18_34::
    .string "Jesus answered him, Sayest thou this\n"
    .string "thing of thyself, or did others\l"
    .string "tell it thee of me?"
Bible_Text_John_18_35::
    .string "Pilate answered, Am I a Jew? Thine\n"
    .string "own nation and the chief priests\l"
    .string "have delivered thee unto me: what\l"
    .string "hast thou done?"
Bible_Text_John_18_36::
    .string "Jesus answered, My kingdom is not of\n"
    .string "this world: if my kingdom were of\l"
    .string "this world, then would my servants\l"
    .string "fight, that I should not be\l"
    .string "delivered to the Jews: but now is my\l"
    .string "kingdom not from hence$"
Bible_Text_John_18_37::
    .string "Pilate therefore said unto him, Art\n"
    .string "thou a king then? Jesus answered,\l"
    .string "Thou sayest that I am a king. To this\l"
    .string "end was I born, and for this cause\l"
    .string "came I into the world, that I should\l"
    .string "bear witness unto the truth. Every\l"
    .string "one that is of the truth heareth my\l"
    .string "voice.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_38::
    .string "Pilate saith unto him, What is\n"
    .string "truth? And when he had said this, he\l"
    .string "went out again unto the Jews, and\l"
    .string "saith unto them, I find in him no\l"
    .string "fault at all.$"
Bible_Text_John_18_39::
    .string "But ye have a custom, that I should\n"
    .string "release unto you one at the\l"
    .string "passover: will ye therefore that I\l"
    .string "release unto you the King of the\l"
    .string "Jews?"
Bible_Text_John_18_40::
    .string "Then cried they all again, saying,\n"
    .string "Not this man, but Barabbas. Now\l"
    .string "Barabbas was a robber$"
Bible_Text_John_19_1::
    .string "Then Pilate therefore took Jesus,\n"
    .string "and scourged him.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_2::
    .string "And the soldiers platted a crown\n"
    .string "of thorns, and put it on his head,\l"
    .string "and they put on him a purple robe,"
Bible_Text_John_19_3::
    .string "And said, Hail, King of the Jews!\n"
    .string "and they smote him with their hands$"
Bible_Text_John_19_4::
    .string "Pilate therefore went forth again,\n"
    .string "and saith unto them, Behold, I bring\l"
    .string "him forth to you, that ye may know\l"
    .string "that I find no fault in him.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_5::
    .string "Then came Jesus forth, wearing the\n"
    .string "crown of thorns, and the purple robe\l"
    .string " And Pilate saith unto them, Behold\l"
    .string "the man!"
Bible_Text_John_19_6::
    .string "When the chief priests therefore\n"
    .string "and officers saw him, they cried out,\l"
    .string "saying, Crucify him, crucify him.\l"
    .string "Pilate saith unto them, Take ye him,\l"
    .string "and crucify him: for I find no fault\l"
    .string "in him$"
Bible_Text_John_19_7::
    .string "The Jews answered him, We have a\n"
    .string "law, and by our law he ought to die,\l"
    .string "because he made himself the Son of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_8::
    .string "When Pilate therefore heard that\n"
    .string "saying, he was the more afraid;"
Bible_Text_John_19_9::
    .string "And went again into the judgment\n"
    .string "hall, and saith unto Jesus, Whence\l"
    .string "art thou? But Jesus gave him no answer$"
Bible_Text_John_19_10::
    .string "Then saith Pilate unto him,\n"
    .string "Speakest thou not unto me? knowest\l"
    .string "thou not that I have power to\l"
    .string "crucify thee, and have power to\l"
    .string "release thee?"
Bible_Text_John_19_11::
    .string "Jesus answered, Thou couldest have\n"
    .string "no power at all against me, except\l"
    .string "it were given thee from above:\l"
    .string "therefore he that delivered me unto\l"
    .string "thee hath the greater sin$"
Bible_Text_John_19_12::
    .string "And from thenceforth Pilate sought\n"
    .string "to release him: but the Jews cried\l"
    .string "out, saying, If thou let this man go,\l"
    .string "thou art not Caesar’s friend:\l"
    .string "whosoever maketh himself a king\l"
    .string "speaketh against Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_13::
    .string "When Pilate therefore heard that\n"
    .string "saying, he brought Jesus forth, and\l"
    .string "sat down in the judgment seat in a\l"
    .string "place that is called the Pavement,\l"
    .string "but in the Hebrew, Gabbatha.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_14::
    .string "And it was the preparation of the\n"
    .string "passover, and about the sixth hour:\l"
    .string "and he saith unto the Jews, Behold\l"
    .string "your King!"
Bible_Text_John_19_15::
    .string "But they cried out, Away with him,\n"
    .string "away with him, crucify him Pilate\l"
    .string "saith unto them, Shall I crucify\l"
    .string "your King? The chief priests\l"
    .string "answered, We have no king but Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_16::
    .string "Then delivered he him therefore\n"
    .string "unto them to be crucified. And they\l"
    .string "took Jesus, and led him away.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_17::
    .string "And he bearing his cross went forth\n"
    .string "into a place called the place of\l"
    .string "a skull, which is called in the\l"
    .string "Hebrew Golgotha:"
Bible_Text_John_19_18::
    .string "Where they crucified him, and two\n"
    .string "other with him, on either side one,\l"
    .string "and Jesus in the midst$"
Bible_Text_John_19_19::
    .string "And Pilate wrote a title, and put\n"
    .string "it on the cross. And the writing was\l"
    .string "JESUS OF NAZARETH THE KING OF THE\l"
    .string "JEWS.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_20::
    .string "This title then read many of the\n"
    .string "Jews: for the place where Jesus was\l"
    .string "crucified was nigh to the city: and\l"
    .string "it was written in Hebrew, and Greek,\l"
    .string "and Latin.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_21::
    .string "Then said the chief priests of the\n"
    .string "Jews to Pilate, Write not, The King\l"
    .string "of the Jews; but that he said, I am\l"
    .string "King of the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_22::
    .string "Pilate answered, What I have\n"
    .string "written I have written.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_23::
    .string "Then the soldiers, when they had\n"
    .string "crucified Jesus, took his garments,\l"
    .string "and made four parts, to every\l"
    .string "soldier a part; and also his coat:\l"
    .string "now the coat was without seam, woven\l"
    .string "from the top throughout.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_24::
    .string "They said therefore among\n"
    .string "themselves, Let us not rend it, but\l"
    .string "cast lots for it, whose it shall\l"
    .string "be: that the scripture might be\l"
    .string "fulfilled, which saith, They\l"
    .string "parted my raiment among them, and for\l"
    .string "my vesture they did cast lots. These\l"
    .string "things therefore the soldiers did.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_25::
    .string "Now there stood by the cross of\n"
    .string "Jesus his mother, and his mother’s\l"
    .string "sister, Mary the wife of Cleophas,\l"
    .string "and Mary Magdalene.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_26::
    .string "When Jesus therefore saw his mother,\n"
    .string "and the disciple standing by, whom\l"
    .string "he loved, he saith unto his mother,\l"
    .string "Woman, behold thy son!"
Bible_Text_John_19_27::
    .string "Then saith he to the disciple,\n"
    .string "Behold thy mother! And from that\l"
    .string "hour that disciple took her unto\l"
    .string "his own home$"
Bible_Text_John_19_28::
    .string "After this, Jesus knowing that all\n"
    .string "things were now accomplished, that\l"
    .string "the scripture might be fulfilled,\l"
    .string "saith, I thirst.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_29::
    .string "Now there was set a vessel full of\n"
    .string "vinegar: and they filled a spunge\l"
    .string "with vinegar, and put it upon\l"
    .string "hyssop, and put it to his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_30::
    .string "When Jesus therefore had received\n"
    .string "the vinegar, he said, It is finished:\l"
    .string "and he bowed his head, and gave up\l"
    .string "the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_31::
    .string "The Jews therefore, because it was\n"
    .string "the preparation, that the bodies\l"
    .string "should not remain upon the cross on\l"
    .string "the sabbath day, (for that sabbath\l"
    .string "day was an high day,) besought\l"
    .string "Pilate that their legs might be\l"
    .string "broken, and that they might be taken\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_32::
    .string "Then came the soldiers, and brake\n"
    .string "the legs of the first, and of the\l"
    .string "other which was crucified with him.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_33::
    .string "But when they came to Jesus, and saw\n"
    .string "that he was dead already, they brake\l"
    .string "not his legs:"
Bible_Text_John_19_34::
    .string "But one of the soldiers with a\n"
    .string "spear pierced his side, and\l"
    .string "forthwith came there out blood and\l"
    .string "water$"
Bible_Text_John_19_35::
    .string "And he that saw it bare record, and\n"
    .string "his record is true: and he knoweth\l"
    .string "that he saith true, that ye might\l"
    .string "believe.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_36::
    .string "For these things were done, that the\n"
    .string "scripture should be fulfilled, A\l"
    .string "bone of him shall not be broken.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_37::
    .string "And again another scripture saith,\n"
    .string "They shall look on him whom they\l"
    .string "pierced.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_38::
    .string "And after this Joseph of\n"
    .string "Arimathaea, being a disciple of\l"
    .string "Jesus, but secretly for fear of the\l"
    .string "Jews, besought Pilate that he might\l"
    .string "take away the body of Jesus: and\l"
    .string "Pilate gave him leave. He came\l"
    .string "therefore, and took the body of Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_39::
    .string "And there came also Nicodemus,\n"
    .string "which at the first came to Jesus by\l"
    .string "night, and brought a mixture of myrrh\l"
    .string "and aloes, about an hundred pound\l"
    .string "weight.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_40::
    .string "Then took they the body of Jesus,\n"
    .string "and wound it in linen clothes with\l"
    .string "the spices, as the manner of the Jews\l"
    .string "is to bury.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_41::
    .string "Now in the place where he was\n"
    .string "crucified there was a garden; and in\l"
    .string "the garden a new sepulchre, wherein\l"
    .string "was never man yet laid.$"
Bible_Text_John_19_42::
    .string "There laid they Jesus therefore\n"
    .string "because of the Jews’ preparation\l"
    .string "day; for the sepulchre was nigh at\l"
    .string "hand.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_1::
    .string "The first day of the week cometh\n"
    .string "Mary Magdalene early, when it was\l"
    .string "yet dark, unto the sepulchre, and\l"
    .string "seeth the stone taken away from the\l"
    .string "sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_2::
    .string "Then she runneth, and cometh to\n"
    .string "Simon Peter, and to the other\l"
    .string "disciple, whom Jesus loved, and\l"
    .string "saith unto them, They have taken away\l"
    .string "the LORD out of the sepulchre, and\l"
    .string "we know not where they have laid him.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_3::
    .string "Peter therefore went forth, and that\n"
    .string "other disciple, and came to the\l"
    .string "sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_4::
    .string "So they ran both together: and the\n"
    .string "other disciple did outrun Peter,\l"
    .string "and came first to the sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_5::
    .string "And he stooping down, and looking\n"
    .string "in, saw the linen clothes lying;\l"
    .string "yet went he not in.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_6::
    .string "Then cometh Simon Peter following\n"
    .string "him, and went into the sepulchre,\l"
    .string "and seeth the linen clothes lie,"
Bible_Text_John_20_7::
    .string "And the napkin, that was about his\n"
    .string "head, not lying with the linen\l"
    .string "clothes, but wrapped together in a\l"
    .string "place by itself$"
Bible_Text_John_20_8::
    .string "Then went in also that other\n"
    .string "disciple, which came first to the\l"
    .string "sepulchre, and he saw, and believed.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_9::
    .string "For as yet they knew not the\n"
    .string "scripture, that he must rise again\l"
    .string "from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_10::
    .string "Then the disciples went away again\n"
    .string "unto their own home.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_11::
    .string "But Mary stood without at the\n"
    .string "sepulchre weeping: and as she\l"
    .string "wept, she stooped down, and looked\l"
    .string "into the sepulchre,"
Bible_Text_John_20_12::
    .string "And seeth two angels in white\n"
    .string "sitting, the one at the head, and the\l"
    .string "other at the feet, where the body of\l"
    .string "Jesus had lain$"
Bible_Text_John_20_13::
    .string "And they say unto her, Woman, why\n"
    .string "weepest thou? She saith unto them,\l"
    .string "Because they have taken away my LORD,\l"
    .string "and I know not where they have laid\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_14::
    .string "And when she had thus said, she\n"
    .string "turned herself back, and saw Jesus\l"
    .string "standing, and knew not that it was\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_15::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Woman, why\n"
    .string "weepest thou? whom seekest thou?\l"
    .string "She, supposing him to be the\l"
    .string "gardener, saith unto him, Sir, if\l"
    .string "thou have borne him hence, tell me\l"
    .string "where thou hast laid him, and I\l"
    .string "will take him away.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_16::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Mary. She\n"
    .string "turned herself, and saith unto him,\l"
    .string "Rabboni; which is to say, Master.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_17::
    .string "Jesus saith unto her, Touch me not;\n"
    .string "for I am not yet ascended to my\l"
    .string "Father: but go to my brethren, and\l"
    .string "say unto them, I ascend unto my\l"
    .string "Father, and your Father; and to my\l"
    .string "God, and your God.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_18::
    .string "Mary Magdalene came and told the\n"
    .string "disciples that she had seen the\l"
    .string "LORD, and that he had spoken these\l"
    .string "things unto her.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_19::
    .string "Then the same day at evening, being\n"
    .string "the first day of the week, when the\l"
    .string "doors were shut where the disciples\l"
    .string "were assembled for fear of the Jews,\l"
    .string "came Jesus and stood in the midst,\l"
    .string "and saith unto them, Peace be unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_20::
    .string "And when he had so said, he shewed\n"
    .string "unto them his hands and his side.\l"
    .string "Then were the disciples glad, when\l"
    .string "they saw the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_21::
    .string "Then said Jesus to them again, Peace\n"
    .string "be unto you: as my Father hath sent\l"
    .string "me, even so send I you.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_22::
    .string "And when he had said this, he\n"
    .string "breathed on them, and saith unto\l"
    .string "them, Receive ye the Holy Ghost:"
Bible_Text_John_20_23::
    .string "Whose soever sins ye remit, they are\n"
    .string "remitted unto them; and whose soever\l"
    .string "sins ye retain, they are retained$"
Bible_Text_John_20_24::
    .string "But Thomas, one of the twelve,\n"
    .string "called Didymus, was not with them\l"
    .string "when Jesus came.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_25::
    .string "The other disciples therefore said\n"
    .string "unto him, We have seen the LORD. But\l"
    .string "he said unto them, Except I shall\l"
    .string "see in his hands the print of the\l"
    .string "nails, and put my finger into the\l"
    .string "print of the nails, and thrust my\l"
    .string "hand into his side, I will not\l"
    .string "believe.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_26::
    .string "And after eight days again his\n"
    .string "disciples were within, and Thomas\l"
    .string "with them: then came Jesus, the doors\l"
    .string "being shut, and stood in the midst,\l"
    .string "and said, Peace be unto you.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_27::
    .string "Then saith he to Thomas, Reach\n"
    .string "hither thy finger, and behold my\l"
    .string "hands; and reach hither thy hand, and\l"
    .string "thrust it into my side: and be not\l"
    .string "faithless, but believing.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_28::
    .string "And Thomas answered and said unto\n"
    .string "him, My LORD and my God.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_29::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, Thomas,\n"
    .string "because thou hast seen me, thou hast\l"
    .string "believed: blessed are they that\l"
    .string "have not seen, and yet have believed.$"
Bible_Text_John_20_30::
    .string "And many other signs truly did\n"
    .string "Jesus in the presence of his\l"
    .string "disciples, which are not written in\l"
    .string "this book:"
Bible_Text_John_20_31::
    .string "But these are written, that ye might\n"
    .string "believe that Jesus is the Christ,\l"
    .string "the Son of God; and that believing ye\l"
    .string "might have life through his name$"
Bible_Text_John_21_1::
    .string "After these things Jesus shewed\n"
    .string "himself again to the disciples at\l"
    .string "the sea of Tiberias; and on this wise\l"
    .string "shewed he himself.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_2::
    .string "There were together Simon Peter, and\n"
    .string "Thomas called Didymus, and\l"
    .string "Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, and\l"
    .string "the sons of Zebedee, and two other of\l"
    .string "his disciples.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_3::
    .string "Simon Peter saith unto them, I go a\n"
    .string "fishing. They say unto him, We also\l"
    .string "go with thee. They went forth, and\l"
    .string "entered into a ship immediately;\l"
    .string "and that night they caught nothing.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_4::
    .string "But when the morning was now come,\n"
    .string "Jesus stood on the shore: but the\l"
    .string "disciples knew not that it was\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_5::
    .string "Then Jesus saith unto them,\n"
    .string "Children, have ye any meat? They\l"
    .string "answered him, No.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_6::
    .string "And he said unto them, Cast the net\n"
    .string "on the right side of the ship, and ye\l"
    .string "shall find. They cast therefore,\l"
    .string "and now they were not able to draw it\l"
    .string "for the multitude of fishes.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_7::
    .string "Therefore that disciple whom Jesus\n"
    .string "loved saith unto Peter, It is the Lord\l"
    .string " Now when Simon Peter heard that it\l"
    .string "was the Lord, he girt his fisher’s\l"
    .string "coat unto him, (for he was naked,)\l"
    .string "and did cast himself into the sea.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_8::
    .string "And the other disciples came in a\n"
    .string "little ship; (for they were not far\l"
    .string "from land, but as it were two hundred\l"
    .string "cubits,) dragging the net with\l"
    .string "fishes.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_9::
    .string "As soon then as they were come to\n"
    .string "land, they saw a fire of coals there,\l"
    .string "and fish laid thereon, and bread.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_10::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, Bring of the\n"
    .string "fish which ye have now caught.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_11::
    .string "Simon Peter went up, and drew the\n"
    .string "net to land full of great fishes,\l"
    .string "an hundred and fifty and three: and\l"
    .string "for all there were so many, yet was\l"
    .string "not the net broken.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_12::
    .string "Jesus saith unto them, Come and\n"
    .string "dine. And none of the disciples\l"
    .string "durst ask him, Who art thou? knowing\l"
    .string "that it was the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_13::
    .string "Jesus then cometh, and taketh bread,\n"
    .string "and giveth them, and fish likewise.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_14::
    .string "This is now the third time that\n"
    .string "Jesus shewed himself to his\l"
    .string "disciples, after that he was risen\l"
    .string "from the dead.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_15::
    .string "So when they had dined, Jesus saith\n"
    .string "to Simon Peter, Simon, son of Jonas,\l"
    .string "lovest thou me more than these? He\l"
    .string "saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou\l"
    .string "knowest that I love thee. He saith\l"
    .string "unto him, Feed my lambs.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_16::
    .string "He saith to him again the second\n"
    .string "time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest\l"
    .string "thou me? He saith unto him, Yea, Lord;\l"
    .string "thou knowest that I love thee. He\l"
    .string "saith unto him, Feed my sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_17::
    .string "He saith unto him the third time,\n"
    .string "Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me?\l"
    .string "Peter was grieved because he said\l"
    .string "unto him the third time, Lovest thou\l"
    .string "me? And he said unto him, Lord, thou\l"
    .string "knowest all things; thou knowest\l"
    .string "that I love thee. Jesus saith unto\l"
    .string "him, Feed my sheep.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_18::
    .string "Verily, verily, I say unto thee,\n"
    .string "When thou wast young, thou girdest\l"
    .string "thyself, and walkedst whither thou\l"
    .string "wouldest: but when thou shalt be\l"
    .string "old, thou shalt stretch forth thy\l"
    .string "hands, and another shall gird thee,\l"
    .string "and carry thee whither thou wouldest\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_19::
    .string "This spake he, signifying by what\n"
    .string "death he should glorify God. And\l"
    .string "when he had spoken this, he saith\l"
    .string "unto him, Follow me.$"
Bible_Text_John_21_20::
    .string "Then Peter, turning about, seeth the\n"
    .string "disciple whom Jesus loved\l"
    .string "following; which also leaned on\l"
    .string "his breast at supper, and said,\l"
    .string "Lord, which is he that betrayeth\l"
    .string "thee?"
Bible_Text_John_21_21::
    .string "Peter seeing him saith to Jesus,\n"
    .string "Lord, and what shall this man do?"
Bible_Text_John_21_22::
    .string "Jesus saith unto him, If I will\n"
    .string "that he tarry till I come, what is\l"
    .string "that to thee? follow thou me$"
Bible_Text_John_21_23::
    .string "Then went this saying abroad among\n"
    .string "the brethren, that that disciple\l"
    .string "should not die: yet Jesus said not\l"
    .string "unto him, He shall not die; but, If I\l"
    .string "will that he tarry till I come,\l"
    .string "what is that to thee?"
Bible_Text_John_21_24::
    .string "This is the disciple which\n"
    .string "testifieth of these things, and wrote\l"
    .string "these things: and we know that his\l"
    .string "testimony is true$"
Bible_Text_John_21_25::
    .string "And there are also many other\n"
    .string "things which Jesus did, the which, if\l"
    .string "they should be written every one, I\l"
    .string "suppose that even the world itself\l"
    .string "could not contain the books that\l"
    .string "should be written. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_1::
    .string "The former treatise have I made, O\n"
    .string "Theophilus, of all that Jesus\l"
    .string "began both to do and teach,"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_2::
    .string "Until the day in which he was taken\n"
    .string "up, after that he through the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost had given commandments unto\l"
    .string "the apostles whom he had chosen:"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_3::
    .string "To whom also he shewed himself\n"
    .string "alive after his passion by many\l"
    .string "infallible proofs, being seen of\l"
    .string "them forty days, and speaking of the\l"
    .string "things pertaining to the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God:"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_4::
    .string "And, being assembled together with\n"
    .string "them, commanded them that they\l"
    .string "should not depart from Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "but wait for the promise of the\l"
    .string "Father, which, saith he, ye have\l"
    .string "heard of me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_5::
    .string "For John truly baptized with\n"
    .string "water; but ye shall be baptized\l"
    .string "with the Holy Ghost not many days\l"
    .string "hence.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_6::
    .string "When they therefore were come\n"
    .string "together, they asked of him, saying,\l"
    .string "Lord, wilt thou at this time restore\l"
    .string "again the kingdom to Israel?"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_7::
    .string "And he said unto them, It is not for\n"
    .string "you to know the times or the seasons,\l"
    .string "which the Father hath put in his own\l"
    .string "power$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_8::
    .string "But ye shall receive power, after\n"
    .string "that the Holy Ghost is come upon\l"
    .string "you: and ye shall be witnesses unto\l"
    .string "me both in Jerusalem, and in all\l"
    .string "Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the\l"
    .string "uttermost part of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_9::
    .string "And when he had spoken these\n"
    .string "things, while they beheld, he was\l"
    .string "taken up; and a cloud received him\l"
    .string "out of their sight.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_10::
    .string "And while they looked stedfastly\n"
    .string "toward heaven as he went up, behold,\l"
    .string "two men stood by them in white\l"
    .string "apparel;"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_11::
    .string "Which also said, Ye men of\n"
    .string "Galilee, why stand ye gazing up\l"
    .string "into heaven? this same Jesus, which\l"
    .string "is taken up from you into heaven,\l"
    .string "shall so come in like manner as ye\l"
    .string "have seen him go into heaven$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_12::
    .string "Then returned they unto Jerusalem\n"
    .string "from the mount called Olivet, which\l"
    .string "is from Jerusalem a sabbath day’s\l"
    .string "journey.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_13::
    .string "And when they were come in, they\n"
    .string "went up into an upper room, where\l"
    .string "abode both Peter, and James, and\l"
    .string "John, and Andrew, Philip, and\l"
    .string "Thomas, Bartholomew, and Matthew,\l"
    .string "James the son of Alphaeus, and Simon\l"
    .string "Zelotes, and Judas the brother of\l"
    .string "James.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_14::
    .string "These all continued with one\n"
    .string "accord in prayer and supplication,\l"
    .string "with the women, and Mary the mother\l"
    .string "of Jesus, and with his brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_15::
    .string "And in those days Peter stood up in\n"
    .string "the midst of the disciples, and\l"
    .string "said, (the number of names together\l"
    .string "were about an hundred and twenty,)"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_16::
    .string "Men and brethren, this scripture\n"
    .string "must needs have been fulfilled,\l"
    .string "which the Holy Ghost by the mouth of\l"
    .string "David spake before concerning Judas,\l"
    .string "which was guide to them that took\l"
    .string "Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_17::
    .string "For he was numbered with us, and had\n"
    .string "obtained part of this ministry.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_18::
    .string "Now this man purchased a field\n"
    .string "with the reward of iniquity; and\l"
    .string "falling headlong, he burst asunder\l"
    .string "in the midst, and all his bowels\l"
    .string "gushed out.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_19::
    .string "And it was known unto all the\n"
    .string "dwellers at Jerusalem; insomuch as\l"
    .string "that field is called in their\l"
    .string "proper tongue, Aceldama, that is to\l"
    .string "say, The field of blood.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_20::
    .string "For it is written in the book of\n"
    .string "Psalms, Let his habitation be\l"
    .string "desolate, and let no man dwell\l"
    .string "therein: and his bishoprick let\l"
    .string "another take.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_21::
    .string "Wherefore of these men which have\n"
    .string "companied with us all the time that\l"
    .string "the Lord Jesus went in and out among\l"
    .string "us,"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_22::
    .string "Beginning from the baptism of John,\n"
    .string "unto that same day that he was taken\l"
    .string "up from us, must one be ordained to\l"
    .string "be a witness with us of his\l"
    .string "resurrection$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_23::
    .string "And they appointed two, Joseph\n"
    .string "called Barsabas, who was surnamed\l"
    .string "Justus, and Matthias.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_24::
    .string "And they prayed, and said, Thou,\n"
    .string "Lord, which knowest the hearts of\l"
    .string "all men, shew whether of these two\l"
    .string "thou hast chosen,"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_25::
    .string "That he may take part of this\n"
    .string "ministry and apostleship, from\l"
    .string "which Judas by transgression fell,\l"
    .string "that he might go to his own place$"
Bible_Text_Acts_1_26::
    .string "And they gave forth their lots; and\n"
    .string "the lot fell upon Matthias; and he\l"
    .string "was numbered with the eleven\l"
    .string "apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_1::
    .string "And when the day of Pentecost was\n"
    .string "fully come, they were all with one\l"
    .string "accord in one place.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_2::
    .string "And suddenly there came a sound\n"
    .string "from heaven as of a rushing mighty\l"
    .string "wind, and it filled all the house\l"
    .string "where they were sitting.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_3::
    .string "And there appeared unto them\n"
    .string "cloven tongues like as of fire, and\l"
    .string "it sat upon each of them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_4::
    .string "And they were all filled with the\n"
    .string "Holy Ghost, and began to speak with\l"
    .string "other tongues, as the Spirit gave\l"
    .string "them utterance.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_5::
    .string "And there were dwelling at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem Jews, devout men, out of\l"
    .string "every nation under heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_6::
    .string "Now when this was noised abroad, the\n"
    .string "multitude came together, and were\l"
    .string "confounded, because that every man\l"
    .string "heard them speak in his own\l"
    .string "language.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_7::
    .string "And they were all amazed and\n"
    .string "marvelled, saying one to another,\l"
    .string "Behold, are not all these which\l"
    .string "speak Galilaeans?"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_8::
    .string "And how hear we every man in our own\n"
    .string "tongue, wherein we were born?"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_9::
    .string "Parthians, and Medes, and Elamites,\n"
    .string "and the dwellers in Mesopotamia,\l"
    .string "and in Judaea, and Cappadocia, in\l"
    .string "Pontus, and Asia,"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_10::
    .string "Phrygia, and Pamphylia, in Egypt,\n"
    .string "and in the parts of Libya about\l"
    .string "Cyrene, and strangers of Rome, Jews\l"
    .string "and proselytes,"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_11::
    .string "Cretes and Arabians, we do hear them\n"
    .string "speak in our tongues the wonderful\l"
    .string "works of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_12::
    .string "And they were all amazed, and were\n"
    .string "in doubt, saying one to another, What\l"
    .string "meaneth this?"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_13::
    .string "Others mocking said, These men are\n"
    .string "full of new wine$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_14::
    .string "But Peter, standing up with the\n"
    .string "eleven, lifted up his voice, and\l"
    .string "said unto them, Ye men of Judaea, and\l"
    .string "all ye that dwell at Jerusalem, be\l"
    .string "this known unto you, and hearken to\l"
    .string "my words:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_15::
    .string "For these are not drunken, as ye\n"
    .string "suppose, seeing it is but the third\l"
    .string "hour of the day$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_16::
    .string "But this is that which was spoken\n"
    .string "by the prophet Joel;"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_17::
    .string "And it shall come to pass in the\n"
    .string "last days, saith God, I will pour\l"
    .string "out of my Spirit upon all flesh:\l"
    .string "and your sons and your daughters\l"
    .string "shall prophesy, and your young men\l"
    .string "shall see visions, and your old men\l"
    .string "shall dream dreams:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_18::
    .string "And on my servants and on my\n"
    .string "handmaidens I will pour out in\l"
    .string "those days of my Spirit; and they\l"
    .string "shall prophesy:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_19::
    .string "And I will shew wonders in heaven\n"
    .string "above, and signs in the earth\l"
    .string "beneath; blood, and fire, and vapour\l"
    .string "of smoke:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_20::
    .string "The sun shall be turned into\n"
    .string "darkness, and the moon into blood,\l"
    .string "before the great and notable day of\l"
    .string "the Lord come:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_21::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "whosoever shall call on the name\l"
    .string "of the Lord shall be saved$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_22::
    .string "Ye men of Israel, hear these words;\n"
    .string "Jesus of Nazareth, a man approved of\l"
    .string "God among you by miracles and\l"
    .string "wonders and signs, which God did by\l"
    .string "him in the midst of you, as ye\l"
    .string "yourselves also know:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_23::
    .string "Him, being delivered by the\n"
    .string "determinate counsel and\l"
    .string "foreknowledge of God, ye have taken,\l"
    .string "and by wicked hands have crucified\l"
    .string "and slain:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_24::
    .string "Whom God hath raised up, having\n"
    .string "loosed the pains of death: because\l"
    .string "it was not possible that he should\l"
    .string "be holden of it$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_25::
    .string "For David speaketh concerning him,\n"
    .string "I foresaw the Lord always before my\l"
    .string "face, for he is on my right hand, that\l"
    .string "I should not be moved:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_26::
    .string "Therefore did my heart rejoice, and\n"
    .string "my tongue was glad; moreover also my\l"
    .string "flesh shall rest in hope:"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_27::
    .string "Because thou wilt not leave my\n"
    .string "soul in hell, neither wilt thou\l"
    .string "suffer thine Holy One to see\l"
    .string "corruption$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_28::
    .string "Thou hast made known to me the ways\n"
    .string "of life; thou shalt make me full of\l"
    .string "joy with thy countenance.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_29::
    .string "Men and brethren, let me freely\n"
    .string "speak unto you of the patriarch\l"
    .string "David, that he is both dead and\l"
    .string "buried, and his sepulchre is with us\l"
    .string "unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_30::
    .string "Therefore being a prophet, and\n"
    .string "knowing that God had sworn with an\l"
    .string "oath to him, that of the fruit of his\l"
    .string "loins, according to the flesh, he\l"
    .string "would raise up Christ to sit on his\l"
    .string "throne;"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_31::
    .string "He seeing this before spake of the\n"
    .string "resurrection of Christ, that his\l"
    .string "soul was not left in hell, neither\l"
    .string "his flesh did see corruption$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_32::
    .string "This Jesus hath God raised up,\n"
    .string "whereof we all are witnesses.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_33::
    .string "Therefore being by the right hand of\n"
    .string "God exalted, and having received of\l"
    .string "the Father the promise of the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost, he hath shed forth this, which\l"
    .string "ye now see and hear.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_34::
    .string "For David is not ascended into the\n"
    .string "heavens: but he saith himself, The\l"
    .string "Lord said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my\l"
    .string "right hand,"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_35::
    .string "Until I make thy foes thy footstool$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_36::
    .string "Therefore let all the house of\n"
    .string "Israel know assuredly, that God\l"
    .string "hath made the same Jesus, whom ye\l"
    .string "have crucified, both Lord and Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_37::
    .string "Now when they heard this, they were\n"
    .string "pricked in their heart, and said unto\l"
    .string "Peter and to the rest of the\l"
    .string "apostles, Men and brethren, what\l"
    .string "shall we do?"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_38::
    .string "Then Peter said unto them, Repent,\n"
    .string "and be baptized every one of you in\l"
    .string "the name of Jesus Christ for the\l"
    .string "remission of sins, and ye shall\l"
    .string "receive the gift of the Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_39::
    .string "For the promise is unto you, and to\n"
    .string "your children, and to all that are\l"
    .string "afar off, even as many as the LORD our\l"
    .string "God shall call.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_40::
    .string "And with many other words did he\n"
    .string "testify and exhort, saying, Save\l"
    .string "yourselves from this untoward\l"
    .string "generation.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_41::
    .string "Then they that gladly received his\n"
    .string "word were baptized: and the same day\l"
    .string "there were added unto them about\l"
    .string "three thousand souls.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_42::
    .string "And they continued stedfastly in\n"
    .string "the apostles’ doctrine and\l"
    .string "fellowship, and in breaking of\l"
    .string "bread, and in prayers.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_43::
    .string "And fear came upon every soul: and\n"
    .string "many wonders and signs were done by\l"
    .string "the apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_44::
    .string "And all that believed were\n"
    .string "together, and had all things\l"
    .string "common;"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_45::
    .string "And sold their possessions and\n"
    .string "goods, and parted them to all men,\l"
    .string "as every man had need$"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_46::
    .string "And they, continuing daily with one\n"
    .string "accord in the temple, and breaking\l"
    .string "bread from house to house, did eat\l"
    .string "their meat with gladness and\l"
    .string "singleness of heart,"
Bible_Text_Acts_2_47::
    .string "Praising God, and having favour with\n"
    .string "all the people. And the Lord added\l"
    .string "to the church daily such as should\l"
    .string "be saved$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_1::
    .string "Now Peter and John went up together\n"
    .string "into the temple at the hour of\l"
    .string "prayer, being the ninth hour.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_2::
    .string "And a certain man lame from his\n"
    .string "mother’s womb was carried, whom they\l"
    .string "laid daily at the gate of the\l"
    .string "temple which is called Beautiful,\l"
    .string "to ask alms of them that entered\l"
    .string "into the temple;"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_3::
    .string "Who seeing Peter and John about to\n"
    .string "go into the temple asked an alms$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_4::
    .string "And Peter, fastening his eyes upon\n"
    .string "him with John, said, Look on us.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_5::
    .string "And he gave heed unto them,\n"
    .string "expecting to receive something of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_6::
    .string "Then Peter said, Silver and gold\n"
    .string "have I none; but such as I have give I\l"
    .string "thee: In the name of Jesus Christ of\l"
    .string "Nazareth rise up and walk.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_7::
    .string "And he took him by the right hand,\n"
    .string "and lifted him up: and immediately\l"
    .string "his feet and ankle bones received\l"
    .string "strength.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_8::
    .string "And he leaping up stood, and\n"
    .string "walked, and entered with them into\l"
    .string "the temple, walking, and leaping,\l"
    .string "and praising God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_9::
    .string "And all the people saw him\n"
    .string "walking and praising God:"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_10::
    .string "And they knew that it was he which\n"
    .string "sat for alms at the Beautiful gate\l"
    .string "of the temple: and they were\l"
    .string "filled with wonder and amazement at\l"
    .string "that which had happened unto him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_11::
    .string "And as the lame man which was\n"
    .string "healed held Peter and John, all\l"
    .string "the people ran together unto them\l"
    .string "in the porch that is called\l"
    .string "Solomon’s, greatly wondering.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_12::
    .string "And when Peter saw it, he answered\n"
    .string "unto the people, Ye men of Israel,\l"
    .string "why marvel ye at this? or why look\l"
    .string "ye so earnestly on us, as though by\l"
    .string "our own power or holiness we had\l"
    .string "made this man to walk?"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_13::
    .string "The God of Abraham, and of Isaac,\n"
    .string "and of Jacob, the God of our fathers,\l"
    .string "hath glorified his Son Jesus; whom\l"
    .string "ye delivered up, and denied him in\l"
    .string "the presence of Pilate, when he was\l"
    .string "determined to let him go$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_14::
    .string "But ye denied the Holy One and the\n"
    .string "Just, and desired a murderer to be\l"
    .string "granted unto you;"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_15::
    .string "And killed the Prince of life,\n"
    .string "whom God hath raised from the dead;\l"
    .string "whereof we are witnesses$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_16::
    .string "And his name through faith in his\n"
    .string "name hath made this man strong, whom\l"
    .string "ye see and know: yea, the faith which\l"
    .string "is by him hath given him this\l"
    .string "perfect soundness in the presence of\l"
    .string "you all.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_17::
    .string "And now, brethren, I wot that\n"
    .string "through ignorance ye did it, as did\l"
    .string "also your rulers.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_18::
    .string "But those things, which God before\n"
    .string "had shewed by the mouth of all his\l"
    .string "prophets, that Christ should\l"
    .string "suffer, he hath so fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_19::
    .string "Repent ye therefore, and be\n"
    .string "converted, that your sins may be\l"
    .string "blotted out, when the times of\l"
    .string "refreshing shall come from the\l"
    .string "presence of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_20::
    .string "And he shall send Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "which before was preached unto you:"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_21::
    .string "Whom the heaven must receive until\n"
    .string "the times of restitution of all\l"
    .string "things, which God hath spoken by the\l"
    .string "mouth of all his holy prophets\l"
    .string "since the world began$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_22::
    .string "For Moses truly said unto the\n"
    .string "fathers, A prophet shall the Lord\l"
    .string "your God raise up unto you of your\l"
    .string "brethren, like unto me; him shall\l"
    .string "ye hear in all things whatsoever he\l"
    .string "shall say unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_23::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that\n"
    .string "every soul, which will not hear\l"
    .string "that prophet, shall be destroyed\l"
    .string "from among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_24::
    .string "Yea, and all the prophets from\n"
    .string "Samuel and those that follow after,\l"
    .string "as many as have spoken, have\l"
    .string "likewise foretold of these days.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_25::
    .string "Ye are the children of the\n"
    .string "prophets, and of the covenant which\l"
    .string "God made with our fathers, saying\l"
    .string "unto Abraham, And in thy seed shall\l"
    .string "all the kindreds of the earth be\l"
    .string "blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_3_26::
    .string "Unto you first God, having raised\n"
    .string "up his Son Jesus, sent him to bless\l"
    .string "you, in turning away every one of you\l"
    .string "from his iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_1::
    .string "And as they spake unto the\n"
    .string "people, the priests, and the\l"
    .string "captain of the temple, and the\l"
    .string "Sadducees, came upon them,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_2::
    .string "Being grieved that they taught the\n"
    .string "people, and preached through Jesus\l"
    .string "the resurrection from the dead$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_3::
    .string "And they laid hands on them, and\n"
    .string "put them in hold unto the next day:\l"
    .string "for it was now eventide.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_4::
    .string "Howbeit many of them which heard the\n"
    .string "word believed; and the number of the\l"
    .string "men was about five thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_5::
    .string "And it came to pass on the morrow,\n"
    .string "that their rulers, and elders, and\l"
    .string "scribes,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_6::
    .string "And Annas the high priest, and\n"
    .string "Caiaphas, and John, and Alexander,\l"
    .string "and as many as were of the kindred of\l"
    .string "the high priest, were gathered\l"
    .string "together at Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_7::
    .string "And when they had set them in the\n"
    .string "midst, they asked, By what power, or\l"
    .string "by what name, have ye done this?"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_8::
    .string "Then Peter, filled with the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost, said unto them, Ye rulers of\l"
    .string "the people, and elders of Israel,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_9::
    .string "If we this day be examined of the\n"
    .string "good deed done to the impotent man,\l"
    .string "by what means he is made whole;"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_10::
    .string "Be it known unto you all, and to\n"
    .string "all the people of Israel, that by\l"
    .string "the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth,\l"
    .string "whom ye crucified, whom God raised\l"
    .string "from the dead, even by him doth this\l"
    .string "man stand here before you whole$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_11::
    .string "This is the stone which was set at\n"
    .string "nought of you builders, which is\l"
    .string "become the head of the corner.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_12::
    .string "Neither is there salvation in any\n"
    .string "other: for there is none other name\l"
    .string "under heaven given among men, whereby\l"
    .string "we must be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_13::
    .string "Now when they saw the boldness of\n"
    .string "Peter and John, and perceived that\l"
    .string "they were unlearned and ignorant\l"
    .string "men, they marvelled; and they took\l"
    .string "knowledge of them, that they had\l"
    .string "been with Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_14::
    .string "And beholding the man which was\n"
    .string "healed standing with them, they\l"
    .string "could say nothing against it.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_15::
    .string "But when they had commanded them to\n"
    .string "go aside out of the council, they\l"
    .string "conferred among themselves,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_16::
    .string "Saying, What shall we do to these\n"
    .string "men? for that indeed a notable\l"
    .string "miracle hath been done by them is\l"
    .string "manifest to all them that dwell in\l"
    .string "Jerusalem; and we cannot deny it$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_17::
    .string "But that it spread no further among\n"
    .string "the people, let us straitly\l"
    .string "threaten them, that they speak\l"
    .string "henceforth to no man in this name.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_18::
    .string "And they called them, and\n"
    .string "commanded them not to speak at all\l"
    .string "nor teach in the name of Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_19::
    .string "But Peter and John answered and said\n"
    .string "unto them, Whether it be right in the\l"
    .string "sight of God to hearken unto you more\l"
    .string "than unto God, judge ye.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_20::
    .string "For we cannot but speak the things\n"
    .string "which we have seen and heard.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_21::
    .string "So when they had further threatened\n"
    .string "them, they let them go, finding\l"
    .string "nothing how they might punish them,\l"
    .string "because of the people: for all men\l"
    .string "glorified God for that which was\l"
    .string "done.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_22::
    .string "For the man was above forty years\n"
    .string "old, on whom this miracle of\l"
    .string "healing was shewed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_23::
    .string "And being let go, they went to their\n"
    .string "own company, and reported all that\l"
    .string "the chief priests and elders had\l"
    .string "said unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_24::
    .string "And when they heard that, they\n"
    .string "lifted up their voice to God with\l"
    .string "one accord, and said, Lord, thou art\l"
    .string "God, which hast made heaven, and\l"
    .string "earth, and the sea, and all that in\l"
    .string "them is:"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_25::
    .string "Who by the mouth of thy servant\n"
    .string "David hast said, Why did the heathen\l"
    .string "rage, and the people imagine vain\l"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_26::
    .string "The kings of the earth stood up, and\n"
    .string "the rulers were gathered together\l"
    .string "against the Lord, and against his\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_27::
    .string "For of a truth against thy holy\n"
    .string "child Jesus, whom thou hast\l"
    .string "anointed, both Herod, and Pontius\l"
    .string "Pilate, with the Gentiles, and the\l"
    .string "people of Israel, were gathered\l"
    .string "together,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_28::
    .string "For to do whatsoever thy hand and\n"
    .string "thy counsel determined before to be\l"
    .string "done$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_29::
    .string "And now, Lord, behold their\n"
    .string "threatenings: and grant unto thy\l"
    .string "servants, that with all boldness\l"
    .string "they may speak thy word,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_30::
    .string "By stretching forth thine hand to\n"
    .string "heal; and that signs and wonders may\l"
    .string "be done by the name of thy holy\l"
    .string "child Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_31::
    .string "And when they had prayed, the\n"
    .string "place was shaken where they were\l"
    .string "assembled together; and they were\l"
    .string "all filled with the Holy Ghost,\l"
    .string "and they spake the word of God with\l"
    .string "boldness.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_32::
    .string "And the multitude of them that\n"
    .string "believed were of one heart and of\l"
    .string "one soul: neither said any of them\l"
    .string "that ought of the things which he\l"
    .string "possessed was his own; but they had\l"
    .string "all things common.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_33::
    .string "And with great power gave the\n"
    .string "apostles witness of the\l"
    .string "resurrection of the Lord Jesus: and\l"
    .string "great grace was upon them all.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_34::
    .string "Neither was there any among them\n"
    .string "that lacked: for as many as were\l"
    .string "possessors of lands or houses sold\l"
    .string "them, and brought the prices of the\l"
    .string "things that were sold,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_35::
    .string "And laid them down at the\n"
    .string "apostles’ feet: and distribution\l"
    .string "was made unto every man according as\l"
    .string "he had need$"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_36::
    .string "And Joses, who by the apostles was\n"
    .string "surnamed Barnabas, (which is, being\l"
    .string "interpreted, The son of\l"
    .string "consolation,) a Levite, and of the\l"
    .string "country of Cyprus,"
Bible_Text_Acts_4_37::
    .string "Having land, sold it, and brought\n"
    .string "the money, and laid it at the\l"
    .string "apostles’ feet$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_1::
    .string "But a certain man named Ananias,\n"
    .string "with Sapphira his wife, sold a\l"
    .string "possession,"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_2::
    .string "And kept back part of the price,\n"
    .string "his wife also being privy to it, and\l"
    .string "brought a certain part, and laid it\l"
    .string "at the apostles’ feet$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_3::
    .string "But Peter said, Ananias, why hath\n"
    .string "Satan filled thine heart to lie to\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost, and to keep back\l"
    .string "part of the price of the land?"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_4::
    .string "Whiles it remained, was it not\n"
    .string "thine own? and after it was sold, was\l"
    .string "it not in thine own power? why hast\l"
    .string "thou conceived this thing in thine\l"
    .string "heart? thou hast not lied unto men,\l"
    .string "but unto God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_5::
    .string "And Ananias hearing these words\n"
    .string "fell down, and gave up the ghost:\l"
    .string "and great fear came on all them that\l"
    .string "heard these things.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_6::
    .string "And the young men arose, wound him\n"
    .string "up, and carried him out, and buried\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_7::
    .string "And it was about the space of three\n"
    .string "hours after, when his wife, not\l"
    .string "knowing what was done, came in.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_8::
    .string "And Peter answered unto her, Tell\n"
    .string "me whether ye sold the land for so\l"
    .string "much? And she said, Yea, for so much.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_9::
    .string "Then Peter said unto her, How is it\n"
    .string "that ye have agreed together to\l"
    .string "tempt the Spirit of the Lord?\l"
    .string "behold, the feet of them which have\l"
    .string "buried thy husband are at the door,\l"
    .string "and shall carry thee out.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_10::
    .string "Then fell she down straightway at\n"
    .string "his feet, and yielded up the ghost:\l"
    .string "and the young men came in, and found\l"
    .string "her dead, and, carrying her forth,\l"
    .string "buried her by her husband.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_11::
    .string "And great fear came upon all the\n"
    .string "church, and upon as many as heard\l"
    .string "these things.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_12::
    .string "And by the hands of the apostles\n"
    .string "were many signs and wonders wrought\l"
    .string "among the people; (and they were\l"
    .string "all with one accord in Solomon’s\l"
    .string "porch.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_13::
    .string "And of the rest durst no man join\n"
    .string "himself to them: but the people\l"
    .string "magnified them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_14::
    .string "And believers were the more added\n"
    .string "to the Lord, multitudes both of men\l"
    .string "and women.)"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_15::
    .string "Insomuch that they brought forth\n"
    .string "the sick into the streets, and laid\l"
    .string "them on beds and couches, that at the\l"
    .string "least the shadow of Peter passing by\l"
    .string "might overshadow some of them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_16::
    .string "There came also a multitude out of\n"
    .string "the cities round about unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, bringing sick folks, and\l"
    .string "them which were vexed with unclean\l"
    .string "spirits: and they were healed every\l"
    .string "one.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_17::
    .string "Then the high priest rose up, and\n"
    .string "all they that were with him, (which\l"
    .string "is the sect of the Sadducees,) and\l"
    .string "were filled with indignation,"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_18::
    .string "And laid their hands on the\n"
    .string "apostles, and put them in the\l"
    .string "common prison$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_19::
    .string "But the angel of the Lord by night\n"
    .string "opened the prison doors, and\l"
    .string "brought them forth, and said,"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_20::
    .string "Go, stand and speak in the temple\n"
    .string "to the people all the words of\l"
    .string "this life$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_21::
    .string "And when they heard that, they\n"
    .string "entered into the temple early in\l"
    .string "the morning, and taught. But the high\l"
    .string "priest came, and they that were with\l"
    .string "him, and called the council\l"
    .string "together, and all the senate of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel, and sent to the\l"
    .string "prison to have them brought.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_22::
    .string "But when the officers came, and\n"
    .string "found them not in the prison, they\l"
    .string "returned and told,"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_23::
    .string "Saying, The prison truly found we\n"
    .string "shut with all safety, and the\l"
    .string "keepers standing without before the\l"
    .string "doors: but when we had opened, we\l"
    .string "found no man within$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_24::
    .string "Now when the high priest and the\n"
    .string "captain of the temple and the chief\l"
    .string "priests heard these things, they\l"
    .string "doubted of them whereunto this would\l"
    .string "grow.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_25::
    .string "Then came one and told them,\n"
    .string "saying, Behold, the men whom ye put\l"
    .string "in prison are standing in the\l"
    .string "temple, and teaching the people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_26::
    .string "Then went the captain with the\n"
    .string "officers, and brought them without\l"
    .string "violence: for they feared the\l"
    .string "people, lest they should have been\l"
    .string "stoned.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_27::
    .string "And when they had brought them, they\n"
    .string "set them before the council: and the\l"
    .string "high priest asked them,"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_28::
    .string "Saying, Did not we straitly command\n"
    .string "you that ye should not teach in this\l"
    .string "name? and, behold, ye have filled\l"
    .string "Jerusalem with your doctrine, and\l"
    .string "intend to bring this man’s blood\l"
    .string "upon us$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_29::
    .string "Then Peter and the other apostles\n"
    .string "answered and said, We ought to obey\l"
    .string "God rather than men.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_30::
    .string "The God of our fathers raised up\n"
    .string "Jesus, whom ye slew and hanged on a\l"
    .string "tree.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_31::
    .string "Him hath God exalted with his right\n"
    .string "hand to be a Prince and a Saviour, for\l"
    .string "to give repentance to Israel, and\l"
    .string "forgiveness of sins.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_32::
    .string "And we are his witnesses of these\n"
    .string "things; and so is also the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost, whom God hath given to them\l"
    .string "that obey him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_33::
    .string "When they heard that, they were cut\n"
    .string "to the heart, and took counsel to\l"
    .string "slay them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_34::
    .string "Then stood there up one in the\n"
    .string "council, a Pharisee, named\l"
    .string "Gamaliel, a doctor of the law, had\l"
    .string "in reputation among all the\l"
    .string "people, and commanded to put the\l"
    .string "apostles forth a little space;"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_35::
    .string "And said unto them, Ye men of\n"
    .string "Israel, take heed to yourselves\l"
    .string "what ye intend to do as touching\l"
    .string "these men$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_36::
    .string "For before these days rose up\n"
    .string "Theudas, boasting himself to be\l"
    .string "somebody; to whom a number of men,\l"
    .string "about four hundred, joined\l"
    .string "themselves: who was slain; and\l"
    .string "all, as many as obeyed him, were\l"
    .string "scattered, and brought to nought.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_37::
    .string "After this man rose up Judas of\n"
    .string "Galilee in the days of the taxing,\l"
    .string "and drew away much people after\l"
    .string "him: he also perished; and all,\l"
    .string "even as many as obeyed him, were\l"
    .string "dispersed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_38::
    .string "And now I say unto you, Refrain from\n"
    .string "these men, and let them alone: for\l"
    .string "if this counsel or this work be of\l"
    .string "men, it will come to nought:"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_39::
    .string "But if it be of God, ye cannot\n"
    .string "overthrow it; lest haply ye be\l"
    .string "found even to fight against God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_40::
    .string "And to him they agreed: and when\n"
    .string "they had called the apostles, and\l"
    .string "beaten them, they commanded that they\l"
    .string "should not speak in the name of\l"
    .string "Jesus, and let them go.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_41::
    .string "And they departed from the\n"
    .string "presence of the council, rejoicing\l"
    .string "that they were counted worthy to\l"
    .string "suffer shame for his name.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_5_42::
    .string "And daily in the temple, and in\n"
    .string "every house, they ceased not to teach\l"
    .string "and preach Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_1::
    .string "And in those days, when the number\n"
    .string "of the disciples was multiplied,\l"
    .string "there arose a murmuring of the\l"
    .string "Grecians against the Hebrews,\l"
    .string "because their widows were neglected\l"
    .string "in the daily ministration.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_2::
    .string "Then the twelve called the\n"
    .string "multitude of the disciples unto\l"
    .string "them, and said, It is not reason that\l"
    .string "we should leave the word of God, and\l"
    .string "serve tables.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_3::
    .string "Wherefore, brethren, look ye out\n"
    .string "among you seven men of honest\l"
    .string "report, full of the Holy Ghost and\l"
    .string "wisdom, whom we may appoint over\l"
    .string "this business.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_4::
    .string "But we will give ourselves\n"
    .string "continually to prayer, and to the\l"
    .string "ministry of the word.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_5::
    .string "And the saying pleased the whole\n"
    .string "multitude: and they chose Stephen,\l"
    .string "a man full of faith and of the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost, and Philip, and Prochorus,\l"
    .string "and Nicanor, and Timon, and Parmenas,\l"
    .string "and Nicolas a proselyte of Antioch:"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_6::
    .string "Whom they set before the apostles:\n"
    .string "and when they had prayed, they laid\l"
    .string "their hands on them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_7::
    .string "And the word of God increased; and\n"
    .string "the number of the disciples\l"
    .string "multiplied in Jerusalem greatly;\l"
    .string "and a great company of the priests\l"
    .string "were obedient to the faith.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_8::
    .string "And Stephen, full of faith and\n"
    .string "power, did great wonders and\l"
    .string "miracles among the people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_9::
    .string "Then there arose certain of the\n"
    .string "synagogue, which is called the\l"
    .string "synagogue of the Libertines, and\l"
    .string "Cyrenians, and Alexandrians, and of\l"
    .string "them of Cilicia and of Asia,\l"
    .string "disputing with Stephen.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_10::
    .string "And they were not able to resist\n"
    .string "the wisdom and the spirit by which\l"
    .string "he spake.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_11::
    .string "Then they suborned men, which said,\n"
    .string "We have heard him speak\l"
    .string "blasphemous words against Moses,\l"
    .string "and against God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_12::
    .string "And they stirred up the people,\n"
    .string "and the elders, and the scribes, and\l"
    .string "came upon him, and caught him, and\l"
    .string "brought him to the council,"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_13::
    .string "And set up false witnesses, which\n"
    .string "said, This man ceaseth not to speak\l"
    .string "blasphemous words against this\l"
    .string "holy place, and the law:"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_14::
    .string "For we have heard him say, that this\n"
    .string "Jesus of Nazareth shall destroy\l"
    .string "this place, and shall change the\l"
    .string "customs which Moses delivered us$"
Bible_Text_Acts_6_15::
    .string "And all that sat in the council,\n"
    .string "looking stedfastly on him, saw his\l"
    .string "face as it had been the face of an\l"
    .string "angel.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_1::
    .string "Then said the high priest, Are\n"
    .string "these things so?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_2::
    .string "And he said, Men, brethren, and\n"
    .string "fathers, hearken; The God of glory\l"
    .string "appeared unto our father Abraham,\l"
    .string "when he was in Mesopotamia, before\l"
    .string "he dwelt in Charran,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_3::
    .string "And said unto him, Get thee out of\n"
    .string "thy country, and from thy kindred,\l"
    .string "and come into the land which I\l"
    .string "shall shew thee$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_4::
    .string "Then came he out of the land of the\n"
    .string "Chaldaeans, and dwelt in Charran:\l"
    .string "and from thence, when his father was\l"
    .string "dead, he removed him into this land,\l"
    .string "wherein ye now dwell.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_5::
    .string "And he gave him none inheritance in\n"
    .string "it, no, not so much as to set his foot\l"
    .string "on: yet he promised that he would\l"
    .string "give it to him for a possession, and\l"
    .string "to his seed after him, when as yet he\l"
    .string "had no child.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_6::
    .string "And God spake on this wise, That his\n"
    .string "seed should sojourn in a strange\l"
    .string "land; and that they should bring\l"
    .string "them into bondage, and entreat them\l"
    .string "evil four hundred years.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_7::
    .string "And the nation to whom they shall\n"
    .string "be in bondage will I judge, said\l"
    .string "God: and after that shall they come\l"
    .string "forth, and serve me in this place.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_8::
    .string "And he gave him the covenant of\n"
    .string "circumcision: and so Abraham begat\l"
    .string "Isaac, and circumcised him the eighth\l"
    .string "day; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob\l"
    .string "begat the twelve patriarchs.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_9::
    .string "And the patriarchs, moved with\n"
    .string "envy, sold Joseph into Egypt: but\l"
    .string "God was with him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_10::
    .string "And delivered him out of all his\n"
    .string "afflictions, and gave him favour and\l"
    .string "wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king\l"
    .string "of Egypt; and he made him governor\l"
    .string "over Egypt and all his house$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_11::
    .string "Now there came a dearth over all\n"
    .string "the land of Egypt and Chanaan, and\l"
    .string "great affliction: and our fathers\l"
    .string "found no sustenance.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_12::
    .string "But when Jacob heard that there was\n"
    .string "corn in Egypt, he sent out our\l"
    .string "fathers first.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_13::
    .string "And at the second time Joseph was\n"
    .string "made known to his brethren; and\l"
    .string "Joseph’s kindred was made known unto\l"
    .string "Pharaoh.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_14::
    .string "Then sent Joseph, and called his\n"
    .string "father Jacob to him, and all his\l"
    .string "kindred, threescore and fifteen\l"
    .string "souls.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_15::
    .string "So Jacob went down into Egypt, and\n"
    .string "died, he, and our fathers,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_16::
    .string "And were carried over into Sychem,\n"
    .string "and laid in the sepulchre that\l"
    .string "Abraham bought for a sum of money of\l"
    .string "the sons of Emmor the father of Sychem$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_17::
    .string "But when the time of the promise\n"
    .string "drew nigh, which God had sworn to\l"
    .string "Abraham, the people grew and\l"
    .string "multiplied in Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_18::
    .string "Till another king arose, which\n"
    .string "knew not Joseph$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_19::
    .string "The same dealt subtilly with our\n"
    .string "kindred, and evil entreated our\l"
    .string "fathers, so that they cast out their\l"
    .string "young children, to the end they\l"
    .string "might not live.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_20::
    .string "In which time Moses was born, and\n"
    .string "was exceeding fair, and nourished up\l"
    .string "in his father’s house three months:"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_21::
    .string "And when he was cast out, Pharaoh’s\n"
    .string "daughter took him up, and nourished\l"
    .string "him for her own son$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_22::
    .string "And Moses was learned in all the\n"
    .string "wisdom of the Egyptians, and was\l"
    .string "mighty in words and in deeds.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_23::
    .string "And when he was full forty years\n"
    .string "old, it came into his heart to visit\l"
    .string "his brethren the children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_24::
    .string "And seeing one of them suffer wrong,\n"
    .string "he defended him, and avenged him that\l"
    .string "was oppressed, and smote the\l"
    .string "Egyptian:"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_25::
    .string "For he supposed his brethren\n"
    .string "would have understood how that God\l"
    .string "by his hand would deliver them: but\l"
    .string "they understood not$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_26::
    .string "And the next day he shewed himself\n"
    .string "unto them as they strove, and would\l"
    .string "have set them at one again, saying,\l"
    .string "Sirs, ye are brethren; why do ye\l"
    .string "wrong one to another?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_27::
    .string "But he that did his neighbour wrong\n"
    .string "thrust him away, saying, Who made\l"
    .string "thee a ruler and a judge over us?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_28::
    .string "Wilt thou kill me, as thou diddest\n"
    .string "the Egyptian yesterday?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_29::
    .string "Then fled Moses at this saying, and\n"
    .string "was a stranger in the land of Madian,\l"
    .string "where he begat two sons$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_30::
    .string "And when forty years were expired,\n"
    .string "there appeared to him in the\l"
    .string "wilderness of mount Sina an angel\l"
    .string "of the Lord in a flame of fire in a\l"
    .string "bush.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_31::
    .string "When Moses saw it, he wondered at\n"
    .string "the sight: and as he drew near to\l"
    .string "behold it, the voice of the LORD came\l"
    .string "unto him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_32::
    .string "Saying, I am the God of thy fathers,\n"
    .string "the God of Abraham, and the God of\l"
    .string "Isaac, and the God of Jacob. Then\l"
    .string "Moses trembled, and durst not behold$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_33::
    .string "Then said the Lord to him, Put off\n"
    .string "thy shoes from thy feet: for the\l"
    .string "place where thou standest is holy\l"
    .string "ground.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_34::
    .string "I have seen, I have seen the\n"
    .string "affliction of my people which is\l"
    .string "in Egypt, and I have heard their\l"
    .string "groaning, and am come down to\l"
    .string "deliver them. And now come, I will\l"
    .string "send thee into Egypt.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_35::
    .string "This Moses whom they refused,\n"
    .string "saying, Who made thee a ruler and a\l"
    .string "judge? the same did God send to be a\l"
    .string "ruler and a deliverer by the hand of\l"
    .string "the angel which appeared to him in\l"
    .string "the bush.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_36::
    .string "He brought them out, after that he\n"
    .string "had shewed wonders and signs in the\l"
    .string "land of Egypt, and in the Red sea,\l"
    .string "and in the wilderness forty years.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_37::
    .string "This is that Moses, which said unto\n"
    .string "the children of Israel, A prophet\l"
    .string "shall the Lord your God raise up\l"
    .string "unto you of your brethren, like unto\l"
    .string "me; him shall ye hear.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_38::
    .string "This is he, that was in the church in\n"
    .string "the wilderness with the angel which\l"
    .string "spake to him in the mount Sina, and\l"
    .string "with our fathers: who received the\l"
    .string "lively oracles to give unto us:"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_39::
    .string "To whom our fathers would not obey,\n"
    .string "but thrust him from them, and in\l"
    .string "their hearts turned back again into\l"
    .string "Egypt,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_40::
    .string "Saying unto Aaron, Make us gods to\n"
    .string "go before us: for as for this Moses,\l"
    .string "which brought us out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, we wot not what is become of\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_41::
    .string "And they made a calf in those days,\n"
    .string "and offered sacrifice unto the idol,\l"
    .string "and rejoiced in the works of their\l"
    .string "own hands.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_42::
    .string "Then God turned, and gave them up to\n"
    .string "worship the host of heaven; as it is\l"
    .string "written in the book of the prophets,\l"
    .string "O ye house of Israel, have ye offered\l"
    .string "to me slain beasts and sacrifices by\l"
    .string "the space of forty years in the\l"
    .string "wilderness?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_43::
    .string "Yea, ye took up the tabernacle of\n"
    .string "Moloch, and the star of your god\l"
    .string "Remphan, figures which ye made to\l"
    .string "worship them: and I will carry you\l"
    .string "away beyond Babylon$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_44::
    .string "Our fathers had the tabernacle of\n"
    .string "witness in the wilderness, as he had\l"
    .string "appointed, speaking unto Moses,\l"
    .string "that he should make it according to\l"
    .string "the fashion that he had seen.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_45::
    .string "Which also our fathers that came\n"
    .string "after brought in with Jesus into the\l"
    .string "possession of the Gentiles, whom God\l"
    .string "drave out before the face of our\l"
    .string "fathers, unto the days of David;"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_46::
    .string "Who found favour before God, and\n"
    .string "desired to find a tabernacle for the\l"
    .string "God of Jacob$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_47::
    .string "But Solomon built him an house.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_48::
    .string "Howbeit the most High dwelleth not\n"
    .string "in temples made with hands; as saith\l"
    .string "the prophet,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_49::
    .string "Heaven is my throne, and earth is my\n"
    .string "footstool: what house will ye\l"
    .string "build me? saith the Lord: or what is\l"
    .string "the place of my rest?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_50::
    .string "Hath not my hand made all these\n"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_51::
    .string "Ye stiffnecked and uncircumcised in\n"
    .string "heart and ears, ye do always resist\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost: as your fathers did,\l"
    .string "so do ye$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_52::
    .string "Which of the prophets have not\n"
    .string "your fathers persecuted? and they\l"
    .string "have slain them which shewed before\l"
    .string "of the coming of the Just One; of whom\l"
    .string "ye have been now the betrayers and\l"
    .string "murderers:"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_53::
    .string "Who have received the law by the\n"
    .string "disposition of angels, and have not\l"
    .string "kept it$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_54::
    .string "When they heard these things, they\n"
    .string "were cut to the heart, and they\l"
    .string "gnashed on him with their teeth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_55::
    .string "But he, being full of the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost, looked up stedfastly into\l"
    .string "heaven, and saw the glory of God, and\l"
    .string "Jesus standing on the right hand of\l"
    .string "God,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_56::
    .string "And said, Behold, I see the heavens\n"
    .string "opened, and the Son of man standing\l"
    .string "on the right hand of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_57::
    .string "Then they cried out with a loud\n"
    .string "voice, and stopped their ears, and\l"
    .string "ran upon him with one accord,"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_58::
    .string "And cast him out of the city, and\n"
    .string "stoned him: and the witnesses laid\l"
    .string "down their clothes at a young man’s\l"
    .string "feet, whose name was Saul$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_59::
    .string "And they stoned Stephen, calling\n"
    .string "upon God, and saying, Lord Jesus,\l"
    .string "receive my spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_7_60::
    .string "And he kneeled down, and cried with\n"
    .string "a loud voice, Lord, lay not this sin\l"
    .string "to their charge. And when he had said\l"
    .string "this, he fell asleep.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_1::
    .string "And Saul was consenting unto his\n"
    .string "death. And at that time there was a\l"
    .string "great persecution against the\l"
    .string "church which was at Jerusalem; and\l"
    .string "they were all scattered abroad\l"
    .string "throughout the regions of Judaea and\l"
    .string "Samaria, except the apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_2::
    .string "And devout men carried Stephen to\n"
    .string "his burial, and made great\l"
    .string "lamentation over him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_3::
    .string "As for Saul, he made havock of the\n"
    .string "church, entering into every house,\l"
    .string "and haling men and women committed\l"
    .string "them to prison.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_4::
    .string "Therefore they that were scattered\n"
    .string "abroad went every where preaching\l"
    .string "the word.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_5::
    .string "Then Philip went down to the city\n"
    .string "of Samaria, and preached Christ unto\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_6::
    .string "And the people with one accord\n"
    .string "gave heed unto those things which\l"
    .string "Philip spake, hearing and seeing\l"
    .string "the miracles which he did.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_7::
    .string "For unclean spirits, crying with\n"
    .string "loud voice, came out of many that\l"
    .string "were possessed with them: and many\l"
    .string "taken with palsies, and that were\l"
    .string "lame, were healed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_8::
    .string "And there was great joy in that city.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_9::
    .string "But there was a certain man, called\n"
    .string "Simon, which beforetime in the same\l"
    .string "city used sorcery, and bewitched the\l"
    .string "people of Samaria, giving out that\l"
    .string "himself was some great one:"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_10::
    .string "To whom they all gave heed, from\n"
    .string "the least to the greatest, saying,\l"
    .string "This man is the great power of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_11::
    .string "And to him they had regard, because\n"
    .string "that of long time he had bewitched\l"
    .string "them with sorceries.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_12::
    .string "But when they believed Philip\n"
    .string "preaching the things concerning the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God, and the name of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, they were baptized, both men\l"
    .string "and women.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_13::
    .string "Then Simon himself believed also:\n"
    .string "and when he was baptized, he\l"
    .string "continued with Philip, and\l"
    .string "wondered, beholding the miracles\l"
    .string "and signs which were done.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_14::
    .string "Now when the apostles which were\n"
    .string "at Jerusalem heard that Samaria had\l"
    .string "received the word of God, they sent\l"
    .string "unto them Peter and John:"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_15::
    .string "Who, when they were come down,\n"
    .string "prayed for them, that they might\l"
    .string "receive the Holy Ghost:"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_16::
    .string "(For as yet he was fallen upon\n"
    .string "none of them: only they were\l"
    .string "baptized in the name of the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus.)"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_17::
    .string "Then laid they their hands on them,\n"
    .string "and they received the Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_18::
    .string "And when Simon saw that through\n"
    .string "laying on of the apostles’ hands\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost was given, he offered\l"
    .string "them money,"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_19::
    .string "Saying, Give me also this power,\n"
    .string "that on whomsoever I lay hands, he\l"
    .string "may receive the Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_20::
    .string "But Peter said unto him, Thy money\n"
    .string "perish with thee, because thou hast\l"
    .string "thought that the gift of God may be\l"
    .string "purchased with money.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_21::
    .string "Thou hast neither part nor lot in\n"
    .string "this matter: for thy heart is not\l"
    .string "right in the sight of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_22::
    .string "Repent therefore of this thy\n"
    .string "wickedness, and pray God, if\l"
    .string "perhaps the thought of thine heart\l"
    .string "may be forgiven thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_23::
    .string "For I perceive that thou art in the\n"
    .string "gall of bitterness, and in the bond\l"
    .string "of iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_24::
    .string "Then answered Simon, and said, Pray\n"
    .string "ye to the LORD for me, that none of\l"
    .string "these things which ye have spoken\l"
    .string "come upon me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_25::
    .string "And they, when they had testified\n"
    .string "and preached the word of the Lord,\l"
    .string "returned to Jerusalem, and preached\l"
    .string "the gospel in many villages of the\l"
    .string "Samaritans.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_26::
    .string "And the angel of the Lord spake\n"
    .string "unto Philip, saying, Arise, and go\l"
    .string "toward the south unto the way that\l"
    .string "goeth down from Jerusalem unto Gaza,\l"
    .string "which is desert.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_27::
    .string "And he arose and went: and, behold,\n"
    .string "a man of Ethiopia, an eunuch of great\l"
    .string "authority under Candace queen of the\l"
    .string "Ethiopians, who had the charge of\l"
    .string "all her treasure, and had come to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem for to worship,"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_28::
    .string "Was returning, and sitting in his\n"
    .string "chariot read Esaias the prophet$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_29::
    .string "Then the Spirit said unto Philip,\n"
    .string "Go near, and join thyself to this\l"
    .string "chariot.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_30::
    .string "And Philip ran thither to him, and\n"
    .string "heard him read the prophet Esaias,\l"
    .string "and said, Understandest thou what\l"
    .string "thou readest?"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_31::
    .string "And he said, How can I, except some\n"
    .string "man should guide me? And he desired\l"
    .string "Philip that he would come up and\l"
    .string "sit with him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_32::
    .string "The place of the scripture which\n"
    .string "he read was this, He was led as a\l"
    .string "sheep to the slaughter; and like a\l"
    .string "lamb dumb before his shearer, so\l"
    .string "opened he not his mouth:"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_33::
    .string "In his humiliation his judgment was\n"
    .string "taken away: and who shall declare\l"
    .string "his generation? for his life is\l"
    .string "taken from the earth$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_34::
    .string "And the eunuch answered Philip,\n"
    .string "and said, I pray thee, of whom\l"
    .string "speaketh the prophet this? of\l"
    .string "himself, or of some other man?"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_35::
    .string "Then Philip opened his mouth, and\n"
    .string "began at the same scripture, and\l"
    .string "preached unto him Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_36::
    .string "And as they went on their way, they\n"
    .string "came unto a certain water: and the\l"
    .string "eunuch said, See, here is water; what\l"
    .string "doth hinder me to be baptized?"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_37::
    .string "And Philip said, If thou believest\n"
    .string "with all thine heart, thou mayest\l"
    .string "And he answered and said, I believe\l"
    .string "that Jesus Christ is the Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_38::
    .string "And he commanded the chariot to\n"
    .string "stand still: and they went down both\l"
    .string "into the water, both Philip and the\l"
    .string "eunuch; and he baptized him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_39::
    .string "And when they were come up out of\n"
    .string "the water, the Spirit of the Lord\l"
    .string "caught away Philip, that the eunuch\l"
    .string "saw him no more: and he went on his\l"
    .string "way rejoicing.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_8_40::
    .string "But Philip was found at Azotus: and\n"
    .string "passing through he preached in all\l"
    .string "the cities, till he came to\l"
    .string "Caesarea.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_1::
    .string "And Saul, yet breathing out\n"
    .string "threatenings and slaughter against\l"
    .string "the disciples of the Lord, went unto\l"
    .string "the high priest,"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_2::
    .string "And desired of him letters to\n"
    .string "Damascus to the synagogues, that if\l"
    .string "he found any of this way, whether\l"
    .string "they were men or women, he might\l"
    .string "bring them bound unto Jerusalem$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_3::
    .string "And as he journeyed, he came near\n"
    .string "Damascus: and suddenly there shined\l"
    .string "round about him a light from heaven:"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_4::
    .string "And he fell to the earth, and heard\n"
    .string "a voice saying unto him, Saul, Saul,\l"
    .string "why persecutest thou me?"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_5::
    .string "And he said, Who art thou, Lord? And\n"
    .string "the Lord said, I am Jesus whom thou\l"
    .string "persecutest: it is hard for thee to\l"
    .string "kick against the pricks$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_6::
    .string "And he trembling and astonished\n"
    .string "said, Lord, what wilt thou have me to\l"
    .string "do? And the Lord said unto him, Arise,\l"
    .string "and go into the city, and it shall\l"
    .string "be told thee what thou must do.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_7::
    .string "And the men which journeyed with him\n"
    .string "stood speechless, hearing a voice,\l"
    .string "but seeing no man.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_8::
    .string "And Saul arose from the earth; and\n"
    .string "when his eyes were opened, he saw no\l"
    .string "man: but they led him by the hand,\l"
    .string "and brought him into Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_9::
    .string "And he was three days without sight,\n"
    .string "and neither did eat nor drink.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_10::
    .string "And there was a certain disciple\n"
    .string "at Damascus, named Ananias; and to\l"
    .string "him said the Lord in a vision, Ananias\l"
    .string " And he said, Behold, I am here,\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_11::
    .string "And the Lord said unto him, Arise,\n"
    .string "and go into the street which is\l"
    .string "called Straight, and enquire in the\l"
    .string "house of Judas for one called Saul,\l"
    .string "of Tarsus: for, behold, he prayeth,"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_12::
    .string "And hath seen in a vision a man\n"
    .string "named Ananias coming in, and putting\l"
    .string "his hand on him, that he might\l"
    .string "receive his sight$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_13::
    .string "Then Ananias answered, Lord, I have\n"
    .string "heard by many of this man, how much\l"
    .string "evil he hath done to thy saints at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem:"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_14::
    .string "And here he hath authority from the\n"
    .string "chief priests to bind all that\l"
    .string "call on thy name$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_15::
    .string "But the Lord said unto him, Go thy\n"
    .string "way: for he is a chosen vessel unto\l"
    .string "me, to bear my name before the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, and kings, and the\l"
    .string "children of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_16::
    .string "For I will shew him how great\n"
    .string "things he must suffer for my name’s\l"
    .string "sake$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_17::
    .string "And Ananias went his way, and\n"
    .string "entered into the house; and putting\l"
    .string "his hands on him said, Brother Saul,\l"
    .string "the Lord, even Jesus, that appeared\l"
    .string "unto thee in the way as thou camest,\l"
    .string "hath sent me, that thou mightest\l"
    .string "receive thy sight, and be filled\l"
    .string "with the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_18::
    .string "And immediately there fell from\n"
    .string "his eyes as it had been scales: and\l"
    .string "he received sight forthwith, and\l"
    .string "arose, and was baptized.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_19::
    .string "And when he had received meat, he\n"
    .string "was strengthened. Then was Saul\l"
    .string "certain days with the disciples\l"
    .string "which were at Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_20::
    .string "And straightway he preached Christ\n"
    .string "in the synagogues, that he is the Son\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_21::
    .string "But all that heard him were amazed,\n"
    .string "and said; Is not this he that\l"
    .string "destroyed them which called on this\l"
    .string "name in Jerusalem, and came hither\l"
    .string "for that intent, that he might bring\l"
    .string "them bound unto the chief priests?"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_22::
    .string "But Saul increased the more in\n"
    .string "strength, and confounded the Jews\l"
    .string "which dwelt at Damascus, proving\l"
    .string "that this is very Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_23::
    .string "And after that many days were\n"
    .string "fulfilled, the Jews took counsel\l"
    .string "to kill him:"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_24::
    .string "But their laying await was known of\n"
    .string "Saul. And they watched the gates day\l"
    .string "and night to kill him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_25::
    .string "Then the disciples took him by\n"
    .string "night, and let him down by the wall\l"
    .string "in a basket.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_26::
    .string "And when Saul was come to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, he assayed to join\l"
    .string "himself to the disciples: but they\l"
    .string "were all afraid of him, and\l"
    .string "believed not that he was a disciple.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_27::
    .string "But Barnabas took him, and brought\n"
    .string "him to the apostles, and declared\l"
    .string "unto them how he had seen the Lord in\l"
    .string "the way, and that he had spoken to\l"
    .string "him, and how he had preached boldly\l"
    .string "at Damascus in the name of Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_28::
    .string "And he was with them coming in and\n"
    .string "going out at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_29::
    .string "And he spake boldly in the name of\n"
    .string "the Lord Jesus, and disputed against\l"
    .string "the Grecians: but they went about to\l"
    .string "slay him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_30::
    .string "Which when the brethren knew, they\n"
    .string "brought him down to Caesarea, and\l"
    .string "sent him forth to Tarsus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_31::
    .string "Then had the churches rest\n"
    .string "throughout all Judaea and Galilee\l"
    .string "and Samaria, and were edified; and\l"
    .string "walking in the fear of the Lord, and\l"
    .string "in the comfort of the Holy Ghost,\l"
    .string "were multiplied.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_32::
    .string "And it came to pass, as Peter\n"
    .string "passed throughout all quarters, he\l"
    .string "came down also to the saints which\l"
    .string "dwelt at Lydda.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_33::
    .string "And there he found a certain man\n"
    .string "named Aeneas, which had kept his bed\l"
    .string "eight years, and was sick of the\l"
    .string "palsy.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_34::
    .string "And Peter said unto him, Aeneas,\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ maketh thee whole:\l"
    .string "arise, and make thy bed. And he arose\l"
    .string "immediately.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_35::
    .string "And all that dwelt at Lydda and\n"
    .string "Saron saw him, and turned to the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_36::
    .string "Now there was at Joppa a certain\n"
    .string "disciple named Tabitha, which by\l"
    .string "interpretation is called Dorcas:\l"
    .string "this woman was full of good works\l"
    .string "and almsdeeds which she did.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_37::
    .string "And it came to pass in those days,\n"
    .string "that she was sick, and died: whom\l"
    .string "when they had washed, they laid her\l"
    .string "in an upper chamber.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_38::
    .string "And forasmuch as Lydda was nigh to\n"
    .string "Joppa, and the disciples had heard\l"
    .string "that Peter was there, they sent unto\l"
    .string "him two men, desiring him that he\l"
    .string "would not delay to come to them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_39::
    .string "Then Peter arose and went with them.\n"
    .string "When he was come, they brought him\l"
    .string "into the upper chamber: and all\l"
    .string "the widows stood by him weeping, and\l"
    .string "shewing the coats and garments which\l"
    .string "Dorcas made, while she was with them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_40::
    .string "But Peter put them all forth, and\n"
    .string "kneeled down, and prayed; and\l"
    .string "turning him to the body said,\l"
    .string "Tabitha, arise. And she opened her\l"
    .string "eyes: and when she saw Peter, she sat\l"
    .string "up.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_41::
    .string "And he gave her his hand, and lifted\n"
    .string "her up, and when he had called the\l"
    .string "saints and widows, presented her\l"
    .string "alive.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_42::
    .string "And it was known throughout all\n"
    .string "Joppa; and many believed in the\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_9_43::
    .string "And it came to pass, that he tarried\n"
    .string "many days in Joppa with one Simon a\l"
    .string "tanner.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_1::
    .string "There was a certain man in Caesarea\n"
    .string "called Cornelius, a centurion of\l"
    .string "the band called the Italian band,"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_2::
    .string "A devout man, and one that feared\n"
    .string "God with all his house, which gave\l"
    .string "much alms to the people, and\l"
    .string "prayed to God alway$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_3::
    .string "He saw in a vision evidently about\n"
    .string "the ninth hour of the day an angel of\l"
    .string "God coming in to him, and saying unto\l"
    .string "him, Cornelius.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_4::
    .string "And when he looked on him, he was\n"
    .string "afraid, and said, What is it, Lord?\l"
    .string "And he said unto him, Thy prayers and\l"
    .string "thine alms are come up for a\l"
    .string "memorial before God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_5::
    .string "And now send men to Joppa, and\n"
    .string "call for one Simon, whose surname is\l"
    .string "Peter:"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_6::
    .string "He lodgeth with one Simon a tanner,\n"
    .string "whose house is by the sea side: he\l"
    .string "shall tell thee what thou oughtest\l"
    .string "to do$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_7::
    .string "And when the angel which spake\n"
    .string "unto Cornelius was departed, he\l"
    .string "called two of his household\l"
    .string "servants, and a devout soldier of\l"
    .string "them that waited on him\l"
    .string "continually;"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_8::
    .string "And when he had declared all these\n"
    .string "things unto them, he sent them to\l"
    .string "Joppa$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_9::
    .string "On the morrow, as they went on their\n"
    .string "journey, and drew nigh unto the city,\l"
    .string "Peter went up upon the housetop to\l"
    .string "pray about the sixth hour:"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_10::
    .string "And he became very hungry, and\n"
    .string "would have eaten: but while they\l"
    .string "made ready, he fell into a trance,"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_11::
    .string "And saw heaven opened, and a\n"
    .string "certain vessel descending upon him,\l"
    .string "as it had been a great sheet knit at\l"
    .string "the four corners, and let down to the\l"
    .string "earth:"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_12::
    .string "Wherein were all manner of\n"
    .string "fourfooted beasts of the earth, and\l"
    .string "wild beasts, and creeping things,\l"
    .string "and fowls of the air$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_13::
    .string "And there came a voice to him, Rise,\n"
    .string "Peter; kill, and eat.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_14::
    .string "But Peter said, Not so, Lord; for I\n"
    .string "have never eaten any thing that is\l"
    .string "common or unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_15::
    .string "And the voice spake unto him again\n"
    .string "the second time, What God hath\l"
    .string "cleansed, that call not thou\l"
    .string "common.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_16::
    .string "This was done thrice: and the\n"
    .string "vessel was received up again into\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_17::
    .string "Now while Peter doubted in himself\n"
    .string "what this vision which he had seen\l"
    .string "should mean, behold, the men which\l"
    .string "were sent from Cornelius had made\l"
    .string "enquiry for Simon’s house, and stood\l"
    .string "before the gate,"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_18::
    .string "And called, and asked whether\n"
    .string "Simon, which was surnamed Peter, were\l"
    .string "lodged there$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_19::
    .string "While Peter thought on the vision,\n"
    .string "the Spirit said unto him, Behold,\l"
    .string "three men seek thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_20::
    .string "Arise therefore, and get thee down,\n"
    .string "and go with them, doubting nothing:\l"
    .string "for I have sent them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_21::
    .string "Then Peter went down to the men\n"
    .string "which were sent unto him from\l"
    .string "Cornelius; and said, Behold, I am he\l"
    .string "whom ye seek: what is the cause\l"
    .string "wherefore ye are come?"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_22::
    .string "And they said, Cornelius the\n"
    .string "centurion, a just man, and one that\l"
    .string "feareth God, and of good report\l"
    .string "among all the nation of the Jews,\l"
    .string "was warned from God by an holy angel\l"
    .string "to send for thee into his house, and\l"
    .string "to hear words of thee$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_23::
    .string "Then called he them in, and lodged\n"
    .string "them. And on the morrow Peter went\l"
    .string "away with them, and certain brethren\l"
    .string "from Joppa accompanied him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_24::
    .string "And the morrow after they entered\n"
    .string "into Caesarea. And Cornelius waited\l"
    .string "for them, and he had called together\l"
    .string "his kinsmen and near friends.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_25::
    .string "And as Peter was coming in,\n"
    .string "Cornelius met him, and fell down at\l"
    .string "his feet, and worshipped him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_26::
    .string "But Peter took him up, saying,\n"
    .string "Stand up; I myself also am a man.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_27::
    .string "And as he talked with him, he went\n"
    .string "in, and found many that were come\l"
    .string "together.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_28::
    .string "And he said unto them, Ye know how\n"
    .string "that it is an unlawful thing for a\l"
    .string "man that is a Jew to keep company,\l"
    .string "or come unto one of another nation;\l"
    .string "but God hath shewed me that I should\l"
    .string "not call any man common or unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_29::
    .string "Therefore came I unto you without\n"
    .string "gainsaying, as soon as I was sent\l"
    .string "for: I ask therefore for what intent\l"
    .string "ye have sent for me?"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_30::
    .string "And Cornelius said, Four days ago I\n"
    .string "was fasting until this hour; and at\l"
    .string "the ninth hour I prayed in my house,\l"
    .string "and, behold, a man stood before me in\l"
    .string "bright clothing,"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_31::
    .string "And said, Cornelius, thy prayer is\n"
    .string "heard, and thine alms are had in\l"
    .string "remembrance in the sight of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_32::
    .string "Send therefore to Joppa, and call\n"
    .string "hither Simon, whose surname is Peter;\l"
    .string "he is lodged in the house of one\l"
    .string "Simon a tanner by the sea side: who,\l"
    .string "when he cometh, shall speak unto\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_33::
    .string "Immediately therefore I sent to\n"
    .string "thee; and thou hast well done that\l"
    .string "thou art come. Now therefore are we\l"
    .string "all here present before God, to\l"
    .string "hear all things that are commanded\l"
    .string "thee of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_34::
    .string "Then Peter opened his mouth, and\n"
    .string "said, Of a truth I perceive that God\l"
    .string "is no respecter of persons:"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_35::
    .string "But in every nation he that feareth\n"
    .string "him, and worketh righteousness, is\l"
    .string "accepted with him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_36::
    .string "The word which God sent unto the\n"
    .string "children of Israel, preaching\l"
    .string "peace by Jesus Christ: (he is Lord of\l"
    .string "all:)"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_37::
    .string "That word, I say, ye know, which was\n"
    .string "published throughout all Judaea,\l"
    .string "and began from Galilee, after the\l"
    .string "baptism which John preached;"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_38::
    .string "How God anointed Jesus of Nazareth\n"
    .string "with the Holy Ghost and with power:\l"
    .string "who went about doing good, and\l"
    .string "healing all that were oppressed\l"
    .string "of the devil; for God was with him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_39::
    .string "And we are witnesses of all things\n"
    .string "which he did both in the land of the\l"
    .string "Jews, and in Jerusalem; whom they\l"
    .string "slew and hanged on a tree:"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_40::
    .string "Him God raised up the third day, and\n"
    .string "shewed him openly;"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_41::
    .string "Not to all the people, but unto\n"
    .string "witnesses chosen before God, even to\l"
    .string "us, who did eat and drink with him\l"
    .string "after he rose from the dead$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_42::
    .string "And he commanded us to preach unto\n"
    .string "the people, and to testify that it\l"
    .string "is he which was ordained of God to be\l"
    .string "the Judge of quick and dead.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_43::
    .string "To him give all the prophets\n"
    .string "witness, that through his name\l"
    .string "whosoever believeth in him shall\l"
    .string "receive remission of sins.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_44::
    .string "While Peter yet spake these words,\n"
    .string "the Holy Ghost fell on all them\l"
    .string "which heard the word.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_45::
    .string "And they of the circumcision which\n"
    .string "believed were astonished, as many as\l"
    .string "came with Peter, because that on the\l"
    .string "Gentiles also was poured out the\l"
    .string "gift of the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_46::
    .string "For they heard them speak with\n"
    .string "tongues, and magnify God. Then\l"
    .string "answered Peter,"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_47::
    .string "Can any man forbid water, that these\n"
    .string "should not be baptized, which have\l"
    .string "received the Holy Ghost as well as\l"
    .string "we?"
Bible_Text_Acts_10_48::
    .string "And he commanded them to be\n"
    .string "baptized in the name of the Lord.\l"
    .string "Then prayed they him to tarry\l"
    .string "certain days$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_1::
    .string "And the apostles and brethren that\n"
    .string "were in Judaea heard that the\l"
    .string "Gentiles had also received the word\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_2::
    .string "And when Peter was come up to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, they that were of the\l"
    .string "circumcision contended with him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_3::
    .string "Saying, Thou wentest in to men\n"
    .string "uncircumcised, and didst eat with\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_4::
    .string "But Peter rehearsed the matter from\n"
    .string "the beginning, and expounded it by\l"
    .string "order unto them, saying,"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_5::
    .string "I was in the city of Joppa\n"
    .string "praying: and in a trance I saw a\l"
    .string "vision, A certain vessel descend, as\l"
    .string "it had been a great sheet, let down\l"
    .string "from heaven by four corners; and it\l"
    .string "came even to me:"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_6::
    .string "Upon the which when I had fastened\n"
    .string "mine eyes, I considered, and saw\l"
    .string "fourfooted beasts of the earth, and\l"
    .string "wild beasts, and creeping things,\l"
    .string "and fowls of the air$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_7::
    .string "And I heard a voice saying unto me,\n"
    .string "Arise, Peter; slay and eat.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_8::
    .string "But I said, Not so, Lord: for nothing\n"
    .string "common or unclean hath at any time\l"
    .string "entered into my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_9::
    .string "But the voice answered me again from\n"
    .string "heaven, What God hath cleansed, that\l"
    .string "call not thou common.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_10::
    .string "And this was done three times: and\n"
    .string "all were drawn up again into heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_11::
    .string "And, behold, immediately there\n"
    .string "were three men already come unto the\l"
    .string "house where I was, sent from Caesarea\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_12::
    .string "And the Spirit bade me go with them,\n"
    .string "nothing doubting. Moreover these six\l"
    .string "brethren accompanied me, and we\l"
    .string "entered into the man’s house:"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_13::
    .string "And he shewed us how he had seen an\n"
    .string "angel in his house, which stood and\l"
    .string "said unto him, Send men to Joppa,\l"
    .string "and call for Simon, whose surname is\l"
    .string "Peter;"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_14::
    .string "Who shall tell thee words,\n"
    .string "whereby thou and all thy house\l"
    .string "shall be saved$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_15::
    .string "And as I began to speak, the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost fell on them, as on us at the\l"
    .string "beginning.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_16::
    .string "Then remembered I the word of the\n"
    .string "Lord, how that he said, John indeed\l"
    .string "baptized with water; but ye shall\l"
    .string "be baptized with the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_17::
    .string "Forasmuch then as God gave them the\n"
    .string "like gift as he did unto us, who\l"
    .string "believed on the Lord Jesus Christ;\l"
    .string "what was I, that I could withstand\l"
    .string "God?"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_18::
    .string "When they heard these things, they\n"
    .string "held their peace, and glorified\l"
    .string "God, saying, Then hath God also to\l"
    .string "the Gentiles granted repentance\l"
    .string "unto life$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_19::
    .string "Now they which were scattered\n"
    .string "abroad upon the persecution that\l"
    .string "arose about Stephen travelled as\l"
    .string "far as Phenice, and Cyprus, and\l"
    .string "Antioch, preaching the word to none\l"
    .string "but unto the Jews only.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_20::
    .string "And some of them were men of Cyprus\n"
    .string "and Cyrene, which, when they were\l"
    .string "come to Antioch, spake unto the\l"
    .string "Grecians, preaching the LORD Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_21::
    .string "And the hand of the Lord was with\n"
    .string "them: and a great number believed,\l"
    .string "and turned unto the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_22::
    .string "Then tidings of these things came\n"
    .string "unto the ears of the church which was\l"
    .string "in Jerusalem: and they sent forth\l"
    .string "Barnabas, that he should go as far as\l"
    .string "Antioch.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_23::
    .string "Who, when he came, and had seen the\n"
    .string "grace of God, was glad, and exhorted\l"
    .string "them all, that with purpose of\l"
    .string "heart they would cleave unto the\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_24::
    .string "For he was a good man, and full of\n"
    .string "the Holy Ghost and of faith: and much\l"
    .string "people was added unto the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_25::
    .string "Then departed Barnabas to Tarsus,\n"
    .string "for to seek Saul:"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_26::
    .string "And when he had found him, he\n"
    .string "brought him unto Antioch. And it came\l"
    .string "to pass, that a whole year they\l"
    .string "assembled themselves with the\l"
    .string "church, and taught much people. And\l"
    .string "the disciples were called\l"
    .string "Christians first in Antioch$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_27::
    .string "And in these days came prophets\n"
    .string "from Jerusalem unto Antioch.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_28::
    .string "And there stood up one of them\n"
    .string "named Agabus, and signified by the\l"
    .string "Spirit that there should be great\l"
    .string "dearth throughout all the world:\l"
    .string "which came to pass in the days of\l"
    .string "Claudius Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_29::
    .string "Then the disciples, every man\n"
    .string "according to his ability, determined\l"
    .string "to send relief unto the brethren\l"
    .string "which dwelt in Judaea:"
Bible_Text_Acts_11_30::
    .string "Which also they did, and sent it to\n"
    .string "the elders by the hands of Barnabas\l"
    .string "and Saul$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_1::
    .string "Now about that time Herod the king\n"
    .string "stretched forth his hands to vex\l"
    .string "certain of the church.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_2::
    .string "And he killed James the brother of\n"
    .string "John with the sword.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_3::
    .string "And because he saw it pleased the\n"
    .string "Jews, he proceeded further to take\l"
    .string "Peter also. (Then were the days of\l"
    .string "unleavened bread.)"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_4::
    .string "And when he had apprehended him, he\n"
    .string "put him in prison, and delivered him\l"
    .string "to four quaternions of soldiers to\l"
    .string "keep him; intending after Easter to\l"
    .string "bring him forth to the people$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_5::
    .string "Peter therefore was kept in\n"
    .string "prison: but prayer was made without\l"
    .string "ceasing of the church unto God for\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_6::
    .string "And when Herod would have brought\n"
    .string "him forth, the same night Peter was\l"
    .string "sleeping between two soldiers,\l"
    .string "bound with two chains: and the\l"
    .string "keepers before the door kept the\l"
    .string "prison.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_7::
    .string "And, behold, the angel of the Lord\n"
    .string "came upon him, and a light shined in\l"
    .string "the prison: and he smote Peter on the\l"
    .string "side, and raised him up, saying,\l"
    .string "Arise up quickly. And his chains\l"
    .string "fell off from his hands.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_8::
    .string "And the angel said unto him, Gird\n"
    .string "thyself, and bind on thy sandals.\l"
    .string "And so he did. And he saith unto him,\l"
    .string "Cast thy garment about thee, and\l"
    .string "follow me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_9::
    .string "And he went out, and followed him;\n"
    .string "and wist not that it was true which\l"
    .string "was done by the angel; but thought he\l"
    .string "saw a vision.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_10::
    .string "When they were past the first and\n"
    .string "the second ward, they came unto the\l"
    .string "iron gate that leadeth unto the\l"
    .string "city; which opened to them of his own\l"
    .string "accord: and they went out, and\l"
    .string "passed on through one street; and\l"
    .string "forthwith the angel departed from\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_11::
    .string "And when Peter was come to himself,\n"
    .string "he said, Now I know of a surety, that\l"
    .string "the LORD hath sent his angel, and\l"
    .string "hath delivered me out of the hand of\l"
    .string "Herod, and from all the expectation\l"
    .string "of the people of the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_12::
    .string "And when he had considered the\n"
    .string "thing, he came to the house of Mary\l"
    .string "the mother of John, whose surname was\l"
    .string "Mark; where many were gathered\l"
    .string "together praying.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_13::
    .string "And as Peter knocked at the door of\n"
    .string "the gate, a damsel came to hearken,\l"
    .string "named Rhoda.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_14::
    .string "And when she knew Peter’s voice, she\n"
    .string "opened not the gate for gladness,\l"
    .string "but ran in, and told how Peter stood\l"
    .string "before the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_15::
    .string "And they said unto her, Thou art\n"
    .string "mad. But she constantly affirmed\l"
    .string "that it was even so. Then said they,\l"
    .string "It is his angel.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_16::
    .string "But Peter continued knocking: and\n"
    .string "when they had opened the door, and\l"
    .string "saw him, they were astonished.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_17::
    .string "But he, beckoning unto them with the\n"
    .string "hand to hold their peace, declared\l"
    .string "unto them how the Lord had brought\l"
    .string "him out of the prison. And he said,\l"
    .string "Go shew these things unto James, and\l"
    .string "to the brethren. And he departed,\l"
    .string "and went into another place.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_18::
    .string "Now as soon as it was day, there was\n"
    .string "no small stir among the soldiers,\l"
    .string "what was become of Peter.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_19::
    .string "And when Herod had sought for him,\n"
    .string "and found him not, he examined the\l"
    .string "keepers, and commanded that they\l"
    .string "should be put to death. And he went\l"
    .string "down from Judaea to Caesarea, and\l"
    .string "there abode.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_20::
    .string "And Herod was highly displeased\n"
    .string "with them of Tyre and Sidon: but they\l"
    .string "came with one accord to him, and,\l"
    .string "having made Blastus the king’s\l"
    .string "chamberlain their friend, desired\l"
    .string "peace; because their country was\l"
    .string "nourished by the king’s country.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_21::
    .string "And upon a set day Herod, arrayed in\n"
    .string "royal apparel, sat upon his\l"
    .string "throne, and made an oration unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_22::
    .string "And the people gave a shout,\n"
    .string "saying, It is the voice of a god, and\l"
    .string "not of a man.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_23::
    .string "And immediately the angel of the\n"
    .string "Lord smote him, because he gave not\l"
    .string "God the glory: and he was eaten of\l"
    .string "worms, and gave up the ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_24::
    .string "But the word of God grew and\n"
    .string "multiplied.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_12_25::
    .string "And Barnabas and Saul returned from\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, when they had fulfilled\l"
    .string "their ministry, and took with them\l"
    .string "John, whose surname was Mark.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_1::
    .string "Now there were in the church that\n"
    .string "was at Antioch certain prophets and\l"
    .string "teachers; as Barnabas, and Simeon\l"
    .string "that was called Niger, and Lucius of\l"
    .string "Cyrene, and Manaen, which had been\l"
    .string "brought up with Herod the tetrarch,\l"
    .string "and Saul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_2::
    .string "As they ministered to the Lord, and\n"
    .string "fasted, the Holy Ghost said,\l"
    .string "Separate me Barnabas and Saul for\l"
    .string "the work whereunto I have called\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_3::
    .string "And when they had fasted and\n"
    .string "prayed, and laid their hands on\l"
    .string "them, they sent them away.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_4::
    .string "So they, being sent forth by the\n"
    .string "Holy Ghost, departed unto\l"
    .string "Seleucia; and from thence they\l"
    .string "sailed to Cyprus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_5::
    .string "And when they were at Salamis, they\n"
    .string "preached the word of God in the\l"
    .string "synagogues of the Jews: and they had\l"
    .string "also John to their minister.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_6::
    .string "And when they had gone through the\n"
    .string "isle unto Paphos, they found a\l"
    .string "certain sorcerer, a false prophet,\l"
    .string "a Jew, whose name was Barjesus:"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_7::
    .string "Which was with the deputy of the\n"
    .string "country, Sergius Paulus, a prudent\l"
    .string "man; who called for Barnabas and\l"
    .string "Saul, and desired to hear the word of\l"
    .string "God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_8::
    .string "But Elymas the sorcerer (for so is\n"
    .string "his name by interpretation)\l"
    .string "withstood them, seeking to turn away\l"
    .string "the deputy from the faith.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_9::
    .string "Then Saul, (who also is called\n"
    .string "Paul,) filled with the Holy Ghost,\l"
    .string "set his eyes on him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_10::
    .string "And said, O full of all subtilty\n"
    .string "and all mischief, thou child of the\l"
    .string "devil, thou enemy of all\l"
    .string "righteousness, wilt thou not cease\l"
    .string "to pervert the right ways of the\l"
    .string "Lord?"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_11::
    .string "And now, behold, the hand of the\n"
    .string "Lord is upon thee, and thou shalt be\l"
    .string "blind, not seeing the sun for a\l"
    .string "season. And immediately there fell\l"
    .string "on him a mist and a darkness; and he\l"
    .string "went about seeking some to lead him\l"
    .string "by the hand$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_12::
    .string "Then the deputy, when he saw what\n"
    .string "was done, believed, being astonished\l"
    .string "at the doctrine of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_13::
    .string "Now when Paul and his company\n"
    .string "loosed from Paphos, they came to\l"
    .string "Perga in Pamphylia: and John\l"
    .string "departing from them returned to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_14::
    .string "But when they departed from Perga,\n"
    .string "they came to Antioch in Pisidia, and\l"
    .string "went into the synagogue on the\l"
    .string "sabbath day, and sat down.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_15::
    .string "And after the reading of the law\n"
    .string "and the prophets the rulers of the\l"
    .string "synagogue sent unto them, saying, Ye\l"
    .string "men and brethren, if ye have any word\l"
    .string "of exhortation for the people, say\l"
    .string "on.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_16::
    .string "Then Paul stood up, and beckoning\n"
    .string "with his hand said, Men of Israel,\l"
    .string "and ye that fear God, give audience.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_17::
    .string "The God of this people of Israel\n"
    .string "chose our fathers, and exalted the\l"
    .string "people when they dwelt as\l"
    .string "strangers in the land of Egypt, and\l"
    .string "with an high arm brought he them out\l"
    .string "of it.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_18::
    .string "And about the time of forty years\n"
    .string "suffered he their manners in the\l"
    .string "wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_19::
    .string "And when he had destroyed seven\n"
    .string "nations in the land of Chanaan, he\l"
    .string "divided their land to them by lot.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_20::
    .string "And after that he gave unto them\n"
    .string "judges about the space of four\l"
    .string "hundred and fifty years, until\l"
    .string "Samuel the prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_21::
    .string "And afterward they desired a king:\n"
    .string "and God gave unto them Saul the son\l"
    .string "of Cis, a man of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, by the space of forty\l"
    .string "years.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_22::
    .string "And when he had removed him, he\n"
    .string "raised up unto them David to be\l"
    .string "their king; to whom also he gave\l"
    .string "their testimony, and said, I have\l"
    .string "found David the son of Jesse, a man\l"
    .string "after mine own heart, which shall\l"
    .string "fulfil all my will.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_23::
    .string "Of this man’s seed hath God\n"
    .string "according to his promise raised unto\l"
    .string "Israel a Saviour, Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_24::
    .string "When John had first preached before\n"
    .string "his coming the baptism of\l"
    .string "repentance to all the people of\l"
    .string "Israel$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_25::
    .string "And as John fulfilled his course,\n"
    .string "he said, Whom think ye that I am? I am\l"
    .string "not he. But, behold, there cometh one\l"
    .string "after me, whose shoes of his feet I am\l"
    .string "not worthy to loose.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_26::
    .string "Men and brethren, children of the\n"
    .string "stock of Abraham, and whosoever among\l"
    .string "you feareth God, to you is the word of\l"
    .string "this salvation sent.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_27::
    .string "For they that dwell at Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "and their rulers, because they knew\l"
    .string "him not, nor yet the voices of the\l"
    .string "prophets which are read every\l"
    .string "sabbath day, they have fulfilled\l"
    .string "them in condemning him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_28::
    .string "And though they found no cause of\n"
    .string "death in him, yet desired they\l"
    .string "Pilate that he should be slain.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_29::
    .string "And when they had fulfilled all\n"
    .string "that was written of him, they took\l"
    .string "him down from the tree, and laid him\l"
    .string "in a sepulchre.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_30::
    .string "But God raised him from the dead:"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_31::
    .string "And he was seen many days of them\n"
    .string "which came up with him from Galilee\l"
    .string "to Jerusalem, who are his witnesses\l"
    .string "unto the people$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_32::
    .string "And we declare unto you glad\n"
    .string "tidings, how that the promise which\l"
    .string "was made unto the fathers,"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_33::
    .string "God hath fulfilled the same unto\n"
    .string "us their children, in that he hath\l"
    .string "raised up Jesus again; as it is also\l"
    .string "written in the second psalm, Thou\l"
    .string "art my Son, this day have I begotten\l"
    .string "thee$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_34::
    .string "And as concerning that he raised him\n"
    .string "up from the dead, now no more to\l"
    .string "return to corruption, he said on\l"
    .string "this wise, I will give you the sure\l"
    .string "mercies of David.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_35::
    .string "Wherefore he saith also in another\n"
    .string "psalm, Thou shalt not suffer thine\l"
    .string "Holy One to see corruption.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_36::
    .string "For David, after he had served his\n"
    .string "own generation by the will of God,\l"
    .string "fell on sleep, and was laid unto\l"
    .string "his fathers, and saw corruption:"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_37::
    .string "But he, whom God raised again, saw\n"
    .string "no corruption$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_38::
    .string "Be it known unto you therefore, men\n"
    .string "and brethren, that through this man\l"
    .string "is preached unto you the forgiveness\l"
    .string "of sins:"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_39::
    .string "And by him all that believe are\n"
    .string "justified from all things, from\l"
    .string "which ye could not be justified by\l"
    .string "the law of Moses$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_40::
    .string "Beware therefore, lest that come\n"
    .string "upon you, which is spoken of in the\l"
    .string "prophets;"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_41::
    .string "Behold, ye despisers, and wonder,\n"
    .string "and perish: for I work a work in your\l"
    .string "days, a work which ye shall in no\l"
    .string "wise believe, though a man declare\l"
    .string "it unto you$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_42::
    .string "And when the Jews were gone out of\n"
    .string "the synagogue, the Gentiles besought\l"
    .string "that these words might be preached\l"
    .string "to them the next sabbath.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_43::
    .string "Now when the congregation was\n"
    .string "broken up, many of the Jews and\l"
    .string "religious proselytes followed\l"
    .string "Paul and Barnabas: who, speaking to\l"
    .string "them, persuaded them to continue in\l"
    .string "the grace of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_44::
    .string "And the next sabbath day came\n"
    .string "almost the whole city together to\l"
    .string "hear the word of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_45::
    .string "But when the Jews saw the\n"
    .string "multitudes, they were filled with\l"
    .string "envy, and spake against those things\l"
    .string "which were spoken by Paul,\l"
    .string "contradicting and blaspheming.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_46::
    .string "Then Paul and Barnabas waxed bold,\n"
    .string "and said, It was necessary that the\l"
    .string "word of God should first have been\l"
    .string "spoken to you: but seeing ye put it\l"
    .string "from you, and judge yourselves\l"
    .string "unworthy of everlasting life, lo,\l"
    .string "we turn to the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_47::
    .string "For so hath the Lord commanded us,\n"
    .string "saying, I have set thee to be a light\l"
    .string "of the Gentiles, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest be for salvation unto the\l"
    .string "ends of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_48::
    .string "And when the Gentiles heard this,\n"
    .string "they were glad, and glorified the\l"
    .string "word of the Lord: and as many as were\l"
    .string "ordained to eternal life believed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_49::
    .string "And the word of the Lord was\n"
    .string "published throughout all the\l"
    .string "region.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_50::
    .string "But the Jews stirred up the devout\n"
    .string "and honourable women, and the chief\l"
    .string "men of the city, and raised\l"
    .string "persecution against Paul and\l"
    .string "Barnabas, and expelled them out of\l"
    .string "their coasts.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_51::
    .string "But they shook off the dust of their\n"
    .string "feet against them, and came unto\l"
    .string "Iconium.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_13_52::
    .string "And the disciples were filled\n"
    .string "with joy, and with the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_1::
    .string "And it came to pass in Iconium, that\n"
    .string "they went both together into the\l"
    .string "synagogue of the Jews, and so spake,\l"
    .string "that a great multitude both of the\l"
    .string "Jews and also of the Greeks\l"
    .string "believed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_2::
    .string "But the unbelieving Jews stirred\n"
    .string "up the Gentiles, and made their\l"
    .string "minds evil affected against the\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_3::
    .string "Long time therefore abode they\n"
    .string "speaking boldly in the Lord, which\l"
    .string "gave testimony unto the word of his\l"
    .string "grace, and granted signs and wonders\l"
    .string "to be done by their hands.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_4::
    .string "But the multitude of the city was\n"
    .string "divided: and part held with the\l"
    .string "Jews, and part with the apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_5::
    .string "And when there was an assault made\n"
    .string "both of the Gentiles, and also of\l"
    .string "the Jews with their rulers, to use\l"
    .string "them despitefully, and to stone\l"
    .string "them,"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_6::
    .string "They were ware of it, and fled unto\n"
    .string "Lystra and Derbe, cities of Lycaonia,\l"
    .string "and unto the region that lieth round\l"
    .string "about:"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_7::
    .string "And there they preached the gospel$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_8::
    .string "And there sat a certain man at\n"
    .string "Lystra, impotent in his feet, being\l"
    .string "a cripple from his mother’s womb,\l"
    .string "who never had walked:"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_9::
    .string "The same heard Paul speak: who\n"
    .string "stedfastly beholding him, and\l"
    .string "perceiving that he had faith to be\l"
    .string "healed,"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_10::
    .string "Said with a loud voice, Stand\n"
    .string "upright on thy feet. And he leaped\l"
    .string "and walked$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_11::
    .string "And when the people saw what Paul\n"
    .string "had done, they lifted up their\l"
    .string "voices, saying in the speech of\l"
    .string "Lycaonia, The gods are come down to\l"
    .string "us in the likeness of men.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_12::
    .string "And they called Barnabas,\n"
    .string "Jupiter; and Paul, Mercurius,\l"
    .string "because he was the chief speaker.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_13::
    .string "Then the priest of Jupiter, which\n"
    .string "was before their city, brought oxen\l"
    .string "and garlands unto the gates, and\l"
    .string "would have done sacrifice with the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_14::
    .string "Which when the apostles, Barnabas\n"
    .string "and Paul, heard of, they rent their\l"
    .string "clothes, and ran in among the\l"
    .string "people, crying out,"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_15::
    .string "And saying, Sirs, why do ye these\n"
    .string "things? We also are men of like\l"
    .string "passions with you, and preach unto\l"
    .string "you that ye should turn from these\l"
    .string "vanities unto the living God, which\l"
    .string "made heaven, and earth, and the sea,\l"
    .string "and all things that are therein:"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_16::
    .string "Who in times past suffered all\n"
    .string "nations to walk in their own ways$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_17::
    .string "Nevertheless he left not himself\n"
    .string "without witness, in that he did good,\l"
    .string "and gave us rain from heaven, and\l"
    .string "fruitful seasons, filling our\l"
    .string "hearts with food and gladness.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_18::
    .string "And with these sayings scarce\n"
    .string "restrained they the people, that\l"
    .string "they had not done sacrifice unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_19::
    .string "And there came thither certain Jews\n"
    .string "from Antioch and Iconium, who\l"
    .string "persuaded the people, and having\l"
    .string "stoned Paul, drew him out of the\l"
    .string "city, supposing he had been dead.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_20::
    .string "Howbeit, as the disciples stood\n"
    .string "round about him, he rose up, and came\l"
    .string "into the city: and the next day he\l"
    .string "departed with Barnabas to Derbe.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_21::
    .string "And when they had preached the\n"
    .string "gospel to that city, and had taught\l"
    .string "many, they returned again to Lystra,\l"
    .string "and to Iconium, and Antioch,"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_22::
    .string "Confirming the souls of the\n"
    .string "disciples, and exhorting them to\l"
    .string "continue in the faith, and that we\l"
    .string "must through much tribulation enter\l"
    .string "into the kingdom of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_23::
    .string "And when they had ordained them\n"
    .string "elders in every church, and had\l"
    .string "prayed with fasting, they commended\l"
    .string "them to the Lord, on whom they\l"
    .string "believed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_24::
    .string "And after they had passed\n"
    .string "throughout Pisidia, they came to\l"
    .string "Pamphylia.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_25::
    .string "And when they had preached the word\n"
    .string "in Perga, they went down into\l"
    .string "Attalia:"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_26::
    .string "And thence sailed to Antioch, from\n"
    .string "whence they had been recommended to\l"
    .string "the grace of God for the work which\l"
    .string "they fulfilled$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_27::
    .string "And when they were come, and had\n"
    .string "gathered the church together, they\l"
    .string "rehearsed all that God had done\l"
    .string "with them, and how he had opened the\l"
    .string "door of faith unto the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_14_28::
    .string "And there they abode long time with\n"
    .string "the disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_1::
    .string "And certain men which came down from\n"
    .string "Judaea taught the brethren, and said,\l"
    .string "Except ye be circumcised after the\l"
    .string "manner of Moses, ye cannot be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_2::
    .string "When therefore Paul and Barnabas\n"
    .string "had no small dissension and\l"
    .string "disputation with them, they\l"
    .string "determined that Paul and Barnabas,\l"
    .string "and certain other of them, should go\l"
    .string "up to Jerusalem unto the apostles\l"
    .string "and elders about this question.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_3::
    .string "And being brought on their way by\n"
    .string "the church, they passed through\l"
    .string "Phenice and Samaria, declaring the\l"
    .string "conversion of the Gentiles: and they\l"
    .string "caused great joy unto all the\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_4::
    .string "And when they were come to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, they were received of the\l"
    .string "church, and of the apostles and\l"
    .string "elders, and they declared all\l"
    .string "things that God had done with them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_5::
    .string "But there rose up certain of the\n"
    .string "sect of the Pharisees which\l"
    .string "believed, saying, That it was\l"
    .string "needful to circumcise them, and to\l"
    .string "command them to keep the law of\l"
    .string "Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_6::
    .string "And the apostles and elders came\n"
    .string "together for to consider of this\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_7::
    .string "And when there had been much\n"
    .string "disputing, Peter rose up, and said\l"
    .string "unto them, Men and brethren, ye know\l"
    .string "how that a good while ago God made\l"
    .string "choice among us, that the Gentiles\l"
    .string "by my mouth should hear the word of\l"
    .string "the gospel, and believe.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_8::
    .string "And God, which knoweth the hearts,\n"
    .string "bare them witness, giving them the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost, even as he did unto us;"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_9::
    .string "And put no difference between us\n"
    .string "and them, purifying their hearts by\l"
    .string "faith$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_10::
    .string "Now therefore why tempt ye God, to\n"
    .string "put a yoke upon the neck of the\l"
    .string "disciples, which neither our\l"
    .string "fathers nor we were able to bear?"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_11::
    .string "But we believe that through the\n"
    .string "grace of the LORD Jesus Christ we\l"
    .string "shall be saved, even as they$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_12::
    .string "Then all the multitude kept\n"
    .string "silence, and gave audience to\l"
    .string "Barnabas and Paul, declaring what\l"
    .string "miracles and wonders God had wrought\l"
    .string "among the Gentiles by them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_13::
    .string "And after they had held their\n"
    .string "peace, James answered, saying, Men\l"
    .string "and brethren, hearken unto me:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_14::
    .string "Simeon hath declared how God at the\n"
    .string "first did visit the Gentiles, to\l"
    .string "take out of them a people for his\l"
    .string "name$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_15::
    .string "And to this agree the words of the\n"
    .string "prophets; as it is written,"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_16::
    .string "After this I will return, and\n"
    .string "will build again the tabernacle of\l"
    .string "David, which is fallen down; and I\l"
    .string "will build again the ruins thereof,\l"
    .string "and I will set it up:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_17::
    .string "That the residue of men might seek\n"
    .string "after the Lord, and all the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, upon whom my name is\l"
    .string "called, saith the Lord, who doeth\l"
    .string "all these things$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_18::
    .string "Known unto God are all his works\n"
    .string "from the beginning of the world.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_19::
    .string "Wherefore my sentence is, that we\n"
    .string "trouble not them, which from among\l"
    .string "the Gentiles are turned to God:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_20::
    .string "But that we write unto them, that\n"
    .string "they abstain from pollutions of\l"
    .string "idols, and from fornication, and\l"
    .string "from things strangled, and from\l"
    .string "blood$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_21::
    .string "For Moses of old time hath in every\n"
    .string "city them that preach him, being\l"
    .string "read in the synagogues every sabbath\l"
    .string "day.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_22::
    .string "Then pleased it the apostles and\n"
    .string "elders with the whole church, to\l"
    .string "send chosen men of their own company\l"
    .string "to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas;\l"
    .string "namely, Judas surnamed Barsabas and\l"
    .string "Silas, chief men among the brethren:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_23::
    .string "And they wrote letters by them\n"
    .string "after this manner; The apostles and\l"
    .string "elders and brethren send greeting\l"
    .string "unto the brethren which are of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles in Antioch and Syria and\l"
    .string "Cilicia$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_24::
    .string "Forasmuch as we have heard, that\n"
    .string "certain which went out from us have\l"
    .string "troubled you with words, subverting\l"
    .string "your souls, saying, Ye must be\l"
    .string "circumcised, and keep the law: to\l"
    .string "whom we gave no such commandment:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_25::
    .string "It seemed good unto us, being\n"
    .string "assembled with one accord, to send\l"
    .string "chosen men unto you with our beloved\l"
    .string "Barnabas and Paul,"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_26::
    .string "Men that have hazarded their lives\n"
    .string "for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_27::
    .string "We have sent therefore Judas and\n"
    .string "Silas, who shall also tell you\l"
    .string "the same things by mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_28::
    .string "For it seemed good to the Holy\n"
    .string "Ghost, and to us, to lay upon you no\l"
    .string "greater burden than these necessary\l"
    .string "things;"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_29::
    .string "That ye abstain from meats offered\n"
    .string "to idols, and from blood, and from\l"
    .string "things strangled, and from\l"
    .string "fornication: from which if ye keep\l"
    .string "yourselves, ye shall do well.\l"
    .string "Fare ye well$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_30::
    .string "So when they were dismissed, they\n"
    .string "came to Antioch: and when they had\l"
    .string "gathered the multitude together,\l"
    .string "they delivered the epistle:"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_31::
    .string "Which when they had read, they\n"
    .string "rejoiced for the consolation$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_32::
    .string "And Judas and Silas, being\n"
    .string "prophets also themselves, exhorted\l"
    .string "the brethren with many words, and\l"
    .string "confirmed them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_33::
    .string "And after they had tarried there a\n"
    .string "space, they were let go in peace\l"
    .string "from the brethren unto the apostles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_34::
    .string "Notwithstanding it pleased Silas\n"
    .string "to abide there still.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_35::
    .string "Paul also and Barnabas continued\n"
    .string "in Antioch, teaching and preaching\l"
    .string "the word of the Lord, with many\l"
    .string "others also.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_36::
    .string "And some days after Paul said unto\n"
    .string "Barnabas, Let us go again and visit\l"
    .string "our brethren in every city where we\l"
    .string "have preached the word of the LORD,\l"
    .string "and see how they do.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_37::
    .string "And Barnabas determined to take\n"
    .string "with them John, whose surname was\l"
    .string "Mark.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_38::
    .string "But Paul thought not good to take\n"
    .string "him with them, who departed from\l"
    .string "them from Pamphylia, and went not\l"
    .string "with them to the work.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_39::
    .string "And the contention was so sharp\n"
    .string "between them, that they departed\l"
    .string "asunder one from the other: and so\l"
    .string "Barnabas took Mark, and sailed unto\l"
    .string "Cyprus;"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_40::
    .string "And Paul chose Silas, and\n"
    .string "departed, being recommended by the\l"
    .string "brethren unto the grace of God$"
Bible_Text_Acts_15_41::
    .string "And he went through Syria and\n"
    .string "Cilicia, confirming the churches.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_1::
    .string "Then came he to Derbe and Lystra:\n"
    .string "and, behold, a certain disciple was\l"
    .string "there, named Timotheus, the son of a\l"
    .string "certain woman, which was a Jewess,\l"
    .string "and believed; but his father was a\l"
    .string "Greek:"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_2::
    .string "Which was well reported of by the\n"
    .string "brethren that were at Lystra and\l"
    .string "Iconium$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_3::
    .string "Him would Paul have to go forth\n"
    .string "with him; and took and circumcised\l"
    .string "him because of the Jews which were in\l"
    .string "those quarters: for they knew all\l"
    .string "that his father was a Greek.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_4::
    .string "And as they went through the cities,\n"
    .string "they delivered them the decrees for\l"
    .string "to keep, that were ordained of the\l"
    .string "apostles and elders which were at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_5::
    .string "And so were the churches\n"
    .string "established in the faith, and\l"
    .string "increased in number daily.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_6::
    .string "Now when they had gone throughout\n"
    .string "Phrygia and the region of Galatia,\l"
    .string "and were forbidden of the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "to preach the word in Asia,"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_7::
    .string "After they were come to Mysia, they\n"
    .string "assayed to go into Bithynia: but the\l"
    .string "Spirit suffered them not$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_8::
    .string "And they passing by Mysia came down\n"
    .string "to Troas.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_9::
    .string "And a vision appeared to Paul in\n"
    .string "the night; There stood a man of\l"
    .string "Macedonia, and prayed him, saying,\l"
    .string "Come over into Macedonia, and help\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_10::
    .string "And after he had seen the vision,\n"
    .string "immediately we endeavoured to go\l"
    .string "into Macedonia, assuredly gathering\l"
    .string "that the Lord had called us for to\l"
    .string "preach the gospel unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_11::
    .string "Therefore loosing from Troas, we\n"
    .string "came with a straight course to\l"
    .string "Samothracia, and the next day to\l"
    .string "Neapolis;"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_12::
    .string "And from thence to Philippi, which\n"
    .string "is the chief city of that part of\l"
    .string "Macedonia, and a colony: and we were\l"
    .string "in that city abiding certain days$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_13::
    .string "And on the sabbath we went out of\n"
    .string "the city by a river side, where\l"
    .string "prayer was wont to be made; and we sat\l"
    .string "down, and spake unto the women which\l"
    .string "resorted thither.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_14::
    .string "And a certain woman named Lydia, a\n"
    .string "seller of purple, of the city of\l"
    .string "Thyatira, which worshipped God,\l"
    .string "heard us: whose heart the Lord\l"
    .string "opened, that she attended unto the\l"
    .string "things which were spoken of Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_15::
    .string "And when she was baptized, and her\n"
    .string "household, she besought us, saying,\l"
    .string "If ye have judged me to be faithful\l"
    .string "to the Lord, come into my house, and\l"
    .string "abide there. And she constrained us.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_16::
    .string "And it came to pass, as we went to\n"
    .string "prayer, a certain damsel possessed\l"
    .string "with a spirit of divination met us,\l"
    .string "which brought her masters much gain\l"
    .string "by soothsaying:"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_17::
    .string "The same followed Paul and us, and\n"
    .string "cried, saying, These men are the\l"
    .string "servants of the most high God, which\l"
    .string "shew unto us the way of salvation$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_18::
    .string "And this did she many days. But\n"
    .string "Paul, being grieved, turned and said\l"
    .string "to the spirit, I command thee in the\l"
    .string "name of Jesus Christ to come out of\l"
    .string "her. And he came out the same hour.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_19::
    .string "And when her masters saw that the\n"
    .string "hope of their gains was gone, they\l"
    .string "caught Paul and Silas, and drew them\l"
    .string "into the marketplace unto the\l"
    .string "rulers,"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_20::
    .string "And brought them to the magistrates,\n"
    .string "saying, These men, being Jews, do\l"
    .string "exceedingly trouble our city,"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_21::
    .string "And teach customs, which are not\n"
    .string "lawful for us to receive, neither to\l"
    .string "observe, being Romans$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_22::
    .string "And the multitude rose up together\n"
    .string "against them: and the magistrates\l"
    .string "rent off their clothes, and\l"
    .string "commanded to beat them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_23::
    .string "And when they had laid many\n"
    .string "stripes upon them, they cast them\l"
    .string "into prison, charging the jailor to\l"
    .string "keep them safely:"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_24::
    .string "Who, having received such a charge,\n"
    .string "thrust them into the inner prison,\l"
    .string "and made their feet fast in the stocks$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_25::
    .string "And at midnight Paul and Silas\n"
    .string "prayed, and sang praises unto God:\l"
    .string "and the prisoners heard them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_26::
    .string "And suddenly there was a great\n"
    .string "earthquake, so that the foundations\l"
    .string "of the prison were shaken: and\l"
    .string "immediately all the doors were\l"
    .string "opened, and every one’s bands were\l"
    .string "loosed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_27::
    .string "And the keeper of the prison\n"
    .string "awaking out of his sleep, and seeing\l"
    .string "the prison doors open, he drew out\l"
    .string "his sword, and would have killed\l"
    .string "himself, supposing that the\l"
    .string "prisoners had been fled.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_28::
    .string "But Paul cried with a loud voice,\n"
    .string "saying, Do thyself no harm: for we\l"
    .string "are all here.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_29::
    .string "Then he called for a light, and\n"
    .string "sprang in, and came trembling, and\l"
    .string "fell down before Paul and Silas,"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_30::
    .string "And brought them out, and said,\n"
    .string "Sirs, what must I do to be saved?"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_31::
    .string "And they said, Believe on the Lord\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be\l"
    .string "saved, and thy house$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_32::
    .string "And they spake unto him the word of\n"
    .string "the Lord, and to all that were in\l"
    .string "his house.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_33::
    .string "And he took them the same hour of\n"
    .string "the night, and washed their stripes;\l"
    .string "and was baptized, he and all his,\l"
    .string "straightway.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_34::
    .string "And when he had brought them into\n"
    .string "his house, he set meat before them,\l"
    .string "and rejoiced, believing in God with\l"
    .string "all his house.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_35::
    .string "And when it was day, the magistrates\n"
    .string "sent the serjeants, saying, Let those\l"
    .string "men go.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_36::
    .string "And the keeper of the prison told\n"
    .string "this saying to Paul, The magistrates\l"
    .string "have sent to let you go: now\l"
    .string "therefore depart, and go in peace.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_37::
    .string "But Paul said unto them, They have\n"
    .string "beaten us openly uncondemned, being\l"
    .string "Romans, and have cast us into\l"
    .string "prison; and now do they thrust us out\l"
    .string "privily? nay verily; but let them\l"
    .string "come themselves and fetch us out.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_38::
    .string "And the serjeants told these words\n"
    .string "unto the magistrates: and they\l"
    .string "feared, when they heard that they\l"
    .string "were Romans.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_39::
    .string "And they came and besought them, and\n"
    .string "brought them out, and desired them to\l"
    .string "depart out of the city.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_16_40::
    .string "And they went out of the prison, and\n"
    .string "entered into the house of Lydia: and\l"
    .string "when they had seen the brethren, they\l"
    .string "comforted them, and departed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_1::
    .string "Now when they had passed through\n"
    .string "Amphipolis and Apollonia, they\l"
    .string "came to Thessalonica, where was a\l"
    .string "synagogue of the Jews:"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_2::
    .string "And Paul, as his manner was, went in\n"
    .string "unto them, and three sabbath days\l"
    .string "reasoned with them out of the\l"
    .string "scriptures,"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_3::
    .string "Opening and alleging, that Christ\n"
    .string "must needs have suffered, and risen\l"
    .string "again from the dead; and that this\l"
    .string "Jesus, whom I preach unto you, is\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_4::
    .string "And some of them believed, and\n"
    .string "consorted with Paul and Silas; and\l"
    .string "of the devout Greeks a great\l"
    .string "multitude, and of the chief women\l"
    .string "not a few.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_5::
    .string "But the Jews which believed not,\n"
    .string "moved with envy, took unto them\l"
    .string "certain lewd fellows of the baser\l"
    .string "sort, and gathered a company, and\l"
    .string "set all the city on an uproar, and\l"
    .string "assaulted the house of Jason, and\l"
    .string "sought to bring them out to the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_6::
    .string "And when they found them not, they\n"
    .string "drew Jason and certain brethren unto\l"
    .string "the rulers of the city, crying,\l"
    .string "These that have turned the world\l"
    .string "upside down are come hither also;"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_7::
    .string "Whom Jason hath received: and these\n"
    .string "all do contrary to the decrees of\l"
    .string "Caesar, saying that there is another\l"
    .string "king, one Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_8::
    .string "And they troubled the people and\n"
    .string "the rulers of the city, when they\l"
    .string "heard these things.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_9::
    .string "And when they had taken security of\n"
    .string "Jason, and of the other, they let\l"
    .string "them go.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_10::
    .string "And the brethren immediately sent\n"
    .string "away Paul and Silas by night unto\l"
    .string "Berea: who coming thither went into\l"
    .string "the synagogue of the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_11::
    .string "These were more noble than those in\n"
    .string "Thessalonica, in that they received\l"
    .string "the word with all readiness of mind,\l"
    .string "and searched the scriptures daily,\l"
    .string "whether those things were so.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_12::
    .string "Therefore many of them believed;\n"
    .string "also of honourable women which were\l"
    .string "Greeks, and of men, not a few.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_13::
    .string "But when the Jews of Thessalonica\n"
    .string "had knowledge that the word of God\l"
    .string "was preached of Paul at Berea, they\l"
    .string "came thither also, and stirred up\l"
    .string "the people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_14::
    .string "And then immediately the brethren\n"
    .string "sent away Paul to go as it were to\l"
    .string "the sea: but Silas and Timotheus\l"
    .string "abode there still.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_15::
    .string "And they that conducted Paul\n"
    .string "brought him unto Athens: and\l"
    .string "receiving a commandment unto Silas\l"
    .string "and Timotheus for to come to him with\l"
    .string "all speed, they departed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_16::
    .string "Now while Paul waited for them at\n"
    .string "Athens, his spirit was stirred in\l"
    .string "him, when he saw the city wholly\l"
    .string "given to idolatry.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_17::
    .string "Therefore disputed he in the\n"
    .string "synagogue with the Jews, and with the\l"
    .string "devout persons, and in the market\l"
    .string "daily with them that met with him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_18::
    .string "Then certain philosophers of the\n"
    .string "Epicureans, and of the Stoicks,\l"
    .string "encountered him. And some said, What\l"
    .string "will this babbler say? other some,\l"
    .string "He seemeth to be a setter forth of\l"
    .string "strange gods: because he preached\l"
    .string "unto them Jesus, and the\l"
    .string "resurrection.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_19::
    .string "And they took him, and brought him\n"
    .string "unto Areopagus, saying, May we know\l"
    .string "what this new doctrine, whereof thou\l"
    .string "speakest, is?"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_20::
    .string "For thou bringest certain strange\n"
    .string "things to our ears: we would know\l"
    .string "therefore what these things mean$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_21::
    .string "(For all the Athenians and\n"
    .string "strangers which were there spent\l"
    .string "their time in nothing else, but\l"
    .string "either to tell, or to hear some new\l"
    .string "thing.)"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_22::
    .string "Then Paul stood in the midst of\n"
    .string "Mars’ hill, and said, Ye men of\l"
    .string "Athens, I perceive that in all\l"
    .string "things ye are too superstitious$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_23::
    .string "For as I passed by, and beheld your\n"
    .string "devotions, I found an altar with\l"
    .string "this inscription, TO THE UNKNOWN\l"
    .string "GOD. Whom therefore ye ignorantly\l"
    .string "worship, him declare I unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_24::
    .string "God that made the world and all\n"
    .string "things therein, seeing that he is\l"
    .string "Lord of heaven and earth, dwelleth\l"
    .string "not in temples made with hands;"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_25::
    .string "Neither is worshipped with men’s\n"
    .string "hands, as though he needed any thing,\l"
    .string "seeing he giveth to all life, and\l"
    .string "breath, and all things;"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_26::
    .string "And hath made of one blood all\n"
    .string "nations of men for to dwell on all\l"
    .string "the face of the earth, and hath\l"
    .string "determined the times before\l"
    .string "appointed, and the bounds of their\l"
    .string "habitation;"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_27::
    .string "That they should seek the Lord, if\n"
    .string "haply they might feel after him,\l"
    .string "and find him, though he be not far\l"
    .string "from every one of us:"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_28::
    .string "For in him we live, and move, and\n"
    .string "have our being; as certain also of\l"
    .string "your own poets have said, For we are\l"
    .string "also his offspring$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_29::
    .string "Forasmuch then as we are the\n"
    .string "offspring of God, we ought not to\l"
    .string "think that the Godhead is like unto\l"
    .string "gold, or silver, or stone, graven by\l"
    .string "art and man’s device.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_30::
    .string "And the times of this ignorance God\n"
    .string "winked at; but now commandeth all\l"
    .string "men every where to repent:"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_31::
    .string "Because he hath appointed a day, in\n"
    .string "the which he will judge the world\l"
    .string "in righteousness by that man whom he\l"
    .string "hath ordained; whereof he hath given\l"
    .string "assurance unto all men, in that he\l"
    .string "hath raised him from the dead$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_32::
    .string "And when they heard of the\n"
    .string "resurrection of the dead, some\l"
    .string "mocked: and others said, We will\l"
    .string "hear thee again of this matter.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_33::
    .string "So Paul departed from among them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_17_34::
    .string "Howbeit certain men clave unto him,\n"
    .string "and believed: among the which was\l"
    .string "Dionysius the Areopagite, and a\l"
    .string "woman named Damaris, and others with\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_1::
    .string "After these things Paul departed\n"
    .string "from Athens, and came to Corinth;"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_2::
    .string "And found a certain Jew named\n"
    .string "Aquila, born in Pontus, lately come\l"
    .string "from Italy, with his wife\l"
    .string "Priscilla; (because that Claudius\l"
    .string "had commanded all Jews to depart\l"
    .string "from Rome:) and came unto them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_3::
    .string "And because he was of the same\n"
    .string "craft, he abode with them, and\l"
    .string "wrought: for by their occupation\l"
    .string "they were tentmakers.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_4::
    .string "And he reasoned in the synagogue\n"
    .string "every sabbath, and persuaded the\l"
    .string "Jews and the Greeks.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_5::
    .string "And when Silas and Timotheus were\n"
    .string "come from Macedonia, Paul was\l"
    .string "pressed in the spirit, and testified\l"
    .string "to the Jews that Jesus was Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_6::
    .string "And when they opposed themselves,\n"
    .string "and blasphemed, he shook his\l"
    .string "raiment, and said unto them, Your\l"
    .string "blood be upon your own heads; I am\l"
    .string "clean; from henceforth I will go\l"
    .string "unto the Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_7::
    .string "And he departed thence, and entered\n"
    .string "into a certain man’s house, named\l"
    .string "Justus, one that worshipped God,\l"
    .string "whose house joined hard to the\l"
    .string "synagogue.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_8::
    .string "And Crispus, the chief ruler of the\n"
    .string "synagogue, believed on the Lord with\l"
    .string "all his house; and many of the\l"
    .string "Corinthians hearing believed, and\l"
    .string "were baptized.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_9::
    .string "Then spake the Lord to Paul in the\n"
    .string "night by a vision, Be not afraid, but\l"
    .string "speak, and hold not thy peace:"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_10::
    .string "For I am with thee, and no man\n"
    .string "shall set on thee to hurt thee: for\l"
    .string "I have much people in this city$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_11::
    .string "And he continued there a year and\n"
    .string "six months, teaching the word of God\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_12::
    .string "And when Gallio was the deputy of\n"
    .string "Achaia, the Jews made insurrection\l"
    .string "with one accord against Paul, and\l"
    .string "brought him to the judgment seat,"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_13::
    .string "Saying, This fellow persuadeth\n"
    .string "men to worship God contrary to the\l"
    .string "law$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_14::
    .string "And when Paul was now about to open\n"
    .string "his mouth, Gallio said unto the\l"
    .string "Jews, If it were a matter of wrong or\l"
    .string "wicked lewdness, O ye Jews, reason\l"
    .string "would that I should bear with you:"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_15::
    .string "But if it be a question of words and\n"
    .string "names, and of your law, look ye to\l"
    .string "it; for I will be no judge of such\l"
    .string "matters$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_16::
    .string "And he drave them from the judgment\n"
    .string "seat.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_17::
    .string "Then all the Greeks took\n"
    .string "Sosthenes, the chief ruler of the\l"
    .string "synagogue, and beat him before the\l"
    .string "judgment seat. And Gallio cared for\l"
    .string "none of those things.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_18::
    .string "And Paul after this tarried there\n"
    .string "yet a good while, and then took his\l"
    .string "leave of the brethren, and sailed\l"
    .string "thence into Syria, and with him\l"
    .string "Priscilla and Aquila; having shorn\l"
    .string "his head in Cenchrea: for he had a\l"
    .string "vow.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_19::
    .string "And he came to Ephesus, and left\n"
    .string "them there: but he himself entered\l"
    .string "into the synagogue, and reasoned with\l"
    .string "the Jews.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_20::
    .string "When they desired him to tarry\n"
    .string "longer time with them, he consented\l"
    .string "not;"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_21::
    .string "But bade them farewell, saying, I\n"
    .string "must by all means keep this feast\l"
    .string "that cometh in Jerusalem: but I\l"
    .string "will return again unto you, if God\l"
    .string "will. And he sailed from Ephesus$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_22::
    .string "And when he had landed at Caesarea,\n"
    .string "and gone up, and saluted the church,\l"
    .string "he went down to Antioch.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_23::
    .string "And after he had spent some time\n"
    .string "there, he departed, and went over\l"
    .string "all the country of Galatia and\l"
    .string "Phrygia in order, strengthening all\l"
    .string "the disciples.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_24::
    .string "And a certain Jew named Apollos,\n"
    .string "born at Alexandria, an eloquent\l"
    .string "man, and mighty in the scriptures,\l"
    .string "came to Ephesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_25::
    .string "This man was instructed in the way\n"
    .string "of the Lord; and being fervent in the\l"
    .string "spirit, he spake and taught\l"
    .string "diligently the things of the Lord,\l"
    .string "knowing only the baptism of John.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_26::
    .string "And he began to speak boldly in\n"
    .string "the synagogue: whom when Aquila and\l"
    .string "Priscilla had heard, they took him\l"
    .string "unto them, and expounded unto him\l"
    .string "the way of God more perfectly.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_27::
    .string "And when he was disposed to pass\n"
    .string "into Achaia, the brethren wrote,\l"
    .string "exhorting the disciples to receive\l"
    .string "him: who, when he was come, helped\l"
    .string "them much which had believed through\l"
    .string "grace:"
Bible_Text_Acts_18_28::
    .string "For he mightily convinced the Jews,\n"
    .string "and that publickly, shewing by the\l"
    .string "scriptures that Jesus was Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, while\n"
    .string "Apollos was at Corinth, Paul\l"
    .string "having passed through the upper\l"
    .string "coasts came to Ephesus: and finding\l"
    .string "certain disciples,"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_2::
    .string "He said unto them, Have ye received\n"
    .string "the Holy Ghost since ye believed?\l"
    .string "And they said unto him, We have not so\l"
    .string "much as heard whether there be any\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_3::
    .string "And he said unto them, Unto what\n"
    .string "then were ye baptized? And they\l"
    .string "said, Unto John’s baptism.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_4::
    .string "Then said Paul, John verily\n"
    .string "baptized with the baptism of\l"
    .string "repentance, saying unto the\l"
    .string "people, that they should believe\l"
    .string "on him which should come after him,\l"
    .string "that is, on Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_5::
    .string "When they heard this, they were\n"
    .string "baptized in the name of the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_6::
    .string "And when Paul had laid his hands\n"
    .string "upon them, the Holy Ghost came on\l"
    .string "them; and they spake with tongues,\l"
    .string "and prophesied.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_7::
    .string "And all the men were about twelve.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_8::
    .string "And he went into the synagogue, and\n"
    .string "spake boldly for the space of\l"
    .string "three months, disputing and\l"
    .string "persuading the things concerning the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_9::
    .string "But when divers were hardened, and\n"
    .string "believed not, but spake evil of\l"
    .string "that way before the multitude, he\l"
    .string "departed from them, and separated\l"
    .string "the disciples, disputing daily in\l"
    .string "the school of one Tyrannus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_10::
    .string "And this continued by the space of\n"
    .string "two years; so that all they which\l"
    .string "dwelt in Asia heard the word of the\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus, both Jews and Greeks.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_11::
    .string "And God wrought special miracles\n"
    .string "by the hands of Paul:"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_12::
    .string "So that from his body were brought\n"
    .string "unto the sick handkerchiefs or\l"
    .string "aprons, and the diseases departed\l"
    .string "from them, and the evil spirits went\l"
    .string "out of them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_13::
    .string "Then certain of the vagabond Jews,\n"
    .string "exorcists, took upon them to call\l"
    .string "over them which had evil spirits\l"
    .string "the name of the LORD Jesus, saying,\l"
    .string "We adjure you by Jesus whom Paul\l"
    .string "preacheth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_14::
    .string "And there were seven sons of one\n"
    .string "Sceva, a Jew, and chief of the\l"
    .string "priests, which did so.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_15::
    .string "And the evil spirit answered and\n"
    .string "said, Jesus I know, and Paul I know;\l"
    .string "but who are ye?"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_16::
    .string "And the man in whom the evil spirit\n"
    .string "was leaped on them, and overcame\l"
    .string "them, and prevailed against them,\l"
    .string "so that they fled out of that house\l"
    .string "naked and wounded$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_17::
    .string "And this was known to all the Jews\n"
    .string "and Greeks also dwelling at\l"
    .string "Ephesus; and fear fell on them\l"
    .string "all, and the name of the Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "was magnified.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_18::
    .string "And many that believed came, and\n"
    .string "confessed, and shewed their deeds.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_19::
    .string "Many of them also which used\n"
    .string "curious arts brought their books\l"
    .string "together, and burned them before\l"
    .string "all men: and they counted the price\l"
    .string "of them, and found it fifty thousand\l"
    .string "pieces of silver.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_20::
    .string "So mightily grew the word of God\n"
    .string "and prevailed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_21::
    .string "After these things were ended, Paul\n"
    .string "purposed in the spirit, when he had\l"
    .string "passed through Macedonia and Achaia,\l"
    .string "to go to Jerusalem, saying, After I\l"
    .string "have been there, I must also see\l"
    .string "Rome.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_22::
    .string "So he sent into Macedonia two of\n"
    .string "them that ministered unto him,\l"
    .string "Timotheus and Erastus; but he\l"
    .string "himself stayed in Asia for a season.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_23::
    .string "And the same time there arose no\n"
    .string "small stir about that way.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_24::
    .string "For a certain man named Demetrius, a\n"
    .string "silversmith, which made silver\l"
    .string "shrines for Diana, brought no small\l"
    .string "gain unto the craftsmen;"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_25::
    .string "Whom he called together with the\n"
    .string "workmen of like occupation, and\l"
    .string "said, Sirs, ye know that by this\l"
    .string "craft we have our wealth$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_26::
    .string "Moreover ye see and hear, that not\n"
    .string "alone at Ephesus, but almost\l"
    .string "throughout all Asia, this Paul hath\l"
    .string "persuaded and turned away much\l"
    .string "people, saying that they be no gods,\l"
    .string "which are made with hands:"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_27::
    .string "So that not only this our craft is\n"
    .string "in danger to be set at nought; but\l"
    .string "also that the temple of the great\l"
    .string "goddess Diana should be despised,\l"
    .string "and her magnificence should be\l"
    .string "destroyed, whom all Asia and the\l"
    .string "world worshippeth$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_28::
    .string "And when they heard these sayings,\n"
    .string "they were full of wrath, and cried\l"
    .string "out, saying, Great is Diana of the\l"
    .string "Ephesians.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_29::
    .string "And the whole city was filled with\n"
    .string "confusion: and having caught Gaius\l"
    .string "and Aristarchus, men of Macedonia,\l"
    .string "Paul’s companions in travel, they\l"
    .string "rushed with one accord into the\l"
    .string "theatre.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_30::
    .string "And when Paul would have entered\n"
    .string "in unto the people, the disciples\l"
    .string "suffered him not.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_31::
    .string "And certain of the chief of Asia,\n"
    .string "which were his friends, sent unto\l"
    .string "him, desiring him that he would not\l"
    .string "adventure himself into the theatre.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_32::
    .string "Some therefore cried one thing, and\n"
    .string "some another: for the assembly was\l"
    .string "confused: and the more part knew not\l"
    .string "wherefore they were come together.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_33::
    .string "And they drew Alexander out of the\n"
    .string "multitude, the Jews putting him\l"
    .string "forward. And Alexander beckoned with\l"
    .string "the hand, and would have made his\l"
    .string "defence unto the people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_34::
    .string "But when they knew that he was a Jew,\n"
    .string "all with one voice about the space\l"
    .string "of two hours cried out, Great is\l"
    .string "Diana of the Ephesians.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_35::
    .string "And when the townclerk had\n"
    .string "appeased the people, he said, Ye\l"
    .string "men of Ephesus, what man is there\l"
    .string "that knoweth not how that the city of\l"
    .string "the Ephesians is a worshipper of\l"
    .string "the great goddess Diana, and of the\l"
    .string "image which fell down from Jupiter?"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_36::
    .string "Seeing then that these things\n"
    .string "cannot be spoken against, ye ought\l"
    .string "to be quiet, and to do nothing rashly$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_37::
    .string "For ye have brought hither these\n"
    .string "men, which are neither robbers of\l"
    .string "churches, nor yet blasphemers of\l"
    .string "your goddess.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_38::
    .string "Wherefore if Demetrius, and the\n"
    .string "craftsmen which are with him, have a\l"
    .string "matter against any man, the law is\l"
    .string "open, and there are deputies: let\l"
    .string "them implead one another.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_39::
    .string "But if ye enquire any thing\n"
    .string "concerning other matters, it shall\l"
    .string "be determined in a lawful assembly.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_40::
    .string "For we are in danger to be called\n"
    .string "in question for this day’s uproar,\l"
    .string "there being no cause whereby we may\l"
    .string "give an account of this concourse.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_19_41::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, he\n"
    .string "dismissed the assembly.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_1::
    .string "And after the uproar was ceased,\n"
    .string "Paul called unto him the\l"
    .string "disciples, and embraced them, and\l"
    .string "departed for to go into Macedonia.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_2::
    .string "And when he had gone over those\n"
    .string "parts, and had given them much\l"
    .string "exhortation, he came into Greece,"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_3::
    .string "And there abode three months. And\n"
    .string "when the Jews laid wait for him, as\l"
    .string "he was about to sail into Syria, he\l"
    .string "purposed to return through Macedonia$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_4::
    .string "And there accompanied him into Asia\n"
    .string "Sopater of Berea; and of the\l"
    .string "Thessalonians, Aristarchus and\l"
    .string "Secundus; and Gaius of Derbe, and\l"
    .string "Timotheus; and of Asia, Tychicus and\l"
    .string "Trophimus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_5::
    .string "These going before tarried for us at\n"
    .string "Troas.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_6::
    .string "And we sailed away from Philippi\n"
    .string "after the days of unleavened bread,\l"
    .string "and came unto them to Troas in five\l"
    .string "days; where we abode seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_7::
    .string "And upon the first day of the week,\n"
    .string "when the disciples came together to\l"
    .string "break bread, Paul preached unto\l"
    .string "them, ready to depart on the morrow;\l"
    .string "and continued his speech until\l"
    .string "midnight.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_8::
    .string "And there were many lights in the\n"
    .string "upper chamber, where they were\l"
    .string "gathered together.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_9::
    .string "And there sat in a window a certain\n"
    .string "young man named Eutychus, being\l"
    .string "fallen into a deep sleep: and as\l"
    .string "Paul was long preaching, he sunk\l"
    .string "down with sleep, and fell down\l"
    .string "from the third loft, and was taken\l"
    .string "up dead.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_10::
    .string "And Paul went down, and fell on\n"
    .string "him, and embracing him said, Trouble\l"
    .string "not yourselves; for his life is in\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_11::
    .string "When he therefore was come up\n"
    .string "again, and had broken bread, and\l"
    .string "eaten, and talked a long while,\l"
    .string "even till break of day, so he\l"
    .string "departed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_12::
    .string "And they brought the young man\n"
    .string "alive, and were not a little\l"
    .string "comforted.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_13::
    .string "And we went before to ship, and\n"
    .string "sailed unto Assos, there intending\l"
    .string "to take in Paul: for so had he\l"
    .string "appointed, minding himself to go\l"
    .string "afoot.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_14::
    .string "And when he met with us at Assos, we\n"
    .string "took him in, and came to Mitylene.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_15::
    .string "And we sailed thence, and came the\n"
    .string "next day over against Chios; and the\l"
    .string "next day we arrived at Samos, and\l"
    .string "tarried at Trogyllium; and the next\l"
    .string "day we came to Miletus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_16::
    .string "For Paul had determined to sail by\n"
    .string "Ephesus, because he would not spend\l"
    .string "the time in Asia: for he hasted, if it\l"
    .string "were possible for him, to be at\l"
    .string "Jerusalem the day of Pentecost.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_17::
    .string "And from Miletus he sent to\n"
    .string "Ephesus, and called the elders of\l"
    .string "the church.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_18::
    .string "And when they were come to him, he\n"
    .string "said unto them, Ye know, from the\l"
    .string "first day that I came into Asia,\l"
    .string "after what manner I have been with\l"
    .string "you at all seasons,"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_19::
    .string "Serving the LORD with all\n"
    .string "humility of mind, and with many\l"
    .string "tears, and temptations, which\l"
    .string "befell me by the lying in wait of\l"
    .string "the Jews:"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_20::
    .string "And how I kept back nothing that\n"
    .string "was profitable unto you, but have\l"
    .string "shewed you, and have taught you\l"
    .string "publickly, and from house to house,"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_21::
    .string "Testifying both to the Jews, and\n"
    .string "also to the Greeks, repentance\l"
    .string "toward God, and faith toward our Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_22::
    .string "And now, behold, I go bound in the\n"
    .string "spirit unto Jerusalem, not knowing\l"
    .string "the things that shall befall me\l"
    .string "there:"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_23::
    .string "Save that the Holy Ghost witnesseth\n"
    .string "in every city, saying that bonds and\l"
    .string "afflictions abide me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_24::
    .string "But none of these things move me,\n"
    .string "neither count I my life dear unto\l"
    .string "myself, so that I might finish my\l"
    .string "course with joy, and the ministry,\l"
    .string "which I have received of the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus, to testify the gospel of the\l"
    .string "grace of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_25::
    .string "And now, behold, I know that ye\n"
    .string "all, among whom I have gone\l"
    .string "preaching the kingdom of God, shall\l"
    .string "see my face no more.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_26::
    .string "Wherefore I take you to record this\n"
    .string "day, that I am pure from the blood\l"
    .string "of all men.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_27::
    .string "For I have not shunned to declare\n"
    .string "unto you all the counsel of God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_28::
    .string "Take heed therefore unto\n"
    .string "yourselves, and to all the flock,\l"
    .string "over the which the Holy Ghost hath\l"
    .string "made you overseers, to feed the\l"
    .string "church of God, which he hath\l"
    .string "purchased with his own blood.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_29::
    .string "For I know this, that after my\n"
    .string "departing shall grievous wolves\l"
    .string "enter in among you, not sparing the\l"
    .string "flock.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_30::
    .string "Also of your own selves shall men\n"
    .string "arise, speaking perverse things, to\l"
    .string "draw away disciples after them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_31::
    .string "Therefore watch, and remember, that\n"
    .string "by the space of three years I ceased\l"
    .string "not to warn every one night and day\l"
    .string "with tears.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_32::
    .string "And now, brethren, I commend you to\n"
    .string "God, and to the word of his grace,\l"
    .string "which is able to build you up, and\l"
    .string "to give you an inheritance among\l"
    .string "all them which are sanctified.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_33::
    .string "I have coveted no man’s silver, or\n"
    .string "gold, or apparel.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_34::
    .string "Yea, ye yourselves know, that these\n"
    .string "hands have ministered unto my\l"
    .string "necessities, and to them that were\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_35::
    .string "I have shewed you all things, how\n"
    .string "that so labouring ye ought to\l"
    .string "support the weak, and to remember\l"
    .string "the words of the Lord Jesus, how he\l"
    .string "said, It is more blessed to give than\l"
    .string "to receive.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_36::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, he\n"
    .string "kneeled down, and prayed with them\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_37::
    .string "And they all wept sore, and fell\n"
    .string "on Paul’s neck, and kissed him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_20_38::
    .string "Sorrowing most of all for the\n"
    .string "words which he spake, that they\l"
    .string "should see his face no more. And they\l"
    .string "accompanied him unto the ship$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_1::
    .string "And it came to pass, that after we\n"
    .string "were gotten from them, and had\l"
    .string "launched, we came with a straight\l"
    .string "course unto Coos, and the day\l"
    .string "following unto Rhodes, and from\l"
    .string "thence unto Patara:"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_2::
    .string "And finding a ship sailing over\n"
    .string "unto Phenicia, we went aboard, and\l"
    .string "set forth$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_3::
    .string "Now when we had discovered Cyprus,\n"
    .string "we left it on the left hand, and\l"
    .string "sailed into Syria, and landed at\l"
    .string "Tyre: for there the ship was to\l"
    .string "unlade her burden.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_4::
    .string "And finding disciples, we tarried\n"
    .string "there seven days: who said to Paul\l"
    .string "through the Spirit, that he should\l"
    .string "not go up to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_5::
    .string "And when we had accomplished those\n"
    .string "days, we departed and went our way;\l"
    .string "and they all brought us on our way,\l"
    .string "with wives and children, till we\l"
    .string "were out of the city: and we kneeled\l"
    .string "down on the shore, and prayed.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_6::
    .string "And when we had taken our leave one\n"
    .string "of another, we took ship; and they\l"
    .string "returned home again.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_7::
    .string "And when we had finished our course\n"
    .string "from Tyre, we came to Ptolemais, and\l"
    .string "saluted the brethren, and abode with\l"
    .string "them one day.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_8::
    .string "And the next day we that were of\n"
    .string "Paul’s company departed, and came\l"
    .string "unto Caesarea: and we entered into\l"
    .string "the house of Philip the evangelist,\l"
    .string "which was one of the seven; and abode\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_9::
    .string "And the same man had four daughters,\n"
    .string "virgins, which did prophesy.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_10::
    .string "And as we tarried there many days,\n"
    .string "there came down from Judaea a certain\l"
    .string "prophet, named Agabus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_11::
    .string "And when he was come unto us, he took\n"
    .string "Paul’s girdle, and bound his own\l"
    .string "hands and feet, and said, Thus saith\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost, So shall the Jews\l"
    .string "at Jerusalem bind the man that\l"
    .string "owneth this girdle, and shall\l"
    .string "deliver him into the hands of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_12::
    .string "And when we heard these things, both\n"
    .string "we, and they of that place, besought\l"
    .string "him not to go up to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_13::
    .string "Then Paul answered, What mean ye to\n"
    .string "weep and to break mine heart? for I\l"
    .string "am ready not to be bound only, but\l"
    .string "also to die at Jerusalem for the\l"
    .string "name of the Lord Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_14::
    .string "And when he would not be persuaded,\n"
    .string "we ceased, saying, The will of the\l"
    .string "Lord be done.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_15::
    .string "And after those days we took up our\n"
    .string "carriages, and went up to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_16::
    .string "There went with us also certain of\n"
    .string "the disciples of Caesarea, and\l"
    .string "brought with them one Mnason of\l"
    .string "Cyprus, an old disciple, with whom\l"
    .string "we should lodge.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_17::
    .string "And when we were come to Jerusalem,\n"
    .string "the brethren received us gladly.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_18::
    .string "And the day following Paul went in\n"
    .string "with us unto James; and all the\l"
    .string "elders were present.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_19::
    .string "And when he had saluted them, he\n"
    .string "declared particularly what things\l"
    .string "God had wrought among the Gentiles\l"
    .string "by his ministry.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_20::
    .string "And when they heard it, they\n"
    .string "glorified the Lord, and said unto\l"
    .string "him, Thou seest, brother, how many\l"
    .string "thousands of Jews there are which\l"
    .string "believe; and they are all zealous\l"
    .string "of the law:"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_21::
    .string "And they are informed of thee, that\n"
    .string "thou teachest all the Jews which\l"
    .string "are among the Gentiles to forsake\l"
    .string "Moses, saying that they ought not to\l"
    .string "circumcise their children, neither\l"
    .string "to walk after the customs$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_22::
    .string "What is it therefore? the multitude\n"
    .string "must needs come together: for they\l"
    .string "will hear that thou art come.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_23::
    .string "Do therefore this that we say to\n"
    .string "thee: We have four men which have a\l"
    .string "vow on them;"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_24::
    .string "Them take, and purify thyself with\n"
    .string "them, and be at charges with them,\l"
    .string "that they may shave their heads: and\l"
    .string "all may know that those things,\l"
    .string "whereof they were informed\l"
    .string "concerning thee, are nothing; but\l"
    .string "that thou thyself also walkest\l"
    .string "orderly, and keepest the law$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_25::
    .string "As touching the Gentiles which\n"
    .string "believe, we have written and\l"
    .string "concluded that they observe no such\l"
    .string "thing, save only that they keep\l"
    .string "themselves from things offered to\l"
    .string "idols, and from blood, and from\l"
    .string "strangled, and from fornication.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_26::
    .string "Then Paul took the men, and the next\n"
    .string "day purifying himself with them\l"
    .string "entered into the temple, to signify\l"
    .string "the accomplishment of the days of\l"
    .string "purification, until that an offering\l"
    .string "should be offered for every one of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_27::
    .string "And when the seven days were almost\n"
    .string "ended, the Jews which were of Asia,\l"
    .string "when they saw him in the temple,\l"
    .string "stirred up all the people, and\l"
    .string "laid hands on him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_28::
    .string "Crying out, Men of Israel, help:\n"
    .string "This is the man, that teacheth all\l"
    .string "men every where against the people,\l"
    .string "and the law, and this place: and\l"
    .string "further brought Greeks also into the\l"
    .string "temple, and hath polluted this\l"
    .string "holy place$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_29::
    .string "(For they had seen before with him\n"
    .string "in the city Trophimus an Ephesian,\l"
    .string "whom they supposed that Paul had\l"
    .string "brought into the temple.)"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_30::
    .string "And all the city was moved, and the\n"
    .string "people ran together: and they took\l"
    .string "Paul, and drew him out of the\l"
    .string "temple: and forthwith the doors\l"
    .string "were shut$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_31::
    .string "And as they went about to kill him,\n"
    .string "tidings came unto the chief captain\l"
    .string "of the band, that all Jerusalem was\l"
    .string "in an uproar.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_32::
    .string "Who immediately took soldiers and\n"
    .string "centurions, and ran down unto them:\l"
    .string "and when they saw the chief captain\l"
    .string "and the soldiers, they left beating\l"
    .string "of Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_33::
    .string "Then the chief captain came near,\n"
    .string "and took him, and commanded him to be\l"
    .string "bound with two chains; and demanded\l"
    .string "who he was, and what he had done.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_34::
    .string "And some cried one thing, some\n"
    .string "another, among the multitude: and\l"
    .string "when he could not know the certainty\l"
    .string "for the tumult, he commanded him to\l"
    .string "be carried into the castle.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_35::
    .string "And when he came upon the stairs, so\n"
    .string "it was, that he was borne of the\l"
    .string "soldiers for the violence of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_36::
    .string "For the multitude of the people\n"
    .string "followed after, crying, Away with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_37::
    .string "And as Paul was to be led into the\n"
    .string "castle, he said unto the chief\l"
    .string "captain, May I speak unto thee? Who\l"
    .string "said, Canst thou speak Greek?"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_38::
    .string "Art not thou that Egyptian, which\n"
    .string "before these days madest an uproar,\l"
    .string "and leddest out into the wilderness\l"
    .string "four thousand men that were\l"
    .string "murderers?"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_39::
    .string "But Paul said, I am a man which am a\n"
    .string "Jew of Tarsus, a city in Cilicia, a\l"
    .string "citizen of no mean city: and, I\l"
    .string "beseech thee, suffer me to speak\l"
    .string "unto the people$"
Bible_Text_Acts_21_40::
    .string "And when he had given him licence,\n"
    .string "Paul stood on the stairs, and\l"
    .string "beckoned with the hand unto the\l"
    .string "people. And when there was made a\l"
    .string "great silence, he spake unto them in\l"
    .string "the Hebrew tongue, saying,"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_1::
    .string "Men, brethren, and fathers, hear ye\n"
    .string "my defence which I make now unto you$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_2::
    .string "(And when they heard that he spake\n"
    .string "in the Hebrew tongue to them, they\l"
    .string "kept the more silence: and he\l"
    .string "saith,)"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_3::
    .string "I am verily a man which am a Jew,\n"
    .string "born in Tarsus, a city in Cilicia,\l"
    .string "yet brought up in this city at the\l"
    .string "feet of Gamaliel, and taught\l"
    .string "according to the perfect manner of\l"
    .string "the law of the fathers, and was\l"
    .string "zealous toward God, as ye all are\l"
    .string "this day$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_4::
    .string "And I persecuted this way unto the\n"
    .string "death, binding and delivering into\l"
    .string "prisons both men and women.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_5::
    .string "As also the high priest doth bear\n"
    .string "me witness, and all the estate of\l"
    .string "the elders: from whom also I\l"
    .string "received letters unto the brethren,\l"
    .string "and went to Damascus, to bring them\l"
    .string "which were there bound unto\l"
    .string "Jerusalem, for to be punished.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_6::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, as I made\n"
    .string "my journey, and was come nigh unto\l"
    .string "Damascus about noon, suddenly there\l"
    .string "shone from heaven a great light\l"
    .string "round about me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_7::
    .string "And I fell unto the ground, and\n"
    .string "heard a voice saying unto me, Saul,\l"
    .string "Saul, why persecutest thou me?"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_8::
    .string "And I answered, Who art thou, Lord?\n"
    .string "And he said unto me, I am Jesus of\l"
    .string "Nazareth, whom thou persecutest$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_9::
    .string "And they that were with me saw\n"
    .string "indeed the light, and were afraid;\l"
    .string "but they heard not the voice of him\l"
    .string "that spake to me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_10::
    .string "And I said, What shall I do, LORD?\n"
    .string "And the Lord said unto me, Arise, and\l"
    .string "go into Damascus; and there it shall\l"
    .string "be told thee of all things which\l"
    .string "are appointed for thee to do.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_11::
    .string "And when I could not see for the\n"
    .string "glory of that light, being led by\l"
    .string "the hand of them that were with me, I\l"
    .string "came into Damascus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_12::
    .string "And one Ananias, a devout man\n"
    .string "according to the law, having a good\l"
    .string "report of all the Jews which dwelt\l"
    .string "there,"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_13::
    .string "Came unto me, and stood, and said\n"
    .string "unto me, Brother Saul, receive thy\l"
    .string "sight. And the same hour I looked up\l"
    .string "upon him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_14::
    .string "And he said, The God of our fathers\n"
    .string "hath chosen thee, that thou\l"
    .string "shouldest know his will, and see\l"
    .string "that Just One, and shouldest hear\l"
    .string "the voice of his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_15::
    .string "For thou shalt be his witness unto\n"
    .string "all men of what thou hast seen and\l"
    .string "heard.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_16::
    .string "And now why tarriest thou? arise,\n"
    .string "and be baptized, and wash away thy\l"
    .string "sins, calling on the name of the\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, that, when I\n"
    .string "was come again to Jerusalem, even\l"
    .string "while I prayed in the temple, I was\l"
    .string "in a trance;"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_18::
    .string "And saw him saying unto me, Make\n"
    .string "haste, and get thee quickly out of\l"
    .string "Jerusalem: for they will not\l"
    .string "receive thy testimony concerning me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_19::
    .string "And I said, Lord, they know that I\n"
    .string "imprisoned and beat in every\l"
    .string "synagogue them that believed on\l"
    .string "thee:"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_20::
    .string "And when the blood of thy martyr\n"
    .string "Stephen was shed, I also was\l"
    .string "standing by, and consenting unto his\l"
    .string "death, and kept the raiment of them\l"
    .string "that slew him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_21::
    .string "And he said unto me, Depart: for I\n"
    .string "will send thee far hence unto the\l"
    .string "Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_22::
    .string "And they gave him audience unto this\n"
    .string "word, and then lifted up their\l"
    .string "voices, and said, Away with such a\l"
    .string "fellow from the earth: for it is not\l"
    .string "fit that he should live.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_23::
    .string "And as they cried out, and cast off\n"
    .string "their clothes, and threw dust into\l"
    .string "the air,"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_24::
    .string "The chief captain commanded him to\n"
    .string "be brought into the castle, and bade\l"
    .string "that he should be examined by\l"
    .string "scourging; that he might know\l"
    .string "wherefore they cried so against him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_25::
    .string "And as they bound him with thongs,\n"
    .string "Paul said unto the centurion that\l"
    .string "stood by, Is it lawful for you to\l"
    .string "scourge a man that is a Roman, and\l"
    .string "uncondemned?"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_26::
    .string "When the centurion heard that, he\n"
    .string "went and told the chief captain,\l"
    .string "saying, Take heed what thou doest:\l"
    .string "for this man is a Roman$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_27::
    .string "Then the chief captain came, and\n"
    .string "said unto him, Tell me, art thou a\l"
    .string "Roman? He said, Yea.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_28::
    .string "And the chief captain answered,\n"
    .string "With a great sum obtained I this\l"
    .string "freedom. And Paul said, But I was\l"
    .string "free born.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_29::
    .string "Then straightway they departed\n"
    .string "from him which should have examined\l"
    .string "him: and the chief captain also was\l"
    .string "afraid, after he knew that he was a\l"
    .string "Roman, and because he had bound him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_22_30::
    .string "On the morrow, because he would\n"
    .string "have known the certainty wherefore\l"
    .string "he was accused of the Jews, he loosed\l"
    .string "him from his bands, and commanded the\l"
    .string "chief priests and all their\l"
    .string "council to appear, and brought\l"
    .string "Paul down, and set him before them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_1::
    .string "And Paul, earnestly beholding the\n"
    .string "council, said, Men and brethren, I\l"
    .string "have lived in all good conscience\l"
    .string "before God until this day.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_2::
    .string "And the high priest Ananias\n"
    .string "commanded them that stood by him to\l"
    .string "smite him on the mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_3::
    .string "Then said Paul unto him, God shall\n"
    .string "smite thee, thou whited wall: for\l"
    .string "sittest thou to judge me after the\l"
    .string "law, and commandest me to be smitten\l"
    .string "contrary to the law?"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_4::
    .string "And they that stood by said,\n"
    .string "Revilest thou God’s high priest?"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_5::
    .string "Then said Paul, I wist not,\n"
    .string "brethren, that he was the high\l"
    .string "priest: for it is written, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt not speak evil of the ruler\l"
    .string "of thy people$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_6::
    .string "But when Paul perceived that the\n"
    .string "one part were Sadducees, and the\l"
    .string "other Pharisees, he cried out in the\l"
    .string "council, Men and brethren, I am a\l"
    .string "Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee: of\l"
    .string "the hope and resurrection of the\l"
    .string "dead I am called in question.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_7::
    .string "And when he had so said, there arose\n"
    .string "a dissension between the Pharisees\l"
    .string "and the Sadducees: and the multitude\l"
    .string "was divided.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_8::
    .string "For the Sadducees say that there is\n"
    .string "no resurrection, neither angel, nor\l"
    .string "spirit: but the Pharisees confess\l"
    .string "both.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_9::
    .string "And there arose a great cry: and the\n"
    .string "scribes that were of the Pharisees’\l"
    .string "part arose, and strove, saying, We\l"
    .string "find no evil in this man: but if a\l"
    .string "spirit or an angel hath spoken to\l"
    .string "him, let us not fight against God.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_10::
    .string "And when there arose a great\n"
    .string "dissension, the chief captain,\l"
    .string "fearing lest Paul should have been\l"
    .string "pulled in pieces of them, commanded\l"
    .string "the soldiers to go down, and to take\l"
    .string "him by force from among them, and to\l"
    .string "bring him into the castle.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_11::
    .string "And the night following the Lord\n"
    .string "stood by him, and said, Be of good\l"
    .string "cheer, Paul: for as thou hast\l"
    .string "testified of me in Jerusalem, so\l"
    .string "must thou bear witness also at Rome.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_12::
    .string "And when it was day, certain of the\n"
    .string "Jews banded together, and bound\l"
    .string "themselves under a curse, saying\l"
    .string "that they would neither eat nor\l"
    .string "drink till they had killed Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_13::
    .string "And they were more than forty which\n"
    .string "had made this conspiracy.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_14::
    .string "And they came to the chief priests\n"
    .string "and elders, and said, We have bound\l"
    .string "ourselves under a great curse, that\l"
    .string "we will eat nothing until we have\l"
    .string "slain Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_15::
    .string "Now therefore ye with the council\n"
    .string "signify to the chief captain that he\l"
    .string "bring him down unto you to morrow, as\l"
    .string "though ye would enquire something\l"
    .string "more perfectly concerning him: and\l"
    .string "we, or ever he come near, are ready to\l"
    .string "kill him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_16::
    .string "And when Paul’s sister’s son heard\n"
    .string "of their lying in wait, he went and\l"
    .string "entered into the castle, and told\l"
    .string "Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_17::
    .string "Then Paul called one of the\n"
    .string "centurions unto him, and said, Bring\l"
    .string "this young man unto the chief\l"
    .string "captain: for he hath a certain thing\l"
    .string "to tell him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_18::
    .string "So he took him, and brought him to\n"
    .string "the chief captain, and said, Paul\l"
    .string "the prisoner called me unto him,\l"
    .string "and prayed me to bring this young\l"
    .string "man unto thee, who hath something to\l"
    .string "say unto thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_19::
    .string "Then the chief captain took him by\n"
    .string "the hand, and went with him aside\l"
    .string "privately, and asked him, What is\l"
    .string "that thou hast to tell me?"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_20::
    .string "And he said, The Jews have agreed to\n"
    .string "desire thee that thou wouldest bring\l"
    .string "down Paul to morrow into the\l"
    .string "council, as though they would\l"
    .string "enquire somewhat of him more\l"
    .string "perfectly$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_21::
    .string "But do not thou yield unto them: for\n"
    .string "there lie in wait for him of them\l"
    .string "more than forty men, which have bound\l"
    .string "themselves with an oath, that they\l"
    .string "will neither eat nor drink till\l"
    .string "they have killed him: and now are\l"
    .string "they ready, looking for a promise\l"
    .string "from thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_22::
    .string "So the chief captain then let the\n"
    .string "young man depart, and charged him,\l"
    .string "See thou tell no man that thou hast\l"
    .string "shewed these things to me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_23::
    .string "And he called unto him two\n"
    .string "centurions, saying, Make ready two\l"
    .string "hundred soldiers to go to Caesarea,\l"
    .string "and horsemen threescore and ten, and\l"
    .string "spearmen two hundred, at the third\l"
    .string "hour of the night;"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_24::
    .string "And provide them beasts, that they\n"
    .string "may set Paul on, and bring him safe\l"
    .string "unto Felix the governor$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_25::
    .string "And he wrote a letter after this\n"
    .string "manner:"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_26::
    .string "Claudius Lysias unto the most\n"
    .string "excellent governor Felix sendeth\l"
    .string "greeting$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_27::
    .string "This man was taken of the Jews, and\n"
    .string "should have been killed of them:\l"
    .string "then came I with an army, and rescued\l"
    .string "him, having understood that he was a\l"
    .string "Roman.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_28::
    .string "And when I would have known the\n"
    .string "cause wherefore they accused him, I\l"
    .string "brought him forth into their\l"
    .string "council:"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_29::
    .string "Whom I perceived to be accused of\n"
    .string "questions of their law, but to have\l"
    .string "nothing laid to his charge worthy of\l"
    .string "death or of bonds$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_30::
    .string "And when it was told me how that the\n"
    .string "Jews laid wait for the man, I sent\l"
    .string "straightway to thee, and gave\l"
    .string "commandment to his accusers also to\l"
    .string "say before thee what they had against\l"
    .string "him. Farewell.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_31::
    .string "Then the soldiers, as it was\n"
    .string "commanded them, took Paul, and\l"
    .string "brought him by night to Antipatris.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_32::
    .string "On the morrow they left the\n"
    .string "horsemen to go with him, and returned\l"
    .string "to the castle:"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_33::
    .string "Who, when they came to Caesarea and\n"
    .string "delivered the epistle to the\l"
    .string "governor, presented Paul also\l"
    .string "before him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_34::
    .string "And when the governor had read the\n"
    .string "letter, he asked of what province he\l"
    .string "was. And when he understood that he\l"
    .string "was of Cilicia;"
Bible_Text_Acts_23_35::
    .string "I will hear thee, said he, when\n"
    .string "thine accusers are also come. And he\l"
    .string "commanded him to be kept in Herod’s\l"
    .string "judgment hall$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_1::
    .string "And after five days Ananias the high\n"
    .string "priest descended with the elders,\l"
    .string "and with a certain orator named\l"
    .string "Tertullus, who informed the\l"
    .string "governor against Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_2::
    .string "And when he was called forth,\n"
    .string "Tertullus began to accuse him,\l"
    .string "saying, Seeing that by thee we enjoy\l"
    .string "great quietness, and that very worthy\l"
    .string "deeds are done unto this nation by\l"
    .string "thy providence,"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_3::
    .string "We accept it always, and in all\n"
    .string "places, most noble Felix, with\l"
    .string "all thankfulness$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_4::
    .string "Notwithstanding, that I be not\n"
    .string "further tedious unto thee, I pray\l"
    .string "thee that thou wouldest hear us of\l"
    .string "thy clemency a few words.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_5::
    .string "For we have found this man a\n"
    .string "pestilent fellow, and a mover of\l"
    .string "sedition among all the Jews\l"
    .string "throughout the world, and a\l"
    .string "ringleader of the sect of the\l"
    .string "Nazarenes:"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_6::
    .string "Who also hath gone about to\n"
    .string "profane the temple: whom we took,\l"
    .string "and would have judged according to\l"
    .string "our law$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_7::
    .string "But the chief captain Lysias came\n"
    .string "upon us, and with great violence\l"
    .string "took him away out of our hands,"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_8::
    .string "Commanding his accusers to come\n"
    .string "unto thee: by examining of whom\l"
    .string "thyself mayest take knowledge of\l"
    .string "all these things, whereof we accuse\l"
    .string "him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_9::
    .string "And the Jews also assented, saying\n"
    .string "that these things were so.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_10::
    .string "Then Paul, after that the governor\n"
    .string "had beckoned unto him to speak,\l"
    .string "answered, Forasmuch as I know that\l"
    .string "thou hast been of many years a judge\l"
    .string "unto this nation, I do the more\l"
    .string "cheerfully answer for myself:"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_11::
    .string "Because that thou mayest\n"
    .string "understand, that there are yet but\l"
    .string "twelve days since I went up to\l"
    .string "Jerusalem for to worship$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_12::
    .string "And they neither found me in the\n"
    .string "temple disputing with any man,\l"
    .string "neither raising up the people,\l"
    .string "neither in the synagogues, nor in the\l"
    .string "city:"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_13::
    .string "Neither can they prove the things\n"
    .string "whereof they now accuse me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_14::
    .string "But this I confess unto thee, that\n"
    .string "after the way which they call\l"
    .string "heresy, so worship I the God of my\l"
    .string "fathers, believing all things\l"
    .string "which are written in the law and in\l"
    .string "the prophets:"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_15::
    .string "And have hope toward God, which\n"
    .string "they themselves also allow, that\l"
    .string "there shall be a resurrection of\l"
    .string "the dead, both of the just and unjust$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_16::
    .string "And herein do I exercise myself, to\n"
    .string "have always a conscience void to\l"
    .string "offence toward God, and toward men.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_17::
    .string "Now after many years I came to bring\n"
    .string "alms to my nation, and offerings.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_18::
    .string "Whereupon certain Jews from Asia\n"
    .string "found me purified in the temple,\l"
    .string "neither with multitude, nor with\l"
    .string "tumult.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_19::
    .string "Who ought to have been here before\n"
    .string "thee, and object, if they had ought\l"
    .string "against me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_20::
    .string "Or else let these same here say, if\n"
    .string "they have found any evil doing in me,\l"
    .string "while I stood before the council,"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_21::
    .string "Except it be for this one voice,\n"
    .string "that I cried standing among them,\l"
    .string "Touching the resurrection of the\l"
    .string "dead I am called in question by you\l"
    .string "this day$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_22::
    .string "And when Felix heard these things,\n"
    .string "having more perfect knowledge of\l"
    .string "that way, he deferred them, and said,\l"
    .string "When Lysias the chief captain\l"
    .string "shall come down, I will know the\l"
    .string "uttermost of your matter.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_23::
    .string "And he commanded a centurion to\n"
    .string "keep Paul, and to let him have\l"
    .string "liberty, and that he should forbid\l"
    .string "none of his acquaintance to minister\l"
    .string "or come unto him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_24::
    .string "And after certain days, when Felix\n"
    .string "came with his wife Drusilla, which\l"
    .string "was a Jewess, he sent for Paul, and\l"
    .string "heard him concerning the faith in\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_25::
    .string "And as he reasoned of righteousness,\n"
    .string "temperance, and judgment to come,\l"
    .string "Felix trembled, and answered, Go\l"
    .string "thy way for this time; when I have a\l"
    .string "convenient season, I will call for\l"
    .string "thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_26::
    .string "He hoped also that money should\n"
    .string "have been given him of Paul, that he\l"
    .string "might loose him: wherefore he sent\l"
    .string "for him the oftener, and communed\l"
    .string "with him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_24_27::
    .string "But after two years Porcius Festus\n"
    .string "came into Felix’ room: and Felix,\l"
    .string "willing to shew the Jews a\l"
    .string "pleasure, left Paul bound.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_1::
    .string "Now when Festus was come into the\n"
    .string "province, after three days he\l"
    .string "ascended from Caesarea to Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_2::
    .string "Then the high priest and the chief\n"
    .string "of the Jews informed him against\l"
    .string "Paul, and besought him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_3::
    .string "And desired favour against him, that\n"
    .string "he would send for him to Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "laying wait in the way to kill him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_4::
    .string "But Festus answered, that Paul\n"
    .string "should be kept at Caesarea, and that\l"
    .string "he himself would depart shortly\l"
    .string "thither.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_5::
    .string "Let them therefore, said he, which\n"
    .string "among you are able, go down with me,\l"
    .string "and accuse this man, if there be any\l"
    .string "wickedness in him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_6::
    .string "And when he had tarried among them\n"
    .string "more than ten days, he went down unto\l"
    .string "Caesarea; and the next day sitting on\l"
    .string "the judgment seat commanded Paul to\l"
    .string "be brought.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_7::
    .string "And when he was come, the Jews which\n"
    .string "came down from Jerusalem stood round\l"
    .string "about, and laid many and grievous\l"
    .string "complaints against Paul, which\l"
    .string "they could not prove.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_8::
    .string "While he answered for himself,\n"
    .string "Neither against the law of the Jews,\l"
    .string "neither against the temple, nor yet\l"
    .string "against Caesar, have I offended any\l"
    .string "thing at all.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_9::
    .string "But Festus, willing to do the Jews\n"
    .string "a pleasure, answered Paul, and\l"
    .string "said, Wilt thou go up to Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and there be judged of these things\l"
    .string "before me?"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_10::
    .string "Then said Paul, I stand at Caesar’s\n"
    .string "judgment seat, where I ought to be\l"
    .string "judged: to the Jews have I done no\l"
    .string "wrong, as thou very well knowest$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_11::
    .string "For if I be an offender, or have\n"
    .string "committed any thing worthy of death,\l"
    .string "I refuse not to die: but if there be\l"
    .string "none of these things whereof these\l"
    .string "accuse me, no man may deliver me unto\l"
    .string "them. I appeal unto Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_12::
    .string "Then Festus, when he had conferred\n"
    .string "with the council, answered, Hast\l"
    .string "thou appealed unto Caesar? unto\l"
    .string "Caesar shalt thou go.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_13::
    .string "And after certain days king\n"
    .string "Agrippa and Bernice came unto\l"
    .string "Caesarea to salute Festus.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_14::
    .string "And when they had been there many\n"
    .string "days, Festus declared Paul’s cause\l"
    .string "unto the king, saying, There is a\l"
    .string "certain man left in bonds by Felix:"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_15::
    .string "About whom, when I was at\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, the chief priests and\l"
    .string "the elders of the Jews informed me,\l"
    .string "desiring to have judgment against him$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_16::
    .string "To whom I answered, It is not the\n"
    .string "manner of the Romans to deliver any\l"
    .string "man to die, before that he which is\l"
    .string "accused have the accusers face to\l"
    .string "face, and have licence to answer for\l"
    .string "himself concerning the crime laid\l"
    .string "against him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_17::
    .string "Therefore, when they were come\n"
    .string "hither, without any delay on the\l"
    .string "morrow I sat on the judgment seat,\l"
    .string "and commanded the man to be brought\l"
    .string "forth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_18::
    .string "Against whom when the accusers\n"
    .string "stood up, they brought none\l"
    .string "accusation of such things as I\l"
    .string "supposed:"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_19::
    .string "But had certain questions against\n"
    .string "him of their own superstition, and\l"
    .string "of one Jesus, which was dead, whom\l"
    .string "Paul affirmed to be alive$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_20::
    .string "And because I doubted of such manner\n"
    .string "of questions, I asked him whether he\l"
    .string "would go to Jerusalem, and there be\l"
    .string "judged of these matters.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_21::
    .string "But when Paul had appealed to be\n"
    .string "reserved unto the hearing of\l"
    .string "Augustus, I commanded him to be kept\l"
    .string "till I might send him to Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_22::
    .string "Then Agrippa said unto Festus, I\n"
    .string "would also hear the man myself. To\l"
    .string "morrow, said he, thou shalt hear him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_23::
    .string "And on the morrow, when Agrippa was\n"
    .string "come, and Bernice, with great pomp,\l"
    .string "and was entered into the place of\l"
    .string "hearing, with the chief captains,\l"
    .string "and principal men of the city, at\l"
    .string "Festus’ commandment Paul was\l"
    .string "brought forth.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_24::
    .string "And Festus said, King Agrippa, and\n"
    .string "all men which are here present with\l"
    .string "us, ye see this man, about whom all\l"
    .string "the multitude of the Jews have\l"
    .string "dealt with me, both at Jerusalem,\l"
    .string "and also here, crying that he ought\l"
    .string "not to live any longer.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_25::
    .string "But when I found that he had\n"
    .string "committed nothing worthy of death,\l"
    .string "and that he himself hath appealed\l"
    .string "to Augustus, I have determined to\l"
    .string "send him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_26::
    .string "Of whom I have no certain thing to\n"
    .string "write unto my lord. Wherefore I have\l"
    .string "brought him forth before you, and\l"
    .string "specially before thee, O king\l"
    .string "Agrippa, that, after examination\l"
    .string "had, I might have somewhat to write.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_25_27::
    .string "For it seemeth to me unreasonable\n"
    .string "to send a prisoner, and not withal\l"
    .string "to signify the crimes laid against\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_1::
    .string "Then Agrippa said unto Paul, Thou\n"
    .string "art permitted to speak for thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_2::
    .string "I think myself happy, king\n"
    .string "Agrippa, because I shall answer\l"
    .string "for myself this day before thee\l"
    .string "touching all the things whereof I\l"
    .string "am accused of the Jews:"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_3::
    .string "Especially because I know thee to\n"
    .string "be expert in all customs and\l"
    .string "questions which are among the Jews:\l"
    .string "wherefore I beseech thee to hear me\l"
    .string "patiently$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_4::
    .string "My manner of life from my youth,\n"
    .string "which was at the first among mine own\l"
    .string "nation at Jerusalem, know all the\l"
    .string "Jews;"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_5::
    .string "Which knew me from the beginning, if\n"
    .string "they would testify, that after the\l"
    .string "most straitest sect of our religion\l"
    .string "I lived a Pharisee$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_6::
    .string "And now I stand and am judged for\n"
    .string "the hope of the promise made of God,\l"
    .string "unto our fathers:"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_7::
    .string "Unto which promise our twelve\n"
    .string "tribes, instantly serving God day\l"
    .string "and night, hope to come. For which\l"
    .string "hope’s sake, king Agrippa, I am\l"
    .string "accused of the Jews$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_8::
    .string "Why should it be thought a thing\n"
    .string "incredible with you, that God\l"
    .string "should raise the dead?"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_9::
    .string "I verily thought with myself, that\n"
    .string "I ought to do many things contrary to\l"
    .string "the name of Jesus of Nazareth$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_10::
    .string "Which thing I also did in\n"
    .string "Jerusalem: and many of the saints\l"
    .string "did I shut up in prison, having\l"
    .string "received authority from the chief\l"
    .string "priests; and when they were put to\l"
    .string "death, I gave my voice against them.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_11::
    .string "And I punished them oft in every\n"
    .string "synagogue, and compelled them to\l"
    .string "blaspheme; and being exceedingly\l"
    .string "mad against them, I persecuted them\l"
    .string "even unto strange cities.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_12::
    .string "Whereupon as I went to Damascus\n"
    .string "with authority and commission from\l"
    .string "the chief priests,"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_13::
    .string "At midday, O king, I saw in the way a\n"
    .string "light from heaven, above the\l"
    .string "brightness of the sun, shining round\l"
    .string "about me and them which journeyed\l"
    .string "with me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_14::
    .string "And when we were all fallen to\n"
    .string "the earth, I heard a voice speaking\l"
    .string "unto me, and saying in the Hebrew\l"
    .string "tongue, Saul, Saul, why persecutest\l"
    .string "thou me? it is hard for thee to kick\l"
    .string "against the pricks.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_15::
    .string "And I said, Who art thou, Lord? And\n"
    .string "he said, I am Jesus whom thou\l"
    .string "persecutest.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_16::
    .string "But rise, and stand upon thy feet:\n"
    .string "for I have appeared unto thee for\l"
    .string "this purpose, to make thee a\l"
    .string "minister and a witness both of these\l"
    .string "things which thou hast seen, and of\l"
    .string "those things in the which I will\l"
    .string "appear unto thee;"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_17::
    .string "Delivering thee from the people,\n"
    .string "and from the Gentiles, unto whom now\l"
    .string "I send thee,"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_18::
    .string "To open their eyes, and to turn them\n"
    .string "from darkness to light, and from the\l"
    .string "power of Satan unto God, that they\l"
    .string "may receive forgiveness of sins, and\l"
    .string "inheritance among them which are\l"
    .string "sanctified by faith that is in me$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_19::
    .string "Whereupon, O king Agrippa, I was\n"
    .string "not disobedient unto the heavenly\l"
    .string "vision:"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_20::
    .string "But shewed first unto them of\n"
    .string "Damascus, and at Jerusalem, and\l"
    .string "throughout all the coasts of\l"
    .string "Judaea, and then to the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "that they should repent and turn to\l"
    .string "God, and do works meet for repentance$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_21::
    .string "For these causes the Jews caught me\n"
    .string "in the temple, and went about to\l"
    .string "kill me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_22::
    .string "Having therefore obtained help of\n"
    .string "God, I continue unto this day,\l"
    .string "witnessing both to small and great,\l"
    .string "saying none other things than those\l"
    .string "which the prophets and Moses did\l"
    .string "say should come:"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_23::
    .string "That Christ should suffer, and that\n"
    .string "he should be the first that should\l"
    .string "rise from the dead, and should shew\l"
    .string "light unto the people, and to the\l"
    .string "Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_24::
    .string "And as he thus spake for himself,\n"
    .string "Festus said with a loud voice, Paul,\l"
    .string "thou art beside thyself; much\l"
    .string "learning doth make thee mad.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_25::
    .string "But he said, I am not mad, most\n"
    .string "noble Festus; but speak forth the\l"
    .string "words of truth and soberness.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_26::
    .string "For the king knoweth of these\n"
    .string "things, before whom also I speak\l"
    .string "freely: for I am persuaded that none\l"
    .string "of these things are hidden from him;\l"
    .string "for this thing was not done in a\l"
    .string "corner.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_27::
    .string "King Agrippa, believest thou the\n"
    .string "prophets? I know that thou\l"
    .string "believest.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_28::
    .string "Then Agrippa said unto Paul,\n"
    .string "Almost thou persuadest me to be a\l"
    .string "Christian.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_29::
    .string "And Paul said, I would to God, that\n"
    .string "not only thou, but also all that\l"
    .string "hear me this day, were both almost,\l"
    .string "and altogether such as I am, except\l"
    .string "these bonds.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_30::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, the\n"
    .string "king rose up, and the governor, and\l"
    .string "Bernice, and they that sat with them:"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_31::
    .string "And when they were gone aside, they\n"
    .string "talked between themselves, saying,\l"
    .string "This man doeth nothing worthy of\l"
    .string "death or of bonds$"
Bible_Text_Acts_26_32::
    .string "Then said Agrippa unto Festus,\n"
    .string "This man might have been set at\l"
    .string "liberty, if he had not appealed\l"
    .string "unto Caesar.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_1::
    .string "And when it was determined that we\n"
    .string "should sail into Italy, they\l"
    .string "delivered Paul and certain other\l"
    .string "prisoners unto one named Julius, a\l"
    .string "centurion of Augustus’ band.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_2::
    .string "And entering into a ship of\n"
    .string "Adramyttium, we launched, meaning to\l"
    .string "sail by the coasts of Asia; one\l"
    .string "Aristarchus, a Macedonian of\l"
    .string "Thessalonica, being with us.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_3::
    .string "And the next day we touched at\n"
    .string "Sidon. And Julius courteously\l"
    .string "entreated Paul, and gave him\l"
    .string "liberty to go unto his friends to\l"
    .string "refresh himself.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_4::
    .string "And when we had launched from\n"
    .string "thence, we sailed under Cyprus,\l"
    .string "because the winds were contrary.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_5::
    .string "And when we had sailed over the sea\n"
    .string "of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came\l"
    .string "to Myra, a city of Lycia.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_6::
    .string "And there the centurion found a\n"
    .string "ship of Alexandria sailing into\l"
    .string "Italy; and he put us therein.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_7::
    .string "And when we had sailed slowly many\n"
    .string "days, and scarce were come over\l"
    .string "against Cnidus, the wind not\l"
    .string "suffering us, we sailed under Crete,\l"
    .string "over against Salmone;"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_8::
    .string "And, hardly passing it, came unto a\n"
    .string "place which is called The fair\l"
    .string "havens; nigh whereunto was the city\l"
    .string "of Lasea$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_9::
    .string "Now when much time was spent, and\n"
    .string "when sailing was now dangerous,\l"
    .string "because the fast was now already\l"
    .string "past, Paul admonished them,"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_10::
    .string "And said unto them, Sirs, I\n"
    .string "perceive that this voyage will be\l"
    .string "with hurt and much damage, not only\l"
    .string "of the lading and ship, but also of\l"
    .string "our lives$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_11::
    .string "Nevertheless the centurion\n"
    .string "believed the master and the owner of\l"
    .string "the ship, more than those things\l"
    .string "which were spoken by Paul.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_12::
    .string "And because the haven was not\n"
    .string "commodious to winter in, the more\l"
    .string "part advised to depart thence also,\l"
    .string "if by any means they might attain to\l"
    .string "Phenice, and there to winter; which\l"
    .string "is an haven of Crete, and lieth\l"
    .string "toward the south west and north west.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_13::
    .string "And when the south wind blew\n"
    .string "softly, supposing that they had\l"
    .string "obtained their purpose, loosing\l"
    .string "thence, they sailed close by Crete.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_14::
    .string "But not long after there arose\n"
    .string "against it a tempestuous wind,\l"
    .string "called Euroclydon.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_15::
    .string "And when the ship was caught, and\n"
    .string "could not bear up into the wind, we\l"
    .string "let her drive.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_16::
    .string "And running under a certain island\n"
    .string "which is called Clauda, we had much\l"
    .string "work to come by the boat:"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_17::
    .string "Which when they had taken up, they\n"
    .string "used helps, undergirding the ship;\l"
    .string "and, fearing lest they should fall\l"
    .string "into the quicksands, strake sail,\l"
    .string "and so were driven$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_18::
    .string "And we being exceedingly tossed\n"
    .string "with a tempest, the next day they\l"
    .string "lightened the ship;"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_19::
    .string "And the third day we cast out with\n"
    .string "our own hands the tackling of the\l"
    .string "ship$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_20::
    .string "And when neither sun nor stars in\n"
    .string "many days appeared, and no small\l"
    .string "tempest lay on us, all hope that\l"
    .string "we should be saved was then taken\l"
    .string "away.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_21::
    .string "But after long abstinence Paul\n"
    .string "stood forth in the midst of them, and\l"
    .string "said, Sirs, ye should have hearkened\l"
    .string "unto me, and not have loosed from\l"
    .string "Crete, and to have gained this harm\l"
    .string "and loss.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_22::
    .string "And now I exhort you to be of good\n"
    .string "cheer: for there shall be no loss\l"
    .string "of any man’s life among you, but of\l"
    .string "the ship.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_23::
    .string "For there stood by me this night the\n"
    .string "angel of God, whose I am, and whom I\l"
    .string "serve,"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_24::
    .string "Saying, Fear not, Paul; thou must be\n"
    .string "brought before Caesar: and, lo, God\l"
    .string "hath given thee all them that sail\l"
    .string "with thee$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_25::
    .string "Wherefore, sirs, be of good cheer:\n"
    .string "for I believe God, that it shall be\l"
    .string "even as it was told me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_26::
    .string "Howbeit we must be cast upon a\n"
    .string "certain island.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_27::
    .string "But when the fourteenth night was\n"
    .string "come, as we were driven up and down\l"
    .string "in Adria, about midnight the shipmen\l"
    .string "deemed that they drew near to some\l"
    .string "country;"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_28::
    .string "And sounded, and found it twenty\n"
    .string "fathoms: and when they had gone a\l"
    .string "little further, they sounded again,\l"
    .string "and found it fifteen fathoms$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_29::
    .string "Then fearing lest we should have\n"
    .string "fallen upon rocks, they cast four\l"
    .string "anchors out of the stern, and wished\l"
    .string "for the day.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_30::
    .string "And as the shipmen were about to\n"
    .string "flee out of the ship, when they had\l"
    .string "let down the boat into the sea, under\l"
    .string "colour as though they would have\l"
    .string "cast anchors out of the foreship,"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_31::
    .string "Paul said to the centurion and to\n"
    .string "the soldiers, Except these abide in\l"
    .string "the ship, ye cannot be saved$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_32::
    .string "Then the soldiers cut off the\n"
    .string "ropes of the boat, and let her fall\l"
    .string "off.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_33::
    .string "And while the day was coming on,\n"
    .string "Paul besought them all to take\l"
    .string "meat, saying, This day is the\l"
    .string "fourteenth day that ye have tarried\l"
    .string "and continued fasting, having taken\l"
    .string "nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_34::
    .string "Wherefore I pray you to take some\n"
    .string "meat: for this is for your health:\l"
    .string "for there shall not an hair fall\l"
    .string "from the head of any of you.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_35::
    .string "And when he had thus spoken, he took\n"
    .string "bread, and gave thanks to God in\l"
    .string "presence of them all: and when he\l"
    .string "had broken it, he began to eat.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_36::
    .string "Then were they all of good cheer,\n"
    .string "and they also took some meat.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_37::
    .string "And we were in all in the ship two\n"
    .string "hundred threescore and sixteen\l"
    .string "souls.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_38::
    .string "And when they had eaten enough, they\n"
    .string "lightened the ship, and cast out the\l"
    .string "wheat into the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_39::
    .string "And when it was day, they knew not\n"
    .string "the land: but they discovered a\l"
    .string "certain creek with a shore, into the\l"
    .string "which they were minded, if it were\l"
    .string "possible, to thrust in the ship.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_40::
    .string "And when they had taken up the\n"
    .string "anchors, they committed themselves\l"
    .string "unto the sea, and loosed the rudder\l"
    .string "bands, and hoised up the mainsail to\l"
    .string "the wind, and made toward shore.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_41::
    .string "And falling into a place where\n"
    .string "two seas met, they ran the ship\l"
    .string "aground; and the forepart stuck\l"
    .string "fast, and remained unmoveable, but\l"
    .string "the hinder part was broken with the\l"
    .string "violence of the waves.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_42::
    .string "And the soldiers’ counsel was to\n"
    .string "kill the prisoners, lest any of\l"
    .string "them should swim out, and escape.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_43::
    .string "But the centurion, willing to save\n"
    .string "Paul, kept them from their\l"
    .string "purpose; and commanded that they\l"
    .string "which could swim should cast\l"
    .string "themselves first into the sea, and\l"
    .string "get to land:"
Bible_Text_Acts_27_44::
    .string "And the rest, some on boards, and\n"
    .string "some on broken pieces of the ship\l"
    .string "And so it came to pass, that they\l"
    .string "escaped all safe to land.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_1::
    .string "And when they were escaped, then\n"
    .string "they knew that the island was\l"
    .string "called Melita.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_2::
    .string "And the barbarous people shewed\n"
    .string "us no little kindness: for they\l"
    .string "kindled a fire, and received us\l"
    .string "every one, because of the present\l"
    .string "rain, and because of the cold.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_3::
    .string "And when Paul had gathered a\n"
    .string "bundle of sticks, and laid them on\l"
    .string "the fire, there came a viper out of\l"
    .string "the heat, and fastened on his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_4::
    .string "And when the barbarians saw the\n"
    .string "venomous beast hang on his hand, they\l"
    .string "said among themselves, No doubt this\l"
    .string "man is a murderer, whom, though he\l"
    .string "hath escaped the sea, yet vengeance\l"
    .string "suffereth not to live.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_5::
    .string "And he shook off the beast into the\n"
    .string "fire, and felt no harm.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_6::
    .string "Howbeit they looked when he should\n"
    .string "have swollen, or fallen down dead\l"
    .string "suddenly: but after they had looked\l"
    .string "a great while, and saw no harm come\l"
    .string "to him, they changed their minds, and\l"
    .string "said that he was a god.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_7::
    .string "In the same quarters were\n"
    .string "possessions of the chief man of the\l"
    .string "island, whose name was Publius; who\l"
    .string "received us, and lodged us three\l"
    .string "days courteously.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_8::
    .string "And it came to pass, that the father\n"
    .string "of Publius lay sick of a fever and\l"
    .string "of a bloody flux: to whom Paul\l"
    .string "entered in, and prayed, and laid his\l"
    .string "hands on him, and healed him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_9::
    .string "So when this was done, others also,\n"
    .string "which had diseases in the island,\l"
    .string "came, and were healed:"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_10::
    .string "Who also honoured us with many\n"
    .string "honours; and when we departed, they\l"
    .string "laded us with such things as were\l"
    .string "necessary$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_11::
    .string "And after three months we departed\n"
    .string "in a ship of Alexandria, which had\l"
    .string "wintered in the isle, whose sign was\l"
    .string "Castor and Pollux.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_12::
    .string "And landing at Syracuse, we tarried\n"
    .string "there three days.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_13::
    .string "And from thence we fetched a\n"
    .string "compass, and came to Rhegium: and\l"
    .string "after one day the south wind blew,\l"
    .string "and we came the next day to Puteoli:"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_14::
    .string "Where we found brethren, and were\n"
    .string "desired to tarry with them seven\l"
    .string "days: and so we went toward Rome$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_15::
    .string "And from thence, when the brethren\n"
    .string "heard of us, they came to meet us as\l"
    .string "far as Appii forum, and The three\l"
    .string "taverns: whom when Paul saw, he\l"
    .string "thanked God, and took courage.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_16::
    .string "And when we came to Rome, the\n"
    .string "centurion delivered the prisoners\l"
    .string "to the captain of the guard: but\l"
    .string "Paul was suffered to dwell by\l"
    .string "himself with a soldier that kept\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_17::
    .string "And it came to pass, that after\n"
    .string "three days Paul called the chief of\l"
    .string "the Jews together: and when they were\l"
    .string "come together, he said unto them, Men\l"
    .string "and brethren, though I have committed\l"
    .string "nothing against the people, or\l"
    .string "customs of our fathers, yet was I\l"
    .string "delivered prisoner from Jerusalem\l"
    .string "into the hands of the Romans.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_18::
    .string "Who, when they had examined me,\n"
    .string "would have let me go, because there\l"
    .string "was no cause of death in me.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_19::
    .string "But when the Jews spake against it,\n"
    .string "I was constrained to appeal unto\l"
    .string "Caesar; not that I had ought to\l"
    .string "accuse my nation of.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_20::
    .string "For this cause therefore have I\n"
    .string "called for you, to see you, and to\l"
    .string "speak with you: because that for the\l"
    .string "hope of Israel I am bound with this\l"
    .string "chain.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_21::
    .string "And they said unto him, We neither\n"
    .string "received letters out of Judaea\l"
    .string "concerning thee, neither any of the\l"
    .string "brethren that came shewed or spake\l"
    .string "any harm of thee.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_22::
    .string "But we desire to hear of thee what\n"
    .string "thou thinkest: for as concerning this\l"
    .string "sect, we know that every where it is\l"
    .string "spoken against.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_23::
    .string "And when they had appointed him a\n"
    .string "day, there came many to him into his\l"
    .string "lodging; to whom he expounded and\l"
    .string "testified the kingdom of God,\l"
    .string "persuading them concerning Jesus,\l"
    .string "both out of the law of Moses, and out\l"
    .string "of the prophets, from morning till\l"
    .string "evening.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_24::
    .string "And some believed the things which\n"
    .string "were spoken, and some believed not.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_25::
    .string "And when they agreed not among\n"
    .string "themselves, they departed, after\l"
    .string "that Paul had spoken one word,\l"
    .string "Well spake the Holy Ghost by\l"
    .string "Esaias the prophet unto our\l"
    .string "fathers,"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_26::
    .string "Saying, Go unto this people, and\n"
    .string "say, Hearing ye shall hear, and\l"
    .string "shall not understand; and seeing ye\l"
    .string "shall see, and not perceive:"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_27::
    .string "For the heart of this people is\n"
    .string "waxed gross, and their ears are dull\l"
    .string "of hearing, and their eyes have they\l"
    .string "closed; lest they should see with\l"
    .string "their eyes, and hear with their ears,\l"
    .string "and understand with their heart, and\l"
    .string "should be converted, and I should\l"
    .string "heal them$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_28::
    .string "Be it known therefore unto you, that\n"
    .string "the salvation of God is sent unto\l"
    .string "the Gentiles, and that they will\l"
    .string "hear it.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_29::
    .string "And when he had said these words,\n"
    .string "the Jews departed, and had great\l"
    .string "reasoning among themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_30::
    .string "And Paul dwelt two whole years in\n"
    .string "his own hired house, and received\l"
    .string "all that came in unto him,"
Bible_Text_Acts_28_31::
    .string "Preaching the kingdom of God, and\n"
    .string "teaching those things which concern\l"
    .string "the Lord Jesus Christ, with all\l"
    .string "confidence, no man forbidding him$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_1::
    .string "Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "called to be an apostle,\l"
    .string "separated unto the gospel of God,"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_2::
    .string "(Which he had promised afore by his\n"
    .string "prophets in the holy scriptures,)"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_3::
    .string "Concerning his Son Jesus Christ our\n"
    .string "Lord, which was made of the seed of\l"
    .string "David according to the flesh;"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_4::
    .string "And declared to be the Son of God\n"
    .string "with power, according to the spirit\l"
    .string "of holiness, by the resurrection\l"
    .string "from the dead:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_5::
    .string "By whom we have received grace and\n"
    .string "apostleship, for obedience to the\l"
    .string "faith among all nations, for his\l"
    .string "name:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_6::
    .string "Among whom are ye also the called\n"
    .string "of Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_7::
    .string "To all that be in Rome, beloved of\n"
    .string "God, called to be saints: Grace to\l"
    .string "you and peace from God our Father,\l"
    .string "and the Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_8::
    .string "First, I thank my God through Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ for you all, that your faith\l"
    .string "is spoken of throughout the whole\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_9::
    .string "For God is my witness, whom I serve\n"
    .string "with my spirit in the gospel of his\l"
    .string "Son, that without ceasing I make\l"
    .string "mention of you always in my prayers;"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_10::
    .string "Making request, if by any means now\n"
    .string "at length I might have a prosperous\l"
    .string "journey by the will of God to come\l"
    .string "unto you$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_11::
    .string "For I long to see you, that I may\n"
    .string "impart unto you some spiritual\l"
    .string "gift, to the end ye may be\l"
    .string "established;"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_12::
    .string "That is, that I may be comforted\n"
    .string "together with you by the mutual\l"
    .string "faith both of you and me$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_13::
    .string "Now I would not have you ignorant,\n"
    .string "brethren, that oftentimes I\l"
    .string "purposed to come unto you, (but was\l"
    .string "let hitherto,) that I might have some\l"
    .string "fruit among you also, even as among\l"
    .string "other Gentiles.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_14::
    .string "I am debtor both to the Greeks, and\n"
    .string "to the Barbarians; both to the wise,\l"
    .string "and to the unwise.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_15::
    .string "So, as much as in me is, I am ready\n"
    .string "to preach the gospel to you that\l"
    .string "are at Rome also.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_16::
    .string "For I am not ashamed of the gospel\n"
    .string "of Christ: for it is the power of God\l"
    .string "unto salvation to every one that\l"
    .string "believeth; to the Jew first, and\l"
    .string "also to the Greek.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_17::
    .string "For therein is the righteousness of\n"
    .string "God revealed from faith to faith: as\l"
    .string "it is written, The just shall live\l"
    .string "by faith.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_18::
    .string "For the wrath of God is revealed\n"
    .string "from heaven against all\l"
    .string "ungodliness and unrighteousness of\l"
    .string "men, who hold the truth in\l"
    .string "unrighteousness;"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_19::
    .string "Because that which may be known of\n"
    .string "God is manifest in them; for God hath\l"
    .string "shewed it unto them$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_20::
    .string "For the invisible things of him\n"
    .string "from the creation of the world are\l"
    .string "clearly seen, being understood by\l"
    .string "the things that are made, even his\l"
    .string "eternal power and Godhead; so that\l"
    .string "they are without excuse:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_21::
    .string "Because that, when they knew God,\n"
    .string "they glorified him not as God,\l"
    .string "neither were thankful; but became\l"
    .string "vain in their imaginations, and their\l"
    .string "foolish heart was darkened$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_22::
    .string "Professing themselves to be wise,\n"
    .string "they became fools,"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_23::
    .string "And changed the glory of the\n"
    .string "uncorruptible God into an image\l"
    .string "made like to corruptible man, and\l"
    .string "to birds, and fourfooted beasts, and\l"
    .string "creeping things$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_24::
    .string "Wherefore God also gave them up to\n"
    .string "uncleanness through the lusts of\l"
    .string "their own hearts, to dishonour their\l"
    .string "own bodies between themselves:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_25::
    .string "Who changed the truth of God into a\n"
    .string "lie, and worshipped and served the\l"
    .string "creature more than the Creator, who\l"
    .string "is blessed for ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_26::
    .string "For this cause God gave them up\n"
    .string "unto vile affections: for even their\l"
    .string "women did change the natural use\l"
    .string "into that which is against nature:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_27::
    .string "And likewise also the men, leaving\n"
    .string "the natural use of the woman, burned\l"
    .string "in their lust one toward another;\l"
    .string "men with men working that which is\l"
    .string "unseemly, and receiving in\l"
    .string "themselves that recompence of their\l"
    .string "error which was meet$"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_28::
    .string "And even as they did not like to\n"
    .string "retain God in their knowledge, God\l"
    .string "gave them over to a reprobate mind,\l"
    .string "to do those things which are not\l"
    .string "convenient;"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_29::
    .string "Being filled with all\n"
    .string "unrighteousness, fornication,\l"
    .string "wickedness, covetousness,\l"
    .string "maliciousness; full of envy,\l"
    .string "murder, debate, deceit, malignity;\l"
    .string "whisperers,"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_30::
    .string "Backbiters, haters of God,\n"
    .string "despiteful, proud, boasters,\l"
    .string "inventors of evil things,\l"
    .string "disobedient to parents,"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_31::
    .string "Without understanding,\n"
    .string "covenantbreakers, without natural\l"
    .string "affection, implacable,\l"
    .string "unmerciful:"
Bible_Text_Paul_1_32::
    .string "Who knowing the judgment of God,\n"
    .string "that they which commit such things\l"
    .string "are worthy of death, not only do the\l"
    .string "same, but have pleasure in them that\l"
    .string "do them$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_1::
    .string "Therefore thou art inexcusable, O\n"
    .string "man, whosoever thou art that judgest:\l"
    .string "for wherein thou judgest another,\l"
    .string "thou condemnest thyself; for thou\l"
    .string "that judgest doest the same things.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_2::
    .string "But we are sure that the judgment of\n"
    .string "God is according to truth against\l"
    .string "them which commit such things.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_3::
    .string "And thinkest thou this, O man, that\n"
    .string "judgest them which do such things,\l"
    .string "and doest the same, that thou shalt\l"
    .string "escape the judgment of God?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_4::
    .string "Or despisest thou the riches of his\n"
    .string "goodness and forbearance and\l"
    .string "longsuffering; not knowing that the\l"
    .string "goodness of God leadeth thee to\l"
    .string "repentance?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_5::
    .string "But after thy hardness and\n"
    .string "impenitent heart treasurest up unto\l"
    .string "thyself wrath against the day of\l"
    .string "wrath and revelation of the\l"
    .string "righteous judgment of God;"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_6::
    .string "Who will render to every man\n"
    .string "according to his deeds:"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_7::
    .string "To them who by patient continuance\n"
    .string "in well doing seek for glory and\l"
    .string "honour and immortality, eternal\l"
    .string "life:"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_8::
    .string "But unto them that are contentious,\n"
    .string "and do not obey the truth, but obey\l"
    .string "unrighteousness, indignation and\l"
    .string "wrath,"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_9::
    .string "Tribulation and anguish, upon\n"
    .string "every soul of man that doeth evil,\l"
    .string "of the Jew first, and also of the\l"
    .string "Gentile;"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_10::
    .string "But glory, honour, and peace, to\n"
    .string "every man that worketh good, to the\l"
    .string "Jew first, and also to the Gentile:"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_11::
    .string "For there is no respect of persons\n"
    .string "with God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_12::
    .string "For as many as have sinned without\n"
    .string "law shall also perish without\l"
    .string "law: and as many as have sinned in the\l"
    .string "law shall be judged by the law;"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_13::
    .string "(For not the hearers of the law are\n"
    .string "just before God, but the doers of the\l"
    .string "law shall be justified$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_14::
    .string "For when the Gentiles, which have\n"
    .string "not the law, do by nature the things\l"
    .string "contained in the law, these, having\l"
    .string "not the law, are a law unto\l"
    .string "themselves:"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_15::
    .string "Which shew the work of the law\n"
    .string "written in their hearts, their\l"
    .string "conscience also bearing witness, and\l"
    .string "their thoughts the mean while\l"
    .string "accusing or else excusing one\l"
    .string "another;)"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_16::
    .string "In the day when God shall judge the\n"
    .string "secrets of men by Jesus Christ\l"
    .string "according to my gospel$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_17::
    .string "Behold, thou art called a Jew, and\n"
    .string "restest in the law, and makest thy\l"
    .string "boast of God,"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_18::
    .string "And knowest his will, and\n"
    .string "approvest the things that are more\l"
    .string "excellent, being instructed out of\l"
    .string "the law;"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_19::
    .string "And art confident that thou thyself\n"
    .string "art a guide of the blind, a light of\l"
    .string "them which are in darkness,"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_20::
    .string "An instructor of the foolish, a\n"
    .string "teacher of babes, which hast the form\l"
    .string "of knowledge and of the truth in the\l"
    .string "law$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_21::
    .string "Thou therefore which teachest\n"
    .string "another, teachest thou not thyself?\l"
    .string "thou that preachest a man should\l"
    .string "not steal, dost thou steal?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_22::
    .string "Thou that sayest a man should not\n"
    .string "commit adultery, dost thou commit\l"
    .string "adultery? thou that abhorrest\l"
    .string "idols, dost thou commit sacrilege?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_23::
    .string "Thou that makest thy boast of the\n"
    .string "law, through breaking the law\l"
    .string "dishonourest thou God?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_24::
    .string "For the name of God is blasphemed\n"
    .string "among the Gentiles through you, as\l"
    .string "it is written$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_25::
    .string "For circumcision verily profiteth,\n"
    .string "if thou keep the law: but if thou be\l"
    .string "a breaker of the law, thy\l"
    .string "circumcision is made uncircumcision.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_26::
    .string "Therefore if the uncircumcision\n"
    .string "keep the righteousness of the law,\l"
    .string "shall not his uncircumcision be\l"
    .string "counted for circumcision?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_27::
    .string "And shall not uncircumcision which\n"
    .string "is by nature, if it fulfil the law,\l"
    .string "judge thee, who by the letter and\l"
    .string "circumcision dost transgress the\l"
    .string "law?"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_28::
    .string "For he is not a Jew, which is one\n"
    .string "outwardly; neither is that\l"
    .string "circumcision, which is outward in the\l"
    .string "flesh:"
Bible_Text_Paul_2_29::
    .string "But he is a Jew, which is one\n"
    .string "inwardly; and circumcision is that\l"
    .string "of the heart, in the spirit, and not\l"
    .string "in the letter; whose praise is not\l"
    .string "of men, but of God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_1::
    .string "What advantage then hath the Jew? or\n"
    .string "what profit is there of\l"
    .string "circumcision?"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_2::
    .string "Much every way: chiefly, because\n"
    .string "that unto them were committed the\l"
    .string "oracles of God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_3::
    .string "For what if some did not believe?\n"
    .string "shall their unbelief make the\l"
    .string "faith of God without effect?"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_4::
    .string "God forbid: yea, let God be true,\n"
    .string "but every man a liar; as it is\l"
    .string "written, That thou mightest be\l"
    .string "justified in thy sayings, and\l"
    .string "mightest overcome when thou art\l"
    .string "judged$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_5::
    .string "But if our unrighteousness commend\n"
    .string "the righteousness of God, what\l"
    .string "shall we say? Is God unrighteous who\l"
    .string "taketh vengeance? (I speak as a man)"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_6::
    .string "God forbid: for then how shall God\n"
    .string "judge the world?"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_7::
    .string "For if the truth of God hath more\n"
    .string "abounded through my lie unto his\l"
    .string "glory; why yet am I also judged as a\l"
    .string "sinner?"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_8::
    .string "And not rather, (as we be\n"
    .string "slanderously reported, and as some\l"
    .string "affirm that we say,) Let us do evil,\l"
    .string "that good may come? whose damnation\l"
    .string "is just$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_9::
    .string "What then? are we better than they?\n"
    .string "No, in no wise: for we have before\l"
    .string "proved both Jews and Gentiles, that\l"
    .string "they are all under sin;"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_10::
    .string "As it is written, There is none\n"
    .string "righteous, no, not one:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_11::
    .string "There is none that understandeth,\n"
    .string "there is none that seeketh after God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_12::
    .string "They are all gone out of the way,\n"
    .string "they are together become\l"
    .string "unprofitable; there is none that\l"
    .string "doeth good, no, not one.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_13::
    .string "Their throat is an open sepulchre;\n"
    .string "with their tongues they have used\l"
    .string "deceit; the poison of asps is under\l"
    .string "their lips:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_14::
    .string "Whose mouth is full of cursing and\n"
    .string "bitterness:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_15::
    .string "Their feet are swift to shed blood:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_16::
    .string "Destruction and misery are in their\n"
    .string "ways:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_17::
    .string "And the way of peace have they not\n"
    .string "known:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_18::
    .string "There is no fear of God before their\n"
    .string "eyes$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_19::
    .string "Now we know that what things soever\n"
    .string "the law saith, it saith to them who\l"
    .string "are under the law: that every mouth\l"
    .string "may be stopped, and all the world\l"
    .string "may become guilty before God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_20::
    .string "Therefore by the deeds of the law\n"
    .string "there shall no flesh be justified\l"
    .string "in his sight: for by the law is the\l"
    .string "knowledge of sin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_21::
    .string "But now the righteousness of God\n"
    .string "without the law is manifested, being\l"
    .string "witnessed by the law and the\l"
    .string "prophets;"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_22::
    .string "Even the righteousness of God which\n"
    .string "is by faith of Jesus Christ unto all\l"
    .string "and upon all them that believe:\l"
    .string "for there is no difference:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_23::
    .string "For all have sinned, and come short\n"
    .string "of the glory of God;"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_24::
    .string "Being justified freely by his grace\n"
    .string "through the redemption that is in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_25::
    .string "Whom God hath set forth to be a\n"
    .string "propitiation through faith in his\l"
    .string "blood, to declare his righteousness\l"
    .string "for the remission of sins that are\l"
    .string "past, through the forbearance of God;"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_26::
    .string "To declare, I say, at this time his\n"
    .string "righteousness: that he might be just,\l"
    .string "and the justifier of him which\l"
    .string "believeth in Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_27::
    .string "Where is boasting then? It is\n"
    .string "excluded. By what law? of works?\l"
    .string "Nay: but by the law of faith.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_28::
    .string "Therefore we conclude that a man is\n"
    .string "justified by faith without the deeds\l"
    .string "of the law.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_29::
    .string "Is he the God of the Jews only? is\n"
    .string "he not also of the Gentiles? Yes, of\l"
    .string "the Gentiles also:"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_30::
    .string "Seeing it is one God, which shall\n"
    .string "justify the circumcision by faith,\l"
    .string "and uncircumcision through faith$"
Bible_Text_Paul_3_31::
    .string "Do we then make void the law\n"
    .string "through faith? God forbid: yea, we\l"
    .string "establish the law.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_1::
    .string "What shall we say then that\n"
    .string "Abraham our father, as pertaining to\l"
    .string "the flesh, hath found?"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_2::
    .string "For if Abraham were justified by\n"
    .string "works, he hath whereof to glory; but\l"
    .string "not before God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_3::
    .string "For what saith the scripture?\n"
    .string "Abraham believed God, and it was\l"
    .string "counted unto him for righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_4::
    .string "Now to him that worketh is the\n"
    .string "reward not reckoned of grace, but of\l"
    .string "debt.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_5::
    .string "But to him that worketh not, but\n"
    .string "believeth on him that justifieth the\l"
    .string "ungodly, his faith is counted for\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_6::
    .string "Even as David also describeth the\n"
    .string "blessedness of the man, unto whom\l"
    .string "God imputeth righteousness without\l"
    .string "works,"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_7::
    .string "Saying, Blessed are they whose\n"
    .string "iniquities are forgiven, and whose\l"
    .string "sins are covered$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_8::
    .string "Blessed is the man to whom the Lord\n"
    .string "will not impute sin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_9::
    .string "Cometh this blessedness then upon\n"
    .string "the circumcision only, or upon the\l"
    .string "uncircumcision also? for we say that\l"
    .string "faith was reckoned to Abraham for\l"
    .string "righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_10::
    .string "How was it then reckoned? when he\n"
    .string "was in circumcision, or in\l"
    .string "uncircumcision? Not in circumcision,\l"
    .string "but in uncircumcision.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_11::
    .string "And he received the sign of\n"
    .string "circumcision, a seal of the\l"
    .string "righteousness of the faith which he\l"
    .string "had yet being uncircumcised: that he\l"
    .string "might be the father of all them that\l"
    .string "believe, though they be not\l"
    .string "circumcised; that righteousness\l"
    .string "might be imputed unto them also:"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_12::
    .string "And the father of circumcision to\n"
    .string "them who are not of the circumcision\l"
    .string "only, but who also walk in the\l"
    .string "steps of that faith of our father\l"
    .string "Abraham, which he had being yet\l"
    .string "uncircumcised$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_13::
    .string "For the promise, that he should be\n"
    .string "the heir of the world, was not to\l"
    .string "Abraham, or to his seed, through the\l"
    .string "law, but through the righteousness of\l"
    .string "faith.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_14::
    .string "For if they which are of the law be\n"
    .string "heirs, faith is made void, and the\l"
    .string "promise made of none effect:"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_15::
    .string "Because the law worketh wrath: for\n"
    .string "where no law is, there is no\l"
    .string "transgression$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_16::
    .string "Therefore it is of faith, that it\n"
    .string "might be by grace; to the end the\l"
    .string "promise might be sure to all the\l"
    .string "seed; not to that only which is of\l"
    .string "the law, but to that also which is\l"
    .string "of the faith of Abraham; who is the\l"
    .string "father of us all,"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_17::
    .string "(As it is written, I have made thee a\n"
    .string "father of many nations,) before him\l"
    .string "whom he believed, even God, who\l"
    .string "quickeneth the dead, and calleth\l"
    .string "those things which be not as though\l"
    .string "they were$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_18::
    .string "Who against hope believed in hope,\n"
    .string "that he might become the father of\l"
    .string "many nations, according to that which\l"
    .string "was spoken, So shall thy seed be.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_19::
    .string "And being not weak in faith, he\n"
    .string "considered not his own body now dead,\l"
    .string "when he was about an hundred years\l"
    .string "old, neither yet the deadness of\l"
    .string "Sarah’s womb:"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_20::
    .string "He staggered not at the promise of\n"
    .string "God through unbelief; but was strong\l"
    .string "in faith, giving glory to God;"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_21::
    .string "And being fully persuaded that,\n"
    .string "what he had promised, he was able\l"
    .string "also to perform$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_22::
    .string "And therefore it was imputed to him\n"
    .string "for righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_23::
    .string "Now it was not written for his sake\n"
    .string "alone, that it was imputed to him;"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_24::
    .string "But for us also, to whom it shall\n"
    .string "be imputed, if we believe on him\l"
    .string "that raised up Jesus our Lord from\l"
    .string "the dead;"
Bible_Text_Paul_4_25::
    .string "Who was delivered for our offences,\n"
    .string "and was raised again for our\l"
    .string "justification$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_1::
    .string "Therefore being justified by faith,\n"
    .string "we have peace with God through our\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_2::
    .string "By whom also we have access by\n"
    .string "faith into this grace wherein we\l"
    .string "stand, and rejoice in hope of the\l"
    .string "glory of God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_3::
    .string "And not only so, but we glory in\n"
    .string "tribulations also: knowing that\l"
    .string "tribulation worketh patience;"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_4::
    .string "And patience, experience; and\n"
    .string "experience, hope:"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_5::
    .string "And hope maketh not ashamed;\n"
    .string "because the love of God is shed\l"
    .string "abroad in our hearts by the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost which is given unto us$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_6::
    .string "For when we were yet without\n"
    .string "strength, in due time Christ died for\l"
    .string "the ungodly.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_7::
    .string "For scarcely for a righteous man\n"
    .string "will one die: yet peradventure for\l"
    .string "a good man some would even dare to\l"
    .string "die.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_8::
    .string "But God commendeth his love toward\n"
    .string "us, in that, while we were yet\l"
    .string "sinners, Christ died for us.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_9::
    .string "Much more then, being now justified\n"
    .string "by his blood, we shall be saved\l"
    .string "from wrath through him.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_10::
    .string "For if, when we were enemies, we\n"
    .string "were reconciled to God by the death\l"
    .string "of his Son, much more, being\l"
    .string "reconciled, we shall be saved by\l"
    .string "his life.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_11::
    .string "And not only so, but we also joy in\n"
    .string "God through our Lord Jesus Christ, by\l"
    .string "whom we have now received the\l"
    .string "atonement.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_12::
    .string "Wherefore, as by one man sin entered\n"
    .string "into the world, and death by sin; and\l"
    .string "so death passed upon all men, for\l"
    .string "that all have sinned:"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_13::
    .string "(For until the law sin was in the\n"
    .string "world: but sin is not imputed when\l"
    .string "there is no law$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_14::
    .string "Nevertheless death reigned from\n"
    .string "Adam to Moses, even over them that\l"
    .string "had not sinned after the similitude\l"
    .string "of Adam’s transgression, who is the\l"
    .string "figure of him that was to come.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_15::
    .string "But not as the offence, so also is\n"
    .string "the free gift. For if through the\l"
    .string "offence of one many be dead, much\l"
    .string "more the grace of God, and the gift by\l"
    .string "grace, which is by one man, Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, hath abounded unto many.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_16::
    .string "And not as it was by one that sinned,\n"
    .string "so is the gift: for the judgment was\l"
    .string "by one to condemnation, but the free\l"
    .string "gift is of many offences unto\l"
    .string "justification.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_17::
    .string "For if by one man’s offence death\n"
    .string "reigned by one; much more they which\l"
    .string "receive abundance of grace and of the\l"
    .string "gift of righteousness shall reign\l"
    .string "in life by one, Jesus Christ.)"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_18::
    .string "Therefore as by the offence of one\n"
    .string "judgment came upon all men to\l"
    .string "condemnation; even so by the\l"
    .string "righteousness of one the free gift\l"
    .string "came upon all men unto\l"
    .string "justification of life$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_19::
    .string "For as by one man’s disobedience\n"
    .string "many were made sinners, so by the\l"
    .string "obedience of one shall many be made\l"
    .string "righteous.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_20::
    .string "Moreover the law entered, that the\n"
    .string "offence might abound. But where sin\l"
    .string "abounded, grace did much more abound:"
Bible_Text_Paul_5_21::
    .string "That as sin hath reigned unto death,\n"
    .string "even so might grace reign through\l"
    .string "righteousness unto eternal life by\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ our Lord$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_1::
    .string "What shall we say then? Shall we\n"
    .string "continue in sin, that grace may\l"
    .string "abound?"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_2::
    .string "God forbid. How shall we, that are\n"
    .string "dead to sin, live any longer\l"
    .string "therein?"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_3::
    .string "Know ye not, that so many of us as\n"
    .string "were baptized into Jesus Christ were\l"
    .string "baptized into his death?"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_4::
    .string "Therefore we are buried with him by\n"
    .string "baptism into death: that like as\l"
    .string "Christ was raised up from the dead\l"
    .string "by the glory of the Father, even so\l"
    .string "we also should walk in newness of\l"
    .string "life$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_5::
    .string "For if we have been planted\n"
    .string "together in the likeness of his\l"
    .string "death, we shall be also in the\l"
    .string "likeness of his resurrection:"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_6::
    .string "Knowing this, that our old man is\n"
    .string "crucified with him, that the body of\l"
    .string "sin might be destroyed, that\l"
    .string "henceforth we should not serve sin$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_7::
    .string "For he that is dead is freed from\n"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_8::
    .string "Now if we be dead with Christ, we\n"
    .string "believe that we shall also live\l"
    .string "with him:"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_9::
    .string "Knowing that Christ being raised\n"
    .string "from the dead dieth no more; death\l"
    .string "hath no more dominion over him$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_10::
    .string "For in that he died, he died unto sin\n"
    .string "once: but in that he liveth, he\l"
    .string "liveth unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_11::
    .string "Likewise reckon ye also yourselves\n"
    .string "to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive\l"
    .string "unto God through Jesus Christ our\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_12::
    .string "Let not sin therefore reign in your\n"
    .string "mortal body, that ye should obey it\l"
    .string "in the lusts thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_13::
    .string "Neither yield ye your members as\n"
    .string "instruments of unrighteousness unto\l"
    .string "sin: but yield yourselves unto God,\l"
    .string "as those that are alive from the\l"
    .string "dead, and your members as instruments\l"
    .string "of righteousness unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_14::
    .string "For sin shall not have dominion\n"
    .string "over you: for ye are not under the\l"
    .string "law, but under grace.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_15::
    .string "What then? shall we sin, because we\n"
    .string "are not under the law, but under\l"
    .string "grace? God forbid.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_16::
    .string "Know ye not, that to whom ye yield\n"
    .string "yourselves servants to obey, his\l"
    .string "servants ye are to whom ye obey;\l"
    .string "whether of sin unto death, or of\l"
    .string "obedience unto righteousness?"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_17::
    .string "But God be thanked, that ye were the\n"
    .string "servants of sin, but ye have obeyed\l"
    .string "from the heart that form of doctrine\l"
    .string "which was delivered you$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_18::
    .string "Being then made free from sin, ye\n"
    .string "became the servants of righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_19::
    .string "I speak after the manner of men\n"
    .string "because of the infirmity of your\l"
    .string "flesh: for as ye have yielded your\l"
    .string "members servants to uncleanness and\l"
    .string "to iniquity unto iniquity; even so\l"
    .string "now yield your members servants to\l"
    .string "righteousness unto holiness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_20::
    .string "For when ye were the servants of\n"
    .string "sin, ye were free from righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_21::
    .string "What fruit had ye then in those\n"
    .string "things whereof ye are now ashamed?\l"
    .string "for the end of those things is death.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_22::
    .string "But now being made free from sin,\n"
    .string "and become servants to God, ye have\l"
    .string "your fruit unto holiness, and the\l"
    .string "end everlasting life.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_6_23::
    .string "For the wages of sin is death; but\n"
    .string "the gift of God is eternal life\l"
    .string "through Jesus Christ our Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_1::
    .string "Know ye not, brethren, (for I speak\n"
    .string "to them that know the law,) how that\l"
    .string "the law hath dominion over a man as\l"
    .string "long as he liveth?"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_2::
    .string "For the woman which hath an husband\n"
    .string "is bound by the law to her husband so\l"
    .string "long as he liveth; but if the husband\l"
    .string "be dead, she is loosed from the law\l"
    .string "of her husband$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_3::
    .string "So then if, while her husband\n"
    .string "liveth, she be married to another\l"
    .string "man, she shall be called an\l"
    .string "adulteress: but if her husband be\l"
    .string "dead, she is free from that law; so\l"
    .string "that she is no adulteress, though\l"
    .string "she be married to another man.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_4::
    .string "Wherefore, my brethren, ye also are\n"
    .string "become dead to the law by the body of\l"
    .string "Christ; that ye should be married to\l"
    .string "another, even to him who is raised\l"
    .string "from the dead, that we should bring\l"
    .string "forth fruit unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_5::
    .string "For when we were in the flesh, the\n"
    .string "motions of sins, which were by the\l"
    .string "law, did work in our members to bring\l"
    .string "forth fruit unto death.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_6::
    .string "But now we are delivered from the\n"
    .string "law, that being dead wherein we were\l"
    .string "held; that we should serve in\l"
    .string "newness of spirit, and not in the\l"
    .string "oldness of the letter.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_7::
    .string "What shall we say then? Is the law\n"
    .string "sin? God forbid. Nay, I had not known\l"
    .string "sin, but by the law: for I had not\l"
    .string "known lust, except the law had\l"
    .string "said, Thou shalt not covet.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_8::
    .string "But sin, taking occasion by the\n"
    .string "commandment, wrought in me all\l"
    .string "manner of concupiscence. For without\l"
    .string "the law sin was dead.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_9::
    .string "For I was alive without the law\n"
    .string "once: but when the commandment came,\l"
    .string "sin revived, and I died.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_10::
    .string "And the commandment, which was\n"
    .string "ordained to life, I found to be unto\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_11::
    .string "For sin, taking occasion by the\n"
    .string "commandment, deceived me, and by it\l"
    .string "slew me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_12::
    .string "Wherefore the law is holy, and the\n"
    .string "commandment holy, and just, and good.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_13::
    .string "Was then that which is good made\n"
    .string "death unto me? God forbid. But sin,\l"
    .string "that it might appear sin, working\l"
    .string "death in me by that which is good;\l"
    .string "that sin by the commandment might\l"
    .string "become exceeding sinful.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_14::
    .string "For we know that the law is\n"
    .string "spiritual: but I am carnal, sold\l"
    .string "under sin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_15::
    .string "For that which I do I allow not:\n"
    .string "for what I would, that do I not; but\l"
    .string "what I hate, that do I.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_16::
    .string "If then I do that which I would not,\n"
    .string "I consent unto the law that it is\l"
    .string "good.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_17::
    .string "Now then it is no more I that do it,\n"
    .string "but sin that dwelleth in me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_18::
    .string "For I know that in me (that is, in my\n"
    .string "flesh,) dwelleth no good thing: for\l"
    .string "to will is present with me; but how\l"
    .string "to perform that which is good I find\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_19::
    .string "For the good that I would I do not:\n"
    .string "but the evil which I would not, that\l"
    .string "I do.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_20::
    .string "Now if I do that I would not, it is\n"
    .string "no more I that do it, but sin that\l"
    .string "dwelleth in me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_21::
    .string "I find then a law, that, when I\n"
    .string "would do good, evil is present with\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_22::
    .string "For I delight in the law of God\n"
    .string "after the inward man:"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_23::
    .string "But I see another law in my members,\n"
    .string "warring against the law of my mind,\l"
    .string "and bringing me into captivity to\l"
    .string "the law of sin which is in my members$"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_24::
    .string "O wretched man that I am! who shall\n"
    .string "deliver me from the body of this\l"
    .string "death?"
Bible_Text_Paul_7_25::
    .string "I thank God through Jesus Christ our\n"
    .string "Lord. So then with the mind I myself\l"
    .string "serve the law of God; but with the\l"
    .string "flesh the law of sin$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_1::
    .string "There is therefore now no\n"
    .string "condemnation to them which are in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus, who walk not after the\l"
    .string "flesh, but after the Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_2::
    .string "For the law of the Spirit of life\n"
    .string "in Christ Jesus hath made me free\l"
    .string "from the law of sin and death.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_3::
    .string "For what the law could not do, in\n"
    .string "that it was weak through the flesh,\l"
    .string "God sending his own Son in the\l"
    .string "likeness of sinful flesh, and for\l"
    .string "sin, condemned sin in the flesh:"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_4::
    .string "That the righteousness of the law\n"
    .string "might be fulfilled in us, who walk\l"
    .string "not after the flesh, but after the\l"
    .string "Spirit$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_5::
    .string "For they that are after the flesh\n"
    .string "do mind the things of the flesh; but\l"
    .string "they that are after the Spirit the\l"
    .string "things of the Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_6::
    .string "For to be carnally minded is death;\n"
    .string "but to be spiritually minded is\l"
    .string "life and peace.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_7::
    .string "Because the carnal mind is enmity\n"
    .string "against God: for it is not subject to\l"
    .string "the law of God, neither indeed can\l"
    .string "be.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_8::
    .string "So then they that are in the flesh\n"
    .string "cannot please God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_9::
    .string "But ye are not in the flesh, but in\n"
    .string "the Spirit, if so be that the Spirit\l"
    .string "of God dwell in you. Now if any man\l"
    .string "have not the Spirit of Christ, he is\l"
    .string "none of his.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_10::
    .string "And if Christ be in you, the body is\n"
    .string "dead because of sin; but the Spirit\l"
    .string "is life because of righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_11::
    .string "But if the Spirit of him that\n"
    .string "raised up Jesus from the dead dwell\l"
    .string "in you, he that raised up Christ from\l"
    .string "the dead shall also quicken your\l"
    .string "mortal bodies by his Spirit that\l"
    .string "dwelleth in you.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_12::
    .string "Therefore, brethren, we are debtors,\n"
    .string "not to the flesh, to live after the\l"
    .string "flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_13::
    .string "For if ye live after the flesh, ye\n"
    .string "shall die: but if ye through the\l"
    .string "Spirit do mortify the deeds of the\l"
    .string "body, ye shall live.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_14::
    .string "For as many as are led by the\n"
    .string "Spirit of God, they are the sons of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_15::
    .string "For ye have not received the spirit\n"
    .string "of bondage again to fear; but ye have\l"
    .string "received the Spirit of adoption,\l"
    .string "whereby we cry, Abba, Father.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_16::
    .string "The Spirit itself beareth witness\n"
    .string "with our spirit, that we are the\l"
    .string "children of God:"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_17::
    .string "And if children, then heirs; heirs\n"
    .string "of God, and joint-heirs with Christ;\l"
    .string "if so be that we suffer with him, that\l"
    .string "we may be also glorified together$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_18::
    .string "For I reckon that the sufferings of\n"
    .string "this present time are not worthy to\l"
    .string "be compared with the glory which\l"
    .string "shall be revealed in us.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_19::
    .string "For the earnest expectation of the\n"
    .string "creature waiteth for the\l"
    .string "manifestation of the sons of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_20::
    .string "For the creature was made subject to\n"
    .string "vanity, not willingly, but by\l"
    .string "reason of him who hath subjected the\l"
    .string "same in hope,"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_21::
    .string "Because the creature itself also\n"
    .string "shall be delivered from the\l"
    .string "bondage of corruption into the\l"
    .string "glorious liberty of the children\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_22::
    .string "For we know that the whole creation\n"
    .string "groaneth and travaileth in pain\l"
    .string "together until now.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_23::
    .string "And not only they, but ourselves\n"
    .string "also, which have the firstfruits of\l"
    .string "the Spirit, even we ourselves groan\l"
    .string "within ourselves, waiting for the\l"
    .string "adoption, to wit, the redemption of\l"
    .string "our body.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_24::
    .string "For we are saved by hope: but hope\n"
    .string "that is seen is not hope: for what a\l"
    .string "man seeth, why doth he yet hope for?"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_25::
    .string "But if we hope for that we see not,\n"
    .string "then do we with patience wait for it$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_26::
    .string "Likewise the Spirit also helpeth\n"
    .string "our infirmities: for we know not what\l"
    .string "we should pray for as we ought: but\l"
    .string "the Spirit itself maketh\l"
    .string "intercession for us with groanings\l"
    .string "which cannot be uttered.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_27::
    .string "And he that searcheth the hearts\n"
    .string "knoweth what is the mind of the\l"
    .string "Spirit, because he maketh\l"
    .string "intercession for the saints\l"
    .string "according to the will of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_28::
    .string "And we know that all things work\n"
    .string "together for good to them that love\l"
    .string "God, to them who are the called\l"
    .string "according to his purpose.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_29::
    .string "For whom he did foreknow, he also\n"
    .string "did predestinate to be conformed to\l"
    .string "the image of his Son, that he might be\l"
    .string "the firstborn among many brethren.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_30::
    .string "Moreover whom he did predestinate,\n"
    .string "them he also called: and whom he\l"
    .string "called, them he also justified: and\l"
    .string "whom he justified, them he also\l"
    .string "glorified.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_31::
    .string "What shall we then say to these\n"
    .string "things? If God be for us, who can be\l"
    .string "against us?"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_32::
    .string "He that spared not his own Son, but\n"
    .string "delivered him up for us all, how\l"
    .string "shall he not with him also freely\l"
    .string "give us all things?"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_33::
    .string "Who shall lay any thing to the\n"
    .string "charge of God’s elect? It is God that\l"
    .string "justifieth$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_34::
    .string "Who is he that condemneth? It is\n"
    .string "Christ that died, yea rather, that is\l"
    .string "risen again, who is even at the right\l"
    .string "hand of God, who also maketh\l"
    .string "intercession for us.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_35::
    .string "Who shall separate us from the\n"
    .string "love of Christ? shall tribulation,\l"
    .string "or distress, or persecution, or\l"
    .string "famine, or nakedness, or peril, or\l"
    .string "sword?"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_36::
    .string "As it is written, For thy sake we are\n"
    .string "killed all the day long; we are\l"
    .string "accounted as sheep for the slaughter$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_37::
    .string "Nay, in all these things we are\n"
    .string "more than conquerors through him\l"
    .string "that loved us.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_38::
    .string "For I am persuaded, that neither\n"
    .string "death, nor life, nor angels, nor\l"
    .string "principalities, nor powers, nor\l"
    .string "things present, nor things to come,"
Bible_Text_Paul_8_39::
    .string "Nor height, nor depth, nor any\n"
    .string "other creature, shall be able to\l"
    .string "separate us from the love of God,\l"
    .string "which is in Christ Jesus our Lord$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_1::
    .string "I say the truth in Christ, I lie\n"
    .string "not, my conscience also bearing me\l"
    .string "witness in the Holy Ghost,"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_2::
    .string "That I have great heaviness and\n"
    .string "continual sorrow in my heart$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_3::
    .string "For I could wish that myself were\n"
    .string "accursed from Christ for my brethren,\l"
    .string "my kinsmen according to the flesh:"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_4::
    .string "Who are Israelites; to whom\n"
    .string "pertaineth the adoption, and the\l"
    .string "glory, and the covenants, and the\l"
    .string "giving of the law, and the service of\l"
    .string "God, and the promises;"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_5::
    .string "Whose are the fathers, and of whom\n"
    .string "as concerning the flesh Christ came,\l"
    .string "who is over all, God blessed for\l"
    .string "ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_6::
    .string "Not as though the word of God hath\n"
    .string "taken none effect. For they are not\l"
    .string "all Israel, which are of Israel:"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_7::
    .string "Neither, because they are the seed\n"
    .string "of Abraham, are they all children:\l"
    .string "but, In Isaac shall thy seed be\l"
    .string "called$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_8::
    .string "That is, They which are the\n"
    .string "children of the flesh, these are not\l"
    .string "the children of God: but the\l"
    .string "children of the promise are counted\l"
    .string "for the seed.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_9::
    .string "For this is the word of promise, At\n"
    .string "this time will I come, and Sarah\l"
    .string "shall have a son.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_10::
    .string "And not only this; but when Rebecca\n"
    .string "also had conceived by one, even by\l"
    .string "our father Isaac;"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_11::
    .string "(For the children being not yet\n"
    .string "born, neither having done any good or\l"
    .string "evil, that the purpose of God\l"
    .string "according to election might stand,\l"
    .string "not of works, but of him that\l"
    .string "calleth;)"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_12::
    .string "It was said unto her, The elder\n"
    .string "shall serve the younger$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_13::
    .string "As it is written, Jacob have I\n"
    .string "loved, but Esau have I hated.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_14::
    .string "What shall we say then? Is there\n"
    .string "unrighteousness with God? God forbid.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_15::
    .string "For he saith to Moses, I will have\n"
    .string "mercy on whom I will have mercy, and\l"
    .string "I will have compassion on whom I\l"
    .string "will have compassion.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_16::
    .string "So then it is not of him that\n"
    .string "willeth, nor of him that runneth,\l"
    .string "but of God that sheweth mercy.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_17::
    .string "For the scripture saith unto\n"
    .string "Pharaoh, Even for this same purpose\l"
    .string "have I raised thee up, that I might\l"
    .string "shew my power in thee, and that my\l"
    .string "name might be declared throughout\l"
    .string "all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_18::
    .string "Therefore hath he mercy on whom he\n"
    .string "will have mercy, and whom he will\l"
    .string "he hardeneth.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_19::
    .string "Thou wilt say then unto me, Why doth\n"
    .string "he yet find fault? For who hath\l"
    .string "resisted his will?"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_20::
    .string "Nay but, O man, who art thou that\n"
    .string "repliest against God? Shall the\l"
    .string "thing formed say to him that formed\l"
    .string "it, Why hast thou made me thus?"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_21::
    .string "Hath not the potter power over the\n"
    .string "clay, of the same lump to make one\l"
    .string "vessel unto honour, and another unto\l"
    .string "dishonour?"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_22::
    .string "What if God, willing to shew his\n"
    .string "wrath, and to make his power known,\l"
    .string "endured with much longsuffering the\l"
    .string "vessels of wrath fitted to\l"
    .string "destruction:"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_23::
    .string "And that he might make known the\n"
    .string "riches of his glory on the vessels\l"
    .string "of mercy, which he had afore\l"
    .string "prepared unto glory,"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_24::
    .string "Even us, whom he hath called, not\n"
    .string "of the Jews only, but also of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles?"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_25::
    .string "As he saith also in Osee, I will\n"
    .string "call them my people, which were\l"
    .string "not my people; and her beloved,\l"
    .string "which was not beloved$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_26::
    .string "And it shall come to pass, that in\n"
    .string "the place where it was said unto\l"
    .string "them, Ye are not my people; there\l"
    .string "shall they be called the children\l"
    .string "of the living God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_27::
    .string "Esaias also crieth concerning\n"
    .string "Israel, Though the number of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel be as the sand of\l"
    .string "the sea, a remnant shall be saved:"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_28::
    .string "For he will finish the work, and\n"
    .string "cut it short in righteousness:\l"
    .string "because a short work will the Lord\l"
    .string "make upon the earth$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_29::
    .string "And as Esaias said before, Except\n"
    .string "the Lord of Sabaoth had left us a\l"
    .string "seed, we had been as Sodoma, and been\l"
    .string "made like unto Gomorrha.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_30::
    .string "What shall we say then? That the\n"
    .string "Gentiles, which followed not after\l"
    .string "righteousness, have attained to\l"
    .string "righteousness, even the\l"
    .string "righteousness which is of faith.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_31::
    .string "But Israel, which followed after\n"
    .string "the law of righteousness, hath not\l"
    .string "attained to the law of righteousness.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_32::
    .string "Wherefore? Because they sought it\n"
    .string "not by faith, but as it were by the\l"
    .string "works of the law. For they stumbled\l"
    .string "at that stumblingstone;"
Bible_Text_Paul_9_33::
    .string "As it is written, Behold, I lay in\n"
    .string "Sion a stumblingstone and rock of\l"
    .string "offence: and whosoever believeth on\l"
    .string "him shall not be ashamed$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_1::
    .string "Brethren, my heart’s desire and\n"
    .string "prayer to God for Israel is, that\l"
    .string "they might be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_2::
    .string "For I bear them record that they\n"
    .string "have a zeal of God, but not according\l"
    .string "to knowledge.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_3::
    .string "For they being ignorant of God’s\n"
    .string "righteousness, and going about to\l"
    .string "establish their own righteousness,\l"
    .string "have not submitted themselves unto\l"
    .string "the righteousness of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_4::
    .string "For Christ is the end of the law for\n"
    .string "righteousness to every one that\l"
    .string "believeth.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_5::
    .string "For Moses describeth the\n"
    .string "righteousness which is of the law,\l"
    .string "That the man which doeth those things\l"
    .string "shall live by them.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_6::
    .string "But the righteousness which is of\n"
    .string "faith speaketh on this wise, Say not\l"
    .string "in thine heart, Who shall ascend\l"
    .string "into heaven? (that is, to bring\l"
    .string "Christ down from above:)"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_7::
    .string "Or, Who shall descend into the\n"
    .string "deep? (that is, to bring up Christ\l"
    .string "again from the dead.)"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_8::
    .string "But what saith it? The word is nigh\n"
    .string "thee, even in thy mouth, and in thy\l"
    .string "heart: that is, the word of faith,\l"
    .string "which we preach;"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_9::
    .string "That if thou shalt confess with thy\n"
    .string "mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt\l"
    .string "believe in thine heart that God hath\l"
    .string "raised him from the dead, thou shalt\l"
    .string "be saved$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_10::
    .string "For with the heart man believeth\n"
    .string "unto righteousness; and with the\l"
    .string "mouth confession is made unto\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_11::
    .string "For the scripture saith, Whosoever\n"
    .string "believeth on him shall not be\l"
    .string "ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_12::
    .string "For there is no difference between\n"
    .string "the Jew and the Greek: for the same\l"
    .string "Lord over all is rich unto all\l"
    .string "that call upon him.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_13::
    .string "For whosoever shall call upon\n"
    .string "the name of the Lord shall be saved.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_14::
    .string "How then shall they call on him\n"
    .string "in whom they have not believed? and\l"
    .string "how shall they believe in him of\l"
    .string "whom they have not heard? and how\l"
    .string "shall they hear without a preacher?"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_15::
    .string "And how shall they preach, except\n"
    .string "they be sent? as it is written, How\l"
    .string "beautiful are the feet of them that\l"
    .string "preach the gospel of peace, and\l"
    .string "bring glad tidings of good things!"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_16::
    .string "But they have not all obeyed the\n"
    .string "gospel. For Esaias saith, Lord, who\l"
    .string "hath believed our report?"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_17::
    .string "So then faith cometh by hearing, and\n"
    .string "hearing by the word of God$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_18::
    .string "But I say, Have they not heard? Yes\n"
    .string "verily, their sound went into all\l"
    .string "the earth, and their words unto the\l"
    .string "ends of the world.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_19::
    .string "But I say, Did not Israel know?\n"
    .string "First Moses saith, I will provoke\l"
    .string "you to jealousy by them that are no\l"
    .string "people, and by a foolish nation I\l"
    .string "will anger you.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_20::
    .string "But Esaias is very bold, and saith,\n"
    .string "I was found of them that sought me\l"
    .string "not; I was made manifest unto them\l"
    .string "that asked not after me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_10_21::
    .string "But to Israel he saith, All day\n"
    .string "long I have stretched forth my hands\l"
    .string "unto a disobedient and gainsaying\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_1::
    .string "I say then, Hath God cast away his\n"
    .string "people? God forbid. For I also am\l"
    .string "an Israelite, of the seed of\l"
    .string "Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_2::
    .string "God hath not cast away his people\n"
    .string "which he foreknew. Wot ye not what\l"
    .string "the scripture saith of Elias? how he\l"
    .string "maketh intercession to God against\l"
    .string "Israel saying,"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_3::
    .string "Lord, they have killed thy\n"
    .string "prophets, and digged down thine\l"
    .string "altars; and I am left alone, and\l"
    .string "they seek my life$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_4::
    .string "But what saith the answer of God\n"
    .string "unto him? I have reserved to myself\l"
    .string "seven thousand men, who have not\l"
    .string "bowed the knee to the image of Baal.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_5::
    .string "Even so then at this present time\n"
    .string "also there is a remnant according to\l"
    .string "the election of grace.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_6::
    .string "And if by grace, then is it no more\n"
    .string "of works: otherwise grace is no more\l"
    .string "grace. But if it be of works, then it\l"
    .string "is no more grace: otherwise work is\l"
    .string "no more work.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_7::
    .string "What then? Israel hath not obtained\n"
    .string "that which he seeketh for; but the\l"
    .string "election hath obtained it, and the\l"
    .string "rest were blinded.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_8::
    .string "(According as it is written, God\n"
    .string "hath given them the spirit of\l"
    .string "slumber, eyes that they should not\l"
    .string "see, and ears that they should not\l"
    .string "hear;) unto this day.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_9::
    .string "And David saith, Let their table be\n"
    .string "made a snare, and a trap, and a\l"
    .string "stumblingblock, and a recompence\l"
    .string "unto them:"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_10::
    .string "Let their eyes be darkened, that\n"
    .string "they may not see, and bow down their\l"
    .string "back alway$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_11::
    .string "I say then, Have they stumbled that\n"
    .string "they should fall? God forbid: but\l"
    .string "rather through their fall\l"
    .string "salvation is come unto the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, for to provoke them to\l"
    .string "jealousy.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_12::
    .string "Now if the fall of them be the\n"
    .string "riches of the world, and the\l"
    .string "diminishing of them the riches of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles; how much more their\l"
    .string "fulness?"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_13::
    .string "For I speak to you Gentiles,\n"
    .string "inasmuch as I am the apostle of the\l"
    .string "Gentiles, I magnify mine office:"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_14::
    .string "If by any means I may provoke to\n"
    .string "emulation them which are my flesh,\l"
    .string "and might save some of them$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_15::
    .string "For if the casting away of them be\n"
    .string "the reconciling of the world, what\l"
    .string "shall the receiving of them be, but\l"
    .string "life from the dead?"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_16::
    .string "For if the firstfruit be holy, the\n"
    .string "lump is also holy: and if the root\l"
    .string "be holy, so are the branches$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_17::
    .string "And if some of the branches be\n"
    .string "broken off, and thou, being a wild\l"
    .string "olive tree, wert graffed in among\l"
    .string "them, and with them partakest of the\l"
    .string "root and fatness of the olive tree;"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_18::
    .string "Boast not against the branches. But\n"
    .string "if thou boast, thou bearest not the\l"
    .string "root, but the root thee$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_19::
    .string "Thou wilt say then, The branches\n"
    .string "were broken off, that I might be\l"
    .string "graffed in.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_20::
    .string "Well; because of unbelief they\n"
    .string "were broken off, and thou standest by\l"
    .string "faith. Be not highminded, but fear:"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_21::
    .string "For if God spared not the natural\n"
    .string "branches, take heed lest he also\l"
    .string "spare not thee$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_22::
    .string "Behold therefore the goodness and\n"
    .string "severity of God: on them which fell,\l"
    .string "severity; but toward thee, goodness,\l"
    .string "if thou continue in his goodness:\l"
    .string "otherwise thou also shalt be cut\l"
    .string "off.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_23::
    .string "And they also, if they abide not\n"
    .string "still in unbelief, shall be\l"
    .string "graffed in: for God is able to graff\l"
    .string "them in again.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_24::
    .string "For if thou wert cut out of the\n"
    .string "olive tree which is wild by nature,\l"
    .string "and wert graffed contrary to nature\l"
    .string "into a good olive tree: how much more\l"
    .string "shall these, which be the natural\l"
    .string "branches, be graffed into their own\l"
    .string "olive tree?"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_25::
    .string "For I would not, brethren, that ye\n"
    .string "should be ignorant of this mystery,\l"
    .string "lest ye should be wise in your own\l"
    .string "conceits; that blindness in part is\l"
    .string "happened to Israel, until the\l"
    .string "fulness of the Gentiles be come in$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_26::
    .string "And so all Israel shall be saved:\n"
    .string "as it is written, There shall come\l"
    .string "out of Sion the Deliverer, and\l"
    .string "shall turn away ungodliness from\l"
    .string "Jacob:"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_27::
    .string "For this is my covenant unto them,\n"
    .string "when I shall take away their sins$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_28::
    .string "As concerning the gospel, they are\n"
    .string "enemies for your sakes: but as\l"
    .string "touching the election, they are\l"
    .string "beloved for the father’s sakes.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_29::
    .string "For the gifts and calling of God\n"
    .string "are without repentance.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_30::
    .string "For as ye in times past have not\n"
    .string "believed God, yet have now obtained\l"
    .string "mercy through their unbelief:"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_31::
    .string "Even so have these also now not\n"
    .string "believed, that through your mercy\l"
    .string "they also may obtain mercy$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_32::
    .string "For God hath concluded them all in\n"
    .string "unbelief, that he might have mercy\l"
    .string "upon all.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_33::
    .string "O the depth of the riches both of\n"
    .string "the wisdom and knowledge of God! how\l"
    .string "unsearchable are his judgments, and\l"
    .string "his ways past finding out!"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_34::
    .string "For who hath known the mind of the\n"
    .string "Lord? or who hath been his\l"
    .string "counsellor?"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_35::
    .string "Or who hath first given to him, and\n"
    .string "it shall be recompensed unto him\l"
    .string "again?"
Bible_Text_Paul_11_36::
    .string "For of him, and through him, and to\n"
    .string "him, are all things: to whom be\l"
    .string "glory for ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_1::
    .string "I beseech you therefore, brethren,\n"
    .string "by the mercies of God, that ye\l"
    .string "present your bodies a living\l"
    .string "sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto\l"
    .string "God, which is your reasonable\l"
    .string "service.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_2::
    .string "And be not conformed to this world:\n"
    .string "but be ye transformed by the renewing\l"
    .string "of your mind, that ye may prove what\l"
    .string "is that good, and acceptable, and\l"
    .string "perfect, will of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_3::
    .string "For I say, through the grace given\n"
    .string "unto me, to every man that is among\l"
    .string "you, not to think of himself more\l"
    .string "highly than he ought to think; but to\l"
    .string "think soberly, according as God hath\l"
    .string "dealt to every man the measure of\l"
    .string "faith.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_4::
    .string "For as we have many members in one\n"
    .string "body, and all members have not the\l"
    .string "same office:"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_5::
    .string "So we, being many, are one body in\n"
    .string "Christ, and every one members one of\l"
    .string "another$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_6::
    .string "Having then gifts differing\n"
    .string "according to the grace that is given\l"
    .string "to us, whether prophecy, let us\l"
    .string "prophesy according to the\l"
    .string "proportion of faith;"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_7::
    .string "Or ministry, let us wait on our\n"
    .string "ministering: or he that teacheth, on\l"
    .string "teaching;"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_8::
    .string "Or he that exhorteth, on\n"
    .string "exhortation: he that giveth, let him\l"
    .string "do it with simplicity; he that\l"
    .string "ruleth, with diligence; he that\l"
    .string "sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_9::
    .string "Let love be without dissimulation.\n"
    .string "Abhor that which is evil; cleave to\l"
    .string "that which is good.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_10::
    .string "Be kindly affectioned one to\n"
    .string "another with brotherly love; in\l"
    .string "honour preferring one another;"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_11::
    .string "Not slothful in business; fervent\n"
    .string "in spirit; serving the Lord;"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_12::
    .string "Rejoicing in hope; patient in\n"
    .string "tribulation; continuing instant in\l"
    .string "prayer;"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_13::
    .string "Distributing to the necessity of\n"
    .string "saints; given to hospitality$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_14::
    .string "Bless them which persecute you:\n"
    .string "bless, and curse not.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_15::
    .string "Rejoice with them that do rejoice,\n"
    .string "and weep with them that weep.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_16::
    .string "Be of the same mind one toward\n"
    .string "another. Mind not high things, but\l"
    .string "condescend to men of low estate. Be\l"
    .string "not wise in your own conceits.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_17::
    .string "Recompense to no man evil for\n"
    .string "evil. Provide things honest in the\l"
    .string "sight of all men.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_18::
    .string "If it be possible, as much as\n"
    .string "lieth in you, live peaceably with\l"
    .string "all men.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_19::
    .string "Dearly beloved, avenge not\n"
    .string "yourselves, but rather give place\l"
    .string "unto wrath: for it is written,\l"
    .string "Vengeance is mine; I will repay,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_20::
    .string "Therefore if thine enemy hunger,\n"
    .string "feed him; if he thirst, give him\l"
    .string "drink: for in so doing thou shalt\l"
    .string "heap coals of fire on his head.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_12_21::
    .string "Be not overcome of evil, but\n"
    .string "overcome evil with good.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_1::
    .string "Let every soul be subject unto the\n"
    .string "higher powers. For there is no power\l"
    .string "but of God: the powers that be are\l"
    .string "ordained of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_2::
    .string "Whosoever therefore resisteth the\n"
    .string "power, resisteth the ordinance of\l"
    .string "God: and they that resist shall\l"
    .string "receive to themselves damnation.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_3::
    .string "For rulers are not a terror to good\n"
    .string "works, but to the evil. Wilt thou\l"
    .string "then not be afraid of the power? do\l"
    .string "that which is good, and thou shalt\l"
    .string "have praise of the same:"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_4::
    .string "For he is the minister of God to\n"
    .string "thee for good. But if thou do that\l"
    .string "which is evil, be afraid; for he\l"
    .string "beareth not the sword in vain: for he\l"
    .string "is the minister of God, a revenger to\l"
    .string "execute wrath upon him that doeth\l"
    .string "evil$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_5::
    .string "Wherefore ye must needs be subject,\n"
    .string "not only for wrath, but also for\l"
    .string "conscience sake.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_6::
    .string "For for this cause pay ye tribute\n"
    .string "also: for they are God’s ministers,\l"
    .string "attending continually upon this\l"
    .string "very thing.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_7::
    .string "Render therefore to all their\n"
    .string "dues: tribute to whom tribute is due;\l"
    .string "custom to whom custom; fear to whom\l"
    .string "fear; honour to whom honour.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_8::
    .string "Owe no man any thing, but to love\n"
    .string "one another: for he that loveth\l"
    .string "another hath fulfilled the law.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_9::
    .string "For this, Thou shalt not commit\n"
    .string "adultery, Thou shalt not kill,\l"
    .string "Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt\l"
    .string "not bear false witness, Thou shalt\l"
    .string "not covet; and if there be any other\l"
    .string "commandment, it is briefly\l"
    .string "comprehended in this saying,\l"
    .string "namely, Thou shalt love thy\l"
    .string "neighbour as thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_10::
    .string "Love worketh no ill to his\n"
    .string "neighbour: therefore love is the\l"
    .string "fulfilling of the law.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_11::
    .string "And that, knowing the time, that now\n"
    .string "it is high time to awake out of\l"
    .string "sleep: for now is our salvation\l"
    .string "nearer than when we believed.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_12::
    .string "The night is far spent, the day is\n"
    .string "at hand: let us therefore cast off\l"
    .string "the works of darkness, and let us\l"
    .string "put on the armour of light.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_13::
    .string "Let us walk honestly, as in the\n"
    .string "day; not in rioting and drunkenness,\l"
    .string "not in chambering and wantonness, not\l"
    .string "in strife and envying.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_13_14::
    .string "But put ye on the Lord Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "and make not provision for the\l"
    .string "flesh, to fulfil the lusts thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_1::
    .string "Him that is weak in the faith\n"
    .string "receive ye, but not to doubtful\l"
    .string "disputations.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_2::
    .string "For one believeth that he may eat\n"
    .string "all things: another, who is weak,\l"
    .string "eateth herbs.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_3::
    .string "Let not him that eateth despise him\n"
    .string "that eateth not; and let not him\l"
    .string "which eateth not judge him that\l"
    .string "eateth: for God hath received him.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_4::
    .string "Who art thou that judgest another\n"
    .string "man’s servant? to his own master he\l"
    .string "standeth or falleth. Yea, he shall\l"
    .string "be holden up: for God is able to\l"
    .string "make him stand.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_5::
    .string "One man esteemeth one day above\n"
    .string "another: another esteemeth every day\l"
    .string "alike. Let every man be fully\l"
    .string "persuaded in his own mind.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_6::
    .string "He that regardeth the day, regardeth\n"
    .string "it unto the Lord; and he that\l"
    .string "regardeth not the day, to the Lord he\l"
    .string "doth not regard it. He that eateth,\l"
    .string "eateth to the Lord, for he giveth God\l"
    .string "thanks; and he that eateth not, to\l"
    .string "the Lord he eateth not, and giveth\l"
    .string "God thanks.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_7::
    .string "For none of us liveth to himself,\n"
    .string "and no man dieth to himself.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_8::
    .string "For whether we live, we live unto\n"
    .string "the Lord; and whether we die, we die\l"
    .string "unto the Lord: whether we live\l"
    .string "therefore, or die, we are the Lord’s.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_9::
    .string "For to this end Christ both died,\n"
    .string "and rose, and revived, that he might\l"
    .string "be Lord both of the dead and living.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_10::
    .string "But why dost thou judge thy brother?\n"
    .string "or why dost thou set at nought thy\l"
    .string "brother? for we shall all stand\l"
    .string "before the judgment seat of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_11::
    .string "For it is written, As I live, saith\n"
    .string "the Lord, every knee shall bow to\l"
    .string "me, and every tongue shall confess\l"
    .string "to God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_12::
    .string "So then every one of us shall give\n"
    .string "account of himself to God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_13::
    .string "Let us not therefore judge one\n"
    .string "another any more: but judge this\l"
    .string "rather, that no man put a\l"
    .string "stumblingblock or an occasion to\l"
    .string "fall in his brother’s way.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_14::
    .string "I know, and am persuaded by the Lord\n"
    .string "Jesus, that there is nothing unclean\l"
    .string "of itself: but to him that esteemeth\l"
    .string "any thing to be unclean, to him it is\l"
    .string "unclean.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_15::
    .string "But if thy brother be grieved with\n"
    .string "thy meat, now walkest thou not\l"
    .string "charitably. Destroy not him with thy\l"
    .string "meat, for whom Christ died.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_16::
    .string "Let not then your good be evil\n"
    .string "spoken of:"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_17::
    .string "For the kingdom of God is not meat\n"
    .string "and drink; but righteousness, and\l"
    .string "peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_18::
    .string "For he that in these things serveth\n"
    .string "Christ is acceptable to God, and\l"
    .string "approved of men.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_19::
    .string "Let us therefore follow after the\n"
    .string "things which make for peace, and\l"
    .string "things wherewith one may edify\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_20::
    .string "For meat destroy not the work of\n"
    .string "God. All things indeed are pure;\l"
    .string "but it is evil for that man who\l"
    .string "eateth with offence.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_21::
    .string "It is good neither to eat flesh, nor\n"
    .string "to drink wine, nor any thing whereby\l"
    .string "thy brother stumbleth, or is\l"
    .string "offended, or is made weak.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_22::
    .string "Hast thou faith? have it to thyself\n"
    .string "before God. Happy is he that\l"
    .string "condemneth not himself in that thing\l"
    .string "which he alloweth.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_14_23::
    .string "And he that doubteth is damned if he\n"
    .string "eat, because he eateth not of faith:\l"
    .string "for whatsoever is not of faith is sin.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_1::
    .string "We then that are strong ought to\n"
    .string "bear the infirmities of the weak, and\l"
    .string "not to please ourselves.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_2::
    .string "Let every one of us please his\n"
    .string "neighbour for his good to\l"
    .string "edification.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_3::
    .string "For even Christ pleased not\n"
    .string "himself; but, as it is written, The\l"
    .string "reproaches of them that reproached\l"
    .string "thee fell on me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_4::
    .string "For whatsoever things were written\n"
    .string "aforetime were written for our\l"
    .string "learning, that we through patience\l"
    .string "and comfort of the scriptures might\l"
    .string "have hope.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_5::
    .string "Now the God of patience and\n"
    .string "consolation grant you to be\l"
    .string "likeminded one toward another\l"
    .string "according to Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_6::
    .string "That ye may with one mind and one\n"
    .string "mouth glorify God, even the Father\l"
    .string "of our Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_7::
    .string "Wherefore receive ye one another, as\n"
    .string "Christ also received us to the\l"
    .string "glory of God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_8::
    .string "Now I say that Jesus Christ was a\n"
    .string "minister of the circumcision for the\l"
    .string "truth of God, to confirm the\l"
    .string "promises made unto the fathers:"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_9::
    .string "And that the Gentiles might\n"
    .string "glorify God for his mercy; as it is\l"
    .string "written, For this cause I will\l"
    .string "confess to thee among the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "and sing unto thy name$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_10::
    .string "And again he saith, Rejoice, ye\n"
    .string "Gentiles, with his people.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_11::
    .string "And again, Praise the Lord, all ye\n"
    .string "Gentiles; and laud him, all ye\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_12::
    .string "And again, Esaias saith, There\n"
    .string "shall be a root of Jesse, and he\l"
    .string "that shall rise to reign over the\l"
    .string "Gentiles; in him shall the\l"
    .string "Gentiles trust.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_13::
    .string "Now the God of hope fill you with\n"
    .string "all joy and peace in believing,\l"
    .string "that ye may abound in hope, through\l"
    .string "the power of the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_14::
    .string "And I myself also am persuaded of\n"
    .string "you, my brethren, that ye also are\l"
    .string "full of goodness, filled with all\l"
    .string "knowledge, able also to admonish\l"
    .string "one another.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_15::
    .string "Nevertheless, brethren, I have\n"
    .string "written the more boldly unto you in\l"
    .string "some sort, as putting you in mind,\l"
    .string "because of the grace that is given to\l"
    .string "me of God,"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_16::
    .string "That I should be the minister of\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ to the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "ministering the gospel of God, that\l"
    .string "the offering up of the Gentiles\l"
    .string "might be acceptable, being\l"
    .string "sanctified by the Holy Ghost$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_17::
    .string "I have therefore whereof I may\n"
    .string "glory through Jesus Christ in those\l"
    .string "things which pertain to God.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_18::
    .string "For I will not dare to speak of\n"
    .string "any of those things which Christ hath\l"
    .string "not wrought by me, to make the\l"
    .string "Gentiles obedient, by word and deed,"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_19::
    .string "Through mighty signs and wonders, by\n"
    .string "the power of the Spirit of God; so\l"
    .string "that from Jerusalem, and round about\l"
    .string "unto Illyricum, I have fully\l"
    .string "preached the gospel of Christ$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_20::
    .string "Yea, so have I strived to preach the\n"
    .string "gospel, not where Christ was named,\l"
    .string "lest I should build upon another\l"
    .string "man’s foundation:"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_21::
    .string "But as it is written, To whom he was\n"
    .string "not spoken of, they shall see: and\l"
    .string "they that have not heard shall\l"
    .string "understand$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_22::
    .string "For which cause also I have been\n"
    .string "much hindered from coming to you.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_23::
    .string "But now having no more place in\n"
    .string "these parts, and having a great\l"
    .string "desire these many years to come unto\l"
    .string "you;"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_24::
    .string "Whensoever I take my journey into\n"
    .string "Spain, I will come to you: for I\l"
    .string "trust to see you in my journey, and to\l"
    .string "be brought on my way thitherward by\l"
    .string "you, if first I be somewhat filled\l"
    .string "with your company$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_25::
    .string "But now I go unto Jerusalem to\n"
    .string "minister unto the saints.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_26::
    .string "For it hath pleased them of\n"
    .string "Macedonia and Achaia to make a\l"
    .string "certain contribution for the poor\l"
    .string "saints which are at Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_27::
    .string "It hath pleased them verily; and\n"
    .string "their debtors they are. For if the\l"
    .string "Gentiles have been made partakers\l"
    .string "of their spiritual things, their\l"
    .string "duty is also to minister unto them\l"
    .string "in carnal things.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_28::
    .string "When therefore I have performed\n"
    .string "this, and have sealed to them this\l"
    .string "fruit, I will come by you into\l"
    .string "Spain.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_29::
    .string "And I am sure that, when I come unto\n"
    .string "you, I shall come in the fulness of\l"
    .string "the blessing of the gospel of\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_30::
    .string "Now I beseech you, brethren, for the\n"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ’s sake, and for the\l"
    .string "love of the Spirit, that ye strive\l"
    .string "together with me in your prayers to\l"
    .string "God for me;"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_31::
    .string "That I may be delivered from them\n"
    .string "that do not believe in Judaea; and\l"
    .string "that my service which I have for\l"
    .string "Jerusalem may be accepted of the\l"
    .string "saints;"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_32::
    .string "That I may come unto you with joy by\n"
    .string "the will of God, and may with you be\l"
    .string "refreshed$"
Bible_Text_Paul_15_33::
    .string "Now the God of peace be with you\n"
    .string "all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_1::
    .string "I commend unto you Phebe our sister,\n"
    .string "which is a servant of the church\l"
    .string "which is at Cenchrea:"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_2::
    .string "That ye receive her in the Lord, as\n"
    .string "becometh saints, and that ye assist\l"
    .string "her in whatsoever business she hath\l"
    .string "need of you: for she hath been a\l"
    .string "succourer of many, and of myself\l"
    .string "also$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_3::
    .string "Greet Priscilla and Aquila my\n"
    .string "helpers in Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_4::
    .string "Who have for my life laid down\n"
    .string "their own necks: unto whom not only I\l"
    .string "give thanks, but also all the\l"
    .string "churches of the Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_5::
    .string "Likewise greet the church that is in\n"
    .string "their house. Salute my\l"
    .string "well-beloved Epaenetus, who is\l"
    .string "the firstfruits of Achaia unto\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_6::
    .string "Greet Mary, who bestowed much\n"
    .string "labour on us.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_7::
    .string "Salute Andronicus and Junia, my\n"
    .string "kinsmen, and my fellow-prisoners,\l"
    .string "who are of note among the apostles,\l"
    .string "who also were in Christ before me.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_8::
    .string "Greet Amplias my beloved in the\n"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_9::
    .string "Salute Urbane, our helper in\n"
    .string "Christ, and Stachys my beloved.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_10::
    .string "Salute Apelles approved in\n"
    .string "Christ. Salute them which are of\l"
    .string "Aristobulus’ household.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_11::
    .string "Salute Herodion my kinsman. Greet\n"
    .string "them that be of the household of\l"
    .string "Narcissus, which are in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_12::
    .string "Salute Tryphena and Tryphosa, who\n"
    .string "labour in the Lord. Salute the\l"
    .string "beloved Persis, which laboured much\l"
    .string "in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_13::
    .string "Salute Rufus chosen in the Lord,\n"
    .string "and his mother and mine.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_14::
    .string "Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon,\n"
    .string "Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the\l"
    .string "brethren which are with them.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_15::
    .string "Salute Philologus, and Julia,\n"
    .string "Nereus, and his sister, and Olympas,\l"
    .string "and all the saints which are with\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_16::
    .string "Salute one another with an holy\n"
    .string "kiss. The churches of Christ salute\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_17::
    .string "Now I beseech you, brethren, mark\n"
    .string "them which cause divisions and\l"
    .string "offences contrary to the doctrine\l"
    .string "which ye have learned; and avoid\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_18::
    .string "For they that are such serve not our\n"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ, but their own\l"
    .string "belly; and by good words and fair\l"
    .string "speeches deceive the hearts of the\l"
    .string "simple.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_19::
    .string "For your obedience is come abroad\n"
    .string "unto all men. I am glad therefore\l"
    .string "on your behalf: but yet I would have\l"
    .string "you wise unto that which is good, and\l"
    .string "simple concerning evil.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_20::
    .string "And the God of peace shall bruise\n"
    .string "Satan under your feet shortly. The\l"
    .string "grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be\l"
    .string "with you. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_21::
    .string "Timotheus my workfellow, and\n"
    .string "Lucius, and Jason, and Sosipater, my\l"
    .string "kinsmen, salute you.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_22::
    .string "I Tertius, who wrote this epistle,\n"
    .string "salute you in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_23::
    .string "Gaius mine host, and of the whole\n"
    .string "church, saluteth you. Erastus the\l"
    .string "chamberlain of the city saluteth\l"
    .string "you, and Quartus a brother.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_24::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_25::
    .string "Now to him that is of power to\n"
    .string "stablish you according to my\l"
    .string "gospel, and the preaching of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, according to the revelation\l"
    .string "of the mystery, which was kept\l"
    .string "secret since the world began,"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_26::
    .string "But now is made manifest, and by the\n"
    .string "scriptures of the prophets,\l"
    .string "according to the commandment of the\l"
    .string "everlasting God, made known to all\l"
    .string "nations for the obedience of faith:"
Bible_Text_Paul_16_27::
    .string "To God only wise, be glory through\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ for ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, called to be an apostle of\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ through the will of\l"
    .string "God, and Sosthenes our brother,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_2::
    .string "Unto the church of God which is at\n"
    .string "Corinth, to them that are sanctified\l"
    .string "in Christ Jesus, called to be\l"
    .string "saints, with all that in every\l"
    .string "place call upon the name of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ our Lord, both theirs and\l"
    .string "ours:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_3::
    .string "Grace be unto you, and peace, from\n"
    .string "God our Father, and from the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_4::
    .string "I thank my God always on your\n"
    .string "behalf, for the grace of God which is\l"
    .string "given you by Jesus Christ;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_5::
    .string "That in every thing ye are enriched\n"
    .string "by him, in all utterance, and in\l"
    .string "all knowledge;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_6::
    .string "Even as the testimony of Christ was\n"
    .string "confirmed in you:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_7::
    .string "So that ye come behind in no gift;\n"
    .string "waiting for the coming of our Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_8::
    .string "Who shall also confirm you unto\n"
    .string "the end, that ye may be blameless in\l"
    .string "the day of our Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_9::
    .string "God is faithful, by whom ye were\n"
    .string "called unto the fellowship of his\l"
    .string "Son Jesus Christ our Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_10::
    .string "Now I beseech you, brethren, by the\n"
    .string "name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that\l"
    .string "ye all speak the same thing, and\l"
    .string "that there be no divisions among you;\l"
    .string "but that ye be perfectly joined\l"
    .string "together in the same mind and in the\l"
    .string "same judgment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_11::
    .string "For it hath been declared unto me\n"
    .string "of you, my brethren, by them which\l"
    .string "are of the house of Chloe, that there\l"
    .string "are contentions among you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_12::
    .string "Now this I say, that every one of you\n"
    .string "saith, I am of Paul; and I of\l"
    .string "Apollos; and I of Cephas; and I of\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_13::
    .string "Is Christ divided? was Paul\n"
    .string "crucified for you? or were ye\l"
    .string "baptized in the name of Paul?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_14::
    .string "I thank God that I baptized none of\n"
    .string "you, but Crispus and Gaius;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_15::
    .string "Lest any should say that I had\n"
    .string "baptized in mine own name$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_16::
    .string "And I baptized also the household\n"
    .string "of Stephanas: besides, I know not\l"
    .string "whether I baptized any other.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_17::
    .string "For Christ sent me not to baptize,\n"
    .string "but to preach the gospel: not with\l"
    .string "wisdom of words, lest the cross of\l"
    .string "Christ should be made of none effect.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_18::
    .string "For the preaching of the cross is\n"
    .string "to them that perish foolishness;\l"
    .string "but unto us which are saved it is the\l"
    .string "power of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_19::
    .string "For it is written, I will destroy\n"
    .string "the wisdom of the wise, and will\l"
    .string "bring to nothing the understanding\l"
    .string "of the prudent.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_20::
    .string "Where is the wise? where is the\n"
    .string "scribe? where is the disputer of\l"
    .string "this world? hath not God made\l"
    .string "foolish the wisdom of this world?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_21::
    .string "For after that in the wisdom of God\n"
    .string "the world by wisdom knew not God, it\l"
    .string "pleased God by the foolishness of\l"
    .string "preaching to save them that believe$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_22::
    .string "For the Jews require a sign, and the\n"
    .string "Greeks seek after wisdom:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_23::
    .string "But we preach Christ crucified,\n"
    .string "unto the Jews a stumblingblock, and\l"
    .string "unto the Greeks foolishness;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_24::
    .string "But unto them which are called,\n"
    .string "both Jews and Greeks, Christ the\l"
    .string "power of God, and the wisdom of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_25::
    .string "Because the foolishness of God is\n"
    .string "wiser than men; and the weakness of\l"
    .string "God is stronger than men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_26::
    .string "For ye see your calling, brethren,\n"
    .string "how that not many wise men after the\l"
    .string "flesh, not many mighty, not many\l"
    .string "noble, are called:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_27::
    .string "But God hath chosen the foolish\n"
    .string "things of the world to confound the\l"
    .string "wise; and God hath chosen the weak\l"
    .string "things of the world to confound the\l"
    .string "things which are mighty;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_28::
    .string "And base things of the world, and\n"
    .string "things which are despised, hath God\l"
    .string "chosen, yea, and things which are\l"
    .string "not, to bring to nought things that\l"
    .string "are:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_29::
    .string "That no flesh should glory in his\n"
    .string "presence$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_30::
    .string "But of him are ye in Christ Jesus,\n"
    .string "who of God is made unto us wisdom, and\l"
    .string "righteousness, and sanctification,\l"
    .string "and redemption:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_1_31::
    .string "That, according as it is written, He\n"
    .string "that glorieth, let him glory in the\l"
    .string "Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_1::
    .string "And I, brethren, when I came to you,\n"
    .string "came not with excellency of speech\l"
    .string "or of wisdom, declaring unto you the\l"
    .string "testimony of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_2::
    .string "For I determined not to know any\n"
    .string "thing among you, save Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "and him crucified.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_3::
    .string "And I was with you in weakness, and\n"
    .string "in fear, and in much trembling.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_4::
    .string "And my speech and my preaching was\n"
    .string "not with enticing words of man’s\l"
    .string "wisdom, but in demonstration of the\l"
    .string "Spirit and of power:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_5::
    .string "That your faith should not stand in\n"
    .string "the wisdom of men, but in the power\l"
    .string "of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_6::
    .string "Howbeit we speak wisdom among them\n"
    .string "that are perfect: yet not the wisdom\l"
    .string "of this world, nor of the princes of\l"
    .string "this world, that come to nought:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_7::
    .string "But we speak the wisdom of God in a\n"
    .string "mystery, even the hidden wisdom,\l"
    .string "which God ordained before the world\l"
    .string "unto our glory:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_8::
    .string "Which none of the princes of this\n"
    .string "world knew: for had they known it,\l"
    .string "they would not have crucified the\l"
    .string "Lord of glory$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_9::
    .string "But as it is written, Eye hath not\n"
    .string "seen, nor ear heard, neither have\l"
    .string "entered into the heart of man, the\l"
    .string "things which God hath prepared for\l"
    .string "them that love him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_10::
    .string "But God hath revealed them unto us\n"
    .string "by his Spirit: for the Spirit\l"
    .string "searcheth all things, yea, the deep\l"
    .string "things of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_11::
    .string "For what man knoweth the things of a\n"
    .string "man, save the spirit of man which is\l"
    .string "in him? even so the things of God\l"
    .string "knoweth no man, but the Spirit of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_12::
    .string "Now we have received, not the\n"
    .string "spirit of the world, but the spirit\l"
    .string "which is of God; that we might know\l"
    .string "the things that are freely given to\l"
    .string "us of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_13::
    .string "Which things also we speak, not in\n"
    .string "the words which man’s wisdom\l"
    .string "teacheth, but which the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "teacheth; comparing spiritual\l"
    .string "things with spiritual.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_14::
    .string "But the natural man receiveth not\n"
    .string "the things of the Spirit of God: for\l"
    .string "they are foolishness unto him:\l"
    .string "neither can he know them, because\l"
    .string "they are spiritually discerned.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_15::
    .string "But he that is spiritual judgeth\n"
    .string "all things, yet he himself is\l"
    .string "judged of no man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_2_16::
    .string "For who hath known the mind of the\n"
    .string "Lord, that he may instruct him? But\l"
    .string "we have the mind of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_1::
    .string "And I, brethren, could not speak\n"
    .string "unto you as unto spiritual, but as\l"
    .string "unto carnal, even as unto babes in\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_2::
    .string "I have fed you with milk, and not\n"
    .string "with meat: for hitherto ye were not\l"
    .string "able to bear it, neither yet now are\l"
    .string "ye able.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_3::
    .string "For ye are yet carnal: for whereas\n"
    .string "there is among you envying, and\l"
    .string "strife, and divisions, are ye not\l"
    .string "carnal, and walk as men?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_4::
    .string "For while one saith, I am of Paul;\n"
    .string "and another, I am of Apollos; are\l"
    .string "ye not carnal?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_5::
    .string "Who then is Paul, and who is\n"
    .string "Apollos, but ministers by whom ye\l"
    .string "believed, even as the Lord gave to\l"
    .string "every man?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_6::
    .string "I have planted, Apollos watered;\n"
    .string "but God gave the increase$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_7::
    .string "So then neither is he that\n"
    .string "planteth any thing, neither he that\l"
    .string "watereth; but God that giveth the\l"
    .string "increase.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_8::
    .string "Now he that planteth and he that\n"
    .string "watereth are one: and every man\l"
    .string "shall receive his own reward\l"
    .string "according to his own labour.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_9::
    .string "For we are labourers together with\n"
    .string "God: ye are God’s husbandry, ye are\l"
    .string "God’s building.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_10::
    .string "According to the grace of God which\n"
    .string "is given unto me, as a wise\l"
    .string "masterbuilder, I have laid the\l"
    .string "foundation, and another buildeth\l"
    .string "thereon. But let every man take heed\l"
    .string "how he buildeth thereupon.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_11::
    .string "For other foundation can no man lay\n"
    .string "than that is laid, which is Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_12::
    .string "Now if any man build upon this\n"
    .string "foundation gold, silver, precious\l"
    .string "stones, wood, hay, stubble;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_13::
    .string "Every man’s work shall be made\n"
    .string "manifest: for the day shall declare\l"
    .string "it, because it shall be revealed by\l"
    .string "fire; and the fire shall try every\l"
    .string "man’s work of what sort it is$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_14::
    .string "If any man’s work abide which he\n"
    .string "hath built thereupon, he shall\l"
    .string "receive a reward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_15::
    .string "If any man’s work shall be burned,\n"
    .string "he shall suffer loss: but he\l"
    .string "himself shall be saved; yet so as\l"
    .string "by fire.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_16::
    .string "Know ye not that ye are the temple\n"
    .string "of God, and that the Spirit of God\l"
    .string "dwelleth in you?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_17::
    .string "If any man defile the temple of\n"
    .string "God, him shall God destroy; for the\l"
    .string "temple of God is holy, which\l"
    .string "temple ye are$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_18::
    .string "Let no man deceive himself. If any\n"
    .string "man among you seemeth to be wise in\l"
    .string "this world, let him become a fool,\l"
    .string "that he may be wise.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_19::
    .string "For the wisdom of this world is\n"
    .string "foolishness with God. For it is\l"
    .string "written, He taketh the wise in their\l"
    .string "own craftiness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_20::
    .string "And again, The Lord knoweth the\n"
    .string "thoughts of the wise, that they are\l"
    .string "vain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_21::
    .string "Therefore let no man glory in men.\n"
    .string "For all things are yours;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_22::
    .string "Whether Paul, or Apollos, or\n"
    .string "Cephas, or the world, or life, or\l"
    .string "death, or things present, or things\l"
    .string "to come; all are yours;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_3_23::
    .string "And ye are Christ’s; and Christ is\n"
    .string "God’s$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_1::
    .string "Let a man so account of us, as of the\n"
    .string "ministers of Christ, and stewards of\l"
    .string "the mysteries of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_2::
    .string "Moreover it is required in stewards,\n"
    .string "that a man be found faithful.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_3::
    .string "But with me it is a very small\n"
    .string "thing that I should be judged of you,\l"
    .string "or of man’s judgment: yea, I judge\l"
    .string "not mine own self.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_4::
    .string "For I know nothing by myself; yet am\n"
    .string "I not hereby justified: but he that\l"
    .string "judgeth me is the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_5::
    .string "Therefore judge nothing before the\n"
    .string "time, until the Lord come, who both\l"
    .string "will bring to light the hidden\l"
    .string "things of darkness, and will make\l"
    .string "manifest the counsels of the hearts:\l"
    .string "and then shall every man have\l"
    .string "praise of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_6::
    .string "And these things, brethren, I have\n"
    .string "in a figure transferred to myself\l"
    .string "and to Apollos for your sakes; that\l"
    .string "ye might learn in us not to think of\l"
    .string "men above that which is written, that\l"
    .string "no one of you be puffed up for one\l"
    .string "against another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_7::
    .string "For who maketh thee to differ from\n"
    .string "another? and what hast thou that thou\l"
    .string "didst not receive? now if thou didst\l"
    .string "receive it, why dost thou glory, as\l"
    .string "if thou hadst not received it?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_8::
    .string "Now ye are full, now ye are rich,\n"
    .string "ye have reigned as kings without us:\l"
    .string "and I would to God ye did reign, that\l"
    .string "we also might reign with you$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_9::
    .string "For I think that God hath set forth\n"
    .string "us the apostles last, as it were\l"
    .string "appointed to death: for we are made\l"
    .string "a spectacle unto the world, and to\l"
    .string "angels, and to men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_10::
    .string "We are fools for Christ’s sake, but\n"
    .string "ye are wise in Christ; we are weak,\l"
    .string "but ye are strong; ye are\l"
    .string "honourable, but we are despised.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_11::
    .string "Even unto this present hour we both\n"
    .string "hunger, and thirst, and are naked,\l"
    .string "and are buffeted, and have no certain\l"
    .string "dwellingplace;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_12::
    .string "And labour, working with our own\n"
    .string "hands: being reviled, we bless;\l"
    .string "being persecuted, we suffer it:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_13::
    .string "Being defamed, we intreat: we are\n"
    .string "made as the filth of the world, and\l"
    .string "are the offscouring of all things\l"
    .string "unto this day$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_14::
    .string "I write not these things to shame\n"
    .string "you, but as my beloved sons I warn\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_15::
    .string "For though ye have ten thousand\n"
    .string "instructers in Christ, yet have ye\l"
    .string "not many fathers: for in Christ Jesus\l"
    .string "I have begotten you through the\l"
    .string "gospel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_16::
    .string "Wherefore I beseech you, be ye\n"
    .string "followers of me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_17::
    .string "For this cause have I sent unto you\n"
    .string "Timotheus, who is my beloved son,\l"
    .string "and faithful in the Lord, who shall\l"
    .string "bring you into remembrance of my ways\l"
    .string "which be in Christ, as I teach every\l"
    .string "where in every church.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_18::
    .string "Now some are puffed up, as though I\n"
    .string "would not come to you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_19::
    .string "But I will come to you shortly, if\n"
    .string "the Lord will, and will know, not\l"
    .string "the speech of them which are puffed\l"
    .string "up, but the power.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_20::
    .string "For the kingdom of God is not in\n"
    .string "word, but in power.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_4_21::
    .string "What will ye? shall I come unto\n"
    .string "you with a rod, or in love, and in\l"
    .string "the spirit of meekness?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_1::
    .string "It is reported commonly that there\n"
    .string "is fornication among you, and such\l"
    .string "fornication as is not so much as\l"
    .string "named among the Gentiles, that one\l"
    .string "should have his father’s wife$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_2::
    .string "And ye are puffed up, and have not\n"
    .string "rather mourned, that he that hath\l"
    .string "done this deed might be taken away\l"
    .string "from among you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_3::
    .string "For I verily, as absent in body, but\n"
    .string "present in spirit, have judged\l"
    .string "already, as though I were present,\l"
    .string "concerning him that hath so done this\l"
    .string "deed,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_4::
    .string "In the name of our Lord Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ, when ye are gathered\l"
    .string "together, and my spirit, with the\l"
    .string "power of our Lord Jesus Christ,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_5::
    .string "To deliver such an one unto Satan\n"
    .string "for the destruction of the flesh,\l"
    .string "that the spirit may be saved in the\l"
    .string "day of the Lord Jesus$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_6::
    .string "Your glorying is not good. Know ye\n"
    .string "not that a little leaven leaveneth\l"
    .string "the whole lump?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_7::
    .string "Purge out therefore the old\n"
    .string "leaven, that ye may be a new lump,\l"
    .string "as ye are unleavened. For even\l"
    .string "Christ our passover is sacrificed\l"
    .string "for us:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_8::
    .string "Therefore let us keep the feast,\n"
    .string "not with old leaven, neither with\l"
    .string "the leaven of malice and\l"
    .string "wickedness; but with the unleavened\l"
    .string "bread of sincerity and truth$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_9::
    .string "I wrote unto you in an epistle not\n"
    .string "to company with fornicators:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_10::
    .string "Yet not altogether with the\n"
    .string "fornicators of this world, or with\l"
    .string "the covetous, or extortioners, or\l"
    .string "with idolaters; for then must ye\l"
    .string "needs go out of the world$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_11::
    .string "But now I have written unto you not\n"
    .string "to keep company, if any man that is\l"
    .string "called a brother be a fornicator, or\l"
    .string "covetous, or an idolater, or a\l"
    .string "railer, or a drunkard, or an\l"
    .string "extortioner; with such an one no not\l"
    .string "to eat.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_12::
    .string "For what have I to do to judge them\n"
    .string "also that are without? do not ye\l"
    .string "judge them that are within?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_5_13::
    .string "But them that are without God\n"
    .string "judgeth. Therefore put away from\l"
    .string "among yourselves that wicked person$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_1::
    .string "Dare any of you, having a matter\n"
    .string "against another, go to law before\l"
    .string "the unjust, and not before the\l"
    .string "saints?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_2::
    .string "Do ye not know that the saints\n"
    .string "shall judge the world? and if the\l"
    .string "world shall be judged by you, are\l"
    .string "ye unworthy to judge the smallest\l"
    .string "matters?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_3::
    .string "Know ye not that we shall judge\n"
    .string "angels? how much more things that\l"
    .string "pertain to this life?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_4::
    .string "If then ye have judgments of things\n"
    .string "pertaining to this life, set them to\l"
    .string "judge who are least esteemed in the\l"
    .string "church$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_5::
    .string "I speak to your shame. Is it so,\n"
    .string "that there is not a wise man among\l"
    .string "you? no, not one that shall be able\l"
    .string "to judge between his brethren?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_6::
    .string "But brother goeth to law with\n"
    .string "brother, and that before the\l"
    .string "unbelievers$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_7::
    .string "Now therefore there is utterly a\n"
    .string "fault among you, because ye go to\l"
    .string "law one with another. Why do ye not\l"
    .string "rather take wrong? why do ye not\l"
    .string "rather suffer yourselves to be\l"
    .string "defrauded?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_8::
    .string "Nay, ye do wrong, and defraud, and\n"
    .string "that your brethren$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_9::
    .string "Know ye not that the unrighteous\n"
    .string "shall not inherit the kingdom of\l"
    .string "God? Be not deceived: neither\l"
    .string "fornicators, nor idolaters, nor\l"
    .string "adulterers, nor effeminate, nor\l"
    .string "abusers of themselves with mankind,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_10::
    .string "Nor thieves, nor covetous, nor\n"
    .string "drunkards, nor revilers, nor\l"
    .string "extortioners, shall inherit the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_11::
    .string "And such were some of you: but ye are\n"
    .string "washed, but ye are sanctified, but ye\l"
    .string "are justified in the name of the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus, and by the Spirit of our God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_12::
    .string "All things are lawful unto me,\n"
    .string "but all things are not expedient:\l"
    .string "all things are lawful for me, but I\l"
    .string "will not be brought under the power\l"
    .string "of any.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_13::
    .string "Meats for the belly, and the\n"
    .string "belly for meats: but God shall\l"
    .string "destroy both it and them. Now the\l"
    .string "body is not for fornication, but for\l"
    .string "the Lord; and the Lord for the body.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_14::
    .string "And God hath both raised up the\n"
    .string "Lord, and will also raise up us by\l"
    .string "his own power.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_15::
    .string "Know ye not that your bodies are the\n"
    .string "members of Christ? shall I then take\l"
    .string "the members of Christ, and make them\l"
    .string "the members of an harlot? God forbid.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_16::
    .string "What? know ye not that he which is\n"
    .string "joined to an harlot is one body? for\l"
    .string "two, saith he, shall be one flesh.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_17::
    .string "But he that is joined unto the Lord\n"
    .string "is one spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_18::
    .string "Flee fornication. Every sin that a\n"
    .string "man doeth is without the body; but he\l"
    .string "that committeth fornication sinneth\l"
    .string "against his own body.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_19::
    .string "What? know ye not that your body is\n"
    .string "the temple of the Holy Ghost which\l"
    .string "is in you, which ye have of God, and\l"
    .string "ye are not your own?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_6_20::
    .string "For ye are bought with a price:\n"
    .string "therefore glorify God in your body,\l"
    .string "and in your spirit, which are God’s$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_1::
    .string "Now concerning the things whereof\n"
    .string "ye wrote unto me: It is good for a man\l"
    .string "not to touch a woman.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_2::
    .string "Nevertheless, to avoid\n"
    .string "fornication, let every man have his\l"
    .string "own wife, and let every woman have\l"
    .string "her own husband.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_3::
    .string "Let the husband render unto the wife\n"
    .string "due benevolence: and likewise also\l"
    .string "the wife unto the husband.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_4::
    .string "The wife hath not power of her own\n"
    .string "body, but the husband: and likewise\l"
    .string "also the husband hath not power of\l"
    .string "his own body, but the wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_5::
    .string "Defraud ye not one the other,\n"
    .string "except it be with consent for a time,\l"
    .string "that ye may give yourselves to\l"
    .string "fasting and prayer; and come\l"
    .string "together again, that Satan tempt you\l"
    .string "not for your incontinency.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_6::
    .string "But I speak this by permission, and\n"
    .string "not of commandment.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_7::
    .string "For I would that all men were even\n"
    .string "as I myself. But every man hath his\l"
    .string "proper gift of God, one after this\l"
    .string "manner, and another after that.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_8::
    .string "I say therefore to the unmarried and\n"
    .string "widows, It is good for them if they\l"
    .string "abide even as I.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_9::
    .string "But if they cannot contain, let\n"
    .string "them marry: for it is better to marry\l"
    .string "than to burn.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_10::
    .string "And unto the married I command, yet\n"
    .string "not I, but the Lord, Let not the wife\l"
    .string "depart from her husband:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_11::
    .string "But and if she depart, let her\n"
    .string "remain unmarried or be reconciled to\l"
    .string "her husband: and let not the husband\l"
    .string "put away his wife$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_12::
    .string "But to the rest speak I, not the\n"
    .string "Lord: If any brother hath a wife that\l"
    .string "believeth not, and she be pleased\l"
    .string "to dwell with him, let him not put\l"
    .string "her away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_13::
    .string "And the woman which hath an husband\n"
    .string "that believeth not, and if he be\l"
    .string "pleased to dwell with her, let her\l"
    .string "not leave him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_14::
    .string "For the unbelieving husband is\n"
    .string "sanctified by the wife, and the\l"
    .string "unbelieving wife is sanctified by\l"
    .string "the husband: else were your\l"
    .string "children unclean; but now are they\l"
    .string "holy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_15::
    .string "But if the unbelieving depart, let\n"
    .string "him depart. A brother or a sister is\l"
    .string "not under bondage in such cases: but\l"
    .string "God hath called us to peace.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_16::
    .string "For what knowest thou, O wife,\n"
    .string "whether thou shalt save thy husband?\l"
    .string "or how knowest thou, O man, whether\l"
    .string "thou shalt save thy wife?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_17::
    .string "But as God hath distributed to every\n"
    .string "man, as the Lord hath called every\l"
    .string "one, so let him walk. And so ordain\l"
    .string "I in all churches$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_18::
    .string "Is any man called being\n"
    .string "circumcised? let him not become\l"
    .string "uncircumcised. Is any called in\l"
    .string "uncircumcision? let him not be\l"
    .string "circumcised.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_19::
    .string "Circumcision is nothing, and\n"
    .string "uncircumcision is nothing, but the\l"
    .string "keeping of the commandments of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_20::
    .string "Let every man abide in the same\n"
    .string "calling wherein he was called.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_21::
    .string "Art thou called being a servant?\n"
    .string "care not for it: but if thou mayest be\l"
    .string "made free, use it rather.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_22::
    .string "For he that is called in the Lord,\n"
    .string "being a servant, is the Lord’s\l"
    .string "freeman: likewise also he that is\l"
    .string "called, being free, is Christ’s\l"
    .string "servant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_23::
    .string "Ye are bought with a price; be not\n"
    .string "ye the servants of men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_24::
    .string "Brethren, let every man, wherein he\n"
    .string "is called, therein abide with God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_25::
    .string "Now concerning virgins I have no\n"
    .string "commandment of the Lord: yet I give\l"
    .string "my judgment, as one that hath\l"
    .string "obtained mercy of the Lord to be\l"
    .string "faithful.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_26::
    .string "I suppose therefore that this is\n"
    .string "good for the present distress, I\l"
    .string "say, that it is good for a man so to\l"
    .string "be.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_27::
    .string "Art thou bound unto a wife? seek not\n"
    .string "to be loosed. Art thou loosed from a\l"
    .string "wife? seek not a wife.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_28::
    .string "But and if thou marry, thou hast not\n"
    .string "sinned; and if a virgin marry, she\l"
    .string "hath not sinned. Nevertheless such\l"
    .string "shall have trouble in the flesh:\l"
    .string "but I spare you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_29::
    .string "But this I say, brethren, the time\n"
    .string "is short: it remaineth, that both\l"
    .string "they that have wives be as though\l"
    .string "they had none;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_30::
    .string "And they that weep, as though they\n"
    .string "wept not; and they that rejoice, as\l"
    .string "though they rejoiced not; and they\l"
    .string "that buy, as though they possessed\l"
    .string "not;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_31::
    .string "And they that use this world, as not\n"
    .string "abusing it: for the fashion of this\l"
    .string "world passeth away$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_32::
    .string "But I would have you without\n"
    .string "carefulness. He that is unmarried\l"
    .string "careth for the things that belong to\l"
    .string "the Lord, how he may please the\l"
    .string "Lord:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_33::
    .string "But he that is married careth for\n"
    .string "the things that are of the world, how\l"
    .string "he may please his wife$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_34::
    .string "There is difference also between a\n"
    .string "wife and a virgin. The unmarried\l"
    .string "woman careth for the things of the\l"
    .string "Lord, that she may be holy both in\l"
    .string "body and in spirit: but she that is\l"
    .string "married careth for the things of the\l"
    .string "world, how she may please her\l"
    .string "husband.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_35::
    .string "And this I speak for your own\n"
    .string "profit; not that I may cast a snare\l"
    .string "upon you, but for that which is\l"
    .string "comely, and that ye may attend upon\l"
    .string "the Lord without distraction.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_36::
    .string "But if any man think that he\n"
    .string "behaveth himself uncomely toward\l"
    .string "his virgin, if she pass the flower\l"
    .string "of her age, and need so require, let\l"
    .string "him do what he will, he sinneth not:\l"
    .string "let them marry.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_37::
    .string "Nevertheless he that standeth\n"
    .string "stedfast in his heart, having no\l"
    .string "necessity, but hath power over his\l"
    .string "own will, and hath so decreed in his\l"
    .string "heart that he will keep his virgin,\l"
    .string "doeth well.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_38::
    .string "So then he that giveth her in\n"
    .string "marriage doeth well; but he that\l"
    .string "giveth her not in marriage doeth\l"
    .string "better.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_39::
    .string "The wife is bound by the law as\n"
    .string "long as her husband liveth; but if\l"
    .string "her husband be dead, she is at\l"
    .string "liberty to be married to whom she\l"
    .string "will; only in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_7_40::
    .string "But she is happier if she so abide,\n"
    .string "after my judgment: and I think also\l"
    .string "that I have the Spirit of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_1::
    .string "Now as touching things offered unto\n"
    .string "idols, we know that we all have\l"
    .string "knowledge. Knowledge puffeth up,\l"
    .string "but charity edifieth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_2::
    .string "And if any man think that he knoweth\n"
    .string "any thing, he knoweth nothing yet as\l"
    .string "he ought to know.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_3::
    .string "But if any man love God, the same is\n"
    .string "known of him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_4::
    .string "As concerning therefore the eating\n"
    .string "of those things that are offered in\l"
    .string "sacrifice unto idols, we know that\l"
    .string "an idol is nothing in the world, and\l"
    .string "that there is none other God but one.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_5::
    .string "For though there be that are\n"
    .string "called gods, whether in heaven or in\l"
    .string "earth, (as there be gods many, and\l"
    .string "lords many,)"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_6::
    .string "But to us there is but one God, the\n"
    .string "Father, of whom are all things, and\l"
    .string "we in him; and one Lord Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "by whom are all things, and we by him$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_7::
    .string "Howbeit there is not in every man\n"
    .string "that knowledge: for some with\l"
    .string "conscience of the idol unto this\l"
    .string "hour eat it as a thing offered unto\l"
    .string "an idol; and their conscience being\l"
    .string "weak is defiled.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_8::
    .string "But meat commendeth us not to God:\n"
    .string "for neither, if we eat, are we the\l"
    .string "better; neither, if we eat not, are we\l"
    .string "the worse.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_9::
    .string "But take heed lest by any means\n"
    .string "this liberty of yours become a\l"
    .string "stumblingblock to them that are\l"
    .string "weak.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_10::
    .string "For if any man see thee which hast\n"
    .string "knowledge sit at meat in the idol’s\l"
    .string "temple, shall not the conscience\l"
    .string "of him which is weak be emboldened\l"
    .string "to eat those things which are offered\l"
    .string "to idols;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_11::
    .string "And through thy knowledge shall\n"
    .string "the weak brother perish, for whom\l"
    .string "Christ died?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_12::
    .string "But when ye sin so against the\n"
    .string "brethren, and wound their weak\l"
    .string "conscience, ye sin against Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_8_13::
    .string "Wherefore, if meat make my brother\n"
    .string "to offend, I will eat no flesh\l"
    .string "while the world standeth, lest I\l"
    .string "make my brother to offend.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_1::
    .string "Am I not an apostle? am I not free?\n"
    .string "have I not seen Jesus Christ our\l"
    .string "Lord? are not ye my work in the Lord?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_2::
    .string "If I be not an apostle unto others,\n"
    .string "yet doubtless I am to you: for the\l"
    .string "seal of mine apostleship are ye in\l"
    .string "the Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_3::
    .string "Mine answer to them that do examine\n"
    .string "me is this,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_4::
    .string "Have we not power to eat and to\n"
    .string "drink?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_5::
    .string "Have we not power to lead about a\n"
    .string "sister, a wife, as well as other\l"
    .string "apostles, and as the brethren of the\l"
    .string "Lord, and Cephas?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_6::
    .string "Or I only and Barnabas, have not we\n"
    .string "power to forbear working?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_7::
    .string "Who goeth a warfare any time at his\n"
    .string "own charges? who planteth a\l"
    .string "vineyard, and eateth not of the fruit\l"
    .string "thereof? or who feedeth a flock, and\l"
    .string "eateth not of the milk of the flock?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_8::
    .string "Say I these things as a man? or saith\n"
    .string "not the law the same also?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_9::
    .string "For it is written in the law of\n"
    .string "Moses, Thou shalt not muzzle the\l"
    .string "mouth of the ox that treadeth out the\l"
    .string "corn. Doth God take care for oxen?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_10::
    .string "Or saith he it altogether for our\n"
    .string "sakes? For our sakes, no doubt, this\l"
    .string "is written: that he that ploweth\l"
    .string "should plow in hope; and that he\l"
    .string "that thresheth in hope should be\l"
    .string "partaker of his hope$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_11::
    .string "If we have sown unto you spiritual\n"
    .string "things, is it a great thing if we\l"
    .string "shall reap your carnal things?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_12::
    .string "If others be partakers of this\n"
    .string "power over you, are not we rather?\l"
    .string "Nevertheless we have not used this\l"
    .string "power; but suffer all things, lest\l"
    .string "we should hinder the gospel of\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_13::
    .string "Do ye not know that they which\n"
    .string "minister about holy things live of\l"
    .string "the things of the temple? and they\l"
    .string "which wait at the altar are\l"
    .string "partakers with the altar?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_14::
    .string "Even so hath the Lord ordained that\n"
    .string "they which preach the gospel\l"
    .string "should live of the gospel$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_15::
    .string "But I have used none of these\n"
    .string "things: neither have I written these\l"
    .string "things, that it should be so done\l"
    .string "unto me: for it were better for me to\l"
    .string "die, than that any man should make my\l"
    .string "glorying void.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_16::
    .string "For though I preach the gospel, I\n"
    .string "have nothing to glory of: for\l"
    .string "necessity is laid upon me; yea, woe\l"
    .string "is unto me, if I preach not the\l"
    .string "gospel!"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_17::
    .string "For if I do this thing willingly,\n"
    .string "I have a reward: but if against my\l"
    .string "will, a dispensation of the\l"
    .string "gospel is committed unto me$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_18::
    .string "What is my reward then? Verily\n"
    .string "that, when I preach the gospel, I\l"
    .string "may make the gospel of Christ\l"
    .string "without charge, that I abuse not my\l"
    .string "power in the gospel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_19::
    .string "For though I be free from all men,\n"
    .string "yet have I made myself servant unto\l"
    .string "all, that I might gain the more.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_20::
    .string "And unto the Jews I became as a Jew,\n"
    .string "that I might gain the Jews; to them\l"
    .string "that are under the law, as under the\l"
    .string "law, that I might gain them that are\l"
    .string "under the law;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_21::
    .string "To them that are without law, as\n"
    .string "without law, (being not without law\l"
    .string "to God, but under the law to Christ,)\l"
    .string "that I might gain them that are\l"
    .string "without law$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_22::
    .string "To the weak became I as weak, that I\n"
    .string "might gain the weak: I am made all\l"
    .string "things to all men, that I might by\l"
    .string "all means save some.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_23::
    .string "And this I do for the gospel’s\n"
    .string "sake, that I might be partaker\l"
    .string "thereof with you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_24::
    .string "Know ye not that they which run in a\n"
    .string "race run all, but one receiveth the\l"
    .string "prize? So run, that ye may obtain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_25::
    .string "And every man that striveth for the\n"
    .string "mastery is temperate in all things.\l"
    .string "Now they do it to obtain a\l"
    .string "corruptible crown; but we an\l"
    .string "incorruptible.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_26::
    .string "I therefore so run, not as\n"
    .string "uncertainly; so fight I, not as one\l"
    .string "that beateth the air:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_9_27::
    .string "But I keep under my body, and bring\n"
    .string "it into subjection: lest that by any\l"
    .string "means, when I have preached to\l"
    .string "others, I myself should be a\l"
    .string "castaway$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_1::
    .string "Moreover, brethren, I would not\n"
    .string "that ye should be ignorant, how that\l"
    .string "all our fathers were under the\l"
    .string "cloud, and all passed through the\l"
    .string "sea;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_2::
    .string "And were all baptized unto Moses\n"
    .string "in the cloud and in the sea;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_3::
    .string "And did all eat the same\n"
    .string "spiritual meat;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_4::
    .string "And did all drink the same\n"
    .string "spiritual drink: for they drank of\l"
    .string "that spiritual Rock that followed\l"
    .string "them: and that Rock was Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_5::
    .string "But with many of them God was not\n"
    .string "well pleased: for they were\l"
    .string "overthrown in the wilderness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_6::
    .string "Now these things were our\n"
    .string "examples, to the intent we should\l"
    .string "not lust after evil things, as they\l"
    .string "also lusted.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_7::
    .string "Neither be ye idolaters, as were\n"
    .string "some of them; as it is written, The\l"
    .string "people sat down to eat and drink,\l"
    .string "and rose up to play.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_8::
    .string "Neither let us commit fornication,\n"
    .string "as some of them committed, and fell\l"
    .string "in one day three and twenty thousand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_9::
    .string "Neither let us tempt Christ, as\n"
    .string "some of them also tempted, and were\l"
    .string "destroyed of serpents.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_10::
    .string "Neither murmur ye, as some of them\n"
    .string "also murmured, and were destroyed of\l"
    .string "the destroyer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_11::
    .string "Now all these things happened\n"
    .string "unto them for ensamples: and they\l"
    .string "are written for our admonition, upon\l"
    .string "whom the ends of the world are come.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_12::
    .string "Wherefore let him that thinketh he\n"
    .string "standeth take heed lest he fall.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_13::
    .string "There hath no temptation taken you\n"
    .string "but such as is common to man: but God\l"
    .string "is faithful, who will not suffer\l"
    .string "you to be tempted above that ye are\l"
    .string "able; but will with the temptation\l"
    .string "also make a way to escape, that ye\l"
    .string "may be able to bear it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_14::
    .string "Wherefore, my dearly beloved,\n"
    .string "flee from idolatry.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_15::
    .string "I speak as to wise men; judge ye\n"
    .string "what I say.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_16::
    .string "The cup of blessing which we\n"
    .string "bless, is it not the communion of the\l"
    .string "blood of Christ? The bread which we\l"
    .string "break, is it not the communion of the\l"
    .string "body of Christ?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_17::
    .string "For we being many are one bread, and\n"
    .string "one body: for we are all partakers\l"
    .string "of that one bread$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_18::
    .string "Behold Israel after the flesh: are\n"
    .string "not they which eat of the sacrifices\l"
    .string "partakers of the altar?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_19::
    .string "What say I then? that the idol is\n"
    .string "any thing, or that which is offered\l"
    .string "in sacrifice to idols is any thing?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_20::
    .string "But I say, that the things which the\n"
    .string "Gentiles sacrifice, they sacrifice\l"
    .string "to devils, and not to God: and I\l"
    .string "would not that ye should have\l"
    .string "fellowship with devils$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_21::
    .string "Ye cannot drink the cup of the Lord,\n"
    .string "and the cup of devils: ye cannot be\l"
    .string "partakers of the Lord’s table, and\l"
    .string "of the table of devils.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_22::
    .string "Do we provoke the Lord to jealousy?\n"
    .string "are we stronger than he?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_23::
    .string "All things are lawful for me, but\n"
    .string "all things are not expedient: all\l"
    .string "things are lawful for me, but all\l"
    .string "things edify not$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_24::
    .string "Let no man seek his own, but every\n"
    .string "man another’s wealth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_25::
    .string "Whatsoever is sold in the\n"
    .string "shambles, that eat, asking no\l"
    .string "question for conscience sake:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_26::
    .string "For the earth is the Lord’s, and the\n"
    .string "fulness thereof$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_27::
    .string "If any of them that believe not bid\n"
    .string "you to a feast, and ye be disposed to\l"
    .string "go; whatsoever is set before you,\l"
    .string "eat, asking no question for\l"
    .string "conscience sake.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_28::
    .string "But if any man say unto you, This is\n"
    .string "offered in sacrifice unto idols, eat\l"
    .string "not for his sake that shewed it, and\l"
    .string "for conscience sake: for the earth is\l"
    .string "the Lord’s, and the fulness thereof:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_29::
    .string "Conscience, I say, not thine own,\n"
    .string "but of the other: for why is my\l"
    .string "liberty judged of another man’s\l"
    .string "conscience?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_30::
    .string "For if I by grace be a partaker, why\n"
    .string "am I evil spoken of for that for\l"
    .string "which I give thanks?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_31::
    .string "Whether therefore ye eat, or drink,\n"
    .string "or whatsoever ye do, do all to the\l"
    .string "glory of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_32::
    .string "Give none offence, neither to the\n"
    .string "Jews, nor to the Gentiles, nor to the\l"
    .string "church of God:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_10_33::
    .string "Even as I please all men in all\n"
    .string "things, not seeking mine own profit,\l"
    .string "but the profit of many, that they may\l"
    .string "be saved$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_1::
    .string "Be ye followers of me, even as I\n"
    .string "also am of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_2::
    .string "Now I praise you, brethren, that ye\n"
    .string "remember me in all things, and keep\l"
    .string "the ordinances, as I delivered them\l"
    .string "to you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_3::
    .string "But I would have you know, that the\n"
    .string "head of every man is Christ; and the\l"
    .string "head of the woman is the man; and the\l"
    .string "head of Christ is God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_4::
    .string "Every man praying or prophesying,\n"
    .string "having his head covered,\l"
    .string "dishonoureth his head.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_5::
    .string "But every woman that prayeth or\n"
    .string "prophesieth with her head uncovered\l"
    .string "dishonoureth her head: for that is\l"
    .string "even all one as if she were shaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_6::
    .string "For if the woman be not covered, let\n"
    .string "her also be shorn: but if it be a\l"
    .string "shame for a woman to be shorn or\l"
    .string "shaven, let her be covered.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_7::
    .string "For a man indeed ought not to cover\n"
    .string "his head, forasmuch as he is the\l"
    .string "image and glory of God: but the woman\l"
    .string "is the glory of the man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_8::
    .string "For the man is not of the woman: but\n"
    .string "the woman of the man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_9::
    .string "Neither was the man created for the\n"
    .string "woman; but the woman for the man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_10::
    .string "For this cause ought the woman to\n"
    .string "have power on her head because of\l"
    .string "the angels.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_11::
    .string "Nevertheless neither is the man\n"
    .string "without the woman, neither the woman\l"
    .string "without the man, in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_12::
    .string "For as the woman is of the man, even\n"
    .string "so is the man also by the woman; but\l"
    .string "all things of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_13::
    .string "Judge in yourselves: is it comely\n"
    .string "that a woman pray unto God\l"
    .string "uncovered?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_14::
    .string "Doth not even nature itself teach\n"
    .string "you, that, if a man have long hair,\l"
    .string "it is a shame unto him?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_15::
    .string "But if a woman have long hair, it is\n"
    .string "a glory to her: for her hair is given\l"
    .string "her for a covering$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_16::
    .string "But if any man seem to be\n"
    .string "contentious, we have no such custom,\l"
    .string "neither the churches of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_17::
    .string "Now in this that I declare unto you\n"
    .string "I praise you not, that ye come\l"
    .string "together not for the better, but for\l"
    .string "the worse.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_18::
    .string "For first of all, when ye come\n"
    .string "together in the church, I hear that\l"
    .string "there be divisions among you; and I\l"
    .string "partly believe it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_19::
    .string "For there must be also heresies\n"
    .string "among you, that they which are\l"
    .string "approved may be made manifest among\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_20::
    .string "When ye come together therefore\n"
    .string "into one place, this is not to eat\l"
    .string "the Lord’s supper.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_21::
    .string "For in eating every one taketh\n"
    .string "before other his own supper: and one\l"
    .string "is hungry, and another is drunken.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_22::
    .string "What? have ye not houses to eat and\n"
    .string "to drink in? or despise ye the church\l"
    .string "of God, and shame them that have not?\l"
    .string "What shall I say to you? shall I\l"
    .string "praise you in this? I praise you not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_23::
    .string "For I have received of the Lord that\n"
    .string "which also I delivered unto you,\l"
    .string "That the Lord Jesus the same night in\l"
    .string "which he was betrayed took bread:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_24::
    .string "And when he had given thanks, he\n"
    .string "brake it, and said, Take, eat: this is\l"
    .string "my body, which is broken for you:\l"
    .string "this do in remembrance of me$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_25::
    .string "After the same manner also he took\n"
    .string "the cup, when he had supped,\l"
    .string "saying, This cup is the new\l"
    .string "testament in my blood: this do ye, as\l"
    .string "oft as ye drink it, in remembrance of\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_26::
    .string "For as often as ye eat this bread,\n"
    .string "and drink this cup, ye do shew the\l"
    .string "Lord’s death till he come.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_27::
    .string "Wherefore whosoever shall eat this\n"
    .string "bread, and drink this cup of the\l"
    .string "Lord, unworthily, shall be guilty\l"
    .string "of the body and blood of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_28::
    .string "But let a man examine himself, and\n"
    .string "so let him eat of that bread, and\l"
    .string "drink of that cup.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_29::
    .string "For he that eateth and drinketh\n"
    .string "unworthily, eateth and drinketh\l"
    .string "damnation to himself, not discerning\l"
    .string "the Lord’s body.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_30::
    .string "For this cause many are weak and\n"
    .string "sickly among you, and many sleep.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_31::
    .string "For if we would judge ourselves, we\n"
    .string "should not be judged.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_32::
    .string "But when we are judged, we are\n"
    .string "chastened of the Lord, that we\l"
    .string "should not be condemned with the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_33::
    .string "Wherefore, my brethren, when ye come\n"
    .string "together to eat, tarry one for\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_11_34::
    .string "And if any man hunger, let him eat\n"
    .string "at home; that ye come not together\l"
    .string "unto condemnation. And the rest\l"
    .string "will I set in order when I come.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_1::
    .string "Now concerning spiritual gifts,\n"
    .string "brethren, I would not have you\l"
    .string "ignorant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_2::
    .string "Ye know that ye were Gentiles,\n"
    .string "carried away unto these dumb idols,\l"
    .string "even as ye were led.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_3::
    .string "Wherefore I give you to understand,\n"
    .string "that no man speaking by the Spirit\l"
    .string "of God calleth Jesus accursed: and\l"
    .string "that no man can say that Jesus is the\l"
    .string "Lord, but by the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_4::
    .string "Now there are diversities of gifts,\n"
    .string "but the same Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_5::
    .string "And there are differences of\n"
    .string "administrations, but the same Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_6::
    .string "And there are diversities of\n"
    .string "operations, but it is the same God\l"
    .string "which worketh all in all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_7::
    .string "But the manifestation of the Spirit\n"
    .string "is given to every man to profit\l"
    .string "withal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_8::
    .string "For to one is given by the Spirit\n"
    .string "the word of wisdom; to another the\l"
    .string "word of knowledge by the same\l"
    .string "Spirit;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_9::
    .string "To another faith by the same\n"
    .string "Spirit; to another the gifts of\l"
    .string "healing by the same Spirit;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_10::
    .string "To another the working of miracles;\n"
    .string "to another prophecy; to another\l"
    .string "discerning of spirits; to another\l"
    .string "divers kinds of tongues; to another\l"
    .string "the interpretation of tongues:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_11::
    .string "But all these worketh that one and\n"
    .string "the selfsame Spirit, dividing to\l"
    .string "every man severally as he will$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_12::
    .string "For as the body is one, and hath many\n"
    .string "members, and all the members of that\l"
    .string "one body, being many, are one body: so\l"
    .string "also is Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_13::
    .string "For by one Spirit are we all\n"
    .string "baptized into one body, whether we\l"
    .string "be Jews or Gentiles, whether we be\l"
    .string "bond or free; and have been all made\l"
    .string "to drink into one Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_14::
    .string "For the body is not one member, but\n"
    .string "many.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_15::
    .string "If the foot shall say, Because I am\n"
    .string "not the hand, I am not of the body; is\l"
    .string "it therefore not of the body?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_16::
    .string "And if the ear shall say, Because I\n"
    .string "am not the eye, I am not of the body;\l"
    .string "is it therefore not of the body?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_17::
    .string "If the whole body were an eye, where\n"
    .string "were the hearing? If the whole were\l"
    .string "hearing, where were the smelling?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_18::
    .string "But now hath God set the members\n"
    .string "every one of them in the body, as it\l"
    .string "hath pleased him$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_19::
    .string "And if they were all one member,\n"
    .string "where were the body?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_20::
    .string "But now are they many members, yet\n"
    .string "but one body$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_21::
    .string "And the eye cannot say unto the\n"
    .string "hand, I have no need of thee: nor\l"
    .string "again the head to the feet, I have no\l"
    .string "need of you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_22::
    .string "Nay, much more those members of the\n"
    .string "body, which seem to be more feeble,\l"
    .string "are necessary:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_23::
    .string "And those members of the body, which\n"
    .string "we think to be less honourable,\l"
    .string "upon these we bestow more abundant\l"
    .string "honour; and our uncomely parts have\l"
    .string "more abundant comeliness$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_24::
    .string "For our comely parts have no need:\n"
    .string "but God hath tempered the body\l"
    .string "together, having given more abundant\l"
    .string "honour to that part which lacked.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_25::
    .string "That there should be no schism in\n"
    .string "the body; but that the members\l"
    .string "should have the same care one for\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_26::
    .string "And whether one member suffer, all\n"
    .string "the members suffer with it; or one\l"
    .string "member be honoured, all the members\l"
    .string "rejoice with it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_27::
    .string "Now ye are the body of Christ, and\n"
    .string "members in particular.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_28::
    .string "And God hath set some in the church,\n"
    .string "first apostles, secondarily\l"
    .string "prophets, thirdly teachers, after\l"
    .string "that miracles, then gifts of\l"
    .string "healings, helps, governments,\l"
    .string "diversities of tongues.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_29::
    .string "Are all apostles? are all\n"
    .string "prophets? are all teachers? are\l"
    .string "all workers of miracles?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_30::
    .string "Have all the gifts of healing? do\n"
    .string "all speak with tongues? do all\l"
    .string "interpret?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_12_31::
    .string "But covet earnestly the best gifts:\n"
    .string "and yet shew I unto you a more\l"
    .string "excellent way$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_1::
    .string "Though I speak with the tongues of\n"
    .string "men and of angels, and have not\l"
    .string "charity, I am become as sounding\l"
    .string "brass, or a tinkling cymbal.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_2::
    .string "And though I have the gift of\n"
    .string "prophecy, and understand all\l"
    .string "mysteries, and all knowledge; and\l"
    .string "though I have all faith, so that I\l"
    .string "could remove mountains, and have not\l"
    .string "charity, I am nothing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_3::
    .string "And though I bestow all my goods to\n"
    .string "feed the poor, and though I give my\l"
    .string "body to be burned, and have not\l"
    .string "charity, it profiteth me nothing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_4::
    .string "Charity suffereth long, and is\n"
    .string "kind; charity envieth not; charity\l"
    .string "vaunteth not itself, is not puffed\l"
    .string "up,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_5::
    .string "Doth not behave itself unseemly,\n"
    .string "seeketh not her own, is not easily\l"
    .string "provoked, thinketh no evil;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_6::
    .string "Rejoiceth not in iniquity, but\n"
    .string "rejoiceth in the truth;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_7::
    .string "Beareth all things, believeth\n"
    .string "all things, hopeth all things,\l"
    .string "endureth all things$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_8::
    .string "Charity never faileth: but whether\n"
    .string "there be prophecies, they shall\l"
    .string "fail; whether there be tongues, they\l"
    .string "shall cease; whether there be\l"
    .string "knowledge, it shall vanish away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_9::
    .string "For we know in part, and we\n"
    .string "prophesy in part.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_10::
    .string "But when that which is perfect is\n"
    .string "come, then that which is in part\l"
    .string "shall be done away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_11::
    .string "When I was a child, I spake as a\n"
    .string "child, I understood as a child, I\l"
    .string "thought as a child: but when I became\l"
    .string "a man, I put away childish things.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_12::
    .string "For now we see through a glass,\n"
    .string "darkly; but then face to face: now I\l"
    .string "know in part; but then shall I know\l"
    .string "even as also I am known.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_13_13::
    .string "And now abideth faith, hope,\n"
    .string "charity, these three; but the\l"
    .string "greatest of these is charity.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_1::
    .string "Follow after charity, and desire\n"
    .string "spiritual gifts, but rather that ye\l"
    .string "may prophesy.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_2::
    .string "For he that speaketh in an unknown\n"
    .string "tongue speaketh not unto men, but\l"
    .string "unto God: for no man understandeth\l"
    .string "him; howbeit in the spirit he\l"
    .string "speaketh mysteries.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_3::
    .string "But he that prophesieth speaketh\n"
    .string "unto men to edification, and\l"
    .string "exhortation, and comfort.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_4::
    .string "He that speaketh in an unknown\n"
    .string "tongue edifieth himself; but he that\l"
    .string "prophesieth edifieth the church.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_5::
    .string "I would that ye all spake with\n"
    .string "tongues but rather that ye\l"
    .string "prophesied: for greater is he that\l"
    .string "prophesieth than he that speaketh\l"
    .string "with tongues, except he interpret,\l"
    .string "that the church may receive edifying.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_6::
    .string "Now, brethren, if I come unto you\n"
    .string "speaking with tongues, what shall I\l"
    .string "profit you, except I shall speak\l"
    .string "to you either by revelation, or by\l"
    .string "knowledge, or by prophesying, or by\l"
    .string "doctrine?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_7::
    .string "And even things without life giving\n"
    .string "sound, whether pipe or harp,\l"
    .string "except they give a distinction in\l"
    .string "the sounds, how shall it be known\l"
    .string "what is piped or harped?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_8::
    .string "For if the trumpet give an\n"
    .string "uncertain sound, who shall prepare\l"
    .string "himself to the battle?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_9::
    .string "So likewise ye, except ye utter by\n"
    .string "the tongue words easy to be\l"
    .string "understood, how shall it be known\l"
    .string "what is spoken? for ye shall speak\l"
    .string "into the air$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_10::
    .string "There are, it may be, so many kinds\n"
    .string "of voices in the world, and none of\l"
    .string "them is without signification.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_11::
    .string "Therefore if I know not the meaning\n"
    .string "of the voice, I shall be unto him\l"
    .string "that speaketh a barbarian, and he\l"
    .string "that speaketh shall be a barbarian\l"
    .string "unto me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_12::
    .string "Even so ye, forasmuch as ye are\n"
    .string "zealous of spiritual gifts, seek\l"
    .string "that ye may excel to the edifying of\l"
    .string "the church.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_13::
    .string "Wherefore let him that speaketh in\n"
    .string "an unknown tongue pray that he may\l"
    .string "interpret.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_14::
    .string "For if I pray in an unknown tongue,\n"
    .string "my spirit prayeth, but my\l"
    .string "understanding is unfruitful.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_15::
    .string "What is it then? I will pray with\n"
    .string "the spirit, and I will pray with\l"
    .string "the understanding also: I will sing\l"
    .string "with the spirit, and I will sing\l"
    .string "with the understanding also.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_16::
    .string "Else when thou shalt bless with\n"
    .string "the spirit, how shall he that\l"
    .string "occupieth the room of the unlearned\l"
    .string "say Amen at thy giving of thanks,\l"
    .string "seeing he understandeth not what\l"
    .string "thou sayest?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_17::
    .string "For thou verily givest thanks\n"
    .string "well, but the other is not edified$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_18::
    .string "I thank my God, I speak with tongues\n"
    .string "more than ye all:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_19::
    .string "Yet in the church I had rather\n"
    .string "speak five words with my\l"
    .string "understanding, that by my voice I\l"
    .string "might teach others also, than ten\l"
    .string "thousand words in an unknown tongue$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_20::
    .string "Brethren, be not children in\n"
    .string "understanding: howbeit in malice be\l"
    .string "ye children, but in understanding be\l"
    .string "men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_21::
    .string "In the law it is written, With men\n"
    .string "of other tongues and other lips\l"
    .string "will I speak unto this people;\l"
    .string "and yet for all that will they not\l"
    .string "hear me, saith the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_22::
    .string "Wherefore tongues are for a sign,\n"
    .string "not to them that believe, but to them\l"
    .string "that believe not: but prophesying\l"
    .string "serveth not for them that believe\l"
    .string "not, but for them which believe.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_23::
    .string "If therefore the whole church be\n"
    .string "come together into one place, and\l"
    .string "all speak with tongues, and there\l"
    .string "come in those that are unlearned, or\l"
    .string "unbelievers, will they not say that\l"
    .string "ye are mad?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_24::
    .string "But if all prophesy, and there\n"
    .string "come in one that believeth not, or\l"
    .string "one unlearned, he is convinced of\l"
    .string "all, he is judged of all:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_25::
    .string "And thus are the secrets of his\n"
    .string "heart made manifest; and so falling\l"
    .string "down on his face he will worship\l"
    .string "God, and report that God is in you of\l"
    .string "a truth$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_26::
    .string "How is it then, brethren? when ye\n"
    .string "come together, every one of you hath\l"
    .string "a psalm, hath a doctrine, hath a\l"
    .string "tongue, hath a revelation, hath an\l"
    .string "interpretation. Let all things be\l"
    .string "done unto edifying.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_27::
    .string "If any man speak in an unknown\n"
    .string "tongue, let it be by two, or at the\l"
    .string "most by three, and that by course;\l"
    .string "and let one interpret.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_28::
    .string "But if there be no interpreter, let\n"
    .string "him keep silence in the church; and\l"
    .string "let him speak to himself, and to God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_29::
    .string "Let the prophets speak two or\n"
    .string "three, and let the other judge.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_30::
    .string "If any thing be revealed to another\n"
    .string "that sitteth by, let the first hold\l"
    .string "his peace.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_31::
    .string "For ye may all prophesy one by\n"
    .string "one, that all may learn, and all\l"
    .string "may be comforted.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_32::
    .string "And the spirits of the prophets\n"
    .string "are subject to the prophets.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_33::
    .string "For God is not the author of\n"
    .string "confusion, but of peace, as in all\l"
    .string "churches of the saints.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_34::
    .string "Let your women keep silence in the\n"
    .string "churches: for it is not permitted\l"
    .string "unto them to speak; but they are\l"
    .string "commanded to be under obedience as\l"
    .string "also saith the law.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_35::
    .string "And if they will learn any thing,\n"
    .string "let them ask their husbands at home:\l"
    .string "for it is a shame for women to speak\l"
    .string "in the church.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_36::
    .string "What? came the word of God out from\n"
    .string "you? or came it unto you only?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_37::
    .string "If any man think himself to be a\n"
    .string "prophet, or spiritual, let him\l"
    .string "acknowledge that the things that I\l"
    .string "write unto you are the commandments\l"
    .string "of the Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_38::
    .string "But if any man be ignorant, let him\n"
    .string "be ignorant.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_39::
    .string "Wherefore, brethren, covet to\n"
    .string "prophesy, and forbid not to speak\l"
    .string "with tongues.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_14_40::
    .string "Let all things be done decently\n"
    .string "and in order.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_1::
    .string "Moreover, brethren, I declare unto\n"
    .string "you the gospel which I preached\l"
    .string "unto you, which also ye have\l"
    .string "received, and wherein ye stand;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_2::
    .string "By which also ye are saved, if ye\n"
    .string "keep in memory what I preached unto\l"
    .string "you, unless ye have believed in vain$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_3::
    .string "For I delivered unto you first of\n"
    .string "all that which I also received, how\l"
    .string "that Christ died for our sins\l"
    .string "according to the scriptures;"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_4::
    .string "And that he was buried, and that he\n"
    .string "rose again the third day according to\l"
    .string "the scriptures:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_5::
    .string "And that he was seen of Cephas, then\n"
    .string "of the twelve:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_6::
    .string "After that, he was seen of above\n"
    .string "five hundred brethren at once; of\l"
    .string "whom the greater part remain unto\l"
    .string "this present, but some are fallen\l"
    .string "asleep$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_7::
    .string "After that, he was seen of James;\n"
    .string "then of all the apostles.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_8::
    .string "And last of all he was seen of me\n"
    .string "also, as of one born out of due time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_9::
    .string "For I am the least of the\n"
    .string "apostles, that am not meet to be\l"
    .string "called an apostle, because I\l"
    .string "persecuted the church of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_10::
    .string "But by the grace of God I am what I\n"
    .string "am: and his grace which was bestowed\l"
    .string "upon me was not in vain; but I\l"
    .string "laboured more abundantly than they\l"
    .string "all: yet not I, but the grace of God\l"
    .string "which was with me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_11::
    .string "Therefore whether it were I or they,\n"
    .string "so we preach, and so ye believed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_12::
    .string "Now if Christ be preached that he\n"
    .string "rose from the dead, how say some\l"
    .string "among you that there is no\l"
    .string "resurrection of the dead?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_13::
    .string "But if there be no resurrection of\n"
    .string "the dead, then is Christ not risen:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_14::
    .string "And if Christ be not risen, then is\n"
    .string "our preaching vain, and your faith\l"
    .string "is also vain$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_15::
    .string "Yea, and we are found false\n"
    .string "witnesses of God; because we have\l"
    .string "testified of God that he raised up\l"
    .string "Christ: whom he raised not up, if so\l"
    .string "be that the dead rise not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_16::
    .string "For if the dead rise not, then is not\n"
    .string "Christ raised:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_17::
    .string "And if Christ be not raised, your\n"
    .string "faith is vain; ye are yet in your sins$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_18::
    .string "Then they also which are fallen\n"
    .string "asleep in Christ are perished.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_19::
    .string "If in this life only we have hope\n"
    .string "in Christ, we are of all men most\l"
    .string "miserable.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_20::
    .string "But now is Christ risen from the\n"
    .string "dead, and become the firstfruits of\l"
    .string "them that slept.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_21::
    .string "For since by man came death, by man\n"
    .string "came also the resurrection of the\l"
    .string "dead.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_22::
    .string "For as in Adam all die, even so in\n"
    .string "Christ shall all be made alive.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_23::
    .string "But every man in his own order:\n"
    .string "Christ the firstfruits; afterward\l"
    .string "they that are Christ’s at his coming.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_24::
    .string "Then cometh the end, when he shall\n"
    .string "have delivered up the kingdom to\l"
    .string "God, even the Father; when he shall\l"
    .string "have put down all rule and all\l"
    .string "authority and power.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_25::
    .string "For he must reign, till he hath\n"
    .string "put all enemies under his feet.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_26::
    .string "The last enemy that shall be\n"
    .string "destroyed is death.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_27::
    .string "For he hath put all things under\n"
    .string "his feet. But when he saith all\l"
    .string "things are put under him, it is\l"
    .string "manifest that he is excepted, which\l"
    .string "did put all things under him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_28::
    .string "And when all things shall be\n"
    .string "subdued unto him, then shall the Son\l"
    .string "also himself be subject unto him\l"
    .string "that put all things under him, that\l"
    .string "God may be all in all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_29::
    .string "Else what shall they do which are\n"
    .string "baptized for the dead, if the dead\l"
    .string "rise not at all? why are they then\l"
    .string "baptized for the dead?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_30::
    .string "And why stand we in jeopardy every\n"
    .string "hour?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_31::
    .string "I protest by your rejoicing which I\n"
    .string "have in Christ Jesus our LORD, I die\l"
    .string "daily$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_32::
    .string "If after the manner of men I have\n"
    .string "fought with beasts at Ephesus, what\l"
    .string "advantageth it me, if the dead rise\l"
    .string "not? let us eat and drink; for to\l"
    .string "morrow we die.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_33::
    .string "Be not deceived: evil\n"
    .string "communications corrupt good manners.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_34::
    .string "Awake to righteousness, and sin not;\n"
    .string "for some have not the knowledge of\l"
    .string "God: I speak this to your shame.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_35::
    .string "But some man will say, How are the\n"
    .string "dead raised up? and with what body do\l"
    .string "they come?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_36::
    .string "Thou fool, that which thou sowest\n"
    .string "is not quickened, except it die:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_37::
    .string "And that which thou sowest, thou\n"
    .string "sowest not that body that shall be,\l"
    .string "but bare grain, it may chance of\l"
    .string "wheat, or of some other grain:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_38::
    .string "But God giveth it a body as it hath\n"
    .string "pleased him, and to every seed his\l"
    .string "own body$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_39::
    .string "All flesh is not the same flesh:\n"
    .string "but there is one kind of flesh of\l"
    .string "men, another flesh of beasts,\l"
    .string "another of fishes, and another of\l"
    .string "birds.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_40::
    .string "There are also celestial bodies,\n"
    .string "and bodies terrestrial: but the\l"
    .string "glory of the celestial is one, and\l"
    .string "the glory of the terrestrial is\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_41::
    .string "There is one glory of the sun, and\n"
    .string "another glory of the moon, and\l"
    .string "another glory of the stars: for one\l"
    .string "star differeth from another star in\l"
    .string "glory.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_42::
    .string "So also is the resurrection of the\n"
    .string "dead. It is sown in corruption; it is\l"
    .string "raised in incorruption:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_43::
    .string "It is sown in dishonour; it is\n"
    .string "raised in glory: it is sown in\l"
    .string "weakness; it is raised in power:"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_44::
    .string "It is sown a natural body; it is\n"
    .string "raised a spiritual body. There is a\l"
    .string "natural body, and there is a\l"
    .string "spiritual body$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_45::
    .string "And so it is written, The first man\n"
    .string "Adam was made a living soul; the\l"
    .string "last Adam was made a quickening\l"
    .string "spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_46::
    .string "Howbeit that was not first which is\n"
    .string "spiritual, but that which is\l"
    .string "natural; and afterward that which is\l"
    .string "spiritual.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_47::
    .string "The first man is of the earth,\n"
    .string "earthy; the second man is the Lord\l"
    .string "from heaven.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_48::
    .string "As is the earthy, such are they also\n"
    .string "that are earthy: and as is the\l"
    .string "heavenly, such are they also that\l"
    .string "are heavenly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_49::
    .string "And as we have borne the image of\n"
    .string "the earthy, we shall also bear the\l"
    .string "image of the heavenly.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_50::
    .string "Now this I say, brethren, that\n"
    .string "flesh and blood cannot inherit the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God; neither doth\l"
    .string "corruption inherit incorruption.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_51::
    .string "Behold, I shew you a mystery; We\n"
    .string "shall not all sleep, but we\l"
    .string "shall all be changed,"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_52::
    .string "In a moment, in the twinkling of an\n"
    .string "eye, at the last trump: for the\l"
    .string "trumpet shall sound, and the dead\l"
    .string "shall be raised incorruptible, and\l"
    .string "we shall be changed$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_53::
    .string "For this corruptible must put on\n"
    .string "incorruption, and this mortal must\l"
    .string "put on immortality.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_54::
    .string "So when this corruptible shall\n"
    .string "have put on incorruption, and this\l"
    .string "mortal shall have put on\l"
    .string "immortality, then shall be brought\l"
    .string "to pass the saying that is written,\l"
    .string "Death is swallowed up in victory.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_55::
    .string "O death, where is thy sting? O grave,\n"
    .string "where is thy victory?"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_56::
    .string "The sting of death is sin; and the\n"
    .string "strength of sin is the law$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_57::
    .string "But thanks be to God, which giveth\n"
    .string "us the victory through our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_15_58::
    .string "Therefore, my beloved brethren, be\n"
    .string "ye stedfast, unmoveable, always\l"
    .string "abounding in the work of the Lord,\l"
    .string "forasmuch as ye know that your\l"
    .string "labour is not in vain in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_1::
    .string "Now concerning the collection for\n"
    .string "the saints, as I have given order to\l"
    .string "the churches of Galatia, even so do\l"
    .string "ye.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_2::
    .string "Upon the first day of the week let\n"
    .string "every one of you lay by him in store,\l"
    .string "as God hath prospered him, that\l"
    .string "there be no gatherings when I come.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_3::
    .string "And when I come, whomsoever ye\n"
    .string "shall approve by your letters,\l"
    .string "them will I send to bring your\l"
    .string "liberality unto Jerusalem.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_4::
    .string "And if it be meet that I go also,\n"
    .string "they shall go with me.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_5::
    .string "Now I will come unto you, when I\n"
    .string "shall pass through Macedonia: for I\l"
    .string "do pass through Macedonia.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_6::
    .string "And it may be that I will abide,\n"
    .string "yea, and winter with you, that ye may\l"
    .string "bring me on my journey whithersoever\l"
    .string "I go.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_7::
    .string "For I will not see you now by the\n"
    .string "way; but I trust to tarry a while\l"
    .string "with you, if the Lord permit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_8::
    .string "But I will tarry at Ephesus until\n"
    .string "Pentecost.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_9::
    .string "For a great door and effectual is\n"
    .string "opened unto me, and there are many\l"
    .string "adversaries.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_10::
    .string "Now if Timotheus come, see that he\n"
    .string "may be with you without fear: for he\l"
    .string "worketh the work of the Lord, as I\l"
    .string "also do.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_11::
    .string "Let no man therefore despise him:\n"
    .string "but conduct him forth in peace, that\l"
    .string "he may come unto me: for I look for\l"
    .string "him with the brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_12::
    .string "As touching our brother Apollos, I\n"
    .string "greatly desired him to come unto you\l"
    .string "with the brethren: but his will was\l"
    .string "not at all to come at this time; but\l"
    .string "he will come when he shall have\l"
    .string "convenient time.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_13::
    .string "Watch ye, stand fast in the faith,\n"
    .string "quit you like men, be strong.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_14::
    .string "Let all your things be done with\n"
    .string "charity.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_15::
    .string "I beseech you, brethren, (ye know\n"
    .string "the house of Stephanas, that it is\l"
    .string "the firstfruits of Achaia, and that\l"
    .string "they have addicted themselves to the\l"
    .string "ministry of the saints,)"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_16::
    .string "That ye submit yourselves unto\n"
    .string "such, and to every one that helpeth\l"
    .string "with us, and laboureth$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_17::
    .string "I am glad of the coming of\n"
    .string "Stephanas and Fortunatus and\l"
    .string "Achaicus: for that which was lacking\l"
    .string "on your part they have supplied.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_18::
    .string "For they have refreshed my spirit\n"
    .string "and yours: therefore acknowledge ye\l"
    .string "them that are such.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_19::
    .string "The churches of Asia salute you.\n"
    .string "Aquila and Priscilla salute you\l"
    .string "much in the Lord, with the church\l"
    .string "that is in their house.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_20::
    .string "All the brethren greet you. Greet\n"
    .string "ye one another with an holy kiss.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_21::
    .string "The salutation of me Paul with\n"
    .string "mine own hand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_22::
    .string "If any man love not the Lord Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ, let him be Anathema\l"
    .string "Maranatha.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_23::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Corinthians_16_24::
    .string "My love be with you all in Christ\n"
    .string "Jesus. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "by the will of God, and Timothy our\l"
    .string "brother, unto the church of God which\l"
    .string "is at Corinth, with all the saints\l"
    .string "which are in all Achaia:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_2::
    .string "Grace be to you and peace from God\n"
    .string "our Father, and from the Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_3::
    .string "Blessed be God, even the Father of\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of\l"
    .string "mercies, and the God of all comfort;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_4::
    .string "Who comforteth us in all our\n"
    .string "tribulation, that we may be able to\l"
    .string "comfort them which are in any\l"
    .string "trouble, by the comfort wherewith we\l"
    .string "ourselves are comforted of God$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_5::
    .string "For as the sufferings of Christ\n"
    .string "abound in us, so our consolation\l"
    .string "also aboundeth by Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_6::
    .string "And whether we be afflicted, it is\n"
    .string "for your consolation and salvation,\l"
    .string "which is effectual in the enduring\l"
    .string "of the same sufferings which we also\l"
    .string "suffer: or whether we be comforted,\l"
    .string "it is for your consolation and\l"
    .string "salvation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_7::
    .string "And our hope of you is stedfast,\n"
    .string "knowing, that as ye are partakers of\l"
    .string "the sufferings, so shall ye be also\l"
    .string "of the consolation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_8::
    .string "For we would not, brethren, have\n"
    .string "you ignorant of our trouble which\l"
    .string "came to us in Asia, that we were\l"
    .string "pressed out of measure, above\l"
    .string "strength, insomuch that we despaired\l"
    .string "even of life:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_9::
    .string "But we had the sentence of death in\n"
    .string "ourselves, that we should not trust\l"
    .string "in ourselves, but in God which\l"
    .string "raiseth the dead:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_10::
    .string "Who delivered us from so great a\n"
    .string "death, and doth deliver: in whom we\l"
    .string "trust that he will yet deliver us;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_11::
    .string "Ye also helping together by\n"
    .string "prayer for us, that for the gift\l"
    .string "bestowed upon us by the means of\l"
    .string "many persons thanks may be given by\l"
    .string "many on our behalf$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_12::
    .string "For our rejoicing is this, the\n"
    .string "testimony of our conscience, that in\l"
    .string "simplicity and godly sincerity,\l"
    .string "not with fleshly wisdom, but by the\l"
    .string "grace of God, we have had our\l"
    .string "conversation in the world, and more\l"
    .string "abundantly to you-ward.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_13::
    .string "For we write none other things unto\n"
    .string "you, than what ye read or\l"
    .string "acknowledge; and I trust ye shall\l"
    .string "acknowledge even to the end;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_14::
    .string "As also ye have acknowledged us in\n"
    .string "part, that we are your rejoicing,\l"
    .string "even as ye also are ours in the day\l"
    .string "of the Lord Jesus$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_15::
    .string "And in this confidence I was minded\n"
    .string "to come unto you before, that ye\l"
    .string "might have a second benefit;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_16::
    .string "And to pass by you into Macedonia,\n"
    .string "and to come again out of Macedonia\l"
    .string "unto you, and of you to be brought on\l"
    .string "my way toward Judaea$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_17::
    .string "When I therefore was thus minded,\n"
    .string "did I use lightness? or the things\l"
    .string "that I purpose, do I purpose\l"
    .string "according to the flesh, that with me\l"
    .string "there should be yea yea, and nay nay?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_18::
    .string "But as God is true, our word toward\n"
    .string "you was not yea and nay$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_19::
    .string "For the Son of God, Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "who was preached among you by us,\l"
    .string "even by me and Silvanus and\l"
    .string "Timotheus, was not yea and nay, but\l"
    .string "in him was yea.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_20::
    .string "For all the promises of God in him\n"
    .string "are yea, and in him Amen, unto the\l"
    .string "glory of God by us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_21::
    .string "Now he which stablisheth us with\n"
    .string "you in Christ, and hath anointed us,\l"
    .string "is God;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_22::
    .string "Who hath also sealed us, and given\n"
    .string "the earnest of the Spirit in our\l"
    .string "hearts$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_23::
    .string "Moreover I call God for a record\n"
    .string "upon my soul, that to spare you I\l"
    .string "came not as yet unto Corinth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_1_24::
    .string "Not for that we have dominion over\n"
    .string "your faith, but are helpers of your\l"
    .string "joy: for by faith ye stand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_1::
    .string "But I determined this with myself,\n"
    .string "that I would not come again to you in\l"
    .string "heaviness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_2::
    .string "For if I make you sorry, who is he\n"
    .string "then that maketh me glad, but the\l"
    .string "same which is made sorry by me?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_3::
    .string "And I wrote this same unto you,\n"
    .string "lest, when I came, I should have\l"
    .string "sorrow from them of whom I ought to\l"
    .string "rejoice; having confidence in you\l"
    .string "all, that my joy is the joy of you\l"
    .string "all$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_4::
    .string "For out of much affliction and\n"
    .string "anguish of heart I wrote unto you\l"
    .string "with many tears; not that ye should\l"
    .string "be grieved, but that ye might know\l"
    .string "the love which I have more\l"
    .string "abundantly unto you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_5::
    .string "But if any have caused grief, he\n"
    .string "hath not grieved me, but in part:\l"
    .string "that I may not overcharge you all.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_6::
    .string "Sufficient to such a man is this\n"
    .string "punishment, which was inflicted of\l"
    .string "many.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_7::
    .string "So that contrariwise ye ought\n"
    .string "rather to forgive him, and comfort\l"
    .string "him, lest perhaps such a one\l"
    .string "should be swallowed up with\l"
    .string "overmuch sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_8::
    .string "Wherefore I beseech you that ye\n"
    .string "would confirm your love toward him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_9::
    .string "For to this end also did I write,\n"
    .string "that I might know the proof of you,\l"
    .string "whether ye be obedient in all\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_10::
    .string "To whom ye forgive any thing, I\n"
    .string "forgive also: for if I forgave any\l"
    .string "thing, to whom I forgave it, for your\l"
    .string "sakes forgave I it in the person of\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_11::
    .string "Lest Satan should get an advantage\n"
    .string "of us: for we are not ignorant of his\l"
    .string "devices$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_12::
    .string "Furthermore, when I came to Troas to\n"
    .string "preach Christ’s gospel, and a door\l"
    .string "was opened unto me of the Lord,"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_13::
    .string "I had no rest in my spirit, because\n"
    .string "I found not Titus my brother: but\l"
    .string "taking my leave of them, I went from\l"
    .string "thence into Macedonia$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_14::
    .string "Now thanks be unto God, which\n"
    .string "always causeth us to triumph in\l"
    .string "Christ, and maketh manifest the\l"
    .string "savour of his knowledge by us in\l"
    .string "every place.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_15::
    .string "For we are unto God a sweet savour\n"
    .string "of Christ, in them that are saved,\l"
    .string "and in them that perish:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_16::
    .string "To the one we are the savour of\n"
    .string "death unto death; and to the other\l"
    .string "the savour of life unto life. And\l"
    .string "who is sufficient for these things?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_2_17::
    .string "For we are not as many, which\n"
    .string "corrupt the word of God: but as of\l"
    .string "sincerity, but as of God, in the\l"
    .string "sight of God speak we in Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_1::
    .string "Do we begin again to commend\n"
    .string "ourselves? or need we, as some\l"
    .string "others, epistles of commendation to\l"
    .string "you, or letters of commendation from\l"
    .string "you?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_2::
    .string "Ye are our epistle written in our\n"
    .string "hearts, known and read of all men:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_3::
    .string "Forasmuch as ye are manifestly\n"
    .string "declared to be the epistle of\l"
    .string "Christ ministered by us, written not\l"
    .string "with ink, but with the Spirit of the\l"
    .string "living God; not in tables of stone,\l"
    .string "but in fleshy tables of the heart$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_4::
    .string "And such trust have we through\n"
    .string "Christ to God-ward:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_5::
    .string "Not that we are sufficient of\n"
    .string "ourselves to think any thing as of\l"
    .string "ourselves; but our sufficiency is of\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_6::
    .string "Who also hath made us able\n"
    .string "ministers of the new testament; not\l"
    .string "of the letter, but of the spirit:\l"
    .string "for the letter killeth, but the\l"
    .string "spirit giveth life$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_7::
    .string "But if the ministration of death,\n"
    .string "written and engraven in stones, was\l"
    .string "glorious, so that the children of\l"
    .string "Israel could not stedfastly\l"
    .string "behold the face of Moses for the\l"
    .string "glory of his countenance; which\l"
    .string "glory was to be done away:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_8::
    .string "How shall not the ministration of\n"
    .string "the spirit be rather glorious?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_9::
    .string "For if the ministration of\n"
    .string "condemnation be glory, much more\l"
    .string "doth the ministration of\l"
    .string "righteousness exceed in glory$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_10::
    .string "For even that which was made\n"
    .string "glorious had no glory in this\l"
    .string "respect, by reason of the glory that\l"
    .string "excelleth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_11::
    .string "For if that which is done away was\n"
    .string "glorious, much more that which\l"
    .string "remaineth is glorious.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_12::
    .string "Seeing then that we have such hope,\n"
    .string "we use great plainness of speech:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_13::
    .string "And not as Moses, which put a vail\n"
    .string "over his face, that the children of\l"
    .string "Israel could not stedfastly look\l"
    .string "to the end of that which is\l"
    .string "abolished:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_14::
    .string "But their minds were blinded: for\n"
    .string "until this day remaineth the same\l"
    .string "vail untaken away in the reading of\l"
    .string "the old testament; which vail is\l"
    .string "done away in Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_15::
    .string "But even unto this day, when Moses\n"
    .string "is read, the vail is upon their\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_16::
    .string "Nevertheless when it shall turn\n"
    .string "to the Lord, the vail shall be\l"
    .string "taken away.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_17::
    .string "Now the Lord is that Spirit: and\n"
    .string "where the Spirit of the Lord is,\l"
    .string "there is liberty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_3_18::
    .string "But we all, with open face\n"
    .string "beholding as in a glass the glory\l"
    .string "of the Lord, are changed into the\l"
    .string "same image from glory to glory, even\l"
    .string "as by the Spirit of the LORD.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_1::
    .string "Therefore seeing we have this\n"
    .string "ministry, as we have received mercy,\l"
    .string "we faint not;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_2::
    .string "But have renounced the hidden\n"
    .string "things of dishonesty, not walking in\l"
    .string "craftiness, nor handling the word of\l"
    .string "God deceitfully; but by\l"
    .string "manifestation of the truth\l"
    .string "commending ourselves to every man’s\l"
    .string "conscience in the sight of God$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_3::
    .string "But if our gospel be hid, it is hid\n"
    .string "to them that are lost:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_4::
    .string "In whom the god of this world hath\n"
    .string "blinded the minds of them which\l"
    .string "believe not, lest the light of the\l"
    .string "glorious gospel of Christ, who is\l"
    .string "the image of God, should shine unto\l"
    .string "them$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_5::
    .string "For we preach not ourselves, but\n"
    .string "Christ Jesus the Lord; and ourselves\l"
    .string "your servants for Jesus’ sake.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_6::
    .string "For God, who commanded the light to\n"
    .string "shine out of darkness, hath shined in\l"
    .string "our hearts, to give the light of the\l"
    .string "knowledge of the glory of God in the\l"
    .string "face of Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_7::
    .string "But we have this treasure in earthen\n"
    .string "vessels, that the excellency of the\l"
    .string "power may be of God, and not of us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_8::
    .string "We are troubled on every side, yet\n"
    .string "not distressed; we are perplexed,\l"
    .string "but not in despair;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_9::
    .string "Persecuted, but not forsaken; cast\n"
    .string "down, but not destroyed;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_10::
    .string "Always bearing about in the body\n"
    .string "the dying of the Lord Jesus, that the\l"
    .string "life also of Jesus might be made\l"
    .string "manifest in our body$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_11::
    .string "For we which live are alway\n"
    .string "delivered unto death for Jesus’\l"
    .string "sake, that the life also of Jesus\l"
    .string "might be made manifest in our mortal\l"
    .string "flesh.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_12::
    .string "So then death worketh in us, but\n"
    .string "life in you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_13::
    .string "We having the same spirit of faith,\n"
    .string "according as it is written, I\l"
    .string "believed, and therefore have I\l"
    .string "spoken; we also believe, and\l"
    .string "therefore speak;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_14::
    .string "Knowing that he which raised up the\n"
    .string "Lord Jesus shall raise up us also\l"
    .string "by Jesus, and shall present us with\l"
    .string "you$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_15::
    .string "For all things are for your sakes,\n"
    .string "that the abundant grace might\l"
    .string "through the thanksgiving of many\l"
    .string "redound to the glory of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_16::
    .string "For which cause we faint not; but\n"
    .string "though our outward man perish, yet\l"
    .string "the inward man is renewed day by day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_17::
    .string "For our light affliction, which is\n"
    .string "but for a moment, worketh for us a far\l"
    .string "more exceeding and eternal weight of\l"
    .string "glory;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_4_18::
    .string "While we look not at the things\n"
    .string "which are seen, but at the things\l"
    .string "which are not seen: for the things\l"
    .string "which are seen are temporal; but the\l"
    .string "things which are not seen are eternal$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_1::
    .string "For we know that if our earthly\n"
    .string "house of this tabernacle were\l"
    .string "dissolved, we have a building of\l"
    .string "God, an house not made with hands,\l"
    .string "eternal in the heavens.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_2::
    .string "For in this we groan, earnestly\n"
    .string "desiring to be clothed upon with\l"
    .string "our house which is from heaven:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_3::
    .string "If so be that being clothed we\n"
    .string "shall not be found naked$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_4::
    .string "For we that are in this tabernacle\n"
    .string "do groan, being burdened: not for\l"
    .string "that we would be unclothed, but\l"
    .string "clothed upon, that mortality might\l"
    .string "be swallowed up of life.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_5::
    .string "Now he that hath wrought us for the\n"
    .string "selfsame thing is God, who also hath\l"
    .string "given unto us the earnest of the\l"
    .string "Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_6::
    .string "Therefore we are always confident,\n"
    .string "knowing that, whilst we are at home\l"
    .string "in the body, we are absent from the\l"
    .string "Lord:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_7::
    .string "(For we walk by faith, not by\n"
    .string "sight:)"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_8::
    .string "We are confident, I say, and\n"
    .string "willing rather to be absent from\l"
    .string "the body, and to be present with the\l"
    .string "Lord$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_9::
    .string "Wherefore we labour, that, whether\n"
    .string "present or absent, we may be\l"
    .string "accepted of him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_10::
    .string "For we must all appear before the\n"
    .string "judgment seat of Christ; that every\l"
    .string "one may receive the things done in\l"
    .string "his body, according to that he hath\l"
    .string "done, whether it be good or bad.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_11::
    .string "Knowing therefore the terror of the\n"
    .string "Lord, we persuade men; but we are\l"
    .string "made manifest unto God; and I trust\l"
    .string "also are made manifest in your\l"
    .string "consciences.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_12::
    .string "For we commend not ourselves again\n"
    .string "unto you, but give you occasion to\l"
    .string "glory on our behalf, that ye may\l"
    .string "have somewhat to answer them which\l"
    .string "glory in appearance, and not in\l"
    .string "heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_13::
    .string "For whether we be beside ourselves,\n"
    .string "it is to God: or whether we be sober,\l"
    .string "it is for your cause.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_14::
    .string "For the love of Christ constraineth\n"
    .string "us; because we thus judge, that if\l"
    .string "one died for all, then were all\l"
    .string "dead:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_15::
    .string "And that he died for all, that they\n"
    .string "which live should not henceforth\l"
    .string "live unto themselves, but unto him\l"
    .string "which died for them, and rose again$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_16::
    .string "Wherefore henceforth know we no man\n"
    .string "after the flesh: yea, though we have\l"
    .string "known Christ after the flesh, yet\l"
    .string "now henceforth know we him no more.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_17::
    .string "Therefore if any man be in Christ,\n"
    .string "he is a new creature: old things are\l"
    .string "passed away; behold, all things are\l"
    .string "become new.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_18::
    .string "And all things are of God, who hath\n"
    .string "reconciled us to himself by Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, and hath given to us the\l"
    .string "ministry of reconciliation;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_19::
    .string "To wit, that God was in Christ,\n"
    .string "reconciling the world unto\l"
    .string "himself, not imputing their\l"
    .string "trespasses unto them; and hath\l"
    .string "committed unto us the word of\l"
    .string "reconciliation$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_20::
    .string "Now then we are ambassadors for\n"
    .string "Christ, as though God did beseech you\l"
    .string "by us: we pray you in Christ’s stead,\l"
    .string "be ye reconciled to God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_5_21::
    .string "For he hath made him to be sin for\n"
    .string "us, who knew no sin; that we might be\l"
    .string "made the righteousness of God in him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_1::
    .string "We then, as workers together with\n"
    .string "him, beseech you also that ye\l"
    .string "receive not the grace of God in vain.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_2::
    .string "(For he saith, I have heard thee in a\n"
    .string "time accepted, and in the day of\l"
    .string "salvation have I succoured thee:\l"
    .string "behold, now is the accepted time;\l"
    .string "behold, now is the day of\l"
    .string "salvation.)"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_3::
    .string "Giving no offence in any thing, that\n"
    .string "the ministry be not blamed:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_4::
    .string "But in all things approving\n"
    .string "ourselves as the ministers of God,\l"
    .string "in much patience, in afflictions,\l"
    .string "in necessities, in distresses,"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_5::
    .string "In stripes, in imprisonments, in\n"
    .string "tumults, in labours, in watchings,\l"
    .string "in fastings;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_6::
    .string "By pureness, by knowledge, by\n"
    .string "longsuffering, by kindness, by the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost, by love unfeigned,"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_7::
    .string "By the word of truth, by the power\n"
    .string "of God, by the armour of\l"
    .string "righteousness on the right hand and\l"
    .string "on the left,"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_8::
    .string "By honour and dishonour, by evil\n"
    .string "report and good report: as\l"
    .string "deceivers, and yet true;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_9::
    .string "As unknown, and yet well known; as\n"
    .string "dying, and, behold, we live; as\l"
    .string "chastened, and not killed;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_10::
    .string "As sorrowful, yet alway rejoicing;\n"
    .string "as poor, yet making many rich; as\l"
    .string "having nothing, and yet possessing\l"
    .string "all things$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_11::
    .string "O ye Corinthians, our mouth is open\n"
    .string "unto you, our heart is enlarged.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_12::
    .string "Ye are not straitened in us, but ye\n"
    .string "are straitened in your own bowels.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_13::
    .string "Now for a recompence in the same, (I\n"
    .string "speak as unto my children,) be ye\l"
    .string "also enlarged.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_14::
    .string "Be ye not unequally yoked together\n"
    .string "with unbelievers: for what\l"
    .string "fellowship hath righteousness with\l"
    .string "unrighteousness? and what communion\l"
    .string "hath light with darkness?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_15::
    .string "And what concord hath Christ with\n"
    .string "Belial? or what part hath he that\l"
    .string "believeth with an infidel?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_16::
    .string "And what agreement hath the temple\n"
    .string "of God with idols? for ye are the\l"
    .string "temple of the living God; as God\l"
    .string "hath said, I will dwell in them,\l"
    .string "and walk in them; and I will be\l"
    .string "their God, and they shall be my\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_17::
    .string "Wherefore come out from among them,\n"
    .string "and be ye separate, saith the Lord,\l"
    .string "and touch not the unclean thing; and\l"
    .string "I will receive you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_6_18::
    .string "And will be a Father unto you, and\n"
    .string "ye shall be my sons and daughters,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_1::
    .string "Having therefore these promises,\n"
    .string "dearly beloved, let us cleanse\l"
    .string "ourselves from all filthiness of\l"
    .string "the flesh and spirit, perfecting\l"
    .string "holiness in the fear of God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_2::
    .string "Receive us; we have wronged no man,\n"
    .string "we have corrupted no man, we have\l"
    .string "defrauded no man.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_3::
    .string "I speak not this to condemn you: for\n"
    .string "I have said before, that ye are in our\l"
    .string "hearts to die and live with you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_4::
    .string "Great is my boldness of speech\n"
    .string "toward you, great is my glorying of\l"
    .string "you: I am filled with comfort, I am\l"
    .string "exceeding joyful in all our\l"
    .string "tribulation.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_5::
    .string "For, when we were come into\n"
    .string "Macedonia, our flesh had no rest,\l"
    .string "but we were troubled on every side;\l"
    .string "without were fightings, within were\l"
    .string "fears.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_6::
    .string "Nevertheless God, that comforteth\n"
    .string "those that are cast down, comforted\l"
    .string "us by the coming of Titus;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_7::
    .string "And not by his coming only, but by\n"
    .string "the consolation wherewith he was\l"
    .string "comforted in you, when he told us\l"
    .string "your earnest desire, your mourning,\l"
    .string "your fervent mind toward me; so that\l"
    .string "I rejoiced the more$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_8::
    .string "For though I made you sorry with a\n"
    .string "letter, I do not repent, though I did\l"
    .string "repent: for I perceive that the same\l"
    .string "epistle hath made you sorry, though\l"
    .string "it were but for a season.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_9::
    .string "Now I rejoice, not that ye were made\n"
    .string "sorry, but that ye sorrowed to\l"
    .string "repentance: for ye were made sorry\l"
    .string "after a godly manner, that ye might\l"
    .string "receive damage by us in nothing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_10::
    .string "For godly sorrow worketh\n"
    .string "repentance to salvation not to be\l"
    .string "repented of: but the sorrow of the\l"
    .string "world worketh death.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_11::
    .string "For behold this selfsame thing,\n"
    .string "that ye sorrowed after a godly sort,\l"
    .string "what carefulness it wrought in you,\l"
    .string "yea, what clearing of yourselves,\l"
    .string "yea, what indignation, yea, what\l"
    .string "fear, yea, what vehement desire, yea,\l"
    .string "what zeal, yea, what revenge! In\l"
    .string "all things ye have approved\l"
    .string "yourselves to be clear in this\l"
    .string "matter.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_12::
    .string "Wherefore, though I wrote unto you,\n"
    .string "I did it not for his cause that had\l"
    .string "done the wrong, nor for his cause\l"
    .string "that suffered wrong, but that our\l"
    .string "care for you in the sight of God\l"
    .string "might appear unto you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_13::
    .string "Therefore we were comforted in your\n"
    .string "comfort: yea, and exceedingly the\l"
    .string "more joyed we for the joy of Titus,\l"
    .string "because his spirit was refreshed by\l"
    .string "you all.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_14::
    .string "For if I have boasted any thing to\n"
    .string "him of you, I am not ashamed; but as\l"
    .string "we spake all things to you in\l"
    .string "truth, even so our boasting, which I\l"
    .string "made before Titus, is found a truth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_15::
    .string "And his inward affection is more\n"
    .string "abundant toward you, whilst he\l"
    .string "remembereth the obedience of you\l"
    .string "all, how with fear and trembling ye\l"
    .string "received him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_7_16::
    .string "I rejoice therefore that I have\n"
    .string "confidence in you in all things.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_1::
    .string "Moreover, brethren, we do you to wit\n"
    .string "of the grace of God bestowed on the\l"
    .string "churches of Macedonia;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_2::
    .string "How that in a great trial of\n"
    .string "affliction the abundance of their\l"
    .string "joy and their deep poverty abounded\l"
    .string "unto the riches of their liberality$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_3::
    .string "For to their power, I bear record,\n"
    .string "yea, and beyond their power they\l"
    .string "were willing of themselves;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_4::
    .string "Praying us with much intreaty that\n"
    .string "we would receive the gift, and take\l"
    .string "upon us the fellowship of the\l"
    .string "ministering to the saints$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_5::
    .string "And this they did, not as we hoped,\n"
    .string "but first gave their own selves to\l"
    .string "the Lord, and unto us by the will of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_6::
    .string "Insomuch that we desired Titus, that\n"
    .string "as he had begun, so he would also\l"
    .string "finish in you the same grace also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_7::
    .string "Therefore, as ye abound in every\n"
    .string "thing, in faith, and utterance, and\l"
    .string "knowledge, and in all diligence,\l"
    .string "and in your love to us, see that ye\l"
    .string "abound in this grace also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_8::
    .string "I speak not by commandment, but by\n"
    .string "occasion of the forwardness of\l"
    .string "others, and to prove the sincerity\l"
    .string "of your love.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_9::
    .string "For ye know the grace of our Lord\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ, that, though he was\l"
    .string "rich, yet for your sakes he became\l"
    .string "poor, that ye through his poverty\l"
    .string "might be rich.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_10::
    .string "And herein I give my advice: for\n"
    .string "this is expedient for you, who have\l"
    .string "begun before, not only to do, but\l"
    .string "also to be forward a year ago.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_11::
    .string "Now therefore perform the doing of\n"
    .string "it; that as there was a readiness to\l"
    .string "will, so there may be a performance\l"
    .string "also out of that which ye have.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_12::
    .string "For if there be first a willing\n"
    .string "mind, it is accepted according to\l"
    .string "that a man hath, and not according to\l"
    .string "that he hath not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_13::
    .string "For I mean not that other men be\n"
    .string "eased, and ye burdened:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_14::
    .string "But by an equality, that now at this\n"
    .string "time your abundance may be a supply\l"
    .string "for their want, that their abundance\l"
    .string "also may be a supply for your want:\l"
    .string "that there may be equality:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_15::
    .string "As it is written, He that had\n"
    .string "gathered much had nothing over; and\l"
    .string "he that had gathered little had no\l"
    .string "lack$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_16::
    .string "But thanks be to God, which put the\n"
    .string "same earnest care into the heart of\l"
    .string "Titus for you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_17::
    .string "For indeed he accepted the\n"
    .string "exhortation; but being more forward,\l"
    .string "of his own accord he went unto you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_18::
    .string "And we have sent with him the\n"
    .string "brother, whose praise is in the\l"
    .string "gospel throughout all the\l"
    .string "churches;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_19::
    .string "And not that only, but who was also\n"
    .string "chosen of the churches to travel\l"
    .string "with us with this grace, which is\l"
    .string "administered by us to the glory of\l"
    .string "the same Lord, and declaration of\l"
    .string "your ready mind:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_20::
    .string "Avoiding this, that no man should\n"
    .string "blame us in this abundance which is\l"
    .string "administered by us:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_21::
    .string "Providing for honest things, not\n"
    .string "only in the sight of the Lord, but\l"
    .string "also in the sight of men$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_22::
    .string "And we have sent with them our\n"
    .string "brother, whom we have oftentimes\l"
    .string "proved diligent in many things, but\l"
    .string "now much more diligent, upon the\l"
    .string "great confidence which I have in you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_23::
    .string "Whether any do enquire of Titus, he\n"
    .string "is my partner and fellowhelper\l"
    .string "concerning you: or our brethren be\l"
    .string "enquired of, they are the messengers\l"
    .string "of the churches, and the glory of\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_8_24::
    .string "Wherefore shew ye to them, and\n"
    .string "before the churches, the proof of\l"
    .string "your love, and of our boasting on\l"
    .string "your behalf.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_1::
    .string "For as touching the ministering to\n"
    .string "the saints, it is superfluous for me\l"
    .string "to write to you:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_2::
    .string "For I know the forwardness of your\n"
    .string "mind, for which I boast of you to them\l"
    .string "of Macedonia, that Achaia was ready a\l"
    .string "year ago; and your zeal hath\l"
    .string "provoked very many$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_3::
    .string "Yet have I sent the brethren, lest\n"
    .string "our boasting of you should be in\l"
    .string "vain in this behalf; that, as I said,\l"
    .string "ye may be ready:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_4::
    .string "Lest haply if they of Macedonia\n"
    .string "come with me, and find you\l"
    .string "unprepared, we (that we say not, ye)\l"
    .string "should be ashamed in this same\l"
    .string "confident boasting$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_5::
    .string "Therefore I thought it necessary to\n"
    .string "exhort the brethren, that they would\l"
    .string "go before unto you, and make up\l"
    .string "beforehand your bounty, whereof ye\l"
    .string "had notice before, that the same\l"
    .string "might be ready, as a matter of\l"
    .string "bounty, and not as of covetousness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_6::
    .string "But this I say, He which soweth\n"
    .string "sparingly shall reap also\l"
    .string "sparingly; and he which soweth\l"
    .string "bountifully shall reap also\l"
    .string "bountifully.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_7::
    .string "Every man according as he\n"
    .string "purposeth in his heart, so let him\l"
    .string "give; not grudgingly, or of\l"
    .string "necessity: for God loveth a\l"
    .string "cheerful giver.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_8::
    .string "And God is able to make all grace\n"
    .string "abound toward you; that ye, always\l"
    .string "having all sufficiency in all\l"
    .string "things, may abound to every good\l"
    .string "work:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_9::
    .string "(As it is written, He hath\n"
    .string "dispersed abroad; he hath given to\l"
    .string "the poor: his righteousness\l"
    .string "remaineth for ever$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_10::
    .string "Now he that ministereth seed to the\n"
    .string "sower both minister bread for your\l"
    .string "food, and multiply your seed sown,\l"
    .string "and increase the fruits of your\l"
    .string "righteousness;)"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_11::
    .string "Being enriched in every thing to\n"
    .string "all bountifulness, which causeth\l"
    .string "through us thanksgiving to God$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_12::
    .string "For the administration of this\n"
    .string "service not only supplieth the\l"
    .string "want of the saints, but is abundant\l"
    .string "also by many thanksgivings unto God;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_13::
    .string "Whiles by the experiment of this\n"
    .string "ministration they glorify God for\l"
    .string "your professed subjection unto the\l"
    .string "gospel of Christ, and for your\l"
    .string "liberal distribution unto them, and\l"
    .string "unto all men;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_14::
    .string "And by their prayer for you, which\n"
    .string "long after you for the exceeding\l"
    .string "grace of God in you$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_9_15::
    .string "Thanks be unto God for his\n"
    .string "unspeakable gift.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_1::
    .string "Now I Paul myself beseech you by\n"
    .string "the meekness and gentleness of\l"
    .string "Christ, who in presence am base\l"
    .string "among you, but being absent am bold\l"
    .string "toward you:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_2::
    .string "But I beseech you, that I may not be\n"
    .string "bold when I am present with that\l"
    .string "confidence, wherewith I think to be\l"
    .string "bold against some, which think of us\l"
    .string "as if we walked according to the\l"
    .string "flesh$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_3::
    .string "For though we walk in the flesh, we\n"
    .string "do not war after the flesh:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_4::
    .string "(For the weapons of our warfare are\n"
    .string "not carnal, but mighty through God\l"
    .string "to the pulling down of strong\l"
    .string "holds;)"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_5::
    .string "Casting down imaginations, and\n"
    .string "every high thing that exalteth\l"
    .string "itself against the knowledge of\l"
    .string "God, and bringing into captivity\l"
    .string "every thought to the obedience of\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_6::
    .string "And having in a readiness to revenge\n"
    .string "all disobedience, when your\l"
    .string "obedience is fulfilled$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_7::
    .string "Do ye look on things after the\n"
    .string "outward appearance? If any man\l"
    .string "trust to himself that he is\l"
    .string "Christ’s, let him of himself think\l"
    .string "this again, that, as he is Christ’s,\l"
    .string "even so are we Christ’s.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_8::
    .string "For though I should boast somewhat\n"
    .string "more of our authority, which the Lord\l"
    .string "hath given us for edification, and\l"
    .string "not for your destruction, I should\l"
    .string "not be ashamed:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_9::
    .string "That I may not seem as if I would\n"
    .string "terrify you by letters$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_10::
    .string "For his letters, say they, are\n"
    .string "weighty and powerful; but his\l"
    .string "bodily presence is weak, and his\l"
    .string "speech contemptible.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_11::
    .string "Let such an one think this, that,\n"
    .string "such as we are in word by letters\l"
    .string "when we are absent, such will we be\l"
    .string "also in deed when we are present.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_12::
    .string "For we dare not make ourselves of\n"
    .string "the number, or compare ourselves\l"
    .string "with some that commend themselves:\l"
    .string "but they measuring themselves by\l"
    .string "themselves, and comparing\l"
    .string "themselves among themselves, are\l"
    .string "not wise.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_13::
    .string "But we will not boast of things\n"
    .string "without our measure, but according to\l"
    .string "the measure of the rule which God\l"
    .string "hath distributed to us, a measure to\l"
    .string "reach even unto you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_14::
    .string "For we stretch not ourselves beyond\n"
    .string "our measure, as though we reached not\l"
    .string "unto you: for we are come as far as to\l"
    .string "you also in preaching the gospel\l"
    .string "of Christ:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_15::
    .string "Not boasting of things without our\n"
    .string "measure, that is, of other men’s\l"
    .string "labours; but having hope, when your\l"
    .string "faith is increased, that we shall be\l"
    .string "enlarged by you according to our\l"
    .string "rule abundantly,"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_16::
    .string "To preach the gospel in the\n"
    .string "regions beyond you, and not to boast\l"
    .string "in another man’s line of things made\l"
    .string "ready to our hand$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_17::
    .string "But he that glorieth, let him\n"
    .string "glory in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_10_18::
    .string "For not he that commendeth himself\n"
    .string "is approved, but whom the Lord\l"
    .string "commendeth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_1::
    .string "Would to God ye could bear with me\n"
    .string "a little in my folly: and indeed\l"
    .string "bear with me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_2::
    .string "For I am jealous over you with\n"
    .string "godly jealousy: for I have espoused\l"
    .string "you to one husband, that I may\l"
    .string "present you as a chaste virgin to\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_3::
    .string "But I fear, lest by any means, as\n"
    .string "the serpent beguiled Eve through\l"
    .string "his subtilty, so your minds should\l"
    .string "be corrupted from the simplicity\l"
    .string "that is in Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_4::
    .string "For if he that cometh preacheth\n"
    .string "another Jesus, whom we have not\l"
    .string "preached, or if ye receive another\l"
    .string "spirit, which ye have not received,\l"
    .string "or another gospel, which ye have not\l"
    .string "accepted, ye might well bear with\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_5::
    .string "For I suppose I was not a whit\n"
    .string "behind the very chiefest apostles.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_6::
    .string "But though I be rude in speech, yet\n"
    .string "not in knowledge; but we have been\l"
    .string "throughly made manifest among you in\l"
    .string "all things.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_7::
    .string "Have I committed an offence in\n"
    .string "abasing myself that ye might be\l"
    .string "exalted, because I have preached to\l"
    .string "you the gospel of God freely?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_8::
    .string "I robbed other churches, taking\n"
    .string "wages of them, to do you service$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_9::
    .string "And when I was present with you, and\n"
    .string "wanted, I was chargeable to no man:\l"
    .string "for that which was lacking to me the\l"
    .string "brethren which came from Macedonia\l"
    .string "supplied: and in all things I have\l"
    .string "kept myself from being burdensome\l"
    .string "unto you, and so will I keep\l"
    .string "myself.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_10::
    .string "As the truth of Christ is in me, no\n"
    .string "man shall stop me of this boasting\l"
    .string "in the regions of Achaia.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_11::
    .string "Wherefore? because I love you not?\n"
    .string "God knoweth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_12::
    .string "But what I do, that I will do, that\n"
    .string "I may cut off occasion from them\l"
    .string "which desire occasion; that wherein\l"
    .string "they glory, they may be found even as\l"
    .string "we.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_13::
    .string "For such are false apostles,\n"
    .string "deceitful workers, transforming\l"
    .string "themselves into the apostles of\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_14::
    .string "And no marvel; for Satan himself is\n"
    .string "transformed into an angel of light.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_15::
    .string "Therefore it is no great thing if\n"
    .string "his ministers also be transformed as\l"
    .string "the ministers of righteousness;\l"
    .string "whose end shall be according to\l"
    .string "their works.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_16::
    .string "I say again, Let no man think me a\n"
    .string "fool; if otherwise, yet as a fool\l"
    .string "receive me, that I may boast myself a\l"
    .string "little.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_17::
    .string "That which I speak, I speak it not\n"
    .string "after the Lord, but as it were\l"
    .string "foolishly, in this confidence of\l"
    .string "boasting.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_18::
    .string "Seeing that many glory after the\n"
    .string "flesh, I will glory also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_19::
    .string "For ye suffer fools gladly, seeing\n"
    .string "ye yourselves are wise.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_20::
    .string "For ye suffer, if a man bring you\n"
    .string "into bondage, if a man devour you, if\l"
    .string "a man take of you, if a man exalt\l"
    .string "himself, if a man smite you on the\l"
    .string "face.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_21::
    .string "I speak as concerning reproach, as\n"
    .string "though we had been weak. Howbeit\l"
    .string "whereinsoever any is bold, (I speak\l"
    .string "foolishly,) I am bold also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_22::
    .string "Are they Hebrews? so am I. Are they\n"
    .string "Israelites? so am I. Are they the\l"
    .string "seed of Abraham? so am I.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_23::
    .string "Are they ministers of Christ? (I\n"
    .string "speak as a fool) I am more; in\l"
    .string "labours more abundant, in stripes\l"
    .string "above measure, in prisons more\l"
    .string "frequent, in deaths oft.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_24::
    .string "Of the Jews five times received I\n"
    .string "forty stripes save one.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_25::
    .string "Thrice was I beaten with rods, once\n"
    .string "was I stoned, thrice I suffered\l"
    .string "shipwreck, a night and a day I have\l"
    .string "been in the deep;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_26::
    .string "In journeyings often, in perils of\n"
    .string "waters, in perils of robbers, in\l"
    .string "perils by mine own countrymen, in\l"
    .string "perils by the heathen, in perils in\l"
    .string "the city, in perils in the\l"
    .string "wilderness, in perils in the sea,\l"
    .string "in perils among false brethren;"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_27::
    .string "In weariness and painfulness, in\n"
    .string "watchings often, in hunger and\l"
    .string "thirst, in fastings often, in cold\l"
    .string "and nakedness$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_28::
    .string "Beside those things that are\n"
    .string "without, that which cometh upon me\l"
    .string "daily, the care of all the churches.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_29::
    .string "Who is weak, and I am not weak? who\n"
    .string "is offended, and I burn not?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_30::
    .string "If I must needs glory, I will\n"
    .string "glory of the things which concern\l"
    .string "mine infirmities$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_31::
    .string "The God and Father of our Lord Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ, which is blessed for\l"
    .string "evermore, knoweth that I lie not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_32::
    .string "In Damascus the governor under\n"
    .string "Aretas the king kept the city of the\l"
    .string "Damascenes with a garrison, desirous\l"
    .string "to apprehend me:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_11_33::
    .string "And through a window in a basket was\n"
    .string "I let down by the wall, and escaped\l"
    .string "his hands$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_1::
    .string "It is not expedient for me\n"
    .string "doubtless to glory. I will come to\l"
    .string "visions and revelations of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_2::
    .string "I knew a man in Christ above\n"
    .string "fourteen years ago, (whether in the\l"
    .string "body, I cannot tell; or whether out\l"
    .string "of the body, I cannot tell: God\l"
    .string "knoweth;) such an one caught up to\l"
    .string "the third heaven.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_3::
    .string "And I knew such a man, (whether in\n"
    .string "the body, or out of the body, I cannot\l"
    .string "tell: God knoweth;)"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_4::
    .string "How that he was caught up into\n"
    .string "paradise, and heard unspeakable\l"
    .string "words, which it is not lawful for a\l"
    .string "man to utter$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_5::
    .string "Of such an one will I glory: yet of\n"
    .string "myself I will not glory, but in\l"
    .string "mine infirmities.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_6::
    .string "For though I would desire to glory,\n"
    .string "I shall not be a fool; for I will\l"
    .string "say the truth: but now I forbear,\l"
    .string "lest any man should think of me\l"
    .string "above that which he seeth me to be, or\l"
    .string "that he heareth of me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_7::
    .string "And lest I should be exalted above\n"
    .string "measure through the abundance of the\l"
    .string "revelations, there was given to me a\l"
    .string "thorn in the flesh, the messenger of\l"
    .string "Satan to buffet me, lest I should be\l"
    .string "exalted above measure.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_8::
    .string "For this thing I besought the Lord\n"
    .string "thrice, that it might depart from me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_9::
    .string "And he said unto me, My grace is\n"
    .string "sufficient for thee: for my strength\l"
    .string "is made perfect in weakness. Most\l"
    .string "gladly therefore will I rather\l"
    .string "glory in my infirmities, that the\l"
    .string "power of Christ may rest upon me.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_10::
    .string "Therefore I take pleasure in\n"
    .string "infirmities, in reproaches, in\l"
    .string "necessities, in persecutions, in\l"
    .string "distresses for Christ’s sake: for\l"
    .string "when I am weak, then am I strong.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_11::
    .string "I am become a fool in glorying; ye\n"
    .string "have compelled me: for I ought to\l"
    .string "have been commended of you: for in\l"
    .string "nothing am I behind the very chiefest\l"
    .string "apostles, though I be nothing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_12::
    .string "Truly the signs of an apostle were\n"
    .string "wrought among you in all patience,\l"
    .string "in signs, and wonders, and mighty\l"
    .string "deeds.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_13::
    .string "For what is it wherein ye were\n"
    .string "inferior to other churches, except\l"
    .string "it be that I myself was not\l"
    .string "burdensome to you? forgive me this\l"
    .string "wrong.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_14::
    .string "Behold, the third time I am ready to\n"
    .string "come to you; and I will not be\l"
    .string "burdensome to you: for I seek not\l"
    .string "yours but you: for the children\l"
    .string "ought not to lay up for the\l"
    .string "parents, but the parents for the\l"
    .string "children.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_15::
    .string "And I will very gladly spend and\n"
    .string "be spent for you; though the more\l"
    .string "abundantly I love you, the less I\l"
    .string "be loved.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_16::
    .string "But be it so, I did not burden you:\n"
    .string "nevertheless, being crafty, I caught\l"
    .string "you with guile.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_17::
    .string "Did I make a gain of you by any of\n"
    .string "them whom I sent unto you?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_18::
    .string "I desired Titus, and with him I sent\n"
    .string "a brother. Did Titus make a gain of\l"
    .string "you? walked we not in the same\l"
    .string "spirit? walked we not in the same\l"
    .string "steps?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_19::
    .string "Again, think ye that we excuse\n"
    .string "ourselves unto you? we speak before\l"
    .string "God in Christ: but we do all things,\l"
    .string "dearly beloved, for your edifying$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_20::
    .string "For I fear, lest, when I come, I\n"
    .string "shall not find you such as I would,\l"
    .string "and that I shall be found unto you\l"
    .string "such as ye would not: lest there be\l"
    .string "debates, envyings, wraths, strifes,\l"
    .string "backbitings, whisperings,\l"
    .string "swellings, tumults:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_12_21::
    .string "And lest, when I come again, my God\n"
    .string "will humble me among you, and that\l"
    .string "I shall bewail many which have\l"
    .string "sinned already, and have not\l"
    .string "repented of the uncleanness and\l"
    .string "fornication and lasciviousness\l"
    .string "which they have committed$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_1::
    .string "This is the third time I am coming\n"
    .string "to you. In the mouth of two or three\l"
    .string "witnesses shall every word be\l"
    .string "established.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_2::
    .string "I told you before, and foretell\n"
    .string "you, as if I were present, the second\l"
    .string "time; and being absent now I write to\l"
    .string "them which heretofore have sinned,\l"
    .string "and to all other, that, if I come\l"
    .string "again, I will not spare:"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_3::
    .string "Since ye seek a proof of Christ\n"
    .string "speaking in me, which to you-ward is\l"
    .string "not weak, but is mighty in you$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_4::
    .string "For though he was crucified through\n"
    .string "weakness, yet he liveth by the power\l"
    .string "of God. For we also are weak in him,\l"
    .string "but we shall live with him by the\l"
    .string "power of God toward you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_5::
    .string "Examine yourselves, whether ye be\n"
    .string "in the faith; prove your own selves.\l"
    .string "Know ye not your own selves, how that\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ is in you, except ye be\l"
    .string "reprobates?"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_6::
    .string "But I trust that ye shall know that\n"
    .string "we are not reprobates$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_7::
    .string "Now I pray to God that ye do no\n"
    .string "evil; not that we should appear\l"
    .string "approved, but that ye should do\l"
    .string "that which is honest, though we be as\l"
    .string "reprobates.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_8::
    .string "For we can do nothing against the\n"
    .string "truth, but for the truth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_9::
    .string "For we are glad, when we are weak,\n"
    .string "and ye are strong: and this also we\l"
    .string "wish, even your perfection.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_10::
    .string "Therefore I write these things\n"
    .string "being absent, lest being present I\l"
    .string "should use sharpness, according to\l"
    .string "the power which the Lord hath given\l"
    .string "me to edification, and not to\l"
    .string "destruction.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_11::
    .string "Finally, brethren, farewell. Be\n"
    .string "perfect, be of good comfort, be of\l"
    .string "one mind, live in peace; and the God\l"
    .string "of love and peace shall be with\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_12::
    .string "Greet one another with an holy kiss.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_13::
    .string "All the saints salute you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Corinthians_13_14::
    .string "The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "and the love of God, and the\l"
    .string "communion of the Holy Ghost, be with\l"
    .string "you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle, (not of men,\n"
    .string "neither by man, but by Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "and God the Father, who raised him\l"
    .string "from the dead;)"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_2::
    .string "And all the brethren which are\n"
    .string "with me, unto the churches of\l"
    .string "Galatia:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_3::
    .string "Grace be to you and peace from God\n"
    .string "the Father, and from our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_4::
    .string "Who gave himself for our sins, that\n"
    .string "he might deliver us from this\l"
    .string "present evil world, according to\l"
    .string "the will of God and our Father:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_5::
    .string "To whom be glory for ever and ever.\n"
    .string "Amen$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_6::
    .string "I marvel that ye are so soon\n"
    .string "removed from him that called you\l"
    .string "into the grace of Christ unto another\l"
    .string "gospel:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_7::
    .string "Which is not another; but there be\n"
    .string "some that trouble you, and would\l"
    .string "pervert the gospel of Christ$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_8::
    .string "But though we, or an angel from\n"
    .string "heaven, preach any other gospel\l"
    .string "unto you than that which we have\l"
    .string "preached unto you, let him be\l"
    .string "accursed.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_9::
    .string "As we said before, so say I now\n"
    .string "again, if any man preach any other\l"
    .string "gospel unto you than that ye have\l"
    .string "received, let him be accursed.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_10::
    .string "For do I now persuade men, or God?\n"
    .string "or do I seek to please men? for if I\l"
    .string "yet pleased men, I should not be\l"
    .string "the servant of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_11::
    .string "But I certify you, brethren, that\n"
    .string "the gospel which was preached of me\l"
    .string "is not after man.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_12::
    .string "For I neither received it of man,\n"
    .string "neither was I taught it, but by the\l"
    .string "revelation of Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_13::
    .string "For ye have heard of my conversation\n"
    .string "in time past in the Jews’ religion,\l"
    .string "how that beyond measure I persecuted\l"
    .string "the church of God, and wasted it:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_14::
    .string "And profited in the Jews’ religion\n"
    .string "above many my equals in mine own\l"
    .string "nation, being more exceedingly\l"
    .string "zealous of the traditions of my\l"
    .string "fathers$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_15::
    .string "But when it pleased God, who\n"
    .string "separated me from my mother’s womb,\l"
    .string "and called me by his grace,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_16::
    .string "To reveal his Son in me, that I\n"
    .string "might preach him among the heathen;\l"
    .string "immediately I conferred not with\l"
    .string "flesh and blood:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_17::
    .string "Neither went I up to Jerusalem to\n"
    .string "them which were apostles before me;\l"
    .string "but I went into Arabia, and returned\l"
    .string "again unto Damascus$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_18::
    .string "Then after three years I went up to\n"
    .string "Jerusalem to see Peter, and abode\l"
    .string "with him fifteen days.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_19::
    .string "But other of the apostles saw I\n"
    .string "none, save James the Lord’s brother.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_20::
    .string "Now the things which I write unto\n"
    .string "you, behold, before God, I lie not.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_21::
    .string "Afterwards I came into the regions\n"
    .string "of Syria and Cilicia;"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_22::
    .string "And was unknown by face unto the\n"
    .string "churches of Judaea which were in\l"
    .string "Christ:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_23::
    .string "But they had heard only, That he\n"
    .string "which persecuted us in times past\l"
    .string "now preacheth the faith which once\l"
    .string "he destroyed$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_1_24::
    .string "And they glorified God in me.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_1::
    .string "Then fourteen years after I went up\n"
    .string "again to Jerusalem with Barnabas,\l"
    .string "and took Titus with me also.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_2::
    .string "And I went up by revelation, and\n"
    .string "communicated unto them that gospel\l"
    .string "which I preach among the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "but privately to them which were of\l"
    .string "reputation, lest by any means I\l"
    .string "should run, or had run, in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_3::
    .string "But neither Titus, who was with me,\n"
    .string "being a Greek, was compelled to be\l"
    .string "circumcised:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_4::
    .string "And that because of false brethren\n"
    .string "unawares brought in, who came in\l"
    .string "privily to spy out our liberty\l"
    .string "which we have in Christ Jesus, that\l"
    .string "they might bring us into bondage:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_5::
    .string "To whom we gave place by\n"
    .string "subjection, no, not for an hour; that\l"
    .string "the truth of the gospel might\l"
    .string "continue with you$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_6::
    .string "But of these who seemed to be\n"
    .string "somewhat, (whatsoever they were, it\l"
    .string "maketh no matter to me: God\l"
    .string "accepteth no man’s person:) for\l"
    .string "they who seemed to be somewhat in\l"
    .string "conference added nothing to me:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_7::
    .string "But contrariwise, when they saw that\n"
    .string "the gospel of the uncircumcision\l"
    .string "was committed unto me, as the gospel\l"
    .string "of the circumcision was unto Peter;"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_8::
    .string "(For he that wrought effectually\n"
    .string "in Peter to the apostleship of the\l"
    .string "circumcision, the same was mighty in\l"
    .string "me toward the Gentiles:)"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_9::
    .string "And when James, Cephas, and John,\n"
    .string "who seemed to be pillars,\l"
    .string "perceived the grace that was given\l"
    .string "unto me, they gave to me and Barnabas\l"
    .string "the right hands of fellowship; that\l"
    .string "we should go unto the heathen, and\l"
    .string "they unto the circumcision$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_10::
    .string "Only they would that we should\n"
    .string "remember the poor; the same which I\l"
    .string "also was forward to do.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_11::
    .string "But when Peter was come to Antioch,\n"
    .string "I withstood him to the face, because\l"
    .string "he was to be blamed.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_12::
    .string "For before that certain came from\n"
    .string "James, he did eat with the Gentiles:\l"
    .string "but when they were come, he withdrew\l"
    .string "and separated himself, fearing them\l"
    .string "which were of the circumcision.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_13::
    .string "And the other Jews dissembled\n"
    .string "likewise with him; insomuch that\l"
    .string "Barnabas also was carried away with\l"
    .string "their dissimulation.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_14::
    .string "But when I saw that they walked not\n"
    .string "uprightly according to the truth of\l"
    .string "the gospel, I said unto Peter before\l"
    .string "them all, If thou, being a Jew,\l"
    .string "livest after the manner of Gentiles,\l"
    .string "and not as do the Jews, why\l"
    .string "compellest thou the Gentiles to\l"
    .string "live as do the Jews?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_15::
    .string "We who are Jews by nature, and not\n"
    .string "sinners of the Gentiles,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_16::
    .string "Knowing that a man is not justified\n"
    .string "by the works of the law, but by the\l"
    .string "faith of Jesus Christ, even we have\l"
    .string "believed in Jesus Christ, that we\l"
    .string "might be justified by the faith of\l"
    .string "Christ, and not by the works of the\l"
    .string "law: for by the works of the law\l"
    .string "shall no flesh be justified$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_17::
    .string "But if, while we seek to be\n"
    .string "justified by Christ, we ourselves\l"
    .string "also are found sinners, is therefore\l"
    .string "Christ the minister of sin? God\l"
    .string "forbid.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_18::
    .string "For if I build again the things\n"
    .string "which I destroyed, I make myself a\l"
    .string "transgressor.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_19::
    .string "For I through the law am dead to the\n"
    .string "law, that I might live unto God.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_20::
    .string "I am crucified with Christ:\n"
    .string "neverthless I live; yet not I, but\l"
    .string "Christ liveth in me: and the life\l"
    .string "which I now live in the flesh I\l"
    .string "live by the faith of the Son of God,\l"
    .string "who loved me, and gave himself for\l"
    .string "me.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_2_21::
    .string "I do not frustrate the grace of God:\n"
    .string "for if righteousness come by the\l"
    .string "law, then Christ is dead in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_1::
    .string "O foolish Galatians, who hath\n"
    .string "bewitched you, that ye should not\l"
    .string "obey the truth, before whose eyes\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ hath been evidently set\l"
    .string "forth, crucified among you?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_2::
    .string "This only would I learn of you,\n"
    .string "Received ye the Spirit by the works\l"
    .string "of the law, or by the hearing of\l"
    .string "faith?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_3::
    .string "Are ye so foolish? having begun in\n"
    .string "the Spirit, are ye now made perfect\l"
    .string "by the flesh?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_4::
    .string "Have ye suffered so many things in\n"
    .string "vain? if it be yet in vain$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_5::
    .string "He therefore that ministereth to\n"
    .string "you the Spirit, and worketh\l"
    .string "miracles among you, doeth he it by\l"
    .string "the works of the law, or by the\l"
    .string "hearing of faith?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_6::
    .string "Even as Abraham believed God, and\n"
    .string "it was accounted to him for\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_7::
    .string "Know ye therefore that they which\n"
    .string "are of faith, the same are the\l"
    .string "children of Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_8::
    .string "And the scripture, foreseeing that\n"
    .string "God would justify the heathen\l"
    .string "through faith, preached before the\l"
    .string "gospel unto Abraham, saying, In\l"
    .string "thee shall all nations be blessed.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_9::
    .string "So then they which be of faith are\n"
    .string "blessed with faithful Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_10::
    .string "For as many as are of the works of\n"
    .string "the law are under the curse: for it\l"
    .string "is written, Cursed is every one that\l"
    .string "continueth not in all things which\l"
    .string "are written in the book of the law to\l"
    .string "do them.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_11::
    .string "But that no man is justified by the\n"
    .string "law in the sight of God, it is\l"
    .string "evident: for, The just shall live\l"
    .string "by faith.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_12::
    .string "And the law is not of faith: but,\n"
    .string "The man that doeth them shall live\l"
    .string "in them.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_13::
    .string "Christ hath redeemed us from the\n"
    .string "curse of the law, being made a curse\l"
    .string "for us: for it is written, Cursed is\l"
    .string "every one that hangeth on a tree:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_14::
    .string "That the blessing of Abraham might\n"
    .string "come on the Gentiles through Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ; that we might receive the\l"
    .string "promise of the Spirit through faith$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_15::
    .string "Brethren, I speak after the manner\n"
    .string "of men; Though it be but a man’s\l"
    .string "covenant, yet if it be confirmed, no\l"
    .string "man disannulleth, or addeth thereto.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_16::
    .string "Now to Abraham and his seed were the\n"
    .string "promises made. He saith not, And to\l"
    .string "seeds, as of many; but as of one, And\l"
    .string "to thy seed, which is Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_17::
    .string "And this I say, that the covenant,\n"
    .string "that was confirmed before of God in\l"
    .string "Christ, the law, which was four\l"
    .string "hundred and thirty years after,\l"
    .string "cannot disannul, that it should\l"
    .string "make the promise of none effect.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_18::
    .string "For if the inheritance be of the\n"
    .string "law, it is no more of promise: but\l"
    .string "God gave it to Abraham by promise.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_19::
    .string "Wherefore then serveth the law? It\n"
    .string "was added because of transgressions,\l"
    .string "till the seed should come to whom\l"
    .string "the promise was made; and it was\l"
    .string "ordained by angels in the hand of a\l"
    .string "mediator.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_20::
    .string "Now a mediator is not a mediator of\n"
    .string "one, but God is one.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_21::
    .string "Is the law then against the\n"
    .string "promises of God? God forbid: for if\l"
    .string "there had been a law given which\l"
    .string "could have given life, verily\l"
    .string "righteousness should have been by\l"
    .string "the law.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_22::
    .string "But the scripture hath concluded\n"
    .string "all under sin, that the promise by\l"
    .string "faith of Jesus Christ might be given\l"
    .string "to them that believe.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_23::
    .string "But before faith came, we were kept\n"
    .string "under the law, shut up unto the\l"
    .string "faith which should afterwards be\l"
    .string "revealed.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_24::
    .string "Wherefore the law was our\n"
    .string "schoolmaster to bring us unto\l"
    .string "Christ, that we might be justified by\l"
    .string "faith.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_25::
    .string "But after that faith is come, we are\n"
    .string "no longer under a schoolmaster.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_26::
    .string "For ye are all the children of God\n"
    .string "by faith in Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_27::
    .string "For as many of you as have been\n"
    .string "baptized into Christ have put on\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_28::
    .string "There is neither Jew nor Greek,\n"
    .string "there is neither bond nor free, there\l"
    .string "is neither male nor female: for ye\l"
    .string "are all one in Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_3_29::
    .string "And if ye be Christ’s, then are ye\n"
    .string "Abraham’s seed, and heirs according\l"
    .string "to the promise.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_1::
    .string "Now I say, That the heir, as long as\n"
    .string "he is a child, differeth nothing\l"
    .string "from a servant, though he be lord of\l"
    .string "all;"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_2::
    .string "But is under tutors and governors\n"
    .string "until the time appointed of the\l"
    .string "father$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_3::
    .string "Even so we, when we were children,\n"
    .string "were in bondage under the elements\l"
    .string "of the world:"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_4::
    .string "But when the fulness of the time\n"
    .string "was come, God sent forth his Son,\l"
    .string "made of a woman, made under the law,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_5::
    .string "To redeem them that were under the\n"
    .string "law, that we might receive the\l"
    .string "adoption of sons$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_6::
    .string "And because ye are sons, God hath\n"
    .string "sent forth the Spirit of his Son\l"
    .string "into your hearts, crying, Abba,\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_7::
    .string "Wherefore thou art no more a\n"
    .string "servant, but a son; and if a son, then\l"
    .string "an heir of God through Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_8::
    .string "Howbeit then, when ye knew not God,\n"
    .string "ye did service unto them which by\l"
    .string "nature are no gods.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_9::
    .string "But now, after that ye have known\n"
    .string "God, or rather are known of God, how\l"
    .string "turn ye again to the weak and\l"
    .string "beggarly elements, whereunto ye\l"
    .string "desire again to be in bondage?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_10::
    .string "Ye observe days, and months, and\n"
    .string "times, and years$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_11::
    .string "I am afraid of you, lest I have\n"
    .string "bestowed upon you labour in vain.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_12::
    .string "Brethren, I beseech you, be as I am;\n"
    .string "for I am as ye are: ye have not\l"
    .string "injured me at all.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_13::
    .string "Ye know how through infirmity of the\n"
    .string "flesh I preached the gospel unto\l"
    .string "you at the first.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_14::
    .string "And my temptation which was in my\n"
    .string "flesh ye despised not, nor\l"
    .string "rejected; but received me as an\l"
    .string "angel of God, even as Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_15::
    .string "Where is then the blessedness ye\n"
    .string "spake of? for I bear you record,\l"
    .string "that, if it had been possible, ye\l"
    .string "would have plucked out your own\l"
    .string "eyes, and have given them to me.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_16::
    .string "Am I therefore become your enemy,\n"
    .string "because I tell you the truth?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_17::
    .string "They zealously affect you, but not\n"
    .string "well; yea, they would exclude you,\l"
    .string "that ye might affect them$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_18::
    .string "But it is good to be zealously\n"
    .string "affected always in a good thing, and\l"
    .string "not only when I am present with you.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_19::
    .string "My little children, of whom I\n"
    .string "travail in birth again until Christ\l"
    .string "be formed in you,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_20::
    .string "I desire to be present with you now,\n"
    .string "and to change my voice; for I stand in\l"
    .string "doubt of you$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_21::
    .string "Tell me, ye that desire to be under\n"
    .string "the law, do ye not hear the law?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_22::
    .string "For it is written, that Abraham had\n"
    .string "two sons, the one by a bondmaid, the\l"
    .string "other by a freewoman$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_23::
    .string "But he who was of the bondwoman was\n"
    .string "born after the flesh; but he of the\l"
    .string "freewoman was by promise.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_24::
    .string "Which things are an allegory: for\n"
    .string "these are the two covenants; the one\l"
    .string "from the mount Sinai, which gendereth\l"
    .string "to bondage, which is Agar.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_25::
    .string "For this Agar is mount Sinai in\n"
    .string "Arabia, and answereth to Jerusalem\l"
    .string "which now is, and is in bondage with\l"
    .string "her children.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_26::
    .string "But Jerusalem which is above is\n"
    .string "free, which is the mother of us all.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_27::
    .string "For it is written, Rejoice, thou\n"
    .string "barren that bearest not; break forth\l"
    .string "and cry, thou that travailest not:\l"
    .string "for the desolate hath many more\l"
    .string "children than she which hath an\l"
    .string "husband.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_28::
    .string "Now we, brethren, as Isaac was, are\n"
    .string "the children of promise.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_29::
    .string "But as then he that was born after\n"
    .string "the flesh persecuted him that was\l"
    .string "born after the Spirit, even so it is\l"
    .string "now.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_30::
    .string "Nevertheless what saith the\n"
    .string "scripture? Cast out the bondwoman\l"
    .string "and her son: for the son of the\l"
    .string "bondwoman shall not be heir with\l"
    .string "the son of the freewoman.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_4_31::
    .string "So then, brethren, we are not\n"
    .string "children of the bondwoman, but of\l"
    .string "the free.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_1::
    .string "Stand fast therefore in the liberty\n"
    .string "wherewith Christ hath made us free,\l"
    .string "and be not entangled again with the\l"
    .string "yoke of bondage.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_2::
    .string "Behold, I Paul say unto you, that\n"
    .string "if ye be circumcised, Christ shall\l"
    .string "profit you nothing.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_3::
    .string "For I testify again to every man\n"
    .string "that is circumcised, that he is a\l"
    .string "debtor to do the whole law.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_4::
    .string "Christ is become of no effect unto\n"
    .string "you, whosoever of you are justified\l"
    .string "by the law; ye are fallen from\l"
    .string "grace.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_5::
    .string "For we through the Spirit wait for\n"
    .string "the hope of righteousness by faith.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_6::
    .string "For in Jesus Christ neither\n"
    .string "circumcision availeth any thing, nor\l"
    .string "uncircumcision; but faith which\l"
    .string "worketh by love.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_7::
    .string "Ye did run well; who did hinder you\n"
    .string "that ye should not obey the truth?"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_8::
    .string "This persuasion cometh not of him\n"
    .string "that calleth you$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_9::
    .string "A little leaven leaveneth the\n"
    .string "whole lump.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_10::
    .string "I have confidence in you through the\n"
    .string "Lord, that ye will be none otherwise\l"
    .string "minded: but he that troubleth you\l"
    .string "shall bear his judgment, whosoever\l"
    .string "he be.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_11::
    .string "And I, brethren, if I yet preach\n"
    .string "circumcision, why do I yet suffer\l"
    .string "persecution? then is the offence of\l"
    .string "the cross ceased.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_12::
    .string "I would they were even cut off\n"
    .string "which trouble you.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_13::
    .string "For, brethren, ye have been called\n"
    .string "unto liberty; only use not liberty\l"
    .string "for an occasion to the flesh, but by\l"
    .string "love serve one another.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_14::
    .string "For all the law is fulfilled in\n"
    .string "one word, even in this; Thou shalt\l"
    .string "love thy neighbour as thyself.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_15::
    .string "But if ye bite and devour one\n"
    .string "another, take heed that ye be not\l"
    .string "consumed one of another.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_16::
    .string "This I say then, Walk in the\n"
    .string "Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil\l"
    .string "the lust of the flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_17::
    .string "For the flesh lusteth against the\n"
    .string "Spirit, and the Spirit against the\l"
    .string "flesh: and these are contrary the\l"
    .string "one to the other: so that ye cannot do\l"
    .string "the things that ye would.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_18::
    .string "But if ye be led of the Spirit, ye\n"
    .string "are not under the law.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_19::
    .string "Now the works of the flesh are\n"
    .string "manifest, which are these; Adultery,\l"
    .string "fornication, uncleanness,\l"
    .string "lasciviousness,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_20::
    .string "Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred,\n"
    .string "variance, emulations, wrath, strife,\l"
    .string "seditions, heresies,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_21::
    .string "Envyings, murders, drunkenness,\n"
    .string "revellings, and such like: of the\l"
    .string "which I tell you before, as I have\l"
    .string "also told you in time past, that\l"
    .string "they which do such things shall not\l"
    .string "inherit the kingdom of God$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_22::
    .string "But the fruit of the Spirit is\n"
    .string "love, joy, peace, longsuffering,\l"
    .string "gentleness, goodness, faith,"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_23::
    .string "Meekness, temperance: against such\n"
    .string "there is no law$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_24::
    .string "And they that are Christ’s have\n"
    .string "crucified the flesh with the\l"
    .string "affections and lusts.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_25::
    .string "If we live in the Spirit, let us\n"
    .string "also walk in the Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_5_26::
    .string "Let us not be desirous of vain\n"
    .string "glory, provoking one another,\l"
    .string "envying one another.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_1::
    .string "Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a\n"
    .string "fault, ye which are spiritual,\l"
    .string "restore such an one in the spirit of\l"
    .string "meekness; considering thyself, lest\l"
    .string "thou also be tempted.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_2::
    .string "Bear ye one another’s burdens, and\n"
    .string "so fulfil the law of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_3::
    .string "For if a man think himself to be\n"
    .string "something, when he is nothing, he\l"
    .string "deceiveth himself.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_4::
    .string "But let every man prove his own\n"
    .string "work, and then shall he have\l"
    .string "rejoicing in himself alone, and not\l"
    .string "in another.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_5::
    .string "For every man shall bear his own\n"
    .string "burden.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_6::
    .string "Let him that is taught in the word\n"
    .string "communicate unto him that teacheth\l"
    .string "in all good things.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_7::
    .string "Be not deceived; God is not mocked:\n"
    .string "for whatsoever a man soweth, that\l"
    .string "shall he also reap.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_8::
    .string "For he that soweth to his flesh\n"
    .string "shall of the flesh reap\l"
    .string "corruption; but he that soweth to\l"
    .string "the Spirit shall of the Spirit\l"
    .string "reap life everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_9::
    .string "And let us not be weary in well\n"
    .string "doing: for in due season we shall\l"
    .string "reap, if we faint not.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_10::
    .string "As we have therefore opportunity,\n"
    .string "let us do good unto all men,\l"
    .string "especially unto them who are of the\l"
    .string "household of faith.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_11::
    .string "Ye see how large a letter I have\n"
    .string "written unto you with mine own hand.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_12::
    .string "As many as desire to make a fair\n"
    .string "shew in the flesh, they constrain\l"
    .string "you to be circumcised; only lest\l"
    .string "they should suffer persecution for\l"
    .string "the cross of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_13::
    .string "For neither they themselves who are\n"
    .string "circumcised keep the law; but\l"
    .string "desire to have you circumcised, that\l"
    .string "they may glory in your flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_14::
    .string "But God forbid that I should glory,\n"
    .string "save in the cross of our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, by whom the world is\l"
    .string "crucified unto me, and I unto the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_15::
    .string "For in Christ Jesus neither\n"
    .string "circumcision availeth any thing, nor\l"
    .string "uncircumcision, but a new creature.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_16::
    .string "And as many as walk according to\n"
    .string "this rule, peace be on them, and\l"
    .string "mercy, and upon the Israel of God.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_17::
    .string "From henceforth let no man trouble\n"
    .string "me: for I bear in my body the marks of\l"
    .string "the Lord Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Galatians_6_18::
    .string "Brethren, the grace of our Lord\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ be with your spirit.\l"
    .string "Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "by the will of God, to the saints\l"
    .string "which are at Ephesus, and to the\l"
    .string "faithful in Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_2::
    .string "Grace be to you, and peace, from God\n"
    .string "our Father, and from the Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_3::
    .string "Blessed be the God and Father of\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ, who hath\l"
    .string "blessed us with all spiritual\l"
    .string "blessings in heavenly places in\l"
    .string "Christ:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_4::
    .string "According as he hath chosen us in\n"
    .string "him before the foundation of the\l"
    .string "world, that we should be holy and\l"
    .string "without blame before him in love:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_5::
    .string "Having predestinated us unto the\n"
    .string "adoption of children by Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ to himself, according to the\l"
    .string "good pleasure of his will,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_6::
    .string "To the praise of the glory of his\n"
    .string "grace, wherein he hath made us\l"
    .string "accepted in the beloved$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_7::
    .string "In whom we have redemption through\n"
    .string "his blood, the forgiveness of sins,\l"
    .string "according to the riches of his grace;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_8::
    .string "Wherein he hath abounded toward us\n"
    .string "in all wisdom and prudence;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_9::
    .string "Having made known unto us the\n"
    .string "mystery of his will, according to\l"
    .string "his good pleasure which he hath\l"
    .string "purposed in himself:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_10::
    .string "That in the dispensation of the\n"
    .string "fulness of times he might gather\l"
    .string "together in one all things in\l"
    .string "Christ, both which are in heaven, and\l"
    .string "which are on earth; even in him:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_11::
    .string "In whom also we have obtained an\n"
    .string "inheritance, being predestinated\l"
    .string "according to the purpose of him who\l"
    .string "worketh all things after the\l"
    .string "counsel of his own will:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_12::
    .string "That we should be to the praise of\n"
    .string "his glory, who first trusted in\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_13::
    .string "In whom ye also trusted, after that\n"
    .string "ye heard the word of truth, the\l"
    .string "gospel of your salvation: in whom\l"
    .string "also after that ye believed, ye were\l"
    .string "sealed with that holy Spirit of\l"
    .string "promise,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_14::
    .string "Which is the earnest of our\n"
    .string "inheritance until the redemption of\l"
    .string "the purchased possession, unto the\l"
    .string "praise of his glory$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_15::
    .string "Wherefore I also, after I heard of\n"
    .string "your faith in the Lord Jesus, and\l"
    .string "love unto all the saints,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_16::
    .string "Cease not to give thanks for you,\n"
    .string "making mention of you in my prayers;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_17::
    .string "That the God of our Lord Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ, the Father of glory, may\l"
    .string "give unto you the spirit of wisdom\l"
    .string "and revelation in the knowledge of\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_18::
    .string "The eyes of your understanding\n"
    .string "being enlightened; that ye may know\l"
    .string "what is the hope of his calling,\l"
    .string "and what the riches of the glory of\l"
    .string "his inheritance in the saints,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_19::
    .string "And what is the exceeding greatness\n"
    .string "of his power to us-ward who\l"
    .string "believe, according to the working of\l"
    .string "his mighty power,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_20::
    .string "Which he wrought in Christ, when he\n"
    .string "raised him from the dead, and set him\l"
    .string "at his own right hand in the\l"
    .string "heavenly places,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_21::
    .string "Far above all principality, and\n"
    .string "power, and might, and dominion, and\l"
    .string "every name that is named, not only in\l"
    .string "this world, but also in that which\l"
    .string "is to come:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_22::
    .string "And hath put all things under his\n"
    .string "feet, and gave him to be the head over\l"
    .string "all things to the church,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_1_23::
    .string "Which is his body, the fulness of\n"
    .string "him that filleth all in all$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_1::
    .string "And you hath he quickened, who were\n"
    .string "dead in trespasses and sins;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_2::
    .string "Wherein in time past ye walked\n"
    .string "according to the course of this\l"
    .string "world, according to the prince of\l"
    .string "the power of the air, the spirit\l"
    .string "that now worketh in the children of\l"
    .string "disobedience:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_3::
    .string "Among whom also we all had our\n"
    .string "conversation in times past in the\l"
    .string "lusts of our flesh, fulfilling the\l"
    .string "desires of the flesh and of the mind;\l"
    .string "and were by nature the children of\l"
    .string "wrath, even as others$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_4::
    .string "But God, who is rich in mercy, for\n"
    .string "his great love wherewith he loved\l"
    .string "us,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_5::
    .string "Even when we were dead in sins, hath\n"
    .string "quickened us together with Christ,\l"
    .string "(by grace ye are saved;)"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_6::
    .string "And hath raised us up together, and\n"
    .string "made us sit together in heavenly\l"
    .string "places in Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_7::
    .string "That in the ages to come he might\n"
    .string "shew the exceeding riches of his\l"
    .string "grace in his kindness toward us\l"
    .string "through Christ Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_8::
    .string "For by grace are ye saved through\n"
    .string "faith; and that not of yourselves:\l"
    .string "it is the gift of God:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_9::
    .string "Not of works, lest any man should\n"
    .string "boast$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_10::
    .string "For we are his workmanship, created\n"
    .string "in Christ Jesus unto good works,\l"
    .string "which God hath before ordained that\l"
    .string "we should walk in them.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_11::
    .string "Wherefore remember, that ye being in\n"
    .string "time past Gentiles in the flesh,\l"
    .string "who are called Uncircumcision by\l"
    .string "that which is called the\l"
    .string "Circumcision in the flesh made by\l"
    .string "hands;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_12::
    .string "That at that time ye were without\n"
    .string "Christ, being aliens from the\l"
    .string "commonwealth of Israel, and\l"
    .string "strangers from the covenants of\l"
    .string "promise, having no hope, and without\l"
    .string "God in the world:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_13::
    .string "But now in Christ Jesus ye who\n"
    .string "sometimes were far off are made nigh\l"
    .string "by the blood of Christ$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_14::
    .string "For he is our peace, who hath made\n"
    .string "both one, and hath broken down the\l"
    .string "middle wall of partition between\l"
    .string "us;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_15::
    .string "Having abolished in his flesh the\n"
    .string "enmity, even the law of commandments\l"
    .string "contained in ordinances; for to make\l"
    .string "in himself of twain one new man, so\l"
    .string "making peace;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_16::
    .string "And that he might reconcile both\n"
    .string "unto God in one body by the cross,\l"
    .string "having slain the enmity thereby:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_17::
    .string "And came and preached peace to you\n"
    .string "which were afar off, and to them that\l"
    .string "were nigh$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_18::
    .string "For through him we both have access\n"
    .string "by one Spirit unto the Father.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_19::
    .string "Now therefore ye are no more\n"
    .string "strangers and foreigners, but\l"
    .string "fellowcitizens with the saints, and\l"
    .string "of the household of God;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_20::
    .string "And are built upon the foundation\n"
    .string "of the apostles and prophets,\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ himself being the chief\l"
    .string "corner stone;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_21::
    .string "In whom all the building fitly\n"
    .string "framed together groweth unto an holy\l"
    .string "temple in the Lord:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_2_22::
    .string "In whom ye also are builded\n"
    .string "together for an habitation of God\l"
    .string "through the Spirit$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_1::
    .string "For this cause I Paul, the prisoner\n"
    .string "of Jesus Christ for you Gentiles,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_2::
    .string "If ye have heard of the\n"
    .string "dispensation of the grace of God\l"
    .string "which is given me to you-ward:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_3::
    .string "How that by revelation he made\n"
    .string "known unto me the mystery; (as I\l"
    .string "wrote afore in few words,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_4::
    .string "Whereby, when ye read, ye may\n"
    .string "understand my knowledge in the\l"
    .string "mystery of Christ)"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_5::
    .string "Which in other ages was not made\n"
    .string "known unto the sons of men, as it is\l"
    .string "now revealed unto his holy\l"
    .string "apostles and prophets by the\l"
    .string "Spirit;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_6::
    .string "That the Gentiles should be\n"
    .string "fellowheirs, and of the same body,\l"
    .string "and partakers of his promise in\l"
    .string "Christ by the gospel:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_7::
    .string "Whereof I was made a minister,\n"
    .string "according to the gift of the grace of\l"
    .string "God given unto me by the effectual\l"
    .string "working of his power$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_8::
    .string "Unto me, who am less than the least\n"
    .string "of all saints, is this grace given,\l"
    .string "that I should preach among the\l"
    .string "Gentiles the unsearchable riches of\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_9::
    .string "And to make all men see what is the\n"
    .string "fellowship of the mystery, which\l"
    .string "from the beginning of the world hath\l"
    .string "been hid in God, who created all\l"
    .string "things by Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_10::
    .string "To the intent that now unto the\n"
    .string "principalities and powers in\l"
    .string "heavenly places might be known by\l"
    .string "the church the manifold wisdom of\l"
    .string "God,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_11::
    .string "According to the eternal purpose\n"
    .string "which he purposed in Christ Jesus\l"
    .string "our Lord:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_12::
    .string "In whom we have boldness and access\n"
    .string "with confidence by the faith of him$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_13::
    .string "Wherefore I desire that ye faint not\n"
    .string "at my tribulations for you, which is\l"
    .string "your glory.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_14::
    .string "For this cause I bow my knees unto\n"
    .string "the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_15::
    .string "Of whom the whole family in heaven\n"
    .string "and earth is named,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_16::
    .string "That he would grant you, according\n"
    .string "to the riches of his glory, to be\l"
    .string "strengthened with might by his\l"
    .string "Spirit in the inner man;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_17::
    .string "That Christ may dwell in your\n"
    .string "hearts by faith; that ye, being\l"
    .string "rooted and grounded in love,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_18::
    .string "May be able to comprehend with\n"
    .string "all saints what is the breadth, and\l"
    .string "length, and depth, and height;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_19::
    .string "And to know the love of Christ,\n"
    .string "which passeth knowledge, that ye\l"
    .string "might be filled with all the\l"
    .string "fulness of God$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_20::
    .string "Now unto him that is able to do\n"
    .string "exceeding abundantly above all\l"
    .string "that we ask or think, according to\l"
    .string "the power that worketh in us,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_3_21::
    .string "Unto him be glory in the church by\n"
    .string "Christ Jesus throughout all ages,\l"
    .string "world without end. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_1::
    .string "I therefore, the prisoner of the\n"
    .string "Lord, beseech you that ye walk\l"
    .string "worthy of the vocation wherewith ye\l"
    .string "are called,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_2::
    .string "With all lowliness and meekness,\n"
    .string "with longsuffering, forbearing one\l"
    .string "another in love;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_3::
    .string "Endeavouring to keep the unity of\n"
    .string "the Spirit in the bond of peace$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_4::
    .string "There is one body, and one Spirit,\n"
    .string "even as ye are called in one hope\l"
    .string "of your calling;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_5::
    .string "One Lord, one faith, one baptism,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_6::
    .string "One God and Father of all, who is\n"
    .string "above all, and through all, and in\l"
    .string "you all$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_7::
    .string "But unto every one of us is given\n"
    .string "grace according to the measure of the\l"
    .string "gift of Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_8::
    .string "Wherefore he saith, When he ascended\n"
    .string "up on high, he led captivity\l"
    .string "captive, and gave gifts unto men.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_9::
    .string "(Now that he ascended, what is it\n"
    .string "but that he also descended first\l"
    .string "into the lower parts of the earth?"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_10::
    .string "He that descended is the same also\n"
    .string "that ascended up far above all\l"
    .string "heavens, that he might fill all\l"
    .string "things.)"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_11::
    .string "And he gave some, apostles; and\n"
    .string "some, prophets; and some,\l"
    .string "evangelists; and some, pastors and\l"
    .string "teachers;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_12::
    .string "For the perfecting of the saints,\n"
    .string "for the work of the ministry, for the\l"
    .string "edifying of the body of Christ:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_13::
    .string "Till we all come in the unity of\n"
    .string "the faith, and of the knowledge of\l"
    .string "the Son of God, unto a perfect man,\l"
    .string "unto the measure of the stature of\l"
    .string "the fulness of Christ:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_14::
    .string "That we henceforth be no more\n"
    .string "children, tossed to and fro, and\l"
    .string "carried about with every wind of\l"
    .string "doctrine, by the sleight of men, and\l"
    .string "cunning craftiness, whereby they lie\l"
    .string "in wait to deceive;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_15::
    .string "But speaking the truth in love, may\n"
    .string "grow up into him in all things,\l"
    .string "which is the head, even Christ:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_16::
    .string "From whom the whole body fitly\n"
    .string "joined together and compacted by\l"
    .string "that which every joint supplieth,\l"
    .string "according to the effectual working\l"
    .string "in the measure of every part, maketh\l"
    .string "increase of the body unto the\l"
    .string "edifying of itself in love$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_17::
    .string "This I say therefore, and testify in\n"
    .string "the Lord, that ye henceforth walk\l"
    .string "not as other Gentiles walk, in the\l"
    .string "vanity of their mind,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_18::
    .string "Having the understanding darkened,\n"
    .string "being alienated from the life of\l"
    .string "God through the ignorance that is in\l"
    .string "them, because of the blindness of\l"
    .string "their heart:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_19::
    .string "Who being past feeling have given\n"
    .string "themselves over unto\l"
    .string "lasciviousness, to work all\l"
    .string "uncleanness with greediness$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_20::
    .string "But ye have not so learned Christ;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_21::
    .string "If so be that ye have heard him, and\n"
    .string "have been taught by him, as the truth\l"
    .string "is in Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_22::
    .string "That ye put off concerning the\n"
    .string "former conversation the old man,\l"
    .string "which is corrupt according to the\l"
    .string "deceitful lusts;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_23::
    .string "And be renewed in the spirit of\n"
    .string "your mind;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_24::
    .string "And that ye put on the new man,\n"
    .string "which after God is created in\l"
    .string "righteousness and true holiness$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_25::
    .string "Wherefore putting away lying,\n"
    .string "speak every man truth with his\l"
    .string "neighbour: for we are members one of\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_26::
    .string "Be ye angry, and sin not: let not\n"
    .string "the sun go down upon your wrath:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_27::
    .string "Neither give place to the devil$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_28::
    .string "Let him that stole steal no more:\n"
    .string "but rather let him labour, working\l"
    .string "with his hands the thing which is\l"
    .string "good, that he may have to give to him\l"
    .string "that needeth.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_29::
    .string "Let no corrupt communication\n"
    .string "proceed out of your mouth, but that\l"
    .string "which is good to the use of edifying,\l"
    .string "that it may minister grace unto the\l"
    .string "hearers.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_30::
    .string "And grieve not the holy Spirit of\n"
    .string "God, whereby ye are sealed unto the\l"
    .string "day of redemption.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_31::
    .string "Let all bitterness, and wrath, and\n"
    .string "anger, and clamour, and evil\l"
    .string "speaking, be put away from you, with\l"
    .string "all malice:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_4_32::
    .string "And be ye kind one to another,\n"
    .string "tenderhearted, forgiving one\l"
    .string "another, even as God for Christ’s\l"
    .string "sake hath forgiven you$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_1::
    .string "Be ye therefore followers of God,\n"
    .string "as dear children;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_2::
    .string "And walk in love, as Christ also\n"
    .string "hath loved us, and hath given\l"
    .string "himself for us an offering and a\l"
    .string "sacrifice to God for a\l"
    .string "sweetsmelling savour$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_3::
    .string "But fornication, and all\n"
    .string "uncleanness, or covetousness, let\l"
    .string "it not be once named among you, as\l"
    .string "becometh saints;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_4::
    .string "Neither filthiness, nor foolish\n"
    .string "talking, nor jesting, which are not\l"
    .string "convenient: but rather giving of\l"
    .string "thanks$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_5::
    .string "For this ye know, that no\n"
    .string "whoremonger, nor unclean person,\l"
    .string "nor covetous man, who is an\l"
    .string "idolater, hath any inheritance in\l"
    .string "the kingdom of Christ and of God.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_6::
    .string "Let no man deceive you with vain\n"
    .string "words: for because of these things\l"
    .string "cometh the wrath of God upon the\l"
    .string "children of disobedience.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_7::
    .string "Be not ye therefore partakers with\n"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_8::
    .string "For ye were sometimes darkness, but\n"
    .string "now are ye light in the Lord: walk\l"
    .string "as children of light:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_9::
    .string "(For the fruit of the Spirit is in\n"
    .string "all goodness and righteousness and\l"
    .string "truth;)"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_10::
    .string "Proving what is acceptable unto\n"
    .string "the Lord$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_11::
    .string "And have no fellowship with the\n"
    .string "unfruitful works of darkness, but\l"
    .string "rather reprove them.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_12::
    .string "For it is a shame even to speak of\n"
    .string "those things which are done of them\l"
    .string "in secret.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_13::
    .string "But all things that are reproved\n"
    .string "are made manifest by the light: for\l"
    .string "whatsoever doth make manifest is\l"
    .string "light.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_14::
    .string "Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that\n"
    .string "sleepest, and arise from the dead,\l"
    .string "and Christ shall give thee light.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_15::
    .string "See then that ye walk\n"
    .string "circumspectly, not as fools, but as\l"
    .string "wise,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_16::
    .string "Redeeming the time, because the days\n"
    .string "are evil$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_17::
    .string "Wherefore be ye not unwise, but\n"
    .string "understanding what the will of the\l"
    .string "Lord is.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_18::
    .string "And be not drunk with wine, wherein\n"
    .string "is excess; but be filled with the\l"
    .string "Spirit;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_19::
    .string "Speaking to yourselves in psalms\n"
    .string "and hymns and spiritual songs,\l"
    .string "singing and making melody in your\l"
    .string "heart to the Lord;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_20::
    .string "Giving thanks always for all\n"
    .string "things unto God and the Father in the\l"
    .string "name of our Lord Jesus Christ;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_21::
    .string "Submitting yourselves one to\n"
    .string "another in the fear of God$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_22::
    .string "Wives, submit yourselves unto your\n"
    .string "own husbands, as unto the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_23::
    .string "For the husband is the head of the\n"
    .string "wife, even as Christ is the head of\l"
    .string "the church: and he is the saviour of\l"
    .string "the body.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_24::
    .string "Therefore as the church is subject\n"
    .string "unto Christ, so let the wives be to\l"
    .string "their own husbands in every thing.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_25::
    .string "Husbands, love your wives, even as\n"
    .string "Christ also loved the church, and\l"
    .string "gave himself for it;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_26::
    .string "That he might sanctify and cleanse\n"
    .string "it with the washing of water by the\l"
    .string "word,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_27::
    .string "That he might present it to\n"
    .string "himself a glorious church, not\l"
    .string "having spot, or wrinkle, or any such\l"
    .string "thing; but that it should be holy\l"
    .string "and without blemish$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_28::
    .string "So ought men to love their wives as\n"
    .string "their own bodies. He that loveth his\l"
    .string "wife loveth himself.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_29::
    .string "For no man ever yet hated his own\n"
    .string "flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth\l"
    .string "it, even as the Lord the church:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_30::
    .string "For we are members of his body, of\n"
    .string "his flesh, and of his bones$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_31::
    .string "For this cause shall a man leave\n"
    .string "his father and mother, and shall be\l"
    .string "joined unto his wife, and they two\l"
    .string "shall be one flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_32::
    .string "This is a great mystery: but I speak\n"
    .string "concerning Christ and the church.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_5_33::
    .string "Nevertheless let every one of you\n"
    .string "in particular so love his wife even\l"
    .string "as himself; and the wife see that she\l"
    .string "reverence her husband.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_1::
    .string "Children, obey your parents in the\n"
    .string "Lord: for this is right.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_2::
    .string "Honour thy father and mother; which\n"
    .string "is the first commandment with\l"
    .string "promise;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_3::
    .string "That it may be well with thee, and\n"
    .string "thou mayest live long on the earth$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_4::
    .string "And, ye fathers, provoke not your\n"
    .string "children to wrath: but bring them up\l"
    .string "in the nurture and admonition of the\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_5::
    .string "Servants, be obedient to them that\n"
    .string "are your masters according to the\l"
    .string "flesh, with fear and trembling, in\l"
    .string "singleness of your heart, as unto\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_6::
    .string "Not with eyeservice, as\n"
    .string "menpleasers; but as the servants of\l"
    .string "Christ, doing the will of God from\l"
    .string "the heart;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_7::
    .string "With good will doing service, as to\n"
    .string "the Lord, and not to men:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_8::
    .string "Knowing that whatsoever good thing\n"
    .string "any man doeth, the same shall he\l"
    .string "receive of the Lord, whether he be\l"
    .string "bond or free$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_9::
    .string "And, ye masters, do the same things\n"
    .string "unto them, forbearing threatening:\l"
    .string "knowing that your Master also is in\l"
    .string "heaven; neither is there respect of\l"
    .string "persons with him.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_10::
    .string "Finally, my brethren, be strong in\n"
    .string "the Lord, and in the power of his\l"
    .string "might.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_11::
    .string "Put on the whole armour of God, that\n"
    .string "ye may be able to stand against the\l"
    .string "wiles of the devil.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_12::
    .string "For we wrestle not against flesh\n"
    .string "and blood, but against\l"
    .string "principalities, against powers,\l"
    .string "against the rulers of the darkness\l"
    .string "of this world, against spiritual\l"
    .string "wickedness in high places.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_13::
    .string "Wherefore take unto you the whole\n"
    .string "armour of God, that ye may be able to\l"
    .string "withstand in the evil day, and\l"
    .string "having done all, to stand.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_14::
    .string "Stand therefore, having your loins\n"
    .string "girt about with truth, and having on\l"
    .string "the breastplate of righteousness;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_15::
    .string "And your feet shod with the\n"
    .string "preparation of the gospel of\l"
    .string "peace;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_16::
    .string "Above all, taking the shield of\n"
    .string "faith, wherewith ye shall be able\l"
    .string "to quench all the fiery darts of the\l"
    .string "wicked$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_17::
    .string "And take the helmet of salvation,\n"
    .string "and the sword of the Spirit, which is\l"
    .string "the word of God:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_18::
    .string "Praying always with all prayer\n"
    .string "and supplication in the Spirit,\l"
    .string "and watching thereunto with all\l"
    .string "perseverance and supplication for\l"
    .string "all saints;"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_19::
    .string "And for me, that utterance may be\n"
    .string "given unto me, that I may open my\l"
    .string "mouth boldly, to make known the\l"
    .string "mystery of the gospel,"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_20::
    .string "For which I am an ambassador in\n"
    .string "bonds: that therein I may speak\l"
    .string "boldly, as I ought to speak$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_21::
    .string "But that ye also may know my\n"
    .string "affairs, and how I do, Tychicus, a\l"
    .string "beloved brother and faithful\l"
    .string "minister in the Lord, shall make\l"
    .string "known to you all things:"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_22::
    .string "Whom I have sent unto you for the\n"
    .string "same purpose, that ye might know our\l"
    .string "affairs, and that he might comfort\l"
    .string "your hearts$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_23::
    .string "Peace be to the brethren, and love\n"
    .string "with faith, from God the Father and\l"
    .string "the Lord Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Ephesians_6_24::
    .string "Grace be with all them that love\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ in sincerity.\l"
    .string "Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_1::
    .string "Paul and Timotheus, the servants of\n"
    .string "Jesus Christ, to all the saints in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus which are at Philippi,\l"
    .string "with the bishops and deacons:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_2::
    .string "Grace be unto you, and peace, from\n"
    .string "God our Father, and from the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_3::
    .string "I thank my God upon every\n"
    .string "remembrance of you,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_4::
    .string "Always in every prayer of mine for\n"
    .string "you all making request with joy,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_5::
    .string "For your fellowship in the\n"
    .string "gospel from the first day until\l"
    .string "now;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_6::
    .string "Being confident of this very thing,\n"
    .string "that he which hath begun a good work\l"
    .string "in you will perform it until the\l"
    .string "day of Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_7::
    .string "Even as it is meet for me to think\n"
    .string "this of you all, because I have you\l"
    .string "in my heart; inasmuch as both in my\l"
    .string "bonds, and in the defence and\l"
    .string "confirmation of the gospel, ye all\l"
    .string "are partakers of my grace$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_8::
    .string "For God is my record, how greatly I\n"
    .string "long after you all in the bowels of\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_9::
    .string "And this I pray, that your love may\n"
    .string "abound yet more and more in\l"
    .string "knowledge and in all judgment;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_10::
    .string "That ye may approve things that\n"
    .string "are excellent; that ye may be\l"
    .string "sincere and without offence till\l"
    .string "the day of Christ$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_11::
    .string "Being filled with the fruits of\n"
    .string "righteousness, which are by Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, unto the glory and praise of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_12::
    .string "But I would ye should understand,\n"
    .string "brethren, that the things which\l"
    .string "happened unto me have fallen out\l"
    .string "rather unto the furtherance of the\l"
    .string "gospel;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_13::
    .string "So that my bonds in Christ are\n"
    .string "manifest in all the palace, and in\l"
    .string "all other places;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_14::
    .string "And many of the brethren in the\n"
    .string "Lord, waxing confident by my bonds,\l"
    .string "are much more bold to speak the word\l"
    .string "without fear$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_15::
    .string "Some indeed preach Christ even of\n"
    .string "envy and strife; and some also of\l"
    .string "good will:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_16::
    .string "The one preach Christ of\n"
    .string "contention, not sincerely,\l"
    .string "supposing to add affliction to my\l"
    .string "bonds:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_17::
    .string "But the other of love, knowing that\n"
    .string "I am set for the defence of the\l"
    .string "gospel$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_18::
    .string "What then? notwithstanding, every\n"
    .string "way, whether in pretence, or in\l"
    .string "truth, Christ is preached; and I\l"
    .string "therein do rejoice, yea, and will\l"
    .string "rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_19::
    .string "For I know that this shall turn to\n"
    .string "my salvation through your prayer,\l"
    .string "and the supply of the Spirit of\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_20::
    .string "According to my earnest\n"
    .string "expectation and my hope, that in\l"
    .string "nothing I shall be ashamed, but that\l"
    .string "with all boldness, as always, so\l"
    .string "now also Christ shall be magnified\l"
    .string "in my body, whether it be by life, or\l"
    .string "by death$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_21::
    .string "For to me to live is Christ, and to\n"
    .string "die is gain.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_22::
    .string "But if I live in the flesh, this is\n"
    .string "the fruit of my labour: yet what I\l"
    .string "shall choose I wot not.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_23::
    .string "For I am in a strait betwixt two,\n"
    .string "having a desire to depart, and to be\l"
    .string "with Christ; which is far better:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_24::
    .string "Nevertheless to abide in the flesh\n"
    .string "is more needful for you$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_25::
    .string "And having this confidence, I know\n"
    .string "that I shall abide and continue\l"
    .string "with you all for your furtherance\l"
    .string "and joy of faith;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_26::
    .string "That your rejoicing may be more\n"
    .string "abundant in Jesus Christ for me by my\l"
    .string "coming to you again$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_27::
    .string "Only let your conversation be as\n"
    .string "it becometh the gospel of Christ:\l"
    .string "that whether I come and see you, or\l"
    .string "else be absent, I may hear of your\l"
    .string "affairs, that ye stand fast in one\l"
    .string "spirit, with one mind striving\l"
    .string "together for the faith of the\l"
    .string "gospel;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_28::
    .string "And in nothing terrified by your\n"
    .string "adversaries: which is to them an\l"
    .string "evident token of perdition, but to\l"
    .string "you of salvation, and that of God$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_29::
    .string "For unto you it is given in the\n"
    .string "behalf of Christ, not only to\l"
    .string "believe on him, but also to suffer\l"
    .string "for his sake;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_1_30::
    .string "Having the same conflict which ye\n"
    .string "saw in me, and now hear to be in me$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_1::
    .string "If there be therefore any\n"
    .string "consolation in Christ, if any\l"
    .string "comfort of love, if any fellowship\l"
    .string "of the Spirit, if any bowels and\l"
    .string "mercies,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_2::
    .string "Fulfil ye my joy, that ye be\n"
    .string "likeminded, having the same love,\l"
    .string "being of one accord, of one mind$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_3::
    .string "Let nothing be done through strife\n"
    .string "or vainglory; but in lowliness of\l"
    .string "mind let each esteem other better\l"
    .string "than themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_4::
    .string "Look not every man on his own\n"
    .string "things, but every man also on the\l"
    .string "things of others.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_5::
    .string "Let this mind be in you, which was\n"
    .string "also in Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_6::
    .string "Who, being in the form of God,\n"
    .string "thought it not robbery to be equal\l"
    .string "with God:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_7::
    .string "But made himself of no reputation,\n"
    .string "and took upon him the form of a\l"
    .string "servant, and was made in the\l"
    .string "likeness of men:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_8::
    .string "And being found in fashion as a man,\n"
    .string "he humbled himself, and became\l"
    .string "obedient unto death, even the death\l"
    .string "of the cross$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_9::
    .string "Wherefore God also hath highly\n"
    .string "exalted him, and given him a name\l"
    .string "which is above every name:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_10::
    .string "That at the name of Jesus every knee\n"
    .string "should bow, of things in heaven, and\l"
    .string "things in earth, and things under the\l"
    .string "earth;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_11::
    .string "And that every tongue should\n"
    .string "confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to\l"
    .string "the glory of God the Father$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_12::
    .string "Wherefore, my beloved, as ye have\n"
    .string "always obeyed, not as in my presence\l"
    .string "only, but now much more in my\l"
    .string "absence, work out your own salvation\l"
    .string "with fear and trembling.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_13::
    .string "For it is God which worketh in you\n"
    .string "both to will and to do of his good\l"
    .string "pleasure.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_14::
    .string "Do all things without murmurings\n"
    .string "and disputings:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_15::
    .string "That ye may be blameless and\n"
    .string "harmless, the sons of God, without\l"
    .string "rebuke, in the midst of a crooked and\l"
    .string "perverse nation, among whom ye shine\l"
    .string "as lights in the world;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_16::
    .string "Holding forth the word of life;\n"
    .string "that I may rejoice in the day of\l"
    .string "Christ, that I have not run in vain,\l"
    .string "neither laboured in vain$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_17::
    .string "Yea, and if I be offered upon the\n"
    .string "sacrifice and service of your faith,\l"
    .string "I joy, and rejoice with you all.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_18::
    .string "For the same cause also do ye joy,\n"
    .string "and rejoice with me.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_19::
    .string "But I trust in the Lord Jesus to\n"
    .string "send Timotheus shortly unto you,\l"
    .string "that I also may be of good comfort,\l"
    .string "when I know your state.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_20::
    .string "For I have no man likeminded, who\n"
    .string "will naturally care for your state.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_21::
    .string "For all seek their own, not the\n"
    .string "things which are Jesus Christ’s.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_22::
    .string "But ye know the proof of him, that,\n"
    .string "as a son with the father, he hath\l"
    .string "served with me in the gospel.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_23::
    .string "Him therefore I hope to send\n"
    .string "presently, so soon as I shall see\l"
    .string "how it will go with me.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_24::
    .string "But I trust in the Lord that I also\n"
    .string "myself shall come shortly.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_25::
    .string "Yet I supposed it necessary to\n"
    .string "send to you Epaphroditus, my\l"
    .string "brother, and companion in labour,\l"
    .string "and fellowsoldier, but your\l"
    .string "messenger, and he that ministered to\l"
    .string "my wants.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_26::
    .string "For he longed after you all, and\n"
    .string "was full of heaviness, because that\l"
    .string "ye had heard that he had been sick.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_27::
    .string "For indeed he was sick nigh unto\n"
    .string "death: but God had mercy on him; and\l"
    .string "not on him only, but on me also,\l"
    .string "lest I should have sorrow upon\l"
    .string "sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_28::
    .string "I sent him therefore the more\n"
    .string "carefully, that, when ye see him\l"
    .string "again, ye may rejoice, and that I may\l"
    .string "be the less sorrowful.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_29::
    .string "Receive him therefore in the Lord\n"
    .string "with all gladness; and hold such\l"
    .string "in reputation:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_2_30::
    .string "Because for the work of Christ he\n"
    .string "was nigh unto death, not regarding\l"
    .string "his life, to supply your lack of\l"
    .string "service toward me$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_1::
    .string "Finally, my brethren, rejoice in\n"
    .string "the Lord. To write the same things to\l"
    .string "you, to me indeed is not grievous,\l"
    .string "but for you it is safe.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_2::
    .string "Beware of dogs, beware of evil\n"
    .string "workers, beware of the concision.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_3::
    .string "For we are the circumcision, which\n"
    .string "worship God in the spirit, and\l"
    .string "rejoice in Christ Jesus, and have no\l"
    .string "confidence in the flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_4::
    .string "Though I might also have confidence\n"
    .string "in the flesh. If any other man\l"
    .string "thinketh that he hath whereof he\l"
    .string "might trust in the flesh, I more:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_5::
    .string "Circumcised the eighth day, of the\n"
    .string "stock of Israel, of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Benjamin, an Hebrew of the Hebrews;\l"
    .string "as touching the law, a Pharisee;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_6::
    .string "Concerning zeal, persecuting the\n"
    .string "church; touching the righteousness\l"
    .string "which is in the law, blameless$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_7::
    .string "But what things were gain to me,\n"
    .string "those I counted loss for Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_8::
    .string "Yea doubtless, and I count all\n"
    .string "things but loss for the excellency\l"
    .string "of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my\l"
    .string "Lord: for whom I have suffered the\l"
    .string "loss of all things, and do count\l"
    .string "them but dung, that I may win Christ,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_9::
    .string "And be found in him, not having mine\n"
    .string "own righteousness, which is of the\l"
    .string "law, but that which is through the\l"
    .string "faith of Christ, the righteousness\l"
    .string "which is of God by faith:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_10::
    .string "That I may know him, and the power\n"
    .string "of his resurrection, and the\l"
    .string "fellowship of his sufferings,\l"
    .string "being made conformable unto his\l"
    .string "death;"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_11::
    .string "If by any means I might attain unto\n"
    .string "the resurrection of the dead$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_12::
    .string "Not as though I had already\n"
    .string "attained, either were already\l"
    .string "perfect: but I follow after, if that\l"
    .string "I may apprehend that for which also\l"
    .string "I am apprehended of Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_13::
    .string "Brethren, I count not myself to\n"
    .string "have apprehended: but this one\l"
    .string "thing I do, forgetting those things\l"
    .string "which are behind, and reaching forth\l"
    .string "unto those things which are before,"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_14::
    .string "I press toward the mark for the\n"
    .string "prize of the high calling of God in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_15::
    .string "Let us therefore, as many as be\n"
    .string "perfect, be thus minded: and if in\l"
    .string "any thing ye be otherwise minded, God\l"
    .string "shall reveal even this unto you.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_16::
    .string "Nevertheless, whereto we have\n"
    .string "already attained, let us walk by\l"
    .string "the same rule, let us mind the same\l"
    .string "thing.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_17::
    .string "Brethren, be followers together of\n"
    .string "me, and mark them which walk so as ye\l"
    .string "have us for an ensample.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_18::
    .string "(For many walk, of whom I have told\n"
    .string "you often, and now tell you even\l"
    .string "weeping, that they are the enemies\l"
    .string "of the cross of Christ:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_19::
    .string "Whose end is destruction, whose God\n"
    .string "is their belly, and whose glory is\l"
    .string "in their shame, who mind earthly\l"
    .string "things.)"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_20::
    .string "For our conversation is in heaven;\n"
    .string "from whence also we look for the\l"
    .string "Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_Philippians_3_21::
    .string "Who shall change our vile body,\n"
    .string "that it may be fashioned like unto\l"
    .string "his glorious body, according to the\l"
    .string "working whereby he is able even to\l"
    .string "subdue all things unto himself$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_1::
    .string "Therefore, my brethren dearly\n"
    .string "beloved and longed for, my joy and\l"
    .string "crown, so stand fast in the Lord, my\l"
    .string "dearly beloved.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_2::
    .string "I beseech Euodias, and beseech\n"
    .string "Syntyche, that they be of the same\l"
    .string "mind in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_3::
    .string "And I intreat thee also, true\n"
    .string "yokefellow, help those women which\l"
    .string "laboured with me in the gospel, with\l"
    .string "Clement also, and with other my\l"
    .string "fellowlabourers, whose names are\l"
    .string "in the book of life.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_4::
    .string "Rejoice in the Lord alway: and\n"
    .string "again I say, Rejoice.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_5::
    .string "Let your moderation be known unto\n"
    .string "all men. The Lord is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_6::
    .string "Be careful for nothing; but in\n"
    .string "every thing by prayer and\l"
    .string "supplication with thanksgiving\l"
    .string "let your requests be made known unto\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_7::
    .string "And the peace of God, which passeth\n"
    .string "all understanding, shall keep\l"
    .string "your hearts and minds through Christ\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_8::
    .string "Finally, brethren, whatsoever\n"
    .string "things are true, whatsoever things\l"
    .string "are honest, whatsoever things are\l"
    .string "just, whatsoever things are pure,\l"
    .string "whatsoever things are lovely,\l"
    .string "whatsoever things are of good\l"
    .string "report; if there be any virtue, and\l"
    .string "if there be any praise, think on\l"
    .string "these things.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_9::
    .string "Those things, which ye have both\n"
    .string "learned, and received, and heard, and\l"
    .string "seen in me, do: and the God of peace\l"
    .string "shall be with you.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_10::
    .string "But I rejoiced in the Lord greatly,\n"
    .string "that now at the last your care of me\l"
    .string "hath flourished again; wherein ye\l"
    .string "were also careful, but ye lacked\l"
    .string "opportunity.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_11::
    .string "Not that I speak in respect of\n"
    .string "want: for I have learned, in\l"
    .string "whatsoever state I am, therewith to\l"
    .string "be content.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_12::
    .string "I know both how to be abased, and I\n"
    .string "know how to abound: every where and\l"
    .string "in all things I am instructed both\l"
    .string "to be full and to be hungry, both to\l"
    .string "abound and to suffer need.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_13::
    .string "I can do all things through Christ\n"
    .string "which strengtheneth me.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_14::
    .string "Notwithstanding ye have well done,\n"
    .string "that ye did communicate with my\l"
    .string "affliction.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_15::
    .string "Now ye Philippians know also,\n"
    .string "that in the beginning of the gospel,\l"
    .string "when I departed from Macedonia, no\l"
    .string "church communicated with me as\l"
    .string "concerning giving and receiving, but\l"
    .string "ye only.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_16::
    .string "For even in Thessalonica ye sent\n"
    .string "once and again unto my necessity.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_17::
    .string "Not because I desire a gift: but I\n"
    .string "desire fruit that may abound to your\l"
    .string "account.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_18::
    .string "But I have all, and abound: I am\n"
    .string "full, having received of\l"
    .string "Epaphroditus the things which were\l"
    .string "sent from you, an odour of a sweet\l"
    .string "smell, a sacrifice acceptable,\l"
    .string "wellpleasing to God.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_19::
    .string "But my God shall supply all\n"
    .string "your need according to his riches in\l"
    .string "glory by Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_20::
    .string "Now unto God and our Father be\n"
    .string "glory for ever and ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_21::
    .string "Salute every saint in Christ Jesus.\n"
    .string "The brethren which are with me greet\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_22::
    .string "All the saints salute you,\n"
    .string "chiefly they that are of Caesar’s\l"
    .string "household.$"
Bible_Text_Philippians_4_23::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "by the will of God, and Timotheus\l"
    .string "our brother,"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_2::
    .string "To the saints and faithful brethren\n"
    .string "in Christ which are at Colosse:\l"
    .string "Grace be unto you, and peace, from\l"
    .string "God our Father and the Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_3::
    .string "We give thanks to God and the Father\n"
    .string "of our Lord Jesus Christ, praying\l"
    .string "always for you,"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_4::
    .string "Since we heard of your faith in\n"
    .string "Christ Jesus, and of the love which\l"
    .string "ye have to all the saints,"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_5::
    .string "For the hope which is laid up for\n"
    .string "you in heaven, whereof ye heard\l"
    .string "before in the word of the truth of\l"
    .string "the gospel;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_6::
    .string "Which is come unto you, as it is in\n"
    .string "all the world; and bringeth forth\l"
    .string "fruit, as it doth also in you, since\l"
    .string "the day ye heard of it, and knew the\l"
    .string "grace of God in truth:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_7::
    .string "As ye also learned of Epaphras\n"
    .string "our dear fellowservant, who is for\l"
    .string "you a faithful minister of Christ;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_8::
    .string "Who also declared unto us your\n"
    .string "love in the Spirit$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_9::
    .string "For this cause we also, since the\n"
    .string "day we heard it, do not cease to pray\l"
    .string "for you, and to desire that ye might\l"
    .string "be filled with the knowledge of his\l"
    .string "will in all wisdom and spiritual\l"
    .string "understanding;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_10::
    .string "That ye might walk worthy of the\n"
    .string "Lord unto all pleasing, being\l"
    .string "fruitful in every good work, and\l"
    .string "increasing in the knowledge of God;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_11::
    .string "Strengthened with all might,\n"
    .string "according to his glorious power,\l"
    .string "unto all patience and\l"
    .string "longsuffering with joyfulness;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_12::
    .string "Giving thanks unto the Father, which\n"
    .string "hath made us meet to be partakers of\l"
    .string "the inheritance of the saints in\l"
    .string "light:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_13::
    .string "Who hath delivered us from the\n"
    .string "power of darkness, and hath\l"
    .string "translated us into the kingdom of\l"
    .string "his dear Son:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_14::
    .string "In whom we have redemption through\n"
    .string "his blood, even the forgiveness of\l"
    .string "sins:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_15::
    .string "Who is the image of the invisible\n"
    .string "God, the firstborn of every creature:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_16::
    .string "For by him were all things created,\n"
    .string "that are in heaven, and that are in\l"
    .string "earth, visible and invisible,\l"
    .string "whether they be thrones, or\l"
    .string "dominions, or principalities, or\l"
    .string "powers: all things were created by\l"
    .string "him, and for him:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_17::
    .string "And he is before all things, and by\n"
    .string "him all things consist$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_18::
    .string "And he is the head of the body, the\n"
    .string "church: who is the beginning, the\l"
    .string "firstborn from the dead; that in all\l"
    .string "things he might have the preeminence.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_19::
    .string "For it pleased the Father that in\n"
    .string "him should all fulness dwell;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_20::
    .string "And, having made peace through the\n"
    .string "blood of his cross, by him to\l"
    .string "reconcile all things unto himself;\l"
    .string "by him, I say, whether they be things\l"
    .string "in earth, or things in heaven$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_21::
    .string "And you, that were sometime\n"
    .string "alienated and enemies in your mind\l"
    .string "by wicked works, yet now hath he\l"
    .string "reconciled"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_22::
    .string "In the body of his flesh through\n"
    .string "death, to present you holy and\l"
    .string "unblameable and unreproveable in\l"
    .string "his sight:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_23::
    .string "If ye continue in the faith grounded\n"
    .string "and settled, and be not moved away\l"
    .string "from the hope of the gospel, which\l"
    .string "ye have heard, and which was\l"
    .string "preached to every creature which is\l"
    .string "under heaven; whereof I Paul am made\l"
    .string "a minister;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_24::
    .string "Who now rejoice in my sufferings for\n"
    .string "you, and fill up that which is\l"
    .string "behind of the afflictions of Christ\l"
    .string "in my flesh for his body’s sake,\l"
    .string "which is the church:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_25::
    .string "Whereof I am made a minister,\n"
    .string "according to the dispensation of God\l"
    .string "which is given to me for you, to\l"
    .string "fulfil the word of God;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_26::
    .string "Even the mystery which hath been hid\n"
    .string "from ages and from generations, but\l"
    .string "now is made manifest to his saints:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_27::
    .string "To whom God would make known what\n"
    .string "is the riches of the glory of this\l"
    .string "mystery among the Gentiles; which is\l"
    .string "Christ in you, the hope of glory:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_28::
    .string "Whom we preach, warning every man,\n"
    .string "and teaching every man in all\l"
    .string "wisdom; that we may present every\l"
    .string "man perfect in Christ Jesus:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_1_29::
    .string "Whereunto I also labour, striving\n"
    .string "according to his working, which\l"
    .string "worketh in me mightily$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_1::
    .string "For I would that ye knew what great\n"
    .string "conflict I have for you, and for them\l"
    .string "at Laodicea, and for as many as have\l"
    .string "not seen my face in the flesh;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_2::
    .string "That their hearts might be\n"
    .string "comforted, being knit together in\l"
    .string "love, and unto all riches of the\l"
    .string "full assurance of understanding, to\l"
    .string "the acknowledgement of the mystery\l"
    .string "of God, and of the Father, and of\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_3::
    .string "In whom are hid all the treasures\n"
    .string "of wisdom and knowledge$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_4::
    .string "And this I say, lest any man should\n"
    .string "beguile you with enticing words.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_5::
    .string "For though I be absent in the flesh,\n"
    .string "yet am I with you in the spirit,\l"
    .string "joying and beholding your order, and\l"
    .string "the stedfastness of your faith in\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_6::
    .string "As ye have therefore received\n"
    .string "Christ Jesus the Lord, so walk ye in\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_7::
    .string "Rooted and built up in him, and\n"
    .string "stablished in the faith, as ye have\l"
    .string "been taught, abounding therein with\l"
    .string "thanksgiving$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_8::
    .string "Beware lest any man spoil you\n"
    .string "through philosophy and vain\l"
    .string "deceit, after the tradition of men,\l"
    .string "after the rudiments of the world,\l"
    .string "and not after Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_9::
    .string "For in him dwelleth all the\n"
    .string "fulness of the Godhead bodily.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_10::
    .string "And ye are complete in him, which\n"
    .string "is the head of all principality\l"
    .string "and power:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_11::
    .string "In whom also ye are circumcised\n"
    .string "with the circumcision made without\l"
    .string "hands, in putting off the body of the\l"
    .string "sins of the flesh by the\l"
    .string "circumcision of Christ:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_12::
    .string "Buried with him in baptism, wherein\n"
    .string "also ye are risen with him through\l"
    .string "the faith of the operation of God,\l"
    .string "who hath raised him from the dead$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_13::
    .string "And you, being dead in your sins and\n"
    .string "the uncircumcision of your flesh,\l"
    .string "hath he quickened together with him,\l"
    .string "having forgiven you all\l"
    .string "trespasses;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_14::
    .string "Blotting out the handwriting of\n"
    .string "ordinances that was against us, which\l"
    .string "was contrary to us, and took it out of\l"
    .string "the way, nailing it to his cross;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_15::
    .string "And having spoiled\n"
    .string "principalities and powers, he made\l"
    .string "a shew of them openly, triumphing\l"
    .string "over them in it$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_16::
    .string "Let no man therefore judge you in\n"
    .string "meat, or in drink, or in respect of\l"
    .string "an holyday, or of the new moon, or of\l"
    .string "the sabbath days:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_17::
    .string "Which are a shadow of things to\n"
    .string "come; but the body is of Christ$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_18::
    .string "Let no man beguile you of your\n"
    .string "reward in a voluntary humility and\l"
    .string "worshipping of angels, intruding\l"
    .string "into those things which he hath not\l"
    .string "seen, vainly puffed up by his\l"
    .string "fleshly mind,"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_19::
    .string "And not holding the Head, from\n"
    .string "which all the body by joints and\l"
    .string "bands having nourishment ministered,\l"
    .string "and knit together, increaseth with\l"
    .string "the increase of God$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_20::
    .string "Wherefore if ye be dead with Christ\n"
    .string "from the rudiments of the world,\l"
    .string "why, as though living in the world,\l"
    .string "are ye subject to ordinances,"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_21::
    .string "(Touch not; taste not; handle not;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_22::
    .string "Which all are to perish with the\n"
    .string "using;) after the commandments and\l"
    .string "doctrines of men?"
Bible_Text_Colossians_2_23::
    .string "Which things have indeed a shew of\n"
    .string "wisdom in will worship, and\l"
    .string "humility, and neglecting of the\l"
    .string "body: not in any honour to the\l"
    .string "satisfying of the flesh$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_1::
    .string "If ye then be risen with Christ,\n"
    .string "seek those things which are above,\l"
    .string "where Christ sitteth on the right\l"
    .string "hand of God.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_2::
    .string "Set your affection on things above,\n"
    .string "not on things on the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_3::
    .string "For ye are dead, and your life is\n"
    .string "hid with Christ in God.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_4::
    .string "When Christ, who is our life,\n"
    .string "shall appear, then shall ye also\l"
    .string "appear with him in glory.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_5::
    .string "Mortify therefore your members\n"
    .string "which are upon the earth;\l"
    .string "fornication, uncleanness,\l"
    .string "inordinate affection, evil\l"
    .string "concupiscence, and covetousness,\l"
    .string "which is idolatry:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_6::
    .string "For which things’ sake the wrath of\n"
    .string "God cometh on the children of\l"
    .string "disobedience:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_7::
    .string "In the which ye also walked some\n"
    .string "time, when ye lived in them$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_8::
    .string "But now ye also put off all these;\n"
    .string "anger, wrath, malice, blasphemy,\l"
    .string "filthy communication out of your\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_9::
    .string "Lie not one to another, seeing that\n"
    .string "ye have put off the old man with his\l"
    .string "deeds;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_10::
    .string "And have put on the new man, which\n"
    .string "is renewed in knowledge after the\l"
    .string "image of him that created him:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_11::
    .string "Where there is neither Greek nor\n"
    .string "Jew, circumcision nor\l"
    .string "uncircumcision, Barbarian, Scythian,\l"
    .string "bond nor free: but Christ is all,\l"
    .string "and in all$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_12::
    .string "Put on therefore, as the elect of\n"
    .string "God, holy and beloved, bowels of\l"
    .string "mercies, kindness, humbleness of\l"
    .string "mind, meekness, longsuffering;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_13::
    .string "Forbearing one another, and\n"
    .string "forgiving one another, if any man\l"
    .string "have a quarrel against any: even as\l"
    .string "Christ forgave you, so also do ye$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_14::
    .string "And above all these things put on\n"
    .string "charity, which is the bond of\l"
    .string "perfectness.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_15::
    .string "And let the peace of God rule in\n"
    .string "your hearts, to the which also ye are\l"
    .string "called in one body; and be ye\l"
    .string "thankful.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_16::
    .string "Let the word of Christ dwell in you\n"
    .string "richly in all wisdom; teaching and\l"
    .string "admonishing one another in psalms\l"
    .string "and hymns and spiritual songs,\l"
    .string "singing with grace in your hearts to\l"
    .string "the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_17::
    .string "And whatsoever ye do in word or\n"
    .string "deed, do all in the name of the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus, giving thanks to God and the\l"
    .string "Father by him.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_18::
    .string "Wives, submit yourselves unto your\n"
    .string "own husbands, as it is fit in the\l"
    .string "Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_19::
    .string "Husbands, love your wives, and be\n"
    .string "not bitter against them.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_20::
    .string "Children, obey your parents in\n"
    .string "all things: for this is well\l"
    .string "pleasing unto the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_21::
    .string "Fathers, provoke not your children\n"
    .string "to anger, lest they be discouraged.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_22::
    .string "Servants, obey in all things your\n"
    .string "masters according to the flesh; not\l"
    .string "with eyeservice, as menpleasers;\l"
    .string "but in singleness of heart, fearing\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_23::
    .string "And whatsoever ye do, do it\n"
    .string "heartily, as to the Lord, and not\l"
    .string "unto men;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_24::
    .string "Knowing that of the Lord ye shall\n"
    .string "receive the reward of the\l"
    .string "inheritance: for ye serve the Lord\l"
    .string "Christ$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_3_25::
    .string "But he that doeth wrong shall\n"
    .string "receive for the wrong which he hath\l"
    .string "done: and there is no respect of\l"
    .string "persons.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_1::
    .string "Masters, give unto your servants\n"
    .string "that which is just and equal;\l"
    .string "knowing that ye also have a Master\l"
    .string "in heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_2::
    .string "Continue in prayer, and watch in\n"
    .string "the same with thanksgiving;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_3::
    .string "Withal praying also for us, that\n"
    .string "God would open unto us a door of\l"
    .string "utterance, to speak the mystery of\l"
    .string "Christ, for which I am also in bonds:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_4::
    .string "That I may make it manifest, as I\n"
    .string "ought to speak$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_5::
    .string "Walk in wisdom toward them that are\n"
    .string "without, redeeming the time.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_6::
    .string "Let your speech be alway with\n"
    .string "grace, seasoned with salt, that ye\l"
    .string "may know how ye ought to answer every\l"
    .string "man.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_7::
    .string "All my state shall Tychicus\n"
    .string "declare unto you, who is a beloved\l"
    .string "brother, and a faithful minister and\l"
    .string "fellowservant in the Lord:"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_8::
    .string "Whom I have sent unto you for the\n"
    .string "same purpose, that he might know\l"
    .string "your estate, and comfort your hearts;"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_9::
    .string "With Onesimus, a faithful and\n"
    .string "beloved brother, who is one of you.\l"
    .string "They shall make known unto you all\l"
    .string "things which are done here$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_10::
    .string "Aristarchus my fellowprisoner\n"
    .string "saluteth you, and Marcus, sister’s\l"
    .string "son to Barnabas, (touching whom ye\l"
    .string "received commandments: if he come\l"
    .string "unto you, receive him;)"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_11::
    .string "And Jesus, which is called Justus,\n"
    .string "who are of the circumcision. These\l"
    .string "only are my fellowworkers unto the\l"
    .string "kingdom of God, which have been a\l"
    .string "comfort unto me$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_12::
    .string "Epaphras, who is one of you, a\n"
    .string "servant of Christ, saluteth you,\l"
    .string "always labouring fervently for you\l"
    .string "in prayers, that ye may stand\l"
    .string "perfect and complete in all the\l"
    .string "will of God.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_13::
    .string "For I bear him record, that he hath a\n"
    .string "great zeal for you, and them that are\l"
    .string "in Laodicea, and them in Hierapolis.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_14::
    .string "Luke, the beloved physician, and\n"
    .string "Demas, greet you.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_15::
    .string "Salute the brethren which are in\n"
    .string "Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the\l"
    .string "church which is in his house.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_16::
    .string "And when this epistle is read\n"
    .string "among you, cause that it be read also\l"
    .string "in the church of the Laodiceans; and\l"
    .string "that ye likewise read the epistle\l"
    .string "from Laodicea.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_17::
    .string "And say to Archippus, Take heed to\n"
    .string "the ministry which thou hast\l"
    .string "received in the Lord, that thou\l"
    .string "fulfil it.$"
Bible_Text_Colossians_4_18::
    .string "The salutation by the hand of me\n"
    .string "Paul. Remember my bonds. Grace be\l"
    .string "with you. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus,\n"
    .string "unto the church of the Thessalonians\l"
    .string "which is in God the Father and in the\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ: Grace be unto you,\l"
    .string "and peace, from God our Father, and\l"
    .string "the Lord Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_2::
    .string "We give thanks to God always for\n"
    .string "you all, making mention of you in\l"
    .string "our prayers;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_3::
    .string "Remembering without ceasing your\n"
    .string "work of faith, and labour of love,\l"
    .string "and patience of hope in our Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ, in the sight of God and\l"
    .string "our Father;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_4::
    .string "Knowing, brethren beloved, your\n"
    .string "election of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_5::
    .string "For our gospel came not unto you in\n"
    .string "word only, but also in power, and\l"
    .string "in the Holy Ghost, and in much\l"
    .string "assurance; as ye know what manner of\l"
    .string "men we were among you for your sake.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_6::
    .string "And ye became followers of us, and\n"
    .string "of the Lord, having received the word\l"
    .string "in much affliction, with joy of the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_7::
    .string "So that ye were ensamples to all\n"
    .string "that believe in Macedonia and Achaia.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_8::
    .string "For from you sounded out the word of\n"
    .string "the Lord not only in Macedonia and\l"
    .string "Achaia, but also in every place\l"
    .string "your faith to God-ward is spread\l"
    .string "abroad; so that we need not to speak\l"
    .string "any thing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_9::
    .string "For they themselves shew of us what\n"
    .string "manner of entering in we had unto\l"
    .string "you, and how ye turned to God from\l"
    .string "idols to serve the living and true\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_1_10::
    .string "And to wait for his Son from heaven,\n"
    .string "whom he raised from the dead, even\l"
    .string "Jesus, which delivered us from the\l"
    .string "wrath to come$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_1::
    .string "For yourselves, brethren, know our\n"
    .string "entrance in unto you, that it was not\l"
    .string "in vain:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_2::
    .string "But even after that we had suffered\n"
    .string "before, and were shamefully\l"
    .string "entreated, as ye know, at Philippi,\l"
    .string "we were bold in our God to speak\l"
    .string "unto you the gospel of God with much\l"
    .string "contention$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_3::
    .string "For our exhortation was not of\n"
    .string "deceit, nor of uncleanness, nor in\l"
    .string "guile:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_4::
    .string "But as we were allowed of God to be\n"
    .string "put in trust with the gospel, even\l"
    .string "so we speak; not as pleasing men,\l"
    .string "but God, which trieth our hearts$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_5::
    .string "For neither at any time used we\n"
    .string "flattering words, as ye know, nor a\l"
    .string "cloke of covetousness; God is\l"
    .string "witness:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_6::
    .string "Nor of men sought we glory, neither\n"
    .string "of you, nor yet of others, when we\l"
    .string "might have been burdensome, as the\l"
    .string "apostles of Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_7::
    .string "But we were gentle among you, even\n"
    .string "as a nurse cherisheth her children:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_8::
    .string "So being affectionately desirous\n"
    .string "of you, we were willing to have\l"
    .string "imparted unto you, not the gospel\l"
    .string "of God only, but also our own\l"
    .string "souls, because ye were dear unto us$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_9::
    .string "For ye remember, brethren, our\n"
    .string "labour and travail: for labouring\l"
    .string "night and day, because we would not\l"
    .string "be chargeable unto any of you, we\l"
    .string "preached unto you the gospel of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_10::
    .string "Ye are witnesses, and God also, how\n"
    .string "holily and justly and unblameably\l"
    .string "we behaved ourselves among you that\l"
    .string "believe:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_11::
    .string "As ye know how we exhorted and\n"
    .string "comforted and charged every one of\l"
    .string "you, as a father doth his children,"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_12::
    .string "That ye would walk worthy of God,\n"
    .string "who hath called you unto his\l"
    .string "kingdom and glory$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_13::
    .string "For this cause also thank we God\n"
    .string "without ceasing, because, when ye\l"
    .string "received the word of God which ye\l"
    .string "heard of us, ye received it not as the\l"
    .string "word of men, but as it is in truth,\l"
    .string "the word of God, which effectually\l"
    .string "worketh also in you that believe.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_14::
    .string "For ye, brethren, became followers\n"
    .string "of the churches of God which in\l"
    .string "Judaea are in Christ Jesus: for ye\l"
    .string "also have suffered like things of\l"
    .string "your own countrymen, even as they\l"
    .string "have of the Jews:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_15::
    .string "Who both killed the Lord Jesus, and\n"
    .string "their own prophets, and have\l"
    .string "persecuted us; and they please not\l"
    .string "God, and are contrary to all men:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_16::
    .string "Forbidding us to speak to the\n"
    .string "Gentiles that they might be saved,\l"
    .string "to fill up their sins alway: for\l"
    .string "the wrath is come upon them to the\l"
    .string "uttermost$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_17::
    .string "But we, brethren, being taken from\n"
    .string "you for a short time in presence, not\l"
    .string "in heart, endeavoured the more\l"
    .string "abundantly to see your face with\l"
    .string "great desire.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_18::
    .string "Wherefore we would have come unto\n"
    .string "you, even I Paul, once and again; but\l"
    .string "Satan hindered us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_19::
    .string "For what is our hope, or joy, or\n"
    .string "crown of rejoicing? Are not even ye\l"
    .string "in the presence of our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ at his coming?"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_2_20::
    .string "For ye are our glory and joy$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_1::
    .string "Wherefore when we could no longer\n"
    .string "forbear, we thought it good to be\l"
    .string "left at Athens alone;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_2::
    .string "And sent Timotheus, our brother, and\n"
    .string "minister of God, and our\l"
    .string "fellowlabourer in the gospel of\l"
    .string "Christ, to establish you, and to\l"
    .string "comfort you concerning your faith:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_3::
    .string "That no man should be moved by\n"
    .string "these afflictions: for yourselves\l"
    .string "know that we are appointed thereunto$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_4::
    .string "For verily, when we were with you,\n"
    .string "we told you before that we should\l"
    .string "suffer tribulation; even as it came\l"
    .string "to pass, and ye know.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_5::
    .string "For this cause, when I could no\n"
    .string "longer forbear, I sent to know your\l"
    .string "faith, lest by some means the\l"
    .string "tempter have tempted you, and our\l"
    .string "labour be in vain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_6::
    .string "But now when Timotheus came from you\n"
    .string "unto us, and brought us good tidings\l"
    .string "of your faith and charity, and that\l"
    .string "ye have good remembrance of us\l"
    .string "always, desiring greatly to see us,\l"
    .string "as we also to see you:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_7::
    .string "Therefore, brethren, we were\n"
    .string "comforted over you in all our\l"
    .string "affliction and distress by your\l"
    .string "faith:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_8::
    .string "For now we live, if ye stand fast in\n"
    .string "the Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_9::
    .string "For what thanks can we render to God\n"
    .string "again for you, for all the joy\l"
    .string "wherewith we joy for your sakes\l"
    .string "before our God;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_10::
    .string "Night and day praying exceedingly\n"
    .string "that we might see your face, and\l"
    .string "might perfect that which is lacking\l"
    .string "in your faith?"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_11::
    .string "Now God himself and our Father, and\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ, direct our way\l"
    .string "unto you$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_12::
    .string "And the Lord make you to increase\n"
    .string "and abound in love one toward\l"
    .string "another, and toward all men, even as\l"
    .string "we do toward you:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_3_13::
    .string "To the end he may stablish your\n"
    .string "hearts unblameable in holiness\l"
    .string "before God, even our Father, at the\l"
    .string "coming of our Lord Jesus Christ with\l"
    .string "all his saints$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_1::
    .string "Furthermore then we beseech you,\n"
    .string "brethren, and exhort you by the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus, that as ye have received of us\l"
    .string "how ye ought to walk and to please\l"
    .string "God, so ye would abound more and\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_2::
    .string "For ye know what commandments we\n"
    .string "gave you by the Lord Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_3::
    .string "For this is the will of God, even\n"
    .string "your sanctification, that ye should\l"
    .string "abstain from fornication:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_4::
    .string "That every one of you should know\n"
    .string "how to possess his vessel in\l"
    .string "sanctification and honour;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_5::
    .string "Not in the lust of concupiscence,\n"
    .string "even as the Gentiles which know not\l"
    .string "God:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_6::
    .string "That no man go beyond and defraud\n"
    .string "his brother in any matter: because\l"
    .string "that the Lord is the avenger of all\l"
    .string "such, as we also have forewarned you\l"
    .string "and testified$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_7::
    .string "For God hath not called us unto\n"
    .string "uncleanness, but unto holiness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_8::
    .string "He therefore that despiseth,\n"
    .string "despiseth not man, but God, who hath\l"
    .string "also given unto us his holy Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_9::
    .string "But as touching brotherly love ye\n"
    .string "need not that I write unto you: for ye\l"
    .string "yourselves are taught of God to\l"
    .string "love one another.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_10::
    .string "And indeed ye do it toward all the\n"
    .string "brethren which are in all\l"
    .string "Macedonia: but we beseech you,\l"
    .string "brethren, that ye increase more and\l"
    .string "more;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_11::
    .string "And that ye study to be quiet, and to\n"
    .string "do your own business, and to work\l"
    .string "with your own hands, as we commanded\l"
    .string "you;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_12::
    .string "That ye may walk honestly toward\n"
    .string "them that are without, and that ye\l"
    .string "may have lack of nothing$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_13::
    .string "But I would not have you to be\n"
    .string "ignorant, brethren, concerning them\l"
    .string "which are asleep, that ye sorrow\l"
    .string "not, even as others which have no\l"
    .string "hope.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_14::
    .string "For if we believe that Jesus died\n"
    .string "and rose again, even so them also\l"
    .string "which sleep in Jesus will God\l"
    .string "bring with him.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_15::
    .string "For this we say unto you by the word\n"
    .string "of the Lord, that we which are alive\l"
    .string "and remain unto the coming of the\l"
    .string "Lord shall not prevent them which\l"
    .string "are asleep.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_16::
    .string "For the Lord himself shall\n"
    .string "descend from heaven with a shout,\l"
    .string "with the voice of the archangel, and\l"
    .string "with the trump of God: and the dead\l"
    .string "in Christ shall rise first:"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_17::
    .string "Then we which are alive and remain\n"
    .string "shall be caught up together with\l"
    .string "them in the clouds, to meet the Lord\l"
    .string "in the air: and so shall we ever be\l"
    .string "with the Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_4_18::
    .string "Wherefore comfort one another with\n"
    .string "these words.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_1::
    .string "But of the times and the seasons,\n"
    .string "brethren, ye have no need that I\l"
    .string "write unto you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_2::
    .string "For yourselves know perfectly\n"
    .string "that the day of the Lord so cometh as\l"
    .string "a thief in the night.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_3::
    .string "For when they shall say, Peace and\n"
    .string "safety; then sudden destruction\l"
    .string "cometh upon them, as travail upon a\l"
    .string "woman with child; and they shall\l"
    .string "not escape.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_4::
    .string "But ye, brethren, are not in\n"
    .string "darkness, that that day should\l"
    .string "overtake you as a thief.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_5::
    .string "Ye are all the children of light,\n"
    .string "and the children of the day: we are\l"
    .string "not of the night, nor of darkness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_6::
    .string "Therefore let us not sleep, as do\n"
    .string "others; but let us watch and be\l"
    .string "sober.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_7::
    .string "For they that sleep sleep in the\n"
    .string "night; and they that be drunken are\l"
    .string "drunken in the night.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_8::
    .string "But let us, who are of the day, be\n"
    .string "sober, putting on the breastplate\l"
    .string "of faith and love; and for an\l"
    .string "helmet, the hope of salvation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_9::
    .string "For God hath not appointed us to\n"
    .string "wrath, but to obtain salvation by\l"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ,"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_10::
    .string "Who died for us, that, whether we\n"
    .string "wake or sleep, we should live\l"
    .string "together with him$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_11::
    .string "Wherefore comfort yourselves\n"
    .string "together, and edify one another, even\l"
    .string "as also ye do.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_12::
    .string "And we beseech you, brethren, to\n"
    .string "know them which labour among you,\l"
    .string "and are over you in the Lord, and\l"
    .string "admonish you;"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_13::
    .string "And to esteem them very highly in\n"
    .string "love for their work’s sake. And be at\l"
    .string "peace among yourselves$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_14::
    .string "Now we exhort you, brethren, warn\n"
    .string "them that are unruly, comfort the\l"
    .string "feebleminded, support the weak, be\l"
    .string "patient toward all men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_15::
    .string "See that none render evil for evil\n"
    .string "unto any man; but ever follow that\l"
    .string "which is good, both among\l"
    .string "yourselves, and to all men.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_16::
    .string "Rejoice evermore.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_17::
    .string "Pray without ceasing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_18::
    .string "In every thing give thanks: for this\n"
    .string "is the will of God in Christ Jesus\l"
    .string "concerning you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_19::
    .string "Quench not the Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_20::
    .string "Despise not prophesyings.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_21::
    .string "Prove all things; hold fast that\n"
    .string "which is good.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_22::
    .string "Abstain from all appearance of\n"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_23::
    .string "And the very God of peace sanctify\n"
    .string "you wholly; and I pray God your\l"
    .string "whole spirit and soul and body be\l"
    .string "preserved blameless unto the coming\l"
    .string "of our Lord Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_24::
    .string "Faithful is he that calleth you,\n"
    .string "who also will do it.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_25::
    .string "Brethren, pray for us.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_26::
    .string "Greet all the brethren with an\n"
    .string "holy kiss.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_27::
    .string "I charge you by the Lord that this\n"
    .string "epistle be read unto all the holy\l"
    .string "brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_Thessalonians_5_28::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_1::
    .string "Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus,\n"
    .string "unto the church of the Thessalonians\l"
    .string "in God our Father and the Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_2::
    .string "Grace unto you, and peace, from God\n"
    .string "our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_3::
    .string "We are bound to thank God always\n"
    .string "for you, brethren, as it is meet,\l"
    .string "because that your faith groweth\l"
    .string "exceedingly, and the charity of\l"
    .string "every one of you all toward each\l"
    .string "other aboundeth;"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_4::
    .string "So that we ourselves glory in you\n"
    .string "in the churches of God for your\l"
    .string "patience and faith in all your\l"
    .string "persecutions and tribulations that\l"
    .string "ye endure:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_5::
    .string "Which is a manifest token of the\n"
    .string "righteous judgment of God, that ye\l"
    .string "may be counted worthy of the kingdom\l"
    .string "of God, for which ye also suffer:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_6::
    .string "Seeing it is a righteous thing with\n"
    .string "God to recompense tribulation to\l"
    .string "them that trouble you;"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_7::
    .string "And to you who are troubled rest\n"
    .string "with us, when the Lord Jesus shall\l"
    .string "be revealed from heaven with his\l"
    .string "mighty angels,"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_8::
    .string "In flaming fire taking vengeance on\n"
    .string "them that know not God, and that obey\l"
    .string "not the gospel of our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_9::
    .string "Who shall be punished with\n"
    .string "everlasting destruction from the\l"
    .string "presence of the Lord, and from the\l"
    .string "glory of his power;"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_10::
    .string "When he shall come to be glorified\n"
    .string "in his saints, and to be admired in\l"
    .string "all them that believe (because our\l"
    .string "testimony among you was believed) in\l"
    .string "that day$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_11::
    .string "Wherefore also we pray always for\n"
    .string "you, that our God would count you\l"
    .string "worthy of this calling, and fulfil\l"
    .string "all the good pleasure of his\l"
    .string "goodness, and the work of faith with\l"
    .string "power:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_1_12::
    .string "That the name of our Lord Jesus\n"
    .string "Christ may be glorified in you, and\l"
    .string "ye in him, according to the grace of\l"
    .string "our God and the Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_1::
    .string "Now we beseech you, brethren, by the\n"
    .string "coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, and\l"
    .string "by our gathering together unto him,"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_2::
    .string "That ye be not soon shaken in mind,\n"
    .string "or be troubled, neither by spirit,\l"
    .string "nor by word, nor by letter as from\l"
    .string "us, as that the day of Christ is at\l"
    .string "hand$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_3::
    .string "Let no man deceive you by any means:\n"
    .string "for that day shall not come, except\l"
    .string "there come a falling away first, and\l"
    .string "that man of sin be revealed, the son\l"
    .string "of perdition;"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_4::
    .string "Who opposeth and exalteth\n"
    .string "himself above all that is called\l"
    .string "God, or that is worshipped; so that\l"
    .string "he as God sitteth in the temple of\l"
    .string "God, shewing himself that he is God$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_5::
    .string "Remember ye not, that, when I was\n"
    .string "yet with you, I told you these\l"
    .string "things?"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_6::
    .string "And now ye know what withholdeth\n"
    .string "that he might be revealed in his time$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_7::
    .string "For the mystery of iniquity doth\n"
    .string "already work: only he who now\l"
    .string "letteth will let, until he be\l"
    .string "taken out of the way.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_8::
    .string "And then shall that Wicked be\n"
    .string "revealed, whom the Lord shall\l"
    .string "consume with the spirit of his\l"
    .string "mouth, and shall destroy with the\l"
    .string "brightness of his coming:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_9::
    .string "Even him, whose coming is after the\n"
    .string "working of Satan with all power and\l"
    .string "signs and lying wonders,"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_10::
    .string "And with all deceivableness of\n"
    .string "unrighteousness in them that perish;\l"
    .string "because they received not the love\l"
    .string "of the truth, that they might be saved$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_11::
    .string "And for this cause God shall send\n"
    .string "them strong delusion, that they\l"
    .string "should believe a lie:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_12::
    .string "That they all might be damned who\n"
    .string "believed not the truth, but had\l"
    .string "pleasure in unrighteousness$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_13::
    .string "But we are bound to give thanks\n"
    .string "alway to God for you, brethren\l"
    .string "beloved of the Lord, because God\l"
    .string "hath from the beginning chosen you to\l"
    .string "salvation through sanctification of\l"
    .string "the Spirit and belief of the truth:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_14::
    .string "Whereunto he called you by our\n"
    .string "gospel, to the obtaining of the\l"
    .string "glory of our Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_15::
    .string "Therefore, brethren, stand fast, and\n"
    .string "hold the traditions which ye have\l"
    .string "been taught, whether by word, or our\l"
    .string "epistle.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_16::
    .string "Now our Lord Jesus Christ himself,\n"
    .string "and God, even our Father, which hath\l"
    .string "loved us, and hath given us\l"
    .string "everlasting consolation and good\l"
    .string "hope through grace,"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_2_17::
    .string "Comfort your hearts, and stablish\n"
    .string "you in every good word and work$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_1::
    .string "Finally, brethren, pray for us,\n"
    .string "that the word of the Lord may have\l"
    .string "free course, and be glorified, even\l"
    .string "as it is with you:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_2::
    .string "And that we may be delivered from\n"
    .string "unreasonable and wicked men: for\l"
    .string "all men have not faith$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_3::
    .string "But the Lord is faithful, who\n"
    .string "shall stablish you, and keep you\l"
    .string "from evil.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_4::
    .string "And we have confidence in the Lord\n"
    .string "touching you, that ye both do and\l"
    .string "will do the things which we command\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_5::
    .string "And the Lord direct your hearts into\n"
    .string "the love of God, and into the\l"
    .string "patient waiting for Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_6::
    .string "Now we command you, brethren, in the\n"
    .string "name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that\l"
    .string "ye withdraw yourselves from every\l"
    .string "brother that walketh disorderly,\l"
    .string "and not after the tradition which he\l"
    .string "received of us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_7::
    .string "For yourselves know how ye ought to\n"
    .string "follow us: for we behaved not\l"
    .string "ourselves disorderly among you;"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_8::
    .string "Neither did we eat any man’s bread\n"
    .string "for nought; but wrought with labour\l"
    .string "and travail night and day, that we\l"
    .string "might not be chargeable to any of\l"
    .string "you:"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_9::
    .string "Not because we have not power, but\n"
    .string "to make ourselves an ensample unto\l"
    .string "you to follow us$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_10::
    .string "For even when we were with you, this\n"
    .string "we commanded you, that if any would\l"
    .string "not work, neither should he eat.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_11::
    .string "For we hear that there are some\n"
    .string "which walk among you disorderly,\l"
    .string "working not at all, but are\l"
    .string "busybodies.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_12::
    .string "Now them that are such we command\n"
    .string "and exhort by our Lord Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "that with quietness they work, and\l"
    .string "eat their own bread.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_13::
    .string "But ye, brethren, be not weary in\n"
    .string "well doing.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_14::
    .string "And if any man obey not our word by\n"
    .string "this epistle, note that man, and\l"
    .string "have no company with him, that he may\l"
    .string "be ashamed.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_15::
    .string "Yet count him not as an enemy, but\n"
    .string "admonish him as a brother.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_16::
    .string "Now the Lord of peace himself give\n"
    .string "you peace always by all means. The\l"
    .string "Lord be with you all.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_17::
    .string "The salutation of Paul with mine\n"
    .string "own hand, which is the token in every\l"
    .string "epistle: so I write.$"
Bible_Text_2_Thessalonians_3_18::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "by the commandment of God our\l"
    .string "Saviour, and Lord Jesus Christ, which\l"
    .string "is our hope;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_2::
    .string "Unto Timothy, my own son in the\n"
    .string "faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from\l"
    .string "God our Father and Jesus Christ our\l"
    .string "Lord$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_3::
    .string "As I besought thee to abide still\n"
    .string "at Ephesus, when I went into\l"
    .string "Macedonia, that thou mightest charge\l"
    .string "some that they teach no other\l"
    .string "doctrine,"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_4::
    .string "Neither give heed to fables and\n"
    .string "endless genealogies, which minister\l"
    .string "questions, rather than godly\l"
    .string "edifying which is in faith: so do$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_5::
    .string "Now the end of the commandment is\n"
    .string "charity out of a pure heart, and of a\l"
    .string "good conscience, and of faith\l"
    .string "unfeigned:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_6::
    .string "From which some having swerved have\n"
    .string "turned aside unto vain jangling;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_7::
    .string "Desiring to be teachers of the law;\n"
    .string "understanding neither what they say,\l"
    .string "nor whereof they affirm$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_8::
    .string "But we know that the law is good, if\n"
    .string "a man use it lawfully;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_9::
    .string "Knowing this, that the law is not\n"
    .string "made for a righteous man, but for the\l"
    .string "lawless and disobedient, for the\l"
    .string "ungodly and for sinners, for unholy\l"
    .string "and profane, for murderers of\l"
    .string "fathers and murderers of mothers, for\l"
    .string "manslayers,"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_10::
    .string "For whoremongers, for them that\n"
    .string "defile themselves with mankind, for\l"
    .string "menstealers, for liars, for\l"
    .string "perjured persons, and if there be\l"
    .string "any other thing that is contrary to\l"
    .string "sound doctrine;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_11::
    .string "According to the glorious gospel\n"
    .string "of the blessed God, which was\l"
    .string "committed to my trust$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_12::
    .string "And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord,\n"
    .string "who hath enabled me, for that he\l"
    .string "counted me faithful, putting me\l"
    .string "into the ministry;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_13::
    .string "Who was before a blasphemer, and a\n"
    .string "persecutor, and injurious: but I\l"
    .string "obtained mercy, because I did it\l"
    .string "ignorantly in unbelief$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_14::
    .string "And the grace of our Lord was\n"
    .string "exceeding abundant with faith and\l"
    .string "love which is in Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_15::
    .string "This is a faithful saying, and\n"
    .string "worthy of all acceptation, that\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus came into the world to\l"
    .string "save sinners; of whom I am chief.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_16::
    .string "Howbeit for this cause I obtained\n"
    .string "mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ\l"
    .string "might shew forth all\l"
    .string "longsuffering, for a pattern to them\l"
    .string "which should hereafter believe on\l"
    .string "him to life everlasting.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_17::
    .string "Now unto the King eternal,\n"
    .string "immortal, invisible, the only wise\l"
    .string "God, be honour and glory for ever and\l"
    .string "ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_18::
    .string "This charge I commit unto thee, son\n"
    .string "Timothy, according to the\l"
    .string "prophecies which went before on\l"
    .string "thee, that thou by them mightest war\l"
    .string "a good warfare;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_19::
    .string "Holding faith, and a good\n"
    .string "conscience; which some having put\l"
    .string "away concerning faith have made\l"
    .string "shipwreck:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_1_20::
    .string "Of whom is Hymenaeus and Alexander;\n"
    .string "whom I have delivered unto Satan,\l"
    .string "that they may learn not to\l"
    .string "blaspheme$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_1::
    .string "I exhort therefore, that, first of\n"
    .string "all, supplications, prayers,\l"
    .string "intercessions, and giving of thanks,\l"
    .string "be made for all men;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_2::
    .string "For kings, and for all that are in\n"
    .string "authority; that we may lead a quiet\l"
    .string "and peaceable life in all\l"
    .string "godliness and honesty$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_3::
    .string "For this is good and acceptable in\n"
    .string "the sight of God our Saviour;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_4::
    .string "Who will have all men to be saved,\n"
    .string "and to come unto the knowledge of\l"
    .string "the truth$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_5::
    .string "For there is one God, and one\n"
    .string "mediator between God and men, the man\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_6::
    .string "Who gave himself a ransom for all,\n"
    .string "to be testified in due time$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_7::
    .string "Whereunto I am ordained a preacher,\n"
    .string "and an apostle, (I speak the truth\l"
    .string "in Christ, and lie not;) a teacher of\l"
    .string "the Gentiles in faith and verity.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_8::
    .string "I will therefore that men pray\n"
    .string "every where, lifting up holy hands,\l"
    .string "without wrath and doubting.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_9::
    .string "In like manner also, that women\n"
    .string "adorn themselves in modest\l"
    .string "apparel, with shamefacedness and\l"
    .string "sobriety; not with broided hair, or\l"
    .string "gold, or pearls, or costly array;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_10::
    .string "But (which becometh women\n"
    .string "professing godliness) with good\l"
    .string "works$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_11::
    .string "Let the woman learn in silence\n"
    .string "with all subjection.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_12::
    .string "But I suffer not a woman to teach,\n"
    .string "nor to usurp authority over the man,\l"
    .string "but to be in silence.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_13::
    .string "For Adam was first formed, then Eve.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_14::
    .string "And Adam was not deceived, but the\n"
    .string "woman being deceived was in the\l"
    .string "transgression.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_2_15::
    .string "Notwithstanding she shall be saved\n"
    .string "in childbearing, if they continue in\l"
    .string "faith and charity and holiness with\l"
    .string "sobriety.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_1::
    .string "This is a true saying, If a man\n"
    .string "desire the office of a bishop, he\l"
    .string "desireth a good work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_2::
    .string "A bishop then must be blameless,\n"
    .string "the husband of one wife, vigilant,\l"
    .string "sober, of good behaviour, given to\l"
    .string "hospitality, apt to teach;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_3::
    .string "Not given to wine, no striker, not\n"
    .string "greedy of filthy lucre; but\l"
    .string "patient, not a brawler, not\l"
    .string "covetous;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_4::
    .string "One that ruleth well his own\n"
    .string "house, having his children in\l"
    .string "subjection with all gravity;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_5::
    .string "(For if a man know not how to rule\n"
    .string "his own house, how shall he take\l"
    .string "care of the church of God?)"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_6::
    .string "Not a novice, lest being lifted up\n"
    .string "with pride he fall into the\l"
    .string "condemnation of the devil$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_7::
    .string "Moreover he must have a good report\n"
    .string "of them which are without; lest he\l"
    .string "fall into reproach and the snare of\l"
    .string "the devil.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_8::
    .string "Likewise must the deacons be grave,\n"
    .string "not doubletongued, not given to much\l"
    .string "wine, not greedy of filthy lucre;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_9::
    .string "Holding the mystery of the faith in\n"
    .string "a pure conscience$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_10::
    .string "And let these also first be\n"
    .string "proved; then let them use the office\l"
    .string "of a deacon, being found blameless.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_11::
    .string "Even so must their wives be grave,\n"
    .string "not slanderers, sober, faithful in\l"
    .string "all things.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_12::
    .string "Let the deacons be the husbands of\n"
    .string "one wife, ruling their children and\l"
    .string "their own houses well.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_13::
    .string "For they that have used the office\n"
    .string "of a deacon well purchase to\l"
    .string "themselves a good degree, and great\l"
    .string "boldness in the faith which is in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_14::
    .string "These things write I unto thee,\n"
    .string "hoping to come unto thee shortly:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_15::
    .string "But if I tarry long, that thou\n"
    .string "mayest know how thou oughtest to\l"
    .string "behave thyself in the house of God,\l"
    .string "which is the church of the living\l"
    .string "God, the pillar and ground of the\l"
    .string "truth$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_3_16::
    .string "And without controversy great is\n"
    .string "the mystery of godliness: God was\l"
    .string "manifest in the flesh, justified in\l"
    .string "the Spirit, seen of angels,\l"
    .string "preached unto the Gentiles,\l"
    .string "believed on in the world, received\l"
    .string "up into glory.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_1::
    .string "Now the Spirit speaketh\n"
    .string "expressly, that in the latter times\l"
    .string "some shall depart from the faith,\l"
    .string "giving heed to seducing spirits, and\l"
    .string "doctrines of devils;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_2::
    .string "Speaking lies in hypocrisy;\n"
    .string "having their conscience seared with\l"
    .string "a hot iron;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_3::
    .string "Forbidding to marry, and commanding\n"
    .string "to abstain from meats, which God hath\l"
    .string "created to be received with\l"
    .string "thanksgiving of them which believe\l"
    .string "and know the truth$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_4::
    .string "For every creature of God is good,\n"
    .string "and nothing to be refused, if it be\l"
    .string "received with thanksgiving:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_5::
    .string "For it is sanctified by the word of\n"
    .string "God and prayer$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_6::
    .string "If thou put the brethren in\n"
    .string "remembrance of these things, thou\l"
    .string "shalt be a good minister of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, nourished up in the words of\l"
    .string "faith and of good doctrine, whereunto\l"
    .string "thou hast attained.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_7::
    .string "But refuse profane and old wives’\n"
    .string "fables, and exercise thyself rather\l"
    .string "unto godliness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_8::
    .string "For bodily exercise profiteth\n"
    .string "little: but godliness is\l"
    .string "profitable unto all things, having\l"
    .string "promise of the life that now is, and\l"
    .string "of that which is to come.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_9::
    .string "This is a faithful saying and\n"
    .string "worthy of all acceptation.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_10::
    .string "For therefore we both labour and\n"
    .string "suffer reproach, because we trust in\l"
    .string "the living God, who is the Saviour of\l"
    .string "all men, specially of those that\l"
    .string "believe.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_11::
    .string "These things command and teach.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_12::
    .string "Let no man despise thy youth; but be\n"
    .string "thou an example of the believers,\l"
    .string "in word, in conversation, in charity,\l"
    .string "in spirit, in faith, in purity.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_13::
    .string "Till I come, give attendance to\n"
    .string "reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_14::
    .string "Neglect not the gift that is in\n"
    .string "thee, which was given thee by\l"
    .string "prophecy, with the laying on of the\l"
    .string "hands of the presbytery.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_15::
    .string "Meditate upon these things; give\n"
    .string "thyself wholly to them; that thy\l"
    .string "profiting may appear to all.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_4_16::
    .string "Take heed unto thyself, and unto\n"
    .string "the doctrine; continue in them: for\l"
    .string "in doing this thou shalt both save\l"
    .string "thyself, and them that hear thee.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_1::
    .string "Rebuke not an elder, but intreat\n"
    .string "him as a father; and the younger men\l"
    .string "as brethren;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_2::
    .string "The elder women as mothers; the\n"
    .string "younger as sisters, with all purity$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_3::
    .string "Honour widows that are widows\n"
    .string "indeed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_4::
    .string "But if any widow have children or\n"
    .string "nephews, let them learn first to\l"
    .string "shew piety at home, and to requite\l"
    .string "their parents: for that is good and\l"
    .string "acceptable before God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_5::
    .string "Now she that is a widow indeed, and\n"
    .string "desolate, trusteth in God, and\l"
    .string "continueth in supplications and\l"
    .string "prayers night and day.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_6::
    .string "But she that liveth in pleasure is\n"
    .string "dead while she liveth.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_7::
    .string "And these things give in charge,\n"
    .string "that they may be blameless.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_8::
    .string "But if any provide not for his own,\n"
    .string "and specially for those of his own\l"
    .string "house, he hath denied the faith, and\l"
    .string "is worse than an infidel.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_9::
    .string "Let not a widow be taken into the\n"
    .string "number under threescore years old,\l"
    .string "having been the wife of one man.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_10::
    .string "Well reported of for good works;\n"
    .string "if she have brought up children, if\l"
    .string "she have lodged strangers, if she\l"
    .string "have washed the saints’ feet, if she\l"
    .string "have relieved the afflicted, if she\l"
    .string "have diligently followed every\l"
    .string "good work.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_11::
    .string "But the younger widows refuse: for\n"
    .string "when they have begun to wax wanton\l"
    .string "against Christ, they will marry;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_12::
    .string "Having damnation, because they have\n"
    .string "cast off their first faith$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_13::
    .string "And withal they learn to be idle,\n"
    .string "wandering about from house to house;\l"
    .string "and not only idle, but tattlers\l"
    .string "also and busybodies, speaking\l"
    .string "things which they ought not.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_14::
    .string "I will therefore that the younger\n"
    .string "women marry, bear children, guide\l"
    .string "the house, give none occasion to the\l"
    .string "adversary to speak reproachfully.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_15::
    .string "For some are already turned aside\n"
    .string "after Satan.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_16::
    .string "If any man or woman that believeth\n"
    .string "have widows, let them relieve them,\l"
    .string "and let not the church be charged;\l"
    .string "that it may relieve them that are\l"
    .string "widows indeed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_17::
    .string "Let the elders that rule well be\n"
    .string "counted worthy of double honour,\l"
    .string "especially they who labour in the\l"
    .string "word and doctrine.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_18::
    .string "For the scripture saith, Thou\n"
    .string "shalt not muzzle the ox that\l"
    .string "treadeth out the corn. And, The\l"
    .string "labourer is worthy of his reward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_19::
    .string "Against an elder receive not an\n"
    .string "accusation, but before two or three\l"
    .string "witnesses.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_20::
    .string "Them that sin rebuke before all,\n"
    .string "that others also may fear.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_21::
    .string "I charge thee before God, and the\n"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ, and the elect\l"
    .string "angels, that thou observe these\l"
    .string "things without preferring one\l"
    .string "before another, doing nothing by\l"
    .string "partiality.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_22::
    .string "Lay hands suddenly on no man,\n"
    .string "neither be partaker of other men’s\l"
    .string "sins: keep thyself pure.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_23::
    .string "Drink no longer water, but use a\n"
    .string "little wine for thy stomach’s sake\l"
    .string "and thine often infirmities.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_24::
    .string "Some men’s sins are open\n"
    .string "beforehand, going before to\l"
    .string "judgment; and some men they follow\l"
    .string "after.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_5_25::
    .string "Likewise also the good works of\n"
    .string "some are manifest beforehand; and\l"
    .string "they that are otherwise cannot be hid.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_1::
    .string "Let as many servants as are under\n"
    .string "the yoke count their own masters\l"
    .string "worthy of all honour, that the name\l"
    .string "of God and his doctrine be not\l"
    .string "blasphemed.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_2::
    .string "And they that have believing\n"
    .string "masters, let them not despise them,\l"
    .string "because they are brethren; but rather\l"
    .string "do them service, because they are\l"
    .string "faithful and beloved, partakers of\l"
    .string "the benefit. These things teach and\l"
    .string "exhort.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_3::
    .string "If any man teach otherwise, and\n"
    .string "consent not to wholesome words, even\l"
    .string "the words of our Lord Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "and to the doctrine which is\l"
    .string "according to godliness;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_4::
    .string "He is proud, knowing nothing, but\n"
    .string "doting about questions and strifes\l"
    .string "of words, whereof cometh envy,\l"
    .string "strife, railings, evil surmisings,"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_5::
    .string "Perverse disputings of men of\n"
    .string "corrupt minds, and destitute of the\l"
    .string "truth, supposing that gain is\l"
    .string "godliness: from such withdraw\l"
    .string "thyself$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_6::
    .string "But godliness with contentment is\n"
    .string "great gain.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_7::
    .string "For we brought nothing into this\n"
    .string "world, and it is certain we can carry\l"
    .string "nothing out.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_8::
    .string "And having food and raiment let us\n"
    .string "be therewith content.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_9::
    .string "But they that will be rich fall\n"
    .string "into temptation and a snare, and\l"
    .string "into many foolish and hurtful\l"
    .string "lusts, which drown men in destruction\l"
    .string "and perdition.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_10::
    .string "For the love of money is the root of\n"
    .string "all evil: which while some coveted\l"
    .string "after, they have erred from the\l"
    .string "faith, and pierced themselves\l"
    .string "through with many sorrows.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_11::
    .string "But thou, O man of God, flee these\n"
    .string "things; and follow after\l"
    .string "righteousness, godliness, faith,\l"
    .string "love, patience, meekness.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_12::
    .string "Fight the good fight of faith, lay\n"
    .string "hold on eternal life, whereunto\l"
    .string "thou art also called, and hast\l"
    .string "professed a good profession before\l"
    .string "many witnesses.$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_13::
    .string "I give thee charge in the sight of\n"
    .string "God, who quickeneth all things, and\l"
    .string "before Christ Jesus, who before\l"
    .string "Pontius Pilate witnessed a good\l"
    .string "confession;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_14::
    .string "That thou keep this commandment\n"
    .string "without spot, unrebukable, until\l"
    .string "the appearing of our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_15::
    .string "Which in his times he shall shew,\n"
    .string "who is the blessed and only\l"
    .string "Potentate, the King of kings, and\l"
    .string "Lord of lords;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_16::
    .string "Who only hath immortality,\n"
    .string "dwelling in the light which no man\l"
    .string "can approach unto; whom no man hath\l"
    .string "seen, nor can see: to whom be honour\l"
    .string "and power everlasting. Amen$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_17::
    .string "Charge them that are rich in this\n"
    .string "world, that they be not highminded,\l"
    .string "nor trust in uncertain riches, but in\l"
    .string "the living God, who giveth us richly\l"
    .string "all things to enjoy;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_18::
    .string "That they do good, that they be rich\n"
    .string "in good works, ready to distribute,\l"
    .string "willing to communicate;"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_19::
    .string "Laying up in store for themselves\n"
    .string "a good foundation against the time to\l"
    .string "come, that they may lay hold on\l"
    .string "eternal life$"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_20::
    .string "O Timothy, keep that which is\n"
    .string "committed to thy trust, avoiding\l"
    .string "profane and vain babblings, and\l"
    .string "oppositions of science falsely so\l"
    .string "called:"
Bible_Text_1_Timothy_6_21::
    .string "Which some professing have erred\n"
    .string "concerning the faith. Grace be with\l"
    .string "thee. Amen$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_1::
    .string "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "by the will of God, according to the\l"
    .string "promise of life which is in Christ\l"
    .string "Jesus,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_2::
    .string "To Timothy, my dearly beloved son:\n"
    .string "Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the\l"
    .string "Father and Christ Jesus our Lord$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_3::
    .string "I thank God, whom I serve from my\n"
    .string "forefathers with pure conscience,\l"
    .string "that without ceasing I have\l"
    .string "remembrance of thee in my prayers\l"
    .string "night and day;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_4::
    .string "Greatly desiring to see thee, being\n"
    .string "mindful of thy tears, that I may be\l"
    .string "filled with joy;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_5::
    .string "When I call to remembrance the\n"
    .string "unfeigned faith that is in thee,\l"
    .string "which dwelt first in thy grandmother\l"
    .string "Lois, and thy mother Eunice; and I am\l"
    .string "persuaded that in thee also$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_6::
    .string "Wherefore I put thee in remembrance\n"
    .string "that thou stir up the gift of God,\l"
    .string "which is in thee by the putting on of\l"
    .string "my hands.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_7::
    .string "For God hath not given us the\n"
    .string "spirit of fear; but of power, and of\l"
    .string "love, and of a sound mind.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_8::
    .string "Be not thou therefore ashamed of the\n"
    .string "testimony of our Lord, nor of me his\l"
    .string "prisoner: but be thou partaker of\l"
    .string "the afflictions of the gospel\l"
    .string "according to the power of God;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_9::
    .string "Who hath saved us, and called us\n"
    .string "with an holy calling, not according\l"
    .string "to our works, but according to his\l"
    .string "own purpose and grace, which was\l"
    .string "given us in Christ Jesus before the\l"
    .string "world began,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_10::
    .string "But is now made manifest by the\n"
    .string "appearing of our Saviour Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, who hath abolished death,\l"
    .string "and hath brought life and\l"
    .string "immortality to light through the\l"
    .string "gospel:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_11::
    .string "Whereunto I am appointed a\n"
    .string "preacher, and an apostle, and a\l"
    .string "teacher of the Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_12::
    .string "For the which cause I also suffer\n"
    .string "these things: nevertheless I am not\l"
    .string "ashamed: for I know whom I have\l"
    .string "believed, and am persuaded that he\l"
    .string "is able to keep that which I have\l"
    .string "committed unto him against that day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_13::
    .string "Hold fast the form of sound words,\n"
    .string "which thou hast heard of me, in faith\l"
    .string "and love which is in Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_14::
    .string "That good thing which was committed\n"
    .string "unto thee keep by the Holy Ghost\l"
    .string "which dwelleth in us.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_15::
    .string "This thou knowest, that all they\n"
    .string "which are in Asia be turned away from\l"
    .string "me; of whom are Phygellus and\l"
    .string "Hermogenes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_16::
    .string "The Lord give mercy unto the house\n"
    .string "of Onesiphorus; for he oft refreshed\l"
    .string "me, and was not ashamed of my chain:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_17::
    .string "But, when he was in Rome, he sought\n"
    .string "me out very diligently, and found me$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_1_18::
    .string "The Lord grant unto him that he may\n"
    .string "find mercy of the Lord in that day:\l"
    .string "and in how many things he ministered\l"
    .string "unto me at Ephesus, thou knowest\l"
    .string "very well.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_1::
    .string "Thou therefore, my son, be strong in\n"
    .string "the grace that is in Christ Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_2::
    .string "And the things that thou hast heard\n"
    .string "of me among many witnesses, the same\l"
    .string "commit thou to faithful men, who\l"
    .string "shall be able to teach others also.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_3::
    .string "Thou therefore endure hardness, as a\n"
    .string "good soldier of Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_4::
    .string "No man that warreth entangleth\n"
    .string "himself with the affairs of this\l"
    .string "life; that he may please him who\l"
    .string "hath chosen him to be a soldier.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_5::
    .string "And if a man also strive for\n"
    .string "masteries, yet is he not crowned,\l"
    .string "except he strive lawfully.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_6::
    .string "The husbandman that laboureth must\n"
    .string "be first partaker of the fruits.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_7::
    .string "Consider what I say; and the Lord\n"
    .string "give thee understanding in all\l"
    .string "things.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_8::
    .string "Remember that Jesus Christ of the\n"
    .string "seed of David was raised from the\l"
    .string "dead according to my gospel:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_9::
    .string "Wherein I suffer trouble, as an\n"
    .string "evil doer, even unto bonds; but the\l"
    .string "word of God is not bound$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_10::
    .string "Therefore I endure all things for\n"
    .string "the elect’s sakes, that they may\l"
    .string "also obtain the salvation which is\l"
    .string "in Christ Jesus with eternal glory.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_11::
    .string "It is a faithful saying: For if we\n"
    .string "be dead with him, we shall also\l"
    .string "live with him:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_12::
    .string "If we suffer, we shall also reign\n"
    .string "with him: if we deny him, he also\l"
    .string "will deny us:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_13::
    .string "If we believe not, yet he abideth\n"
    .string "faithful: he cannot deny himself$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_14::
    .string "Of these things put them in\n"
    .string "remembrance, charging them before\l"
    .string "the Lord that they strive not about\l"
    .string "words to no profit, but to the\l"
    .string "subverting of the hearers.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_15::
    .string "Study to shew thyself approved\n"
    .string "unto God, a workman that needeth not\l"
    .string "to be ashamed, rightly dividing the\l"
    .string "word of truth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_16::
    .string "But shun profane and vain\n"
    .string "babblings: for they will increase\l"
    .string "unto more ungodliness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_17::
    .string "And their word will eat as doth a\n"
    .string "canker: of whom is Hymenaeus and\l"
    .string "Philetus;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_18::
    .string "Who concerning the truth have erred,\n"
    .string "saying that the resurrection is past\l"
    .string "already; and overthrow the faith of\l"
    .string "some$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_19::
    .string "Nevertheless the foundation of God\n"
    .string "standeth sure, having this seal, The\l"
    .string "Lord knoweth them that are his. And,\l"
    .string "Let every one that nameth the name of\l"
    .string "Christ depart from iniquity.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_20::
    .string "But in a great house there are not\n"
    .string "only vessels of gold and of\l"
    .string "silver, but also of wood and of\l"
    .string "earth; and some to honour, and some\l"
    .string "to dishonour.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_21::
    .string "If a man therefore purge himself\n"
    .string "from these, he shall be a vessel\l"
    .string "unto honour, sanctified, and meet for\l"
    .string "the master’s use, and prepared unto\l"
    .string "every good work.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_22::
    .string "Flee also youthful lusts: but\n"
    .string "follow righteousness, faith,\l"
    .string "charity, peace, with them that call\l"
    .string "on the Lord out of a pure heart.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_23::
    .string "But foolish and unlearned\n"
    .string "questions avoid, knowing that they do\l"
    .string "gender strifes.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_24::
    .string "And the servant of the Lord must not\n"
    .string "strive; but be gentle unto all men,\l"
    .string "apt to teach, patient,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_25::
    .string "In meekness instructing those that\n"
    .string "oppose themselves; if God\l"
    .string "peradventure will give them\l"
    .string "repentance to the acknowledging of\l"
    .string "the truth;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_2_26::
    .string "And that they may recover\n"
    .string "themselves out of the snare of the\l"
    .string "devil, who are taken captive by him\l"
    .string "at his will$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_1::
    .string "This know also, that in the last\n"
    .string "days perilous times shall come.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_2::
    .string "For men shall be lovers of their\n"
    .string "own selves, covetous, boasters,\l"
    .string "proud, blasphemers, disobedient to\l"
    .string "parents, unthankful, unholy,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_3::
    .string "Without natural affection,\n"
    .string "trucebreakers, false accusers,\l"
    .string "incontinent, fierce, despisers of\l"
    .string "those that are good,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_4::
    .string "Traitors, heady, highminded, lovers\n"
    .string "of pleasures more than lovers of\l"
    .string "God;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_5::
    .string "Having a form of godliness, but\n"
    .string "denying the power thereof: from such\l"
    .string "turn away$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_6::
    .string "For of this sort are they which\n"
    .string "creep into houses, and lead captive\l"
    .string "silly women laden with sins, led\l"
    .string "away with divers lusts,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_7::
    .string "Ever learning, and never able to\n"
    .string "come to the knowledge of the truth$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_8::
    .string "Now as Jannes and Jambres withstood\n"
    .string "Moses, so do these also resist the\l"
    .string "truth: men of corrupt minds,\l"
    .string "reprobate concerning the faith.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_9::
    .string "But they shall proceed no further:\n"
    .string "for their folly shall be manifest\l"
    .string "unto all men, as theirs also was.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_10::
    .string "But thou hast fully known my\n"
    .string "doctrine, manner of life, purpose,\l"
    .string "faith, longsuffering, charity,\l"
    .string "patience,"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_11::
    .string "Persecutions, afflictions, which\n"
    .string "came unto me at Antioch, at Iconium,\l"
    .string "at Lystra; what persecutions I\l"
    .string "endured: but out of them all the\l"
    .string "Lord delivered me$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_12::
    .string "Yea, and all that will live\n"
    .string "godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer\l"
    .string "persecution.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_13::
    .string "But evil men and seducers shall\n"
    .string "wax worse and worse, deceiving, and\l"
    .string "being deceived.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_14::
    .string "But continue thou in the things\n"
    .string "which thou hast learned and hast\l"
    .string "been assured of, knowing of whom thou\l"
    .string "hast learned them;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_15::
    .string "And that from a child thou hast\n"
    .string "known the holy scriptures, which\l"
    .string "are able to make thee wise unto\l"
    .string "salvation through faith which is in\l"
    .string "Christ Jesus$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_16::
    .string "All scripture is given by\n"
    .string "inspiration of God, and is\l"
    .string "profitable for doctrine, for\l"
    .string "reproof, for correction, for\l"
    .string "instruction in righteousness:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_3_17::
    .string "That the man of God may be perfect,\n"
    .string "throughly furnished unto all good\l"
    .string "works$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_1::
    .string "I charge thee therefore before God,\n"
    .string "and the Lord Jesus Christ, who shall\l"
    .string "judge the quick and the dead at his\l"
    .string "appearing and his kingdom;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_2::
    .string "Preach the word; be instant in\n"
    .string "season, out of season; reprove,\l"
    .string "rebuke, exhort with all\l"
    .string "longsuffering and doctrine$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_3::
    .string "For the time will come when they\n"
    .string "will not endure sound doctrine; but\l"
    .string "after their own lusts shall they\l"
    .string "heap to themselves teachers, having\l"
    .string "itching ears;"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_4::
    .string "And they shall turn away their\n"
    .string "ears from the truth, and shall be\l"
    .string "turned unto fables$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_5::
    .string "But watch thou in all things,\n"
    .string "endure afflictions, do the work of\l"
    .string "an evangelist, make full proof of\l"
    .string "thy ministry.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_6::
    .string "For I am now ready to be offered, and\n"
    .string "the time of my departure is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_7::
    .string "I have fought a good fight, I have\n"
    .string "finished my course, I have kept the\l"
    .string "faith:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_8::
    .string "Henceforth there is laid up for me\n"
    .string "a crown of righteousness, which the\l"
    .string "Lord, the righteous judge, shall\l"
    .string "give me at that day: and not to me\l"
    .string "only, but unto all them also that\l"
    .string "love his appearing$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_9::
    .string "Do thy diligence to come shortly\n"
    .string "unto me:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_10::
    .string "For Demas hath forsaken me, having\n"
    .string "loved this present world, and is\l"
    .string "departed unto Thessalonica;\l"
    .string "Crescens to Galatia, Titus unto\l"
    .string "Dalmatia$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_11::
    .string "Only Luke is with me. Take Mark, and\n"
    .string "bring him with thee: for he is\l"
    .string "profitable to me for the ministry.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_12::
    .string "And Tychicus have I sent to Ephesus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_13::
    .string "The cloke that I left at Troas with\n"
    .string "Carpus, when thou comest, bring with\l"
    .string "thee, and the books, but especially\l"
    .string "the parchments.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_14::
    .string "Alexander the coppersmith did me\n"
    .string "much evil: the Lord reward him\l"
    .string "according to his works:"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_15::
    .string "Of whom be thou ware also; for he\n"
    .string "hath greatly withstood our words$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_16::
    .string "At my first answer no man stood with\n"
    .string "me, but all men forsook me: I pray\l"
    .string "God that it may not be laid to their\l"
    .string "charge.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_17::
    .string "Notwithstanding the Lord stood with\n"
    .string "me, and strengthened me; that by me\l"
    .string "the preaching might be fully known,\l"
    .string "and that all the Gentiles might\l"
    .string "hear: and I was delivered out of the\l"
    .string "mouth of the lion.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_18::
    .string "And the Lord shall deliver me from\n"
    .string "every evil work, and will preserve\l"
    .string "me unto his heavenly kingdom: to\l"
    .string "whom be glory for ever and ever.\l"
    .string "Amen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_19::
    .string "Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the\n"
    .string "household of Onesiphorus.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_20::
    .string "Erastus abode at Corinth: but\n"
    .string "Trophimus have I left at Miletum\l"
    .string "sick.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_21::
    .string "Do thy diligence to come before\n"
    .string "winter. Eubulus greeteth thee, and\l"
    .string "Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and\l"
    .string "all the brethren.$"
Bible_Text_2_Timothy_4_22::
    .string "The Lord Jesus Christ be with thy\n"
    .string "spirit. Grace be with you. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_1::
    .string "Paul, a servant of God, and an\n"
    .string "apostle of Jesus Christ, according\l"
    .string "to the faith of God’s elect, and the\l"
    .string "acknowledging of the truth which is\l"
    .string "after godliness;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_2::
    .string "In hope of eternal life, which\n"
    .string "God, that cannot lie, promised\l"
    .string "before the world began;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_3::
    .string "But hath in due times manifested his\n"
    .string "word through preaching, which is\l"
    .string "committed unto me according to the\l"
    .string "commandment of God our Saviour;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_4::
    .string "To Titus, mine own son after the\n"
    .string "common faith: Grace, mercy, and\l"
    .string "peace, from God the Father and the\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_5::
    .string "For this cause left I thee in Crete,\n"
    .string "that thou shouldest set in order the\l"
    .string "things that are wanting, and ordain\l"
    .string "elders in every city, as I had\l"
    .string "appointed thee:"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_6::
    .string "If any be blameless, the husband of\n"
    .string "one wife, having faithful children\l"
    .string "not accused of riot or unruly$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_7::
    .string "For a bishop must be blameless, as\n"
    .string "the steward of God; not selfwilled,\l"
    .string "not soon angry, not given to wine, no\l"
    .string "striker, not given to filthy lucre;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_8::
    .string "But a lover of hospitality, a\n"
    .string "lover of good men, sober, just, holy,\l"
    .string "temperate;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_9::
    .string "Holding fast the faithful word as\n"
    .string "he hath been taught, that he may be\l"
    .string "able by sound doctrine both to\l"
    .string "exhort and to convince the gainsayers$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_10::
    .string "For there are many unruly and vain\n"
    .string "talkers and deceivers, specially\l"
    .string "they of the circumcision:"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_11::
    .string "Whose mouths must be stopped, who\n"
    .string "subvert whole houses, teaching\l"
    .string "things which they ought not, for\l"
    .string "filthy lucre’s sake$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_12::
    .string "One of themselves, even a prophet\n"
    .string "of their own, said, The Cretians are\l"
    .string "alway liars, evil beasts, slow\l"
    .string "bellies.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_13::
    .string "This witness is true. Wherefore\n"
    .string "rebuke them sharply, that they may\l"
    .string "be sound in the faith;"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_14::
    .string "Not giving heed to Jewish fables,\n"
    .string "and commandments of men, that turn\l"
    .string "from the truth$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_15::
    .string "Unto the pure all things are\n"
    .string "pure: but unto them that are defiled\l"
    .string "and unbelieving is nothing pure;\l"
    .string "but even their mind and conscience is\l"
    .string "defiled.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_1_16::
    .string "They profess that they know God;\n"
    .string "but in works they deny him, being\l"
    .string "abominable, and disobedient, and\l"
    .string "unto every good work reprobate.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_1::
    .string "But speak thou the things which\n"
    .string "become sound doctrine:"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_2::
    .string "That the aged men be sober, grave,\n"
    .string "temperate, sound in faith, in\l"
    .string "charity, in patience$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_3::
    .string "The aged women likewise, that they\n"
    .string "be in behaviour as becometh\l"
    .string "holiness, not false accusers, not\l"
    .string "given to much wine, teachers of good\l"
    .string "things;"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_4::
    .string "That they may teach the young women\n"
    .string "to be sober, to love their husbands,\l"
    .string "to love their children,"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_5::
    .string "To be discreet, chaste, keepers at\n"
    .string "home, good, obedient to their own\l"
    .string "husbands, that the word of God be not\l"
    .string "blasphemed$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_6::
    .string "Young men likewise exhort to be\n"
    .string "sober minded.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_7::
    .string "In all things shewing thyself a\n"
    .string "pattern of good works: in doctrine\l"
    .string "shewing uncorruptness, gravity,\l"
    .string "sincerity,"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_8::
    .string "Sound speech, that cannot be\n"
    .string "condemned; that he that is of the\l"
    .string "contrary part may be ashamed, having\l"
    .string "no evil thing to say of you$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_9::
    .string "Exhort servants to be obedient unto\n"
    .string "their own masters, and to please\l"
    .string "them well in all things; not\l"
    .string "answering again;"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_10::
    .string "Not purloining, but shewing all\n"
    .string "good fidelity; that they may adorn\l"
    .string "the doctrine of God our Saviour in\l"
    .string "all things$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_11::
    .string "For the grace of God that bringeth\n"
    .string "salvation hath appeared to all\l"
    .string "men,"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_12::
    .string "Teaching us that, denying\n"
    .string "ungodliness and worldly lusts, we\l"
    .string "should live soberly, righteously,\l"
    .string "and godly, in this present world;"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_13::
    .string "Looking for that blessed hope, and\n"
    .string "the glorious appearing of the\l"
    .string "great God and our Saviour Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ;"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_14::
    .string "Who gave himself for us, that he\n"
    .string "might redeem us from all iniquity,\l"
    .string "and purify unto himself a peculiar\l"
    .string "people, zealous of good works$"
Bible_Text_Titus_2_15::
    .string "These things speak, and exhort, and\n"
    .string "rebuke with all authority. Let no\l"
    .string "man despise thee.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_1::
    .string "Put them in mind to be subject to\n"
    .string "principalities and powers, to obey\l"
    .string "magistrates, to be ready to every\l"
    .string "good work,"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_2::
    .string "To speak evil of no man, to be no\n"
    .string "brawlers, but gentle, shewing all\l"
    .string "meekness unto all men$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_3::
    .string "For we ourselves also were\n"
    .string "sometimes foolish, disobedient,\l"
    .string "deceived, serving divers lusts and\l"
    .string "pleasures, living in malice and\l"
    .string "envy, hateful, and hating one\l"
    .string "another.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_4::
    .string "But after that the kindness and\n"
    .string "love of God our Saviour toward man\l"
    .string "appeared,"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_5::
    .string "Not by works of righteousness which\n"
    .string "we have done, but according to his\l"
    .string "mercy he saved us, by the washing of\l"
    .string "regeneration, and renewing of the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost;"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_6::
    .string "Which he shed on us abundantly\n"
    .string "through Jesus Christ our Saviour;"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_7::
    .string "That being justified by his grace,\n"
    .string "we should be made heirs according to\l"
    .string "the hope of eternal life$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_8::
    .string "This is a faithful saying, and\n"
    .string "these things I will that thou\l"
    .string "affirm constantly, that they which\l"
    .string "have believed in God might be\l"
    .string "careful to maintain good works.\l"
    .string "These things are good and\l"
    .string "profitable unto men.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_9::
    .string "But avoid foolish questions, and\n"
    .string "genealogies, and contentions, and\l"
    .string "strivings about the law; for they\l"
    .string "are unprofitable and vain.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_10::
    .string "A man that is an heretick after the\n"
    .string "first and second admonition reject;"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_11::
    .string "Knowing that he that is such is\n"
    .string "subverted, and sinneth, being\l"
    .string "condemned of himself$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_12::
    .string "When I shall send Artemas unto\n"
    .string "thee, or Tychicus, be diligent to\l"
    .string "come unto me to Nicopolis: for I\l"
    .string "have determined there to winter.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_13::
    .string "Bring Zenas the lawyer and\n"
    .string "Apollos on their journey\l"
    .string "diligently, that nothing be wanting\l"
    .string "unto them.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_14::
    .string "And let ours also learn to\n"
    .string "maintain good works for necessary\l"
    .string "uses, that they be not unfruitful.$"
Bible_Text_Titus_3_15::
    .string "All that are with me salute thee.\n"
    .string "Greet them that love us in the faith.\l"
    .string "Grace be with you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_1::
    .string "Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "and Timothy our brother, unto\l"
    .string "Philemon our dearly beloved, and\l"
    .string "fellowlabourer,"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_2::
    .string "And to our beloved Apphia, and\n"
    .string "Archippus our fellowsoldier, and\l"
    .string "to the church in thy house:"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_3::
    .string "Grace to you, and peace, from God\n"
    .string "our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_4::
    .string "I thank my God, making mention of\n"
    .string "thee always in my prayers,"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_5::
    .string "Hearing of thy love and faith,\n"
    .string "which thou hast toward the Lord\l"
    .string "Jesus, and toward all saints;"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_6::
    .string "That the communication of thy faith\n"
    .string "may become effectual by the\l"
    .string "acknowledging of every good thing\l"
    .string "which is in you in Christ Jesus$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_7::
    .string "For we have great joy and\n"
    .string "consolation in thy love, because\l"
    .string "the bowels of the saints are\l"
    .string "refreshed by thee, brother.$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_8::
    .string "Wherefore, though I might be much\n"
    .string "bold in Christ to enjoin thee that\l"
    .string "which is convenient,"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_9::
    .string "Yet for love’s sake I rather\n"
    .string "beseech thee, being such an one as\l"
    .string "Paul the aged, and now also a\l"
    .string "prisoner of Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_10::
    .string "I beseech thee for my son Onesimus,\n"
    .string "whom I have begotten in my bonds:"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_11::
    .string "Which in time past was to thee\n"
    .string "unprofitable, but now profitable\l"
    .string "to thee and to me:"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_12::
    .string "Whom I have sent again: thou\n"
    .string "therefore receive him, that is, mine\l"
    .string "own bowels:"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_13::
    .string "Whom I would have retained with me,\n"
    .string "that in thy stead he might have\l"
    .string "ministered unto me in the bonds of\l"
    .string "the gospel:"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_14::
    .string "But without thy mind would I do\n"
    .string "nothing; that thy benefit should not\l"
    .string "be as it were of necessity, but\l"
    .string "willingly$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_15::
    .string "For perhaps he therefore departed\n"
    .string "for a season, that thou shouldest\l"
    .string "receive him for ever;"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_16::
    .string "Not now as a servant, but above a\n"
    .string "servant, a brother beloved,\l"
    .string "specially to me, but how much more\l"
    .string "unto thee, both in the flesh, and in\l"
    .string "the Lord?"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_17::
    .string "If thou count me therefore a\n"
    .string "partner, receive him as myself$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_18::
    .string "If he hath wronged thee, or oweth\n"
    .string "thee ought, put that on mine\l"
    .string "account;"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_19::
    .string "I Paul have written it with mine\n"
    .string "own hand, I will repay it: albeit I\l"
    .string "do not say to thee how thou owest\l"
    .string "unto me even thine own self besides$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_20::
    .string "Yea, brother, let me have joy of\n"
    .string "thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels\l"
    .string "in the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_21::
    .string "Having confidence in thy obedience\n"
    .string "I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou\l"
    .string "wilt also do more than I say.$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_22::
    .string "But withal prepare me also a\n"
    .string "lodging: for I trust that through\l"
    .string "your prayers I shall be given unto\l"
    .string "you.$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_23::
    .string "There salute thee Epaphras, my\n"
    .string "fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_24::
    .string "Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas,\n"
    .string "my fellowlabourers$"
Bible_Text_Philemon_1_25::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with your spirit. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_1::
    .string "God, who at sundry times and in\n"
    .string "divers manners spake in time past\l"
    .string "unto the fathers by the prophets,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_2::
    .string "Hath in these last days spoken\n"
    .string "unto us by his Son, whom he hath\l"
    .string "appointed heir of all things, by\l"
    .string "whom also he made the worlds;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_3::
    .string "Who being the brightness of his\n"
    .string "glory, and the express image of his\l"
    .string "person, and upholding all things\l"
    .string "by the word of his power, when he had\l"
    .string "by himself purged our sins, sat down\l"
    .string "on the right hand of the Majesty on\l"
    .string "high:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_4::
    .string "Being made so much better than the\n"
    .string "angels, as he hath by inheritance\l"
    .string "obtained a more excellent name than\l"
    .string "they$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_5::
    .string "For unto which of the angels said\n"
    .string "he at any time, Thou art my Son, this\l"
    .string "day have I begotten thee? And again,\l"
    .string "I will be to him a Father, and he\l"
    .string "shall be to me a Son?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_6::
    .string "And again, when he bringeth in the\n"
    .string "firstbegotten into the world, he\l"
    .string "saith, And let all the angels of\l"
    .string "God worship him$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_7::
    .string "And of the angels he saith, Who\n"
    .string "maketh his angels spirits, and his\l"
    .string "ministers a flame of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_8::
    .string "But unto the Son he saith, Thy\n"
    .string "throne, O God, is for ever and ever: a\l"
    .string "sceptre of righteousness is the\l"
    .string "sceptre of thy kingdom.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_9::
    .string "Thou hast loved righteousness, and\n"
    .string "hated iniquity; therefore God, even\l"
    .string "thy God, hath anointed thee with the\l"
    .string "oil of gladness above thy fellows.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_10::
    .string "And, Thou, Lord, in the beginning\n"
    .string "hast laid the foundation of the\l"
    .string "earth; and the heavens are the works\l"
    .string "of thine hands:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_11::
    .string "They shall perish; but thou\n"
    .string "remainest; and they all shall wax\l"
    .string "old as doth a garment;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_12::
    .string "And as a vesture shalt thou fold\n"
    .string "them up, and they shall be changed:\l"
    .string "but thou art the same, and thy years\l"
    .string "shall not fail$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_13::
    .string "But to which of the angels said he\n"
    .string "at any time, Sit on my right hand,\l"
    .string "until I make thine enemies thy\l"
    .string "footstool?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_1_14::
    .string "Are they not all ministering\n"
    .string "spirits, sent forth to minister for\l"
    .string "them who shall be heirs of\l"
    .string "salvation?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_1::
    .string "Therefore we ought to give the more\n"
    .string "earnest heed to the things which we\l"
    .string "have heard, lest at any time we\l"
    .string "should let them slip$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_2::
    .string "For if the word spoken by angels\n"
    .string "was stedfast, and every\l"
    .string "transgression and disobedience\l"
    .string "received a just recompence of\l"
    .string "reward;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_3::
    .string "How shall we escape, if we\n"
    .string "neglect so great salvation; which\l"
    .string "at the first began to be spoken by\l"
    .string "the Lord, and was confirmed unto us\l"
    .string "by them that heard him;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_4::
    .string "God also bearing them witness, both\n"
    .string "with signs and wonders, and with\l"
    .string "divers miracles, and gifts of the\l"
    .string "Holy Ghost, according to his own\l"
    .string "will?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_5::
    .string "For unto the angels hath he not put\n"
    .string "in subjection the world to come,\l"
    .string "whereof we speak$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_6::
    .string "But one in a certain place\n"
    .string "testified, saying, What is man, that\l"
    .string "thou art mindful of him? or the son\l"
    .string "of man that thou visitest him?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_7::
    .string "Thou madest him a little lower\n"
    .string "than the angels; thou crownedst him\l"
    .string "with glory and honour, and didst set\l"
    .string "him over the works of thy hands:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_8::
    .string "Thou hast put all things in\n"
    .string "subjection under his feet. For in\l"
    .string "that he put all in subjection under\l"
    .string "him, he left nothing that is not put\l"
    .string "under him But now we see not yet all\l"
    .string "things put under him.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_9::
    .string "But we see Jesus, who was made a\n"
    .string "little lower than the angels for\l"
    .string "the suffering of death, crowned with\l"
    .string "glory and honour; that he by the\l"
    .string "grace of God should taste death for\l"
    .string "every man.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_10::
    .string "For it became him, for whom are all\n"
    .string "things, and by whom are all things,\l"
    .string "in bringing many sons unto glory, to\l"
    .string "make the captain of their salvation\l"
    .string "perfect through sufferings.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_11::
    .string "For both he that sanctifieth and\n"
    .string "they who are sanctified are all of\l"
    .string "one: for which cause he is not\l"
    .string "ashamed to call them brethren,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_12::
    .string "Saying, I will declare thy name\n"
    .string "unto my brethren, in the midst of the\l"
    .string "church will I sing praise unto thee$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_13::
    .string "And again, I will put my trust in\n"
    .string "him. And again, Behold I and the\l"
    .string "children which God hath given me.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_14::
    .string "Forasmuch then as the children are\n"
    .string "partakers of flesh and blood, he\l"
    .string "also himself likewise took part of\l"
    .string "the same; that through death he might\l"
    .string "destroy him that had the power of\l"
    .string "death, that is, the devil;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_15::
    .string "And deliver them who through fear\n"
    .string "of death were all their lifetime\l"
    .string "subject to bondage$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_16::
    .string "For verily he took not on him the\n"
    .string "nature of angels; but he took on him\l"
    .string "the seed of Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_17::
    .string "Wherefore in all things it behoved\n"
    .string "him to be made like unto his\l"
    .string "brethren, that he might be a\l"
    .string "merciful and faithful high priest\l"
    .string "in things pertaining to God, to make\l"
    .string "reconciliation for the sins of the\l"
    .string "people.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_2_18::
    .string "For in that he himself hath\n"
    .string "suffered being tempted, he is able\l"
    .string "to succour them that are tempted.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_1::
    .string "Wherefore, holy brethren,\n"
    .string "partakers of the heavenly calling,\l"
    .string "consider the Apostle and High\l"
    .string "Priest of our profession, Christ\l"
    .string "Jesus;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_2::
    .string "Who was faithful to him that\n"
    .string "appointed him, as also Moses was\l"
    .string "faithful in all his house$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_3::
    .string "For this man was counted worthy of\n"
    .string "more glory than Moses, inasmuch as\l"
    .string "he who hath builded the house hath\l"
    .string "more honour than the house.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_4::
    .string "For every house is builded by some\n"
    .string "man; but he that built all things\l"
    .string "is God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_5::
    .string "And Moses verily was faithful in\n"
    .string "all his house, as a servant, for a\l"
    .string "testimony of those things which were\l"
    .string "to be spoken after;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_6::
    .string "But Christ as a son over his own\n"
    .string "house; whose house are we, if we hold\l"
    .string "fast the confidence and the\l"
    .string "rejoicing of the hope firm unto the\l"
    .string "end$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_7::
    .string "Wherefore (as the Holy Ghost saith,\n"
    .string "To day if ye will hear his voice,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_8::
    .string "Harden not your hearts, as in the\n"
    .string "provocation, in the day of\l"
    .string "temptation in the wilderness:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_9::
    .string "When your fathers tempted me,\n"
    .string "proved me, and saw my works forty\l"
    .string "years$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_10::
    .string "Wherefore I was grieved with that\n"
    .string "generation, and said, They do alway\l"
    .string "err in their heart; and they have not\l"
    .string "known my ways.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_11::
    .string "So I sware in my wrath, They shall\n"
    .string "not enter into my rest.)"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_12::
    .string "Take heed, brethren, lest there be\n"
    .string "in any of you an evil heart of\l"
    .string "unbelief, in departing from the\l"
    .string "living God$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_13::
    .string "But exhort one another daily,\n"
    .string "while it is called To day; lest any\l"
    .string "of you be hardened through the\l"
    .string "deceitfulness of sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_14::
    .string "For we are made partakers of\n"
    .string "Christ, if we hold the beginning of\l"
    .string "our confidence stedfast unto the end;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_15::
    .string "While it is said, To day if ye will\n"
    .string "hear his voice, harden not your\l"
    .string "hearts, as in the provocation$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_16::
    .string "For some, when they had heard, did\n"
    .string "provoke: howbeit not all that came\l"
    .string "out of Egypt by Moses.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_17::
    .string "But with whom was he grieved forty\n"
    .string "years? was it not with them that had\l"
    .string "sinned, whose carcases fell in the\l"
    .string "wilderness?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_18::
    .string "And to whom sware he that they\n"
    .string "should not enter into his rest, but\l"
    .string "to them that believed not?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_3_19::
    .string "So we see that they could not enter\n"
    .string "in because of unbelief$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_1::
    .string "Let us therefore fear, lest, a\n"
    .string "promise being left us of entering\l"
    .string "into his rest, any of you should seem\l"
    .string "to come short of it.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_2::
    .string "For unto us was the gospel\n"
    .string "preached, as well as unto them: but\l"
    .string "the word preached did not profit\l"
    .string "them, not being mixed with faith in\l"
    .string "them that heard it.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_3::
    .string "For we which have believed do enter\n"
    .string "into rest, as he said, As I have sworn\l"
    .string "in my wrath, if they shall enter\l"
    .string "into my rest: although the works\l"
    .string "were finished from the foundation of\l"
    .string "the world.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_4::
    .string "For he spake in a certain place of\n"
    .string "the seventh day on this wise, And God\l"
    .string "did rest the seventh day from all\l"
    .string "his works.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_5::
    .string "And in this place again, If they\n"
    .string "shall enter into my rest.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_6::
    .string "Seeing therefore it remaineth that\n"
    .string "some must enter therein, and they to\l"
    .string "whom it was first preached entered\l"
    .string "not in because of unbelief:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_7::
    .string "Again, he limiteth a certain day,\n"
    .string "saying in David, To day, after so\l"
    .string "long a time; as it is said, To day if\l"
    .string "ye will hear his voice, harden not\l"
    .string "your hearts$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_8::
    .string "For if Jesus had given them rest,\n"
    .string "then would he not afterward have\l"
    .string "spoken of another day.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_9::
    .string "There remaineth therefore a rest to\n"
    .string "the people of God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_10::
    .string "For he that is entered into his\n"
    .string "rest, he also hath ceased from his\l"
    .string "own works, as God did from his.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_11::
    .string "Let us labour therefore to enter\n"
    .string "into that rest, lest any man fall\l"
    .string "after the same example of unbelief.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_12::
    .string "For the word of God is quick, and\n"
    .string "powerful, and sharper than any\l"
    .string "twoedged sword, piercing even to the\l"
    .string "dividing asunder of soul and\l"
    .string "spirit, and of the joints and\l"
    .string "marrow, and is a discerner of the\l"
    .string "thoughts and intents of the heart.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_13::
    .string "Neither is there any creature that\n"
    .string "is not manifest in his sight: but\l"
    .string "all things are naked and opened\l"
    .string "unto the eyes of him with whom we\l"
    .string "have to do.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_14::
    .string "Seeing then that we have a great\n"
    .string "high priest, that is passed into the\l"
    .string "heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us\l"
    .string "hold fast our profession.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_15::
    .string "For we have not an high priest\n"
    .string "which cannot be touched with the\l"
    .string "feeling of our infirmities; but was\l"
    .string "in all points tempted like as we\l"
    .string "are, yet without sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_4_16::
    .string "Let us therefore come boldly unto\n"
    .string "the throne of grace, that we may\l"
    .string "obtain mercy, and find grace to help\l"
    .string "in time of need.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_1::
    .string "For every high priest taken from\n"
    .string "among men is ordained for men in\l"
    .string "things pertaining to God, that he\l"
    .string "may offer both gifts and sacrifices\l"
    .string "for sins:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_2::
    .string "Who can have compassion on the\n"
    .string "ignorant, and on them that are out of\l"
    .string "the way; for that he himself also is\l"
    .string "compassed with infirmity$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_3::
    .string "And by reason hereof he ought, as\n"
    .string "for the people, so also for\l"
    .string "himself, to offer for sins.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_4::
    .string "And no man taketh this honour unto\n"
    .string "himself, but he that is called of\l"
    .string "God, as was Aaron.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_5::
    .string "So also Christ glorified not\n"
    .string "himself to be made an high priest;\l"
    .string "but he that said unto him, Thou art my\l"
    .string "Son, to day have I begotten thee.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_6::
    .string "As he saith also in another place,\n"
    .string "Thou art a priest for ever after the\l"
    .string "order of Melchisedec.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_7::
    .string "Who in the days of his flesh, when\n"
    .string "he had offered up prayers and\l"
    .string "supplications with strong crying\l"
    .string "and tears unto him that was able to\l"
    .string "save him from death, and was heard in\l"
    .string "that he feared;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_8::
    .string "Though he were a Son, yet learned he\n"
    .string "obedience by the things which he\l"
    .string "suffered;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_9::
    .string "And being made perfect, he became\n"
    .string "the author of eternal salvation\l"
    .string "unto all them that obey him;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_10::
    .string "Called of God an high priest after\n"
    .string "the order of Melchisedec$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_11::
    .string "Of whom we have many things to say,\n"
    .string "and hard to be uttered, seeing ye are\l"
    .string "dull of hearing.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_12::
    .string "For when for the time ye ought to be\n"
    .string "teachers, ye have need that one teach\l"
    .string "you again which be the first\l"
    .string "principles of the oracles of God;\l"
    .string "and are become such as have need of\l"
    .string "milk, and not of strong meat.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_13::
    .string "For every one that useth milk is\n"
    .string "unskilful in the word of\l"
    .string "righteousness: for he is a babe.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_5_14::
    .string "But strong meat belongeth to them\n"
    .string "that are of full age, even those who\l"
    .string "by reason of use have their senses\l"
    .string "exercised to discern both good and\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_1::
    .string "Therefore leaving the principles\n"
    .string "of the doctrine of Christ, let us go\l"
    .string "on unto perfection; not laying\l"
    .string "again the foundation of repentance\l"
    .string "from dead works, and of faith toward\l"
    .string "God,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_2::
    .string "Of the doctrine of baptisms, and of\n"
    .string "laying on of hands, and of\l"
    .string "resurrection of the dead, and of\l"
    .string "eternal judgment$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_3::
    .string "And this will we do, if God permit.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_4::
    .string "For it is impossible for those who\n"
    .string "were once enlightened, and have\l"
    .string "tasted of the heavenly gift, and\l"
    .string "were made partakers of the Holy\l"
    .string "Ghost,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_5::
    .string "And have tasted the good word of\n"
    .string "God, and the powers of the world to\l"
    .string "come,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_6::
    .string "If they shall fall away, to renew\n"
    .string "them again unto repentance; seeing\l"
    .string "they crucify to themselves the Son\l"
    .string "of God afresh, and put him to an\l"
    .string "open shame$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_7::
    .string "For the earth which drinketh in the\n"
    .string "rain that cometh oft upon it, and\l"
    .string "bringeth forth herbs meet for them by\l"
    .string "whom it is dressed, receiveth\l"
    .string "blessing from God:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_8::
    .string "But that which beareth thorns and\n"
    .string "briers is rejected, and is nigh unto\l"
    .string "cursing; whose end is to be burned$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_9::
    .string "But, beloved, we are persuaded\n"
    .string "better things of you, and things that\l"
    .string "accompany salvation, though we thus\l"
    .string "speak.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_10::
    .string "For God is not unrighteous to forget\n"
    .string "your work and labour of love, which\l"
    .string "ye have shewed toward his name, in\l"
    .string "that ye have ministered to the\l"
    .string "saints, and do minister.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_11::
    .string "And we desire that every one of you\n"
    .string "do shew the same diligence to the\l"
    .string "full assurance of hope unto the\l"
    .string "end:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_12::
    .string "That ye be not slothful, but\n"
    .string "followers of them who through faith\l"
    .string "and patience inherit the promises$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_13::
    .string "For when God made promise to\n"
    .string "Abraham, because he could swear by\l"
    .string "no greater, he sware by himself,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_14::
    .string "Saying, Surely blessing I will\n"
    .string "bless thee, and multiplying I\l"
    .string "will multiply thee$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_15::
    .string "And so, after he had patiently\n"
    .string "endured, he obtained the promise.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_16::
    .string "For men verily swear by the\n"
    .string "greater: and an oath for confirmation\l"
    .string "is to them an end of all strife.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_17::
    .string "Wherein God, willing more\n"
    .string "abundantly to shew unto the heirs of\l"
    .string "promise the immutability of his\l"
    .string "counsel, confirmed it by an oath:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_18::
    .string "That by two immutable things, in\n"
    .string "which it was impossible for God to\l"
    .string "lie, we might have a strong\l"
    .string "consolation, who have fled for\l"
    .string "refuge to lay hold upon the hope\l"
    .string "set before us:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_19::
    .string "Which hope we have as an anchor of\n"
    .string "the soul, both sure and stedfast,\l"
    .string "and which entereth into that within\l"
    .string "the veil;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_6_20::
    .string "Whither the forerunner is for us\n"
    .string "entered, even Jesus, made an high\l"
    .string "priest for ever after the order of\l"
    .string "Melchisedec$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_1::
    .string "For this Melchisedec, king of\n"
    .string "Salem, priest of the most high God,\l"
    .string "who met Abraham returning from the\l"
    .string "slaughter of the kings, and blessed\l"
    .string "him;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_2::
    .string "To whom also Abraham gave a tenth\n"
    .string "part of all; first being by\l"
    .string "interpretation King of\l"
    .string "righteousness, and after that also\l"
    .string "King of Salem, which is, King of\l"
    .string "peace;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_3::
    .string "Without father, without mother,\n"
    .string "without descent, having neither\l"
    .string "beginning of days, nor end of life;\l"
    .string "but made like unto the Son of God;\l"
    .string "abideth a priest continually$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_4::
    .string "Now consider how great this man was,\n"
    .string "unto whom even the patriarch Abraham\l"
    .string "gave the tenth of the spoils.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_5::
    .string "And verily they that are of the\n"
    .string "sons of Levi, who receive the office\l"
    .string "of the priesthood, have a\l"
    .string "commandment to take tithes of the\l"
    .string "people according to the law, that\l"
    .string "is, of their brethren, though they\l"
    .string "come out of the loins of Abraham:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_6::
    .string "But he whose descent is not counted\n"
    .string "from them received tithes of Abraham,\l"
    .string "and blessed him that had the\l"
    .string "promises$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_7::
    .string "And without all contradiction the\n"
    .string "less is blessed of the better.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_8::
    .string "And here men that die receive\n"
    .string "tithes; but there he receiveth them,\l"
    .string "of whom it is witnessed that he\l"
    .string "liveth.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_9::
    .string "And as I may so say, Levi also, who\n"
    .string "receiveth tithes, payed tithes in\l"
    .string "Abraham.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_10::
    .string "For he was yet in the loins of his\n"
    .string "father, when Melchisedec met him.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_11::
    .string "If therefore perfection were by the\n"
    .string "Levitical priesthood, (for under it\l"
    .string "the people received the law,) what\l"
    .string "further need was there that another\l"
    .string "priest should rise after the order\l"
    .string "of Melchisedec, and not be called\l"
    .string "after the order of Aaron?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_12::
    .string "For the priesthood being changed,\n"
    .string "there is made of necessity a change\l"
    .string "also of the law$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_13::
    .string "For he of whom these things are\n"
    .string "spoken pertaineth to another tribe,\l"
    .string "of which no man gave attendance at\l"
    .string "the altar.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_14::
    .string "For it is evident that our Lord\n"
    .string "sprang out of Juda; of which tribe\l"
    .string "Moses spake nothing concerning\l"
    .string "priesthood.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_15::
    .string "And it is yet far more evident: for\n"
    .string "that after the similitude of\l"
    .string "Melchisedec there ariseth another\l"
    .string "priest,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_16::
    .string "Who is made, not after the law of a\n"
    .string "carnal commandment, but after the\l"
    .string "power of an endless life$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_17::
    .string "For he testifieth, Thou art a\n"
    .string "priest for ever after the order of\l"
    .string "Melchisedec.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_18::
    .string "For there is verily a\n"
    .string "disannulling of the commandment\l"
    .string "going before for the weakness and\l"
    .string "unprofitableness thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_19::
    .string "For the law made nothing perfect,\n"
    .string "but the bringing in of a better hope\l"
    .string "did; by the which we draw nigh unto\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_20::
    .string "And inasmuch as not without an oath\n"
    .string "he was made priest:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_21::
    .string "(For those priests were made\n"
    .string "without an oath; but this with an\l"
    .string "oath by him that said unto him, The\l"
    .string "Lord sware and will not repent,\l"
    .string "Thou art a priest for ever after the\l"
    .string "order of Melchisedec:)"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_22::
    .string "By so much was Jesus made a surety\n"
    .string "of a better testament$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_23::
    .string "And they truly were many priests,\n"
    .string "because they were not suffered to\l"
    .string "continue by reason of death:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_24::
    .string "But this man, because he continueth\n"
    .string "ever, hath an unchangeable\l"
    .string "priesthood$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_25::
    .string "Wherefore he is able also to save\n"
    .string "them to the uttermost that come unto\l"
    .string "God by him, seeing he ever liveth to\l"
    .string "make intercession for them.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_26::
    .string "For such an high priest became us,\n"
    .string "who is holy, harmless, undefiled,\l"
    .string "separate from sinners, and made\l"
    .string "higher than the heavens;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_27::
    .string "Who needeth not daily, as those\n"
    .string "high priests, to offer up\l"
    .string "sacrifice, first for his own sins,\l"
    .string "and then for the people’s: for this\l"
    .string "he did once, when he offered up\l"
    .string "himself$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_7_28::
    .string "For the law maketh men high\n"
    .string "priests which have infirmity; but the\l"
    .string "word of the oath, which was since the\l"
    .string "law, maketh the Son, who is\l"
    .string "consecrated for evermore.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_1::
    .string "Now of the things which we have\n"
    .string "spoken this is the sum: We have such\l"
    .string "an high priest, who is set on the\l"
    .string "right hand of the throne of the\l"
    .string "Majesty in the heavens;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_2::
    .string "A minister of the sanctuary, and of\n"
    .string "the true tabernacle, which the Lord\l"
    .string "pitched, and not man$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_3::
    .string "For every high priest is ordained\n"
    .string "to offer gifts and sacrifices:\l"
    .string "wherefore it is of necessity that\l"
    .string "this man have somewhat also to offer.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_4::
    .string "For if he were on earth, he should\n"
    .string "not be a priest, seeing that there\l"
    .string "are priests that offer gifts\l"
    .string "according to the law:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_5::
    .string "Who serve unto the example and\n"
    .string "shadow of heavenly things, as Moses\l"
    .string "was admonished of God when he was\l"
    .string "about to make the tabernacle: for,\l"
    .string "See, saith he, that thou make all\l"
    .string "things according to the pattern\l"
    .string "shewed to thee in the mount$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_6::
    .string "But now hath he obtained a more\n"
    .string "excellent ministry, by how much\l"
    .string "also he is the mediator of a better\l"
    .string "covenant, which was established\l"
    .string "upon better promises.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_7::
    .string "For if that first covenant had been\n"
    .string "faultless, then should no place\l"
    .string "have been sought for the second.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_8::
    .string "For finding fault with them, he\n"
    .string "saith, Behold, the days come, saith\l"
    .string "the Lord, when I will make a new\l"
    .string "covenant with the house of Israel\l"
    .string "and with the house of Judah:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_9::
    .string "Not according to the covenant that I\n"
    .string "made with their fathers in the day\l"
    .string "when I took them by the hand to lead\l"
    .string "them out of the land of Egypt;\l"
    .string "because they continued not in my\l"
    .string "covenant, and I regarded them not,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_10::
    .string "For this is the covenant that I\n"
    .string "will make with the house of Israel\l"
    .string "after those days, saith the Lord; I\l"
    .string "will put my laws into their mind,\l"
    .string "and write them in their hearts: and I\l"
    .string "will be to them a God, and they\l"
    .string "shall be to me a people:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_11::
    .string "And they shall not teach every man\n"
    .string "his neighbour, and every man his\l"
    .string "brother, saying, Know the Lord: for\l"
    .string "all shall know me, from the least\l"
    .string "to the greatest$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_12::
    .string "For I will be merciful to their\n"
    .string "unrighteousness, and their sins and\l"
    .string "their iniquities will I remember no\l"
    .string "more.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_8_13::
    .string "In that he saith, A new covenant, he\n"
    .string "hath made the first old. Now that\l"
    .string "which decayeth and waxeth old is\l"
    .string "ready to vanish away.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_1::
    .string "Then verily the first covenant had\n"
    .string "also ordinances of divine service,\l"
    .string "and a worldly sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_2::
    .string "For there was a tabernacle made;\n"
    .string "the first, wherein was the\l"
    .string "candlestick, and the table, and the\l"
    .string "shewbread; which is called the\l"
    .string "sanctuary.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_3::
    .string "And after the second veil, the\n"
    .string "tabernacle which is called the\l"
    .string "Holiest of all;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_4::
    .string "Which had the golden censer, and\n"
    .string "the ark of the covenant overlaid\l"
    .string "round about with gold, wherein was\l"
    .string "the golden pot that had manna, and\l"
    .string "Aaron’s rod that budded, and the\l"
    .string "tables of the covenant;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_5::
    .string "And over it the cherubims of glory\n"
    .string "shadowing the mercyseat; of which we\l"
    .string "cannot now speak particularly$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_6::
    .string "Now when these things were thus\n"
    .string "ordained, the priests went always\l"
    .string "into the first tabernacle,\l"
    .string "accomplishing the service of God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_7::
    .string "But into the second went the high\n"
    .string "priest alone once every year, not\l"
    .string "without blood, which he offered for\l"
    .string "himself, and for the errors of the\l"
    .string "people:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_8::
    .string "The Holy Ghost this signifying,\n"
    .string "that the way into the holiest of\l"
    .string "all was not yet made manifest,\l"
    .string "while as the first tabernacle was\l"
    .string "yet standing:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_9::
    .string "Which was a figure for the time then\n"
    .string "present, in which were offered both\l"
    .string "gifts and sacrifices, that could not\l"
    .string "make him that did the service\l"
    .string "perfect, as pertaining to the\l"
    .string "conscience;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_10::
    .string "Which stood only in meats and\n"
    .string "drinks, and divers washings, and\l"
    .string "carnal ordinances, imposed on them\l"
    .string "until the time of reformation$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_11::
    .string "But Christ being come an high\n"
    .string "priest of good things to come, by a\l"
    .string "greater and more perfect\l"
    .string "tabernacle, not made with hands,\l"
    .string "that is to say, not of this building;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_12::
    .string "Neither by the blood of goats and\n"
    .string "calves, but by his own blood he\l"
    .string "entered in once into the holy\l"
    .string "place, having obtained eternal\l"
    .string "redemption for us$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_13::
    .string "For if the blood of bulls and of\n"
    .string "goats, and the ashes of an heifer\l"
    .string "sprinkling the unclean,\l"
    .string "sanctifieth to the purifying of the\l"
    .string "flesh:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_14::
    .string "How much more shall the blood of\n"
    .string "Christ, who through the eternal\l"
    .string "Spirit offered himself without\l"
    .string "spot to God, purge your conscience\l"
    .string "from dead works to serve the living\l"
    .string "God?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_15::
    .string "And for this cause he is the\n"
    .string "mediator of the new testament, that\l"
    .string "by means of death, for the\l"
    .string "redemption of the transgressions\l"
    .string "that were under the first testament,\l"
    .string "they which are called might receive\l"
    .string "the promise of eternal inheritance$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_16::
    .string "For where a testament is, there must\n"
    .string "also of necessity be the death of\l"
    .string "the testator.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_17::
    .string "For a testament is of force after\n"
    .string "men are dead: otherwise it is of no\l"
    .string "strength at all while the testator\l"
    .string "liveth.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_18::
    .string "Whereupon neither the first\n"
    .string "testament was dedicated without\l"
    .string "blood.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_19::
    .string "For when Moses had spoken every\n"
    .string "precept to all the people\l"
    .string "according to the law, he took the\l"
    .string "blood of calves and of goats, with\l"
    .string "water, and scarlet wool, and\l"
    .string "hyssop, and sprinkled both the\l"
    .string "book, and all the people,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_20::
    .string "Saying, This is the blood of the\n"
    .string "testament which God hath enjoined\l"
    .string "unto you$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_21::
    .string "Moreover he sprinkled with blood\n"
    .string "both the tabernacle, and all the\l"
    .string "vessels of the ministry.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_22::
    .string "And almost all things are by the\n"
    .string "law purged with blood; and without\l"
    .string "shedding of blood is no remission.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_23::
    .string "It was therefore necessary that the\n"
    .string "patterns of things in the heavens\l"
    .string "should be purified with these; but\l"
    .string "the heavenly things themselves with\l"
    .string "better sacrifices than these.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_24::
    .string "For Christ is not entered into the\n"
    .string "holy places made with hands, which\l"
    .string "are the figures of the true; but into\l"
    .string "heaven itself, now to appear in the\l"
    .string "presence of God for us:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_25::
    .string "Nor yet that he should offer\n"
    .string "himself often, as the high priest\l"
    .string "entereth into the holy place every\l"
    .string "year with blood of others;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_26::
    .string "For then must he often have suffered\n"
    .string "since the foundation of the world:\l"
    .string "but now once in the end of the world\l"
    .string "hath he appeared to put away sin by\l"
    .string "the sacrifice of himself$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_27::
    .string "And as it is appointed unto men\n"
    .string "once to die, but after this the\l"
    .string "judgment:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_9_28::
    .string "So Christ was once offered to bear\n"
    .string "the sins of many; and unto them that\l"
    .string "look for him shall he appear the\l"
    .string "second time without sin unto\l"
    .string "salvation$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_1::
    .string "For the law having a shadow of good\n"
    .string "things to come, and not the very\l"
    .string "image of the things, can never with\l"
    .string "those sacrifices which they offered\l"
    .string "year by year continually make the\l"
    .string "comers thereunto perfect.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_2::
    .string "For then would they not have ceased\n"
    .string "to be offered? because that the\l"
    .string "worshippers once purged should\l"
    .string "have had no more conscience of sins.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_3::
    .string "But in those sacrifices there is a\n"
    .string "remembrance again made of sins every\l"
    .string "year.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_4::
    .string "For it is not possible that the\n"
    .string "blood of bulls and of goats should\l"
    .string "take away sins.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_5::
    .string "Wherefore when he cometh into the\n"
    .string "world, he saith, Sacrifice and\l"
    .string "offering thou wouldest not, but a\l"
    .string "body hast thou prepared me:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_6::
    .string "In burnt offerings and sacrifices\n"
    .string "for sin thou hast had no pleasure$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_7::
    .string "Then said I, Lo, I come (in the\n"
    .string "volume of the book it is written of\l"
    .string "me,) to do thy will, O God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_8::
    .string "Above when he said, Sacrifice and\n"
    .string "offering and burnt offerings and\l"
    .string "offering for sin thou wouldest not,\l"
    .string "neither hadst pleasure therein;\l"
    .string "which are offered by the law;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_9::
    .string "Then said he, Lo, I come to do thy\n"
    .string "will, O God. He taketh away the\l"
    .string "first, that he may establish the\l"
    .string "second$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_10::
    .string "By the which will we are\n"
    .string "sanctified through the offering of\l"
    .string "the body of Jesus Christ once for\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_11::
    .string "And every priest standeth daily\n"
    .string "ministering and offering oftentimes\l"
    .string "the same sacrifices, which can never\l"
    .string "take away sins:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_12::
    .string "But this man, after he had offered\n"
    .string "one sacrifice for sins for ever, sat\l"
    .string "down on the right hand of God;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_13::
    .string "From henceforth expecting till\n"
    .string "his enemies be made his footstool$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_14::
    .string "For by one offering he hath\n"
    .string "perfected for ever them that are\l"
    .string "sanctified.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_15::
    .string "Whereof the Holy Ghost also is a\n"
    .string "witness to us: for after that he had\l"
    .string "said before,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_16::
    .string "This is the covenant that I will\n"
    .string "make with them after those days,\l"
    .string "saith the Lord, I will put my laws\l"
    .string "into their hearts, and in their minds\l"
    .string "will I write them;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_17::
    .string "And their sins and iniquities will\n"
    .string "I remember no more$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_18::
    .string "Now where remission of these is,\n"
    .string "there is no more offering for sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_19::
    .string "Having therefore, brethren,\n"
    .string "boldness to enter into the holiest\l"
    .string "by the blood of Jesus,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_20::
    .string "By a new and living way, which he\n"
    .string "hath consecrated for us, through the\l"
    .string "veil, that is to say, his flesh;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_21::
    .string "And having an high priest over the\n"
    .string "house of God;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_22::
    .string "Let us draw near with a true heart\n"
    .string "in full assurance of faith, having\l"
    .string "our hearts sprinkled from an evil\l"
    .string "conscience, and our bodies washed\l"
    .string "with pure water$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_23::
    .string "Let us hold fast the profession of\n"
    .string "our faith without wavering; (for he\l"
    .string "is faithful that promised;)"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_24::
    .string "And let us consider one another to\n"
    .string "provoke unto love and to good works:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_25::
    .string "Not forsaking the assembling of\n"
    .string "ourselves together, as the manner of\l"
    .string "some is; but exhorting one another:\l"
    .string "and so much the more, as ye see the\l"
    .string "day approaching$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_26::
    .string "For if we sin wilfully after that\n"
    .string "we have received the knowledge of\l"
    .string "the truth, there remaineth no more\l"
    .string "sacrifice for sins,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_27::
    .string "But a certain fearful looking for\n"
    .string "of judgment and fiery indignation,\l"
    .string "which shall devour the adversaries$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_28::
    .string "He that despised Moses’ law died\n"
    .string "without mercy under two or three\l"
    .string "witnesses:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_29::
    .string "Of how much sorer punishment,\n"
    .string "suppose ye, shall he be thought\l"
    .string "worthy, who hath trodden under foot\l"
    .string "the Son of God, and hath counted the\l"
    .string "blood of the covenant, wherewith he\l"
    .string "was sanctified, an unholy thing, and\l"
    .string "hath done despite unto the Spirit\l"
    .string "of grace?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_30::
    .string "For we know him that hath said,\n"
    .string "Vengeance belongeth unto me, I will\l"
    .string "recompense, saith the Lord. And\l"
    .string "again, The Lord shall judge his\l"
    .string "people$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_31::
    .string "It is a fearful thing to fall into\n"
    .string "the hands of the living God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_32::
    .string "But call to remembrance the former\n"
    .string "days, in which, after ye were\l"
    .string "illuminated, ye endured a great\l"
    .string "fight of afflictions;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_33::
    .string "Partly, whilst ye were made a\n"
    .string "gazingstock both by reproaches and\l"
    .string "afflictions; and partly, whilst ye\l"
    .string "became companions of them that were\l"
    .string "so used$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_34::
    .string "For ye had compassion of me in my\n"
    .string "bonds, and took joyfully the\l"
    .string "spoiling of your goods, knowing in\l"
    .string "yourselves that ye have in heaven a\l"
    .string "better and an enduring substance.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_35::
    .string "Cast not away therefore your\n"
    .string "confidence, which hath great\l"
    .string "recompence of reward.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_36::
    .string "For ye have need of patience, that,\n"
    .string "after ye have done the will of God,\l"
    .string "ye might receive the promise.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_37::
    .string "For yet a little while, and he\n"
    .string "that shall come will come, and\l"
    .string "will not tarry.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_38::
    .string "Now the just shall live by faith:\n"
    .string "but if any man draw back, my soul\l"
    .string "shall have no pleasure in him.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_10_39::
    .string "But we are not of them who draw back\n"
    .string "unto perdition; but of them that\l"
    .string "believe to the saving of the soul.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_1::
    .string "Now faith is the substance of things\n"
    .string "hoped for, the evidence of things\l"
    .string "not seen.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_2::
    .string "For by it the elders obtained a\n"
    .string "good report.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_3::
    .string "Through faith we understand that\n"
    .string "the worlds were framed by the word\l"
    .string "of God, so that things which are seen\l"
    .string "were not made of things which do\l"
    .string "appear.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_4::
    .string "By faith Abel offered unto God a\n"
    .string "more excellent sacrifice than Cain,\l"
    .string "by which he obtained witness that he\l"
    .string "was righteous, God testifying of his\l"
    .string "gifts: and by it he being dead yet\l"
    .string "speaketh.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_5::
    .string "By faith Enoch was translated that\n"
    .string "he should not see death; and was not\l"
    .string "found, because God had translated\l"
    .string "him: for before his translation he\l"
    .string "had this testimony, that he pleased\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_6::
    .string "But without faith it is impossible\n"
    .string "to please him: for he that cometh to\l"
    .string "God must believe that he is, and that\l"
    .string "he is a rewarder of them that\l"
    .string "diligently seek him.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_7::
    .string "By faith Noah, being warned of God\n"
    .string "of things not seen as yet, moved with\l"
    .string "fear, prepared an ark to the saving\l"
    .string "of his house; by the which he\l"
    .string "condemned the world, and became heir\l"
    .string "of the righteousness which is by\l"
    .string "faith.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_8::
    .string "By faith Abraham, when he was\n"
    .string "called to go out into a place\l"
    .string "which he should after receive for an\l"
    .string "inheritance, obeyed; and he went out,\l"
    .string "not knowing whither he went.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_9::
    .string "By faith he sojourned in the land\n"
    .string "of promise, as in a strange country,\l"
    .string "dwelling in tabernacles with Isaac\l"
    .string "and Jacob, the heirs with him of the\l"
    .string "same promise:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_10::
    .string "For he looked for a city which hath\n"
    .string "foundations, whose builder and maker\l"
    .string "is God$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_11::
    .string "Through faith also Sara herself\n"
    .string "received strength to conceive seed,\l"
    .string "and was delivered of a child when\l"
    .string "she was past age, because she judged\l"
    .string "him faithful who had promised.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_12::
    .string "Therefore sprang there even of one,\n"
    .string "and him as good as dead, so many as\l"
    .string "the stars of the sky in multitude,\l"
    .string "and as the sand which is by the sea\l"
    .string "shore innumerable.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_13::
    .string "These all died in faith, not having\n"
    .string "received the promises, but having\l"
    .string "seen them afar off, and were\l"
    .string "persuaded of them, and embraced them,\l"
    .string "and confessed that they were\l"
    .string "strangers and pilgrims on the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_14::
    .string "For they that say such things\n"
    .string "declare plainly that they seek a\l"
    .string "country.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_15::
    .string "And truly, if they had been mindful\n"
    .string "of that country from whence they came\l"
    .string "out, they might have had\l"
    .string "opportunity to have returned.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_16::
    .string "But now they desire a better\n"
    .string "country, that is, an heavenly:\l"
    .string "wherefore God is not ashamed to be\l"
    .string "called their God: for he hath\l"
    .string "prepared for them a city.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_17::
    .string "By faith Abraham, when he was tried,\n"
    .string "offered up Isaac: and he that had\l"
    .string "received the promises offered up\l"
    .string "his only begotten son,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_18::
    .string "Of whom it was said, That in Isaac\n"
    .string "shall thy seed be called:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_19::
    .string "Accounting that God was able to\n"
    .string "raise him up, even from the dead;\l"
    .string "from whence also he received him in\l"
    .string "a figure$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_20::
    .string "By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and\n"
    .string "Esau concerning things to come.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_21::
    .string "By faith Jacob, when he was a dying,\n"
    .string "blessed both the sons of Joseph; and\l"
    .string "worshipped, leaning upon the top\l"
    .string "of his staff.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_22::
    .string "By faith Joseph, when he died, made\n"
    .string "mention of the departing of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel; and gave\l"
    .string "commandment concerning his bones.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_23::
    .string "By faith Moses, when he was born,\n"
    .string "was hid three months of his parents,\l"
    .string "because they saw he was a proper\l"
    .string "child; and they were not afraid of\l"
    .string "the king’s commandment.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_24::
    .string "By faith Moses, when he was come to\n"
    .string "years, refused to be called the son\l"
    .string "of Pharaoh’s daughter;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_25::
    .string "Choosing rather to suffer\n"
    .string "affliction with the people of God,\l"
    .string "than to enjoy the pleasures of sin\l"
    .string "for a season;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_26::
    .string "Esteeming the reproach of Christ\n"
    .string "greater riches than the treasures in\l"
    .string "Egypt: for he had respect unto the\l"
    .string "recompence of the reward$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_27::
    .string "By faith he forsook Egypt, not\n"
    .string "fearing the wrath of the king: for he\l"
    .string "endured, as seeing him who is\l"
    .string "invisible.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_28::
    .string "Through faith he kept the\n"
    .string "passover, and the sprinkling of\l"
    .string "blood, lest he that destroyed the\l"
    .string "firstborn should touch them.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_29::
    .string "By faith they passed through the\n"
    .string "Red sea as by dry land: which the\l"
    .string "Egyptians assaying to do were\l"
    .string "drowned.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_30::
    .string "By faith the walls of Jericho\n"
    .string "fell down, after they were\l"
    .string "compassed about seven days.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_31::
    .string "By faith the harlot Rahab perished\n"
    .string "not with them that believed not,\l"
    .string "when she had received the spies with\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_32::
    .string "And what shall I more say? for the\n"
    .string "time would fail me to tell of\l"
    .string "Gedeon, and of Barak, and of Samson,\l"
    .string "and of Jephthae; of David also, and\l"
    .string "Samuel, and of the prophets:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_33::
    .string "Who through faith subdued kingdoms,\n"
    .string "wrought righteousness, obtained\l"
    .string "promises, stopped the mouths of\l"
    .string "lions$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_34::
    .string "Quenched the violence of fire,\n"
    .string "escaped the edge of the sword, out of\l"
    .string "weakness were made strong, waxed\l"
    .string "valiant in fight, turned to flight\l"
    .string "the armies of the aliens.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_35::
    .string "Women received their dead raised to\n"
    .string "life again: and others were tortured,\l"
    .string "not accepting deliverance; that\l"
    .string "they might obtain a better\l"
    .string "resurrection:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_36::
    .string "And others had trial of cruel\n"
    .string "mockings and scourgings, yea,\l"
    .string "moreover of bonds and imprisonment:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_37::
    .string "They were stoned, they were sawn\n"
    .string "asunder, were tempted, were slain\l"
    .string "with the sword: they wandered about\l"
    .string "in sheepskins and goatskins; being\l"
    .string "destitute, afflicted, tormented;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_38::
    .string "(Of whom the world was not worthy:)\n"
    .string "they wandered in deserts, and in\l"
    .string "mountains, and in dens and caves of\l"
    .string "the earth$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_39::
    .string "And these all, having obtained a\n"
    .string "good report through faith, received\l"
    .string "not the promise:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_11_40::
    .string "God having provided some better\n"
    .string "thing for us, that they without us\l"
    .string "should not be made perfect$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_1::
    .string "Wherefore seeing we also are\n"
    .string "compassed about with so great a\l"
    .string "cloud of witnesses, let us lay\l"
    .string "aside every weight, and the sin which\l"
    .string "doth so easily beset us, and let us\l"
    .string "run with patience the race that is\l"
    .string "set before us,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_2::
    .string "Looking unto Jesus the author and\n"
    .string "finisher of our faith; who for the\l"
    .string "joy that was set before him endured\l"
    .string "the cross, despising the shame, and\l"
    .string "is set down at the right hand of the\l"
    .string "throne of God$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_3::
    .string "For consider him that endured such\n"
    .string "contradiction of sinners against\l"
    .string "himself, lest ye be wearied and\l"
    .string "faint in your minds.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_4::
    .string "Ye have not yet resisted unto\n"
    .string "blood, striving against sin.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_5::
    .string "And ye have forgotten the\n"
    .string "exhortation which speaketh unto you\l"
    .string "as unto children, My son, despise\l"
    .string "not thou the chastening of the Lord,\l"
    .string "nor faint when thou art rebuked of\l"
    .string "him:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_6::
    .string "For whom the Lord loveth he\n"
    .string "chasteneth, and scourgeth every son\l"
    .string "whom he receiveth$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_7::
    .string "If ye endure chastening, God\n"
    .string "dealeth with you as with sons; for\l"
    .string "what son is he whom the father\l"
    .string "chasteneth not?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_8::
    .string "But if ye be without chastisement,\n"
    .string "whereof all are partakers, then are\l"
    .string "ye bastards, and not sons$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_9::
    .string "Furthermore we have had fathers of\n"
    .string "our flesh which corrected us, and we\l"
    .string "gave them reverence: shall we not\l"
    .string "much rather be in subjection unto the\l"
    .string "Father of spirits, and live?"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_10::
    .string "For they verily for a few days\n"
    .string "chastened us after their own\l"
    .string "pleasure; but he for our profit,\l"
    .string "that we might be partakers of his\l"
    .string "holiness$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_11::
    .string "Now no chastening for the present\n"
    .string "seemeth to be joyous, but grievous:\l"
    .string "nevertheless afterward it yieldeth\l"
    .string "the peaceable fruit of\l"
    .string "righteousness unto them which are\l"
    .string "exercised thereby.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_12::
    .string "Wherefore lift up the hands which\n"
    .string "hang down, and the feeble knees;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_13::
    .string "And make straight paths for your\n"
    .string "feet, lest that which is lame be\l"
    .string "turned out of the way; but let it\l"
    .string "rather be healed$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_14::
    .string "Follow peace with all men, and\n"
    .string "holiness, without which no man\l"
    .string "shall see the Lord:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_15::
    .string "Looking diligently lest any man\n"
    .string "fail of the grace of God; lest any\l"
    .string "root of bitterness springing up\l"
    .string "trouble you, and thereby many be\l"
    .string "defiled;"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_16::
    .string "Lest there be any fornicator, or\n"
    .string "profane person, as Esau, who for one\l"
    .string "morsel of meat sold his birthright$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_17::
    .string "For ye know how that afterward, when\n"
    .string "he would have inherited the\l"
    .string "blessing, he was rejected: for he\l"
    .string "found no place of repentance,\l"
    .string "though he sought it carefully with\l"
    .string "tears.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_18::
    .string "For ye are not come unto the mount\n"
    .string "that might be touched, and that\l"
    .string "burned with fire, nor unto\l"
    .string "blackness, and darkness, and\l"
    .string "tempest,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_19::
    .string "And the sound of a trumpet, and the\n"
    .string "voice of words; which voice they that\l"
    .string "heard intreated that the word should\l"
    .string "not be spoken to them any more:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_20::
    .string "(For they could not endure that\n"
    .string "which was commanded, And if so much\l"
    .string "as a beast touch the mountain, it\l"
    .string "shall be stoned, or thrust through\l"
    .string "with a dart:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_21::
    .string "And so terrible was the sight, that\n"
    .string "Moses said, I exceedingly fear and\l"
    .string "quake:)"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_22::
    .string "But ye are come unto mount Sion, and\n"
    .string "unto the city of the living God, the\l"
    .string "heavenly Jerusalem, and to an\l"
    .string "innumerable company of angels,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_23::
    .string "To the general assembly and church\n"
    .string "of the firstborn, which are written\l"
    .string "in heaven, and to God the Judge of\l"
    .string "all, and to the spirits of just men\l"
    .string "made perfect,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_24::
    .string "And to Jesus the mediator of the new\n"
    .string "covenant, and to the blood of\l"
    .string "sprinkling, that speaketh better\l"
    .string "things than that of Abel$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_25::
    .string "See that ye refuse not him that\n"
    .string "speaketh. For if they escaped not\l"
    .string "who refused him that spake on earth,\l"
    .string "much more shall not we escape, if\l"
    .string "we turn away from him that speaketh\l"
    .string "from heaven:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_26::
    .string "Whose voice then shook the earth:\n"
    .string "but now he hath promised, saying,\l"
    .string "Yet once more I shake not the earth\l"
    .string "only, but also heaven$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_27::
    .string "And this word, Yet once more,\n"
    .string "signifieth the removing of those\l"
    .string "things that are shaken, as of things\l"
    .string "that are made, that those things\l"
    .string "which cannot be shaken may remain.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_28::
    .string "Wherefore we receiving a kingdom\n"
    .string "which cannot be moved, let us have\l"
    .string "grace, whereby we may serve God\l"
    .string "acceptably with reverence and\l"
    .string "godly fear:"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_12_29::
    .string "For our God is a consuming fire$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_1::
    .string "Let brotherly love continue.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_2::
    .string "Be not forgetful to entertain\n"
    .string "strangers: for thereby some have\l"
    .string "entertained angels unawares.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_3::
    .string "Remember them that are in bonds, as\n"
    .string "bound with them; and them which\l"
    .string "suffer adversity, as being\l"
    .string "yourselves also in the body.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_4::
    .string "Marriage is honourable in all, and\n"
    .string "the bed undefiled: but whoremongers\l"
    .string "and adulterers God will judge.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_5::
    .string "Let your conversation be without\n"
    .string "covetousness; and be content with\l"
    .string "such things as ye have: for he hath\l"
    .string "said, I will never leave thee, nor\l"
    .string "forsake thee.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_6::
    .string "So that we may boldly say, The Lord\n"
    .string "is my helper, and I will not fear\l"
    .string "what man shall do unto me.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_7::
    .string "Remember them which have the rule\n"
    .string "over you, who have spoken unto you\l"
    .string "the word of God: whose faith follow,\l"
    .string "considering the end of their\l"
    .string "conversation.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_8::
    .string "Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and\n"
    .string "to day, and for ever.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_9::
    .string "Be not carried about with divers and\n"
    .string "strange doctrines. For it is a good\l"
    .string "thing that the heart be established\l"
    .string "with grace; not with meats, which\l"
    .string "have not profited them that have\l"
    .string "been occupied therein.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_10::
    .string "We have an altar, whereof they have\n"
    .string "no right to eat which serve the\l"
    .string "tabernacle.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_11::
    .string "For the bodies of those beasts,\n"
    .string "whose blood is brought into the\l"
    .string "sanctuary by the high priest for\l"
    .string "sin, are burned without the camp.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_12::
    .string "Wherefore Jesus also, that he might\n"
    .string "sanctify the people with his own\l"
    .string "blood, suffered without the gate.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_13::
    .string "Let us go forth therefore unto him\n"
    .string "without the camp, bearing his\l"
    .string "reproach.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_14::
    .string "For here have we no continuing city,\n"
    .string "but we seek one to come.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_15::
    .string "By him therefore let us offer the\n"
    .string "sacrifice of praise to God\l"
    .string "continually, that is, the fruit of\l"
    .string "our lips giving thanks to his name.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_16::
    .string "But to do good and to communicate\n"
    .string "forget not: for with such sacrifices\l"
    .string "God is well pleased.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_17::
    .string "Obey them that have the rule over\n"
    .string "you, and submit yourselves: for they\l"
    .string "watch for your souls, as they that\l"
    .string "must give account, that they may do\l"
    .string "it with joy, and not with grief: for\l"
    .string "that is unprofitable for you.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_18::
    .string "Pray for us: for we trust we have a\n"
    .string "good conscience, in all things\l"
    .string "willing to live honestly.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_19::
    .string "But I beseech you the rather to do\n"
    .string "this, that I may be restored to you\l"
    .string "the sooner.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_20::
    .string "Now the God of peace, that brought\n"
    .string "again from the dead our Lord Jesus,\l"
    .string "that great shepherd of the sheep,\l"
    .string "through the blood of the\l"
    .string "everlasting covenant,"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_21::
    .string "Make you perfect in every good work\n"
    .string "to do his will, working in you that\l"
    .string "which is wellpleasing in his\l"
    .string "sight, through Jesus Christ; to whom\l"
    .string "be glory for ever and ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_22::
    .string "And I beseech you, brethren, suffer\n"
    .string "the word of exhortation: for I have\l"
    .string "written a letter unto you in few\l"
    .string "words.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_23::
    .string "Know ye that our brother Timothy is\n"
    .string "set at liberty; with whom, if he come\l"
    .string "shortly, I will see you.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_24::
    .string "Salute all them that have the\n"
    .string "rule over you, and all the saints.\l"
    .string "They of Italy salute you.$"
Bible_Text_Hebrews_13_25::
    .string "Grace be with you all. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_1::
    .string "James, a servant of God and of the\n"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve\l"
    .string "tribes which are scattered abroad,\l"
    .string "greeting.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_2::
    .string "My brethren, count it all joy when\n"
    .string "ye fall into divers temptations;"
Bible_Text_James_1_3::
    .string "Knowing this, that the trying of\n"
    .string "your faith worketh patience$"
Bible_Text_James_1_4::
    .string "But let patience have her perfect\n"
    .string "work, that ye may be perfect and\l"
    .string "entire, wanting nothing.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_5::
    .string "If any of you lack wisdom, let him\n"
    .string "ask of God, that giveth to all men\l"
    .string "liberally, and upbraideth not; and\l"
    .string "it shall be given him.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_6::
    .string "But let him ask in faith, nothing\n"
    .string "wavering. For he that wavereth is\l"
    .string "like a wave of the sea driven with\l"
    .string "the wind and tossed.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_7::
    .string "For let not that man think that he\n"
    .string "shall receive any thing of the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_8::
    .string "A double minded man is unstable in\n"
    .string "all his ways.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_9::
    .string "Let the brother of low degree\n"
    .string "rejoice in that he is exalted:"
Bible_Text_James_1_10::
    .string "But the rich, in that he is made\n"
    .string "low: because as the flower of the\l"
    .string "grass he shall pass away$"
Bible_Text_James_1_11::
    .string "For the sun is no sooner risen with\n"
    .string "a burning heat, but it withereth the\l"
    .string "grass, and the flower thereof\l"
    .string "falleth, and the grace of the\l"
    .string "fashion of it perisheth: so also\l"
    .string "shall the rich man fade away in his\l"
    .string "ways.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_12::
    .string "Blessed is the man that endureth\n"
    .string "temptation: for when he is tried, he\l"
    .string "shall receive the crown of life,\l"
    .string "which the Lord hath promised to them\l"
    .string "that love him.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_13::
    .string "Let no man say when he is tempted, I\n"
    .string "am tempted of God: for God cannot be\l"
    .string "tempted with evil, neither\l"
    .string "tempteth he any man:"
Bible_Text_James_1_14::
    .string "But every man is tempted, when he is\n"
    .string "drawn away of his own lust, and\l"
    .string "enticed$"
Bible_Text_James_1_15::
    .string "Then when lust hath conceived, it\n"
    .string "bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it\l"
    .string "is finished, bringeth forth death.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_16::
    .string "Do not err, my beloved brethren.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_17::
    .string "Every good gift and every perfect\n"
    .string "gift is from above, and cometh down\l"
    .string "from the Father of lights, with whom\l"
    .string "is no variableness, neither shadow\l"
    .string "of turning.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_18::
    .string "Of his own will begat he us with\n"
    .string "the word of truth, that we should be\l"
    .string "a kind of firstfruits of his\l"
    .string "creatures.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_19::
    .string "Wherefore, my beloved brethren,\n"
    .string "let every man be swift to hear, slow\l"
    .string "to speak, slow to wrath:"
Bible_Text_James_1_20::
    .string "For the wrath of man worketh not the\n"
    .string "righteousness of God$"
Bible_Text_James_1_21::
    .string "Wherefore lay apart all\n"
    .string "filthiness and superfluity of\l"
    .string "naughtiness, and receive with\l"
    .string "meekness the engrafted word, which is\l"
    .string "able to save your souls.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_22::
    .string "But be ye doers of the word, and not\n"
    .string "hearers only, deceiving your own\l"
    .string "selves.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_23::
    .string "For if any be a hearer of the word,\n"
    .string "and not a doer, he is like unto a man\l"
    .string "beholding his natural face in a\l"
    .string "glass:"
Bible_Text_James_1_24::
    .string "For he beholdeth himself, and\n"
    .string "goeth his way, and straightway\l"
    .string "forgetteth what manner of man he was$"
Bible_Text_James_1_25::
    .string "But whoso looketh into the perfect\n"
    .string "law of liberty, and continueth\l"
    .string "therein, he being not a forgetful\l"
    .string "hearer, but a doer of the work, this\l"
    .string "man shall be blessed in his deed.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_26::
    .string "If any man among you seem to be\n"
    .string "religious, and bridleth not his\l"
    .string "tongue, but deceiveth his own heart,\l"
    .string "this man’s religion is vain.$"
Bible_Text_James_1_27::
    .string "Pure religion and undefiled before\n"
    .string "God and the Father is this, To visit\l"
    .string "the fatherless and widows in their\l"
    .string "affliction, and to keep himself\l"
    .string "unspotted from the world.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_1::
    .string "My brethren, have not the faith of\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of\l"
    .string "glory, with respect of persons.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_2::
    .string "For if there come unto your\n"
    .string "assembly a man with a gold ring, in\l"
    .string "goodly apparel, and there come in\l"
    .string "also a poor man in vile raiment;"
Bible_Text_James_2_3::
    .string "And ye have respect to him that\n"
    .string "weareth the gay clothing, and say\l"
    .string "unto him, Sit thou here in a good\l"
    .string "place; and say to the poor, Stand\l"
    .string "thou there, or sit here under my\l"
    .string "footstool:"
Bible_Text_James_2_4::
    .string "Are ye not then partial in\n"
    .string "yourselves, and are become judges of\l"
    .string "evil thoughts?"
Bible_Text_James_2_5::
    .string "Hearken, my beloved brethren, Hath\n"
    .string "not God chosen the poor of this\l"
    .string "world rich in faith, and heirs of the\l"
    .string "kingdom which he hath promised to\l"
    .string "them that love him?"
Bible_Text_James_2_6::
    .string "But ye have despised the poor. Do\n"
    .string "not rich men oppress you, and draw\l"
    .string "you before the judgment seats?"
Bible_Text_James_2_7::
    .string "Do not they blaspheme that worthy\n"
    .string "name by the which ye are called?"
Bible_Text_James_2_8::
    .string "If ye fulfil the royal law\n"
    .string "according to the scripture, Thou\l"
    .string "shalt love thy neighbour as\l"
    .string "thyself, ye do well:"
Bible_Text_James_2_9::
    .string "But if ye have respect to persons,\n"
    .string "ye commit sin, and are convinced of\l"
    .string "the law as transgressors$"
Bible_Text_James_2_10::
    .string "For whosoever shall keep the\n"
    .string "whole law, and yet offend in one\l"
    .string "point, he is guilty of all.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_11::
    .string "For he that said, Do not commit\n"
    .string "adultery, said also, Do not kill.\l"
    .string "Now if thou commit no adultery, yet\l"
    .string "if thou kill, thou art become a\l"
    .string "transgressor of the law.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_12::
    .string "So speak ye, and so do, as they that\n"
    .string "shall be judged by the law of\l"
    .string "liberty.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_13::
    .string "For he shall have judgment without\n"
    .string "mercy, that hath shewed no mercy; and\l"
    .string "mercy rejoiceth against judgment.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_14::
    .string "What doth it profit, my brethren,\n"
    .string "though a man say he hath faith, and\l"
    .string "have not works? can faith save him?"
Bible_Text_James_2_15::
    .string "If a brother or sister be naked, and\n"
    .string "destitute of daily food,"
Bible_Text_James_2_16::
    .string "And one of you say unto them, Depart\n"
    .string "in peace, be ye warmed and filled;\l"
    .string "notwithstanding ye give them not\l"
    .string "those things which are needful to\l"
    .string "the body; what doth it profit?"
Bible_Text_James_2_17::
    .string "Even so faith, if it hath not works,\n"
    .string "is dead, being alone$"
Bible_Text_James_2_18::
    .string "Yea, a man may say, Thou hast faith,\n"
    .string "and I have works: shew me thy faith\l"
    .string "without thy works, and I will shew\l"
    .string "thee my faith by my works.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_19::
    .string "Thou believest that there is one\n"
    .string "God; thou doest well: the devils\l"
    .string "also believe, and tremble.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_20::
    .string "But wilt thou know, O vain man, that\n"
    .string "faith without works is dead?"
Bible_Text_James_2_21::
    .string "Was not Abraham our father\n"
    .string "justified by works, when he had\l"
    .string "offered Isaac his son upon the\l"
    .string "altar?"
Bible_Text_James_2_22::
    .string "Seest thou how faith wrought with\n"
    .string "his works, and by works was faith\l"
    .string "made perfect?"
Bible_Text_James_2_23::
    .string "And the scripture was fulfilled\n"
    .string "which saith, Abraham believed God,\l"
    .string "and it was imputed unto him for\l"
    .string "righteousness: and he was called\l"
    .string "the Friend of God$"
Bible_Text_James_2_24::
    .string "Ye see then how that by works a man\n"
    .string "is justified, and not by faith only.$"
Bible_Text_James_2_25::
    .string "Likewise also was not Rahab the\n"
    .string "harlot justified by works, when she\l"
    .string "had received the messengers, and had\l"
    .string "sent them out another way?"
Bible_Text_James_2_26::
    .string "For as the body without the spirit\n"
    .string "is dead, so faith without works is\l"
    .string "dead also$"
Bible_Text_James_3_1::
    .string "My brethren, be not many masters,\n"
    .string "knowing that we shall receive the\l"
    .string "greater condemnation.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_2::
    .string "For in many things we offend all.\n"
    .string "If any man offend not in word, the\l"
    .string "same is a perfect man, and able\l"
    .string "also to bridle the whole body.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_3::
    .string "Behold, we put bits in the horses’\n"
    .string "mouths, that they may obey us; and we\l"
    .string "turn about their whole body.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_4::
    .string "Behold also the ships, which\n"
    .string "though they be so great, and are\l"
    .string "driven of fierce winds, yet are they\l"
    .string "turned about with a very small\l"
    .string "helm, whithersoever the governor\l"
    .string "listeth.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_5::
    .string "Even so the tongue is a little\n"
    .string "member, and boasteth great things.\l"
    .string "Behold, how great a matter a little\l"
    .string "fire kindleth!$"
Bible_Text_James_3_6::
    .string "And the tongue is a fire, a world of\n"
    .string "iniquity: so is the tongue among our\l"
    .string "members, that it defileth the whole\l"
    .string "body, and setteth on fire the course\l"
    .string "of nature; and it is set on fire of\l"
    .string "hell.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_7::
    .string "For every kind of beasts, and of\n"
    .string "birds, and of serpents, and of\l"
    .string "things in the sea, is tamed, and hath\l"
    .string "been tamed of mankind:"
Bible_Text_James_3_8::
    .string "But the tongue can no man tame; it is\n"
    .string "an unruly evil, full of deadly\l"
    .string "poison$"
Bible_Text_James_3_9::
    .string "Therewith bless we God, even the\n"
    .string "Father; and therewith curse we men,\l"
    .string "which are made after the similitude\l"
    .string "of God.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_10::
    .string "Out of the same mouth proceedeth\n"
    .string "blessing and cursing. My brethren,\l"
    .string "these things ought not so to be.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_11::
    .string "Doth a fountain send forth at the\n"
    .string "same place sweet water and bitter?"
Bible_Text_James_3_12::
    .string "Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear\n"
    .string "olive berries? either a vine, figs?\l"
    .string "so can no fountain both yield salt\l"
    .string "water and fresh$"
Bible_Text_James_3_13::
    .string "Who is a wise man and endued with\n"
    .string "knowledge among you? let him shew\l"
    .string "out of a good conversation his works\l"
    .string "with meekness of wisdom.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_14::
    .string "But if ye have bitter envying and\n"
    .string "strife in your hearts, glory not,\l"
    .string "and lie not against the truth.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_15::
    .string "This wisdom descendeth not from\n"
    .string "above, but is earthly, sensual,\l"
    .string "devilish.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_16::
    .string "For where envying and strife is,\n"
    .string "there is confusion and every evil\l"
    .string "work.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_17::
    .string "But the wisdom that is from above is\n"
    .string "first pure, then peaceable,\l"
    .string "gentle, and easy to be intreated,\l"
    .string "full of mercy and good fruits,\l"
    .string "without partiality, and without\l"
    .string "hypocrisy.$"
Bible_Text_James_3_18::
    .string "And the fruit of righteousness is\n"
    .string "sown in peace of them that make\l"
    .string "peace.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_1::
    .string "From whence come wars and fightings\n"
    .string "among you? come they not hence, even\l"
    .string "of your lusts that war in your\l"
    .string "members?"
Bible_Text_James_4_2::
    .string "Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and\n"
    .string "desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye\l"
    .string "fight and war, yet ye have not,\l"
    .string "because ye ask not$"
Bible_Text_James_4_3::
    .string "Ye ask, and receive not, because ye\n"
    .string "ask amiss, that ye may consume it\l"
    .string "upon your lusts.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_4::
    .string "Ye adulterers and adulteresses,\n"
    .string "know ye not that the friendship of\l"
    .string "the world is enmity with God?\l"
    .string "whosoever therefore will be a\l"
    .string "friend of the world is the enemy of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_5::
    .string "Do ye think that the scripture\n"
    .string "saith in vain, The spirit that\l"
    .string "dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?"
Bible_Text_James_4_6::
    .string "But he giveth more grace. Wherefore\n"
    .string "he saith, God resisteth the proud,\l"
    .string "but giveth grace unto the humble$"
Bible_Text_James_4_7::
    .string "Submit yourselves therefore to God.\n"
    .string "Resist the devil, and he will flee\l"
    .string "from you.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_8::
    .string "Draw nigh to God, and he will draw\n"
    .string "nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye\l"
    .string "sinners; and purify your hearts, ye\l"
    .string "double minded.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_9::
    .string "Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep:\n"
    .string "let your laughter be turned to\l"
    .string "mourning, and your joy to heaviness.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_10::
    .string "Humble yourselves in the sight of\n"
    .string "the Lord, and he shall lift you up.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_11::
    .string "Speak not evil one of another,\n"
    .string "brethren. He that speaketh evil of\l"
    .string "his brother, and judgeth his brother,\l"
    .string "speaketh evil of the law, and\l"
    .string "judgeth the law: but if thou judge\l"
    .string "the law, thou art not a doer of the\l"
    .string "law, but a judge.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_12::
    .string "There is one lawgiver, who is able\n"
    .string "to save and to destroy: who art thou\l"
    .string "that judgest another?"
Bible_Text_James_4_13::
    .string "Go to now, ye that say, To day or to\n"
    .string "morrow we will go into such a city,\l"
    .string "and continue there a year, and buy\l"
    .string "and sell, and get gain:"
Bible_Text_James_4_14::
    .string "Whereas ye know not what shall be\n"
    .string "on the morrow. For what is your life?\l"
    .string "It is even a vapour, that appeareth\l"
    .string "for a little time, and then\l"
    .string "vanisheth away$"
Bible_Text_James_4_15::
    .string "For that ye ought to say, If the Lord\n"
    .string "will, we shall live, and do this,\l"
    .string "or that.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_16::
    .string "But now ye rejoice in your\n"
    .string "boastings: all such rejoicing is\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_James_4_17::
    .string "Therefore to him that knoweth to do\n"
    .string "good, and doeth it not, to him it is\l"
    .string "sin.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_1::
    .string "Go to now, ye rich men, weep and\n"
    .string "howl for your miseries that shall\l"
    .string "come upon you.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_2::
    .string "Your riches are corrupted, and your\n"
    .string "garments are motheaten.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_3::
    .string "Your gold and silver is cankered;\n"
    .string "and the rust of them shall be a\l"
    .string "witness against you, and shall eat\l"
    .string "your flesh as it were fire. Ye have\l"
    .string "heaped treasure together for the\l"
    .string "last days.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_4::
    .string "Behold, the hire of the labourers\n"
    .string "who have reaped down your fields,\l"
    .string "which is of you kept back by fraud,\l"
    .string "crieth: and the cries of them which\l"
    .string "have reaped are entered into the\l"
    .string "ears of the Lord of sabaoth.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_5::
    .string "Ye have lived in pleasure on the\n"
    .string "earth, and been wanton; ye have\l"
    .string "nourished your hearts, as in a day of\l"
    .string "slaughter.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_6::
    .string "Ye have condemned and killed the\n"
    .string "just; and he doth not resist you.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_7::
    .string "Be patient therefore, brethren,\n"
    .string "unto the coming of the Lord. Behold,\l"
    .string "the husbandman waiteth for the\l"
    .string "precious fruit of the earth, and hath\l"
    .string "long patience for it, until he\l"
    .string "receive the early and latter rain.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_8::
    .string "Be ye also patient; stablish your\n"
    .string "hearts: for the coming of the Lord\l"
    .string "draweth nigh.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_9::
    .string "Grudge not one against another,\n"
    .string "brethren, lest ye be condemned:\l"
    .string "behold, the judge standeth before\l"
    .string "the door.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_10::
    .string "Take, my brethren, the prophets,\n"
    .string "who have spoken in the name of the\l"
    .string "Lord, for an example of suffering\l"
    .string "affliction, and of patience.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_11::
    .string "Behold, we count them happy which\n"
    .string "endure. Ye have heard of the\l"
    .string "patience of Job, and have seen the\l"
    .string "end of the Lord; that the Lord is very\l"
    .string "pitiful, and of tender mercy.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_12::
    .string "But above all things, my brethren,\n"
    .string "swear not, neither by heaven, neither\l"
    .string "by the earth, neither by any other\l"
    .string "oath: but let your yea be yea; and\l"
    .string "your nay, nay; lest ye fall into\l"
    .string "condemnation.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_13::
    .string "Is any among you afflicted? let him\n"
    .string "pray. Is any merry? let him sing\l"
    .string "psalms.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_14::
    .string "Is any sick among you? let him\n"
    .string "call for the elders of the church;\l"
    .string "and let them pray over him,\l"
    .string "anointing him with oil in the name\l"
    .string "of the Lord:"
Bible_Text_James_5_15::
    .string "And the prayer of faith shall save\n"
    .string "the sick, and the Lord shall raise\l"
    .string "him up; and if he have committed\l"
    .string "sins, they shall be forgiven him$"
Bible_Text_James_5_16::
    .string "Confess your faults one to another,\n"
    .string "and pray one for another, that ye may\l"
    .string "be healed. The effectual fervent\l"
    .string "prayer of a righteous man availeth\l"
    .string "much.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_17::
    .string "Elias was a man subject to like\n"
    .string "passions as we are, and he prayed\l"
    .string "earnestly that it might not rain:\l"
    .string "and it rained not on the earth by the\l"
    .string "space of three years and six months.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_18::
    .string "And he prayed again, and the heaven\n"
    .string "gave rain, and the earth brought\l"
    .string "forth her fruit.$"
Bible_Text_James_5_19::
    .string "Brethren, if any of you do err from\n"
    .string "the truth, and one convert him;"
Bible_Text_James_5_20::
    .string "Let him know, that he which\n"
    .string "converteth the sinner from the error\l"
    .string "of his way shall save a soul from\l"
    .string "death, and shall hide a multitude\l"
    .string "of sins$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_1::
    .string "Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "to the strangers scattered\l"
    .string "throughout Pontus, Galatia,\l"
    .string "Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_2::
    .string "Elect according to the\n"
    .string "foreknowledge of God the Father,\l"
    .string "through sanctification of the\l"
    .string "Spirit, unto obedience and\l"
    .string "sprinkling of the blood of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ: Grace unto you, and peace, be\l"
    .string "multiplied$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_3::
    .string "Blessed be the God and Father of\n"
    .string "our Lord Jesus Christ, which\l"
    .string "according to his abundant mercy hath\l"
    .string "begotten us again unto a lively\l"
    .string "hope by the resurrection of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ from the dead,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_4::
    .string "To an inheritance incorruptible,\n"
    .string "and undefiled, and that fadeth not\l"
    .string "away, reserved in heaven for you,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_5::
    .string "Who are kept by the power of God\n"
    .string "through faith unto salvation ready\l"
    .string "to be revealed in the last time$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_6::
    .string "Wherein ye greatly rejoice, though\n"
    .string "now for a season, if need be, ye are\l"
    .string "in heaviness through manifold\l"
    .string "temptations:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_7::
    .string "That the trial of your faith, being\n"
    .string "much more precious than of gold\l"
    .string "that perisheth, though it be tried\l"
    .string "with fire, might be found unto\l"
    .string "praise and honour and glory at the\l"
    .string "appearing of Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_8::
    .string "Whom having not seen, ye love; in\n"
    .string "whom, though now ye see him not, yet\l"
    .string "believing, ye rejoice with joy\l"
    .string "unspeakable and full of glory:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_9::
    .string "Receiving the end of your faith,\n"
    .string "even the salvation of your souls$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_10::
    .string "Of which salvation the prophets\n"
    .string "have enquired and searched\l"
    .string "diligently, who prophesied of the\l"
    .string "grace that should come unto you:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_11::
    .string "Searching what, or what manner of\n"
    .string "time the Spirit of Christ which was\l"
    .string "in them did signify, when it\l"
    .string "testified beforehand the sufferings\l"
    .string "of Christ, and the glory that should\l"
    .string "follow$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_12::
    .string "Unto whom it was revealed, that not\n"
    .string "unto themselves, but unto us they\l"
    .string "did minister the things, which are\l"
    .string "now reported unto you by them that\l"
    .string "have preached the gospel unto you\l"
    .string "with the Holy Ghost sent down from\l"
    .string "heaven; which things the angels\l"
    .string "desire to look into.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_13::
    .string "Wherefore gird up the loins of\n"
    .string "your mind, be sober, and hope to the\l"
    .string "end for the grace that is to be\l"
    .string "brought unto you at the revelation\l"
    .string "of Jesus Christ;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_14::
    .string "As obedient children, not\n"
    .string "fashioning yourselves according to\l"
    .string "the former lusts in your ignorance:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_15::
    .string "But as he which hath called you is\n"
    .string "holy, so be ye holy in all manner\l"
    .string "of conversation;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_16::
    .string "Because it is written, Be ye holy;\n"
    .string "for I am holy$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_17::
    .string "And if ye call on the Father, who\n"
    .string "without respect of persons judgeth\l"
    .string "according to every man’s work, pass\l"
    .string "the time of your sojourning here in\l"
    .string "fear:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_18::
    .string "Forasmuch as ye know that ye were\n"
    .string "not redeemed with corruptible\l"
    .string "things, as silver and gold, from\l"
    .string "your vain conversation received by\l"
    .string "tradition from your fathers;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_19::
    .string "But with the precious blood of\n"
    .string "Christ, as of a lamb without blemish\l"
    .string "and without spot:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_20::
    .string "Who verily was foreordained before\n"
    .string "the foundation of the world, but was\l"
    .string "manifest in these last times for\l"
    .string "you,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_21::
    .string "Who by him do believe in God, that\n"
    .string "raised him up from the dead, and gave\l"
    .string "him glory; that your faith and hope\l"
    .string "might be in God$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_22::
    .string "Seeing ye have purified your souls\n"
    .string "in obeying the truth through the\l"
    .string "Spirit unto unfeigned love of the\l"
    .string "brethren, see that ye love one\l"
    .string "another with a pure heart\l"
    .string "fervently:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_23::
    .string "Being born again, not of\n"
    .string "corruptible seed, but of\l"
    .string "incorruptible, by the word of God,\l"
    .string "which liveth and abideth for ever$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_24::
    .string "For all flesh is as grass, and\n"
    .string "all the glory of man as the flower\l"
    .string "of grass. The grass withereth, and\l"
    .string "the flower thereof falleth away:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_1_25::
    .string "But the word of the Lord endureth\n"
    .string "for ever. And this is the word which\l"
    .string "by the gospel is preached unto you$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_1::
    .string "Wherefore laying aside all\n"
    .string "malice, and all guile, and\l"
    .string "hypocrisies, and envies, all evil\l"
    .string "speakings,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_2::
    .string "As newborn babes, desire the sincere\n"
    .string "milk of the word, that ye may grow\l"
    .string "thereby:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_3::
    .string "If so be ye have tasted that the\n"
    .string "Lord is gracious$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_4::
    .string "To whom coming, as unto a living\n"
    .string "stone, disallowed indeed of men,\l"
    .string "but chosen of God, and precious,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_5::
    .string "Ye also, as lively stones, are\n"
    .string "built up a spiritual house, an\l"
    .string "holy priesthood, to offer up\l"
    .string "spiritual sacrifices, acceptable\l"
    .string "to God by Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_6::
    .string "Wherefore also it is contained in\n"
    .string "the scripture, Behold, I lay in\l"
    .string "Sion a chief corner stone, elect,\l"
    .string "precious: and he that believeth on\l"
    .string "him shall not be confounded.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_7::
    .string "Unto you therefore which believe he\n"
    .string "is precious: but unto them which be\l"
    .string "disobedient, the stone which the\l"
    .string "builders disallowed, the same is\l"
    .string "made the head of the corner,"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_8::
    .string "And a stone of stumbling, and a rock\n"
    .string "of offence, even to them which\l"
    .string "stumble at the word, being\l"
    .string "disobedient: whereunto also they\l"
    .string "were appointed$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_9::
    .string "But ye are a chosen generation, a\n"
    .string "royal priesthood, an holy nation, a\l"
    .string "peculiar people; that ye should\l"
    .string "shew forth the praises of him who\l"
    .string "hath called you out of darkness\l"
    .string "into his marvellous light;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_10::
    .string "Which in time past were not a\n"
    .string "people, but are now the people of\l"
    .string "God: which had not obtained mercy,\l"
    .string "but now have obtained mercy$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_11::
    .string "Dearly beloved, I beseech you as\n"
    .string "strangers and pilgrims, abstain\l"
    .string "from fleshly lusts, which war\l"
    .string "against the soul;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_12::
    .string "Having your conversation honest\n"
    .string "among the Gentiles: that, whereas\l"
    .string "they speak against you as\l"
    .string "evildoers, they may by your good\l"
    .string "works, which they shall behold,\l"
    .string "glorify God in the day of visitation$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_13::
    .string "Submit yourselves to every\n"
    .string "ordinance of man for the Lord’s sake:\l"
    .string "whether it be to the king, as\l"
    .string "supreme;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_14::
    .string "Or unto governors, as unto them that\n"
    .string "are sent by him for the punishment\l"
    .string "of evildoers, and for the praise of\l"
    .string "them that do well$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_15::
    .string "For so is the will of God, that\n"
    .string "with well doing ye may put to\l"
    .string "silence the ignorance of foolish\l"
    .string "men:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_16::
    .string "As free, and not using your liberty\n"
    .string "for a cloke of maliciousness, but as\l"
    .string "the servants of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_17::
    .string "Honour all men. Love the\n"
    .string "brotherhood. Fear God. Honour the\l"
    .string "king.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_18::
    .string "Servants, be subject to your masters\n"
    .string "with all fear; not only to the good\l"
    .string "and gentle, but also to the froward.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_19::
    .string "For this is thankworthy, if a man\n"
    .string "for conscience toward God endure\l"
    .string "grief, suffering wrongfully.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_20::
    .string "For what glory is it, if, when ye be\n"
    .string "buffeted for your faults, ye shall\l"
    .string "take it patiently? but if, when ye\l"
    .string "do well, and suffer for it, ye take\l"
    .string "it patiently, this is acceptable\l"
    .string "with God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_21::
    .string "For even hereunto were ye called:\n"
    .string "because Christ also suffered for us,\l"
    .string "leaving us an example, that ye\l"
    .string "should follow his steps:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_22::
    .string "Who did no sin, neither was guile\n"
    .string "found in his mouth:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_23::
    .string "Who, when he was reviled, reviled\n"
    .string "not again; when he suffered, he\l"
    .string "threatened not; but committed\l"
    .string "himself to him that judgeth\l"
    .string "righteously:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_24::
    .string "Who his own self bare our sins in\n"
    .string "his own body on the tree, that we,\l"
    .string "being dead to sins, should live unto\l"
    .string "righteousness: by whose stripes ye\l"
    .string "were healed$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_2_25::
    .string "For ye were as sheep going astray;\n"
    .string "but are now returned unto the\l"
    .string "Shepherd and Bishop of your souls.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_1::
    .string "Likewise, ye wives, be in subjection\n"
    .string "to your own husbands; that, if any\l"
    .string "obey not the word, they also may\l"
    .string "without the word be won by the\l"
    .string "conversation of the wives;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_2::
    .string "While they behold your chaste\n"
    .string "conversation coupled with fear$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_3::
    .string "Whose adorning let it not be that\n"
    .string "outward adorning of plaiting the\l"
    .string "hair, and of wearing of gold, or of\l"
    .string "putting on of apparel;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_4::
    .string "But let it be the hidden man of the\n"
    .string "heart, in that which is not\l"
    .string "corruptible, even the ornament of a\l"
    .string "meek and quiet spirit, which is in\l"
    .string "the sight of God of great price$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_5::
    .string "For after this manner in the old\n"
    .string "time the holy women also, who\l"
    .string "trusted in God, adorned themselves,\l"
    .string "being in subjection unto their own\l"
    .string "husbands:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_6::
    .string "Even as Sara obeyed Abraham,\n"
    .string "calling him lord: whose daughters\l"
    .string "ye are, as long as ye do well, and\l"
    .string "are not afraid with any amazement$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_7::
    .string "Likewise, ye husbands, dwell with\n"
    .string "them according to knowledge, giving\l"
    .string "honour unto the wife, as unto the\l"
    .string "weaker vessel, and as being heirs\l"
    .string "together of the grace of life; that\l"
    .string "your prayers be not hindered.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_8::
    .string "Finally, be ye all of one mind,\n"
    .string "having compassion one of another,\l"
    .string "love as brethren, be pitiful, be\l"
    .string "courteous:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_9::
    .string "Not rendering evil for evil, or\n"
    .string "railing for railing: but\l"
    .string "contrariwise blessing; knowing that\l"
    .string "ye are thereunto called, that ye\l"
    .string "should inherit a blessing$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_10::
    .string "For he that will love life, and\n"
    .string "see good days, let him refrain his\l"
    .string "tongue from evil, and his lips that\l"
    .string "they speak no guile:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_11::
    .string "Let him eschew evil, and do good;\n"
    .string "let him seek peace, and ensue it$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_12::
    .string "For the eyes of the Lord are over\n"
    .string "the righteous, and his ears are open\l"
    .string "unto their prayers: but the face of\l"
    .string "the Lord is against them that do\l"
    .string "evil.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_13::
    .string "And who is he that will harm you,\n"
    .string "if ye be followers of that which is\l"
    .string "good?"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_14::
    .string "But and if ye suffer for\n"
    .string "righteousness’ sake, happy are ye:\l"
    .string "and be not afraid of their terror,\l"
    .string "neither be troubled;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_15::
    .string "But sanctify the Lord God in your\n"
    .string "hearts: and be ready always to give\l"
    .string "an answer to every man that asketh\l"
    .string "you a reason of the hope that is in\l"
    .string "you with meekness and fear:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_16::
    .string "Having a good conscience; that,\n"
    .string "whereas they speak evil of you, as\l"
    .string "of evildoers, they may be ashamed\l"
    .string "that falsely accuse your good\l"
    .string "conversation in Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_17::
    .string "For it is better, if the will of\n"
    .string "God be so, that ye suffer for well\l"
    .string "doing, than for evil doing.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_18::
    .string "For Christ also hath once suffered\n"
    .string "for sins, the just for the unjust,\l"
    .string "that he might bring us to God, being\l"
    .string "put to death in the flesh, but\l"
    .string "quickened by the Spirit:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_19::
    .string "By which also he went and preached\n"
    .string "unto the spirits in prison;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_20::
    .string "Which sometime were disobedient,\n"
    .string "when once the longsuffering of God\l"
    .string "waited in the days of Noah, while the\l"
    .string "ark was a preparing, wherein few,\l"
    .string "that is, eight souls were saved by\l"
    .string "water$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_21::
    .string "The like figure whereunto even\n"
    .string "baptism doth also now save us (not\l"
    .string "the putting away of the filth of the\l"
    .string "flesh, but the answer of a good\l"
    .string "conscience toward God,) by the\l"
    .string "resurrection of Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_3_22::
    .string "Who is gone into heaven, and is on\n"
    .string "the right hand of God; angels and\l"
    .string "authorities and powers being made\l"
    .string "subject unto him$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_1::
    .string "Forasmuch then as Christ hath\n"
    .string "suffered for us in the flesh, arm\l"
    .string "yourselves likewise with the same\l"
    .string "mind: for he that hath suffered in\l"
    .string "the flesh hath ceased from sin;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_2::
    .string "That he no longer should live the\n"
    .string "rest of his time in the flesh to the\l"
    .string "lusts of men, but to the will of God$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_3::
    .string "For the time past of our life may\n"
    .string "suffice us to have wrought the will\l"
    .string "of the Gentiles, when we walked in\l"
    .string "lasciviousness, lusts, excess of\l"
    .string "wine, revellings, banquetings, and\l"
    .string "abominable idolatries:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_4::
    .string "Wherein they think it strange that\n"
    .string "ye run not with them to the same\l"
    .string "excess of riot, speaking evil of\l"
    .string "you:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_5::
    .string "Who shall give account to him that\n"
    .string "is ready to judge the quick and the\l"
    .string "dead$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_6::
    .string "For for this cause was the gospel\n"
    .string "preached also to them that are dead,\l"
    .string "that they might be judged according\l"
    .string "to men in the flesh, but live\l"
    .string "according to God in the spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_7::
    .string "But the end of all things is at\n"
    .string "hand: be ye therefore sober, and\l"
    .string "watch unto prayer.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_8::
    .string "And above all things have fervent\n"
    .string "charity among yourselves: for\l"
    .string "charity shall cover the multitude\l"
    .string "of sins.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_9::
    .string "Use hospitality one to another\n"
    .string "without grudging.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_10::
    .string "As every man hath received the gift,\n"
    .string "even so minister the same one to\l"
    .string "another, as good stewards of the\l"
    .string "manifold grace of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_11::
    .string "If any man speak, let him speak as\n"
    .string "the oracles of God; if any man\l"
    .string "minister, let him do it as of the\l"
    .string "ability which God giveth: that God\l"
    .string "in all things may be glorified\l"
    .string "through Jesus Christ, to whom be\l"
    .string "praise and dominion for ever and\l"
    .string "ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_12::
    .string "Beloved, think it not strange\n"
    .string "concerning the fiery trial which is\l"
    .string "to try you, as though some strange\l"
    .string "thing happened unto you:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_13::
    .string "But rejoice, inasmuch as ye are\n"
    .string "partakers of Christ’s sufferings;\l"
    .string "that, when his glory shall be\l"
    .string "revealed, ye may be glad also with\l"
    .string "exceeding joy$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_14::
    .string "If ye be reproached for the name of\n"
    .string "Christ, happy are ye; for the\l"
    .string "spirit of glory and of God resteth\l"
    .string "upon you: on their part he is evil\l"
    .string "spoken of, but on your part he is\l"
    .string "glorified.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_15::
    .string "But let none of you suffer as a\n"
    .string "murderer, or as a thief, or as an\l"
    .string "evildoer, or as a busybody in other\l"
    .string "men’s matters.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_16::
    .string "Yet if any man suffer as a\n"
    .string "Christian, let him not be ashamed;\l"
    .string "but let him glorify God on this\l"
    .string "behalf.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_17::
    .string "For the time is come that judgment\n"
    .string "must begin at the house of God: and if\l"
    .string "it first begin at us, what shall the\l"
    .string "end be of them that obey not the\l"
    .string "gospel of God?"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_18::
    .string "And if the righteous scarcely be\n"
    .string "saved, where shall the ungodly and\l"
    .string "the sinner appear?"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_4_19::
    .string "Wherefore let them that suffer\n"
    .string "according to the will of God commit\l"
    .string "the keeping of their souls to him in\l"
    .string "well doing, as unto a faithful\l"
    .string "Creator$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_1::
    .string "The elders which are among you I\n"
    .string "exhort, who am also an elder, and a\l"
    .string "witness of the sufferings of Christ,\l"
    .string "and also a partaker of the glory\l"
    .string "that shall be revealed:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_2::
    .string "Feed the flock of God which is\n"
    .string "among you, taking the oversight\l"
    .string "thereof, not by constraint, but\l"
    .string "willingly; not for filthy lucre,\l"
    .string "but of a ready mind;"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_3::
    .string "Neither as being lords over God’s\n"
    .string "heritage, but being ensamples to\l"
    .string "the flock$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_4::
    .string "And when the chief Shepherd shall\n"
    .string "appear, ye shall receive a crown\l"
    .string "of glory that fadeth not away.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_5::
    .string "Likewise, ye younger, submit\n"
    .string "yourselves unto the elder. Yea,\l"
    .string "all of you be subject one to\l"
    .string "another, and be clothed with\l"
    .string "humility: for God resisteth the\l"
    .string "proud, and giveth grace to the\l"
    .string "humble.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_6::
    .string "Humble yourselves therefore under\n"
    .string "the mighty hand of God, that he may\l"
    .string "exalt you in due time:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_7::
    .string "Casting all your care upon him;\n"
    .string "for he careth for you$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_8::
    .string "Be sober, be vigilant; because your\n"
    .string "adversary the devil, as a roaring\l"
    .string "lion, walketh about, seeking whom he\l"
    .string "may devour:"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_9::
    .string "Whom resist stedfast in the faith,\n"
    .string "knowing that the same afflictions\l"
    .string "are accomplished in your brethren\l"
    .string "that are in the world$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_10::
    .string "But the God of all grace, who hath\n"
    .string "called us unto his eternal glory\l"
    .string "by Christ Jesus, after that ye have\l"
    .string "suffered a while, make you perfect,\l"
    .string "stablish, strengthen, settle you.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_11::
    .string "To him be glory and dominion for\n"
    .string "ever and ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_12::
    .string "By Silvanus, a faithful brother\n"
    .string "unto you, as I suppose, I have\l"
    .string "written briefly, exhorting, and\l"
    .string "testifying that this is the true\l"
    .string "grace of God wherein ye stand.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_13::
    .string "The church that is at Babylon,\n"
    .string "elected together with you, saluteth\l"
    .string "you; and so doth Marcus my son.$"
Bible_Text_1_Peter_5_14::
    .string "Greet ye one another with a kiss of\n"
    .string "charity. Peace be with you all that\l"
    .string "are in Christ Jesus. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_1::
    .string "Simon Peter, a servant and an\n"
    .string "apostle of Jesus Christ, to them\l"
    .string "that have obtained like precious\l"
    .string "faith with us through the\l"
    .string "righteousness of God and our Saviour\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_2::
    .string "Grace and peace be multiplied\n"
    .string "unto you through the knowledge of\l"
    .string "God, and of Jesus our Lord,"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_3::
    .string "According as his divine power hath\n"
    .string "given unto us all things that\l"
    .string "pertain unto life and godliness,\l"
    .string "through the knowledge of him that\l"
    .string "hath called us to glory and virtue:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_4::
    .string "Whereby are given unto us exceeding\n"
    .string "great and precious promises: that\l"
    .string "by these ye might be partakers of\l"
    .string "the divine nature, having escaped\l"
    .string "the corruption that is in the world\l"
    .string "through lust$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_5::
    .string "And beside this, giving all\n"
    .string "diligence, add to your faith virtue;\l"
    .string "and to virtue knowledge;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_6::
    .string "And to knowledge temperance; and\n"
    .string "to temperance patience; and to\l"
    .string "patience godliness;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_7::
    .string "And to godliness brotherly\n"
    .string "kindness; and to brotherly kindness\l"
    .string "charity$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_8::
    .string "For if these things be in you, and\n"
    .string "abound, they make you that ye shall\l"
    .string "neither be barren nor unfruitful in\l"
    .string "the knowledge of our Lord Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_9::
    .string "But he that lacketh these things is\n"
    .string "blind, and cannot see afar off, and\l"
    .string "hath forgotten that he was purged\l"
    .string "from his old sins.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_10::
    .string "Wherefore the rather, brethren,\n"
    .string "give diligence to make your\l"
    .string "calling and election sure: for if\l"
    .string "ye do these things, ye shall never\l"
    .string "fall:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_11::
    .string "For so an entrance shall be\n"
    .string "ministered unto you abundantly into\l"
    .string "the everlasting kingdom of our Lord\l"
    .string "and Saviour Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_12::
    .string "Wherefore I will not be negligent\n"
    .string "to put you always in remembrance of\l"
    .string "these things, though ye know them,\l"
    .string "and be established in the present\l"
    .string "truth.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_13::
    .string "Yea, I think it meet, as long as I\n"
    .string "am in this tabernacle, to stir you\l"
    .string "up by putting you in remembrance;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_14::
    .string "Knowing that shortly I must put\n"
    .string "off this my tabernacle, even as our\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ hath shewed me$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_15::
    .string "Moreover I will endeavour that ye\n"
    .string "may be able after my decease to have\l"
    .string "these things always in remembrance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_16::
    .string "For we have not followed\n"
    .string "cunningly devised fables, when we\l"
    .string "made known unto you the power and\l"
    .string "coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but\l"
    .string "were eyewitnesses of his majesty.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_17::
    .string "For he received from God the Father\n"
    .string "honour and glory, when there came\l"
    .string "such a voice to him from the\l"
    .string "excellent glory, This is my\l"
    .string "beloved Son, in whom I am well\l"
    .string "pleased.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_18::
    .string "And this voice which came from\n"
    .string "heaven we heard, when we were with\l"
    .string "him in the holy mount.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_19::
    .string "We have also a more sure word of\n"
    .string "prophecy; whereunto ye do well that\l"
    .string "ye take heed, as unto a light that\l"
    .string "shineth in a dark place, until the\l"
    .string "day dawn, and the day star arise in\l"
    .string "your hearts:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_20::
    .string "Knowing this first, that no\n"
    .string "prophecy of the scripture is of any\l"
    .string "private interpretation$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_1_21::
    .string "For the prophecy came not in old\n"
    .string "time by the will of man: but holy\l"
    .string "men of God spake as they were moved\l"
    .string "by the Holy Ghost.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_1::
    .string "But there were false prophets\n"
    .string "also among the people, even as\l"
    .string "there shall be false teachers\l"
    .string "among you, who privily shall bring\l"
    .string "in damnable heresies, even denying\l"
    .string "the Lord that bought them, and bring\l"
    .string "upon themselves swift destruction.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_2::
    .string "And many shall follow their\n"
    .string "pernicious ways; by reason of whom\l"
    .string "the way of truth shall be evil\l"
    .string "spoken of.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_3::
    .string "And through covetousness shall\n"
    .string "they with feigned words make\l"
    .string "merchandise of you: whose judgment\l"
    .string "now of a long time lingereth not,\l"
    .string "and their damnation slumbereth not.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_4::
    .string "For if God spared not the angels\n"
    .string "that sinned, but cast them down to\l"
    .string "hell, and delivered them into\l"
    .string "chains of darkness, to be reserved\l"
    .string "unto judgment;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_5::
    .string "And spared not the old world, but\n"
    .string "saved Noah the eighth person, a\l"
    .string "preacher of righteousness, bringing\l"
    .string "in the flood upon the world of the\l"
    .string "ungodly;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_6::
    .string "And turning the cities of Sodom and\n"
    .string "Gomorrha into ashes condemned them\l"
    .string "with an overthrow, making them an\l"
    .string "ensample unto those that after\l"
    .string "should live ungodly;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_7::
    .string "And delivered just Lot, vexed with\n"
    .string "the filthy conversation of the\l"
    .string "wicked:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_8::
    .string "(For that righteous man dwelling\n"
    .string "among them, in seeing and hearing,\l"
    .string "vexed his righteous soul from day to\l"
    .string "day with their unlawful deeds;)"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_9::
    .string "The Lord knoweth how to deliver the\n"
    .string "godly out of temptations, and to\l"
    .string "reserve the unjust unto the day of\l"
    .string "judgment to be punished:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_10::
    .string "But chiefly them that walk after\n"
    .string "the flesh in the lust of\l"
    .string "uncleanness, and despise government\l"
    .string " Presumptuous are they,\l"
    .string "selfwilled, they are not afraid to\l"
    .string "speak evil of dignities$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_11::
    .string "Whereas angels, which are greater\n"
    .string "in power and might, bring not\l"
    .string "railing accusation against them\l"
    .string "before the Lord.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_12::
    .string "But these, as natural brute beasts,\n"
    .string "made to be taken and destroyed,\l"
    .string "speak evil of the things that they\l"
    .string "understand not; and shall utterly\l"
    .string "perish in their own corruption;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_13::
    .string "And shall receive the reward of\n"
    .string "unrighteousness, as they that count\l"
    .string "it pleasure to riot in the day time.\l"
    .string "Spots they are and blemishes,\l"
    .string "sporting themselves with their own\l"
    .string "deceivings while they feast with\l"
    .string "you;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_14::
    .string "Having eyes full of adultery, and\n"
    .string "that cannot cease from sin;\l"
    .string "beguiling unstable souls: an heart\l"
    .string "they have exercised with covetous\l"
    .string "practices; cursed children:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_15::
    .string "Which have forsaken the right way,\n"
    .string "and are gone astray, following the\l"
    .string "way of Balaam the son of Bosor, who\l"
    .string "loved the wages of unrighteousness;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_16::
    .string "But was rebuked for his iniquity:\n"
    .string "the dumb ass speaking with man’s\l"
    .string "voice forbad the madness of the\l"
    .string "prophet$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_17::
    .string "These are wells without water,\n"
    .string "clouds that are carried with a\l"
    .string "tempest; to whom the mist of\l"
    .string "darkness is reserved for ever.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_18::
    .string "For when they speak great\n"
    .string "swelling words of vanity, they\l"
    .string "allure through the lusts of the\l"
    .string "flesh, through much wantonness,\l"
    .string "those that were clean escaped from\l"
    .string "them who live in error.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_19::
    .string "While they promise them liberty,\n"
    .string "they themselves are the servants of\l"
    .string "corruption: for of whom a man is\l"
    .string "overcome, of the same is he brought\l"
    .string "in bondage.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_20::
    .string "For if after they have escaped the\n"
    .string "pollutions of the world through\l"
    .string "the knowledge of the Lord and\l"
    .string "Saviour Jesus Christ, they are again\l"
    .string "entangled therein, and overcome, the\l"
    .string "latter end is worse with them than\l"
    .string "the beginning.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_21::
    .string "For it had been better for them not\n"
    .string "to have known the way of\l"
    .string "righteousness, than, after they have\l"
    .string "known it, to turn from the holy\l"
    .string "commandment delivered unto them.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_2_22::
    .string "But it is happened unto them\n"
    .string "according to the true proverb, The\l"
    .string "dog is turned to his own vomit again;\l"
    .string "and the sow that was washed to her\l"
    .string "wallowing in the mire.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_1::
    .string "This second epistle, beloved, I\n"
    .string "now write unto you; in both which I\l"
    .string "stir up your pure minds by way of\l"
    .string "remembrance:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_2::
    .string "That ye may be mindful of the words\n"
    .string "which were spoken before by the\l"
    .string "holy prophets, and of the\l"
    .string "commandment of us the apostles of\l"
    .string "the Lord and Saviour:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_3::
    .string "Knowing this first, that there\n"
    .string "shall come in the last days\l"
    .string "scoffers, walking after their own\l"
    .string "lusts,"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_4::
    .string "And saying, Where is the promise of\n"
    .string "his coming? for since the fathers\l"
    .string "fell asleep, all things continue\l"
    .string "as they were from the beginning of\l"
    .string "the creation$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_5::
    .string "For this they willingly are\n"
    .string "ignorant of, that by the word of God\l"
    .string "the heavens were of old, and the\l"
    .string "earth standing out of the water and\l"
    .string "in the water:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_6::
    .string "Whereby the world that then was,\n"
    .string "being overflowed with water,\l"
    .string "perished:"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_7::
    .string "But the heavens and the earth, which\n"
    .string "are now, by the same word are kept in\l"
    .string "store, reserved unto fire against the\l"
    .string "day of judgment and perdition of\l"
    .string "ungodly men$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_8::
    .string "But, beloved, be not ignorant of\n"
    .string "this one thing, that one day is with\l"
    .string "the Lord as a thousand years, and a\l"
    .string "thousand years as one day.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_9::
    .string "The Lord is not slack concerning\n"
    .string "his promise, as some men count\l"
    .string "slackness; but is longsuffering to\l"
    .string "us-ward, not willing that any\l"
    .string "should perish, but that all\l"
    .string "should come to repentance.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_10::
    .string "But the day of the Lord will come\n"
    .string "as a thief in the night; in the which\l"
    .string "the heavens shall pass away with a\l"
    .string "great noise, and the elements shall\l"
    .string "melt with fervent heat, the earth\l"
    .string "also and the works that are therein\l"
    .string "shall be burned up.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_11::
    .string "Seeing then that all these things\n"
    .string "shall be dissolved, what manner of\l"
    .string "persons ought ye to be in all holy\l"
    .string "conversation and godliness,"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_12::
    .string "Looking for and hasting unto the\n"
    .string "coming of the day of God, wherein the\l"
    .string "heavens being on fire shall be\l"
    .string "dissolved, and the elements shall\l"
    .string "melt with fervent heat?"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_13::
    .string "Nevertheless we, according to his\n"
    .string "promise, look for new heavens and a\l"
    .string "new earth, wherein dwelleth\l"
    .string "righteousness$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_14::
    .string "Wherefore, beloved, seeing that ye\n"
    .string "look for such things, be diligent\l"
    .string "that ye may be found of him in peace,\l"
    .string "without spot, and blameless.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_15::
    .string "And account that the longsuffering\n"
    .string "of our Lord is salvation; even as our\l"
    .string "beloved brother Paul also\l"
    .string "according to the wisdom given unto\l"
    .string "him hath written unto you;"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_16::
    .string "As also in all his epistles,\n"
    .string "speaking in them of these things; in\l"
    .string "which are some things hard to be\l"
    .string "understood, which they that are\l"
    .string "unlearned and unstable wrest, as\l"
    .string "they do also the other scriptures,\l"
    .string "unto their own destruction$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_17::
    .string "Ye therefore, beloved, seeing ye\n"
    .string "know these things before, beware\l"
    .string "lest ye also, being led away with\l"
    .string "the error of the wicked, fall from\l"
    .string "your own stedfastness.$"
Bible_Text_2_Peter_3_18::
    .string "But grow in grace, and in the\n"
    .string "knowledge of our Lord and Saviour\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ. To him be glory both\l"
    .string "now and for ever. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_1::
    .string "That which was from the beginning,\n"
    .string "which we have heard, which we have\l"
    .string "seen with our eyes, which we have\l"
    .string "looked upon, and our hands have\l"
    .string "handled, of the Word of life;"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_2::
    .string "(For the life was manifested, and\n"
    .string "we have seen it, and bear witness,\l"
    .string "and shew unto you that eternal life,\l"
    .string "which was with the Father, and was\l"
    .string "manifested unto us;)"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_3::
    .string "That which we have seen and heard\n"
    .string "declare we unto you, that ye also\l"
    .string "may have fellowship with us: and\l"
    .string "truly our fellowship is with the\l"
    .string "Father, and with his Son Jesus Christ$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_4::
    .string "And these things write we unto you,\n"
    .string "that your joy may be full.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_5::
    .string "This then is the message which we\n"
    .string "have heard of him, and declare unto\l"
    .string "you, that God is light, and in him is\l"
    .string "no darkness at all.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_6::
    .string "If we say that we have fellowship\n"
    .string "with him, and walk in darkness, we\l"
    .string "lie, and do not the truth:"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_7::
    .string "But if we walk in the light, as he\n"
    .string "is in the light, we have\l"
    .string "fellowship one with another, and\l"
    .string "the blood of Jesus Christ his Son\l"
    .string "cleanseth us from all sin$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_8::
    .string "If we say that we have no sin, we\n"
    .string "deceive ourselves, and the truth is\l"
    .string "not in us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_9::
    .string "If we confess our sins, he is\n"
    .string "faithful and just to forgive us our\l"
    .string "sins, and to cleanse us from all\l"
    .string "unrighteousness.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_1_10::
    .string "If we say that we have not sinned, we\n"
    .string "make him a liar, and his word is not\l"
    .string "in us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_1::
    .string "My little children, these things\n"
    .string "write I unto you, that ye sin not. And\l"
    .string "if any man sin, we have an advocate\l"
    .string "with the Father, Jesus Christ the\l"
    .string "righteous:$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_2::
    .string "And he is the propitiation for our\n"
    .string "sins: and not for ours only, but\l"
    .string "also for the sins of the whole\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_3::
    .string "And hereby we do know that we know\n"
    .string "him, if we keep his commandments.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_4::
    .string "He that saith, I know him, and\n"
    .string "keepeth not his commandments, is a\l"
    .string "liar, and the truth is not in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_5::
    .string "But whoso keepeth his word, in him\n"
    .string "verily is the love of God\l"
    .string "perfected: hereby know we that we are\l"
    .string "in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_6::
    .string "He that saith he abideth in him\n"
    .string "ought himself also so to walk, even\l"
    .string "as he walked.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_7::
    .string "Brethren, I write no new commandment\n"
    .string "unto you, but an old commandment\l"
    .string "which ye had from the beginning. The\l"
    .string "old commandment is the word which ye\l"
    .string "have heard from the beginning.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_8::
    .string "Again, a new commandment I write\n"
    .string "unto you, which thing is true in him\l"
    .string "and in you: because the darkness is\l"
    .string "past, and the true light now shineth.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_9::
    .string "He that saith he is in the light,\n"
    .string "and hateth his brother, is in\l"
    .string "darkness even until now.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_10::
    .string "He that loveth his brother abideth\n"
    .string "in the light, and there is none\l"
    .string "occasion of stumbling in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_11::
    .string "But he that hateth his brother is in\n"
    .string "darkness, and walketh in darkness,\l"
    .string "and knoweth not whither he goeth,\l"
    .string "because that darkness hath blinded\l"
    .string "his eyes.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_12::
    .string "I write unto you, little children,\n"
    .string "because your sins are forgiven you\l"
    .string "for his name’s sake.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_13::
    .string "I write unto you, fathers, because\n"
    .string "ye have known him that is from the\l"
    .string "beginning. I write unto you, young\l"
    .string "men, because ye have overcome the\l"
    .string "wicked one. I write unto you, little\l"
    .string "children, because ye have known the\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_14::
    .string "I have written unto you, fathers,\n"
    .string "because ye have known him that is\l"
    .string "from the beginning. I have written\l"
    .string "unto you, young men, because ye are\l"
    .string "strong, and the word of God abideth\l"
    .string "in you, and ye have overcome the\l"
    .string "wicked one.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_15::
    .string "Love not the world, neither the\n"
    .string "things that are in the world. If any\l"
    .string "man love the world, the love of the\l"
    .string "Father is not in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_16::
    .string "For all that is in the world, the\n"
    .string "lust of the flesh, and the lust of\l"
    .string "the eyes, and the pride of life, is\l"
    .string "not of the Father, but is of the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_17::
    .string "And the world passeth away, and the\n"
    .string "lust thereof: but he that doeth the\l"
    .string "will of God abideth for ever.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_18::
    .string "Little children, it is the last\n"
    .string "time: and as ye have heard that\l"
    .string "antichrist shall come, even now are\l"
    .string "there many antichrists; whereby we\l"
    .string "know that it is the last time.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_19::
    .string "They went out from us, but they were\n"
    .string "not of us; for if they had been of us,\l"
    .string "they would no doubt have continued\l"
    .string "with us: but they went out, that they\l"
    .string "might be made manifest that they were\l"
    .string "not all of us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_20::
    .string "But ye have an unction from the\n"
    .string "Holy One, and ye know all things.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_21::
    .string "I have not written unto you because\n"
    .string "ye know not the truth, but because ye\l"
    .string "know it, and that no lie is of the\l"
    .string "truth.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_22::
    .string "Who is a liar but he that denieth\n"
    .string "that Jesus is the Christ? He is\l"
    .string "antichrist, that denieth the Father\l"
    .string "and the Son.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_23::
    .string "Whosoever denieth the Son, the same\n"
    .string "hath not the Father: he that\l"
    .string "acknowledgeth the Son hath the\l"
    .string "Father also.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_24::
    .string "Let that therefore abide in you,\n"
    .string "which ye have heard from the\l"
    .string "beginning. If that which ye have\l"
    .string "heard from the beginning shall\l"
    .string "remain in you, ye also shall\l"
    .string "continue in the Son, and in the\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_25::
    .string "And this is the promise that he\n"
    .string "hath promised us, even eternal\l"
    .string "life.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_26::
    .string "These things have I written unto you\n"
    .string "concerning them that seduce you.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_27::
    .string "But the anointing which ye have\n"
    .string "received of him abideth in you, and\l"
    .string "ye need not that any man teach you:\l"
    .string "but as the same anointing teacheth\l"
    .string "you of all things, and is truth, and\l"
    .string "is no lie, and even as it hath taught\l"
    .string "you, ye shall abide in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_28::
    .string "And now, little children, abide in\n"
    .string "him; that, when he shall appear, we\l"
    .string "may have confidence, and not be\l"
    .string "ashamed before him at his coming.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_2_29::
    .string "If ye know that he is righteous, ye\n"
    .string "know that every one that doeth\l"
    .string "righteousness is born of him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_1::
    .string "Behold, what manner of love the\n"
    .string "Father hath bestowed upon us, that\l"
    .string "we should be called the sons of\l"
    .string "God: therefore the world knoweth us\l"
    .string "not, because it knew him not.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_2::
    .string "Beloved, now are we the sons of God,\n"
    .string "and it doth not yet appear what we\l"
    .string "shall be: but we know that, when he\l"
    .string "shall appear, we shall be like\l"
    .string "him; for we shall see him as he is.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_3::
    .string "And every man that hath this hope\n"
    .string "in him purifieth himself, even as he\l"
    .string "is pure.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_4::
    .string "Whosoever committeth sin\n"
    .string "transgresseth also the law: for sin\l"
    .string "is the transgression of the law.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_5::
    .string "And ye know that he was manifested\n"
    .string "to take away our sins; and in him is\l"
    .string "no sin.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_6::
    .string "Whosoever abideth in him sinneth\n"
    .string "not: whosoever sinneth hath not seen\l"
    .string "him, neither known him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_7::
    .string "Little children, let no man\n"
    .string "deceive you: he that doeth\l"
    .string "righteousness is righteous, even as\l"
    .string "he is righteous.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_8::
    .string "He that committeth sin is of the\n"
    .string "devil; for the devil sinneth from\l"
    .string "the beginning. For this purpose the\l"
    .string "Son of God was manifested, that he\l"
    .string "might destroy the works of the devil.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_9::
    .string "Whosoever is born of God doth not\n"
    .string "commit sin; for his seed remaineth in\l"
    .string "him: and he cannot sin, because he is\l"
    .string "born of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_10::
    .string "In this the children of God are\n"
    .string "manifest, and the children of the\l"
    .string "devil: whosoever doeth not\l"
    .string "righteousness is not of God, neither\l"
    .string "he that loveth not his brother.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_11::
    .string "For this is the message that ye\n"
    .string "heard from the beginning, that we\l"
    .string "should love one another.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_12::
    .string "Not as Cain, who was of that wicked\n"
    .string "one, and slew his brother. And\l"
    .string "wherefore slew he him? Because his\l"
    .string "own works were evil, and his\l"
    .string "brother’s righteous.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_13::
    .string "Marvel not, my brethren, if the\n"
    .string "world hate you.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_14::
    .string "We know that we have passed from\n"
    .string "death unto life, because we love the\l"
    .string "brethren. He that loveth not his\l"
    .string "brother abideth in death.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_15::
    .string "Whosoever hateth his brother is a\n"
    .string "murderer: and ye know that no\l"
    .string "murderer hath eternal life abiding\l"
    .string "in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_16::
    .string "Hereby perceive we the love of God,\n"
    .string "because he laid down his life for\l"
    .string "us: and we ought to lay down our\l"
    .string "lives for the brethren.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_17::
    .string "But whoso hath this world’s good,\n"
    .string "and seeth his brother have need, and\l"
    .string "shutteth up his bowels of\l"
    .string "compassion from him, how dwelleth\l"
    .string "the love of God in him?"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_18::
    .string "My little children, let us not\n"
    .string "love in word, neither in tongue; but\l"
    .string "in deed and in truth$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_19::
    .string "And hereby we know that we are of\n"
    .string "the truth, and shall assure our\l"
    .string "hearts before him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_20::
    .string "For if our heart condemn us, God is\n"
    .string "greater than our heart, and knoweth\l"
    .string "all things.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_21::
    .string "Beloved, if our heart condemn us\n"
    .string "not, then have we confidence toward\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_22::
    .string "And whatsoever we ask, we receive of\n"
    .string "him, because we keep his\l"
    .string "commandments, and do those things\l"
    .string "that are pleasing in his sight.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_23::
    .string "And this is his commandment, That we\n"
    .string "should believe on the name of his\l"
    .string "Son Jesus Christ, and love one\l"
    .string "another, as he gave us commandment.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_3_24::
    .string "And he that keepeth his\n"
    .string "commandments dwelleth in him, and\l"
    .string "he in him. And hereby we know that he\l"
    .string "abideth in us, by the Spirit which he\l"
    .string "hath given us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_1::
    .string "Beloved, believe not every\n"
    .string "spirit, but try the spirits whether\l"
    .string "they are of God: because many false\l"
    .string "prophets are gone out into the\l"
    .string "world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_2::
    .string "Hereby know ye the Spirit of God:\n"
    .string "Every spirit that confesseth that\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is\l"
    .string "of God:"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_3::
    .string "And every spirit that confesseth\n"
    .string "not that Jesus Christ is come in the\l"
    .string "flesh is not of God: and this is that\l"
    .string "spirit of antichrist, whereof ye\l"
    .string "have heard that it should come; and\l"
    .string "even now already is it in the world$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_4::
    .string "Ye are of God, little children,\n"
    .string "and have overcome them: because\l"
    .string "greater is he that is in you, than he\l"
    .string "that is in the world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_5::
    .string "They are of the world: therefore\n"
    .string "speak they of the world, and the\l"
    .string "world heareth them.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_6::
    .string "We are of God: he that knoweth God\n"
    .string "heareth us; he that is not of God\l"
    .string "heareth not us. Hereby know we the\l"
    .string "spirit of truth, and the spirit of\l"
    .string "error.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_7::
    .string "Beloved, let us love one another:\n"
    .string "for love is of God; and every one\l"
    .string "that loveth is born of God, and\l"
    .string "knoweth God.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_8::
    .string "He that loveth not knoweth not God;\n"
    .string "for God is love.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_9::
    .string "In this was manifested the love of\n"
    .string "God toward us, because that God sent\l"
    .string "his only begotten Son into the\l"
    .string "world, that we might live through\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_10::
    .string "Herein is love, not that we loved\n"
    .string "God, but that he loved us, and sent\l"
    .string "his Son to be the propitiation for\l"
    .string "our sins.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_11::
    .string "Beloved, if God so loved us, we\n"
    .string "ought also to love one another.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_12::
    .string "No man hath seen God at any time. If\n"
    .string "we love one another, God dwelleth\l"
    .string "in us, and his love is perfected in\l"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_13::
    .string "Hereby know we that we dwell in\n"
    .string "him, and he in us, because he hath\l"
    .string "given us of his Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_14::
    .string "And we have seen and do testify that\n"
    .string "the Father sent the Son to be the\l"
    .string "Saviour of the world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_15::
    .string "Whosoever shall confess that Jesus\n"
    .string "is the Son of God, God dwelleth in\l"
    .string "him, and he in God.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_16::
    .string "And we have known and believed the\n"
    .string "love that God hath to us. God is\l"
    .string "love; and he that dwelleth in love\l"
    .string "dwelleth in God, and God in him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_17::
    .string "Herein is our love made perfect,\n"
    .string "that we may have boldness in the day\l"
    .string "of judgment: because as he is, so are\l"
    .string "we in this world.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_18::
    .string "There is no fear in love; but\n"
    .string "perfect love casteth out fear:\l"
    .string "because fear hath torment. He that\l"
    .string "feareth is not made perfect in love.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_19::
    .string "We love him, because he first loved\n"
    .string "us.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_20::
    .string "If a man say, I love God, and hateth\n"
    .string "his brother, he is a liar: for he\l"
    .string "that loveth not his brother whom he\l"
    .string "hath seen, how can he love God whom\l"
    .string "he hath not seen?"
Bible_Text_1_John_4_21::
    .string "And this commandment have we from\n"
    .string "him, That he who loveth God love his\l"
    .string "brother also$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_1::
    .string "Whosoever believeth that Jesus is\n"
    .string "the Christ is born of God: and every\l"
    .string "one that loveth him that begat\l"
    .string "loveth him also that is begotten of\l"
    .string "him.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_2::
    .string "By this we know that we love the\n"
    .string "children of God, when we love God,\l"
    .string "and keep his commandments.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_3::
    .string "For this is the love of God, that we\n"
    .string "keep his commandments: and his\l"
    .string "commandments are not grievous.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_4::
    .string "For whatsoever is born of God\n"
    .string "overcometh the world: and this is\l"
    .string "the victory that overcometh the\l"
    .string "world, even our faith.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_5::
    .string "Who is he that overcometh the\n"
    .string "world, but he that believeth that\l"
    .string "Jesus is the Son of God?"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_6::
    .string "This is he that came by water and\n"
    .string "blood, even Jesus Christ; not by\l"
    .string "water only, but by water and blood.\l"
    .string "And it is the Spirit that beareth\l"
    .string "witness, because the Spirit is truth$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_7::
    .string "For there are three that bear record\n"
    .string "in heaven, the Father, the Word, and\l"
    .string "the Holy Ghost: and these three are\l"
    .string "one.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_8::
    .string "And there are three that bear\n"
    .string "witness in earth, the Spirit, and\l"
    .string "the water, and the blood: and these\l"
    .string "three agree in one.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_9::
    .string "If we receive the witness of men,\n"
    .string "the witness of God is greater: for\l"
    .string "this is the witness of God which he\l"
    .string "hath testified of his Son.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_10::
    .string "He that believeth on the Son of God\n"
    .string "hath the witness in himself: he that\l"
    .string "believeth not God hath made him a\l"
    .string "liar; because he believeth not the\l"
    .string "record that God gave of his Son.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_11::
    .string "And this is the record, that God\n"
    .string "hath given to us eternal life, and\l"
    .string "this life is in his Son.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_12::
    .string "He that hath the Son hath life; and\n"
    .string "he that hath not the Son of God hath\l"
    .string "not life.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_13::
    .string "These things have I written unto you\n"
    .string "that believe on the name of the Son\l"
    .string "of God; that ye may know that ye have\l"
    .string "eternal life, and that ye may\l"
    .string "believe on the name of the Son of God.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_14::
    .string "And this is the confidence that we\n"
    .string "have in him, that, if we ask any thing\l"
    .string "according to his will, he heareth\l"
    .string "us:"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_15::
    .string "And if we know that he hear us,\n"
    .string "whatsoever we ask, we know that we\l"
    .string "have the petitions that we desired\l"
    .string "of him$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_16::
    .string "If any man see his brother sin a sin\n"
    .string "which is not unto death, he shall\l"
    .string "ask, and he shall give him life for\l"
    .string "them that sin not unto death. There\l"
    .string "is a sin unto death: I do not say that\l"
    .string "he shall pray for it.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_17::
    .string "All unrighteousness is sin: and\n"
    .string "there is a sin not unto death.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_18::
    .string "We know that whosoever is born of\n"
    .string "God sinneth not; but he that is\l"
    .string "begotten of God keepeth himself,\l"
    .string "and that wicked one toucheth him not.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_19::
    .string "And we know that we are of God, and\n"
    .string "the whole world lieth in\l"
    .string "wickedness.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_20::
    .string "And we know that the Son of God is\n"
    .string "come, and hath given us an\l"
    .string "understanding, that we may know him\l"
    .string "that is true, and we are in him that\l"
    .string "is true, even in his Son Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ. This is the true God, and\l"
    .string "eternal life.$"
Bible_Text_1_John_5_21::
    .string "Little children, keep yourselves\n"
    .string "from idols. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_1::
    .string "The elder unto the elect lady and\n"
    .string "her children, whom I love in the\l"
    .string "truth; and not I only, but also all\l"
    .string "they that have known the truth;"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_2::
    .string "For the truth’s sake, which\n"
    .string "dwelleth in us, and shall be with\l"
    .string "us for ever$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_3::
    .string "Grace be with you, mercy, and peace,\n"
    .string "from God the Father, and from the\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the\l"
    .string "Father, in truth and love.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_4::
    .string "I rejoiced greatly that I found of\n"
    .string "thy children walking in truth, as we\l"
    .string "have received a commandment from the\l"
    .string "Father.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_5::
    .string "And now I beseech thee, lady, not as\n"
    .string "though I wrote a new commandment unto\l"
    .string "thee, but that which we had from the\l"
    .string "beginning, that we love one another.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_6::
    .string "And this is love, that we walk\n"
    .string "after his commandments. This is the\l"
    .string "commandment, That, as ye have heard\l"
    .string "from the beginning, ye should walk\l"
    .string "in it.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_7::
    .string "For many deceivers are entered into\n"
    .string "the world, who confess not that\l"
    .string "Jesus Christ is come in the flesh.\l"
    .string "This is a deceiver and an antichrist.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_8::
    .string "Look to yourselves, that we lose\n"
    .string "not those things which we have\l"
    .string "wrought, but that we receive a full\l"
    .string "reward.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_9::
    .string "Whosoever transgresseth, and\n"
    .string "abideth not in the doctrine of\l"
    .string "Christ, hath not God. He that abideth\l"
    .string "in the doctrine of Christ, he hath\l"
    .string "both the Father and the Son.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_10::
    .string "If there come any unto you, and\n"
    .string "bring not this doctrine, receive him\l"
    .string "not into your house, neither bid him\l"
    .string "God speed:"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_11::
    .string "For he that biddeth him God speed\n"
    .string "is partaker of his evil deeds$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_12::
    .string "Having many things to write unto\n"
    .string "you, I would not write with paper\l"
    .string "and ink: but I trust to come unto you,\l"
    .string "and speak face to face, that our joy\l"
    .string "may be full.$"
Bible_Text_2_John_1_13::
    .string "The children of thy elect sister\n"
    .string "greet thee. Amen.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_1::
    .string "The elder unto the wellbeloved\n"
    .string "Gaius, whom I love in the truth.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_2::
    .string "Beloved, I wish above all things\n"
    .string "that thou mayest prosper and be in\l"
    .string "health, even as thy soul\l"
    .string "prospereth.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_3::
    .string "For I rejoiced greatly, when the\n"
    .string "brethren came and testified of the\l"
    .string "truth that is in thee, even as thou\l"
    .string "walkest in the truth.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_4::
    .string "I have no greater joy than to hear\n"
    .string "that my children walk in truth.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_5::
    .string "Beloved, thou doest faithfully\n"
    .string "whatsoever thou doest to the\l"
    .string "brethren, and to strangers;"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_6::
    .string "Which have borne witness of thy\n"
    .string "charity before the church: whom if\l"
    .string "thou bring forward on their journey\l"
    .string "after a godly sort, thou shalt do\l"
    .string "well:"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_7::
    .string "Because that for his name’s sake\n"
    .string "they went forth, taking nothing of\l"
    .string "the Gentiles$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_8::
    .string "We therefore ought to receive such,\n"
    .string "that we might be fellowhelpers to\l"
    .string "the truth.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_9::
    .string "I wrote unto the church: but\n"
    .string "Diotrephes, who loveth to have the\l"
    .string "preeminence among them, receiveth us\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_10::
    .string "Wherefore, if I come, I will\n"
    .string "remember his deeds which he doeth,\l"
    .string "prating against us with malicious\l"
    .string "words: and not content therewith,\l"
    .string "neither doth he himself receive the\l"
    .string "brethren, and forbiddeth them that\l"
    .string "would, and casteth them out of the\l"
    .string "church.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_11::
    .string "Beloved, follow not that which is\n"
    .string "evil, but that which is good. He that\l"
    .string "doeth good is of God: but he that\l"
    .string "doeth evil hath not seen God.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_12::
    .string "Demetrius hath good report of all\n"
    .string "men, and of the truth itself: yea,\l"
    .string "and we also bear record; and ye know\l"
    .string "that our record is true.$"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_13::
    .string "I had many things to write, but I\n"
    .string "will not with ink and pen write\l"
    .string "unto thee:"
Bible_Text_3_John_1_14::
    .string "But I trust I shall shortly see\n"
    .string "thee, and we shall speak face to\l"
    .string "face. Peace be to thee. Our friends\l"
    .string "salute thee. Greet the friends by\l"
    .string "name$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_1::
    .string "Jude, the servant of Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "and brother of James, to them that\l"
    .string "are sanctified by God the Father, and\l"
    .string "preserved in Jesus Christ, and\l"
    .string "called:"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_2::
    .string "Mercy unto you, and peace, and\n"
    .string "love, be multiplied$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_3::
    .string "Beloved, when I gave all\n"
    .string "diligence to write unto you of the\l"
    .string "common salvation, it was needful\l"
    .string "for me to write unto you, and exhort\l"
    .string "you that ye should earnestly\l"
    .string "contend for the faith which was once\l"
    .string "delivered unto the saints.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_4::
    .string "For there are certain men crept in\n"
    .string "unawares, who were before of old\l"
    .string "ordained to this condemnation,\l"
    .string "ungodly men, turning the grace of\l"
    .string "our God into lasciviousness, and\l"
    .string "denying the only Lord God, and our\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_5::
    .string "I will therefore put you in\n"
    .string "remembrance, though ye once knew\l"
    .string "this, how that the Lord, having saved\l"
    .string "the people out of the land of\l"
    .string "Egypt, afterward destroyed them that\l"
    .string "believed not.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_6::
    .string "And the angels which kept not\n"
    .string "their first estate, but left their\l"
    .string "own habitation, he hath reserved in\l"
    .string "everlasting chains under darkness\l"
    .string "unto the judgment of the great day.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_7::
    .string "Even as Sodom and Gomorrha, and the\n"
    .string "cities about them in like manner,\l"
    .string "giving themselves over to\l"
    .string "fornication, and going after strange\l"
    .string "flesh, are set forth for an\l"
    .string "example, suffering the vengeance of\l"
    .string "eternal fire.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_8::
    .string "Likewise also these filthy\n"
    .string "dreamers defile the flesh, despise\l"
    .string "dominion, and speak evil of\l"
    .string "dignities.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_9::
    .string "Yet Michael the archangel, when\n"
    .string "contending with the devil he\l"
    .string "disputed about the body of Moses,\l"
    .string "durst not bring against him a\l"
    .string "railing accusation, but said, The\l"
    .string "Lord rebuke thee.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_10::
    .string "But these speak evil of those\n"
    .string "things which they know not: but what\l"
    .string "they know naturally, as brute\l"
    .string "beasts, in those things they corrupt\l"
    .string "themselves.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_11::
    .string "Woe unto them! for they have gone in\n"
    .string "the way of Cain, and ran greedily\l"
    .string "after the error of Balaam for\l"
    .string "reward, and perished in the\l"
    .string "gainsaying of Core.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_12::
    .string "These are spots in your feasts of\n"
    .string "charity, when they feast with you,\l"
    .string "feeding themselves without fear:\l"
    .string "clouds they are without water,\l"
    .string "carried about of winds; trees whose\l"
    .string "fruit withereth, without fruit,\l"
    .string "twice dead, plucked up by the\l"
    .string "roots;"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_13::
    .string "Raging waves of the sea, foaming out\n"
    .string "their own shame; wandering stars, to\l"
    .string "whom is reserved the blackness of\l"
    .string "darkness for ever$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_14::
    .string "And Enoch also, the seventh from\n"
    .string "Adam, prophesied of these, saying,\l"
    .string "Behold, the Lord cometh with ten\l"
    .string "thousands of his saints,"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_15::
    .string "To execute judgment upon all, and\n"
    .string "to convince all that are ungodly\l"
    .string "among them of all their ungodly\l"
    .string "deeds which they have ungodly\l"
    .string "committed, and of all their hard\l"
    .string "speeches which ungodly sinners have\l"
    .string "spoken against him$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_16::
    .string "These are murmurers, complainers,\n"
    .string "walking after their own lusts; and\l"
    .string "their mouth speaketh great\l"
    .string "swelling words, having men’s\l"
    .string "persons in admiration because of\l"
    .string "advantage.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_17::
    .string "But, beloved, remember ye the words\n"
    .string "which were spoken before of the\l"
    .string "apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ;"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_18::
    .string "How that they told you there\n"
    .string "should be mockers in the last time,\l"
    .string "who should walk after their own\l"
    .string "ungodly lusts$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_19::
    .string "These be they who separate\n"
    .string "themselves, sensual, having not the\l"
    .string "Spirit.$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_20::
    .string "But ye, beloved, building up\n"
    .string "yourselves on your most holy faith,\l"
    .string "praying in the Holy Ghost,"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_21::
    .string "Keep yourselves in the love of\n"
    .string "God, looking for the mercy of our\l"
    .string "Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_22::
    .string "And of some have compassion, making\n"
    .string "a difference:"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_23::
    .string "And others save with fear, pulling\n"
    .string "them out of the fire; hating even the\l"
    .string "garment spotted by the flesh$"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_24::
    .string "Now unto him that is able to keep\n"
    .string "you from falling, and to present\l"
    .string "you faultless before the presence\l"
    .string "of his glory with exceeding joy,"
Bible_Text_Jude_1_25::
    .string "To the only wise God our Saviour, be\n"
    .string "glory and majesty, dominion and\l"
    .string "power, both now and ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_1::
    .string "The Revelation of Jesus Christ,\n"
    .string "which God gave unto him, to shew unto\l"
    .string "his servants things which must\l"
    .string "shortly come to pass; and he sent\l"
    .string "and signified it by his angel unto\l"
    .string "his servant John:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_2::
    .string "Who bare record of the word of God,\n"
    .string "and of the testimony of Jesus Christ,\l"
    .string "and of all things that he saw$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_3::
    .string "Blessed is he that readeth, and\n"
    .string "they that hear the words of this\l"
    .string "prophecy, and keep those things\l"
    .string "which are written therein: for the\l"
    .string "time is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_4::
    .string "John to the seven churches which are\n"
    .string "in Asia: Grace be unto you, and\l"
    .string "peace, from him which is, and which\l"
    .string "was, and which is to come; and from\l"
    .string "the seven Spirits which are before\l"
    .string "his throne;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_5::
    .string "And from Jesus Christ, who is the\n"
    .string "faithful witness, and the first\l"
    .string "begotten of the dead, and the prince\l"
    .string "of the kings of the earth. Unto him\l"
    .string "that loved us, and washed us from our\l"
    .string "sins in his own blood,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_6::
    .string "And hath made us kings and priests\n"
    .string "unto God and his Father; to him be\l"
    .string "glory and dominion for ever and\l"
    .string "ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_7::
    .string "Behold, he cometh with clouds; and\n"
    .string "every eye shall see him, and they\l"
    .string "also which pierced him: and all\l"
    .string "kindreds of the earth shall wail\l"
    .string "because of him. Even so, Amen.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_8::
    .string "I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning\n"
    .string "and the ending, saith the Lord, which\l"
    .string "is, and which was, and which is to\l"
    .string "come, the Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_9::
    .string "I John, who also am your brother,\n"
    .string "and companion in tribulation, and\l"
    .string "in the kingdom and patience of Jesus\l"
    .string "Christ, was in the isle that is\l"
    .string "called Patmos, for the word of God,\l"
    .string "and for the testimony of Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_10::
    .string "I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s\n"
    .string "day, and heard behind me a great\l"
    .string "voice, as of a trumpet,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_11::
    .string "Saying, I am Alpha and Omega, the\n"
    .string "first and the last: and, What thou\l"
    .string "seest, write in a book, and send it\l"
    .string "unto the seven churches which are in\l"
    .string "Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna,\l"
    .string "and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira,\l"
    .string "and unto Sardis, and unto\l"
    .string "Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_12::
    .string "And I turned to see the voice that\n"
    .string "spake with me. And being turned, I\l"
    .string "saw seven golden candlesticks;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_13::
    .string "And in the midst of the seven\n"
    .string "candlesticks one like unto the Son\l"
    .string "of man, clothed with a garment down\l"
    .string "to the foot, and girt about the paps\l"
    .string "with a golden girdle$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_14::
    .string "His head and his hairs were white\n"
    .string "like wool, as white as snow; and his\l"
    .string "eyes were as a flame of fire;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_15::
    .string "And his feet like unto fine brass,\n"
    .string "as if they burned in a furnace; and\l"
    .string "his voice as the sound of many waters$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_16::
    .string "And he had in his right hand seven\n"
    .string "stars: and out of his mouth went a\l"
    .string "sharp twoedged sword: and his\l"
    .string "countenance was as the sun shineth in\l"
    .string "his strength.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_17::
    .string "And when I saw him, I fell at his\n"
    .string "feet as dead. And he laid his right\l"
    .string "hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear\l"
    .string "not; I am the first and the last:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_18::
    .string "I am he that liveth, and was dead;\n"
    .string "and, behold, I am alive for\l"
    .string "evermore, Amen; and have the keys of\l"
    .string "hell and of death$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_19::
    .string "Write the things which thou hast\n"
    .string "seen, and the things which are, and\l"
    .string "the things which shall be\l"
    .string "hereafter;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_1_20::
    .string "The mystery of the seven stars which\n"
    .string "thou sawest in my right hand, and the\l"
    .string "seven golden candlesticks. The\l"
    .string "seven stars are the angels of the\l"
    .string "seven churches: and the seven\l"
    .string "candlesticks which thou sawest are\l"
    .string "the seven churches$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_1::
    .string "Unto the angel of the church of\n"
    .string "Ephesus write; These things saith he\l"
    .string "that holdeth the seven stars in his\l"
    .string "right hand, who walketh in the midst\l"
    .string "of the seven golden candlesticks;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_2::
    .string "I know thy works, and thy labour,\n"
    .string "and thy patience, and how thou canst\l"
    .string "not bear them which are evil: and\l"
    .string "thou hast tried them which say they\l"
    .string "are apostles, and are not, and hast\l"
    .string "found them liars:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_3::
    .string "And hast borne, and hast patience,\n"
    .string "and for my name’s sake hast\l"
    .string "laboured, and hast not fainted$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_4::
    .string "Nevertheless I have somewhat\n"
    .string "against thee, because thou hast left\l"
    .string "thy first love.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_5::
    .string "Remember therefore from whence thou\n"
    .string "art fallen, and repent, and do the\l"
    .string "first works; or else I will come\l"
    .string "unto thee quickly, and will remove\l"
    .string "thy candlestick out of his place,\l"
    .string "except thou repent.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_6::
    .string "But this thou hast, that thou hatest\n"
    .string "the deeds of the Nicolaitanes, which\l"
    .string "I also hate.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_7::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches; To him that overcometh\l"
    .string "will I give to eat of the tree of\l"
    .string "life, which is in the midst of the\l"
    .string "paradise of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_8::
    .string "And unto the angel of the church in\n"
    .string "Smyrna write; These things saith the\l"
    .string "first and the last, which was dead,\l"
    .string "and is alive;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_9::
    .string "I know thy works, and tribulation,\n"
    .string "and poverty, (but thou art rich) and\l"
    .string "I know the blasphemy of them which\l"
    .string "say they are Jews, and are not, but\l"
    .string "are the synagogue of Satan$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_10::
    .string "Fear none of those things which thou\n"
    .string "shalt suffer: behold, the devil\l"
    .string "shall cast some of you into prison,\l"
    .string "that ye may be tried; and ye shall\l"
    .string "have tribulation ten days: be thou\l"
    .string "faithful unto death, and I will\l"
    .string "give thee a crown of life.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_11::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches; He that overcometh shall\l"
    .string "not be hurt of the second death.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_12::
    .string "And to the angel of the church in\n"
    .string "Pergamos write; These things saith he\l"
    .string "which hath the sharp sword with two\l"
    .string "edges;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_13::
    .string "I know thy works, and where thou\n"
    .string "dwellest, even where Satan’s seat\l"
    .string "is: and thou holdest fast my name,\l"
    .string "and hast not denied my faith, even in\l"
    .string "those days wherein Antipas was my\l"
    .string "faithful martyr, who was slain\l"
    .string "among you, where Satan dwelleth$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_14::
    .string "But I have a few things against\n"
    .string "thee, because thou hast there them\l"
    .string "that hold the doctrine of Balaam,\l"
    .string "who taught Balac to cast a\l"
    .string "stumblingblock before the children\l"
    .string "of Israel, to eat things sacrificed\l"
    .string "unto idols, and to commit\l"
    .string "fornication.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_15::
    .string "So hast thou also them that hold\n"
    .string "the doctrine of the Nicolaitanes,\l"
    .string "which thing I hate.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_16::
    .string "Repent; or else I will come unto\n"
    .string "thee quickly, and will fight\l"
    .string "against them with the sword of my\l"
    .string "mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_17::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches; To him that overcometh\l"
    .string "will I give to eat of the hidden\l"
    .string "manna, and will give him a white\l"
    .string "stone, and in the stone a new name\l"
    .string "written, which no man knoweth saving\l"
    .string "he that receiveth it.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_18::
    .string "And unto the angel of the church in\n"
    .string "Thyatira write; These things saith\l"
    .string "the Son of God, who hath his eyes\l"
    .string "like unto a flame of fire, and his\l"
    .string "feet are like fine brass;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_19::
    .string "I know thy works, and charity, and\n"
    .string "service, and faith, and thy\l"
    .string "patience, and thy works; and the\l"
    .string "last to be more than the first$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_20::
    .string "Notwithstanding I have a few things\n"
    .string "against thee, because thou sufferest\l"
    .string "that woman Jezebel, which calleth\l"
    .string "herself a prophetess, to teach and\l"
    .string "to seduce my servants to commit\l"
    .string "fornication, and to eat things\l"
    .string "sacrificed unto idols.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_21::
    .string "And I gave her space to repent of\n"
    .string "her fornication; and she repented\l"
    .string "not.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_22::
    .string "Behold, I will cast her into a\n"
    .string "bed, and them that commit adultery\l"
    .string "with her into great tribulation,\l"
    .string "except they repent of their deeds.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_23::
    .string "And I will kill her children\n"
    .string "with death; and all the churches\l"
    .string "shall know that I am he which\l"
    .string "searcheth the reins and hearts: and I\l"
    .string "will give unto every one of you\l"
    .string "according to your works.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_24::
    .string "But unto you I say, and unto the rest\n"
    .string "in Thyatira, as many as have not this\l"
    .string "doctrine, and which have not known\l"
    .string "the depths of Satan, as they speak;\l"
    .string "I will put upon you none other\l"
    .string "burden.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_25::
    .string "But that which ye have already\n"
    .string "hold fast till I come.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_26::
    .string "And he that overcometh, and keepeth\n"
    .string "my works unto the end, to him will I\l"
    .string "give power over the nations:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_27::
    .string "And he shall rule them with a rod\n"
    .string "of iron; as the vessels of a potter\l"
    .string "shall they be broken to shivers:\l"
    .string "even as I received of my Father$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_28::
    .string "And I will give him the morning\n"
    .string "star.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_2_29::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_1::
    .string "And unto the angel of the church in\n"
    .string "Sardis write; These things saith he\l"
    .string "that hath the seven Spirits of God,\l"
    .string "and the seven stars; I know thy\l"
    .string "works, that thou hast a name that\l"
    .string "thou livest, and art dead.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_2::
    .string "Be watchful, and strengthen the\n"
    .string "things which remain, that are ready\l"
    .string "to die: for I have not found thy works\l"
    .string "perfect before God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_3::
    .string "Remember therefore how thou hast\n"
    .string "received and heard, and hold fast,\l"
    .string "and repent. If therefore thou shalt\l"
    .string "not watch, I will come on thee as a\l"
    .string "thief, and thou shalt not know what\l"
    .string "hour I will come upon thee.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_4::
    .string "Thou hast a few names even in Sardis\n"
    .string "which have not defiled their\l"
    .string "garments; and they shall walk with\l"
    .string "me in white: for they are worthy.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_5::
    .string "He that overcometh, the same shall\n"
    .string "be clothed in white raiment; and I\l"
    .string "will not blot out his name out of\l"
    .string "the book of life, but I will\l"
    .string "confess his name before my Father,\l"
    .string "and before his angels.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_6::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_7::
    .string "And to the angel of the church in\n"
    .string "Philadelphia write; These things\l"
    .string "saith he that is holy, he that is\l"
    .string "true, he that hath the key of David,\l"
    .string "he that openeth, and no man\l"
    .string "shutteth; and shutteth, and no man\l"
    .string "openeth;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_8::
    .string "I know thy works: behold, I have set\n"
    .string "before thee an open door, and no man\l"
    .string "can shut it: for thou hast a little\l"
    .string "strength, and hast kept my word, and\l"
    .string "hast not denied my name$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_9::
    .string "Behold, I will make them of the\n"
    .string "synagogue of Satan, which say they\l"
    .string "are Jews, and are not, but do lie;\l"
    .string "behold, I will make them to come\l"
    .string "and worship before thy feet, and to\l"
    .string "know that I have loved thee.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_10::
    .string "Because thou hast kept the word of\n"
    .string "my patience, I also will keep thee\l"
    .string "from the hour of temptation, which\l"
    .string "shall come upon all the world, to\l"
    .string "try them that dwell upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_11::
    .string "Behold, I come quickly: hold that\n"
    .string "fast which thou hast, that no man\l"
    .string "take thy crown.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_12::
    .string "Him that overcometh will I make a\n"
    .string "pillar in the temple of my God, and\l"
    .string "he shall go no more out: and I will\l"
    .string "write upon him the name of my God,\l"
    .string "and the name of the city of my God,\l"
    .string "which is new Jerusalem, which cometh\l"
    .string "down out of heaven from my God: and I\l"
    .string "will write upon him my new name.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_13::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_14::
    .string "And unto the angel of the church of\n"
    .string "the Laodiceans write; These things\l"
    .string "saith the Amen, the faithful and\l"
    .string "true witness, the beginning of the\l"
    .string "creation of God;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_15::
    .string "I know thy works, that thou art\n"
    .string "neither cold nor hot: I would thou\l"
    .string "wert cold or hot$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_16::
    .string "So then because thou art lukewarm,\n"
    .string "and neither cold nor hot, I will\l"
    .string "spue thee out of my mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_17::
    .string "Because thou sayest, I am rich, and\n"
    .string "increased with goods, and have need\l"
    .string "of nothing; and knowest not that thou\l"
    .string "art wretched, and miserable, and\l"
    .string "poor, and blind, and naked:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_18::
    .string "I counsel thee to buy of me gold\n"
    .string "tried in the fire, that thou mayest\l"
    .string "be rich; and white raiment, that thou\l"
    .string "mayest be clothed, and that the\l"
    .string "shame of thy nakedness do not\l"
    .string "appear; and anoint thine eyes with\l"
    .string "eyesalve, that thou mayest see$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_19::
    .string "As many as I love, I rebuke and\n"
    .string "chasten: be zealous therefore, and\l"
    .string "repent.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_20::
    .string "Behold, I stand at the door, and\n"
    .string "knock: if any man hear my voice, and\l"
    .string "open the door, I will come in to\l"
    .string "him, and will sup with him, and he\l"
    .string "with me.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_21::
    .string "To him that overcometh will I\n"
    .string "grant to sit with me in my throne,\l"
    .string "even as I also overcame, and am set\l"
    .string "down with my Father in his throne.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_3_22::
    .string "He that hath an ear, let him hear\n"
    .string "what the Spirit saith unto the\l"
    .string "churches.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_1::
    .string "After this I looked, and, behold, a\n"
    .string "door was opened in heaven: and the\l"
    .string "first voice which I heard was as it\l"
    .string "were of a trumpet talking with me;\l"
    .string "which said, Come up hither, and I\l"
    .string "will shew thee things which must be\l"
    .string "hereafter.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_2::
    .string "And immediately I was in the\n"
    .string "spirit: and, behold, a throne was\l"
    .string "set in heaven, and one sat on the\l"
    .string "throne.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_3::
    .string "And he that sat was to look upon\n"
    .string "like a jasper and a sardine stone:\l"
    .string "and there was a rainbow round about\l"
    .string "the throne, in sight like unto an\l"
    .string "emerald.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_4::
    .string "And round about the throne were four\n"
    .string "and twenty seats: and upon the seats\l"
    .string "I saw four and twenty elders\l"
    .string "sitting, clothed in white raiment;\l"
    .string "and they had on their heads crowns of\l"
    .string "gold.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_5::
    .string "And out of the throne proceeded\n"
    .string "lightnings and thunderings and\l"
    .string "voices: and there were seven lamps\l"
    .string "of fire burning before the throne,\l"
    .string "which are the seven Spirits of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_6::
    .string "And before the throne there was a\n"
    .string "sea of glass like unto crystal: and\l"
    .string "in the midst of the throne, and round\l"
    .string "about the throne, were four beasts\l"
    .string "full of eyes before and behind.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_7::
    .string "And the first beast was like a\n"
    .string "lion, and the second beast like a\l"
    .string "calf, and the third beast had a face\l"
    .string "as a man, and the fourth beast was\l"
    .string "like a flying eagle.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_8::
    .string "And the four beasts had each of them\n"
    .string "six wings about him; and they were\l"
    .string "full of eyes within: and they rest\l"
    .string "not day and night, saying, Holy,\l"
    .string "holy, holy, LORD God Almighty,\l"
    .string "which was, and is, and is to come.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_9::
    .string "And when those beasts give glory\n"
    .string "and honour and thanks to him that sat\l"
    .string "on the throne, who liveth for ever\l"
    .string "and ever,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_10::
    .string "The four and twenty elders fall\n"
    .string "down before him that sat on the\l"
    .string "throne, and worship him that liveth\l"
    .string "for ever and ever, and cast their\l"
    .string "crowns before the throne, saying,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_4_11::
    .string "Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive\n"
    .string "glory and honour and power: for thou\l"
    .string "hast created all things, and for thy\l"
    .string "pleasure they are and were created$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_1::
    .string "And I saw in the right hand of him\n"
    .string "that sat on the throne a book written\l"
    .string "within and on the backside, sealed\l"
    .string "with seven seals.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_2::
    .string "And I saw a strong angel\n"
    .string "proclaiming with a loud voice, Who\l"
    .string "is worthy to open the book, and to\l"
    .string "loose the seals thereof?"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_3::
    .string "And no man in heaven, nor in earth,\n"
    .string "neither under the earth, was able to\l"
    .string "open the book, neither to look\l"
    .string "thereon$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_4::
    .string "And I wept much, because no man was\n"
    .string "found worthy to open and to read the\l"
    .string "book, neither to look thereon.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_5::
    .string "And one of the elders saith unto me,\n"
    .string "Weep not: behold, the Lion of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Juda, the Root of David,\l"
    .string "hath prevailed to open the book,\l"
    .string "and to loose the seven seals\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_6::
    .string "And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst\n"
    .string "of the throne and of the four beasts,\l"
    .string "and in the midst of the elders, stood\l"
    .string "a Lamb as it had been slain, having\l"
    .string "seven horns and seven eyes, which are\l"
    .string "the seven Spirits of God sent forth\l"
    .string "into all the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_7::
    .string "And he came and took the book out of\n"
    .string "the right hand of him that sat upon\l"
    .string "the throne.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_8::
    .string "And when he had taken the book, the\n"
    .string "four beasts and four and twenty\l"
    .string "elders fell down before the Lamb,\l"
    .string "having every one of them harps, and\l"
    .string "golden vials full of odours, which\l"
    .string "are the prayers of saints.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_9::
    .string "And they sung a new song, saying,\n"
    .string "Thou art worthy to take the book, and\l"
    .string "to open the seals thereof: for thou\l"
    .string "wast slain, and hast redeemed us to\l"
    .string "God by thy blood out of every\l"
    .string "kindred, and tongue, and people,\l"
    .string "and nation;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_10::
    .string "And hast made us unto our God kings\n"
    .string "and priests: and we shall reign on\l"
    .string "the earth$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_11::
    .string "And I beheld, and I heard the voice\n"
    .string "of many angels round about the\l"
    .string "throne and the beasts and the\l"
    .string "elders: and the number of them was\l"
    .string "ten thousand times ten thousand, and\l"
    .string "thousands of thousands;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_12::
    .string "Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is\n"
    .string "the Lamb that was slain to receive\l"
    .string "power, and riches, and wisdom, and\l"
    .string "strength, and honour, and glory, and\l"
    .string "blessing$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_13::
    .string "And every creature which is in\n"
    .string "heaven, and on the earth, and under\l"
    .string "the earth, and such as are in the sea,\l"
    .string "and all that are in them, heard I\l"
    .string "saying, Blessing, and honour, and\l"
    .string "glory, and power, be unto him that\l"
    .string "sitteth upon the throne, and unto\l"
    .string "the Lamb for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_5_14::
    .string "And the four beasts said, Amen. And\n"
    .string "the four and twenty elders fell\l"
    .string "down and worshipped him that\l"
    .string "liveth for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_1::
    .string "And I saw when the Lamb opened one\n"
    .string "of the seals, and I heard, as it were\l"
    .string "the noise of thunder, one of the four\l"
    .string "beasts saying, Come and see.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_2::
    .string "And I saw, and behold a white horse:\n"
    .string "and he that sat on him had a bow; and\l"
    .string "a crown was given unto him: and he\l"
    .string "went forth conquering, and to\l"
    .string "conquer.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_3::
    .string "And when he had opened the second\n"
    .string "seal, I heard the second beast say,\l"
    .string "Come and see.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_4::
    .string "And there went out another horse\n"
    .string "that was red: and power was given to\l"
    .string "him that sat thereon to take peace\l"
    .string "from the earth, and that they should\l"
    .string "kill one another: and there was\l"
    .string "given unto him a great sword.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_5::
    .string "And when he had opened the third\n"
    .string "seal, I heard the third beast say,\l"
    .string "Come and see. And I beheld, and lo a\l"
    .string "black horse; and he that sat on him\l"
    .string "had a pair of balances in his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_6::
    .string "And I heard a voice in the midst of\n"
    .string "the four beasts say, A measure of\l"
    .string "wheat for a penny, and three\l"
    .string "measures of barley for a penny; and\l"
    .string "see thou hurt not the oil and the\l"
    .string "wine.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_7::
    .string "And when he had opened the fourth\n"
    .string "seal, I heard the voice of the fourth\l"
    .string "beast say, Come and see.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_8::
    .string "And I looked, and behold a pale\n"
    .string "horse: and his name that sat on him\l"
    .string "was Death, and Hell followed with\l"
    .string "him. And power was given unto them\l"
    .string "over the fourth part of the earth, to\l"
    .string "kill with sword, and with hunger,\l"
    .string "and with death, and with the beasts\l"
    .string "of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_9::
    .string "And when he had opened the fifth\n"
    .string "seal, I saw under the altar the\l"
    .string "souls of them that were slain for\l"
    .string "the word of God, and for the\l"
    .string "testimony which they held:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_10::
    .string "And they cried with a loud voice,\n"
    .string "saying, How long, O Lord, holy and\l"
    .string "true, dost thou not judge and avenge\l"
    .string "our blood on them that dwell on the\l"
    .string "earth?"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_11::
    .string "And white robes were given unto\n"
    .string "every one of them; and it was said\l"
    .string "unto them, that they should rest yet\l"
    .string "for a little season, until their\l"
    .string "fellowservants also and their\l"
    .string "brethren, that should be killed as\l"
    .string "they were, should be fulfilled$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_12::
    .string "And I beheld when he had opened the\n"
    .string "sixth seal, and, lo, there was a\l"
    .string "great earthquake; and the sun became\l"
    .string "black as sackcloth of hair, and the\l"
    .string "moon became as blood;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_13::
    .string "And the stars of heaven fell unto\n"
    .string "the earth, even as a fig tree casteth\l"
    .string "her untimely figs, when she is\l"
    .string "shaken of a mighty wind$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_14::
    .string "And the heaven departed as a\n"
    .string "scroll when it is rolled together;\l"
    .string "and every mountain and island were\l"
    .string "moved out of their places.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_15::
    .string "And the kings of the earth, and the\n"
    .string "great men, and the rich men, and the\l"
    .string "chief captains, and the mighty men,\l"
    .string "and every bondman, and every free\l"
    .string "man, hid themselves in the dens and\l"
    .string "in the rocks of the mountains;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_16::
    .string "And said to the mountains and rocks,\n"
    .string "Fall on us, and hide us from the\l"
    .string "face of him that sitteth on the\l"
    .string "throne, and from the wrath of the\l"
    .string "Lamb:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_6_17::
    .string "For the great day of his wrath is\n"
    .string "come; and who shall be able to\l"
    .string "stand?"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_1::
    .string "And after these things I saw four\n"
    .string "angels standing on the four corners\l"
    .string "of the earth, holding the four winds\l"
    .string "of the earth, that the wind should\l"
    .string "not blow on the earth, nor on the\l"
    .string "sea, nor on any tree$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_2::
    .string "And I saw another angel ascending\n"
    .string "from the east, having the seal of the\l"
    .string "living God: and he cried with a loud\l"
    .string "voice to the four angels, to whom it\l"
    .string "was given to hurt the earth and the\l"
    .string "sea,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_3::
    .string "Saying, Hurt not the earth, neither\n"
    .string "the sea, nor the trees, till we have\l"
    .string "sealed the servants of our God in\l"
    .string "their foreheads$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_4::
    .string "And I heard the number of them which\n"
    .string "were sealed: and there were sealed\l"
    .string "an hundred and forty and four\l"
    .string "thousand of all the tribes of the\l"
    .string "children of Israel.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_5::
    .string "Of the tribe of Juda were sealed\n"
    .string "twelve thousand. Of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Reuben were sealed twelve thousand.\l"
    .string "Of the tribe of Gad were sealed\l"
    .string "twelve thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_6::
    .string "Of the tribe of Aser were sealed\n"
    .string "twelve thousand. Of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Nephthalim were sealed twelve\l"
    .string "thousand. Of the tribe of Manasses\l"
    .string "were sealed twelve thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_7::
    .string "Of the tribe of Simeon were sealed\n"
    .string "twelve thousand. Of the tribe of\l"
    .string "Levi were sealed twelve thousand.\l"
    .string "Of the tribe of Issachar were sealed\l"
    .string "twelve thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_8::
    .string "Of the tribe of Zabulon were\n"
    .string "sealed twelve thousand. Of the\l"
    .string "tribe of Joseph were sealed twelve\l"
    .string "thousand. Of the tribe of Benjamin\l"
    .string "were sealed twelve thousand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_9::
    .string "After this I beheld, and, lo, a\n"
    .string "great multitude, which no man could\l"
    .string "number, of all nations, and\l"
    .string "kindreds, and people, and tongues,\l"
    .string "stood before the throne, and before\l"
    .string "the Lamb, clothed with white robes,\l"
    .string "and palms in their hands;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_10::
    .string "And cried with a loud voice,\n"
    .string "saying, Salvation to our God which\l"
    .string "sitteth upon the throne, and unto\l"
    .string "the Lamb$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_11::
    .string "And all the angels stood round\n"
    .string "about the throne, and about the\l"
    .string "elders and the four beasts, and\l"
    .string "fell before the throne on their\l"
    .string "faces, and worshipped God,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_12::
    .string "Saying, Amen: Blessing, and glory,\n"
    .string "and wisdom, and thanksgiving, and\l"
    .string "honour, and power, and might, be unto\l"
    .string "our God for ever and ever. Amen$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_13::
    .string "And one of the elders answered,\n"
    .string "saying unto me, What are these which\l"
    .string "are arrayed in white robes? and\l"
    .string "whence came they?"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_14::
    .string "And I said unto him, Sir, thou\n"
    .string "knowest. And he said to me, These are\l"
    .string "they which came out of great\l"
    .string "tribulation, and have washed their\l"
    .string "robes, and made them white in the\l"
    .string "blood of the Lamb$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_15::
    .string "Therefore are they before the\n"
    .string "throne of God, and serve him day and\l"
    .string "night in his temple: and he that\l"
    .string "sitteth on the throne shall dwell\l"
    .string "among them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_16::
    .string "They shall hunger no more, neither\n"
    .string "thirst any more; neither shall the\l"
    .string "sun light on them, nor any heat.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_7_17::
    .string "For the Lamb which is in the midst\n"
    .string "of the throne shall feed them, and\l"
    .string "shall lead them unto living\l"
    .string "fountains of waters: and God shall\l"
    .string "wipe away all tears from their eyes.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_1::
    .string "And when he had opened the seventh\n"
    .string "seal, there was silence in heaven\l"
    .string "about the space of half an hour.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_2::
    .string "And I saw the seven angels which\n"
    .string "stood before God; and to them were\l"
    .string "given seven trumpets.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_3::
    .string "And another angel came and stood at\n"
    .string "the altar, having a golden censer;\l"
    .string "and there was given unto him much\l"
    .string "incense, that he should offer it\l"
    .string "with the prayers of all saints\l"
    .string "upon the golden altar which was\l"
    .string "before the throne.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_4::
    .string "And the smoke of the incense, which\n"
    .string "came with the prayers of the saints,\l"
    .string "ascended up before God out of the\l"
    .string "angel’s hand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_5::
    .string "And the angel took the censer, and\n"
    .string "filled it with fire of the altar,\l"
    .string "and cast it into the earth: and there\l"
    .string "were voices, and thunderings, and\l"
    .string "lightnings, and an earthquake.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_6::
    .string "And the seven angels which had the\n"
    .string "seven trumpets prepared\l"
    .string "themselves to sound.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_7::
    .string "The first angel sounded, and there\n"
    .string "followed hail and fire mingled\l"
    .string "with blood, and they were cast upon\l"
    .string "the earth: and the third part of\l"
    .string "trees was burnt up, and all green\l"
    .string "grass was burnt up.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_8::
    .string "And the second angel sounded, and\n"
    .string "as it were a great mountain burning\l"
    .string "with fire was cast into the sea: and\l"
    .string "the third part of the sea became\l"
    .string "blood;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_9::
    .string "And the third part of the creatures\n"
    .string "which were in the sea, and had life,\l"
    .string "died; and the third part of the\l"
    .string "ships were destroyed$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_10::
    .string "And the third angel sounded, and\n"
    .string "there fell a great star from heaven,\l"
    .string "burning as it were a lamp, and it\l"
    .string "fell upon the third part of the\l"
    .string "rivers, and upon the fountains of\l"
    .string "waters;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_11::
    .string "And the name of the star is called\n"
    .string "Wormwood: and the third part of the\l"
    .string "waters became wormwood; and many men\l"
    .string "died of the waters, because they were\l"
    .string "made bitter$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_12::
    .string "And the fourth angel sounded, and\n"
    .string "the third part of the sun was\l"
    .string "smitten, and the third part of the\l"
    .string "moon, and the third part of the\l"
    .string "stars; so as the third part of them\l"
    .string "was darkened, and the day shone not\l"
    .string "for a third part of it, and the night\l"
    .string "likewise.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_8_13::
    .string "And I beheld, and heard an angel\n"
    .string "flying through the midst of heaven,\l"
    .string "saying with a loud voice, Woe, woe,\l"
    .string "woe, to the inhabiters of the earth\l"
    .string "by reason of the other voices of the\l"
    .string "trumpet of the three angels, which\l"
    .string "are yet to sound!"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_1::
    .string "And the fifth angel sounded, and I\n"
    .string "saw a star fall from heaven unto the\l"
    .string "earth: and to him was given the key of\l"
    .string "the bottomless pit$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_2::
    .string "And he opened the bottomless pit;\n"
    .string "and there arose a smoke out of the\l"
    .string "pit, as the smoke of a great furnace;\l"
    .string "and the sun and the air were darkened\l"
    .string "by reason of the smoke of the pit.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_3::
    .string "And there came out of the smoke\n"
    .string "locusts upon the earth: and unto\l"
    .string "them was given power, as the\l"
    .string "scorpions of the earth have power.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_4::
    .string "And it was commanded them that they\n"
    .string "should not hurt the grass of the\l"
    .string "earth, neither any green thing,\l"
    .string "neither any tree; but only those men\l"
    .string "which have not the seal of God in\l"
    .string "their foreheads.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_5::
    .string "And to them it was given that they\n"
    .string "should not kill them, but that they\l"
    .string "should be tormented five months: and\l"
    .string "their torment was as the torment of a\l"
    .string "scorpion, when he striketh a man.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_6::
    .string "And in those days shall men seek\n"
    .string "death, and shall not find it; and\l"
    .string "shall desire to die, and death\l"
    .string "shall flee from them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_7::
    .string "And the shapes of the locusts were\n"
    .string "like unto horses prepared unto\l"
    .string "battle; and on their heads were as it\l"
    .string "were crowns like gold, and their\l"
    .string "faces were as the faces of men.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_8::
    .string "And they had hair as the hair of\n"
    .string "women, and their teeth were as the\l"
    .string "teeth of lions.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_9::
    .string "And they had breastplates, as it\n"
    .string "were breastplates of iron; and the\l"
    .string "sound of their wings was as the sound\l"
    .string "of chariots of many horses running to\l"
    .string "battle.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_10::
    .string "And they had tails like unto\n"
    .string "scorpions, and there were stings in\l"
    .string "their tails: and their power was to\l"
    .string "hurt men five months.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_11::
    .string "And they had a king over them, which\n"
    .string "is the angel of the bottomless pit,\l"
    .string "whose name in the Hebrew tongue is\l"
    .string "Abaddon, but in the Greek tongue hath\l"
    .string "his name Apollyon.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_12::
    .string "One woe is past; and, behold, there\n"
    .string "come two woes more hereafter.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_13::
    .string "And the sixth angel sounded, and I\n"
    .string "heard a voice from the four horns of\l"
    .string "the golden altar which is before\l"
    .string "God,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_14::
    .string "Saying to the sixth angel which had\n"
    .string "the trumpet, Loose the four angels\l"
    .string "which are bound in the great river\l"
    .string "Euphrates$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_15::
    .string "And the four angels were loosed,\n"
    .string "which were prepared for an hour, and\l"
    .string "a day, and a month, and a year, for to\l"
    .string "slay the third part of men.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_16::
    .string "And the number of the army of the\n"
    .string "horsemen were two hundred thousand\l"
    .string "thousand: and I heard the number of\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_17::
    .string "And thus I saw the horses in the\n"
    .string "vision, and them that sat on them,\l"
    .string "having breastplates of fire, and of\l"
    .string "jacinth, and brimstone: and the heads\l"
    .string "of the horses were as the heads of\l"
    .string "lions; and out of their mouths issued\l"
    .string "fire and smoke and brimstone.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_18::
    .string "By these three was the third part\n"
    .string "of men killed, by the fire, and by\l"
    .string "the smoke, and by the brimstone,\l"
    .string "which issued out of their mouths.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_19::
    .string "For their power is in their mouth,\n"
    .string "and in their tails: for their tails\l"
    .string "were like unto serpents, and had\l"
    .string "heads, and with them they do hurt.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_20::
    .string "And the rest of the men which were\n"
    .string "not killed by these plagues yet\l"
    .string "repented not of the works of their\l"
    .string "hands, that they should not worship\l"
    .string "devils, and idols of gold, and\l"
    .string "silver, and brass, and stone, and of\l"
    .string "wood: which neither can see, nor\l"
    .string "hear, nor walk:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_9_21::
    .string "Neither repented they of their\n"
    .string "murders, nor of their sorceries, nor\l"
    .string "of their fornication, nor of their\l"
    .string "thefts$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_1::
    .string "And I saw another mighty angel come\n"
    .string "down from heaven, clothed with a\l"
    .string "cloud: and a rainbow was upon his\l"
    .string "head, and his face was as it were the\l"
    .string "sun, and his feet as pillars of\l"
    .string "fire:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_2::
    .string "And he had in his hand a little\n"
    .string "book open: and he set his right foot\l"
    .string "upon the sea, and his left foot on\l"
    .string "the earth,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_3::
    .string "And cried with a loud voice, as when\n"
    .string "a lion roareth: and when he had\l"
    .string "cried, seven thunders uttered their\l"
    .string "voices$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_4::
    .string "And when the seven thunders had\n"
    .string "uttered their voices, I was about to\l"
    .string "write: and I heard a voice from\l"
    .string "heaven saying unto me, Seal up those\l"
    .string "things which the seven thunders\l"
    .string "uttered, and write them not.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_5::
    .string "And the angel which I saw stand\n"
    .string "upon the sea and upon the earth\l"
    .string "lifted up his hand to heaven,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_6::
    .string "And sware by him that liveth for\n"
    .string "ever and ever, who created heaven,\l"
    .string "and the things that therein are, and\l"
    .string "the earth, and the things that\l"
    .string "therein are, and the sea, and the\l"
    .string "things which are therein, that there\l"
    .string "should be time no longer:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_7::
    .string "But in the days of the voice of the\n"
    .string "seventh angel, when he shall begin\l"
    .string "to sound, the mystery of God should\l"
    .string "be finished, as he hath declared to\l"
    .string "his servants the prophets$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_8::
    .string "And the voice which I heard from\n"
    .string "heaven spake unto me again, and\l"
    .string "said, Go and take the little book\l"
    .string "which is open in the hand of the\l"
    .string "angel which standeth upon the sea\l"
    .string "and upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_9::
    .string "And I went unto the angel, and said\n"
    .string "unto him, Give me the little book.\l"
    .string "And he said unto me, Take it, and eat\l"
    .string "it up; and it shall make thy belly\l"
    .string "bitter, but it shall be in thy mouth\l"
    .string "sweet as honey.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_10::
    .string "And I took the little book out of\n"
    .string "the angel’s hand, and ate it up; and\l"
    .string "it was in my mouth sweet as honey: and\l"
    .string "as soon as I had eaten it, my belly\l"
    .string "was bitter.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_10_11::
    .string "And he said unto me, Thou must\n"
    .string "prophesy again before many\l"
    .string "peoples, and nations, and tongues,\l"
    .string "and kings.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_1::
    .string "And there was given me a reed like\n"
    .string "unto a rod: and the angel stood,\l"
    .string "saying, Rise, and measure the\l"
    .string "temple of God, and the altar, and\l"
    .string "them that worship therein.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_2::
    .string "But the court which is without the\n"
    .string "temple leave out, and measure it\l"
    .string "not; for it is given unto the\l"
    .string "Gentiles: and the holy city shall\l"
    .string "they tread under foot forty and two\l"
    .string "months.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_3::
    .string "And I will give power unto my two\n"
    .string "witnesses, and they shall prophesy\l"
    .string "a thousand two hundred and\l"
    .string "threescore days, clothed in\l"
    .string "sackcloth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_4::
    .string "These are the two olive trees, and\n"
    .string "the two candlesticks standing\l"
    .string "before the God of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_5::
    .string "And if any man will hurt them, fire\n"
    .string "proceedeth out of their mouth, and\l"
    .string "devoureth their enemies: and if any\l"
    .string "man will hurt them, he must in this\l"
    .string "manner be killed.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_6::
    .string "These have power to shut heaven,\n"
    .string "that it rain not in the days of their\l"
    .string "prophecy: and have power over\l"
    .string "waters to turn them to blood, and to\l"
    .string "smite the earth with all plagues,\l"
    .string "as often as they will.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_7::
    .string "And when they shall have finished\n"
    .string "their testimony, the beast that\l"
    .string "ascendeth out of the bottomless pit\l"
    .string "shall make war against them, and\l"
    .string "shall overcome them, and kill them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_8::
    .string "And their dead bodies shall lie in\n"
    .string "the street of the great city, which\l"
    .string "spiritually is called Sodom and\l"
    .string "Egypt, where also our Lord was\l"
    .string "crucified.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_9::
    .string "And they of the people and\n"
    .string "kindreds and tongues and nations\l"
    .string "shall see their dead bodies three\l"
    .string "days and an half, and shall not\l"
    .string "suffer their dead bodies to be put\l"
    .string "in graves.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_10::
    .string "And they that dwell upon the earth\n"
    .string "shall rejoice over them, and make\l"
    .string "merry, and shall send gifts one to\l"
    .string "another; because these two prophets\l"
    .string "tormented them that dwelt on the\l"
    .string "earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_11::
    .string "And after three days and an half\n"
    .string "the spirit of life from God entered\l"
    .string "into them, and they stood upon their\l"
    .string "feet; and great fear fell upon them\l"
    .string "which saw them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_12::
    .string "And they heard a great voice from\n"
    .string "heaven saying unto them, Come up\l"
    .string "hither. And they ascended up to\l"
    .string "heaven in a cloud; and their enemies\l"
    .string "beheld them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_13::
    .string "And the same hour was there a great\n"
    .string "earthquake, and the tenth part of\l"
    .string "the city fell, and in the earthquake\l"
    .string "were slain of men seven thousand:\l"
    .string "and the remnant were affrighted, and\l"
    .string "gave glory to the God of heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_14::
    .string "The second woe is past; and,\n"
    .string "behold, the third woe cometh\l"
    .string "quickly.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_15::
    .string "And the seventh angel sounded; and\n"
    .string "there were great voices in heaven,\l"
    .string "saying, The kingdoms of this world\l"
    .string "are become the kingdoms of our Lord,\l"
    .string "and of his Christ; and he shall\l"
    .string "reign for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_16::
    .string "And the four and twenty elders,\n"
    .string "which sat before God on their seats,\l"
    .string "fell upon their faces, and\l"
    .string "worshipped God,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_17::
    .string "Saying, We give thee thanks, O LORD\n"
    .string "God Almighty, which art, and wast,\l"
    .string "and art to come; because thou hast\l"
    .string "taken to thee thy great power, and\l"
    .string "hast reigned$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_18::
    .string "And the nations were angry, and thy\n"
    .string "wrath is come, and the time of the\l"
    .string "dead, that they should be judged,\l"
    .string "and that thou shouldest give reward\l"
    .string "unto thy servants the prophets, and\l"
    .string "to the saints, and them that fear thy\l"
    .string "name, small and great; and\l"
    .string "shouldest destroy them which\l"
    .string "destroy the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_11_19::
    .string "And the temple of God was opened\n"
    .string "in heaven, and there was seen in his\l"
    .string "temple the ark of his testament: and\l"
    .string "there were lightnings, and voices,\l"
    .string "and thunderings, and an earthquake,\l"
    .string "and great hail.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_1::
    .string "And there appeared a great wonder\n"
    .string "in heaven; a woman clothed with the\l"
    .string "sun, and the moon under her feet, and\l"
    .string "upon her head a crown of twelve\l"
    .string "stars:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_2::
    .string "And she being with child cried,\n"
    .string "travailing in birth, and pained to\l"
    .string "be delivered$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_3::
    .string "And there appeared another wonder\n"
    .string "in heaven; and behold a great red\l"
    .string "dragon, having seven heads and ten\l"
    .string "horns, and seven crowns upon his\l"
    .string "heads.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_4::
    .string "And his tail drew the third part of\n"
    .string "the stars of heaven, and did cast\l"
    .string "them to the earth: and the dragon\l"
    .string "stood before the woman which was\l"
    .string "ready to be delivered, for to devour\l"
    .string "her child as soon as it was born.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_5::
    .string "And she brought forth a man child,\n"
    .string "who was to rule all nations with a\l"
    .string "rod of iron: and her child was caught\l"
    .string "up unto God, and to his throne.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_6::
    .string "And the woman fled into the\n"
    .string "wilderness, where she hath a place\l"
    .string "prepared of God, that they should\l"
    .string "feed her there a thousand two hundred\l"
    .string "and threescore days.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_7::
    .string "And there was war in heaven:\n"
    .string "Michael and his angels fought\l"
    .string "against the dragon; and the dragon\l"
    .string "fought and his angels,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_8::
    .string "And prevailed not; neither was\n"
    .string "their place found any more in heaven$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_9::
    .string "And the great dragon was cast out,\n"
    .string "that old serpent, called the\l"
    .string "Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth\l"
    .string "the whole world: he was cast out\l"
    .string "into the earth, and his angels were\l"
    .string "cast out with him.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_10::
    .string "And I heard a loud voice saying in\n"
    .string "heaven, Now is come salvation, and\l"
    .string "strength, and the kingdom of our God,\l"
    .string "and the power of his Christ: for the\l"
    .string "accuser of our brethren is cast down,\l"
    .string "which accused them before our God day\l"
    .string "and night.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_11::
    .string "And they overcame him by the blood\n"
    .string "of the Lamb, and by the word of their\l"
    .string "testimony; and they loved not their\l"
    .string "lives unto the death.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_12::
    .string "Therefore rejoice, ye heavens, and\n"
    .string "ye that dwell in them. Woe to the\l"
    .string "inhabiters of the earth and of the\l"
    .string "sea! for the devil is come down unto\l"
    .string "you, having great wrath, because he\l"
    .string "knoweth that he hath but a short time.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_13::
    .string "And when the dragon saw that he was\n"
    .string "cast unto the earth, he persecuted\l"
    .string "the woman which brought forth the man\l"
    .string "child.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_14::
    .string "And to the woman were given two\n"
    .string "wings of a great eagle, that she\l"
    .string "might fly into the wilderness, into\l"
    .string "her place, where she is nourished\l"
    .string "for a time, and times, and half a\l"
    .string "time, from the face of the serpent.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_15::
    .string "And the serpent cast out of his\n"
    .string "mouth water as a flood after the\l"
    .string "woman, that he might cause her to be\l"
    .string "carried away of the flood.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_16::
    .string "And the earth helped the woman, and\n"
    .string "the earth opened her mouth, and\l"
    .string "swallowed up the flood which the\l"
    .string "dragon cast out of his mouth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_12_17::
    .string "And the dragon was wroth with the\n"
    .string "woman, and went to make war with the\l"
    .string "remnant of her seed, which keep the\l"
    .string "commandments of God, and have the\l"
    .string "testimony of Jesus Christ.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_1::
    .string "And I stood upon the sand of the\n"
    .string "sea, and saw a beast rise up out of\l"
    .string "the sea, having seven heads and ten\l"
    .string "horns, and upon his horns ten\l"
    .string "crowns, and upon his heads the name\l"
    .string "of blasphemy.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_2::
    .string "And the beast which I saw was like\n"
    .string "unto a leopard, and his feet were as\l"
    .string "the feet of a bear, and his mouth as\l"
    .string "the mouth of a lion: and the dragon\l"
    .string "gave him his power, and his seat, and\l"
    .string "great authority.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_3::
    .string "And I saw one of his heads as it were\n"
    .string "wounded to death; and his deadly\l"
    .string "wound was healed: and all the\l"
    .string "world wondered after the beast.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_4::
    .string "And they worshipped the dragon\n"
    .string "which gave power unto the beast: and\l"
    .string "they worshipped the beast, saying,\l"
    .string "Who is like unto the beast? who is\l"
    .string "able to make war with him?"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_5::
    .string "And there was given unto him a mouth\n"
    .string "speaking great things and\l"
    .string "blasphemies; and power was given\l"
    .string "unto him to continue forty and two\l"
    .string "months$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_6::
    .string "And he opened his mouth in\n"
    .string "blasphemy against God, to\l"
    .string "blaspheme his name, and his\l"
    .string "tabernacle, and them that dwell in\l"
    .string "heaven.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_7::
    .string "And it was given unto him to make\n"
    .string "war with the saints, and to overcome\l"
    .string "them: and power was given him over\l"
    .string "all kindreds, and tongues, and\l"
    .string "nations.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_8::
    .string "And all that dwell upon the\n"
    .string "earth shall worship him, whose\l"
    .string "names are not written in the book of\l"
    .string "life of the Lamb slain from the\l"
    .string "foundation of the world.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_9::
    .string "If any man have an ear, let him hear.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_10::
    .string "He that leadeth into captivity\n"
    .string "shall go into captivity: he that\l"
    .string "killeth with the sword must be\l"
    .string "killed with the sword. Here is the\l"
    .string "patience and the faith of the saints.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_11::
    .string "And I beheld another beast coming\n"
    .string "up out of the earth; and he had two\l"
    .string "horns like a lamb, and he spake as a\l"
    .string "dragon.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_12::
    .string "And he exerciseth all the power of\n"
    .string "the first beast before him, and\l"
    .string "causeth the earth and them which\l"
    .string "dwell therein to worship the first\l"
    .string "beast, whose deadly wound was\l"
    .string "healed.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_13::
    .string "And he doeth great wonders, so that\n"
    .string "he maketh fire come down from heaven\l"
    .string "on the earth in the sight of men,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_14::
    .string "And deceiveth them that dwell on\n"
    .string "the earth by the means of those\l"
    .string "miracles which he had power to do in\l"
    .string "the sight of the beast; saying to\l"
    .string "them that dwell on the earth, that\l"
    .string "they should make an image to the\l"
    .string "beast, which had the wound by a\l"
    .string "sword, and did live$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_15::
    .string "And he had power to give life unto\n"
    .string "the image of the beast, that the\l"
    .string "image of the beast should both\l"
    .string "speak, and cause that as many as\l"
    .string "would not worship the image of the\l"
    .string "beast should be killed.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_16::
    .string "And he causeth all, both small\n"
    .string "and great, rich and poor, free and\l"
    .string "bond, to receive a mark in their\l"
    .string "right hand, or in their foreheads:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_17::
    .string "And that no man might buy or sell,\n"
    .string "save he that had the mark, or the name\l"
    .string "of the beast, or the number of his\l"
    .string "name$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_13_18::
    .string "Here is wisdom. Let him that hath\n"
    .string "understanding count the number of\l"
    .string "the beast: for it is the number of a\l"
    .string "man; and his number is Six hundred\l"
    .string "threescore and six.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_1::
    .string "And I looked, and, lo, a Lamb stood\n"
    .string "on the mount Sion, and with him an\l"
    .string "hundred forty and four thousand,\l"
    .string "having his Father’s name written in\l"
    .string "their foreheads.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_2::
    .string "And I heard a voice from heaven, as\n"
    .string "the voice of many waters, and as the\l"
    .string "voice of a great thunder: and I heard\l"
    .string "the voice of harpers harping with\l"
    .string "their harps:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_3::
    .string "And they sung as it were a new song\n"
    .string "before the throne, and before the\l"
    .string "four beasts, and the elders: and no\l"
    .string "man could learn that song but the\l"
    .string "hundred and forty and four thousand,\l"
    .string "which were redeemed from the earth$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_4::
    .string "These are they which were not\n"
    .string "defiled with women; for they are\l"
    .string "virgins. These are they which\l"
    .string "follow the Lamb whithersoever he\l"
    .string "goeth. These were redeemed from among\l"
    .string "men, being the firstfruits unto God\l"
    .string "and to the Lamb.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_5::
    .string "And in their mouth was found no\n"
    .string "guile: for they are without fault\l"
    .string "before the throne of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_6::
    .string "And I saw another angel fly in the\n"
    .string "midst of heaven, having the\l"
    .string "everlasting gospel to preach unto\l"
    .string "them that dwell on the earth, and to\l"
    .string "every nation, and kindred, and\l"
    .string "tongue, and people,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_7::
    .string "Saying with a loud voice, Fear God,\n"
    .string "and give glory to him; for the hour\l"
    .string "of his judgment is come: and worship\l"
    .string "him that made heaven, and earth, and\l"
    .string "the sea, and the fountains of waters$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_8::
    .string "And there followed another angel,\n"
    .string "saying, Babylon is fallen, is\l"
    .string "fallen, that great city, because\l"
    .string "she made all nations drink of the\l"
    .string "wine of the wrath of her fornication.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_9::
    .string "And the third angel followed them,\n"
    .string "saying with a loud voice, If any man\l"
    .string "worship the beast and his image, and\l"
    .string "receive his mark in his forehead, or\l"
    .string "in his hand,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_10::
    .string "The same shall drink of the wine of\n"
    .string "the wrath of God, which is poured out\l"
    .string "without mixture into the cup of his\l"
    .string "indignation; and he shall be\l"
    .string "tormented with fire and brimstone in\l"
    .string "the presence of the holy angels,\l"
    .string "and in the presence of the Lamb:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_11::
    .string "And the smoke of their torment\n"
    .string "ascendeth up for ever and ever: and\l"
    .string "they have no rest day nor night, who\l"
    .string "worship the beast and his image, and\l"
    .string "whosoever receiveth the mark of his\l"
    .string "name$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_12::
    .string "Here is the patience of the saints:\n"
    .string "here are they that keep the\l"
    .string "commandments of God, and the faith of\l"
    .string "Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_13::
    .string "And I heard a voice from heaven\n"
    .string "saying unto me, Write, Blessed are\l"
    .string "the dead which die in the Lord from\l"
    .string "henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit,\l"
    .string "that they may rest from their\l"
    .string "labours; and their works do follow\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_14::
    .string "And I looked, and behold a white\n"
    .string "cloud, and upon the cloud one sat\l"
    .string "like unto the Son of man, having on\l"
    .string "his head a golden crown, and in his\l"
    .string "hand a sharp sickle.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_15::
    .string "And another angel came out of the\n"
    .string "temple, crying with a loud voice to\l"
    .string "him that sat on the cloud, Thrust in\l"
    .string "thy sickle, and reap: for the time\l"
    .string "is come for thee to reap; for the\l"
    .string "harvest of the earth is ripe.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_16::
    .string "And he that sat on the cloud thrust\n"
    .string "in his sickle on the earth; and the\l"
    .string "earth was reaped.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_17::
    .string "And another angel came out of the\n"
    .string "temple which is in heaven, he also\l"
    .string "having a sharp sickle.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_18::
    .string "And another angel came out from the\n"
    .string "altar, which had power over fire;\l"
    .string "and cried with a loud cry to him that\l"
    .string "had the sharp sickle, saying,\l"
    .string "Thrust in thy sharp sickle, and\l"
    .string "gather the clusters of the vine of\l"
    .string "the earth; for her grapes are fully\l"
    .string "ripe.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_19::
    .string "And the angel thrust in his sickle\n"
    .string "into the earth, and gathered the vine\l"
    .string "of the earth, and cast it into the\l"
    .string "great winepress of the wrath of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_14_20::
    .string "And the winepress was trodden\n"
    .string "without the city, and blood came out\l"
    .string "of the winepress, even unto the\l"
    .string "horse bridles, by the space of a\l"
    .string "thousand and six hundred furlongs.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_1::
    .string "And I saw another sign in heaven,\n"
    .string "great and marvellous, seven angels\l"
    .string "having the seven last plagues; for\l"
    .string "in them is filled up the wrath of\l"
    .string "God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_2::
    .string "And I saw as it were a sea of glass\n"
    .string "mingled with fire: and them that had\l"
    .string "gotten the victory over the beast,\l"
    .string "and over his image, and over his\l"
    .string "mark, and over the number of his\l"
    .string "name, stand on the sea of glass,\l"
    .string "having the harps of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_3::
    .string "And they sing the song of Moses the\n"
    .string "servant of God, and the song of the\l"
    .string "Lamb, saying, Great and marvellous\l"
    .string "are thy works, Lord God Almighty;\l"
    .string "just and true are thy ways, thou King\l"
    .string "of saints.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_4::
    .string "Who shall not fear thee, O Lord,\n"
    .string "and glorify thy name? for thou only\l"
    .string "art holy: for all nations shall\l"
    .string "come and worship before thee; for\l"
    .string "thy judgments are made manifest.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_5::
    .string "And after that I looked, and,\n"
    .string "behold, the temple of the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of the testimony in\l"
    .string "heaven was opened:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_6::
    .string "And the seven angels came out of\n"
    .string "the temple, having the seven\l"
    .string "plagues, clothed in pure and white\l"
    .string "linen, and having their breasts\l"
    .string "girded with golden girdles$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_7::
    .string "And one of the four beasts gave unto\n"
    .string "the seven angels seven golden\l"
    .string "vials full of the wrath of God, who\l"
    .string "liveth for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_15_8::
    .string "And the temple was filled with\n"
    .string "smoke from the glory of God, and from\l"
    .string "his power; and no man was able to\l"
    .string "enter into the temple, till the\l"
    .string "seven plagues of the seven angels\l"
    .string "were fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_1::
    .string "And I heard a great voice out of the\n"
    .string "temple saying to the seven angels,\l"
    .string "Go your ways, and pour out the vials\l"
    .string "of the wrath of God upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_2::
    .string "And the first went, and poured out\n"
    .string "his vial upon the earth; and there\l"
    .string "fell a noisome and grievous sore\l"
    .string "upon the men which had the mark of\l"
    .string "the beast, and upon them which\l"
    .string "worshipped his image.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_3::
    .string "And the second angel poured out\n"
    .string "his vial upon the sea; and it became\l"
    .string "as the blood of a dead man: and every\l"
    .string "living soul died in the sea.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_4::
    .string "And the third angel poured out his\n"
    .string "vial upon the rivers and fountains\l"
    .string "of waters; and they became blood.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_5::
    .string "And I heard the angel of the waters\n"
    .string "say, Thou art righteous, O Lord,\l"
    .string "which art, and wast, and shalt be,\l"
    .string "because thou hast judged thus.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_6::
    .string "For they have shed the blood of\n"
    .string "saints and prophets, and thou hast\l"
    .string "given them blood to drink; for they\l"
    .string "are worthy.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_7::
    .string "And I heard another out of the\n"
    .string "altar say, Even so, Lord God\l"
    .string "Almighty, true and righteous are thy\l"
    .string "judgments.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_8::
    .string "And the fourth angel poured out\n"
    .string "his vial upon the sun; and power\l"
    .string "was given unto him to scorch men with\l"
    .string "fire.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_9::
    .string "And men were scorched with great\n"
    .string "heat, and blasphemed the name of\l"
    .string "God, which hath power over these\l"
    .string "plagues: and they repented not to\l"
    .string "give him glory.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_10::
    .string "And the fifth angel poured out his\n"
    .string "vial upon the seat of the beast; and\l"
    .string "his kingdom was full of darkness;\l"
    .string "and they gnawed their tongues for\l"
    .string "pain,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_11::
    .string "And blasphemed the God of heaven\n"
    .string "because of their pains and their\l"
    .string "sores, and repented not of their\l"
    .string "deeds$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_12::
    .string "And the sixth angel poured out his\n"
    .string "vial upon the great river\l"
    .string "Euphrates; and the water thereof was\l"
    .string "dried up, that the way of the kings\l"
    .string "of the east might be prepared.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_13::
    .string "And I saw three unclean spirits\n"
    .string "like frogs come out of the mouth of\l"
    .string "the dragon, and out of the mouth of\l"
    .string "the beast, and out of the mouth of the\l"
    .string "false prophet.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_14::
    .string "For they are the spirits of devils,\n"
    .string "working miracles, which go forth\l"
    .string "unto the kings of the earth and of\l"
    .string "the whole world, to gather them to\l"
    .string "the battle of that great day of God\l"
    .string "Almighty.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_15::
    .string "Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed\n"
    .string "is he that watcheth, and keepeth his\l"
    .string "garments, lest he walk naked, and\l"
    .string "they see his shame.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_16::
    .string "And he gathered them together into a\n"
    .string "place called in the Hebrew tongue\l"
    .string "Armageddon.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_17::
    .string "And the seventh angel poured out\n"
    .string "his vial into the air; and there came\l"
    .string "a great voice out of the temple of\l"
    .string "heaven, from the throne, saying, It\l"
    .string "is done.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_18::
    .string "And there were voices, and thunders,\n"
    .string "and lightnings; and there was a\l"
    .string "great earthquake, such as was not\l"
    .string "since men were upon the earth, so\l"
    .string "mighty an earthquake, and so great.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_19::
    .string "And the great city was divided into\n"
    .string "three parts, and the cities of the\l"
    .string "nations fell: and great Babylon\l"
    .string "came in remembrance before God, to\l"
    .string "give unto her the cup of the wine of\l"
    .string "the fierceness of his wrath.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_20::
    .string "And every island fled away, and the\n"
    .string "mountains were not found.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_16_21::
    .string "And there fell upon men a great\n"
    .string "hail out of heaven, every stone\l"
    .string "about the weight of a talent: and men\l"
    .string "blasphemed God because of the\l"
    .string "plague of the hail; for the plague\l"
    .string "thereof was exceeding great.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_1::
    .string "And there came one of the seven\n"
    .string "angels which had the seven vials,\l"
    .string "and talked with me, saying unto me,\l"
    .string "Come hither; I will shew unto thee\l"
    .string "the judgment of the great whore that\l"
    .string "sitteth upon many waters:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_2::
    .string "With whom the kings of the earth\n"
    .string "have committed fornication, and the\l"
    .string "inhabitants of the earth have been\l"
    .string "made drunk with the wine of her\l"
    .string "fornication$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_3::
    .string "So he carried me away in the spirit\n"
    .string "into the wilderness: and I saw a\l"
    .string "woman sit upon a scarlet coloured\l"
    .string "beast, full of names of blasphemy,\l"
    .string "having seven heads and ten horns.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_4::
    .string "And the woman was arrayed in\n"
    .string "purple and scarlet colour, and\l"
    .string "decked with gold and precious\l"
    .string "stones and pearls, having a golden\l"
    .string "cup in her hand full of\l"
    .string "abominations and filthiness of her\l"
    .string "fornication:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_5::
    .string "And upon her forehead was a name\n"
    .string "written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT,\l"
    .string "THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND\l"
    .string "ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_6::
    .string "And I saw the woman drunken with the\n"
    .string "blood of the saints, and with the\l"
    .string "blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and\l"
    .string "when I saw her, I wondered with great\l"
    .string "admiration.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_7::
    .string "And the angel said unto me,\n"
    .string "Wherefore didst thou marvel? I will\l"
    .string "tell thee the mystery of the woman,\l"
    .string "and of the beast that carrieth her,\l"
    .string "which hath the seven heads and ten\l"
    .string "horns.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_8::
    .string "The beast that thou sawest was, and\n"
    .string "is not; and shall ascend out of the\l"
    .string "bottomless pit, and go into\l"
    .string "perdition: and they that dwell on\l"
    .string "the earth shall wonder, whose names\l"
    .string "were not written in the book of life\l"
    .string "from the foundation of the world,\l"
    .string "when they behold the beast that was,\l"
    .string "and is not, and yet is.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_9::
    .string "And here is the mind which hath\n"
    .string "wisdom. The seven heads are seven\l"
    .string "mountains, on which the woman\l"
    .string "sitteth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_10::
    .string "And there are seven kings: five are\n"
    .string "fallen, and one is, and the other is\l"
    .string "not yet come; and when he cometh, he\l"
    .string "must continue a short space.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_11::
    .string "And the beast that was, and is not,\n"
    .string "even he is the eighth, and is of the\l"
    .string "seven, and goeth into perdition.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_12::
    .string "And the ten horns which thou sawest\n"
    .string "are ten kings, which have received no\l"
    .string "kingdom as yet; but receive power as\l"
    .string "kings one hour with the beast.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_13::
    .string "These have one mind, and shall give\n"
    .string "their power and strength unto the\l"
    .string "beast.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_14::
    .string "These shall make war with the Lamb,\n"
    .string "and the Lamb shall overcome them:\l"
    .string "for he is Lord of lords, and King of\l"
    .string "kings: and they that are with him are\l"
    .string "called, and chosen, and faithful.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_15::
    .string "And he saith unto me, The waters\n"
    .string "which thou sawest, where the whore\l"
    .string "sitteth, are peoples, and\l"
    .string "multitudes, and nations, and tongues.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_16::
    .string "And the ten horns which thou sawest\n"
    .string "upon the beast, these shall hate\l"
    .string "the whore, and shall make her\l"
    .string "desolate and naked, and shall eat\l"
    .string "her flesh, and burn her with fire.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_17::
    .string "For God hath put in their hearts to\n"
    .string "fulfil his will, and to agree, and\l"
    .string "give their kingdom unto the beast,\l"
    .string "until the words of God shall be\l"
    .string "fulfilled.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_17_18::
    .string "And the woman which thou sawest is\n"
    .string "that great city, which reigneth over\l"
    .string "the kings of the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_1::
    .string "And after these things I saw another\n"
    .string "angel come down from heaven, having\l"
    .string "great power; and the earth was\l"
    .string "lightened with his glory.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_2::
    .string "And he cried mightily with a strong\n"
    .string "voice, saying, Babylon the great is\l"
    .string "fallen, is fallen, and is become\l"
    .string "the habitation of devils, and the\l"
    .string "hold of every foul spirit, and a\l"
    .string "cage of every unclean and hateful\l"
    .string "bird.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_3::
    .string "For all nations have drunk of the\n"
    .string "wine of the wrath of her fornication,\l"
    .string "and the kings of the earth have\l"
    .string "committed fornication with her, and\l"
    .string "the merchants of the earth are waxed\l"
    .string "rich through the abundance of her\l"
    .string "delicacies.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_4::
    .string "And I heard another voice from\n"
    .string "heaven, saying, Come out of her, my\l"
    .string "people, that ye be not partakers of\l"
    .string "her sins, and that ye receive not of\l"
    .string "her plagues.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_5::
    .string "For her sins have reached unto\n"
    .string "heaven, and God hath remembered her\l"
    .string "iniquities.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_6::
    .string "Reward her even as she rewarded you,\n"
    .string "and double unto her double\l"
    .string "according to her works: in the cup\l"
    .string "which she hath filled fill to her\l"
    .string "double.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_7::
    .string "How much she hath glorified\n"
    .string "herself, and lived deliciously, so\l"
    .string "much torment and sorrow give her: for\l"
    .string "she saith in her heart, I sit a queen,\l"
    .string "and am no widow, and shall see no\l"
    .string "sorrow.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_8::
    .string "Therefore shall her plagues come\n"
    .string "in one day, death, and mourning, and\l"
    .string "famine; and she shall be utterly\l"
    .string "burned with fire: for strong is the\l"
    .string "Lord God who judgeth her.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_9::
    .string "And the kings of the earth, who have\n"
    .string "committed fornication and lived\l"
    .string "deliciously with her, shall\l"
    .string "bewail her, and lament for her, when\l"
    .string "they shall see the smoke of her\l"
    .string "burning,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_10::
    .string "Standing afar off for the fear of\n"
    .string "her torment, saying, Alas, alas that\l"
    .string "great city Babylon, that mighty\l"
    .string "city! for in one hour is thy judgment\l"
    .string "come$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_11::
    .string "And the merchants of the earth\n"
    .string "shall weep and mourn over her; for\l"
    .string "no man buyeth their merchandise any\l"
    .string "more:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_12::
    .string "The merchandise of gold, and\n"
    .string "silver, and precious stones, and of\l"
    .string "pearls, and fine linen, and\l"
    .string "purple, and silk, and scarlet, and\l"
    .string "all thyine wood, and all manner\l"
    .string "vessels of ivory, and all manner\l"
    .string "vessels of most precious wood, and\l"
    .string "of brass, and iron, and marble,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_13::
    .string "And cinnamon, and odours, and\n"
    .string "ointments, and frankincense, and\l"
    .string "wine, and oil, and fine flour, and\l"
    .string "wheat, and beasts, and sheep, and\l"
    .string "horses, and chariots, and slaves,\l"
    .string "and souls of men$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_14::
    .string "And the fruits that thy soul\n"
    .string "lusted after are departed from thee,\l"
    .string "and all things which were dainty\l"
    .string "and goodly are departed from thee,\l"
    .string "and thou shalt find them no more at\l"
    .string "all.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_15::
    .string "The merchants of these things, which\n"
    .string "were made rich by her, shall stand\l"
    .string "afar off for the fear of her torment,\l"
    .string "weeping and wailing,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_16::
    .string "And saying, Alas, alas that great\n"
    .string "city, that was clothed in fine\l"
    .string "linen, and purple, and scarlet,\l"
    .string "and decked with gold, and precious\l"
    .string "stones, and pearls!"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_17::
    .string "For in one hour so great riches is\n"
    .string "come to nought. And every\l"
    .string "shipmaster, and all the company in\l"
    .string "ships, and sailors, and as many as\l"
    .string "trade by sea, stood afar off,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_18::
    .string "And cried when they saw the smoke of\n"
    .string "her burning, saying, What city is\l"
    .string "like unto this great city!"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_19::
    .string "And they cast dust on their heads,\n"
    .string "and cried, weeping and wailing,\l"
    .string "saying, Alas, alas that great city,\l"
    .string "wherein were made rich all that had\l"
    .string "ships in the sea by reason of her\l"
    .string "costliness! for in one hour is she\l"
    .string "made desolate$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_20::
    .string "Rejoice over her, thou heaven, and\n"
    .string "ye holy apostles and prophets;\l"
    .string "for God hath avenged you on her.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_21::
    .string "And a mighty angel took up a stone\n"
    .string "like a great millstone, and cast it\l"
    .string "into the sea, saying, Thus with\l"
    .string "violence shall that great city\l"
    .string "Babylon be thrown down, and shall\l"
    .string "be found no more at all.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_22::
    .string "And the voice of harpers, and\n"
    .string "musicians, and of pipers, and\l"
    .string "trumpeters, shall be heard no more\l"
    .string "at all in thee; and no craftsman, of\l"
    .string "whatsoever craft he be, shall be\l"
    .string "found any more in thee; and the sound\l"
    .string "of a millstone shall be heard no\l"
    .string "more at all in thee;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_23::
    .string "And the light of a candle shall\n"
    .string "shine no more at all in thee; and\l"
    .string "the voice of the bridegroom and of\l"
    .string "the bride shall be heard no more at\l"
    .string "all in thee: for thy merchants were\l"
    .string "the great men of the earth; for by thy\l"
    .string "sorceries were all nations deceived$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_18_24::
    .string "And in her was found the blood of\n"
    .string "prophets, and of saints, and of all\l"
    .string "that were slain upon the earth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_1::
    .string "And after these things I heard a\n"
    .string "great voice of much people in\l"
    .string "heaven, saying, Alleluia;\l"
    .string "Salvation, and glory, and honour,\l"
    .string "and power, unto the Lord our God:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_2::
    .string "For true and righteous are his\n"
    .string "judgments: for he hath judged the\l"
    .string "great whore, which did corrupt the\l"
    .string "earth with her fornication, and hath\l"
    .string "avenged the blood of his servants at\l"
    .string "her hand$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_3::
    .string "And again they said, Alleluia. And\n"
    .string "her smoke rose up for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_4::
    .string "And the four and twenty elders and\n"
    .string "the four beasts fell down and\l"
    .string "worshipped God that sat on the\l"
    .string "throne, saying, Amen; Alleluia.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_5::
    .string "And a voice came out of the throne,\n"
    .string "saying, Praise our God, all ye his\l"
    .string "servants, and ye that fear him, both\l"
    .string "small and great.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_6::
    .string "And I heard as it were the voice of a\n"
    .string "great multitude, and as the voice of\l"
    .string "many waters, and as the voice of\l"
    .string "mighty thunderings, saying,\l"
    .string "Alleluia: for the Lord God\l"
    .string "omnipotent reigneth.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_7::
    .string "Let us be glad and rejoice, and give\n"
    .string "honour to him: for the marriage of\l"
    .string "the Lamb is come, and his wife hath\l"
    .string "made herself ready.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_8::
    .string "And to her was granted that she\n"
    .string "should be arrayed in fine linen,\l"
    .string "clean and white: for the fine linen\l"
    .string "is the righteousness of saints.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_9::
    .string "And he saith unto me, Write,\n"
    .string "Blessed are they which are called\l"
    .string "unto the marriage supper of the Lamb\l"
    .string " And he saith unto me, These are the\l"
    .string "true sayings of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_10::
    .string "And I fell at his feet to worship\n"
    .string "him. And he said unto me, See thou do\l"
    .string "it not: I am thy fellowservant, and\l"
    .string "of thy brethren that have the\l"
    .string "testimony of Jesus: worship God: for\l"
    .string "the testimony of Jesus is the spirit\l"
    .string "of prophecy.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_11::
    .string "And I saw heaven opened, and behold\n"
    .string "a white horse; and he that sat upon\l"
    .string "him was called Faithful and True,\l"
    .string "and in righteousness he doth judge\l"
    .string "and make war.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_12::
    .string "His eyes were as a flame of fire,\n"
    .string "and on his head were many crowns; and\l"
    .string "he had a name written, that no man\l"
    .string "knew, but he himself.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_13::
    .string "And he was clothed with a vesture\n"
    .string "dipped in blood: and his name is\l"
    .string "called The Word of God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_14::
    .string "And the armies which were in heaven\n"
    .string "followed him upon white horses,\l"
    .string "clothed in fine linen, white and\l"
    .string "clean.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_15::
    .string "And out of his mouth goeth a sharp\n"
    .string "sword, that with it he should smite\l"
    .string "the nations: and he shall rule them\l"
    .string "with a rod of iron: and he treadeth\l"
    .string "the winepress of the fierceness and\l"
    .string "wrath of Almighty God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_16::
    .string "And he hath on his vesture and on\n"
    .string "his thigh a name written, KING OF\l"
    .string "KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_17::
    .string "And I saw an angel standing in the\n"
    .string "sun; and he cried with a loud voice,\l"
    .string "saying to all the fowls that fly\l"
    .string "in the midst of heaven, Come and\l"
    .string "gather yourselves together unto the\l"
    .string "supper of the great God;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_18::
    .string "That ye may eat the flesh of kings,\n"
    .string "and the flesh of captains, and the\l"
    .string "flesh of mighty men, and the flesh\l"
    .string "of horses, and of them that sit on\l"
    .string "them, and the flesh of all men,\l"
    .string "both free and bond, both small and\l"
    .string "great$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_19::
    .string "And I saw the beast, and the kings of\n"
    .string "the earth, and their armies, gathered\l"
    .string "together to make war against him that\l"
    .string "sat on the horse, and against his\l"
    .string "army.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_20::
    .string "And the beast was taken, and with\n"
    .string "him the false prophet that wrought\l"
    .string "miracles before him, with which he\l"
    .string "deceived them that had received the\l"
    .string "mark of the beast, and them that\l"
    .string "worshipped his image. These both\l"
    .string "were cast alive into a lake of fire\l"
    .string "burning with brimstone.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_19_21::
    .string "And the remnant were slain with the\n"
    .string "sword of him that sat upon the horse,\l"
    .string "which sword proceeded out of his\l"
    .string "mouth: and all the fowls were\l"
    .string "filled with their flesh.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_1::
    .string "And I saw an angel come down from\n"
    .string "heaven, having the key of the\l"
    .string "bottomless pit and a great chain in\l"
    .string "his hand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_2::
    .string "And he laid hold on the dragon,\n"
    .string "that old serpent, which is the\l"
    .string "Devil, and Satan, and bound him a\l"
    .string "thousand years,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_3::
    .string "And cast him into the bottomless\n"
    .string "pit, and shut him up, and set a seal\l"
    .string "upon him, that he should deceive the\l"
    .string "nations no more, till the thousand\l"
    .string "years should be fulfilled: and\l"
    .string "after that he must be loosed a\l"
    .string "little season$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_4::
    .string "And I saw thrones, and they sat upon\n"
    .string "them, and judgment was given unto\l"
    .string "them: and I saw the souls of them\l"
    .string "that were beheaded for the witness of\l"
    .string "Jesus, and for the word of God, and\l"
    .string "which had not worshipped the beast,\l"
    .string "neither his image, neither had\l"
    .string "received his mark upon their\l"
    .string "foreheads, or in their hands; and\l"
    .string "they lived and reigned with Christ a\l"
    .string "thousand years.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_5::
    .string "But the rest of the dead lived not\n"
    .string "again until the thousand years were\l"
    .string "finished. This is the first\l"
    .string "resurrection.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_6::
    .string "Blessed and holy is he that hath\n"
    .string "part in the first resurrection: on\l"
    .string "such the second death hath no power,\l"
    .string "but they shall be priests of God\l"
    .string "and of Christ, and shall reign with\l"
    .string "him a thousand years.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_7::
    .string "And when the thousand years are\n"
    .string "expired, Satan shall be loosed out\l"
    .string "of his prison,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_8::
    .string "And shall go out to deceive the\n"
    .string "nations which are in the four\l"
    .string "quarters of the earth, Gog, and\l"
    .string "Magog, to gather them together to\l"
    .string "battle: the number of whom is as the\l"
    .string "sand of the sea$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_9::
    .string "And they went up on the breadth of\n"
    .string "the earth, and compassed the camp of\l"
    .string "the saints about, and the beloved\l"
    .string "city: and fire came down from God out\l"
    .string "of heaven, and devoured them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_10::
    .string "And the devil that deceived them\n"
    .string "was cast into the lake of fire and\l"
    .string "brimstone, where the beast and the\l"
    .string "false prophet are, and shall be\l"
    .string "tormented day and night for ever and\l"
    .string "ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_11::
    .string "And I saw a great white throne, and\n"
    .string "him that sat on it, from whose face\l"
    .string "the earth and the heaven fled away;\l"
    .string "and there was found no place for\l"
    .string "them.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_12::
    .string "And I saw the dead, small and\n"
    .string "great, stand before God; and the\l"
    .string "books were opened: and another book\l"
    .string "was opened, which is the book of\l"
    .string "life: and the dead were judged out of\l"
    .string "those things which were written in\l"
    .string "the books, according to their works.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_13::
    .string "And the sea gave up the dead which\n"
    .string "were in it; and death and hell\l"
    .string "delivered up the dead which were in\l"
    .string "them: and they were judged every man\l"
    .string "according to their works.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_14::
    .string "And death and hell were cast into\n"
    .string "the lake of fire. This is the second\l"
    .string "death.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_20_15::
    .string "And whosoever was not found written\n"
    .string "in the book of life was cast into the\l"
    .string "lake of fire.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_1::
    .string "And I saw a new heaven and a new\n"
    .string "earth: for the first heaven and the\l"
    .string "first earth were passed away; and\l"
    .string "there was no more sea.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_2::
    .string "And I John saw the holy city, new\n"
    .string "Jerusalem, coming down from God out\l"
    .string "of heaven, prepared as a bride\l"
    .string "adorned for her husband.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_3::
    .string "And I heard a great voice out of\n"
    .string "heaven saying, Behold, the\l"
    .string "tabernacle of God is with men, and he\l"
    .string "will dwell with them, and they\l"
    .string "shall be his people, and God\l"
    .string "himself shall be with them, and be\l"
    .string "their God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_4::
    .string "And God shall wipe away all\n"
    .string "tears from their eyes; and there\l"
    .string "shall be no more death, neither\l"
    .string "sorrow, nor crying, neither shall\l"
    .string "there be any more pain: for the\l"
    .string "former things are passed away.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_5::
    .string "And he that sat upon the throne\n"
    .string "said, Behold, I make all things\l"
    .string "new. And he said unto me, Write: for\l"
    .string "these words are true and faithful.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_6::
    .string "And he said unto me, It is done. I am\n"
    .string "Alpha and Omega, the beginning and\l"
    .string "the end. I will give unto him that\l"
    .string "is athirst of the fountain of the\l"
    .string "water of life freely.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_7::
    .string "He that overcometh shall inherit\n"
    .string "all things; and I will be his God,\l"
    .string "and he shall be my son.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_8::
    .string "But the fearful, and unbelieving,\n"
    .string "and the abominable, and murderers,\l"
    .string "and whoremongers, and sorcerers, and\l"
    .string "idolaters, and all liars, shall\l"
    .string "have their part in the lake which\l"
    .string "burneth with fire and brimstone:\l"
    .string "which is the second death.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_9::
    .string "And there came unto me one of the\n"
    .string "seven angels which had the seven\l"
    .string "vials full of the seven last\l"
    .string "plagues, and talked with me, saying,\l"
    .string "Come hither, I will shew thee the\l"
    .string "bride, the Lamb’s wife.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_10::
    .string "And he carried me away in the\n"
    .string "spirit to a great and high mountain,\l"
    .string "and shewed me that great city, the\l"
    .string "holy Jerusalem, descending out of\l"
    .string "heaven from God,"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_11::
    .string "Having the glory of God: and her\n"
    .string "light was like unto a stone most\l"
    .string "precious, even like a jasper stone,\l"
    .string "clear as crystal;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_12::
    .string "And had a wall great and high, and\n"
    .string "had twelve gates, and at the gates\l"
    .string "twelve angels, and names written\l"
    .string "thereon, which are the names of the\l"
    .string "twelve tribes of the children of\l"
    .string "Israel:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_13::
    .string "On the east three gates; on the\n"
    .string "north three gates; on the south three\l"
    .string "gates; and on the west three gates$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_14::
    .string "And the wall of the city had\n"
    .string "twelve foundations, and in them the\l"
    .string "names of the twelve apostles of the\l"
    .string "Lamb.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_15::
    .string "And he that talked with me had a\n"
    .string "golden reed to measure the city, and\l"
    .string "the gates thereof, and the wall\l"
    .string "thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_16::
    .string "And the city lieth foursquare, and\n"
    .string "the length is as large as the\l"
    .string "breadth: and he measured the city\l"
    .string "with the reed, twelve thousand\l"
    .string "furlongs. The length and the\l"
    .string "breadth and the height of it are\l"
    .string "equal.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_17::
    .string "And he measured the wall thereof,\n"
    .string "an hundred and forty and four cubits,\l"
    .string "according to the measure of a man,\l"
    .string "that is, of the angel.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_18::
    .string "And the building of the wall of it\n"
    .string "was of jasper: and the city was pure\l"
    .string "gold, like unto clear glass.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_19::
    .string "And the foundations of the wall of\n"
    .string "the city were garnished with all\l"
    .string "manner of precious stones. The first\l"
    .string "foundation was jasper; the second,\l"
    .string "sapphire; the third, a chalcedony;\l"
    .string "the fourth, an emerald;"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_20::
    .string "The fifth, sardonyx; the sixth,\n"
    .string "sardius; the seventh, chrysolyte;\l"
    .string "the eighth, beryl; the ninth, a\l"
    .string "topaz; the tenth, a chrysoprasus;\l"
    .string "the eleventh, a jacinth; the\l"
    .string "twelfth, an amethyst$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_21::
    .string "And the twelve gates were twelve\n"
    .string "pearls: every several gate was of\l"
    .string "one pearl: and the street of the\l"
    .string "city was pure gold, as it were\l"
    .string "transparent glass.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_22::
    .string "And I saw no temple therein: for\n"
    .string "the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb\l"
    .string "are the temple of it.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_23::
    .string "And the city had no need of the sun,\n"
    .string "neither of the moon, to shine in it:\l"
    .string "for the glory of God did lighten it,\l"
    .string "and the Lamb is the light thereof.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_24::
    .string "And the nations of them which are\n"
    .string "saved shall walk in the light of\l"
    .string "it: and the kings of the earth do\l"
    .string "bring their glory and honour into it.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_25::
    .string "And the gates of it shall not be\n"
    .string "shut at all by day: for there shall\l"
    .string "be no night there.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_26::
    .string "And they shall bring the glory and\n"
    .string "honour of the nations into it.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_21_27::
    .string "And there shall in no wise enter\n"
    .string "into it any thing that defileth,\l"
    .string "neither whatsoever worketh\l"
    .string "abomination, or maketh a lie: but\l"
    .string "they which are written in the Lamb’s\l"
    .string "book of life.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_1::
    .string "And he shewed me a pure river of\n"
    .string "water of life, clear as crystal,\l"
    .string "proceeding out of the throne of God\l"
    .string "and of the Lamb.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_2::
    .string "In the midst of the street of it, and\n"
    .string "on either side of the river, was\l"
    .string "there the tree of life, which bare\l"
    .string "twelve manner of fruits, and\l"
    .string "yielded her fruit every month: and\l"
    .string "the leaves of the tree were for the\l"
    .string "healing of the nations.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_3::
    .string "And there shall be no more curse:\n"
    .string "but the throne of God and of the Lamb\l"
    .string "shall be in it; and his servants\l"
    .string "shall serve him:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_4::
    .string "And they shall see his face; and\n"
    .string "his name shall be in their foreheads$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_5::
    .string "And there shall be no night there;\n"
    .string "and they need no candle, neither\l"
    .string "light of the sun; for the Lord God\l"
    .string "giveth them light: and they shall\l"
    .string "reign for ever and ever.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_6::
    .string "And he said unto me, These sayings\n"
    .string "are faithful and true: and the Lord\l"
    .string "God of the holy prophets sent his\l"
    .string "angel to shew unto his servants the\l"
    .string "things which must shortly be done.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_7::
    .string "Behold, I come quickly: blessed is\n"
    .string "he that keepeth the sayings of the\l"
    .string "prophecy of this book.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_8::
    .string "And I John saw these things, and\n"
    .string "heard them. And when I had heard and\l"
    .string "seen, I fell down to worship before\l"
    .string "the feet of the angel which shewed\l"
    .string "me these things.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_9::
    .string "Then saith he unto me, See thou do it\n"
    .string "not: for I am thy fellowservant, and\l"
    .string "of thy brethren the prophets, and of\l"
    .string "them which keep the sayings of this\l"
    .string "book: worship God.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_10::
    .string "And he saith unto me, Seal not the\n"
    .string "sayings of the prophecy of this\l"
    .string "book: for the time is at hand.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_11::
    .string "He that is unjust, let him be unjust\n"
    .string "still: and he which is filthy, let\l"
    .string "him be filthy still: and he that is\l"
    .string "righteous, let him be righteous\l"
    .string "still: and he that is holy, let him\l"
    .string "be holy still.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_12::
    .string "And, behold, I come quickly; and my\n"
    .string "reward is with me, to give every man\l"
    .string "according as his work shall be.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_13::
    .string "I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning\n"
    .string "and the end, the first and the last.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_14::
    .string "Blessed are they that do his\n"
    .string "commandments, that they may have\l"
    .string "right to the tree of life, and may\l"
    .string "enter in through the gates into the\l"
    .string "city.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_15::
    .string "For without are dogs, and sorcerers,\n"
    .string "and whoremongers, and murderers, and\l"
    .string "idolaters, and whosoever loveth and\l"
    .string "maketh a lie.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_16::
    .string "I Jesus have sent mine angel to\n"
    .string "testify unto you these things in the\l"
    .string "churches. I am the root and the\l"
    .string "offspring of David, and the bright\l"
    .string "and morning star.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_17::
    .string "And the Spirit and the bride say,\n"
    .string "Come. And let him that heareth say,\l"
    .string "Come. And let him that is athirst\l"
    .string "come. And whosoever will, let him\l"
    .string "take the water of life freely.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_18::
    .string "For I testify unto every man that\n"
    .string "heareth the words of the prophecy\l"
    .string "of this book, If any man shall add\l"
    .string "unto these things, God shall add\l"
    .string "unto him the plagues that are\l"
    .string "written in this book:"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_19::
    .string "And if any man shall take away from\n"
    .string "the words of the book of this\l"
    .string "prophecy, God shall take away his\l"
    .string "part out of the book of life, and out\l"
    .string "of the holy city, and from the things\l"
    .string "which are written in this book$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_20::
    .string "He which testifieth these things\n"
    .string "saith, Surely I come quickly. Amen.\l"
    .string "Even so, come, Lord Jesus.$"
Bible_Text_Revelation_22_21::
    .string "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ\n"
    .string "be with you all. Amen.$"

